// Generated by tools/generate-writing-submission-reference-data.mjs. Do not edit by hand.
const referenceData = {"business-english-standard-response-book-1-q1":{"exerciseId":"business-english-standard-response-book-1-q1","essayKey":"","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=business-english-standard-response-book-1-q1","flashDeckId":"","paragraphs":[{"label":"1. Idea","english":"I would say uncertainty makes business decisions harder, slower, and more delicate, because leaders often have to act without having the full picture.","chinese":"我會說，不確定性會令商業決策變得更困難、更緩慢，也更需要拿捏分寸，因為領導者很多時都要在資訊並不完整的情況下作出決定。"},{"label":"2. Explanation","english":"In business, uncertainty can cloud demand, costs, competition, regulation, and timing. When a company is unsure how the market will move, how customers will respond, or what risks may appear next, every major decision carries more weight. As a result, firms tend to be more cautious with hiring, investment, pricing, and expansion. In that sense, uncertainty does not just create risk; it puts real pressure on judgment.","chinese":"在商業環境裡，不確定性會令需求、成本、競爭、監管以及時機都變得不明朗。當一家公司不確定市場會怎樣走、客戶會如何反應，或者下一個風險會從哪裡冒出來時，每一個重要決策的分量都會變得更重。因此，公司通常會在招聘、投資、定價和擴張方面變得更審慎。從這個角度來看，不確定性不只是帶來風險；它其實是在考驗判斷力。"},{"label":"3. Example","english":"For example, if a company is considering a new product launch but demand is still unclear, it may avoid a full-scale rollout and test the market first. That is often the smarter move, because it limits the downside while keeping the opportunity alive. In uncertain conditions, strong businesses do not bet the farm; they usually stage their decisions.","chinese":"例如，如果一家公司正在考慮推出新產品，但市場需求仍然不明朗，它可能不會一開始就全面推出，而是先做市場測試。這通常是更聰明的做法，因為它一方面能控制下行風險，另一方面又保留住機會。在不確定的環境下，強的企業不會孤注一擲；它們會分階段作決策。"},{"label":"4. Conclusion","english":"So, to me, uncertainty affects business decisions by forcing leaders to balance speed with caution. They still need to move, but they need to move with discipline.","chinese":"所以，在我看來，不確定性對商業決策的影響，在於它迫使領導者在速度和審慎之間取得平衡。他們仍然要行動，只是行動必須更有紀律。"},{"label":"5. Idea 2","english":"That said, uncertainty is not always a purely negative force; sometimes it sharpens decision-making.","chinese":"不過，不確定性也不一定完全是壞事；有時候，它反而會令決策變得更銳利。"},{"label":"6. Explanation 2","english":"When the ground is shifting, weak thinking gets exposed very quickly. Uncertainty forces companies to question assumptions, stress-test plans, protect cash flow, and stay close to customers. It separates businesses that are merely busy from those that are genuinely strategic. In other words, uncertainty can be uncomfortable, but it can also be clarifying.","chinese":"當外部環境不斷變動時，薄弱的思考方式很快就會露出破綻。不確定性會迫使公司重新檢視假設、壓力測試計劃、保護現金流，並且更貼近客戶。它會把那些只是看起來很忙的企業，和那些真正有策略的企業區分開來。換句話說，不確定性也許令人不安，但它有時反而能讓問題變得更清楚。"},{"label":"7. Example","english":"For instance, when market conditions are unstable, a strong management team may break one big decision into smaller moves: they may run a pilot, review the numbers, refine the offer, and scale only when the signal is strong enough. That kind of disciplined flexibility is often what keeps a business resilient.","chinese":"例如，當市場環境不穩定時，一個強的管理團隊可能會把一個大的決策拆成較小的步驟：先做試點、再看數字、再調整方案，然後只在訊號夠明確時才擴大規模。這種有紀律的靈活性，往往正是企業保持韌性的關鍵。"},{"label":"8. Conclusion 2","english":"Overall, I’d say uncertainty does not mean a business should freeze; what it really demands is clearer thinking, better preparation, and smarter decisions. In business, you rarely get perfect clarity, so the real skill is not waiting for the fog to lift, but learning how to lead through it.","chinese":"總結來說，我會說，不確定性並不代表企業應該停住不動；它真正要求的是更清晰的思考、更周全的準備，以及更聰明的決策。在商業世界裡，你很少會得到百分之百的清晰度，所以真正的能力，不是等迷霧散去，而是學會在迷霧中帶路。"}],"vocabulary":[]},"business-english-standard-response-book-1-q2":{"exerciseId":"business-english-standard-response-book-1-q2","essayKey":"","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=business-english-standard-response-book-1-q2","flashDeckId":"","paragraphs":[{"label":"1. Idea","english":"If I had to choose one, I would say interest rates often put the greatest pressure on businesses overall, because they hit both the cost of money and the pace of demand.","chinese":"如果要我選一項，我會說，整體而言，利率往往對企業造成最大的壓力，因為它同時打擊資金成本，以及市場需求的節奏。"},{"label":"2. Explanation","english":"The reason is that higher interest rates do not just make borrowing more expensive. They also make customers more cautious, slow down investment, tighten cash flow, and raise the bar for every major decision. In that sense, rising rates can squeeze a business from both sides: they push costs up while pulling momentum down. Inflation, rent, and wages are all serious pressures, of course, but interest rates tend to cast the widest shadow.","chinese":"原因在於，較高的利率不只是令借錢變得更昂貴。它同時也會令客戶消費更審慎、投資放慢、現金流收緊，並提高每一個重大決策的門檻。從這個角度來看，利率上升會從兩邊夾擊企業：一邊推高成本，另一邊拖慢動能。當然，通脹、租金和人工上升也都是很嚴重的壓力，但利率的影響範圍通常最廣。"},{"label":"3. Example","english":"For example, if a company has loans, expansion plans, or heavy equipment to finance, a rise in interest rates can bite almost immediately. A firm may delay hiring, cut back investment, or shelve a new project simply because the numbers no longer stack up. It is a bit like driving with both the handbrake on and the road getting steeper.","chinese":"例如，如果一家公司本身有貸款、擴張計劃，或者需要為重型設備融資，利率一上升，壓力往往幾乎立刻就會出現。公司可能會延後招聘、削減投資，甚至把新項目擱置，原因只是那盤數已經不再划算。這有點像一邊拉着手掣開車，一邊前面的路還變得更斜。"},{"label":"4. Conclusion","english":"So, in broad business terms, I would say interest rates are often the heaviest pressure point because they affect financing, confidence, spending, and growth all at once.","chinese":"所以，從整體商業角度來說，我會認為利率往往是最沉重的壓力點，因為它會同時影響融資、信心、消費，以及增長。"},{"label":"5. Idea 2","english":"That said, the real answer still depends on the business model, because pressure lands differently in different industries.","chinese":"不過，真正的答案其實仍然取決於商業模式，因為不同產業承受壓力的方式並不一樣。"},{"label":"6. Explanation 2","english":"For a restaurant, retailer, or labour-intensive service business, rising wages or rent may hurt more directly. For example, if your margins are already thin, even a modest jump in payroll or occupancy costs can eat into profit very quickly. Inflation is also dangerous when a business cannot pass higher costs on to customers. So the bottom line is this: interest rates may be the broadest threat overall, but for some firms, wages or rent are where the pain is felt most sharply.","chinese":"對餐廳、零售商，或者勞動密集型的服務業來說，人工或租金上升可能會帶來更直接的打擊。舉例來說，如果本身利潤空間已經很薄，那麼即使只是薪酬成本或租用成本輕微上升，也可能很快侵蝕利潤。當企業無法把更高的成本轉嫁給客戶時，通脹同樣很危險。所以，最核心的一點是：利率也許是整體上最廣泛的威脅，但對某些公司來說，真正最痛的地方其實是人工或租金。"},{"label":"7. Example","english":"For instance, a software firm with low rent and strong margins may worry far more about interest rates and weaker demand, whereas a small café may feel rising wages and rent far more brutally, because those costs hit the business line by line, month after month.","chinese":"例如，一間租金負擔不高、利潤空間較大的軟件公司，可能更擔心利率上升和需求轉弱；相反，一間小型咖啡店則可能會更直接、更猛烈地感受到人工和租金上升的壓力，因為那些成本是一行一行、每個月都真實地壓在生意上。"},{"label":"8. Conclusion 2","english":"Overall, I’d say interest rates usually create the biggest pressure in the bigger picture, but the sharpest pain depends on where a business is most exposed. In business, pressure rarely arrives in a neat little box; it hits where the model is weakest.","chinese":"總結來說，我會說，從大局來看，利率通常帶來最大的壓力；但最尖銳的痛點，仍然取決於一家企業最脆弱的暴露點在哪裡。在商業世界裡，壓力很少會整整齊齊地裝在一個小盒子裡出現；它往往是朝着商業模式最弱的地方打下去。"}],"vocabulary":[]},"business-english-standard-response-book-1-q3":{"exerciseId":"business-english-standard-response-book-1-q3","essayKey":"","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=business-english-standard-response-book-1-q3","flashDeckId":"","paragraphs":[{"label":"1. Idea","english":"If I had to boil it down to three, I would choose judgment, communication, and execution.","chinese":"如果要我把它濃縮成三項，我會選判斷力、溝通力，以及執行力。"},{"label":"2. Explanation","english":"To begin with, judgment matters because managers are not paid merely to stay busy; they are paid to make sound calls. They need to separate signals from noise, decide what matters most, and know when to move. Just as importantly, communication is what turns a decision into a shared direction. A vague message creates drift, whereas a clear one creates alignment. Then comes execution, which is where plans either take shape or fall apart. Strategy may win attention, but follow-through wins trust.","chinese":"首先，判斷力之所以重要，是因為管理者的價值不只是忙碌，而是在於能作出穩健決定。他們要分辨甚麼是關鍵訊號、甚麼只是雜音，知道甚麼最重要，也知道何時出手。同樣重要的是，溝通力能把決定轉化為共同方向。訊息一旦含糊，團隊就容易漂移；訊息一旦清楚，方向就能對齊。然後就是執行力，因為計劃究竟能不能落地，往往就在這裡見真章。策略可以吸引注意，但真正贏得信任的，是後續落實。"},{"label":"3. Example","english":"Take a delayed product launch as an example. A strong manager will first identify the real bottleneck, then explain the priority in plain, direct language, and finally get the right people moving in step. That is management in the real world: make the call, bring people with you, and get the work over the line.","chinese":"以產品延期為例，一位強的管理者會先找出真正的卡點，然後用清楚直接的語言講明優先次序，最後推動合適的人同步行動。這就是現實世界裡的管理：作出決定、帶著團隊前進，並把事情真正做完。"},{"label":"4. Conclusion","english":"Seen in that light, the heart of management is not control for its own sake, but the ability to think clearly, align people, and deliver results.","chinese":"從這個角度看，管理的核心並不是為了控制而控制，而是能夠清楚思考、對齊團隊，並交出結果。"},{"label":"5. Idea 2","english":"Even so, those three abilities do not operate in neat little boxes; people leadership runs through all of them.","chinese":"即便如此，這三種能力也不是各自獨立運作的；帶人能力其實貫穿在三者之中。"},{"label":"6. Explanation 2","english":"Put differently, judgment without trust can feel cold, communication without empathy can ring hollow, and execution without buy-in can burn a team out. So, beneath the surface, strong management is also about reading the room, staying steady under pressure, and helping people perform without feeling crushed by the weight of it.","chinese":"換句話說，只有判斷而沒有信任，會顯得冷；只有溝通而沒有同理，會顯得空；只有執行而沒有認同，則很容易把團隊推到耗盡。所以，更深一層來看，強的管理也關乎看懂氣氛、在壓力下保持穩定，以及讓團隊在高表現之下不至於被壓垮。"},{"label":"7. Example","english":"That is why a technically brilliant manager can still fall short. They may spot the issue quickly enough, yet if they cannot build trust or create momentum, the team stalls. By the same token, a manager who is clear, calm, and consistent can often get more done with less friction.","chinese":"這也是為甚麼有些技術上非常出色的管理者，最後仍然帶不好團隊。他們也許很快就能看出問題，但如果無法建立信任，或者無法帶出動能，團隊仍然會卡住。相反，一位清晰、冷靜而且穩定的管理者，往往能以更少的摩擦做成更多事情。"},{"label":"8. Conclusion 2","english":"All told, if you strip management back to its bones, it comes down to three things: sound judgment, clear communication, and disciplined execution. Everything else matters, of course, but those three are the engine room. If they are weak, the whole machine starts to wobble.","chinese":"總結來說，如果把管理拆到最核心的骨架，它其實歸結為三件事：穩健的判斷、清晰的溝通，以及有紀律的執行。其他能力當然也重要，但這三項才是真正的引擎室。一旦它們弱下來，整部機器就會開始搖晃。"}],"vocabulary":[]},"business-english-standard-response-book-1-q4":{"exerciseId":"business-english-standard-response-book-1-q4","essayKey":"","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=business-english-standard-response-book-1-q4","flashDeckId":"","paragraphs":[{"label":"1. Idea","english":"Micromanagement usually creates three major problems: it weakens trust, slows execution, and reduces ownership.","chinese":"微觀管理通常會帶來三個主要問題：削弱信任、拖慢執行，以及降低責任感。"},{"label":"2. Explanation","english":"When a manager checks every tiny detail, people start to feel second-guessed rather than supported. That quickly drains confidence. Instead of thinking independently, employees wait for approval, play it safe, and stop taking initiative. The manager then becomes a bottleneck, so even simple decisions take longer than they should.","chinese":"當一位管理者連每一個小細節都要盯緊，員工感受到的往往不是支持，而是不被信任、處處被懷疑。這很快就會消磨他們的信心。員工不再主動思考，而是凡事等批准、走最保守的路，也不再主動出擊。到最後，管理者自己反而變成了瓶頸，令本來很簡單的決定都要花更久時間。"},{"label":"3. Example","english":"For example, if a team leader rewrites every email, approves every minor change, and questions every small decision, the team may still look busy, but real progress slows to a crawl. People spend more time managing upwards than solving real problems.","chinese":"例如，如果一位主管連每一封電郵都要改、每一個小改動都要批、每一個小決定都要追問，團隊表面上可能看起來很忙，但真正的進度卻會慢得像爬行一樣。大家花在「向上管理」的時間，可能比真正解決問題的時間還多。"},{"label":"4. Conclusion","english":"So, in practical terms, micromanagement may reduce small short-term risks, but it often creates much bigger long-term costs: lower morale, slower work, and weaker accountability.","chinese":"所以，從實際角度來看，微觀管理也許能減少一些短期的小風險，但它往往會製造更大的長期代價：士氣更低、工作更慢，以及問責更弱。"},{"label":"5. Idea 2","english":"On top of that, micromanagement can quietly damage innovation and retention.","chinese":"除此之外，微觀管理還會在不知不覺間傷害創新能力和人才留任。"},{"label":"6. Explanation 2","english":"When people feel watched at every turn, they usually stop speaking up. They avoid bold ideas, hide small mistakes, and stick to the safest possible option. Over time, capable employees feel boxed in and disengaged, and some eventually walk away. In that sense, micromanagement does not just control work; it shrinks the room people need in order to do their best work.","chinese":"當員工覺得自己每一步都被盯著看時，他們通常就不再願意多說、不再願意主動表達。他們會避開大膽的想法、掩飾小錯誤，並且只選最安全的做法。久而久之，有能力的員工會覺得自己被困住、慢慢失去投入感，有些人最後甚至會選擇離開。從這個角度來看，微觀管理不只是控制工作；它其實是在壓縮員工發揮最佳表現所需要的空間。"},{"label":"7. Example 2","english":"A strong employee in marketing, operations, or product development may have sharp ideas, but if every move is picked apart, that person will soon stop going the extra mile. They will do the job, but they will stop bringing their best judgment to it.","chinese":"一位在市場推廣、營運或產品開發方面本來很有想法的員工，起初也許會提出不少好點子；但如果他做的每一步都被過度挑剔，那麼他很快就不會再願意多走一步。他會把工作做完，但不再把自己最好的判斷力和心力帶進工作裡。"},{"label":"8. Conclusion 2","english":"Overall, micromanagement creates a fragile team: people become dependent, managers become overloaded, and performance loses momentum. That said, close guidance can still be useful when someone is new, when the stakes are unusually high, or when a team is in crisis. The key is to provide direction without choking initiative.","chinese":"總結來說，微觀管理會造成一個脆弱的團隊：員工變得依賴、管理者變得過載，而整體表現也會失去動能。不過，當一個人是新手、事情風險特別高，或者團隊正處於危機時，更密切的指導仍然可能有用。關鍵不在於放任不管，而是在提供方向的同時，不要扼殺主動性。"}],"vocabulary":[]},"business-english-standard-response-book-1-q5":{"exerciseId":"business-english-standard-response-book-1-q5","essayKey":"","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=business-english-standard-response-book-1-q5","flashDeckId":"","paragraphs":[{"label":"1. Idea","english":"If I had to give one clean answer, I’d say consumers usually come in through function, choose through feeling, and stay through identity.","chinese":"如果要我給一個乾淨俐落的答案，我會說，消費者通常是因功能而走進來，因感受而作出選擇，並因身份認同而留下來。"},{"label":"2. Explanation","english":"At the most basic level, a product has to do the job. If it fails on quality, reliability, or convenience, the rest is just window dressing. That said, once the functional baseline is in place, emotion starts to carry real weight. People are drawn to what feels reassuring, elegant, exciting, safe, or enjoyable. Beyond that, the strongest brands tap into identity: they help customers express who they are, or perhaps who they aspire to be. Put simply, function gets a brand onto the shortlist, but feeling and identity often tip the decision.","chinese":"在最基本的層面，一件產品首先必須把事情做好。如果它在品質、可靠性或便利性上站不住腳，其他包裝其實都只是表面工夫。不過，一旦功能底線已經到位，情感就開始真正發揮分量。人們往往會被那些令人安心、優雅、興奮、安全，或者愉悅的東西吸引。再進一步說，最強的品牌還會觸及身份認同：它們幫助顧客表達自己是怎樣的人，或者想成為怎樣的人。簡單來說，功能讓品牌進入候選名單，但感受和身份認同，往往才是最後推動決定的力量。"},{"label":"3. Example","english":"Take smartphones, for instance. Most major brands are already good enough on the basic functions, so the decision often shifts from “Can it work?” to “How does it feel to use, own, and be seen with it?” That helps explain why a brand like Apple is not selling hardware alone; it is also selling simplicity, taste, and a certain sense of self.","chinese":"以智能手機為例，大多數主要品牌在基本功能上其實都已經「夠用」了，所以決策重心往往會從「它能不能用？」轉向「用起來感覺如何、擁有它感覺如何、被別人看見時又代表甚麼？」這也正好說明了，像 Apple 這樣的品牌賣的並不只是硬件；它同時也在賣簡潔感、品味，以及某種自我形象。"},{"label":"4. Conclusion","english":"Seen in that light, consumers are rarely buying just one thing. On the surface, they may be paying for function, but underneath that, the purchase is often emotional and symbolic as well.","chinese":"從這個角度看，消費者其實很少只是在買單一樣東西。表面上，他們也許是在為功能付款；但更深一層來說，那筆購買往往同時帶有情感和象徵意義。"},{"label":"5. Idea 2","english":"Even so, the balance shifts from category to category, so the real answer depends on what is being sold and what is at stake.","chinese":"即便如此，三者的比重也會因品類而變，所以真正答案仍然取決於賣的是甚麼，以及風險有多高。"},{"label":"6. Explanation 2","english":"In practical, high-stakes, or technical categories, function tends to carry more weight. Nobody wants medicine, financial services, or cybersecurity that sounds impressive but falls apart when it matters. By contrast, in fashion, beauty, hospitality, or premium consumer goods, feeling and identity often move much closer to the centre. In fact, the more interchangeable the function becomes, the more brand meaning starts to matter.","chinese":"在實用型、高風險，或者技術性較強的品類裡，功能通常會佔更重的分量。沒有人會想要那種聽起來很厲害、但關鍵時刻卻掉鏈子的藥物、金融服務或網絡安全方案。相反，在時尚、美妝、酒店服務，或者高端消費品這些領域，感受和身份認同往往就更接近核心位置。事實上，當功能越來越容易被替代時，品牌意義就會變得越來越重要。"},{"label":"7. Example","english":"A bottle of pain relief is bought first for effectiveness. A luxury watch, on the other hand, is bought just as much for what it says. A brand like Nike sits somewhere in the middle: the product still has to perform, of course, but the brand also sells aspiration, confidence, and belonging.","chinese":"一瓶止痛藥，首先是因為有效才會被買下來。相對地，一隻名錶被購買，很大程度上也在於它「說明了甚麼」。像 Nike 這樣的品牌則處於中間位置：產品當然仍然要有表現，但品牌同時也在賣向上追求、自信，以及歸屬感。"},{"label":"8. Conclusion 2","english":"All told, I would not frame it as function or feeling or identity. It is more like a ladder. Function earns credibility, feeling creates preference, and identity builds loyalty. The brands that truly win are the ones that can cover all three, rather than putting all their chips on just one.","chinese":"總結來說，我不會把它理解成「功能、感受、身份認同三選一」。它更像是一道階梯：功能建立可信度，感受創造偏好，而身份認同培養忠誠。真正能贏的品牌，往往是三者都能兼顧，而不是把所有籌碼都押在其中一項上。"}],"vocabulary":[]},"business-english-standard-response-book-1-q6":{"exerciseId":"business-english-standard-response-book-1-q6","essayKey":"","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=business-english-standard-response-book-1-q6","flashDeckId":"","paragraphs":[{"label":"1. Response Part 1","english":"If I had to choose, I’d say the more important strategic question is usually what not to do.","chinese":"如果一定要我選，我會說更重要的策略問題通常是「不做甚麼」。"},{"label":"2. Response Part 2","english":"The reason is quite simple: strategy is not just about chasing opportunities; it is about making disciplined choices. Every company has limited time, capital, talent, and management attention. If a business tries to do everything, it spreads itself too thin, loses focus, and ends up being busy rather than effective. In that sense, what not to do is where real strategy begins, because it separates priority from distraction.","chinese":"原因其實很簡單：策略不只是追逐機會，更是有紀律地作出取捨。每一家公司都有有限的時間、資金、人才，以及管理層的注意力。如果一間企業甚麼都想做，它就很容易把資源攤得太薄、失去焦點，最後變成看起來很忙，卻未必真的有效。從這個角度來看，「不做甚麼」其實正是策略真正開始的地方，因為它把優先事項和分心因素分開了。"},{"label":"3. Response Part 3","english":"For example, a company may turn down an attractive partnership, drop a weak product line, or stop pursuing a market that looks exciting but does not fit its core strengths. Those decisions can feel uncomfortable in the short term, but they often protect focus and sharpen execution. That is why strong strategy is often less about adding more and more, and more about cutting with precision.","chinese":"例如，一間公司可能會拒絕一個看似吸引的合作機會、砍掉表現疲弱的產品線，或者停止追逐一個雖然很有話題性、卻不符合自己核心優勢的市場。這些決定在短期內也許會讓人覺得可惜，但它們往往能保住焦點，並且令執行更有力。這也就是為甚麼強策略很多時候不是一味加法，而是精準地做減法。"},{"label":"4. Response Part 4","english":"So, from a strategic point of view, knowing what not to do usually protects clarity, speed, and competitive edge.","chinese":"所以，從策略角度來看，知道「不做甚麼」往往更能保護清晰度、速度，以及競爭優勢。"},{"label":"5. Response Part 5","english":"That said, I would not say what to do is unimportant. In fact, without a clear direction, saying no to things becomes empty.","chinese":"不過，我也不會說「做甚麼」不重要。事實上，如果沒有清楚的方向，那麼對很多事情說不，其實也會變得空泛。"},{"label":"6. Response Part 6","english":"A business still needs a strong positive choice: which customers to serve, what value to create, and where it wants to win. In other words, what to do sets the destination, while what not to do protects the route. One gives direction; the other gives focus. The strongest strategies need both, but the harder and more defining discipline is often the ability to say no.","chinese":"一間企業始終還是需要一個明確而正面的選擇：要服務哪些客戶、要創造甚麼價值，以及要在哪裡取勝。換句話說，「做甚麼」決定目的地，而「不做甚麼」保護前進路線。前者提供方向，後者提供焦點。最強的策略其實兩者都需要，但更困難、也更能定義策略功力的，往往是說不的能力。"},{"label":"7. Response Part 7","english":"For instance, an early-stage company may need to explore several options before it knows where its real edge lies. At that stage, deciding what to do may matter more. But once the direction becomes clearer, disciplined restraint becomes critical; otherwise, the company can drift, dilute its brand, and burn energy in too many directions at once.","chinese":"例如，一間早期階段的公司在真正看清自己的優勢之前，可能需要探索幾個不同方向。在那個階段，先決定「做甚麼」也許會更重要。不過，一旦方向開始清晰，有紀律的克制就會變得非常關鍵；否則，公司很容易失焦、稀釋品牌，並且把精力同時耗在太多方向上。"},{"label":"8. Response Part 8","english":"Overall, I’d say strategy is built on both choice and sacrifice, but if a company wants to stay sharp, the more decisive question is often what not to do. After all, strategy is not just about opening doors; it is also about having the judgment to close the wrong ones.","chinese":"總結來說，我會說策略是建立在選擇與取捨之上的；但如果一間公司想保持銳利，那麼更關鍵的問題往往是「不做甚麼」。畢竟，策略不只是打開門，更在於有判斷力去關掉不該走的門。"}],"vocabulary":[]},"business-english-standard-response-book-1-q7":{"exerciseId":"business-english-standard-response-book-1-q7","essayKey":"","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=business-english-standard-response-book-1-q7","flashDeckId":"","paragraphs":[{"label":"1. Response Part 1","english":"If I had to give one answer, I’d say it is usually a management problem first, even when it looks like a process or talent problem on the surface.","chinese":"如果一定要我只給一個答案，我會說通常首先是管理問題，即使表面上看起來像流程問題或人才問題。"},{"label":"2. Response Part 2","english":"The reason is that management sets direction, priorities, accountability, and operating rhythm. If those things are weak, even strong people and reasonable processes can break down. Teams become unclear about who owns what, decisions move too slowly, and work starts slipping through the cracks. In other words, poor execution is often less about people not working hard, and more about the system around them not giving them a clear path to perform well.","chinese":"原因在於，管理層決定方向、優先次序、問責方式，以及整體運作節奏。如果這些東西本身不夠強，即使有不錯的人才和還算合理的流程，也一樣可能失靈。團隊會開始不清楚誰負責甚麼，決策推進太慢，工作也會一件一件從縫隙中漏掉。換句話說，執行力差很多時候不是因為員工不努力，而是因為他們所處的整個運作系統沒有給他們一條清晰的路去把事情做好。"},{"label":"3. Response Part 3","english":"For example, a company may have smart employees and detailed procedures, but if leaders keep changing priorities, avoid hard decisions, or fail to hold people accountable, execution will still be messy. Meetings multiply, follow-up weakens, and deadlines start to drift. At that point, blaming the team is often missing the main point.","chinese":"例如，一間公司可能擁有聰明的員工，也有很詳細的程序，但如果領導層不斷改變優先事項、迴避困難決定，或者沒有真正做好問責，那麼執行仍然會很混亂。會議愈開愈多，跟進卻愈來愈弱，截止日期也開始一再往後滑。到了這個時候，單純怪罪團隊，往往就是抓錯重點。"},{"label":"4. Response Part 4","english":"So, in many cases, management is the master lever, because it shapes how process and talent actually work in practice.","chinese":"所以，在很多情況下，管理其實是最關鍵的總槓桿，因為它決定了流程和人才在實際上能否真正發揮作用。"},{"label":"5. Response Part 5","english":"That said, I would not say process and talent are secondary in every case. Sometimes they are the immediate cause, even if management is the deeper one.","chinese":"不過，我也不會說流程和人才在每一種情況下都只是次要因素。有時候，它們確實是最直接的問題，即使更深層的原因仍然來自管理。"},{"label":"6. Response Part 6","english":"If the process is bloated, slow, or full of unnecessary approvals, execution can stall even with capable people. Likewise, if the company has the wrong people in key roles, no amount of structure will fully save performance. A weak manager can create confusion, but an outdated process can create friction, and a poor hire can create drag. That is why strong diagnosis matters: the visible symptom and the root cause are not always the same thing.","chinese":"如果流程本身過於肥大、太慢，或者充滿不必要的審批，即使團隊有能力，執行也可能卡住。同樣地，如果公司在關鍵位置放錯了人，再好的架構也未必救得回表現。弱的管理者會製造混亂，過時的流程會製造摩擦，而錯的人選則會拖慢整個團隊。這也就是為甚麼準確診斷很重要：表面症狀和真正根源，不一定是同一件事。"},{"label":"7. Response Part 7","english":"For instance, if sales keeps missing targets, the problem could be poor coaching from managers, but it could also be a broken approval flow, unclear pricing authority, or a team that simply lacks the commercial skills for the role. The smart question is not “Who do we blame?” but “Where is execution losing force?”","chinese":"例如，如果銷售團隊一直達不到目標，問題可能是管理者帶隊和指導做得不好，但也可能是審批流程失靈、定價權限不清，或者團隊本身根本缺乏這個職位所需要的商業能力。真正聰明的問題不是「應該怪誰」，而是「執行力到底在哪一個環節開始流失」。"},{"label":"8. Response Part 8","english":"Overall, I’d say poor execution is usually diagnosed as a process or talent issue, but more often than not, it traces back to management. Good management brings clarity, discipline, and follow-through. Without those, the process becomes paperwork, and talent becomes wasted potential.","chinese":"總結來說，我會說，執行力差表面上常常被診斷成流程問題或人才問題，但很多時候，追根究底還是會回到管理問題。好的管理能帶來清晰度、紀律，以及真正落地的跟進。沒有這些，流程就只會變成文書工作，而人才也只會變成被浪費的潛力。"}],"vocabulary":[]},"business-english-standard-response-book-1-q8":{"exerciseId":"business-english-standard-response-book-1-q8","essayKey":"","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=business-english-standard-response-book-1-q8","flashDeckId":"","paragraphs":[{"label":"1. Idea","english":"In most cases, I would say no — not unless the value they bring clearly outweighs the disruption they create.","chinese":"在大多數情況下，我會說不應該——除非他帶來的價值，明顯大於他製造的破壞。"},{"label":"2. Explanation","english":"At first glance, raw ability can look irresistible. A brilliant candidate may seem like a shortcut to stronger results. The trouble is that business is rarely a solo sport. Once someone is hard to work with, their talent can come with hidden costs: slower collaboration, weaker trust, lower morale, and constant friction. In other words, a high performer can still be a bad hire if they poison the well around them.","chinese":"乍看之下，純粹的能力確實很吸引。一位非常出色的候選人，看起來好像能成為快速提升表現的捷徑。但問題在於，商業世界很少是單打獨鬥的遊戲。一旦某個人很難合作，他的才能往往就會夾帶隱藏成本：協作變慢、信任削弱、士氣下降，以及持續不斷的摩擦。換句話說，一個高表現者，仍然可能是一個糟糕的聘用決定，因為他會把周圍的環境搞壞。"},{"label":"3. Example","english":"Picture a senior salesperson who brings in big numbers but undermines colleagues, hoards information, and creates tension at every meeting. On paper, that person looks like an asset. In practice, they can burn management time, push good people out, and leave the team walking on eggshells. That is a very expensive kind of brilliance.","chinese":"試想像一位高級業務員，他的業績很亮眼，卻經常拆同事台、把資訊收起來不共享，而且每次開會都搞到氣氛緊張。從紙面上看，這個人像是一項資產；但在現實裡，他可能會消耗管理層大量時間、逼走優秀同事，並讓整個團隊如履薄冰。那其實是一種代價非常高的「聰明」。"},{"label":"4. Conclusion","english":"So, by and large, I would not hire for talent alone. If someone lifts results but drags down the team, the business may still come out behind.","chinese":"所以，整體而言，我不會只因為能力強就聘用一個人。如果一個人提升了表面結果，卻拖垮了整個團隊，那麼企業最後仍然可能是得不償失。"},{"label":"5. Idea 2","english":"That said, I would not rule it out completely, because there are rare situations where the answer could be yes.","chinese":"不過，我也不會完全排除這種可能，因為在少數情況下，答案也可以是「可以」。"},{"label":"6. Explanation 2","english":"A more defensible case would be a highly specialised role, especially when the work is less interdependent, the expectations are crystal clear, and the manager is strong enough to set hard boundaries. Even then, the company should go in with its eyes open. The key question is not “Is this person talented?” but “Can this talent be contained, directed, and made useful without tearing the fabric of the team?” If the answer is no, then the hire is a gamble.","chinese":"比較站得住腳的情況，會是某種高度專業化的角色，尤其當工作本身對跨部門合作依賴較低、要求非常清晰，而且主管也夠強，能夠設下明確界線。即使如此，公司也必須睜大眼睛去看。關鍵問題不在於「這個人有沒有才華」，而在於「這份才華能否被妥善管理、清楚引導，並在不撕裂團隊的前提下發揮價值？」如果答案是否定的，那這個聘用就是一場賭博。"},{"label":"7. Example","english":"Say a company needs a rare technical expert for a short, high-impact project. If the role is tightly scoped, the reporting line is firm, and the behavioural standards are spelled out from day one, the risk may be manageable. Even so, I would treat that as a controlled exception, not a hiring philosophy.","chinese":"假設一家公司因一個短期但影響很大的項目，需要一位極罕有的技術專家。如果那個職位的範圍被清楚界定、匯報線很明確，而且從第一天開始就把行為標準講清楚，那麼風險或許是可控的。即便如此，我也只會把這視為一個受控例外，而不是一種長期招聘理念。"},{"label":"8. Conclusion 2","english":"All things considered, I would say companies should hire not just for horsepower, but for fit, trust, and team effect. A sharp mind is valuable, of course, but if it comes with sharp elbows, the cost can spread fast. Talent may win attention; character decides whether the win lasts.","chinese":"總結來說，我會說，公司招聘時不應只看「馬力」，也應看匹配度、信任感，以及對整個團隊的影響。敏銳的頭腦當然有價值，但如果同時帶著強烈的攻擊性和難合作的個性，代價往往會迅速擴散。才華也許能贏得注意，但真正決定勝負能否持久的，還是品格。"}],"vocabulary":[]},"business-english-standard-response-book-1-q9":{"exerciseId":"business-english-standard-response-book-1-q9","essayKey":"","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=business-english-standard-response-book-1-q9","flashDeckId":"","paragraphs":[{"label":"1. Idea","english":"Not necessarily. High profit is a strong signal, but it is not a full health check.","chinese":"不一定。高利潤是一個強烈訊號，但它並不是一份完整的健康檢查。"},{"label":"2. Explanation","english":"The trouble is that profit shows one outcome, whereas business health is a much bigger picture. A company can post impressive profits and still have weak cash flow, heavy debt, overreliance on one customer, exhausted staff, or a product line that is quietly losing steam. On top of that, profits can be boosted for a season by raising prices aggressively, cutting too deep, or delaying investment. In other words, the numbers may sparkle, but the foundations may already be cracking.","chinese":"問題在於，利潤反映的只是一個結果，而企業健康其實是一幅更大的全景圖。一家公司即使交出亮眼利潤，仍然可能同時存在現金流薄弱、債務沉重、過度依賴單一客戶、員工過勞，或者產品線正在悄悄失去動能等問題。除此之外，利潤有時也可以靠短期手段被推高，例如激進加價、過度削成本，或者延後必要投資。數字也許很亮，但地基可能早已開始出現裂痕。"},{"label":"3. Example","english":"Take a company that slashes training, freezes hiring, and cuts maintenance to lift earnings this year. On paper, the profit looks superb. In reality, service quality may slip, good people may walk, and future growth may dry up. That is the business version of painting over damp walls: it looks tidy for a while, but the problem is still there.","chinese":"例如，一家公司為了推高今年盈利，大幅削減培訓、凍結招聘，並壓低維修開支。從帳面上看，利潤非常漂亮；但在現實裡，服務質素可能會下滑，優秀員工可能會離開，未來增長也可能慢慢枯萎。這就像把潮濕的牆面重新粉飾一樣：一時之間看起來很整齊，但問題其實還在。"},{"label":"4. Conclusion","english":"Seen that way, high profit can mean strength, but by itself it does not prove health. Profit is a snapshot, not the whole film.","chinese":"從這個角度看，高利潤可以代表實力，但單靠它本身並不能證明企業健康。利潤像一張照片，而不是整部影片。"},{"label":"5. Idea 2","english":"Still, it would be wrong to say profit does not matter. In fact, strong profit becomes very meaningful when it is backed by the right fundamentals.","chinese":"不過，若因此說利潤不重要，那也不對。事實上，當高利潤背後有正確的基本面支撐時，它就非常有意義。"},{"label":"6. Explanation 2","english":"What matters, then, is the quality of the profit. If earnings are recurring, cash-backed, supported by loyal customers, sensible debt levels, and ongoing reinvestment, that is a far healthier picture. In that case, profit is not just a headline number; it is evidence of a business model with real muscle and staying power.","chinese":"因此，真正重要的是利潤的「質素」。如果盈利是可持續、能重複出現的，有現金支持的，而且建立在忠誠客戶、合理債務水平，以及持續再投資之上，那就會是一幅健康得多的圖像。在那種情況下，利潤就不只是一個標題數字，而是商業模式具備真正實力與持久力的證據。"},{"label":"7. Example","english":"Think of a firm with steady repeat business, healthy cash flow, disciplined spending, and enough room to invest in people and products. There, high profit is not smoke and mirrors; it usually reflects a business that is genuinely well run.","chinese":"可以想像一間公司，它擁有穩定的回頭生意、穩健的現金流、紀律良好的開支控制，並且仍有空間投資在人和產品上。在這種情況下，高利潤就不是障眼法，而通常反映這是一門真正被經營得很扎實的生意。"},{"label":"8. Conclusion 2","english":"All told, high profit is a clue, not a verdict. A healthy company is not merely one that makes money today, but one that can keep making money tomorrow without hollowing itself out.","chinese":"總結來說，高利潤是一條線索，但不是最終判決。真正健康的公司，不只是今天賺得到錢的公司，而是明天仍能持續賺錢，同時又不會把自己慢慢掏空的公司。"}],"vocabulary":[]},"business-english-standard-response-book-1-q10":{"exerciseId":"business-english-standard-response-book-1-q10","essayKey":"","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=business-english-standard-response-book-1-q10","flashDeckId":"","paragraphs":[{"label":"1. Response Part 1","english":"In my view, the biggest reason is that companies like the upside of innovation, but fear the downside of change.","chinese":"在我看來，最大的原因是，企業喜歡創新可能帶來的上升空間，卻害怕改變所附帶的下行風險。"},{"label":"2. Response Part 2","english":"Innovation sounds exciting in principle because it suggests growth, relevance, and competitive edge. However, in practice, real innovation is disruptive. It costs money, creates uncertainty, slows people down in the short term, and sometimes threatens the very systems that currently make the business profitable. That is why many firms praise innovation in meetings and slide decks, but become cautious the moment it starts touching budgets, power structures, or quarterly targets. Put simply, they want the fruit, but not always the shake of the tree.","chinese":"創新在原則上聽起來很吸引，因為它代表增長、競爭力，以及不被時代拋下。不過，真正的創新在實際上往往帶有破壞性。它要花錢、會帶來不確定性、短期內會拖慢節奏，有時甚至會威脅到目前正為公司賺錢的那套系統。這就是為甚麼很多企業在會議和簡報裡都大談創新，但一旦創新真的碰到預算、權力結構，或者季度業績目標時，就立刻變得保守。說白一點，他們想要果實，卻未必真的想承受搖樹的震動。"},{"label":"3. Response Part 3","english":"For example, a company may say it wants fresh ideas, but when a team proposes a new product, a different pricing model, or a faster digital process, the response is often, “Let’s study it further,” “This is not the right time,” or “What if it affects the core business?” On the surface, that sounds prudent. In reality, it can be a polished way of saying no.","chinese":"例如，一間公司可能口頭上說自己歡迎新想法，但當團隊真的提出新產品、不同的定價模式，或者更快的數碼流程時，常見回應往往是：「我們再研究一下」、「現在不是最合適的時機」，或者「如果影響到核心業務怎麼辦？」表面上，這些說法聽起來很審慎；但實際上，它有時只是比較包裝得體的拒絕。"},{"label":"4. Response Part 4","english":"So, very often, the gap between talk and action comes down to incentives: people are rewarded for protecting results, not for disturbing them.","chinese":"所以，很多時候，企業嘴上說創新、行動上卻保守，關鍵就在於激勵機制：人們得到獎勵，往往是因為守住業績，而不是因為打破現狀。"},{"label":"5. Response Part 5","english":"On top of that, large organisations tend to become conservative because size brings layers, and layers bring friction.","chinese":"除此之外，大型組織之所以容易變保守，還有一個原因：規模一大，層級就會變多；層級一多，摩擦也會跟著增加。"},{"label":"6. Response Part 6","english":"The more approvals, stakeholders, and reporting lines a company has, the harder it becomes to move with speed and conviction. New ideas are often watered down, delayed, or pushed into endless review. At the same time, middle managers may be especially cautious, because they are expected to deliver results without making visible mistakes. In that environment, safe choices look sensible, while bold choices start to feel career-limiting. In other words, the organisation may speak the language of innovation, but emotionally it is still wired for control.","chinese":"一間公司愈多審批、愈多持份者、愈多匯報線，想要快速而果斷地推動新想法就愈困難。很多新點子最後不是被稀釋，就是被拖延，或者被送進沒完沒了的檢討程序裡。與此同時，中層管理者往往特別謹慎，因為他們被要求交出成果，卻又不能犯下太明顯的錯誤。在這種環境下，安全選擇看起來就很合理，而大膽選擇反而開始像是在拿自己的職涯冒險。換句話說，整個組織嘴巴上講的是創新，但情感和本能上仍然是為了控制而設計的。"},{"label":"7. Response Part 7","english":"A good example would be a company that sets up an “innovation task force” but gives it little budget, little authority, and no real protection from short-term performance pressure. That team may produce ideas, but without backing, those ideas rarely leave the whiteboard. Innovation then becomes theatre rather than transformation.","chinese":"一個很好的例子，就是公司成立了一個所謂的「創新小組」，但給它的預算很少、權限很弱，也沒有真正替它擋住短期業績壓力。那個團隊也許能想出不少點子，但如果沒有真正支持，這些點子通常很難走出白板。到了最後，創新就變成一場表演，而不是真正的轉變。"},{"label":"8. Response Part 8","english":"Overall, I’d say companies often sound innovative because the market rewards that language, but they behave conservatively because their incentives, structures, and fears pull in the opposite direction. Real innovation only happens when a business is willing not just to praise new ideas, but to fund them, protect them, and live with the discomfort that comes with them.","chinese":"總結來說，我會說，企業之所以常常在口頭上很創新，是因為市場喜歡聽這種語言；但它們在行動上卻很保守，是因為激勵機制、組織結構，以及對風險的恐懼，把它們拉向了相反方向。真正的創新，只有在一間企業不只是稱讚新想法，而是願意為它們投資、保護它們，並且承受創新本身帶來的不舒服時，才真正會發生。"}],"vocabulary":[]},"dse-writing-2012-part-a":{"exerciseId":"dse-writing-2012-part-a","essayKey":"","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=dse-writing-2012-part-a","flashDeckId":"dse/writing/part-a/2012","paragraphs":[{"label":"Title","english":"Chasing Truth, Not Headlines","chinese":"追求真相，而不是追逐標題"},{"label":"The best part of my job","english":"The best part of my job","chinese":"我工作中最美好的部分"},{"label":"The best part of my job","english":"Reporting has taken me from subdivided flats to international summits. Yet the greatest privilege is not interviewing celebrities; it is earning ordinary people’s trust. When someone shares a story others have ignored, I can carry that voice beyond one room and, occasionally, prompt real change. A reporter has a front-row seat to history—and a duty to record it honestly.","chinese":"新聞報道工作曾帶我從劏房走到國際峰會。 然而，最大的榮幸並不是訪問名人，而是贏得普通人的信任。 當有人分享一個被其他人忽略的故事時，我能夠把那把聲音帶出一個房間之外，並偶爾促成真正的改變。 記者能夠坐在歷史前排見證時代，也有責任誠實地記錄它。"},{"label":"The biggest challenge I have ever faced in my job","english":"The biggest challenge I have ever faced in my job","chinese":"我工作中曾面對過的最大挑戰"},{"label":"The biggest challenge I have ever faced in my job","english":"While I was covering a devastating earthquake in Sichuan, aftershocks shook the ground beneath us. The danger was frightening; interviewing grieving families was harder. One mother held a dusty schoolbag and asked me to tell Hong Kong about her son. I checked every fact and let her speak in her own words, without asking intrusive questions. Only then did I understand that accuracy without humanity is not enough.","chinese":"當我報道四川一場嚴重地震時，餘震搖晃着我們腳下的土地。 危險令人恐懼；但訪問悲痛的家庭更加艱難。 一位母親拿着一個滿是塵土的書包，請我把她兒子的故事告訴香港。 我核實每一項事實，並讓她用自己的說話表達，而沒有提出冒犯性的問題。 直到那一刻，我才明白，只有準確而缺乏人情味是不足夠的。"},{"label":"My school days","english":"My school days","chinese":"我的求學時光"},{"label":"My school days","english":"My career began here, with the school magazine. My first article came back covered in red ink, but my English teacher wrote, “Keep asking why.” I did. Those words still guide every investigation.","chinese":"我的事業就是從這裏、從校刊開始的。 我第一篇文章被改得滿是紅筆痕跡，但我的英文老師寫下了：「Keep asking why.」 我照做了。 那些說話至今仍然指引着我的每一次調查。"},{"label":"A word to future reporters","english":"A word to future reporters","chinese":"給未來記者的一句話"},{"label":"A word to future reporters","english":"Stay curious, but verify before publishing. Above all, never turn another person’s pain into entertainment. A microphone can amplify a voice, but it is integrity that gives it value.","chinese":"保持好奇，但在發布之前必須核實。 最重要的是，永遠不要把別人的痛苦變成娛樂。 咪高峰可以放大一把聲音，但真正賦予它價值的，是誠信。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"chase truth, not headlines","chinese":"追求真相，而不是追逐標題"},{"english":"the best part of my job","chinese":"我工作中最美好的部分"},{"english":"reporting","chinese":"新聞報道工作"},{"english":"take someone from ... to ...","chinese":"帶某人由……走到……"},{"english":"subdivided flats","chinese":"劏房"},{"english":"international summits","chinese":"國際峰會"},{"english":"the greatest privilege","chinese":"最大的榮幸"},{"english":"interview celebrities","chinese":"訪問名人"},{"english":"earn someone's trust","chinese":"贏得某人的信任"},{"english":"ordinary people","chinese":"普通人"},{"english":"share a story","chinese":"分享一個故事"},{"english":"others have ignored","chinese":"其他人忽略了的"},{"english":"carry that voice beyond one room","chinese":"將那把聲音帶出一個房間之外"},{"english":"beyond one room","chinese":"超越一個房間的範圍"},{"english":"occasionally","chinese":"偶爾"},{"english":"prompt real change","chinese":"促成真正改變"},{"english":"have a front-row seat to history","chinese":"近距離見證歷史"},{"english":"a duty to","chinese":"有責任去……"},{"english":"record it honestly","chinese":"誠實地記錄它"},{"english":"the biggest challenge I have ever faced","chinese":"我曾面對過的最大挑戰"},{"english":"cover an earthquake","chinese":"採訪地震"},{"english":"devastating earthquake","chinese":"災情嚴重的地震"},{"english":"aftershocks","chinese":"餘震"},{"english":"shake the ground beneath us","chinese":"震動我們腳下的地面"},{"english":"beneath us","chinese":"在我們腳下"},{"english":"the danger was frightening","chinese":"危險令人恐懼"},{"english":"grieving families","chinese":"悲痛的家庭"},{"english":"hold a dusty schoolbag","chinese":"拿着一個滿是灰塵的書包"},{"english":"tell Hong Kong about","chinese":"向香港講述……"},{"english":"check every fact","chinese":"核實每一項事實"},{"english":"let someone speak","chinese":"讓某人發聲"},{"english":"in her own words","chinese":"用她自己的說話"},{"english":"intrusive questions","chinese":"冒犯私隱的問題"},{"english":"only then","chinese":"直到那時才"},{"english":"accuracy without humanity","chinese":"沒有人性的準確並不足夠"},{"english":"not enough","chinese":"並不足夠"},{"english":"school days","chinese":"學生時代"},{"english":"career began here","chinese":"事業從這裏開始"},{"english":"school magazine","chinese":"校刊"},{"english":"come back covered in red ink","chinese":"被紅筆改得滿篇都是"},{"english":"covered in red ink","chinese":"滿是紅筆批改"},{"english":"keep asking why","chinese":"不斷追問原因"},{"english":"guide every investigation","chinese":"指引每一次調查"},{"english":"investigation","chinese":"調查"},{"english":"a word to future reporters","chinese":"給未來記者的一句話"},{"english":"stay curious","chinese":"保持好奇心"},{"english":"verify before publishing","chinese":"發表前先核實"},{"english":"above all","chinese":"最重要的是"},{"english":"turn someone's pain into entertainment","chinese":"將他人的痛苦變成娛樂"},{"english":"microphone","chinese":"麥克風"},{"english":"amplify a voice","chinese":"放大一把聲音"},{"english":"integrity","chinese":"誠信；操守"},{"english":"give something value","chinese":"賦予……價值"}]},"dse-writing-2012-part-b-q2":{"exerciseId":"dse-writing-2012-part-b-q2","essayKey":"","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=dse-writing-2012-part-b-q2","flashDeckId":"dse/writing/part-b/2012/Q2","paragraphs":[{"label":"Paragraph 1","english":"Virtual Sports Can Open the Door — But Real Sports Keep Us Moving","chinese":"虛擬運動可以打開大門——但實體運動讓我們持續動起來。"},{"label":"Paragraph 2","english":"Posted by: Chris","chinese":"發帖者：Chris"},{"label":"Paragraph 3","english":"I have been following this debate with interest, and I think we are asking the wrong question. The issue is not whether virtual sports, such as Wii tennis, are “real” enough to deserve respect; it is whether they can improve our health in a way that lasts. Since many teenagers spend long hours revising, commuting and scrolling, people are considering virtual sports as less intimidating exercise, so that those who would otherwise stay on the sofa can start moving. As far as I am concerned, virtual sports are useful as a doorway into fitness, but they should not be treated as a replacement for real sports. They widen access and motivation, but real sports develop the body, mind and character more deeply.","chinese":"我一直很有興趣地關注這場辯論，而且我認為我們問錯了問題。 重點不在於虛擬運動，例如 Wii 網球，是否「真實」到值得被尊重；重點在於它們能否以持久的方式改善我們的健康。 由於許多青少年長時間溫習、通勤和滑手機，人們開始把虛擬運動視為較不令人卻步的運動方式，好讓那些原本會留在沙發上的人開始動起來。 就我而言，虛擬運動可以作為通往健身的一道門，但不應被視為實體運動的替代品。 它們能擴大參與機會，也能提升動機，但實體運動能更深入地培養身體、心智和品格。"},{"label":"Paragraph 4","english":"First, virtual sports deserve credit - they lower the barrier to exercise. Not everyone has a basketball court downstairs, a free afternoon, or the confidence to join a team where stronger players may judge them. A Wii game, by contrast, can turn a small living room into a tennis court, a bowling alley or a boxing ring. A shy student who avoids PE may be willing to swing a controller at home; a grandparent who cannot run safely outdoors may still enjoy virtual bowling with grandchildren. What virtual sports lack in authenticity, they make up for in accessibility. More importantly, their points, levels and instant feedback can make movement addictive. When a game records your best score and asks you to try again, exercise no longer feels like punishment. It becomes play. A perfect fitness plan that nobody follows is no better than a treadmill covered in dust. Virtual sports, therefore, are not a joke; instead, they are a practical starting point.","chinese":"首先，虛擬運動值得肯定——它們降低了運動的門檻。 並非每個人樓下都有籃球場、有空閒的下午，或有信心加入一支較強球員可能會對他們評頭品足的隊伍。 相比之下，一款 Wii 遊戲可以把小客廳變成網球場、保齡球場或拳擊擂台 一位避開體育課的害羞學生，可能願意在家揮動手掣；一位不能安全地在戶外跑步的祖父或祖母，仍可能和孫兒一起享受虛擬保齡球。 虛擬運動在真實感方面有所欠缺，卻以可及性補足了這一點。 更重要的是，它們的分數、關卡和即時回饋，可以令身體活動變得令人欲罷不能。 當遊戲記錄你的最高分並要求你再試一次時，運動便不再像懲罰。 它變成了遊戲。 一個沒有人跟從的完美健身計劃，並不比一部鋪滿灰塵的跑步機好多少。 因此，虛擬運動絕非玩笑；相反，它們是一個實際的起步點。"},{"label":"Paragraph 5","english":"That said, real sports offer a physical challenge that a screen can only imitate. On the face of it, swinging a Wii remote looks like playing tennis. On closer inspection, it is a far cry from chasing a ball across a court, adjusting your footwork, reading your opponent and coping with wind, heat and pressure. In virtual tennis, a quick wrist movement may produce a powerful shot; in real tennis, your legs, core, shoulders, timing and stamina all have to work together. The same applies to basketball, football, swimming or badminton. Real sports force the whole body to respond to space, speed and uncertainty. They build endurance because players must sprint, stop, turn, jump and recover. They sharpen coordination because the body is not merely copying a programmed gesture; it is solving a moving problem. If fitness is the goal, it would be wrong to pretend that pressing buttons and playing matches are equal. Virtual sports may make us move, but real sports make us train.","chinese":"話雖如此，實體運動提供的是螢幕只能模仿的身體挑戰。 表面看來，揮動 Wii 遙控器像是在打網球。 仔細一看，這與在球場上追球、調整步法、讀懂對手，以及應對風、熱和壓力相差甚遠。 在虛擬網球中，快速的手腕動作可能打出一記有力擊球；在真正的網球中，雙腿、核心、肩膀、時機掌握和耐力都必須共同運作。 籃球、足球、游泳或羽毛球亦是如此。 實體運動迫使整個身體回應空間、速度和不確定性。 它們能建立耐力，因為球員必須衝刺、停下、轉向、跳躍和恢復。 它們能磨練協調能力，因為身體並非只是複製一個被編好的動作；更準確地說，它正在解決一個會移動的問題。 如果健身是目標，假裝按按鈕和真正打比賽是同等一回事，便是錯的。 虛擬運動或許能讓我們動起來，但實體運動讓我們真正訓練自己。"},{"label":"Paragraph 6","english":"Some supporters of virtual sports may argue that they are safer, cleaner and more inclusive. I hear that. Granted, virtual sports can protect players from harsh weather, rough opponents and public embarrassment. However, avoiding discomfort altogether comes at a cost. Real sports teach lessons that cannot be downloaded: how to lose without sulking, how to pass instead of showing off, how to trust a teammate, how to shake hands after a bad call and how to stand tall after missing the final shot. A teenager who plays football in the park learns more than shooting technique; he learns patience when the team is losing, courage when stronger players challenge him, and humility when someone else scores. A virtual match may connect players online, but an in-person match creates eye contact, shared laughter, arguments, apologies and memories. There is more to sport than movement; there is community.","chinese":"有些支持虛擬運動的人可能會主張，它們更安全、更乾淨，也更具包容性。 這一點我明白。 誠然，虛擬運動可以保護玩家免受惡劣天氣、粗野對手和公開出醜的影響。 然而，完全避開不適是有代價的。 實體運動教會人的課，是無法下載的：如何輸了也不鬧情緒、如何傳球而不炫耀、如何信任隊友、如何在一次糟糕判罰後握手，以及如何在錯失最後一球後仍能昂首挺立。 一個在公園踢足球的青少年學到的不止是射門技巧；當球隊落後時，他學會耐性；當更強的球員挑戰他時，他學會勇氣；當別人入球時，他學會謙卑。 一場虛擬比賽或許能在線上連接玩家，但一場面對面的比賽能創造眼神交流、共同笑聲、爭執、道歉和回憶。 運動的意義不止於活動身體；其中還有社群連結。"},{"label":"Paragraph 7","english":"All things considered, virtual sports should be welcomed, but not worshipped. They are a bridge, not the destination. Parents can use them to get children off the sofa; schools can use them on rainy days; beginners can use them to build confidence. Yet the next step should always be towards real participation - joining a school team, playing badminton with friends, jogging in the park or trying a new sport without fear of looking foolish. So my answer is not a resounding no to virtual sports, but a qualified yes. Let the Wii open the door. Then step outside. That is where sport truly begins.","chinese":"總體而言，虛擬運動應該被接納，但不應被崇拜。 它們是一座橋樑，並非終點。 父母可以利用它們讓孩子離開沙發；學校可以在下雨天使用它們；初學者可以靠它們建立信心。 然而，下一步始終應該走向真正參與——加入校隊、和朋友打羽毛球、在公園慢跑，或嘗試一項新運動，不用害怕自己顯得笨拙。 所以，對虛擬運動，我的答案並非斬釘截鐵地否定；更準確地說，那是一個有保留的肯定。 讓 Wii 打開那道門吧。 然後，走出去。 真正的運動，正是在那裡開始。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"virtual sports","chinese":"虛擬運動"},{"english":"open the door","chinese":"打開大門；帶來開始"},{"english":"real sports keep us moving","chinese":"真實運動令我們持續活動"},{"english":"follow this debate with interest","chinese":"饒有興趣地關注這場辯論"},{"english":"ask the wrong question","chinese":"問錯問題"},{"english":"the issue is not whether...it is whether...","chinese":"問題不在於……而在於……"},{"english":"Wii tennis","chinese":"Wii 網球"},{"english":"real enough to deserve respect","chinese":"真實到值得尊重"},{"english":"improve our health","chinese":"改善我們的健康"},{"english":"in a way that lasts","chinese":"以持久的方式"},{"english":"spend long hours","chinese":"花長時間"},{"english":"revising, commuting and scrolling","chinese":"溫習、通勤和滑手機"},{"english":"consider something as","chinese":"把……視為"},{"english":"less intimidating exercise","chinese":"沒那麼令人卻步的運動"},{"english":"would otherwise stay on the sofa","chinese":"否則只會留在梳化上"},{"english":"start moving","chinese":"開始活動身體"},{"english":"as far as I am concerned","chinese":"就我而言"},{"english":"a doorway into fitness","chinese":"進入健身的門口"},{"english":"be treated as a replacement for","chinese":"被視為……的替代品"},{"english":"widen access and motivation","chinese":"擴闊參與機會並提升動力"},{"english":"develop the body, mind and character","chinese":"培養身體、心智和品格"},{"english":"more deeply","chinese":"更深入地"},{"english":"deserve credit","chinese":"值得肯定"},{"english":"lower the barrier to exercise","chinese":"降低做運動的門檻"},{"english":"basketball court downstairs","chinese":"樓下的籃球場"},{"english":"a free afternoon","chinese":"空閒的下午"},{"english":"the confidence to join a team","chinese":"加入隊伍的信心"},{"english":"stronger players may judge them","chinese":"較強的球員可能會評價他們"},{"english":"by contrast","chinese":"相比之下"},{"english":"turn a small living room into","chinese":"把小客廳變成"},{"english":"tennis court","chinese":"網球場"},{"english":"bowling alley","chinese":"保齡球場"},{"english":"boxing ring","chinese":"拳擊台"},{"english":"shy student","chinese":"害羞的學生"},{"english":"avoid PE","chinese":"逃避體育課"},{"english":"be willing to","chinese":"願意去"},{"english":"swing a controller","chinese":"揮動控制器"},{"english":"safely outdoors","chinese":"在戶外安全地"},{"english":"virtual bowling","chinese":"虛擬保齡球"},{"english":"what something lacks in...it makes up for in...","chinese":"在……方面有所不足，卻以……彌補"},{"english":"authenticity","chinese":"真實感"},{"english":"accessibility","chinese":"易參與程度"},{"english":"instant feedback","chinese":"即時回饋"},{"english":"make movement addictive","chinese":"令活動身體變得令人上癮"},{"english":"record your best score","chinese":"記錄你的最佳分數"},{"english":"try again","chinese":"再試一次"},{"english":"no longer feels like punishment","chinese":"不再感覺像懲罰"},{"english":"become play","chinese":"變成玩樂"},{"english":"fitness plan","chinese":"健身計劃"},{"english":"no better than","chinese":"不比……好"},{"english":"treadmill covered in dust","chinese":"滿佈灰塵的跑步機"},{"english":"a practical starting point","chinese":"實際可行的起點"},{"english":"that said","chinese":"話雖如此"},{"english":"offer a physical challenge","chinese":"提供身體挑戰"},{"english":"a screen can only imitate","chinese":"屏幕只能模仿"},{"english":"on the face of it","chinese":"表面看來"},{"english":"Wii remote","chinese":"Wii 遙控器"},{"english":"on closer inspection","chinese":"仔細看來"},{"english":"a far cry from","chinese":"與……相差甚遠"},{"english":"chase a ball across a court","chinese":"在球場上追球"},{"english":"adjust your footwork","chinese":"調整步法"},{"english":"read your opponent","chinese":"判斷對手意圖"},{"english":"cope with wind, heat and pressure","chinese":"應付風、熱和壓力"},{"english":"quick wrist movement","chinese":"快速手腕動作"},{"english":"produce a powerful shot","chinese":"打出有力一擊"},{"english":"legs, core and shoulders","chinese":"雙腿、核心肌群和肩膀"},{"english":"timing and stamina","chinese":"時機掌握和耐力"},{"english":"work together","chinese":"一起配合"},{"english":"the same applies to","chinese":"同樣適用於"},{"english":"force the whole body to respond","chinese":"迫使全身作出反應"},{"english":"space, speed and uncertainty","chinese":"空間、速度和不確定性"},{"english":"build endurance","chinese":"建立耐力"},{"english":"sprint, stop, turn, jump and recover","chinese":"衝刺、停下、轉身、跳躍和恢復"},{"english":"sharpen coordination","chinese":"提升協調能力"},{"english":"programmed gesture","chinese":"預設動作"},{"english":"solve a moving problem","chinese":"解決一個移動中的問題"},{"english":"if fitness is the goal","chinese":"如果目標是健身"},{"english":"it would be wrong to pretend that","chinese":"假裝……是錯誤的"},{"english":"pressing buttons","chinese":"按掣"},{"english":"playing matches","chinese":"進行比賽"},{"english":"make us train","chinese":"令我們真正訓練"},{"english":"supporters of virtual sports","chinese":"虛擬運動的支持者"},{"english":"safer, cleaner and more inclusive","chinese":"更安全、更乾淨、更共融"},{"english":"I hear that","chinese":"我明白這一點"},{"english":"granted","chinese":"無可否認"},{"english":"protect players from","chinese":"保護玩家免受……"},{"english":"harsh weather","chinese":"惡劣天氣"},{"english":"rough opponents","chinese":"粗魯的對手"},{"english":"public embarrassment","chinese":"當眾尷尬"},{"english":"avoiding discomfort altogether","chinese":"完全避開不適"},{"english":"come at a cost","chinese":"有代價"},{"english":"lessons that cannot be downloaded","chinese":"下載不到的人生課"},{"english":"lose without sulking","chinese":"輸了也不鬧彆扭"},{"english":"pass instead of showing off","chinese":"傳球而不是炫耀"},{"english":"trust a teammate","chinese":"信任隊友"},{"english":"shake hands after a bad call","chinese":"在一次錯判後仍握手"},{"english":"stand tall after","chinese":"在……之後仍昂然面對"},{"english":"miss the final shot","chinese":"錯失最後一球"},{"english":"shooting technique","chinese":"射門技巧"},{"english":"patience when the team is losing","chinese":"球隊落後時的耐性"},{"english":"courage when stronger players challenge him","chinese":"面對較強球員挑戰時的勇氣"},{"english":"humility when someone else scores","chinese":"別人入球時的謙遜"},{"english":"virtual match","chinese":"虛擬賽事"},{"english":"connect players online","chinese":"在網上連繫玩家"},{"english":"in-person match","chinese":"實體比賽"},{"english":"eye contact","chinese":"眼神接觸"},{"english":"shared laughter","chinese":"共同笑聲"},{"english":"arguments, apologies and memories","chinese":"爭執、道歉和回憶"},{"english":"there is more to sport than","chinese":"運動不止是……"},{"english":"community","chinese":"社群；群體連結"},{"english":"all things considered","chinese":"總括而言"},{"english":"be welcomed, but not worshipped","chinese":"應被歡迎，但不應被崇拜"},{"english":"a bridge, not the destination","chinese":"是橋樑，不是終點"},{"english":"get children off the sofa","chinese":"令孩子離開梳化"},{"english":"on rainy days","chinese":"在雨天"},{"english":"build confidence","chinese":"建立信心"},{"english":"the next step","chinese":"下一步"},{"english":"real participation","chinese":"真正參與"},{"english":"joining a school team","chinese":"加入校隊"},{"english":"playing badminton with friends","chinese":"跟朋友打羽毛球"},{"english":"trying a new sport","chinese":"嘗試一項新運動"},{"english":"without fear of looking foolish","chinese":"不怕看起來笨拙"},{"english":"a resounding no","chinese":"一個響亮的「不」"},{"english":"a qualified yes","chinese":"有保留的「是」"},{"english":"step outside","chinese":"走到戶外；踏出去"},{"english":"where sport truly begins","chinese":"運動真正開始的地方"}]},"dse-writing-2012-part-b-q3":{"exerciseId":"dse-writing-2012-part-b-q3","essayKey":"","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=dse-writing-2012-part-b-q3","flashDeckId":"dse/writing/part-b/2012/Q3","paragraphs":[{"label":"Paragraph 1","english":"Drama Is Not a Break from Learning — It Is Learning in Action","chinese":"戲劇並非學習的中斷——它是行動中的學習。"},{"label":"Paragraph 2","english":"Hi everyone,","chinese":"大家好："},{"label":"Paragraph 3","english":"I understand why some parents worry when they hear that a class is “doing drama”. In their eyes, a lesson should look like students sitting upright, copying notes and preparing for tests. However, with more teachers incorporating role-play, hot-seating and short performances into lessons, I believe schools are considering drama not to entertain students, but to help them understand ideas more deeply, remember them more vividly and speak with greater confidence. My stance is clear: drama, when carefully planned, is one of the most effective ways to learn. It is not the opposite of serious study; it is a bridge between knowledge and experience.","chinese":"我明白為甚麼有些家長一聽到某一堂課在「做戲劇活動」就會擔心。 在他們眼中，一堂課應該呈現出學生坐得端正、抄寫筆記並準備考試的樣子 然而，隨著越來越多老師把角色扮演、熱椅活動和短劇表演融入課堂，我相信學校考慮採用戲劇，重點不在娛樂學生，重點在幫助他們更深入地理解概念、更鮮明地記住所學，並更有自信地表達。 我的立場很清楚：只要經過周詳規劃，戲劇就是其中一種最有效的學習方式 它並非嚴肅學習的對立面；它是一座連接知識與經驗的橋樑。"},{"label":"Paragraph 4","english":"First, drama turns abstract knowledge into lived understanding. It is one thing to read about peer pressure, empathy or moral courage; it is another to step into a situation where those ideas have to be tested through words, silence and action. In one English lesson, our teacher gave each group a simple scenario: a new student had been left out of a class chat, and different classmates had to decide whether to laugh along, remain silent or speak up. At first glance, the task looked like a harmless skit; on closer inspection, it required careful reading, emotional awareness and serious judgment. The student playing the victim had to explain why silence could hurt as much as direct insults. The “bystanders” had to justify their choices. The “class teacher” had to ask questions instead of simply giving punishment. The more we rehearsed, the more we realised that words such as “respect”, “responsibility” and “empathy” were not empty slogans in a textbook, but choices people make in real situations. By the time we wrote our reflection, even students who seldom spoke in class could identify the conflict, describe the characters’ motives and explain how tone, gesture and hesitation changed the meaning of a sentence. In other words, drama did not distract us from learning; rather, it made the learning visible.","chinese":"首先，戲劇能把抽象知識轉化為親身體會到的理解。 閱讀同儕壓力、同理心或道德勇氣是一回事；真正走進一個情境，讓這些概念透過言語、沉默和行動接受考驗，則是另一回事。 在某一節英文課，老師給每一組一個簡單情境：一位新同學被排除在班級聊天群組之外，不同同學必須決定是要跟著笑、保持沉默，還是站出來說話。 乍看之下，這個任務像一齣無傷大雅的小短劇；仔細一看，它其實要求細緻閱讀、情感覺察和嚴肅判斷。 扮演受害者的學生必須解釋，為甚麼沉默造成的傷害可以和直接侮辱一樣深 那些「旁觀者」必須為自己的選擇提出理由。 那位「班主任」必須提出問題，而非只是給予懲罰。 我們排練得越多，就越明白「尊重」、「責任」和「同理心」這些詞語並非課本裡空洞的口號；它們是人們在真實情境中作出的選擇。 到我們寫反思時，即使是平日很少在課堂發言的學生，也能指出衝突、描述角色動機，並解釋語氣、姿態和猶豫如何改變一句說話的意思。 換言之，戲劇沒有使我們偏離學習；相反，它讓學習變得看得見。"},{"label":"Paragraph 5","english":"More importantly, drama helps students develop skills that ordinary worksheets can hardly train. Learning is not just about storing information; it is about explaining, listening, negotiating and responding under pressure. In another lesson, my group created a short scene about cyberbullying. One student played the victim, another the bystander, another the parent, and I played the class teacher. At first glance, the task looked simple; on closer inspection, it forced us to consider tone, body language and responsibility. Should the bystander report the incident or stay silent? How should the parent react without making the child feel ashamed? How could the teacher protect the victim without turning the classroom into a court? These were not questions with one neat answer. Through role reversal, we began to see how one person’s “joke” might be another person’s wound. That kind of empathy is no less important than vocabulary or grammar, especially in a world where young people communicate quickly but not always wisely.","chinese":"更重要的是，戲劇能幫助學生培養一般工作紙幾乎無法訓練的技能。 學習不只關乎儲存資訊；它也關乎解釋、聆聽、協商，以及在壓力下作出回應 在另一堂課中，我的小組創作了一個關於網絡欺凌的短場景。 一位同學扮演受害者，另一位扮演旁觀者，另一位扮演家長，而我則扮演班主任。 乍看之下，這個任務似乎簡單；仔細一看，它迫使我們思考語氣、肢體語言與責任。 旁觀者應該舉報事件，還是保持沉默？ 家長應該如何回應，才不會令孩子感到羞愧？ 老師又可以如何保護受害者，同時避免把課室變成法庭？ 這些問題並沒有一個整齊劃一的答案。 透過角色倒置，我們開始明白，一個人的「玩笑」可能是另一個人的傷口。 那種同理心的重要性絕不低於詞彙或文法，尤其是在一個年輕人溝通速度很快、卻未必總是溝通得明智的世界裡。"},{"label":"Paragraph 6","english":"Granted, some parents have a point: drama can be noisy, and if it is poorly planned, it may become little more than laughter and movement. I take that concern seriously. Yet to say that drama can be misused is not to say that drama is useless. The same applies to group discussion, presentations and even homework. Without clear objectives, any method can fail. With clear instructions, a time limit, assigned roles, reflection questions and assessment criteria, drama becomes a structured learning activity. Students can be asked to write a diary entry after a role-play, compare their performance with the original text, or explain what their character’s choices reveal. That way, parents can see that the acting is not the final goal; it is the route towards deeper thinking.","chinese":"誠然，有些家長有一定道理：戲劇活動可以很吵鬧，而且如果規劃不周，它可能變成只剩笑聲和動作的活動。 我認真看待這種憂慮。 然而，說戲劇可能被誤用，並不等於說戲劇毫無用處。 小組討論、匯報，甚至功課，也同樣如此。 沒有清晰目標，任何方法都可能失敗。 在清楚指示、時間限制、分配角色、反思問題和評估準則之下，戲劇就會成為一項有結構的學習活動。 學生可以被要求在角色扮演後寫一篇日記，將自己的表現與原文比較，或解釋角色的選擇揭示了甚麼。 這樣一來，家長就能看見，演出並非最終目標；它是通往更深入思考的路徑"},{"label":"Paragraph 7","english":"All things considered, I would argue that drama deserves a secure place in education. Not every lesson should become a performance, and no teacher should use drama merely to make a lesson look fashionable. However, when used with purpose, it brings ideas off the page, gives students room to speak, and makes learning memorable in a way that silent copying rarely can. Schools should explain the purpose of drama-based tasks to parents, teachers should design them carefully, and students should reflect on what they have learnt afterwards. Drama may look like play from the outside, but in the classroom, at its best, it is serious learning wearing a human face.","chinese":"總括而言，我會主張，戲劇值得在教育中佔有穩固的位置。 並非每一堂課都應變成一場表演，也沒有老師應該只是為了讓課堂看起來時髦才使用戲劇。 然而，當戲劇被有目的地使用時，它能把概念從書頁中帶出來，給予學生發聲空間，並以一種安靜抄寫很少能做到的方式，使學習變得難忘。 學校應向家長解釋戲劇式學習活動的目的，老師應細心設計活動，學生也應在活動後反思自己學到了甚麼。 從外面看，戲劇也許像玩樂；可是在課堂裡，當它發揮得最好時，它其實是帶有人性面貌的嚴肅學習。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"a break from learning","chinese":"學習的休息；脫離學習"},{"english":"learning in action","chinese":"實踐中的學習"},{"english":"understand why","chinese":"理解為甚麼"},{"english":"doing drama","chinese":"上戲劇活動課"},{"english":"in their eyes","chinese":"在他們眼中"},{"english":"sitting upright","chinese":"坐得筆直"},{"english":"copying notes","chinese":"抄筆記"},{"english":"preparing for tests","chinese":"準備測驗"},{"english":"incorporating","chinese":"加入；融入"},{"english":"role-play","chinese":"角色扮演"},{"english":"hot-seating","chinese":"熱座提問"},{"english":"short performances","chinese":"簡短表演"},{"english":"considering drama not to entertain students, but to help them","chinese":"考慮使用戲劇不是為了娛樂學生，而是為了幫助他們"},{"english":"understand ideas more deeply","chinese":"更深入理解概念"},{"english":"remember them more vividly","chinese":"更生動地記住它們"},{"english":"speak with greater confidence","chinese":"更有信心地說話"},{"english":"my stance is clear","chinese":"我的立場很清楚"},{"english":"when carefully planned","chinese":"在經過仔細規劃時"},{"english":"one of the most effective ways to","chinese":"最有效的……方法之一"},{"english":"the opposite of","chinese":"……的相反"},{"english":"serious study","chinese":"認真學習"},{"english":"a bridge between","chinese":"……之間的橋樑"},{"english":"knowledge and experience","chinese":"知識與經驗"},{"english":"turns abstract knowledge into","chinese":"把抽象知識轉化為"},{"english":"abstract knowledge","chinese":"抽象知識"},{"english":"lived understanding","chinese":"親身體會得來的理解"},{"english":"it is one thing to…, it is another to…","chinese":"……是一回事，……又是另一回事"},{"english":"peer pressure","chinese":"同輩壓力"},{"english":"empathy","chinese":"同理心"},{"english":"moral courage","chinese":"道德勇氣"},{"english":"step into a situation","chinese":"進入某個情境"},{"english":"have to be tested through","chinese":"必須透過……接受考驗"},{"english":"through words, silence and action","chinese":"透過語言、沉默和行動"},{"english":"a simple scenario","chinese":"一個簡單情境"},{"english":"left out of","chinese":"被排除在……之外"},{"english":"class chat","chinese":"班群組聊天"},{"english":"laugh along","chinese":"跟着一起笑"},{"english":"remain silent","chinese":"保持沉默"},{"english":"speak up","chinese":"出聲；發聲"},{"english":"at first glance","chinese":"乍看之下"},{"english":"harmless skit","chinese":"無傷大雅的小短劇"},{"english":"on closer inspection","chinese":"仔細看時"},{"english":"emotional awareness","chinese":"情感覺察"},{"english":"serious judgment","chinese":"認真判斷"},{"english":"playing the victim","chinese":"扮演受害者"},{"english":"direct insults","chinese":"直接侮辱"},{"english":"bystanders","chinese":"旁觀者"},{"english":"justify their choices","chinese":"為自己的選擇辯解"},{"english":"instead of simply","chinese":"而不是單純"},{"english":"giving punishment","chinese":"作出懲罰"},{"english":"the more…, the more…","chinese":"越……就越……"},{"english":"rehearsed","chinese":"排練"},{"english":"empty slogans","chinese":"空洞口號"},{"english":"choices people make","chinese":"人們作出的選擇"},{"english":"real situations","chinese":"真實情境"},{"english":"by the time","chinese":"到……的時候"},{"english":"wrote our reflection","chinese":"寫反思"},{"english":"seldom spoke in class","chinese":"很少在課堂上發言"},{"english":"identify the conflict","chinese":"識別衝突"},{"english":"characters' motives","chinese":"角色動機"},{"english":"tone, gesture and hesitation","chinese":"語氣、手勢和遲疑"},{"english":"changed the meaning of","chinese":"改變……的意思"},{"english":"distract someone from learning","chinese":"使某人分心而不能學習"},{"english":"made the learning visible","chinese":"令學習變得看得見"},{"english":"more importantly","chinese":"更重要的是"},{"english":"develop skills","chinese":"培養技能"},{"english":"ordinary worksheets","chinese":"普通工作紙"},{"english":"can hardly train","chinese":"很難訓練"},{"english":"storing information","chinese":"儲存資料"},{"english":"negotiating","chinese":"協商；磋商"},{"english":"responding under pressure","chinese":"在壓力下回應"},{"english":"created a short scene","chinese":"創作一個短場景"},{"english":"cyberbullying","chinese":"網絡欺凌"},{"english":"played the victim","chinese":"扮演受害者"},{"english":"bystander","chinese":"旁觀者"},{"english":"played the class teacher","chinese":"扮演班主任"},{"english":"forced us to consider","chinese":"迫使我們思考"},{"english":"body language","chinese":"身體語言"},{"english":"report the incident","chinese":"報告事件"},{"english":"stay silent","chinese":"保持沉默"},{"english":"react without making someone feel ashamed","chinese":"回應時不令某人感到羞愧"},{"english":"feel ashamed","chinese":"感到羞愧"},{"english":"protect the victim","chinese":"保護受害者"},{"english":"turn the classroom into a court","chinese":"把課室變成法庭"},{"english":"one neat answer","chinese":"一個簡單俐落的答案"},{"english":"role reversal","chinese":"角色互換"},{"english":"one person's joke","chinese":"某人的玩笑"},{"english":"another person's wound","chinese":"另一個人的傷口"},{"english":"no less important than","chinese":"不比……較不重要"},{"english":"communicate quickly but not always wisely","chinese":"溝通很快但不一定明智"},{"english":"granted","chinese":"誠然"},{"english":"have a point","chinese":"說得有道理"},{"english":"poorly planned","chinese":"規劃不善的"},{"english":"little more than","chinese":"只不過是"},{"english":"take that concern seriously","chinese":"認真看待那個憂慮"},{"english":"to say that… is not to say that…","chinese":"說……並不等於說……"},{"english":"be misused","chinese":"被誤用"},{"english":"the same applies to","chinese":"同樣適用於"},{"english":"group discussion","chinese":"小組討論"},{"english":"presentations","chinese":"匯報；演講"},{"english":"clear objectives","chinese":"清晰目標"},{"english":"any method can fail","chinese":"任何方法都可能失敗"},{"english":"clear instructions","chinese":"清晰指示"},{"english":"time limit","chinese":"時限"},{"english":"assigned roles","chinese":"指定角色"},{"english":"reflection questions","chinese":"反思問題"},{"english":"assessment criteria","chinese":"評核準則"},{"english":"structured learning activity","chinese":"有結構的學習活動"},{"english":"diary entry","chinese":"日記"},{"english":"compare their performance with","chinese":"把自己的表現與……比較"},{"english":"original text","chinese":"原文"},{"english":"character's choices","chinese":"角色的選擇"},{"english":"that way","chinese":"這樣"},{"english":"the final goal","chinese":"最終目標"},{"english":"the route towards","chinese":"通往……的途徑"},{"english":"deeper thinking","chinese":"更深入的思考"},{"english":"all things considered","chinese":"綜合而言"},{"english":"I would argue that","chinese":"我會主張"},{"english":"deserves a secure place in","chinese":"應在……中佔有穩固位置"},{"english":"not every lesson should","chinese":"並非每堂課都應該"},{"english":"merely to","chinese":"只是為了"},{"english":"look fashionable","chinese":"看起來時髦"},{"english":"when used with purpose","chinese":"當有目的地使用時"},{"english":"brings ideas off the page","chinese":"把書本上的概念帶進現實"},{"english":"gives students room to speak","chinese":"給學生發言空間"},{"english":"makes learning memorable","chinese":"令學習令人難忘"},{"english":"silent copying","chinese":"沉默抄寫"},{"english":"drama-based tasks","chinese":"以戲劇為本的課業"},{"english":"explain the purpose of","chinese":"解釋……的目的"},{"english":"design them carefully","chinese":"仔細設計它們"},{"english":"reflect on what they have learnt","chinese":"反思自己學到的東西"},{"english":"from the outside","chinese":"從外面看"},{"english":"at its best","chinese":"在最佳情況下"},{"english":"serious learning wearing a human face","chinese":"有人情味的認真學習"}]},"dse-writing-2012-part-b-q4":{"exerciseId":"dse-writing-2012-part-b-q4","essayKey":"","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=dse-writing-2012-part-b-q4","flashDeckId":"dse/writing/part-b/2012/Q4","paragraphs":[{"label":"Paragraph 1","english":"Still Shaking - Our First Festival Stage at Victoria Park","chinese":"仍在震顫：我們在維多利亞公園的第一個音樂節舞台"},{"label":"Paragraph 2","english":"Last week, my band, Neon Harbour, did something we had been dreaming about since we first squeezed into a tiny rehearsal room in Kwun Tong - we performed at a music festival in Victoria Park. As the lead singer, I had imagined this moment so many times that I thought I would know exactly how it would feel. I was wrong. There is a world of difference between singing to four walls and singing to a field of strangers whose faces are lit by stage lights, phone screens and curiosity. This post is my attempt to remember the night honestly - the joy, the electricity, the mistakes and the lessons.","chinese":"上星期，我的樂隊 Neon Harbour 做了一件我們自從第一次擠進觀塘一間狹小排練室以來一直夢想的事——我們在維多利亞公園的一個音樂節上演出了。 作為主音歌手，我曾經想像這一刻無數次，多到我以為自己會清楚知道它到底會是甚麼感覺。 我錯了。 對着四面牆唱歌，和對着一大片陌生人唱歌，完全是兩回事；那些陌生人的臉，被舞台燈光、手機螢幕和好奇心照亮着。 這篇文章，是我試着誠實記下那一晚：喜悅、電流般的震撼、錯誤和教訓。"},{"label":"Paragraph 3","english":"Before we went on, I was anything but calm. Backstage, my hands were cold, my throat felt dry, and every small sound seemed enormous—the click of a guitar pedal, the crackle of a walkie-talkie, the drummer tapping nervous rhythms on his knees. I kept telling myself that nerves were simply excitement looking for somewhere to go, but even that did not stop my heart from racing. When the announcer called our name, I walked out as if I were stepping onto a moving bridge. For one terrifying second, the crowd looked endless. Then someone near the front shouted our band name, and the fear loosened its grip.","chinese":"在我們上台之前，我完全談不上冷靜。 在後台，我的雙手冰冷，喉嚨發乾，每一點細小聲音都像被放大了一樣—— 結他效果器的咔嗒聲、對講機的沙沙聲、鼓手在膝蓋上敲出緊張節奏的聲音 我一直告訴自己，緊張只是興奮在尋找出口，但即使這樣也無法阻止我的心跳狂奔。 當司儀叫出我們的名字時，我走了出去，感覺像踏上一座正在晃動的橋。 有那麼令人害怕的一秒鐘，人群看起來彷彿沒有盡頭。 然後，前排附近有人喊出我們樂隊的名字，恐懼才稍稍鬆開了手。"},{"label":"Paragraph 4","english":"The atmosphere was beyond words. Victoria Park, usually a place of joggers, families and weekend football matches, had turned into a glowing island of music. Food stalls sent up the smell of grilled squid and curry fish balls; coloured banners moved in the evening breeze; somewhere behind us, another stage was booming with electronic beats. Yet when our first chord rang out, the space in front of us suddenly felt intimate. People who had never heard of us began nodding along. A group of children danced near the barrier. Two girls in raincoats waved their light sticks as though we were already famous. We were not, of course, but for those thirty minutes, we were allowed to pretend.","chinese":"那種氣氛難以言喻。 平日屬於跑步人士、家庭和週末足球賽的維多利亞公園，當晚變成了一座閃閃發亮的音樂之島。 小食攤飄來燒魷魚和咖喱魚蛋的氣味；彩色旗幟在晚風中擺動；在我們身後某處，另一個舞台正轟鳴着電子節拍。 然而，當我們第一個和弦響起時，眼前的空間突然變得親近起來。 從未聽過我們的人開始跟着點頭。 一群小朋友在圍欄附近跳舞。 兩個穿着雨衣的女生揮動着螢光棒，好像我們早已成名。 當然，我們並未成名；但在那三十分鐘裡，我們可以暫時假裝自己已經成名"},{"label":"Paragraph 5","english":"The best moment came during our third song, “Harbour Lights”. Halfway through the chorus, my microphone cable caught under the stand, and I missed a line. Disaster, right? Not quite. Without being asked, the audience finished the lyric for me. I cannot begin to describe what that sounded like from the stage. It was not perfect singing; it was something better—generous, spontaneous and human. I looked at my bandmates, and all of us were grinning. At that point, the performance stopped being about proving ourselves. It became a conversation between us and everyone listening.","chinese":"最美好的一刻，出現在我們第三首歌《Harbour Lights》之中。 副歌唱到一半時，我的咪高峰線被支架卡住，而我漏唱了一句歌詞。 災難，對吧？ 也不完全對。 沒有人要求他們這樣做，觀眾卻替我唱完了那句歌詞。 我幾乎無法形容，在舞台上聽見那一刻究竟是甚麼感覺。 那並非完美的歌聲；那是更好的東西——慷慨、自發，而且有人味。 我看向我的樂隊隊友，我們全都咧嘴笑了起來。 到了那一刻，這場演出不再只是關於證明自己。 它變成了我們和每一位聽眾之間的一場對話。"},{"label":"Paragraph 6","english":"That said, honesty matters. Our first festival show was unforgettable, but there is certainly room for improvement. For one thing, we should have checked the sound monitors more carefully. During the opening song, I could barely hear my own voice, so I pushed too hard and nearly lost control of the high notes. For another, our transitions between songs were not smooth enough. We had practised the songs, but not the silence between them, and those awkward seconds felt much longer on stage than they had in rehearsal. I also wish I had spoken to the audience more naturally. Instead of trying to sound like a polished superstar, I should have sounded more like myself.","chinese":"話雖如此，誠實也很重要。 我們的第一場音樂節演出令人難忘，但它絕對仍有改善空間。 一方面，我們本應更仔細地檢查監聽音響。 在開場歌曲期間，我幾乎聽不到自己的聲音，所以我唱得太用力，差點控制不了高音。 另一方面，我們歌曲之間的銜接也不夠流暢。 我們練習過歌曲本身，卻沒有練習歌曲之間的沉默，而那些尷尬的幾秒鐘，在台上感覺比排練時漫長得多。 我也希望自己當時能更自然地和觀眾說話。 與其努力讓自己聽起來像一位經過精心包裝的巨星，我本應聽起來更像我自己"},{"label":"Paragraph 7","english":"Still, I would not trade that night for anything. The mistakes did not ruin the performance; if anything, they made the achievement feel real. A perfect show might have been impressive, but this imperfect one taught us how far we have come and how far we still have to go. Next time, we will arrive earlier, test every cable, rehearse our stage talk and leave more room for the unexpected. Most importantly, we will remember that live music is not just about hitting every note; it is about sharing a pulse with people who choose, for a few precious minutes, to listen.","chinese":"即便如此，我不會拿那一晚去換任何東西。 那些錯誤沒有毀掉演出；真要說的話，它們讓這份成就更顯得真實。 一場完美演出也許會令人印象深刻，但這場不完美的演出教會我們，我們已經走了多遠，也仍有多遠的路要走。 下一次，我們會更早到場、測試每一條電線、排練舞台上的說話，並為突發情況留下更多空間。 最重要的是，我們會記住，現場音樂不只關乎唱準每一個音；它的核心在於和那些願意用短短幾分鐘聆聽的人共享同一種脈搏。"},{"label":"Paragraph 8","english":"So thank you, Victoria Park. Thank you to every friend, stranger and accidental listener who stayed. Our first festival performance is over, but the echo of it is still ringing in my chest.","chinese":"所以，謝謝你，維多利亞公園。 謝謝每一位留下來的朋友、陌生人，以及偶然停下腳步的聽眾。 我們的第一場音樂節演出已經結束，但它的迴響仍在我胸口鳴響。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"still shaking","chinese":"仍然激動；仍在發抖"},{"english":"first festival performance","chinese":"首次音樂節演出"},{"english":"Victoria Park","chinese":"維多利亞公園"},{"english":"last week","chinese":"上星期"},{"english":"my band","chinese":"我的樂隊"},{"english":"Neon Harbour","chinese":"Neon Harbour"},{"english":"had been dreaming about","chinese":"一直夢想"},{"english":"since we first","chinese":"自從我們第一次……以來"},{"english":"squeeze into","chinese":"擠進"},{"english":"tiny rehearsal room","chinese":"細小的排練室"},{"english":"Kwun Tong","chinese":"觀塘"},{"english":"perform at","chinese":"在……表演"},{"english":"music festival","chinese":"音樂節"},{"english":"as the lead singer","chinese":"作為主音歌手"},{"english":"imagined this moment","chinese":"想像過這一刻"},{"english":"so many times that","chinese":"……很多次，以致"},{"english":"know exactly how it would feel","chinese":"完全知道感覺會是怎樣"},{"english":"I was wrong","chinese":"我錯了"},{"english":"a world of difference between","chinese":"……之間有天壤之別"},{"english":"singing to four walls","chinese":"對著四面牆唱歌"},{"english":"a field of strangers","chinese":"一大片陌生觀眾"},{"english":"faces are lit by","chinese":"面孔被……照亮"},{"english":"stage lights","chinese":"舞台燈光"},{"english":"phone screens","chinese":"手機螢幕"},{"english":"this post is my attempt to","chinese":"這篇帖文是我嘗試……"},{"english":"remember the night honestly","chinese":"真誠地記下那一晚"},{"english":"the joy, the electricity, the mistakes and the lessons","chinese":"喜悅、震撼、錯誤和教訓"},{"english":"before we went on","chinese":"上台前"},{"english":"anything but calm","chinese":"一點也不冷靜"},{"english":"backstage","chinese":"後台"},{"english":"my throat felt dry","chinese":"喉嚨乾澀"},{"english":"every small sound seemed enormous","chinese":"每個細小聲音都顯得巨大"},{"english":"the click of","chinese":"……的喀噠聲"},{"english":"guitar pedal","chinese":"結他效果器踏板"},{"english":"the crackle of","chinese":"……的沙沙聲"},{"english":"walkie-talkie","chinese":"對講機"},{"english":"tap nervous rhythms","chinese":"敲出緊張的節奏"},{"english":"nervous rhythms","chinese":"緊張的節奏"},{"english":"keep telling myself that","chinese":"不斷告訴自己"},{"english":"nerves","chinese":"緊張情緒"},{"english":"excitement looking for somewhere to go","chinese":"無處安放的興奮"},{"english":"stop my heart from racing","chinese":"阻止我心跳加速"},{"english":"heart from racing","chinese":"心跳急速"},{"english":"the announcer","chinese":"司儀；報幕員"},{"english":"called our name","chinese":"叫出我們的名字"},{"english":"walked out as if","chinese":"走出去時像是"},{"english":"step onto","chinese":"踏上"},{"english":"a moving bridge","chinese":"移動中的橋"},{"english":"for one terrifying second","chinese":"在令人害怕的一秒間"},{"english":"the crowd looked endless","chinese":"人群看似無邊無際"},{"english":"near the front","chinese":"靠近前排"},{"english":"shouted our band name","chinese":"大叫我們樂隊的名字"},{"english":"loosen its grip","chinese":"鬆開束縛"},{"english":"beyond words","chinese":"難以用言語形容"},{"english":"a place of","chinese":"一個……的地方"},{"english":"joggers","chinese":"緩跑人士"},{"english":"weekend football matches","chinese":"週末足球賽"},{"english":"turn into","chinese":"變成"},{"english":"glowing island of music","chinese":"發光的音樂小島"},{"english":"food stalls","chinese":"小食檔"},{"english":"sent up the smell of","chinese":"散發出……的氣味"},{"english":"grilled squid","chinese":"燒魷魚"},{"english":"curry fish balls","chinese":"咖喱魚蛋"},{"english":"coloured banners","chinese":"彩色橫額"},{"english":"evening breeze","chinese":"傍晚微風"},{"english":"somewhere behind us","chinese":"在我們身後某處"},{"english":"boom with","chinese":"充滿轟鳴的……"},{"english":"electronic beats","chinese":"電子節拍"},{"english":"first chord rang out","chinese":"第一個和弦響起"},{"english":"rang out","chinese":"響起"},{"english":"suddenly felt intimate","chinese":"突然感覺親密"},{"english":"had never heard of us","chinese":"從未聽過我們"},{"english":"began nodding along","chinese":"開始跟著點頭"},{"english":"near the barrier","chinese":"在欄杆附近"},{"english":"light sticks","chinese":"螢光棒"},{"english":"as though","chinese":"好像"},{"english":"already famous","chinese":"已經成名"},{"english":"for those thirty minutes","chinese":"在那三十分鐘裏"},{"english":"be allowed to pretend","chinese":"被允許假裝"},{"english":"the best moment came during","chinese":"最精彩的一刻出現在"},{"english":"third song","chinese":"第三首歌"},{"english":"halfway through","chinese":"進行到一半時"},{"english":"chorus","chinese":"副歌"},{"english":"microphone cable","chinese":"麥克風線"},{"english":"caught under","chinese":"卡在……下面"},{"english":"mic stand","chinese":"麥克風架"},{"english":"missed a line","chinese":"漏唱一句"},{"english":"not quite","chinese":"不完全是"},{"english":"without being asked","chinese":"無需被要求"},{"english":"finished the lyric for me","chinese":"替我唱完歌詞"},{"english":"cannot begin to describe","chinese":"無法充分描述"},{"english":"from the stage","chinese":"從舞台上聽來"},{"english":"perfect singing","chinese":"完美的歌聲"},{"english":"something better","chinese":"更好的東西"},{"english":"generous, spontaneous and human","chinese":"慷慨、自然流露而有人情味"},{"english":"spontaneous","chinese":"自發的；自然流露的"},{"english":"bandmates","chinese":"樂隊成員"},{"english":"all of us were grinning","chinese":"我們全都咧嘴笑"},{"english":"at that point","chinese":"在那一刻"},{"english":"proving ourselves","chinese":"證明自己"},{"english":"became a conversation between","chinese":"變成……之間的對話"},{"english":"everyone listening","chinese":"每一位聆聽的人"},{"english":"that said","chinese":"話雖如此"},{"english":"honesty matters","chinese":"誠實很重要"},{"english":"unforgettable","chinese":"難忘的"},{"english":"room for improvement","chinese":"有改善空間"},{"english":"for one thing","chinese":"首先"},{"english":"sound monitors","chinese":"舞台監聽"},{"english":"more carefully","chinese":"更仔細地"},{"english":"opening song","chinese":"開場歌曲"},{"english":"could barely hear","chinese":"幾乎聽不到"},{"english":"pushed too hard","chinese":"太用力"},{"english":"nearly lost control of","chinese":"差點失控"},{"english":"high notes","chinese":"高音"},{"english":"for another","chinese":"其次"},{"english":"transitions between songs","chinese":"歌與歌之間的銜接"},{"english":"not smooth enough","chinese":"不夠流暢"},{"english":"had practised the songs","chinese":"練習過歌曲"},{"english":"the silence between them","chinese":"歌與歌之間的沉默"},{"english":"awkward seconds","chinese":"尷尬的幾秒"},{"english":"much longer on stage","chinese":"在台上感覺長得多"},{"english":"in rehearsal","chinese":"在排練中"},{"english":"wish I had","chinese":"希望自己當時有"},{"english":"speak to the audience","chinese":"跟觀眾說話"},{"english":"more naturally","chinese":"更自然地"},{"english":"instead of trying to","chinese":"而不是試圖"},{"english":"polished superstar","chinese":"包裝成熟的巨星"},{"english":"sound like myself","chinese":"聽起來更像自己"},{"english":"would not trade that night for anything","chinese":"我不會用任何東西交換那一晚"},{"english":"ruin the performance","chinese":"破壞演出"},{"english":"if anything","chinese":"反而"},{"english":"make the achievement feel real","chinese":"令成就感變得真實"},{"english":"perfect show","chinese":"完美演出"},{"english":"imperfect one","chinese":"這場不完美的演出"},{"english":"how far we have come","chinese":"我們已走了多遠"},{"english":"how far we still have to go","chinese":"我們仍有多遠的路要走"},{"english":"arrive earlier","chinese":"早點到達"},{"english":"test every cable","chinese":"測試每條電線"},{"english":"rehearse our stage talk","chinese":"排練台上說話"},{"english":"stage talk","chinese":"台上說話"},{"english":"leave more room for","chinese":"為……預留更多空間"},{"english":"the unexpected","chinese":"意料之外的事"},{"english":"most importantly","chinese":"最重要的是"},{"english":"live music","chinese":"現場音樂"},{"english":"not just about hitting every note","chinese":"不只是唱準每一個音"},{"english":"hitting every note","chinese":"唱準每一個音"},{"english":"sharing a pulse with","chinese":"與……分享同一種脈搏"},{"english":"a few precious minutes","chinese":"珍貴的幾分鐘"},{"english":"accidental listener","chinese":"偶然聽到的觀眾"},{"english":"every friend, stranger and accidental listener","chinese":"每位朋友、陌生人和偶然聽眾"},{"english":"who stayed","chinese":"留下來的人"},{"english":"first festival performance is over","chinese":"首次音樂節演出已經結束"},{"english":"the echo of it","chinese":"它的回響"},{"english":"still ringing in my chest","chinese":"仍在我胸口迴盪"}]},"dse-writing-2012-part-b-q5":{"exerciseId":"dse-writing-2012-part-b-q5","essayKey":"","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=dse-writing-2012-part-b-q5","flashDeckId":"dse/writing/part-b/2012/Q5","paragraphs":[{"label":"Paragraph 1","english":"Speak Up, Think Sharply, Stand Tall","chinese":"發聲、銳思、昂首前行"},{"label":"Paragraph 2","english":"Good morning Principal, teachers and fellow students,","chinese":"早安，校長、各位老師、各位同學："},{"label":"Paragraph 3","english":"Have you ever sat in a classroom, heard a comment you disagreed with, and thought of the perfect reply only after the lesson had ended?","chinese":"你是否曾經坐在課室裡，聽到一句你不同意的話，卻直到課堂結束後才想到最完美的回應？"},{"label":"Paragraph 4","english":"If so, you are not alone.","chinese":"如果有，你並不孤單。"},{"label":"Paragraph 5","english":"In a world where opinions travel faster than facts, many students want to speak up, but do not quite know how.","chinese":"在一個意見比事實傳播得更快的世界裡，許多學生都想發聲，卻不太知道應該如何開口。 其實不然。"},{"label":"Paragraph 6","english":"That is why our school debating club is looking for new members: we want to make room for students who are curious, nervous, outspoken, quiet, experienced or completely new, so that more of us can learn to think clearly, speak confidently and listen respectfully.","chinese":"這正是本校辯論學會正在招募新成員的原因：我們希望為好奇的、緊張的、敢言的、安靜的、有經驗的，或完全沒有經驗的同學騰出空間，讓更多人學會清晰思考、自信發言，並以尊重的態度聆聽。"},{"label":"Paragraph 7","english":"Today, I would like to show you that debating is not just an activity for the loudest students; it is training for anyone who wants to become sharper, braver and fairer.","chinese":"今天，我想讓大家看見，辯論不只是最響亮的學生才參與的活動；它也是一種訓練，適合任何想變得更敏銳、更勇敢、更公正的人。"},{"label":"Paragraph 8","english":"First, there is more to the debating club than standing behind a lectern and arguing for six minutes.","chinese":"首先，辯論學會的內容，遠遠不止於站在講台後爭辯六分鐘。"},{"label":"Paragraph 9","english":"Every week, we organise practical training sessions on case-building, rebuttal, delivery and current affairs.","chinese":"每個星期，我們都會舉辦實用的訓練課節，內容包括立論、反駁、演說技巧和時事議題。"},{"label":"Paragraph 10","english":"One week, we may examine whether homework should be reduced; the next, we may debate artificial intelligence, animal protection, school uniforms or Hong Kong’s waste problem.","chinese":"某一個星期，我們可能會探討功課是否應該減少；下一個星期，我們又可能辯論人工智能、動物保護、校服，或香港的垃圾問題。"},{"label":"Paragraph 11","english":"From brainstorming motions to polishing speeches, from mock debates to post-match feedback, every activity is designed to help members improve step by step.","chinese":"從構思辯題到打磨演辭，從模擬辯論到賽後回饋，每一項活動的設計，都是為了幫助成員一步一步進步。"},{"label":"Paragraph 12","english":"We also run “impromptu challenge” afternoons, where students are given a motion and only fifteen minutes to prepare.","chinese":"我們也會舉辦「即興挑戰」下午活動，學生會即場取得一個辯題，並且只有十五分鐘準備。"},{"label":"Paragraph 13","english":"It sounds terrifying, right?","chinese":"聽起來很可怕，對吧？"},{"label":"Paragraph 14","english":"Not quite.","chinese":"在一個意見比事實傳播得更快的世界裡，許多學生都想發聲，卻不太知道應該如何開口。 其實不然。"},{"label":"Paragraph 15","english":"In fact, those sessions often become the funniest part of the term, because members learn to think on their feet, support one another and laugh at mistakes instead of fearing them.","chinese":"事實上，那些課節常常成為整個學期最有趣的部分，因為成員會學習即場思考、互相支持，並學會笑著面對錯誤，而非害怕它們。"},{"label":"Paragraph 16","english":"Better still, our club joins inter-school competitions and friendly debates with neighbouring schools, giving members the chance to meet people whose ideas, accents and styles are completely different from their own.","chinese":"更理想的是，我們學會也會參加校際比賽，並與鄰近學校進行友誼辯論，讓成員有機會認識想法、口音和風格都與自己截然不同的人。"},{"label":"Paragraph 17","english":"Secondly, the benefits of joining the club go far beyond trophies.","chinese":"第二，加入辯論學會的好處遠遠超越獎盃本身。"},{"label":"Paragraph 18","english":"Debating strengthens English because it forces us to choose words precisely, structure ideas logically and speak to a real audience.","chinese":"辯論能強化英語能力，因為它迫使我們精準選詞、有邏輯地組織觀點，並向真實聽眾發言。"},{"label":"Paragraph 19","english":"Reading model essays is useful; having to defend your own argument under pressure is another matter altogether.","chinese":"閱讀範文固然有用；然而，要壓力下捍衛自己的論點，就是完全另一回事了"},{"label":"Paragraph 20","english":"Take a shy junior student, for example.","chinese":"以一位害羞的低年級學生為例。"},{"label":"Paragraph 21","english":"At first, she may whisper from a script, avoid eye contact and panic when challenged.","chinese":"起初，她可能會對著稿子小聲朗讀、避免眼神接觸，並在受到挑戰時感慌張"},{"label":"Paragraph 22","english":"Little by little, however, she learns to open with a hook, signpost her points, respond to objections and end with impact.","chinese":"然而，一點一滴地，她會學懂用吸引人的開首破題、清楚標示論點、回應反對意見，並以有力的方式收結。"},{"label":"Paragraph 23","english":"By the second or third debate, she may not become a champion yet, but she will already be a more confident speaker.","chinese":"到了第二或第三場辯論時，她可能還未成為冠軍，但她已經會是一位更有自信的演說者。"},{"label":"Paragraph 24","english":"More importantly, debating makes us better teammates.","chinese":"更重要的是，辯論使我們成為更好的隊友。"},{"label":"Paragraph 25","english":"In strong teams, people challenge each other without humiliating one another.","chinese":"在優秀的團隊中，成員會互相挑戰，但不會彼此羞辱。"},{"label":"Paragraph 26","english":"We learn that disagreement is not disrespect, and that a stronger argument often begins with better listening.","chinese":"我們會明白，意見分歧並不等於不尊重，而更有力的論點往往始於更好的聆聽"},{"label":"Paragraph 27","english":"Finally, being a good debater is important in life because life itself is full of arguments.","chinese":"最後，成為一位優秀辯手在人生中十分重要，因為人生本身就充滿不同的論辯"},{"label":"Paragraph 28","english":"Advertisements tell us what to buy.","chinese":"廣告告訴我們應該買甚麼。"},{"label":"Paragraph 29","english":"Social media tells us what to believe.","chinese":"社交媒體告訴我們應該相信甚麼。"},{"label":"Paragraph 30","english":"Friends, parents, teachers and future employers will all, in different ways, ask us to explain what we think and why.","chinese":"朋友、父母、老師和未來僱主，都會以不同方式要求我們解釋自己的想法及其理由。"},{"label":"Paragraph 31","english":"If we cannot separate evidence from emotion, confidence from accuracy, or persuasion from manipulation, we run the risk of being led by the loudest voice in the room.","chinese":"如果我們無法把證據與情緒、信心與準確性，或說服與操控區分開來，我們就有可能被房間裡最大聲的人牽著走。"},{"label":"Paragraph 32","english":"A good debater does not simply ask, “How can I win?”","chinese":"一位優秀辯手不會只問：「我怎樣才能贏？」"},{"label":"Paragraph 33","english":"Rather, a good debater asks, “What is true? What is fair? What have I failed to consider?”","chinese":"更準確地說，一位優秀辯手會問：「甚麼才是真實的？甚麼才是公平的？我有甚麼尚未考慮到？」"},{"label":"Paragraph 34","english":"Only by asking these questions can we become citizens who speak with courage and listen with humility.","chinese":"只有透過提出這些問題，我們才能成為敢於發言、謙卑聆聽的公民。"},{"label":"Paragraph 35","english":"The pen may be mightier than the sword, but a well-reasoned voice can be just as powerful.","chinese":"筆也許比劍更有力量，但有充分理據支撐的聲音，同樣可以極具力量。"},{"label":"Paragraph 36","english":"So, fellow students, whether you dream of becoming a lawyer, a journalist, a doctor, an entrepreneur, or simply someone who can stand tall when it matters, the debating club has something to offer you.","chinese":"所以，各位同學，無論你夢想成為律師、記者、醫生、企業家，還是只想在關鍵時刻能昂首挺立的人，辯論學會都能給你一些有價值的東西。"},{"label":"Paragraph 37","english":"Do not wait until you are “good enough” to join; join so that you can become good enough.","chinese":"不要等到自己「夠好」才加入；你應該加入，然後讓自己變得夠好。"},{"label":"Paragraph 38","english":"Sign up at our booth outside the hall after assembly, or speak to any committee member this week.","chinese":"請在早會後到禮堂外的攤位報名，或在本週內向任何一位幹事查詢。"},{"label":"Paragraph 39","english":"The sooner you begin, the better.","chinese":"你開始得越早越好。"},{"label":"Paragraph 40","english":"One thing is for sure - your voice is worth training, and we would love to have you on the team.","chinese":"有一件事可以肯定——你的聲音值得訓練，我們也非常希望你加入這個團隊"},{"label":"Paragraph 41","english":"Thank you.","chinese":"謝謝大家。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"speak up","chinese":"大膽發言"},{"english":"think sharply","chinese":"敏銳地思考"},{"english":"stand tall","chinese":"堂堂正正地站穩"},{"english":"Principal, teachers and fellow students","chinese":"校長、老師及各位同學"},{"english":"have you ever","chinese":"你有沒有試過"},{"english":"hear a comment","chinese":"聽到一句評論"},{"english":"disagree with","chinese":"不同意"},{"english":"the perfect reply","chinese":"最完美的回應"},{"english":"only after","chinese":"直到……之後才"},{"english":"you are not alone","chinese":"你並不孤單"},{"english":"a world where","chinese":"一個……的世界"},{"english":"opinions travel faster than facts","chinese":"意見比事實傳播得更快"},{"english":"want to speak up","chinese":"想大膽發言"},{"english":"do not quite know how","chinese":"不太知道怎樣做"},{"english":"school debating club","chinese":"學校辯論學會"},{"english":"look for new members","chinese":"招募新會員"},{"english":"make room for","chinese":"為……騰出位置"},{"english":"curious","chinese":"好奇的"},{"english":"nervous","chinese":"緊張的"},{"english":"outspoken","chinese":"直言不諱的"},{"english":"completely new","chinese":"完全沒有經驗的"},{"english":"think clearly","chinese":"清晰思考"},{"english":"speak confidently","chinese":"有信心地說話"},{"english":"listen respectfully","chinese":"尊重地聆聽"},{"english":"I would like to show you that","chinese":"我想向你們說明"},{"english":"not just an activity for","chinese":"不只是給……的活動"},{"english":"the loudest students","chinese":"聲音最大的學生"},{"english":"training for anyone who","chinese":"給任何想……的人的訓練"},{"english":"sharper, braver and fairer","chinese":"更敏銳、更勇敢、更公平"},{"english":"there is more to…than…","chinese":"……不只是……"},{"english":"stand behind a lectern","chinese":"站在講台後"},{"english":"argue for","chinese":"支持……作出論證"},{"english":"practical training sessions","chinese":"實用訓練課節"},{"english":"case-building","chinese":"建構論點"},{"english":"rebuttal","chinese":"反駁"},{"english":"delivery","chinese":"演說表達"},{"english":"current affairs","chinese":"時事"},{"english":"examine whether","chinese":"探討是否"},{"english":"be reduced","chinese":"被減少"},{"english":"artificial intelligence","chinese":"人工智能"},{"english":"animal protection","chinese":"動物保護"},{"english":"school uniforms","chinese":"校服"},{"english":"waste problem","chinese":"廢物問題"},{"english":"brainstorming motions","chinese":"集思廣益想辯題"},{"english":"polishing speeches","chinese":"打磨演辭"},{"english":"mock debates","chinese":"模擬辯論"},{"english":"post-match feedback","chinese":"賽後回饋"},{"english":"be designed to","chinese":"旨在"},{"english":"improve step by step","chinese":"一步一步進步"},{"english":"impromptu challenge","chinese":"即興挑戰"},{"english":"be given a motion","chinese":"獲給予一個辯題"},{"english":"prepare","chinese":"準備"},{"english":"sounds terrifying","chinese":"聽起來很可怕"},{"english":"not quite","chinese":"並不完全是這樣"},{"english":"in fact","chinese":"事實上"},{"english":"the funniest part of the term","chinese":"學期中最有趣的部分"},{"english":"think on their feet","chinese":"即場思考"},{"english":"support one another","chinese":"互相支持"},{"english":"laugh at mistakes","chinese":"對錯誤一笑置之"},{"english":"instead of fearing them","chinese":"而不是害怕它們"},{"english":"better still","chinese":"更好的是"},{"english":"inter-school competitions","chinese":"聯校比賽"},{"english":"friendly debates","chinese":"友誼辯論賽"},{"english":"neighbouring schools","chinese":"鄰近學校"},{"english":"give members the chance to","chinese":"給會員機會去……"},{"english":"accents and styles","chinese":"口音和風格"},{"english":"different from their own","chinese":"與自己的不同"},{"english":"the benefits of joining","chinese":"加入……的好處"},{"english":"go far beyond","chinese":"遠遠超出"},{"english":"trophies","chinese":"獎盃"},{"english":"strengthens English","chinese":"增強英文能力"},{"english":"force someone to","chinese":"迫使某人去……"},{"english":"choose words precisely","chinese":"精準用字"},{"english":"structure ideas logically","chinese":"有邏輯地組織想法"},{"english":"speak to a real audience","chinese":"對真正的觀眾說話"},{"english":"model essays","chinese":"範文"},{"english":"defend your own argument","chinese":"捍衛自己的論點"},{"english":"under pressure","chinese":"在壓力下"},{"english":"another matter altogether","chinese":"完全是另一回事"},{"english":"take…for example","chinese":"以……為例"},{"english":"shy junior student","chinese":"害羞的低年級學生"},{"english":"whisper from a script","chinese":"照著稿子小聲讀"},{"english":"avoid eye contact","chinese":"避免眼神接觸"},{"english":"panic when challenged","chinese":"被質疑時慌張"},{"english":"little by little","chinese":"漸漸地"},{"english":"open with a hook","chinese":"以吸引人的開場開始"},{"english":"signpost her points","chinese":"清楚標示自己的論點"},{"english":"respond to objections","chinese":"回應反對意見"},{"english":"end with impact","chinese":"以有力方式結尾"},{"english":"become a champion","chinese":"成為冠軍"},{"english":"a more confident speaker","chinese":"更有信心的演說者"},{"english":"more importantly","chinese":"更重要的是"},{"english":"better teammates","chinese":"更好的隊友"},{"english":"strong teams","chinese":"強大的團隊"},{"english":"challenge each other","chinese":"互相挑戰"},{"english":"without humiliating one another","chinese":"不羞辱彼此"},{"english":"disagreement is not disrespect","chinese":"不同意並不等於不尊重"},{"english":"a stronger argument","chinese":"更有力的論點"},{"english":"better listening","chinese":"更好的聆聽"},{"english":"being a good debater","chinese":"成為一名優秀辯手"},{"english":"life itself","chinese":"生活本身"},{"english":"full of arguments","chinese":"充滿爭論"},{"english":"advertisements","chinese":"廣告"},{"english":"what to believe","chinese":"該相信甚麼"},{"english":"future employers","chinese":"未來僱主"},{"english":"in different ways","chinese":"以不同方式"},{"english":"explain what we think and why","chinese":"解釋我們的想法及原因"},{"english":"separate evidence from emotion","chinese":"分辨證據與情緒"},{"english":"confidence from accuracy","chinese":"分辨自信與準確性"},{"english":"persuasion from manipulation","chinese":"分辨說服與操控"},{"english":"run the risk of","chinese":"冒着……的風險"},{"english":"be led by","chinese":"被……帶着走"},{"english":"the loudest voice in the room","chinese":"房間裏最大聲的聲音"},{"english":"does not simply ask","chinese":"不只是問"},{"english":"rather","chinese":"反而；更準確地說"},{"english":"what have I failed to consider?","chinese":"我忽略了甚麼？"},{"english":"only by asking","chinese":"只有透過提出"},{"english":"speak with courage","chinese":"勇敢地發言"},{"english":"listen with humility","chinese":"謙卑地聆聽"},{"english":"the pen may be mightier than the sword","chinese":"筆比劍更有力量"},{"english":"a well-reasoned voice","chinese":"有充分理據的聲音"},{"english":"just as powerful","chinese":"同樣有力量"},{"english":"whether you dream of becoming","chinese":"無論你夢想成為"},{"english":"lawyer","chinese":"律師"},{"english":"journalist","chinese":"記者"},{"english":"entrepreneur","chinese":"企業家"},{"english":"when it matters","chinese":"在關鍵時刻"},{"english":"have something to offer","chinese":"能給予……一些有價值的東西"},{"english":"good enough to join","chinese":"好到足以加入"},{"english":"join so that","chinese":"加入，好讓"},{"english":"sign up at our booth","chinese":"在我們的攤位報名"},{"english":"outside the hall","chinese":"禮堂外"},{"english":"after assembly","chinese":"早會後"},{"english":"committee member","chinese":"委員會成員"},{"english":"the sooner…the better","chinese":"越早……越好"},{"english":"one thing is for sure","chinese":"有一點可以肯定"},{"english":"worth training","chinese":"值得訓練"},{"english":"love to have you on the team","chinese":"很希望你加入我們的團隊"}]},"dse-writing-2012-part-b-q6":{"exerciseId":"dse-writing-2012-part-b-q6","essayKey":"","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=dse-writing-2012-part-b-q6","flashDeckId":"dse/writing/part-b/2012/Q6","paragraphs":[{"label":"Paragraph 1","english":"Beyond the Mirror: Hong Kong Must Resist the Tyranny of Beauty","chinese":""},{"label":"Paragraph 2","english":"Dear Editor,","chinese":""},{"label":"Paragraph 3","english":"I am writing to express my deep concern about Hong Kong’s growing obsession with physical beauty. The wish to look attractive is, of course, human and understandable. Yet, with beauty filters, celebrity culture and cosmetic-surgery advertisements appearing everywhere from MTR billboards to social media feeds, many citizens—especially young people—are being encouraged to alter their faces and bodies in order to gain confidence, acceptance and even opportunities. As far as I am concerned, this trend is not merely a matter of personal taste; it reflects a culture that has begun to confuse appearance with worth. Unless we challenge this unhealthy obsession, we will raise a generation that knows how to edit a selfie but not how to value itself.","chinese":""},{"label":"Paragraph 4","english":"First and foremost, the worship of physical beauty damages people’s self-esteem by turning ordinary features into supposed defects. A teenager with single eyelids, freckles or a round face may once have regarded these as harmless parts of their identity. Now, after scrolling through endless images of sharpened jawlines, flawless skin and impossibly slim bodies, they may start to see themselves as unfinished projects. The more they compare, the less they accept; the less they accept, the more vulnerable they become to products and procedures promising a “better” face. Take a Secondary Four student, for example. If she receives fewer “likes” than a classmate who uses filters, she may conclude not that the online world is artificial, but that she herself is inadequate. Such thinking can lead to anxiety, social withdrawal, disordered eating and a constant fear of being judged. Beauty, in this sense, is no longer a pleasure. It becomes a test that nobody can pass for long. A society that teaches its young people to examine every pore is, in effect, teaching them to doubt every part of themselves.","chinese":""},{"label":"Paragraph 5","english":"Equally worrying is the way the beauty industry profits from insecurity while pretending to sell empowerment. Cosmetic surgery may be a legitimate choice for adults who make informed decisions, and far be it from me to condemn every individual who chooses it. The problem is that the industry often creates the very dissatisfaction it claims to cure. Clinics advertise “small improvements” as if natural faces were problems waiting to be corrected. Influencers describe injections, eyelid surgery or nose reshaping as casually as buying lipstick. Before long, what was once exceptional begins to look normal; what was once normal begins to look unacceptable. For one thing, this places financial pressure on people who can barely afford tuition fees, rent or family expenses. For another, it reinforces discrimination against those who cannot or do not wish to conform. If job applicants, flight attendants, receptionists or even dating-app users feel that looking polished matters more than being capable, then our city is rewarding surface over substance. That is not progress. It is simply vanity dressed up as success.","chinese":""},{"label":"Paragraph 6","english":"Some may argue that caring about appearance is harmless because a smart outfit, clear skin or a confident smile can open doors. I take that point, but it does not solve the deeper problem. There is a difference between healthy grooming and obsessive self-reconstruction. The former helps people present themselves respectfully; the latter persuades them that they are never enough. Just because beauty can bring advantages does not mean society should magnify those advantages until character, kindness and competence are pushed aside. After all, a friendly nurse, an honest salesperson or a patient teacher contributes far more to Hong Kong than someone whose only achievement is looking flawless online. Handsome is as handsome does.","chinese":""},{"label":"Paragraph 7","english":"Therefore, the time has come for schools, parents, advertisers and the media to restore balance. Schools should include media-literacy education so that students can identify edited images and manipulative advertising. Parents should praise effort, courage and compassion more often than appearance. Newspapers such as the Hong Kong Express can also help by featuring people of different ages, sizes and appearances, not only those who fit a narrow commercial ideal. Beauty is not the enemy; obsession is. We should teach our young people to look in the mirror and see a person, not a product.","chinese":""},{"label":"Paragraph 8","english":"Yours faithfully,","chinese":""},{"label":"Paragraph 9","english":"Chris Wong","chinese":""}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"beyond the mirror","chinese":"超越鏡中的外貌"},{"english":"resist the tyranny of beauty","chinese":"抵抗美貌霸權"},{"english":"tyranny of beauty","chinese":"美貌霸權"},{"english":"Dear Editor","chinese":"尊敬的編輯"},{"english":"express my deep concern about","chinese":"表達我對……的深切關注"},{"english":"growing obsession with","chinese":"對……日益沉迷"},{"english":"physical beauty","chinese":"外貌美"},{"english":"the wish to look attractive","chinese":"想變得吸引人的願望"},{"english":"of course","chinese":"當然"},{"english":"human and understandable","chinese":"合乎人性而可以理解"},{"english":"beauty filters","chinese":"美顏濾鏡"},{"english":"celebrity culture","chinese":"名人文化"},{"english":"cosmetic-surgery advertisements","chinese":"整容廣告"},{"english":"appear everywhere from…to…","chinese":"從……到……隨處可見"},{"english":"MTR billboards","chinese":"港鐵廣告牌"},{"english":"social media feeds","chinese":"社交媒體動態"},{"english":"especially young people","chinese":"尤其是年輕人"},{"english":"be encouraged to","chinese":"被鼓勵去"},{"english":"alter their faces and bodies","chinese":"改變面貌和身體"},{"english":"in order to","chinese":"為了"},{"english":"gain confidence, acceptance and opportunities","chinese":"獲得自信、認同和機會"},{"english":"as far as I am concerned","chinese":"就我而言"},{"english":"not merely a matter of personal taste","chinese":"不只是個人品味問題"},{"english":"reflect a culture that","chinese":"反映一種……的文化"},{"english":"confuse appearance with worth","chinese":"混淆外貌與價值"},{"english":"unless we challenge","chinese":"除非我們挑戰"},{"english":"unhealthy obsession","chinese":"不健康的沉迷"},{"english":"raise a generation that","chinese":"培養出一代……的人"},{"english":"edit a selfie","chinese":"修圖自拍"},{"english":"value itself","chinese":"重視自身價值"},{"english":"first and foremost","chinese":"首先；最重要的是"},{"english":"the worship of physical beauty","chinese":"對外貌美的崇拜"},{"english":"damage self-esteem","chinese":"損害自尊"},{"english":"turn ordinary features into supposed defects","chinese":"把普通特徵變成所謂缺陷"},{"english":"ordinary features","chinese":"普通外貌特徵"},{"english":"supposed defects","chinese":"所謂缺陷"},{"english":"single eyelids","chinese":"單眼皮"},{"english":"freckles","chinese":"雀斑"},{"english":"a round face","chinese":"圓臉"},{"english":"regard these as","chinese":"把這些視為"},{"english":"harmless parts of their identity","chinese":"身分中無害的一部分"},{"english":"scroll through endless images","chinese":"不停瀏覽無窮無盡的圖片"},{"english":"sharpened jawlines","chinese":"尖削下顎線"},{"english":"flawless skin","chinese":"無瑕肌膚"},{"english":"impossibly slim bodies","chinese":"瘦得不切實際的身形"},{"english":"start to see themselves as","chinese":"開始把自己視為"},{"english":"unfinished projects","chinese":"未完成的改造項目"},{"english":"the more…, the less…","chinese":"越……，就越少……"},{"english":"the less…, the more vulnerable…","chinese":"越少……，就越容易受……影響"},{"english":"become vulnerable to","chinese":"容易受……影響"},{"english":"products and procedures","chinese":"產品和療程"},{"english":"promise a “better” face","chinese":"承諾帶來一張「更好」的臉"},{"english":"take…, for example","chinese":"以……為例"},{"english":"receive fewer “likes”","chinese":"獲得較少「讚好」"},{"english":"use filters","chinese":"使用濾鏡"},{"english":"conclude not that…, but that…","chinese":"得出的結論不是……，而是……"},{"english":"the online world is artificial","chinese":"網上世界是人為加工的"},{"english":"feel inadequate","chinese":"覺得自己不夠好"},{"english":"such thinking","chinese":"這種想法"},{"english":"lead to anxiety","chinese":"導致焦慮"},{"english":"social withdrawal","chinese":"社交退縮"},{"english":"disordered eating","chinese":"飲食失調"},{"english":"a constant fear of being judged","chinese":"持續害怕被評價"},{"english":"in this sense","chinese":"從這個意義上說"},{"english":"no longer a pleasure","chinese":"不再是一種愉悅"},{"english":"a test that nobody can pass for long","chinese":"沒有人能長久通過的考驗"},{"english":"examine every pore","chinese":"檢視每一個毛孔"},{"english":"in effect","chinese":"實際上"},{"english":"doubt every part of themselves","chinese":"懷疑自己的每一部分"},{"english":"equally worrying","chinese":"同樣令人憂慮的是"},{"english":"profit from insecurity","chinese":"從不安全感中獲利"},{"english":"pretend to sell empowerment","chinese":"假裝出售自主力量"},{"english":"cosmetic surgery","chinese":"整容手術"},{"english":"legitimate choice","chinese":"合理選擇"},{"english":"make informed decisions","chinese":"作出知情決定"},{"english":"far be it from me to","chinese":"我絕不會……"},{"english":"condemn every individual","chinese":"譴責每一個人"},{"english":"the problem is that","chinese":"問題是"},{"english":"create the very dissatisfaction it claims to cure","chinese":"製造它聲稱要治癒的不滿"},{"english":"claim to cure","chinese":"聲稱能治癒"},{"english":"advertise “small improvements”","chinese":"宣傳「小改善」"},{"english":"as if","chinese":"彷彿"},{"english":"natural faces","chinese":"天然面貌"},{"english":"problems waiting to be corrected","chinese":"等待被修正的問題"},{"english":"influencers describe","chinese":"網紅形容"},{"english":"injections","chinese":"注射療程"},{"english":"eyelid surgery","chinese":"眼皮手術"},{"english":"nose reshaping","chinese":"鼻形重塑"},{"english":"as casually as buying lipstick","chinese":"像買唇膏一樣隨便"},{"english":"before long","chinese":"不久之後"},{"english":"what was once exceptional","chinese":"曾經非比尋常的事"},{"english":"begin to look normal","chinese":"開始顯得正常"},{"english":"what was once normal","chinese":"曾經正常的事"},{"english":"begin to look unacceptable","chinese":"開始顯得不可接受"},{"english":"for one thing","chinese":"一方面"},{"english":"place financial pressure on","chinese":"對……造成經濟壓力"},{"english":"can barely afford","chinese":"勉強負擔得起"},{"english":"tuition fees","chinese":"學費"},{"english":"rent","chinese":"租金"},{"english":"family expenses","chinese":"家庭開支"},{"english":"for another","chinese":"另一方面"},{"english":"reinforce discrimination against","chinese":"加深對……的歧視"},{"english":"conform","chinese":"順從；迎合"},{"english":"job applicants","chinese":"求職者"},{"english":"flight attendants","chinese":"空中服務員"},{"english":"receptionists","chinese":"接待員"},{"english":"dating-app users","chinese":"交友應用程式用戶"},{"english":"looking polished","chinese":"外表得體"},{"english":"matter more than being capable","chinese":"比有能力更重要"},{"english":"reward surface over substance","chinese":"重外表多於內涵"},{"english":"that is not progress","chinese":"那不是進步"},{"english":"vanity dressed up as success","chinese":"披着成功外衣的虛榮"},{"english":"some may argue that","chinese":"有些人可能會認為"},{"english":"caring about appearance","chinese":"注重外表"},{"english":"a smart outfit","chinese":"得體醒目的衣着"},{"english":"clear skin","chinese":"乾淨透亮的皮膚"},{"english":"a confident smile","chinese":"自信的笑容"},{"english":"open doors","chinese":"帶來機會"},{"english":"I take that point","chinese":"我明白這一點"},{"english":"the deeper problem","chinese":"更深層的問題"},{"english":"there is a difference between","chinese":"……和……之間有分別"},{"english":"healthy grooming","chinese":"健康得體的打扮"},{"english":"obsessive self-reconstruction","chinese":"令人着迷的自我改造"},{"english":"the former","chinese":"前者"},{"english":"the latter","chinese":"後者"},{"english":"present themselves respectfully","chinese":"得體地展現自己"},{"english":"persuade someone that","chinese":"說服某人相信"},{"english":"never enough","chinese":"永遠不夠好"},{"english":"just because…does not mean…","chinese":"只是因為……並不代表……"},{"english":"bring advantages","chinese":"帶來優勢"},{"english":"magnify those advantages","chinese":"放大那些優勢"},{"english":"character, kindness and competence","chinese":"品格、善良和能力"},{"english":"be pushed aside","chinese":"被擠到一旁"},{"english":"after all","chinese":"畢竟"},{"english":"a friendly nurse","chinese":"友善的護士"},{"english":"an honest salesperson","chinese":"誠實的銷售員"},{"english":"a patient teacher","chinese":"有耐性的老師"},{"english":"contribute far more to","chinese":"對……貢獻大得多"},{"english":"only achievement","chinese":"唯一成就"},{"english":"looking flawless online","chinese":"在網上看起來完美無瑕"},{"english":"Handsome is as handsome does","chinese":"行為美才是真正美"},{"english":"the time has come for","chinese":"是時候……"},{"english":"restore balance","chinese":"恢復平衡"},{"english":"media-literacy education","chinese":"媒體素養教育"},{"english":"identify edited images","chinese":"辨認經修圖的圖片"},{"english":"manipulative advertising","chinese":"具操控性的廣告"},{"english":"praise effort, courage and compassion","chinese":"讚賞努力、勇氣和同情心"},{"english":"more often than appearance","chinese":"比外貌更常"},{"english":"newspapers such as","chinese":"例如……這類報章"},{"english":"feature people of different ages, sizes and appearances","chinese":"報道不同年齡、身形和外貌的人"},{"english":"fit a narrow commercial ideal","chinese":"符合狹窄的商業理想"},{"english":"Beauty is not the enemy; obsession is","chinese":"美不是敵人，沉迷才是"},{"english":"look in the mirror","chinese":"照鏡"},{"english":"see a person, not a product","chinese":"看見一個人，而不是一件產品"},{"english":"Yours faithfully","chinese":"此致敬禮"}]},"dse-writing-2012-part-b-q7":{"exerciseId":"dse-writing-2012-part-b-q7","essayKey":"","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=dse-writing-2012-part-b-q7","flashDeckId":"dse/writing/part-b/2012/Q7","paragraphs":[{"label":"Paragraph 1","english":"The Key That Wasn’t His","chinese":"那把不屬於他的鑰匙"},{"label":"Paragraph 2","english":"Hardly had the rain stopped when the Peninsula Hotel began to shine.","chinese":"雨才剛停，半島酒店便開始閃耀起來。"},{"label":"Paragraph 3","english":"I was walking by the Peninsula Hotel in Tsim Sha Tsui, my bag biting into my shoulder and the smell of wet traffic rising from Salisbury Road. Then a silver sports car slid towards the entrance, its engine purring like an animal that knew people were watching.","chinese":"我正走過尖沙咀半島酒店旁邊，袋子勒得我的肩膀隱隱作痛，濕漉漉的車流氣味從梳士巴利道升起。 接着，一輛銀色跑車滑向入口，引擎低低轟鳴，像一頭知道眾人正在注視牠的動物。"},{"label":"Paragraph 4","english":"At the wheel was my brother, Aaron.","chinese":"坐在駕駛座上的，是我的哥哥 Aaron。"},{"label":"Paragraph 5","english":"For a moment, I simply stared. The last time we had spoken, he had been sitting at our kitchen table in a faded T-shirt, circling job advertisements with a pencil. “I’ll take anything,” he had said. “Office assistant, delivery worker, waiter—anything.” Now he was wearing a dark suit and driving a car that probably cost more than our flat.","chinese":"有那麼一刻，我只是呆呆地看着。 我們上一次說話時，他還坐在家中廚房的餐桌旁，穿着一件褪色的 T 恤，用鉛筆圈着招聘廣告。 「甚麼工作我都願意做，」他當時說。 「辦公室助理、送貨員、侍應——甚麼都可以。」 現在，他穿着深色西裝，駕駛着一輛價錢大概比我們的單位還要高的車。"},{"label":"Paragraph 6","english":"Before I could call his name, a woman in a cream coat stepped forward and handed him a white envelope. Aaron looked around quickly, not proudly, but nervously. Then he drove off.","chinese":"我還未來得及叫他的名字，一位穿着米色外套的女人便走上前，把一個白色信封交給他。 然後，他開車離開了。"},{"label":"Paragraph 7","english":"Something felt wrong.","chinese":"事情總有點不對勁。"},{"label":"Paragraph 8","english":"I should have gone home. Instead, I jumped into the first taxi I saw and pointed at the sports car disappearing down the road.","chinese":"我本來應該回家。 相反，我跳進看到的第一輛的士，指向那輛正沿路消失的跑車。"},{"label":"Paragraph 9","english":"“Follow that car, please,” I said.","chinese":"「請跟着那輛車，」我說。"},{"label":"Paragraph 10","english":"The driver glanced at me in the mirror. “Movie scene?”","chinese":"司機從倒後鏡瞥了我一眼。 「拍電影？」"},{"label":"Paragraph 11","english":"“Family problem,” I muttered.","chinese":"「家庭問題，」我低聲說。"},{"label":"Paragraph 12","english":"No sooner had we turned past the harbour than my mind began to betray Aaron. Was he working for some rich stranger? Had he borrowed money? Worse still, had he become involved in something illegal? I hated myself for thinking it, but worry has a cruel imagination.","chinese":"我們剛轉過海旁，我的腦袋便開始背叛 Aaron。 他是在替某個有錢陌生人辦事嗎？ 他借了錢嗎？ 更糟的是，他會否已經牽涉到某些非法事情？ 我憎恨自己竟然這樣想，可是憂慮總有一種殘忍的想像力。"},{"label":"Paragraph 13","english":"The car finally stopped outside a hospital in Kowloon. Aaron got out and hurried to the passenger side. I stepped from the taxi, ready to demand an explanation, only to find myself frozen by what I saw.","chinese":"那輛車最後停在九龍一間醫院外。 我從的士走出來，本來準備要求他解釋，結果卻被眼前所見震得僵在原地。"},{"label":"Paragraph 14","english":"A little girl in a wheelchair was waiting under the shelter. She wore a woollen hat decorated with yellow stars, and her face was so pale that the hat looked brighter than the rest of her. The woman in the cream coat stood behind her, clutching the folder.","chinese":"一個坐在輪椅上的小女孩正在簷篷下等待。 她戴着一頂綴有黃色星星的羊毛帽，臉色蒼白得令那頂帽子比她身上其他一切都更明亮。 那位穿着米色外套的女人站在她身後，緊緊抱着文件夾。"},{"label":"Paragraph 15","english":"Aaron knelt beside the girl and smiled.","chinese":"在女孩身旁跪下，向她微笑。"},{"label":"Paragraph 16","english":"“Miss Chloe,” he said, “your carriage awaits.”","chinese":"小姐，」他說，「你的馬車正在恭候。」"},{"label":"Paragraph 17","english":"The girl laughed brightly enough to cut through the grey afternoon.","chinese":"女孩笑得明亮，彷彿足以劃破灰沉沉的午後。"},{"label":"Paragraph 18","english":"Only then did I notice the small sticker on the car door: Dream Ride Foundation.","chinese":"直到那時，我才注意到車門上的小貼紙：Dream Ride Foundation。"},{"label":"Paragraph 19","english":"Aaron saw me a second later. His smile faded.","chinese":"一秒後，Aaron 看見了我。 他的笑容淡了下來。"},{"label":"Paragraph 20","english":"“What are you doing here, Mary?”","chinese":"你在這裡做甚麼？」"},{"label":"Paragraph 21","english":"“I could ask you the same thing,” I said, though my anger was already weakening.","chinese":"「我也可以問你同一個問題，」我說，雖然我的怒氣已經開始減弱。"},{"label":"Paragraph 22","english":"He looked at Chloe, then at me. “Give me twenty minutes.”","chinese":"他看了看 Chloe，又看了看我。 「給我二十分鐘。」"},{"label":"Paragraph 23","english":"I waited by the entrance as Aaron helped Chloe into the car with a care I had never seen in him before. They did not race away. They drove slowly, almost ceremonially, around the block while Chloe waved at her mother as if she were a princess in a parade.","chinese":"我在入口旁等着，看着 Aaron 以一種我從未在他身上見過的細心，把 Chloe 扶進車裡。 他們沒有疾馳而去。 他們緩緩地繞着街區行駛，幾乎像在進行某種儀式，而 Chloe 向母親揮手，彷彿自己是巡遊中的公主。"},{"label":"Paragraph 24","english":"When Aaron returned, he loosened his tie and came over.","chinese":"回來時，鬆了鬆領帶，然後走過來。"},{"label":"Paragraph 25","english":"“The car isn’t mine,” he said before I could speak. “It belongs to a businessman who lends it to the foundation twice a month. The envelope had Chloe’s medical consent forms.”","chinese":"我還未開口，他便說：「那輛車不屬於我。」 「它屬於一位商人，他每個月會把車借給基金會兩次。 那個信封裡裝着 Chloe 的醫療同意書。」"},{"label":"Paragraph 26","english":"“And the Peninsula?”","chinese":"「那半島酒店呢？」"},{"label":"Paragraph 27","english":"“Chloe loves old Hong Kong movies. She wanted to arrive there like a film star before her treatment.” He gave a tired smile. “I’m the driver and programme assistant. Temporary, poorly paid, and definitely not glamorous.”","chinese":"她想在治療前像電影明星一樣抵達那裡。」 他露出一個疲憊的笑容。 「我是司機，也是項目助理。 臨時性質、薪水微薄，而且絕對稱不上風光。」"},{"label":"Paragraph 28","english":"I was silent.","chinese":"我沉默了。"},{"label":"Paragraph 29","english":"He continued, “I didn’t tell Mum and Dad because I wanted to make sure I could keep the job first. After being rejected so many times, I couldn’t bear another disappointed look. But this place gave me a chance. The children don’t care about my exam results. They care whether I show up.”","chinese":"他繼續說：「我沒有告訴爸媽，因為我想先確定自己能保住這份工作。 被拒絕那麼多次之後，我再也承受不起另一個失望的眼神。 但這個地方給了我一次機會。 孩子們並不在意我的考試成績。 他們在意的是我會不會出現。」"},{"label":"Paragraph 30","english":"It dawned on me then that I had mistaken appearance for truth. All that glittered was not gold; sometimes it was only borrowed metal, polished for a child who needed one beautiful afternoon.","chinese":"那一刻我才明白，我把外表誤認成了真相。 凡是閃亮的東西都未必是黃金；有時，它只是借來的金屬，為了一個需要美好午後的孩子而被擦亮。"},{"label":"Paragraph 31","english":"“I’m sorry,” I whispered.","chinese":"「對不起，」我低聲說。"},{"label":"Paragraph 32","english":"Aaron shrugged, but his eyes softened. “You were worried. That counts for something.”","chinese":"「你只是擔心我。 這已經有它的意義了。」"},{"label":"Paragraph 33","english":"That evening, we went home together by minibus, not sports car. Aaron carried no secret fortune, no miracle. Only a job badge, a tired smile and, in his pocket, a key that was never his.","chinese":"那天晚上，我們一起坐小巴回家，沒有坐跑車。 只有一個工作證、一個疲憊的笑容，還有他口袋裡那把從未屬於他的鑰匙。"},{"label":"Paragraph 34","english":"Yet in my eyes, he had never looked richer.","chinese":"然而在我眼中，他從未如此富有。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"the key that wasn't his","chinese":"不屬於他的鑰匙"},{"english":"Hardly had… when…","chinese":"剛……就……"},{"english":"the rain stopped","chinese":"雨停了"},{"english":"the Peninsula Hotel","chinese":"半島酒店"},{"english":"begin to shine","chinese":"開始發亮"},{"english":"walk by","chinese":"走過"},{"english":"Tsim Sha Tsui","chinese":"尖沙咀"},{"english":"bag biting into my shoulder","chinese":"袋子勒得肩膀發痛"},{"english":"smell of wet traffic","chinese":"雨後車流的氣味"},{"english":"rise from","chinese":"從……升起"},{"english":"Salisbury Road","chinese":"梳士巴利道"},{"english":"silver sports car","chinese":"銀色跑車"},{"english":"slide towards","chinese":"滑向"},{"english":"hotel entrance","chinese":"酒店入口"},{"english":"engine purring","chinese":"引擎低聲嗚嗚作響"},{"english":"like an animal that knew people were watching","chinese":"像一隻知道有人注視的動物"},{"english":"at the wheel","chinese":"在駕駛座上"},{"english":"for a moment","chinese":"有一刻"},{"english":"simply stared","chinese":"只是呆望着"},{"english":"the last time we had spoken","chinese":"我們上次說話時"},{"english":"kitchen table","chinese":"廚房餐枱"},{"english":"faded T-shirt","chinese":"褪色T恤"},{"english":"circle job advertisements","chinese":"圈起招聘廣告"},{"english":"job advertisements","chinese":"招聘廣告"},{"english":"I'll take anything","chinese":"甚麼工作都願意做"},{"english":"office assistant","chinese":"辦公室助理"},{"english":"delivery worker","chinese":"送貨員"},{"english":"dark suit","chinese":"深色西裝"},{"english":"cost more than","chinese":"比……更貴"},{"english":"before I could","chinese":"還未及我……"},{"english":"call his name","chinese":"叫他的名字"},{"english":"cream coat","chinese":"米色外套"},{"english":"step forward","chinese":"走上前"},{"english":"hand someone an envelope","chinese":"遞給某人一個信封"},{"english":"white envelope","chinese":"白色信封"},{"english":"look around quickly","chinese":"迅速四處張望"},{"english":"not proudly, but nervously","chinese":"不是驕傲地，而是緊張地"},{"english":"drive off","chinese":"開車離開"},{"english":"something felt wrong","chinese":"感覺有點不對勁"},{"english":"should have gone home","chinese":"本應回家"},{"english":"jump into the first taxi","chinese":"跳上第一輛的士"},{"english":"point at","chinese":"指向"},{"english":"disappear down the road","chinese":"沿路遠去"},{"english":"follow that car","chinese":"跟着那輛車"},{"english":"glance at someone in the mirror","chinese":"從倒後鏡瞥某人"},{"english":"movie scene","chinese":"電影場面"},{"english":"family problem","chinese":"家庭問題"},{"english":"mutter","chinese":"低聲咕噥"},{"english":"No sooner had… than…","chinese":"一……就……"},{"english":"turn past the harbour","chinese":"駛過海旁"},{"english":"my mind began to betray","chinese":"我的思緒開始背叛"},{"english":"rich stranger","chinese":"有錢陌生人"},{"english":"borrow money","chinese":"借錢"},{"english":"worse still","chinese":"更糟的是"},{"english":"become involved in","chinese":"捲入"},{"english":"something illegal","chinese":"非法事情"},{"english":"hate myself for thinking it","chinese":"恨自己竟然這樣想"},{"english":"worry has a cruel imagination","chinese":"擔憂會令人想像殘酷的可能"},{"english":"finally stopped outside","chinese":"最後停在……外面"},{"english":"hospital in Kowloon","chinese":"九龍一間醫院"},{"english":"hurry to","chinese":"匆忙走向"},{"english":"passenger side","chinese":"乘客座一邊"},{"english":"step from the taxi","chinese":"從的士下車"},{"english":"ready to demand an explanation","chinese":"準備要求解釋"},{"english":"demand an explanation","chinese":"要求解釋"},{"english":"only to find myself frozen","chinese":"結果卻發現自己僵住"},{"english":"frozen by what I saw","chinese":"被眼前所見嚇得僵住"},{"english":"little girl in a wheelchair","chinese":"坐輪椅的小女孩"},{"english":"under the shelter","chinese":"在上蓋下"},{"english":"woollen hat","chinese":"羊毛帽"},{"english":"decorated with","chinese":"以……裝飾"},{"english":"yellow stars","chinese":"黃色星星"},{"english":"so pale that","chinese":"蒼白得……"},{"english":"brighter than the rest of her","chinese":"比她整個人更鮮亮"},{"english":"stand behind","chinese":"站在……後面"},{"english":"clutch the folder","chinese":"緊握文件夾"},{"english":"kneel beside","chinese":"跪在……旁邊"},{"english":"your carriage awaits","chinese":"你的馬車已經準備好了"},{"english":"laugh brightly enough to","chinese":"笑得明亮得足以……"},{"english":"cut through","chinese":"穿透"},{"english":"grey afternoon","chinese":"灰沉沉的下午"},{"english":"only then did I notice","chinese":"直到那時我才留意到"},{"english":"small sticker","chinese":"小貼紙"},{"english":"car door","chinese":"車門"},{"english":"Dream Ride Foundation","chinese":"夢想乘車基金會"},{"english":"a second later","chinese":"一秒後"},{"english":"his smile faded","chinese":"他的笑容消失"},{"english":"I could ask you the same thing","chinese":"我也可以問你同一個問題"},{"english":"my anger was already weakening","chinese":"我的怒氣已經開始減弱"},{"english":"give me twenty minutes","chinese":"給我二十分鐘"},{"english":"wait by the entrance","chinese":"在入口旁等候"},{"english":"help someone into the car","chinese":"扶某人上車"},{"english":"with a care I had never seen in him before","chinese":"以一種我從未見過的細心"},{"english":"race away","chinese":"飛快駛走"},{"english":"almost ceremonially","chinese":"近乎莊重地"},{"english":"around the block","chinese":"繞着街區"},{"english":"wave at","chinese":"向……揮手"},{"english":"as if she were","chinese":"彷彿她是"},{"english":"princess in a parade","chinese":"巡遊中的公主"},{"english":"loosen his tie","chinese":"鬆開領呔"},{"english":"come over","chinese":"走過來"},{"english":"before I could speak","chinese":"還未等我開口"},{"english":"belong to","chinese":"屬於"},{"english":"businessman","chinese":"商人"},{"english":"lend something to","chinese":"把某物借給"},{"english":"foundation","chinese":"基金會"},{"english":"twice a month","chinese":"每月兩次"},{"english":"medical consent forms","chinese":"醫療同意書"},{"english":"old Hong Kong movies","chinese":"香港舊電影"},{"english":"arrive there like a film star","chinese":"像電影明星般到達那裏"},{"english":"film star","chinese":"電影明星"},{"english":"before her treatment","chinese":"在她接受治療之前"},{"english":"give a tired smile","chinese":"露出疲倦的笑容"},{"english":"programme assistant","chinese":"活動助理"},{"english":"temporary","chinese":"臨時的"},{"english":"poorly paid","chinese":"薪酬低的"},{"english":"definitely not glamorous","chinese":"絕不光鮮"},{"english":"make sure","chinese":"確定"},{"english":"keep the job","chinese":"保住工作"},{"english":"after being rejected","chinese":"在被拒絕之後"},{"english":"so many times","chinese":"很多次"},{"english":"couldn't bear","chinese":"無法忍受"},{"english":"disappointed look","chinese":"失望的眼神"},{"english":"give someone a chance","chinese":"給某人機會"},{"english":"care about","chinese":"在意"},{"english":"exam results","chinese":"考試成績"},{"english":"show up","chinese":"出現；守約到場"},{"english":"it dawned on me","chinese":"我突然明白"},{"english":"mistake appearance for truth","chinese":"將表象誤當真相"},{"english":"all that glittered was not gold","chinese":"閃閃發光的不一定是金子"},{"english":"borrowed metal","chinese":"借來的金屬"},{"english":"polished for","chinese":"為……擦亮"},{"english":"one beautiful afternoon","chinese":"一個美好的下午"},{"english":"whisper","chinese":"低聲說"},{"english":"shrug","chinese":"聳肩"},{"english":"his eyes softened","chinese":"他的眼神變柔和"},{"english":"count for something","chinese":"仍然有點意義"},{"english":"go home together","chinese":"一起回家"},{"english":"by minibus","chinese":"乘小巴"},{"english":"secret fortune","chinese":"秘密財富"},{"english":"no miracle","chinese":"沒有奇蹟"},{"english":"job badge","chinese":"工作證"},{"english":"tired smile","chinese":"疲倦的笑容"},{"english":"in his pocket","chinese":"在他的口袋裏"},{"english":"never his","chinese":"從來不屬於他"},{"english":"in my eyes","chinese":"在我眼中"},{"english":"had never looked richer","chinese":"從未顯得如此富有"}]},"dse-writing-2012-part-b-q8":{"exerciseId":"dse-writing-2012-part-b-q8","essayKey":"","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=dse-writing-2012-part-b-q8","flashDeckId":"dse/writing/part-b/2012/Q8","paragraphs":[{"label":"Paragraph 1","english":"Second Chance, Stronger Business","chinese":"第二次機會，更強企業"},{"label":"Paragraph 2","english":"Dear Hong Kong Business Leaders,","chinese":"各位香港商界領袖："},{"label":"Paragraph 3","english":"Hong Kong has long been admired for turning pressure into progress. Yet one group is still too often left outside the workplace: reformed offenders and rehabilitated former drug abusers who are ready to rebuild their lives. To support their reintegration, the Government has launched Second Chance, a campaign encouraging local businesses to offer suitable employment to rehabilitated persons. As an intern at Hong Kong Correctional Services, I am writing to invite your company to join this scheme so as to strengthen your workforce, enhance your reputation and help create a safer community. Fair employment can turn past mistakes into future contributions.","chinese":"香港一直因能夠把壓力轉化為進步而備受讚賞。 然而，有一群人仍然太常被排除在職場之外：他們是已經改過自新的犯事者，以及已經康復、並準備重建人生的前吸毒者。 為了支持他們重新融入社會，政府推出了 Second Chance 這項運動，鼓勵本地企業為更生人士提供合適的就業機會。 作為香港懲教署的一名實習生，我寫這封信，是為了邀請貴公司加入這計劃，以加強貴公司的工作團隊、提升企業聲譽，並協助建立一個更安全的社區 公平的就業機會，能夠把過去的錯誤轉化為未來的貢獻。 實習生 香港懲教署"},{"label":"Paragraph 4","english":"Under Second Chance, participating businesses may register vacancies, attend briefing sessions, interview recommended candidates and receive follow-up support from rehabilitation officers. Applicants will be matched according to their skills, work attitude and readiness for employment, so employers are not left to make decisions without guidance. From hiring to workplace adjustment, the project aims to make recruitment clear, safe and practical. There is no need to lower your standards; rather, the scheme asks companies to judge candidates by their present capability and future potential.","chinese":"在 Second Chance 計劃下，參與企業可以登記職位空缺、出席簡介會、面試獲推薦的求職者，並獲得更生事務人員的後續支援。 申請者會按照技能、工作態度以及就業準備程度進行配對，因此僱主不會在缺乏指引的情況下自行作出決定。 從招聘到工作場所適應，這項計劃旨在使聘用過程清晰、安全且實際可行。 貴公司無須降低標準；更準確地說，這項計劃是希望企業根據求職者目前的能力和未來潛力來作出判斷。"},{"label":"Paragraph 5","english":"First, joining Second Chance can bring genuine business value. In service and manual industries, employers often struggle to recruit reliable workers who are willing to start with modest duties and grow steadily. Many rehabilitated persons are eager to prove themselves because they know that good opportunities seldom arrive twice. Given proper training and patient supervision, such employees can become disciplined, loyal and deeply appreciative members of staff. A company which gives someone a lawful livelihood does not simply fill a vacancy; it builds commitment. Take a small restaurant, for example. A rehabilitated former drug addict may begin by washing dishes or preparing ingredients. With punctuality, coaching and trust, he may later become a kitchen assistant who encourages newcomers to stay away from drugs. The more room we give people to rebuild, the more likely they are to repay that trust with effort.","chinese":"首先，加入 Second Chance 可以帶來真正的商業價值。 在服務業和體力勞動行業中，僱主往往難以招聘可靠、願意從基本職責做起並穩步成長的員工。 許多更生人士都渴望證明自己，因為他們明白良好機會很少會再次出現。 只要獲得適當培訓和耐心督導，這些員工可以成為守紀律、忠誠，並深懂感恩的團隊成員。 一間公司為某人提供合法生計，不只是填補一個職位空缺；它同時是在建立員工的承擔感。 以一間小餐廳為例。 一位已康復的前吸毒者，可能會從洗碗或準備食材開始。 憑著準時、指導和信任，他日後可能成為一名廚房助理，並鼓勵新來的人遠離毒品。 我們越給予人們重建人生的空間，他們就越有可能以努力來回報這份信任。"},{"label":"Paragraph 6","english":"Second, the scheme strengthens corporate reputation in a meaningful way. Today’s customers, investors and employees increasingly notice whether a business acts with social responsibility. Sponsoring a slogan is one thing; creating a job for a person of determination is another. By joining Second Chance, your company can show that it believes in rehabilitation, inclusion and practical compassion. This is not charity dressed up as business, but social responsibility translated into daily operations. In the eyes of the public, a company that treats people fairly is more than a profit-making organisation; it is a responsible member of the community. Such goodwill cannot be bought through advertising alone.","chinese":"第二，這項計劃能以有意義的方式提升企業聲譽。 今日的顧客、投資者和員工，越來越重視一家企業是否具備社會責任感。 贊助一句口號是一回事；為一位有決心的人創造一份工作，則是另一種更實在的承擔。 透過加入 Second Chance，貴公司可以展示自己相信更生、共融和實際的關懷 這並非把慈善包裝成商業行為；更準確地說，這是把社會責任轉化為日常營運 在公眾眼中，一間公平待人的公司不只是一個牟利機構；它也是社區中負責任的一員。 這樣的善意與信任，單靠廣告是買不到的。"},{"label":"Paragraph 7","english":"Understandably, some employers may worry about safety, discipline or public perception. These concerns deserve honest answers. However, it would be wrong to assume that a past conviction or addiction automatically predicts future failure. The purpose of rehabilitation is to help people accept responsibility, develop routines and return to society. Under the scheme, employers can select suitable posts, conduct interviews, set probation periods and maintain normal workplace rules. If necessary, support officers can offer advice so that problems are handled early. Second Chance does not ask businesses to take blind risks; it helps them take informed, humane and manageable steps.","chinese":"可以理解的是，有些僱主可能會擔心安全、紀律或公眾觀感。 這些憂慮值得獲得坦誠的回應。 然而，若認為過去的定罪或毒癮會自動預示未來的失敗，這種想法並不正確 更生的目的，是幫助人們承擔責任、建立生活規律，並重新回到社會之中。 在這項計劃下，僱主可以選擇合適的職位、進行面試、設定試用期，並維持正常的工作場所規則。 如有需要，支援人員可以提供建議，使問題能夠及早處理。 Second Chance 並沒有要求企業承擔盲目的風險；它協助企業採取有資訊基礎、人道，而且可管理的步驟。"},{"label":"Paragraph 8","english":"Without employment, rehabilitation remains unfinished. A person may leave custody or treatment with determination, but without a job, dignity is hard to restore and temptation is harder to resist. By contrast, a stable workplace gives structure to the day, income to the family and hope to the individual. One person’s second chance can become a child’s calmer home, a team’s reliable pair of hands and a community’s safer future.","chinese":"沒有就業機會，更生便仍未完成。 一個人也許帶著決心離開羈押或治療環境，但如果沒有工作，尊嚴便難以恢復，誘惑也會更難抵抗。 相比之下，一個穩定的工作場所能為一天帶來規律、為家庭帶來收入，也為個人帶來希望。 一個人的第二次機會，可以成為一個孩子更安穩的家庭、一個團隊可靠的幫手，以及一個社區更安全的未來。"},{"label":"Paragraph 9","english":"I therefore sincerely urge your business to take part in Second Chance. Register your interest, identify suitable vacancies, and allow our team to discuss how the scheme can fit your company’s needs. Hong Kong cannot become a truly resilient city by leaving people permanently defined by yesterday’s mistakes. Only by opening doors can we make way for responsibility, recovery and renewal. Please join us in giving a second chance—and in building a stronger Hong Kong.","chinese":"因此，我誠懇呼籲貴公司參與 Second Chance。 請登記貴公司的參與意向、找出合適的職位空缺，並讓我們的團隊與貴公司討論這項計劃如何配合貴公司的需要。 如果讓人們永遠被昨日的錯誤所定義，香港便無法成為一座真正有韌性的城市 只有透過打開大門，我們才能為責任、復原與更新開路。 請與我們一起給予第二次機會，並共同建設一個更強大的香港。"},{"label":"Paragraph 10","english":"Yours faithfully, Chris Wong Intern Hong Kong Correctional Services","chinese":"此致 Chris Wong 實習生 香港懲教署"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"second chance","chinese":"第二次機會"},{"english":"stronger business","chinese":"更強大的企業"},{"english":"business leaders","chinese":"商界領袖"},{"english":"have long been admired for","chinese":"一直因……而備受讚賞"},{"english":"turn pressure into progress","chinese":"化壓力為進步"},{"english":"one group is still too often left outside","chinese":"有一群人仍經常被排拒於……之外"},{"english":"the workplace","chinese":"職場"},{"english":"reformed offenders","chinese":"改過自新的違法者"},{"english":"rehabilitated former drug abusers","chinese":"戒毒康復者"},{"english":"be ready to rebuild their lives","chinese":"準備好重建人生"},{"english":"support their reintegration","chinese":"支援他們重新融入社會"},{"english":"reintegration","chinese":"重新融入社會"},{"english":"launch a campaign","chinese":"推出一項運動"},{"english":"encourage local businesses to","chinese":"鼓勵本地企業去"},{"english":"suitable employment","chinese":"合適就業機會"},{"english":"rehabilitated persons","chinese":"更生人士"},{"english":"intern at","chinese":"在……實習"},{"english":"Hong Kong Correctional Services","chinese":"香港懲教署"},{"english":"invite your company to join","chinese":"邀請貴公司加入"},{"english":"join this scheme","chinese":"加入這項計劃"},{"english":"so as to","chinese":"以便；為了"},{"english":"strengthen your workforce","chinese":"加強貴公司的員工隊伍"},{"english":"enhance your reputation","chinese":"提升貴公司的聲譽"},{"english":"create a safer community","chinese":"建立更安全的社區"},{"english":"fair employment","chinese":"公平就業"},{"english":"turn past mistakes into future contributions","chinese":"把過去的錯誤轉化為未來的貢獻"},{"english":"under Second Chance","chinese":"在「第二次機會」計劃下"},{"english":"participating businesses","chinese":"參與企業"},{"english":"register vacancies","chinese":"登記職位空缺"},{"english":"attend briefing sessions","chinese":"出席簡介會"},{"english":"interview recommended candidates","chinese":"面見獲推薦的候選人"},{"english":"receive follow-up support","chinese":"獲得跟進支援"},{"english":"rehabilitation officers","chinese":"更生輔導人員"},{"english":"be matched according to","chinese":"根據……作配對"},{"english":"work attitude","chinese":"工作態度"},{"english":"readiness for employment","chinese":"就業準備程度"},{"english":"be left to make decisions without guidance","chinese":"被迫在沒有指引下作決定"},{"english":"from hiring to workplace adjustment","chinese":"從招聘到適應職場"},{"english":"workplace adjustment","chinese":"適應職場"},{"english":"make recruitment clear, safe and practical","chinese":"令招聘清晰、安全而實際可行"},{"english":"lower your standards","chinese":"降低標準"},{"english":"rather","chinese":"而是"},{"english":"judge candidates by","chinese":"根據……評估候選人"},{"english":"present capability","chinese":"現有能力"},{"english":"future potential","chinese":"未來潛力"},{"english":"bring genuine business value","chinese":"帶來真正的商業價值"},{"english":"service and manual industries","chinese":"服務業和體力勞動行業"},{"english":"struggle to recruit","chinese":"難以招聘"},{"english":"reliable workers","chinese":"可靠員工"},{"english":"be willing to start with","chinese":"願意從……開始"},{"english":"modest duties","chinese":"基本職責"},{"english":"grow steadily","chinese":"穩步成長"},{"english":"be eager to prove themselves","chinese":"渴望證明自己"},{"english":"opportunities seldom arrive twice","chinese":"好機會很少再次出現"},{"english":"given proper training","chinese":"在獲得適當訓練下"},{"english":"patient supervision","chinese":"耐心督導"},{"english":"disciplined and loyal","chinese":"有紀律而忠誠"},{"english":"deeply appreciative","chinese":"深深感激的"},{"english":"members of staff","chinese":"職員；員工"},{"english":"lawful livelihood","chinese":"合法生計"},{"english":"fill a vacancy","chinese":"填補職位空缺"},{"english":"build commitment","chinese":"建立投入感；建立忠誠"},{"english":"take a small restaurant, for example","chinese":"以一間小餐廳為例"},{"english":"former drug addict","chinese":"前吸毒者"},{"english":"wash dishes","chinese":"洗碗"},{"english":"prepare ingredients","chinese":"準備食材"},{"english":"with punctuality, coaching and trust","chinese":"憑着守時、指導和信任"},{"english":"kitchen assistant","chinese":"廚房助理"},{"english":"encourage newcomers to","chinese":"鼓勵新來者去"},{"english":"stay away from drugs","chinese":"遠離毒品"},{"english":"the more..., the more likely...","chinese":"越……就越可能……"},{"english":"give people room to rebuild","chinese":"給人重建人生的空間"},{"english":"repay that trust with effort","chinese":"以努力回報信任"},{"english":"strengthen corporate reputation","chinese":"加強企業聲譽"},{"english":"in a meaningful way","chinese":"以有意義的方式"},{"english":"customers, investors and employees","chinese":"顧客、投資者和員工"},{"english":"increasingly notice whether","chinese":"越來越留意是否"},{"english":"act with social responsibility","chinese":"以社會責任行事"},{"english":"sponsor a slogan","chinese":"贊助一句口號"},{"english":"a person of determination","chinese":"有決心的人"},{"english":"believe in rehabilitation","chinese":"相信更生"},{"english":"inclusion","chinese":"共融"},{"english":"practical compassion","chinese":"實際的關懷"},{"english":"charity dressed up as business","chinese":"披上商業外衣的慈善"},{"english":"social responsibility translated into daily operations","chinese":"把社會責任轉化為日常營運"},{"english":"in the eyes of the public","chinese":"在公眾眼中"},{"english":"profit-making organisation","chinese":"牟利機構"},{"english":"responsible member of the community","chinese":"負責任的社區一分子"},{"english":"such goodwill","chinese":"這種善意和好感"},{"english":"cannot be bought through advertising alone","chinese":"不能單靠廣告買到"},{"english":"understandably","chinese":"可以理解地"},{"english":"worry about safety","chinese":"擔心安全問題"},{"english":"public perception","chinese":"公眾觀感"},{"english":"deserve honest answers","chinese":"值得得到坦誠回應"},{"english":"assume that","chinese":"假設；認為"},{"english":"past conviction","chinese":"過往定罪紀錄"},{"english":"addiction","chinese":"毒癮"},{"english":"automatically predicts","chinese":"自動預示"},{"english":"future failure","chinese":"未來失敗"},{"english":"the purpose of rehabilitation","chinese":"更生的目的"},{"english":"accept responsibility","chinese":"承擔責任"},{"english":"develop routines","chinese":"建立生活規律"},{"english":"return to society","chinese":"重返社會"},{"english":"select suitable posts","chinese":"選擇合適職位"},{"english":"conduct interviews","chinese":"進行面試"},{"english":"set probation periods","chinese":"設定試用期"},{"english":"maintain normal workplace rules","chinese":"維持正常職場規則"},{"english":"if necessary","chinese":"如有需要"},{"english":"support officers","chinese":"支援人員"},{"english":"offer advice","chinese":"提供建議"},{"english":"problems are handled early","chinese":"問題及早處理"},{"english":"take blind risks","chinese":"盲目冒險"},{"english":"informed, humane and manageable steps","chinese":"有根據、人道而可管理的步驟"},{"english":"without employment","chinese":"沒有就業"},{"english":"remain unfinished","chinese":"仍未完成"},{"english":"leave custody","chinese":"離開羈押；獲釋"},{"english":"treatment","chinese":"治療；戒毒治療"},{"english":"with determination","chinese":"帶着決心"},{"english":"dignity is hard to restore","chinese":"尊嚴難以恢復"},{"english":"temptation is harder to resist","chinese":"更難抵抗誘惑"},{"english":"by contrast","chinese":"相比之下"},{"english":"stable workplace","chinese":"穩定工作場所"},{"english":"give structure to the day","chinese":"為一天帶來規律"},{"english":"income to the family","chinese":"為家庭帶來收入"},{"english":"hope to the individual","chinese":"為個人帶來希望"},{"english":"one person's second chance","chinese":"一個人的第二次機會"},{"english":"calmer home","chinese":"更安穩的家"},{"english":"reliable pair of hands","chinese":"可靠幫手"},{"english":"safer future","chinese":"更安全的未來"},{"english":"sincerely urge","chinese":"誠懇呼籲"},{"english":"take part in","chinese":"參與"},{"english":"register your interest","chinese":"登記參與意向"},{"english":"identify suitable vacancies","chinese":"找出合適職位空缺"},{"english":"fit your company's needs","chinese":"配合貴公司的需要"},{"english":"truly resilient city","chinese":"真正有韌性的城市"},{"english":"be permanently defined by","chinese":"被……永久定義"},{"english":"yesterday's mistakes","chinese":"昔日的錯誤"},{"english":"open doors","chinese":"打開大門；提供機會"},{"english":"make way for","chinese":"為……鋪路"},{"english":"responsibility, recovery and renewal","chinese":"責任、更生和更新"},{"english":"join us in giving","chinese":"加入我們一起給予"},{"english":"build a stronger Hong Kong","chinese":"建設更強大的香港"},{"english":"Yours faithfully","chinese":"謹啟"},{"english":"intern","chinese":"實習生"}]},"dse-writing-2012-part-b-q9":{"exerciseId":"dse-writing-2012-part-b-q9","essayKey":"","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=dse-writing-2012-part-b-q9","flashDeckId":"dse/writing/part-b/2012/Q9","paragraphs":[{"label":"Paragraph 1","english":"When the Smile Disappears","chinese":"當笑容消失時"},{"label":"Paragraph 2","english":"By Chris Wong, 6A","chinese":"6A Chris Wong 撰"},{"label":"Paragraph 3","english":"When our school magazine decided to run a special feature on mental health, I immediately thought of a friend I shall call Ethan. As students, we are trained to chase marks, meet deadlines and look “fine” even when we are anything but fine. Ethan’s depression made our school community consider speaking more honestly about pain, so that no student has to suffer quietly behind a polite smile. Depression, in my view, is anything but weakness; silence is the real danger. Through Ethan’s story, this article hopes to show that recovery begins with noticing, listening and seeking help early.","chinese":"當我們的校刊決定刊登一個關於精神健康的專題特輯時，我立刻想起了一位朋友；在這篇文章中，我會稱他為 Ethan。 作為學生，我們被訓練去追逐分數、趕上期限，並在自己根本談不上安好時仍然看起來「沒事」。 Ethan 的抑鬱症讓我們的校園群體開始思考，是否應該更坦誠地談論痛苦，好讓沒有任何學生需要躲在禮貌的微笑背後默默受苦。 在我看來，抑鬱絕非軟弱；沉默才是真正的危險。 透過 Ethan 的故事，本文希望說明，康復始於留意、聆聽，以及及早尋求幫助"},{"label":"Paragraph 4","english":"Up until Secondary Five, Ethan was the kind of boy who could make the whole row laugh before assembly. He played basketball, chaired our English Society meetings and remembered everyone’s birthday. Then, almost without warning, the lights seemed to go out. He stopped eating with us. His homework, once neat enough to be used as a model answer, became late or missing. When teachers asked whether anything was wrong, he answered, “I’m just tired.” At first glance, it looked like laziness; on closer inspection, it was exhaustion. Depression did not arrive with thunder. Quite the contrary - it arrived quietly, turning ordinary things — getting out of bed, replying to messages, opening a textbook — into tasks that felt too heavy to lift. Not until I saw him sitting alone after school, staring at a blank test paper, did it dawn on me that he was not trying to avoid life; he was trying to survive it.","chinese":"直到中五，Ethan 仍是那種能在早會前把整排同學逗笑的男孩。 他打籃球、主持英文學會會議，還記得每個人的生日。 接着，幾乎毫無預兆地，他身上的光好像熄滅了。 他不再和我們一起吃飯。 他的功課曾經整潔得足以用作範文答案，後來卻變得遲交，甚至缺交。 當老師問他是否有甚麼不妥時，他回答：「我只是累了。」 乍看之下，那像是懶惰；仔細看清楚後，那其實更接近身心俱疲。 抑鬱來臨時沒有雷聲大作。 恰恰相反，它是悄悄到來的，把平常不過的事情——起床、回覆訊息、翻開課本——都變成沉重得彷彿無法抬起的任務。 直到我看見他放學後獨自坐着，盯着一張空白的測驗卷，我才突然明白：他並非試圖逃避生活；他只是努力在生活中撐下去。"},{"label":"Paragraph 5","english":"What helped him was not one dramatic rescue, but many small acts of courage. One afternoon, instead of saying, “Cheer up,” I asked, “Would it help if I just sat here with you?” For what felt like forever, he said nothing. Eventually, he admitted that he had not slept properly for weeks and had begun to believe that everyone would be better off without him. That frightened me, but I knew better than to leave him hanging. With his knowledge, and because safety mattered more than embarrassment, I spoke to our class teacher, who brought in the school social worker and later helped Ethan talk to his parents. Thereafter, recovery began to take shape. He met the counsellor regularly, saw a doctor, reduced his workload for a while and rebuilt a routine around sleep, meals, exercise and manageable revision. Progress came in fits and starts: two steps forward, one step back. Yet little by little, Ethan came a long way. For the first time in forever, he laughed at a joke during lunch. By the time Speech Day arrived, he was still quiet, but he was also still standing.","chinese":"真正幫助他的，並非一場戲劇性的拯救；發揮作用的，是許多微小而勇敢的行動。 一個下午，我沒有對他說「振作一點」，只問他：「如果我只是坐在你旁邊，會不會有幫助？」 在一段感覺漫長得像永遠的時間裡，他一句話也沒有說。 最後，他承認自己已經連續幾個星期沒有好好睡覺，也開始相信，如果沒有他，所有人都會過得更好。 這令我感到害怕，但我清楚知道，不能讓他懸在那裡、孤立無援。 在他知情的情況下，也因為安全比尷尬更重要，我告訴了班主任；班主任請來學校社工，後來也協助 Ethan 與父母交談。 之後，康復的輪廓開始逐漸成形。 他定期見輔導員、看醫生、暫時減輕學業負擔，並重新建立一套圍繞睡眠、飲食、運動和可處理溫習量的日常規律。 進展並不穩定：走前兩步，又退後一步。 然而，一點一點地，Ethan 已經走了很遠。 很久以來第一次，他在午膳時因一句笑話笑了出來。 到學校頒獎典禮那天，他仍然安靜，但他也依然站着，沒有被打倒。"},{"label":"Paragraph 6","english":"There are a few things every student should know about fighting depression. First, notice changes. Few, if any, depressed students will announce their suffering in perfect sentences. Look out for sudden isolation, constant tiredness, unusual anger, declining marks or comments such as “Nothing matters.” Second, speak gently and specifically. Instead of saying, “What’s wrong with you?”, try, “I’ve noticed you haven’t been yourself lately. I’m here if you want to talk.” That way, you open a door without forcing them through it. Third, listen without rushing to fix everything. Advice has its place, but a soft answer often helps more than a clever lecture. Fourth, never turn depression into gossip. Trust is hard to build and painfully easy to break. That said, if someone may hurt himself or herself, do not promise secrecy. Tell a teacher, counsellor, parent or social worker as soon as possible. The sooner help arrives, the better. Finally, keep inviting the person back into ordinary life - a short walk, a library seat, a simple lunch. These small invitations remind them that they still belong.","chinese":"關於對抗抑鬱，每位學生都應該知道幾件事。 第一，留意變化。 患上抑鬱的學生很少會把自己的痛苦整理成完美句子再說出來，甚至可能完全不會。 要留意突然孤立自己、持續疲倦、異常憤怒、成績下滑，或像「甚麼都不重要」 這類說話。 第二，說話要溫和，也要具體。 與其說「你到底有甚麼問題？」，不如嘗試說：「我留意到你最近好像不太像平時的自己。如果你想談，我在這裡。」 這樣一來，你是在替對方打開一扇門，卻沒有強迫他們走進去。 第三，聆聽時不要急着把一切都修好。 建議自有其價值，但一句溫柔的回應，往往比一場聰明的說教更有幫助。 第四，絕不要把抑鬱變成八卦。 信任很難建立，卻痛苦地容易被破壞。 話雖如此，如果某人可能傷害自己，便不要承諾保密。 請盡快告訴老師、輔導員、家長或社工。 幫助越早到來越好。 最後，繼續邀請那個人回到日常生活之中——一次短短的散步、圖書館的一個座位、一頓簡單的午餐。 這些小小的邀請會提醒他們，他們依然屬於這裡。"},{"label":"Paragraph 7","english":"Ethan once told me that depression made him feel as if he had nowhere to go. Our job, as classmates, is to make sure that no one in our school is left with nowhere to turn. We cannot replace doctors or counsellors, but we can notice, listen, include and speak up. If we do that, our mental health feature will be more than an article. It will be a promise - in this school, pain will not be mocked, hidden or ignored — not on our watch.","chinese":"Ethan 曾經告訴我，抑鬱令他覺得自己好像無處可去。 作為同學，我們的責任是確保學校裡沒有任何人會落得求助無門。 我們無法取代醫生或輔導員，但我們可以留意、聆聽、接納，並在需要時站出來說話。 如果我們做到這一點，我們的精神健康專題就會超越一篇文章本身。 它會成為一個承諾——在這所學校裡，痛苦不會被嘲笑、不會被掩藏，也不會被忽視——只要我們仍在，就絕不容許這種事發生。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"when the smile disappears","chinese":"當笑容消失時"},{"english":"school magazine","chinese":"學校雜誌"},{"english":"run a special feature on","chinese":"刊登關於……的專題"},{"english":"mental health","chinese":"精神健康"},{"english":"immediately thought of","chinese":"立即想起"},{"english":"a friend I shall call","chinese":"一位我姑且稱為……的朋友"},{"english":"be trained to","chinese":"被訓練去"},{"english":"chase marks","chinese":"追逐分數"},{"english":"meet deadlines","chinese":"趕上截止日期"},{"english":"look fine","chinese":"看起來沒事"},{"english":"anything but fine","chinese":"絕不是沒事"},{"english":"school community","chinese":"學校社群"},{"english":"speak more honestly about","chinese":"更坦誠地談論"},{"english":"suffer quietly","chinese":"默默承受痛苦"},{"english":"behind a polite smile","chinese":"在禮貌微笑背後"},{"english":"in my view","chinese":"在我看來"},{"english":"anything but weakness","chinese":"絕不是軟弱"},{"english":"the real danger","chinese":"真正的危險"},{"english":"recovery begins with","chinese":"康復始於"},{"english":"seeking help early","chinese":"及早求助"},{"english":"up until","chinese":"直到……為止"},{"english":"Secondary Five","chinese":"中五"},{"english":"the kind of boy who","chinese":"那種會……的男生"},{"english":"make the whole row laugh","chinese":"令整排人發笑"},{"english":"before assembly","chinese":"早會前"},{"english":"chaired meetings","chinese":"主持會議"},{"english":"English Society","chinese":"英文學會"},{"english":"almost without warning","chinese":"幾乎毫無預兆地"},{"english":"the lights seemed to go out","chinese":"光像是突然熄滅了"},{"english":"stopped eating with us","chinese":"不再和我們一起吃飯"},{"english":"neat enough to be used as","chinese":"整齊得足以被用作"},{"english":"model answer","chinese":"範文；標準答案"},{"english":"became late or missing","chinese":"變成遲交或欠交"},{"english":"anything was wrong","chinese":"是否有甚麼不妥"},{"english":"just tired","chinese":"只是累了"},{"english":"at first glance","chinese":"乍看之下"},{"english":"looked like laziness","chinese":"看起來像懶惰"},{"english":"on closer inspection","chinese":"仔細看時"},{"english":"exhaustion","chinese":"身心俱疲"},{"english":"did not arrive with thunder","chinese":"並不是轟然降臨"},{"english":"quite the contrary","chinese":"恰恰相反"},{"english":"arrived quietly","chinese":"靜悄悄地到來"},{"english":"turning ordinary things into","chinese":"把平常事變成"},{"english":"ordinary things","chinese":"平常事"},{"english":"getting out of bed","chinese":"起床"},{"english":"replying to messages","chinese":"回覆訊息"},{"english":"opening a textbook","chinese":"打開教科書"},{"english":"too heavy to lift","chinese":"沉重得難以承受"},{"english":"not until… did…","chinese":"直到……才……"},{"english":"sitting alone","chinese":"獨自坐着"},{"english":"staring at","chinese":"凝望着"},{"english":"blank test paper","chinese":"空白測驗卷"},{"english":"it dawned on me that","chinese":"我才明白"},{"english":"avoid life","chinese":"逃避生活"},{"english":"survive it","chinese":"撐過去"},{"english":"what helped him","chinese":"幫助他的事"},{"english":"not one dramatic rescue, but…","chinese":"不是一次戲劇性的拯救，而是……"},{"english":"dramatic rescue","chinese":"戲劇性的拯救"},{"english":"small acts of courage","chinese":"細小而勇敢的行動"},{"english":"instead of saying","chinese":"而不是說"},{"english":"cheer up","chinese":"振作起來"},{"english":"would it help if","chinese":"如果……會有幫助嗎"},{"english":"sit here with you","chinese":"坐在這裏陪你"},{"english":"for what felt like forever","chinese":"彷彿過了很久"},{"english":"eventually","chinese":"最後；終於"},{"english":"admitted that","chinese":"承認"},{"english":"slept properly","chinese":"睡得好"},{"english":"for weeks","chinese":"好幾星期"},{"english":"begun to believe","chinese":"開始相信"},{"english":"be better off without","chinese":"沒有……會過得更好"},{"english":"frightened me","chinese":"令我害怕"},{"english":"knew better than to","chinese":"明知不應該"},{"english":"leave him hanging","chinese":"讓他孤立無援；不理會他"},{"english":"with his knowledge","chinese":"在他知情下"},{"english":"safety mattered more than embarrassment","chinese":"安全比尷尬更重要"},{"english":"class teacher","chinese":"班主任"},{"english":"brought in","chinese":"請來；引入"},{"english":"school social worker","chinese":"學校社工"},{"english":"helped someone talk to","chinese":"幫助某人與……交談"},{"english":"thereafter","chinese":"其後"},{"english":"began to take shape","chinese":"開始成形"},{"english":"counsellor","chinese":"輔導員"},{"english":"regularly","chinese":"定期地"},{"english":"reduced his workload","chinese":"減輕工作量"},{"english":"for a while","chinese":"一段時間"},{"english":"rebuilt a routine around","chinese":"圍繞……重建日常規律"},{"english":"manageable revision","chinese":"可應付的溫習"},{"english":"progress came in fits and starts","chinese":"進展斷斷續續"},{"english":"two steps forward, one step back","chinese":"進兩步退一步"},{"english":"little by little","chinese":"一點一點地"},{"english":"came a long way","chinese":"取得很大進展"},{"english":"for the first time in forever","chinese":"久違地"},{"english":"by the time","chinese":"到……的時候"},{"english":"Speech Day","chinese":"畢業頒獎禮；學校頒獎日"},{"english":"still standing","chinese":"仍然撐着；仍然站着"},{"english":"fighting depression","chinese":"對抗抑鬱症"},{"english":"notice changes","chinese":"留意變化"},{"english":"few, if any","chinese":"即使有也很少"},{"english":"depressed students","chinese":"患抑鬱症的學生"},{"english":"announce their suffering","chinese":"說出自己的痛苦"},{"english":"in perfect sentences","chinese":"用完整清楚的句子"},{"english":"look out for","chinese":"留意"},{"english":"sudden isolation","chinese":"突然孤立自己"},{"english":"constant tiredness","chinese":"長期疲倦"},{"english":"unusual anger","chinese":"異常憤怒"},{"english":"declining marks","chinese":"成績下滑"},{"english":"comments such as","chinese":"例如……的說話"},{"english":"nothing matters","chinese":"一切都不重要"},{"english":"speak gently and specifically","chinese":"溫和而具體地說"},{"english":"haven't been yourself lately","chinese":"你最近不像平時的自己"},{"english":"I'm here if you want to talk","chinese":"如果你想傾，我在這裏"},{"english":"that way","chinese":"這樣"},{"english":"open a door","chinese":"打開一扇門；提供機會"},{"english":"without forcing them through it","chinese":"不強迫他們走進去"},{"english":"rushing to fix everything","chinese":"急着解決所有問題"},{"english":"advice has its place","chinese":"建議有其作用"},{"english":"a soft answer","chinese":"溫和的回應"},{"english":"clever lecture","chinese":"聰明但說教式的訓話"},{"english":"turn depression into gossip","chinese":"把抑鬱症變成八卦"},{"english":"trust is hard to build","chinese":"信任很難建立"},{"english":"painfully easy to break","chinese":"非常容易被破壞"},{"english":"that said","chinese":"話雖如此"},{"english":"hurt himself or herself","chinese":"傷害自己"},{"english":"promise secrecy","chinese":"承諾保密"},{"english":"as soon as possible","chinese":"盡快"},{"english":"the sooner…, the better","chinese":"越早……越好"},{"english":"keep inviting someone back into","chinese":"繼續邀請某人回到……"},{"english":"ordinary life","chinese":"日常生活"},{"english":"a short walk","chinese":"一段短短的散步"},{"english":"library seat","chinese":"圖書館座位"},{"english":"simple lunch","chinese":"簡單午餐"},{"english":"small invitations","chinese":"細小的邀請"},{"english":"still belong","chinese":"仍然屬於這裏"},{"english":"made him feel as if","chinese":"令他感覺好像"},{"english":"nowhere to go","chinese":"無處可去"},{"english":"our job, as classmates","chinese":"作為同學，我們的責任"},{"english":"make sure that","chinese":"確保"},{"english":"be left with nowhere to turn","chinese":"求助無門"},{"english":"replace doctors or counsellors","chinese":"取代醫生或輔導員"},{"english":"notice, listen, include and speak up","chinese":"留意、聆聽、接納並發聲"},{"english":"speak up","chinese":"發聲；出聲求助"},{"english":"more than an article","chinese":"不只是一篇文章"},{"english":"a promise","chinese":"一個承諾"},{"english":"will not be mocked, hidden or ignored","chinese":"不會被嘲笑、隱藏或忽視"},{"english":"not on our watch","chinese":"在我們看顧下絕不會發生"}]},"dse-writing-2013-part-a":{"exerciseId":"dse-writing-2013-part-a","essayKey":"","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=dse-writing-2013-part-a","flashDeckId":"dse/writing/part-a/2013","paragraphs":[{"label":"Photo 1: “Chalkboard Dreams”","english":"Photo 1: “Chalkboard Dreams”","chinese":"照片一：「黑板上的夢想」"},{"label":"Photo 1: “Chalkboard Dreams”","english":"This photo features a concentrated young schoolgirl standing at a large blackboard, intently writing with a piece of chalk. It immediately transports me back to my primary school days, where every blank space on the board felt like an invitation to explore new ideas. The girl’s focused posture reminds me of the pure excitement I once felt whenever I was given the precious opportunity to stand in front of the class, sharing my original thoughts and practicing my handwriting. For me, this image symbolizes not only the innocence of childhood but also the boundless potential we as teenagers possess at a young age. It serves as a vivid reminder that every journey of learning, in fact, begins with a simple spark of curiosity, with an incentive as simple as a little chalk. Even now, I look at this photo to rekindle that sense of wonder and remind myself never to lose my love for discovering something new, and never cease thinking.","chinese":"這張照片呈現了一名專心致志的年輕女學生站在一塊大黑板前，正專注地用粉筆書寫。 它立刻把我帶回小學時光，那時黑板上的每一處空白位置，都像是在邀請我探索新的想法。 那女孩專注的姿態，令我想起昔日每當我獲得寶貴機會站在全班面前，分享自己的原創想法並練習書寫時，心中那份純粹的興奮。 對我而言，這張照片不但象徵童年的純真，也象徵我們作為青少年在年輕時所擁有的無限潛能。 它生動地提醒我，每一段學習旅程，其實都始於一點簡單的好奇心，也可以由一支小小的粉筆這樣簡單的推動力開始。 即使到了現在，我仍會看着這張照片，重新燃起那份驚奇感，並提醒自己永遠不要失去探索新事物的熱愛，也不要停止思考。"},{"label":"Photo 2: “Circle of Friendship”","english":"Photo 2: “Circle of Friendship”","chinese":"照片二：「友誼之圈」"},{"label":"Photo 2: “Circle of Friendship”","english":"In contrast, my second photo shows a tight circle of friends standing in a huddle with their hands joined at the focal point. It captures a heartwarming sense of unity and mutual support between the companions. Whenever I gaze at this snapshot, I recall how friendship empowers us to overcome obstacles we cannot tackle alone. These interlocked arms remind me of a project we once completed as a close-knit team, celebrating every small but significant victory, and encouraging one another through setbacks from life. That experience taught me the true value of trust, empathy, and collaboration. Today, this photo continues to inspire me to appreciate the people in my life, and to remain grateful for the unwavering support that friendship offers.","chinese":"相比之下，我的第二張照片展示了一群朋友緊密地圍成一圈站在一起，他們的手在畫面焦點處交疊。 它捕捉了朋友之間令人感到溫暖的團結感和互相支持。 每當我凝望這張照片時，我都會想起友誼如何賦予我們力量，去克服那些我們無法獨自應付的障礙。 這些交纏在一起的手臂，令我想起我們曾經作為一個緊密團隊完成的一項計劃；我們慶祝每一個細小卻重要的勝利，也在人生的挫折中互相鼓勵。 那次經歷教會了我信任、同理心和合作的真正價值。 直到今天，這張照片仍然激勵我珍惜生命中的人，並繼續感激友誼所帶來的堅定支持。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"Chalkboard Dreams","chinese":"黑板上的夢想"},{"english":"feature","chinese":"以……為主要內容；呈現"},{"english":"a concentrated young schoolgirl","chinese":"一名專心致志的年輕女學生"},{"english":"stand at a large blackboard","chinese":"站在一塊大黑板前"},{"english":"intently","chinese":"專注地"},{"english":"write with a piece of chalk","chinese":"用粉筆書寫"},{"english":"immediately transport someone back to","chinese":"立即把某人帶回……"},{"english":"primary school days","chinese":"小學時光"},{"english":"blank space","chinese":"空白位置"},{"english":"an invitation to","chinese":"一種……的邀請"},{"english":"explore new ideas","chinese":"探索新想法"},{"english":"focused posture","chinese":"專注的姿勢"},{"english":"remind someone of","chinese":"令某人想起……"},{"english":"pure excitement","chinese":"純粹的興奮"},{"english":"be given the precious opportunity to","chinese":"獲得寶貴機會去……"},{"english":"stand in front of the class","chinese":"站在全班面前"},{"english":"share my original thoughts","chinese":"分享自己的原創想法"},{"english":"practise my handwriting","chinese":"練習書法；練習書寫"},{"english":"symbolise not only…but also…","chinese":"不但象徵……亦象徵……"},{"english":"the innocence of childhood","chinese":"童年的純真"},{"english":"boundless potential","chinese":"無限潛能"},{"english":"possess at a young age","chinese":"年紀輕輕便擁有"},{"english":"serve as a vivid reminder that","chinese":"生動地提醒我們……"},{"english":"a journey of learning","chinese":"學習旅程"},{"english":"begin with","chinese":"由……開始"},{"english":"a simple spark of curiosity","chinese":"一點簡單的好奇心"},{"english":"something as simple as","chinese":"像……般簡單的東西"},{"english":"rekindle that sense of wonder","chinese":"重新燃起那份驚奇感"},{"english":"a sense of wonder","chinese":"驚奇感；對世界的好奇"},{"english":"never lose my love for","chinese":"永遠不要失去對……的熱愛"},{"english":"discover something new","chinese":"發現新事物"},{"english":"never stop thinking","chinese":"永遠不要停止思考"},{"english":"Circle of Friendship","chinese":"友誼之圈"},{"english":"in contrast","chinese":"相比之下"},{"english":"a tight circle of friends","chinese":"一群緊密圍成一圈的朋友"},{"english":"stand in a huddle","chinese":"圍在一起站立"},{"english":"with their hands joined","chinese":"雙手合在一起"},{"english":"at the focal point","chinese":"在焦點位置"},{"english":"capture a heartwarming sense of","chinese":"捕捉到一種溫暖的……感覺"},{"english":"unity and mutual support","chinese":"團結與互相支持"},{"english":"between the companions","chinese":"同伴之間"},{"english":"gaze at this snapshot","chinese":"凝望這張照片"},{"english":"recall how","chinese":"想起……如何"},{"english":"empower someone to","chinese":"使某人有力量去……"},{"english":"overcome obstacles","chinese":"克服困難"},{"english":"tackle something alone","chinese":"獨自處理……"},{"english":"interlocked arms","chinese":"交疊相扣的手臂"},{"english":"close-knit team","chinese":"緊密合作的團隊"},{"english":"celebrate every small but significant victory","chinese":"慶祝每一個細小但重要的勝利"},{"english":"small but significant","chinese":"細小但重要的"},{"english":"encourage one another through","chinese":"在……中互相鼓勵"},{"english":"setbacks in life","chinese":"人生中的挫折"},{"english":"teach someone the true value of","chinese":"使某人明白……的真正價值"},{"english":"trust, empathy, and collaboration","chinese":"信任、同理心與合作"},{"english":"continue to inspire someone to","chinese":"繼續啟發某人去……"},{"english":"appreciate the people in my life","chinese":"珍惜生命中的人"},{"english":"remain grateful for","chinese":"對……一直心存感激"},{"english":"unwavering support","chinese":"堅定不移的支持"},{"english":"friendship offers","chinese":"友誼所帶來的……"}]},"dse-writing-2013-part-b-q2":{"exerciseId":"dse-writing-2013-part-b-q2","essayKey":"","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=dse-writing-2013-part-b-q2","flashDeckId":"dse/writing/part-b/2013/Q2","paragraphs":[{"label":"Paragraph 1","english":"Subject: Proposal for a Campus TV Programme — Running Hong Kong Together","chinese":"主旨：校園電視節目建議——《一起奔跑香港》"},{"label":"Paragraph 2","english":"Dear Ms Chan,","chinese":"陳老師："},{"label":"Paragraph 3","english":"Thank you for inviting me to produce a 30-minute Campus TV programme about a local sporting event. Given that many students now see sport mainly as PE lessons, fitness tests or competitions between elite athletes, I would like to propose covering the Hong Kong Marathon. It is not just a race; rather, it is a city-wide story about discipline, courage and community. My aim is to show how an ordinary Hong Kong street can, for one morning, become a stage where professional runners, office workers, parents, students, volunteers and supporters all move towards the same finishing line. In short, I hope the programme will encourage schoolmates to see sport as something close to their own lives, rather than something distant on television.","chinese":"感謝您邀請我製作一個關於本地體育盛事的三十分鐘校園電視節目。 考慮到現今許多學生主要把運動理解為體育課、體能測驗，或精英運動員之間的競賽，我想建議以香港馬拉松作為節目主題。 它不只是一場賽跑；更準確地說，它是一個關於紀律、勇氣與社群精神的全城故事。 我的目標是呈現一條普通的香港街道，如何能在一個早上化成一個舞台，讓專業跑手、上班族、家長、學生、義工和支持者一起朝同一條終點線前進。 簡而言之，我希望這個節目能鼓勵同學把運動看成貼近自己生活的事物，而非電視上遙不可及的東西。"},{"label":"Paragraph 4","english":"The programme would open with a two-minute montage called “Before the Starting Gun”. We would show runners stretching under the city lights, volunteers handing out water, police officers preparing road arrangements, and spectators finding the best places to cheer. Instead of giving a dry introduction, the host would ask, “What makes thousands of people wake up early to run across Hong Kong?” That question would lead naturally into the first main section, “The Event and the City”. In this part, we would briefly introduce the marathon, the different kinds of runners who join it, and the way the event turns familiar roads into a shared sporting arena. Take Causeway Bay, Tsim Sha Tsui or the harbourfront, for example - students usually pass these places for shopping or transport, but during the event, they become symbols of endurance and public spirit.","chinese":"節目會以一段名為「起跑槍響之前」的兩分鐘蒙太奇作開場。 我們會展示跑手在城市燈光下伸展、義工派發食水、警務人員準備道路安排，以及觀眾尋找最佳打氣位置的畫面。 節目一開始會避免沉悶介紹，由主持人提出這個問題：「是甚麼令成千上萬的人一大清早醒來，跑遍香港？」 這個問題會自然引入第一個主要環節「賽事與城市」。 在這部分，我們會簡要介紹馬拉松、參與其中的不同類型跑手，以及這項活動如何把熟悉的道路轉化為一個共享的運動場域。 以銅鑼灣、尖沙咀或海濱為例——學生平日通常因購物或交通需要經過這些地方，但在賽事期間，它們會成為耐力與公共精神的象徵。 2nd Topic Sentence（主題句） The second section, lasting around ten minutes, would focus on the people. 第二個環節約長十分鐘，會聚焦於人物。"},{"label":"Paragraph 5","english":"The second section, lasting around ten minutes, would focus on the people. More specifically, I would interview three individuals - a runner preparing for the race, a volunteer supporting participants, and a spectator cheering for a family member or friend. What matters is not only who finishes first, but also why people run in the first place. One runner may be trying to recover from illness; another may be running in memory of a loved one; a student participant may simply want to prove that discipline can beat laziness. These human stories would prevent the programme from becoming a plain sports report. They would also give our schoolmates someone to identify with, which is essential if we want them to keep watching.","chinese":"更具體地說，我會訪問三位人士——一位正在備戰的跑手、一位支援參賽者的義工，以及一位為家人或朋友打氣的觀眾。 重要的不僅是誰最先衝線，也包括人們最初為甚麼選擇跑步。 有些跑手可能正努力從疾病中康復；另一些人可能為了紀念摯愛而跑；一位學生參賽者也可能只是想證明紀律能戰勝懶散。 這些有人情味的故事，能避免節目淪為一則平淡的體育報道。 它們也會讓我們的同學找到能夠代入的人物；如果我們希望他們繼續觀看，這一點至關重要。 3rd Topic Sentence（主題句） The final main section, “Could We Do It Too?”, would bring the programme back to our school. 最後一個主要環節「我們也能做到嗎？」會把節目帶回我們的學校。"},{"label":"Paragraph 6","english":"The final main section, “Could We Do It Too?”, would bring the programme back to our school. We could invite two students and a PE teacher to complete a short “mini-marathon challenge” on campus. The PE teacher could explain basic running techniques, warm-up routines, pacing, hydration and injury prevention. Meanwhile, the student hosts could try the exercises and react honestly. If they find the training tiring, that is not a problem; in fact, it would make the programme more authentic. Few students, if any, enjoy being lectured about health, but many will watch classmates struggle, laugh, improve and finally complete a challenge. By showing effort step by step, we can make sport feel achievable rather than intimidating.","chinese":"我們可以邀請兩位學生和一位體育老師，在校園內完成一個簡短的「迷你馬拉松挑戰」。 體育老師可以講解基本跑步技巧、熱身程序、配速、補水方法和預防受傷的知識。 與此同時，學生主持可以親身嘗試這些練習，並真實地作出反應。 如果他們覺得訓練辛苦，這並非問題；事實上，這會令節目更加真實。 即使有學生喜歡被人說教式地講健康，數量也極少；但很多人會願意觀看同學掙扎、發笑、進步，最後完成挑戰。 透過一步一步展示努力的過程，我們可以讓運動感覺可以做到，而非令人卻步"},{"label":"Paragraph 7","english":"To make the programme interesting, I would use a fast but clear structure - exciting opening, human-centred interviews, campus challenge and closing reflection. Visually, I would include close-up shots of shoes hitting the road, slow-motion cheering, quick captions explaining key terms, and a simple map showing where the race takes place. Better still, we could add interactive elements, such as a short quiz on Campus TV’s social media page: “How long is a full marathon?” or “Which teacher would you nominate for our next running challenge?” This would give students room to participate instead of merely watching. The more they see familiar faces and have a reason to respond, the more likely they are to talk about the programme afterwards.","chinese":"為了令節目有趣，我會採用節奏明快但清晰的結構——刺激的開場、以人物為中心的訪問、校園挑戰和結尾反思。 在視覺呈現方面，我會加入跑鞋踏在路面的特寫鏡頭、慢動作打氣畫面、解釋關鍵詞的簡短字幕，以及一張顯示賽事地點的簡單地圖。 更理想的是，我們可以加入互動元素，例如在 Campus TV 的社交媒體專頁上設置小測：「全程馬拉松有多長？」或「你會提名哪位老師參加我們下一次的跑步挑戰？」 這會給予學生參與空間，避免他們只是被動觀看。 他們看見的熟悉面孔越多，又越有理由作出回應，之後談論這個節目的可能性就越高。"},{"label":"Paragraph 8","english":"All things considered, I believe the Hong Kong Marathon would be the best choice because it combines local identity, dramatic visuals and relatable personal stories. With your approval, I will draft a shooting schedule, contact the PE Department for advice and form a small production team for filming, interviewing and editing. I would appreciate it if you could let me know whether this direction is suitable.","chinese":"綜合各方面來看，我相信香港馬拉松會是最佳選擇，因為它結合了本地身份、富有戲劇感的畫面和令人有共鳴的個人故事。 如果得到您的批准，我會草擬拍攝時間表、聯絡體育科尋求意見，並組成一支小型製作隊伍，負責拍攝、訪問和剪輯。 如您能告知我這個方向是否合適，我將十分感謝。"},{"label":"Paragraph 9","english":"Yours sincerely,","chinese":"此致"},{"label":"Paragraph 10","english":"Chris Wong","chinese":"Chris Wong"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"proposal for","chinese":"關於……的建議書"},{"english":"Campus TV programme","chinese":"校園電視節目"},{"english":"running Hong Kong together","chinese":"一起跑遍香港"},{"english":"thank you for inviting me to","chinese":"感謝你邀請我……"},{"english":"produce a 30-minute programme","chinese":"製作一個30分鐘節目"},{"english":"local sporting event","chinese":"本地體育盛事"},{"english":"given that","chinese":"鑑於"},{"english":"see sport mainly as","chinese":"主要把運動視為……"},{"english":"PE lessons","chinese":"體育課"},{"english":"fitness tests","chinese":"體能測試"},{"english":"elite athletes","chinese":"精英運動員"},{"english":"propose covering","chinese":"建議報道"},{"english":"Hong Kong Marathon","chinese":"香港馬拉松"},{"english":"not just a race","chinese":"不只是一場比賽"},{"english":"rather","chinese":"而是"},{"english":"city-wide story","chinese":"全城故事"},{"english":"discipline, courage and community","chinese":"紀律、勇氣和社群精神"},{"english":"my aim is to","chinese":"我的目標是"},{"english":"ordinary Hong Kong street","chinese":"普通香港街道"},{"english":"for one morning","chinese":"在一個早上"},{"english":"become a stage","chinese":"成為舞台"},{"english":"professional runners","chinese":"專業跑手"},{"english":"office workers","chinese":"上班族"},{"english":"volunteers and supporters","chinese":"義工和支持者"},{"english":"move towards","chinese":"朝着……前進"},{"english":"finishing line","chinese":"終點線"},{"english":"in short","chinese":"簡而言之"},{"english":"encourage schoolmates to","chinese":"鼓勵同學……"},{"english":"close to their own lives","chinese":"貼近他們自己的生活"},{"english":"rather than","chinese":"而不是"},{"english":"distant on television","chinese":"在電視上遙不可及"},{"english":"open with","chinese":"以……開場"},{"english":"two-minute montage","chinese":"兩分鐘蒙太奇片段"},{"english":"before the starting gun","chinese":"起步槍聲響起之前"},{"english":"stretch under the city lights","chinese":"在城市燈光下伸展"},{"english":"hand out water","chinese":"派發食水"},{"english":"road arrangements","chinese":"道路安排"},{"english":"find the best places to cheer","chinese":"找最佳位置打氣"},{"english":"instead of giving","chinese":"而不是作出……"},{"english":"dry introduction","chinese":"枯燥的介紹"},{"english":"lead naturally into","chinese":"自然引入"},{"english":"first main section","chinese":"第一個主要部分"},{"english":"the event and the city","chinese":"活動與城市"},{"english":"briefly introduce","chinese":"簡略介紹"},{"english":"different kinds of runners","chinese":"不同類型的跑手"},{"english":"turn familiar roads into","chinese":"把熟悉道路變成……"},{"english":"shared sporting arena","chinese":"共享的體育舞台"},{"english":"take…for example","chinese":"以……為例"},{"english":"harbourfront","chinese":"海濱"},{"english":"pass these places for","chinese":"為了……而經過這些地方"},{"english":"become symbols of","chinese":"成為……的象徵"},{"english":"endurance","chinese":"耐力"},{"english":"public spirit","chinese":"公民精神；公共精神"},{"english":"lasting around ten minutes","chinese":"長約十分鐘"},{"english":"focus on","chinese":"聚焦於"},{"english":"more specifically","chinese":"更具體來說"},{"english":"interview three individuals","chinese":"訪問三位人士"},{"english":"prepare for the race","chinese":"為比賽作準備"},{"english":"support participants","chinese":"支援參加者"},{"english":"cheer for","chinese":"為……打氣"},{"english":"what matters is not only…but also…","chinese":"重要的不只是……還有……"},{"english":"finish first","chinese":"第一個完成"},{"english":"in the first place","chinese":"一開始；本來"},{"english":"recover from illness","chinese":"從疾病中康復"},{"english":"in memory of","chinese":"為紀念……"},{"english":"a loved one","chinese":"摯愛的人"},{"english":"prove that","chinese":"證明"},{"english":"beat laziness","chinese":"戰勝懶惰"},{"english":"human stories","chinese":"人情故事"},{"english":"prevent…from becoming","chinese":"防止……變成"},{"english":"plain sports report","chinese":"平淡的體育報道"},{"english":"give someone to identify with","chinese":"給某人可以認同的人"},{"english":"identify with","chinese":"產生共鳴"},{"english":"essential if","chinese":"如果……就是必不可少的"},{"english":"keep watching","chinese":"繼續觀看"},{"english":"final main section","chinese":"最後一個主要部分"},{"english":"bring…back to","chinese":"把……帶回到"},{"english":"invite someone to","chinese":"邀請某人去……"},{"english":"mini-marathon challenge","chinese":"迷你馬拉松挑戰"},{"english":"on campus","chinese":"在校園內"},{"english":"basic running techniques","chinese":"基本跑步技巧"},{"english":"warm-up routines","chinese":"熱身程序"},{"english":"pacing","chinese":"配速"},{"english":"hydration","chinese":"補充水分"},{"english":"injury prevention","chinese":"預防受傷"},{"english":"meanwhile","chinese":"與此同時"},{"english":"react honestly","chinese":"真實地反應"},{"english":"find the training tiring","chinese":"覺得訓練辛苦"},{"english":"that is not a problem","chinese":"那不是問題"},{"english":"in fact","chinese":"事實上"},{"english":"more authentic","chinese":"更真實"},{"english":"few students, if any","chinese":"即使有，也很少學生"},{"english":"being lectured about","chinese":"被說教有關……"},{"english":"struggle, laugh, improve and complete","chinese":"掙扎、歡笑、進步並完成"},{"english":"by showing effort step by step","chinese":"透過一步步展示努力"},{"english":"achievable","chinese":"可達成的"},{"english":"intimidating","chinese":"令人卻步的"},{"english":"to make the programme interesting","chinese":"為了令節目有趣"},{"english":"fast but clear structure","chinese":"節奏快但清晰的結構"},{"english":"exciting opening","chinese":"精彩開場"},{"english":"human-centred interviews","chinese":"以人為本的訪問"},{"english":"campus challenge","chinese":"校園挑戰"},{"english":"closing reflection","chinese":"結尾反思"},{"english":"visually","chinese":"在視覺上"},{"english":"close-up shots","chinese":"特寫鏡頭"},{"english":"shoes hitting the road","chinese":"鞋子踏上路面"},{"english":"slow-motion cheering","chinese":"慢鏡打氣畫面"},{"english":"quick captions","chinese":"快速字幕"},{"english":"key terms","chinese":"關鍵詞語"},{"english":"a simple map showing","chinese":"一幅簡單地圖顯示"},{"english":"take place","chinese":"舉行"},{"english":"better still","chinese":"更好的是"},{"english":"interactive elements","chinese":"互動元素"},{"english":"social media page","chinese":"社交媒體專頁"},{"english":"short quiz","chinese":"小測驗"},{"english":"full marathon","chinese":"全程馬拉松"},{"english":"nominate someone for","chinese":"提名某人參加……"},{"english":"running challenge","chinese":"跑步挑戰"},{"english":"give students room to participate","chinese":"給學生參與空間"},{"english":"instead of merely watching","chinese":"而不是只觀看"},{"english":"familiar faces","chinese":"熟悉的面孔"},{"english":"have a reason to respond","chinese":"有理由作出回應"},{"english":"the more…, the more likely…","chinese":"越……就越有可能……"},{"english":"talk about the programme afterwards","chinese":"之後談論這個節目"},{"english":"all things considered","chinese":"總括而言"},{"english":"the best choice","chinese":"最佳選擇"},{"english":"combine local identity with","chinese":"把本地身份與……結合"},{"english":"local identity","chinese":"本地身份認同"},{"english":"dramatic visuals","chinese":"富戲劇性的畫面"},{"english":"relatable personal stories","chinese":"令人有共鳴的個人故事"},{"english":"with your approval","chinese":"如獲你批准"},{"english":"draft a shooting schedule","chinese":"草擬拍攝時間表"},{"english":"contact the PE Department","chinese":"聯絡體育科"},{"english":"form a small production team","chinese":"組成小型製作團隊"},{"english":"production team","chinese":"製作團隊"},{"english":"filming, interviewing and editing","chinese":"拍攝、訪問和剪接"},{"english":"I would appreciate it if","chinese":"如你能……我將不勝感激"},{"english":"let me know whether","chinese":"讓我知道是否"},{"english":"this direction is suitable","chinese":"這個方向是否合適"},{"english":"Yours sincerely","chinese":"謹啟"}]},"dse-writing-2013-part-b-q3":{"exerciseId":"dse-writing-2013-part-b-q3","essayKey":"","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=dse-writing-2013-part-b-q3","flashDeckId":"dse/writing/part-b/2013/Q3","paragraphs":[{"label":"Paragraph 1","english":"The Day I Became Brutus","chinese":"我成為布魯圖的那一天"},{"label":"Paragraph 2","english":"26 March 2013","chinese":"2013 年 3 月 26 日"},{"label":"Paragraph 3","english":"Dear Diary,","chinese":"親愛的日記："},{"label":"Paragraph 4","english":"I cannot begin to describe how heavy my schoolbag felt today. It carried only a drama book, two exercise books and a lunchbox, yet it might as well have contained a knife. This morning in drama class, Ms Lau asked whether Brutus was a villain or a patriot when he betrayed Caesar “for Rome”. I answered too quickly: “He did what he thought was right.” By four o’clock, that answer no longer sounded clever. It sounded dangerous.","chinese":"我真的無法形容，今天我的書包感覺有多沉重。 它裡面明明只有一本戲劇書、兩本練習簿和一個飯盒，卻彷彿裝著一把刀。 今天早上的戲劇課上，劉老師問我們，當布魯圖「為了羅馬」背叛凱撒時，他究竟是惡人，還是愛國者。 我回答得太快：「他做了自己認為正確的事。」 到了四點，那個答案聽起來已不再聰明。 它聽起來很危險。"},{"label":"Paragraph 5","english":"The person I betrayed was Ryan, my best friend since Primary Four. We have survived almost everything together - our first detention, the lonely first week of Secondary One, and last year’s debate competition, when I froze on stage and he whispered, “Breathe. I’m here.” No words can do justice to what that meant to me. Ryan has always been the kind of friend who notices when my smile is only half working.","chinese":"我背叛的人是 Ryan，他是我自小四以來最好的朋友。 我們幾乎一起捱過了所有事情——第一次留堂、中一第一個星期的孤單，還有去年的辯論比賽；當時我在台上僵住了，他卻在旁邊低聲說：「呼吸。我在這裡。」 任何文字都不足以完整呈現那句話對我的意義。 Ryan 一直都是那種朋友：當我的笑容只是勉強撐起來時，他也會察覺得到。"},{"label":"Paragraph 6","english":"That is what made today unbearable.","chinese":"正正是這一點，令今天變得令人難以承受。"},{"label":"Paragraph 7","english":"Our school is preparing for the Inter-school English Drama Competition. Ryan wrote most of our script, and it was brilliant—sharp, funny and painful in all the right places. Then, during lunch, I found him in the library, hunched over a laptop. Hidden behind his document was another file: a script from a school in Kowloon, dated 2019. Several scenes were almost exactly the same as ours. Not inspired. Not influenced. Copied.","chinese":"我們學校正在準備校際英語話劇比賽。 Ryan 寫了我們劇本的大部分內容，而那劇本非常出色——尖銳、幽默，該令人心痛的地方也恰到好處。 然後，午飯時間，我在圖書館看到他彎著身子伏在一部手提電腦前。 藏在他的文件後面的，是另一個檔案：一份來自九龍某間學校、標示日期為 2019 年的劇本。 有好幾場戲幾乎和我們的一模一樣。 並非受到啟發。 也談不上受到影響。 那是抄襲。"},{"label":"Paragraph 8","english":"At first, I wanted to believe there was some explanation. Perhaps he was only comparing structures. Perhaps the lines were temporary. But when I asked him, he went pale. “Please,” he said. “Just this once. My parents think winning will help my scholarship application. I changed enough of it. Nobody will know.”","chinese":"起初，我想相信這件事總有某種解釋。 也許他只是在比較結構。 也許那些台詞只是暫時放在那裡。 但當我問他時，他的臉色變得蒼白。 「求你，」他說。 「就這一次。 我爸媽覺得得獎會有助我申請獎學金。 我已經改了夠多了。 沒有人會知道。」 沒有人會知道。 已經足夠了。"},{"label":"Paragraph 9","english":"Nobody will know.","chinese":"沒有人會知道。」 沒有人會知道。"},{"label":"Paragraph 10","english":"That was the sentence that broke something in me. I thought of our teammates, who had stayed after school for weeks to rehearse. I thought of Chloe, who had cried because she could not pronounce “inevitably” but kept practising anyway. I thought of Ms Lau, whose faith in us was almost embarrassing. More than that, I thought of Ryan himself. If I protected him, I would not be saving him; I would be teaching him that talent gave him permission to cheat. The fact that I loved him did not alter the fact that what he had done was wrong.","chinese":"正是那一句話，把我心裡某樣東西折斷了。 我想起我們的隊友，他們連續幾個星期放學後留下來排練。 我想起 Chloe，她曾因為讀不出 “inevitably” 這個字而哭了出來，卻仍然繼續練習。 我想起劉老師，她對我們的信任甚至令人有點不好意思。 更重要的是，我想起 Ryan 本人。 如果我保護他，我並沒有真正拯救他；我會是在教他，才華可以給他作弊的特權。 我愛惜他這個事實，並不能改變另一個事實：他所做的事是錯的。"},{"label":"Paragraph 11","english":"Still, I had promised him I would not tell. Had I known what that promise would cost, I might never have made it.","chinese":"然而，我曾經答應過他，我不會說出去。 如果我早知道那個承諾會付出怎樣的代價，我也許從一開始就不會許下它。"},{"label":"Paragraph 12","english":"After school, I walked to the staff room three times and walked away twice. My hands shook so badly that I nearly dropped my phone. Finally, I sent Ms Lau the screenshots and asked her not to reveal my name. Cowardly? Maybe. Necessary? I do not know anymore. All I know is that I could not let our whole team walk onto that stage carrying a lie.","chinese":"放學後，我三次走到教員室門前，卻有兩次轉身離開。 我的手抖得很厲害，差點連手機也拿不穩。 最後，我把截圖傳給劉老師，並請她不要透露我的名字。 懦弱嗎？ 也許吧。 必要嗎？ 我已經不知道了。 我唯一知道的是，我不能讓整個團隊帶著一個謊言走上舞台。"},{"label":"Paragraph 13","english":"No one saw the storm coming. By the last lesson, Ryan had been called out. The competition entry was suspended. Our classmates were left whispering, confused and furious, while Ms Lau told us to go home and wait. Then Ryan found me near the staircase. He did not shout. He simply looked at me with a strange, empty calm and said, “It was you.”","chinese":"沒有人預料到那場風暴會來。 到了最後一節課，Ryan 已經被叫了出去。 比賽參賽資格被暫停了。 同學們都被弄得竊竊私語，又困惑又憤怒，而劉老師叫我們先回家等消息。 然後，Ryan 在樓梯附近找到了我。 他沒有大叫。 他只是帶著一種奇怪而空洞的平靜看著我，然後說：「是你。」"},{"label":"Paragraph 14","english":"Two words. Enough.","chinese":"兩個詞。 已經足夠了。"},{"label":"Paragraph 15","english":"I wanted to explain that I did it for the team, for fairness, even for him. Instead, I stood there like Brutus at Caesar’s feet, holding reasons that suddenly felt too small. Ryan walked away, and for the first time in forever, I had no idea whether I had saved my friend or destroyed him.","chinese":"我想解釋，我這樣做是為了團隊、為了公平，甚至是為了他。 結果，我只是站在那裡，像凱撒腳邊的布魯圖一樣，手裡握著那些突然顯得太渺小的理由。 Ryan 轉身離開，而很久以來第一次，我不知道自己究竟是救了朋友，還是毀了他。"},{"label":"Paragraph 16","english":"Now my room is dark except for this page. I keep telling myself that honesty is the best policy, that actions have consequences, that as you sow, so you reap. All of that may be true. Even so, truth has not made my heart lighter.","chinese":"現在，我的房間一片漆黑，只剩下這一頁還在眼前。 我一直告訴自己，誠實是上策，行動必有後果，種甚麼因，就得甚麼果。 這一切也許都是真的。 即使如此，真相並沒有讓我的心變得輕一點。"},{"label":"Paragraph 17","english":"Tomorrow, I will speak to Ryan in person. I will apologise—not for telling the truth, but for making a promise I should never have made and for hurting him behind his back. If he never forgives me, so be it. With every choice comes a consequence. Tonight, mine is silence.","chinese":"明天，我會親自和 Ryan 說話。 我會道歉——並非因為我說出了真相；真正原因是我曾許下一個不該許下的承諾，還在他背後傷害了他。 如果他永遠不原諒我，那我也只能接受。 每一個選擇，都會伴隨一個後果。 今晚，我的後果是沉默。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"Dear Diary","chinese":"親愛的日記"},{"english":"cannot begin to describe","chinese":"無法形容"},{"english":"schoolbag felt heavy","chinese":"書包感覺很沉重"},{"english":"might as well have contained","chinese":"簡直像是裝著"},{"english":"drama class","chinese":"戲劇課"},{"english":"whether…or…","chinese":"是……還是……"},{"english":"a villain or a patriot","chinese":"反派還是愛國者"},{"english":"betrayed Caesar","chinese":"背叛凱撒"},{"english":"for Rome","chinese":"為了羅馬"},{"english":"answer too quickly","chinese":"回答得太快"},{"english":"what he thought was right","chinese":"他認為正確的事"},{"english":"no longer sounded clever","chinese":"聽起來不再聰明"},{"english":"sounded dangerous","chinese":"聽起來危險"},{"english":"the person I betrayed","chinese":"我背叛的人"},{"english":"best friend since","chinese":"自……以來的好朋友"},{"english":"Primary Four","chinese":"小四"},{"english":"survive almost everything together","chinese":"一起熬過幾乎所有事情"},{"english":"first detention","chinese":"第一次留堂"},{"english":"the lonely first week","chinese":"孤單的第一個星期"},{"english":"Secondary One","chinese":"中一"},{"english":"debate competition","chinese":"辯論比賽"},{"english":"froze on stage","chinese":"在台上呆住"},{"english":"whispered","chinese":"低聲說"},{"english":"no words can do justice to","chinese":"言語無法充分表達"},{"english":"the kind of friend who","chinese":"那種會……的朋友"},{"english":"half working","chinese":"只勉強撐起"},{"english":"made today unbearable","chinese":"令今天難以承受"},{"english":"prepare for","chinese":"為……作準備"},{"english":"Inter-school English Drama Competition","chinese":"聯校英文戲劇比賽"},{"english":"wrote most of","chinese":"寫了……的大部分"},{"english":"sharp, funny and painful","chinese":"犀利、有趣而恰到好處地令人心痛"},{"english":"in all the right places","chinese":"在恰當之處"},{"english":"during lunch","chinese":"午膳期間"},{"english":"hunched over","chinese":"彎腰伏在……前"},{"english":"hidden behind","chinese":"隱藏在……後面"},{"english":"another file","chinese":"另一個檔案"},{"english":"dated 2019","chinese":"日期為二零一九年"},{"english":"almost exactly the same as","chinese":"幾乎與……完全一樣"},{"english":"inspired","chinese":"受到啟發"},{"english":"influenced","chinese":"受影響"},{"english":"copied","chinese":"抄襲的"},{"english":"at first","chinese":"起初"},{"english":"some explanation","chinese":"某種解釋"},{"english":"comparing structures","chinese":"比較結構"},{"english":"the lines were temporary","chinese":"台詞只是暫時的"},{"english":"went pale","chinese":"臉色發白"},{"english":"just this once","chinese":"就這一次"},{"english":"scholarship application","chinese":"獎學金申請"},{"english":"changed enough of it","chinese":"已經改了足夠多"},{"english":"nobody will know","chinese":"沒有人會知道"},{"english":"broke something in me","chinese":"令我內心某部分崩塌"},{"english":"teammates","chinese":"隊友"},{"english":"stayed after school","chinese":"放學後留下來"},{"english":"rehearse","chinese":"排練"},{"english":"pronounce","chinese":"發音"},{"english":"inevitably","chinese":"不可避免地"},{"english":"kept practising anyway","chinese":"仍然繼續練習"},{"english":"faith in us","chinese":"對我們的信任"},{"english":"almost embarrassing","chinese":"幾乎令人不好意思"},{"english":"more than that","chinese":"更重要的是"},{"english":"protect him","chinese":"保護他"},{"english":"not be saving him","chinese":"並不是真的在救他"},{"english":"give someone permission to","chinese":"給某人……的許可"},{"english":"cheat","chinese":"作弊"},{"english":"the fact that","chinese":"……這個事實"},{"english":"alter the fact that","chinese":"改變……這個事實"},{"english":"what he had done was wrong","chinese":"他所做的事是錯的"},{"english":"had promised him","chinese":"曾經答應他"},{"english":"what that promise would cost","chinese":"那個承諾會付出甚麼代價"},{"english":"might never have made it","chinese":"可能從來不會作出它"},{"english":"walked to the staff room","chinese":"走到教員室"},{"english":"walked away","chinese":"走開"},{"english":"shook so badly","chinese":"抖得很厲害"},{"english":"nearly dropped","chinese":"差點掉下"},{"english":"finally","chinese":"最後"},{"english":"screenshots","chinese":"截圖"},{"english":"reveal my name","chinese":"透露我的名字"},{"english":"cowardly","chinese":"懦弱的"},{"english":"necessary","chinese":"必要的"},{"english":"do not know anymore","chinese":"已經不知道"},{"english":"all I know is that","chinese":"我只知道"},{"english":"walk onto that stage","chinese":"走上那個舞台"},{"english":"carrying a lie","chinese":"帶著謊言"},{"english":"saw the storm coming","chinese":"預見風暴來臨"},{"english":"by the last lesson","chinese":"到最後一堂課時"},{"english":"called out","chinese":"被叫出去"},{"english":"competition entry","chinese":"比賽參賽資格"},{"english":"suspended","chinese":"暫停；擱置"},{"english":"left whispering","chinese":"只剩下竊竊私語"},{"english":"confused and furious","chinese":"困惑而憤怒"},{"english":"go home and wait","chinese":"回家等候"},{"english":"near the staircase","chinese":"在樓梯附近"},{"english":"did not shout","chinese":"沒有大叫"},{"english":"simply looked at me","chinese":"只是看著我"},{"english":"strange, empty calm","chinese":"奇怪而空洞的平靜"},{"english":"enough","chinese":"足夠了"},{"english":"wanted to explain","chinese":"想解釋"},{"english":"for the team","chinese":"為了團隊"},{"english":"for fairness","chinese":"為了公平"},{"english":"even for him","chinese":"甚至是為了他"},{"english":"instead","chinese":"反而"},{"english":"like Brutus at Caesar's feet","chinese":"像站在凱撒腳邊的布魯圖斯"},{"english":"holding reasons","chinese":"握著理由"},{"english":"suddenly felt too small","chinese":"突然顯得太渺小"},{"english":"for the first time in forever","chinese":"久違地第一次"},{"english":"had no idea whether","chinese":"完全不知道是否"},{"english":"saved my friend","chinese":"救了我的朋友"},{"english":"destroyed him","chinese":"毀了他"},{"english":"except for this page","chinese":"除了這一頁之外"},{"english":"keep telling myself","chinese":"不斷告訴自己"},{"english":"honesty is the best policy","chinese":"誠實是上策"},{"english":"actions have consequences","chinese":"行為會帶來後果"},{"english":"as you sow, so you reap","chinese":"種瓜得瓜，種豆得豆"},{"english":"may be true","chinese":"也許是真的"},{"english":"even so","chinese":"即使如此"},{"english":"made my heart lighter","chinese":"令我的心變得輕鬆"},{"english":"speak to Ryan in person","chinese":"親身跟 Ryan 說話"},{"english":"apologise for","chinese":"為……道歉"},{"english":"not for telling the truth","chinese":"不是為說出真相"},{"english":"make a promise","chinese":"作出承諾"},{"english":"should never have made","chinese":"本不應作出"},{"english":"behind his back","chinese":"在他背後"},{"english":"if he never forgives me","chinese":"如果他永遠不原諒我"},{"english":"so be it","chinese":"那也只好如此"},{"english":"with every choice comes a consequence","chinese":"每個選擇都伴隨後果"},{"english":"tonight, mine is silence","chinese":"今晚，我的後果是沉默"}]},"dse-writing-2013-part-b-q4":{"exerciseId":"dse-writing-2013-part-b-q4","essayKey":"","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=dse-writing-2013-part-b-q4","flashDeckId":"dse/writing/part-b/2013/Q4","paragraphs":[{"label":"Paragraph 1","english":"Children Are Not Parcels: Making Private School Bus Services Safe","chinese":"孩子不是包裹：讓私人校巴服務變得安全"},{"label":"Paragraph 2","english":"Dear Sir or Madam,","chinese":"敬啟者："},{"label":"Paragraph 3","english":"I am writing on behalf of many worried parents and students to express my deep concern about the safety of private school bus services in Hong Kong. In a city where thousands of young children depend on school buses every day, school transport should be a quiet assurance, not a daily anxiety. Recently, however, many parents have raised concern that some operators may treat safety as a matter of habit rather than a set of non-negotiable procedures. With drivers rushing to complete routes and escorts handling several toddlers at once, one missed step can quickly become a serious danger. The Association, as the body representing private school bus service operators, should therefore take the lead in tightening industry standards in order to rebuild public confidence and, more importantly, protect children whose age makes them unable to protect themselves. I strongly recommend that your Association introduce compulsory safety training, a standardised child-check system, and a transparent monitoring mechanism.","chinese":"本人謹代表許多憂心的家長和學生，表達我對香港私人校巴服務安全的深切關注。 在一個每天有成千上萬名幼童依賴校巴的城市裡，學校交通應該是一份無聲的保障，而非每日的焦慮來源。 然而，最近許多家長提出憂慮，擔心部分營辦商可能把安全視為一種慣常做法，而非一套絕不能妥協的程序。 當司機急於完成路線，而保姆同時照顧數名幼童時，一個被忽略的步驟很快便可能變成嚴重危險。 因此，貴會作為代表私人校巴服務營辦商的組織，應帶頭收緊業界標準，以重建公眾信心；更重要的是，保護那些因年紀尚小而無法自我保護的兒童。 本人強烈建議貴會引入強制安全培訓、標準化兒童檢查制度，以及透明的監察機制。"},{"label":"Paragraph 4","english":"First, all drivers and bus escorts should be required to complete recognised child-safety training before they are allowed to serve school routes. It is one thing to drive carefully; it is another to look after three-year-olds who may unbuckle their belts, cry suddenly, fall asleep, or run towards the road when the door opens. A trained escort would know how to seat younger pupils first, calm a frightened child, and stop children from standing while the bus is moving. For example, every operator could send staff to an annual course covering first aid, emergency evacuation, child psychology, traffic-side hazards and communication with schools. After the course, staff should receive a certificate and display their identification clearly. This may involve time and cost; nevertheless, when it comes to children’s safety, professionalism must matter more than convenience. Better training translates into fewer careless decisions and safer journeys.","chinese":"首先，所有司機和校巴保姆都應被要求完成認可的兒童安全培訓，才可服務學校路線。 謹慎駕駛是一回事；照顧三歲幼童則是另一回事，因為他們可能會解開安全帶、突然哭泣、睡著，或在車門打開時衝向馬路。 受過訓練的保姆會知道如何先安排年幼學生入座、安撫受驚的孩子，並阻止兒童在校巴行駛時站起來。 例如，每間營辦商都可以安排員工參加年度課程，內容涵蓋急救、緊急疏散、兒童心理、靠近車流一側的危險，以及與學校溝通的方法。 完成課程後，員工應獲發證書，並清楚展示其身份識別。 這或許會涉及時間和成本；然而，談到兒童安全時，專業精神必須比方便更重要。 更完善的培訓會轉化為更少粗心決定，以及更安全的車程。"},{"label":"Paragraph 5","english":"Second, operators should adopt a strict step-by-step procedure for boarding, travelling and alighting. At present, parents are often unsure whether every child has been counted, seated properly and handed over to the right adult. This uncertainty leaves too much room for error. Each bus should therefore have a printed or digital attendance list, with the escort ticking off pupils when they get on and when they get off. Before leaving the bus, the driver and escort should check every row, including the back seats, to make sure no child is asleep or left behind. Seat belts should be fastened before the bus moves, and children should only be allowed to get off on the pavement side. Take a kindergarten pupil carrying a large schoolbag, for example - without adult guidance, even stepping down from a bus can become risky. A clear routine would make safety automatic rather than dependent on individual memory.","chinese":"第二，營辦商應採用嚴格的逐步程序，涵蓋上車、行車和下車三個階段。 目前，家長往往不確定每名兒童是否已被點算、妥善入座，並交到正確的成人手中。 這種不確定性留下了太多出錯空間。 因此，每輛校巴都應備有紙本或電子點名名單，由保姆在學生上車和下車時逐一剔名確認。 在離開校巴之前，司機和保姆應檢查每一排座位，包括後排座位，以確保沒有兒童睡著或被遺留車內。 校巴開動前，安全帶應已扣好；兒童亦只應獲准從行人路一側下車。 以一名背著大書包的幼稚園學生為例——如果沒有成人指引，即使只是從校巴踏下來，也可能變得危險。 清晰的日常流程會令安全成為自動執行的安排，而非依賴個別人士的記憶。"},{"label":"Paragraph 6","english":"Third, the Association should set up a transparent monitoring and complaint system. Rules that exist only on paper are no better than promises. Parents need to know who is responsible when a bus arrives late, when a child is dropped off at the wrong place, or when an escort repeatedly ignores seat-belt rules. I suggest that the Association issue a code of practice, conduct random inspections, and require operators to keep journey records. Better still, a simple communication channel—such as a hotline or messaging system—could allow parents and schools to report problems promptly. Operators with repeated complaints should be required to undergo retraining; serious or repeated breaches should lead to suspension from school routes. This is not meant to punish responsible operators. Rather, it would protect their reputation by separating careful services from careless ones.","chinese":"第三，貴會應設立透明的監察和投訴制度。 只存在於紙面上的規則，並不比空洞承諾好多少。 當校巴遲到、兒童被送到錯誤地點，或保姆多次無視安全帶規則時，家長需要知道應由誰負責。 本人建議貴會發出實務守則、進行突擊檢查，並要求營辦商保存行車記錄。 更理想的是，一個簡單的溝通渠道——例如熱線或訊息系統——可讓家長和學校迅速報告問題。 屢次被投訴的營辦商應被要求接受重新培訓；嚴重或重複違規的個案，則應導致相關營辦商被暫停服務學校路線。 這樣做的目的並非懲罰負責任的營辦商。 更準確地說，這能把謹慎的服務與粗疏的服務區分開來，從而保障負責任營辦商的聲譽。"},{"label":"Paragraph 7","english":"In conclusion, private school bus services are not merely transport businesses; they carry children, trust and public responsibility. The present concerns should not be dismissed as parental overreaction, because prevention is always better than cure. I sincerely urge the Bus Operators Association of Hong Kong to act before an avoidable tragedy forces change upon the industry. By training staff properly, standardising daily procedures and monitoring operators openly, your Association can make private school buses safer, more professional and more worthy of parents’ trust. I would be grateful if you could consider these recommendations and share with schools and parents what action will be taken in due course.","chinese":"總結來說，私人校巴服務不單是運輸業務；它們承載的是兒童、信任與公共責任。 目前的憂慮不應被視為家長過度反應，因為預防永遠勝於補救。 本人誠懇敦促香港校巴營辦商協會在可避免的悲劇迫使業界改革之前，主動採取行動。 透過妥善培訓員工、標準化日常程序，以及公開監察營辦商，貴會能使私人校巴更安全、更專業，也更值得家長信任。 如蒙貴會考慮以上建議，並在適當時候向學校和家長交代將會採取的行動，本人將不勝感激。"},{"label":"Paragraph 8","english":"Yours faithfully,","chinese":"此致敬禮"},{"label":"Paragraph 9","english":"Chris Wong","chinese":"Chris Wong"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"children are not parcels","chinese":"孩子不是包裹"},{"english":"private school bus services","chinese":"私營校巴服務"},{"english":"Dear Sir or Madam","chinese":"敬啟者"},{"english":"write on behalf of","chinese":"代表……寫信"},{"english":"worried parents and students","chinese":"憂心的家長和學生"},{"english":"express my deep concern about","chinese":"表達我對……的深切關注"},{"english":"the safety of","chinese":"……的安全"},{"english":"depend on school buses","chinese":"依賴校巴"},{"english":"school transport","chinese":"學校交通服務"},{"english":"a quiet assurance","chinese":"默默帶來安心的保障"},{"english":"not a daily anxiety","chinese":"而不是每日的焦慮"},{"english":"raise concerns that","chinese":"提出憂慮指"},{"english":"operators","chinese":"營辦商"},{"english":"treat safety as","chinese":"把安全視為"},{"english":"a matter of habit","chinese":"習慣問題"},{"english":"rather than","chinese":"而不是"},{"english":"non-negotiable procedures","chinese":"不容妥協的程序"},{"english":"drivers rushing to complete routes","chinese":"司機趕着完成路線"},{"english":"complete routes","chinese":"完成行車路線"},{"english":"bus escorts","chinese":"校巴保姆；隨車照顧員"},{"english":"handle several toddlers at once","chinese":"同時照顧幾名幼兒"},{"english":"toddlers","chinese":"幼兒"},{"english":"one missed step","chinese":"一個疏漏"},{"english":"serious danger","chinese":"嚴重危險"},{"english":"the body representing","chinese":"代表……的機構"},{"english":"private school bus service operators","chinese":"私營校巴服務營辦商"},{"english":"take the lead in","chinese":"帶頭"},{"english":"tightening industry standards","chinese":"收緊行業標準"},{"english":"in order to","chinese":"為了"},{"english":"rebuild public confidence","chinese":"重建公眾信心"},{"english":"protect children","chinese":"保護兒童"},{"english":"unable to protect themselves","chinese":"無法保護自己"},{"english":"strongly recommend that","chinese":"強烈建議"},{"english":"introduce compulsory safety training","chinese":"推行強制安全培訓"},{"english":"standardised child-check system","chinese":"標準化兒童點算系統"},{"english":"transparent monitoring mechanism","chinese":"透明監察機制"},{"english":"be required to complete","chinese":"被要求完成"},{"english":"recognised child-safety training","chinese":"認可兒童安全培訓"},{"english":"be allowed to serve school routes","chinese":"獲准服務校巴路線"},{"english":"It is one thing to…, it is another to…","chinese":"……是一回事，……是另一回事"},{"english":"drive carefully","chinese":"小心駕駛"},{"english":"look after three-year-olds","chinese":"照顧三歲幼兒"},{"english":"unbuckle their belts","chinese":"解開安全帶"},{"english":"cry suddenly","chinese":"突然哭起來"},{"english":"fall asleep","chinese":"睡着"},{"english":"run towards the road","chinese":"跑向馬路"},{"english":"when the door opens","chinese":"當車門打開時"},{"english":"a trained escort","chinese":"受過訓練的隨車照顧員"},{"english":"seat younger pupils first","chinese":"先安排年幼學生入座"},{"english":"calm a frightened child","chinese":"安撫受驚的孩子"},{"english":"stop children from standing","chinese":"阻止兒童站立"},{"english":"while the bus is moving","chinese":"當校巴行駛時"},{"english":"send staff to an annual course","chinese":"派職員參加年度課程"},{"english":"first aid","chinese":"急救"},{"english":"emergency evacuation","chinese":"緊急疏散"},{"english":"child psychology","chinese":"兒童心理學"},{"english":"traffic-side hazards","chinese":"近車路一邊的危險"},{"english":"communication with schools","chinese":"與學校溝通"},{"english":"receive a certificate","chinese":"獲發證書"},{"english":"display their identification clearly","chinese":"清楚展示身分證明"},{"english":"involve time and cost","chinese":"涉及時間和成本"},{"english":"nevertheless","chinese":"然而"},{"english":"when it comes to","chinese":"當談到……時"},{"english":"professionalism","chinese":"專業精神"},{"english":"matter more than convenience","chinese":"比方便更重要"},{"english":"translate into","chinese":"轉化為"},{"english":"careless decisions","chinese":"粗心的決定"},{"english":"safer journeys","chinese":"更安全的車程"},{"english":"adopt a strict step-by-step procedure","chinese":"採用嚴格的逐步程序"},{"english":"boarding, travelling and alighting","chinese":"上車、乘車和下車"},{"english":"at present","chinese":"目前"},{"english":"be unsure whether","chinese":"不確定是否"},{"english":"be counted","chinese":"被點算"},{"english":"seated properly","chinese":"正確就座"},{"english":"handed over to the right adult","chinese":"交給正確的成人"},{"english":"uncertainty","chinese":"不確定性"},{"english":"leave too much room for error","chinese":"留下太多出錯空間"},{"english":"printed or digital attendance list","chinese":"紙本或電子點名表"},{"english":"tick off pupils","chinese":"為學生剔名"},{"english":"get on","chinese":"上車"},{"english":"get off","chinese":"下車"},{"english":"before leaving the bus","chinese":"離開校巴前"},{"english":"check every row","chinese":"檢查每一排座位"},{"english":"back seats","chinese":"後排座位"},{"english":"make sure no child is asleep or left behind","chinese":"確保沒有孩子睡着或被遺留"},{"english":"be left behind","chinese":"被遺留"},{"english":"seat belts should be fastened","chinese":"安全帶應扣好"},{"english":"before the bus moves","chinese":"在校巴開動前"},{"english":"only be allowed to","chinese":"只獲准"},{"english":"pavement side","chinese":"行人路一邊"},{"english":"kindergarten pupil","chinese":"幼稚園學生"},{"english":"carrying a large schoolbag","chinese":"背着大書包"},{"english":"without adult guidance","chinese":"沒有成人指導"},{"english":"step down from a bus","chinese":"從巴士下車"},{"english":"become risky","chinese":"變得有風險"},{"english":"a clear routine","chinese":"清晰常規"},{"english":"make safety automatic","chinese":"令安全步驟成為自然習慣"},{"english":"dependent on individual memory","chinese":"依賴個人記憶"},{"english":"set up","chinese":"設立"},{"english":"transparent monitoring and complaint system","chinese":"透明監察及投訴系統"},{"english":"exist only on paper","chinese":"只存在於紙上"},{"english":"no better than promises","chinese":"與空口承諾無異"},{"english":"know who is responsible","chinese":"知道誰負責"},{"english":"arrive late","chinese":"遲到"},{"english":"be dropped off at the wrong place","chinese":"被送到錯誤地點下車"},{"english":"repeatedly ignore","chinese":"一再忽視"},{"english":"seat-belt rules","chinese":"安全帶規則"},{"english":"issue a code of practice","chinese":"發出實務守則"},{"english":"conduct random inspections","chinese":"進行突擊檢查"},{"english":"keep journey records","chinese":"保存行車紀錄"},{"english":"better still","chinese":"更好的是"},{"english":"communication channel","chinese":"溝通渠道"},{"english":"hotline","chinese":"熱線"},{"english":"messaging system","chinese":"訊息系統"},{"english":"report problems promptly","chinese":"及時匯報問題"},{"english":"operators with repeated complaints","chinese":"屢遭投訴的營辦商"},{"english":"undergo retraining","chinese":"接受再培訓"},{"english":"serious or repeated breaches","chinese":"嚴重或重複違規"},{"english":"lead to suspension","chinese":"導致停牌；導致暫停服務"},{"english":"suspension from school routes","chinese":"暫停營運校巴路線"},{"english":"not meant to punish","chinese":"並非旨在懲罰"},{"english":"responsible operators","chinese":"負責任的營辦商"},{"english":"protect their reputation","chinese":"保護他們的聲譽"},{"english":"separate careful services from careless ones","chinese":"區分謹慎服務和馬虎服務"},{"english":"in conclusion","chinese":"總括而言"},{"english":"not merely transport businesses","chinese":"不只是交通生意"},{"english":"carry children, trust and public responsibility","chinese":"承載孩子、信任和公共責任"},{"english":"present concerns","chinese":"目前的憂慮"},{"english":"be dismissed as","chinese":"被視為……而不予理會"},{"english":"parental overreaction","chinese":"家長反應過度"},{"english":"prevention is always better than cure","chinese":"預防勝於治療"},{"english":"sincerely urge","chinese":"誠懇敦促"},{"english":"act before","chinese":"在……之前採取行動"},{"english":"avoidable tragedy","chinese":"可避免的悲劇"},{"english":"force change upon the industry","chinese":"迫使行業作出改變"},{"english":"train staff properly","chinese":"正確培訓職員"},{"english":"standardise daily procedures","chinese":"標準化日常程序"},{"english":"monitor operators openly","chinese":"公開透明地監察營辦商"},{"english":"more worthy of parents' trust","chinese":"更值得家長信任"},{"english":"I would be grateful if you could consider","chinese":"如你能考慮……，我將不勝感激"},{"english":"share with schools and parents","chinese":"與學校和家長分享"},{"english":"what action will be taken","chinese":"將會採取甚麼行動"},{"english":"in due course","chinese":"適時；在適當時候"},{"english":"Yours faithfully","chinese":"此致敬禮"}]},"dse-writing-2013-part-b-q5":{"exerciseId":"dse-writing-2013-part-b-q5","essayKey":"","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=dse-writing-2013-part-b-q5","flashDeckId":"dse/writing/part-b/2013/Q5","paragraphs":[{"label":"Paragraph 1","english":"A Minor Detour Is Not a Major Injustice","chinese":"小小繞路並非重大不公"},{"label":"Paragraph 2","english":"Dear Editor,","chinese":"編輯先生／女士："},{"label":"Paragraph 3","english":"I am writing in response to a series of complaints I heard last weekend outside the newly renovated footbridge near our district MTR station. The government has temporarily narrowed part of the pavement in order to install a lift, tactile paving and a covered ramp for elderly residents, wheelchair users and parents with prams. Yet several passers-by were condemning the works as “a waste of money” and “a nuisance to ordinary people”. With all due respect, I take issue with that view. Their irritation may be understandable, but their complaint is unreasonable because it mistakes a small, temporary inconvenience for a serious injustice and forgets those for whom accessibility is not a luxury, but a daily necessity.","chinese":"我寫信是為了回應上週末在我們區內港鐵站附近、新近翻修的行人天橋外所聽到的一連串投訴。 政府暫時收窄了部分行人路，以便為長者、輪椅使用者和推嬰兒車的家長安裝升降機、觸覺引路磚和有蓋斜道。 然而，有幾名路人卻把這項工程斥為「浪費金錢」和「對普通人造成滋擾」 恕我直言，我不同意這種看法。 他們感到煩躁也許可以理解；然而，他們的投訴並不合理，因為它把一點短暫的小不便誤認為嚴重的不公，也忘記了對某些人而言，無障礙通達並非奢侈享受，反倒是日常生活的必需。"},{"label":"Paragraph 4","english":"The complainants’ argument, as far as I could tell, was built on three points. First, they said the barriers forced pedestrians to walk an extra few minutes during the morning rush hour. Secondly, they complained that the construction noise disturbed nearby shops and residents. Thirdly, some insisted that, since “most people can use the stairs”, public money should not be spent on facilities for a minority. On the face of it, these concerns may sound practical. Nobody enjoys squeezing past metal fences or listening to drilling before breakfast. However, at first glance, the complaint concerns efficiency; on closer inspection, it reveals a narrower attitude: public space is being judged only through the eyes of the fastest and healthiest users.","chinese":"就我所能判斷，投訴者的論點主要建立在三點之上。 第一，他們說圍欄迫使行人在早上繁忙時間多走幾分鐘路。 第二，他們投訴工程噪音滋擾附近商店和居民。 第三，有些人堅持認為，既然「大部分人都可以使用樓梯」，公帑就不應花在為少數人而設的設施上。 表面看來，這些憂慮也許聽起來很實際。 沒有人喜歡在早餐前擠過金屬圍欄，或聽著鑽孔聲。 然而，乍看之下，這宗投訴關乎效率；細看之下，它揭示了一種更狹隘的心態：人們只透過行動最快、身體最健康的使用者眼光去評價公共空間。"},{"label":"Paragraph 5","english":"What the complainants failed to see was that a staircase is not merely inconvenient to some people; it is a closed door. Take an elderly woman carrying groceries, a father pushing a sleeping child, a delivery worker with a heavy trolley, or a student recovering from a leg injury. For them, “just use the stairs” is not advice, but exclusion disguised as common sense. A five-minute detour for an able-bodied pedestrian is annoying; the absence of a lift for a wheelchair user can mean cancelling a medical appointment, avoiding a library, or depending on a stranger for help. The more we design the city only for those who move quickly, the more invisible we make those who cannot. It therefore follows that spending public money on accessibility is not special treatment. Instead, it is a way to make an already public place truly public.","chinese":"投訴者未能看見的是：樓梯對某些人而言，並非只造成不便；它更像一道關上的門。 試想像一位提著日用品的老婦人、一位推著熟睡孩子的父親、一名推著沉重手推車的送貨員，或一名腿傷康復中的學生。 對他們來說，「走樓梯就好了」並非建議；這是披著常識外衣的排斥。 對健全行人而言，五分鐘的繞路令人煩厭；但對輪椅使用者而言，沒有升降機可能意味著取消覆診、避開圖書館，或要依靠陌生人幫忙。 我們越是只為行動迅速的人設計城市，就越會令行動不便的人變得隱形。 因此，用公帑改善無障礙通達，順理成章並非特殊待遇。 相反，這是一種讓本來屬於公眾的地方真正向所有人開放的方法。"},{"label":"Paragraph 6","english":"Granted, the works could have been better managed. The authorities should display clearer notices, finish noisy procedures as efficiently as possible, and leave enough room for safe pedestrian flow. Shop owners, too, deserve to be informed if their entrances may be affected. This is not to say that residents have no right to complain about poor arrangements. They do. The point is not whether people may object to inconvenience, but whether every inconvenience deserves moral outrage. Here, the answer should be a resounding no. If the complaint had been, “Please improve the temporary route,” it would have been reasonable. Yet demanding that the project be cancelled simply because it disrupts a familiar shortcut is another matter altogether.","chinese":"誠然，這項工程本可以管理得更好。 當局應張貼更清晰的告示，盡可能有效率地完成產生噪音的工序，並預留足夠空間讓行人安全通過。 如果店舖入口可能受影響，店主也理應得到通知。 這並非要說居民沒有權利投訴安排不善。 他們當然有這個權利。 重點並非人們可否反對不便，重點在於是否每一種不便都值得上升至道德憤怒 在這件事上，答案應該是非常明確的否定。 如果投訴內容是「請改善臨時路線」，那本來會是合理的。 然而，僅僅因為工程打亂了一條熟悉的捷徑，就要求取消整個項目，則完全是另一回事。"},{"label":"Paragraph 7","english":"More importantly, such complaints encourage an ungenerous civic culture. In Hong Kong, where space is limited and everyone is in a hurry, we are often tempted to measure fairness by how little our own routine is disturbed. However, a decent city cannot be built on “my convenience first”. With every public improvement comes some disturbance - road repairs, drainage works, barrier-free facilities and even school-zone safety measures all require patience before they bring benefits. If we object whenever the immediate gain is not ours, where does that leave the elderly, the disabled and the less vocal? Few, if any, of us would want to live in a city where the loudest pedestrians always outrank the most vulnerable ones.","chinese":"更重要的是，這類投訴會助長一種缺乏寬厚精神的公民文化。 在香港這個空間有限、人人都步履匆忙的地方，我們往往容易用自己的日常安排受干擾的程度來衡量公平。 然而，一座文明的城市不能建立在「我的方便優先」之上。 每一項公共改善都會伴隨某種干擾——修路、渠務工程、無障礙設施，甚至校區安全措施，都需要市民先付出耐性，然後才帶來好處。 如果每當即時得益不屬於我們時，我們就提出反對，那麼長者、殘疾人士和較少發聲的人又會被置於何地？ 我們當中即使有人願意，也必定極少人會想生活在一座由聲音最大的行人永遠排在最弱勢者之前的城市。"},{"label":"Paragraph 8","english":"Therefore, I urge residents to direct their frustration at practical shortcomings, not at the principle of accessibility. The District Office should communicate clearly and complete the works responsibly; meanwhile, citizens should give the project room to succeed. A city is not just about speed; it is about whether different people can move through it with dignity. A short detour will soon be forgotten. A lift that restores someone’s independence may change a life.","chinese":"因此，我促請居民把不滿指向實際安排上的不足，而非針對無障礙通達這個原則本身。 民政事務處應清楚溝通，並負責任地完成工程；與此同時，市民也應給予這項工程成功的空間。 一座城市關乎的不只是速度；核心在於不同人能否有尊嚴地在其中往來。 一小段繞路很快便會被遺忘。 一部能讓某人重拾獨立的升降機，卻可能改變一生。"},{"label":"Paragraph 9","english":"Yours faithfully,","chinese":"謹啟"},{"label":"Paragraph 10","english":"Chris Wong","chinese":"Chris Wong"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"minor detour","chinese":"小小繞路"},{"english":"major injustice","chinese":"重大不公"},{"english":"Dear Editor","chinese":"編輯先生／女士"},{"english":"write in response to","chinese":"寫信回應"},{"english":"a series of complaints","chinese":"一連串投訴"},{"english":"newly renovated footbridge","chinese":"新近翻新的行人天橋"},{"english":"district MTR station","chinese":"區內港鐵站"},{"english":"temporarily narrowed","chinese":"暫時收窄"},{"english":"pavement","chinese":"行人路"},{"english":"in order to install","chinese":"為了安裝"},{"english":"lift","chinese":"升降機"},{"english":"tactile paving","chinese":"觸覺引路帶"},{"english":"covered ramp","chinese":"有上蓋斜道"},{"english":"elderly residents","chinese":"年長居民"},{"english":"wheelchair users","chinese":"輪椅使用者"},{"english":"parents with prams","chinese":"推嬰兒車的父母"},{"english":"passers-by","chinese":"路人"},{"english":"condemn the works as","chinese":"將工程譴責為"},{"english":"a waste of money","chinese":"浪費金錢"},{"english":"a nuisance to","chinese":"對……造成滋擾"},{"english":"with all due respect","chinese":"恕我直言"},{"english":"take issue with","chinese":"不同意；對……提出異議"},{"english":"irritation","chinese":"不滿；煩躁"},{"english":"understandable","chinese":"可以理解的"},{"english":"unreasonable","chinese":"不合理的"},{"english":"mistake… for…","chinese":"將……誤當作……"},{"english":"temporary inconvenience","chinese":"暫時不便"},{"english":"serious injustice","chinese":"嚴重不公"},{"english":"forget those for whom","chinese":"忘記對某些人來說"},{"english":"accessibility","chinese":"無障礙設施；可達性"},{"english":"not a luxury, but a daily necessity","chinese":"不是奢侈品，而是日常必需"},{"english":"complainants' argument","chinese":"投訴者的論點"},{"english":"as far as I could tell","chinese":"據我所知；依我判斷"},{"english":"be built on three points","chinese":"建基於三點"},{"english":"barriers","chinese":"圍欄；障礙物"},{"english":"force pedestrians to","chinese":"迫使行人去"},{"english":"pedestrians","chinese":"行人"},{"english":"an extra few minutes","chinese":"額外幾分鐘"},{"english":"morning rush hour","chinese":"早上繁忙時間"},{"english":"construction noise","chinese":"建築噪音"},{"english":"nearby shops and residents","chinese":"附近商店和居民"},{"english":"insist that","chinese":"堅稱"},{"english":"public money","chinese":"公帑"},{"english":"be spent on","chinese":"被花在"},{"english":"facilities for a minority","chinese":"為少數人而設的設施"},{"english":"on the face of it","chinese":"表面看來"},{"english":"sound practical","chinese":"聽起來實際"},{"english":"squeeze past","chinese":"擠過"},{"english":"metal fences","chinese":"金屬圍欄"},{"english":"drilling before breakfast","chinese":"早餐前的鑽鑿聲"},{"english":"at first glance","chinese":"乍看之下"},{"english":"on closer inspection","chinese":"仔細看來"},{"english":"reveal a narrower attitude","chinese":"顯示較狹隘的態度"},{"english":"public space","chinese":"公共空間"},{"english":"be judged through the eyes of","chinese":"透過……的眼光判斷"},{"english":"the fastest and healthiest users","chinese":"行得最快、最健康的使用者"},{"english":"fail to see","chinese":"未能看見；忽略"},{"english":"staircase","chinese":"樓梯"},{"english":"not merely inconvenient","chinese":"不只是造成不便"},{"english":"a closed door","chinese":"一扇關上的門"},{"english":"take… for example","chinese":"以……為例"},{"english":"carry groceries","chinese":"拿着雜貨"},{"english":"push a sleeping child","chinese":"推着熟睡的孩子"},{"english":"delivery worker","chinese":"送貨員"},{"english":"heavy trolley","chinese":"沉重手推車"},{"english":"recover from","chinese":"從……康復中"},{"english":"leg injury","chinese":"腿傷"},{"english":"not advice, but exclusion","chinese":"不是建議，而是排斥"},{"english":"disguised as common sense","chinese":"偽裝成常識"},{"english":"common sense","chinese":"常識"},{"english":"five-minute detour","chinese":"五分鐘繞路"},{"english":"able-bodied pedestrian","chinese":"身體健全的行人"},{"english":"absence of a lift","chinese":"缺少升降機"},{"english":"cancelling a medical appointment","chinese":"取消覆診／醫療預約"},{"english":"medical appointment","chinese":"醫療預約"},{"english":"avoid a library","chinese":"避開圖書館"},{"english":"depend on a stranger for help","chinese":"依賴陌生人幫忙"},{"english":"the more…, the more…","chinese":"越……就越……"},{"english":"design the city","chinese":"設計城市"},{"english":"move quickly","chinese":"行動迅速"},{"english":"make someone invisible","chinese":"令某人被忽視"},{"english":"it therefore follows that","chinese":"因此可以推論"},{"english":"spending public money on accessibility","chinese":"將公帑用於無障礙設施"},{"english":"special treatment","chinese":"特別待遇"},{"english":"truly public","chinese":"真正屬於公眾"},{"english":"granted","chinese":"誠然"},{"english":"better managed","chinese":"管理得更好"},{"english":"authorities","chinese":"當局"},{"english":"display clearer notices","chinese":"展示更清晰的告示"},{"english":"noisy procedures","chinese":"噪音較大的工序"},{"english":"as efficiently as possible","chinese":"盡可能有效率地"},{"english":"leave enough room for","chinese":"留出足夠空間予"},{"english":"safe pedestrian flow","chinese":"安全行人流動"},{"english":"shop owners","chinese":"店主"},{"english":"deserve to be informed","chinese":"應該被通知"},{"english":"entrances may be affected","chinese":"入口可能受影響"},{"english":"this is not to say that","chinese":"這並不是說"},{"english":"have no right to complain","chinese":"沒有權投訴"},{"english":"poor arrangements","chinese":"欠佳安排"},{"english":"the point is not whether…, but whether…","chinese":"重點不在於是否……，而在於是否……"},{"english":"object to inconvenience","chinese":"反對不便"},{"english":"moral outrage","chinese":"道德憤怒"},{"english":"a resounding no","chinese":"響亮的否定答案"},{"english":"temporary route","chinese":"臨時路線"},{"english":"demand that","chinese":"要求"},{"english":"the project be cancelled","chinese":"取消工程"},{"english":"simply because","chinese":"只是因為"},{"english":"disrupt a familiar shortcut","chinese":"打亂熟悉的捷徑"},{"english":"another matter altogether","chinese":"完全是另一回事"},{"english":"more importantly","chinese":"更重要的是"},{"english":"encourage an ungenerous civic culture","chinese":"助長缺乏包容的公民文化"},{"english":"ungenerous","chinese":"不夠寬厚的；缺乏包容的"},{"english":"civic culture","chinese":"公民文化"},{"english":"space is limited","chinese":"空間有限"},{"english":"in a hurry","chinese":"匆忙"},{"english":"be tempted to","chinese":"忍不住想"},{"english":"measure fairness by","chinese":"以……衡量公平"},{"english":"our own routine","chinese":"自己的日常習慣"},{"english":"be disturbed","chinese":"被打擾"},{"english":"decent city","chinese":"像樣的城市"},{"english":"be built on","chinese":"建基於"},{"english":"my convenience first","chinese":"我的方便優先"},{"english":"with every public improvement comes","chinese":"每項公共改善都會帶來"},{"english":"public improvement","chinese":"公共改善工程"},{"english":"disturbance","chinese":"滋擾；干擾"},{"english":"road repairs","chinese":"道路維修"},{"english":"drainage works","chinese":"渠務工程"},{"english":"barrier-free facilities","chinese":"無障礙設施"},{"english":"school-zone safety measures","chinese":"學校區域安全措施"},{"english":"require patience","chinese":"需要耐性"},{"english":"bring benefits","chinese":"帶來好處"},{"english":"object whenever","chinese":"每當……便反對"},{"english":"immediate gain","chinese":"即時好處"},{"english":"where does that leave…?","chinese":"那會令……處於甚麼境地？"},{"english":"the elderly","chinese":"長者"},{"english":"the disabled","chinese":"殘疾人士"},{"english":"the less vocal","chinese":"較少發聲的人"},{"english":"few, if any","chinese":"即使有，也少之又少"},{"english":"live in a city where","chinese":"生活在一個……的城市"},{"english":"the loudest pedestrians","chinese":"最大聲的行人"},{"english":"outrank","chinese":"凌駕於"},{"english":"vulnerable ones","chinese":"弱勢人士"},{"english":"urge residents to","chinese":"敦促居民去"},{"english":"direct frustration at","chinese":"將不滿指向"},{"english":"practical shortcomings","chinese":"實際不足之處"},{"english":"the principle of accessibility","chinese":"無障礙原則"},{"english":"District Office","chinese":"民政事務處"},{"english":"communicate clearly","chinese":"清楚溝通"},{"english":"complete the works responsibly","chinese":"負責任地完成工程"},{"english":"meanwhile","chinese":"與此同時"},{"english":"give the project room to succeed","chinese":"給予工程成功的空間"},{"english":"not just about speed","chinese":"不只是講求速度"},{"english":"move through it with dignity","chinese":"有尊嚴地在其中出行"},{"english":"dignity","chinese":"尊嚴"},{"english":"soon be forgotten","chinese":"很快被忘記"},{"english":"restore someone's independence","chinese":"恢復某人的獨立能力"},{"english":"change a life","chinese":"改變一生"},{"english":"Yours faithfully","chinese":"謹啟"}]},"dse-writing-2013-part-b-q6":{"exerciseId":"dse-writing-2013-part-b-q6","essayKey":"","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=dse-writing-2013-part-b-q6","flashDeckId":"dse/writing/part-b/2013/Q6","paragraphs":[{"label":"Paragraph 1","english":"Leaving Late Should Not Become Our Normal","chinese":"晚下班不應成為我們的常態"},{"label":"Paragraph 2","english":"At 7:30 in the evening, the office should be winding down. Recently, however, rows of computer screens have still been glowing, with colleagues typing reports, answering emails and making “one last” change to a proposal. As a human resources assistant, I believe this observation should concern all of us. It has prompted management to consider how we can improve our working arrangements so that staff can remain efficient without sacrificing their health, family life or judgement. Overtime may occasionally be necessary, especially during urgent client projects, but it should not become our invisible routine.","chinese":"晚上七時三十分，辦公室本應逐漸安靜下來。 然而，最近一排排電腦螢幕仍然亮着，同事們仍在撰寫報告、回覆電郵，並為一份建議書作出「最後一個」修改。 作為一名人力資源助理，我認為這個現象應該引起我們所有人的關注。 這已促使管理層思考，我們可以如何改善工作安排，讓員工能保持效率，同時不必犧牲健康、家庭生活或判斷力。 加班偶爾可能有其必要，尤其是在處理緊急客戶項目時；但它不應成為我們無形的日常慣例。"},{"label":"Paragraph 3","english":"The situation is not caused by laziness, nor should it be treated as a simple matter of personal choice. Many employees stay because tasks arrive late in the afternoon, meetings occupy the most productive hours, and deadlines are sometimes unclear until the day is almost over. During month-end reporting or product launches, staying late may be understandable. The problem is the repeated pattern. Some staff postpone dinner; others reply to messages on the train; junior colleagues see senior staff remaining at their desks and assume they had better do the same. Over time, what begins as dedication can turn into silent expectation. When everyone treats every delay as an emergency, no one has room to work calmly.","chinese":"這種情況並非由懶惰造成，也不應被簡化為單純的個人選擇問題。 許多員工留下來，是因為工作在下午較晚才出現，會議佔用了最有生產力的時段，而截止日期有時直到一天快要結束時仍未清晰。 在月結報告或產品發布期間，留得較晚也許可以理解。 問題在於這種模式一再重複。 有些同事延遲晚餐；另一些人在車上回覆訊息；資歷較淺的同事看見資深員工仍留在座位上，便以為自己最好也照樣做。 久而久之，原本出於投入的行為，可能會變成一種沉默的期待。 當每個人都把每一次延誤視作緊急事故，便沒有人有空間從容工作。"},{"label":"Paragraph 4","english":"The first negative effect is that excessive overtime damages both well-being and performance. A tired employee may still be present, but presence is not the same as productivity. Without sufficient rest, people lose concentration, communicate less patiently and make mistakes that later require more correction. Take a finance colleague checking a spreadsheet after ten hours of work, for example: one careless formula can delay an entire report. The same applies to customer service, where an exhausted reply can sound cold even when the intention is helpful. More importantly, long hours eat into exercise, sleep and family time, leaving colleagues with little room to recover. In other words, overtime may appear to save time tonight, but it can create tomorrow’s errors, absences and resignations.","chinese":"第一個負面影響是，過度加班會同時損害身心健康和工作表現。 疲倦的員工也許仍然人在辦公室，但人在場不等同於有生產力。 沒有足夠休息，人們會失去專注力、溝通時較缺乏耐性，並犯下日後需要更多修正的錯誤。 以一位財務部同事工作十小時後仍在檢查試算表為例：一個粗心輸入的公式，就可能拖延整份報告。 同樣情況也適用於客戶服務，疲憊時寫出的回覆，即使本意是提供幫助，也可能聽起來冷淡。 更重要的是，長工時會侵蝕運動、睡眠和家庭時間，使同事幾乎沒有空間恢復精力。 換言之，加班今晚看似節省了時間，卻可能製造明天的錯誤、缺勤和離職。"},{"label":"Paragraph 5","english":"The second effect is cultural. When leaving late becomes a badge of loyalty, commitment is measured by visibility rather than results. Few, if any, colleagues want to be the first to pack up while their team is still typing. As a result, some stay not because the work truly requires it, but because they do not want to look irresponsible. Such pressure is unfair to parents, caregivers and colleagues with long journeys home. It also damages trust: staff may start wondering whether poor planning, understaffing or unrealistic expectations are being disguised as “team spirit”. Once that belief spreads, morale is difficult to rebuild.","chinese":"第二個影響是文化上的。 當晚下班變成忠誠的象徵，投入程度便會以可見度來衡量，多於以成果判斷 當團隊仍在打字時，幾乎沒有同事願意率先收拾離開。 結果，有些人會留下來，並非因為工作真正需要如此；更準確地說，是因為他們不想顯得不負責任。 這種壓力對父母、照顧者，以及通勤路程漫長的同事都不公平。 它也會破壞信任：員工可能開始懷疑，規劃不周、人手不足或不切實際的期望，是否正被包裝成「團隊精神」。 一旦這種想法蔓延，士氣便很難重建。"},{"label":"Paragraph 6","english":"Two practical steps should be introduced. First, each department should hold a weekly workload check to separate urgent work from work that can wait. Tasks should be grouped into “must finish today”, “can finish this week” and “can be postponed”. If a task is assigned after 5 p.m., the manager should clarify whether it is genuinely urgent; otherwise, it should be scheduled for the next working day. This would help teams plan ahead, distribute work fairly and prevent last-minute pressure from falling on the same people again and again.","chinese":"我們應該引入兩項實際措施。 第一，每個部門應該每週進行一次工作量檢視，把緊急工作與可以等待的工作分開。 工作應該分為「今天必須完成」、「本週可以完成」和「可以延後」三類。 如果一項工作在下午五時後才被分派，經理應該釐清它是否真的緊急；否則，便應安排到下一個工作天處理。 這將有助團隊提前規劃、公平分配工作，並防止最後一刻的壓力一次又一次落在同一批人身上。"},{"label":"Paragraph 7","english":"Second, we should create a healthier after-hours communication policy. Unless there is a real emergency, non-urgent emails and messages should not require replies after office hours. Managers should model this by leaving on time where possible and by scheduling emails for the next morning. Where late work is unavoidable, staff should record it and receive time off in lieu or adjusted deadlines. This is not about lowering standards; rather, it is about making high standards sustainable.","chinese":"第二，我們應該建立更健康的辦公時間後溝通政策。 除非出現真正緊急情況，非緊急電郵和訊息不應要求員工在辦公時間後回覆 經理應該以身作則，在可行情況下準時離開，並把電郵排程到翌日早上才發送。 如晚間工作無法避免，員工應該作出記錄，並獲得補假或調整後的截止日期 這並非降低標準；重點在於讓高標準能夠持續。"},{"label":"Paragraph 8","english":"All things considered, the time has come to treat late departures as a warning sign, not a trophy. With clearer priorities and healthier boundaries, we can build a workplace where commitment is measured not by the hour people leave, but by the quality of the work they are able to do.","chinese":"總括而言，是時候把晚下班視為警號，而非獎盃。 只要有更清晰的優先次序和更健康的界線，我們就能建立一個職場：投入程度的衡量標準，不再是員工幾點離開，而在於他們能交出甚麼品質的工作。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"leaving late","chinese":"遲下班"},{"english":"become our normal","chinese":"成為我們的常態"},{"english":"wind down","chinese":"逐漸安靜下來；準備收工"},{"english":"rows of computer screens","chinese":"一排排電腦屏幕"},{"english":"still be glowing","chinese":"仍然亮著"},{"english":"type reports","chinese":"撰寫報告"},{"english":"answer emails","chinese":"回覆電郵"},{"english":"make one last change to","chinese":"對……作最後一次修改"},{"english":"human resources assistant","chinese":"人力資源助理"},{"english":"this observation should concern all of us","chinese":"這個觀察應該令我們所有人關注"},{"english":"prompt management to consider","chinese":"促使管理層考慮"},{"english":"improve our working arrangements","chinese":"改善我們的工作安排"},{"english":"remain efficient","chinese":"保持效率"},{"english":"without sacrificing","chinese":"不犧牲……"},{"english":"health, family life and judgement","chinese":"健康、家庭生活和判斷力"},{"english":"overtime","chinese":"加班"},{"english":"occasionally be necessary","chinese":"偶爾是必要的"},{"english":"urgent client projects","chinese":"緊急客戶項目"},{"english":"invisible routine","chinese":"無形的慣例"},{"english":"be caused by laziness","chinese":"由懶惰造成"},{"english":"be treated as","chinese":"被視為"},{"english":"a simple matter of personal choice","chinese":"簡單的個人選擇問題"},{"english":"arrive late in the afternoon","chinese":"在下午較遲時間才到來"},{"english":"occupy the most productive hours","chinese":"佔據最高效的工作時段"},{"english":"deadlines are unclear","chinese":"截止時間不清晰"},{"english":"until the day is almost over","chinese":"直到一天快要結束時"},{"english":"month-end reporting","chinese":"月結報告"},{"english":"product launches","chinese":"產品發布"},{"english":"staying late may be understandable","chinese":"遲下班或許可以理解"},{"english":"repeated pattern","chinese":"重複出現的模式"},{"english":"postpone dinner","chinese":"延遲吃晚飯"},{"english":"reply to messages on the train","chinese":"在火車上回覆訊息"},{"english":"junior colleagues","chinese":"初級同事"},{"english":"senior staff","chinese":"資深職員"},{"english":"remain at their desks","chinese":"留在辦公桌前"},{"english":"assume they had better do the same","chinese":"以為自己最好也照做"},{"english":"over time","chinese":"隨著時間過去"},{"english":"what begins as...can turn into...","chinese":"原本是……的事可能變成……"},{"english":"dedication","chinese":"奉獻；投入"},{"english":"silent expectation","chinese":"不明言的期望"},{"english":"treat every delay as an emergency","chinese":"把每次延誤都當成緊急事件"},{"english":"have room to work calmly","chinese":"有空間冷靜工作"},{"english":"negative effect","chinese":"負面影響"},{"english":"excessive overtime","chinese":"過度加班"},{"english":"damage both well-being and performance","chinese":"損害身心健康和工作表現"},{"english":"well-being","chinese":"身心健康"},{"english":"performance","chinese":"工作表現"},{"english":"be present","chinese":"身在場"},{"english":"presence is not the same as productivity","chinese":"在場不等於有生產力"},{"english":"productivity","chinese":"生產力"},{"english":"sufficient rest","chinese":"足夠休息"},{"english":"lose concentration","chinese":"失去專注力"},{"english":"communicate less patiently","chinese":"溝通時較沒耐性"},{"english":"make mistakes","chinese":"犯錯"},{"english":"require more correction","chinese":"需要更多修正"},{"english":"finance colleague","chinese":"財務部同事"},{"english":"check a spreadsheet","chinese":"檢查試算表"},{"english":"after ten hours of work","chinese":"工作十小時後"},{"english":"careless formula","chinese":"粗心大意的公式"},{"english":"delay an entire report","chinese":"延誤整份報告"},{"english":"the same applies to","chinese":"同樣適用於"},{"english":"customer service","chinese":"客戶服務"},{"english":"exhausted reply","chinese":"疲憊狀態下的回覆"},{"english":"sound cold","chinese":"聽起來冷淡"},{"english":"the intention is helpful","chinese":"原意是想幫忙"},{"english":"long hours","chinese":"長時間工作"},{"english":"eat into","chinese":"侵佔；佔用"},{"english":"family time","chinese":"家庭時間"},{"english":"little room to recover","chinese":"幾乎沒有恢復空間"},{"english":"in other words","chinese":"換句話說"},{"english":"appear to save time","chinese":"看似節省時間"},{"english":"tomorrow's errors","chinese":"明天的錯誤"},{"english":"absences and resignations","chinese":"缺勤和辭職"},{"english":"cultural effect","chinese":"文化上的影響"},{"english":"badge of loyalty","chinese":"忠誠的標誌"},{"english":"commitment is measured by","chinese":"投入程度以……衡量"},{"english":"visibility rather than results","chinese":"能見度而非成果"},{"english":"few, if any","chinese":"即使有也很少"},{"english":"pack up","chinese":"收拾東西準備離開"},{"english":"as a result","chinese":"因此"},{"english":"not because...but because...","chinese":"不是因為……而是因為……"},{"english":"look irresponsible","chinese":"看起來不負責任"},{"english":"such pressure","chinese":"這種壓力"},{"english":"be unfair to","chinese":"對……不公平"},{"english":"parents and caregivers","chinese":"父母和照顧者"},{"english":"long journeys home","chinese":"漫長回家路程"},{"english":"damage trust","chinese":"損害信任"},{"english":"start wondering whether","chinese":"開始懷疑是否"},{"english":"poor planning","chinese":"規劃不善"},{"english":"understaffing","chinese":"人手不足"},{"english":"unrealistic expectations","chinese":"不切實際的期望"},{"english":"be disguised as","chinese":"被包裝成；被偽裝成"},{"english":"team spirit","chinese":"團隊精神"},{"english":"once that belief spreads","chinese":"一旦這種信念傳開"},{"english":"morale","chinese":"士氣"},{"english":"difficult to rebuild","chinese":"難以重建"},{"english":"practical steps","chinese":"實際措施"},{"english":"be introduced","chinese":"被引入；被推行"},{"english":"each department","chinese":"每個部門"},{"english":"weekly workload check","chinese":"每週工作量檢查"},{"english":"separate urgent work from work that can wait","chinese":"區分緊急工作和可等待的工作"},{"english":"be grouped into","chinese":"被分成"},{"english":"must finish today","chinese":"今日必須完成"},{"english":"can finish this week","chinese":"本週內可完成"},{"english":"can be postponed","chinese":"可以延後"},{"english":"be assigned after 5 p.m.","chinese":"下午五時後被分派"},{"english":"clarify whether","chinese":"澄清是否"},{"english":"genuinely urgent","chinese":"真正緊急"},{"english":"otherwise","chinese":"否則"},{"english":"the next working day","chinese":"下一個工作天"},{"english":"plan ahead","chinese":"預先計劃"},{"english":"distribute work fairly","chinese":"公平分配工作"},{"english":"prevent last-minute pressure","chinese":"防止臨時壓力"},{"english":"fall on the same people","chinese":"落在同一批人身上"},{"english":"again and again","chinese":"一再；反覆地"},{"english":"after-hours communication policy","chinese":"非辦公時間溝通政策"},{"english":"unless there is a real emergency","chinese":"除非有真正緊急情況"},{"english":"non-urgent emails and messages","chinese":"非緊急電郵和訊息"},{"english":"require replies after office hours","chinese":"要求在辦公時間後回覆"},{"english":"office hours","chinese":"辦公時間"},{"english":"model this","chinese":"以身作則示範這一點"},{"english":"leave on time","chinese":"準時下班"},{"english":"where possible","chinese":"在可行情況下"},{"english":"schedule emails for the next morning","chinese":"安排電郵於翌日早上發送"},{"english":"late work is unavoidable","chinese":"加班無法避免"},{"english":"record it","chinese":"記錄下來"},{"english":"time off in lieu","chinese":"補假"},{"english":"adjusted deadlines","chinese":"調整後的截止日期"},{"english":"lowering standards","chinese":"降低標準"},{"english":"high standards","chinese":"高標準"},{"english":"make high standards sustainable","chinese":"令高標準可以持續"},{"english":"all things considered","chinese":"總括而言"},{"english":"the time has come to","chinese":"是時候"},{"english":"late departures","chinese":"遲下班"},{"english":"warning sign","chinese":"警號"},{"english":"not a trophy","chinese":"不是值得炫耀的獎盃"},{"english":"clearer priorities","chinese":"更清晰的優先次序"},{"english":"healthier boundaries","chinese":"更健康的界線"},{"english":"build a workplace where","chinese":"建立一個……的工作場所"},{"english":"measured not by...but by...","chinese":"不是以……而是以……衡量"},{"english":"the quality of the work","chinese":"工作質素"},{"english":"be able to do","chinese":"能夠做到"}]},"dse-writing-2013-part-b-q7":{"exerciseId":"dse-writing-2013-part-b-q7","essayKey":"","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=dse-writing-2013-part-b-q7","flashDeckId":"dse/writing/part-b/2013/Q7","paragraphs":[{"label":"Paragraph 1","english":"From Local Screens to Global Stages:","chinese":"從本地螢幕到全球舞台：亞洲明星為何贏得西方觀眾的心"},{"label":"Paragraph 2","english":"Why Asian Stars Are Winning Western Hearts","chinese":"從本地螢幕到全球舞台：亞洲明星為何贏得西方觀眾的心"},{"label":"Paragraph 3","english":"In recent years, it has become normal for a student in London to hum a Korean chorus, for an American family to discuss Japanese animation, or for a French teenager to quote a line from a Korean drama. This cultural shift has made Western audiences reconsider what “mainstream entertainment” means, because fame is no longer controlled only by Hollywood studios or English-language radio stations. To find fresher voices, stronger stories and more adventurous performances, viewers are turning to Asian singers and movie stars. This article explains that their popularity in Western countries is driven by digital access, artistic distinctiveness and a new hunger for representation.","chinese":"近年來，倫敦學生哼唱韓文副歌、美國家庭討論日本動畫，或法國青少年引用一句韓劇台詞，都已經變得很平常。 這種文化轉變令西方觀眾重新思考「主流娛樂」的意思，因為名氣已不再只由荷里活電影公司或英語電台掌控。 為了尋找更新鮮的聲音、更有力量的故事和更具冒險精神的表演，觀眾正轉向亞洲歌手和電影明星。 本文將解釋，亞洲明星在西方國家的受歡迎程度，是由數碼接觸渠道、藝術獨特性，以及人們對代表性的新渴求所推動的。"},{"label":"Paragraph 4","english":"First, Asian stars are gaining attention because technology has removed many of the old barriers between cultures. Gone are the days when a film had to be shown in a local cinema or a song had to be played on Western radio before it could become popular. Today, a fan can discover a Thai actor through a short clip, learn the lyrics of a Korean song through subtitles, and share a Japanese trailer within seconds. The more often algorithms recommend such content, the more familiar Asian faces become. This matters because audiences rarely love what they never meet. BTS’s “Dynamite”, for instance, topped the Billboard Hot 100 in 2020, while Netflix lists Squid Game: Season 1 as its most popular non-English TV show by views. Put simply, the screen has become a passport. Once access becomes easy, curiosity can quickly become loyalty.","chinese":"首先，亞洲明星正在獲得關注，因為科技已經移除了許多昔日存在於文化之間的障礙。 一部電影必須先在本地戲院上映，或一首歌曲必須先在西方電台播放，才可能變得受歡迎的日子已經過去。 今天，一名粉絲可以透過一段短片發現一位泰國演員，透過字幕學會一首韓文歌曲的歌詞，並在數秒之內分享一段日本預告片。 演算法越經常推薦這類內容，亞洲面孔就越會變得熟悉。 這一點很重要，因為觀眾很少會喜歡上自己從未接觸過的事物。 例如，BTS 的《Dynamite》在 2020 年登上 Billboard Hot 100 榜首，而 Netflix 則把 《魷魚遊戲：第一季》列為按觀看量計算最受歡迎的非英語電視節目。 簡單來說，螢幕已經成為一張通行證。 一旦接觸變得容易，好奇心便可以迅速轉化為忠誠支持。"},{"label":"Paragraph 5","english":"Second, Asian stars appeal to Western audiences because they offer something both fresh and emotionally universal. What makes many of them memorable is not that they copy Western styles, but that they combine local cultural identity with feelings everyone can recognise. K-pop is known for disciplined choreography, sharp styling and carefully built group chemistry. Korean films often mix humour, suspense and social criticism in unpredictable ways. Japanese animation can turn food, silence or childhood memory into something poetic. Take Parasite, for example: it is deeply Korean in its setting, yet its story about class inequality, family pressure and moral compromise can be understood anywhere; it became the first non-English-language film to win the Oscar for Best Picture. Asian celebrities also often train for years, thereby producing performances that look effortless but are anything but casual. Western viewers may first be attracted by the novelty, but they stay for the craft. In other words, the appeal lies not in exotic decoration, but in storytelling with heart, precision and personality.","chinese":"第二，亞洲明星吸引西方觀眾，是因為他們提供的東西既新鮮，又在情感上具有普遍共鳴。 令其中許多人令人難忘的地方，並不在於他們模仿西方風格，重點在於他們把本土文化身份與人人都能理解的情感結合起來。 K-pop 以嚴整的編舞、鮮明俐落的造型，以及精心建立的團隊默契見稱。 韓國電影經常以難以預料的方式，把幽默、懸疑和社會批判混合起來。 日本動畫能夠把食物、沉默或童年記憶，化成帶有詩意的東西。 以《上流寄生族》為例：它的背景深深植根於韓國，但它關於階級不平等、家庭壓力和道德妥協的故事，卻能在任何地方被理解；它更成為首部贏得奧斯卡最佳電影獎的非英語電影。 亞洲藝人也經常接受多年訓練，從而呈現出看似毫不費力、實際上絕非隨意的表演。 西方觀眾最初也許會被新鮮感吸引，但真正令他們留下來的，是當中的技藝 換句話說，其吸引力的重點不在異國情調的裝飾，重點在於有溫度、有精準度、有個性的敘事。"},{"label":"Paragraph 6","english":"Third, the rise of Asian stars reflects changing attitudes in Western societies themselves. Many Western countries are now more multicultural than before, with Asian communities contributing to schools, workplaces, food, fashion and popular culture. For young people whose families come from Asia, seeing Asian actors and singers succeed internationally can be more than entertainment; it can be a quiet form of recognition. For non-Asian viewers, meanwhile, these stars provide a chance to see the world through different eyes. Michelle Yeoh’s Oscar win for Everything Everywhere All at Once mattered not only because she gave a superb performance, but also because it challenged the old belief that Asian women must remain side characters in global cinema. Representation, however, is not only about fairness. It also makes entertainment richer. With more cultures come more stories, more emotions and more images to remember. Slowly but surely, Asian stars are becoming part of the shared imagination of global youth.","chinese":"第三，亞洲明星的崛起反映了西方社會本身正在改變的態度。 許多西方國家如今比以往更加多元文化，而亞洲社群也在學校、職場、飲食、時尚和流行文化中作出貢獻。 對於家庭來自亞洲的年輕人而言，看見亞洲演員和歌手在國際上取得成功，可以不只是娛樂；它也可以是一種安靜的認可。 與此同時，對非亞洲觀眾來說，這些明星提供了一個透過不同眼光看世界的機會。 楊紫瓊憑《奇異女俠玩救宇宙》奪得奧斯卡獎，其意義重大，不僅因為她交出了一場出色的演出，也因為這挑戰了亞洲女性必須在全球電影中停留於配角位置的舊有觀念。 然而，代表性不僅關乎公平。 它也令娛樂變得更加豐富。 隨著更多文化出現，更多故事、更多情感，以及更多令人記得的畫面也會隨之而來。 緩慢卻穩定地，亞洲明星正在成為全球年輕人共同想像的一部分。"},{"label":"Paragraph 7","english":"All things considered, the growing popularity of Asian singers and movie stars in Western countries is not a passing accident. It is the result of easier access, stronger cross-cultural storytelling and a wider desire to see different lives represented on screen and on stage. Schools, media organisations and audiences should therefore treat this trend as an opportunity rather than a surprise. Students should explore films and songs beyond their usual languages; critics should judge Asian works by their quality rather than by their origin; and fans should support artists without reducing them to stereotypes. The world of entertainment is changing, and there is every reason to believe that Asian stars will continue to shine—not as guests in Western culture, but as creators of global culture.","chinese":"總括而言，亞洲歌手和電影明星在西方國家日益受歡迎，非一場短暫的偶然 這是更容易的接觸渠道、更有力量的跨文化敘事，以及人們更渴望在銀幕與舞台上看見不同人生被呈現所帶來的結果。 因此，學校、媒體機構和觀眾都應該把這個趨勢視為機會，而非驚訝之事。 學生應該探索平日常用語言以外的電影和歌曲；評論者應該根據亞洲作品的質素評價它們，而非根據其出身地；粉絲也應該支持藝術家，不應把他們簡化成刻板印象。 娛樂世界正在改變，而我們完全有理由相信，亞洲明星將繼續發光發亮—— 他們在西方文化中不再只是客人，更會成為全球文化的創造者。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"local screens","chinese":"本地螢幕"},{"english":"global stages","chinese":"全球舞台"},{"english":"win Western hearts","chinese":"贏得西方觀眾的心"},{"english":"in recent years","chinese":"近年"},{"english":"it has become normal for","chinese":"……已變得平常"},{"english":"hum a Korean chorus","chinese":"哼唱韓文副歌"},{"english":"Korean chorus","chinese":"韓文副歌"},{"english":"Japanese animation","chinese":"日本動畫"},{"english":"quote a line from","chinese":"引用……的一句對白"},{"english":"Korean drama","chinese":"韓劇"},{"english":"cultural shift","chinese":"文化轉變"},{"english":"Western audiences","chinese":"西方觀眾"},{"english":"reconsider","chinese":"重新思考"},{"english":"mainstream entertainment","chinese":"主流娛樂"},{"english":"no longer controlled only by","chinese":"不再只由……控制"},{"english":"Hollywood studios","chinese":"荷里活片廠"},{"english":"English-language radio stations","chinese":"英語電台"},{"english":"fresher voices","chinese":"更新鮮的聲音"},{"english":"stronger stories","chinese":"更有力的故事"},{"english":"adventurous performances","chinese":"更具冒險精神的演出"},{"english":"turn to","chinese":"轉向"},{"english":"movie stars","chinese":"電影明星"},{"english":"popularity in Western countries","chinese":"在西方國家的受歡迎程度"},{"english":"be driven by","chinese":"由……推動"},{"english":"digital access","chinese":"數碼接觸渠道"},{"english":"artistic distinctiveness","chinese":"藝術特色"},{"english":"a new hunger for representation","chinese":"對代表性的新增渴求"},{"english":"gain attention","chinese":"獲得關注"},{"english":"removed barriers","chinese":"消除障礙"},{"english":"barriers between cultures","chinese":"文化之間的障礙"},{"english":"Gone are the days when","chinese":"……的日子已經過去"},{"english":"local cinema","chinese":"本地戲院"},{"english":"played on Western radio","chinese":"在西方電台播放"},{"english":"become popular","chinese":"變得受歡迎"},{"english":"discover a Thai actor","chinese":"發現一位泰國演員"},{"english":"through a short clip","chinese":"透過短片"},{"english":"learn the lyrics of","chinese":"學會……的歌詞"},{"english":"through subtitles","chinese":"透過字幕"},{"english":"share a Japanese trailer","chinese":"分享日本電影預告片"},{"english":"within seconds","chinese":"在數秒之內"},{"english":"algorithms recommend","chinese":"演算法推薦"},{"english":"such content","chinese":"這類內容"},{"english":"Asian faces","chinese":"亞洲面孔"},{"english":"become familiar","chinese":"變得熟悉"},{"english":"this matters because","chinese":"這很重要，因為"},{"english":"rarely","chinese":"很少"},{"english":"what they never meet","chinese":"從未接觸過的事物"},{"english":"for instance","chinese":"例如"},{"english":"topped the Billboard Hot 100","chinese":"登上 Billboard Hot 100 榜首"},{"english":"Billboard Hot 100","chinese":"Billboard 百大單曲榜"},{"english":"Netflix lists","chinese":"Netflix 列出"},{"english":"Squid Game: Season 1","chinese":"《魷魚遊戲》第一季"},{"english":"non-English TV show","chinese":"非英語電視節目"},{"english":"by views","chinese":"按觀看次數計"},{"english":"put simply","chinese":"簡單來說"},{"english":"the screen has become a passport","chinese":"螢幕成了通往其他文化的通行證"},{"english":"once access becomes easy","chinese":"一旦接觸變得容易"},{"english":"curiosity can become loyalty","chinese":"好奇可以變成忠誠支持"},{"english":"appeal to","chinese":"吸引"},{"english":"emotionally universal","chinese":"情感上具有普世性"},{"english":"what makes someone memorable","chinese":"令某人難忘的原因"},{"english":"copy Western styles","chinese":"模仿西方風格"},{"english":"combine local cultural identity with","chinese":"把本地文化身份與……結合"},{"english":"local cultural identity","chinese":"本地文化身份"},{"english":"feelings everyone can recognise","chinese":"人人都能理解的感受"},{"english":"K-pop","chinese":"韓國流行音樂"},{"english":"be known for","chinese":"以……聞名"},{"english":"disciplined choreography","chinese":"嚴謹的舞蹈編排"},{"english":"sharp styling","chinese":"鮮明利落的造型"},{"english":"carefully built group chemistry","chinese":"精心建立的團隊默契"},{"english":"group chemistry","chinese":"團隊默契"},{"english":"Korean films","chinese":"韓國電影"},{"english":"mix humour, suspense and social criticism","chinese":"融合幽默、懸疑和社會批判"},{"english":"suspense","chinese":"懸疑"},{"english":"social criticism","chinese":"社會批判"},{"english":"in unpredictable ways","chinese":"以難以預料的方式"},{"english":"turn something into something poetic","chinese":"把……化成詩意的事物"},{"english":"childhood memory","chinese":"童年回憶"},{"english":"take Parasite, for example","chinese":"以《上流寄生族》為例"},{"english":"deeply Korean in its setting","chinese":"場景設定深具韓國特色"},{"english":"setting","chinese":"背景設定"},{"english":"class inequality","chinese":"階級不平等"},{"english":"family pressure","chinese":"家庭壓力"},{"english":"moral compromise","chinese":"道德妥協"},{"english":"be understood anywhere","chinese":"在任何地方都能被理解"},{"english":"non-English-language film","chinese":"非英語電影"},{"english":"win the Oscar for Best Picture","chinese":"贏得奧斯卡最佳電影獎"},{"english":"Oscar for Best Picture","chinese":"奧斯卡最佳電影獎"},{"english":"train for years","chinese":"訓練多年"},{"english":"thereby producing","chinese":"從而產生"},{"english":"look effortless","chinese":"看起來毫不費力"},{"english":"anything but casual","chinese":"絕非隨意"},{"english":"be attracted by","chinese":"被……吸引"},{"english":"novelty","chinese":"新鮮感"},{"english":"stay for the craft","chinese":"因技藝而留下"},{"english":"the craft","chinese":"技藝；手藝"},{"english":"in other words","chinese":"換句話說"},{"english":"the appeal lies in","chinese":"吸引力在於"},{"english":"exotic decoration","chinese":"異國情調的裝飾"},{"english":"storytelling with heart","chinese":"有真情的故事敘述"},{"english":"precision and personality","chinese":"精準和個性"},{"english":"the rise of","chinese":"……的崛起"},{"english":"reflects changing attitudes","chinese":"反映態度轉變"},{"english":"Western societies","chinese":"西方社會"},{"english":"multicultural","chinese":"多元文化的"},{"english":"Asian communities","chinese":"亞洲社群"},{"english":"contributing to","chinese":"為……作出貢獻"},{"english":"workplaces","chinese":"工作場所"},{"english":"popular culture","chinese":"流行文化"},{"english":"for young people whose families come from Asia","chinese":"對於家庭來自亞洲的年輕人來說"},{"english":"seeing someone succeed internationally","chinese":"看見某人在國際上成功"},{"english":"more than entertainment","chinese":"不只是娛樂"},{"english":"a quiet form of recognition","chinese":"一種默默的認同"},{"english":"non-Asian viewers","chinese":"非亞洲觀眾"},{"english":"meanwhile","chinese":"同時；另一方面"},{"english":"provide a chance to","chinese":"提供機會去"},{"english":"see the world through different eyes","chinese":"以不同眼光看世界"},{"english":"Michelle Yeoh's Oscar win","chinese":"楊紫瓊奧斯卡獲獎"},{"english":"superb performance","chinese":"出色演出"},{"english":"challenged the old belief","chinese":"挑戰舊有觀念"},{"english":"old belief","chinese":"舊有觀念"},{"english":"remain side characters","chinese":"一直做配角"},{"english":"global cinema","chinese":"全球電影"},{"english":"representation","chinese":"代表性；呈現"},{"english":"not only about fairness","chinese":"不只是關乎公平"},{"english":"makes entertainment richer","chinese":"令娛樂內容更豐富"},{"english":"with more cultures come more stories","chinese":"文化越多，故事也越多"},{"english":"images to remember","chinese":"令人記住的畫面"},{"english":"slowly but surely","chinese":"慢慢但確定地"},{"english":"shared imagination","chinese":"共同想像"},{"english":"global youth","chinese":"全球青年"},{"english":"all things considered","chinese":"綜合而言"},{"english":"growing popularity","chinese":"日益增長的受歡迎程度"},{"english":"not a passing trend","chinese":"不是短暫潮流"},{"english":"the result of","chinese":"……的結果"},{"english":"easier access","chinese":"更容易接觸"},{"english":"cross-cultural storytelling","chinese":"跨文化故事敘述"},{"english":"wider desire to","chinese":"更廣泛希望去"},{"english":"different lives represented","chinese":"不同人生被呈現"},{"english":"on screen and on stage","chinese":"在螢幕上和舞台上"},{"english":"media organisations","chinese":"傳媒機構"},{"english":"treat this trend as","chinese":"把這股潮流視為"},{"english":"an opportunity rather than a surprise","chinese":"一個機會，而不是驚訝"},{"english":"beyond their usual languages","chinese":"超越自己平日使用的語言"},{"english":"critics","chinese":"評論家"},{"english":"judge something by","chinese":"按……評價"},{"english":"by their quality rather than by their origin","chinese":"按質素而非出身地評價"},{"english":"support artists","chinese":"支持藝人"},{"english":"without reducing them to stereotypes","chinese":"不把他們簡化為刻板印象"},{"english":"stereotypes","chinese":"刻板印象"},{"english":"the world of entertainment","chinese":"娛樂世界"},{"english":"there is every reason to believe that","chinese":"完全有理由相信"},{"english":"continue to shine","chinese":"繼續發光發亮"},{"english":"not as guests in Western culture","chinese":"不是作為西方文化中的客人"},{"english":"creators of global culture","chinese":"全球文化的創造者"}]},"dse-writing-2013-part-b-q8":{"exerciseId":"dse-writing-2013-part-b-q8","essayKey":"","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=dse-writing-2013-part-b-q8","flashDeckId":"dse/writing/part-b/2013/Q8","paragraphs":[{"label":"Paragraph 1","english":"Before the Song Ends","chinese":"歌聲結束之前"},{"label":"Paragraph 2","english":"Good morning Principal, teachers, parents, and, above all, my fellow graduates,","chinese":"校長、各位老師、各位家長，最重要的是各位畢業同學，大家早上好："},{"label":"Paragraph 3","english":"A popular song tells us that “Time waits for no one.” It also gives us two unforgettable images: time can reduce even solid buildings to ruins, and our hours are as precious as jewels. At first, these may sound like gloomy lines from a sad song. Yet standing here today, wearing the uniform of a student for perhaps one of the last times, I hear something wiser. The song is not asking us to fear time. Instead, it is asking us to respect it. As President of the Students’ Union, I have watched us count down to examinations, celebrations and today’s ceremony. Now this moment has made us, the graduating class, consider how we should use the years ahead, so that we do not merely grow older, but grow deeper, kinder and braver. My fellow graduates, do not wait for life to begin; spend your time as if every hour matters, because it does.","chinese":"一首流行歌曲告訴我們：「時間不等人。」 它也給了我們兩個令人難忘的畫面：時間甚至能把堅固的建築物化為廢墟，而我們的光陰也像珠寶一樣珍貴。 乍聽之下，這些歌詞也許像一首悲傷歌曲中陰鬱的句子。 然而，今天站在這裡，也許是最後幾次穿上學生制服的時刻之一，我聽見了更深的智慧。 這首歌並沒有要求我們害怕時間。 相反，它要求我們尊重時間。 作為學生會會長，我看著我們一路倒數考試、慶祝活動，以及今天這場典禮 此刻讓我們這一屆畢業生思考，未來的歲月應該如何運用，好讓我們不只年歲漸長，更能變得更有深度、更仁厚、更勇敢。 各位畢業同學，不要等待人生開始；請像每一小時都至關重要那樣運用時間，因為它確實如此。"},{"label":"Paragraph 4","english":"First, let time humble us. When we entered this school, graduation seemed impossibly far away. One moment, we were asking seniors where the hall was; the next, younger students were calling us seniors. Between those two moments came thousands of ordinary scenes - rushing to morning assembly, laughing in the canteen, staring helplessly at past papers, whispering encouragement before a competition. None of those days felt historic while we were living them. Nevertheless, together they became our youth. If time can tear down a building, it can certainly erase our excuses, our laziness and our illusion that “later” is a safe place to store our dreams. Not until today do we fully realise that the small habits we repeated were quietly writing our character. Therefore, let us leave with humility - we are not masters of time, but we can be faithful stewards of it.","chinese":"首先，讓時間教會我們謙卑。 當我們踏進這所學校時，畢業似乎遙不可及。 前一刻，我們還在問師兄師姐禮堂在哪裡；下一刻，低年級同學已經稱我們為師兄師姐。 在這兩個時刻之間，是無數平凡片段——趕去早會、在飯堂大笑、無助地盯著歷屆試題、在比賽前低聲為彼此打氣。 我們身處其中時，沒有一天讓人覺得會成為歷史。 然而，這些日子加起來，就成了我們的青春。 如果時間可以摧毀一座建築物，它當然也可以抹去我們的藉口、我們的懶惰，以及我們以為「遲一點」可以安全存放夢想的幻覺。 直到今天我們才完全明白，那些反覆出現的小習慣一直在悄悄書寫我們品格 因此，讓我們帶著謙卑離開——我們並非時間的主人，卻可以成為它忠實的守護者。"},{"label":"Paragraph 5","english":"Second, let time teach us gratitude. A diamond is valuable not because it is large, but because it is rare. The same is true of an afternoon with a friend, a teacher’s patient advice after school, or a family dinner waiting at home while we complained about stress. Many of us have spent the past years chasing results, and rightly so; public examinations matter. Granted, grades may open doors. However, it is people who give those doors meaning. What use is a bright future if we enter it alone, carrying regret like an unpaid debt? Before we scatter to universities, workplaces and new cities, say what should be said. Thank the teacher who believed in you before you believed in yourself. Apologise to the friend you hurt. Tell your parents that their quiet sacrifices were seen. Do it now, not because tomorrow will not come, but because tomorrow may come with distance.","chinese":"第二，讓時間教會我們感恩。 鑽石之所以珍貴，原因不在於體積大，重點在於它稀有。 這道理同樣適用於與朋友共度的一個下午、老師放學後耐心給予的建議，以及在我們抱怨壓力時，家中那頓一直等待我們的晚飯。 過去幾年，我們很多人一直追逐成績；這樣做也有充分理由，因為公開考試確實重要。 誠然，成績或許能打開機會之門。 然而，賦予這些門意義的，是人。 如果我們獨自走進光明的未來，還背著像未還債務一樣的遺憾，那樣的未來又有甚麼用？ 在我們各自走向大學、職場和新的城市之前，把該說的話說出口。 感謝那位在你相信自己以前，已經相信你的老師。 向你曾經傷害的朋友道歉。 告訴父母，他們那些安靜的付出，你都看見了。 現在就去做；並非因為明天不會來臨，只因明天來臨時可能已帶著距離。"},{"label":"Paragraph 6","english":"Finally, let time call us to courage. Some of us are excited; others are terrified. We may wonder whether we are ready for the world beyond these gates. The honest answer is: probably not completely. But who ever is? A journey is not completed by waiting at the starting line. It is completed step by step, mistake by mistake, lesson by lesson. Apply for the course. Join the team. Learn the skill. Serve the community. Ask for help when pride tells you to pretend. Even if failure comes, let it make you wiser rather than smaller. The more we postpone our courage, the more fear becomes a habit. The sooner we begin, the sooner our future begins to take shape.","chinese":"最後，讓時間召喚我們拿出勇氣。 有些人興奮；另一些人卻害怕。 我們也許會問，自己是否已準備好走向校門外的世界。 坦白說，答案大概是：還未完全準備好。 但又有誰能完全準備好呢？ 一段旅程不會因我們站在起點等待而完成。 它是一步一步、一次錯誤一次錯誤、一堂課一堂課地完成的。 報讀那個課程。 加入那個團隊。 學會那項技能。 服務社區。 當自尊叫你假裝沒事時，開口求助。 即使失敗來臨，也讓它使你更有智慧，而不要使你變得更渺小。 我們越推遲拿出勇氣，恐懼就越會變成一種習慣。 我們越早開始，未來就越早開始成形。"},{"label":"Paragraph 7","english":"Fellow graduates, today the clock does not stop for us. The song will end. The applause will fade. The chairs in this hall will be cleared away. Yet what we do after this morning can still turn passing time into lasting meaning. Let us protect our hours, honour our people and begin our next chapter with courage. Years from now, may we look back and say not that time slipped away from us, but that we held it carefully, spent it generously and lived it well.","chinese":"各位畢業同學，今天，時鐘不會為我們停下。 歌聲會結束。 掌聲會淡去。 這禮堂裡的椅子將會被收走。 然而，今天早上之後我們所做的事，仍然可以把流逝的時間轉為持久的意義 讓我們珍惜自己的光陰，珍視身邊的人，並以勇氣展開人生下一章。 願多年之後，我們回望今天時，能夠說：時間沒有白白從我們手中溜走；我們曾小心握住它、慷慨地使用它，也好好地活出了它。"},{"label":"Paragraph 8","english":"Thank you, and congratulations to the graduating classes.","chinese":"謝謝大家，並恭喜各位畢業班同學。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"before the song ends","chinese":"在歌曲完結之前"},{"english":"good morning, Principal","chinese":"校長早晨"},{"english":"above all","chinese":"最重要的是"},{"english":"my fellow graduates","chinese":"各位畢業同學"},{"english":"a popular song","chinese":"一首流行歌曲"},{"english":"tells us that","chinese":"告訴我們"},{"english":"time waits for no one","chinese":"時間不等人"},{"english":"unforgettable images","chinese":"難忘的意象"},{"english":"reduce buildings to ruins","chinese":"使建築物化為廢墟"},{"english":"solid buildings","chinese":"堅固的建築物"},{"english":"to ruins","chinese":"成為廢墟"},{"english":"as precious as jewels","chinese":"像珠寶一樣珍貴"},{"english":"at first","chinese":"起初"},{"english":"gloomy lines","chinese":"悲觀陰沉的歌詞"},{"english":"standing here today","chinese":"今天站在這裏"},{"english":"wearing the uniform","chinese":"穿着校服"},{"english":"for perhaps one of the last times","chinese":"也許是最後幾次之一"},{"english":"hear something wiser","chinese":"聽出更有智慧的意思"},{"english":"asking us to fear time","chinese":"要我們害怕時間"},{"english":"asking us to respect it","chinese":"要我們尊重它"},{"english":"President of the Students' Union","chinese":"學生會主席"},{"english":"count down to","chinese":"倒數迎接"},{"english":"today's ceremony","chinese":"今天的典禮"},{"english":"the graduating class","chinese":"畢業班"},{"english":"the years ahead","chinese":"未來的歲月"},{"english":"not merely grow older","chinese":"不只是年紀增長"},{"english":"grow deeper, kinder and braver","chinese":"變得更有深度、更仁慈和更勇敢"},{"english":"do not wait for life to begin","chinese":"不要等待人生開始"},{"english":"spend your time as if","chinese":"像……般運用時間"},{"english":"every hour matters","chinese":"每一小時都重要"},{"english":"let time humble us","chinese":"讓時間使我們謙卑"},{"english":"enter this school","chinese":"進入這所學校"},{"english":"impossibly far away","chinese":"遙不可及"},{"english":"one moment…, the next…","chinese":"前一刻……下一刻……"},{"english":"asking seniors","chinese":"向師兄師姐詢問"},{"english":"calling us seniors","chinese":"稱我們為師兄師姐"},{"english":"between those two moments","chinese":"在那兩個時刻之間"},{"english":"ordinary scenes","chinese":"平凡場景"},{"english":"morning assembly","chinese":"早會"},{"english":"in the canteen","chinese":"在飯堂"},{"english":"stare helplessly at","chinese":"無助地盯着"},{"english":"past papers","chinese":"歷屆試題"},{"english":"whisper encouragement","chinese":"低聲鼓勵"},{"english":"before a competition","chinese":"比賽前"},{"english":"feel historic","chinese":"感覺具歷史意義"},{"english":"while we were living them","chinese":"當我們正在經歷它們時"},{"english":"become our youth","chinese":"成為我們的青春"},{"english":"tear down a building","chinese":"拆毀一座建築物"},{"english":"erase our excuses","chinese":"抹去我們的藉口"},{"english":"our laziness","chinese":"我們的懶惰"},{"english":"the illusion that","chinese":"……的錯覺"},{"english":"a safe place to store our dreams","chinese":"存放夢想的安全地方"},{"english":"not until today do we realise","chinese":"直到今天我們才明白"},{"english":"small habits","chinese":"小習慣"},{"english":"quietly writing our character","chinese":"悄悄塑造我們的品格"},{"english":"leave with humility","chinese":"帶着謙卑離開"},{"english":"masters of time","chinese":"時間的主人"},{"english":"faithful stewards of","chinese":"忠誠的管理者"},{"english":"let time teach us gratitude","chinese":"讓時間教會我們感恩"},{"english":"valuable not because…, but because…","chinese":"有價值不是因為……而是因為……"},{"english":"the same is true of","chinese":"……也是如此"},{"english":"an afternoon with a friend","chinese":"與朋友共度的下午"},{"english":"patient advice","chinese":"耐心的建議"},{"english":"after school","chinese":"放學後"},{"english":"family dinner","chinese":"家庭晚飯"},{"english":"complain about stress","chinese":"抱怨壓力"},{"english":"spend years chasing results","chinese":"多年來追逐成績"},{"english":"rightly so","chinese":"這樣做也有道理"},{"english":"public examinations matter","chinese":"公開考試很重要"},{"english":"granted","chinese":"誠然"},{"english":"open doors","chinese":"打開機會之門"},{"english":"give those doors meaning","chinese":"賦予那些機會意義"},{"english":"what use is","chinese":"……有甚麼用"},{"english":"a bright future","chinese":"光明的未來"},{"english":"carrying regret like an unpaid debt","chinese":"帶着像未還債務般的遺憾"},{"english":"unpaid debt","chinese":"未還清的債"},{"english":"scatter to","chinese":"分散到"},{"english":"universities, workplaces and new cities","chinese":"大學、工作場所和新城市"},{"english":"say what should be said","chinese":"說出該說的話"},{"english":"believed in you","chinese":"相信你"},{"english":"before you believed in yourself","chinese":"在你相信自己之前"},{"english":"apologise to","chinese":"向……道歉"},{"english":"the friend you hurt","chinese":"你曾傷害的朋友"},{"english":"quiet sacrifices","chinese":"默默的犧牲"},{"english":"were seen","chinese":"被看見"},{"english":"do it now","chinese":"現在就做"},{"english":"tomorrow may come with distance","chinese":"明天可能伴隨距離而來"},{"english":"let time call us to courage","chinese":"讓時間召喚我們拿出勇氣"},{"english":"some…, others…","chinese":"有些人……另一些人……"},{"english":"terrified","chinese":"非常害怕"},{"english":"the world beyond these gates","chinese":"校門外的世界"},{"english":"the honest answer is","chinese":"誠實的答案是"},{"english":"probably not completely","chinese":"可能還未完全"},{"english":"who ever is","chinese":"又有誰完全準備好呢"},{"english":"a journey is not completed by","chinese":"一段旅程不是靠……完成的"},{"english":"waiting at the starting line","chinese":"在起點線等待"},{"english":"step by step","chinese":"一步一步地"},{"english":"mistake by mistake","chinese":"從一個又一個錯誤中"},{"english":"lesson by lesson","chinese":"從一課又一課中"},{"english":"apply for the course","chinese":"申請課程"},{"english":"join the team","chinese":"加入隊伍"},{"english":"learn the skill","chinese":"學習技能"},{"english":"serve the community","chinese":"服務社區"},{"english":"ask for help","chinese":"求助"},{"english":"pride tells you to pretend","chinese":"自尊叫你假裝沒事"},{"english":"even if failure comes","chinese":"即使失敗來臨"},{"english":"make you wiser rather than smaller","chinese":"令你更有智慧，而不是更渺小"},{"english":"postpone our courage","chinese":"延後拿出勇氣"},{"english":"fear becomes a habit","chinese":"恐懼變成習慣"},{"english":"begin to take shape","chinese":"開始成形"},{"english":"the clock does not stop","chinese":"時鐘不會停下"},{"english":"the applause will fade","chinese":"掌聲會漸漸消散"},{"english":"be cleared away","chinese":"被清走"},{"english":"turn passing time into lasting meaning","chinese":"把流逝的時間化為長久的意義"},{"english":"passing time","chinese":"流逝的時間"},{"english":"lasting meaning","chinese":"長久的意義"},{"english":"protect our hours","chinese":"珍惜我們的時間"},{"english":"honour our people","chinese":"珍重我們身邊的人"},{"english":"begin our next chapter","chinese":"開展人生下一章"},{"english":"with courage","chinese":"帶着勇氣"},{"english":"years from now","chinese":"多年以後"},{"english":"look back","chinese":"回望"},{"english":"time slipped away from us","chinese":"時間從我們手中溜走"},{"english":"held it carefully","chinese":"小心珍惜它"},{"english":"spent it generously","chinese":"慷慨地運用它"},{"english":"lived it well","chinese":"好好地活過"},{"english":"congratulations to","chinese":"恭喜……"},{"english":"graduating classes","chinese":"各畢業班"}]},"dse-writing-2013-part-b-q9":{"exerciseId":"dse-writing-2013-part-b-q9","essayKey":"","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=dse-writing-2013-part-b-q9","flashDeckId":"dse/writing/part-b/2013/Q9","paragraphs":[{"label":"Paragraph 1","english":"When we entered the conservation room, Kelvin was scrubbing his hands although he was wearing gloves. On the table lay reversible black pigment and a cutter with a blade thinner than a fingernail. He smiled too quickly. “Inspector, I was preparing restoration materials. The museum must act fast.” Lam lifted the report. “You signed this yesterday?” “Yes.” “Then you knew the painting’s real condition.” Kelvin blinked. “The words say TRUTH HAS A PRICE,” Lam continued. “The truth is that The Returning Junk was already damaged before last night, wasn’t it?” For once, the room went silent. It turned out that, during a private preview two nights earlier, a sponsor’s child had knocked a display light onto The Returning Junk, scorching one corner. Kelvin had been told to hide the accident until after the overseas loan. Instead of confessing, he staged a larger crime: smear two works, fake a political message, create three minutes of static, and let the public blame “ vandals”. Insurance would pay. The real shame would disappear beneath the invented one. “But you missed the dust,” Lam said. “And the blade was too careful.” Kelvin whispered, “I was trying to save my career.” “No,” I said before I could stop myself. “You were saving your name, not the art.” By evening, the harbour lights returned to the windows. The masterpieces were wounded, but not beyond repair. Kelvin left in handcuffs, small and ordinary in a way that disappointed me. I had expected a monster; instead, I saw a frightened man who had mistaken reputation for truth. Before I went home, Inspector Lam handed me a pair of white gloves. “Keep volunteering,” he said. “Museums need people who notice dust.” I took them as if they were a badge. Outside, the city glittered, flawless. Inside, every masterpiece kept its secrets in the cracks.","chinese":""}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"conservation room","chinese":"文物修復室"},{"english":"scrub his hands","chinese":"用力洗手"},{"english":"wearing gloves","chinese":"戴着手套"},{"english":"reversible black pigment","chinese":"可逆黑色顏料"},{"english":"a cutter with a blade","chinese":"一把有刀片的 刀"},{"english":"thinner than a fingernail","chinese":"比指甲還薄"},{"english":"smiled too quickly","chinese":"笑得太快；笑得不自然"},{"english":"prepare restoration materials","chinese":"準備修復材料"},{"english":"restoration materials","chinese":"修復材料"},{"english":"act fast","chinese":"迅速行動"},{"english":"lifted the report","chinese":"舉起報告"},{"english":"signed this yesterday","chinese":"昨天簽署這份文件"},{"english":"the painting's real condition","chinese":"畫作的真實狀況"},{"english":"blinked","chinese":"眨眼"},{"english":"TRUTH HAS A PRICE","chinese":"真相是有代價的"},{"english":"already damaged","chinese":"已經受損"},{"english":"before last night","chinese":"在昨晚之前"},{"english":"wasn't it?","chinese":"不是嗎？"},{"english":"for once","chinese":"這一次；難得一次"},{"english":"went silent","chinese":"變得沉默"},{"english":"it turned out that","chinese":"原來"},{"english":"private preview","chinese":"私人預展"},{"english":"two nights earlier","chinese":"兩晚前"},{"english":"sponsor's child","chinese":"贊助人的孩子"},{"english":"knock something onto","chinese":"把某物撞到……上"},{"english":"display light","chinese":"展示燈"},{"english":"The Returning Junk","chinese":"《歸來的帆船》"},{"english":"scorch one corner","chinese":"燒焦一角"},{"english":"be told to","chinese":"被告知要……"},{"english":"hide the accident","chinese":"隱瞞意外"},{"english":"until after","chinese":"直到……之後"},{"english":"overseas loan","chinese":"海外借展"},{"english":"instead of confessing","chinese":"沒有承認，反而……"},{"english":"stage a crime","chinese":"製造一宗罪案"},{"english":"a louder crime","chinese":"更轟動的罪案"},{"english":"smear two works","chinese":"塗污兩件作品"},{"english":"fake a political message","chinese":"偽造政治訊息"},{"english":"create three minutes of static","chinese":"製造三分鐘雜訊"},{"english":"let the public blame","chinese":"讓公眾責怪"},{"english":"vandals","chinese":"破壞公物者"},{"english":"insurance would pay","chinese":"保險會賠償"},{"english":"the real shame","chinese":"真正的醜聞"},{"english":"disappear beneath","chinese":"消失在……之下"},{"english":"the invented one","chinese":"虛構出來的那件事"},{"english":"missed the dust","chinese":"忽略了塵埃"},{"english":"too careful","chinese":"過於小心"},{"english":"whispered","chinese":"低聲說"},{"english":"try to save my career","chinese":"試圖保住事業"},{"english":"before I could stop myself","chinese":"我還未能阻止自己便……"},{"english":"save your name","chinese":"保住名聲"},{"english":"not the art","chinese":"而不是藝術品"},{"english":"by evening","chinese":"到了傍晚"},{"english":"harbour lights","chinese":"海港燈光"},{"english":"returned to the windows","chinese":"映回窗上"},{"english":"masterpieces","chinese":"傑作；名作"},{"english":"wounded","chinese":"受創"},{"english":"not beyond repair","chinese":"並非無法修復"},{"english":"left in handcuffs","chinese":"戴着手銬離開"},{"english":"small and ordinary","chinese":"渺小而平凡"},{"english":"in a way that disappointed me","chinese":"以一種令我失望的方式"},{"english":"expected a monster","chinese":"原以為會是個怪物"},{"english":"instead","chinese":"反而"},{"english":"a frightened man","chinese":"一個受驚的人"},{"english":"mistake reputation for truth","chinese":"把名聲誤當成真相"},{"english":"before I went home","chinese":"在我回家之前"},{"english":"handed me","chinese":"遞給我"},{"english":"a pair of white gloves","chinese":"一雙白手套"},{"english":"keep volunteering","chinese":"繼續做義工"},{"english":"people who notice dust","chinese":"會留意塵埃的人"},{"english":"took them as if","chinese":"像……一樣接過它們"},{"english":"a badge","chinese":"徽章；象徵身份的標誌"},{"english":"the city glittered","chinese":"城市閃閃發亮"},{"english":"flawless","chinese":"完美無瑕的"},{"english":"kept its secrets","chinese":"保守它的秘密"},{"english":"in the cracks","chinese":"在裂縫之中"}]},"dse-writing-2014-part-a":{"exerciseId":"dse-writing-2014-part-a","essayKey":"","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=dse-writing-2014-part-a","flashDeckId":"dse/writing/part-a/2014","paragraphs":[{"label":"Title","english":"Lucky Village: Where Tradition Meets Transformation","chinese":"幸運村：傳統與蛻變交匯之地"},{"label":"Background","english":"Located on the outskirts of Hong Kong, Lucky Village was once a peaceful farming community with just a handful of wooden huts and lush rice fields. Forty years ago, residents rose at sunrise to tend their crops and shared simple meals cooked over charcoal stoves. Electricity was scarce, so families often gathered by candlelight and passed down stories that united the community.","chinese":"Lucky Village 位於香港市郊，曾經是一個寧靜的農村社區，只有寥寥幾間木屋和一片片茂盛的稻田。 四十年前，居民日出而作，照料農作物，並分享用炭爐煮成的簡樸飯菜。 當時電力稀少，因此一家人經常在燭光下聚在一起，傳承凝聚社區的故事。"},{"label":"Transformation","english":"Everything changed in 1974, when a massive redevelopment project introduced modern roads, electricity, and piped water. Although many locals initially worried about losing their traditional lifestyle, better infrastructure brought exciting new opportunities. The village school expanded, and small businesses sprang up, allowing families to improve their quality of life and attract visitors from neighboring towns.","chinese":"1974 年，一項大型重建計劃引入了現代化道路、電力和自來水，一切從此改變 雖然許多本地居民最初擔心會失去傳統的生活方式，但更完善的基礎設施帶來了令人振奮的新機遇。 村內學校得以擴建，小型商店也紛紛興起，讓家庭能夠改善生活質素，並吸引來自鄰近城鎮的遊客。"},{"label":"Present Day","english":"Today, Lucky Village is famous for its vibrant Spring Festival, held every April to honor the village’s rich heritage. Thousands of tourists flock here to watch colorful parades, sample homemade pastries, and admire the centuries‐old banyan trees lining the main street. This unique blend of old and new has turned Lucky Village into a captivating destination for anyone seeking a glimpse of Hong Kong’s rural past—while still enjoying modern conveniences. Locals proudly carry on their cherished traditions, ensuring Lucky Village remains true to its name.","chinese":"如今，Lucky Village 以每年四月舉行、充滿活力的春季節慶聞名，藉此紀念村莊豐富的文化傳承。 成千上萬的遊客蜂擁而至，觀看色彩繽紛的巡遊、品嘗自家製糕點，並欣賞排列在大街兩旁、已有數百年歷史的榕樹。 這種新舊交融的獨特特色，令 Lucky Village 成為一個迷人的目的地，適合任何想一窺香港昔日鄉村面貌，同時又享受現代便利的人。 本地居民自豪地延續他們珍視的傳統，確保 Lucky Village 名副其實，繼續成為一個充滿福氣與魅力的地方。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"Where Tradition Meets Transformation","chinese":"傳統與蛻變交匯之地"},{"english":"located on the outskirts of","chinese":"位於……市郊"},{"english":"the outskirts of Hong Kong","chinese":"香港市郊"},{"english":"was once","chinese":"曾經是"},{"english":"a peaceful farming community","chinese":"寧靜的農村社區"},{"english":"a handful of","chinese":"少數；寥寥幾個"},{"english":"wooden huts","chinese":"木屋"},{"english":"lush rice fields","chinese":"茂盛的稻田"},{"english":"forty years ago","chinese":"四十年前"},{"english":"rise at sunrise","chinese":"日出時起床"},{"english":"tend their crops","chinese":"照料農作物"},{"english":"simple meals","chinese":"簡樸的飯菜"},{"english":"cooked over charcoal stoves","chinese":"用炭爐煮成"},{"english":"charcoal stoves","chinese":"炭爐"},{"english":"electricity was scarce","chinese":"電力供應不足"},{"english":"gather by candlelight","chinese":"在燭光下聚集"},{"english":"pass down stories","chinese":"傳承故事"},{"english":"unite the community","chinese":"凝聚社區"},{"english":"Everything changed in","chinese":"一切在……改變"},{"english":"a massive redevelopment project","chinese":"大型重建計劃"},{"english":"introduce modern roads","chinese":"引入現代道路"},{"english":"piped water","chinese":"自來水"},{"english":"many locals","chinese":"很多本地居民"},{"english":"initially worried about","chinese":"起初擔心"},{"english":"lose their traditional lifestyle","chinese":"失去傳統生活方式"},{"english":"better infrastructure","chinese":"更完善的基建"},{"english":"exciting new opportunities","chinese":"令人振奮的新機會"},{"english":"the village school expanded","chinese":"村校擴展"},{"english":"small businesses sprang up","chinese":"小商戶湧現"},{"english":"allow families to","chinese":"讓家庭能夠……"},{"english":"improve their quality of life","chinese":"改善生活質素"},{"english":"attract visitors from","chinese":"吸引來自……的遊客"},{"english":"neighboring towns","chinese":"鄰近城鎮"},{"english":"be famous for","chinese":"以……聞名"},{"english":"vibrant Spring Festival","chinese":"充滿活力的春季節慶"},{"english":"held every April","chinese":"每年四月舉行"},{"english":"honor the village's rich heritage","chinese":"表揚村莊豐富的文化傳承"},{"english":"rich heritage","chinese":"豐富的文化傳承"},{"english":"thousands of tourists","chinese":"數以千計的遊客"},{"english":"flock here","chinese":"蜂擁而至"},{"english":"colorful parades","chinese":"色彩繽紛的巡遊"},{"english":"sample homemade pastries","chinese":"品嘗自家製糕點"},{"english":"homemade pastries","chinese":"自家製糕點"},{"english":"admire the centuries-old banyan trees","chinese":"欣賞百年榕樹"},{"english":"centuries-old banyan trees","chinese":"百年榕樹"},{"english":"lining the main street","chinese":"沿着大街排列"},{"english":"a unique blend of old and new","chinese":"新舊交融的獨特結合"},{"english":"turn something into","chinese":"把……變成"},{"english":"a captivating destination","chinese":"迷人的旅遊目的地"},{"english":"anyone seeking","chinese":"任何尋找……的人"},{"english":"a glimpse of","chinese":"一瞥；短暫感受"},{"english":"Hong Kong's rural past","chinese":"香港昔日鄉郊面貌"},{"english":"while still enjoying","chinese":"同時仍然享受"},{"english":"modern conveniences","chinese":"現代化便利設施"},{"english":"proudly carry on","chinese":"自豪地延續"},{"english":"cherished traditions","chinese":"珍而重之的傳統"},{"english":"ensure something remains","chinese":"確保……保持"},{"english":"remain true to its name","chinese":"名副其實"}]},"dse-writing-2014-part-b-q2":{"exerciseId":"dse-writing-2014-part-b-q2","essayKey":"","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=dse-writing-2014-part-b-q2","flashDeckId":"dse/writing/part-b/2014/Q2","paragraphs":[{"label":"Paragraph 1","english":"Giving Old Equipment a Second Life - Request for Donation of Old Fitness Equipment","chinese":"讓舊器材重獲新生命 申請捐贈舊健身器材"},{"label":"Paragraph 2","english":"Dear Manager,","chinese":"敬啟者："},{"label":"Paragraph 3","english":"I am writing on behalf of the Sports Club of Evergreen Secondary School. We understand that your fitness centre is being renovated and that some of your existing equipment may soon be replaced. While renovation usually means clearing space for something newer, it can also create an opportunity to give useful resources a second life. Therefore, I would be grateful if your centre could consider donating any safe, serviceable equipment to our school, so that we may build a purposeful fitness corner for students. Such a donation would not merely improve our sports facilities; it would also allow your centre to demonstrate community leadership, environmental responsibility and care for young people in the district.","chinese":"本人謹代表 Evergreen Secondary School 體育學會致函。 我們得知貴健身中心現正進行翻新，而部分現有器材可能即將被更換。 雖然翻新通常意味著騰出空間迎接更新的事物，但它同時也可以創造一個機會，讓有用的資源重獲新生命。 因此，若貴中心能考慮將任何安全且仍可正常使用的器材捐贈予本校，讓我們為學生建立一個具明確用途的健身角，本人將不勝感激。 這項捐贈不只會改善本校的體育設施；它也能讓貴中心展現社區領導力、環境責任感，以及對區內年輕人的關懷。 體育學會"},{"label":"Paragraph 4","english":"To begin with, the donation would make regular exercise more accessible to students who need it most. At present, our school hall and playground are heavily used, and students who are not members of school teams often find themselves with nowhere suitable to train after class. A few exercise bikes, yoga mats, resistance bands, benches or light dumbbells would immediately change that. Instead of treating fitness as something available only to students who can afford private gyms, we could open supervised lunchtime and after-school sessions for beginners, examination classes and students recovering from minor injuries. More importantly, proper equipment would make training safer and more systematic. Our senior Sports Club members, guided by Physical Education teachers, could teach juniors how to warm up, stretch, record progress and use equipment responsibly. In this way, your old machines would not sit forgotten in a storeroom; they would help students build discipline, confidence and healthier routines.","chinese":"首先，這項捐贈會讓最需要運動的學生更容易定期鍛鍊。 目前，本校禮堂和操場使用率很高，而並非校隊成員的學生，課後往往發現自己沒有合適的地方進行訓練。 幾部健身單車、瑜伽墊、阻力帶、長凳或輕量啞鈴，便能立即改變這種情況 相比把健身視為只有負擔得起私人健身室的學生才能享有的東西，我們可以開設有監督的午膳和課後時段，讓初學者、應考班學生，以及正從輕微傷患中恢復的學生使用。 更重要的是，合適的器材會使訓練更安全，也更有系統。 在體育老師的指導下，本會高年級成員可以教導低年級學生如何熱身、伸展、記錄進度，並負責任地使用器材。 透過這種方式，貴中心的舊器材將不會被遺忘在儲物室內；它們會幫助學生建立紀律、自信和更健康的生活習慣。 體育學會"},{"label":"Paragraph 5","english":"The donation would also enrich the wider school community. Sport is also about learning how to look after oneself and one another. With donated equipment, we could organise a “Healthy Start” programme before school, a stress-relief fitness session during examinations, and basic strength-training workshops. Take an exercise bike, for example. In a commercial gym, an older bike may seem modest beside the latest model; in our school, however, it could become the first machine a shy Form One student uses to discover that exercise is not embarrassing but empowering. Even ordinary equipment—such as mats, skipping ropes and medicine balls—could support warm-ups for athletics, conditioning for basketball players and rehabilitation exercises for students advised to avoid high-impact sports. The more chances students have to move safely, the more likely they are to see exercise as a habit rather than a punishment.","chinese":"這項捐贈也會豐富整個學校社群。 運動也關乎學習如何照顧自己和彼此。 有了捐贈器材後，我們可以在上課前舉辦「健康開始」計劃、在考試期間安排減壓健身活動，以及開設基礎肌力訓練工作坊。 以一部健身單車為例。 在商業健身室裡，一部較舊的單車放在最新型號旁邊，也許顯得平凡；然而在本校，它卻可能成為一位害羞的中一學生第一次使用的健身器材，讓他發現運動並不尷尬，反而能令人更有力量。 即使是普通器材，例如墊子、跳繩和藥球，也可以支援田徑熱身、籃球員體能訓練，以及被建議避免高衝擊運動的學生進行復康練習。 學生安全活動身體的機會越多，他們便越有可能把運動視為一種習慣，而非一種懲罰。"},{"label":"Paragraph 6","english":"Your fitness centre, too, would benefit meaningfully from this act of generosity. First, it would strengthen your reputation as a responsible local business. We would acknowledge your donation on our school noticeboard, in our newsletter and at our annual Sports Day. With your permission, we would also place a small thank-you sign near the fitness corner. Parents, teachers and students would see not only a fitness brand, but a neighbour willing to invest in the well-being of the next generation. Secondly, the donation would reduce unnecessary waste. Instead of sending usable equipment away during renovation, your centre could show that improvement does not have to come at the cost of sustainability. One person’s surplus can become another community’s resource. By choosing donation over disposal, your centre would turn a practical renovation decision into a public example of social responsibility.","chinese":"貴健身中心也會從這項慷慨之舉中獲得實質而有意義的好處。 首先，這會加強貴中心作為負責任本地企業的聲譽。 我們會在學校告示板、校內通訊以及周年運動會上鳴謝貴中心的捐贈。 在獲得貴中心同意後，我們也會在健身角附近放置一個小型致謝牌。 家長、老師和學生看到的將不只是一個健身品牌，也是一位願意投資於下一代福祉的社區鄰里。 其次，這項捐贈會減少不必要的浪費。 貴中心無須在翻新期間把仍可使用的器材送走，而可以藉此展示：進步並不一定要以可持續性作為代價。 一個人的盈餘，可以成為另一個社群的資源。 透過選擇捐贈而非棄置，貴中心可以把一個實際的翻新決定，轉化為社會責任的公開示範。"},{"label":"Paragraph 7","english":"For safety reasons, we would only accept equipment that your staff consider suitable for continued use. Our school is prepared to arrange collection at a time convenient to you, and our teachers will inspect and supervise the equipment carefully before students use it. If you wish, we would be delighted to visit your centre in person to discuss which items may be available.","chinese":"基於安全理由，我們只會接收貴中心職員認為適合繼續使用的器材。 本校願意在貴中心方便的時間安排收取器材，而本校老師也會在學生使用前仔細檢查並監督有關器材。 如貴中心願意，我們很樂意親身到訪貴中心，商討哪些物品可以捐出。"},{"label":"Paragraph 8","english":"Thank you for considering our request. I sincerely hope your renovation will be a great success, and I would be grateful if you could let us know whether a donation is possible. We would be proud to build a lasting partnership with your centre—one that helps our students stand taller, train wiser and live healthier lives.","chinese":"感謝貴中心考慮我們的請求。 本人衷心祝願貴中心翻新工程圓滿成功；若貴中心能告知我們捐贈是否可行，本人將十分感激。 我們將十分榮幸能與貴中心建立長久的合作關係——這段關係將幫助本校學生更有自信地挺立、更明智地訓練，並活出更健康的人生。"},{"label":"Paragraph 9","english":"Yours faithfully,","chinese":"此致敬禮"},{"label":"Paragraph 10","english":"Chris Wong","chinese":"Chris Wong"},{"label":"Paragraph 11","english":"Chairperson","chinese":"主席"},{"label":"Paragraph 12","english":"Sports Club","chinese":"本人謹代表 Evergreen Secondary School 體育學會致函。 在體育老師的指導下，本會高年級成員可以教導低年級學生如何熱身、伸展、記錄進度，並負責任地使用器材。 體育學會"},{"label":"Paragraph 13","english":"Evergreen Secondary School","chinese":"本人謹代表 Evergreen Secondary School 體育學會致函。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"give old equipment a second life","chinese":"讓舊設備重獲新生"},{"english":"Dear Manager","chinese":"經理鈞鑒"},{"english":"request for donation","chinese":"捐贈請求"},{"english":"old fitness equipment","chinese":"舊健身設備"},{"english":"write on behalf of","chinese":"代表……寫信"},{"english":"Sports Club","chinese":"體育學會"},{"english":"understand that","chinese":"得悉"},{"english":"fitness centre","chinese":"健身中心"},{"english":"be renovated","chinese":"正在翻新"},{"english":"existing equipment","chinese":"現有設備"},{"english":"be replaced","chinese":"被更換"},{"english":"clearing space for","chinese":"騰出空間給"},{"english":"create an opportunity to","chinese":"創造機會去"},{"english":"useful resources","chinese":"有用資源"},{"english":"a second life","chinese":"第二生命；重新使用的機會"},{"english":"I would be grateful if","chinese":"如能……，我將不勝感激"},{"english":"consider donating","chinese":"考慮捐贈"},{"english":"safe, serviceable equipment","chinese":"安全而仍可使用的設備"},{"english":"build a purposeful fitness corner","chinese":"建立有明確用途的健身角"},{"english":"such a donation","chinese":"這樣的捐贈"},{"english":"not merely","chinese":"不只是"},{"english":"improve our sports facilities","chinese":"改善我們的體育設施"},{"english":"allow your centre to demonstrate","chinese":"讓貴中心展示"},{"english":"community leadership","chinese":"社區領導作用"},{"english":"environmental responsibility","chinese":"環保責任"},{"english":"care for young people","chinese":"關心年輕人"},{"english":"in the district","chinese":"在區內"},{"english":"to begin with","chinese":"首先"},{"english":"make regular exercise more accessible","chinese":"令恆常運動更容易接觸"},{"english":"students who need it most","chinese":"最需要它的學生"},{"english":"at present","chinese":"目前"},{"english":"school hall and playground","chinese":"禮堂和操場"},{"english":"heavily used","chinese":"使用率很高"},{"english":"school teams","chinese":"校隊"},{"english":"find themselves with nowhere suitable to train","chinese":"發現自己沒有合適地方訓練"},{"english":"after class","chinese":"課後"},{"english":"exercise bikes","chinese":"健身單車"},{"english":"yoga mats","chinese":"瑜伽墊"},{"english":"resistance bands","chinese":"阻力帶"},{"english":"benches","chinese":"健身椅；長凳"},{"english":"light dumbbells","chinese":"輕量啞鈴"},{"english":"immediately change that","chinese":"立即改變這種情況"},{"english":"instead of treating fitness as","chinese":"而不是把健身視為"},{"english":"available only to","chinese":"只提供給"},{"english":"afford private gyms","chinese":"負擔得起私人健身室"},{"english":"open supervised sessions","chinese":"開設有監督的活動時段"},{"english":"lunchtime sessions","chinese":"午膳時間活動"},{"english":"after-school sessions","chinese":"課後活動"},{"english":"students preparing for examinations","chinese":"準備考試的學生"},{"english":"recover from minor injuries","chinese":"從輕傷中康復"},{"english":"more importantly","chinese":"更重要的是"},{"english":"proper equipment","chinese":"合適設備"},{"english":"safer and more systematic","chinese":"更安全和更有系統"},{"english":"senior Sports Club members","chinese":"體育學會高年級成員"},{"english":"guided by Physical Education teachers","chinese":"由體育老師指導"},{"english":"Physical Education teachers","chinese":"體育老師"},{"english":"teach juniors how to","chinese":"教導低年級學生如何"},{"english":"warm up","chinese":"熱身"},{"english":"stretch","chinese":"拉筋"},{"english":"record progress","chinese":"記錄進度"},{"english":"use equipment responsibly","chinese":"負責任地使用設備"},{"english":"in this way","chinese":"這樣一來"},{"english":"sit forgotten in a storeroom","chinese":"被遺忘在儲物室"},{"english":"help students build discipline","chinese":"幫助學生建立紀律"},{"english":"healthier routines","chinese":"更健康的日常習慣"},{"english":"enrich the wider school community","chinese":"豐富整個學校群體"},{"english":"look after oneself and one another","chinese":"照顧自己和彼此"},{"english":"donated equipment","chinese":"捐贈設備"},{"english":"organise a programme","chinese":"舉辦計劃"},{"english":"Healthy Start programme","chinese":"健康起步計劃"},{"english":"stress-relief fitness session","chinese":"減壓健身活動"},{"english":"during examinations","chinese":"考試期間"},{"english":"basic strength-training workshops","chinese":"基礎肌力訓練工作坊"},{"english":"take…, for example","chinese":"以……為例"},{"english":"commercial gym","chinese":"商業健身室"},{"english":"seem modest beside","chinese":"在……旁邊顯得普通"},{"english":"the latest model","chinese":"最新型號"},{"english":"in our school, however","chinese":"然而，在我們學校"},{"english":"a shy Form One student","chinese":"害羞的中一學生"},{"english":"not embarrassing but empowering","chinese":"不是尷尬，而是令人有力量"},{"english":"ordinary equipment","chinese":"普通設備"},{"english":"skipping ropes","chinese":"跳繩"},{"english":"medicine balls","chinese":"藥球"},{"english":"support warm-ups","chinese":"支援熱身"},{"english":"athletics","chinese":"田徑"},{"english":"conditioning for basketball players","chinese":"籃球員的體能訓練"},{"english":"rehabilitation exercises","chinese":"復康運動"},{"english":"be advised to avoid","chinese":"被建議避免"},{"english":"high-impact sports","chinese":"高撞擊運動"},{"english":"the more…, the more likely…","chinese":"越……，就越有可能……"},{"english":"move safely","chinese":"安全地活動身體"},{"english":"see exercise as a habit rather than a punishment","chinese":"把運動視為習慣，而不是懲罰"},{"english":"benefit meaningfully from","chinese":"從……中有實質得益"},{"english":"act of generosity","chinese":"慷慨之舉"},{"english":"strengthen your reputation","chinese":"提升貴中心聲譽"},{"english":"responsible local business","chinese":"負責任的本地企業"},{"english":"acknowledge your donation","chinese":"鳴謝貴方捐贈"},{"english":"school noticeboard","chinese":"學校告示板"},{"english":"newsletter","chinese":"通訊"},{"english":"annual Sports Day","chinese":"每年一度的陸運會"},{"english":"with your permission","chinese":"如蒙允許"},{"english":"thank-you sign","chinese":"感謝牌"},{"english":"near the fitness corner","chinese":"在健身角附近"},{"english":"not only a fitness brand, but a neighbour","chinese":"不只是一個健身品牌，而是一位鄰里"},{"english":"be willing to invest in","chinese":"願意投放資源於"},{"english":"well-being","chinese":"身心健康"},{"english":"the next generation","chinese":"下一代"},{"english":"reduce unnecessary waste","chinese":"減少不必要的浪費"},{"english":"send usable equipment away","chinese":"把可用設備送走"},{"english":"during renovation","chinese":"在翻新期間"},{"english":"improvement does not have to come at the cost of sustainability","chinese":"改善不必以犧牲可持續性為代價"},{"english":"come at the cost of","chinese":"以……為代價"},{"english":"sustainability","chinese":"可持續發展"},{"english":"surplus","chinese":"多餘物資"},{"english":"another community's resource","chinese":"另一個社群的資源"},{"english":"choose donation over disposal","chinese":"選擇捐贈而不是棄置"},{"english":"disposal","chinese":"棄置"},{"english":"turn…into…","chinese":"把……變成……"},{"english":"a practical renovation decision","chinese":"實際的翻新決定"},{"english":"a public example of social responsibility","chinese":"履行社會責任的公開例子"},{"english":"for safety reasons","chinese":"基於安全理由"},{"english":"only accept equipment that","chinese":"只接受……的設備"},{"english":"suitable for continued use","chinese":"適合繼續使用"},{"english":"be prepared to","chinese":"準備好"},{"english":"arrange collection","chinese":"安排收取"},{"english":"at a time convenient to you","chinese":"在你方便的時間"},{"english":"inspect and supervise","chinese":"檢查並監督"},{"english":"before students use it","chinese":"在學生使用之前"},{"english":"if you wish","chinese":"如你願意"},{"english":"be delighted to","chinese":"很樂意"},{"english":"in person","chinese":"親身"},{"english":"discuss which items may be available","chinese":"商討哪些物品可供捐贈"},{"english":"thank you for considering","chinese":"感謝你考慮"},{"english":"sincerely hope","chinese":"衷心希望"},{"english":"a great success","chinese":"非常成功；圓滿成功"},{"english":"let us know whether","chinese":"告知我們是否"},{"english":"donation is possible","chinese":"可以捐贈"},{"english":"be proud to","chinese":"很榮幸能夠"},{"english":"build a lasting partnership","chinese":"建立長久合作關係"},{"english":"help students stand taller","chinese":"幫助學生更有自信"},{"english":"train more wisely","chinese":"更明智地訓練"},{"english":"live healthier lives","chinese":"過更健康的生活"},{"english":"Yours faithfully","chinese":"此致敬禮"},{"english":"Chairperson","chinese":"主席"},{"english":"Evergreen Secondary School","chinese":"長青中學"}]},"dse-writing-2014-part-b-q3":{"exerciseId":"dse-writing-2014-part-b-q3","essayKey":"","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=dse-writing-2014-part-b-q3","flashDeckId":"dse/writing/part-b/2014/Q3","paragraphs":[{"label":"Paragraph 1","english":"Subject: Restoring the Good Name of Our Drama Club","chinese":"主旨：重建我們戲劇學會的良好名聲"},{"label":"Paragraph 2","english":"To: All Drama Club Members","chinese":"收件人：全體戲劇學會會員"},{"label":"Paragraph 3","english":"From: Chairperson, Drama Club","chinese":"發件人：戲劇學會主席 戲劇學會主席"},{"label":"Paragraph 4","english":"Subject: Complaint from City Hall Concerning Our Conduct","chinese":"主旨：有關大會堂就我們行為提出的投訴"},{"label":"Paragraph 5","english":"Date: 26 March 2018","chinese":""},{"label":"Paragraph 6","english":"Dear Drama Club members,","chinese":"親愛的戲劇學會會員："},{"label":"Paragraph 7","english":"I regret to inform you that our school has received a formal complaint from City Hall about the behaviour of a group of our Drama Club members who attended the drama performance last week. As the chairperson of the Drama Club, I am writing not to embarrass anyone, but to address the matter honestly, to remind all of us of our responsibilities as audience members, and to make clear what we must do to rebuild the trust that has been damaged. The incident has made both our teacher adviser and the school consider introducing clearer rules for future outings so that our club can continue representing the school with maturity, respect and pride.","chinese":"我很遺憾地通知大家，本校收到大會堂的正式投訴，內容涉及本會一批成員上星期觀看戲劇表演時的行為。 身為戲劇學會主席，我寫這封電郵，目的並非令任何人難堪，重點在於坦誠處理這件事、提醒我們每一位成員作為觀眾應負的責任，並清楚說明我們必須怎樣重建已受損的信任。 這件事使我們的指導老師和學校都考慮為日後校外活動引入更清晰的規則，好讓本會能繼續以成熟、尊重和自豪的態度代表學校。"},{"label":"Paragraph 8","english":"According to the complaint, several members disturbed the performance by talking during scenes, laughing at inappropriate moments, using mobile phones and failing to follow the instructions of the venue staff. While it would be unfair to suggest that every member behaved poorly, this does not alter the fact that the complaint reflects badly on the whole Drama Club. When we attend a performance in school uniform, we are no longer watching as private individuals; we are representing our club, our teachers and our school. The audience around us has paid for a meaningful theatre experience, the actors have spent months rehearsing, and the venue staff have worked hard to maintain order. If our members talk, check messages or treat the theatre as if it were a classroom corridor, we interrupt the concentration of the actors, distract other audience members and show little respect for the art form we claim to love. Put simply, drama is not just about performing on stage; it is about understanding how live performance should be respected from the audience’s side as well.","chinese":"根據投訴內容，數名成員在演出期間說話、在不適當的時候大笑、使用手機，並未有遵從場地職員的指示，因而打擾了表演。 雖然若說每位成員都表現欠佳並不公平，但這並不改變一個事實：這宗投訴令整個戲劇學會的形象受損。 當我們穿著校服觀看演出時，我們已不再只是以私人身份觀賞；我們代表的是本會、老師和學校。 我們身邊的觀眾付費，是為了獲得有意義的劇場體驗；演員花了數月排練；場地職員也努力維持秩序。 如果本會成員說話、查看訊息，或把劇場當成課室走廊一樣對待，我們就會干擾演員的專注、分散其他觀眾的注意力，也顯得並不尊重我們自稱熱愛的藝術形式。 簡單來說，戲劇並不只關乎在舞台上表演；它也關乎明白現場演出在觀眾席上同樣應受到尊重。"},{"label":"Paragraph 9","english":"More importantly, this incident should serve as a serious reminder of what membership in the Drama Club means. We often say that drama teaches empathy, discipline and teamwork. However, those values mean very little if they disappear the moment we leave the school campus. A good performer knows when to speak, when to listen and when silence itself carries meaning. By contrast, careless audience behaviour suggests that we appreciate drama only when we are the ones under the spotlight. That is not the kind of club we should become. Consider this: if visiting students behaved noisily during our annual school production, would we not feel disappointed, even hurt? The same standard applies to us. Manners maketh man, and in the theatre, manners also protect the dignity of everyone involved.","chinese":"更重要的是，這件事應該成為一次嚴肅提醒，讓我們重新思考身為戲劇學會成員的意義。 我們經常說，戲劇教會人同理心、紀律和團隊合作。 然而，如果我們一離開校園便把這些價值拋諸腦後，它們便幾乎沒有意義。 一位出色的表演者知道甚麼時候該說話、甚麼時候該聆聽，也知道沉默本身何時帶有意義。 相比之下，粗心大意的觀眾行為會令人覺得，我們只有在自己站在聚光燈下時才欣賞戲劇。 那絕非我們應該成為的學會。 請試想：如果有外校學生在我們學校年度演出期間吵鬧，我們難道不會感到失望，甚至受傷嗎？ 同樣的標準也適用於我們。 禮貌造就人格；在劇場裡，禮貌也維護每一位參與者的尊嚴。"},{"label":"Paragraph 10","english":"With this in mind, the committee will take several immediate steps. First, I will send a written apology to City Hall on behalf of the Drama Club. Members who were directly involved should also come forward and apologise to our teacher adviser by Friday. Second, before our next external activity, all members will attend a short briefing on theatre etiquette, including punctuality, phone use, seating arrangements and how to respond to venue staff. Third, for future performances, at least two committee members will be assigned to each row so that problems can be dealt with quietly before they escalate. This is not meant to police everyone unnecessarily; rather, it is a practical way to ensure that a few irresponsible actions do not put future outings at risk for all members.","chinese":"有鑑於此，委員會將立即採取數項行動。 首先，我會代表戲劇學會向大會堂發出書面道歉。 直接涉事的成員也應主動站出來，並在星期五或之前向我們的指導老師道歉 其次，在下一次校外活動之前，所有成員都將出席一場簡短的劇場禮儀簡介會，內容包括守時、手機使用、座位安排，以及如何回應場地職員。 第三，在日後觀看演出時，每一排座位將至少安排兩名委員負責，好讓問題在惡化之前能夠被安靜地處理。 這項安排的目的並非對所有人作出不必要的監管；更準確地說，這是一個實際的方法，以確保少數不負責任的行為不會令全體成員日後的校外活動受到威脅。"},{"label":"Paragraph 11","english":"I would appreciate it if every member could treat this matter seriously, whether or not you were personally involved. There is no use blaming one another endlessly. What matters now is that we face up to the complaint, learn from it and prove through our future conduct that this incident does not define us. Should you have any concerns, please speak to me or our teacher adviser after school this week.","chinese":"無論你本人是否涉事，我都懇請每一位成員認真看待這件事。 無止境地互相責怪並沒有用。 現在真正重要的，是我們正視這宗投訴、從中學習，並透過日後的行為證明這件事不能定義我們。 如有任何疑慮，請於本星期放學後與我或我們的指導老師聯絡。"},{"label":"Paragraph 12","english":"The Drama Club has built a good reputation through years of hard work, and one unpleasant incident should not be allowed to destroy it. Let us apologise where necessary, behave better from now on, and show that we are mature enough not only to perform drama, but also to honour it.","chinese":"戲劇學會多年來憑著努力建立了良好聲譽，而一件不愉快的事件不應被容許摧毀它。 讓我們在有需要的地方作出道歉，從現在起表現得更好，並展示我們不僅成熟到能夠演出戲劇，也成熟到能夠尊重戲劇。"},{"label":"Paragraph 13","english":"Yours sincerely,","chinese":"謹啟："},{"label":"Paragraph 14","english":"Chris Wong","chinese":"Chris Wong"},{"label":"Paragraph 15","english":"Chairperson, Drama Club","chinese":"發件人：戲劇學會主席 戲劇學會主席"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"restore the good name of","chinese":"挽回……的良好名聲"},{"english":"good name","chinese":"良好名聲"},{"english":"Drama Club members","chinese":"戲劇學會會員"},{"english":"formal complaint","chinese":"正式投訴"},{"english":"concerning our conduct","chinese":"關於我們的行為"},{"english":"conduct","chinese":"行為；舉止"},{"english":"I regret to inform you that","chinese":"很遺憾通知你"},{"english":"receive a formal complaint","chinese":"收到正式投訴"},{"english":"City Hall","chinese":"大會堂"},{"english":"behaviour of a group of","chinese":"一群……的行為"},{"english":"attend the drama performance","chinese":"觀看戲劇演出"},{"english":"drama performance","chinese":"戲劇演出"},{"english":"as the chairperson of","chinese":"作為……的主席"},{"english":"not to embarrass anyone, but to","chinese":"不是為了令任何人難堪，而是為了"},{"english":"embarrass anyone","chinese":"令任何人難堪"},{"english":"address the matter honestly","chinese":"坦誠處理事件"},{"english":"remind all of us of","chinese":"提醒我們所有人"},{"english":"responsibilities as audience members","chinese":"作為觀眾的責任"},{"english":"make clear","chinese":"清楚說明"},{"english":"rebuild the trust","chinese":"重建已受損的信任"},{"english":"be damaged","chinese":"受損"},{"english":"the incident","chinese":"事件"},{"english":"teacher adviser","chinese":"指導老師"},{"english":"consider introducing","chinese":"考慮引入"},{"english":"clearer rules","chinese":"更清晰的規則"},{"english":"future outings","chinese":"日後外出活動"},{"english":"continue representing the school","chinese":"繼續代表學校"},{"english":"maturity, respect and pride","chinese":"成熟、尊重和自豪"},{"english":"according to the complaint","chinese":"根據投訴內容"},{"english":"disturb the performance","chinese":"騷擾演出"},{"english":"talking during scenes","chinese":"在場景進行時說話"},{"english":"inappropriate moments","chinese":"不合適的時候"},{"english":"use mobile phones","chinese":"使用手提電話"},{"english":"fail to follow instructions","chinese":"未能遵從指示"},{"english":"venue staff","chinese":"場地職員"},{"english":"while it would be unfair to suggest that","chinese":"雖然說……並不公平"},{"english":"behave poorly","chinese":"表現不當"},{"english":"alter the fact that","chinese":"改變……這個事實"},{"english":"reflect badly on","chinese":"對……造成負面形象"},{"english":"the whole Drama Club","chinese":"整個戲劇學會"},{"english":"in school uniform","chinese":"穿着校服"},{"english":"no longer","chinese":"不再"},{"english":"private individuals","chinese":"私人個體"},{"english":"represent our club","chinese":"代表我們的學會"},{"english":"the audience around us","chinese":"我們身邊的觀眾"},{"english":"pay for","chinese":"付款享有"},{"english":"meaningful theatre experience","chinese":"有意義的劇場體驗"},{"english":"spend months rehearsing","chinese":"花數月排練"},{"english":"rehearse","chinese":"排練"},{"english":"maintain order","chinese":"維持秩序"},{"english":"treat the theatre as if","chinese":"把劇場當作"},{"english":"classroom corridor","chinese":"課室走廊"},{"english":"interrupt the concentration of","chinese":"打斷……的專注"},{"english":"concentration","chinese":"專注"},{"english":"distract other audience members","chinese":"分散其他觀眾的注意力"},{"english":"show little respect for","chinese":"對……缺乏尊重"},{"english":"art form","chinese":"藝術形式"},{"english":"claim to love","chinese":"聲稱熱愛"},{"english":"put simply","chinese":"簡單來說"},{"english":"not just about","chinese":"不只是關於"},{"english":"perform on stage","chinese":"在台上表演"},{"english":"live performance","chinese":"現場演出"},{"english":"from the audience's side","chinese":"從觀眾一方"},{"english":"more importantly","chinese":"更重要的是"},{"english":"serve as a serious reminder","chinese":"作為嚴肅提醒"},{"english":"membership in the Drama Club","chinese":"戲劇學會會員身分"},{"english":"drama teaches empathy","chinese":"戲劇教導同理心"},{"english":"empathy","chinese":"同理心"},{"english":"discipline","chinese":"紀律"},{"english":"teamwork","chinese":"團隊合作"},{"english":"mean very little","chinese":"意義不大"},{"english":"the moment","chinese":"一……的時候"},{"english":"school campus","chinese":"校園"},{"english":"know when to speak","chinese":"知道何時說話"},{"english":"know when to listen","chinese":"知道何時聆聽"},{"english":"silence itself carries meaning","chinese":"沉默本身帶有意義"},{"english":"by contrast","chinese":"相比之下"},{"english":"careless audience behaviour","chinese":"粗心失禮的觀眾行為"},{"english":"under the spotlight","chinese":"在聚光燈下"},{"english":"the kind of club we should become","chinese":"我們應該成為的那種學會"},{"english":"consider this","chinese":"試想想"},{"english":"visiting students","chinese":"到訪學生"},{"english":"behave noisily","chinese":"吵鬧地表現"},{"english":"annual school production","chinese":"一年一度的學校劇目"},{"english":"feel disappointed","chinese":"感到失望"},{"english":"even hurt","chinese":"甚至受傷"},{"english":"the same standard applies to","chinese":"同樣標準也適用於"},{"english":"Manners maketh man","chinese":"禮貌造就人品"},{"english":"protect the dignity of","chinese":"維護……的尊嚴"},{"english":"dignity","chinese":"尊嚴"},{"english":"everyone involved","chinese":"所有相關人士"},{"english":"with this in mind","chinese":"考慮到這一點"},{"english":"the committee","chinese":"委員會"},{"english":"take immediate steps","chinese":"立即採取措施"},{"english":"written apology","chinese":"書面道歉"},{"english":"on behalf of","chinese":"代表"},{"english":"be directly involved","chinese":"直接涉事"},{"english":"come forward","chinese":"主動站出來"},{"english":"apologise to","chinese":"向……道歉"},{"english":"by Friday","chinese":"在星期五或之前"},{"english":"external activity","chinese":"校外活動"},{"english":"attend a short briefing","chinese":"出席簡短簡介會"},{"english":"theatre etiquette","chinese":"劇場禮儀"},{"english":"punctuality","chinese":"準時"},{"english":"phone use","chinese":"電話使用"},{"english":"seating arrangements","chinese":"座位安排"},{"english":"respond to venue staff","chinese":"回應場地職員"},{"english":"future performances","chinese":"日後演出"},{"english":"at least two","chinese":"至少兩名"},{"english":"be assigned to","chinese":"被分配到"},{"english":"each row","chinese":"每一行座位"},{"english":"deal with quietly","chinese":"低調處理"},{"english":"before they escalate","chinese":"在問題升級之前"},{"english":"not meant to","chinese":"並非旨在"},{"english":"police everyone","chinese":"監視所有人"},{"english":"unnecessarily","chinese":"不必要地"},{"english":"practical way to ensure that","chinese":"確保……的實際方法"},{"english":"irresponsible actions","chinese":"不負責任的行為"},{"english":"put future outings at risk","chinese":"令日後外出活動受威脅"},{"english":"I would appreciate it if","chinese":"如……我將不勝感激"},{"english":"treat this matter seriously","chinese":"認真看待此事"},{"english":"whether or not","chinese":"不論是否"},{"english":"personally involved","chinese":"親身涉事"},{"english":"there is no use","chinese":"……沒有用"},{"english":"blame one another","chinese":"互相責怪"},{"english":"endlessly","chinese":"無休止地"},{"english":"what matters now is that","chinese":"現在重要的是"},{"english":"face up to","chinese":"正視"},{"english":"learn from it","chinese":"從中學習"},{"english":"prove through our future conduct","chinese":"透過日後行為證明"},{"english":"future conduct","chinese":"日後行為"},{"english":"define us","chinese":"定義我們"},{"english":"should you have any concerns","chinese":"如你有任何疑慮"},{"english":"speak to","chinese":"與……交談"},{"english":"after school","chinese":"放學後"},{"english":"build a good reputation","chinese":"建立良好聲譽"},{"english":"reputation","chinese":"聲譽"},{"english":"through years of hard work","chinese":"透過多年努力"},{"english":"unpleasant incident","chinese":"不愉快事件"},{"english":"should not be allowed to","chinese":"不應被容許"},{"english":"from now on","chinese":"從現在起"},{"english":"mature enough to","chinese":"足夠成熟去"},{"english":"not only to…, but also to…","chinese":"不僅……而且……"},{"english":"honour it","chinese":"尊重它；珍視它"},{"english":"Yours sincerely","chinese":"謹啟"},{"english":"Chairperson, Drama Club","chinese":"戲劇學會主席"}]},"dse-writing-2014-part-b-q4":{"exerciseId":"dse-writing-2014-part-b-q4","essayKey":"","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=dse-writing-2014-part-b-q4","flashDeckId":"dse/writing/part-b/2014/Q4","paragraphs":[{"label":"Paragraph 1","english":"Let Cameras Roll—With Rules, Not a Ban","chinese":"讓攝影機繼續運轉——要有規則，而非禁令"},{"label":"Paragraph 2","english":"Dear Editor,","chinese":"敬愛的編輯："},{"label":"Paragraph 3","english":"I am writing in response to the debate over whether filming movies in the city centre should be prohibited. With complaints about blocked pavements, late-night lighting and traffic diversions becoming more visible, some residents are understandably considering a ban in order to restore convenience and quiet. Yet a total prohibition would be an overreaction. As far as I am concerned, Hong Kong should continue to allow film crews to work in central districts, provided that strict permits, time limits and public notices are enforced. My view rests on three reasons - that city-centre filming strengthens Hong Kong’s cultural identity, supports the local economy, and can be regulated without sacrificing public order.","chinese":"本人來信，是為了回應有關應否禁止在市中心拍攝電影的討論。 隨着有關行人路受阻、深夜燈光滋擾以及交通改道的投訴變得更明顯，一些居民為了恢復便利與寧靜，考慮實施禁令，也是可以理解的。 然而，全面禁止將會是過度反應。 就我而言，只要嚴格執行許可證制度、時間限制和公眾通知，香港應該繼續容許電影拍攝團隊在市中心地區工作。 我的看法建基於三個理由：市中心拍攝能夠加強香港的文化身份、支持本地經濟，而且可以在不犧牲公共秩序的情況下受到規管。"},{"label":"Paragraph 4","english":"To begin with, filming in the heart of the city helps preserve and project Hong Kong’s identity. A film is not merely entertainment; rather, it is a visual record of how a place feels, moves and breathes. When a scene is shot beside a tram stop in Central, under the neon glow of Mong Kok, or near the harbour in Tsim Sha Tsui, the city itself becomes part of the story. Studio sets may imitate streets, but they rarely capture the impatient footsteps, crowded crossings and vertical skyline that make Hong Kong unmistakable. More importantly, these images travel far beyond the cinema. A viewer overseas who sees our ferries, wet markets, footbridges and glass towers may become curious about the city behind the story. To forbid filming in these places is, in effect, to tell our filmmakers to hide the very face of Hong Kong. The city centre should not become a blank space in our own imagination.","chinese":"首先，在城市核心地帶拍攝，有助保存並展現香港的身份。 電影不僅僅是娛樂；更準確地說，它是一個地方如何被感受、如何運轉、如何呼吸的視覺紀錄。 當一個場景在中環的電車站旁、旺角的霓虹燈光下，或尖沙咀的海港附近拍攝時，城市本身便成為故事的一部分。 電影廠佈景也許可以模仿街道，卻很少能捕捉到那些急促的腳步、擁擠的過路處，以及令香港一眼可辨的垂直天際線。 更重要的是，這些影像的影響會遠遠超出電影院。 海外觀眾看見我們的渡輪、街市、行人天橋和玻璃高樓後，可能會對故事背後的這座城市產生好奇。 禁止在這些地方拍攝，實際上等於要求我們的電影人把香港最鮮明的面貌隱藏起來。 市中心不應在我們自己的想像中變成一片空白。"},{"label":"Paragraph 5","english":"Secondly, allowing filming brings practical economic benefits. A movie shoot may look like a temporary nuisance, but behind the camera stand directors, lighting technicians, make-up artists, drivers, caterers, security staff and extras, all earning a living from the project. Nearby businesses can also benefit - a café may serve the crew breakfast, a tailor may provide costumes, and a small printing shop may prepare signs or props. In an expensive city where creative workers often struggle for stable opportunities, every production matters. Some may argue that one afternoon of filming blocks customers from entering a shop. That concern is real, but it is not a reason for a blanket ban. With fair compensation, advance notice and sensible scheduling, short-term inconvenience can be balanced against wider economic gain. The question is not whether filming causes disruption, but whether the disruption is proportionate to the value created. More often than not, it is.","chinese":"第二，容許拍攝能帶來實際的經濟利益。 一次電影拍攝看起來可能只是暫時的滋擾，但鏡頭背後站着導演、燈光技師、化妝師、司機、餐飲供應人員、保安人員和臨時演員，他們都靠這個項目謀生。 附近商戶也可以受惠——一間咖啡店可能為拍攝團隊供應早餐，一位裁縫可能提供服裝，一間小型印刷店也可能準備標誌或道具。 在一個生活成本高昂、創意工作者常常難以獲得穩定機會的城市裡，每一個製作項目都十分重要。 有些人可能會指出，一個下午的拍攝會阻礙顧客進入商店。 這種憂慮確實存在，但並不足以成為全面禁令的理由。 透過公平賠償、預先通知和合理編排，短期不便可以與更廣泛的經濟收益取得平衡。 問題的重點不在於拍攝是否造成滋擾，重點在於這種滋擾與其創造的價值是否相稱。 在多數情況下，答案是肯定的。"},{"label":"Paragraph 6","english":"Thirdly, the problems associated with filming can be managed by better rules, not by prohibition. Granted, nobody wants a camera crew to occupy a busy road during rush hour, blast music outside homes at midnight, or leave rubbish behind. However, irresponsible filming is not the same as filming itself. The government can require crews to apply for permits, consult affected shops and residents, display clear notices several days in advance, and restore the area immediately after shooting. Police and transport officers can limit filming to off-peak hours, while penalties can be imposed on companies that break the conditions. Take a hypothetical shoot in Causeway Bay, for example. If one lane is closed only after 11 p.m., if residents are informed, and if emergency access is kept open, the inconvenience becomes limited and predictable. Only by setting clear boundaries can we protect both daily life and artistic freedom. A ban, by contrast, is easy to announce but poor in judgment.","chinese":"第三，與拍攝相關的問題可以透過更完善的規則處理，而非靠禁止來解決。 誠然，沒有人希望拍攝團隊在繁忙時間佔用繁忙道路、在午夜於民居外播放嘈吵音樂，或留下垃圾。 然而，不負責任的拍攝與拍攝本身並不能混為一談。 政府可以要求拍攝團隊申請許可證、諮詢受影響的商戶和居民、提前數天展示清晰通知，並在拍攝後立即恢復場地原狀。 警方和運輸部門人員可以把拍攝限制在非繁忙時段，而違反條件的公司則可被施加罰則。 以銅鑼灣一次假設性的拍攝為例。 如果一條行車線只在晚上十一時後關閉，如果居民已獲通知，而緊急通道亦保持開放，那麼不便便會變得有限而且可預計。 只有透過設立清晰界線，我們才能同時保障日常生活和藝術自由。 相比之下，禁令容易宣布，判斷卻欠周詳。"},{"label":"Paragraph 7","english":"All things considered, Hong Kong should not shut its city centre to filmmakers. There is no denying that residents, commuters and shopkeepers deserve respect; they should never be treated as background objects in someone else’s production. Nevertheless, respect does not require exclusion. It requires planning, accountability and communication. The authorities should therefore improve the permit system, publish filming schedules, require compensation where appropriate, and punish careless crews. Let cameras roll—but let them roll responsibly. That is how Hong Kong can remain both a well-run city and a city with a story worth telling.","chinese":"綜合而言，香港不應把市中心向電影人關上大門。 無可否認，居民、通勤人士和店主都應得到尊重；他們絕不應被當作他人製作中的背景物件。 然而，尊重並不等於排除。 它需要的是規劃、問責和溝通。 因此，當局應改善許可證制度、公布拍攝時間表、在適當情況下要求賠償，並懲罰疏忽的拍攝團隊。 讓攝影機繼續運轉——但必須負責任地運轉。 這樣，香港才能既是一座運作良好的城市，也是一座擁有值得述說故事的城市。"},{"label":"Paragraph 8","english":"Yours faithfully,","chinese":"此致"},{"label":"Paragraph 9","english":"Chris Wong","chinese":"Chris Wong"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"let cameras roll","chinese":"讓攝影機開拍"},{"english":"with rules, not a ban","chinese":"要有規則，而不是禁令"},{"english":"in response to","chinese":"回應……"},{"english":"the debate over whether","chinese":"關於是否……的爭議"},{"english":"filming movies in the city centre","chinese":"在市中心拍攝電影"},{"english":"be prohibited","chinese":"被禁止"},{"english":"complaints about","chinese":"關於……的投訴"},{"english":"blocked pavements","chinese":"被阻塞的行人路"},{"english":"late-night lighting","chinese":"深夜燈光"},{"english":"traffic diversions","chinese":"交通改道"},{"english":"become more visible","chinese":"變得更明顯"},{"english":"understandably","chinese":"可以理解地"},{"english":"consider a ban","chinese":"考慮禁令"},{"english":"in order to restore","chinese":"為了恢復"},{"english":"convenience and quiet","chinese":"便利和安寧"},{"english":"a total prohibition","chinese":"全面禁止"},{"english":"an overreaction","chinese":"反應過度"},{"english":"as far as I am concerned","chinese":"就我而言"},{"english":"continue to allow","chinese":"繼續容許"},{"english":"film crews","chinese":"電影攝製隊；劇組"},{"english":"central districts","chinese":"市中心地區"},{"english":"provided that","chinese":"只要；假如"},{"english":"strict permits","chinese":"嚴格許可證"},{"english":"time limits","chinese":"時間限制"},{"english":"public notices","chinese":"公眾告示"},{"english":"be enforced","chinese":"被執行"},{"english":"my view rests on three reasons","chinese":"我的觀點基於三個原因"},{"english":"cultural identity","chinese":"文化身份"},{"english":"support the local economy","chinese":"支持本地經濟"},{"english":"be regulated without sacrificing","chinese":"可被規管而不犧牲……"},{"english":"public order","chinese":"公共秩序"},{"english":"to begin with","chinese":"首先"},{"english":"in the heart of the city","chinese":"在城市中心"},{"english":"preserve and project","chinese":"保存並展示"},{"english":"not merely entertainment","chinese":"不僅僅是娛樂"},{"english":"rather","chinese":"而是"},{"english":"a visual record of","chinese":"……的視覺紀錄"},{"english":"how a place feels, moves and breathes","chinese":"一個地方的感覺、流動和生命力"},{"english":"be shot beside","chinese":"在……旁邊拍攝"},{"english":"tram stop","chinese":"電車站"},{"english":"under the neon glow of","chinese":"在……霓虹光影下"},{"english":"the neon glow","chinese":"霓虹光影"},{"english":"near the harbour","chinese":"在海港附近"},{"english":"become part of the story","chinese":"成為故事的一部分"},{"english":"studio sets","chinese":"攝影棚佈景"},{"english":"imitate streets","chinese":"模仿街道"},{"english":"rarely capture","chinese":"很少能捕捉"},{"english":"impatient footsteps","chinese":"匆忙的腳步"},{"english":"crowded crossings","chinese":"擁擠的過路處"},{"english":"vertical skyline","chinese":"垂直天際線"},{"english":"make Hong Kong unmistakable","chinese":"令香港一眼可辨"},{"english":"more importantly","chinese":"更重要的是"},{"english":"travel far beyond","chinese":"傳到遠遠超出……的地方"},{"english":"a viewer overseas","chinese":"海外觀眾"},{"english":"become curious about","chinese":"對……產生好奇"},{"english":"the city behind the story","chinese":"故事背後的城市"},{"english":"forbid filming","chinese":"禁止拍攝"},{"english":"in effect","chinese":"實際上"},{"english":"tell filmmakers to hide","chinese":"叫電影人隱藏"},{"english":"the very face of Hong Kong","chinese":"香港最具代表性的面貌"},{"english":"blank space","chinese":"空白位置"},{"english":"in our own imagination","chinese":"在我們自己的想像中"},{"english":"practical economic benefits","chinese":"實際經濟利益"},{"english":"a movie shoot","chinese":"電影拍攝"},{"english":"temporary nuisance","chinese":"暫時滋擾"},{"english":"behind the camera stand","chinese":"鏡頭背後有……"},{"english":"lighting technicians","chinese":"燈光技術員"},{"english":"make-up artists","chinese":"化妝師"},{"english":"caterers","chinese":"膳食供應商"},{"english":"security staff","chinese":"保安人員"},{"english":"extras","chinese":"臨時演員"},{"english":"earn a living from","chinese":"靠……謀生"},{"english":"nearby businesses","chinese":"附近商戶"},{"english":"serve the crew breakfast","chinese":"為劇組供應早餐"},{"english":"provide costumes","chinese":"提供戲服"},{"english":"prepare signs or props","chinese":"準備告示牌或道具"},{"english":"creative workers","chinese":"創意工作者"},{"english":"struggle for stable opportunities","chinese":"難以爭取穩定機會"},{"english":"every production matters","chinese":"每個製作都很重要"},{"english":"some may argue that","chinese":"有些人可能會認為"},{"english":"block customers from entering","chinese":"阻礙顧客進入"},{"english":"that concern is real","chinese":"這個關注是真實的"},{"english":"a blanket ban","chinese":"一刀切禁令；全面禁令"},{"english":"fair compensation","chinese":"公平補償"},{"english":"advance notice","chinese":"預先通知"},{"english":"sensible scheduling","chinese":"合理時間安排"},{"english":"short-term inconvenience","chinese":"短期不便"},{"english":"be balanced against","chinese":"與……作平衡"},{"english":"wider economic gain","chinese":"更廣泛的經濟收益"},{"english":"proportionate to","chinese":"與……相稱"},{"english":"the value created","chinese":"所創造的價值"},{"english":"more often than not","chinese":"多數情況下"},{"english":"problems associated with","chinese":"與……相關的問題"},{"english":"be managed by better rules","chinese":"可透過更好的規則處理"},{"english":"prohibition","chinese":"禁止"},{"english":"granted","chinese":"無可否認"},{"english":"camera crew","chinese":"攝影隊"},{"english":"occupy a busy road","chinese":"佔用繁忙道路"},{"english":"rush hour","chinese":"繁忙時間"},{"english":"blast music outside homes","chinese":"在民居外大聲播放音樂"},{"english":"leave rubbish behind","chinese":"留下垃圾"},{"english":"irresponsible filming","chinese":"不負責任的拍攝"},{"english":"not the same as","chinese":"不等同於"},{"english":"apply for permits","chinese":"申請許可證"},{"english":"consult affected shops and residents","chinese":"諮詢受影響商戶和居民"},{"english":"display clear notices","chinese":"張貼清晰告示"},{"english":"several days in advance","chinese":"提前數天"},{"english":"restore the area","chinese":"恢復該區原狀"},{"english":"immediately after shooting","chinese":"拍攝後立即"},{"english":"transport officers","chinese":"交通人員"},{"english":"limit filming to","chinese":"把拍攝限制在……"},{"english":"off-peak hours","chinese":"非繁忙時段"},{"english":"penalties can be imposed on","chinese":"可對……施加罰則"},{"english":"break the conditions","chinese":"違反條件"},{"english":"hypothetical shoot","chinese":"假設的拍攝"},{"english":"one lane is closed","chinese":"一條行車線被封閉"},{"english":"residents are informed","chinese":"居民獲通知"},{"english":"emergency access","chinese":"緊急通道"},{"english":"be kept open","chinese":"保持開放"},{"english":"limited and predictable","chinese":"有限而可預計"},{"english":"setting clear boundaries","chinese":"設定清晰界線"},{"english":"protect both...and...","chinese":"同時保護……和……"},{"english":"daily life","chinese":"日常生活"},{"english":"artistic freedom","chinese":"藝術自由"},{"english":"by contrast","chinese":"相比之下"},{"english":"easy to announce","chinese":"容易宣布"},{"english":"poor in judgement","chinese":"判斷欠佳"},{"english":"all things considered","chinese":"總括而言"},{"english":"shut its city centre to filmmakers","chinese":"對電影人關上市中心"},{"english":"there is no denying that","chinese":"無可否認"},{"english":"residents, commuters and shopkeepers","chinese":"居民、通勤人士和店主"},{"english":"deserve respect","chinese":"值得被尊重"},{"english":"be treated as background objects","chinese":"被當作背景物件"},{"english":"someone else's production","chinese":"別人的製作"},{"english":"nevertheless","chinese":"然而"},{"english":"require exclusion","chinese":"需要排除；需要拒諸門外"},{"english":"planning, accountability and communication","chinese":"規劃、問責和溝通"},{"english":"the authorities","chinese":"當局"},{"english":"improve the permit system","chinese":"改善許可證制度"},{"english":"publish filming schedules","chinese":"公布拍攝時間表"},{"english":"require compensation where appropriate","chinese":"在適當情況下要求補償"},{"english":"punish careless crews","chinese":"懲罰粗心大意的劇組"},{"english":"let them roll responsibly","chinese":"讓它們負責任地開拍"},{"english":"a well-run city","chinese":"運作良好的城市"},{"english":"a city with a story worth telling","chinese":"一個有值得訴說故事的城市"},{"english":"Yours faithfully","chinese":"謹啟"}]},"dse-writing-2014-part-b-q5":{"exerciseId":"dse-writing-2014-part-b-q5","essayKey":"","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=dse-writing-2014-part-b-q5","flashDeckId":"dse/writing/part-b/2014/Q5","paragraphs":[{"label":"Paragraph 1","english":"A Fairer Locker Policy for a Healthier School","chinese":"一項更公平的儲物櫃政策，成就更健康的校園"},{"label":"Paragraph 2","english":"Dear Ms Lee,","chinese":"李校長："},{"label":"Paragraph 3","english":"As chairperson of the Student Union, I am writing on behalf of students from S1 to S6 about the present locker policy. At present, only a small number of students have access to lockers, and this has led many classmates to ask whether a basic school facility is being shared fairly. After collecting views from students in different classes, I respectfully urge the school to review this arrangement so that every student can study in a safer, fairer environment. Our position is that lockers should be made available to all students through a phased, transparent and need-sensitive system. This is not merely a request for convenience; it is a proposal to protect well-being, improve learning efficiency and strengthen students’ trust in the school.","chinese":"作為學生會主席，我代表中一至中六的學生，就現行儲物櫃政策致函給您。 目前，只有少數學生可以使用儲物櫃，這令許多同學開始質疑，一項基本校園設施是否得到了公平分配。 在收集不同班別學生的意見後，我謹此懇請學校檢討這項安排，好讓每位學生都能在更安全、更公平的環境中學習。 我們的立場是，學校應透過分階段、透明且能照顧實際需要的制度，讓所有學生都有機會使用儲物櫃。 這不只是一項為了方便的請求；更是一個旨在保障學生身心健康、提升學習效率，並加強學生對學校信任的建議。"},{"label":"Paragraph 4","english":"First and foremost, the present policy unintentionally creates an avoidable sense of unfairness. Many students cannot understand why classmates in the same school, following the same timetable and paying the same school fees, should receive such different treatment. The problem is not that some students have lockers; rather, the problem is that most students have little idea how places are allocated. When a rule affects students every day but its reasons are unclear, misunderstanding is bound to grow. Take Form Four students, for example. They often carry textbooks, exercise books, files and reference materials for several electives, whereas some junior-form students also need art materials, musical instruments or sports gear after school. Without lockers, these students must carry everything from classroom to classroom, while a fortunate few can store their belongings safely. Only by making the policy transparent and expanding access can the school show that fairness is not just preached in assemblies, but practised.","chinese":"首先，現行政策無意之間造成了一種本可避免的不公平感。 許多學生無法理解，為何同在一所學校、跟從同一時間表並繳付相同學費的同學，會受到如此不同的待遇。 問題並非在於有些學生擁有儲物櫃；更準確地說，核心在於大多數學生幾乎不知道名額是如何分配的。 當一項規則每天都影響學生，而背後原因卻不清晰時，誤解自然會逐漸增加 以中四學生為例。 他們經常要攜帶幾個選修科的課本、作業簿、文件夾和參考資料；與此同時，一些初中學生課後也需要美術用品、樂器或運動裝備。 沒有儲物櫃，這些學生便必須把所有物品從一間課室帶到另一間課室，而少數幸運的同學卻可以安全地存放自己的物品。 只有透過提高政策透明度並擴大使用機會，學校才能證明公平不能只在早會上被宣講，更要在制度中被實踐。"},{"label":"Paragraph 5","english":"A more inclusive locker policy would also bring clear health and academic benefits. Several junior-form students reported that their schoolbags are so heavy that they leave reference books at home, only to find themselves unprepared during lessons. Senior students preparing for public examinations face a similar problem - they may need past-paper folders, dictionaries, laboratory manuals and supplementary notes on the same day. If they carry all of them, their shoulders and backs suffer; if they do not, their learning suffers. Neither choice is satisfactory. A locker is a simple way to break this unhealthy trade-off. Students could keep non-urgent books at school, bring home only what they need for homework, and organise materials by subject. In other words, wider locker access translates into better health, better preparation and better learning.","chinese":"一項更具包容性的儲物櫃政策，也會帶來明顯的健康和學業益處。 幾位初中學生反映，他們的書包沉重得令他們把參考書留在家中，結果到了上課時才發現自己準備不足。 正在準備公開考試的高中學生也面對類似問題——他們可能在同一天需要歷屆試題文件夾、字典、實驗室手冊和補充筆記。 如果他們全部帶上，肩膀和背部便會受苦；如果他們沒有帶齊，學習便會受影響。 兩種選擇都不能令人滿意。 儲物櫃是一個簡單的方法，可以打破這種不健康的取捨。 學生可以把非即時需要的書本存放在學校，只把做功課所需的物品帶回家，並按科目整理學習材料。 換言之，更廣泛的儲物櫃使用機會，會轉化為更好的健康狀況、更充分的準備和更有效的學習。"},{"label":"Paragraph 6","english":"Granted, the school may be concerned about cost, space and management. However, these concerns are reasons for careful planning, not reasons for doing nothing. We are not asking the school to install hundreds of lockers overnight. Instead, the Student Union proposes a three-step plan. First, the school could conduct an audit of underused spaces, such as areas beside staircases, covered playground walls and corners near special rooms, while ensuring fire safety is not compromised. Secondly, lockers could be introduced in phases, beginning with students who have genuine needs: those with medical conditions, long travelling distances, heavy subject combinations or regular after-school activities. Thirdly, the system could be funded partly through a refundable deposit and partly through school resources or alumni donations. To prevent misuse, students could sign a locker agreement, and class teachers could conduct brief checks at the end of each term. There is no getting around the fact that implementation requires effort, but a manageable policy should not be confused with an impossible one.","chinese":"誠然，學校可能會擔心成本、空間和管理問題。 然而，這些憂慮應成為周詳規劃的理由，不能成為原地不動的理由。 我們並沒有要求學校在一夜之間安裝數百個儲物櫃。 相反，學生會建議採取三步計劃。 首先，學校可以審視未被充分使用的空間，例如樓梯旁的位置、有蓋操場牆邊，以及特別室附近的角落，同時確保消防安全不受影響。 其次，儲物櫃可以分階段引入，先由有真正需要的學生開始，包括有健康狀況、上學路程較長、科目組合較繁重，或經常參與課後活動的學生。 第三，這個制度可以部分透過可退還按金資助，部分則由學校資源或校友捐款支持。 為防止濫用，學生可以簽署儲物櫃使用協議，而班主任亦可在每個學期結束時進行簡短檢查。 無可否認，實施這項政策需要付出努力，但一項可以管理的政策不應被誤認為不可能推行的政策。"},{"label":"Paragraph 7","english":"In conclusion, I sincerely hope you will reconsider the present arrangement. The issue is not so much storage as fairness, health and dignity. By expanding locker access through a transparent and phased policy, the school can ease students’ daily burden, support effective learning and demonstrate that students’ voices are taken seriously. I would be grateful if you could meet the Student Union and class representatives to discuss this proposal, and I respectfully suggest setting up a working group before the end of this term. With thoughtful planning, a fairer locker policy is not beyond reach; it is long overdue.","chinese":"總結來說，我衷心希望您能重新考慮現行安排。 這個議題與其說關乎儲物空間，不如說關乎公平、健康與尊嚴。 透過透明且分階段的政策擴大儲物櫃使用機會，學校可以減輕學生的日常負擔、支持有效學習，並展示學生的聲音受到認真對待。 如您能與學生會及各班代表會面，討論這項建議，我們將不勝感激；我亦謹此建議在本學期結束前成立一個工作小組。 只要規劃周詳，一項更公平的儲物櫃政策並非遙不可及；它早已應該落實。"},{"label":"Paragraph 8","english":"Yours sincerely,","chinese":"謹上，"},{"label":"Paragraph 9","english":"Chris Wong","chinese":"Chris Wong"},{"label":"Paragraph 10","english":"Chairperson, Student Union","chinese":"學生會主席"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"a fairer locker policy","chinese":"更公平的儲物櫃政策"},{"english":"a healthier school","chinese":"更健康的學校"},{"english":"chairperson of","chinese":"……的主席"},{"english":"Student Union","chinese":"學生會"},{"english":"writing on behalf of","chinese":"代表……寫信"},{"english":"from S1 to S6","chinese":"中一至中六"},{"english":"present locker policy","chinese":"現行儲物櫃政策"},{"english":"at present","chinese":"目前"},{"english":"have access to","chinese":"可以使用"},{"english":"led many classmates to ask whether","chinese":"令很多同學質疑是否"},{"english":"basic school facility","chinese":"基本學校設施"},{"english":"shared fairly","chinese":"被公平分配"},{"english":"after collecting views","chinese":"收集意見後"},{"english":"students in different classes","chinese":"不同班別的學生"},{"english":"respectfully urge","chinese":"鄭重促請"},{"english":"review this arrangement","chinese":"檢討這項安排"},{"english":"so that","chinese":"以便；使得"},{"english":"safer, fairer environment","chinese":"更安全、更公平的環境"},{"english":"our position is that","chinese":"我們的立場是"},{"english":"be made available to","chinese":"可供……使用"},{"english":"phased system","chinese":"分階段制度"},{"english":"transparent system","chinese":"透明制度"},{"english":"need-sensitive system","chinese":"顧及需要的制度"},{"english":"not merely","chinese":"不只是"},{"english":"request for convenience","chinese":"為了方便而提出的要求"},{"english":"protect well-being","chinese":"保障身心健康"},{"english":"improve learning efficiency","chinese":"提升學習效率"},{"english":"strengthen students' trust","chinese":"加強學生對學校的信任"},{"english":"first and foremost","chinese":"首先；最重要的是"},{"english":"unintentionally creates","chinese":"無意中造成"},{"english":"avoidable sense of unfairness","chinese":"可避免的不公平感"},{"english":"the same timetable","chinese":"相同時間表"},{"english":"paying the same school fees","chinese":"繳付相同學費"},{"english":"receive such different treatment","chinese":"受到如此不同的待遇"},{"english":"the problem is not that","chinese":"問題並不是"},{"english":"rather","chinese":"而是"},{"english":"have little idea how","chinese":"不太知道如何"},{"english":"places are allocated","chinese":"名額如何分配"},{"english":"affects students every day","chinese":"每天影響學生"},{"english":"its reasons are unclear","chinese":"其原因不清楚"},{"english":"be bound to","chinese":"必然會"},{"english":"misunderstanding","chinese":"誤解"},{"english":"take someone for example","chinese":"以某人為例"},{"english":"Form Four students","chinese":"中四學生"},{"english":"reference materials","chinese":"參考資料"},{"english":"several electives","chinese":"幾個選修科"},{"english":"whereas","chinese":"而"},{"english":"junior-form students","chinese":"初中學生"},{"english":"art materials","chinese":"美術用品"},{"english":"musical instruments","chinese":"樂器"},{"english":"sports gear","chinese":"運動用品"},{"english":"from classroom to classroom","chinese":"從一間課室到另一間課室"},{"english":"a fortunate few","chinese":"少數幸運的人"},{"english":"store their belongings safely","chinese":"安全存放個人物品"},{"english":"only by","chinese":"只有透過"},{"english":"making the policy transparent","chinese":"令政策透明"},{"english":"expanding access","chinese":"擴大使用機會"},{"english":"fairness is not just preached","chinese":"公平不只是被宣講"},{"english":"preached in assemblies","chinese":"在早會中宣講"},{"english":"but practised","chinese":"而是被實踐"},{"english":"more inclusive","chinese":"更具包容性的"},{"english":"clear health and academic benefits","chinese":"明顯的健康和學業好處"},{"english":"reported that","chinese":"匯報；表示"},{"english":"so heavy that","chinese":"重得以致"},{"english":"leave reference books at home","chinese":"把參考書留在家中"},{"english":"only to find themselves","chinese":"結果卻發現自己"},{"english":"unprepared during lessons","chinese":"上課時準備不足"},{"english":"senior students","chinese":"高中學生"},{"english":"public examinations","chinese":"公開考試"},{"english":"face a similar problem","chinese":"面對類似問題"},{"english":"past-paper folders","chinese":"歷屆試題文件夾"},{"english":"dictionaries","chinese":"字典"},{"english":"laboratory manuals","chinese":"實驗手冊"},{"english":"supplementary notes","chinese":"補充筆記"},{"english":"on the same day","chinese":"同一天"},{"english":"shoulders and backs suffer","chinese":"肩膀和背部受苦"},{"english":"neither choice is satisfactory","chinese":"兩個選擇都不理想"},{"english":"break this unhealthy trade-off","chinese":"打破這種不健康的取捨"},{"english":"unhealthy trade-off","chinese":"不健康的取捨"},{"english":"non-urgent books","chinese":"非急用書本"},{"english":"bring home only what they need","chinese":"只帶回所需物品"},{"english":"organise materials by subject","chinese":"按科目整理物品"},{"english":"in other words","chinese":"換句話說"},{"english":"wider locker access","chinese":"更廣泛的儲物櫃使用機會"},{"english":"translates into","chinese":"轉化為；帶來"},{"english":"better preparation","chinese":"更充分準備"},{"english":"granted","chinese":"誠然"},{"english":"be concerned about","chinese":"擔心"},{"english":"cost, space and management","chinese":"成本、空間和管理"},{"english":"reasons for careful planning","chinese":"需要審慎規劃的理由"},{"english":"reasons for doing nothing","chinese":"無所作為的理由"},{"english":"install hundreds of lockers","chinese":"安裝數百個儲物櫃"},{"english":"overnight","chinese":"一夜之間；立即"},{"english":"three-step plan","chinese":"三步計劃"},{"english":"conduct an audit","chinese":"進行審查"},{"english":"underused spaces","chinese":"未充分使用的空間"},{"english":"areas beside staircases","chinese":"樓梯旁的地方"},{"english":"covered playground walls","chinese":"有蓋操場牆邊"},{"english":"corners near special rooms","chinese":"特別室附近的角落"},{"english":"while ensuring","chinese":"同時確保"},{"english":"fire safety","chinese":"消防安全"},{"english":"not be compromised","chinese":"不受損害；不被削弱"},{"english":"introduced in phases","chinese":"分階段推出"},{"english":"beginning with","chinese":"由……開始"},{"english":"genuine needs","chinese":"真正需要"},{"english":"medical conditions","chinese":"健康狀況；疾病"},{"english":"long travelling distances","chinese":"遙遠上學路程"},{"english":"heavy subject combinations","chinese":"繁重的科目組合"},{"english":"regular after-school activities","chinese":"恆常課後活動"},{"english":"funded partly through","chinese":"部分透過……資助"},{"english":"refundable deposit","chinese":"可退還按金"},{"english":"school resources","chinese":"學校資源"},{"english":"alumni donations","chinese":"校友捐款"},{"english":"prevent misuse","chinese":"防止濫用"},{"english":"sign a locker agreement","chinese":"簽署儲物櫃使用協議"},{"english":"class teachers","chinese":"班主任"},{"english":"conduct brief checks","chinese":"進行簡短檢查"},{"english":"at the end of each term","chinese":"每個學期末"},{"english":"there is no getting around the fact that","chinese":"無可否認"},{"english":"implementation requires effort","chinese":"執行需要努力"},{"english":"manageable policy","chinese":"可管理的政策"},{"english":"be confused with","chinese":"被混同為"},{"english":"impossible one","chinese":"不可能實行的事情"},{"english":"in conclusion","chinese":"總而言之"},{"english":"sincerely hope","chinese":"衷心希望"},{"english":"reconsider","chinese":"重新考慮"},{"english":"not so much… as…","chinese":"與其說是……不如說是……"},{"english":"storage","chinese":"儲物空間"},{"english":"dignity","chinese":"尊嚴"},{"english":"by expanding locker access","chinese":"透過擴大儲物櫃使用機會"},{"english":"ease students' daily burden","chinese":"減輕學生每日負擔"},{"english":"support effective learning","chinese":"支持有效學習"},{"english":"demonstrate that","chinese":"顯示；證明"},{"english":"students' voices are taken seriously","chinese":"學生的聲音受到重視"},{"english":"I would be grateful if","chinese":"如能……我將不勝感激"},{"english":"class representatives","chinese":"班代表"},{"english":"discuss this proposal","chinese":"討論這項建議"},{"english":"respectfully suggest","chinese":"鄭重建議"},{"english":"setting up a working group","chinese":"成立工作小組"},{"english":"before the end of this term","chinese":"本學期結束前"},{"english":"with thoughtful planning","chinese":"透過周詳規劃"},{"english":"not beyond reach","chinese":"並非遙不可及"},{"english":"long overdue","chinese":"早就應該實行"},{"english":"Yours sincerely","chinese":"謹啟；此致"},{"english":"Chairperson, Student Union","chinese":"學生會主席"}]},"dse-writing-2014-part-b-q6":{"exerciseId":"dse-writing-2014-part-b-q6","essayKey":"","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=dse-writing-2014-part-b-q6","flashDeckId":"dse/writing/part-b/2014/Q6","paragraphs":[{"label":"Paragraph 1","english":"Inside the Suit - My Summer in a Theme Park Costume","chinese":"戲服之內——我在主題樂園穿上角色戲服的夏天"},{"label":"Paragraph 2","english":"By a student contributor","chinese":"學生投稿者"},{"label":"Paragraph 3","english":"For many students, a summer job means air-conditioning, flexible hours and a little extra money. Last summer, however, I chose something less comfortable but far more memorable - I became a costumed character performer in a local theme park. The park hired young performers like me to brighten its peak-season atmosphere so that families could leave not only with photographs, but with stories worth retelling. My view, after two sweaty months, is simple. The job was exhausting, occasionally awkward and far from glamorous; nevertheless, it was one of the most meaningful experiences I have ever had. It taught me that entertainment is not just about smiling for the camera, but about discipline, empathy and invisible labour.","chinese":"對許多學生來說，暑期工意味著冷氣、彈性工時，以及一點額外收入。 然而，去年夏天，我選擇了一份沒有那麼舒適、卻難忘得多的工作——我成為了本地主題樂園中穿上角色戲服的表演員。 樂園聘請像我這樣的年輕表演者，為旺季增添氣氛，好讓一家大小離開時帶走的不只有照片，也有值得一再回味的故事。 經過兩個汗流浹背的月後，我的看法很簡單。 這份工作令人筋疲力盡，偶爾也尷尬，而且一點也不光鮮；儘管如此，它仍然是我至今最有意義的經歷之一。 它讓我明白，娛樂的重點不只在於對着鏡頭微笑，也在於紀律、同理心，以及那些看不見的勞動。"},{"label":"Paragraph 4","english":"A typical working day began before the gates opened. I arrived at the staff entrance at 8:15 a.m., signed in, changed into a black base layer and attended a safety briefing. Thereafter, our team leader reminded us of the day’s character schedule, parade route and emergency hand signals. Once the costume was brought out, the real transformation began. My headpiece blocked half my vision, my gloves made simple gestures clumsy, and my shoes were so wide that every step had to be planned. The first thing to know is that a costumed performer cannot simply “act cute”. We had to move slowly enough for children to follow us, energetically enough to look alive, and carefully enough not to knock anyone over. During each appearance, a handler guided the queue, protected us from overexcited visitors and reminded us when to retreat for water. From photo sessions to mini-dances, the day moved in cycles of performance and recovery. By the time I clocked out, my T-shirt was soaked, but my character’s painted smile still looked perfect.","chinese":"一個典型的工作天，在樂園大門打開之前便已經開始。 我早上八時十五分抵達員工入口，簽到，換上黑色貼身底衣，然後參加安全簡報。 之後，組長提醒我們當天的角色演出時間表、巡遊路線，以及緊急手勢信號 戲服一被拿出來，真正的轉變便開始了。 我的頭套擋住了半邊視線，手套令簡單的動作也變得笨拙，而鞋子寬大得讓我每一步都必須小心安排。 首先要知道的是，穿上角色戲服的表演員不能只是「扮可愛」。 我們的動作要慢得足以讓孩子跟得上，要有活力得足以令角色看起來生動，也要小心得足以避免撞倒任何人。 每次出場時，隨行工作人員都會引導隊伍，保護我們免受過度興奮的遊客碰撞，並提醒我們甚麼時候要退場喝水。 從拍照環節到小型舞蹈，整個工作天就在一輪又一輪的表演與休息之間推進 到我打卡下班時，T 恤已經濕透，但我所扮演的角色臉上那個畫上去的笑容，依然完美無瑕。"},{"label":"Paragraph 5","english":"The best part of the job was the direct happiness it created. One afternoon, a little boy wearing a birthday badge ran towards me, hugged my furry waist and whispered, “I found you!” Of course, I could not reply, but I knelt down, tapped my heart and gave him the most dramatic thumbs-up I could manage. His mother cried. That moment alone made the whole shift worthwhile. What I loved about the job was that it forced me to communicate without words. I learnt how to calm a crying toddler with smaller movements, how to entertain bored teenagers with exaggerated embarrassment, and how to make shy children feel seen. More importantly, the work made me a better team player. The handler, parade dancers, cleaning staff and performers had to trust one another. Many visitors, if not most, noticed only the cheerful character; what they did not see was the well-organised team keeping the magic alive.","chinese":"這份工作最美好的地方，是它能直接帶來快樂。 有一天下午，一個戴着生日襟章的小男孩向我跑來，抱住我毛茸茸的腰，然後低聲說：「我找到你了！」 當然，我不能開口回應，但我跪下來，輕拍胸口，然後用盡全力給了他一個最誇張的讚好手勢。 他的媽媽哭了。 單是那一刻，便令整個班次都變得值得。 我喜歡這份工作的地方，在於它迫使我不用言語去溝通。 我學會了如何用較細微的動作安撫正在哭泣的幼兒，如何用誇張的尷尬反應娛樂百無聊賴的青少年，也學會了如何讓害羞的孩子感到自己被看見。 更重要的是，這份工作令我成為一個更好的團隊成員。 隨行工作人員、巡遊舞蹈員、清潔員工和表演者都必須彼此信任。 很多遊客，甚至可以說大多數遊客，只看見那個開朗的角色；他們沒有看見的，是背後那支井然有序、一直維持魔法感的團隊。"},{"label":"Paragraph 6","english":"That said, the job was not without its problems. The most obvious difficulty was the heat. On some afternoons the costume felt less like a uniform than a private sauna, and it took forever for my breathing to settle after a dance set. Physical discomfort, however, was only part of the challenge. The worse problem was that some visitors forgot there was a person inside. At one point, a teenager slapped the character’s head “as a joke”, while another guest pulled my tail to make his friends laugh. I could not shout, argue or break character; instead, I had to step back and let my handler deal with it. Even when I was tired, dizzy or upset, I still had to look delighted. The price of being magical, I discovered, is often being invisible.","chinese":"話雖如此，這份工作也並非毫無問題。 最明顯的困難是炎熱。 有些下午，那套戲服與其說像制服，不如說更像一個私人桑拿房；每次跳完一組舞後，我總要過很久才能讓呼吸平復下來。 然而，身體上的不適只是挑戰的一部分。 更嚴重的問題是，有些遊客忘記了戲服裡面其實有一個人。 有一次，一名青少年「開玩笑」地拍打角色的頭，另一位遊客則拉我的尾巴來逗朋友發笑。 我不能大叫，不能爭辯，也不能脫離角色；相反，我只能退後一步，讓隨行工作人員處理。 即使我感到疲倦、頭暈或委屈，我仍然必須看起來很高興。 我後來發現，成為魔法的一部分所付出的代價，往往就是讓自己變得隱形。"},{"label":"Paragraph 7","english":"All things considered, I would still recommend this job to students who want more than easy pocket money. It is demanding, but that is exactly why it is valuable. Students who take it up should be punctual, patient and prepared to sweat; theme parks, for their part, should provide enough breaks, shade and protection for young performers. As for me, I no longer look at mascots in the same way. Behind every perfect photograph stands a real worker, silently waving, carefully breathing and trying, one child at a time, to make summer unforgettable.","chinese":"整體而言，我仍然會向那些想得到的不只是輕鬆零用錢的學生推薦這份工作 它要求很高，但也正因如此，它才有價值。 選擇這份工作的學生應該守時、有耐性，並準備好流汗；至於主題樂園方面，則應為年輕表演者提供足夠休息時間、遮蔭空間和保護。 至於我，我已經不再用以往的方式看待吉祥物。 每一張完美照片的背後，都站着一位真實的工作者，默默地揮手，小心地呼吸，並努力逐個孩子地，讓這個夏天變得難以忘懷。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"inside the suit","chinese":"在服裝裏面"},{"english":"theme park costume","chinese":"主題公園角色服裝"},{"english":"by a student contributor","chinese":"由學生投稿人撰寫"},{"english":"for many students","chinese":"對很多學生來說"},{"english":"a summer job","chinese":"暑期工"},{"english":"air-conditioning","chinese":"冷氣"},{"english":"flexible hours","chinese":"彈性工時"},{"english":"a little extra money","chinese":"一點額外收入"},{"english":"last summer","chinese":"去年暑假"},{"english":"something less comfortable but far more memorable","chinese":"較不舒服但難忘得多的事"},{"english":"far more memorable","chinese":"難忘得多"},{"english":"a costumed character performer","chinese":"穿着角色服裝的表演者"},{"english":"local theme park","chinese":"本地主題公園"},{"english":"hired young performers","chinese":"聘請年輕表演者"},{"english":"brighten its peak-season atmosphere","chinese":"為旺季氣氛增添活力"},{"english":"peak-season atmosphere","chinese":"旺季氣氛"},{"english":"not only with photographs, but with stories","chinese":"不但帶着照片，還帶着故事"},{"english":"stories worth retelling","chinese":"值得重述的故事"},{"english":"after two sweaty months","chinese":"經過兩個汗流浹背的月份"},{"english":"exhausting","chinese":"令人筋疲力盡的"},{"english":"occasionally awkward","chinese":"偶爾尷尬的"},{"english":"far from glamorous","chinese":"一點也不風光"},{"english":"nevertheless","chinese":"儘管如此"},{"english":"meaningful experiences","chinese":"有意義的經歷"},{"english":"taught me that","chinese":"教會我"},{"english":"not just about","chinese":"不只是關於"},{"english":"smiling for the camera","chinese":"對着鏡頭微笑"},{"english":"discipline","chinese":"紀律"},{"english":"empathy","chinese":"同理心"},{"english":"invisible labour","chinese":"隱形勞動"},{"english":"a typical working day","chinese":"典型工作日"},{"english":"before the gates opened","chinese":"在園區開門之前"},{"english":"staff entrance","chinese":"職員入口"},{"english":"signed in","chinese":"簽到"},{"english":"changed into","chinese":"換上"},{"english":"black base layer","chinese":"黑色貼身底衣"},{"english":"safety briefing","chinese":"安全簡介會"},{"english":"thereafter","chinese":"其後"},{"english":"team leader","chinese":"組長"},{"english":"remind someone of","chinese":"提醒某人……"},{"english":"character schedule","chinese":"角色出場時間表"},{"english":"parade route","chinese":"巡遊路線"},{"english":"emergency hand signals","chinese":"緊急手勢"},{"english":"brought out","chinese":"被拿出來"},{"english":"the real transformation began","chinese":"真正的轉變開始"},{"english":"headpiece","chinese":"頭套"},{"english":"block half my vision","chinese":"擋住我一半視線"},{"english":"simple gestures","chinese":"簡單手勢"},{"english":"make gestures clumsy","chinese":"令手勢變得笨拙"},{"english":"so wide that","chinese":"闊得……以致"},{"english":"every step had to be planned","chinese":"每一步都要事先想好"},{"english":"the first thing to know","chinese":"首先要知道的是"},{"english":"act cute","chinese":"扮可愛"},{"english":"slowly enough for","chinese":"慢到足以讓……"},{"english":"energetically enough to","chinese":"有活力到足以……"},{"english":"look alive","chinese":"看起來生動"},{"english":"carefully enough not to","chinese":"小心到不會……"},{"english":"knock anyone over","chinese":"撞倒任何人"},{"english":"during each appearance","chinese":"每次出場期間"},{"english":"handler","chinese":"隨行工作人員"},{"english":"guide the queue","chinese":"指引排隊人龍"},{"english":"overexcited visitors","chinese":"過度興奮的遊客"},{"english":"retreat for water","chinese":"退下來喝水"},{"english":"photo sessions","chinese":"拍照時段"},{"english":"mini-dances","chinese":"小型舞蹈"},{"english":"move in cycles of","chinese":"以……循環進行"},{"english":"performance and recovery","chinese":"表演與恢復"},{"english":"by the time","chinese":"到……的時候"},{"english":"clocked out","chinese":"下班打卡"},{"english":"soaked","chinese":"濕透"},{"english":"painted smile","chinese":"畫上去的笑容"},{"english":"the best part of","chinese":"最好的部分"},{"english":"direct happiness","chinese":"直接帶來的快樂"},{"english":"wearing a birthday badge","chinese":"戴着生日襟章"},{"english":"ran towards me","chinese":"向我跑來"},{"english":"furry waist","chinese":"毛茸茸的腰部"},{"english":"whispered","chinese":"低聲說"},{"english":"could not reply","chinese":"不能回答"},{"english":"knelt down","chinese":"跪下；蹲下"},{"english":"tapped my heart","chinese":"輕拍心口"},{"english":"dramatic thumbs-up","chinese":"誇張的豎拇指手勢"},{"english":"the whole shift","chinese":"整個更次"},{"english":"worthwhile","chinese":"值得的"},{"english":"what I loved about","chinese":"我喜歡……的地方是"},{"english":"forced me to","chinese":"迫使我"},{"english":"communicate without words","chinese":"不用言語溝通"},{"english":"calm a crying toddler","chinese":"安撫哭泣的幼童"},{"english":"smaller movements","chinese":"較細小的動作"},{"english":"bored teenagers","chinese":"感到沉悶的青少年"},{"english":"exaggerated embarrassment","chinese":"誇張的尷尬反應"},{"english":"make shy children feel seen","chinese":"令害羞的孩子感到被看見"},{"english":"more importantly","chinese":"更重要的是"},{"english":"team player","chinese":"團隊合作者"},{"english":"parade dancers","chinese":"巡遊舞蹈員"},{"english":"cleaning staff","chinese":"清潔職員"},{"english":"trust one another","chinese":"互相信任"},{"english":"if not most","chinese":"即使不是大多數，也是很多"},{"english":"cheerful character","chinese":"開朗的角色"},{"english":"what they did not see","chinese":"他們看不見的是"},{"english":"well-organised team","chinese":"組織良好的團隊"},{"english":"keep the magic alive","chinese":"讓魔法般的氣氛延續"},{"english":"that said","chinese":"話雖如此"},{"english":"not without its problems","chinese":"並非沒有問題"},{"english":"the most obvious difficulty","chinese":"最明顯的困難"},{"english":"less like…than…","chinese":"與其說像……不如說像……"},{"english":"private sauna","chinese":"私人桑拿房"},{"english":"take forever","chinese":"花很久時間"},{"english":"breathing to settle","chinese":"呼吸平復"},{"english":"dance set","chinese":"一段舞蹈表演"},{"english":"physical discomfort","chinese":"身體不適"},{"english":"part of the challenge","chinese":"挑戰的一部分"},{"english":"the more serious problem","chinese":"更嚴重的問題"},{"english":"a person inside","chinese":"服裝裏面的人"},{"english":"at one point","chinese":"有一次"},{"english":"slap the character's head","chinese":"拍打角色的頭"},{"english":"as a joke","chinese":"當作玩笑"},{"english":"pull my tail","chinese":"拉我的尾巴"},{"english":"make his friends laugh","chinese":"逗朋友發笑"},{"english":"break character","chinese":"跳出角色"},{"english":"step back","chinese":"後退一步"},{"english":"deal with it","chinese":"處理這件事"},{"english":"even when","chinese":"即使"},{"english":"dizzy","chinese":"頭暈"},{"english":"look delighted","chinese":"看起來很高興"},{"english":"the price of being magical","chinese":"製造魔法感的代價"},{"english":"being invisible","chinese":"變得隱形；不被看見"},{"english":"all things considered","chinese":"總括而言"},{"english":"recommend this job to","chinese":"向……推薦這份工作"},{"english":"more than easy pocket money","chinese":"不只是輕鬆賺零用錢"},{"english":"demanding","chinese":"要求高的；辛苦的"},{"english":"exactly why","chinese":"正正是為甚麼"},{"english":"take it up","chinese":"接受這份工作"},{"english":"punctual","chinese":"守時"},{"english":"prepared to sweat","chinese":"準備好流汗"},{"english":"for their part","chinese":"就……而言"},{"english":"provide enough breaks","chinese":"提供足夠休息"},{"english":"shade","chinese":"遮蔭處"},{"english":"young performers","chinese":"年輕表演者"},{"english":"no longer look at","chinese":"不再以同一方式看待"},{"english":"mascots","chinese":"吉祥物"},{"english":"behind every perfect photograph stands","chinese":"每張完美照片背後都有……"},{"english":"a real worker","chinese":"真正的工作者"},{"english":"silently waving","chinese":"默默揮手"},{"english":"carefully breathing","chinese":"小心地呼吸"},{"english":"one child at a time","chinese":"一次服務一個孩子"},{"english":"make summer unforgettable","chinese":"令夏天難忘"}]},"dse-writing-2014-part-b-q7":{"exerciseId":"dse-writing-2014-part-b-q7","essayKey":"","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=dse-writing-2014-part-b-q7","flashDeckId":"dse/writing/part-b/2014/Q7","paragraphs":[{"label":"Paragraph 1","english":"More Than a Punchline: The Night Comedy Taught Us to Listen","chinese":"不只是一個笑位：那一晚，喜劇教會我們聆聽"},{"label":"Paragraph 2","english":"By Chris Wong, 6A","chinese":"6A 班 Chris Wong 撰"},{"label":"Paragraph 3","english":"When our English Society arranged for us to attend a local stand-up comedy show last Friday, I expected a pleasant evening of jokes. I did not expect to leave a small black-box theatre thinking about courage, language and human connection. With students increasingly buried under tests, tutorials and glowing phone screens, our school community should consider giving us more chances to watch live performances so that we can learn confidence, empathy and expressive power beyond the classroom. Stand-up comedy, I discovered, is not just about making people laugh; more importantly, it is about making people see ordinary life in a sharper, warmer and braver way.","chinese":"上星期五，英文學會安排我們觀看一場本地棟篤笑表演時，我原本以為那只會是一個充滿笑話的愉快晚上。 我沒有料到自己離開那個小型黑盒劇場時，腦海裡竟然在思考勇氣、語言，以及人與人之間的連結。 在學生愈來愈被測驗、補習和發亮的手機螢幕重重包圍的情況下，我們的學校社群應該考慮給予我們更多觀看現場表演的機會，讓我們能在課室之外學習自信、同理心和表達力量。 我發現，棟篤笑不只在於令人發笑；更重要的是，它在於讓人以更敏銳、更溫暖、更勇敢的方式看見平凡生活。"},{"label":"Paragraph 4","english":"The show began almost too quietly. A single microphone stood under a cone of yellow light, while rows of folding chairs pressed close to the stage. Then the comedian walked out, looked at the audience, and said, “I know this theatre is small. Even my mother’s expectations of me needed more space.” The room exploded. From that moment on, he turned everyday Hong Kong frustrations into sparkling stories - the MTR passenger who treats the pole like private property, the parent who asks where the other four marks went when a child scores 96, and the student who opens a textbook like a hero but closes it five minutes later like a defeated tourist. What impressed me most was the precision behind the humour. Every pause had a purpose; every raised eyebrow worked like punctuation. The show felt spontaneous, yet it had clearly been built, tested and polished line by line.","chinese":"表演開始時幾乎安靜得有點過分。 一支咪高峰立在一道錐形黃光之下，一排排摺椅則緊貼著舞台。 接著，那位喜劇演員走出來，看著觀眾說：「我知道這個劇場很小。就連我媽媽對我的期望，也需要更多空間。」 全場瞬間爆笑起來。 從那一刻起，他把香港人日常的種種煩躁轉化成閃閃發亮的故事——把扶手柱當成私人財產的港鐵乘客、孩子考了 96 分還問另外 4 分去了哪裡的家長，以及打開課本時像英雄、五分鐘後合上時卻像戰敗旅客的學生。 最令我印象深刻的，是幽默背後的精準。 每一次停頓都有目的；每一次揚眉都像標點符號一樣發揮作用。 整場表演感覺即興自然，卻明顯是一句一句建立、測試和打磨出來的。"},{"label":"Paragraph 5","english":"However, such effortless laughter hides enormous difficulty. For one thing, stand-up performers face the pressure of originality and timing. It is one thing to complain about homework, public transport or parents; it is another to find an angle that feels fresh, remove anything unnecessary and deliver it before the moment grows cold. There is no orchestra, costume change or dramatic lighting to rescue a weak joke. If the audience falls silent, the silence is immediate and public. At one point, a joke about online lessons did not quite land. Instead of panicking, the comedian smiled and said, “That reaction was so quiet even Zoom would call it an unstable connection.” In seconds, he won us back. For another, comedians must know where to draw the line. Comedy often touches on family pressure, inequality, appearance and language ability. What is harmless entertainment to one person may be hurtful to another. The performer laughed at exam culture without humiliating students and teased parents without making them villains. For all its glamour, stand-up is emotionally demanding work - it requires not only a sharp tongue, but also a generous heart.","chinese":"然而，這種看似毫不費力的笑聲背後，隱藏著巨大的難度。 首先，棟篤笑表演者要面對原創性與節奏掌握的壓力。 抱怨功課、公共交通或父母是一回事；要找到一個新鮮的角度、刪去所有多餘部分，並在時機冷卻之前把笑話說出來，又是另一回事。 沒有管弦樂隊、服裝轉換或戲劇化燈光可以拯救一個薄弱的笑話。 如果觀眾陷入沉默，那份沉默就是即時而公開的。 在某一刻，一個關於網課的笑話並沒有完全奏效。 那位喜劇演員沒有慌張，反倒笑著說：「大家的反應安靜得連 Zoom 都會稱它為連線不穩。」 幾秒之內，他便重新贏回了我們。 其次，喜劇演員必須知道界線應該畫在哪裡。 喜劇往往觸及家庭壓力、不平等、外貌和語言能力。 對一個人來說無傷大雅的娛樂，對另一個人來說卻可能造成傷害。 那位表演者以考試文化開玩笑，卻沒有羞辱學生；他也拿父母打趣，卻沒有把他們塑造成反派。 儘管棟篤笑有其光彩，它仍是一份情感上要求很高的工作——它不只需要犀利的口才，也需要一顆寬厚的心。"},{"label":"Paragraph 6","english":"Students can benefit greatly from watching such performances. First, stand-up comedy trains our ear for language. We see how a single word can change a sentence, how a pause can create suspense, and how a comparison can make an idea memorable. This is useful for English speaking exams, debate competitions and class presentations. A student who learns to speak with timing and audience awareness will sound more confident than one who simply memorises impressive vocabulary. More importantly, comedy teaches us to think. A good joke often begins with a familiar situation and ends with an unexpected truth; in other words, it encourages us to question habits we usually accept without thinking. It also builds empathy. When we laughed at jokes about tests, family expectations and awkward friendships, we were admitting that many of us share the same worries.","chinese":"學生可以從觀看這類表演中獲益良多。 首先，棟篤笑能訓練我們對語言的敏感度。 我們會看見一個字如何改變一句話，一次停頓如何製造懸念，以及一個比較如何令人記住一個想法。 這對英文口試、辯論比賽和課堂演說都很有用。 學會掌握說話節奏和觀眾意識的學生，會比只背誦華麗詞彙的學生聽起來更有自信。 更重要的是，喜劇教會我們思考。 一個好的笑話往往從熟悉的情境開始，最後帶出意想不到的真相；換言之，它鼓勵我們質疑那些平日不假思索便接受的習慣。 它也培養同理心。 當我們因關於測驗、家庭期望和尷尬友情的笑話而發笑時，我們其實是在承認，很多人都分擔著相同的煩惱。"},{"label":"Paragraph 7","english":"Most importantly, watching comedy can make school life healthier. Laughter is not an escape from reality; sometimes it is a way of facing reality together. The school could invite local comedians, organise student comedy workshops or include humorous speeches in English activities. If we can learn to laugh thoughtfully, speak bravely and listen generously, we will become not only better English users, but also kinder classmates. The show lasted just over an hour, but its message is still echoing in my mind. Sometimes, the shortest distance between people is a punchline.","chinese":"最重要的是，觀看喜劇能讓校園生活更健康。 笑聲並非逃避現實；有時，它是一種共同面對現實的方法。 學校可以邀請本地喜劇演員、舉辦學生喜劇工作坊，或把幽默演說納入英文活動。 如果我們能學會有思考地笑、勇敢地說話、寬厚地聆聽，我們就不只會成為更好的英語使用者，也會成為更友善的同學。 這場表演只持續了一小時多一點，但它的訊息仍然在我腦海中迴響。 有時，人與人之間最短的距離，就是一句笑位。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"more than a punchline","chinese":"不只是笑點"},{"english":"taught us to listen","chinese":"教會我們聆聽"},{"english":"English Society","chinese":"英文學會"},{"english":"arrange for someone to","chinese":"安排某人去……"},{"english":"attend a local stand-up comedy show","chinese":"觀看本地棟篤笑表演"},{"english":"stand-up comedy show","chinese":"棟篤笑表演"},{"english":"a pleasant evening of jokes","chinese":"一個充滿笑話的愉快晚上"},{"english":"did not expect to","chinese":"沒有預期會……"},{"english":"black-box theatre","chinese":"黑盒劇場"},{"english":"human connection","chinese":"人與人之間的連繫"},{"english":"increasingly buried under","chinese":"越來越被……壓住"},{"english":"tests and tutorials","chinese":"測驗和補習"},{"english":"glowing phone screens","chinese":"發光的手機屏幕"},{"english":"school community","chinese":"學校社群"},{"english":"consider giving us more chances to","chinese":"考慮給我們更多機會去……"},{"english":"live performances","chinese":"現場表演"},{"english":"beyond the classroom","chinese":"課室以外"},{"english":"confidence, empathy and expressive power","chinese":"自信、同理心和表達力"},{"english":"not just about","chinese":"不只是關於……"},{"english":"making people laugh","chinese":"令人發笑"},{"english":"more importantly","chinese":"更重要的是"},{"english":"ordinary life","chinese":"平凡生活"},{"english":"in a sharper, warmer and braver way","chinese":"以更敏銳、更溫暖、更勇敢的方式"},{"english":"began almost too quietly","chinese":"開始得幾乎過於安靜"},{"english":"a single microphone","chinese":"一支麥克風"},{"english":"a cone of yellow light","chinese":"一束黃色燈光"},{"english":"rows of folding chairs","chinese":"一排排摺椅"},{"english":"pressed close to","chinese":"緊貼着"},{"english":"walk out","chinese":"走出來"},{"english":"the audience","chinese":"觀眾"},{"english":"mother's expectations of me","chinese":"媽媽對我的期望"},{"english":"needed more space","chinese":"需要更多空間"},{"english":"the room exploded","chinese":"全場爆笑"},{"english":"from that moment on","chinese":"從那一刻起"},{"english":"everyday Hong Kong frustrations","chinese":"香港日常生活中的煩惱"},{"english":"turn something into","chinese":"把某事變成"},{"english":"sparkling stories","chinese":"精彩生動的故事"},{"english":"treats the pole like private property","chinese":"把扶手柱當成私人財產"},{"english":"private property","chinese":"私人財產"},{"english":"where the other four marks went","chinese":"餘下四分去了哪裏"},{"english":"open a textbook like a hero","chinese":"像英雄般打開課本"},{"english":"close it like a defeated tourist","chinese":"像落敗的旅客般合上它"},{"english":"what impressed me most","chinese":"最令我印象深刻的是"},{"english":"the precision behind the humour","chinese":"幽默背後的精準"},{"english":"every pause had a purpose","chinese":"每個停頓都有目的"},{"english":"raised eyebrow","chinese":"揚起的眉毛"},{"english":"worked like punctuation","chinese":"像標點符號一樣發揮作用"},{"english":"felt spontaneous","chinese":"感覺自然即興"},{"english":"yet it had clearly been","chinese":"但它明顯已經被……"},{"english":"built, tested and polished","chinese":"經過建立、測試和打磨"},{"english":"line by line","chinese":"逐句"},{"english":"effortless laughter","chinese":"看似輕鬆的笑聲"},{"english":"hides enormous difficulty","chinese":"隱藏巨大的難度"},{"english":"for one thing","chinese":"首先；其中一點是"},{"english":"stand-up performers","chinese":"棟篤笑表演者"},{"english":"face the pressure of","chinese":"面對……的壓力"},{"english":"originality and timing","chinese":"原創性和時機掌握"},{"english":"it is one thing to","chinese":"做……是一回事"},{"english":"it is another to","chinese":"做到……又是另一回事"},{"english":"find an angle","chinese":"找到角度"},{"english":"feels fresh","chinese":"感覺新鮮"},{"english":"remove anything unnecessary","chinese":"刪去不必要的東西"},{"english":"deliver it","chinese":"說出它；演繹它"},{"english":"before the moment grows cold","chinese":"在時機冷卻之前"},{"english":"dramatic lighting","chinese":"戲劇化燈光"},{"english":"rescue a weak joke","chinese":"挽救一個薄弱的笑話"},{"english":"the audience falls silent","chinese":"觀眾變得沉默"},{"english":"immediate and public","chinese":"即時而公開"},{"english":"at one point","chinese":"在某一刻"},{"english":"online lessons","chinese":"網上課堂"},{"english":"did not quite land","chinese":"未能完全奏效"},{"english":"instead of panicking","chinese":"沒有驚慌失措，而是……"},{"english":"win us back","chinese":"重新贏回我們的注意"},{"english":"for another","chinese":"另一方面"},{"english":"draw the line","chinese":"知道界線在哪裏"},{"english":"touch on","chinese":"觸及"},{"english":"family pressure","chinese":"家庭壓力"},{"english":"inequality","chinese":"不平等"},{"english":"appearance","chinese":"外貌"},{"english":"language ability","chinese":"語言能力"},{"english":"harmless entertainment","chinese":"無傷大雅的娛樂"},{"english":"hurtful to another","chinese":"對另一個人造成傷害"},{"english":"laughed at exam culture","chinese":"取笑考試文化"},{"english":"exam culture","chinese":"考試文化"},{"english":"without humiliating","chinese":"沒有羞辱"},{"english":"teased parents","chinese":"打趣地取笑父母"},{"english":"making them villains","chinese":"把他們塑造成壞人"},{"english":"for all its glamour","chinese":"儘管看起來風光"},{"english":"emotionally demanding work","chinese":"情緒上要求很高的工作"},{"english":"requires not only…but also…","chinese":"不但需要……而且需要……"},{"english":"a sharp tongue","chinese":"口才尖銳"},{"english":"a generous heart","chinese":"寬厚的心"},{"english":"benefit greatly from","chinese":"從……中大大受益"},{"english":"train our ear for language","chinese":"訓練我們對語言的敏感度"},{"english":"a single word","chinese":"一個字詞"},{"english":"create suspense","chinese":"製造懸念"},{"english":"make an idea memorable","chinese":"令一個想法令人難忘"},{"english":"English speaking exams","chinese":"英文口試"},{"english":"debate competitions","chinese":"辯論比賽"},{"english":"class presentations","chinese":"課堂匯報"},{"english":"speak with timing","chinese":"說話有節奏和時機"},{"english":"audience awareness","chinese":"觀眾意識"},{"english":"simply memorises","chinese":"只是背誦"},{"english":"impressive vocabulary","chinese":"令人印象深刻的詞彙"},{"english":"teaches us to think","chinese":"教我們思考"},{"english":"a familiar situation","chinese":"熟悉的情境"},{"english":"an unexpected truth","chinese":"意想不到的真相"},{"english":"in other words","chinese":"換言之"},{"english":"encourages us to question","chinese":"鼓勵我們質疑"},{"english":"accept without thinking","chinese":"不假思索地接受"},{"english":"builds empathy","chinese":"建立同理心"},{"english":"awkward friendships","chinese":"尷尬的友誼"},{"english":"admitting that","chinese":"承認"},{"english":"share the same worries","chinese":"有相同的憂慮"},{"english":"most importantly","chinese":"最重要的是"},{"english":"school life","chinese":"校園生活"},{"english":"an escape from reality","chinese":"逃避現實"},{"english":"facing reality together","chinese":"一起面對現實"},{"english":"invite local comedians","chinese":"邀請本地棟篤笑演員"},{"english":"organise student comedy workshops","chinese":"舉辦學生喜劇工作坊"},{"english":"humorous speeches","chinese":"幽默演講"},{"english":"English activities","chinese":"英文活動"},{"english":"laugh thoughtfully","chinese":"有思考地笑"},{"english":"speak bravely","chinese":"勇敢地說話"},{"english":"listen generously","chinese":"慷慨地聆聽"},{"english":"not only…but also…","chinese":"不但……而且……"},{"english":"better English users","chinese":"更好的英文使用者"},{"english":"kinder classmates","chinese":"更友善的同學"},{"english":"lasted just over an hour","chinese":"持續剛超過一小時"},{"english":"still echoing in my mind","chinese":"仍在我腦海中迴響"},{"english":"the shortest distance between people","chinese":"人與人之間最短的距離"},{"english":"a punchline","chinese":"笑點；妙語結尾"}]},"dse-writing-2014-part-b-q8":{"exerciseId":"dse-writing-2014-part-b-q8","essayKey":"","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=dse-writing-2014-part-b-q8","flashDeckId":"dse/writing/part-b/2014/Q8","paragraphs":[{"label":"Paragraph 1","english":"More Than a Voice: What the Poetry Festival Taught Me","chinese":"不只是一把聲音：詩歌節教會我的事"},{"label":"Paragraph 2","english":"When our English teacher invited us to join the Hong Kong Schools Poetry Festival, I first saw it as another activity to squeeze into an already crowded term. With tests approaching and club duties piling up, entering a poetry competition felt ambitious, if not slightly reckless. For context, our school has always encouraged students to step beyond examination routines; this opportunity made me consider preparing seriously so that I could represent the school with confidence and discover what a poem can become when lifted from the page. Looking back, I would go so far as to say that the Festival was not merely a contest of pronunciation, but a lesson in discipline, interpretation and courage.","chinese":"當我們的英文老師邀請我們參加香港學校詩歌節時，我起初只把它看成另一項要硬塞進本已排得滿滿的學期中的活動。 隨著測驗臨近，社團職責也越積越多，參加詩歌比賽顯得頗有雄心，甚至可說有點魯莽。 補充背景來說，我們學校一直鼓勵學生走出考試常規；這次機會令我開始認真考慮備賽，好讓自己能有信心地代表學校，並發現一首詩從紙頁上被帶到聲音之中後，可以成為甚麼。 回望過去，我甚至會說，這個詩歌節不只是一場發音比賽，更是一堂關於紀律、詮釋與勇氣的課。"},{"label":"Paragraph 3","english":"My preparation began with choosing a poem that looked deceptively simple. At first glance, it seemed to require only clear reading and accurate memorisation; on closer inspection, every pause, stress and image carried meaning. Miss Chan asked me three questions: Who is speaking? To whom? What changes from the first line to the last? Only after I tried to answer them did I realise that reciting a poem is not about decorating words with emotion. It is about understanding why the emotion is there. I annotated the poem line by line, underlining key verbs, circling turning points and marking where the voice should soften, rise or fall. One stanza sounded confident; another, uncertain; the ending, quiet but firm. Slowly but surely, a printed page began to take shape as a living voice.","chinese":"我的準備工作由選擇一首看似簡單卻暗藏難度的詩開始。 乍看之下，它似乎只需要清晰朗讀和準確背誦；仔細一看，每個停頓、重音和意象都承載著意義。 陳老師問了我三個問題：誰在說話？說給誰聽？從第一行到最後一行，有甚麼變化？ 只有在我嘗試回答這些問題之後，我才明白，朗誦詩歌並非給文字加上情感裝飾。 重點在於理解那份情感為何存在。 我逐行為詩作註記，劃下關鍵動詞，圈出轉折位置，並標記聲音應在哪裡放柔、提高或下降。 其中一節聽起來自信；另一節則帶著猶疑；結尾安靜，卻堅定。 緩慢但穩定地，一頁印刷文字逐漸成形，變成一把活生生的聲音。"},{"label":"Paragraph 4","english":"The technical training was just as demanding. Every afternoon for three weeks, I spent twenty minutes practising in an empty classroom, using my phone to record myself and a chair at the back as my imaginary adjudicator. The first recording was painful to hear - I rushed through commas, swallowed final consonants and stared at the floor as if the audience were my enemy. Instead of giving up, I broke the poem into smaller units. I practised breathing before long sentences, projecting vowels without shouting, and pausing before important words rather than after every line. Better still, my classmates became a mock audience. They noted that my hands moved too much, that my pace was uneven and that one emotional line sounded forced. Much as their comments embarrassed me, they made the performance more honest.","chinese":"技巧訓練同樣要求很高。 連續三個星期，每天下午我都會花二十分鐘在空課室練習，用手機錄下自己的聲音，並把後排的一張椅子當成想像中的評判。 第一次錄音令人不忍卒聽——我匆匆略過逗號，吞掉字尾輔音，又盯著地板，彷彿觀眾是我的敵人。 我沒有放棄，反而把詩拆成較小的部分。 我練習在長句之前換氣，在不叫喊的情況下把元音送出去，並在重要詞語之前停頓，而非每一行之後都停。 更理想的是，我的同學成了模擬觀眾。 他們指出我的手部動作太多，節奏不均，而且其中一句帶有情感的詩句聽起來有點刻意。 儘管他們的意見令我尷尬，這些回饋卻讓我的演繹變得更真誠。"},{"label":"Paragraph 5","english":"On the day of the competition, the atmosphere was unforgettable. Standing backstage among students from different schools, I could hear all sorts of voices - nervous whispers, repeated lines, sudden laughter and complete silence. No sooner had my number been called than my heartbeat seemed to fill the room. For what felt like forever, the microphone looked less like equipment than a test of character. Yet the moment I began, the weeks of preparation quietly took over. I remembered to breathe; I found the rhythm; I looked up. By the final stanza, I was no longer asking whether I would win. I was asking whether I had served the poem well.","chinese":"在比賽當天，氣氛令人難忘。 我站在後台，身旁是來自不同學校的學生，耳邊聽見各式各樣的聲音——緊張的低語、反覆默念的詩句、突如其來的笑聲，以及一片徹底的寂靜。 我的號碼才剛被叫到，我的心跳便彷彿充滿了整個房間。 在那段感覺漫長得像永遠的時間裡，麥克風看起來與其說是一件設備，不如說是一場品格的考驗。 然而，我一開始朗誦，那幾星期的準備便悄然接管一切。 我記得要呼吸；我找到了節奏；我抬起頭來。 到了最後一節，我不再問自己會不會贏。 我問的是，自己是否真正把這首詩演繹好。"},{"label":"Paragraph 6","english":"What I learned, therefore, went far beyond public speaking. First, preparation is not the enemy of creativity; rather, it is what gives creativity room to appear. Without repeated practice, inspiration remains a lucky accident. With preparation, however, even nervousness can be turned into energy. Second, poetry taught me empathy. To recite is to borrow another person’s voice responsibly. Whether the poem is humorous, sorrowful or reflective, the performer has to listen before being heard. Finally, I learned that confidence does not mean having no fear. Quite the contrary, it means standing tall while fear is still present.","chinese":"因此，我學到的東西遠遠超出公共演說本身。 首先，準備並非創意的敵人；更準確地說，它給予創意出現的空間。 沒有反覆練習，靈感仍然只是一場幸運的偶然。 然而，有了準備，甚至連緊張也可以轉化成能量。 第二，詩歌教會我同理心。 朗誦，就是負責任地借用另一個人的聲音。 無論詩作是幽默、悲傷還是帶有反思意味，表演者都須先聆聽，才能被聽見 最後，我明白到，自信並不等於毫無恐懼。 正正相反，它意味著在恐懼仍然存在時，依然能挺直站立。"},{"label":"Paragraph 7","english":"I did not bring home the champion’s trophy, but I brought back something more lasting - a better ear for language and a stronger belief in patient effort. If another Poetry Festival comes, I hope more schoolmates will join, not because prizes are guaranteed, but because the process itself can make us better listeners, speakers and thinkers. Our school should continue to make room for the arts. After all, a poem on paper may be quiet, but in the right voice, it can fill a room.","chinese":"我沒有把冠軍獎盃帶回家，但我帶回了一些更持久的東西——更敏銳的語感，以及對耐心努力更堅定的信念。 如果再有另一屆詩歌節，我希望更多同學會參加，並非因為獎項一定有保證；原因在於這個過程本身能讓我們成為更好的聆聽者、演說者和思考者。 我們學校應該繼續為藝術騰出空間。 畢竟，紙上的詩也許安靜；一旦遇上合適的聲音，它卻能填滿整個房間。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"more than a voice","chinese":"不只是一把聲音"},{"english":"taught me","chinese":"教會我"},{"english":"invite someone to join","chinese":"邀請某人參加"},{"english":"the Hong Kong Schools Poetry Festival","chinese":"香港學校詩歌節"},{"english":"see it as","chinese":"把它視為"},{"english":"squeeze into","chinese":"擠進；勉強安排進"},{"english":"an already crowded term","chinese":"已經很忙碌的學期"},{"english":"with tests approaching","chinese":"隨着測驗臨近"},{"english":"club duties piling up","chinese":"學會職務愈積愈多"},{"english":"entering a poetry competition","chinese":"參加詩歌比賽"},{"english":"felt ambitious","chinese":"感覺很有挑戰性"},{"english":"if not slightly reckless","chinese":"甚至有點魯莽"},{"english":"for context","chinese":"作為背景"},{"english":"step beyond","chinese":"走出……之外"},{"english":"examination routines","chinese":"考試常規"},{"english":"make me consider","chinese":"令我考慮"},{"english":"prepare seriously","chinese":"認真準備"},{"english":"represent the school","chinese":"代表學校"},{"english":"with confidence","chinese":"有信心地"},{"english":"discover what a poem can become","chinese":"探索一首詩可以變成甚麼"},{"english":"be lifted from the page","chinese":"從紙上被帶到現實中"},{"english":"looking back","chinese":"回望起來"},{"english":"go so far as to say","chinese":"甚至可以說"},{"english":"not merely a contest of pronunciation","chinese":"不只是發音比賽"},{"english":"a lesson in discipline","chinese":"一堂關於紀律的課"},{"english":"interpretation and courage","chinese":"演繹與勇氣"},{"english":"preparation began with","chinese":"準備由……開始"},{"english":"deceptively simple","chinese":"看似簡單但其實不然"},{"english":"at first glance","chinese":"乍看之下"},{"english":"clear reading","chinese":"清晰朗讀"},{"english":"accurate memorisation","chinese":"準確背誦"},{"english":"on closer inspection","chinese":"仔細看來"},{"english":"every pause, stress and image","chinese":"每個停頓、重音和意象"},{"english":"carry meaning","chinese":"承載意思"},{"english":"Who is speaking?","chinese":"誰在說話？"},{"english":"To whom?","chinese":"對誰說？"},{"english":"from the first line to the last","chinese":"從第一行到最後一行"},{"english":"only after…did I realise","chinese":"直到……之後我才明白"},{"english":"reciting a poem","chinese":"朗誦一首詩"},{"english":"not about decorating words with emotion","chinese":"不是用情感裝飾文字"},{"english":"understand why the emotion is there","chinese":"明白情感為何存在"},{"english":"annotate the poem line by line","chinese":"逐行註釋詩歌"},{"english":"underline key verbs","chinese":"在關鍵動詞下劃線"},{"english":"circle turning points","chinese":"圈出轉折點"},{"english":"mark where","chinese":"標記哪裏"},{"english":"soften, rise or fall","chinese":"放柔、提高或降低"},{"english":"sound confident","chinese":"聽起來自信"},{"english":"sound uncertain","chinese":"聽起來不確定"},{"english":"quiet but firm","chinese":"平靜但堅定"},{"english":"slowly but surely","chinese":"慢慢而穩定地"},{"english":"take shape as","chinese":"逐漸形成為"},{"english":"a living voice","chinese":"有生命力的聲音"},{"english":"technical training","chinese":"技術訓練"},{"english":"just as demanding","chinese":"同樣要求很高"},{"english":"every afternoon for three weeks","chinese":"連續三星期的每個下午"},{"english":"practise in an empty classroom","chinese":"在空課室練習"},{"english":"record myself","chinese":"錄下自己"},{"english":"imaginary adjudicator","chinese":"想像中的評判"},{"english":"painful to hear","chinese":"聽起來很難受"},{"english":"rush through commas","chinese":"匆匆讀過逗號"},{"english":"swallow final consonants","chinese":"吞掉字尾輔音"},{"english":"stare at the floor","chinese":"盯着地板"},{"english":"as if the audience were my enemy","chinese":"彷彿觀眾是我的敵人"},{"english":"instead of giving up","chinese":"而不是放棄"},{"english":"break something into smaller units","chinese":"把……分成較小部分"},{"english":"practise breathing","chinese":"練習呼吸"},{"english":"long sentences","chinese":"長句"},{"english":"project vowels without shouting","chinese":"不用大叫也能把元音發清楚"},{"english":"pause before important words","chinese":"在重要字詞前停頓"},{"english":"rather than after every line","chinese":"而不是每行之後"},{"english":"better still","chinese":"更好的是"},{"english":"a mock audience","chinese":"模擬觀眾"},{"english":"note that","chinese":"指出"},{"english":"move too much","chinese":"動得太多"},{"english":"pace was uneven","chinese":"速度不均"},{"english":"sound forced","chinese":"聽起來不自然；像硬擠出來"},{"english":"much as","chinese":"儘管"},{"english":"embarrass me","chinese":"令我尷尬"},{"english":"make the performance more honest","chinese":"令表演更真誠"},{"english":"on the day of the competition","chinese":"比賽當日"},{"english":"atmosphere was unforgettable","chinese":"氣氛令人難忘"},{"english":"standing backstage","chinese":"站在後台"},{"english":"among students from different schools","chinese":"在來自不同學校的學生之中"},{"english":"all sorts of voices","chinese":"各種各樣的聲音"},{"english":"nervous whispers","chinese":"緊張的低語"},{"english":"repeated lines","chinese":"反覆背誦的句子"},{"english":"sudden laughter","chinese":"突然的笑聲"},{"english":"complete silence","chinese":"一片沉默"},{"english":"no sooner had…than…","chinese":"一……就……"},{"english":"my number had been called","chinese":"我的號碼被叫到"},{"english":"heartbeat seemed to fill the room","chinese":"心跳聲彷彿充滿整個房間"},{"english":"for what felt like forever","chinese":"感覺像很久的一段時間"},{"english":"less like…than…","chinese":"與其說像……不如說像……"},{"english":"equipment","chinese":"設備"},{"english":"a test of character","chinese":"對性格的考驗"},{"english":"the moment I began","chinese":"我一開始的那一刻"},{"english":"take over","chinese":"接管；自然發揮作用"},{"english":"remember to breathe","chinese":"記得呼吸"},{"english":"find the rhythm","chinese":"找到節奏"},{"english":"look up","chinese":"抬頭看"},{"english":"by the final stanza","chinese":"到最後一節時"},{"english":"no longer asking whether","chinese":"不再問自己是否"},{"english":"serve the poem well","chinese":"好好演繹那首詩"},{"english":"go far beyond","chinese":"遠遠超出"},{"english":"public speaking","chinese":"公開演說"},{"english":"the enemy of creativity","chinese":"創意的敵人"},{"english":"give creativity room to appear","chinese":"給創意出現的空間"},{"english":"repeated practice","chinese":"反覆練習"},{"english":"inspiration remains a lucky accident","chinese":"靈感仍只是幸運的偶然"},{"english":"nervousness can be turned into energy","chinese":"緊張可以轉化為力量"},{"english":"turn into energy","chinese":"轉化為力量"},{"english":"teach me empathy","chinese":"教會我同理心"},{"english":"to recite is to","chinese":"朗誦就是去……"},{"english":"borrow another person's voice","chinese":"借用另一個人的聲音"},{"english":"responsibly","chinese":"負責任地"},{"english":"humorous, sorrowful or reflective","chinese":"幽默、悲傷或帶反思意味"},{"english":"listen before being heard","chinese":"在被聽見之前先聆聽"},{"english":"confidence does not mean","chinese":"自信並不代表"},{"english":"having no fear","chinese":"毫無恐懼"},{"english":"quite the contrary","chinese":"恰恰相反"},{"english":"stand tall","chinese":"昂首站立；保持自信"},{"english":"while fear is still present","chinese":"當恐懼仍然存在時"},{"english":"bring home the champion's trophy","chinese":"捧回冠軍獎盃"},{"english":"bring back something more lasting","chinese":"帶回更持久的東西"},{"english":"a better ear for language","chinese":"更敏銳的語感"},{"english":"a stronger belief in","chinese":"對……有更強信念"},{"english":"patient effort","chinese":"耐心努力"},{"english":"prizes are guaranteed","chinese":"獎項有保證"},{"english":"the process itself","chinese":"過程本身"},{"english":"make us better listeners, speakers and thinkers","chinese":"令我們成為更好的聆聽者、說話者和思考者"},{"english":"continue to make room for","chinese":"繼續為……騰出空間"},{"english":"the arts","chinese":"藝術"},{"english":"after all","chinese":"畢竟"},{"english":"a poem on paper","chinese":"紙上的詩"},{"english":"in the right voice","chinese":"以合適的聲音"},{"english":"fill a room","chinese":"充滿整個房間"}]},"dse-writing-2014-part-b-q9":{"exerciseId":"dse-writing-2014-part-b-q9","essayKey":"","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=dse-writing-2014-part-b-q9","flashDeckId":"dse/writing/part-b/2014/Q9","paragraphs":[{"label":"Paragraph 1","english":"The Last Bus Home","chinese":"末班車回家"},{"label":"Paragraph 2","english":"By the time I returned to Room 913, Chris’s bed had become a bare rectangle of sunlight. His posters were gone. His laundry basket was gone. Even the cracked cup he used for instant coffee and late-night noodles had disappeared. On my pillow lay his key card and a note in his neat handwriting: I’ve gone home. Keep the kettle.","chinese":"當我回到 913 房時，Chris 的床已經變成了一塊被陽光照着的空白長方形。 他的海報不見了。 他的洗衣籃不見了。 就連那隻他用來喝即溶咖啡、吃深夜杯麵的裂口杯子，也消失了。 我的枕頭上放着他的門卡，還有一張字跡工整的字條：我已經回家了。水壺你留着吧。"},{"label":"Paragraph 3","english":"No one on our floor saw Chris’s departure coming. He was the kind of roommate every first-year wanted - tidy, cheerful and generous with the last biscuit in the tin. During our first week in hall, he taught me how to stop the window from rattling during storms. He laughed at everyone’s terrible jokes. He once said that university life was “freedom with a timetable”.","chinese":"我們那一層樓沒有人預料到 Chris 會突然離開。 他是那種每個一年級生都想遇到的室友——整潔、開朗，還願意把罐中最後一塊餅乾分給別人。 入住宿舍的第一個星期，他教我怎樣在暴風雨時阻止窗戶喀喀作響。 每個人說了爛笑話，他都會笑。 他曾經說，大學生活就是「有時間表的自由」。"},{"label":"Paragraph 4","english":"Still, the signs had been there.","chinese":"可是，那些徵兆其實早已存在。"},{"label":"Paragraph 5","english":"It began with the phone calls. Every night, at around eleven, Chris would step into the corridor and speak in a voice so soft that it was almost not a voice at all. “No, Mum, I can come after class,” he would say. Or, “Tell Mary to do her homework first.” When I asked whether everything was fine, he smiled too quickly.","chinese":"一切是從那些電話開始的。 每天晚上大約十一點，Chris 都會走到走廊，用一種輕得幾乎稱不上聲音的聲線說話。 他會說：「不，媽媽，我下課後可以過來。」 又或者說：「叫 Mary 先做功課。」 當我問一切是否還好時，他笑得太快了。"},{"label":"Paragraph 6","english":"“Just family stuff,” he said.","chinese":"他說：「只是家裡的事。」"},{"label":"Paragraph 7","english":"The problem with “just family stuff” is that it can mean anything from a broken tap to a breaking heart.","chinese":"「只是家裡的事」的問題在於，這句話可以指水龍頭壞了，也可以指一顆心正在碎裂。"},{"label":"Paragraph 8","english":"Then there was the hotpot night. Our floor had squeezed two tables into the common room, and everyone was laughing too loudly over fish balls, cabbage and cheap beef slices. Someone knocked over a plate of food and groaned, “Never mind, we ordered too much anyway.”","chinese":"然後是那個火鍋之夜。 我們那層樓把兩張桌子硬塞進公共休息室，大家一邊吃着魚蛋、白菜和便宜牛肉片，一邊笑得太大聲。 有人撞翻了一碟食物，呻吟似地說：「不要緊，反正我們點太多了。」"},{"label":"Paragraph 9","english":"Chris froze. For a second, something hard moved across his face.","chinese":"有一秒鐘，一種僵硬的神情掠過他的臉。"},{"label":"Paragraph 10","english":"“Don’t waste it,” he said.","chinese":"他說：「不要浪費。」"},{"label":"Paragraph 11","english":"The room fell silent. He looked embarrassed at once, picked up the plate and muttered that he was tired. Later, I found him in the pantry, washing reusable takeaway boxes as if they were made of glass.","chinese":"整個房間安靜下來。 他立刻顯得尷尬，撿起那隻碟，低聲說自己累了。 後來，我在茶水間找到他，他正清洗可重用的外賣盒，彷彿那些盒子是玻璃造的一樣。"},{"label":"Paragraph 12","english":"“My family runs a small cha chaan teng,” he said at last. “My dad hurt his back last month. My mum opens the shop at six and closes after midnight. Mary is only sixteen. I stay here because Mum says I should study properly, but every night she calls because something has gone wrong.”","chinese":"他終於說：「我家經營一間小茶餐廳。」 「我爸爸上個月弄傷了背部。 我媽媽早上六點開舖，午夜後才收舖。 我留在這裡，是因為媽媽說我應該好好讀書；可是每天晚上她都打電話來，因為又有事情出錯了。」"},{"label":"Paragraph 13","english":"There was no getting around the fact that he had been living two lives - one in our hall, where people argued about laundry queues and tutorial readings; another at home, where every bowl of rice, every electricity bill and every tired customer mattered. All the while, he had been trying to make both lives fit into one exhausted body.","chinese":"有一個事實無法迴避：他一直過着兩種生活——一種在我們的宿舍裡，在那裡，人們為洗衣隊伍和導修閱讀材料爭論；另一種在家裡，在那裡，每一碗飯、每一張電費單、每一位疲憊的顧客都很重要。 在整個過程中，他一直試圖把兩種生活塞進一個疲憊的身體裡。"},{"label":"Paragraph 14","english":"The last straw came on a rainy Thursday. I was revising in bed when Chris’s phone rang. He listened for three seconds, then stood up so fast that his chair hit the wall.","chinese":"壓垮他的最後一根稻草，出現在一個下雨的星期四。 他聽了三秒，然後猛然站起來，快得椅子撞上了牆。"},{"label":"Paragraph 15","english":"“What happened?” I asked.","chinese":"我問：「發生甚麼事？」"},{"label":"Paragraph 16","english":"“Mum fainted at the shop.”","chinese":"「媽媽在店裡暈倒了。」"},{"label":"Paragraph 17","english":"We ran through the rain to the bus stop, sharing one umbrella badly. By the time we reached the restaurant, his sister was crying beside the cashier. His father, pale with pain, was apologising to customers. Steam clouded the windows. Orders were clipped above the stove like small white flags.","chinese":"我們冒雨跑到巴士站，兩個人笨拙地共用一把傘。 當我們到達餐廳時，他妹妹正站在收銀機旁哭。 他的父親因疼痛而臉色蒼白，正向顧客道歉。 蒸氣蒙住了窗戶。 一張張訂單夾在爐灶上方，像一面面小小的白旗。"},{"label":"Paragraph 18","english":"Chris did not hesitate. He took off his wet jacket, tied on an apron and stepped behind the counter. He chopped spring onions, carried bowls, wiped tables and comforted Mary between orders. I stood there uselessly until he handed me a cloth.","chinese":"他脫下濕透的外套，繫上圍裙，走到櫃檯後面。 他切葱、端碗、抹桌，還在一道道訂單之間安慰 Mary。 我像個沒用的人一樣站在那裡，直到他遞給我一塊布。"},{"label":"Paragraph 19","english":"“Wipe table three,” he said.","chinese":"他說：「抹三號桌。」"},{"label":"Paragraph 20","english":"So I did.","chinese":"於是我照做了。"},{"label":"Paragraph 21","english":"At three in the morning, we returned to hall. He sat on his bed without turning on the light.","chinese":"凌晨三點，我們回到宿舍。 他坐在床上，沒有開燈。"},{"label":"Paragraph 22","english":"“I’m leaving,” he said.","chinese":"他說：「我要走了。」"},{"label":"Paragraph 23","english":"“You mean tonight?”","chinese":"「你是說今晚？」"},{"label":"Paragraph 24","english":"“Tomorrow morning. I’ll commute from home. Maybe I’ll take fewer courses. I don’t know yet.”","chinese":"「明天早上。我會從家裡通勤。也許我會少修幾門課。我還不知道。」"},{"label":"Paragraph 25","english":"“That sudden?”","chinese":"「這麼突然？」"},{"label":"Paragraph 26","english":"He looked at me, not angrily, but sadly. “It only looks sudden if you haven’t been hearing the phone ring.”","chinese":"他看着我，沒有生氣，更多是難過。 「如果你一直沒有聽見那些電話響，它才會看起來突然。」"},{"label":"Paragraph 27","english":"I had no answer.","chinese":"我無言以對。"},{"label":"Paragraph 28","english":"Now his side of the room is empty, and the kettle he left behind whistles whenever the water boils, filling the room with a thin, lonely cry. I used to think people left because they had given up. Chris taught me otherwise. Sometimes people leave not because they no longer belong, but because someone elsewhere needs them more.","chinese":"現在，他那一邊的房間空了；他留下的水壺每次水滾時都會鳴響，讓房間充滿一種單薄而孤獨的哭聲。 我以前總以為，人們離開是因為他們已經放棄了。 有時候，人們離開，並非因為他們不再屬於那個地方；真正原因是，別處有人更需要他們。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"the last bus home","chinese":"回家的尾班車"},{"english":"by the time","chinese":"到……的時候"},{"english":"return to","chinese":"回到"},{"english":"a bare rectangle of sunlight","chinese":"一個空蕩蕩的陽光長方形"},{"english":"posters were gone","chinese":"海報不見了"},{"english":"laundry basket","chinese":"洗衣籃"},{"english":"cracked cup","chinese":"有裂痕的杯"},{"english":"instant coffee","chinese":"即溶咖啡"},{"english":"late-night noodles","chinese":"深夜杯麵"},{"english":"had disappeared","chinese":"已經消失"},{"english":"on my pillow lay","chinese":"在我的枕頭上放著"},{"english":"key card","chinese":"門卡"},{"english":"neat handwriting","chinese":"整齊的字跡"},{"english":"go home","chinese":"回家"},{"english":"keep the kettle","chinese":"留下水煲"},{"english":"see someone's departure coming","chinese":"預料到某人會離開"},{"english":"departure","chinese":"離開"},{"english":"the kind of roommate","chinese":"那種室友"},{"english":"first-year","chinese":"大學一年級學生"},{"english":"tidy, cheerful and generous","chinese":"整潔、開朗又慷慨"},{"english":"generous with","chinese":"對……很慷慨"},{"english":"the last biscuit in the tin","chinese":"罐裏最後一塊餅乾"},{"english":"during our first week","chinese":"在我們第一星期"},{"english":"in hall","chinese":"在宿舍"},{"english":"stop the window from rattling","chinese":"阻止窗戶發出震動聲"},{"english":"rattle during storms","chinese":"在暴風雨中咯咯作響"},{"english":"laugh at everyone's terrible jokes","chinese":"笑大家很爛的笑話"},{"english":"freedom with a timetable","chinese":"有時間表的自由"},{"english":"the signs had been there","chinese":"其實跡象早已存在"},{"english":"begin with","chinese":"由……開始"},{"english":"phone calls","chinese":"電話"},{"english":"at around eleven","chinese":"大約十一點"},{"english":"step into the corridor","chinese":"走到走廊"},{"english":"speak in a voice so soft that","chinese":"用非常輕的聲音說話，以致"},{"english":"almost not a voice at all","chinese":"幾乎不像聲音"},{"english":"come after class","chinese":"下課後過來"},{"english":"do her homework first","chinese":"先做功課"},{"english":"whether everything was fine","chinese":"是否一切安好"},{"english":"smile too quickly","chinese":"太快露出笑容"},{"english":"family stuff","chinese":"家裏的事"},{"english":"can mean anything from… to…","chinese":"可以指從……到……任何事"},{"english":"broken tap","chinese":"壞掉的水龍頭"},{"english":"breaking heart","chinese":"破碎的心"},{"english":"hotpot night","chinese":"火鍋夜"},{"english":"squeeze two tables into","chinese":"把兩張枱擠進"},{"english":"common room","chinese":"交誼廳"},{"english":"laugh too loudly","chinese":"笑得太大聲"},{"english":"fish balls","chinese":"魚蛋"},{"english":"cheap beef slices","chinese":"平價肥牛片"},{"english":"knock over","chinese":"撞跌；打翻"},{"english":"never mind","chinese":"不要緊"},{"english":"order too much","chinese":"點得太多"},{"english":"freeze","chinese":"呆住；僵住"},{"english":"for a second","chinese":"有一秒鐘"},{"english":"something hard moved across his face","chinese":"臉上閃過一種僵硬神情"},{"english":"don't waste it","chinese":"不要浪費"},{"english":"fall silent","chinese":"安靜下來"},{"english":"look embarrassed at once","chinese":"立刻顯得尷尬"},{"english":"pick up the plate","chinese":"拿起碟子"},{"english":"mutter","chinese":"低聲咕噥"},{"english":"pantry","chinese":"茶水間"},{"english":"reusable takeaway boxes","chinese":"可重用外賣盒"},{"english":"as if they were made of glass","chinese":"彷彿它們是玻璃造的"},{"english":"at last","chinese":"終於"},{"english":"run a small cha chaan teng","chinese":"經營一間小茶餐廳"},{"english":"hurt his back","chinese":"弄傷背部"},{"english":"open the shop","chinese":"開舖"},{"english":"close after midnight","chinese":"午夜後收舖"},{"english":"study properly","chinese":"好好讀書"},{"english":"something has gone wrong","chinese":"出了問題"},{"english":"there was no getting around the fact that","chinese":"無法迴避……這個事實"},{"english":"live two lives","chinese":"過著兩種生活"},{"english":"argue about","chinese":"為……爭論"},{"english":"laundry queues","chinese":"洗衣輪候隊伍"},{"english":"tutorial readings","chinese":"導修課閱讀材料"},{"english":"every bowl of rice","chinese":"每一碗飯"},{"english":"electricity bill","chinese":"電費單"},{"english":"tired customer","chinese":"疲倦的顧客"},{"english":"all the while","chinese":"與此同時"},{"english":"make both lives fit into","chinese":"將兩種生活塞進"},{"english":"exhausted body","chinese":"疲憊的身體"},{"english":"the last straw","chinese":"最後一擊；壓垮人的最後一根稻草"},{"english":"rainy Thursday","chinese":"下雨的星期四"},{"english":"revise in bed","chinese":"在床上溫習"},{"english":"phone rang","chinese":"電話響起"},{"english":"listen for three seconds","chinese":"聽了三秒鐘"},{"english":"stand up so fast that","chinese":"站起來快得……"},{"english":"chair hit the wall","chinese":"椅子撞到牆"},{"english":"faint at the shop","chinese":"在店裏暈倒"},{"english":"run through the rain","chinese":"冒雨跑過"},{"english":"bus stop","chinese":"巴士站"},{"english":"share one umbrella badly","chinese":"笨拙地共用一把傘"},{"english":"by the time we reached","chinese":"到我們到達……時"},{"english":"beside the cashier","chinese":"在收銀處旁邊"},{"english":"pale with pain","chinese":"痛得臉色蒼白"},{"english":"apologise to customers","chinese":"向顧客道歉"},{"english":"steam clouded the windows","chinese":"蒸氣令窗戶變得模糊"},{"english":"orders were clipped above the stove","chinese":"菜單夾在爐上方"},{"english":"above the stove","chinese":"在爐上方"},{"english":"like small white flags","chinese":"像一面面小白旗"},{"english":"did not hesitate","chinese":"毫不猶豫"},{"english":"take off his wet jacket","chinese":"脫下濕外套"},{"english":"tie on an apron","chinese":"繫上圍裙"},{"english":"step behind the counter","chinese":"走到櫃位後面"},{"english":"chop spring onions","chinese":"切蔥"},{"english":"carry bowls","chinese":"端碗"},{"english":"wipe tables","chinese":"抹枱"},{"english":"comfort someone between orders","chinese":"在處理訂單之間安慰某人"},{"english":"between orders","chinese":"在一道道訂單之間"},{"english":"stand there uselessly","chinese":"無助地站在那裏"},{"english":"hand someone a cloth","chinese":"遞給某人一塊布"},{"english":"table three","chinese":"三號枱"},{"english":"at three in the morning","chinese":"凌晨三點"},{"english":"without turning on the light","chinese":"沒有開燈"},{"english":"commute from home","chinese":"從家中通勤上學"},{"english":"take fewer courses","chinese":"修讀較少科目"},{"english":"that sudden","chinese":"那麼突然"},{"english":"not angrily, but sadly","chinese":"不是憤怒地，而是傷心地"},{"english":"it only looks sudden if","chinese":"只有在……時才看似突然"},{"english":"hear the phone ring","chinese":"聽見電話響"},{"english":"have no answer","chinese":"無言以對"},{"english":"his side of the room","chinese":"房間裏屬於他的那一邊"},{"english":"leave behind","chinese":"留下"},{"english":"whistle whenever","chinese":"每當……便發出聲響"},{"english":"water boils","chinese":"水煲滾"},{"english":"fill the room with","chinese":"令房間充滿"},{"english":"thin, lonely cry","chinese":"微弱而孤單的聲音"},{"english":"used to think","chinese":"以前以為"},{"english":"give up","chinese":"放棄"},{"english":"teach me otherwise","chinese":"令我明白並非如此"},{"english":"not because…, but because…","chinese":"不是因為……而是因為……"},{"english":"no longer belong","chinese":"不再屬於這裏"},{"english":"someone elsewhere","chinese":"別處的某個人"},{"english":"need them more","chinese":"更需要他們"}]},"dse-writing-2015-part-a-argument-against":{"exerciseId":"dse-writing-2015-part-a-argument-against","essayKey":"","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=dse-writing-2015-part-a-argument-against","flashDeckId":"dse/writing/part-a/2015","paragraphs":[{"label":"Salutation","english":"Dear Editor,","chinese":"編輯先生／女士："},{"label":"Introduction","english":"I am writing in response to the recent article in the Young Post suggesting that an 8:00 am start makes students tired and sleepy. As a secondary student, I agree that the early bell is part of the problem, but it is far from the whole story.","chinese":"本人寫信是為了回應《Young Post》最近一篇文章，該文章指出早上 8 時上課會令學生疲倦和昏昏欲睡。 作為一名中學生，我同意清晨的上課鐘聲是問題的一部分，但這遠遠不是全部原因。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"Many students are exhausted not because they are lazy, but because their day does not end when school ends. After lessons, they rush to tutorials, activities and revision. By the time their homework is finished, it may already be late. Long commutes make matters worse, as some classmates leave home before sunrise, so breakfast is rushed and sleep is cut short. Screen time is another quiet culprit. A phone beside the pillow can turn “five minutes” into an hour, leaving the brain awake when the body should be resting.","chinese":"許多學生感到疲憊，並不是因為他們懶惰，而是因為他們的一天並不會在放學時結束。 下課後，他們趕去補習、參與活動和溫習。 當他們完成家課時，時間可能已經很晚。 漫長的通勤令情況更加嚴重，因為有些同學在日出前已經離家，所以早餐吃得匆忙，睡眠時間也被縮短。 螢幕時間是另一個不易察覺的元兇。 放在枕頭旁的手機，可以把「五分鐘」變成一小時，令身體本應休息時，大腦卻仍然清醒。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"A 9:00 am start would certainly help. It would give students a more humane morning and allow many to gain precious extra sleep. However, it would not solve the problem by itself. If schools simply push lessons later but keep the same workload, students may only go home later and sleep no earlier.","chinese":"上午 9 時上課當然會有幫助。 這會給學生一個更人性化的早晨，並讓許多人獲得寶貴的額外睡眠。 然而，它本身並不能解決問題。 如果學校只是把課堂推遲，卻維持相同的功課量，學生可能只會更晚回家，而不會更早入睡。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"Therefore, schools should consider a later start together with lighter homework, better timetable planning and education on healthy digital habits. Sleep is not a luxury, but the foundation of learning.","chinese":"因此，學校應該在考慮較遲上課的同時，也減少功課量、改善時間表規劃，並教育學生建立健康的數碼習慣。 睡眠不是奢侈品，而是學習的基礎。"},{"label":"Sign-off","english":"Yours faithfully,","chinese":"此致"},{"label":"Signature","english":"Chris Wong","chinese":"Chris Wong"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"Dear Editor","chinese":"編輯先生／女士"},{"english":"write in response to","chinese":"寫信回應……"},{"english":"recent article","chinese":"最近的文章"},{"english":"suggest that","chinese":"指出；認為"},{"english":"starting school at 8:00 a.m.","chinese":"早上八時上課"},{"english":"leave students drained and unfocused","chinese":"令學生精疲力竭、難以集中精神"},{"english":"while it is true that","chinese":"雖然……是真的"},{"english":"half-asleep","chinese":"半睡半醒；未完全清醒"},{"english":"the roots of","chinese":"……的根源"},{"english":"exhaustion","chinese":"疲憊；精疲力竭"},{"english":"go far deeper than","chinese":"遠比……深層"},{"english":"early morning routine","chinese":"早晨作息；早上上學安排"},{"english":"face overwhelming schedules","chinese":"面對繁重得令人吃不消的日程"},{"english":"overwhelming","chinese":"壓倒性的；令人吃不消的"},{"english":"juggle","chinese":"同時應付"},{"english":"after-school activities","chinese":"課後活動"},{"english":"heavy homework loads","chinese":"繁重的功課量"},{"english":"part-time jobs","chinese":"兼職工作"},{"english":"force someone to","chinese":"迫使某人……"},{"english":"stay up late","chinese":"熬夜"},{"english":"reduce essential sleeping hours","chinese":"減少必要睡眠時間"},{"english":"essential sleeping hours","chinese":"必要睡眠時間"},{"english":"moreover","chinese":"此外"},{"english":"modern teenagers","chinese":"現代青少年"},{"english":"electronic devices","chinese":"電子裝置"},{"english":"disrupt natural circadian rhythms","chinese":"擾亂自然生理時鐘"},{"english":"circadian rhythms","chinese":"生理時鐘；晝夜節律"},{"english":"make it harder to","chinese":"令……更加困難"},{"english":"fall asleep","chinese":"入睡"},{"english":"at a reasonable time","chinese":"在合理時間"},{"english":"moving the start time to","chinese":"把開始時間改至……"},{"english":"provide valuable extra rest","chinese":"提供寶貴的額外休息"},{"english":"valuable extra rest","chinese":"寶貴的額外休息"},{"english":"by no means","chinese":"絕不是"},{"english":"cure-all solution","chinese":"萬靈丹式的解決方法"},{"english":"clash with","chinese":"與……衝突"},{"english":"parents' work schedules","chinese":"父母的工作時間表"},{"english":"push extracurriculars further into the evening","chinese":"把課外活動推遲至更晚時間"},{"english":"extracurriculars","chinese":"課外活動"},{"english":"potentially","chinese":"有可能"},{"english":"perpetuate","chinese":"使……持續下去"},{"english":"the cycle of sleep deprivation","chinese":"睡眠不足的惡性循環"},{"english":"sleep deprivation","chinese":"睡眠不足"},{"english":"what truly matters is","chinese":"真正重要的是"},{"english":"time-management skills","chinese":"時間管理技巧"},{"english":"promote a healthier lifestyle","chinese":"推廣更健康的生活方式"},{"english":"healthier lifestyle","chinese":"更健康的生活方式"},{"english":"such as","chinese":"例如"},{"english":"limit late-night screen time","chinese":"限制深夜使用電子屏幕的時間"},{"english":"late-night screen time","chinese":"深夜使用電子屏幕的時間"},{"english":"ultimately","chinese":"最終；歸根究底"},{"english":"address the issue of","chinese":"處理……問題"},{"english":"student tiredness","chinese":"學生疲倦問題"},{"english":"real progress demands","chinese":"真正進展需要……"},{"english":"holistic approach","chinese":"全面的方法"},{"english":"involve parents, schools, and students alike","chinese":"涉及家長、學校和學生各方"},{"english":"alike","chinese":"同樣地；都"},{"english":"Yours faithfully","chinese":"謹啟（正式信件結尾）"},{"english":"tired and sleepy","chinese":"疲倦和眼睏"},{"english":"as a secondary student","chinese":"作為一名中學生"},{"english":"the early bell","chinese":"早響的上課鐘"},{"english":"be part of the problem","chinese":"是問題的一部分"},{"english":"far from the whole story","chinese":"遠非問題的全部"},{"english":"be exhausted","chinese":"筋疲力盡"},{"english":"not because…, but because…","chinese":"不是因為……，而是因為……"},{"english":"their day does not end","chinese":"他們的一天並未結束"},{"english":"when school ends","chinese":"放學時"},{"english":"rush to","chinese":"匆忙趕去……"},{"english":"tutorials, activities and revision","chinese":"補習、活動和溫習"},{"english":"by the time","chinese":"到……的時候"},{"english":"homework is finished","chinese":"功課完成"},{"english":"it may already be late","chinese":"可能已經很晚"},{"english":"long commutes","chinese":"長途通勤"},{"english":"make matters worse","chinese":"令情況更糟"},{"english":"leave home before sunrise","chinese":"日出前離家"},{"english":"breakfast is rushed","chinese":"匆忙吃早餐"},{"english":"sleep is cut short","chinese":"睡眠時間被縮短"},{"english":"screen time","chinese":"使用電子屏幕的時間"},{"english":"a quiet culprit","chinese":"隱形元兇"},{"english":"beside the pillow","chinese":"放在枕邊"},{"english":"turn “five minutes” into an hour","chinese":"把「五分鐘」變成一小時"},{"english":"leave the brain awake","chinese":"令大腦保持清醒"},{"english":"when the body should be resting","chinese":"當身體本應休息時"},{"english":"would certainly help","chinese":"一定會有幫助"},{"english":"a more humane morning","chinese":"較人性化的早上安排"},{"english":"allow someone to","chinese":"讓某人能夠"},{"english":"gain precious extra sleep","chinese":"獲得寶貴的額外睡眠"},{"english":"solve the problem by itself","chinese":"單靠本身解決問題"},{"english":"push lessons later","chinese":"把課堂推遲"},{"english":"keep the same workload","chinese":"維持相同功課量"},{"english":"go home later","chinese":"更遲回家"},{"english":"sleep no earlier","chinese":"不會更早睡"},{"english":"therefore","chinese":"因此"},{"english":"consider a later start","chinese":"考慮較遲上課"},{"english":"together with","chinese":"連同；與……一起"},{"english":"lighter homework","chinese":"較少功課"},{"english":"better timetable planning","chinese":"更好的時間表規劃"},{"english":"education on healthy digital habits","chinese":"健康數碼習慣教育"},{"english":"healthy digital habits","chinese":"健康數碼習慣"},{"english":"not a luxury, but…","chinese":"不是奢侈品，而是……"},{"english":"the foundation of learning","chinese":"學習的基礎"}]},"dse-writing-2015-part-a-argument-for":{"exerciseId":"dse-writing-2015-part-a-argument-for","essayKey":"","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=dse-writing-2015-part-a-argument-for","flashDeckId":"dse/writing/part-a/2015","paragraphs":[{"label":"Salutation","english":"Dear Editor,","chinese":"編輯先生／女士："},{"label":"Introduction","english":"I am writing in response to the recent article suggesting that starting school at 8:00 a.m. leaves students drained and unfocused. While it is true that many teenagers arrive half-asleep, the roots of their exhaustion go far deeper than just an early morning routine.","chinese":"本人寫信是為了回應最近一篇文章，該文章指出早上 8 時上課會令學生精疲力竭、難以集中精神。 雖然許多青少年半睡半醒地到校確實是事實，但他們疲倦的根源遠不只是早上的作息安排。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"Firstly, most students face overwhelming schedules, juggling after-school activities, heavy homework loads, and even part-time jobs. This often forces them to stay up late, reducing essential sleeping hours. Moreover, modern teenagers frequently use electronic devices at night, which disrupts their natural circadian rhythms and makes it harder to fall asleep at a reasonable time.","chinese":"首先，大多數學生都面對令人吃不消的時間表，要同時應付課後活動、沉重的功課量，甚至兼職工作。 這往往迫使他們熬夜，從而減少必要的睡眠時間。 此外，現代青少年經常在晚上使用電子裝置，這會擾亂他們自然的生理時鐘，令他們更難在合理時間入睡。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"Although moving the start time to 9:00 a.m. may provide valuable extra rest, it is by no means a cure-all solution. A later start could clash with parents’ work schedules and push extracurriculars further into the evening, potentially perpetuating the cycle of sleep deprivation. What truly matters is teaching time-management skills and promoting a healthier lifestyle, such as limiting late-night screen time.","chinese":"雖然把上課時間延遲至上午 9 時，可能會提供寶貴的額外休息時間，但它絕不是萬能的解決方法。 較遲上課可能會與家長的工作時間表產生衝突，並把課外活動進一步推遲至晚上，從而可能延續睡眠不足的循環。 真正重要的是教授時間管理技巧，並推廣更健康的生活方式，例如限制深夜使用螢幕的時間。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"Ultimately, while a later school start can help address the issue of student tiredness, real progress demands a holistic approach, involving parents, schools, and students alike.","chinese":"最終，雖然較遲開始上課能夠幫助處理學生疲倦的問題，但真正的進展需要一個全面的方法，並讓家長、學校和學生共同參與。"},{"label":"Sign-off","english":"Yours faithfully,","chinese":"此致"},{"label":"Signature","english":"Chris Wong","chinese":"Chris Wong"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"Dear Editor","chinese":"編輯先生／女士"},{"english":"write in response to","chinese":"寫信回應……"},{"english":"recent article","chinese":"最近的文章"},{"english":"suggest that","chinese":"指出；認為"},{"english":"starting school at 8:00 a.m.","chinese":"早上八時上課"},{"english":"leave students drained and unfocused","chinese":"令學生精疲力竭、難以集中精神"},{"english":"while it is true that","chinese":"雖然……是真的"},{"english":"half-asleep","chinese":"半睡半醒；未完全清醒"},{"english":"the roots of","chinese":"……的根源"},{"english":"exhaustion","chinese":"疲憊；精疲力竭"},{"english":"go far deeper than","chinese":"遠比……深層"},{"english":"early morning routine","chinese":"早晨作息；早上上學安排"},{"english":"face overwhelming schedules","chinese":"面對繁重得令人吃不消的日程"},{"english":"overwhelming","chinese":"壓倒性的；令人吃不消的"},{"english":"juggle","chinese":"同時應付"},{"english":"after-school activities","chinese":"課後活動"},{"english":"heavy homework loads","chinese":"繁重的功課量"},{"english":"part-time jobs","chinese":"兼職工作"},{"english":"force someone to","chinese":"迫使某人……"},{"english":"stay up late","chinese":"熬夜"},{"english":"reduce essential sleeping hours","chinese":"減少必要睡眠時間"},{"english":"essential sleeping hours","chinese":"必要睡眠時間"},{"english":"moreover","chinese":"此外"},{"english":"modern teenagers","chinese":"現代青少年"},{"english":"electronic devices","chinese":"電子裝置"},{"english":"disrupt natural circadian rhythms","chinese":"擾亂自然生理時鐘"},{"english":"circadian rhythms","chinese":"生理時鐘；晝夜節律"},{"english":"make it harder to","chinese":"令……更加困難"},{"english":"fall asleep","chinese":"入睡"},{"english":"at a reasonable time","chinese":"在合理時間"},{"english":"moving the start time to","chinese":"把開始時間改至……"},{"english":"provide valuable extra rest","chinese":"提供寶貴的額外休息"},{"english":"valuable extra rest","chinese":"寶貴的額外休息"},{"english":"by no means","chinese":"絕不是"},{"english":"cure-all solution","chinese":"萬靈丹式的解決方法"},{"english":"clash with","chinese":"與……衝突"},{"english":"parents' work schedules","chinese":"父母的工作時間表"},{"english":"push extracurriculars further into the evening","chinese":"把課外活動推遲至更晚時間"},{"english":"extracurriculars","chinese":"課外活動"},{"english":"potentially","chinese":"有可能"},{"english":"perpetuate","chinese":"使……持續下去"},{"english":"the cycle of sleep deprivation","chinese":"睡眠不足的惡性循環"},{"english":"sleep deprivation","chinese":"睡眠不足"},{"english":"what truly matters is","chinese":"真正重要的是"},{"english":"time-management skills","chinese":"時間管理技巧"},{"english":"promote a healthier lifestyle","chinese":"推廣更健康的生活方式"},{"english":"healthier lifestyle","chinese":"更健康的生活方式"},{"english":"such as","chinese":"例如"},{"english":"limit late-night screen time","chinese":"限制深夜使用電子屏幕的時間"},{"english":"late-night screen time","chinese":"深夜使用電子屏幕的時間"},{"english":"ultimately","chinese":"最終；歸根究底"},{"english":"address the issue of","chinese":"處理……問題"},{"english":"student tiredness","chinese":"學生疲倦問題"},{"english":"real progress demands","chinese":"真正進展需要……"},{"english":"holistic approach","chinese":"全面的方法"},{"english":"involve parents, schools, and students alike","chinese":"涉及家長、學校和學生各方"},{"english":"alike","chinese":"同樣地；都"},{"english":"Yours faithfully","chinese":"謹啟（正式信件結尾）"},{"english":"tired and sleepy","chinese":"疲倦和眼睏"},{"english":"as a secondary student","chinese":"作為一名中學生"},{"english":"the early bell","chinese":"早響的上課鐘"},{"english":"be part of the problem","chinese":"是問題的一部分"},{"english":"far from the whole story","chinese":"遠非問題的全部"},{"english":"be exhausted","chinese":"筋疲力盡"},{"english":"not because…, but because…","chinese":"不是因為……，而是因為……"},{"english":"their day does not end","chinese":"他們的一天並未結束"},{"english":"when school ends","chinese":"放學時"},{"english":"rush to","chinese":"匆忙趕去……"},{"english":"tutorials, activities and revision","chinese":"補習、活動和溫習"},{"english":"by the time","chinese":"到……的時候"},{"english":"homework is finished","chinese":"功課完成"},{"english":"it may already be late","chinese":"可能已經很晚"},{"english":"long commutes","chinese":"長途通勤"},{"english":"make matters worse","chinese":"令情況更糟"},{"english":"leave home before sunrise","chinese":"日出前離家"},{"english":"breakfast is rushed","chinese":"匆忙吃早餐"},{"english":"sleep is cut short","chinese":"睡眠時間被縮短"},{"english":"screen time","chinese":"使用電子屏幕的時間"},{"english":"a quiet culprit","chinese":"隱形元兇"},{"english":"beside the pillow","chinese":"放在枕邊"},{"english":"turn “five minutes” into an hour","chinese":"把「五分鐘」變成一小時"},{"english":"leave the brain awake","chinese":"令大腦保持清醒"},{"english":"when the body should be resting","chinese":"當身體本應休息時"},{"english":"would certainly help","chinese":"一定會有幫助"},{"english":"a more humane morning","chinese":"較人性化的早上安排"},{"english":"allow someone to","chinese":"讓某人能夠"},{"english":"gain precious extra sleep","chinese":"獲得寶貴的額外睡眠"},{"english":"solve the problem by itself","chinese":"單靠本身解決問題"},{"english":"push lessons later","chinese":"把課堂推遲"},{"english":"keep the same workload","chinese":"維持相同功課量"},{"english":"go home later","chinese":"更遲回家"},{"english":"sleep no earlier","chinese":"不會更早睡"},{"english":"therefore","chinese":"因此"},{"english":"consider a later start","chinese":"考慮較遲上課"},{"english":"together with","chinese":"連同；與……一起"},{"english":"lighter homework","chinese":"較少功課"},{"english":"better timetable planning","chinese":"更好的時間表規劃"},{"english":"education on healthy digital habits","chinese":"健康數碼習慣教育"},{"english":"healthy digital habits","chinese":"健康數碼習慣"},{"english":"not a luxury, but…","chinese":"不是奢侈品，而是……"},{"english":"the foundation of learning","chinese":"學習的基礎"}]},"dse-writing-2015-part-b-q2":{"exerciseId":"dse-writing-2015-part-b-q2","essayKey":"","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=dse-writing-2015-part-b-q2","flashDeckId":"dse/writing/part-b/2015/Q2","paragraphs":[{"label":"Paragraph 1","english":"Revitalising PE Lessons: Giving Students a Reason to Move","chinese":"重振體育課：給學生一個動起來的理由"},{"label":"Paragraph 2","english":"Dear Ms Chan,","chinese":"尊敬的陳校長："},{"label":"Paragraph 3","english":"As chairperson of the Class Association, I am writing to reflect a concern raised repeatedly by my classmates - many of us feel disappointed with our present physical education lessons. This is not because we dislike exercise. Rather, PE, which should help students discover the joy of movement and develop healthy habits, has become predictable, narrow and, for some students, discouraging. With this in mind, I hope the school will consider refreshing the PE curriculum so that lessons can become more inclusive, varied and meaningful. In particular, I would like to explain why students are unhappy with the existing lessons and suggest two activities which, I believe, would be warmly welcomed.","chinese":"身為班會主席，我寫信是為了反映同學們多次提出的一項關注——我們當中許多人都對目前的體育課感到失望。 這並非因為我們不喜歡運動。 更準確地說，體育課本應幫助學生發現運動的樂趣並培養健康習慣，如今卻變得可預測、單一，而且對部分學生而言令人洩氣。 有見及此，我希望學校會考慮更新體育課程，讓課堂變得更具包容性、更多元，也更有意義。 具體而言，我想解釋學生為何對現有課堂感到不滿，並建議兩項我相信會受到同學歡迎的活動。"},{"label":"Paragraph 4","english":"To begin with, many classmates find current PE lessons uninteresting because the format seldom changes. More often than not, we move from warm-up drills to a familiar ball game, such as basketball, volleyball or badminton, and then repeat similar skills under time pressure. At first glance, this arrangement seems practical as the rules are known, the equipment is available and teachers can manage the class easily. On closer inspection, however, the lesson benefits mainly students who are already confident in those sports. Stronger players dominate the games, while quieter or less athletic students are left standing at the side, afraid of making mistakes in front of others. Some classmates have told me that they spend more time waiting for their turn than actually moving. Others feel that performing the same drills in front of the class makes PE feel more like a test than a break from academic pressure. It is therefore easy to see why students gradually lose motivation - when an activity offers little choice, little success and little room for personal improvement, enjoyment naturally disappears.","chinese":"首先，許多同學覺得現時的體育課並不有趣，原因是課堂形式甚少改變。 很多時候，我們會先做熱身訓練，接着轉到熟悉的球類活動，例如籃球、排球或羽毛球，然後在時間壓力下重複相似的技巧。 乍看之下，這種安排似乎實際可行，因為規則人人熟悉、器材現成，老師也能輕鬆管理課堂。 然而，仔細一看，課堂真正受惠者主要是那些本來已經對這些運動有信心的學生。 能力較強的學生主導比賽，較安靜或運動能力較弱的學生則只能站在一旁，害怕在別人面前犯錯。 有些同學告訴我，他們花在等待輪到自己的時間，比真正活動的時間還要多 另一些同學覺得，在全班面前做相同的訓練，令體育課更像一次測驗，少了一種從學業壓力中暫時喘息的感覺。 因此，我們很容易明白為甚麼學生會逐漸失去動力——當一項活動幾乎沒有選擇、很少成功感，也缺乏個人進步空間時，樂趣自然會消失。"},{"label":"Paragraph 5","english":"One activity I respectfully suggest is station-based fitness circuit training. In a typical lesson, the playground or hall could be divided into several stations, including skipping, agility ladders, resistance-band exercises, balance tasks and stretching. Students would work in small groups and rotate every few minutes. More importantly, each station could offer three levels: beginner, standard and challenge. That way, a student who is less fit can still participate safely, while a more athletic student can push himself or herself further. This activity would be preferred because it changes the focus of PE from comparison to personal progress. Instead of asking, “Who is the best player?”, students would ask, “Can I improve my own result from last week?” It would also allow everyone to stay active at the same time, thereby reducing long queues and embarrassment. For example, a student who dislikes competitive ball games might still enjoy recording how many skips he can complete in one minute. Such small, visible improvements would make PE feel achievable and rewarding.","chinese":"我謹此建議引入的一項活動，是分站式體能循環訓練。 在一堂典型課中，操場或禮堂可以分成幾個站點，包括跳繩、敏捷梯、彈力帶訓練、平衡任務和伸展。 學生會以小組形式進行活動，並每隔幾分鐘輪換一次。 更重要的是，每個站點都可以提供三個等級：初學級、標準級和挑戰級。 這樣一來，體能較弱的學生仍能安全參與，體能較佳的學生也可以進一步挑戰自己。 學生會更喜歡這項活動，因為它把體育課的焦點從互相比較轉向個人進步。 學生不再只問：「誰是最好的選手？」他們會改為問：「我能否比上星期的自己做得更好？」 它也能讓所有人同時保持活動，從而減少排隊時間和尷尬感。 例如，一位不喜歡競爭性球類運動的學生，仍可能享受記錄自己一分鐘能完成多少下跳繩的過程。 這些細小且看得見的進步，會令體育課變得更容易達成，也更有成就感。"},{"label":"Paragraph 6","english":"A second activity worth introducing is ultimate frisbee. Unlike some traditional team sports, ultimate frisbee is easy to learn, inexpensive to organise and suitable for mixed-ability groups. A class only needs a few discs, cones and an open space. Because the game involves passing, running into space and defending without heavy physical contact, it is safer and less intimidating than many highly competitive ball games. Students would prefer it because it gives different types of learners a meaningful role: fast runners can create space, careful thinkers can plan passes, and less aggressive students can still contribute through communication and positioning. Better still, ultimate frisbee encourages fair play, since players are expected to respect rules and resolve minor disputes calmly. In this sense, PE would not merely train our bodies; it would also teach cooperation, responsibility and sportsmanship.","chinese":"第二項值得引入的活動是極限飛盤。 有別於一些傳統團隊運動，極限飛盤容易學習、組織成本低，也適合能力不同的小組。 一班學生只需要幾個飛盤、標誌筒和一片空地。 由於這項運動涉及傳球、跑到空位和防守，卻沒有大量身體碰撞，所以它比許多高度競爭性的球類運動更安全，也較不令人卻步。 學生會更喜歡它，因為它給予不同類型的學習者有意義的角色：跑得快的同學可以製造空位，思考細密的同學可以策劃傳球，較不進取的同學仍可透過溝通和走位作出貢獻。 更理想的是，極限飛盤鼓勵公平競技，因為參加者需要尊重規則，並冷靜地處理細小爭議。 從這個意義上說，體育課不只會訓練我們的身體，也會教會我們合作、責任感和體育精神。"},{"label":"Paragraph 7","english":"To conclude, I sincerely hope the school will review our PE lessons, not because the existing programme has no value, but because there is considerable room for improvement. If the school could pilot fitness circuit training and ultimate frisbee once or twice a month, the Class Association would be willing to help collect student feedback afterwards. I believe these changes would make PE lessons more enjoyable, more inclusive and more effective in promoting lifelong exercise. I would be grateful if you could consider our views.","chinese":"總結而言，我誠懇希望學校能檢視我們的體育課；原因並非現有課程毫無價值，重點在於它仍有相當大的改善空間。 如果學校能每月試行一至兩次體能循環訓練和極限飛盤，班會願意在活動後協助收集學生意見。 我相信這些改變會令體育課更有趣、更具包容性，也更能有效推動學生養成終身運動的習慣。 如您能考慮我們的意見，我將不勝感激。"},{"label":"Paragraph 8","english":"Yours sincerely,","chinese":"謹上，"},{"label":"Paragraph 9","english":"Chris Wong","chinese":"Chris Wong"},{"label":"Paragraph 10","english":"Chairperson, Class Association","chinese":"班會主席"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"revitalising PE lessons","chinese":"振興體育課"},{"english":"give students a reason to move","chinese":"給學生一個活動身體的理由"},{"english":"chairperson of the Class Association","chinese":"班會主席"},{"english":"raise a concern","chinese":"提出關注"},{"english":"raised repeatedly by","chinese":"被反覆提出"},{"english":"feel disappointed with","chinese":"對……感到失望"},{"english":"present physical education lessons","chinese":"現時的體育課"},{"english":"this is not because...rather...","chinese":"這不是因為……而是……"},{"english":"discover the joy of movement","chinese":"發現活動身體的樂趣"},{"english":"develop healthy habits","chinese":"培養健康習慣"},{"english":"predictable, narrow and discouraging","chinese":"可預測、狹窄而令人氣餒"},{"english":"with this in mind","chinese":"有見及此"},{"english":"refresh the PE curriculum","chinese":"更新體育課程"},{"english":"more inclusive, varied and meaningful","chinese":"更共融、更多元、更有意義"},{"english":"in particular","chinese":"尤其是"},{"english":"existing lessons","chinese":"現有課堂"},{"english":"suggest two activities","chinese":"建議兩項活動"},{"english":"be warmly welcomed","chinese":"受到熱烈歡迎"},{"english":"to begin with","chinese":"首先"},{"english":"current PE lessons","chinese":"現時的體育課"},{"english":"the format seldom changes","chinese":"形式很少改變"},{"english":"more often than not","chinese":"多數情況下"},{"english":"warm-up drills","chinese":"熱身操練"},{"english":"familiar ball game","chinese":"熟悉的球類活動"},{"english":"repeat similar skills","chinese":"重複相似技巧"},{"english":"under time pressure","chinese":"在時間壓力下"},{"english":"at first glance","chinese":"乍看之下"},{"english":"practical arrangement","chinese":"實際可行的安排"},{"english":"the rules are known","chinese":"規則已為人熟悉"},{"english":"equipment is available","chinese":"器材可供使用"},{"english":"manage the class easily","chinese":"容易管理班級"},{"english":"on closer inspection","chinese":"仔細看來"},{"english":"benefit mainly","chinese":"主要令……受益"},{"english":"confident in those sports","chinese":"對那些運動有信心"},{"english":"dominate the games","chinese":"主導比賽"},{"english":"less athletic students","chinese":"運動能力較弱的學生"},{"english":"be left standing at the side","chinese":"被晾在一旁站着"},{"english":"afraid of making mistakes","chinese":"害怕犯錯"},{"english":"in front of others","chinese":"在其他人面前"},{"english":"spend more time...than...","chinese":"花更多時間……而不是……"},{"english":"waiting for their turn","chinese":"等候輪到自己"},{"english":"actually moving","chinese":"真正活動身體"},{"english":"performing the same drills","chinese":"做同樣的操練"},{"english":"feel more like a test than a break","chinese":"感覺更像測驗而不是休息"},{"english":"academic pressure","chinese":"學業壓力"},{"english":"it is therefore easy to see why","chinese":"因此很容易理解為何"},{"english":"gradually lose motivation","chinese":"逐漸失去動力"},{"english":"little room for personal improvement","chinese":"很少個人進步空間"},{"english":"enjoyment naturally disappears","chinese":"樂趣自然消失"},{"english":"respectfully suggest","chinese":"恭敬地建議"},{"english":"station-based fitness circuit training","chinese":"分站式體能循環訓練"},{"english":"in a typical lesson","chinese":"在一節典型課堂中"},{"english":"be divided into several stations","chinese":"被分成幾個訓練站"},{"english":"skipping","chinese":"跳繩"},{"english":"agility ladders","chinese":"敏捷梯"},{"english":"resistance-band exercises","chinese":"阻力帶練習"},{"english":"balance tasks","chinese":"平衡訓練"},{"english":"stretching","chinese":"伸展運動"},{"english":"work in small groups","chinese":"以小組形式活動"},{"english":"rotate every few minutes","chinese":"每隔幾分鐘輪換"},{"english":"offer three levels","chinese":"提供三個難度級別"},{"english":"beginner, standard and challenge","chinese":"初階、標準和挑戰"},{"english":"participate safely","chinese":"安全地參與"},{"english":"push oneself further","chinese":"進一步挑戰自己"},{"english":"change the focus from...to...","chinese":"把焦點由……轉為……"},{"english":"personal progress","chinese":"個人進步"},{"english":"instead of asking","chinese":"而不是問"},{"english":"improve my own result","chinese":"改善自己的成績"},{"english":"stay active at the same time","chinese":"同時保持活動"},{"english":"thereby reducing","chinese":"從而減少"},{"english":"long queues","chinese":"長長的人龍"},{"english":"embarrassment","chinese":"尷尬"},{"english":"competitive ball games","chinese":"競爭性球類活動"},{"english":"record how many skips","chinese":"記錄能跳多少次繩"},{"english":"complete in one minute","chinese":"在一分鐘內完成"},{"english":"small, visible improvements","chinese":"細小而看得見的進步"},{"english":"achievable and rewarding","chinese":"做得到而有滿足感"},{"english":"worth introducing","chinese":"值得引入"},{"english":"ultimate frisbee","chinese":"極限飛盤"},{"english":"unlike traditional team sports","chinese":"不像傳統團隊運動"},{"english":"easy to learn","chinese":"容易學習"},{"english":"inexpensive to organise","chinese":"籌辦成本低"},{"english":"suitable for mixed-ability groups","chinese":"適合能力混合的小組"},{"english":"a few discs, cones and an open space","chinese":"幾個飛盤、雪糕筒和一片空地"},{"english":"running into space","chinese":"跑到空位"},{"english":"heavy physical contact","chinese":"激烈身體碰撞"},{"english":"safer and less intimidating","chinese":"更安全、沒那麼令人卻步"},{"english":"highly competitive ball games","chinese":"高度競爭性的球類活動"},{"english":"different types of learners","chinese":"不同類型的學習者"},{"english":"meaningful role","chinese":"有意義的角色"},{"english":"fast runners","chinese":"跑得快的學生"},{"english":"create space","chinese":"拉開空位"},{"english":"careful thinkers","chinese":"思考細心的學生"},{"english":"plan passes","chinese":"計劃傳球"},{"english":"less aggressive students","chinese":"較不進取的學生"},{"english":"contribute through communication and positioning","chinese":"透過溝通和走位作出貢獻"},{"english":"better still","chinese":"更好的是"},{"english":"encourage fair play","chinese":"鼓勵公平競賽"},{"english":"be expected to","chinese":"被期望"},{"english":"respect rules","chinese":"尊重規則"},{"english":"resolve minor disputes calmly","chinese":"冷靜解決小爭議"},{"english":"in this sense","chinese":"從這個意義上說"},{"english":"not merely train our bodies","chinese":"不只是鍛鍊身體"},{"english":"teach cooperation, responsibility and sportsmanship","chinese":"教導合作、責任感和運動精神"},{"english":"to conclude","chinese":"總括而言"},{"english":"sincerely hope","chinese":"衷心希望"},{"english":"review our PE lessons","chinese":"檢討我們的體育課"},{"english":"existing programme","chinese":"現有課程"},{"english":"considerable room for improvement","chinese":"有相當大的改善空間"},{"english":"pilot fitness circuit training","chinese":"試行體能循環訓練"},{"english":"once or twice a month","chinese":"每月一至兩次"},{"english":"be willing to help","chinese":"願意協助"},{"english":"collect student feedback","chinese":"收集學生意見"},{"english":"make PE lessons more enjoyable","chinese":"令體育課更有趣"},{"english":"more inclusive and more effective","chinese":"更共融、更有效"},{"english":"promote lifelong exercise","chinese":"推廣終身運動"},{"english":"I would be grateful if","chinese":"如你能……我將不勝感激"},{"english":"consider our views","chinese":"考慮我們的意見"},{"english":"Yours sincerely","chinese":"謹啟"},{"english":"Chairperson, Class Association","chinese":"班會主席"}]},"dse-writing-2015-part-b-q3":{"exerciseId":"dse-writing-2015-part-b-q3","essayKey":"","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=dse-writing-2015-part-b-q3","flashDeckId":"dse/writing/part-b/2015/Q3","paragraphs":[{"label":"Paragraph 1","english":"The First Line","chinese":"第一句 「我們會從第一句開始。」"},{"label":"Paragraph 2","english":"Every afternoon, while the city hurried past, Mrs Lam sat beside the window of the Sham Shui Po Elderly Centre and stitched costumes for other people’s dreams.","chinese":"每天下午，當城市在窗外匆匆流過時，林太坐在深水埗長者中心的窗邊，縫製着屬於別人夢想的戲服。"},{"label":"Paragraph 3","english":"At seventy-six, she had the steady hands of a seamstress and the quiet eyes of someone who had spent a lifetime being useful. Hidden in her biscuit tin, however, was a faded photograph of a girl in embroidered sleeves, standing outside a Cantonese opera studio.","chinese":"七十六歲的她，有着裁縫師穩定的雙手，也有一雙安靜的眼睛，像一個花了一輩子讓自己派上用場的人。 然而，在她的餅乾鐵盒裡，藏着一張已經褪色的照片：照片中，一個穿着繡花水袖的女孩站在一間粵劇訓練室外。"},{"label":"Paragraph 4","english":"That girl had once wanted to sing.","chinese":"那個女孩曾經想唱戲。"},{"label":"Paragraph 5","english":"“Por Por, were you really going to be an opera star?” asked Jason, a Form Four student from the school drama club, when he found the photo while looking for buttons.","chinese":"「婆婆，你以前真的打算成為粵劇明星嗎？」學校戲劇學會的中四學生 Jason 在找鈕扣時發現了那張照片，便這樣問道。"},{"label":"Paragraph 6","english":"Mrs Lam snatched it back. “That was another life.”","chinese":"林太一把將照片搶了回來。 「那是另一段人生。」"},{"label":"Paragraph 7","english":"“Maybe it was unfinished,” he said.","chinese":"「也許那段人生還未完成。」他說。"},{"label":"Paragraph 8","english":"She laughed. Dreams, in her experience, belonged to luckier people. Her father had fallen ill; her brothers needed school fees; later came marriage, children and bills. By the time she was free, her knees hurt, her voice shook, and the world seemed too loud for old wishes.","chinese":"她笑了。 以她的經驗，夢想屬於運氣更好的人。 她父親病倒了；她的兄弟需要學費；後來接踵而來的，是婚姻、孩子和帳單 等到她終於有了自由，她的膝蓋已會疼痛，嗓音已會顫抖，而這個世界對那些陳年的願望來說，似乎太吵了。"},{"label":"Paragraph 9","english":"Still, every Wednesday, the students rehearsed at the centre. Their play was about the elderly realising their dreams, though none of them knew how an old woman might carry disappointment without showing it. Mrs Lam helped with props, corrected a line, and taught Jason how pride and regret could live in the same smile. Little by little, the play began to take shape.","chinese":"即使如此，每逢星期三，學生們仍會在中心排練。 他們的劇本講述長者實現夢想，然而他們之中沒有一個人懂得，一位老婦人可以如何把失望藏在身上，卻不讓人看見。 林太幫忙處理道具、修改一句台詞，也教 Jason 明白，驕傲與遺憾如何能同時住在同一個微笑裡。 一點一點地，這齣戲開始成形。"},{"label":"Paragraph 10","english":"One rainy evening, while sewing a phoenix robe, Mrs Lam forgot herself and sang a few lines from The Floral Princess. The room fell silent.","chinese":"一個下雨的傍晚，林太正在縫一件鳳袍，竟一時忘我，唱了幾句《帝女花》。 整個房間安靜了下來。"},{"label":"Paragraph 11","english":"“That voice,” Jason whispered, “is our ending.”","chinese":"「那把嗓音，」Jason 低聲說，「就是我們的結局。」"},{"label":"Paragraph 12","english":"“No,” she said. “I only sew.”","chinese":"「不，」她說。 「我只會縫。」"},{"label":"Paragraph 13","english":"“You don’t just sew,” he replied. “You remember.”","chinese":"「你不只是縫戲服，」他回答。 「你還記得。」"},{"label":"Paragraph 14","english":"For once in her life, Mrs Lam had no answer.","chinese":"人生中難得一次，林太答不上來。"},{"label":"Paragraph 15","english":"Practice was hard. She missed cues, lost breath, and once walked off because two boys were giggling. “They are laughing at my age,” she said.","chinese":"排練很艱難。 她錯過提示、氣息不足，還曾因為兩個男孩在竊笑而離場。 「他們在笑我的年紀。」她說。"},{"label":"Paragraph 16","english":"“Even if they were,” Jason replied, “stand your ground.”","chinese":"「即使真的是這樣，」Jason 回答，「也要站穩立場。」"},{"label":"Paragraph 17","english":"She wanted to quit. At one point, she folded the phoenix robe into a plastic bag and told herself enough was enough. But that night, she dreamed of the girl in the photograph. The girl did not accuse her. She simply stood under a paper moon and waited.","chinese":"她想放棄。 有那麼一刻，她把鳳袍摺進膠袋裡，告訴自己，這樣已經夠了。 可是那一晚，她夢見了照片中的女孩。 那個女孩沒有責怪她。 她只是站在一輪紙月亮下等待。"},{"label":"Paragraph 18","english":"Not until then did Mrs Lam understand: the dream was not applause or youth restored. It was permission—permission to take up space, to become visible, to finish a song she had been carrying for sixty years.","chinese":"直到那一刻，林太才明白：那個夢並非掌聲，也非重拾青春。 那是一種允許——允許她佔有一席之地，允許她被看見，也允許她唱完那首背負了六十年的歌。"},{"label":"Paragraph 19","english":"On the night of the performance, the hall was packed. Behind the curtain, Mrs Lam could hear her heart beating louder than the drums. Her grandson, who had once told her to “act normal” in public, sat in the third row, eyes fixed on his phone.","chinese":"演出當晚，禮堂座無虛席。 在布幕後，林太聽見自己的心跳比鼓聲還要響。 她的孫子曾經叫她在公眾場合「正常一點」，此刻坐在第三排，眼睛一直盯着手機。"},{"label":"Paragraph 20","english":"Then the music began.","chinese":"然後，音樂響起。"},{"label":"Paragraph 21","english":"At first, her voice was thin. A few notes wavered. Mrs Lam nearly looked down. Instead, she lifted her sleeve, drew a breath from somewhere deeper than fear, and sang—not as a young woman pretending life had been easy, but as an old woman who had survived it.","chinese":"一開始，她的聲音很單薄。 幾個音顫了一下。 林太差點低下頭。 相反，她抬起衣袖，從比恐懼更深的地方吸了一口氣，然後唱了起來——她並非以一名假裝人生輕易的年輕女子之姿歌唱；她以一位熬過人生的老婦人之姿歌唱。"},{"label":"Paragraph 22","english":"People stopped shifting in their seats. The elderly residents sat taller. Mrs Lam’s grandson slowly lowered his phone. By the final note, her voice had grown so steady that even the rain outside seemed to pause.","chinese":"人們停止在座位上挪動身子。 中心的長者坐得更直了。 林太的孫子慢慢放下手機。 唱到最後一個音時，她的聲音已變得如此穩定，連窗外的雨都彷彿停住了。"},{"label":"Paragraph 23","english":"For a second, there was silence. Then the hall rose.","chinese":"有一秒鐘，四周一片沉默。 然後，整個禮堂的人都站了起來。"},{"label":"Paragraph 24","english":"Mrs Lam bowed, and in that bow were all the years she had lost and all the years she still had. She was not young again. She was something better - herself, fully and fearlessly.","chinese":"林太鞠了一躬；那一躬裡，藏着她失去的所有歲月，也藏着她仍然擁有的所有歲月。 她沒有重返青春。 她成為了更好的存在——完整而無懼的自己。"},{"label":"Paragraph 25","english":"After the performance, her grandson ran to her with wet eyes.","chinese":"演出結束後，她的孫子眼眶濕潤地跑向她。"},{"label":"Paragraph 26","english":"“Por Por,” he said, “will you teach me that song?”","chinese":"「婆婆，」他說，「你可以教我那首歌嗎？」"},{"label":"Paragraph 27","english":"Mrs Lam looked at the phoenix robe beneath the stage lights. Slowly but surely, a smile crossed her face.","chinese":"林太望着舞台燈光下的鳳袍。 緩慢卻確定地，一抹微笑浮現在她臉上。"},{"label":"Paragraph 28","english":"“Come next Wednesday,” she said. “We will start with the first line.”","chinese":"第一句 「下個星期三來吧。」她說。 「我們會從第一句開始。」"},{"label":"Paragraph 29","english":"By the following month, the elderly centre had a new poster on its door:","chinese":"到了下一個月，長者中心的門上貼了一張新海報："},{"label":"Paragraph 30","english":"Cantonese Opera Workshop","chinese":"粵劇工作坊"},{"label":"Paragraph 31","english":"No audition. No age limit.","chinese":"毋須試音。 不設年齡限制。"},{"label":"Paragraph 32","english":"Dreams welcome.","chinese":"夢想，一律歡迎。"},{"label":"Paragraph 33","english":"For years, Mrs Lam had believed her chance had passed her by. No one saw what was coming - the woman who had spent her life sewing costumes had stepped into one of her own.","chinese":"多年來，林太一直相信，自己的機會早已從身邊溜走。 沒有人預料到接下來會發生甚麼——那個把一生都用來縫製戲服的女人，終於走進了屬於自己的一套戲服裡。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"the first line","chinese":"第一行；第一句"},{"english":"every afternoon","chinese":"每天下午"},{"english":"while the city hurried past","chinese":"當城市匆匆流過時"},{"english":"sat beside the window","chinese":"坐在窗邊"},{"english":"Sham Shui Po Elderly Centre","chinese":"深水埗長者中心"},{"english":"stitched costumes","chinese":"縫製戲服"},{"english":"other people's dreams","chinese":"別人的夢想"},{"english":"at seventy-six","chinese":"七十六歲時"},{"english":"steady hands","chinese":"穩定的雙手"},{"english":"seamstress","chinese":"女裁縫；縫紉師"},{"english":"quiet eyes","chinese":"沉靜的眼神"},{"english":"spent a lifetime being useful","chinese":"一生都在做個有用的人"},{"english":"hidden in her biscuit tin","chinese":"藏在她的餅乾罐裏"},{"english":"biscuit tin","chinese":"餅乾罐"},{"english":"faded photograph","chinese":"褪色照片"},{"english":"embroidered sleeves","chinese":"繡花衣袖"},{"english":"Cantonese opera studio","chinese":"粵劇戲棚；粵劇訓練室"},{"english":"had once wanted to","chinese":"曾經想要"},{"english":"Por Por","chinese":"婆婆"},{"english":"opera star","chinese":"粵劇明星"},{"english":"Form Four student","chinese":"中四學生"},{"english":"school drama club","chinese":"學校戲劇學會"},{"english":"looking for buttons","chinese":"尋找鈕扣時"},{"english":"snatched it back","chinese":"一把搶回來"},{"english":"another life","chinese":"另一段人生"},{"english":"unfinished","chinese":"未完成的"},{"english":"in her experience","chinese":"以她的經驗來說"},{"english":"belonged to luckier people","chinese":"屬於較幸運的人"},{"english":"fallen ill","chinese":"病倒"},{"english":"school fees","chinese":"學費"},{"english":"later came","chinese":"後來接踵而來的是"},{"english":"marriage, children and bills","chinese":"婚姻、子女和帳單"},{"english":"by the time","chinese":"到……的時候"},{"english":"her knees hurt","chinese":"她的膝蓋疼痛"},{"english":"her voice shook","chinese":"她的聲音顫抖"},{"english":"too loud for old wishes","chinese":"對昔日願望來說太嘈雜"},{"english":"still","chinese":"儘管如此"},{"english":"rehearsed at the centre","chinese":"在中心排練"},{"english":"the elderly","chinese":"長者"},{"english":"realising their dreams","chinese":"實現夢想"},{"english":"though none of them knew","chinese":"雖然他們沒有一個知道"},{"english":"carry disappointment","chinese":"承受失望"},{"english":"without showing it","chinese":"沒有表露出來"},{"english":"helped with props","chinese":"幫忙處理道具"},{"english":"props","chinese":"道具"},{"english":"corrected a line","chinese":"修改一句台詞"},{"english":"pride and regret","chinese":"驕傲與遺憾"},{"english":"live in the same smile","chinese":"同時存在於同一個笑容中"},{"english":"little by little","chinese":"一點一點地"},{"english":"take shape","chinese":"成形"},{"english":"rainy evening","chinese":"下雨的晚上"},{"english":"phoenix robe","chinese":"鳳袍"},{"english":"forgot herself","chinese":"忘我"},{"english":"sang a few lines from","chinese":"唱了幾句……"},{"english":"The Floral Princess","chinese":"《帝女花》"},{"english":"fell silent","chinese":"安靜下來"},{"english":"is our ending","chinese":"是我們的結尾"},{"english":"I only sew","chinese":"我只負責縫製"},{"english":"don't just","chinese":"不只是"},{"english":"for once in her life","chinese":"生平第一次"},{"english":"had no answer","chinese":"無言以對"},{"english":"practice was hard","chinese":"練習很艱難"},{"english":"missed cues","chinese":"錯過提示"},{"english":"lost breath","chinese":"喘不過氣；氣息不足"},{"english":"walked off","chinese":"離場；走開"},{"english":"were giggling","chinese":"在咯咯地笑"},{"english":"laughing at my age","chinese":"嘲笑我的年紀"},{"english":"even if they were","chinese":"即使他們真的是"},{"english":"stand your ground","chinese":"堅持立場；不要退縮"},{"english":"wanted to quit","chinese":"想放棄"},{"english":"at one point","chinese":"有一刻"},{"english":"folded something into","chinese":"把……摺進"},{"english":"plastic bag","chinese":"膠袋"},{"english":"enough was enough","chinese":"夠了；到此為止"},{"english":"dreamed of","chinese":"夢見"},{"english":"accuse her","chinese":"指責她"},{"english":"under a paper moon","chinese":"在紙月亮下"},{"english":"not until then did","chinese":"直到那時才"},{"english":"applause","chinese":"掌聲"},{"english":"youth restored","chinese":"青春復還"},{"english":"permission to","chinese":"去……的許可"},{"english":"take up space","chinese":"佔有自己的位置"},{"english":"become visible","chinese":"變得被看見"},{"english":"finish a song","chinese":"唱完一首歌"},{"english":"had been carrying for sixty years","chinese":"已經背負了六十年"},{"english":"on the night of the performance","chinese":"演出當晚"},{"english":"the hall was packed","chinese":"禮堂坐滿了人"},{"english":"behind the curtain","chinese":"在布幕後"},{"english":"heart beating louder than the drums","chinese":"心跳聲比鼓聲更響"},{"english":"drums","chinese":"鼓"},{"english":"act normal","chinese":"表現正常"},{"english":"in public","chinese":"在公眾場合"},{"english":"third row","chinese":"第三排"},{"english":"eyes fixed on","chinese":"眼睛盯着"},{"english":"at first","chinese":"起初"},{"english":"voice was thin","chinese":"聲音單薄"},{"english":"notes wavered","chinese":"音符顫動；走音不穩"},{"english":"nearly looked down","chinese":"差點低頭"},{"english":"instead","chinese":"反而"},{"english":"lifted her sleeve","chinese":"抬起衣袖"},{"english":"drew a breath","chinese":"吸了一口氣"},{"english":"deeper than fear","chinese":"比恐懼更深處"},{"english":"not as…, but as…","chinese":"不是以……而是以……"},{"english":"pretending life had been easy","chinese":"假裝人生一直容易"},{"english":"had survived it","chinese":"熬過了它"},{"english":"shifting in their seats","chinese":"在座位上坐立不安"},{"english":"sat taller","chinese":"坐得更挺直"},{"english":"lowered his phone","chinese":"放下電話"},{"english":"by the final note","chinese":"到最後一個音符時"},{"english":"grown so steady that","chinese":"變得如此穩定以致"},{"english":"seemed to pause","chinese":"似乎停了下來"},{"english":"for a second","chinese":"有一秒"},{"english":"the hall rose","chinese":"全場站起來"},{"english":"bowed","chinese":"鞠躬"},{"english":"in that bow","chinese":"在那一鞠躬之中"},{"english":"the years she had lost","chinese":"她失去的歲月"},{"english":"the years she still had","chinese":"她仍然擁有的歲月"},{"english":"not young again","chinese":"並非再次年輕"},{"english":"something better","chinese":"更好的東西；更珍貴的狀態"},{"english":"fully and fearlessly","chinese":"完整而無懼地"},{"english":"after the performance","chinese":"演出後"},{"english":"wet eyes","chinese":"眼泛淚光"},{"english":"beneath the stage lights","chinese":"在舞台燈光下"},{"english":"slowly but surely","chinese":"慢慢但確定地"},{"english":"a smile crossed her face","chinese":"笑容在她臉上浮現"},{"english":"come next Wednesday","chinese":"下星期三來"},{"english":"start with","chinese":"從……開始"},{"english":"by the following month","chinese":"到了下個月"},{"english":"on its door","chinese":"在門上"},{"english":"Cantonese Opera Workshop","chinese":"粵劇工作坊"},{"english":"no audition","chinese":"毋須試音"},{"english":"no age limit","chinese":"不設年齡限制"},{"english":"dreams welcome","chinese":"歡迎帶着夢想前來"},{"english":"for years","chinese":"多年來"},{"english":"her chance had passed her by","chinese":"她的機會已經錯過"},{"english":"no one saw what was coming","chinese":"沒有人預料到接下來的事"},{"english":"spent her life sewing costumes","chinese":"一生都在縫製戲服"},{"english":"stepped into one of her own","chinese":"走進屬於自己的夢想；穿上自己的人生戲服"}]},"dse-writing-2015-part-b-q4":{"exerciseId":"dse-writing-2015-part-b-q4","essayKey":"","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=dse-writing-2015-part-b-q4","flashDeckId":"dse/writing/part-b/2015/Q4","paragraphs":[{"label":"Paragraph 1","english":"When Classrooms Cross Borders","chinese":"當課室跨越國界"},{"label":"Paragraph 2","english":"At Hong Kong International Airport, it is no longer unusual to see a twelve-year-old student pulling a suitcase larger than himself, smiling bravely while his parents try not to cry. This quiet scene reflects a growing educational trend. Against the background of intense academic competition, many Hong Kong parents are considering overseas schooling so that their children can gain broader opportunities, develop independence and escape a system they regard as too narrow. This article examines two major reasons behind this phenomenon and considers its impact on local schools and on the children who leave.","chinese":"在香港國際機場，看見一名十二歲學生拉着比自己還大的行李箱、勇敢地微笑，而他的父母卻努力忍住眼淚，已不再是罕見的畫面。 這個安靜的場景，反映出一股日漸明顯的教育趨勢。 在激烈學業競爭的背景下，許多香港家長正考慮讓子女到海外升學，好讓他們能獲得更廣闊的機會、培養獨立能力，並離開一個他們認為過於狹窄的制度 本文將探討這種現象背後的兩個主要原因，並思考它對本地學校以及離港升學兒童所帶來的影響。"},{"label":"Paragraph 3","english":"The first reason is the pressure of Hong Kong’s examination-oriented culture. From primary-school dictations to public examinations, students are trained to perform under relentless assessment. Not that discipline is unimportant; rather, the problem is that education can become so focused on marks that curiosity is pushed to the margins. Many parents fear that their children are becoming excellent test-takers but exhausted learners. Overseas systems, especially those with coursework, projects and a wider choice of subjects, appear to offer a healthier balance between achievement and personal growth. Take a student who loves drama, environmental science or design technology, for example. In Hong Kong, such interests may be squeezed in after tutorial classes. In some overseas schools, by contrast, they can become proper academic pathways. It is therefore easy to see why parents regard foreign schooling as a way to protect both results and enthusiasm.","chinese":"第一個原因，是香港以考試為中心的文化所帶來的壓力。 從小學默書到公開考試，學生一直被訓練在無休止的評估之下表現自己。 這並非說紀律不重要；更準確地說，問題在於教育有時會過度集中於分數，以至於好奇心被推到邊緣位置。 許多家長擔心，自己的子女正成為優秀的應試者，卻同時成為疲憊的學習者 海外制度，尤其是那些包含課程作業、專題研習以及更廣泛科目選擇的制度，似乎能在學業成就與個人成長之間提供更健康的平衡。 以一名熱愛戲劇、環境科學或設計科技的學生為例。 在香港，這些興趣可能只能被勉強塞進補習課之後的時間。 相比之下，在一些海外學校裡，這些興趣可以發展成正式的學術路徑。 因此，我們不難理解，為何家長會把海外升學視為同時保護成績與學習熱情的一種方法。"},{"label":"Paragraph 4","english":"Another reason is the desire for global exposure. With families becoming more outward-looking, many parents want their children to master English, understand different cultures and prepare for university life abroad. Education is not just about passing examinations; it is about learning how to think, speak and live among people whose assumptions are different from one’s own. A teenager studying in Canada, Britain or Australia may have to debate in class, cook simple meals, manage pocket money and solve problems without immediately asking parents for help. These experiences can make students more confident and adaptable. Moreover, overseas schooling may help them enter foreign universities more smoothly, since they are already used to the teaching style and campus culture. For such families, sending a child abroad is not so much an escape from Hong Kong as an investment in mobility.","chinese":"另一個原因，是家長希望子女獲得國際視野。 隨着家庭變得更加放眼世界，許多家長希望子女掌握英語、理解不同文化，並為海外大學生活作好準備。 教育不只是關於通過考試；它更關乎學習如何在觀念與自己不同的人群之中思考、說話和生活。 一名在加拿大、英國或澳洲讀書的青少年，可能需要在課堂上辯論、煮簡單的飯菜、管理零用錢，並在不立刻向父母求助的情況下自行解決問題。 這些經歷能使學生變得更加自信，也更能適應不同環境。 此外，海外中學教育也可能幫助他們更順利地升讀外國大學，因為他們已經習慣當地的教學模式和校園文化。 對這些家庭而言，把子女送到海外，與其說是逃離香港，不如說是對未來流動能力的一種投資。"},{"label":"Paragraph 5","english":"However, this trend has a real impact on local schools. When more students leave, schools may lose not only enrolment numbers but also diversity of talent. A student who might have led the debate team, strengthened the orchestra or raised the standard of classroom discussion may suddenly disappear from the community. If the outflow becomes significant, some schools may face smaller senior forms, fewer subject combinations and tighter resources. Nevertheless, the trend also serves as a warning. Local schools are being reminded that reputation alone is no longer enough. They may need to provide stronger counselling, more flexible curricula, better mental-health support and learning experiences that connect Hong Kong students with the wider world. In that sense, the departure of some students could push local education to improve for those who remain.","chinese":"然而，這股趨勢確實會對本地學校造成實際影響。 當更多學生離開時，學校失去的不只是收生人數，也包括人才的多樣性。 一名原本可能帶領辯論隊、提升管弦樂團水平，或提高課堂討論質素的學生，可能突然從校園群體中消失。 如果學生外流變得明顯，一些學校可能會面對高中班級縮小、科目組合減少，以及資源更加緊絀的情況。 儘管如此，這股趨勢也像一個警號。 本地學校正被提醒，單靠聲譽已經不再足夠。 它們可能需要提供更有力的輔導支援、更靈活的課程、更完善的心理健康支援，以及能把香港學生與更廣闊世界連結起來的學習經歷。 從這個角度來看，部分學生的離開，反而可能推動本地教育為留下來的學生作出改善。"},{"label":"Paragraph 6","english":"For the children who leave, the impact is mixed. On the positive side, overseas study can be life-changing. Students may become more independent, more fluent in English and more open-minded. They may return with a broader view of success and a stronger ability to stand on their own feet. Yet the price of independence can be loneliness. A child who seems mature enough to board a plane may still be too young to handle homesickness, cultural misunderstanding or the pressure of justifying the family’s sacrifice. Some may feel caught between two worlds: not fully local in their new school, but gradually distant from friends back home. Social media can connect them, but it cannot replace a family dinner or the comfort of Cantonese conversation after a difficult day.","chinese":"對於離開香港升學的兒童而言，影響是好壞參半的。 從正面來看，海外升學可以改變人生。 學生可能會變得更加獨立、英語更加流利，也更加思想開放。 他們日後回來時，可能會帶着更廣闊的成功觀，以及更強的自立能力。 然而，獨立的代價可能是孤獨。 一個看似成熟到足以登上飛機的孩子，可能仍然太年幼，未必能承受思鄉之苦、文化誤解，或證明家人犧牲值得的壓力。 有些人可能會感到自己被夾在兩個世界之間：在新學校裡未能完全融入當地，與香港朋友之間的距離卻又逐漸拉遠。 社交媒體可以把他們連繫起來，但它無法取代一頓家庭晚餐，也無法取代艱難一天過後用廣東話交談所帶來的安慰。"},{"label":"Paragraph 7","english":"All things considered, the growing number of Hong Kong children studying overseas reflects parental hope and anxiety. Local schools should learn from the trend, while families must remember that overseas education is not a magic door to success. Only when children are prepared emotionally, not just academically, can a foreign classroom become a place of genuine growth.","chinese":"整體而言，越來越多香港兒童到海外升學，反映出家長的希望，也反映出他們的焦慮。 本地學校應該從這股趨勢中學習，而家庭也必須記住，海外教育並不是通往成功的魔法之門。 只有當孩子在情感上也準備好，而不只是學業上準備好，外國課室才可以成為真正成長的地方。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"when classrooms cross borders","chinese":"當課室跨越國界"},{"english":"Hong Kong International Airport","chinese":"香港國際機場"},{"english":"it is no longer unusual to","chinese":"……已不再罕見"},{"english":"a twelve-year-old student","chinese":"十二歲學生"},{"english":"pull a suitcase","chinese":"拉着行李箱"},{"english":"larger than himself","chinese":"比他自己還大"},{"english":"smile bravely","chinese":"勇敢地微笑"},{"english":"try not to cry","chinese":"努力不哭出來"},{"english":"this quiet scene reflects","chinese":"這個安靜場面反映"},{"english":"a growing educational trend","chinese":"日益增長的教育趨勢"},{"english":"against the background of","chinese":"在……背景下"},{"english":"intense academic competition","chinese":"激烈的學業競爭"},{"english":"considering overseas schooling","chinese":"考慮海外升學"},{"english":"gain broader opportunities","chinese":"獲得更廣闊的機會"},{"english":"develop independence","chinese":"培養獨立能力"},{"english":"escape a system","chinese":"逃離一個制度"},{"english":"regard as too narrow","chinese":"視為過於狹窄"},{"english":"this article examines","chinese":"本文探討"},{"english":"major reasons behind","chinese":"……背後的主要原因"},{"english":"this phenomenon","chinese":"這個現象"},{"english":"considers its impact on","chinese":"考慮其對……的影響"},{"english":"local schools","chinese":"本地學校"},{"english":"the children who leave","chinese":"離開的孩子"},{"english":"examination-oriented culture","chinese":"考試導向文化"},{"english":"from…to…","chinese":"由……到……"},{"english":"primary-school dictations","chinese":"小學默書"},{"english":"public examinations","chinese":"公開考試"},{"english":"be trained to","chinese":"被訓練去……"},{"english":"perform under","chinese":"在……下表現"},{"english":"relentless assessment","chinese":"持續不斷的評核"},{"english":"not that…","chinese":"這並不是說……"},{"english":"discipline","chinese":"紀律"},{"english":"become so focused on","chinese":"變得過於集中於……"},{"english":"marks","chinese":"分數"},{"english":"curiosity is pushed to the margins","chinese":"好奇心被推到邊緣"},{"english":"fear that","chinese":"擔心"},{"english":"excellent test-takers","chinese":"出色的應試者"},{"english":"exhausted learners","chinese":"疲憊的學習者"},{"english":"coursework","chinese":"課程習作"},{"english":"a wider choice of subjects","chinese":"更廣泛的科目選擇"},{"english":"appear to offer","chinese":"似乎提供"},{"english":"a healthier balance between","chinese":"……之間更健康的平衡"},{"english":"achievement","chinese":"成就"},{"english":"personal growth","chinese":"個人成長"},{"english":"take…for example","chinese":"以……為例"},{"english":"environmental science","chinese":"環境科學"},{"english":"design technology","chinese":"設計與科技"},{"english":"be squeezed in","chinese":"被勉強塞進時間表"},{"english":"tutorial classes","chinese":"補習班"},{"english":"by contrast","chinese":"相比之下"},{"english":"proper academic pathways","chinese":"正式的學術路徑"},{"english":"it is therefore easy to see why","chinese":"因此不難理解為甚麼"},{"english":"foreign schooling","chinese":"海外教育"},{"english":"a way to protect","chinese":"保護……的方法"},{"english":"results and enthusiasm","chinese":"成績和熱情"},{"english":"the desire for","chinese":"對……的渴望"},{"english":"global exposure","chinese":"國際視野；國際接觸"},{"english":"outward-looking","chinese":"具國際視野的"},{"english":"master English","chinese":"掌握英語"},{"english":"understand different cultures","chinese":"了解不同文化"},{"english":"prepare for university life abroad","chinese":"為海外大學生活作準備"},{"english":"not just about","chinese":"不只是關於"},{"english":"passing examinations","chinese":"通過考試"},{"english":"learn how to think","chinese":"學會思考"},{"english":"live among people","chinese":"與人共同生活"},{"english":"assumptions are different from","chinese":"想法與……不同"},{"english":"a teenager studying in","chinese":"在……讀書的青少年"},{"english":"debate in class","chinese":"在課堂上辯論"},{"english":"cook simple meals","chinese":"煮簡單飯菜"},{"english":"manage pocket money","chinese":"管理零用錢"},{"english":"solve problems","chinese":"解決問題"},{"english":"without immediately asking","chinese":"不立即請求……"},{"english":"make students more confident and adaptable","chinese":"令學生更自信和適應力更強"},{"english":"adaptable","chinese":"適應力強"},{"english":"moreover","chinese":"此外"},{"english":"enter foreign universities","chinese":"入讀外國大學"},{"english":"more smoothly","chinese":"更順利地"},{"english":"be used to","chinese":"習慣"},{"english":"teaching style","chinese":"教學模式"},{"english":"campus culture","chinese":"校園文化"},{"english":"for such families","chinese":"對這類家庭而言"},{"english":"sending a child abroad","chinese":"送孩子到海外"},{"english":"not so much…as…","chinese":"與其說是……不如說是……"},{"english":"an escape from Hong Kong","chinese":"逃離香港"},{"english":"an investment in mobility","chinese":"對流動力的投資"},{"english":"this trend has a real impact on","chinese":"這個趨勢對……有實際影響"},{"english":"enrolment numbers","chinese":"入學人數"},{"english":"diversity of talent","chinese":"人才多樣性"},{"english":"not only…but also…","chinese":"不但……而且……"},{"english":"might have led","chinese":"原本可能帶領"},{"english":"debate team","chinese":"辯論隊"},{"english":"strengthen the orchestra","chinese":"加強管弦樂團實力"},{"english":"raise the standard of","chinese":"提高……的水平"},{"english":"classroom discussion","chinese":"課堂討論"},{"english":"disappear from the community","chinese":"從社群中消失"},{"english":"if the outflow becomes significant","chinese":"如果外流變得明顯"},{"english":"outflow","chinese":"外流"},{"english":"smaller senior forms","chinese":"較小規模的高中級別"},{"english":"fewer subject combinations","chinese":"較少科目組合"},{"english":"tighter resources","chinese":"更緊絀的資源"},{"english":"nevertheless","chinese":"儘管如此"},{"english":"serve as a warning","chinese":"作為警號"},{"english":"be reminded that","chinese":"被提醒"},{"english":"reputation alone","chinese":"單靠聲譽"},{"english":"no longer enough","chinese":"不再足夠"},{"english":"stronger counselling","chinese":"更有力的輔導"},{"english":"flexible curricula","chinese":"更靈活的課程"},{"english":"mental-health support","chinese":"精神健康支援"},{"english":"learning experiences","chinese":"學習經歷"},{"english":"connect students with","chinese":"把學生連繫到……"},{"english":"the wider world","chinese":"更廣闊的世界"},{"english":"in that sense","chinese":"從這個意義上說"},{"english":"the departure of","chinese":"……的離開"},{"english":"push local education to improve","chinese":"推動本地教育改善"},{"english":"those who remain","chinese":"留下來的人"},{"english":"the impact is mixed","chinese":"影響有好有壞"},{"english":"on the positive side","chinese":"從正面來看"},{"english":"overseas study","chinese":"海外升學"},{"english":"life-changing","chinese":"改變人生的"},{"english":"fluent in English","chinese":"英語更流利"},{"english":"open-minded","chinese":"思想開明"},{"english":"return with","chinese":"帶着……回來"},{"english":"a broader view of success","chinese":"對成功更廣闊的看法"},{"english":"stand on their own feet","chinese":"自立"},{"english":"the price of independence","chinese":"獨立的代價"},{"english":"mature enough to","chinese":"成熟到足以……"},{"english":"board a plane","chinese":"登機"},{"english":"too young to handle","chinese":"太年幼而無法處理"},{"english":"homesickness","chinese":"思鄉"},{"english":"cultural misunderstanding","chinese":"文化誤解"},{"english":"justifying the family's sacrifice","chinese":"證明家人的犧牲值得"},{"english":"family's sacrifice","chinese":"家人的犧牲"},{"english":"caught between two worlds","chinese":"夾在兩個世界之間"},{"english":"not fully local","chinese":"未能完全融入當地"},{"english":"gradually distant from","chinese":"與……逐漸疏遠"},{"english":"friends back home","chinese":"家鄉的朋友"},{"english":"social media","chinese":"社交媒體"},{"english":"replace a family dinner","chinese":"取代一頓家庭晚飯"},{"english":"the comfort of","chinese":"……帶來的安慰"},{"english":"Cantonese conversation","chinese":"廣東話對話"},{"english":"after a difficult day","chinese":"在艱難的一天之後"},{"english":"all things considered","chinese":"總括而言"},{"english":"the growing number of","chinese":"越來越多的……"},{"english":"studying overseas","chinese":"到海外讀書"},{"english":"reflect parental hope and anxiety","chinese":"反映父母的希望與焦慮"},{"english":"learn from the trend","chinese":"從趨勢中學習"},{"english":"a magic door to success","chinese":"通往成功的魔法門"},{"english":"only when","chinese":"只有當……才"},{"english":"prepared emotionally","chinese":"情感上準備好"},{"english":"not just academically","chinese":"不只是學業上"},{"english":"a foreign classroom","chinese":"外國課室"},{"english":"genuine growth","chinese":"真正成長"}]},"dse-writing-2015-part-b-q5":{"exerciseId":"dse-writing-2015-part-b-q5","essayKey":"","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=dse-writing-2015-part-b-q5","flashDeckId":"dse/writing/part-b/2015/Q5","paragraphs":[{"label":"Paragraph 1","english":"A Harbour for All, Not a Commodity for Some","chinese":"全民共享的海港，並非少數人的商品"},{"label":"Paragraph 2","english":"Dear Editor,","chinese":"編輯先生／女士："},{"label":"Paragraph 3","english":"I am writing to express my strong support for leaving Hong Kong’s undeveloped harbourfront areas as open spaces for public use. Victoria Harbour is more than a strip of valuable land; in fact, it is the city’s breathing space, shared memory and public face. With land shortage and commercial pressure worsening, developers may be tempted to convert these sites into flats, offices and shopping malls so as to increase supply and revenue. As far as I am concerned, that would be a serious mistake. The remaining harbourfront should be protected because it promotes social fairness, improves urban well-being, and strengthens Hong Kong’s long-term appeal.","chinese":"本人來函，是為了表達我對將香港尚未發展的海濱地帶保留為供公眾使用的開放空間的堅定支持。 維多利亞港不只是一片有價值的土地；事實上，它是這座城市的喘息空間、共同記憶和公共面貌。 隨著土地短缺和商業壓力惡化，發展商可能會想把這些地點改建成住宅單位、辦公室和商場，以增加供應和收益。 就我而言，這將會是一個嚴重錯誤。 餘下的海濱應該受到保護，因為它能促進社會公平、改善城市福祉，並增強香港的長遠吸引力。"},{"label":"Paragraph 4","english":"First and foremost, an open harbourfront is one of the few public assets that belongs equally to everyone. Luxury flats and grade-A offices may look impressive, but they are accessible mainly to those who can afford them. By contrast, a promenade, a lawn or a sitting-out area can be used by a child from Sham Shui Po, an elderly couple from North Point and an office worker from Central without paying a cent. This distinction matters. In a city where private space is limited and daily life is crowded, public space is a form of everyday dignity instead of a decorative extra. Families can picnic, domestic helpers can rest on Sundays, teenagers can practise photography, and elderly residents can exercise while looking across the water. Only when waterfront land remains open, can ordinary citizens feel that the harbour is not being walled off by privilege. To turn such sites into private developments would be to replace a common good with a gated view. That runs counter to the spirit of a harbour city.","chinese":"首先，開放的海濱是少數真正平等地屬於每一個人的公共資產之一。 豪宅和甲級寫字樓看起來也許令人印象深刻，但主要只有負擔得起的人才能享用。 相比之下，一條海濱長廊、一片草地或一個休憩處，可以讓一個來自深水埗的孩子、一對來自北角的長者夫婦，以及一位來自中環的上班族一分錢也不用付便可使用。 這種分別十分重要。 在一座私人空間有限、日常生活擁擠的城市裡，公共空間是一種日常尊嚴，並非可有可無的裝飾品。 家庭可以野餐，外傭可以在星期日休息，青少年可以練習攝影，而年長居民也可以一邊望向海面，一邊做運動。 只有當海濱土地保持開放時，普通市民才會感到海港沒有被特權築牆隔開。 把這些地點改作私人發展，等於用只有門禁內才可享用的景觀取代共同利益 這違背了一座海港城市應有的精神。"},{"label":"Paragraph 5","english":"Moreover, open harbourfront areas make Hong Kong healthier, calmer and more liveable. The more densely a city is built, the more urgently it needs breathing room. Parks and promenades encourage walking, jogging, cycling and quiet conversation, thereby improving both physical and mental health. Take the existing promenades in Tsim Sha Tsui and Kwun Tong, for example: whenever people visit them, they are not merely exercising; they are escaping, even briefly, from traffic noise, concrete walls and workplace pressure. Green and open spaces also allow wind corridors, shade and vegetation to soften the urban heat that high-rise blocks can intensify. If the harbourfront is filled with towers, the result may be more floor area, but also more traffic, less airflow and a skyline that feels increasingly closed in. Rarely does a city get a chance to reserve land beside the sea. Once it is lost to permanent construction, it will be almost impossible to regain.","chinese":"此外，開放的海濱地帶能使香港更健康、更平靜，也更宜居。 一座城市建得越密集，就越迫切需要喘息空間。 公園和海濱長廊鼓勵人們散步、緩跑、踏單車和安靜交談，從而改善身心健康 以尖沙咀和觀塘現有的海濱長廊為例：每當人們到訪這些地方時，他們做的並不只是運動；即使只是短暫片刻，他們也是在逃離交通噪音、石屎牆和職場壓力。 綠化和開放空間也能提供通風廊、樹蔭和植被，以緩和高樓大廈可能加劇的城市熱力。 如果海濱被高樓填滿，結果也許會是更多樓面面積，但同時也會帶來更多交通、更少氣流，以及一條感覺越來越壓迫的天際線。 一座城市很少有機會把海邊土地保留下來。 一旦它被永久建築奪去，日後要重新取回幾乎不可能。"},{"label":"Paragraph 6","english":"Granted, Hong Kong needs more housing and economic activity. However, it does not follow that the harbourfront should be sacrificed for these purposes. Housing should be pursued through brownfield redevelopment, urban renewal, better use of idle sites and well-planned new development areas, not by consuming the most symbolically valuable edge of the city. Commercial use, too, can benefit from open public space. A beautiful waterfront attracts local visitors, tourists, cultural events, weekend markets, outdoor performances and small businesses in surrounding districts. In other words, leaving the harbourfront open is not anti-development; quite the contrary, it is a wiser kind of development. Cities such as Sydney and Singapore are admired not because every inch of waterfront is sold to the highest bidder, but because people can gather, walk, celebrate and remember who they are beside the water. All in all, what makes a city world-class is the quality of life it offers at street level, not simply the height of its buildings.","chinese":"誠然，香港需要更多房屋和經濟活動。 然而，這並不自然代表海濱就應該為這些目的而被犧牲。 房屋供應應透過棕地重建、市區更新、更妥善使用閒置土地，以及規劃完善的新發展區來推動，而非消耗這座城市最具象徵價值的邊緣地帶。 商業用途同樣可以受惠於開放的公共空間。 一個美麗的海濱能吸引本地訪客、遊客、文化活動、週末市集、戶外表演，以及周邊地區的小型商戶。 換言之，保留海濱開放並非反對發展；正好相反，這是一種更明智的發展方式 悉尼和新加坡等城市之所以受人欣賞，原因並非每一寸海濱都被賣給出價最高者；真正原因在於人們能夠在水邊聚集、散步、慶祝，並記起自己與城市的身份。 總括而言，令一座城市成為世界級城市的，是它在街道層面提供的生活質素，不僅僅是建築物的高度。"},{"label":"Paragraph 7","english":"For these reasons, I strongly believe that Hong Kong’s undeveloped harbourfront should be left as open space for public use. The Government, urban planners and district councils should design these areas with shaded walkways, barrier-free access, lawns, cultural facilities and family-friendly seating, while ensuring that no single commercial operator dominates them. Victoria Harbour has always been central to Hong Kong’s identity. Let us not treat it as merely another piece of land to be sold, leased or fenced off. The harbour should remain what it ought to be - a place where the whole city can breathe.","chinese":"基於以上原因，我堅定相信香港尚未發展的海濱應該保留為供公眾使用的開放空間。 政府、城市規劃師和區議會應該為這些地區設計遮蔭步道、無障礙通道、草地、文化設施和適合家庭使用的座椅，同時確保沒有單一商業經營者支配這些地方。 維多利亞港一直是香港身份的核心。 讓我們不要把它視作另一幅可供出售、出租或圍封的土地。 海港應該保持它本來應有的模樣——一個讓整座城市都能呼吸的地方。"},{"label":"Paragraph 8","english":"Yours faithfully,","chinese":"此致敬禮"},{"label":"Paragraph 9","english":"Chris Wong","chinese":"Chris Wong"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"for all, not for some","chinese":"為所有人而設，而非只屬於部分人"},{"english":"a commodity","chinese":"商品；可買賣的東西"},{"english":"Dear Editor","chinese":"尊敬的編輯"},{"english":"express my strong support for","chinese":"表達我對……的強烈支持"},{"english":"undeveloped harbourfront areas","chinese":"尚未發展的海濱地區"},{"english":"open spaces","chinese":"開放空間"},{"english":"public use","chinese":"公眾使用"},{"english":"Victoria Harbour","chinese":"維多利亞港"},{"english":"more than a strip of valuable land","chinese":"不只是一片有價值的土地"},{"english":"a strip of valuable land","chinese":"一幅有價值的土地"},{"english":"in fact","chinese":"事實上"},{"english":"breathing space","chinese":"透氣空間"},{"english":"shared memory","chinese":"共同記憶"},{"english":"public face","chinese":"公眾形象；城市門面"},{"english":"land shortage","chinese":"土地短缺"},{"english":"commercial pressure","chinese":"商業壓力"},{"english":"worsening","chinese":"惡化"},{"english":"be tempted to","chinese":"可能會忍不住想"},{"english":"convert these sites into","chinese":"把這些地點改建成"},{"english":"flats, offices and shopping malls","chinese":"住宅單位、辦公室和商場"},{"english":"so as to increase","chinese":"以增加"},{"english":"supply and revenue","chinese":"供應和收入"},{"english":"as far as I am concerned","chinese":"就我而言"},{"english":"a serious mistake","chinese":"嚴重錯誤"},{"english":"the remaining harbourfront","chinese":"餘下的海濱地區"},{"english":"should be protected","chinese":"應該受到保護"},{"english":"promotes social fairness","chinese":"促進社會公平"},{"english":"improves urban well-being","chinese":"改善城市福祉"},{"english":"strengthens long-term appeal","chinese":"增強長遠吸引力"},{"english":"first and foremost","chinese":"首先；最重要的是"},{"english":"public assets","chinese":"公共資產"},{"english":"belongs equally to everyone","chinese":"平等地屬於所有人"},{"english":"luxury flats","chinese":"豪宅單位"},{"english":"grade-A offices","chinese":"甲級寫字樓"},{"english":"look impressive","chinese":"看起來氣派"},{"english":"accessible mainly to","chinese":"主要供……使用"},{"english":"those who can afford them","chinese":"負擔得起的人"},{"english":"by contrast","chinese":"相比之下"},{"english":"a promenade","chinese":"海濱長廊"},{"english":"a lawn","chinese":"草地"},{"english":"sitting-out area","chinese":"休憩處"},{"english":"without paying a cent","chinese":"不用付一分錢"},{"english":"this distinction matters","chinese":"這個分別很重要"},{"english":"private space","chinese":"私人空間"},{"english":"daily life is crowded","chinese":"日常生活擠迫"},{"english":"a form of everyday dignity","chinese":"一種日常尊嚴"},{"english":"instead of a decorative extra","chinese":"而不是額外裝飾"},{"english":"picnic","chinese":"野餐"},{"english":"domestic helpers","chinese":"家庭傭工"},{"english":"practise photography","chinese":"練習攝影"},{"english":"elderly residents","chinese":"年長居民"},{"english":"looking across the water","chinese":"望向水面"},{"english":"only when","chinese":"只有當……時"},{"english":"waterfront land","chinese":"海濱土地"},{"english":"ordinary citizens","chinese":"普通市民"},{"english":"walled off by privilege","chinese":"被特權圍起來"},{"english":"turn such sites into","chinese":"把這些地方變成"},{"english":"private developments","chinese":"私人發展項目"},{"english":"replace a common good with","chinese":"以……取代公共利益"},{"english":"a common good","chinese":"公共利益；共有資源"},{"english":"a gated view","chinese":"被圍起來的景觀"},{"english":"run counter to","chinese":"違背"},{"english":"the spirit of a harbour city","chinese":"海港城市的精神"},{"english":"moreover","chinese":"此外"},{"english":"healthier, calmer and more liveable","chinese":"更健康、更平靜、更宜居"},{"english":"densely built","chinese":"建築密集"},{"english":"urgently needs","chinese":"迫切需要"},{"english":"breathing room","chinese":"透氣空間"},{"english":"encourage walking","chinese":"鼓勵步行"},{"english":"jogging","chinese":"緩步跑"},{"english":"cycling","chinese":"踩單車"},{"english":"quiet conversation","chinese":"安靜交談"},{"english":"thereby improving","chinese":"從而改善"},{"english":"physical and mental health","chinese":"身心健康"},{"english":"existing promenades","chinese":"現有海濱長廊"},{"english":"Tsim Sha Tsui","chinese":"尖沙咀"},{"english":"Kwun Tong","chinese":"觀塘"},{"english":"not merely exercising","chinese":"不只是在做運動"},{"english":"escaping from","chinese":"逃離"},{"english":"even briefly","chinese":"即使只是短暫地"},{"english":"traffic noise","chinese":"交通噪音"},{"english":"concrete walls","chinese":"石屎牆"},{"english":"workplace pressure","chinese":"工作壓力"},{"english":"green and open spaces","chinese":"綠化及開放空間"},{"english":"wind corridors","chinese":"通風廊"},{"english":"shade and vegetation","chinese":"樹蔭和植被"},{"english":"soften the urban heat","chinese":"紓緩城市熱力"},{"english":"high-rise blocks","chinese":"高樓大廈"},{"english":"intensify","chinese":"加劇"},{"english":"be filled with towers","chinese":"被高樓填滿"},{"english":"floor area","chinese":"樓面面積"},{"english":"less airflow","chinese":"較少空氣流通"},{"english":"skyline","chinese":"天際線"},{"english":"increasingly closed in","chinese":"越來越封閉"},{"english":"rarely does a city get a chance to","chinese":"一個城市很少有機會……"},{"english":"reserve land","chinese":"保留土地"},{"english":"beside the sea","chinese":"在海邊"},{"english":"lost to permanent construction","chinese":"因永久建築而失去"},{"english":"permanent construction","chinese":"永久建築"},{"english":"almost impossible to regain","chinese":"幾乎不可能取回"},{"english":"granted","chinese":"誠然"},{"english":"economic activity","chinese":"經濟活動"},{"english":"it does not follow that","chinese":"這並不代表"},{"english":"be sacrificed for","chinese":"為……而犧牲"},{"english":"for these purposes","chinese":"為了這些目的"},{"english":"be pursued through","chinese":"應透過……來推動"},{"english":"brownfield redevelopment","chinese":"棕地重建"},{"english":"urban renewal","chinese":"市區重建"},{"english":"better use of idle sites","chinese":"更善用閒置土地"},{"english":"idle sites","chinese":"閒置土地"},{"english":"well-planned new development areas","chinese":"規劃完善的新發展區"},{"english":"consuming","chinese":"消耗；佔用"},{"english":"symbolically valuable edge of the city","chinese":"城市最具象徵價值的邊緣"},{"english":"commercial use","chinese":"商業用途"},{"english":"benefit from","chinese":"受惠於"},{"english":"local visitors","chinese":"本地遊客；本地訪客"},{"english":"tourists","chinese":"遊客"},{"english":"cultural events","chinese":"文化活動"},{"english":"weekend markets","chinese":"週末市集"},{"english":"outdoor performances","chinese":"戶外表演"},{"english":"surrounding districts","chinese":"周邊地區"},{"english":"in other words","chinese":"換言之"},{"english":"anti-development","chinese":"反發展"},{"english":"quite the contrary","chinese":"正好相反"},{"english":"a wiser kind of development","chinese":"更明智的發展方式"},{"english":"cities such as","chinese":"例如……的城市"},{"english":"admired","chinese":"受人欣賞"},{"english":"every inch of waterfront","chinese":"每一吋海濱"},{"english":"be sold to the highest bidder","chinese":"賣給出價最高者"},{"english":"gather, walk, celebrate and remember","chinese":"聚集、散步、慶祝和回憶"},{"english":"beside the water","chinese":"在水邊"},{"english":"all in all","chinese":"總括而言"},{"english":"world-class","chinese":"世界級"},{"english":"quality of life","chinese":"生活質素"},{"english":"at street level","chinese":"在街道層面"},{"english":"not simply","chinese":"不只是"},{"english":"the height of its buildings","chinese":"建築物的高度"},{"english":"for these reasons","chinese":"基於這些原因"},{"english":"should be left as","chinese":"應該保留作"},{"english":"the Government","chinese":"政府"},{"english":"urban planners","chinese":"城市規劃師"},{"english":"district councils","chinese":"區議會"},{"english":"shaded walkways","chinese":"有遮蔭的行人道"},{"english":"barrier-free access","chinese":"無障礙通道"},{"english":"lawns","chinese":"草地"},{"english":"cultural facilities","chinese":"文化設施"},{"english":"family-friendly seating","chinese":"適合家庭使用的座椅"},{"english":"ensuring that","chinese":"確保"},{"english":"commercial operator","chinese":"商業營運者"},{"english":"dominate","chinese":"主導"},{"english":"central to Hong Kong's identity","chinese":"對香港身份十分重要"},{"english":"let us not treat it as","chinese":"讓我們不要把它視為"},{"english":"merely another piece of land","chinese":"只不過是另一幅土地"},{"english":"be sold, leased or fenced off","chinese":"被出售、出租或圍封"},{"english":"fenced off","chinese":"被圍封"},{"english":"remain what it ought to be","chinese":"保持它應有的樣子"},{"english":"where the whole city can breathe","chinese":"讓整個城市都能呼吸的地方"},{"english":"Yours faithfully","chinese":"謹啟"}]},"dse-writing-2015-part-b-q6":{"exerciseId":"dse-writing-2015-part-b-q6","essayKey":"","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=dse-writing-2015-part-b-q6","flashDeckId":"dse/writing/part-b/2015/Q6","paragraphs":[{"label":"Paragraph 1","english":"To: Jackie Lee","chinese":"收件人：Jackie Lee"},{"label":"Paragraph 2","english":"From: Chris Wong, Summer Intern, Customer Services Department","chinese":"寄件人：Chris Wong，客戶服務部暑期實習生 Summer Intern 暑期實習生 Customer Services Department 客戶服務部 Hong Kong Mobile 香港流動通訊"},{"label":"Paragraph 3","english":"Subject: Recent Complaint Concerning 5G Plan Upgrade and Recommended Follow-up","chinese":"主旨：關於近期5G計劃升級投訴及建議跟進安排"},{"label":"Paragraph 4","english":"Dear Ms Lee,","chinese":"李女士："},{"label":"Paragraph 5","english":"I am writing to summarise a recent complaint received from Ms Katherine Chan, a long-standing customer of Hong Kong Mobile, and to suggest three possible actions for your consideration. By way of background, Ms Chan upgraded from her existing 4G plan to our “5G Unlimited Plus” plan at the Causeway Bay branch on 18 July. She said she did so because our sales representative assured her that the new plan would provide stronger coverage, faster data speed and no unexpected additional charges. The complaint has made the Customer Services Department consider immediate compensation, a technical review and clearer sales procedures in order to restore the customer’s confidence, prevent the matter from escalating and protect the company’s reputation. In my view, it should be handled as both an individual service failure and a warning sign about our communication with customers.","chinese":"我寫此電郵，是為了概述近期收到的一宗投訴；投訴人是香港流動通訊的長期客戶 Katherine Chan 女士，並向你提出三項可供考慮的處理行動。 作為背景資料，Chan 女士於7月18日在銅鑼灣分店，將原有的4G計劃升級至我們的「5G Unlimited Plus」計劃。 她表示，自己之所以這樣做，是因為我們的銷售代表向她保證，新計劃會提供更強的網絡覆蓋、更快的數據速度，以及不會有意料之外的額外收費。 這宗投訴令客戶服務部需要考慮即時補償、技術檢查，以及更清晰的銷售程序，以恢復客戶信心、防止事件升級，並保障公司聲譽。 在我看來，這宗個案應同時被視為一次個別服務失誤，以及一個反映我們與客戶溝通方式需要改善的警號。"},{"label":"Paragraph 6","english":"According to Ms Chan, three problems occurred after the upgrade. First, the network performance was far from satisfactory. She reported that calls were repeatedly cut off in her flat in Taikoo Shing and that mobile data often slowed down to the point where video meetings became impossible. Secondly, her first bill included a HK$120 SIM replacement fee and a HK$280 “administrative adjustment”, neither of which, she claims, was clearly explained when she signed the contract. Thirdly, she contacted our hotline on 22, 24 and 28 July but was given different explanations each time. One colleague told her to restart her phone; another said the district was under maintenance; a third promised a call-back which, to date, has not been made. Understandably, Ms Chan feels that she has been “sold a promise rather than a service”. She is now asking either to return to her previous plan without penalty or to receive a written apology and compensation.","chinese":"根據 Chan 女士所述，升級後出現了三個問題。 首先，網絡表現遠遠未能令人滿意。 她表示，在太古城的住所內，電話通話多次中斷，而流動數據也經常慢到連視像會議都無法進行的程度。 其次，她的第一張帳單包括120港元的SIM卡更換費，以及280港元的「行政調整費」；她聲稱，這兩項收費在她簽署合約時都沒有被清楚解釋。 第三，她曾於7月22、24及28日聯絡我們的熱線，但每次都得到不同解釋 一位同事叫她重新啟動手機；另一位同事表示該區正在維修；第三位同事承諾會回電，但截至目前仍未做到。 可以理解的是，Chan 女士覺得自己買到的是「一個承諾」，實際得到的服務卻不相稱。 她現在要求無罰款地轉回原有計劃，或者收到書面道歉及補償。"},{"label":"Paragraph 7","english":"The first action I recommend is to appoint one case officer to contact Ms Chan personally and resolve the billing dispute no later than this Friday. Instead of asking her to repeat the same details to different staff members, we should acknowledge the inconvenience, waive the two disputed charges while the case is being investigated, and offer a goodwill credit of one month’s service fee. This would not amount to admitting full liability before the investigation is complete; rather, it would show that we take her experience seriously. If we leave the complaint hanging, we run the risk of turning one disappointed customer into a public criticism on social media.","chinese":"我建議的第一項行動，是委派一名個案主任親自聯絡 Chan 女士，並最遲於本星期五解決帳單爭議。 我們不應要求她向不同員工重複相同細節；相反，我們應承認她所遇到的不便，在調查期間豁免兩項有爭議的收費，並提供相當於一個月服務費的善意回贈。 這樣做並不等於在調查完成前承認全部責任；更準確地說，這能顯示我們認真看待她的經歷。 如果我們繼續讓這宗投訴懸而未決，就有可能把一位失望的客戶，變成社交媒體上的公開批評。"},{"label":"Paragraph 8","english":"The second action is to ask the network operations team to conduct a coverage and speed test near Ms Chan’s home and office. If the problem is caused by temporary maintenance, we should tell her clearly when the work will be completed. If the coverage is genuinely weak, she should be allowed to downgrade or return to her previous plan without an early termination charge. We may also provide a temporary data pass or portable Wi-Fi device so that she can continue working while the issue is being examined. Only by checking the technical facts can we give her an answer that is accurate, fair and defensible.","chinese":"第二項行動，是請網絡營運團隊在 Chan 女士的住所和辦公室附近進行覆蓋及速度測試。 如果問題是由臨時維修造成的，我們應清楚告知她工程何時完成。 如果覆蓋確實薄弱，她應獲准降級或轉回原有計劃，而無須支付提早終止合約費用。 我們也可以提供臨時數據通行證或便攜式 Wi-Fi 裝置，讓她在問題接受檢查期間仍能繼續工作。 只有核實技術事實，我們才能給她一個準確、公平，而且站得住腳的答覆。"},{"label":"Paragraph 9","english":"The third action is to review the sales and follow-up procedure. Branch staff should use a short disclosure checklist covering coverage limitations, one-off fees and cooling-off arrangements before any customer signs a new contract. A confirmation email should then be sent automatically, setting out the key terms in plain English and Chinese. Moreover, hotline staff should record all promises of call-backs in the complaint system, with overdue cases flagged to supervisors. That way, customers will no longer be passed from one colleague to another without a clear answer.","chinese":"第三項行動，是檢討銷售及跟進程序。 分店員工應在任何客戶簽署新合約前，使用一份簡短的資料披露清單，涵蓋網絡覆蓋限制、一次性收費及冷靜期安排。 之後，系統應自動發出確認電郵，以淺白英文和中文列明主要條款。 此外，熱線員工應在投訴系統中記錄所有回電承諾，並把逾期個案標示給主管跟進。 這樣一來，客戶就不會再在不同同事之間被轉來轉去，卻始終得不到清楚答覆"},{"label":"Paragraph 10","english":"In conclusion, I believe Ms Chan’s complaint should be dealt with promptly, politely and transparently. The immediate objective is to settle her case; the wider objective is to make sure that similar complaints do not arise again. I would be grateful if you could advise whether I should draft a reply to Ms Chan based on the above recommendations.","chinese":"總結來說，我認為 Chan 女士的投訴應該以迅速、禮貌和透明的方式處理。 即時目標是解決她的個案；更長遠的目標，是確保類似投訴不會再次出現。 如你能告知我是否應根據以上建議草擬給 Chan 女士的回覆，我將不勝感激"},{"label":"Paragraph 11","english":"Yours sincerely,","chinese":"謹啟"},{"label":"Paragraph 12","english":"Chris Wong","chinese":"寄件人：Chris Wong，客戶服務部暑期實習生 Summer Intern 暑期實習生 Customer Services Department 客戶服務部 Hong Kong Mobile 香港流動通訊"},{"label":"Paragraph 13","english":"Summer Intern","chinese":"寄件人：Chris Wong，客戶服務部暑期實習生"},{"label":"Paragraph 14","english":"Customer Services Department","chinese":"寄件人：Chris Wong，客戶服務部暑期實習生 這宗投訴令客戶服務部需要考慮即時補償、技術檢查，以及更清晰的銷售程序，以恢復客戶信心、防止事件升級，並保障公司聲譽。"},{"label":"Paragraph 15","english":"Hong Kong Mobile","chinese":"我寫此電郵，是為了概述近期收到的一宗投訴；投訴人是香港流動通訊的長期客戶 Katherine Chan 女士，並向你提出三項可供考慮的處理行動。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"Dear Ms Lee","chinese":"李女士鈞鑒"},{"english":"recent complaint concerning","chinese":"關於……的近期投訴"},{"english":"5G plan upgrade","chinese":"5G計劃升級"},{"english":"recommended follow-up","chinese":"建議跟進行動"},{"english":"I am writing to summarise","chinese":"我寫信是為了概述"},{"english":"received from","chinese":"收到來自……"},{"english":"a long-standing customer","chinese":"長期客戶"},{"english":"suggest three possible actions","chinese":"建議三項可行行動"},{"english":"for your consideration","chinese":"供你考慮"},{"english":"by way of background","chinese":"作為背景資料"},{"english":"upgrade from…to…","chinese":"由……升級至……"},{"english":"existing 4G plan","chinese":"現有4G計劃"},{"english":"5G Unlimited Plus plan","chinese":"5G無限Plus計劃"},{"english":"Causeway Bay branch","chinese":"銅鑼灣分店"},{"english":"sales representative","chinese":"銷售代表"},{"english":"assure someone that","chinese":"向某人保證"},{"english":"provide stronger coverage","chinese":"提供更強網絡覆蓋"},{"english":"faster data speed","chinese":"更快數據速度"},{"english":"unexpected additional charges","chinese":"意料之外的額外收費"},{"english":"lead someone to consider","chinese":"令某人考慮"},{"english":"immediate compensation","chinese":"即時賠償"},{"english":"a technical review","chinese":"技術檢視"},{"english":"clearer sales procedures","chinese":"更清晰的銷售程序"},{"english":"in order to","chinese":"為了"},{"english":"restore the customer's confidence","chinese":"恢復顧客信心"},{"english":"prevent the matter from escalating","chinese":"防止事件升級"},{"english":"protect the company's reputation","chinese":"保護公司聲譽"},{"english":"in my view","chinese":"我認為"},{"english":"be handled as","chinese":"被視作……處理"},{"english":"an individual service failure","chinese":"個別服務失誤"},{"english":"a warning sign about","chinese":"關於……的警號"},{"english":"communication with customers","chinese":"與顧客溝通"},{"english":"according to","chinese":"根據"},{"english":"problems occurred","chinese":"問題發生"},{"english":"after the upgrade","chinese":"升級後"},{"english":"network performance","chinese":"網絡表現"},{"english":"far from satisfactory","chinese":"遠未令人滿意"},{"english":"report that","chinese":"報稱"},{"english":"calls were repeatedly cut off","chinese":"通話多次中斷"},{"english":"in her flat","chinese":"在她的單位內"},{"english":"mobile data","chinese":"流動數據"},{"english":"slow down","chinese":"變慢"},{"english":"to the point where","chinese":"到……的程度"},{"english":"video meetings","chinese":"視像會議"},{"english":"first bill","chinese":"第一張帳單"},{"english":"SIM replacement fee","chinese":"SIM卡更換費"},{"english":"administrative adjustment","chinese":"行政調整費"},{"english":"neither of which","chinese":"兩者均不"},{"english":"clearly explained","chinese":"清楚解釋"},{"english":"sign the contract","chinese":"簽署合約"},{"english":"contact our hotline","chinese":"聯絡我們的熱線"},{"english":"be given different explanations","chinese":"獲得不同解釋"},{"english":"each time","chinese":"每次"},{"english":"restart her phone","chinese":"重新啟動手機"},{"english":"be under maintenance","chinese":"正在維修"},{"english":"promise a call-back","chinese":"承諾回覆電話"},{"english":"to date","chinese":"至今"},{"english":"has not been made","chinese":"尚未作出"},{"english":"understandably","chinese":"可以理解的是"},{"english":"be sold a promise rather than a service","chinese":"買到的是承諾而不是服務"},{"english":"ask either to…or to…","chinese":"要求要麼……要麼……"},{"english":"return to her previous plan","chinese":"回復原本的計劃"},{"english":"without penalty","chinese":"無需罰款"},{"english":"written apology","chinese":"書面道歉"},{"english":"receive compensation","chinese":"獲得賠償"},{"english":"the first action I recommend","chinese":"我建議的第一項行動"},{"english":"appoint one case officer","chinese":"指派一名個案主任"},{"english":"contact someone personally","chinese":"親自聯絡某人"},{"english":"resolve the billing dispute","chinese":"解決帳單爭議"},{"english":"no later than this Friday","chinese":"不遲於本星期五"},{"english":"instead of asking her to","chinese":"而不是要求她"},{"english":"repeat the same details","chinese":"重複相同細節"},{"english":"staff members","chinese":"職員"},{"english":"acknowledge the inconvenience","chinese":"承認造成不便"},{"english":"waive the disputed charges","chinese":"豁免有爭議的收費"},{"english":"while the case is being investigated","chinese":"在個案調查期間"},{"english":"offer a goodwill credit","chinese":"提供善意回贈"},{"english":"one month's service fee","chinese":"一個月服務費"},{"english":"amount to","chinese":"等同於"},{"english":"admit full liability","chinese":"承認全部責任"},{"english":"before the investigation is complete","chinese":"在調查完成之前"},{"english":"take someone's experience seriously","chinese":"認真看待某人的經歷"},{"english":"leave the complaint hanging","chinese":"讓投訴懸而未決"},{"english":"run the risk of","chinese":"冒着……的風險"},{"english":"turn one disappointed customer into","chinese":"把一名失望顧客變成"},{"english":"public criticism on social media","chinese":"社交媒體上的公開批評"},{"english":"network operations team","chinese":"網絡營運團隊"},{"english":"conduct a coverage and speed test","chinese":"進行網絡覆蓋及速度測試"},{"english":"near her home and office","chinese":"在她的住所和辦公室附近"},{"english":"be caused by","chinese":"由……引起"},{"english":"temporary maintenance","chinese":"臨時維修"},{"english":"tell her clearly when","chinese":"清楚告知她何時"},{"english":"the work will be completed","chinese":"工程將會完成"},{"english":"genuinely weak","chinese":"真正薄弱"},{"english":"be allowed to downgrade","chinese":"獲准降級"},{"english":"early termination charge","chinese":"提前終止合約費"},{"english":"temporary data pass","chinese":"臨時數據套票"},{"english":"portable Wi-Fi device","chinese":"便攜式Wi-Fi裝置"},{"english":"continue working","chinese":"繼續工作"},{"english":"while the issue is being examined","chinese":"在問題檢查期間"},{"english":"only by checking…can…","chinese":"只有透過檢查……才可以……"},{"english":"technical facts","chinese":"技術事實"},{"english":"accurate, fair and defensible","chinese":"準確、公平且站得住腳"},{"english":"review the sales and follow-up procedure","chinese":"檢討銷售及跟進程序"},{"english":"branch staff","chinese":"分店職員"},{"english":"disclosure checklist","chinese":"披露清單"},{"english":"cover coverage limitations","chinese":"涵蓋網絡覆蓋限制"},{"english":"coverage limitations","chinese":"網絡覆蓋限制"},{"english":"one-off fees","chinese":"一次性費用"},{"english":"cooling-off arrangements","chinese":"冷靜期安排"},{"english":"sign a new contract","chinese":"簽署新合約"},{"english":"confirmation email","chinese":"確認電郵"},{"english":"be sent automatically","chinese":"自動發送"},{"english":"set out the key terms","chinese":"列明主要條款"},{"english":"key terms","chinese":"主要條款"},{"english":"in plain English and Chinese","chinese":"以淺白中英文"},{"english":"moreover","chinese":"此外"},{"english":"hotline staff","chinese":"熱線職員"},{"english":"record all promises of call-backs","chinese":"記錄所有回覆電話承諾"},{"english":"complaint system","chinese":"投訴系統"},{"english":"overdue cases","chinese":"逾期個案"},{"english":"be flagged to supervisors","chinese":"被標示給主管跟進"},{"english":"that way","chinese":"這樣一來"},{"english":"be passed from one colleague to another","chinese":"被不同同事推來推去"},{"english":"without a clear answer","chinese":"沒有清晰答覆"},{"english":"in conclusion","chinese":"總括而言"},{"english":"be dealt with promptly","chinese":"迅速處理"},{"english":"politely and transparently","chinese":"有禮且透明地"},{"english":"immediate objective","chinese":"即時目標"},{"english":"settle her case","chinese":"解決她的個案"},{"english":"wider objective","chinese":"更廣泛的目標"},{"english":"make sure that","chinese":"確保"},{"english":"similar complaints","chinese":"類似投訴"},{"english":"arise again","chinese":"再次出現"},{"english":"I would be grateful if you could advise","chinese":"如你能指示……，我將不勝感激"},{"english":"draft a reply","chinese":"草擬回覆"},{"english":"based on the above recommendations","chinese":"根據上述建議"},{"english":"Yours sincerely","chinese":"謹啟"},{"english":"Summer Intern","chinese":"暑期實習生"},{"english":"Customer Services Department","chinese":"客戶服務部"}]},"dse-writing-2015-part-b-q7":{"exerciseId":"dse-writing-2015-part-b-q7","essayKey":"","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=dse-writing-2015-part-b-q7","flashDeckId":"dse/writing/part-b/2015/Q7","paragraphs":[{"label":"Paragraph 1","english":"Report on the Decline in Cinema Attendance in Hong Kong","chinese":"關於香港戲院入場人次下降的報告"},{"label":"Paragraph 2","english":"To: The English Panel","chinese":"致：英文科組"},{"label":"Paragraph 3","english":"From: Chris Wong","chinese":"由：Chris Wong 撰寫"},{"label":"Paragraph 4","english":"Subject: Cinemas in Hong Kong","chinese":"主題：香港戲院"},{"label":"Paragraph 5","english":"Introduction","chinese":"引言"},{"label":"Paragraph 6","english":"This report has been prepared for the Learning English through Popular Culture module project “Cinemas in Hong Kong”. Fewer people now choose to watch films in cinemas. This has made cinema operators consider how to turn cinema-going from a routine purchase into a memorable social experience. This report explains the main reasons for the decline and suggests practical ways to increase the number of moviegoers. The central finding is that Hong Kong cinemas can regain audiences only if they improve both value and experience.","chinese":"本報告是為「透過流行文化學習英語」單元項目《香港戲院》而撰寫。 現時選擇到戲院觀看電影的人比以往少。 這令戲院營運者開始思考，如何把入戲院觀影由一項日常消費，轉化為令人難忘的社交體驗。 本報告會解釋人數下降的主要原因，並建議實際可行的方法，以增加入場觀眾人數。 核心發現是，香港戲院只有在同時提升價值和體驗的情況下，才可以重新吸引觀眾。 人數下降的原因"},{"label":"Paragraph 7","english":"Reasons for the Decline","chinese":"本報告會解釋人數下降的主要原因，並建議實際可行的方法，以增加入場觀眾人數。 人數下降的原因"},{"label":"Paragraph 8","english":"The first reason is that the cost-benefit balance has changed. A cinema ticket is no longer compared only with another night out; it is now compared with streaming platforms, mobile games and short videos. Between transport, food and tickets, even a casual evening can feel expensive. By contrast, watching a film at home allows viewers to pause the story, choose subtitles, avoid queues and relax in private. For a teenager rushing home after tutorial classes or a parent exhausted after work, such convenience is hard to resist. As a result, many people ask themselves a simple question - “why go out if the same story can be watched later with less effort?”","chinese":"第一個原因是成本與得益之間的平衡已經改變。 一張戲票如今已不再只會與另一個外出晚上的消費相比；它現在還會與串流平台、手機遊戲和短影片相比。 在交通、食物和戲票的花費之間，即使只是普通的一晚外出，也可能令人覺得昂貴。 相比之下，在家看電影能讓觀眾暫停故事、選擇字幕、避開排隊，並在私人空間中放鬆。 對於補習後匆忙回家的青少年，或下班後筋疲力盡的家長而言，這種便利很難抗拒。 結果，許多人會問自己一個簡單的問題——「如果之後可以用更少力氣看到同一個故事，為甚麼還要外出？」"},{"label":"Paragraph 9","english":"Another reason is that the special feeling of cinema-going has become weaker. In the past, cinemas were among the few places where people could enjoy new films on a large screen. Now, entertainment is everywhere. Trailers, reviews, spoilers and film clips appear on social media before friends have even agreed on a showtime. Meanwhile, some cinemas offer a rather ordinary experience - a plain lobby, similar snacks, high prices and little interaction before or after the film. If a cinema is seen merely as a bigger screen, it will struggle to compete with the screens people already carry in their pockets. Put simply, cinemas are losing not because films are unimportant, but because the trip itself no longer feels important enough.","chinese":"另一個原因是，入戲院觀影那種特別感已經變弱。 在過去，戲院是少數能讓人們在大銀幕上欣賞新電影的地方之一。 如今，娛樂無處不在。 在朋友甚至還未約好場次之前，預告片、影評、劇透和電影片段已經出現在社交媒體上。 與此同時，一些戲院提供的體驗相當普通——平淡無奇的大堂、相似的小食、高昂的價格，以及電影前後甚少互動。 如果戲院只被視為一塊較大的螢幕，它便難以與人們早已放在口袋裡的螢幕競爭。 簡單來說，戲院正在流失觀眾，原因並非電影不重要；真正關鍵在於這趟外出本身已不再令人覺得足夠重要。 Suggestions 建議"},{"label":"Paragraph 10","english":"Suggestions","chinese":""},{"label":"Paragraph 11","english":"First, cinemas should make each visit feel like an event. Going to the cinema should not be merely about watching a film; rather, it should be about entering a shared world. To achieve this, cinemas could organise themed screenings, director talks, audience discussions, costume nights and small exhibitions about film-making. For example, during a week of Hong Kong films, the lobby could display old posters and invite viewers to vote for their favourite classic. These activities would give audiences something they cannot get from a sofa at home. More importantly, they would turn passive viewing into social participation.","chinese":"首先，戲院應該令每一次入場都像一場活動。 到戲院觀影不應只關乎觀看一部電影；更準確地說，它應該關乎進入一個共同的世界。 為了做到這一點，戲院可以舉辦主題放映、導演講座、觀眾討論、造型之夜，以及關於電影製作的小型展覽。 例如，在香港電影週期間，大堂可以展示舊海報，並邀請觀眾投票選出他們最喜愛的經典電影。 這些活動能給予觀眾一些他們坐在家中梳化上無法得到的東西。 更重要的是，它們會把被動觀看轉化為社交參與。"},{"label":"Paragraph 12","english":"Second, cinemas should improve affordability without making discounts confusing. Student tickets on weekday evenings, family packages, “bring a friend” offers and combined coupons with nearby restaurants could reduce the psychological barrier to going out. Dynamic pricing could also be used for older films or less popular showtimes. Cinemas should not simply cut prices blindly. Instead, they should make the evening worth paying for. If students know that certain evenings are reliably affordable, they are more likely to develop a habit of returning.","chinese":"第二，戲院應該提高可負擔程度，同時避免令折扣安排變得混亂。 平日晚上的學生票、家庭套票、「帶朋友同行」優惠，以及與附近餐廳合作的組合優惠券，都可以降低人們外出的心理門檻。 動態定價也可以用於較舊的電影或較不受歡迎的場次。 戲院不應只是盲目減價。 相反，它們應該令那一晚變得值得付費。 如果學生知道某些晚上確實負擔得起，他們便更有可能養成再次入場的習慣"},{"label":"Paragraph 13","english":"Third, schools and cinemas should work together to rebuild young people’s interest in films. Since films are part of popular culture, they can be used to teach language, values and creativity. Cinemas could offer school screenings of film adaptations, documentaries or local productions, followed by short talks on subtitles, music, camera angles or storytelling. Students who first visit a cinema through a school activity may later return with friends. In the meantime, cinema operators should use social media not only to advertise, but also to invite young people to choose films and share recommendations. That way, moviegoers become part of a community rather than just customers.","chinese":"第三，學校和戲院應該合作，重建年輕人對電影的興趣。 由於電影是流行文化的一部分，它們可以用來教授語言、價值觀和創意。 戲院可以為學校提供改編電影、紀錄片或本地製作的放映活動，之後再安排關於字幕、音樂、鏡頭角度或敘事技巧的短講座。 透過學校活動第一次走進戲院的學生，日後可能會與朋友再次到訪。 在此期間，戲院營運者使用社交媒體時，不應只用來宣傳，也應邀請年輕人選擇電影並分享推介。 這樣一來，入場觀眾就會成為社群的一部分，不再只是顧客。"},{"label":"Paragraph 14","english":"Conclusion","chinese":""},{"label":"Paragraph 15","english":"All things considered, the decline in cinema attendance is serious but not irreversible. People have not stopped loving stories; they have simply become harder to persuade. Therefore, cinema operators, schools, malls and local film-makers should act together to make cinema-going affordable, distinctive and socially meaningful. If cinemas can offer an experience that home viewing cannot replace, Hong Kong’s big-screen culture will not become a thing of the past.","chinese":"綜合而言，戲院入場人次下降是一個嚴重問題，但並非無法逆轉。 人們並沒有停止熱愛故事；只是要說服他們入場變得更困難。 因此，戲院營運者、學校、商場和本地電影工作者應該共同採取行動，令入戲院觀影變得負擔得起、具特色，並具有社交意義。 如果戲院能提供一種在家觀影無法取代的體驗，香港的大銀幕文化就不會成為過去式。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"report on","chinese":"關於……的報告"},{"english":"decline in","chinese":"……下降"},{"english":"cinema attendance","chinese":"戲院入場人次"},{"english":"The English Panel","chinese":"英文科組"},{"english":"subject","chinese":"主題"},{"english":"introduction","chinese":"引言"},{"english":"be prepared for","chinese":"為……而準備"},{"english":"Learning English through Popular Culture","chinese":"透過流行文化學習英語"},{"english":"module project","chinese":"單元專題報告"},{"english":"choose to watch films","chinese":"選擇看電影"},{"english":"in cinemas","chinese":"在戲院"},{"english":"cinema operators","chinese":"戲院經營者"},{"english":"consider how to","chinese":"考慮如何"},{"english":"turn… from… into…","chinese":"將……由……變成……"},{"english":"cinema-going","chinese":"入戲院看電影"},{"english":"routine purchase","chinese":"例行消費"},{"english":"memorable social experience","chinese":"難忘的社交體驗"},{"english":"main reasons for","chinese":"……的主要原因"},{"english":"practical ways to","chinese":"……的實際方法"},{"english":"increase the number of","chinese":"增加……的數目"},{"english":"moviegoers","chinese":"電影觀眾；入戲院看電影的人"},{"english":"central finding","chinese":"主要結論"},{"english":"regain audiences","chinese":"重新吸引觀眾"},{"english":"only if","chinese":"只有在……情況下"},{"english":"value and experience","chinese":"價值與體驗"},{"english":"reasons for the decline","chinese":"衰退的原因"},{"english":"cost-benefit balance","chinese":"成本效益平衡"},{"english":"has changed","chinese":"已經改變"},{"english":"no longer compared only with","chinese":"不再只與……比較"},{"english":"another night out","chinese":"另一次外出消遣"},{"english":"streaming platforms","chinese":"串流平台"},{"english":"mobile games","chinese":"手機遊戲"},{"english":"short videos","chinese":"短片"},{"english":"between transport, food and tickets","chinese":"連同交通、食物和門票"},{"english":"casual evening","chinese":"輕鬆晚間活動"},{"english":"feel expensive","chinese":"感覺昂貴"},{"english":"by contrast","chinese":"相比之下"},{"english":"watching a film at home","chinese":"在家看電影"},{"english":"allow viewers to","chinese":"讓觀眾能夠"},{"english":"pause the story","chinese":"暫停劇情"},{"english":"choose subtitles","chinese":"選擇字幕"},{"english":"avoid queues","chinese":"避免排隊"},{"english":"relax in private","chinese":"私下放鬆"},{"english":"rushing home after","chinese":"在……後趕回家"},{"english":"tutorial classes","chinese":"補習課"},{"english":"exhausted after work","chinese":"下班後筋疲力盡"},{"english":"such convenience","chinese":"這種方便"},{"english":"hard to resist","chinese":"難以抗拒"},{"english":"as a result","chinese":"因此"},{"english":"ask themselves","chinese":"問自己"},{"english":"why go out if…","chinese":"如果……，為何要外出？"},{"english":"the same story","chinese":"同一個故事"},{"english":"be watched later","chinese":"稍後觀看"},{"english":"with less effort","chinese":"用較少精力"},{"english":"another reason","chinese":"另一個原因"},{"english":"special feeling","chinese":"特別感覺"},{"english":"become weaker","chinese":"變弱"},{"english":"in the past","chinese":"在過去"},{"english":"among the few places","chinese":"少數地方之一"},{"english":"large screen","chinese":"大銀幕"},{"english":"entertainment is everywhere","chinese":"娛樂無處不在"},{"english":"trailers","chinese":"預告片"},{"english":"reviews","chinese":"影評"},{"english":"spoilers","chinese":"劇透"},{"english":"film clips","chinese":"電影片段"},{"english":"social media","chinese":"社交媒體"},{"english":"agree on a showtime","chinese":"決定放映時間"},{"english":"showtime","chinese":"放映時間"},{"english":"meanwhile","chinese":"與此同時"},{"english":"rather ordinary experience","chinese":"相當普通的體驗"},{"english":"plain lobby","chinese":"平平無奇的大堂"},{"english":"similar snacks","chinese":"類似的小食"},{"english":"little interaction","chinese":"甚少互動"},{"english":"before or after the film","chinese":"電影前後"},{"english":"be seen merely as","chinese":"僅被視為"},{"english":"bigger screen","chinese":"較大的螢幕"},{"english":"struggle to compete with","chinese":"難以與……競爭"},{"english":"carry in their pockets","chinese":"隨身攜帶"},{"english":"put simply","chinese":"簡單來說"},{"english":"losing not because…, but because…","chinese":"不是因為……而是因為……"},{"english":"the trip itself","chinese":"這趟外出本身"},{"english":"no longer feels important enough","chinese":"不再感覺足夠重要"},{"english":"suggestions","chinese":"建議"},{"english":"make each visit feel like an event","chinese":"令每次到訪都像一場活動"},{"english":"not merely about","chinese":"不只是關於"},{"english":"rather","chinese":"相反；更準確地說"},{"english":"enter a shared world","chinese":"進入一個共享世界"},{"english":"to achieve this","chinese":"為了做到這一點"},{"english":"organise themed screenings","chinese":"舉辦主題放映"},{"english":"themed screenings","chinese":"主題放映"},{"english":"director talks","chinese":"導演分享會"},{"english":"audience discussions","chinese":"觀眾討論"},{"english":"costume nights","chinese":"服裝主題夜"},{"english":"small exhibitions","chinese":"小型展覽"},{"english":"film-making","chinese":"電影製作"},{"english":"a week of Hong Kong films","chinese":"香港電影周"},{"english":"display old posters","chinese":"展示舊海報"},{"english":"invite viewers to vote for","chinese":"邀請觀眾投票選出"},{"english":"favourite classic","chinese":"最喜愛的經典作品"},{"english":"these activities","chinese":"這些活動"},{"english":"give audiences something","chinese":"給觀眾一些……"},{"english":"cannot get from a sofa at home","chinese":"在家中梳化上得不到的"},{"english":"more importantly","chinese":"更重要的是"},{"english":"turn passive viewing into","chinese":"將被動觀看變成"},{"english":"passive viewing","chinese":"被動觀看"},{"english":"social participation","chinese":"社交參與"},{"english":"improve affordability","chinese":"提高可負擔性"},{"english":"affordability","chinese":"可負擔性"},{"english":"without making discounts confusing","chinese":"在不令優惠混亂的情況下"},{"english":"student tickets","chinese":"學生票"},{"english":"weekday evenings","chinese":"平日晚上"},{"english":"family packages","chinese":"家庭套票"},{"english":"bring-a-friend offers","chinese":"帶朋友同行優惠"},{"english":"combined coupons","chinese":"聯合優惠券"},{"english":"nearby restaurants","chinese":"附近餐廳"},{"english":"reduce the psychological barrier","chinese":"降低心理門檻"},{"english":"psychological barrier","chinese":"心理門檻"},{"english":"going out","chinese":"外出消遣"},{"english":"dynamic pricing","chinese":"動態定價"},{"english":"older films","chinese":"較舊的電影"},{"english":"less popular showtimes","chinese":"較冷門的放映時段"},{"english":"cut prices blindly","chinese":"盲目減價"},{"english":"make the evening worth paying for","chinese":"令這個晚上值得付款"},{"english":"certain evenings","chinese":"某些晚上"},{"english":"reliably affordable","chinese":"穩定地負擔得起"},{"english":"be more likely to","chinese":"更有可能"},{"english":"develop a habit of returning","chinese":"培養回來的習慣"},{"english":"work together","chinese":"合作"},{"english":"rebuild young people's interest in","chinese":"重建年輕人對……的興趣"},{"english":"part of popular culture","chinese":"流行文化的一部分"},{"english":"be used to teach","chinese":"被用來教授"},{"english":"language, values and creativity","chinese":"語言、價值觀和創意"},{"english":"school screenings","chinese":"學校專場放映"},{"english":"film adaptations","chinese":"改編電影"},{"english":"documentaries","chinese":"紀錄片"},{"english":"local productions","chinese":"本地製作"},{"english":"followed by","chinese":"隨後有"},{"english":"short talks on","chinese":"關於……的簡短講座"},{"english":"subtitles","chinese":"字幕"},{"english":"camera angles","chinese":"鏡頭角度"},{"english":"storytelling","chinese":"敘事技巧"},{"english":"through a school activity","chinese":"透過學校活動"},{"english":"later return with friends","chinese":"之後和朋友再來"},{"english":"in the meantime","chinese":"與此同時"},{"english":"not only to…, but also to…","chinese":"不只是為了……也為了……"},{"english":"advertise","chinese":"宣傳"},{"english":"share recommendations","chinese":"分享推薦"},{"english":"that way","chinese":"這樣一來"},{"english":"become part of a community","chinese":"成為社群的一部分"},{"english":"rather than just customers","chinese":"而不只是顧客"},{"english":"all things considered","chinese":"綜合而言"},{"english":"serious but not irreversible","chinese":"嚴重但並非不可逆轉"},{"english":"irreversible","chinese":"不可逆轉的"},{"english":"have not stopped loving stories","chinese":"並沒有停止喜愛故事"},{"english":"harder to persuade","chinese":"更難說服"},{"english":"act together","chinese":"一起行動"},{"english":"local film-makers","chinese":"本地電影人"},{"english":"affordable, distinctive and socially meaningful","chinese":"負擔得起、有特色、有社交意義"},{"english":"home viewing","chinese":"在家觀看"},{"english":"cannot replace","chinese":"不能取代"},{"english":"big-screen culture","chinese":"大銀幕文化"},{"english":"become a thing of the past","chinese":"成為過去式"}]},"dse-writing-2015-part-b-q8":{"exerciseId":"dse-writing-2015-part-b-q8","essayKey":"","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=dse-writing-2015-part-b-q8","flashDeckId":"dse/writing/part-b/2015/Q8","paragraphs":[{"label":"Paragraph 1","english":"Re: Let Words Walk Off the Page:","chinese":"關於：讓文字走出紙頁："},{"label":"Paragraph 2","english":"Two Proposed Activities for the Language Arts Festival","chinese":"語文藝術節的兩項建議活動"},{"label":"Paragraph 3","english":"Dear Sir/Madam,","chinese":"敬啟者："},{"label":"Paragraph 4","english":"On behalf of our school’s Poetry Club, I am delighted to submit our suggestions for the Central Library’s summer language arts festival. In Hong Kong, many students meet English mainly through tests, grammar drills and model answers, so they may respect the language without truly enjoying it. The Central Library can help change this by offering activities that are lively, inclusive and memorable. In order to enhance students’ interest in learning English, I would like to suggest two activities—“Poetry Alive: Page-to-Stage Studio” and “The Library Story Quest”. My central belief is that students become interested in English when they can use it to perform, solve problems and express themselves.","chinese":"我很高興代表本校詩社，就中央圖書館暑期語文藝術節提交我們的建議。 在香港，許多學生主要透過測驗、文法操練和範文接觸英語，因此他們也許尊重這種語言，卻未必真正享受它。 中央圖書館可以透過提供生動、共融而令人難忘的活動，幫助改變這種情況 為了提升學生學習英語的興趣，我想建議兩項活動——「詩歌活起來：從頁面到舞台工作坊」和「圖書館故事探索」。 我的核心信念是，當學生能夠運用英語去表演、解決問題和表達自己時，他們便會對英語產生興趣。"},{"label":"Paragraph 5","english":"The first activity, “Poetry Alive: Page-to-Stage Studio”, would be a workshop in which students turn poems into short performances. Participants would choose a poem from a “poetry wall”, including classic poems, humorous verse and poems written by Hong Kong students. They would then join small groups led by student ambassadors. Step by step, they would read the poem aloud, identify its mood, mark its pauses, experiment with sound effects and create a two-minute performance using voice, gesture or simple props. The session could end with a friendly mini-slam, with awards such as “Most Expressive Voice” and “Most Original Interpretation”.","chinese":"第一項活動「詩歌活起來：從頁面到舞台工作坊」將會是一個讓學生把詩歌轉化成短劇式表演的工作坊。 參加者會從「詩歌牆」上選擇一首詩，當中包括經典詩作、幽默詩歌，以及香港學生創作的詩。 之後，他們會加入由學生大使帶領的小組。 他們會一步一步朗讀詩歌、辨識詩中的情緒、標記停頓位置、嘗試音效，並運用聲音、動作或簡單道具創作一段兩分鐘的表演。 活動可以以一場友善的小型詩歌擂台作結，並設立「最具表現力聲音」和「最具原創性演繹」等獎項。"},{"label":"Paragraph 6","english":"This activity would increase students’ interest in English because it changes how they encounter difficult language. Many students are put off by poetry because they meet it silently, alone and under pressure. In this workshop, however, meaning develops naturally - first through rhythm, then through discussion, then through performance. A shy Form Three student, for example, may begin by reading only one line; after practising with teammates, she may find herself speaking confidently before an audience. The more students use English to create emotion, the less they see vocabulary as an examination burden. More importantly, literary terms such as tone, alliteration and imagery would no longer be abstract labels. When students decide whether a line should sound angry, playful or sorrowful, they are analysing language without feeling that they are completing yet another worksheet. Poetry, in other words, becomes something to be experienced, not merely decoded.","chinese":"這項活動能夠提升學生對英語的興趣，因為它改變學生接觸困難語言的方式 許多學生對詩歌卻步，是因為他們往往在沉默、孤立和壓力之下接觸詩歌。 然而，在這個工作坊中，意義會自然地發展出來——先透過節奏，再透過討論，最後透過表演。 例如，一位害羞的中三學生起初也許只讀一句詩；在與隊友練習之後，她可能會發現自己能夠自信地在觀眾面前說話。 學生越能運用英語創造情感，就越不會把詞彙視為考試負擔。 更重要的是，tone、alliteration 和 imagery 等文學術語將不再只是抽象標籤。 當學生決定一句詩應該聽起來憤怒、俏皮還是悲傷時，他們其實正在分析語言，卻不會覺得自己又在完成另一份工作紙。 換句話說，詩歌會成為一種值得親身體驗的東西，非單純需要被解碼的文字"},{"label":"Paragraph 7","english":"The second activity I propose is “The Library Story Quest”, an interactive treasure hunt using different zones of the Central Library. Upon registration, teams of four would receive a “missing ending” booklet: a short detective story in which several clues have disappeared. To recover them, participants would visit stations around the library. These stations could ask them to solve an idiom puzzle, listen to a ninety-second conversation, match book blurbs with character motives and compose a four-line clue. After collecting the clues, each team would write its own ending and present it in sixty seconds at the “Publisher’s Desk”.","chinese":"我建議的第二項活動是「圖書館故事探索」，這是一個利用中央圖書館不同區域進行的互動尋寶活動。 登記後，每組四人的隊伍會收到一本「遺失結局」小冊子：那是一篇有幾條線索消失了的短篇偵探故事。 為了找回這些線索，參加者需要前往圖書館各處的站點。 這些站點可以要求他們解開一個習語謎題、聆聽一段九十秒的對話、把書籍簡介與人物動機配對，並創作一條四行線索。 收集線索後，每隊會寫出自己的結局，並在「出版人辦公桌」前用六十秒展示出來。"},{"label":"Paragraph 8","english":"This quest would make English purposeful, and that is why it would be powerful. Students would read because they wanted clues, listen because they needed evidence, speak because their teammates depended on them, and write because the story could not be completed without their imagination. The activity would also suit students of different abilities. Stronger students could craft elegant endings, while less confident students could contribute by spotting key words, drawing maps or reading short dialogues. With word banks, sentence starters and QR-code audio support, few, if any, participants would be left staring helplessly at a blank page. In addition, the quest would introduce students to the library itself. They would realise that the Central Library is not a silent warehouse of books, but a place where stories begin, questions grow and curiosity is rewarded.","chinese":"這個探索活動會令英語變得有目的，也正因如此，它會具有強大的吸引力。 學生會因為想要線索而閱讀，因為需要證據而聆聽，因為隊友依賴他們而說話，也因為故事需要他們的想像力才能完成而寫作。 這項活動亦能適合不同能力的學生。 能力較強的學生可以創作優雅的結局，而信心較低的學生則可以透過找出關鍵詞、繪製地圖或朗讀簡短對話作出貢獻。 有了詞彙庫、句子開首提示和 QR code 音頻支援後，即使仍有參加者面對空白頁感到無助，這樣的人數也會極少。 此外，這個探索活動也會讓學生認識圖書館本身。 他們會意識到，中央圖書館並非一座安靜的藏書倉庫，更是一個故事開始、問題滋長、好奇心得到回應的地方。"},{"label":"Paragraph 9","english":"All things considered, “Poetry Alive” and “The Library Story Quest” would serve the same educational purpose in different but complementary ways - the former gives students a voice, while the latter gives them a mission. Together, they would make English less distant, less mechanical and far more memorable. I sincerely hope the Central Library will consider these suggestions. Our Poetry Club would also be honoured to provide student helpers should the activities be adopted.","chinese":"總括而言，「詩歌活起來」和「圖書館故事探索」會以不同卻互補的方式服務同一個教育目的——前者給予學生聲音，後者則給予他們任務。 兩者結合起來，會令英語不再那麼遙遠，不再那麼機械化，並變得更加難忘 我衷心希望中央圖書館能考慮這些建議。 如活動獲採納，本校詩社亦十分榮幸能提供學生助手。"},{"label":"Paragraph 10","english":"Yours faithfully,","chinese":"謹此致意，"},{"label":"Paragraph 11","english":"Chris Wong","chinese":"Chris Wong"},{"label":"Paragraph 12","english":"Chairperson, Poetry Club","chinese":"詩社主席"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"let words walk off the page","chinese":"讓文字走出書頁"},{"english":"proposed activities","chinese":"建議活動"},{"english":"Language Arts Festival","chinese":"語文藝術節"},{"english":"on behalf of","chinese":"代表"},{"english":"Poetry Club","chinese":"詩會"},{"english":"be delighted to submit","chinese":"很高興提交"},{"english":"suggestions for","chinese":"給予……的建議"},{"english":"summer language arts festival","chinese":"夏季語文藝術節"},{"english":"meet English mainly through","chinese":"主要透過……接觸英語"},{"english":"grammar drills","chinese":"文法操練"},{"english":"model answers","chinese":"模範答案"},{"english":"respect the language","chinese":"尊重這種語言"},{"english":"without truly enjoying it","chinese":"卻沒有真正享受它"},{"english":"help change this","chinese":"幫助改變這種情況"},{"english":"by offering activities","chinese":"透過提供活動"},{"english":"lively, inclusive and memorable","chinese":"生動、共融而難忘"},{"english":"in order to enhance","chinese":"為了提升"},{"english":"students' interest in learning English","chinese":"學生學習英語的興趣"},{"english":"central belief","chinese":"核心信念"},{"english":"become interested in","chinese":"對……產生興趣"},{"english":"use it to perform","chinese":"用它來表演"},{"english":"solve problems","chinese":"解決問題"},{"english":"express themselves","chinese":"表達自己"},{"english":"Page-to-Stage Studio","chinese":"從書頁到舞台工作室"},{"english":"a workshop in which","chinese":"一個讓……的工作坊"},{"english":"turn poems into short performances","chinese":"把詩變成短表演"},{"english":"participants","chinese":"參加者"},{"english":"poetry wall","chinese":"詩牆"},{"english":"classic poems","chinese":"經典詩作"},{"english":"humorous verse","chinese":"幽默詩"},{"english":"poems written by Hong Kong students","chinese":"由香港學生創作的詩"},{"english":"join small groups","chinese":"加入小組"},{"english":"led by student ambassadors","chinese":"由學生大使帶領"},{"english":"step by step","chinese":"逐步地"},{"english":"read the poem aloud","chinese":"朗讀詩作"},{"english":"identify its mood","chinese":"辨認它的情緒"},{"english":"mark its pauses","chinese":"標示停頓"},{"english":"experiment with sound effects","chinese":"嘗試音效"},{"english":"create a two-minute performance","chinese":"創作兩分鐘表演"},{"english":"voice, gesture or simple props","chinese":"聲音、手勢或簡單道具"},{"english":"the session could end with","chinese":"該節活動可以以……作結"},{"english":"friendly mini-slam","chinese":"友善的小型詩歌表演賽"},{"english":"awards such as","chinese":"例如……的獎項"},{"english":"expressive voice","chinese":"富表現力的聲音"},{"english":"original interpretation","chinese":"原創演繹"},{"english":"increase students' interest in","chinese":"提升學生對……的興趣"},{"english":"encounter difficult language","chinese":"接觸艱深語言"},{"english":"be put off by","chinese":"對……卻步；被……嚇怕"},{"english":"silently, alone and under pressure","chinese":"沉默地、獨自地、在壓力下"},{"english":"meaning develops naturally","chinese":"意義自然形成"},{"english":"first through rhythm","chinese":"首先透過節奏"},{"english":"then through discussion","chinese":"然後透過討論"},{"english":"through performance","chinese":"透過表演"},{"english":"shy Form Three student","chinese":"害羞的中三學生"},{"english":"begin by","chinese":"以……開始"},{"english":"after practising with teammates","chinese":"與隊友練習之後"},{"english":"find herself speaking confidently","chinese":"發現自己自信地說話"},{"english":"before an audience","chinese":"在觀眾面前"},{"english":"the more..., the less...","chinese":"越……就越不……"},{"english":"create emotion","chinese":"創造情感"},{"english":"see vocabulary as","chinese":"把詞彙視為"},{"english":"examination burden","chinese":"考試負擔"},{"english":"more importantly","chinese":"更重要的是"},{"english":"literary terms","chinese":"文學術語"},{"english":"tone, alliteration and imagery","chinese":"語氣、頭韻和意象"},{"english":"no longer","chinese":"不再"},{"english":"abstract labels","chinese":"抽象標籤"},{"english":"decide whether","chinese":"決定是否"},{"english":"sound angry, playful or sorrowful","chinese":"聽起來憤怒、俏皮或悲傷"},{"english":"analyse language","chinese":"分析語言"},{"english":"without feeling that","chinese":"而不覺得"},{"english":"complete another worksheet","chinese":"完成另一份工作紙"},{"english":"in other words","chinese":"換句話說"},{"english":"be experienced, not merely decoded","chinese":"被體驗，而不只是被解碼"},{"english":"the second activity I propose","chinese":"我建議的第二項活動"},{"english":"interactive treasure hunt","chinese":"互動尋寶遊戲"},{"english":"different zones of the Central Library","chinese":"中央圖書館的不同區域"},{"english":"upon registration","chinese":"登記後"},{"english":"teams of four","chinese":"四人小隊"},{"english":"missing ending booklet","chinese":"缺失結局小冊子"},{"english":"short detective story","chinese":"短篇偵探故事"},{"english":"clues have disappeared","chinese":"線索消失了"},{"english":"recover them","chinese":"找回它們"},{"english":"visit stations around the library","chinese":"到訪圖書館各個站點"},{"english":"solve an idiom puzzle","chinese":"解開成語謎題"},{"english":"listen to a ninety-second conversation","chinese":"聽一段九十秒對話"},{"english":"match book blurbs with character motives","chinese":"把書籍簡介與角色動機配對"},{"english":"book blurbs","chinese":"書籍簡介"},{"english":"character motives","chinese":"角色動機"},{"english":"compose a four-line clue","chinese":"創作四行線索"},{"english":"after collecting the clues","chinese":"收集線索後"},{"english":"write its own ending","chinese":"寫出自己的結局"},{"english":"present it in sixty seconds","chinese":"在六十秒內匯報"},{"english":"Publisher's Desk","chinese":"出版人工作枱"},{"english":"make English purposeful","chinese":"令英語有目的"},{"english":"that is why it would be powerful","chinese":"這就是它有力量的原因"},{"english":"read because they wanted clues","chinese":"因為想找線索而閱讀"},{"english":"listen because they needed evidence","chinese":"因為需要證據而聆聽"},{"english":"teammates depended on them","chinese":"隊友依靠他們"},{"english":"could not be completed without","chinese":"沒有……就不能完成"},{"english":"suit students of different abilities","chinese":"適合不同能力的學生"},{"english":"stronger students","chinese":"能力較強的學生"},{"english":"craft elegant endings","chinese":"寫出優雅的結局"},{"english":"less confident students","chinese":"較缺乏信心的學生"},{"english":"contribute by","chinese":"透過……作出貢獻"},{"english":"spotting key words","chinese":"找出關鍵詞"},{"english":"drawing maps","chinese":"繪畫地圖"},{"english":"reading short dialogues","chinese":"朗讀短對話"},{"english":"word banks","chinese":"詞彙庫"},{"english":"sentence starters","chinese":"句子開首提示"},{"english":"QR-code audio support","chinese":"QR code 音訊支援"},{"english":"few, if any","chinese":"即使有也很少"},{"english":"be left staring helplessly at","chinese":"被留下無助地望着"},{"english":"a blank page","chinese":"空白頁"},{"english":"in addition","chinese":"此外"},{"english":"introduce students to","chinese":"向學生介紹"},{"english":"the library itself","chinese":"圖書館本身"},{"english":"a silent warehouse of books","chinese":"沉默的書本倉庫"},{"english":"stories begin","chinese":"故事開始"},{"english":"questions grow","chinese":"問題滋長"},{"english":"curiosity is rewarded","chinese":"好奇心得到回報"},{"english":"all things considered","chinese":"總括而言"},{"english":"serve the same educational purpose","chinese":"達到相同的教育目的"},{"english":"in different but complementary ways","chinese":"以不同但互補的方式"},{"english":"the former","chinese":"前者"},{"english":"the latter","chinese":"後者"},{"english":"give students a voice","chinese":"給學生發聲的機會"},{"english":"give them a mission","chinese":"給他們一個任務"},{"english":"less distant","chinese":"沒那麼遙遠"},{"english":"less mechanical","chinese":"沒那麼機械化"},{"english":"far more memorable","chinese":"難忘得多"},{"english":"sincerely hope","chinese":"衷心希望"},{"english":"consider these suggestions","chinese":"考慮這些建議"},{"english":"be honoured to","chinese":"很榮幸能夠"},{"english":"provide student helpers","chinese":"提供學生助手"},{"english":"should the activities be adopted","chinese":"如活動獲採納"},{"english":"Yours faithfully","chinese":"謹啟"},{"english":"Chairperson, Poetry Club","chinese":"詩會主席"}]},"dse-writing-2015-part-b-q9":{"exerciseId":"dse-writing-2015-part-b-q9","essayKey":"","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=dse-writing-2015-part-b-q9","flashDeckId":"dse/writing/part-b/2015/Q9","paragraphs":[{"label":"Paragraph 1","english":"Dear Ms Li,","chinese":"親愛的李老師："},{"label":"Paragraph 2","english":"I hope you are well. As chairperson of the Reading Club, I am writing to recommend that we invite James Clear, author of Atomic Habits, to be our guest speaker for the “Meet the Author” evening during Reading Week. The purpose of this week is not simply to add another activity to the school calendar, but to help students see reading as useful, enjoyable and connected to their own lives. Given that many students are under pressure from tests and examinations, a book about small, realistic improvements would speak directly to their concerns. I therefore believe Mr Clear would be the most suitable choice - he can attract reluctant readers, improve students’ English through accessible non-fiction, and show them how to build a lasting reading habit.","chinese":"希望您一切安好。 作為閱讀學會主席，我寫這封電郵，是想建議我們邀請《Atomic Habits》的作者 James Clear 擔任閱讀週「Meet the Author」晚會的嘉賓講者。 這一週的目的不只是為校曆增添另一項活動，更是要幫助學生看見閱讀實用、有趣，並且與自己的生活息息相關。 考慮到許多學生正承受測驗和考試的壓力，一本關於細小而實際改善的書，會直接回應他們的憂慮。 因此，我相信 Clear 先生會是最合適的人選——他能吸引不太願意閱讀的學生，透過易懂的非小說作品提升學生的英語能力，並向他們展示如何建立持久的閱讀習慣。"},{"label":"Paragraph 3","english":"First, Mr Clear is an excellent choice because Atomic Habits is highly relevant to Hong Kong students. Many of us know that reading is beneficial; the problem is that we often fail to turn this knowledge into action. A student may buy an English book with enthusiasm, read ten pages on the first night, and then leave it untouched for three months. Sounds familiar, doesn’t it? Clear’s central message—that tiny repeated actions can lead to remarkable long-term change—directly addresses this difficulty. Instead of telling students vaguely to “read more”, he can show them how to make reading obvious, attractive, easy and satisfying. For example, students could place a short English book beside their bed, read two pages before using their phone, and record their progress on a tracker. Little by little, what once felt like a burden can become part of their identity. Put simply, inviting him would allow Reading Week to promote not only a love of books, but also the discipline needed to keep reading after the event.","chinese":"首先，Clear 先生是一個極佳人選，因為《Atomic Habits》與香港學生高度相關 我們很多人都知道閱讀有益；問題在於我們往往未能把這份認知轉化為行動 一名學生可能滿懷熱情地買了一本英文書，第一晚讀了十頁，然後把它放在一旁，三個月也沒有再碰。 聽起來很熟悉，對嗎？ Clear 的核心訊息——微小而重複的行動可以帶來顯著的長遠改變——正好直接回應這個困難。 與其含糊地叫學生「多閱讀」，他可以向他們展示如何讓閱讀變得明顯、吸引、容易而令人滿足。 例如，學生可以把一本較短的英文書放在床邊，在使用手機之前先讀兩頁，並在記錄表上記下自己的進度。 一點一點地，曾經像負擔的事情可以成為他們身份認同的一部分。 簡單來說，邀請他可以讓閱讀週推廣的不只是對書籍的喜愛，更包括活動結束後仍能持續閱讀所需要的紀律。"},{"label":"Paragraph 4","english":"Secondly, his book is particularly suitable for improving students’ English because it is practical, modern and accessible. Some students assume that good English can only be learned through classic novels or examination passages. This is not to say that literature is unimportant; rather, non-fiction like Atomic Habits can serve as a bridge for students who find long stories intimidating. The book introduces useful vocabulary connected with routines, motivation, identity, progress and self-control—topics students can use in speaking, writing and reflection. Better still, Clear’s style is well-structured, which makes it an excellent model for DSE writing. Students can observe how an argument is built: a problem is introduced, an example is given, a principle is explained, and an action step follows. This structure is as useful for writing an essay as it is for changing a habit.","chinese":"第二，他的書特別適合用來提升學生的英語能力，因為它實用、現代，而且容易理解。 有些學生以為，良好的英語能力只能透過經典小說或考試篇章來學習。 這並不代表文學不重要；更準確地說，像《Atomic Habits》這樣的非小說作品，可以成為一座橋樑，幫助那些對長篇故事感到畏懼的學生進入閱讀世界。 這本書介紹了與日常規律、動力、身份認同、進步和自我控制相關的實用詞彙——這些題材都可以被學生運用於說話、寫作和反思之中。 更理想的是，Clear 寫作風格結構清晰，令這本書成為 DSE 寫作的優秀範本 學生可以觀察一個論點如何建立起來：先提出一個問題，再給出一個例子，然後解釋一項原則，最後接上一個行動步驟。 這種結構對寫文章和改變習慣同樣有用。"},{"label":"Paragraph 5","english":"To make the evening engaging, I suggest that Mr Clear lead three activities. The first could be a short talk entitled “How to Build an English Reading Habit”. He could explain how students can start with a habit so small that it is almost impossible to refuse, such as reading one paragraph a day. The second activity could be a mini workshop called “Design Your Reading Environment”. Students would work in groups to redesign a typical student’s day, deciding where to place books, when to read, how to reduce distractions and how to reward themselves. Take a Form Five student, for example: by linking ten minutes of English reading to the end of dinner, he or she may create a realistic routine even during a busy term. Finally, we could hold a question-and-answer session about procrastination, motivation and consistency. To extend the impact, the Reading Club could launch a seven-day “Atomic Reading Challenge”, in which students read a little every day and post a short reflection outside the library.","chinese":"為了令晚會更具吸引力，我建議由 Clear 先生帶領三項活動。 第一項可以是一場題為「How to Build an English Reading Habit」的簡短演講 他可以解釋學生如何從小到幾乎無法拒絕的習慣開始，例如每天閱讀一段文字 第二項活動可以是一個名為「Design Your Reading Environment」小型工作坊 學生會分組重新設計一名典型學生的一天，決定書本應放在哪裡、何時閱讀、如何減少干擾，以及如何獎勵自己。 以一名中五學生為例：透過把十分鐘英文閱讀連繫到晚飯之後，他或她即使在繁忙的學期中，也可能建立一個現實可行的日常習慣。 最後，我們可以舉行一場關於拖延、動力和持續性的問答環節。 為了延續影響力，閱讀學會可以推出為期七天的「Atomic Reading Challenge」，讓學生每天閱讀一點，並在圖書館外張貼一段簡短反思。"},{"label":"Paragraph 6","english":"All things considered, I strongly recommend inviting James Clear for our “Meet the Author” evening. He would not only bring star appeal to Reading Week, but also give students a practical reason to pick up English books and keep going. If you approve of this suggestion, I would be delighted to help prepare the invitation email, design the reading tracker and collect questions from different classes. This event would help our students understand one simple truth - the more consistently we read, the more confidently we use English.","chinese":"綜合而言，我強烈建議邀請 James Clear 出席我們的「Meet the Author」晚會 他不僅能為閱讀週帶來明星吸引力，也能給學生一個實際理由去拿起英文書並持續讀下去。 如果您批准這項建議，我很樂意協助準備邀請電郵、設計閱讀記錄表，並向不同班別收集問題。 這項活動將幫助學生明白一個簡單道理——我們閱讀得越持續，使用英語時就越有信心。"},{"label":"Paragraph 7","english":"Yours sincerely,","chinese":"此致"},{"label":"Paragraph 8","english":"Chris Wong","chinese":"Chris Wong"},{"label":"Paragraph 9","english":"Chairperson, Reading Club","chinese":"閱讀學會主席"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"I hope you are well","chinese":"希望你一切安好"},{"english":"chairperson of","chinese":"……的主席"},{"english":"Reading Club","chinese":"閱讀學會"},{"english":"I am writing to recommend that","chinese":"我寫信建議"},{"english":"invite someone to be","chinese":"邀請某人成為"},{"english":"author of","chinese":"……的作者"},{"english":"guest speaker","chinese":"嘉賓講者"},{"english":"Meet the Author evening","chinese":"與作者見面晚會"},{"english":"during Reading Week","chinese":"在閱讀週期間"},{"english":"the purpose of","chinese":"……的目的"},{"english":"not simply to","chinese":"不只是為了"},{"english":"add another activity to","chinese":"加多一項活動到"},{"english":"school calendar","chinese":"學校行事曆"},{"english":"see reading as","chinese":"把閱讀視為"},{"english":"connected to their own lives","chinese":"與他們自己的生活有關"},{"english":"given that","chinese":"鑑於"},{"english":"under pressure from","chinese":"承受來自……的壓力"},{"english":"tests and examinations","chinese":"測驗和考試"},{"english":"small, realistic improvements","chinese":"細小而實際的改善"},{"english":"speak directly to","chinese":"直接回應"},{"english":"students' concerns","chinese":"學生的憂慮"},{"english":"I therefore believe","chinese":"因此我相信"},{"english":"the most suitable choice","chinese":"最合適的選擇"},{"english":"attract reluctant readers","chinese":"吸引抗拒閱讀的人"},{"english":"reluctant readers","chinese":"抗拒閱讀的人"},{"english":"accessible non-fiction","chinese":"易懂的非小說類作品"},{"english":"build a lasting reading habit","chinese":"建立持久的閱讀習慣"},{"english":"excellent choice","chinese":"出色的選擇"},{"english":"highly relevant to","chinese":"與……高度相關"},{"english":"beneficial","chinese":"有益的"},{"english":"fail to","chinese":"未能"},{"english":"turn knowledge into action","chinese":"把知識化為行動"},{"english":"with enthusiasm","chinese":"滿懷熱情地"},{"english":"on the first night","chinese":"在第一晚"},{"english":"leave it untouched","chinese":"把它放着不碰"},{"english":"sounds familiar","chinese":"聽起來很熟悉"},{"english":"central message","chinese":"核心訊息"},{"english":"tiny repeated actions","chinese":"細小而重複的行動"},{"english":"lead to","chinese":"導致；帶來"},{"english":"remarkable long-term change","chinese":"顯著的長遠改變"},{"english":"directly addresses","chinese":"直接處理"},{"english":"instead of","chinese":"而不是"},{"english":"vaguely","chinese":"含糊地"},{"english":"make reading obvious","chinese":"令閱讀變得明顯"},{"english":"make reading attractive","chinese":"令閱讀變得吸引"},{"english":"make reading easy","chinese":"令閱讀變得容易"},{"english":"make reading satisfying","chinese":"令閱讀帶來滿足感"},{"english":"place a book beside their bed","chinese":"把書放在床邊"},{"english":"before using their phone","chinese":"在使用電話之前"},{"english":"record their progress","chinese":"記錄進度"},{"english":"progress tracker","chinese":"進度記錄表"},{"english":"little by little","chinese":"一點一點地"},{"english":"what once felt like","chinese":"曾經感覺像……的事物"},{"english":"a burden","chinese":"負擔"},{"english":"become part of their identity","chinese":"成為他們身份的一部分"},{"english":"put simply","chinese":"簡單來說"},{"english":"allow Reading Week to","chinese":"讓閱讀週能夠"},{"english":"promote a love of books","chinese":"推廣對書本的熱愛"},{"english":"not only…, but also…","chinese":"不只……而且……"},{"english":"the discipline needed to","chinese":"做……所需的自律"},{"english":"keep reading","chinese":"持續閱讀"},{"english":"after the event","chinese":"活動之後"},{"english":"particularly suitable for","chinese":"特別適合"},{"english":"practical, modern and accessible","chinese":"實用、現代而易懂"},{"english":"assume that","chinese":"假設；以為"},{"english":"classic novels","chinese":"經典小說"},{"english":"examination passages","chinese":"考試篇章"},{"english":"this is not to say that","chinese":"這並不是說"},{"english":"literature","chinese":"文學"},{"english":"rather","chinese":"而是"},{"english":"serve as a bridge","chinese":"充當橋樑"},{"english":"find long stories intimidating","chinese":"覺得長篇故事令人卻步"},{"english":"intimidating","chinese":"令人卻步的"},{"english":"useful vocabulary connected with","chinese":"與……有關的實用詞彙"},{"english":"routines","chinese":"日常習慣；常規"},{"english":"motivation","chinese":"動力"},{"english":"identity","chinese":"身份認同"},{"english":"progress","chinese":"進步；進展"},{"english":"self-control","chinese":"自制力"},{"english":"speaking, writing and reflection","chinese":"說話、寫作和反思"},{"english":"better still","chinese":"更好的是"},{"english":"well-structured","chinese":"結構清晰的"},{"english":"an excellent model for","chinese":"……的出色範例"},{"english":"DSE writing","chinese":"文憑試寫作"},{"english":"observe how","chinese":"觀察如何"},{"english":"an argument is built","chinese":"論點如何建立"},{"english":"a problem is introduced","chinese":"問題被提出"},{"english":"an example is given","chinese":"例子被提出"},{"english":"a principle is explained","chinese":"原則被解釋"},{"english":"an action step follows","chinese":"接着是行動步驟"},{"english":"as useful for… as…","chinese":"對……和對……一樣有用"},{"english":"writing an essay","chinese":"寫文章"},{"english":"changing a habit","chinese":"改變習慣"},{"english":"make the evening engaging","chinese":"令晚會更吸引"},{"english":"lead three activities","chinese":"主持三項活動"},{"english":"a short talk entitled","chinese":"題為……的簡短演講"},{"english":"build an English reading habit","chinese":"建立英文閱讀習慣"},{"english":"start with a habit so small that","chinese":"從小到……的習慣開始"},{"english":"almost impossible to refuse","chinese":"幾乎不可能拒絕"},{"english":"one paragraph a day","chinese":"每日一段"},{"english":"mini workshop","chinese":"小型工作坊"},{"english":"Design Your Reading Environment","chinese":"設計你的閱讀環境"},{"english":"work in groups","chinese":"分組合作"},{"english":"redesign a typical student's day","chinese":"重新設計一個普通學生的一天"},{"english":"typical student","chinese":"普通學生"},{"english":"reduce distractions","chinese":"減少分心事物"},{"english":"reward themselves","chinese":"獎勵自己"},{"english":"take someone for example","chinese":"以某人為例"},{"english":"Form Five student","chinese":"中五學生"},{"english":"by linking… to…","chinese":"透過把……連繫到……"},{"english":"ten minutes of English reading","chinese":"十分鐘英文閱讀"},{"english":"the end of dinner","chinese":"晚飯結束時"},{"english":"create a realistic routine","chinese":"建立實際可行的日常安排"},{"english":"even during","chinese":"即使在……期間"},{"english":"a busy term","chinese":"繁忙的學期"},{"english":"question-and-answer session","chinese":"問答環節"},{"english":"procrastination","chinese":"拖延症"},{"english":"consistency","chinese":"持之以恆；一致性"},{"english":"extend the impact","chinese":"延伸影響"},{"english":"launch a challenge","chinese":"推出挑戰活動"},{"english":"seven-day challenge","chinese":"七日挑戰"},{"english":"Atomic Reading Challenge","chinese":"原子閱讀挑戰"},{"english":"in which","chinese":"在當中"},{"english":"read a little every day","chinese":"每天閱讀一點"},{"english":"post a short reflection","chinese":"張貼簡短反思"},{"english":"outside the library","chinese":"在圖書館外"},{"english":"all things considered","chinese":"綜合而言"},{"english":"strongly recommend inviting","chinese":"強烈建議邀請"},{"english":"bring star appeal to","chinese":"為……帶來明星吸引力"},{"english":"star appeal","chinese":"明星吸引力"},{"english":"practical reason to","chinese":"做……的實際理由"},{"english":"pick up English books","chinese":"拿起英文書閱讀"},{"english":"keep going","chinese":"堅持下去"},{"english":"approve of this suggestion","chinese":"批准這個建議"},{"english":"be delighted to","chinese":"很樂意"},{"english":"prepare the invitation email","chinese":"準備邀請電郵"},{"english":"design the reading tracker","chinese":"設計閱讀記錄表"},{"english":"collect questions from","chinese":"從……收集問題"},{"english":"different classes","chinese":"不同班別"},{"english":"one simple truth","chinese":"一個簡單道理"},{"english":"the more…, the more…","chinese":"越……就越……"},{"english":"consistently","chinese":"持之以恆地"},{"english":"confidently","chinese":"有信心地"},{"english":"Yours sincerely","chinese":"謹啟；此致"},{"english":"Chairperson, Reading Club","chinese":"閱讀學會主席"}]},"dse-writing-2016-part-a":{"exerciseId":"dse-writing-2016-part-a","essayKey":"","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=dse-writing-2016-part-a","flashDeckId":"dse/writing/part-a/2016","paragraphs":[{"label":"Advice on School Rules","english":"First, please take school rules seriously. Rules are not there to make your school life dull or restrictive. Rather, they are there to make sure everyone can learn in a safe and respectful environment. When you arrive on time, wear your uniform properly, keep the campus clean and use your phone responsibly, you are showing respect not only for the school, but also for the people around you. These habits may seem small at first, but over time, they assist you to become more disciplined and dependable. After all, students who can manage themselves well are more likely to make the most of every opportunity here.","chinese":"首先，請認真看待校規。 校規的存在，並不是為了令你的校園生活變得沉悶或受到束縛。 相反，校規是為了確保每個人都能在安全而互相尊重的環境中學習。 當你準時到校、正確穿著校服、保持校園清潔，並負責任地使用手機時，你所展現的尊重不只是對學校的尊重，也是對身邊人的尊重。 這些習慣一開始或許看似微小，但長遠而言，它們會幫助你變得更自律，也更值得信賴。 畢竟，能夠好好管理自己的學生，更有可能充分把握這裏遇到的每一個機會"},{"label":"Advice on Relationships","english":"At the same time, school life is never just about grades. The friends you make, the teachers you learn from and the people you meet in different activities will shape your experience in important ways. Be willing to listen, even when others see things differently. If you make a mistake, apologise sincerely; If someone looks lost or nervous, offer a hand, because a friendly word at the right moment may mean more than you realise.","chinese":"同時，校園生活從來不只是關於成績。 你結交的朋友、向其學習的老師，以及在不同活動中遇到的人，都會以重要的方式塑造你的校園經歷。 即使別人的看法與你不同，也要願意聆聽。 如果你犯了錯，請真誠道歉；如果有人看起來迷惘或緊張，請伸出援手，因為在適當時候一句友善的說話，可能比你想像中更有意義。"},{"label":"Closing","english":"As you begin this new chapter, I sincerely hope you will see our school not only as a place to study, but as a community where you can grow with confidence. I wish you all a happy and meaningful school year. Thank you.","chinese":"當你開始這個新篇章時，我衷心希望你不只把我們的學校視為一個學習的地方，也把它看作一個能讓你自信成長的社群。 我祝願大家度過一個愉快而有意義的學年。 謝謝大家。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"take school rules seriously","chinese":"認真看待校規"},{"english":"school rules","chinese":"校規"},{"english":"be not there to","chinese":"並不是為了……而存在"},{"english":"make your school life dull","chinese":"令你的校園生活沉悶"},{"english":"restrictive","chinese":"限制多的；束縛人的"},{"english":"rather","chinese":"相反；反而"},{"english":"make sure","chinese":"確保"},{"english":"safe and respectful environment","chinese":"安全而互相尊重的環境"},{"english":"arrive on time","chinese":"準時到達"},{"english":"wear your uniform properly","chinese":"整齊穿着校服"},{"english":"keep the campus clean","chinese":"保持校園清潔"},{"english":"use your phone responsibly","chinese":"負責任地使用電話"},{"english":"show respect for","chinese":"表示對……的尊重"},{"english":"not only for..., but also for...","chinese":"不但對……，也對……"},{"english":"the people around you","chinese":"你身邊的人"},{"english":"seem small at first","chinese":"起初看似微不足道"},{"english":"over time","chinese":"隨着時間過去"},{"english":"help you become","chinese":"幫助你變得……"},{"english":"more disciplined","chinese":"更自律"},{"english":"dependable","chinese":"可靠的"},{"english":"after all","chinese":"畢竟"},{"english":"manage themselves well","chinese":"好好管理自己"},{"english":"be more likely to","chinese":"更有可能"},{"english":"make the most of","chinese":"充分利用"},{"english":"every opportunity","chinese":"每一個機會"},{"english":"at the same time","chinese":"與此同時"},{"english":"school life","chinese":"校園生活"},{"english":"be never just about","chinese":"從來不只是關於……"},{"english":"grades","chinese":"成績"},{"english":"the friends you make","chinese":"你結交的朋友"},{"english":"the teachers you learn from","chinese":"你向其學習的老師"},{"english":"people you meet","chinese":"你遇到的人"},{"english":"in different activities","chinese":"在不同活動中"},{"english":"shape your experience","chinese":"塑你的經歷"},{"english":"in important ways","chinese":"以重要的方式"},{"english":"be willing to","chinese":"願意去……"},{"english":"listen","chinese":"聆聽"},{"english":"see things differently","chinese":"有不同看法"},{"english":"make a mistake","chinese":"犯錯"},{"english":"apologise sincerely","chinese":"真誠道歉"},{"english":"look lost or nervous","chinese":"看起來迷惘或緊張"},{"english":"offer a hand","chinese":"伸出援手"},{"english":"a friendly word","chinese":"一句友善的說話"},{"english":"at the right moment","chinese":"在適當時候"},{"english":"mean more than you realise","chinese":"比你想像中更有意義"},{"english":"begin this new chapter","chinese":"開始這個新篇章"},{"english":"sincerely hope","chinese":"衷心希望"},{"english":"not only as..., but as...","chinese":"不只視為……，而是視為……"},{"english":"a place to study","chinese":"學習的地方"},{"english":"a community where","chinese":"一個讓你……的群體"},{"english":"grow with confidence","chinese":"自信地成長"},{"english":"a happy and meaningful school year","chinese":"快樂而有意義的學年"},{"english":"thank you","chinese":"謝謝"}]},"dse-writing-2016-part-b-q2":{"exerciseId":"dse-writing-2016-part-b-q2","essayKey":"","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=dse-writing-2016-part-b-q2","flashDeckId":"dse/writing/part-b/2016/Q2","paragraphs":[{"label":"Paragraph 1","english":"Opening School Gates, Without Opening the Door to Chaos","chinese":"開放校門，不必打開混亂之門"},{"label":"Paragraph 2","english":"To the Editor","chinese":"致編輯："},{"label":"Paragraph 3","english":"Hong Kong Daily","chinese":""},{"label":"Paragraph 4","english":"Dear Editor,","chinese":"編輯先生／女士："},{"label":"Paragraph 5","english":"I am writing in response to the suggestion that schools in our community should allow members of the public to use their sports facilities after school hours. With public courts fully booked, private clubs expensive and open spaces shrinking, many residents now find it difficult to exercise regularly. This has led some people to ask whether school playgrounds, halls and courts should remain locked after the final bell. As far as I am concerned, the answer should be a qualified but firm yes. Provided that access is properly regulated, opening school facilities to the public would make wiser use of scarce resources, improve community health and strengthen trust between schools and residents.","chinese":"本人來函回應一項建議：本社區的學校應容許公眾人士在課後時間使用其體育設施。 隨著公共球場長期爆滿、私人會所收費高昂，以及開放空間不斷縮減，許多居民如今發現要定期運動相當困難。 這使一些人開始追問，在最後一節鐘聲響起之後，學校的操場、禮堂和球場是否仍應上鎖。 就我而言，答案應該是一個有條件但堅定的「是」。 只要出入安排受到妥善規管，向公眾開放學校設施，便能更明智地運用稀缺資源、改善社區健康，並加強學校與居民之間的信任。"},{"label":"Paragraph 6","english":"The first reason is that Hong Kong cannot afford to leave useful sports facilities idle when land is so limited. Building a new sports centre may require years of planning and construction, whereas using existing school facilities after lessons could increase community capacity almost immediately. Many schools already have basketball courts, covered playgrounds, badminton halls and small fitness areas. Once students have gone home and teachers have finished their activities, these spaces often serve no one. A school basketball court that stands empty from 6 p.m. to 9 p.m., for instance, could accommodate several one-hour sessions for teenagers, office workers and elderly residents. This is not a matter of taking something away from students; it is a matter of allowing public resources to serve the public more fully. In a crowded city, such efficiency is not optional. It is common sense.","chinese":"第一個原因是，在土地如此有限的情況下，香港實在承受不起讓有用體育設施閒置的代價。 興建一座新的體育中心可能需要多年規劃和施工；相比之下，在課後使用現有學校設施，幾乎能即時增加社區可用的體育空間。 許多學校已經設有籃球場、有蓋操場、羽毛球場館和小型健身區。 一旦學生回家、教師完成活動，這些空間往往便無人使用。 例如，一個由下午六時至晚上九時空置的學校籃球場，可以容納多個一小時使用時段，供青少年、上班族和長者使用。 這不單關乎從學生手中拿走某些東西；重點在於讓公共資源更充分地服務公眾 在一個擠迫的城市，這種效率並非可有可無。 這只是常識。"},{"label":"Paragraph 7","english":"The second reason is that wider access to sports facilities would promote healthier and more connected communities. Exercise is not just about winning matches; it is about building habits, relieving stress and giving people a constructive way to spend their evenings. Without affordable venues nearby, many residents simply give up. Teenagers may end up wandering around shopping centres, adults may remain glued to their screens after work, and elderly people may lose chances to stay active safely. By contrast, a well-run after-school booking scheme could give different groups a regular place to play basketball, practise table tennis, do stretching exercises or organise parent-child sports activities. For example, early evening slots could be reserved for youth teams, later slots for adult groups, and weekend mornings for elderly fitness classes. Such arrangements would not only improve physical health but also allow neighbours to meet one another. Schools would then become more than examination factories; they would become living parts of the community.","chinese":"第二個原因是，體育設施若能更廣泛開放，便能促進更健康、更有連繫的社區 運動不只關乎贏得比賽；它也關乎建立習慣、紓緩壓力，並讓人們有一種建設性的方式度過晚上。 如果附近沒有負擔得起的場地，許多居民最終只會放棄。 青少年最後可能在商場遊蕩，成年人下班後可能繼續黏在螢幕前，長者亦可能失去安全地保持活躍的機會。 相比之下，一個運作良好的課後預約制度，可以為不同群體提供固定場地，讓他們打籃球、練習乒乓球、做伸展運動，或舉辦親子體育活動。 例如，傍晚較早時段可以預留給青年隊伍，較晚時段可供成人團體使用，而週末上午則可安排長者健體班。 這些安排不僅能改善身體健康，也能讓鄰里彼此認識。 這樣一來，學校就會超越考試工廠的角色，成為社區中有生命力的一部分。"},{"label":"Paragraph 8","english":"The third reason is that the risks, while real, can be managed through clear rules rather than used as an excuse for doing nothing. Granted, schools have every reason to worry about security, damage to property and disruption to students. However, these concerns do not prove that the proposal is impractical; they prove that it must be designed carefully. Public users could be required to register in advance, pay a small maintenance fee and leave a deposit. Classrooms, staff rooms and laboratories should remain strictly out of bounds, while only designated sports areas are opened. Schools could also employ security guards, install access-control gates, keep CCTV in public zones and require community groups to sign responsibility agreements. In case of damage, the responsible group should pay for repairs. In case of school activities, student use must take priority. With these safeguards, the scheme would not be a free-for-all. Rather, it would be a controlled partnership in which rights come with responsibilities.","chinese":"第三個原因是，風險雖然真實存在，卻可以透過清晰規則加以管理，不應被用作無所作為的藉口。 誠然，學校完全有理由擔心保安、財物損壞以及對學生造成滋擾。 然而，這些憂慮並不能證明建議不可行；它們證明這項建議必須經過仔細設計 公眾使用者可被要求預先登記、支付小額維修費並繳交按金。 課室、教員室和實驗室應嚴格列為禁區，只有指定體育範圍才會開放。 學校也可以聘請保安員、安裝出入管制閘門、在公共區域保留閉路電視，並要求社區團體簽署責任協議。 如有損壞，負責團體應支付維修費用。 如有學校活動，學生使用必須享有優先權。 有了這些保障措施，這個計劃就不會變成人人任意使用的局面。 更準確地說，它會成為一種受控的夥伴關係，當中權利與責任相伴而來。"},{"label":"Paragraph 9","english":"All things considered, I support allowing the public to use school sports facilities after school hours, provided that schools, parents and residents agree on sensible conditions. The Education Bureau, district councils and school management committees should work together to launch pilot schemes in selected schools, consult parent-teacher associations and review the results after several months. The shortage of sports facilities will not disappear overnight, but we need not wait passively for a perfect solution. The time has come to open our school gates wisely, safely and generously.","chinese":"綜合而言，我支持公眾在課後時間使用學校體育設施，前提是學校、家長和居民能就合理條件達成共識。 教育局、區議會和學校管理委員會應該合作，在部分學校推行試驗計劃，諮詢家長教師會，並在數個月後檢討成效。 體育設施短缺的問題不會一夜之間消失，但我們不必被動等待一個完美方案 現在是時候以明智、安全和慷慨的方式打開校門了。"},{"label":"Paragraph 10","english":"Yours faithfully,","chinese":"謹啟"},{"label":"Paragraph 11","english":"Chris Wong","chinese":"Chris Wong"},{"label":"Paragraph 12","english":"A concerned resident","chinese":"一位關心社區的居民"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"opening school gates","chinese":"開放校園"},{"english":"without opening the door to chaos","chinese":"不引發混亂"},{"english":"to the Editor","chinese":"致編輯"},{"english":"Dear Editor","chinese":"編輯先生／女士鈞鑒"},{"english":"I am writing in response to","chinese":"本人寫信回應……"},{"english":"the suggestion that","chinese":"……的建議"},{"english":"in our community","chinese":"在我們社區"},{"english":"allow members of the public to","chinese":"允許公眾人士……"},{"english":"members of the public","chinese":"公眾人士"},{"english":"sports facilities","chinese":"體育設施"},{"english":"after school hours","chinese":"課後時間"},{"english":"public courts","chinese":"公共球場"},{"english":"fully booked","chinese":"預訂已滿"},{"english":"private clubs","chinese":"私人會所"},{"english":"open spaces","chinese":"休憩空間；開放空間"},{"english":"open spaces shrinking","chinese":"開放空間減少"},{"english":"find it difficult to","chinese":"覺得難以……"},{"english":"exercise regularly","chinese":"定期做運動"},{"english":"this has led some people to ask whether","chinese":"這令一些人提出是否……"},{"english":"school playgrounds","chinese":"學校操場"},{"english":"halls and courts","chinese":"禮堂和球場"},{"english":"remain locked","chinese":"繼續上鎖"},{"english":"after the final bell","chinese":"放學鐘聲響起後"},{"english":"as far as I am concerned","chinese":"就我而言"},{"english":"a qualified but firm yes","chinese":"有條件但堅定的同意"},{"english":"provided that","chinese":"只要；前提是"},{"english":"access is properly regulated","chinese":"使用權受到妥善規管"},{"english":"make wiser use of","chinese":"更明智地運用"},{"english":"scarce resources","chinese":"稀缺資源"},{"english":"improve community health","chinese":"改善社區健康"},{"english":"strengthen trust between","chinese":"加強……之間的信任"},{"english":"schools and residents","chinese":"學校和居民"},{"english":"the first reason is that","chinese":"第一個原因是"},{"english":"cannot afford to","chinese":"承受不起；不能夠"},{"english":"leave facilities idle","chinese":"讓設施閒置"},{"english":"land is so limited","chinese":"土地非常有限"},{"english":"building a new sports centre","chinese":"興建新的體育中心"},{"english":"require years of","chinese":"需要多年……"},{"english":"planning and construction","chinese":"規劃和建設"},{"english":"whereas","chinese":"然而"},{"english":"existing school facilities","chinese":"現有學校設施"},{"english":"after lessons","chinese":"課後"},{"english":"increase community capacity","chinese":"增加社區容量"},{"english":"almost immediately","chinese":"幾乎即時"},{"english":"covered playgrounds","chinese":"有蓋操場"},{"english":"badminton halls","chinese":"羽毛球場館"},{"english":"fitness areas","chinese":"健身區"},{"english":"once students have gone home","chinese":"學生回家後"},{"english":"serve no one","chinese":"沒有服務任何人"},{"english":"stand empty","chinese":"空置"},{"english":"accommodate","chinese":"容納"},{"english":"one-hour sessions","chinese":"一小時時段"},{"english":"elderly residents","chinese":"年長居民"},{"english":"not a matter of","chinese":"並不是……的問題"},{"english":"take something away from","chinese":"從……手中拿走某物"},{"english":"a matter of","chinese":"是……的問題"},{"english":"public resources","chinese":"公共資源"},{"english":"serve the public more fully","chinese":"更充分地服務公眾"},{"english":"in a crowded city","chinese":"在擠迫的城市中"},{"english":"such efficiency","chinese":"這種效率"},{"english":"not optional","chinese":"不是可有可無"},{"english":"common sense","chinese":"常識"},{"english":"wider access to","chinese":"更廣泛使用……的機會"},{"english":"promote healthier communities","chinese":"促進更健康的社區"},{"english":"more connected communities","chinese":"聯繫更緊密的社區"},{"english":"winning matches","chinese":"贏得比賽"},{"english":"building habits","chinese":"建立習慣"},{"english":"relieving stress","chinese":"紓緩壓力"},{"english":"a constructive way to","chinese":"一種有建設性的方式去……"},{"english":"spend their evenings","chinese":"度過晚上"},{"english":"affordable venues nearby","chinese":"附近負擔得起的場地"},{"english":"give up","chinese":"放棄"},{"english":"end up wandering around","chinese":"最後四處閒逛"},{"english":"shopping centres","chinese":"商場"},{"english":"remain glued to their screens","chinese":"一直黏着螢幕"},{"english":"lose chances to","chinese":"失去……的機會"},{"english":"stay active safely","chinese":"安全地保持活躍"},{"english":"by contrast","chinese":"相比之下"},{"english":"a well-run booking scheme","chinese":"管理良好的預訂計劃"},{"english":"different groups","chinese":"不同群體"},{"english":"a regular place to","chinese":"一個固定地方去……"},{"english":"practise table tennis","chinese":"練習乒乓球"},{"english":"stretching exercises","chinese":"伸展運動"},{"english":"parent-child sports activities","chinese":"親子體育活動"},{"english":"early evening slots","chinese":"傍晚早段時段"},{"english":"be reserved for","chinese":"預留給……"},{"english":"youth teams","chinese":"青少年隊伍"},{"english":"adult groups","chinese":"成人組別"},{"english":"weekend mornings","chinese":"週末早上"},{"english":"elderly fitness classes","chinese":"長者健體班"},{"english":"such arrangements","chinese":"這些安排"},{"english":"physical health","chinese":"身體健康"},{"english":"neighbours","chinese":"鄰居"},{"english":"more than examination factories","chinese":"不只是考試工廠"},{"english":"living parts of the community","chinese":"社區中有生命力的一部分"},{"english":"the risks, while real","chinese":"風險雖然真實存在"},{"english":"be managed through","chinese":"透過……管理"},{"english":"clear rules","chinese":"清晰規則"},{"english":"rather than used as an excuse","chinese":"而不是被用作藉口"},{"english":"an excuse for doing nothing","chinese":"不作為的藉口"},{"english":"granted","chinese":"誠然"},{"english":"have every reason to","chinese":"完全有理由去……"},{"english":"security","chinese":"保安"},{"english":"damage to property","chinese":"財物損毀"},{"english":"disruption to students","chinese":"對學生造成滋擾"},{"english":"these concerns do not prove that","chinese":"這些憂慮並不證明……"},{"english":"impractical","chinese":"不切實際"},{"english":"designed carefully","chinese":"經過仔細設計"},{"english":"be required to","chinese":"被要求"},{"english":"register in advance","chinese":"預先登記"},{"english":"pay a small maintenance fee","chinese":"支付小額保養費"},{"english":"maintenance fee","chinese":"保養費"},{"english":"leave a deposit","chinese":"繳付按金"},{"english":"staff rooms","chinese":"教員室"},{"english":"laboratories","chinese":"實驗室"},{"english":"remain strictly out of bounds","chinese":"嚴格禁止進入"},{"english":"designated sports areas","chinese":"指定體育範圍"},{"english":"employ security guards","chinese":"聘請保安員"},{"english":"install access-control gates","chinese":"安裝出入控制閘"},{"english":"access-control gates","chinese":"出入控制閘"},{"english":"keep CCTV in public zones","chinese":"在公共區域設置閉路電視"},{"english":"public zones","chinese":"公共區域"},{"english":"responsibility agreements","chinese":"責任協議"},{"english":"in case of damage","chinese":"如有損毀"},{"english":"responsible group","chinese":"負責團體"},{"english":"pay for repairs","chinese":"支付維修費"},{"english":"in case of school activities","chinese":"如遇學校活動"},{"english":"take priority","chinese":"優先"},{"english":"with these safeguards","chinese":"有了這些保障措施"},{"english":"safeguards","chinese":"保障措施"},{"english":"a free-for-all","chinese":"任意混亂的情況"},{"english":"a controlled partnership","chinese":"受規管的合作關係"},{"english":"rights come with responsibilities","chinese":"權利伴隨責任"},{"english":"all things considered","chinese":"總括而言"},{"english":"agree on sensible conditions","chinese":"就合理條件達成共識"},{"english":"sensible conditions","chinese":"合理條件"},{"english":"Education Bureau","chinese":"教育局"},{"english":"district councils","chinese":"區議會"},{"english":"school management committees","chinese":"學校管理委員會"},{"english":"work together to","chinese":"合作去……"},{"english":"launch pilot schemes","chinese":"推出試驗計劃"},{"english":"selected schools","chinese":"選定學校"},{"english":"consult parent-teacher associations","chinese":"諮詢家長教師會"},{"english":"parent-teacher associations","chinese":"家長教師會"},{"english":"review the results","chinese":"檢討成效"},{"english":"after several months","chinese":"數個月後"},{"english":"shortage of sports facilities","chinese":"體育設施短缺"},{"english":"disappear overnight","chinese":"一夜之間消失"},{"english":"need not wait passively for","chinese":"不必被動等待……"},{"english":"a perfect solution","chinese":"完美解決方案"},{"english":"the time has come to","chinese":"是時候……"},{"english":"wisely, safely and generously","chinese":"明智、安全而慷慨地"},{"english":"Yours faithfully","chinese":"謹啟"},{"english":"a concerned resident","chinese":"一名關心社區的居民"}]},"dse-writing-2016-part-b-q3":{"exerciseId":"dse-writing-2016-part-b-q3","essayKey":"","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=dse-writing-2016-part-b-q3","flashDeckId":"dse/writing/part-b/2016/Q3","paragraphs":[{"label":"Paragraph 1","english":"Beyond Hong Kong: Why Our Graduates Should Look Across Asia","chinese":"超越香港： 為何我們的畢業生應該放眼亞洲"},{"label":"Paragraph 2","english":"Every graduation season, the same uneasy question returns to our city - after years of study, where can young people find a meaningful first job? With many Hong Kong graduates facing fierce competition, schools and career advisers have begun to consider encouraging those who cannot secure local employment to explore other Asian cities, so that they can widen their choices and build stronger careers. As far as I am concerned, this suggestion deserves our firm support. Looking beyond Hong Kong is not a confession of failure; rather, it is a practical response to a crowded market. I would argue that graduates should consider other Asian cities because doing so expands their opportunities, sharpens their professional abilities and, in the long run, benefits Hong Kong itself.","chinese":"超越香港： 每逢畢業季節，同一個令人不安的問題都會再次回到我們的城市：經過多年學習之後，年輕人可以在哪裡找到一份有意義的第一份工作？ 面對許多香港畢業生激烈競爭，學校和升學就業輔導人員已開始考慮鼓勵那些無法在本地找到工作的畢業生探索亞洲其他城市，好讓他們擴闊選擇，建立更有實力的職業道路。 就我而言，這個建議值得我們堅定支持。 放眼香港以外，並非承認失敗；更準確地說，這是在面對擁擠就業市場時作出的務實回應。 我認為，畢業生應該考慮亞洲其他城市，因為這樣做能擴大他們的機會、磨練他們的專業能力，長遠而言也能令香港本身受惠。"},{"label":"Paragraph 3","english":"First and foremost, Asia offers a wider and more varied employment market than Hong Kong alone can provide. Hong Kong is dynamic, but it is also small. Each year, thousands of fresh graduates compete for similar entry-level posts in finance, marketing, education, design and technology. When too many applicants crowd into the same narrow doorway, even capable young people may be left waiting outside. By contrast, cities such as Singapore, Shenzhen, Taipei, Tokyo, Seoul and Bangkok may need different kinds of talent at different times. A business graduate who cannot find a local banking post may discover opportunities in Singapore’s fintech sector; a design student may find a place in Seoul’s creative industries; an engineering graduate may learn more quickly in Shenzhen’s technology firms. One person’s disappointment in Hong Kong can become another city’s opportunity. Instead of treating unemployment as a dead end, graduates can treat Asia as a larger map on which more doors are open.","chinese":"首先，亞洲所能提供的就業市場，比香港單一城市更廣闊，也更多元。 香港充滿活力，但城市規模始終有限。 每年，成千上萬的應屆畢業生都在金融、市場推廣、教育、設計和科技等領域，競逐相似的初級職位。 當太多求職者擠進同一道狹窄門口時，即使有能力的年輕人也可能被留在門外等待。 相比之下，新加坡、深圳、台北、東京、首爾和曼谷等城市，在不同時期可能需要不同種類的人才。 一名找不到本地銀行職位的商科畢業生，可能會在新加坡的金融科技行業發現機會；一名設計學生，可能會在首爾的創意產業找到位置；一名工程畢業生，則可能會在深圳的科技企業學得更快。 一個人在香港的失落，可以成為另一座城市的機遇。 與其把失業視為死胡同，畢業生可以把亞洲看作一幅更大的地圖，而在這幅地圖上，更多大門正在打開。"},{"label":"Paragraph 4","english":"The second reason is that working elsewhere can make graduates more mature, adaptable and employable. Employers today do not merely ask whether a candidate has a degree; they ask whether that person can solve problems, communicate across cultures and remain calm under pressure. Only by entering an unfamiliar environment can many graduates discover what they are truly capable of. Imagine a Hong Kong graduate working in a hotel group in Bangkok, negotiating with colleagues from different countries, handling customers whose expectations differ from our own, and learning to explain ideas in English, Putonghua or even a local language. With new opportunities come new risks, but every opportunity also comes with training. A graduate who has survived homesickness, cultural misunderstanding and demanding supervisors abroad will return not just with a line on a CV, but with judgment, confidence and resilience. That kind of education is as valuable as anything taught in a lecture theatre.","chinese":"第二個原因是，在其他地方工作能令畢業生更成熟、更具適應力，也更符合僱主要求。 今天的僱主問的，不只是一名候選人是否擁有學位；他們也會問，這個人能否解決問題、跨文化溝通，並在壓力下保持冷靜。 只有進入陌生環境，許多畢業生才能發現自己真正具備甚麼能力。 試想像一名香港畢業生在曼谷一家酒店集團工作，與來自不同國家的同事協商，處理期望與我們不同的顧客，並學習用英文、普通話，甚至當地語言解釋想法。 新的機會會帶來新的風險，但每個機會同時也帶來訓練。 一名在海外經歷過思鄉、文化誤解和嚴格上司考驗的畢業生，帶回來的不單是一行履歷上的經歷，更有判斷力、自信和韌性。 這種教育，與任何在講堂中學到的東西一樣寶貴。"},{"label":"Paragraph 5","english":"Thirdly, seeking work in Asia does not mean abandoning Hong Kong. Some people fear that encouraging graduates to leave will drain our city of talent. I take their concern seriously, but I do not think it follows. To say that young people should look beyond Hong Kong is not to say that they should forget Hong Kong. On the contrary, regional experience can turn them into bridges between Hong Kong and the rest of Asia. A graduate who spends three years in Singapore may later help a Hong Kong start-up understand Southeast Asian customers. Someone who works in a mainland technology company may bring back knowledge about production, logistics and innovation. Even if they do not return immediately, their networks can still connect back to our city. The question, therefore, is not whether graduates should stay or leave forever, but whether they should be brave enough to grow where opportunities appear.","chinese":"超越香港： 第三，到亞洲尋找工作機會，並不等於拋棄香港。 有些人擔心，鼓勵畢業生離開會令本城人才流失。 我認真看待他們的憂慮，但我不認為這個結論自然成立。 說年輕人應該放眼香港以外，並不等於說他們應該忘記香港。 相反，區域經驗能把他們變成連接香港與亞洲其他地區的橋樑。 一名在新加坡工作三年的畢業生，日後可能會幫助一家香港初創企業了解東南亞顧客。 在內地科技公司工作的人，可能會帶回有關生產、物流和創新的知識。 即使他們沒有立即回來，他們的人脈仍然可以與本城重新連結。 因此，關鍵不在於畢業生應該留下還是永遠離開，重點在於他們是否有足夠勇氣，在機會出現的地方成長。"},{"label":"Paragraph 6","english":"All things considered, I strongly support the suggestion that graduates who cannot find jobs in Hong Kong should look for opportunities in other Asian cities. The path may involve uncertainty, homesickness and practical costs, so students must research carefully, prepare financially and respect local cultures. Schools can invite alumni working in Asia to share their experiences; universities can strengthen regional internship schemes; and graduates themselves should build language skills and professional networks early. Gone are the days when a young person’s future had to fit inside one city. If Hong Kong’s graduates wish to stand tall in a competitive world, they should not ask, “Why leave?” They should ask, “Why not explore?”","chinese":"綜合而言，我強烈支持這個建議：無法在香港找到工作的畢業生，應該到亞洲其他城市尋找機會。 這條路可能涉及不確定性、思鄉之情和實際成本，因此學生必須謹慎研究、做好財務準備，並尊重當地文化。 學校可以邀請在亞洲工作的校友分享經驗；大學可以加強區域實習計劃；畢業生自己也應及早建立語言能力和專業人脈。 年輕人的未來必須被限制在一座城市之內的年代，已經過去了。 如果香港畢業生希望在競爭激烈的世界中昂首而立，他們不應問：「為甚麼要離開？」 他們應該問：「為甚麼不去探索？」"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"beyond Hong Kong","chinese":"香港以外"},{"english":"look across Asia","chinese":"放眼亞洲"},{"english":"graduation season","chinese":"畢業季節"},{"english":"uneasy question","chinese":"令人不安的問題"},{"english":"after years of study","chinese":"經過多年學習後"},{"english":"meaningful first job","chinese":"有意義的第一份工作"},{"english":"face fierce competition","chinese":"面對激烈競爭"},{"english":"career advisers","chinese":"就業輔導人員"},{"english":"consider encouraging","chinese":"考慮鼓勵"},{"english":"cannot secure local employment","chinese":"未能找到本地工作"},{"english":"explore other Asian cities","chinese":"探索其他亞洲城市"},{"english":"widen their choices","chinese":"擴闊選擇"},{"english":"build stronger careers","chinese":"建立更穩固的事業"},{"english":"as far as I am concerned","chinese":"就我而言"},{"english":"deserves our firm support","chinese":"值得我們堅定支持"},{"english":"looking beyond Hong Kong","chinese":"放眼香港以外"},{"english":"a confession of failure","chinese":"承認失敗"},{"english":"rather","chinese":"反而；更準確地說"},{"english":"practical response to","chinese":"對……的實際回應"},{"english":"crowded market","chinese":"擠迫的市場"},{"english":"I would argue that","chinese":"我會主張"},{"english":"expands their opportunities","chinese":"擴大他們的機會"},{"english":"sharpens their professional abilities","chinese":"提升他們的專業能力"},{"english":"in the long run","chinese":"長遠而言"},{"english":"benefits Hong Kong itself","chinese":"對香港本身有利"},{"english":"first and foremost","chinese":"首先；最重要的是"},{"english":"a wider and more varied employment market","chinese":"更廣闊和更多元的就業市場"},{"english":"Hong Kong alone","chinese":"單靠香港"},{"english":"dynamic","chinese":"充滿活力的"},{"english":"fresh graduates","chinese":"應屆畢業生"},{"english":"compete for","chinese":"競爭爭取"},{"english":"similar entry-level posts","chinese":"相似的入門職位"},{"english":"finance","chinese":"金融"},{"english":"marketing","chinese":"市場推廣"},{"english":"design and technology","chinese":"設計及科技"},{"english":"applicants","chinese":"申請者"},{"english":"crowd into","chinese":"擠進"},{"english":"the same narrow doorway","chinese":"同一扇狹窄的門"},{"english":"capable young people","chinese":"有能力的年輕人"},{"english":"be left waiting outside","chinese":"被留在門外等候"},{"english":"by contrast","chinese":"相比之下"},{"english":"cities such as","chinese":"例如……的城市"},{"english":"different kinds of talent","chinese":"不同類型的人才"},{"english":"at different times","chinese":"在不同時候"},{"english":"business graduate","chinese":"商科畢業生"},{"english":"local banking post","chinese":"本地銀行職位"},{"english":"discover opportunities in","chinese":"在……發現機會"},{"english":"Singapore's fintech sector","chinese":"新加坡金融科技行業"},{"english":"design student","chinese":"設計學生"},{"english":"find a place in","chinese":"在……找到位置"},{"english":"creative industries","chinese":"創意產業"},{"english":"engineering graduate","chinese":"工程畢業生"},{"english":"technology firms","chinese":"科技公司"},{"english":"one person's disappointment","chinese":"一個人的失望"},{"english":"another city's opportunity","chinese":"另一個城市的機會"},{"english":"instead of treating…as…","chinese":"與其把……視為……"},{"english":"unemployment","chinese":"失業"},{"english":"a dead end","chinese":"死胡同"},{"english":"a larger map","chinese":"更大的地圖"},{"english":"more doors are open","chinese":"更多機會之門打開"},{"english":"working elsewhere","chinese":"到其他地方工作"},{"english":"mature","chinese":"成熟"},{"english":"adaptable","chinese":"適應力強的"},{"english":"employable","chinese":"更具就業能力"},{"english":"employers today","chinese":"現今僱主"},{"english":"not merely ask whether","chinese":"不只是問是否"},{"english":"candidate","chinese":"求職者"},{"english":"solve problems","chinese":"解決問題"},{"english":"communicate across cultures","chinese":"跨文化溝通"},{"english":"remain calm under pressure","chinese":"在壓力下保持冷靜"},{"english":"only by entering","chinese":"只有透過進入"},{"english":"unfamiliar environment","chinese":"陌生環境"},{"english":"discover what they are truly capable of","chinese":"發現自己真正能做到甚麼"},{"english":"imagine","chinese":"試想"},{"english":"hotel group","chinese":"酒店集團"},{"english":"negotiating with","chinese":"與……協商"},{"english":"colleagues from different countries","chinese":"來自不同國家的同事"},{"english":"handling customers","chinese":"接待顧客；處理顧客需要"},{"english":"expectations differ from","chinese":"期望與……不同"},{"english":"explain ideas in","chinese":"用……解釋想法"},{"english":"local language","chinese":"當地語言"},{"english":"with new opportunities come new risks","chinese":"新機會伴隨新風險"},{"english":"comes with training","chinese":"伴隨訓練"},{"english":"survive homesickness","chinese":"捱過思鄉"},{"english":"cultural misunderstanding","chinese":"文化誤解"},{"english":"demanding supervisors","chinese":"要求高的上司"},{"english":"abroad","chinese":"在海外"},{"english":"not just with…but with…","chinese":"不只是帶著……而是帶著……"},{"english":"a line on a CV","chinese":"履歷上的一行"},{"english":"judgment","chinese":"判斷力"},{"english":"confidence and resilience","chinese":"信心和抗逆力"},{"english":"as valuable as","chinese":"與……一樣有價值"},{"english":"lecture theatre","chinese":"演講廳；大講堂"},{"english":"seeking work in Asia","chinese":"在亞洲尋找工作"},{"english":"abandoning Hong Kong","chinese":"放棄香港"},{"english":"fear that","chinese":"擔心"},{"english":"drain our city of talent","chinese":"令我們城市人才流失"},{"english":"take their concern seriously","chinese":"認真看待他們的憂慮"},{"english":"I do not think it follows","chinese":"我不認為這必然成立"},{"english":"to say that…is not to say that…","chinese":"說……並不是說……"},{"english":"forget Hong Kong","chinese":"忘記香港"},{"english":"on the contrary","chinese":"相反"},{"english":"regional experience","chinese":"區域經驗"},{"english":"turn them into bridges","chinese":"把他們變成橋樑"},{"english":"the rest of Asia","chinese":"亞洲其他地區"},{"english":"spend three years in","chinese":"在……度過三年"},{"english":"start-up","chinese":"初創企業"},{"english":"Southeast Asian customers","chinese":"東南亞客戶"},{"english":"mainland technology company","chinese":"內地科技公司"},{"english":"bring back knowledge about","chinese":"帶回關於……的知識"},{"english":"production","chinese":"生產"},{"english":"logistics","chinese":"物流"},{"english":"innovation","chinese":"創新"},{"english":"even if","chinese":"即使"},{"english":"return immediately","chinese":"立即回來"},{"english":"professional networks","chinese":"專業人脈網絡"},{"english":"connect back to","chinese":"重新連接到"},{"english":"the question, therefore, is not whether…but whether…","chinese":"因此，問題不是是否……而是是否……"},{"english":"stay or leave forever","chinese":"留下或永遠離開"},{"english":"brave enough to grow","chinese":"有足夠勇氣成長"},{"english":"where opportunities appear","chinese":"在機會出現的地方"},{"english":"all things considered","chinese":"綜合考慮各方面"},{"english":"strongly support the suggestion","chinese":"堅決支持這項建議"},{"english":"look for opportunities","chinese":"尋找機會"},{"english":"the path may involve","chinese":"這條路可能涉及"},{"english":"uncertainty","chinese":"不確定性"},{"english":"homesickness","chinese":"思鄉"},{"english":"practical costs","chinese":"實際開支"},{"english":"research carefully","chinese":"仔細研究"},{"english":"prepare financially","chinese":"在財政上做好準備"},{"english":"respect local cultures","chinese":"尊重當地文化"},{"english":"invite alumni","chinese":"邀請校友"},{"english":"alumni working in Asia","chinese":"在亞洲工作的校友"},{"english":"share their experiences","chinese":"分享他們的經驗"},{"english":"strengthen regional internship schemes","chinese":"加強區域實習計劃"},{"english":"regional internship schemes","chinese":"區域實習計劃"},{"english":"build language skills","chinese":"建立語言能力"},{"english":"professional networks","chinese":"專業人脈"},{"english":"gone are the days when","chinese":"……的日子已經過去"},{"english":"fit inside one city","chinese":"局限於一個城市之內"},{"english":"stand tall","chinese":"堂堂正正地站穩"},{"english":"competitive world","chinese":"競爭激烈的世界"},{"english":"why leave?","chinese":"為甚麼要離開？"},{"english":"why not explore?","chinese":"為甚麼不探索？"}]},"dse-writing-2016-part-b-q4":{"exerciseId":"dse-writing-2016-part-b-q4","essayKey":"","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=dse-writing-2016-part-b-q4","flashDeckId":"dse/writing/part-b/2016/Q4","paragraphs":[{"label":"Paragraph 1","english":"Protection, Not Possession","chinese":"保護，不等於佔有"},{"label":"Paragraph 2","english":"Dear Editor,","chinese":"編輯先生／女士："},{"label":"Paragraph 3","english":"It has recently been reported that some parents in Asian countries are installing apps on their children’s mobile phones to monitor their activities, hoping to make sure that these devices are used responsibly. With phones now serving as schoolbags, cameras, libraries, diaries and social spaces all at once, parents are understandably anxious about gaming addiction, online scams and cyberbullying. Granted, parents have a duty to protect their children. However, I do not agree with turning monitoring apps into a normal parenting tool. As far as I am concerned, such surveillance damages trust, weakens self-discipline and creates risks that are easily overlooked.","chinese":"近日有報道指出，一些亞洲國家的父母正在子女的手機上安裝應用程式，以監察他們的活動，希望確保這些裝置能被負責任地使用。 隨著手機如今同時扮演書包、相機、圖書館、日記和社交空間的角色，父母對遊戲成癮、網絡詐騙和網絡欺凌感到焦慮，是可以理解的。 誠然，父母有責任保護自己的孩子。 然而，我不同意把監察應用程式變成一種正常的育兒工具。 就我而言，這種監視會破壞信任、削弱自律，並製造一些容易被忽視的風險。"},{"label":"Paragraph 4","english":"First and foremost, monitoring apps invade a young person’s privacy and, in doing so, poison the trust between parents and children. A teenager’s phone is not merely a machine; it contains private conversations, awkward questions, friendship problems, photos, draft messages and sometimes cries for help. When parents read, track or record everything, the child is no longer being guided; he or she is being investigated. The result is not necessarily honesty. More often than not, it is secrecy. A fifteen-year-old who knows every message may be checked may simply create another account, borrow a friend’s phone or delete conversations before going home. Worse still, if a student is struggling with bullying, anxiety or a broken friendship, he may hide it for fear that his parents will overreact. What parents gain in information, they may lose in openness. Responsible use begins with trust; without it, supervision becomes suspicion.","chinese":"首先，監察應用程式侵犯年輕人的私隱，並在過程中毒害父母與子女之間的信任。 青少年的手機不單是一部機器；它包含私人對話、尷尬的問題、友情困擾、相片、訊息草稿，有時甚至是求助的呼聲。 當父母閱讀、追蹤或記錄一切時，孩子不再是在被引導；他或她其實是在被調查。 結果未必一定是誠實。 更多時候，帶來的是隱瞞。 一名知道每則訊息都可能被檢查的十五歲孩子，可能只會另開帳戶、借用朋友的手機，或在回家前刪除對話。 更糟的是，如果一名學生正在承受欺凌、焦慮或一段破裂的友誼，他可能會因為害怕父母反應過激而把事情藏起來。 父母在資訊上得到的，可能會在坦誠上失去。 負責任地使用手機始於信任；沒有信任，監督就會變成懷疑。"},{"label":"Paragraph 5","english":"Secondly, constant monitoring does not teach responsibility. It only teaches children how to behave when they are being watched. The point is not whether children should use phones freely, but whether they can learn to make wise choices when no one is standing behind them. If an app blocks games after thirty minutes, a child may stop playing, but he may not understand why sleep, revision and face-to-face conversation matter. By contrast, if parents sit down with their children to set screen-time rules, discuss online etiquette and review habits together, children learn the reasons behind the rules. Take a Secondary Four student preparing for exams, for example. What he needs is not simply an app that shuts down Instagram, but the ability to mute notifications, plan revision breaks and resist the pressure to reply instantly to every group chat. Only by giving young people room to practise judgment can parents help them become disciplined users rather than obedient ones.","chinese":"第二，持續監察並不能教會孩子責任感。 它只會教孩子如何在被觀看時行事。 重點不在於孩子是否應該自由使用手機，重點在於他們能否在沒有人站在身後時學會作出明智選擇。 如果一個應用程式在三十分鐘後封鎖遊戲，孩子可能會停止玩樂，但他未必明白為甚麼睡眠、溫習和面對面的交流如此重要。 相比之下，如果父母坐下來與孩子一起訂立螢幕時間規則、討論網絡禮儀並共同檢視習慣，孩子便會明白規則背後的原因。 以一名正在準備考試的中四學生為例。 他需要的並非單純是一個會關閉 Instagram 的應用程式；真正重要的，是把通知靜音、安排溫習休息，並抵抗即時回覆每個群組聊天壓力的能力。 只有給予年輕人練習判斷的空間，父母才能幫助他們成為有紀律的使用者，而非只懂服從的人。"},{"label":"Paragraph 6","english":"Thirdly, monitoring apps can create new dangers while giving parents a false sense of security. Many of these apps collect sensitive information, including locations, browsing records and contact lists. If such data is leaked, misused or accessed by the wrong person, the child may be placed in greater danger, not less. Besides, technology works only up to a point. An app may show that a child is at school, but it cannot tell whether he feels lonely there. It may record screen time, but it cannot detect whether a joke in a group chat has become humiliation. It may block one website, only for the problem to move elsewhere. Parents who rely too heavily on monitoring may end up looking at dashboards instead of listening at the dinner table. A better approach would be a transparent family digital agreement: phones outside bedrooms after bedtime, no devices during meals, permission before downloading unknown apps, and emergency location-sharing only with the child’s knowledge. In serious cases, such as repeated contact from strangers or clear signs of addiction, temporary monitoring may be justified, but it should be explained, limited and reviewed.","chinese":"第三，監察應用程式會製造新的危險，同時令父母產生一種虛假的安全感。 這些應用程式有許多會收集敏感資料，包括位置、瀏覽記錄和聯絡人清單。 如果這些資料被洩露、被濫用或被不當人士取用，孩子可能會陷入更大的危險，而非更安全。 此外，科技只能在一定程度上發揮作用。 一個應用程式可能顯示孩子在學校，但它無法告訴父母他在那裡是否感到孤單 它可能記錄螢幕使用時間，但無法察覺群組聊天中一個笑話是否已變成羞辱 它可能封鎖一個網站，問題卻只是轉移到別處。 過度依賴監察的父母，到最後可能只是在查看數據面板，卻沒有在飯桌上聆聽孩子。 更好的做法，是訂立一份透明的家庭數碼協議：睡前把手機放在睡房外、用餐時不使用裝置、下載不明應用程式前先取得准許，以及只在孩子知情的情況下進行緊急位置分享。 在嚴重情況下，例如陌生人反覆聯絡或出現明顯成癮跡象，臨時監察也許有其合理之處，但必須加以解釋、限制和檢討。"},{"label":"Paragraph 7","english":"All things considered, I believe parents should not install monitoring apps as a routine way to control their children’s phones. Protection is necessary, but protection should not become possession. The time has come for parents, schools and teenagers to work together - teach digital literacy, set clear boundaries, talk about online pressure and adjust rules as children mature. A mobile phone should be a tool for learning and connection, not a leash. If we want young people to act responsibly, we must give them not only rules to follow, but also trust to grow into.","chinese":"綜合而言，我認為父母不應把安裝監察應用程式視為控制子女手機的常規方式 保護是必要的，但保護不應變成佔有。 現在是父母、學校和青少年攜手合作的時候——教授數碼素養、訂立清晰界線、討論網絡壓力，並隨著孩子成熟而調整規則。 手機應該是用來學習和連繫的工具，不應成為拴住孩子的繩索。 如果我們希望年輕人負責任地行事，就必須給予他們的不只是需要遵守的規則，也包括能讓他們逐漸成熟的信任。"},{"label":"Paragraph 8","english":"Yours faithfully,","chinese":"謹此致意，"},{"label":"Paragraph 9","english":"Chris Wong","chinese":"Chris Wong"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"Dear Editor","chinese":"尊敬的編輯"},{"english":"protection, not possession","chinese":"保護，而不是佔有"},{"english":"It has recently been reported that","chinese":"最近有報道指"},{"english":"install apps on","chinese":"在……安裝應用程式"},{"english":"children's mobile phones","chinese":"子女的手機"},{"english":"monitor their activities","chinese":"監察他們的活動"},{"english":"hoping to make sure that","chinese":"希望確保"},{"english":"be used responsibly","chinese":"被負責任地使用"},{"english":"serve as","chinese":"充當；用作"},{"english":"all at once","chinese":"同時"},{"english":"understandably anxious about","chinese":"對……感到焦慮是可以理解的"},{"english":"gaming addiction","chinese":"遊戲成癮"},{"english":"online scams","chinese":"網上騙案"},{"english":"cyberbullying","chinese":"網絡欺凌"},{"english":"Granted","chinese":"誠然"},{"english":"have a duty to","chinese":"有責任去"},{"english":"turn something into","chinese":"把……變成"},{"english":"monitoring apps","chinese":"監控應用程式"},{"english":"a normal parenting tool","chinese":"常規育兒工具"},{"english":"As far as I am concerned","chinese":"就我而言"},{"english":"such surveillance","chinese":"這種監控"},{"english":"damage trust","chinese":"破壞信任"},{"english":"weaken self-discipline","chinese":"削弱自律"},{"english":"create risks","chinese":"製造風險"},{"english":"easily overlooked","chinese":"容易被忽略"},{"english":"first and foremost","chinese":"首先；最重要的是"},{"english":"invade someone's privacy","chinese":"侵犯某人的私隱"},{"english":"a young person's privacy","chinese":"年輕人的私隱"},{"english":"in doing so","chinese":"這樣做的同時"},{"english":"poison the trust between","chinese":"破壞……之間的信任"},{"english":"not merely","chinese":"不只是"},{"english":"private conversations","chinese":"私人對話"},{"english":"awkward questions","chinese":"尷尬的問題"},{"english":"friendship problems","chinese":"友情問題"},{"english":"draft messages","chinese":"訊息草稿"},{"english":"cries for help","chinese":"求助信號"},{"english":"read, track or record","chinese":"閱讀、追蹤或記錄"},{"english":"no longer being guided","chinese":"不再是被引導"},{"english":"be investigated","chinese":"被調查"},{"english":"the result is not necessarily","chinese":"結果未必是"},{"english":"more often than not","chinese":"往往；多數情況下"},{"english":"create another account","chinese":"開設另一個帳戶"},{"english":"borrow a friend's phone","chinese":"借朋友的手機"},{"english":"delete conversations","chinese":"刪除對話"},{"english":"worse still","chinese":"更糟的是"},{"english":"struggle with","chinese":"受……困擾"},{"english":"bullying","chinese":"欺凌"},{"english":"anxiety","chinese":"焦慮"},{"english":"a broken friendship","chinese":"破裂的友情"},{"english":"hide it for fear that","chinese":"因害怕……而隱瞞"},{"english":"overreact","chinese":"反應過激"},{"english":"What parents gain in…, they may lose in…","chinese":"父母在……方面得到的，可能會在……方面失去"},{"english":"openness","chinese":"坦誠；開放溝通"},{"english":"responsible use","chinese":"負責任的使用方式"},{"english":"begin with trust","chinese":"由信任開始"},{"english":"supervision becomes suspicion","chinese":"監督變成猜疑"},{"english":"constant monitoring","chinese":"持續監控"},{"english":"teach responsibility","chinese":"教導責任感"},{"english":"behave when they are being watched","chinese":"在被監視時表現得規矩"},{"english":"the point is not whether…, but whether…","chinese":"重點不在於是否……，而在於是否……"},{"english":"use phones freely","chinese":"自由使用手機"},{"english":"make wise choices","chinese":"作出明智選擇"},{"english":"when no one is standing behind them","chinese":"當沒有人在背後監督時"},{"english":"block games after thirty minutes","chinese":"三十分鐘後封鎖遊戲"},{"english":"stop playing","chinese":"停止玩"},{"english":"understand why","chinese":"明白為甚麼"},{"english":"revision","chinese":"溫習"},{"english":"face-to-face conversation","chinese":"面對面交談"},{"english":"matter","chinese":"重要"},{"english":"by contrast","chinese":"相比之下"},{"english":"sit down with","chinese":"坐下來與……"},{"english":"set screen-time rules","chinese":"訂立屏幕使用時間規則"},{"english":"discuss online etiquette","chinese":"討論網上禮儀"},{"english":"review habits together","chinese":"一起檢視習慣"},{"english":"the reasons behind the rules","chinese":"規則背後的原因"},{"english":"take…, for example","chinese":"以……為例"},{"english":"prepare for exams","chinese":"準備考試"},{"english":"not simply…, but…","chinese":"不只是……，而是……"},{"english":"shut down Instagram","chinese":"關閉 Instagram"},{"english":"the ability to","chinese":"……的能力"},{"english":"mute notifications","chinese":"將通知靜音"},{"english":"plan revision breaks","chinese":"安排溫習小休"},{"english":"resist the pressure to","chinese":"抵抗……的壓力"},{"english":"reply instantly to","chinese":"立即回覆"},{"english":"group chat","chinese":"群組聊天"},{"english":"only by giving… can…","chinese":"只有透過給予……才可以……"},{"english":"room to practise judgment","chinese":"練習判斷的空間"},{"english":"disciplined users","chinese":"自律的使用者"},{"english":"rather than obedient ones","chinese":"而不是只懂服從的人"},{"english":"create new dangers","chinese":"製造新的危險"},{"english":"a false sense of security","chinese":"虛假的安全感"},{"english":"collect sensitive information","chinese":"收集敏感資料"},{"english":"sensitive information","chinese":"敏感資料"},{"english":"browsing records","chinese":"瀏覽紀錄"},{"english":"contact lists","chinese":"聯絡人名單"},{"english":"data is leaked","chinese":"資料外洩"},{"english":"be misused","chinese":"被濫用"},{"english":"accessed by the wrong person","chinese":"被不當人士取得"},{"english":"be placed in greater danger","chinese":"陷入更大危險"},{"english":"not less","chinese":"而不是更少"},{"english":"work only up to a point","chinese":"只在某程度上有效"},{"english":"show that","chinese":"顯示"},{"english":"cannot tell whether","chinese":"無法判斷是否"},{"english":"feel lonely","chinese":"感到孤單"},{"english":"record screen time","chinese":"記錄屏幕使用時間"},{"english":"detect whether","chinese":"偵測是否"},{"english":"become humiliation","chinese":"變成羞辱"},{"english":"block one website","chinese":"封鎖一個網站"},{"english":"move elsewhere","chinese":"轉移到其他地方"},{"english":"rely too heavily on","chinese":"過度依賴"},{"english":"end up doing","chinese":"最終變成做……"},{"english":"dashboards","chinese":"數據面板"},{"english":"instead of listening","chinese":"而不是聆聽"},{"english":"at the dinner table","chinese":"在飯桌上"},{"english":"a better approach","chinese":"更好的做法"},{"english":"transparent","chinese":"透明的"},{"english":"family digital agreement","chinese":"家庭數碼使用協議"},{"english":"phones outside bedrooms after bedtime","chinese":"睡覺時間後手機放在睡房外"},{"english":"no devices during meals","chinese":"用膳時不使用電子裝置"},{"english":"permission before downloading unknown apps","chinese":"下載不明應用程式前先獲准"},{"english":"emergency location-sharing","chinese":"緊急位置分享"},{"english":"with the child's knowledge","chinese":"在孩子知情的情況下"},{"english":"in serious cases","chinese":"在嚴重情況下"},{"english":"repeated contact from strangers","chinese":"陌生人反覆聯絡"},{"english":"clear signs of addiction","chinese":"明顯的成癮跡象"},{"english":"temporary monitoring","chinese":"暫時監控"},{"english":"may be justified","chinese":"可能有合理理由"},{"english":"explained, limited and reviewed","chinese":"經解釋、有限度並定期檢討"},{"english":"all things considered","chinese":"綜合而言"},{"english":"as a routine way to","chinese":"作為常規方式去"},{"english":"control their children's phones","chinese":"控制子女的手機"},{"english":"Protection is necessary","chinese":"保護是必要的"},{"english":"protection should not become possession","chinese":"保護不應變成佔有"},{"english":"The time has come for","chinese":"是時候……"},{"english":"work together","chinese":"合作"},{"english":"teach digital literacy","chinese":"教授數碼素養"},{"english":"set clear boundaries","chinese":"訂立清晰界線"},{"english":"online pressure","chinese":"網上壓力"},{"english":"adjust rules","chinese":"調整規則"},{"english":"as children mature","chinese":"隨着孩子成熟"},{"english":"a tool for learning and connection","chinese":"學習和聯繫的工具"},{"english":"not a leash","chinese":"不是牽制人的繩索"},{"english":"act responsibly","chinese":"負責任地行事"},{"english":"not only rules to follow, but also trust to grow into","chinese":"不但需要可遵守的規則，也需要可讓他們成長的信任"},{"english":"Yours faithfully","chinese":"此致敬禮"}]},"dse-writing-2016-part-b-q5":{"exerciseId":"dse-writing-2016-part-b-q5","essayKey":"","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=dse-writing-2016-part-b-q5","flashDeckId":"dse/writing/part-b/2016/Q5","paragraphs":[{"label":"Paragraph 1","english":"Still Hot, Still Human: Why Dai Pai Dongs Deserve a Future","chinese":"仍然熱騰騰，仍然有人情味：為甚麼大牌檔值得擁有未來"},{"label":"Paragraph 2","english":"In Hong Kong, street life used to announce itself before we even saw it: the clatter of woks, the hiss of blue flames and the smell of fried noodles drifting through a crowded pavement. Yet the open-air dai pai dong, once part of this urban music, is being pushed aside by redevelopment, rising rents, licensing restrictions and chain restaurants. This has made citizens, officials and students consider whether such stalls should be left to disappear, or whether they should be preserved so the city can remain alive. As far as I am concerned, dai pai dongs are worth preserving not merely because they are old, but because they protect our shared memory, sustain human connection and give future generations a taste of an authentic Hong Kong.","chinese":"在香港，街頭生活昔日總會在我們看見它之前，先行宣告自己的存在：鐵鑊鏗鏘作響，藍色爐火嘶嘶燃燒，炒麵香氣在擁擠的行人路上飄散。 然而，露天大牌檔曾經是這首城市樂章的一部分，如今卻正被重建、租金上升、牌照限制和連鎖食肆一步步擠到邊緣。 這種情況令市民、官員和學生都開始思考，這些攤檔是否應該被任由消失，還是應該被保存下來，好讓這座城市繼續保有生命力。 就我而言，大牌檔值得保存，並不單因為它們古老，更因為它們守護我們共同的記憶、維繫人與人之間的連繫，並讓下一代品嚐到真正香港的味道。"},{"label":"Paragraph 3","english":"To begin with, dai pai dongs are living archives of Hong Kong history. Unlike a museum display behind glass, a street stall allows history to be tasted, heard and spoken. A plate of wok-fried beef noodles tells us how earlier generations turned cheap ingredients into comfort; a battered folding table shows how families built livelihoods with limited space. Few, if any, chain restaurants can carry this density of memory. Take an old stall in Sham Shui Po, for example: its plastic stools may not look elegant, yet every scratch on them suggests years of office workers, taxi drivers, students and elderly neighbours sitting down for the same honest meal. What matters is not decoration, but continuity. If these stalls vanish, the loss will not be limited to food. We will also lose the language of hawkers, the rhythm of Cantonese orders and the evidence that Hong Kong was built not only by bankers and developers, but also by people who worked beside hot stoves late into the night. Preserving dai pai dongs is therefore an act of cultural respect.","chinese":"首先，大牌檔是香港歷史的活檔案。 與隔着玻璃的博物館展品不同，街頭攤檔讓歷史可以被品嚐、被聽見、被說出來。 一碟鑊炒牛肉麵告訴我們，上一代如何把廉價食材變成慰藉；一張破舊折枱則展示出許多家庭如何在有限空間中建立生計。 即使有連鎖食肆能承載這種記憶厚度，數量也寥寥無幾。 以深水埗一間老攤檔為例：它的塑膠凳看起來也許不算優雅，但每一道刮痕都彷彿訴說着多年來上班族、的士司機、學生和年長街坊坐下來吃同一頓樸實飯菜的痕跡。 Elaboration 闡述 What matters is not decoration, but continuity. 真正重要的並非裝潢，重點在於延續。 如果這些攤檔消失，損失將不止於食物。 我們也會失去小販的語言、廣東話落單的節奏，以及一項證據：香港的建立，靠的不僅有銀行家和發展商，也有那些深夜在灼熱爐火旁工作的人。 因此，保存大牌檔是一種對文化的尊重。"},{"label":"Paragraph 4","english":"Equally important, dai pai dongs preserve a rare form of public intimacy in an increasingly private city. Modern Hong Kong is efficient, but efficiency often comes at the cost of warmth. We order through screens, eat in silence and leave as soon as the bill is paid. By contrast, a dai pai dong encourages people to share tables, exchange glances, complain about the weather and laugh at the cook’s affectionate remarks. You do not just go there to fill your stomach; you go there to feel that the city still has a human pulse. Imagine a student eating noodles beside a minibus driver, while an elderly regular recommends the best dish to a tourist. Such encounters may seem small, but many small encounters make a neighbourhood feel less lonely. These informal meeting places are no less important than libraries or community centres. They remind us that culture is not always performed on a stage; more often than not, it is created when strangers become temporary neighbours.","chinese":"同樣重要的是，在一個愈來愈私密化的城市中，大牌檔保存了一種罕有的公共親切感。 現代香港講求效率，但效率往往以溫度作為代價。 我們透過螢幕點餐，沉默用餐，帳單一付清便離開。 相比之下，大牌檔鼓勵人們共享桌子、交換眼神、抱怨天氣，並因廚師親切的幾句話會心一笑。 你去那裡，並不只是為了填飽肚子；你去那裡，是為了感受這座城市仍然有人的脈搏。 試想像，一名學生在小巴司機旁邊吃麵，同時一位年長熟客向遊客推薦最佳菜式。 這些相遇看似微小，但許多微小相遇累積起來，便會令一個社區少一點孤單 這些非正式的相聚場所，重要性絕不低於圖書館或社區中心。 它們提醒我們，文化並不總是在舞台上演出；很多時候，文化是在陌生人成為短暫鄰居的一刻形成的。"},{"label":"Paragraph 5","english":"Granted, some people argue that dai pai dongs are noisy, smoky and difficult to regulate. That concern is reasonable; preservation should never become an excuse for poor hygiene or blocked pavements. However, to acknowledge the problem is not to concede that disappearance is the only solution. The better answer is careful adaptation. The government could designate suitable cooked-food zones, offer renewable licences to responsible operators and require modern safety equipment without destroying the stalls’ character. Schools, meanwhile, could organise local culture projects in which students interview hawkers, record menus and learn how a bowl of noodles can reflect migration, labour and family sacrifice. Preservation would not freeze dai pai dongs in the past. Rather, it would make room for them in the future. A cleaner stall can still be lively; a safer kitchen can still produce food with soul.","chinese":"誠然，有些人認為大牌檔嘈雜、油煙大，而且難以規管。 這種憂慮合情合理；保存文化絕不應成為衛生欠佳或阻塞行人路的藉口。 然而，承認問題存在，並不等於承認消失是唯一的出路。 更理想的答案，是審慎調整。 政府可以劃定合適的熟食區，向負責任的經營者提供可續期牌照，並要求使用現代安全設備，同時不破壞攤檔特色。 與此同時，學校可以舉辦本地文化專題研習，讓學生訪問小販、記錄餐牌，並學會一碗麵如何反映遷徙、勞動與家庭犧牲。 保存大牌檔並不會把它們冰封在過去。 相反，它會為它們在未來騰出位置。 更乾淨的攤檔依然可以熱鬧；更安全的廚房依然可以煮出有靈魂的食物。"},{"label":"Paragraph 6","english":"All things considered, Hong Kong should preserve dai pai dongs because they are more than eating places; they are classrooms of memory, theatres of community and symbols of local resilience. The time has come for the government to protect them sensibly, for schools to teach their value, and for young people to support them willingly. One day, if the last wok falls silent, we may realise that what disappeared was not just a meal, but a piece of ourselves.","chinese":"綜合而言，香港應該保存大牌檔，因為它們遠遠超越普通食肆；它們是記憶的課室、社群的劇場，也是本地韌性的象徵。 現在是時候讓政府理性地保護它們，讓學校教導它們的價值，也讓年輕人心甘情願地支持它們。 有一天，如果最後一口鑊沉默下來，我們或許才會明白，消失的並不只是一頓飯，更是我們自身的一部分。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"still hot, still human","chinese":"仍然熱騰騰，仍然有人情味"},{"english":"deserve a future","chinese":"值得擁有未來"},{"english":"street life","chinese":"街頭生活"},{"english":"used to","chinese":"過去常常"},{"english":"announce itself","chinese":"展現自身存在"},{"english":"before we even saw it","chinese":"甚至在我們看見之前"},{"english":"clatter of woks","chinese":"鑊鏟聲"},{"english":"hiss of blue flames","chinese":"藍色火焰的嘶嘶聲"},{"english":"fried noodles","chinese":"炒麵"},{"english":"drift through","chinese":"飄過"},{"english":"crowded pavement","chinese":"擠迫的行人路"},{"english":"open-air dai pai dong","chinese":"露天大牌檔"},{"english":"once part of","chinese":"曾經是……的一部分"},{"english":"urban music","chinese":"城市樂章"},{"english":"be pushed aside by","chinese":"被……擠走"},{"english":"redevelopment","chinese":"重建"},{"english":"rising rents","chinese":"租金上升"},{"english":"licensing restrictions","chinese":"牌照限制"},{"english":"chain restaurants","chinese":"連鎖餐廳"},{"english":"this has made citizens consider whether","chinese":"這令市民思考是否"},{"english":"officials","chinese":"官員"},{"english":"be left to disappear","chinese":"被任由消失"},{"english":"be preserved","chinese":"被保育；被保存"},{"english":"remain alive","chinese":"保持活力"},{"english":"as far as I am concerned","chinese":"就我而言"},{"english":"worth preserving","chinese":"值得保育"},{"english":"not merely because…, but because…","chinese":"不只是因為……而是因為……"},{"english":"shared memory","chinese":"共同記憶"},{"english":"sustain human connection","chinese":"維繫人與人之間的聯繫"},{"english":"future generations","chinese":"未來世代"},{"english":"a taste of","chinese":"……的體驗；……的味道"},{"english":"authentic Hong Kong","chinese":"真實的香港"},{"english":"to begin with","chinese":"首先"},{"english":"living archives","chinese":"活生生的歷史檔案"},{"english":"museum display","chinese":"博物館展品"},{"english":"behind glass","chinese":"玻璃後面"},{"english":"street stall","chinese":"街頭小食檔"},{"english":"allow history to be tasted","chinese":"讓人品嚐歷史"},{"english":"wok-fried beef noodles","chinese":"鑊炒牛肉麵"},{"english":"earlier generations","chinese":"上一代人"},{"english":"cheap ingredients","chinese":"廉價食材"},{"english":"turn… into comfort","chinese":"將……變成安慰"},{"english":"battered folding table","chinese":"殘舊摺枱"},{"english":"folding table","chinese":"摺枱"},{"english":"build livelihoods","chinese":"維持生計"},{"english":"limited space","chinese":"有限空間"},{"english":"few, if any","chinese":"即使有，也少之又少"},{"english":"carry this density of memory","chinese":"承載如此濃厚的記憶"},{"english":"density of memory","chinese":"濃厚的記憶"},{"english":"take… for example","chinese":"以……為例"},{"english":"old stall","chinese":"老檔口"},{"english":"Sham Shui Po","chinese":"深水埗"},{"english":"plastic stools","chinese":"膠凳"},{"english":"look elegant","chinese":"看起來優雅"},{"english":"every scratch on them","chinese":"上面的每一道刮痕"},{"english":"suggest years of","chinese":"顯示多年……"},{"english":"office workers","chinese":"上班族"},{"english":"taxi drivers","chinese":"的士司機"},{"english":"elderly neighbours","chinese":"年長街坊"},{"english":"sit down for","chinese":"坐下來吃"},{"english":"honest meal","chinese":"實在的一餐"},{"english":"what matters is not…, but…","chinese":"重要的不是……而是……"},{"english":"decoration","chinese":"裝飾"},{"english":"continuity","chinese":"延續性"},{"english":"if these stalls vanish","chinese":"如果這些檔口消失"},{"english":"the loss will not be limited to","chinese":"損失不會限於"},{"english":"lose the language of hawkers","chinese":"失去小販的語言"},{"english":"hawkers","chinese":"小販"},{"english":"rhythm of Cantonese orders","chinese":"廣東話落單的節奏"},{"english":"evidence that","chinese":"……的證據"},{"english":"not only by…, but also by…","chinese":"不只是由……也是由……"},{"english":"bankers and developers","chinese":"銀行家和發展商"},{"english":"people who worked beside hot stoves","chinese":"在熱爐旁工作的人"},{"english":"late into the night","chinese":"直到深夜"},{"english":"act of cultural respect","chinese":"文化尊重的行動"},{"english":"equally important","chinese":"同樣重要的是"},{"english":"rare form of","chinese":"罕有形式的"},{"english":"public intimacy","chinese":"公共親密感"},{"english":"increasingly private city","chinese":"越來越私人化的城市"},{"english":"efficient","chinese":"高效率的"},{"english":"come at the cost of","chinese":"以犧牲……為代價"},{"english":"warmth","chinese":"人情味；溫暖"},{"english":"order through screens","chinese":"透過螢幕落單"},{"english":"eat in silence","chinese":"默默進食"},{"english":"as soon as","chinese":"一……就……"},{"english":"bill is paid","chinese":"付完帳"},{"english":"by contrast","chinese":"相比之下"},{"english":"encourage people to","chinese":"鼓勵人們去"},{"english":"share tables","chinese":"搭枱"},{"english":"exchange glances","chinese":"交換眼神"},{"english":"complain about the weather","chinese":"抱怨天氣"},{"english":"affectionate remarks","chinese":"親切的說話"},{"english":"fill your stomach","chinese":"填飽肚子"},{"english":"human pulse","chinese":"人情脈搏"},{"english":"imagine","chinese":"試想像"},{"english":"minibus driver","chinese":"小巴司機"},{"english":"elderly regular","chinese":"年長熟客"},{"english":"recommend the best dish","chinese":"推薦最佳菜式"},{"english":"tourist","chinese":"遊客"},{"english":"such encounters","chinese":"這些相遇"},{"english":"seem small","chinese":"看似微小"},{"english":"make a neighbourhood feel less lonely","chinese":"令社區感覺不那麼孤單"},{"english":"informal meeting places","chinese":"非正式聚腳點"},{"english":"no less important than","chinese":"不亞於……重要"},{"english":"community centres","chinese":"社區中心"},{"english":"remind us that","chinese":"提醒我們"},{"english":"performed on a stage","chinese":"在舞台上表演"},{"english":"more often than not","chinese":"往往；多數情況下"},{"english":"strangers become temporary neighbours","chinese":"陌生人成為短暫鄰居"},{"english":"temporary neighbours","chinese":"短暫鄰居"},{"english":"granted","chinese":"誠然"},{"english":"argue that","chinese":"認為；主張"},{"english":"noisy, smoky and difficult to regulate","chinese":"嘈雜、多煙、難以規管"},{"english":"difficult to regulate","chinese":"難以規管"},{"english":"that concern is reasonable","chinese":"這個憂慮是合理的"},{"english":"preservation","chinese":"保育"},{"english":"become an excuse for","chinese":"成為……的藉口"},{"english":"poor hygiene","chinese":"衞生欠佳"},{"english":"blocked pavements","chinese":"被阻塞的行人路"},{"english":"acknowledge the problem","chinese":"承認問題"},{"english":"concede that","chinese":"承認"},{"english":"disappearance","chinese":"消失"},{"english":"the only solution","chinese":"唯一解決方法"},{"english":"careful adaptation","chinese":"審慎調適"},{"english":"designate suitable cooked-food zones","chinese":"指定合適熟食區"},{"english":"cooked-food zones","chinese":"熟食區"},{"english":"renewable licences","chinese":"可續期牌照"},{"english":"responsible operators","chinese":"負責任的經營者"},{"english":"modern safety equipment","chinese":"現代安全設備"},{"english":"without destroying","chinese":"在不破壞……的情況下"},{"english":"stalls' character","chinese":"檔口特色"},{"english":"meanwhile","chinese":"與此同時"},{"english":"organise local culture projects","chinese":"舉辦本地文化專題研習"},{"english":"local culture projects","chinese":"本地文化專題研習"},{"english":"interview hawkers","chinese":"訪問小販"},{"english":"record menus","chinese":"記錄餐牌"},{"english":"reflect migration","chinese":"反映移民"},{"english":"labour","chinese":"勞動"},{"english":"family sacrifice","chinese":"家庭犧牲"},{"english":"freeze… in the past","chinese":"將……凍結在過去"},{"english":"make room for","chinese":"為……留出空間"},{"english":"in the future","chinese":"在未來"},{"english":"cleaner stall","chinese":"更潔淨的檔口"},{"english":"lively","chinese":"熱鬧的；有活力的"},{"english":"safer kitchen","chinese":"更安全的廚房"},{"english":"food with soul","chinese":"有靈魂的食物"},{"english":"all things considered","chinese":"綜合而言"},{"english":"more than eating places","chinese":"不只是用餐地方"},{"english":"classrooms of memory","chinese":"記憶的課室"},{"english":"theatres of community","chinese":"社區的劇場"},{"english":"symbols of local resilience","chinese":"本地韌性的象徵"},{"english":"local resilience","chinese":"本地韌性"},{"english":"the time has come for","chinese":"是時候……"},{"english":"protect them sensibly","chinese":"明智地保護它們"},{"english":"teach their value","chinese":"教導其價值"},{"english":"support them willingly","chinese":"自願支持它們"},{"english":"if the last wok falls silent","chinese":"如果最後一口鑊沉默下來"},{"english":"fall silent","chinese":"沉寂下來"},{"english":"what disappeared was not just…, but…","chinese":"消失的不只是……而是……"},{"english":"a piece of ourselves","chinese":"我們自身的一部分"}]},"dse-writing-2016-part-b-q6":{"exerciseId":"dse-writing-2016-part-b-q6","essayKey":"","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=dse-writing-2016-part-b-q6","flashDeckId":"dse/writing/part-b/2016/Q6","paragraphs":[{"label":"Paragraph 1","english":"The Taste of Honey","chinese":"蜜糖的味道"},{"label":"Paragraph 2","english":"By the time the posters for Creative Writing Week appeared along the corridor, I had learned that silence could be worn like a school cardigan - ordinary, neat, and useful for hiding stains.","chinese":"當創意寫作週的海報出現在走廊上的時候，我已經學會了，沉默也可以像校服外套一樣穿在身上——普通、整齊，而且很適合遮掩污漬。"},{"label":"Paragraph 3","english":"Last year, Chris Wong had stolen my short story.","chinese":"去年，Chris Wong 偷走了我的短篇故事。"},{"label":"Paragraph 4","english":"Stolen was a word I used only inside my head. In public, people said “similarity” and “coincidence”. Chris had submitted my story about an old woman selling paper lanterns. He changed the names, polished two metaphors, and won first prize. I complained. However, without proof, my anger sounded childish. The panel smiled, leaving me with more questions than answers.","chinese":"「偷」這個字，我只敢在心裡使用。 在公開場合，人們只會說那是「相似」和「巧合」。 Chris 遞交了我那篇關於一位賣紙燈籠老婦人的故事。 他改了名字，修飾了兩個比喻，然後拿了第一名。 我投訴了。 然而，沒有證據，我的憤怒聽起來就像小孩子鬧脾氣。 評審團只是微笑，留給我的疑問比答案更多。"},{"label":"Paragraph 5","english":"After that, I stopped writing in the library. I stopped raising my hand in English lessons. I even stopped using blue ink, because Chris had once borrowed my fountain pen and returned it empty.","chinese":"那之後，我不再在圖書館寫作。 我不再在英文課上舉手。 我甚至不再使用藍墨水，因為 Chris 曾經借走我的鋼筆，歸還時已經把墨水用盡。"},{"label":"Paragraph 6","english":"Then this year’s theme was announced: Revenge is Sweet.","chinese":"然後，今年的主題公布了：復仇是甜的。"},{"label":"Paragraph 7","english":"No one saw me coming.","chinese":"沒有人預料到我會出手。"},{"label":"Paragraph 8","english":"For three nights, I wrote a story called “The Honey Jar”. It was about a boy who stole recipes from his grandmother and became famous for cakes he could not bake. Each paragraph began innocently enough, but the first letters formed a sentence: Chris STOLE MY STORY. Better still, I planted details only I could explain: a blue fountain pen, a lantern woman, and one sentence from my original draft.","chinese":"連續三個晚上，我寫了一篇名為《蜜糖罐》的故事。 故事寫一個男孩偷走祖母的食譜，並因自己根本不會烘焙的蛋糕而成名。 每一段的開頭看起來都相當無害，然而每段第一個字母卻連成一句話：Chris STOLE MY STORY。 更妙的是，我埋下了只有我才能解釋的細節：一支藍色鋼筆、一位燈籠婦人，以及我原稿中的一句話。"},{"label":"Paragraph 9","english":"On Friday afternoon, I printed two copies. One went into my bag. The other I left beneath a dictionary in the library, its title page facing up, as though I had forgotten it. Earlier, I had emailed the same file to Mrs Chan: Evidence, if necessary. Then I sat three tables away.","chinese":"星期五下午，我列印了兩份。 一份放進了我的書包。 另一份，我留在圖書館一本字典下面，標題頁朝上，彷彿我不小心忘了帶走 更早之前，我已經把同一份檔案電郵給陳老師：必要時，這就是證據。 然後，我坐在三張桌子之外。"},{"label":"Paragraph 10","english":"Chris arrived at four. He glanced around, lifted the dictionary, and smiled.","chinese":"Chris 四點到了。 他環顧四周，掀起那本字典，笑了。"},{"label":"Paragraph 11","english":"It was not a guilty smile. That would have been too simple. It was a hungry one.","chinese":"那個笑容沒有半點愧疚。 事情若只到愧疚，就太簡單了。 那是一個飢餓的笑容。"},{"label":"Paragraph 12","english":"All the while, I kept my eyes on my notes. Subject, verb, object. Thief, steals, story.","chinese":"整段時間裡，我的眼睛一直停在筆記上。 主詞、動詞、受詞。 賊，偷，故事。"},{"label":"Paragraph 13","english":"The following Wednesday, the hall was packed for the finalists’ readings. Chris had been chosen again. He walked onstage in a white shirt so crisp it seemed ironed by angels.","chinese":"接下來的星期三，禮堂擠滿了來聽決賽作品朗讀的人。 Chris 又再入選了。 他穿著一件筆挺得彷彿由天使熨過的白恤衫走上台。"},{"label":"Paragraph 14","english":"“My story is called ‘The Honey Jar’,” he announced.","chinese":"「我的故事叫做《蜜糖罐》，」他宣布。"},{"label":"Paragraph 15","english":"Behind me, someone whispered, “Isn’t he brilliant?”","chinese":"我身後有人低聲說：「他是不是很出色？」"},{"label":"Paragraph 16","english":"“Brilliant,” I said. “Absolutely.”","chinese":"「出色，」我說。 「當然。」"},{"label":"Paragraph 17","english":"He read beautifully. His pauses were perfect; his voice warmed the hall like afternoon sunlight. Yet the more confidently he performed, the more completely he wrapped the string around himself. When he reached the last paragraph, I saw Mrs Chan, our English teacher, straighten in her seat. Mr Lau, the head of the panel, looked down at the printed copy in his hands. Letter by letter, the trap opened.","chinese":"他朗讀得漂亮極了。 他的停頓完美無瑕；他的聲音像午後陽光一樣溫暖了整個禮堂。 然而，他表演得越自信，就越徹底地把繩索繞到自己身上。 當他讀到最後一段時，我看見我們的英文老師陳老師在座位上挺直了身子。 評審團主席劉先生低頭看著手中的列印稿。 一個字母接一個字母，陷阱打開了。"},{"label":"Paragraph 18","english":"When Chris finished, applause broke out. He bowed before anyone had decided whether he deserved it.","chinese":"Chris 讀完時，掌聲響起。 在人們還未決定他是否配得上掌聲之前，他已經鞠躬了。"},{"label":"Paragraph 19","english":"Then Mrs Chan stood up.","chinese":"然後，陳老師站了起來。"},{"label":"Paragraph 20","english":"“Chris,” she said, “could you explain why the first letters of your paragraphs spell an unusual message?”","chinese":"「Chris，」她說，「你能不能解釋一下，為甚麼你每段開首的字母會拼出一個不尋常的訊息？」"},{"label":"Paragraph 21","english":"The hall went still.","chinese":"整個禮堂瞬間靜了下來。"},{"label":"Paragraph 22","english":"“What message?” he asked.","chinese":"「甚麼訊息？」他問。"},{"label":"Paragraph 23","english":"She handed him the paper. For once, his face was worth writing about. The confidence drained first from his eyes, then from his mouth, leaving behind a frightened boy in an expensive shirt.","chinese":"她把那張紙遞給他。 這一次，他的臉終於值得被寫進故事裡。 自信先從他的眼睛流走，再從他的嘴角消失，留下的只是一個穿著昂貴恤衫、滿臉驚恐的男孩。"},{"label":"Paragraph 24","english":"“I—I didn’t notice.”","chinese":"「我——我沒有留意到。」"},{"label":"Paragraph 25","english":"“That,” Mrs Chan said, “is precisely the problem.”","chinese":"「這一點，」陳老師說，「正正就是問題所在。」"},{"label":"Paragraph 26","english":"No sooner had the words left her mouth than murmurs swept across the hall. Chris looked at me then, not angrily, but as if he had finally realised that a quiet person was not necessarily an empty one.","chinese":"她話音剛落，低語聲便席捲整個禮堂。 那時 Chris 看向我，目光裡沒有怒氣；他的神情彷彿終於明白，一個安靜的人，心裡未必空無一物。"},{"label":"Paragraph 27","english":"My own story was read last. It was not “The Honey Jar”. It was called “The Girl Who Waited”, and it told the truth without naming him. I wrote about a girl who had mistaken silence for weakness, patience for surrender, and kindness for permission. I wrote about how revenge, if it is merely cruel, leaves a bitter taste. But justice—patient, precise, and earned—can taste unexpectedly sweet.","chinese":"我的故事最後才被朗讀。 那篇作品並非《蜜糖罐》。 它叫做《等待的女孩》，並在沒有點名他的情況下說出了真相。 我寫一個女孩，她曾把沉默誤認為軟弱，把耐心誤認為投降，把善良誤認為許可。 我寫到復仇若只有殘忍，留下的味道會是苦的。 可是，耐心、精準而靠自己爭回來的公義，竟可以有出人意料的甜味。"},{"label":"Paragraph 28","english":"I won.","chinese":"我贏了。"},{"label":"Paragraph 29","english":"After the ceremony, Chris tried to speak to me near the noticeboard.","chinese":"典禮之後，Chris 在壁報板附近試圖跟我說話。"},{"label":"Paragraph 30","english":"“Mary, I—”","chinese":"「Mary，我——」"},{"label":"Paragraph 31","english":"“Keep it,” I said, handing him the blue fountain pen he had emptied months before. “It has run out.”","chinese":"「留著吧，」我說，把那支他幾個月前用光墨水的藍色鋼筆遞給他。 「它已經沒墨水了。」"},{"label":"Paragraph 32","english":"Outside, the tuck shop was selling honey cakes. I bought one and ate slowly.","chinese":"外面，小食部正在賣蜜糖蛋糕。 我買了一個，慢慢地吃。"},{"label":"Paragraph 33","english":"Revenge was sweet.","chinese":"復仇是甜的。"},{"label":"Paragraph 34","english":"Not because Chris had fallen.","chinese":"並非因為 Chris 倒下了。"},{"label":"Paragraph 35","english":"Because, at last, my voice had risen.","chinese":"因為，我的聲音終於站了起來。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"the taste of honey","chinese":"蜂蜜的滋味"},{"english":"by the time","chinese":"到……的時候"},{"english":"Creative Writing Week","chinese":"創意寫作週"},{"english":"appear along the corridor","chinese":"出現在走廊沿途"},{"english":"silence could be worn like","chinese":"沉默可以像……一樣穿在身上"},{"english":"school cardigan","chinese":"校服冷衫"},{"english":"useful for hiding stains","chinese":"可用來遮掩污漬"},{"english":"steal my short story","chinese":"偷走我的短篇故事"},{"english":"inside my head","chinese":"在我腦海裏"},{"english":"in public","chinese":"在公開場合"},{"english":"similarity and coincidence","chinese":"相似和巧合"},{"english":"submit my story","chinese":"提交我的故事"},{"english":"paper lanterns","chinese":"紙燈籠"},{"english":"change the names","chinese":"改掉名字"},{"english":"polish two metaphors","chinese":"修飾兩個比喻"},{"english":"win first prize","chinese":"贏得一等獎"},{"english":"without proof","chinese":"沒有證據"},{"english":"sound childish","chinese":"聽起來幼稚"},{"english":"the panel","chinese":"評審團"},{"english":"leave someone with more questions than answers","chinese":"令某人留下更多疑問而非答案"},{"english":"stop raising my hand","chinese":"不再舉手"},{"english":"borrow my fountain pen","chinese":"借我的鋼筆"},{"english":"return it empty","chinese":"把它用光後歸還"},{"english":"this year's theme was announced","chinese":"今年的主題被公布"},{"english":"Revenge is Sweet","chinese":"復仇是甜蜜的"},{"english":"no one saw me coming","chinese":"沒有人預料到我會出手"},{"english":"for three nights","chinese":"連續三晚"},{"english":"a story called","chinese":"一個名為……的故事"},{"english":"steal recipes from","chinese":"從……偷食譜"},{"english":"become famous for","chinese":"因……而成名"},{"english":"could not bake","chinese":"不會焗製"},{"english":"each paragraph began","chinese":"每一段開始時"},{"english":"innocently enough","chinese":"看似無辜地；看似平常地"},{"english":"the first letters formed a sentence","chinese":"首字母拼成一句句子"},{"english":"better still","chinese":"更妙的是"},{"english":"plant details","chinese":"埋下細節"},{"english":"only I could explain","chinese":"只有我能解釋"},{"english":"original draft","chinese":"原稿"},{"english":"print two copies","chinese":"列印兩份"},{"english":"go into my bag","chinese":"放進我的袋裏"},{"english":"leave beneath a dictionary","chinese":"留在字典下面"},{"english":"title page facing up","chinese":"封面朝上"},{"english":"as though","chinese":"好像；彷彿"},{"english":"email the same file to","chinese":"把同一個檔案電郵給……"},{"english":"evidence, if necessary","chinese":"如有需要，可作證據"},{"english":"sit three tables away","chinese":"坐在三張桌子之外"},{"english":"glance around","chinese":"環顧四周"},{"english":"lift the dictionary","chinese":"拿起字典"},{"english":"a guilty smile","chinese":"心虛的笑容"},{"english":"too simple","chinese":"太簡單"},{"english":"a hungry smile","chinese":"貪婪的笑容"},{"english":"all the while","chinese":"一直；期間始終"},{"english":"keep my eyes on","chinese":"把目光放在……上"},{"english":"subject, verb, object","chinese":"主語、動詞、賓語"},{"english":"the following Wednesday","chinese":"接下來的星期三"},{"english":"the hall was packed","chinese":"禮堂擠滿了人"},{"english":"finalists' readings","chinese":"入圍者朗讀"},{"english":"be chosen again","chinese":"再次被選中"},{"english":"walk onstage","chinese":"走上台"},{"english":"so crisp it seemed","chinese":"筆挺得像……"},{"english":"ironed by angels","chinese":"像由天使燙過"},{"english":"announce","chinese":"宣布"},{"english":"behind me","chinese":"在我身後"},{"english":"whisper","chinese":"低聲說；耳語"},{"english":"read beautifully","chinese":"朗讀得很動聽"},{"english":"pauses were perfect","chinese":"停頓恰到好處"},{"english":"voice warmed the hall","chinese":"聲音令禮堂變得溫暖"},{"english":"like afternoon sunlight","chinese":"像午後陽光一樣"},{"english":"the more..., the more...","chinese":"越……就越……"},{"english":"perform confidently","chinese":"自信地表演"},{"english":"wrap the string around himself","chinese":"把繩索繞到自己身上"},{"english":"reach the last paragraph","chinese":"讀到最後一段"},{"english":"straighten in her seat","chinese":"在座位上坐直"},{"english":"head of the panel","chinese":"評審團主席"},{"english":"look down at","chinese":"低頭看着"},{"english":"printed copy","chinese":"列印本"},{"english":"letter by letter","chinese":"一個字母一個字母地"},{"english":"the trap opened","chinese":"陷阱打開"},{"english":"applause broke out","chinese":"掌聲響起"},{"english":"bow before","chinese":"在……之前鞠躬"},{"english":"deserve it","chinese":"值得得到它"},{"english":"stand up","chinese":"站起來"},{"english":"explain why","chinese":"解釋為何"},{"english":"spell an unusual message","chinese":"拼出一段不尋常的信息"},{"english":"go still","chinese":"變得一片寂靜"},{"english":"hand someone the paper","chinese":"把紙遞給某人"},{"english":"for once","chinese":"這一次；難得地"},{"english":"worth writing about","chinese":"值得寫下來"},{"english":"confidence drained from","chinese":"自信從……流失"},{"english":"leave behind","chinese":"留下"},{"english":"a frightened boy","chinese":"驚慌的男孩"},{"english":"expensive shirt","chinese":"昂貴的恤衫"},{"english":"precisely the problem","chinese":"正正是問題所在"},{"english":"no sooner had...than...","chinese":"一……就……"},{"english":"murmurs swept across the hall","chinese":"竊竊私語傳遍禮堂"},{"english":"look at me then","chinese":"那時看着我"},{"english":"not angrily, but as if","chinese":"不是憤怒地，而是好像"},{"english":"finally realise","chinese":"終於明白"},{"english":"a quiet person","chinese":"安靜的人"},{"english":"not necessarily","chinese":"不一定"},{"english":"an empty one","chinese":"內心空白的人"},{"english":"be read last","chinese":"最後被朗讀"},{"english":"tell the truth without naming him","chinese":"不點名地說出真相"},{"english":"mistake silence for weakness","chinese":"錯把沉默當成軟弱"},{"english":"patience for surrender","chinese":"錯把耐性當成投降"},{"english":"kindness for permission","chinese":"錯把善意當成許可"},{"english":"merely cruel","chinese":"只是殘忍的"},{"english":"leave a bitter taste","chinese":"留下苦澀滋味"},{"english":"patient, precise and earned","chinese":"有耐性、精準而應得的"},{"english":"taste unexpectedly sweet","chinese":"嚐起來意想不到地甜"},{"english":"after the ceremony","chinese":"典禮之後"},{"english":"near the noticeboard","chinese":"在告示板附近"},{"english":"try to speak to","chinese":"嘗試跟……說話"},{"english":"hand someone something","chinese":"把某物遞給某人"},{"english":"months before","chinese":"幾個月前"},{"english":"run out","chinese":"用完；耗盡"},{"english":"tuck shop","chinese":"小食部"},{"english":"honey cakes","chinese":"蜂蜜蛋糕"},{"english":"eat slowly","chinese":"慢慢吃"},{"english":"not because...because...","chinese":"不是因為……而是因為……"},{"english":"fall","chinese":"倒下；失勢"},{"english":"at last","chinese":"終於"},{"english":"my voice had risen","chinese":"我的聲音終於響起"}]},"dse-writing-2016-part-b-q7":{"exerciseId":"dse-writing-2016-part-b-q7","essayKey":"","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=dse-writing-2016-part-b-q7","flashDeckId":"dse/writing/part-b/2016/Q7","paragraphs":[{"label":"Paragraph 1","english":"Proposal for the Hong Kong Youth Festival: “From Screen to Street”","chinese":"香港青年節建議書：「從螢幕到街頭」"},{"label":"Paragraph 2","english":"To: The Organising Committee, Hong Kong Youth Association","chinese":"致：香港青年協會籌委會"},{"label":"Paragraph 3","english":"From: Chris Wong","chinese":"發件人：Chris Wong"},{"label":"Paragraph 4","english":"Introduction","chinese":"引言"},{"label":"Paragraph 5","english":"Hong Kong’s young people are no longer passive followers of fashion, entertainment or technology. With smartphones in their hands and social awareness in their minds, many of them are turning everyday life into a form of creativity. In order to make the Youth Festival both lively and meaningful, I propose that the Festival showcase two major youth trends: short-form digital content creation and sustainable streetwear culture. These trends should be presented not merely as displays, but as interactive experiences through which visitors can create, perform, exchange ideas and reflect on what youth culture means in Hong Kong today.","chinese":"香港年輕人已不再是時尚、娛樂或科技的被動追隨者。 他們手握智能電話，心中也有社會意識，當中許多人正把日常生活轉化成一種創意形式。 為了讓青年節既充滿活力又富有意義，我建議青年節展示兩大青年潮流：短片形式的數碼內容創作，以及可持續街頭服飾文化。 這些潮流不應只作為展示來呈現，還應以互動體驗的形式呈現，讓參觀者能夠創作、表演、交流想法，並反思今日香港青年文化的意義。"},{"label":"Paragraph 6","english":"Trend One: Short-form Digital Content Creation","chinese":"潮流一：短片形式的數碼內容創作"},{"label":"Paragraph 7","english":"The first trend worth presenting is short-form digital content creation, especially videos filmed for platforms such as Instagram, YouTube Shorts and TikTok-style channels. Many young people now use short videos to record food reviews, school life, dance routines, social commentary and local neighbourhood stories. This trend is popular because it gives teenagers a low-cost way to express themselves. A student who may be too shy to speak on a stage can still edit a thirty-second video about Sham Shui Po snacks, hidden basketball courts or examination stress. In other words, digital content is not just about entertainment; it is about identity, confidence and voice.","chinese":"第一個值得呈現的潮流，是短片形式的數碼內容創作，尤其是為 Instagram、 YouTube Shorts 和 TikTok 類型頻道等平台拍攝的影片。 現時許多年輕人會使用短片記錄食評、校園生活、舞蹈動作、社會評論和本地社區故事。 這個潮流受歡迎，是因為它給予青少年一種低成本的自我表達方式。 一名可能太害羞而不敢在舞台上發言的學生，仍然可以剪輯一段三十秒的影片，介紹深水埗小食、隱蔽的籃球場，或考試壓力。 換句話說，數碼內容不只是關於娛樂；它關乎身份、信心和發聲的能力。"},{"label":"Paragraph 8","english":"To present this trend effectively, I suggest setting up a “Creator Studio Zone” at the Festival. This zone could include three booths: a filming corner with simple lighting and backdrops, an editing station where volunteers teach basic captioning and transitions, and a “One-Minute Hong Kong Challenge” in which participants create a short video introducing something meaningful about youth life. The best entries could be shown on a central screen every hour. This format would be more engaging than a lecture because visitors would not simply watch creators; they would become creators themselves. It would also encourage responsible online behaviour, as short workshops could remind participants how to respect copyright, protect privacy and avoid cyberbullying.","chinese":"為了有效呈現這個潮流，我建議在青年節設立一個「創作者工作室區」。 這個區域可以包括三個攤位：一個配備簡單燈光和背景板的拍攝角落、一個由義工教授基本字幕和轉場技巧的剪輯站，以及一個「一分鐘香港挑戰」，讓參加者製作短片，介紹一些對青年生活有意義的事物。 最佳作品可以每小時在中央屏幕上播放。 這種形式會比講座更具吸引力，因為參觀者不會只是觀看創作者；他們會親自成為創作者。 它也能鼓勵負責任的網上行為，因為短工作坊可以提醒參加者如何尊重版權、保護私隱，以及避免網絡欺凌。"},{"label":"Paragraph 9","english":"Trend Two: Sustainable Streetwear and Thrifting","chinese":"潮流二：可持續街頭服飾與二手購物"},{"label":"Paragraph 10","english":"The second trend I propose is sustainable streetwear, including thrift shopping, upcycling and outfit customisation. Among young people, fashion is no longer limited to buying expensive new items. Many prefer second-hand jackets, redesigned tote bags, handmade accessories and clothes that reflect their personality. While some adults may see youth fashion as superficial, this trend actually reveals young people’s concern for both individuality and the environment. Fast fashion produces waste; by contrast, thrifting and upcycling allow students to look stylish without encouraging unnecessary consumption.","chinese":"我提出的第二個潮流是可持續街頭服飾，包括二手購物、升級再造和服裝個人化改造。 在年輕人之間，時尚已不再局限於購買昂貴的新商品。 許多人更喜歡二手外套、重新設計的帆布袋、手工飾物，以及能反映個性的衣服。 雖然有些成年人可能會把青年時尚視為膚淺，這個潮流其實反映出年輕人同時重視個人特色和環境。 快速時尚會製造浪費；相比之下，二手購物和升級再造能讓學生保持時尚，同時不鼓勵不必要的消費。"},{"label":"Paragraph 11","english":"This trend could be presented through a “Streetwear Swap and Upcycling Market”. Visitors would be invited to bring clean clothes, bags or accessories they no longer use and exchange them for tokens. These tokens could then be used to “buy” other second-hand items at the market. Beside the swap area, local young designers and art students could run mini-workshops on embroidery, fabric painting and patch-making. A short “Re-made Runway” could also be held twice a day, allowing participants to model outfits they have redesigned. This would create a festival atmosphere while showing that sustainability can be practical, creative and enjoyable. The more visitors participate, the more clearly they will understand that protecting the environment does not have to be dull or expensive.","chinese":"這個潮流可以透過「街頭服飾交換與升級再造市集」來呈現。 參觀者可受邀帶來自己不再使用的乾淨衣服、袋或飾物，並把它們換成代幣 這些代幣之後可以在市集中用來「購買」其他二手物品。 在交換區旁邊，本地年輕設計師和藝術學生可以舉辦關於刺繡、布料繪畫和布章製作的小型工作坊。 每天也可以舉行兩次簡短的「再造時裝天橋」，讓參加者展示他們重新設計的服裝。 這樣做能營造節日氣氛，同時展示可持續生活可以是實用、有創意並令人享受的。 參觀者參與得越多，他們就會越清楚明白，保護環境不一定要沉悶或昂貴。"},{"label":"Paragraph 12","english":"Justification and Expected Benefits","chinese":"理據與預期效益"},{"label":"Paragraph 13","english":"The proposed presentation method is suitable for three reasons. First, it is interactive. A successful youth festival should not make young people feel as if adults are simply explaining youth culture back to them. Instead, it should give them room to take ownership of the event. Secondly, the two trends balance technology and real-life community. Digital creation appeals to students who enjoy online expression, whereas sustainable fashion attracts those interested in design, lifestyle and environmental responsibility. Together, they show that Hong Kong youth culture exists both on screens and on the streets.","chinese":"上述呈現方法適合採用，原因有三個。 第一，它具有互動性。 一個成功的青年節，不應令年輕人覺得成年人只是把青年文化重新解釋給他們聽。 相反，它應該給予年輕人空間，讓他們對活動產生主導感和歸屬感。 第二，這兩個潮流能在科技與現實社群之間取得平衡。 數碼創作能吸引喜歡網上表達的學生，而可持續時尚則能吸引對設計、生活風格和環境責任感興趣的人。 兩者結合起來，能顯示香港青年文化同時存在於螢幕上和街道之中。"},{"label":"Paragraph 14","english":"More importantly, the plan is realistic. The Creator Studio requires only basic lighting, phones, microphones and volunteer guidance. The upcycling market can be supported by schools, youth centres and local design groups. To minimise the risk of disorder, the Association could require advance registration for workshops and set clear rules for clothing donations. In this way, the Festival would remain well-organised while still feeling energetic and youth-led.","chinese":"更重要的是，這個計劃是現實可行的。 「創作者工作室」只需要基本燈光、電話、麥克風和義工指導。 升級再造市集可以由學校、青年中心和本地設計團體支持。 為了減低混亂的風險，協會可以要求參加者預先登記工作坊，並為衣物捐贈制定清晰規則。 這樣一來，青年節既能保持妥善，也能保留充滿活力和由青年主導的感覺"},{"label":"Paragraph 15","english":"Conclusion","chinese":"結論"},{"label":"Paragraph 16","english":"All things considered, I strongly recommend that the Hong Kong Youth Association adopt the theme “From Screen to Street” and present short-form digital content creation together with sustainable streetwear culture. These two trends are popular, visually attractive and rich in educational value. If the organising committee can invite youth volunteers, local creators and student designers to help run the booths, the Festival will not only showcase what young people like, but also celebrate what they can create.","chinese":"綜合考慮，我強烈建議香港青年協會採用「從螢幕到街頭」這個主題，並同時呈現短片形式的數碼內容創作和可持續街頭服飾文化。 這兩個潮流受歡迎、視覺上具吸引力，而且富有教育價值。 如果籌委會能邀請青年義工、本地創作者和學生設計師協助營運攤位，青年節不只會展示年輕人喜歡甚麼，還會讚揚他們能創造甚麼。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"proposal for","chinese":"關於……的建議書"},{"english":"organising committee","chinese":"籌備委員會"},{"english":"showcasing youth trends","chinese":"展示青年潮流"},{"english":"youth trends","chinese":"青年潮流"},{"english":"passive followers of","chinese":"……的被動追隨者"},{"english":"fashion, entertainment or technology","chinese":"時尚、娛樂或科技"},{"english":"social awareness","chinese":"社會意識"},{"english":"turn everyday life into","chinese":"把日常生活變成"},{"english":"a form of creativity","chinese":"一種創意形式"},{"english":"in order to","chinese":"為了"},{"english":"lively and meaningful","chinese":"生動而有意義"},{"english":"propose that","chinese":"建議"},{"english":"major youth trends","chinese":"主要青年潮流"},{"english":"short-form digital content creation","chinese":"短影片數碼內容創作"},{"english":"sustainable streetwear culture","chinese":"可持續街頭服飾文化"},{"english":"not merely as displays","chinese":"不只是作為展示"},{"english":"interactive experiences","chinese":"互動體驗"},{"english":"through which","chinese":"透過……"},{"english":"exchange ideas","chinese":"交流想法"},{"english":"reflect on","chinese":"反思"},{"english":"youth culture","chinese":"青年文化"},{"english":"worth presenting","chinese":"值得呈現"},{"english":"filmed for platforms","chinese":"為平台拍攝"},{"english":"platforms such as","chinese":"例如……的平台"},{"english":"YouTube Shorts","chinese":"YouTube 短片"},{"english":"TikTok-style channels","chinese":"TikTok 式頻道"},{"english":"record food reviews","chinese":"記錄食評"},{"english":"school life","chinese":"校園生活"},{"english":"dance routines","chinese":"舞蹈動作；舞蹈編排"},{"english":"social commentary","chinese":"社會評論"},{"english":"local neighbourhood stories","chinese":"本區社區故事"},{"english":"low-cost way to","chinese":"低成本的……方法"},{"english":"express themselves","chinese":"表達自己"},{"english":"too shy to speak","chinese":"太害羞而不敢說話"},{"english":"on a stage","chinese":"在舞台上"},{"english":"edit a thirty-second video","chinese":"剪輯一段三十秒短片"},{"english":"hidden basketball courts","chinese":"隱藏的籃球場"},{"english":"examination stress","chinese":"考試壓力"},{"english":"in other words","chinese":"換句話說"},{"english":"not just about entertainment","chinese":"不只是關於娛樂"},{"english":"identity, confidence and voice","chinese":"身份、信心和聲音"},{"english":"present this trend effectively","chinese":"有效呈現這股潮流"},{"english":"setting up","chinese":"設立"},{"english":"Creator Studio Zone","chinese":"創作者工作室區"},{"english":"filming corner","chinese":"拍攝角"},{"english":"simple lighting and backdrops","chinese":"簡單燈光和背景板"},{"english":"editing station","chinese":"剪片站"},{"english":"basic captioning","chinese":"基本字幕製作"},{"english":"transitions","chinese":"轉場效果"},{"english":"One-Minute Hong Kong Challenge","chinese":"一分鐘香港挑戰"},{"english":"create a short video","chinese":"創作一段短片"},{"english":"introducing something meaningful","chinese":"介紹有意義的事物"},{"english":"youth life","chinese":"青年生活"},{"english":"best entries","chinese":"最佳作品"},{"english":"central screen","chinese":"中央屏幕"},{"english":"every hour","chinese":"每小時"},{"english":"more engaging than","chinese":"比……更吸引"},{"english":"would not simply watch","chinese":"不只是觀看"},{"english":"become creators themselves","chinese":"親自成為創作者"},{"english":"encourage responsible online behaviour","chinese":"鼓勵負責任的網上行為"},{"english":"responsible online behaviour","chinese":"負責任的網上行為"},{"english":"short workshops","chinese":"短工作坊"},{"english":"remind participants how to","chinese":"提醒參加者如何"},{"english":"respect copyright","chinese":"尊重版權"},{"english":"protect privacy","chinese":"保護私隱"},{"english":"avoid cyberbullying","chinese":"避免網絡欺凌"},{"english":"sustainable streetwear","chinese":"可持續街頭服飾"},{"english":"thrift shopping","chinese":"二手購物"},{"english":"upcycling","chinese":"升級再造"},{"english":"outfit customisation","chinese":"服裝個人化改造"},{"english":"among young people","chinese":"在年輕人之中"},{"english":"no longer limited to","chinese":"不再局限於"},{"english":"expensive new items","chinese":"昂貴新貨品"},{"english":"second-hand jackets","chinese":"二手外套"},{"english":"redesigned tote bags","chinese":"改造帆布袋"},{"english":"handmade accessories","chinese":"手工飾物"},{"english":"reflect their personality","chinese":"反映個性"},{"english":"see youth fashion as superficial","chinese":"視青年時裝為膚淺"},{"english":"concern for","chinese":"對……的關注"},{"english":"individuality","chinese":"個人特色"},{"english":"the environment","chinese":"環境"},{"english":"fast fashion","chinese":"快時尚"},{"english":"produces waste","chinese":"製造浪費"},{"english":"by contrast","chinese":"相比之下"},{"english":"look stylish","chinese":"看起來有時尚感"},{"english":"unnecessary consumption","chinese":"不必要消費"},{"english":"be presented through","chinese":"透過……呈現"},{"english":"Streetwear Swap and Upcycling Market","chinese":"街頭服飾交換及升級再造市集"},{"english":"be invited to","chinese":"被邀請去"},{"english":"clean clothes","chinese":"乾淨衣物"},{"english":"accessories they no longer use","chinese":"不再使用的飾物"},{"english":"exchange them for tokens","chinese":"把它們換成代幣"},{"english":"tokens","chinese":"代幣"},{"english":"second-hand items","chinese":"二手物品"},{"english":"swap area","chinese":"交換區"},{"english":"local young designers","chinese":"本地年輕設計師"},{"english":"art students","chinese":"藝術學生"},{"english":"run mini-workshops","chinese":"舉辦小型工作坊"},{"english":"embroidery","chinese":"刺繡"},{"english":"fabric painting","chinese":"布料繪畫"},{"english":"patch-making","chinese":"布章製作"},{"english":"Re-made Runway","chinese":"再造時裝天橋"},{"english":"held twice a day","chinese":"每日舉行兩次"},{"english":"model outfits","chinese":"展示服裝"},{"english":"redesigned","chinese":"重新設計的"},{"english":"create a festival atmosphere","chinese":"營造節日氣氛"},{"english":"sustainability","chinese":"可持續發展"},{"english":"practical, creative and enjoyable","chinese":"實用、有創意而有趣"},{"english":"the more…, the more…","chinese":"越……就越……"},{"english":"participate","chinese":"參與"},{"english":"protecting the environment","chinese":"保護環境"},{"english":"does not have to be","chinese":"不一定要"},{"english":"dull or expensive","chinese":"沉悶或昂貴"},{"english":"justification","chinese":"理據"},{"english":"expected benefits","chinese":"預期效益"},{"english":"presentation method","chinese":"呈現方法"},{"english":"suitable for three reasons","chinese":"基於三個原因而合適"},{"english":"interactive","chinese":"互動的"},{"english":"a successful youth festival","chinese":"成功的青年節"},{"english":"make young people feel as if","chinese":"令年輕人覺得好像"},{"english":"explaining youth culture back to them","chinese":"向年輕人反過來解釋青年文化"},{"english":"instead","chinese":"相反；而是"},{"english":"give them room to","chinese":"給他們空間去"},{"english":"take ownership of","chinese":"主導；有主人翁意識"},{"english":"balance technology and real-life community","chinese":"平衡科技與現實社區"},{"english":"appeals to","chinese":"吸引"},{"english":"online expression","chinese":"網上表達"},{"english":"whereas","chinese":"而"},{"english":"attracts those interested in","chinese":"吸引對……有興趣的人"},{"english":"design, lifestyle and environmental responsibility","chinese":"設計、生活方式和環保責任"},{"english":"together","chinese":"合起來"},{"english":"exists both on screens and on the streets","chinese":"同時存在於屏幕上和街頭"},{"english":"more importantly","chinese":"更重要的是"},{"english":"realistic","chinese":"實際可行的"},{"english":"requires only","chinese":"只需要"},{"english":"basic lighting","chinese":"基本燈光"},{"english":"microphones","chinese":"麥克風"},{"english":"volunteer guidance","chinese":"義工指導"},{"english":"be supported by","chinese":"由……支持"},{"english":"youth centres","chinese":"青年中心"},{"english":"local design groups","chinese":"本地設計團體"},{"english":"minimise the risk of disorder","chinese":"減低混亂風險"},{"english":"advance registration","chinese":"預先登記"},{"english":"set clear rules","chinese":"訂立清晰規則"},{"english":"clothing donations","chinese":"衣物捐贈"},{"english":"in this way","chinese":"以這種方式"},{"english":"remain well-organised","chinese":"保持井然有序"},{"english":"energetic and youth-led","chinese":"充滿活力並由青年主導"},{"english":"all things considered","chinese":"綜合而言"},{"english":"strongly recommend that","chinese":"強烈建議"},{"english":"adopt the theme","chinese":"採用主題"},{"english":"visually attractive","chinese":"視覺上吸引"},{"english":"rich in educational value","chinese":"富有教育價值"},{"english":"organising committee","chinese":"籌備委員會"},{"english":"youth volunteers","chinese":"青年義工"},{"english":"local creators","chinese":"本地創作者"},{"english":"student designers","chinese":"學生設計師"},{"english":"run the booths","chinese":"營運攤位"},{"english":"not only showcase…, but also celebrate…","chinese":"不只展示……而且頌揚……"},{"english":"what young people like","chinese":"年輕人喜歡的事物"},{"english":"what they can create","chinese":"他們能夠創造的東西"}]},"dse-writing-2016-part-b-q8":{"exerciseId":"dse-writing-2016-part-b-q8","essayKey":"","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=dse-writing-2016-part-b-q8","flashDeckId":"dse/writing/part-b/2016/Q8","paragraphs":[{"label":"Paragraph 1","english":"Looking Fear in the Eye","chinese":"直視恐懼"},{"label":"Paragraph 2","english":"A famous songwriter once said, “Expose yourself to your deepest fear; after that, fear has no power.” Although the line sounds dramatic, it speaks directly to ordinary life. From examinations to friendships, challenges do not disappear because we refuse to name them; instead, they grow quietly in the dark. This has made many young people consider whether they should hide their weaknesses or face them openly in order to become calmer and stronger. In my view, acknowledging challenges and finding ways to cope with them is essential, because only by recognising what frightens us can we understand it, manage it and outgrow it.","chinese":"一位著名歌曲創作者曾說：「讓自己面對內心最深的恐懼；此後，恐懼便再也沒有力量。」 雖然這句話聽起來很戲劇化，但它其實直接點出了平凡生活中的真相。 從考試到友誼，挑戰不會因為我們拒絕說出它們的名字而消失；相反，它們會在黑暗中悄悄滋長。 這使許多年輕人開始思考，自己應該隱藏弱點，還是坦然面對它們，以變得更冷靜、更強大。 在我看來，承認挑戰並尋找應對方法是不可或缺的，因為只有認清令我們害怕的事物，我們才能理解它、處理它，並最終超越它。"},{"label":"Paragraph 3","english":"First, acknowledging a challenge gives fear a clear shape. A nameless fear is like smoke in a closed room: it spreads everywhere and makes it hard to breathe. Once we name it, however, we can locate its source and decide what to do next. I learnt this in Form Four, when I had to give an English presentation. I told myself that I was “just not a speaking person”. In reality, I was terrified of being laughed at. Because I refused to admit this, I avoided practice, rushed my preparation and finally stood before my classmates with shaking hands and a blank mind. It was not the presentation itself that defeated me; it was my refusal to face the fear behind it. After that failure, my teacher asked, “What exactly are you afraid of?” That question forced me to separate the problem into smaller parts—pronunciation, eye contact, memory and nervousness. Step by step, I recorded my voice, practiced in an empty classroom and asked two close friends to listen to me. Slowly but surely, the fear became less mysterious. It did not vanish overnight, but it no longer controlled me.","chinese":"首先，承認挑戰能讓恐懼呈現出清晰的形狀。 一種沒有名字的恐懼，就像密閉房間裡的煙霧：它四處蔓延，令人難以呼吸 然而，一旦我們為它命名，就能找出它的源頭，並決定下一步該怎樣做。 我是在中四那年明白這一點的，當時我需要做一次英文簡報。 我告訴自己，我「本來就不是擅長說話的人」。 實際上，我真正害怕的是被人取笑。 因為我拒絕承認這一點，所以我逃避練習，匆忙準備，最後站在同學面前時雙手顫抖，腦海一片空白。 真正擊敗我的並非簡報本身；關鍵在於我拒絕面對它背後的恐懼。 那次失敗之後，我的老師問我：「你到底害怕甚麼？」 這個問題迫使我把困難拆分成較小的部分—發音、眼神交流、記憶和緊張感 一步一步地，我錄下自己的聲音，在空課室裡練習，並請兩位好友聽我試講 慢慢地，但穩定地，那份恐懼變得不再那麼神秘。 它沒有一夜之間消失，但它已經不再控制我。"},{"label":"Paragraph 4","english":"Moreover, coping with challenges teaches us that courage is not the absence of fear, but the ability to act despite it. Many people imagine that “facing fear” means throwing oneself into pain recklessly. I disagree. To acknowledge fear is not to worship it; to cope with it is not to suffer silently. When I prepared for my first public speech competition, I felt so anxious that I could hardly sleep. Instead of pretending to be fine, I wrote down my worries and discovered that most of them were questions, not facts: What if I forget my lines? What if the judges look bored? What if my classmates think I am ridiculous? Once I saw these thoughts on paper, I could answer them rationally. I divided the speech into five sections, highlighted the opening sentence of each part and practised breathing slowly before I began. On the day of the competition, my voice still trembled. Nevertheless, I completed the speech, and walked away knowing that fear could travel with me without driving the vehicle.","chinese":"此外，應對挑戰讓我們明白，勇氣並非沒有恐懼；勇氣的核心在於即使害怕，仍然能夠行動。 許多人以為「面對恐懼」就是魯莽地把自己推進痛苦之中。 我不同意。 承認恐懼並不等於把它奉為主宰；應對恐懼也不等於默默承受痛苦。 當我準備第一次公開演講比賽時，我焦慮得幾乎睡不著。 我沒有假裝一切正常，反而把自己的憂慮寫下來，然後發現其中大多數都是疑問，並非事實： 如果我忘記台詞怎麼辦？ 如果評判看起來很沉悶怎麼辦？ 如果同學覺得我很可笑怎麼辦？ 一旦我在紙上看見這些想法，我就能理性地回應它們。 我把演講分成五個部分，標示每一部分的開首句，並在開始前練習慢慢呼吸 比賽當天，我的聲音仍然在顫抖。 儘管如此，我完成了演講，並在離開時明白到：恐懼可以與我同行，卻不必掌控方向盤。"},{"label":"Paragraph 5","english":"Some may argue that focusing on difficulties only makes people more negative. This view is understandable, especially when excessive worry can indeed become unhealthy. However, there is a crucial difference between acknowledging a challenge and dwelling on it. Ignoring a fever does not heal the body; ignoring anxiety does not heal the mind. In Form Five, after doing badly in a mock examination, I protected my pride by saying that the paper was unfair. My marks, of course, did not improve. Only when I admitted that my study method was shallow did real progress begin. I stopped copying notes mindlessly, started doing timed practices and discussed mistakes with classmates. A trouble shared was, in a very real sense, a trouble halved. The challenge remained, but it became something I could work with.","chinese":"有些人可能會主張，專注於困難只會令人變得更加消極。 這種看法是可以理解的，尤其是過度憂慮確實可能變得不健康。 然而，承認挑戰和沉溺於挑戰之間，存在一個關鍵分別。 忽視發燒不能治癒身體；忽視焦慮也不能治癒心靈。 中五時，在一次模擬考試中表現欠佳之後，我說試卷不公平，以此保護自己的自尊心。 當然，我的分數並沒有改善。 只有當我承認自己的溫習方法流於表面時，真正的進步才開始出現。 我停止盲目抄寫筆記，開始進行限時練習，並和同學討論錯誤。 從非常真實的意義上說，與人分擔困難，困難便減輕了一半。 挑戰仍然存在，但它變成了我能夠處理的東西。"},{"label":"Paragraph 6","english":"All in all, acknowledging challenges and finding ways to cope with them is not merely important; it is indispensable for us. Fear gains power when it is hidden, exaggerated and left unexplained. It loses power when it is named, examined and answered with practical action. As students, we should speak honestly about our struggles. As friends, teachers and family members, we should create an environment in which asking for help is seen not as weakness, but as wisdom. Life will always contain storms. What matters is whether we shut our eyes and sink, or open them, steady ourselves, and walk through the rain.","chinese":"總括而言，承認挑戰並尋找應對方法不只是重要；對我們來說，它更是不可或缺。 當恐懼被隱藏、被誇大，又得不到解釋時，它就會獲得力量。 當它被命名、被審視，並以實際行動回應時，它的力量就會減弱。 作為學生，我們應該坦誠說出自己的掙扎。 作為朋友、老師和家人，我們應該創造一種環境，讓求助不被視為軟弱，而被視為智慧。 人生總會有風暴。 真正重要的是，我們會閉上眼睛任由自己沉下去，還是睜開雙眼、穩住自己，然後穿過雨中前行。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"look fear in the eye","chinese":"直視恐懼；正視恐懼"},{"english":"a famous songwriter","chinese":"著名創作歌手"},{"english":"once said","chinese":"曾經說過"},{"english":"expose yourself to","chinese":"讓自己面對……"},{"english":"deepest fear","chinese":"最深層的恐懼"},{"english":"after that","chinese":"在那之後"},{"english":"have no power","chinese":"沒有力量"},{"english":"although the line sounds dramatic","chinese":"雖然這句話聽起來戲劇化"},{"english":"speak directly to","chinese":"直接切中……"},{"english":"ordinary life","chinese":"日常生活"},{"english":"from examinations to friendships","chinese":"由考試到友誼"},{"english":"challenges do not disappear","chinese":"挑戰不會消失"},{"english":"refuse to name","chinese":"拒絕指出；拒絕說出"},{"english":"instead","chinese":"反而"},{"english":"grow quietly in the dark","chinese":"在黑暗中悄悄壯大"},{"english":"this has made many young people consider whether","chinese":"這使很多年輕人思考是否"},{"english":"hide their weaknesses","chinese":"隱藏自己的弱點"},{"english":"face them openly","chinese":"坦然面對它們"},{"english":"in order to become","chinese":"為了變得"},{"english":"calmer and stronger","chinese":"更冷靜和更堅強"},{"english":"in my view","chinese":"在我看來"},{"english":"acknowledging challenges","chinese":"承認挑戰"},{"english":"finding ways to cope with","chinese":"找方法應對……"},{"english":"cope with","chinese":"應對"},{"english":"is essential","chinese":"是必不可少的"},{"english":"only by recognising","chinese":"只有透過認清"},{"english":"what frightens us","chinese":"令我們害怕的事"},{"english":"manage it","chinese":"管理它；控制它"},{"english":"outgrow it","chinese":"成長至不再受它限制"},{"english":"give fear a clear shape","chinese":"令恐懼有清晰形狀"},{"english":"a nameless fear","chinese":"無名的恐懼"},{"english":"a closed room","chinese":"密閉房間"},{"english":"spread everywhere","chinese":"到處蔓延"},{"english":"make it hard to breathe","chinese":"令人難以呼吸"},{"english":"once we name it","chinese":"一旦我們把它說出來"},{"english":"locate its source","chinese":"找出其源頭"},{"english":"decide what to do next","chinese":"決定下一步做甚麼"},{"english":"I learnt this in Form Four","chinese":"我在中四學到這一點"},{"english":"give an English presentation","chinese":"做英文匯報"},{"english":"not good at public speaking","chinese":"不擅長公開演說"},{"english":"in reality","chinese":"事實上"},{"english":"be terrified of","chinese":"非常害怕"},{"english":"being laughed at","chinese":"被取笑"},{"english":"refuse to admit","chinese":"拒絕承認"},{"english":"avoid practice","chinese":"逃避練習"},{"english":"rush my preparation","chinese":"匆忙準備"},{"english":"stand before my classmates","chinese":"站在同學面前"},{"english":"shaking hands","chinese":"顫抖的雙手"},{"english":"a blank mind","chinese":"腦海一片空白"},{"english":"not the presentation itself","chinese":"不是匯報本身"},{"english":"defeat me","chinese":"擊敗我"},{"english":"the fear behind it","chinese":"背後的恐懼"},{"english":"after that failure","chinese":"那次失敗之後"},{"english":"what exactly","chinese":"到底甚麼"},{"english":"force someone to","chinese":"迫使某人"},{"english":"separate the problem into smaller parts","chinese":"把問題拆成較小部分"},{"english":"eye contact","chinese":"眼神接觸"},{"english":"nervousness","chinese":"緊張"},{"english":"step by step","chinese":"一步一步地"},{"english":"record my voice","chinese":"錄下自己的聲音"},{"english":"practise in an empty classroom","chinese":"在空課室練習"},{"english":"close friends","chinese":"親密朋友；好友"},{"english":"listen to me","chinese":"聽我練習"},{"english":"slowly but surely","chinese":"慢慢但穩定地"},{"english":"become less mysterious","chinese":"變得不再那麼神秘"},{"english":"vanish overnight","chinese":"一夜之間消失"},{"english":"no longer controlled me","chinese":"不再控制我"},{"english":"moreover","chinese":"此外"},{"english":"coping with challenges","chinese":"應對挑戰"},{"english":"courage is not the absence of fear","chinese":"勇氣並不是沒有恐懼"},{"english":"the ability to act despite it","chinese":"即使害怕仍能行動的能力"},{"english":"imagine that","chinese":"以為；想像"},{"english":"facing fear","chinese":"面對恐懼"},{"english":"throw oneself into pain","chinese":"讓自己投進痛苦之中"},{"english":"recklessly","chinese":"魯莽地"},{"english":"to acknowledge fear is not to worship it","chinese":"承認恐懼並不是崇拜恐懼"},{"english":"worship it","chinese":"崇拜它"},{"english":"suffer silently","chinese":"默默忍受"},{"english":"prepare for","chinese":"為……作準備"},{"english":"public speech competition","chinese":"公開演講比賽"},{"english":"so anxious that","chinese":"焦慮得……"},{"english":"could hardly sleep","chinese":"幾乎睡不着"},{"english":"instead of pretending to be fine","chinese":"而不是假裝沒事"},{"english":"write down my worries","chinese":"寫下自己的憂慮"},{"english":"questions, not facts","chinese":"是問題，而不是事實"},{"english":"what if","chinese":"如果……怎麼辦"},{"english":"forget my lines","chinese":"忘記台詞"},{"english":"look bored","chinese":"看起來感到沉悶"},{"english":"think I am ridiculous","chinese":"覺得我很可笑"},{"english":"see these thoughts on paper","chinese":"在紙上看見這些想法"},{"english":"answer them rationally","chinese":"理性地回應它們"},{"english":"divide the speech into","chinese":"把演講分成……"},{"english":"five sections","chinese":"五個部分"},{"english":"highlight the opening sentence","chinese":"標示開首句"},{"english":"opening sentence","chinese":"開首句"},{"english":"practise breathing slowly","chinese":"練習慢慢呼吸"},{"english":"on the day of the competition","chinese":"比賽當日"},{"english":"voice still trembled","chinese":"聲音仍然顫抖"},{"english":"nevertheless","chinese":"儘管如此"},{"english":"complete the speech","chinese":"完成演講"},{"english":"walk away knowing that","chinese":"離開時明白"},{"english":"travel with me","chinese":"與我同行"},{"english":"drive the vehicle","chinese":"掌控方向；駕駛車輛"},{"english":"some may argue that","chinese":"有些人可能會認為"},{"english":"focus on difficulties","chinese":"專注於困難"},{"english":"more negative","chinese":"更負面"},{"english":"this view is understandable","chinese":"這種看法可以理解"},{"english":"excessive worry","chinese":"過度憂慮"},{"english":"indeed","chinese":"確實"},{"english":"become unhealthy","chinese":"變得不健康"},{"english":"crucial difference between","chinese":"……之間的關鍵分別"},{"english":"dwell on","chinese":"反覆糾結於……"},{"english":"ignoring a fever","chinese":"忽視發燒"},{"english":"heal the body","chinese":"治癒身體"},{"english":"ignoring anxiety","chinese":"忽視焦慮"},{"english":"heal the mind","chinese":"治癒心靈"},{"english":"do badly in","chinese":"在……表現差"},{"english":"mock examination","chinese":"模擬考試"},{"english":"protect my pride by","chinese":"透過……保護自尊"},{"english":"the paper was unfair","chinese":"試卷不公平"},{"english":"of course","chinese":"當然"},{"english":"only when I admitted that","chinese":"只有當我承認……時"},{"english":"study method","chinese":"學習方法"},{"english":"shallow","chinese":"浮淺的；不深入的"},{"english":"real progress began","chinese":"真正的進步開始"},{"english":"copy notes mindlessly","chinese":"盲目抄筆記"},{"english":"timed practice","chinese":"限時練習"},{"english":"discuss mistakes with","chinese":"與……討論錯誤"},{"english":"a trouble shared is a trouble halved","chinese":"困難有人分擔就減半"},{"english":"in a very real sense","chinese":"在很真實的意義上"},{"english":"remain","chinese":"仍然存在"},{"english":"work with","chinese":"可以處理；可以着手改善"},{"english":"all in all","chinese":"總括而言"},{"english":"not merely important","chinese":"不只是重要"},{"english":"indispensable","chinese":"不可或缺的"},{"english":"gain power","chinese":"變得更有力量"},{"english":"be hidden","chinese":"被隱藏"},{"english":"be exaggerated","chinese":"被誇大"},{"english":"be left unexplained","chinese":"未被解釋"},{"english":"lose power","chinese":"失去力量"},{"english":"be named and examined","chinese":"被說出並被審視"},{"english":"practical action","chinese":"實際行動"},{"english":"speak honestly about","chinese":"坦誠談論……"},{"english":"struggles","chinese":"掙扎；困難"},{"english":"create an environment in which","chinese":"創造一個……的環境"},{"english":"asking for help","chinese":"求助"},{"english":"be seen not as…, but as…","chinese":"不應被視為……而應被視為……"},{"english":"weakness","chinese":"軟弱"},{"english":"wisdom","chinese":"智慧"},{"english":"contain storms","chinese":"充滿風暴；總有風雨"},{"english":"what matters is whether","chinese":"重要的是是否"},{"english":"shut our eyes","chinese":"閉上眼睛"},{"english":"sink","chinese":"沉下去"},{"english":"steady ourselves","chinese":"穩住自己"},{"english":"walk through the rain","chinese":"走過風雨"}]},"dse-writing-2016-part-b-q9":{"exerciseId":"dse-writing-2016-part-b-q9","essayKey":"","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=dse-writing-2016-part-b-q9","flashDeckId":"dse/writing/part-b/2016/Q9","paragraphs":[{"label":"Paragraph 1","english":"Subject: Please support my application to HKAPA","chinese":"主旨：請支持我申請香港演藝學院。"},{"label":"Paragraph 2","english":"Dear Mum and Dad,","chinese":"親愛的爸爸媽媽："},{"label":"Paragraph 3","english":"I hope your trip is going well. As the application deadline is drawing near, I have been thinking carefully about life after HKDSE. Because I want to take up an acting career, I intend to apply to HKAPA. I am writing not to reject your advice, but to ask for your trust. I understand that you prefer a more academic subject because you want my future to be secure. My position, however, is that HKAPA is the most suitable choice for me, because it matches my strengths, provides professional training and still allows me to manage the risks sensibly.","chinese":"希望你們的旅程一切順利。 隨著申請截止日期逐漸臨近，我一直在認真思考中學文憑試之後的人生路向 因為我想投身演員事業，所以我打算申請香港演藝學院。 我寫這封電郵，並非要否定你們的建議；我真正想要的，是得到你們的信任 我明白你們較希望我修讀更學術性的科目，因為你們希望我的將來更有保障 然而，我的立場是，香港演藝學院最適合我，因為它切合我的長處、提供專業訓練，也仍然讓我能夠理性地管理風險。"},{"label":"Paragraph 4","english":"First, HKAPA is not an escape from academic discipline; it is the most direct and serious route to the career I am prepared to work for. Acting is not merely memorising lines under bright lights. It requires voice control, physical training, script analysis, emotional intelligence, teamwork and resilience. In a conventional academic programme, I might receive a respectable degree, but I would not receive daily training in the craft I want to practise. Over the past two years, I have joined school drama productions, volunteered backstage and watched performances to understand how actors build characters. The more I perform, the more I realise how demanding the profession is. That is exactly why proper training matters. If future doctors need medical school and future engineers need engineering training, why should a future actor avoid a performing arts academy? Choosing HKAPA is therefore not a childish impulse; to me, it is a practical alignment between my goal and my education.","chinese":"首先，香港演藝學院並非逃避學術訓練的地方；它是通往我已準備努力追求的職業最直接、最認真的道路。 演戲並不只是站在耀眼燈光下背誦台詞。 它需要聲線控制、形體訓練、劇本分析、情緒智商、團隊合作以及抗逆能力 在傳統學術課程中，我或許會取得一個受人尊重的學位，但我不會每天接受我真正想鑽研的表演技藝訓練。 在過去兩年，我參與了學校戲劇製作、自願協助後台工作，也觀看不同演出，以了解演員如何塑造角色。 我表演得越多，就越明白這個行業有多麼高要求。 這正正說明了為甚麼適當訓練如此重要。 如果未來的醫生需要醫學院，未來的工程師需要工程訓練，那麼未來的演員為甚麼要避開一所表演藝術學院呢？ 因此，選擇香港演藝學院並非孩子氣的衝動；對我來說，這是讓我的目標與教育方向實際配合起來的選擇。"},{"label":"Paragraph 5","english":"More importantly, I am not asking you to support a dream with no plan. I know you worry about income, competition and stability, and I do too. However, what concerns me more is the risk of spending four years studying something that I respect but do not truly belong to. A degree that looks safe on paper may become unsafe in reality if I study it without passion, confidence or direction. At HKAPA, I will build transferable skills such as clear communication, public speaking, collaboration, discipline and the ability to handle criticism. These skills are valuable not only on stage, but also in teaching, media, cultural management and public relations. In other words, I am not choosing “acting or nothing”; I am choosing a field that can open several doors in the creative industry. To minimise the risk, I will apply for scholarships, take part-time work only when it does not harm my training, keep improving my English and Putonghua, and review my progress with you after the first year. That way, my choice will be bold, but not blind.","chinese":"更重要的是，我並沒有要求你們支持一個毫無計劃的夢想。 我知道你們擔心收入、競爭和穩定性，而我也同樣擔心。 然而，令我更擔心的，是花四年時間修讀一個我尊重、但並不真正屬於我的科目所帶來的風險。 一個表面上看似安全的學位，如果我帶著缺乏熱情、信心和方向的狀態去修讀，現實中也可能變得不安全。 在香港演藝學院，我會建立可轉移的技能，例如清晰溝通、公眾演說、協作能力、紀律，以及處理批評的能力。 這些技能不只在舞台上有價值，也在教學、媒體、文化管理和公共關係等領域同樣有用。 換言之，我並非在選擇「除了演戲便一無所有」；我是在選擇一個能夠為我打開創意產業中多扇門的領域。 為了把風險降到最低，我會申請獎學金，只在不影響訓練的情況下兼職，繼續提升英文和普通話，並在第一年後與你們檢視我的進展。 那樣的話，我的選擇會是勇敢的，但絕不盲目。"},{"label":"Paragraph 6","english":"I know there is one objection you may still have: an academic subject at another institution may appear more respectable and stable in the eyes of relatives, employers and society. I hear you. You have worked so hard to give me options, and I would never treat that lightly. Still, respectability should not be confused with suitability. Studying a subject mainly to satisfy other people may keep me comfortable for a while, but it may also leave me wondering, for years, what would have happened if I had been brave enough to try. Just because the acting path is difficult does not mean it is irresponsible. If anything, knowing that it is difficult makes me more determined to prepare well. I am not asking you to lower your expectations of me; I am asking you to let me meet them in a field where I can stand tall.","chinese":"我知道你們可能仍然有一個反對理由：在另一所院校修讀學術科目，在親戚、僱主和社會眼中可能顯得更體面、更穩定。 我明白你們的感受。 你們一直如此努力，為我創造選擇，而我絕不會輕視這一點。 即使如此，體面不應與適合混為一談。 主要為了滿足別人而修讀某個科目，也許能讓我暫時感到安穩，但它也可能讓我在多年之後仍然反覆想着：如果當初我夠勇敢去嘗試，結果會怎樣？ 演員這條路困難，並不代表選擇它就是不負責任。 真要說的話，正因為我知道它困難，我才更加決心要好好準備。 我並非要求你們降低對我的期望；我希望你們容許我在一個能讓我昂首挺立的領域裡達到那些期望。"},{"label":"Paragraph 7","english":"Therefore, Mum and Dad, please support my application to HKAPA before the deadline. I promise that I will not take your support for granted. I will show you my application materials, practise seriously for the audition and keep you updated while you are away. It would mean a lot to me if, when I press “submit”, I could feel that I am not walking away from my family, but walking forward with your blessing. I love you both, and I hope you can count on me to turn this choice into something worthy of your trust.","chinese":"因此，爸爸媽媽，請在截止日期前支持我申請香港演藝學院。 我承諾，我絕不會把你們的支持視作理所當然。 我會把申請資料給你們看，認真準備試鏡，並在你們外遊期間持續向你們交代最新情況。 如果在我按下「提交」的一刻，我能感到自己並非正在離開家庭；相反，我是在帶著你們的祝福向前走，這對我來說會意義重大。 我愛你們兩位，也希望你們可以相信我會把這個選擇變成一件值得你們信任的事。 愛你們的，"},{"label":"Paragraph 8","english":"Love,","chinese":"我愛你們兩位，也希望你們可以相信我會把這個選擇變成一件值得你們信任的事。 愛你們的，"},{"label":"Paragraph 9","english":"Chris","chinese":"Chris"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"support my application to","chinese":"支持我申請……"},{"english":"HKAPA","chinese":"香港演藝學院"},{"english":"Dear Mum and Dad","chinese":"親愛的爸爸媽媽"},{"english":"I hope your trip is going well","chinese":"希望你們旅途順利"},{"english":"application deadline","chinese":"申請截止日期"},{"english":"draw near","chinese":"逐漸迫近"},{"english":"think carefully about","chinese":"認真思考"},{"english":"life after HKDSE","chinese":"文憑試後的人生"},{"english":"HKDSE","chinese":"香港中學文憑試"},{"english":"pursue an acting career","chinese":"投身演員事業"},{"english":"intend to apply to","chinese":"打算申請"},{"english":"I am writing not to…but to…","chinese":"我寫信不是為了……而是為了……"},{"english":"reject your advice","chinese":"拒絕你們的建議"},{"english":"ask for your trust","chinese":"請求你們信任"},{"english":"prefer a more academic subject","chinese":"較喜歡學術性較強的科目"},{"english":"want my future to be secure","chinese":"希望我的前途有保障"},{"english":"my position is that","chinese":"我的立場是"},{"english":"the most suitable choice","chinese":"最合適的選擇"},{"english":"match my strengths","chinese":"符合我的強項"},{"english":"provide professional training","chinese":"提供專業訓練"},{"english":"manage the risks sensibly","chinese":"理性地管理風險"},{"english":"not an escape from","chinese":"不是逃避……"},{"english":"academic discipline","chinese":"學術紀律；學術訓練"},{"english":"the most direct and serious route","chinese":"最直接而認真的途徑"},{"english":"be prepared to work for","chinese":"準備為……努力"},{"english":"not merely","chinese":"不只是"},{"english":"memorise lines","chinese":"背台詞"},{"english":"under bright lights","chinese":"在明亮燈光下"},{"english":"voice control","chinese":"聲線控制"},{"english":"physical training","chinese":"身體訓練"},{"english":"script analysis","chinese":"劇本分析"},{"english":"emotional intelligence","chinese":"情緒智商"},{"english":"teamwork and resilience","chinese":"團隊合作和抗逆力"},{"english":"conventional academic programme","chinese":"傳統學術課程"},{"english":"respectable degree","chinese":"受尊重的學位"},{"english":"daily training in","chinese":"每日接受……訓練"},{"english":"the craft I want to practise","chinese":"我想鑽研的技藝"},{"english":"over the past two years","chinese":"在過去兩年"},{"english":"school drama productions","chinese":"學校戲劇製作"},{"english":"volunteer backstage","chinese":"自願到後台幫忙"},{"english":"watch performances","chinese":"觀看演出"},{"english":"build characters","chinese":"塑造角色"},{"english":"the more…the more…","chinese":"越……越……"},{"english":"how demanding the profession is","chinese":"這個職業有多高要求"},{"english":"proper training matters","chinese":"正規訓練很重要"},{"english":"medical school","chinese":"醫學院"},{"english":"engineering training","chinese":"工程訓練"},{"english":"performing arts academy","chinese":"表演藝術學院"},{"english":"childish impulse","chinese":"幼稚衝動"},{"english":"practical alignment between…and…","chinese":"……與……之間的實際契合"},{"english":"my goal and my education","chinese":"我的目標和我的教育"},{"english":"more importantly","chinese":"更重要的是"},{"english":"support a dream with no plan","chinese":"支持一個沒有計劃的夢想"},{"english":"worry about","chinese":"擔心"},{"english":"income, competition and stability","chinese":"收入、競爭和穩定性"},{"english":"what concerns me more","chinese":"更令我擔心的是"},{"english":"the risk of spending four years","chinese":"花四年的風險"},{"english":"truly belong to","chinese":"真正屬於；真正適合"},{"english":"look safe on paper","chinese":"紙面上看似安全"},{"english":"become unsafe in reality","chinese":"在現實中變得有風險"},{"english":"without passion, confidence or direction","chinese":"沒有熱誠、信心或方向"},{"english":"transferable skills","chinese":"可轉移技能"},{"english":"clear communication","chinese":"清晰溝通"},{"english":"public speaking","chinese":"公開演說"},{"english":"collaboration","chinese":"協作"},{"english":"the ability to handle criticism","chinese":"承受批評的能力"},{"english":"valuable not only…but also…","chinese":"不但對……有價值，而且對……也有價值"},{"english":"on stage","chinese":"在舞台上"},{"english":"cultural management","chinese":"文化管理"},{"english":"public relations","chinese":"公共關係"},{"english":"in other words","chinese":"換言之"},{"english":"acting or nothing","chinese":"演戲或一無所有"},{"english":"open several doors","chinese":"打開幾扇門；帶來多種機會"},{"english":"creative industry","chinese":"創意產業"},{"english":"minimise the risk","chinese":"將風險減至最低"},{"english":"apply for scholarships","chinese":"申請獎學金"},{"english":"take part-time work","chinese":"做兼職工作"},{"english":"harm my training","chinese":"影響我的訓練"},{"english":"keep improving","chinese":"持續改善"},{"english":"English and Putonghua","chinese":"英文和普通話"},{"english":"review my progress with","chinese":"與……檢討我的進度"},{"english":"after the first year","chinese":"第一年後"},{"english":"bold, but not blind","chinese":"大膽但不盲目"},{"english":"one objection","chinese":"一個反對意見"},{"english":"academic subject","chinese":"學術科目"},{"english":"another institution","chinese":"另一所院校"},{"english":"appear more respectable and stable","chinese":"看起來更體面和穩定"},{"english":"in the eyes of","chinese":"在……眼中"},{"english":"relatives, employers and society","chinese":"親戚、僱主和社會"},{"english":"I hear you","chinese":"我明白你們的想法"},{"english":"work so hard to","chinese":"非常努力去……"},{"english":"give me options","chinese":"給我選擇"},{"english":"treat that lightly","chinese":"輕視這一點"},{"english":"respectability","chinese":"體面；受尊重"},{"english":"be confused with","chinese":"與……混為一談"},{"english":"suitability","chinese":"合適程度"},{"english":"mainly to satisfy other people","chinese":"主要為了滿足別人"},{"english":"keep me comfortable for a while","chinese":"令我暫時安心"},{"english":"leave me wondering","chinese":"令我一直疑惑"},{"english":"for years","chinese":"多年來"},{"english":"what would have happened if","chinese":"如果……會發生甚麼"},{"english":"brave enough to try","chinese":"有足夠勇氣嘗試"},{"english":"just because…does not mean…","chinese":"只因……並不代表……"},{"english":"the acting path","chinese":"演員道路"},{"english":"irresponsible","chinese":"不負責任"},{"english":"if anything","chinese":"反而；如果說有甚麼"},{"english":"more determined to","chinese":"更加下定決心去……"},{"english":"prepare well","chinese":"好好準備"},{"english":"lower your expectations of me","chinese":"降低你們對我的期望"},{"english":"meet them","chinese":"達到它們；符合期望"},{"english":"in a field where","chinese":"在一個……的領域"},{"english":"stand tall","chinese":"堂堂正正地站穩"},{"english":"support my application","chinese":"支持我的申請"},{"english":"before the deadline","chinese":"在截止日期前"},{"english":"promise that","chinese":"承諾"},{"english":"take your support for granted","chinese":"把你們的支持視為理所當然"},{"english":"application materials","chinese":"申請材料"},{"english":"practise seriously for","chinese":"為……認真練習"},{"english":"audition","chinese":"試鏡"},{"english":"keep you updated","chinese":"讓你們知道最新情況"},{"english":"while you are away","chinese":"在你們不在香港期間"},{"english":"mean a lot to me","chinese":"對我意義重大"},{"english":"press submit","chinese":"按下「提交」"},{"english":"not walking away from…but walking forward with…","chinese":"不是離開……而是帶著……向前走"},{"english":"walking away from my family","chinese":"離開家人；背棄家庭"},{"english":"walking forward with your blessing","chinese":"帶著你們的祝福向前走"},{"english":"count on me","chinese":"相信我；依靠我"},{"english":"turn this choice into","chinese":"把這個選擇變成"},{"english":"worthy of your trust","chinese":"對得起你們信任"},{"english":"Love","chinese":"愛你的"}]},"dse-writing-2017-part-a":{"exerciseId":"dse-writing-2017-part-a","essayKey":"","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=dse-writing-2017-part-a","flashDeckId":"dse/writing/part-a/2017","paragraphs":[{"label":"Salutation","english":"Dear Ms Lee,","chinese":"李女士鈞鑒："},{"label":"Salutation","english":"I hope this letter finds you well. As Chairperson of the Social Service Club, I would like to propose a novel project to strengthen our school’s relationship with the community, particularly with Evergreen Elderly Home. Instead of reading sessions or technology workshops, we wish to implement a weekly “Taste of Traditions” cooking program.","chinese":"祝安。 作為社會服務學會主席，我希望提出一個新穎的項目，以加強本校與社區的關係，尤其是與 Evergreen Elderly Home 的聯繫。 我們希望推行一個每週舉行的「Taste of Traditions」烹飪活動，而不是舉辦閱讀活動或科技工作坊。"},{"label":"Project Details","english":"During each session, our student volunteers and the elderly residents will come together to cook simple, culturally significant dishes such as handmade dumplings or traditional desserts. By pairing each student with a senior “cooking mentor,” we can provide ample one-on-one interaction, enabling both parties to share skills and family recipes while exchanging stories behind each dish. These sessions will culminate in a mini-tasting event, where participants can appreciate one another’s creations and celebrate cultural diversity.","chinese":"在每一節活動中，我們的學生義工和長者院友將會聚在一起，烹調一些簡單而具有文化意義的菜式，例如手製餃子或傳統甜品。 透過把每位學生與一位長者「烹飪導師」配對，我們可以提供充足的一對一互動機會，讓雙方分享技巧和家傳食譜，同時交流每道菜背後的故事。 這些活動將以一個小型試食活動作結，讓參加者欣賞彼此的作品，並慶祝文化多樣性。"},{"label":"Benefits","english":"I firmly believe that “Taste of Traditions” will benefit Evergreen Elderly Home by enhancing its residents’ sense of purpose and belonging, as they pass on cherished knowledge. At the same time, our students will broaden their culinary horizons and gain deeper respect for older generations. Through this collaborative and creative atmosphere, we can forge meaningful bonds and enrich everyone’s overall well-being.","chinese":"我堅信，「Taste of Traditions」將會令 Evergreen Elderly Home 受益，因為長者院友在傳承珍貴知識的過程中，能夠提升自己的目標感和歸屬感。 與此同時，我們的學生將能擴闊自己的烹飪視野，並對年長一輩產生更深的尊重。 透過這種協作而富創意的氛圍，我們可以建立有意義的聯繫，並提升每個人的整體福祉。"},{"label":"Closing","english":"Thank you for considering my proposal, and please feel free to contact me should you have any questions.","chinese":"感謝您考慮我的建議；如有任何問題，請隨時與我聯絡。"},{"label":"Closing","english":"Yours sincerely,","chinese":"謹啟"},{"label":"Closing","english":"Chris Wong","chinese":"Chris Wong"},{"label":"Closing","english":"Chairperson, Social Service Club","chinese":"社會服務學會主席"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"Dear Ms Lee","chinese":"李女士鈞鑒"},{"english":"I hope this letter finds you well","chinese":"祝安；希望你一切安好"},{"english":"Chairperson of","chinese":"……主席"},{"english":"Social Service Club","chinese":"社會服務學會"},{"english":"would like to propose","chinese":"希望提出"},{"english":"novel project","chinese":"新穎的項目"},{"english":"strengthen our school's relationship with","chinese":"加強我們學校與……的關係"},{"english":"the community","chinese":"社區"},{"english":"particularly with","chinese":"尤其是與……"},{"english":"Evergreen Elderly Home","chinese":"Evergreen Elderly Home"},{"english":"instead of","chinese":"而不是"},{"english":"reading sessions","chinese":"閱讀活動"},{"english":"technology workshops","chinese":"科技工作坊"},{"english":"wish to implement","chinese":"希望推行"},{"english":"weekly cooking programme","chinese":"每週烹飪活動"},{"english":"Taste of Traditions","chinese":"Taste of Traditions（傳統滋味）"},{"english":"during each session","chinese":"在每節活動中"},{"english":"student volunteers","chinese":"學生義工"},{"english":"elderly residents","chinese":"長者院友"},{"english":"come together to","chinese":"聚在一起去……"},{"english":"culturally significant dishes","chinese":"具有文化意義的菜式"},{"english":"handmade dumplings","chinese":"手製餃子"},{"english":"traditional desserts","chinese":"傳統甜品"},{"english":"pair each student with","chinese":"將每名學生與……配對"},{"english":"senior cooking mentor","chinese":"長者烹飪導師"},{"english":"provide ample interaction","chinese":"提供充足互動"},{"english":"one-on-one interaction","chinese":"一對一互動"},{"english":"enabling both parties to","chinese":"讓雙方能夠……"},{"english":"both parties","chinese":"雙方"},{"english":"share skills","chinese":"分享技能"},{"english":"family recipes","chinese":"家傳食譜"},{"english":"exchange stories behind each dish","chinese":"交流每道菜背後的故事"},{"english":"culminate in","chinese":"以……作結"},{"english":"mini-tasting event","chinese":"小型試食活動"},{"english":"appreciate one another's creations","chinese":"欣賞彼此的作品"},{"english":"celebrate cultural diversity","chinese":"慶祝文化多元"},{"english":"firmly believe that","chinese":"堅信"},{"english":"benefit","chinese":"使……受益"},{"english":"enhance someone's sense of purpose","chinese":"提升某人的人生目標感"},{"english":"sense of belonging","chinese":"歸屬感"},{"english":"pass on cherished knowledge","chinese":"傳承珍貴知識"},{"english":"at the same time","chinese":"與此同時"},{"english":"broaden their culinary horizons","chinese":"擴闊烹飪視野"},{"english":"gain deeper respect for","chinese":"對……有更深尊重"},{"english":"older generations","chinese":"老一輩"},{"english":"collaborative and creative atmosphere","chinese":"協作而富創意的氣氛"},{"english":"forge meaningful bonds","chinese":"建立有意義的連繫"},{"english":"enrich everyone's overall well-being","chinese":"提升每個人的整體身心健康"},{"english":"thank you for considering","chinese":"感謝你考慮……"},{"english":"please feel free to","chinese":"歡迎隨時……"},{"english":"should you have any questions","chinese":"如有任何問題"},{"english":"Yours sincerely","chinese":"謹啟"},{"english":"Chairperson, Social Service Club","chinese":"社會服務學會主席"}]},"dse-writing-2017-part-b-q2":{"exerciseId":"dse-writing-2017-part-b-q2","essayKey":"","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=dse-writing-2017-part-b-q2","flashDeckId":"dse/writing/part-b/2017/Q2","paragraphs":[{"label":"Paragraph 1","english":"The Chance I Let Slip, the Chance I Chose","chinese":"我錯失的機會，我選擇把握的機會"},{"label":"Paragraph 2","english":"Posted after midnight, while a song is still looping in my head.","chinese":"午夜過後發佈，腦海裡仍然循環播放著那首歌。"},{"label":"Paragraph 3","english":"Some songs do not merely play; they interrogate you. The one I heard tonight asks what we would do if life handed us “one shot”. Would we take it, or let it slip? We like to imagine opportunities as grand entrances - imagine a stage, a prize, applause. In reality, they often arrive in ordinary forms — a form on a teacher’s desk, a message we hesitate to answer, a seat where our voice might shake. The song has made me look back at two moments - one when fear chose for me, and one when, for once, I chose for myself.","chinese":"有些歌並不只是響起；它們會拷問你。 我今晚聽到的那一首，在問我們：假如人生把「一次機會」遞到我們面前，我們會怎樣做。 我們會把它抓住，還是任由它溜走？ 我們喜歡把機會想像成盛大的登場——想像一下舞台、獎項和掌聲。 現實中，機會往往以平凡的形式出現——老師桌上的一張表格、一則我們猶豫著要不要回覆的訊息、一個輪到我們開口時聲音可能發抖的位置。 這首歌令我回望兩個瞬間——一個是恐懼替我作了決定的瞬間，另一個是我終於罕有地替自己作出決定的瞬間。"},{"label":"Paragraph 4","english":"The opportunity I missed came in Secondary Three, when my English teacher encouraged me to enter an inter-school speech festival. Public speaking had always fascinated me. Deep down, I wanted to be one of those people who could turn silence into attention. The trouble was that wanting something is one thing; being seen wanting it is another. I imagined forgetting my lines, hearing classmates laugh and having my nervous face remembered after the competition. The application form stayed in my bag for a week like a secret. Each day I told myself I would submit it tomorrow. By the time I unfolded it, the deadline had passed.","chinese":"我錯過的那次機會出現在中三，當時英文老師鼓勵我參加校際演講比賽。 公開演說一直令我著迷。 在內心深處，我想成為那種能把沉默轉化為全場注視的人。 問題在於，想要某樣東西是一回事；讓別人看見自己想要它，又是另一回事 我想像自己忘詞、聽見同學發笑，還想像比賽後大家仍記得我那張緊張的臉 那張報名表像秘密一樣，在我的書包裡放了一星期。 每天我都告訴自己，明天就會交上去。 等到我把它攤開時，截止日期已經過了。"},{"label":"Paragraph 5","english":"For a while, I pretended it did not matter. “There will be other chances,” I said, as if regret could be reasoned with. Then my classmate Mary joined the festival instead. She did not win; she even lost her place once. Yet she returned to school laughing at herself, and something about her had changed. She stood taller. She spoke more freely in lessons. Watching her, I realised that I had misunderstood failure. I had thought embarrassment would break me; instead, hesitation quietly diminished me. Not until then did I understand that the cost of a missed opportunity is not only what we fail to achieve, but also the person we postpone becoming.","chinese":"有一段時間，我假裝這件事並不重要。 「之後還會有其他機會的，」我這樣對自己說，彷彿遺憾可以靠道理說服。 後來，我的同學瑪麗反而參加了那個比賽。 她沒有勝出；她甚至一度忘記自己講到哪裡。 可是她回到學校時，還能笑自己，而她身上有些東西已經改變了。 她站得更挺直了。 她在課堂上說話也更自在了。 看著她，我才意識到自己誤解了失敗。 我原以為尷尬會擊垮我；結果，真正悄悄削弱我的，是猶豫。 直到那時我才明白，錯過機會的代價，不只是我們未能達成甚麼，也包括我們延遲成為的那個自己。"},{"label":"Paragraph 6","english":"The opportunity I took arrived the following year, with far less glamour. Our school was recruiting volunteers to run Saturday storytelling sessions for children at a community centre. No stage lights. No judges. No prize. Just twenty restless children and a stack of picture books. At first glance, it seemed small. On closer inspection, it was exactly the kind of test I needed. Before I could talk myself out of it, I signed up.","chinese":"我把握住的機會在第二年出現，形式遠沒有那麼耀眼。 學校當時正在招募義工，於星期六在社區中心為小朋友主持故事時間。 沒有舞台燈光。 沒有評判。 沒有獎項。 只有二十個坐不定的小朋友和一疊圖畫書。 乍看之下，這件事似乎很小。 細看之後，它正正是我需要面對的那種考驗。 在我來得及說服自己退出之前，我已經報名了。"},{"label":"Paragraph 7","english":"The first session was painful in a very educational way. My voice shook so badly that one boy asked whether I was cold. Another child kept interrupting to ask if the dragon could eat the king immediately. At one point, I nearly gave up and read as quickly as possible just to escape. Then I remembered the folded application form from the year before. Enough already, I told the old version of myself. I slowed down. I gave the dragon a ridiculous voice and asked the children to invent the ending. Little by little, the room changed. By the second session, they were shouting ideas before I had turned the first page.","chinese":"第一節課痛苦得很有教育意義。 我的聲音抖得太厲害，以至於有個男孩問我是不是很冷。 另一個孩子不停打斷我，問那條龍可不可以立刻吃掉國王。 有一刻，我差點放棄，只想盡快讀完，逃離現場。 然後，我想起了前一年那張被我摺起來的報名表。 夠了，我對過去那個自己說。 我慢了下來。 我用荒謬的聲線扮演那條龍，然後請孩子們創作結局。 一點一點地，房間裡的氣氛改變了。 到了第二節課，我還沒翻開第一頁，他們已經在喊出各種想法。"},{"label":"Paragraph 8","english":"What surprised me most was not that I became more confident, although I did. It was that an opportunity was not just a doorway for personal success; it was a way to make room for other people. A quiet girl named Jane stayed behind after one session and asked if she could borrow the book to read to her younger brother. That tiny request made my day. It meant that my trembling voice had still carried something useful across the room. What the experience lacked in glamour, it made up for in meaning.","chinese":"最令我驚訝的，並非我變得更有信心，雖然我的確如此。 真正令我驚訝的，是機會不只是通往個人成功的一道門；它也是為別人騰出空間的一種方法。 一個名叫珍的安靜女孩在某次課後留下來，問我可不可以借那本書回去讀給弟弟聽。 那個小小的請求讓我整天都很開心。 這代表我那把顫抖的聲音，終究仍把一些有用的東西帶到了房間另一端。 這段經歷在光彩上有所欠缺，卻在意義上補了回來。"},{"label":"Paragraph 9","english":"So tonight, as the song keeps echoing in my mind, I am left with a simple truth - the truth that opportunities do not always announce themselves as life-changing. Some slip away because we wait too long; others open only because we move before fear finishes its argument. I cannot undo the speech festival. Things past cannot be recalled. But the next time life asks whether I will capture the moment, I hope my answer will be quicker, braver and louder - yes.","chinese":"所以今晚，當那首歌仍在我腦海中回響時，我最後得到一個簡單的真相—— 機會並不總會以改變人生的姿態宣告自己來臨。 有些機會會因為我們等得太久而溜走；另一些機會只會在我們趕在恐懼把理由說完之前行動時打開。 我無法重來那次演講比賽。 過去的事無法重來。 但下一次人生問我會不會抓住那一刻時，我希望我的答案會更快、更勇敢、也更響亮——會。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"let slip","chinese":"錯失；白白放走"},{"english":"the chance I chose","chinese":"我選擇把握的機會"},{"english":"posted after midnight","chinese":"午夜後發布"},{"english":"while a song is still looping in my head","chinese":"當一首歌仍在腦海中不斷播放"},{"english":"loop in my head","chinese":"在腦海中不斷重播"},{"english":"do not merely play","chinese":"不只是播放"},{"english":"interrogate you","chinese":"盤問；深深追問"},{"english":"the one I heard tonight","chinese":"我今晚聽到的那一首"},{"english":"life handed us “one shot”","chinese":"人生給予我們一次機會"},{"english":"take it","chinese":"把握它"},{"english":"let it slip","chinese":"錯失它"},{"english":"like to imagine","chinese":"喜歡想像"},{"english":"opportunities as grand entrances","chinese":"把機會想像成隆重登場"},{"english":"a stage, a prize and applause","chinese":"舞台、獎項和掌聲"},{"english":"in reality","chinese":"事實上"},{"english":"arrive in ordinary forms","chinese":"以平凡的形式出現"},{"english":"a form on a teacher's desk","chinese":"老師桌上的一張表格"},{"english":"hesitate to answer","chinese":"猶豫是否回覆"},{"english":"a seat where our voice might shake","chinese":"一個可能令我們聲音顫抖的位置"},{"english":"make me look back at","chinese":"令我回望"},{"english":"fear chose for me","chinese":"恐懼替我作出選擇"},{"english":"for once","chinese":"終於有一次"},{"english":"choose for myself","chinese":"為自己作出選擇"},{"english":"the opportunity I missed","chinese":"我錯失的機會"},{"english":"came in Secondary Three","chinese":"在中三時出現"},{"english":"encourage someone to","chinese":"鼓勵某人去……"},{"english":"enter a speech festival","chinese":"參加朗誦節"},{"english":"inter-school speech festival","chinese":"校際朗誦節"},{"english":"public speaking","chinese":"公開演說"},{"english":"fascinate someone","chinese":"深深吸引某人"},{"english":"deep down","chinese":"內心深處"},{"english":"one of those people who","chinese":"那種能夠……的人之一"},{"english":"turn silence into attention","chinese":"把沉默變成專注"},{"english":"the trouble was that","chinese":"問題是"},{"english":"wanting something is one thing","chinese":"想要某件事是一回事"},{"english":"being seen wanting it is another","chinese":"被人看見自己渴望它又是另一回事"},{"english":"forget my lines","chinese":"忘記台詞"},{"english":"hear classmates laugh","chinese":"聽到同學嘲笑"},{"english":"have my nervous face remembered","chinese":"讓自己緊張的樣子被記住"},{"english":"application form","chinese":"報名表；申請表"},{"english":"stay in my bag like a secret","chinese":"像秘密一樣留在書包裏"},{"english":"told myself I would","chinese":"告訴自己會……"},{"english":"submit it tomorrow","chinese":"明天才交"},{"english":"by the time","chinese":"到……的時候"},{"english":"unfold it","chinese":"打開它；攤開它"},{"english":"the deadline had passed","chinese":"截止日期已經過了"},{"english":"for a while","chinese":"有一段時間"},{"english":"pretend it did not matter","chinese":"假裝這不重要"},{"english":"There will be other chances","chinese":"將來還會有其他機會"},{"english":"as if regret could be reasoned with","chinese":"彷彿可以用道理說服遺憾"},{"english":"regret could be reasoned with","chinese":"遺憾可以被說服"},{"english":"joined the festival instead","chinese":"反而參加了比賽"},{"english":"lose her place","chinese":"忘記講到哪裏"},{"english":"return to school laughing at herself","chinese":"回到學校時自嘲地笑"},{"english":"something about her had changed","chinese":"她身上有些東西改變了"},{"english":"stand taller","chinese":"站得更挺直；更有自信"},{"english":"speak more freely","chinese":"說話更自在"},{"english":"watching her","chinese":"看着她"},{"english":"misunderstand failure","chinese":"誤解失敗"},{"english":"embarrassment would break me","chinese":"尷尬會擊垮我"},{"english":"hesitation quietly diminished me","chinese":"猶豫悄悄削弱了我"},{"english":"not until then did I understand","chinese":"直到那時我才明白"},{"english":"the cost of a missed opportunity","chinese":"錯失機會的代價"},{"english":"what we fail to achieve","chinese":"我們未能達成的事"},{"english":"the person we postpone becoming","chinese":"我們延遲成為的那個自己"},{"english":"postpone becoming","chinese":"延遲成為"},{"english":"the opportunity I took","chinese":"我把握的機會"},{"english":"the following year","chinese":"第二年；翌年"},{"english":"with far less glamour","chinese":"遠沒有那麼光鮮"},{"english":"recruit volunteers","chinese":"招募義工"},{"english":"run storytelling sessions","chinese":"舉辦講故事活動"},{"english":"Saturday storytelling sessions","chinese":"星期六講故事活動"},{"english":"community centre","chinese":"社區中心"},{"english":"no stage lights, no judges and no prize","chinese":"沒有舞台燈光、評判和獎項"},{"english":"restless children","chinese":"坐不定的小朋友"},{"english":"a stack of picture books","chinese":"一疊圖畫書"},{"english":"at first glance","chinese":"乍看之下"},{"english":"on closer inspection","chinese":"仔細看來"},{"english":"exactly the kind of test","chinese":"正正是那種考驗"},{"english":"before I could talk myself out of it","chinese":"在我說服自己退縮之前"},{"english":"talk myself out of it","chinese":"說服自己放棄"},{"english":"sign up","chinese":"報名參加"},{"english":"painful in a very educational way","chinese":"痛苦但很有教育意義"},{"english":"voice shook so badly that","chinese":"聲音抖得厲害，以致……"},{"english":"ask whether","chinese":"問是否"},{"english":"keep interrupting","chinese":"不斷打斷"},{"english":"immediately","chinese":"立即；馬上"},{"english":"at one point","chinese":"有一刻"},{"english":"nearly give up","chinese":"差點放棄"},{"english":"as quickly as possible","chinese":"盡快"},{"english":"just to escape","chinese":"只為了逃避"},{"english":"remember the folded application form","chinese":"想起摺起的報名表"},{"english":"from the year before","chinese":"前一年"},{"english":"Enough already","chinese":"夠了"},{"english":"the old version of myself","chinese":"過去那個自己"},{"english":"slow down","chinese":"放慢下來"},{"english":"give the dragon a ridiculous voice","chinese":"用滑稽的聲音扮演巨龍"},{"english":"invent the ending","chinese":"創作結局"},{"english":"little by little","chinese":"一點一點地"},{"english":"by the second session","chinese":"到第二次活動時"},{"english":"shout ideas","chinese":"大聲提出想法"},{"english":"before I had turned the first page","chinese":"在我翻開第一頁之前"},{"english":"what surprised me most was","chinese":"最令我驚訝的是"},{"english":"become more confident","chinese":"變得更有自信"},{"english":"not just a doorway for","chinese":"不只是通往……的門口"},{"english":"personal success","chinese":"個人成功"},{"english":"make room for other people","chinese":"為他人騰出空間"},{"english":"a quiet girl named Jane","chinese":"一個名叫Jane的文靜女孩"},{"english":"stay behind","chinese":"留下來"},{"english":"borrow the book","chinese":"借那本書"},{"english":"younger brother","chinese":"弟弟"},{"english":"tiny request","chinese":"小小的請求"},{"english":"make my day","chinese":"令我非常開心"},{"english":"trembling voice","chinese":"顫抖的聲音"},{"english":"carry something useful across the room","chinese":"把有用的東西傳到房間另一邊"},{"english":"lack in glamour","chinese":"缺少光彩"},{"english":"make up for in meaning","chinese":"以意義彌補"},{"english":"keep echoing in my mind","chinese":"在腦海中迴響"},{"english":"be left with a simple truth","chinese":"留下一個簡單的道理"},{"english":"announce themselves as life-changing","chinese":"以改變人生的姿態出現"},{"english":"slip away","chinese":"悄悄溜走"},{"english":"wait too long","chinese":"等得太久"},{"english":"open only because","chinese":"只因為……才打開"},{"english":"move before fear finishes its argument","chinese":"在恐懼說服我們之前先行動"},{"english":"fear finishes its argument","chinese":"恐懼完成它的說服"},{"english":"cannot undo","chinese":"無法改變；無法挽回"},{"english":"What is past cannot be recalled","chinese":"往事不可追"},{"english":"the next time life asks whether","chinese":"下一次人生問我是否……"},{"english":"capture the moment","chinese":"把握當下"},{"english":"quicker, braver and louder","chinese":"更快、更勇敢、更響亮"},{"english":"prove the point","chinese":"證明這一點"}]},"dse-writing-2017-part-b-q3":{"exerciseId":"dse-writing-2017-part-b-q3","essayKey":"","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=dse-writing-2017-part-b-q3","flashDeckId":"dse/writing/part-b/2017/Q3","paragraphs":[{"label":"Paragraph 1","english":"The Lion at the Fridge The first thing people ask is how a lion got into our kitchen. The better question is why it came back.","chinese":"冰箱旁的獅子 人們問的第一件事，是一頭獅子究竟怎樣走進我們的廚房。 更值得問的問題，是牠為甚麼會回來。"},{"label":"Paragraph 2","english":"Seven years before the photograph was taken, my father brought home a cardboard box that breathed.","chinese":"那張照片拍下來的七年前，爸爸帶回家一個會呼吸的紙箱。"},{"label":"Paragraph 3","english":"It was a black summer night, the kind of night when rain hammered the windows as if trying to get in. Father, a wildlife veterinarian, had been called to a warehouse near the harbour after customs officers discovered a shipment of illegal animals. One had been left behind: a lion cub no longer than my schoolbag, shivering in the dark.","chinese":"那是一個漆黑的夏夜，雨水猛烈敲打著窗戶，彷彿正試圖闖進屋內。 爸爸是一名野生動物獸醫；在海關人員發現一批非法運送的動物後，他被召到海港附近的一個貨倉。 其中一隻被遺留下來：那是一頭小獅子，身長還不及我的書包，正在黑暗中顫抖。"},{"label":"Paragraph 4","english":"“Just until morning,” Father told Mum, though his “until morning” often meant “until my heart lets go.”","chinese":"「只到明天早上，」爸爸對媽媽說，儘管他的「到明天早上」往往意味着「直到我的心願意放手為止」。"},{"label":"Paragraph 5","english":"The cub had amber eyes, mud in his whiskers and a thin white scar above his nose. I named him Kito. He spent that first night in our kitchen because it was the warmest room in the flat. I fed him milk from a bottle while Father cleaned the wound on his paw. Whenever thunder cracked, Kito pressed his forehead against my knee, not like a king of beasts, but like a frightened kitten whose kingdom had been stolen.","chinese":"那頭小獅子有一雙琥珀色的眼睛，鬍鬚上沾著泥，鼻子上方還有一道細細的白色疤痕。 我給牠取名為 Kito。 牠第一晚留在我們的廚房裡，因為那是整個單位最溫暖的房間。 爸爸替牠清理爪上的傷口時，我用奶瓶餵牠喝奶。 每當雷聲炸裂，Kito 都會把額頭貼在我的膝蓋上；牠不像萬獸之王，反倒像一隻王國被奪走的受驚小貓。"},{"label":"Paragraph 6","english":"For three weeks, our kitchen became his world. The fridge hummed; Kito learned that the sound of my whistle meant food. No words can do justice to the tenderness of being trusted by something that should have feared me. Still, Father kept reminding me, “Wildlife is not ours to keep. Love is not the same as ownership.”","chinese":"整整三個星期，我們的廚房成了牠的整個世界。 冰箱嗡嗡作響；Kito 學會了我的口哨聲代表有食物。 被一個原本理應害怕我的生命信任，那份溫柔，任何文字都無法充分呈現。 即使如此，爸爸仍不斷提醒我：「野生動物不屬於我們，不能被我們私自留下。愛與擁有並不相同。」"},{"label":"Paragraph 7","english":"When Kito was strong enough, he was taken to Green Ark Sanctuary. I cried so hard that Father let me keep his old feeding bowl. After that, life moved on. Exams replaced bedtime stories; Kito became a framed photograph on our shelf. Up until then, I had believed that farewell meant ending.","chinese":"當 Kito 變得足夠強壯時，牠被送到了 Green Ark Sanctuary。 我哭得太厲害，所以爸爸讓我留下牠那個舊餵食碗。 在那之後，生活繼續向前走。 考試取代了睡前故事；Kito 則成了我們架上一張鑲在相框裡的照片。 直到那一刻之前，我一直相信告別就代表結束。"},{"label":"Paragraph 8","english":"Then came Typhoon Helena.","chinese":"然後，颱風 Helena 來了。"},{"label":"Paragraph 9","english":"By seven in the evening, the city had vanished behind sheets of rain. At eight, Father received a call from Green Ark. A section of fencing had collapsed. Several animals had been found, but one adult male lion was missing.","chinese":"到了晚上七時，整座城市已經消失在一層層雨幕之後。 八時，爸爸接到了 Green Ark 打來的電話。 有一段圍欄倒塌了。 幾隻動物已經被找回，可是有一頭成年雄獅仍然失蹤。"},{"label":"Paragraph 10","english":"Kito.","chinese":"我給牠取名為 Kito。 每當雷聲炸裂，Kito 都會把額頭貼在我的膝蓋上；牠不像萬獸之王，反倒像一隻王國被奪走的受驚小貓。 冰箱嗡嗡作響；Kito 學會了我的口哨聲代表有食物。 當 Kito 變得足夠強壯時，牠被送到了 Green Ark Sanctuary。 考試取代了睡前故事；Kito 則成了我們架上一張鑲在相框裡的照片。 Kito 絕非一則新聞標題。 「Kito，」我低聲說。 Kito 跟了上來，原因並非牠已被馴服；更準確地說，是因為記憶就像飢餓一樣，幾乎能熬過任何事情。 我把 Kito 帶進廚房。 Kito 慢慢站起來，把兩隻前爪放在打開的冰箱旁邊那張廚房桌上，然後把牠金色的頭低向那隻碗。"},{"label":"Paragraph 11","english":"Father drove out immediately. I was told to stay home with Mum. I did—until a voice on the radio announced that armed officers were searching nearby. “If the animal charges,” the presenter said, “they may have no choice.”","chinese":"爸爸立刻開車出去。 我被叮囑要留在家裡陪媽媽。 我照做了——直到收音機裡有把聲音宣布，持槍人員正在附近搜索。 「如果那隻動物衝過來，」主持人說，「他們可能別無選擇。」 別無選擇。"},{"label":"Paragraph 12","english":"No choice. The phrase struck me like a slap. Kito was not a headline. He was not a monster. He was a frightened animal in a storm, chasing whatever memory still smelled like safety.","chinese":"別無選擇。 這個說法像一記耳光般打在我心上。 Kito 絕非一則新聞標題。 牠也絕非怪物。 牠只是一隻在暴風雨中受驚的動物，正在追尋任何仍帶有安全氣味的記憶。"},{"label":"Paragraph 13","english":"I pulled on Father’s raincoat and ran.","chinese":"我套上爸爸的雨衣，跑了出去。"},{"label":"Paragraph 14","english":"Outside, branches clawed at the road. I whistled between my teeth—the same three notes I had used when I was eleven.","chinese":"外面，樹枝像爪子一樣抓刮著路面。 我從齒縫間吹出口哨——那三個音符，正是我十一歲時用過的。"},{"label":"Paragraph 15","english":"Nothing.","chinese":"沒有回應。"},{"label":"Paragraph 16","english":"I whistled again.","chinese":"我再次吹響口哨。"},{"label":"Paragraph 17","english":"From somewhere beyond the playground came a sound: low, rough and familiar. Little by little, a shape emerged from the rain. First the mane, dark with water. Then the scar above the nose. Then the eyes, still amber, still searching.","chinese":"遊樂場之外的某處，傳來了一種聲音：低沉、粗啞，卻熟悉。 一點一點地，一個身影從雨中浮現。 先是那被雨水浸得發黑的鬃毛。 然後，是鼻子上方那道疤痕。 接著，是那雙眼睛，依舊琥珀色，依舊在尋找。"},{"label":"Paragraph 18","english":"“Kito,” I whispered.","chinese":"「Kito，」我低聲說。"},{"label":"Paragraph 19","english":"He limped towards me. A red warning light swept across the street as a police van turned the corner. Men shouted. A rifle was raised.","chinese":"牠一拐一拐地朝我走來。 一輛警車轉過街角時，紅色警示燈掃過整條街道。 有人大喊。 一支步槍被舉了起來。"},{"label":"Paragraph 20","english":"“Don’t shoot!” I screamed, stepping between them.","chinese":"「不要開槍！」我尖叫著，衝到他們之間。"},{"label":"Paragraph 21","english":"Had I known how foolish I looked, a schoolgirl facing a lion in a flooded street, I might have lost my courage. Instead, I whistled once more and backed towards our building. Kito followed, not because he was tame, but because memory, like hunger, can survive almost anything.","chinese":"假如我當時知道自己看起來有多愚蠢——一個女學生在水浸街道上面對一頭獅子——我也許早已失去勇氣。 相反，我再次吹響口哨，然後一步一步退向我們的大廈。 Kito 跟了上來，原因並非牠已被馴服；更準確地說，是因為記憶就像飢餓一樣，幾乎能熬過任何事情。"},{"label":"Paragraph 22","english":"Mum opened the door before I knocked. For once in her life, she did not ask questions. She simply moved aside.","chinese":"我還未敲門，媽媽已經把門打開。 她人生中罕有地沒有問任何問題。 她只是移到一旁。"},{"label":"Paragraph 23","english":"I led Kito into the kitchen. Water dripped from his mane onto the tiles. I opened the fridge with shaking hands, grabbed a tray of meat, and set the old feeding bowl on the table.","chinese":"我把 Kito 帶進廚房。 雨水從牠的鬃毛滴到地磚上。 我用顫抖的雙手打開冰箱，抓起一盤肉，然後把那個舊餵食碗放到桌上。"},{"label":"Paragraph 24","english":"Only then did I understand what Father meant. I had not brought wildlife home to possess it. I had brought it home to protect it until it could be free again.","chinese":"直到那一刻，我才明白爸爸的意思。 我把野生動物帶回家，並不是為了佔有牠。 我把牠帶回家，是為了保護牠，直到牠能再次自由。"},{"label":"Paragraph 25","english":"Behind me, Mum gasped. Kito rose slowly, placed his two front paws on the kitchen table beside the open fridge, and lowered his golden head towards the bowl.","chinese":"在我身後，媽媽倒抽了一口氣。 Kito 慢慢站起來，把兩隻前爪放在打開的冰箱旁邊那張廚房桌上，然後把牠金色的頭低向那隻碗。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"the first thing people ask","chinese":"人們首先會問的事"},{"english":"got into our kitchen","chinese":"走進我們的廚房"},{"english":"the better question","chinese":"更值得問的問題"},{"english":"came back","chinese":"回來"},{"english":"seven years before","chinese":"七年前"},{"english":"the photograph was taken","chinese":"相片被拍下"},{"english":"bring home","chinese":"帶回家"},{"english":"a cardboard box that breathed","chinese":"一個會呼吸的紙皮箱"},{"english":"black summer night","chinese":"漆黑的夏夜"},{"english":"the kind of night when","chinese":"那種……的夜晚"},{"english":"hammer the windows","chinese":"猛烈敲打窗戶"},{"english":"as if trying to get in","chinese":"彷彿想闖進來"},{"english":"wildlife veterinarian","chinese":"野生動物獸醫"},{"english":"be called to","chinese":"被召到"},{"english":"warehouse","chinese":"倉庫"},{"english":"near the harbour","chinese":"在海港附近"},{"english":"customs officers","chinese":"海關人員"},{"english":"a shipment of illegal animals","chinese":"一批非法動物貨運"},{"english":"be left behind","chinese":"被遺下"},{"english":"lion cub","chinese":"幼獅"},{"english":"no longer than","chinese":"長度不超過"},{"english":"shiver in the dark","chinese":"在黑暗中發抖"},{"english":"just until morning","chinese":"只到明早"},{"english":"let go","chinese":"放手"},{"english":"amber eyes","chinese":"琥珀色眼睛"},{"english":"mud in his whiskers","chinese":"鬍鬚上沾着泥"},{"english":"a thin white scar","chinese":"一道幼細的白色疤痕"},{"english":"above his nose","chinese":"在鼻子上方"},{"english":"name him","chinese":"為他改名"},{"english":"the warmest room in the flat","chinese":"單位裏最暖的房間"},{"english":"feed him milk from a bottle","chinese":"用奶樽餵牠飲奶"},{"english":"clean the wound","chinese":"清理傷口"},{"english":"on his paw","chinese":"在牠的爪上"},{"english":"whenever thunder cracked","chinese":"每當雷聲炸響"},{"english":"press his forehead against","chinese":"把額頭貼着"},{"english":"not like…, but like…","chinese":"不是像……而是像……"},{"english":"king of beasts","chinese":"百獸之王"},{"english":"frightened kitten","chinese":"受驚的小貓"},{"english":"whose kingdom had been stolen","chinese":"王國被奪走的"},{"english":"became his world","chinese":"成為牠的世界"},{"english":"the fridge hummed","chinese":"雪櫃發出嗡嗡聲"},{"english":"the sound of my whistle","chinese":"我的口哨聲"},{"english":"meant food","chinese":"代表有食物"},{"english":"do justice to","chinese":"充分表達"},{"english":"tenderness","chinese":"溫柔感；柔情"},{"english":"be trusted by","chinese":"被……信任"},{"english":"should have feared me","chinese":"本應害怕我"},{"english":"keep reminding someone","chinese":"不斷提醒某人"},{"english":"wildlife","chinese":"野生動物"},{"english":"not ours to keep","chinese":"不是屬於我們可以留下的"},{"english":"love is not the same as ownership","chinese":"愛不等於擁有"},{"english":"ownership","chinese":"擁有權；佔有"},{"english":"strong enough","chinese":"足夠強壯"},{"english":"be taken to","chinese":"被帶到"},{"english":"sanctuary","chinese":"動物保護中心"},{"english":"cry so hard that","chinese":"哭得非常厲害，以致"},{"english":"feeding bowl","chinese":"餵食碗"},{"english":"life moved on","chinese":"生活繼續"},{"english":"exams replaced bedtime stories","chinese":"考試取代睡前故事"},{"english":"framed photograph","chinese":"裱起來的相片"},{"english":"on our shelf","chinese":"在我們的架上"},{"english":"up until then","chinese":"直到那時為止"},{"english":"farewell meant ending","chinese":"告別等於結束"},{"english":"then came","chinese":"然後……來臨"},{"english":"typhoon","chinese":"颱風"},{"english":"by seven in the evening","chinese":"到晚上七點時"},{"english":"vanish behind","chinese":"消失在……後面"},{"english":"sheets of rain","chinese":"傾盆大雨；雨幕"},{"english":"receive a call from","chinese":"接到……的電話"},{"english":"a section of fencing","chinese":"一段圍欄"},{"english":"fencing","chinese":"圍欄"},{"english":"collapse","chinese":"倒塌"},{"english":"adult male lion","chinese":"成年雄獅"},{"english":"go missing","chinese":"失蹤"},{"english":"drive out immediately","chinese":"立即開車出去"},{"english":"be told to stay home","chinese":"被吩咐留在家中"},{"english":"armed officers","chinese":"武裝人員"},{"english":"search nearby","chinese":"在附近搜索"},{"english":"if the animal charges","chinese":"如果動物衝過來"},{"english":"have no choice","chinese":"別無選擇"},{"english":"strike me like a slap","chinese":"像一巴掌打中我"},{"english":"headline","chinese":"新聞標題"},{"english":"monster","chinese":"怪物"},{"english":"frightened animal","chinese":"受驚的動物"},{"english":"chasing whatever memory","chinese":"追尋任何仍然存在的記憶"},{"english":"smelled like safety","chinese":"聞起來像安全"},{"english":"pull on","chinese":"匆匆穿上"},{"english":"raincoat","chinese":"雨衣"},{"english":"branches clawed at","chinese":"樹枝像爪子般抓着"},{"english":"whistle between my teeth","chinese":"用牙縫吹口哨"},{"english":"the same three notes","chinese":"同樣三個音"},{"english":"from somewhere beyond","chinese":"從……外某處"},{"english":"playground","chinese":"遊樂場"},{"english":"low, rough and familiar","chinese":"低沉、沙啞而熟悉"},{"english":"little by little","chinese":"一點一點地；漸漸地"},{"english":"emerge from","chinese":"從……中出現"},{"english":"mane","chinese":"鬃毛"},{"english":"dark with water","chinese":"因沾水而變深色"},{"english":"still searching","chinese":"仍在尋找"},{"english":"limp towards","chinese":"一拐一拐地走向"},{"english":"warning light","chinese":"警示燈"},{"english":"sweep across","chinese":"掃過"},{"english":"police van","chinese":"警車"},{"english":"turn the corner","chinese":"轉過街角"},{"english":"a rifle was raised","chinese":"步槍被舉起"},{"english":"step between","chinese":"站到……之間"},{"english":"had I known","chinese":"如果我當時知道"},{"english":"face a lion","chinese":"面對一隻獅子"},{"english":"flooded street","chinese":"水浸街道"},{"english":"lose my courage","chinese":"失去勇氣"},{"english":"once more","chinese":"再一次"},{"english":"back towards","chinese":"向……後退"},{"english":"not because…, but because…","chinese":"不是因為……而是因為……"},{"english":"tame","chinese":"馴服的"},{"english":"memory, like hunger","chinese":"記憶像飢餓一樣"},{"english":"survive almost anything","chinese":"幾乎任何事都能熬過"},{"english":"for once in her life","chinese":"她人生中難得一次"},{"english":"move aside","chinese":"讓開"},{"english":"lead someone into","chinese":"帶領某人進入"},{"english":"drip from","chinese":"從……滴下"},{"english":"onto the tiles","chinese":"滴到瓷磚上"},{"english":"with shaking hands","chinese":"用發抖的手"},{"english":"tray of meat","chinese":"一盤肉"},{"english":"set the bowl on","chinese":"把碗放在……上"},{"english":"only then did I understand","chinese":"直到那時我才明白"},{"english":"bring wildlife home","chinese":"把野生動物帶回家"},{"english":"possess","chinese":"佔有"},{"english":"protect it","chinese":"保護它"},{"english":"until it could be free again","chinese":"直到它能再次自由"},{"english":"gasp","chinese":"倒抽一口氣"},{"english":"rise slowly","chinese":"慢慢站起來"},{"english":"front paws","chinese":"前爪"},{"english":"beside the open fridge","chinese":"在打開的雪櫃旁"},{"english":"lower his golden head","chinese":"低下金色的頭"},{"english":"towards the bowl","chinese":"向着那隻碗"}]},"dse-writing-2017-part-b-q4":{"exerciseId":"dse-writing-2017-part-b-q4","essayKey":"","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=dse-writing-2017-part-b-q4","flashDeckId":"dse/writing/part-b/2017/Q4","paragraphs":[{"label":"Paragraph 1","english":"A Marriage Needs More Than Moonlight","chinese":"婚姻需要的不只是月光"},{"label":"Paragraph 2","english":"From Romeo’s famous declaration—“Did my heart love till now?”— romantic love is often presented in drama as sudden, dazzling and almost sacred. In our drama lessons, this has made students consider whether passionate attraction should be treated as the foundation of marriage so that a couple can secure lasting happiness. As far as I am concerned, romantic love is desirable, but it is not strictly necessary for a happy marriage. A happy marriage depends less on thunderbolt emotion than on trust, character, communication and the willingness to choose one another.","chinese":"從羅密歐那句著名宣言——「我的心此前曾真正愛過嗎？」——可見，浪漫愛情在戲劇中常常被呈現為突如其來、耀眼奪目，甚至近乎神聖。 在我們的戲劇課中，這使學生開始思考，激情吸引是否應被視為婚姻的基礎，好讓一對伴侶能穩穩守住長久的幸福。 就我而言，浪漫愛情固然可取，但對幸福婚姻來說，它並非嚴格必要。 幸福婚姻較少依靠一見鍾情般的強烈情感，更多依靠信任、品格、溝通，以及願意彼此選擇的心。"},{"label":"Paragraph 3","english":"First of all, romantic love is too unstable to be the only necessary condition for marital happiness. Romance often magnifies the beloved: a smile becomes a promise, a glance becomes destiny, and a disagreement is easily explained away. This enchantment can draw two people closer and give them the courage to begin. However, the very intensity that makes romance thrilling can also make judgement weaker. Take Romeo and Juliet, for example: their love is sincere, but it moves so quickly that neither family conflict nor practical consequence is properly considered. Had their passion been given time to mature into patience and wisdom, their story might have been less poetic but far less tragic. In real life, too, a couple may fall deeply in love, only to discover after marriage that they disagree about money, children or elderly parents. By contrast, two respectful companions may slowly build confidence in each other. Little by little, shared habits become trust, and trust becomes emotional safety. Thus, romantic love may open the door, but reliability keeps the home warm.","chinese":"首先，浪漫愛情太不穩定，難以成為婚姻幸福的唯一必要條件。 浪漫情感往往會放大所愛之人：一個微笑變成承諾，一個眼神變成命運，一場分歧也很容易被輕輕帶過。 這種迷醉能拉近兩個人的距離，也能給予他們開始一段關係的勇氣。 然而，正是那份使浪漫令人心動的強烈程度，也可能削弱人的判斷力。 以羅密歐與茱麗葉為例：他們的愛是真誠的，但發展得如此迅速，以致家族衝突和實際後果都沒有得到適當考慮。 假如他們的激情曾被給予時間，得以成熟為耐性與智慧，他們的故事或許會少一點詩意，卻遠遠少一點悲劇。 在現實生活中，一對伴侶同樣可能深深相愛，婚後才發現彼此在金錢、子女或年邁父母方面意見不合。 相比之下，兩位彼此尊重的伴侶，可能會慢慢建立對對方的信心。 一點一滴地，共同習慣會變成信任，而信任會變成情感上的安全感。 因此，浪漫愛情也許能打開一扇門，但可靠才能讓這個家保持溫暖。"},{"label":"Paragraph 4","english":"Secondly, marriage is not just about feeling loved; it is about living responsibly with another person. The trouble with simple slogans such as “love conquers all” is that they hide the ordinary burdens of married life. After the wedding, there are bills to discuss, careers to balance, illnesses to face, relatives to respect and, perhaps, children to raise. In such situations, what matters is not whether a husband still writes beautiful messages every night, but whether he listens when his wife is exhausted. For instance, a couple caring for a sick child may have little time for romantic dinners. Nevertheless, if they divide duties fairly, speak gently under pressure and protect each other from despair, their marriage can be profoundly happy. It may not look like a stage romance. Yet there is more to happiness than excitement: a peaceful home where both partners feel seen, forgiven and trusted can be no less precious than passionate courtship.","chinese":"第二，婚姻不只是感到被愛；它也關乎與另一個人負責任地生活。 「愛能戰勝一切」這類簡單口號的問題在於，它們掩蓋了婚姻生活中的日常負擔。 婚禮之後，有帳單要商量，有事業要平衡，有疾病要面對，有親友要尊重，也許還有孩子要撫養。 在這些情況下，關鍵並非丈夫是否仍然每晚寫下美麗的訊息，重點在於妻子疲憊時，他是否願意聆聽。 例如，一對照顧患病孩子的夫婦，也許沒有多少時間享受浪漫晚餐。 儘管如此，如果他們能公平分擔責任，在壓力下溫柔說話，並保護彼此免於陷入絕望，他們的婚姻仍可以非常幸福。 它也許看起來不像舞台劇式的浪漫。 然而，幸福之中有比興奮更深的東西：一個讓雙方都感到被看見、被原諒、被信任的安穩之家，可以與激情追求同樣珍貴，甚至毫不遜色。"},{"label":"Paragraph 5","english":"Admittedly, some people argue that without romantic love, marriage becomes little more than a contract. I take this point. A marriage completely devoid of warmth, tenderness or attraction may leave both partners lonely, and few people would choose a life in which they are merely efficient housemates. Romance can make sacrifice feel lighter and remind a couple that they are chosen companions. That said, this argument proves only that affection matters, not that initial romantic passion is necessary. Romantic love works up to a point, but beyond that point it must either deepen or fade. Many marriages that begin with intense passion collapse when selfishness, pride or poor communication take over. Meanwhile, some friendship-based marriages become happy because the couple learn to admire, protect and cherish each other. In other words, the question is not whether love should exist in marriage, but what kind of love can survive time. Only when romance grows into respect can it truly serve a marriage.","chinese":"誠然，有些人主張，如果沒有浪漫愛情，婚姻就會變得幾乎只剩下一紙契約 我明白這個觀點。 一段完全缺乏溫暖、溫柔或吸引力的婚姻，可能會令雙方都感到孤單；也很少有人會選擇一種只是高效室友的生活。 浪漫可以讓犧牲感覺輕一點，也能提醒一對伴侶，他們是彼此選擇的同行者 話雖如此，這個論點只能證明情感很重要，並不能證明最初的浪漫激情必不可少。 浪漫愛情在某個程度內有效，但超過那個程度之後，它要麼深化，要麼消退 許多以強烈激情開始的婚姻，一旦自私、驕傲或溝通不良佔上風，便會走向崩潰。 與此同時，有些以友誼為基礎的婚姻會變得幸福，因為伴侶學會欣賞、保護並珍惜彼此。 換句話說，問題的核心並非愛是否應存在於婚姻之中，重點在於哪一種愛能經得起時間考驗。 只有當浪漫成長為尊重時，它才真正能成為婚姻的助力。"},{"label":"Paragraph 6","english":"All things considered, I would answer the question with a qualified no. Romantic love can enrich a marriage, but it is not the indispensable foundation of a happy one. Trust, commitment, maturity and kindness are far more necessary because they remain when beauty fades, routine arrives and difficulties test the couple’s promises. When Romeo believes he has discovered “true beauty,” we should admire the spark—but not mistake it for the whole fire. For young people thinking about marriage, the wiser action is clear: enjoy romance, but examine character; treasure emotion, but build trust; seek not merely someone who can make the heart race, but someone with whom the heart can rest.","chinese":"綜合而言，我會以一個有保留的「不」來回答這個問題。 浪漫愛情能夠豐富婚姻，但它並非幸福婚姻不可取代的基礎。 信任、承諾、成熟與善良更加必要，因為當美貌褪去、平淡日常來臨、困難考驗伴侶的承諾時，它們仍會留下。 當羅密歐相信自己發現了「真正的美」時，我們應該欣賞那一點火花——但不應把它誤認為整團火焰。 對正在思考婚姻的年輕人而言，更明智的行動很清楚：享受浪漫，但也要審視品格；珍惜情感，但也要建立信任；尋找的不應只是一個能令心跳加速的人，更應是一個能讓心安頓下來的人。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"more than moonlight","chinese":"不只是月光；不只是浪漫"},{"english":"famous declaration","chinese":"著名宣言"},{"english":"romantic love","chinese":"浪漫愛情"},{"english":"be presented in drama as","chinese":"在戲劇中被呈現為"},{"english":"sudden, dazzling and almost sacred","chinese":"突然、耀眼而近乎神聖"},{"english":"drama lessons","chinese":"戲劇課"},{"english":"consider whether","chinese":"思考是否"},{"english":"passionate attraction","chinese":"熱烈的吸引"},{"english":"be treated as","chinese":"被視為"},{"english":"the foundation of marriage","chinese":"婚姻的基礎"},{"english":"secure lasting happiness","chinese":"確保持久幸福"},{"english":"as far as I am concerned","chinese":"就我而言"},{"english":"be desirable","chinese":"值得擁有；令人嚮往"},{"english":"strictly necessary for","chinese":"對……來說絕對必要"},{"english":"depend less on...than on...","chinese":"與其依靠……不如依靠……"},{"english":"thunderbolt emotion","chinese":"霹靂般的強烈情感"},{"english":"trust, character and communication","chinese":"信任、品格和溝通"},{"english":"the willingness to","chinese":"願意去……"},{"english":"choose one another","chinese":"彼此選擇；互相堅守"},{"english":"first of all","chinese":"首先"},{"english":"too unstable to","chinese":"太不穩定以致不能"},{"english":"the only necessary condition","chinese":"唯一必要條件"},{"english":"marital happiness","chinese":"婚姻幸福"},{"english":"magnify the beloved","chinese":"美化所愛的人"},{"english":"a smile becomes a promise","chinese":"一個微笑變成承諾"},{"english":"a glance becomes destiny","chinese":"一眼變成命運"},{"english":"be explained away","chinese":"被輕易合理化"},{"english":"enchantment","chinese":"迷戀；着迷"},{"english":"draw two people closer","chinese":"拉近兩人的距離"},{"english":"give someone the courage to begin","chinese":"給某人開始的勇氣"},{"english":"the very intensity that","chinese":"正是那種……的強烈程度"},{"english":"make romance thrilling","chinese":"令浪漫令人心跳"},{"english":"make judgement weaker","chinese":"令判斷力變弱"},{"english":"take Romeo and Juliet, for example","chinese":"以羅密歐與茱麗葉為例"},{"english":"their love is sincere","chinese":"他們的愛是真誠的"},{"english":"move so quickly","chinese":"發展得太快"},{"english":"family conflict","chinese":"家族衝突"},{"english":"practical consequence","chinese":"實際後果"},{"english":"properly considered","chinese":"被妥善考慮"},{"english":"be given time to","chinese":"獲給予時間去"},{"english":"mature into","chinese":"成熟為；發展成"},{"english":"patience and wisdom","chinese":"耐性和智慧"},{"english":"less poetic but far less tragic","chinese":"較不詩意但遠不那麼悲劇"},{"english":"in real life","chinese":"在現實生活中"},{"english":"fall deeply in love","chinese":"深深相愛"},{"english":"only to discover","chinese":"結果卻發現"},{"english":"disagree about","chinese":"在……方面意見不合"},{"english":"elderly parents","chinese":"年老父母"},{"english":"by contrast","chinese":"相比之下"},{"english":"respectful companions","chinese":"互相尊重的伴侶"},{"english":"build confidence in each other","chinese":"建立對彼此的信心"},{"english":"little by little","chinese":"一點一滴地"},{"english":"shared habits","chinese":"共同習慣"},{"english":"emotional safety","chinese":"情感上的安全感"},{"english":"open the door","chinese":"打開大門；帶來開始"},{"english":"reliability keeps the home warm","chinese":"可靠才令家庭溫暖"},{"english":"secondly","chinese":"其次"},{"english":"not just about...but about...","chinese":"不只是關於……而是關於……"},{"english":"feeling loved","chinese":"感到被愛"},{"english":"live responsibly with","chinese":"負責任地與……生活"},{"english":"the trouble with","chinese":"……的問題在於"},{"english":"simple slogans","chinese":"簡單口號"},{"english":"love conquers all","chinese":"愛能征服一切"},{"english":"hide the ordinary burdens of","chinese":"掩蓋……的日常負擔"},{"english":"married life","chinese":"婚姻生活"},{"english":"after the wedding","chinese":"婚禮之後"},{"english":"bills to discuss","chinese":"要商量的賬單"},{"english":"careers to balance","chinese":"要平衡的事業"},{"english":"illnesses to face","chinese":"要面對的疾病"},{"english":"relatives to respect","chinese":"要尊重的親戚"},{"english":"children to raise","chinese":"要撫養的孩子"},{"english":"in such situations","chinese":"在這些情況下"},{"english":"what matters is not whether...but whether...","chinese":"重要的不是……而是……"},{"english":"write beautiful messages","chinese":"寫動人的訊息"},{"english":"be exhausted","chinese":"筋疲力盡"},{"english":"care for a sick child","chinese":"照顧生病的孩子"},{"english":"have little time for","chinese":"很少有時間做……"},{"english":"romantic dinners","chinese":"浪漫晚餐"},{"english":"nevertheless","chinese":"然而"},{"english":"divide duties fairly","chinese":"公平分擔責任"},{"english":"speak gently under pressure","chinese":"在壓力下溫柔說話"},{"english":"protect each other from despair","chinese":"保護彼此免於絕望"},{"english":"profoundly happy","chinese":"深切幸福"},{"english":"stage romance","chinese":"舞台上的浪漫愛情"},{"english":"there is more to happiness than","chinese":"幸福不止是……"},{"english":"feel seen","chinese":"感到被看見；被理解"},{"english":"feel forgiven","chinese":"感到被原諒"},{"english":"feel trusted","chinese":"感到被信任"},{"english":"no less precious than","chinese":"不比……遜色；同樣珍貴"},{"english":"passionate courtship","chinese":"熱烈的追求期"},{"english":"admittedly","chinese":"無可否認"},{"english":"argue that","chinese":"主張；認為"},{"english":"without romantic love","chinese":"沒有浪漫愛情"},{"english":"little more than","chinese":"不過是；只不過是"},{"english":"a contract","chinese":"合約"},{"english":"take this point","chinese":"明白這一點；接受這一點"},{"english":"completely devoid of","chinese":"完全沒有"},{"english":"warmth, tenderness or attraction","chinese":"溫暖、溫柔和吸引力"},{"english":"leave both partners lonely","chinese":"令雙方都感到孤單"},{"english":"merely efficient housemates","chinese":"只是有效率的同屋人"},{"english":"make sacrifice feel lighter","chinese":"令犧牲感覺輕鬆一點"},{"english":"remind a couple that","chinese":"提醒一對夫婦"},{"english":"chosen companions","chinese":"彼此選擇的伴侶"},{"english":"that said","chinese":"話雖如此"},{"english":"prove only that","chinese":"只證明"},{"english":"affection matters","chinese":"感情很重要"},{"english":"initial romantic passion","chinese":"最初的浪漫激情"},{"english":"work up to a point","chinese":"在某程度上有效"},{"english":"beyond that point","chinese":"超過那個程度之後"},{"english":"deepen or fade","chinese":"加深或淡去"},{"english":"intense passion","chinese":"強烈激情"},{"english":"collapse when","chinese":"在……時崩潰"},{"english":"selfishness, pride and poor communication","chinese":"自私、驕傲和溝通不良"},{"english":"take over","chinese":"佔上風；主導"},{"english":"meanwhile","chinese":"與此同時"},{"english":"friendship-based marriages","chinese":"以友誼為基礎的婚姻"},{"english":"admire, protect and cherish each other","chinese":"欣賞、保護和珍惜彼此"},{"english":"in other words","chinese":"換句話說"},{"english":"survive time","chinese":"經得起時間考驗"},{"english":"grow into respect","chinese":"發展成尊重"},{"english":"truly serve a marriage","chinese":"真正有助於婚姻"},{"english":"all things considered","chinese":"總括而言"},{"english":"a qualified no","chinese":"有保留的否定答案"},{"english":"enrich a marriage","chinese":"豐富一段婚姻"},{"english":"indispensable foundation","chinese":"不可或缺的基礎"},{"english":"trust, commitment, maturity and kindness","chinese":"信任、承諾、成熟和善良"},{"english":"far more necessary","chinese":"遠比……更必要"},{"english":"beauty fades","chinese":"美貌褪去"},{"english":"routine arrives","chinese":"日常生活來臨"},{"english":"difficulties test the couple's promises","chinese":"困難考驗夫妻的承諾"},{"english":"discover true beauty","chinese":"發現真正的美"},{"english":"admire the spark","chinese":"欣賞那一點火花"},{"english":"mistake it for the whole fire","chinese":"誤把它當成整團火"},{"english":"think about marriage","chinese":"思考婚姻"},{"english":"the wiser action is clear","chinese":"更明智的做法很清楚"},{"english":"enjoy romance","chinese":"享受浪漫"},{"english":"examine character","chinese":"審視品格"},{"english":"treasure emotion","chinese":"珍惜情感"},{"english":"build trust","chinese":"建立信任"},{"english":"seek not merely someone who","chinese":"不只尋找能夠……的人"},{"english":"make the heart race","chinese":"令心跳加速"},{"english":"with whom the heart can rest","chinese":"能讓心安定下來的人"}]},"dse-writing-2017-part-b-q5":{"exerciseId":"dse-writing-2017-part-b-q5","essayKey":"","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=dse-writing-2017-part-b-q5","flashDeckId":"dse/writing/part-b/2017/Q5","paragraphs":[{"label":"Paragraph 1","english":"Protecting Hong Kong’s Living Heritage: Egg Tarts and Mahjong","chinese":"守護香港的活態文化遺產：蛋撻與麻將"},{"label":"Paragraph 2","english":"Dear Editor,","chinese":"編輯先生／女士："},{"label":"Paragraph 3","english":"In recent years, Hong Kong has become increasingly aware that culture does not exist only in grand monuments, old temples or museum cabinets. It also lives in the smell of a warm bakery at four o’clock, the clatter of mahjong tiles on a family table, and the small rituals through which ordinary people recognise home. Therefore, I strongly support the Government’s decision to include traditional egg tarts and mahjong on the list of intangible cultural heritage items. Far from being trivial, these two features reveal Hong Kong’s mixed history, social warmth and everyday creativity. They are worth protecting not because they are rare, but because they are so deeply woven into our common life that we may take them for granted until they disappear.","chinese":"近年來，香港越來越意識到，文化並不只存在於宏偉的古蹟、古老的廟宇或博物館的展櫃之中。 它也存在於下午四時溫暖麵包店的香氣裡、家庭桌上麻將牌碰撞的聲音裡，以及普通人從中認出「家」的那些小小日常儀式之中。 因此，我強烈支持政府把傳統蛋撻和麻將列入非物質文化遺產項目名單的決定 這兩項特色絕非微不足道；它們揭示了香港混合交融的歷史、人情味，以及日常生活中的創意。 它們值得保護，原因並非它們罕見；重點在於它們已如此深深編織進我們共同的生活之中，以至於我們可能一直視之為理所當然，直到它們消失才懂得珍惜。"},{"label":"Paragraph 4","english":"First, traditional egg tarts deserve protection because they are more than just a sweet snack - they tell the story of Hong Kong as a place where Chinese and Western influences met, adapted and became something unmistakably local. A buttery crust, a silky custard filling and a paper bag from a neighbourhood bakery may seem simple at first glance; on closer inspection, however, they represent generations of craftsmanship. From old-style bakeries in Sham Shui Po to cha chaan tengs in Wan Chai, egg tarts have accompanied office workers, schoolchildren, taxi drivers and elderly residents alike. You do not just buy an egg tart to fill your stomach; you buy a small piece of shared memory. The problem is that this craft is now under pressure. Rising rents, standardised chain-store production and changing eating habits may gradually push traditional recipes and baking skills aside. To protect egg tarts, the Government should record oral histories from veteran bakers, support apprenticeship schemes, and create a recognised “traditional Hong Kong egg tart” label for shops that preserve authentic methods. Schools could also organise bakery visits so that students understand how food can carry history. That way, protection would not be reduced to a slogan; it would become a living process of transmission.","chinese":"首先，傳統蛋撻值得保護，因為它們遠遠不只是一款甜點——它們訴說了香港這個地方的故事：中西影響在此相遇、調整，最後成為一種 unmistakably local、帶有鮮明本地特色的東西。 牛油香濃的撻皮、幼滑的蛋漿餡，以及街坊麵包店的一個紙袋，乍看之下也許很簡單；然而，仔細觀察便會發現，它們承載的是幾代人的手藝。 從深水埗的舊式麵包店，到灣仔的茶餐廳，蛋撻一直陪伴著上班族、學生、的士司機和年長居民。 你買一個蛋撻，不只是為了填飽肚子；你買下的，也是一小片共同記憶。 問題在於，這門手藝如今正承受壓力。 租金上升、連鎖店標準化生產，以及飲食習慣改變，都可能逐漸把傳統食譜和烘焙技術推到一旁。 為了保護蛋撻，政府應該記錄資深烘焙師傅的口述歷史、支持學徒培訓計劃，並為保留正宗製作方法的店舖設立一個受認可的「傳統香港蛋撻」標籤。 學校也可以安排學生參觀麵包店，好讓他們明白食物如何承載歷史。 那樣一來，保護工作便不會淪為一句口號；它會成為一個活生生的傳承過程"},{"label":"Paragraph 5","english":"Mahjong, by the same token, is worth preserving because it is one of Hong Kong’s most recognisable social languages. For many families, especially during Lunar New Year, mahjong is not merely a game of winning and losing. It is a way for grandparents, parents and young people to sit at the same table, exchange jokes, practise calculation and read one another’s expressions. The sound of tiles being shuffled is almost as familiar to many Hongkongers as the ding-ding of the tram. What makes mahjong culturally valuable is not only its rules, but also the atmosphere around it: the Cantonese expressions, the family teasing, the patience required, and the unspoken understanding between players. Without such activities, intergenerational bonds may become weaker, especially in a city where small flats, long working hours and digital entertainment already leave families with fewer chances to gather. To protect mahjong responsibly, community centres and schools could introduce non-gambling mahjong workshops focusing on strategy, arithmetic and cultural history. Museums could display traditional tile sets and interview tile-makers, while youth groups could record grandparents explaining local playing styles. In this way, mahjong can be presented not as a vice, but as a form of social heritage.","chinese":"同樣道理，麻將也值得保存，因為它是香港最容易辨認的社交語言之一。 對許多家庭而言，尤其是在農曆新年期間，麻將並非純粹是一場輸贏遊戲。 它是一種讓祖父母、父母和年輕人坐在同一張桌旁、互相說笑、練習計算，並觀察彼此表情的方式。 對許多香港人來說，洗牌時麻將牌互相碰撞的聲音，幾乎就像電車的「叮叮」 聲一樣熟悉。 令麻將具有文化價值的，不單是它的規則，也包括它周圍形成的氛圍：廣東話用語、家人之間的玩笑、遊戲所需要的耐性，以及玩家之間不言而喻的默契 沒有這類活動，代際之間的連結可能會變得更薄弱；在香港這樣一個居住空間狹小、工時漫長、數碼娛樂又早已令家庭聚首機會減少的城市裡，情況尤其如此。 為了負責任地保護麻將，社區中心和學校可以開設不涉及賭博的麻將工作坊，集中介紹策略、算術和文化歷史。 博物館可以展出傳統麻將牌套裝，並訪問製牌師傅；與此同時，青年團體也可以錄下祖父母講解本地打法的片段。 透過這種方式，麻將便能以社會文化遺產的形式呈現，而不會只被視作一種惡習。"},{"label":"Paragraph 6","english":"Admittedly, some people may argue that egg tarts are too ordinary and mahjong is too closely associated with gambling to deserve official protection. That view is understandable, but it misses the point. Intangible cultural heritage is not about declaring something perfect; it is about recognising practices that have shaped a community’s identity. Protecting egg tarts does not mean encouraging unhealthy eating, just as protecting mahjong does not mean promoting gambling. Rather, it means preserving knowledge, stories and social meaning while guiding the public towards responsible appreciation. If anything, official recognition gives Hong Kong a chance to explain these traditions more carefully instead of leaving them to fade, commercialise or be misunderstood.","chinese":"誠然，有些人可能會認為，蛋撻太普通，而麻將又與賭博的關聯太密切，因此不值得獲得官方保護。 這種看法可以理解，卻沒有抓住重點。 非物質文化遺產的重點並非把某樣東西宣稱為完美；它的核心在於承認那些曾經塑造一個社群身份的生活實踐。 保護蛋撻並不等於鼓勵不健康飲食；同樣地，保護麻將也不等於推廣賭博。 更準確地說，這意味著在保存知識、故事和社會意義的同時，引導公眾以負責任的態度欣賞這些傳統。 真要說的話，官方認可反而給予香港一個機會，讓我們能夠更仔細地解釋這些傳統，而不至於任由它們淡出、被過度商業化，或遭到誤解。"},{"label":"Paragraph 7","english":"All things considered, the Government has made a wise choice. Traditional egg tarts and mahjong are humble, familiar and deeply human; precisely for that reason, they reveal Hong Kong more honestly than many polished tourist attractions do. The next step is clear - the Government, schools, museums, businesses and citizens should work together to document, teach and practise these traditions. Heritage should not be locked behind glass. It should be tasted, heard, shared and passed on.","chinese":"綜合而言，政府作出了一個明智的選擇。 傳統蛋撻和麻將樸素、熟悉，而且充滿人情味；正正因為如此，它們比許多包裝精美的旅遊景點更真實地呈現香港。 下一步十分清晰——政府、學校、博物館、商界和市民應該共同合作，記錄、教導並實踐這些傳統。 文化遺產不應被鎖在玻璃之後。 它應該被品嚐、被聽見、被分享，並被一代一代傳承下去。"},{"label":"Paragraph 8","english":"Yours faithfully,","chinese":"此致"},{"label":"Paragraph 9","english":"Chris Wong","chinese":"Chris Wong"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"living heritage","chinese":"活態文化遺產"},{"english":"egg tarts","chinese":"蛋撻"},{"english":"mahjong","chinese":"麻雀"},{"english":"in recent years","chinese":"近年"},{"english":"increasingly aware that","chinese":"越來越意識到"},{"english":"exist only in","chinese":"只存在於"},{"english":"grand monuments","chinese":"宏偉紀念建築"},{"english":"old temples","chinese":"古老廟宇"},{"english":"museum cabinets","chinese":"博物館展櫃"},{"english":"lives in","chinese":"存在於"},{"english":"a warm bakery","chinese":"溫暖的麵包店"},{"english":"the clatter of mahjong tiles","chinese":"麻雀牌碰撞聲"},{"english":"mahjong tiles","chinese":"麻雀牌"},{"english":"family table","chinese":"家庭餐桌；家中桌子"},{"english":"small rituals","chinese":"小儀式；日常習慣"},{"english":"through which","chinese":"透過……"},{"english":"ordinary people","chinese":"普通人"},{"english":"recognise home","chinese":"認出家的感覺"},{"english":"strongly support","chinese":"強烈支持"},{"english":"the Government's decision","chinese":"政府的決定"},{"english":"include something on the list","chinese":"把……列入名單"},{"english":"traditional egg tarts","chinese":"傳統蛋撻"},{"english":"the list of","chinese":"……名單"},{"english":"intangible cultural heritage","chinese":"非物質文化遺產"},{"english":"cultural heritage items","chinese":"文化遺產項目"},{"english":"far from being trivial","chinese":"絕非微不足道"},{"english":"reveal","chinese":"展現；反映"},{"english":"mixed history","chinese":"融合中西的歷史"},{"english":"social warmth","chinese":"社會人情味"},{"english":"everyday creativity","chinese":"日常創意"},{"english":"worth protecting","chinese":"值得保護"},{"english":"not because…, but because…","chinese":"不是因為……而是因為……"},{"english":"deeply woven into","chinese":"深深融入"},{"english":"common life","chinese":"共同生活"},{"english":"take something for granted","chinese":"視……為理所當然"},{"english":"until they disappear","chinese":"直到它們消失"},{"english":"deserve protection","chinese":"值得受到保護"},{"english":"more than just","chinese":"不只是"},{"english":"a sweet snack","chinese":"甜點；甜食"},{"english":"tell the story of","chinese":"講述……的故事"},{"english":"a place where","chinese":"一個……的地方"},{"english":"Chinese and Western influences","chinese":"中西影響"},{"english":"met, adapted and became","chinese":"相遇、適應並變成"},{"english":"unmistakably local","chinese":"明顯具本地特色"},{"english":"buttery crust","chinese":"牛油酥皮"},{"english":"silky custard filling","chinese":"幼滑蛋漿餡"},{"english":"paper bag","chinese":"紙袋"},{"english":"neighbourhood bakery","chinese":"街坊麵包店"},{"english":"may seem simple","chinese":"可能看似簡單"},{"english":"at first glance","chinese":"乍看之下"},{"english":"on closer inspection","chinese":"仔細看時"},{"english":"represent generations of","chinese":"代表幾代人的……"},{"english":"craftsmanship","chinese":"手藝；工藝"},{"english":"old-style bakeries","chinese":"舊式麵包店"},{"english":"cha chaan tengs","chinese":"茶餐廳"},{"english":"have accompanied","chinese":"陪伴着"},{"english":"office workers","chinese":"上班族"},{"english":"schoolchildren","chinese":"學童"},{"english":"taxi drivers","chinese":"的士司機"},{"english":"elderly residents","chinese":"年長居民"},{"english":"alike","chinese":"同樣地"},{"english":"fill your stomach","chinese":"填飽肚子"},{"english":"a small piece of shared memory","chinese":"一小片共同回憶"},{"english":"shared memory","chinese":"共同回憶"},{"english":"under pressure","chinese":"承受壓力"},{"english":"rising rents","chinese":"租金上升"},{"english":"standardised chain-store production","chinese":"標準化連鎖店生產"},{"english":"changing eating habits","chinese":"飲食習慣改變"},{"english":"gradually push aside","chinese":"逐漸排擠"},{"english":"traditional recipes","chinese":"傳統食譜"},{"english":"baking skills","chinese":"烘焙技術"},{"english":"record oral histories","chinese":"記錄口述歷史"},{"english":"oral histories","chinese":"口述歷史"},{"english":"veteran bakers","chinese":"資深麵包師傅"},{"english":"support apprenticeship schemes","chinese":"支持學徒計劃"},{"english":"apprenticeship schemes","chinese":"學徒計劃"},{"english":"create a recognised label","chinese":"設立認可標籤"},{"english":"preserve authentic methods","chinese":"保留正宗做法"},{"english":"authentic methods","chinese":"正宗做法"},{"english":"organise bakery visits","chinese":"組織麵包店參觀"},{"english":"understand how food can carry history","chinese":"明白食物如何承載歷史"},{"english":"carry history","chinese":"承載歷史"},{"english":"that way","chinese":"這樣"},{"english":"be reduced to a slogan","chinese":"淪為口號"},{"english":"a living process of transmission","chinese":"活生生的傳承過程"},{"english":"transmission","chinese":"傳承"},{"english":"by the same token","chinese":"同樣道理"},{"english":"worth preserving","chinese":"值得保存"},{"english":"recognisable social languages","chinese":"最具辨識度的社交語言"},{"english":"during Lunar New Year","chinese":"農曆新年期間"},{"english":"not merely","chinese":"不只是"},{"english":"winning and losing","chinese":"勝負"},{"english":"sit at the same table","chinese":"坐在同一張桌旁"},{"english":"exchange jokes","chinese":"開玩笑；互相說笑"},{"english":"practise calculation","chinese":"練習計算"},{"english":"read one another's expressions","chinese":"讀懂彼此表情"},{"english":"tiles being shuffled","chinese":"麻雀牌被洗動"},{"english":"almost as familiar as","chinese":"幾乎像……一樣熟悉"},{"english":"Hongkongers","chinese":"香港人"},{"english":"the ding-ding of the tram","chinese":"電車叮叮聲"},{"english":"culturally valuable","chinese":"具有文化價值"},{"english":"not only…, but also…","chinese":"不只是……而且是……"},{"english":"the atmosphere around it","chinese":"圍繞它的氣氛"},{"english":"Cantonese expressions","chinese":"廣東話用語"},{"english":"family teasing","chinese":"家人之間的玩笑取笑"},{"english":"patience required","chinese":"所需的耐性"},{"english":"unspoken understanding","chinese":"心照不宣的默契"},{"english":"between players","chinese":"玩家之間"},{"english":"intergenerational bonds","chinese":"跨代聯繫"},{"english":"become weaker","chinese":"變得較弱"},{"english":"small flats","chinese":"細小單位"},{"english":"long working hours","chinese":"長工時"},{"english":"digital entertainment","chinese":"數碼娛樂"},{"english":"leave families with fewer chances to gather","chinese":"令家庭較少機會相聚"},{"english":"protect something responsibly","chinese":"負責任地保護"},{"english":"community centres","chinese":"社區中心"},{"english":"non-gambling mahjong workshops","chinese":"非賭博麻雀工作坊"},{"english":"focusing on","chinese":"集中於"},{"english":"strategy","chinese":"策略"},{"english":"arithmetic","chinese":"算術"},{"english":"cultural history","chinese":"文化歷史"},{"english":"display traditional tile sets","chinese":"展示傳統麻雀牌套裝"},{"english":"traditional tile sets","chinese":"傳統麻雀牌套裝"},{"english":"interview tile-makers","chinese":"訪問麻雀牌製作師傅"},{"english":"tile-makers","chinese":"麻雀牌製作師傅"},{"english":"youth groups","chinese":"青年團體"},{"english":"local playing styles","chinese":"本地玩法"},{"english":"in this way","chinese":"以這種方式"},{"english":"be presented not as…, but as…","chinese":"不被呈現為……而是呈現為……"},{"english":"a vice","chinese":"惡習"},{"english":"a form of social heritage","chinese":"一種社會文化遺產"},{"english":"admittedly","chinese":"誠然"},{"english":"argue that","chinese":"認為；主張"},{"english":"too ordinary","chinese":"太普通"},{"english":"closely associated with","chinese":"與……密切相關"},{"english":"gambling","chinese":"賭博"},{"english":"deserve official protection","chinese":"值得官方保護"},{"english":"that view is understandable","chinese":"這種看法可以理解"},{"english":"misses the point","chinese":"沒有抓住重點"},{"english":"declaring something perfect","chinese":"宣稱某事物完美"},{"english":"recognising practices","chinese":"承認某些習俗"},{"english":"shaped a community's identity","chinese":"塑造了一個社群的身份"},{"english":"community's identity","chinese":"社群身份"},{"english":"encouraging unhealthy eating","chinese":"鼓勵不健康飲食"},{"english":"promoting gambling","chinese":"推廣賭博"},{"english":"preserving knowledge","chinese":"保存知識"},{"english":"social meaning","chinese":"社會意義"},{"english":"guiding the public towards","chinese":"引導公眾走向"},{"english":"responsible appreciation","chinese":"負責任的欣賞"},{"english":"if anything","chinese":"反而；真要說的話"},{"english":"official recognition","chinese":"官方認可"},{"english":"gives Hong Kong a chance to","chinese":"給香港一個機會去"},{"english":"more carefully","chinese":"更仔細地"},{"english":"instead of leaving them to","chinese":"而不是任由它們"},{"english":"fade","chinese":"淡出；消失"},{"english":"commercialise","chinese":"商業化"},{"english":"be misunderstood","chinese":"被誤解"},{"english":"all things considered","chinese":"綜合而言"},{"english":"made a wise choice","chinese":"作出明智選擇"},{"english":"humble, familiar and deeply human","chinese":"樸實、熟悉而充滿人情味"},{"english":"precisely for that reason","chinese":"正正因為這個原因"},{"english":"polished tourist attractions","chinese":"包裝精美的旅遊景點"},{"english":"the next step is clear","chinese":"下一步很清楚"},{"english":"work together to","chinese":"共同努力去"},{"english":"document, teach and practise","chinese":"記錄、教授和實踐"},{"english":"locked behind glass","chinese":"被鎖在玻璃後"},{"english":"tasted, heard, shared and passed on","chinese":"被品嚐、聽見、分享和傳承"},{"english":"passed on","chinese":"傳承下去"},{"english":"Yours faithfully","chinese":"謹啟；此致"}]},"dse-writing-2017-part-b-q6":{"exerciseId":"dse-writing-2017-part-b-q6","essayKey":"","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=dse-writing-2017-part-b-q6","flashDeckId":"dse/writing/part-b/2017/Q6","paragraphs":[{"label":"Paragraph 1","english":"The Screen That Sharpens the Mind","chinese":"磨亮思維的螢幕"},{"label":"Paragraph 2","english":"Good morning, adjudicators, teachers, fellow students and honourable opponents.","chinese":"各位評判、老師、同學，以及尊敬的反方辯友，早晨。 不"},{"label":"Paragraph 3","english":"For years, television has been accused of being the “idiot box”: a glowing rectangle that steals our time, weakens our concentration and turns active students into passive viewers. Understandably, parents and schools sometimes consider cutting it out in order to protect young people’s learning. Today, however, as captain of the debate team, I stand firmly for the motion that watching TV makes us smarter. Let me be clear: I am not defending endless channel-surfing or careless binge-watching. I am arguing that when television is watched thoughtfully, it broadens our knowledge, trains our judgement and deepens our command of language as well as human experience.","chinese":"多年來，電視一直被指責為所謂的「傻瓜盒」：一個發光的長方形，偷走我們的時間、削弱我們的專注力，並把主動學習的學生變成被動的觀眾。 可以理解的是，家長和學校有時會考慮把電視從年輕人的生活中剔除，以保護他們的學習。 然而，今天，作為辯論隊隊長，我堅定支持「看電視讓我們變得更聰明」這項辯題。 讓我清楚說明：我並不是在為無止境地轉台或漫不經心地煲劇辯護。 我主張的是，當人們以深思熟慮的方式觀看電視，它會拓闊我們的知識、訓練我們的判斷力，並加深我們對語言以及人類經驗的掌握。 不"},{"label":"Paragraph 4","english":"First, television makes us smarter by opening a window onto knowledge that textbooks alone cannot always provide. Reading about volcanoes is useful; seeing molten lava, ash clouds and terrified villagers on screen makes the science memorable. A documentary about coral reefs can show how warmer oceans bleach living ecosystems; a news feature on food waste can take us from a supermarket shelf to a landfill. Step by step, the viewer connects cause and effect because images capture attention, attention encourages curiosity, curiosity leads to questions, and questions push learning beyond the living room. Some may say that this is only entertainment. No. What matters is not the screen itself, but the quality of what appears on it. If a student learns about space exploration from a science programme, world poverty from a report, or ancient Egypt from a history series, television has not dulled the mind; instead, it has enlarged it.","chinese":"首先，電視能為我們打開一扇通往知識的窗，而有些知識並非單靠課本便能提供。 閱讀有關火山的內容固然有用；但在螢幕上看見熔岩、火山灰雲和驚恐的村民，會令科學知識變得難忘。 一套關於珊瑚礁的紀錄片，可以展示海洋升溫如何令活生生的生態系統白化；一個有關食物浪費的新聞專題，則可以把我們從超市貨架帶到堆填區。 一步一步地，觀眾會把原因和結果連結起來，因為影像抓住注意力，注意力激發好奇，好奇引出提問，而提問又把學習推向客廳之外。 有人或許會說，這只是娛樂。 不 真正重要的，並非螢幕本身；重點在於螢幕上呈現的內容質素。 如果一名學生從科學節目中認識太空探索、從報導中了解世界貧窮，或從歷史系列中學習古埃及，電視並沒有令他的頭腦變得遲鈍；相反，它拓闊了他的思維。"},{"label":"Paragraph 5","english":"Second, watching TV can sharpen critical thinking. Unlike a worksheet that often has one correct answer, television constantly presents voices that clash: a politician defending a policy, a resident opposing it, an expert explaining the evidence, and a presenter challenging weak claims. When we watch a debate programme or a serious interview, we learn to ask: “Is this argument logical?” “Is the evidence strong?” “Has something important been left out?” This is precisely the habit that schools try to cultivate. Even drama can help. In a legal series, for example, we may first sympathise with one character, only to discover later that the truth is more complicated. That twist teaches us not to judge too quickly. Television, therefore, is not so much a replacement for thinking as a training ground for thinking. The more carefully we watch, the more intelligently we question.","chinese":"不 第二，看電視能夠磨練批判性思考。 工作紙通常只有一個正確答案；相比之下，電視經常呈現互相碰撞的聲音：有政客為政策辯護，有居民提出反對，有專家解釋證據，也有主持人挑戰薄弱的論點。 當我們觀看辯論節目或嚴肅訪談時，我們會學懂追問：「這個論點合乎邏輯嗎？」「證據有力嗎？」「是否有重要內容被遺漏？」 這正正是學校努力培養的習慣。 即使是劇集，也能帶來幫助。 以法律劇集為例，我們一開始可能會同情某個角色，後來才發現真相其實更加複雜。 這種轉折教會我們不要太快下判斷。 因此，電視與其說是思考的替代品，不如說是思考的訓練場。 我們看得越仔細，就越能聰明地發問。"},{"label":"Paragraph 6","english":"Third, television makes us smarter because it strengthens language, empathy and cultural understanding. For Hong Kong students learning English, well-produced TV programmes offer rhythm, pronunciation, idioms and natural interaction that a vocabulary list can hardly reproduce. A student who watches an English documentary hears how ideas are organised; a student who follows a drama notices how tone changes with anger, fear or embarrassment. More importantly, television lets us step into lives far beyond our own. We may meet a refugee family, a doctor under pressure, an athlete recovering from failure, or a child growing up in a culture different from ours. Such stories do not merely feed us information; they make us better listeners. Intelligence is not only the ability to calculate; it is also the ability to understand people. In that sense, good television educates both the mind and the heart.","chinese":"不 第三，電視令我們變得更聰明，因為它能增強語言能力、同理心和文化理解 對正在學習英文的香港學生而言，製作精良的電視節目提供了語言節奏、發音、習語和自然互動；這些都是生字表幾乎無法重現的內容。 觀看英文紀錄片的學生會聽見思想如何被組織；追看劇集的學生則會留意語氣如何隨憤怒、恐懼或尷尬而改變。 更重要的是，電視讓我們走進遠超自身經驗的生命之中。 我們可能會遇見一個難民家庭、一位承受壓力的醫生、一名正從失敗中重新站起來的運動員，或一個在與我們不同的文化中成長的孩子。 這些故事並不只是向我們提供資訊；它們也讓我們成為更好的聆聽者。 智慧不僅是計算的能力；它同時也是理解他人的能力。 從這個意義上說，優質電視既教育頭腦，也教育心靈。"},{"label":"Paragraph 7","english":"Honourable opponents may warn us that television can be addictive, shallow or misleading. I hear that concern, but it does not defeat our case. Food can be unhealthy if we eat badly; that does not mean food is the enemy. The answer is not to reject television, but to choose it wisely, discuss it actively and watch it with purpose. Parents should guide, schools can recommend quality programmes, and students must learn to question what they see. Watching TV makes us smarter not because every programme is brilliant, but because the best television turns information into images, arguments into questions, and strangers into human beings we can understand. So the next time someone calls television an idiot box, I would ask: is the box foolish, or is it foolish only when we watch without thinking? Thank you.","chinese":"不 尊敬的反方辯友可能會警告我們，電視可能令人上癮、流於膚淺，甚至帶有誤導性。 我理解這份憂慮，但它並不能推翻我方的論點。 如果吃得不好，食物也可以不健康；但這並不代表食物本身就是敵人。 答案並非拒絕電視；答案在於明智地選擇、積極地討論，並有目的地觀看。 家長應該加以引導，學校可以推薦優質節目，而學生則必須學會質疑自己所看見的內容。 看電視讓我們變得更聰明，原因並不在於每個節目都精彩絕倫；真正原因在於最優質的電視能把資訊轉化為影像，把論點轉化為問題，也把陌生人轉化為我們能理解的人。 所以，下次有人把電視稱為傻瓜盒時，我會這樣問：愚蠢的是那個盒子，還是只有當我們不思考地觀看時，它才會顯得愚蠢？ 多謝各位。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"sharpen the mind","chinese":"令頭腦更敏銳"},{"english":"good morning, adjudicators","chinese":"各位評判早晨"},{"english":"fellow students","chinese":"各位同學"},{"english":"honourable opponents","chinese":"尊敬的對方辯友"},{"english":"for years","chinese":"多年來"},{"english":"be accused of","chinese":"被指責為……"},{"english":"the idiot box","chinese":"傻瓜盒；令人變笨的電視"},{"english":"a glowing rectangle","chinese":"發光的長方形"},{"english":"steal our time","chinese":"偷走我們的時間"},{"english":"weaken our concentration","chinese":"削弱我們的專注力"},{"english":"turn active students into passive viewers","chinese":"把主動的學生變成被動觀眾"},{"english":"active students","chinese":"主動的學生"},{"english":"passive viewers","chinese":"被動觀眾"},{"english":"understandably","chinese":"可以理解地"},{"english":"consider cutting television out","chinese":"考慮戒掉電視"},{"english":"in order to","chinese":"為了"},{"english":"protect young people's learning","chinese":"保護年輕人的學習"},{"english":"today, however","chinese":"然而今天"},{"english":"as captain of","chinese":"作為……隊長"},{"english":"debate team","chinese":"辯論隊"},{"english":"stand firmly for the motion","chinese":"堅定支持辯題"},{"english":"the motion that","chinese":"……這個辯題"},{"english":"watching TV makes us smarter","chinese":"看電視令我們更聰明"},{"english":"let me be clear","chinese":"讓我說清楚"},{"english":"defend endless channel-surfing","chinese":"為無止境轉台辯護"},{"english":"channel-surfing","chinese":"不停轉台"},{"english":"careless binge-watching","chinese":"漫無目的地煲劇"},{"english":"argue that","chinese":"主張；論證"},{"english":"watched thoughtfully","chinese":"被有思考地觀看"},{"english":"broaden our knowledge","chinese":"擴闊我們的知識"},{"english":"train our judgement","chinese":"訓練我們的判斷力"},{"english":"deepen our command of language","chinese":"加深我們對語言的掌握"},{"english":"command of language","chinese":"語言掌握能力"},{"english":"as well as","chinese":"以及"},{"english":"human experience","chinese":"人生經驗；人類經驗"},{"english":"open a window onto","chinese":"打開通往……的窗口"},{"english":"textbooks alone","chinese":"單靠課本"},{"english":"cannot always provide","chinese":"未必總能提供"},{"english":"reading about","chinese":"閱讀有關……的內容"},{"english":"molten lava","chinese":"熔岩"},{"english":"ash clouds","chinese":"火山灰雲"},{"english":"terrified villagers","chinese":"驚恐的村民"},{"english":"on screen","chinese":"在螢幕上"},{"english":"make the science memorable","chinese":"令科學知識令人難忘"},{"english":"a documentary about","chinese":"關於……的紀錄片"},{"english":"coral reefs","chinese":"珊瑚礁"},{"english":"warmer oceans","chinese":"變暖的海洋"},{"english":"bleach living ecosystems","chinese":"令活生態系統白化"},{"english":"living ecosystems","chinese":"活生態系統"},{"english":"a news feature on","chinese":"關於……的新聞專題"},{"english":"food waste","chinese":"食物浪費"},{"english":"take us from…to…","chinese":"帶我們由……到……"},{"english":"supermarket shelf","chinese":"超級市場貨架"},{"english":"landfill","chinese":"堆填區"},{"english":"step by step","chinese":"一步一步地"},{"english":"connect cause and effect","chinese":"連繫因果關係"},{"english":"capture attention","chinese":"吸引注意力"},{"english":"encourage curiosity","chinese":"激發好奇心"},{"english":"lead to questions","chinese":"引出問題"},{"english":"push learning beyond","chinese":"把學習推到……之外"},{"english":"beyond the living room","chinese":"客廳以外"},{"english":"some may say that","chinese":"有些人可能會說"},{"english":"only entertainment","chinese":"只是娛樂"},{"english":"what matters is not…, but…","chinese":"重要的不是……而是……"},{"english":"the screen itself","chinese":"螢幕本身"},{"english":"the quality of what appears on it","chinese":"螢幕上內容的質素"},{"english":"space exploration","chinese":"太空探索"},{"english":"science programme","chinese":"科學節目"},{"english":"world poverty","chinese":"世界貧窮問題"},{"english":"ancient Egypt","chinese":"古埃及"},{"english":"history series","chinese":"歷史系列節目"},{"english":"dull the mind","chinese":"令頭腦遲鈍"},{"english":"enlarge the mind","chinese":"擴闊思維"},{"english":"sharpen critical thinking","chinese":"提升批判性思維"},{"english":"unlike","chinese":"不像……"},{"english":"a worksheet","chinese":"工作紙"},{"english":"one correct answer","chinese":"一個正確答案"},{"english":"constantly presents","chinese":"不斷呈現"},{"english":"voices that clash","chinese":"互相衝突的聲音"},{"english":"defend a policy","chinese":"為政策辯護"},{"english":"oppose a policy","chinese":"反對政策"},{"english":"explain the evidence","chinese":"解釋證據"},{"english":"challenge weak claims","chinese":"質疑薄弱的說法"},{"english":"debate programme","chinese":"辯論節目"},{"english":"serious interview","chinese":"嚴肅訪問"},{"english":"learn to ask","chinese":"學會提問"},{"english":"logical","chinese":"合乎邏輯的"},{"english":"strong evidence","chinese":"有力證據"},{"english":"be left out","chinese":"被遺漏"},{"english":"precisely the habit","chinese":"正正是這種習慣"},{"english":"cultivate","chinese":"培養"},{"english":"even drama","chinese":"甚至劇集"},{"english":"legal series","chinese":"法律劇"},{"english":"sympathise with","chinese":"同情；認同"},{"english":"only to discover later that","chinese":"結果後來才發現"},{"english":"more complicated","chinese":"更複雜"},{"english":"that twist","chinese":"那個反轉情節"},{"english":"judge too quickly","chinese":"太快下判斷"},{"english":"not so much…as…","chinese":"與其說是……不如說是……"},{"english":"a replacement for thinking","chinese":"思考的替代品"},{"english":"a training ground for thinking","chinese":"思考的訓練場"},{"english":"the more carefully…, the more intelligently…","chinese":"越仔細……就越有智慧地……"},{"english":"question intelligently","chinese":"有智慧地質疑"},{"english":"strengthen language","chinese":"強化語言能力"},{"english":"empathy","chinese":"同理心"},{"english":"cultural understanding","chinese":"文化理解"},{"english":"well-produced TV programmes","chinese":"製作優良的電視節目"},{"english":"offer rhythm and pronunciation","chinese":"提供語調節奏和發音"},{"english":"idioms","chinese":"慣用語"},{"english":"natural interaction","chinese":"自然互動"},{"english":"vocabulary list","chinese":"生字表"},{"english":"can hardly reproduce","chinese":"難以重現"},{"english":"English documentary","chinese":"英文紀錄片"},{"english":"how ideas are organised","chinese":"思想如何組織"},{"english":"follow a drama","chinese":"追看劇集"},{"english":"tone changes with","chinese":"語氣隨……而轉變"},{"english":"embarrassment","chinese":"尷尬"},{"english":"more importantly","chinese":"更重要的是"},{"english":"step into lives","chinese":"走進別人的人生"},{"english":"far beyond our own","chinese":"遠超我們自身的"},{"english":"refugee family","chinese":"難民家庭"},{"english":"under pressure","chinese":"在壓力下"},{"english":"recover from failure","chinese":"從失敗中恢復"},{"english":"grow up in a culture different from ours","chinese":"在與我們不同的文化中成長"},{"english":"such stories","chinese":"這類故事"},{"english":"not merely feed us information","chinese":"不只是向我們灌輸資料"},{"english":"make us better listeners","chinese":"令我們成為更好的聆聽者"},{"english":"the ability to calculate","chinese":"計算能力"},{"english":"the ability to understand people","chinese":"理解他人的能力"},{"english":"in that sense","chinese":"從這個意義上說"},{"english":"educate both the mind and the heart","chinese":"同時教育頭腦和心靈"},{"english":"honourable opponents may warn us that","chinese":"對方辯友可能警告我們"},{"english":"addictive","chinese":"令人上癮的"},{"english":"shallow","chinese":"膚淺的"},{"english":"misleading","chinese":"誤導人的"},{"english":"I hear that concern","chinese":"我明白這個憂慮"},{"english":"defeat our case","chinese":"推翻我們的論點"},{"english":"unhealthy","chinese":"不健康的"},{"english":"eat badly","chinese":"飲食不當"},{"english":"the enemy","chinese":"敵人"},{"english":"the answer is not to…, but to…","chinese":"答案不是……而是……"},{"english":"reject television","chinese":"拒絕電視"},{"english":"choose it wisely","chinese":"明智地選擇"},{"english":"discuss it actively","chinese":"主動討論"},{"english":"watch it with purpose","chinese":"有目的地觀看"},{"english":"recommend quality programmes","chinese":"推薦優質節目"},{"english":"learn to question what they see","chinese":"學會質疑自己所看到的內容"},{"english":"not because…, but because…","chinese":"不是因為……而是因為……"},{"english":"every programme is brilliant","chinese":"每個節目都出色"},{"english":"the best television","chinese":"最優質的電視節目"},{"english":"turn information into images","chinese":"把資料轉化為影像"},{"english":"turn arguments into questions","chinese":"把論點轉化為問題"},{"english":"turn strangers into human beings","chinese":"把陌生人變成我們能理解的人"},{"english":"the next time","chinese":"下一次"},{"english":"call television an idiot box","chinese":"把電視稱為傻瓜盒"},{"english":"watch without thinking","chinese":"不經思考地觀看"},{"english":"thank you","chinese":"多謝"}]},"dse-writing-2017-part-b-q7":{"exerciseId":"dse-writing-2017-part-b-q7","essayKey":"","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=dse-writing-2017-part-b-q7","flashDeckId":"","paragraphs":[{"label":"Paragraph 1","english":"Reconnecting Hong Kong’s NEETs: From Isolation to Opportunity","chinese":"重新連結香港的 NEET 青年：從孤立走向機會"},{"label":"Paragraph 2","english":"To: Project Supervisor","chinese":"收件人：專題督導老師"},{"label":"Paragraph 3","english":"From: Chris Wong","chinese":"撰寫人：Chris Wong"},{"label":"Paragraph 4","english":"Date: 7 April 2018","chinese":"日期：2018年4月7日"},{"label":"Paragraph 5","english":"Subject: Report on the rising number of NEETs in Hong Kong","chinese":"主旨：有關香港 NEET 青年人數上升的報告"},{"label":"Paragraph 6","english":"Introduction","chinese":""},{"label":"Paragraph 7","english":"This report examines why more young people in Hong Kong are becoming NEETs, meaning they are not in education, employment or training. For context, many of them are absent from classrooms, workplaces and training centres, spending long hours at home playing video games or surfing the Internet. This situation has made educators, social workers and employers consider how to reconnect these youths with purposeful routines, so as to prevent long-term unemployment and social isolation. The central finding is as follows: the problem is not so much laziness as disconnection, and it must be answered with early identification, flexible training and patient community support.","chinese":"本報告探討為甚麼香港有越來越多年輕人成為 NEET 青年，即沒有接受教育、沒有就業，也沒有參與培訓的年輕人。 作為背景補充，他們當中許多人都離開了課室、工作場所和培訓中心，長時間留在家中玩電子遊戲或瀏覽互聯網。 這種情況使教育工作者、社工和僱主開始思考，如何讓這些青年重新建立有目標的生活規律，以防止長期失業和社會孤立。 核心發現如下：問題的本質與其說是懶惰，不如說是脫節；要處理這個問題，必須依靠及早識別、彈性培訓和有耐性的社區支援。 Reasons for the rise 人數上升的原因"},{"label":"Paragraph 8","english":"Reasons for the rise","chinese":""},{"label":"Paragraph 9","english":"The first reason is that the transition from school to work has become frighteningly narrow. Hong Kong students are often told that examination results determine their future. As a result, a young person who performs poorly in the DSE may feel that he has missed the only respectable route forward. It is one thing to say that there are many pathways; it is another to make those pathways visible and dignified. For example, a graduate who fails to enter university may not know whether to repeat, enrol in a diploma course, look for a service job or wait at home. Each week of waiting weakens his confidence; each unsuccessful application makes him more reluctant to try again. Before long, staying at home feels safer than facing another rejection.","chinese":"第一個原因是，從學校過渡到職場的道路已經變得狹窄得令人不安。 香港學生經常被告知，考試成績決定他們的未來。 結果，一個在 DSE 表現不佳的年輕人，可能會覺得自己已經錯過了唯一體面的前進道路。 說有許多出路是一回事；真正讓這些出路變得清晰而有尊嚴，又是另一回事 例如，一名未能升讀大學的畢業生，可能不知道自己應該重讀、報讀文憑課程、尋找服務業工作，還是留在家中等待。 每等待多一個星期，他的信心就會被削弱；每一次求職失敗，都會令他更不願意再次嘗試。 不久之後，留在家中便會比再次面對拒絕更有安全感。"},{"label":"Paragraph 10","english":"The second reason is psychological and social. Many NEETs retreat online not because games are always better than real life, but because real life has become too embarrassing to face. Online, they can win points, receive instant feedback and belong to a team. Offline, they may be asked uncomfortable questions: “Why are you not studying?” “Why have you not found a job?” Such questions, even when well-meant, can leave young people ashamed and defensive. With more time spent at home, sleep patterns may deteriorate, communication skills may become rusty and anxiety may deepen. The more they avoid society, the harder returning becomes.","chinese":"第二個原因涉及心理和社交層面。 許多 NEET 青年退到網絡世界，原因並非遊戲永遠比現實生活更好，更多是因為現實生活已經變得太令人尷尬，難以面對。 在線上世界，他們可以得分、即時獲得回饋，並成為團隊的一員。 回到現實世界，他們可能會被問到令人不自在的問題：「為甚麼你沒有讀書？」「為甚麼你還沒有找到工作？」 這些問題即使出於好意，也可能令年輕人感到羞愧，並變得自我防衛。 隨著留在家中的時間增加，他們的睡眠模式可能惡化，溝通技巧可能變得生疏，焦慮也可能加深。 他們越逃避社會，重返社會就越困難。 Recommended measures 建議措施"},{"label":"Paragraph 11","english":"Recommended measures","chinese":""},{"label":"Paragraph 12","english":"Schools should first build an early-warning and follow-up system for students at risk after graduation. Teachers, career masters and social workers should identify students with poor attendance, repeated failure, family stress or no clear post-school plan. They should then provide one-to-one counselling, career mapping and short exposure activities. Take vocational education, for example: many students reject it because they associate it with low status. However, if they can visit training centres, speak to apprentices and try practical workshops in digital design, elderly care, catering or building services, they may see a future that is concrete rather than abstract. This works because it gives students information before they disappear from the system.","chinese":"學校首先應該為畢業後有風險的學生建立早期預警和跟進系統。 教師、升學及就業輔導主任和社工應該識別那些出席率低、屢次失敗、面對家庭壓力，或沒有清晰離校後計劃的學生。 之後，他們應該提供一對一輔導、職涯規劃和短期體驗活動。 以職業教育為例：許多學生拒絕它，是因為他們把它與較低社會地位聯想在一起。 然而，如果他們能夠參觀培訓中心、與學徒交流，並嘗試數碼設計、安老服務、餐飲或屋宇設備方面的實用工作坊，他們或許會看見一個具體而非抽象的未來。 這個方法有效，因為它能在學生從制度中消失之前，先給予他們所需資訊。"},{"label":"Paragraph 13","english":"Employers and community organisations should also create low-risk stepping stones back into society. Instead of expecting long-inactive youths to accept a full-time job immediately, NGOs could arrange three-month paid internships, mentorship schemes and part-time community projects. These programmes should include punctuality training, teamwork, emotional support and basic financial planning. Employers could receive recognition or subsidies if they train NEETs patiently rather than treat them as disposable labour. A young person who learns to arrive on time, communicate with customers and complete small tasks reliably is rebuilding the habits that make stable employment possible. Only by combining compassion with accountability can society help them stand on their own feet.","chinese":"僱主和社區組織也應該創造低風險的踏腳石，幫助他們重返社會。 與其期望長期沒有活動的青年立即接受全職工作，非政府組織不如安排為期三個月的有薪實習、師友計劃和兼職社區項目。 這些計劃應該包括守時訓練、團隊合作、情緒支援和基本財務規劃。 如果僱主願意耐心培訓 NEET 青年，而非把他們視為可隨意替換的勞動力，他們可以獲得表揚或津貼。 一個學會準時到達、與顧客溝通，並可靠地完成小任務的年輕人，正在重建那些使穩定就業成為可能的習慣。 只有把同理心與問責結合起來，社會才能幫助他們自立。"},{"label":"Paragraph 14","english":"Conclusion","chinese":""},{"label":"Paragraph 15","english":"Hong Kong’s NEET problem is rising because some young people are trapped between an unforgiving education system, an intimidating labour market and the temporary comfort of the online world. The way forward is not to blame them, nor to leave them hidden behind bedroom doors. Schools must identify them earlier, social workers must reach them more patiently, employers must offer realistic first steps and families must encourage without humiliating. If Hong Kong can turn isolation into guidance and hesitation into opportunity, many NEETs will not remain lost; slowly but surely, they can return to learning, working and living with confidence.","chinese":"香港的 NEET 問題正在惡化，因為一些年輕人被困在嚴苛的教育制度、令人卻步的勞動市場，以及網絡世界短暫的安慰之間。 前進的方向並非責備他們，也不應讓他們繼續躲在睡房門後。 學校必須更早識別他們，社工必須更有耐性地接觸他們，僱主必須提供現實可行的第一步，而家庭則必須在不羞辱他們的情況下給予鼓勵。 如果香港能夠把孤立轉化為引導，把猶豫轉化為機會，許多 NEET 青年就不會一直迷失；慢慢地，但穩定地，他們可以重新回到學習、工作和有信心生活的道路上。"}],"vocabulary":[]},"dse-writing-2017-part-b-q8":{"exerciseId":"dse-writing-2017-part-b-q8","essayKey":"","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=dse-writing-2017-part-b-q8","flashDeckId":"dse/writing/part-b/2017/Q8","paragraphs":[{"label":"Paragraph 1","english":"Dancers Are Athletes","chinese":"舞者也是運動員 舞者是運動員，因為舞蹈需要卓越的體能、精煉的技巧、嚴格的自律，以及持續不懈的訓練。 更重要的是，舞者之所以是運動員，是因為他們的進步取決於有紀律的訓練 舞者就是運動員——我們是時候以運動員應得的方式看待他們了。"},{"label":"Paragraph 2","english":"For years, the word “athlete” has brought to mind swimmers slicing through water, basketball players sprinting across the court, or runners collapsing breathlessly at the finish line. Dancers, by contrast, are often pictured under soft stage lights, dressed beautifully and smiling effortlessly. Yet this picture is incomplete. As a member of our school dance team, I am writing to ask our school community to see dance not as decoration for assemblies, but as a demanding sport in its own right. Dancers are athletes because dance requires exceptional physical strength, refined skills, strict self-discipline as well as relentless training.","chinese":"舞者也是運動員 多年來，「運動員」這個詞總令人聯想到在水中破浪前進的游泳選手、在球場上疾跑的籃球員，或是在終點線前氣喘吁吁倒下的跑手。 相比之下，舞者在人們想像中，往往站在柔和的舞台燈光下，穿著漂亮服裝，毫不費力地微笑著。 然而，這幅想像其實並不完整。 作為本校舞蹈隊的一員，我寫這篇文章，是希望校內各位不要把舞蹈只看作集會上的裝飾，更要把它視為一項本身極具要求的運動。 舞者是運動員，因為舞蹈需要卓越的體能、精煉的技巧、嚴格的自律，以及持續不懈的訓練。"},{"label":"Paragraph 3","english":"Physical Strength & Skills","chinese":"體能與技巧"},{"label":"Paragraph 4","english":"To begin with, dancers possess a kind of athletic strength that is easy to overlook precisely because it is made to look effortless. When a basketball player jumps, the audience expects power; when a dancer leaps, turns and lands silently, the audience often sees only grace. However, grace is far from the absence of strength. Rather, it is strength controlled so precisely and completely that it becomes beautiful. A dancer must hold the core tight, keep the back lifted, extend the legs, control the arms and still remember the rhythm, spacing and facial expression. One weak muscle can ruin a turn; worse still, one careless landing can lead to potentially permanent injury.","chinese":"首先，舞者擁有一種很容易被忽視的運動力量，原因正正在於他們把一切都呈現得像毫不費力一樣。 當籃球員跳起時，觀眾會期待力量；當舞者躍起、旋轉並安靜落地時，觀眾卻往往只看見優雅。 然而，優雅絕不等於缺乏力量。 更準確地說，它是一種被精準而完整地控制到近乎美感的力量。 舞者必須收緊核心肌群、保持背部挺直、伸展雙腿、控制手臂，同時仍要記住節奏、走位和面部表情。 一塊肌肉力量不足，就可能破壞一次旋轉；更嚴重的是，一次落地不慎，甚至可能導致潛在的永久傷患。"},{"label":"Paragraph 5","english":"Take our school team’s recent jazz routine, for example. During one thirty-second section, we had to complete a jump, drop to the floor, roll, stand up, turn twice and move into a new formation—all without losing the beat. It looked smooth on stage, but behind those thirty seconds were aching thighs, bruised knees and repeated corrections from our coach. Unlike many sports, dance does not allow athletes to show how tired they are. A swimmer may gasp after a race, but a dancer must finish the final pose as if the whole routine has cost nothing. That is not easier than sport. If anything, it is more demanding in an entirely different manner.","chinese":"以我們校隊最近的爵士舞表演為例。 在其中一段三十秒的部分，我們要完成一次跳躍、落到地面、翻滾、站起來、轉兩圈，然後移到新的隊形——整個過程還不能失去節拍。 在舞台上看起來流暢自然，但那三十秒背後，是痠痛的大腿、瘀傷的膝蓋，以及教練一次又一次的糾正。 與許多運動不同，舞蹈不容許運動員把疲憊表現出來。 游泳選手比賽後可以喘著氣，但舞者必須完成最後一個姿勢，彷彿整段舞蹈從未消耗過任何力氣。 這絕對不比其他運動容易。 真要說的話，它是在一種完全不同的層面上更加艱難。"},{"label":"Paragraph 6","english":"Dance also requires a rare combination of flexibility, coordination, balance and spatial awareness. A dancer has to know not only what their own body is doing, but also where every teammate is moving. In a group performance, if one person travels too far forward or turns half a beat late, the whole formation simply changes. This is similar to basketball teamwork: each player must pass, defend and move according to others. The same applies to dancers. We count music like athletes read the game. We react to pressure, adjust to mistakes and carry on instantly. Physical beauty, therefore, is only the surface; underneath it lies athletic precision.","chinese":"舞蹈也需要一種難得的組合：柔韌度、協調能力、平衡力和空間感。 舞者不僅要知道自己的身體正在做甚麼，也要知道每位隊友正在移向哪裡。 在團體表演中，如果有一個人走得太前，或慢了半拍才轉身，整個隊形就會直接改變。 這與籃球中的團隊合作相似：每位球員都必須根據其他人的位置去傳球、防守和走動。 同樣的道理也適用於舞者。 我們數著音樂拍子，就像運動員閱讀比賽局勢一樣。 我們要應對壓力、修正錯誤，並立刻繼續表演。 因此，身體呈現出的美感只是表層；藏在其下的，是運動員般的精準。"},{"label":"Paragraph 7","english":"Self-discipline & Training","chinese":"自律與訓練"},{"label":"Paragraph 8","english":"More importantly, dancers are athletes because their progress depends on disciplined training. It is neither luck nor natural talent alone. Fundamentally, it is discipline that determines long-term success, rather than mere talent. Many people see the final performance, yet few see the repeated stretching, strengthening and drilling that come before it. Before competitions or school shows, our team often rehearses after lessons when others are already going home. We practise the same eight counts again and again, until the timing becomes automatic. By the time we step onto the stage, and through enormous effort and sacrifice, the routine has already been built into our muscles.","chinese":"舞者也是運動員 更重要的是，舞者之所以是運動員，是因為他們的進步取決於有紀律的訓練 這既非單靠運氣，也非單靠天賦。 從根本上說，決定長遠成功的，是紀律，而非純粹天賦。 很多人看見的是最後的演出，卻很少人看見在此之前一遍又一遍的拉筋、體能強化和反覆操練。 在比賽或學校表演前，當其他同學已經回家時，我們校隊經常還在課後排練 我們一次又一次練習同樣的八拍，直到時間掌握變成身體的自然反應。 到我們踏上舞台時，經過巨大的努力與犧牲，整段舞步早已刻進肌肉之中。"},{"label":"Paragraph 9","english":"This training also demands mental toughness. There are days when the mirror feels cruel, when the body refuses to cooperate and when criticism from the coach sounds sharper than usual. Still, dancers have to return the next day. We learn to accept corrections without taking them personally. We learn to support teammates whose confidence has dropped. We learn that “practice makes perfect” is not a cheerful slogan, but a daily discipline. Every sharper turn, cleaner line and stronger jump is earned little by little, with blood, sweat and tears.","chinese":"這種訓練也要求強大的心理韌性。 有些日子，鏡子看起來格外殘酷，身體怎樣也不肯配合，教練的批評也聽起來比平常更尖銳。 即使如此，舞者第二天仍然必須回到排練室。 我們學會接受糾正，而不把它視為針對自己。 我們學會支持那些信心下跌的隊友。 我們明白，「熟能生巧」不只是一句令人振奮的口號，更是一種每天都要實踐的紀律。 每一次更俐落的旋轉、更乾淨的線條和更有力的跳躍，都是靠著血、汗與淚，一點一滴換來的。"},{"label":"Paragraph 10","english":"Self-discipline also means looking after the body. Dancers must warm up properly, stretch safely, sleep enough and avoid careless injuries. A dancer who ignores fitness soon loses stamina; a dancer who skips practice quickly falls behind. In this sense, dance is no less serious than swimming, athletics or basketball. The costume may sparkle, but the training behind it is sweat, repetition and responsibility.","chinese":"自律也意味著要好好照顧身體。 舞者必須正確熱身、安全拉筋、保持充足睡眠，並避免因疏忽而受傷。 忽視體能的舞者很快就會失去耐力；逃避練習的舞者也會迅速落後。 從這個意義上說，舞蹈的嚴肅程度絕不低於游泳、田徑或籃球。 服裝也許閃閃發亮，但支撐它的訓練，是汗水、重複和責任。"},{"label":"Paragraph 11","english":"Ultimately, our school should recognise dancers as athletes, not merely performers. This means giving dance the same respect we give to other sports teams: proper rehearsal space, serious encouragement and genuine applause. The next time you watch dancers on stage, do not ask, “Is this really sport?” Ask instead: “How much strength, control and discipline did this take?” The answer, surely, is more than enough to prove the point. Dancers are athletes—and it is time we treated them as such.","chinese":"舞者也是運動員 歸根究柢，我們學校應該承認舞者是運動員，不應只把他們看作表演者。 這意味著我們應該給予舞蹈與其他運動隊伍同等的尊重：合適的排練空間、認真的鼓勵，以及真誠的掌聲。 下一次你在舞台上看見舞者時，不要問：「這真的算是運動嗎？」 你應該改為問：「這到底需要多少力量、控制和紀律？」 答案無疑已經非常充分，足以證明這個觀點。 舞者就是運動員——我們是時候以運動員應得的方式看待他們了。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"brought to mind","chinese":"令人想起"},{"english":"swimmers slicing through water","chinese":"游泳健兒破水前進"},{"english":"sprinting across the court","chinese":"在球場上衝刺"},{"english":"collapsing breathlessly","chinese":"氣喘吁吁地倒下"},{"english":"at the finish line","chinese":"在終點線"},{"english":"by contrast","chinese":"相比之下"},{"english":"be pictured under","chinese":"被想像成在……之下"},{"english":"soft stage lights","chinese":"柔和的舞台燈光"},{"english":"dressed beautifully","chinese":"打扮得漂亮"},{"english":"smiling effortlessly","chinese":"看似毫不費力地微笑"},{"english":"this picture is incomplete","chinese":"這種看法並不完整"},{"english":"as a member of","chinese":"作為……的一員"},{"english":"school dance team","chinese":"學校舞蹈隊"},{"english":"school community","chinese":"學校群體"},{"english":"see dance not as…, but as…","chinese":"不把舞蹈視為……，而是視為……"},{"english":"decoration for assemblies","chinese":"集會上的點綴"},{"english":"a demanding sport","chinese":"要求極高的運動"},{"english":"in its own right","chinese":"本身就是；憑本身條件"},{"english":"exceptional physical strength","chinese":"出色的體能力量"},{"english":"refined skills","chinese":"精細的技巧"},{"english":"strict self-discipline","chinese":"嚴格的自律"},{"english":"relentless training","chinese":"不懈的訓練"},{"english":"to begin with","chinese":"首先"},{"english":"possess a kind of","chinese":"擁有一種……"},{"english":"athletic strength","chinese":"運動員般的力量"},{"english":"easy to overlook","chinese":"容易被忽略"},{"english":"precisely because","chinese":"正正因為"},{"english":"be made to look effortless","chinese":"被塑造成看似毫不費力"},{"english":"expect power","chinese":"預期看到力量"},{"english":"leaps, turns and lands silently","chinese":"跳躍、轉身並輕聲落地"},{"english":"see only grace","chinese":"只看到優雅"},{"english":"far from the absence of","chinese":"絕不是沒有……"},{"english":"the absence of strength","chinese":"缺乏力量"},{"english":"strength controlled so precisely","chinese":"被精準控制的力量"},{"english":"hold the core tight","chinese":"收緊核心肌群"},{"english":"keep the back lifted","chinese":"保持背部挺直上提"},{"english":"extend the legs","chinese":"伸展雙腿"},{"english":"control the arms","chinese":"控制手臂動作"},{"english":"remember the rhythm","chinese":"記住節奏"},{"english":"spacing","chinese":"走位距離；空間安排"},{"english":"facial expression","chinese":"面部表情"},{"english":"one weak muscle","chinese":"一塊乏力的肌肉"},{"english":"ruin a turn","chinese":"毀掉一個轉身動作"},{"english":"worse still","chinese":"更糟的是"},{"english":"careless landing","chinese":"不小心的落地"},{"english":"lead to","chinese":"導致"},{"english":"potentially permanent injury","chinese":"可能永久性的受傷"},{"english":"take…, for example","chinese":"以……為例"},{"english":"recent jazz routine","chinese":"最近的爵士舞套路"},{"english":"thirty-second section","chinese":"三十秒的一段"},{"english":"complete a jump","chinese":"完成一個跳躍動作"},{"english":"drop to the floor","chinese":"倒到地上"},{"english":"move into a new formation","chinese":"走入新的隊形"},{"english":"without losing the beat","chinese":"沒有失去拍子"},{"english":"look smooth on stage","chinese":"在舞台上看起來流暢"},{"english":"behind those thirty seconds","chinese":"在那三十秒背後"},{"english":"aching thighs","chinese":"痠痛的大腿"},{"english":"bruised knees","chinese":"瘀傷的膝蓋"},{"english":"repeated corrections","chinese":"反覆的糾正"},{"english":"unlike many sports","chinese":"不同於許多運動"},{"english":"show how tired they are","chinese":"表現出自己有多疲倦"},{"english":"gasp after a race","chinese":"比賽後大口喘氣"},{"english":"finish the final pose","chinese":"完成最後定格姿勢"},{"english":"as if","chinese":"彷彿"},{"english":"the whole routine","chinese":"整套舞蹈"},{"english":"cost nothing","chinese":"毫不費力"},{"english":"if anything","chinese":"甚至可以說"},{"english":"more demanding","chinese":"要求更高"},{"english":"in an entirely different way","chinese":"以完全不同的方式"},{"english":"a rare combination of","chinese":"罕見的……組合"},{"english":"flexibility","chinese":"柔韌性"},{"english":"coordination","chinese":"協調能力"},{"english":"balance","chinese":"平衡力"},{"english":"spatial awareness","chinese":"空間感"},{"english":"not only…, but also…","chinese":"不但……，而且……"},{"english":"what their own body is doing","chinese":"自己身體正在做甚麼"},{"english":"where every teammate is moving","chinese":"每位隊友正移向哪裏"},{"english":"a group performance","chinese":"群舞表演"},{"english":"travel too far forward","chinese":"向前移動得太多"},{"english":"half a beat late","chinese":"慢了半拍"},{"english":"the whole formation","chinese":"整個隊形"},{"english":"be similar to","chinese":"與……相似"},{"english":"basketball teamwork","chinese":"籃球團隊合作"},{"english":"according to others","chinese":"按照其他人的動作"},{"english":"the same applies to","chinese":"同樣適用於"},{"english":"count music","chinese":"數音樂拍子"},{"english":"read the game","chinese":"判讀比賽形勢"},{"english":"react to pressure","chinese":"應對壓力"},{"english":"adjust to mistakes","chinese":"因應錯誤作出調整"},{"english":"carry on instantly","chinese":"立即繼續"},{"english":"physical beauty","chinese":"身體美感"},{"english":"only the surface","chinese":"只是表面"},{"english":"underneath it lies","chinese":"其背後是"},{"english":"athletic precision","chinese":"運動員般的精準"},{"english":"more importantly","chinese":"更重要的是"},{"english":"progress depends on","chinese":"進步取決於"},{"english":"disciplined training","chinese":"有紀律的訓練"},{"english":"neither…nor…","chinese":"既不是……也不是……"},{"english":"natural talent alone","chinese":"單靠天賦"},{"english":"fundamentally","chinese":"從根本上來說"},{"english":"determine long-term success","chinese":"決定長遠成功"},{"english":"rather than mere talent","chinese":"而不是單靠天分"},{"english":"final performance","chinese":"最後演出"},{"english":"repeated stretching","chinese":"反覆拉筋"},{"english":"strengthening and drilling","chinese":"強化訓練和反覆操練"},{"english":"before competitions","chinese":"比賽前"},{"english":"school shows","chinese":"學校表演"},{"english":"rehearse after lessons","chinese":"放學後排練"},{"english":"practise the same eight counts","chinese":"反覆練習同樣八拍"},{"english":"again and again","chinese":"一次又一次"},{"english":"timing becomes automatic","chinese":"時間掌握變成自然反應"},{"english":"step onto the stage","chinese":"踏上舞台"},{"english":"through enormous effort and sacrifice","chinese":"經過巨大努力和犧牲"},{"english":"be built into our muscles","chinese":"已經成為肌肉記憶"},{"english":"demand mental toughness","chinese":"需要心理韌性"},{"english":"mental toughness","chinese":"心理韌性"},{"english":"There are days when","chinese":"有些日子"},{"english":"the mirror feels cruel","chinese":"鏡子顯得殘酷"},{"english":"refuse to cooperate","chinese":"不肯配合"},{"english":"criticism from the coach","chinese":"教練的批評"},{"english":"sound sharper than usual","chinese":"聽起來比平日更刺耳"},{"english":"return the next day","chinese":"第二天再回來"},{"english":"accept corrections","chinese":"接受糾正"},{"english":"without taking them personally","chinese":"不把它們視作針對自己"},{"english":"support teammates","chinese":"支持隊友"},{"english":"confidence has dropped","chinese":"信心下跌"},{"english":"practice makes perfect","chinese":"熟能生巧"},{"english":"a cheerful slogan","chinese":"樂觀口號"},{"english":"a daily discipline","chinese":"每天的紀律"},{"english":"sharper turn","chinese":"更俐落的轉身"},{"english":"cleaner line","chinese":"更乾淨俐落的線條"},{"english":"stronger jump","chinese":"更有力的跳躍"},{"english":"be earned little by little","chinese":"一點一滴掙回來"},{"english":"with blood, sweat and tears","chinese":"以血汗和淚水換來"},{"english":"look after the body","chinese":"照顧身體"},{"english":"warm up properly","chinese":"正確熱身"},{"english":"stretch safely","chinese":"安全地拉筋"},{"english":"sleep enough","chinese":"睡眠充足"},{"english":"avoid careless injuries","chinese":"避免因疏忽而受傷"},{"english":"ignore fitness","chinese":"忽視體能"},{"english":"lose stamina","chinese":"失去耐力"},{"english":"skip practice","chinese":"缺席練習"},{"english":"fall behind","chinese":"落後"},{"english":"in this sense","chinese":"從這個意義上說"},{"english":"no less serious than","chinese":"不比……遜色；同樣嚴肅"},{"english":"athletics","chinese":"田徑"},{"english":"the costume may sparkle","chinese":"服裝或許閃亮"},{"english":"sweat, repetition and responsibility","chinese":"汗水、重複和責任"},{"english":"ultimately","chinese":"最終"},{"english":"recognise dancers as athletes","chinese":"承認舞者是運動員"},{"english":"not merely performers","chinese":"不只是表演者"},{"english":"give dance the same respect","chinese":"給予舞蹈同等尊重"},{"english":"sports teams","chinese":"運動隊伍"},{"english":"proper rehearsal space","chinese":"合適的排練空間"},{"english":"serious encouragement","chinese":"認真的鼓勵"},{"english":"genuine applause","chinese":"真誠的掌聲"},{"english":"the next time","chinese":"下一次"},{"english":"on stage","chinese":"在舞台上"},{"english":"ask instead","chinese":"反而要問"},{"english":"strength, control and discipline","chinese":"力量、控制力和紀律"},{"english":"more than enough to","chinese":"足以……"},{"english":"prove the point","chinese":"證明這一點"},{"english":"treat them as such","chinese":"以此身分看待他們"}]},"dse-writing-2017-part-b-q9":{"exerciseId":"dse-writing-2017-part-b-q9","essayKey":"","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=dse-writing-2017-part-b-q9","flashDeckId":"","paragraphs":[{"label":"Paragraph 1","english":"A Misjudgement of Hong Kong’s Young Graduates","chinese":"對香港年輕畢業生的錯判"},{"label":"Paragraph 2","english":"Dear Editor,","chinese":"編輯先生／女士："},{"label":"Paragraph 3","english":"In recent months, a familiar complaint has resurfaced - fresh university graduates in Hong Kong are supposedly less hard-working and less willing to face challenges than their predecessors. Such a claim has led some employers and senior workers to question whether young recruits deserve trust, training or meaningful responsibility in the workplace. The apparent aim is to protect productivity and maintain professional standards. With all due respect, I strongly disagree. To call today’s graduates lazy is not merely unfair; it is a serious misreading of how work, pressure and ambition have fundamentally changed. Hong Kong’s young graduates are not weaker than those in the past. Rather, they are working under different conditions, facing new forms of difficulty and redefining professionalism in ways that many older observers have yet to fully understand.","chinese":"近月來，一種熟悉的抱怨再次浮現：香港新近大學畢業生據稱比過去的畢業生較不勤奮，也較不願意面對挑戰。 這種說法令一些僱主和資深員工開始質疑，年輕新入職員工是否值得在職場上獲得信任、培訓或有意義的責任。 表面目的，是要保障生產力並維持專業標準。 恕我直言，我強烈不同意。 把今天的畢業生稱為懶惰，不只不公平；更是對工作、壓力和抱負如何從根本上改變的一種嚴重誤讀。 香港的年輕畢業生並不比過去的人脆弱。 更準確地說，他們正在不同條件下工作，面對新的困難形式，並以許多年長觀察者尚未完全理解的方式重新界定專業精神。"},{"label":"Paragraph 4","english":"First, fresh graduates today are anything but unwilling to work hard; in fact, many start preparing for their careers long before they officially enter the workplace. Gone are the days when a university degree alone could open most doors. Today, students are expected to build portfolios, complete internships, join competitions, learn digital tools, improve their Putonghua and English, and still maintain respectable academic results. A business student, for instance, may spend the semester attending lectures, the summer working as an intern in Central, and the evenings preparing for case competitions or professional examinations. This is not laziness, but effort spread across many fronts. If some graduates appear cautious when they begin full-time employment, it is often because they are trying to understand complicated office expectations, not because they are avoiding responsibility. Put simply, a generation that has survived years of academic competition, unpaid or low-paid internships and rising living costs cannot reasonably be dismissed as unwilling to work.","chinese":"首先，今天的新近畢業生絕非不願努力工作；事實上，許多人早在正式進入職場之前，已經開始為自己的事業作準備。 單靠一張大學學位便能打開大多數大門的日子，已經一去不返。 今天，學生被期望建立作品集、完成實習、參加比賽、學習數碼工具、提升普通話和英語能力，同時仍要維持體面的學業成績。 例如，一名商科學生可能整個學期都在上課，暑假則在中環做實習生，晚上還要準備商業個案比賽或專業考試。 這並非懶惰；更準確來說，這是分散在多個層面上的努力。 如果有些畢業生在開始全職工作時看起來較為謹慎，原因往往是他們正在嘗試理解複雜的辦公室期望，並非因為他們逃避責任。 簡單來說，一代人既然經歷了多年的學業競爭、無薪或低薪實習，以及不斷上升的生活成本，就不應被輕率地說成不願工作。"},{"label":"Paragraph 5","english":"Second, the challenges facing today’s graduates are different from those faced by earlier generations. In the past, hard work was often measured by visible signs as in staying late, following instructions silently and accepting hardship without complaint. However, modern workplaces require conditions beyond endurance. Young employees must deal with artificial intelligence, online communication, data security, global clients, hybrid meetings and rapidly changing business models. A fresh graduate joining a marketing firm may have to interpret online analytics, produce short videos, respond to customers on social media and adapt to new software within the same week. These tasks may not look like traditional “hard work”, but they demand speed, creativity and constant learning. It is one thing to work long hours; it is another to keep learning while the rules of the game are changing. In other words, it is young graduates’ ability to adapt that make them valuable, rather than a blind obedience. Their willingness to ask questions should by no means be mistaken for weakness. Very often, it is the first step towards solving problems properly.","chinese":"第二，今天畢業生所面對的挑戰，與較早世代所面對的挑戰並不相同。 在過去，努力工作往往由一些可見跡象來衡量，例如留到很晚、默默服從指示，以及毫無怨言地承受艱辛。 然而，現代職場的要求已經超越單純忍耐。 年輕員工必須處理人工智能、網上溝通、數據安全、全球客戶、混合式會議，以及快速變化的商業模式。 一名剛加入市場推廣公司的新近畢業生，可能要在同一個星期內解讀網上分析數據、製作短片、在社交媒體上回應顧客，並適應新的軟件。 這些任務看起來未必像傳統意義上的「努力工作」，卻要求速度、創意和持續學習。 長時間工作是一回事；在遊戲規則不斷改變時仍持續學習，則是另一回事。 換句話說，令年輕畢業生具有價值的，是他們的適應能力，並非盲目的服從 他們願意發問，絕不應被誤解為軟弱。 很多時候，這正是妥善解決問題的第一步。"},{"label":"Paragraph 6","english":"Third, the accusation also confuses healthy boundaries with a poor work ethic. Some fresh graduates do object to meaningless overtime, unclear instructions or unreasonable management. Yet that does not imply that they fear challenges. Rather, it shows that they want challenges to be purposeful. There is a world of difference between refusing hard work and refusing exploitation. For example, a young engineer may gladly stay late to fix a genuine safety problem, but question why a report has to be rewritten three times simply because the requirements were never clearly explained. Similarly, a junior teacher may willingly spend hours preparing lessons for students, while still believing that constant administrative work harms the quality of teaching. Such attitudes reflect maturity that is wrongly believed to be “modern laziness”. Hong Kong employers should welcome workers who can think, communicate and improve systems, instead of expecting silent suffering as superficial proof of commitment.","chinese":"第三，這項指控也把健康界線和欠佳工作態度混為一談。 有些新畢業生確實會反對沒有意義的加班、模糊不清的指示或不合理的管理 然而，這並不表示他們害怕挑戰。 更準確地說，這反映他們希望挑戰本身具有目的和意義。 拒絕艱苦工作與拒絕被剝削之間，有著天壤之別。 例如，一名年輕工程師可能很願意留到很晚去處理真正的安全問題，但也會質疑為甚麼一份報告只因要求從未被清楚解釋，就必須重寫三次。 同樣地，一名初級教師可能願意花上數小時為學生備課，同時仍然相信持續不斷的行政工作會損害教學質素。 這些態度反映的是成熟，卻被錯誤地理解為「現代懶惰」。 香港僱主應該歡迎能夠思考、溝通和改善制度的員工，而不應期望員工以沉默受苦來作為投入工作的表面證明。"},{"label":"Paragraph 7","english":"In conclusion, the idea that Hong Kong’s fresh university graduates are less hard-working and less willing to face challenges is unfair, outdated and ultimately, damaging. They are not avoiding hardship; quite the contrary, they are facing a never-before-seen kind of hardship. They are not rejecting work; they are asking for work that is meaningful, well-managed and worthy of their effort. Employers, senior colleagues and the wider public should therefore stop using stereotypes as shortcuts. Instead, companies should provide clearer training, fairer feedback and real opportunities for young employees to prove themselves. Only by making room at the table for this new generation can Hong Kong continue to build a workplace that is both productive and humane.","chinese":"總而言之，認為香港新近大學畢業生較不勤奮、較不願面對挑戰這種想法，是不公平、過時，而且最終會造成傷害的。 他們並沒有逃避艱辛；恰恰相反，他們正在面對一種前所未見的艱辛。 他們並沒有拒絕工作；他們所要求的，是有意義、管理得宜，而且值得他們付出努力的工作。 因此，僱主、資深同事以及更廣泛的公眾，都應該停止把刻板印象當作理解年輕人的捷徑。 相反，公司應該提供更清晰的培訓、更公平的回饋，以及真正讓年輕員工證明自己的機會。 只有讓這一代新人在討論和決策中真正佔有一席之地，香港才能繼續建立一個既有生產力又有人性的職場。"},{"label":"Paragraph 8","english":"Yours faithfully,","chinese":"此致"},{"label":"Paragraph 9","english":"Chris Wong","chinese":"Chris Wong"}],"vocabulary":[]},"dse-writing-2018-part-a":{"exerciseId":"dse-writing-2018-part-a","essayKey":"","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=dse-writing-2018-part-a","flashDeckId":"dse/writing/part-a/2018","paragraphs":[{"label":"Salutation","english":"Dear Parents/Carers,","chinese":"各位家長／照顧者："},{"label":"Salutation","english":"I hope this letter finds you well.","chinese":"展信安好。"},{"label":"Introduction","english":"I am writing to inform you about an exciting school trip for Class 6A, which will be held next month. We will be visiting sky100 Hong Kong Observation Deck, located on the 100th floor of the International Commerce Centre (ICC) in West Kowloon. This is the highest indoor observation deck in the city, and our main goal of the school outing is to broaden students’ horizons by showing them Hong Kong’s spectacular skyline from an entirely new perspective.","chinese":"本人寫信是為了通知各位有關 6A 班下月舉行的一次精彩學校旅行。 我們將參觀位於西九龍環球貿易廣場（ICC）100 樓的 sky100 香港觀景台。 這是全城最高的室內觀景台，而是次學校外出的主要目標，是透過讓學生從一個全新的角度欣賞香港壯麗的天際線，從而擴闊他們的視野。"},{"label":"Trip Details","english":"With respect to the details of the school trip, we will first depart from the school by coach at 9:00 a.m. and shall be dismissed at 4:00 p.m. The entrance fee is HKD 150, and the transportation cost will be HKD 20 per student. Students are advised to wear comfortable and casual outfits and bring a small backpack for personal belongings. We will have lunch together at a nearby restaurant; however, those with special dietary requirements are welcome to pack their own meals. After lunch, there will be a short debriefing session, during which students will work in groups to discuss their observations and gain insights into Hong Kong’s architecture.","chinese":"關於是次學校旅行的詳情，我們將首先於上午 9 時乘坐旅遊巴從學校出發，並於下午 4 時解散。 入場費為 HKD 150，而每位學生的交通費為 HKD 20。 學生宜穿著舒適的便服，並攜帶一個小背包放置個人物品。 我們將在附近一間餐廳一同用膳；然而，如學生有特殊飲食需要，亦歡迎自行攜帶午餐。 午膳後，學生將參與一個簡短的匯報環節，期間他們會分組討論自己的觀察，並加深對香港建築的理解。"},{"label":"Action Required","english":"To proceed, please complete and return the permission slip attached in the letter. Should you have any questions or concerns, please do not hesitate to contact me at the school office. Thank you for your cooperation, and I look forward to an enriching and memorable trip.","chinese":"為便安排，請填妥並交回本信所附的同意書。 如各位有任何問題或疑慮，請隨時透過學校辦公室與本人聯絡。 感謝各位的合作，本人期待這次旅程能夠充實而難忘。"},{"label":"Sign-off","english":"Yours sincerely,","chinese":"此致"},{"label":"Sign-off","english":"Chris Wong","chinese":"Chris Wong"},{"label":"Sign-off","english":"Class Teacher of 6A","chinese":"6A 班班主任"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"Dear Parents/Carers","chinese":"親愛的家長／照顧者"},{"english":"I hope this letter finds you well","chinese":"希望你們一切安好"},{"english":"I am writing to inform you about","chinese":"現寫信通知你們有關……"},{"english":"an exciting school trip","chinese":"一次令人期待的學校旅行"},{"english":"be held next month","chinese":"將於下月舉行"},{"english":"be visiting","chinese":"將會參觀"},{"english":"sky100 Hong Kong Observation Deck","chinese":"香港天際100觀景台"},{"english":"be located on","chinese":"位於……"},{"english":"the 100th floor of","chinese":"……的一百樓"},{"english":"International Commerce Centre","chinese":"環球貿易廣場"},{"english":"West Kowloon","chinese":"西九龍"},{"english":"indoor observation deck","chinese":"室內觀景台"},{"english":"the highest indoor observation deck","chinese":"最高的室內觀景台"},{"english":"main goal","chinese":"主要目的"},{"english":"school outing","chinese":"學校郊遊；學校旅行"},{"english":"broaden students' horizons","chinese":"擴闊學生的視野"},{"english":"Hong Kong's spectacular skyline","chinese":"香港壯麗的天際線"},{"english":"from an entirely new perspective","chinese":"從全新的角度"},{"english":"with respect to","chinese":"關於……"},{"english":"details of the school trip","chinese":"學校旅行詳情"},{"english":"depart from the school","chinese":"從學校出發"},{"english":"by coach","chinese":"乘旅遊巴"},{"english":"at 9:00 a.m.","chinese":"上午九時"},{"english":"be dismissed at","chinese":"於……解散"},{"english":"entrance fee","chinese":"入場費"},{"english":"transportation cost","chinese":"交通費"},{"english":"per student","chinese":"每名學生"},{"english":"be advised to","chinese":"建議……"},{"english":"wear comfortable and casual clothes","chinese":"穿着舒適便服"},{"english":"comfortable and casual clothes","chinese":"舒適便服"},{"english":"bring a small backpack","chinese":"帶備小背囊"},{"english":"personal belongings","chinese":"個人物品"},{"english":"have lunch together","chinese":"一起用膳"},{"english":"nearby restaurant","chinese":"附近餐廳"},{"english":"special dietary requirements","chinese":"特別飲食需要"},{"english":"be welcome to","chinese":"歡迎……"},{"english":"pack their own meals","chinese":"自備飯餐"},{"english":"after lunch","chinese":"午膳後"},{"english":"debriefing session","chinese":"總結環節；匯報環節"},{"english":"during which","chinese":"在此期間"},{"english":"work in groups","chinese":"分組合作"},{"english":"discuss their observations","chinese":"討論他們的觀察"},{"english":"gain insights into","chinese":"深入了解……"},{"english":"Hong Kong's architecture","chinese":"香港建築"},{"english":"to proceed","chinese":"如要參加；為了辦理相關安排"},{"english":"complete and return","chinese":"填妥並交回"},{"english":"permission slip","chinese":"回條；同意書"},{"english":"attached to the letter","chinese":"附於信件內"},{"english":"Should you have any questions or concerns","chinese":"如有任何疑問或關注"},{"english":"questions or concerns","chinese":"疑問或關注"},{"english":"please do not hesitate to","chinese":"請隨時……"},{"english":"contact me at the school office","chinese":"透過學校辦公室聯絡我"},{"english":"Thank you for your cooperation","chinese":"感謝你們的合作"},{"english":"look forward to","chinese":"期待"},{"english":"an enriching and memorable trip","chinese":"一次充實而難忘的旅程"},{"english":"Yours sincerely","chinese":"此致"},{"english":"Class Teacher of 6A","chinese":"6A班主任"}]},"dse-writing-2018-part-b-q2":{"exerciseId":"dse-writing-2018-part-b-q2","essayKey":"","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=dse-writing-2018-part-b-q2","flashDeckId":"dse/writing/part-b/2018/Q2","paragraphs":[{"label":"Paragraph 1","english":"One Step, One Breath, One Finish Line","chinese":"一步，一口呼吸，一道終點線"},{"label":"Paragraph 2","english":"Have you ever looked at marathon runners on television and thought, “That could never be me”? I used to think exactly the same thing. Running 42.195 kilometres sounded like something for professional athletes, not ordinary young people with homework, exams, part-time jobs and alarm clocks we keep snoozing. Yet, a few weeks ago, I ran the Hong Kong Marathon for the first time. I was not the fastest runner, and neither was I the strongest of all. At one point, I was not even sure I was still sane. However, crossing that finish line changed the way I saw myself. It made me realise that the marathon is not just a race; in fact, it is a challenge that truly teaches young people courage, discipline and connection, and that is why I am writing this blog - to encourage you to sign up for the next one, no matter if you are nervous, inexperienced or full of doubts.","chinese":"你可曾在電視上看著馬拉松跑手，心裡想：「那個人絕不可能是我」？ 我以前也有過完全相同的想法。 跑完 42.195 公里聽起來像是專業運動員才會做的事，並非屬於那些要面對功課、考試、兼職，以及總是被我們一再按下貪睡模式鬧鐘的普通年輕人。 然而，幾個星期前，我第一次跑完了香港馬拉松。 我並非跑得最快的跑手，也絕不是眾人之中最強壯的一位。 在某一刻，我甚至不太確定自己是否還算清醒理智。 然而，衝過那道終點線，改變了我看待自己的方式。 它讓我明白，馬拉松不只是一場比賽；事實上，它是一項真正教會年輕人勇氣、紀律和連結感的挑戰，這也正是我寫下這篇網誌的原因——我希望鼓勵你報名參加下一屆香港馬拉松，無論你感到緊張、缺乏經驗，還是心中充滿懷疑。"},{"label":"Paragraph 3","english":"The first thing the marathon gave me was confidence that no classroom speech could have taught me. Before I started training, I could barely run three kilometres without bargaining with myself: “Just reach the next lamp post, then stop.” Slowly but surely, that lamp post became a park, the park became a promenade, and the promenade became a weekend long run. The more I trained, the more I understood that confidence does not arrive suddenly; in reality, it is built step by step, breath by breath. On race day, standing among thousands of runners before sunrise, I felt my stomach twist with fear. What if I cramped? What if I gave up? What if everyone else was better prepared? Then the starting signal sounded, and all I could do was move forward. By the time I reached the final stretch, my legs were heavy, but my mind was strangely clear. I had proved to myself that I could face something difficult without running away from it. For young people, especially those who often feel judged by marks, rankings and expectations, that lesson is priceless.","chinese":"馬拉松給我的第一樣東西，是任何課堂演講都無法教會我的自信。 在我開始訓練之前，我幾乎無法跑完三公里而不和自己討價還價：「只要跑到下一支燈柱，就可以停下來。」 慢慢地，也穩穩地，那支燈柱變成了一個公園，那個公園變成了一條海濱長廊，而那條海濱長廊又變成了週末的長跑訓練。 我訓練得越多，就越明白自信不會突然降臨；現實中，它是一個人一步一步、一口呼吸一口呼吸建立起來的。 比賽當日，日出之前，我站在成千上萬名跑手之中，緊張得胃部彷彿扭成一團 萬一我抽筋怎麼辦？ 萬一我放棄怎麼辦？ 萬一其他人都準備得比我更充分怎麼辦？ 然後，起跑信號響起，而我唯一能做的，就是向前跑。 當我抵達最後一段路時，我的雙腿沉重無比，但我的頭腦卻出奇地清晰。 我向自己證明了，我有能力面對困難，而不必從它面前逃開。 對年輕人來說，尤其是那些經常覺得自己被分數、排名和期望評價的人，這一課實在無價。"},{"label":"Paragraph 4","english":"The marathon also taught me that health goes beyond simply looking fit; health is about respecting your body and mind. During my training, I learnt to sleep earlier, drink more water and eat properly instead of surviving on snacks and endless excuses. More importantly, running became the best way to clear my head. Whenever schoolwork felt overwhelming, a short jog helped me breathe, think and return stronger. Of course, preparation is essential - you should not rush into a full marathon without training; otherwise, excitement may turn into injury. Start with short distances, join a running group, follow a sensible plan and listen to your body. There is no shame in walking for a while. There is no glory in ignoring pain. What matters is not pretending to be invincible, but becoming disciplined enough to improve safely.","chinese":"馬拉松也教會我，健康遠遠超出外表看起來健美這件事；健康的核心在於尊重自己的身體和心靈。 在訓練期間，我學會了早點睡覺、多喝水和好好進食，而不再靠零食和無止境的藉口勉強過日子。 更重要的是，跑步成為了我整理思緒的最佳方法。 每當功課壓得我喘不過氣時，一次短跑都能幫助我重新呼吸、思考，然後以更強大的狀態回來。 當然，準備是必不可少的——你不應在沒有訓練的情況下匆忙參加全程馬拉松，否則，興奮可能會變成傷患。 先從短距離開始，加入跑步小組，跟隨合理的訓練計劃，並聆聽身體的訊號 途中步行一會兒，並沒有甚麼可羞愧。 忽視痛楚，也沒有任何光榮可言。 真正重要的，並非假裝自己無堅不摧；重點在於培養足夠的紀律，讓自己能夠安全地進步。"},{"label":"Paragraph 5","english":"What surprised me most, however, was the sense of community. I had expected the marathon to be lonely - essentially, one runner, one road, one battle, but the experience proved me downright wrong. Volunteers handed out water with smiles as bright as medals. Strangers shouted, “Keep going!” as if they had known me for years. A runner beside me noticed I was slowing down and simply said, “One step at a time.” Those five words carried me for another kilometre. In that moment, Hong Kong felt far from rushed, impatient or distant, but generous. From teenagers in school team shirts to elderly runners still going strong, everyone seemed to be telling the same story - ordinary people can do extraordinary things when they simply refuse to quit.","chinese":"然而，最令我驚訝的，是那份社群感。 我原本以為馬拉松會很孤獨——本質上就是一個跑手、一條道路、一場戰鬥；但這次經歷徹底證明我錯了。 義工派發清水時，臉上的笑容像獎牌一樣閃亮。 陌生人大喊著：「繼續跑！」彷彿他們已經認識我多年。 我身旁的一位跑手留意到我正在慢下來，只是簡單地說了一句：「一步一步來。」 那五個字支撐著我又跑了一公里。 在那一刻，香港給我的感覺一點也不匆忙、不急躁，也不疏離，反倒充滿慷慨與溫度。 從穿著校隊 T 恤的青少年，到仍然精神抖擻向前跑的年長跑手，每個人似乎都在訴說同一個故事——只要普通人拒絕放棄，也可以完成不平凡的事。"},{"label":"Paragraph 6","english":"So, should you join the next Hong Kong Marathon? My answer is a resounding yes. Join not because you are already perfect, but because you are willing to begin. Join not because it will be easy, but because difficult things often make us better people. Ask a friend to train with you. Make room in your schedule. Register when the opportunity comes. Then, on race day, when your shoes hit the road and the city wakes around you, you may discover what I discovered - the finish line is not where the journey ends; it is where a braver version of yourself has just begun.","chinese":"所以，你應該參加下一屆香港馬拉松嗎？ 我的答案是非常肯定的：應該。 參加吧，並非因為你已經完美，原因在於你願意開始。 參加吧，並非因為它會容易，原因在於困難的事情往往會讓我們成為更好的人 邀請一位朋友和你一起訓練。 在你的時間表中騰出空間。 當機會來臨時，就報名參加。 然後，在比賽當日，當你的跑鞋踏上道路，而城市在你身邊逐漸醒來時，你也許會發現我曾經發現的事——終點線並非旅程結束的地方；它是一個更勇敢的自己剛剛開始的地方。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"one step, one breath, one finish line","chinese":"一步、一口氣、一條終點線"},{"english":"finish line","chinese":"終點線"},{"english":"have you ever looked at","chinese":"你有沒有看過"},{"english":"marathon runners","chinese":"馬拉松跑手"},{"english":"That could never be me","chinese":"那永遠不可能是我"},{"english":"used to think","chinese":"以前常常認為"},{"english":"exactly the same thing","chinese":"完全一樣的想法"},{"english":"sounded like something for","chinese":"聽起來像是……才會做的事"},{"english":"professional athletes","chinese":"職業運動員"},{"english":"ordinary young people","chinese":"普通年輕人"},{"english":"part-time jobs","chinese":"兼職工作"},{"english":"keep snoozing","chinese":"不斷按鬧鐘延後"},{"english":"for the first time","chinese":"第一次"},{"english":"neither was I","chinese":"我也不是"},{"english":"at one point","chinese":"有一刻；某一刻"},{"english":"not even sure","chinese":"甚至不確定"},{"english":"still sane","chinese":"仍然神志清醒"},{"english":"crossing that finish line","chinese":"衝過那條終點線"},{"english":"change the way I saw myself","chinese":"改變我看待自己的方式"},{"english":"make me realise that","chinese":"令我明白"},{"english":"not just a race","chinese":"不只是一場比賽"},{"english":"in fact","chinese":"事實上"},{"english":"truly teach young people","chinese":"真正教會年輕人"},{"english":"courage, discipline and connection","chinese":"勇氣、紀律和連結"},{"english":"encourage you to sign up for","chinese":"鼓勵你報名參加"},{"english":"no matter whether","chinese":"無論是否"},{"english":"full of doubts","chinese":"充滿疑慮"},{"english":"the first thing","chinese":"第一樣東西"},{"english":"confidence that no classroom speech could have taught me","chinese":"課堂演講教不到的自信"},{"english":"start training","chinese":"開始訓練"},{"english":"could barely run","chinese":"幾乎跑不了"},{"english":"bargain with myself","chinese":"跟自己討價還價"},{"english":"reach the next lamp post","chinese":"跑到下一支燈柱"},{"english":"slowly but surely","chinese":"慢慢但穩步地"},{"english":"weekend long run","chinese":"週末長課；週末長跑訓練"},{"english":"the more..., the more...","chinese":"越……就越……"},{"english":"arrive suddenly","chinese":"突然出現"},{"english":"built step by step","chinese":"一步一步建立"},{"english":"breath by breath","chinese":"一口氣一口氣地"},{"english":"on race day","chinese":"比賽當日"},{"english":"stand among thousands of runners","chinese":"站在數千名跑手之中"},{"english":"before sunrise","chinese":"日出前"},{"english":"stomach twist with fear","chinese":"緊張得胃部一縮"},{"english":"What if...?","chinese":"如果……怎麼辦"},{"english":"cramp","chinese":"抽筋"},{"english":"give up","chinese":"放棄"},{"english":"better prepared","chinese":"準備得更好"},{"english":"the starting signal sounded","chinese":"起步訊號響起"},{"english":"move forward","chinese":"向前走；向前跑"},{"english":"by the time","chinese":"到……的時候"},{"english":"final stretch","chinese":"最後一段路"},{"english":"legs were heavy","chinese":"雙腿沉重"},{"english":"strangely clear","chinese":"異常清晰"},{"english":"prove to myself that","chinese":"向自己證明"},{"english":"face something difficult","chinese":"面對困難的事"},{"english":"without running away from it","chinese":"而不是逃避它"},{"english":"feel judged by","chinese":"感到被……評價"},{"english":"marks, rankings and expectations","chinese":"分數、排名和期望"},{"english":"that lesson is priceless","chinese":"那個教訓十分寶貴"},{"english":"health goes beyond","chinese":"健康不止於"},{"english":"looking fit","chinese":"看起來健美"},{"english":"respect your body and mind","chinese":"尊重自己的身體和心靈"},{"english":"sleep earlier","chinese":"早點睡"},{"english":"eat properly","chinese":"好好進食"},{"english":"survive on","chinese":"靠……勉強過活"},{"english":"endless excuses","chinese":"沒完沒了的藉口"},{"english":"clear my head","chinese":"令頭腦清醒"},{"english":"schoolwork felt overwhelming","chinese":"課業令人不勝負荷"},{"english":"short jog","chinese":"短跑；慢跑一會"},{"english":"return stronger","chinese":"以更好的狀態回來"},{"english":"preparation is essential","chinese":"準備是必要的"},{"english":"rush into","chinese":"倉促投入"},{"english":"full marathon","chinese":"全程馬拉松"},{"english":"excitement may turn into injury","chinese":"興奮可能變成受傷"},{"english":"start with short distances","chinese":"從短距離開始"},{"english":"join a running group","chinese":"加入跑步小組"},{"english":"follow a sensible plan","chinese":"跟從合理的計劃"},{"english":"listen to your body","chinese":"聆聽身體的訊號"},{"english":"no shame in","chinese":"……並不羞恥"},{"english":"walking for a while","chinese":"走一會兒"},{"english":"no glory in","chinese":"……並不光榮"},{"english":"ignoring pain","chinese":"無視痛楚"},{"english":"what matters is not..., but...","chinese":"重要的不是……而是……"},{"english":"pretend to be invincible","chinese":"假裝自己無敵"},{"english":"disciplined enough to","chinese":"有足夠紀律去"},{"english":"improve safely","chinese":"安全地進步"},{"english":"what surprised me most","chinese":"最令我驚訝的是"},{"english":"sense of community","chinese":"社群感；社區連結感"},{"english":"expect something to be lonely","chinese":"以為……會很孤單"},{"english":"one runner, one road, one battle","chinese":"一個跑手、一條路、一場戰鬥"},{"english":"prove someone downright wrong","chinese":"證明某人完全錯了"},{"english":"hand out water","chinese":"派發水"},{"english":"as bright as medals","chinese":"像獎牌一樣耀眼"},{"english":"shout encouragement","chinese":"大聲打氣"},{"english":"Keep going","chinese":"繼續加油"},{"english":"as if they had known me for years","chinese":"好像認識我多年一樣"},{"english":"notice I was slowing down","chinese":"留意到我正在慢下來"},{"english":"one step at a time","chinese":"一步一步來"},{"english":"carry me for another kilometre","chinese":"支撐我再跑一公里"},{"english":"in that moment","chinese":"在那一刻"},{"english":"far from","chinese":"絕不是；遠非"},{"english":"rushed, impatient or distant","chinese":"匆忙、不耐煩或疏離"},{"english":"teenagers in school team shirts","chinese":"穿校隊衫的青少年"},{"english":"elderly runners still going strong","chinese":"仍然精力充沛的年長跑手"},{"english":"going strong","chinese":"仍然很有活力"},{"english":"tell the same story","chinese":"訴說同一個故事"},{"english":"ordinary people can do extraordinary things","chinese":"普通人也能做出非凡的事"},{"english":"refuse to quit","chinese":"拒絕放棄"},{"english":"a resounding yes","chinese":"一個響亮的「是」"},{"english":"not because..., but because...","chinese":"不是因為……而是因為……"},{"english":"willing to begin","chinese":"願意開始"},{"english":"difficult things often make us better people","chinese":"困難的事往往令我們成為更好的人"},{"english":"ask a friend to train with you","chinese":"邀請朋友一起訓練"},{"english":"make room in your schedule","chinese":"在日程中騰出時間"},{"english":"register when the opportunity comes","chinese":"有機會時就報名"},{"english":"on race day","chinese":"比賽當日"},{"english":"shoes hit the road","chinese":"鞋踏上路面"},{"english":"the city wakes around you","chinese":"城市在你身邊醒來"},{"english":"discover what I discovered","chinese":"發現我所發現的事"},{"english":"where the journey ends","chinese":"旅程結束的地方"},{"english":"a braver version of yourself","chinese":"更勇敢的自己"},{"english":"has just begun","chinese":"才剛剛開始"}]},"dse-writing-2018-part-b-q3":{"exerciseId":"dse-writing-2018-part-b-q3","essayKey":"","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=dse-writing-2018-part-b-q3","flashDeckId":"dse/writing/part-b/2018/Q3","paragraphs":[{"label":"Paragraph 1","english":"Protecting Our Time, Protecting Our Team","chinese":"保護我們的時間，守護我們的團隊"},{"label":"Paragraph 2","english":"Reboot Online Company","chinese":"Reboot Online 公司 作為 Reboot Online 公司的董事總經理，我嚴肅看待這些憂慮，因為它們觸及我們一直聲稱要建立的職場核心。 Reboot Online Company"},{"label":"Paragraph 3","english":"9 April 2018","chinese":""},{"label":"Paragraph 4","english":"Dear colleagues,","chinese":"各位同事："},{"label":"Paragraph 5","english":"Re: New guidelines on after-hours work messages","chinese":"主旨：有關辦公時間以外工作訊息的新指引"},{"label":"Paragraph 6","english":"Over the past fortnight, I have received several thoughtful complaints about the number of work-related emails and text messages reaching staff after office hours. As Managing Director of Reboot Online Company, I take these concerns seriously because they go to the heart of the workplace we claim to be. As projects move across time zones, some of us have begun sending updates late at night or during weekends. This has made the company consider introducing clearer communication rules in order to protect rest, reduce unnecessary pressure and sustain high-quality work. Let me be clear to everyone - our success must never come at the cost of your health, family life or personal time.","chinese":"Reboot Online 公司 在過去兩星期，我收到數宗認真而具建設性的投訴，內容關於員工在辦公時間以外收到過多與工作相關的電郵和文字訊息。 作為 Reboot Online 公司的董事總經理，我嚴肅看待這些憂慮，因為它們觸及我們一直聲稱要建立的職場核心。 隨著項目跨越不同時區進行，我們當中有人開始在深夜或週末發送工作更新 這使公司開始考慮引入更清晰的溝通規則，以保障休息、減少不必要的壓力，並維持高質素的工作表現。 請容許我向各位清楚說明——我們的成功絕不能以你們的健康、家庭生活或私人時間作為代價。 董事總經理 Reboot Online Company"},{"label":"Paragraph 7","english":"First, I want to acknowledge the problem plainly. It is easy to say that “just one quick email” does no harm; the reality is that a string of small interruptions can turn an evening into another work session. By the time a designer has answered one message, checked an attachment and clarified a deadline, private time has already been swallowed by work. Some colleagues may be caring for children or elderly parents; others may simply need dinner without a phone flashing beside them. If a system leaves people anxious whenever a notification appears, it is not efficient; it is unhealthy. I hear you, and I apologise that this issue was not addressed earlier.","chinese":"首先，我想坦率承認這個問題。 我們很容易說「只是一封很快處理的電郵」並無害處；現實卻是，一連串細小的打擾可以把一個晚上變成另一段工作時間。 到一位設計師回覆了一則訊息、檢查了一個附件並釐清了一個截止日期時，私人時間已經被工作吞噬了。 有些同事可能正在照顧孩子或年邁父母；另一些同事也許只是需要吃一頓沒有手機在旁邊閃動的晚餐。 如果一個制度令人在每次通知出現時都感到焦慮，那就談不上有效率；它是不健康的。 我明白你們的感受，也為公司沒有更早處理這個問題而道歉。"},{"label":"Paragraph 8","english":"From 1 May, Reboot Online will adopt an “after-hours communication policy”. Unless a matter is genuinely urgent, staff should not send work emails, WhatsApp messages or platform notifications between 7.30 p.m. and 8.30 a.m. on weekdays, or during weekends and public holidays. Instead, messages should be scheduled for the next working morning. More importantly, employees are not expected to read or reply to non-urgent messages outside office hours. No manager may treat a delayed after-hours response as a lack of commitment. An urgent matter means a live client-system failure, a security risk, a legal deadline within 24 hours, or an operational issue that would cause serious damage if left until morning. Anything else, however important it may feel at midnight, must wait.","chinese":"由5月1日起，Reboot Online 將採納「辦公時間以外溝通政策」。 除非事情真正緊急，否則員工不應在平日晚上7時30分至翌日上午8時30分之間，或在週末及公眾假期期間，發送工作電郵、WhatsApp 訊息或平台通知。 相反，訊息應設定在下一個工作天早上發送。 更重要的是，員工無需在辦公時間以外閱讀或回覆非緊急訊息。 任何經理都不得把員工延遲回覆辦公時間以外訊息，視為缺乏投入。 緊急事項是指客戶系統即時故障、安全風險、24小時內屆滿的法律期限，或若留待早上才處理便會造成嚴重損害的營運問題。 其他任何事情，無論在午夜時感覺多麼重要，都必須等待。"},{"label":"Paragraph 9","english":"Second, we will improve communication during office hours so that fewer matters spill over into private time. Each department will set aside two fixed windows for project updates, so information is shared in batches. Email subject lines should state the action required, the deadline and the urgency. “For approval by Friday 4 p.m.” is far better than “Quick question”. Managers should also distinguish between “for information”, “for discussion” and “for action”. Such simple practices will reduce confusion, prevent duplication and give everyone more breathing room. Put simply, clear messages make for calmer teams.","chinese":"第二，我們會改善辦公時間內的溝通，好讓較少事情外溢到私人時間。 每個部門將預留兩個固定時段作項目更新，使資訊能夠分批分享。 電郵標題應列明所需行動、截止日期和緊急程度。 「請於星期五下午4時前批核」遠比「簡單一問」更清楚。 經理也應區分「供參考」、「供討論」和「需行動」三類訊息。 這些簡單做法將減少混亂、防止重複工作，並給予每個人更多喘息空間。 簡單來說，清晰的訊息有助於建立更從容的團隊。"},{"label":"Paragraph 10","english":"Third, we will review workloads, not merely message habits. If staff are contacting one another late at night because deadlines are unrealistic, the problem is not so much communication as planning. Department heads will review project timelines every Monday and identify tasks that can be postponed, reassigned or simplified. Human Resources will also open a confidential channel for reporting repeated after-hours contact. This is not meant to punish honest mistakes; rather, it is a way to notice patterns before they become a culture.","chinese":"第三，我們會檢視工作量，而不只檢視訊息習慣。 如果員工因截止日期不切實際而在深夜互相聯絡，問題與其說在於溝通，毋寧說在於規劃。 部門主管將於每週一檢視項目時間表，並找出可以延後、重新分配或簡化的工作。 人力資源部也會開設保密渠道，讓員工匯報重複出現的辦公時間以外聯絡情況 這並非旨在懲罰真誠的錯誤；更準確地說，這是一種在問題變成文化之前及早察覺模式的方法。"},{"label":"Paragraph 11","english":"I ask all staff, especially managers, to help us make this policy work. Use scheduled sending. Think twice before marking a message urgent. Respect your colleagues’ silence after work. Should a true emergency arise, call the responsible department head first so that one person can coordinate the response instead of disturbing an entire team.","chinese":"我請求所有員工，尤其是管理人員，協助我們使這項政策真正發揮作用。 請使用定時發送功能。 在把訊息標記為緊急之前，請三思。 請尊重同事下班後的安靜時間。 如果真的出現緊急情況，請先致電負責的部門主管，好讓一人統籌回應，而無需打擾整個團隊。"},{"label":"Paragraph 12","english":"Reboot Online has come a long way because of your professionalism and resilience. Yet the core of leadership lies in creating the desirable conditions in which good people can continue doing good work. The time has come to draw a healthier line between working hard and being permanently available. I will review this arrangement after one month and share the findings with all staff. Thank you for raising the issue honestly, and thank you in advance for helping us build a more respectful, focused and sustainable workplace.","chinese":"Reboot Online 能走到今天，很大程度上有賴你們的專業精神和韌性。 然而，領導的核心在於創造理想條件，讓優秀的人能夠繼續做好工作。 現在是時候在努力工作與長期隨時候命之間劃出一條更健康的界線。 我會在一個月後檢討這項安排，並與全體員工分享結果。 感謝你們坦誠提出這個問題，也預先感謝大家協助我們建立一個更互相尊重、更專注和更可持續的工作環境。"},{"label":"Paragraph 13","english":"Yours sincerely,","chinese":"謹啟，"},{"label":"Paragraph 14","english":"Chris Wong","chinese":"Chris Wong"},{"label":"Paragraph 15","english":"Managing Director","chinese":"作為 Reboot Online 公司的董事總經理，我嚴肅看待這些憂慮，因為它們觸及我們一直聲稱要建立的職場核心。 董事總經理"},{"label":"Paragraph 16","english":"Reboot Online Company","chinese":"Reboot Online 公司 作為 Reboot Online 公司的董事總經理，我嚴肅看待這些憂慮，因為它們觸及我們一直聲稱要建立的職場核心。 Reboot Online Company"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"protecting our time","chinese":"保護我們的時間"},{"english":"protecting our team","chinese":"保護我們的團隊"},{"english":"new guidelines","chinese":"新指引"},{"english":"after-hours work messages","chinese":"下班後工作訊息"},{"english":"over the past fortnight","chinese":"在過去兩星期"},{"english":"thoughtful complaints","chinese":"經深思熟慮的投訴；有建設性的意見"},{"english":"work-related emails","chinese":"與工作有關的電郵"},{"english":"text messages","chinese":"短訊"},{"english":"reaching staff","chinese":"傳到職員那裏"},{"english":"after office hours","chinese":"辦公時間後"},{"english":"Managing Director","chinese":"董事總經理"},{"english":"take these concerns seriously","chinese":"認真看待這些憂慮"},{"english":"go to the heart of","chinese":"觸及……的核心"},{"english":"the workplace we claim to be","chinese":"我們聲稱要建立的工作場所"},{"english":"move across time zones","chinese":"跨越不同時區"},{"english":"sending updates","chinese":"發送最新進度"},{"english":"late at night","chinese":"深夜"},{"english":"during weekends","chinese":"週末期間"},{"english":"led the company to consider","chinese":"促使公司考慮"},{"english":"introducing clearer communication rules","chinese":"推出更清晰的溝通規則"},{"english":"in order to","chinese":"為了"},{"english":"protect rest","chinese":"保障休息時間"},{"english":"reduce unnecessary pressure","chinese":"減少不必要壓力"},{"english":"sustain high-quality work","chinese":"維持高質素工作"},{"english":"let me be clear","chinese":"讓我說清楚"},{"english":"come at the cost of","chinese":"以犧牲……為代價"},{"english":"family life","chinese":"家庭生活"},{"english":"personal time","chinese":"私人時間"},{"english":"acknowledge the problem plainly","chinese":"坦率承認問題"},{"english":"just one quick email","chinese":"只是一封簡短電郵"},{"english":"does no harm","chinese":"沒有害處；無傷大雅"},{"english":"the reality is that","chinese":"現實是"},{"english":"a string of small interruptions","chinese":"一連串小干擾"},{"english":"turn an evening into","chinese":"把一個晚上變成"},{"english":"another work session","chinese":"另一段工作時間"},{"english":"by the time","chinese":"到……的時候"},{"english":"answered one message","chinese":"回覆了一個訊息"},{"english":"checked an attachment","chinese":"查看附件"},{"english":"clarified a deadline","chinese":"釐清截止日期"},{"english":"private time","chinese":"私人時間"},{"english":"swallowed by work","chinese":"被工作吞噬"},{"english":"caring for children","chinese":"照顧小朋友"},{"english":"elderly parents","chinese":"年邁父母"},{"english":"flashing beside them","chinese":"在旁邊閃亮"},{"english":"leaves people anxious","chinese":"令人感到焦慮"},{"english":"whenever a notification appears","chinese":"每當通知出現時"},{"english":"it is not efficient; it is unhealthy","chinese":"這不是高效，而是不健康"},{"english":"I hear you","chinese":"我聽到你們的意見"},{"english":"apologise that","chinese":"為……道歉"},{"english":"addressed earlier","chinese":"更早處理"},{"english":"from 1 May","chinese":"自5月1日起"},{"english":"adopt a policy","chinese":"採用一項政策"},{"english":"after-hours communication policy","chinese":"下班後溝通政策"},{"english":"unless a matter is genuinely urgent","chinese":"除非事情真正緊急"},{"english":"genuinely urgent","chinese":"真正緊急"},{"english":"work emails","chinese":"工作電郵"},{"english":"WhatsApp messages","chinese":"WhatsApp 訊息"},{"english":"platform notifications","chinese":"平台通知"},{"english":"between 7.30 p.m. and 8.30 a.m.","chinese":"晚上7時半至早上8時半之間"},{"english":"on weekdays","chinese":"在平日"},{"english":"public holidays","chinese":"公眾假期"},{"english":"scheduled for","chinese":"安排在……發送"},{"english":"the next working morning","chinese":"下一個工作天早上"},{"english":"more importantly","chinese":"更重要的是"},{"english":"are not expected to","chinese":"毋須；不被期望"},{"english":"read or reply to","chinese":"閱讀或回覆"},{"english":"non-urgent messages","chinese":"非緊急訊息"},{"english":"outside office hours","chinese":"辦公時間以外"},{"english":"treat something as","chinese":"把……視為"},{"english":"delayed after-hours response","chinese":"下班後延遲回覆"},{"english":"lack of commitment","chinese":"缺乏承擔"},{"english":"urgent matter","chinese":"緊急事項"},{"english":"live client-system failure","chinese":"正在運作的客戶系統故障"},{"english":"security risk","chinese":"保安風險"},{"english":"legal deadline within 24 hours","chinese":"24小時內的法律期限"},{"english":"operational issue","chinese":"營運問題"},{"english":"cause serious damage","chinese":"造成嚴重損害"},{"english":"if left until morning","chinese":"如果留到早上才處理"},{"english":"anything else","chinese":"其他任何事情"},{"english":"however important it may feel","chinese":"不論當下感覺多重要"},{"english":"must wait","chinese":"必須等待"},{"english":"improve communication","chinese":"改善溝通"},{"english":"during office hours","chinese":"在辦公時間內"},{"english":"spill over into","chinese":"延伸至；蔓延到"},{"english":"private time","chinese":"私人時間"},{"english":"set aside","chinese":"預留"},{"english":"fixed windows","chinese":"固定時段"},{"english":"project updates","chinese":"項目最新進度"},{"english":"shared in batches","chinese":"分批分享"},{"english":"email subject lines","chinese":"電郵主旨"},{"english":"state the action required","chinese":"說明所需行動"},{"english":"the deadline and the urgency","chinese":"截止日期和緊急程度"},{"english":"for approval by Friday 4 p.m.","chinese":"於星期五下午4時前批核"},{"english":"far better than","chinese":"遠比……好"},{"english":"distinguish between","chinese":"區分"},{"english":"for information","chinese":"供參考"},{"english":"for discussion","chinese":"供討論"},{"english":"for action","chinese":"需要行動"},{"english":"such simple practices","chinese":"這些簡單做法"},{"english":"reduce confusion","chinese":"減少混亂"},{"english":"prevent duplication","chinese":"避免重複"},{"english":"breathing room","chinese":"喘息空間"},{"english":"put simply","chinese":"簡單來說"},{"english":"make for calmer teams","chinese":"有助團隊更冷靜"},{"english":"review workloads","chinese":"檢視工作量"},{"english":"not merely","chinese":"不只是"},{"english":"message habits","chinese":"發訊習慣"},{"english":"contacting one another","chinese":"彼此聯絡"},{"english":"deadlines are unrealistic","chinese":"截止日期不切實際"},{"english":"not so much… as…","chinese":"與其說是……不如說是……"},{"english":"department heads","chinese":"部門主管"},{"english":"project timelines","chinese":"項目時間表"},{"english":"identify tasks","chinese":"找出任務"},{"english":"be postponed","chinese":"被延後"},{"english":"be reassigned","chinese":"被重新分配"},{"english":"be simplified","chinese":"被簡化"},{"english":"Human Resources","chinese":"人力資源部"},{"english":"confidential channel","chinese":"保密渠道"},{"english":"reporting repeated after-hours contact","chinese":"匯報多次下班後聯絡"},{"english":"meant to punish","chinese":"旨在懲罰"},{"english":"honest mistakes","chinese":"無心之失"},{"english":"rather","chinese":"而是"},{"english":"notice patterns","chinese":"察覺模式"},{"english":"become a culture","chinese":"變成一種文化"},{"english":"make this policy work","chinese":"令這項政策奏效"},{"english":"scheduled sending","chinese":"預約發送"},{"english":"think twice before","chinese":"三思而後"},{"english":"marking a message urgent","chinese":"將訊息標記為緊急"},{"english":"respect your colleagues' silence","chinese":"尊重同事的安靜時間"},{"english":"after work","chinese":"下班後"},{"english":"should a true emergency arise","chinese":"如真正緊急情況發生"},{"english":"responsible department head","chinese":"相關部門主管"},{"english":"coordinate the response","chinese":"協調應對"},{"english":"instead of disturbing","chinese":"而不是打擾"},{"english":"an entire team","chinese":"整個團隊"},{"english":"come a long way","chinese":"取得長足進步"},{"english":"professionalism and resilience","chinese":"專業精神和韌性"},{"english":"the core of leadership","chinese":"領導的核心"},{"english":"lies in","chinese":"在於"},{"english":"the right conditions","chinese":"合適條件"},{"english":"continue doing good work","chinese":"繼續做好工作"},{"english":"the time has come to","chinese":"是時候"},{"english":"draw a healthier line","chinese":"劃下更健康的界線"},{"english":"working hard","chinese":"努力工作"},{"english":"permanently available","chinese":"永遠待命"},{"english":"review this arrangement","chinese":"檢討這項安排"},{"english":"after one month","chinese":"一個月後"},{"english":"share the findings","chinese":"分享結果"},{"english":"raising the issue honestly","chinese":"坦誠提出問題"},{"english":"thank you in advance","chinese":"預先感謝"},{"english":"respectful, focused and sustainable workplace","chinese":"互相尊重、專注而可持續的工作場所"},{"english":"Yours sincerely","chinese":"謹啟；此致"},{"english":"Managing Director","chinese":"董事總經理"}]},"dse-writing-2018-part-b-q4":{"exerciseId":"dse-writing-2018-part-b-q4","essayKey":"","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=dse-writing-2018-part-b-q4","flashDeckId":"dse/writing/part-b/2018/Q4","paragraphs":[{"label":"Paragraph 1","english":"When a Dream Meets a Door Dear J.C.,","chinese":"當夢想遇上一扇門 親愛的 J.C.："},{"label":"Paragraph 2","english":"Thank you for writing to Teen. First, take a breath. When your parents said no, it must have felt as if they were shutting a door you had been walking towards for years. It is easy to see why you feel frustrated - you are not asking for a new phone or a weekend outing; you are talking about a future that matters to you. Still, their first reaction does not have to be the final answer. The way I see it, your aim now is not to win an argument overnight, but to turn your love for animals into a calm, realistic plan your parents can respect.","chinese":"謝謝你寫信給《Teen》。 首先，先深呼吸一下。 當你的父母說不可以時，那感覺一定像是他們把一扇你多年來一直走向的門關上了。 你感到沮喪是很容易理解的——你想要的並非一部新手機，也並非一次週末外出；你談論的是一個對你而言十分重要的未來。 即使如此，他們的第一個反應並不一定要成為最後答案。 在我看來，你現在的目標並非一夜之間贏得一場爭辯，重點在於把你對動物的熱愛轉化成一個冷靜、現實，而且能讓父母尊重的計劃。"},{"label":"Paragraph 3","english":"The first thing to do is to understand what their “no” actually means. Are they worried that becoming a vet is too difficult, too expensive, too competitive, or too emotionally demanding? Do they think you only like playing with pets, whereas veterinary work also involves studying biology, treating sick animals, speaking to anxious owners and sometimes making painful decisions? If you argue before you know the real reason, you may end up fighting the wrong battle. Choose a quiet time and say, “I hear you, but could you help me understand what worries you most?” This sentence matters because it shows respect without surrendering your dream. Parents, more often than not, say “no” quickly when they are afraid. If you can hear the fear beneath the refusal, you can answer it more intelligently.","chinese":"第一件要做的事，是了解他們那個「不可以」實際上代表甚麼。 他們是否擔心成為獸醫太困難、太昂貴、競爭太激烈，或者在情感上要求太高？ 他們是否覺得你只是喜歡和寵物玩耍，然而獸醫工作同時涉及研讀生物學、治療生病的動物、與焦急的主人溝通，有時還要作出令人難受的決定？ 如果你在知道真正原因之前就開始爭辯，你最後可能會打錯一場仗。 選一個安靜的時間，然後說：「我明白你的想法，但你可否幫我理解你最擔心的是甚麼？」 這句話很重要，因為它顯示尊重，同時沒有放棄你的夢想。 很多時候，父母在害怕時會很快說「不可以」。 如果你能聽見拒絕背後的恐懼，你就能以更聰明的方式回應。"},{"label":"Paragraph 4","english":"After that, show them evidence, not emotion alone. Loving animals is a beautiful beginning, but it is not enough by itself. You need to demonstrate that you understand both the charm and the burden of the profession. Make a simple career folder. In it, include the subjects you may need, possible university courses, entry requirements, estimated costs, scholarships, related jobs such as veterinary nursing or animal welfare work, and the daily duties of a vet. Better still, try to gain experience. Volunteer at an animal shelter, help at a pet adoption event, interview a local vet, or join a biology-related activity at school. Take caring for an injured stray cat, for example: feeding it is kind, but noticing symptoms, keeping records, cleaning responsibly and asking an expert for help show maturity. When your parents see that you are willing to wake up early, clean cages, read science texts and face unpleasant realities, their impression may change from “J.C. likes animals” to “J.C. is becoming someone disciplined enough to work with animals.”, and remember, that shift is really powerful.","chinese":"之後，向他們展示證據，不要只展示情緒。 熱愛動物是一個美好的開始，但單靠這一點並不足夠。 你需要證明自己同時明白這個職業的吸引之處和沉重之處。 製作一份簡單的職業資料夾。 在裡面放入你可能需要修讀的科目、可考慮的大學課程、入學要求、預計費用、獎學金、相關工作，如獸醫護理或動物福利工作，以及獸醫的日常職責 更理想的是，嘗試累積實際經驗。 你可以到動物收容所做義工、協助寵物領養活動、訪問一位本地獸醫，或者參加學校裏與生物學相關的活動。 以照顧一隻受傷的流浪貓為例：餵牠固然是善良的表現，但能留意症狀、保存紀錄、負責任地清潔，並向專家求助，才更能顯示成熟。 當你的父母看見你願意早起、清潔籠子、閱讀科學文本，並面對令人不舒服的現實時，他們對你的印象可能會從「J.C. 喜歡動物」轉變成「J.C. 正在成為一個有足夠紀律與動物工作的年輕人。」 而且請記住，這種轉變真的很有力量"},{"label":"Paragraph 5","english":"At the same time, be prepared to compromise without giving up. You could ask your parents for a three-month trial period: you continue working hard at school, do some supervised animal-related volunteering, and then sit down together to review what you have learned. This gives them breathing room and gives you a fair chance. You may also wish to ask a teacher, careers adviser, relative or family friend to join one conversation, not to pressure your parents, but to make the discussion less emotional. However, do not make the mistake of presenting your dream as “vet or nothing”. If veterinary medicine proves unsuitable later, your love for animals could still lead to animal science, conservation, research, pet nutrition, animal-assisted therapy or charity work. Knowing these alternatives does not weaken your ambition; if anything, it makes your plan safer and more mature. Only by showing that you have thought about risks can you earn the freedom to pursue the possibility.","chinese":"同時，你要準備好作出妥協，但不要放棄。 你可以向父母提出一個三個月的試行期：你繼續在學校努力讀書，做一些有監督的動物相關義工服務，然後大家坐下來，一起檢視你學到了甚麼。 這能給他們一點喘息空間，也給你一個公平的機會。 你也可以考慮邀請一位老師、升學就業顧問、親戚或家庭朋友參與一次對話；目的並非向你的父母施壓，重點是讓討論少一點情緒化。 然而，不要犯下把你的夢想說成「要麼做獸醫，要麼甚麼都不要」這個錯誤 如果日後證明獸醫學並不適合你，你對動物的熱愛仍然可以引領你走向動物科學、保育、研究、寵物營養、動物輔助治療或慈善工作。 了解這些其他出路並不會削弱你的志向；真要說，這反而會讓你的計劃更安全，也更成熟。 只有透過展示你已經思考過風險，你才可以贏得追求這個可能性的自由。"},{"label":"Paragraph 6","english":"Finally, please remember this: a parent’s first “no” can hurt, but it is not a verdict on your whole future. Stand firm, but stay gracious. Prepare well, speak respectfully, listen carefully and let your actions do part of the talking. The more responsible you become, the harder it will be for anyone to dismiss your dream as childish. Start with one conversation, one piece of research and one practical experience. Little by little, your dream will either grow stronger or become clearer in a different shape. Either way, you will not be lost. You will be learning how to build a future that truly belongs to your confident self.","chinese":"最後，請記住這一點：父母最初的一句「不可以」可能會令人受傷，但這並不等同於對你整個未來下判決。 立場要堅定，但態度要保持溫和有禮。 好好準備，尊重地說話，仔細地聆聽，也讓你的行動替你說一部分話。 你變得越負責任，別人就越難把你的夢想當成幼稚的想法來否定。 先從一次對話、一份資料搜集和一次實際經驗開始。 一點一點地，你的夢想要麼會變得更堅定，要麼會以另一種形式變得更清晰 無論哪一種情況，你都不會迷失方向。 你將會學習如何建立一個真正屬於那個更有自信的自己的未來。"},{"label":"Paragraph 7","english":"Warmly,","chinese":"溫暖地祝福你，"},{"label":"Paragraph 8","english":"Teen Advice Column","chinese":"建議專欄"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"when a dream meets a door","chinese":"當夢想遇上阻礙"},{"english":"thank you for writing to","chinese":"感謝你寫信給……"},{"english":"take a breath","chinese":"深呼吸；先冷靜下來"},{"english":"it must have felt as if","chinese":"一定感覺好像"},{"english":"shut a door","chinese":"關上一扇門"},{"english":"walk towards something for years","chinese":"多年來一直朝着……走"},{"english":"it is easy to see why","chinese":"不難理解為甚麼"},{"english":"feel frustrated","chinese":"感到沮喪"},{"english":"a weekend outing","chinese":"週末外出活動"},{"english":"a future that matters to you","chinese":"對你重要的未來"},{"english":"their first reaction","chinese":"他們的第一反應"},{"english":"the final answer","chinese":"最終答案"},{"english":"the way I see it","chinese":"在我看來"},{"english":"win an argument overnight","chinese":"一夜之間贏得爭論"},{"english":"turn your love for animals into","chinese":"把你對動物的熱愛轉化為……"},{"english":"a calm, realistic plan","chinese":"冷靜而實際的計劃"},{"english":"respect a plan","chinese":"尊重一個計劃"},{"english":"the first thing to do","chinese":"第一件要做的事"},{"english":"what their “no” actually means","chinese":"他們說「不」真正代表甚麼"},{"english":"becoming a vet","chinese":"成為獸醫"},{"english":"too emotionally demanding","chinese":"情感負擔太重"},{"english":"playing with pets","chinese":"和寵物玩耍"},{"english":"whereas","chinese":"然而；但是"},{"english":"veterinary work","chinese":"獸醫工作"},{"english":"involve studying biology","chinese":"涉及學習生物"},{"english":"treating sick animals","chinese":"治療生病動物"},{"english":"anxious owners","chinese":"焦急的主人"},{"english":"make painful decisions","chinese":"作出痛苦的決定"},{"english":"the real reason","chinese":"真正原因"},{"english":"end up fighting the wrong battle","chinese":"最終打錯仗；爭錯焦點"},{"english":"choose a quiet time","chinese":"選一個安靜的時間"},{"english":"I hear you","chinese":"我明白你的意思"},{"english":"help me understand","chinese":"幫我明白"},{"english":"what worries you most","chinese":"你最擔心的是甚麼"},{"english":"show respect","chinese":"表示尊重"},{"english":"without surrendering your dream","chinese":"不放棄夢想"},{"english":"more often than not","chinese":"往往；通常"},{"english":"beneath the refusal","chinese":"拒絕背後"},{"english":"answer it more intelligently","chinese":"更明智地回應"},{"english":"show evidence","chinese":"展示證據"},{"english":"not emotion alone","chinese":"不只是情緒"},{"english":"a beautiful beginning","chinese":"美好的開始"},{"english":"not enough by itself","chinese":"本身並不足夠"},{"english":"demonstrate that","chinese":"證明"},{"english":"both the charm and the burden","chinese":"魅力與負擔兩者"},{"english":"the burden of the profession","chinese":"這個職業的負擔"},{"english":"career folder","chinese":"職業資料夾"},{"english":"possible university courses","chinese":"可能的大學課程"},{"english":"entry requirements","chinese":"入學要求"},{"english":"estimated costs","chinese":"估計費用"},{"english":"scholarships","chinese":"獎學金"},{"english":"related jobs such as","chinese":"相關工作，例如……"},{"english":"veterinary nursing","chinese":"獸醫護理"},{"english":"animal welfare work","chinese":"動物福利工作"},{"english":"the daily duties of a vet","chinese":"獸醫的日常職責"},{"english":"better still","chinese":"更好的是"},{"english":"gain experience","chinese":"累積經驗"},{"english":"volunteer at an animal shelter","chinese":"在動物收容所做義工"},{"english":"animal shelter","chinese":"動物收容所"},{"english":"pet adoption event","chinese":"寵物領養活動"},{"english":"interview a local vet","chinese":"訪問本地獸醫"},{"english":"biology-related activity","chinese":"與生物相關的活動"},{"english":"take…for example","chinese":"以……為例"},{"english":"caring for","chinese":"照顧"},{"english":"injured stray cat","chinese":"受傷流浪貓"},{"english":"noticing symptoms","chinese":"留意症狀"},{"english":"keeping records","chinese":"保存記錄"},{"english":"cleaning responsibly","chinese":"負責任地清潔"},{"english":"ask an expert for help","chinese":"向專家求助"},{"english":"show maturity","chinese":"顯示成熟"},{"english":"be willing to","chinese":"願意"},{"english":"wake up early","chinese":"早起"},{"english":"clean cages","chinese":"清潔籠子"},{"english":"read science texts","chinese":"閱讀科學文本"},{"english":"face unpleasant realities","chinese":"面對不愉快的現實"},{"english":"impression may change from…to…","chinese":"印象可能由……變成……"},{"english":"disciplined enough to","chinese":"有足夠紀律去……"},{"english":"that shift is really powerful","chinese":"那個轉變很有力量"},{"english":"at the same time","chinese":"與此同時"},{"english":"be prepared to","chinese":"準備好去"},{"english":"compromise without giving up","chinese":"妥協但不放棄"},{"english":"three-month trial period","chinese":"三個月試行期"},{"english":"continue working hard","chinese":"繼續努力"},{"english":"supervised animal-related volunteering","chinese":"受監督的動物相關義工服務"},{"english":"sit down together","chinese":"坐下來一起"},{"english":"review what you have learned","chinese":"檢視你學到了甚麼"},{"english":"give someone breathing room","chinese":"給某人喘息空間"},{"english":"a fair chance","chinese":"公平的機會"},{"english":"careers adviser","chinese":"升學及就業輔導老師"},{"english":"relative or family friend","chinese":"親戚或家庭朋友"},{"english":"not to pressure your parents, but to","chinese":"不是為了……而是為了……"},{"english":"make the discussion less emotional","chinese":"令討論沒那麼情緒化"},{"english":"make the mistake of","chinese":"犯下……的錯誤"},{"english":"present your dream as","chinese":"把夢想呈現為……"},{"english":"vet or nothing","chinese":"非獸醫不可"},{"english":"veterinary medicine","chinese":"獸醫學"},{"english":"prove unsuitable","chinese":"證明不適合"},{"english":"lead to","chinese":"通向；帶來"},{"english":"animal science","chinese":"動物科學"},{"english":"conservation","chinese":"保育"},{"english":"pet nutrition","chinese":"寵物營養"},{"english":"animal-assisted therapy","chinese":"動物輔助治療"},{"english":"charity work","chinese":"慈善工作"},{"english":"weaken your ambition","chinese":"削弱你的抱負"},{"english":"if anything","chinese":"反而"},{"english":"safer and more mature","chinese":"更穩妥和成熟"},{"english":"only by showing that","chinese":"只有透過證明……才可以"},{"english":"think about risks","chinese":"考慮風險"},{"english":"earn the freedom to","chinese":"贏得……的自由"},{"english":"pursue the possibility","chinese":"追求這個可能性"},{"english":"a verdict on","chinese":"對……的判決"},{"english":"whole future","chinese":"整個未來"},{"english":"stand firm","chinese":"立場堅定"},{"english":"stay gracious","chinese":"保持有禮大方"},{"english":"speak respectfully","chinese":"尊重地說話"},{"english":"let your actions do part of the talking","chinese":"讓行動替你說明一部分"},{"english":"the more…, the harder…","chinese":"越……就越難……"},{"english":"dismiss your dream as childish","chinese":"把你的夢想視為幼稚而否定"},{"english":"one piece of research","chinese":"一項資料搜集"},{"english":"practical experience","chinese":"實際經驗"},{"english":"little by little","chinese":"一點一點地"},{"english":"grow stronger","chinese":"變得更堅定"},{"english":"become clearer in a different shape","chinese":"以另一種形式變得更清晰"},{"english":"either way","chinese":"無論如何"},{"english":"build a future","chinese":"建立未來"},{"english":"truly belongs to","chinese":"真正屬於……"},{"english":"your confident self","chinese":"自信的自己"},{"english":"warmly","chinese":"溫暖地；祝好"},{"english":"advice column","chinese":"諮詢專欄"}]},"dse-writing-2018-part-b-q5":{"exerciseId":"dse-writing-2018-part-b-q5","essayKey":"","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=dse-writing-2018-part-b-q5","flashDeckId":"dse/writing/part-b/2018/Q5","paragraphs":[{"label":"Paragraph 1","english":"Abolish the Rank, Preserve the Standard","chinese":"廢除排名，守住標準"},{"label":"Paragraph 2","english":"Chairperson, adjudicators and fellow students, good afternoon. Today I stand firmly for the motion that the policy of reporting students’ class position should be abolished.","chinese":"主席、各位評判、各位同學，午安。 今天，我堅定支持這項動議：公布學生班級名次的政策應該被廢除。"},{"label":"Paragraph 3","english":"For years, many report cards have told students not only what marks they have obtained, but also whether they are first, tenth or fortieth in class. This practice may look efficient. One number, one hierarchy, one clear message; Yet its very simplicity is exactly the problem. In pursuit of better education, schools are now forced to consider whether they should keep ranking children against their classmates, or report learning in a way that actually helps students improve. Our stance is clear - that class position should go. It distorts learning, damages students’ confidence and can be replaced by fairer, richer feedback.","chinese":"多年來，許多成績表告訴學生的不只是他們取得了多少分數，也包括他們在班中排名第一、第十，還是第四十。 這種做法看起來可能很有效率。 一個數字、一個等級、一個清晰訊息；然而，問題正正在於它過分簡化。 為了追求更好的教育，學校如今不得不思考：究竟應該繼續讓學生與同班同學互相比較排名，還是應該以真正有助學生進步的方式匯報學習情況。 我們的立場很清楚——班級名次應該取消。 它扭曲學習、損害學生的自信，並且可以由更公平、更豐富的回饋取代。"},{"label":"Paragraph 4","english":"Our first argument is that class position turns education into a narrow race instead of a meaningful process of learning. A ranking tells a student where he stands among classmates, but it does not tell him what he has mastered, what he has misunderstood, or what to do next. The fundamental logic goes as such: If an entire class improves, someone must still be last; If a class is weak, someone may still be first. In other words, class position measures comparison more than competence. Worse still, it encourages students to protect marks rather than pursue understanding. Take a capable Form Four student, for example. If every mark may affect her rank, she may choose safe essay structures, avoid challenging books and memorise model answers instead of developing her own voice. A weaker student, meanwhile, may see “38th out of 40 students in class” and conclude that effort is pointless, even though he has improved greatly. What matters is not whether a child is above or below another child, but whether he or she is actually moving forward. A system that hides progress behind comparison is therefore educationally unsound.","chinese":"我們的第一個論點是，班級名次會把教育變成一場狹隘的競賽，而失去作為有意義學習過程的本質。 排名能告訴一名學生他在同學之間所處的位置，卻不能告訴他已經掌握了甚麼、誤解了甚麼，或下一步應該怎樣做。 其基本邏輯如下：如果全班都有進步，仍然必定有人排最後；如果整班程度偏弱，仍然可能有人排第一。 換句話說，班級名次衡量比較多於衡量能力。 更糟的是，它鼓勵學生保住分數，多於追求真正理解。 以一名有能力的中四學生為例。 如果每一分都可能影響她的排名，她可能會選擇安全的作文結構、避開具挑戰性的書籍，並背誦範文，而不去發展自己的聲音。 與此同時，一名較弱的學生可能看到「全班 40 人中排名第 38」，便斷定努力毫無意義，即使他其實已經大有進步。 真正重要的，並非一個孩子排在另一個孩子之上或之下，重點在於他或她是否真的正在向前進步。 因此，一個把進步隱藏在比較背後的制度，在教育上並不健全。"},{"label":"Paragraph 5","english":"Our second argument is that reporting class position harms students’ emotional wellbeing and relationships. Some argue, “It is only a number.” With all due respect, it is not. In the eyes of a twelve-year-old, that number can become a label; At home, it can turn a report card into a trial. In class, it can divide friends into winners and losers. The more schools attach identity to ranking, the more students learn to see one another as threats. Consider a newly arrived student adapting to an English-medium environment. She may be hardworking, responsible and brave enough to ask for help; nevertheless, one low class position may make her look, unfairly, like a failure. No student should be made to feel small simply because others scored higher in the same group. Competition works up to a point, but beyond that it can damage trust, cooperation and self-respect. Education should stretch students; it should not sort their dignity.","chinese":"我們的第二個論點是，公布班級名次會傷害學生的情緒健康和人際關係。 有些人主張：「這只是一個數字。」 恕我直言，事情並沒有這麼簡單。 在一個十二歲孩子眼中，那個數字可以變成一個標籤；在家中，它可以把成績表變成一場審判。 在課室裡，它可以把朋友分成勝利者和失敗者。 學校越把身份與排名連在一起，學生就越會學懂把彼此視為威脅。 試想像一名新來港、正在適應英語教學環境的學生。 她可能勤奮、負責，而且勇於求助；儘管如此，一個偏低的班級名次仍可能不公平地令她看起來像個失敗者。 任何學生都不應只因同一組別中其他人分數更高，就被迫感到自己渺小。 競爭在某個限度內確實有效，但超過那個限度，它就可能破壞信任、合作和自尊。 教育應該拓展學生的能力；它不應把學生的尊嚴分等級。"},{"label":"Paragraph 6","english":"Our opponents may argue that class position motivates students and helps parents understand performance. Granted, parents deserve clear information, and students need standards.However , class position is a crude answer to a legitimate need. It tells parents that their child is “25th”, but not whether his vocabulary is weak, his reasoning is shallow, his exam technique is careless, or his improvement is remarkable. Better yet, schools can provide subject grades, standards-based descriptors, progress indicators and teacher comments. Instead of writing “42nd in class”, a report could say, “Reading comprehension is secure; argumentative writing needs stronger evidence; overall score has improved by eight marks.” That way, parents receive direction, students receive hope, and teachers remain accountable. To say that we should abolish class position is not to say that we should abolish excellence. Rather, it is to say that excellence should be measured intelligently.","chinese":"我方對手可能會主張，班級名次能激勵學生，並幫助家長了解表現。 誠然，家長理應得到清晰資訊，而學生也需要標準。 然而，班級名次只是對一項合理需要作出的粗糙回應。 它告訴家長，他們的孩子是「第 25 名」，卻沒有說明他的詞彙是否薄弱、推理是否膚淺、考試技巧是否粗心，或他的進步是否值得肯定。 更理想的是，學校可以提供科目等級、以標準為本的描述、進步指標以及教師評語。 相比寫上「全班第 42 名」，一份報告可以寫道：「閱讀理解穩固；議論文寫作需要更有力的證據；總分已提高八分。」 這樣一來，家長得到方向，學生得到希望，教師也能保持問責。 主張廢除班級名次，並不等於主張廢除卓越。 更準確地說，卓越應該被更明智地衡量。"},{"label":"Paragraph 7","english":"Adjudicators, the question before us is not whether students should work hard. Of course they should. The question is whether schools should keep using a ranking system that often rewards relative position at the cost of real growth. We say no. The time has come for schools to stop printing class positions, to give parents diagnostic reports, and to recognise students not as numbers in a queue but as learners with different starting points, strengths and paths. For the sake of fair assessment, healthier motivation and genuine progress, I urge you to support the motion. Thank you.","chinese":"各位評判，我們面前的問題，重點不在於學生是否應該努力。 他們當然應該努力。 真正的問題在於，學校是否應該繼續使用一套經常以犧牲真正成長為代價、去獎勵相對位置的排名制度。 我們的答案是否定的。 現在是時候讓學校停止印上班級名次，改為向家長提供診斷式報告，並承認學生並非隊列中的數字，而是有不同起點、強項和道路的學習者。 為了公平的評估、更健康的學習動力，以及真正的進步，我懇請各位支持這項動議。 多謝各位。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"abolish the rank","chinese":"廢除排名"},{"english":"preserve the standard","chinese":"保留標準"},{"english":"Chairperson, adjudicators and fellow students","chinese":"主席、評判及各位同學"},{"english":"stand firmly for the motion","chinese":"堅定支持辯題"},{"english":"the motion that","chinese":"……這項辯題"},{"english":"class position","chinese":"班內排名；班名次"},{"english":"should be abolished","chinese":"應該被廢除"},{"english":"report cards","chinese":"成績表"},{"english":"not only…but also…","chinese":"不但……而且……"},{"english":"marks they have obtained","chinese":"他們取得的分數"},{"english":"first, tenth or fortieth in class","chinese":"全班第一、第十或第四十"},{"english":"this practice","chinese":"這種做法"},{"english":"look efficient","chinese":"看似有效率"},{"english":"one number, one hierarchy, one clear message","chinese":"一個數字、一個階級、一個清晰訊息"},{"english":"its very simplicity","chinese":"它本身的簡單"},{"english":"exactly the problem","chinese":"正正是問題所在"},{"english":"in pursuit of","chinese":"為了追求……"},{"english":"better education","chinese":"更好的教育"},{"english":"be forced to consider whether","chinese":"被迫考慮是否"},{"english":"ranking children against","chinese":"把孩子與……比較排名"},{"english":"report learning","chinese":"匯報學習情況"},{"english":"in a way that","chinese":"以……的方式"},{"english":"actually helps students improve","chinese":"真正幫助學生進步"},{"english":"our stance is clear","chinese":"我們的立場清楚"},{"english":"should go","chinese":"應該取消"},{"english":"distort learning","chinese":"扭曲學習"},{"english":"damage students' confidence","chinese":"損害學生信心"},{"english":"be replaced by","chinese":"被……取代"},{"english":"fairer, richer feedback","chinese":"更公平、更豐富的回饋"},{"english":"our first argument is that","chinese":"我們的第一個論點是"},{"english":"turn education into","chinese":"把教育變成"},{"english":"a narrow race","chinese":"狹隘的競賽"},{"english":"instead of","chinese":"而不是"},{"english":"a meaningful process of learning","chinese":"有意義的學習過程"},{"english":"where he stands among","chinese":"在……之中處於甚麼位置"},{"english":"has mastered","chinese":"已經掌握"},{"english":"has misunderstood","chinese":"誤解了"},{"english":"what to do next","chinese":"下一步該做甚麼"},{"english":"the fundamental logic","chinese":"基本邏輯"},{"english":"is as follows","chinese":"如下"},{"english":"the entire class improves","chinese":"全班都有進步"},{"english":"someone must still be last","chinese":"仍然有人必定排最後"},{"english":"if a class is weak","chinese":"如果全班水平較弱"},{"english":"in other words","chinese":"換言之"},{"english":"measure comparison","chinese":"衡量比較"},{"english":"more than competence","chinese":"多於衡量能力"},{"english":"worse still","chinese":"更糟的是"},{"english":"protect marks","chinese":"保住分數"},{"english":"rather than pursue understanding","chinese":"而不是追求理解"},{"english":"take…for example","chinese":"以……為例"},{"english":"a capable Form Four student","chinese":"有能力的中四學生"},{"english":"affect her rank","chinese":"影響她的排名"},{"english":"safe essay structures","chinese":"穩妥的作文結構"},{"english":"challenging books","chinese":"有挑戰性的書籍"},{"english":"memorise model answers","chinese":"背誦範文答案"},{"english":"develop her own voice","chinese":"發展自己的聲音；形成個人風格"},{"english":"a weaker student","chinese":"較弱的學生"},{"english":"meanwhile","chinese":"與此同時"},{"english":"conclude that","chinese":"得出……的結論"},{"english":"effort is pointless","chinese":"努力是沒有意義的"},{"english":"even though","chinese":"即使"},{"english":"improved greatly","chinese":"大有進步"},{"english":"what matters is not whether…but whether…","chinese":"重要的不是是否……而是是否……"},{"english":"above or below another child","chinese":"排在另一個孩子之上或之下"},{"english":"moving forward","chinese":"正在進步"},{"english":"hide progress behind comparison","chinese":"讓比較掩蓋進步"},{"english":"educationally unsound","chinese":"在教育上站不住腳"},{"english":"our second argument is that","chinese":"我們的第二個論點是"},{"english":"emotional wellbeing","chinese":"情緒健康"},{"english":"relationships","chinese":"人際關係"},{"english":"some argue","chinese":"有些人認為"},{"english":"with all due respect","chinese":"恕我直言"},{"english":"in the eyes of","chinese":"在……眼中"},{"english":"become a label","chinese":"變成標籤"},{"english":"turn a report card into a trial","chinese":"把成績表變成審判"},{"english":"divide friends into","chinese":"把朋友分成"},{"english":"winners and losers","chinese":"勝利者和失敗者"},{"english":"the more…the more…","chinese":"越……越……"},{"english":"attach identity to ranking","chinese":"把身分與排名掛鈎"},{"english":"see one another as threats","chinese":"把彼此視為威脅"},{"english":"consider","chinese":"試想；考慮"},{"english":"a newly arrived student","chinese":"新來港學生；新轉入的學生"},{"english":"adapt to","chinese":"適應"},{"english":"an English-medium environment","chinese":"英語教學環境"},{"english":"brave enough to ask for help","chinese":"有足夠勇氣求助"},{"english":"nevertheless","chinese":"然而"},{"english":"one low class position","chinese":"一個低班名次"},{"english":"unfairly","chinese":"不公平地"},{"english":"look like a failure","chinese":"看起來像失敗者"},{"english":"be made to feel small","chinese":"被迫感到自己渺小"},{"english":"simply because","chinese":"只因為"},{"english":"scored higher","chinese":"取得較高分數"},{"english":"in the same group","chinese":"在同一組別中"},{"english":"work up to a point","chinese":"在某程度上有效"},{"english":"beyond that","chinese":"超過那個限度後"},{"english":"damage trust","chinese":"損害信任"},{"english":"cooperation","chinese":"合作"},{"english":"self-respect","chinese":"自尊"},{"english":"stretch students","chinese":"促使學生突破自己"},{"english":"sort their dignity","chinese":"將學生的尊嚴分等級"},{"english":"our opponents may argue that","chinese":"我方對手可能會認為"},{"english":"motivate students","chinese":"激勵學生"},{"english":"understand performance","chinese":"了解表現"},{"english":"granted","chinese":"誠然"},{"english":"deserve clear information","chinese":"應得到清晰資料"},{"english":"need standards","chinese":"需要標準"},{"english":"a crude answer to","chinese":"對……的粗糙回應"},{"english":"a legitimate need","chinese":"合理需要"},{"english":"vocabulary is weak","chinese":"詞彙薄弱"},{"english":"reasoning is shallow","chinese":"推理膚淺"},{"english":"exam technique is careless","chinese":"考試技巧粗心"},{"english":"improvement is remarkable","chinese":"進步顯著"},{"english":"better yet","chinese":"更好的是"},{"english":"subject grades","chinese":"科目等級"},{"english":"standards-based descriptors","chinese":"按標準描述的評語"},{"english":"progress indicators","chinese":"進度指標"},{"english":"teacher comments","chinese":"老師評語"},{"english":"instead of writing","chinese":"與其寫上……"},{"english":"reading comprehension","chinese":"閱讀理解"},{"english":"is secure","chinese":"穩固"},{"english":"argumentative writing","chinese":"議論文寫作"},{"english":"stronger evidence","chinese":"更有力的證據"},{"english":"overall score","chinese":"總分"},{"english":"has improved by","chinese":"提高了……"},{"english":"that way","chinese":"這樣一來"},{"english":"receive direction","chinese":"得到方向"},{"english":"receive hope","chinese":"得到希望"},{"english":"remain accountable","chinese":"保持問責"},{"english":"to say that…is not to say that…","chinese":"說……並不是說……"},{"english":"abolish excellence","chinese":"廢除卓越"},{"english":"be measured intelligently","chinese":"被明智地衡量"},{"english":"adjudicators","chinese":"評判"},{"english":"the question before us","chinese":"擺在我們面前的問題"},{"english":"of course","chinese":"當然"},{"english":"keep using","chinese":"繼續使用"},{"english":"ranking system","chinese":"排名制度"},{"english":"relative position","chinese":"相對位置"},{"english":"at the cost of","chinese":"以犧牲……為代價"},{"english":"real growth","chinese":"真正成長"},{"english":"the time has come for","chinese":"是時候……"},{"english":"stop printing class positions","chinese":"停止印上班名次"},{"english":"diagnostic reports","chinese":"診斷式報告"},{"english":"recognise students not as…but as…","chinese":"不把學生視為……而視為……"},{"english":"numbers in a queue","chinese":"隊列中的數字"},{"english":"learners with different starting points","chinese":"起點不同的學習者"},{"english":"strengths and paths","chinese":"強項與路徑"},{"english":"for the sake of","chinese":"為了……"},{"english":"fair assessment","chinese":"公平評估"},{"english":"healthier motivation","chinese":"更健康的動力"},{"english":"genuine progress","chinese":"真正進步"},{"english":"urge you to support the motion","chinese":"敦促你們支持辯題"},{"english":"Thank you","chinese":"多謝"}]},"dse-writing-2018-part-b-q6":{"exerciseId":"dse-writing-2018-part-b-q6","essayKey":"","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=dse-writing-2018-part-b-q6","flashDeckId":"dse/writing/part-b/2018/Q6","paragraphs":[{"label":"Paragraph 1","english":"A New Uniform for Modern Life: Why Athleisure Is Everywhere","chinese":"現代生活的新制服：為甚麼運動休閒風無處不在"},{"label":"Paragraph 2","english":"Gone are the days when sportswear belonged only in gyms, stadiums and school playgrounds. Today, a pair of sleek trainers may appear in an office lift, a hoodie may be seen in a café meeting, and yoga pants may travel from a fitness studio to the supermarket without looking out of place. This shift has made consumers reconsider what they expect from clothing, while fashion brands have been pushed to design outfits that offer comfort, movement and style at the same time. The rise of athleisure is therefore not a sudden accident. It reflects changing lifestyles, a stronger health-conscious culture and the growing influence of social media on what people see as fashionable.","chinese":"運動服只屬於健身室、運動場和學校操場的日子已經過去了。 今天，一雙時尚俐落的運動鞋可能出現在辦公室升降機裡，一件連帽衛衣可能出現在咖啡店會議中，而瑜伽褲也可能從健身室一路穿到超級市場，卻完全不顯得格格不入。 這種轉變令消費者重新思考自己對衣服的期待，同時也推動時裝品牌設計出能同時提供舒適感、活動彈性和時尚感的服裝。 因此，運動休閒風的興起並非一場突如其來的偶然。 它反映的是生活方式的改變、更強烈的健康意識文化，以及社交媒體對人們時尚觀念日益增長的影響。"},{"label":"Paragraph 3","english":"The first and simple reason for the popularity of athleisure is that modern life demands convenience. In a fast-moving city like Hong Kong, many people move from one activity to another with little breathing room. A student may attend lessons, go to tutorial classes, meet friends and squeeze in a short workout before returning home. An office worker may commute by MTR, climb several flights of stairs, sit through meetings and run errands after work. In such a packed schedule, changing clothes repeatedly is impractical. Athleisure solves this problem by combining flexibility with presentability. Stretchy joggers, breathable tops and lightweight jackets allow people to walk, sit, rush and exercise without feeling restricted. At the same time, many designs are neat enough to be worn in public without giving the impression that the wearer has just left a football pitch. In other words, athleisure is popular because it fits the rhythm of urban life, which tends to be quick, crowded, mobile and often unpredictable.","chinese":"運動休閒風受歡迎的第一個簡單原因，是現代生活需要便利。 在香港這樣節奏急速的城市裡，許多人從一項活動趕往另一項活動，幾乎沒有喘息空間。 一名學生可能要上課、去補習、見朋友，然後在回家前擠出時間做一次短暫運動。 一名上班族可能要乘搭港鐵通勤、爬上幾層樓梯、坐完整場會議，並在下班後處理各種雜務。 在如此緊湊的日程中，反覆更換衣服並不實際。 運動休閒服透過結合活動彈性與得體外觀，解決了這個問題。 有彈性的運動長褲、透氣上衣和輕便外套，讓人們無論走路、坐下、趕路還是運動時，都不會感到受束縛。 同時，許多設計也足夠整潔，可以穿到公共場合，而不會令人覺得穿著者剛剛離開足球場。 換言之，運動休閒風之所以流行，是因為它配合了城市生活的節奏，而這種節奏往往快速、擁擠、流動性高，而且經常難以預測。"},{"label":"Paragraph 4","english":"Another important reason is the growing desire to look and feel healthy. Fitness is no longer viewed merely as a private hobby; it has slowly but steadily become part of many people’s identity. Wearing athleisure can quietly signal that one is active, disciplined and energetic, even on days when the most athletic activity one does is walking quickly to catch a bus. This may sound superficial, but clothing has always helped people express who they are or who they want to become. A person wearing running shoes may be more willing to walk home instead of taking a taxi; someone already dressed in gym leggings may find it easier to join a yoga class after school or work. The clothes do not create health by themselves, but, at the very least, they lower the barrier to healthy choices. Not surprisingly, as people gradually pay more attention to mental well-being, body image and work-life balance, they are drawn to functional clothes that make an active lifestyle feel more achievable.","chinese":"另一個重要原因，是人們越來越渴望看起來健康，也感覺健康。 健身已經不再只被視為私人興趣；它已經緩慢但穩定地成為許多人身份的一部分。 穿著運動休閒服可以低調地傳達出一個人活躍、自律和充滿活力，即使在某些日子裡，那個人最像運動的活動只是快步走去趕巴士。 這聽起來也許有點膚淺，但衣服一直都幫助人們表達自己是怎樣的人，或自己想成為怎樣的人。 一個穿著跑鞋的人，可能更願意步行回家，而不選擇乘搭的士；一個已經穿上健身緊身褲的人，也可能更容易在放學或下班後參加瑜伽課。 衣服本身並不能創造健康，但至少能降低人們作出健康選擇的門檻。 毫不令人意外的是，隨著人們逐漸更加重視心理健康、身體形象和工作生活平衡，他們自然會被功能性服裝吸引，因為這類衣服令積極生活方式感覺更容易實現。"},{"label":"Paragraph 5","english":"The third reason lies in the fundamental way fashion itself has changed. Athleisure is not simply about comfort; underneath the surface, it is closely associated with making comfort look deliberate. In the past, loose T-shirts and sweatpants might have been seen as careless by most. Now, on the contrary, with better cutting, premium fabrics and minimalist colours, even similar items can appear polished. A black hoodie under a blazer, white trainers with cropped trousers, or a sports jacket matched with a simple dress can look modern rather than lazy. Furthermore, social media has accelerated this change. When celebrities, athletes, influencers and K-pop stars are photographed in stylish casual wear, their followers quickly learn that “relaxed” can also mean “fashionable”. Brands then respond by producing more attractive designs, which further normalises and reinforces the trend. The more people see athleisure in public, the more acceptable it becomes; the more acceptable it becomes, the more people are willing to wear it, naturally speaking.","chinese":"第三個原因在於時裝本身已經出現了根本性的改變。 運動休閒風並不只是關乎舒適；在表面之下，它其實與把舒適塑造成一種有意識的時尚選擇密切相關。 在過去，寬鬆 T 恤和運動褲可能會被大多數人視為隨便。 如今，相反地，透過更好的剪裁、高級面料和簡約色彩，即使是相似的單品也可以顯得精緻。 西裝外套下的一件黑色連帽衛衣、白色運動鞋配九分褲，或運動外套配簡約連身裙，都可以顯得現代，而非懶散。 此外，社交媒體也加速了這種轉變。 當名人、運動員、網紅和韓流明星被拍到穿著時尚休閒服時，他們的追隨者很快便學會，「放鬆」也可以意味著「時尚」。 品牌於是透過生產更吸引人的設計作出回應，從而進一步令這股潮流變得正常化，並加強其影響力。 人們在公共場合越常看到運動休閒服，它就越容易被接受；它越容易被接受，就會有越多人願意穿著它，這是很自然的。"},{"label":"Paragraph 6","english":"All things considered, the rise of athleisure is easy to understand. It gives busy people practical clothing, allows health-conscious consumers to project an active image, and satisfies a fashion culture that increasingly values effortless style. For better or worse, our clothes now have to do more than look good on a hanger; they have to support real life, ultimately. Fashion brands should therefore design athleisure that is durable and tasteful, while consumers should choose pieces that suit both their lifestyle and the occasion. Athleisure may have begun as a trend, but its success shows something deeper - that in today’s world, comfort and style are no longer enemies.","chinese":"綜合各方面來看，運動休閒風的興起是容易理解的。 它為忙碌的人提供實用服裝，讓注重健康的消費者展現活躍形象，並滿足一種越來越重視輕鬆時尚感的時裝文化。 無論好壞，我們的衣服如今要做的，已經超越掛在衣架上時好看而已；歸根結底，它們還必須支撐真實生活。 因此，時裝品牌應該設計出耐用而有品味的運動休閒服，而消費者也應該選擇同時適合自己生活方式和場合的單品。 運動休閒風也許始於一股潮流，但它的成功顯示出更深層的意義——在今日世界裡，舒適與風格已經不再是敵人。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"a new uniform for modern life","chinese":"現代生活的新制服"},{"english":"athleisure","chinese":"運動休閒服飾"},{"english":"Gone are the days when","chinese":"……的日子已經過去"},{"english":"sportswear","chinese":"運動服飾"},{"english":"belong only in","chinese":"只屬於……"},{"english":"sleek trainers","chinese":"時尚俐落的運動鞋"},{"english":"an office lift","chinese":"辦公室升降機"},{"english":"a café meeting","chinese":"咖啡店會面"},{"english":"yoga pants","chinese":"瑜伽褲"},{"english":"a fitness studio","chinese":"健身工作室"},{"english":"without looking out of place","chinese":"不顯得格格不入"},{"english":"reconsider what they expect from","chinese":"重新思考對……的期望"},{"english":"be pushed to design","chinese":"被推動去設計"},{"english":"offer comfort and style","chinese":"提供舒適感和時尚感"},{"english":"at the same time","chinese":"同時"},{"english":"the rise of athleisure","chinese":"運動休閒服飾的興起"},{"english":"a sudden accident","chinese":"突然出現的偶然現象"},{"english":"reflect changing lifestyles","chinese":"反映生活方式的轉變"},{"english":"health-conscious culture","chinese":"注重健康的文化"},{"english":"the growing influence of","chinese":"……日益增長的影響力"},{"english":"what people see as fashionable","chinese":"人們眼中時尚的事物"},{"english":"the popularity of","chinese":"……的受歡迎程度"},{"english":"modern life demands convenience","chinese":"現代生活講求方便"},{"english":"a fast-moving city","chinese":"節奏急速的城市"},{"english":"move from one activity to another","chinese":"從一項活動趕到另一項活動"},{"english":"with little breathing room","chinese":"幾乎沒有喘息空間"},{"english":"attend lessons","chinese":"上課"},{"english":"tutorial classes","chinese":"補習班"},{"english":"squeeze in a short workout","chinese":"抽時間做短暫運動"},{"english":"commute by MTR","chinese":"乘港鐵通勤"},{"english":"climb several flights of stairs","chinese":"爬幾層樓梯"},{"english":"sit through meetings","chinese":"捱完整場會議"},{"english":"run errands","chinese":"辦雜務"},{"english":"a packed schedule","chinese":"滿滿的日程"},{"english":"changing clothes repeatedly","chinese":"反覆更換衣服"},{"english":"be impractical","chinese":"不切實際"},{"english":"solve this problem by","chinese":"透過……解決這個問題"},{"english":"combine flexibility with presentability","chinese":"結合靈活性和得體外觀"},{"english":"presentability","chinese":"得體外觀"},{"english":"stretchy joggers","chinese":"有彈性的運動長褲"},{"english":"breathable tops","chinese":"透氣上衣"},{"english":"lightweight jackets","chinese":"輕便外套"},{"english":"without feeling restricted","chinese":"不覺得受束縛"},{"english":"neat enough to be worn in public","chinese":"整齊得足以在公眾場合穿着"},{"english":"give the impression that","chinese":"給人……的印象"},{"english":"the wearer","chinese":"穿着者"},{"english":"a football pitch","chinese":"足球場"},{"english":"fit the rhythm of urban life","chinese":"符合城市生活節奏"},{"english":"urban life","chinese":"城市生活"},{"english":"quick, crowded and mobile","chinese":"急速、擠迫而流動性高"},{"english":"often unpredictable","chinese":"往往難以預測"},{"english":"the growing desire to","chinese":"越來越渴望……"},{"english":"look and feel healthy","chinese":"看起來和感覺都健康"},{"english":"no longer viewed merely as","chinese":"不再只被視為……"},{"english":"a private hobby","chinese":"私人嗜好"},{"english":"slowly but steadily","chinese":"緩慢但穩步地"},{"english":"become part of someone's identity","chinese":"成為某人身分認同的一部分"},{"english":"quietly signal that","chinese":"默默傳達……"},{"english":"active, disciplined and energetic","chinese":"活躍、自律而有活力"},{"english":"on days when","chinese":"在……的日子"},{"english":"athletic activity","chinese":"體能活動"},{"english":"catch a bus","chinese":"趕巴士"},{"english":"sound superficial","chinese":"聽起來膚淺"},{"english":"express who they are","chinese":"表達自己是怎樣的人"},{"english":"who they want to become","chinese":"自己想成為怎樣的人"},{"english":"be more willing to","chinese":"更願意……"},{"english":"instead of taking a taxi","chinese":"而不是乘的士"},{"english":"dressed in gym leggings","chinese":"穿着健身緊身褲"},{"english":"join a yoga class","chinese":"參加瑜伽班"},{"english":"by themselves","chinese":"單靠本身"},{"english":"at the very least","chinese":"至少"},{"english":"lower the barrier to","chinese":"降低……的門檻"},{"english":"healthy choices","chinese":"健康選擇"},{"english":"pay more attention to","chinese":"更加留意"},{"english":"mental well-being","chinese":"精神健康；心理健康"},{"english":"body image","chinese":"身體形象"},{"english":"work-life balance","chinese":"工作與生活平衡"},{"english":"be drawn to","chinese":"被……吸引"},{"english":"functional clothes","chinese":"功能性服裝"},{"english":"make an active lifestyle feel more achievable","chinese":"令活躍生活方式感覺更容易做到"},{"english":"the fundamental way","chinese":"根本方式"},{"english":"fashion itself has changed","chinese":"時尚本身已經改變"},{"english":"not simply about","chinese":"不單純是關於……"},{"english":"underneath the surface","chinese":"表面之下；深層而言"},{"english":"be closely associated with","chinese":"與……密切相關"},{"english":"make comfort look deliberate","chinese":"令舒適看起來像刻意設計"},{"english":"loose T-shirts","chinese":"鬆身T恤"},{"english":"sweatpants","chinese":"運動褲"},{"english":"be seen as careless","chinese":"被視為隨便"},{"english":"on the contrary","chinese":"相反"},{"english":"better cutting","chinese":"更好的剪裁"},{"english":"premium fabrics","chinese":"優質布料"},{"english":"minimalist colours","chinese":"極簡色系"},{"english":"appear polished","chinese":"顯得精緻得體"},{"english":"a black hoodie under a blazer","chinese":"西裝外套內配黑色連帽衫"},{"english":"cropped trousers","chinese":"九分褲"},{"english":"matched with","chinese":"與……配搭"},{"english":"rather than lazy","chinese":"而不是懶散"},{"english":"accelerate this change","chinese":"加快這種轉變"},{"english":"celebrities, athletes and influencers","chinese":"名人、運動員和網紅"},{"english":"K-pop stars","chinese":"韓國流行音樂明星"},{"english":"be photographed in","chinese":"被拍到穿着……"},{"english":"stylish casual wear","chinese":"時尚休閒服"},{"english":"relaxed can also mean fashionable","chinese":"休閒也可以代表時尚"},{"english":"respond by producing","chinese":"以生產……作回應"},{"english":"attractive designs","chinese":"吸引人的設計"},{"english":"further normalise","chinese":"進一步令……正常化"},{"english":"reinforce the trend","chinese":"強化這股潮流"},{"english":"the more…, the more…","chinese":"越……，就越……"},{"english":"in public","chinese":"在公眾場合"},{"english":"acceptable","chinese":"可接受的"},{"english":"be willing to wear","chinese":"願意穿着"},{"english":"all things considered","chinese":"綜合而言"},{"english":"be easy to understand","chinese":"容易理解"},{"english":"practical clothing","chinese":"實用服裝"},{"english":"health-conscious consumers","chinese":"注重健康的消費者"},{"english":"project an active image","chinese":"展現活躍形象"},{"english":"satisfy a fashion culture","chinese":"滿足一種時尚文化"},{"english":"increasingly values","chinese":"越來越重視"},{"english":"effortless style","chinese":"不費力的時尚感"},{"english":"for better or worse","chinese":"不論好壞"},{"english":"do more than","chinese":"不只是……"},{"english":"look good on a hanger","chinese":"掛起來好看"},{"english":"support real life","chinese":"配合現實生活"},{"english":"durable and tasteful","chinese":"耐用而有品味"},{"english":"choose pieces that suit","chinese":"選擇適合……的單品"},{"english":"suit both their lifestyle and the occasion","chinese":"同時配合生活方式和場合"},{"english":"begin as a trend","chinese":"以潮流的形式開始"},{"english":"show something deeper","chinese":"反映更深層的事情"},{"english":"comfort and style are no longer enemies","chinese":"舒適與時尚不再互相排斥"}]},"dse-writing-2018-part-b-q7":{"exerciseId":"dse-writing-2018-part-b-q7","essayKey":"","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=dse-writing-2018-part-b-q7","flashDeckId":"dse/writing/part-b/2018/Q7","paragraphs":[{"label":"Paragraph 1","english":"Screen First, Stage Next: Why HKAPA’s Drama Recordings Could Win New Theatre Fans","chinese":"先看螢幕，再走進劇場：為何香港演藝學院的戲劇錄影能吸引新的劇場觀眾"},{"label":"Paragraph 2","english":"Theatre has always had one awkward problem - people who already love it know why it matters, while those who do not often assume it is expensive, slow or “not for them”. Against this background, the Hong Kong Academy for Performing Arts is considering screening video-recordings of live drama performances from theatres around the world to widen public access and turn curiosity into actual attendance. Having just watched one of these recordings, I would argue that the idea is not a replacement for live theatre, but it is a remarkably effective doorway into it. These recordings are, from my perspective, a good way to attract more people to stage plays, provided that HKAPA presents them as a first step rather than the final destination.","chinese":"劇場一直有一個尷尬的難題——已經熱愛它的人明白它為何重要，尚未接觸它的人卻往往以為它昂貴、緩慢，或者「不適合自己」。 剛看完其中一段錄影後，我認為這個構思並非要取代現場劇場；更準確地說，它是一道相當有效的入口，能把觀眾帶進劇場世界。 在我看來，只要香港演藝學院把這些錄影定位為第一步，而非最終目的地，它們確實是吸引更多人觀看舞台劇的好方法。"},{"label":"Paragraph 3","english":"The greatest strength of recorded theatre is that it lowers the psychological barrier to entry. For many non-theatre-goers, a stage play can feel unfamiliar before it even begins. “What if the language is difficult?”, “What if the acting feels exaggerated?”, “What if I do not understand the plot?” A recording answers these fears in a low-risk way. Viewers can first encounter the rhythm of stage dialogue, the intimacy of a monologue and the tension of a crisis scene without paying for an expensive seat or worrying about theatre etiquette. In the recording I watched, close-up shots allowed me to notice small changes in facial expression, while wider shots revealed the careful blocking and lighting that shaped the emotional atmosphere. In other words, the camera did not destroy the stage; it guided my inexperienced eye through it. Take a student who has only watched films and online videos, for example. Once he sees that a play can be suspenseful, funny and visually powerful, he is more likely to think, “If it is this good on screen, what would it feel like in person?” That question is exactly where interest begins.","chinese":"劇場錄影最大的優勢，在於它能降低觀眾踏入劇場世界的心理門檻。 對許多平日不看劇場演出的人來說，舞台劇甚至在開始前已經令人感到陌生 「如果語言很難懂怎麼辦？」、「如果表演感覺很誇張怎麼辦？」、「如果我看不懂劇情怎麼辦？」 錄影能以低風險的方式回應這些憂慮。 觀眾可以先接觸舞台對白的節奏、獨白的親密感，以及危機場面的張力，無須立即支付昂貴票價，也不用擔心自己不懂劇場禮儀。 在我觀看的錄影中，特寫鏡頭讓我留意到演員面部表情的細微變化；較寬闊的鏡頭則展現出精心安排的走位和燈光，如何塑造整體情緒氛圍。 換言之，鏡頭沒有削弱舞台，反倒引導我這雙尚未受過訓練的眼睛讀懂舞台 以一位平日只看電影和網上影片的學生為例。 一旦他看見原來一齣戲可以緊張、幽默，而且在視覺上充滿力量，他便更有可能心想：「如果在螢幕上已經這麼精彩，親身觀看又會是甚麼感覺？」 這個問題，正正就是興趣開始萌芽的地方。"},{"label":"Paragraph 4","english":"Another reason the scheme may work is that it gives Hong Kong audiences a taste of theatrical variety that one city alone cannot provide. Stage plays are not all Shakespearean kings, tragic speeches and wooden chairs under yellow lights. A recording programme can bring viewers from a minimalist Japanese production to a bold British political drama, from an American family tragedy to a Korean black comedy. Such range matters because one person’s “boring theatre” may be another person’s perfect entry point. A teenager who dislikes classical tragedy may respond to a sharp contemporary comedy; a parent who avoids experimental drama may be moved by a realistic family story. The more examples HKAPA offers, the more likely different audiences will find something that speaks to them. More importantly, recordings can be paired with short introductions, post-screening talks and ticket discounts for related live productions. That way, the programme does not merely entertain people for one evening; it builds a bridge from passive watching to active theatre-going.","chinese":"這項計劃可能奏效的另一個原因，是它能讓香港觀眾接觸到單靠一座城市難以提供的劇場多樣性。 舞台劇絕非只有莎士比亞式的君王、悲壯的演說，以及黃燈下的木椅。 一個錄影放映計劃，可以帶領觀眾由極簡風格的日本製作，走向大膽的英國政治劇；也可以由美國家庭悲劇，延伸至韓國黑色喜劇。 這種範圍之所以重要，是因為某人眼中「沉悶的劇場」，可能正是另一個人最理想的入門點。 一位不喜歡古典悲劇的青少年，可能會被尖銳的當代喜劇吸引；一位避開實驗劇場的家長，則可能被寫實的家庭故事打動。 香港演藝學院提供的例子越多，不同觀眾就越有可能找到某些能觸動自己的作品。 更重要的是，錄影可以配合簡短導賞、映後分享，以及相關現場製作的門票優惠。 如此一來，這項計劃就不單單是在一個晚上娛樂觀眾，更是在被動觀看與主動入場之間搭建橋樑。"},{"label":"Paragraph 5","english":"Granted, critics have a point when they say that a recording can never fully reproduce a live performance. Theatre is not just about plot; it is about shared breath, silence, risk and presence. When an actor pauses on stage, the whole audience feels the pause together. When a joke lands, laughter travels through the room. When a blackout falls, darkness seems to belong to everyone. A screen, however well filmed, keeps us at a slight distance. Worse still, viewers may wrongly assume that watching recordings is “enough” and never buy a theatre ticket. This is a real risk. Yet to acknowledge the limitation is not to reject the idea. The problem is not the recording itself, but how it is framed. If HKAPA promotes the screenings as “the theatre experience at home”, the scheme may weaken live attendance. If it presents them as “your first step into the theatre”, the same recordings can become invitations. The cinema trailer has never made cinema unnecessary; it makes people want the full film. Theatre recordings can do the same for stage plays.","chinese":"誠然，批評者說錄影永遠無法完整重現現場演出的質感，這種說法有其道理 劇場不只關乎情節；它也關乎共同的呼吸、沉默、風險與臨場感。 當演員在台上停頓時，整個觀眾席都會一同感受那一刻的停頓。 當一句笑話成功引起反應時，笑聲會在整個空間中流動。 當燈光突然熄滅時，黑暗彷彿同時屬於在場的每一個人。 螢幕拍得再好，也始終讓我們與演出保持一點距離。 更糟的是，觀眾可能會錯誤地以為觀看錄影已經「足夠」，結果從不購買劇場門票。 這的確是一個真實的風險。 然而，承認限制，並不等於否定整個構思。 問題的核心不在錄影本身，重點在於香港演藝學院如何定位它。 如果香港演藝學院把放映宣傳成「在家中的劇場體驗」，這項計劃可能會削弱現場入場率。 如果它把這些錄影呈現為「你踏入劇場的第一步」，同一批錄影就能變成邀請 電影預告片從未令電影院變得多餘；相反，它讓人想看完整電影。 劇場錄影對舞台劇也能發揮同樣作用。"},{"label":"Paragraph 6","english":"All things considered, HKAPA should go ahead with the plan, but with a clear strategy. It should curate accessible productions, explain key dramatic features, invite actors or directors to speak after screenings, and offer practical next steps, such as beginner-friendly live shows and student tickets. The purpose should not be to make theatre flatter, cheaper and safer forever. It should be to make theatre less intimidating at first. After all, the art form itself is still alive because nothing quite replaces the moment when performers and audience meet in the same room. Let people discover that magic on screen; then give them every reason to seek it on stage.","chinese":"綜合而言，香港演藝學院應該推行這項計劃，但必須配合清晰策略。 它應該精選較容易入門的作品，解釋關鍵戲劇特色，邀請演員或導演出席映後分享，並提供實際的下一步，例如適合初接觸者的現場演出和學生票。 這項計劃的目的，不應該是把劇場永遠變得更平面、更便宜、更安全。 它應該是先讓劇場變得較不令人卻步。 畢竟，這門藝術之所以仍然有生命力，正因為演員與觀眾在同一個空間相遇的瞬間，始終難以被完全取代。 先讓人們在螢幕上發現那份魔力；接著，給他們所有理由親身走進劇場。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"Screen First, Stage Next","chinese":"先看螢幕，再進劇場"},{"english":"drama recordings","chinese":"戲劇錄像"},{"english":"win new theatre fans","chinese":"吸引新的劇場觀眾"},{"english":"theatre fans","chinese":"劇場愛好者"},{"english":"awkward problem","chinese":"尷尬的問題"},{"english":"people who already love it","chinese":"已經喜歡它的人"},{"english":"know why it matters","chinese":"明白它為何重要"},{"english":"assume it is expensive","chinese":"以為它很昂貴"},{"english":"not for them","chinese":"不適合他們"},{"english":"against this background","chinese":"在這背景下"},{"english":"the Hong Kong Academy for Performing Arts","chinese":"香港演藝學院"},{"english":"be considering","chinese":"正在考慮"},{"english":"screen video recordings","chinese":"放映錄像"},{"english":"live drama performances","chinese":"現場戲劇演出"},{"english":"from theatres around the world","chinese":"來自世界各地劇院"},{"english":"widen public access","chinese":"擴大公眾接觸機會"},{"english":"public access","chinese":"公眾接觸機會"},{"english":"turn curiosity into actual attendance","chinese":"將好奇心轉化為實際入場"},{"english":"having just watched","chinese":"剛剛看完"},{"english":"I would argue that","chinese":"我會認為"},{"english":"replacement for","chinese":"……的替代品"},{"english":"live theatre","chinese":"現場劇場"},{"english":"remarkably effective doorway into","chinese":"進入……非常有效的門路"},{"english":"from my perspective","chinese":"從我的角度看"},{"english":"attract more people to","chinese":"吸引更多人接觸"},{"english":"stage plays","chinese":"舞台劇"},{"english":"provided that","chinese":"前提是；只要"},{"english":"present them as","chinese":"將它們定位為"},{"english":"a first step","chinese":"第一步"},{"english":"rather than the final destination","chinese":"而不是最終目的地"},{"english":"greatest strength","chinese":"最大優點"},{"english":"recorded theatre","chinese":"錄製劇場"},{"english":"lower the psychological barrier to entry","chinese":"降低入門心理門檻"},{"english":"psychological barrier","chinese":"心理門檻"},{"english":"barrier to entry","chinese":"入門門檻"},{"english":"non-theatre-goers","chinese":"平日不看劇場的人"},{"english":"feel unfamiliar","chinese":"感到陌生"},{"english":"before it even begins","chinese":"甚至在開始之前"},{"english":"What if…?","chinese":"如果……怎麼辦？"},{"english":"language is difficult","chinese":"語言艱深"},{"english":"acting feels exaggerated","chinese":"演技感覺誇張"},{"english":"understand the plot","chinese":"明白情節"},{"english":"answer these fears","chinese":"回應這些憂慮"},{"english":"in a low-risk way","chinese":"以低風險方式"},{"english":"first encounter","chinese":"初次接觸"},{"english":"rhythm of stage dialogue","chinese":"舞台對白的節奏"},{"english":"intimacy of a monologue","chinese":"獨白的親密感"},{"english":"monologue","chinese":"獨白"},{"english":"tension of a crisis scene","chinese":"危機場面的緊張感"},{"english":"crisis scene","chinese":"危機場面"},{"english":"without paying for","chinese":"不用支付……"},{"english":"expensive seat","chinese":"昂貴座位"},{"english":"theatre etiquette","chinese":"劇場禮儀"},{"english":"close-up shots","chinese":"特寫鏡頭"},{"english":"allow someone to notice","chinese":"讓某人留意到"},{"english":"facial expression","chinese":"面部表情"},{"english":"wider shots","chinese":"廣角鏡頭"},{"english":"reveal the careful blocking","chinese":"展現精心安排的舞台調度"},{"english":"blocking and lighting","chinese":"舞台調度和燈光"},{"english":"emotional atmosphere","chinese":"情感氣氛"},{"english":"in other words","chinese":"換句話說"},{"english":"destroy the stage","chinese":"破壞舞台感"},{"english":"guide my inexperienced eye through","chinese":"引導我這雙缺乏經驗的眼睛去理解"},{"english":"inexperienced eye","chinese":"缺乏經驗的眼光"},{"english":"take… for example","chinese":"以……為例"},{"english":"online videos","chinese":"網上影片"},{"english":"once he sees that","chinese":"一旦他看到"},{"english":"suspenseful, funny and visually powerful","chinese":"有懸念、有趣而視覺效果強"},{"english":"be more likely to","chinese":"更有可能"},{"english":"on screen","chinese":"在螢幕上"},{"english":"in person","chinese":"親身；現場"},{"english":"where interest begins","chinese":"興趣開始的地方"},{"english":"another reason","chinese":"另一個原因"},{"english":"the scheme may work","chinese":"這計劃可能奏效"},{"english":"Hong Kong audiences","chinese":"香港觀眾"},{"english":"a taste of","chinese":"初步體驗；嘗試"},{"english":"theatrical variety","chinese":"劇場的多樣性"},{"english":"one city alone","chinese":"單靠一個城市"},{"english":"not all…","chinese":"並非全都是……"},{"english":"Shakespearean kings","chinese":"莎士比亞式君王"},{"english":"tragic speeches","chinese":"悲劇式演說"},{"english":"wooden chairs under yellow lights","chinese":"黃燈下的木椅"},{"english":"recording programme","chinese":"錄像放映計劃"},{"english":"bring viewers from… to…","chinese":"帶領觀眾從……到……"},{"english":"minimalist Japanese production","chinese":"極簡日本製作"},{"english":"bold British political drama","chinese":"大膽的英國政治劇"},{"english":"American family tragedy","chinese":"美國家庭悲劇"},{"english":"Korean black comedy","chinese":"韓國黑色喜劇"},{"english":"such range matters","chinese":"這種多樣性很重要"},{"english":"entry point","chinese":"入門點"},{"english":"perfect entry point","chinese":"最理想的入門點"},{"english":"classical tragedy","chinese":"古典悲劇"},{"english":"respond to","chinese":"對……有反應；受……吸引"},{"english":"sharp contemporary comedy","chinese":"尖銳的當代喜劇"},{"english":"experimental drama","chinese":"實驗劇場"},{"english":"be moved by","chinese":"被……打動"},{"english":"realistic family story","chinese":"寫實家庭故事"},{"english":"the more…, the more likely…","chinese":"越……就越有可能……"},{"english":"speak to them","chinese":"打動他們；引起共鳴"},{"english":"more importantly","chinese":"更重要的是"},{"english":"be paired with","chinese":"與……配合"},{"english":"short introductions","chinese":"簡短介紹"},{"english":"post-screening talks","chinese":"放映後座談"},{"english":"ticket discounts","chinese":"門票折扣"},{"english":"related live productions","chinese":"相關現場演出"},{"english":"that way","chinese":"這樣一來"},{"english":"merely entertain people","chinese":"只是娛樂大眾"},{"english":"for one evening","chinese":"一個晚上"},{"english":"build a bridge from… to…","chinese":"建立由……到……的橋樑"},{"english":"passive watching","chinese":"被動觀看"},{"english":"active theatre-going","chinese":"主動入場看劇"},{"english":"critics have a point","chinese":"批評者有道理"},{"english":"fully reproduce","chinese":"完全重現"},{"english":"live performance","chinese":"現場演出"},{"english":"not just about","chinese":"不只是關於"},{"english":"shared breath","chinese":"共同呼吸"},{"english":"risk and presence","chinese":"風險與臨場感"},{"english":"actor pauses on stage","chinese":"演員在台上停頓"},{"english":"whole audience","chinese":"全場觀眾"},{"english":"feel the pause together","chinese":"一起感受停頓"},{"english":"joke lands","chinese":"笑話奏效"},{"english":"laughter travels through the room","chinese":"笑聲在場內傳開"},{"english":"blackout falls","chinese":"燈光全黑的一刻"},{"english":"belong to everyone","chinese":"屬於所有人"},{"english":"however well filmed","chinese":"無論拍得多好"},{"english":"at a slight distance","chinese":"保持一點距離"},{"english":"worse still","chinese":"更糟的是"},{"english":"wrongly assume that","chinese":"錯誤地以為"},{"english":"watching recordings is enough","chinese":"看錄像已經足夠"},{"english":"buy a theatre ticket","chinese":"買劇場門票"},{"english":"a real risk","chinese":"真正的風險"},{"english":"acknowledge the limitation","chinese":"承認限制"},{"english":"reject the idea","chinese":"否定這個想法"},{"english":"how it is framed","chinese":"它如何被定位"},{"english":"promote the screenings as","chinese":"將放映宣傳為"},{"english":"the theatre experience at home","chinese":"在家中的劇場體驗"},{"english":"weaken live attendance","chinese":"削弱現場入場人數"},{"english":"live attendance","chinese":"現場入場人數"},{"english":"first step into the theatre","chinese":"走進劇場的第一步"},{"english":"become invitations","chinese":"變成邀請"},{"english":"cinema trailer","chinese":"電影預告片"},{"english":"make cinema unnecessary","chinese":"令電影變得不必要"},{"english":"want the full film","chinese":"想看完整電影"},{"english":"do the same for","chinese":"對……產生同樣作用"},{"english":"all things considered","chinese":"綜合而言"},{"english":"go ahead with the plan","chinese":"推行這項計劃"},{"english":"clear strategy","chinese":"清晰策略"},{"english":"curate accessible productions","chinese":"策劃易於入門的製作"},{"english":"accessible productions","chinese":"易於理解的製作"},{"english":"key dramatic features","chinese":"主要戲劇特色"},{"english":"dramatic features","chinese":"戲劇特色"},{"english":"actors or directors","chinese":"演員或導演"},{"english":"speak after screenings","chinese":"放映後分享"},{"english":"practical next steps","chinese":"實際的下一步"},{"english":"beginner-friendly live shows","chinese":"適合初學者的現場演出"},{"english":"student tickets","chinese":"學生票"},{"english":"the purpose should not be to","chinese":"目的不應該是"},{"english":"flatter, cheaper and safer","chinese":"更平面、更便宜、更安全"},{"english":"less intimidating","chinese":"較不令人卻步"},{"english":"at first","chinese":"起初；一開始"},{"english":"art form","chinese":"藝術形式"},{"english":"still alive","chinese":"仍然有生命力"},{"english":"nothing quite replaces","chinese":"沒有東西真正取代"},{"english":"performers and audience","chinese":"表演者和觀眾"},{"english":"meet in the same room","chinese":"在同一空間相遇"},{"english":"discover that magic on screen","chinese":"先在螢幕上發現那份魔力"},{"english":"give them every reason to","chinese":"給他們充分理由去"},{"english":"seek it on stage","chinese":"在舞台上尋找它"}]},"dse-writing-2018-part-b-q8":{"exerciseId":"dse-writing-2018-part-b-q8","essayKey":"","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=dse-writing-2018-part-b-q8","flashDeckId":"dse/writing/part-b/2018/Q8","paragraphs":[{"label":"Paragraph 1","english":"Application for the Poetry House Summer Poetry Workshop Scholarship","chinese":"夏季詩歌工作坊獎學金申請"},{"label":"Paragraph 2","english":"Dear Members of the Scholarship Selection Committee,","chinese":"獎學金遴選委員會各位委員："},{"label":"Paragraph 3","english":"I am writing to apply for the Poetry House Summer Poetry Workshop Scholarship. Poetry is often described as a private art, yet your workshop suggests something larger - that poems can grow in a creative community, sharpened by craft, conversation and contact with voices from beyond one’s own city. As a young writer in Hong Kong whose interest in poetry has developed from a quiet habit into a serious commitment, I would be deeply grateful for the opportunity to take part in a programme that promotes both the art and the craft of poetry. I believe I should be selected because I would not only benefit from the workshop, but also contribute to it with curiosity, discipline and a sincere respect for language.","chinese":"本人謹此申請 Poetry House 夏季詩歌工作坊獎學金。 詩歌常被形容為一種私密的藝術；然而，貴工作坊展示了更廣闊的意義—— 詩可以在富有創意的群體中成長，並透過寫作技巧、交流對話，以及接觸來自自身城市以外的聲音而變得更精煉。 作為一名來自香港的年輕寫作者，我對詩歌的興趣已由一個安靜的習慣，逐漸發展成一份認真的追求；若能有機會參與一個同時推廣詩歌藝術與寫作技藝的課程，我將深感榮幸。 我相信自己值得獲選，因為我不只會從工作坊中受益，也會以好奇心、紀律，以及對語言真誠的尊重，為這個工作坊作出貢獻。"},{"label":"Paragraph 4","english":"My interest in poetry began in an ordinary place - the back of a school notebook. At first, I wrote short lines only to record what I could not say aloud—my grandmother’s fading Cantonese songs, the loneliness of crossing a crowded MTR platform, the strange silence after an argument at home. Over time, however, I realised that poetry was not simply a way to express emotion; rather, it was a way to pay attention. A successful poem can turn a streetlamp, a receipt or a half-finished bowl of noodles into something unexpectedly human. What fascinates me most is how poetry balances compression and expansion; a few words may open a whole landscape of memory. This is why I have continued writing even when schoolwork was demanding. I keep a small notebook with me, revise drafts after lessons and read poems in English and Chinese so that I can understand how rhythm, image and voice work differently across languages.","chinese":"我對詩歌的興趣，始於一個很平凡的地方——一本學校筆記簿的背頁。 起初，我寫下一些短短的句子，只是為了記錄那些我無法說出口的東西—— 祖母逐漸模糊的廣東歌聲、穿過擠迫港鐵月台時的孤獨感，以及家中爭吵過後那種奇異的沉默。 然而，隨著時間過去，我逐漸明白，詩歌並非單純用來表達情感；更準確地說，它是一種學會留心觀看世界的方法。 一首成功的詩，可以把一盞街燈、一張收據，或一碗吃到一半的麵，轉化成某種意想不到地具有人情味的東西。 最令我著迷的，是詩歌如何在濃縮與擴展之間取得平衡；寥寥數語，已足以打開一整片記憶的風景。 這正是為甚麼即使學業繁重，我仍然持續寫作。 我會隨身帶著一本小筆記簿，在課後修改草稿，並閱讀英文和中文詩，好讓自己明白節奏、意象和聲音如何在不同語言之間發揮不同作用。"},{"label":"Paragraph 5","english":"I am particularly drawn to Poetry House’s workshop because it offers what young writers rarely receive, which is serious guidance in a creative environment. Writing alone is necessary, but writing only alone can become limiting. A workshop would give me the chance to test whether my images are clear, whether my endings are earned and whether my poems invite readers in rather than merely display my private feelings. More importantly, discussing my work with guest poets from around the world would broaden my understanding of what poetry can be. A poet from another culture may notice assumptions hidden in my lines; another may challenge my rhythm, my diction or even my idea of what a poem should look like. Such criticism would not discourage me. Instead, it would make me a more careful and courageous writer. Only by listening to readers beyond my usual circle can I learn whether my voice is genuinely communicative.","chinese":"獨自寫作是必要的，但若只習慣獨自寫作，視野也可能逐漸受限。 工作坊會讓我有機會檢視自己的意象是否清晰、結尾是否有足夠鋪墊，以及我的詩是否能邀請讀者走進其中，而非單純展示我個人的感受。 更重要的是，與來自世界各地的客席詩人討論自己的作品，將會拓寬我對詩歌可能性的理解。 一位來自另一種文化的詩人，或許會留意到我詩句中隱藏的假設；另一位則可能挑戰我的節奏、措辭，甚至我對詩應該呈現甚麼形態的想像。 這樣的批評不會令我氣餒。 相反，它會令我成為一位更細心、更勇敢的寫作者。 只有聆聽日常圈子以外的讀者，我才可以知道自己的聲音是否真正具備與人溝通的能力。"},{"label":"Paragraph 6","english":"I also believe I would be a suitable participant because I take both creativity and responsibility seriously. In my school, I helped organise a lunchtime “Poetry Wall”, inviting students to post short poems anonymously about friendship, exams and family expectations. Some contributions were rough; some were moving; all of them showed that young people have much to say when given a respectful space. This experience taught me that poetry is not an ornament for talented individuals alone. It can make room for those who are shy, overwhelmed or unsure how to begin. If selected, I would bring this spirit of openness to the workshop. I would read others’ drafts carefully, offer honest but considerate feedback, and take no discussion lightly. After the workshop, I hope to share what I have learnt by running a small school-based poetry sharing session, so that the scholarship’s impact may extend beyond myself.","chinese":"我也相信自己會是一位合適參加者，因為我認真看待創意，也同樣重視責任 在學校，我曾協助籌辦午膳時間的「詩歌牆」，邀請同學匿名貼上關於友誼、考試和家庭期望的短詩。 有些作品仍然粗糙；有些則令人動容；它們全都證明，只要得到一個受尊重的空間，年輕人其實有很多話想說。 這次經驗讓我明白，詩歌並非只屬於有才華者的裝飾品。 它也可以為那些害羞、感到不知所措，或不知道如何開始的人，騰出一個能夠發聲的空間。 若能獲選，我會把這份開放的精神帶到工作坊之中。 我會細心閱讀其他參加者的草稿，提供坦誠但體貼的回饋，並認真看待每一次討論。 工作坊結束後，我希望透過在學校舉辦一個小型詩歌分享會，把自己所學到的東西分享出去，讓這份獎學金的影響能夠延伸至我個人以外。"},{"label":"Paragraph 7","english":"Needless to say, being one of only ten young writers selected would be a privilege. Yet I see the scholarship not as a reward for what I have already written, but as a responsibility to grow further. I am ready to revise, to question my own habits and to learn from poets whose experiences differ from mine. Poetry has taught me that a small line can carry a large truth. With your support, I hope to discover how much further my own lines can travel.","chinese":"不用多說，能成為十位獲選年輕寫作者之一，將會是一份殊榮。 然而，我看待這份獎學金，並非把它視為對我過往作品的獎賞；我更把它理解為一份推動自己繼續成長的責任。 我已準備好修改自己的作品、反思自己的寫作習慣，並向人生經驗與我不同的詩人學習。 詩歌教會我，一行短短的文字，也可以承載巨大的真理。 在貴機構的支持下，我希望能探索自己的詩句究竟還可以走得多遠。"},{"label":"Paragraph 8","english":"Thank you very much for considering my application. I look forward to hearing from you.","chinese":"非常感謝各位考慮我的申請。 期待收到各位的回覆。"},{"label":"Paragraph 9","english":"Yours faithfully,","chinese":"此致 , 敬禮"},{"label":"Paragraph 10","english":"Chris Wong","chinese":"Chris Wong"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"apply for the scholarship","chinese":"申請獎學金"},{"english":"Summer Poetry Workshop Scholarship","chinese":"夏季詩歌工作坊獎學金"},{"english":"Scholarship Selection Committee","chinese":"獎學金遴選委員會"},{"english":"be often described as","chinese":"常被形容為"},{"english":"a private art","chinese":"私人的藝術"},{"english":"suggest something larger","chinese":"意味着更宏大的東西"},{"english":"creative community","chinese":"創作社群"},{"english":"be sharpened by","chinese":"透過……變得更精煉"},{"english":"craft, conversation and contact","chinese":"技巧、交流與接觸"},{"english":"voices from beyond one's own city","chinese":"來自自己城市以外的聲音"},{"english":"young writer","chinese":"年輕作家"},{"english":"develop from...into...","chinese":"由……發展成……"},{"english":"a quiet habit","chinese":"靜靜培養的習慣"},{"english":"serious commitment","chinese":"認真的投入；嚴肅承諾"},{"english":"be deeply grateful for","chinese":"對……深表感激"},{"english":"the opportunity to take part in","chinese":"參加……的機會"},{"english":"promote both the art and the craft of poetry","chinese":"推廣詩歌的藝術與技巧"},{"english":"be selected","chinese":"被選中"},{"english":"not only benefit from...but also contribute to...","chinese":"不但從……受益，也為……作出貢獻"},{"english":"contribute to it with","chinese":"以……為其作出貢獻"},{"english":"curiosity, discipline and respect","chinese":"好奇心、紀律和尊重"},{"english":"a sincere respect for language","chinese":"對語言的真誠尊重"},{"english":"begin in an ordinary place","chinese":"始於一個平凡的地方"},{"english":"the back of a school notebook","chinese":"學校筆記簿後頁"},{"english":"at first","chinese":"起初"},{"english":"short lines","chinese":"短短的詩句"},{"english":"say aloud","chinese":"說出口"},{"english":"fading Cantonese songs","chinese":"漸漸淡去的廣東歌"},{"english":"the loneliness of crossing","chinese":"穿過……時的孤獨感"},{"english":"crowded MTR platform","chinese":"擠迫的港鐵月台"},{"english":"strange silence","chinese":"奇怪的沉默"},{"english":"an argument at home","chinese":"家中的爭執"},{"english":"over time","chinese":"隨着時間過去"},{"english":"not simply...rather...","chinese":"不只是……而是……"},{"english":"express emotion","chinese":"表達情感"},{"english":"pay attention","chinese":"留心觀察"},{"english":"a successful poem","chinese":"成功的詩"},{"english":"turn something into","chinese":"把……變成"},{"english":"a half-finished bowl of noodles","chinese":"吃了一半的麵"},{"english":"unexpectedly human","chinese":"意想不到地有人情味"},{"english":"what fascinates me most","chinese":"最令我着迷的是"},{"english":"balance compression and expansion","chinese":"平衡凝練與延展"},{"english":"a few words","chinese":"寥寥數語"},{"english":"open a whole landscape of memory","chinese":"展開一整片記憶風景"},{"english":"continue writing","chinese":"繼續寫作"},{"english":"schoolwork was demanding","chinese":"課業繁重"},{"english":"keep a notebook with me","chinese":"隨身帶着筆記簿"},{"english":"revise drafts","chinese":"修改草稿"},{"english":"read poems in English and Chinese","chinese":"閱讀中英文詩"},{"english":"rhythm, image and voice","chinese":"節奏、意象和聲音"},{"english":"work differently across languages","chinese":"在不同語言中運作方式不同"},{"english":"be particularly drawn to","chinese":"對……特別嚮往"},{"english":"offer what young writers rarely receive","chinese":"提供年輕作家少有的東西"},{"english":"serious guidance","chinese":"認真的指導"},{"english":"creative environment","chinese":"創意環境"},{"english":"writing alone is necessary","chinese":"獨自寫作是必要的"},{"english":"become limiting","chinese":"變得有局限"},{"english":"give me the chance to","chinese":"給我機會去"},{"english":"test whether","chinese":"檢視是否"},{"english":"images are clear","chinese":"意象清晰"},{"english":"endings are earned","chinese":"結尾自然有力；結尾有其鋪墊"},{"english":"invite readers in","chinese":"邀請讀者走進作品"},{"english":"rather than merely display","chinese":"而不只是展示"},{"english":"private feelings","chinese":"私人感受"},{"english":"guest poets from around the world","chinese":"來自世界各地的客席詩人"},{"english":"broaden my understanding of","chinese":"擴闊我對……的理解"},{"english":"what poetry can be","chinese":"詩可以是甚麼"},{"english":"from another culture","chinese":"來自另一種文化"},{"english":"notice assumptions hidden in my lines","chinese":"留意到我詩句中隱藏的假設"},{"english":"challenge my rhythm","chinese":"挑戰我的節奏"},{"english":"challenge my diction","chinese":"挑戰我的用字"},{"english":"what a poem should look like","chinese":"一首詩應該是甚麼模樣"},{"english":"such criticism","chinese":"這樣的批評"},{"english":"discourage me","chinese":"令我氣餒"},{"english":"make me a more careful and courageous writer","chinese":"令我成為更細心、更勇敢的作家"},{"english":"beyond my usual circle","chinese":"在我平常圈子以外"},{"english":"genuinely communicative","chinese":"真正能與人溝通的"},{"english":"a suitable participant","chinese":"合適的參加者"},{"english":"take creativity and responsibility seriously","chinese":"認真看待創意和責任"},{"english":"helped organise","chinese":"協助籌辦"},{"english":"lunchtime Poetry Wall","chinese":"午膳時間詩牆"},{"english":"invite students to","chinese":"邀請學生去"},{"english":"post short poems anonymously","chinese":"匿名張貼短詩"},{"english":"family expectations","chinese":"家庭期望"},{"english":"contributions were rough","chinese":"投稿較粗糙"},{"english":"contributions were moving","chinese":"投稿令人感動"},{"english":"have much to say","chinese":"有很多話想說"},{"english":"given a respectful space","chinese":"獲得一個受尊重的空間"},{"english":"this experience taught me that","chinese":"這次經歷讓我明白"},{"english":"not an ornament for","chinese":"不是……的裝飾"},{"english":"talented individuals alone","chinese":"只有有才華的人"},{"english":"make room for","chinese":"為……騰出空間"},{"english":"shy, overwhelmed or unsure","chinese":"害羞、壓力大或不確定的"},{"english":"unsure how to begin","chinese":"不知道如何開始"},{"english":"if selected","chinese":"如獲選"},{"english":"bring this spirit of openness","chinese":"帶着這種開放精神"},{"english":"read others' drafts carefully","chinese":"細心閱讀別人的草稿"},{"english":"honest but considerate feedback","chinese":"誠實而體貼的回饋"},{"english":"take no discussion lightly","chinese":"不會輕視任何討論"},{"english":"after the workshop","chinese":"工作坊之後"},{"english":"share what I have learnt","chinese":"分享我所學到的東西"},{"english":"school-based poetry sharing session","chinese":"校內詩歌分享會"},{"english":"the scholarship's impact","chinese":"獎學金的影響"},{"english":"extend beyond myself","chinese":"延伸至我本人以外"},{"english":"needless to say","chinese":"不用說；毋庸置疑"},{"english":"one of only ten young writers","chinese":"僅有十名年輕作家之一"},{"english":"selected would be a privilege","chinese":"獲選將是一份榮幸"},{"english":"not as a reward for","chinese":"不是作為對……的獎勵"},{"english":"a responsibility to grow further","chinese":"繼續成長的責任"},{"english":"ready to revise","chinese":"準備好修改"},{"english":"question my own habits","chinese":"質疑自己的習慣"},{"english":"learn from poets whose experiences differ from mine","chinese":"向經歷與我不同的詩人學習"},{"english":"a small line can carry a large truth","chinese":"小小一行詩能承載巨大的真理"},{"english":"with your support","chinese":"在你們的支持下"},{"english":"how much further my own lines can travel","chinese":"我的詩句能走得多遠"},{"english":"thank you for considering my application","chinese":"感謝你考慮我的申請"},{"english":"I look forward to hearing from you","chinese":"期待你的回覆"},{"english":"Yours faithfully","chinese":"謹啟"}]},"dse-writing-2018-part-b-q9":{"exerciseId":"dse-writing-2018-part-b-q9","essayKey":"","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=dse-writing-2018-part-b-q9","flashDeckId":"dse/writing/part-b/2018/Q9","paragraphs":[{"label":"Paragraph 1","english":"The Door Left Open","chinese":"那扇沒有關上的門"},{"label":"Paragraph 2","english":"When I was young, I believed the world ended at the brass bars of my cage. There was my blue water cup, my round mirror, my wooden perch, and Mina, whose school uniform smelled faintly of rain and chalk. Every morning she whispered, “Good boy, Kiwi,” as if my name were a song she had invented. I sang back because singing was the one freedom nobody had thought to lock away.","chinese":"小時候，我以為世界就在鳥籠的黃銅欄杆前到了盡頭。 那裡有我的藍色水杯、圓圓的小鏡子、木製棲架，還有 Mina；她的校服隱約帶著雨水和粉筆的氣味。 每天早上，她都會低聲說：「乖孩子，Kiwi。」那語氣彷彿我的名字是一首她親手創作的歌。 我用歌聲回應她，因為歌唱是唯一一種沒有人想到要鎖起來的自由。"},{"label":"Paragraph 3","english":"Up until that afternoon, the cage door had always been shut with a small silver hook. I knew its sound: click, final and neat. Then, one Thursday, Mina rushed in, changed my water, forgot the hook, and ran out again. The door remained open.","chinese":"直到那天下午之前，籠門一直由一個小小的銀色掛鉤扣住。 我熟悉那個聲音：喀的一下，乾脆、俐落，帶著一種終結的意味。 後來，在一個星期四，Mina 匆匆跑進來，替我換了水，卻忘了扣上掛鉤，然後又跑了出去。 籠門就那樣開著。"},{"label":"Paragraph 4","english":"At first, nothing happened. The room was so still that I could hear the refrigerator humming and the traffic breathing below the flat. A thin line of sunlight lay across the open doorway. No words can do justice to how wide that little gap appeared. It was not more than two inches, yet it looked larger than the sky in my dreams.","chinese":"起初，甚麼也沒有發生。 房間靜得連雪櫃的低鳴，以及樓下車流像呼吸一樣起伏的聲音，我都聽得見 一道細細的陽光橫在敞開的門口。 任何文字都不足以寫出那道小縫在我眼中有多麼遼闊。 它不過兩吋寬，看起來卻比我夢中的天空還要廣闊。"},{"label":"Paragraph 5","english":"I hopped towards it. One step. Another. My heart beat so violently that my feathers trembled. For once in my life, the bars were not stopping me. The problem was that I was stopping myself.","chinese":"我朝它跳了過去。 一步。 再一步。 我的心跳猛烈得連羽毛也微微發抖。 有生以來難得一次，那些欄杆已經沒有攔住我。 問題在於，是我自己攔住了自己。"},{"label":"Paragraph 6","english":"Beyond the cage stood Mina’s desk, crowded with textbooks. Beyond the desk was the window. Beyond the window were clouds moving without permission. I had watched sparrows cut through the air like thrown stones. I had hated them, admired them, and envied them until all three feelings became one.","chinese":"鳥籠之外，是 Mina 的書桌，上面堆滿了課本。 書桌之外，是那扇窗。 窗外，是那些不需要任何允許便能移動的雲。 我曾經看著麻雀像被拋出的石子一樣劃破空氣。 我曾恨過牠們，仰慕過牠們，也羨慕過牠們；到了最後，這三種感覺竟融成同一種心情。"},{"label":"Paragraph 7","english":"The instant I pushed the door with my head, it swung open. I froze. Silence rushed at me. Then I leapt.","chinese":"我用頭一推籠門，它便立刻盪開了。 我僵住了。 沉默猛然向我湧來。 然後，我跳了出去。"},{"label":"Paragraph 8","english":"For a terrifying second, I fell rather than flew. My wings, unused to decision, beat the air clumsily. I knocked over a pencil holder, scattered Mina’s notes and landed, panting, on the curtain rail. From above, the cage, which had once seemed like the whole universe, was merely a golden box on a table.","chinese":"有那麼令人恐懼的一秒，我與其說是在飛，倒更像是在墜落。 我的翅膀早已不習慣作出選擇，只能笨拙地拍打著空氣。 我撞翻了筆筒，弄散了 Mina 的筆記，最後氣喘吁吁地落在窗簾桿上。 從高處望下去，那個曾經像整個宇宙一樣龐大的鳥籠，如今只是一個放在桌上的金色盒子。"},{"label":"Paragraph 9","english":"The window was open too. Wind entered the room. It smelled of wet pavement, trees and exhaust fumes. Freedom did not smell clean. It smelled dangerous, confusing and alive. With freedom, I suddenly understood, comes not only space but choice; and choice is heavier than any chain.","chinese":"窗也開著。 風走進了房間。 它帶著濕漉漉的行人路、樹木和廢氣的氣味。 自由聞起來並不純淨。 它聞起來危險、混亂，卻又鮮活。 我突然明白，伴隨自由而來的，不單是空間，還有選擇；而選擇比任何鎖鏈都更加沉重。"},{"label":"Paragraph 10","english":"I flew to the window ledge. Beneath me, the city dropped away: balconies, laundry, buses, heads, umbrellas. Somewhere nearby, a sparrow chirped sharply, as if laughing. I spread my wings. One more movement, and the world would have me.","chinese":"我飛到窗台上。 在我下方，城市一路向下展開：露台、晾著的衣服、巴士、人頭、雨傘。 附近某處，一隻麻雀尖聲啾叫，彷彿正在發笑。 我張開翅膀。 只要再動一下，我便會屬於那個世界。"},{"label":"Paragraph 11","english":"Then I heard it: a sob from the corridor.","chinese":"就在那時，我聽見了：走廊傳來一聲啜泣。"},{"label":"Paragraph 12","english":"Mina stumbled in. For a moment, she did not see me. She saw the empty cage. Her hand flew to her mouth, and she whispered my name with such fear that the sound struck me harder than the wind. Only then did I understand something I had never considered. My cage had imprisoned me; but my presence had comforted her. Perhaps both things could be true.","chinese":"Mina 踉蹌地走了進來。 有那麼一刻，她沒有看見我。 她看見的是空了的鳥籠。 她的手一下子掩住嘴，帶著那樣深的恐懼低聲喚我的名字；那聲音擊中我的力度，比窗外的風還要猛烈。 直到那一刻，我才明白一件自己從未想過的事。 我的鳥籠曾經困住我；可我的存在，也曾經安慰著她。 也許，這兩件事可以同時成立。"},{"label":"Paragraph 13","english":"She turned and saw me on the ledge.","chinese":"她轉過身，看見我站在窗台上。"},{"label":"Paragraph 14","english":"“Kiwi,” she breathed. Not a command. Not even a plea. Just my name, broken open.","chinese":"「Kiwi，」她像呼吸般喚了一聲。 沒有命令的意味。 甚至也談不上懇求。 只有我的名字，被她喚得像裂開了一樣。"},{"label":"Paragraph 15","english":"I looked out once more. The sky was endless, if not merciless. The room was small, if not safe. I wanted the clouds. I wanted Mina. I wanted a life with no bars and no goodbyes, which was perhaps the one thing no bird, no human, no creature could have.","chinese":"我又一次望向窗外。 天空無邊無際，甚至帶著幾分無情。 房間很小，卻也未必沒有安全感。 我想要那些雲。 我也想要 Mina。 我想要一種沒有欄杆、也沒有告別的生活；可那也許正是鳥、人，以及世上一切生命都無法真正擁有的東西。"},{"label":"Paragraph 16","english":"So I did the only brave thing I could think of. I flew—not away, but back. I landed on Mina’s shoulder, trembling. She cried into my feathers, and I let her.","chinese":"於是，我做了當時唯一想得到的勇敢之事。 我飛了——沒有飛向遠方，卻飛了回去。 我落在 Mina 的肩膀上，身體仍在發抖。 她把眼淚埋進我的羽毛裡，而我沒有躲開。"},{"label":"Paragraph 17","english":"That night, she did not close the cage door. She placed my food inside and left the hook hanging loose. I slept on the top of the cage, under a square of moonlight. The bars were still there, but something between us had changed.","chinese":"那天晚上，她沒有關上籠門。 她把我的食物放進籠裡，卻讓掛鉤鬆鬆地垂著。 我睡在鳥籠頂上，身下是一方月光。 那些欄杆仍然存在，可我和她之間，有些東西已經改變了。"},{"label":"Paragraph 18","english":"The next morning, when Mina opened the window, I flew around the room twice before returning to her hand. Outside, the sparrows were calling. One day, perhaps, I would answer them. But that day, I learned that freedom was not simply the chance to leave. Sometimes, freedom was being trusted enough to return.","chinese":"第二天早上，Mina 打開窗戶時，我繞著房間飛了兩圈，然後回到她的手上。 窗外，麻雀仍在呼喚。 也許有一天，我會回應牠們。 但在那一天，我明白了自由並不只是離開的機會。 有時，自由是在被充分信任之後，仍然可以選擇回來。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"left open","chinese":"被留下打開"},{"english":"when I was young","chinese":"當我年幼時"},{"english":"the world ended at","chinese":"世界止於……"},{"english":"brass bars","chinese":"黃銅籠條"},{"english":"blue water cup","chinese":"藍色水杯"},{"english":"round mirror","chinese":"圓鏡"},{"english":"wooden perch","chinese":"木棲架"},{"english":"school uniform","chinese":"校服"},{"english":"smelled faintly of","chinese":"隱約有……的氣味"},{"english":"rain and chalk","chinese":"雨水和粉筆的氣味"},{"english":"as if","chinese":"好像；彷彿"},{"english":"a song she had invented","chinese":"她創作出來的一首歌"},{"english":"sang back","chinese":"唱歌回應"},{"english":"the one freedom","chinese":"唯一的自由"},{"english":"thought to","chinese":"想到要"},{"english":"lock away","chinese":"鎖起來"},{"english":"up until","chinese":"直到……為止"},{"english":"cage door","chinese":"籠門"},{"english":"had always been shut","chinese":"一直關上"},{"english":"silver hook","chinese":"銀色小鉤"},{"english":"final and neat","chinese":"乾脆俐落而不可逆轉"},{"english":"rushed in","chinese":"匆忙進來"},{"english":"forgot the hook","chinese":"忘記扣上鉤子"},{"english":"ran out again","chinese":"又跑出去"},{"english":"remained open","chinese":"仍然開着"},{"english":"at first","chinese":"起初"},{"english":"so still that","chinese":"靜得以致"},{"english":"refrigerator humming","chinese":"雪櫃嗡嗡作響"},{"english":"traffic breathing below the flat","chinese":"單位下方的車流聲"},{"english":"below the flat","chinese":"在單位下方"},{"english":"a thin line of sunlight","chinese":"一線薄薄的陽光"},{"english":"lay across","chinese":"橫落在……上"},{"english":"open doorway","chinese":"開着的門口"},{"english":"do justice to","chinese":"充分表達"},{"english":"little gap","chinese":"小小的空隙"},{"english":"not more than","chinese":"不超過"},{"english":"looked larger than","chinese":"看起來比……更大"},{"english":"in my dreams","chinese":"在我的夢裏"},{"english":"hopped towards","chinese":"跳向"},{"english":"heart beat so violently","chinese":"心跳得非常劇烈"},{"english":"feathers trembled","chinese":"羽毛顫抖"},{"english":"for once in my life","chinese":"生平第一次"},{"english":"the bars were not stopping me","chinese":"籠條沒有阻止我"},{"english":"I was stopping myself","chinese":"是我在阻止自己"},{"english":"beyond the cage","chinese":"籠子之外"},{"english":"crowded with textbooks","chinese":"堆滿教科書"},{"english":"moving without permission","chinese":"未經允許地移動"},{"english":"sparrows","chinese":"麻雀"},{"english":"cut through the air","chinese":"劃破空氣"},{"english":"like thrown stones","chinese":"像被擲出的石頭"},{"english":"hated, admired and envied","chinese":"憎恨、欣賞並羨慕"},{"english":"became one","chinese":"合而為一"},{"english":"the instant","chinese":"一……就"},{"english":"pushed the door with my head","chinese":"用頭推門"},{"english":"swung open","chinese":"猛地打開"},{"english":"froze","chinese":"僵住"},{"english":"silence rushed at me","chinese":"寂靜向我湧來"},{"english":"leapt","chinese":"跳起；躍起"},{"english":"for a terrifying second","chinese":"在可怕的一秒間"},{"english":"rather than","chinese":"而不是"},{"english":"unused to decision","chinese":"不習慣作決定"},{"english":"beat the air clumsily","chinese":"笨拙地拍打空氣"},{"english":"knocked over","chinese":"撞倒"},{"english":"pencil holder","chinese":"筆筒"},{"english":"scattered Mina's notes","chinese":"撒亂 Mina 的筆記"},{"english":"landed, panting","chinese":"氣喘吁吁地降落"},{"english":"curtain rail","chinese":"窗簾路軌"},{"english":"from above","chinese":"從上方看"},{"english":"had once seemed like","chinese":"曾經看起來像"},{"english":"the whole universe","chinese":"整個宇宙"},{"english":"merely","chinese":"只是；僅僅"},{"english":"a golden box","chinese":"金色盒子"},{"english":"the window was open too","chinese":"窗也開着"},{"english":"entered the room","chinese":"進入房間"},{"english":"wet pavement","chinese":"濕潤的行人路"},{"english":"exhaust fumes","chinese":"廢氣"},{"english":"did not smell clean","chinese":"聞起來並不清新"},{"english":"dangerous, confusing and alive","chinese":"危險、混亂而充滿生命力"},{"english":"with freedom comes","chinese":"自由帶來"},{"english":"not only… but…","chinese":"不只……而且……"},{"english":"choice is heavier than any chain","chinese":"選擇比任何鎖鏈都沉重"},{"english":"window ledge","chinese":"窗台"},{"english":"beneath me","chinese":"在我下方"},{"english":"the city dropped away","chinese":"城市向下展開"},{"english":"balconies","chinese":"露台"},{"english":"laundry","chinese":"晾曬的衣物"},{"english":"somewhere nearby","chinese":"附近某處"},{"english":"chirped sharply","chinese":"尖聲啁啾"},{"english":"as if laughing","chinese":"好像在笑"},{"english":"spread my wings","chinese":"張開翅膀"},{"english":"one more movement","chinese":"再多一個動作"},{"english":"the world would have me","chinese":"世界便會接住我；我便屬於世界"},{"english":"a sob from the corridor","chinese":"走廊傳來的抽泣聲"},{"english":"stumbled in","chinese":"踉蹌走進來"},{"english":"for a moment","chinese":"有一刻"},{"english":"empty cage","chinese":"空籠"},{"english":"her hand flew to her mouth","chinese":"她的手猛地掩住嘴"},{"english":"with such fear that","chinese":"帶着如此恐懼以致"},{"english":"struck me harder than","chinese":"比……更猛烈地擊中我"},{"english":"only then did I understand","chinese":"直到那時我才明白"},{"english":"had never considered","chinese":"從未考慮過"},{"english":"imprisoned me","chinese":"囚禁我"},{"english":"my presence","chinese":"我的存在"},{"english":"comforted her","chinese":"安慰了她"},{"english":"both things could be true","chinese":"兩件事可以同時成立"},{"english":"on the ledge","chinese":"在窗台上"},{"english":"she breathed","chinese":"她輕聲說"},{"english":"not a command","chinese":"不是命令"},{"english":"not even a plea","chinese":"甚至不是懇求"},{"english":"broken open","chinese":"破碎地敞開"},{"english":"looked out once more","chinese":"再次望出去"},{"english":"endless, if not merciless","chinese":"即使不算無情，也是無邊無際"},{"english":"small, if not safe","chinese":"即使不算安全，也是狹小"},{"english":"a life with no bars and no goodbyes","chinese":"沒有籠條、沒有道別的生活"},{"english":"perhaps the one thing","chinese":"也許是唯一一件事"},{"english":"no bird, no human, no creature","chinese":"沒有鳥、沒有人、沒有生物"},{"english":"the only brave thing","chinese":"唯一勇敢的事"},{"english":"could think of","chinese":"想得到"},{"english":"not away, but back","chinese":"不是飛走，而是飛回來"},{"english":"landed on Mina's shoulder","chinese":"落在 Mina 的肩上"},{"english":"cried into my feathers","chinese":"伏在我的羽毛中哭"},{"english":"I let her","chinese":"我由得她"},{"english":"left the hook hanging loose","chinese":"讓鉤子鬆鬆地掛着"},{"english":"on the top of the cage","chinese":"在籠頂上"},{"english":"under a square of moonlight","chinese":"在一方月光下"},{"english":"the bars were still there","chinese":"籠條仍然存在"},{"english":"something between us had changed","chinese":"我們之間有些東西改變了"},{"english":"opened the window","chinese":"打開窗戶"},{"english":"flew around the room","chinese":"在房間裏飛來飛去"},{"english":"before returning to","chinese":"然後回到"},{"english":"returned to her hand","chinese":"回到她手上"},{"english":"the sparrows were calling","chinese":"麻雀在呼喚"},{"english":"one day, perhaps","chinese":"也許有一天"},{"english":"answer them","chinese":"回應牠們"},{"english":"not simply the chance to leave","chinese":"不只是離開的機會"},{"english":"being trusted enough to return","chinese":"被信任到可以回來"}]},"dse-writing-2019-part-a":{"exerciseId":"dse-writing-2019-part-a","essayKey":"","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=dse-writing-2019-part-a","flashDeckId":"dse/writing/part-a/2019","paragraphs":[{"label":"Title","english":"Yearbook Entry: Class 6C – Reflections","chinese":"年刊文章：6C 班回顧"},{"label":"1.1: ACADEMIC LIFE","english":"Looking back on my years at Kowloon Secondary School, one subject that truly captivated me was Biology. Delving into microscopic worlds and conducting hands‐on experiments in the lab never ceased to amaze me. Although memorizing complicated processes and Latin names could be daunting, that sense of challenge spurred me to push my limits and achieve more than I ever thought possible. To this day, I still recall how exhilarating it felt to unravel the mysteries of life—from cells dividing under the microscope to analyzing blood samples during practical sessions.","chinese":"回顧我在九龍中學的歲月，其中一科真正令我著迷的是生物。 探索微觀世界，以及在實驗室親手進行實驗，總是令我驚嘆不已。 雖然記憶複雜的過程和拉丁名稱有時令人卻步，但那份挑戰感推動我突破自己的極限，成就比我原本想像中更多的事。 直到今天，我仍然記得揭開生命奧秘時那種令人振奮的感覺——從在顯微鏡下觀察細胞分裂，到在實習課中分析血液樣本，都是難忘的經歷。"},{"label":"1.2: STUDENT LIFE","english":"Beyond academics, what I will miss most about Class 6C is our unbreakable bond. Whether we were working together on group projects, sharing jokes in the corridor, or encouraging one another before crucial exams, our camaraderie made every moment truly special. I especially cherish how we supported each other, turning stressful deadlines into opportunities for collaboration. These small acts of kindness and mutual respect transformed our classroom into a second home. As we embark on new journeys, I feel grateful for the friendships forged in Class 6C and I truly believe these precious memories will forever light up our paths ahead.","chinese":"除了學業之外，最令我懷念 6C 班的，是我們之間牢不可破的情誼。 無論我們是在小組專題中一起合作、在走廊上分享笑話，還是在重要考試前互相鼓勵，這份同窗情誼都令每一刻變得格外珍貴。 我尤其珍惜我們彼此支持的方式，因為我們把充滿壓力的截止日期，轉化成互相合作的機會 這些細小的善意和彼此尊重，讓我們的課室變成了第二個家。 當我們踏上新的旅程時，我很感激在 6C 班建立起來的友誼，也真心相信這些珍貴回憶將永遠照亮我們前方的道路。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"Yearbook Entry","chinese":"畢業紀念冊文章"},{"english":"reflections","chinese":"感想；回顧"},{"english":"looking back on","chinese":"回顧……"},{"english":"my years at","chinese":"我在……的歲月"},{"english":"one subject that truly captivated me","chinese":"一科真正吸引我的科目"},{"english":"truly captivated me","chinese":"深深吸引我"},{"english":"delve into","chinese":"深入探索"},{"english":"microscopic worlds","chinese":"微觀世界"},{"english":"conduct hands-on experiments","chinese":"進行親身實驗"},{"english":"hands-on experiments","chinese":"親身實驗；實作實驗"},{"english":"in the lab","chinese":"在實驗室"},{"english":"never ceased to amaze me","chinese":"一直令我驚嘆"},{"english":"memorising complicated processes","chinese":"記憶複雜過程"},{"english":"complicated processes","chinese":"複雜過程"},{"english":"Latin names","chinese":"拉丁名稱"},{"english":"could be daunting","chinese":"可能令人卻步"},{"english":"that sense of challenge","chinese":"那種挑戰感"},{"english":"spur someone to","chinese":"激勵某人去……"},{"english":"push my limits","chinese":"挑戰自己的極限"},{"english":"achieve more than","chinese":"成就比……更多"},{"english":"ever thought possible","chinese":"曾經以為可能的"},{"english":"To this day","chinese":"直到今天"},{"english":"still recall","chinese":"仍然記得"},{"english":"how exhilarating it felt to","chinese":"……是多麼令人振奮"},{"english":"unravel the mysteries of life","chinese":"解開生命的奧秘"},{"english":"cells dividing under the microscope","chinese":"顯微鏡下正在分裂的細胞"},{"english":"under the microscope","chinese":"在顯微鏡下"},{"english":"analyse blood samples","chinese":"分析血液樣本"},{"english":"blood samples","chinese":"血液樣本"},{"english":"practical sessions","chinese":"實習課；實驗課"},{"english":"beyond academics","chinese":"除了學業之外"},{"english":"what I will miss most","chinese":"我最會懷念的"},{"english":"unbreakable bond","chinese":"牢不可破的情誼"},{"english":"whether we were","chinese":"無論我們是……"},{"english":"work together on","chinese":"一起做……"},{"english":"group projects","chinese":"小組專題"},{"english":"sharing jokes in the corridor","chinese":"在走廊說笑"},{"english":"encourage one another","chinese":"互相鼓勵"},{"english":"before crucial exams","chinese":"在重要考試之前"},{"english":"camaraderie","chinese":"同窗情誼；友愛"},{"english":"make every moment truly special","chinese":"令每一刻都格外珍貴"},{"english":"especially cherish","chinese":"特別珍惜"},{"english":"support each other","chinese":"互相支持"},{"english":"stressful deadlines","chinese":"令人有壓力的截止日期"},{"english":"turn something into opportunities for","chinese":"把……轉化成……的機會"},{"english":"opportunities for collaboration","chinese":"合作的機會"},{"english":"small acts of kindness","chinese":"細微的善意"},{"english":"mutual respect","chinese":"互相尊重"},{"english":"transform something into","chinese":"把……轉化成"},{"english":"a second home","chinese":"第二個家"},{"english":"embark on new journeys","chinese":"展開新的旅程"},{"english":"feel grateful for","chinese":"感激……"},{"english":"friendships forged in","chinese":"在……建立的友誼"},{"english":"precious memories","chinese":"珍貴回憶"},{"english":"forever light up our paths ahead","chinese":"永遠照亮我們前方的路"}]},"dse-writing-2019-part-b-q2":{"exerciseId":"dse-writing-2019-part-b-q2","essayKey":"","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=dse-writing-2019-part-b-q2","flashDeckId":"dse/writing/part-b/2019/Q2","paragraphs":[{"label":"Paragraph 1","english":"Opening the Door Without Leaving Locals Outside","chinese":"開門迎才，不把本地人拒於門外"},{"label":"Paragraph 2","english":"Gone are the days when a city could prosper by relying only on talent born within its borders. In the past, Hong Kong firms might have hired mainly from the local community; today, companies search the world for people whose skills meet international standards. This change has led Hong Kong companies and the government to attract international talent so as to strengthen the economy, sharpen competitiveness and broaden society’s outlook. My view is not that Hong Kong should choose foreigners over locals, or locals over foreigners. Rather, it should welcome the world while ensuring that its own people are not pushed aside. International talent can raise standards and connect Hong Kong to wider networks, but only fair policy and serious local training can turn competition into shared progress.","chinese":"一個城市只靠本土出生的人才便能繁榮的日子，已經一去不返。 過去，香港公司或許主要從本地社區招聘人才；如今，企業卻放眼全球，尋找技能達到國際標準的人才。 這種轉變促使香港企業和政府吸引國際人才，以鞏固經濟、提升競爭力，並拓寬社會的視野。 我的看法並不是香港應該選擇外來人才而放棄本地人，或選擇本地人而排斥外來人才。 更準確地說，香港應該擁抱世界，同時確保自己的市民不會被推到一旁。 國際人才可以提升標準，並把香港連接到更廣闊的網絡；然而，只有公平的政策和認真的本地培訓，才能把競爭轉化為共同進步。"},{"label":"Paragraph 3","english":"First, international talent brings economic and professional benefits. Skilled newcomers bring new methods, fresh habits and different ways of solving problems. A financial analyst from London may understand European regulations; an engineer from India may have experience in large-scale software systems; a scientist from Canada may know how to commercialise research. Working beside them, local employees can learn global standards instead of being locked inside familiar routines. The more diverse a workplace becomes, the more likely it is that weak assumptions will be questioned before they become expensive mistakes. Moreover, overseas professionals can act as human bridges. A Hong Kong start-up entering the Middle Eastern market, for example, may gain not only language support but also an understanding of customs and consumer expectations. In that sense, talent attraction is not just about filling vacancies; it is ultimately about enlarging Hong Kong’s reach.","chinese":"首先，國際人才帶來經濟和專業方面的好處。 具備技能的新來者會帶來新的方法、新的工作習慣，以及不同的解難方式。 一位來自倫敦的金融分析師可能熟悉歐洲法規；一位來自印度的工程師可能擁有大型軟件系統的經驗；一位來自加拿大的科學家可能知道如何把研究商業化。 本地員工與他們並肩工作，便可以學習全球標準，而不是被困在熟悉的工作模式之中。 工作場所越多元，一些薄弱的假設便越有可能在變成昂貴錯誤之前受到質疑 此外，海外專業人士可以充當人與人之間的橋樑。 例如，一間準備進入中東市場的香港初創企業，得到的可能不只是語言支援，還包括對當地習俗和消費者期望的理解。 從這個意義上說，吸引人才並不只是填補職位空缺；歸根究底，它是為了擴大香港的影響範圍。"},{"label":"Paragraph 4","english":"That said, the arrival of overseas talent is not without challenges. The first concern is fairness. If companies recruit internationally while local graduates are offered only low-paid junior posts, resentment is bound to grow. A young Hong Kong engineer who has studied hard may feel discouraged if senior positions always seem to go to people brought in from elsewhere. The problem is not the presence of outsiders per se, but the absence of a visible pathway for locals to advance. Another challenge is social integration. Different working styles can easily create misunderstanding: what one culture sees as confidence may be seen by another as arrogance, while modesty may be mistaken for passivity. Outside the workplace, pressure on housing and public services may also make residents wonder whether people are paying the hidden price of global ambition. If such worries are ignored, a policy meant to strengthen Hong Kong may instead divide it.","chinese":"不過，海外人才的到來並非沒有挑戰。 第一個令人關注的問題是公平。 如果企業在全球招聘人才，卻只向本地畢業生提供低薪的初級職位，不滿情緒必然會增加。 一位努力讀書的香港年輕工程師，如果總是看見高級職位落入外地引入的人才手中，便可能感到灰心。 問題本身並不在於外來者的存在，而在於本地人缺乏一條清晰可見的晉升道路 另一個挑戰是社會融合。 不同的工作風格很容易造成誤解：一種文化視為自信的表現，在另一種文化眼中可能被看成傲慢；而謙遜也可能被誤解為被動。 在工作場所之外，住屋和公共服務所承受的壓力，也可能令居民思考：市民是否正在為全球化雄心付出隱藏代價。 如果這些憂慮被忽視，一項原本旨在強化香港的政策，反而可能令社會分裂"},{"label":"Paragraph 5","english":"Therefore, Hong Kong must welcome international talent in a way that protects and develops local people. Companies should be encouraged to link overseas recruitment with local training. For every senior specialist hired from abroad, there should be mentorship schemes, knowledge-transfer targets and clear promotion pathways for local staff. Take a technology company hiring an experienced artificial-intelligence researcher: real success would not be that one expert completes one project, but that local colleagues learn enough to lead the next one. The government and educational institutions also have a role to play. Universities, vocational bodies and employers should design courses around emerging industries, such as biotechnology, green finance and digital security, so that Hong Kong students are not always catching up after the market has changed. Scholarships, internships and subsidised re-training should be expanded for young workers and mid-career employees who risk being left behind. At the same time, promotion criteria should be transparent, and pay should reflect responsibility rather than nationality.","chinese":"因此，香港必須以一種能夠保護並培養本地人的方式歡迎國際人才。 企業應被鼓勵把海外招聘與本地培訓連繫起來。 每當企業從海外聘請一位高級專才時，便應該同時設立導師制度、知識轉移目標，以及本地員工清晰的晉升途徑。 以一間科技公司聘請一位經驗豐富的人工智能研究員為例：真正的成功，不是那位專家完成了一個項目，而是本地同事學到足夠知識，能夠領導下一個項目。 政府和教育機構同樣有其角色。 大學、職業培訓機構和僱主應該圍繞新興行業設計課程，例如生物科技、綠色金融和數碼安全，好讓香港學生不會總是在市場改變之後才急於追趕。 獎學金、實習機會和受資助的再培訓計劃，應該擴展至有可能被時代拋下的年輕工人和中年在職人士。 與此同時，晉升準則應該透明，而薪酬亦應反映職責，而不是國籍。"},{"label":"Paragraph 6","english":"All things considered, Hong Kong should not close its door to international talent; doing so would be shortsighted for a city that has always survived by connecting with the world. However, opening the door is not the same as allowing locals to be pushed into the corridor. The best policy is a balanced one - bring in talent where Hong Kong genuinely needs it, require knowledge to be shared, invest seriously in local training and keep opportunity fair from hiring to promotion. If Hong Kong can do this, international talent will not become a threat to the local community. It will become a catalyst for a more capable, confident and outward-looking city.","chinese":"綜合而言，香港不應向國際人才關上大門；對於一個一直靠連接世界而生存的城市來說，這樣做是短視的。 然而，打開大門並不等於容許本地人被推到走廊之外。 最好的政策應該是平衡的：在香港真正需要人才的地方引入人才，要求知識得以分享，認真投資於本地培訓，並從招聘到晉升都保持機會公平。 如果香港能夠做到這一點，國際人才便不會成為本地社區的威脅。 它反而會成為催化劑，推動香港成為一個更有能力、更有信心，也更具國際視野的城市。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"opening the door","chinese":"敞開大門"},{"english":"without leaving locals outside","chinese":"不把本地人排除在外"},{"english":"gone are the days when","chinese":"……的日子已經過去"},{"english":"prosper by relying on","chinese":"靠……而繁榮"},{"english":"talent born within its borders","chinese":"在本地出生的人才"},{"english":"within its borders","chinese":"在其境內"},{"english":"in the past","chinese":"在過去"},{"english":"hire mainly from","chinese":"主要從……聘請"},{"english":"the local community","chinese":"本地社群"},{"english":"search the world for","chinese":"在全球尋找"},{"english":"meet international standards","chinese":"符合國際標準"},{"english":"international standards","chinese":"國際標準"},{"english":"this change has led","chinese":"這個轉變導致"},{"english":"attract international talent","chinese":"吸引國際人才"},{"english":"so as to","chinese":"以便；為了"},{"english":"strengthen the economy","chinese":"強化經濟"},{"english":"sharpen competitiveness","chinese":"提升競爭力"},{"english":"broaden society's outlook","chinese":"擴闊社會視野"},{"english":"my view is not that","chinese":"我的看法並不是"},{"english":"choose foreigners over locals","chinese":"選擇外地人而忽略本地人"},{"english":"locals over foreigners","chinese":"選擇本地人而忽略外地人"},{"english":"rather","chinese":"而是"},{"english":"welcome the world","chinese":"歡迎世界各地的人"},{"english":"ensuring that","chinese":"確保"},{"english":"be pushed aside","chinese":"被擠到一旁"},{"english":"raise standards","chinese":"提高標準"},{"english":"connect Hong Kong to","chinese":"把香港連繫到……"},{"english":"wider networks","chinese":"更廣闊的人脈及網絡"},{"english":"fair policy","chinese":"公平政策"},{"english":"serious local training","chinese":"認真的本地培訓"},{"english":"turn competition into","chinese":"把競爭轉化為……"},{"english":"shared progress","chinese":"共同進步"},{"english":"economic and professional benefits","chinese":"經濟和專業上的好處"},{"english":"skilled newcomers","chinese":"有技能的新來者"},{"english":"fresh habits","chinese":"新做法；新習慣"},{"english":"different ways of solving problems","chinese":"不同的解難方法"},{"english":"a financial analyst","chinese":"金融分析師"},{"english":"European regulations","chinese":"歐洲法規"},{"english":"large-scale software systems","chinese":"大型軟件系統"},{"english":"commercialise research","chinese":"將研究商業化"},{"english":"working beside them","chinese":"與他們共事"},{"english":"local employees","chinese":"本地僱員"},{"english":"global standards","chinese":"全球標準"},{"english":"instead of","chinese":"而不是"},{"english":"locked inside familiar routines","chinese":"被困在熟悉的慣常做法中"},{"english":"familiar routines","chinese":"熟悉的慣常做法"},{"english":"the more diverse…, the more likely…","chinese":"越多元，就越有可能……"},{"english":"a diverse workplace","chinese":"多元化的工作場所"},{"english":"weak assumptions","chinese":"站不住腳的假設"},{"english":"be questioned","chinese":"受到質疑"},{"english":"expensive mistakes","chinese":"代價高昂的錯誤"},{"english":"moreover","chinese":"此外"},{"english":"overseas professionals","chinese":"海外專業人士"},{"english":"act as human bridges","chinese":"充當人際橋樑"},{"english":"a Hong Kong start-up","chinese":"香港初創公司"},{"english":"entering the market","chinese":"進入市場"},{"english":"Middle Eastern market","chinese":"中東市場"},{"english":"language support","chinese":"語言支援"},{"english":"not only…but also…","chinese":"不但……而且……"},{"english":"customs and consumer expectations","chinese":"習俗和消費者期望"},{"english":"in that sense","chinese":"從這個意義上說"},{"english":"talent attraction","chinese":"人才吸引"},{"english":"filling vacancies","chinese":"填補職位空缺"},{"english":"ultimately","chinese":"最終"},{"english":"enlarging Hong Kong's reach","chinese":"擴大香港的影響範圍"},{"english":"that said","chinese":"話雖如此"},{"english":"arrival of overseas talent","chinese":"海外人才的到來"},{"english":"not without challenges","chinese":"並非沒有挑戰"},{"english":"the first concern is","chinese":"第一個關注是"},{"english":"fairness","chinese":"公平"},{"english":"recruit internationally","chinese":"在國際上招聘"},{"english":"local graduates","chinese":"本地畢業生"},{"english":"low-paid junior posts","chinese":"低薪初級職位"},{"english":"resentment is bound to grow","chinese":"不滿情緒必然增加"},{"english":"be bound to","chinese":"必然會"},{"english":"feel discouraged","chinese":"感到氣餒"},{"english":"senior positions","chinese":"高級職位"},{"english":"seem to go to","chinese":"看似落入……手中"},{"english":"brought in from elsewhere","chinese":"從其他地方引入"},{"english":"the presence of outsiders","chinese":"外來者的存在"},{"english":"per se","chinese":"本身"},{"english":"the absence of","chinese":"缺乏"},{"english":"a visible pathway","chinese":"清晰可見的途徑"},{"english":"advance","chinese":"晉升；發展"},{"english":"social integration","chinese":"社會融合"},{"english":"working styles","chinese":"工作方式"},{"english":"create misunderstanding","chinese":"造成誤解"},{"english":"what one culture sees as","chinese":"一種文化視為……的東西"},{"english":"confidence","chinese":"自信"},{"english":"arrogance","chinese":"傲慢"},{"english":"modesty","chinese":"謙遜"},{"english":"be mistaken for","chinese":"被誤以為是……"},{"english":"passivity","chinese":"被動"},{"english":"outside the workplace","chinese":"在工作場所之外"},{"english":"pressure on housing","chinese":"住屋壓力"},{"english":"public services","chinese":"公共服務"},{"english":"residents","chinese":"居民"},{"english":"hidden price","chinese":"隱藏代價"},{"english":"global ambition","chinese":"全球化抱負"},{"english":"such worries","chinese":"這些憂慮"},{"english":"be ignored","chinese":"被忽視"},{"english":"be meant to","chinese":"旨在"},{"english":"instead divide it","chinese":"反而使其分裂"},{"english":"in a way that","chinese":"以一種……的方式"},{"english":"protects and develops","chinese":"保護並培育"},{"english":"be encouraged to","chinese":"應被鼓勵"},{"english":"link…with…","chinese":"把……與……連繫起來"},{"english":"overseas recruitment","chinese":"海外招聘"},{"english":"local training","chinese":"本地培訓"},{"english":"for every senior specialist","chinese":"每聘請一位高級專才"},{"english":"hired from abroad","chinese":"從海外聘請"},{"english":"mentorship schemes","chinese":"導師計劃"},{"english":"knowledge-transfer targets","chinese":"知識轉移目標"},{"english":"promotion pathways","chinese":"晉升途徑"},{"english":"local staff","chinese":"本地員工"},{"english":"artificial-intelligence researcher","chinese":"人工智能研究員"},{"english":"experienced researcher","chinese":"有經驗的研究員"},{"english":"real success would not be that…, but that…","chinese":"真正的成功不在於……而在於……"},{"english":"complete one project","chinese":"完成一個項目"},{"english":"learn enough to lead","chinese":"學到足以帶領"},{"english":"the next one","chinese":"下一個"},{"english":"educational institutions","chinese":"教育機構"},{"english":"have a role to play","chinese":"有角色可發揮"},{"english":"vocational bodies","chinese":"職業培訓機構"},{"english":"design courses around","chinese":"圍繞……設計課程"},{"english":"emerging industries","chinese":"新興產業"},{"english":"biotechnology","chinese":"生物科技"},{"english":"green finance","chinese":"綠色金融"},{"english":"digital security","chinese":"數碼安全"},{"english":"catch up","chinese":"追趕"},{"english":"after the market has changed","chinese":"在市場改變之後"},{"english":"scholarships","chinese":"獎學金"},{"english":"internships","chinese":"實習機會"},{"english":"subsidised re-training","chinese":"受資助再培訓"},{"english":"be expanded for","chinese":"為……擴大"},{"english":"young workers","chinese":"年輕工作者"},{"english":"mid-career employees","chinese":"中年在職人士"},{"english":"risk being left behind","chinese":"有被拋離的風險"},{"english":"at the same time","chinese":"與此同時"},{"english":"promotion criteria","chinese":"晉升準則"},{"english":"transparent","chinese":"透明"},{"english":"pay should reflect responsibility","chinese":"薪酬應反映責任"},{"english":"rather than nationality","chinese":"而不是國籍"},{"english":"close its door to","chinese":"對……關上大門"},{"english":"doing so","chinese":"這樣做"},{"english":"shortsighted","chinese":"目光短淺"},{"english":"survived by connecting with","chinese":"靠連繫……而生存"},{"english":"connecting with the world","chinese":"與世界連繫"},{"english":"not the same as","chinese":"與……並不相同"},{"english":"pushed into the corridor","chinese":"被擠到走廊上"},{"english":"a balanced policy","chinese":"平衡的政策"},{"english":"bring in talent","chinese":"引入人才"},{"english":"genuinely needs it","chinese":"真正需要"},{"english":"require knowledge to be shared","chinese":"要求知識被分享"},{"english":"invest seriously in","chinese":"認真投資於……"},{"english":"keep opportunity fair","chinese":"保持機會公平"},{"english":"from hiring to promotion","chinese":"由招聘到晉升"},{"english":"become a threat to","chinese":"成為對……的威脅"},{"english":"the local community","chinese":"本地社群"},{"english":"a catalyst for","chinese":"……的催化劑"},{"english":"more capable","chinese":"更有能力的"},{"english":"confident and outward-looking","chinese":"自信而具國際視野"},{"english":"outward-looking city","chinese":"面向世界的城市"}]},"dse-writing-2019-part-b-q3":{"exerciseId":"dse-writing-2019-part-b-q3","essayKey":"","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=dse-writing-2019-part-b-q3","flashDeckId":"dse/writing/part-b/2019/Q3","paragraphs":[{"label":"Paragraph 1","english":"When social media was first celebrated, it seemed to offer a democratic miracle: a public square in every pocket. From students discussing school rules to citizens commenting on government policy, anyone could speak, respond and be heard. This has made ordinary users, journalists and platform owners reconsider whether these platforms should shape public conversation so freely in order to protect rational discussion, mutual understanding and civic trust. As far as I am concerned, social media platforms such as Facebook and Twitter do far more to stifle than to encourage public debate. This essay argues that they reward emotional performance over reasoned analysis, trap people in echo chambers and, despite their apparent openness, frighten many reasonable voices into silence.","chinese":""},{"label":"Paragraph 2","english":"First, social media stifles public debate because its design rewards speed, anger and simplicity, not careful thought. A transport fare rise, for example, involves company costs, workers’ wages, passengers’ burdens and long-term planning. Yet once such an issue appears online, it is often squeezed into a slogan, a meme or a sarcastic comment. The more extreme the wording, the more likely it is to attract likes; the more balanced the explanation, the more likely it is to be ignored. In other words, the platform does not merely host debate; it trains users to perform for attention. Before long, people learn that “winning” an argument means sounding confident and humiliating opponents. Complexity is cut down, context is removed, emotion rises, and truth becomes secondary to popularity. Put simply, when attention becomes the prize, logic becomes the casualty.","chinese":""},{"label":"Paragraph 3","english":"Moreover, these platforms push people into echo chambers, thereby weakening the foundation of public debate. A genuine debate requires citizens to meet opposing views, test their assumptions and revise their opinions when evidence points elsewhere. Social media often does the opposite. Users follow friends, influencers and pages that already reflect their tastes; algorithms then supply more of the same because agreement keeps people scrolling. Over time, each feed begins to look like common sense, while the other side appears foolish, immoral or dangerous. Take environmental policy. One user may see posts insisting that any new restriction is an attack on freedom, while another may see posts claiming that any hesitation is selfish. Both may believe they are seeing “public opinion”, when in fact they are seeing a filtered version of it. The result is not a shared forum but a collection of private mirrors. Only when people are exposed to serious disagreement can they learn to argue responsibly.","chinese":""},{"label":"Paragraph 4","english":"Granted, it would be unfair to say that social media never encourages debate. It can give ordinary people a voice, allow citizens to respond instantly to public events and make room at the table for groups that traditional media once overlooked. A resident affected by noise pollution, a student worried about school pressure or a customer treated unfairly can raise an issue without waiting for a newspaper editor’s approval. However, access to a microphone is not the same as access to a meaningful conversation. Many online discussions quickly turn into personal attacks, pile-ons and public shaming. A student who writes, “I support part of the school’s phone policy, but not the punishment system,” may be accused by one side of being obedient and by the other of being irresponsible. Screenshots spread, strangers mock, and the original issue disappears. Under such pressure, many moderate users stay silent. The platform remains noisy, but debate becomes poorer.","chinese":""},{"label":"Paragraph 5","english":"All things considered, social media platforms such as Facebook and Twitter stifle public debate more than they encourage it. They may create the appearance of openness, but they too often reward outrage, divide citizens into like-minded groups and punish nuance. The time has come for platform owners to redesign recommendation systems, for users to verify before sharing, and for schools to teach digital citizenship as seriously as grammar or mathematics. Newspapers, too, should offer moderated spaces where disagreement can be firm without becoming cruel. A healthy society does not need everyone to agree; it needs people to disagree intelligently. Until social media learns to value reason more than reaction, it will remain a crowded square in which everyone is speaking, but too few are truly listening.","chinese":""}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"a public forum","chinese":"公共論壇"},{"english":"social media","chinese":"社交媒體"},{"english":"was first celebrated","chinese":"最初受到讚揚時"},{"english":"democratic miracle","chinese":"民主奇蹟"},{"english":"a public square in every pocket","chinese":"每個人口袋裏的公共廣場"},{"english":"school rules","chinese":"校規"},{"english":"government policy","chinese":"政府政策"},{"english":"comment on","chinese":"評論……"},{"english":"be heard","chinese":"被聽見"},{"english":"ordinary users","chinese":"普通用戶"},{"english":"platform owners","chinese":"平台擁有人"},{"english":"reconsider whether","chinese":"重新考慮是否"},{"english":"shape public conversation","chinese":"塑造公共討論"},{"english":"so freely","chinese":"如此自由地"},{"english":"in order to protect","chinese":"為了保護"},{"english":"rational discussion","chinese":"理性討論"},{"english":"mutual understanding","chinese":"相互理解"},{"english":"civic trust","chinese":"公民信任；社會信任"},{"english":"as far as I am concerned","chinese":"就我而言"},{"english":"platforms such as","chinese":"例如……的平台"},{"english":"do far more to…than to…","chinese":"更大程度上……而不是……"},{"english":"stifle public debate","chinese":"扼殺公眾辯論"},{"english":"encourage public debate","chinese":"鼓勵公眾辯論"},{"english":"reward emotional performance","chinese":"獎勵情緒化表演"},{"english":"over reasoned analysis","chinese":"而不是有理據的分析"},{"english":"trap people in echo chambers","chinese":"把人困在同溫層中"},{"english":"echo chambers","chinese":"同溫層；回音室效應"},{"english":"despite apparent openness","chinese":"儘管表面開放"},{"english":"apparent openness","chinese":"表面上的開放"},{"english":"frighten voices into silence","chinese":"嚇得……不敢發聲"},{"english":"reasonable voices","chinese":"理性的聲音"},{"english":"rewards speed, anger and simplicity","chinese":"獎勵速度、憤怒和簡化"},{"english":"careful thought","chinese":"細心思考"},{"english":"a transport fare rise","chinese":"交通票價上升"},{"english":"for example","chinese":"例如"},{"english":"company costs","chinese":"公司成本"},{"english":"workers' wages","chinese":"工人工資"},{"english":"passengers' burdens","chinese":"乘客負擔"},{"english":"long-term planning","chinese":"長遠規劃"},{"english":"such an issue","chinese":"這類議題"},{"english":"be squeezed into","chinese":"被壓縮成"},{"english":"a slogan","chinese":"口號"},{"english":"a meme","chinese":"網絡迷因"},{"english":"a sarcastic comment","chinese":"諷刺評論"},{"english":"the more…the more…","chinese":"越……越……"},{"english":"extreme wording","chinese":"極端措辭"},{"english":"be likely to","chinese":"很可能"},{"english":"attract likes","chinese":"吸引讚好"},{"english":"balanced explanation","chinese":"平衡的解釋"},{"english":"be ignored","chinese":"被忽略"},{"english":"in other words","chinese":"換言之"},{"english":"not merely host debate","chinese":"不只是承載辯論"},{"english":"train users to","chinese":"訓練用戶去……"},{"english":"perform for attention","chinese":"為吸引注意而表演"},{"english":"before long","chinese":"不久之後"},{"english":"winning an argument","chinese":"贏得爭論"},{"english":"sound confident","chinese":"聽起來有信心"},{"english":"humiliate opponents","chinese":"羞辱對手"},{"english":"complexity is cut down","chinese":"複雜性被削減"},{"english":"context is removed","chinese":"背景脈絡被刪去"},{"english":"emotion rises","chinese":"情緒升溫"},{"english":"become secondary to","chinese":"變得次於……"},{"english":"popularity","chinese":"受歡迎程度；人氣"},{"english":"put simply","chinese":"簡單來說"},{"english":"attention becomes the prize","chinese":"注意力成為獎賞"},{"english":"logic becomes the casualty","chinese":"邏輯成為犧牲品"},{"english":"moreover","chinese":"此外"},{"english":"push people into","chinese":"把人推進……"},{"english":"thereby weakening","chinese":"從而削弱"},{"english":"the foundation of public debate","chinese":"公眾辯論的基礎"},{"english":"genuine debate","chinese":"真正的辯論"},{"english":"opposing views","chinese":"相反意見"},{"english":"test their assumptions","chinese":"檢視自己的假設"},{"english":"revise their opinions","chinese":"修正自己的看法"},{"english":"evidence points elsewhere","chinese":"證據指向其他結論"},{"english":"do the opposite","chinese":"做相反的事"},{"english":"influencers","chinese":"網絡紅人；意見領袖"},{"english":"reflect their tastes","chinese":"反映他們的喜好"},{"english":"algorithms","chinese":"演算法"},{"english":"supply more of the same","chinese":"提供更多同類內容"},{"english":"agreement keeps people scrolling","chinese":"認同感令用戶不斷滑動瀏覽"},{"english":"over time","chinese":"隨著時間過去"},{"english":"each feed","chinese":"每個資訊流"},{"english":"common sense","chinese":"常識"},{"english":"the other side","chinese":"另一方"},{"english":"appear foolish","chinese":"顯得愚蠢"},{"english":"immoral or dangerous","chinese":"不道德或危險"},{"english":"environmental policy","chinese":"環境政策"},{"english":"posts insisting that","chinese":"堅稱……的帖文"},{"english":"any new restriction","chinese":"任何新限制"},{"english":"an attack on freedom","chinese":"對自由的攻擊"},{"english":"posts claiming that","chinese":"聲稱……的帖文"},{"english":"any hesitation","chinese":"任何猶豫"},{"english":"selfish","chinese":"自私的"},{"english":"public opinion","chinese":"公眾意見"},{"english":"when in fact","chinese":"但事實上"},{"english":"a filtered version of","chinese":"經過篩選的版本"},{"english":"the result is not…but…","chinese":"結果不是……而是……"},{"english":"a shared forum","chinese":"共同論壇"},{"english":"a collection of private mirrors","chinese":"一堆私人鏡子"},{"english":"only when","chinese":"只有當……時"},{"english":"be exposed to","chinese":"接觸到……"},{"english":"serious disagreement","chinese":"嚴肅的分歧"},{"english":"argue responsibly","chinese":"負責任地辯論"},{"english":"granted","chinese":"誠然"},{"english":"it would be unfair to say","chinese":"說……並不公平"},{"english":"give ordinary people a voice","chinese":"讓普通人有發聲機會"},{"english":"respond instantly to","chinese":"即時回應……"},{"english":"public events","chinese":"公共事件"},{"english":"make room at the table for","chinese":"為……提供參與空間"},{"english":"traditional media","chinese":"傳統媒體"},{"english":"overlook","chinese":"忽略"},{"english":"noise pollution","chinese":"噪音污染"},{"english":"school pressure","chinese":"學校壓力"},{"english":"treated unfairly","chinese":"受到不公平對待"},{"english":"raise an issue","chinese":"提出問題"},{"english":"newspaper editor's approval","chinese":"報章編輯的批准"},{"english":"access to a microphone","chinese":"有機會發聲"},{"english":"not the same as","chinese":"不等同於"},{"english":"meaningful conversation","chinese":"有意義的對話"},{"english":"turn into","chinese":"變成"},{"english":"personal attacks","chinese":"人身攻擊"},{"english":"pile-ons","chinese":"群起圍攻"},{"english":"public shaming","chinese":"公開羞辱"},{"english":"support part of","chinese":"支持……的一部分"},{"english":"phone policy","chinese":"手機政策"},{"english":"punishment system","chinese":"懲罰制度"},{"english":"be accused by one side of","chinese":"被其中一方指責為……"},{"english":"obedient","chinese":"順從的"},{"english":"irresponsible","chinese":"不負責任的"},{"english":"screenshots spread","chinese":"截圖傳開"},{"english":"strangers mock","chinese":"陌生人嘲笑"},{"english":"the original issue disappears","chinese":"原本的議題消失"},{"english":"under such pressure","chinese":"在這種壓力下"},{"english":"moderate users","chinese":"立場溫和的用戶"},{"english":"stay silent","chinese":"保持沉默"},{"english":"remains noisy","chinese":"仍然嘈雜"},{"english":"becomes poorer","chinese":"變得更貧乏"},{"english":"all things considered","chinese":"綜合考慮各方面"},{"english":"more than they encourage it","chinese":"多於鼓勵它"},{"english":"create the appearance of","chinese":"製造……的表象"},{"english":"openness","chinese":"開放性"},{"english":"reward outrage","chinese":"獎勵憤怒情緒"},{"english":"divide citizens into","chinese":"把市民分成……"},{"english":"like-minded groups","chinese":"想法相近的群體"},{"english":"punish nuance","chinese":"懲罰細緻觀點"},{"english":"the time has come for","chinese":"是時候……"},{"english":"recommendation systems","chinese":"推薦系統"},{"english":"verify before sharing","chinese":"分享前核實"},{"english":"digital citizenship","chinese":"數碼公民意識"},{"english":"as seriously as","chinese":"像……一樣認真地"},{"english":"moderated spaces","chinese":"有管理的討論空間"},{"english":"disagreement","chinese":"分歧；不同意見"},{"english":"firm without becoming cruel","chinese":"堅定而不變得殘酷"},{"english":"a healthy society","chinese":"健康的社會"},{"english":"disagree intelligently","chinese":"理性而聰明地表達不同意見"},{"english":"value reason more than reaction","chinese":"重視理性多於即時反應"},{"english":"remain a crowded square","chinese":"仍然是一個擁擠的廣場"},{"english":"truly listening","chinese":"真正聆聽"}]},"dse-writing-2019-part-b-q4":{"exerciseId":"dse-writing-2019-part-b-q4","essayKey":"","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=dse-writing-2019-part-b-q4","flashDeckId":"dse/writing/part-b/2019/Q4","paragraphs":[{"label":"Paragraph 1","english":"Rival captain’s quick thinking steals spotlight in season finale","chinese":"對手隊長的機警反應，成為球季決賽焦點"},{"label":"Paragraph 2","english":"By Chris Wong, Young Post Sports Reporter","chinese":"《Young Post》體育版記者 Chris Wong 報道"},{"label":"Paragraph 3","english":"The final game of the season between St. George’s School and Royal College was expected to decide a championship. Instead, it delivered a moment of courage that left both sets of supporters applauding the same player.","chinese":"St. George’s School 與 Royal College 之間的球季最後一戰，原本被視為決定冠軍誰屬的一場比賽。 結果，這場比賽呈現了一個勇氣時刻，令雙方支持者都為同一名球員鼓掌。"},{"label":"Paragraph 4","english":"The highly anticipated football match at King’s Park Sports Ground was suspended yesterday after St. George’s striker Marcus Lee collapsed following a heavy collision in the 68th minute. With the score locked at 1-1 and the crowd roaring for a winner, Lee chased a long pass into the penalty area and collided with Royal College goalkeeper Ryan Ho, who had rushed out to clear the ball. For a few seconds, the stadium seemed to hold its breath.","chinese":"這場備受期待、昨日在京士柏運動場舉行的足球賽，在第 68 分鐘因 St. George’s 前鋒 Marcus Lee 在一次猛烈碰撞後倒地而暫停。 當時比分仍然停留在 1 比 1，觀眾正高聲期待勝負分曉；Lee 追逐一記長傳衝入禁區，並與衝出來解圍的 Royal College 守門員 Ryan Ho 相撞。 有幾秒鐘，整個球場彷彿屏住了呼吸。"},{"label":"Paragraph 5","english":"No one saw it coming. At first, several players thought Lee was simply winded. However, Royal College captain Adrian Wong, standing barely five metres away, noticed that Lee was not responding. He immediately waved frantically towards the referee and shouted for the medical team. While others froze, Wong knelt beside his rival, told players not to move him, and kept talking to him until the school nurses arrived.","chinese":"沒有人預料到這一幕會發生。 起初，幾名球員以為 Lee 只是被撞得一時喘不過氣。 然而，當時站在不到五米外的 Royal College 隊長 Adrian Wong 留意到 Lee 已經沒有反應。 他立即焦急地向球證揮手，並大聲呼叫醫療隊入場。 其他人一時愣住之際，Wong 跪在對手身旁，叫其他球員不要移動他，並一直對他說話，直到校方護士到場。"},{"label":"Paragraph 6","english":"“I only remembered what our first-aid teacher had drilled into us,” Wong said after the match. “You do not see a St. George’s shirt or a Royal College shirt in that moment. You see a person who needs help.”","chinese":"「我只是記起急救老師一直反覆教我們的東西，」Wong 在賽後說。 「在那一刻，你看到的已不再是一件 St. George’s 球衣或 Royal College 球衣。 你看到的是一個需要幫助的人。」"},{"label":"Paragraph 7","english":"Referee Daniel Yip stopped the match at once and cleared the area around Lee. As a precaution, both teams were sent to their benches while teachers moved spectators back from the touchline. Two school nurses, an off-duty parent who works as an emergency doctor, and St. George’s coach Mr Anthony Lam attended to Lee before paramedics arrived eight minutes later. When Lee was carried into the ambulance, conscious and able to raise his thumb, the anxious silence finally broke into applause.","chinese":"球證 Daniel Yip 立即暫停比賽，並清空 Lee 身旁的範圍。 為安全起見，兩隊球員都被安排返回後備席，教師則把觀眾從邊線旁移後。 兩名校方護士、一名休班急症室醫生家長，以及 St. George’s 教練 Anthony Lam 先生，在救護員八分鐘後抵達前一直照料 Lee。 當 Lee 被抬上救護車時，他仍然清醒，並能夠豎起拇指；現場緊張的沉默終於化成掌聲。"},{"label":"Paragraph 8","english":"Following the incident, officials held a 20-minute discussion with both principals, coaches and the referee. Although the players were willing to continue, the match was abandoned on safety grounds and will resume next Saturday from the 68th minute, with the score remaining 1-1.","chinese":"事件發生後，賽事負責人與雙方校長、教練及球證進行了 20 分鐘討論。 雖然球員都願意繼續比賽，但基於安全理由，賽事最終被腰斬，並會於下星期六由第 68 分鐘起重新開始，比分維持 1 比 1。"},{"label":"Paragraph 9","english":"Mr Lam, who looked visibly shaken, praised Wong for acting “with remarkable calm”. “Rivalry is part of school sport, but there is a line we never cross,” he said. “Adrian understood that faster than any adult on the field. His response may have prevented the situation from becoming much worse.”","chinese":"Lam 先生明顯仍受驚，但他讚揚 Wong 表現出「令人印象深刻的冷靜」。 「競爭是學界運動的一部分，但有一條界線是我們永遠不能越過的，」他說。 「Adrian 比場上任何一位成年人都更快明白這一點。 他的反應可能阻止了情況進一步惡化。」"},{"label":"Paragraph 10","english":"Royal College coach Ms Grace Tang said her team had been desperate to win the league title, but the incident had put the result into perspective. “Of course our boys want the trophy,” she said. “That said, what happened today reminds them that sport is not just about beating opponents; Most importantly, it is about respecting them.”","chinese":"Royal College 教練 Grace Tang 女士表示，她的球隊原本極度渴望贏得聯賽冠軍，但這次事件讓大家重新看待比賽結果的意義。 「我們的男孩當然想要獎盃，」她說。 「不過，今天發生的事提醒了他們，運動不只是擊敗對手；最重要的是尊重對手。」"},{"label":"Paragraph 11","english":"Not everyone was able to process the sudden turn calmly. St. George’s midfielder Jayden Fong, Lee’s closest friend on the team, admitted that he had “felt completely helpless”. “One moment we were pushing for the winning goal; the next, Marcus was on the ground and nobody knew what was happening,” he said. “I cannot thank Adrian enough.”","chinese":"並非每個人都能冷靜地消化這個突如其來的轉折。 St. George’s 中場球員 Jayden Fong 是 Lee 在隊中最親近的朋友；他承認自己當時「感到完全無助」。 「前一刻我們還在爭取致勝入球；下一刻 Marcus 已經倒在地上，沒有人知道發生甚麼事，」他說。 「我怎樣感謝 Adrian 都不夠。」"},{"label":"Paragraph 12","english":"The two student sections, usually famous for trading chants, also changed tone. Several Royal College students started chanting Lee’s name as he was taken away, while St. George’s supporters later applauded Wong when he left the pitch. Many, if not most, spectators remained in their seats long after the announcement, discussing the incident in unusually quiet voices.","chinese":"兩邊學生觀眾區平日以互相叫喊打氣聞名，但這次語氣也改變了。 當 Lee 被送走時，幾名 Royal College 學生開始高喊他的名字；其後 Wong 離場時，St. George’s 支持者也向他鼓掌。 許多觀眾，甚至可以說大部分觀眾，在賽會宣布決定後仍久久留在座位上，以異常安靜的聲音討論這次事件。"},{"label":"Paragraph 13","english":"In a statement released last night, St. George’s said Lee was in stable condition and would remain under observation. Lee also sent a short message through his coach: “Thank you to everyone who helped me. I am fine, and Adrian is a legend.”","chinese":"St. George’s 昨晚發表聲明，表示 Lee 情況穩定，並會繼續留院觀察。 Lee 也透過教練傳來一段簡短訊息：「多謝每一位幫助我的人。 我沒事，Adrian 是傳奇。」"},{"label":"Paragraph 14","english":"Once the dust settles, the league title will still have to be decided. Yet whatever happens when the rivals meet again, yesterday’s match has already produced its defining image: a Royal College captain kneeling beside a St. George’s player, proving that the fiercest rivalry can still leave room for humanity.","chinese":"待事件平靜下來後，聯賽冠軍仍然需要分出高下。 然而，無論這對宿敵再次交手時會發生甚麼，昨天的比賽已經留下了最具代表性的畫面：一名 Royal College 隊長跪在一名 St. George’s 球員身旁，證明即使是最激烈的競爭，也仍然可以為人性留下一席之地。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"rival captain","chinese":"對手隊長"},{"english":"quick thinking","chinese":"快速反應；機智反應"},{"english":"steal the spotlight","chinese":"搶盡風頭"},{"english":"season finale","chinese":"賽季最後一場比賽"},{"english":"sports reporter","chinese":"體育記者"},{"english":"final game of the season","chinese":"賽季最後一場比賽"},{"english":"be expected to","chinese":"預計會"},{"english":"decide a championship","chinese":"決定冠軍誰屬"},{"english":"deliver a moment of courage","chinese":"帶來勇敢的一刻"},{"english":"both sets of supporters","chinese":"雙方支持者"},{"english":"applaud the same player","chinese":"為同一名球員鼓掌"},{"english":"highly anticipated","chinese":"備受期待的"},{"english":"football match","chinese":"足球賽"},{"english":"sports ground","chinese":"運動場"},{"english":"be suspended","chinese":"被暫停"},{"english":"striker","chinese":"前鋒"},{"english":"collapse following","chinese":"在……後倒下"},{"english":"heavy collision","chinese":"嚴重碰撞"},{"english":"in the 68th minute","chinese":"在第68分鐘"},{"english":"with the score locked at","chinese":"比分鎖定在"},{"english":"the crowd roaring for","chinese":"觀眾高呼希望……"},{"english":"chase a long pass","chinese":"追逐一記長傳"},{"english":"penalty area","chinese":"禁區"},{"english":"collide with","chinese":"與……相撞"},{"english":"goalkeeper","chinese":"守門員"},{"english":"rush out to","chinese":"衝出來去"},{"english":"clear the ball","chinese":"解圍"},{"english":"for a few seconds","chinese":"有幾秒鐘"},{"english":"hold its breath","chinese":"屏息以待"},{"english":"no one saw it coming","chinese":"沒有人預料到"},{"english":"at first","chinese":"起初"},{"english":"simply winded","chinese":"只是喘不過氣"},{"english":"standing barely five metres away","chinese":"站在不足五米外"},{"english":"barely","chinese":"僅僅；不足"},{"english":"not responding","chinese":"沒有反應"},{"english":"immediately","chinese":"立即"},{"english":"wave frantically","chinese":"拼命揮手"},{"english":"towards the referee","chinese":"向裁判"},{"english":"shout for","chinese":"大聲呼叫"},{"english":"medical team","chinese":"醫療隊"},{"english":"while others froze","chinese":"當其他人愣住時"},{"english":"freeze","chinese":"呆住；愣住"},{"english":"kneel beside","chinese":"跪在……旁邊"},{"english":"rival","chinese":"對手"},{"english":"tell players not to","chinese":"告訴球員不要"},{"english":"move him","chinese":"移動他"},{"english":"keep talking to","chinese":"一直跟……說話"},{"english":"school nurses","chinese":"學校護士"},{"english":"after the match","chinese":"賽後"},{"english":"first-aid teacher","chinese":"急救老師"},{"english":"drill something into someone","chinese":"反覆教導某人"},{"english":"in that moment","chinese":"在那一刻"},{"english":"needs help","chinese":"需要幫助"},{"english":"at once","chinese":"立即"},{"english":"clear the area around","chinese":"清空……周圍範圍"},{"english":"as a precaution","chinese":"作為預防措施"},{"english":"be sent to their benches","chinese":"被安排返回後備席"},{"english":"move spectators back","chinese":"叫觀眾退後"},{"english":"touchline","chinese":"邊線"},{"english":"off-duty parent","chinese":"休班家長"},{"english":"emergency doctor","chinese":"急症科醫生"},{"english":"attend to","chinese":"照顧；處理"},{"english":"paramedics","chinese":"救護員"},{"english":"eight minutes later","chinese":"八分鐘後"},{"english":"be carried into the ambulance","chinese":"被抬上救護車"},{"english":"conscious","chinese":"清醒的"},{"english":"raise his thumb","chinese":"豎起拇指"},{"english":"anxious silence","chinese":"焦急的沉默"},{"english":"break into applause","chinese":"爆發掌聲"},{"english":"following the incident","chinese":"事件發生後"},{"english":"officials","chinese":"賽事職員；官方人員"},{"english":"hold a discussion","chinese":"進行討論"},{"english":"principals","chinese":"校長"},{"english":"willing to continue","chinese":"願意繼續"},{"english":"be abandoned on safety grounds","chinese":"基於安全理由被腰斬"},{"english":"safety grounds","chinese":"安全理由"},{"english":"resume next Saturday","chinese":"下星期六恢復進行"},{"english":"from the 68th minute","chinese":"由第68分鐘開始"},{"english":"with the score remaining","chinese":"比分維持在"},{"english":"visibly shaken","chinese":"明顯受驚；神情震驚"},{"english":"praise someone for","chinese":"因……讚揚某人"},{"english":"act with remarkable calm","chinese":"表現得異常冷靜"},{"english":"remarkable calm","chinese":"非常冷靜"},{"english":"rivalry","chinese":"競爭；敵對關係"},{"english":"school sport","chinese":"校園體育"},{"english":"a line we never cross","chinese":"絕不能越過的底線"},{"english":"on the field","chinese":"在球場上"},{"english":"prevent the situation from","chinese":"防止情況……"},{"english":"becoming much worse","chinese":"變得嚴重得多"},{"english":"be desperate to","chinese":"非常渴望"},{"english":"league title","chinese":"聯賽冠軍"},{"english":"put the result into perspective","chinese":"令人重新看待賽果的重要性"},{"english":"want the trophy","chinese":"想贏得獎盃"},{"english":"that said","chinese":"話雖如此"},{"english":"not just about","chinese":"不只是關於"},{"english":"beat opponents","chinese":"擊敗對手"},{"english":"most importantly","chinese":"最重要的是"},{"english":"process the sudden turn","chinese":"消化突如其來的轉變"},{"english":"sudden turn","chinese":"突如其來的轉變"},{"english":"calmly","chinese":"冷靜地"},{"english":"midfielder","chinese":"中場球員"},{"english":"closest friend on the team","chinese":"隊中最親密的朋友"},{"english":"admit that","chinese":"承認"},{"english":"feel completely helpless","chinese":"感到完全無助"},{"english":"one moment…, the next…","chinese":"前一刻……下一刻……"},{"english":"push for","chinese":"努力爭取"},{"english":"winning goal","chinese":"致勝入球"},{"english":"on the ground","chinese":"倒在地上"},{"english":"cannot thank someone enough","chinese":"對某人感激不盡"},{"english":"student sections","chinese":"學生打氣區"},{"english":"be famous for","chinese":"以……聞名"},{"english":"trade chants","chinese":"互相喊打氣口號"},{"english":"change tone","chinese":"改變語氣；氣氛轉變"},{"english":"chant someone's name","chinese":"高呼某人的名字"},{"english":"be taken away","chinese":"被送走"},{"english":"supporters","chinese":"支持者"},{"english":"leave the pitch","chinese":"離開球場"},{"english":"many, if not most","chinese":"很多，甚至大多數"},{"english":"remain in their seats","chinese":"留在座位上"},{"english":"long after","chinese":"在……很久之後"},{"english":"announcement","chinese":"公告"},{"english":"unusually quiet voices","chinese":"異常安靜的聲音"},{"english":"in a statement released last night","chinese":"在昨晚發出的聲明中"},{"english":"released last night","chinese":"昨晚發出"},{"english":"in stable condition","chinese":"情況穩定"},{"english":"remain under observation","chinese":"留院觀察"},{"english":"send a short message through","chinese":"透過……發出簡短訊息"},{"english":"everyone who helped me","chinese":"所有幫助過我的人"},{"english":"a legend","chinese":"傳奇人物；非常了不起的人"},{"english":"once the dust settles","chinese":"待事情平息後"},{"english":"have to be decided","chinese":"仍須決定"},{"english":"whatever happens","chinese":"無論發生甚麼"},{"english":"meet again","chinese":"再次交手"},{"english":"defining image","chinese":"最具代表性的畫面"},{"english":"kneeling beside","chinese":"跪在……旁邊"},{"english":"prove that","chinese":"證明"},{"english":"the fiercest rivalry","chinese":"最激烈的競爭"},{"english":"leave room for","chinese":"為……留下空間"},{"english":"humanity","chinese":"人性；人情味"}]},"dse-writing-2019-part-b-q5":{"exerciseId":"dse-writing-2019-part-b-q5","essayKey":"","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=dse-writing-2019-part-b-q5","flashDeckId":"dse/writing/part-b/2019/Q5","paragraphs":[{"label":"Paragraph 1","english":"Beyond the Scroll: How I Follow Fashion and Music Without Losing My Head","chinese":"超越滑動螢幕：我是如何追蹤時尚與音樂潮流而不迷失方向"},{"label":"Paragraph 2","english":"For better or worse, pop culture no longer waits for Saturday newspapers or monthly magazines. A lipstick shade can go viral before the model leaves the lift; a singer’s acoustic clip can turn a quiet song into everyone’s homework soundtrack overnight. This has made young readers like me look for a wiser way to follow trends, not just to seem fashionable, but to enjoy culture without becoming a puppet of the algorithm. My answer is neither “old media” nor “new media” alone. For style and beauty, and for music and concerts, I prefer a mixed menu: quick videos to spot what is moving, then reliable magazines and reviews to decide whether it is worth my attention.","chinese":"無論好壞，流行文化已不再等待星期六出版的報紙或每月一期的雜誌。 一款唇膏色號可以在模特兒離開升降機之前就爆紅；一位歌手的不插電片段，也可以在一夜之間把一首安靜的歌曲變成大家做功課時的背景音樂。 這使像我一樣的年輕讀者開始尋找一種更明智的方式去追蹤潮流：不只是為了顯得時尚，也是為了享受文化，同時避免成為演算法的傀儡。 我的答案並非單純選擇「舊媒體」或「新媒體」其中一方。 在時尚與美容，以及音樂與演唱會方面，我偏好一份混合式的資訊餐單：先用快速影片留意正在流行的事物，再用可靠的雜誌和評論判斷它是否值得我的注意。"},{"label":"Paragraph 3","english":"When it comes to style and beauty, my first stop is social media, especially TikTok, Instagram Reels and YouTube Shorts, because fashion is visual by nature. You do not just read about a jacket; you want to see how it falls on different bodies, how it moves, and how people style it outside a studio. For example, when “clean girl” make-up, ballet-core ribbons or oversized denim began appearing everywhere, I noticed them first through students, stylists and make-up artists posting get-ready-with-me clips. The more frequently a look appears across different accounts, the more confident I become that it is a wider trend taking shape. That way, I can identify the mood early.","chinese":"談到時尚與美容，我的第一站是社交媒體，尤其是 TikTok、Instagram Reels 和 YouTube Shorts，因為時尚本質上是一種視覺文化。 閱讀一件外套的介紹並不足夠；你會想看它穿在不同身形上的垂墜感、它如何隨身體移動，以及人們在攝影棚以外如何配搭它。 例如，當「clean girl」妝容、芭蕾風絲帶或寬鬆牛仔服開始到處出現時，我最先是透過學生、造型師和化妝師發布的 get-ready-with-me 影片留意到它們。 一種造型在不同帳戶中出現得越頻繁，我就越有信心相信它是一個正在成形的更大潮流。 這樣一來，我便能及早辨認出當下的潮流氣氛。"},{"label":"Paragraph 4","english":"However, speed by itself is not enough. The trouble with social media is that it can make every product look essential, even when the recommendation is little more than an advertisement in disguise. For that reason, I usually check Teen Vogue and Highsnobiety before deciding whether a trend deserves my money or attention. Teen Vogue explains fashion in a student-friendly voice, while Highsnobiety is excellent for streetwear and youth culture. Take the “quiet luxury” look, for example: videos may show the beige blazer, but magazines explain the deeper idea behind it—minimal branding, better tailoring and long-term wear. This is why my recommendation is using social media to discover style, but digital magazines to judge it.","chinese":"然而，速度本身並不足夠。 社交媒體的問題在於，它可以令每件產品看起來都必不可少，即使那些推薦說穿了只是一則披著分享外衣的廣告。 正因如此，在決定一個潮流是否值得我花錢或投入注意力之前，我通常會查看 Teen Vogue 和 Highsnobiety。 Teen Vogue 會用適合學生理解的語氣解釋時尚；Highsnobiety 則非常擅長介紹街頭服飾和青年文化。 以「quiet luxury」造型為例：影片可能會展示米色西裝外套，但雜誌會解釋其背後更深層的理念——低調品牌標誌、更好的剪裁，以及長期穿著價值。 因此，我的建議很清楚：用社交媒體去發現時尚，再用數碼雜誌去判斷時尚"},{"label":"Paragraph 5","english":"Music and concerts are slightly different. I still read reviews from Pitchfork because good criticism teaches me how to listen. It points out the production, lyrics and cultural references that I may miss on first hearing. Nevertheless, I would be lying if I said I discovered most new songs through written reviews. Most of the time, music reaches me through short videos, playlists and live clips. A song that sounds ordinary on a streaming platform may suddenly make sense when I see the singer perform it live. That is why I often turn to YouTube, especially Tiny Concerts Live Studio. The setting is small, but that is exactly its charm. Without fireworks or heavy editing, an artist has nowhere to hide.","chinese":"音樂和演唱會則稍為不同。 我仍然會閱讀 Pitchfork 的評論，因為好的評論能教我如何聆聽音樂。 它會指出我第一次聽歌時可能錯過的製作細節、歌詞意義和文化指涉。 然而，如果我說自己大多數新歌都是透過文字評論發現的，那就未免不誠實 大多數時候，音樂是透過短片、播放清單和現場演出片段傳到我耳中的。 一首在串流平台上聽起來平平無奇的歌曲，當我看到歌手現場演唱時，可能突然變得合理而動人。 這就是為甚麼我經常轉向 YouTube，尤其是 Tiny Concerts Live Studio。 場景雖小，魅力恰恰也在這裡。 少了煙火效果，也少了大量剪接，藝術家便無處可藏。"},{"label":"Paragraph 6","english":"My favourite routine is to use Pitchfork for context and Tiny Concerts Live Studio for proof. A case in point is discovering an artist through a review, then watching a live session to see whether the music stands up without studio polish. This method has saved me from following hype blindly. Not every viral chorus belongs on my playlist, and not every underrated singer is boring. Sometimes the online crowd is right; sometimes it is simply loud. What matters is not whether a source is traditional or trendy, but whether it helps me think more clearly.","chinese":"我最喜歡的習慣，是用 Pitchfork 來獲取背景脈絡，再用 Tiny Concerts Live Studio 來驗證實力。 一個恰當的例子是：先透過一篇評論發現一位音樂人，然後觀看其現場演出，看看那些音樂在沒有錄音室修飾的情況下是否仍然站得住腳。 這個方法讓我避免盲目追隨炒作。 並非每段爆紅副歌都應該出現在我的播放清單中；每位被低估的歌手也不一定沉悶無趣。 有時網上群眾是對的；有時他們只是聲音很大。 關鍵不在於一個資訊來源是傳統還是時髦，重點在於它能否幫助我更清晰地思考。"},{"label":"Paragraph 7","english":"So, to readers of Young Post, I would say this: do not choose between newspapers and social media as if one must destroy the other. There is something to be said for both. Social media gives us immediacy, colour and surprise; magazines and reviews give us background, judgement and vocabulary. If you haven’t already, try building your own pop-culture “information diet”: TikTok and Instagram for first impressions, Teen Vogue and Highsnobiety for style, Pitchfork for music criticism, and Tiny Concerts Live Studio for live performance. Trends will keep changing—sooner or later, today’s must-have item will become tomorrow’s joke. Still, with the right sources, we can enjoy the scroll without being controlled by it. Pop culture, after all, is not just about keeping up; it is also about knowing what is worth carrying with us.","chinese":"所以，對《Young Post》的讀者，我會這樣說：不要在報紙和社交媒體之間作出非此即彼的選擇，彷彿其中一方一定要消滅另一方。 兩者其實都有值得肯定之處。 社交媒體給予我們即時性、色彩和驚喜；雜誌與評論則給予我們背景、判斷力和表達詞彙。 如果你還未這樣做，不妨嘗試建立自己的流行文化「資訊餐單」：用 TikTok 和 Instagram 形成第一印象，用 Teen Vogue 和 Highsnobiety 了解時尚，用 Pitchfork 閱讀音樂評論，再用 Tiny Concerts Live Studio 觀看現場演出。 潮流會不斷改變——遲早有一天，今天人人都說必須擁有的東西，會變成明天的笑話。 儘管如此，只要有合適的資訊來源，我們仍然可以享受滑動螢幕的樂趣，同時不被它控制。 畢竟，流行文化不只關乎追上潮流；它同樣關乎知道甚麼值得我們一直帶在身邊。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"beyond the scroll","chinese":"不止於滑手機瀏覽"},{"english":"follow fashion and music","chinese":"關注時裝和音樂潮流"},{"english":"without losing my head","chinese":"不失去理性；不被衝昏頭腦"},{"english":"for better or worse","chinese":"不論好壞；無論利弊"},{"english":"pop culture","chinese":"流行文化"},{"english":"no longer waits for","chinese":"不再等待"},{"english":"Saturday newspapers","chinese":"星期六報紙"},{"english":"monthly magazines","chinese":"月刊"},{"english":"lipstick shade","chinese":"唇膏色號"},{"english":"go viral","chinese":"在網上爆紅；瘋傳"},{"english":"before the model leaves the lift","chinese":"在模特兒離開升降機前"},{"english":"acoustic clip","chinese":"原音片段"},{"english":"turn something into","chinese":"把……變成"},{"english":"quiet song","chinese":"安靜的歌曲"},{"english":"homework soundtrack","chinese":"做功課時的背景音樂"},{"english":"overnight","chinese":"一夜之間"},{"english":"young readers like me","chinese":"像我這樣的年輕讀者"},{"english":"a wiser way to","chinese":"更明智地……的方法"},{"english":"follow trends","chinese":"追蹤潮流"},{"english":"not just to seem fashionable","chinese":"不只是為了顯得時尚"},{"english":"enjoy culture","chinese":"享受文化"},{"english":"become a puppet of","chinese":"成為……的傀儡"},{"english":"the algorithm","chinese":"推薦算法"},{"english":"neither...nor...alone","chinese":"既不是單靠……也不是單靠……"},{"english":"old media","chinese":"舊媒體；傳統媒體"},{"english":"new media","chinese":"新媒體"},{"english":"style and beauty","chinese":"造型與美容"},{"english":"music and concerts","chinese":"音樂與演唱會"},{"english":"a mixed menu","chinese":"混合選擇"},{"english":"quick videos","chinese":"短片；快速影片"},{"english":"spot what is moving","chinese":"察覺正在流行的東西"},{"english":"reliable magazines and reviews","chinese":"可靠的雜誌和評論"},{"english":"worth my attention","chinese":"值得我注意"},{"english":"when it comes to","chinese":"說到……"},{"english":"my first stop","chinese":"我的第一站"},{"english":"social media","chinese":"社交媒體"},{"english":"by nature","chinese":"本質上"},{"english":"read about","chinese":"閱讀關於……的資料"},{"english":"see how it falls on different bodies","chinese":"看它穿在不同身形上的垂墜效果"},{"english":"style it outside a studio","chinese":"在攝影棚外配搭它"},{"english":"clean girl make-up","chinese":"clean girl 妝容"},{"english":"ballet-core ribbons","chinese":"芭蕾風絲帶"},{"english":"oversized denim","chinese":"寬鬆牛仔服飾"},{"english":"begin appearing everywhere","chinese":"開始到處出現"},{"english":"notice something first through","chinese":"最先透過……留意到某事"},{"english":"make-up artists","chinese":"化妝師"},{"english":"get-ready-with-me clips","chinese":"一起準備出門短片"},{"english":"across different accounts","chinese":"在不同帳戶上"},{"english":"a wider trend taking shape","chinese":"一個更廣泛的潮流正在形成"},{"english":"identify the mood early","chinese":"及早掌握潮流氣氛"},{"english":"speed by itself","chinese":"單靠速度"},{"english":"the trouble with","chinese":"……的問題在於"},{"english":"make every product look essential","chinese":"令每件產品看似必不可少"},{"english":"little more than","chinese":"不過是；只不過是"},{"english":"an advertisement in disguise","chinese":"變相廣告"},{"english":"for that reason","chinese":"因此"},{"english":"before deciding whether","chinese":"在決定是否……之前"},{"english":"deserve my money or attention","chinese":"值得我花錢或注意"},{"english":"student-friendly voice","chinese":"適合學生閱讀的語氣"},{"english":"streetwear","chinese":"街頭服飾"},{"english":"youth culture","chinese":"青年文化"},{"english":"quiet luxury look","chinese":"低調奢華風"},{"english":"beige blazer","chinese":"米色西裝外套"},{"english":"the deeper idea behind","chinese":"背後更深層的理念"},{"english":"minimal branding","chinese":"極簡品牌標誌"},{"english":"better tailoring","chinese":"更好的剪裁"},{"english":"long-term wear","chinese":"長期穿着；耐穿性"},{"english":"use social media to discover style","chinese":"用社交媒體發現風格"},{"english":"use magazines to judge it","chinese":"用雜誌判斷它"},{"english":"slightly different","chinese":"略有不同"},{"english":"good criticism","chinese":"好的評論"},{"english":"teach me how to listen","chinese":"教我如何聆聽"},{"english":"point out","chinese":"指出"},{"english":"production","chinese":"音樂製作"},{"english":"lyrics","chinese":"歌詞"},{"english":"cultural references","chinese":"文化典故；文化指涉"},{"english":"miss on first hearing","chinese":"第一次聽時錯過"},{"english":"nevertheless","chinese":"然而"},{"english":"I would be lying if I said","chinese":"如果我說……就是在說謊"},{"english":"written reviews","chinese":"文字評論"},{"english":"most of the time","chinese":"大多數時候"},{"english":"music reaches me through","chinese":"音樂透過……傳到我耳邊"},{"english":"short videos, playlists and live clips","chinese":"短片、播放清單和現場片段"},{"english":"streaming platform","chinese":"串流平台"},{"english":"suddenly make sense","chinese":"突然變得合理；突然打動人"},{"english":"perform it live","chinese":"現場演唱它"},{"english":"turn to","chinese":"轉向；求助於"},{"english":"the setting is small","chinese":"場地細小"},{"english":"exactly its charm","chinese":"正正是它的魅力所在"},{"english":"without fireworks","chinese":"沒有煙花效果"},{"english":"heavy editing","chinese":"大量剪接"},{"english":"have nowhere to hide","chinese":"無處可躲；不能掩飾實力"},{"english":"favourite routine","chinese":"最喜歡的習慣"},{"english":"use something for context","chinese":"用……了解背景"},{"english":"use something for proof","chinese":"用……作為證明"},{"english":"a case in point","chinese":"一個例子是"},{"english":"discover an artist through a review","chinese":"透過評論發掘歌手"},{"english":"live session","chinese":"現場錄音演出"},{"english":"stand up without studio polish","chinese":"沒有錄音室修飾也站得住腳"},{"english":"studio polish","chinese":"錄音室修飾"},{"english":"save me from","chinese":"令我避免"},{"english":"follow hype blindly","chinese":"盲目追捧熱潮"},{"english":"viral chorus","chinese":"爆紅副歌"},{"english":"belong on my playlist","chinese":"值得放進我的播放清單"},{"english":"underrated singer","chinese":"被低估的歌手"},{"english":"the online crowd","chinese":"網上群眾"},{"english":"simply loud","chinese":"只是聲音很大；只是很吵"},{"english":"what matters is not whether..., but whether...","chinese":"重要的不是……而是……"},{"english":"traditional or trendy","chinese":"傳統或潮流"},{"english":"think more clearly","chinese":"更清晰地思考"},{"english":"choose between","chinese":"在……之間二選一"},{"english":"as if","chinese":"彷彿；好像"},{"english":"one must destroy the other","chinese":"一方必須取代另一方"},{"english":"there is something to be said for both","chinese":"兩者都有可取之處"},{"english":"immediacy","chinese":"即時性"},{"english":"colour and surprise","chinese":"色彩和驚喜"},{"english":"background, judgement and vocabulary","chinese":"背景、判斷力和詞彙"},{"english":"build your own information diet","chinese":"建立自己的資訊飲食"},{"english":"pop-culture information diet","chinese":"流行文化資訊飲食"},{"english":"first impressions","chinese":"第一印象"},{"english":"music criticism","chinese":"音樂評論"},{"english":"live performance","chinese":"現場表演"},{"english":"trends will keep changing","chinese":"潮流會不斷改變"},{"english":"sooner or later","chinese":"遲早"},{"english":"must-have item","chinese":"必買單品；必備物品"},{"english":"tomorrow's joke","chinese":"明天的笑話"},{"english":"with the right sources","chinese":"有了合適的資訊來源"},{"english":"enjoy the scroll","chinese":"享受滑手機瀏覽的樂趣"},{"english":"be controlled by","chinese":"被……控制"},{"english":"after all","chinese":"畢竟"},{"english":"keeping up","chinese":"跟上潮流"},{"english":"worth carrying with us","chinese":"值得帶着前行；值得保留下來"}]},"dse-writing-2019-part-b-q6":{"exerciseId":"dse-writing-2019-part-b-q6","essayKey":"","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=dse-writing-2019-part-b-q6","flashDeckId":"dse/writing/part-b/2019/Q6","paragraphs":[{"label":"Paragraph 1","english":"Cinderella Takes Flight: A Slipper-Fast Superhero Fairytale","chinese":"《Cinderella》展翅高飛：玻璃鞋疾速版超級英雄童話"},{"label":"Paragraph 2","english":"At first glance, Cinderella sounds like the safest film in the world: a pretty girl, a cruel stepmother, a grand ball and a lost shoe. On closer inspection, this new adaptation of the 1950s comic series Princesses of Power is anything but safe. It takes the fairy tale most audiences think they know and straps a cape onto it. The result is a colourful, confident and surprisingly moving adventure in which Cinderella does not simply dream of being chosen by a prince. She chooses to save the world.","chinese":"乍看之下，《Cinderella》聽起來像世上最穩陣的電影：一位漂亮女孩、一個殘酷繼母、一場盛大舞會，以及一隻遺失了的鞋。 仔細一看，這部改編自 1950 年代漫畫系列《Princesses of Power》的新作，絕非穩陣保守。 它把大多數觀眾以為早已熟悉的童話故事，直接披上一件英雄披風。 結果是一場色彩繽紛、自信十足、並且出乎意料地動人的冒險；在這段冒險中，Cinderella 不再只夢想被王子選中。 她選擇拯救世界。"},{"label":"Paragraph 3","english":"The film begins with a lovely comic-book opening. A hand turns the pages of an old twelve-cent issue, and we are taken into the smoky kingdom of Belloria, where the sky has been frozen at eleven minutes to midnight. Ella, nicknamed Cinderella because she works among the ashes of the palace furnace, is no ordinary servant. Before her father disappeared, she was one of the Princesses of Power, a secret order of young heroines who protected the realm. However, her stepmother, Lady Malvora, has stolen her public identity, her beauty and most of her powers, leaving Ella invisible in her own home. Only when the clock strikes midnight can her true form be restored. The catch is that, at midnight, Malvora also plans to open the dark gate above the castle. If Cinderella cannot recover the glass slipper—here reimagined as a crystal power-core—the kingdom will fall.","chinese":"電影以一個可愛的漫畫書式開場展開。 一隻手翻開一本古老的十二美分漫畫，我們隨即被帶進煙霧瀰漫的 Belloria 王國；在那裡，天空停留在距離午夜十一分鐘的時刻。 在父親失蹤之前，她曾是 Princesses of Power 的一員；那是一個由年輕女英雄組成、負責守護王國的秘密組織。 然而，她的繼母 Lady Malvora 偷走了她的公開身份、美貌，以及大部分力量，令 Ella 在自己家中也彷彿無人看見。 唯有當時鐘敲響午夜，她真正的形態才會恢復。 吊詭的是，在午夜時分，Malvora 也計劃打開城堡上方的黑暗之門。 如果 Cinderella 不能奪回玻璃鞋——在這部電影中被重新想像成水晶能量核心——整個王國便會淪陷。"},{"label":"Paragraph 4","english":"This plot could easily have become ridiculous. Instead, director Chris Wong keeps it swift and sincere. The flying scenes are especially impressive: one moment Cinderella is sweeping cinders from the floor; the next, she is soaring over black towers with her cape cutting through the clouds. The image of the slipper tumbling from the sky is used cleverly, not as a symbol of romantic helplessness, but as a sign that power can be lost, found and shared. What makes the story work is not the magic by itself, but the emotional pressure behind it. Ella is not trying to become beautiful enough to be loved; she is trying to become brave enough to be seen.","chinese":"這樣的情節本來很容易變得荒謬可笑。 相反，導演 Chris Wong 讓故事保持明快節奏與真誠情感。 飛行場面尤其令人印象深刻：前一刻 Cinderella 還在地上掃著灰燼；下一刻，她已經飛越黑色高塔，披風劃破雲層。 玻璃鞋從天空墜落的畫面運用得十分巧妙；它並非象徵浪漫式無助，更準確地說，它顯示力量可以失去、找回，並與他人分享。 真正令故事成立的核心，不在於魔法本身；重點在於其背後的情感壓力。"},{"label":"Paragraph 5","english":"The characters are portrayed with far more care than in the traditional version. Cinderella is kind, but she is no longer obedient to the point of silence. She questions, plans, fights and occasionally fails. In one of the film’s best scenes, she admits that she misses her old face because being unrecognised by the people she saved has left her lonely. Prince Theo, thankfully, is not a shining trophy waiting at the end of the story. He is a young reporter who investigates the royal cover-up and learns to support Cinderella without taking over her mission. The stepsisters are comic without being cruelly mocked: spoiled, yes, but also trapped by their mother’s hunger for status. As for Lady Malvora, she is a superb villain because she understands exactly how public image can become a weapon.","chinese":"這部電影對人物的刻畫，比傳統版本細緻得多。 她會質疑、計劃、戰鬥，也偶爾會失敗。 在電影其中一個最精彩的場面中，她承認自己想念從前那張臉，原因在於被自己曾經拯救的人認不出來，令她感到孤單。 值得慶幸的是，Prince Theo 並非故事結尾等待被獲得的閃亮獎盃。 他是一位年輕記者，負責調查皇室掩蓋真相的事件，並學會支持 Cinderella，同時不接管她的使命。 繼姊妹帶有喜劇效果，卻沒有被殘忍嘲弄：她們確實被寵壞了，同時也困在母親對地位的渴求之中。 至於 Lady Malvora，她是一位出色的反派，因為她非常清楚公眾形象如何可以化為武器。"},{"label":"Paragraph 6","english":"The director clearly wanted to make this film for a generation that has grown up questioning old fairy tales. Gone are the days when a heroine could simply wait by the fireplace and be rewarded for suffering quietly. This version asks a sharper question: what if Cinderella’s real enemy is not poverty, but the belief that a girl’s worth depends on how others look at her? By blending a retro comic-book style with a modern message, the film reminds young viewers that courage and appearance are not the same thing.","chinese":"導演顯然想為一個已經長大、並開始質疑舊式童話的世代製作這部電影。 那種女主角只要在壁爐旁等待、再因默默受苦而得到獎賞的年代，已經過去了 這個版本提出了一個更尖銳的問題：假如 Cinderella 真正的敵人並非貧窮，問題核心卻是那種認為女孩價值取決於他人目光的信念，那又如何？ 透過把復古漫畫風格與現代訊息結合起來，這部電影提醒年輕觀眾，勇氣與外貌不能混為一談。"},{"label":"Paragraph 7","english":"Admittedly, the film is not perfect. The final battle is a little crowded, and two of the other Princesses of Power deserve more screen time. Even so, the film’s energy, humour and heart more than make up for these flaws. Cinderella is fast, bright and emotionally generous. By the time the last clock tower lights up, the film has turned a familiar fairy tale into something fresh: not a story about losing a slipper, but a story about finding a self. For families, comic fans and anyone tired of helpless princesses, this Cinderella is well worth watching.","chinese":"誠然，這部電影並不完美。 最後一場戰鬥略嫌擁擠，另外兩位 Princesses of Power 也值得擁有更多出場時間 即使如此，電影的活力、幽默與真心，已經足以充分彌補這些缺點。 當最後一座鐘樓亮起時，這部電影已經把一個熟悉的童話變成了新鮮的故事：它講述的已不止於遺失玻璃鞋，更聚焦於找回自我。 對家庭觀眾、漫畫迷，以及任何已經厭倦無助公主的人來說，這部《Cinderella 》絕對值得一看。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"takes flight","chinese":"起飛；展翅高飛"},{"english":"slipper-fast","chinese":"像玻璃鞋般飛快的；飛快的"},{"english":"superhero fairytale","chinese":"超級英雄童話"},{"english":"at first glance","chinese":"乍看之下"},{"english":"sounds like","chinese":"聽起來像"},{"english":"the safest film in the world","chinese":"最穩陣保守的電影"},{"english":"a cruel stepmother","chinese":"惡毒繼母"},{"english":"a grand ball","chinese":"盛大舞會"},{"english":"on closer inspection","chinese":"仔細看時"},{"english":"new adaptation","chinese":"新改編作品"},{"english":"comic series","chinese":"漫畫系列"},{"english":"anything but safe","chinese":"絕不保守；絕不穩陣"},{"english":"most audiences think they know","chinese":"大多數觀眾以為自己熟悉的"},{"english":"straps a cape onto","chinese":"為……披上斗篷"},{"english":"the result is","chinese":"結果是"},{"english":"surprisingly moving","chinese":"出乎意料地動人"},{"english":"does not simply dream of","chinese":"不只是夢想"},{"english":"being chosen by","chinese":"被……選中"},{"english":"chooses to save the world","chinese":"選擇拯救世界"},{"english":"begins with","chinese":"以……開始"},{"english":"comic-book opening","chinese":"漫畫式開場"},{"english":"turns the pages of","chinese":"翻動……的頁面"},{"english":"a twelve-cent issue","chinese":"一本售價十二美仙的期刊"},{"english":"taken into","chinese":"被帶進"},{"english":"smoky kingdom","chinese":"煙霧瀰漫的王國"},{"english":"has been frozen at","chinese":"被凍結在"},{"english":"eleven minutes to midnight","chinese":"午夜前十一分鐘"},{"english":"nicknamed","chinese":"被暱稱為"},{"english":"works among the ashes","chinese":"在灰燼中工作"},{"english":"palace furnace","chinese":"宮殿火爐"},{"english":"no ordinary servant","chinese":"並非普通僕人"},{"english":"before her father disappeared","chinese":"在她父親失蹤之前"},{"english":"one of the Princesses of Power","chinese":"Power 公主團的一員"},{"english":"secret order","chinese":"秘密組織"},{"english":"young heroines","chinese":"年輕女英雄"},{"english":"protected the realm","chinese":"保護王國"},{"english":"public identity","chinese":"公眾身份"},{"english":"most of her powers","chinese":"她大部分的力量"},{"english":"leaving someone invisible","chinese":"令某人像隱形一樣"},{"english":"in her own home","chinese":"在她自己的家裏"},{"english":"only when","chinese":"只有當……才"},{"english":"the clock strikes midnight","chinese":"時鐘敲響午夜"},{"english":"true form","chinese":"真正形態"},{"english":"be restored","chinese":"被恢復"},{"english":"the catch is that","chinese":"問題是；難處在於"},{"english":"plans to","chinese":"計劃去"},{"english":"dark gate","chinese":"黑暗之門"},{"english":"above the castle","chinese":"在城堡上方"},{"english":"recover the glass slipper","chinese":"取回玻璃鞋"},{"english":"reimagined as","chinese":"被重新想像成"},{"english":"crystal power-core","chinese":"水晶能量核心"},{"english":"the kingdom will fall","chinese":"王國將會淪陷"},{"english":"could easily have become","chinese":"本來很容易變成"},{"english":"ridiculous","chinese":"荒謬的"},{"english":"keeps it swift and sincere","chinese":"令……節奏明快而真誠"},{"english":"swift and sincere","chinese":"節奏明快而真誠"},{"english":"flying scenes","chinese":"飛行場面"},{"english":"especially impressive","chinese":"特別令人印象深刻"},{"english":"one moment…, the next…","chinese":"前一刻……下一刻……"},{"english":"sweeping cinders","chinese":"清掃煤灰"},{"english":"soaring over","chinese":"在……上空翱翔"},{"english":"black towers","chinese":"黑色高塔"},{"english":"cape cutting through the clouds","chinese":"斗篷劃破雲層"},{"english":"tumbling from the sky","chinese":"從天空翻滾墜下"},{"english":"used cleverly","chinese":"被巧妙運用"},{"english":"not as…, but as…","chinese":"不是作為……而是作為……"},{"english":"a symbol of","chinese":"……的象徵"},{"english":"romantic helplessness","chinese":"浪漫化的無助感"},{"english":"a sign that","chinese":"表示……的象徵"},{"english":"lost, found and shared","chinese":"失去、尋回和分享"},{"english":"what makes the story work","chinese":"令故事成功的原因"},{"english":"by itself","chinese":"本身；單靠"},{"english":"emotional pressure","chinese":"情感張力"},{"english":"behind it","chinese":"在其背後"},{"english":"trying to become","chinese":"努力成為"},{"english":"beautiful enough to be loved","chinese":"美麗得足以被愛"},{"english":"brave enough to be seen","chinese":"勇敢得足以被看見"},{"english":"portrayed with far more care","chinese":"被刻畫得細心得多"},{"english":"the traditional version","chinese":"傳統版本"},{"english":"no longer","chinese":"不再"},{"english":"obedient to the point of silence","chinese":"順從到沉默的程度"},{"english":"occasionally fails","chinese":"偶爾失敗"},{"english":"in one of the film's best scenes","chinese":"在電影其中一場最佳戲份中"},{"english":"admits that","chinese":"承認"},{"english":"misses her old face","chinese":"想念自己從前的樣子"},{"english":"being unrecognised by","chinese":"不被……認出"},{"english":"the people she saved","chinese":"她曾拯救的人"},{"english":"has left her lonely","chinese":"令她感到孤獨"},{"english":"thankfully","chinese":"幸好"},{"english":"a shining trophy","chinese":"閃亮的獎品"},{"english":"waiting at the end of the story","chinese":"在故事結尾等待着"},{"english":"young reporter","chinese":"年輕記者"},{"english":"investigates","chinese":"調查"},{"english":"royal cover-up","chinese":"王室掩飾事件"},{"english":"learns to support","chinese":"學會支持"},{"english":"without taking over","chinese":"沒有接管"},{"english":"mission","chinese":"使命"},{"english":"comic without being cruelly mocked","chinese":"有喜劇感但沒有被殘酷嘲笑"},{"english":"spoiled","chinese":"被寵壞的"},{"english":"trapped by","chinese":"被……困住"},{"english":"hunger for status","chinese":"對地位的渴求"},{"english":"as for","chinese":"至於"},{"english":"superb villain","chinese":"出色的反派"},{"english":"public image","chinese":"公眾形象"},{"english":"become a weapon","chinese":"變成武器"},{"english":"clearly wanted to","chinese":"明顯想要"},{"english":"a generation that has grown up","chinese":"成長於……的一代"},{"english":"questioning old fairy tales","chinese":"質疑舊童話"},{"english":"Gone are the days when","chinese":"……的日子已經過去"},{"english":"heroine","chinese":"女主角；女英雄"},{"english":"wait by the fireplace","chinese":"在壁爐旁等待"},{"english":"be rewarded for","chinese":"因……而得到獎賞"},{"english":"suffering quietly","chinese":"默默受苦"},{"english":"asks a sharper question","chinese":"提出更尖銳的問題"},{"english":"real enemy","chinese":"真正敵人"},{"english":"the belief that","chinese":"……這種信念"},{"english":"depends on","chinese":"取決於"},{"english":"how others look at her","chinese":"別人如何看待她"},{"english":"by blending","chinese":"透過融合"},{"english":"retro comic-book style","chinese":"復古漫畫風格"},{"english":"modern message","chinese":"現代訊息"},{"english":"reminds young viewers that","chinese":"提醒年輕觀眾"},{"english":"courage and appearance","chinese":"勇氣與外貌"},{"english":"not the same thing","chinese":"不是同一回事"},{"english":"admittedly","chinese":"誠然"},{"english":"final battle","chinese":"最終決戰"},{"english":"a little crowded","chinese":"稍為擁擠；元素太多"},{"english":"deserve more screen time","chinese":"值得有更多出場時間"},{"english":"screen time","chinese":"出場時間"},{"english":"even so","chinese":"即使如此"},{"english":"energy, humour and heart","chinese":"活力、幽默和真情"},{"english":"more than make up for","chinese":"足以彌補；遠遠彌補"},{"english":"flaws","chinese":"缺點"},{"english":"emotionally generous","chinese":"情感豐沛的"},{"english":"by the time","chinese":"到……的時候"},{"english":"lights up","chinese":"亮起"},{"english":"familiar fairy tale","chinese":"熟悉的童話"},{"english":"into something fresh","chinese":"變成新鮮的東西"},{"english":"not a story about…, but a story about…","chinese":"不是關於……而是關於……"},{"english":"finding a self","chinese":"找回自我"},{"english":"comic fans","chinese":"漫畫迷"},{"english":"anyone tired of","chinese":"任何厭倦……的人"},{"english":"helpless princesses","chinese":"無助的公主"},{"english":"well worth watching","chinese":"非常值得觀看"}]},"dse-writing-2019-part-b-q7":{"exerciseId":"dse-writing-2019-part-b-q7","essayKey":"","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=dse-writing-2019-part-b-q7","flashDeckId":"dse/writing/part-b/2019/Q7","paragraphs":[{"label":"Paragraph 1","english":"From Blame to Better Art: Learning to Criticise with Courage and Kindness","chinese":"從指責到更好的藝術：以勇氣與善意學習批評"},{"label":"Paragraph 2","english":"Good afternoon, everyone,","chinese":"各位午安。"},{"label":"Paragraph 3","english":"Taylor Swift once said that criticism is unavoidable, but there is a line people cross when they stop reviewing the work and start attacking the person. As members of our after-school arts club, we create, perform, paint, write, design and sometimes expose the most private parts of ourselves to other people’s eyes. That is exciting; it is also frightening. This is why we need to learn how to review one another’s work properly, not so that we can sound clever, but so that we can help each other grow. Today, I would like to discuss three things: what a critic does, how to give criticism, and how to respond to criticism with maturity.","chinese":"作為課後藝術學會的成員，我們會創作、表演、繪畫、寫作、設計，有時甚至把自己最私密的一面展現在別人眼前。 這令人興奮；同時也令人害怕。 這就是為甚麼我們需要學會如何恰當地評論彼此的作品；目的不是為了顯得聰明，而是為了幫助彼此成長。 今天，我想討論三件事：評論者的角色、如何提出批評，以及如何成熟地回應批評。"},{"label":"Paragraph 4","english":"First, what does a critic actually do? A critic is not a professional fault-finder. A critic is a careful observer, a fair interpreter and, at best, a helpful guide between the artist and the audience. When we review a poem, a painting, a short film or a dance performance, we should ask: What is the creator trying to achieve? How is the work constructed? What effect does it have on the audience? Does the choice of colour, rhythm, image, dialogue or movement support the artist’s intention? Take a poster, for example. If its purpose is to promote a charity concert, a critic should not merely say, “I like it” or “I hate it.” Instead, the critic may notice that the red background creates energy, that the singer’s photo attracts attention, but that the date is too small to read from a distance. That is useful criticism because it examines purpose, technique and effect. Put simply, a critic does not just judge a work; a critic helps the creator see the work more clearly.","chinese":"首先，評論者到底做些甚麼？ 評論者並不是專業挑錯的人。 評論者是一位細心的觀察者、公平的詮釋者；在最理想的情況下，更是藝術家與觀眾之間有幫助的引路人。 當我們評論一首詩、一幅畫、一部短片或一場舞蹈表演時，我們應該問：創作者想達到甚麼目的？ 作品是如何構成的？ 它對觀眾產生了甚麼效果？ 顏色、節奏、意象、對白或動作的選擇，是否支持了藝術家的創作意圖？ 以一張海報為例。 如果它的目的是宣傳一場慈善音樂會，評論者不應只是說： 「我喜歡」或「我討厭」。 相反，評論者可以指出紅色背景營造了活力，歌手的照片吸引了注意，但日期太小，遠看時難以閱讀。 這就是有用的批評，因為它檢視了目的、技巧和效果。 簡單來說，評論者不只是評判作品；評論者幫助創作者更清楚地看見自己的作品"},{"label":"Paragraph 5","english":"Second, how should we give criticism? The golden rule is simple - criticise the work, not the worth of the person. We may say, “The ending feels rushed,” but not, “You are careless.” We may say, “The melody becomes repetitive after the second verse,” but not, “You are boring.” There is a world of difference between the two. Good criticism should be specific, evidence-based and actionable. Start by identifying one genuine strength. Then point out one area for improvement. After that, explain why it matters and suggest a possible solution. For instance, instead of saying, “Your monologue is bad,” say, “Your opening line is powerful, but the middle section repeats the same emotion for too long. Perhaps you could add a moment of silence, a change in tone, or a memory to reveal the character more deeply.” That way, the artist knows what worked, what did not, why it matters and what to try next. Also, ask questions. “What mood were you hoping to create?” is often more respectful than “Why did you do this?” Only when people feel safe do they speak honestly; only when criticism is honest can art improve.","chinese":"第二，我們應該如何提出批評？ 黃金法則很簡單——批評作品，而不是否定一個人的價值。 我們可以說：「結尾感覺有點倉促」，但不應說：「你很粗心。」 我們可以說：「第二段之後，旋律變得重複」，但不應說：「你很沉悶。」 兩者之間有天壤之別。 好的批評應該具體、有根據，而且能讓人採取行動。 首先指出一個真正的優點。 然後指出一個可以改善的地方。 之後解釋為甚麼這一點重要，並提出一個可行的解決方法。 例如，與其說「你的獨白很差」，不如說：「你的開場句很有力量，但中段把同一種情緒重複得太久。」 也許你可以加入一刻沉默、一個語氣轉變，或一段回憶，從而更深入地展現角色。 這樣一來，創作者便會知道甚麼有效、甚麼無效、為何重要，以及下一步可以嘗試甚麼。 此外，要提出問題。 「你希望營造甚麼氣氛？」通常比「你為甚麼這樣做？」更尊重對方。 只有當人們感到安全時，他們才會坦誠發言；也只有當批評是誠實的時候，藝術才可以進步。"},{"label":"Paragraph 6","english":"Finally, how should we respond when we receive criticism? Let me be clear: listening to criticism does not mean obeying every comment. Your work is still yours. However, if your first reaction is to defend everything, you may miss something valuable. When someone comments on your work, pause. Take notes. Ask follow-up questions. You might say, “I hear you. Could you show me which part felt unclear?” or “I see your point, but I intended the ending to feel unresolved.” Then decide what to accept, what to adapt and what to leave aside. Some criticism will be fair; some will be mistaken; some may even be unkind. If a comment attacks your identity rather than your work, you have every right to draw the line. Still, do not let one harsh voice silence your creativity. Taylor Swift turned cruel reviews into a song. In the same spirit, we can turn useful criticism into better drafts, stronger performances and braver choices.","chinese":"最後，當我們接受批評時，應該如何回應？ 讓我說清楚：聆聽批評並不代表要服從每一個意見。 你的作品仍然屬於你。 然而，如果你的第一反應是為所有事情辯護，你可能會錯過一些寶貴的意見 當有人評論你的作品時，先停一停。 做筆記。 提出跟進問題。 你可以說：「我明白你的意思。你可以指出哪一部分讓你覺得不清楚嗎？」 或者說：「我明白你的觀點，但我原本是想讓結尾帶有未解決的感覺。」 然後決定甚麼意見要接受、甚麼要調整、甚麼要暫時放下。 有些批評會是公平的；有些會是錯誤的；有些甚至可能是不友善的。 如果一個評論攻擊的是你的身份，而不是你的作品，你完全有權劃清界線。 即使如此，也不要讓一句尖刻的說話壓制你的創意。 同樣地，我們也可以把有用的批評轉化成更好的草稿、更有力的表演和更勇敢的選擇。"},{"label":"Paragraph 7","english":"To conclude, our club should be a workshop, not a courtroom. We are here not to prove that we are perfect, but to help one another become more thoughtful artists. From today onwards, when we review each other’s work, let us remember three promises: be observant, be specific and be humane. If we can do that, criticism will no longer feel like an attack. It will become one of the best tools we have for turning effort into excellence. Thank you.","chinese":"總括而言，我們的學會應該是一個工作坊，而不是一個法庭。 我們在這裡不是為了證明自己完美，而是為了幫助彼此成為更有思考力的藝術家。 從今天開始，當我們評論彼此的作品時，請記住三個承諾：要善於觀察、要具體、要有人性。 如果我們能做到這一點，批評便不再會像攻擊。 它會成為我們把努力轉化為卓越的最佳工具之一。 謝謝各位。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"from blame to better art","chinese":"由責備走向更好的藝術"},{"english":"learn to criticise","chinese":"學會批評"},{"english":"with courage and kindness","chinese":"以勇氣與善意"},{"english":"good afternoon, everyone","chinese":"各位午安"},{"english":"once said that","chinese":"曾經說過"},{"english":"criticism is unavoidable","chinese":"批評是無可避免的"},{"english":"cross a line","chinese":"越界"},{"english":"reviewing the work","chinese":"評論作品"},{"english":"attacking the person","chinese":"攻擊個人"},{"english":"as members of","chinese":"作為……的成員"},{"english":"after-school arts club","chinese":"課後藝術學會"},{"english":"expose the most private parts of ourselves","chinese":"展露自己最私密的一面"},{"english":"to other people's eyes","chinese":"在別人的目光下"},{"english":"exciting and frightening","chinese":"令人興奮又害怕"},{"english":"this is why","chinese":"這就是為甚麼"},{"english":"review one another's work","chinese":"評論彼此的作品"},{"english":"not so that…, but so that…","chinese":"不是為了……而是為了……"},{"english":"sound clever","chinese":"聽起來聰明"},{"english":"help each other grow","chinese":"幫助彼此成長"},{"english":"I would like to discuss","chinese":"我想討論"},{"english":"give criticism","chinese":"提出批評"},{"english":"respond to criticism","chinese":"回應批評"},{"english":"with maturity","chinese":"成熟地"},{"english":"actually do","chinese":"實際上做甚麼"},{"english":"professional fault-finder","chinese":"專門挑錯的人"},{"english":"careful observer","chinese":"細心觀察者"},{"english":"fair interpreter","chinese":"公正的詮釋者"},{"english":"at best","chinese":"最理想情況下"},{"english":"a helpful guide","chinese":"有幫助的引導者"},{"english":"between the artist and the audience","chinese":"在藝術家與觀眾之間"},{"english":"review a poem","chinese":"評論一首詩"},{"english":"a dance performance","chinese":"舞蹈表演"},{"english":"trying to achieve","chinese":"試圖達成"},{"english":"how the work is constructed","chinese":"作品如何構成"},{"english":"have an effect on","chinese":"對……產生影響"},{"english":"choice of colour","chinese":"色彩選擇"},{"english":"support the artist's intention","chinese":"配合藝術家的意圖"},{"english":"artist's intention","chinese":"藝術家的意圖"},{"english":"take…for example","chinese":"以……為例"},{"english":"promote a charity concert","chinese":"宣傳慈善音樂會"},{"english":"not merely say","chinese":"不只是說"},{"english":"create energy","chinese":"營造活力"},{"english":"attract attention","chinese":"吸引注意"},{"english":"from a distance","chinese":"從遠處"},{"english":"useful criticism","chinese":"有用的批評"},{"english":"examine purpose, technique and effect","chinese":"審視目的、技巧和效果"},{"english":"put simply","chinese":"簡單來說"},{"english":"judge a work","chinese":"評價一件作品"},{"english":"help the creator see","chinese":"幫助創作者看清"},{"english":"the golden rule","chinese":"黃金法則"},{"english":"criticise the work, not the worth of the person","chinese":"批評作品，而不是否定人的價值"},{"english":"the worth of the person","chinese":"一個人的價值"},{"english":"feels rushed","chinese":"感覺倉促"},{"english":"the melody becomes repetitive","chinese":"旋律變得重複"},{"english":"after the second verse","chinese":"第二段之後"},{"english":"a world of difference between","chinese":"……之間有天壤之別"},{"english":"specific, evidence-based and actionable","chinese":"具體、有證據支持而且可實行"},{"english":"evidence-based","chinese":"有證據支持的"},{"english":"actionable","chinese":"可實行的"},{"english":"start by identifying","chinese":"先指出"},{"english":"one genuine strength","chinese":"一個真正的優點"},{"english":"point out","chinese":"指出"},{"english":"one area for improvement","chinese":"一個有待改善的地方"},{"english":"explain why it matters","chinese":"解釋為何重要"},{"english":"suggest a possible solution","chinese":"提出一個可行解決方法"},{"english":"instead of saying","chinese":"與其說"},{"english":"monologue","chinese":"獨白"},{"english":"opening line","chinese":"開場白"},{"english":"powerful","chinese":"有力量的"},{"english":"middle section","chinese":"中段"},{"english":"repeat the same emotion","chinese":"重複同一種情緒"},{"english":"for too long","chinese":"太久"},{"english":"add a moment of silence","chinese":"加入一刻沉默"},{"english":"a change in tone","chinese":"語氣轉變"},{"english":"reveal the character more deeply","chinese":"更深入展現角色"},{"english":"that way","chinese":"這樣一來"},{"english":"what worked","chinese":"哪些地方有效"},{"english":"what did not","chinese":"哪些地方無效"},{"english":"what to try next","chinese":"下一步可以嘗試甚麼"},{"english":"ask questions","chinese":"提問"},{"english":"what mood were you hoping to create","chinese":"你希望營造甚麼氣氛"},{"english":"more respectful than","chinese":"比……更尊重人"},{"english":"only when…do…","chinese":"只有當……才會……"},{"english":"feel safe","chinese":"感到安全"},{"english":"speak honestly","chinese":"坦誠發言"},{"english":"can art improve","chinese":"藝術才能進步"},{"english":"let me be clear","chinese":"讓我說清楚"},{"english":"listening to criticism","chinese":"聆聽批評"},{"english":"obey every comment","chinese":"接受每一個意見"},{"english":"your work is still yours","chinese":"你的作品仍然屬於你"},{"english":"first reaction","chinese":"第一反應"},{"english":"defend everything","chinese":"為一切辯護"},{"english":"miss something valuable","chinese":"錯過有價值的東西"},{"english":"take notes","chinese":"做筆記"},{"english":"ask follow-up questions","chinese":"追問跟進問題"},{"english":"I hear you","chinese":"我明白你的意思"},{"english":"show me which part","chinese":"指給我看是哪一部分"},{"english":"felt unclear","chinese":"感覺不清楚"},{"english":"I see your point","chinese":"我明白你的觀點"},{"english":"intended the ending to feel unresolved","chinese":"原意是讓結局感覺未解決"},{"english":"feel unresolved","chinese":"感覺懸而未決"},{"english":"decide what to accept","chinese":"決定接受甚麼"},{"english":"adapt","chinese":"調整"},{"english":"leave aside","chinese":"暫且放下；不採納"},{"english":"some criticism will be fair","chinese":"有些批評會是公道的"},{"english":"some will be mistaken","chinese":"有些會是錯誤的"},{"english":"unkind","chinese":"不友善的"},{"english":"attack your identity","chinese":"攻擊你的身份"},{"english":"rather than your work","chinese":"而不是你的作品"},{"english":"have every right to","chinese":"完全有權"},{"english":"draw the line","chinese":"劃清界線"},{"english":"harsh voice","chinese":"刺耳的聲音"},{"english":"silence your creativity","chinese":"令你的創意沉默"},{"english":"turn cruel reviews into","chinese":"把殘酷評論轉化成……"},{"english":"in the same spirit","chinese":"本着同樣精神"},{"english":"turn useful criticism into","chinese":"把有用批評轉化成……"},{"english":"better drafts","chinese":"更好的草稿"},{"english":"stronger performances","chinese":"更有力的表演"},{"english":"braver choices","chinese":"更勇敢的選擇"},{"english":"to conclude","chinese":"總結來說"},{"english":"a workshop, not a courtroom","chinese":"工作坊，而不是法庭"},{"english":"prove that we are perfect","chinese":"證明自己完美"},{"english":"become more thoughtful artists","chinese":"成為更有思想的藝術創作者"},{"english":"from today onwards","chinese":"由今天起"},{"english":"let us remember","chinese":"讓我們記住"},{"english":"be observant","chinese":"善於觀察"},{"english":"be specific","chinese":"具體"},{"english":"be humane","chinese":"有人情味；仁厚"},{"english":"no longer feel like","chinese":"不再感覺像"},{"english":"feel like an attack","chinese":"感覺像攻擊"},{"english":"one of the best tools","chinese":"最好的工具之一"},{"english":"turn effort into excellence","chinese":"把努力轉化為卓越"},{"english":"thank you","chinese":"多謝"}]},"dse-writing-2019-part-b-q8":{"exerciseId":"dse-writing-2019-part-b-q8","essayKey":"","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=dse-writing-2019-part-b-q8","flashDeckId":"dse/writing/part-b/2019/Q8","paragraphs":[{"label":"Paragraph 1","english":"Dear Members of the Council Election Committee,","chinese":"尊敬的區議會選舉委員會成員："},{"label":"Paragraph 2","english":"In the run-up to the council election, Ricky Kwan’s posters should be more than attractive decoration; they should tell residents what kind of representative he hopes to become. With this in mind, I have designed Posters A and B around three connected ideas: listening, connection and creative action. My recommendation is that they should form a campaign theme called “From Concern to Solution”, with Poster C completing the sequence by showing how residents’ voices can become practical improvement.","chinese":"在區議會選舉臨近之際，Ricky Kwan 的海報不應只是吸引眼球的裝飾；更重要的是，它們應該向居民傳達他希望成為一位怎樣的民意代表。 有見及此，我在設計海報 A 和海報 B 時，圍繞三個互相關連的理念：聆聽、連繫，以及具創意的行動。 我的建議是，這組海報應該形成一個名為「從關注到方案」的競選主題，而海報 C 則可以完成整個系列，展示居民的聲音如何轉化為實際改善。"},{"label":"Paragraph 3","english":"Poster A is built around the image of two people shaking hands across a gap, with a bridge placed above them. At first glance, it is warm and simple; on closer inspection, it carries a clear message. The question “Have ideas, problems or concerns?” directly invites residents to speak, whether they wish to suggest a community activity, complain about a damaged pavement, or raise concerns about hygiene, transport or elderly care. The gap between the two figures symbolises the distance that can exist between residents and public bodies, between younger and older generations, or between complaints and solutions. By placing the handshake at the centre, the design suggests that Ricky does not see district work as giving orders from above. Rather, he sees it as building trust face to face. The line “Let’s cross the bridge together” is effective because it avoids an arrogant promise of instant success. Instead, it offers partnership. This would make a good campaign theme because it presents Ricky as approachable, patient and willing to walk with residents through difficult issues.","chinese":"海報 A 以兩個人隔着一道缺口握手的畫面為核心，而他們上方則放置了一道橋 乍看之下，這設計溫暖而簡潔；但細看之下，它其實傳遞了一個清晰的信息 「Have ideas, problems or concerns?」這個問題直接邀請居民發聲，不論他們是想建議一項社區活動、投訴損壞的行人路，還是提出對環境衞生、交通或長者照顧的關注。 兩個人物之間的缺口，象徵居民與公共機構之間、年輕一代與年長一代之間，或投訴與解決方案之間可能存在的距離。 透過把握手的畫面放在中央，這個設計暗示 Ricky 並不把地區工作視為由上而下發號施令。 更準確地說，他把地區工作視為一個面對面建立信任的過程。 「Let’s cross the bridge together」這句口號之所以有效，是因為它避免作出一種自大的、承諾即時成功的姿態。 相反，它帶出的是一種同行合作的關係。 這會成為一個良好的競選主題，因為它把 Ricky 塑造成一位親民、有耐性，並願意陪同居民一起面對棘手問題的候選人。"},{"label":"Paragraph 4","english":"Whereas Poster A stresses relationship, Poster B presents Ricky as a fresh thinker. The visual design shows a light bulb rising out of an open box, with bird-like shapes inside the bulb. The box suggests old assumptions, rigid routines and the familiar excuse that “this is how things have always been done”. The light bulb, by contrast, suggests invention, while the birds imply that ideas are being released rather than trapped. This matters because district problems rarely fit into neat categories. Traffic noise, recycling, youth facilities and support for elderly residents may overlap, so a single old answer is often not enough. The slogan “Think outside the box” is short enough for passers-by to remember, but meaningful enough to support Ricky’s image as someone who will search for better solutions. For example, he could explore pop-up consultation booths, a mobile reporting system for broken facilities or shared spaces for different generations. Poster B also balances Poster A: one may seem caring but not dynamic, while the other may seem clever but distant. Together, they show Ricky as both compassionate and capable.","chinese":"海報 A 強調人與人之間的關係，而海報 B 則把 Ricky 呈現為一位具備新思維的人。 這個視覺設計展示一個燈泡從打開的盒子中升起，而燈泡裡則有像鳥一樣的圖案。 盒子象徵舊有假設、僵化程序，以及那句常見的藉口：「事情一直都是這樣做的。」 相比之下，燈泡象徵創新；而那些鳥形圖案則暗示意念正在被釋放，而不是被困住。 這一點十分重要，因為地區問題很少能夠被整齊地歸入單一類別。 交通噪音、回收、青年設施和長者支援等問題可能彼此重疊，因此一個老套而單一的答案往往並不足夠。 「Think outside the box」這句口號短得足以讓途人記住，同時又有足夠意思去支撐 Ricky 作為一位願意尋找更佳方案的候選人形象。 例如，他可以考慮設立流動諮詢攤位、推出供居民匯報設施損壞的手機系統，或建立供不同世代共用的社區空間。 海報 B 亦能平衡海報 A：海報 A 可能顯得關懷備至，卻未必夠有動感；海報 B 則可能顯得聰明創新，卻未必夠親近。 兩者結合起來，便能展現 Ricky 既有同理心，又有辦事能力。"},{"label":"Paragraph 5","english":"For Poster C, I propose the slogan “Your voice lights the way. Vote Ricky Kwan!” The centre image would combine the strongest symbols from the first two posters. At the bottom, several residents—perhaps an elderly man, a parent with a child, a shopkeeper and a student—would be represented by simple speech bubbles. These bubbles would rise into a large light bulb, and the light from the bulb would form a bridge or path leading towards a cleaner, brighter street. Along one side, three concise words could appear: “Listen. Think. Act.” This design would show a process: residents speak, Ricky studies their concerns creatively, and council work follows. To avoid overcrowding, I would use two or three soft colours and leave enough white space around the main image. That way, the poster would feel positive rather than noisy, and practical rather than vague. It would also complete a logical sequence: Poster A invites residents to cross the bridge; Poster B promises creative thinking; Poster C shows how residents’ voices can light the route towards action.","chinese":"至於海報 C，我建議採用口號：「Your voice lights the way. Vote Ricky Kwan!」 中央圖像可以結合前兩張海報中最有力的象徵。 在海報底部，幾位居民——例如一位長者、一位帶着孩子的家長、一位店主和一名學生——可以用簡潔的對話泡泡來呈現。 這些對話泡泡會向上升起，匯聚成一個大型燈泡；而燈泡發出的光，則會形成一道橋或一條路，通往一條更清潔、更明亮的街道。 海報一側可以放上三個簡潔有力的字詞：「Listen. Think. Act.」 這個設計會展示一個清晰的過程：居民發聲，Ricky 以具創意的方式研究他們的關注，然後區議會工作隨之展開。 這樣一來，海報便會予人正面而不嘈雜、實在而不空泛的感覺。 它亦會完成一個合乎邏輯的系列：海報 A 邀請居民一同跨過橋樑；海報 B 承諾以創意思維解決問題；海報 C 則展示居民的聲音如何照亮通往行動的道路"},{"label":"Paragraph 6","english":"All things considered, the three posters could work as a coherent campaign series. Poster A builds trust, Poster B builds confidence in Ricky’s ideas, and Poster C builds belief in action. I would appreciate it if the committee could review these proposals and advise whether the final campaign theme should be presented as “From Concern to Solution” or “Listen. Think. Act.” Once your preference is confirmed, I will refine Poster C accordingly.","chinese":"總括而言，這三張海報可以組成一個連貫的競選系列。 海報 A 建立信任，海報 B 建立居民對 Ricky 構思的信心，而海報 C 則建立大家對實際行動的相信。 如委員會能審閱以上建議，並告知最終競選主題應採用「From Concern to Solution」還是「Listen. Think. Act.」，本人將不勝感激。 一旦確認委員會的取向，我便會相應地修改和完善海報 C。"},{"label":"Paragraph 7","english":"Yours faithfully,","chinese":"謹啟"},{"label":"Paragraph 8","english":"Chris Wong","chinese":"Chris Wong"},{"label":"Paragraph 9","english":"Volunteer, District Council Office","chinese":"區議會辦事處義工"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"making room at","chinese":"為……騰出位置"},{"english":"a proposal to include","chinese":"建議納入……"},{"english":"Dear Members of","chinese":"各位……成員"},{"english":"the Council Election Committee","chinese":"選舉委員會"},{"english":"in the run-up to","chinese":"在……前夕"},{"english":"council election","chinese":"區議會選舉"},{"english":"should be more than","chinese":"應該不只是……"},{"english":"attractive decoration","chinese":"好看的裝飾"},{"english":"tell residents","chinese":"告訴居民"},{"english":"what kind of representative","chinese":"甚麼樣的代表"},{"english":"hopes to become","chinese":"希望成為"},{"english":"with this in mind","chinese":"考慮到這一點"},{"english":"design something around","chinese":"圍繞……設計某物"},{"english":"three connected ideas","chinese":"三個互相關連的理念"},{"english":"listening, connection and creative action","chinese":"聆聽、連繫和創意行動"},{"english":"my recommendation is that","chinese":"我的建議是"},{"english":"form a campaign theme","chinese":"形成一個競選主題"},{"english":"From Concern to Solution","chinese":"由關注到解決方案"},{"english":"complete the sequence","chinese":"完成這個系列"},{"english":"residents' voices","chinese":"居民的聲音"},{"english":"practical improvement","chinese":"實際改善"},{"english":"be built around","chinese":"以……為核心設計"},{"english":"shaking hands","chinese":"握手"},{"english":"across a gap","chinese":"跨越一道距離"},{"english":"placed above","chinese":"放在……上方"},{"english":"at first glance","chinese":"乍看之下"},{"english":"on closer inspection","chinese":"仔細一看"},{"english":"carry a clear message","chinese":"傳達清晰訊息"},{"english":"directly invite someone to","chinese":"直接邀請某人去……"},{"english":"suggest a community activity","chinese":"建議社區活動"},{"english":"complain about","chinese":"投訴……"},{"english":"a damaged pavement","chinese":"損壞的行人路"},{"english":"raise concerns about","chinese":"提出對……的關注"},{"english":"hygiene","chinese":"衞生"},{"english":"elderly care","chinese":"長者照顧"},{"english":"symbolise the distance","chinese":"象徵距離"},{"english":"public bodies","chinese":"公共機構"},{"english":"younger and older generations","chinese":"年輕一代和年長一代"},{"english":"complaints and solutions","chinese":"投訴與解決方案"},{"english":"by placing","chinese":"透過放置……"},{"english":"at the centre","chinese":"在中心位置"},{"english":"district work","chinese":"地區工作"},{"english":"giving orders from above","chinese":"從上而下發號施令"},{"english":"rather","chinese":"反而；更準確地說"},{"english":"build trust","chinese":"建立信任"},{"english":"face to face","chinese":"面對面"},{"english":"cross the bridge together","chinese":"一起跨過橋樑"},{"english":"be effective because","chinese":"有效，因為……"},{"english":"avoid an arrogant promise","chinese":"避免傲慢的承諾"},{"english":"instant success","chinese":"即時成功"},{"english":"offer partnership","chinese":"提供合作關係"},{"english":"a good campaign theme","chinese":"好的競選主題"},{"english":"present someone as","chinese":"把某人塑造成"},{"english":"approachable","chinese":"平易近人的"},{"english":"patient","chinese":"有耐性的"},{"english":"willing to","chinese":"願意"},{"english":"walk with residents","chinese":"與居民同行"},{"english":"difficult issues","chinese":"棘手問題"},{"english":"whereas","chinese":"而；相對於"},{"english":"stress relationship","chinese":"強調關係"},{"english":"present someone as a fresh thinker","chinese":"把某人塑造成思維新穎的人"},{"english":"visual design","chinese":"視覺設計"},{"english":"a light bulb rising out of","chinese":"從……升起的燈泡"},{"english":"an open box","chinese":"打開的盒子"},{"english":"bird-like shapes","chinese":"像雀鳥的形狀"},{"english":"old assumptions","chinese":"舊有假設"},{"english":"rigid routines","chinese":"僵化常規"},{"english":"familiar excuse","chinese":"熟悉的藉口"},{"english":"how things have always been done","chinese":"一直以來的做法"},{"english":"by contrast","chinese":"相比之下"},{"english":"suggest invention","chinese":"象徵創新"},{"english":"imply that","chinese":"暗示"},{"english":"be released rather than trapped","chinese":"被釋放而不是被困住"},{"english":"district problems","chinese":"地區問題"},{"english":"fit into neat categories","chinese":"能清楚歸入不同類別"},{"english":"traffic noise","chinese":"交通噪音"},{"english":"recycling","chinese":"回收"},{"english":"youth facilities","chinese":"青少年設施"},{"english":"support for elderly residents","chinese":"對長者居民的支援"},{"english":"overlap","chinese":"重疊；互相關連"},{"english":"a single old answer","chinese":"單一舊方法"},{"english":"think outside the box","chinese":"跳出框框思考"},{"english":"short enough for passers-by to remember","chinese":"簡短到讓路人記得"},{"english":"passers-by","chinese":"路人"},{"english":"meaningful enough to","chinese":"有足夠意義去……"},{"english":"search for better solutions","chinese":"尋找更好的解決方案"},{"english":"pop-up consultation booths","chinese":"快閃諮詢站"},{"english":"mobile reporting system","chinese":"流動通報系統"},{"english":"broken facilities","chinese":"損壞設施"},{"english":"shared spaces","chinese":"共用空間"},{"english":"different generations","chinese":"不同世代"},{"english":"balance Poster A","chinese":"與海報 A 取得平衡"},{"english":"caring but not dynamic","chinese":"關懷但不夠有活力"},{"english":"clever but distant","chinese":"聰明但有距離感"},{"english":"compassionate and capable","chinese":"有同理心且有能力"},{"english":"I propose the slogan","chinese":"我建議口號"},{"english":"light the way","chinese":"照亮方向"},{"english":"vote for","chinese":"投票支持"},{"english":"centre image","chinese":"中央圖像"},{"english":"combine the strongest symbols","chinese":"結合最有力的象徵"},{"english":"at the bottom","chinese":"在底部"},{"english":"be represented by","chinese":"由……代表"},{"english":"speech bubbles","chinese":"對話泡泡"},{"english":"rise into","chinese":"升進"},{"english":"form a bridge or path","chinese":"形成橋樑或道路"},{"english":"lead towards","chinese":"通往"},{"english":"a cleaner, brighter street","chinese":"更清潔、更明亮的街道"},{"english":"along one side","chinese":"沿著一邊"},{"english":"concise words","chinese":"簡潔的字詞"},{"english":"Listen. Think. Act.","chinese":"聆聽、思考、行動"},{"english":"show a process","chinese":"展示一個過程"},{"english":"study their concerns creatively","chinese":"有創意地研究他們的關注"},{"english":"council work follows","chinese":"議會工作隨之展開"},{"english":"avoid overcrowding","chinese":"避免過於擠迫"},{"english":"soft colours","chinese":"柔和色彩"},{"english":"leave enough white space","chinese":"留下足夠留白"},{"english":"around the main image","chinese":"在主圖像周圍"},{"english":"that way","chinese":"這樣一來"},{"english":"positive rather than noisy","chinese":"正面而不雜亂"},{"english":"practical rather than vague","chinese":"實際而不空泛"},{"english":"complete a logical sequence","chinese":"完成一個合乎邏輯的系列"},{"english":"invite residents to","chinese":"邀請居民去……"},{"english":"promise creative thinking","chinese":"承諾創意思考"},{"english":"light the route towards action","chinese":"照亮通往行動的路線"},{"english":"all things considered","chinese":"綜合考慮各方面"},{"english":"a coherent campaign series","chinese":"連貫的競選宣傳系列"},{"english":"build trust","chinese":"建立信任"},{"english":"build confidence in","chinese":"建立對……的信心"},{"english":"build belief in action","chinese":"建立對行動的信念"},{"english":"I would appreciate it if","chinese":"如蒙……我將十分感激"},{"english":"review these proposals","chinese":"審視這些建議"},{"english":"advise whether","chinese":"建議是否"},{"english":"final campaign theme","chinese":"最終競選主題"},{"english":"be presented as","chinese":"被呈現為"},{"english":"once your preference is confirmed","chinese":"一旦確認你們的偏好"},{"english":"refine Poster C accordingly","chinese":"相應修改海報 C"},{"english":"Yours faithfully","chinese":"謹啟"},{"english":"Volunteer, District Council Office","chinese":"區議會辦事處義工"}]},"dse-writing-2019-part-b-q9":{"exerciseId":"dse-writing-2019-part-b-q9","essayKey":"","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=dse-writing-2019-part-b-q9","flashDeckId":"dse/writing/part-b/2019/Q9","paragraphs":[{"label":"Paragraph 1","english":"Long after the tortoise had beaten the hare, the animals of Greenwood still told the story whenever someone became too proud. Every time a squirrel whispered, “ Slow and steady,” the hare’s ears burned. Yet he knew the tale was true. He had been fast, careless and foolish; the tortoise had been slow, patient and impossible to shake.","chinese":""},{"label":"Paragraph 2","english":"One golden morning, a poster appeared on the old oak: THE GREAT GREENWOOD CHALLENGE Teams of two only. Mountains, river, meadow and maze. First pair to cross the line together wins.","chinese":""},{"label":"Paragraph 3","english":"By noon, the clearing was buzzing. The fox chose the weasel, both clever and sharp-eyed. The stag chose the squirrel, one strong and one nimble. The otter chose the kingfisher, one at home in water and one in the air. The hare stood alone, pretending not to care.","chinese":""},{"label":"Paragraph 4","english":"Then a calm voice came from behind him. “We could enter together.”","chinese":""},{"label":"Paragraph 5","english":"The hare spun round. There stood the tortoise.","chinese":""},{"label":"Paragraph 6","english":"“You and me?” the hare said. “After what happened?”","chinese":""},{"label":"Paragraph 7","english":"“Because of what happened,” replied the tortoise. “You know speed. I know patience. Neither of us knows enough alone.” The hare wanted to prove that he could win without help. Yet the course stretched beyond the meadow, across the river and into the thorn maze, and there was no getting around the fact that speed alone would not be enough.","chinese":""},{"label":"Paragraph 8","english":"So he nodded. “All right. But if we lose—”","chinese":""},{"label":"Paragraph 9","english":"“We lose together,” said the tortoise.","chinese":""},{"label":"Paragraph 10","english":"At dawn the next day, the contestants lined up beneath fluttering leaves. The owl raised one wing. “Remember: both members must finish together.”","chinese":""},{"label":"Paragraph 11","english":"“Together,” muttered the hare, as if the word were heavier than a boulder.","chinese":""},{"label":"Paragraph 12","english":"The wing fell.","chinese":""},{"label":"Paragraph 13","english":"No sooner had the race begun than the hare shot forward like an arrow. The tortoise called after him, “Not the middle path! The grass is wet there!”","chinese":""},{"label":"Paragraph 14","english":"For once, the hare listened. He curved towards the dry ridge. Behind them, the stag slipped, sending the squirrel tumbling into a mushroom patch. The fox laughed too soon, took a shortcut through mud, and lost a shoe. Slowly but surely, the tortoise’s advice became as valuable as the hare’s legs.","chinese":""},{"label":"Paragraph 15","english":"At the river, however, the hare stopped dead. The water foamed over smooth black stones. “I can jump streams,” he said. “Not rivers.”","chinese":""},{"label":"Paragraph 16","english":"The otter and kingfisher were already gliding ahead.","chinese":""},{"label":"Paragraph 17","english":"“Climb on,” said the tortoise. “My shell. Unless you would rather argue until sunset.”","chinese":""},{"label":"Paragraph 18","english":"It was ridiculous. It was embarrassing. It was necessary. The hare climbed onto the tortoise’s back, and bit by bit they crossed. The current shoved them sideways; the hare leaned left, then right, balancing them. The tortoise swam on, while the hare kept them from rolling over. By the time they reached the opposite bank, neither could say who had saved whom.","chinese":""},{"label":"Paragraph 19","english":"The final obstacle was the thorn maze. The fox and weasel had entered first, only to blame each other at every turn. Their cleverness, divided, became little more than noise.","chinese":""},{"label":"Paragraph 20","english":"The tortoise studied the ground. “The roots bend towards the hill. Follow them.”","chinese":""},{"label":"Paragraph 21","english":"The hare dashed ahead, then stopped himself. Up until yesterday, he would have run on alone. Now he looked back. The tortoise was stuck beneath a tangle of thorns, his shell wedged tight.","chinese":""},{"label":"Paragraph 22","english":"For a heartbeat, the finishing line flashed before the hare’s eyes. So close. So tempting.","chinese":""},{"label":"Paragraph 23","english":"Then he turned around. He dug, pulled and scratched until the tortoise was free. The other teams burst from the maze. The line was only a few leaps away.","chinese":""},{"label":"Paragraph 24","english":"“Go,” panted the tortoise.","chinese":""},{"label":"Paragraph 25","english":"“No,” said the hare. “ Not this time.”","chinese":""},{"label":"Paragraph 26","english":"He lowered his back. The tortoise climbed on, and the hare ran— not wildly, not proudly, but carefully, feeling every breath of his partner behind him. They crossed the line together, just one whisker ahead of the otter and kingfisher.","chinese":""},{"label":"Paragraph 27","english":"The clearing erupted.","chinese":""},{"label":"Paragraph 28","english":"The hare looked at the tortoise. “I suppose the message is still ‘slow and steady wins the race’?”","chinese":""},{"label":"Paragraph 29","english":"The tortoise smiled. “Not exactly.”","chinese":""},{"label":"Paragraph 30","english":"That evening, the owl carved new words beneath the old oak:","chinese":""},{"label":"Paragraph 31","english":"Speed may win a moment. Patience may win a mile. But trust wins the race that no one can finish alone.","chinese":""}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"need two","chinese":"需要兩個人；需要兩位拍檔"},{"english":"long after","chinese":"在……很久之後"},{"english":"the tortoise","chinese":"陸龜"},{"english":"beat the hare","chinese":"擊敗野兔"},{"english":"the hare","chinese":"野兔"},{"english":"tell the story","chinese":"講述這個故事"},{"english":"whenever someone became too proud","chinese":"每當有人變得太驕傲時"},{"english":"slow and steady","chinese":"慢而穩"},{"english":"ears burned","chinese":"耳朵發燙；感到尷尬"},{"english":"the tale was true","chinese":"這個故事是真的"},{"english":"careless and foolish","chinese":"粗心而愚蠢"},{"english":"impossible to shake","chinese":"難以動搖"},{"english":"one golden morning","chinese":"一個金色的早晨"},{"english":"a poster appeared","chinese":"一張海報出現"},{"english":"the old oak","chinese":"老橡樹"},{"english":"teams of two only","chinese":"只限二人隊伍"},{"english":"mountains, river, meadow and maze","chinese":"山、河、草地和迷宮"},{"english":"meadow","chinese":"草地"},{"english":"maze","chinese":"迷宮"},{"english":"first pair to cross the line","chinese":"首對衝線的組合"},{"english":"cross the line together","chinese":"一起衝線"},{"english":"by noon","chinese":"到了中午"},{"english":"the clearing","chinese":"林中空地"},{"english":"be buzzing","chinese":"熱鬧起來；充滿興奮氣氛"},{"english":"clever and sharp-eyed","chinese":"聰明而眼利"},{"english":"sharp-eyed","chinese":"眼利的；眼光敏銳的"},{"english":"one strong and one nimble","chinese":"一個強壯、一個敏捷"},{"english":"nimble","chinese":"敏捷的"},{"english":"at home in water","chinese":"熟習水性"},{"english":"in the air","chinese":"在空中"},{"english":"stand alone","chinese":"獨自站着"},{"english":"pretend not to care","chinese":"假裝不在乎"},{"english":"a calm voice","chinese":"平靜的聲音"},{"english":"enter together","chinese":"一起參賽"},{"english":"spin round","chinese":"猛地轉身"},{"english":"after what happened","chinese":"在發生那件事之後"},{"english":"because of what happened","chinese":"正正因為發生過那件事"},{"english":"know speed","chinese":"懂得速度"},{"english":"know patience","chinese":"懂得耐性"},{"english":"neither of us","chinese":"我們兩個都不"},{"english":"know enough alone","chinese":"單靠自己知道得不夠"},{"english":"want to prove that","chinese":"想證明"},{"english":"win without help","chinese":"不靠幫助而取勝"},{"english":"the course stretched beyond","chinese":"賽道延伸至……以外"},{"english":"beyond the meadow","chinese":"在草地之外"},{"english":"thorn maze","chinese":"荊棘迷宮"},{"english":"there was no getting around the fact that","chinese":"無法迴避……這個事實"},{"english":"speed alone","chinese":"單靠速度"},{"english":"would not be enough","chinese":"並不足夠"},{"english":"nod","chinese":"點頭"},{"english":"if we lose","chinese":"如果我們輸了"},{"english":"lose together","chinese":"一起輸"},{"english":"at dawn","chinese":"黎明時分"},{"english":"contestants","chinese":"參賽者"},{"english":"line up","chinese":"排成一列；列隊"},{"english":"beneath fluttering leaves","chinese":"在飄動的樹葉下"},{"english":"fluttering leaves","chinese":"飄動的樹葉"},{"english":"raise one wing","chinese":"舉起一邊翅膀"},{"english":"both members","chinese":"兩名隊員"},{"english":"finish together","chinese":"一起完成"},{"english":"mutter","chinese":"低聲咕噥"},{"english":"as if","chinese":"好像"},{"english":"heavier than a boulder","chinese":"比巨石更重"},{"english":"boulder","chinese":"巨石"},{"english":"No sooner had… than…","chinese":"一……就……"},{"english":"shoot forward","chinese":"飛奔向前"},{"english":"like an arrow","chinese":"像箭一樣"},{"english":"call after someone","chinese":"在某人身後喊"},{"english":"the middle path","chinese":"中間的小路"},{"english":"for once","chinese":"這一次；難得一次"},{"english":"curve towards","chinese":"轉向"},{"english":"dry ridge","chinese":"乾爽的山脊；高地"},{"english":"slip","chinese":"滑倒"},{"english":"send someone tumbling","chinese":"令某人摔倒"},{"english":"mushroom patch","chinese":"蘑菇叢"},{"english":"laugh too soon","chinese":"笑得太早"},{"english":"take a shortcut","chinese":"抄捷徑"},{"english":"through mud","chinese":"穿過泥濘"},{"english":"slowly but surely","chinese":"緩慢但穩定地"},{"english":"advice became valuable","chinese":"建議變得有價值"},{"english":"as valuable as","chinese":"和……一樣有價值"},{"english":"stop dead","chinese":"突然停住"},{"english":"foam over","chinese":"在……上泛起泡沫"},{"english":"smooth black stones","chinese":"光滑的黑石"},{"english":"jump streams","chinese":"跳過小溪"},{"english":"glide ahead","chinese":"向前滑行"},{"english":"climb on","chinese":"爬上來"},{"english":"unless you would rather","chinese":"除非你寧願"},{"english":"argue until sunset","chinese":"爭論到日落"},{"english":"ridiculous, embarrassing and necessary","chinese":"荒謬、尷尬但必要"},{"english":"climb onto","chinese":"爬到……上"},{"english":"bit by bit","chinese":"一點一點地"},{"english":"the current","chinese":"水流"},{"english":"shove someone sideways","chinese":"把某人推向一邊"},{"english":"lean left and right","chinese":"左右傾斜"},{"english":"balance them","chinese":"令他們保持平衡"},{"english":"swim on","chinese":"繼續游"},{"english":"keep someone from doing something","chinese":"防止某人做某事"},{"english":"roll over","chinese":"翻側"},{"english":"by the time","chinese":"到……的時候"},{"english":"opposite bank","chinese":"對岸"},{"english":"neither could say","chinese":"兩者都說不出"},{"english":"who had saved whom","chinese":"誰救了誰"},{"english":"final obstacle","chinese":"最後一個障礙"},{"english":"enter first","chinese":"率先進入"},{"english":"only to","chinese":"結果卻"},{"english":"blame each other","chinese":"互相責怪"},{"english":"at every turn","chinese":"每到一個轉角；每一步"},{"english":"cleverness, divided","chinese":"分裂的聰明才智"},{"english":"little more than","chinese":"只不過是"},{"english":"study the ground","chinese":"細看地面"},{"english":"bend towards","chinese":"向……彎曲"},{"english":"follow them","chinese":"跟着它們走"},{"english":"dash ahead","chinese":"向前衝"},{"english":"stop himself","chinese":"使自己停下來"},{"english":"up until yesterday","chinese":"直到昨天為止"},{"english":"run on alone","chinese":"獨自繼續跑"},{"english":"look back","chinese":"回頭看"},{"english":"be stuck beneath","chinese":"被困在……下面"},{"english":"a tangle of thorns","chinese":"一團荊棘"},{"english":"shell wedged tight","chinese":"龜殼被緊緊卡住"},{"english":"for a heartbeat","chinese":"一瞬間"},{"english":"finishing line","chinese":"終點線"},{"english":"flash before someone's eyes","chinese":"在某人眼前閃過"},{"english":"so close, so tempting","chinese":"如此接近，如此誘人"},{"english":"turn around","chinese":"轉身回去"},{"english":"dig, pull and scratch","chinese":"挖、拉、抓"},{"english":"until someone was free","chinese":"直到某人脫困"},{"english":"burst from the maze","chinese":"從迷宮中衝出"},{"english":"a few leaps away","chinese":"只差幾步之遙"},{"english":"pant","chinese":"氣喘吁吁地說"},{"english":"not this time","chinese":"這次不會"},{"english":"lower his back","chinese":"壓低背部"},{"english":"not wildly, not proudly, but carefully","chinese":"不是魯莽地，也不是驕傲地，而是小心地"},{"english":"feel every breath","chinese":"感受到每一下呼吸"},{"english":"partner","chinese":"拍檔"},{"english":"just one whisker ahead of","chinese":"只以極微距離領先"},{"english":"the clearing erupted","chinese":"林中空地爆發歡呼"},{"english":"I suppose","chinese":"我想；我猜"},{"english":"not exactly","chinese":"不完全是"},{"english":"carve new words","chinese":"刻上新字"},{"english":"beneath the old oak","chinese":"在老橡樹下"},{"english":"speed may win a moment","chinese":"速度也許能贏得一刻"},{"english":"patience may win a mile","chinese":"耐性也許能贏得一里路"},{"english":"trust wins the race","chinese":"信任贏得比賽"},{"english":"no one can finish alone","chinese":"沒有人能獨自完成"}]},"dse-writing-2020-part-a":{"exerciseId":"dse-writing-2020-part-a","essayKey":"","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=dse-writing-2020-part-a","flashDeckId":"dse/writing/part-a/2020","paragraphs":[{"label":"Title","english":"Restaurant Review: Dim Sum One","chinese":"餐廳評論：Dim Sum One"},{"label":"Introduction","english":"I recently visited Dim Sum One, Hong Kong’s hottest new dim sum restaurant, and was eager to find out if it lived up to its impressive reputation. From the moment I walked in, I was greeted by a friendly hostess and ushered to a sleek, modern dining area that still managed to feel remarkably cozy.","chinese":"我最近到訪了 Dim Sum One，這間香港最炙手可熱的新點心餐廳，並十分期待看看它是否名副其實，配得上那令人印象深刻的聲譽。 從我走進餐廳的一刻起，一位友善的女接待員便向我打招呼，並帶我前往一個設計時尚現代、卻仍然令人感到格外舒適的用餐區。"},{"label":"Food and Service","english":"The food was simply outstanding, with delicate shrimp dumplings and perfectly steamed barbecue pork buns stealing the spotlight. Each dish was artfully presented and bursting with authentic Cantonese flavors. Furthermore, the service was top-notch; staff members politely explained each item on the menu and kept our teapots filled without delay.","chinese":"食物實在非常出色，其中精緻的蝦餃和蒸得恰到好處的叉燒包尤其搶眼。 每一道菜都擺盤講究，並充滿正宗的廣東風味。 此外，服務也是一流的；職員有禮貌地講解餐牌上每一款食品，並且總是及時為我們添茶"},{"label":"Drawbacks","english":"Nevertheless, I found the prices slightly steep compared to other dim sum spots in the city. Additionally, the seating felt a bit cramped during peak hours, which might diminish the otherwise relaxed ambiance. Despite these drawbacks, the overall dining environment remained inviting and well-lit.","chinese":"不過，與城中其他點心店相比，我覺得這裏的價格略為偏高。 此外，在繁忙時段，座位感覺有點擠迫，這可能會削弱原本輕鬆的氣氛。 儘管有這些不足之處，整體用餐環境仍然舒適宜人，而且光線充足。"},{"label":"Recommendation","english":"In my opinion, Dim Sum One is an excellent choice for small gatherings and special occasions, thanks to its premium food quality and warm hospitality. I wholeheartedly recommend it if you are willing to pay a little extra for a memorable feast.","chinese":"在我看來，Dim Sum One 是小型聚會和特別場合的絕佳選擇，因為它擁有高質素的食物和親切周到的款待。 如果你願意多花一點錢，享受一頓難忘的盛宴，我會衷心推薦這間餐廳。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"restaurant review","chinese":"餐廳評論"},{"english":"recently visited","chinese":"最近到訪"},{"english":"Hong Kong's hottest new","chinese":"香港最熱門的新……"},{"english":"dim sum restaurant","chinese":"點心餐廳"},{"english":"be eager to","chinese":"急切想"},{"english":"find out if","chinese":"弄清楚是否"},{"english":"live up to","chinese":"不負……；符合……期望"},{"english":"impressive reputation","chinese":"令人印象深刻的名聲"},{"english":"from the moment","chinese":"從……一刻起"},{"english":"walk in","chinese":"走進去"},{"english":"be greeted by","chinese":"受到……迎接"},{"english":"friendly hostess","chinese":"友善的女接待員"},{"english":"be ushered to","chinese":"被帶到"},{"english":"sleek, modern dining area","chinese":"時尚現代的用餐區"},{"english":"still managed to feel","chinese":"仍然令人感到"},{"english":"remarkably cosy","chinese":"格外舒適"},{"english":"simply outstanding","chinese":"非常出色"},{"english":"delicate shrimp dumplings","chinese":"精緻蝦餃"},{"english":"perfectly steamed","chinese":"蒸得恰到好處"},{"english":"barbecue pork buns","chinese":"叉燒包"},{"english":"steal the spotlight","chinese":"成為焦點；最搶眼"},{"english":"artfully presented","chinese":"擺盤精美"},{"english":"burst with","chinese":"充滿……"},{"english":"authentic Cantonese flavours","chinese":"正宗廣東風味"},{"english":"furthermore","chinese":"此外"},{"english":"top-notch","chinese":"一流的；非常出色的"},{"english":"staff members","chinese":"職員"},{"english":"politely explained","chinese":"有禮貌地解釋"},{"english":"each item on the menu","chinese":"餐牌上的每一款食品"},{"english":"keep our teapots filled","chinese":"不斷為我們添茶"},{"english":"without delay","chinese":"毫不耽誤；很快"},{"english":"nevertheless","chinese":"然而"},{"english":"slightly steep","chinese":"稍為偏貴"},{"english":"compared to","chinese":"與……相比"},{"english":"dim sum spots","chinese":"點心店；點心餐廳"},{"english":"in the city","chinese":"在市內"},{"english":"additionally","chinese":"另外"},{"english":"seating","chinese":"座位安排"},{"english":"a bit cramped","chinese":"有點擠迫"},{"english":"during peak hours","chinese":"在繁忙時間"},{"english":"diminish","chinese":"減弱；削弱"},{"english":"otherwise relaxed ambiance","chinese":"原本輕鬆的氣氛"},{"english":"despite these drawbacks","chinese":"儘管有這些缺點"},{"english":"overall dining environment","chinese":"整體用餐環境"},{"english":"remain inviting","chinese":"仍然吸引；仍令人感到親切"},{"english":"well-lit","chinese":"光線充足"},{"english":"in my opinion","chinese":"依我看"},{"english":"an excellent choice for","chinese":"……的絕佳選擇"},{"english":"small gatherings","chinese":"小型聚會"},{"english":"special occasions","chinese":"特別場合"},{"english":"thanks to","chinese":"由於；多虧"},{"english":"premium food quality","chinese":"高級食物質素"},{"english":"warm hospitality","chinese":"熱情款待"},{"english":"wholeheartedly recommend","chinese":"真心推薦"},{"english":"be willing to","chinese":"願意"},{"english":"pay a little extra","chinese":"額外多付一點"},{"english":"memorable feast","chinese":"難忘盛宴"}]},"dse-writing-2020-part-b-q2":{"exerciseId":"dse-writing-2020-part-b-q2","essayKey":"","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=dse-writing-2020-part-b-q2","flashDeckId":"dse/writing/part-b/2020/Q2","paragraphs":[{"label":"Paragraph 1","english":"More Than a Backdrop","chinese":"不只是背景"},{"label":"Paragraph 2","english":"For better or worse, social media has changed the way Hong Kong’s public housing estates are seen. Once simply homes for ordinary families, they have become colourful backdrops for online self-expression. For my class assignment, I visited Choi Hung Estate in Wong Tai Sin, one of Hong Kong’s top ten photo spots, and interviewed Instagrammers and residents. I wanted to understand what draws young people there and what this attention means to those who live there. This essay will explain that Instagrammers are attracted by visual beauty and local identity, while residents feel both pride and unease.","chinese":"不論好壞，社交媒體已經改變了人們看待香港公共屋邨的方式。 這些屋邨曾經只是普通家庭的居所，如今卻成為網上自我表達的繽紛背景。 為了完成我的課堂習作，我到訪了位於黃大仙的彩虹邨——香港十大拍照熱點之一，並訪問了 Instagram 打卡者和居民。 我想了解的是，究竟是甚麼吸引年輕人到那裡，以及這份關注對居住在那裡的人意味著甚麼。 本文將說明，Instagram 打卡者受到視覺美感和本地身份的吸引，而居民則既感到自豪，也感到不安。"},{"label":"Paragraph 3","english":"The first attraction is the striking appearance of the estates. Choi Hung Estate is not merely a group of residential blocks; collectively it is an instantly recognisable composition of colour, lines and space. Its rainbow-painted walls, basketball court and long corridors create the kind of symmetrical background that works naturally on a phone screen. One student I interviewed said that “every corner already looks edited”, meaning that little, if any, effort is needed to make the photos attractive. Take the rooftop court, for example: a person standing in front of the pastel walls can become the centre of a picture without destroying the pattern behind. The attraction, therefore, not only is beauty in the traditional sense, but also visual clarity. The estate gives Instagrammers something bold enough to catch attention and simple enough to fit the square frame of social media.","chinese":"第一個吸引之處，是屋邨那奪目的外觀。 彩虹邨並不僅僅是一組住宅大廈；整體而言，它是一幅令人一眼便能認出的色彩、線條與空間構圖。 它那塗上彩虹色的牆身、籃球場和長長的走廊，創造出一種在手機屏幕上自然成立的對稱背景。 我訪問的一名學生說，「每個角落都已經像修過圖一樣」，意思是要把照片拍得吸引，幾乎不需要任何努力。 以天台球場為例：一個人站在柔和色調的牆身前，便可以成為照片的中心，同時不會破壞背後的圖案。 因此，這種吸引力不僅在於傳統意義上的美感，也在於視覺上的清晰。 屋邨給了 Instagram 打卡者一種既足夠鮮明、能吸引注意，又足夠簡潔、能配合社交媒體方形相框的東西。"},{"label":"Paragraph 4","english":"Another reason is that these estates offer something more meaningful than an artificial tourist attraction - namely - a sense of local identity. Unlike shopping malls, which often look similar in any modern city, Hong Kong’s older housing estates show the city’s density, history and everyday rhythm. At Yik Cheong Building in Quarry Bay, for instance, the tightly packed flats form a dramatic “concrete canyon”; at Choi Hung, elderly neighbours exercising and children playing after school remind visitors that this is a living community, not a museum set. Several Instagrammers said they preferred these places because they felt “more Hong Kong” than luxury hotels or harbour-view cafés. The more global Instagram becomes, the more people search for images rooted in a real place. Paradoxically, what attracts visitors is precisely what residents consider ordinary: laundry on rails, old lifts, tiled walls and open spaces between blocks.","chinese":"另一個原因是，這些屋邨提供了比人工打造的旅遊景點更有意義的東西—— 也就是一種本地身份感。 商場在任何現代城市中往往看起來相似；相比之下，香港較舊的屋邨展現了這座城市的密度、歷史和日常節奏。 以鰂魚涌益昌大廈為例，密密麻麻的單位形成了一道戲劇性的「石屎峽谷」；而在彩虹邨，做運動的長者鄰里和放學後玩耍的孩子，提醒訪客這是一個正在生活的社區，而不是博物館布景。 幾位 Instagram 打卡者說，他們偏愛這些地方，因為它們比豪華酒店或海景咖啡店「更有香港味」。 Instagram 越是全球化，人們便越會尋找植根於真實地方的影像。 矛盾的是，吸引訪客的，正正是居民眼中最普通的東西：欄杆上的衣物、舊式升降機、瓷磚牆身，以及大廈之間的空地。"},{"label":"Paragraph 5","english":"Residents’ feelings, however, are far from simple. Some are pleased that their estate has become famous. A retired resident, Mrs Lau, told me that she had lived there for more than forty years and felt proud when visitors praised the colours of the buildings. In her eyes, the attention proves that public housing is not necessarily dull or embarrassing; it can be part of Hong Kong’s visual culture. With popularity comes recognition, and recognition can make an ordinary neighbourhood feel valued. Nevertheless, many residents are uncomfortable with the disturbance created by Instagram tourism. Their complaint is not that visitors take photos, but that some forget the estate is first of all a home. During my visit, a middle-aged resident said he had seen people blocking staircases, shouting across the basketball court and taking photos of residents without permission. What is harmless fun to one person may be an invasion of privacy to another. A young mother put it best: she did not mind visitors coming, provided that they “remember people live here”. Her words reveal the central tension. Instagrammers see a backdrop; residents see their front door, their safety and their right to live without being watched.","chinese":"然而，居民的感受遠非簡單。 有些居民很高興自己的屋邨變得有名。 一位退休居民劉太告訴我，她已經在那裡住了四十多年；當訪客稱讚大廈的顏色時，她會感到自豪。 在她眼中，這份關注證明公共房屋並不一定沉悶或令人尷尬；它也可以成為香港視覺文化的一部分。 有了人氣，便有了認同；而認同可以令一個普通社區感到自己被重視。 儘管如此，許多居民對 Instagram 旅遊所造成的滋擾感到不自在。 他們投訴的並不是訪客拍照，而是有些人忘記了屋邨首先是一個家。 在我到訪期間，一位中年居民說，他曾見過有人堵塞樓梯、在籃球場上大聲呼喊，以及未經同意便拍攝居民。 對一個人來說無傷大雅的樂趣，對另一個人來說卻可能是對私隱的侵犯。 一位年輕母親說得最好：她不介意訪客到來，只要他們「記得這裡有人居住」。 她的話揭示了核心矛盾。 Instagram 打卡者看見的是背景；居民看見的，是自己的家門、自己的安全，以及自己不被旁人觀看地生活的權利。"},{"label":"Paragraph 6","english":"All things considered, the popularity of Hong Kong’s housing estates on Instagram shows both the power and the danger of visual culture. These estates attract Instagrammers because they combine colour, geometry, local character and online appeal in a way few purpose-built attractions can match. At the same time, residents respond with mixed feelings: pride when their neighbourhood is appreciated, and frustration when appreciation comes at the cost of privacy and peace. The way forward is not to ban visitors, but to build a more respectful photo culture. Only by asking permission, keeping voices down and avoiding private areas can visitors treat every estate as a community rather than simply a stage.","chinese":"綜合而言，香港屋邨在 Instagram 上的受歡迎程度，展現了視覺文化的力量，也展現了它的危險。 這些屋邨吸引 Instagram 打卡者，是因為它們把色彩、幾何美感、本地特色和網上吸引力結合起來，而這種效果是少數專門打造的景點也難以媲美的。 與此同時，居民的反應是複雜的：當自己的社區受到欣賞時，他們感到自豪；但當這種欣賞以私隱和寧靜為代價時，他們也會感到沮喪。 未來的方向不是禁止訪客，而是建立一種更尊重他人的拍照文化。 只有透過先徵求同意、降低聲量並避開私人範圍，訪客才能把每一個屋邨視為一個社區，而不僅僅是一個舞台。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"more than a backdrop","chinese":"不只是背景"},{"english":"for better or worse","chinese":"不論好壞；無論利弊"},{"english":"social media","chinese":"社交媒體"},{"english":"change the way something is seen","chinese":"改變……被看待的方式"},{"english":"public housing estates","chinese":"公共屋邨"},{"english":"once simply homes for","chinese":"曾經只是……的家"},{"english":"ordinary families","chinese":"普通家庭"},{"english":"colourful backdrops","chinese":"色彩繽紛的背景"},{"english":"online self-expression","chinese":"網上自我表達"},{"english":"class assignment","chinese":"課堂習作"},{"english":"top ten photo spots","chinese":"十大打卡熱點"},{"english":"interviewed Instagrammers and residents","chinese":"訪問 Instagram 用戶和居民"},{"english":"what draws young people there","chinese":"是甚麼吸引年輕人到那裏"},{"english":"what this attention means to","chinese":"這種關注對……有甚麼意義"},{"english":"visual beauty","chinese":"視覺美感"},{"english":"local identity","chinese":"本地身份；地方認同"},{"english":"both pride and unease","chinese":"既自豪又不安"},{"english":"the first attraction","chinese":"第一個吸引之處"},{"english":"striking appearance","chinese":"醒目的外觀"},{"english":"not merely","chinese":"不僅僅是"},{"english":"residential blocks","chinese":"住宅大廈"},{"english":"collectively","chinese":"整體來說"},{"english":"instantly recognisable","chinese":"一眼就能認出的"},{"english":"composition of colour, lines and space","chinese":"色彩、線條與空間的構圖"},{"english":"rainbow-painted walls","chinese":"彩虹色外牆"},{"english":"basketball court","chinese":"籃球場"},{"english":"long corridors","chinese":"長長的走廊"},{"english":"symmetrical background","chinese":"對稱的背景"},{"english":"work naturally on a phone screen","chinese":"在手機屏幕上自然好看"},{"english":"every corner already looks edited","chinese":"每個角落都像已修圖一樣"},{"english":"little, if any, effort","chinese":"幾乎不需要任何努力"},{"english":"make the photos attractive","chinese":"令相片吸引"},{"english":"rooftop court","chinese":"天台球場"},{"english":"standing in front of","chinese":"站在……前面"},{"english":"pastel walls","chinese":"淺色柔和的牆身"},{"english":"become the centre of a picture","chinese":"成為相片的焦點"},{"english":"the pattern behind","chinese":"背後的圖案"},{"english":"not only...but also","chinese":"不但……而且……"},{"english":"beauty in the traditional sense","chinese":"傳統意義上的美"},{"english":"visual clarity","chinese":"視覺清晰度"},{"english":"bold enough to catch attention","chinese":"夠鮮明去吸引注意"},{"english":"simple enough to fit","chinese":"夠簡潔去配合……"},{"english":"the square frame of social media","chinese":"社交媒體的方形畫面"},{"english":"another reason is that","chinese":"另一個原因是"},{"english":"something more meaningful than","chinese":"比……更有意義的東西"},{"english":"artificial tourist attraction","chinese":"人工化的旅遊景點"},{"english":"a sense of local identity","chinese":"本地身份感；地方認同感"},{"english":"unlike shopping malls","chinese":"不像商場"},{"english":"look similar in any modern city","chinese":"在任何現代城市都看起來相似"},{"english":"older housing estates","chinese":"較舊的屋邨"},{"english":"density, history and everyday rhythm","chinese":"密度、歷史和日常節奏"},{"english":"tightly packed flats","chinese":"密集的住宅單位"},{"english":"form a dramatic concrete canyon","chinese":"形成震撼的石屎峽谷"},{"english":"concrete canyon","chinese":"石屎峽谷"},{"english":"elderly neighbours exercising","chinese":"做運動的長者街坊"},{"english":"children playing after school","chinese":"放學後玩耍的小朋友"},{"english":"remind visitors that","chinese":"提醒訪客"},{"english":"living community","chinese":"仍有人生活的社區"},{"english":"museum set","chinese":"博物館佈景；展覽佈景"},{"english":"several Instagrammers said","chinese":"幾位 Instagram 用戶表示"},{"english":"feel more Hong Kong","chinese":"更有香港味"},{"english":"luxury hotels","chinese":"豪華酒店"},{"english":"harbour-view cafés","chinese":"海景咖啡店"},{"english":"the more..., the more...","chinese":"越……就越……"},{"english":"rooted in a real place","chinese":"植根於真實地方"},{"english":"paradoxically","chinese":"矛盾的是"},{"english":"precisely what","chinese":"正正是"},{"english":"consider ordinary","chinese":"視為平常"},{"english":"laundry on rails","chinese":"晾在欄杆上的衣物"},{"english":"old lifts","chinese":"舊式升降機"},{"english":"tiled walls","chinese":"瓷磚牆"},{"english":"open spaces between blocks","chinese":"大廈之間的公共空間"},{"english":"feelings are far from simple","chinese":"感受絕不簡單"},{"english":"be pleased that","chinese":"對……感到高興"},{"english":"become famous","chinese":"變得有名"},{"english":"retired resident","chinese":"退休居民"},{"english":"live there for more than forty years","chinese":"在那裏住了四十多年"},{"english":"feel proud when","chinese":"當……時感到自豪"},{"english":"praise the colours of","chinese":"讚賞……的顏色"},{"english":"in her eyes","chinese":"在她眼中"},{"english":"attention proves that","chinese":"這種關注證明"},{"english":"public housing","chinese":"公共房屋"},{"english":"not necessarily","chinese":"不一定"},{"english":"dull or embarrassing","chinese":"沉悶或令人尷尬"},{"english":"visual culture","chinese":"視覺文化"},{"english":"with popularity comes recognition","chinese":"受歡迎帶來認同"},{"english":"make a neighbourhood feel valued","chinese":"令社區感到受重視"},{"english":"ordinary neighbourhood","chinese":"普通社區"},{"english":"nevertheless","chinese":"然而"},{"english":"be uncomfortable with","chinese":"對……感到不舒服"},{"english":"disturbance created by","chinese":"由……造成的滋擾"},{"english":"Instagram tourism","chinese":"Instagram 打卡旅遊"},{"english":"the complaint is not that..., but that...","chinese":"投訴的不是……而是……"},{"english":"first of all a home","chinese":"首先是一個家"},{"english":"middle-aged resident","chinese":"中年居民"},{"english":"block staircases","chinese":"阻塞樓梯"},{"english":"shout across","chinese":"隔着……大聲呼喊"},{"english":"take photos without permission","chinese":"未經同意拍照"},{"english":"harmless fun","chinese":"無傷大雅的玩樂"},{"english":"an invasion of privacy","chinese":"侵犯私隱"},{"english":"put it best","chinese":"說得最好；最能概括"},{"english":"not mind visitors coming","chinese":"不介意訪客到來"},{"english":"provided that","chinese":"只要；假如"},{"english":"remember people live here","chinese":"記得這裏有人居住"},{"english":"reveal the central tension","chinese":"揭示核心矛盾"},{"english":"central tension","chinese":"核心矛盾"},{"english":"see a backdrop","chinese":"視為背景"},{"english":"front door","chinese":"家門口"},{"english":"right to live without being watched","chinese":"不被注視地生活的權利"},{"english":"all things considered","chinese":"總括而言"},{"english":"the power and the danger of","chinese":"……的力量與危險"},{"english":"visual culture","chinese":"視覺文化"},{"english":"combine colour, geometry and local character","chinese":"結合色彩、幾何感和本地特色"},{"english":"online appeal","chinese":"網上吸引力"},{"english":"purpose-built attractions","chinese":"特意建造的景點"},{"english":"respond with mixed feelings","chinese":"以複雜心情回應"},{"english":"mixed feelings","chinese":"複雜心情"},{"english":"neighbourhood is appreciated","chinese":"社區受到欣賞"},{"english":"frustration","chinese":"挫敗感；不滿"},{"english":"come at the cost of","chinese":"以犧牲……為代價"},{"english":"privacy and peace","chinese":"私隱與安寧"},{"english":"the way forward","chinese":"未來方向；解決方法"},{"english":"ban visitors","chinese":"禁止訪客"},{"english":"build a more respectful photo culture","chinese":"建立更尊重他人的拍照文化"},{"english":"asking permission","chinese":"徵求同意"},{"english":"keeping voices down","chinese":"放低聲浪"},{"english":"avoiding private areas","chinese":"避開私人範圍"},{"english":"treat every estate as a community","chinese":"把每個屋邨視為社區"},{"english":"rather than simply a stage","chinese":"而不只是舞台"}]},"dse-writing-2020-part-b-q3":{"exerciseId":"dse-writing-2020-part-b-q3","essayKey":"","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=dse-writing-2020-part-b-q3","flashDeckId":"dse/writing/part-b/2020/Q3","paragraphs":[{"label":"Paragraph 1","english":"Independent Stationery Shops Fight for Survival as Hong Kong Goes Digital","chinese":"獨立文具店在香港走向數碼化之際力求生存"},{"label":"Paragraph 2","english":"By Chris Wong","chinese":"報道"},{"label":"Paragraph 3","english":"Hong Kong Post","chinese":"香港郵報"},{"label":"Paragraph 4","english":"HONG KONG — In recent years, the sight of small, independent stationery shops tucked beside schools and housing estates has become less common. Rising rents, changing study habits and online shopping have turned a once-stable neighbourhood business into a fragile trade. The decline has made shop owners, parents and community groups ask whether these stores can still have a place in Hong Kong’s retail landscape. This report finds that independent stationery shops are under serious pressure, but they can survive if they stop competing as ordinary retailers and rebuild themselves as specialist, service-driven community shops.","chinese":"香港——近年來，藏身於學校和屋邨旁邊的小型獨立文具店，已經越來越少見 租金上升、學習習慣改變，以及網上購物興起，令這門曾經穩定的社區生意變成一個脆弱的行業。 這種衰落令店主、家長和社區團體開始思考，這些店舖是否仍能在香港的零售版圖中佔有一席之地。 本報發現，獨立文具店正面對沉重壓力；然而，如果它們停止以普通零售商的方式競爭，並把自己重新定位為專門化、以服務為本的社區小店，它們仍然可以生存下去。"},{"label":"Paragraph 5","english":"The first reason for the fall is straightforward - that the old business model no longer matches the way families shop. In the past, pupils went to nearby shops for exercise books, coloured paper, correction tape and last-minute project materials. Today, many parents buy stationery in bulk from chain stores, supermarkets or online platforms, where prices are lower and delivery is convenient. A pack of pens can be compared, ordered and delivered without a child stepping into a shop. For customers, this saves time; for shop owners, it removes the daily foot traffic on which they used to depend. “Students still need pens,” said Mr Wong, who runs a stationery shop in Sham Shui Po, “but they no longer buy them one by one after school.”","chinese":"這種衰落的第一個原因十分直接——舊有的營運模式已經不再配合家庭的購物方式。 過去，學生會到附近的文具店購買練習簿、彩色紙、改錯帶，以及最後一刻才需要的專題研習材料。 如今，許多家長會從連鎖店、超級市場或網上平台大量購買文具，因為那裡價格較低，送貨也方便。 一包原子筆可以在網上比較、下單並送到家中，而孩子甚至不用踏進文具店一步 對顧客而言，這節省了時間；但對店主而言，這卻奪走了他們過去賴以維生的日常人流。 「學生仍然需要筆，」在深水埗經營文具店的黃先生說，「但他們已經不再放學後一支一支地買了。」"},{"label":"Paragraph 6","english":"Rent is another burden. Unlike large retailers, independent shops cannot easily absorb months of weak sales or negotiate favourable leases. A small shop selling $8 notebooks and $15 files must sell many items simply to cover rent, wages, electricity and unsold stock. The problem is not so much that people have stopped writing as that the profit on each item is too thin. Once a shop loses regular student customers, it is caught in a painful cycle: fewer sales mean less money to refresh stock; older stock makes the shop look less attractive; an unattractive shop draws even fewer customers.","chinese":"租金是另一項負擔。 與大型零售商不同，獨立小店難以承受連續數月的銷售疲弱，也不容易談判到有利的租約。 一間售賣八元筆記簿和十五元文件夾的小店，必須賣出大量貨品，才勉強足以支付租金、工資、電費和滯銷存貨的成本。 問題並不在於人們已經停止書寫，而在於每件貨品的利潤實在太薄。 一旦一間文具店失去固定的學生顧客，它便會陷入一個痛苦的循環：銷售減少意味着可用來更新存貨的資金減少；較舊的貨品令店舖看起來欠缺吸引力；而欠缺吸引力的店舖又會吸引更少顧客。"},{"label":"Paragraph 7","english":"Schools’ digital transformation has added to the pressure. With more teachers using e-notes, online worksheets and learning apps, some families need fewer folders, refill paper and printed past papers than before. Even when stationery is still required, schools may arrange group purchases directly through suppliers. This is efficient for parents, but it quietly cuts out the small shops that once served as informal supply centres. As Ms Chan, a mother of two, put it, “I like the old shops, but if the school gives us one online order form, of course I use it.”","chinese":"學校的數碼轉型也加重了這種壓力。 隨着更多教師使用電子筆記、網上工作紙和學習應用程式，一些家庭對文件夾、補充紙和印刷版歷屆試題的需求已比以前減少。 即使仍然需要文具，學校也可能直接透過供應商安排集體訂購。 這對家長而言很有效率，卻也悄悄地繞過了那些曾經作為非正式供應中心的小店。 正如育有兩名子女的陳女士所說：「我喜歡那些舊式小店，但如果學校給我們一張網上訂購表格，我當然會使用它。」"},{"label":"Paragraph 8","english":"Yet it would be wrong to say these shops have no future. What they lack in scale, they can make up for in personality, advice and immediacy. A chain store can sell a pen; a good independent shopkeeper can recommend the right ink for left-handed students, suggest affordable art materials for a school project, or assemble an exam kit at short notice. Some shops have already moved in this direction by selling Japanese masking tape, fountain-pen ink, handmade notebooks, calligraphy brushes and craft supplies that are difficult to choose without seeing them in person. Others run simple workshops, take WhatsApp orders from parents, or prepare customised school packs before the term begins.","chinese":"然而，說這些店舖完全沒有未來，並不正確。 它們在規模上有所不足，卻可以用個性、建議和即時性來彌補。 連鎖店可以售賣一支筆；但一位優秀的獨立店主，卻可以為左撇子學生推薦合適的墨水、為學校專題研習建議價格相宜的美術材料，或在短時間內準備好一套考試文具包。 一些店舖已經朝這個方向轉型，售賣日本和紙膠帶、鋼筆墨水、手工筆記簿、毛筆，以及一些若不親眼看見便難以選擇的手工藝用品。 另一些店舖則舉辦簡單工作坊、接受家長透過 WhatsApp 下單，或在開學前準備度身訂造的開學文具套裝。"},{"label":"Paragraph 9","english":"Survival, however, will not happen by nostalgia alone. Shop owners need to build online catalogues, keep a sharper selection of products and work more closely with schools and local artists. Schools can help by allowing small shops to bid for supply lists instead of relying only on large distributors. Landlords, district organisations and residents also have a role to play: if every neighbourhood shop is replaced by the same chain stores, Hong Kong will lose not just variety but also a kind of everyday warmth.","chinese":"然而，單靠懷舊並不能帶來生存。 店主需要建立網上產品目錄，維持更精準的貨品選擇，並與學校和本地藝術家更緊密合作。 學校也可以提供幫助，讓小店競投供應清單，而不是只依賴大型分銷商。 業主、地區組織和居民同樣有角色要扮演：如果每一間社區小店都被相同的連鎖店取代，香港失去的將不只是多樣性，還有一種日常生活中的人情味。"},{"label":"Paragraph 10","english":"For now, independent stationery shops are down, but not necessarily out. The shops that merely wait for the old days to return are likely to disappear. Those that offer expertise, character and convenience, however, may still be standing when the dust settles. In Hong Kong’s fast-changing retail scene, the smallest shops may survive not by being cheaper, but by being more useful, more personal and more deeply rooted in the communities they serve.","chinese":"目前，獨立文具店雖然受挫，但未必已經出局。 那些只是等待昔日光景回來的店舖，很可能會消失。 Conditional Hope / Shops with a Viable Strategy（有條件的希望／具可行策略的店舖） 然而，那些能夠提供專業知識、個性和便利的店舖，在風波平息之後，或許仍然能夠屹立不倒。 在香港瞬息萬變的零售環境中，最小的店舖能夠生存下去，靠的也許不是更低的價格，而是更實用、更有人情味，並且更深深紮根於它們所服務的社區"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"independent stationery shops","chinese":"獨立文具店"},{"english":"fight for survival","chinese":"為生存而掙扎"},{"english":"go digital","chinese":"數碼化"},{"english":"in recent years","chinese":"近年"},{"english":"the sight of","chinese":"……的景象"},{"english":"tucked beside","chinese":"隱身於……旁邊"},{"english":"housing estates","chinese":"屋邨"},{"english":"become less common","chinese":"變得較少見"},{"english":"rising rents","chinese":"租金上升"},{"english":"changing study habits","chinese":"學習習慣改變"},{"english":"online shopping","chinese":"網上購物"},{"english":"turn something into","chinese":"把……變成"},{"english":"a once-stable neighbourhood business","chinese":"曾經穩定的社區生意"},{"english":"a fragile trade","chinese":"脆弱的行業"},{"english":"the decline","chinese":"衰落；下滑"},{"english":"shop owners","chinese":"店主"},{"english":"community groups","chinese":"社區團體"},{"english":"have a place in","chinese":"在……中佔一席位"},{"english":"retail landscape","chinese":"零售格局"},{"english":"under serious pressure","chinese":"承受沉重壓力"},{"english":"competing as ordinary retailers","chinese":"以普通零售商身分競爭"},{"english":"rebuild themselves as","chinese":"把自己重新定位為"},{"english":"specialist shops","chinese":"專門店"},{"english":"service-driven community shops","chinese":"以服務為主導的社區小店"},{"english":"the first reason for the fall","chinese":"衰落的第一個原因"},{"english":"the reason is straightforward","chinese":"原因很直接"},{"english":"old business model","chinese":"舊有經營模式"},{"english":"no longer matches","chinese":"不再配合"},{"english":"the way families shop","chinese":"家庭購物的方式"},{"english":"in the past","chinese":"過去"},{"english":"pupils","chinese":"學生；小學生"},{"english":"nearby shops","chinese":"附近店舖"},{"english":"exercise books","chinese":"練習簿"},{"english":"coloured paper","chinese":"顏色紙"},{"english":"correction tape","chinese":"改錯帶"},{"english":"last-minute project materials","chinese":"臨急需要的專題研習材料"},{"english":"buy stationery in bulk","chinese":"大量購買文具"},{"english":"chain stores","chinese":"連鎖店"},{"english":"online platforms","chinese":"網上平台"},{"english":"prices are lower","chinese":"價格較低"},{"english":"delivery is convenient","chinese":"送貨方便"},{"english":"a pack of pens","chinese":"一包筆"},{"english":"compared, ordered and delivered","chinese":"可比較、訂購並送貨"},{"english":"without stepping into a shop","chinese":"無需走進店舖"},{"english":"this saves time","chinese":"這樣節省時間"},{"english":"removes the daily foot traffic","chinese":"減少每日客流"},{"english":"used to depend on","chinese":"過去依賴"},{"english":"run a stationery shop","chinese":"經營文具店"},{"english":"no longer","chinese":"不再"},{"english":"one by one","chinese":"一支一支地"},{"english":"rent is another burden","chinese":"租金是另一個負擔"},{"english":"unlike large retailers","chinese":"不像大型零售商"},{"english":"large retailers","chinese":"大型零售商"},{"english":"absorb months of weak sales","chinese":"承受數個月生意淡靜"},{"english":"weak sales","chinese":"生意淡靜"},{"english":"negotiate favourable leases","chinese":"商討有利租約"},{"english":"favourable leases","chinese":"有利租約"},{"english":"cover rent, wages and electricity","chinese":"支付租金、工資和電費"},{"english":"unsold stock","chinese":"滯銷存貨"},{"english":"not so much… as…","chinese":"與其說是……不如說是……"},{"english":"profit on each item","chinese":"每件貨品的利潤"},{"english":"too thin","chinese":"太薄；太微薄"},{"english":"regular student customers","chinese":"固定學生顧客"},{"english":"caught in a painful cycle","chinese":"陷入痛苦循環"},{"english":"fewer sales mean less money","chinese":"銷售減少代表資金減少"},{"english":"refresh stock","chinese":"更新存貨"},{"english":"older stock","chinese":"舊存貨"},{"english":"look less attractive","chinese":"看起來較不吸引"},{"english":"draws even fewer customers","chinese":"吸引更少顧客"},{"english":"digital transformation","chinese":"數碼轉型"},{"english":"added to the pressure","chinese":"增加壓力"},{"english":"e-notes","chinese":"電子筆記"},{"english":"online worksheets","chinese":"網上工作紙"},{"english":"learning apps","chinese":"學習應用程式"},{"english":"folders","chinese":"文件夾"},{"english":"refill paper","chinese":"活頁紙"},{"english":"printed past papers","chinese":"印刷版歷屆試卷"},{"english":"even when","chinese":"即使"},{"english":"arrange group purchases","chinese":"安排集體採購"},{"english":"directly through suppliers","chinese":"直接經供應商"},{"english":"efficient for parents","chinese":"對家長來說有效率"},{"english":"quietly cuts out","chinese":"悄悄繞過"},{"english":"served as informal supply centres","chinese":"曾經充當非正式供應中心"},{"english":"informal supply centres","chinese":"非正式供應中心"},{"english":"as someone put it","chinese":"正如某人所說"},{"english":"online order form","chinese":"網上訂購表格"},{"english":"it would be wrong to say","chinese":"說……是錯的"},{"english":"have no future","chinese":"沒有未來"},{"english":"lack in scale","chinese":"規模不足"},{"english":"make up for","chinese":"彌補"},{"english":"personality, advice and immediacy","chinese":"特色、建議和即時性"},{"english":"chain store","chinese":"連鎖店"},{"english":"independent shopkeeper","chinese":"獨立店主"},{"english":"recommend the right ink","chinese":"推薦合適墨水"},{"english":"left-handed students","chinese":"左撇子學生"},{"english":"affordable art materials","chinese":"負擔得起的美術材料"},{"english":"school project","chinese":"學校專題研習"},{"english":"assemble an exam kit","chinese":"組合考試用品套裝"},{"english":"at short notice","chinese":"在短時間通知下"},{"english":"moved in this direction","chinese":"朝這個方向發展"},{"english":"Japanese masking tape","chinese":"日本和紙膠帶"},{"english":"fountain-pen ink","chinese":"鋼筆墨水"},{"english":"handmade notebooks","chinese":"手工筆記簿"},{"english":"calligraphy brushes","chinese":"毛筆"},{"english":"craft supplies","chinese":"手工藝材料"},{"english":"difficult to choose without seeing them in person","chinese":"不親眼看就難以選擇"},{"english":"in person","chinese":"親身；當面"},{"english":"run simple workshops","chinese":"舉辦簡單工作坊"},{"english":"take WhatsApp orders","chinese":"接受 WhatsApp 訂單"},{"english":"prepare customised school packs","chinese":"準備度身訂造的學校用品套裝"},{"english":"before the term begins","chinese":"開學前"},{"english":"by nostalgia alone","chinese":"單靠懷舊情懷"},{"english":"build online catalogues","chinese":"建立網上目錄"},{"english":"keep a sharper selection of products","chinese":"保持更精準的選品"},{"english":"work more closely with","chinese":"與……更緊密合作"},{"english":"local artists","chinese":"本地藝術家"},{"english":"bid for supply lists","chinese":"競投用品清單"},{"english":"supply lists","chinese":"用品清單"},{"english":"relying only on","chinese":"只依賴"},{"english":"large distributors","chinese":"大型分銷商"},{"english":"landlords","chinese":"業主"},{"english":"district organisations","chinese":"地區組織"},{"english":"have a role to play","chinese":"有角色要發揮"},{"english":"be replaced by","chinese":"被……取代"},{"english":"not just… but also…","chinese":"不只是……而且是……"},{"english":"everyday warmth","chinese":"日常人情味"},{"english":"for now","chinese":"目前"},{"english":"down, but not necessarily out","chinese":"受挫但未必出局"},{"english":"not necessarily","chinese":"未必"},{"english":"merely wait for","chinese":"只是等待"},{"english":"the old days to return","chinese":"昔日光景重臨"},{"english":"likely to disappear","chinese":"很可能消失"},{"english":"offer expertise","chinese":"提供專業知識"},{"english":"character and convenience","chinese":"特色和便利"},{"english":"still be standing","chinese":"仍然屹立不倒"},{"english":"when the dust settles","chinese":"塵埃落定時"},{"english":"fast-changing retail scene","chinese":"變化急速的零售環境"},{"english":"not by being cheaper, but by being more useful","chinese":"不是靠更便宜，而是靠更有用"},{"english":"more personal","chinese":"更有人情味；更個人化"},{"english":"deeply rooted in","chinese":"深深紮根於"},{"english":"the communities they serve","chinese":"它們服務的社區"}]},"dse-writing-2020-part-b-q4":{"exerciseId":"dse-writing-2020-part-b-q4","essayKey":"","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=dse-writing-2020-part-b-q4","flashDeckId":"dse/writing/part-b/2020/Q4","paragraphs":[{"label":"Paragraph 1","english":"Application for Transfer to the Shanghai Branch Dear Mr Wong,","chinese":"申請調職至上海分店 黃先生："},{"label":"Paragraph 2","english":"I am writing to apply for a transfer from Park Hotel Hong Kong to our Shanghai branch, should a suitable position become available. Having served the hotel for four years, most recently as a Senior Guest Relations Officer, I have come to see hospitality not simply as providing rooms and meals, but importantly as earning trust at every point of a guest’s journey. As our organisation continues to strengthen its presence in the Mainland market, I believe a staff member who understands both Hong Kong service culture and Putonghua-speaking guests could help the Shanghai team achieve smoother operations, stronger guest loyalty and closer cooperation between the two branches. For these reasons, I respectfully ask for your support in considering my application.","chinese":"本人現謹此申請由香港 Park Hotel 調職至本酒店上海分店，倘若有合適職位空缺。 本人已在酒店服務四年，最近擔任高級賓客服務主任；在這段時間中，我逐漸明白，酒店款待並不只是提供房間與餐飲，更重要的是在賓客旅程的每一個接觸點上建立信任。 隨着本機構繼續加強在內地市場的業務，我相信一位同時了解香港服務文化及普通話賓客需要的員工，能協助上海團隊實現更順暢的營運、更穩固的賓客忠誠度，以及兩地分店之間更緊密的合作。 基於以上原因，本人懇請閣下支持並考慮我的申請。"},{"label":"Paragraph 3","english":"In terms of work experience, I have been involved in many areas of front-office operations. From check-in procedures and room allocation to complaint handling and post-stay follow-up, I have learnt how small details shape a guest’s impression of the hotel. For example, during Golden Week last year, a group of 120 business delegates arrived two hours earlier than scheduled, while several rooms were still being inspected. Instead of leaving them waiting in the lobby, I coordinated with Housekeeping, arranged temporary luggage storage, prepared refreshments in the lounge and explained the revised schedule in English and Putonghua. By the time the rooms were ready, what could have become a serious complaint had turned into several written compliments. This experience made me a better communicator, not to mention a calmer decision-maker under pressure. I have also trained six junior colleagues on service recovery scripts and the guest-preference log, thereby helping the team respond more consistently when difficulties arise.","chinese":"在工作經驗方面，本人曾參與前堂營運的多個範疇。 從入住登記程序、房間分配，到處理投訴及退房後跟進，我學會了細節如何塑造賓客對酒店的印象。 例如，去年黃金周期間，一個由 120 名商務代表組成的團隊比原定時間早到兩小時，而當時仍有數間客房正在檢查。 本人沒有讓他們在大堂空等，而是與房務部協調，安排臨時行李寄存，在貴賓室準備茶點，並以英語和普通話向他們解釋經修訂的安排。 客房準備妥當時，原本可能演變成嚴重投訴的情況，已轉化為數封書面讚賞 這次經驗令我成為更出色的溝通者，更不用說也令我在壓力下成為更冷靜的決策者。 我亦曾培訓六位初級同事使用服務補救話術及賓客偏好紀錄，從而協助團隊在困難出現時作出更一致的回應。"},{"label":"Paragraph 4","english":"My wish to transfer is not based on impatience with my current post; rather, it comes from a sincere desire to grow with the company. Shanghai is one of the most competitive hospitality markets in the region, attracting domestic tourists, expatriates, conference organisers and luxury travellers from around the world. Working there would allow me to understand what counts as excellent service in a different cultural and commercial setting. While Hong Kong has taught me speed, flexibility and international etiquette, Shanghai would broaden my understanding of Mainland consumer expectations, digital payment habits and corporate travel needs. Only by working in such an environment can I develop the wider judgement required of a future manager. In other words, this transfer would be an opportunity to turn my existing experience into cross-market expertise.","chinese":"本人希望調職，並不是因為對現時職位感到急躁或不滿；相反，這是出於一份真誠希望與公司共同成長的願望。 上海是區內競爭最激烈的酒店款待市場之一，吸引本地旅客、外籍人士、會議主辦者，以及來自世界各地的高端旅客。 在當地工作將使我能夠了解，在另一種文化與商業環境中，甚麼才算是卓越服務。 香港教會了我效率、靈活性和國際禮儀，而上海則能擴闊我對內地消費者期望、電子支付習慣及企業差旅需求的理解。 只有在這樣的環境中工作，我才能培養未來管理人員所需要的更廣闊判斷力 換言之，這次調職將是一個把我現有經驗轉化為跨市場專業能力的機會。"},{"label":"Paragraph 5","english":"More importantly, I believe my transfer would benefit the organisation in practical ways. First, I could serve as a bridge between the Hong Kong and Shanghai branches. Since many guests travel between the two cities for finance, trade fairs and family visits, better sharing of guest profiles, room preferences and complaint records would make their stays feel more personal. Second, I could contribute to staff training in Shanghai by sharing procedures that have worked well here, especially our approach to handling dissatisfied guests without making them feel blamed. A hotel’s reputation is not built only when everything goes smoothly; quite the contrary - it is often protected when something goes wrong and the staff respond with dignity. Third, because I already understand Park Hotel’s standards, reservation system and brand values, the company would not have to invest as much time in basic orientation as it would with an external recruit. What the Shanghai branch would gain, therefore, is a colleague who can carry proven practices across borders.","chinese":"更重要的是，我相信我的調職能以實際方式為機構帶來裨益。 首先，我可以成為香港與上海兩間分店之間的橋樑。 由於不少賓客會因金融業務、貿易展覽及家庭探訪而往返兩地，更完善地共享賓客資料、房間偏好及投訴紀錄，將能令他們的住宿體驗更具個人化。 其次，我可以透過分享在香港行之有效的程序，為上海的員工培訓作出貢獻，尤其是我們在處理不滿賓客時，如何避免令他們感到被責怪。 酒店的聲譽並不只是在一切順利時建立起來的；恰恰相反——它往往是在事情出錯，而員工仍能以尊重和得體的方式回應時得到維護。 第三，由於我已熟悉 Park Hotel 的服務標準、訂房系統及品牌價值，公司無須像聘請外部員工一樣，在基本入職培訓上投入同樣多的時間。 因此，上海分店所得到的，將是一位能把經實證有效的做法帶到不同市場的同事。"},{"label":"Paragraph 6","english":"I fully understand that any transfer must be arranged without weakening the Hong Kong team. If my application is approved, I would be glad to prepare a detailed handover plan, update the front-desk training notes and assist in coaching my replacement before departure. I would also remain available to answer follow-up questions from Hong Kong after settling in Shanghai, so that the transition can be as smooth as possible.","chinese":"我完全明白，任何調職安排都必須在不削弱香港團隊的前提下進行。 倘若我的申請獲批，本人十分樂意在離任前準備詳細的交接計劃、更新前台培訓筆記，並協助指導接替我的同事。 即使日後到上海安頓下來，我亦會繼續回應香港方面的後續問題，好讓整個過渡過程盡可能順暢。"},{"label":"Paragraph 7","english":"Thank you very much for considering my request. I would appreciate it if you could advise me on the next steps or grant me an opportunity to discuss the matter in person. I look forward to your guidance.","chinese":"非常感謝閣下考慮本人的請求。 若閣下能就下一步安排給予指示，或給予本人一次親身討論此事的機會，本人將不勝感激。 期待閣下的指導。"},{"label":"Paragraph 8","english":"Yours sincerely,","chinese":"謹啟"},{"label":"Paragraph 9","english":"Chris Wong","chinese":""}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"application for transfer","chinese":"調職申請"},{"english":"transfer to","chinese":"調職到……"},{"english":"Shanghai branch","chinese":"上海分店"},{"english":"Dear Mr Wong","chinese":"黃先生鈞鑒"},{"english":"I am writing to apply for","chinese":"本人寫信申請……"},{"english":"should a suitable position become available","chinese":"如有合適職位空缺"},{"english":"a suitable position","chinese":"合適職位"},{"english":"become available","chinese":"有空缺；可供申請"},{"english":"having served","chinese":"在……服務了"},{"english":"most recently as","chinese":"最近擔任"},{"english":"Senior Guest Relations Officer","chinese":"高級賓客服務主任"},{"english":"come to see","chinese":"逐漸明白"},{"english":"hospitality","chinese":"酒店款待服務"},{"english":"not simply as…, but more importantly as…","chinese":"不只是……更重要是……"},{"english":"earn trust","chinese":"贏得信任"},{"english":"at every point of","chinese":"在……的每一個環節"},{"english":"a guest's journey","chinese":"住客旅程"},{"english":"strengthen its presence in","chinese":"加強在……的地位"},{"english":"the Mainland market","chinese":"內地市場"},{"english":"Putonghua-speaking guests","chinese":"說普通話的住客"},{"english":"smoother operations","chinese":"更順暢的運作"},{"english":"stronger guest loyalty","chinese":"更高的住客忠誠度"},{"english":"closer cooperation","chinese":"更緊密的合作"},{"english":"between the two branches","chinese":"兩間分店之間"},{"english":"for these reasons","chinese":"基於以上原因"},{"english":"respectfully ask for","chinese":"恭敬地請求"},{"english":"your support in considering","chinese":"支持考慮……"},{"english":"in terms of","chinese":"就……而言"},{"english":"work experience","chinese":"工作經驗"},{"english":"be involved in","chinese":"參與"},{"english":"many areas of","chinese":"多個範疇的……"},{"english":"front-office operations","chinese":"前堂運作"},{"english":"from…to…","chinese":"由……到……"},{"english":"check-in procedures","chinese":"入住登記程序"},{"english":"room allocation","chinese":"房間分配"},{"english":"complaint handling","chinese":"投訴處理"},{"english":"post-stay follow-up","chinese":"退房後跟進"},{"english":"small details shape","chinese":"小細節塑造……"},{"english":"a guest's impression of","chinese":"住客對……的印象"},{"english":"during Golden Week","chinese":"在黃金周期間"},{"english":"business delegates","chinese":"商務代表團成員"},{"english":"earlier than scheduled","chinese":"比原定時間早"},{"english":"still being inspected","chinese":"仍在檢查中"},{"english":"instead of","chinese":"而不是"},{"english":"leave someone waiting","chinese":"讓某人等候"},{"english":"in the lobby","chinese":"在酒店大堂"},{"english":"coordinate with","chinese":"與……協調"},{"english":"Housekeeping","chinese":"房務部"},{"english":"temporary luggage storage","chinese":"臨時行李寄存"},{"english":"prepare refreshments","chinese":"準備茶點"},{"english":"in the lounge","chinese":"在休息室"},{"english":"the revised schedule","chinese":"修改後的時間表"},{"english":"by the time","chinese":"到……的時候"},{"english":"what could have become","chinese":"原本可能變成……的事"},{"english":"a serious complaint","chinese":"嚴重投訴"},{"english":"turn into","chinese":"變成"},{"english":"written compliments","chinese":"書面讚揚"},{"english":"not to mention","chinese":"更不用說"},{"english":"a calmer decision-maker","chinese":"更沉着的決策者"},{"english":"under pressure","chinese":"在壓力下"},{"english":"train junior colleagues on","chinese":"培訓初級同事使用……"},{"english":"junior colleagues","chinese":"初級同事"},{"english":"service recovery scripts","chinese":"服務補救話術"},{"english":"guest-preference log","chinese":"住客偏好記錄"},{"english":"thereby helping","chinese":"從而幫助"},{"english":"respond more consistently","chinese":"更一致地回應"},{"english":"when difficulties arise","chinese":"當困難出現時"},{"english":"my wish to transfer","chinese":"我的調職意願"},{"english":"be based on","chinese":"基於"},{"english":"impatience with","chinese":"對……感到不耐煩"},{"english":"current post","chinese":"現任職位"},{"english":"rather","chinese":"而是"},{"english":"a sincere desire to","chinese":"真誠希望"},{"english":"grow with the company","chinese":"與公司一同成長"},{"english":"one of the most competitive","chinese":"最具競爭力的……之一"},{"english":"hospitality markets","chinese":"酒店業市場"},{"english":"in the region","chinese":"在區內"},{"english":"domestic tourists","chinese":"內地遊客"},{"english":"expatriates","chinese":"外籍居民"},{"english":"conference organisers","chinese":"會議籌辦者"},{"english":"luxury travellers","chinese":"高端旅客"},{"english":"from around the world","chinese":"來自世界各地"},{"english":"allow me to understand","chinese":"讓我了解"},{"english":"what counts as","chinese":"怎樣才算是"},{"english":"excellent service","chinese":"優質服務"},{"english":"cultural and commercial setting","chinese":"文化和商業環境"},{"english":"teach someone speed and flexibility","chinese":"教會某人速度與靈活性"},{"english":"international etiquette","chinese":"國際禮儀"},{"english":"broaden my understanding of","chinese":"擴闊我對……的理解"},{"english":"Mainland consumer expectations","chinese":"內地消費者期望"},{"english":"digital payment habits","chinese":"電子支付習慣"},{"english":"corporate travel needs","chinese":"商務旅遊需要"},{"english":"only by working in","chinese":"只有在……工作才可以"},{"english":"develop the wider judgement required of","chinese":"培養……所需的更全面判斷力"},{"english":"a future manager","chinese":"未來管理人員"},{"english":"in other words","chinese":"換言之"},{"english":"turn existing experience into","chinese":"把現有經驗轉化為……"},{"english":"cross-market expertise","chinese":"跨市場專業知識"},{"english":"benefit the organisation","chinese":"對機構有利"},{"english":"in practical ways","chinese":"以實際方式"},{"english":"serve as a bridge between","chinese":"作為……之間的橋樑"},{"english":"travel between the two cities","chinese":"往返兩地"},{"english":"finance","chinese":"金融業務"},{"english":"trade fairs","chinese":"貿易展覽"},{"english":"family visits","chinese":"探親"},{"english":"sharing of guest profiles","chinese":"住客資料共享"},{"english":"room preferences","chinese":"房間偏好"},{"english":"complaint records","chinese":"投訴記錄"},{"english":"make their stays feel more personal","chinese":"令住宿體驗更個人化"},{"english":"contribute to","chinese":"為……作出貢獻"},{"english":"staff training","chinese":"職員培訓"},{"english":"procedures that have worked well","chinese":"行之有效的程序"},{"english":"approach to handling","chinese":"處理……的方法"},{"english":"dissatisfied guests","chinese":"不滿的住客"},{"english":"without making someone feel blamed","chinese":"不令某人覺得被責怪"},{"english":"reputation","chinese":"聲譽"},{"english":"not built only when","chinese":"不只是在……時建立"},{"english":"go smoothly","chinese":"順利進行"},{"english":"quite the contrary","chinese":"正好相反"},{"english":"when something goes wrong","chinese":"當事情出錯時"},{"english":"respond with dignity","chinese":"有尊嚴地回應"},{"english":"brand values","chinese":"品牌價值"},{"english":"reservation system","chinese":"預訂系統"},{"english":"invest time in","chinese":"投入時間於……"},{"english":"basic orientation","chinese":"基本入職指導"},{"english":"external recruit","chinese":"外部招聘人員"},{"english":"what the Shanghai branch would gain","chinese":"上海分店將會得到的是"},{"english":"carry proven practices across borders","chinese":"跨地區帶來已驗證的做法"},{"english":"fully understand that","chinese":"充分明白"},{"english":"be arranged without weakening","chinese":"在不削弱……的情況下安排"},{"english":"if my application is approved","chinese":"如果我的申請獲批"},{"english":"be glad to","chinese":"很樂意"},{"english":"a detailed handover plan","chinese":"詳細交接計劃"},{"english":"update the front-desk training notes","chinese":"更新前台培訓筆記"},{"english":"front-desk training notes","chinese":"前台培訓筆記"},{"english":"assist in coaching","chinese":"協助指導"},{"english":"my replacement","chinese":"接替我的同事"},{"english":"before departure","chinese":"離任前；出發前"},{"english":"remain available to","chinese":"繼續可以"},{"english":"follow-up questions","chinese":"跟進問題"},{"english":"after settling in","chinese":"安頓下來後"},{"english":"the transition","chinese":"過渡"},{"english":"as smooth as possible","chinese":"盡量順利"},{"english":"thank you very much for considering","chinese":"非常感謝你考慮……"},{"english":"I would appreciate it if","chinese":"如你能……我將不勝感激"},{"english":"advise me on","chinese":"就……給予指示"},{"english":"the next steps","chinese":"下一步"},{"english":"grant me an opportunity to","chinese":"給予我機會去"},{"english":"discuss the matter in person","chinese":"親身商討此事"},{"english":"look forward to your guidance","chinese":"期待你的指導"},{"english":"Yours sincerely","chinese":"謹啟"}]},"dse-writing-2020-part-b-q5":{"exerciseId":"dse-writing-2020-part-b-q5","essayKey":"","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=dse-writing-2020-part-b-q5","flashDeckId":"dse/writing/part-b/2020/Q5","paragraphs":[{"label":"Paragraph 1","english":"Making Room at the Games: A Proposal to Include Dragon Boat Racing","chinese":"為奧運騰出空間：納入龍舟競渡的建議"},{"label":"Paragraph 2","english":"Dear President,","chinese":"尊敬的主席："},{"label":"Paragraph 3","english":"I am writing in response to the IOC’s invitation to suggest sports for future Olympic Games. For better or worse, the Olympic programme can no longer be judged only by tradition; it must also simultaneously speak to young spectators, model equality and attract attention in a crowded media landscape. This has made the IOC consider events that can refresh the Games without weakening their dignity. I strongly believe that Dragon Boat Racing should be included, for it is youthful in spirit, naturally inclusive and made for powerful broadcasting.","chinese":"我寫信是為了回應國際奧委會邀請公眾為未來奧運會建議新增運動項目一事 無論好壞，奧運項目如今已不能只以傳統作為評判標準；它同時也必須能吸引年輕觀眾、樹立平等典範，並在競爭激烈的媒體環境中引起關注。 這使國際奧委會開始考慮一些既能為奧運注入新活力、又不會削弱其莊嚴性的項目。 我堅信龍舟競渡應被納入奧運，因為它在精神上充滿青春活力，本質上具備包容性，而且非常適合有感染力的轉播。"},{"label":"Paragraph 4","english":"First, Dragon Boat Racing would appeal to young people because it turns sport into shared energy. Many teenagers are drawn to activities that are fast, social and visually exciting, and dragon boat racing offers all three. A race is short enough to hold attention, physical enough to command respect, and simple enough to understand instantly: the boat surges forward, paddlers strike the water together, the drummer drives the rhythm, and the finish may be decided by inches. Unlike sports whose rules take years to appreciate, dragon boat can be enjoyed the moment one sees it. More importantly, it gives young athletes a rare lesson in teamwork. A school crew in Hong Kong or a university team overseas can train beginners quickly, yet no one can win on enthusiasm alone. Timing matters more than ego; discipline matters more than display. In that sense, dragon boat would not just entertain the young. It would show them what collective excellence looks like.","chinese":"首先，龍舟競渡能吸引年輕人，因為它把運動轉化成一種共同燃燒的能量。 許多青少年都會被節奏快速、具社交性而且視覺上令人興奮的活動吸引，而龍舟競渡正正同時具備這三種特質。 一場比賽短得足以抓住觀眾注意力，體能要求高得足以令人敬佩，也簡單得足以讓人一看便明白：龍舟向前衝刺，槳手齊心擊水，鼓手帶動節奏，而勝負可能只由數吋之差決定。 有些運動的規則需要多年才能真正欣賞；相比之下，龍舟競渡在觀眾看見的一刻便能被享受。 更重要的是，它給予年輕運動員一堂難得的團隊合作課。 香港的校隊或海外的大學隊伍都可以很快訓練初學者，但沒有人能單靠熱情取勝。 節奏配合比個人自我更重要；紀律比表面表現更重要。 從這個意義上說，龍舟競渡不只是娛樂年輕人。 它會向他們展示集體卓越真正是甚麼模樣。"},{"label":"Paragraph 5","english":"Second, Dragon Boat Racing is exceptionally well suited to promoting gender equality. Some sports have had to redesign formats to include women more fully; dragon boat, by contrast, already lends itself to mixed participation. Men and women can paddle side by side, share the same rhythm and contribute to the same result. This is not symbolic equality, where athletes are separated and merely given similar labels. Rather; It is practical equality, where everyone in the boat matters. The paddlers, drummer and steersperson may have different roles, but no role is ornamental. Granted, critics may argue that differences in physical strength could make mixed racing unfair. However, standardised crew requirements could address this concern clearly. Provided that every team included a fixed number of male and female athletes, fairness would be protected while cooperation would be celebrated. Few sports, if any, show so naturally that equality is not about making everyone identical, but about allowing different athletes to pull towards the same finish line.","chinese":"第二，龍舟競渡非常適合促進性別平等。 有些運動不得不重新設計比賽形式，才能更全面地納入女性；相比之下，龍舟競渡本身已經很適合男女混合參與。 男性和女性可以並肩划槳，共享同一節奏，並為同一結果作出貢獻。 這不是象徵式平等，也不是把運動員分隔開來後只是給予相似標籤。 更準確地說；這是實際的平等，因為船上的每一個人都重要。 槳手、鼓手和舵手也許擔當不同角色，但沒有任何一個角色只是裝飾性的。 誠然，批評者可能會指出，體能差異可能令混合賽事變得不公平。 然而，標準化的隊伍人數及性別要求可以清楚處理這項憂慮。 只要每支隊伍都包含固定數目的男性和女性運動員，公平便能得到保障，而合作精神也能受到推崇。 即使有其他運動能做到，也極少有運動能如此自然地展現：平等並不是要令每個人完全相同，而是讓不同的運動員共同朝同一條終點線奮力前進。"},{"label":"Paragraph 6","english":"Third, Dragon Boat Racing would attract media coverage because it is spectacular, culturally distinctive and easy to broadcast. Television and online audiences respond to movement, colour, sound and suspense; dragon boat racing supplies them all. The boats are striking, the drumbeat is memorable, and the image of a crew moving as one is powerful even without commentary. Better still, the sport carries cultural depth. It is rooted in Chinese tradition, yet it has travelled far beyond one community through festivals, charity races and school competitions around the world. In media terms, this gives journalists two stories at once: a thrilling race and a living heritage. Some may worry that the Olympic schedule is already crowded. That concern is understandable, but it should not rule out a sport that meets the IOC’s criteria so directly. Compact sprint events could be held over a limited number of days, using waterfront facilities where possible. The question is not whether every sport deserves a place, but whether this sport brings something distinctive, and Dragon Boat Racing does.","chinese":"第三，龍舟競渡能吸引媒體報道，因為它場面壯觀、文化特色鮮明，而且容易轉播。 電視和網上觀眾會對動感、色彩、聲音和懸念產生反應；而龍舟競渡全都具備 龍舟本身非常搶眼，鼓聲令人難忘，而一整支隊伍如同一體般前進的畫面，即使沒有旁述也充滿力量。 更理想的是，這項運動承載着深厚的文化底蘊。 它植根於中國傳統，卻已經透過世界各地的節慶活動、慈善賽事和校際比賽，遠遠超越了單一社群。 從媒體角度來看，這讓記者同時擁有兩個故事：一場扣人心弦的比賽，以及一項仍然活着的文化傳承。 有些人可能會擔心，奧運賽程已經十分擁擠。 這種憂慮可以理解，但它不應排除一項如此直接符合國際奧委會標準的運動 緊湊的短途衝刺賽可以在有限日數內舉行，並在可行情況下使用海濱設施。 問題並不在於每項運動是否都值得一席之地，而在於這項運動是否帶來獨特價值，而龍舟競渡確實如此。"},{"label":"Paragraph 7","english":"All things considered, I respectfully urge the IOC to give Dragon Boat Racing serious consideration. It would make room at the Olympic table for a sport that appeals to youth, advances gender equality and offers the media a vivid global story. The Olympics are at their best when they honour tradition while welcoming new forms of human excellence. I would be grateful if the Committee could explore a demonstration event, consult international dragon boat bodies and consider a mixed-team sprint format as a first step.","chinese":"綜合以上各點，我謹此誠懇促請國際奧委會認真考慮龍舟競渡。 它將為一項能吸引青年、推動性別平等，並為媒體提供鮮明全球故事的運動，在奧運舞台上騰出一席之地。 奧運最出色之處，正在於它能一邊尊重傳統，一邊歡迎人類卓越表現的新形式 若委員會能探索舉辦示範項目、諮詢國際龍舟組織，並考慮以混合隊伍短途賽作為第一步，我將不勝感激。"},{"label":"Paragraph 8","english":"Yours faithfully,","chinese":"此致"},{"label":"Paragraph 9","english":"Chris Wong","chinese":"Chris Wong"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"making room at","chinese":"為……騰出位置"},{"english":"a proposal to include","chinese":"建議納入……"},{"english":"Dragon Boat Racing","chinese":"龍舟競賽"},{"english":"Dear President","chinese":"尊敬的主席"},{"english":"in response to","chinese":"回應……"},{"english":"the IOC's invitation","chinese":"國際奧委會的邀請"},{"english":"suggest sports for","chinese":"為……建議運動項目"},{"english":"future Olympic Games","chinese":"未來的奧運會"},{"english":"for better or worse","chinese":"不論好壞；無論如何"},{"english":"the Olympic programme","chinese":"奧運項目安排"},{"english":"can no longer be judged only by","chinese":"不能再只以……判斷"},{"english":"tradition","chinese":"傳統"},{"english":"simultaneously","chinese":"同時"},{"english":"speak to young spectators","chinese":"打動年輕觀眾"},{"english":"model equality","chinese":"示範平等"},{"english":"attract attention","chinese":"吸引注意"},{"english":"a crowded media landscape","chinese":"擁擠的媒體環境"},{"english":"make someone consider","chinese":"令某人考慮"},{"english":"refresh the Games","chinese":"為奧運注入新氣象"},{"english":"without weakening","chinese":"而不削弱"},{"english":"dignity","chinese":"莊嚴性；尊嚴"},{"english":"strongly believe that","chinese":"堅信"},{"english":"should be included","chinese":"應該被納入"},{"english":"youthful in spirit","chinese":"精神上充滿青春活力"},{"english":"naturally inclusive","chinese":"自然具包容性"},{"english":"made for powerful broadcasting","chinese":"適合製作具震撼力的轉播"},{"english":"appeal to young people","chinese":"吸引年輕人"},{"english":"turn sport into shared energy","chinese":"把運動變成共同的力量"},{"english":"be drawn to","chinese":"被……吸引"},{"english":"fast, social and visually exciting","chinese":"快速、具社交性和視覺刺激"},{"english":"offer all three","chinese":"三者兼備"},{"english":"short enough to","chinese":"短到足以……"},{"english":"hold attention","chinese":"吸引注意力"},{"english":"physical enough to","chinese":"體能要求足以……"},{"english":"command respect","chinese":"令人尊重"},{"english":"simple enough to understand instantly","chinese":"簡單到即時明白"},{"english":"surge forward","chinese":"向前衝"},{"english":"strike the water together","chinese":"一起划水"},{"english":"drive the rhythm","chinese":"帶動節奏"},{"english":"be decided by inches","chinese":"以些微距離分勝負"},{"english":"unlike sports whose rules","chinese":"不像那些規則……的運動"},{"english":"take years to appreciate","chinese":"需要多年才懂得欣賞"},{"english":"the moment one sees it","chinese":"一看見就"},{"english":"more importantly","chinese":"更重要的是"},{"english":"give young athletes a rare lesson in","chinese":"給年輕運動員上了難得的一課"},{"english":"teamwork","chinese":"團隊合作"},{"english":"a school crew","chinese":"學校隊伍"},{"english":"a university team overseas","chinese":"海外大學隊伍"},{"english":"train beginners quickly","chinese":"快速訓練初學者"},{"english":"on enthusiasm alone","chinese":"單靠熱情"},{"english":"timing matters more than ego","chinese":"配合時機比自我更重要"},{"english":"discipline matters more than display","chinese":"紀律比表現自己更重要"},{"english":"in that sense","chinese":"從這個意義上說"},{"english":"not just entertain","chinese":"不只是娛樂"},{"english":"collective excellence","chinese":"集體卓越"},{"english":"what something looks like","chinese":"……是甚麼模樣"},{"english":"exceptionally well suited to","chinese":"極為適合"},{"english":"promote gender equality","chinese":"推動性別平等"},{"english":"redesign formats","chinese":"重新設計賽制"},{"english":"include women more fully","chinese":"更全面地納入女性"},{"english":"by contrast","chinese":"相比之下"},{"english":"lend itself to","chinese":"適合用於……"},{"english":"mixed participation","chinese":"男女混合參與"},{"english":"side by side","chinese":"並肩"},{"english":"share the same rhythm","chinese":"共享同一節奏"},{"english":"contribute to the same result","chinese":"為同一結果作出貢獻"},{"english":"symbolic equality","chinese":"象徵式平等"},{"english":"be separated","chinese":"被分開"},{"english":"merely given similar labels","chinese":"只是被給予相似標籤"},{"english":"practical equality","chinese":"實際平等"},{"english":"everyone in the boat matters","chinese":"船上每個人都重要"},{"english":"paddlers, drummer and steersperson","chinese":"划手、鼓手和舵手"},{"english":"have different roles","chinese":"擔任不同角色"},{"english":"no role is ornamental","chinese":"沒有角色只是裝飾"},{"english":"granted","chinese":"誠然"},{"english":"physical strength","chinese":"體力"},{"english":"mixed racing","chinese":"男女混合賽"},{"english":"standardised crew requirements","chinese":"標準化隊伍要求"},{"english":"address this concern","chinese":"處理這個憂慮"},{"english":"provided that","chinese":"只要"},{"english":"a fixed number of","chinese":"固定數目的……"},{"english":"male and female athletes","chinese":"男、女運動員"},{"english":"fairness would be protected","chinese":"公平會得到保障"},{"english":"cooperation would be celebrated","chinese":"合作會受到肯定"},{"english":"few sports, if any","chinese":"即使有，也很少"},{"english":"making everyone identical","chinese":"令每個人變得一模一樣"},{"english":"allowing different athletes to","chinese":"讓不同運動員去……"},{"english":"pull towards the same finish line","chinese":"朝同一終點努力"},{"english":"attract media coverage","chinese":"吸引傳媒報道"},{"english":"spectacular","chinese":"壯觀的"},{"english":"culturally distinctive","chinese":"具文化特色"},{"english":"easy to broadcast","chinese":"易於轉播"},{"english":"television and online audiences","chinese":"電視及網上觀眾"},{"english":"respond to","chinese":"對……有反應；受……吸引"},{"english":"movement, colour, sound and suspense","chinese":"動感、色彩、聲音和懸念"},{"english":"supply them all","chinese":"全部具備"},{"english":"striking","chinese":"醒目；引人注目"},{"english":"drumbeat","chinese":"鼓聲節奏"},{"english":"memorable","chinese":"令人難忘"},{"english":"a crew moving as one","chinese":"一隊人動作一致"},{"english":"even without commentary","chinese":"即使沒有旁述"},{"english":"better still","chinese":"更理想的是"},{"english":"cultural depth","chinese":"文化深度"},{"english":"be rooted in","chinese":"植根於"},{"english":"Chinese tradition","chinese":"中華傳統"},{"english":"travel far beyond","chinese":"遠遠傳播至……之外"},{"english":"one community","chinese":"單一社群"},{"english":"charity races","chinese":"慈善賽事"},{"english":"school competitions","chinese":"學校比賽"},{"english":"around the world","chinese":"世界各地"},{"english":"in media terms","chinese":"從媒體角度而言"},{"english":"journalists","chinese":"記者"},{"english":"two stories at once","chinese":"同時提供兩個故事"},{"english":"a thrilling race","chinese":"刺激的比賽"},{"english":"a living heritage","chinese":"活的文化傳承"},{"english":"the Olympic schedule","chinese":"奧運賽程"},{"english":"already crowded","chinese":"已經很擁擠"},{"english":"that concern is understandable","chinese":"這個憂慮可以理解"},{"english":"rule out","chinese":"排除"},{"english":"meet the IOC's criteria","chinese":"符合國際奧委會的準則"},{"english":"compact sprint events","chinese":"緊湊的短途競賽項目"},{"english":"be held over","chinese":"在……期間舉行"},{"english":"a limited number of days","chinese":"有限數目的日子"},{"english":"waterfront facilities","chinese":"海濱設施"},{"english":"where possible","chinese":"在可行情況下"},{"english":"the question is not whether…but whether…","chinese":"問題不在於是否……而在於是否……"},{"english":"deserve a place","chinese":"值得佔一席位"},{"english":"bring something distinctive","chinese":"帶來獨特之處"},{"english":"all things considered","chinese":"綜合考慮各方面"},{"english":"respectfully urge","chinese":"恭敬地敦促"},{"english":"give serious consideration","chinese":"認真考慮"},{"english":"make room at the Olympic table","chinese":"在奧運舞台上騰出位置"},{"english":"appeal to youth","chinese":"吸引年輕人"},{"english":"advance gender equality","chinese":"推動性別平等"},{"english":"offer the media","chinese":"為傳媒提供"},{"english":"a vivid global story","chinese":"生動的全球故事"},{"english":"at their best","chinese":"處於最佳狀態"},{"english":"honour tradition","chinese":"尊重傳統"},{"english":"welcome new forms of","chinese":"歡迎新的……形式"},{"english":"human excellence","chinese":"人類卓越表現"},{"english":"I would be grateful if","chinese":"如蒙……我將十分感激"},{"english":"the Committee","chinese":"委員會"},{"english":"explore a demonstration event","chinese":"探討示範項目"},{"english":"consult international dragon boat bodies","chinese":"諮詢國際龍舟組織"},{"english":"international dragon boat bodies","chinese":"國際龍舟組織"},{"english":"consider a mixed-team sprint format","chinese":"考慮男女混合短途賽制"},{"english":"as a first step","chinese":"作為第一步"}]},"dse-writing-2020-part-b-q6":{"exerciseId":"dse-writing-2020-part-b-q6","essayKey":"","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=dse-writing-2020-part-b-q6","flashDeckId":"dse/writing/part-b/2020/Q6","paragraphs":[{"label":"Paragraph 1","english":"Warning Labels: A Small Sign with a Large Public Purpose","chinese":"警告標籤：一個小標示，一個重大的公共目的"},{"label":"Paragraph 2","english":"As supermarket shelves become crowded with snacks, instant meals and sweetened drinks, unhealthy eating is no longer simply a matter of weak will. It is also a matter of information, habit and marketing. In response, public health authorities in some countries now require warning labels on products high in sugar, saturated fat and salt, so that consumers can recognise nutritional risks before the packet reaches the checkout. I strongly believe that such labels are effective in changing people’s eating habits, not because they can magically turn everyone into a nutritionist, but because they interrupt careless choices, reshape the food environment and give families a simple language for healthier decisions.","chinese":"隨著超級市場的貨架上擺滿零食、即食食品和含糖飲品，不健康飲食已不再單純是意志薄弱的問題。 它同時也是資訊、習慣和市場推廣的問題。 為了作出回應，一些國家的公共衛生機構如今要求糖分、飽和脂肪和鹽分含量高的產品貼上警告標籤，好讓消費者在商品到達收銀處之前，便能識別其中的營養風險。 我堅信這類標籤能有效改變人們的飲食習慣，並不是因為它們能神奇地把每個人都變成營養師，而是因為它們能打斷粗心大意的選擇、重塑食物環境，並給予家庭一種簡單的語言去作出更健康的決定。"},{"label":"Paragraph 3","english":"First, warning labels are effective because they turn nutrition from a hidden technical issue into an immediate everyday choice. Most consumers do not buy after calmly calculating grams of sugar, percentages of fat or daily sodium limits. More often than not, they shop quickly, respond to taste, and trust attractive packaging. A chocolate cereal can look cheerful, an energy drink can look sporty, and a packet of crisps can look harmless; all the while, the health cost remains buried in a small nutrition table. A clear warning label changes that moment. It does not merely provide data; it creates a pause. A student reaching for a bottled tea may notice a “high sugar” warning and choose water instead. A parent comparing two brands of noodles may pick the one without a “high salt” label. These choices may appear small, but habits are built through repetition. The more often consumers are reminded, the more likely they are to associate certain products with risk. In this sense, warning labels work nudging them where decisions are made.","chinese":"首先，警告標籤之所以有效，是因為它們把營養從一個隱藏的技術性問題，轉化為一個即時的日常選擇。 大多數消費者並不是在冷靜計算糖的克數、脂肪比例或每日鈉攝取上限之後才購物。 很多時候，他們購物時速度很快，受味道吸引，並相信具吸引力的包裝。 一款朱古力早餐穀物可以看起來令人愉快，一款能量飲品可以看起來充滿運動感，而一包薯片也可以看起來毫無害處；然而在這整個過程中，健康代價卻仍然被埋藏在一個細小的營養標籤之中。 一個清晰的警告標籤會改變那一刻。 它不只是提供數據；它製造了一次停頓。 一名正伸手拿瓶裝茶的學生，可能會注意到「高糖」警告，並轉而選擇清水 一位正在比較兩個麵食品牌的家長，可能會選擇沒有「高鹽」標籤的那一款 這些選擇看似微小，但習慣正是透過重複建立起來的。 消費者被提醒得越頻繁，就越有可能把某些產品與風險聯繫起來。 從這個意義上說，警告標籤是在消費者作出決定的地方發揮推動作用。"},{"label":"Paragraph 4","english":"Second, warning labels can change eating habits indirectly by putting pressure on food manufacturers and social groups. In the eyes of the public, a product carrying several warnings is no longer just “tasty”; it is also visibly unhealthy. A company whose biscuits, drinks or ready-made meals are covered with warnings risks losing the image of being family-friendly. It therefore follows that manufacturers have a practical reason to reduce sugar, saturated fat and salt, thereby making healthier options more common. This matters because personal choice is shaped by what is available. If fewer products are excessively sweet or salty, consumers do not have to depend on discipline alone. The same principle applies to schools, offices and families. When a class chooses snacks for a picnic, warning labels make it easier to compare options without embarrassing anyone. When grandparents buy food for children, the label gives them a simple sign to follow even if they do not understand complex nutrition terms. Thus, labels can gradually change what counts as normal food.","chinese":"第二，警告標籤可以透過向食品製造商和社會群體施加壓力，間接改變飲食習慣。 在公眾眼中，一件帶有多個警告的產品不再只是「美味」；它同時也是明顯不健康的。 如果一間公司的餅乾、飲品或即食餐點都佈滿警告標籤，它便有可能失去親家庭品牌的形象。 因此，食品製造商自然有實際理由去減少糖分、飽和脂肪和鹽分，從而令較健康的選擇變得更加普遍。 這一點十分重要，因為個人選擇會受到可得選項的塑造。 如果過甜或過鹹的產品減少，消費者便不必單靠自律。 同樣的原則也適用於學校、辦公室和家庭。 當一個班級為野餐選擇零食時，警告標籤能讓大家更容易比較選項，而不會令任何人尷尬。 當祖父母為孩子購買食物時，即使他們不明白複雜的營養術語，標籤也能給他們一個簡單的標示去遵循。 因此，標籤能逐漸改變人們對「正常食物」的理解。"},{"label":"Paragraph 5","english":"Granted, critics may argue that warning labels are too simple to overcome strong cravings, low prices and long-established eating habits. There is no denying that a person who loves sugary drinks may ignore the label, just as some people ignore exercise advice. However, to say that labels are imperfect is not to say that they are ineffective. The real question is not whether labels can solve unhealthy eating by themselves, but whether they can make healthier choices more likely. On that test, they clearly have value. Even if only some consumers switch from a heavily labelled snack to a less harmful one, the effect is meaningful because food decisions are made every day. Besides, labels are not meant to replace nutrition education, affordable fresh food or responsible advertising rules. Rather, they work best alongside these measures. Only when consumers are warned clearly and given realistic alternatives can healthy eating become practical rather than idealistic.","chinese":"誠然，批評者可能會指出，警告標籤過於簡單，難以克服強烈的食慾、低廉的價格和長久形成的飲食習慣。 無可否認，一個喜愛含糖飲品的人可能會忽視標籤，正如有些人會忽視運動建議一樣。 然而，說標籤並不完美，並不等於說它們沒有效用。 真正的問題並不是標籤能否單獨解決不健康飲食，而是它們能否令較健康的選擇更有可能出現。 以這個標準來衡量，它們顯然具有價值。 即使只有部分消費者從一款貼滿警告標籤的零食，轉向一款危害較低的零食，這種效果仍然有意義，因為人們每天都在作出食物選擇。 此外，標籤並不是為了取代營養教育、價格可負擔的新鮮食物，或負責任的廣告規管。 更準確地說，它們與這些措施配合時最能發揮作用。 只有當消費者獲得清晰警示，並得到現實可行的替代選擇時，健康飲食才會變得實際，而不是只停留在理想層面。"},{"label":"Paragraph 6","english":"Overall, food warning labels are an effective way to change people’s eating habits. They make hidden risks visible, influence manufacturers, and help families make quicker, wiser choices. Governments should therefore keep labels simple, prominent and standardised; schools should teach students how to interpret them; and manufacturers should reformulate products instead of merely defending unhealthy recipes. Eating well will not happen overnight, but prevention is better than cure. If society wants healthier citizens, the warning should appear before the illness, not after it.","chinese":"總括而言，食物警告標籤是改變人們飲食習慣的一種有效方法。 它們使隱藏的風險變得可見，影響食品製造商，並幫助家庭作出更快捷、更明智的選擇。 因此，政府應該保持標籤簡單、醒目和標準化；學校應教導學生如何解讀標籤；而食品製造商也應重新調整產品配方，而不是僅僅為不健康的食譜辯護 健康飲食不會一夜之間實現，但預防勝於治療。 如果社會希望擁有更健康的市民，警告就應該在疾病出現之前出現，而不是在疾病出現之後才出現。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"warning labels","chinese":"警告標籤"},{"english":"a small sign with a large public purpose","chinese":"小標誌，大公共用途"},{"english":"supermarket shelves","chinese":"超級市場貨架"},{"english":"become crowded with","chinese":"充斥著"},{"english":"instant meals","chinese":"即食餐"},{"english":"sweetened drinks","chinese":"加糖飲品"},{"english":"unhealthy eating","chinese":"不健康飲食"},{"english":"no longer simply","chinese":"不再只是"},{"english":"a matter of","chinese":"關乎……的事"},{"english":"weak will","chinese":"意志薄弱"},{"english":"in response","chinese":"作為回應"},{"english":"public health authorities","chinese":"公共衞生當局"},{"english":"require warning labels on","chinese":"要求在……加上警告標籤"},{"english":"high in sugar","chinese":"糖分高"},{"english":"saturated fat","chinese":"飽和脂肪"},{"english":"high in salt","chinese":"鹽分高"},{"english":"consumers","chinese":"消費者"},{"english":"recognise nutritional risks","chinese":"識別營養風險"},{"english":"nutritional risks","chinese":"營養風險"},{"english":"before the packet reaches the checkout","chinese":"在付款前"},{"english":"checkout","chinese":"收銀處；結帳處"},{"english":"strongly believe that","chinese":"堅信"},{"english":"effective in changing","chinese":"有效改變"},{"english":"eating habits","chinese":"飲食習慣"},{"english":"not because…, but because…","chinese":"不是因為……，而是因為……"},{"english":"turn someone into","chinese":"將某人變成"},{"english":"nutritionist","chinese":"營養師"},{"english":"interrupt careless choices","chinese":"打斷不經意的選擇"},{"english":"reshape the food environment","chinese":"重塑食物環境"},{"english":"give families a simple language for","chinese":"為家庭提供……的簡單語言"},{"english":"healthier decisions","chinese":"較健康的決定"},{"english":"hidden technical issue","chinese":"隱藏的技術性問題"},{"english":"immediate everyday choice","chinese":"即時的日常選擇"},{"english":"buy after calmly calculating","chinese":"在冷靜計算後購買"},{"english":"grams of sugar","chinese":"糖的克數"},{"english":"percentages of fat","chinese":"脂肪百分比"},{"english":"daily sodium limits","chinese":"每日鈉攝取上限"},{"english":"more often than not","chinese":"往往；多數情況下"},{"english":"respond to taste","chinese":"受味道影響"},{"english":"attractive packaging","chinese":"吸引人的包裝"},{"english":"chocolate cereal","chinese":"朱古力早餐穀物"},{"english":"look cheerful","chinese":"看起來令人愉快"},{"english":"energy drink","chinese":"能量飲品"},{"english":"look sporty","chinese":"看起來有運動感"},{"english":"packet of crisps","chinese":"一包薯片"},{"english":"look harmless","chinese":"看起來無害"},{"english":"all the while","chinese":"與此同時"},{"english":"health cost","chinese":"健康代價"},{"english":"remain buried in","chinese":"仍然隱藏在"},{"english":"nutrition table","chinese":"營養資料表"},{"english":"clear warning label","chinese":"清晰的警告標籤"},{"english":"create a pause","chinese":"令人停一停想一想"},{"english":"reach for","chinese":"伸手拿"},{"english":"bottled tea","chinese":"樽裝茶"},{"english":"high-sugar warning","chinese":"高糖警告"},{"english":"choose water instead","chinese":"改為選擇水"},{"english":"compare two brands of","chinese":"比較兩個品牌的……"},{"english":"pick the one without","chinese":"選擇沒有……的那一款"},{"english":"high-salt label","chinese":"高鹽標籤"},{"english":"appear small","chinese":"看似微小"},{"english":"built through repetition","chinese":"透過重複建立"},{"english":"the more often…, the more likely…","chinese":"越經常……，就越有可能……"},{"english":"be reminded","chinese":"被提醒"},{"english":"associate certain products with risk","chinese":"將某些產品與風險聯繫起來"},{"english":"in this sense","chinese":"從這個意義上說"},{"english":"work by nudging","chinese":"透過輕推發揮作用"},{"english":"nudge consumers","chinese":"輕推消費者"},{"english":"where decisions are made","chinese":"在作出決定的地方"},{"english":"indirectly","chinese":"間接地"},{"english":"put pressure on","chinese":"向……施壓"},{"english":"food manufacturers","chinese":"食品製造商"},{"english":"social groups","chinese":"社群；社會群體"},{"english":"in the eyes of the public","chinese":"在公眾眼中"},{"english":"carrying several warnings","chinese":"帶有多個警告"},{"english":"no longer just","chinese":"不再只是"},{"english":"visibly unhealthy","chinese":"明顯不健康"},{"english":"ready-made meals","chinese":"現成餐食"},{"english":"covered with warnings","chinese":"滿是警告"},{"english":"risk losing","chinese":"冒著失去……的風險"},{"english":"family-friendly","chinese":"適合家庭的"},{"english":"it therefore follows that","chinese":"因此可以推論"},{"english":"practical reason to","chinese":"實際理由去"},{"english":"reduce sugar","chinese":"減糖"},{"english":"thereby","chinese":"從而"},{"english":"healthier options","chinese":"較健康的選擇"},{"english":"more common","chinese":"更常見"},{"english":"personal choice","chinese":"個人選擇"},{"english":"be shaped by","chinese":"受……塑造"},{"english":"what is available","chinese":"可選擇的東西"},{"english":"excessively sweet or salty","chinese":"過甜或過鹹"},{"english":"depend on discipline alone","chinese":"單靠自律"},{"english":"the same principle applies to","chinese":"同一道理適用於"},{"english":"choose snacks for a picnic","chinese":"為野餐選擇零食"},{"english":"compare options","chinese":"比較選項"},{"english":"without embarrassing anyone","chinese":"不令任何人尷尬"},{"english":"grandparents","chinese":"祖父母；外祖父母"},{"english":"a simple sign to follow","chinese":"可跟隨的簡單標誌"},{"english":"complex nutrition terms","chinese":"複雜營養術語"},{"english":"gradually change","chinese":"逐漸改變"},{"english":"what counts as","chinese":"被視為"},{"english":"normal food","chinese":"正常食物"},{"english":"granted","chinese":"誠然"},{"english":"critics may argue that","chinese":"批評者可能會認為"},{"english":"too simple to overcome","chinese":"太簡單而不能克服"},{"english":"strong cravings","chinese":"強烈渴望"},{"english":"low prices","chinese":"低價"},{"english":"long-established eating habits","chinese":"長久形成的飲食習慣"},{"english":"there is no denying that","chinese":"無可否認"},{"english":"sugary drinks","chinese":"含糖飲品"},{"english":"ignore the label","chinese":"無視標籤"},{"english":"just as","chinese":"正如"},{"english":"exercise advice","chinese":"運動建議"},{"english":"to say that… is not to say that…","chinese":"說……並不等於說……"},{"english":"imperfect","chinese":"不完美的"},{"english":"ineffective","chinese":"無效的"},{"english":"the real question is not whether…, but whether…","chinese":"真正問題不是是否……，而是是否……"},{"english":"by themselves","chinese":"單靠它們自己"},{"english":"make healthier choices more likely","chinese":"令較健康選擇更有可能出現"},{"english":"on that test","chinese":"以這個標準來看"},{"english":"have value","chinese":"有價值"},{"english":"switch from… to…","chinese":"從……轉為……"},{"english":"heavily labelled snack","chinese":"帶有多個標籤的零食"},{"english":"less harmful","chinese":"危害較小的"},{"english":"meaningful","chinese":"有意義的"},{"english":"food decisions","chinese":"飲食決定"},{"english":"not meant to replace","chinese":"不是用來取代"},{"english":"nutrition education","chinese":"營養教育"},{"english":"affordable fresh food","chinese":"買得起的新鮮食物"},{"english":"responsible advertising rules","chinese":"負責任的廣告規則"},{"english":"work best alongside","chinese":"與……配合時最有效"},{"english":"these measures","chinese":"這些措施"},{"english":"warned clearly","chinese":"獲得清楚警告"},{"english":"realistic alternatives","chinese":"實際可行的替代選擇"},{"english":"practical rather than idealistic","chinese":"實際可行，而非空談理想"},{"english":"overall","chinese":"總括而言"},{"english":"effective way to","chinese":"有效方法去"},{"english":"hidden risks","chinese":"隱藏風險"},{"english":"make hidden risks visible","chinese":"令隱藏風險變得可見"},{"english":"influence manufacturers","chinese":"影響製造商"},{"english":"quicker, wiser choices","chinese":"更快捷、更明智的選擇"},{"english":"governments should therefore","chinese":"因此政府應該"},{"english":"simple, prominent and standardised","chinese":"簡單、顯眼和標準化"},{"english":"prominent","chinese":"顯眼的"},{"english":"standardised","chinese":"標準化的"},{"english":"interpret them","chinese":"解讀它們"},{"english":"reformulate products","chinese":"重新調整產品配方"},{"english":"instead of merely","chinese":"而不是只顧"},{"english":"defend unhealthy recipes","chinese":"為不健康配方辯護"},{"english":"will not happen overnight","chinese":"不會一夜之間發生"},{"english":"prevention is better than cure","chinese":"預防勝於治療"},{"english":"healthier citizens","chinese":"更健康的市民"},{"english":"the warning should appear before the illness","chinese":"警告應在疾病出現前出現"}]},"dse-writing-2020-part-b-q7":{"exerciseId":"dse-writing-2020-part-b-q7","essayKey":"","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=dse-writing-2020-part-b-q7","flashDeckId":"dse/writing/part-b/2020/Q7","paragraphs":[{"label":"Paragraph 1","english":"From MTR Platforms to Music Awards: Zoe Kwan’s Unlikely First Verse","chinese":"從港鐵月台到音樂頒獎禮：Zoe Kwan 意想不到的第一段主歌"},{"label":"Paragraph 2","english":"By Do-Re-Mi Magazine","chinese":"由《Do-Re-Mi》音樂雜誌撰寫"},{"label":"Paragraph 3","english":"No one saw Zoe Kwan coming. Not the commuters who once walked past her outside Prince Edward Station, not the classmates who knew her as “the quiet girl with the guitar”, and certainly not Zoe herself. Yet, last Saturday night, the 19-year-old singer-songwriter stood under the dazzling lights of the HKTV Music Awards, holding the trophy for Best New Artist with trembling hands and tearful eyes. “I thought I would cry if I lost,” she told Do-Re-Mi with a shy laugh. “It turns out I cried because I won.”","chinese":"沒有人預料到 Zoe Kwan 會突然出現。 不是那些曾經在太子站外從她身旁走過的乘客，不是那些只知道她是「那個拿着結他的安靜女孩」的同學，當然也不是 Zoe 自己。 然而，上星期六晚上，這位 19 歲的創作歌手站在 HKTV Music Awards 璀璨的燈光下，雙手顫抖、眼含淚水地捧着 Best New Artist 獎座。 她帶着害羞的笑容告訴《Do-Re-Mi》：「我原本以為如果輸了，我會哭。」 「結果我哭，是因為我贏了。」"},{"label":"Paragraph 4","english":"Zoe’s sudden rise to fame has been nothing short of remarkable. Up until last year, she was performing acoustic covers after school, uploading short clips to social media, and helping her mother at a small flower shop in Tai Kok Tsui. Her breakthrough came when a 45-second video of her original song, Last Train Home, was reposted by a popular music blogger. By the next morning, the clip had gathered hundreds of thousands of views; by the end of the week, record companies were calling. “One moment I was checking homework messages,” Zoe recalled. “The next, strangers were asking when my album would come out.”","chinese":"Zoe 突如其來的成名之路，絕對稱得上非凡。 直到去年，她還只是在放學後演唱 acoustic 翻唱歌曲，把短片上載到社交媒體，並在大角咀一間小花店幫媽媽的忙。 她的突破來自一段 45 秒的原創歌曲 Last Train Home 影片，該片被一位人氣音樂博客轉發。 到了第二天早上，那段影片已經累積了數十萬觀看次數；到了那個星期結束時，唱片公司已經開始致電給她。 Zoe 回憶道：「前一刻我還在查看功課訊息。」 「下一刻，陌生人已經在問我的專輯甚麼時候推出。」"},{"label":"Paragraph 5","english":"What makes Zoe’s story refreshing is not just the speed of her success, but the way she has remained grounded all the while. In person, she is soft-spoken, almost cautious, choosing her words the way she chooses her chords: slowly, carefully, and with feeling. She does not make herself out to be a genius discovered overnight. Instead, she insists that her music grew out of ordinary Hong Kong life. “People think songs come from dramatic heartbreak,” she said. “Mine usually come from bus rides, family dinners and things I was too shy to say.”","chinese":"Zoe 的故事令人耳目一新的地方，不只是她成功的速度，而是她在整個過程中始終保持腳踏實地。 親身見到她時，她說話溫柔，甚至帶點謹慎；她選擇字句的方式，就像她選擇和弦一樣：慢慢地、仔細地、帶着感情地。 她並沒有把自己塑造成一個一夜之間被發掘的天才。 相反，她堅持自己的音樂是從平凡的香港生活中長出來的。 她說：「人們以為歌曲都來自戲劇性的心碎經歷。」 「我的歌通常來自巴士車程、家庭晚餐，以及那些我太害羞而說不出口的事情。」"},{"label":"Paragraph 6","english":"Take Last Train Home, for example. The song was inspired by late-night journeys after tutorial classes, when Zoe noticed students, cleaners, nurses and office workers sharing the same tired silence. “Everyone looked exhausted, but everyone was still going somewhere,” she explained. That observation became a tender ballad about growing up in a city where ambition often comes at the cost of rest. Its chorus, gentle yet haunting, captures the loneliness of crowded places—an emotion many young listeners immediately recognised.","chinese":"以 Last Train Home 為例。 這首歌的靈感來自補習班後的深夜歸途，當時 Zoe 注意到學生、清潔工、護士和上班族都共同分享着同一種疲憊的沉默。 她解釋道：「每個人看起來都筋疲力盡，但每個人仍然在前往某個地方。」 這個觀察後來成為一首溫柔的抒情歌，描寫人在一座野心往往以休息為代價的城市中成長。 它的副歌溫柔卻縈繞心頭，捕捉了擁擠地方中的孤獨感——這是一種許多年輕聽眾立刻認出的情緒。"},{"label":"Paragraph 7","english":"Another fan favourite, Plastic Roses, came from her mother’s flower shop. Zoe noticed that customers often bought artificial flowers for hospital visits because they lasted longer. At first glance, the idea seemed practical; on closer inspection, it made her wonder whether people sometimes choose what lasts over what lives. The result is a song about love that looks perfect from the outside but has lost its warmth within. “It is not so much a sad song as a careful one,” Zoe said. “I wanted to ask whether beauty still matters if it cannot breathe.”","chinese":"另一首深受歌迷喜愛的作品 Plastic Roses，則來自她母親的花店。 Zoe 注意到，顧客探病時經常購買人造花，因為它們能保存得更久。 乍看之下，這個想法似乎很實際；但仔細一想，這令她開始思考，人們有時是否會選擇能持久的東西，而不是有生命的東西。 結果，這成為一首關於愛的歌曲：那份愛從外表看來完美，內裡卻已經失去了溫度。 Zoe 說：「它與其說是一首悲傷的歌，不如說是一首小心翼翼的歌。」 「我想問的是，如果美麗不能呼吸，它是否仍然重要。」"},{"label":"Paragraph 8","english":"Her newest single, Borrowed Light, reveals a more personal side. Written during a period when Zoe felt overwhelmed by sudden attention, the song describes a young artist learning to stand under a spotlight without being blinded by it. With success comes pressure, and Zoe admits that fame has not been entirely easy to handle. She has had to get used to interviews, rehearsals, public comments and the strange feeling of being recognised while buying egg waffles. “Sometimes I miss being invisible,” she confessed. “But then someone messages me and says a song helped them feel less alone. That makes everything worth it.”","chinese":"她最新的單曲 Borrowed Light，展現了更個人的一面。 這首歌寫於 Zoe 被突如其來的關注壓得喘不過氣的時期，描寫一位年輕藝術家學習如何站在聚光燈下，卻不被它刺盲。 伴隨成功而來的是壓力，而 Zoe 也承認，成名並不完全容易應付。 她必須習慣訪問、綵排、公眾評論，以及在買雞蛋仔時被人認出的那種奇怪感覺。 她坦言：「有時候，我會懷念自己隱形的日子。」 「但後來有人傳訊息給我，說一首歌幫助他們覺得自己不那麼孤單。這就令一切都值得了。」"},{"label":"Paragraph 9","english":"Zoe’s appeal lies in this balance between innocence and emotional intelligence. She writes about small things, yet somehow makes them feel large. She sings softly, yet her words linger. She does not just entertain her audience; she gives them room to understand themselves. Perhaps that is why her rise, though sudden, does not feel accidental. Great oaks grow from little acorns, and Zoe’s first award may simply be the first visible branch of something much deeper.","chinese":"Zoe 的吸引力，正在於這種純真與情感智慧之間的平衡。 她書寫細小的事情，卻總能以某種方式使它們變得重大。 她歌唱得輕柔，但她的文字卻久久停留。 她不只是娛樂觀眾；她給予他們空間去理解自己。 也許正因如此，她的崛起雖然突然，卻並不令人覺得只是偶然。 參天大樹由小小橡子長成，而 Zoe 的第一個獎項，也許只是某種更深厚事物露出地面的第一根枝椏。"},{"label":"Paragraph 10","english":"As our interview ended, Zoe held her trophy as if it still belonged to someone else. Then she smiled and said, “I don’t want my next songs to sound famous. I want them to sound honest.” For a new artist surrounded by applause, that may be the most promising note of all.","chinese":"訪問結束時，Zoe 捧着她的獎座，彷彿它仍然屬於別人。 然後她微笑着說：「我不希望我接下來的歌曲聽起來很有名氣。我希望它們聽起來很真誠。」 對一位被掌聲包圍的新晉歌手而言，這也許就是最令人期待的一個音符。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"from MTR platforms to music awards","chinese":"從港鐵月台到音樂頒獎禮"},{"english":"an unlikely first verse","chinese":"意想不到的開端"},{"english":"no one saw someone coming","chinese":"沒有人預料到某人會冒起"},{"english":"walk past","chinese":"走過；路過"},{"english":"outside Prince Edward Station","chinese":"太子站外"},{"english":"the quiet girl with the guitar","chinese":"那個拿着結他的安靜女生"},{"english":"certainly not","chinese":"當然不是"},{"english":"singer-songwriter","chinese":"創作歌手"},{"english":"stand under the dazzling lights","chinese":"站在耀眼燈光下"},{"english":"hold the trophy for","chinese":"手持……獎座"},{"english":"Best New Artist","chinese":"最佳新人"},{"english":"trembling hands","chinese":"顫抖的雙手"},{"english":"tearful eyes","chinese":"含淚的雙眼"},{"english":"it turns out","chinese":"結果是；原來"},{"english":"sudden rise to fame","chinese":"突然成名"},{"english":"nothing short of remarkable","chinese":"非常出色；非凡"},{"english":"up until last year","chinese":"直到去年為止"},{"english":"perform acoustic covers","chinese":"演唱原音翻唱歌曲"},{"english":"after school","chinese":"放學後"},{"english":"upload short clips to social media","chinese":"上載短片到社交媒體"},{"english":"social media","chinese":"社交媒體"},{"english":"help her mother at","chinese":"在……幫媽媽手"},{"english":"a small flower shop","chinese":"小花店"},{"english":"breakthrough came when","chinese":"突破出現在……的時候"},{"english":"a 45-second video","chinese":"一段45秒影片"},{"english":"original song","chinese":"原創歌曲"},{"english":"be reposted by","chinese":"被……轉發"},{"english":"popular music blogger","chinese":"受歡迎的音樂博客"},{"english":"by the next morning","chinese":"到第二天早上"},{"english":"gather hundreds of thousands of views","chinese":"累積數十萬瀏覽量"},{"english":"by the end of the week","chinese":"到該星期結束時"},{"english":"record companies","chinese":"唱片公司"},{"english":"checking homework messages","chinese":"查看功課訊息"},{"english":"strangers were asking","chinese":"陌生人在問"},{"english":"album would come out","chinese":"專輯會推出"},{"english":"what makes someone's story refreshing","chinese":"令某人的故事令人耳目一新的地方"},{"english":"the speed of her success","chinese":"成功的速度"},{"english":"remain grounded","chinese":"保持腳踏實地"},{"english":"all the while","chinese":"一直；期間始終"},{"english":"in person","chinese":"親身見面時"},{"english":"soft-spoken","chinese":"說話溫柔的；輕聲細語的"},{"english":"almost cautious","chinese":"幾乎顯得謹慎"},{"english":"choose her words","chinese":"斟酌用詞"},{"english":"choose her chords","chinese":"選擇和弦"},{"english":"with feeling","chinese":"帶着感情"},{"english":"make herself out to be","chinese":"把自己說成……"},{"english":"a genius discovered overnight","chinese":"一夜之間被發掘的天才"},{"english":"insist that","chinese":"堅持認為"},{"english":"grow out of","chinese":"源自；由……而來"},{"english":"ordinary Hong Kong life","chinese":"平凡的香港生活"},{"english":"dramatic heartbreak","chinese":"戲劇性的心碎經歷"},{"english":"bus rides","chinese":"巴士車程"},{"english":"family dinners","chinese":"家庭晚飯"},{"english":"too shy to say","chinese":"太害羞而說不出口"},{"english":"take something for example","chinese":"以……為例"},{"english":"be inspired by","chinese":"受……啟發"},{"english":"late-night journeys","chinese":"深夜路程"},{"english":"tutorial classes","chinese":"補習班；補習堂"},{"english":"notice students and workers","chinese":"留意到學生和工人"},{"english":"sharing the same tired silence","chinese":"共享同一種疲憊的沉默"},{"english":"look exhausted","chinese":"看起來筋疲力盡"},{"english":"still going somewhere","chinese":"仍然在前往某處"},{"english":"that observation became","chinese":"那個觀察變成了"},{"english":"a tender ballad","chinese":"溫柔的抒情歌"},{"english":"growing up in a city","chinese":"在城市中長大"},{"english":"come at the cost of","chinese":"以犧牲……為代價"},{"english":"at the cost of rest","chinese":"以休息作代價"},{"english":"gentle yet haunting","chinese":"溫柔卻縈繞心頭"},{"english":"capture the loneliness of","chinese":"捕捉……的孤獨感"},{"english":"crowded places","chinese":"擠迫的地方"},{"english":"immediately recognised","chinese":"立即認出；馬上有共鳴"},{"english":"fan favourite","chinese":"歌迷喜愛的作品"},{"english":"come from","chinese":"來自；源自"},{"english":"artificial flowers","chinese":"人造花"},{"english":"hospital visits","chinese":"探病"},{"english":"last longer","chinese":"維持得更久"},{"english":"at first glance","chinese":"乍看之下"},{"english":"on closer inspection","chinese":"仔細看來"},{"english":"choose what lasts over what lives","chinese":"選擇持久而非有生命的東西"},{"english":"the result is","chinese":"結果是"},{"english":"from the outside","chinese":"從外表看來"},{"english":"lose its warmth within","chinese":"內裏失去溫度"},{"english":"not so much...as...","chinese":"與其說是……不如說是……"},{"english":"a careful song","chinese":"細膩謹慎的歌曲"},{"english":"beauty still matters","chinese":"美是否仍然重要"},{"english":"reveal a more personal side","chinese":"展現更個人的一面"},{"english":"newest single","chinese":"最新單曲"},{"english":"during a period when","chinese":"在……的一段時期"},{"english":"feel overwhelmed by","chinese":"被……壓得喘不過氣"},{"english":"sudden attention","chinese":"突如其來的關注"},{"english":"learn to stand under a spotlight","chinese":"學習站在聚光燈下"},{"english":"without being blinded by it","chinese":"而不被它蒙蔽"},{"english":"with success comes pressure","chinese":"成功伴隨壓力"},{"english":"not entirely easy to handle","chinese":"並非完全容易應付"},{"english":"get used to","chinese":"習慣於"},{"english":"interviews and rehearsals","chinese":"訪問和綵排"},{"english":"public comments","chinese":"公眾評論"},{"english":"the strange feeling of being recognised","chinese":"被人認出的奇怪感覺"},{"english":"buying egg waffles","chinese":"買雞蛋仔"},{"english":"miss being invisible","chinese":"懷念不被注意的感覺"},{"english":"feel less alone","chinese":"感到不那麼孤單"},{"english":"make everything worth it","chinese":"令一切都值得"},{"english":"someone's appeal lies in","chinese":"某人的吸引力在於"},{"english":"balance between innocence and emotional intelligence","chinese":"天真與情緒智慧之間的平衡"},{"english":"emotional intelligence","chinese":"情緒智慧"},{"english":"write about small things","chinese":"書寫小事情"},{"english":"make them feel large","chinese":"令它們顯得重大"},{"english":"her words linger","chinese":"她的文字令人回味"},{"english":"entertain her audience","chinese":"娛樂觀眾"},{"english":"give someone room to","chinese":"給某人空間去……"},{"english":"understand themselves","chinese":"理解自己"},{"english":"perhaps that is why","chinese":"也許這就是為何"},{"english":"feel accidental","chinese":"感覺像偶然"},{"english":"Great oaks grow from little acorns","chinese":"偉大成就始於微小起點"},{"english":"first visible branch","chinese":"第一根看得見的枝椏；初步成果"},{"english":"something much deeper","chinese":"更深層的東西"},{"english":"as our interview ended","chinese":"當訪問結束時"},{"english":"belong to someone else","chinese":"屬於別人"},{"english":"surrounded by applause","chinese":"被掌聲包圍"},{"english":"sound famous","chinese":"聽起來有名氣"},{"english":"sound honest","chinese":"聽起來真誠"},{"english":"the most promising note of all","chinese":"最令人期待的一點"}]},"dse-writing-2020-part-b-q8":{"exerciseId":"dse-writing-2020-part-b-q8","essayKey":"","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=dse-writing-2020-part-b-q8","flashDeckId":"dse/writing/part-b/2020/Q8","paragraphs":[{"label":"Paragraph 1","english":"The Station That Heard Us","chinese":"聽見我們的研究站"},{"label":"Paragraph 2","english":"Chapter One: White Noise","chinese":"第一章：白噪音"},{"label":"Paragraph 3","english":"The first thing to know about silence in the Arctic is that it is not quiet. It breathes. It presses its white mouth against windows, slips through screws in steel, and waits at the edge of every sentence. Before I went north, I thought silence meant the absence of sound. By the time I reached Borealis-7, I knew better.","chinese":"關於北極的寂靜，首先要知道的一點是：它並不安靜。 它會呼吸。 它把白色的嘴壓在窗上，從鋼鐵的螺絲縫間滲入，並在每一句說話邊緣等待 在我北上之前，我一直以為寂靜意味著聲音的缺席。 等我抵達 Borealis-7 時，我才明白自己錯了。"},{"label":"Paragraph 4","english":"The Ministry called the matter “a temporary staffing irregularity”. My editor was less delicate. “Chris,” he said, sliding a thin folder across his desk, “four scientists have vanished from a locked research station. One by one. Find out why—and try not to become number five.”","chinese":"部方把這件事稱為「暫時性人手異常」。 我的編輯就沒有那麼委婉了。 「Chris，」他一邊說，一邊把一份薄薄的文件夾沿著桌面推到我面前，「四名科學家從一座上鎖的研究站裡消失了。 一個接一個。 查出原因——還有，盡量不要成為第五個。」"},{"label":"Paragraph 5","english":"So there I was, two days later, dropping from a supply helicopter onto a rectangle of blue ice at the top of the world. The pilot did not land properly. She only lowered the craft long enough for me to jump, my duffel thudding beside me like a body.","chinese":"於是兩天後，我就出現在那裡，從一架補給直升機上降落到世界頂端一塊長方形的藍冰之上。 機師並沒有真正降落。 她只是把飛機降得足夠低，低到讓我跳下去；我的行李袋砰的一聲落在我身旁，像一具屍體。"},{"label":"Paragraph 6","english":"“No offence, Mr. Wong,” she shouted, “but this place makes the instruments lie.”","chinese":"「無意冒犯，Wong 先生，」她大聲喊道，「但這地方會讓儀器說謊。」"},{"label":"Paragraph 7","english":"Then she rose into the bruised sky and left me alone at the station.","chinese":"然後，她升入那片像淤青一樣的天空，把我獨自留在研究站那裡。"},{"label":"Paragraph 8","english":"At first glance, Borealis-7 looked exactly like the Ministry’s photograph: three silver modules linked by sealed corridors, a wind turbine turning with slow, unwilling grace, and a radio mast pointing at the clouds like an accusation. On closer inspection, however, several details refused to fit. The eastern airlock stood open. The security light blinked red, then green, then red again. There were no fresh footprints leading out.","chinese":"乍看之下，Borealis-7 和部方照片裡的樣子完全一樣：三個銀色艙體由密封走廊連接起來，一座風力渦輪以緩慢而不情願的優雅轉動著，還有一支無線電桅杆像控訴一樣指向雲層。 然而，仔細一看，有幾個細節卻怎樣也對不上。 東面的氣閘門是開著的。 保安燈先閃紅色，再閃綠色，然後又閃回紅色。 沒有任何新鮮腳印通往外面。"},{"label":"Paragraph 9","english":"I stepped inside.","chinese":"我踏了進去。"},{"label":"Paragraph 10","english":"Heat struck me first, then the smell: coffee, disinfectant, metal, fear. Somewhere deep in the station, a machine clicked steadily, as if counting down. I called out, but the corridor swallowed my voice before it could travel far.","chinese":"最先襲來的是熱氣，然後是氣味：咖啡、消毒藥水、金屬，還有恐懼。 在研究站深處的某個地方，一部機器穩定地咔嗒作響，彷彿正在倒數。 我喊了一聲，但我的聲音還未傳遠，便被走廊吞了下去。"},{"label":"Paragraph 11","english":"“Mr. Wong,” said a speaker above my head.","chinese":"「Wong 先生，」我頭頂上的揚聲器說道。"},{"label":"Paragraph 12","english":"The camera beside it turned to face me.","chinese":"旁邊的攝影機轉了過來，對準了我。"},{"label":"Paragraph 13","english":"“Proceed to decontamination. Dr Soren is expecting you.”","chinese":"「請前往消毒室。Soren 博士正在等你。」"},{"label":"Paragraph 14","english":"The voice was calm enough to be human, and flat enough not to be. I obeyed, if only because the inner door had locked behind me. While the chamber hissed with antiseptic vapour, I read the notice printed on the glass:","chinese":"那把聲音冷靜得像人類，卻又平板得不像人類。 我照做了，至少是因為我身後的內門已經鎖上。 當消毒艙嘶嘶噴出消毒蒸氣時，我讀著印在玻璃上的告示："},{"label":"Paragraph 15","english":"IN CASE OF AUDITORY HALLUCINATION, REPORT IMMEDIATELY.","chinese":"如遇聽覺幻覺，請立即報告。"},{"label":"Paragraph 16","english":"DO NOT ANSWER UNFAMILIAR VOICES.","chinese":"不要回應陌生聲音。 Warning Notice / Third Rule / Central Foreshadowing（警告告示／第三條規則／核心伏筆）"},{"label":"Paragraph 17","english":"DO NOT ANSWER FAMILIAR VOICES AFTER 00:00.","chinese":"午夜零時後，不要回應熟悉聲音。"},{"label":"Paragraph 18","english":"Journalists are paid to be curious. That notice made me wish, briefly and shamefully, that I had chosen advertising instead.","chinese":"記者的薪水，就是用來購買他們的好奇心的。 可是那張告示讓我短暫而羞愧地希望，自己當初選的是廣告業。"},{"label":"Paragraph 19","english":"Dr Elias Soren met me in the common room. He was tall, hollow-eyed, and wrapped in two sweaters. Behind him stood two others: a young systems engineer named Lena Cho, who kept rubbing her left wrist, and an older medic, Dr Malek, whose smile arrived late and left early.","chinese":"Elias Soren 博士在公共休息室見了我。 他身形高瘦，眼窩深陷，身上裹著兩件毛衣。 他身後站著另外兩個人：一位年輕的系統工程師，名叫 Lena Cho，她一直揉著自己的左手腕；還有一位年紀較大的醫療人員 Malek 博士，他的笑容來得很遲，離開得很早。"},{"label":"Paragraph 20","english":"“There were twelve of you originally,” I said, taking out my recorder. “Now there are three.”","chinese":"「你們原本有十二個人，」我一邊拿出錄音筆，一邊說。 「現在只剩下三個。」"},{"label":"Paragraph 21","english":"“Eight,” Soren corrected.","chinese":"「八個。」Soren 糾正道。"},{"label":"Paragraph 22","english":"I frowned. “The file says four missing.”","chinese":"我皺起眉。 「文件上說失蹤的是四個。」"},{"label":"Paragraph 23","english":"“The file is outdated.”","chinese":"「那份文件已經過時了。」"},{"label":"Paragraph 24","english":"No sooner had he said it than the overhead lights dimmed. Somewhere beyond the wall, ice gave a long, animal groan. Lena shut her eyes. Dr Malek whispered something I did not catch.","chinese":"他話音剛落，頭頂的燈便暗了下來。 牆的另一邊某處，冰層發出一聲漫長而像動物般的呻吟。 Lena 閉上眼睛。 Malek 博士低聲說了些甚麼，但我沒有聽清楚。"},{"label":"Paragraph 25","english":"Soren leaned closer. “Listen carefully. Dr Iversen disappeared from the weather tower. Professor Hale from his locked laboratory. Chen from the hydroponic bay. After that, we stopped sleeping alone. It did not help. Yesterday, Anika went missing from the infirmary while Malek stood outside.”","chinese":"Soren 靠近了一點。 「仔細聽。 Iversen 博士是從氣象塔消失的。 Hale 教授是從他上鎖的實驗室消失的。 Chen 是從水耕艙消失的。 那之後，我們不再單獨睡覺。 沒有用。 昨天，Anika 在醫療室裡失蹤，而 Malek 當時就站在外面。」"},{"label":"Paragraph 26","english":"“That is impossible.”","chinese":"「那是不可能的。」"},{"label":"Paragraph 27","english":"“So was the first disappearance,” he said. “So was the second.”","chinese":"「第一次失蹤也是不可能的，」他說。 「第二次也是。」"},{"label":"Paragraph 28","english":"The trouble with fear is that it can look like madness until the evidence starts breathing down your neck. I asked for the security footage. Soren’s face tightened, but he led me to the control room, where six monitors flickered in the blue half-light.","chinese":"恐懼的問題在於，在證據開始逼近你之前，它看起來可以像瘋狂一樣。 我要求查看保安錄像。 Soren 的臉繃緊了，但他還是帶我去了控制室。那裡有六部螢幕在藍色的半明半暗中閃爍。"},{"label":"Paragraph 29","english":"“Watch,” he said.","chinese":"「看。」他說。"},{"label":"Paragraph 30","english":"The screen showed the infirmary corridor at 23:59. Anika, in a red parka, stood behind a glass door. Malek sat outside, awake. The clock changed to 00:00. The lights went out for exactly eleven seconds. When they returned, the room was empty.","chinese":"螢幕顯示的是 23:59 的醫療室走廊。 Anika 穿著一件紅色厚外套，站在玻璃門後。 Malek 坐在外面，清醒著。 時鐘跳到 00:00。 燈光熄滅了整整十一秒。 等燈光重新亮起時，房間已經空了。"},{"label":"Paragraph 31","english":"Not a door opened. Not a shadow moved. Anika was simply gone.","chinese":"沒有任何一道門打開。 沒有任何一道影子移動。 Anika 就只是消失了。"},{"label":"Paragraph 32","english":"Then the speakers crackled.","chinese":"然後，揚聲器發出噼啪聲。"},{"label":"Paragraph 33","english":"At first, I thought it was static. Then I heard my own voice, soft and close, coming from under the floor.","chinese":"起初，我以為那只是雜音。 然後，我聽見了自己的聲音，柔和而貼近，從地板底下傳來。"},{"label":"Paragraph 34","english":"“Chris,” it said. “You’re late.”","chinese":"「Chris，」它說。 「你遲到了。」"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"white noise","chinese":"白噪音"},{"english":"the first thing to know about","chinese":"首先要知道的是"},{"english":"silence in the Arctic","chinese":"北極的寂靜"},{"english":"the Arctic","chinese":"北極"},{"english":"presses against","chinese":"壓向；貼着"},{"english":"slips through","chinese":"從……鑽進去"},{"english":"screws in steel","chinese":"鋼鐵上的螺絲"},{"english":"at the edge of","chinese":"在……邊緣"},{"english":"before I went north","chinese":"在我北上之前"},{"english":"the absence of sound","chinese":"沒有聲音"},{"english":"by the time","chinese":"到……的時候"},{"english":"knew better","chinese":"已經明白事實並非如此"},{"english":"called the matter","chinese":"把事情稱為"},{"english":"a temporary staffing irregularity","chinese":"暫時性人手異常"},{"english":"less delicate","chinese":"沒那麼婉轉"},{"english":"slid a folder across","chinese":"把文件夾推過去"},{"english":"a thin folder","chinese":"一個薄薄的文件夾"},{"english":"have vanished from","chinese":"從……消失"},{"english":"a locked research station","chinese":"上鎖的研究站"},{"english":"one by one","chinese":"一個接一個"},{"english":"find out why","chinese":"查明原因"},{"english":"become number five","chinese":"成為第五個失蹤者"},{"english":"so there I was","chinese":"於是我就這樣"},{"english":"a supply helicopter","chinese":"補給直升機"},{"english":"a rectangle of blue ice","chinese":"一塊長方形藍冰"},{"english":"at the top of the world","chinese":"在世界之巔"},{"english":"land properly","chinese":"正式着陸"},{"english":"lowered the craft","chinese":"降低飛行器"},{"english":"long enough for","chinese":"足夠讓……"},{"english":"duffel","chinese":"帆布旅行袋"},{"english":"thudded beside","chinese":"砰一聲落在旁邊"},{"english":"like a body","chinese":"像一具屍體"},{"english":"No offence","chinese":"無意冒犯"},{"english":"makes the instruments lie","chinese":"令儀器顯示錯誤"},{"english":"rose into","chinese":"升進"},{"english":"the bruised sky","chinese":"暗紫色的天空"},{"english":"left me alone","chinese":"留下我獨自一人"},{"english":"at first glance","chinese":"乍看之下"},{"english":"looked exactly like","chinese":"看起來完全像"},{"english":"linked by sealed corridors","chinese":"由密封走廊連接"},{"english":"sealed corridors","chinese":"密封走廊"},{"english":"a wind turbine","chinese":"風力渦輪機"},{"english":"with slow, unwilling grace","chinese":"緩慢而勉強地優雅轉動"},{"english":"a radio mast","chinese":"無線電桅杆"},{"english":"pointing at","chinese":"指向"},{"english":"like an accusation","chinese":"像一種控訴"},{"english":"on closer inspection","chinese":"仔細看時"},{"english":"refused to fit","chinese":"顯得格格不入；不對勁"},{"english":"eastern airlock","chinese":"東面氣閘"},{"english":"stood open","chinese":"開着"},{"english":"security light","chinese":"保安燈"},{"english":"blinked red and green","chinese":"閃着紅綠燈"},{"english":"fresh footprints","chinese":"新近的腳印"},{"english":"leading out","chinese":"往外延伸"},{"english":"stepped inside","chinese":"走進去"},{"english":"heat struck me first","chinese":"熱氣首先迎面襲來"},{"english":"the smell of","chinese":"……的氣味"},{"english":"disinfectant","chinese":"消毒藥水"},{"english":"deep in the station","chinese":"在研究站深處"},{"english":"clicked steadily","chinese":"有規律地滴答作響"},{"english":"as if counting down","chinese":"好像在倒數"},{"english":"called out","chinese":"大聲呼叫"},{"english":"swallowed my voice","chinese":"吞沒我的聲音"},{"english":"before it could travel far","chinese":"在它能傳遠之前"},{"english":"speaker above my head","chinese":"頭頂上的喇叭"},{"english":"turned to face me","chinese":"轉過來面向我"},{"english":"proceed to decontamination","chinese":"前往除污程序"},{"english":"decontamination","chinese":"除污；消毒程序"},{"english":"is expecting you","chinese":"正在等你"},{"english":"calm enough to be human","chinese":"平靜得像人聲"},{"english":"flat enough not to be","chinese":"平板得不像人聲"},{"english":"if only because","chinese":"只因為"},{"english":"locked behind me","chinese":"在我身後鎖上"},{"english":"chamber","chinese":"小室；艙"},{"english":"hissed with","chinese":"發出嘶嘶聲並充滿"},{"english":"antiseptic vapour","chinese":"消毒蒸氣"},{"english":"in case of","chinese":"如遇到"},{"english":"auditory hallucination","chinese":"幻聽"},{"english":"report immediately","chinese":"立即報告"},{"english":"unfamiliar voices","chinese":"陌生聲音"},{"english":"familiar voices after 00:00","chinese":"午夜後熟悉的聲音"},{"english":"paid to be curious","chinese":"以好奇心為工作"},{"english":"made me wish","chinese":"令我希望"},{"english":"briefly and shamefully","chinese":"短暫而羞愧地"},{"english":"chosen advertising instead","chinese":"改為選擇廣告業"},{"english":"common room","chinese":"公共休息室"},{"english":"hollow-eyed","chinese":"眼窩深陷的"},{"english":"wrapped in","chinese":"裹着"},{"english":"systems engineer","chinese":"系統工程師"},{"english":"kept rubbing","chinese":"不停揉"},{"english":"medic","chinese":"醫護人員"},{"english":"arrived late and left early","chinese":"來得遲、消失得快"},{"english":"originally","chinese":"原本"},{"english":"took out my recorder","chinese":"拿出錄音機"},{"english":"the file is outdated","chinese":"文件已過時"},{"english":"no sooner had… than…","chinese":"剛一……就……"},{"english":"overhead lights","chinese":"頭頂燈"},{"english":"dimmed","chinese":"變暗"},{"english":"beyond the wall","chinese":"在牆後某處"},{"english":"gave a long, animal groan","chinese":"發出長長的獸性呻吟"},{"english":"whispered something","chinese":"低聲說了些話"},{"english":"I did not catch","chinese":"我沒有聽清楚"},{"english":"listen carefully","chinese":"仔細聽"},{"english":"disappeared from","chinese":"從……消失"},{"english":"weather tower","chinese":"氣象塔"},{"english":"locked laboratory","chinese":"上鎖的實驗室"},{"english":"hydroponic bay","chinese":"水耕栽培艙"},{"english":"stopped sleeping alone","chinese":"不再單獨睡覺"},{"english":"it did not help","chinese":"這也沒有用"},{"english":"went missing","chinese":"失蹤"},{"english":"infirmary","chinese":"醫務室"},{"english":"stood outside","chinese":"站在外面"},{"english":"that is impossible","chinese":"那是不可能的"},{"english":"so was","chinese":"……也是"},{"english":"the trouble with fear is that","chinese":"恐懼的問題在於"},{"english":"look like madness","chinese":"看起來像瘋狂"},{"english":"until the evidence starts","chinese":"直到證據開始"},{"english":"breathing down your neck","chinese":"緊逼着你；迫在眉睫"},{"english":"security footage","chinese":"保安錄影片段"},{"english":"face tightened","chinese":"臉色繃緊"},{"english":"led me to","chinese":"帶我到"},{"english":"control room","chinese":"控制室"},{"english":"monitors flickered","chinese":"監視器閃爍"},{"english":"blue half-light","chinese":"半明半暗的藍光"},{"english":"infirmary corridor","chinese":"醫務室走廊"},{"english":"in a red parka","chinese":"穿着紅色防寒外套"},{"english":"glass door","chinese":"玻璃門"},{"english":"the clock changed to","chinese":"時鐘轉到"},{"english":"went out","chinese":"熄滅"},{"english":"for exactly eleven seconds","chinese":"整整十一秒"},{"english":"when they returned","chinese":"當它們恢復時"},{"english":"the room was empty","chinese":"房間空無一人"},{"english":"not a door opened","chinese":"沒有任何門打開"},{"english":"not a shadow moved","chinese":"沒有任何影子移動"},{"english":"simply gone","chinese":"就這樣消失了"},{"english":"speakers crackled","chinese":"喇叭發出雜音"},{"english":"static","chinese":"靜電雜音"},{"english":"my own voice","chinese":"我自己的聲音"},{"english":"soft and close","chinese":"輕柔而貼近"},{"english":"coming from under the floor","chinese":"從地板下面傳來"},{"english":"You're late","chinese":"你遲到了"}]},"dse-writing-2020-part-b-q9":{"exerciseId":"dse-writing-2020-part-b-q9","essayKey":"","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=dse-writing-2020-part-b-q9","flashDeckId":"dse/writing/part-b/2020/Q9","paragraphs":[{"label":"Paragraph 1","english":"From Sceptic to Spellbound: A Night at Hong Kong’s Xiqu Centre","chinese":"從懷疑到著迷：香港戲曲中心的一夜"},{"label":"Paragraph 2","english":"When my friend Chris suggested that we spend my third evening in Hong Kong watching Chinese opera at the new Xiqu Centre in the West Kowloon Cultural District, my first reaction was embarrassingly honest: would I understand a single minute of it? Up until then, Chinese opera had been, in my imagination, a museum piece — beautiful perhaps, but remote, slow and difficult to enter. Still, travelling is not just about collecting skyline photographs; more importantly, it is about letting a place challenge your assumptions. So I followed Chris through the glowing entrance, in order to see a Hong Kong that lay beyond ferries, malls and neon signs. By the end of the night, I had not merely changed my mind about Xiqu; I had changed the way I listened to a culture.","chinese":"當我的朋友 Chris 建議我在香港的第三個晚上，到西九文化區全新的戲曲中心觀看中國戲曲時，我第一個反應坦白得有點尷尬：我會聽得懂哪怕一分鐘嗎？ 在那之前，在我的想像中，中國戲曲一直像是一件博物館展品——也許美麗，卻遙遠、緩慢，而且難以親近。 然而，旅行不只是收集城市天際線的照片；更重要的是，它是讓一個地方挑戰你的既有想法。 於是，我跟着 Chris 走過那道發光的入口，為的是看見一個存在於渡輪、商場和霓虹招牌之外的香港。 到那晚結束時，我不只是改變了對戲曲的看法；我也改變了聆聽一種文化的方式。"},{"label":"Paragraph 3","english":"The experience began before the first note was played. Standing in the foyer, I felt as if the building itself was easing me into another world. Outside, West Kowloon was full of harbour breeze and Saturday-night energy. Inside, however, the atmosphere slowed down. Elderly opera lovers chatted beside tourists with wide eyes; a young couple took photos under the warm lights; a child pointed at a poster showing embroidered robes and painted faces. What surprised me most was that the Xiqu Centre did not make the art feel locked away. Instead, it made room for newcomers. Chris showed me the subtitles, explained that a tiny movement of the hand could reveal rank, anger or grief, and told me not to worry about “understanding everything”. Few, if any, first-time visitors could catch every reference. Yet the setting and his patient explanations gave me enough confidence to stay open.","chinese":"這段經歷在第一個音符奏響之前便已經開始。 站在大堂裡，我覺得彷彿建築物本身正在把我慢慢帶進另一個世界。 外面的西九充滿海港微風和星期六夜晚的活力。 然而，裡面的氣氛卻慢了下來。 年長的戲曲愛好者在睜大眼睛的遊客旁聊天；一對年輕情侶在溫暖的燈光下拍照；一個孩子指着一張展示刺繡戲服和臉譜的海報。 最令我驚訝的是，戲曲中心並沒有讓這門藝術感覺像被鎖起來一樣。 相反，它為初來乍到的人留下了空間。 Chris 給我看字幕，解釋說一個細微的手部動作也可以透露身份地位、憤怒或悲傷，並告訴我不必擔心要「明白所有東西」。 即使有初次觀看的訪客能捕捉到每一個典故，恐怕也少之又少。 然而，那個環境，加上他耐心的解釋，給了我足夠信心去保持開放的心態。"},{"label":"Paragraph 4","english":"Then the curtain rose, and my doubts began to fall away. At first, the singing startled me. It was sharper and higher than anything I usually listen to, and I wondered whether I could grow used to it. But the longer I watched, the more I realised that the voice was not merely “singing”; it was carrying pain, pride and longing across the stage. A sleeve flicked like a wave. A fan opened, and suddenly a character seemed powerful. A slow step across the stage stretched time until even silence felt meaningful. Meanwhile, the percussion did not simply accompany the actors; it controlled the pulse of the story. One moment, the wooden clappers made my heart jump; the next, the strings softened the scene so gently that the hall seemed to hold its breath. I cannot begin to describe every detail, but one image remains: a warrior, standing still under bright light, whose painted face looked fierce and sorrowful at once.","chinese":"然後幕布升起，我的疑慮也開始逐漸消散。 一開始，唱腔令我有點吃驚。 它比我平日聽的任何聲音都更尖、更高，而我不禁想自己能否慢慢習慣。 但我看得越久，就越明白那聲音不只是「唱歌」；它正把痛苦、驕傲和渴望傳遍整個舞台。 一截水袖像波浪般一揮。 一把摺扇打開，角色忽然顯得威嚴有力。 一個緩慢跨過舞台的步伐把時間拉長，直到連沉默也變得富有意義。 與此同時，敲擊樂並不只是為演員伴奏；它掌控着故事的脈搏。 前一刻，木梆聲令我心頭一震；下一刻，弦樂又如此溫柔地軟化了場景，讓整個劇場彷彿屏住了呼吸。 我實在無法一一形容每一個細節，但有一個畫面仍然留在心裡：一位武士站在明亮燈光下靜止不動，他的臉譜同時顯得威猛而哀傷。"},{"label":"Paragraph 5","english":"Only after the final bow did the real impact of the evening dawn on me. Before the performance, I had mistaken unfamiliarity for boredom. I had assumed that because I did not know the codes, the art would have little to offer me. In fact, the opposite was true. Xiqu taught me that culture is not always designed to be consumed quickly. Some things ask us to slow down, observe carefully and accept that we may understand little by little rather than all at once. That lesson felt powerful in Hong Kong, a city often described through speed - fast trains, fast service, fast deals, fast lives. Yet here was another Hong Kong — patient, disciplined, symbolic and deeply rooted. Far from being an old-fashioned performance for specialists, Chinese opera became, in my eyes, a living conversation between past and present.","chinese":"直到最後謝幕之後，那個晚上真正帶給我的影響才在我心中浮現。 演出之前，我曾把陌生誤以為沉悶。 我曾假設，因為我不懂那些符碼，這門藝術便不會給我甚麼。 事實上，情況正好相反。 戲曲教會我，文化並不總是被設計成可以被快速消費的東西。 有些事物要求我們慢下來、仔細觀察，並接受我們也許是逐點逐點地理解，而不是一下子全部明白。 在香港這座常被速度描述的城市裡——快速列車、快速服務、快速交易、快速生活——這一課尤其有力。 然而，這裡呈現的是另一個香港——耐心、嚴謹、富有象徵意義，而且根基深厚。 在我眼中，中國戲曲遠不是只給專家欣賞的過時表演，而是一場連接過去與現在的活生生對話。"},{"label":"Paragraph 6","english":"So, should you visit the Xiqu Centre? My answer is a resounding yes. Arrive early, read the story summary, watch the audience as well as the stage, and let yourself be confused for a while. Travel broadens the mind not because every place immediately feels familiar, but because some places make us question what we thought we knew. Last night, I entered the theatre expecting to endure a cultural duty. I left carrying a tune I could not sing, a story I could not fully retell, and a respect I could not shake off. No words can do the experience justice — but perhaps that is why you should see it in person.","chinese":"那麼，你應該參觀戲曲中心嗎？ 我的答案是非常肯定的：應該。 提早到達，閱讀故事摘要，既觀看舞台，也觀看觀眾，並容許自己暫時感到困惑。 旅行之所以能開闊人的思想，不是因為每個地方都會立即令人覺得熟悉，而是因為有些地方會讓我們質疑自己以為已經知道的事情。 昨晚，我走進劇場時，本以為自己要忍受一項文化義務。 離開時，我帶着一段自己唱不出的旋律、一個無法完整重述的故事，以及一份揮之不去的敬意。 任何文字都無法充分呈現這段經歷——但也許正因如此，你才應該親身去看看"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"from sceptic to spellbound","chinese":"由懷疑到着迷"},{"english":"sceptic","chinese":"懷疑者"},{"english":"spellbound","chinese":"着迷的；入神的"},{"english":"a night at","chinese":"在……的一晚"},{"english":"Xiqu Centre","chinese":"戲曲中心"},{"english":"suggested that","chinese":"建議"},{"english":"spend my third evening","chinese":"度過我第三個晚上"},{"english":"watching Chinese opera","chinese":"欣賞中國戲曲"},{"english":"Chinese opera","chinese":"中國戲曲"},{"english":"West Kowloon Cultural District","chinese":"西九文化區"},{"english":"my first reaction was","chinese":"我的第一反應是"},{"english":"embarrassingly honest","chinese":"誠實得令人尷尬"},{"english":"understand a single minute of","chinese":"聽懂其中一分一秒"},{"english":"up until then","chinese":"在那之前"},{"english":"in my imagination","chinese":"在我的想像中"},{"english":"a museum piece","chinese":"像博物館藏品般的舊事物"},{"english":"remote, slow and difficult to enter","chinese":"遙遠、緩慢而難以投入"},{"english":"collecting skyline photographs","chinese":"拍攝城市天際線照片"},{"english":"more importantly","chinese":"更重要的是"},{"english":"challenge your assumptions","chinese":"挑戰你的既有想法"},{"english":"followed someone through","chinese":"跟隨某人穿過"},{"english":"the glowing entrance","chinese":"亮着燈光的入口"},{"english":"in order to","chinese":"為了"},{"english":"lay beyond","chinese":"存在於……之外"},{"english":"ferries, malls and neon signs","chinese":"渡輪、商場和霓虹招牌"},{"english":"by the end of the night","chinese":"到那晚結束時"},{"english":"not merely","chinese":"不只是"},{"english":"change my mind about","chinese":"改變對……的看法"},{"english":"the way I listened to a culture","chinese":"我聆聽一種文化的方式"},{"english":"the first note was played","chinese":"第一個音符奏起"},{"english":"standing in the foyer","chinese":"站在大堂裏"},{"english":"felt as if","chinese":"感覺好像"},{"english":"ease someone into","chinese":"引導某人慢慢進入"},{"english":"another world","chinese":"另一個世界"},{"english":"harbour breeze","chinese":"海港微風"},{"english":"Saturday-night energy","chinese":"星期六晚上的活力"},{"english":"the atmosphere slowed down","chinese":"氣氛慢了下來"},{"english":"elderly opera lovers","chinese":"年長戲曲愛好者"},{"english":"tourists with wide eyes","chinese":"睜大眼睛的遊客"},{"english":"under the warm lights","chinese":"在溫暖的燈光下"},{"english":"embroidered robes","chinese":"繡花戲服"},{"english":"painted faces","chinese":"臉譜；彩繪面孔"},{"english":"what surprised me most was that","chinese":"最令我驚訝的是"},{"english":"locked away","chinese":"被封存；被隔絕"},{"english":"make room for","chinese":"為……留出空間"},{"english":"newcomers","chinese":"初次接觸的人"},{"english":"a tiny movement of the hand","chinese":"手部一個細微動作"},{"english":"reveal rank, anger or grief","chinese":"顯示身份、憤怒或悲傷"},{"english":"rank","chinese":"身份；地位"},{"english":"grief","chinese":"悲傷"},{"english":"not to worry about","chinese":"不必擔心"},{"english":"few, if any","chinese":"即使有，也很少"},{"english":"first-time visitors","chinese":"首次到訪的人"},{"english":"catch every reference","chinese":"聽懂每個典故"},{"english":"patient explanations","chinese":"耐心的解釋"},{"english":"give someone enough confidence to","chinese":"給予某人足夠信心去"},{"english":"stay open","chinese":"保持開放態度"},{"english":"the curtain rose","chinese":"幕布升起"},{"english":"doubts began to fall away","chinese":"疑慮開始消散"},{"english":"at first","chinese":"起初"},{"english":"startled me","chinese":"令我吃驚"},{"english":"grow used to","chinese":"逐漸習慣"},{"english":"the longer…, the more…","chinese":"越……就越……"},{"english":"not merely singing","chinese":"不只是唱歌"},{"english":"carrying pain, pride and longing","chinese":"承載痛苦、驕傲和渴望"},{"english":"longing","chinese":"渴望；思念"},{"english":"across the stage","chinese":"橫越舞台"},{"english":"flicked like a wave","chinese":"像浪一樣一甩"},{"english":"a fan opened","chinese":"扇子打開"},{"english":"a slow step across the stage","chinese":"橫過舞台的緩慢步伐"},{"english":"stretch time","chinese":"拉長時間"},{"english":"even silence felt meaningful","chinese":"連沉默也變得有意義"},{"english":"meanwhile","chinese":"與此同時"},{"english":"percussion","chinese":"敲擊樂"},{"english":"accompany the actors","chinese":"為演員伴奏"},{"english":"control the pulse of the story","chinese":"控制故事的節奏"},{"english":"one moment…, the next…","chinese":"前一刻……下一刻……"},{"english":"wooden clappers","chinese":"木拍板"},{"english":"make my heart jump","chinese":"令我心頭一震"},{"english":"the strings","chinese":"弦樂"},{"english":"soften the scene","chinese":"令場面柔和下來"},{"english":"hold its breath","chinese":"屏息靜氣"},{"english":"cannot begin to describe","chinese":"無法充分描述"},{"english":"one image remains","chinese":"有一個畫面仍然留在腦海"},{"english":"a warrior","chinese":"武士；戰士"},{"english":"standing still","chinese":"站着不動"},{"english":"under bright light","chinese":"在強光下"},{"english":"looked fierce and sorrowful at once","chinese":"同時顯得兇猛而哀傷"},{"english":"at once","chinese":"同時"},{"english":"the final bow","chinese":"謝幕"},{"english":"the real impact","chinese":"真正的影響"},{"english":"dawn on me","chinese":"使我恍然大悟"},{"english":"mistake unfamiliarity for boredom","chinese":"把陌生誤以為沉悶"},{"english":"assume that","chinese":"以為；假設"},{"english":"know the codes","chinese":"懂得當中的符碼"},{"english":"have little to offer","chinese":"沒有甚麼可給予"},{"english":"the opposite was true","chinese":"事實剛好相反"},{"english":"be designed to","chinese":"被設計成用來"},{"english":"be consumed quickly","chinese":"被快速消費"},{"english":"ask us to slow down","chinese":"要求我們慢下來"},{"english":"observe carefully","chinese":"細心觀察"},{"english":"little by little","chinese":"一點一點地"},{"english":"rather than all at once","chinese":"而不是一下子全部"},{"english":"described through speed","chinese":"透過速度來形容"},{"english":"fast deals","chinese":"快速交易"},{"english":"another Hong Kong","chinese":"另一個香港"},{"english":"patient, disciplined, symbolic and deeply rooted","chinese":"有耐性、有紀律、富象徵性而且根基深厚"},{"english":"deeply rooted","chinese":"根基深厚"},{"english":"far from being","chinese":"絕不是"},{"english":"an old-fashioned performance","chinese":"老套的表演"},{"english":"specialists","chinese":"專家；行家"},{"english":"in my eyes","chinese":"在我眼中"},{"english":"a living conversation","chinese":"有生命力的對話"},{"english":"between past and present","chinese":"在過去與現在之間"},{"english":"a resounding yes","chinese":"非常肯定的「是」"},{"english":"arrive early","chinese":"早點到達"},{"english":"read the story summary","chinese":"閱讀故事簡介"},{"english":"as well as","chinese":"以及"},{"english":"let yourself be confused","chinese":"容許自己困惑"},{"english":"for a while","chinese":"一會兒"},{"english":"broaden the mind","chinese":"擴闊眼界"},{"english":"not because…, but because…","chinese":"不是因為……而是因為……"},{"english":"immediately feels familiar","chinese":"立即令人感到熟悉"},{"english":"question what we thought we knew","chinese":"質疑自己原本以為知道的事"},{"english":"expecting to endure","chinese":"預期要忍受"},{"english":"a cultural duty","chinese":"一項文化責任"},{"english":"carrying a tune I could not sing","chinese":"帶着一段自己唱不出的旋律離開"},{"english":"fully retell","chinese":"完整複述"},{"english":"a respect I could not shake off","chinese":"一份揮之不去的敬意"},{"english":"shake off","chinese":"擺脫"},{"english":"do the experience justice","chinese":"充分表達那段經歷"},{"english":"see it in person","chinese":"親身觀看"}]},"dse-writing-2021-part-a":{"exerciseId":"dse-writing-2021-part-a","essayKey":"","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=dse-writing-2021-part-a","flashDeckId":"dse/writing/part-a/2021","paragraphs":[{"label":"Greeting","english":"Good morning, everyone!","chinese":"各位早上好！"},{"label":"Introduction","english":"I am thrilled to announce that our annual School Fair will take place on Saturday, 29 May 2021, from 12 p.m. to 4 p.m. With tickets at only $10, this unmissable event promises an afternoon filled with excitement, creativity, and camaraderie.","chinese":"我很高興宣布，我們一年一度的學校園遊會將於 2021 年 5 月 29 日星期六中午 12 時至下午 4 時舉行。 門票只需 $10，這場不容錯過的活動將為大家帶來一個充滿興奮、創意和同伴情誼的下午。"},{"label":"Event Activities","english":"There will be lively food stalls showcasing both local and international treats, alongside fun-filled games and arts & crafts stations that will challenge your imagination. For those who love the spotlight, we have student performances and a special alumni football match where our former players return to face our current school team. Don’t forget to check out the displays of student work, which highlight the diverse talents here at Hong Kong Banyan School. Best of all, prizes await lucky winners in various competitions!","chinese":"屆時將設有熱鬧的美食攤位，展示本地及國際特色小食，旁邊亦會有充滿樂趣的遊戲和美術工藝攤位，挑戰大家的想像力。 對於喜歡站在舞台焦點之中的同學，我們將安排學生表演，以及一場特別的校友足球賽，屆時昔日球員將重返校園，與現任校隊對壘。 不要忘記參觀學生作品展覽，這些展品將展現香港榕樹學校學生多方面的才華。 最令人期待的是，各項比賽的幸運得獎者將有機會獲得獎品！"},{"label":"Invitation","english":"We warmly invite all past and present pupils, teachers, friends, and family to come along. If you would like to help make this fair even more successful, we need volunteers for setting up booths and managing visitor flow. Simply email Mr. Chris Wong at chriswong@hkbs.edu.hk to sign up.","chinese":"我們誠意邀請所有舊生、在校學生、老師、朋友和家人一同參與。 如果你希望協助我們令這次園遊會更加成功，我們現正招募義工，協助設置攤位及管理訪客人流。 如欲報名，只需電郵至 chriswong@hkbs.edu.hk 聯絡 Chris Wong 先生。"},{"label":"Closing","english":"Mark your calendars and spread the word. We look forward to seeing you all there!","chinese":"請大家記下日期，並把這個消息告訴身邊的人。 我們期待在當天見到大家！"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"be thrilled to announce","chinese":"很高興宣布"},{"english":"annual School Fair","chinese":"一年一度的學校嘉年華"},{"english":"take place on","chinese":"於……舉行"},{"english":"from 12 p.m. to 4 p.m.","chinese":"中午十二時至下午四時"},{"english":"with tickets at only","chinese":"門票只需……"},{"english":"unmissable event","chinese":"不容錯過的活動"},{"english":"promise an afternoon filled with","chinese":"承諾帶來一個充滿……的下午"},{"english":"filled with excitement","chinese":"充滿刺激和興奮"},{"english":"creativity","chinese":"創意"},{"english":"camaraderie","chinese":"友誼；團結情誼"},{"english":"lively food stalls","chinese":"熱鬧的食物攤位"},{"english":"showcase","chinese":"展示；呈現"},{"english":"local and international treats","chinese":"本地及國際美食"},{"english":"alongside","chinese":"與……一同"},{"english":"fun-filled games","chinese":"充滿樂趣的遊戲"},{"english":"arts and crafts stations","chinese":"手工藝攤位"},{"english":"challenge your imagination","chinese":"激發你的想像力"},{"english":"for those who love the spotlight","chinese":"對於喜歡成為焦點的人來說"},{"english":"love the spotlight","chinese":"喜歡成為眾人焦點"},{"english":"student performances","chinese":"學生表演"},{"english":"special alumni football match","chinese":"特別校友足球賽"},{"english":"alumni","chinese":"校友"},{"english":"former players","chinese":"前球員；舊生球員"},{"english":"return to face","chinese":"回來對戰……"},{"english":"current school team","chinese":"現屆校隊"},{"english":"Don't forget to","chinese":"不要忘記……"},{"english":"check out","chinese":"看看；參觀"},{"english":"displays of student work","chinese":"學生作品展覽"},{"english":"highlight","chinese":"突顯"},{"english":"diverse talents","chinese":"多元才華"},{"english":"best of all","chinese":"最好的是"},{"english":"prizes await","chinese":"獎品等待着……"},{"english":"lucky winners","chinese":"幸運得獎者"},{"english":"various competitions","chinese":"各項比賽"},{"english":"warmly invite","chinese":"熱誠邀請"},{"english":"past and present pupils","chinese":"舊生和現屆學生"},{"english":"friends and family","chinese":"朋友和家人"},{"english":"come along","chinese":"一同前來參加"},{"english":"help make this fair even more successful","chinese":"幫助令嘉年華更加成功"},{"english":"need volunteers for","chinese":"需要義工協助……"},{"english":"set up booths","chinese":"設置攤位"},{"english":"manage visitor flow","chinese":"管理人流"},{"english":"simply email","chinese":"只需電郵……"},{"english":"sign up","chinese":"報名"},{"english":"Mark your calendars","chinese":"記下這個日子"},{"english":"spread the word","chinese":"廣傳消息"},{"english":"look forward to seeing you all there","chinese":"期待在那裏見到大家"}]},"dse-writing-2021-part-b-q2":{"exerciseId":"dse-writing-2021-part-b-q2","essayKey":"","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=dse-writing-2021-part-b-q2","flashDeckId":"dse/writing/part-b/2021/Q2","paragraphs":[{"label":"Paragraph 1","english":"Electric Cars Will Sell Only When Going Green Is Made Easy","chinese":"只有當綠色出行變得容易，電動車才會暢銷"},{"label":"Paragraph 2","english":"Dear Editor,","chinese":"尊敬的編輯："},{"label":"Paragraph 3","english":"Although research indicates that electric vehicles are greener than petrol cars, less than 3% of vehicles sold worldwide in 2020 were electric. This contrast should make Hong Kong policymakers, car dealers and drivers reflect on one question: why has an apparently better technology not become a popular choice? I believe the answer is not so much a lack of environmental concern as a lack of everyday confidence. To turn electric cars from a principled purchase into a practical one, society must reduce their cost, remove the inconvenience of charging and rebuild public trust in the technology.","chinese":"雖然研究顯示電動車比汽油車更環保，但在 2020 年，全球售出的車輛中少於 3% 是電動車。 這種反差應該促使香港政策制定者、汽車經銷商和駕駛者反思一個問題：為甚麼一項看似更好的技術，仍未成為受歡迎的選擇？ 我認為，答案與其說是人們缺乏環保意識，不如說是他們缺乏日常使用上的信心。 為了把電動車從一種基於原則的購買選擇，變成一種實際可行的選擇，社會必須降低其成本、消除充電的不便，並重建公眾對這項技術的信任。"},{"label":"Paragraph 4","english":"First, many motorists are put off by the cost. An electric car may be greener for society, but for an individual family it can still look like a financial gamble. The initial price is often higher than that of a petrol car, while future expenses remain uncertain, as is the case in battery replacement, resale value, insurance and specialist repairs, all of which certainly worry potential buyers. Unlike petrol cars, whose running costs and second-hand prices are familiar, electric vehicles are still seen by many as machines with hidden risks. Take a young couple, for example. They may care about roadside pollution, yet choose a cheaper petrol car if an electric model stretches their mortgage budget or requires charging equipment they cannot install. That decision is not hypocrisy; Rather, it is household arithmetic. Unless electric vehicles are financially comparable, the environmental argument will lose to the monthly payment.","chinese":"首先，許多駕駛人士因成本而卻步。 電動車對社會而言也許更環保，但對一個個別家庭來說，它仍可能看似一場財務賭注。 電動車的初始價格往往高於汽油車，而未來開支仍然不確定，例如電池更換、轉售價值、保險和專門維修等，而這些因素都必然令潛在買家感到憂慮 與使用成本和二手價格都為人熟悉的汽油車不同，電動車仍被許多人視為帶有隱藏風險的機器。 以一對年輕夫婦為例。 他們也許關心路邊空氣污染，但如果電動車款令他們的按揭預算更吃緊，或需要安裝他們無法安裝的充電設備，他們仍可能選擇較便宜的汽油車。 這個決定並不是虛偽；更準確地說，它只是家庭財務計算。 除非電動車在價格和成本上能與汽油車相若，否則環保論點將會敗給每月供款"},{"label":"Paragraph 5","english":"Second, battery charging remains the greatest practical barrier. Hong Kong is a city of high-rise buildings and shared car parks, not detached houses with private garages. Even when drivers are willing to switch, they may have nowhere reliable to charge their cars overnight. A petrol car can be refuelled in minutes almost anywhere; by contrast, an electric car may require a working charger, an available parking space and several hours of waiting. For a taxi driver, a delivery van operator or a parent rushing between work and school, that uncertainty translates directly into lost time and stress. More precisely, the question is not only whether electric cars can travel far enough, but whether drivers can fit charging into crowded lives. No wonder many people hesitate: convenience is not a luxury in modern transport; it is the condition on which adoption depends.","chinese":"第二，電池充電仍然是最大的實際障礙。 香港是一個由高樓大廈和共用停車場組成的城市，而不是一個充滿帶私人車房的獨立屋的地方。 即使駕駛者願意轉用電動車，他們也可能沒有可靠的地方讓汽車通宵充電。 汽油車幾乎可以在任何地方於數分鐘內加油；相比之下，電動車可能需要一個可用的充電器、一個可用的泊車位，以及數小時的等待。 對的士司機、客貨車營運者，或一位在工作與學校之間奔波的家長而言，這種不確定性會直接轉化為流失的時間和壓力。 更準確地說，問題不只是電動車能否行駛得足夠遠，而是駕駛者能否把充電安排擠進繁忙的生活之中。 難怪許多人猶豫不決：在現代交通中，便利並不是奢侈品；它是能否被廣泛採用所依賴的條件。"},{"label":"Paragraph 6","english":"Third, electric vehicles still suffer from a trust gap. Many buyers have heard that they are clean, quiet and economical, but few fully understand battery warranties, safety in heavy rain, or long-term savings. Meanwhile, a single story about a broken charger or a degraded battery can spread quickly and make the whole technology look unreliable. In the eyes of the public, uncertainty can be as damaging as actual weakness. Therefore, the government and the motor industry should not merely praise electric cars; they should make the experience transparent. Public test-drive days, clear cost calculators, independent battery-health certificates and honest comparisons between petrol and electric models would help consumers make informed decisions instead of relying on rumours.","chinese":"第三，電動車仍然面對信任落差。 許多買家都聽說電動車潔淨、安靜而且經濟，但很少人充分了解電池保養、暴雨中的安全性，或長遠節省的開支。 與此同時，一個關於充電器故障或電池衰退的故事，便可以迅速傳播，並令整項技術看起來不可靠。 在公眾眼中，不確定性可以和真正的弱點一樣具破壞力。 因此，政府和汽車業界不應只是讚揚電動車；它們應該讓整個使用體驗變得透明。 公共試駕日、清晰的成本計算器、獨立的電池健康狀況證書，以及汽油車與電動車之間的誠實比較，都有助消費者作出知情決定，而不是依賴傳聞。"},{"label":"Paragraph 7","english":"To attract more drivers, Hong Kong needs a coordinated plan rather than scattered incentives. The government should offer targeted subsidies or low-interest green loans for families and commercial drivers, especially those replacing older, more polluting vehicles. At the same time, new residential and commercial buildings should include charging-ready parking spaces, while older estates should receive support to upgrade their electrical systems. Shopping centres, government car parks and transport interchanges should install more fast chargers so that drivers can top up during ordinary activities. Better still, taxis, minibuses and delivery fleets should be encouraged to switch first, because visible commercial vehicles can prove that electric transport works under pressure.","chinese":"為了吸引更多駕駛者，香港需要一個協調一致的計劃，而不是零散的誘因。 政府應為家庭和商用車駕駛者提供針對性的補貼或低息綠色貸款，尤其是那些正在替換較舊、污染較嚴重車輛的人。 同時，新的住宅和商業大廈應包括已預備充電設施的泊車位，而較舊的屋苑則應獲得支援，以升級其電力系統。 商場、政府停車場和交通交匯處應安裝更多快速充電器，好讓駕駛者能在日常活動期間補充電量。 更理想的是，的士、小巴和送貨車隊應首先受到鼓勵轉用電動車，因為可見的商用車輛能證明電動交通在高壓使用情況下也行得通。"},{"label":"Paragraph 8","english":"In conclusion, the low sales of electric vehicles do not prove that people reject green living. Quite the contrary, they show that good intentions are not enough by themselves. If electric cars are to become common, they must be affordable to buy, convenient to charge and trustworthy to own. The government, developers, car dealers and power companies should act together. The future of clean transport will arrive only when choosing the greener car also becomes the easier choice.","chinese":"總結來說，電動車銷量低並不證明人們拒絕綠色生活。 恰恰相反，它們顯示單靠良好意願本身是不足夠的。 如果電動車要變得普及，它們就必須買得起、充電方便，而且擁有起來值得信任。 政府、發展商、汽車經銷商和電力公司應共同採取行動。 只有當選擇較環保的汽車也成為較容易的選擇時，潔淨交通的未來才會到來。"},{"label":"Paragraph 9","english":"Yours faithfully,","chinese":"謹啟"},{"label":"Paragraph 10","english":"Chris Wong","chinese":"Chris Wong"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"going green","chinese":"實踐環保"},{"english":"be made easy","chinese":"變得容易"},{"english":"Dear Editor","chinese":"尊敬的編輯"},{"english":"research indicates that","chinese":"研究顯示"},{"english":"electric vehicles","chinese":"電動車"},{"english":"greener than","chinese":"比……更環保"},{"english":"petrol cars","chinese":"汽油車"},{"english":"vehicles sold worldwide","chinese":"全球售出的車輛"},{"english":"this contrast","chinese":"這種反差"},{"english":"policymakers","chinese":"政策制定者"},{"english":"car dealers","chinese":"車行；汽車經銷商"},{"english":"reflect on","chinese":"反思"},{"english":"apparently better technology","chinese":"看似更好的技術"},{"english":"a popular choice","chinese":"受歡迎的選擇"},{"english":"not so much…as…","chinese":"與其說是……不如說是……"},{"english":"environmental concern","chinese":"環保意識"},{"english":"everyday confidence","chinese":"日常使用上的信心"},{"english":"turn something from…into…","chinese":"把某物由……變成……"},{"english":"a principled purchase","chinese":"基於理念的購買"},{"english":"a practical one","chinese":"實際可行的選擇"},{"english":"reduce their cost","chinese":"降低其成本"},{"english":"remove the inconvenience of","chinese":"消除……的不便"},{"english":"rebuild public trust in","chinese":"重建公眾對……的信任"},{"english":"the technology","chinese":"這項技術"},{"english":"motorists","chinese":"駕駛人士"},{"english":"be put off by","chinese":"因……而卻步"},{"english":"for society","chinese":"對社會而言"},{"english":"an individual family","chinese":"個別家庭"},{"english":"look like a financial gamble","chinese":"看起來像一場財務賭博"},{"english":"initial price","chinese":"初始價格"},{"english":"higher than that of","chinese":"高於……的"},{"english":"future expenses","chinese":"未來開支"},{"english":"remain uncertain","chinese":"仍然不明朗"},{"english":"in areas such as","chinese":"在……等方面"},{"english":"battery replacement","chinese":"更換電池"},{"english":"resale value","chinese":"轉售價值"},{"english":"specialist repairs","chinese":"專門維修"},{"english":"potential buyers","chinese":"潛在買家"},{"english":"running costs","chinese":"日常使用成本"},{"english":"second-hand prices","chinese":"二手價格"},{"english":"be familiar","chinese":"為人熟悉"},{"english":"hidden risks","chinese":"隱藏風險"},{"english":"take…for example","chinese":"以……為例"},{"english":"roadside pollution","chinese":"路邊空氣污染"},{"english":"yet choose","chinese":"但仍然選擇"},{"english":"a cheaper petrol car","chinese":"較便宜的汽油車"},{"english":"electric model","chinese":"電動車款"},{"english":"stretch their mortgage budget","chinese":"令供樓預算吃緊"},{"english":"charging equipment","chinese":"充電設備"},{"english":"cannot install","chinese":"無法安裝"},{"english":"hypocrisy","chinese":"虛偽"},{"english":"rather","chinese":"反而；更準確地說"},{"english":"household arithmetic","chinese":"家庭財務計算"},{"english":"unless","chinese":"除非"},{"english":"financially comparable","chinese":"在價格上可相比"},{"english":"environmental argument","chinese":"環保論點"},{"english":"lose to","chinese":"輸給"},{"english":"monthly payment","chinese":"每月供款"},{"english":"battery charging","chinese":"電池充電"},{"english":"practical barrier","chinese":"實際障礙"},{"english":"high-rise buildings","chinese":"高樓大廈"},{"english":"shared car parks","chinese":"共用停車場"},{"english":"detached houses","chinese":"獨立屋"},{"english":"private garages","chinese":"私家車房"},{"english":"be willing to switch","chinese":"願意轉用"},{"english":"nowhere reliable to","chinese":"沒有可靠地方去……"},{"english":"charge their cars overnight","chinese":"通宵為汽車充電"},{"english":"be refuelled in minutes","chinese":"幾分鐘內加滿燃油"},{"english":"by contrast","chinese":"相比之下"},{"english":"a working charger","chinese":"可正常運作的充電器"},{"english":"an available parking space","chinese":"可用的車位"},{"english":"several hours of waiting","chinese":"幾小時的等待"},{"english":"taxi driver","chinese":"的士司機"},{"english":"delivery van operator","chinese":"送貨客貨車營運者"},{"english":"rush between work and school","chinese":"在工作和學校之間奔波"},{"english":"translate directly into","chinese":"直接變成"},{"english":"lost time and stress","chinese":"浪費的時間和壓力"},{"english":"more precisely","chinese":"更準確地說"},{"english":"not only whether…but whether…","chinese":"不只是是否……而是是否……"},{"english":"travel far enough","chinese":"行駛距離是否足夠"},{"english":"fit charging into","chinese":"把充電安排進……之中"},{"english":"crowded lives","chinese":"忙碌的生活"},{"english":"no wonder","chinese":"難怪"},{"english":"hesitate","chinese":"猶豫"},{"english":"convenience","chinese":"便利"},{"english":"not a luxury","chinese":"不是奢侈品"},{"english":"modern transport","chinese":"現代交通"},{"english":"the condition on which","chinese":"……所依賴的條件"},{"english":"adoption depends","chinese":"採用與否取決於"},{"english":"suffer from","chinese":"受……困擾"},{"english":"a trust gap","chinese":"信任缺口"},{"english":"fully understand","chinese":"充分了解"},{"english":"battery warranties","chinese":"電池保養"},{"english":"safety in heavy rain","chinese":"暴雨中的安全性"},{"english":"long-term savings","chinese":"長遠節省"},{"english":"meanwhile","chinese":"與此同時"},{"english":"a broken charger","chinese":"壞掉的充電器"},{"english":"a degraded battery","chinese":"性能衰退的電池"},{"english":"spread quickly","chinese":"迅速傳開"},{"english":"make something look unreliable","chinese":"令某物看起來不可靠"},{"english":"in the eyes of the public","chinese":"在公眾眼中"},{"english":"actual weakness","chinese":"實際弱點"},{"english":"as damaging as","chinese":"與……一樣具破壞性"},{"english":"therefore","chinese":"因此"},{"english":"the motor industry","chinese":"汽車業"},{"english":"not merely","chinese":"不只是"},{"english":"praise electric cars","chinese":"稱讚電動車"},{"english":"make the experience transparent","chinese":"令體驗透明化"},{"english":"public test-drive days","chinese":"公眾試駕日"},{"english":"clear cost calculators","chinese":"清晰的成本計算器"},{"english":"independent battery-health certificates","chinese":"獨立電池健康證明"},{"english":"honest comparisons between…and…","chinese":"……與……之間的誠實比較"},{"english":"make informed decisions","chinese":"作出知情決定"},{"english":"instead of relying on","chinese":"而不是依賴"},{"english":"rely on rumours","chinese":"依賴傳聞"},{"english":"attract more drivers","chinese":"吸引更多駕駛人士"},{"english":"a coordinated plan","chinese":"協調一致的計劃"},{"english":"rather than","chinese":"而不是"},{"english":"scattered incentives","chinese":"零散的誘因"},{"english":"targeted subsidies","chinese":"針對性資助"},{"english":"low-interest green loans","chinese":"低息綠色貸款"},{"english":"commercial drivers","chinese":"商用車司機"},{"english":"replacing older vehicles","chinese":"更換較舊車輛"},{"english":"more polluting vehicles","chinese":"污染較嚴重的車輛"},{"english":"at the same time","chinese":"與此同時"},{"english":"residential and commercial buildings","chinese":"住宅及商業大廈"},{"english":"charging-ready parking spaces","chinese":"已預留充電設施的車位"},{"english":"older estates","chinese":"較舊屋苑"},{"english":"receive support to","chinese":"獲得支援去……"},{"english":"upgrade their electrical systems","chinese":"升級電力系統"},{"english":"shopping centres","chinese":"商場"},{"english":"government car parks","chinese":"政府停車場"},{"english":"transport interchanges","chinese":"交通交匯處"},{"english":"fast chargers","chinese":"快速充電器"},{"english":"top up","chinese":"補充電量"},{"english":"ordinary activities","chinese":"日常活動"},{"english":"better still","chinese":"更理想的是"},{"english":"delivery fleets","chinese":"送貨車隊"},{"english":"be encouraged to switch first","chinese":"獲鼓勵率先轉用"},{"english":"visible commercial vehicles","chinese":"常見的商用車輛"},{"english":"prove that","chinese":"證明"},{"english":"electric transport","chinese":"電動交通"},{"english":"work under pressure","chinese":"在壓力下仍能運作"},{"english":"in conclusion","chinese":"總括而言"},{"english":"low sales","chinese":"銷量低"},{"english":"prove that","chinese":"證明"},{"english":"reject green living","chinese":"拒絕環保生活"},{"english":"quite the contrary","chinese":"正好相反"},{"english":"good intentions","chinese":"良好意願"},{"english":"by themselves","chinese":"單靠本身"},{"english":"become common","chinese":"變得普遍"},{"english":"affordable to buy","chinese":"買得起"},{"english":"convenient to charge","chinese":"充電方便"},{"english":"trustworthy to own","chinese":"擁有起來令人放心"},{"english":"act together","chinese":"共同採取行動"},{"english":"power companies","chinese":"電力公司"},{"english":"the future of clean transport","chinese":"清潔交通的未來"},{"english":"choosing the greener car","chinese":"選擇較環保的車"},{"english":"the easier choice","chinese":"較容易的選擇"},{"english":"Yours faithfully","chinese":"謹啟"}]},"dse-writing-2021-part-b-q3":{"exerciseId":"dse-writing-2021-part-b-q3","essayKey":"","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=dse-writing-2021-part-b-q3","flashDeckId":"dse/writing/part-b/2021/Q3","paragraphs":[{"label":"Paragraph 1","english":"To: Ms Lin, Sales Manager","chinese":""},{"label":"Paragraph 2","english":"From: Chris Wong, Sales Department","chinese":"銷售部"},{"label":"Paragraph 3","english":"Subject: A Fairer Returns Policy That Protects Customers and Fast Fashion","chinese":"主旨：一項既保障顧客亦保障 Fast Fashion 的更公平退貨政策"},{"label":"Paragraph 4","english":"Dear Ms Lin,","chinese":""},{"label":"Paragraph 5","english":"Following the recent rise in customer complaints about our no-exchange/no-refund policy, I am writing as a member of the sales department to recommend a carefully controlled revision. The aim is not to give away profit, but to reduce frustration, rebuild confidence and protect repeat business. In my view, the current policy should be changed. A limited, evidence-based exchange and refund system would be fairer to customers and still safe from abuse if clear safeguards are built in.","chinese":"在最近顧客對我們不設換貨／退款政策的投訴增加之後，我謹以銷售部成員的身份寫信，建議公司作出一項經審慎控制的修訂。 目的並不是要犧牲利潤，而是要減少顧客的不滿、重建信心，並保護回頭客生意。 在我看來，現行政策應該作出改變。 如果加入清晰的保障措施，一套有限度、以證據為基礎的換貨及退款制度，會對顧客更公平，同時仍然可以避免被濫用。 銷售部"},{"label":"Paragraph 6","english":"At issue is not whether customers should be allowed to change their minds without limit, but whether our present rule is proportionate for online fashion. Unlike shoppers in a physical boutique, our customers cannot try on a dress, feel the fabric or compare two sizes in front of a mirror. They rely on photos, size charts and delivery accuracy. If a blouse arrives with sleeves far longer than expected, or a pair of jeans fits differently from the chart, the customer feels punished for trusting us. At first glance, a strict policy saves handling costs; on closer inspection, it turns ordinary sizing problems into arguments, negative reviews and lost repeat purchases. A disappointed first-time customer may abandon her cart next time and warn friends in group chats. In a market where alternatives are one click away, keeping the rule unchanged risks costing us more than it saves.","chinese":"問題的核心並不是顧客是否應該被允許無限制地改變主意，而是我們現行的規則對網上時裝業而言是否合乎比例。 與實體時裝店的顧客不同，我們的顧客不能試穿裙子、觸摸布料，或在鏡子前比較兩個尺碼。 他們只能依靠照片、尺碼表和送貨準確度。 如果一件女裝上衣送到時袖子比預期長得多，或者一條牛仔褲的穿著效果與尺碼表不符，顧客便會覺得自己因信任我們而受到懲罰。 乍看之下，嚴格的政策可以節省處理成本；但仔細一看，它卻會把普通的尺碼問題變成爭執、負評和流失的回購。 一位失望的首次顧客，下一次可能會放棄購物車，並在群組聊天中提醒朋友不要光顧。 在一個替代選擇只需點擊一下便可取得的市場中，維持這項規則不變，可能令我們損失的比節省的更多。"},{"label":"Paragraph 7","english":"In addition, the policy leaves our team with little room to resolve fair cases. Recently, we have had to repeat “sorry, nothing can be done” even when customers reported a defective zip, a wrong colour or a size guide that clearly misled them. This makes us look as though we are hiding behind fine print rather than serving customers. I suggest replacing the blanket ban with a conditional fourteen-day policy. Customers should be allowed one exchange for size or colour if the item is unworn and unwashed. Refunds should be available only when the item is defective, wrongly delivered or materially different from its description. For simple change-of-mind cases, store credit would be more suitable than cash refunds. Final-sale items, underwear, earrings and other hygiene-sensitive goods should remain non-returnable, provided that this is clearly stated before payment. Return postage could be paid by customers for ordinary exchanges, but by Fast Fashion when the fault is ours. Such a system would give genuine customers a fair remedy without turning returns into free wardrobe rental.","chinese":"此外，這項政策令我們的團隊幾乎沒有空間處理合理個案。 最近，即使顧客投訴拉鏈有問題、顏色錯誤，或尺碼指南明顯誤導了他們，我們也只能不斷重複「抱歉，我們無能為力」。 這使我們看起來好像是在躲在細則背後，而不是在服務顧客。 我建議以一項有條件的十四天政策，取代現時一刀切的禁制規定。 如果貨品未曾穿著及清洗，顧客應可因尺碼或顏色問題獲准換貨一次。 只有在貨品有瑕疵、送錯，或與描述有實質差異時，才應提供退款。 對於單純改變主意的個案，店舖積分會比現金退款更合適。 特價清貨貨品、內衣、耳環和其他涉及衛生風險的商品，應繼續不可退換，但前提是付款前必須清楚列明。 一般換貨的退貨郵費可由顧客承擔，但若錯誤在於 Fast Fashion，郵費則應由公司支付。 這樣的制度可以給真正有需要的顧客一個公平的補救方法，同時不會把退貨變成免費租衣服務。"},{"label":"Paragraph 8","english":"Granted, a more flexible policy may encourage abuse. Some customers may wear a dress once for a party and send it back; others may order several sizes with no intention of keeping more than one. However, to acknowledge the risk is not to concede that the policy should remain unchanged. We can prevent misuse by designing the policy carefully. First, every return request should require an order number, a reason and, where relevant, clear photos. Secondly, refunds or credits should be issued only after warehouse staff have inspected the item for missing tags, stains, perfume, make-up marks or damage. Thirdly, each discretionary exchange could be limited to two items per customer within thirty days, with unusual return patterns flagged for review. Better still, we could use tamper-evident tags on higher-risk items; once removed, the item would no longer qualify for return. Finally, customers should tick a short acknowledgement of the conditions at checkout so that nobody can claim surprise later.","chinese":"誠然，一項較具彈性的政策可能會鼓勵濫用。 有些顧客可能會為了一場派對穿一次裙子後便退回；另一些人則可能訂購多個尺碼，卻從一開始就沒有打算留下超過一件。 然而，承認風險存在，並不等於承認政策應該維持不變。 我們可以透過仔細設計政策來防止濫用。 首先，每宗退貨申請都應要求顧客提供訂單編號、原因，以及在相關情況下提供清晰照片。 第二，退款或積分應只在倉務員工檢查貨品是否有吊牌遺失、污漬、香水味、化妝痕跡或損壞後才發出。 第三，每位顧客在三十天內可酌情換貨的貨品數量可限制為兩件，而異常退貨模式則應被標記作進一步審查。 更理想的是，我們可以在較高風險的貨品上使用防拆標籤；一旦標籤被移除，該貨品便不再符合退貨資格。 最後，顧客在付款時應勾選一份簡短的條款確認聲明，這樣之後便沒有人可以聲稱自己事前不知情。"},{"label":"Paragraph 9","english":"All things considered, I strongly recommend a three-month pilot of this revised policy. The current rule was perhaps introduced to protect our margins, but the way things are going, it is becoming a source of avoidable distrust. If we adopt a controlled exchange and refund system, the sales, customer service and warehouse teams should agree on standard scripts, inspection criteria and reporting procedures. After the pilot, we can review complaint volume, repeat purchases and return rates before making a permanent decision. What matters is balance - we should be firm against abuse, but fair to honest customers. I would appreciate it if you could raise this proposal at the next management meeting.","chinese":"綜合考慮各方面因素，我強烈建議先試行這項修訂政策三個月。 現行規則當初也許是為了保障我們的利潤率而設，但按目前情況發展下去，它正逐漸成為一個本可避免的不信任來源。 如果我們採用一套受控的換貨及退款制度，銷售、客戶服務和倉務團隊應就標準回覆用語、檢查準則和匯報程序達成共識。 試行期結束後，我們可以檢視投訴數量、回購情況和退貨率，然後才作出永久決定。 最重要的是取得平衡：我們應堅決防止濫用，但也要公平對待誠實的顧客。 如你能在下一次管理層會議上提出這項建議，我將不勝感激。"},{"label":"Paragraph 10","english":"Yours sincerely,","chinese":"謹啟"},{"label":"Paragraph 11","english":"Chris Wong","chinese":""},{"label":"Paragraph 12","english":"Sales Department","chinese":"寄件人：Alex Lee，銷售部 在最近顧客對我們不設換貨／退款政策的投訴增加之後，我謹以銷售部成員的身份寫信，建議公司作出一項經審慎控制的修訂。 銷售部"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"Sales Manager","chinese":"銷售經理"},{"english":"Sales Department","chinese":"銷售部"},{"english":"returns policy","chinese":"退貨政策"},{"english":"protect customers and the business","chinese":"保障顧客及業務"},{"english":"following the recent rise in","chinese":"鑑於最近……增加"},{"english":"customer complaints","chinese":"顧客投訴"},{"english":"no-exchange, no-refund policy","chinese":"不設換貨、不設退款政策"},{"english":"as a member of","chinese":"作為……的一員"},{"english":"recommend a revision","chinese":"建議作出修訂"},{"english":"carefully controlled revision","chinese":"經過嚴格控制的修訂"},{"english":"the aim is not to…, but to…","chinese":"目的不是……，而是……"},{"english":"sacrifice profit","chinese":"犧牲利潤"},{"english":"reduce frustration","chinese":"減少不滿"},{"english":"rebuild confidence","chinese":"重建信心"},{"english":"protect repeat business","chinese":"保住回頭客生意"},{"english":"in my view","chinese":"在我看來"},{"english":"a limited system","chinese":"有限制的制度"},{"english":"evidence-based","chinese":"以證據為本的"},{"english":"exchange and refund system","chinese":"換貨及退款制度"},{"english":"safe from abuse","chinese":"可避免被濫用"},{"english":"safeguards","chinese":"保障措施；防範措施"},{"english":"built in","chinese":"內置；加入"},{"english":"at issue is not whether…, but whether…","chinese":"問題不在於是否……，而在於是否……"},{"english":"change their minds","chinese":"改變主意"},{"english":"without limit","chinese":"無限制地"},{"english":"present rule","chinese":"現行規則"},{"english":"proportionate for","chinese":"對……而言合乎比例"},{"english":"online fashion","chinese":"網上時裝"},{"english":"unlike shoppers in","chinese":"不像……的顧客"},{"english":"physical boutique","chinese":"實體精品店"},{"english":"try on","chinese":"試穿"},{"english":"feel the fabric","chinese":"觸摸布料"},{"english":"compare two sizes","chinese":"比較兩個尺碼"},{"english":"in front of a mirror","chinese":"在鏡子前"},{"english":"rely on","chinese":"依賴"},{"english":"size charts","chinese":"尺碼表"},{"english":"delivery accuracy","chinese":"送貨準確度"},{"english":"far longer than expected","chinese":"比預期長得多"},{"english":"fit differently from","chinese":"與……的合身程度不同"},{"english":"feel punished for","chinese":"因……而覺得受罰"},{"english":"at first glance","chinese":"乍看之下"},{"english":"handling costs","chinese":"處理成本"},{"english":"on closer inspection","chinese":"仔細看來"},{"english":"turn problems into arguments","chinese":"將問題變成爭拗"},{"english":"ordinary sizing problems","chinese":"普通尺碼問題"},{"english":"negative reviews","chinese":"負面評價"},{"english":"lost repeat purchases","chinese":"流失的回購"},{"english":"disappointed first-time customer","chinese":"失望的首次顧客"},{"english":"abandon her cart","chinese":"放棄購物車"},{"english":"warn friends","chinese":"提醒朋友；警告朋友"},{"english":"group chats","chinese":"群組聊天"},{"english":"alternatives are one click away","chinese":"替代選擇只需一按"},{"english":"keeping the rule unchanged","chinese":"保持規則不變"},{"english":"cost more than it saves","chinese":"得不償失"},{"english":"in addition","chinese":"此外"},{"english":"leave someone with little room to","chinese":"令某人幾乎沒有空間去……"},{"english":"resolve fair cases","chinese":"處理合理個案"},{"english":"defective zip","chinese":"有問題的拉鏈"},{"english":"wrong colour","chinese":"錯誤顏色"},{"english":"size guide","chinese":"尺碼指南"},{"english":"mislead someone","chinese":"誤導某人"},{"english":"look as though","chinese":"看起來好像"},{"english":"hide behind fine print","chinese":"躲在細則背後"},{"english":"fine print","chinese":"細則；小字條款"},{"english":"serve customers","chinese":"服務顧客"},{"english":"replace the blanket ban with","chinese":"以……取代一刀切禁令"},{"english":"blanket ban","chinese":"一刀切禁令"},{"english":"conditional fourteen-day policy","chinese":"有條件的十四日政策"},{"english":"one exchange","chinese":"一次換貨"},{"english":"size or colour","chinese":"尺碼或顏色"},{"english":"unworn and unwashed","chinese":"未穿過及未洗過"},{"english":"refunds should be available only when","chinese":"退款只應在……情況下提供"},{"english":"defective","chinese":"有瑕疵的"},{"english":"wrongly delivered","chinese":"送錯的"},{"english":"materially different from","chinese":"與……有重大差異"},{"english":"product description","chinese":"產品描述"},{"english":"change-of-mind cases","chinese":"改變主意的個案"},{"english":"store credit","chinese":"店舖購物金"},{"english":"cash refunds","chinese":"現金退款"},{"english":"final-sale items","chinese":"清貨不設退換貨品"},{"english":"hygiene-sensitive goods","chinese":"涉及衞生問題的貨品"},{"english":"remain non-returnable","chinese":"維持不可退貨"},{"english":"provided that","chinese":"只要；前提是"},{"english":"clearly stated before payment","chinese":"付款前清楚列明"},{"english":"return postage","chinese":"退貨郵費"},{"english":"ordinary exchanges","chinese":"一般換貨"},{"english":"when the fault is ours","chinese":"當錯在我們一方"},{"english":"genuine customers","chinese":"真正有需要的顧客"},{"english":"fair remedy","chinese":"公平補救方法"},{"english":"turn returns into","chinese":"將退貨變成……"},{"english":"free wardrobe rental","chinese":"免費租衫"},{"english":"granted","chinese":"誠然"},{"english":"flexible policy","chinese":"較靈活的政策"},{"english":"encourage abuse","chinese":"鼓勵濫用"},{"english":"wear something once","chinese":"只穿一次"},{"english":"send it back","chinese":"寄回；退回"},{"english":"order several sizes","chinese":"訂購多個尺碼"},{"english":"with no intention of","chinese":"無意……"},{"english":"acknowledge the risk","chinese":"承認風險"},{"english":"concede that","chinese":"承認"},{"english":"remain unchanged","chinese":"維持不變"},{"english":"prevent misuse","chinese":"防止濫用"},{"english":"return request","chinese":"退貨申請"},{"english":"order number","chinese":"訂單編號"},{"english":"where relevant","chinese":"在相關情況下"},{"english":"clear photos","chinese":"清晰相片"},{"english":"refunds or credits","chinese":"退款或購物金"},{"english":"issued only after","chinese":"只在……之後發出"},{"english":"warehouse staff","chinese":"倉務職員"},{"english":"inspect the item","chinese":"檢查貨品"},{"english":"missing tags","chinese":"吊牌遺失"},{"english":"make-up marks","chinese":"化妝痕跡"},{"english":"discretionary exchange","chinese":"酌情換貨"},{"english":"be limited to","chinese":"限於"},{"english":"per customer","chinese":"每名顧客"},{"english":"within thirty days","chinese":"三十日內"},{"english":"unusual return patterns","chinese":"異常退貨模式"},{"english":"flagged for review","chinese":"標記作審查"},{"english":"better still","chinese":"更好的是"},{"english":"tamper-evident tags","chinese":"防拆封吊牌"},{"english":"higher-risk items","chinese":"較高風險貨品"},{"english":"once removed","chinese":"一經移除"},{"english":"no longer qualify for","chinese":"不再符合……資格"},{"english":"tick an acknowledgement","chinese":"勾選確認聲明"},{"english":"conditions at checkout","chinese":"結帳時的條款"},{"english":"claim surprise later","chinese":"事後聲稱不知情"},{"english":"all things considered","chinese":"綜合而言"},{"english":"strongly recommend","chinese":"強烈建議"},{"english":"three-month pilot","chinese":"三個月試行計劃"},{"english":"revised policy","chinese":"經修訂的政策"},{"english":"protect our margins","chinese":"保障我們的利潤率"},{"english":"the way things are going","chinese":"按目前情況來看"},{"english":"a source of avoidable distrust","chinese":"可避免的不信任來源"},{"english":"adopt a controlled system","chinese":"採用受控的制度"},{"english":"customer service","chinese":"客戶服務"},{"english":"standard scripts","chinese":"標準應對稿"},{"english":"inspection criteria","chinese":"檢查準則"},{"english":"reporting procedures","chinese":"匯報程序"},{"english":"review complaint volume","chinese":"檢視投訴量"},{"english":"repeat purchases","chinese":"回購"},{"english":"return rates","chinese":"退貨率"},{"english":"make a permanent decision","chinese":"作出永久決定"},{"english":"what matters is balance","chinese":"重要的是取得平衡"},{"english":"firm against abuse","chinese":"對濫用行為堅決"},{"english":"fair to honest customers","chinese":"對誠實顧客公平"},{"english":"raise this proposal","chinese":"提出這項建議"},{"english":"management meeting","chinese":"管理層會議"},{"english":"Yours sincerely","chinese":"謹啟"}]},"dse-writing-2021-part-b-q4":{"exerciseId":"dse-writing-2021-part-b-q4","essayKey":"","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=dse-writing-2021-part-b-q4","flashDeckId":"dse/writing/part-b/2021/Q4","paragraphs":[{"label":"Paragraph 1","english":"Application for the Position of Assistant Coach","chinese":"助理教練職位申請"},{"label":"Paragraph 2","english":"Dear Sir/Madam,","chinese":"尊敬的先生／女士："},{"label":"Paragraph 3","english":"I am writing to apply for the position of Assistant Coach at the Hong Kong Sports Foundation. Having spent the past twelve years as a professional middle-distance runner, I am now seeking a career change that will allow me to remain in the world of elite sport while contributing more directly to the development of other athletes. What matters in high-performance sport is not talent alone, but the environment in which that talent is trained, tested and protected. With my athletic background, practical knowledge of competition, and commitment to youth development, I believe I am well suited to support the Foundation’s mission.","chinese":"本人謹此來函申請香港體育基金會助理教練一職。 在過去十二年中，我一直是一名職業中距離跑手；如今，我正尋求一次職業轉變，希望能繼續留在精英體育的世界，同時更直接地為其他運動員的發展作出貢獻。 在高水平競技體育中，真正重要的並不只是天賦本身，而是讓天賦得以被訓練、被考驗和被保護的環境。 憑藉我的運動員背景、對比賽的實際認識，以及對青年發展的承諾，我相信自己非常適合支持貴基金會的使命。"},{"label":"Paragraph 4","english":"By way of background, I began formal athletics training at the age of thirteen and later represented Hong Kong in regional and international competitions, including the Asian Junior Athletics Championships and several invitation meets in Japan, Taiwan and Singapore. As captain of my club team, I learned to perform under pressure, communicate with coaches and physiotherapists, and support younger teammates who were adjusting to the demands of elite sport. At one point, I trained twice a day while completing my university studies, so I understand the balance between ambition, discipline and recovery. These experiences have made me not merely a strong competitor, but a person of resilience, patience and responsibility.","chinese":"作為背景介紹，我在十三歲時開始接受正式田徑訓練，其後代表香港參加地區及國際賽事，包括亞洲青年田徑錦標賽，以及在日本、台灣和新加坡舉行的數項邀請賽。 作為我所屬俱樂部隊伍的隊長，我學會了如何在壓力下表現、與教練及物理治療師溝通，並支援正在適應精英體育要求的年輕隊友。 有一段時間，我一邊完成大學課程，一邊每天訓練兩次，因此我明白抱負、紀律與恢復之間需要取得平衡。 這些經歷使我不僅成為一名強大的競賽者，也成為一個具備韌性、耐性和責任感的人。"},{"label":"Paragraph 5","english":"I am particularly interested in the duty of designing training programmes for elite athletes. During my career, I worked with periodised training plans covering endurance, speed work, strength conditioning, injury prevention and tapering before major events. More importantly, I came to understand why the same plan cannot serve every athlete. For example, a sprinter returning from a hamstring injury may need a progressive programme built around mobility and acceleration mechanics, whereas a distance runner preparing for a championship requires carefully managed mileage and recovery. If appointed, I would help design evidence-informed, athlete-centred programmes, using performance records, training diaries and regular feedback to ensure that every session has a clear purpose.","chinese":"我尤其對為精英運動員設計訓練計劃這項職責感興趣。 在我的職業生涯中，我曾接觸週期化訓練計劃，內容涵蓋耐力、速度訓練、肌力體能訓練、傷患預防，以及大型賽事前的減量調整。 更重要的是，我逐漸明白為甚麼同一套訓練計劃不能適用於每一位運動員。 例如，一名剛從腿後肌傷患中恢復的短跑運動員，可能需要一套以活動能力和加速動作力學為核心的漸進式計劃；然而，一名正準備錦標賽的長跑運動員，則需要被仔細管理的跑量和恢復安排。 如獲聘任，我將協助設計以證據為基礎、以運動員為中心的訓練計劃，並運用表現記錄、訓練日誌和定期回饋，確保每一節訓練都有清晰目的。"},{"label":"Paragraph 6","english":"I am also confident that I could assist in organising international sporting competitions. As an athlete, I have seen how much invisible work lies behind a successful event, such as transport, accommodation, warm-up facilities, equipment checks, volunteer coordination, safety arrangements and communication with visiting teams. Small mistakes can unsettle athletes, while careful planning allows them to focus on performance. In previous club competitions, I helped liaise with overseas teams, brief junior volunteers and solve last-minute scheduling problems. Those responsibilities taught me to stay calm, think step by step and leave nothing to chance. I would bring the same professionalism to events organised by the Foundation.","chinese":"我亦有信心能夠協助籌辦國際體育賽事。 作為運動員，我親眼見過一項成功賽事背後包含多少幕後工作，例如交通、住宿、熱身設施、器材檢查、義工協調、安全安排，以及與到訪隊伍的溝通 細小的失誤可以令運動員感到不安，而周詳的規劃則能讓他們專注於表現。 在過往的俱樂部賽事中，我曾協助與海外隊伍聯絡、向年輕義工簡介工作，並處理最後一刻出現的賽程問題。 這些責任教會我保持冷靜、按部就班地思考，並且不把任何細節交給運氣。 我會把同樣的專業態度帶到貴基金會所舉辦的活動之中。"},{"label":"Paragraph 7","english":"Equally important is the responsibility to identify and support local talent. Hong Kong has many promising young athletes whose potential may remain unnoticed simply because they lack guidance, confidence or access to the right pathway. I have volunteered in school athletics clinics in Sha Tin and Tuen Mun, where I saw students with raw speed, courage and curiosity. However, early success does not necessarily mean long-term development. Young athletes need technical coaching, mental support and realistic advice about education, family expectations and injury management. As someone who has lived through these challenges, I can build trust with them and their parents. I would be eager to assist with talent days, school outreach, mentorship schemes and follow-up training plans so that potential is not wasted.","chinese":"同樣重要的，是發掘並支援本地人才的責任。 香港有許多有前途的年輕運動員，他們的潛能可能只因缺乏指導、信心或合適的發展途徑而一直未被發現。 我曾在沙田和屯門的學校田徑訓練班擔任義工，在那裡我見到一些學生具備原始速度、勇氣和好奇心。 然而，早期成功並不一定代表長遠發展。 年輕運動員需要技術指導、心理支援，以及關於教育、家庭期望和傷患管理的務實建議。 作為一個親身經歷過這些挑戰的人，我能夠與他們及其父母建立信任。 我非常願意協助選材日、學校外展、師友計劃和跟進訓練計劃，好讓潛能不被浪費。"},{"label":"Paragraph 8","english":"In addition, I can communicate fluently in English, Cantonese and Putonghua, which would be useful when working with local athletes and international guests. I am organised, punctual and used to working in a team where coaches, medical staff and administrators must support one another. I do not see coaching as giving instructions from the side of a track; rather, I see it as creating the conditions in which athletes can train bravely, compete wisely and stand tall whatever the result may be.","chinese":"此外，我能流利地以英語、廣東話和普通話溝通，這在與本地運動員及國際嘉賓合作時將會十分有用。 我做事有條理、守時，並且習慣在一個教練、醫療人員和行政人員必須互相支援的團隊中工作。 我並不把教練工作視為站在跑道旁發出指示；更準確地說，我認為教練工作是創造一種條件，讓運動員能勇敢地訓練、明智地比賽，並且無論結果如何都能昂首挺胸。"},{"label":"Paragraph 9","english":"I enclose my curriculum vitae for your consideration. I would appreciate the opportunity to attend an interview and explain in greater detail how my experience could benefit the Hong Kong Sports Foundation. Thank you for considering my application. I look forward to hearing from you.","chinese":"現隨函附上本人的履歷，供閣下考慮。 如能獲得面試機會，讓我更詳細地說明我的經驗如何能夠為香港體育基金會帶來貢獻，我將不勝感激。 感謝閣下考慮我的申請。 期待收到閣下的回覆。"},{"label":"Paragraph 10","english":"Yours faithfully,","chinese":"謹啟"},{"label":"Paragraph 11","english":"Chris Wong","chinese":""}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"apply for the position of","chinese":"申請……職位"},{"english":"Assistant Coach","chinese":"助理教練"},{"english":"having spent","chinese":"在……之後；花了……之後"},{"english":"professional middle-distance runner","chinese":"職業中距離跑手"},{"english":"seek a career change","chinese":"尋求轉行；轉換事業方向"},{"english":"remain in the world of","chinese":"留在……的領域"},{"english":"elite sport","chinese":"精英體育"},{"english":"contribute more directly to","chinese":"更直接地貢獻於……"},{"english":"the development of other athletes","chinese":"其他運動員的發展"},{"english":"high-performance sport","chinese":"高水平競技體育"},{"english":"talent alone","chinese":"單靠天分"},{"english":"the environment in which","chinese":"……所在的環境"},{"english":"trained, tested and protected","chinese":"受訓練、受考驗和受保護"},{"english":"athletic background","chinese":"運動員背景"},{"english":"practical knowledge of competition","chinese":"實戰比賽知識"},{"english":"commitment to youth development","chinese":"對青年發展的承諾"},{"english":"be well suited to","chinese":"非常適合"},{"english":"support the Foundation's mission","chinese":"支持基金會的使命"},{"english":"by way of background","chinese":"作為背景資料"},{"english":"formal athletics training","chinese":"正規田徑訓練"},{"english":"at the age of","chinese":"在……歲時"},{"english":"represent Hong Kong","chinese":"代表香港"},{"english":"regional and international competitions","chinese":"區域及國際比賽"},{"english":"invitation meets","chinese":"邀請賽"},{"english":"as captain of","chinese":"作為……隊長"},{"english":"perform under pressure","chinese":"在壓力下表現"},{"english":"communicate with","chinese":"與……溝通"},{"english":"physiotherapists","chinese":"物理治療師"},{"english":"support younger teammates","chinese":"支持年輕隊友"},{"english":"adjust to the demands of","chinese":"適應……的要求"},{"english":"trained twice a day","chinese":"每日訓練兩次"},{"english":"completing university studies","chinese":"完成大學學業"},{"english":"balance between ambition, discipline and recovery","chinese":"雄心、紀律與恢復之間的平衡"},{"english":"resilience, patience and responsibility","chinese":"抗逆力、耐性和責任感"},{"english":"be particularly interested in","chinese":"對……特別感興趣"},{"english":"the duty of designing","chinese":"設計……的職責"},{"english":"training programmes","chinese":"訓練計劃"},{"english":"elite athletes","chinese":"精英運動員"},{"english":"periodised training plans","chinese":"分期訓練計劃"},{"english":"endurance","chinese":"耐力"},{"english":"speed work","chinese":"速度訓練"},{"english":"strength conditioning","chinese":"體能及力量訓練"},{"english":"injury prevention","chinese":"預防受傷"},{"english":"tapering before major events","chinese":"大賽前減量調整"},{"english":"came to understand why","chinese":"逐漸明白為何"},{"english":"the same plan cannot serve every athlete","chinese":"同一個計劃不能適用於每位運動員"},{"english":"returning from a hamstring injury","chinese":"腿後肌受傷後復出"},{"english":"a progressive programme","chinese":"漸進式計劃"},{"english":"built around","chinese":"以……為核心設計"},{"english":"mobility","chinese":"活動能力；關節靈活度"},{"english":"acceleration mechanics","chinese":"加速動作機制"},{"english":"preparing for a championship","chinese":"備戰錦標賽"},{"english":"carefully managed mileage","chinese":"妥善控制的跑量"},{"english":"evidence-informed","chinese":"以證據為本的"},{"english":"athlete-centred programmes","chinese":"以運動員為中心的計劃"},{"english":"performance records","chinese":"表現紀錄"},{"english":"training diaries","chinese":"訓練日誌"},{"english":"regular feedback","chinese":"定期回饋"},{"english":"every session has a clear purpose","chinese":"每節訓練都有明確目的"},{"english":"be confident that","chinese":"有信心"},{"english":"assist in organising","chinese":"協助籌辦"},{"english":"international sporting competitions","chinese":"國際體育賽事"},{"english":"invisible work lies behind","chinese":"背後有很多看不見的工作"},{"english":"a successful event","chinese":"成功的活動；成功的賽事"},{"english":"transport and accommodation","chinese":"交通及住宿安排"},{"english":"warm-up facilities","chinese":"熱身設施"},{"english":"equipment checks","chinese":"器材檢查"},{"english":"volunteer coordination","chinese":"義工協調"},{"english":"safety arrangements","chinese":"安全安排"},{"english":"communication with visiting teams","chinese":"與到訪隊伍溝通"},{"english":"unsettle athletes","chinese":"令運動員不安"},{"english":"focus on performance","chinese":"專注於表現"},{"english":"club competitions","chinese":"會內比賽"},{"english":"liaise with overseas teams","chinese":"與海外隊伍聯絡"},{"english":"brief junior volunteers","chinese":"向年輕義工簡介工作"},{"english":"last-minute scheduling problems","chinese":"臨時賽程問題"},{"english":"stay calm","chinese":"保持冷靜"},{"english":"think step by step","chinese":"逐步思考"},{"english":"leave nothing to chance","chinese":"不把事情交給運氣；事事預先準備"},{"english":"bring the same professionalism to","chinese":"把同樣的專業態度帶到……"},{"english":"equally important","chinese":"同樣重要的是"},{"english":"identify and support local talent","chinese":"發掘並支援本地人才"},{"english":"promising young athletes","chinese":"有潛質的年輕運動員"},{"english":"remain unnoticed","chinese":"未被注意；被忽略"},{"english":"lack guidance","chinese":"缺乏指導"},{"english":"access to the right pathway","chinese":"接觸合適發展途徑的機會"},{"english":"volunteered in school athletics clinics","chinese":"在學校田徑訓練班做義工"},{"english":"raw speed","chinese":"天然速度；未經雕琢的速度"},{"english":"courage and curiosity","chinese":"勇氣和好奇心"},{"english":"early success","chinese":"早期成功"},{"english":"long-term development","chinese":"長遠發展"},{"english":"technical coaching","chinese":"技術指導"},{"english":"mental support","chinese":"心理支援"},{"english":"realistic advice about","chinese":"關於……的實際建議"},{"english":"family expectations","chinese":"家庭期望"},{"english":"injury management","chinese":"傷患管理"},{"english":"lived through these challenges","chinese":"親身經歷過這些挑戰"},{"english":"build trust with","chinese":"與……建立信任"},{"english":"be eager to assist with","chinese":"渴望協助"},{"english":"talent days","chinese":"人才選拔日"},{"english":"school outreach","chinese":"學校外展"},{"english":"mentorship schemes","chinese":"導師計劃"},{"english":"follow-up training plans","chinese":"跟進訓練計劃"},{"english":"potential is not wasted","chinese":"才能不被浪費"},{"english":"communicate fluently in","chinese":"能流利地以……溝通"},{"english":"Cantonese and Putonghua","chinese":"廣東話和普通話"},{"english":"international guests","chinese":"國際來賓"},{"english":"organised, punctual and used to","chinese":"有條理、守時並習慣於"},{"english":"working in a team","chinese":"團隊合作"},{"english":"medical staff","chinese":"醫療團隊"},{"english":"administrators","chinese":"行政人員"},{"english":"support one another","chinese":"互相支援"},{"english":"giving instructions from the side of a track","chinese":"在跑道旁發號施令"},{"english":"creating the conditions in which","chinese":"創造讓……能夠……的條件"},{"english":"train bravely","chinese":"勇敢地訓練"},{"english":"compete wisely","chinese":"明智地比賽"},{"english":"stand tall","chinese":"昂然面對；保持自信"},{"english":"whatever the result may be","chinese":"無論結果如何"},{"english":"I enclose my curriculum vitae","chinese":"隨函附上我的履歷"},{"english":"for your consideration","chinese":"供你考慮"},{"english":"appreciate the opportunity to","chinese":"感激有機會……"},{"english":"attend an interview","chinese":"出席面試"},{"english":"explain in greater detail","chinese":"更詳細地解釋"},{"english":"benefit the Foundation","chinese":"使基金會受益"},{"english":"Thank you for considering my application","chinese":"感謝你考慮我的申請"},{"english":"I look forward to hearing from you","chinese":"期待你的回覆"},{"english":"Yours faithfully","chinese":"謹啟"}]},"dse-writing-2021-part-b-q5":{"exerciseId":"dse-writing-2021-part-b-q5","essayKey":"","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=dse-writing-2021-part-b-q5","flashDeckId":"dse/writing/part-b/2021/Q5","paragraphs":[{"label":"Paragraph 1","english":"In an age when a phone screen has become both a shopping mall and a conversation, advertising no longer waits between television programmes. It slips into daily routines, livestreams and “ honest reviews”. Since surveys show that many millennials trust influencers more than traditional advertisements, companies are increasingly tempted to use personal recommendations to sell products in order to make marketing appear warmer and more believable. As far as I am concerned, social media influencers are not more trustworthy than traditional media advertisements. They may be more relatable and persuasive, but trust should rest not on familiarity, but on transparency, accountability and evidence.","chinese":""},{"label":"Paragraph 2","english":"The first reason is that influencer marketing often blurs the line between personal recommendation and paid promotion. A traditional advertisement, whether on television, in a newspaper or on a billboard, normally announces itself openly as an advertisement. The audience is well informed that a company is trying to sell something, so they can watch with caution. By contrast, an influencer’s promotion is often placed inside ordinary-looking content: a morning routine, a “what I eat in a day” video, a travel vlog or a livestream chat. After following the same creator for months, viewers may feel as if they know that person personally. That emotional closeness makes the message sound like friendly advice instead of commercial persuasion. Take a skincare influencer, for example. When she says, “This serum saved my skin,” followers may focus on her confidence and familiar tone, not on whether she has been paid, whether the product suits different skin types, or whether the claim is supported by evidence. The more personal the delivery is, the easier it becomes for advertising to borrow the language of friendship. That makes influencers powerful, but not necessarily trustworthy.","chinese":""},{"label":"Paragraph 3","english":"The second reason is that influencers are not always held to the same standard of expertise or accountability as traditional advertisers. This is not to say that traditional advertisements are perfectly honest; far from it, indeed. They exaggerate, simplify and beautify reality. Nevertheless, traditional media campaigns usually involve companies, agencies and public scrutiny. If a television commercial makes an obviously false claim, the brand can be challenged, criticised and remembered for it. An influencer, however, may promote a product today and move on tomorrow, leaving disappointed consumers with little more than a deleted post or a vague apology. More importantly, popularity is not the same as competence. A fitness influencer may look healthy without understanding nutrition; a lifestyle vlogger may recommend an expensive gadget after using it for only two days; a finance influencer may speak confidently about investment while lacking professional training. When charisma replaces expertise, followers risk mistaking confidence for credibility. Trust built on personality alone is therefore a fragile foundation.","chinese":""},{"label":"Paragraph 4","english":"Granted, supporters of influencers have a reasonable point: influencers can sometimes be more useful than traditional advertisements because they demonstrate products in real-life situations. A makeup tutorial may show texture better than a magazine advert; a gaming reviewer may explain performance more clearly than a poster; a travel influencer may reveal details that a hotel brochure conveniently ignores. In addition, influencers depend on their reputation, so careless promotion may damage their long-term relationship with followers. These advantages should not be dismissed. Even so, they do not prove that influencers are generally more trustworthy. Comments can be filtered; negative experiences can be edited out; and “authentic” content can still be carefully scripted. Just because a message looks spontaneous does not mean it is honest. Indeed, the real danger lies in the fact that sponsored advice can appear independent when it is not. At least with traditional advertisements, the commercial motive is usually visible from the start. All things considered, social media influencers may be more engaging than traditional media advertisements, but they are not more trustworthy. What matters is not whether a message comes from a smiling individual or a polished company, but whether it is transparent, verifiable and responsible. Consumers should check sponsorship labels, compare different sources and ask whether the influencer has the knowledge to make the claim. Companies and platforms, meanwhile, should make paid promotions as clear as possible. In the end, trust should be earned by honesty, not manufactured by intimacy.","chinese":""}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"familiarity","chinese":"熟悉感"},{"english":"not the same as","chinese":"與……並不相同"},{"english":"in an age when","chinese":"在一個……的時代"},{"english":"a phone screen","chinese":"手機螢幕"},{"english":"become both…and…","chinese":"既成為……又成為……"},{"english":"no longer waits between","chinese":"不再只等在……之間出現"},{"english":"television programmes","chinese":"電視節目"},{"english":"slips into","chinese":"悄悄滲入"},{"english":"daily routines","chinese":"日常生活習慣"},{"english":"livestreams","chinese":"直播"},{"english":"honest reviews","chinese":"真誠評測"},{"english":"surveys show that","chinese":"調查顯示"},{"english":"millennials","chinese":"千禧世代"},{"english":"trust influencers more than","chinese":"比起……更信任KOL"},{"english":"traditional advertisements","chinese":"傳統廣告"},{"english":"be increasingly tempted to","chinese":"越來越想"},{"english":"personal relationships","chinese":"私人關係"},{"english":"sell products","chinese":"銷售產品"},{"english":"in order to","chinese":"為了"},{"english":"make marketing appear warmer","chinese":"令市場推廣顯得更親切"},{"english":"more believable","chinese":"更可信"},{"english":"as far as I am concerned","chinese":"就我而言"},{"english":"social media influencers","chinese":"社交媒體KOL"},{"english":"not more trustworthy than","chinese":"不比……更值得信任"},{"english":"traditional media advertisements","chinese":"傳統媒體廣告"},{"english":"relatable and persuasive","chinese":"容易令人產生共鳴而且有說服力"},{"english":"relatable","chinese":"容易令人產生共鳴"},{"english":"persuasive","chinese":"有說服力"},{"english":"rest not on…, but on…","chinese":"不應建基於……而應建基於……"},{"english":"transparency","chinese":"透明度"},{"english":"accountability","chinese":"問責性"},{"english":"evidence","chinese":"證據"},{"english":"the first reason is that","chinese":"第一個原因是"},{"english":"influencer marketing","chinese":"KOL市場推廣"},{"english":"blur the line between","chinese":"模糊……之間的界線"},{"english":"personal recommendation","chinese":"個人推薦"},{"english":"paid persuasion","chinese":"付費說服"},{"english":"whether…or…","chinese":"無論是……還是……"},{"english":"on a billboard","chinese":"在廣告牌上"},{"english":"announce itself officially as","chinese":"正式表明自己是……"},{"english":"be well informed that","chinese":"清楚知道"},{"english":"try to sell something","chinese":"試圖銷售某物"},{"english":"watch with caution","chinese":"帶着警覺觀看"},{"english":"by contrast","chinese":"相比之下"},{"english":"an influencer's promotion","chinese":"KOL的推廣內容"},{"english":"ordinary-looking content","chinese":"看似普通的內容"},{"english":"a morning routine","chinese":"早晨日常影片"},{"english":"what I eat in a day","chinese":"一日飲食影片"},{"english":"a travel vlog","chinese":"旅行影片網誌"},{"english":"a livestream chat","chinese":"直播聊天"},{"english":"after following the same creator for months","chinese":"追蹤同一位創作者數月後"},{"english":"feel as if","chinese":"感覺好像"},{"english":"know someone personally","chinese":"親身認識某人"},{"english":"emotional closeness","chinese":"情感上的親近感"},{"english":"make the message sound like","chinese":"令訊息聽起來像"},{"english":"friendly advice","chinese":"朋友般的建議"},{"english":"instead of","chinese":"而不是"},{"english":"commercial persuasion","chinese":"商業說服"},{"english":"take…for example","chinese":"以……為例"},{"english":"a skincare influencer","chinese":"護膚KOL"},{"english":"save my skin","chinese":"拯救了我的皮膚"},{"english":"focus on","chinese":"專注於"},{"english":"familiar tone","chinese":"熟悉的語氣"},{"english":"whether she has been paid","chinese":"她是否收了費"},{"english":"suit different skin types","chinese":"適合不同膚質"},{"english":"be supported by evidence","chinese":"得到證據支持"},{"english":"the more…, the easier…","chinese":"越……就越容易……"},{"english":"personal delivery","chinese":"個人化的表達方式"},{"english":"borrow the language of friendship","chinese":"借用友誼的語言"},{"english":"not necessarily trustworthy","chinese":"不一定值得信任"},{"english":"be held to the same standard","chinese":"被要求達到同一標準"},{"english":"expertise","chinese":"專業知識"},{"english":"not to say that","chinese":"這並不是說"},{"english":"perfectly honest","chinese":"完全誠實"},{"english":"far from it","chinese":"絕非如此"},{"english":"exaggerate reality","chinese":"誇大現實"},{"english":"simplify reality","chinese":"簡化現實"},{"english":"beautify reality","chinese":"美化現實"},{"english":"traditional media campaigns","chinese":"傳統媒體宣傳活動"},{"english":"public scrutiny","chinese":"公眾監察"},{"english":"make a false claim","chinese":"作出虛假聲稱"},{"english":"be challenged","chinese":"受到質疑"},{"english":"be criticised","chinese":"受到批評"},{"english":"be remembered for it","chinese":"因此被記住"},{"english":"move on tomorrow","chinese":"明天就轉到下一件事"},{"english":"disappointed consumers","chinese":"感到失望的消費者"},{"english":"little more than","chinese":"只剩下；不過是"},{"english":"a deleted post","chinese":"一篇已刪除的帖文"},{"english":"a vague apology","chinese":"含糊的道歉"},{"english":"popularity is not the same as competence","chinese":"受歡迎並不等於有能力"},{"english":"competence","chinese":"能力；勝任能力"},{"english":"a fitness influencer","chinese":"健身KOL"},{"english":"look healthy","chinese":"看起來健康"},{"english":"understand nutrition","chinese":"了解營養學"},{"english":"a lifestyle vlogger","chinese":"生活影片網誌創作者"},{"english":"recommend an expensive gadget","chinese":"推薦昂貴電子產品"},{"english":"a finance influencer","chinese":"財經KOL"},{"english":"speak confidently about","chinese":"自信地談論"},{"english":"lack professional training","chinese":"缺乏專業訓練"},{"english":"charisma replaces expertise","chinese":"個人魅力取代專業知識"},{"english":"mistake confidence for credibility","chinese":"把自信誤當成可信度"},{"english":"credibility","chinese":"可信度"},{"english":"built on personality alone","chinese":"單靠個人魅力建立"},{"english":"a fragile foundation","chinese":"脆弱的基礎"},{"english":"granted","chinese":"誠然"},{"english":"supporters of influencers","chinese":"KOL支持者"},{"english":"have a reasonable point","chinese":"有合理之處"},{"english":"demonstrate products","chinese":"示範產品"},{"english":"real-life situations","chinese":"真實生活情境"},{"english":"a makeup tutorial","chinese":"化妝教學"},{"english":"show texture","chinese":"展示質感"},{"english":"a magazine advert","chinese":"雜誌廣告"},{"english":"a gaming reviewer","chinese":"遊戲評測者"},{"english":"explain performance","chinese":"解釋性能表現"},{"english":"a travel influencer","chinese":"旅遊KOL"},{"english":"reveal details","chinese":"揭示細節"},{"english":"a hotel brochure","chinese":"酒店小冊子"},{"english":"conveniently ignore","chinese":"為求方便而略過"},{"english":"depend on reputation","chinese":"依賴聲譽"},{"english":"careless promotion","chinese":"草率的推廣"},{"english":"damage a long-term relationship with","chinese":"損害與……的長期關係"},{"english":"long-term relationship","chinese":"長期關係"},{"english":"be dismissed","chinese":"被否定；被忽視"},{"english":"even so","chinese":"即使如此"},{"english":"generally more trustworthy","chinese":"一般而言更值得信任"},{"english":"comments can be filtered","chinese":"留言可以被篩選"},{"english":"negative experiences","chinese":"負面經歷"},{"english":"be edited out","chinese":"被剪走；被刪去"},{"english":"authentic content","chinese":"真實感內容"},{"english":"carefully scripted","chinese":"經仔細編排"},{"english":"just because…does not mean…","chinese":"只是因為……並不代表……"},{"english":"look spontaneous","chinese":"看似即興"},{"english":"the real danger lies in","chinese":"真正的危險在於"},{"english":"sponsored advice","chinese":"贊助建議"},{"english":"appear independent","chinese":"看似獨立"},{"english":"at least","chinese":"至少"},{"english":"commercial motive","chinese":"商業動機"},{"english":"visible from the start","chinese":"一開始已清楚可見"},{"english":"all things considered","chinese":"總括而言"},{"english":"more engaging than","chinese":"比……更吸引人"},{"english":"what matters is not whether…, but whether…","chinese":"重要的不是……而是……"},{"english":"a smiling individual","chinese":"面帶笑容的個人"},{"english":"a polished company","chinese":"包裝精美的公司"},{"english":"transparent, verifiable and responsible","chinese":"透明、可核實和負責任"},{"english":"verifiable","chinese":"可核實的"},{"english":"check sponsorship labels","chinese":"查看贊助標籤"},{"english":"compare different sources","chinese":"比較不同資料來源"},{"english":"have the knowledge to","chinese":"有知識去……"},{"english":"make the claim","chinese":"作出聲稱"},{"english":"companies and platforms","chinese":"公司和平台"},{"english":"meanwhile","chinese":"與此同時"},{"english":"paid promotions","chinese":"付費推廣"},{"english":"as clear as possible","chinese":"盡量清晰"},{"english":"in the end","chinese":"最終"},{"english":"be earned by honesty","chinese":"靠誠實贏得"},{"english":"manufactured by intimacy","chinese":"靠親密感製造出來"}]},"dse-writing-2021-part-b-q6":{"exerciseId":"dse-writing-2021-part-b-q6","essayKey":"","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=dse-writing-2021-part-b-q6","flashDeckId":"dse/writing/part-b/2021/Q6","paragraphs":[{"label":"Paragraph 1","english":"Twenty-One Days, One Quiet Revolution","chinese":"二十一天，一場寧靜的內在革命"},{"label":"Paragraph 2","english":"Before this challenge, gratitude sounded to me like one of those pretty words people put under sunset photos. Nice, but not exactly life-changing. For better or worse, social media had taught me to measure my life in likes, marks and other people’s highlights. I accepted the 21-day Gratitude Challenge because I was tired of feeling as if everyone else was moving ahead while I was merely keeping up. By writing a journal entry every night for three weeks, I hoped to slow down, notice what I still had, and become less trapped by comparison. Looking back, I would say the challenge did not turn me into a completely different person, but it did something better - it made me a more attentive one.","chinese":"在參加這個挑戰之前，「感恩」對我來說，就像人們放在日落照片下面那些漂亮卻有點空泛的字眼。 聽起來不錯，但還不至於能改變人生。 不論好壞，社交媒體曾教會我用按讚數、分數和別人的精彩片段來衡量自己的人生。 我接受「二十一天感恩挑戰」，是因為我已厭倦了那種彷彿所有人都在向前走，而我只是勉強跟上的感覺。 透過連續三星期每晚寫一篇日記，我希望自己能慢下來，留意自己仍然擁有的東西，並減少被比較困住。 回望過去，我會說這個挑戰沒有把我變成一個完全不同的人，但它做了一件更好的事——它令我成為一個更懂得留心生活的人。"},{"label":"Paragraph 3","english":"At first, I treated the journal like homework. On Day 1, I wrote down the obvious things - my family, my health, and my friends. They were true, of course, but the words felt distant, almost copied from a moral education poster. By Day 4, however, I began to understand the point. Gratitude is not just about naming the big blessings; it is about training your eyes to catch the small ones before they disappear. I wrote about the security guard who held the lift for me when I was late, the bowl of hot noodles my mother left on the table, and the classmate who sent me notes without making me feel guilty for being absent. None of these moments was dramatic. Yet recording them gave them weight. Little by little, my day no longer looked like a list of problems. It looked like a collection of quiet gifts in my life.","chinese":"一開始，我把這本日記當成功課一樣看待。 第一天，我寫下了一些最明顯的事物——我的家人、我的健康和我的朋友。 當然，這些都是真的，但那些文字感覺很遙遠，幾乎像是從德育海報上抄下來的一樣。 然而，到了第四天，我開始明白這個挑戰的真正意義。 感恩不只是把重大的幸福列舉出來；它更是訓練自己的眼睛，在細小的美好消失之前捕捉到它們。 我寫下那位在我遲到時替我按住電梯的保安員、媽媽留在桌上的一碗熱湯麵，以及那位把筆記傳給我卻沒有讓我因缺席而感到內疚的同學。 這些時刻沒有一個是戲劇性的。 然而，把它們記錄下來，卻令它們有了重量。 一點一滴地，我的一天不再看起來像一張問題清單。 它反而像是我生命中一系列安靜而珍貴的禮物。"},{"label":"Paragraph 4","english":"The second week was harder, and for that reason, more honest. One rainy Tuesday, I lost my temper at my younger brother over something embarrassingly small; Essentially, he had borrowed my charger without asking. My first instinct was to write, “Nothing to be grateful for today.” Still, I forced myself to sit with the page. After a few minutes, I wrote that I was grateful he still wanted to come into my room and talk to me, even though I often pushed him away. That sentence left me uncomfortable, but in a useful way. It made me realise that gratitude does not cancel frustration; rather, it prevents frustration from becoming the whole story. The same happened after I received a disappointing test result. I was grateful not for the mark, but for a teacher who wrote, “Come and see me if you need help.” For once, I saw support where I would usually have seen failure.","chinese":"第二個星期比較困難，也正因如此，它更加真實。 一個下雨的星期二，我因為一件小得令人尷尬的事情對弟弟發脾氣；簡單來說，他沒有問過我就借用了我的充電器。 我的第一個本能反應是寫下：「今天沒有甚麼值得感恩。」 即使如此，我仍然強迫自己坐在那一頁面前。 幾分鐘後，我寫下自己感激他仍然願意走進我的房間和我說話，即使我常常把他推開。 那句話令我感到不自在，但那是一種有用的不自在。 它令我明白，感恩不會把挫敗感取消；更準確地說，它會防止挫敗感變成整個故事。 在我收到一個令人失望的測驗成績後，同樣的事情也發生了。 我感激的不是那個分數，是一位寫下「如果你需要幫助，就來找我」的老師 這一次，我在平時只會看見失敗的地方，看見了支持。"},{"label":"Paragraph 5","english":"By the final week, the challenge had begun to affect my behaviour, not just my mood. I thanked people more directly. I told my mother that her late-night fruit plates meant a lot to me. I messaged a friend, not to ask for notes or gossip, but simply to say I appreciated how she always checked whether I had eaten lunch. The funny thing is, these small messages made me feel less awkward, not more. They opened doors to warmer conversations. I also noticed that I complained less online. Before posting a sarcastic story about a bad day, I would ask myself: “am I being honest, or am I only performing disappointment for attention?” That question alone was already worth the whole challenge.","chinese":"到了最後一個星期，這個挑戰已經開始影響我的行為，而不只是我的心情。 我更直接地向別人表達感謝。 我告訴媽媽，她深夜為我準備的水果盤對我來說意義很大。 我傳訊息給一位朋友，不是為了問筆記或八卦，而只是想說我很感激她總會關心我有沒有吃午飯。 有趣的是，這些小小的訊息沒有令我更尷尬，反而令我少了一點不自在。 它們打開了通往更溫暖對話的大門。 我也發現自己在網上抱怨少了。 在發布一則諷刺自己糟糕一天的限時動態之前，我會問自己：「我是在誠實表達，還是只是在為了得到關注而表演失望？」 單是這個問題本身，就已經令整個挑戰值得了。"},{"label":"Paragraph 6","english":"So, has the 21-day Gratitude Challenge changed me? My answer is a resounding yes, though not in a magical, movie-ending kind of way. I still get annoyed. I still worry about exams, and I still compare myself with others more often than I should. But I am no longer as quick to assume that a difficult day is an empty day. Gratitude has become a small pause between what happens to me and how I choose to understand it. Going forward, I plan to keep writing three lines every night, especially on days when I feel I have nothing to say. If you are reading this and wondering whether twenty-one days can really matter, try it. The best things in life may be free, but we still have to notice them.","chinese":"那麼，「二十一天感恩挑戰」改變了我嗎？ 我的答案是非常肯定的「有」，雖然不是以一種神奇而像電影結局般的方式 我仍然會感到惱怒。 我仍然會擔心考試，也仍然比自己應該做的更常與別人比較。 但是，我不再那麼快便假定艱難的一天就是空洞的一天。 感恩已經成為發生在我身上的事情，與我選擇如何理解它之間的一個小小停頓 往後，我打算每晚繼續寫三行字，尤其是在那些我覺得自己無話可說的日子 如果你正在閱讀這篇文章，並想知道二十一天是否真的能產生意義，那就試一試吧 人生中最美好的事物或許是免費的，但我們仍然必須學會留意它們。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"one quiet revolution","chinese":"一場靜靜的改變"},{"english":"before this challenge","chinese":"在這次挑戰之前"},{"english":"gratitude","chinese":"感恩；感激之情"},{"english":"sounded to me like","chinese":"在我聽來像是"},{"english":"one of those","chinese":"那些……之一"},{"english":"pretty words","chinese":"漂亮但空泛的字眼"},{"english":"sunset photos","chinese":"日落照片"},{"english":"not exactly life-changing","chinese":"不算真的改變人生"},{"english":"for better or worse","chinese":"不論好壞；無論如何"},{"english":"social media","chinese":"社交媒體"},{"english":"had taught me to","chinese":"教會了我去……"},{"english":"measure my life in","chinese":"用……衡量我的人生"},{"english":"likes and marks","chinese":"讚好數和分數"},{"english":"other people's highlights","chinese":"別人生活中的精彩時刻"},{"english":"accept the challenge","chinese":"接受挑戰"},{"english":"the 21-day Gratitude Challenge","chinese":"二十一日感恩挑戰"},{"english":"be tired of feeling as if","chinese":"厭倦了覺得好像"},{"english":"move ahead","chinese":"向前走；取得進展"},{"english":"merely keeping up","chinese":"只是勉強跟上"},{"english":"write a journal entry","chinese":"寫日記"},{"english":"every night for three weeks","chinese":"連續三星期每晚"},{"english":"hoped to slow down","chinese":"希望放慢腳步"},{"english":"notice what I still had","chinese":"留意自己仍然擁有的東西"},{"english":"become less trapped by comparison","chinese":"不再那麼困於比較之中"},{"english":"trapped by comparison","chinese":"被比較困住"},{"english":"looking back","chinese":"回望起來"},{"english":"turn me into","chinese":"把我變成"},{"english":"a completely different person","chinese":"一個完全不同的人"},{"english":"did something better","chinese":"做到更好的事"},{"english":"a more attentive one","chinese":"一個更懂得留意的人"},{"english":"at first","chinese":"起初"},{"english":"treat something like homework","chinese":"把某事當成功課"},{"english":"write down","chinese":"寫下"},{"english":"the obvious things","chinese":"顯而易見的事情"},{"english":"felt distant","chinese":"感覺遙遠；不貼近自己"},{"english":"almost copied from","chinese":"像是從……抄來"},{"english":"a moral education poster","chinese":"德育海報"},{"english":"began to understand the point","chinese":"開始明白重點"},{"english":"not just about","chinese":"不只是關於……"},{"english":"big blessings","chinese":"重大的福氣"},{"english":"train your eyes to","chinese":"訓練自己去留意"},{"english":"catch the small ones","chinese":"捕捉那些小小的事物"},{"english":"before they disappear","chinese":"在它們消失之前"},{"english":"hold the lift for someone","chinese":"替某人按住升降機"},{"english":"when I was late","chinese":"當我遲到時"},{"english":"a bowl of hot noodles","chinese":"一碗熱湯麵"},{"english":"leave something on the table","chinese":"把某物放在桌上"},{"english":"send me notes","chinese":"傳筆記給我"},{"english":"without making me feel guilty","chinese":"沒有令我感到內疚"},{"english":"feel guilty for","chinese":"因……而感到內疚"},{"english":"being absent","chinese":"缺席"},{"english":"none of these moments","chinese":"這些時刻都不是"},{"english":"recording them","chinese":"把它們記錄下來"},{"english":"give something weight","chinese":"令某事變得有分量"},{"english":"little by little","chinese":"漸漸地"},{"english":"no longer looked like","chinese":"不再看起來像"},{"english":"a list of problems","chinese":"一連串問題"},{"english":"a collection of","chinese":"一組；一系列"},{"english":"quiet gifts","chinese":"靜靜出現的禮物"},{"english":"the second week","chinese":"第二星期"},{"english":"for that reason","chinese":"正因如此"},{"english":"more honest","chinese":"更真實；更坦誠"},{"english":"lose my temper at","chinese":"對……發脾氣"},{"english":"over something small","chinese":"因一件小事"},{"english":"embarrassingly small","chinese":"小得令人尷尬"},{"english":"essentially","chinese":"基本上；實際上"},{"english":"borrow something without asking","chinese":"未經同意借走某物"},{"english":"my first instinct","chinese":"我的第一反應"},{"english":"nothing to be grateful for","chinese":"沒有甚麼值得感恩"},{"english":"force myself to","chinese":"迫自己去……"},{"english":"sit with the page","chinese":"坐下來面對那一頁"},{"english":"after a few minutes","chinese":"幾分鐘後"},{"english":"come into my room","chinese":"走進我的房間"},{"english":"push someone away","chinese":"推開某人；疏遠某人"},{"english":"leave me uncomfortable","chinese":"令我感到不自在"},{"english":"in a useful way","chinese":"以一種有幫助的方式"},{"english":"make me realise that","chinese":"令我意識到"},{"english":"cancel frustration","chinese":"抵消挫敗感"},{"english":"rather","chinese":"反而；更準確地說"},{"english":"prevent something from becoming","chinese":"防止某事變成"},{"english":"the whole story","chinese":"整個故事；全部真相"},{"english":"the same happened after","chinese":"同樣的情況發生在……之後"},{"english":"a disappointing test result","chinese":"令人失望的測驗成績"},{"english":"not for…but for…","chinese":"不是因為……而是因為……"},{"english":"come and see me","chinese":"來找我"},{"english":"if you need help","chinese":"如果你需要幫助"},{"english":"for once","chinese":"這一次；難得一次"},{"english":"see support","chinese":"看見支持"},{"english":"would usually have seen","chinese":"以往通常會看到"},{"english":"by the final week","chinese":"到最後一星期"},{"english":"affect my behaviour","chinese":"影響我的行為"},{"english":"not just my mood","chinese":"不只是我的心情"},{"english":"thank people more directly","chinese":"更直接地感謝別人"},{"english":"late-night fruit plates","chinese":"深夜準備的水果盤"},{"english":"mean a lot to me","chinese":"對我意義重大"},{"english":"message a friend","chinese":"傳訊息給朋友"},{"english":"not to ask for","chinese":"不是為了索取"},{"english":"notes or gossip","chinese":"筆記或八卦消息"},{"english":"simply to say","chinese":"只是為了說"},{"english":"appreciate how","chinese":"感激……的方式"},{"english":"check whether","chinese":"查看是否；問清楚是否"},{"english":"the funny thing is","chinese":"有趣的是"},{"english":"less awkward","chinese":"沒那麼尷尬"},{"english":"open doors to","chinese":"打開通往……的大門"},{"english":"warmer conversations","chinese":"更溫暖的對話"},{"english":"complain less online","chinese":"較少在網上抱怨"},{"english":"before posting","chinese":"在發布之前"},{"english":"a sarcastic story","chinese":"帶諷刺意味的限時動態"},{"english":"ask myself","chinese":"問自己"},{"english":"being honest","chinese":"坦誠；誠實"},{"english":"perform disappointment for attention","chinese":"為博取注意而表演失望"},{"english":"that question alone","chinese":"單是那個問題"},{"english":"worth the whole challenge","chinese":"值得整個挑戰"},{"english":"a resounding yes","chinese":"響亮而肯定的「是」"},{"english":"not in a magical way","chinese":"不是以神奇的方式"},{"english":"movie-ending kind of way","chinese":"像電影結局那樣"},{"english":"get annoyed","chinese":"感到煩躁；生氣"},{"english":"worry about exams","chinese":"擔心考試"},{"english":"compare myself with others","chinese":"拿自己和別人比較"},{"english":"more often than I should","chinese":"比我應該做的更頻密"},{"english":"no longer as quick to assume","chinese":"不再那麼快就假定"},{"english":"a difficult day","chinese":"艱難的一天"},{"english":"an empty day","chinese":"空無收穫的一天"},{"english":"a small pause between…and…","chinese":"……與……之間的小停頓"},{"english":"what happens to me","chinese":"發生在我身上的事"},{"english":"how I choose to understand it","chinese":"我選擇如何理解它"},{"english":"going forward","chinese":"展望將來；往後"},{"english":"keep writing","chinese":"繼續寫"},{"english":"three lines every night","chinese":"每晚三行"},{"english":"especially on days when","chinese":"尤其是在……的日子"},{"english":"have nothing to say","chinese":"沒有話可說"},{"english":"wondering whether","chinese":"想知道是否"},{"english":"can really matter","chinese":"真的有意義；真的重要"},{"english":"the best things in life","chinese":"生命中最美好的事物"},{"english":"may be free","chinese":"可能是免費的"},{"english":"still have to notice them","chinese":"仍然要留意它們"}]},"dse-writing-2021-part-b-q7":{"exerciseId":"dse-writing-2021-part-b-q7","essayKey":"","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=dse-writing-2021-part-b-q7","flashDeckId":"dse/writing/part-b/2021/Q7","paragraphs":[{"label":"Paragraph 1","english":"After Midnight at Page & Co.","chinese":""},{"label":"Paragraph 2","english":"When Mr Wong clocked in at 11:45 p.m., Page & Co. already smelled of dust, glue and rain. After the last cashier left, the bookshop became his kingdom: one security room, sixteen grey monitors, a dented flask, and six hours to survive until the next morning.","chinese":"當黃先生在晚上十一時四十五分打卡上班時，Page & Co. 已經瀰漫着灰塵、膠水和雨水的氣味。 最後一名收銀員離開後，這間書店便成了他的王國：一間保安室、十六個灰濛濛的監視器、一個凹陷了的水壺，以及六個小時，讓他撐到翌日清晨。 當黃先生在晚上十一時四十五分打卡上班時，Page & Co. 已經瀰漫着灰塵、膠水和雨水的氣味。"},{"label":"Paragraph 3","english":"“The door sensor at the rear keeps acting up,” said Nico, the day guard. “If it rings, check it. That’s all.”","chinese":"「後門的感應器一直不太正常，」日更保安 Nico 說。 「如果它響了，就去檢查一下。就這樣。」"},{"label":"Paragraph 4","english":"Mr Wong smiled. “I’ve guarded banks, jewellery shops and car parks. I can handle a bookshop.”","chinese":"黃先生笑了笑。 「銀行、珠寶店和停車場我都守過。一間書店，我應付得來。」"},{"label":"Paragraph 5","english":"“Books remember things,” Nico said.","chinese":"「書是會記住事情的，」Nico 說。"},{"label":"Paragraph 6","english":"He laughed, but after she left, the words stayed with him.","chinese":"他笑了出來，但在她離開後，那句話卻一直留在他腦海裡。懸疑"},{"label":"Paragraph 7","english":"For the first hour, nothing moved except the second hand of the clock. It clicked its way towards one, then two. On Camera 3, the counter slept beneath a thin blue light. On Camera 6, the rear door stood shut. On Camera 9, Mr Wong saw himself sitting in the security room, shoulders bent, eyes heavy.","chinese":"第一個小時裡，除了時鐘的秒針，甚麼也沒有動。 它滴答滴答地走向一點，然後走向兩點。 在三號鏡頭裡，收銀櫃檯沉睡在一層淡淡的藍光之下。 在六號鏡頭裡，後門緊緊關着。 在九號鏡頭裡，黃先生看見自己坐在保安室內，肩膀垂下，眼皮沉重。"},{"label":"Paragraph 8","english":"The strange thing was that he was still wide awake.","chinese":"奇怪的是，他明明仍然十分清醒。"},{"label":"Paragraph 9","english":"He leaned closer. On the screen, the man in the chair lowered his head onto his arms and began to sleep. At the same moment, Mr Wong felt a weight press down on his eyelids. The room stretched and blurred. The monitors became pale windows. He told himself to stand up.","chinese":"他湊近了一點。 螢幕上，椅子上的男人把頭低低地伏在手臂上，開始睡着。 就在同一刻，黃先生感到一股沉重的力量壓在他的眼皮上。 房間像被拉長了一樣，逐漸變得模糊。 那些監視器變成了一扇扇蒼白的窗。 他告訴自己要站起來。"},{"label":"Paragraph 10","english":"Too late.","chinese":"太遲了。"},{"label":"Paragraph 11","english":"The alarm screamed.","chinese":"警鐘尖叫起來。"},{"label":"Paragraph 12","english":"Mr Wong jerked awake so violently that his flask rolled off the desk. A red warning light flashed beside Camera 6: REAR DOOR OPEN. On the monitor, the door was not merely open; it was swinging slowly, as though someone had just passed through it.","chinese":"黃先生猛然驚醒，動作劇烈得令水壺從桌上滾了下去。 六號鏡頭旁邊閃着紅色警示燈：後門開啟。 在監視器上，那扇門不只是開着；它還在慢慢擺動，彷彿剛剛有人從中走過"},{"label":"Paragraph 13","english":"He grabbed his torch and radio. “Security patrol to rear corridor,” he said, though there was no one to hear him.","chinese":"他抓起手電筒和對講機。 「保安巡邏，前往後方走廊，」他說，儘管根本沒有人會聽見。"},{"label":"Paragraph 14","english":"The arcade outside was colder than it should have been. His footsteps came back to him a second late, as if another guard were following just out of sight. At the bookshop’s rear entrance, the sensor blinked above the door. Green. Red. Green. Red.","chinese":"外面的商場走廊冷得不合常理。 他的腳步聲遲了一秒才回到耳邊，彷彿有另一名保安正跟在他身後，只是剛好不在視線之內。 在書店後門入口處，感應器在門上方閃爍着。 綠色。紅色。綠色。紅色。"},{"label":"Paragraph 15","english":"The door was locked.","chinese":"門是鎖上的。"},{"label":"Paragraph 16","english":"Behind it, pages rustled.","chinese":"門後，紙頁沙沙作響。"},{"label":"Paragraph 17","english":"“Enough already,” Mr Wong muttered, forcing the key into the lock.","chinese":"「夠了吧，」黃先生低聲說，把鑰匙硬塞進鎖孔。發現"},{"label":"Paragraph 18","english":"Inside, the shelves seemed taller than before. His torchlight moved over travel guides, cookbooks and romance novels before landing on a poster near the children’s corner:","chinese":"裡面，書架看起來比之前更高了。 他的手電筒光線掃過旅遊指南、食譜和愛情小說，最後落在兒童角附近的一張海報上："},{"label":"Paragraph 19","english":"SHORT STORY CONTEST","chinese":"短篇故事比賽"},{"label":"Paragraph 20","english":"Write a scary story about a security guard on duty one night.","chinese":"寫一個關於一名保安在某夜當值時的恐怖故事。"},{"label":"Paragraph 21","english":"Beneath it lay four black-and-white drawings: a security room, a sleeping guard, an alarmed door and a lone guard walking into darkness.","chinese":"海報下面放着四幅黑白圖畫：一間保安室、一名睡着的保安、一扇響起警報的門，以及一名獨自走進黑暗中的保安。"},{"label":"Paragraph 22","english":"Mr Wong’s mouth went dry. The last picture was unfinished. Only the guard’s legs had been drawn. The rest of the body was missing.","chinese":"黃先生口乾舌燥。 最後一幅圖還沒有完成。 畫中只畫出了那名保安的雙腿。 身體其餘部分都不見了。"},{"label":"Paragraph 23","english":"No sooner had he touched the paper than the public-address system crackled. A voice whispered through every speaker in the shop.","chinese":"他剛一碰到那張紙，廣播系統便發出劈啪聲。 一道聲音從店內每一個揚聲器中低聲傳出。"},{"label":"Paragraph 24","english":"“Finish your patrol.”","chinese":"「完成你的巡邏。」"},{"label":"Paragraph 25","english":"A book slid from the shelf and landed open at his feet. On the page was a neat line of handwriting:","chinese":"一本書從書架上滑落，在他腳邊攤開。 頁面上有一行整齊的筆跡："},{"label":"Paragraph 26","english":"Mr Wong returned to the security room and found himself still asleep.","chinese":"黃先生回到保安室，發現自己仍然睡着。"},{"label":"Paragraph 27","english":"He ran.","chinese":"他拔腿就跑。"},{"label":"Paragraph 28","english":"The corridor bent in the wrong direction. The bookshop door opened into the staff toilet, the staff toilet into the staircase, the staircase back into Fiction. All the while, the alarm kept ringing, louder and louder, until it sounded less like a machine than a child laughing behind metal teeth.","chinese":"走廊朝着錯誤的方向彎曲。 書店的門通往員工洗手間，員工洗手間通往樓梯，樓梯又通回小說區。 一直以來，警鐘不停地響着，越來越大聲，到最後聽起來已不像機器，反而像一個孩子在金屬牙齒後面發笑。"},{"label":"Paragraph 29","english":"At last, he burst into the security room.","chinese":"最後，他衝進了保安室。"},{"label":"Paragraph 30","english":"Someone was sleeping at the desk.","chinese":"有人正趴在桌上睡覺。"},{"label":"Paragraph 31","english":"Mr Wong stepped closer. The man wore his uniform, his name badge and even the scar above his left eyebrow. On the monitors, all sixteen cameras showed the same picture: Mr Wong standing behind the chair, one trembling hand reaching out.","chinese":"黃先生走近了一步。 那個男人穿着他的制服，戴着他的名牌，甚至連左邊眉毛上方的疤痕也一模一樣。 在監視器上，十六個鏡頭全部顯示着同一幅畫面：黃先生站在椅子後面，一隻顫抖的手正伸出去。"},{"label":"Paragraph 32","english":"“Wake up,” he whispered.","chinese":"「醒來，」他低聲說。"},{"label":"Paragraph 33","english":"The sleeping man opened his eyes on the screen first.","chinese":"那個睡着的男人先是在螢幕上睜開了眼睛。"},{"label":"Paragraph 34","english":"Then, without turning around, he smiled.","chinese":"然後，他沒有轉身，卻笑了。"},{"label":"Paragraph 35","english":"By morning, Nico found the security room empty. The flask lay on the floor. The rear door sensor was silent. On the desk was a contest entry, freshly printed, with no author’s name.","chinese":"到了早上，Nico 發現保安室空無一人。 水壺躺在地上。 後門感應器一片寂靜。 桌上放着一份剛列印出來的參賽作品，沒有作者姓名。"},{"label":"Paragraph 36","english":"Its title was The Guard Who Never Clocked Out.","chinese":"標題是《從未下班的保安》。"},{"label":"Paragraph 37","english":"Nico read the first line and dropped the pages.","chinese":"Nico 讀了第一行，手中的紙張便掉了下來。"},{"label":"Paragraph 38","english":"When Mr Wong clocked in at 11:45 p.m., Page & Co. already smelled of dust, glue and rain.","chinese":"當黃先生在晚上十一時四十五分打卡上班時，Page & Co. 已經瀰漫着灰塵、膠水和雨水的氣味。 當黃先生在晚上十一時四十五分打卡上班時，Page & Co. 已經瀰漫着灰塵、膠水和雨水的氣味。"},{"label":"Paragraph 39","english":"After Midnight at Page & Co. 午夜過後的 Page & Co.","chinese":""}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"after midnight","chinese":"午夜過後"},{"english":"clocked in","chinese":"打卡上班"},{"english":"smelled of","chinese":"有……的氣味"},{"english":"dust, glue and rain","chinese":"灰塵、膠水和雨水的氣味"},{"english":"the last cashier left","chinese":"最後一位收銀員離開"},{"english":"became his kingdom","chinese":"成了他的地盤；成了他的王國"},{"english":"security room","chinese":"保安室"},{"english":"grey monitors","chinese":"灰色監視器"},{"english":"a dented flask","chinese":"凹了的保溫壺"},{"english":"survive until the next morning","chinese":"撐到翌日早上"},{"english":"door sensor","chinese":"門感應器"},{"english":"at the rear","chinese":"在後方"},{"english":"keep acting up","chinese":"不斷出問題"},{"english":"I can handle","chinese":"我應付得來"},{"english":"Books remember things","chinese":"書會記住事情"},{"english":"the words stayed with him","chinese":"那些話一直縈繞在心頭"},{"english":"for the first hour","chinese":"起初的一小時"},{"english":"nothing moved except","chinese":"除了……之外沒有東西動"},{"english":"the second hand of the clock","chinese":"時鐘的秒針"},{"english":"clicked its way towards","chinese":"滴答滴答地走向"},{"english":"beneath a thin blue light","chinese":"在微弱的藍光下"},{"english":"stood shut","chinese":"緊閉着"},{"english":"shoulders bent","chinese":"肩膊彎着；駝着背"},{"english":"eyes heavy","chinese":"眼皮沉重"},{"english":"the strange thing was that","chinese":"奇怪的是"},{"english":"wide awake","chinese":"十分清醒"},{"english":"leaned closer","chinese":"靠近一點"},{"english":"lowered his head onto","chinese":"把頭垂到……上"},{"english":"at the same moment","chinese":"與此同時"},{"english":"press down on","chinese":"壓在……上"},{"english":"eyelids","chinese":"眼皮"},{"english":"stretched and blurred","chinese":"拉長並變得模糊"},{"english":"told himself to","chinese":"告訴自己要"},{"english":"jerked awake","chinese":"猛然驚醒"},{"english":"so violently that","chinese":"猛烈得以致"},{"english":"rolled off","chinese":"從……滾落"},{"english":"warning light","chinese":"警示燈"},{"english":"flashed beside","chinese":"在……旁邊閃爍"},{"english":"not merely","chinese":"不只是"},{"english":"swinging slowly","chinese":"慢慢擺動"},{"english":"as though","chinese":"好像；彷彿"},{"english":"pass through","chinese":"穿過"},{"english":"grabbed his torch and radio","chinese":"拿起手電筒和對講機"},{"english":"security patrol","chinese":"保安巡邏"},{"english":"rear corridor","chinese":"後方走廊"},{"english":"there was no one to hear him","chinese":"沒有人會聽見他"},{"english":"the arcade outside","chinese":"外面的商場通道"},{"english":"colder than it should have been","chinese":"冷得不尋常"},{"english":"footsteps came back to him","chinese":"腳步聲傳回來"},{"english":"a second late","chinese":"慢了一秒"},{"english":"as if another guard were following","chinese":"好像另一名保安員正跟着"},{"english":"just out of sight","chinese":"剛好在視線之外"},{"english":"rear entrance","chinese":"後方入口"},{"english":"blinked above the door","chinese":"在門上方閃爍"},{"english":"forcing the key into the lock","chinese":"硬把鑰匙插進鎖裏"},{"english":"pages rustled","chinese":"書頁沙沙作響"},{"english":"seemed taller than before","chinese":"看起來比之前更高"},{"english":"torchlight moved over","chinese":"手電筒的光掃過"},{"english":"travel guides","chinese":"旅遊指南"},{"english":"cookbooks","chinese":"烹飪書"},{"english":"romance novels","chinese":"愛情小說"},{"english":"landed on","chinese":"照到；落在"},{"english":"children's corner","chinese":"兒童圖書角"},{"english":"short story contest","chinese":"短篇小說比賽"},{"english":"scary story","chinese":"恐怖故事"},{"english":"security guard on duty","chinese":"當值的保安員"},{"english":"beneath it lay","chinese":"……下面放着"},{"english":"black-and-white drawings","chinese":"黑白圖畫"},{"english":"a lone guard","chinese":"孤身一人的保安員"},{"english":"walking into darkness","chinese":"走進黑暗中"},{"english":"mouth went dry","chinese":"口乾舌燥"},{"english":"unfinished","chinese":"未完成的"},{"english":"the rest of the body","chinese":"身體其餘部分"},{"english":"was missing","chinese":"不見了"},{"english":"No sooner had he touched… than…","chinese":"剛一……就……"},{"english":"public-address system","chinese":"廣播系統"},{"english":"crackled","chinese":"發出沙沙聲；發出雜音"},{"english":"whispered through every speaker","chinese":"從每個喇叭低聲傳出"},{"english":"finish your patrol","chinese":"完成你的巡邏"},{"english":"slid from the shelf","chinese":"從書架滑落"},{"english":"landed open at his feet","chinese":"攤開落在他腳邊"},{"english":"a neat line of handwriting","chinese":"一行整齊的手寫字"},{"english":"returned to","chinese":"回到……"},{"english":"found himself still asleep","chinese":"發現自己仍然睡着"},{"english":"the corridor bent","chinese":"走廊彎曲"},{"english":"in the wrong direction","chinese":"朝錯誤方向"},{"english":"opened into","chinese":"通往；開向"},{"english":"staff toilet","chinese":"職員洗手間"},{"english":"back into Fiction","chinese":"回到小說區"},{"english":"all the while","chinese":"期間一直；同時"},{"english":"kept ringing","chinese":"不停響"},{"english":"less like… than…","chinese":"與其說像……不如說像……"},{"english":"a child laughing behind metal teeth","chinese":"像孩子在金屬牙齒後面笑"},{"english":"at last","chinese":"終於"},{"english":"burst into","chinese":"衝進"},{"english":"sleeping at the desk","chinese":"伏在桌前睡着"},{"english":"stepped closer","chinese":"走近一點"},{"english":"wore his uniform","chinese":"穿着他的制服"},{"english":"name badge","chinese":"名牌"},{"english":"scar above his left eyebrow","chinese":"左眉上方的疤痕"},{"english":"all sixteen cameras showed","chinese":"十六部鏡頭全部顯示"},{"english":"the same picture","chinese":"同一幅畫面"},{"english":"one trembling hand","chinese":"一隻顫抖的手"},{"english":"reaching out","chinese":"伸出去"},{"english":"on the screen first","chinese":"先在螢幕上"},{"english":"without turning around","chinese":"沒有轉身"},{"english":"by morning","chinese":"到了早上"},{"english":"found the security room empty","chinese":"發現保安室空無一人"},{"english":"the sensor was silent","chinese":"感應器沒有再響"},{"english":"contest entry","chinese":"比賽參賽作品"},{"english":"freshly printed","chinese":"剛列印出來的"},{"english":"with no author's name","chinese":"沒有作者署名"},{"english":"dropped the pages","chinese":"嚇得把紙張掉下"},{"english":"the first line","chinese":"第一行"},{"english":"never clocked out","chinese":"從未打卡下班"},{"english":"clocked out","chinese":"打卡下班"},{"english":"the opening line","chinese":"開首第一句"},{"english":"freshly printed entry","chinese":"剛列印出來的參賽作品"},{"english":"no author's name","chinese":"沒有作者署名"}]},"dse-writing-2021-part-b-q8":{"exerciseId":"dse-writing-2021-part-b-q8","essayKey":"","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=dse-writing-2021-part-b-q8","flashDeckId":"dse/writing/part-b/2021/Q8","paragraphs":[{"label":"Paragraph 1","english":"Silver Is Bright, but Gold Has Been Through Fire","chinese":"銀會發亮，但金已經歷過火的淬煉。"},{"label":"Paragraph 2","english":"In Joseph Parry’s poem, friendship is compared to precious metals: new friends are silver, while old friends are gold. In school life, friendships are constantly reshaped - a new seatmate may become a lunch companion, while a childhood friend may move into another class, district or dream. This has made young people consider how to balance old and new friendships in order to build emotionally rich lives. My stance is that older friendships are better, because time, change and hardship reveal the depth of trust. Friendship should be judged not by freshness, but by faithfulness.","chinese":"在 Joseph Parry 的詩中，友誼被比作珍貴的金屬：新朋友是銀，而老朋友是金 在校園生活中，友誼不斷被重新塑造——一位新的同桌可能成為午餐夥伴，而一位童年好友則可能走進另一個班別、另一個地區，甚至另一個夢想之中 這使年輕人開始思考如何在新舊友誼之間取得平衡，從而建立情感豐富的人生 我的立場是，較長久的友誼更好，因為時間、改變與困難能揭示信任的深度 友誼不應以新鮮感來判斷，而應以忠誠和可靠來衡量。"},{"label":"Paragraph 3","english":"The first difference between old and new friendships lies in shared history. New friendships often begin with similarity, such as the same class, hobby, online game or taste in music. They are exciting because both sides can present polished versions of themselves. By contrast, an old friend knows not only the public version of us but also the unfinished one - the timid child, the awkward teenager, the person who cried after a failed test and pretended to be fine. This history shortens emotional distance. A single phrase—“remember that day?”—can reopen a whole room of memory. More importantly, history gives context. When an old friend notices that I am unusually silent, he does not merely ask whether I am tired; he may recognise my habit of withdrawing when I feel disappointed. Take two classmates who have studied together since junior secondary. By Form Six, one look at a trembling hand before an examination may be enough for one to offer a spare pen, a joke, or quiet company. New friends can be kind, but older friends often understand with greater precision. Old friendship is gold because it carries memory, and memory makes care more intelligent.","chinese":"新舊友誼之間的第一個差別，在於是否擁有共同的過去。 新的友誼往往始於相似之處，例如同一個班別、同一種興趣、同一款網上遊戲，或相近的音樂品味。 它們令人興奮，因為雙方都可以展現自己較完美、較修飾過的一面。 相比之下，一位老朋友認識的不只是我們公開示人的版本，也認識那個尚未完成的自己——那個膽怯的孩子、笨拙的少年，以及那個考試失敗後哭過卻假裝沒事的人。 這段共同歷史縮短了情感上的距離。 一句簡單的話——「還記得那一天嗎？」——便能重新打開整個盛滿回憶的房間。 更重要的是，歷史給予理解的背景。 當一位老朋友注意到我異常沉默時，他不只是問我是否疲倦；他可能會認出我在失望時便會退縮的習慣。 以兩位自初中起便一起學習的同學為例。 到了中六，考試前看見對方顫抖的手，也許已足以讓其中一人遞上一支後備筆、說一句笑話，或只是安靜地陪伴在旁。 新朋友可以很善良，但老朋友往往理解得更加準確細膩。 老友誼之所以是金，是因為它承載著記憶，而記憶使關懷變得更有智慧。"},{"label":"Paragraph 4","english":"Secondly, older friendships are more dependable because they have survived disruption. It is easy to be friendly when life is convenient; when timetables match, jokes land easily and everyone has time to reply. However, the real test comes when circumstances become inconvenient. Friends enter different classes, join different teams, prepare for different futures and, at times, disappoint one another. A friendship that remains respectful through these changes has passed examinations that no written promise can replace. Suppose a student is excluded from a group chat after a misunderstanding. A new friend may hesitate, fearing that taking a side will make him unpopular. An old friend, however, may ask what truly happened, defend him when rumours spread, and still correct him privately if he was wrong. Such loyalty is not blind agreement; rather, it is the courage to stand beside someone without abandoning moral judgement. Thus, friendships that have endured conflict, distance and personal growth deserve special trust. They are not perfect, but they have been tested.","chinese":"第二，較長久的友誼更加可靠，因為它們經歷過動盪仍然留存下來。 當生活方便時，保持友善是容易的；當時間表配合、笑話容易被接住、每個人都有時間回覆時，友誼自然顯得輕鬆。 然而，真正的考驗會在環境變得不方便時出現。 朋友會進入不同班別、加入不同隊伍、準備不同的未來，有時也會令彼此失望 一段能在這些變化中仍然保持尊重的友誼，已經通過了任何書面承諾都無法取代的考驗。 假設一名學生因誤會而被排除在群組聊天之外。 一位新朋友可能會猶豫，因為他害怕表態會令自己不受歡迎。 然而，一位老朋友可能會詢問真正發生了甚麼，在謠言散播時為他辯護，並在他真的做錯時私下糾正他。 這樣的忠誠不是盲目附和；更準確地說，它是一種在不放棄道德判斷的同時仍願意站在某人身旁的勇氣。 因此，那些經歷過衝突、距離與個人成長的友誼，值得特別的信任。 它們並不完美，但它們已經受過考驗。"},{"label":"Paragraph 5","english":"Granted, it would be unfair to dismiss new friendships as shallow. New friends can bring energy, curiosity and fresh perspectives. Sometimes they understand who we are becoming, not only who we used to be. A new friend in a debate club, for instance, may encourage a quiet student to speak publicly, while an old friend may assume that silence means comfort. This is why Parry says not only, “Make new friends,” but also, “keep the old.” Silver has value. It shines, attracts and, given enough time, may become part of the treasure of our lives. Even so, new friendship is more of a promise than proof. Until it is tested by disagreement, boredom or distance, there is no telling whether it is admiration, convenience or genuine commitment. Old friendships are not automatically superior, but when they remain warm after years of change, they have earned a confidence that new friendships have yet to build.","chinese":"誠然，把新的友誼一概視為膚淺是不公平的。 新朋友能帶來活力、好奇心和嶄新的視角。 有時候，他們理解的是我們正在成為怎樣的人，而不只是我們過去是怎樣的人 例如，辯論學會中的一位新朋友可能會鼓勵一名安靜的學生公開發言，而一位老朋友卻可能以為沉默代表自在。 這就是為甚麼 Parry 不只是說「結交新朋友」，也說要「保留老朋友」。 銀也有價值。 它會發亮、會吸引人，而且只要給予足夠時間，也可能成為我們人生寶藏的一部分。 即使如此，新的友誼更多是一種承諾，而不是一種證明。 在它被分歧、沉悶或距離考驗之前，沒有人能說清楚它究竟是欣賞、便利，還是真正的承諾。 老友誼並不是自動更優越；但當它們在多年改變之後仍然保持溫暖時，它們便已贏得一份新友誼尚未建立起來的信心。"},{"label":"Paragraph 6","english":"All things considered, I agree that older friendships are generally better, provided that “better” means deeper, steadier and more fully tested. Students should neither worship the past nor chase every new connection. They should make room for new classmates; at the same time, they should send the message, make the call and repair small misunderstandings before they harden into distance. New friends may add brightness to our lives, but old friends give that brightness a home. Silver is beautiful; gold has been through fire.","chinese":"綜合而言，我同意較長久的友誼通常更好，前提是「更好」的意思是更深厚、更穩定，也更充分地受過考驗。 學生既不應盲目崇拜過去，也不應追逐每一段新的關係。 他們應該為新同學留出空間；與此同時，也應該發出那則訊息、打出那通電話，並在小誤會凝固成距離之前修補它們。 新朋友也許能為我們的人生增添光亮，但老朋友能給那份光亮一個歸宿。 銀很美；但金已經歷過火的淬煉。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"compared to","chinese":"被比作……"},{"english":"precious metals","chinese":"貴金屬"},{"english":"new friends are silver","chinese":"新朋友如銀"},{"english":"old friends are gold","chinese":"舊朋友如金"},{"english":"school life","chinese":"校園生活"},{"english":"constantly reshaped","chinese":"不斷被重塑"},{"english":"a new seatmate","chinese":"新同桌"},{"english":"a lunch companion","chinese":"午餐同伴"},{"english":"a childhood friend","chinese":"童年朋友"},{"english":"move into another class","chinese":"轉到另一班"},{"english":"balance old and new friendships","chinese":"平衡新舊友誼"},{"english":"emotionally rich lives","chinese":"情感豐富的生活"},{"english":"my stance is that","chinese":"我的立場是"},{"english":"time, change and hardship","chinese":"時間、轉變與困難"},{"english":"reveal the depth of trust","chinese":"顯示信任的深度"},{"english":"not by freshness, but by faithfulness","chinese":"不是憑新鮮感，而是憑忠誠"},{"english":"shared history","chinese":"共同經歷"},{"english":"lies in","chinese":"在於……"},{"english":"begin with similarity","chinese":"始於相似之處"},{"english":"the same class","chinese":"同一班"},{"english":"taste in music","chinese":"音樂品味"},{"english":"present polished versions of themselves","chinese":"展示經修飾的自己"},{"english":"by contrast","chinese":"相比之下"},{"english":"the public version of us","chinese":"我們展現於人前的一面"},{"english":"the unfinished one","chinese":"尚未成熟的一面"},{"english":"a timid child","chinese":"膽怯的孩子"},{"english":"an awkward teenager","chinese":"尷尬青澀的少年"},{"english":"pretend to be fine","chinese":"假裝沒事"},{"english":"shorten emotional distance","chinese":"縮短情感距離"},{"english":"a single phrase","chinese":"一句說話"},{"english":"reopen a whole room of memory","chinese":"重新喚起大量回憶"},{"english":"give context","chinese":"提供背景脈絡"},{"english":"unusually silent","chinese":"異常沉默"},{"english":"not merely","chinese":"不只是"},{"english":"recognise my habit of withdrawing","chinese":"察覺我退縮的習慣"},{"english":"feel disappointed","chinese":"感到失望"},{"english":"study together since junior secondary","chinese":"自初中起一起讀書"},{"english":"by Form Six","chinese":"到中六時"},{"english":"one look at","chinese":"看一眼……"},{"english":"a trembling hand","chinese":"顫抖的手"},{"english":"before an examination","chinese":"考試前"},{"english":"offer a spare pen","chinese":"提供一支後備筆"},{"english":"quiet company","chinese":"安靜的陪伴"},{"english":"with greater precision","chinese":"更準確地"},{"english":"carries memory","chinese":"承載回憶"},{"english":"make care more intelligent","chinese":"令關心更懂得分寸"},{"english":"more dependable","chinese":"更可靠"},{"english":"survive disruption","chinese":"經受變動"},{"english":"when life is convenient","chinese":"當生活方便時"},{"english":"timetables match","chinese":"時間表配合"},{"english":"jokes land easily","chinese":"玩笑容易被接住"},{"english":"the real test comes when","chinese":"真正的考驗在於"},{"english":"circumstances become inconvenient","chinese":"情況變得不方便"},{"english":"prepare for different futures","chinese":"為不同的未來作準備"},{"english":"disappoint one another","chinese":"令彼此失望"},{"english":"remain respectful through these changes","chinese":"在轉變中仍保持尊重"},{"english":"pass examinations that no written promise can replace","chinese":"經過文字承諾無法取代的考驗"},{"english":"be excluded from a group chat","chinese":"被群組排除在外"},{"english":"after a misunderstanding","chinese":"在誤會之後"},{"english":"hesitate","chinese":"猶豫"},{"english":"take a side","chinese":"表態支持某一方"},{"english":"make someone unpopular","chinese":"令某人不受歡迎"},{"english":"ask what truly happened","chinese":"問清楚真相"},{"english":"defend someone when rumours spread","chinese":"在謠言傳開時維護某人"},{"english":"correct someone privately","chinese":"私下糾正某人"},{"english":"blind agreement","chinese":"盲目認同"},{"english":"stand beside someone","chinese":"站在某人身旁"},{"english":"moral judgement","chinese":"道德判斷"},{"english":"endure conflict, distance and personal growth","chinese":"經歷衝突、距離與個人成長"},{"english":"deserve special trust","chinese":"值得特別信任"},{"english":"granted","chinese":"誠然"},{"english":"dismiss something as shallow","chinese":"把……視為膚淺而否定"},{"english":"bring energy, curiosity and fresh perspectives","chinese":"帶來活力、好奇心和新觀點"},{"english":"fresh perspectives","chinese":"新角度"},{"english":"who we are becoming","chinese":"我們正在成為怎樣的人"},{"english":"who we used to be","chinese":"我們過去的樣子"},{"english":"encourage someone to speak publicly","chinese":"鼓勵某人公開發言"},{"english":"assume that","chinese":"假設；以為"},{"english":"silence means comfort","chinese":"沉默代表自在"},{"english":"not only…, but also…","chinese":"不但……而且……"},{"english":"keep the old","chinese":"保持舊友誼"},{"english":"have value","chinese":"有價值"},{"english":"given enough time","chinese":"假以時日"},{"english":"become part of the treasure of our lives","chinese":"成為人生寶藏的一部分"},{"english":"more of a promise than proof","chinese":"更像承諾，而非證明"},{"english":"be tested by disagreement","chinese":"受到分歧考驗"},{"english":"there is no telling whether","chinese":"無法判斷是否……"},{"english":"genuine commitment","chinese":"真正的承諾"},{"english":"not automatically superior","chinese":"並非必然較優勝"},{"english":"remain warm after years of change","chinese":"經多年轉變後仍然溫暖"},{"english":"earn confidence","chinese":"贏得信心"},{"english":"have yet to build","chinese":"尚未建立"},{"english":"all things considered","chinese":"總括而言"},{"english":"generally better","chinese":"一般而言更好"},{"english":"provided that","chinese":"前提是"},{"english":"deeper, steadier and more fully tested","chinese":"更深厚、更穩定、更經考驗"},{"english":"worship the past","chinese":"盲目崇拜過去"},{"english":"chase every new connection","chinese":"追逐每一段新關係"},{"english":"make room for","chinese":"為……留位置"},{"english":"send the message","chinese":"傳訊息"},{"english":"make the call","chinese":"打電話"},{"english":"repair small misunderstandings","chinese":"修補小誤會"},{"english":"harden into distance","chinese":"變成疏離"},{"english":"add brightness to our lives","chinese":"為生活增添亮光"},{"english":"give that brightness a home","chinese":"讓那份亮光有歸屬"},{"english":"has been through fire","chinese":"經歷過烈火考驗"}]},"dse-writing-2021-part-b-q9":{"exerciseId":"dse-writing-2021-part-b-q9","essayKey":"","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=dse-writing-2021-part-b-q9","flashDeckId":"dse/writing/part-b/2021/Q9","paragraphs":[{"label":"Paragraph 1","english":"Beneath the Same Roof: A Family Drama for Every Generation","chinese":"同一屋簷下：獻給每一代人的家庭劇"},{"label":"Paragraph 2","english":"The Production Manager TV-Station X","chinese":"製作經理"},{"label":"Paragraph 3","english":"Dear Sir/Madam,","chinese":"敬啟者："},{"label":"Paragraph 4","english":"Re: Proposal for a new TV drama series — Beneath the Same Roof","chinese":"事由：全新電視劇集《同一屋簷下》提案"},{"label":"Paragraph 5","english":"I am writing to propose an original television drama series entitled Beneath the Same Roof, a twelve-episode family story set in present-day Hong Kong. In recent years, many viewers have been drawn to programmes that do not simply entertain them, but also help them recognise their own homes, worries and hopes on screen. With this in mind, I have developed a drama about three generations of the Lau family, who live above a fading cha chaan teng in Sham Shui Po. The series is not just about family quarrels; it is about memory, sacrifice and the quiet courage needed to love people across different ages.","chinese":"本人現寫信提出一個原創電視劇集構思，名為《同一屋簷下》。這是一個以現代香港為背景、共十二集的家庭故事。 近年來，許多觀眾被一些節目吸引，不只是因為它們能帶來娛樂，更因為它們能讓觀眾在螢幕上認出自己的家庭、憂慮與希望。 基於這一點，我構思了一齣關於劉家三代人的劇集；他們住在深水埗一間逐漸褪色的茶餐廳樓上。 這套劇集並不只是關於家庭爭吵；它關乎記憶、犧牲，以及跨越不同年齡去愛人所需要的安靜勇氣。"},{"label":"Paragraph 6","english":"The main characters are deliberately ordinary, because ordinary people often carry the most moving stories. Lau Man-chung, the grandfather, is a retired neon-sign craftsman whose stubborn silence hides years of regret. His daughter, Lau Mei-yan, is a hardworking single mother who manages the family café while trying to keep everyone together. Her younger brother, Lau Wai-hong, has returned from Canada after a failed business venture and is treated as both a stranger and a son. The youngest generation consists of Chloe, a Form Six student who wants to become a documentary filmmaker, and Marcus, her twelve-year-old brother, who understands the family better than the adults realise. Standing between old habits and new ambitions, they give the drama both warmth and tension.","chinese":"主要角色是刻意設定得平凡的，因為平凡人往往承載着最動人的故事。 祖父劉文忠是一位退休霓虹招牌工匠，他固執的沉默背後隱藏着多年的悔疚 他的女兒劉美欣是一位勤奮的單親母親，一邊打理家族咖啡店，一邊努力把所有人維繫在一起。 她的弟弟劉偉康在一次創業失敗後從加拿大回來，在家中既被視為陌生人，也被視為兒子。 最年輕的一代則包括 Chloe，一位想成為紀錄片導演的中六學生，以及她十二歲的弟弟 Marcus；他比成年人所意識到的更了解這個家庭。 站在舊習慣與新抱負之間，他們為這套劇集帶來溫暖，也帶來張力。"},{"label":"Paragraph 7","english":"The setting is central to the story. The Lau family’s café, Golden Years, sits under old signboards, beside newly built flats and opposite a soon-to-close cinema. From the noisy kitchen to the narrow rooftop where Chloe secretly films interviews, every corner reveals a different layer of Hong Kong life. The café is also under threat: a developer offers to buy the building, promising each family member a share of the money. At first glance, selling seems sensible. On closer inspection, however, the offer forces each character to ask what a home is worth when it contains not only property, but also grief, promises and unfinished apologies.","chinese":"故事的場景是整套劇的核心。 劉家的咖啡店 Golden Years 位於舊招牌之下，旁邊是新建成的住宅大廈，對面則是一間即將結業的戲院。 從嘈雜的廚房，到 Chloe 偷偷拍攝訪問的狹窄天台，每一個角落都揭示出香港生活的不同層次。 這間咖啡店同時也面臨威脅：一名發展商提出收購整幢大廈，並承諾每位家庭成員都能分得一筆金錢。 乍看之下，出售似乎是合理的。 可是，仔細一看，這個提議迫使每個角色思考：當一個家所包含的不只是物業，還有悲傷、承諾和未完成的道歉時，它究竟值多少？"},{"label":"Paragraph 8","english":"The plot begins when Chloe discovers a box of old video tapes recorded by her late grandmother. Each tape is linked to one episode and one family secret: a vanished savings book, an unsent letter, a broken wedding bracelet, a quarrel that split the siblings apart. Take episode four, for example: a city-wide blackout traps the family in the café, and, without phones or customers, they finally talk about why Wai-hong left Hong Kong years ago. By the final episode, the family must decide whether to sell Golden Years or turn it into a community kitchen that serves elderly neighbours after closing hours. The ending is hopeful, but not unrealistically perfect: they save part of the café, lose part of the building, and learn that reconciliation, like love, must be rebuilt one conversation at a time.","chinese":"劇情由 Chloe 發現一盒由已故祖母錄下的舊錄影帶開始。 每一盒錄影帶都連繫着一集故事和一個家庭秘密：一本消失的存摺、一封未寄出的信、一隻破裂的結婚手鐲，以及一場令兄妹分裂的爭吵。 以第四集為例：一場全城停電令一家人被困在咖啡店裡；沒有電話，也沒有客人，他們終於談起偉康多年以前離開香港的原因。 到了最後一集，這個家庭必須決定是出售 Golden Years，還是把它變成一間在營業時間後為鄰近長者服務的社區廚房。 結局是充滿希望的，但並不是不切實際的完美：他們保住了咖啡店的一部分，失去了大廈的一部分，也學會了和解就像愛一樣，必須透過一次又一次的對話重新建立。"},{"label":"Paragraph 9","english":"I believe this series would be popular with viewers for two main reasons. First, it speaks to all age groups. Older viewers will respond to Man-chung’s fear of being forgotten; parents will understand Mei-yan’s exhaustion; teenagers will see themselves in Chloe’s hunger to be heard. Few, if any, families are free from misunderstandings, and this drama turns those misunderstandings into scenes of humour, conflict and tenderness. Secondly, the idea has strong visual and emotional appeal. The neon signs, the handwritten menus, the cramped flat and the rooftop skyline would give the drama a distinctive identity, while the mystery of the tapes would encourage viewers to return every week. The more the audience discovers about the Lau family, the more they will want to know whether the family can stay together.","chinese":"我相信這套劇集會受到觀眾歡迎，主要有兩個原因。 首先，它能與所有年齡層的觀眾對話。 年長觀眾會對文忠害怕被遺忘的心情產生共鳴；父母會理解美欣的疲憊；青少年則會在 Chloe 渴望被聆聽的心情中看見自己。 很少家庭，如果有的話，能完全免於誤解，而這套劇集正是把這些誤解轉化為充滿幽默、衝突與溫柔的場景。 其次，這個構思具有強烈的視覺與情感吸引力。 霓虹招牌、手寫餐牌、狹窄單位和天台天際線，都會賦予這套劇鮮明的身份；而錄影帶背後的謎團，則會鼓勵觀眾每週繼續追看。 觀眾越了解劉家，就越想知道這個家庭能否繼續留在一起。"},{"label":"Paragraph 10","english":"I would be grateful if you would consider this proposal for development. Beneath the Same Roof has the potential to become a memorable prime-time drama because it combines a recognisable Hong Kong setting with universal emotions. Home, after all, is where people hurt one another, forgive one another and, one way or another, find their way back.","chinese":"若閣下能考慮把這個提案發展成劇集，本人將不勝感激。 《同一屋簷下》有潛力成為一套令人難忘的黃金時段劇集，因為它把觀眾熟悉的香港場景與普世情感結合起來。 畢竟，家就是人們彼此傷害、彼此原諒，並以某種方式重新找到回去方向的地方。"},{"label":"Paragraph 11","english":"Yours faithfully, Chris Wong","chinese":"謹啟： Chris Wong"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"a family drama for every generation","chinese":"適合各代人觀看的家庭劇"},{"english":"Production Manager","chinese":"製作經理"},{"english":"TV station","chinese":"電視台"},{"english":"a proposal for","chinese":"關於……的建議書"},{"english":"a new TV drama series","chinese":"新電視劇集"},{"english":"I am writing to propose","chinese":"我寫信是為了提議"},{"english":"an original television drama series","chinese":"原創電視劇集"},{"english":"entitled","chinese":"名為"},{"english":"a twelve-episode family story","chinese":"十二集家庭故事"},{"english":"set in present-day Hong Kong","chinese":"以當代香港為背景"},{"english":"in recent years","chinese":"近年來"},{"english":"be drawn to","chinese":"被……吸引"},{"english":"do not simply entertain","chinese":"不只是娛樂"},{"english":"recognise their own homes","chinese":"認出自己的家庭生活"},{"english":"worries and hopes","chinese":"憂慮與希望"},{"english":"on screen","chinese":"在螢幕上"},{"english":"with this in mind","chinese":"考慮到這一點"},{"english":"three generations of","chinese":"三代……"},{"english":"live above","chinese":"住在……樓上"},{"english":"a fading cha chaan teng","chinese":"日漸式微的茶餐廳"},{"english":"family quarrels","chinese":"家庭爭執"},{"english":"not just about","chinese":"不只是關於……"},{"english":"memory and sacrifice","chinese":"回憶與犧牲"},{"english":"quiet courage","chinese":"默默的勇氣"},{"english":"across generations","chinese":"跨世代"},{"english":"deliberately ordinary","chinese":"刻意塑造成平凡"},{"english":"ordinary people","chinese":"平凡人"},{"english":"moving stories","chinese":"動人的故事"},{"english":"a retired neon-sign craftsman","chinese":"退休霓虹招牌工匠"},{"english":"stubborn silence","chinese":"固執的沉默"},{"english":"hide years of regret","chinese":"隱藏多年的遺憾"},{"english":"a hardworking single mother","chinese":"勤奮的單親媽媽"},{"english":"manage the family café","chinese":"經營家庭茶餐廳"},{"english":"keep everyone together","chinese":"維繫一家人"},{"english":"return from Canada","chinese":"從加拿大回來"},{"english":"a failed business venture","chinese":"失敗的創業項目"},{"english":"be treated as both…and…","chinese":"被視為既是……又是……"},{"english":"the youngest generation","chinese":"最年輕一代"},{"english":"consist of","chinese":"由……組成"},{"english":"a Form Six student","chinese":"中六學生"},{"english":"documentary filmmaker","chinese":"紀錄片導演"},{"english":"better than the adults realise","chinese":"比成年人意識到的更清楚"},{"english":"stand between…and…","chinese":"站在……與……之間"},{"english":"old habits","chinese":"舊習慣"},{"english":"new ambitions","chinese":"新抱負"},{"english":"warmth and tension","chinese":"溫情與張力"},{"english":"central to the story","chinese":"對故事十分重要"},{"english":"old signboards","chinese":"舊招牌"},{"english":"newly built flats","chinese":"新建住宅單位"},{"english":"a soon-to-close cinema","chinese":"即將結業的戲院"},{"english":"the noisy kitchen","chinese":"嘈雜的廚房"},{"english":"narrow rooftop","chinese":"狹窄的天台"},{"english":"secretly films interviews","chinese":"偷偷拍攝訪問"},{"english":"every corner reveals","chinese":"每個角落都展現"},{"english":"a different layer of","chinese":"……的不同層面"},{"english":"Hong Kong life","chinese":"香港生活"},{"english":"under threat","chinese":"受到威脅"},{"english":"a developer","chinese":"地產發展商"},{"english":"offer to buy","chinese":"提出收購"},{"english":"promise someone a share of","chinese":"承諾給某人一份……"},{"english":"a share of the money","chinese":"一份金錢；一份款項"},{"english":"at first glance","chinese":"乍看之下"},{"english":"seem sensible","chinese":"看似合理"},{"english":"on closer inspection","chinese":"仔細一看"},{"english":"force someone to ask","chinese":"迫使某人思考"},{"english":"what a home is worth","chinese":"一個家的價值"},{"english":"not only…but also…","chinese":"不但……而且……"},{"english":"unfinished apologies","chinese":"未說出口的道歉"},{"english":"the plot begins when","chinese":"劇情開始於……"},{"english":"discover a box of","chinese":"發現一箱……"},{"english":"old videotapes","chinese":"舊錄影帶"},{"english":"recorded by","chinese":"由……錄製"},{"english":"late grandmother","chinese":"已故祖母"},{"english":"be linked to","chinese":"與……有關"},{"english":"one family secret","chinese":"一個家庭秘密"},{"english":"a vanished savings book","chinese":"消失了的存摺"},{"english":"an unsent letter","chinese":"未寄出的信"},{"english":"a broken wedding bracelet","chinese":"破碎的結婚手鏈"},{"english":"split the siblings apart","chinese":"令兄弟姊妹反目"},{"english":"take episode four, for example","chinese":"以第四集為例"},{"english":"a city-wide blackout","chinese":"全城停電"},{"english":"trap the family in","chinese":"把一家人困在……"},{"english":"without phones or customers","chinese":"沒有電話，也沒有顧客"},{"english":"finally talk about","chinese":"終於談及"},{"english":"years ago","chinese":"多年前"},{"english":"by the final episode","chinese":"到最後一集"},{"english":"decide whether to","chinese":"決定是否"},{"english":"turn it into","chinese":"把它變成"},{"english":"a community kitchen","chinese":"社區廚房"},{"english":"serve elderly neighbours","chinese":"服務長者鄰居"},{"english":"after closing hours","chinese":"營業時間結束後"},{"english":"hopeful but not unrealistically perfect","chinese":"有希望但不過分理想化"},{"english":"save part of","chinese":"保住……的一部分"},{"english":"lose part of","chinese":"失去……的一部分"},{"english":"reconciliation","chinese":"和解"},{"english":"must be rebuilt","chinese":"必須重新建立"},{"english":"one conversation at a time","chinese":"一次談話一步步地"},{"english":"would be popular with viewers","chinese":"會受觀眾歡迎"},{"english":"for two main reasons","chinese":"基於兩個主要原因"},{"english":"speak to all age groups","chinese":"打動各年齡層"},{"english":"respond to","chinese":"對……有共鳴"},{"english":"fear of being forgotten","chinese":"害怕被遺忘"},{"english":"understand someone's exhaustion","chinese":"理解某人的疲累"},{"english":"see themselves in","chinese":"在……身上看到自己"},{"english":"hunger to be heard","chinese":"渴望被聽見"},{"english":"few, if any","chinese":"即使有，也很少"},{"english":"be free from","chinese":"沒有……；不受……影響"},{"english":"misunderstandings","chinese":"誤會"},{"english":"scenes of humour, conflict and tenderness","chinese":"帶有幽默、衝突和溫情的場面"},{"english":"strong visual and emotional appeal","chinese":"強烈的視覺及情感吸引力"},{"english":"neon signs","chinese":"霓虹招牌"},{"english":"handwritten menus","chinese":"手寫餐牌"},{"english":"cramped flat","chinese":"狹小的單位"},{"english":"rooftop skyline","chinese":"天台天際線"},{"english":"distinctive identity","chinese":"鮮明特色"},{"english":"the mystery of the tapes","chinese":"錄影帶之謎"},{"english":"encourage viewers to return","chinese":"鼓勵觀眾繼續收看"},{"english":"every week","chinese":"每星期"},{"english":"the more…the more…","chinese":"越……越……"},{"english":"stay together","chinese":"維繫在一起"},{"english":"I would be grateful if","chinese":"如蒙……我將十分感激"},{"english":"consider this proposal","chinese":"考慮這份建議書"},{"english":"for development","chinese":"作進一步開發"},{"english":"have the potential to","chinese":"有潛力……"},{"english":"a memorable prime-time drama","chinese":"令人難忘的黃金時段劇集"},{"english":"combine…with…","chinese":"把……與……結合"},{"english":"a recognisable Hong Kong setting","chinese":"令人熟悉的香港背景"},{"english":"universal emotions","chinese":"普世情感"},{"english":"home, after all","chinese":"畢竟，家是……"},{"english":"hurt one another","chinese":"互相傷害"},{"english":"forgive one another","chinese":"互相原諒"},{"english":"one way or another","chinese":"無論如何；總會有辦法"},{"english":"find their way back","chinese":"找到回去的路；重修舊好"},{"english":"Yours faithfully","chinese":"謹啟"}]},"dse-writing-2022-part-a":{"exerciseId":"dse-writing-2022-part-a","essayKey":"","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=dse-writing-2022-part-a","flashDeckId":"dse/writing/part-a/2022","paragraphs":[{"label":"Title","english":"A First-Time Visitor’s Guide to Hong Kong Adventure Farm","chinese":"首次遊覽香港冒險農場指南"},{"label":"About Hong Kong Adventure Farm","english":"About Hong Kong Adventure Farm","chinese":"關於香港冒險農場"},{"label":"About Hong Kong Adventure Farm","english":"Established in 2010 and nestled in the green hills of Sai Kung, Hong Kong Adventure Farm is a refreshing escape from city life. Our scenic railway links four stations, placing spectacular views, outdoor adventures and farm-fresh food within easy reach of visitors of all ages seeking an unforgettable day out.","chinese":"香港冒險農場成立於 2010 年，坐落於西貢青翠的山丘之中，是一個讓人暫時遠離城市生活、煥然一新的好去處。 我們的觀景鐵路連接四個車站，讓各個年齡層的遊客都能輕鬆欣賞壯麗景色、體驗戶外歷險，並品嘗農場新鮮美食，度過難忘的一天。"},{"label":"Top three things to see and do","english":"Top three things to see and do","chinese":"三大必看必玩活動"},{"label":"Activity 1: Waterfall Station","english":"Board the railway at Entrance Main Station and make Waterfall Station your first stop. A short walk leads to the farm’s natural showpiece: a magnificent waterfall. Stop at the marked photo point to frame the cascading water against the surrounding greenery—an unforgettable snapshot of your visit.","chinese":"在入口主站登上鐵路，並把瀑布站作為你的第一站。 步行一小段路後，便會到達農場最具代表性的自然景觀：一座壯麗的瀑布。 你可以在標示清楚的拍照點停下來，把飛瀉而下的水流與四周綠意一同收進鏡頭，為這次旅程留下難忘的一幕。"},{"label":"Activity 2: Lake Side Station","english":"Next, continue to Lake Side Station and try kayaking. As you paddle across the water, the wooded landscape unfolds around you, making the experience peaceful yet exhilarating. Those wishing to slow down can also pause nearby for a warm drink before continuing their journey.","chinese":"接着，繼續前往湖畔站，體驗划獨木舟。 當你划槳穿過水面時，林木環繞的景色會在你身邊徐徐展開，令整個體驗既寧靜又令人振奮。 想放慢腳步的遊客，也可以在附近稍作停留，喝一杯暖飲後再繼續旅程。"},{"label":"Activity 3: Riding Area and Farmers’ Market","english":"Finally, make your way to the riding area on the eastern side of the farm. Exploring the countryside on horseback offers a change of pace and a closer connection with nature. Before leaving, travel to Farmers’ Market Station, where you can enjoy a hearty meal and browse fresh farm produce—the perfect way to round off an action-packed day.","chinese":"最後，你可以前往農場東面的騎乘區。 騎馬探索鄉郊景色，能讓旅程節奏有所轉變，也讓你與大自然建立更親近的連繫。 離開之前，你可以前往農夫市集站，在那裏享用一頓豐富的餐點，並選購新鮮農產品，為充滿活動的一天畫上完美句號。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"first-time visitor","chinese":"首次到訪的遊客"},{"english":"visitor's guide","chinese":"遊客指南"},{"english":"Hong Kong Adventure Farm","chinese":"香港冒險農場"},{"english":"established in","chinese":"於……成立"},{"english":"nestled in","chinese":"坐落於；隱於"},{"english":"green hills","chinese":"翠綠山丘"},{"english":"Sai Kung","chinese":"西貢"},{"english":"refreshing escape from","chinese":"令人放鬆的逃離……之地"},{"english":"city life","chinese":"城市生活"},{"english":"scenic railway","chinese":"景觀鐵路"},{"english":"link four stations","chinese":"連接四個車站"},{"english":"spectacular views","chinese":"壯麗景色"},{"english":"outdoor adventures","chinese":"戶外冒險活動"},{"english":"farm-fresh food","chinese":"農場新鮮食物"},{"english":"within easy reach of","chinese":"讓……輕易到達"},{"english":"visitors of all ages","chinese":"各個年齡層的遊客"},{"english":"seek an unforgettable day out","chinese":"尋找難忘的一日遊"},{"english":"unforgettable day out","chinese":"難忘的一日遊"},{"english":"top three things to see and do","chinese":"三大必看必玩活動"},{"english":"board the railway","chinese":"登上鐵路"},{"english":"Entrance Main Station","chinese":"Entrance Main Station（正門站）"},{"english":"make something your first stop","chinese":"將……作為第一站"},{"english":"Waterfall Station","chinese":"Waterfall Station（瀑布站）"},{"english":"a short walk leads to","chinese":"步行一小段路便到達"},{"english":"natural showpiece","chinese":"自然景觀亮點"},{"english":"magnificent waterfall","chinese":"壯觀的瀑布"},{"english":"marked photo point","chinese":"指定拍照點"},{"english":"frame something against","chinese":"以……作背景拍攝……"},{"english":"cascading water","chinese":"傾瀉而下的流水"},{"english":"surrounding greenery","chinese":"周圍的綠意"},{"english":"unforgettable snapshot","chinese":"難忘的照片"},{"english":"continue to","chinese":"繼續前往"},{"english":"Lake Side Station","chinese":"Lake Side Station（湖畔站）"},{"english":"try kayaking","chinese":"嘗試划獨木舟"},{"english":"paddle across the water","chinese":"划過水面"},{"english":"wooded landscape","chinese":"樹林景觀"},{"english":"unfold around you","chinese":"在你身邊展開"},{"english":"peaceful yet exhilarating","chinese":"寧靜卻令人振奮"},{"english":"slow down","chinese":"放慢節奏"},{"english":"pause nearby","chinese":"在附近稍作停留"},{"english":"warm drink","chinese":"熱飲"},{"english":"continue their journey","chinese":"繼續旅程"},{"english":"make your way to","chinese":"前往"},{"english":"riding area","chinese":"騎馬區"},{"english":"eastern side of","chinese":"……的東面"},{"english":"explore the countryside","chinese":"探索郊野"},{"english":"on horseback","chinese":"騎馬"},{"english":"offer a change of pace","chinese":"帶來不同節奏"},{"english":"closer connection with nature","chinese":"與大自然更親近"},{"english":"before leaving","chinese":"離開前"},{"english":"Farmers' Market Station","chinese":"Farmers' Market Station（農墟站）"},{"english":"hearty meal","chinese":"豐富的一餐"},{"english":"browse fresh farm produce","chinese":"瀏覽新鮮農產品"},{"english":"fresh farm produce","chinese":"新鮮農產品"},{"english":"the perfect way to","chinese":"……的完美方式"},{"english":"round off","chinese":"圓滿結束"},{"english":"action-packed day","chinese":"充滿活動的一天"}]},"dse-writing-2022-part-b-q3":{"exerciseId":"dse-writing-2022-part-b-q3","essayKey":"","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=dse-writing-2022-part-b-q3","flashDeckId":"dse/writing/part-b/2022/Q3","paragraphs":[{"label":"Title","english":"A Dream Needs More Than a Dream","chinese":"夢想需要的不只是夢想"},{"label":"Salutation","english":"Dear Kam Chai,","chinese":"親愛的 Kam Chai："},{"label":"Introduction","english":"Your letter has the smell of roasted coffee, but also the weight of a real decision. At 25, you are standing between two doors: one opens to a better-paid promotion in work that does not excite you; the other opens to a café dream shared with friends, full of freedom, risk and possibility. The stakeholder who matters most here is not your company, your friends, or even your future customers. It is you. On balance, my advice is clear: do not resign immediately. Accept the promotion for now, but treat it not as a surrender of your dream, but as a strategic bridge towards it.","chinese":"你的來信帶有烘焙咖啡的香氣，但同時也承載着一個真正重大決定的重量。 在 25 歲的年紀，你正站在兩扇門之間：一扇門通往一份薪酬更高的晉升機會，但那份工作並不能令你感到興奮；另一扇門則通往你與朋友共同擁有的咖啡店夢想，當中充滿自由、風險與可能性。 在這件事上，最重要的持份者不是你的公司、你的朋友，甚至也不是你未來的顧客。 而是你自己。 整體衡量之下，我的建議很清楚：不要立即辭職。 暫時接受這次晉升，但不要把它視為對夢想的放棄，而要把它看成通往夢想的一座策略性橋樑。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"First, a café is a business before it is a romance. Many people imagine warm lighting, the handwritten menu and the smell of fresh pastries; fewer imagine rent, renovation costs, staff wages, food waste, licensing rules, supplier problems and quiet Tuesdays when only three customers walk in. The trouble with passion is that it can make danger look decorative. If you leave now without a financial cushion, one bad month may force you to borrow money, quarrel with your friends, or close before your idea has had time to breathe. Instead, use the promotion to build a runway. For example, set a target: save twelve months of personal expenses and six months of basic business costs; research three possible districts; compare rents; calculate how many cups of coffee and meals you must sell each day to break even. Better still, test the concept through weekend pop-ups, an Instagram pre-order dessert menu, or a booth at a community market. Only when customers pay for your idea, not merely praise it, will you know whether your dream has commercial legs. In practical terms, staying now protects your future freedom.","chinese":"首先，咖啡店在成為一種浪漫之前，先是一門生意。 很多人會想像溫暖的燈光、手寫的餐牌，以及新鮮糕點的香氣；但較少人會想像租金、裝修費、員工薪金、食物浪費、牌照規定、供應商問題，以及只有三位顧客走進來的冷清星期二。 熱情的問題在於，它有時會把危險裝飾得像美好的東西一樣。 如果你現在在沒有財務緩衝的情況下離職，一個差劣的月份就可能迫使你借錢、與朋友爭吵，甚至在你的構思還未有時間發展之前便結業。 相反，你應該利用這次晉升去建立一條起飛跑道。 例如，設定一個目標：儲起十二個月的個人生活開支和六個月的基本營運成本；研究三個可能的地區；比較租金；計算你每天必須賣出多少杯咖啡和多少份餐點才能收支平衡。 更理想的是，透過週末快閃店、Instagram 預訂甜品餐牌，或社區市集攤位來測試這個概念。 只有當顧客願意為你的構思付錢，而不只是口頭稱讚它時，你才會知道你的夢想是否具有商業可行性。 從實際角度來說，現在留下來是在保護你未來的自由。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"Second, the promotion may give you skills that a young café owner badly needs. You say you are “not that interested” in the work. That matters, but boredom does not always mean uselessness. If the new role involves supervising people, handling clients, meeting targets, preparing budgets or solving complaints, it can become a training ground in disguise. A café owner must negotiate with landlords, manage staff, control costs, respond to bad reviews, design promotions and stay calm when the espresso machine breaks down during the lunch rush. These are not dreamy tasks; they are daily survival. Your company, dull as it may seem, might teach you how to listen, decide and act under pressure. Meanwhile, the higher salary can fund your café instead of replacing it. Ask yourself: can I turn this job into a paid apprenticeship for entrepreneurship? If the answer is yes, the promotion is not a cage. It is capital, training and time.","chinese":"第二，這次晉升可能會給你一位年輕咖啡店老闆非常需要的技能。 你說你對這份工作「並不是那麼感興趣」。 這一點很重要，但沉悶並不總是等於無用。 如果新的職位涉及管理員工、處理客戶、達成目標、準備預算或解決投訴，它就可以成為一個偽裝起來的訓練場。 一位咖啡店老闆必須與業主談判、管理員工、控制成本、回應負評、設計推廣活動，並在午餐繁忙時段意式咖啡機壞掉時保持冷靜。 這些不是夢幻的任務；它們是日常生存。 你的公司雖然看起來沉悶，卻可能教會你如何在壓力下聆聽、決定和行動。 與此同時，更高的薪金可以資助你的咖啡店夢想，而不是取代它。 問問自己：我能否把這份工作變成一個有薪的創業學徒訓練？ 如果答案是肯定的，那麼這次晉升就不是一個牢籠。 它是資本、訓練和時間。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 3","english":"Granted, your friends may say, “Why wait? You are young only once.” They have a point. Dreams can become dusty if they are postponed forever. Comfort has a quiet way of becoming a chain, and a good salary can make an unhappy person stay “just one more year” until the dream becomes a dinner story. Be that as it may, the solution is not reckless resignation; it is a deadline with conditions. Do not say vaguely, “I’ll wait a few years.” Say, “I will prepare for eighteen to twenty-four months, and I will leave only if these milestones are met.” Those milestones should include a written partnership agreement with your friends, a tested menu, a realistic budget, a clear division of duties, savings, and evidence of real customer demand. If, after that period, the job is still draining your spirit and the café plan has become solid, leave with courage. If the evidence is weak, revise the plan instead of gambling your future on wishful thinking.","chinese":"誠然，你的朋友可能會說：「為甚麼要等？青春只有一次。」 他們有一定道理。 如果夢想被永遠推遲，它們也會蒙上灰塵。 安逸會悄悄變成鎖鏈，而一份不錯的薪水也可能令一個不快樂的人一年又一年地說「再多做一年」，直到夢想變成飯桌上的故事。 即便如此，解決方法也不是魯莽辭職；而是一個附帶條件的期限。 不要含糊地說：「我會等幾年。」 你應該說：「我會準備十八至二十四個月，而且只有在這些里程碑達成後，我才會離開。」 這些里程碑應包括一份與朋友簽訂的書面合夥協議、一份經過測試的餐牌、一個現實可行的預算、清晰的職責分工、儲蓄，以及真實顧客需求的證據。 如果在那段時間之後，這份工作仍然在耗盡你的精神，而咖啡店計劃已經變得穩固，那就勇敢離開。 如果證據薄弱，就應該修改計劃，而不是把自己的未來押在一廂情願的想法上"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"So, Kam Chai, choose neither fear nor fantasy. Accept the promotion, build your financial base, test your café idea, and set a firm departure date tied to measurable progress. At the end of the day, the best entrepreneurs are not those who leap blindly, but those who prepare so well that the leap becomes smaller. Your dream deserves bravery, yes — but it also deserves discipline. Brew it slowly, and when the time comes, serve it well.","chinese":"所以，Kam Chai，不要選擇恐懼，也不要選擇幻想。 接受這次晉升，建立你的財務基礎，測試你的咖啡店構思，並設定一個與可衡量進展掛鉤的明確離職日期。 說到底，最好的創業者不是那些盲目跳躍的人，而是那些準備得非常充分，以至於跳躍本身變得更小的人。 你的夢想確實值得勇氣——但它同樣值得紀律。 慢慢沖泡它；到了時機成熟之時，就把它好好端上桌。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"needs more than","chinese":"需要的不只是"},{"english":"has the smell of","chinese":"有……的氣息"},{"english":"roasted coffee","chinese":"烘焙咖啡"},{"english":"the weight of","chinese":"……的分量"},{"english":"a real decision","chinese":"真正重大的決定"},{"english":"standing between two doors","chinese":"站在兩個選擇之間"},{"english":"opens to","chinese":"通向"},{"english":"a better-paid promotion","chinese":"薪酬較高的升職機會"},{"english":"does not excite you","chinese":"不能令你感到興奮"},{"english":"opens to a café dream","chinese":"通向開咖啡店的夢想"},{"english":"shared with friends","chinese":"與朋友共同擁有"},{"english":"full of freedom, risk and possibility","chinese":"充滿自由、風險和可能性"},{"english":"the stakeholder who matters most","chinese":"最重要的持份者"},{"english":"matters most","chinese":"最重要"},{"english":"future customers","chinese":"未來顧客"},{"english":"on balance","chinese":"整體來說"},{"english":"do not resign immediately","chinese":"不要立即辭職"},{"english":"accept the promotion for now","chinese":"暫時接受升職"},{"english":"treat it not as ... but as ...","chinese":"不要把它視為……而要視為……"},{"english":"a surrender of your dream","chinese":"放棄夢想"},{"english":"a strategic bridge towards","chinese":"通向……的策略性橋樑"},{"english":"before it is a romance","chinese":"在浪漫想像之前首先是生意"},{"english":"warm lighting","chinese":"溫暖燈光"},{"english":"handwritten menu","chinese":"手寫餐牌"},{"english":"fresh pastries","chinese":"新鮮酥皮糕點"},{"english":"fewer imagine","chinese":"較少人會想像"},{"english":"renovation costs","chinese":"裝修成本"},{"english":"staff wages","chinese":"員工薪酬"},{"english":"food waste","chinese":"食物浪費"},{"english":"licensing rules","chinese":"牌照規定"},{"english":"supplier problems","chinese":"供應商問題"},{"english":"quiet Tuesdays","chinese":"生意冷清的星期二"},{"english":"walk in","chinese":"走進來；光顧"},{"english":"the trouble with","chinese":"……的問題在於"},{"english":"make danger look decorative","chinese":"令危險看起來像裝飾一樣無害"},{"english":"leave now","chinese":"現在離開"},{"english":"without a financial cushion","chinese":"沒有財政緩衝"},{"english":"one bad month","chinese":"一個生意差的月份"},{"english":"force you to","chinese":"迫使你"},{"english":"borrow money","chinese":"借錢"},{"english":"quarrel with","chinese":"與……爭吵"},{"english":"close before","chinese":"在……之前結業"},{"english":"has had time to breathe","chinese":"有時間發展"},{"english":"build a runway","chinese":"建立起步緩衝"},{"english":"set a target","chinese":"訂立目標"},{"english":"personal expenses","chinese":"個人開支"},{"english":"basic business costs","chinese":"基本營運成本"},{"english":"research three possible districts","chinese":"研究三個可能地區"},{"english":"compare rents","chinese":"比較租金"},{"english":"calculate how many","chinese":"計算多少"},{"english":"cups of coffee","chinese":"杯咖啡"},{"english":"meals you must sell","chinese":"你必須售出的餐點"},{"english":"break even","chinese":"收支平衡"},{"english":"better still","chinese":"更好的是"},{"english":"test the concept","chinese":"測試概念"},{"english":"weekend pop-ups","chinese":"週末快閃店"},{"english":"Instagram pre-order dessert menu","chinese":"Instagram 預訂甜品餐牌"},{"english":"a booth at","chinese":"在……的攤位"},{"english":"community market","chinese":"社區市集"},{"english":"only when","chinese":"只有當……才"},{"english":"pay for your idea","chinese":"為你的想法付款"},{"english":"not merely praise it","chinese":"不只是稱讚它"},{"english":"commercial legs","chinese":"商業可行性"},{"english":"in practical terms","chinese":"從實際角度來說"},{"english":"protects your future freedom","chinese":"保護你未來的自由"},{"english":"may give you skills","chinese":"可能給你技能"},{"english":"badly needs","chinese":"非常需要"},{"english":"not that interested in","chinese":"對……不是那麼感興趣"},{"english":"that matters","chinese":"那是重要的"},{"english":"boredom does not always mean uselessness","chinese":"沉悶不一定代表沒有用"},{"english":"the new role involves","chinese":"新職位涉及"},{"english":"supervising people","chinese":"管理員工；督導別人"},{"english":"handling clients","chinese":"處理客戶"},{"english":"meeting targets","chinese":"達成目標"},{"english":"preparing budgets","chinese":"制定預算"},{"english":"solving complaints","chinese":"處理投訴"},{"english":"a training ground in disguise","chinese":"變相的訓練場"},{"english":"negotiate with landlords","chinese":"與業主談判"},{"english":"manage staff","chinese":"管理員工"},{"english":"control costs","chinese":"控制成本"},{"english":"respond to bad reviews","chinese":"回應負評"},{"english":"design promotions","chinese":"設計推廣活動"},{"english":"stay calm when","chinese":"在……時保持冷靜"},{"english":"the espresso machine breaks down","chinese":"咖啡機壞掉"},{"english":"during the lunch rush","chinese":"午餐繁忙時段"},{"english":"dreamy tasks","chinese":"夢幻的工作"},{"english":"daily survival","chinese":"每日生存所需"},{"english":"dull as it may seem","chinese":"雖然看似沉悶"},{"english":"act under pressure","chinese":"在壓力下行動"},{"english":"higher salary","chinese":"較高薪酬"},{"english":"fund your café","chinese":"資助你的咖啡店"},{"english":"instead of replacing it","chinese":"而不是取代它"},{"english":"turn this job into","chinese":"把這份工作變成"},{"english":"a paid apprenticeship","chinese":"有薪學徒訓練"},{"english":"entrepreneurship","chinese":"創業"},{"english":"if the answer is yes","chinese":"如果答案是肯定的"},{"english":"not a cage","chinese":"不是牢籠"},{"english":"capital, training and time","chinese":"資金、訓練和時間"},{"english":"granted","chinese":"誠然"},{"english":"Why wait?","chinese":"為甚麼要等？"},{"english":"young only once","chinese":"青春只有一次"},{"english":"have a point","chinese":"他們說得有道理"},{"english":"become dusty","chinese":"變得塵封"},{"english":"postponed forever","chinese":"永遠被推遲"},{"english":"has a quiet way of","chinese":"會在不知不覺間"},{"english":"becoming a chain","chinese":"變成枷鎖"},{"english":"make an unhappy person stay","chinese":"令不快樂的人留下"},{"english":"just one more year","chinese":"再多留一年"},{"english":"becomes a dinner story","chinese":"變成飯桌上的故事"},{"english":"be that as it may","chinese":"即使如此"},{"english":"reckless resignation","chinese":"魯莽辭職"},{"english":"a deadline with conditions","chinese":"有條件的限期"},{"english":"say vaguely","chinese":"含糊地說"},{"english":"prepare for","chinese":"為……作準備"},{"english":"eighteen to twenty-four months","chinese":"十八至二十四個月"},{"english":"only if","chinese":"只有在……才"},{"english":"milestones are met","chinese":"達到里程碑"},{"english":"a written partnership agreement","chinese":"書面合夥協議"},{"english":"a tested menu","chinese":"經測試的餐牌"},{"english":"a realistic budget","chinese":"實際可行的預算"},{"english":"a clear division of duties","chinese":"清晰的職責分工"},{"english":"evidence of real customer demand","chinese":"真實顧客需求的證據"},{"english":"after that period","chinese":"在那段時間之後"},{"english":"draining your spirit","chinese":"消耗你的精神"},{"english":"has become solid","chinese":"變得穩健"},{"english":"leave with courage","chinese":"勇敢離開"},{"english":"revise the plan","chinese":"修改計劃"},{"english":"instead of gambling","chinese":"而不是拿……去冒險"},{"english":"gambling your future on","chinese":"把未來押在……上"},{"english":"wishful thinking","chinese":"一廂情願的想法"},{"english":"choose neither fear nor fantasy","chinese":"不要選擇恐懼，也不要選擇幻想"},{"english":"build your financial base","chinese":"建立財政基礎"},{"english":"set a firm departure date","chinese":"訂下明確離職日期"},{"english":"tied to","chinese":"與……掛鈎"},{"english":"measurable progress","chinese":"可衡量的進展"},{"english":"at the end of the day","chinese":"說到底"},{"english":"leap blindly","chinese":"盲目一跳"},{"english":"prepare so well that","chinese":"準備得如此充足，以致"},{"english":"the leap becomes smaller","chinese":"風險變得較小"},{"english":"deserves bravery","chinese":"值得你勇敢追求"},{"english":"deserves discipline","chinese":"也值得你有紀律地實踐"},{"english":"brew it slowly","chinese":"慢慢醞釀它"},{"english":"when the time comes","chinese":"當時機成熟時"},{"english":"serve it well","chinese":"好好呈現它"}]},"dse-writing-2023-part-a":{"exerciseId":"dse-writing-2023-part-a","essayKey":"","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=dse-writing-2023-part-a","flashDeckId":"dse/writing/part-a/2023","paragraphs":[{"label":"Title","english":"Pop-up Shop Application Form","chinese":"快閃店申請表"},{"label":"Section A: Company Profile","english":"Section A: Company Profile","chinese":"A 部分：公司簡介"},{"label":"Section A: Company Profile","english":"Planet Smart is a Hong Kong-based enterprise dedicated to designing and distributing eco-friendly household and lifestyle products. Established five years ago, we have steadily built a reputation for championing sustainability through ethically sourced materials, carbon-neutral shipping, and active community outreach programs. Our vision is to reduce plastic waste and promote greener consumption habits across the city.","chinese":"Planet Smart 是一家以香港為基地的企業，致力於設計及分銷環保家居和生活產品。 成立於五年前，我們透過符合道德標準採購的材料、碳中和運輸，以及積極的社區外展計劃，逐步建立起倡導可持續發展的聲譽。 我們的願景是在全城減少塑膠廢物，並推廣更環保的消費習慣。"},{"label":"Section B: Best-selling Product","english":"Section B: Best-selling Product","chinese":"B 部分：最暢銷產品"},{"label":"Section B: Best-selling Product","english":"Among our wide range of items, our reusable BambooSip Water Bottle has emerged as a customer favorite. Crafted from responsibly harvested bamboo, it offers outstanding insulation while remaining lightweight and durable. By switching to BambooSip, users can decrease single-use plastic bottle usage and enjoy a stylish, minimalist design perfect for daily commutes or weekend hikes.","chinese":"在我們種類繁多的產品之中，可重用的 BambooSip Water Bottle 已成為顧客最喜愛的產品。 它由負責任採伐的竹材製成，既具備出色的保溫效能，同時又保持輕巧耐用。 透過轉用 BambooSip，使用者可以減少一次性塑膠瓶的使用，並享受時尚而簡約的設計，非常適合日常通勤或週末遠足。"},{"label":"Section C: In-store Event","english":"Section C: In-store Event","chinese":"C 部分：店內活動"},{"label":"Section C: In-store Event","english":"To spark interest and educate new customers, we plan to host a “Zero-Waste Living Workshop” at our pop-up shop. Participants will learn practical tips to reduce waste at home, including food storage hacks and DIY cleaning solutions. By sharing hands-on demonstrations and offering exclusive product discounts, we aim to inspire our visitors to adopt more sustainable lifestyles and boost our brand’s visibility.","chinese":"為了引起興趣並教育新顧客，我們計劃在快閃店舉辦一個「零廢生活工作坊」。 參加者將學習在家中減少廢物的實用貼士，包括食物儲存技巧和自製清潔方案。 透過分享親身示範並提供專屬產品折扣，我們旨在啟發訪客採納更可持續的生活方式，並提升我們品牌的知名度。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"Pop-up Shop Application Form","chinese":"快閃店申請表"},{"english":"company profile","chinese":"公司簡介"},{"english":"Hong Kong-based enterprise","chinese":"以香港為基地的企業"},{"english":"dedicated to","chinese":"致力於"},{"english":"designing and distributing","chinese":"設計和分銷"},{"english":"eco-friendly household and lifestyle products","chinese":"環保家居及生活用品"},{"english":"established five years ago","chinese":"五年前成立"},{"english":"steadily built a reputation for","chinese":"逐步建立……的名聲"},{"english":"championing sustainability","chinese":"倡導可持續發展"},{"english":"ethically sourced materials","chinese":"符合道德採購原則的材料"},{"english":"carbon-neutral shipping","chinese":"碳中和運送"},{"english":"active community outreach programs","chinese":"積極的社區外展計劃"},{"english":"our vision is to","chinese":"我們的願景是"},{"english":"reduce plastic waste","chinese":"減少塑膠廢物"},{"english":"promote greener consumption habits","chinese":"推廣更環保的消費習慣"},{"english":"across the city","chinese":"在全城；遍及全市"},{"english":"best-selling product","chinese":"最暢銷產品"},{"english":"among our wide range of items","chinese":"在我們眾多產品之中"},{"english":"wide range of","chinese":"種類繁多的"},{"english":"has emerged as","chinese":"已成為"},{"english":"customer favorite","chinese":"深受顧客喜愛的產品"},{"english":"crafted from","chinese":"由……製成"},{"english":"responsibly harvested bamboo","chinese":"負責任採收的竹材"},{"english":"offers outstanding insulation","chinese":"具備出色保溫效能"},{"english":"remaining lightweight and durable","chinese":"同時保持輕巧耐用"},{"english":"lightweight and durable","chinese":"輕巧耐用"},{"english":"by switching to","chinese":"透過轉用"},{"english":"decrease single-use plastic bottle usage","chinese":"減少即棄膠樽使用量"},{"english":"single-use plastic bottle","chinese":"即棄膠樽"},{"english":"stylish, minimalist design","chinese":"時尚簡約的設計"},{"english":"perfect for","chinese":"非常適合"},{"english":"daily commutes","chinese":"日常通勤"},{"english":"weekend hikes","chinese":"週末遠足"},{"english":"in-store event","chinese":"店內活動"},{"english":"spark interest","chinese":"激發興趣"},{"english":"educate new customers","chinese":"教育新顧客"},{"english":"plan to host","chinese":"計劃舉辦"},{"english":"Zero-Waste Living Workshop","chinese":"零廢生活工作坊"},{"english":"participants will learn","chinese":"參加者將會學習"},{"english":"practical tips","chinese":"實用貼士"},{"english":"reduce waste at home","chinese":"減少家居廢物"},{"english":"food storage hacks","chinese":"食物儲存小技巧"},{"english":"DIY cleaning solutions","chinese":"自製清潔用品方法"},{"english":"hands-on demonstrations","chinese":"實際示範"},{"english":"exclusive product discounts","chinese":"獨家產品折扣"},{"english":"aim to inspire","chinese":"旨在啟發"},{"english":"adopt more sustainable lifestyles","chinese":"採納更可持續的生活方式"},{"english":"boost our brand's visibility","chinese":"提升品牌曝光度"}]},"dse-writing-2023-part-b-q5":{"exerciseId":"dse-writing-2023-part-b-q5","essayKey":"","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=dse-writing-2023-part-b-q5","flashDeckId":"dse/writing/part-b/2023/Q5","paragraphs":[{"label":"Paragraph 1","english":"The Wisdom Behind “Once Upon a Time”","chinese":"「從前」背後的智慧"},{"label":"Paragraph 2","english":"When I look at the illustration of children and animals in a forest, I see more than a scene. I see a world where the weak are heard, the lonely are loved and the frightened learn to walk on. In an age of examinations and social comparison, fairy tales and fables may seem childish. Yet they have made young readers like me read not merely for entertainment, but for guidance. From my perspective, these stories have taught me that love begins with understanding, conflict can be survived through forgiveness, and real happiness is built on character rather than luck.","chinese":"當我看着那幅孩子與動物在森林中玩樂的插圖時，我看見的不只是一個場景 我看見的是一個弱小者能被聆聽、孤單者能被愛護，而受驚者也學會繼續前行的世界。 在一個充滿考試與社會比較的年代，童話和寓言也許看似幼稚。 然而，它們讓像我這樣的年輕讀者明白，閱讀不只是為了娛樂，是為了尋找指引。 在我看來，這些故事教會我：愛始於理解，衝突可以透過寬恕而被熬過，而真正的幸福是建立在品格之上，而不是運氣之上。"},{"label":"Paragraph 3","english":"First, fairy tales have taught me that love is not a glittering prize won by beauty, wealth or charm, but a form of patient attention. As a child, I thought stories about princes and princesses were simply about romance. Only later did I notice their deeper question: who is willing to see the hidden worth of another person? In Beauty and the Beast, Belle’s love begins when she recognises loneliness behind ugliness and humanity beneath anger. Likewise, in tales where animals speak and strangers offer help, kindness is returned because it is given without calculation. This has shaped the way I treat people at school. A quiet classmate may be shy rather than unfriendly; a difficult friend may be hurt rather than cold. Once I learned to look beyond the surface, relationships became less like transactions and more like bridges. Love, these stories suggest, is found not by chasing perfection, but by understanding imperfection.","chinese":"首先，童話教會我，愛並不是一件靠美貌、財富或魅力贏回來的閃亮獎品，是一種耐心的關注。 小時候，我以為關於王子和公主的故事單純只是關於浪漫愛情。 直到後來，我才留意到它們更深層的問題：誰願意看見另一個人隱藏起來的價值？ 在《美女與野獸》中，Belle 的愛始於她認出醜陋背後的孤獨，以及憤怒之下的人性。 同樣地，在那些動物會說話、陌生人會伸出援手的故事中，善意之所以得到回報，是因為它本來就是不帶計算地付出。 這也塑造了我在學校待人處事的方式。 一位沉默的同學可能只是害羞，而不是不友善；一位難相處的朋友可能只是受了傷，而不是冷漠。 當我學會看穿表面之後，人際關係便不再那麼像交易，更像一座座橋樑。"},{"label":"Paragraph 4","english":"Second, fairy tales have taught me how to survive family conflicts without allowing bitterness to harden my heart. Many old stories begin at home, not in castles or battlefields: Cinderella is humiliated by her stepfamily; Hansel and Gretel are abandoned; the youngest child in countless tales is ignored or underestimated. These plots may seem extreme, but the emotions behind them are familiar. Every family has moments of jealousy, silence and misunderstanding. What matters is not whether conflict appears, but how we respond when it does. Cinderella’s gentleness is sometimes mistaken for weakness, yet her endurance prevents cruelty from making her cruel. Hansel and Gretel survive because they cooperate, think clearly and protect each other when adults fail them. Therefore, when I quarrel with my parents over grades or with my brother over trivial matters, I try to pause before speaking, because words can become thorns. Family love is not the absence of conflict; it is the decision to keep a door open after conflict.","chinese":"第二，童話教會我如何熬過家庭衝突，同時不讓怨恨使自己的心變得冷硬。 許多古老故事並不是從城堡或戰場開始，是從家中開始：《灰姑娘》被繼母一家羞辱；Hansel 和 Gretel 被遺棄；無數故事中的幼子都被忽視或低估。 這些情節也許看似極端，但它們背後的情感卻並不陌生。 每個家庭都有嫉妒、沉默和誤解的時刻。 重要的不是衝突會不會出現，是當衝突出現時，我們如何回應。 灰姑娘的溫柔有時會被誤解為軟弱，但她的忍耐阻止了殘酷把她也變成殘酷的人。 Hansel 和 Gretel 之所以能生存下來，是因為當大人未能保護他們時，他們選擇合作、冷靜思考，並彼此守護。 因此，當我因成績與父母爭吵，或因瑣事與兄弟爭執時，我會嘗試在說話前停一停，因為言語可以變成刺。"},{"label":"Paragraph 5","english":"Third, fables have taught me to challenge power wisely and to define victory morally. In the real world, the rich and powerful are not always defeated by magic swords. More often, they are challenged by patience, intelligence and integrity. The tortoise defeats the hare not because he is stronger, but because he refuses to be distracted by arrogance. The mouse helps the lion not because he is mighty, but because small kindness can rescue great power from its own limitations. Jack’s adventure up the beanstalk, meanwhile, warns me that courage without judgement can become greed, while daring guided by necessity can break fear. These stories are useful in school life. When an aggressive student dominates a group project, shouting back may only feed the giant. Preparing evidence, dividing duties fairly and speaking calmly are often more effective. We do not defeat unfairness by becoming crueller than the unfair; we defeat it by refusing to surrender our judgement.","chinese":"第三，寓言教會我如何有智慧地挑戰權力，並以道德來定義勝利。 在現實世界裡，富人和有權勢者並不總是被魔法寶劍擊敗。 更多時候，他們是被耐心、智慧和正直所挑戰。 烏龜擊敗兔子，不是因為牠更強壯，是因為牠拒絕被傲慢分散注意力。 老鼠幫助獅子，不是因為牠強大，是因為微小的善意也能把巨大的力量從自身的局限中拯救出來。 同時，Jack 爬上豆莖的冒險提醒我，沒有判斷力的勇氣可以變成貪婪，而由需要引導的膽識則能打破恐懼。 這些故事在校園生活中也很有用。 當一位強勢的同學主導小組報告時，回罵也許只會餵大那個巨人。 準備證據、公平分配職責，並冷靜地表達，往往更加有效。 我們不是透過變得比不公更殘酷來擊敗不公；我們是透過拒絕放棄自己的判斷力來擊敗它。"},{"label":"Paragraph 6","english":"Finally, these stories have changed my understanding of “happily ever after”. When I was young, I imagined it as a palace, a wedding or a treasure chest. Now I see it as something quieter: the peace of knowing that one has loved sincerely, endured pain without losing kindness, and stood up to injustice without selling one’s soul. Fairy tales and fables are not childish escapes from life. They are maps drawn in bright colours, showing us how to walk through dark forests. The children, animals and trees in the picture may belong to a magical world, but the lessons are real. If we carry them into our ordinary lives, we may not live perfectly ever after—but we can live more wisely, more gently and more bravely.","chinese":"最後，這些故事改變了我對「從此幸福快樂」的理解。 小時候，我把它想像成宮殿、婚禮或藏寶箱。 現在，我把它看成一種更安靜的東西：那就是知道自己曾真誠地愛過、在痛苦中仍沒有失去善良，並在面對不公時沒有出賣靈魂的平靜。 童話和寓言並不是逃避人生的幼稚幻想。 它們是一張張以鮮明色彩繪成的地圖，教我們如何穿越黑暗的森林。 如果我們把這些教訓帶進平凡生活中，我們未必能從此完美地生活下去—— 但我們可以活得更有智慧、更溫柔，也更勇敢。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"the wisdom behind","chinese":"……背後的智慧"},{"english":"Once Upon a Time","chinese":"從前；很久很久以前"},{"english":"illustration","chinese":"插圖"},{"english":"children and animals","chinese":"小朋友和動物"},{"english":"in a forest","chinese":"在森林裏"},{"english":"more than a scene","chinese":"不只是一個場景"},{"english":"a world where","chinese":"一個……的世界"},{"english":"the weak are heard","chinese":"弱者被聽見"},{"english":"the lonely are loved","chinese":"孤獨的人被愛"},{"english":"the frightened learn to walk on","chinese":"受驚的人學會繼續前行"},{"english":"in an age of","chinese":"在……的時代"},{"english":"examinations","chinese":"考試"},{"english":"social comparison","chinese":"社會比較"},{"english":"may seem childish","chinese":"可能看似幼稚"},{"english":"fairy tales and fables","chinese":"童話和寓言"},{"english":"young readers","chinese":"年輕讀者"},{"english":"not merely for entertainment","chinese":"不只是為了娛樂"},{"english":"but for guidance","chinese":"而是為了得到指引"},{"english":"from my perspective","chinese":"從我的角度來看"},{"english":"taught me that","chinese":"教曉我"},{"english":"begins with understanding","chinese":"始於理解"},{"english":"conflict can be survived through forgiveness","chinese":"衝突可以透過寬恕渡過"},{"english":"real happiness","chinese":"真正的幸福"},{"english":"built on character rather than luck","chinese":"建基於品格而非運氣"},{"english":"glittering prize","chinese":"閃閃發光的獎品"},{"english":"won by beauty, wealth or charm","chinese":"靠美貌、財富或魅力贏得"},{"english":"a form of patient attention","chinese":"一種耐心的關注"},{"english":"as a child","chinese":"小時候"},{"english":"princes and princesses","chinese":"王子和公主"},{"english":"simply about romance","chinese":"只是關於愛情"},{"english":"only later did I notice","chinese":"直到後來我才注意到"},{"english":"deeper question","chinese":"更深層的問題"},{"english":"willing to see","chinese":"願意看見"},{"english":"hidden worth","chinese":"隱藏的價值"},{"english":"Beauty and the Beast","chinese":"《美女與野獸》"},{"english":"Belle's love begins when","chinese":"Belle 的愛始於"},{"english":"recognises loneliness behind ugliness","chinese":"看見醜陋背後的孤獨"},{"english":"humanity beneath anger","chinese":"憤怒底下的人性"},{"english":"likewise","chinese":"同樣地"},{"english":"tales where animals speak","chinese":"動物會說話的故事"},{"english":"strangers offer help","chinese":"陌生人伸出援手"},{"english":"kindness is returned","chinese":"善意得到回報"},{"english":"given without calculation","chinese":"不計算回報地付出"},{"english":"shaped the way I treat people","chinese":"影響我待人的方式"},{"english":"rather than unfriendly","chinese":"是害羞而不是不友善"},{"english":"difficult friend","chinese":"難相處的朋友"},{"english":"hurt rather than cold","chinese":"是受傷而不是冷漠"},{"english":"look beyond the surface","chinese":"看穿表面"},{"english":"relationships became less like transactions","chinese":"關係變得不再像交易"},{"english":"more like bridges","chinese":"更像橋樑"},{"english":"not by chasing perfection","chinese":"不是靠追求完美"},{"english":"understanding imperfection","chinese":"理解不完美"},{"english":"survive family conflicts","chinese":"渡過家庭衝突"},{"english":"without allowing bitterness to","chinese":"不讓怨恨……"},{"english":"bitterness","chinese":"怨恨"},{"english":"harden my heart","chinese":"令我的心變硬"},{"english":"begin at home","chinese":"從家裏開始"},{"english":"not in castles or battlefields","chinese":"不是在城堡或戰場"},{"english":"castles","chinese":"城堡"},{"english":"battlefields","chinese":"戰場"},{"english":"humiliated by","chinese":"被……羞辱"},{"english":"stepfamily","chinese":"繼親家庭"},{"english":"abandoned","chinese":"被遺棄"},{"english":"the youngest child","chinese":"最年幼的孩子"},{"english":"countless tales","chinese":"無數故事"},{"english":"ignored or underestimated","chinese":"被忽視或低估"},{"english":"seem extreme","chinese":"看似極端"},{"english":"emotions behind them","chinese":"背後的情感"},{"english":"moments of jealousy","chinese":"嫉妒的時刻"},{"english":"silence and misunderstanding","chinese":"沉默和誤解"},{"english":"what matters is not whether…, but how…","chinese":"重要的不是……而是……"},{"english":"conflict appears","chinese":"衝突出現"},{"english":"respond when it does","chinese":"當它出現時作出回應"},{"english":"gentleness","chinese":"溫柔"},{"english":"mistaken for weakness","chinese":"被誤認為軟弱"},{"english":"endurance","chinese":"忍耐；承受力"},{"english":"prevents cruelty from making her cruel","chinese":"防止殘酷令她也變得殘酷"},{"english":"cooperate","chinese":"合作"},{"english":"think clearly","chinese":"清晰思考"},{"english":"protect each other","chinese":"保護彼此"},{"english":"when adults fail them","chinese":"當成年人辜負他們時"},{"english":"quarrel with","chinese":"與……爭吵"},{"english":"over grades","chinese":"因成績"},{"english":"trivial matters","chinese":"瑣碎事情"},{"english":"pause before speaking","chinese":"說話前停一停"},{"english":"words can become thorns","chinese":"說話可以變成刺"},{"english":"the absence of conflict","chinese":"沒有衝突"},{"english":"the decision to keep a door open","chinese":"衝突後仍留下溝通空間的決定"},{"english":"after conflict","chinese":"衝突過後"},{"english":"challenge power wisely","chinese":"明智地挑戰權力"},{"english":"define victory morally","chinese":"以道德方式界定勝利"},{"english":"in the real world","chinese":"在現實世界中"},{"english":"the rich and powerful","chinese":"富有而有權勢的人"},{"english":"defeated by","chinese":"被……打敗"},{"english":"magic swords","chinese":"魔法劍"},{"english":"more often","chinese":"更常見的是"},{"english":"challenged by","chinese":"被……挑戰"},{"english":"patience, intelligence and integrity","chinese":"耐性、智慧和正直"},{"english":"the tortoise defeats the hare","chinese":"龜打敗兔子"},{"english":"refuses to be distracted by","chinese":"拒絕被……分散注意力"},{"english":"arrogance","chinese":"傲慢"},{"english":"the mouse helps the lion","chinese":"老鼠幫助獅子"},{"english":"mighty","chinese":"強大的"},{"english":"small kindness","chinese":"細小的善意"},{"english":"rescue great power from","chinese":"把強大的力量從……中拯救出來"},{"english":"its own limitations","chinese":"自身的限制"},{"english":"meanwhile","chinese":"同時；另一方面"},{"english":"adventure up the beanstalk","chinese":"爬上豆莖的冒險"},{"english":"warns me that","chinese":"警告我"},{"english":"courage without judgement","chinese":"沒有判斷力的勇氣"},{"english":"daring guided by necessity","chinese":"由需要引導的膽量"},{"english":"break fear","chinese":"打破恐懼"},{"english":"school life","chinese":"校園生活"},{"english":"aggressive student","chinese":"具攻擊性的學生"},{"english":"dominates a group project","chinese":"主導小組習作"},{"english":"shouting back","chinese":"回罵"},{"english":"feed the giant","chinese":"只會助長對方氣焰"},{"english":"preparing evidence","chinese":"準備證據"},{"english":"dividing duties fairly","chinese":"公平分配職責"},{"english":"speaking calmly","chinese":"冷靜說話"},{"english":"more effective","chinese":"更有效"},{"english":"defeat unfairness","chinese":"戰勝不公平"},{"english":"by becoming crueller than","chinese":"透過變得比……更殘酷"},{"english":"refuse to surrender","chinese":"拒絕放棄"},{"english":"surrender our judgement","chinese":"放棄判斷力"},{"english":"understanding of","chinese":"對……的理解"},{"english":"happily ever after","chinese":"從此幸福快樂"},{"english":"imagined it as","chinese":"把它想像成"},{"english":"treasure chest","chinese":"寶箱"},{"english":"see it as something quieter","chinese":"把它看成更平靜的東西"},{"english":"the peace of knowing that","chinese":"知道……而得到的平靜"},{"english":"loved sincerely","chinese":"真誠地愛過"},{"english":"endured pain","chinese":"承受痛苦"},{"english":"without losing kindness","chinese":"沒有失去善良"},{"english":"stood up to injustice","chinese":"挺身面對不公義"},{"english":"without selling one's soul","chinese":"沒有出賣靈魂"},{"english":"childish escapes from life","chinese":"逃避人生的幼稚幻想"},{"english":"maps drawn in bright colours","chinese":"用鮮明色彩繪成的地圖"},{"english":"walk through dark forests","chinese":"走過黑暗森林"},{"english":"belong to a magical world","chinese":"屬於魔法世界"},{"english":"the lessons are real","chinese":"教訓是真實的"},{"english":"carry them into","chinese":"把它們帶進"},{"english":"ordinary lives","chinese":"平凡生活"},{"english":"live perfectly ever after","chinese":"從此完美地生活"},{"english":"live more wisely","chinese":"活得更有智慧"},{"english":"more gently","chinese":"活得更溫柔"},{"english":"more bravely","chinese":"活得更勇敢"}]},"dse-writing-2023-part-b-q8":{"exerciseId":"dse-writing-2023-part-b-q8","essayKey":"","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=dse-writing-2023-part-b-q8","flashDeckId":"","paragraphs":[{"label":"Paragraph 1","english":"Should AI-Composed Songs Be Excluded or Accommodated?","chinese":""},{"label":"Paragraph 2","english":"To the Editor:","chinese":""},{"label":"Paragraph 3","english":"I am writing in response to the ongoing debate regarding the recent songwriting competition in which an artificially composed track triumphed, to the dismay of many human contestants. Although I sympathize with the concerns about fairness and creativity, I believe that computer-generated music is an inevitable facet of our digital age. Rather than excluding AI-composed songs altogether, competition organizers can take steps to preserve the contest’s integrity while embracing the future of musical innovation.","chinese":""},{"label":"Paragraph 4","english":"First, one must acknowledge that the boundaries between technology and art have been shifting for decades. From modern studio technology that can correct pitch or layer complex sounds to digital libraries of pre-recorded loops, human composers already rely on a variety of automated tools. Indeed, AI-driven systems represent a natural progression of this process, producing compositions that draw upon vast databases of musical styles, chord structures, and even cultural influences. This technology can free artists from repetitive tasks, allowing them to focus on more nuanced aspects of songwriting such as developing a compelling message or experimenting with new harmonic directions. Consequently, banning AI contributions outright may hinder the evolution of music, undermining the potential for a fresh era of innovation.","chinese":""},{"label":"Paragraph 5","english":"Still, there is no denying that fairness is a legitimate concern for contestants who devote weeks or even months to perfecting their craft, only to find that an algorithm can generate multiple prototypes in mere minutes. It is thus vital to ensure transparency in the competition’s rules. Organizers should require that participants disclose any AI-driven processes or software they utilize in composing their entries. By mandating open declarations of AI involvement, judges and audiences would be better able to discern how much of a track’s originality stems from human effort. In cases where AI has played the dominant role, separate awards or specialized categories could be established for those pieces, allowing human-composed works to remain on a comparable playing field.","chinese":""},{"label":"Paragraph 6","english":"Moreover, one must consider the broader educational and cultural implications. With artificial intelligence proliferating in diverse creative spheres, it is beneficial for aspiring musicians to observe how machine learning and algorithmic tools can expedite production and spark new artistic ideas. By exposing students and amateur composers to these technologies, the competition can expand their horizons in terms of technique and inspiration, bridging the gap between tradition and cutting-edge developments. This intersection of music and data science likewise paves the way for unexpected collaborations, as teams composed of programmers, composers, and sound engineers pool their distinct expertise to craft original pieces that transcend conventional genres.","chinese":""},{"label":"Paragraph 7","english":"Admittedly, there are critics who question whether AI-generated songs can convey genuine human emotion. They argue that the poignancy of a meaningful track derives from personal experience, a dimension that computers are unable to replicate. While it is true that no algorithm has consciousness or emotional depth, listeners ultimately judge a song by how it resonates with them. If an AI-composed melody stirs one’s emotions, then dismissing it on the basis that it is “less authentic” may be arbitrary. Nevertheless, to respect the essence of human expression, organizers might implement criteria that reward authenticity and personal storytelling, giving an edge to contestants who compose without machine assistance. Through such scoring standards, competitions could recognize the intangible element of human sentiment while still acknowledging AI’s capacity to produce intriguing new works.","chinese":""},{"label":"Paragraph 8","english":"Ultimately, a blanket exclusion of AI from songwriting contests may do more harm than good, depriving both audiences and creators of a unique opportunity to witness musical frontiers being pushed ever outward. The right path forward involves establishing transparent rules, encouraging separate categories where appropriate, and celebrating the diverse modes of creation that now exist. Music has always been characterized by the interplay between tradition and experimentation, and artificial intelligence represents the latest chapter in that story. By allowing it a place—albeit a carefully structured one—competitions can honor the nuanced talent of human composers while keeping pace with the thrilling innovations reshaping our cultural landscape.","chinese":""},{"label":"Paragraph 9","english":"Yours faithfully,","chinese":""},{"label":"Paragraph 10","english":"Chris Wong","chinese":""}],"vocabulary":[]},"dse-writing-2023-part-b-q8-bilingual":{"exerciseId":"dse-writing-2023-part-b-q8-bilingual","essayKey":"","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=dse-writing-2023-part-b-q8-bilingual","flashDeckId":"","paragraphs":[{"label":"Paragraph 1","english":"Let AI Inspire Songs, Not Win Human Songwriting Prizes","chinese":"讓 AI 啟發歌曲，而不是贏走人類作曲獎項"},{"label":"Paragraph 2","english":"Dear Editor,","chinese":"編輯先生／女士："},{"label":"Paragraph 3","english":"No sooner had the result of the recent “Best Song Writer” competition been announced than complaints spread: first prize had gone to a song created by AI software.","chinese":"最近「Best Song Writer」比賽結果才剛公布，投訴便隨即傳開：首獎落入了一首由 AI 軟件創作的歌曲手中。"},{"label":"Paragraph 4","english":"The event logo captures the awkward question facing organisers and contestants: should a machine be treated as a competitor in a contest designed to reward human creativity?","chinese":"這個活動標誌正好呈現了主辦方和參賽者所面對的尷尬問題：在一個旨在獎勵人類創意的比賽中，一台機器是否應被視為競爭者？"},{"label":"Paragraph 5","english":"To my mind, computer-generated songs should not compete in the same category as songs written by people.","chinese":"在我看來，電腦生成歌曲不應與人類創作的歌曲在同一組別中競爭。"},{"label":"Paragraph 6","english":"AI may be used as a declared tool, and AI-only sections may be created, but ordinary songwriting prizes should remain reserved for human authorship.","chinese":"AI 可以作為已申報的工具使用，也可以設立 AI 專屬組別，但一般作曲獎項仍應保留給人類創作。"},{"label":"Paragraph 7","english":"Otherwise, competitions will reward technical access rather than artistic imagination, weaken public trust and confuse the meaning of “best songwriter.”","chinese":"否則，比賽所獎勵的將會是取得技術的能力，而不是藝術想像力；這也會削弱公眾信任，並混淆「最佳作曲人」的真正含義。"},{"label":"Paragraph 8","english":"First, allowing AI-generated songs to compete directly with human entries would make the competition fundamentally unfair.","chinese":"首先，容許 AI 生成歌曲與人類作品直接競爭，會令比賽從根本上變得不公平"},{"label":"Paragraph 9","english":"A human songwriter starts with memory, emotion, musical training and trial and error.","chinese":"一位人類作曲人的創作，是從記憶、情感、音樂訓練，以及反覆嘗試與修正開始的。"},{"label":"Paragraph 10","english":"She may rewrite one line to capture heartbreak; he may hum a melody on a minibus before shaping it into a chorus at midnight.","chinese":"她也許會重寫一句歌詞，只為捕捉心碎的感覺；他也許會在小巴上哼出一段旋律，然後在午夜把它塑造成副歌。"},{"label":"Paragraph 11","english":"By contrast, an AI system can produce polished versions in minutes once a user enters a prompt.","chinese":"相比之下，只要使用者輸入一個提示，AI 系統便可以在數分鐘內產出經打磨的版本。"},{"label":"Paragraph 12","english":"The issue is not that technology is evil; it is that the starting points are not comparable.","chinese":"問題並不是科技邪惡，而是兩者的起點並不可相比。"},{"label":"Paragraph 13","english":"In a school sports day, we would not let one runner use an electric scooter and then praise him for speed.","chinese":"在學校運動會中，我們不會容許一名跑手使用電動滑板車，然後再稱讚他速度快。"},{"label":"Paragraph 14","english":"Similarly, in a songwriting contest, we should not let a contestant outsource most of the creative labour to software and then claim the same recognition as those who wrestled with silence, doubt and revision.","chinese":"同樣地，在作曲比賽中，我們不應容許參賽者把大部分創作勞動外判給軟件，然後要求得到與那些曾經面對沉默、懷疑和反覆修改的創作者相同的認可"},{"label":"Paragraph 15","english":"Competitions exist to compare similar forms of effort.","chinese":"比賽的存在，是為了比較相近形式的努力。"},{"label":"Paragraph 16","english":"Once the method of creation differs so radically, the prize rewards the better tool, not necessarily the better songwriting talent.","chinese":"一旦創作方法存在如此根本的差異，獎項所獎勵的便是更優勝的工具，而不一定是更出色的作曲才能。"},{"label":"Paragraph 17","english":"More importantly, AI-generated songs threaten the integrity and purpose of such competitions.","chinese":"更重要的是，AI 生成歌曲會威脅這類比賽的公正性與宗旨。"},{"label":"Paragraph 18","english":"A songwriting prize is not merely a search for a catchy tune.","chinese":"作曲獎項並不只是尋找一段朗朗上口的旋律。"},{"label":"Paragraph 19","english":"It is a public recognition of originality, voice and human experience.","chinese":"它是對原創性、個人聲音和人類經驗的一種公開肯定。"},{"label":"Paragraph 20","english":"Behind a good song there is usually a point of view: a teenager’s loneliness, a parent’s regret, a city’s restless energy, or a community memory that refuses to disappear.","chinese":"一首好歌背後，通常都有一種觀點：一名青少年的孤獨、一位父母的遺憾、一座城市躁動不安的能量，或一段拒絕消失的社群記憶。"},{"label":"Paragraph 21","english":"AI can imitate these emotions, sometimes impressively, but imitation is not lived feeling.","chinese":"AI 可以模仿這些情感，有時甚至模仿得令人印象深刻；但模仿並不等於親身活過的感受。"},{"label":"Paragraph 22","english":"If a computer-generated song wins, listeners may reasonably ask: who is responsible for the lyric?","chinese":"如果一首電腦生成歌曲勝出，聽眾很合理地可以問：誰應該為歌詞負責？"},{"label":"Paragraph 23","english":"Who made the artistic choice?","chinese":"是誰作出了藝術選擇？"},{"label":"Paragraph 24","english":"Who owns the emotional truth—the contestant, the programmer, or the dataset?","chinese":"誰擁有那份情感上的真實性——參賽者、程式設計師，還是數據集？"},{"label":"Paragraph 25","english":"Such uncertainty damages trust.","chinese":"這種不確定性會損害信任。"},{"label":"Paragraph 26","english":"It may also discourage young writers without expensive software from joining future competitions.","chinese":"它也可能令沒有昂貴軟件的年輕創作者不願參加日後的比賽。"},{"label":"Paragraph 27","english":"If contestants begin to believe that the surest path to victory is simply to generate, select and submit, the event will become less a celebration of art than a test of prompt engineering.","chinese":"如果參賽者開始相信，通往勝利最穩妥的方法只是生成、挑選和提交，那麼這項活動便不再像是對藝術的慶祝，而更像是一場提示工程的測試。"},{"label":"Paragraph 28","english":"Admittedly, some may argue that banning AI entries is old-fashioned.","chinese":"誠然，有些人可能會認為，禁止 AI 作品參賽是一種守舊做法。"},{"label":"Paragraph 29","english":"After all, musicians have always used new tools, from synthesisers to digital editing software.","chinese":"畢竟，音樂人一直都有使用新工具，從合成器到數碼剪輯軟件皆是如此。"},{"label":"Paragraph 30","english":"This argument deserves respect, but it misses the central distinction.","chinese":"這個論點值得尊重，但它忽略了核心分別。"},{"label":"Paragraph 31","english":"A tool assists; a substitute replaces.","chinese":"工具是輔助；替代品則是取代。"},{"label":"Paragraph 32","english":"A keyboard does not decide the melody for the composer.","chinese":"鍵盤不會替作曲人決定旋律。"},{"label":"Paragraph 33","english":"Auto-tune does not, by itself, invent the theme of a song.","chinese":"自動修音本身不會創造一首歌的主題。"},{"label":"Paragraph 34","english":"AI, however, can generate the lyrics, chords and structure before the so-called songwriter has made any meaningful artistic decision.","chinese":"然而，AI 可以在所謂作曲人作出任何有實質意義的藝術決定之前，已經生成歌詞、和弦和結構。"},{"label":"Paragraph 35","english":"Therefore, the sensible answer is not to reject AI completely, but to regulate it honestly.","chinese":"因此，合理的答案並不是完全拒絕 AI，而是以誠實透明的方式規管它。"},{"label":"Paragraph 36","english":"Competitions could require contestants to declare how AI was used, allow minor AI assistance for editing or arrangement, and create a separate “AI-assisted music” category.","chinese":"比賽可以要求參賽者申報 AI 的使用方式，容許 AI 在編輯或編曲方面提供輕微協助，並設立一個獨立的「AI 輔助音樂」組別。"},{"label":"Paragraph 37","english":"That way, innovation is welcomed without pretending that all creative processes are identical.","chinese":"這樣一來，創新可以被接納，同時也無需假裝所有創作過程都是相同的。"},{"label":"Paragraph 38","english":"Transparency, not blind enthusiasm, is the bridge between technology and fairness.","chinese":"透明度，而不是盲目熱情，才是科技與公平之間的橋樑。"},{"label":"Paragraph 39","english":"In conclusion, computer-generated songs should not be allowed to compete against human-written songs in ordinary songwriting competitions.","chinese":"總而言之，電腦生成歌曲不應被允許在一般作曲比賽中與人類創作的歌曲競爭"},{"label":"Paragraph 40","english":"Such entries may sound impressive, but they raise serious concerns about fairness, authorship and trust.","chinese":"這類作品聽起來也許令人印象深刻，但它們會引起關於公平、作者身份和信任的嚴重疑慮。"},{"label":"Paragraph 41","english":"Organisers should revise their rules, define acceptable AI assistance clearly and introduce separate categories where necessary.","chinese":"主辦方應該修訂規則，清楚界定可接受的 AI 協助，並在有需要時引入獨立組別。"},{"label":"Paragraph 42","english":"AI may become a valuable partner in music-making, but it should not be allowed to wear the medal meant for human imagination.","chinese":"AI 也許會成為音樂創作中有價值的夥伴，但它不應被容許戴上本應屬於人類想像力的獎牌。"},{"label":"Paragraph 43","english":"A song can be produced by a machine; a songwriter, in the deepest sense, must still be human.","chinese":"一首歌可以由機器生產；但作曲人，在最深層的意義上，仍然必須是人。"},{"label":"Paragraph 44","english":"Yours faithfully,","chinese":"謹啟，"}],"vocabulary":[]},"dse-writing-2024-part-a":{"exerciseId":"dse-writing-2024-part-a","essayKey":"","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=dse-writing-2024-part-a","flashDeckId":"dse/writing/part-a/2024","paragraphs":[{"label":"Salutation","english":"Dear Hotel Manager,","chinese":"尊敬的酒店經理："},{"label":"Introduction","english":"I am writing to lodge a formal complaint about my recent one-night stay at the Seaside Hotel, booked through your website for HK$1,580. I made the reservation in good faith because the advertisement clearly promised a non-smoking room with a balcony, an ocean view, Wi-Fi, room service, air conditioning, and all taxes and fees included.","chinese":"本人寫信是為了就最近透過貴酒店網站預訂、價值港幣 1,580 元的 Seaside Hotel 一晚住宿，正式提出投訴。 本人是基於信任而作出預訂，因為該廣告清楚承諾房間為非吸煙客房，並設有露台、海景、Wi-Fi、客房送餐服務、空調，而且所有稅項及費用均已包括在內。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"Unfortunately, the room allocated to me fell far below this description. Far from enjoying an ocean view, I was given a room facing a noisy main road, and there was no balcony at all. In addition, the Wi-Fi connection was so weak that it was practically unusable, while the air conditioner was both loud and ineffective. When I attempted to order room service, I was informed that it was unavailable. Most disturbingly, the room smelled strongly of cigarette smoke despite being advertised as non-smoking. To make matters worse, I was charged an additional service fee at check-out, even though your website explicitly stated that taxes and fees were included.","chinese":"可惜，分配給本人的房間遠遠低於上述描述。 本人不但沒有享受到海景，反而被安排入住一間面向嘈雜大馬路的房間，而且完全沒有露台。 此外，Wi-Fi 連線非常微弱，實際上幾乎無法使用，而空調既嘈吵又沒有實際效用。 當本人嘗試要求客房送餐服務時，卻被告知該服務並不提供。 最令人不安的是，儘管該房間被宣傳為非吸煙客房，房內卻有濃烈的香煙氣味。 更糟糕的是，本人在退房時被額外收取服務費，儘管貴酒店網站明確列明稅項及費用均已包括在內。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"As I relied on the accuracy of your advertisement when making my booking, I find this discrepancy both misleading and unacceptable. I would therefore expect a partial refund, a written apology, and a clear explanation of how this matter will be addressed. I also strongly urge your hotel to amend the online advertisement immediately so that future guests will not be similarly misled.","chinese":"由於本人在預訂時依賴貴酒店廣告內容的準確性，因此本人認為這種差異既具誤導性，也令人無法接受。 因此，本人期望獲得部分退款、書面道歉，以及一個清楚說明貴酒店將如何處理此事的解釋。 本人強烈敦促貴酒店立即修改網上廣告，以免日後的住客同樣受到類似誤導。"},{"label":"Sign-off","english":"Yours faithfully,","chinese":"此致"},{"label":"Name","english":"Chris Wong","chinese":"Chris Wong"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"lodge a formal complaint","chinese":"正式投訴"},{"english":"recent one-night stay","chinese":"最近一晚的住宿"},{"english":"booked through","chinese":"透過……預訂"},{"english":"made the reservation","chinese":"作出預訂"},{"english":"in good faith","chinese":"出於信任；真誠地"},{"english":"the advertisement clearly promised","chinese":"廣告清楚承諾"},{"english":"non-smoking room","chinese":"非吸煙房"},{"english":"with a balcony","chinese":"設有露台"},{"english":"an ocean view","chinese":"海景"},{"english":"room service","chinese":"客房送餐服務"},{"english":"air conditioning","chinese":"空調"},{"english":"all taxes and fees included","chinese":"已包括所有稅項及費用"},{"english":"the room allocated to me","chinese":"分配給我的房間"},{"english":"fell far below","chinese":"遠遠低於；與……相差甚遠"},{"english":"this description","chinese":"這個描述"},{"english":"far from enjoying","chinese":"不但沒有……反而"},{"english":"facing a noisy main road","chinese":"面向嘈雜的大路"},{"english":"no balcony at all","chinese":"完全沒有露台"},{"english":"in addition","chinese":"此外"},{"english":"Wi-Fi connection","chinese":"Wi-Fi 連接"},{"english":"so weak that","chinese":"弱到……以致"},{"english":"practically unusable","chinese":"幾乎無法使用"},{"english":"both loud and ineffective","chinese":"既嘈吵又無效"},{"english":"attempted to order","chinese":"嘗試點叫"},{"english":"was informed that","chinese":"被告知"},{"english":"most disturbingly","chinese":"最令人不安的是"},{"english":"smelled strongly of","chinese":"有強烈的……氣味"},{"english":"cigarette smoke","chinese":"香煙煙味"},{"english":"despite being advertised as","chinese":"儘管被宣傳為"},{"english":"to make matters worse","chinese":"更糟的是"},{"english":"was charged","chinese":"被收取"},{"english":"an additional service fee","chinese":"額外服務費"},{"english":"at check-out","chinese":"退房時"},{"english":"even though","chinese":"即使"},{"english":"explicitly stated that","chinese":"明確說明"},{"english":"taxes and fees","chinese":"稅項及費用"},{"english":"relied on the accuracy of","chinese":"依賴……的準確性"},{"english":"when making my booking","chinese":"預訂時"},{"english":"this discrepancy","chinese":"這種不符之處"},{"english":"both misleading and unacceptable","chinese":"既具誤導性又不可接受"},{"english":"would therefore expect","chinese":"因此期望"},{"english":"a partial refund","chinese":"部分退款"},{"english":"a written apology","chinese":"書面道歉"},{"english":"a clear explanation of","chinese":"清楚解釋"},{"english":"how this matter will be addressed","chinese":"這件事將如何處理"},{"english":"strongly urge","chinese":"強烈敦促"},{"english":"amend the online advertisement","chinese":"修改網上廣告"},{"english":"future guests","chinese":"日後住客"},{"english":"similarly misled","chinese":"同樣被誤導"}]},"dse-writing-2024-part-b-q4":{"exerciseId":"dse-writing-2024-part-b-q4","essayKey":"","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=dse-writing-2024-part-b-q4","flashDeckId":"","paragraphs":[{"label":"Paragraph 1","english":"Dog-Friendly, Not Dog-Dominated: A Fairer Way Forward","chinese":"對狗友善，而非由狗主導：邁向更公平的出路"},{"label":"Paragraph 2","english":"Dear Editor,","chinese":"編輯先生／女士："},{"label":"Paragraph 3","english":"In recent years, Hong Kong’s relationship with pets has changed visibly. Parks now welcome leashed companions, shops place water bowls outside, and some restaurants even offer pet-friendly seating. With more residents treating dogs as family members, businesses and public bodies have opened more spaces to them in order to make city life warmer and more inclusive. I support this dog-friendly trend, provided that it is guided by clear rules and civic responsibility. The real challenge is not whether dogs belong in the city, but how humans can share space decently.","chinese":"近年來，香港與寵物之間的關係出現了明顯變化。 如今，公園歡迎繫上狗帶的動物夥伴，商店在門外放置水碗，一些餐廳甚至提供寵物友善座位。 隨着越來越多居民把狗隻視為家庭成員，商界和公共機構也向牠們開放更多空間，目的是讓城市生活變得更溫暖、更具包容性。 我支持這股對狗友善的趨勢，前提是它必須受到清晰規則和公民責任所引導 真正的挑戰並不是狗隻是否屬於這座城市，是人類如何能夠得體地共享空間"},{"label":"Paragraph 4","english":"First, a more dog-friendly Hong Kong improves the quality of urban life in a city where private space is painfully limited. Many owners live in small flats, work long hours and rely on short walks as their main way of bonding with their pets. If dogs are excluded from most parks, promenades and casual dining areas, owners are pushed onto narrow pavements or into unofficial gathering spots, which creates more inconvenience for everyone. By contrast, designated dog-friendly zones allow behaviour to be managed openly. Owners can exercise their dogs, cleaners know where bins are needed, and other users know what to expect. For example, a waterfront park with leashed-dog hours, waste bags and clear signs is far safer than a crowded footpath outside an MTR station. More importantly, dogs can soften a city that often feels rushed and impersonal. A child approaching a calm dog politely, an elderly owner chatting with a neighbour, or a shopkeeper placing a water bowl by the entrance may seem insignificant, but such moments create everyday warmth. Making room for dogs, when done properly, is therefore part of building a more humane community.","chinese":"首先，在一個私人空間極度有限的城市裡，一個更對狗友善的香港能夠改善城市生活質素。 許多主人住在狹小單位、工時漫長，並主要依靠短暫散步來與寵物建立情感聯繫。 如果狗隻被大多數公園、海濱長廊和休閒餐飲區排除在外，主人便會被迫走到狹窄行人路或非正式聚集地，這反而為所有人帶來更多不便。 相比之下，指定的狗隻友善區域能讓相關行為得到公開而有序的管理。 主人可以讓狗隻活動，清潔工人知道哪些地方需要垃圾桶，其他使用者也知道自己會遇到甚麼情況。 例如，一個設有牽狗時段、垃圾袋和清晰標示的海濱公園，遠比港鐵站外一條擠迫的行人路安全得多。 更重要的是，狗隻可以為一座經常顯得急促而缺乏人情味的城市增添柔和感 一個孩子禮貌地走近一隻安靜的狗、一位年長主人與鄰居閒聊，或一位店主在門口放置水碗，這些情景看似微不足道，卻能創造日常生活中的溫暖。 因此，只要做得恰當，為狗隻騰出空間，其實也是建設一個更有人情味社區的一部分"},{"label":"Paragraph 5","english":"Second, this trend can encourage responsible pet ownership and bring practical benefits to local businesses. When society treats dogs as a nuisance to be hidden away, some owners become careless because they feel excluded from normal public life. However, when parks, shops and restaurants welcome dogs under reasonable conditions, expectations can be made visible: keep dogs on a lead, clean up waste, avoid peak hours, and leave if the animal becomes noisy or aggressive. In other words, access and accountability can go hand in hand. Restaurants with outdoor seating, pet cafés and small boutiques can attract customers who might otherwise stay home. A couple choosing brunch may pick a restaurant because their dog can sit beside them; a pet-friendly mall may draw families who combine shopping with a walk. This is not merely sentimental. It is sensible urban management and a modest economic opportunity. Good policy does not reward selfishness; it channels ordinary needs into orderly habits.","chinese":"第二，這趨勢能夠鼓勵負責任的寵物飼養方式，並為本地商戶帶來實際好處 當社會把狗隻視為應被藏起來的滋擾時，一些主人會變得粗心，因為他們覺得自己被正常公共生活排除在外。 然而，當公園、商店和餐廳在合理條件下歡迎狗隻時，社會期望便可以變得清晰可見：為狗隻繫上狗帶、清理排泄物、避開繁忙時段，以及當動物變得嘈吵或具攻擊性時便離開。 換言之，進入公共空間的權利與承擔責任可以並行不悖。 設有戶外座位的餐廳、寵物咖啡店和小型精品店，能夠吸引一些原本可能留在家中的顧客。 一對情侶選擇吃早午餐時，可能會因為他們的狗可以坐在旁邊而選擇某間餐廳；一個寵物友善商場也可能吸引把購物和散步結合起來的家庭。 這並不只是感情用事。 這是明智的城市管理，也是一個溫和而實際的經濟機會。"},{"label":"Paragraph 6","english":"Admittedly, critics have a legitimate concern. Not everyone likes dogs, and some people are allergic, frightened or simply tired of seeing pets in places meant for human comfort. A restaurant is not a kennel, and a public park should not become an obstacle course of barking animals, tangled leashes and unpleasant smells. This point must be respected. Yet it does not follow that the city has gone too far simply because more places welcome dogs. The answer to poor manners is better regulation, not blanket rejection. Dog-friendly venues should state hygiene rules, seating areas and penalties for irresponsible owners. Parks can separate dog zones from children’s playgrounds, while restaurants can limit dogs to outdoor or specially ventilated sections. Owners who fail to control their pets should lose the privilege of entry. Rights without duties become selfishness; duties without rights become exclusion.","chinese":"誠然，批評者有合理的憂慮。 並非每個人都喜歡狗隻，有些人會過敏、感到害怕，或只是厭倦了在原本為人類舒適而設的地方看見寵物。 餐廳不是狗舍，而公共公園也不應變成一個充滿狗吠聲、糾纏狗帶和難聞氣味的障礙場。 這一點必須受到尊重。 然而，這並不代表只要更多地方歡迎狗隻，這座城市就已經走得太遠。 面對不良行為，答案應該是更完善的規管，而不是一概拒絕。 狗隻友善場所應清楚列明衞生規則、座位區域，以及對不負責任主人的罰則 公園可以把狗隻區域與兒童遊樂場分開，而餐廳則可以把狗隻限制在戶外區域或特別通風的區域。 未能控制寵物的主人，應失去進入相關場所的特權。 沒有義務的權利會變成自私；沒有權利的義務則會變成排斥。"},{"label":"Paragraph 7","english":"In conclusion, I support Hong Kong’s move towards becoming more dog-friendly, but only if the trend remains disciplined, considerate and well managed. Dogs should not be allowed everywhere, but they should not be banned almost everywhere either. The government can provide clearer guidelines, businesses can set transparent house rules, and owners must prove through their actions that public trust is deserved. At the end of the day, the question is not whether Hong Kong loves dogs too much. The question is whether we love our shared city enough to make room for one another—two-legged and four-legged alike.","chinese":"總而言之，我支持香港朝着更對狗友善的方向發展，但前提是這股趨勢必須保持有紀律、體諒他人，並受到妥善管理。 狗隻不應該被允許進入每一個地方，但牠們也不應幾乎在所有地方都被禁止 政府可以提供更清晰的指引，商戶可以制定透明的場地規則，而主人則必須透過自己的行動證明他們值得公眾信任。 說到底，問題並不是香港是否太愛狗。 問題是，我們是否足夠愛這座共同擁有的城市，以致願意為彼此騰出空間 ——無論是兩條腿的，還是四條腿的。"},{"label":"Paragraph 8","english":"Yours faithfully, Chris Wong","chinese":"謹啟："}],"vocabulary":[]},"dse-writing-2024-part-b-q5":{"exerciseId":"dse-writing-2024-part-b-q5","essayKey":"","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=dse-writing-2024-part-b-q5","flashDeckId":"dse/writing/part-b/2024/Q5","paragraphs":[{"label":"Title","english":"One Night, 100,000 Likes, and a Lesson I Never Expected","chinese":"一夜之間，十萬個讚，以及一個我從未預料到的教訓"},{"label":"Intro","english":"At 10:58 p.m. on a perfectly ordinary Tuesday, I posted a 45-second video and put my phone aside, expecting nothing more than a few amused comments from friends. By the time I woke up the next morning, however, that same video had gathered over 100,000 likes. For a few stunned seconds, I simply stared at the screen, wondering whether I was still half asleep. In an age when social media can turn an ordinary student into a minor celebrity overnight, many young people dream of going viral. After experiencing it myself, though, I have realised that sudden online fame is not only exciting but also unexpectedly exhausting, unsettling and deeply instructive.","chinese":"在一個再普通不過的星期二晚上 10 點 58 分，我發佈了一段 45 秒的影片，然後把手機放到一旁，原本只預期朋友們會留下幾則覺得好笑的留言而已。 然而，等我隔天早上醒來時，那段影片竟然已經累積超過十萬個讚。 有好幾秒鐘，我只是愣愣地盯著螢幕，懷疑自己是不是還沒完全睡醒。 在這個社群媒體可以一夜之間把普通學生變成小小網紅的時代，許多年輕人都夢想著自己能爆紅。 但親身經歷之後，我明白到，突如其來的網路名氣不僅令人興奮，也會出乎意料地讓人疲憊、不安，並帶來深刻的啟發。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"The video itself was hardly a masterpiece. It was a short, light-hearted clip showing “a day in the life of a Hong Kong student before exams”. I had filmed myself rushing to school, balancing a sandwich and revision notes in one hand, falling asleep briefly on the bus, and then pretending to be full of energy in class. I added some humorous captions, a trending sound effect and posted it without much thought. Apparently, however, thousands of students found it painfully relatable. Within hours, the notifications on my phone were exploding so rapidly that I could barely read them. Likes were rising by the second. Comments came from people I had never met, from different schools, cities and even countries. At first, the experience felt almost magical. It was flattering to know that something I had created in my bedroom could make so many strangers laugh.","chinese":"那段影片本身其實根本算不上什麼傑作。 那只是一段簡短而輕鬆的影片，內容是「香港學生考試前一天的生活」。 我拍下自己匆忙趕去上學、一手拿著三明治和複習筆記、在巴士上短暫睡著，然後到了課堂上又假裝精神飽滿的樣子。 我加上了一些幽默字幕和一個流行音效，沒有多想就把它發出去了。 然而，顯然有成千上萬的學生都覺得那內容真是太有共鳴了。 短短幾個小時內，我手機上的通知爆炸式地增加，快到我幾乎來不及看清楚。 按讚數每一秒都在上升，留言則來自我從未見過的人，他們來自不同的學校、城市，甚至不同國家。 一開始，這種經歷幾乎讓人覺得像魔法一樣。 知道自己在房間裡做出來的東西，竟然能讓那麼多陌生人發笑，的確令人感到受寵若驚。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"Yet the thrill did not last in its pure form for very long. The first change was practical: my phone became impossible to ignore. Every few seconds, it lit up again. Every buzz seemed to demand my attention. Instead of doing homework, I kept checking the latest numbers, wondering whether the video had reached 120,000 or 130,000 views. In other words, I was no longer using social media; social media was using me. What surprised me most was how quickly enjoyment turned into dependence. The more attention I received, the more I wanted. A single successful post, rather than making me satisfied, made me anxious about whether I could repeat that success. What had begun as a joke was slowly turning into pressure.","chinese":"然而，這份興奮並沒有長久維持最初那種單純的樣子。 第一個改變是很實際的：我的手機變得讓人無法忽視。 每隔幾秒，它就又亮起來一次；每一次震動都像是在要求我立刻注意它。 我沒有好好做功課，反而一直在查看最新數字，想知道影片是不是已經到了十二萬或十三萬觀看次數。 換句話說，不再是我在使用社群媒體，而是社群媒體在使用我。 最讓我驚訝的是，快樂竟然那麼迅速地轉變成依賴。 我得到的關注越多，就越想要更多。 一則成功的貼文，不但沒有讓我感到滿足，反而讓我開始焦慮自己是否還能再複製同樣的成功。 原本只是個玩笑的事情，慢慢地卻變成了一種壓力。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 3","english":"A second lesson came from reading the comments. Many were kind, generous and genuinely funny. Some people wrote that they had never felt so “seen” before, while others tagged their friends and said, “This is literally us.” Those responses reminded me that social media can create connections in a powerful and immediate way. A simple video can reassure people that they are not alone in their stress, awkwardness or daily struggles. However, not all comments were encouraging. A few criticised my appearance, my voice or even the way I walked. One accused me of “trying too hard to be relatable”, while another claimed the video was “cringe”. I knew, logically, that strangers on the internet do not know me well enough to define me. Even so, harsh words have a peculiar way of lingering longer than praise. That was when I understood a difficult truth: online popularity brings not only visibility, but also vulnerability.","chinese":"第二個教訓來自閱讀留言。 其中很多留言都很友善、很大方，也真的很有趣。 有些人寫道，他們從來沒有像這次一樣感到自己「被看見」；也有人標記朋友並說：「這根本就是我們。」 這些回應提醒了我，社群媒體確實能夠以強而有力又直接的方式創造連結。 一段簡單的影片，就能讓人明白自己在壓力、尷尬或日常掙扎中並不孤單。 然而，並不是所有留言都令人鼓舞。 有些人批評我的外表、聲音，甚至連我走路的樣子也不放過。 有人指責我「太刻意想讓人產生共鳴」，還有人說那支影片「很尷尬」。 從理性上來說，我知道網路上的陌生人其實並不了解我，沒有資格定義我是誰。 即使如此，刺耳的話總有一種特別的力量，會比稱讚停留得更久。 就在那一刻，我明白了一個不容易接受的事實：網路上的受歡迎，不只帶來曝光，也帶來脆弱。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 4","english":"Most importantly, the whole experience changed the way I think about success. Before this happened, I might have assumed that getting 100,000 likes would feel like reaching a finish line. In reality, it felt more like stepping onto a moving treadmill. Numbers rise, people react, trends shift, and attention moves on. By the following week, the excitement had already begun to fade. The internet, after all, has a very short memory. What remains, however, is not the number itself but the lesson behind it. I learned that recognition is enjoyable, but it is unreliable if it becomes the main source of one’s confidence. I also learned that creativity matters far more than chasing approval. The happiest moment in the entire experience was not seeing the number 100,000; it was creating something honest that others connected with.","chinese":"最重要的是，整個經歷改變了我對成功的看法。 在這件事發生之前，我也許會以為得到十萬個讚，就像抵達終點線一樣。 但實際上，那感覺更像是踏上了一台不停移動的跑步機。 數字會上升，人們會反應，潮流會改變，而注意力也會很快轉移。 到了下一個星期，那份興奮感其實已經開始消退。 畢竟，網路的記憶是非常短暫的。 然而，真正留下來的，並不是那個數字本身，而是它背後帶來的教訓。 我明白了，被認可固然令人開心，但如果它變成一個人自信的主要來源，那就是不可靠的。 我也學會了，創意遠比追逐認同更加重要。 整個經歷中最快樂的時刻，不是看見十萬這個數字，而是創造出一樣真誠的東西，並讓別人與之產生共鳴。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"Looking back, I am grateful that the video went viral, not because it made me “famous” for a day, but because it taught me to view social media more critically and more calmly. It can be a platform for humour, creativity and shared experience, but it can also be addictive and emotionally unpredictable. If there is one message I would like to leave with fellow students, it is this: enjoy the excitement of online attention if it comes, but do not build your self-worth on it. A viral post may last for a night, but self-knowledge lasts much longer.","chinese":"回頭看，我很感激那支影片爆紅，不是因為它讓我「紅了一天」，而是因為它教會我用更冷靜、更有批判性的眼光去看待社群媒體。 它可以是一個承載幽默、創意與共同經驗的平台，但同時也可能令人上癮，並在情緒上難以預測。 如果我想留給同學們一個訊息，那就是：如果網路上的關注真的來了，就享受那份興奮吧，但不要把自己的自我價值建立在它上面。 一則爆紅的貼文也許只會持續一晚，但對自我的了解卻會長久得多。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"a lesson I never expected","chinese":"我意想不到的一課"},{"english":"a perfectly ordinary Tuesday","chinese":"一個再普通不過的星期二"},{"english":"posted a 45-second video","chinese":"發布一段45秒的影片"},{"english":"put my phone aside","chinese":"把手機放到一旁"},{"english":"expecting nothing more than","chinese":"只期望；沒有期望多於"},{"english":"amused comments","chinese":"覺得有趣的留言"},{"english":"by the time","chinese":"到……的時候"},{"english":"had gathered over","chinese":"已累積超過"},{"english":"over 100,000 likes","chinese":"超過十萬個讚好"},{"english":"for a few stunned seconds","chinese":"有幾秒鐘驚呆了"},{"english":"stared at the screen","chinese":"盯着螢幕看"},{"english":"wondering whether","chinese":"在想是否"},{"english":"half asleep","chinese":"半睡半醒"},{"english":"in an age when","chinese":"在一個……的時代"},{"english":"social media","chinese":"社交媒體"},{"english":"turn ... into","chinese":"把……變成"},{"english":"an ordinary student","chinese":"一個普通學生"},{"english":"a minor celebrity","chinese":"小名人"},{"english":"overnight","chinese":"一夜之間"},{"english":"dream of going viral","chinese":"夢想爆紅"},{"english":"after experiencing it myself","chinese":"親身經歷之後"},{"english":"sudden online fame","chinese":"突如其來的網上名氣"},{"english":"not only ... but also","chinese":"不但……而且"},{"english":"unexpectedly exhausting","chinese":"出乎意料地令人疲累"},{"english":"unsettling","chinese":"令人不安"},{"english":"deeply instructive","chinese":"很有啟發性"},{"english":"was hardly a masterpiece","chinese":"絕非傑作"},{"english":"light-hearted clip","chinese":"輕鬆有趣的短片"},{"english":"a day in the life of","chinese":"……的一日生活"},{"english":"before exams","chinese":"考試前"},{"english":"filmed myself rushing to","chinese":"拍下自己趕往……"},{"english":"balancing ... and ... in one hand","chinese":"一隻手同時拿着……和……"},{"english":"revision notes","chinese":"溫習筆記"},{"english":"falling asleep briefly","chinese":"短暫睡着"},{"english":"pretending to be full of energy","chinese":"假裝精力充沛"},{"english":"humorous captions","chinese":"幽默字幕"},{"english":"a trending sound effect","chinese":"熱門音效"},{"english":"without much thought","chinese":"沒有多想"},{"english":"painfully relatable","chinese":"非常有共鳴；貼切得令人心酸"},{"english":"within hours","chinese":"數小時內"},{"english":"notifications on my phone","chinese":"手機通知"},{"english":"were exploding","chinese":"不斷湧現；爆炸式增加"},{"english":"so rapidly that","chinese":"快得以致"},{"english":"could barely read","chinese":"幾乎看不過來"},{"english":"rising by the second","chinese":"每秒都在增加"},{"english":"comments came from","chinese":"留言來自"},{"english":"people I had never met","chinese":"我從未見過的人"},{"english":"different schools, cities and even countries","chinese":"不同學校、城市甚至國家"},{"english":"at first","chinese":"起初"},{"english":"felt almost magical","chinese":"感覺幾乎像魔法一樣"},{"english":"it was flattering to know that","chinese":"得知……令人受寵若驚"},{"english":"something I had created","chinese":"我創作出來的東西"},{"english":"in my bedroom","chinese":"在我的睡房裏"},{"english":"make so many strangers laugh","chinese":"令那麼多陌生人發笑"},{"english":"the thrill did not last","chinese":"興奮感沒有持續"},{"english":"in its pure form","chinese":"以最純粹的形式"},{"english":"for very long","chinese":"很久"},{"english":"the first change","chinese":"第一個變化"},{"english":"became impossible to ignore","chinese":"變得無法忽視"},{"english":"every few seconds","chinese":"每隔幾秒"},{"english":"lit up","chinese":"亮起來"},{"english":"every buzz","chinese":"每一下震動"},{"english":"seemed to demand","chinese":"似乎在要求"},{"english":"demand my attention","chinese":"要求我注意"},{"english":"instead of doing homework","chinese":"沒有做功課，反而"},{"english":"kept checking","chinese":"不斷查看"},{"english":"the latest numbers","chinese":"最新數字"},{"english":"wondering whether","chinese":"想知道是否"},{"english":"reached 120,000 views","chinese":"達到十二萬次觀看"},{"english":"in other words","chinese":"換句話說"},{"english":"no longer","chinese":"不再"},{"english":"social media was using me","chinese":"社交媒體反過來操控我"},{"english":"what surprised me most","chinese":"最令我驚訝的是"},{"english":"how quickly","chinese":"多麼迅速地"},{"english":"enjoyment turned into dependence","chinese":"享受變成依賴"},{"english":"the more ..., the more ...","chinese":"越……就越……"},{"english":"attention I received","chinese":"我得到的關注"},{"english":"a single successful post","chinese":"一個成功的帖文"},{"english":"rather than","chinese":"而不是"},{"english":"making me satisfied","chinese":"令我滿足"},{"english":"made me anxious about","chinese":"令我為……感到焦慮"},{"english":"repeat that success","chinese":"重複那次成功"},{"english":"had begun as","chinese":"原本是"},{"english":"slowly turning into","chinese":"慢慢變成"},{"english":"turning into pressure","chinese":"變成壓力"},{"english":"a second lesson came from","chinese":"第二個教訓來自"},{"english":"reading the comments","chinese":"閱讀留言"},{"english":"kind, generous and genuinely funny","chinese":"友善、大方而真心有趣"},{"english":"genuinely funny","chinese":"真心好笑"},{"english":"had never felt so \"seen\" before","chinese":"從未覺得如此被理解"},{"english":"tagged their friends","chinese":"標註朋友"},{"english":"literally us","chinese":"簡直就是我們"},{"english":"those responses reminded me that","chinese":"那些回應提醒我"},{"english":"create connection","chinese":"建立連繫"},{"english":"in a powerful and immediate way","chinese":"以強大而即時的方式"},{"english":"reassure people that","chinese":"讓人安心知道"},{"english":"not alone in","chinese":"在……方面並不孤單"},{"english":"daily struggles","chinese":"日常掙扎"},{"english":"not all comments were encouraging","chinese":"並非所有留言都是鼓勵性的"},{"english":"criticised my appearance","chinese":"批評我的外表"},{"english":"the way I walked","chinese":"我走路的方式"},{"english":"accused me of","chinese":"指責我"},{"english":"trying too hard to","chinese":"過分刻意地"},{"english":"be relatable","chinese":"令人有共鳴"},{"english":"claimed the video was","chinese":"聲稱影片是"},{"english":"cringe","chinese":"尷尬得令人不適；尷尬"},{"english":"I knew, logically, that","chinese":"理性上我知道"},{"english":"strangers on the internet","chinese":"網上的陌生人"},{"english":"well enough to","chinese":"足夠……去"},{"english":"define me","chinese":"定義我"},{"english":"even so","chinese":"即使如此"},{"english":"harsh words","chinese":"尖刻的說話"},{"english":"have a peculiar way of","chinese":"有一種奇特的方式會"},{"english":"lingering longer than praise","chinese":"比讚美停留得更久"},{"english":"that was when","chinese":"就是在那時候"},{"english":"a difficult truth","chinese":"一個令人難受的真相"},{"english":"online popularity","chinese":"網上人氣"},{"english":"brings not only ... but also","chinese":"帶來的不只是……還有"},{"english":"visibility","chinese":"能見度；曝光"},{"english":"vulnerability","chinese":"脆弱；容易受傷害"},{"english":"most importantly","chinese":"最重要的是"},{"english":"the whole experience","chinese":"整個經歷"},{"english":"changed the way I think about","chinese":"改變了我對……的看法"},{"english":"think about success","chinese":"看待成功"},{"english":"before this happened","chinese":"在這件事發生之前"},{"english":"might have assumed that","chinese":"可能會以為"},{"english":"getting 100,000 likes","chinese":"得到十萬個讚好"},{"english":"would feel like","chinese":"會感覺像"},{"english":"reaching a finish line","chinese":"到達終點線"},{"english":"in reality","chinese":"事實上"},{"english":"felt more like","chinese":"感覺更像"},{"english":"stepping onto","chinese":"踏上"},{"english":"a moving treadmill","chinese":"不斷移動的跑步機"},{"english":"numbers rise","chinese":"數字上升"},{"english":"people react","chinese":"人們作出反應"},{"english":"trends shift","chinese":"潮流轉變"},{"english":"attention moves on","chinese":"關注轉移到別處"},{"english":"by the following week","chinese":"到了接下來的一星期"},{"english":"had already begun to fade","chinese":"已經開始消退"},{"english":"after all","chinese":"畢竟"},{"english":"has a very short memory","chinese":"記憶很短暫"},{"english":"what remains","chinese":"留下來的東西"},{"english":"the number itself","chinese":"數字本身"},{"english":"the lesson behind it","chinese":"背後的教訓"},{"english":"recognition is enjoyable","chinese":"獲得認同是令人愉快的"},{"english":"is unreliable if","chinese":"如果……就不可靠"},{"english":"the main source of","chinese":"……的主要來源"},{"english":"one's confidence","chinese":"一個人的自信"},{"english":"creativity matters far more than","chinese":"創意遠比……重要"},{"english":"chasing approval","chinese":"追求認可"},{"english":"the happiest moment","chinese":"最快樂的時刻"},{"english":"in the entire experience","chinese":"在整個經歷中"},{"english":"creating something honest","chinese":"創作真誠的東西"},{"english":"connected with","chinese":"與……產生共鳴"},{"english":"looking back","chinese":"回頭看"},{"english":"am grateful that","chinese":"感激……"},{"english":"went viral","chinese":"在網上爆紅"},{"english":"not because ... but because","chinese":"不是因為……而是因為"},{"english":"made me \"famous\" for a day","chinese":"讓我「出名」一天"},{"english":"taught me to","chinese":"教會我去"},{"english":"view social media more critically","chinese":"更批判地看待社交媒體"},{"english":"more calmly","chinese":"更冷靜地"},{"english":"a platform for","chinese":"……的平台"},{"english":"humour, creativity and shared experience","chinese":"幽默、創意和共同經歷"},{"english":"shared experience","chinese":"共同經歷"},{"english":"addictive","chinese":"令人上癮"},{"english":"emotionally unpredictable","chinese":"在情緒上難以預測"},{"english":"if there is one message","chinese":"如果有一個訊息"},{"english":"would like to leave with","chinese":"想留給"},{"english":"fellow students","chinese":"同學們"},{"english":"online attention","chinese":"網上關注"},{"english":"if it comes","chinese":"如果它出現"},{"english":"build your self-worth on","chinese":"把自我價值建立在……之上"},{"english":"self-worth","chinese":"自我價值"},{"english":"a viral post","chinese":"爆紅帖文"},{"english":"may last for","chinese":"可能持續"},{"english":"self-knowledge","chinese":"自我認識"},{"english":"lasts much longer","chinese":"持續得更久"}]},"dse-writing-2025-part-a":{"exerciseId":"dse-writing-2025-part-a","essayKey":"","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=dse-writing-2025-part-a","flashDeckId":"dse/writing/part-a/2025","paragraphs":[{"label":"Our background","english":"Our background","chinese":"我們的背景"},{"label":"Our background","english":"Founded by local artists and dedicated teachers, 852 Teen Art Club believes every teenager deserves a chance to express themselves through art. Over the years, we have welcomed students from different schools and backgrounds to explore painting, photography, ceramics and calligraphy in a friendly, inspiring environment. More than a place to learn techniques, the club helps young people exchange ideas, gain confidence, build friendships and discover their creative identity.","chinese":"852 Teen Art Club 由本地藝術家和敬業的老師創立，深信每一位青少年都應該有機會透過藝術表達自己。 多年來，我們歡迎來自不同學校和背景的學生，在一個友善而富啟發性的環境中探索繪畫、攝影、陶藝和書法。 本會不只是一個學習技巧的地方，更幫助年輕人交流想法、建立信心、建立友誼，並發掘自己的創意身份。"},{"label":"A club member’s most memorable experience","english":"A club member’s most memorable experience","chinese":"一位會員最難忘的經歷"},{"label":"A club member’s most memorable experience","english":"For Jason, a Secondary Four member, his most memorable experience was last summer’s community mural project. Although he had never painted on such a large wall before, encouragement from other members helped him step out of his comfort zone. His sketch of old Hong Kong streets became part of a colourful public mural. Seeing passers-by stop, smile and take photos gave him a deep sense of pride. As he said, art can speak to people and bring a community closer together.","chinese":"對中四會員 Jason 來說，他最難忘的經歷是去年夏天的社區壁畫計劃。 雖然他以前從未在這麼大的牆上作畫，但其他會員的鼓勵幫助他走出舒適圈。 他筆下舊香港街道的草圖，最終成為一幅色彩繽紛的公共壁畫的一部分。 看見途人停下腳步、露出笑容並拍照，令他產生了深深的自豪感。 正如他所說，藝術能夠與人溝通，並令社區更加團結。"},{"label":"Our future activities","english":"Our future activities","chinese":"我們未來的活動"},{"label":"Our future activities","english":"This term, members can join a street photography walk, a pottery workshop, an inter-school exhibition, museum visits and a charity art sale. Whether experienced or new to art, teenagers are welcome to explore their potential and let their creativity flourish.","chinese":"本學期，會員可以參加街頭攝影步行活動、陶藝工作坊、校際展覽、博物館參觀活動，以及慈善藝術義賣。 無論是有經驗，還是剛接觸藝術的青少年，我們都歡迎他們發掘自己的潛能，讓創意盡情綻放。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"founded by","chinese":"由……創立"},{"english":"local artists","chinese":"本地藝術家"},{"english":"dedicated teachers","chinese":"盡心盡力的老師"},{"english":"believe every teenager deserves","chinese":"相信每位青少年都值得……"},{"english":"deserve a chance to","chinese":"值得有機會去……"},{"english":"express themselves through art","chinese":"透過藝術表達自己"},{"english":"over the years","chinese":"多年來"},{"english":"welcome students from","chinese":"歡迎來自……的學生"},{"english":"different schools and backgrounds","chinese":"不同學校及背景"},{"english":"explore painting, photography, ceramics and calligraphy","chinese":"探索繪畫、攝影、陶藝及書法"},{"english":"painting","chinese":"繪畫"},{"english":"photography","chinese":"攝影"},{"english":"ceramics","chinese":"陶藝"},{"english":"calligraphy","chinese":"書法"},{"english":"friendly, inspiring environment","chinese":"友善而啟發人的環境"},{"english":"more than a place to","chinese":"不只是一個……的地方"},{"english":"learn techniques","chinese":"學習技巧"},{"english":"exchange ideas","chinese":"交流想法"},{"english":"gain confidence","chinese":"建立自信"},{"english":"build friendships","chinese":"建立友誼"},{"english":"discover their creative identity","chinese":"發掘自己的創意身份"},{"english":"a club member's most memorable experience","chinese":"一名會員最難忘的經歷"},{"english":"Secondary Four member","chinese":"中四會員"},{"english":"community mural project","chinese":"社區壁畫計劃"},{"english":"last summer's","chinese":"去年夏天的"},{"english":"although","chinese":"雖然"},{"english":"paint on such a large wall","chinese":"在如此大的牆上作畫"},{"english":"encouragement from","chinese":"來自……的鼓勵"},{"english":"step out of his comfort zone","chinese":"走出舒適圈"},{"english":"sketch of","chinese":"……的素描"},{"english":"old Hong Kong streets","chinese":"舊香港街道"},{"english":"become part of","chinese":"成為……的一部分"},{"english":"colourful public mural","chinese":"色彩繽紛的公共壁畫"},{"english":"passers-by","chinese":"路人"},{"english":"take photos","chinese":"拍照"},{"english":"give someone a deep sense of pride","chinese":"令某人深感自豪"},{"english":"a deep sense of pride","chinese":"深深的自豪感"},{"english":"art can speak to people","chinese":"藝術能打動人心"},{"english":"bring a community closer together","chinese":"拉近社區之間的距離"},{"english":"future activities","chinese":"未來活動"},{"english":"this term","chinese":"本學期"},{"english":"street photography walk","chinese":"街頭攝影漫步"},{"english":"pottery workshop","chinese":"陶藝工作坊"},{"english":"inter-school exhibition","chinese":"聯校展覽"},{"english":"museum visits","chinese":"博物館參觀活動"},{"english":"charity art sale","chinese":"慈善藝術義賣"},{"english":"whether experienced or new to art","chinese":"不論有經驗還是初學藝術"},{"english":"be welcome to","chinese":"歡迎……"},{"english":"explore their potential","chinese":"發掘自己的潛能"},{"english":"let their creativity flourish","chinese":"讓創意蓬勃發展"}]},"dse-writing-2025-part-b-q2":{"exerciseId":"dse-writing-2025-part-b-q2","essayKey":"","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=dse-writing-2025-part-b-q2","flashDeckId":"dse/writing/part-b/2025/Q2","paragraphs":[{"label":"Paragraph 1","english":"The Boy I Thought Would Never Change","chinese":""},{"label":"Paragraph 2","english":"The last person I expected to see at a theme park was Kelvin Chan.","chinese":"我最沒想到會在主題樂園見到的人，就是 Kelvin Chan。 的母親慌了，而 Kelvin 自己也完全愣住了。"},{"label":"Paragraph 3","english":"It was a hot Saturday afternoon. Roller coasters thundered overhead, music blasted from loudspeakers, and the air smelled of popcorn and sunscreen. I had just stepped out of a queue when I noticed a little girl crying outside a souvenir shop. Before I could move, a young man crouched beside her, spoke gently, and handed her a tissue.","chinese":"雲霄飛車在頭頂轟隆作響，喇叭裡播放著震耳欲聾的音樂，空氣中瀰漫著爆米花和防曬乳的味道。 我剛走出排隊隊伍，就注意到一個小女孩在紀念品店外哭泣。 還沒等我走過去，一名年輕男子已經蹲到她身旁，溫柔地對她說話，還遞給她一張紙巾。"},{"label":"Paragraph 4","english":"Then he turned around.","chinese":"接著，他轉過身來。"},{"label":"Paragraph 5","english":"It was Kelvin.","chinese":"那竟然是 Kelvin。 的母親慌了，而 Kelvin 自己也完全愣住了。"},{"label":"Paragraph 6","english":"At school, Kelvin had been notorious for all the wrong reasons. He mocked weaker students, hid people’s belongings for fun, and once made a girl cry by laughing at her presentation in front of the whole class. He seemed to enjoy making others feel small.","chinese":"在學校裡，Kelvin 之所以出名，完全是因為那些糟糕的原因。 他會嘲笑較弱小的同學，為了好玩把別人的東西藏起來，還曾經當著全班的面取笑一位女生的報告，把她弄哭。 他似乎很享受讓別人感到自己很渺小。 的母親慌了，而 Kelvin 自己也完全愣住了。"},{"label":"Paragraph 7","english":"Yet the Kelvin in front of me looked completely different. He stayed with the little girl until a staff member arrived, then gave her a reassuring smile. When he recognised me, he looked surprised.","chinese":"然而，站在我面前的 Kelvin 看起來卻完全不一樣。 他一直陪著那個小女孩，直到工作人員趕來，然後還給了她一個令人安心的微笑。 當他認出我時，他看起來也有些驚訝。 的母親慌了，而 Kelvin 自己也完全愣住了。"},{"label":"Paragraph 8","english":"“Long time no see.”","chinese":"「好久不見。」"},{"label":"Paragraph 9","english":"Soon, we were sitting on a bench near the Ferris wheel with cups of lemonade in our hands. After a few awkward updates about university and work, I finally said what I had been thinking.","chinese":"不久後，我們坐在摩天輪附近的一張長椅上，手裡各拿著一杯檸檬水。 在尷尬地聊了幾句大學和工作的近況後，我終於說出了我心裡一直在想的話"},{"label":"Paragraph 10","english":"“You’ve changed.”","chinese":"「你變了。」"},{"label":"Paragraph 11","english":"Kelvin looked down and gave a faint smile. “Yeah,” he said. “Last year changed me.”","chinese":"「對啊，」他說，「去年改變了我。」 的母親慌了，而 Kelvin 自己也完全愣住了。"},{"label":"Paragraph 12","english":"He told me that one night, during a typhoon, his father suddenly collapsed at home. One minute he was talking; the next, he could not move the right side of his body. Kelvin’s mother panicked. Kelvin himself froze. The building had lost power, the lift had stopped working, and the ambulance was delayed because of the weather.","chinese":"他告訴我，有一天晚上，颱風來襲時，他的父親突然在家中倒下了。 前一分鐘他還在說話，下一分鐘，他的右半邊身體就無法動彈了。 的母親慌了，而 Kelvin 自己也完全愣住了。 大樓停電了，電梯也停止運作，而救護車因為天氣惡劣而延誤。"},{"label":"Paragraph 13","english":"For the first time in his life, Kelvin realised that all his swagger meant nothing in a real crisis.","chinese":"的母親慌了，而 Kelvin 自己也完全愣住了。 生平第一次意識到，在真正的危機面前，他平日那種張揚自大的樣子根本毫無意義。"},{"label":"Paragraph 14","english":"Then someone knocked on the door.","chinese":"就在那時，有人敲門了。"},{"label":"Paragraph 15","english":"It was Mr Leung, the elderly security guard from their estate.","chinese":"來的人是梁先生——他們屋苑那位年長的保全員。"},{"label":"Paragraph 16","english":"Kelvin admitted that before that night, he would probably not even have noticed him. At school, he had always looked down on people he considered weak, quiet or unimportant. But Mr Leung did what Kelvin could not. He checked his father’s breathing, called the ambulance again, and when the paramedics finally arrived, helped carry Kelvin’s father down seventeen flights of stairs because the lift was still out of order.","chinese":"的母親慌了，而 Kelvin 自己也完全愣住了。 在學校時，他一向看不起那些他認為軟弱、安靜或不重要的人。 但梁先生做到了 Kelvin 做不到的事。 他檢查了 Kelvin 父親的呼吸，再次打電話叫救護車，而當救護人員終於抵達時，他還因為電梯依然故障，幫忙把 Kelvin 的父親從十七層樓一路抬下去。"},{"label":"Paragraph 17","english":"Even then, he did not leave. At the hospital, while Kelvin and his mother sat outside the emergency room in shock, Mr Leung bought them water and stayed with them until early morning.","chinese":"的母親慌了，而 Kelvin 自己也完全愣住了。 即使如此，他也沒有離開。 在醫院裡，當 Kelvin 和母親震驚地坐在急診室外時，梁先生替他們買了水， 還一直陪著他們直到清晨。"},{"label":"Paragraph 18","english":"“He barely knew us,” Kelvin said quietly. “But he stayed.”","chinese":"的母親慌了，而 Kelvin 自己也完全愣住了。 「他幾乎不認識我們，」Kelvin 輕聲說，「但他留下來了。」"},{"label":"Paragraph 19","english":"That, he told me, was the moment everything changed. Sitting in that hospital corridor, he suddenly saw himself clearly. He had spent years trying to look powerful by humiliating others, yet when real trouble came, the strongest person in the room was the old man he would once have ignored.","chinese":"他告訴我，那一刻就是改變一切的時刻。 坐在那條醫院走廊裡時，他突然清楚地看見了真正的自己。 多年來，他一直靠羞辱別人來讓自己看起來很有力量；可是當真正的麻煩來臨時，房間裡最堅強的人，卻是那位他過去可能根本不屑一顧的老人。"},{"label":"Paragraph 20","english":"His father survived, though recovery was slow. Over the following months, Kelvin accompanied him to physiotherapy sessions and helped more at home. Later, he began volunteering at a community centre on weekends. At first, he said, it was almost a way of apologising. Then it became a habit. He helped children with homework, accompanied elderly people to appointments, and discovered that real maturity was not about being noticed, but about being dependable.","chinese":"的母親慌了，而 Kelvin 自己也完全愣住了。 他的父親活了下來，雖然康復的過程很緩慢。 在接下來的幾個月裡，Kelvin 陪父親去做物理治療，也在家裡幫了更多忙。 後來，他開始在週末到社區中心當義工。 他說，一開始，那幾乎像是一種道歉的方式。 但後來，這變成了一種習慣。 他幫孩子做功課、陪長者去赴約，也逐漸明白真正的成熟，不在於引人注意 ，而在於讓人可以依靠。"},{"label":"Paragraph 21","english":"“I used to think strength meant being feared,” he said. “Now I think it means being useful.”","chinese":"「我以前以為，力量就是讓人害怕，」他說，「現在我覺得，力量是成為一個有用的人。」"},{"label":"Paragraph 22","english":"Just then, the little girl from earlier walked past with her mother. She spotted Kelvin and waved shyly. He waved back with such natural warmth that, for a second, I forgot this was the same person I had once disliked so intensely.","chinese":"的母親慌了，而 Kelvin 自己也完全愣住了。 就在這時，剛才那個小女孩和她的母親從我們身旁走過。 她看見 Kelvin，害羞地向他揮了揮手。 他也自然又溫暖地揮手回應，那一瞬間，我幾乎忘了，眼前這個人就是那個我曾經非常討厭的人。"},{"label":"Paragraph 23","english":"As evening fell and the lights of the park flickered on, I looked at Kelvin and realised that some people do change—not because time softens them, but because life forces them to confront the truth. In Kelvin’s case, it was the truth that kindness is not weakness, and that character reveals itself most clearly in moments of crisis.","chinese":"的母親慌了，而 Kelvin 自己也完全愣住了。 當夜色降臨、樂園的燈光一一亮起時，我看著 Kelvin，意識到有些人真的會改變——不是因為時間讓他們變柔和了，而是因為人生逼著他們去正視真相。 對 Kelvin 而言，那個真相就是：善良並不是軟弱，而一個人的品格，往往會在危機時刻最清楚地顯露出來。"},{"label":"Paragraph 24","english":"When we stood up to leave, I felt as though I had met two versions of the same person: the boy I had known at school, and the man standing before me now. The first had wanted attention. The second had learned compassion.","chinese":"當我們起身準備離開時，我感覺自己像是見到了同一個人的兩個版本：一個是我在學校認識的那個男孩，另一個則是如今站在我面前的男人。 前者渴望的是他人的注意；後者學會的卻是同理與憐憫。"},{"label":"Paragraph 25","english":"And somehow, in the middle of that noisy theme park, that quiet change seemed more remarkable than any ride around us.","chinese":"不知怎麼地，在那座喧鬧的主題樂園中央，這份安靜的改變，竟比四周任何遊樂設施都來得更加令人驚嘆。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"the boy I thought would never change","chinese":"我以為永遠不會改變的男孩"},{"english":"the last person I expected to see","chinese":"我最意想不到會見到的人"},{"english":"theme park","chinese":"主題公園"},{"english":"a hot Saturday afternoon","chinese":"一個炎熱的星期六下午"},{"english":"roller coasters","chinese":"過山車"},{"english":"thundered overhead","chinese":"在頭頂轟隆駛過"},{"english":"music blasted from","chinese":"音樂從……大聲播放"},{"english":"loudspeakers","chinese":"擴音器"},{"english":"smelled of","chinese":"有……的氣味"},{"english":"popcorn and sunscreen","chinese":"爆谷和防曬霜"},{"english":"step out of a queue","chinese":"從隊伍中走出來"},{"english":"noticed","chinese":"注意到"},{"english":"souvenir shop","chinese":"紀念品店"},{"english":"before I could move","chinese":"我還未來得及行動"},{"english":"crouched beside","chinese":"蹲在……旁邊"},{"english":"spoke gently","chinese":"溫柔地說話"},{"english":"handed her a tissue","chinese":"遞給她一張紙巾"},{"english":"turned around","chinese":"轉過身來"},{"english":"notorious for","chinese":"因……而臭名遠播"},{"english":"for all the wrong reasons","chinese":"因為不好的原因"},{"english":"mocked weaker students","chinese":"嘲笑較弱的學生"},{"english":"hid people's belongings","chinese":"藏起別人的物品"},{"english":"for fun","chinese":"為了好玩"},{"english":"in front of the whole class","chinese":"在全班面前"},{"english":"seemed to enjoy","chinese":"似乎享受……"},{"english":"make others feel small","chinese":"令別人覺得渺小"},{"english":"the Kelvin in front of me","chinese":"我眼前的 Kelvin"},{"english":"completely different","chinese":"完全不同"},{"english":"stayed with","chinese":"留在……身邊"},{"english":"staff member","chinese":"職員"},{"english":"reassuring smile","chinese":"令人安心的微笑"},{"english":"recognised me","chinese":"認出我"},{"english":"long time no see","chinese":"好耐冇見"},{"english":"sitting on a bench","chinese":"坐在長椅上"},{"english":"Ferris wheel","chinese":"摩天輪"},{"english":"cups of lemonade","chinese":"幾杯檸檬水"},{"english":"awkward updates","chinese":"尷尬的近況分享"},{"english":"what I had been thinking","chinese":"我一直在想的事"},{"english":"looked down","chinese":"低頭望下"},{"english":"gave a faint smile","chinese":"淡淡一笑"},{"english":"changed me","chinese":"改變了我"},{"english":"one night, during a typhoon","chinese":"在一個颱風夜晚"},{"english":"suddenly collapsed","chinese":"突然昏倒"},{"english":"one minute…the next…","chinese":"前一刻……下一刻……"},{"english":"the right side of his body","chinese":"身體右邊"},{"english":"panicked","chinese":"驚慌失措"},{"english":"froze","chinese":"呆住；不知所措"},{"english":"lost power","chinese":"停電"},{"english":"stopped working","chinese":"停止運作"},{"english":"the ambulance was delayed","chinese":"救護車延誤"},{"english":"because of the weather","chinese":"因為天氣"},{"english":"for the first time in his life","chinese":"他人生中第一次"},{"english":"swagger","chinese":"神氣；自大姿態"},{"english":"meant nothing","chinese":"毫無意義"},{"english":"in a real crisis","chinese":"在真正危機中"},{"english":"knocked on the door","chinese":"敲門"},{"english":"elderly security guard","chinese":"年長保安員"},{"english":"from their estate","chinese":"來自他們屋苑"},{"english":"admitted that","chinese":"承認"},{"english":"before that night","chinese":"在那晚之前"},{"english":"not even have noticed","chinese":"甚至不會留意到"},{"english":"looked down on","chinese":"看不起"},{"english":"considered weak","chinese":"認為是軟弱的"},{"english":"quiet or unimportant","chinese":"安靜或不重要"},{"english":"what Kelvin could not","chinese":"Kelvin 做不到的事"},{"english":"checked his father's breathing","chinese":"檢查他父親的呼吸"},{"english":"called the ambulance again","chinese":"再次致電救護車"},{"english":"paramedics","chinese":"救護員"},{"english":"helped carry","chinese":"幫忙抬"},{"english":"down seventeen flights of stairs","chinese":"走下十七層樓梯"},{"english":"out of order","chinese":"壞了；不能使用"},{"english":"even then","chinese":"即使那樣"},{"english":"emergency room","chinese":"急症室"},{"english":"in shock","chinese":"驚魂未定"},{"english":"stayed with them","chinese":"留下來陪著他們"},{"english":"barely knew us","chinese":"幾乎不認識我們"},{"english":"the moment everything changed","chinese":"一切改變的時刻"},{"english":"hospital corridor","chinese":"醫院走廊"},{"english":"saw himself clearly","chinese":"清楚看見自己"},{"english":"spent years trying to","chinese":"花了多年試圖"},{"english":"look powerful","chinese":"看起來強大"},{"english":"humiliating others","chinese":"羞辱別人"},{"english":"real trouble","chinese":"真正的麻煩；真正危機"},{"english":"the strongest person in the room","chinese":"房間裏最強大的人"},{"english":"survived","chinese":"活了下來"},{"english":"recovery was slow","chinese":"康復過程緩慢"},{"english":"over the following months","chinese":"在接下來幾個月"},{"english":"accompanied him to","chinese":"陪同他去……"},{"english":"physiotherapy sessions","chinese":"物理治療療程"},{"english":"helped more at home","chinese":"在家中幫忙更多"},{"english":"began volunteering","chinese":"開始做義工"},{"english":"community centre","chinese":"社區中心"},{"english":"on weekends","chinese":"在週末"},{"english":"a way of apologising","chinese":"一種道歉的方式"},{"english":"became a habit","chinese":"變成習慣"},{"english":"helped children with homework","chinese":"幫助小朋友做功課"},{"english":"accompanied elderly people to appointments","chinese":"陪長者赴約"},{"english":"discovered that","chinese":"發現"},{"english":"real maturity","chinese":"真正成熟"},{"english":"being noticed","chinese":"被注意"},{"english":"being dependable","chinese":"可靠；值得依靠"},{"english":"used to think","chinese":"以前認為"},{"english":"being feared","chinese":"令人害怕"},{"english":"being useful","chinese":"有用；能幫上忙"},{"english":"just then","chinese":"就在那時"},{"english":"walked past","chinese":"走過"},{"english":"spotted Kelvin","chinese":"看見 Kelvin"},{"english":"waved shyly","chinese":"害羞地揮手"},{"english":"waved back","chinese":"揮手回應"},{"english":"natural warmth","chinese":"自然的溫暖"},{"english":"for a second","chinese":"有一秒鐘"},{"english":"disliked so intensely","chinese":"曾經那麼強烈地討厭"},{"english":"as evening fell","chinese":"隨著黃昏降臨"},{"english":"flickered on","chinese":"閃爍亮起"},{"english":"realised that","chinese":"意識到"},{"english":"time softens them","chinese":"時間使他們變得溫和"},{"english":"forces them to confront","chinese":"迫使他們面對"},{"english":"confront the truth","chinese":"面對真相"},{"english":"in Kelvin's case","chinese":"就 Kelvin 而言"},{"english":"kindness is not weakness","chinese":"善良不是軟弱"},{"english":"character reveals itself","chinese":"品格會顯露出來"},{"english":"moments of crisis","chinese":"危機時刻"},{"english":"stood up to leave","chinese":"站起來準備離開"},{"english":"felt as though","chinese":"感覺好像"},{"english":"two versions of the same person","chinese":"同一個人的兩個版本"},{"english":"standing before me","chinese":"站在我面前"},{"english":"wanted attention","chinese":"想得到注意"},{"english":"learned compassion","chinese":"學會同情與體恤"},{"english":"somehow","chinese":"不知怎的"},{"english":"in the middle of","chinese":"在……中間"},{"english":"noisy theme park","chinese":"嘈雜的主題公園"},{"english":"quiet change","chinese":"靜靜的改變"},{"english":"more remarkable than","chinese":"比……更了不起"},{"english":"any ride around us","chinese":"我們周圍任何機動遊戲"}]},"dse-writing-2025-part-b-q3":{"exerciseId":"dse-writing-2025-part-b-q3","essayKey":"","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=dse-writing-2025-part-b-q3","flashDeckId":"dse/writing/part-b/2025/Q3","paragraphs":[{"label":"Title","english":"When Eateries Become Classrooms","chinese":"當食肆變成課室"},{"label":"Salutation","english":"Dear Editor,","chinese":"尊敬的編輯："},{"label":"Intro","english":"In recent years, coffee shops and fast-food restaurants in Hong Kong have quietly taken on a new role. Besides serving meals, they are increasingly being used for lengthy activities such as tutorial lessons, mock interviews and worksheet drilling. In a city defined by cramped flats, soaring rents and limited public space, this trend may appear understandable at first glance. Yet it has also led restaurant owners, frontline staff and ordinary customers to ask whether private educational activities should be allowed to occupy commercial dining space for hours at a time. In my view, this practice should not be accepted as normal, because it places an unfair burden on businesses, inconveniences the public and conceals a deeper problem that Hong Kong should address properly. If we continue treating eateries as makeshift classrooms, we will not solve the city’s space problem; we will merely shift its cost onto others.","chinese":"近年來，香港的咖啡店和快餐店悄悄地承擔起了一種新的角色。 除了供應餐飲之外，它們也越來越常被用來進行長時間的活動，例如補習課、模擬面試以及反覆操練作業。 在一個以居住空間狹小、租金高昂以及公共空間有限為特徵的城市裡，這種趨勢乍看之下似乎可以理解。 然而，這也讓餐廳東主、前線員工以及一般顧客開始質疑，私人教育活動是否應該被允許一連數小時佔用商業餐飲空間。 在我看來，這種做法不應該被視為正常，因為它對商家造成不公平的負擔、為公眾帶來不便，並掩蓋了一個香港應該妥善處理的更深層問題。 如果我們繼續把食肆當成臨時教室，我們並不會解決這座城市的空間問題；我們只是把其代價轉嫁到別人身上而已。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"First, using restaurants as tutorial venues is fundamentally unfair to the businesses involved. A café or fast-food shop exists to serve diners efficiently, not to function as a low-cost classroom rented out through a single cup of coffee. When a tutor and several students occupy a four-person table for two or three hours after ordering the bare minimum, the shop loses far more than one seat. It loses turnover during peak hours, staff must manage lingering customers tactfully, and new diners may leave after seeing a lack of available tables. In Hong Kong, where rent and labour costs are notoriously high, such lost business is not a minor inconvenience but a real financial penalty. The problem becomes even worse once a venue develops a reputation as a “good place for tutoring”, because one lesson quickly attracts another. What begins as an individual choice can therefore become a systematic misuse of space. Put simply, tutors earn private income while restaurants absorb the hidden overhead. That is neither fair nor sustainable.","chinese":"首先，把餐廳當作補習場所，從根本上來說對相關商家並不公平。 咖啡店或快餐店存在的目的，是要有效率地服務用餐顧客，而不是透過一杯咖啡就被當成低成本教室來出租。 當一位補習老師和幾名學生只點最基本的餐飲，卻佔據一張四人桌兩三個小時時，店家失去的遠遠不只是一個座位。 店家在繁忙時段失去翻桌率，員工必須小心地處理久坐不走的顧客，而新來的食客看到沒有空位，也可能直接離開。 在香港這個租金與勞工成本都出名高昂的地方，這種生意損失不是小小的不便，而是真正的經濟懲罰。 一旦某個地點形成了「適合補習的好地方」這種名聲，問題就會變得更嚴重，因為一堂課很快就會吸引另一堂課。 因此，原本只是個人的選擇，最後可能演變成一種制度化的空間濫用。 簡單來說，補習老師賺取的是私人收入，而餐廳卻承擔了隱藏的營運成本。這既不公平，也無法長久持續。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"Moreover, this habit damages the wider social environment and promotes the wrong values. Education should cultivate discipline, respect and social awareness. However, holding tutorial lessons in eateries often teaches the opposite lesson: that as long as one can pay for a drink, one may effectively privatise shared space. Other patrons then bear the consequences. Office workers on a short lunch break may struggle to find seats. Elderly customers who simply want a place to rest are squeezed out. Families with children may have to carry trays around crowded dining areas because several tables have already been turned into mini-classrooms covered in notes, pens and past papers. At the same time, the learning environment itself is far from ideal. The constant clatter of trays, background chatter and frequent interruptions are hardly conducive to serious concentration. Students may complete exercises, but they are also absorbing an unhealthy message: convenience matters more than consideration. A city already under pressure should not normalize behaviour that erodes everyday courtesy.","chinese":"此外，這種習慣會破壞更廣泛的社會環境，並傳遞錯誤的價值觀。 教育本應培養紀律、尊重以及社會意識。 然而，在食肆裡進行補習，往往教會人的卻是相反的一課：只要付得起一杯飲料的錢，就可以實際上把共享空間私有化。 接著，其他顧客便必須承受後果。 在短暫午休中的上班族，可能會很難找到座位。 只想找個地方稍作休息的長者，也會被擠出去。 帶著孩子的家庭，可能得端著餐盤在擁擠的用餐區四處尋找座位，因為好幾張桌子早已被變成堆滿筆記、筆和歷屆試題的小型教室。 同時，這種學習環境本身也遠遠稱不上理想。 餐盤碰撞的聲音、背景雜談，以及頻繁的干擾，幾乎不利於真正專心學習。 學生也許完成了練習，但他們同時也在吸收一個不健康的訊息：方便比體諒他人更重要。 一座本來就壓力沉重的城市，不應該把侵蝕日常禮貌的行為視為正常。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 3","english":"Admittedly, some people defend this practice by arguing that many Hong Kong students do not have quiet homes, while libraries and study rooms are often full. That concern is real and should not be dismissed. Nevertheless, sympathy should not become justification. The fact that proper study space is insufficient does not mean restaurants should be expected to fill the gap for free. That is the wrong solution to the right problem. If tutorial activities are genuinely necessary, then tutorial centres should rent appropriate premises, schools should open more classrooms after hours, and community centres or public libraries should expand accessible study areas during examination seasons. Allowing commercial eateries to become unofficial classrooms simply lets the private tutoring industry externalise its operating costs while avoiding responsibility. In other words, it relieves pressure for a few individuals but entrenches the larger structural problem for everyone else.","chinese":"誠然，有些人為這種做法辯護，理由是許多香港學生家中並沒有安靜的學習環境，而圖書館和自修室也常常爆滿。 這種憂慮是真實存在的，不應被忽視。 然而，同情不應該變成合理化的藉口。 適當的學習空間不足，並不代表餐廳就應該被期待免費填補這個缺口。 這是用錯誤的方法去處理正確的問題。 如果補習活動真的是必要的，那麼補習社就應該租用合適的場地，學校應該在課後開放更多課室，而社區中心或公共圖書館也應該在考試季擴充可供使用的溫習空間。 讓商業食肆變成非正式教室，實際上只是讓私人補習產業把營運成本外部化，同時逃避本應承擔的責任。 換句話說，這樣做或許減輕了少數人的壓力，卻讓更大的結構性問題對所有其他人更加根深蒂固。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, I firmly believe that coffee shops and fast-food restaurants should not be treated as long-stay tutorial venues. Such a practice is unfair to businesses, inconsiderate to other customers and educationally misguided. Hong Kong needs proper answers, not improvised ones. Restaurant chains can introduce clearer seating policies, tutors should act more responsibly, and schools as well as the government should expand affordable study spaces so that students have somewhere suitable to learn without inconveniencing the public. If we truly care about both education and civic responsibility, we must stop pretending that a corner table and a cheap drink are an acceptable substitute for a real classroom.","chinese":"總而言之，我堅定相信咖啡店和快餐店不應該被當作可長時間逗留的補習場所。 這種做法對商家不公平、對其他顧客缺乏體諒，而且在教育上也有誤導之嫌。 香港需要的是妥善的解決方法，而不是臨時拼湊的權宜之計。 連鎖餐廳可以制定更清楚的座位使用政策，補習老師應該更負責任地行事，而學校與政府也應擴充可負擔的學習空間，讓學生能有適合學習的地方，同時不會打擾公眾。 如果我們真的同時重視教育與公民責任，我們就必須停止假裝角落裡的一張桌子和一杯便宜飲料，可以成為真正教室的合理替代品。"},{"label":"Closing","english":"Yours faithfully, Chris Wong","chinese":"此致敬禮， Chris Wong"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"In recent years","chinese":"近年來"},{"english":"coffee shops and fast-food restaurants","chinese":"咖啡店和快餐店"},{"english":"have quietly taken on a new role","chinese":"悄悄承擔新角色"},{"english":"besides serving meals","chinese":"除了供應膳食之外"},{"english":"are increasingly being used for","chinese":"越來越多被用作……"},{"english":"lengthy activities","chinese":"長時間活動"},{"english":"tutorial lessons","chinese":"補習課"},{"english":"mock interviews","chinese":"模擬面試"},{"english":"worksheet drilling","chinese":"操練工作紙"},{"english":"a city defined by","chinese":"一個以……為特徵的城市"},{"english":"cramped flats","chinese":"狹小單位"},{"english":"soaring rents","chinese":"飆升的租金"},{"english":"limited public space","chinese":"有限的公共空間"},{"english":"may appear understandable","chinese":"可能看似可以理解"},{"english":"at first glance","chinese":"乍看之下"},{"english":"has led people to ask whether","chinese":"使人開始質疑是否……"},{"english":"restaurant owners","chinese":"餐廳東主"},{"english":"frontline staff","chinese":"前線職員"},{"english":"ordinary customers","chinese":"普通顧客"},{"english":"private educational activities","chinese":"私人教育活動"},{"english":"occupy commercial dining space","chinese":"佔用商業用餐空間"},{"english":"for hours at a time","chinese":"一次佔用數小時"},{"english":"In my view","chinese":"在我看來"},{"english":"should not be accepted as normal","chinese":"不應被視為正常"},{"english":"places an unfair burden on","chinese":"對……造成不公平負擔"},{"english":"inconveniences the public","chinese":"令公眾不便"},{"english":"conceals a deeper problem","chinese":"掩蓋更深層問題"},{"english":"address properly","chinese":"妥善處理"},{"english":"treating eateries as makeshift classrooms","chinese":"把食肆當作臨時課室"},{"english":"makeshift classrooms","chinese":"臨時課室"},{"english":"the city's space problem","chinese":"城市空間問題"},{"english":"shift its cost onto others","chinese":"把成本轉嫁給他人"},{"english":"tutorial venues","chinese":"補習場所"},{"english":"fundamentally unfair to","chinese":"對……根本不公平"},{"english":"the businesses involved","chinese":"相關商戶"},{"english":"serve diners efficiently","chinese":"有效率地服務食客"},{"english":"function as a low-cost classroom","chinese":"充當低成本課室"},{"english":"rented out through a single cup of coffee","chinese":"只靠一杯咖啡就租用"},{"english":"a tutor and several students","chinese":"一名導師和幾名學生"},{"english":"occupy a four-person table","chinese":"佔用一張四人枱"},{"english":"ordering the bare minimum","chinese":"只點最低限度的消費"},{"english":"loses far more than one seat","chinese":"損失的不止一個座位"},{"english":"loses turnover","chinese":"失去翻枱機會"},{"english":"during peak hours","chinese":"在繁忙時間"},{"english":"manage lingering customers tactfully","chinese":"得體地處理久坐不走的顧客"},{"english":"lingering customers","chinese":"久坐不走的顧客"},{"english":"a lack of available tables","chinese":"沒有空枱"},{"english":"available tables","chinese":"可用的枱；空枱"},{"english":"rent and labour costs","chinese":"租金和人工成本"},{"english":"notoriously high","chinese":"出名地高昂"},{"english":"lost business","chinese":"流失的生意"},{"english":"a minor inconvenience","chinese":"小小的不便"},{"english":"a real financial penalty","chinese":"真正的財務代價"},{"english":"develops a reputation as","chinese":"形成……的名聲"},{"english":"a good place for tutoring","chinese":"適合補習的地方"},{"english":"one lesson quickly attracts another","chinese":"一堂課很快吸引另一堂課"},{"english":"begins as an individual choice","chinese":"起初只是個人選擇"},{"english":"systematic misuse of space","chinese":"系統性濫用空間"},{"english":"Put simply","chinese":"簡單來說"},{"english":"earn private income","chinese":"賺取私人收入"},{"english":"absorb the hidden overhead","chinese":"承擔隱藏營運成本"},{"english":"hidden overhead","chinese":"隱藏營運成本"},{"english":"neither fair nor sustainable","chinese":"既不公平也不可持續"},{"english":"damages the wider social environment","chinese":"損害更廣泛的社會環境"},{"english":"promotes the wrong values","chinese":"宣揚錯誤價值觀"},{"english":"cultivate discipline, respect and social awareness","chinese":"培養紀律、尊重和社會意識"},{"english":"teaches the opposite lesson","chinese":"傳遞相反教訓"},{"english":"as long as","chinese":"只要"},{"english":"pay for a drink","chinese":"付一杯飲品的錢"},{"english":"effectively privatise shared space","chinese":"實際上把共享空間私有化"},{"english":"shared space","chinese":"共享空間"},{"english":"bear the consequences","chinese":"承受後果"},{"english":"other patrons","chinese":"其他顧客"},{"english":"on a short lunch break","chinese":"午飯時間有限"},{"english":"struggle to find seats","chinese":"難以找到座位"},{"english":"elderly customers","chinese":"長者顧客"},{"english":"a place to rest","chinese":"休息的地方"},{"english":"are squeezed out","chinese":"被擠走"},{"english":"families with children","chinese":"帶小朋友的家庭"},{"english":"carry trays around","chinese":"拿着托盤到處走"},{"english":"crowded dining areas","chinese":"擠迫的用餐區"},{"english":"turned into mini-classrooms","chinese":"被變成小型課室"},{"english":"covered in notes, pens and past papers","chinese":"佈滿筆記、筆和歷屆試卷"},{"english":"past papers","chinese":"歷屆試卷"},{"english":"At the same time","chinese":"同時"},{"english":"the learning environment itself","chinese":"學習環境本身"},{"english":"far from ideal","chinese":"遠非理想"},{"english":"the constant clatter of trays","chinese":"托盤持續碰撞聲"},{"english":"background chatter","chinese":"背景談話聲"},{"english":"frequent interruptions","chinese":"頻繁干擾"},{"english":"hardly conducive to","chinese":"不利於……"},{"english":"serious concentration","chinese":"認真專注"},{"english":"complete exercises","chinese":"完成練習"},{"english":"absorbing an unhealthy message","chinese":"吸收不健康的信息"},{"english":"convenience matters more than consideration","chinese":"方便比體諒更重要"},{"english":"under pressure","chinese":"承受壓力"},{"english":"normalize behaviour","chinese":"將行為正常化"},{"english":"erodes everyday courtesy","chinese":"破壞日常禮貌"},{"english":"everyday courtesy","chinese":"日常禮貌"},{"english":"Admittedly","chinese":"誠然"},{"english":"defend this practice by arguing that","chinese":"以……為理由替這做法辯護"},{"english":"quiet homes","chinese":"安靜的家居環境"},{"english":"libraries and study rooms","chinese":"圖書館和自修室"},{"english":"are often full","chinese":"經常爆滿"},{"english":"should not be dismissed","chinese":"不應被忽視"},{"english":"Nevertheless","chinese":"然而"},{"english":"sympathy should not become justification","chinese":"同情不應變成合理化理由"},{"english":"proper study space","chinese":"合適的學習空間"},{"english":"insufficient","chinese":"不足夠"},{"english":"fill the gap for free","chinese":"免費填補缺口"},{"english":"the wrong solution to the right problem","chinese":"對正確問題採用錯誤解決方法"},{"english":"genuinely necessary","chinese":"真正有需要"},{"english":"rent appropriate premises","chinese":"租用合適處所"},{"english":"open more classrooms after hours","chinese":"課後開放更多課室"},{"english":"community centres","chinese":"社區中心"},{"english":"expand accessible study areas","chinese":"擴大可使用的自修空間"},{"english":"during examination seasons","chinese":"在考試季期間"},{"english":"unofficial classrooms","chinese":"非官方課室"},{"english":"the private tutoring industry","chinese":"私人補習行業"},{"english":"externalise its operating costs","chinese":"將營運成本外部化"},{"english":"avoiding responsibility","chinese":"逃避責任"},{"english":"relieves pressure for","chinese":"為……紓緩壓力"},{"english":"entrenches the larger structural problem","chinese":"使更大的結構性問題根深蒂固"},{"english":"everyone else","chinese":"其他所有人"},{"english":"In conclusion","chinese":"總括而言"},{"english":"firmly believe that","chinese":"堅信"},{"english":"long-stay tutorial venues","chinese":"長時間逗留的補習場所"},{"english":"inconsiderate to other customers","chinese":"對其他顧客不體諒"},{"english":"educationally misguided","chinese":"在教育上方向錯誤"},{"english":"proper answers, not improvised ones","chinese":"需要妥善答案，而非臨時湊合方案"},{"english":"restaurant chains","chinese":"連鎖餐廳"},{"english":"clearer seating policies","chinese":"更清晰的座位政策"},{"english":"act more responsibly","chinese":"更負責任地行事"},{"english":"schools as well as the government","chinese":"學校以及政府"},{"english":"affordable study spaces","chinese":"負擔得起的學習空間"},{"english":"somewhere suitable to learn","chinese":"適合學習的地方"},{"english":"without inconveniencing the public","chinese":"不令公眾不便"},{"english":"truly care about","chinese":"真正關心"},{"english":"civic responsibility","chinese":"公民責任"},{"english":"stop pretending that","chinese":"停止假裝"},{"english":"a corner table and a cheap drink","chinese":"一張角落枱和一杯廉價飲品"},{"english":"an acceptable substitute for ……","chinese":"的可接受替代品"},{"english":"a real classroom","chinese":"真正的課室"}]},"dse-writing-2025-part-b-q4":{"exerciseId":"dse-writing-2025-part-b-q4","essayKey":"","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=dse-writing-2025-part-b-q4","flashDeckId":"dse/writing/part-b/2025/Q4","paragraphs":[{"label":"Paragraph 1","english":"Making Teamwork Work: Overcoming the Hidden Difficulties of Group Work","chinese":""},{"label":"Paragraph 2","english":"In today’s workplace, few important tasks are completed by one employee alone. As companies deal with increasingly complex problems, from product design to crisis management, they have come to rely heavily on group work in order to combine expertise, improve decision-making and produce stronger results. Yet, despite its recognised value, teamwork is often met with reluctance rather than enthusiasm. Many workers associate it with wasted time, uneven effort and unnecessary conflict. Although group work is essential in the modern workplace, it often becomes unpopular because of unequal participation, poor communication and clashes of personality; these problems, however, can be overcome through clear structures, effective leadership and a culture of mutual accountability.","chinese":"在今日的職場中，很少有重要工作是由單一員工獨自完成的。 隨著公司要處理愈來愈複雜的問題，從產品設計到危機管理，它們越來越依賴團隊合作，以結合專業知識、改善決策，並產生更好的成果。 然而，儘管團隊合作的價值早已被認可，人們對它的反應往往不是熱情，而是抗拒。 許多員工會把它和浪費時間、付出不均以及不必要的衝突聯想在一起。 雖然團隊合作在現代職場中不可或缺，但它往往因為參與不均、溝通不良以及個性衝突而不受歡迎；然而，這些問題可以透過清楚的制度、有效的領導以及彼此負責的文化來克服。"},{"label":"Paragraph 3","english":"One major challenge of group work is the unequal distribution of effort. In many teams, some employees shoulder most of the burden while others contribute very little. This creates resentment almost immediately. When diligent workers realise that their performance is being tied to colleagues who are less committed, motivation begins to decline. Instead of focusing on the quality of the task, they become preoccupied with the unfairness of the process. Over time, this not only damages morale but also discourages high performers from cooperating wholeheartedly in future projects. A simple example can be seen in office presentations: while two members may spend hours researching data and preparing slides, another may merely read from the script on the day itself and still receive equal credit. To solve this problem, responsibilities should be divided clearly from the outset. Each member should have a defined role, a deadline and a measurable output. Managers can also introduce progress checks and individual evaluations so that contribution becomes visible rather than assumed. When accountability is built into the system, teamwork stops feeling like exploitation and starts feeling like genuine collaboration.","chinese":"團隊合作的一大挑戰，就是付出分配不均。 在許多團隊中，有些員工承擔了大部分工作，而其他人卻幾乎沒有什麼貢獻。 這幾乎會立刻引發不滿情緒。 當認真的員工發現自己的表現竟然和那些不夠投入的同事綁在一起時，他們的動力便開始下降。 他們不再專注於工作的品質，反而會一直掛念整個過程有多麼不公平。 久而久之，這不僅會打擊士氣，也會讓高表現者在未來的合作中不願全心投入。 一個簡單的例子可以在辦公室簡報中看到：兩位成員可能花上好幾個小時蒐集資料、準備投影片，而另一位成員卻可能只是在當天照稿朗讀，卻仍然得到同樣的功勞。 要解決這個問題，責任必須從一開始就清楚分配。 每位成員都應該有明確的角色、截止日期以及可衡量的成果。 管理者也可以加入進度檢查和個別評估，使每個人的貢獻能被看見，而不是只靠想像。 當問責機制被納入制度中，團隊合作就不再像是一種剝削，而會更像是真正的合作。"},{"label":"Paragraph 4","english":"A second difficulty is poor communication, which can quietly ruin even a talented team. Group work often fails not because members lack ability, but because they misunderstand one another’s expectations. If tasks are vaguely assigned, employees may duplicate work, overlook crucial details or proceed in completely different directions. As a result, time is wasted correcting mistakes that could have been prevented through simple clarification. This problem is especially serious in large organisations, where departments such as marketing, finance and operations may use different professional language and priorities. For instance, a product team may push for speed, while the compliance team insists on caution; without proper communication, these differing aims can delay the entire project. The solution is not merely “talking more”, but communicating more precisely. Teams should begin with a shared objective, a realistic timeline and agreed channels for updates. Brief but regular meetings, written summaries and digital project-management tools can reduce confusion substantially. Moreover, workers should be encouraged to ask questions early rather than conceal uncertainty out of embarrassment. Once communication becomes structured, group work becomes far more efficient, because people are no longer guessing what others mean or need.","chinese":"第二個困難是溝通不良，而這種問題甚至能悄悄毀掉一支有才華的團隊。 團隊合作之所以失敗，往往不是因為成員缺乏能力，而是因為他們誤解了彼此的期望。 如果工作分配得模糊不清，員工可能會重複做同樣的事、忽略關鍵細節，或朝著完全不同的方向進行。 結果就是，大家把時間浪費在修正那些本來只要稍微釐清一下就能避免的錯誤上。 這個問題在大型機構中特別嚴重，因為像市場部、財務部和營運部等不同部門，往往使用不同的專業語言，也有不同的優先考量。 例如，產品團隊可能追求速度，而合規團隊則堅持謹慎；如果缺乏適當溝通， 這些不同目標就可能拖慢整個計畫。 解決方法不只是「多說一點」，而是更精準地溝通。 團隊應該從共同目標、實際可行的時間表，以及雙方同意的更新管道開始。 簡短但定期的會議、書面摘要以及數位專案管理工具，都能大幅減少混亂。 此外，員工也應該被鼓勵及早提出問題，而不是因為尷尬就把不確定藏起來。 一旦溝通變得有結構，團隊合作就會有效率得多，因為人們不再需要猜測別人真正的意思或需求。"},{"label":"Paragraph 5","english":"A third and often underestimated challenge is interpersonal conflict. Group work brings together individuals with different temperaments, habits and values. Some employees are direct and fast-paced; others are cautious and reflective. Some prefer to dominate discussion, whereas quieter members may hesitate to speak even when they have valuable ideas. Under pressure, these differences can easily escalate into tension. A team meeting that should generate solutions may instead turn into a contest of egos, with people defending pride rather than pursuing results. Such conflict is not only emotionally draining but also professionally damaging, because it weakens trust, which is the foundation of all effective teamwork. Nevertheless, personality clashes need not destroy cooperation. Strong leadership is crucial here. A competent team leader should ensure that discussion remains respectful, that quieter members are invited to contribute and that disagreement is directed towards ideas rather than individuals. In addition, workplaces should provide training in conflict resolution and emotional intelligence, since technical skills alone do not guarantee productive collaboration. When differences are managed maturely, diversity becomes an advantage rather than a source of division.","chinese":"第三個而且經常被低估的挑戰，是人際衝突。 團隊合作會把不同性格、習慣和價值觀的人聚集在一起。 有些員工做事直接、節奏快速；另一些則較為謹慎、善於思考。 有些人喜歡主導討論，而較安靜的成員即使有寶貴的想法，也可能不敢開口。 在壓力之下，這些差異很容易升高成緊張關係。 原本應該產生解決方案的團隊會議，反而可能變成自尊心的競賽，人們維護的是自己的面子，而不是追求成果。 這樣的衝突不僅會讓人情緒上疲憊，也會對專業表現造成傷害，因為它削弱了信任，而信任正是所有有效團隊合作的基礎。 然而，個性衝突不一定非得破壞合作不可。 在這裡，強而有力的領導非常重要。 一位有能力的團隊領導者應該確保討論保持尊重、較安靜的成員被邀請發言，以及分歧是針對觀點而不是針對個人。 此外，職場也應該提供衝突處理和情緒智商方面的訓練，因為只有技術能力並不能保證合作會有成效。 當差異能夠被成熟地處理時，多樣性就會成為優勢，而不是分裂的來源。"},{"label":"Paragraph 6","english":"In conclusion, group work may be unpopular among workers because it often suffers from free-riding, miscommunication and interpersonal tension. However, these problems do not prove that teamwork is flawed by nature; rather, they show that teamwork must be managed carefully if it is to fulfil its promise. Group work is most effective when contribution is transparent, communication is disciplined and leadership is strong enough to unite different personalities around a common purpose. Employers, therefore, should not simply require workers to collaborate; they should create the conditions that make collaboration fair, focused and fruitful. Only then will group work be valued not merely in theory, but in everyday professional life.","chinese":"總而言之，團隊合作之所以不受員工歡迎，是因為它常常受到搭便車、溝通失誤以及人際緊張關係的影響。 然而，這些問題並不能證明團隊合作天生就有缺陷；相反地，它們顯示的是， 若要讓團隊合作真正發揮應有的價值，就必須被妥善管理。 當貢獻是透明的、溝通是有紀律的，而領導又足夠強大去把不同性格的人團結在共同目標之下時，團隊合作才會最有效。 因此，僱主不應只是要求員工合作；他們更應該創造出讓合作變得公平、專注而且有成果的條件。 只有到了那個時候，團隊合作才不會只是理論上受到重視，而是真正在日常職場生活中被珍惜。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"making teamwork work","chinese":"令團隊合作發揮作用"},{"english":"overcoming hidden difficulties","chinese":"克服隱藏困難"},{"english":"hidden difficulties","chinese":"隱藏困難"},{"english":"in today's workplace","chinese":"在今天的職場"},{"english":"few important tasks","chinese":"很少重要任務"},{"english":"by one employee alone","chinese":"只由一名員工獨自完成"},{"english":"deal with increasingly complex problems","chinese":"處理越來越複雜的問題"},{"english":"increasingly complex problems","chinese":"越來越複雜的問題"},{"english":"from product design to crisis management","chinese":"由產品設計到危機管理"},{"english":"product design","chinese":"產品設計"},{"english":"crisis management","chinese":"危機管理"},{"english":"come to rely heavily on","chinese":"逐漸非常依賴"},{"english":"group work","chinese":"小組工作；團隊工作"},{"english":"in order to","chinese":"為了"},{"english":"combine expertise","chinese":"結合專業知識"},{"english":"improve decision-making","chinese":"改善決策"},{"english":"produce stronger results","chinese":"產生更佳成果"},{"english":"despite its recognised value","chinese":"儘管其價值獲得承認"},{"english":"recognised value","chinese":"公認價值"},{"english":"be met with reluctance","chinese":"遭到不情願的反應"},{"english":"rather than enthusiasm","chinese":"而不是熱情"},{"english":"associate something with","chinese":"把……與……聯繫起來"},{"english":"wasted time","chinese":"浪費時間"},{"english":"uneven effort","chinese":"付出不均"},{"english":"unnecessary conflict","chinese":"不必要的衝突"},{"english":"essential in the modern workplace","chinese":"在現代職場中不可或缺"},{"english":"unequal participation","chinese":"參與不均"},{"english":"poor communication","chinese":"溝通不善"},{"english":"clashes of personality","chinese":"性格衝突"},{"english":"be overcome through","chinese":"透過……克服"},{"english":"clear structures","chinese":"清晰架構"},{"english":"effective leadership","chinese":"有效領導"},{"english":"mutual accountability","chinese":"互相問責"},{"english":"one major challenge","chinese":"一個主要挑戰"},{"english":"unequal distribution of effort","chinese":"付出分配不均"},{"english":"shoulder most of the burden","chinese":"承擔大部分負擔"},{"english":"contribute very little","chinese":"貢獻很少"},{"english":"create resentment","chinese":"造成不滿"},{"english":"almost immediately","chinese":"幾乎即時"},{"english":"diligent workers","chinese":"勤奮的員工"},{"english":"be tied to","chinese":"與……掛鈎"},{"english":"less committed","chinese":"較不投入的"},{"english":"motivation begins to decline","chinese":"動力開始下降"},{"english":"instead of focusing on","chinese":"而不是專注於"},{"english":"the quality of the task","chinese":"任務質素"},{"english":"become preoccupied with","chinese":"滿腦子想着；過分關注"},{"english":"the unfairness of the process","chinese":"過程的不公平"},{"english":"over time","chinese":"隨着時間過去"},{"english":"damage morale","chinese":"打擊士氣"},{"english":"discourage high performers from","chinese":"令表現優秀者不願……"},{"english":"high performers","chinese":"表現優秀者"},{"english":"cooperate wholeheartedly","chinese":"全心全意合作"},{"english":"future projects","chinese":"未來項目"},{"english":"a simple example can be seen in","chinese":"一個簡單例子可見於"},{"english":"office presentations","chinese":"辦公室匯報"},{"english":"spend hours doing","chinese":"花數小時做……"},{"english":"researching data","chinese":"搜集數據"},{"english":"preparing slides","chinese":"準備簡報"},{"english":"merely read from the script","chinese":"只是照稿讀"},{"english":"on the day itself","chinese":"在當日"},{"english":"receive equal credit","chinese":"獲得同等功勞"},{"english":"to solve this problem","chinese":"為了解決這個問題"},{"english":"divide responsibilities clearly","chinese":"清楚分配責任"},{"english":"from the outset","chinese":"從一開始"},{"english":"a defined role","chinese":"明確角色"},{"english":"a measurable output","chinese":"可衡量的成果"},{"english":"introduce progress checks","chinese":"引入進度檢查"},{"english":"individual evaluations","chinese":"個人評估"},{"english":"contribution becomes visible","chinese":"貢獻變得可見"},{"english":"rather than assumed","chinese":"而不是被假定"},{"english":"be built into the system","chinese":"被納入制度之中"},{"english":"stop feeling like exploitation","chinese":"不再感覺像被剝削"},{"english":"genuine collaboration","chinese":"真正合作"},{"english":"a second difficulty","chinese":"第二個困難"},{"english":"quietly ruin","chinese":"悄悄破壞"},{"english":"talented team","chinese":"有才能的團隊"},{"english":"not because…, but because…","chinese":"不是因為……而是因為……"},{"english":"lack ability","chinese":"缺乏能力"},{"english":"misunderstand one another's expectations","chinese":"誤解彼此的期望"},{"english":"tasks are vaguely assigned","chinese":"任務被含糊分配"},{"english":"duplicate work","chinese":"重複工作"},{"english":"overlook crucial details","chinese":"忽略關鍵細節"},{"english":"proceed in different directions","chinese":"朝不同方向進行"},{"english":"as a result","chinese":"結果"},{"english":"time is wasted","chinese":"時間被浪費"},{"english":"correcting mistakes","chinese":"改正錯誤"},{"english":"could have been prevented","chinese":"原本可以被避免"},{"english":"simple clarification","chinese":"簡單澄清"},{"english":"especially serious","chinese":"尤其嚴重"},{"english":"large organisations","chinese":"大型機構"},{"english":"departments such as","chinese":"例如……等部門"},{"english":"marketing, finance and operations","chinese":"市場推廣、財務和營運"},{"english":"professional language","chinese":"專業用語"},{"english":"priorities","chinese":"優先事項"},{"english":"push for speed","chinese":"追求速度"},{"english":"compliance team","chinese":"合規團隊"},{"english":"insist on caution","chinese":"堅持謹慎"},{"english":"differing aims","chinese":"不同目標"},{"english":"delay the entire project","chinese":"延誤整個項目"},{"english":"not merely “talking more”","chinese":"不只是「多說話」"},{"english":"communicating more precisely","chinese":"更精準地溝通"},{"english":"shared objective","chinese":"共同目標"},{"english":"realistic timeline","chinese":"實際可行的時間表"},{"english":"agreed channels for updates","chinese":"約定好的更新渠道"},{"english":"brief but regular meetings","chinese":"簡短但定期的會議"},{"english":"written summaries","chinese":"書面摘要"},{"english":"digital project-management tools","chinese":"數碼項目管理工具"},{"english":"reduce confusion substantially","chinese":"大幅減少混亂"},{"english":"be encouraged to ask questions early","chinese":"被鼓勵及早提問"},{"english":"conceal uncertainty","chinese":"隱藏不確定"},{"english":"out of embarrassment","chinese":"出於尷尬"},{"english":"communication becomes structured","chinese":"溝通變得有系統"},{"english":"far more efficient","chinese":"效率高得多"},{"english":"no longer guessing","chinese":"不再猜測"},{"english":"a third and often underestimated challenge","chinese":"第三個經常被低估的挑戰"},{"english":"interpersonal conflict","chinese":"人際衝突"},{"english":"bring together","chinese":"把……聚在一起"},{"english":"different temperaments","chinese":"不同性情"},{"english":"habits and values","chinese":"習慣和價值觀"},{"english":"direct and fast-paced","chinese":"直接而節奏快"},{"english":"cautious and reflective","chinese":"謹慎而善於反思"},{"english":"dominate discussion","chinese":"主導討論"},{"english":"quieter members","chinese":"較沉默的成員"},{"english":"hesitate to speak","chinese":"猶豫是否發言"},{"english":"valuable ideas","chinese":"有價值的想法"},{"english":"under pressure","chinese":"在壓力下"},{"english":"escalate into tension","chinese":"升級成緊張關係"},{"english":"generate solutions","chinese":"產生解決方案"},{"english":"turn into a contest of egos","chinese":"變成自我較量"},{"english":"defend pride","chinese":"維護自尊"},{"english":"pursue results","chinese":"追求成果"},{"english":"emotionally draining","chinese":"令人情緒疲憊"},{"english":"professionally damaging","chinese":"對工作有害"},{"english":"weaken trust","chinese":"削弱信任"},{"english":"the foundation of","chinese":"……的基礎"},{"english":"effective teamwork","chinese":"有效團隊合作"},{"english":"nevertheless","chinese":"儘管如此"},{"english":"personality clashes","chinese":"性格衝突"},{"english":"need not destroy cooperation","chinese":"不一定會破壞合作"},{"english":"strong leadership","chinese":"強而有力的領導"},{"english":"crucial","chinese":"關鍵的"},{"english":"competent team leader","chinese":"稱職的團隊領袖"},{"english":"ensure that","chinese":"確保"},{"english":"discussion remains respectful","chinese":"討論保持尊重"},{"english":"invited to contribute","chinese":"被邀請作出貢獻"},{"english":"disagreement is directed towards ideas","chinese":"分歧應針對想法"},{"english":"rather than individuals","chinese":"而不是個人"},{"english":"conflict resolution","chinese":"衝突處理"},{"english":"emotional intelligence","chinese":"情緒智商"},{"english":"technical skills alone","chinese":"單靠技術能力"},{"english":"guarantee productive collaboration","chinese":"保證有成效的合作"},{"english":"productive collaboration","chinese":"有成效的合作"},{"english":"managed maturely","chinese":"成熟地管理"},{"english":"diversity becomes an advantage","chinese":"多元性成為優勢"},{"english":"a source of division","chinese":"分裂的來源"},{"english":"in conclusion","chinese":"總結而言"},{"english":"unpopular among workers","chinese":"不受員工歡迎"},{"english":"suffer from","chinese":"受到……困擾"},{"english":"free-riding","chinese":"搭便車；坐享其成"},{"english":"miscommunication","chinese":"溝通失誤"},{"english":"interpersonal tension","chinese":"人際緊張"},{"english":"flawed by nature","chinese":"本質上有缺陷"},{"english":"fulfil its promise","chinese":"發揮其應有潛力"},{"english":"contribution is transparent","chinese":"貢獻透明"},{"english":"communication is disciplined","chinese":"溝通有紀律"},{"english":"unite different personalities around","chinese":"團結不同性格的人圍繞……"},{"english":"common purpose","chinese":"共同目標"},{"english":"employers","chinese":"僱主"},{"english":"require workers to collaborate","chinese":"要求員工合作"},{"english":"create the conditions","chinese":"創造條件"},{"english":"fair, focused and fruitful","chinese":"公平、專注而有成果"},{"english":"only then","chinese":"只有到那時"},{"english":"valued not merely in theory","chinese":"不只是理論上被重視"},{"english":"everyday professional life","chinese":"日常職業生活"}]},"hkfsd-incident-report-3":{"exerciseId":"hkfsd-incident-report-3","essayKey":"","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=hkfsd-incident-report-3","flashDeckId":"government/hkfsd/incident-reports/incident-report-3","paragraphs":[{"label":"Paragraph 1","english":"At 18:07 hours on 9 July 2026, crews from Kowloon Bay Fire Station were dispatched through the Fire Services Communications Centre to a road traffic accident on Wang Chiu Road, Kowloon Bay. The initial report indicated that a private car had collided with a light goods vehicle and that one person was trapped inside the private car.","chinese":""},{"label":"Paragraph 2","english":"Upon arrival at 18:14 hours, the fire crew found the private car with extensive damage to the front driver's side. The male driver, aged approximately 40, was conscious and responsive but was trapped in the driver's seat by deformation of the door and dashboard. A female passenger had already exited the vehicle and complained of minor chest pain. The driver of the light goods vehicle was uninjured. No fire or fuel leakage was detected.","chinese":""},{"label":"Paragraph 3","english":"The incident commander established a safe working area and ordered the damaged private car to be stabilised before extrication commenced. The vehicle's electrical system was isolated as a precaution. Ambulance personnel entered the vehicle to assess and monitor the trapped driver while firefighters deployed hydraulic rescue tools. A spreader was used to force open the damaged driver's door, followed by a hydraulic cutter to remove sections of the door frame. The dashboard was then displaced sufficiently to free the driver's lower limbs.","chinese":""},{"label":"Paragraph 4","english":"The casualty was successfully extricated from the vehicle at 18:46 hours and transferred onto an ambulance stretcher. He sustained suspected fractures to his left leg and minor facial injuries but remained conscious throughout the operation. The female passenger was also treated by ambulance personnel at the scene. Both casualties were subsequently transported to hospital for further examination and treatment.","chinese":""},{"label":"Paragraph 5","english":"A final inspection confirmed that there was no fire, fuel leak, or other immediate hazard from either vehicle. The scene was handed over to the Hong Kong Police Force for traffic investigation and vehicle recovery arrangements. The fire crew completed the operation and returned to the station at 19:18 hours.","chinese":""}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"Fire Services Department","chinese":"消防處"},{"english":"Incident Report","chinese":"事故報告"},{"english":"Date of Report","chinese":"報告日期"},{"english":"Incident Number","chinese":"事故編號"},{"english":"Reporting Officer","chinese":"報告人員"},{"english":"Station Officer","chinese":"消防隊長"},{"english":"Fire Station","chinese":"消防局"},{"english":"at 18:07 hours","chinese":"於18時07分"},{"english":"crews from","chinese":"來自……的隊伍"},{"english":"be dispatched through","chinese":"經由……調派"},{"english":"Fire Services Communications Centre","chinese":"消防通訊中心"},{"english":"road traffic accident","chinese":"道路交通意外"},{"english":"initial report","chinese":"初步報告"},{"english":"indicate that","chinese":"顯示；指出"},{"english":"private car","chinese":"私家車"},{"english":"collide with","chinese":"與……相撞"},{"english":"light goods vehicle","chinese":"輕型貨車"},{"english":"one person was trapped","chinese":"一人被困"},{"english":"inside the private car","chinese":"在私家車內"},{"english":"upon arrival","chinese":"到場後"},{"english":"fire crew","chinese":"消防隊伍"},{"english":"extensive damage","chinese":"嚴重損毀"},{"english":"front driver's side","chinese":"司機位前方一側"},{"english":"male driver","chinese":"男司機"},{"english":"aged approximately","chinese":"年約"},{"english":"conscious and responsive","chinese":"清醒並有反應"},{"english":"trapped in the driver's seat","chinese":"被困於司機位"},{"english":"deformation of","chinese":"……變形"},{"english":"door and dashboard","chinese":"車門及儀錶板"},{"english":"female passenger","chinese":"女乘客"},{"english":"exit the vehicle","chinese":"離開車輛"},{"english":"complain of","chinese":"報稱有……不適"},{"english":"minor chest pain","chinese":"胸口輕微疼痛"},{"english":"be uninjured","chinese":"沒有受傷"},{"english":"fuel leakage","chinese":"燃油洩漏"},{"english":"be detected","chinese":"被發現；被探測到"},{"english":"incident commander","chinese":"事故指揮官"},{"english":"establish a safe working area","chinese":"設立安全工作區"},{"english":"safe working area","chinese":"安全工作區"},{"english":"order something to be stabilised","chinese":"下令穩固……"},{"english":"damaged private car","chinese":"受損私家車"},{"english":"be stabilised","chinese":"被穩固；被固定"},{"english":"before extrication commenced","chinese":"在脫困行動開始前"},{"english":"extrication","chinese":"拯救脫困行動"},{"english":"commence","chinese":"開始；展開"},{"english":"vehicle's electrical system","chinese":"車輛電力系統"},{"english":"be isolated as a precaution","chinese":"作為預防措施被隔離"},{"english":"ambulance personnel","chinese":"救護人員"},{"english":"enter the vehicle","chinese":"進入車輛"},{"english":"assess and monitor","chinese":"評估並監察"},{"english":"trapped driver","chinese":"被困司機"},{"english":"deploy hydraulic rescue tools","chinese":"部署液壓救援工具"},{"english":"hydraulic rescue tools","chinese":"液壓救援工具"},{"english":"spreader","chinese":"擴張器"},{"english":"force open","chinese":"強行撬開"},{"english":"damaged driver's door","chinese":"受損司機位車門"},{"english":"hydraulic cutter","chinese":"液壓剪"},{"english":"remove sections of","chinese":"移除……部分"},{"english":"door frame","chinese":"車門框架"},{"english":"dashboard was displaced","chinese":"儀錶板被移開"},{"english":"sufficiently","chinese":"足夠地；充分地"},{"english":"free someone's lower limbs","chinese":"釋放某人的下肢"},{"english":"lower limbs","chinese":"下肢"},{"english":"casualty","chinese":"傷者"},{"english":"be successfully extricated","chinese":"成功被救出"},{"english":"be transferred onto","chinese":"被移送到……上"},{"english":"ambulance stretcher","chinese":"救護車擔架"},{"english":"sustain suspected fractures","chinese":"懷疑骨折"},{"english":"minor facial injuries","chinese":"面部輕傷"},{"english":"remain conscious throughout","chinese":"全程保持清醒"},{"english":"throughout the operation","chinese":"在整個行動期間"},{"english":"be treated at the scene","chinese":"在現場接受治理"},{"english":"at the scene","chinese":"在現場"},{"english":"be subsequently transported to hospital","chinese":"隨後被送往醫院"},{"english":"further examination and treatment","chinese":"進一步檢查及治療"},{"english":"final inspection","chinese":"最後檢查"},{"english":"confirm that","chinese":"確認"},{"english":"fuel leak","chinese":"燃油洩漏"},{"english":"immediate hazard","chinese":"即時危險"},{"english":"either vehicle","chinese":"任何一輛車"},{"english":"be handed over to","chinese":"移交予……"},{"english":"Hong Kong Police Force","chinese":"香港警務處"},{"english":"traffic investigation","chinese":"交通調查"},{"english":"vehicle recovery arrangements","chinese":"車輛拖走及善後安排"},{"english":"complete the operation","chinese":"完成行動"},{"english":"return to the station","chinese":"返回消防局"}]},"hkpf-civic-composition-4":{"exerciseId":"hkpf-civic-composition-4","essayKey":"","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=hkpf-civic-composition-4","flashDeckId":"government/hkpf/writing-composition/composition-4","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"The proposal to raise the non-local student ceiling should be supported in principle, but not as a race for numbers. Hong Kong benefits when its universities attract bright students from the mainland, Asia and beyond: a more international campus can sharpen ideas, deepen cultural understanding and strengthen the city’s role as an education hub. However, the final arrangement must be built on one firm principle: local students must not lose opportunities in practice, even if their funded places remain unchanged on paper.","chinese":"提高非本地學生比例上限的建議，原則上值得支持，但它不應變成一場追逐數字的競賽。 當香港的大學能夠吸引來自內地、亞洲以至其他地區的優秀學生時，香港可以從中受益：一個更國際化的校園能夠激發思想、深化文化理解，並加強香港作為教育樞紐的角色。 然而，最終安排必須建立在一項堅定原則之上：即使本地學生的資助學額在紙面上維持不變，他們在實際上也不應失去機會。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"The main risk is that university life is more than admission quotas. Hostel rooms, laboratory space, tutorial attention, counselling services, exchange places and internships are all limited resources. If enrolment grows faster than capacity, the policy may look like a golden bridge but feel like a crowded corridor. Local students could then face stronger competition for campus opportunities, while non-local students may also receive weaker support after arrival. Therefore, the Government should require each university to conduct a capacity audit before further expansion is approved. Non-local tuition income should be partly ring-fenced for new hostel places, upgraded teaching facilities, mental health services, language support and career guidance. Clear indicators, such as hostel supply, staff-student ratios and internship availability, should be published annually.","chinese":"主要風險在於，大學生活並不只是取錄名額的問題。 宿舍房間、實驗室空間、小組教學關注、輔導服務、交換生名額和實習機會，全部都是有限資源。 如果收生增長快於大學承載能力，這項政策表面上可能像一座黃金橋樑，但實際感受卻可能像一條擠迫的走廊。 到時本地學生可能會在校園機會上面對更強競爭，而非本地學生抵港後也可能得不到足夠支援。 因此，政府應要求每所大學在批准進一步擴收之前，先進行承載能力審核。 非本地學生的學費收入應部分指定用於新增宿舍宿位、改善教學設施、加強心理健康服務、語言支援及就業輔導。 政府和大學亦應每年公布清晰指標，例如宿舍供應、師生比例及實習機會數量"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"Universities should also manage the change through phased implementation rather than a sudden leap. They should set transparent rules for hostel allocation, exchange nominations and scholarship distribution, so that fairness is seen as well as claimed. At the same time, universities can work with employers, alumni and professional bodies to create more internships, mentoring schemes and community projects for both local and non-local students. In this way, internationalisation will not become a zero-sum game. With careful planning, honest communication and measurable safeguards, Hong Kong can open its doors wider without squeezing its own students out of the room.","chinese":"大學亦應透過分階段推行來管理這項轉變，而不是突然大幅擴展。 大學應就宿舍分配、交換生提名及獎學金分配訂立透明規則，讓公平不只是口頭承諾，而是清楚可見。 同時，大學可以與僱主、校友及專業團體合作，為本地和非本地學生創造更多實習、師友計劃和社區項目。 這樣一來，國際化便不會變成一場零和遊戲。 只要有周詳規劃、坦誠溝通和可量度的保障措施，香港便可以把大門開得更闊，而不會把本地學生擠出房間之外。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"the proposal to raise","chinese":"提高……的建議"},{"english":"raise the non-local student ceiling","chinese":"提高非本地學生上限"},{"english":"non-local student ceiling","chinese":"非本地學生上限"},{"english":"be supported in principle","chinese":"原則上應支持"},{"english":"in principle","chinese":"原則上"},{"english":"not as a race for numbers","chinese":"不應變成追逐數字的競賽"},{"english":"a race for numbers","chinese":"追逐數字的競賽"},{"english":"Hong Kong benefits when","chinese":"當……時，香港會受惠"},{"english":"attract bright students","chinese":"吸引優秀學生"},{"english":"bright students","chinese":"優秀學生"},{"english":"from the mainland, Asia and beyond","chinese":"來自內地、亞洲及其他地區"},{"english":"the mainland","chinese":"內地"},{"english":"Asia and beyond","chinese":"亞洲及其他地區"},{"english":"a more international campus","chinese":"更國際化的校園"},{"english":"sharpen ideas","chinese":"激發思維；磨礪想法"},{"english":"deepen cultural understanding","chinese":"加深文化理解"},{"english":"strengthen the city's role as","chinese":"加強城市作為……的角色"},{"english":"the city's role as","chinese":"城市作為……的角色"},{"english":"an education hub","chinese":"教育樞紐"},{"english":"the final arrangement","chinese":"最終安排"},{"english":"be built on","chinese":"建基於……"},{"english":"one firm principle","chinese":"一個堅定原則"},{"english":"local students","chinese":"本地學生"},{"english":"lose opportunities in practice","chinese":"實際上失去機會"},{"english":"in practice","chinese":"實際上"},{"english":"funded places","chinese":"資助學額"},{"english":"remain unchanged on paper","chinese":"紙面上維持不變"},{"english":"on paper","chinese":"紙面上"},{"english":"the main risk","chinese":"主要風險"},{"english":"university life","chinese":"大學生活"},{"english":"more than admission quotas","chinese":"不只是收生限額"},{"english":"admission quotas","chinese":"收生限額"},{"english":"hostel rooms","chinese":"宿位"},{"english":"laboratory space","chinese":"實驗室空間"},{"english":"tutorial attention","chinese":"導修支援；導修課上的關注"},{"english":"counselling services","chinese":"輔導服務"},{"english":"exchange places","chinese":"交流名額"},{"english":"internships","chinese":"實習機會"},{"english":"limited resources","chinese":"有限資源"},{"english":"enrollment grows faster than capacity","chinese":"收生增長快於承載能力"},{"english":"capacity","chinese":"承載能力"},{"english":"look like a golden bridge","chinese":"看似一座黃金橋樑"},{"english":"feel like a crowded corridor","chinese":"感覺像一條擠迫走廊"},{"english":"a golden bridge","chinese":"黃金橋樑"},{"english":"a crowded corridor","chinese":"擠迫走廊"},{"english":"face stronger competition for","chinese":"面對更激烈的……競爭"},{"english":"stronger competition","chinese":"更激烈的競爭"},{"english":"campus opportunities","chinese":"校園機會"},{"english":"receive weaker support","chinese":"得到較弱支援"},{"english":"after arrival","chinese":"抵港後；到埗後"},{"english":"require each university to","chinese":"要求每間大學……"},{"english":"conduct a capacity audit","chinese":"進行承載能力審核"},{"english":"a capacity audit","chinese":"承載能力審核"},{"english":"before further expansion is approved","chinese":"在進一步擴展獲批之前"},{"english":"further expansion","chinese":"進一步擴展"},{"english":"be approved","chinese":"獲得批准"},{"english":"non-local tuition income","chinese":"非本地學生學費收入"},{"english":"be partly ring-fenced for","chinese":"部分撥作指定用途"},{"english":"ring-fenced","chinese":"指定用途的；專款專用的"},{"english":"new hostel places","chinese":"新宿位"},{"english":"upgraded teaching facilities","chinese":"升級後的教學設施"},{"english":"teaching facilities","chinese":"教學設施"},{"english":"mental health services","chinese":"精神健康服務"},{"english":"language support","chinese":"語言支援"},{"english":"career guidance","chinese":"就業輔導；職涯指導"},{"english":"clear indicators","chinese":"清晰指標"},{"english":"hostel supply","chinese":"宿位供應"},{"english":"staff-student ratios","chinese":"師生比例"},{"english":"internship availability","chinese":"實習機會供應情況"},{"english":"be published annually","chinese":"每年公布"},{"english":"manage the change","chinese":"管理這項轉變"},{"english":"phased implementation","chinese":"分階段實施"},{"english":"rather than a sudden leap","chinese":"而不是突然大幅躍進"},{"english":"a sudden leap","chinese":"突然大幅躍進"},{"english":"set transparent rules for","chinese":"為……訂立透明規則"},{"english":"transparent rules","chinese":"透明規則"},{"english":"hostel allocation","chinese":"宿位分配"},{"english":"exchange nominations","chinese":"交流提名"},{"english":"scholarship distribution","chinese":"獎學金分配"},{"english":"fairness is seen as well as claimed","chinese":"不但聲稱公平，也要讓人看見公平"},{"english":"as well as claimed","chinese":"不只是口頭聲稱"},{"english":"work with employers","chinese":"與僱主合作"},{"english":"employers","chinese":"僱主"},{"english":"alumni","chinese":"校友"},{"english":"professional bodies","chinese":"專業團體"},{"english":"create more internships","chinese":"創造更多實習機會"},{"english":"mentoring schemes","chinese":"導師計劃"},{"english":"community projects","chinese":"社區項目"},{"english":"for both local and non-local students","chinese":"為本地及非本地學生"},{"english":"internationalisation","chinese":"國際化"},{"english":"a zero-sum game","chinese":"零和遊戲"},{"english":"with careful planning","chinese":"透過周詳規劃"},{"english":"honest communication","chinese":"坦誠溝通"},{"english":"measurable safeguards","chinese":"可量度的保障措施"},{"english":"open its doors wider","chinese":"進一步開放大門"},{"english":"squeeze someone out of","chinese":"把某人擠出……"},{"english":"without squeezing its own students out of the room","chinese":"在不擠走本地學生的情況下"},{"english":"its own students","chinese":"本地學生；自己的學生"},{"english":"student numbers","chinese":"學生人數"},{"english":"put pressure on","chinese":"對……造成壓力"},{"english":"campus resources","chinese":"校園資源"},{"english":"keep up with","chinese":"跟上……"},{"english":"student growth","chinese":"學生人數增長"},{"english":"adapt to university life","chinese":"適應大學生活"},{"english":"invest more in","chinese":"加大投放於……"},{"english":"be used as a measure of","chinese":"被用作衡量……的指標"},{"english":"allocated","chinese":"被分配"},{"english":"career opportunities","chinese":"就業機會；職業發展機會"},{"english":"benefit the whole university community","chinese":"令整個大學社群受惠"},{"english":"reduce misunderstanding","chinese":"減少誤解"},{"english":"attract talent from elsewhere","chinese":"從其他地方吸引人才"}]},"hkpf-civic-composition-5":{"exerciseId":"hkpf-civic-composition-5","essayKey":"","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=hkpf-civic-composition-5","flashDeckId":"government/hkpf/writing-composition/composition-5","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"Hong Kong is competing with Singapore, Dubai and other financial centres for global capital, family offices and investment talent. In this context, expanding tax concessions for asset and wealth managers is understandable. The proposal should be supported in principle, but not as a blank cheque for the wealthy. The final scheme must attract genuine economic activity while protecting revenue, fairness and public confidence.","chinese":"香港正與新加坡、杜拜及其他金融中心競爭，以吸引全球資本、家族辦公室及投資人才 在這個背景下，擴大資產及財富管理行業的稅務優惠，是可以理解的。 原則上，這項建議值得支持，但它不應成為給富裕人士的「空白支票」。最終方案必須吸引真正的經濟活動，同時保障公共收入、稅制公平及公眾信心"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"The strongest argument for the proposal is that it could deepen Hong Kong’s asset-management ecosystem. Funds bring more than money; they create legal, accounting, compliance and banking work, and they help anchor skilled professionals in the city. Clearer carried-interest relief may encourage managers to place real decision-making teams in Hong Kong instead of using the city as a convenient label. However, the benefit should be earned, not simply handed out. The Government should require economic substance, such as local staff, local investment committees, audited operations and a minimum amount of assets managed from Hong Kong. Paper companies should not receive golden treatment.","chinese":"支持這項建議最有力的理由是，它可以深化香港的資產管理生態系統。 基金帶來的不只是資金；它們還會創造法律、會計、合規及銀行相關工作，並有助於吸引專業人才留在香港。 更清晰的附帶權益稅務寬免，可能會鼓勵基金經理把真正的決策團隊設在香港，而不是只把香港當作一個方便使用的名義標籤。 然而，這種優惠應該是憑實質貢獻而獲得，而不是簡單派發。 政府應要求受惠者具備實質經濟活動，例如本地員工、本地投資委員會、經審計的營運紀錄，以及一定規模由香港管理的資產。 空殼公司不應享有黃金待遇。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"At the same time, fairness concerns cannot be brushed aside. A tax break for wealthy investors can look like a private lift for those already on the top floor, especially when ordinary residents face heavy living costs. Therefore, the Financial Services and the Treasury Bureau, the Inland Revenue Department and regulators should shape the scheme through consultation, clear eligibility rules, anti-abuse tests and annual reporting. There should also be a sunset review, so ineffective concessions can be revised or withdrawn. Part of the extra economic gain should support financial-talent training, financial-crime compliance and public services. With firm safeguards, Hong Kong can open the door to quality capital without selling the house.","chinese":"與此同時，公平方面的憂慮不應被輕輕帶過。 在普通市民面對沉重生活成本的情況下，為富裕投資者提供稅務優惠，很容易看起來像是為本來已在頂層的人提供私人升降機。 因此，財經事務及庫務局、稅務局及相關監管機構應透過諮詢、清晰的資格要求、防濫用審查及年度匯報來制定最終方案。 方案亦應設有日落檢討機制，以便修改或撤回成效不佳的優惠安排。 部分額外經濟收益應用於支持金融人才培訓、金融罪案合規工作及公共服務。 只要設有穩固的保障，香港便可以向優質資本打開大門，而不必犧牲自身根基"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"compete with","chinese":"與……競爭"},{"english":"financial centres","chinese":"金融中心"},{"english":"global capital","chinese":"全球資本"},{"english":"family offices","chinese":"家族辦公室"},{"english":"investment talent","chinese":"投資人才"},{"english":"in this context","chinese":"在這個背景下"},{"english":"tax concessions","chinese":"稅務優惠"},{"english":"asset and wealth managers","chinese":"資產及財富管理人"},{"english":"understandable","chinese":"可以理解的"},{"english":"be supported in principle","chinese":"原則上應予支持"},{"english":"in principle","chinese":"原則上"},{"english":"a blank cheque for","chinese":"給予……的空白支票；無限制好處"},{"english":"the wealthy","chinese":"富裕人士"},{"english":"the final scheme","chinese":"最終方案"},{"english":"attract genuine economic activity","chinese":"吸引真正經濟活動"},{"english":"genuine economic activity","chinese":"真正經濟活動"},{"english":"protect revenue","chinese":"保障收入"},{"english":"fairness","chinese":"公平"},{"english":"public confidence","chinese":"公眾信心"},{"english":"the strongest argument for","chinese":"支持……的最有力論點"},{"english":"deepen Hong Kong's asset-management ecosystem","chinese":"深化香港資產管理生態系統"},{"english":"asset-management ecosystem","chinese":"資產管理生態系統"},{"english":"funds bring more than money","chinese":"基金帶來的不只是資金"},{"english":"legal, accounting, compliance and banking work","chinese":"法律、會計、合規及銀行工作"},{"english":"compliance","chinese":"合規"},{"english":"anchor skilled professionals in","chinese":"吸引並留住熟練專業人士於……"},{"english":"skilled professionals","chinese":"熟練專業人士"},{"english":"clearer carried-interest relief","chinese":"更清晰的附帶權益稅務寬免"},{"english":"carried-interest relief","chinese":"附帶權益稅務寬免"},{"english":"place real decision-making teams in","chinese":"將真正決策團隊設於……"},{"english":"real decision-making teams","chinese":"真正決策團隊"},{"english":"instead of using the city as","chinese":"而不是將該城市用作……"},{"english":"a convenient label","chinese":"方便的標籤"},{"english":"the benefit should be earned","chinese":"好處應靠實質貢獻換取"},{"english":"not simply handed out","chinese":"不是簡單派發"},{"english":"simply handed out","chinese":"直接派發；隨便給予"},{"english":"require economic substance","chinese":"要求經濟實質"},{"english":"economic substance","chinese":"經濟實質"},{"english":"local staff","chinese":"本地員工"},{"english":"local investment committees","chinese":"本地投資委員會"},{"english":"audited operations","chinese":"經審計的營運"},{"english":"a minimum amount of assets managed from Hong Kong","chinese":"從香港管理的最低資產規模"},{"english":"assets managed from Hong Kong","chinese":"從香港管理的資產"},{"english":"paper companies","chinese":"空殼公司"},{"english":"receive golden treatment","chinese":"獲得優厚待遇"},{"english":"at the same time","chinese":"與此同時"},{"english":"fairness concerns","chinese":"公平方面的關注"},{"english":"cannot be brushed aside","chinese":"不能被輕輕帶過；不能被忽視"},{"english":"a tax break for","chinese":"給予……的稅務減免"},{"english":"wealthy investors","chinese":"富裕投資者"},{"english":"look like a private lift for","chinese":"看起來像給……的私人升降機"},{"english":"already on the top floor","chinese":"已經位於最上層"},{"english":"ordinary residents","chinese":"普通市民"},{"english":"face heavy living costs","chinese":"面對沉重生活成本"},{"english":"the Financial Services and the Treasury Bureau","chinese":"財經事務及庫務局"},{"english":"the Inland Revenue Department","chinese":"稅務局"},{"english":"regulators","chinese":"監管機構"},{"english":"shape the scheme through consultation","chinese":"透過諮詢制定方案"},{"english":"consultation","chinese":"諮詢"},{"english":"clear eligibility rules","chinese":"清晰資格準則"},{"english":"eligibility rules","chinese":"資格準則"},{"english":"anti-abuse tests","chinese":"防濫用測試"},{"english":"annual reporting","chinese":"年度匯報"},{"english":"a sunset review","chinese":"日落檢討；定期屆滿檢討"},{"english":"ineffective concessions","chinese":"無效的稅務優惠"},{"english":"be revised or withdrawn","chinese":"被修訂或撤回"},{"english":"withdrawn","chinese":"撤回"},{"english":"extra economic gain","chinese":"額外經濟收益"},{"english":"support financial-talent training","chinese":"支持金融人才培訓"},{"english":"financial-talent training","chinese":"金融人才培訓"},{"english":"financial-crime compliance","chinese":"金融罪行合規工作"},{"english":"public services","chinese":"公共服務"},{"english":"with firm safeguards","chinese":"在有堅實保障措施下"},{"english":"firm safeguards","chinese":"堅實保障措施"},{"english":"open the door to","chinese":"向……打開大門"},{"english":"quality capital","chinese":"優質資本"},{"english":"without selling the house","chinese":"不犧牲自身根基；不賤賣家當"},{"english":"short-term money","chinese":"短期資金"},{"english":"protect fairness and public confidence","chinese":"保障公平和公眾信心"}]},"hkpf-civic-composition-6":{"exerciseId":"hkpf-civic-composition-6","essayKey":"","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=hkpf-civic-composition-6","flashDeckId":"government/hkpf/writing-composition/composition-6","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"Encouraging primary school mergers is a reasonable response to Hong Kong’s shrinking student population, but the final scheme must be handled with care, transparency and compassion. With some schools unable to admit even 16 Primary One pupils, maintaining every campus unchanged may stretch public resources and weaken students’ learning environment. Still, a school is not just bricks and walls; it is a small community built on trust.","chinese":"鼓勵小學合併，是應對香港學齡人口下降的一個合理方向；然而，最終方案必須以謹慎、透明和具同理心的方式處理。 由於部分學校甚至未能取錄十六名小一學生，若所有校舍都維持不變，可能會令公共資源承受壓力，亦會削弱學生的學習環境。 然而，學校並不只是磚牆與校舍；它是一個建立在信任之上的小社群。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"One major concern is that a one-year grace period may be too short for schools to merge properly. Mergers involve far more than combining two nameplates. Principals must redesign classes, teachers may need redeployment, parents need reassurance, and young pupils require emotional support. Therefore, the Education Bureau should offer a three-year transition framework instead of a sudden countdown. Each merging school should submit a clear roadmap covering staffing, curriculum integration, student counselling, transport arrangements and parent communication. The Government should also provide targeted merger grants so that schools can upgrade facilities and support affected students. This would give schools breathing space rather than pushing them to jump before the ground is ready.","chinese":"一個主要憂慮是，一年的寬限期可能太短，未必足以讓學校妥善完成合併。 合併所涉及的，遠不只是把兩間學校的名字合在一起。 校長必須重新設計班級安排，教師可能需要重新調配，家長需要得到安心解釋，而年幼學生亦需要情緒支援。 因此，教育局應提供一個三年過渡框架，而不是只給學校一個突然開始倒數的期限。 每間準備合併的學校都應提交清晰路線圖，涵蓋人手安排、課程整合、學生輔導、交通安排及家長溝通。 政府亦應提供具針對性的合併津貼，讓學校能夠改善設施，並支援受影響的學生。 這樣做能給予學校喘息空間，而不是在基礎尚未準備好之前，迫使它們倉促跳下去。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"The final scheme should also be district-based and child-centred. Clear criteria should be published to explain when merger, closure or special support will apply, so that parents do not feel decisions are made behind a closed door. Extra help should be given to pupils with special educational needs, low-income families and children in remote districts, because distance can become a silent barrier. Unused campuses should be converted into special education centres, after-school care hubs or community learning spaces. With careful planning, Hong Kong can reduce empty classrooms without abandoning children, teachers or neighbourhood trust.","chinese":"最終方案亦應以地區為本，並以兒童福祉為中心。 政府應公布清晰準則，說明在甚麼情況下會推動合併、停辦或提供特別支援，讓家長不會覺得決定是在閉門之後作出的。 政府應為有特殊教育需要的學生、低收入家庭及偏遠地區兒童提供額外支援，因為距離往往會成為一種無聲的障礙。 空置校舍應改作特殊教育中心、課後照顧中心或社區學習空間。 只要規劃周詳，香港既可以減少空置課室，也不必放棄學生、教師或社區信任"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"encouraging primary school mergers","chinese":"鼓勵小學合併"},{"english":"primary school mergers","chinese":"小學合併"},{"english":"a reasonable response to","chinese":"對……的合理回應"},{"english":"Hong Kong's shrinking student population","chinese":"香港學生人口萎縮"},{"english":"shrinking student population","chinese":"學生人口萎縮"},{"english":"the final scheme","chinese":"最終方案"},{"english":"be handled with care","chinese":"需要謹慎處理"},{"english":"transparency and compassion","chinese":"透明度與同理心"},{"english":"unable to admit","chinese":"未能取錄"},{"english":"Primary One pupils","chinese":"小一學生"},{"english":"maintaining every campus unchanged","chinese":"維持每個校舍不變"},{"english":"stretch public resources","chinese":"令公共資源吃緊"},{"english":"public resources","chinese":"公共資源"},{"english":"weaken students' learning environment","chinese":"削弱學生的學習環境"},{"english":"learning environment","chinese":"學習環境"},{"english":"bricks and walls","chinese":"磚牆；硬件建築"},{"english":"a small community","chinese":"一個小社群"},{"english":"built on trust","chinese":"建基於信任"},{"english":"one major concern","chinese":"一個主要憂慮"},{"english":"a one-year grace period","chinese":"一年寬限期"},{"english":"merge properly","chinese":"妥善合併"},{"english":"involve far more than","chinese":"遠不止於……"},{"english":"combining two nameplates","chinese":"合併兩塊校名牌"},{"english":"redesign classes","chinese":"重新設計班級安排"},{"english":"need redeployment","chinese":"需要重新調配"},{"english":"redeployment","chinese":"重新調配；調職安排"},{"english":"need reassurance","chinese":"需要安心；需要得到安撫"},{"english":"require emotional support","chinese":"需要情緒支援"},{"english":"emotional support","chinese":"情緒支援"},{"english":"the Education Bureau","chinese":"教育局"},{"english":"offer a three-year transition framework","chinese":"提供三年過渡框架"},{"english":"a three-year transition framework","chinese":"三年過渡框架"},{"english":"instead of a sudden countdown","chinese":"而不是突然倒數"},{"english":"a sudden countdown","chinese":"突然倒數；突然限期"},{"english":"each merging school","chinese":"每間合併中的學校"},{"english":"submit a clear roadmap","chinese":"提交清晰路線圖"},{"english":"a clear roadmap","chinese":"清晰路線圖"},{"english":"staffing","chinese":"人手安排"},{"english":"curriculum integration","chinese":"課程整合"},{"english":"student counselling","chinese":"學生輔導"},{"english":"transport arrangements","chinese":"交通安排"},{"english":"parent communication","chinese":"家長溝通"},{"english":"provide targeted merger grants","chinese":"提供具針對性的合併資助"},{"english":"targeted merger grants","chinese":"具針對性的合併資助"},{"english":"upgrade facilities","chinese":"改善設施；提升設施"},{"english":"support affected students","chinese":"支援受影響學生"},{"english":"affected students","chinese":"受影響學生"},{"english":"give schools breathing space","chinese":"給學校喘息空間"},{"english":"breathing space","chinese":"喘息空間"},{"english":"push someone to jump before the ground is ready","chinese":"在準備不足時迫使某人倉促行動"},{"english":"the ground is ready","chinese":"條件成熟"},{"english":"district-based","chinese":"以地區為本"},{"english":"child-centred","chinese":"以兒童為本"},{"english":"clear criteria","chinese":"清晰準則"},{"english":"be published","chinese":"被公布"},{"english":"merger, closure or special support","chinese":"合併、停辦或特別支援"},{"english":"special support","chinese":"特別支援"},{"english":"will apply","chinese":"適用"},{"english":"behind a closed door","chinese":"閉門作決定；暗中決定"},{"english":"extra help","chinese":"額外幫助"},{"english":"pupils with special educational needs","chinese":"有特殊教育需要的學生"},{"english":"special educational needs","chinese":"特殊教育需要"},{"english":"low-income families","chinese":"低收入家庭"},{"english":"remote districts","chinese":"偏遠地區"},{"english":"distance can become a silent barrier","chinese":"距離可以成為無聲障礙"},{"english":"a silent barrier","chinese":"無聲障礙；隱形障礙"},{"english":"unused campuses","chinese":"空置校舍"},{"english":"be converted into","chinese":"被改建成"},{"english":"special education centres","chinese":"特殊教育中心"},{"english":"after-school care hubs","chinese":"課後照顧中心"},{"english":"community learning spaces","chinese":"社區學習空間"},{"english":"with careful planning","chinese":"透過周詳規劃"},{"english":"reduce empty classrooms","chinese":"減少空置課室"},{"english":"without abandoning","chinese":"而不放棄……"},{"english":"neighbourhood trust","chinese":"社區信任"}]},"hkpf-civic-composition-7":{"exerciseId":"hkpf-civic-composition-7","essayKey":"","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=hkpf-civic-composition-7","flashDeckId":"","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"Hong Kong’s taxi trade has long been a vital part of public transport, but its payment practice has not always kept pace with a cashless city and a tourism-driven economy. The new requirement for taxi drivers to provide at least two electronic payment methods is therefore a reasonable step towards modernisation. It can make journeys smoother for tourists, office workers and younger passengers, while still preserving cash as a safety net. However, e-payment should be treated as a bridge to better service, not a magic wand.","chinese":"香港的的士行業一直是公共交通的重要一環，但其付款方式並不總是能夠跟上無現金城市和旅遊經濟的步伐。 因此，要求的士司機提供最少兩種電子支付方式，是邁向現代化的合理一步。 這可以令遊客、上班族和年輕乘客的乘車過程更加順暢，同時仍然保留現金作為安全網。然而，電子支付應被視為改善服務的橋樑，而不是一支能解決所有問題的魔法棒。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"The main benefit is convenience. When passengers can pay by QR code or card, they avoid the small but familiar frustration of having no cash, no change or no suitable banknotes. This is especially important for visitors, who may see taxis as the city’s moving front door. If the first ride feels slow, awkward or outdated, Hong Kong’s image suffers. To implement the policy effectively, the Government, payment operators and taxi associations should provide hands-on training, simple operating manuals, a driver hotline and short video demonstrations. Older drivers should not be left to wrestle with new machines like swimmers thrown into deep water.","chinese":"主要好處是便利。 當乘客可以透過二維碼或卡付款時，他們便可以避免沒有現金、沒有零錢或沒有合適紙幣這種雖小卻常見的煩惱。 這對旅客尤其重要，因為他們可能會把的士視為這座城市「流動的門面」。 如果他們第一次乘車時感到緩慢、尷尬或落後，香港的形象便會受損。 為了有效推行這項政策，政府、支付平台營辦商和的士業界組織應提供實務培訓、簡明操作手冊、司機支援熱線和簡短教學影片。 年長司機不應被迫獨自應付新設備，就像被扔進深水中的泳客一樣手足無措"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"At the same time, the policy must be practical and enforceable. Payment devices can fail, signals can be weak, and some drivers may fear transaction fees or technical disputes. Therefore, the Government should offer time-limited subsidies for approved devices, require clear stickers showing accepted payment methods, and set a grace period before strict penalties begin. Transport officers should focus first on education and repeated non-compliance, rather than heavy-handed punishment. More importantly, e-payment alone will not rescue poor service. Fare transparency, polite conduct, clean vehicles and an efficient complaint channel must develop hand in hand. With training, fair enforcement and wider service standards, this reform can modernise taxis without leaving drivers behind.","chinese":"同時，這項政策必須具備實際可行性和執法可操作性。 付款設備可能會故障，網絡訊號可能較弱，而部分司機亦可能擔心交易費用或技術爭議。 因此，政府應為認可設備提供有時限的資助，要求車廂內張貼清晰標示以顯示可接受的付款方式，並在嚴格罰則實施前設立寬限期。 運輸部門人員應先著重教育和處理屢次違規個案，而不是一開始便採取高壓式懲罰。 更重要的是，單靠電子支付並不能拯救差劣服務。 收費透明度、禮貌態度、車廂整潔和高效投訴渠道必須同步發展。 只要有培訓、公平執法和更全面的服務標準，這項改革便能令的士服務現代化，同時不會把司機拋在後面。"}],"vocabulary":[]},"model-essay-1-ielts-task1-bar-charts":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-1-ielts-task1-bar-charts","essayKey":"bar-charts:1","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-1-ielts-task1-bar-charts","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-1/bar-charts/bar-chart-1","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"The bar chart compares the number of US households, measured in millions, across five annual income bands in 2007, 2011 and 2015.","chinese":"這張柱狀圖比較了 2007 年、 2011 年和 2015 年美國家庭在五個年收入組別中的數量，單位為百萬戶。"},{"label":"Overview","english":"Overall, the distribution was dominated by households earning below $50,000 and by those earning $100,000 or more, while the two middle-income groups were consistently smaller. The highest-income category became clearly the largest by 2015, whereas the $75,000–$99,999 group remained the least common throughout.","chinese":"整體而言，年收入低於 50,000 美元的家庭以及年收入 100,000 美元或以上的家庭佔比較大，而兩個中等收入組別的家庭數量一直較少。 到 2015 年，最高收入組別明顯成為最大的類別；相反， 75,000 至 99,999 美元收入組在整段期間都是最少見的組別。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"In 2007, about 25 million households earned under $25,000, compared with roughly 27 million in the $25,000–$49,999 bracket. Both groups increased by 2011, reaching just under 29 million and around 30 million, respectively. By 2015, they had edged down slightly, to approximately 28 million and 29 million, although they were still among the largest categories.","chinese":"在 2007 年，約有 2,500 萬戶家庭年收入低於 25,000 美元，而 25,000 至 49,999 美元收入組則約有 2,700 萬戶。 到 2011 年，這兩個組別均有所上升，分別達到接近 2,900 萬戶和約 3,000 萬戶。 到 2015 年，兩者都輕微回落，分別降至約 2,800 萬戶和 2,900 萬戶，但它們仍然屬於最大的組別之一。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"The remaining three bands showed less uniform movement. The number of households earning $50,000–$74,999 stayed almost unchanged at about 21 million in all three years. Those in the $75,000–$99,999 range were consistently the smallest group, at around 14–15 million. By contrast, households with incomes of at least $100,000 dipped from about 29 million to 28 million in 2011, before rising sharply to approximately 33 million in 2015.","chinese":"其餘三個收入組別的變化則沒有那麼一致。 年收入 50,000 至 74,999 美元的家庭數量在三個年份中幾乎沒有變化，均約為2,100 萬戶。 年收入 75,000 至 99,999 美元的家庭一直是最小的組別，數量約為 1,400 萬至1,500 萬戶。 相比之下，年收入至少 100,000 美元的家庭數量先從約 2,900 萬戶下降至 2011年的 2,800 萬戶，之後在 2015 年大幅上升至約 3,300 萬戶。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"the bar chart compares","chinese":"柱形圖比較"},{"english":"the number of US households","chinese":"美國住戶數目"},{"english":"measured in millions","chinese":"以百萬計"},{"english":"across five annual income bands","chinese":"涵蓋五個全年收入組別"},{"english":"annual income bands","chinese":"全年收入組別"},{"english":"Overall","chinese":"整體而言"},{"english":"the distribution was dominated by","chinese":"分佈主要由……佔主導"},{"english":"households earning below $50,000","chinese":"年收入低於50,000美元的住戶"},{"english":"earning $100,000 or more","chinese":"年收入達100,000美元或以上"},{"english":"middle-income groups","chinese":"中等收入組別"},{"english":"were consistently smaller","chinese":"一直較少"},{"english":"the highest-income category","chinese":"最高收入類別"},{"english":"became clearly the largest","chinese":"明顯成為最大類別"},{"english":"by 2015","chinese":"到2015年"},{"english":"the $75,000–$99,999 group","chinese":"75,000至99,999美元組別"},{"english":"remained the least common throughout","chinese":"全期一直最少見"},{"english":"In 2007","chinese":"在2007年"},{"english":"about 25 million households","chinese":"約2,500萬戶"},{"english":"earned under $25,000","chinese":"年收入低於25,000美元"},{"english":"compared with","chinese":"與……相比"},{"english":"roughly 27 million","chinese":"約2,700萬"},{"english":"the $25,000–$49,999 bracket","chinese":"25,000至49,999美元組別"},{"english":"both groups increased","chinese":"兩個組別均有所增加"},{"english":"by 2011","chinese":"到2011年"},{"english":"reaching just under 29 million","chinese":"達到略低於2,900萬"},{"english":"around 30 million","chinese":"約3,000萬"},{"english":"respectively","chinese":"分別"},{"english":"edged down slightly","chinese":"輕微下降"},{"english":"to approximately 28 million","chinese":"至約2,800萬"},{"english":"although","chinese":"雖然；儘管"},{"english":"still among the largest categories","chinese":"仍屬最大類別之一"},{"english":"the remaining three bands","chinese":"其餘三個組別"},{"english":"showed less uniform movement","chinese":"走勢較不一致"},{"english":"households earning $50,000–$74,999","chinese":"年收入50,000至74,999美元的住戶"},{"english":"stayed almost unchanged","chinese":"幾乎維持不變"},{"english":"at about 21 million","chinese":"約2,100萬"},{"english":"in all three years","chinese":"在三個年份中"},{"english":"those in the $75,000–$99,999 range","chinese":"75,000至99,999美元範圍內的住戶"},{"english":"consistently the smallest group","chinese":"一直是最小組別"},{"english":"at around 14–15 million","chinese":"約1,400萬至1,500萬"},{"english":"By contrast","chinese":"相比之下"},{"english":"households with incomes of at least $100,000","chinese":"收入最少100,000美元的住戶"},{"english":"dipped from about 29 million to 28 million","chinese":"由約2,900萬跌至2,800萬"},{"english":"before rising sharply to","chinese":"隨後急升至"},{"english":"approximately 33 million","chinese":"約3,300萬"}]},"model-essay-1-ielts-task1-line-graph":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-1-ielts-task1-line-graph","essayKey":"line-graph:1","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-1-ielts-task1-line-graph","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-1/line-graphs/line-graph-1","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"The line graph illustrates the number of participants in five activities at a social centre in Melbourne, Australia, from 2000 to 2020.","chinese":"這張折線圖說明了澳洲墨爾本一所社交中心在 2000 年至 2020 年間五項活動的參加人數。"},{"label":"Overview","english":"Overall, the film club remained the leading activity throughout, despite minor fluctuations. Table tennis recorded by far the most dramatic growth and became second by 2020, whereas amateur dramatics declined after a brief rise and finished as the least popular option.","chinese":"整體而言，電影俱樂部雖然有輕微波動，但在整個期間一直是參加人數最多的活動。 乒乓球的增長幅度明顯最大，並在 2020 年成為第二受歡迎的活動；相反，業餘戲劇在短暫上升後下跌，最後成為最不受歡迎的選項。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"In 2000, around 65 people attended the film club, compared with 36 for martial arts and 26 for amateur dramatics. The film club then dipped slightly to 60 in 2010 before recovering to about 66 at the end of the period. Martial arts showed no clear long-term change: after falling to 32 in 2005, it rose to 38 in 2010 and ended close to its starting point, at roughly 36.","chinese":"在 2000 年，約有 65 人參加電影俱樂部，相比之下，武術約有 36 人，而業餘戲劇約有 26 人。 之後，電影俱樂部的人數在 2010 年小幅下降至 60 人，然後在期末回升至約 66人。 武術沒有明顯的長期變化：它在 2005 年跌至 32 人後，於 2010 年升至 38 人，最後以約 36 人結束，接近起點水平。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"The remaining activities changed more noticeably. Table tennis increased only modestly from 16 to 20 participants between 2000 and 2010, but then climbed sharply to 35 in 2015 and approximately 54 in 2020. Musical performances, which had no participants in the first two years shown, rose gradually to 18. By contrast, amateur dramatics fell from a peak of 28 in 2005 to just 6 by 2020.","chinese":"其餘活動的變化則更加明顯。 乒乓球在 2000 年至 2010 年間只從 16 人小幅增加至 20 人，但之後迅速上升，在2015 年達到 35 人，並在 2020 年達到約 54 人。 音樂表演在圖中最初兩個年份沒有參加者，但之後逐漸上升至 18 人。 相比之下，業餘戲劇從 2005 年的峰值 28 人下降至 2020 年的僅 6 人。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"The line graph illustrates","chinese":"折線圖顯示"},{"english":"the number of participants","chinese":"參加者人數"},{"english":"participants in five activities","chinese":"五項活動的參加者"},{"english":"at a social centre","chinese":"在一間社交中心"},{"english":"from 2000 to 2020","chinese":"從2000年至2020年"},{"english":"Overall","chinese":"整體而言"},{"english":"the film club","chinese":"電影俱樂部"},{"english":"remained the leading activity","chinese":"仍然是最受歡迎的活動"},{"english":"throughout","chinese":"整個期間"},{"english":"despite minor fluctuations","chinese":"儘管有輕微波動"},{"english":"minor fluctuations","chinese":"輕微波動"},{"english":"table tennis","chinese":"乒乓球"},{"english":"recorded by far the most dramatic growth","chinese":"錄得遠遠最顯著的增長"},{"english":"the most dramatic growth","chinese":"最顯著的增長"},{"english":"became second by 2020","chinese":"到2020年成為第二位"},{"english":"whereas","chinese":"而；然而"},{"english":"amateur dramatics","chinese":"業餘戲劇"},{"english":"declined after a brief rise","chinese":"在短暫上升後下降"},{"english":"a brief rise","chinese":"短暫上升"},{"english":"finished as the least popular option","chinese":"最後成為最不受歡迎的選項"},{"english":"the least popular option","chinese":"最不受歡迎的選項"},{"english":"around 65 people attended","chinese":"約65人參加"},{"english":"attended the film club","chinese":"參加電影俱樂部"},{"english":"compared with","chinese":"與……相比"},{"english":"martial arts","chinese":"武術"},{"english":"amateur dramatics","chinese":"業餘戲劇"},{"english":"dipped slightly to 60","chinese":"輕微下降至60"},{"english":"before recovering to","chinese":"隨後回升至"},{"english":"recovering to about 66","chinese":"回升至約66"},{"english":"at the end of the period","chinese":"在期末"},{"english":"showed no clear long-term change","chinese":"沒有明顯長期變化"},{"english":"long-term change","chinese":"長期變化"},{"english":"after falling to 32","chinese":"在跌至32後"},{"english":"rose to 38","chinese":"上升至38"},{"english":"ended close to its starting point","chinese":"最終接近起點水平"},{"english":"its starting point","chinese":"其起點水平"},{"english":"at roughly 36","chinese":"約為36"},{"english":"the remaining activities","chinese":"其餘活動"},{"english":"changed more noticeably","chinese":"變化更明顯"},{"english":"increased only modestly","chinese":"只輕微增加"},{"english":"from 16 to 20 participants","chinese":"由16名增至20名參加者"},{"english":"between 2000 and 2010","chinese":"在2000年至2010年間"},{"english":"climbed sharply to 35","chinese":"急升至35"},{"english":"approximately 54","chinese":"約54"},{"english":"musical performances","chinese":"音樂表演"},{"english":"had no participants","chinese":"沒有參加者"},{"english":"the first two years shown","chinese":"圖中顯示的首兩年"},{"english":"rose gradually to 18","chinese":"逐步上升至18"},{"english":"By contrast","chinese":"相比之下"},{"english":"fell from a peak of 28","chinese":"從28的高峰下跌"},{"english":"a peak of 28","chinese":"28的高峰"},{"english":"to just 6 by 2020","chinese":"到2020年跌至僅6"}]},"model-essay-1-ielts-task1-maps":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-1-ielts-task1-maps","essayKey":"maps:1","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-1-ielts-task1-maps","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-1/maps/maps-1","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"The two plans illustrate the layout of Beechwood Farm in 1950 and the arrangement of the same site today.","chinese":"這兩張平面圖展示了比奇伍德農場在 1950 年的佈局，以及同一地點現今的安排。"},{"label":"Overview","english":"Overall, the farm has been transformed from a mainly agricultural site into a more diversified complex. The river, main road, farmhouse, chicken enclosure and three crop areas have been retained, whereas the sheep field and basic tracks have given way to roads, visitor facilities and solar panels.","chinese":"整體而言，該農場已由一個主要用於農業的地點，轉變成一個功能更多元化的綜合場地。 河流、主要道路、農舍、雞舍和三個種植區都被保留下來；相反，原本的羊群牧場和簡單小徑則已被道路、遊客設施和太陽能板取代。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"In 1950, the western half was used for crops: fruit trees lay in the northwest, with soft fruits and vegetables in adjacent plots to the south. A large sheep field occupied most of the north-eastern area. Access was provided only by tracks, one running from the main road towards the barn and another leading to the farmhouse. The farmhouse stood in the southeast, just above the chickens and inside the bend of the river.","chinese":"在 1950 年，西半部主要用作種植農作物：果樹位於西北部，而漿果類作物和蔬菜則分別位於其南面的相鄰地塊。 一大片羊群牧場佔據了東北部的大部分地方。 當時的通道只由小徑提供，其中一條由主要道路通往穀倉，另一條則通向農舍。 農舍位於東南部，正好在雞舍上方，並坐落於河流彎曲處的內側。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"Today, the crop plots remain in similar positions, but a farm shop and car park have been added near the entrance. The former sheep pasture is now divided between a camping field and a solar-panel area, with another car park nearby. In the east, holiday cottages have been built above the farmhouse, while the barn has been moved south-west.","chinese":"現今，農作物地塊仍大致保留在相似的位置，但入口附近新增了一間農場商店和一個停車場。 昔日的羊群牧場現在被分成露營地和太陽能板區，附近還設有另一個停車場。 在東部，度假小屋已建於農舍上方，而穀倉則被移至西南方向。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"the plans below","chinese":"以下平面圖"},{"english":"the site of a farm","chinese":"一個農場的所在地"},{"english":"the same site today","chinese":"現今同一地點"},{"english":"summarise the information","chinese":"概述資料"},{"english":"by selecting and reporting","chinese":"透過選取並報告……"},{"english":"the main features","chinese":"主要特徵"},{"english":"make comparisons where relevant","chinese":"在相關之處作出比較"},{"english":"illustrate the layout of","chinese":"展示……的佈局"},{"english":"the arrangement of","chinese":"……的安排；佈局"},{"english":"has been transformed from","chinese":"已由……轉變"},{"english":"a mainly agricultural site","chinese":"以農業為主的場地"},{"english":"a more diversified complex","chinese":"更多元化的綜合場地"},{"english":"have been retained","chinese":"得以保留"},{"english":"chicken enclosure","chinese":"雞隻圍欄區"},{"english":"crop areas","chinese":"作物種植區"},{"english":"whereas","chinese":"而；相反"},{"english":"have given way to","chinese":"已讓位予……；被……取代"},{"english":"basic tracks","chinese":"簡單小路；基本路徑"},{"english":"visitor facilities","chinese":"遊客設施"},{"english":"solar panels","chinese":"太陽能板"},{"english":"the western half","chinese":"西半部"},{"english":"was used for crops","chinese":"被用作種植作物"},{"english":"fruit trees","chinese":"果樹"},{"english":"lay in the north-west","chinese":"位於西北面"},{"english":"soft fruits","chinese":"軟果類水果"},{"english":"adjacent plots","chinese":"相鄰地塊"},{"english":"to the south","chinese":"在南面"},{"english":"a large sheep field","chinese":"大型羊群牧場"},{"english":"occupied most of","chinese":"佔據……的大部分"},{"english":"the north-eastern area","chinese":"東北部地區"},{"english":"access was provided by","chinese":"通道由……提供"},{"english":"running from…towards…","chinese":"由……伸延至……"},{"english":"the main road","chinese":"主要道路"},{"english":"leading to","chinese":"通往……"},{"english":"the farmhouse","chinese":"農舍"},{"english":"stood in the south-east","chinese":"位於東南面"},{"english":"just above","chinese":"就在……上方"},{"english":"inside the bend of the river","chinese":"位於河道彎位之內"},{"english":"crop plots","chinese":"作物地塊"},{"english":"remain in similar positions","chinese":"保持在相若位置"},{"english":"have been added near","chinese":"已在……附近增設"},{"english":"near the entrance","chinese":"在入口附近"},{"english":"farm shop","chinese":"農場商店"},{"english":"car park","chinese":"停車場"},{"english":"the former sheep pasture","chinese":"昔日的牧羊草地"},{"english":"is now divided between","chinese":"現時分為……"},{"english":"camping field","chinese":"露營場地"},{"english":"solar-panel area","chinese":"太陽能板區"},{"english":"with another car park nearby","chinese":"附近另有一個停車場"},{"english":"in the east","chinese":"在東面"},{"english":"holiday cottages","chinese":"度假小屋"},{"english":"have been built above","chinese":"已建於……上方"},{"english":"the barn","chinese":"穀倉"},{"english":"has been moved south-west","chinese":"已遷往西南面"},{"english":"a more developed road system","chinese":"更完善的道路系統"},{"english":"replaced by","chinese":"被……取代"},{"english":"tourist and energy-related facilities","chinese":"旅遊及能源相關設施"}]},"model-essay-1-ielts-task1-mixed-charts":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-1-ielts-task1-mixed-charts","essayKey":"mixed-charts:1","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-1-ielts-task1-mixed-charts","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-1/mixed-charts/mixed-charts-1","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"The graphics summarise Little Chalfont Library’s age profile, loan categories in 2016, and annual loan totals from 2007 to 2016.","chinese":"這些圖表概述了 Little Chalfont Library 的會員年齡分布、2016年的借閱類別，以及2007年至2016年間每年的總借閱量。"},{"label":"Overview","english":"Overall, adults aged 18–64 made up the majority of members, while fiction was by far the dominant type of borrowing. Total lending rose across the period, despite a brief dip around 2013.","chinese":"整體而言，18至64歲的成年人佔會員的大多數，而小說明顯是最主要的借閱類型。 儘管在2013年前後曾短暫下降，整體借閱量在整段期間仍然上升。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"In 2016, adults aged 18–64 accounted for 51% of members, more than twice the share of children, at 22%. Young adults and people aged 65 or over were smaller groups, at 15% and 12% respectively. Loans were concentrated in two categories: children’s fiction and adult fiction each represented 38%, together making up just over three quarters of all borrowing. Adult non-fiction was next, at 13%, whereas children’s non-fiction accounted for only 6%. Young adults and adult audio books stood at 2% each, and children’s DVDs were negligible, at 1%.","chinese":"在2016年，18至64歲的成年人佔會員的51%，是兒童比例22%的兩倍多。 青年成人和65歲或以上人士則是較小的群體，分別佔15%和12%。 借閱主要集中在兩個類別：兒童小說和成人小說各佔38%，兩者合計佔全部借閱量的四分之三多一點。 成人非小說類排在其後，佔13%；相比之下，兒童非小說類只佔6%。 青年成人類和成人有聲書各佔2%，而兒童 DVDs 幾乎可以忽略，只佔1%。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"Annual loans increased from just under 16,000 in 2007 to about 19,000 in 2008 and 2009. The figure then stayed mostly above 20,000 until 2012, fell slightly below this level in 2013, and recovered steadily to a peak of roughly 21,500 in 2016.","chinese":"每年借閱量由2007年的略低於16,000次，上升至2008年和2009年的約19,000次。 此後，該數字到2012年大多維持在20,000次以上，2013年略跌至此水平以下，然後穩步回升，並在2016年達到約21,500次的高峰。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"give information about","chinese":"提供關於……的資料"},{"english":"a public library","chinese":"公共圖書館"},{"english":"a town called","chinese":"一個名為……的小鎮"},{"english":"Little Chalfont","chinese":"Little Chalfont"},{"english":"summarise the information","chinese":"概述資料"},{"english":"selecting and reporting","chinese":"選取並報告"},{"english":"the main features","chinese":"主要特徵"},{"english":"make comparisons where relevant","chinese":"在相關之處作出比較"},{"english":"the charts summarise","chinese":"圖表概述"},{"english":"age profile","chinese":"年齡分佈"},{"english":"loan categories","chinese":"借閱類別"},{"english":"annual loan totals","chinese":"每年借出總數"},{"english":"from 2007 to 2016","chinese":"由2007年至2016年"},{"english":"Overall","chinese":"整體而言"},{"english":"adults aged 18–64","chinese":"18至64歲的成年人"},{"english":"made up the majority of","chinese":"佔……的大多數"},{"english":"library members","chinese":"圖書館會員"},{"english":"while","chinese":"而"},{"english":"fiction","chinese":"小說"},{"english":"by far the dominant type of","chinese":"遠遠是最主要的……類型"},{"english":"type of borrowing","chinese":"借閱類型"},{"english":"total lending","chinese":"總借出量"},{"english":"rose across the period","chinese":"在整個時期內上升"},{"english":"despite a brief dip","chinese":"儘管短暫下跌"},{"english":"a brief dip around","chinese":"在……左右短暫下跌"},{"english":"In 2016","chinese":"在2016年"},{"english":"accounted for 51% of","chinese":"佔……的51%"},{"english":"more than twice the share of","chinese":"超過……比例的兩倍"},{"english":"the share of children","chinese":"兒童所佔比例"},{"english":"at 22%","chinese":"為22%"},{"english":"young adults","chinese":"青年成年人"},{"english":"people aged 65 or over","chinese":"65歲或以上人士"},{"english":"smaller groups","chinese":"較小的群組"},{"english":"respectively","chinese":"分別"},{"english":"were concentrated in","chinese":"集中於"},{"english":"children's fiction","chinese":"兒童小說"},{"english":"adult fiction","chinese":"成人小說"},{"english":"each represented 38%","chinese":"各佔38%"},{"english":"represented","chinese":"佔"},{"english":"together making up","chinese":"合共佔"},{"english":"just over three quarters of","chinese":"略高於四分之三"},{"english":"all borrowing","chinese":"所有借閱量"},{"english":"adult non-fiction","chinese":"成人非小說類書籍"},{"english":"was next","chinese":"其次是"},{"english":"whereas","chinese":"而；相比之下"},{"english":"children's non-fiction","chinese":"兒童非小說類書籍"},{"english":"accounted for only","chinese":"僅佔"},{"english":"young adult books","chinese":"青年讀物"},{"english":"adult audio books","chinese":"成人有聲書"},{"english":"stood at 2% each","chinese":"各為2%"},{"english":"children's DVDs","chinese":"兒童DVD"},{"english":"were negligible","chinese":"微不足道"},{"english":"at 1%","chinese":"為1%"},{"english":"annual loans","chinese":"每年借出量"},{"english":"increased from … to …","chinese":"由……增加至……"},{"english":"just under 16,000","chinese":"略低於16,000"},{"english":"about 19,000","chinese":"約19,000"},{"english":"the figure then","chinese":"其後該數字"},{"english":"stayed mostly above","chinese":"大多保持在……以上"},{"english":"above 20,000","chinese":"高於20,000"},{"english":"until 2012","chinese":"直到2012年"},{"english":"fell slightly below","chinese":"略跌至……以下"},{"english":"this level","chinese":"這一水平"},{"english":"recovered steadily","chinese":"穩步回升"},{"english":"to a peak of","chinese":"達到……的高峰"},{"english":"roughly 21,500","chinese":"約21,500"}]},"model-essay-1-ielts-task1-pie-charts":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-1-ielts-task1-pie-charts","essayKey":"pie-charts:1","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-1-ielts-task1-pie-charts","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-1/pie-charts/pie-chart-1","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"The three pie charts compare the average shares of sodium, saturated fat and added sugar consumed at breakfast, lunch, dinner and snack times in the USA.","chinese":"這三個圓餅圖比較了美國人在早餐、午餐、晚餐和零食時間中攝入的鈉、飽和脂肪和添加糖的平均比例。"},{"label":"Overview","english":"Overall, dinner is the main contributor to sodium and saturated fat intake, whereas snacks account for the greatest proportion of added sugar. Breakfast consistently makes the smallest, or joint-smallest, contribution, while lunch occupies an intermediate position across all three nutrients.","chinese":"整體而言，晚餐是鈉和飽和脂肪攝入的主要來源，而零食則佔添加糖的最大比例。 早餐在各項中一直佔最小或並列最小比例，而午餐在三種營養素中大致處於中間位置。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"Breakfast is comparatively light in all categories, representing 14% of sodium and 16% of both saturated fat and added sugar. Lunch contributes noticeably more sodium and saturated fat, at 29% and 26% respectively, but its share of added sugar is lower, at 19%. Thus, these two earlier meals are generally less dominant than the later ones, although lunch is still a substantial source of sodium.","chinese":"早餐在所有類別中所佔比例都相對較低，分別佔鈉的 14% ，以及飽和脂肪和添加糖的 16% 。 午餐所佔的鈉和飽和脂肪比例明顯較高，分別為 29% 和 26% ，但其添加糖比例較低，為 19% 。 因此，這兩個較早的餐次整體上不及較晚的餐次突出，不過午餐仍然是鈉的一個重要來源。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"Dinner is the most sodium-heavy meal, with its share reaching 43%, and it also leads saturated fat consumption at 37%. Its contribution to added sugar, however, is much lower, at 23%. Snacks show the reverse pattern: they account for only 14% of sodium and 21% of saturated fat, but dominate added sugar at 42%, almost double the dinner figure.","chinese":"晚餐是含鈉比例最高的一餐，佔 43% ，同時也以 37% 成為飽和脂肪比例最高的一餐。 然而，它在添加糖方面的比例低得多，只有 23% 。 零食則呈現相反模式：它們只佔鈉的 14% 和飽和脂肪的 21% ，但在添加糖方面佔主導地位，達到 42% ，幾乎是晚餐比例的兩倍。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"the three pie charts compare","chinese":"三個圓形圖比較"},{"english":"the average shares of","chinese":"平均所佔比例"},{"english":"sodium","chinese":"鈉"},{"english":"saturated fat","chinese":"飽和脂肪"},{"english":"added sugar","chinese":"添加糖"},{"english":"consumed at breakfast","chinese":"在早餐時攝取"},{"english":"snack times","chinese":"小食時間"},{"english":"in the USA","chinese":"在美國"},{"english":"Overall","chinese":"整體而言"},{"english":"the main contributor to","chinese":"……的主要來源"},{"english":"sodium and saturated fat intake","chinese":"鈉和飽和脂肪攝取量"},{"english":"whereas","chinese":"然而；而"},{"english":"account for the greatest proportion of","chinese":"佔……的最大比例"},{"english":"the greatest proportion of added sugar","chinese":"添加糖的最大比例"},{"english":"consistently makes the smallest contribution","chinese":"一直作出最小貢獻"},{"english":"joint-smallest contribution","chinese":"並列最小貢獻"},{"english":"while","chinese":"而；同時"},{"english":"occupies an intermediate position","chinese":"處於中間位置"},{"english":"across all three nutrients","chinese":"在三種營養成分中"},{"english":"comparatively light","chinese":"相對較少"},{"english":"in all categories","chinese":"在所有類別中"},{"english":"representing 14% of sodium","chinese":"佔鈉攝取量的14%"},{"english":"16% of both saturated fat and added sugar","chinese":"飽和脂肪和添加糖均佔16%"},{"english":"contributes noticeably more","chinese":"貢獻明顯較多"},{"english":"at 29% and 26% respectively","chinese":"分別為29%和26%"},{"english":"respectively","chinese":"分別"},{"english":"its share of added sugar","chinese":"其添加糖所佔比例"},{"english":"is lower, at 19%","chinese":"較低，為19%"},{"english":"Thus","chinese":"因此"},{"english":"these two earlier meals","chinese":"這兩個較早進食的餐次"},{"english":"generally less dominant than","chinese":"一般不及……佔主導"},{"english":"the later ones","chinese":"較後的餐次"},{"english":"although","chinese":"雖然；儘管"},{"english":"a substantial source of sodium","chinese":"鈉的重要來源"},{"english":"Dinner is the most sodium-heavy meal","chinese":"晚餐是含鈉比例最高的一餐"},{"english":"sodium-heavy meal","chinese":"含鈉比例高的一餐"},{"english":"with its share reaching 43%","chinese":"其比例達43%"},{"english":"leads saturated fat consumption","chinese":"在飽和脂肪攝取方面居首"},{"english":"at 37%","chinese":"為37%"},{"english":"its contribution to added sugar","chinese":"其對添加糖的貢獻"},{"english":"much lower","chinese":"低得多"},{"english":"show the reverse pattern","chinese":"呈現相反模式"},{"english":"the reverse pattern","chinese":"相反模式"},{"english":"account for only 14% of sodium","chinese":"僅佔鈉的14%"},{"english":"21% of saturated fat","chinese":"佔飽和脂肪的21%"},{"english":"dominate added sugar","chinese":"在添加糖方面佔主導"},{"english":"at 42%","chinese":"為42%"},{"english":"almost double the dinner figure","chinese":"幾乎是晚餐數字的兩倍"},{"english":"the dinner figure","chinese":"晚餐的數字"}]},"model-essay-1-ielts-task1-process-diagram":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-1-ielts-task1-process-diagram","essayKey":"process-diagram:1","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-1-ielts-task1-process-diagram","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-1/process-diagrams/process-diagram-1","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"The diagram illustrates the process by which bamboo is converted into fabric and, ultimately, clothing items.","chinese":"該圖說明竹子如何被轉化成布料，並最終製成衣物。"},{"label":"Overview","english":"Overall, this is a linear, nine-stage manufacturing process, beginning with the cultivation of bamboo plants in spring and ending with finished garments. The early stages are concerned with growing and mechanically preparing the bamboo, while the later stages turn the extracted fibres into yarn and woven cloth.","chinese":"整體而言，這是一個線性的九階段製造流程，從春季種植竹子開始，以製成成衣結束。 前期階段主要涉及竹子的生長和機械處理，而後期階段則把提取出的纖維轉化為紗線和織布。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"At the outset, bamboo plants are planted in spring and left to mature until autumn, when they are harvested. Once the crop has been collected, the stems are cut into narrow strips. These strips are then crushed so that they are reduced to a liquid pulp. Following this, the pulp is filtered in order to separate the long fibres from the remaining liquid.","chinese":"一開始，竹子在春季被種下，並被留待生長至秋季，然後被收割。 當作物被收集後，竹莖會被切成細條。 然後，這些竹條會被壓碎，使其變成液態漿料。 接著，漿料會被過濾，以便把長纖維從剩餘液體中分離出來。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"In the next stage, the extracted fibres are softened through the addition of water and amine oxide. After they have been treated in this way, they are spun into yarn. The yarn is subsequently woven to produce bamboo fabric. Finally, this fabric is made into everyday clothing products, such as socks and T-shirts.","chinese":"在下一階段，提取出的纖維會透過加入水和胺氧化物而被軟化。 當它們以這種方式處理後，便會被紡成紗線。 隨後，紗線會被編織成竹纖維布料。 最後，這些布料會被製成日常衣物產品，例如襪子和 T 恤。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"The diagram illustrates","chinese":"圖解顯示"},{"english":"the process by which","chinese":"……的過程"},{"english":"is converted into","chinese":"被轉化成"},{"english":"fabric","chinese":"布料"},{"english":"ultimately","chinese":"最終"},{"english":"clothing items","chinese":"衣物"},{"english":"a linear, nine-stage manufacturing process","chinese":"線性的九階段製造過程"},{"english":"linear process","chinese":"線性過程"},{"english":"nine-stage manufacturing process","chinese":"九階段製造過程"},{"english":"beginning with","chinese":"以……開始"},{"english":"ending with","chinese":"以……結束"},{"english":"the cultivation of bamboo plants","chinese":"種植竹子"},{"english":"finished garments","chinese":"製成衣物"},{"english":"the early stages","chinese":"早期階段"},{"english":"are concerned with","chinese":"涉及；關乎"},{"english":"mechanically preparing","chinese":"以機械方式處理"},{"english":"the later stages","chinese":"後期階段"},{"english":"turn the extracted fibres into","chinese":"將提取出的纖維變成"},{"english":"extracted fibres","chinese":"提取出的纖維"},{"english":"yarn","chinese":"紗線"},{"english":"woven cloth","chinese":"梭織布料"},{"english":"At the outset","chinese":"一開始"},{"english":"are planted in spring","chinese":"在春天種植"},{"english":"left to mature","chinese":"被留待成熟"},{"english":"until autumn","chinese":"直到秋天"},{"english":"are harvested","chinese":"被收割"},{"english":"Once the crop has been collected","chinese":"當農作物被收集後"},{"english":"the crop","chinese":"農作物"},{"english":"has been collected","chinese":"已被收集"},{"english":"stems","chinese":"莖"},{"english":"are cut into narrow strips","chinese":"被切成幼長條"},{"english":"narrow strips","chinese":"幼長條"},{"english":"are then crushed","chinese":"然後被壓碎"},{"english":"are reduced to","chinese":"被變成；被分解成"},{"english":"liquid pulp","chinese":"液態漿"},{"english":"Following this","chinese":"隨後"},{"english":"is filtered","chinese":"被過濾"},{"english":"in order to separate","chinese":"以便分離"},{"english":"long fibres","chinese":"長纖維"},{"english":"remaining liquid","chinese":"餘下液體"},{"english":"In the next stage","chinese":"在下一階段"},{"english":"are softened through","chinese":"透過……被軟化"},{"english":"the addition of","chinese":"加入……"},{"english":"water and amine oxide","chinese":"水和氧化胺"},{"english":"amine oxide","chinese":"氧化胺"},{"english":"treated in this way","chinese":"以這種方式處理"},{"english":"are spun into yarn","chinese":"被紡成紗線"},{"english":"subsequently woven","chinese":"隨後被編織"},{"english":"produce bamboo fabric","chinese":"製成竹纖維布料"},{"english":"bamboo fabric","chinese":"竹纖維布料"},{"english":"Finally","chinese":"最後"},{"english":"is made into","chinese":"被製成"},{"english":"everyday clothing products","chinese":"日常衣物產品"},{"english":"such as socks and T-shirts","chinese":"例如襪和T恤"}]},"model-essay-1-ielts-task1-tables":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-1-ielts-task1-tables","essayKey":"tables:1","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-1-ielts-task1-tables","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-1/tables/table-1","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"The tables present changes in the population of New York City as a whole and compare Manhattan with the other four districts between 1800 and 2000.","chinese":"這些表格呈現了 1800 年至 2000 年間整個紐約市人口的變化，並將曼哈頓與其他四個區作比較。"},{"label":"Overview","english":"Overall, the city’s population rose dramatically across the two centuries, but the balance shifted sharply away from Manhattan. While Manhattan made up more than three quarters of New York’s residents in 1800, the other districts accounted for over four fifths by 2000.","chinese":"整體而言，在這兩個世紀中，該市人口大幅上升，但人口分布的重心明顯從曼哈頓轉移開來。 雖然曼哈頓在 1800 年佔紐約居民的四分之三以上，但到 2000 年，其他區已佔超過五分之四。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"In 1800, New York City had only 79,216 inhabitants. By 1900 this figure had increased to 3,437,202, before reaching 8,009,185 in 2000. The first century therefore saw the more explosive expansion, with the population multiplying more than fortyfold; over the following hundred years it still grew substantially, though by a little over twice.","chinese":"1800 年，紐約市只有 79,216 名居民。 到 1900 年，這一數字已增至 3,437,202 ，之後在 2000 年達到 8,009,185 。 因此，第一個世紀出現了更爆炸性的增長，人口增加了四十多倍；在接下來的一百年中，人口仍然大幅增長，儘管只是略多於兩倍。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"Manhattan followed a different path from the rest of the city. Its population climbed from 60,515 in 1800 to 1,850,093 in 1900, but then declined to 1,538,096 by 2000. Its share consequently fell from 76% to 54%, and finally to just 19%. By contrast, the other districts grew continuously, from 18,701 to 1,587,109 and then to 6,471,089, raising their combined share from 24% to 81%.","chinese":"曼哈頓的發展路徑與城市其他地區不同。 其人口從 1800 年的 60,515 上升至 1900 年的 1,850,093 ，但到 2000 年又下降至。 因此，其所佔比例從 76% 下降至 54% ，最後降至僅 19% 。 相比之下，其他區的人口持續增長，從 18,701 上升至 1,587,109 ，然後再增至6,471,089 ，使它們的合計比例從 24% 上升至 81% 。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"the first table below shows","chinese":"下方第一個表格顯示"},{"english":"changes in the total population","chinese":"總人口的變化"},{"english":"the total population of","chinese":"……的總人口"},{"english":"New York City","chinese":"紐約市"},{"english":"from 1800 to 2000","chinese":"由1800年至2000年"},{"english":"the second and third tables show","chinese":"第二和第三個表格顯示"},{"english":"the population of the five boroughs","chinese":"五個行政區的人口"},{"english":"five boroughs of the city","chinese":"該市五個行政區"},{"english":"Manhattan","chinese":"曼哈頓"},{"english":"Brooklyn","chinese":"布魯克林"},{"english":"the Bronx","chinese":"布朗克斯"},{"english":"Queens","chinese":"皇后區"},{"english":"Staten Island","chinese":"史泰登島"},{"english":"over the same period","chinese":"在同一時期內"},{"english":"summarise the information","chinese":"概述資料"},{"english":"selecting and reporting","chinese":"選取並報告"},{"english":"the main features","chinese":"主要特徵"},{"english":"make comparisons where relevant","chinese":"在相關之處作出比較"},{"english":"the tables present changes in","chinese":"表格呈現……的變化"},{"english":"as a whole","chinese":"作為一個整體"},{"english":"compare Manhattan with","chinese":"將曼哈頓與……作比較"},{"english":"the other four boroughs","chinese":"其他四個行政區"},{"english":"between 1800 and 2000","chinese":"在1800年至2000年間"},{"english":"Overall","chinese":"整體而言"},{"english":"the city's population","chinese":"該市人口"},{"english":"rose dramatically","chinese":"大幅上升"},{"english":"across the two centuries","chinese":"在這兩個世紀中"},{"english":"the balance shifted sharply away from","chinese":"重心大幅從……轉移"},{"english":"shifted sharply away from","chinese":"大幅從……轉移"},{"english":"made up more than three quarters of","chinese":"佔……超過四分之三"},{"english":"more than three quarters of","chinese":"超過四分之三"},{"english":"New York's residents","chinese":"紐約居民"},{"english":"accounted for over four fifths","chinese":"佔超過五分之四"},{"english":"over four fifths","chinese":"超過五分之四"},{"english":"by 2000","chinese":"到2000年"},{"english":"had only 79,216 inhabitants","chinese":"只有79,216名居民"},{"english":"inhabitants","chinese":"居民"},{"english":"by 1900","chinese":"到1900年"},{"english":"this figure had increased to","chinese":"這一數字已增加至"},{"english":"3,437,202","chinese":"3,437,202"},{"english":"before reaching","chinese":"之後達到"},{"english":"reached 8,009,185","chinese":"達到8,009,185"},{"english":"the first century","chinese":"第一個世紀"},{"english":"saw the more explosive expansion","chinese":"出現更爆炸性的擴張"},{"english":"explosive expansion","chinese":"爆炸性擴張"},{"english":"multiplying more than fortyfold","chinese":"增加超過四十倍"},{"english":"more than fortyfold","chinese":"超過四十倍"},{"english":"over the following hundred years","chinese":"在接下來的一百年間"},{"english":"grew substantially","chinese":"大幅增長"},{"english":"though by a little over twice","chinese":"但只是略多於兩倍"},{"english":"a little over twice","chinese":"略多於兩倍"},{"english":"followed a different path from","chinese":"走勢與……不同"},{"english":"the rest of the city","chinese":"該市其餘地區"},{"english":"climbed from … to …","chinese":"由……上升至……"},{"english":"from 60,515 to 1,850,093","chinese":"由60,515升至1,850,093"},{"english":"then declined to","chinese":"其後下降至"},{"english":"declined to 1,538,096","chinese":"下降至1,538,096"},{"english":"its share consequently fell","chinese":"其比例因此下降"},{"english":"consequently","chinese":"因此"},{"english":"fell from 76% to 54%","chinese":"由76%跌至54%"},{"english":"finally to just 19%","chinese":"最終只剩19%"},{"english":"just 19%","chinese":"只有19%"},{"english":"By contrast","chinese":"相比之下"},{"english":"grew continuously","chinese":"持續增長"},{"english":"from 18,701 to 1,587,109","chinese":"由18,701升至1,587,109"},{"english":"then to 6,471,089","chinese":"其後升至6,471,089"},{"english":"raising their combined share","chinese":"使其合計比例上升"},{"english":"combined share","chinese":"合計比例"},{"english":"from 24% to 81%","chinese":"由24%升至81%"}]},"model-essay-2-ielts-advantage-disadvantage":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-2-ielts-advantage-disadvantage","essayKey":"advantage-disadvantage:2","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-2-ielts-advantage-disadvantage","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/advantage-and-disadvantage/EdmundBd9AdDisAd-Q2","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"In many countries, purchasing goods through digital platforms has become part of everyday life. This development brings clear benefits to both consumers and businesses, particularly in terms of convenience and efficiency, although it also creates several notable drawbacks. Overall, I believe that online shopping is a positive trend because its advantages are more significant than its disadvantages for both individuals and companies.","chinese":"在許多國家，透過數位平台購買商品已成為日常生活的一部分。 這種發展為消費者和企業都帶來了明顯好處，尤其是在便利性和效率方面，儘管它也造成了一些值得注意的缺點。 總的來說，我認為網上購物是一項正面的趨勢，因為對個人和企業而言，它的優點比缺點更為顯著。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"The principal advantage of online shopping is the efficiency it creates. For individuals, online marketplaces allow people to compare prices, read reviews, and complete purchases within minutes, which saves both time and effort. Instead of travelling from one shop to another, a busy parent, for example, can order groceries or school supplies during a lunch break and have them delivered directly home. This convenience is especially valuable for those with demanding schedules or limited access to physical stores. Companies also benefit substantially. By selling online, businesses can reduce costs related to rent, shop maintenance, and in-store staff, while at the same time reaching a much wider customer base. A small independent bookshop, for instance, can move beyond relying on local foot traffic and sell to buyers across the country through a website or online marketplace. As a result, online retailing increases accessibility for consumers and improves commercial efficiency for firms.","chinese":"網上購物最主要的優點是它所帶來的效率。 對個人而言，網上市場讓人們可以在幾分鐘內比價、閱讀評論並完成購買，這樣能同時節省時間與精力。 例如，一位忙碌的家長不必一家店接一家店地奔波，只需在午休時間訂購雜貨或學用品，並直接送到家中。 這種便利對於行程繁忙或不容易前往實體商店的人尤其有價值。 企業同樣能獲得相當大的好處。 透過線上銷售，企業可以降低與租金、店面維護及店內員工相關的成本，同時接觸到更廣大的顧客群。 例如，一家小型獨立書店可以不再只依賴在地客流，而是透過網站或網上市場把書賣給全國各地的買家。 因此，線上零售提升了消費者的可及性，也改善了企業的商業效率。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"However, online shopping also has clear disadvantages. For individuals, the inability to inspect products physically means that purchases are often based only on pictures and descriptions, which can be misleading. This can lead to disappointment when an item arrives in the wrong size, poor quality, or a different appearance from what was advertised. Someone who buys clothing or furniture online, for example, may have to go through an inconvenient returns process after discovering that the product does not meet expectations. For companies, the digital marketplace is highly competitive and fragile. Because customers can compare dozens of sellers instantly, businesses are forced into price competition that can reduce profit margins. In addition, one delivery failure, data breach, or widely shared negative review can rapidly damage a company’s reputation. Therefore, while e-commerce offers speed and reach, it also exposes both shoppers and firms to significant risks.","chinese":"然而，網上購物也有明顯的缺點。 對個人而言，無法親自檢查商品意味著購買往往只能根據圖片與描述作出，而這些資訊可能具有誤導性。 這可能導致失望，因為商品送達時可能尺寸不對、品質不佳，或外觀與廣告宣傳不符。 例如，某人若在網上購買衣服或家具，發現商品不符合預期後，可能必須經歷一個麻煩的退貨流程。 對企業而言，數位市場競爭非常激烈，而且相當脆弱。 由於顧客能夠立即比較數十家賣家，企業被迫陷入價格競爭，而這可能壓縮利潤空間。 此外，一次配送失誤、資料外洩，或一則被廣泛傳播的負評，都可能迅速損害一家公司的聲譽。 因此，雖然電子商務提供了速度與廣泛觸及的優勢，但它也使消費者與企業同時面臨重大的風險。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, online shopping does present disadvantages, particularly product uncertainty for consumers and competitive pressure for businesses. Nevertheless, because it provides greater convenience for individuals and lower costs together with broader market access for companies, the advantages of shopping online clearly outweigh the disadvantages.","chinese":"總結來說，網上購物確實帶來缺點，尤其是消費者面臨商品不確定性，以及企業承受競爭壓力。 然而，由於它為個人帶來更大的便利，也為企業帶來更低的成本與更廣的市場接觸，因此網上購物的優點明顯大於缺點。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"purchasing goods","chinese":"購買商品"},{"english":"digital platforms","chinese":"數碼平台"},{"english":"everyday life","chinese":"日常生活"},{"english":"this development","chinese":"這項發展"},{"english":"clear benefits","chinese":"明顯好處"},{"english":"consumers and businesses","chinese":"消費者和企業"},{"english":"particularly in terms of","chinese":"尤其在……方面"},{"english":"convenience and efficiency","chinese":"方便和效率"},{"english":"notable drawbacks","chinese":"明顯缺點"},{"english":"a positive trend","chinese":"正面的趨勢"},{"english":"more significant than","chinese":"比……更重要"},{"english":"individuals and companies","chinese":"個人和公司"},{"english":"the principal advantage of","chinese":"……的主要好處"},{"english":"online marketplaces","chinese":"網上平台；網上市場"},{"english":"compare prices","chinese":"比較價格"},{"english":"read reviews","chinese":"閱讀評價"},{"english":"complete purchases","chinese":"完成購物"},{"english":"within minutes","chinese":"在數分鐘內"},{"english":"saves both time and effort","chinese":"節省時間和精力"},{"english":"instead of travelling from one shop to another","chinese":"而不是從一間店走到另一間店"},{"english":"a busy parent","chinese":"忙碌的家長"},{"english":"order groceries","chinese":"訂購日用品；訂購雜貨"},{"english":"school supplies","chinese":"學校用品"},{"english":"during a lunch break","chinese":"午膳休息期間"},{"english":"delivered directly home","chinese":"直接送到家中"},{"english":"especially valuable for","chinese":"對……尤其有價值"},{"english":"demanding schedules","chinese":"繁忙的日程"},{"english":"limited access to","chinese":"接觸……的機會有限"},{"english":"physical stores","chinese":"實體店"},{"english":"benefit substantially","chinese":"大大受惠"},{"english":"by selling online","chinese":"透過網上銷售"},{"english":"reduce costs related to","chinese":"減少與……有關的成本"},{"english":"shop maintenance","chinese":"店舖維修保養"},{"english":"in-store staff","chinese":"店內職員"},{"english":"at the same time","chinese":"同時"},{"english":"reach a much wider customer base","chinese":"接觸更廣泛的顧客群"},{"english":"customer base","chinese":"顧客群"},{"english":"a small independent bookshop","chinese":"小型獨立書店"},{"english":"move beyond relying on","chinese":"不再只依賴"},{"english":"local foot traffic","chinese":"本地店舖人流"},{"english":"across the country","chinese":"全國各地"},{"english":"online retailing","chinese":"網上零售"},{"english":"increases accessibility for","chinese":"增加……的可接觸性"},{"english":"commercial efficiency","chinese":"商業效率"},{"english":"clear disadvantages","chinese":"明顯缺點"},{"english":"the inability to inspect products physically","chinese":"無法親身檢查產品"},{"english":"inspect products physically","chinese":"親身檢查產品"},{"english":"be based only on","chinese":"只基於"},{"english":"pictures and descriptions","chinese":"圖片和描述"},{"english":"be misleading","chinese":"具誤導性"},{"english":"lead to disappointment","chinese":"導致失望"},{"english":"the wrong size","chinese":"尺碼錯誤"},{"english":"poor quality","chinese":"質素差"},{"english":"a different appearance from","chinese":"外觀與……不同"},{"english":"what was advertised","chinese":"廣告所展示的內容"},{"english":"clothing or furniture","chinese":"衣服或家具"},{"english":"go through","chinese":"經歷"},{"english":"an inconvenient returns process","chinese":"麻煩的退貨程序"},{"english":"does not meet expectations","chinese":"不符合期望"},{"english":"the digital marketplace","chinese":"數碼市場"},{"english":"highly competitive","chinese":"競爭激烈"},{"english":"fragile","chinese":"脆弱"},{"english":"dozens of sellers","chinese":"數十個賣家"},{"english":"instantly","chinese":"即時"},{"english":"be forced into","chinese":"被迫陷入"},{"english":"price competition","chinese":"價格競爭"},{"english":"reduce profit margins","chinese":"降低利潤率"},{"english":"profit margins","chinese":"利潤率"},{"english":"in addition","chinese":"此外"},{"english":"delivery failure","chinese":"送貨失誤"},{"english":"data breach","chinese":"資料外洩"},{"english":"widely shared negative review","chinese":"被廣泛分享的負面評價"},{"english":"rapidly damage","chinese":"迅速損害"},{"english":"a company's reputation","chinese":"公司的聲譽"},{"english":"e-commerce","chinese":"電子商貿"},{"english":"speed and reach","chinese":"速度和接觸範圍"},{"english":"exposes both shoppers and firms to","chinese":"令購物者和企業面對"},{"english":"significant risks","chinese":"重大風險"},{"english":"does present disadvantages","chinese":"確實存在缺點"},{"english":"product uncertainty","chinese":"產品不確定性"},{"english":"competitive pressure","chinese":"競爭壓力"},{"english":"nevertheless","chinese":"然而"},{"english":"greater convenience","chinese":"更大的便利"},{"english":"lower costs","chinese":"較低成本"},{"english":"broader market access","chinese":"更廣泛的市場接觸機會"},{"english":"clearly outweigh","chinese":"明顯大於"}]},"model-essay-2-ielts-cause-solution":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-2-ielts-cause-solution","essayKey":"cause-solution:2","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-2-ielts-cause-solution","flashDeckId":"","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"Large companies are often able to spend heavily on advertising, sponsorship and online promotion, so their products become more visible than those made by smaller local producers. This trend can damage local economies and weaken choice, but measures can make local goods easier to buy.","chinese":"大型企業通常有能力在廣告、贊助和網上推廣方面投入大量資金，因此它們的產品會比小型本地生產商所製造的產品更加顯眼。 這種趨勢可能損害本地經濟並削弱消費者選擇，但一些措施可以令本地產品更容易被購買。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"The first problem is that smaller firms are pushed into the shadows. When shoppers repeatedly see the same brands on television, social media and supermarket shelves, they tend to trust those names almost automatically, even when a local alternative is just as good. As sales move towards large corporations, independent shops and small manufacturers lose revenue, cut jobs and, in the worst cases, close altogether. This drains money from the community and leaves high streets less varied and less alive. A second problem is that consumer decisions become shaped by image rather than real value. A heavily advertised snack, for instance, may seem superior simply because its packaging, slogan and celebrity endorsement are everywhere. As a result, people may pay more for familiarity, while healthier or fresher local products are overlooked.","chinese":"第一個問題是，小型企業會被推到陰影之中。 當消費者不斷在電視、社交媒體和超市貨架上看到相同品牌時，他們往往會幾乎自動地信任這些品牌名稱，即使本地替代產品同樣出色。 隨著銷售額流向大型企業，獨立商店和小型製造商會失去收入、削減職位，最嚴重時甚至完全結業。 這會使金錢從社區中流走，並令商業街變得較缺乏多樣性，也較沒有生氣。 第二個問題是，消費者的決定會被形象塑造，而不是由真正價值決定。 例如，一款被大量宣傳的零食，可能只是因為它的包裝、標語和名人代言隨處可見，便顯得更優越。 結果，人們可能會為熟悉感支付更高價格，而更健康或更新鮮的本地產品卻被忽略。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"To encourage local purchasing, governments and councils should first make local products more visible. They could fund farmers’ markets, local-product sections in supermarkets, and digital platforms where nearby producers can sell directly to residents. If a family can find local vegetables, bread or handmade goods as easily as a global brand, buying locally becomes a convenient habit rather than a moral chore. Retailers can also help by using clear labelling and fair shelf space. A simple “made locally” label, paired with brief information about the producer, can turn an ordinary purchase into a small act of community support. Public campaigns can also remind consumers that local spending sustains jobs, skills and neighbourhood identity.","chinese":"為了鼓勵人們購買本地產品，政府和地方議會首先應該讓本地產品更加顯眼。 它們可以資助農夫市集、超市中的本地產品專區，以及讓附近生產商能夠直接向居民銷售的數碼平台。 如果一個家庭能夠像找到全球品牌一樣容易地找到本地蔬菜、麵包或手工製品，那麼購買本地產品就會變成一種方便的習慣，而不是一項道德上的苦差。 零售商也可以透過清晰標籤和公平的貨架空間提供幫助。 一個簡單的「本地製造」標籤，再配上關於生產者的簡短資料，可以把一次普通的購物轉化為一個支持社區的小小行動。 公共宣傳活動也可以提醒消費者，本地消費能夠維持就業、技術和社區身份。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, the marketing power of large businesses can undermine local firms and encourage more brand-led consumption. However, if local goods are made visible, convenient and meaningful to consumers, communities can tilt demand back towards their own producers.","chinese":"總結來說，大型企業的行銷力量可能削弱本地企業，並鼓勵更多由品牌主導的消費。 然而，如果本地商品能夠變得顯眼、方便，並且對消費者具有意義，社區便能夠把需求重新引導回自己的生產者身上。"}],"vocabulary":[]},"model-essay-2-ielts-direct-question":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-2-ielts-direct-question","essayKey":"direct-question:2","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-2-ielts-direct-question","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/direct-question/EdmundBd9Dir-Q2","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"The success of a company often depends less on ambitious strategy than on how consistently its employees perform in daily work. To increase staff productivity, firms should focus on two practical areas: making work easier to do well and creating conditions in which people want to do their best.","chinese":"一家公司的成功往往與其說取決於雄心勃勃的策略，不如說取決於員工在日常工作中能否持續穩定地表現。 為了提高員工生產力，企業應該專注於兩個實際範疇：讓工作更容易被做好，以及創造一種讓人願意盡力而為的環境。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"The first step is to make work clearer, better supported, and less wasteful. Many employees are not unproductive because they are lazy; rather, they lose time because instructions are vague, systems are slow, or priorities change too often. Companies should therefore set clear targets, divide large projects into manageable tasks, and ensure that workers know exactly what is expected of them. Regular but concise feedback is also important, as it allows staff to correct mistakes before small problems become expensive ones. Training should also be treated as a core investment rather than an occasional extra. When employees are taught how to use new software, communicate with clients, or manage their workload, they can work with greater confidence and fewer errors. A well-trained team is rarely a luxury; it is the engine of a productive company.","chinese":"第一步是讓工作變得更清晰、得到更好的支援，並減少浪費。 許多員工缺乏生產力並不是因為他們懶惰；相反，他們浪費時間，是因為指示含糊、系統緩慢，或者優先事項變動太頻繁。 因此，公司應該設定清晰目標，將大型項目分拆成可管理的任務，並確保員工準確知道自己被期望完成甚麼。 定期但簡潔的回饋同樣重要，因為它能讓員工在小問題變成昂貴錯誤之前及時修正。 培訓也應該被視為一項核心投資，而不是偶爾才提供的額外安排。 當員工被教導如何使用新軟件、與客戶溝通，或管理自己的工作量時，他們便能更有信心地工作，並減少錯誤。 一支訓練有素的團隊很少只是奢侈品；它是一間高生產力公司的引擎。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"Another effective way to improve productivity is to protect employees’ motivation and well-being. If staff are constantly exhausted, underpaid, or ignored, their performance will eventually decline, even if they are talented. Companies can prevent this by offering fair salaries, recognising good work, and giving employees realistic workloads. Flexible working arrangements can also help, especially when they reduce unnecessary commuting and allow workers to concentrate during their most productive hours. Managers should also create a culture in which employees feel trusted rather than watched. People usually work harder when they feel respected, because they see their job not merely as a duty, but as a contribution.","chinese":"另一個提高生產力的有效方法，是保護員工的動力和身心健康。 如果員工長期感到疲憊、薪酬不足，或被忽視，即使他們很有才華，表現最終也會下降 公司可以透過提供公平薪酬、認可優秀工作，以及給予員工合理的工作量來防止這種情況 彈性工作安排也能有所幫助，尤其是當它們能減少不必要的通勤，並讓員工在自己最有效率的時間集中工作時。 管理者也應該創造一種讓員工感到被信任，而不是被監視的文化。 當人們感到被尊重時，通常會更努力工作，因為他們不只是把工作看作一項職責，而是把它看作一種貢獻。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, companies can raise staff productivity by improving work systems, providing useful training, and maintaining a healthy, motivating workplace. Productivity grows best when efficiency and morale move together.","chinese":"總結來說，公司可以透過改善工作制度、提供有用的培訓，以及維持一個健康而具激勵性的工作環境來提升員工生產力。 當效率與士氣同步提升時，生產力最能自然增長。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"the success of a company","chinese":"一間公司的成功"},{"english":"depends less on...than on...","chinese":"與其取決於……不如取決於……"},{"english":"ambitious strategy","chinese":"具雄心的策略"},{"english":"consistently perform","chinese":"持續表現良好"},{"english":"daily work","chinese":"日常工作"},{"english":"increase staff productivity","chinese":"提高員工生產力"},{"english":"focus on","chinese":"專注於"},{"english":"practical areas","chinese":"實際範疇"},{"english":"making work easier to do well","chinese":"令工作更容易做好"},{"english":"creating conditions in which","chinese":"創造讓……的條件"},{"english":"do their best","chinese":"盡力做到最好"},{"english":"the first step","chinese":"第一步"},{"english":"better supported","chinese":"得到更好支援"},{"english":"less wasteful","chinese":"減少浪費"},{"english":"unproductive","chinese":"生產力低"},{"english":"lose time because","chinese":"因為……而浪費時間"},{"english":"instructions are vague","chinese":"指示含糊"},{"english":"systems are slow","chinese":"系統緩慢"},{"english":"priorities change too often","chinese":"優先事項變動太頻繁"},{"english":"set clear targets","chinese":"訂立清晰目標"},{"english":"divide large projects into","chinese":"將大型項目分成……"},{"english":"manageable tasks","chinese":"可處理的任務"},{"english":"ensure that","chinese":"確保"},{"english":"what is expected of them","chinese":"對他們的期望"},{"english":"regular but concise feedback","chinese":"定期但簡潔的回饋"},{"english":"correct mistakes","chinese":"改正錯誤"},{"english":"small problems become expensive ones","chinese":"小問題變成代價高昂的問題"},{"english":"be treated as","chinese":"被視為"},{"english":"a core investment","chinese":"核心投資"},{"english":"rather than an occasional extra","chinese":"而不是偶爾才有的額外安排"},{"english":"an occasional extra","chinese":"偶爾才有的額外安排"},{"english":"be taught how to","chinese":"被教導如何……"},{"english":"use new software","chinese":"使用新軟件"},{"english":"communicate with clients","chinese":"與客戶溝通"},{"english":"manage their workload","chinese":"管理工作量"},{"english":"work with greater confidence","chinese":"更有信心地工作"},{"english":"fewer errors","chinese":"較少錯誤"},{"english":"a well-trained team","chinese":"受過良好培訓的團隊"},{"english":"rarely a luxury","chinese":"很少是奢侈品"},{"english":"the engine of","chinese":"……的引擎；推動力"},{"english":"a productive company","chinese":"高生產力的公司"},{"english":"another effective way to","chinese":"另一個有效方法去……"},{"english":"protect employees' motivation and well-being","chinese":"保護員工的動力和身心健康"},{"english":"well-being","chinese":"身心健康"},{"english":"constantly exhausted","chinese":"長期疲憊"},{"english":"underpaid","chinese":"薪酬過低"},{"english":"ignored","chinese":"被忽視"},{"english":"eventually decline","chinese":"最終下降"},{"english":"talented","chinese":"有才能的"},{"english":"offering fair salaries","chinese":"提供公平薪酬"},{"english":"recognising good work","chinese":"認可出色工作"},{"english":"realistic workloads","chinese":"合理工作量"},{"english":"flexible working arrangements","chinese":"彈性工作安排"},{"english":"reduce unnecessary commuting","chinese":"減少不必要的通勤"},{"english":"concentrate during","chinese":"在……期間專心"},{"english":"most productive hours","chinese":"生產力最高的時段"},{"english":"create a culture in which","chinese":"建立一種讓……的文化"},{"english":"feel trusted rather than watched","chinese":"感到被信任，而不是被監視"},{"english":"feel respected","chinese":"感到被尊重"},{"english":"not merely as a duty","chinese":"不只是作為責任"},{"english":"as a contribution","chinese":"作為一種貢獻"},{"english":"raise staff productivity","chinese":"提高員工生產力"},{"english":"improving work systems","chinese":"改善工作系統"},{"english":"providing useful training","chinese":"提供有用培訓"},{"english":"maintaining a healthy, motivating workplace","chinese":"維持健康而有激勵性的工作場所"},{"english":"efficiency and morale","chinese":"效率和士氣"},{"english":"move together","chinese":"一起提升；並行發展"}]},"model-essay-2-ielts-task1-bar-charts":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-2-ielts-task1-bar-charts","essayKey":"bar-charts:2","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-2-ielts-task1-bar-charts","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-1/bar-charts/bar-chart-2","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"The bar chart compares the proportions of weekly income that families in one country spent on eight categories in 1968 and 2018.","chinese":"這張柱狀圖比較了一個國家的家庭在 1968 年和 2018 年把每週收入花在八個類別上的比例。"},{"label":"Overview","english":"Overall, household spending shifted noticeably over the 50-year period. Food was by far the dominant item in 1968, but its share fell sharply by 2018, when leisure, housing and transport had become much more significant. Several smaller categories declined, while household goods remained broadly stable.","chinese":"整體而言，在這 50 年間，家庭支出結構出現了明顯轉變。 食物在 1968 年是遠遠最主要的支出項目，但到 2018 年其比例大幅下降；同時，休閒、住房和交通變得重要得多。 幾個較小的類別有所下降，而家居用品則大致保持穩定。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"In 1968, families allocated about 35% of their income to food, more than three times the proportion spent on housing or clothing and footwear, each at around 10%. Leisure and transport were also relatively modest, at just under 10% and about 8% respectively. Household goods and personal goods accounted for similar shares, at roughly 7–8%, while fuel and power was slightly lower, at around 6%.","chinese":"在 1968 年，家庭把大約 35% 的收入花在食物上，這是住房或服裝及鞋類支出比例的三倍多；後兩者各約佔 10% 。 休閒和交通的比例也相對較低，分別為略低於 10% 和約 8% 。 家居用品和個人用品所佔比例相近，約為 7% 至 8% ；而燃料和能源則稍低，約為 6% 。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"By 2018, leisure had become the largest category, rising to just over a fifth of income. Housing almost doubled to approximately 19%, and transport increased to about 14%. In contrast, food dropped to around 17%, clothing and footwear halved to 5%, and personal goods and fuel and power both fell to about 4%. Household goods changed very little, remaining near 7%.","chinese":"到 2018 年，休閒已成為最大的類別，上升至略高於收入的五分之一。 住房幾乎翻倍，升至約 19% ；交通則增加至約 14% 。 相比之下，食物下降至約 17% ，服裝及鞋類減半至 5% ，而個人用品以及燃料和能源都下降至約 4% 。 家居用品變化很小，仍維持在約 7% 。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"bar chart","chinese":"棒形圖"},{"english":"compares the proportions of","chinese":"比較……的比例"},{"english":"proportions of weekly income","chinese":"每週收入的比例"},{"english":"spent on eight categories","chinese":"用於八個類別"},{"english":"household spending","chinese":"家庭開支"},{"english":"shifted noticeably","chinese":"明顯轉變"},{"english":"over the 50-year period","chinese":"在50年間"},{"english":"by far the dominant item","chinese":"遠遠是最主要的項目"},{"english":"dominant item","chinese":"主要項目"},{"english":"its share fell sharply","chinese":"其比例大幅下降"},{"english":"by 2018","chinese":"到2018年時"},{"english":"had become much more significant","chinese":"已變得重要得多"},{"english":"leisure","chinese":"消閒"},{"english":"housing","chinese":"住屋"},{"english":"transport","chinese":"交通"},{"english":"several smaller categories","chinese":"數個較小類別"},{"english":"declined","chinese":"下降"},{"english":"household goods","chinese":"家庭用品"},{"english":"remained broadly stable","chinese":"大致保持穩定"},{"english":"allocated about 35% of their income to","chinese":"將約35%的收入分配予……"},{"english":"allocated income to","chinese":"將收入分配予……"},{"english":"more than three times the proportion","chinese":"超過三倍比例"},{"english":"proportion spent on","chinese":"用於……的比例"},{"english":"clothing and footwear","chinese":"衣履"},{"english":"each at around 10%","chinese":"各約10%"},{"english":"relatively modest","chinese":"相對較少；相對不高"},{"english":"just under 10%","chinese":"略低於10%"},{"english":"respectively","chinese":"分別"},{"english":"accounted for similar shares","chinese":"佔相近比例"},{"english":"similar shares","chinese":"相近比例"},{"english":"at roughly 7–8%","chinese":"約7至8%"},{"english":"fuel and power","chinese":"燃料及電力"},{"english":"slightly lower","chinese":"略低"},{"english":"had become the largest category","chinese":"已成為最大類別"},{"english":"the largest category","chinese":"最大類別"},{"english":"rising to","chinese":"上升至"},{"english":"just over a fifth of income","chinese":"收入的略多於五分之一"},{"english":"almost doubled to","chinese":"幾乎翻倍至"},{"english":"approximately 19%","chinese":"約19%"},{"english":"increased to","chinese":"增至"},{"english":"in contrast","chinese":"相比之下"},{"english":"dropped to around 17%","chinese":"下降至約17%"},{"english":"halved to 5%","chinese":"減半至5%"},{"english":"personal goods","chinese":"個人用品"},{"english":"both fell to about 4%","chinese":"兩者均下降至約4%"},{"english":"changed very little","chinese":"變化很小"},{"english":"remaining near 7%","chinese":"維持在接近7%"}]},"model-essay-2-ielts-task1-line-graph":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-2-ielts-task1-line-graph","essayKey":"line-graph:2","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-2-ielts-task1-line-graph","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-1/line-graphs/line-graph-2","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"The line graph compares the percentage of people living in cities in the Philippines, Malaysia, Thailand and Indonesia from 1970 to 2020, with forecasts to 2040.","chinese":"這張折線圖比較了 1970 年至 2020 年間菲律賓、馬來西亞、泰國和印尼城市人口所佔百分比，並附有到 2040 年的預測。"},{"label":"Overview","english":"Overall, all four countries became more urbanised. Malaysia rose to and is expected to remain the clear leader, while Indonesia records the fastest long-term growth, moving from the lowest position to second place. By contrast, the Philippines fluctuated, and Thailand grew more slowly, becoming the least urbanised country from 2010 onwards.","chinese":"整體而言，四個國家的城市化程度都提高了。 馬來西亞上升後成為、並預計會繼續保持明顯領先的位置；與此同時，印尼錄得最顯著的長期增長，從最低位置升至第二位。 相比之下，菲律賓的數據有所波動，而泰國增長較慢，從 2010 年起成為城市化比例最低的國家。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"In 1970, the Philippines led slightly, at just over 30%, compared with about 30% in Malaysia. The Philippine figure reached nearly 50% in 1990, then declined to just above 40% in 2010, before recovering to roughly 46% in 2020; it is projected to rise to about 56% by 2040. Malaysia, however, climbed steadily from around 30% to 60% between 1970 and 2000, and is forecast to exceed 80% by the end.","chinese":"在 1970 年，菲律賓以略高於 30% 的城市人口比例小幅領先，而馬來西亞約為。 菲律賓的數據在 1990 年達到接近 50% ，之後在 2010 年下降至略高於 40% ，再於2020 年回升至約 46% ；預計到 2040 年將升至約 56% 。 然而，馬來西亞從 1970 年的約 30% 穩步上升至 2000 年的 60% ，並預計在最後一年超過 80% 。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"Indonesia began at only about 13%, but rose continuously, equalling the Philippines at around 43% in 2010 and reaching just over 50% in 2020. It should climb further to the mid-60s, whereas Thailand is expected to grow from just above 30% in 2020 to 50% in 2040.","chinese":"印尼的起點只有約 13% ，但其比例持續上升，在 2010 年以約 43% 追平菲律賓，並於 2020 年達到略高於 50% 。 預計印尼會進一步升至 60 多 % 的中段，而泰國則預計會從 2020 年的略高於30% 升至 2040 年的 50% 。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"line graph","chinese":"折線圖"},{"english":"compares the percentage of","chinese":"比較……的百分比"},{"english":"people living in cities","chinese":"居於城市的人口"},{"english":"from 1970 to 2020","chinese":"由1970年至2020年"},{"english":"with forecasts to 2040","chinese":"並預測至2040年"},{"english":"forecasts","chinese":"預測"},{"english":"became more urbanised","chinese":"變得更城市化"},{"english":"more urbanised","chinese":"城市化程度較高"},{"english":"rose to","chinese":"上升至"},{"english":"is expected to remain","chinese":"預料會維持"},{"english":"the clear leader","chinese":"明顯領先者"},{"english":"records the fastest long-term growth","chinese":"錄得最快長期增長"},{"english":"fastest long-term growth","chinese":"最快長期增長"},{"english":"moving from the lowest position to second place","chinese":"由最低位置升至第二位"},{"english":"the lowest position","chinese":"最低位置"},{"english":"second place","chinese":"第二位"},{"english":"by contrast","chinese":"相比之下"},{"english":"fluctuated","chinese":"波動"},{"english":"grew more slowly","chinese":"增長較慢"},{"english":"the least urbanised country","chinese":"城市化程度最低的國家"},{"english":"from 2010 onwards","chinese":"從2010年起"},{"english":"led slightly","chinese":"略為領先"},{"english":"at just over 30%","chinese":"略高於30%"},{"english":"compared with","chinese":"與……相比"},{"english":"reached nearly 50%","chinese":"達接近50%"},{"english":"the Philippine figure","chinese":"菲律賓的數字"},{"english":"then declined to","chinese":"然後下降至"},{"english":"just above 40%","chinese":"略高於40%"},{"english":"before recovering to","chinese":"之後回升至"},{"english":"roughly 46%","chinese":"約46%"},{"english":"is projected to rise to","chinese":"預計上升至"},{"english":"by 2040","chinese":"到2040年時"},{"english":"however","chinese":"然而"},{"english":"climbed steadily","chinese":"穩步上升"},{"english":"from around 30% to 60%","chinese":"由約30%升至60%"},{"english":"between 1970 and 2000","chinese":"在1970年至2000年間"},{"english":"is forecast to exceed","chinese":"預測會超過"},{"english":"exceed 80%","chinese":"超過80%"},{"english":"by the end","chinese":"到期末時"},{"english":"began at only about 13%","chinese":"起初只有約13%"},{"english":"rose continuously","chinese":"持續上升"},{"english":"equalling the Philippines","chinese":"與菲律賓持平"},{"english":"at around 43%","chinese":"約43%"},{"english":"reaching just over 50%","chinese":"達略高於50%"},{"english":"should climb further to","chinese":"應會進一步上升至"},{"english":"the mid-60s","chinese":"60多個百分點的中段"},{"english":"whereas","chinese":"而；相比之下"},{"english":"is expected to grow from…to…","chinese":"預計由……增至……"},{"english":"just above 30%","chinese":"略高於30%"},{"english":"to 50% in 2040","chinese":"到2040年增至50%"},{"english":"urbanisation rate","chinese":"城市化率"},{"english":"long-term trend","chinese":"長期趨勢"},{"english":"upward trend","chinese":"上升趨勢"},{"english":"projected figure","chinese":"預測數字"},{"english":"urban population","chinese":"城市人口比例"},{"english":"over the period","chinese":"在整段期間"}]},"model-essay-2-ielts-task1-maps":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-2-ielts-task1-maps","essayKey":"maps:2","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-2-ielts-task1-maps","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-1/maps/maps-2","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"The two plans illustrate how Porth Harbour has changed since 2000.","chinese":"這兩幅平面圖展示了 Porth Harbour 自 2000 年以來的變化。"},{"label":"Overview","english":"Overall, the harbour has become more developed and visitor-oriented. The main changes are the addition of hotel and commercial facilities, the creation of a private beach, the expansion of the dock area, and the relocation of the marina and fishing boats.","chinese":"整體而言，這個港口變得更加發達，也更以遊客為導向。 主要變化包括新增酒店和商業設施、設立私人海灘、擴建碼頭區，以及搬遷私人遊艇碼頭和漁船停泊區。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"On the western side, the two car parks and the main road are still in place, and the original showers and toilets have been retained beside the northern car park. However, the marina for private yachts, formerly in the north-west basin, has been moved southwards to the area once used by fishing boats. These boats now occupy the former marina site. A second block of showers and toilets has been built near the lower car park, while cafés and shops have been added west of the lifeboat station.","chinese":"在西面，兩個停車場和主路仍然保留，而原有的淋浴間和洗手間也保留在北面停車場旁邊。 然而，原本位於西北面水域的私人遊艇碼頭，已經向南遷移到原本停泊漁船的區域。 這些漁船現在則停泊在原本私人遊艇碼頭所在的位置。 另一座淋浴間和洗手間已在較南面的停車場附近建成，而咖啡店和商店則新增在救生艇站的西面。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"Further east, the dock has been enlarged with extra mooring space, although the passenger ferries remain nearby. The disused castle on the small peninsula has been replaced by a hotel, accessed by an extended road. The southern beach is now reserved for hotel guests, whereas the northern public beach and lifeboat station remain largely unchanged.","chinese":"再往東面，碼頭已經擴建，並增加了停泊空間，不過客運渡輪仍停留在附近。 小半島上原本廢棄的城堡已被一間酒店取代，而該酒店可通過延伸道路到達。 南面的海灘現在只供酒店住客使用；相反，北面的公共海灘和救生艇站則大致保持不變。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"the plans below show","chinese":"下列平面圖顯示"},{"english":"a harbour","chinese":"港口"},{"english":"how it looks today","chinese":"它現時的樣貌"},{"english":"summarise the information","chinese":"概述資料"},{"english":"selecting and reporting the main features","chinese":"選取並報告主要特徵"},{"english":"make comparisons where relevant","chinese":"在相關之處作出比較"},{"english":"The two plans illustrate how","chinese":"兩幅平面圖顯示……如何"},{"english":"Porth Harbour","chinese":"Porth Harbour"},{"english":"has changed since","chinese":"自……以來已有變化"},{"english":"since 2000","chinese":"自2000年以來"},{"english":"Overall","chinese":"整體而言"},{"english":"has become more developed","chinese":"變得發展程度更高"},{"english":"visitor-oriented","chinese":"以遊客為導向"},{"english":"the main changes are","chinese":"主要變化是"},{"english":"the addition of","chinese":"增設……"},{"english":"hotel and commercial facilities","chinese":"酒店及商業設施"},{"english":"the creation of","chinese":"設立……"},{"english":"a private beach","chinese":"私人海灘"},{"english":"the expansion of","chinese":"……的擴建"},{"english":"the dock area","chinese":"碼頭區"},{"english":"the relocation of","chinese":"……的搬遷"},{"english":"the marina","chinese":"遊艇碼頭"},{"english":"fishing boats","chinese":"漁船"},{"english":"On the western side","chinese":"在西面"},{"english":"car parks","chinese":"停車場"},{"english":"the main road","chinese":"主要道路"},{"english":"still in place","chinese":"仍然保留原位"},{"english":"the original showers and toilets","chinese":"原有的淋浴及洗手間設施"},{"english":"have been retained","chinese":"已被保留"},{"english":"retained beside","chinese":"保留在……旁邊"},{"english":"the northern car park","chinese":"北面的停車場"},{"english":"However","chinese":"然而"},{"english":"private yachts","chinese":"私人遊艇"},{"english":"formerly in","chinese":"以前位於"},{"english":"the north-west basin","chinese":"西北面的港池"},{"english":"has been moved southwards","chinese":"已向南搬遷"},{"english":"the area once used by","chinese":"以往由……使用的地方"},{"english":"once used by fishing boats","chinese":"以往由漁船使用"},{"english":"now occupy","chinese":"現時佔用"},{"english":"the former marina site","chinese":"原來的遊艇碼頭位置"},{"english":"a second block of","chinese":"第二座；第二組"},{"english":"has been built near","chinese":"已在……附近興建"},{"english":"the lower car park","chinese":"下方的停車場"},{"english":"cafés and shops","chinese":"咖啡店及商店"},{"english":"have been added west of","chinese":"已在……以西增設"},{"english":"the lifeboat station","chinese":"救生艇站"},{"english":"Further east","chinese":"再往東面"},{"english":"has been enlarged with","chinese":"已擴建並加入……"},{"english":"extra mooring space","chinese":"額外停泊空間"},{"english":"although","chinese":"雖然"},{"english":"passenger ferries","chinese":"客運渡輪"},{"english":"remain nearby","chinese":"仍然在附近"},{"english":"the disused castle","chinese":"荒廢城堡"},{"english":"the small peninsula","chinese":"小半島"},{"english":"has been replaced by","chinese":"已被……取代"},{"english":"accessed by","chinese":"經由……到達"},{"english":"an extended road","chinese":"延伸道路"},{"english":"the southern beach","chinese":"南面的海灘"},{"english":"is now reserved for","chinese":"現時專供……使用"},{"english":"hotel guests","chinese":"酒店住客"},{"english":"whereas","chinese":"而；相比之下"},{"english":"the northern public beach","chinese":"北面的公眾海灘"},{"english":"remain largely unchanged","chinese":"大致維持不變"}]},"model-essay-2-ielts-task1-mixed-charts":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-2-ielts-task1-mixed-charts","essayKey":"mixed-charts:2","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-2-ielts-task1-mixed-charts","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-1/mixed-charts/mixed-charts-2","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"The pie chart shows where young people in an Australian town attend dance classes, while the bar chart compares the numbers of under-11s and 11- to 16-year-olds taking ballet, tap and modern dance.","chinese":"圓餅圖顯示澳洲某城鎮的年輕人在哪些地點上舞蹈課，而柱狀圖則比較了 11歲以下以及 11 至 16 歲學生參加芭蕾舞、踢踏舞和現代舞課程的人數。"},{"label":"Overview","english":"Overall, private studios are by far the most common venue, accounting for nearly half of all classes, whereas college-based studios represent the smallest share. In terms of dance style, ballet is clearly the leading choice among younger children, while modern dance is more popular with the older group; tap attracts broadly similar numbers in both age bands.","chinese":"整體而言，私人舞蹈室是目前最常見的上課地點，佔所有課程的接近一半；相反，設於學院的舞蹈室所佔比例最小。 就舞蹈類型而言，芭蕾舞明顯是較年幼兒童的首選，而現代舞則更受年齡較大的學生歡迎；踢踏舞在兩個年齡組中的人數大致相近。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"Looking first at locations, 48% of classes are held in private studios, exactly twice the proportion taking place in after-school sessions in school halls, at 24%. Community halls and other venues make up a further 18%, leaving college-based studios with only 10%, or around one tenth of the total.","chinese":"先看上課地點， 48% 的課程在私人舞蹈室舉行，這正好是學校禮堂課後課程比例的兩倍，後者為 24% 。 社區禮堂和其他場地另佔 18% ，而學院舞蹈室只佔 10% ，即大約佔整體的十分之一。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"Regarding class types, about 600 children under 11 attend ballet, compared with roughly 300 students aged 11–16. Modern dance shows the opposite pattern, with just under 300 younger participants but approximately 520 older ones. Tap is more evenly balanced, at around 450 under-11s and slightly over 400 students in the older age group.","chinese":"就課程類型而言，大約 600 名 11 歲以下兒童參加芭蕾舞課，相比之下， 11 至16 歲的學生約為 300 人。 現代舞則呈現相反模式，較年幼組別的人數略低於 300 ，而較年長組別約有520 人。 踢踏舞的人數分布較平均， 11 歲以下學生約為 450 人，而較年長組別則略高於 400 人。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"the charts below","chinese":"以下圖表"},{"english":"give information on","chinese":"提供關於……的資料"},{"english":"the location and types of","chinese":"……的地點及類型"},{"english":"dance classes","chinese":"舞蹈班"},{"english":"young people in a town","chinese":"一個城鎮的年輕人"},{"english":"a town in Australia","chinese":"澳洲一個城鎮"},{"english":"are currently attending","chinese":"現時正在參加"},{"english":"summarise the information","chinese":"概述資料"},{"english":"by selecting and reporting","chinese":"透過選取並報告……"},{"english":"the main features","chinese":"主要特徵"},{"english":"make comparisons where relevant","chinese":"在相關之處作出比較"},{"english":"the pie chart shows where","chinese":"圓形圖顯示……在哪裏"},{"english":"attend dance classes","chinese":"參加舞蹈班"},{"english":"the bar chart compares","chinese":"柱形圖比較……"},{"english":"the numbers of","chinese":"……的人數"},{"english":"under-11s","chinese":"11歲以下兒童"},{"english":"11- to 16-year-olds","chinese":"11至16歲學生"},{"english":"taking ballet","chinese":"學習芭蕾舞"},{"english":"ballet","chinese":"芭蕾舞"},{"english":"tap","chinese":"踢踏舞"},{"english":"modern dance","chinese":"現代舞"},{"english":"private studios","chinese":"私人舞蹈室"},{"english":"by far the most common","chinese":"遠遠是最常見的"},{"english":"the most common venue","chinese":"最常見場地"},{"english":"accounting for","chinese":"佔……"},{"english":"nearly half of","chinese":"接近一半"},{"english":"all classes","chinese":"所有課堂"},{"english":"whereas","chinese":"而；相反"},{"english":"college-based studios","chinese":"設於學院的舞蹈室"},{"english":"represent the smallest share","chinese":"佔最小比例"},{"english":"the smallest share","chinese":"最小比例"},{"english":"in terms of","chinese":"就……而言"},{"english":"dance style","chinese":"舞蹈類型"},{"english":"the leading choice","chinese":"最主要選擇"},{"english":"among younger children","chinese":"在較年幼兒童之中"},{"english":"more popular with","chinese":"較受……歡迎"},{"english":"the older group","chinese":"較年長組別"},{"english":"attracts broadly similar numbers","chinese":"吸引大致相若的人數"},{"english":"broadly similar numbers","chinese":"大致相若的人數"},{"english":"in both age bands","chinese":"在兩個年齡組別中"},{"english":"looking first at","chinese":"首先看……"},{"english":"are held in","chinese":"在……舉行"},{"english":"exactly twice the proportion","chinese":"比例剛好是……的兩倍"},{"english":"taking place in","chinese":"在……舉行"},{"english":"after-school sessions","chinese":"課後課程"},{"english":"school halls","chinese":"學校禮堂"},{"english":"at 24%","chinese":"為24%"},{"english":"community halls","chinese":"社區會堂"},{"english":"other venues","chinese":"其他場地"},{"english":"make up a further","chinese":"另佔……"},{"english":"leaving X with Y","chinese":"令 X 只佔 Y"},{"english":"only 10%","chinese":"只有10%"},{"english":"around one tenth of","chinese":"約十分之一"},{"english":"the total","chinese":"總數"},{"english":"regarding class types","chinese":"關於課堂類型"},{"english":"about 600 children","chinese":"約600名兒童"},{"english":"children under 11","chinese":"11歲以下兒童"},{"english":"compared with","chinese":"相比之下"},{"english":"roughly 300 students","chinese":"約300名學生"},{"english":"aged 11–16","chinese":"年齡介乎11至16歲"},{"english":"shows the opposite pattern","chinese":"呈現相反模式"},{"english":"the opposite pattern","chinese":"相反模式"},{"english":"just under 300","chinese":"不足300"},{"english":"younger participants","chinese":"較年幼參加者"},{"english":"approximately 520","chinese":"約520"},{"english":"older ones","chinese":"較年長的一批"},{"english":"more evenly balanced","chinese":"分佈較平均"},{"english":"at around 450","chinese":"約為450"},{"english":"slightly over 400","chinese":"略多於400"},{"english":"the older age group","chinese":"較年長年齡組別"},{"english":"class locations","chinese":"課堂地點"},{"english":"class types","chinese":"課堂類型"},{"english":"venue distribution","chinese":"場地分佈"},{"english":"age-group comparison","chinese":"年齡組別比較"},{"english":"dance-class preferences","chinese":"舞蹈班偏好"},{"english":"a clear preference for","chinese":"明顯偏好……"},{"english":"be dominated by","chinese":"由……主導"},{"english":"remain relatively close","chinese":"保持相對接近"},{"english":"the gap between","chinese":"……之間的差距"},{"english":"twice as high as","chinese":"約為……的兩倍"},{"english":"a noticeable contrast","chinese":"明顯對比"}]},"model-essay-2-ielts-task1-pie-charts":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-2-ielts-task1-pie-charts","essayKey":"pie-charts:2","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-2-ielts-task1-pie-charts","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-1/pie-charts/pie-chart-2","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"The six pie charts compare how water is allocated to agriculture, industry and domestic purposes in six regions of the world.","chinese":"六個餅圖比較了世界六個地區的用水如何分配於農業、工業和家庭用途。"},{"label":"Overview","english":"Overall, agriculture dominates water consumption in four of the six regions, particularly Central Asia, Africa and South East Asia. By contrast, industrial use takes the largest share in Europe and North America, while household use remains comparatively small everywhere and never represents the leading category.","chinese":"整體而言，農業在六個地區中的四個地區佔據用水主導地位，尤其是在中亞、非洲和東南亞。 相比之下，工業用途在歐洲和北美佔最大比例，而家庭用水在所有地區都相對較小，並且從未成為主導類別。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"In the two regions where industry is the main user, Europe records the highest industrial proportion, at 53%, slightly above North America’s 48%. Agricultural use is lower in both places, accounting for 32% in Europe and 39% in North America, whereas domestic consumption is modest, at 15% and 13% respectively.","chinese":"在工業是主要用水者的兩個地區中，歐洲的工業用水比例最高，為 53% ，略高於北美的 48% 。 在這兩個地區，農業用水比例都較低，歐洲為 32% ，北美為 39% ；而家庭用水比例則較溫和，分別為 15% 和 13% 。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"The remaining four regions are clearly agriculture-centred. Central Asia has the most pronounced reliance on farming, with 88% of water used for this purpose, followed closely by Africa at 84% and South East Asia at 81%. South America also devotes a large majority to agriculture, at 71%, although its domestic share, 19%, is noticeably higher than in the other agriculture-dominated regions. Industrial use is minimal in these areas, ranging from only 5% in Central Asia to 12% in South East Asia.","chinese":"其餘四個地區明顯以農業用水為中心。 中亞對農業用水的依賴最明顯，有 88% 的水用於此目的，其次是非洲的 84% 和東南亞的 81% 。 南美洲也將絕大部分水用於農業，比例為 71% ；不過其家庭用水比例為 19% ，明顯高於其他以農業為主的地區。 在這些地區，工業用水比例很低，從中亞的僅 5% 到東南亞的 12% 不等。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"six pie charts","chinese":"六個圓形圖"},{"english":"compare how water is allocated to","chinese":"比較水資源如何分配予……"},{"english":"be allocated to","chinese":"被分配予……"},{"english":"agriculture","chinese":"農業"},{"english":"industry","chinese":"工業"},{"english":"domestic purposes","chinese":"家居用途"},{"english":"six regions of the world","chinese":"世界六個地區"},{"english":"dominates water consumption","chinese":"主導用水量"},{"english":"water consumption","chinese":"用水量"},{"english":"in four of the six regions","chinese":"在六個地區中的四個"},{"english":"particularly","chinese":"尤其是"},{"english":"Central Asia","chinese":"中亞"},{"english":"South East Asia","chinese":"東南亞"},{"english":"by contrast","chinese":"相比之下"},{"english":"industrial use","chinese":"工業用水"},{"english":"takes the largest share","chinese":"佔最大比例"},{"english":"household use","chinese":"家居用水"},{"english":"remains comparatively small","chinese":"仍然相對較小"},{"english":"comparatively small","chinese":"相對較小"},{"english":"never represents the leading category","chinese":"從未成為主要類別"},{"english":"leading category","chinese":"主要類別"},{"english":"the main user","chinese":"主要使用者"},{"english":"records the highest industrial proportion","chinese":"錄得最高工業比例"},{"english":"industrial proportion","chinese":"工業比例"},{"english":"at 53%","chinese":"達53%"},{"english":"slightly above","chinese":"略高於"},{"english":"agricultural use","chinese":"農業用水"},{"english":"lower in both places","chinese":"在兩地均較低"},{"english":"in both places","chinese":"在兩地"},{"english":"accounting for","chinese":"佔"},{"english":"whereas","chinese":"而；相比之下"},{"english":"domestic consumption","chinese":"家居用水量"},{"english":"modest","chinese":"不高；有限"},{"english":"respectively","chinese":"分別"},{"english":"the remaining four regions","chinese":"其餘四個地區"},{"english":"agriculture-centred","chinese":"以農業為中心的"},{"english":"the most pronounced reliance on","chinese":"對……最明顯依賴"},{"english":"reliance on farming","chinese":"對農業的依賴"},{"english":"with 88% of water used for this purpose","chinese":"有88%的水用於此用途"},{"english":"used for this purpose","chinese":"用於此用途"},{"english":"followed closely by","chinese":"緊隨其後的是"},{"english":"at 84%","chinese":"達84%"},{"english":"devotes a large majority to","chinese":"將大部分……用於"},{"english":"a large majority","chinese":"大部分"},{"english":"although","chinese":"雖然"},{"english":"domestic share","chinese":"家居用水比例"},{"english":"noticeably higher than","chinese":"明顯高於"},{"english":"agriculture-dominated regions","chinese":"以農業為主的地區"},{"english":"industrial use is minimal","chinese":"工業用水極少"},{"english":"minimal","chinese":"極少的"},{"english":"ranging from…to…","chinese":"介乎……至……"},{"english":"ranging from only 5%","chinese":"由僅5%起"},{"english":"to 12%","chinese":"至12%"},{"english":"these areas","chinese":"這些地區"}]},"model-essay-2-ielts-task1-process-diagram":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-2-ielts-task1-process-diagram","essayKey":"process-diagram:2","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-2-ielts-task1-process-diagram","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-1/process-diagrams/process-diagram-2","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"The diagram illustrates the cyclical process by which the biofuel ethanol is produced from plant material and then used as an energy source.","chinese":"該圖說明生物燃料乙醇如何由植物材料製成，然後被用作能源的循環過程。"},{"label":"Overview","english":"Overall, ethanol production begins with the growth of plants and trees, which use sunlight and carbon dioxide, and ends with ethanol being consumed by vehicles. A key feature is that the carbon dioxide released during use is returned to the atmosphere and can be absorbed by new vegetation, allowing the cycle to continue.","chinese":"整體而言，乙醇的生產始於植物和樹木的生長，它們利用陽光和二氧化碳；最後則以乙醇被交通工具消耗作結。 一個關鍵特徵是，使用過程中釋放出的二氧化碳會回到大氣中，並可被新的植被吸收，使整個循環得以持續。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"In the first stage, plants and trees grow through exposure to sunlight and carbon dioxide. Once mature, they are harvested by machinery and sent for pre-processing, where the raw biomass is prepared. The material is then reduced to cellulose, which is transferred to a processing plant.","chinese":"在第一階段，植物和樹木透過接觸陽光和二氧化碳而生長。 當它們成熟後，會由機械收割，並送往預處理階段，在那裡原始生物質會被準備好。 接著，這些材料會被轉化為纖維素，並被送往加工廠。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"Inside the plant, cellulose is broken down into sugars. Microbes are subsequently added to these sugars, and this biological stage converts them into ethanol. The finished fuel is then distributed for use in transport, including cars, lorries and aircraft. As these vehicles consume ethanol, carbon dioxide is emitted; this gas then becomes part of the next growing stage when it is taken up again by plants and trees.","chinese":"在加工廠內，纖維素會被分解成糖。 隨後，微生物會被加入這些糖中，而這一生物階段會把它們轉化為乙醇。 完成後的燃料接著會被分配到交通運輸中使用，包括汽車、貨車和飛機。 當這些交通工具消耗乙醇時，二氧化碳會被排放出來；之後，這種氣體會在再次被植物和樹木吸收時，成為下一個生長階段的一部分。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"diagram illustrates","chinese":"圖示說明"},{"english":"cyclical process","chinese":"循環過程"},{"english":"by which","chinese":"藉此；通過這個方式"},{"english":"biofuel ethanol","chinese":"生物燃料乙醇"},{"english":"is produced from","chinese":"由……生產"},{"english":"plant material","chinese":"植物材料"},{"english":"used as an energy source","chinese":"用作能源"},{"english":"energy source","chinese":"能源"},{"english":"ethanol production","chinese":"乙醇生產"},{"english":"begins with","chinese":"以……開始"},{"english":"the growth of plants and trees","chinese":"植物及樹木的生長"},{"english":"carbon dioxide","chinese":"二氧化碳"},{"english":"ends with","chinese":"以……結束"},{"english":"being consumed by vehicles","chinese":"被車輛消耗"},{"english":"a key feature is that","chinese":"一個主要特點是"},{"english":"released during use","chinese":"在使用期間釋放"},{"english":"returned to the atmosphere","chinese":"返回大氣層"},{"english":"atmosphere","chinese":"大氣層"},{"english":"absorbed by new vegetation","chinese":"被新植被吸收"},{"english":"new vegetation","chinese":"新植被"},{"english":"allowing the cycle to continue","chinese":"使循環得以延續"},{"english":"the cycle to continue","chinese":"循環延續"},{"english":"in the first stage","chinese":"在第一階段"},{"english":"grow through exposure to","chinese":"通過接觸……而生長"},{"english":"exposure to sunlight","chinese":"接觸陽光"},{"english":"once mature","chinese":"成熟後"},{"english":"are harvested by machinery","chinese":"由機器收割"},{"english":"machinery","chinese":"機器；機械"},{"english":"sent for pre-processing","chinese":"被送往預處理"},{"english":"pre-processing","chinese":"預處理"},{"english":"raw biomass","chinese":"原始生物質"},{"english":"is prepared","chinese":"被準備；被處理"},{"english":"is reduced to cellulose","chinese":"被分解成纖維素"},{"english":"cellulose","chinese":"纖維素"},{"english":"transferred to","chinese":"被轉移至"},{"english":"processing plant","chinese":"加工廠"},{"english":"inside the plant","chinese":"在工廠內"},{"english":"broken down into","chinese":"被分解成"},{"english":"sugars","chinese":"糖分"},{"english":"microbes","chinese":"微生物"},{"english":"are subsequently added to","chinese":"隨後被加入……"},{"english":"subsequently","chinese":"隨後"},{"english":"biological stage","chinese":"生物階段"},{"english":"converts them into","chinese":"將它們轉化成"},{"english":"finished fuel","chinese":"製成的燃料"},{"english":"distributed for use in transport","chinese":"被分發作交通用途"},{"english":"transport","chinese":"交通運輸"},{"english":"including cars, lorries and aircraft","chinese":"包括汽車、貨車及飛機"},{"english":"lorries","chinese":"貨車"},{"english":"aircraft","chinese":"飛機"},{"english":"consume ethanol","chinese":"消耗乙醇"},{"english":"is emitted","chinese":"被排放"},{"english":"becomes part of","chinese":"成為……的一部分"},{"english":"the next growing stage","chinese":"下一個生長階段"},{"english":"taken up again by","chinese":"再次被……吸收"},{"english":"process diagram","chinese":"流程圖"},{"english":"production cycle","chinese":"生產循環"},{"english":"renewable fuel","chinese":"可再生燃料"},{"english":"carbon cycle","chinese":"碳循環"}]},"model-essay-2-ielts-task1-tables":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-2-ielts-task1-tables","essayKey":"tables:2","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-2-ielts-task1-tables","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-1/tables/table-2","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"The tables compare sales of Fairtrade-labelled coffee and bananas, measured in millions of euros, in five European countries in 1999 and 2004.","chinese":"這些表格比較了 1999 年和 2004 年五個歐洲國家的公平貿易標籤咖啡和香蕉銷售額，單位為百萬歐元。"},{"label":"Overview","english":"Overall, coffee sales increased in every market, with the UK recording by far the most striking rise and becoming the leading purchaser by 2004. Banana sales showed a less even pattern: Switzerland remained dominant and grew sharply, whereas Sweden and Denmark experienced declines.","chinese":"整體而言，咖啡銷售額在每個市場都有上升，其中英國的升幅最為顯著，並在 2004 年成為最大的購買國。 香蕉銷售額的變化則沒有那麼一致：瑞士仍然佔主導地位並大幅增長，而瑞典和丹麥則出現下降。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"Regarding coffee, Switzerland had the highest figure in 1999, at 3 million euros, followed by Denmark at 1.8 million and the UK at 1.5 million. By 2004, however, the UK had surged to 20 million euros, more than three times Switzerland’s figure of 6 million. The remaining countries saw only modest growth, with Denmark edging up to 2 million, Belgium to 1.7 million and Sweden to 1 million.","chinese":"就咖啡而言，瑞士在 1999 年的銷售額最高，為 300 萬歐元，其次是丹麥的 180 萬歐元和英國的 150 萬歐元。 然而，到 2004 年，英國銷售額激增至 2,000 萬歐元，是瑞士 600 萬歐元的三倍多。 其餘國家只錄得溫和增長，其中丹麥微升至 200 萬歐元，比利時升至 170 萬歐元，瑞典則升至 100 萬歐元。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"Banana sales were led by Switzerland in both years, rising from 15 to 47 million euros, which was far ahead of all other markets. The UK and Belgium also increased substantially, reaching 5.5 million and 4 million respectively in 2004. By contrast, Sweden fell from 1.8 to 1 million, while Denmark dropped from 2 to 0.9 million, becoming the smallest market.","chinese":"香蕉銷售額在兩個年份都由瑞士領先，從 1,500 萬歐元上升至 4,700 萬歐元，遠高於所有其他市場。 英國和比利時也大幅增長，在 2004 年分別達到 550 萬歐元和 400 萬歐元。 相比之下，瑞典從 180 萬歐元下降至 100 萬歐元，而丹麥則從 200 萬歐元跌至 90萬歐元，成為最小的市場。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"give information about","chinese":"提供關於……的資料"},{"english":"sales of","chinese":"……的銷售額"},{"english":"Fairtrade-labelled coffee","chinese":"貼有公平貿易標籤的咖啡"},{"english":"Fairtrade-labelled bananas","chinese":"貼有公平貿易標籤的香蕉"},{"english":"in 1999 and 2004","chinese":"在1999年和2004年"},{"english":"five European countries","chinese":"五個歐洲國家"},{"english":"summarise the information","chinese":"概述資料"},{"english":"selecting and reporting","chinese":"選取並報告"},{"english":"the main features","chinese":"主要特徵"},{"english":"make comparisons where relevant","chinese":"在相關之處作出比較"},{"english":"the tables compare","chinese":"表格比較"},{"english":"measured in millions of euros","chinese":"以百萬歐元計算"},{"english":"millions of euros","chinese":"百萬歐元"},{"english":"Overall","chinese":"整體而言"},{"english":"coffee sales","chinese":"咖啡銷售額"},{"english":"increased in every market","chinese":"在每個市場均上升"},{"english":"every market","chinese":"每個市場"},{"english":"with the UK recording","chinese":"其中英國錄得"},{"english":"by far the most striking rise","chinese":"遠遠最顯著的升幅"},{"english":"the most striking rise","chinese":"最顯著的升幅"},{"english":"becoming the leading purchaser","chinese":"成為最大購買國"},{"english":"the leading purchaser","chinese":"最大購買國"},{"english":"by 2004","chinese":"到2004年"},{"english":"banana sales","chinese":"香蕉銷售額"},{"english":"showed a less even pattern","chinese":"呈現較不平均的模式"},{"english":"a less even pattern","chinese":"較不平均的模式"},{"english":"remained dominant","chinese":"仍然佔主導地位"},{"english":"grew sharply","chinese":"大幅增長"},{"english":"whereas","chinese":"而；相比之下"},{"english":"experienced declines","chinese":"經歷下跌"},{"english":"Regarding coffee","chinese":"至於咖啡方面"},{"english":"had the highest figure","chinese":"數字最高"},{"english":"the highest figure","chinese":"最高數字"},{"english":"at 3 million euros","chinese":"為300萬歐元"},{"english":"followed by","chinese":"其次是"},{"english":"at 1.8 million","chinese":"為180萬"},{"english":"at 1.5 million","chinese":"為150萬"},{"english":"however","chinese":"然而"},{"english":"had surged to","chinese":"已急升至"},{"english":"20 million euros","chinese":"2,000萬歐元"},{"english":"more than three times","chinese":"超過三倍"},{"english":"Switzerland's figure","chinese":"瑞士的數字"},{"english":"the remaining countries","chinese":"其餘國家"},{"english":"saw only modest growth","chinese":"只錄得溫和增長"},{"english":"modest growth","chinese":"溫和增長"},{"english":"edging up to","chinese":"輕微上升至"},{"english":"Belgium","chinese":"比利時"},{"english":"Sweden","chinese":"瑞典"},{"english":"Banana sales were led by","chinese":"香蕉銷售由……領先"},{"english":"in both years","chinese":"在兩年中"},{"english":"rising from … to …","chinese":"由……上升至……"},{"english":"from 15 to 47 million euros","chinese":"由1,500萬歐元升至4,700萬歐元"},{"english":"far ahead of","chinese":"遠遠領先於"},{"english":"all other markets","chinese":"所有其他市場"},{"english":"also increased substantially","chinese":"亦大幅增加"},{"english":"increased substantially","chinese":"大幅增加"},{"english":"reaching 5.5 million","chinese":"達到550萬"},{"english":"reaching 4 million respectively","chinese":"分別達到400萬"},{"english":"respectively","chinese":"分別"},{"english":"By contrast","chinese":"相比之下"},{"english":"fell from … to …","chinese":"由……跌至……"},{"english":"from 1.8 to 1 million","chinese":"由180萬跌至100萬"},{"english":"while","chinese":"而"},{"english":"dropped from … to …","chinese":"由……下降至……"},{"english":"from 2 to 0.9 million","chinese":"由200萬跌至90萬"},{"english":"becoming the smallest market","chinese":"成為最小的市場"},{"english":"the smallest market","chinese":"最小的市場"}]},"model-essay-3-ielts-advantage-disadvantage":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-3-ielts-advantage-disadvantage","essayKey":"advantage-disadvantage:3","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-3-ielts-advantage-disadvantage","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/advantage-and-disadvantage/EdmundBd9AdDisAd-Q3","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"It has become increasingly common for school-leavers to spend a gap year doing charitable work in less developed countries before entering university. Although this choice can create emotional and academic difficulties, it is ultimately a highly positive experience for young people because it develops maturity and gives them a far deeper understanding of society than a conventional year at home would.","chinese":"在進入大學前先花一年到海外從事慈善工作，已愈來愈成為離校生常見的選擇。 雖然這個決定可能帶來情緒壓力，並打亂原有的學習習慣， 本文將論證，這樣的經歷對年輕人而言最終是有益的，因為它能加速個人成長，並加深他們對社會的理解。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"The primary advantage is accelerated personal growth. When young volunteers live abroad, they must budget, solve practical problems and communicate in unfamiliar settings without the daily support of parents or teachers. This pushes them to become more self-reliant, adaptable and resilient, which are precisely the qualities needed for university life and later employment. A student helping to organise food distribution, for example, may need to cope with transport failures, limited resources and language barriers on a daily basis. A second benefit is the way such work broadens moral and intellectual perspective. Seeing inadequate schooling, poor sanitation or limited medical care at first hand turns abstract global issues into concrete human realities. As a result, many young people become more socially aware and more purposeful about their future. Someone who assists in a rural clinic, for instance, may return home determined to study medicine, public health or international development.","chinese":"到海外從事義工工作的第一個優點，是它能促進快速的個人成長。 生活在一個陌生的國家，會迫使年輕人自己管理金錢、處理日常問題，並在沒有父母或老師持續支援的情況下獨立與人溝通。 因此，他們會變得更獨立、更有適應力，也更堅韌，而這些正是大學生活及未來就業所必需的特質。 例如，一名協助安排糧食分發的學生，可能每天都要處理交通失誤、資源不足以及語言障礙。 義工工作也能擴闊年輕人的道德與思想視野。 親眼看到教育體系薄弱、衛生條件惡劣或醫療資源不足，會把抽象的全球問題轉化為具體的人類現實。 這往往會使義工變得更有社會意識，也更清楚自己未來的人生方向。 例如，一位在鄉村診所幫忙的人，回國後可能會下定決心修讀醫學、公共衛生或國際發展。 基於以上原因，義工工作能在個人層面與思想層面同時令年輕人受益。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"However, there are undeniable disadvantages. One is the emotional strain of working in communities affected by poverty, illness or trauma. Many teenagers are still psychologically inexperienced, so constant exposure to suffering can leave them distressed, guilty or overwhelmed rather than inspired. A volunteer in an orphanage, for example, may form strong attachments and then find the eventual separation deeply upsetting. Another drawback is that a gap year can weaken academic momentum. After spending many months outside formal education, some students struggle to readjust to lectures, deadlines and examinations, especially when university courses demand intense concentration from the outset. For example, a school-leaver who has spent a year on construction or community projects may find essay writing and exam preparation unexpectedly difficult on returning to study.","chinese":"然而，主要的缺點在於情緒壓力與學業中斷。 在受貧窮、疾病或創傷影響的社區工作，對於心理上仍未成熟的青少年而言，可能會造成沉重的心理負擔。 長期接觸苦難，可能不會令他們受到鼓舞，反而會使他們感到痛苦、內疚或不堪負荷。 例如，一名在孤兒院服務的義工，可能會與孩子建立深厚感情，而最終的分離則會令他十分難受。 空檔年也可能削弱原有的學習節奏。 在離開正規教育數月之後，有些學生在大學開始時，會難以重新適應講課、截止日期和考試。 尤其當學位課程一開始就要求高度專注與嚴格的學習習慣時，這種情況更為明顯。 例如，一名把一年時間投入建設或社區項目的畢業生，在回到校園後，可能會發現寫論文與準備考試比預期更困難。 即便如此，這些缺點仍不足以蓋過這段經歷的長遠價值。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, volunteering abroad is not an easy option for young people, as it can be emotionally demanding and can interrupt study habits. Even so, it remains a profoundly worthwhile experience, since few alternatives cultivate independence, perspective and long-term purpose so effectively.","chinese":"總而言之，我認為在空檔年到海外從事義工工作，對年輕人而言最終是利大於弊的。 雖然它可能帶來情緒壓力並打斷學習習慣，但它能培養獨立性、韌性與社會意識，而這些往往是一般經歷難以帶來的。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"increasingly common for","chinese":"對……來說越來越常見"},{"english":"school-leavers","chinese":"中學畢業生"},{"english":"spend a gap year","chinese":"度過空檔年"},{"english":"charitable work","chinese":"慈善工作"},{"english":"less developed countries","chinese":"發展程度較低的國家"},{"english":"before entering university","chinese":"入讀大學之前"},{"english":"this choice","chinese":"這個選擇"},{"english":"emotional and academic difficulties","chinese":"情緒和學業上的困難"},{"english":"ultimately","chinese":"最終"},{"english":"a highly positive experience","chinese":"非常正面的經歷"},{"english":"develops maturity","chinese":"培養成熟度"},{"english":"gives them a far deeper understanding of","chinese":"令他們對……有深入得多的理解"},{"english":"a conventional year at home","chinese":"傳統留在本地的一年"},{"english":"the primary advantage","chinese":"主要好處"},{"english":"accelerated personal growth","chinese":"加速的個人成長"},{"english":"live abroad","chinese":"在海外生活"},{"english":"budget","chinese":"管理預算"},{"english":"solve practical problems","chinese":"解決實際問題"},{"english":"unfamiliar settings","chinese":"陌生環境"},{"english":"without the daily support of","chinese":"沒有……的日常支援"},{"english":"pushes them to become","chinese":"推動他們變得"},{"english":"self-reliant","chinese":"自力更生"},{"english":"adaptable","chinese":"適應力強的"},{"english":"resilient","chinese":"有抗逆力的"},{"english":"precisely the qualities needed for","chinese":"正正是……所需要的素質"},{"english":"university life","chinese":"大學生活"},{"english":"later employment","chinese":"日後就業"},{"english":"helping to organise","chinese":"協助組織"},{"english":"food distribution","chinese":"食物派發"},{"english":"cope with","chinese":"應付"},{"english":"transport failures","chinese":"交通失誤；交通安排出問題"},{"english":"limited resources","chinese":"有限資源"},{"english":"language barriers","chinese":"語言障礙"},{"english":"on a daily basis","chinese":"每日；日常地"},{"english":"a second benefit","chinese":"第二個好處"},{"english":"broadens moral and intellectual perspective","chinese":"擴闊道德和思想視野"},{"english":"inadequate schooling","chinese":"不足的學校教育"},{"english":"poor sanitation","chinese":"惡劣衞生環境"},{"english":"limited medical care","chinese":"有限醫療服務"},{"english":"at first hand","chinese":"親身"},{"english":"abstract global issues","chinese":"抽象的全球議題"},{"english":"concrete human realities","chinese":"具體的人類現實"},{"english":"as a result","chinese":"因此"},{"english":"socially aware","chinese":"有社會意識的"},{"english":"more purposeful about","chinese":"對……更有目標"},{"english":"assists in","chinese":"在……協助"},{"english":"a rural clinic","chinese":"鄉村診所"},{"english":"return home determined to","chinese":"回家後決心去……"},{"english":"public health","chinese":"公共衞生"},{"english":"international development","chinese":"國際發展"},{"english":"undeniable disadvantages","chinese":"無可否認的缺點"},{"english":"emotional strain","chinese":"情緒壓力"},{"english":"communities affected by","chinese":"受……影響的社區"},{"english":"poverty, illness or trauma","chinese":"貧窮、疾病或創傷"},{"english":"psychologically inexperienced","chinese":"心理上仍缺乏經驗"},{"english":"constant exposure to","chinese":"持續接觸……"},{"english":"suffering","chinese":"苦難"},{"english":"leave them distressed","chinese":"令他們感到痛苦"},{"english":"guilty or overwhelmed","chinese":"愧疚或不知所措"},{"english":"rather than inspired","chinese":"而不是受到啟發"},{"english":"form strong attachments","chinese":"建立深厚感情"},{"english":"an orphanage","chinese":"孤兒院"},{"english":"eventual separation","chinese":"最終分離"},{"english":"deeply upsetting","chinese":"令人非常難過"},{"english":"another drawback","chinese":"另一個缺點"},{"english":"weaken academic momentum","chinese":"削弱學習動力和節奏"},{"english":"outside formal education","chinese":"在正規教育之外"},{"english":"struggle to readjust to","chinese":"難以重新適應"},{"english":"lectures, deadlines and examinations","chinese":"講課、限期和考試"},{"english":"demand intense concentration","chinese":"要求高度專注"},{"english":"from the outset","chinese":"從一開始"},{"english":"construction or community projects","chinese":"建築或社區項目"},{"english":"essay writing","chinese":"文章寫作"},{"english":"exam preparation","chinese":"考試準備"},{"english":"unexpectedly difficult","chinese":"出乎意料地困難"},{"english":"returning to study","chinese":"重返學習"},{"english":"not an easy option","chinese":"不是輕鬆的選擇"},{"english":"emotionally demanding","chinese":"情緒上要求很高的"},{"english":"interrupt study habits","chinese":"打斷學習習慣"},{"english":"even so","chinese":"即使如此"},{"english":"profoundly worthwhile","chinese":"非常值得的"},{"english":"few alternatives","chinese":"很少其他選擇"},{"english":"cultivate independence","chinese":"培養獨立性"},{"english":"long-term purpose","chinese":"長遠目標感"},{"english":"so effectively","chinese":"如此有效地"}]},"model-essay-3-ielts-cause-solution":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-3-ielts-cause-solution","essayKey":"cause-solution:3","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-3-ielts-cause-solution","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/problem-and-cause/EdmundBd9CnS-Q3","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"The gap between wealthy and impoverished nations has widened in many parts of the world, creating a cycle in which prosperity attracts more prosperity while poverty becomes harder to escape. The main cause of this problem is the unequal access countries have to the systems that create long-term wealth. This essay will explain this cause and suggest practical ways to address it.","chinese":"在世界許多地方，富裕國家與貧困國家之間的差距已經擴大，形成了一種富裕吸引更多富裕、而貧困變得更難擺脫的循環。 這個問題的主要原因是，各國在取得能夠創造長期財富的系統方面存在不平等。 本文將解釋這個原因，並提出實際可行的方法來處理這個問題。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"The central reason is that rich countries usually possess better education systems, stronger institutions, advanced technology and easier access to investment. These advantages allow them to produce high-value goods and services, such as medicines, software and financial products, which generate large profits. Poor countries, by contrast, often depend on exporting raw materials or low-paid labour. As a result, they earn less, collect less tax and struggle to build the roads, schools and hospitals that would help them compete. This becomes a vicious circle: the less a country can invest in its people and infrastructure, the harder it is for that country to move beyond survival and into genuine development.","chinese":"核心原因是，富裕國家通常擁有更好的教育制度、更強大的制度、先進科技，以及更容易取得投資的渠道。 這些優勢使它們能夠生產高價值的商品和服務，例如藥物、軟件和金融產品，而這些都能創造龐大利潤。 相比之下，貧困國家往往依賴出口原材料或低薪勞動力。 結果是，它們賺得更少、徵收的稅收更少，也難以建設能幫助它們競爭的道路、學校和醫院。 這便形成了一個惡性循環：一個國家越無法投資於人民和基礎建設，它就越難從僅僅維持生存，走向真正的發展。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"To reduce this gap, both international reform and domestic improvement are needed. Wealthier countries and global institutions should make trade rules fairer, reduce unfair debt burdens and support poorer nations with targeted investment in education, healthcare and clean infrastructure. This would give developing economies the tools to grow rather than leaving them permanently dependent on aid. At the same time, governments in poorer countries must strengthen transparency, reduce corruption and invest public money in industries that can create skilled employment. For example, supporting vocational training and small local businesses can help workers move from unstable informal jobs into more productive work. In this way, aid becomes a stepping stone, not a crutch.","chinese":"要縮小這個差距，國際層面的改革和國內層面的改善都是必要的。 較富裕的國家和全球機構應該使貿易規則更加公平、減少不公平的債務負擔，並透過針對教育、醫療和清潔基礎建設的投資來支持較貧困的國家。 這將給予發展中經濟體成長所需的工具，而不是讓它們永久依賴援助。 與此同時，貧困國家的政府必須加強透明度、減少貪污，並把公共資金投放於能夠創造技術型就業的產業。 例如，支持職業培訓和本地小型企業，可以幫助工人從不穩定的非正式工作轉向更具生產力的工作。 這樣一來，援助便會成為踏腳石，而不是拐杖。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, the widening wealth gap is mainly caused by unequal access to education, technology, capital and stable institutions. It can be reduced through fairer global rules, responsible investment and stronger domestic governance.","chinese":"總結來說，財富差距擴大的主要原因，是各國在取得教育、科技、資本和穩定制度方面存在不平等。 這個問題可以透過更公平的全球規則、負責任的投資，以及更強大的國內治理來減輕。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"the gap between","chinese":"……之間的差距"},{"english":"wealthy and impoverished nations","chinese":"富裕國家和貧困國家"},{"english":"has widened","chinese":"已經擴大"},{"english":"creating a cycle","chinese":"形成一個循環"},{"english":"prosperity attracts more prosperity","chinese":"繁榮吸引更多繁榮"},{"english":"harder to escape","chinese":"更難擺脫"},{"english":"the main cause of","chinese":"……的主要原因"},{"english":"unequal access to","chinese":"不平等地獲得……的機會"},{"english":"the systems that create long-term wealth","chinese":"創造長遠財富的系統"},{"english":"practical ways to address it","chinese":"處理它的實際方法"},{"english":"the central reason","chinese":"核心原因"},{"english":"possess better education systems","chinese":"擁有較好的教育制度"},{"english":"stronger institutions","chinese":"更健全的制度"},{"english":"advanced technology","chinese":"先進科技"},{"english":"easier access to investment","chinese":"較容易獲得投資"},{"english":"these advantages","chinese":"這些優勢"},{"english":"allow them to","chinese":"讓他們能夠"},{"english":"high-value goods and services","chinese":"高價值商品和服務"},{"english":"financial products","chinese":"金融產品"},{"english":"generate large profits","chinese":"產生巨額利潤"},{"english":"by contrast","chinese":"相比之下"},{"english":"depend on exporting","chinese":"依賴出口"},{"english":"raw materials","chinese":"原材料"},{"english":"low-paid labour","chinese":"低薪勞工"},{"english":"as a result","chinese":"因此；結果"},{"english":"collect less tax","chinese":"收取較少稅款"},{"english":"struggle to build","chinese":"難以建設"},{"english":"help them compete","chinese":"幫助他們競爭"},{"english":"a vicious circle","chinese":"惡性循環"},{"english":"invest in its people and infrastructure","chinese":"投資於人民和基礎設施"},{"english":"move beyond survival","chinese":"超越僅僅維持生存的階段"},{"english":"genuine development","chinese":"真正發展"},{"english":"reduce this gap","chinese":"縮小這個差距"},{"english":"international reform","chinese":"國際改革"},{"english":"domestic improvement","chinese":"國內改善"},{"english":"global institutions","chinese":"全球機構"},{"english":"make trade rules fairer","chinese":"令貿易規則更公平"},{"english":"reduce unfair debt burdens","chinese":"減輕不公平的債務負擔"},{"english":"targeted investment in","chinese":"對……的針對性投資"},{"english":"clean infrastructure","chinese":"清潔基礎設施"},{"english":"developing economies","chinese":"發展中經濟體"},{"english":"the tools to grow","chinese":"增長所需的工具"},{"english":"rather than leaving them","chinese":"而不是令它們……"},{"english":"permanently dependent on aid","chinese":"長期依賴援助"},{"english":"at the same time","chinese":"與此同時"},{"english":"strengthen transparency","chinese":"加強透明度"},{"english":"reduce corruption","chinese":"減少貪污"},{"english":"invest public money in","chinese":"將公帑投資於……"},{"english":"skilled employment","chinese":"技術型就業"},{"english":"vocational training","chinese":"職業培訓"},{"english":"small local businesses","chinese":"小型本地企業"},{"english":"unstable informal jobs","chinese":"不穩定的非正式工作"},{"english":"more productive work","chinese":"生產力更高的工作"},{"english":"in this way","chinese":"這樣一來"},{"english":"a stepping stone, not a crutch","chinese":"踏腳石，而不是拐杖"},{"english":"the widening wealth gap","chinese":"不斷擴大的財富差距"},{"english":"capital","chinese":"資本"},{"english":"stable institutions","chinese":"穩定制度"},{"english":"fairer global rules","chinese":"更公平的全球規則"},{"english":"responsible investment","chinese":"負責任的投資"},{"english":"stronger domestic governance","chinese":"更強的國內治理"}]},"model-essay-3-ielts-direct-question":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-3-ielts-direct-question","essayKey":"direct-question:3","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-3-ielts-direct-question","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/direct-question/EdmundBd9Dir-Q3","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"Many organisations require employees to wear a standard uniform whenever they are on duty. Although this may seem like a simple rule about clothing, it can serve several important business purposes and can also make daily working life easier for employees.","chinese":"許多機構要求員工在值班時必須穿著標準制服。 儘管這看起來可能只是一項關於服裝的簡單規定，但它可以服務於幾個重要的商業目的，也可以讓員工的日常工作生活變得更容易。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"For companies, the clearest advantage is that uniforms create a consistent and professional public image. When customers see staff dressed in the same recognisable way, the business appears more organised, reliable and trustworthy. This is especially important in service industries such as hotels, airlines and restaurants, where first impressions can shape the customer’s view of the whole company. A uniform also makes employees easy to identify. As a result, customers can ask for help more quickly, managers can supervise the workplace more efficiently, and outsiders are less likely to enter restricted areas unnoticed. In jobs involving food, healthcare or machinery, a uniform can also support hygiene and safety because workers are dressed in clothing designed for that particular environment.","chinese":"對公司而言，最明顯的優點是制服能夠塑造一致而專業的公眾形象。 當顧客看到員工以同樣容易識別的方式穿著時，該企業會顯得更有組織、更可靠，也更值得信任。 這在酒店、航空公司和餐廳等服務行業中尤其重要，因為第一印象可以塑造顧客對整間公司的看法。 制服也讓員工容易被識別。 因此，顧客可以更快尋求幫助，管理人員可以更有效率地監督工作場所，而外來人士也較不可能在未被察覺的情況下進入限制區域。 在涉及食品、醫療或機械的工作中，制服也可以支持衛生和安全，因為員工穿著的是為該特定環境而設計的服裝。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"There are clear benefits for staff as well. First, uniforms remove the daily pressure of deciding what to wear and reduce the need to spend money on fashionable or work-appropriate clothes. This is a practical advantage, particularly for lower-paid employees who might otherwise feel judged by their appearance. Secondly, uniforms can create a stronger sense of equality and belonging. When everyone wears similar clothing, differences in wealth, taste or social background become less visible, and staff may feel that they are part of the same team. In addition, well-designed uniforms can be comfortable and protective, allowing employees to focus on their tasks rather than on their clothing.","chinese":"對員工而言，也有明顯的好處。 首先，制服消除了每天決定穿甚麼的壓力，也減少了在時尚服裝或適合工作的服裝上花錢的需要。 這是一個實際的優點，尤其是對收入較低的員工而言，否則他們可能會因自己的外表而感到被評價。 其次，制服可以創造更強的平等感和歸屬感。 當每個人穿著相似的服裝時，財富、品味或社會背景上的差異會變得較不明顯，而員工也可能會覺得自己是同一個團隊的一部分。 此外，設計良好的制服可以既舒適又具保護性，讓員工能夠專注於自己的工作任務，而不是自己的衣著。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, uniforms benefit companies by strengthening brand image, improving identification and supporting workplace control. They can also benefit employees by saving time and money, reducing social pressure and encouraging a shared sense of professionalism.","chinese":"總結來說，制服透過強化品牌形象、改善識別度和支持工作場所管理，為公司帶來好處 它們也可以透過節省時間和金錢、減少社交壓力，以及鼓勵共同的專業意識，為員工帶來好處。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"require employees to","chinese":"要求員工去"},{"english":"a standard uniform","chinese":"標準制服"},{"english":"on duty","chinese":"當值；值勤"},{"english":"may seem like","chinese":"可能看似"},{"english":"a simple rule about clothing","chinese":"關於衣着的簡單規則"},{"english":"serve several important business purposes","chinese":"發揮幾個重要商業作用"},{"english":"daily working life","chinese":"日常工作生活"},{"english":"the clearest advantage","chinese":"最明顯的好處"},{"english":"create a consistent and professional public image","chinese":"建立一致而專業的公眾形象"},{"english":"dressed in the same recognisable way","chinese":"以相同而容易辨認的方式穿着"},{"english":"appears more organised","chinese":"顯得更有組織"},{"english":"reliable and trustworthy","chinese":"可靠而值得信任"},{"english":"service industries","chinese":"服務行業"},{"english":"first impressions","chinese":"第一印象"},{"english":"shape the customer's view of","chinese":"塑造顧客對……的看法"},{"english":"the whole company","chinese":"整間公司"},{"english":"easy to identify","chinese":"容易辨認"},{"english":"as a result","chinese":"因此"},{"english":"ask for help more quickly","chinese":"更快尋求協助"},{"english":"supervise the workplace more efficiently","chinese":"更有效率地監督工作場所"},{"english":"outsiders","chinese":"外來人士"},{"english":"restricted areas","chinese":"限制進入區域"},{"english":"enter restricted areas unnoticed","chinese":"未被察覺地進入限制區域"},{"english":"jobs involving food, healthcare or machinery","chinese":"涉及食物、醫療或機械的工作"},{"english":"support hygiene and safety","chinese":"支持衞生和安全"},{"english":"designed for","chinese":"為……而設計"},{"english":"that particular environment","chinese":"該特定環境"},{"english":"benefits for staff","chinese":"對員工的好處"},{"english":"remove the daily pressure of","chinese":"消除每日……的壓力"},{"english":"deciding what to wear","chinese":"決定穿甚麼"},{"english":"reduce the need to","chinese":"減少……的需要"},{"english":"spend money on","chinese":"花錢在……上"},{"english":"fashionable clothes","chinese":"時尚衣服"},{"english":"work-appropriate clothes","chinese":"適合工作的衣服"},{"english":"a practical advantage","chinese":"實際好處"},{"english":"lower-paid employees","chinese":"薪酬較低的員工"},{"english":"might otherwise feel judged by","chinese":"否則可能因……而覺得被評頭品足"},{"english":"their appearance","chinese":"他們的外表"},{"english":"create a stronger sense of equality","chinese":"建立更強的平等感"},{"english":"belonging","chinese":"歸屬感"},{"english":"similar clothing","chinese":"相似的衣着"},{"english":"differences in wealth","chinese":"財富差異"},{"english":"taste or social background","chinese":"品味或社會背景"},{"english":"become less visible","chinese":"變得較不明顯"},{"english":"part of the same team","chinese":"同一團隊的一分子"},{"english":"well-designed uniforms","chinese":"設計良好的制服"},{"english":"comfortable and protective","chinese":"舒適並具保護作用"},{"english":"allowing employees to","chinese":"讓員工能夠"},{"english":"focus on their tasks","chinese":"專注於工作任務"},{"english":"rather than on their clothing","chinese":"而不是放在衣着上"},{"english":"strengthening brand image","chinese":"加強品牌形象"},{"english":"improving identification","chinese":"改善識別度"},{"english":"supporting workplace control","chinese":"支持工作場所管理"},{"english":"saving time and money","chinese":"節省時間和金錢"},{"english":"reducing social pressure","chinese":"減少社交壓力"},{"english":"encouraging a shared sense of professionalism","chinese":"鼓勵共同的專業感"}]},"model-essay-3-ielts-opinion":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-3-ielts-opinion","essayKey":"opinion:3","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-3-ielts-opinion","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/opinions/EdmundBd9OP-Q3","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"Museums and galleries help shape how the public understands art, history and cultural identity. Some people therefore argue that these institutions should display only local artists instead of showing work from other countries. This essay strongly disagrees with that view because international collections broaden public understanding and also strengthen the long-term development of local art.","chinese":"博物館和美術館有助塑造公眾如何理解藝術、歷史和文化身分認同。 因此，有些人主張這些機構應只展示本地藝術家，而不應展出其他國家的作品。 本文強烈不同意這種看法。 因為國際館藏既能擴闊公眾理解，也能加強本地藝術的長遠發展。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"Showing foreign work makes museums far more educational. First, if visitors see only domestic traditions, their understanding of art becomes narrow because they have no meaningful basis for comparison. When a gallery places local painting beside Japanese prints or African sculpture, for example, students can immediately see how different cultures use colour, symbolism and form to express similar human concerns. Second, exposure to international art can deepen social understanding. Works produced in other societies often reflect war, migration, religion or inequality, so encountering them helps viewers appreciate experiences beyond their own environment. For that reason, excluding foreign art would reduce both the intellectual and the cultural value of museums.","chinese":"展示外國作品會使博物館變得更具教育意義。 第一，如果參觀者只看到本國傳統，他們對藝術的理解便會變得狹窄，因為他們沒有有意義的比較基礎。 當美術館把本地繪畫與日本版畫或非洲雕塑並列展示時，例如，學生便能立即看見不同文化如何運用色彩、象徵和形式來表達相似的人類關懷。 第二，接觸國際藝術能加深社會理解。 其他社會所創作的作品往往反映戰爭、遷徙、宗教或不平等，因此接觸這些作品能幫助觀眾理解自己環境以外的經驗。 正因如此，排除外國藝術會削弱博物館在知識和文化上的價值。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"Displaying international art also benefits local artists and the institutions that support them. First, artists improve when they are challenged by unfamiliar techniques and artistic philosophies. If museums show only local work, the creative environment can become repetitive; by contrast, exposure to outside influences encourages painters, sculptors and photographers to refine their methods and produce more original work. A young artist who studies European modernism, for instance, may return to local subjects with fresher ways of representing light, space or emotion. Second, varied exhibitions attract broader audiences and keep galleries vibrant. When institutions alternate local shows with international ones, they draw more students, critics and repeat visitors, who then become more likely to discover local talent as well.","chinese":"展出國際藝術也能使本地藝術家及支持他們的機構受益。 第一，當藝術家受到陌生技法和藝術理念的挑戰時，他們便會進步。 如果博物館只展示本地作品，創作環境可能會變得重複乏味；相反，接觸外來影響會鼓勵畫家、雕塑家和攝影師精煉自己的方法，並創作出更原創的作品。 例如，一位研究歐洲現代主義的年輕藝術家，可能會以更新鮮的方式回到本地題材，去表現光線、空間或情感。 第二，多元展覽會吸引更廣泛的觀眾，並使美術館保持活力。 當機構把本地展覽與國際展覽交替安排時，它們會吸引更多學生、評論家和回流觀眾，而這些人之後也更可能發掘本地人才。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, museums and galleries should not restrict themselves to local artists. I strongly disagree with this view because international art both enriches public understanding and creates a healthier environment for local artistic growth.","chinese":"總而言之，博物館和美術館不應把自己限制於本地藝術家。 我強烈不同意這種看法。 因為國際藝術既能豐富公眾理解，也能為本地藝術成長創造更健康的環境。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"museums and galleries","chinese":"博物館和美術館"},{"english":"shape how the public understands","chinese":"塑造公眾如何理解"},{"english":"cultural identity","chinese":"文化身份"},{"english":"these institutions","chinese":"這些機構"},{"english":"display only local artists","chinese":"只展出本地藝術家"},{"english":"instead of showing","chinese":"而不是展示"},{"english":"work from other countries","chinese":"來自其他國家的作品"},{"english":"strongly disagrees with","chinese":"強烈不同意"},{"english":"international collections","chinese":"國際館藏"},{"english":"broaden public understanding","chinese":"擴闊公眾理解"},{"english":"strengthen the long-term development of","chinese":"加強……的長遠發展"},{"english":"local art","chinese":"本地藝術"},{"english":"foreign work","chinese":"外國作品"},{"english":"far more educational","chinese":"教育價值高得多"},{"english":"domestic traditions","chinese":"本土傳統"},{"english":"become narrow","chinese":"變得狹窄"},{"english":"meaningful basis for comparison","chinese":"有意義的比較基礎"},{"english":"place local painting beside","chinese":"將本地繪畫放在……旁邊"},{"english":"Japanese prints","chinese":"日本版畫"},{"english":"African sculpture","chinese":"非洲雕塑"},{"english":"immediately see how","chinese":"立刻看出如何"},{"english":"different cultures","chinese":"不同文化"},{"english":"symbolism and form","chinese":"象徵手法和形式"},{"english":"express similar human concerns","chinese":"表達相似的人類關注"},{"english":"exposure to international art","chinese":"接觸國際藝術"},{"english":"deepen social understanding","chinese":"加深社會理解"},{"english":"works produced in other societies","chinese":"其他社會創作的作品"},{"english":"reflect war, migration, religion or inequality","chinese":"反映戰爭、移民、宗教或不平等"},{"english":"encountering them","chinese":"接觸它們"},{"english":"appreciate experiences beyond","chinese":"理解……以外的經歷"},{"english":"their own environment","chinese":"他們自身的環境"},{"english":"for that reason","chinese":"因此"},{"english":"excluding foreign art","chinese":"排除外國藝術"},{"english":"reduce both the intellectual and the cultural value of","chinese":"同時降低……的知識和文化價值"},{"english":"displaying international art","chinese":"展出國際藝術"},{"english":"benefit local artists","chinese":"令本地藝術家受惠"},{"english":"the institutions that support them","chinese":"支持他們的機構"},{"english":"be challenged by","chinese":"受到……挑戰"},{"english":"unfamiliar techniques","chinese":"不熟悉的技巧"},{"english":"artistic philosophies","chinese":"藝術理念"},{"english":"creative environment","chinese":"創作環境"},{"english":"become repetitive","chinese":"變得重複乏味"},{"english":"by contrast","chinese":"相反"},{"english":"outside influences","chinese":"外來影響"},{"english":"encourage painters, sculptors and photographers to","chinese":"鼓勵畫家、雕塑家和攝影師去"},{"english":"refine their methods","chinese":"改進自己的方法"},{"english":"produce more original work","chinese":"創作更具原創性的作品"},{"english":"European modernism","chinese":"歐洲現代主義"},{"english":"return to local subjects","chinese":"回到本地題材"},{"english":"fresher ways of representing","chinese":"更新鮮的表現方式"},{"english":"light, space or emotion","chinese":"光線、空間或情感"},{"english":"varied exhibitions","chinese":"多元化展覽"},{"english":"attract broader audiences","chinese":"吸引更廣泛觀眾"},{"english":"keep galleries vibrant","chinese":"令美術館保持活力"},{"english":"alternate local shows with international ones","chinese":"本地展覽和國際展覽輪流舉行"},{"english":"draw more students, critics and repeat visitors","chinese":"吸引更多學生、評論家和回頭訪客"},{"english":"become more likely to","chinese":"變得更有可能"},{"english":"discover local talent","chinese":"發掘本地人才"},{"english":"restrict themselves to","chinese":"將自己限制於"},{"english":"enrich public understanding","chinese":"豐富公眾理解"},{"english":"create a healthier environment for","chinese":"為……創造更健康的環境"},{"english":"local artistic growth","chinese":"本地藝術發展"}]},"model-essay-3-ielts-task1-bar-charts":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-3-ielts-task1-bar-charts","essayKey":"bar-charts:3","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-3-ielts-task1-bar-charts","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-1/bar-charts/bar-chart-3","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"The bar chart compares the proportions of residents in Sydney, Melbourne, Brisbane, Adelaide and Hobart who bought fresh or instant coffee, or visited a café for coffee or tea, over the previous four weeks.","chinese":"這張柱狀圖比較了悉尼、墨爾本、布里斯本、阿德萊德和霍巴特居民在過去四星期內購買新鮮咖啡、即溶咖啡，或到咖啡店喝咖啡或茶的比例。"},{"label":"Overview","english":"Overall, going to a café was the most common habit in most cities, while buying fresh coffee was consistently the least popular option. Instant coffee was more widely purchased than fresh coffee in every city, and Adelaide was the only place where café visits did not occupy first position.","chinese":"整體而言，在大多數城市中，到咖啡店是最常見的習慣，而購買新鮮咖啡則一直是最不受歡迎的選項。 在每個城市中，即溶咖啡的購買比例都高於新鮮咖啡；而阿德萊德是唯一一個咖啡店到訪率沒有排在第一位的城市。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"Café-going was especially popular in Melbourne and Hobart, at about 64% and 63% respectively, followed by Sydney, where just over three fifths of residents reported doing so. The figures were lower in Brisbane, at around 56%, and Adelaide, at just under 50%, making it the weakest city for café visits.","chinese":"到咖啡店在墨爾本和霍巴特尤其普遍，比例分別約為 64% 和 63% ；其次是悉尼，當地略多於五分之三的居民表示曾這樣做。 布里斯本的比例較低，約為 56% ；而阿德萊德則略低於 50% ，因此成為咖啡店到訪率最低的城市。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"In terms of coffee purchases, instant coffee recorded relatively high figures in Hobart and Brisbane, at roughly 54% and 53%. Adelaide stood at about 50%, while Melbourne and Sydney were slightly lower, at approximately 48% and 45% respectively. By contrast, fresh coffee attracted smaller shares everywhere: around 44% in Sydney, 43% in Melbourne, 39% in Hobart, and only about 34% in Brisbane and 35% in Adelaide.","chinese":"就咖啡購買而言，即溶咖啡在霍巴特和布里斯本錄得相對較高的比例，分別約為 54% 和 53% 。 阿德萊德約為 50% ；而墨爾本和悉尼則稍低，分別約為 48% 和 45% 。 相比之下，新鮮咖啡在所有城市中的比例都較低：悉尼約為 44% ，墨爾本約為43% ，霍巴特約為 39% ，而布里斯本和阿德萊德分別只有約 34% 和 35% 。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"compares the proportions of residents","chinese":"比較居民比例"},{"english":"the proportions of residents","chinese":"居民比例"},{"english":"bought fresh or instant coffee","chinese":"購買新鮮咖啡或即溶咖啡"},{"english":"visited a café for coffee or tea","chinese":"到咖啡店飲咖啡或茶"},{"english":"over the previous four weeks","chinese":"在過去四星期內"},{"english":"going to a café","chinese":"到咖啡店"},{"english":"the most common habit","chinese":"最普遍的習慣"},{"english":"in most cities","chinese":"在大部分城市"},{"english":"buying fresh coffee","chinese":"購買新鮮咖啡"},{"english":"consistently the least popular option","chinese":"一直是最不受歡迎的選項"},{"english":"instant coffee","chinese":"即溶咖啡"},{"english":"more widely purchased than","chinese":"較……更多人購買"},{"english":"in every city","chinese":"在每個城市"},{"english":"the only place where","chinese":"唯一一個……的地方"},{"english":"café visits","chinese":"到咖啡店"},{"english":"occupy first position","chinese":"佔據第一位"},{"english":"café-going","chinese":"到咖啡店的習慣"},{"english":"especially popular in","chinese":"在……尤其受歡迎"},{"english":"at about 64% and 63% respectively","chinese":"分別約為64%和63%"},{"english":"respectively","chinese":"分別"},{"english":"followed by Sydney","chinese":"其次是悉尼"},{"english":"just over three fifths of residents","chinese":"略高於五分之三的居民"},{"english":"reported doing so","chinese":"表示有這樣做"},{"english":"the figures were lower","chinese":"數字較低"},{"english":"at around 56%","chinese":"約為56%"},{"english":"at just under 50%","chinese":"略低於50%"},{"english":"making it the weakest city for","chinese":"使其成為……方面最弱的城市"},{"english":"the weakest city for café visits","chinese":"到咖啡店比例最低的城市"},{"english":"in terms of coffee purchases","chinese":"就咖啡購買而言"},{"english":"coffee purchases","chinese":"咖啡購買情況"},{"english":"recorded relatively high figures","chinese":"錄得相對較高的數字"},{"english":"relatively high figures","chinese":"相對較高的數字"},{"english":"at roughly 54% and 53%","chinese":"約為54%和53%"},{"english":"stood at about 50%","chinese":"處於約50%"},{"english":"slightly lower","chinese":"稍低"},{"english":"at approximately 48% and 45% respectively","chinese":"分別約為48%和45%"},{"english":"By contrast","chinese":"相比之下"},{"english":"fresh coffee","chinese":"新鮮咖啡"},{"english":"attracted smaller shares","chinese":"吸引較小比例"},{"english":"smaller shares everywhere","chinese":"各地比例均較小"},{"english":"around 44% in Sydney","chinese":"悉尼約為44%"},{"english":"43% in Melbourne","chinese":"墨爾本為43%"},{"english":"39% in Hobart","chinese":"荷伯特為39%"},{"english":"only about 34% in Brisbane","chinese":"布里斯本僅約34%"},{"english":"35% in Adelaide","chinese":"阿德萊德為35%"}]},"model-essay-3-ielts-task1-line-graph":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-3-ielts-task1-line-graph","essayKey":"line-graph:3","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-3-ielts-task1-line-graph","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-1/line-graphs/line-graph-3","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"The line graph illustrates month-on-month percentage changes in the prices of copper, nickel and zinc in 2014.","chinese":"這張折線圖說明了 2014 年銅、鎳和鋅價格相對上個月的百分比變化。"},{"label":"Overview","english":"Overall, nickel was the most volatile metal, starting with the strongest rise but later recording the steepest fall. Copper changed more modestly, whereas zinc ended the year with the highest monthly change. All three metals weakened around mid-year before recovering in November and December.","chinese":"整體而言，鎳是波動最大的金屬，年初錄得最強升幅，但之後又出現最大跌幅。 銅的變化較為溫和；相反，鋅在年底錄得最高的月度變化。 三種金屬都在年中附近走弱，然後在 11 月和 12 月回升。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"At the beginning of the year, nickel rose by about 6%, compared with 2% for copper and 1% for zinc. In February, nickel remained high at roughly 4%, while zinc peaked at 3%. After this, the figures for all three metals fell steadily: by May, nickel and zinc had dropped to around 0.5% and 1% respectively, while copper had slipped to about -0.5%.","chinese":"年初，鎳上升約 6% ，相比之下，銅和鋅分別上升約 2% 和 1% 。 2 月，鎳仍維持在約 4% 的高位，而鋅則達到 3% 的高峰。 此後，三種金屬的數字都穩步下降：到 5 月，鎳和鋅分別跌至約 0.5% 和 1% ，而銅則下滑至約 -0.5% 。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"June was the clear low point. Nickel plunged to approximately -3%, far below zinc at -1% and copper at about -0.5%. From July to September, copper recovered to around 1%, whereas nickel stayed at -1% and zinc hovered near -0.5%. In October, nickel slipped again to -2%, but by December all three were positive, with zinc at 2%, copper at around 1.5% and nickel at 1%.","chinese":"6 月是明顯的低點。 鎳急跌至約 -3% ，遠低於鋅的 -1% 和銅的約 -0.5% 。 從 7 月到 9 月，銅回升至約 1% ；相反，鎳維持在 -1% ，而鋅則徘徊在約 -0.5% 。 10 月，鎳再次下滑至 -2% ；但到 12 月，三種金屬都回到正值，其中鋅為 2% ，銅約為 1.5% ，鎳為 1% 。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"The line graph illustrates","chinese":"折線圖顯示"},{"english":"month-on-month percentage changes","chinese":"按月百分比變化"},{"english":"the prices of copper, nickel and zinc","chinese":"銅、鎳和鋅的價格"},{"english":"copper","chinese":"銅"},{"english":"nickel","chinese":"鎳"},{"english":"zinc","chinese":"鋅"},{"english":"in 2014","chinese":"在2014年"},{"english":"Overall","chinese":"整體而言"},{"english":"the most volatile metal","chinese":"波動最大的金屬"},{"english":"starting with the strongest rise","chinese":"一開始錄得最大升幅"},{"english":"the strongest rise","chinese":"最大升幅"},{"english":"later recording the steepest fall","chinese":"其後錄得最急跌幅"},{"english":"the steepest fall","chinese":"最急跌幅"},{"english":"changed more modestly","chinese":"變化較溫和"},{"english":"ended the year with","chinese":"以……結束全年"},{"english":"the highest monthly change","chinese":"最高的按月變化"},{"english":"all three metals","chinese":"三種金屬全部"},{"english":"weakened around mid-year","chinese":"在年中左右走弱"},{"english":"mid-year","chinese":"年中"},{"english":"before recovering in November and December","chinese":"隨後在11月和12月回升"},{"english":"recovering in November and December","chinese":"在11月和12月回升"},{"english":"at the beginning of the year","chinese":"在年初"},{"english":"rose by about 6%","chinese":"上升約6%"},{"english":"compared with","chinese":"與……相比"},{"english":"2% for copper","chinese":"銅為2%"},{"english":"1% for zinc","chinese":"鋅為1%"},{"english":"remained high at roughly 4%","chinese":"維持在約4%的高位"},{"english":"peaked at 3%","chinese":"在3%見頂"},{"english":"After this","chinese":"此後"},{"english":"the figures for all three metals","chinese":"三種金屬的數字"},{"english":"fell steadily","chinese":"穩步下跌"},{"english":"by May","chinese":"到5月"},{"english":"had dropped to around 0.5%","chinese":"已跌至約0.5%"},{"english":"1% respectively","chinese":"分別為0.5%和1%"},{"english":"respectively","chinese":"分別"},{"english":"had slipped to about −0.5%","chinese":"已跌至約負0.5%"},{"english":"slipped to","chinese":"下滑至"},{"english":"June was the clear low point","chinese":"6月是明顯低位"},{"english":"the clear low point","chinese":"明顯低位"},{"english":"plunged to approximately −3%","chinese":"急跌至約負3%"},{"english":"far below","chinese":"遠低於"},{"english":"zinc at −1%","chinese":"鋅為負1%"},{"english":"copper at about −0.5%","chinese":"銅約為負0.5%"},{"english":"from July to September","chinese":"從7月至9月"},{"english":"recovered to around 1%","chinese":"回升至約1%"},{"english":"whereas","chinese":"而；然而"},{"english":"stayed at −1%","chinese":"維持在負1%"},{"english":"hovered near −0.5%","chinese":"徘徊在約負0.5%附近"},{"english":"slipped again to −2%","chinese":"再次下滑至負2%"},{"english":"by December","chinese":"到12月"},{"english":"all three were positive","chinese":"三者均錄得正數"},{"english":"with zinc at 2%","chinese":"其中鋅為2%"},{"english":"copper at around 1.5%","chinese":"銅約為1.5%"},{"english":"nickel at 1%","chinese":"鎳為1%"}]},"model-essay-3-ielts-task1-maps":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-3-ielts-task1-maps","essayKey":"maps:3","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-3-ielts-task1-maps","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-1/maps/maps-3","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"The two plans illustrate how the Central Library has been reorganised over the last two decades.","chinese":"這兩張平面圖說明中央圖書館在過去二十年間如何被重新規劃。"},{"label":"Overview","english":"Overall, the library has changed from a mainly book- and reading-based space into a more varied facility, with new areas for technology, events, lectures and refreshments. Although the entrance remains in the same position, the central seating has disappeared and several services have been relocated or modernised.","chinese":"整體而言，該圖書館已經從一個主要以藏書和閱讀為主的空間，轉變成一個功能更為多元的設施，新增了科技、活動、講座和餐飲相關區域。 雖然入口仍在相同位置，但中央座位區已經消失，而多項服務已被重新安置或現代化。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"Twenty years ago, the middle of the library was occupied by tables and chairs, with rooms arranged around it. On the left, there was a media room for CDs, videos and computer games in the north-west corner, adult fiction books in the centre, and a reading room for newspapers and magazines near the entrance. Today, this side has been fully reorganised: the former media and fiction sections contain children’s fiction books, storytelling space and sofas, while the old reading room has become a computer room. A section for all reference books has also been introduced.","chinese":"二十年前，圖書館中央設有桌椅，周圍則分布著不同房間。 在左側，西北角有一個供放置 CDs 、錄像和電腦遊戲的媒體室，中部是成人小說書籍區，靠近入口處則是供閱讀報紙和雜誌的閱覽室。 如今，這一側已被完全重新規劃：原來的媒體室和成人小說區變成兒童小說書籍區、講故事活動空間和沙發區，而舊閱覽室則變成電腦室。 此外，圖書館亦新增了一個全部參考書區。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"On the right, the old children’s books area has been replaced by a lecture room. The former adult non-fiction section now houses adult fiction, an information desk and self-service machines, whereas the old enquiry desk has been converted into a café.","chinese":"在右側，舊兒童書籍區已被講座室取代。 原本的成人非小說書籍區現在設有成人小說、資訊服務台和自助服務機，而舊詢問處則已被改建成咖啡館。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"the floor plan of","chinese":"……的平面圖"},{"english":"a public library","chinese":"公共圖書館"},{"english":"20 years ago","chinese":"20年前"},{"english":"how it looks now","chinese":"它現時的樣貌"},{"english":"summarise the information","chinese":"概述資料"},{"english":"selecting and reporting","chinese":"選取並報告"},{"english":"the main features","chinese":"主要特徵"},{"english":"make comparisons where relevant","chinese":"在相關之處作出比較"},{"english":"The two plans illustrate how","chinese":"兩幅平面圖顯示……如何"},{"english":"the Central Library","chinese":"Central Library"},{"english":"has been reorganised","chinese":"已被重新規劃"},{"english":"over the last two decades","chinese":"在過去二十年間"},{"english":"Overall","chinese":"整體而言"},{"english":"has changed from … into …","chinese":"由……變成……"},{"english":"a mainly book- and reading-based space","chinese":"以藏書及閱讀為主的空間"},{"english":"a more varied facility","chinese":"功能更多元化的設施"},{"english":"new areas for","chinese":"……的新區域"},{"english":"technology, events, lectures and refreshments","chinese":"科技、活動、講座及茶點飲品"},{"english":"although","chinese":"雖然"},{"english":"the entrance remains in the same position","chinese":"入口仍在同一位置"},{"english":"remains in the same position","chinese":"仍在同一位置"},{"english":"the central seating","chinese":"中央座位區"},{"english":"has disappeared","chinese":"已消失；已不復存在"},{"english":"services have been relocated","chinese":"服務已被遷移"},{"english":"have been relocated or modernised","chinese":"已被遷移或現代化"},{"english":"Twenty years ago","chinese":"20年前"},{"english":"the middle of the library","chinese":"圖書館中央"},{"english":"was occupied by","chinese":"被……佔據"},{"english":"tables and chairs","chinese":"桌椅"},{"english":"with rooms arranged around it","chinese":"房間圍繞它排列"},{"english":"arranged around","chinese":"圍繞……排列"},{"english":"On the left","chinese":"在左邊"},{"english":"a media room","chinese":"媒體室"},{"english":"CDs, videos and computer games","chinese":"CD、影片及電腦遊戲"},{"english":"in the north-west corner","chinese":"在西北角"},{"english":"adult fiction books","chinese":"成人小說"},{"english":"in the centre","chinese":"在中央"},{"english":"a reading room for","chinese":"供……使用的閱覽室"},{"english":"newspapers and magazines","chinese":"報紙及雜誌"},{"english":"near the entrance","chinese":"在入口附近"},{"english":"Today","chinese":"現時"},{"english":"this side","chinese":"這一邊"},{"english":"has been fully reorganised","chinese":"已被全面重新規劃"},{"english":"the former media section","chinese":"原來的媒體區"},{"english":"the former fiction section","chinese":"原來的小說區"},{"english":"children's fiction books","chinese":"兒童小說"},{"english":"storytelling space","chinese":"講故事空間"},{"english":"sofas","chinese":"梳化"},{"english":"while","chinese":"而"},{"english":"the old reading room","chinese":"原來的閱覽室"},{"english":"has become","chinese":"已變成"},{"english":"a computer room","chinese":"電腦室"},{"english":"a section for","chinese":"……專區"},{"english":"reference books","chinese":"參考書"},{"english":"has also been introduced","chinese":"亦已增設"},{"english":"On the right","chinese":"在右邊"},{"english":"the old children's books area","chinese":"原來的兒童圖書區"},{"english":"has been replaced by","chinese":"已被……取代"},{"english":"a lecture room","chinese":"講座室"},{"english":"the former adult non-fiction section","chinese":"原來的成人非小說區"},{"english":"adult non-fiction","chinese":"成人非小說書籍"},{"english":"now houses","chinese":"現時設有"},{"english":"adult fiction","chinese":"成人小說"},{"english":"an information desk","chinese":"查詢處；服務台"},{"english":"self-service machines","chinese":"自助服務機"},{"english":"whereas","chinese":"而；相比之下"},{"english":"the old enquiry desk","chinese":"原來的查詢處"},{"english":"has been converted into","chinese":"已被改建成"},{"english":"a café","chinese":"咖啡店"}]},"model-essay-3-ielts-task1-mixed-charts":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-3-ielts-task1-mixed-charts","essayKey":"mixed-charts:3","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-3-ielts-task1-mixed-charts","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-1/mixed-charts/mixed-charts-3","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"The table compares the police budget in one area of Britain in 2017 and 2018 by funding source, while the pie charts show how the money was spent.","chinese":"該表格按照資金來源比較了英國某地區在2017年和2018年的警察預算，而餅圖則顯示了這筆錢的支出方式。"},{"label":"Overview","english":"Overall, the budget rose modestly over the two years. The national government remained the main source of funding, although the increase came chiefly from local taxes. In terms of expenditure, salaries continued to dominate the budget, but their share fell as technology took a larger proportion.","chinese":"整體而言，這兩年間警察預算有小幅上升。 中央政府仍然是主要資金來源，儘管預算增幅主要來自地方稅收。 在支出方面，薪金仍然佔據預算的最大部分，但其比例有所下降，而科技支出所佔比例則增加了。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"In 2017, the total police budget stood at £304.7 million. Of this, £175.5 million came from the national government, far more than the £91.2 million raised through local taxes and the £38 million from other sources, such as grants. By 2018, the total had climbed to £318.6 million. Government funding increased only slightly, to £177.8 million, while local-tax revenue rose more sharply to £102.3 million. Other sources changed very little, reaching £38.5 million.","chinese":"2017年，警察總預算為3.047億英鎊。 其中，1.755億英鎊來自中央政府，遠高於地方稅收籌得的9,120萬英鎊，以及來自其他來源如補助金的3,800萬英鎊。 到2018年，總預算上升至3.186億英鎊。 政府撥款只小幅增加至1.778億英鎊，而地方稅收則更明顯地上升至1.023億英鎊。 其他來源變化很小，達到3,850萬英鎊。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"Regarding spending, salaries accounted for three quarters of the budget in 2017, before declining to 69% in 2018. By contrast, technology almost doubled its share, rising from 8% to 14%, whereas buildings and transport remained unchanged at 17%.","chinese":"在支出方面，薪金在2017年佔預算的四分之三，之後在2018年下降至69%。 相比之下，科技支出所佔比例幾乎翻倍，從8%上升至14%；而建築物和交通支出則保持不變，均為17%。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"give information on","chinese":"提供關於……的資料"},{"english":"the police budget","chinese":"警察預算"},{"english":"for 2017 and 2018","chinese":"2017年和2018年的"},{"english":"in one area of Britain","chinese":"在英國某一地區"},{"english":"where the money came from","chinese":"資金來自哪裏"},{"english":"how it was distributed","chinese":"它如何分配"},{"english":"summarise the information","chinese":"概述資料"},{"english":"selecting and reporting","chinese":"選取並報告"},{"english":"the main features","chinese":"主要特徵"},{"english":"make comparisons where relevant","chinese":"在相關之處作出比較"},{"english":"the table compares","chinese":"表格比較"},{"english":"by funding source","chinese":"按資金來源"},{"english":"funding source","chinese":"資金來源"},{"english":"while","chinese":"而"},{"english":"pie charts","chinese":"餅圖"},{"english":"how the money was spent","chinese":"資金如何使用"},{"english":"Overall","chinese":"整體而言"},{"english":"rose modestly","chinese":"小幅上升"},{"english":"over the two years","chinese":"在這兩年間"},{"english":"the national government","chinese":"中央政府"},{"english":"remained the main source of funding","chinese":"仍然是主要資金來源"},{"english":"the main source of funding","chinese":"主要資金來源"},{"english":"although","chinese":"雖然；儘管"},{"english":"the increase came chiefly from","chinese":"增幅主要來自"},{"english":"came chiefly from","chinese":"主要來自"},{"english":"local taxes","chinese":"地方稅收"},{"english":"In terms of expenditure","chinese":"在支出方面"},{"english":"expenditure","chinese":"支出"},{"english":"salaries","chinese":"薪金"},{"english":"continued to dominate","chinese":"繼續佔主導地位"},{"english":"dominate the budget","chinese":"佔預算最大部分"},{"english":"their share fell","chinese":"其所佔比例下降"},{"english":"as technology took a larger proportion","chinese":"隨着科技佔比增加"},{"english":"technology","chinese":"科技"},{"english":"took a larger proportion","chinese":"佔較大比例"},{"english":"the total police budget","chinese":"警察總預算"},{"english":"stood at £304.7 million","chinese":"為3.047億英鎊"},{"english":"Of this","chinese":"其中"},{"english":"came from the national government","chinese":"來自中央政府"},{"english":"£175.5 million","chinese":"1.755億英鎊"},{"english":"far more than","chinese":"遠多於"},{"english":"raised through local taxes","chinese":"透過地方稅收籌得"},{"english":"£91.2 million","chinese":"9,120萬英鎊"},{"english":"other sources","chinese":"其他來源"},{"english":"such as grants","chinese":"例如補助金"},{"english":"grants","chinese":"補助金"},{"english":"By 2018","chinese":"到2018年"},{"english":"the total had climbed to","chinese":"總額已上升至"},{"english":"climbed to £318.6 million","chinese":"上升至3.186億英鎊"},{"english":"government funding","chinese":"政府撥款"},{"english":"increased only slightly","chinese":"只小幅增加"},{"english":"to £177.8 million","chinese":"至1.778億英鎊"},{"english":"local tax revenue","chinese":"地方稅收收入"},{"english":"rose more sharply","chinese":"上升得更明顯"},{"english":"to £102.3 million","chinese":"至1.023億英鎊"},{"english":"changed very little","chinese":"變化很小"},{"english":"reaching £38.5 million","chinese":"達到3,850萬英鎊"},{"english":"Regarding spending","chinese":"在支出方面"},{"english":"accounted for three quarters of","chinese":"佔……的四分之三"},{"english":"three quarters of the budget","chinese":"預算的四分之三"},{"english":"before declining to","chinese":"之後下降至"},{"english":"declining to 69%","chinese":"下降至69%"},{"english":"By contrast","chinese":"相比之下"},{"english":"almost doubled its share","chinese":"所佔比例幾乎翻倍"},{"english":"doubled its share","chinese":"所佔比例翻倍"},{"english":"rising from 8% to 14%","chinese":"由8%上升至14%"},{"english":"whereas","chinese":"而；相比之下"},{"english":"buildings and transport","chinese":"建築物及交通"},{"english":"remained unchanged at 17%","chinese":"維持在17%不變"}]},"model-essay-3-ielts-task1-pie-charts":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-3-ielts-task1-pie-charts","essayKey":"pie-charts:3","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-3-ielts-task1-pie-charts","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-1/pie-charts/pie-chart-3","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"The two pie charts compare British students at a university in England according to the additional language or languages they could speak besides English in 2000 and 2010.","chinese":"這兩個圓餅圖比較了英格蘭一所大學的英國學生在 2000 年和 2010 年除英語以外能說的額外語言情況。"},{"label":"Overview","english":"Overall, students became more likely to speak at least one language besides English: the share reporting no additional language fell markedly, while Spanish, another language and two other languages all increased. Spanish remained the dominant category in both years.","chinese":"整體而言，學生變得更有可能會說至少一種英語以外的語言：表示不會任何額外語言的比例明顯下降，而除英語外只會西班牙語、另一種語言以及另外兩種語言的比例均有所上升。 除英語外只會西班牙語在兩個年份中都保持為最大類別。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"In 2000, Spanish only accounted for the largest segment, at 30% of students. This was followed by those with no other language, who made up one fifth of the total. French only and another language were equal at 15% each, whereas German only and two other languages were the smallest categories, both standing at 10%.","chinese":"在 2000 年，除英語外只會西班牙語佔最大部分，為學生總數的 30% 。 其次是不會任何其他語言的學生，他們佔總數的五分之一。 除英語外只會法語和會另一種語言的比例相同，均為 15% ；相反，只會德語和會另外兩種語言是最小的類別，兩者都為 10% 。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"By 2010, Spanish had strengthened its lead, rising to 35%. The proportion speaking another language also increased, from 15% to 20%, while the figure for students able to speak two other languages grew by five percentage points to 15%. By contrast, the percentage with no additional language halved to 10%, and French only fell to the same level. German remained unchanged at 10%.","chinese":"到 2010 年，除英語外只會西班牙語進一步擴大領先優勢，上升至 35% 。 會另一種語言的比例也從 15% 上升至 20% ，而能說另外兩種語言的學生比例則增加了五個百分點，達到 15% 。 相比之下，不會任何額外語言的比例減半至 10% ，而除英語外只會法語的比例也下降至同一水平。 除英語外只會德語的比例則保持不變，仍為 10% 。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"the two pie charts compare","chinese":"兩個圓形圖比較"},{"english":"British students","chinese":"英國學生"},{"english":"at a university in England","chinese":"在英格蘭一所大學"},{"english":"according to","chinese":"根據"},{"english":"additional language or languages","chinese":"額外一種或多種語言"},{"english":"could speak","chinese":"能夠說"},{"english":"besides English","chinese":"除英語以外"},{"english":"in 2000 and 2010","chinese":"在2000年和2010年"},{"english":"became more likely to","chinese":"變得更有可能"},{"english":"speak at least one language","chinese":"說至少一種語言"},{"english":"at least one language besides English","chinese":"除英語外至少一種語言"},{"english":"the share reporting no additional language","chinese":"表示沒有額外語言的比例"},{"english":"no additional language","chinese":"沒有額外語言"},{"english":"fell markedly","chinese":"明顯下降"},{"english":"another language","chinese":"另一種語言"},{"english":"two other languages","chinese":"另外兩種語言"},{"english":"remained the dominant category","chinese":"仍然是主導類別"},{"english":"the dominant category","chinese":"主導類別"},{"english":"in both years","chinese":"在兩個年份中"},{"english":"accounted for the largest segment","chinese":"佔最大部分"},{"english":"the largest segment","chinese":"最大部分"},{"english":"at 30% of students","chinese":"佔學生的30%"},{"english":"This was followed by","chinese":"其次是"},{"english":"those with no other language","chinese":"沒有其他語言的人"},{"english":"made up one fifth of the total","chinese":"佔總數五分之一"},{"english":"one fifth of the total","chinese":"總數的五分之一"},{"english":"French only","chinese":"只懂法語"},{"english":"were equal at 15% each","chinese":"各佔15%，比例相同"},{"english":"whereas","chinese":"而；然而"},{"english":"German only","chinese":"只懂德語"},{"english":"the smallest categories","chinese":"最小的類別"},{"english":"both standing at 10%","chinese":"兩者均為10%"},{"english":"By 2010","chinese":"到2010年"},{"english":"strengthened its lead","chinese":"擴大其領先優勢"},{"english":"rising to 35%","chinese":"上升至35%"},{"english":"the proportion speaking another language","chinese":"說另一種語言的比例"},{"english":"increased from 15% to 20%","chinese":"由15%增至20%"},{"english":"the figure for students able to speak","chinese":"能夠說……的學生數字"},{"english":"able to speak two other languages","chinese":"能夠說另外兩種語言"},{"english":"grew by five percentage points","chinese":"增加了五個百分點"},{"english":"percentage points","chinese":"百分點"},{"english":"By contrast","chinese":"相比之下"},{"english":"the percentage with no additional language","chinese":"沒有額外語言的百分比"},{"english":"halved to 10%","chinese":"減半至10%"},{"english":"fell to the same level","chinese":"下降至相同水平"},{"english":"the same level","chinese":"相同水平"},{"english":"remained unchanged at 10%","chinese":"維持10%不變"}]},"model-essay-3-ielts-task1-process-diagram":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-3-ielts-task1-process-diagram","essayKey":"process-diagram:3","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-3-ielts-task1-process-diagram","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-1/process-diagrams/process-diagram-3","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"The diagram illustrates the process by which sugar is produced from sugar cane.","chinese":"該圖說明糖是如何由甘蔗製成的。"},{"label":"Overview","english":"Overall, the production of sugar is a linear, seven-stage process that begins with growing cane and ends with drying and cooling the finished crystals. Broadly, it moves from an agricultural phase, involving cultivation and harvesting, to an industrial phase in which juice is extracted, purified, thickened and separated.","chinese":"整體而言，糖的生產是一個線性的七階段流程，從種植甘蔗開始，最後以乾燥和冷卻成品糖晶體結束。 大致來說，這個流程由涉及栽培和收割的農業階段，轉向工業階段；在工業階段中，汁液會被提取、淨化、濃縮並分離。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"First, sugar cane is grown for 12 to 18 months until it reaches maturity. It is then harvested in one of two ways: mechanically, with a vehicle cutting and loading the crop, or manually, with workers cutting the stalks by hand. After harvesting, the cane is crushed in a machine, and this step squeezes out the juice required for the later stages.","chinese":"首先，甘蔗會被種植十二至十八個月，直到成熟。 然後，甘蔗會以兩種方式之一被收割：一種是機械收割，由車輛切割並裝載作物；另一種是人工收割，由工人用手切割甘蔗莖。 收割後，甘蔗會在機器中被壓碎，而這一步會擠出後續階段所需的汁液。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"The extracted juice is next purified by passing through a limestone filter. Once it has been cleaned, it is heated in an evaporator, where excess water is removed and the liquid becomes syrup. This syrup is then spun in a centrifuge, which separates sugar crystals from the remaining syrup. In the final stage, the crystals are dried and cooled, leaving the finished sugar.","chinese":"提取出的汁液接著會通過石灰石過濾器被淨化。 當汁液被清潔後，它會在蒸發器中被加熱；在這一步中，多餘的水分會被去除，而液體會變成糖漿。 然後，糖漿會在離心機中旋轉，離心機會把糖晶體從剩餘糖漿中分離出來。 在最後階段，糖晶體會被乾燥和冷卻，最終留下成品糖。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"The diagram illustrates","chinese":"圖解顯示"},{"english":"the process by which","chinese":"……的過程"},{"english":"sugar is produced from sugar cane","chinese":"糖由甘蔗製成"},{"english":"sugar cane","chinese":"甘蔗"},{"english":"the production of sugar","chinese":"糖的生產"},{"english":"a linear, seven-stage process","chinese":"線性的七階段過程"},{"english":"begins with growing cane","chinese":"以種植甘蔗開始"},{"english":"ends with drying and cooling","chinese":"以烘乾和冷卻結束"},{"english":"finished crystals","chinese":"製成的晶體"},{"english":"Broadly","chinese":"廣義而言；概括來說"},{"english":"moves from an agricultural phase to","chinese":"由農業階段轉向"},{"english":"an agricultural phase","chinese":"農業階段"},{"english":"involving cultivation and harvesting","chinese":"涉及種植和收割"},{"english":"cultivation","chinese":"種植"},{"english":"harvesting","chinese":"收割"},{"english":"an industrial phase","chinese":"工業階段"},{"english":"juice is extracted","chinese":"汁液被提取"},{"english":"purified, thickened and separated","chinese":"被淨化、濃縮和分離"},{"english":"reaches maturity","chinese":"達到成熟"},{"english":"is grown for 12 to 18 months","chinese":"種植12至18個月"},{"english":"is then harvested","chinese":"然後被收割"},{"english":"in one of two ways","chinese":"以兩種方式之一"},{"english":"mechanically","chinese":"以機械方式"},{"english":"cutting and loading the crop","chinese":"切割並裝載農作物"},{"english":"the crop","chinese":"農作物"},{"english":"manually","chinese":"以人手方式"},{"english":"workers cutting the stalks by hand","chinese":"工人用手切割莖幹"},{"english":"stalks","chinese":"莖幹"},{"english":"by hand","chinese":"用手；人手"},{"english":"After harvesting","chinese":"收割後"},{"english":"is crushed in a machine","chinese":"在機器中被壓榨"},{"english":"squeezes out the juice","chinese":"擠出汁液"},{"english":"required for the later stages","chinese":"後續階段所需"},{"english":"the extracted juice","chinese":"提取出的汁液"},{"english":"is next purified","chinese":"接着被淨化"},{"english":"by passing through","chinese":"透過經過……"},{"english":"a limestone filter","chinese":"石灰石過濾器"},{"english":"Once it has been cleaned","chinese":"當它被清潔後"},{"english":"is heated in an evaporator","chinese":"在蒸發器中被加熱"},{"english":"evaporator","chinese":"蒸發器"},{"english":"excess water is removed","chinese":"多餘水分被去除"},{"english":"the liquid becomes syrup","chinese":"液體變成糖漿"},{"english":"syrup","chinese":"糖漿"},{"english":"is then spun in a centrifuge","chinese":"然後在離心機中旋轉"},{"english":"centrifuge","chinese":"離心機"},{"english":"separates sugar crystals from","chinese":"將糖晶體與……分離"},{"english":"sugar crystals","chinese":"糖晶體"},{"english":"the remaining syrup","chinese":"餘下糖漿"},{"english":"In the final stage","chinese":"在最後階段"},{"english":"are dried and cooled","chinese":"被烘乾和冷卻"},{"english":"leaving the finished sugar","chinese":"最後形成製成糖"},{"english":"the finished sugar","chinese":"製成糖"}]},"model-essay-3-ielts-task1-tables":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-3-ielts-task1-tables","essayKey":"tables:3","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-3-ielts-task1-tables","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-1/tables/table-3","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"The table compares six major MRT systems by year of completion, network length and annual carrying capacity.","chinese":"這個表格比較了六個主要地鐵系統的完工年份、網絡長度和年度載客容量。"},{"label":"Overview","english":"Overall, London and Paris are the earliest and most extensive systems, with London’s network standing well ahead of all the others in length. In contrast, Tokyo has by far the greatest yearly capacity despite being much shorter, while Kyoto is the smallest system on both measures.","chinese":"整體而言，倫敦和巴黎是最早完工且網絡規模最大的系統，其中倫敦的路線長度明顯遠超所有其他城市。 相比之下，東京雖然路線短得多，卻擁有遠遠最高的年度載客容量；而京都在路線長度和載客容量兩方面都是最小的系統。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"London was completed first, in 1863, and covers 1,100 kilometres, almost twice Paris’s 594 kilometres. Paris, which opened in 1890, nevertheless carries more passengers annually than London, at 850 million compared with 548 million. Tokyo was completed in 1904 and is only 149 kilometres long, yet it dominates in capacity, handling 1,434 million passengers per year.","chinese":"倫敦最早完工，時間是 1863 年，總長度為 1,100 公里，幾乎是巴黎 594 公里的兩倍。 巴黎於 1890 年開通，但其年度載客容量仍高於倫敦，分別為 8.5 億和 5.48 億。 東京於 1904 年完工，長度只有 149 公里，但它在載客容量方面居於首位，每年可承載 14.34 億乘客。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"The other three systems are on a much smaller scale. Washington DC, completed in 1921, has 114 kilometres of track, but its annual capacity is just 70 million. Kyoto and Los Angeles are the newest networks, finished in 1980 and 2001 respectively, and both are extremely short, at 11 and 14 kilometres. However, Los Angeles can carry 90 million passengers annually, far more than Kyoto’s 11 million.","chinese":"另外三個系統的規模則小得多。 華盛頓特區於 1921 年完工，擁有 114 公里路線，但其年度載客容量只有 7,000 萬。 京都和洛杉磯是最新的兩個網絡，分別於 1980 年和 2001 年完工，而且兩者都非常短，分別只有 11 公里和 14 公里。 然而，洛杉磯每年可承載 9,000 萬乘客，遠高於京都的 1,100 萬。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"compares six major MRT systems","chinese":"比較六個主要地鐵系統"},{"english":"six major MRT systems","chinese":"六個主要地鐵系統"},{"english":"year of completion","chinese":"完工年份；落成年份"},{"english":"network length","chinese":"路網長度"},{"english":"annual carrying capacity","chinese":"每年載客能力"},{"english":"Overall","chinese":"整體而言"},{"english":"the earliest and most extensive systems","chinese":"最早及規模最大的系統"},{"english":"most extensive","chinese":"規模最大的；覆蓋最廣的"},{"english":"standing well ahead of","chinese":"遠遠領先於"},{"english":"all the others","chinese":"其他所有"},{"english":"in length","chinese":"在長度方面"},{"english":"In contrast","chinese":"相比之下"},{"english":"by far the greatest yearly capacity","chinese":"遠遠最高的每年載客能力"},{"english":"yearly capacity","chinese":"每年載客能力"},{"english":"despite being much shorter","chinese":"儘管短得多"},{"english":"much shorter","chinese":"短得多"},{"english":"the smallest system on both measures","chinese":"在兩項指標上都是最小的系統"},{"english":"on both measures","chinese":"在兩項指標上"},{"english":"was completed first","chinese":"最早完工"},{"english":"in 1863","chinese":"在1863年"},{"english":"covers 1,100 kilometres","chinese":"覆蓋1,100公里"},{"english":"covers","chinese":"覆蓋；全長為"},{"english":"almost twice","chinese":"幾乎是兩倍"},{"english":"Paris's 594 kilometres","chinese":"巴黎的594公里"},{"english":"opened in 1890","chinese":"於1890年開通"},{"english":"nevertheless","chinese":"然而；儘管如此"},{"english":"carries more passengers annually","chinese":"每年運載更多乘客"},{"english":"annually","chinese":"每年"},{"english":"at 850 million","chinese":"為8.5億"},{"english":"compared with","chinese":"與……相比"},{"english":"548 million","chinese":"5.48億"},{"english":"was completed in 1904","chinese":"於1904年完工"},{"english":"only 149 kilometres long","chinese":"全長只有149公里"},{"english":"yet","chinese":"然而"},{"english":"dominates in capacity","chinese":"在載客能力方面佔主導地位"},{"english":"handling 1,434 million passengers per year","chinese":"每年運載14.34億乘客"},{"english":"passengers per year","chinese":"每年乘客量"},{"english":"the other three systems","chinese":"其餘三個系統"},{"english":"on a much smaller scale","chinese":"規模小得多"},{"english":"much smaller scale","chinese":"小得多的規模"},{"english":"completed in 1921","chinese":"於1921年完工"},{"english":"has 114 kilometres of track","chinese":"擁有114公里路軌"},{"english":"kilometres of track","chinese":"公里路軌"},{"english":"annual capacity","chinese":"每年載客能力"},{"english":"just 70 million","chinese":"只有7,000萬"},{"english":"the newest networks","chinese":"最新的路網"},{"english":"finished in 1980 and 2001 respectively","chinese":"分別於1980年和2001年完成"},{"english":"respectively","chinese":"分別"},{"english":"extremely short","chinese":"極短"},{"english":"at 11 and 14 kilometres","chinese":"分別為11和14公里"},{"english":"However","chinese":"然而"},{"english":"can carry","chinese":"可運載"},{"english":"90 million passengers annually","chinese":"每年9,000萬乘客"},{"english":"far more than","chinese":"遠多於"},{"english":"Kyoto's 11 million","chinese":"京都的1,100萬"}]},"model-essay-4-ielts-advantage-disadvantage":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-4-ielts-advantage-disadvantage","essayKey":"advantage-disadvantage:4","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-4-ielts-advantage-disadvantage","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/advantage-and-disadvantage/EdmundBd9AdDisAd-Q4","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"Change is an inevitable part of modern life, yet people respond to it in very different ways. While some actively welcome new experiences, others prefer to protect their routines and avoid disruption whenever possible. Although both approaches bring certain benefits and drawbacks, embracing change is ultimately the more advantageous mindset because it fosters adaptability and growth, whereas avoiding change mainly provides short-term security.","chinese":"[改變是現代生活中不可避免的一部分，然而人們對它的反應卻非常不同。] [有些人會主動迎接新的經驗，另一些人則傾向維持原有的生活規律，並在可能的情況下避免干擾。] [雖然這兩種做法都有一些優點和缺點，但擁抱改變最終是更有利的心態，因為它能培養適應力與成長，而避免改變主要只是提供短期的安全感。]"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"People who enjoy change usually gain stronger long-term benefits, even though this way of life is not without cost. When individuals enter unfamiliar situations, they are forced to learn new skills, solve unexpected problems and interact with different kinds of people, which gradually makes them more resilient and capable. For example, a graduate who moves abroad for work must adjust to a new culture, new colleagues and new expectations, and this process often leaves them more confident and employable. However, constant change can also create instability. If someone changes jobs, cities or relationships too frequently, they may struggle to build lasting support networks or any real sense of security. A worker who continually moves from one short-term role to another, for instance, may enjoy variety, but may also feel financially and emotionally unsettled.","chinese":"[喜歡改變的人通常能獲得更強的長遠好處，儘管這種生活方式並非毫無代價。] [當人們進入陌生情境時，他們會被迫學習新技能、解決意料之外的問題，並與不同類型的人互動，而這些過程會逐漸令他們變得更有韌性、更有能力。] [例如，一位到國外工作的畢業生必須適應新的文化、新的同事以及新的期待，而這個過程往往會讓他變得更有自信，也更具就業競爭力。] [然而，不斷的改變也可能造成不穩定。] [如果一個人過於頻繁地更換工作、城市或人際關係，他們可能難以建立持久的支持網絡，或任何真正的安全感。] [例如，一位不斷在不同短期工作之間轉換的員工，也許會享受多樣性，但同時也可能在經濟和情緒上感到不安定。] [即便如此，改變所帶來的個人成長，往往仍然大於它暫時造成的不穩定。]"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"By contrast, people who try to avoid change benefit from stability, but this preference can easily become a serious limitation. Remaining in a familiar environment reduces stress because routines are predictable, responsibilities are clear and long-term relationships can deepen over time. Someone who stays in one community for many years, for example, may enjoy close friendships, a reliable support system and a steady career path. The disadvantage, however, is that excessive caution often leads to stagnation. When people reject new technology, training or opportunities simply because these feel uncomfortable, they may fall behind both personally and professionally. An employee who refuses to learn new digital systems may preserve the comfort of old habits for a while, but may eventually become less useful in a changing workplace.","chinese":"[相比之下，試圖避免改變的人可以從穩定中獲益，但這種偏好也很容易成為一種嚴重的限制。] [留在熟悉的環境中能減少壓力，因為生活規律是可預測的、責任是清晰的，而且長期關係也能隨時間加深。] [例如，一個在同一個社區生活多年的人，可能會擁有親密的友誼、可靠的支持系統，以及穩定的職涯道路。] [然而，這種做法的缺點在於，過度謹慎往往會導致停滯。] [當人們只是因為新科技、培訓或機會讓人感到不舒服，就拒絕接受它們時，他們可能會在個人和職業層面上同時落後。] [一名拒絕學習新數位系統的員工，也許能暫時保住舊習慣帶來的舒適感，但最終可能會在不斷改變的職場中變得不那麼有用。] [基於這一點，避免改變所獲得的穩定，往往會被這種謹慎所扼殺的機會抵消。]"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, both attitudes have understandable advantages: enjoying change encourages development, while avoiding it offers stability. Nevertheless, welcoming change is clearly the better approach, because a flexible person can still create stability, whereas an inflexible one may lose valuable opportunities that never return.","chinese":"[總而言之，雖然這兩種態度都提供了一些好處，但擁抱改變顯然是更好的做法。] [這是因為它能促進韌性、成長與適應力；相反地，避免改變主要只是提供暫時的舒適，卻同時增加停滯與錯失機會的風險。]"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"an inevitable part of","chinese":"……中不可避免的一部分"},{"english":"modern life","chinese":"現代生活"},{"english":"respond to it in very different ways","chinese":"以很不同的方式回應它"},{"english":"actively welcome","chinese":"積極歡迎"},{"english":"new experiences","chinese":"新體驗"},{"english":"protect their routines","chinese":"保護自己的日常規律"},{"english":"avoid disruption","chinese":"避免干擾；避免被打亂"},{"english":"whenever possible","chinese":"只要可能"},{"english":"both approaches","chinese":"兩種做法"},{"english":"bring certain benefits and drawbacks","chinese":"帶來某些好處和缺點"},{"english":"embracing change","chinese":"擁抱改變"},{"english":"the more advantageous mindset","chinese":"較有利的心態"},{"english":"fosters adaptability and growth","chinese":"培養適應力和成長"},{"english":"whereas","chinese":"而；相比之下"},{"english":"short-term security","chinese":"短期安全感"},{"english":"gain stronger long-term benefits","chinese":"獲得更大的長遠好處"},{"english":"not without cost","chinese":"並非沒有代價"},{"english":"enter unfamiliar situations","chinese":"進入陌生情況"},{"english":"be forced to","chinese":"被迫去"},{"english":"learn new skills","chinese":"學習新技能"},{"english":"solve unexpected problems","chinese":"解決意想不到的問題"},{"english":"interact with different kinds of people","chinese":"與不同類型的人互動"},{"english":"gradually makes them","chinese":"逐漸令他們"},{"english":"more resilient and capable","chinese":"更有抗逆力和能力"},{"english":"moves abroad for work","chinese":"移居海外工作"},{"english":"adjust to","chinese":"適應"},{"english":"a new culture","chinese":"新文化"},{"english":"new colleagues","chinese":"新同事"},{"english":"new expectations","chinese":"新期望"},{"english":"leaves them more confident and employable","chinese":"令他們變得更有信心和更具就業能力"},{"english":"constant change","chinese":"持續不斷的改變"},{"english":"create instability","chinese":"造成不穩定"},{"english":"too frequently","chinese":"過於頻繁地"},{"english":"struggle to build","chinese":"難以建立"},{"english":"lasting support networks","chinese":"持久的支援網絡"},{"english":"a real sense of security","chinese":"真正的安全感"},{"english":"continually moves from...to...","chinese":"不斷從……轉到……"},{"english":"one short-term role to another","chinese":"一份短期職位到另一份短期職位"},{"english":"enjoy variety","chinese":"享受變化"},{"english":"financially and emotionally unsettled","chinese":"在財務和情感上感到不安定"},{"english":"by contrast","chinese":"相比之下"},{"english":"try to avoid change","chinese":"嘗試避免改變"},{"english":"benefit from stability","chinese":"從穩定中受惠"},{"english":"become a serious limitation","chinese":"成為嚴重限制"},{"english":"remaining in a familiar environment","chinese":"留在熟悉的環境"},{"english":"reduces stress","chinese":"減少壓力"},{"english":"routines are predictable","chinese":"日常規律是可預期的"},{"english":"responsibilities are clear","chinese":"責任清晰"},{"english":"long-term relationships","chinese":"長遠關係"},{"english":"deepen over time","chinese":"隨時間加深"},{"english":"stays in one community","chinese":"留在同一個社區"},{"english":"close friendships","chinese":"親密友誼"},{"english":"a reliable support system","chinese":"可靠的支援系統"},{"english":"a steady career path","chinese":"穩定的事業發展路徑"},{"english":"excessive caution","chinese":"過度謹慎"},{"english":"leads to stagnation","chinese":"導致停滯不前"},{"english":"reject new technology","chinese":"拒絕新科技"},{"english":"simply because","chinese":"只是因為"},{"english":"feel uncomfortable","chinese":"感到不舒服；不自在"},{"english":"fall behind","chinese":"落後"},{"english":"both personally and professionally","chinese":"在個人和專業方面"},{"english":"refuses to learn","chinese":"拒絕學習"},{"english":"digital systems","chinese":"數碼系統"},{"english":"preserve the comfort of old habits","chinese":"保持舊習慣帶來的舒適感"},{"english":"for a while","chinese":"一段時間"},{"english":"eventually become less useful","chinese":"最終變得較沒用處"},{"english":"a changing workplace","chinese":"不斷變化的工作場所"},{"english":"both attitudes","chinese":"兩種態度"},{"english":"understandable advantages","chinese":"可以理解的好處"},{"english":"encourages development","chinese":"鼓勵發展"},{"english":"offers stability","chinese":"提供穩定"},{"english":"nevertheless","chinese":"然而"},{"english":"welcoming change","chinese":"歡迎改變"},{"english":"a flexible person","chinese":"靈活的人"},{"english":"an inflexible one","chinese":"不靈活的人"},{"english":"lose valuable opportunities","chinese":"失去寶貴機會"},{"english":"never return","chinese":"永不再來"}]},"model-essay-4-ielts-cause-solution":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-4-ielts-cause-solution","essayKey":"cause-solution:4","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-4-ielts-cause-solution","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/problem-and-cause/EdmundBd9CnS-Q4","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"Internet access has become a normal part of childhood, especially as many children now use online platforms to chat, play games and build friendships. However, when this happens without adult supervision, children may be exposed to risks which they are not mature enough to recognise. The main problems are contact with dangerous strangers and cyberbullying, and these can be addressed through stronger parental guidance, school education and platform responsibility.","chinese":"互聯網使用已成為童年生活中很正常的一部分，尤其是現在許多兒童都會使用網上平台聊天、玩遊戲和建立友誼。 然而，當這種情況在沒有成年人監督下發生時，兒童可能會接觸到一些他們尚未成熟到能夠辨認的風險。 主要問題是接觸危險的陌生人以及網絡欺凌，而這些問題可以透過更強的家長引導、學校教育和平台責任來解決。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"The first major problem is that children can come into contact with people who hide their real identity. In gaming platforms, messaging apps or social media groups, an adult may pretend to be another child in order to gain trust, ask for private information, or persuade the child to keep secrets from their family. Since young children are often trusting and eager to be accepted, this can lead to grooming, blackmail or exploitation. A second problem is cyberbullying. Unlike ordinary playground conflict, online abuse can follow a child home, spread quickly, and feel impossible to escape. Repeated insults, rumours or humiliating images can seriously damage a child’s confidence and mental well-being.","chinese":"第一個主要問題是，兒童可能會接觸到隱藏自己真實身份的人。 在遊戲平台、即時通訊應用程式或社交媒體群組中，成年人可能會假裝成另一名兒童，以取得信任、索取私人資料，或說服孩子向家人保守秘密。 由於年幼兒童通常容易信任別人，而且渴望被接納，這可能會導致誘導、勒索或剝削。 第二個問題是網絡欺凌。 與普通的操場衝突不同，網上辱罵可以跟隨孩子回到家中，迅速擴散，並讓人感到無法逃避。 反覆的侮辱、謠言或令人羞辱的圖片，可能會嚴重損害孩子的自信心和心理健康。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"These problems can be reduced if parents take an active but sensible role in children’s internet use. Rather than simply banning the internet, parents should set clear rules, use age-appropriate safety settings, and regularly talk to their children about what they see online. This makes supervision feel like protection rather than punishment. Schools also have an important role to play. Digital safety lessons should teach children how to identify suspicious behaviour, protect personal information, block abusive users and report threatening messages. At the same time, technology companies should design safer spaces for young users, with stronger age checks, easier reporting tools and faster removal of harmful content.","chinese":"如果父母在孩子使用互聯網時扮演積極而理性的角色，這些問題是可以被減少的。 父母不應只是簡單地禁止孩子使用互聯網，而應該設定清晰的規則，使用適合年齡的安全設定，並定期與孩子談論他們在網上看到的內容。 這會令監督感覺像是一種保護，而不是懲罰。 學校也有重要的角色要發揮。 數碼安全課程應該教導兒童如何辨認可疑行為、保護個人資料、封鎖辱罵性的使用者，以及舉報具威脅性的訊息。 與此同時，科技公司應該為年幼使用者設計更安全的空間，包括更嚴格的年齡檢查、更容易使用的舉報工具，以及更快速移除有害內容的機制。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, unsupervised internet use can expose children to manipulation by strangers and damaging forms of cyberbullying. These dangers are best tackled through responsible parenting, practical digital education and safer online platforms.","chinese":"總結來說，沒有監督的互聯網使用可能會令兒童暴露於陌生人的操控，以及具傷害性的網絡欺凌之中。 這些危險最好透過負責任的家長教育、實用的數碼教育，以及更安全的網上平台來處理。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"internet access","chinese":"互聯網使用；上網渠道"},{"english":"a normal part of childhood","chinese":"童年生活的正常一部分"},{"english":"online platforms","chinese":"網上平台"},{"english":"build friendships","chinese":"建立友誼"},{"english":"without adult supervision","chinese":"沒有成人監督"},{"english":"be exposed to risks","chinese":"暴露於風險之中"},{"english":"mature enough to recognise","chinese":"成熟到足以辨認"},{"english":"dangerous strangers","chinese":"危險的陌生人"},{"english":"cyberbullying","chinese":"網絡欺凌"},{"english":"be addressed through","chinese":"可透過……處理"},{"english":"parental guidance","chinese":"家長指導"},{"english":"school education","chinese":"學校教育"},{"english":"platform responsibility","chinese":"平台責任"},{"english":"come into contact with","chinese":"接觸到；遇上"},{"english":"hide their real identity","chinese":"隱藏真實身份"},{"english":"gaming platforms","chinese":"遊戲平台"},{"english":"messaging apps","chinese":"即時通訊應用程式"},{"english":"social media groups","chinese":"社交媒體群組"},{"english":"pretend to be","chinese":"假扮成"},{"english":"gain trust","chinese":"取得信任"},{"english":"private information","chinese":"私人資料"},{"english":"persuade the child to keep secrets from","chinese":"說服孩子向……隱瞞秘密"},{"english":"trusting and eager to be accepted","chinese":"容易信任別人並渴望被接納"},{"english":"lead to grooming","chinese":"導致兒童誘騙"},{"english":"blackmail","chinese":"勒索"},{"english":"exploitation","chinese":"剝削；利用"},{"english":"ordinary playground conflict","chinese":"一般校園衝突"},{"english":"online abuse","chinese":"網上辱罵；網上傷害"},{"english":"follow a child home","chinese":"追到孩子家中；延伸到家中"},{"english":"spread quickly","chinese":"迅速傳開"},{"english":"impossible to escape","chinese":"令人覺得無法逃避"},{"english":"repeated insults","chinese":"反覆侮辱"},{"english":"rumours","chinese":"謠言"},{"english":"humiliating images","chinese":"令人羞辱的圖片"},{"english":"damage a child's confidence","chinese":"打擊孩子的自信"},{"english":"mental well-being","chinese":"精神健康"},{"english":"take an active but sensible role in","chinese":"在……中採取積極但理性的角色"},{"english":"children's internet use","chinese":"兒童使用互聯網"},{"english":"rather than simply banning","chinese":"而不是單純禁止"},{"english":"set clear rules","chinese":"訂立清晰規則"},{"english":"age-appropriate safety settings","chinese":"適合年齡的安全設定"},{"english":"regularly talk to","chinese":"定期與……交談"},{"english":"what they see online","chinese":"他們在網上看到的內容"},{"english":"supervision feel like protection rather than punishment","chinese":"令監督感覺像保護而不是懲罰"},{"english":"have an important role to play","chinese":"有重要角色"},{"english":"digital safety lessons","chinese":"數碼安全課程"},{"english":"identify suspicious behaviour","chinese":"辨認可疑行為"},{"english":"protect personal information","chinese":"保護個人資料"},{"english":"block abusive users","chinese":"封鎖辱罵性用戶"},{"english":"report threatening messages","chinese":"舉報威脅訊息"},{"english":"technology companies","chinese":"科技公司"},{"english":"safer spaces for young users","chinese":"給年輕用戶的更安全空間"},{"english":"stronger age checks","chinese":"更嚴格的年齡核查"},{"english":"easier reporting tools","chinese":"更易用的舉報工具"},{"english":"faster removal of harmful content","chinese":"更快移除有害內容"},{"english":"harmful content","chinese":"有害內容"},{"english":"unsupervised internet use","chinese":"無人監督下使用互聯網"},{"english":"expose children to manipulation by strangers","chinese":"令兒童暴露於陌生人的操控之中"},{"english":"manipulation by strangers","chinese":"被陌生人操控"},{"english":"damaging forms of cyberbullying","chinese":"具傷害性的網絡欺凌形式"},{"english":"be best tackled through","chinese":"最好透過……處理"},{"english":"responsible parenting","chinese":"負責任的家長管教"},{"english":"practical digital education","chinese":"實用的數碼教育"},{"english":"safer online platforms","chinese":"更安全的網上平台"}]},"model-essay-4-ielts-direct-question":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-4-ielts-direct-question","essayKey":"direct-question:4","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-4-ielts-direct-question","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/direct-question/EdmundBd9Dir-Q4","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"In sales, it is tempting to assume that the best employees are those who chase money most aggressively, because commission rewards output directly. I disagree with this view: money is not the true driving force behind sustained hard work, and recruitment should focus on character and customer-facing ability rather than financial hunger alone.","chinese":"在銷售行業中，人們很容易假設最好的員工就是那些最積極追求金錢的人，因為佣金會直接獎勵工作成果。 我不同意這種觀點：金錢並不是持續努力工作的真正推動力，而招聘應該著重於品格和面對客戶的能力，而不是單靠對金錢的渴望。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"Money may push people to make an extra call or close one more deal, but it rarely produces lasting dedication by itself. If a salesperson is motivated only by income, their effort depends on whether a reward is immediately visible. When targets become harder, customers become cautious, or rejection piles up, that motivation can burn out quickly. More importantly, a money-first employee may treat clients as transactions rather than people, which can damage trust and weaken long-term business relationships. Genuine hard work is more likely to come from professional pride, resilience, and a belief in the product being sold. These qualities keep a person steady when the easy rewards disappear.","chinese":"金錢也許能推動人們多打一通電話，或多完成一筆交易，但它本身很少能產生持久的投入感。 如果一名銷售人員只受到收入驅動，他們的努力便取決於回報是否能夠即時看見。 當目標變得更困難、客戶變得更謹慎，或者拒絕不斷累積時，這種動力便可能很快耗盡。 更重要的是，一個金錢至上的員工可能會把客戶視為交易，而不是有真實需要的人，這可能會損害信任，並削弱長期商業關係。 真正的努力工作更有可能來自專業自豪感、抗壓能力，以及對所銷售產品的信念。 當容易得到的回報消失時，這些特質能讓一個人保持穩定。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"When recruiting sales staff, companies should therefore consider several practical qualities. The first is communication skill: a good salesperson must listen carefully, explain benefits clearly, and adjust their tone to different customers. Sales is not merely talking; it is reading people. The second factor is resilience, because rejection is part of the job. A candidate who can stay calm after losing a deal is far more valuable than one who is energetic only when everything goes well. Finally, integrity should be treated as essential. Sales staff represent the company’s face, and one dishonest promise can poison a brand’s reputation for years.","chinese":"因此，在招聘銷售員工時，公司應該考慮幾項實際的特質。 第一項是溝通能力：一名優秀的銷售人員必須細心聆聽、清楚解釋產品好處，並根據不同客戶調整語氣。 銷售不只是說話；它是理解人。 第二個因素是抗壓能力，因為被拒絕是這份工作的一部分。 一個在失去交易後仍能保持冷靜的求職者，遠比一個只有在一切順利時才充滿幹勁的人更有價值。 最後，誠信應該被視為不可或缺的特質。 銷售員工代表公司的形象，而一個不誠實的承諾可能會多年來損害一個品牌的聲譽。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, money may be a useful incentive, but it should not be seen as the main engine of hard work. For sales positions, firms should recruit people who are persuasive, resilient, ethical, and genuinely capable of building trust with customers.","chinese":"總結來說，金錢也許是一種有用的激勵，但不應被視為努力工作的主要引擎。 對於銷售職位，公司應該招聘那些具說服力、有抗壓能力、有道德操守，並真正能夠與客戶建立信任的人。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"in sales","chinese":"在銷售行業"},{"english":"it is tempting to assume that","chinese":"很容易假設"},{"english":"chase money aggressively","chinese":"積極追求金錢"},{"english":"commission rewards output directly","chinese":"佣金直接獎勵業績"},{"english":"disagree with this view","chinese":"不同意這個看法"},{"english":"the true driving force behind","chinese":"……背後真正的推動力"},{"english":"sustained hard work","chinese":"持續努力工作"},{"english":"recruitment should focus on","chinese":"招聘應集中於"},{"english":"character","chinese":"品格"},{"english":"customer-facing ability","chinese":"面對顧客的能力"},{"english":"rather than financial hunger alone","chinese":"而不是單靠對金錢的渴求"},{"english":"financial hunger","chinese":"對金錢的渴求"},{"english":"make an extra call","chinese":"多打一個電話"},{"english":"close one more deal","chinese":"多完成一宗交易"},{"english":"lasting dedication","chinese":"持久的投入"},{"english":"by itself","chinese":"單靠本身"},{"english":"motivated only by income","chinese":"只受收入推動"},{"english":"depend on whether","chinese":"取決於是否"},{"english":"immediately visible","chinese":"即時可見"},{"english":"targets become harder","chinese":"目標變得更難"},{"english":"customers become cautious","chinese":"顧客變得謹慎"},{"english":"rejection piles up","chinese":"被拒絕的次數累積"},{"english":"burn out quickly","chinese":"很快耗盡"},{"english":"more importantly","chinese":"更重要的是"},{"english":"a money-first employee","chinese":"金錢至上的員工"},{"english":"treat clients as transactions","chinese":"將客戶視為交易"},{"english":"rather than people","chinese":"而不是視為人"},{"english":"damage trust","chinese":"損害信任"},{"english":"weaken long-term business relationships","chinese":"削弱長遠商業關係"},{"english":"genuine hard work","chinese":"真正的努力工作"},{"english":"be more likely to come from","chinese":"更可能來自"},{"english":"professional pride","chinese":"專業自豪感"},{"english":"a belief in the product","chinese":"對產品的信念"},{"english":"keep a person steady","chinese":"令一個人保持穩定"},{"english":"the easy rewards disappear","chinese":"容易得到的回報消失"},{"english":"sales staff","chinese":"銷售職員"},{"english":"practical qualities","chinese":"實際特質"},{"english":"communication skill","chinese":"溝通能力"},{"english":"listen carefully","chinese":"細心聆聽"},{"english":"explain benefits clearly","chinese":"清楚解釋好處"},{"english":"adjust their tone to","chinese":"按……調整語氣"},{"english":"different customers","chinese":"不同顧客"},{"english":"not merely talking","chinese":"不只是說話"},{"english":"reading people","chinese":"讀懂別人"},{"english":"part of the job","chinese":"工作的一部分"},{"english":"stay calm after losing a deal","chinese":"失去交易後保持冷靜"},{"english":"far more valuable than","chinese":"比……有價值得多"},{"english":"energetic only when","chinese":"只有在……時才有幹勁"},{"english":"everything goes well","chinese":"一切順利"},{"english":"integrity","chinese":"誠信"},{"english":"be treated as essential","chinese":"應被視為必要"},{"english":"represent the company's face","chinese":"代表公司的形象"},{"english":"a dishonest promise","chinese":"不誠實的承諾"},{"english":"poison a brand's reputation","chinese":"破壞品牌聲譽"},{"english":"for years","chinese":"多年來"},{"english":"a useful incentive","chinese":"有用的誘因"},{"english":"the main engine of hard work","chinese":"努力工作的主要動力"},{"english":"sales positions","chinese":"銷售職位"},{"english":"persuasive","chinese":"有說服力的"},{"english":"ethical","chinese":"有道德的"},{"english":"genuinely capable of","chinese":"真正有能力"},{"english":"building trust with customers","chinese":"與顧客建立信任"}]},"model-essay-4-ielts-discuss-both-views":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-4-ielts-discuss-both-views","essayKey":"discuss-both-views:4","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-4-ielts-discuss-both-views","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/discuss-both-views-your-opinion/EdmundBd9ExpBth-Q4","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"In many countries, small and medium-sized firms are built around family ownership, and this arrangement is often seen as a strong foundation for commercial success. I disagree. In my view, running a business mainly through family ties is not the best model, because it can weaken professional judgement and turn private conflict into commercial risk.","chinese":"在許多國家，中小型企業都是圍繞家族所有權建立起來的，而這種安排常被視為商業成功的穩固基礎。 我不同意。 在我看來，主要依靠家族關係來經營企業並不是最佳模式，因為這可能削弱專業判斷，並把私人衝突轉化為商業風險。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"The first problem is that family-run firms often blur the line between affection and competence. A successful company needs employees who are selected, promoted, and corrected according to performance. When relatives are given senior roles because of blood rather than ability, poor management may be protected by loyalty. This creates a serious chain of damage: capable non-family workers feel undervalued, standards become inconsistent, and difficult decisions are delayed. For example, if an owner’s son repeatedly loses important clients, other managers may hesitate to challenge him because criticism could be treated as a family insult. Over time, such favouritism reduces trust within the workplace and makes the firm less competitive.","chinese":"第一個問題是，家族經營的企業往往會模糊親情與能力之間的界線。 一間成功的公司需要根據表現來選拔、晉升和糾正員工。 當親屬因血緣而不是能力獲得高層職位時，糟糕的管理可能會受到忠誠感的保護。這會造成一連串嚴重損害：有能力的非家族員工會覺得自己不受重視，標準會變得不一致，而艱難的決定也會被拖延。 例如，如果老闆的兒子不斷失去重要客戶，其他經理可能會猶豫是否要質疑他，因為批評可能會被視為對家族的侮辱。 長遠而言，這種偏袒會削弱工作場所內的信任，並使企業的競爭力下降。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"Another major issue is that family disputes can easily spill into the business. In a professionally managed company, disagreements can be handled through contracts, clear job descriptions, and formal procedures. In a family firm, however, arguments over inheritance, leadership, or money may become deeply personal. A disagreement between siblings over who should take control of the company, for instance, can paralyse hiring, investment, and expansion plans. Ordinary staff may also feel forced to take sides, creating an unhealthy atmosphere in which business priorities are pushed behind personal loyalties. This is especially dangerous during succession, when the firm needs stability rather than rivalry. A company cannot grow steadily if its steering wheel is constantly pulled by family tension.","chinese":"另一個主要問題是，家族糾紛很容易蔓延到企業之中。 在一間由專業方式管理的公司中，分歧可透過合約、清晰的職責說明和正式程序來處理 然而，在家族企業中，圍繞繼承權、領導權或金錢的爭執可能會變得非常私人化。 例如，兄弟姊妹之間若因誰應該掌管公司而產生分歧，便可能令招聘、投資和擴展計劃陷入停頓。 普通員工也可能覺得自己被迫選邊站，從而造成一種不健康的氣氛，使商業優先事項被個人忠誠壓到後面。 這在接班期間尤其危險，因為企業在這個時候需要的是穩定，而不是競爭。 如果一間公司的方向盤不斷被家族矛盾拉扯，它就不可能穩定成長。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"Overall, I believe family-run businesses are more likely to create problems than provide the ideal business structure. Businesses need fairness, expertise, and clear governance, and these qualities are often compromised when family relationships dominate commercial decisions.","chinese":"總結來說，我認為家族經營的企業更可能製造問題，而不是提供理想的企業結構。 企業需要公平、專業知識和清晰的治理，而當家族關係主導商業決策時，這些特質往往會受到損害。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"small and medium-sized firms","chinese":"中小型企業"},{"english":"be built around","chinese":"以……為核心建立"},{"english":"family ownership","chinese":"家族擁有權"},{"english":"this arrangement","chinese":"這種安排"},{"english":"be seen as","chinese":"被視為"},{"english":"a strong foundation for","chinese":"……的穩固基礎"},{"english":"commercial success","chinese":"商業成功"},{"english":"In my view","chinese":"在我看來"},{"english":"family ties","chinese":"家族關係"},{"english":"the best model","chinese":"最佳模式"},{"english":"weaken professional judgement","chinese":"削弱專業判斷"},{"english":"private conflict","chinese":"私人衝突"},{"english":"commercial risk","chinese":"商業風險"},{"english":"The first problem is that","chinese":"第一個問題是"},{"english":"family-run firms","chinese":"家族經營企業"},{"english":"blur the line between","chinese":"模糊……之間的界線"},{"english":"affection and competence","chinese":"感情和能力"},{"english":"selected, promoted, and corrected","chinese":"被挑選、晉升和糾正"},{"english":"according to performance","chinese":"根據表現"},{"english":"given senior roles","chinese":"被給予高級職位"},{"english":"because of blood rather than ability","chinese":"因血緣而不是能力"},{"english":"poor management","chinese":"糟糕的管理"},{"english":"protected by loyalty","chinese":"受到忠誠保護"},{"english":"a serious chain of damage","chinese":"一連串嚴重損害"},{"english":"capable non-family workers","chinese":"有能力的非家族員工"},{"english":"feel undervalued","chinese":"感到不受重視"},{"english":"standards become inconsistent","chinese":"標準變得不一致"},{"english":"difficult decisions are delayed","chinese":"困難決定被拖延"},{"english":"repeatedly loses important clients","chinese":"反覆失去重要客戶"},{"english":"hesitate to challenge","chinese":"猶豫是否挑戰；不敢質疑"},{"english":"be treated as","chinese":"被視為"},{"english":"a family insult","chinese":"對家族的冒犯"},{"english":"Over time","chinese":"隨時間"},{"english":"favouritism","chinese":"偏私；偏袒"},{"english":"reduces trust within","chinese":"降低……內部的信任"},{"english":"less competitive","chinese":"競爭力較弱"},{"english":"Another major issue is that","chinese":"另一個主要問題是"},{"english":"family disputes","chinese":"家族糾紛"},{"english":"spill into","chinese":"蔓延到"},{"english":"professionally managed company","chinese":"專業管理的公司"},{"english":"be handled through","chinese":"透過……處理"},{"english":"clear job descriptions","chinese":"清晰的職位說明"},{"english":"formal procedures","chinese":"正式程序"},{"english":"arguments over","chinese":"關於……的爭執"},{"english":"inheritance","chinese":"繼承權；遺產"},{"english":"deeply personal","chinese":"非常私人化"},{"english":"a disagreement between siblings","chinese":"兄弟姊妹之間的分歧"},{"english":"take control of","chinese":"掌控"},{"english":"paralyse hiring","chinese":"令招聘停頓"},{"english":"investment and expansion plans","chinese":"投資和擴展計劃"},{"english":"ordinary staff","chinese":"普通員工"},{"english":"feel forced to","chinese":"感到被迫"},{"english":"take sides","chinese":"選邊站"},{"english":"an unhealthy atmosphere","chinese":"不健康的氣氛"},{"english":"business priorities","chinese":"商業優先事項"},{"english":"pushed behind","chinese":"被放在……之後"},{"english":"personal loyalties","chinese":"私人忠誠"},{"english":"especially dangerous during","chinese":"在……期間特別危險"},{"english":"succession","chinese":"接班；繼承"},{"english":"stability rather than rivalry","chinese":"穩定而不是競爭"},{"english":"grow steadily","chinese":"穩定成長"},{"english":"steering wheel","chinese":"方向盤"},{"english":"family tension","chinese":"家族緊張關係"},{"english":"more likely to","chinese":"更有可能"},{"english":"create problems than provide","chinese":"造成問題而不是提供"},{"english":"the ideal business structure","chinese":"理想的企業結構"},{"english":"fairness, expertise, and clear governance","chinese":"公平、專業知識和清晰管治"},{"english":"clear governance","chinese":"清晰管治"},{"english":"be compromised","chinese":"被削弱；受到損害"},{"english":"family relationships dominate","chinese":"家族關係佔主導"},{"english":"commercial decisions","chinese":"商業決策"}]},"model-essay-4-ielts-opinion":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-4-ielts-opinion","essayKey":"opinion:4","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-4-ielts-opinion","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/opinions/EdmundBd9OP-Q4","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"Artists are often expected to challenge convention, so some degree of creative freedom is clearly necessary. Some people therefore argue that they should have total freedom to express any thoughts they choose. This essay will argue that this view is wrong because unlimited artistic expression can damage society and because no one who speaks to the public should escape responsibility.","chinese":"人們通常期待藝術家挑戰傳統，因此某種程度的創作自由顯然是必要的。 因此，有些人主張，藝術家應該擁有完全的自由，去表達任何他們想表達的想法。 本文將論證，這種觀點是錯誤的，因為毫無限制的藝術表達可能會傷害社會，而且任何向公眾發聲的人都不應逃避責任。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"The first reason total freedom should not be allowed is that art can shape attitudes, not merely reflect them. When films, lyrics or exhibitions glorify racial hatred, violence or extremism, repeated exposure can make such ideas seem less shocking and more defensible. Once this happens, discrimination and aggression become easier to excuse in daily life. For example, propaganda art has often been used to dehumanise minorities before broader hostility followed. Unrestricted expression can also harm people directly. Work that humiliates vulnerable groups for attention may create fear, distress and exclusion, especially when it spreads rapidly online. Artistic freedom, therefore, cannot be unlimited.","chinese":"第一個不應允許完全自由的原因是，藝術不只是反映態度，它也能塑造態度。 當電影、歌詞或展覽美化種族仇恨、暴力或極端思想時，反覆接觸這些內容會讓這些想法看起來不再那麼令人震驚，甚至更容易被辯護。 一旦出現這種情況，歧視與攻擊行為在日常生活中就會變得更容易被合理化。 例如，宣傳藝術經常被用來先剝奪少數群體的人性，而更廣泛的敵意往往隨後而來。 不受限制的表達也可能直接傷害他人。 那些為了吸引關注而羞辱弱勢群體的作品，可能會造成恐懼、痛苦與排斥，尤其當它們在網路上快速傳播時更是如此。 因此，藝術自由不可能是毫無限制的。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"A second reason is that public expression always carries public responsibility. Once a work is published or performed, it is no longer a private thought; it becomes an act that can affect other people's dignity, safety and reputation. If artists received absolute protection, they could evade accountability for defamation or incitement simply by calling such acts art. No fair society should place any group above the law. Moreover, creativity itself does not require total freedom. Boundaries often force artists to rely on symbolism, irony and craft, which can make criticism more powerful rather than less. Many great novels, films and satirical works challenge authority strongly without crossing basic legal or moral lines.","chinese":"第二個原因是，公開表達永遠伴隨著公開責任。 一旦作品被出版或表演，它就不再只是私人想法；它會變成一種可能影響他人尊嚴、安全與名譽的行為。 如果藝術家獲得絕對保護，他們就可能只靠把某些行為稱為藝術，來逃避對誹謗或煽動行為的責任。 任何公平的社會都不應把任何群體置於法律之上。 此外，創造力本身並不需要完全的自由。 界線往往會迫使藝術家依靠象徵、反諷與技巧，而這反而可能使批評更有力量，而不是削弱它。 許多偉大的小說、電影和諷刺作品，都能強烈挑戰權威，同時又不越過基本的法律或道德界線。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, I completely disagree that artists should have total freedom to express any idea whatsoever. Creativity needs room to develop, but once expression seriously harms others or violates their rights, society is justified in imposing limits.","chinese":"總而言之，我完全不同意藝術家應該擁有表達任何想法的絕對自由。 創造力的確需要發展空間，但一旦某種表達嚴重傷害他人，或侵犯他人的權利，社會就有正當理由加以限制。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"be expected to","chinese":"被期望去"},{"english":"challenge convention","chinese":"挑戰傳統；挑戰常規"},{"english":"some degree of creative freedom","chinese":"某程度的創作自由"},{"english":"clearly necessary","chinese":"明顯必要"},{"english":"total freedom to","chinese":"完全自由去"},{"english":"express any thoughts they choose","chinese":"表達任何自己選擇的想法"},{"english":"this view is wrong","chinese":"這個觀點是錯誤的"},{"english":"unlimited artistic expression","chinese":"無限制的藝術表達"},{"english":"damage society","chinese":"損害社會"},{"english":"speak to the public","chinese":"向公眾發聲"},{"english":"escape responsibility","chinese":"逃避責任"},{"english":"should not be allowed","chinese":"不應被容許"},{"english":"shape attitudes","chinese":"塑造態度"},{"english":"not merely reflect them","chinese":"不只是反映它們"},{"english":"films, lyrics or exhibitions","chinese":"電影、歌詞或展覽"},{"english":"glorify racial hatred","chinese":"美化種族仇恨"},{"english":"violence or extremism","chinese":"暴力或極端主義"},{"english":"repeated exposure","chinese":"反覆接觸"},{"english":"make such ideas seem less shocking","chinese":"令這些想法顯得不那麼令人震驚"},{"english":"more defensible","chinese":"更像是可以辯護的"},{"english":"once this happens","chinese":"一旦這種情況發生"},{"english":"discrimination and aggression","chinese":"歧視和攻擊行為"},{"english":"become easier to excuse","chinese":"變得更容易被合理化"},{"english":"in daily life","chinese":"在日常生活中"},{"english":"propaganda art","chinese":"宣傳藝術"},{"english":"be used to","chinese":"被用作"},{"english":"dehumanise minorities","chinese":"將少數群體非人化"},{"english":"broader hostility","chinese":"更廣泛的敵意"},{"english":"unrestricted expression","chinese":"不受限制的表達"},{"english":"harm people directly","chinese":"直接傷害他人"},{"english":"work that humiliates vulnerable groups","chinese":"羞辱弱勢群體的作品"},{"english":"vulnerable groups","chinese":"弱勢群體"},{"english":"for attention","chinese":"為了吸引注意"},{"english":"create fear, distress and exclusion","chinese":"製造恐懼、困擾和排斥"},{"english":"especially when","chinese":"尤其當"},{"english":"spread rapidly online","chinese":"在網上迅速傳播"},{"english":"cannot be unlimited","chinese":"不能是無限制的"},{"english":"public expression","chinese":"公開表達"},{"english":"carry public responsibility","chinese":"承擔公共責任"},{"english":"be published or performed","chinese":"被出版或演出"},{"english":"no longer a private thought","chinese":"不再是私人想法"},{"english":"become an act that","chinese":"成為一種會……的行為"},{"english":"affect other people's dignity","chinese":"影響他人的尊嚴"},{"english":"safety and reputation","chinese":"安全和名譽"},{"english":"receive absolute protection","chinese":"獲得絕對保護"},{"english":"evade accountability for","chinese":"逃避對……的問責"},{"english":"defamation","chinese":"誹謗"},{"english":"incitement","chinese":"煽動"},{"english":"simply by calling such acts art","chinese":"只靠把這些行為稱為藝術"},{"english":"no fair society should","chinese":"沒有公平社會應該"},{"english":"place any group above the law","chinese":"令任何群體凌駕於法律之上"},{"english":"moreover","chinese":"此外"},{"english":"creativity itself","chinese":"創意本身"},{"english":"require total freedom","chinese":"需要完全自由"},{"english":"boundaries","chinese":"界限；限制"},{"english":"force artists to rely on","chinese":"迫使藝術家依靠"},{"english":"symbolism","chinese":"象徵手法"},{"english":"irony","chinese":"反諷"},{"english":"craft","chinese":"技巧；藝術手法"},{"english":"make criticism more powerful","chinese":"令批判更有力量"},{"english":"rather than less","chinese":"而不是更少"},{"english":"satirical works","chinese":"諷刺作品"},{"english":"challenge authority","chinese":"挑戰權威"},{"english":"without crossing","chinese":"在不越過……的情況下"},{"english":"basic legal or moral lines","chinese":"基本法律或道德界線"},{"english":"any idea whatsoever","chinese":"任何想法"},{"english":"room to develop","chinese":"發展空間"},{"english":"seriously harms others","chinese":"嚴重傷害他人"},{"english":"violates their rights","chinese":"侵犯他人的權利"},{"english":"be justified in","chinese":"有合理理由去"},{"english":"imposing limits","chinese":"施加限制"}]},"model-essay-4-ielts-task1-bar-charts":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-4-ielts-task1-bar-charts","essayKey":"bar-charts:4","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-4-ielts-task1-bar-charts","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-1/bar-charts/bar-chart-4","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"The bar chart compares the percentages of households living in owner-occupied and rented accommodation in England and Wales between 1918 and 2011.","chinese":"這張柱狀圖比較了 1918 年至 2011 年間，英格蘭和威爾斯居住在自有住房和租住住房中的家庭比例。"},{"label":"Overview","english":"Overall, home ownership followed a clear upward trajectory for most of the period, whereas renting moved in the opposite direction. The two categories were equal in 1971, after which ownership became dominant, although it slipped slightly in the final year.","chinese":"整體而言，在大部分期間，自有住房比例呈現明顯上升趨勢；相反，租住住房比例則朝相反方向變化。 這兩個類別在 1971 年持平；其後，自有住房成為主導類別，儘管它在最後一年略有回落。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"In 1918, renting accounted for by far the larger share, at just under four fifths of households, while ownership stood at only about 22%. By 1939 and 1953, the rental figure had fallen to around 68%, with owner-occupation rising to roughly 31–32%. The gap narrowed further in 1961, when about 42% of households owned their homes, compared with just under 60% that rented.","chinese":"在 1918 年，租住住房佔明顯較大的比例，略低於五分之四；而自有住房比例僅約為 22% 。 到 1939 年和 1953 年，租住住房比例已下降至約 68% ，而自有住房比例則上升至約 31% 至 32% 。 到 1961 年，兩者之間的差距進一步收窄，當時約 42% 的家庭擁有自己的住房，而租住住房的比例則略低於 60% 。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"The turning point came in 1971, when both categories stood at exactly 50%. Thereafter, ownership climbed to approximately 60% in 1981 and almost 70% in 2001, reaching its peak. By contrast, renting declined to just over 30% by 2001. In 2011, however, the pattern changed modestly: ownership decreased to about 64%, while renting recovered to around 36%.","chinese":"轉折點出現在 1971 年，當時兩個類別的比例均為 50% 。 此後，自有住房比例在 1981 年上升至約 60% ，並在 2001 年接近 70% ，達最高點。 相比之下，租住住房比例到 2001 年下降至略高於 30% 。 然而，到 2011 年，這一模式出現了輕微變化：自有住房比例下降至約 64% ，而租住住房比例則回升至約 36% 。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"compares the percentages of households","chinese":"比較住戶百分比"},{"english":"households living in","chinese":"居於……的住戶"},{"english":"owner-occupied accommodation","chinese":"自置物業"},{"english":"rented accommodation","chinese":"租住物業"},{"english":"between 1918 and 2011","chinese":"在1918年至2011年之間"},{"english":"home ownership","chinese":"置業；自置居所"},{"english":"followed a clear upward trajectory","chinese":"呈現明顯上升趨勢"},{"english":"for most of the period","chinese":"在大部分時期"},{"english":"whereas","chinese":"然而；而"},{"english":"moved in the opposite direction","chinese":"朝相反方向變化"},{"english":"the two categories were equal","chinese":"兩個類別相同"},{"english":"after which","chinese":"此後；之後"},{"english":"ownership became dominant","chinese":"自置居所成為主導"},{"english":"slipped slightly","chinese":"輕微下跌"},{"english":"in the final year","chinese":"在最後一年"},{"english":"renting accounted for","chinese":"租住佔"},{"english":"by far the larger share","chinese":"遙遙領先的較大比例"},{"english":"at just under four fifths","chinese":"略低於五分之四"},{"english":"while ownership stood at","chinese":"而自置居所處於"},{"english":"stood at only about 22%","chinese":"僅約為22%"},{"english":"by 1939 and 1953","chinese":"到1939年和1953年"},{"english":"the rental figure","chinese":"租住比例"},{"english":"had fallen to around 68%","chinese":"已跌至約68%"},{"english":"owner-occupation","chinese":"自置居所"},{"english":"rising to roughly 31–32%","chinese":"上升至約31%至32%"},{"english":"the gap narrowed further","chinese":"差距進一步收窄"},{"english":"in 1961","chinese":"在1961年"},{"english":"owned their homes","chinese":"擁有自己的住所"},{"english":"compared with","chinese":"與……相比"},{"english":"just under 60%","chinese":"略低於60%"},{"english":"the turning point came in","chinese":"轉捩點出現在"},{"english":"stood at exactly 50%","chinese":"正好處於50%"},{"english":"Thereafter","chinese":"此後"},{"english":"climbed to approximately 60%","chinese":"攀升至約60%"},{"english":"almost 70%","chinese":"接近70%"},{"english":"reaching its peak","chinese":"達到高峰"},{"english":"By contrast","chinese":"相比之下"},{"english":"declined to just over 30%","chinese":"下降至略高於30%"},{"english":"by 2001","chinese":"到2001年"},{"english":"the pattern changed modestly","chinese":"模式出現輕微變化"},{"english":"ownership decreased to about 64%","chinese":"自置居所下降至約64%"},{"english":"while renting recovered to","chinese":"而租住回升至"},{"english":"recovered to around 36%","chinese":"回升至約36%"}]},"model-essay-4-ielts-task1-line-graph":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-4-ielts-task1-line-graph","essayKey":"line-graph:4","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-4-ielts-task1-line-graph","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-1/line-graphs/line-graph-4","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"The line graph compares the numbers of shop closures and openings in one country from 2011 to 2018.","chinese":"這張折線圖比較了某一國家在 2011 年至 2018 年間商店關閉和新開商店的數量。"},{"label":"Overview","english":"Overall, shop openings showed a clear downward trend, ending at their lowest point, while closures fluctuated markedly. Apart from the initial year and the exceptional trough in closures in 2015, more shops closed than opened.","chinese":"整體而言，新開商店數量呈現明顯下降趨勢，並在最後達到最低點；相反，關店數量則大幅波動。 除第一年以及 2015 年關店數出現異常低谷之外，關閉的商店數量多於新開商店數量。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"In 2011, openings were far higher, at about 8,500, compared with roughly 6,400 closures. The number of new shops then almost halved to around 4,000 in 2012, before recovering to about 5,000 in 2013 and just over 6,000 in 2014. After this brief rebound, openings fell back to 4,000 in 2015 and 2016, edged up slightly to around 4,200 in 2017, and then declined to approximately 3,000 in 2018.","chinese":"2011 年，新開商店數量遠高於關店數，約為 8,500 間，而關店數約為 6,400 間。 之後，新開商店數量在 2012 年幾乎減半至約 4,000 間，然後在 2013 年回升至約5,000 間，並在 2014 年升至略高於 6,000 間。 在這次短暫回升之後，新開商店數量在 2015 年和 2016 年回落至 4,000 間， 2017年小幅上升至約 4,200 間，然後在 2018 年下降至約 3,000 間。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"Closures followed a less steady pattern. The figure slipped from around 6,400 to just under 6,000 in 2012, then rose to a peak of about 7,200 in 2013. It remained high in 2014, at roughly 6,500, before plunging to only about 500 in 2015. However, closures rebounded sharply to just over 5,000 in 2016 and then stayed close to this level in the final two years.","chinese":"關店數量的走勢則較不穩定。 該數字從約 6,400 間下降至 2012 年的略低於 6,000 間，之後在 2013 年上升至約7,200 間的高峰。 2014 年，關店數仍然維持在較高水平，約為 6,500 間，然後在 2015 年急跌至只有約 500 間。 然而，關店數在 2016 年大幅反彈至略高於 5,000 間，之後在最後兩年保持在接近這一水平。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"line graph","chinese":"折線圖"},{"english":"shop closures and openings","chinese":"商店結業及開業"},{"english":"shop closures","chinese":"商店結業"},{"english":"shop openings","chinese":"商店開業"},{"english":"from 2011 to 2018","chinese":"由2011年至2018年"},{"english":"showed a clear downward trend","chinese":"呈現明顯下降趨勢"},{"english":"downward trend","chinese":"下降趨勢"},{"english":"ending at their lowest point","chinese":"最後跌至最低點"},{"english":"lowest point","chinese":"最低點"},{"english":"fluctuated markedly","chinese":"明顯波動"},{"english":"apart from","chinese":"除了……之外"},{"english":"the initial year","chinese":"最初一年"},{"english":"exceptional trough","chinese":"異常低谷"},{"english":"trough in closures","chinese":"結業數字的低谷"},{"english":"more shops closed than opened","chinese":"結業商店多於開業商店"},{"english":"far higher","chinese":"高得多"},{"english":"at about 8,500","chinese":"約為8,500"},{"english":"compared with roughly","chinese":"與約……相比"},{"english":"roughly 6,400 closures","chinese":"約6,400宗結業"},{"english":"the number of new shops","chinese":"新開商店數目"},{"english":"almost halved to","chinese":"幾乎減半至"},{"english":"around 4,000","chinese":"約4,000"},{"english":"before recovering to","chinese":"之後回升至"},{"english":"recovering to","chinese":"回升至"},{"english":"just over 6,000","chinese":"略高於6,000"},{"english":"brief rebound","chinese":"短暫反彈"},{"english":"fell back to","chinese":"回落至"},{"english":"edged up slightly","chinese":"輕微上升"},{"english":"declined to approximately","chinese":"下降至約"},{"english":"approximately 3,000","chinese":"約3,000"},{"english":"followed a less steady pattern","chinese":"呈現較不穩定的模式"},{"english":"less steady pattern","chinese":"較不穩定的模式"},{"english":"the figure slipped from…to…","chinese":"數字由……微跌至……"},{"english":"slipped from","chinese":"由……微跌"},{"english":"just under 6,000","chinese":"略低於6,000"},{"english":"rose to a peak of","chinese":"上升至峰值"},{"english":"peak of about 7,200","chinese":"約7,200的峰值"},{"english":"remained high","chinese":"維持高水平"},{"english":"at roughly 6,500","chinese":"約為6,500"},{"english":"before plunging to","chinese":"之後急跌至"},{"english":"plunged to only about","chinese":"急跌至只有約"},{"english":"only about 500","chinese":"只有約500"},{"english":"however","chinese":"然而"},{"english":"rebounded sharply","chinese":"大幅反彈"},{"english":"just over 5,000","chinese":"略高於5,000"},{"english":"stayed close to this level","chinese":"維持接近這一水平"},{"english":"this level","chinese":"這一水平"},{"english":"in the final two years","chinese":"在最後兩年"},{"english":"clear downward movement","chinese":"明顯下跌走勢"},{"english":"marked fluctuation","chinese":"明顯波動"},{"english":"initial gap","chinese":"初期差距"},{"english":"final figure","chinese":"最終數字"}]},"model-essay-4-ielts-task1-maps":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-4-ielts-task1-maps","essayKey":"maps:4","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-4-ielts-task1-maps","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-1/maps/maps-4","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"The two maps compare the present industrial area in Norbiton with the proposed redevelopment of the site.","chinese":"這兩幅地圖比較了諾比頓目前的工業區與該地點擬議的未來重建規劃。"},{"label":"Overview","english":"Overall, the area is set to be transformed from a factory complex into a residential district with public amenities. The road network will also be expanded, especially northwards across the river and southwards to the main road, while the river and the main east–west road will largely remain in place.","chinese":"整體而言，該區域將由一個工廠群轉變為設有公共設施的住宅區。 道路網也將會擴展，尤其會向北跨過河流，並向南連接主要道路；同時，河流和主要東西向道路大致會保留在原位。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"Currently, the site is centred on a roundabout south of the river. From this junction, one road runs east, with several factories on both sides and another at its far end. Other factories stand immediately north and west of the roundabout, and a short road links the junction to the main east–west road. The town lies to the west.","chinese":"目前，該地點以河流以南的一個迴旋處為中心。 從這個交匯處，一條道路向東延伸，道路兩側有數間工廠，最東端還有另一間工廠。 其他工廠位於迴旋處正北方和西側，而一條短路把這個交匯處連接到主要的東西向道路。 城鎮位於西側。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"In the future plan, all factories will be removed and replaced mainly by housing. Homes will be added west of the roundabout, along the eastern road and, after a bridge is built, north of the river. A second roundabout will be constructed on the southern access road. Shops, a medical centre, a playground and a school will also be introduced in the southern, eastern and northeastern parts of the site.","chinese":"在未來規劃中，所有工廠都將被移除，並主要由住宅取代。 住宅將會被增設在迴旋處西側、東面道路沿線，及在橋樑建成後的河流北側。 第二個迴旋處將會建在南面的通道上。 商店、醫療中心、遊樂場和學校也將分別被引入該地點南部、東部和東北部。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"the maps below","chinese":"以下地圖"},{"english":"an industrial area","chinese":"工業區"},{"english":"the town of Norbiton","chinese":"Norbiton 鎮"},{"english":"planned future development","chinese":"計劃中的未來發展"},{"english":"future development of the site","chinese":"該地點的未來發展"},{"english":"summarise the information","chinese":"概述資料"},{"english":"by selecting and reporting","chinese":"透過選取並報告……"},{"english":"the main features","chinese":"主要特徵"},{"english":"make comparisons where relevant","chinese":"在相關之處作出比較"},{"english":"compare X with Y","chinese":"比較 X 和 Y"},{"english":"the present industrial area","chinese":"現時的工業區"},{"english":"the proposed redevelopment","chinese":"擬議的重建計劃"},{"english":"redevelopment of the site","chinese":"該地點的重建"},{"english":"is set to be transformed","chinese":"將會被改造成"},{"english":"be transformed from X into Y","chinese":"由 X 改造成 Y"},{"english":"a factory complex","chinese":"工廠群；工廠綜合區"},{"english":"a residential district","chinese":"住宅區"},{"english":"public amenities","chinese":"公共設施"},{"english":"the road network","chinese":"道路網絡"},{"english":"will be expanded","chinese":"將會擴展"},{"english":"northwards across the river","chinese":"向北跨過河流"},{"english":"southwards to the main road","chinese":"向南伸延至主要道路"},{"english":"the main road","chinese":"主要道路"},{"english":"the main east–west road","chinese":"主要東西向道路"},{"english":"will largely remain in place","chinese":"大致保留原位"},{"english":"be centred on","chinese":"以……為中心"},{"english":"a roundabout","chinese":"迴旋處"},{"english":"south of the river","chinese":"在河流以南"},{"english":"from this junction","chinese":"從這個交匯處"},{"english":"run east","chinese":"向東伸延"},{"english":"on both sides","chinese":"在兩旁"},{"english":"at its far end","chinese":"在其盡頭"},{"english":"stand immediately north and west of","chinese":"緊接位於……的北面和西面"},{"english":"immediately north of","chinese":"緊接在……北面"},{"english":"west of the roundabout","chinese":"在迴旋處西面"},{"english":"a short road","chinese":"一條短路"},{"english":"link X to Y","chinese":"連接 X 和 Y"},{"english":"the junction","chinese":"交匯處"},{"english":"lie to the west","chinese":"位於西面"},{"english":"in the future plan","chinese":"在未來規劃中"},{"english":"will be removed","chinese":"將會被拆除"},{"english":"be replaced mainly by","chinese":"主要被……取代"},{"english":"housing","chinese":"住宅"},{"english":"homes will be added","chinese":"將會增建住宅"},{"english":"to the west of the roundabout","chinese":"在迴旋處以西"},{"english":"along the eastern road","chinese":"沿着東面道路"},{"english":"after a bridge is built","chinese":"在橋建成後"},{"english":"a bridge is built","chinese":"建成一條橋"},{"english":"north of the river","chinese":"在河流以北"},{"english":"a second roundabout","chinese":"第二個迴旋處"},{"english":"will be constructed","chinese":"將會建成"},{"english":"the southern access road","chinese":"南面的出入通道"},{"english":"will also be introduced","chinese":"亦會增設"},{"english":"shops","chinese":"商店"},{"english":"a medical centre","chinese":"醫療中心"},{"english":"a playground","chinese":"遊樂場"},{"english":"in the southern part of the site","chinese":"在該地點南部"},{"english":"in the eastern part of the site","chinese":"在該地點東部"},{"english":"in the north-eastern part of the site","chinese":"在該地點東北部"},{"english":"residential and community facilities","chinese":"住宅及社區設施"},{"english":"replace industrial land with housing","chinese":"以住宅取代工業用地"}]},"model-essay-4-ielts-task1-mixed-charts":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-4-ielts-task1-mixed-charts","essayKey":"mixed-charts:4","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-4-ielts-task1-mixed-charts","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-1/mixed-charts/mixed-charts-4","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"The bar chart compares the export earnings of a country in five product categories in 2015 and 2016, while the table indicates the percentage change in each category over the same period.","chinese":"這張柱狀圖比較了一個國家在 2015 年和 2016 年五個產品類別的出口收入，而表格則顯示了同一期間每個類別出口價值的百分比變化。"},{"label":"Overview","english":"Overall, export revenue rose in four of the five categories, with gems and jewellery being the only sector to decline. Petroleum products remained the largest earner in both years, whereas textiles, despite starting from the lowest base, recorded the fastest growth.","chinese":"整體而言，五個類別中有四個的出口收入上升，只有寶石與珠寶這一類出現下降。 石油產品在兩年中都是出口收入最高的類別；相反，紡織品雖然起點最低，卻錄得最快的增長。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"In 2015, petroleum products generated about $61 billion, slightly more than engineered goods, at roughly $58 billion. Both categories increased in 2016: the former rose modestly by 3% to around $63 billion, while the latter climbed more sharply, by 8.5%, to approximately $62 billion. Gems and jewellery followed a different path, falling from about $43 billion to roughly $41 billion, a decrease of 5.18%.","chinese":"2015 年，石油產品創造了約 610 億美元的出口收入，略高於工程產品的約 580億美元。 這兩個類別在 2016 年均有所上升：前者溫和增長 3% ，達到約 630 億美元；後者則上升更明顯，增幅為 8.5% ，達到約 620 億美元。 寶石與珠寶則呈現不同走勢，從約 430 億美元下降至約 410 億美元，跌幅為。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"Among the lower-earning categories, agricultural products changed very little, remaining at around $31 billion in both years after a marginal rise of 0.81%. Textiles, by contrast, grew markedly from about $26 billion to roughly $31 billion, representing a 15.24% increase and making it nearly equal to agricultural products by 2016.","chinese":"在收入較低的類別中，農產品變化非常小，在輕微上升 0.81% 後，兩年都維持在約 310 億美元左右。 相比之下，紡織品從約 260 億美元顯著增長至約 310 億美元，增幅為 15.24% ，到2016 年幾乎與農產品持平。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"the chart below","chinese":"以下圖表"},{"english":"give information on","chinese":"提供關於……的資料"},{"english":"Anthropology graduates","chinese":"人類學畢業生"},{"english":"from one university","chinese":"來自某一所大學"},{"english":"after finishing","chinese":"完成……後"},{"english":"undergraduate degree course","chinese":"本科學位課程"},{"english":"the table shows","chinese":"表格顯示"},{"english":"salaries of","chinese":"……的薪酬"},{"english":"anthropologists in work","chinese":"在職人類學家"},{"english":"after five years","chinese":"五年後"},{"english":"summarise the information","chinese":"概述資料"},{"english":"by selecting and reporting","chinese":"透過選取並報告……"},{"english":"the main features","chinese":"主要特徵"},{"english":"make comparisons where relevant","chinese":"在相關之處作出比較"},{"english":"the bar chart compares","chinese":"柱形圖比較"},{"english":"export earnings","chinese":"出口收益"},{"english":"product categories","chinese":"產品類別"},{"english":"in 2015 and 2016","chinese":"在2015年和2016年"},{"english":"while the table indicates","chinese":"而表格顯示"},{"english":"percentage change","chinese":"百分比變化"},{"english":"in each category","chinese":"在每個類別中"},{"english":"over the same period","chinese":"在同一期間"},{"english":"export revenue","chinese":"出口收入"},{"english":"rose in four of the five categories","chinese":"在五個類別中的四個上升"},{"english":"with X being the only Y","chinese":"其中 X 是唯一的 Y"},{"english":"gems and jewellery","chinese":"寶石及珠寶"},{"english":"the only sector to decline","chinese":"唯一下跌的行業"},{"english":"petroleum products","chinese":"石油產品"},{"english":"remained the largest earner","chinese":"仍然是最大收益來源"},{"english":"in both years","chinese":"在兩年中"},{"english":"whereas","chinese":"而；相反"},{"english":"textiles","chinese":"紡織品"},{"english":"despite starting from","chinese":"儘管由……開始"},{"english":"the lowest base","chinese":"最低基數；最低起點"},{"english":"recorded the fastest growth","chinese":"錄得最快增長"},{"english":"generated about","chinese":"創造約……收益"},{"english":"slightly more than","chinese":"略多於"},{"english":"engineered goods","chinese":"工程產品"},{"english":"at roughly","chinese":"約為"},{"english":"both categories increased","chinese":"兩個類別均上升"},{"english":"the former","chinese":"前者"},{"english":"rose modestly by","chinese":"溫和上升……"},{"english":"to around","chinese":"至約……"},{"english":"while the latter","chinese":"而後者"},{"english":"climbed more sharply","chinese":"更大幅上升"},{"english":"followed a different path","chinese":"走勢不同"},{"english":"falling from X to Y","chinese":"由 X 下跌至 Y"},{"english":"a decrease of","chinese":"……的跌幅"},{"english":"lower-earning categories","chinese":"收益較低的類別"},{"english":"agricultural products","chinese":"農產品"},{"english":"changed very little","chinese":"變化很小"},{"english":"remaining at around","chinese":"維持在約……"},{"english":"a marginal rise","chinese":"輕微升幅"},{"english":"by contrast","chinese":"相比之下"},{"english":"grew markedly","chinese":"顯著增長"},{"english":"representing a 15.24% increase","chinese":"代表15.24%的升幅"},{"english":"making it nearly equal to","chinese":"使其幾乎等同於……"},{"english":"nearly equal to","chinese":"幾乎等同於"},{"english":"by 2016","chinese":"到2016年時"},{"english":"the highest-earning export","chinese":"最高收益出口產品"},{"english":"the fastest-growing category","chinese":"增長最快的類別"},{"english":"the only declining category","chinese":"唯一下跌的類別"},{"english":"narrow the gap","chinese":"收窄差距"},{"english":"a more modest increase","chinese":"較溫和的升幅"},{"english":"a sharper increase","chinese":"較大幅的升幅"},{"english":"remained broadly stable","chinese":"大致保持穩定"},{"english":"experienced a decline","chinese":"經歷下跌"},{"english":"showed little movement","chinese":"變動不大"},{"english":"almost caught up with","chinese":"幾乎追上"},{"english":"compared with","chinese":"與……相比"},{"english":"over the two-year period","chinese":"在兩年間"},{"english":"the overall trend","chinese":"整體趨勢"},{"english":"the strongest percentage growth","chinese":"最強百分比增長"},{"english":"the weakest performance","chinese":"最弱表現"}]},"model-essay-4-ielts-task1-pie-charts":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-4-ielts-task1-pie-charts","essayKey":"pie-charts:4","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-4-ielts-task1-pie-charts","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-1/pie-charts/pie-chart-4","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"The two pie charts compare energy consumption in an average Australian household with the proportions of greenhouse gas emissions produced by each use.","chinese":"這兩個圓餅圖比較澳洲一般家庭的能源消耗，以及每種能源用途所產生的溫室氣體排放比例。"},{"label":"Overview","english":"Overall, heating and water heating account for most household energy use, whereas emissions are more evenly distributed. Although heating is by far the largest consumer of energy, it produces a much smaller share of emissions; by contrast, other appliances, refrigeration and lighting generate proportionally more greenhouse gas than the energy they use.","chinese":"整體而言，供暖和熱水加熱佔家庭能源使用的大部分；相反，溫室氣體排放的分布則更加平均。 雖然供暖是迄今最大的能源消耗項目，但它產生的排放比例卻小得多；相反，其他電器、冷藏和照明所產生的溫室氣體比例高於它們所使用的能源比例。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"In the first chart, heating makes up 42% of total energy consumption, making it the dominant category. Water heating is second at 30%, so these two uses together represent almost three quarters of household energy demand. The remaining categories are much smaller: other appliances account for 15%, refrigeration for 7%, lighting for 4%, and cooling for just 2%.","chinese":"在第一個圖中，供暖佔總能源消耗的 42% ，使其成為主導類別。 熱水加熱位居第二，佔 30% ，因此這兩種用途合計幾乎佔家庭能源需求的四分之三。 其餘類別則小得多：其他電器佔 15% ，冷藏佔 7% ，照明佔 4% ，而冷氣只佔 2%。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"In the emissions chart, water heating is the leading source, at 32%, while other appliances almost double their energy share, producing 28% of emissions. Heating, however, is responsible for only 15%. Refrigeration and lighting also have higher emission figures, at 14% and 8% respectively, while cooling remains the smallest contributor, at 3%.","chinese":"在排放圖中，熱水加熱是最大的來源，佔 32% ；同時，其他電器的排放比例幾乎是其能源使用比例的兩倍，產生 28% 的排放。 然而，供暖只佔 15% 的排放。 冷藏和照明的排放數字也較高，分別為 14% 和 8% ；而冷氣仍然是最小的排放來源，佔 3% 。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"two pie charts","chinese":"兩個圓形圖"},{"english":"energy consumption","chinese":"能源消耗"},{"english":"an average Australian household","chinese":"一個澳洲普通家庭"},{"english":"proportions of greenhouse gas emissions","chinese":"溫室氣體排放比例"},{"english":"greenhouse gas emissions","chinese":"溫室氣體排放"},{"english":"produced by each use","chinese":"由每種用途產生"},{"english":"account for most","chinese":"佔大部分"},{"english":"household energy use","chinese":"家庭能源使用量"},{"english":"whereas","chinese":"而；相比之下"},{"english":"more evenly distributed","chinese":"分佈較平均"},{"english":"by far the largest consumer of energy","chinese":"明顯是最大的能源消耗項目"},{"english":"consumer of energy","chinese":"能源消耗項目"},{"english":"a much smaller share of emissions","chinese":"小得多的排放比例"},{"english":"by contrast","chinese":"相比之下"},{"english":"other appliances","chinese":"其他電器"},{"english":"refrigeration","chinese":"冷藏設備；雪櫃冷藏"},{"english":"lighting","chinese":"照明"},{"english":"generate proportionally more","chinese":"按比例產生更多"},{"english":"greenhouse gas","chinese":"溫室氣體"},{"english":"the energy they use","chinese":"它們所使用的能源"},{"english":"makes up 42% of","chinese":"佔……的42%"},{"english":"total energy consumption","chinese":"總能源消耗量"},{"english":"making it the dominant category","chinese":"使其成為主要類別"},{"english":"dominant category","chinese":"主要類別"},{"english":"water heating","chinese":"熱水加熱"},{"english":"is second at","chinese":"以……位居第二"},{"english":"these two uses together","chinese":"這兩種用途合共"},{"english":"represent almost three quarters of","chinese":"佔接近四分之三"},{"english":"household energy demand","chinese":"家庭能源需求"},{"english":"the remaining categories","chinese":"其餘類別"},{"english":"much smaller","chinese":"小得多"},{"english":"account for 15%","chinese":"佔15%"},{"english":"for just 2%","chinese":"僅佔2%"},{"english":"cooling","chinese":"製冷；冷氣"},{"english":"emissions chart","chinese":"排放圖"},{"english":"the leading source","chinese":"主要來源"},{"english":"while","chinese":"而；同時"},{"english":"almost double their energy share","chinese":"幾乎是其能源使用比例的兩倍"},{"english":"energy share","chinese":"能源使用比例"},{"english":"producing 28% of emissions","chinese":"產生28%的排放"},{"english":"is responsible for only","chinese":"只佔……的責任；只產生"},{"english":"only 15%","chinese":"僅15%"},{"english":"higher emission figures","chinese":"較高的排放數字"},{"english":"emission figures","chinese":"排放數字"},{"english":"at 14% and 8% respectively","chinese":"分別為14%及8%"},{"english":"respectively","chinese":"分別"},{"english":"remains the smallest contributor","chinese":"仍然是最小的來源"},{"english":"smallest contributor","chinese":"最小的來源"},{"english":"contributor","chinese":"來源；促成因素"}]},"model-essay-4-ielts-task1-process-diagram":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-4-ielts-task1-process-diagram","essayKey":"process-diagram:4","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-4-ielts-task1-process-diagram","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-1/process-diagrams/process-diagram-4","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"The diagram illustrates the process by which plastic bottles are recycled and converted into new goods.","chinese":"該圖說明塑膠瓶如何被回收，並轉化為新的商品。"},{"label":"Overview","english":"Overall, the procedure contains nine main stages, beginning with the disposal of used bottles and ending with the manufacture of various end products. It is largely linear, although the production of new bottles means that some items can re-enter the same recycling loop.","chinese":"整體而言，這個流程包含九個主要階段，從丟棄使用過的塑膠瓶開始，到製造各種最終產品結束。 它大致上是一個線性流程；不過，由於最終產品中包括新的塑膠瓶，一些物品可以重新進入同一個回收循環。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"At the initial stage, consumers place discarded plastic bottles in dedicated recycling bins. These containers are then emptied by a collection truck, which transports the waste to a recycling centre. Once there, the bottles are sorted on a conveyor belt, with suitable items separated from rejected materials. The accepted bottles are subsequently compressed into dense blocks, making them easier to handle before further processing.","chinese":"在最初階段，消費者把丟棄的塑膠瓶放入專門的回收箱中。 這些回收箱隨後由收集卡車清空，而卡車會把廢棄物運送到回收中心。 到達回收中心後，塑膠瓶會在輸送帶上被分類，合適的物品會與被拒收的材料分開。 合格的塑膠瓶隨後被壓縮成密集的方塊，以便在進一步加工前更容易處理。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"In the next phase, the compacted blocks are crushed into small fragments, which are washed to remove impurities. The cleaned pieces are fed into a machine and turned into plastic pellets. After this, the pellets are heated and transformed into raw material, which is stored in large bundles. Finally, this material is used to manufacture a range of products, including new bottles, food containers, T-shirts, shopping bags and pencils.","chinese":"在下一階段，被壓縮的方塊會被粉碎成小碎片，然後被清洗以去除雜質。 清洗後的碎片會被送入機器，並轉化成塑膠顆粒。 之後，這些塑膠粒會被加熱並轉化為原材料，而原材料會被存放成大型捆包。 最後，這些材料會被用來製造一系列產品，包括新的塑膠瓶、食物容器、 T 恤、購物袋和鉛筆。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"diagram illustrates","chinese":"圖示說明"},{"english":"the process by which","chinese":"……的過程"},{"english":"plastic bottles are recycled","chinese":"膠樽被回收"},{"english":"converted into new goods","chinese":"被轉化成新產品"},{"english":"new goods","chinese":"新產品"},{"english":"the procedure contains","chinese":"這個程序包含"},{"english":"nine main stages","chinese":"九個主要階段"},{"english":"beginning with","chinese":"以……開始"},{"english":"disposal of used bottles","chinese":"棄置用過的膠樽"},{"english":"ending with","chinese":"以……結束"},{"english":"manufacture of various end products","chinese":"製造各種最終產品"},{"english":"end products","chinese":"最終產品"},{"english":"largely linear","chinese":"大致是線性的"},{"english":"the production of new bottles","chinese":"生產新膠樽"},{"english":"re-enter the same recycling loop","chinese":"重新進入同一個回收循環"},{"english":"recycling loop","chinese":"回收循環"},{"english":"at the initial stage","chinese":"在最初階段"},{"english":"discarded plastic bottles","chinese":"被棄置的膠樽"},{"english":"dedicated recycling bins","chinese":"指定回收箱"},{"english":"these containers are then emptied","chinese":"這些容器隨後被清空"},{"english":"emptied by a collection truck","chinese":"由收集車清空"},{"english":"collection truck","chinese":"收集車"},{"english":"transports the waste to","chinese":"將廢物運送到……"},{"english":"recycling centre","chinese":"回收中心"},{"english":"once there","chinese":"到達那裏後"},{"english":"sorted on a conveyor belt","chinese":"在輸送帶上分類"},{"english":"conveyor belt","chinese":"輸送帶"},{"english":"suitable items","chinese":"合適物品"},{"english":"separated from rejected materials","chinese":"與被拒收的物料分開"},{"english":"rejected materials","chinese":"被拒收的物料"},{"english":"accepted bottles","chinese":"合格膠樽"},{"english":"are subsequently compressed into","chinese":"隨後被壓縮成"},{"english":"subsequently","chinese":"隨後"},{"english":"dense blocks","chinese":"緊密塊狀物"},{"english":"easier to handle","chinese":"較容易處理"},{"english":"before further processing","chinese":"在進一步加工之前"},{"english":"further processing","chinese":"進一步加工"},{"english":"in the next phase","chinese":"在下一階段"},{"english":"compacted blocks","chinese":"壓實塊"},{"english":"crushed into small fragments","chinese":"被壓碎成小碎片"},{"english":"small fragments","chinese":"小碎片"},{"english":"washed to remove impurities","chinese":"被清洗以去除雜質"},{"english":"remove impurities","chinese":"去除雜質"},{"english":"cleaned pieces","chinese":"清潔後的碎片"},{"english":"fed into a machine","chinese":"被送入機器"},{"english":"turned into plastic pellets","chinese":"被製成塑膠粒"},{"english":"plastic pellets","chinese":"塑膠粒"},{"english":"after this","chinese":"之後"},{"english":"heated and transformed into","chinese":"被加熱並轉化成"},{"english":"raw material","chinese":"原材料"},{"english":"stored in large bundles","chinese":"以大捆形式儲存"},{"english":"large bundles","chinese":"大捆"},{"english":"used to manufacture","chinese":"用於製造"},{"english":"a range of products","chinese":"一系列產品"},{"english":"including new bottles","chinese":"包括新膠樽"},{"english":"food containers","chinese":"食物容器"},{"english":"shopping bags","chinese":"購物袋"},{"english":"recycling process","chinese":"回收過程"},{"english":"manufacturing stage","chinese":"製造階段"},{"english":"linear process","chinese":"線性流程"}]},"model-essay-4-ielts-task1-tables":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-4-ielts-task1-tables","essayKey":"tables:4","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-4-ielts-task1-tables","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-1/tables/table-4","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"The table presents data on the number of nights spent in Germany by domestic and international tourists between 2016 and 2022, measured in millions.","chinese":"這個表格呈現了 2016 年至 2022 年間，本地及國際遊客在德國逗留晚數的數據，單位為百萬晚。"},{"label":"Overview","english":"Overall, domestic tourism accounted for far more overnight stays than international tourism throughout the period. Both categories rose steadily until 2019, before falling sharply in 2020; although they recovered strongly by 2022, neither returned fully to its pre-decline peak.","chinese":"整體而言，在整個時期內，本地旅遊所佔的過夜住宿晚數遠遠高於國際旅遊。 兩個類別都穩步上升至 2019 年，之後在 2020 年急劇下跌；雖然到 2022 年兩者均明顯回升，但都未完全恢復至下跌前的高峰。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"From 2016 to 2019, domestic-tourist nights increased consistently, rising from 366.4 million to 405.7 million. The international figure followed a similar but much smaller upward trend, climbing from 80.8 million to 89.9 million over the same years. As a result, domestic stays were roughly four and a half times as high as overseas stays during this initial period.","chinese":"從 2016 年至 2019 年，本地遊客住宿晚數持續上升，從 3.664 億晚增至 4.057 億晚。 國際遊客的數字也呈現相似但規模小得多的上升趨勢，同期從 8,080 萬晚增至 8,990 萬晚。 因此，在這一初期階段，本地住宿晚數大約是海外遊客住宿晚數的四倍半。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"The pattern changed markedly after 2019. Domestic nights dropped to 270.3 million in 2020, a fall of more than 130 million, before edging up to 279.23 million in 2021. International nights fell even more steeply in proportional terms, plunging from 89.9 million in 2019 to 32 million in 2020 and then slipping to 31.01 million in 2021. By 2022, domestic and international figures had rebounded to 382.62 million and 68.09 million respectively, but both remained below their 2019 levels.","chinese":"2019 年之後，這一模式出現了明顯變化。 本地遊客住宿晚數在 2020 年跌至 2.703 億晚，下降超過 1.3 億晚，之後在 2021 年小幅回升至 2.7923 億晚。 按比例來看，國際遊客住宿晚數跌幅更為陡峭，從 2019 年的 8,990 萬晚急跌至2020 年的 3,200 萬晚，之後在 2021 年再微跌至 3,101 萬晚。 到 2022 年，本地及國際遊客住宿晚數分別反彈至 3.8262 億晚和 6,809 萬晚，但兩者仍低於 2019 年的水平。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"the table below shows","chinese":"下列表格顯示"},{"english":"the number of nights spent","chinese":"留宿晚數"},{"english":"domestic and international tourists","chinese":"本地及國際旅客"},{"english":"in Germany","chinese":"在德國"},{"english":"from 2016 to 2022","chinese":"由2016年至2022年"},{"english":"measured in millions","chinese":"以百萬計算"},{"english":"summarise the information","chinese":"概述資料"},{"english":"selecting and reporting","chinese":"選取並報告"},{"english":"the main features","chinese":"主要特徵"},{"english":"make comparisons where relevant","chinese":"在相關之處作出比較"},{"english":"presents data on","chinese":"呈現關於……的數據"},{"english":"nights spent in Germany","chinese":"在德國留宿的晚數"},{"english":"by domestic and international tourists","chinese":"由本地及國際旅客"},{"english":"between 2016 and 2022","chinese":"在2016年至2022年間"},{"english":"Overall","chinese":"整體而言"},{"english":"domestic tourism","chinese":"本地旅遊"},{"english":"international tourism","chinese":"國際旅遊"},{"english":"accounted for far more","chinese":"佔遠多於"},{"english":"overnight stays","chinese":"過夜住宿晚數"},{"english":"throughout the period","chinese":"在整個時期內"},{"english":"both categories","chinese":"兩個類別"},{"english":"rose steadily until","chinese":"穩步上升至"},{"english":"before falling sharply","chinese":"之後急跌"},{"english":"falling sharply","chinese":"急劇下跌"},{"english":"although","chinese":"雖然"},{"english":"recovered strongly","chinese":"強勁回升"},{"english":"by 2022","chinese":"到2022年"},{"english":"neither returned fully to","chinese":"兩者均未完全回到"},{"english":"its pre-decline peak","chinese":"下跌前高峰"},{"english":"From 2016 to 2019","chinese":"由2016年至2019年"},{"english":"domestic-tourist nights","chinese":"本地旅客留宿晚數"},{"english":"increased consistently","chinese":"持續上升"},{"english":"rising from … to …","chinese":"由……上升至……"},{"english":"from 366.4 million to 405.7 million","chinese":"由3.664億升至4.057億"},{"english":"the international figure","chinese":"國際旅客的數字"},{"english":"followed a similar but much smaller upward trend","chinese":"呈現相似但規模小得多的上升趨勢"},{"english":"a similar upward trend","chinese":"相似的上升趨勢"},{"english":"much smaller","chinese":"小得多"},{"english":"climbing from … to …","chinese":"由……攀升至……"},{"english":"from 80.8 million to 89.9 million","chinese":"由8,080萬升至8,990萬"},{"english":"over the same years","chinese":"在同一幾年間"},{"english":"as a result","chinese":"因此"},{"english":"domestic stays","chinese":"本地旅客住宿晚數"},{"english":"overseas stays","chinese":"海外旅客住宿晚數"},{"english":"roughly four and a half times as high as","chinese":"大約是……的四倍半"},{"english":"during this initial period","chinese":"在最初這段時期"},{"english":"the pattern changed markedly","chinese":"模式明顯改變"},{"english":"after 2019","chinese":"2019年之後"},{"english":"domestic nights","chinese":"本地旅客留宿晚數"},{"english":"dropped to","chinese":"下降至"},{"english":"270.3 million","chinese":"2.703億"},{"english":"a fall of more than","chinese":"超過……的跌幅"},{"english":"more than 130 million","chinese":"超過1.3億"},{"english":"before edging up to","chinese":"之後輕微回升至"},{"english":"edging up to","chinese":"輕微上升至"},{"english":"279.23 million","chinese":"2.7923億"},{"english":"international nights","chinese":"國際旅客留宿晚數"},{"english":"fell even more steeply","chinese":"下跌得更加急劇"},{"english":"in proportional terms","chinese":"按比例計算"},{"english":"plunging from … to …","chinese":"由……暴跌至……"},{"english":"plunged from 89.9 million to 32 million","chinese":"由8,990萬暴跌至3,200萬"},{"english":"then slipping to","chinese":"其後再下滑至"},{"english":"slipped to 31.01 million","chinese":"下滑至3,101萬"},{"english":"had rebounded to","chinese":"已反彈至"},{"english":"domestic and international figures","chinese":"本地及國際旅客數字"},{"english":"382.62 million and 68.09 million respectively","chinese":"分別為3.8262億及6,809萬"},{"english":"respectively","chinese":"分別"},{"english":"remained below","chinese":"仍低於"},{"english":"their 2019 levels","chinese":"它們2019年的水平"}]},"model-essay-5-ielts-advantage-disadvantage":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-5-ielts-advantage-disadvantage","essayKey":"advantage-disadvantage:5","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-5-ielts-advantage-disadvantage","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/advantage-and-disadvantage/EdmundBd9AdDisAd-Q5","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"In both working life and private life, a growing proportion of communication is now conducted through digital technology instead of face-to-face interaction. Although this development can weaken the quality of human relationships and increase the risk of misunderstanding, I believe its advantages are greater overall because it makes communication far more efficient and keeps people connected despite geographical separation.","chinese":"無論在工作還是私人生活中，越來越多的溝通如今都是透過數位科技進行，而不是面對面交流。 儘管這種發展可能削弱人際關係的品質，並增加誤解的風險， 我認為整體而言，它的優點更大，因為它使溝通更有效率，並能讓人們即使相隔遙遠也保持聯繫。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"The main benefit of technology-based communication is speed and convenience. In professional settings, email, messaging platforms and video conferencing remove the need for travel and allow decisions to be made almost immediately. This shortens response times, reduces operating costs and enables companies to coordinate teams across different cities or even continents with remarkable ease. For instance, a manager can resolve a production issue with overseas colleagues in a single online meeting rather than waiting days for an in-person discussion. The same principle applies socially: parents, children and friends who live far apart can speak daily through calls and messages, thereby maintaining close relationships that might otherwise weaken over time.","chinese":"科技化溝通最主要的優點是速度和便利性。 在專業環境中，電子郵件、即時通訊平台和視像會議免除了人們出行的需要，並使決策幾乎可以即時作出。 這不但縮短了回應時間、降低了營運成本，還使公司能夠非常輕鬆地協調分布在不同城市甚至不同大洲的團隊。 例如，一位經理可以透過一次線上會議便與海外同事解決生產問題，而不是等待數天才進行一次面對面的討論。 同樣的情況也適用於社交層面：住得很遠的父母、子女和朋友仍然可以透過通話和訊息每天聯絡。 結果是，人際關係更容易維持，也較不會隨時間而逐漸淡化。 例如，一個家庭即使成員分散在不同國家，仍然可以透過視像通話分享日常近況並提供情感支持。 因此，數位溝通大大提升了工作和個人生活中的效率與可及性。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"Nevertheless, digital communication has important drawbacks, the most serious of which is its lack of emotional richness. Face-to-face conversation conveys tone, facial expression and body language, which help people interpret meaning accurately, show empathy and build trust. When these cues disappear, messages are more easily misread; a brief email or text, for example, may sound cold or hostile even when no offence was intended. This is especially problematic in workplaces, where trust and nuance are essential for leadership, negotiation and teamwork. Over time, heavy reliance on screens may also encourage shallow social habits. People can remain constantly in contact online yet still feel isolated, because frequent messaging is not the same as receiving genuine attention and human presence.","chinese":"然而，數位溝通也有重要的缺點，其中最嚴重的是它缺乏情感上的豐富性。 面對面的交談能傳達語氣、面部表情和肢體語言，這些都有助於人們準確理解意思、表達同理心並建立信任。 當這些線索消失時，訊息便更容易被誤解，從而導致困惑甚至衝突。 例如，一封簡短的電郵或文字訊息即使本無惡意，也可能顯得冷淡甚至帶有敵意。 這在職場中尤其成問題，因為信任和細膩的理解對領導、協商和團隊合作都至關重要。 長遠而言，過度依賴螢幕也可能助長膚淺的社交習慣，因此人們即使在線上一直保持聯絡，仍可能感到孤立。 例如，一個人即使經常透過社交媒體聊天，仍可能感到孤單，因為數位接觸始終無法完全取代真正的關注和人的陪伴。 因此，儘管科技讓溝通成為可能，它同時也可能削弱清晰度、信任感和情感深度。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, communicating through technology offers clear advantages in terms of efficiency and accessibility, even though it may reduce the depth and clarity of human interaction. Overall, I believe the benefits outweigh the disadvantages because digital tools allow both professional and personal communication to function effectively across time and distance.","chinese":"總結來說，透過科技進行溝通在效率和可及性方面具有明顯優勢，儘管它可能削弱人際互動的深度與清晰度。 整體而言，我認為其優點大於缺點，因為數位工具使工作和個人生活中的溝通都能跨越時間與距離而有效運作。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"working life and private life","chinese":"工作生活和私人生活"},{"english":"a growing proportion of","chinese":"越來越大比例的……"},{"english":"be conducted through","chinese":"透過……進行"},{"english":"digital technology","chinese":"數碼科技"},{"english":"instead of face-to-face interaction","chinese":"而不是面對面互動"},{"english":"face-to-face interaction","chinese":"面對面互動"},{"english":"weaken the quality of","chinese":"削弱……的質素"},{"english":"human relationships","chinese":"人際關係"},{"english":"increase the risk of misunderstanding","chinese":"增加誤解風險"},{"english":"greater overall","chinese":"整體上較大"},{"english":"far more efficient","chinese":"效率高得多"},{"english":"keep people connected","chinese":"讓人保持聯繫"},{"english":"despite geographical separation","chinese":"儘管地理上分隔"},{"english":"technology-based communication","chinese":"以科技為基礎的溝通"},{"english":"speed and convenience","chinese":"速度和便利"},{"english":"professional settings","chinese":"專業工作環境"},{"english":"messaging platforms","chinese":"訊息平台"},{"english":"video conferencing","chinese":"視像會議"},{"english":"remove the need for travel","chinese":"免卻出行需要"},{"english":"allow decisions to be made","chinese":"讓決定得以作出"},{"english":"almost immediately","chinese":"幾乎即時"},{"english":"shorten response times","chinese":"縮短回應時間"},{"english":"reduce operating costs","chinese":"降低營運成本"},{"english":"coordinate teams across","chinese":"協調分佈於……的團隊"},{"english":"different cities or even continents","chinese":"不同城市甚至不同洲份"},{"english":"with remarkable ease","chinese":"非常輕易地"},{"english":"resolve a production issue","chinese":"解決生產問題"},{"english":"overseas colleagues","chinese":"海外同事"},{"english":"in a single online meeting","chinese":"在一次網上會議中"},{"english":"rather than waiting days for","chinese":"而不是等數天才……"},{"english":"an in-person discussion","chinese":"面對面討論"},{"english":"the same principle applies socially","chinese":"同一道理也適用於社交方面"},{"english":"live far apart","chinese":"相隔很遠居住"},{"english":"speak daily through calls and messages","chinese":"透過電話和訊息每日交談"},{"english":"maintaining close relationships","chinese":"維持親密關係"},{"english":"might otherwise weaken over time","chinese":"否則可能隨時間逐漸減弱"},{"english":"digital communication has important drawbacks","chinese":"數碼溝通有重要缺點"},{"english":"the most serious of which","chinese":"其中最嚴重的是"},{"english":"lack of emotional richness","chinese":"缺乏情感層次"},{"english":"conveys tone","chinese":"傳達語氣"},{"english":"facial expression and body language","chinese":"面部表情和身體語言"},{"english":"interpret meaning accurately","chinese":"準確理解意思"},{"english":"show empathy","chinese":"表達同理心"},{"english":"build trust","chinese":"建立信任"},{"english":"these cues disappear","chinese":"這些提示消失"},{"english":"more easily misread","chinese":"更容易被誤解"},{"english":"a brief email or text","chinese":"簡短的電郵或短訊"},{"english":"sound cold or hostile","chinese":"聽起來冷淡或帶敵意"},{"english":"no offence was intended","chinese":"本無冒犯之意"},{"english":"especially problematic in workplaces","chinese":"在工作場尤其成問題"},{"english":"trust and nuance","chinese":"信任和細微語意"},{"english":"essential for leadership","chinese":"對領導力不可或缺"},{"english":"negotiation and teamwork","chinese":"談判和團隊合作"},{"english":"heavy reliance on screens","chinese":"對屏幕的高度依賴"},{"english":"encourage shallow social habits","chinese":"助長膚淺的社交習慣"},{"english":"remain constantly in contact online","chinese":"在網上持續保持聯絡"},{"english":"yet still feel isolated","chinese":"但仍然感到孤立"},{"english":"frequent messaging","chinese":"頻繁傳訊息"},{"english":"genuine attention","chinese":"真誠的關注"},{"english":"human presence","chinese":"人與人真實相處的存在感"},{"english":"in terms of efficiency and accessibility","chinese":"在效率和可取得性方面"},{"english":"reduce the depth and clarity of","chinese":"降低……的深度和清晰度"},{"english":"outweigh the disadvantages","chinese":"利多於弊"},{"english":"function effectively across time and distance","chinese":"跨越時間和距離有效運作"},{"english":"across time and distance","chinese":"跨越時間和距離"}]},"model-essay-5-ielts-direct-question":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-5-ielts-direct-question","essayKey":"direct-question:5","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-5-ielts-direct-question","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/direct-question/EdmundBd9Dir-Q5","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"In consumer markets, price is more than a number on a label; it often functions as a signal. I would argue that price strongly influences potential buyers, especially when it suggests status or quality, but the final decision is also shaped by practical factors such as need, trust and personal experience.","chinese":"在消費市場中，價格不僅僅是標籤上的一個數字；它往往也具有信號作用。 我會主張，價格會強烈影響潛在買家，尤其當它暗示地位或品質時；但最終決定也會受到實際因素影響，例如需要、信任和個人經驗。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"A high price can attract consumers because many people associate cost with quality. When buyers do not have specialist knowledge, they may use price as a shortcut: an expensive phone, watch or handbag is assumed to be better designed, more durable or more prestigious. This is particularly true in luxury markets, where the price itself becomes part of the appeal. A cheap diamond necklace, for instance, may make buyers suspicious rather than excited, because its low price weakens the image of rarity. In this sense, price can create desire by giving a product an aura of value. It tells buyers not only what the item costs, but also what owning it might say about them.","chinese":"高價格可以吸引消費者，因為很多人會把成本與品質聯繫起來。 當買家沒有專業知識時，他們可能會把價格當作一種捷徑：一部昂貴的手機、一隻手錶或一個手袋，往往會被認為設計更好、更耐用或更有聲望。 這在奢侈品市場中尤其真實，因為價格本身已成為吸引力的一部分。 例如，一條便宜的鑽石項鏈可能會令買家感到懷疑，而不是興奮，因為它的低價削弱了稀有性的形象。 從這個意義上說，價格可以透過賦予產品一種價值光環來創造購買慾望。它告訴買家的不只是這件物品的成本，也包括擁有它可能代表著他們是怎樣的人。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"However, price alone rarely carries a purchase decision from beginning to end. Buyers are also influenced by the usefulness of the product, the reputation of the brand, reviews from other customers and the emotional experience attached to ownership. A parent choosing a child’s laptop, for example, may care less about whether it looks fashionable and more about battery life, reliability and after-sales support. Similarly, a product with strong advertising may initially catch the eye, but poor reviews can quickly pour cold water on that interest. Convenience also matters: people often choose items that are easy to obtain, simple to use and compatible with their daily routines.","chinese":"然而，單靠價格很少能從頭到尾支撐一個購買決定。 買家也會受到產品實用性、品牌聲譽、其他顧客評價，以及擁有該產品所帶來的情感體驗所影響。 例如，一位家長為孩子選擇手提電腦時，可能不太在意它看起來是否時尚，而更重視電池壽命、可靠性和售後支援。 同樣地，一件擁有強力廣告宣傳的產品一開始可能會吸引目光，但差劣的評價很快就會為這份興趣潑冷水。 便利性同樣重要：人們往往會選擇容易取得、使用簡單，並且能配合他們日常生活習慣的物品。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, price has a powerful influence because it can suggest quality, prestige and social meaning. Nevertheless, people ultimately buy products when price works together with trust, usefulness, reputation and convenience. A high price may open the door, but other factors usually decide whether buyers walk through it.","chinese":"總結來說，價格具有強大的影響力，因為它可以暗示品質、聲望和社會意義。 然而，人們最終會在價格與信任、實用性、聲譽和便利性共同發揮作用時購買產品。 高價格也許能打開那扇門，但其他因素通常才決定買家是否真的會走進去。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"consumer markets","chinese":"消費市場"},{"english":"more than a number on a label","chinese":"不只是標籤上的數字"},{"english":"functions as a signal","chinese":"發揮信號作用"},{"english":"strongly influences potential buyers","chinese":"強烈影響潛在買家"},{"english":"potential buyers","chinese":"潛在買家"},{"english":"suggests status or quality","chinese":"暗示地位或質素"},{"english":"the final decision","chinese":"最終決定"},{"english":"be shaped by","chinese":"受到……塑造；受……影響"},{"english":"practical factors","chinese":"實際因素"},{"english":"personal experience","chinese":"個人經驗"},{"english":"associate cost with quality","chinese":"將價格與質素聯繫起來"},{"english":"specialist knowledge","chinese":"專門知識"},{"english":"use price as a shortcut","chinese":"將價格當作捷徑"},{"english":"be assumed to be","chinese":"被假定為"},{"english":"better designed","chinese":"設計得更好"},{"english":"more durable","chinese":"更耐用"},{"english":"more prestigious","chinese":"更有地位；更高檔"},{"english":"luxury markets","chinese":"奢侈品市場"},{"english":"part of the appeal","chinese":"吸引力的一部分"},{"english":"make buyers suspicious","chinese":"令買家起疑"},{"english":"rather than excited","chinese":"而不是興奮"},{"english":"weakens the image of","chinese":"削弱……的形象"},{"english":"the image of rarity","chinese":"稀有性的形象"},{"english":"in this sense","chinese":"從這個意義上說"},{"english":"create desire","chinese":"製造渴望"},{"english":"an aura of value","chinese":"價值感；價值光環"},{"english":"what owning it might say about them","chinese":"擁有它可能反映出的身份"},{"english":"price alone","chinese":"單靠價格"},{"english":"carries a purchase decision","chinese":"支撐一個購買決定"},{"english":"from beginning to end","chinese":"由始至終"},{"english":"be influenced by","chinese":"受到……影響"},{"english":"the usefulness of the product","chinese":"產品的實用性"},{"english":"the reputation of the brand","chinese":"品牌聲譽"},{"english":"reviews from other customers","chinese":"其他顧客的評價"},{"english":"emotional experience","chinese":"情感體驗"},{"english":"attached to ownership","chinese":"與擁有某物相關的"},{"english":"care less about whether","chinese":"較不在意是否……"},{"english":"looks fashionable","chinese":"看起來時尚"},{"english":"battery life","chinese":"電池續航力"},{"english":"reliability","chinese":"可靠性"},{"english":"after-sales support","chinese":"售後支援"},{"english":"strong advertising","chinese":"強力廣告宣傳"},{"english":"initially catch the eye","chinese":"起初吸引注意"},{"english":"poor reviews","chinese":"差評"},{"english":"pour cold water on","chinese":"對……潑冷水；打擊……"},{"english":"that interest","chinese":"那份興趣"},{"english":"convenience also matters","chinese":"便利性也很重要"},{"english":"easy to obtain","chinese":"容易取得"},{"english":"simple to use","chinese":"使用簡單"},{"english":"compatible with","chinese":"與……配合"},{"english":"daily routines","chinese":"日常生活習慣"},{"english":"a powerful influence","chinese":"強大的影響力"},{"english":"social meaning","chinese":"社會意義"},{"english":"ultimately buy products","chinese":"最終購買產品"},{"english":"works together with","chinese":"與……共同發揮作用"},{"english":"open the door","chinese":"打開機會之門"},{"english":"walk through it","chinese":"真的走進去；採取下一步"}]},"model-essay-5-ielts-discuss-both-views":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-5-ielts-discuss-both-views","essayKey":"discuss-both-views:5","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-5-ielts-discuss-both-views","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/discuss-both-views-your-opinion/EdmundBd9ExpBth-Q5","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"Recruitment is one of the most important decisions a company makes because employees shape not only its output but also its culture. Some argue that firms should hire people who are imaginative and capable of working without close supervision, whereas others believe that cooperative candidates who can follow directions are more valuable. Although independent thinkers can help a business grow, I believe companies should mainly prioritise people who can work well in teams and respect instructions.","chinese":"招聘是公司所作出的最重要決定之一，因為員工不但塑造公司的產出，也塑造公司文化 有些人認為公司應該聘請富有想像力、並且能夠在沒有密切監督下工作的人；然而，另一些人則認為能夠合作並遵從指示的求職者更有價值。 儘管獨立思考者能幫助企業成長，我認為公司應主要優先考慮那些能夠良好團隊合作並尊重指示的人。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"There are clear reasons why innovative and self-reliant employees are attractive to employers. In competitive markets, companies cannot survive by repeating the same methods year after year. Workers who question old practices, suggest fresh solutions and take ownership of tasks can help an organisation move faster than its rivals. For example, a software developer who notices an inefficient internal system may design a better tool without waiting for a manager to point out the problem. In this sense, independent employees can act as engines of progress, especially in industries where creativity and rapid problem-solving are essential.","chinese":"創新而自立的員工對僱主具有吸引力，這背後有明顯原因。 在競爭激烈的市場中，公司不能年復一年只靠重複相同的方法生存。 那些會質疑舊做法、提出新解決方法並主動承擔工作的員工，能夠幫助一個機構比競爭對手行動得更快。 例如，一位注意到內部系統效率低下的軟件開發人員，可能會在不等待經理指出問題的情況下，設計出一個更好的工具。 從這個意義上說，獨立的員工可以成為推動進步的引擎，尤其是在創意和快速解決問題至關重要的行業中。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"However, the stronger argument is that most companies depend more heavily on teamwork and disciplined execution. A business is rarely a collection of isolated individuals; it is a network of departments, deadlines and shared responsibilities. If employees are unable to communicate, accept feedback or follow established procedures, even brilliant ideas can become disruptive rather than useful. For instance, in healthcare, construction or finance, ignoring instructions can lead to serious mistakes, legal problems or safety risks. Team-oriented workers, by contrast, help create a stable workplace where tasks are completed consistently and colleagues can trust one another.","chinese":"然而，更有力的論點是，大多數公司更加依賴團隊合作和有紀律的執行。 一間企業很少只是一群孤立個體的集合；它是一個由部門、期限和共同責任組成的網絡 如果員工不能溝通、接受回饋或遵從既定程序，即使是出色的想法也可能變得具有破壞性，而不是有用。 例如，在醫療、建築或金融行業中，忽視指示可能導致嚴重錯誤、法律問題或安全風險 相比之下，以團隊為本的員工能夠幫助建立一個穩定的工作場所，讓任務能夠穩定完成，同事之間也能互相信任。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In my view, therefore, while innovation and independence are valuable qualities, they should not be the main priority in recruitment. A company can train creative thinking over time, but it is much harder to function when employees resist cooperation or basic rules. Overall, businesses should first recruit people who can contribute reliably to a team, because shared discipline is the foundation on which real innovation can later be built.","chinese":"因此，在我看來，雖然創新能力和獨立性是有價值的特質，但它們不應該是招聘中的主要優先考慮。 公司可以隨著時間訓練員工的創意思維，但當員工抗拒合作或基本規則時，公司要正常運作就困難得多。 整體而言，企業應該首先招聘那些能夠可靠地為團隊作出貢獻的人，因為共同的紀律正是真正創新日後得以建立的基礎。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"recruitment","chinese":"招聘"},{"english":"one of the most important decisions","chinese":"最重要的決定之一"},{"english":"shape not only...but also...","chinese":"不但塑造……，也塑造……"},{"english":"output","chinese":"產出"},{"english":"company culture","chinese":"公司文化"},{"english":"hire people who","chinese":"聘請……的人"},{"english":"imaginative","chinese":"有想像力的"},{"english":"capable of working without","chinese":"有能力在沒有……下工作"},{"english":"close supervision","chinese":"緊密監督"},{"english":"whereas","chinese":"然而；而"},{"english":"cooperative candidates","chinese":"合作型求職者"},{"english":"follow directions","chinese":"遵從指示"},{"english":"more valuable","chinese":"更有價值"},{"english":"independent thinkers","chinese":"獨立思考者"},{"english":"help a business grow","chinese":"幫助企業成長"},{"english":"mainly prioritise","chinese":"主要優先考慮"},{"english":"work well in teams","chinese":"在團隊中合作良好"},{"english":"respect instructions","chinese":"尊重指示"},{"english":"clear reasons why","chinese":"明確原因解釋為何"},{"english":"innovative","chinese":"有創新能力的"},{"english":"self-reliant employees","chinese":"自力更生的員工"},{"english":"attractive to employers","chinese":"對僱主有吸引力"},{"english":"competitive markets","chinese":"競爭激烈的市場"},{"english":"cannot survive by","chinese":"不能靠……生存"},{"english":"repeating the same methods","chinese":"重複相同方法"},{"english":"year after year","chinese":"年復一年"},{"english":"question old practices","chinese":"質疑舊做法"},{"english":"suggest fresh solutions","chinese":"提出新穎解決方案"},{"english":"take ownership of tasks","chinese":"主動承擔工作責任"},{"english":"move faster than its rivals","chinese":"比競爭對手行動更快"},{"english":"software developer","chinese":"軟件開發人員"},{"english":"inefficient internal system","chinese":"低效的內部系統"},{"english":"design a better tool","chinese":"設計更好的工具"},{"english":"without waiting for","chinese":"不用等待"},{"english":"point out the problem","chinese":"指出問題"},{"english":"In this sense","chinese":"從這個意義上說"},{"english":"act as engines of progress","chinese":"成為進步的推動力"},{"english":"especially in industries where","chinese":"尤其在……的行業中"},{"english":"rapid problem-solving","chinese":"快速解難"},{"english":"are essential","chinese":"是不可或缺的"},{"english":"the stronger argument","chinese":"更有力的論點"},{"english":"depend more heavily on","chinese":"更大程度上依賴"},{"english":"teamwork","chinese":"團隊合作"},{"english":"disciplined execution","chinese":"有紀律的執行"},{"english":"a collection of isolated individuals","chinese":"一群互不相干的個體"},{"english":"a network of","chinese":"由……組成的網絡"},{"english":"departments","chinese":"部門"},{"english":"deadlines","chinese":"截止期限"},{"english":"shared responsibilities","chinese":"共同責任"},{"english":"unable to communicate","chinese":"無法溝通"},{"english":"accept feedback","chinese":"接受意見"},{"english":"follow established procedures","chinese":"遵循既定程序"},{"english":"brilliant ideas","chinese":"出色想法"},{"english":"disruptive rather than useful","chinese":"造成干擾而不是有用"},{"english":"ignoring instructions","chinese":"忽視指示"},{"english":"lead to serious mistakes","chinese":"導致嚴重錯誤"},{"english":"legal problems","chinese":"法律問題"},{"english":"safety risks","chinese":"安全風險"},{"english":"team-oriented workers","chinese":"以團隊為本的員工"},{"english":"by contrast","chinese":"相比之下"},{"english":"a stable workplace","chinese":"穩定的工作環境"},{"english":"completed consistently","chinese":"穩定一致地完成"},{"english":"trust one another","chinese":"互相信任"},{"english":"valuable qualities","chinese":"有價值的特質"},{"english":"the main priority in recruitment","chinese":"招聘中的首要考慮"},{"english":"train creative thinking","chinese":"培養創意思維"},{"english":"over time","chinese":"隨時間"},{"english":"much harder to function","chinese":"更難運作"},{"english":"resist cooperation","chinese":"抗拒合作"},{"english":"basic rules","chinese":"基本規則"},{"english":"recruit people who","chinese":"招聘……的人"},{"english":"contribute reliably to","chinese":"可靠地為……作出貢獻"},{"english":"shared discipline","chinese":"共同紀律"},{"english":"the foundation on which","chinese":"……得以建立的基礎"},{"english":"real innovation","chinese":"真正創新"}]},"model-essay-5-ielts-opinion":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-5-ielts-opinion","essayKey":"opinion:5","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-5-ielts-opinion","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/opinions/EdmundBd9OP-Q5","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"Because market demand does not always reward socially valuable work, some professions remain poorly paid despite making an important contribution to society. For this reason, some people argue that artists, who often earn low salaries, should receive government funding so that they can continue producing their work. I completely agree because artistic labour strengthens cultural life and also supports significant economic activity.","chinese":"由於市場需求並不總是會回報那些具有社會價值的工作，因此有些職業雖然對社會作出重要貢獻，薪酬卻依然偏低。 基於這個原因，有些人主張，藝術家因為收入往往偏低，應該獲得政府資助，讓他們能夠繼續創作。 我完全同意。 因為藝術勞動不但能強化文化生活，也能支持重要的經濟活動。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"The first reason public funding is justified is that art creates public benefits which private income alone does not reflect. When artists cannot earn enough to remain in the profession, many are forced to leave for more stable jobs. As a result, fewer plays, exhibitions, concerts and community projects are produced, which reduces the public’s access to culture. Over time, this weakens social cohesion because shared stories, traditions and forms of expression become less visible in everyday life. For example, if a local theatre or music programme must survive only through ticket sales, it may disappear from poorer communities altogether, whereas public support allows children and families to engage with the arts regularly. This exposure also develops imagination, empathy and communication skills, so funding artists benefits society in educational as well as cultural terms.","chinese":"第一個支持公共資助的理由是，藝術能創造公共利益，而這些利益單靠私人收入是無法充分反映的。 當藝術家無法靠這個職業獲得足夠收入時，許多人就會被迫離開，轉而從事更穩定的工作。 結果就是，戲劇、展覽、音樂會和社區計畫都會減少，從而削弱公眾接觸文化的機會。 久而久之，這會削弱社會凝聚力，因為共同的故事、傳統與表達方式在日常生活中會變得愈來愈不明顯。 例如，如果一個地方劇院或音樂計畫只能依靠售票維持生存，那麼它可能會完全從較貧困的社區中消失；相反，有了公共資助，孩子和家庭就能定期接觸藝術。 這種接觸同時也能培養想像力、同理心與溝通能力，因此資助藝術家不但有文化上的好處，也有教育上的價值。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"Government support for artists is also economically sensible rather than merely charitable. Stable grants or commissions allow creators to keep producing work, purchasing materials and collaborating with venues, technicians and small businesses, so the initial investment quickly circulates through the wider economy. More importantly, many profitable industries depend on artistic talent at an earlier stage of development. Film, design, advertising, fashion and digital media all rely on writers, musicians and visual artists whose skills are often developed in publicly supported spaces. If these people are pushed out of the profession by persistently low pay, a country eventually loses both creative capacity and future revenue. Cities that invest in artists, by contrast, often attract visitors, revive cultural districts and create employment beyond the arts themselves.","chinese":"政府支持藝術家在經濟上也是合理的，而不只是出於慈善考慮。 穩定的補助或委託能讓創作者持續創作、購買材料，並與場地、技術人員和小型企業合作，因此最初的投資很快便會在更廣泛的經濟體系中流動。 更重要的是，許多有利潤的產業在發展初期都依賴藝術人才。 電影、設計、廣告、時尚以及數位媒體都依賴作家、音樂家和視覺藝術家，而這些人的能力往往是在受到公共資助的空間中培養出來的。 如果這些人因長期低薪而被迫退出這個行業，一個國家最終失去的將不只是創造力，也包括未來的收入來源。 相反，那些投資藝術家的城市，往往能吸引遊客、帶動文化區復興，並創造出藝術本身以外的就業機會。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, I completely agree that artists should receive government funding. Their work preserves public access to culture, develops valuable human qualities and sustains wider economic growth, so supporting them is a necessary and well-judged public policy.","chinese":"總而言之，我完全同意藝術家應該獲得政府資助。 他們的工作能維持公眾接觸文化的機會，培養有價值的人文素質，並支撐更廣泛的經濟成長， 因此，支持藝術家是一項必要而且明智的公共政策。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"market demand","chinese":"市場需求"},{"english":"reward socially valuable work","chinese":"回報具社會價值的工作"},{"english":"socially valuable work","chinese":"具社會價值的工作"},{"english":"remain poorly paid","chinese":"仍然薪酬偏低"},{"english":"despite making an important contribution to","chinese":"儘管對……作出重要貢獻"},{"english":"an important contribution to society","chinese":"對社會的重要貢獻"},{"english":"for this reason","chinese":"因此"},{"english":"earn low salaries","chinese":"薪酬偏低"},{"english":"receive government funding","chinese":"獲得政府資助"},{"english":"continue producing their work","chinese":"繼續創作"},{"english":"artistic labour","chinese":"藝術勞動；藝術工作"},{"english":"strengthen cultural life","chinese":"豐富文化生活"},{"english":"support significant economic activity","chinese":"支持重要經濟活動"},{"english":"public funding is justified","chinese":"公帑資助是合理的"},{"english":"create public benefits","chinese":"創造公共利益"},{"english":"private income alone","chinese":"單靠私人收入"},{"english":"does not reflect","chinese":"未能反映"},{"english":"earn enough to remain in","chinese":"賺到足以留在……的收入"},{"english":"remain in the profession","chinese":"留在這個行業"},{"english":"be forced to leave","chinese":"被迫離開"},{"english":"more stable jobs","chinese":"更穩定的工作"},{"english":"as a result","chinese":"因此"},{"english":"plays, exhibitions, concerts and community projects","chinese":"戲劇、展覽、音樂會和社區項目"},{"english":"reduce the public's access to","chinese":"減少公眾接觸……的機會"},{"english":"access to culture","chinese":"接觸文化的機會"},{"english":"over time","chinese":"隨時間"},{"english":"weaken social cohesion","chinese":"削弱社會凝聚力"},{"english":"shared stories","chinese":"共同故事"},{"english":"traditions and forms of expression","chinese":"傳統和表達形式"},{"english":"become less visible","chinese":"變得較不明顯"},{"english":"everyday life","chinese":"日常生活"},{"english":"local theatre","chinese":"本地劇院"},{"english":"music programme","chinese":"音樂節目；音樂計劃"},{"english":"survive only through ticket sales","chinese":"只靠門票收入生存"},{"english":"ticket sales","chinese":"門票收入"},{"english":"disappear from poorer communities altogether","chinese":"從較貧困社區完全消失"},{"english":"whereas","chinese":"然而"},{"english":"public support","chinese":"公共支持；政府支持"},{"english":"engage with the arts","chinese":"接觸藝術；參與藝術活動"},{"english":"regularly","chinese":"定期地"},{"english":"this exposure","chinese":"這種接觸"},{"english":"develop imagination","chinese":"培養想像力"},{"english":"empathy","chinese":"同理心"},{"english":"communication skills","chinese":"溝通技巧"},{"english":"in educational as well as cultural terms","chinese":"從教育和文化角度來看"},{"english":"economically sensible","chinese":"在經濟上合理"},{"english":"rather than merely charitable","chinese":"而不只是慈善"},{"english":"stable grants","chinese":"穩定撥款"},{"english":"commissions","chinese":"委約創作；委託項目"},{"english":"creators","chinese":"創作者"},{"english":"keep producing work","chinese":"持續創作"},{"english":"purchasing materials","chinese":"購買材料"},{"english":"collaborating with","chinese":"與……合作"},{"english":"venues","chinese":"場地"},{"english":"technicians","chinese":"技術人員"},{"english":"initial investment","chinese":"初始投資"},{"english":"circulate through","chinese":"在……中流動"},{"english":"the wider economy","chinese":"更廣泛的經濟"},{"english":"profitable industries","chinese":"有盈利的行業"},{"english":"depend on artistic talent","chinese":"依賴藝術人才"},{"english":"at an earlier stage of development","chinese":"在較早發展階段"},{"english":"digital media","chinese":"數碼媒體"},{"english":"rely on","chinese":"依賴"},{"english":"visual artists","chinese":"視覺藝術家"},{"english":"publicly supported spaces","chinese":"由公帑支持的空間"},{"english":"be pushed out of","chinese":"被迫離開"},{"english":"persistently low pay","chinese":"長期偏低薪酬"},{"english":"eventually loses","chinese":"最終失去"},{"english":"creative capacity","chinese":"創意能力"},{"english":"future revenue","chinese":"未來收入"},{"english":"by contrast","chinese":"相反"},{"english":"invest in artists","chinese":"投資於藝術家"},{"english":"attract visitors","chinese":"吸引遊客"},{"english":"revive cultural districts","chinese":"重振文化區"},{"english":"create employment beyond","chinese":"在……以外創造就業"},{"english":"the arts themselves","chinese":"藝術本身"},{"english":"preserves public access to culture","chinese":"保留公眾接觸文化的機會"},{"english":"valuable human qualities","chinese":"寶貴的人文素質"},{"english":"sustain wider economic growth","chinese":"維持更廣泛的經濟增長"},{"english":"well-judged public policy","chinese":"明智的公共政策"}]},"model-essay-5-ielts-task1-bar-charts":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-5-ielts-task1-bar-charts","essayKey":"bar-charts:5","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-5-ielts-task1-bar-charts","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-1/bar-charts/bar-chart-5","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"The bar chart compares electricity production and consumption in the ten leading countries in 2014, in billions of kilowatt-hours.","chinese":"這張柱狀圖比較了 2014 年十大主要國家的電力生產量和耗電量，單位為十億千瓦時。"},{"label":"Overview","english":"Overall, China and the United States were by far the largest producers and users, whereas the other eight countries recorded much lower figures. It is also clear that output exceeded consumption in every country except Germany.","chinese":"整體而言，中國和美國是明顯最大的電力生產國和消耗國，而其餘八個國家的數字則低得多。 另一個明顯特徵是，除了德國之外，每個國家的電力產量都高於耗電量。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"China led the ranking, producing 5,398 billion kWh and consuming a marginally lower 5,322 billion kWh. The United States was second, at 4,099 billion kWh for production and 3,866 billion kWh for consumption; despite being well behind China, it remained far ahead of all other nations. Russia ranked third, generating 1,057 billion kWh and using 1,038 billion kWh, while Japan followed with 936.2 and 856.7 billion kWh, respectively.","chinese":"中國位居第一，電力產量為 5,398 十億千瓦時，耗電量則略低，為 5,322 十億千瓦時。 美國排名第二，電力產量為 4,099 十億千瓦時，耗電量為 3,866 十億千瓦時；雖然明顯落後於中國，但仍遠遠高於其他所有國家。 俄羅斯排名第三，發電量為 1,057 十億千瓦時，用電量為 1,038 十億千瓦時；日本緊隨其後，生產和消耗分別為 936.2 和 856.7 十億千瓦時。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"In the remaining countries, the figures were much smaller. India produced 871 billion kWh but consumed only 698.8 billion kWh. Canada, France and Brazil showed broadly similar patterns, each generating more electricity than it used, with production between 530.7 and 618.9 billion kWh. Germany was the only exception, consuming 582.5 billion kWh compared with output of 526.6 billion kWh. South Korea had the lowest totals, at 485.1 and 449.5 billion kWh.","chinese":"在其餘國家中，相關數字要小得多。 印度生產了 871 十億千瓦時的電力，但只消耗了 698.8 十億千瓦時。 加拿大、法國和巴西呈現大致相似的模式，三國的發電量都高於耗電量，而產量介乎 530.7 至 618.9 十億千瓦時之間。 德國是唯一例外，其耗電量為 582.5 十億千瓦時，高於 526.6 十億千瓦時的產量。 南韓的總量最低，產量和耗電量分別為 485.1 和 449.5 十億千瓦時。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"electricity production and consumption","chinese":"電力生產及消耗"},{"english":"the ten leading countries","chinese":"十個領先國家"},{"english":"in billions of kilowatt-hours","chinese":"以十億千瓦時為單位"},{"english":"kilowatt-hours","chinese":"千瓦時"},{"english":"by far the largest","chinese":"明顯是最大的"},{"english":"producers and users","chinese":"生產及使用電力的國家"},{"english":"whereas","chinese":"而；相比之下"},{"english":"recorded much lower figures","chinese":"錄得低得多的數字"},{"english":"It is also clear that","chinese":"亦可清楚看出"},{"english":"output exceeded consumption","chinese":"產量超過消耗量"},{"english":"in every country except","chinese":"除了……以外的每個國家"},{"english":"led the ranking","chinese":"位居榜首"},{"english":"producing…and consuming…","chinese":"生產……並消耗……"},{"english":"a marginally lower","chinese":"略低的"},{"english":"was second","chinese":"位居第二"},{"english":"at…for production","chinese":"生產量為……"},{"english":"for consumption","chinese":"消耗量為……"},{"english":"despite being well behind","chinese":"儘管遠遠落後於……"},{"english":"remained far ahead of","chinese":"仍然遠遠領先於……"},{"english":"all other nations","chinese":"所有其他國家"},{"english":"ranked third","chinese":"排名第三"},{"english":"generating…and using…","chinese":"發電……並使用……"},{"english":"followed with","chinese":"隨後錄得"},{"english":"respectively","chinese":"分別"},{"english":"the remaining countries","chinese":"其餘國家"},{"english":"the figures were much smaller","chinese":"數字小得多"},{"english":"produced…but consumed only…","chinese":"生產……但只消耗……"},{"english":"consumed only","chinese":"只消耗"},{"english":"showed broadly similar patterns","chinese":"呈現大致相似的模式"},{"english":"broadly similar patterns","chinese":"大致相似的模式"},{"english":"each generating more electricity than it used","chinese":"各自發電量高於用電量"},{"english":"with production between…and…","chinese":"產量介乎……與……之間"},{"english":"between 530.7 and 618.9 billion kWh","chinese":"介乎530.7至618.9十億千瓦時"},{"english":"the only exception","chinese":"唯一例外"},{"english":"compared with output of","chinese":"相比之下產量為……"},{"english":"had the lowest totals","chinese":"總數最低"},{"english":"lowest totals","chinese":"最低總數"},{"english":"among the ten countries","chinese":"在十個國家之中"},{"english":"electricity figures","chinese":"電力數據"},{"english":"production and consumption figures","chinese":"生產及消耗數據"},{"english":"much lower figures","chinese":"低得多的數字"},{"english":"well behind China","chinese":"遠遠落後於中國"},{"english":"far ahead of all other nations","chinese":"遠遠領先於所有其他國家"},{"english":"general pattern","chinese":"整體模式"},{"english":"compared with","chinese":"與……相比"},{"english":"output","chinese":"產量；發電量"}]},"model-essay-5-ielts-task1-line-graph":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-5-ielts-task1-line-graph","essayKey":"line-graph:5","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-5-ielts-task1-line-graph","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-1/line-graphs/line-graph-5","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"The two line charts illustrate changes in the proportion of households owning three electrical appliances and the average time spent on housework each week in one country from 1920 to 2019.","chinese":"這兩張折線圖說明了 1920 年至 2019 年間，某一國家家庭擁有三種電器的比例變化，以及每週平均花在家務上的時間變化。"},{"label":"Overview","english":"Overall, ownership of all three appliances increased, with refrigerators and vacuum cleaners becoming almost universal by the end of the period. Meanwhile, weekly housework fell markedly, from 50 hours to only 10.","chinese":"整體而言，三種電器的擁有率均有所上升，其中雪櫃和吸塵機到期末時幾乎已普及到所有家庭。 與此同時，每週家務時間大幅下降，從 50 小時減少至僅 10 小時。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"In 1920, washing machines were the most common appliance, at around 40%, compared with 30% for vacuum cleaners and almost no refrigerator ownership. The refrigerator then recorded the sharpest growth, rising to about 55% in 1940 and 90% in 1960, before reaching full ownership in 1980. Vacuum cleaners increased more steadily, climbing from 30% to 70% between 1920 and 1960 and reaching 100% by 2000. By contrast, washing machines grew more modestly, from 40% to 70% in 1960, dipped to roughly 65% in 1980, and then recovered to about 75% in 2019.","chinese":"在 1920 年，洗衣機是最常見的電器，約有 40% 的家庭擁有；相比之下，吸塵機的擁有率為 30% ，而幾乎沒有家庭擁有雪櫃。 之後，雪櫃的增長最為顯著，擁有率在 1940 年升至約 55% ， 1960 年升至 90% ，並在 1980 年達到完全普及。 吸塵機的擁有率則以較穩定的方式上升，從 1920 年的 30% 增至 1960 年的 70% ，並在 2000 年達到 100% 。 相比之下，洗衣機的增長較為溫和，從 1920 年的 40% 升至 1960 年的 70% ，其後在 1980 年下降至約 65% ，最後在 2019 年回升至約 75% 。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"The second chart shows an opposite pattern. Housework declined from 50 hours per week in 1920 to 35 in 1940, then fell further to 20 by 1960. Thereafter, the decrease was slower, reaching 15 hours in 1980 and 2000, before dropping to 10 in 2019.","chinese":"第二張圖顯示出相反的趨勢。 每週家務時間從 1920 年的 50 小時下降至 1940 年的 35 小時，然後到 1960 年進一步下降至 20 小時。 此後，下降速度放緩，在 1980 年和 2000 年達到 15 小時，最後在 2019 年降至 10 小時。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"the two line charts illustrate","chinese":"兩個折線圖顯示"},{"english":"changes in the proportion of households","chinese":"住戶比例的變化"},{"english":"the proportion of households owning","chinese":"擁有……的住戶比例"},{"english":"electrical appliances","chinese":"電器"},{"english":"average time spent on housework","chinese":"平均花在家務上的時間"},{"english":"housework","chinese":"家務"},{"english":"each week","chinese":"每星期"},{"english":"in one country","chinese":"在某一個國家"},{"english":"from 1920 to 2019","chinese":"從1920年至2019年"},{"english":"Overall","chinese":"整體而言"},{"english":"ownership of all three appliances","chinese":"三種電器的擁有率"},{"english":"increased","chinese":"上升"},{"english":"with refrigerators and vacuum cleaners becoming","chinese":"其中雪櫃和吸塵機變得……"},{"english":"refrigerators","chinese":"雪櫃"},{"english":"vacuum cleaners","chinese":"吸塵機"},{"english":"almost universal","chinese":"幾乎普及"},{"english":"by the end of the period","chinese":"到期末"},{"english":"Meanwhile","chinese":"與此同時"},{"english":"weekly housework","chinese":"每星期家務時間"},{"english":"fell markedly","chinese":"明顯下降"},{"english":"from 50 hours to only 10","chinese":"由50小時降至僅10小時"},{"english":"washing machines","chinese":"洗衣機"},{"english":"the most common appliance","chinese":"最常見的電器"},{"english":"at around 40%","chinese":"約為40%"},{"english":"compared with","chinese":"與……相比"},{"english":"almost no refrigerator ownership","chinese":"幾乎沒有人擁有雪櫃"},{"english":"recorded the sharpest growth","chinese":"錄得最急劇增長"},{"english":"the sharpest growth","chinese":"最急劇增長"},{"english":"rising to about 55%","chinese":"上升至約55%"},{"english":"before reaching full ownership","chinese":"隨後達至全面擁有"},{"english":"full ownership","chinese":"全面擁有；百分百擁有率"},{"english":"increased more steadily","chinese":"更穩定地上升"},{"english":"climbing from 30% to 70%","chinese":"由30%攀升至70%"},{"english":"between 1920 and 1960","chinese":"在1920年至1960年間"},{"english":"reaching 100% by 2000","chinese":"到2000年達到100%"},{"english":"By contrast","chinese":"相比之下"},{"english":"grew more modestly","chinese":"增長較溫和"},{"english":"dipped to roughly 65%","chinese":"下跌至約65%"},{"english":"then recovered to about 75%","chinese":"隨後回升至約75%"},{"english":"the second chart shows","chinese":"第二個圖表顯示"},{"english":"an opposite pattern","chinese":"相反模式"},{"english":"declined from 50 hours per week","chinese":"由每星期50小時下降"},{"english":"hours per week","chinese":"每星期小時數"},{"english":"then fell further to","chinese":"然後進一步下降至"},{"english":"by 1960","chinese":"到1960年"},{"english":"Thereafter","chinese":"此後"},{"english":"the decrease was slower","chinese":"下降速度較慢"},{"english":"reaching 15 hours","chinese":"達到15小時"},{"english":"before dropping to 10","chinese":"隨後下降至10"},{"english":"dropping to 10 in 2019","chinese":"在2019年下降至10小時"}]},"model-essay-5-ielts-task1-maps":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-5-ielts-task1-maps","essayKey":"maps:5","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-5-ielts-task1-maps","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-1/maps/maps-5","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"The two plans illustrate the current layout of Southwest Airport and the way it is expected to look after redevelopment next year.","chinese":"這兩張平面圖展示了 Southwest Airport 現時的布局，以及它預計在明年重新發展後的樣貌。"},{"label":"Overview","english":"Overall, the airport will be substantially enlarged, especially airside, where the existing pier with eight gates will be replaced by a Y-shaped concourse containing eighteen gates and a sky train. The terminal will also offer more passenger facilities, although its basic division into departures and arrivals will remain.","chinese":"整體而言，該機場將會大幅擴建，尤其是在空側區域；現有設有八個登機閘口的登機廊將被一個 Y 形候機大廳取代，當中會有十八個登機閘口和一條空中列車。Main Feature 2 （主要特徵二）。 航站樓亦會提供更多乘客服務設施，不過其基本的離境和入境分區將會保留。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"At present, the airport has a small terminal, with departures on the left and arrivals on the right. Departing passengers pass through security and passport control before using a walkway to reach eight gates arranged around a rectangular pier. The departures area contains only check-in facilities and a café, while arrivals are limited to passport control and customs.","chinese":"目前，該機場有一個較小的航站樓，離境區位於左邊，入境區位於右邊。 離境乘客會先通過安檢和護照檢查，然後經由一條步行通道前往圍繞矩形登機廊排列的八個登機閘口。 離境區只設有辦理登機手續的設施和一間咖啡店，而入境區則只包括護照檢查和海關。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"After redevelopment, the departures hall will include a bag drop, check-in area and café. Shops will be added beyond security, leading to the enlarged concourse. Instead of a simple walkway, passengers will use a sky train along the main pier, which will branch into two arms and increase the number of gates to eighteen. The arrivals side will also gain a café, an ATM and car-hire facilities near the exit.","chinese":"重新發展後，離境大堂將會包括行李托運處、辦理登機手續區和咖啡店。 商店將會增設在安檢之後的位置，並通往擴大的候機大廳。 乘客將不再只使用簡單的步行通道，而是會沿著主登機廊乘坐空中列車；該登機廊會分成兩條支線，並把登機閘口數量增加至十八個。 入境區一側亦會在出口附近增設咖啡店、自動櫃員機和租車設施。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"the plans below show","chinese":"下列平面圖顯示"},{"english":"the site of an airport","chinese":"機場所在地；機場範圍"},{"english":"how it will look","chinese":"它將來的樣貌"},{"english":"after redevelopment","chinese":"重建後"},{"english":"next year","chinese":"明年"},{"english":"summarise the information","chinese":"概述資料"},{"english":"selecting and reporting","chinese":"選取並報告"},{"english":"the main features","chinese":"主要特徵"},{"english":"make comparisons where relevant","chinese":"在相關之處作出比較"},{"english":"The two plans illustrate","chinese":"兩幅平面圖顯示"},{"english":"the current layout of","chinese":"……目前的佈局"},{"english":"Southwest Airport","chinese":"Southwest Airport"},{"english":"the way it is expected to look","chinese":"預計將會呈現的樣貌"},{"english":"is expected to look","chinese":"預計會呈現……的樣貌"},{"english":"Overall","chinese":"整體而言"},{"english":"will be substantially enlarged","chinese":"將會大幅擴建"},{"english":"substantially enlarged","chinese":"大幅擴大"},{"english":"especially airside","chinese":"尤其是機場禁區範圍"},{"english":"airside","chinese":"機場禁區範圍；空側"},{"english":"the existing pier","chinese":"現有客運廊"},{"english":"with eight gates","chinese":"設有八個閘口"},{"english":"will be replaced by","chinese":"將被……取代"},{"english":"a Y-shaped concourse","chinese":"Y形客運廊"},{"english":"containing eighteen gates","chinese":"設有十八個閘口"},{"english":"a sky train","chinese":"機場列車"},{"english":"the terminal","chinese":"客運大樓"},{"english":"will also offer","chinese":"亦會提供"},{"english":"passenger facilities","chinese":"旅客服務設施"},{"english":"its basic division into","chinese":"其分為……的基本劃分"},{"english":"departures and arrivals","chinese":"離境及抵達區"},{"english":"will remain","chinese":"將會保留"},{"english":"At present","chinese":"目前"},{"english":"a small terminal","chinese":"小型客運大樓"},{"english":"departures on the left","chinese":"離境區在左邊"},{"english":"arrivals on the right","chinese":"抵達區在右邊"},{"english":"departing passengers","chinese":"離境旅客"},{"english":"pass through security","chinese":"通過保安檢查"},{"english":"passport control","chinese":"護照檢查；出入境檢查"},{"english":"before using","chinese":"在使用……之前"},{"english":"a walkway","chinese":"行人通道"},{"english":"to reach eight gates","chinese":"前往八個閘口"},{"english":"arranged around","chinese":"圍繞……排列"},{"english":"a rectangular pier","chinese":"長方形客運廊"},{"english":"the departures area","chinese":"離境區"},{"english":"contains only","chinese":"只設有"},{"english":"check-in facilities","chinese":"辦理登機手續設施"},{"english":"while arrivals are limited to","chinese":"而抵達區只限於"},{"english":"are limited to","chinese":"僅限於；只有"},{"english":"customs","chinese":"海關"},{"english":"After redevelopment","chinese":"重建後"},{"english":"the departures hall","chinese":"離境大堂"},{"english":"will include","chinese":"將包括"},{"english":"a bag drop","chinese":"行李托運處"},{"english":"check-in area","chinese":"辦理登機手續區"},{"english":"shops will be added","chinese":"將增設商店"},{"english":"beyond security","chinese":"過了保安檢查後"},{"english":"leading to","chinese":"通往；連接至"},{"english":"the enlarged concourse","chinese":"擴建後的客運廊"},{"english":"Instead of","chinese":"而不是"},{"english":"a simple walkway","chinese":"簡單的行人通道"},{"english":"along the main pier","chinese":"沿着主客運廊"},{"english":"the main pier","chinese":"主客運廊"},{"english":"will branch into two arms","chinese":"將分成兩條分支"},{"english":"two arms","chinese":"兩條分支"},{"english":"increase the number of gates","chinese":"增加閘口數目"},{"english":"to eighteen","chinese":"增至十八個"},{"english":"the arrivals side","chinese":"抵達區一邊"},{"english":"will also gain","chinese":"亦會增設"},{"english":"an ATM","chinese":"自動櫃員機"},{"english":"car-hire facilities","chinese":"租車設施"},{"english":"near the exit","chinese":"在出口附近"}]},"model-essay-5-ielts-task1-mixed-charts":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-5-ielts-task1-mixed-charts","essayKey":"mixed-charts:5","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-5-ielts-task1-mixed-charts","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-1/mixed-charts/mixed-charts-5","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"The bar chart compares the export earnings of five product categories in one country in 2015 and 2016, while the table indicates the percentage change in each category over the same period.","chinese":"這張柱狀圖比較了一個國家在 2015 年和 2016 年五個產品類別的出口收入，而表格則顯示同一期間每個類別的百分比變化。"},{"label":"Overview","english":"Overall, export revenues increased in four of the five categories, with gems and jewellery being the only sector to decline. Petroleum products remained the highest-earning export in both years, while textiles recorded the strongest percentage growth despite starting from the lowest base.","chinese":"整體而言，五個出口類別中有四個的收入上升，而寶石和珠寶是唯一下降的類別。 石油產品在兩年中都是收入最高的出口類別；相反，紡織品雖然起點最低，但錄得最強的百分比增長。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"In 2015, petroleum products generated about $61 billion, slightly more than engineered goods, which stood at roughly $58 billion. By 2016, both categories had risen, to approximately $63 billion and $62 billion respectively. Although petroleum products still led the chart, engineered goods narrowed the gap after an 8.5% increase, compared with a more modest 3% rise in petroleum exports.","chinese":"2015 年，石油產品創造了約 610 億美元的收入，略高於工程產品約 580 億美元。 到 2016 年，這兩個類別均有所上升，分別達到約 630 億美元和 620 億美元。 雖然石油產品仍然位居首位，但工程產品在增長 8.5% 後縮小了差距；相比之下，石油產品的增幅較溫和，只有 3% 。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"The remaining categories earned less. Gems and jewellery fell from around $43 billion to about $41 billion, representing a decline of 5.18%. Agricultural products changed very little, edging up by only 0.81% from just over $30 billion. By contrast, textiles climbed markedly from approximately $26 billion to $31 billion, making it the fastest-growing category at 15.24%.","chinese":"其餘類別的收入較低。 寶石和珠寶的收入從約 430 億美元下降至約 410 億美元，代表下降了 5.18% 。 農產品變化非常小，從略高於 300 億美元的水平只微升了 0.81% 。 相比之下，紡織品從約 260 億美元顯著上升至 310 億美元，使其成為增長最快的類別，增幅達 15.24% 。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"the chart below shows","chinese":"下列圖表顯示"},{"english":"the value of exports","chinese":"出口價值"},{"english":"one country's exports","chinese":"某國的出口"},{"english":"in various categories","chinese":"在不同類別中"},{"english":"during 2015 and 2016","chinese":"在2015年和2016年間"},{"english":"the table shows","chinese":"表格顯示"},{"english":"the percentage change in","chinese":"……的百分比變化"},{"english":"each category of exports","chinese":"每個出口類別"},{"english":"compared with 2015","chinese":"與2015年相比"},{"english":"summarise the information","chinese":"概述資料"},{"english":"selecting and reporting","chinese":"選取並報告"},{"english":"the main features","chinese":"主要特徵"},{"english":"make comparisons where relevant","chinese":"在相關之處作出比較"},{"english":"the bar chart compares","chinese":"柱狀圖比較"},{"english":"export earnings","chinese":"出口收入"},{"english":"five product categories","chinese":"五個產品類別"},{"english":"while","chinese":"而"},{"english":"indicates the percentage change","chinese":"顯示百分比變化"},{"english":"over the same period","chinese":"在同一時期內"},{"english":"Overall","chinese":"整體而言"},{"english":"export revenues","chinese":"出口收入"},{"english":"increased in four of the five categories","chinese":"在五個類別中的四個上升"},{"english":"with … being the only sector to decline","chinese":"其中……是唯一下降的行業"},{"english":"gems and jewellery","chinese":"寶石及首飾"},{"english":"the only sector to decline","chinese":"唯一下跌的行業"},{"english":"petroleum products","chinese":"石油產品"},{"english":"remained the highest-earning export","chinese":"仍然是收入最高的出口"},{"english":"in both years","chinese":"在兩年中"},{"english":"textiles","chinese":"紡織品"},{"english":"recorded the strongest percentage growth","chinese":"錄得最大百分比升幅"},{"english":"percentage growth","chinese":"百分比增長"},{"english":"despite starting from","chinese":"儘管起點是……"},{"english":"the lowest base","chinese":"最低基數；最低起點"},{"english":"generated about $61 billion","chinese":"創造約610億美元"},{"english":"slightly more than","chinese":"略多於"},{"english":"engineered goods","chinese":"工程產品"},{"english":"stood at roughly","chinese":"約為"},{"english":"roughly $58 billion","chinese":"約580億美元"},{"english":"By 2016","chinese":"到2016年"},{"english":"both categories had risen","chinese":"兩個類別均已上升"},{"english":"approximately $63 billion","chinese":"約630億美元"},{"english":"$62 billion respectively","chinese":"分別為620億美元"},{"english":"respectively","chinese":"分別"},{"english":"Although","chinese":"雖然"},{"english":"still led the chart","chinese":"仍然在圖表中居首"},{"english":"narrowed the gap","chinese":"收窄差距"},{"english":"after an 8.5% increase","chinese":"在上升8.5%後"},{"english":"compared with","chinese":"與……相比"},{"english":"a more modest 3% rise","chinese":"較溫和的3%升幅"},{"english":"petroleum exports","chinese":"石油出口"},{"english":"the remaining categories","chinese":"其餘類別"},{"english":"earned less","chinese":"收入較低"},{"english":"fell from … to …","chinese":"由……跌至……"},{"english":"around $43 billion","chinese":"約430億美元"},{"english":"about $41 billion","chinese":"約410億美元"},{"english":"representing a decline of","chinese":"代表下降……"},{"english":"a decline of 5.18%","chinese":"5.18%的跌幅"},{"english":"agricultural products","chinese":"農產品"},{"english":"changed very little","chinese":"變化很小"},{"english":"edging up by only","chinese":"只輕微上升"},{"english":"by only 0.81%","chinese":"只增加0.81%"},{"english":"from just over $30 billion","chinese":"由剛高於300億美元"},{"english":"By contrast","chinese":"相比之下"},{"english":"climbed markedly","chinese":"大幅上升"},{"english":"from approximately $26 billion to $31 billion","chinese":"由約260億美元升至310億美元"},{"english":"making it the fastest-growing category","chinese":"使其成為增長最快的類別"},{"english":"the fastest-growing category","chinese":"增長最快的類別"},{"english":"at 15.24%","chinese":"達15.24%"}]},"model-essay-5-ielts-task1-pie-charts":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-5-ielts-task1-pie-charts","essayKey":"pie-charts:5","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-5-ielts-task1-pie-charts","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-1/pie-charts/pie-chart-5","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"The pie charts compare the age profiles of the populations of Yemen and Italy in 2000 and show projections for 2050.","chinese":"這些圓餅圖比較了葉門和意大利在 2000 年的人口年齡結構，並展示了 2050 年的預測。"},{"label":"Overview","english":"Overall, Yemen had a markedly younger population than Italy in 2000, and this is expected to remain the case in 2050. However, both countries are projected to age: the share of children will decline, while older groups, especially those aged 60 and above in Italy, will become more prominent.","chinese":"整體而言，葉門在 2000 年的人口明顯比意大利年輕，而這種情況預計在 2050年仍會維持。 然而，兩國人口都預計會老化：兒童所佔比例將會下降，而較年長的群體會變得更突出，尤其是意大利 60 歲及以上的人口。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"In Yemen, children aged 0–14 made up just over half of the population in 2000, at 50.1%, slightly exceeding the 46.3% recorded for people aged 15–59. By 2050, this pattern is forecast to reverse, with the working-age group rising to 57.3% and children falling to 37.0%. The elderly population will remain comparatively small, though it is expected to increase from 3.6% to 5.7%.","chinese":"在葉門， 0 至 14 歲兒童在 2000 年佔人口略多於一半，為 50.1% ，稍高於 15 至 59 歲人口的 46.3% 。 到 2050 年，這種模式預計會逆轉，工作年齡人口將上升至 57.3% ，而兒童比例則下降至 37.0% 。 老年人口仍會相對較少，儘管預計會從 3.6% 上升至 5.7% 。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"Italy showed a far older structure. In 2000, people aged 15–59 accounted for the largest proportion, at 61.6%, while those over 60 represented 24.1%; children made up only 14.3%. By 2050, the 60-plus group is projected to surge to 42.3%, close to the working-age share of 46.2%, whereas the youngest group will shrink slightly to 11.5%.","chinese":"意大利則呈現出明顯更老化的人口結構。 在 2000 年， 15 至 59 歲人口佔最大比例，為 61.6% ； 60 歲以上人口佔 24.1% ；兒童則只佔 14.3% 。 到 2050 年， 60 歲以上人口預計會大幅上升至 42.3% ，接近工作年齡人口的46.2% ；相反，最年輕組別將小幅下降至 11.5% 。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"the pie charts compare","chinese":"圓形圖比較"},{"english":"age profiles","chinese":"年齡結構"},{"english":"the populations of Yemen and Italy","chinese":"也門和意大利的人口"},{"english":"show projections for 2050","chinese":"顯示2050年的預測"},{"english":"projections for 2050","chinese":"2050年的預測"},{"english":"Overall","chinese":"整體而言"},{"english":"a markedly younger population","chinese":"明顯較年輕的人口"},{"english":"than Italy","chinese":"比意大利"},{"english":"is expected to remain the case","chinese":"預計情況仍會如此"},{"english":"remain the case","chinese":"情況仍然如此"},{"english":"However","chinese":"然而"},{"english":"are projected to age","chinese":"預計會人口老化"},{"english":"the share of children","chinese":"兒童所佔比例"},{"english":"will decline","chinese":"將會下降"},{"english":"older groups","chinese":"較年長組別"},{"english":"especially those aged 60 and above","chinese":"尤其是60歲或以上人士"},{"english":"aged 60 and above","chinese":"60歲或以上"},{"english":"become more prominent","chinese":"變得更突出"},{"english":"children aged 0–14","chinese":"0至14歲兒童"},{"english":"made up just over half of","chinese":"佔略多於一半"},{"english":"just over half of the population","chinese":"人口的略多於一半"},{"english":"at 50.1%","chinese":"為50.1%"},{"english":"slightly exceeding","chinese":"略高於"},{"english":"recorded for people aged 15–59","chinese":"15至59歲人士錄得的數字"},{"english":"people aged 15–59","chinese":"15至59歲人士"},{"english":"By 2050","chinese":"到2050年"},{"english":"this pattern is forecast to reverse","chinese":"預測這一模式會逆轉"},{"english":"is forecast to reverse","chinese":"預測會逆轉"},{"english":"the working-age group","chinese":"工作年齡組別"},{"english":"rising to 57.3%","chinese":"上升至57.3%"},{"english":"falling to 37.0%","chinese":"下降至37.0%"},{"english":"the elderly population","chinese":"老年人口"},{"english":"remain comparatively small","chinese":"仍然相對較小"},{"english":"though","chinese":"雖然；不過"},{"english":"is expected to increase from","chinese":"預計由……增加"},{"english":"from 3.6% to 5.7%","chinese":"由3.6%增至5.7%"},{"english":"showed a far older structure","chinese":"呈現年老得多的人口結構"},{"english":"a far older structure","chinese":"年老得多的結構"},{"english":"accounted for the largest proportion","chinese":"佔最大比例"},{"english":"the largest proportion","chinese":"最大比例"},{"english":"while those over 60","chinese":"而60歲以上人士"},{"english":"those over 60","chinese":"60歲以上人士"},{"english":"represented 24.1%","chinese":"佔24.1%"},{"english":"made up only 14.3%","chinese":"僅佔14.3%"},{"english":"the 60-plus group","chinese":"60歲以上組別"},{"english":"is projected to surge to","chinese":"預計會急升至"},{"english":"surge to 42.3%","chinese":"急升至42.3%"},{"english":"close to the working-age share","chinese":"接近工作年齡人口比例"},{"english":"the working-age share","chinese":"工作年齡人口比例"},{"english":"whereas","chinese":"而；然而"},{"english":"the youngest group","chinese":"最年輕組別"},{"english":"shrink slightly to 11.5%","chinese":"輕微縮減至11.5%"}]},"model-essay-5-ielts-task1-process-diagram":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-5-ielts-task1-process-diagram","essayKey":"process-diagram:5","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-5-ielts-task1-process-diagram","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-1/process-diagrams/process-diagram-5","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"The diagram illustrates the industrial process by which instant noodles are manufactured.","chinese":"該圖說明即食麵是如何透過工業流程被製造出來的。"},{"label":"Overview","english":"Overall, this is a linear, eight-stage procedure that starts with flour being stored in silos and ends with finished noodle cups being sealed and labelled. Broadly, the process can be divided into two phases: preparing and shaping the dough, followed by cooking, flavouring and packaging the product.","chinese":"整體而言，這是一個線性的八階段流程，從麵粉被存放在筒倉開始，以完成的麵杯被密封並貼上標籤結束。 大致上，該流程可分為兩個階段：先準備並塑造麵團，然後烹煮、調味並包裝產品。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"At the beginning, flour is delivered by truck and kept in storage silos. It is then transferred to a mixer, where water and oil are added to form dough. After this mixture has been prepared, it passes through a series of rollers, which flatten it into thin dough sheets. These sheets are subsequently cut into narrow strips, and the strips are shaped into round noodle discs.","chinese":"一開始，麵粉由貨車運送，並被存放在儲存筒倉中。 然後，麵粉被轉移到攪拌機中，在那裡加入水和油以形成麵團。 當這種混合物準備完成後，它會通過一系列滾軸，被壓平成薄薄的麵團片。 隨後，這些麵團片被切成狹長條狀，而這些條狀物再被塑造成圓形麵餅。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"In the second half of the process, the noodle discs are cooked in oil and then dried. Once this heating stage has been completed, the dried discs are placed into individual cups. Vegetables and spices are added at this point, turning the plain noodles into a complete convenience product. Finally, the cups are sealed and labelled before leaving the production line.","chinese":"在流程的後半部分，麵餅會在油中被烹煮，然後被烘乾。 當這個加熱階段完成後，乾燥的麵餅會被放入各自的杯子中。 在這個階段，蔬菜和香料會被加入，使原本普通的麵條變成完整的便利食品。 最後，杯子在離開生產線前會被密封並貼上標籤。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"The diagram illustrates","chinese":"圖解顯示"},{"english":"industrial process","chinese":"工業流程"},{"english":"the process by which","chinese":"……的過程"},{"english":"instant noodles","chinese":"即食麵"},{"english":"are manufactured","chinese":"被製造"},{"english":"a linear, eight-stage procedure","chinese":"線性的八階段程序"},{"english":"starts with","chinese":"以……開始"},{"english":"flour being stored in silos","chinese":"麵粉被儲存在筒倉內"},{"english":"ends with","chinese":"以……結束"},{"english":"finished noodle cups","chinese":"完成的杯麵"},{"english":"being sealed and labelled","chinese":"被密封和貼上標籤"},{"english":"Broadly","chinese":"概括來說"},{"english":"can be divided into","chinese":"可分為"},{"english":"two phases","chinese":"兩個階段"},{"english":"preparing and shaping the dough","chinese":"準備和塑造麵團"},{"english":"followed by","chinese":"隨後是"},{"english":"cooking, flavouring and packaging","chinese":"烹煮、調味和包裝"},{"english":"the product","chinese":"產品"},{"english":"At the beginning","chinese":"一開始"},{"english":"is delivered by truck","chinese":"由貨車運送"},{"english":"kept in storage silos","chinese":"儲存在筒倉內"},{"english":"storage silos","chinese":"儲存筒倉"},{"english":"transferred to a mixer","chinese":"被轉移到攪拌機"},{"english":"a mixer","chinese":"攪拌機"},{"english":"water and oil are added","chinese":"加入水和油"},{"english":"to form dough","chinese":"以形成麵團"},{"english":"dough","chinese":"麵團"},{"english":"this mixture has been prepared","chinese":"這混合物被準備好後"},{"english":"passes through","chinese":"經過"},{"english":"a series of rollers","chinese":"一系列滾軸"},{"english":"flatten it into","chinese":"將它壓平成"},{"english":"thin dough sheets","chinese":"薄麵皮"},{"english":"are subsequently cut into","chinese":"隨後被切成"},{"english":"narrow strips","chinese":"幼長條"},{"english":"are shaped into","chinese":"被塑造成"},{"english":"round noodle discs","chinese":"圓形麵餅"},{"english":"in the second half of the process","chinese":"在流程的後半部分"},{"english":"are cooked in oil","chinese":"在油中烹煮"},{"english":"then dried","chinese":"然後被烘乾"},{"english":"this heating stage","chinese":"這個加熱階段"},{"english":"has been completed","chinese":"已經完成"},{"english":"the dried discs","chinese":"烘乾後的麵餅"},{"english":"are placed into individual cups","chinese":"被放入獨立杯中"},{"english":"individual cups","chinese":"獨立杯"},{"english":"vegetables and spices","chinese":"蔬菜和香料"},{"english":"are added at this point","chinese":"在這一點加入"},{"english":"turning the plain noodles into","chinese":"將普通麵條變成"},{"english":"plain noodles","chinese":"普通麵條"},{"english":"a complete convenience product","chinese":"完整的便利食品"},{"english":"Finally","chinese":"最後"},{"english":"are sealed and labelled","chinese":"被密封和貼上標籤"},{"english":"before leaving the production line","chinese":"在離開生產線之前"},{"english":"the production line","chinese":"生產線"}]},"model-essay-5-ielts-task1-tables":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-5-ielts-task1-tables","essayKey":"tables:5","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-5-ielts-task1-tables","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-1/tables/table-5","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"The table compares the global market shares of mobile phone sales held by several manufacturers in 2005 and 2006.","chinese":"這張表比較了數間手機製造商在 2005 年和 2006 年所佔的全球手機銷售市場份額。Overview （總覽）Main Feature 1 （主要特徵一）。"},{"label":"Overview","english":"Overall, Nokia remained the clear market leader and slightly strengthened its position, while Motorola recorded the most notable gain among the named companies. By contrast, Samsung, LG, BenQ Mobile and the collective “Others” category all lost market share; Sony Ericsson was the only smaller named brand to grow.","chinese":"整體而言， Nokia 仍然是明顯的市場領導者，並略微鞏固了其地位；而在所有列名公司之中， Motorola 錄得最顯著的增長。Main Feature 2 （主要特徵二）。 相比之下， Samsung 、 LG 、 BenQ Mobile 以及合併計算的「其他」類別均失去市場份額； Sony Ericsson 則是較小型列名品牌中唯一錄得增長的一間。Body Paragraph 1 （正文第一段）Leading Companies Details （主要公司細節）。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"In 2005, Nokia accounted for 32.5% of worldwide sales, almost twice Motorola’s share of 17.7% and well ahead of Samsung, at 12.7%. One year later, Nokia had risen to 35%, widening its lead despite Motorola’s increase to 21.1%. Motorola’s rise, at 3.4 percentage points, was the largest improvement in the table, whereas Samsung slipped slightly to 11.8%.","chinese":"2005 年， Nokia 佔全球銷售的 32.5% ，幾乎是 Motorola 17.7% 的兩倍，並遠高於Samsung 的 12.7% 。 一年後， Nokia 上升至 35% ；儘管 Motorola 也增至 21.1% ， Nokia 仍進一步擴大其領先優勢。 Motorola 上升了 3.4 個百分點，是表中最大增幅；相反， Samsung 則輕微下跌至 11.8% 。Body Paragraph 2 （正文第二段）Smaller Companies and Others （較小公司及其他類別）。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"The remaining named manufacturers held much smaller shares. Sony Ericsson rose from 6.3% to 7.4%, overtaking LG, whose figure declined marginally from 6.7% to 6.3%. The steepest fall was seen in BenQ Mobile, which more than halved from 4.9% to 2.4%. Other manufacturers also became less significant collectively, dropping from 19.2% to 16.2%.","chinese":"其餘列名製造商所佔的市場份額明顯較小。 Sony Ericsson 從 6.3% 上升至 7.4% ，並超越了 LG ；後者的數字則由 6.7% 輕微下降至 6.3% 。 最大跌幅出現在 BenQ Mobile ，其市場份額由 4.9% 跌至 2.4% ，縮減了一半以上。 其他製造商合計所佔的重要性亦有所下降，從 19.2% 跌至 16.2% 。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"the table shows","chinese":"表格顯示"},{"english":"worldwide market share","chinese":"全球市場佔有率"},{"english":"the mobile phone market","chinese":"手提電話市場"},{"english":"manufacturers","chinese":"製造商"},{"english":"in the years 2005 and 2006","chinese":"在2005年和2006年"},{"english":"summarise the information","chinese":"概述資料"},{"english":"by selecting and reporting","chinese":"透過選取並報告……"},{"english":"the main features","chinese":"主要特徵"},{"english":"make comparisons where relevant","chinese":"在相關之處作出比較"},{"english":"the table compares","chinese":"表格比較"},{"english":"global market shares","chinese":"全球市場佔有率"},{"english":"mobile phone sales","chinese":"手提電話銷售"},{"english":"held by","chinese":"由……持有"},{"english":"several manufacturers","chinese":"幾間製造商"},{"english":"remained the clear market leader","chinese":"仍然是明顯的市場領導者"},{"english":"the clear market leader","chinese":"明顯的市場領導者"},{"english":"slightly strengthened its position","chinese":"稍為鞏固其地位"},{"english":"recorded the most notable gain","chinese":"錄得最明顯增長"},{"english":"the most notable gain","chinese":"最明顯增幅"},{"english":"among the named companies","chinese":"在列明名稱的公司之中"},{"english":"by contrast","chinese":"相比之下"},{"english":"collective “Others” category","chinese":"「其他」合計類別"},{"english":"lost market share","chinese":"失去市場佔有率"},{"english":"the only smaller named brand to grow","chinese":"唯一增長的較小型具名品牌"},{"english":"smaller named brand","chinese":"較小型具名品牌"},{"english":"in 2005","chinese":"在2005年"},{"english":"accounted for","chinese":"佔……"},{"english":"worldwide sales","chinese":"全球銷售"},{"english":"almost twice","chinese":"幾乎是……的兩倍"},{"english":"Motorola's share","chinese":"Motorola 的佔有率"},{"english":"well ahead of","chinese":"遠高於；大幅領先"},{"english":"at 12.7%","chinese":"為12.7%"},{"english":"one year later","chinese":"一年後"},{"english":"had risen to","chinese":"已上升至"},{"english":"widening its lead","chinese":"擴大其領先優勢"},{"english":"despite","chinese":"儘管"},{"english":"Motorola's increase","chinese":"Motorola 的升幅"},{"english":"increase to","chinese":"增加至"},{"english":"percentage points","chinese":"百分點"},{"english":"the largest improvement","chinese":"最大改善；最大升幅"},{"english":"whereas","chinese":"而；相反"},{"english":"slipped slightly to","chinese":"輕微下跌至"},{"english":"the remaining named manufacturers","chinese":"其餘具名製造商"},{"english":"held much smaller shares","chinese":"佔有率低得多"},{"english":"rose from X to Y","chinese":"由 X 上升至 Y"},{"english":"overtaking","chinese":"超越"},{"english":"whose figure declined marginally","chinese":"其數字輕微下降"},{"english":"declined marginally","chinese":"輕微下降"},{"english":"the steepest fall","chinese":"最大跌幅"},{"english":"was seen in","chinese":"出現在……"},{"english":"more than halved","chinese":"跌幅超過一半"},{"english":"from 4.9% to 2.4%","chinese":"由4.9%跌至2.4%"},{"english":"other manufacturers","chinese":"其他製造商"},{"english":"became less significant collectively","chinese":"整體重要性下降"},{"english":"collectively","chinese":"整體而言；合計"},{"english":"dropping from X to Y","chinese":"由 X 下降至 Y"},{"english":"market share increased","chinese":"市場佔有率上升"},{"english":"market share declined","chinese":"市場佔有率下降"},{"english":"strengthen its lead","chinese":"鞏固其領先地位"},{"english":"maintain first place","chinese":"保持第一位"},{"english":"narrow the gap","chinese":"收窄差距"},{"english":"gain ground","chinese":"取得進展；擴大佔有率"},{"english":"lose ground","chinese":"失去優勢；佔有率下降"},{"english":"a slight increase","chinese":"輕微增幅"},{"english":"a noticeable increase","chinese":"明顯增幅"},{"english":"a marginal decline","chinese":"輕微跌幅"},{"english":"a sharp decline","chinese":"大幅下跌"},{"english":"the dominant company","chinese":"佔主導地位的公司"},{"english":"the second-largest manufacturer","chinese":"第二大製造商"},{"english":"smaller competitors","chinese":"較小型競爭者"},{"english":"the gap between X and Y","chinese":"X 和 Y 之間的差距"},{"english":"widened in 2006","chinese":"在2006年擴大"},{"english":"the overall pattern","chinese":"整體模式"},{"english":"the strongest performer","chinese":"表現最強者"},{"english":"the weakest performer","chinese":"表現最弱者"},{"english":"in terms of percentage-point growth","chinese":"就百分點增長而言"}]},"model-essay-6-ielts-advantage-disadvantage":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-6-ielts-advantage-disadvantage","essayKey":"advantage-disadvantage:6","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-6-ielts-advantage-disadvantage","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/advantage-and-disadvantage/EdmundBd9AdDisAd-Q6","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"In today’s highly connected world, digital communication has made it possible for people from different countries to interact instantly and regularly. Through social media, messaging apps and video calls, individuals who would otherwise never meet are now able to exchange ideas, build relationships and work together. This is an overwhelmingly positive development because it expands access to valuable opportunities and promotes greater understanding between societies, although a few disadvantages do exist.","chinese":"在當今高度互聯的世界裡，數位溝通已使來自不同國家的人能夠即時而持續地互動。 透過社交媒體、即時通訊應用程式和視像通話，那些原本根本沒有機會相遇的人，如今也能交流想法、建立關係並彼此合作。 這無疑是一項整體上非常正面的發展，因為它擴大了人們接觸寶貴機會的途徑，並促進了不同社會之間更深入的理解，儘管它確實也存在一些缺點。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"The most significant advantage is that online international communication gives people access to relationships and opportunities that geography would normally prevent. A student in Hong Kong, for instance, can seek advice from a university mentor in Britain, join an online discussion group with members from several countries, and later develop academic or professional connections that would have been impossible in the past. This matters because such interaction is not merely casual conversation; it can lead to practical outcomes such as improved education, better employment prospects and broader career networks. Another major benefit is that regular contact with people from other cultures can reduce ignorance and prejudice. When individuals communicate directly with foreigners, they are exposed to different customs, viewpoints and lifestyles, which makes them more open-minded and better prepared for life in a globalised society. Therefore, online international communication is highly beneficial because it creates both practical opportunities and deeper intercultural understanding.","chinese":"最重要的優點是，跨國網上溝通讓人們得以接觸那些原本會因地理限制而無法建立的人際關係與機會。 例如，一名身在香港的學生可以向英國的大學導師請教，加入由多個國家成員組成的網上討論群組，並進一步發展出過去根本不可能建立的學術或專業聯繫。 這一點之所以重要，是因為這種互動並不只是隨意閒聊；它可以帶來實際成果，例如提升教育機會、改善就業前景，以及擴闊職業人脈網絡。 另一項主要好處是，與不同文化背景的人保持經常接觸，可以減少無知與偏見。 當人們直接與外國人交流時，他們會接觸到不同的習俗、觀點和生活方式，這會使他們變得更開放，也更能為全球化社會中的生活作好準備。 因此，跨國網上溝通極具價值，因為它同時創造了實際機會，並促進了更深層次的跨文化理解。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"There are, however, some disadvantages. The most serious is that online platforms can spread false or harmful information across borders with alarming speed. Misleading claims about politics, health or social issues can reach large audiences before they are corrected, which may create confusion or mistrust. In addition, digital interaction can sometimes be less genuine than face-to-face communication. Because people can hide behind anonymous accounts or present edited versions of themselves, online relationships may occasionally be superficial or even deceptive. Nevertheless, these problems are relatively limited and are usually caused by irresponsible use of technology rather than by international communication itself.","chinese":"然而，這種溝通方式也的確存在一些缺點。 其中最嚴重的一點是，網上平台能夠以驚人的速度跨越國界傳播錯誤或有害的信息。 有關政治、健康或社會議題的誤導性言論，往往在被更正之前便已傳播給大量受眾，從而造成混亂或不信任。 此外，數位互動有時不如面對面交流那樣真誠。 由於人們可以躲在匿名帳戶背後，或只展示經過修飾的自己，網上關係有時可能流於表面，甚至帶有欺騙性。 儘管如此，這些問題相對有限，而且通常是由不負責任地使用科技所造成的，而非跨國網上溝通本身所必然導致的結果。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, the ability to communicate online with people from other countries brings substantial benefits, especially by creating opportunities and encouraging intercultural understanding. Although it may also enable misinformation and insincere interaction, these drawbacks are minor in comparison, so the overall effect is clearly positive.","chinese":"總結來說，能夠在網上與來自其他國家的人交流，帶來了重大的好處，尤其體現在創造機會以及促進跨文化理解方面。 雖然它也可能助長錯誤資訊的傳播，以及不夠真誠的互動，但與其優點相比，這些缺點只是次要的。 因此，整體影響顯然是正面的。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"introduction","chinese":"引言"},{"english":"background","chinese":"背景"},{"english":"in today's highly connected world","chinese":"在當今高度互聯的世界"},{"english":"digital communication","chinese":"數碼溝通"},{"english":"make it possible for","chinese":"令……成為可能"},{"english":"interact instantly and regularly","chinese":"即時而定期互動"},{"english":"paraphrasing","chinese":"改寫"},{"english":"social media","chinese":"社交媒體"},{"english":"messaging apps","chinese":"即時通訊應用程式"},{"english":"video calls","chinese":"視像通話"},{"english":"would otherwise never meet","chinese":"否則永遠不會相遇"},{"english":"exchange ideas","chinese":"交流想法"},{"english":"build relationships","chinese":"建立關係"},{"english":"thesis statement","chinese":"中心論點"},{"english":"an overwhelmingly positive development","chinese":"極為正面的發展"},{"english":"expands access to","chinese":"擴大接觸……的機會"},{"english":"valuable opportunities","chinese":"寶貴機會"},{"english":"promotes greater understanding between","chinese":"促進……之間更深入的理解"},{"english":"a few disadvantages do exist","chinese":"確實存在一些缺點"},{"english":"body paragraph","chinese":"正文段落"},{"english":"topic sentence","chinese":"主題句"},{"english":"the most significant advantage","chinese":"最重要的優點"},{"english":"online international communication","chinese":"跨國網上溝通"},{"english":"gives people access to","chinese":"讓人們接觸到"},{"english":"geography would normally prevent","chinese":"地理因素通常會阻礙"},{"english":"supporting detail","chinese":"支持細節"},{"english":"seek advice from","chinese":"向……請教"},{"english":"a university mentor","chinese":"大學導師"},{"english":"join an online discussion group","chinese":"加入網上討論群組"},{"english":"develop academic or professional connections","chinese":"建立學術或專業聯繫"},{"english":"would have been impossible in the past","chinese":"在過去本來不可能"},{"english":"logic chain","chinese":"邏輯鏈"},{"english":"this matters because","chinese":"這一點重要，因為"},{"english":"not merely casual conversation","chinese":"不只是隨意閒聊"},{"english":"lead to practical outcomes","chinese":"帶來實際成果"},{"english":"improved education","chinese":"改善了的教育"},{"english":"better employment prospects","chinese":"更好的就業前景"},{"english":"broader career networks","chinese":"更廣闊的職業人脈網絡"},{"english":"another major benefit","chinese":"另一個主要好處"},{"english":"regular contact with","chinese":"與……定期接觸"},{"english":"other cultures","chinese":"其他文化"},{"english":"reduce ignorance and prejudice","chinese":"減少無知和偏見"},{"english":"communicate directly with","chinese":"直接與……溝通"},{"english":"be exposed to","chinese":"接觸到"},{"english":"different customs","chinese":"不同習俗"},{"english":"viewpoints and lifestyles","chinese":"觀點和生活方式"},{"english":"open-minded","chinese":"思想開放的"},{"english":"better prepared for","chinese":"更能為……作好準備"},{"english":"a globalised society","chinese":"全球化社會"},{"english":"highly beneficial","chinese":"極有益"},{"english":"practical opportunities","chinese":"實際機會"},{"english":"intercultural understanding","chinese":"跨文化理解"},{"english":"there are, however","chinese":"然而，也有"},{"english":"online platforms","chinese":"網上平台"},{"english":"false or harmful information","chinese":"錯誤或有害資料"},{"english":"across borders","chinese":"跨越國界"},{"english":"with alarming speed","chinese":"以驚人的速度"},{"english":"misleading claims","chinese":"誤導性說法"},{"english":"social issues","chinese":"社會議題"},{"english":"reach large audiences","chinese":"傳到大量受眾"},{"english":"before they are corrected","chinese":"在被更正之前"},{"english":"create confusion or mistrust","chinese":"造成混亂或不信任"},{"english":"in addition","chinese":"此外"},{"english":"digital interaction","chinese":"數碼互動"},{"english":"less genuine than","chinese":"不如……真誠"},{"english":"face-to-face communication","chinese":"面對面溝通"},{"english":"hide behind anonymous accounts","chinese":"躲在匿名帳戶背後"},{"english":"anonymous accounts","chinese":"匿名帳戶"},{"english":"present edited versions of themselves","chinese":"展示經修飾的自己"},{"english":"superficial","chinese":"表面的；膚淺的"},{"english":"deceptive","chinese":"具欺騙性的"},{"english":"nevertheless","chinese":"儘管如此"},{"english":"relatively limited","chinese":"相對有限"},{"english":"irresponsible use of technology","chinese":"不負責任地使用科技"},{"english":"rather than by","chinese":"而不是由……造成"},{"english":"international communication itself","chinese":"跨國溝通本身"},{"english":"reiterating stance","chinese":"重申立場"},{"english":"substantial benefits","chinese":"重大好處"},{"english":"encouraging intercultural understanding","chinese":"促進跨文化理解"},{"english":"misinformation","chinese":"錯誤資訊"},{"english":"insincere interaction","chinese":"不真誠的互動"},{"english":"minor in comparison","chinese":"相比之下是次要的"},{"english":"final judgment","chinese":"最終判斷"},{"english":"the overall effect","chinese":"整體影響"},{"english":"clearly positive","chinese":"明顯正面"}]},"model-essay-6-ielts-cause-solution":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-6-ielts-cause-solution","essayKey":"cause-solution:6","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-6-ielts-cause-solution","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/problem-and-cause/EdmundBd9CnS-Q6","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"In many parts of the world, cities record more crime than villages and small towns. This is not simply because urban residents are less law-abiding; rather, city life creates conditions in which crime is easier to commit and harder to prevent. The most effective response is therefore to reduce both the opportunities for crime and the pressures that push people towards it.","chinese":"在世界許多地方，城市錄得的犯罪比鄉村和小鎮更多。 這並不只是因為城市居民較不守法；相反，城市生活創造了一些條件，使犯罪更容易發生，也更難預防。 因此，最有效的應對方法，是同時減少犯罪機會，以及減輕那些把人推向犯罪的壓力。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"One major reason is the anonymity of urban life. In a small rural community, people tend to know one another, so suspicious behaviour is more visible and social pressure acts as a quiet form of control. In a large city, by contrast, offenders can disappear into the crowd. For example, pickpocketing is easier in a packed train station than in a village market, because victims, witnesses and police officers may struggle to identify the offender. Another reason is inequality. Cities often bring wealth and poverty face to face: luxury apartments may stand only a few streets away from overcrowded housing. When people feel excluded from the prosperity around them, some may turn to theft, drug dealing or gang activity, especially if legal routes to success seem blocked.","chinese":"其中一個主要原因，是城市生活的匿名性。 在一個細小的鄉村社區中，人們往往彼此認識，因此可疑行為更容易被看見，而社會壓力也會成為一種安靜但有效的控制力量。 相比之下，在大城市裡，犯罪者可以消失在人群之中。 例如，在擠迫的火車站裡扒竊，會比在鄉村市場中更容易，因為受害者、目擊者和警察都可能難以辨認犯罪者。 另一個原因是不平等。 城市往往使富裕與貧窮正面相遇：豪華住宅可能只與擁擠的住房相隔幾條街。 當人們覺得自己被排除在周圍的繁榮之外時，有些人可能會轉向盜竊、販毒或幫派活動，尤其是在合法取得成功的途徑似乎被堵塞時。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"To reduce urban crime, governments should first design cities in ways that make offending more difficult. Better lighting, reliable public transport, visible community policing and well-maintained public spaces can all reduce the sense that certain areas are unsafe or uncontrolled. For instance, a park that is clean, busy and properly lit is far less likely to become a place for drug dealing or violence. At the same time, prevention must go deeper than surveillance. Cities need stronger youth services, affordable education, job training and support for families under pressure. If young people can see a realistic path into work and belonging, crime becomes less attractive and less necessary.","chinese":"為了減少城市犯罪，政府首先應該以令犯罪更困難的方式來設計城市。 更好的照明、可靠的公共交通、可見的社區警務，以及保養良好的公共空間，都能減少某些地區不安全或失控的感覺。 例如，一個乾淨、熱鬧而且照明充足的公園，遠不容易變成販毒或暴力活動的場所。 與此同時，預防工作必須比監控走得更深入。 城市需要更完善的青少年服務、可負擔的教育、職業培訓，以及對承受壓力的家庭的支援。 如果年輕人能看見一條通向工作和歸屬感的現實道路，犯罪便會變得較不吸引，也較不必要。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, crime is often higher in urban areas because cities combine anonymity with sharper social inequality. Reducing it requires both practical safety measures and long-term social investment.","chinese":"總結來說，城市地區的犯罪率往往較高，是因為城市結合了匿名性和更尖銳的社會不平等。 要減少犯罪，既需要實際的安全措施，也需要長遠的社會投資。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"in many parts of the world","chinese":"在世界很多地方"},{"english":"record more crime than","chinese":"錄得比……更多罪案"},{"english":"villages and small towns","chinese":"鄉村和小鎮"},{"english":"not simply because","chinese":"不只是因為"},{"english":"urban residents","chinese":"城市居民"},{"english":"law-abiding","chinese":"守法的"},{"english":"creates conditions in which","chinese":"創造出……的條件"},{"english":"easier to commit","chinese":"較容易犯下"},{"english":"harder to prevent","chinese":"較難預防"},{"english":"the most effective response","chinese":"最有效的應對方法"},{"english":"opportunities for crime","chinese":"犯罪機會"},{"english":"pressures that push people towards","chinese":"將人推向……的壓力"},{"english":"one major reason","chinese":"一個主要原因"},{"english":"the anonymity of urban life","chinese":"城市生活的匿名性"},{"english":"a small rural community","chinese":"小型鄉郊社區"},{"english":"tend to know one another","chinese":"往往彼此認識"},{"english":"suspicious behaviour","chinese":"可疑行為"},{"english":"more visible","chinese":"更容易被看見"},{"english":"social pressure","chinese":"社會壓力"},{"english":"acts as","chinese":"發揮……作用"},{"english":"a quiet form of control","chinese":"一種無形的控制"},{"english":"by contrast","chinese":"相比之下"},{"english":"offenders","chinese":"犯罪者"},{"english":"disappear into the crowd","chinese":"消失在人群中"},{"english":"pickpocketing","chinese":"扒竊"},{"english":"a packed train station","chinese":"擠迫的火車站"},{"english":"village market","chinese":"鄉村市場"},{"english":"victims, witnesses and police officers","chinese":"受害人、目擊者和警員"},{"english":"struggle to identify","chinese":"難以辨認"},{"english":"the offender","chinese":"犯罪者"},{"english":"another reason is","chinese":"另一個原因是"},{"english":"inequality","chinese":"不平等"},{"english":"bring wealth and poverty face to face","chinese":"令富裕與貧窮正面並存"},{"english":"luxury apartments","chinese":"豪華住宅"},{"english":"stand only a few streets away from","chinese":"只相隔幾條街"},{"english":"overcrowded housing","chinese":"過度擠迫的住房"},{"english":"feel excluded from","chinese":"感到被排除於……之外"},{"english":"prosperity around them","chinese":"身邊的繁榮"},{"english":"turn to theft","chinese":"轉向盜竊"},{"english":"drug dealing","chinese":"販毒"},{"english":"gang activity","chinese":"幫派活動"},{"english":"legal routes to success","chinese":"通往成功的合法途徑"},{"english":"seem blocked","chinese":"似乎受阻"},{"english":"reduce urban crime","chinese":"減少城市罪案"},{"english":"design cities in ways that","chinese":"以……的方式設計城市"},{"english":"make offending more difficult","chinese":"令犯罪更困難"},{"english":"better lighting","chinese":"更好的照明"},{"english":"reliable public transport","chinese":"可靠的公共交通"},{"english":"visible community policing","chinese":"明顯可見的社區警政"},{"english":"well-maintained public spaces","chinese":"保養良好的公共空間"},{"english":"reduce the sense that","chinese":"減少……的感覺"},{"english":"unsafe or uncontrolled","chinese":"不安全或無人管理"},{"english":"properly lit","chinese":"照明充足"},{"english":"far less likely to","chinese":"可能性低得多"},{"english":"become a place for","chinese":"成為……的地方"},{"english":"violence","chinese":"暴力"},{"english":"go deeper than","chinese":"必須比……更深入"},{"english":"surveillance","chinese":"監察"},{"english":"youth services","chinese":"青少年服務"},{"english":"affordable education","chinese":"負擔得起的教育"},{"english":"job training","chinese":"職業培訓"},{"english":"support for families under pressure","chinese":"對受壓家庭的支援"},{"english":"a realistic path into work","chinese":"進入職場的現實途徑"},{"english":"belonging","chinese":"歸屬感"},{"english":"less attractive and less necessary","chinese":"較不吸引，也較不必要"},{"english":"higher in urban areas","chinese":"在城市地區較高"},{"english":"combine anonymity with","chinese":"將匿名性與……結合"},{"english":"sharper social inequality","chinese":"更明顯的社會不平等"},{"english":"practical safety measures","chinese":"實際安全措施"},{"english":"long-term social investment","chinese":"長期社會投資"}]},"model-essay-6-ielts-direct-question":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-6-ielts-direct-question","essayKey":"direct-question:6","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-6-ielts-direct-question","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/direct-question/EdmundBd9Dir-Q6","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"Many people equate business success with the amount of money a company or entrepreneur earns. However, money is not a true indicator of success, because it can hide weak foundations, poor ethics and unstable growth. A business should instead be judged by whether it creates lasting value for customers, workers and society.","chinese":"許多人把商業成功等同於一間公司或一位企業家所賺取的金錢數量。 然而，金錢並不是成功的真正指標，因為它可能掩蓋薄弱的基礎、不良的道德操守，以及不穩定的增長。 相反，一門生意應該根據它是否為顧客、員工和社會創造持久價值來評判。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"The main problem with using money as the only measure is that financial results can be misleading. A company may make large profits by cutting corners, underpaying staff or selling low-quality products aggressively. On paper, such a business may look successful; in reality, it is building a house on sand. If customers eventually lose trust, employees leave and the brand becomes associated with dishonesty, its short-term income means very little. In this sense, money shows that a business is earning, but it does not prove that the business is healthy, respected or likely to survive.","chinese":"把金錢作為唯一衡量標準的主要問題在於，財務結果可能具有誤導性。 一間公司可能透過偷工減料、低薪對待員工，或積極銷售低質素產品來獲取龐大利潤。 從表面上看，這樣的生意可能顯得成功；但實際上，它是在沙上建屋，根基並不穩固。 如果顧客最終失去信任、員工離職，而品牌也變得與不誠實聯繫在一起，那麼它的短期收入其實意義不大。 從這個角度來看，金錢只能顯示一門生意正在賺錢，但不能證明這門生意是健康的、受人尊重的，或有可能長久生存。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"There are several better ways to measure business success. One key measure is customer loyalty, because repeated purchases and positive word of mouth show that people genuinely value what the company provides. Another important measure is employee retention. A business whose staff feel fairly treated is more likely to maintain quality, innovation and strong internal culture. Success can also be judged by long-term sustainability, such as whether the company adapts to changing markets without damaging the environment or exploiting vulnerable people. For example, a modest local company that pays fair wages, keeps loyal customers and operates responsibly may be more successful than a larger firm that earns more money but burns trust as quickly as it generates revenue.","chinese":"衡量商業成功有幾種更好的方法。 其中一個關鍵衡量標準是顧客忠誠度，因為重複購買和正面的口碑顯示，人們真正重視這間公司所提供的東西。 另一個重要的衡量標準是員工留任率。 如果一間公司的員工覺得自己受到公平對待，這間公司便更有可能維持品質、創新能力和強大的內部文化。 成功也可以根據長期可持續性來評判，例如公司是否能夠適應不斷變化的市場，同時不破壞環境或剝削弱勢群體。 例如，一間規模不大的本地公司，如果能支付公平薪酬、留住忠實顧客，並以負責任的方式經營，可能比一間賺更多錢、但在創造收入的同時迅速消耗信任的大公司更成功。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, money is not a true indicator of business success. It is only a surface-level sign of financial performance. Real success should be measured by trust, stability, ethical conduct and the ability to create value that lasts.","chinese":"總結來說，金錢並不是商業成功的真正指標。 它只是一種表層的財務表現標誌。 真正的成功應該由信任、穩定性、道德操守，以及創造持久價值的能力來衡量。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"equate business success with","chinese":"將商業成功等同於"},{"english":"the amount of money","chinese":"金錢數額"},{"english":"a company or entrepreneur","chinese":"公司或企業家"},{"english":"earns","chinese":"賺取"},{"english":"a true indicator of","chinese":"……的真正指標"},{"english":"hide weak foundations","chinese":"掩蓋薄弱基礎"},{"english":"poor ethics","chinese":"不良道德操守"},{"english":"unstable growth","chinese":"不穩定的增長"},{"english":"be judged by","chinese":"根據……來判斷"},{"english":"creates lasting value for","chinese":"為……創造持久價值"},{"english":"customers, workers and society","chinese":"顧客、員工和社會"},{"english":"the only measure","chinese":"唯一衡量標準"},{"english":"financial results","chinese":"財務表現"},{"english":"be misleading","chinese":"具誤導性"},{"english":"make large profits","chinese":"賺取巨額利潤"},{"english":"cutting corners","chinese":"走捷徑；偷工減料"},{"english":"underpaying staff","chinese":"給員工過低薪酬"},{"english":"low-quality products","chinese":"低質素產品"},{"english":"selling low-quality products aggressively","chinese":"大力銷售低質素產品"},{"english":"on paper","chinese":"表面上；從數字上看"},{"english":"in reality","chinese":"實際上"},{"english":"building a house on sand","chinese":"建在沙上的房子；基礎不穩"},{"english":"eventually lose trust","chinese":"最終失去信任"},{"english":"employees leave","chinese":"員工離職"},{"english":"become associated with","chinese":"與……聯繫起來"},{"english":"dishonesty","chinese":"不誠實"},{"english":"short-term income","chinese":"短期收入"},{"english":"means very little","chinese":"意義不大"},{"english":"in this sense","chinese":"從這個意義上說"},{"english":"prove that","chinese":"證明"},{"english":"healthy, respected or likely to survive","chinese":"健康、受尊重或有可能生存下去"},{"english":"several better ways to","chinese":"幾種更好的方法去"},{"english":"measure business success","chinese":"衡量商業成功"},{"english":"one key measure","chinese":"一個關鍵衡量標準"},{"english":"customer loyalty","chinese":"顧客忠誠度"},{"english":"repeated purchases","chinese":"重複購買"},{"english":"positive word of mouth","chinese":"正面口碑"},{"english":"genuinely value","chinese":"真正重視"},{"english":"what the company provides","chinese":"公司所提供的東西"},{"english":"employee retention","chinese":"員工留任率"},{"english":"feel fairly treated","chinese":"感到受到公平對待"},{"english":"maintain quality","chinese":"維持質素"},{"english":"innovation","chinese":"創新"},{"english":"strong internal culture","chinese":"強大的內部文化"},{"english":"long-term sustainability","chinese":"長遠可持續性"},{"english":"adapts to changing markets","chinese":"適應不斷變化的市場"},{"english":"damaging the environment","chinese":"破壞環境"},{"english":"exploiting vulnerable people","chinese":"剝削弱勢人士"},{"english":"a modest local company","chinese":"規模不大的本地公司"},{"english":"pays fair wages","chinese":"支付公平工資"},{"english":"loyal customers","chinese":"忠實顧客"},{"english":"operates responsibly","chinese":"負責任地營運"},{"english":"a larger firm","chinese":"較大型公司"},{"english":"burns trust","chinese":"消耗信任"},{"english":"generates revenue","chinese":"產生收入"},{"english":"a surface-level sign of","chinese":"……的表面跡象"},{"english":"financial performance","chinese":"財務表現"},{"english":"real success","chinese":"真正的成功"},{"english":"be measured by","chinese":"以……來衡量"},{"english":"trust","chinese":"信任"},{"english":"stability","chinese":"穩定性"},{"english":"ethical conduct","chinese":"道德行為"},{"english":"the ability to create value that lasts","chinese":"創造持久價值的能力"}]},"model-essay-6-ielts-discuss-both-views":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-6-ielts-discuss-both-views","essayKey":"discuss-both-views:6","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-6-ielts-discuss-both-views","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/discuss-both-views-your-opinion/EdmundBd9ExpBth-Q6","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"Some people argue that a business can only become successful if it offers a unique product. While originality can certainly help a company stand out, I do not believe it is the only factor behind commercial success. In my view, a company succeeds mainly because it understands its customers, manages its operations well, and builds long-term trust.","chinese":"有些人認為，一間企業只有在提供獨特產品的情況下，才能取得成功。 雖然原創性確實能幫助一間公司脫穎而出，但我不認為它是商業成功背後的唯一因素。 在我看來，一間公司之所以成功，主要是因為它了解顧客、良好管理營運，並建立長期信任。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"The first major factor is whether a company can meet real customer needs. A product does not have to be completely original if it solves a problem better, faster, or more conveniently than its competitors. In fact, many successful businesses sell ordinary products, such as food, clothing, or household goods, but they do so in a way that customers find reliable and accessible. For example, a small café may not offer anything revolutionary, yet it can become profitable if it provides good coffee, fair prices, and a comfortable atmosphere. This shows that success often depends less on being unique and more on being useful, consistent, and relevant to the market.","chinese":"第一個主要因素是，一間公司能否滿足真正的顧客需求。 如果一件產品能比競爭對手更好、更快或更方便地解決問題，它並不一定需要完全原創 事實上，許多成功的企業出售的都是普通產品，例如食物、衣服或家居用品，但它們以一種讓顧客覺得可靠且容易接觸的方式去經營。 例如，一間小咖啡店未必提供任何革命性的東西，但如果它能提供好咖啡、公道價格和舒適環境，它仍然可以獲利。 這表明，成功往往較少取決於是否獨特，而更多取決於是否實用、穩定，並且符合市場需要。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"Another important factor is the quality of management. Even an excellent product can fail if a company has poor leadership, weak financial control, or careless customer service. Good managers make sensible decisions about pricing, staff training, marketing, and cost control. They also adapt when the market changes, instead of clinging to old methods. For instance, a business that responds quickly to online shopping trends or changing consumer habits is more likely to survive than one that refuses to modernise. In addition, companies that treat customers well can develop a strong reputation, and this reputation becomes a powerful asset over time.","chinese":"另一個重要因素是管理質素。 即使產品十分出色，如果公司領導不善、財務控制薄弱，或顧客服務粗心大意，它仍然可能失敗。 優秀的管理者會在定價、員工培訓、市場推廣和成本控制方面作出明智決定。 當市場發生變化時，他們也會作出調整，而不是死守舊方法。 例如，一間能夠快速回應網上購物趨勢或消費者習慣變化的企業，比一間拒絕現代化的企業更有可能生存下來。 此外，善待顧客的公司能夠建立良好聲譽，而這種聲譽隨著時間會成為一項強大的資"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, having a unique product can give a business an initial advantage, but it is not the only route to success. The most successful companies are those that understand their market, operate efficiently, adapt intelligently, and earn the trust of their customers.","chinese":"總結來說，擁有獨特產品可以給企業帶來初步優勢，但這並不是通往成功的唯一途徑。 最成功的公司，是那些了解市場、高效營運、明智適應變化，並贏得顧客信任的公司。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"can only become successful if","chinese":"只有在……情況下才能成功"},{"english":"offers a unique product","chinese":"提供獨特產品"},{"english":"originality","chinese":"原創性"},{"english":"stand out","chinese":"突圍而出；突出"},{"english":"the only factor behind","chinese":"……背後的唯一因素"},{"english":"commercial success","chinese":"商業成功"},{"english":"In my view","chinese":"在我看來"},{"english":"succeeds mainly because","chinese":"成功主要是因為"},{"english":"understands its customers","chinese":"了解顧客"},{"english":"manages its operations well","chinese":"妥善管理營運"},{"english":"builds long-term trust","chinese":"建立長遠信任"},{"english":"the first major factor","chinese":"第一個主要因素"},{"english":"meet real customer needs","chinese":"滿足真正的顧客需要"},{"english":"does not have to be","chinese":"不一定要"},{"english":"completely original","chinese":"完全原創"},{"english":"solves a problem","chinese":"解決問題"},{"english":"better, faster, or more conveniently","chinese":"更好、更快或更方便地"},{"english":"than its competitors","chinese":"比競爭對手"},{"english":"In fact","chinese":"事實上"},{"english":"successful businesses","chinese":"成功企業"},{"english":"ordinary products","chinese":"普通產品"},{"english":"household goods","chinese":"家居用品"},{"english":"do so in a way that","chinese":"以一種……的方式這樣做"},{"english":"find reliable and accessible","chinese":"覺得可靠而容易接觸"},{"english":"a small café","chinese":"小型咖啡店"},{"english":"anything revolutionary","chinese":"任何革命性的東西"},{"english":"become profitable","chinese":"變得有盈利"},{"english":"fair prices","chinese":"公道價格"},{"english":"a comfortable atmosphere","chinese":"舒適的氣氛"},{"english":"This shows that","chinese":"這顯示"},{"english":"depends less on","chinese":"較少取決於"},{"english":"being unique","chinese":"獨特性"},{"english":"more on being useful","chinese":"更多取決於有用"},{"english":"consistent","chinese":"穩定一致"},{"english":"relevant to the market","chinese":"符合市場需要"},{"english":"another important factor","chinese":"另一個重要因素"},{"english":"the quality of management","chinese":"管理質素"},{"english":"an excellent product","chinese":"出色產品"},{"english":"poor leadership","chinese":"糟糕的領導"},{"english":"weak financial control","chinese":"薄弱的財務控制"},{"english":"careless customer service","chinese":"粗心大意的客戶服務"},{"english":"make sensible decisions about","chinese":"就……作出明智決定"},{"english":"pricing","chinese":"定價"},{"english":"staff training","chinese":"員工培訓"},{"english":"cost control","chinese":"成本控制"},{"english":"adapt when the market changes","chinese":"在市場變化時適應"},{"english":"instead of clinging to","chinese":"而不是死守"},{"english":"old methods","chinese":"舊方法"},{"english":"responds quickly to","chinese":"迅速回應"},{"english":"online shopping trends","chinese":"網上購物趨勢"},{"english":"changing consumer habits","chinese":"不斷改變的消費者習慣"},{"english":"more likely to survive","chinese":"更有可能生存下去"},{"english":"refuses to modernise","chinese":"拒絕現代化"},{"english":"In addition","chinese":"此外"},{"english":"treat customers well","chinese":"善待顧客"},{"english":"develop a strong reputation","chinese":"建立良好聲譽"},{"english":"a powerful asset","chinese":"強大的資產"},{"english":"over time","chinese":"隨時間"},{"english":"give a business an initial advantage","chinese":"給企業初期優勢"},{"english":"an initial advantage","chinese":"初期優勢"},{"english":"the only route to success","chinese":"成功的唯一途徑"},{"english":"understand their market","chinese":"了解市場"},{"english":"operate efficiently","chinese":"高效營運"},{"english":"adapt intelligently","chinese":"明智地適應"},{"english":"earn the trust of","chinese":"贏得……的信任"}]},"model-essay-6-ielts-opinion":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-6-ielts-opinion","essayKey":"opinion:6","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-6-ielts-opinion","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/opinions/EdmundBd9OP-Q6","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"Because retail markets are increasingly dominated by supermarket chains, independent shops in many towns now struggle to survive. I completely agree that the disappearance of small local businesses can lead to the death of local communities, because these businesses sustain both social relationships and the economic life on which community identity depends.","chinese":"由於零售市場愈來愈被連鎖超級市場主導，許多城鎮中的獨立商店如今都在艱難求存。 我完全同意，小型本地企業的消失可能會導致地方社區走向衰亡，因為這些企業維繫着社區賴以建立自身認同的人際關係，以及其所依存的經濟生活。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"First, small businesses function as social anchors rather than mere places of transaction. When residents regularly visit the same bakery, grocer or café, they develop familiarity with the people who work there. Over time, these repeated exchanges create trust, local knowledge and a sense of belonging. This matters especially for older residents and people who live alone, for whom such encounters may form an important part of daily life. Once these shops close, shopping becomes more impersonal, as people simply visit a supermarket, pay and leave. For example, an elderly customer who once spoke to a local shopkeeper every morning may lose one of his few social contacts. As a result, the informal ties that hold a neighbourhood together begin to weaken.","chinese":"首先，小型企業的作用不只是交易場所，更是社交關係的支點。 當居民經常光顧同一家麵包店、雜貨店或咖啡館時，他們便會逐漸熟悉在那裏工作的人。 隨着時間過去，這些一再出現的互動會建立起信任、對地方的了解，以及歸屬感。 這一點對年長居民和獨居人士尤其重要，因為這類相遇很可能構成了他們日常生活中重要的一部分。 一旦這些商店倒閉，購物便會變得更加缺乏人情味，因為人們只是走進超市、付款，然後離開。 例如，一位原本每早都會和本地店主交談的長者，可能會失去他少數的社交接觸之一 結果，維繫整個社區的非正式聯繫便開始削弱。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"Local businesses also keep money and character within the area. Because they are often owned by local families, their earnings are more likely to be reinvested nearby through local hiring, nearby suppliers and support for neighbourhood events. This creates a cycle in which local spending helps other local services survive. Independent shops also give a town centre its distinctive identity; a street filled with family-run bookstores, cafés and food stalls reflects the people who live there. By contrast, when chain supermarkets dominate, profits and decision-making are centralised, and high streets gradually become uniform. A place may still contain shops and consumers, but it no longer functions as a genuine community in the fuller social sense.","chinese":"本地企業也能把資金和地方特色留在社區之內。 由於它們往往由本地家庭擁有，因此其收益更有可能透過聘用本地員工、採用附近供應商，以及支持社區活動等方式，再投放回當地。 這便形成了一個循環：本地消費幫助其他本地服務持續生存。 獨立商店也賦予城鎮中心鮮明而獨特的身分；一條街若佈滿家庭經營的書店、咖啡館和小吃攤，便能反映出居住於此的人們的面貌。 相反，當連鎖超級市場佔據主導地位時，利潤和決策權都會被集中起來，而商業街也會逐漸變得千篇一律。 一個地方也許仍然有商店和消費者，但從更完整的社會意義來看，它已不再作為一個真正的社區而存在。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, I strongly agree that the closure of small local businesses can bring about the death of local communities. Without them, neighbourhoods lose both the human relationships and the locally rooted economic networks that make communal life possible.","chinese":"總而言之，我強烈同意，小型本地企業的倒閉可能會導致地方社區的消亡。 沒有了它們，社區失去的將不只是人與人之間的聯繫，還有那些扎根於本地、使共同生活成為可能的經濟網絡。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"retail markets","chinese":"零售市場"},{"english":"be increasingly dominated by","chinese":"越來越受……主導"},{"english":"supermarket chains","chinese":"連鎖超級市場"},{"english":"independent shops","chinese":"獨立店舖"},{"english":"struggle to survive","chinese":"難以生存"},{"english":"the disappearance of","chinese":"……的消失"},{"english":"small local businesses","chinese":"本地小商戶"},{"english":"lead to","chinese":"導致"},{"english":"the death of local communities","chinese":"本地社區的消亡"},{"english":"sustain both","chinese":"同時維持"},{"english":"social relationships","chinese":"社交關係"},{"english":"the economic life","chinese":"經濟生活；經濟活力"},{"english":"community identity","chinese":"社區身份"},{"english":"depend on","chinese":"取決於；依賴"},{"english":"function as","chinese":"發揮……作用"},{"english":"social anchors","chinese":"社交支柱；社區連繫的支點"},{"english":"rather than mere places of transaction","chinese":"而不只是交易場所"},{"english":"places of transaction","chinese":"交易場所"},{"english":"regularly visit","chinese":"定期到訪"},{"english":"develop familiarity with","chinese":"對……產生熟悉感"},{"english":"over time","chinese":"隨時間"},{"english":"repeated exchanges","chinese":"重複的交流"},{"english":"create trust","chinese":"建立信任"},{"english":"local knowledge","chinese":"本地資訊；對本地的了解"},{"english":"a sense of belonging","chinese":"歸屬感"},{"english":"this matters especially for","chinese":"這對……尤其重要"},{"english":"older residents","chinese":"年長居民"},{"english":"live alone","chinese":"獨居"},{"english":"for whom","chinese":"對……來說"},{"english":"such encounters","chinese":"這類相遇；這類接觸"},{"english":"form an important part of","chinese":"構成……的重要部分"},{"english":"daily life","chinese":"日常生活"},{"english":"once these shops close","chinese":"一旦這些店舖結業"},{"english":"become more impersonal","chinese":"變得更沒有人情味"},{"english":"simply visit a supermarket, pay and leave","chinese":"只是去超級市場付款後離開"},{"english":"a local shopkeeper","chinese":"本地店主"},{"english":"one of his few social contacts","chinese":"他為數不多的社交接觸之一"},{"english":"as a result","chinese":"因此"},{"english":"informal ties","chinese":"非正式聯繫"},{"english":"hold a neighbourhood together","chinese":"凝聚社區"},{"english":"begin to weaken","chinese":"開始減弱"},{"english":"keep money and character within the area","chinese":"將金錢和特色留在區內"},{"english":"be owned by local families","chinese":"由本地家庭擁有"},{"english":"earnings","chinese":"收入；收益"},{"english":"be reinvested nearby","chinese":"在附近再投資"},{"english":"local hiring","chinese":"本地招聘"},{"english":"nearby suppliers","chinese":"附近供應商"},{"english":"support for neighbourhood events","chinese":"對社區活動的支持"},{"english":"create a cycle in which","chinese":"形成一個……的循環"},{"english":"local spending","chinese":"本地消費"},{"english":"local services","chinese":"本地服務"},{"english":"give a town centre its distinctive identity","chinese":"賦予市中心獨特身份"},{"english":"distinctive identity","chinese":"獨特身份；獨有特色"},{"english":"family-run bookstores","chinese":"家庭經營的書店"},{"english":"food stalls","chinese":"小食檔；食物攤檔"},{"english":"reflect the people who live there","chinese":"反映當地居民的特色"},{"english":"by contrast","chinese":"相反"},{"english":"chain supermarkets","chinese":"連鎖超級市場"},{"english":"dominate","chinese":"主導"},{"english":"profits and decision-making","chinese":"利潤和決策"},{"english":"be centralised","chinese":"被集中"},{"english":"high streets","chinese":"主要商業街"},{"english":"gradually become uniform","chinese":"逐漸變得千篇一律"},{"english":"contain shops and consumers","chinese":"有店舖和消費者"},{"english":"no longer functions as","chinese":"不再發揮……作用"},{"english":"a genuine community","chinese":"真正的社區"},{"english":"in the fuller social sense","chinese":"從更完整的社會意義上"},{"english":"the closure of","chinese":"……的結業"},{"english":"bring about","chinese":"帶來；導致"},{"english":"without them","chinese":"沒有它們"},{"english":"human relationships","chinese":"人與人之間的關係"},{"english":"locally rooted economic networks","chinese":"扎根本地的經濟網絡"},{"english":"communal life","chinese":"社群生活；社區生活"},{"english":"make communal life possible","chinese":"令社區生活成為可能"}]},"model-essay-6-ielts-task1-bar-charts":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-6-ielts-task1-bar-charts","essayKey":"bar-charts:6","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-6-ielts-task1-bar-charts","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-1/bar-charts/bar-chart-6","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"The bar chart compares the percentages of Australian men and women in six age groups who did regular physical activity in 2010.","chinese":"這張柱狀圖比較了 2010 年澳洲男性和女性在六個年齡組中定期進行體育活動的百分比。"},{"label":"Overview","english":"Overall, women were more active than men in all age groups except 15–24. Male participation was highest among the youngest adults, then fell to a low in middle age before rising gradually, while the female figures remained relatively steady at around 48% to 53%.","chinese":"整體而言，除了 15 至 24 歲組之外，女性在所有年齡組中都比男性更活躍。 男性參與率在最年輕的成年人中最高，之後下降至中年低點，然後逐漸回升；相比之下，女性數據則相對穩定，大約維持在 48% 至 53% 之間。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"In the 15–24 group, 52.8% of men exercised regularly, compared with 47.7% of women. The pattern then reversed: male participation dropped to 42.2% among 25- to 34-year-olds and reached its lowest point, 39.5%, in the 35–44 category. By contrast, the corresponding female rates rose from 48.9% to 52.5%, creating the largest gender gap, at 13 percentage points.","chinese":"在 15 至 24 歲組中， 52.8% 的男性定期運動，而女性則為 47.7% 。 之後，這一模式出現逆轉： 25 至 34 歲男性的參與率下降至 42.2% ，並在 35 至 44 歲組達到最低點，為 39.5% 。 相比之下，相應的女性比率從 48.9% 上升至 52.5% ，形成了最大的性別差距，達13 個百分點。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"In the older age groups, the male figure recovered from 43.1% for those aged 45–54 to 45.1% among 55–64s and 46.7% among people aged 65 and over. Women reached their peak in the 45–54 group, at 53.3%, and remained almost as high for 55–64s, at 53.0%. In the oldest cohort, however, female participation fell to 47.1%, almost matching the male rate.","chinese":"在較年長的年齡組中，男性數據有所回升： 45 至 54 歲組為 43.1% ， 55 至 64 歲組升至 45.1% ， 65 歲及以上組則達到 46.7% 。 女性在 45 至 54 歲組達到最高點，為 53.3% ；在 55 至 64 歲組中仍幾乎同樣高，為。 然而，在最年長的群體中，女性參與率下降至 47.1% ，幾乎與男性比率相同。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"compares the percentages of","chinese":"比較……的百分比"},{"english":"Australian men and women","chinese":"澳洲男性及女性"},{"english":"in six age groups","chinese":"在六個年齡組別中"},{"english":"did regular physical activity","chinese":"定期做體能活動"},{"english":"regular physical activity","chinese":"定期體能活動"},{"english":"Overall","chinese":"整體而言"},{"english":"more active than","chinese":"比……更活躍"},{"english":"in all age groups except","chinese":"除……外所有年齡組別"},{"english":"male participation","chinese":"男性參與率"},{"english":"was highest among","chinese":"在……之中最高"},{"english":"the youngest adults","chinese":"最年輕的成年人"},{"english":"fell to a low","chinese":"跌至低位"},{"english":"in middle age","chinese":"在中年時期"},{"english":"before rising gradually","chinese":"隨後逐漸上升"},{"english":"female figures","chinese":"女性數字"},{"english":"remained relatively steady","chinese":"保持相對穩定"},{"english":"at around 48% to 53%","chinese":"約在48%至53%之間"},{"english":"in the 15–24 group","chinese":"在15至24歲組別中"},{"english":"exercised regularly","chinese":"定期運動"},{"english":"compared with","chinese":"與……相比"},{"english":"the pattern then reversed","chinese":"之後模式逆轉"},{"english":"dropped to","chinese":"下降至"},{"english":"among 25- to 34-year-olds","chinese":"在25至34歲人士之中"},{"english":"reached its lowest point","chinese":"達到最低點"},{"english":"the 35–44 category","chinese":"35至44歲類別"},{"english":"By contrast","chinese":"相比之下"},{"english":"the corresponding female rates","chinese":"相應的女性比率"},{"english":"rose from 48.9% to 52.5%","chinese":"由48.9%上升至52.5%"},{"english":"creating the largest gender gap","chinese":"形成最大的性別差距"},{"english":"the largest gender gap","chinese":"最大的性別差距"},{"english":"at 13 percentage points","chinese":"達13個百分點"},{"english":"percentage points","chinese":"百分點"},{"english":"in the older age groups","chinese":"在較年長組別中"},{"english":"the male figure","chinese":"男性數字"},{"english":"recovered from","chinese":"從……回升"},{"english":"those aged 45–54","chinese":"45至54歲人士"},{"english":"among 55–64s","chinese":"在55至64歲人士之中"},{"english":"people aged 65 and over","chinese":"65歲或以上人士"},{"english":"reached their peak","chinese":"達到高峰"},{"english":"in the 45–54 group","chinese":"在45至54歲組別中"},{"english":"remained almost as high","chinese":"仍然幾乎一樣高"},{"english":"for 55–64s","chinese":"對55至64歲人士而言"},{"english":"in the oldest cohort","chinese":"在最年長群組中"},{"english":"female participation","chinese":"女性參與率"},{"english":"fell to 47.1%","chinese":"下降至47.1%"},{"english":"almost matching the male rate","chinese":"幾乎與男性比率相同"},{"english":"the male rate","chinese":"男性比率"}]},"model-essay-6-ielts-task1-line-graph":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-6-ielts-task1-line-graph","essayKey":"line-graph:6","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-6-ielts-task1-line-graph","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-1/line-graphs/line-graph-6","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"The line graph illustrates tourist numbers on a Caribbean island between 2010 and 2017, separating visitors who stayed on cruise ships from those accommodated on the island.","chinese":"這張折線圖說明了 2010 年至 2017 年間前往某個加勒比海島嶼的遊客人數，並區分了住在遊輪上的遊客和住在島上的遊客。"},{"label":"Overview","english":"Overall, total arrivals rose substantially, more than tripling across the period. Island-based tourists were the larger group at first, but cruise passengers grew much faster and had become the leading category by 2017.","chinese":"整體而言，總到訪人數在整段期間大幅上升，增加了超過三倍。 起初，住在島上的遊客是較大的群體，但遊輪遊客增長得更快，並在 2017 年成為主要類別。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"In 2010, the island attracted 1 million visitors, about three quarters of whom stayed on the island. This total rose steadily to 2 million in 2013, when island-based tourists reached 1.5 million. Over the same early period, the cruise-ship figure moved unevenly, increasing from 250,000 to 500,000 in 2011 before falling back to 250,000 in 2012.","chinese":"2010 年，該島吸引了 100 萬名遊客，其中約四分之三住在島上。 到 2013 年，總遊客人數穩步上升至 200 萬，而當時住在島上的遊客達到 150 萬。 在同一前期階段，遊輪遊客人數變化不太穩定，先從 25 萬上升至 2011 年的 50萬，然後在 2012 年回落至 25 萬。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"From 2014 onwards, cruise passengers became the main driver of growth. Their number climbed from 1 million in 2014 to 1.5 million in 2016, overtaking the island-based group, before reaching 2 million in 2017. By contrast, tourists staying on the island remained close to 1.5 million after 2013, except for a slight fall in 2016. Consequently, total arrivals plateaued at around 2.75 million in 2015 and 2016, then rose sharply to 3.5 million.","chinese":"從 2014 年起，遊輪遊客成為推動增長的主要因素。 其人數從 2014 年的 100 萬上升至 2016 年的 150 萬，超過了住在島上的遊客，並在 2017 年達到 200 萬。 相比之下， 2013 年之後，住在島上的遊客人數大致維持在接近 150 萬的水平，只是在 2016 年略有下降。 因此，總到訪人數在 2015 年和 2016 年停留在約 275 萬，隨後急升至 350 萬。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"line graph","chinese":"折線圖"},{"english":"illustrates tourist numbers","chinese":"顯示遊客人數"},{"english":"tourist numbers","chinese":"遊客人數"},{"english":"a Caribbean island","chinese":"一個加勒比海島嶼"},{"english":"between 2010 and 2017","chinese":"在2010年至2017年間"},{"english":"separating visitors who stayed on cruise ships from","chinese":"將住在郵輪上的遊客與……分開"},{"english":"stayed on cruise ships","chinese":"住在郵輪上"},{"english":"accommodated on the island","chinese":"在島上住宿"},{"english":"total arrivals","chinese":"總到訪人數"},{"english":"rose substantially","chinese":"大幅上升"},{"english":"more than tripling","chinese":"增加至三倍以上"},{"english":"across the period","chinese":"在整段期間"},{"english":"island-based tourists","chinese":"住在島上的遊客"},{"english":"the larger group at first","chinese":"起初是較大組別"},{"english":"cruise passengers","chinese":"郵輪乘客"},{"english":"grew much faster","chinese":"增長快得多"},{"english":"had become the leading category","chinese":"已成為主要類別"},{"english":"leading category","chinese":"主要類別"},{"english":"by 2017","chinese":"到2017年時"},{"english":"attracted 1 million visitors","chinese":"吸引100萬名遊客"},{"english":"about three quarters of whom","chinese":"其中約四分之三"},{"english":"stayed on the island","chinese":"住在島上"},{"english":"this total rose steadily to","chinese":"這個總數穩步上升至"},{"english":"rose steadily to","chinese":"穩步上升至"},{"english":"when island-based tourists reached","chinese":"當時住在島上的遊客達到"},{"english":"reached 1.5 million","chinese":"達到150萬"},{"english":"over the same early period","chinese":"在同一早期時段"},{"english":"cruise-ship figure","chinese":"郵輪遊客數字"},{"english":"moved unevenly","chinese":"走勢不平均"},{"english":"increasing from…to…","chinese":"由……增加至……"},{"english":"before falling back to","chinese":"之後回落至"},{"english":"falling back to","chinese":"回落至"},{"english":"from 2014 onwards","chinese":"從2014年起"},{"english":"the main driver of growth","chinese":"增長的主要推動因素"},{"english":"driver of growth","chinese":"增長推動因素"},{"english":"their number climbed from…to…","chinese":"其數字由……上升至……"},{"english":"climbed from 1 million to 1.5 million","chinese":"由100萬上升至150萬"},{"english":"overtaking","chinese":"超越"},{"english":"the island-based group","chinese":"住在島上的組別"},{"english":"before reaching 2 million","chinese":"之後達到200萬"},{"english":"by contrast","chinese":"相比之下"},{"english":"tourists staying on the island","chinese":"住在島上的遊客"},{"english":"remained close to","chinese":"維持接近"},{"english":"after 2013","chinese":"2013年之後"},{"english":"except for","chinese":"除了……之外"},{"english":"a slight fall","chinese":"輕微下降"},{"english":"consequently","chinese":"因此"},{"english":"plateaued at around","chinese":"穩定在約……"},{"english":"around 2.75 million","chinese":"約275萬"},{"english":"in the final two years","chinese":"在最後兩年"},{"english":"then rose sharply to","chinese":"然後急升至"},{"english":"rose sharply to","chinese":"急升至"},{"english":"3.5 million","chinese":"350萬"},{"english":"visitor arrivals","chinese":"遊客到訪人數"},{"english":"cruise-ship visitors","chinese":"郵輪遊客"},{"english":"island accommodation","chinese":"島上住宿"},{"english":"long-term increase","chinese":"長期增長"},{"english":"overall growth","chinese":"整體增長"}]},"model-essay-6-ielts-task1-maps":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-6-ielts-task1-maps","essayKey":"maps:6","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-6-ielts-task1-maps","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-1/maps/maps-6","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"The two plans illustrate the layout of Grange Park when it opened in 1920 and its arrangement today.","chinese":"這兩張平面圖展示了格蘭奇公園在 1920 年首次開放時的布局，以及它今天的安排。"},{"label":"Overview","english":"Overall, the park has been substantially modernised, with recreational facilities such as an amphitheatre, café, children’s play area and underground parking added. However, the two main entrances on Arnold Avenue and Eldon Street have been retained, and rose gardens remain important, although they have been reduced and reorganised.","chinese":"整體而言，該公園已大幅現代化，新增了露天劇場、咖啡館、兒童遊樂區和地下停車場等休閒設施。 然而，位於阿諾德大道和埃爾登街的兩個主要入口被保留下來，而玫瑰園仍然是重要元素，儘管它們的數量已減少並被重新安排。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"In 1920, the park had a formal layout. A fountain stood at its centre, while a stage for musicians occupied the western side. Three rose gardens were located in the northwest, northeast and southwest corners, and seating was distributed around the edges. The eastern half contained a pond for water plants in the northeast and a glasshouse in the southeast.","chinese":"在 1920 年，該公園具有較正式的布局。 一座噴泉位於公園中央，而音樂家表演台則佔據西側位置。 三個玫瑰園分別位於西北角、東北角和西南角，座位則分布在公園邊緣一帶。 公園東半部包含位於東北方的水生植物池，以及位於東南方的玻璃溫室。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"Today, the central fountain has been replaced by a square rose garden, surrounded by seats on all four sides. The former musicians’ stage has given way to a larger amphitheatre for concerts. On the eastern side, the old pond and glasshouse have disappeared; in their place are a café, a children’s play area and a water feature. A new entrance to an underground car park has also been introduced from the southeast.","chinese":"如今，中央噴泉已被一個方形玫瑰園取代，而其四周均設有座位。 原本的音樂家表演台已被一個更大的露天音樂會劇場取代。 在東側，舊有的池塘和玻璃溫室已經消失；取而代之的是咖啡館、兒童遊樂區和水景設施。 此外，東南方也新增了一個通往地下停車場的入口。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"the plans below","chinese":"以下平面圖"},{"english":"a public park","chinese":"公園"},{"english":"when it first opened","chinese":"初次開放時"},{"english":"the same park today","chinese":"現今同一個公園"},{"english":"summarise the information","chinese":"概述資料"},{"english":"by selecting and reporting","chinese":"透過選取並報告……"},{"english":"the main features","chinese":"主要特徵"},{"english":"make comparisons where relevant","chinese":"在相關之處作出比較"},{"english":"illustrate the layout of","chinese":"展示……的佈局"},{"english":"Grange Park","chinese":"Grange Park 公園"},{"english":"its arrangement today","chinese":"其現今佈局"},{"english":"has been substantially modernised","chinese":"已大幅現代化"},{"english":"recreational facilities","chinese":"康樂設施"},{"english":"such as","chinese":"例如"},{"english":"an amphitheatre","chinese":"露天劇場"},{"english":"children's play area","chinese":"兒童遊樂區"},{"english":"underground parking","chinese":"地下停車場"},{"english":"have been retained","chinese":"得以保留"},{"english":"main entrances","chinese":"主要入口"},{"english":"rose gardens remain important","chinese":"玫瑰園仍然重要"},{"english":"have been reduced and reorganised","chinese":"已縮減並重新規劃"},{"english":"had a formal layout","chinese":"採用正式對稱的佈局"},{"english":"stood at its centre","chinese":"位於其中央"},{"english":"a fountain","chinese":"噴水池"},{"english":"a stage for musicians","chinese":"音樂家表演台"},{"english":"occupied the western side","chinese":"佔據西面"},{"english":"three rose gardens","chinese":"三個玫瑰園"},{"english":"were located in","chinese":"位於……"},{"english":"the north-west corner","chinese":"西北角"},{"english":"the north-east corner","chinese":"東北角"},{"english":"the south-west corner","chinese":"西南角"},{"english":"seating was distributed around","chinese":"座位分佈於……周圍"},{"english":"around the edges","chinese":"沿邊緣"},{"english":"the eastern half","chinese":"東半部"},{"english":"contained","chinese":"設有；包含"},{"english":"a pond for water plants","chinese":"水生植物池"},{"english":"water plants","chinese":"水生植物"},{"english":"a glasshouse","chinese":"溫室"},{"english":"the south-east","chinese":"東南面"},{"english":"the central fountain","chinese":"中央噴水池"},{"english":"has been replaced by","chinese":"已被……取代"},{"english":"a square rose garden","chinese":"正方形玫瑰園"},{"english":"surrounded by","chinese":"被……包圍"},{"english":"on all four sides","chinese":"在四邊"},{"english":"the former musicians' stage","chinese":"昔日的音樂家表演台"},{"english":"has given way to","chinese":"已讓位予……；被……取代"},{"english":"a larger amphitheatre","chinese":"較大型露天劇場"},{"english":"for concerts","chinese":"用作舉行音樂會"},{"english":"on the eastern side","chinese":"在東面"},{"english":"have disappeared","chinese":"已消失"},{"english":"in their place","chinese":"取而代之的是"},{"english":"a water feature","chinese":"水景設施"},{"english":"a new entrance to","chinese":"通往……的新入口"},{"english":"underground car park","chinese":"地下停車場"},{"english":"has also been introduced","chinese":"亦已增設"},{"english":"from the south-east","chinese":"從東南面"},{"english":"remain in place","chinese":"保持原位"},{"english":"be reorganised around","chinese":"圍繞……重新規劃"},{"english":"modern visitor facilities","chinese":"現代化遊客設施"},{"english":"leisure-oriented space","chinese":"以休閒為主的空間"},{"english":"formal garden features","chinese":"正式園林特色"},{"english":"be converted into","chinese":"被改造成"},{"english":"the overall structure","chinese":"整體結構"},{"english":"the original layout","chinese":"原本佈局"},{"english":"the present layout","chinese":"現時佈局"}]},"model-essay-6-ielts-task1-mixed-charts":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-6-ielts-task1-mixed-charts","essayKey":"mixed-charts:6","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-6-ielts-task1-mixed-charts","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-1/mixed-charts/mixed-charts-6","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"The table and pie charts compare attendance at Ashdown Museum and visitors’ satisfaction levels in the years before and after its refurbishment.","chinese":"該表格和圓餅圖比較了阿什當博物館翻新前後兩年中的參觀人數，以及訪客對參觀體驗的滿意程度。"},{"label":"Overview","english":"Overall, the museum became both more popular and more highly rated after the work was completed. The total number of visitors rose markedly, while positive responses replaced dissatisfaction as the dominant pattern.","chinese":"整體而言，翻新工程完成後，該博物館不但更受歡迎，也獲得了更高的評價。 總訪客人數明顯上升，而正面回應也取代不滿意，成為主要的滿意度模式。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"In terms of attendance, the museum received 74,000 visitors before the refurbishment, but this figure increased to 92,000 in the following year, a rise of 18,000. The improvement in satisfaction was even more striking. Before the changes, only 15% of respondents said they were very satisfied and a further 30% were satisfied, meaning that positive feedback accounted for less than half of all responses. After refurbishment, however, these two categories climbed to 35% and 40%, respectively, so three quarters of visitors expressed satisfaction.","chinese":"就參觀人數而言，該博物館在翻新前一年接待了 74,000 名訪客，但在翻新後一年，這一數字上升至 92,000 ，增加了 18,000 人。 滿意度方面的改善甚至更加明顯。 在翻新前，只有 15% 的受訪者表示非常滿意，另有 30% 表示滿意，這意味著正面回饋佔所有回應不到一半。 然而，翻新後，這兩個類別分別上升至 35% 和 40% ，因此有四分之三的訪客表達了滿意。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"By contrast, the proportion of dissatisfied visitors fell sharply. In the year before refurbishment, 40% reported being dissatisfied, making this the largest single group, while 10% were very dissatisfied. In the year after refurbishment, these figures dropped to 15% and 5%, respectively. The share giving no response remained unchanged at 5% in both years.","chinese":"相比之下，不滿意訪客的比例大幅下降。 在翻新前一年， 40% 的訪客表示不滿意，使其成為最大的單一組別，而另有10% 表示非常不滿意。 在翻新後一年，這兩項數字分別下降至 15% 和 5% 。 沒有回應的比例在兩年中都保持在 5% ，沒有變化。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"the table below","chinese":"以下表格"},{"english":"the number of visitors","chinese":"參觀人數"},{"english":"Ashdown Museum","chinese":"Ashdown博物館"},{"english":"during the year before","chinese":"在……前一年期間"},{"english":"during the year after","chinese":"在……後一年期間"},{"english":"was refurbished","chinese":"經過翻新"},{"english":"the results of surveys","chinese":"調查結果"},{"english":"asking visitors how satisfied they were","chinese":"詢問遊客滿意程度"},{"english":"how satisfied they were with","chinese":"對……有多滿意"},{"english":"during the same two periods","chinese":"在同樣兩個時期"},{"english":"summarise the information","chinese":"概述資料"},{"english":"by selecting and reporting","chinese":"透過選取並報告……"},{"english":"the main features","chinese":"主要特徵"},{"english":"make comparisons where relevant","chinese":"在相關之處作出比較"},{"english":"the table and pie charts","chinese":"表格及圓形圖"},{"english":"compare attendance at","chinese":"比較……的入場人數"},{"english":"visitors' satisfaction levels","chinese":"遊客滿意程度"},{"english":"in the years before and after","chinese":"在……前後兩年"},{"english":"its refurbishment","chinese":"其翻新工程"},{"english":"became both more popular and more highly rated","chinese":"變得更受歡迎且評價更高"},{"english":"more popular","chinese":"更受歡迎"},{"english":"more highly rated","chinese":"評價更高"},{"english":"after the work was completed","chinese":"工程完成後"},{"english":"the total number of visitors","chinese":"總參觀人數"},{"english":"rose markedly","chinese":"顯著上升"},{"english":"positive responses","chinese":"正面回應"},{"english":"replaced dissatisfaction as","chinese":"取代不滿成為……"},{"english":"dissatisfaction","chinese":"不滿"},{"english":"the dominant pattern","chinese":"主要模式"},{"english":"in terms of attendance","chinese":"就參觀人數而言"},{"english":"received 74,000 visitors","chinese":"接待了74,000名遊客"},{"english":"before the refurbishment","chinese":"翻新前"},{"english":"this figure increased to","chinese":"這個數字增加至"},{"english":"in the following year","chinese":"在隨後一年"},{"english":"a rise of 18,000","chinese":"增加18,000"},{"english":"the improvement in satisfaction","chinese":"滿意度的改善"},{"english":"even more striking","chinese":"更加明顯；更為突出"},{"english":"before the changes","chinese":"改動前"},{"english":"respondents","chinese":"受訪者"},{"english":"very satisfied","chinese":"非常滿意"},{"english":"a further 30%","chinese":"另外30%"},{"english":"were satisfied","chinese":"感到滿意"},{"english":"meaning that","chinese":"這意味著"},{"english":"positive feedback","chinese":"正面評價"},{"english":"accounted for","chinese":"佔……"},{"english":"less than half of","chinese":"少於一半"},{"english":"all responses","chinese":"所有回應"},{"english":"after refurbishment","chinese":"翻新後"},{"english":"these two categories","chinese":"這兩個類別"},{"english":"climbed to","chinese":"上升至"},{"english":"respectively","chinese":"分別"},{"english":"three quarters of","chinese":"四分之三"},{"english":"expressed satisfaction","chinese":"表示滿意"},{"english":"by contrast","chinese":"相比之下"},{"english":"the proportion of dissatisfied visitors","chinese":"不滿遊客的比例"},{"english":"fell sharply","chinese":"大幅下跌"},{"english":"reported being dissatisfied","chinese":"表示不滿"},{"english":"dissatisfied","chinese":"不滿意"},{"english":"the largest single group","chinese":"最大單一組別"},{"english":"very dissatisfied","chinese":"非常不滿意"},{"english":"in the year after refurbishment","chinese":"翻新後一年"},{"english":"these figures dropped to","chinese":"這些數字下降至"},{"english":"dropped to","chinese":"下降至"},{"english":"the share giving no response","chinese":"沒有回應者的比例"},{"english":"no response","chinese":"沒有回應"},{"english":"remained unchanged","chinese":"維持不變"},{"english":"at 5%","chinese":"為5%"},{"english":"in both years","chinese":"在兩年中"},{"english":"attendance figures","chinese":"入場人數數據"},{"english":"satisfaction survey results","chinese":"滿意度調查結果"},{"english":"visitor numbers","chinese":"遊客人數"},{"english":"an increase from X to Y","chinese":"由X增加至Y"},{"english":"a marked increase","chinese":"顯著增加"},{"english":"a sharp fall","chinese":"大幅下跌"},{"english":"negative responses","chinese":"負面回應"},{"english":"a clear shift from X to Y","chinese":"由X明顯轉向Y"},{"english":"from dissatisfaction to satisfaction","chinese":"由不滿轉為滿意"},{"english":"the most notable change","chinese":"最明顯的變化"},{"english":"the least changed category","chinese":"變化最少的類別"},{"english":"the combined share of","chinese":"……的合計比例"},{"english":"satisfied visitors","chinese":"滿意的遊客"},{"english":"dissatisfied visitors","chinese":"不滿的遊客"},{"english":"reached 75%","chinese":"達到75%"},{"english":"fell to 20%","chinese":"下降至20%"},{"english":"showed a major improvement","chinese":"顯示重大改善"},{"english":"became the clear majority","chinese":"成為明顯多數"},{"english":"the refurbishment appears to have","chinese":"翻新工程似乎已經……"},{"english":"improved both X and Y","chinese":"同時改善X和Y"}]},"model-essay-6-ielts-task1-pie-charts":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-6-ielts-task1-pie-charts","essayKey":"pie-charts:6","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-6-ielts-task1-pie-charts","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-1/pie-charts/pie-chart-6","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"The three pie charts compare how a UK school allocated its annual budget across five categories in 1981, 1991 and 2001.","chinese":"這三個圓餅圖比較了一所英國學校在 1981 年、 1991 年和 2001 年如何將年度預算分配到五個項目中。"},{"label":"Overview","english":"Overall, teachers’ salaries consistently took the largest share of spending, although this figure peaked in 1991 before declining slightly. Insurance remained the smallest item throughout, while spending on other workers fell steadily and the two material-related categories moved in opposite directions.","chinese":"整體而言，教師薪資一直佔學校開支中最大的比例，不過這一數字在 1991 年達到最高點後略有下降。 保險在整段期間一直是最小的支出項目，而其他員工薪資持續下降；同時，兩個與物資和設備相關的項目呈現相反走勢。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"In 1981, staff pay was the dominant expense, with teachers’ salaries at 40% and other workers’ pay at 28%. A decade later, teachers’ salaries rose to half of total expenditure, while spending on other employees fell to 22%, so staff costs together accounted for 72%. By 2001, the former had eased to 45% and the latter had dropped more sharply to 15%, reducing the combined salary share to 60%.","chinese":"在 1981 年，員工薪資是主要支出，其中教師薪資佔 40% ，其他員工薪資佔 28%。 十年後，教師薪資上升至總開支的一半，而其他員工薪資則下降至 22% ，因此兩項員工薪資合計佔 72% 。 到 2001 年，前者回落至 45% ，後者則更明顯地下降至 15% ，使整體薪資開支比例降至 60% 。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"The remaining items changed unevenly. Resources such as books increased from 15% in 1981 to 20% in 1991, before falling to 9% in 2001. In contrast, furniture and equipment followed the opposite path: it fell from 15% to 5%, then climbed to 23%, becoming the second-largest item in 2001. Insurance, although always the smallest category, rose steadily from 2% to 3% and finally to 8%.","chinese":"其餘項目的變化並不一致。 書本等資源開支由 1981 年的 15% 上升至 1991 年的 20% ，之後在 2001 年下降至 9%。 相反，家具和設備開支呈現相反走勢：它先由 15% 下降至 5% ，然後上升至 23%，並在 2001 年成為第二大支出項目。 保險雖然一直是最小的類別，但仍由 2% 持續上升至 3% ，最後達到 8% 。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"three pie charts","chinese":"三個圓形圖"},{"english":"allocated its annual budget","chinese":"分配其年度預算"},{"english":"annual budget","chinese":"年度預算"},{"english":"across five categories","chinese":"分配至五個類別"},{"english":"teachers' salaries","chinese":"教師薪金"},{"english":"consistently took the largest share","chinese":"一直佔最大比例"},{"english":"largest share of spending","chinese":"開支中最大比例"},{"english":"peaked in 1991","chinese":"在1991年達到最高點"},{"english":"before declining slightly","chinese":"之後輕微下降"},{"english":"declining slightly","chinese":"輕微下降"},{"english":"insurance","chinese":"保險"},{"english":"remained the smallest item throughout","chinese":"全期一直是最小項目"},{"english":"the smallest item","chinese":"最小項目"},{"english":"throughout","chinese":"在整段期間"},{"english":"spending on other workers","chinese":"其他員工開支"},{"english":"fell steadily","chinese":"穩步下降"},{"english":"material-related categories","chinese":"與物資相關的類別"},{"english":"moved in opposite directions","chinese":"走勢相反"},{"english":"staff pay","chinese":"員工薪酬"},{"english":"dominant expense","chinese":"主要開支"},{"english":"other workers' pay","chinese":"其他員工薪金"},{"english":"at 40%","chinese":"為40%"},{"english":"a decade later","chinese":"十年後"},{"english":"rose to half of","chinese":"上升至……的一半"},{"english":"half of total expenditure","chinese":"總開支的一半"},{"english":"total expenditure","chinese":"總開支"},{"english":"spending on other employees","chinese":"其他員工開支"},{"english":"fell to 22%","chinese":"下降至22%"},{"english":"staff costs together","chinese":"員工成本合共"},{"english":"accounted for 72%","chinese":"佔72%"},{"english":"by 2001","chinese":"到2001年時"},{"english":"the former","chinese":"前者"},{"english":"had eased to","chinese":"回落至"},{"english":"the latter","chinese":"後者"},{"english":"dropped more sharply to","chinese":"更大幅下降至"},{"english":"reducing the combined salary share","chinese":"令合計薪金比例下降"},{"english":"combined salary share","chinese":"合計薪金比例"},{"english":"the remaining items","chinese":"其餘項目"},{"english":"changed unevenly","chinese":"變化不平均"},{"english":"resources such as books","chinese":"書本等資源"},{"english":"increased from…to…","chinese":"由……增加至……"},{"english":"before falling to","chinese":"之後下降至"},{"english":"in contrast","chinese":"相比之下"},{"english":"furniture and equipment","chinese":"傢俬及設備"},{"english":"followed the opposite path","chinese":"走勢相反"},{"english":"fell from…to…","chinese":"由……下降至……"},{"english":"then climbed to","chinese":"然後上升至"},{"english":"becoming the second-largest item","chinese":"成為第二大項目"},{"english":"second-largest item","chinese":"第二大項目"},{"english":"although always the smallest category","chinese":"雖然一直是最小類別"},{"english":"rose steadily","chinese":"穩步上升"},{"english":"from 2% to 3% and finally to 8%","chinese":"由2%升至3%，最後升至8%"},{"english":"salary share","chinese":"薪金比例"},{"english":"school budget","chinese":"學校預算"},{"english":"spending category","chinese":"開支類別"}]},"model-essay-6-ielts-task1-process-diagram":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-6-ielts-task1-process-diagram","essayKey":"process-diagram:6","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-6-ielts-task1-process-diagram","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-1/process-diagrams/process-diagram-6","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"The diagram illustrates how a hydroelectric power station produces electricity by using water stored at different heights.","chinese":"該圖說明一座水力發電站如何利用儲存在不同高度的水來產生電力。"},{"label":"Overview","english":"Overall, the system works as a daily cycle: during the day, water flows downwards from an upper reservoir to generate electricity, while at night the same water is pumped back uphill for reuse. A dam and reversible turbines are the central features, and the electricity produced is sent to the national grid.","chinese":"整體而言，該系統以每日循環的方式運作：白天，水從上方水庫向下流動以產生電力；夜晚，同一批水會被抽回高處，以便再次使用。 水壩和可逆式渦輪機是該系統的核心部件，而產生的電力會被輸送到國家電網。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"In the daytime, river water is held in the high-level reservoir behind the dam. When the intake is opened, the stored water is released through a sloping pipe towards the power station. As it passes through the reversible turbines, these operate a generator, which converts the energy from the moving water into electricity. The power is then transmitted by power lines to the national grid, while the used water is discharged into the low-level reservoir.","chinese":"白天，河水被儲存在水壩後方的高位水庫中。 當進水口打開時，儲存的水會通過一條傾斜的管道流向發電站。 當水流經可逆式渦輪機時，渦輪機會帶動發電機，而發電機會把水流的能量轉化為電力。 隨後，電力會通過電力線輸送到國家電網，而使用過的水則被排入低位水。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"At night, the direction of movement is reversed. The intake at the dam is closed, and water from the lower reservoir is pumped back through the same turbine system and conduit to the upper reservoir. This restores the supply of water, allowing the process to begin again the following day.","chinese":"到了夜晚，水流方向會反過來。 水壩處的進水口會關閉，而低位水庫中的水會通過同一套渦輪系統和導管被抽回高位水庫。 這樣可以恢復高位水庫中的水量，使整個過程能夠在第二天再次開始。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"diagram illustrates","chinese":"圖示說明"},{"english":"hydroelectric power station","chinese":"水力發電站"},{"english":"produces electricity by using","chinese":"透過使用……來發電"},{"english":"water stored at different heights","chinese":"儲存在不同高度的水"},{"english":"different heights","chinese":"不同高度"},{"english":"the system works as","chinese":"這個系統以……方式運作"},{"english":"daily cycle","chinese":"每日循環"},{"english":"during the day","chinese":"在日間"},{"english":"flows downwards from","chinese":"從……向下流"},{"english":"upper reservoir","chinese":"上水庫"},{"english":"generate electricity","chinese":"發電"},{"english":"while at night","chinese":"而在夜間"},{"english":"pumped back uphill","chinese":"被泵回高處"},{"english":"for reuse","chinese":"供再次使用"},{"english":"dam","chinese":"水壩"},{"english":"reversible turbines","chinese":"可逆式渦輪機"},{"english":"central features","chinese":"主要特徵；核心部分"},{"english":"electricity produced","chinese":"所產生的電力"},{"english":"sent to the national grid","chinese":"被送往全國電網"},{"english":"national grid","chinese":"全國電網"},{"english":"in the daytime","chinese":"在日間"},{"english":"river water","chinese":"河水"},{"english":"held in the high-level reservoir","chinese":"被儲存在高位水庫"},{"english":"high-level reservoir","chinese":"高位水庫"},{"english":"behind the dam","chinese":"在水壩後方"},{"english":"when the intake is opened","chinese":"當進水口打開時"},{"english":"intake","chinese":"進水口"},{"english":"stored water","chinese":"儲存的水"},{"english":"released through","chinese":"經由……釋放"},{"english":"sloping pipe","chinese":"傾斜管道"},{"english":"towards the power station","chinese":"朝向發電站"},{"english":"as it passes through","chinese":"當它流經……時"},{"english":"passes through","chinese":"流經"},{"english":"operate a generator","chinese":"驅動發電機"},{"english":"generator","chinese":"發電機"},{"english":"converts the energy from…into…","chinese":"將來自……的能量轉化成……"},{"english":"moving water","chinese":"流動的水"},{"english":"power is then transmitted","chinese":"電力隨後被輸送"},{"english":"transmitted by power lines","chinese":"透過電纜輸送"},{"english":"power lines","chinese":"電纜；輸電線"},{"english":"used water","chinese":"使用後的水"},{"english":"discharged into","chinese":"被排入"},{"english":"low-level reservoir","chinese":"低位水庫"},{"english":"direction of movement","chinese":"移動方向"},{"english":"is reversed","chinese":"被反轉"},{"english":"intake at the dam","chinese":"水壩的進水口"},{"english":"is closed","chinese":"被關閉"},{"english":"lower reservoir","chinese":"下水庫"},{"english":"pumped back through","chinese":"被泵回並通過……"},{"english":"turbine system","chinese":"渦輪系統"},{"english":"conduit","chinese":"導管；水道"},{"english":"restores the supply of water","chinese":"恢復供水"},{"english":"supply of water","chinese":"供水量；水源"},{"english":"allowing the process to begin again","chinese":"使過程可以重新開始"},{"english":"begin again","chinese":"重新開始"},{"english":"the following day","chinese":"翌日；第二天"},{"english":"daytime operation","chinese":"日間運作"},{"english":"night-time operation","chinese":"夜間運作"},{"english":"pumped-storage system","chinese":"抽水蓄能系統"},{"english":"water flow","chinese":"水流"},{"english":"energy conversion","chinese":"能量轉換"}]},"model-essay-6-ielts-task1-tables":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-6-ielts-task1-tables","essayKey":"tables:6","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-6-ielts-task1-tables","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-1/tables/table-6","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"The table compares the percentages of first-year students in Economics, Law and Commerce who rated five aspects of their course as “very good”.","chinese":"該表格比較了經濟學、法律和商科三個課程中，一年級學生把其課程五個方面評為「非常好」的比例。"},{"label":"Overview","english":"Overall, Commerce received the strongest evaluations, leading or sharing first place in every aspect. Economics was rated highly for teaching and tutor support but much less favourably for pre-course information and resources, whereas Law showed a more balanced pattern, with teaching quality its weakest area.","chinese":"整體而言，商科獲得最強的評價，在每一個方面都位列第一或並列第一。 經濟學在教學質素和導師支援方面評價很高，但在課前資訊和資源方面明顯較不理想；相比之下，法律的表現較為均衡，而教學質素是其最弱的一項。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"In terms of teaching-related measures, Economics and Commerce both recorded 95% for teaching quality, far above Law at 67%. Tutor support followed a similar pattern: Commerce was marginally ahead at 93%, with Economics close behind at 92%, while Law was lower, though still fairly positive, at 79%. These figures made Economics and Commerce the clear leaders in these two areas.","chinese":"在教學相關指標方面，經濟學和商科的教學質素同樣錄得 95% ，遠高於法律的 67% 。 導師支援呈現相似模式：商科以 93% 略微領先，經濟學以 92% 緊隨其後，而法律則較低，儘管 79% 仍算相當正面。 這些數字使經濟學和商科在這兩個方面明顯領先。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"For the remaining aspects, Commerce again stood out. It achieved 95% for pre-course information, compared with 72% for Law and just 55% for Economics. The same hierarchy appeared for printed resources, at 81%, 70% and 59%, respectively. Other resources were also rated most highly in Commerce, at 85%, followed by Law at 80%, leaving Economics clearly behind at 62%.","chinese":"至於其餘方面，商科再次突出。 它在課前資訊方面達到 95% ，相比之下，法律為 72% ，經濟學只有 55% 。 印刷資源方面也出現相同排序，商科、法律和經濟學分別為 81% 、 70% 和 59%。 其他資源方面，商科亦獲最高評價，達 85% ；法律以 80% 居次，而經濟學則以62% 明顯落後。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"the results of a survey","chinese":"調查結果"},{"english":"first-year students","chinese":"一年級學生"},{"english":"taking various courses","chinese":"修讀不同課程"},{"english":"a particular university","chinese":"某一所大學"},{"english":"various aspects of their course","chinese":"課程的不同方面"},{"english":"considered X to be Y","chinese":"認為 X 是 Y"},{"english":"rated X as “very good”","chinese":"將 X 評為「非常好」"},{"english":"summarise the information","chinese":"概述資料"},{"english":"by selecting and reporting","chinese":"透過選取並報告……"},{"english":"the main features","chinese":"主要特徵"},{"english":"make comparisons where relevant","chinese":"在相關之處作出比較"},{"english":"the table compares","chinese":"表格比較"},{"english":"the percentages of","chinese":"……的百分比"},{"english":"Economics, Law and Commerce","chinese":"經濟學、法律及商科"},{"english":"five aspects of their course","chinese":"課程的五個方面"},{"english":"received the strongest evaluations","chinese":"獲得最高評價"},{"english":"the strongest evaluations","chinese":"最高評價"},{"english":"leading or sharing first place","chinese":"領先或並列第一"},{"english":"in every aspect","chinese":"在每一方面"},{"english":"rated highly for","chinese":"在……方面獲得高評價"},{"english":"teaching","chinese":"教學"},{"english":"tutor support","chinese":"導師支援"},{"english":"much less favourably","chinese":"評價低得多"},{"english":"pre-course information","chinese":"課程前資料"},{"english":"resources","chinese":"資源"},{"english":"whereas","chinese":"而；相反"},{"english":"showed a more balanced pattern","chinese":"呈現較平均的模式"},{"english":"teaching quality","chinese":"教學質素"},{"english":"its weakest area","chinese":"其最弱的一方面"},{"english":"in terms of","chinese":"就……而言"},{"english":"teaching-related measures","chinese":"與教學相關的指標"},{"english":"both recorded 95%","chinese":"兩者均錄得95%"},{"english":"far above","chinese":"遠高於"},{"english":"at 67%","chinese":"為67%"},{"english":"followed a similar pattern","chinese":"呈現相似模式"},{"english":"marginally ahead","chinese":"略為領先"},{"english":"close behind","chinese":"緊隨其後"},{"english":"while Law was lower","chinese":"而法律較低"},{"english":"though still fairly positive","chinese":"雖然仍算正面"},{"english":"fairly positive","chinese":"相當正面"},{"english":"the clear leaders","chinese":"明顯領先者"},{"english":"in these two areas","chinese":"在這兩個方面"},{"english":"the remaining aspects","chinese":"其餘方面"},{"english":"stood out","chinese":"表現突出"},{"english":"achieved 95% for","chinese":"在……取得95%"},{"english":"compared with","chinese":"與……相比"},{"english":"just 55%","chinese":"只有55%"},{"english":"the same hierarchy","chinese":"相同排名"},{"english":"printed resources","chinese":"印刷資料"},{"english":"respectively","chinese":"分別"},{"english":"other resources","chinese":"其他資源"},{"english":"rated most highly","chinese":"評價最高"},{"english":"followed by","chinese":"其次是"},{"english":"leaving Economics clearly behind","chinese":"令經濟學明顯落後"},{"english":"clearly behind","chinese":"明顯落後"},{"english":"course evaluation","chinese":"課程評價"},{"english":"student satisfaction","chinese":"學生滿意度"},{"english":"survey respondents","chinese":"調查受訪者"},{"english":"percentage of respondents","chinese":"受訪者百分比"},{"english":"give very good ratings","chinese":"給予「非常好」評價"},{"english":"score highly","chinese":"取得高分"},{"english":"score poorly","chinese":"得分較低"},{"english":"perform best overall","chinese":"整體表現最佳"},{"english":"perform weakest overall","chinese":"整體表現最弱"},{"english":"lead the table","chinese":"在表格中領先"},{"english":"share the top position","chinese":"並列第一"},{"english":"rank second","chinese":"排名第二"},{"english":"rank last","chinese":"排名最後"},{"english":"across the five categories","chinese":"在五個類別中"},{"english":"a consistent pattern","chinese":"一貫模式"},{"english":"a mixed picture","chinese":"好壞參半的情況"},{"english":"a clear contrast","chinese":"明顯對比"},{"english":"resource-related categories","chinese":"與資源相關的類別"},{"english":"teaching-related categories","chinese":"與教學相關的類別"},{"english":"the highest figure","chinese":"最高數字"},{"english":"the lowest figure","chinese":"最低數字"},{"english":"the largest gap","chinese":"最大差距"},{"english":"a gap of 40 percentage points","chinese":"40個百分點的差距"},{"english":"percentage-point gap","chinese":"百分點差距"},{"english":"considerably higher than","chinese":"明顯高於"},{"english":"slightly higher than","chinese":"略高於"},{"english":"broadly similar to","chinese":"與……大致相若"},{"english":"remain above","chinese":"維持在……以上"},{"english":"fall below","chinese":"低於……"},{"english":"above 90%","chinese":"超過90%"},{"english":"below 60%","chinese":"低於60%"},{"english":"the most favourable ratings","chinese":"最有利評價"},{"english":"the least favourable ratings","chinese":"最不理想評價"},{"english":"course aspects","chinese":"課程方面"},{"english":"quality of support","chinese":"支援質素"},{"english":"information provided before the course","chinese":"課程開始前提供的資料"},{"english":"availability of resources","chinese":"資源供應情況"},{"english":"relatively strong performance","chinese":"相對強勁表現"},{"english":"relatively weak performance","chinese":"相對較弱表現"},{"english":"the overall leader","chinese":"整體領先者"},{"english":"the lowest-ranked course","chinese":"排名最低的課程"},{"english":"strongest in teaching quality","chinese":"在教學質素方面最強"},{"english":"weakest in pre-course information","chinese":"在課程前資料方面最弱"}]},"model-essay-7-ielts-advantage-disadvantage":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-7-ielts-advantage-disadvantage","essayKey":"advantage-disadvantage:7","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-7-ielts-advantage-disadvantage","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/advantage-and-disadvantage/EdmundBd9AdDisAd-Q7","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"In many legal systems, judges are expected to decide punishments after considering both the crime itself and the circumstances surrounding it. Some people, however, argue that a system of fixed punishments would be more efficient. While this approach does offer certain practical benefits, I believe its disadvantages are considerably greater because it would undermine justice and could even worsen crime in the long term.","chinese":"無論在工作還是私人生活中，越來越多的溝通如今都是透過數位科技進行，而不是面對面交流。 儘管這種發展可能削弱人際關係的品質，並增加誤解的風險， 我認為整體而言，它的優點更大，因為它使溝通更有效率，並能讓人們即使相隔遙遠也保持聯繫。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"The main advantage of fixed sentencing is that it would make the legal process faster and more straightforward. If the penalty for each offence were predetermined, courts would spend less time debating the appropriate sentence, which would reduce delays and lower administrative costs. As a result, cases could be resolved more quickly, and victims would not have to wait as long for closure. Another benefit is greater consistency. When punishments are standardised, similar offences are more likely to receive similar penalties, which may strengthen public confidence in the justice system. For example, fixed fines and licence suspensions for traffic offences are often accepted because they are transparent and easy for the public to understand.","chinese":"科技化溝通最主要的優點是速度和便利性。 在專業環境中，電子郵件、即時通訊平台和視像會議免除了人們出行的需要，並使決策幾乎可以即時作出。 這不但縮短了回應時間、降低了營運成本，還使公司能夠非常輕鬆地協調分布在不同城市甚至不同大洲的團隊。 例如，一位經理可以透過一次線上會議便與海外同事解決生產問題，而不是等待數天才進行一次面對面的討論。 同樣的情況也適用於社交層面：住得很遠的父母、子女和朋友仍然可以透過通話和訊息每天聯絡。 結果是，人際關係更容易維持，也較不會隨時間而逐漸淡化。 例如，一個家庭即使成員分散在不同國家，仍然可以透過視像通話分享日常近況並提供情感支持。 因此，數位溝通大大提升了工作和個人生活中的效率與可及性。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"Nevertheless, the disadvantages of such a system are far more serious. Most importantly, fixed punishments ignore the fact that crimes differ enormously in motive, severity and context. A person who steals food out of desperation should not automatically receive the same sentence as a repeat offender who commits theft for profit. If the law fails to recognise such differences, justice becomes mechanical rather than fair. In addition, rigid sentencing can damage rehabilitation and ultimately make society less safe. When first-time or low-risk offenders are given the same punishment as hardened criminals, they may leave prison more alienated, less employable and more likely to reoffend. For instance, a teenager involved in a minor drug offence may be pushed further into criminal behaviour if treated identically to an experienced trafficker.","chinese":"然而，數位溝通也有重要的缺點，其中最嚴重的是它缺乏情感上的豐富性。 面對面的交談能傳達語氣、面部表情和肢體語言，這些都有助於人們準確理解意思、表達同理心並建立信任。 當這些線索消失時，訊息便更容易被誤解，從而導致困惑甚至衝突。 例如，一封簡短的電郵或文字訊息即使本無惡意，也可能顯得冷淡甚至帶有敵意。 這在職場中尤其成問題，因為信任和細膩的理解對領導、協商和團隊合作都至關重要。 長遠而言，過度依賴螢幕也可能助長膚淺的社交習慣，因此人們即使在線上一直保持聯絡，仍可能感到孤立。 例如，一個人即使經常透過社交媒體聊天，仍可能感到孤單，因為數位接觸始終無法完全取代真正的關注和人的陪伴。 因此，儘管科技讓溝通成為可能，它同時也可能削弱清晰度、信任感和情感深度。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, fixed punishments may improve efficiency and consistency, but these benefits are outweighed by their profound weaknesses. Because crime must be judged in relation to both the act and the offender, a flexible sentencing system is clearly the more just and effective approach.","chinese":"總結來說，透過科技進行溝通在效率和可及性方面具有明顯優勢，儘管它可能削弱人際互動的深度與清晰度。 整體而言，我認為其優點大於缺點，因為數位工具使工作和個人生活中的溝通都能跨越時間與距離而有效運作。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"legal systems","chinese":"法律制度"},{"english":"be expected to","chinese":"被期望要……"},{"english":"decide punishments","chinese":"決定刑罰"},{"english":"after considering both...and...","chinese":"在同時考慮……和……之後"},{"english":"the crime itself","chinese":"罪行本身"},{"english":"the circumstances surrounding it","chinese":"圍繞該事件的情況"},{"english":"a system of fixed punishments","chinese":"固定刑罰制度"},{"english":"more efficient","chinese":"更有效率"},{"english":"this approach","chinese":"這種做法"},{"english":"certain practical benefits","chinese":"某些實際好處"},{"english":"considerably greater","chinese":"大得多"},{"english":"undermine justice","chinese":"損害公義"},{"english":"worsen crime in the long term","chinese":"長遠而言令罪案惡化"},{"english":"fixed sentencing","chinese":"固定判刑"},{"english":"the legal process","chinese":"法律程序"},{"english":"faster and more straightforward","chinese":"更快捷和更簡單直接"},{"english":"the penalty for","chinese":"……的刑罰"},{"english":"each offence","chinese":"每項罪行"},{"english":"predetermined","chinese":"預先決定的"},{"english":"spend less time debating","chinese":"花較少時間爭論"},{"english":"the appropriate sentence","chinese":"合適刑期；合適判刑"},{"english":"reduce delays","chinese":"減少延誤"},{"english":"lower administrative costs","chinese":"降低行政成本"},{"english":"as a result","chinese":"因此；結果"},{"english":"be resolved more quickly","chinese":"更快得到解決"},{"english":"victims","chinese":"受害人"},{"english":"wait as long for closure","chinese":"等那麼久才得到了結"},{"english":"greater consistency","chinese":"更高一致性"},{"english":"be standardised","chinese":"被標準化"},{"english":"similar offences","chinese":"類似罪行"},{"english":"receive similar penalties","chinese":"得到類似刑罰"},{"english":"strengthen public confidence in","chinese":"增強公眾對……的信心"},{"english":"the justice system","chinese":"司法制度"},{"english":"fixed fines","chinese":"固定罰款"},{"english":"licence suspensions","chinese":"暫停駕駛執照"},{"english":"traffic offences","chinese":"交通違例"},{"english":"transparent and easy to understand","chinese":"透明而容易理解"},{"english":"such a system","chinese":"這樣的制度"},{"english":"far more serious","chinese":"嚴重得多"},{"english":"most importantly","chinese":"最重要的是"},{"english":"ignore the fact that","chinese":"忽視……這個事實"},{"english":"differ enormously in","chinese":"在……方面有極大差異"},{"english":"motive, severity and context","chinese":"動機、嚴重程度和背景"},{"english":"steals food out of desperation","chinese":"因絕望而偷食物"},{"english":"automatically receive","chinese":"自動得到"},{"english":"the same sentence as","chinese":"與……相同的判刑"},{"english":"a repeat offender","chinese":"重犯者"},{"english":"commits theft for profit","chinese":"為牟利而盜竊"},{"english":"fails to recognise","chinese":"未能承認"},{"english":"such differences","chinese":"這些差異"},{"english":"mechanical rather than fair","chinese":"機械化而非公平"},{"english":"rigid sentencing","chinese":"僵化判刑"},{"english":"damage rehabilitation","chinese":"損害更生"},{"english":"ultimately make society less safe","chinese":"最終令社會更不安全"},{"english":"first-time offenders","chinese":"初犯者"},{"english":"low-risk offenders","chinese":"低風險罪犯"},{"english":"hardened criminals","chinese":"慣犯；老練罪犯"},{"english":"leave prison more alienated","chinese":"離開監獄時更加疏離"},{"english":"less employable","chinese":"就業能力較低"},{"english":"more likely to reoffend","chinese":"更有可能再犯"},{"english":"a minor drug offence","chinese":"輕微毒品罪行"},{"english":"be pushed further into","chinese":"被進一步推向……"},{"english":"criminal behaviour","chinese":"犯罪行為"},{"english":"treated identically to","chinese":"被以完全相同方式對待"},{"english":"an experienced trafficker","chinese":"有經驗的販毒者"},{"english":"efficiency and consistency","chinese":"效率和一致性"},{"english":"be outweighed by","chinese":"被……超過；不及……重要"},{"english":"profound weaknesses","chinese":"深層弱點"},{"english":"be judged in relation to","chinese":"必須按……來判斷"},{"english":"the act and the offender","chinese":"行為和犯罪者"},{"english":"a flexible sentencing system","chinese":"靈活判刑制度"},{"english":"the more just and effective approach","chinese":"更公正和有效的做法"}]},"model-essay-7-ielts-cause-solution":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-7-ielts-cause-solution","essayKey":"cause-solution:7","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-7-ielts-cause-solution","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/problem-and-cause/EdmundBd9CnS-Q7","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"At university level, science courses remain unevenly populated, with male students greatly outnumbering female students. This imbalance is not mainly a question of ability. It is more often caused by social expectations that shape girls’ confidence and subject choices long before they apply to university. To balance the numbers, schools and universities need to change both the image of science and the support available to female students.","chinese":"在大學階段，科學課程中的學生比例仍然不均衡，男學生的人數遠遠多於女學生。 這種不平衡主要並不是能力問題。 它更多是由社會期望所造成，而這些期望早在女生申請大學之前，已經塑造了她們的自信和科目選擇。 為了平衡人數，學校和大學需要同時改變科學的形象，以及提供給女學生的支援。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"The main reason is that science is still widely presented, directly or indirectly, as a male domain. From childhood, boys are more often encouraged to build, experiment and solve technical problems, while girls may be guided towards subjects seen as more caring, verbal or socially suitable. As a result, many capable female students begin to doubt whether they belong in physics, engineering or computer science. This doubt can become self-fulfilling: if a girl rarely sees female scientists, teachers or classmates around her, science starts to look less like an open door and more like a room built for someone else.","chinese":"主要原因是，科學在很大程度上仍然被直接或間接地呈現為男性領域。 從童年開始，男孩往往更常被鼓勵去建造、實驗和解決技術問題，而女孩則可能被引導到一些被認為更具照顧性、更偏語言性，或更符合社會期待的科目。 結果是，許多有能力的女學生開始懷疑自己是否屬於物理、工程或電腦科學這些領域。 這種懷疑可能會變成自我實現的結果：如果一個女孩很少在身邊看見女性科學家、教師或同學，科學便開始不像一扇向她敞開的門，而更像是一個為別人而建的房間。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"One effective solution is to intervene earlier, before university choices are fixed. Schools should expose girls to practical science projects, female role models and career talks that show the real range of scientific work, from medical research to environmental technology. At the same time, teachers should actively challenge the quiet stereotypes that influence subject selection, so that girls are not simply allowed to study science but genuinely expected to succeed in it.","chinese":"一個有效的解決方法是在大學選擇確定之前，更早作出干預。 學校應該讓女生接觸實用的科學項目、女性榜樣，以及能展示科學工作真正範圍的職業講座，從醫學研究到環境科技都應包括在內。 同時，教師應該積極挑戰那些悄悄影響科目選擇的刻板印象，讓女生不只是被允許修讀科學，而是真正被期待能在科學中取得成功。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 3","english":"Universities can also help by making science courses feel less isolating. Mentoring schemes, scholarships, outreach programmes and visible female academic staff can reassure applicants that they will not be walking into hostile territory alone. Admission campaigns should also show science as collaborative, creative and socially valuable, rather than only technical and competitive.","chinese":"大學也可以透過讓科學課程感覺不那麼孤立來提供幫助。 導師計劃、獎學金、外展項目，以及可見的女性學術人員，都可以讓申請者放心，知道自己並不是獨自走進一片充滿敵意的領地。 招生宣傳也應該把科學呈現為合作性強、富有創意並具有社會價值的領域，而不只是技術性強和競爭激烈的領域。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, the gender gap in university science is largely rooted in early stereotypes and a lack of visible belonging. It can be narrowed through earlier encouragement, stronger role models and more supportive university environments.","chinese":"總結來說，大學科學領域中的性別差距，很大程度上源於早期形成的刻板印象，以及缺乏可見的歸屬感。 這種差距可以透過更早的鼓勵、更有力的榜樣，以及更具支援性的university環境來縮小"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"at university level","chinese":"在大學層面"},{"english":"science courses","chinese":"科學課程"},{"english":"remain unevenly populated","chinese":"人數分佈仍然不平均"},{"english":"male students greatly outnumbering female students","chinese":"男學生人數大大多於女學生"},{"english":"this imbalance","chinese":"這種不平衡"},{"english":"a question of ability","chinese":"能力問題"},{"english":"social expectations","chinese":"社會期望"},{"english":"shape girls' confidence","chinese":"塑造女生的信心"},{"english":"subject choices","chinese":"科目選擇"},{"english":"long before they apply to university","chinese":"早在她們申請大學之前"},{"english":"balance the numbers","chinese":"平衡人數"},{"english":"the image of science","chinese":"科學的形象"},{"english":"support available to","chinese":"可供……使用的支援"},{"english":"the main reason","chinese":"主要原因"},{"english":"widely presented","chinese":"被廣泛呈現"},{"english":"directly or indirectly","chinese":"直接或間接地"},{"english":"a male domain","chinese":"男性的領域"},{"english":"from childhood","chinese":"從童年開始"},{"english":"be encouraged to","chinese":"被鼓勵去"},{"english":"build, experiment and solve technical problems","chinese":"建造、實驗和解決技術問題"},{"english":"technical problems","chinese":"技術問題"},{"english":"be guided towards","chinese":"被引導去選擇"},{"english":"subjects seen as","chinese":"被視為……的科目"},{"english":"more caring, verbal or socially suitable","chinese":"較照顧性、語文性或社會上較合適的"},{"english":"as a result","chinese":"因此"},{"english":"capable female students","chinese":"有能力的女學生"},{"english":"begin to doubt whether","chinese":"開始懷疑是否"},{"english":"belong in","chinese":"屬於；適合留在"},{"english":"physics, engineering or computer science","chinese":"物理、工程或電腦科學"},{"english":"self-fulfilling","chinese":"自我實現的"},{"english":"rarely sees","chinese":"很少看見"},{"english":"female scientists","chinese":"女性科學家"},{"english":"starts to look less like","chinese":"開始看起來不像"},{"english":"an open door","chinese":"敞開的大門；開放的機會"},{"english":"a room built for someone else","chinese":"為別人而設的房間"},{"english":"one effective solution","chinese":"一個有效的解決方法"},{"english":"intervene earlier","chinese":"更早介入"},{"english":"university choices are fixed","chinese":"大學選擇已定下來"},{"english":"expose girls to","chinese":"讓女生接觸"},{"english":"practical science projects","chinese":"實用科學項目"},{"english":"female role models","chinese":"女性榜樣"},{"english":"career talks","chinese":"職業講座"},{"english":"the real range of","chinese":"……的真正範圍"},{"english":"scientific work","chinese":"科學工作"},{"english":"medical research","chinese":"醫學研究"},{"english":"environmental technology","chinese":"環境科技"},{"english":"at the same time","chinese":"與此同時"},{"english":"actively challenge","chinese":"積極挑戰"},{"english":"quiet stereotypes","chinese":"隱性的刻板印象"},{"english":"influence subject selection","chinese":"影響科目選擇"},{"english":"not simply allowed to","chinese":"不只是被容許去"},{"english":"genuinely expected to succeed","chinese":"真正被期望成功"},{"english":"making science courses feel less isolating","chinese":"令科學課程感覺較不孤立"},{"english":"mentoring schemes","chinese":"導師計劃"},{"english":"scholarships","chinese":"獎學金"},{"english":"outreach programmes","chinese":"外展計劃"},{"english":"visible female academic staff","chinese":"可見的女性學術人員"},{"english":"reassure applicants","chinese":"讓申請者安心"},{"english":"walking into hostile territory alone","chinese":"獨自走進充滿敵意的地方"},{"english":"admission campaigns","chinese":"招生活動"},{"english":"collaborative, creative and socially valuable","chinese":"需要合作、有創意並對社會有價值的"},{"english":"rather than only technical and competitive","chinese":"而不只是技術性和競爭性的"},{"english":"the gender gap","chinese":"性別差距"},{"english":"be largely rooted in","chinese":"主要根源於"},{"english":"early stereotypes","chinese":"早期形成的刻板印象"},{"english":"a lack of visible belonging","chinese":"缺乏可見的歸屬感"},{"english":"be narrowed through","chinese":"透過……收窄"},{"english":"earlier encouragement","chinese":"更早的鼓勵"},{"english":"stronger role models","chinese":"更有力的榜樣"},{"english":"supportive university environments","chinese":"支援性的大學環境"}]},"model-essay-7-ielts-direct-question":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-7-ielts-direct-question","essayKey":"direct-question:7","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-7-ielts-direct-question","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/direct-question/EdmundBd9Dir-Q7","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"Success at school and success in life do not always depend on the same abilities. While education is valuable, it measures only a limited range of skills. Some people therefore succeed after academic failure because life rewards broader strengths, and the most important of these is resilience.","chinese":"學校中的成功與人生中的成功並不總是取決於相同的能力。雖然教育很有價值，但它只衡量有限範圍的技能。 因此，有些人在學業失敗後仍然取得成功，是因為人生獎賞的是更廣泛的能力，而其中最重要的是韌性。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"One reason is that schools often reward discipline, memory, examination technique and the ability to follow a fixed system. These qualities are useful, but they are not the whole story. Outside the classroom, people may succeed because they are practical, socially intelligent, creative or willing to take calculated risks. A student who struggles with written exams, for example, may still have a sharp instinct for business, an ability to understand customers, or the courage to start again after failure. In this sense, poor school results are not always a final judgement on a person’s ability; they may simply show that one particular system did not suit them. Once such people find work that feels purposeful, they can develop the focus and confidence that they never showed in school.","chinese":"其中一個原因是，學校往往獎賞紀律、記憶力、考試技巧，以及遵從固定制度的能力。 這些素質是有用的，但它們並不是全部。 在課室之外，人們可能會成功，是因為他們務實、具備社交智慧、有創意，或者願意承擔經過計算的風險。 例如，一個在筆試中表現吃力的學生，仍然可能擁有敏銳的商業直覺、理解顧客的能力，或者在失敗後重新開始的勇氣。 從這個意義上說，糟糕的學校成績並不總是對一個人能力的最終判斷；它們可能只是顯示某一個特定制度並不適合他們。 一旦這些人找到讓他們感到有目標的工作，他們便能培養出在學校裡從未展現過的專注力和自信。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"The most important thing for success in life is resilience. Talent, education and luck all matter, but they are fragile advantages if a person gives up too easily. Life rarely moves in a straight line: people lose jobs, make poor decisions, face rejection and meet problems that no textbook has prepared them for. Resilience allows them to absorb these setbacks without being defined by them. More importantly, it turns failure into feedback. For instance, a young entrepreneur whose first idea collapses may learn how to manage money, listen to customers and build a stronger plan. Without resilience, that first failure becomes an ending; with resilience, it becomes a rough but useful apprenticeship.","chinese":"人生成功最重要的東西是韌性。 天賦、教育和運氣都很重要，但如果一個人太容易放棄，這些優勢都是脆弱的。 人生很少會沿著一條直線前進：人們會失去工作、作出錯誤決定、面對拒絕，並遇上沒有任何教科書曾經讓他們準備好的問題。 韌性使他們能夠承受這些挫折，而不被這些挫折所定義。 更重要的是，它把失敗轉化為回饋。 例如，一位年輕創業者的第一個想法失敗後，可能會學會如何管理金錢、聆聽顧客，以及建立一個更強的計劃。 沒有韌性，那第一次失敗便會成為終點；有了韌性，它便會成為一段艱難但有用的學徒期。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, some people succeed after failing at school because life rewards far more than academic performance. Resilience is the most essential quality because it helps people keep learning, adapting and moving forward when things go wrong.","chinese":"總結來說，有些人在學校失敗後仍然成功，是因為人生獎賞的遠遠不只是學業表現。 韌性是最重要的素質，因為它能幫助人們在事情出錯時繼續學習、適應，並向前走。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"success at school","chinese":"學業上的成功"},{"english":"success in life","chinese":"人生中的成功"},{"english":"depend on","chinese":"取決於"},{"english":"the same abilities","chinese":"相同的能力"},{"english":"education is valuable","chinese":"教育是有價值的"},{"english":"a limited range of skills","chinese":"有限範圍的技能"},{"english":"academic failure","chinese":"學業失敗"},{"english":"life rewards broader strengths","chinese":"人生會回報更廣泛的長處"},{"english":"broader strengths","chinese":"更廣泛的長處"},{"english":"the most important of these","chinese":"其中最重要的是"},{"english":"resilience","chinese":"抗逆力"},{"english":"reward discipline","chinese":"重視自律"},{"english":"examination technique","chinese":"考試技巧"},{"english":"follow a fixed system","chinese":"跟從固定制度"},{"english":"these qualities","chinese":"這些特質"},{"english":"not the whole story","chinese":"不是全部"},{"english":"outside the classroom","chinese":"在課室以外"},{"english":"socially intelligent","chinese":"有社交智慧"},{"english":"willing to take calculated risks","chinese":"願意承擔經過衡量的風險"},{"english":"calculated risks","chinese":"經過衡量的風險"},{"english":"struggles with written exams","chinese":"應付筆試有困難"},{"english":"a sharp instinct for business","chinese":"敏銳的商業直覺"},{"english":"understand customers","chinese":"了解顧客"},{"english":"the courage to start again","chinese":"重新開始的勇氣"},{"english":"after failure","chinese":"失敗之後"},{"english":"in this sense","chinese":"從這個意義上說"},{"english":"poor school results","chinese":"差的學業成績"},{"english":"a final judgement on","chinese":"對……的最終判斷"},{"english":"one particular system","chinese":"某一套特定制度"},{"english":"did not suit them","chinese":"不適合他們"},{"english":"find work that feels purposeful","chinese":"找到有意義的工作"},{"english":"feels purposeful","chinese":"感覺有意義"},{"english":"develop the focus and confidence","chinese":"培養專注力和信心"},{"english":"the most important thing for","chinese":"對……最重要的事情"},{"english":"fragile advantages","chinese":"脆弱的優勢"},{"english":"give up too easily","chinese":"太容易放棄"},{"english":"rarely moves in a straight line","chinese":"很少一帆風順"},{"english":"make poor decisions","chinese":"作出錯誤決定"},{"english":"face rejection","chinese":"面對拒絕"},{"english":"no textbook has prepared them for","chinese":"沒有課本能讓他們預先準備"},{"english":"absorb these setbacks","chinese":"承受這些挫折"},{"english":"be defined by","chinese":"被……界定"},{"english":"turn failure into feedback","chinese":"將失敗變成回饋"},{"english":"a young entrepreneur","chinese":"年輕創業者"},{"english":"first idea collapses","chinese":"第一個想法失敗"},{"english":"manage money","chinese":"管理金錢"},{"english":"listen to customers","chinese":"聆聽顧客意見"},{"english":"build a stronger plan","chinese":"制定更完善的計劃"},{"english":"becomes an ending","chinese":"變成終點"},{"english":"a rough but useful apprenticeship","chinese":"艱辛但有用的學習過程"},{"english":"far more than academic performance","chinese":"遠不止學業表現"},{"english":"academic performance","chinese":"學業表現"},{"english":"the most essential quality","chinese":"最必要的特質"},{"english":"keep learning, adapting and moving forward","chinese":"繼續學習、適應和向前走"},{"english":"when things go wrong","chinese":"當事情出錯時"}]},"model-essay-7-ielts-discuss-both-views":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-7-ielts-discuss-both-views","essayKey":"discuss-both-views:7","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-7-ielts-discuss-both-views","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/discuss-both-views-your-opinion/EdmundBd9ExpBth-Q7","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"How citizens use their income has a major influence on a country’s economy. While some argue that consumer spending keeps businesses alive and creates employment, others believe that saving is more beneficial because it strengthens financial stability and supports long-term investment. In my view, although spending is useful in the short term, a culture of saving is ultimately better for the economy.","chinese":"公民如何使用自己的收入，對一個國家的經濟有重大影響。 雖然有些人認為，消費支出能讓企業維持運作並創造就業，但另一些人則認為，儲蓄更有利，因為它能加強財務穩定並支持長期投資。 在我看來，雖然消費在短期內是有用的，但儲蓄文化最終對經濟更好。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"Those who support spending have a reasonable argument. When people buy goods and services, money circulates rather than sitting idle. Restaurants, shops, transport companies and online businesses all depend on customers who are ready to pay for what they want or need. If consumers suddenly stopped spending, many firms would lose revenue, reduce production, or lay off staff. For example, a family that regularly eats out, buys clothes and travels is not only satisfying its own needs; it is also helping waiters, shop assistants and drivers earn a living. In this sense, spending acts as the bloodstream of an economy because it keeps trade moving and confidence alive.","chinese":"支持消費的人有其合理的論點。 當人們購買商品和服務時，金錢會流通，而不是閒置不動。 餐廳、商店、運輸公司和網上企業都依賴那些願意為自己想要或需要的東西付款的顧客。 如果消費者突然停止消費，許多公司便會失去收入、減少生產，或裁減員工。 例如，一個經常外出用餐、購買衣服和旅遊的家庭，不只是滿足自己的需要；它同時也在幫助侍應、店員和司機維持生計。 從這個意義上說，消費就像經濟的血液，因為它讓貿易保持流動，也讓信心保持活力。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"However, I believe saving offers a deeper and more sustainable economic benefit. People who save are less vulnerable to sudden unemployment, illness or price rises, so they are less likely to depend heavily on government support during difficult periods. More importantly, savings can become investment. Banks can lend deposited money to businesses, families can fund education, and individuals can start small enterprises without falling into dangerous debt. A society that spends every dollar may look prosperous on the surface, but it can become fragile, like a house built on sand. By contrast, widespread saving creates a financial cushion and provides the capital needed for future growth. This makes the economy more resilient, not merely more active.","chinese":"然而，我認為儲蓄能帶來更深層、更可持續的經濟好處。 有儲蓄的人較不容易受到突然失業、疾病或物價上升的嚴重影響，因此在困難時期，他們也較不可能嚴重依賴政府支援。 更重要的是，儲蓄可以轉化為投資。 銀行可以把存款借給企業，家庭可以資助教育，而個人也可以在不陷入危險債務的情況下創辦小型企業。 一個把每一元都花掉的社會，表面上可能看似繁榮，但它可能變得脆弱，就像建在沙上的房子一樣。 相比之下，廣泛的儲蓄能創造財務緩衝，並提供未來增長所需的資本。 這會使經濟更有韌性，而不只是更活躍。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, consumer spending is important because it supports demand, jobs and business income. Nevertheless, I firmly believe that saving is more valuable for a nation’s economy, as it promotes stability, reduces financial risk and lays a stronger foundation for long-term development.","chinese":"總結來說，消費支出是重要的，因為它支持需求、就業和企業收入。 然而，我堅定認為，儲蓄對一個國家的經濟更有價值，因為它能促進穩定、降低財務風險，並為長期發展奠定更強大的基礎。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"use their income","chinese":"運用收入"},{"english":"has a major influence on","chinese":"對……有重大影響"},{"english":"a country's economy","chinese":"一個國家的經濟"},{"english":"consumer spending","chinese":"消費開支"},{"english":"keeps businesses alive","chinese":"令企業得以生存"},{"english":"creates employment","chinese":"創造就業"},{"english":"more beneficial","chinese":"更有益"},{"english":"strengthens financial stability","chinese":"加強財務穩定"},{"english":"supports long-term investment","chinese":"支持長遠投資"},{"english":"in the short term","chinese":"短期內"},{"english":"a culture of saving","chinese":"儲蓄文化"},{"english":"ultimately better for","chinese":"最終對……更好"},{"english":"support spending","chinese":"支持消費"},{"english":"a reasonable argument","chinese":"合理的論點"},{"english":"buy goods and services","chinese":"購買商品和服務"},{"english":"money circulates","chinese":"金錢流通"},{"english":"rather than sitting idle","chinese":"而不是閒置"},{"english":"depend on customers","chinese":"依賴顧客"},{"english":"ready to pay for","chinese":"願意為……付款"},{"english":"stopped spending","chinese":"停止消費"},{"english":"lose revenue","chinese":"失去收入"},{"english":"reduce production","chinese":"減少生產"},{"english":"lay off staff","chinese":"裁員"},{"english":"regularly eats out","chinese":"經常外出用餐"},{"english":"satisfying its own needs","chinese":"滿足自己的需要"},{"english":"earn a living","chinese":"謀生"},{"english":"In this sense","chinese":"從這個意義上說"},{"english":"acts as the bloodstream of","chinese":"像……的血液一樣發揮作用"},{"english":"keeps trade moving","chinese":"令貿易持續運作"},{"english":"keeps confidence alive","chinese":"維持信心"},{"english":"offers a deeper and more sustainable benefit","chinese":"提供更深層、更可持續的好處"},{"english":"economic benefit","chinese":"經濟好處"},{"english":"less vulnerable to","chinese":"較不容易受……影響"},{"english":"sudden unemployment","chinese":"突然失業"},{"english":"price rises","chinese":"物價上升"},{"english":"less likely to","chinese":"較不可能"},{"english":"depend heavily on","chinese":"嚴重依賴"},{"english":"government support","chinese":"政府支援"},{"english":"during difficult periods","chinese":"在困難時期"},{"english":"become investment","chinese":"變成投資"},{"english":"lend deposited money to","chinese":"把存款借給"},{"english":"deposited money","chinese":"存款"},{"english":"fund education","chinese":"資助教育"},{"english":"start small enterprises","chinese":"創辦小型企業"},{"english":"fall into dangerous debt","chinese":"陷入危險債務"},{"english":"spends every dollar","chinese":"花光每一元"},{"english":"look prosperous on the surface","chinese":"表面上看起來繁榮"},{"english":"become fragile","chinese":"變得脆弱"},{"english":"built on sand","chinese":"建在沙上的"},{"english":"By contrast","chinese":"相比之下"},{"english":"widespread saving","chinese":"普遍儲蓄"},{"english":"creates a financial cushion","chinese":"建立財務緩衝"},{"english":"provides the capital needed for","chinese":"提供……所需的資本"},{"english":"future growth","chinese":"未來增長"},{"english":"more resilient","chinese":"更有韌性"},{"english":"not merely more active","chinese":"不只是更活躍"},{"english":"supports demand","chinese":"支持需求"},{"english":"business income","chinese":"企業收入"},{"english":"Nevertheless","chinese":"然而"},{"english":"more valuable for","chinese":"對……更有價值"},{"english":"a nation's economy","chinese":"國家經濟"},{"english":"promotes stability","chinese":"促進穩定"},{"english":"reduces financial risk","chinese":"降低財務風險"},{"english":"lays a stronger foundation for","chinese":"為……奠定更穩固基礎"},{"english":"long-term development","chinese":"長遠發展"}]},"model-essay-7-ielts-opinion":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-7-ielts-opinion","essayKey":"opinion:7","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-7-ielts-opinion","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/opinions/EdmundBd9OP-Q7","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"Modern businesses derive substantial benefits from the communities in which they operate, so it is reasonable to expect something in return. I completely agree that companies should provide sports and social facilities for local residents, because these amenities improve public well-being and because profitable firms have a clear responsibility to reinvest locally.","chinese":"現代企業從營運所在的社區中獲得了大量利益，因此合理地可以期待它們作出某種回饋 我完全同意。 企業應該為當地居民提供體育及社交設施，因為這些設施能提升公眾福祉，而獲利企業也明確有責任把資源重新投放到本地社區。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"The first reason is that such facilities generate direct social gains. When a company funds a sports ground, gym or community hall, residents gain affordable access to exercise and organised interaction. This can improve physical health, since people who have safe and convenient places to be active are more likely to form regular habits rather than drift into sedentary lifestyles. The effects are psychological as well. Team sports, clubs and neighbourhood events reduce isolation, especially among teenagers and older people, which in turn can strengthen confidence, lower stress and create a stronger sense of belonging. For example, if a factory sponsors an evening football league and opens a social centre at weekends, it gives young people structure and helps families mix more regularly.","chinese":"第一個原因是，這類設施能帶來直接的社會效益。 當企業資助興建運動場、健身房或社區會堂時，居民便能以可負擔的方式接觸運動與有組織的社交活動。 這能改善身體健康，因為當人們擁有安全而方便的活動空間時，他們更有可能養成規律習慣，而不是逐漸陷入久坐不動的生活方式。 這種影響也同樣體現在心理層面上。 團隊運動、興趣社團與社區活動能減少孤立感，尤其對青少年和長者而言更是如此，而這進一步能增強自信、減低壓力，並建立更強的歸屬感。 例如，如果一間工廠資助夜間足球聯賽，並在週末開放社交中心，這就能為年輕人提供有規律的活動，也能幫助家庭之間更經常地互動交流。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"There is also a strong moral and practical case for expecting companies to make this contribution. Large firms profit from local labour, use public infrastructure and sometimes place pressure on the surrounding environment. In return, they should help raise the quality of life in the same area. More importantly, this is not merely charitable, because businesses benefit when communities are healthier and more cohesive. Areas with better facilities are likely to experience less social tension, stronger goodwill towards employers and a more stable workforce. For instance, a company that builds a shared sports complex near its offices may find it easier to recruit staff, maintain a positive public image and secure long-term public support for its operations.","chinese":"此外，從道德和實際層面來看，要求企業作出這種貢獻也同樣有充分理由。 大型企業從本地勞動力中獲利，使用公共基礎建設，並且有時也會對周邊環境造成壓力。 因此，作為回報，它們應該幫助提升同一地區居民的生活質素。 更重要的是，這不僅僅是慈善行為，因為當社區更健康、更有凝聚力時，企業本身也會受益。 擁有更完善設施的地區，往往較少出現社會緊張關係，居民對僱主也會有更強的善意，而勞動力也會更穩定。 例如，一間在辦公地點附近興建共享體育設施的公司，可能會發現自己更容易招聘員工、維持正面的公眾形象，並獲得社會對其長期營運的支持。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, I completely agree that companies should provide sports and social facilities for local communities. Such investment improves health, strengthens social cohesion and represents a fair return to the communities that help businesses prosper.","chinese":"總而言之，我完全同意企業應該為本地社區提供體育和社交設施。 這類投資能改善健康、加強社會凝聚力，並且是企業對那些幫助其繁榮發展的社區所作出的公平回饋。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"derive substantial benefits from","chinese":"從……獲得重大好處"},{"english":"the communities in which they operate","chinese":"它們營運所在的社區"},{"english":"it is reasonable to expect","chinese":"期望……是合理的"},{"english":"something in return","chinese":"回報；作為回饋"},{"english":"provide sports and social facilities","chinese":"提供運動及社交設施"},{"english":"local residents","chinese":"本地居民"},{"english":"these amenities","chinese":"這些設施"},{"english":"improve public well-being","chinese":"改善公眾福祉"},{"english":"profitable firms","chinese":"有盈利的公司"},{"english":"have a clear responsibility to","chinese":"明確有責任去"},{"english":"reinvest locally","chinese":"在本地再投資"},{"english":"such facilities","chinese":"這類設施"},{"english":"generate direct social gains","chinese":"帶來直接社會效益"},{"english":"fund a sports ground","chinese":"資助運動場"},{"english":"community hall","chinese":"社區會堂"},{"english":"gain affordable access to","chinese":"以可負擔價錢使用"},{"english":"organised interaction","chinese":"有組織的互動"},{"english":"improve physical health","chinese":"改善身體健康"},{"english":"safe and convenient places","chinese":"安全方便的地方"},{"english":"be active","chinese":"活動身體；保持活躍"},{"english":"form regular habits","chinese":"養成規律習慣"},{"english":"rather than drift into","chinese":"而不是漸漸陷入"},{"english":"sedentary lifestyles","chinese":"久坐少動的生活方式"},{"english":"the effects are psychological as well","chinese":"影響亦包括心理層面"},{"english":"team sports","chinese":"團隊運動"},{"english":"neighbourhood events","chinese":"社區活動"},{"english":"reduce isolation","chinese":"減少孤立感"},{"english":"especially among","chinese":"尤其在……之中"},{"english":"which in turn","chinese":"這反過來"},{"english":"strengthen confidence","chinese":"增強信心"},{"english":"lower stress","chinese":"減低壓力"},{"english":"create a stronger sense of belonging","chinese":"建立更強的歸屬感"},{"english":"sponsor an evening football league","chinese":"贊助夜間足球聯賽"},{"english":"open a social centre","chinese":"開放社交中心"},{"english":"at weekends","chinese":"在週末"},{"english":"give young people structure","chinese":"令年輕人生活更有規律"},{"english":"help families mix more regularly","chinese":"幫助家庭更經常交流"},{"english":"a strong moral and practical case for","chinese":"有強烈的道德及實際理由支持"},{"english":"make this contribution","chinese":"作出這份貢獻"},{"english":"profit from local labour","chinese":"從本地勞動力獲利"},{"english":"use public infrastructure","chinese":"使用公共基建"},{"english":"place pressure on","chinese":"對……造成壓力"},{"english":"the surrounding environment","chinese":"周邊環境"},{"english":"in return","chinese":"作為回報"},{"english":"raise the quality of life","chinese":"提高生活質素"},{"english":"in the same area","chinese":"在同一地區"},{"english":"not merely charitable","chinese":"不只是慈善"},{"english":"benefit when","chinese":"在……時受惠"},{"english":"healthier and more cohesive","chinese":"更健康、更有凝聚力"},{"english":"better facilities","chinese":"更好的設施"},{"english":"be likely to experience","chinese":"有可能經歷"},{"english":"less social tension","chinese":"較少社會緊張"},{"english":"stronger goodwill towards","chinese":"對……有更強善意"},{"english":"employers","chinese":"僱主"},{"english":"a more stable workforce","chinese":"更穩定的勞動力"},{"english":"build a shared sports complex","chinese":"興建共用運動綜合設施"},{"english":"near its offices","chinese":"在辦公室附近"},{"english":"find it easier to","chinese":"發現更容易"},{"english":"recruit staff","chinese":"招聘員工"},{"english":"maintain a positive public image","chinese":"維持正面的公眾形象"},{"english":"secure long-term public support","chinese":"獲得長期公眾支持"},{"english":"its operations","chinese":"其營運"},{"english":"local communities","chinese":"本地社區"},{"english":"such investment","chinese":"這類投資"},{"english":"strengthen social cohesion","chinese":"加強社會凝聚力"},{"english":"represent a fair return to","chinese":"代表對……的合理回報"},{"english":"help businesses prosper","chinese":"幫助企業興旺發展"}]},"model-essay-7-ielts-task1-bar-charts":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-7-ielts-task1-bar-charts","essayKey":"bar-charts:7","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-7-ielts-task1-bar-charts","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-1/bar-charts/bar-chart-7","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"The two bar charts compare the destinations of UK graduates and postgraduates who left college in 2008 but did not enter full-time employment.","chinese":"這兩張柱狀圖比較了 2008 年英國大學畢業生和研究生離開學院後，在沒有進入全職工作的情況下所選擇的去向。"},{"label":"Overview","english":"Overall, further study was the most common route for both groups, whereas voluntary work attracted the fewest students. Although the graduate figures were much higher in every category, the overall pattern was broadly similar.","chinese":"整體而言，繼續深造是兩組學生最常見的去向，而從事志願工作的人數最少。 雖然大學畢業生在每一個類別中人數都遠高於研究生，但整體模式大致相似。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"Among graduates, almost 30,000 continued their education, making further study the clear leading destination. Part-time work came next, at 17,735, only slightly ahead of unemployment, which stood at 16,235. By contrast, just 3,500 graduates chose voluntary work, less than a quarter of the number without a job and far below the total in further study.","chinese":"在大學畢業生中，接近 30,000 人繼續學業，使繼續深造成為明顯最多人選擇的去向。 兼職工作位居第二，有 17,735 人，只比失業人數 16,235 略高。 相比之下，只有 3,500 名畢業生選擇志願工作，這還不到失業人數的四分之一，也遠低於繼續深造的人數。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"The same order was evident among postgraduates, though the numbers were smaller. Further study again ranked first, with 2,725 students, but it was only narrowly higher than part-time work, at 2,535. Unemployment involved 1,625 postgraduates, while voluntary work remained the least common option, at 345. Across all four destinations, graduates outnumbered postgraduates substantially, especially in further study, where the difference exceeded 26,000.","chinese":"研究生中也呈現相同的排序，不過人數較少。 繼續深造再次排名第一，有 2,725 人，但它只略高於兼職工作的 2,535 人。 失業的研究生人數為 1,625 ，而志願工作仍然是最不常見的選項，只有 345 人。 在四個去向中，大學畢業生的人數都明顯多於研究生，尤其是在繼續深造方面，兩者差距超過 26,000 人。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"two bar charts","chinese":"兩個棒形圖"},{"english":"compare the destinations of","chinese":"比較……的去向"},{"english":"UK graduates and postgraduates","chinese":"英國大學畢業生及研究院畢業生"},{"english":"left college","chinese":"離開大學；畢業"},{"english":"enter full-time employment","chinese":"進入全職就業"},{"english":"full-time employment","chinese":"全職就業"},{"english":"further study","chinese":"繼續升學"},{"english":"the most common route","chinese":"最常見的去向"},{"english":"for both groups","chinese":"對兩個組別而言"},{"english":"whereas","chinese":"而；相比之下"},{"english":"voluntary work","chinese":"義務工作"},{"english":"attracted the fewest students","chinese":"吸引最少學生"},{"english":"graduate figures","chinese":"大學畢業生的數字"},{"english":"much higher in every category","chinese":"在每個類別都高得多"},{"english":"overall pattern","chinese":"整體模式"},{"english":"broadly similar","chinese":"大致相似"},{"english":"among graduates","chinese":"在大學畢業生當中"},{"english":"almost 30,000","chinese":"接近30,000人"},{"english":"continued their education","chinese":"繼續接受教育；繼續升學"},{"english":"making further study the clear leading destination","chinese":"使繼續升學成為明顯最主要去向"},{"english":"the clear leading destination","chinese":"明顯最主要的去向"},{"english":"part-time work","chinese":"兼職工作"},{"english":"came next","chinese":"位居其次"},{"english":"at 17,735","chinese":"數字為17,735"},{"english":"only slightly ahead of","chinese":"只略高於……"},{"english":"unemployment","chinese":"失業"},{"english":"stood at","chinese":"處於；數字為"},{"english":"by contrast","chinese":"相比之下"},{"english":"chose voluntary work","chinese":"選擇義務工作"},{"english":"less than a quarter of","chinese":"少於……的四分之一"},{"english":"the number without a job","chinese":"沒有工作的人的數目"},{"english":"far below","chinese":"遠低於"},{"english":"the total in further study","chinese":"繼續升學的總數"},{"english":"the same order was evident","chinese":"呈現相同排序"},{"english":"among postgraduates","chinese":"在研究院畢業生當中"},{"english":"though the numbers were smaller","chinese":"雖然數字較小"},{"english":"ranked first","chinese":"排名第一"},{"english":"with 2,725 students","chinese":"有2,725名學生"},{"english":"narrowly higher than","chinese":"僅略高於"},{"english":"involved 1,625 postgraduates","chinese":"涉及1,625名研究院畢業生"},{"english":"remained the least common option","chinese":"仍然是最少見的選項"},{"english":"the least common option","chinese":"最少見的選項"},{"english":"across all four destinations","chinese":"在全部四個去向中"},{"english":"outnumbered postgraduates substantially","chinese":"數量大幅多於研究院畢業生"},{"english":"substantially","chinese":"大幅地；顯著地"},{"english":"especially in further study","chinese":"尤其是在繼續升學方面"},{"english":"the difference exceeded","chinese":"差距超過"},{"english":"exceeded 26,000","chinese":"超過26,000"},{"english":"destinations","chinese":"去向"},{"english":"category","chinese":"類別"},{"english":"route","chinese":"路徑；去向"}]},"model-essay-7-ielts-task1-line-graph":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-7-ielts-task1-line-graph","essayKey":"line-graph:7","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-7-ielts-task1-line-graph","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-1/line-graphs/line-graph-7","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"The line graph compares average carbon dioxide emissions per person in the United Kingdom, Sweden, Italy and Portugal from 1967 to 2007, measured in metric tonnes.","chinese":"該折線圖比較了 1967 年至 2007 年間英國、瑞典、義大利和葡萄牙的人均二氧化碳排放量，單位為公噸。"},{"label":"Overview","english":"Overall, the United Kingdom remained the highest emitter throughout, although its figure declined gradually. Sweden also ended lower than it began after reaching a peak in the late 1970s, whereas Italy and Portugal recorded steady growth, with Italy ranking second by 2007.","chinese":"整體而言，英國在整段期間一直是人均排放量最高的國家，儘管其數字逐漸下降。 瑞典在 1970 年代末達到高峰後，最終排放量低於起點；相反，義大利和葡萄牙均穩定上升，其中義大利到 2007 年排名第二。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"In 1967, the UK produced just under 11 tonnes per person, compared with about 8.7 tonnes in Sweden. Sweden then rose to just over 10 tonnes in 1977, almost matching the UK, before falling markedly to around 7 tonnes in 1987 and then to approximately 5.5 tonnes by the final year. The UK followed a gentler downward path, slipping from nearly 11 tonnes to about 8.7 tonnes over the same period.","chinese":"1967 年，英國人均二氧化碳排放量略低於 11 公噸，而瑞典約為 8.7 公噸。 瑞典隨後在 1977 年升至略高於 10 公噸，幾乎追平英國，之後在 1987 年大幅下降至約 7 公噸，並在最後一年降至約 5.5 公噸。 英國則呈現較溫和的下降趨勢，在同一期間由接近 11 公噸降至約 8.7 公噸。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"By contrast, Italy climbed from roughly 4.2 tonnes in 1967 to about 6.3 tonnes in 1977, and then increased further to around 7.7 tonnes in 1997, where it levelled off. Portugal, initially the lowest at just over 1 tonne, rose steadily to about 5.5 tonnes in 2007, almost converging with Sweden.","chinese":"相比之下，義大利的人均排放量從 1967 年的約 4.2 公噸上升至 1977 年的約 6.3 公噸，之後進一步升至 1997 年的約 7.7 公噸，並在此後趨於平穩。 葡萄牙起初最低，略高於 1 公噸，但到 2007 年穩定上升至約 5.5 公噸，幾乎與瑞典匯合。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"The line graph compares","chinese":"折線圖比較"},{"english":"average carbon dioxide emissions","chinese":"平均二氧化碳排放量"},{"english":"carbon dioxide emissions","chinese":"二氧化碳排放量"},{"english":"per person","chinese":"每人"},{"english":"the United Kingdom","chinese":"英國"},{"english":"Sweden","chinese":"瑞典"},{"english":"Italy","chinese":"意大利"},{"english":"Portugal","chinese":"葡萄牙"},{"english":"from 1967 to 2007","chinese":"從1967年至2007年"},{"english":"measured in metric tonnes","chinese":"以公噸計"},{"english":"metric tonnes","chinese":"公噸"},{"english":"Overall","chinese":"整體而言"},{"english":"remained the highest emitter throughout","chinese":"全期一直是最高排放國"},{"english":"the highest emitter","chinese":"最高排放國"},{"english":"throughout","chinese":"整個期間"},{"english":"although","chinese":"雖然；儘管"},{"english":"its figure declined gradually","chinese":"其數字逐漸下降"},{"english":"declined gradually","chinese":"逐漸下降"},{"english":"ended lower than it began","chinese":"結束時低於起點"},{"english":"after reaching a peak","chinese":"在達到高峰後"},{"english":"reaching a peak","chinese":"達到高峰"},{"english":"in the late 1970s","chinese":"在1970年代後期"},{"english":"whereas","chinese":"而；然而"},{"english":"recorded steady growth","chinese":"錄得穩定增長"},{"english":"steady growth","chinese":"穩定增長"},{"english":"with Italy ranking second by 2007","chinese":"其中意大利到2007年排名第二"},{"english":"ranking second","chinese":"排名第二"},{"english":"produced just under 11 tonnes","chinese":"排放略低於11公噸"},{"english":"just under 11 tonnes","chinese":"略低於11公噸"},{"english":"compared with","chinese":"與……相比"},{"english":"about 8.7 tonnes","chinese":"約8.7公噸"},{"english":"rose to just over 10 tonnes","chinese":"上升至略高於10公噸"},{"english":"just over 10 tonnes","chinese":"略高於10公噸"},{"english":"almost matching the UK","chinese":"幾乎追平英國"},{"english":"before falling markedly to","chinese":"隨後明顯下降至"},{"english":"falling markedly","chinese":"明顯下降"},{"english":"around 7 tonnes","chinese":"約7公噸"},{"english":"approximately 5.5 tonnes","chinese":"約5.5公噸"},{"english":"by the final year","chinese":"到最後一年"},{"english":"followed a gentler downward path","chinese":"呈現較溫和的下降走勢"},{"english":"a gentler downward path","chinese":"較溫和的下降走勢"},{"english":"slipping from nearly 11 tonnes to about 8.7 tonnes","chinese":"由接近11公噸下滑至約8.7公噸"},{"english":"over the same period","chinese":"在同一期間"},{"english":"By contrast","chinese":"相比之下"},{"english":"climbed from roughly 4.2 tonnes","chinese":"由約4.2公噸攀升"},{"english":"roughly 4.2 tonnes","chinese":"約4.2公噸"},{"english":"increased further to around 7.7 tonnes","chinese":"進一步上升至約7.7公噸"},{"english":"where it levelled off","chinese":"隨後在該水平持平"},{"english":"levelled off","chinese":"趨於平穩"},{"english":"initially the lowest","chinese":"最初最低"},{"english":"at just over 1 tonne","chinese":"略高於1公噸"},{"english":"rose steadily to about 5.5 tonnes","chinese":"穩步上升至約5.5公噸"},{"english":"almost converging with Sweden","chinese":"幾乎與瑞典匯合"},{"english":"converging with","chinese":"與……趨於一致"}]},"model-essay-7-ielts-task1-maps":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-7-ielts-task1-maps","essayKey":"maps:7","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-7-ielts-task1-maps","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-1/maps/maps-7","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"The maps compare road access to a city hospital in 2007 and 2010.","chinese":"這兩幅地圖比較了 2007 年和 2010 年通往一所城市醫院的道路通達情況。"},{"label":"Overview","english":"Overall, the layout was substantially reorganised: two roundabouts and a bus station were introduced, and the original combined car park was replaced by separate staff and public parking facilities. The three main roads, however, remained in the same positions.","chinese":"整體而言，該區佈局被大幅重新規劃：新增了兩個迴旋處和一個巴士總站，而原本供員工和公眾共同使用的停車場則被分成員工停車場和公眾停車場。 然而，三條主要道路的位置保持不變。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"In 2007, Hospital Road ran northwards from City Road to the Ring Road, which surrounded the hospital. Six small bus stops were placed along Hospital Road, three on each side. A single car park for both staff and the public stood to the east of this road, just below the Ring Road.","chinese":"2007 年，醫院路從城市路向北延伸至環路，而環路圍繞著醫院。 六個小型巴士站沿醫院路設置，左右兩側各三個。 一個供員工和公眾共同使用的停車場位於這條路以東、環路正下方。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"By 2010, traffic flow had been redesigned more systematically. A roundabout had been built at each end of Hospital Road, one at its junction with City Road and the other where it joined the Ring Road. The bus stops had been removed and replaced by a bus station on the western side, with access links to both roundabouts. Parking was also separated: the staff car park occupied the area east of Hospital Road, while a new public car park was constructed east of the hospital, reached directly from the Ring Road.","chinese":"到 2010 年，交通流線已被更有系統地重新設計。 醫院路兩端各建了一個迴旋處，一個位於它與城市路的交界處，另一個位於它與環路相接的位置。 原有巴士站被移除，並由西側的一個巴士總站取代，而該巴士總站有道路連接至兩個迴旋處。 停車安排也被分開：員工停車場佔據醫院路以東的區域，而一個新的公眾停車場則建於醫院東側，可直接從環路進入。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"the two maps below show","chinese":"下列兩幅地圖顯示"},{"english":"road access to","chinese":"前往……的道路通達情況"},{"english":"a city hospital","chinese":"城市醫院"},{"english":"in 2007 and in 2010","chinese":"在2007年及2010年"},{"english":"summarise the information","chinese":"概述資料"},{"english":"selecting and reporting","chinese":"選取並報告"},{"english":"the main features","chinese":"主要特徵"},{"english":"make comparisons where relevant","chinese":"在相關之處作出比較"},{"english":"The maps compare","chinese":"兩幅地圖比較"},{"english":"compare road access","chinese":"比較道路通達情況"},{"english":"Overall","chinese":"整體而言"},{"english":"the layout","chinese":"佈局"},{"english":"was substantially reorganised","chinese":"已被大幅重新規劃"},{"english":"substantially reorganised","chinese":"大幅重新規劃"},{"english":"two roundabouts","chinese":"兩個迴旋處"},{"english":"a bus station","chinese":"巴士站；巴士總站"},{"english":"were introduced","chinese":"已被增設"},{"english":"the original combined car park","chinese":"原來共用的停車場"},{"english":"combined car park","chinese":"共用停車場"},{"english":"was replaced by","chinese":"已被……取代"},{"english":"separate staff and public parking facilities","chinese":"分開的職員及公眾泊車設施"},{"english":"parking facilities","chinese":"泊車設施"},{"english":"the three main roads","chinese":"三條主要道路"},{"english":"however","chinese":"然而"},{"english":"remained in the same positions","chinese":"仍在相同位置"},{"english":"In 2007","chinese":"在2007年"},{"english":"Hospital Road","chinese":"Hospital Road"},{"english":"ran northwards from","chinese":"由……向北延伸"},{"english":"City Road","chinese":"City Road"},{"english":"the Ring Road","chinese":"Ring Road；環形道路"},{"english":"surrounded the hospital","chinese":"圍繞醫院"},{"english":"six small bus stops","chinese":"六個小型巴士站"},{"english":"were placed along","chinese":"沿着……設置"},{"english":"along Hospital Road","chinese":"沿着 Hospital Road"},{"english":"three on each side","chinese":"每邊三個"},{"english":"a single car park","chinese":"單一停車場"},{"english":"for both staff and the public","chinese":"供職員及公眾使用"},{"english":"stood to the east of","chinese":"位於……以東"},{"english":"to the east of this road","chinese":"在這條路以東"},{"english":"just below","chinese":"就在……下方"},{"english":"By 2010","chinese":"到2010年"},{"english":"traffic flow","chinese":"交通流向"},{"english":"had been redesigned","chinese":"已被重新設計"},{"english":"more systematically","chinese":"更有系統地"},{"english":"a roundabout had been built","chinese":"已建成一個迴旋處"},{"english":"at each end of","chinese":"在……兩端各處"},{"english":"its junction with","chinese":"與……的交匯處"},{"english":"where it joined","chinese":"在它連接……的位置"},{"english":"the bus stops had been removed","chinese":"巴士站已被移除"},{"english":"removed and replaced by","chinese":"被移除並由……取代"},{"english":"on the western side","chinese":"在西面"},{"english":"with access links to","chinese":"設有通往……的連接路"},{"english":"both roundabouts","chinese":"兩個迴旋處"},{"english":"parking was also separated","chinese":"泊車區亦被分開"},{"english":"the staff car park","chinese":"職員停車場"},{"english":"occupied the area east of","chinese":"佔據……以東的區域"},{"english":"while","chinese":"而"},{"english":"a new public car park","chinese":"新的公眾停車場"},{"english":"was constructed east of","chinese":"已在……以東興建"},{"english":"east of the hospital","chinese":"在醫院以東"},{"english":"reached directly from","chinese":"可由……直接到達"},{"english":"directly from the Ring Road","chinese":"直接由 Ring Road 到達"}]},"model-essay-7-ielts-task1-mixed-charts":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-7-ielts-task1-mixed-charts","essayKey":"mixed-charts:7","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-7-ielts-task1-mixed-charts","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-1/mixed-charts/mixed-charts-7","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"The table and pie charts compare attendance at Ashdown Museum and visitors’ satisfaction levels in the years before and after its refurbishment.","chinese":"該表格和圓餅圖比較了阿什當博物館翻新前後兩年中的參觀人數，以及訪客對參觀體驗的滿意程度。"},{"label":"Overview","english":"Overall, the museum became both more popular and more highly rated after the work was completed. The total number of visitors rose markedly, while positive responses replaced dissatisfaction as the dominant pattern.","chinese":"整體而言，翻新工程完成後，該博物館不但更受歡迎，也獲得了更高的評價。 總訪客人數明顯上升，而正面回應也取代不滿意，成為主要的滿意度模式。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"In terms of attendance, the museum received 74,000 visitors before the refurbishment, but this figure increased to 92,000 in the following year, a rise of 18,000. The improvement in satisfaction was even more striking. Before the changes, only 15% of respondents said they were very satisfied and a further 30% were satisfied, meaning that positive feedback accounted for less than half of all responses. After refurbishment, however, these two categories climbed to 35% and 40%, respectively, so three quarters of visitors expressed satisfaction.","chinese":"就參觀人數而言，該博物館在翻新前一年接待了 74,000 名訪客，但在翻新後一年，這一數字上升至 92,000 ，增加了 18,000 人。 滿意度方面的改善甚至更加明顯。 在翻新前，只有 15% 的受訪者表示非常滿意，另有 30% 表示滿意，這意味著正面回饋佔所有回應不到一半。 然而，翻新後，這兩個類別分別上升至 35% 和 40% ，因此有四分之三的訪客表達了滿意。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"By contrast, the proportion of dissatisfied visitors fell sharply. In the year before refurbishment, 40% reported being dissatisfied, making this the largest single group, while 10% were very dissatisfied. In the year after refurbishment, these figures dropped to 15% and 5%, respectively. The share giving no response remained unchanged at 5% in both years.","chinese":"相比之下，不滿意訪客的比例大幅下降。 在翻新前一年， 40% 的訪客表示不滿意，使其成為最大的單一組別，而另有10% 表示非常不滿意。 在翻新後一年，這兩項數字分別下降至 15% 和 5% 。 沒有回應的比例在兩年中都保持在 5% ，沒有變化。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"the table below","chinese":"以下表格"},{"english":"the number of visitors","chinese":"參觀人數"},{"english":"Ashdown Museum","chinese":"Ashdown博物館"},{"english":"during the year before","chinese":"在……前一年期間"},{"english":"during the year after","chinese":"在……後一年期間"},{"english":"was refurbished","chinese":"經過翻新"},{"english":"the results of surveys","chinese":"調查結果"},{"english":"asking visitors how satisfied they were","chinese":"詢問遊客滿意程度"},{"english":"how satisfied they were with","chinese":"對……有多滿意"},{"english":"during the same two periods","chinese":"在同樣兩個時期"},{"english":"summarise the information","chinese":"概述資料"},{"english":"by selecting and reporting","chinese":"透過選取並報告……"},{"english":"the main features","chinese":"主要特徵"},{"english":"make comparisons where relevant","chinese":"在相關之處作出比較"},{"english":"the table and pie charts","chinese":"表格及圓形圖"},{"english":"compare attendance at","chinese":"比較……的入場人數"},{"english":"visitors' satisfaction levels","chinese":"遊客滿意程度"},{"english":"in the years before and after","chinese":"在……前後兩年"},{"english":"its refurbishment","chinese":"其翻新工程"},{"english":"became both more popular and more highly rated","chinese":"變得更受歡迎且評價更高"},{"english":"more popular","chinese":"更受歡迎"},{"english":"more highly rated","chinese":"評價更高"},{"english":"after the work was completed","chinese":"工程完成後"},{"english":"the total number of visitors","chinese":"總參觀人數"},{"english":"rose markedly","chinese":"顯著上升"},{"english":"positive responses","chinese":"正面回應"},{"english":"replaced dissatisfaction as","chinese":"取代不滿成為……"},{"english":"dissatisfaction","chinese":"不滿"},{"english":"the dominant pattern","chinese":"主要模式"},{"english":"in terms of attendance","chinese":"就參觀人數而言"},{"english":"received 74,000 visitors","chinese":"接待了74,000名遊客"},{"english":"before the refurbishment","chinese":"翻新前"},{"english":"this figure increased to","chinese":"這個數字增加至"},{"english":"in the following year","chinese":"在隨後一年"},{"english":"a rise of 18,000","chinese":"增加18,000"},{"english":"the improvement in satisfaction","chinese":"滿意度的改善"},{"english":"even more striking","chinese":"更加明顯；更為突出"},{"english":"before the changes","chinese":"改動前"},{"english":"respondents","chinese":"受訪者"},{"english":"very satisfied","chinese":"非常滿意"},{"english":"a further 30%","chinese":"另外30%"},{"english":"were satisfied","chinese":"感到滿意"},{"english":"meaning that","chinese":"這意味著"},{"english":"positive feedback","chinese":"正面評價"},{"english":"accounted for","chinese":"佔……"},{"english":"less than half of","chinese":"少於一半"},{"english":"all responses","chinese":"所有回應"},{"english":"after refurbishment","chinese":"翻新後"},{"english":"these two categories","chinese":"這兩個類別"},{"english":"climbed to","chinese":"上升至"},{"english":"respectively","chinese":"分別"},{"english":"three quarters of","chinese":"四分之三"},{"english":"expressed satisfaction","chinese":"表示滿意"},{"english":"by contrast","chinese":"相比之下"},{"english":"the proportion of dissatisfied visitors","chinese":"不滿遊客的比例"},{"english":"fell sharply","chinese":"大幅下跌"},{"english":"reported being dissatisfied","chinese":"表示不滿"},{"english":"dissatisfied","chinese":"不滿意"},{"english":"the largest single group","chinese":"最大單一組別"},{"english":"very dissatisfied","chinese":"非常不滿意"},{"english":"in the year after refurbishment","chinese":"翻新後一年"},{"english":"these figures dropped to","chinese":"這些數字下降至"},{"english":"dropped to","chinese":"下降至"},{"english":"the share giving no response","chinese":"沒有回應者的比例"},{"english":"no response","chinese":"沒有回應"},{"english":"remained unchanged","chinese":"維持不變"},{"english":"at 5%","chinese":"為5%"},{"english":"in both years","chinese":"在兩年中"},{"english":"attendance figures","chinese":"入場人數數據"},{"english":"satisfaction survey results","chinese":"滿意度調查結果"},{"english":"visitor numbers","chinese":"遊客人數"},{"english":"an increase from X to Y","chinese":"由X增加至Y"},{"english":"a marked increase","chinese":"顯著增加"},{"english":"a sharp fall","chinese":"大幅下跌"},{"english":"negative responses","chinese":"負面回應"},{"english":"a clear shift from X to Y","chinese":"由X明顯轉向Y"},{"english":"from dissatisfaction to satisfaction","chinese":"由不滿轉為滿意"},{"english":"the most notable change","chinese":"最明顯的變化"},{"english":"the least changed category","chinese":"變化最少的類別"},{"english":"the combined share of","chinese":"……的合計比例"},{"english":"satisfied visitors","chinese":"滿意的遊客"},{"english":"dissatisfied visitors","chinese":"不滿的遊客"},{"english":"reached 75%","chinese":"達到75%"},{"english":"fell to 20%","chinese":"下降至20%"},{"english":"showed a major improvement","chinese":"顯示重大改善"},{"english":"became the clear majority","chinese":"成為明顯多數"},{"english":"the refurbishment appears to have","chinese":"翻新工程似乎已經……"},{"english":"improved both X and Y","chinese":"同時改善X和Y"}]},"model-essay-7-ielts-task1-process-diagram":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-7-ielts-task1-process-diagram","essayKey":"process-diagram:7","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-7-ielts-task1-process-diagram","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-1/process-diagrams/process-diagram-7","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"The diagram illustrates the operation of a geothermal power plant and the stages through which underground heat is converted into electricity.","chinese":"該圖說明地熱發電廠的運作方式，以及地下熱能如何經過多個階段被轉化為電力。"},{"label":"Overview","english":"Overall, this is a five-stage, linear process. It begins with cold water being pumped deep below the surface and ends with electricity being generated, with the key transformation occurring when water is heated by hot rocks and then used to produce steam.","chinese":"整體而言，這是一個五階段的線性流程。 它從冷水被泵入地表深處開始，以電力的產生結束；其中關鍵轉化發生在水被熱岩加熱後，再被用來產生蒸汽。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"At the first stage, cold water stored at ground level is forced down through an injection well to a depth of about 4.5 kilometres. Once it reaches the geothermal zone, the water passes horizontally through an area of hot rocks, where it absorbs heat. It then travels back towards the surface through a separate production well, in contrast to the initial downward movement through the injection well.","chinese":"第一階段，儲存在地面上的冷水被迫通過注入井下送至約 4.5 公里深處。 當水到達地熱區後，它會水平流經一片熱岩區，並在此吸收熱量。 然後，它會通過一口獨立的生產井返回地表；這與最初通過注入井向下流動形成對比。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"After the heated water has been pumped up, it enters a condenser, from which steam is released. This steam is directed into a turbine, causing the turbine blades to rotate. In the final stage, the rotating turbine powers a generator, which produces electricity that is then transmitted through power lines.","chinese":"加熱後的水被泵上來後，會進入冷凝器，並由此釋放出蒸汽。 這些蒸汽被引導進入渦輪機，使渦輪葉片旋轉。 在最後階段，旋轉的渦輪機帶動發電機，而發電機產生的電力隨後通過電線輸送出去。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"The diagram illustrates","chinese":"圖解顯示"},{"english":"the operation of","chinese":"……的運作"},{"english":"a geothermal power plant","chinese":"地熱發電廠"},{"english":"the stages through which","chinese":"……所經過的階段"},{"english":"underground heat","chinese":"地底熱能"},{"english":"is converted into electricity","chinese":"被轉化成電力"},{"english":"a five-stage, linear process","chinese":"線性的五階段過程"},{"english":"begins with","chinese":"以……開始"},{"english":"cold water being pumped","chinese":"冷水被泵送"},{"english":"deep below the surface","chinese":"地面深處"},{"english":"ends with","chinese":"以……結束"},{"english":"electricity being generated","chinese":"電力被產生"},{"english":"the key transformation","chinese":"關鍵轉化"},{"english":"occurring when","chinese":"發生於……時"},{"english":"is heated by hot rocks","chinese":"被熱岩石加熱"},{"english":"hot rocks","chinese":"熱岩石"},{"english":"used to produce steam","chinese":"用作產生蒸汽"},{"english":"At the first stage","chinese":"在第一階段"},{"english":"stored at ground level","chinese":"儲存在地面水平"},{"english":"ground level","chinese":"地面水平"},{"english":"is forced down through","chinese":"被迫向下通過"},{"english":"an injection well","chinese":"注入井"},{"english":"to a depth of about 4.5 kilometres","chinese":"到約4.5公里深處"},{"english":"Once it reaches","chinese":"一旦到達"},{"english":"the geothermal zone","chinese":"地熱區"},{"english":"passes horizontally through","chinese":"水平流經"},{"english":"an area of hot rocks","chinese":"一片熱岩石區"},{"english":"absorbs heat","chinese":"吸收熱力"},{"english":"travels back towards the surface","chinese":"回流至地面方向"},{"english":"a separate production well","chinese":"另一條生產井"},{"english":"in contrast to","chinese":"與……相反"},{"english":"the initial downward movement","chinese":"最初的向下流動"},{"english":"through the injection well","chinese":"經由注入井"},{"english":"After the heated water has been pumped up","chinese":"當熱水被泵回上來後"},{"english":"the heated water","chinese":"加熱後的水"},{"english":"has been pumped up","chinese":"已被泵回上來"},{"english":"enters a condenser","chinese":"進入冷凝器"},{"english":"a condenser","chinese":"冷凝器"},{"english":"from which steam is released","chinese":"蒸汽從中被釋放"},{"english":"steam is released","chinese":"蒸汽被釋放"},{"english":"is directed into a turbine","chinese":"被引導進入渦輪機"},{"english":"a turbine","chinese":"渦輪機"},{"english":"causing the turbine blades to rotate","chinese":"令渦輪葉片旋轉"},{"english":"turbine blades","chinese":"渦輪葉片"},{"english":"to rotate","chinese":"旋轉"},{"english":"In the final stage","chinese":"在最後階段"},{"english":"the rotating turbine","chinese":"旋轉中的渦輪機"},{"english":"powers a generator","chinese":"驅動發電機"},{"english":"a generator","chinese":"發電機"},{"english":"produces electricity","chinese":"產生電力"},{"english":"is then transmitted through","chinese":"然後經由……輸送"},{"english":"power lines","chinese":"輸電線"}]},"model-essay-7-ielts-task1-tables":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-7-ielts-task1-tables","essayKey":"tables:7","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-7-ielts-task1-tables","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-1/tables/table-7","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"The table compares international tourist arrivals, measured in millions, in the listed destinations in 2009 and 2010, together with the percentage change over the period.","chinese":"該表格比較了所列目的地在 2009 年和 2010 年的國際遊客到訪人數，以百萬為單位，並展示了期間的百分比變化。"},{"label":"Overview","english":"Overall, France remained the most visited destination, despite recording no growth. Most places attracted more tourists in the second year, but the increases were generally modest among the larger markets and far stronger among Germany, China and Turkey. Hong Kong was the only destination to decline.","chinese":"整體而言，法國雖然沒有錄得增長，但仍然是最多遊客到訪的目的地。 大部分地區在第二年吸引了更多遊客，但較大型市場的升幅普遍溫和，而德國、中國和土耳其的增長則強勁得多。 香港是唯一出現下跌的目的地。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"Among the leading destinations, France received 76 million tourists in both years, staying well ahead of the US, whose figure edged up from 66 to 67 million. Spain and the UK were level at 55 million in 2009, but the UK grew more quickly, reaching 57 million and narrowly overtaking Spain, which rose to 56 million. Italy also increased slightly, from 44 to 45 million.","chinese":"在主要目的地之中，法國兩年均接待了 7,600 萬名遊客，仍然大幅領先美國；而美國的數字則由 6,600 萬微升至 6,700 萬。 西班牙和英國在 2009 年同為 5,500 萬，但英國增長較快，達到 5,700 萬，並以輕微差距超越西班牙；西班牙則上升至 5,600 萬。 意大利亦輕微上升，由 4,400 萬增至 4,500 萬。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"The remaining destinations showed much sharper relative changes. Turkey, China and Germany each gained 12 million arrivals, climbing from 33 to 45 million, 22 to 34 million and 11 to 23 million respectively. Because Germany started from the lowest base, this represented the largest percentage rise, at 109%. By contrast, Hong Kong fell from 10 to 9 million, a decrease of 11%.","chinese":"其餘目的地則呈現出更明顯的相對變化。 土耳其、中國和德國的到訪人數均增加了 1,200 萬，分別由 3,300 萬升至 4,500萬、由 2,200 萬升至 3,400 萬，以及由 1,100 萬升至 2,300 萬。 由於德國的起點最低，因此這代表了最大的百分比升幅，達 109% 。 相比之下，香港由 1,000 萬下降至 900 萬，跌幅為 11% 。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"the table compares","chinese":"表格比較"},{"english":"international tourist arrivals","chinese":"國際旅客到訪人次"},{"english":"measured in millions","chinese":"以百萬計"},{"english":"listed destinations","chinese":"列出的目的地"},{"english":"in 2009 and 2010","chinese":"在2009年和2010年"},{"english":"together with","chinese":"連同；以及"},{"english":"percentage change","chinese":"百分比變化"},{"english":"over the period","chinese":"在該期間"},{"english":"remained the most visited destination","chinese":"仍然是最多人到訪的目的地"},{"english":"the most visited destination","chinese":"最多人到訪的目的地"},{"english":"despite recording no growth","chinese":"儘管沒有錄得增長"},{"english":"recording no growth","chinese":"沒有錄得增長"},{"english":"most places attracted more tourists","chinese":"大部分地方吸引更多旅客"},{"english":"in the second year","chinese":"在第二年"},{"english":"generally modest","chinese":"普遍溫和"},{"english":"larger markets","chinese":"較大型市場"},{"english":"far stronger among","chinese":"在……之中強勁得多"},{"english":"the only destination to decline","chinese":"唯一下跌的目的地"},{"english":"leading destinations","chinese":"主要目的地"},{"english":"received 76 million tourists","chinese":"接待了7,600萬名旅客"},{"english":"in both years","chinese":"在兩年中"},{"english":"staying well ahead of","chinese":"保持大幅領先"},{"english":"well ahead of","chinese":"遠高於；大幅領先"},{"english":"the US","chinese":"美國"},{"english":"whose figure edged up","chinese":"其數字輕微上升"},{"english":"edged up from X to Y","chinese":"由 X 輕微上升至 Y"},{"english":"Spain and the UK","chinese":"西班牙和英國"},{"english":"were level at","chinese":"同為；持平於"},{"english":"but the UK grew more quickly","chinese":"但英國增長較快"},{"english":"reaching 57 million","chinese":"達到5,700萬"},{"english":"narrowly overtaking","chinese":"僅僅超越"},{"english":"which rose to","chinese":"而……上升至"},{"english":"increased slightly","chinese":"輕微增加"},{"english":"the remaining destinations","chinese":"其餘目的地"},{"english":"much sharper relative changes","chinese":"相對變化大得多"},{"english":"relative changes","chinese":"相對變化"},{"english":"each gained","chinese":"各增加"},{"english":"gained 12 million arrivals","chinese":"增加1,200萬到訪人次"},{"english":"climbing from X to Y","chinese":"由 X 攀升至 Y"},{"english":"respectively","chinese":"分別"},{"english":"started from the lowest base","chinese":"從最低基數開始"},{"english":"the lowest base","chinese":"最低基數；最低起點"},{"english":"this represented","chinese":"這代表"},{"english":"the largest percentage rise","chinese":"最大百分比升幅"},{"english":"at 109%","chinese":"為109%"},{"english":"by contrast","chinese":"相比之下"},{"english":"fell from X to Y","chinese":"由 X 下跌至 Y"},{"english":"a decrease of 11%","chinese":"11%的跌幅"},{"english":"tourist numbers","chinese":"旅客人數"},{"english":"visitor arrivals","chinese":"旅客到訪人次"},{"english":"tourist destinations","chinese":"旅遊目的地"},{"english":"attract tourists","chinese":"吸引旅客"},{"english":"no change","chinese":"沒有變化"},{"english":"modest growth","chinese":"溫和增長"},{"english":"strong growth","chinese":"強勁增長"},{"english":"a sharp increase","chinese":"大幅增加"},{"english":"a slight increase","chinese":"輕微增加"},{"english":"a small rise","chinese":"小幅上升"},{"english":"a fall in arrivals","chinese":"到訪人次下跌"},{"english":"unchanged at","chinese":"維持在"},{"english":"rose by 12 million","chinese":"增加1,200萬"},{"english":"more than doubled","chinese":"增加超過一倍"},{"english":"overtook Spain","chinese":"超越西班牙"},{"english":"remained ahead of","chinese":"仍然領先於"},{"english":"ranked first","chinese":"排名第一"},{"english":"ranked second","chinese":"排名第二"},{"english":"among the top destinations","chinese":"在主要目的地之中"},{"english":"smaller markets","chinese":"較小型市場"},{"english":"a higher growth rate","chinese":"較高增長率"},{"english":"the greatest absolute increase","chinese":"最大實際增幅"},{"english":"absolute increase","chinese":"實際增幅"},{"english":"percentage increase","chinese":"百分比升幅"},{"english":"percentage decline","chinese":"百分比跌幅"},{"english":"the overall pattern","chinese":"整體模式"},{"english":"remained dominant","chinese":"仍然佔主導地位"},{"english":"widened the gap","chinese":"擴大差距"},{"english":"narrowed the gap","chinese":"收窄差距"},{"english":"caught up with","chinese":"追上"},{"english":"broadly stable","chinese":"大致穩定"},{"english":"stronger relative performance","chinese":"最強相對表現"},{"english":"weaker performance","chinese":"較弱表現"},{"english":"the only negative figure","chinese":"唯一負數"},{"english":"positive growth","chinese":"正增長"},{"english":"the highest figure","chinese":"最高數字"},{"english":"the lowest figure","chinese":"最低數字"},{"english":"compared with","chinese":"與……相比"},{"english":"by the end of the period","chinese":"到該期間結束時"},{"english":"from a lower starting point","chinese":"從較低起點開始"},{"english":"in absolute terms","chinese":"以實際數字計"},{"english":"in percentage terms","chinese":"以百分比計"},{"english":"tourist arrivals rose","chinese":"旅客到訪人次上升"},{"english":"tourist arrivals declined","chinese":"旅客到訪人次下跌"}]},"model-essay-8-ielts-advantage-disadvantage":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-8-ielts-advantage-disadvantage","essayKey":"advantage-disadvantage:8","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-8-ielts-advantage-disadvantage","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/advantage-and-disadvantage/EdmundBd9AdDisAd-Q8","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"Schools are increasingly expected to prepare young people not only for academic success but also for life in an interconnected world. In this context, some educators argue that international exchange visits are beneficial for teenagers. I strongly believe that the advantages of these programmes far outweigh the disadvantages, because they develop maturity and intercultural competence in ways that ordinary classroom learning rarely can, whereas the drawbacks are generally short-lived and manageable.","chinese":"無論在工作還是私人生活中，越來越多的溝通如今都是透過數位科技進行，而不是面對面交流。 儘管這種發展可能削弱人際關係的品質，並增加誤解的風險， 我認為整體而言，它的優點更大，因為它使溝通變得更有效率，並讓人們即使相隔遙遠也能保持聯繫。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"The greatest advantage of international exchange visits is that they accelerate teenagers’ personal growth. When students spend time in a different country, they are forced to deal with unfamiliar routines, different school expectations and everyday practical challenges without depending entirely on their parents. This process makes them more independent, adaptable and responsible. For example, a student staying with a host family may initially struggle to follow a new timetable or communicate minor needs, but very quickly that student learns to ask questions confidently, manage time more effectively and solve problems calmly. A second major benefit is that these visits deepen cultural and linguistic understanding. Instead of learning about another society in an abstract way, teenagers experience it directly through conversation, school life and daily interaction. As a result, they often become more open-minded and more capable of communicating with people from different backgrounds.","chinese":"科技化溝通最主要的優點是速度和便利性。 在專業環境中，電子郵件、即時通訊平台和視像會議免除了人們出行的需要，並使決策幾乎可以即時作出。 這不但縮短了回應時間、降低了營運成本，還使公司能夠非常輕鬆地協調分布在不同城市甚至不同大洲的團隊。 例如，一位經理可以透過一次線上會議便與海外同事解決生產問題，而不是等待數天才進行一次面對面的討論。 同樣的情況也適用於社交層面：住得很遠的父母、子女和朋友仍然可以透過通話和訊息每天聯絡。 結果是，人際關係更容易維持，也較不會隨時間而逐漸淡化。 例如，一個家庭即使成員分散在不同國家，仍然可以透過視像通話分享日常近況並提供情感支持。 因此，數位溝通大大提升了工作和個人生活中的效率與可及性。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"Admittedly, there are some disadvantages, but they are not significant enough to challenge the overall value of such visits. One concern is cost, since travel, accommodation and insurance can be expensive. However, many exchange programmes are short, subsidised or organised through school partnerships, so the financial burden is often reduced considerably. Another possible drawback is that some teenagers may feel homesick or anxious in an unfamiliar environment. Nevertheless, this discomfort is usually temporary and can even be beneficial, because overcoming it helps young people build emotional resilience. For instance, a student who feels lonely during the first few days of an exchange often returns home noticeably more confident after forming friendships and adapting successfully.","chinese":"然而，數位溝通也有重要的缺點，其中最嚴重的是它缺乏情感上的豐富性。 面對面的交談能傳達語氣、面部表情和肢體語言，這些都有助於人們準確理解意思、表達同理心並建立信任。 當這些線索消失時，訊息便更容易被誤解，從而導致困惑甚至衝突。 例如，一封簡短的電郵或文字訊息即使本無惡意，也可能顯得冷淡甚至帶有敵意。 這在職場中尤其成問題，因為信任和細膩的理解對領導、協商和團隊合作都至關重要。 長遠而言，過度依賴螢幕也可能助長膚淺的社交習慣，因此人們即使在線上一直保持聯絡，仍可能感到孤立。 例如，一個人即使經常透過社交媒體聊天，仍可能感到孤單，因為數位接觸無法完全取代真正的關注和人的陪伴。 因此，儘管科技讓溝通成為可能，它同時也可能削弱清晰度、信任感和情感深度。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, international exchange visits offer teenagers far more than a simple change of scenery. Because they foster independence, cultural awareness and real-world communication skills, and because their disadvantages are limited and manageable, their advantages decisively outweigh their disadvantages.","chinese":"總結來說，透過科技進行溝通在效率和可及性方面具有明顯優勢，儘管它可能削弱人際互動的深度與清晰度。 整體而言，我認為其優點大於缺點，因為數位工具使工作和個人生活中的溝通都能跨越時間與距離而有效運作。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"increasingly expected to","chinese":"越來越被期望／要求去……"},{"english":"prepare young people for","chinese":"為年輕人準備好面對……"},{"english":"not only for...but also for...","chinese":"不只為了……也為了……"},{"english":"academic success","chinese":"學業成功"},{"english":"an interconnected world","chinese":"互相聯繫的世界"},{"english":"in this context","chinese":"在這個背景下"},{"english":"educators argue that","chinese":"教育工作者認為"},{"english":"international exchange visits","chinese":"國際交流訪問"},{"english":"beneficial for teenagers","chinese":"對青少年有益"},{"english":"strongly believe that","chinese":"強烈相信"},{"english":"the advantages of these programmes","chinese":"這些計劃的好處"},{"english":"far outweigh the disadvantages","chinese":"遠遠大於缺點"},{"english":"develop maturity","chinese":"培養成熟"},{"english":"intercultural competence","chinese":"跨文化能力"},{"english":"ordinary classroom learning","chinese":"普通課堂學習"},{"english":"rarely can","chinese":"很少能夠"},{"english":"whereas","chinese":"而；相比之下"},{"english":"drawbacks","chinese":"缺點"},{"english":"short-lived and manageable","chinese":"短暫且可處理的"},{"english":"the greatest advantage","chinese":"最大的好處"},{"english":"accelerate teenagers' personal growth","chinese":"加快青少年的個人成長"},{"english":"personal growth","chinese":"個人成長"},{"english":"spend time in a different country","chinese":"在不同國家逗留"},{"english":"be forced to deal with","chinese":"被迫處理"},{"english":"unfamiliar routines","chinese":"不熟悉的日常規律"},{"english":"different school expectations","chinese":"不同的學校期望"},{"english":"everyday practical challenges","chinese":"日常實際挑戰"},{"english":"without depending entirely on","chinese":"不完全依賴"},{"english":"this process","chinese":"這個過程"},{"english":"independent, adaptable and responsible","chinese":"獨立、有適應力和負責任"},{"english":"staying with a host family","chinese":"與寄宿家庭同住"},{"english":"initially struggle to","chinese":"起初難以"},{"english":"follow a new timetable","chinese":"遵循新的時間表"},{"english":"communicate minor needs","chinese":"表達小需要"},{"english":"very quickly","chinese":"很快"},{"english":"ask questions confidently","chinese":"有信心地提問"},{"english":"manage time more effectively","chinese":"更有效地管理時間"},{"english":"solve problems calmly","chinese":"冷靜地解決問題"},{"english":"a second major benefit","chinese":"第二個主要好處"},{"english":"deepen cultural and linguistic understanding","chinese":"加深文化和語言理解"},{"english":"instead of","chinese":"而不是"},{"english":"in an abstract way","chinese":"以抽象方式"},{"english":"experience it directly","chinese":"直接體驗它"},{"english":"daily interaction","chinese":"日常互動"},{"english":"as a result","chinese":"因此"},{"english":"open-minded","chinese":"思想開明的"},{"english":"capable of communicating with","chinese":"有能力與……溝通"},{"english":"different backgrounds","chinese":"不同背景"},{"english":"admittedly","chinese":"誠然"},{"english":"significant enough to","chinese":"重要到足以……"},{"english":"challenge the overall value of","chinese":"質疑……的整體價值"},{"english":"such visits","chinese":"這類訪問"},{"english":"one concern is cost","chinese":"其中一個憂慮是費用"},{"english":"travel, accommodation and insurance","chinese":"交通、住宿和保險"},{"english":"exchange programmes","chinese":"交流計劃"},{"english":"subsidised","chinese":"受資助的"},{"english":"organised through school partnerships","chinese":"透過學校合作安排"},{"english":"financial burden","chinese":"財政負擔"},{"english":"reduced considerably","chinese":"大幅減輕／降低"},{"english":"possible drawback","chinese":"可能的缺點"},{"english":"homesick","chinese":"思鄉的"},{"english":"anxious","chinese":"焦慮的"},{"english":"an unfamiliar environment","chinese":"陌生環境"},{"english":"nevertheless","chinese":"然而"},{"english":"temporary","chinese":"暫時的"},{"english":"can even be beneficial","chinese":"甚至可以是有益的"},{"english":"overcoming it","chinese":"克服它"},{"english":"build emotional resilience","chinese":"建立情緒抗逆力"},{"english":"during the first few days of","chinese":"在……最初幾天"},{"english":"returns home","chinese":"回家；回到本地"},{"english":"noticeably more confident","chinese":"明顯更有信心"},{"english":"forming friendships","chinese":"建立友誼"},{"english":"adapting successfully","chinese":"成功適應"},{"english":"offer teenagers far more than","chinese":"給青少年的遠不止……"},{"english":"a simple change of scenery","chinese":"簡單換個環境"},{"english":"foster independence","chinese":"培養獨立性"},{"english":"cultural awareness","chinese":"文化意識"},{"english":"real-world communication skills","chinese":"現實世界中的溝通技巧"},{"english":"limited and manageable","chinese":"有限且可處理的"},{"english":"decisively outweigh","chinese":"明顯大於"}]},"model-essay-8-ielts-direct-question":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-8-ielts-direct-question","essayKey":"direct-question:8","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-8-ielts-direct-question","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/direct-question/EdmundBd9Dir-Q8","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"Management interviews often examine far more than a candidate’s technical competence, because managers are expected to influence people, make decisions and represent the values of an organisation. In my view, leadership is not an innate skill; rather, it is a practical ability developed through training, experience and self-awareness. Companies also tend to look for emotional intelligence, sound judgement and reliability when selecting managers.","chinese":"管理層面試通常考察的遠遠不只是候選人的專業能力，因為經理被期望能影響他人、作出決策，並代表一個機構的價值觀。 在我看來，領導力並不是一種天生技能；相反，它是一種透過訓練、經驗和自我覺察而發展出來的實用能力。 公司在挑選經理時，通常也會尋找情緒智商、良好判斷力和可靠性。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"Leadership should not be seen as something people are simply born with. Although some individuals may naturally appear more confident or charismatic, these qualities alone do not make them effective leaders. Real leadership involves listening carefully, resolving conflict, setting clear expectations and helping others perform well under pressure. These abilities are usually built through repeated exposure to difficult situations. For example, a junior employee who gradually learns how to handle dissatisfied clients, support weaker colleagues and organise team projects may become a far stronger leader than someone who merely has a naturally dominant personality. In this sense, leadership is less like a gift and more like a muscle: it becomes stronger when it is trained, tested and corrected.","chinese":"領導力不應被視為人們只是天生便擁有的東西。 儘管有些人可能天生看起來更有自信或更有魅力，但單靠這些特質並不能使他們成為有效的領導者。 真正的領導力包括仔細聆聽、解決衝突、設定清晰期望，以及幫助他人在壓力下有良好表現。 這些能力通常是透過反覆面對困難情況而建立起來的。 例如，一位初級員工如果逐漸學會如何處理不滿的客戶、支援能力較弱的同事，以及組織團隊項目，可能會比一個只是天生性格強勢的人，成為更出色的領導者。 從這個意義上說，領導力與其說像一份天賦，不如說更像一塊肌肉：當它被訓練、考驗和修正時，它就會變得更強。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"Apart from leadership, companies usually want managers who can understand people and make balanced decisions. Emotional intelligence is essential because a manager who cannot read the mood of a team may create unnecessary tension, even if their technical knowledge is excellent. A good manager must know when to encourage, when to challenge and when to step back. In addition, firms look for integrity and accountability. Managers often control budgets, evaluate staff and communicate sensitive information, so they must be trusted to act fairly rather than protect their own interests. Without these qualities, a manager may become efficient on paper but harmful in practice.","chinese":"除了領導力之外，公司通常希望經理能夠理解他人，並作出平衡的決定。 情緒智商是必不可少的，因為一位無法察覺團隊氣氛的經理，即使技術知識很出色，也可能製造不必要的緊張。 一位好的經理必須知道何時應該鼓勵、何時應該提出挑戰，以及何時應該退一步。 此外，企業也會尋找誠信和問責能力。 經理經常掌管預算、評估員工，並傳達敏感資訊，因此他們必須被信任會公平行事，而不是保護自己的利益。 如果沒有這些品質，一位經理可能在表面上顯得有效率，但在實際工作中卻會造成傷害"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, leadership is not an inborn talent but a skill shaped by experience and deliberate improvement. For this reason, companies rightly assess personality as well as knowledge, especially qualities such as empathy, judgement, integrity and responsibility.","chinese":"總結來說，領導力並不是一種天生才能，而是一種由經驗和有意識的改進所塑造的技能 基於這個原因，公司不只評估知識，也評估性格是合理的，尤其是同理心、判斷力、誠信和責任感等品質。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"management interviews","chinese":"管理層面試"},{"english":"examine far more than","chinese":"考核的遠不止……"},{"english":"technical competence","chinese":"技術能力"},{"english":"be expected to","chinese":"被期望要……"},{"english":"influence people","chinese":"影響他人"},{"english":"make decisions","chinese":"作出決定"},{"english":"represent the values of","chinese":"代表……的價值觀"},{"english":"an organisation","chinese":"一個機構"},{"english":"an innate skill","chinese":"天生技能"},{"english":"a practical ability","chinese":"實際能力"},{"english":"developed through","chinese":"透過……培養出來"},{"english":"self-awareness","chinese":"自我覺察"},{"english":"tend to look for","chinese":"傾向尋找"},{"english":"emotional intelligence","chinese":"情緒智商"},{"english":"sound judgement","chinese":"良好的判斷力"},{"english":"reliability","chinese":"可靠性"},{"english":"be seen as","chinese":"被視為"},{"english":"be born with","chinese":"與生俱來"},{"english":"appear more confident","chinese":"顯得更有信心"},{"english":"charismatic","chinese":"有魅力的"},{"english":"these qualities alone","chinese":"單靠這些特質"},{"english":"effective leaders","chinese":"有效的領袖"},{"english":"real leadership involves","chinese":"真正的領導力包括"},{"english":"listening carefully","chinese":"細心聆聽"},{"english":"resolving conflict","chinese":"解決衝突"},{"english":"setting clear expectations","chinese":"訂立清晰期望"},{"english":"perform well under pressure","chinese":"在壓力下表現良好"},{"english":"repeated exposure to","chinese":"反覆接觸……"},{"english":"difficult situations","chinese":"困難情況"},{"english":"a junior employee","chinese":"初級員工"},{"english":"gradually learns how to","chinese":"逐漸學會如何……"},{"english":"handle dissatisfied clients","chinese":"處理不滿的客戶"},{"english":"support weaker colleagues","chinese":"支援能力較弱的同事"},{"english":"organise team projects","chinese":"組織團隊項目"},{"english":"a far stronger leader","chinese":"強得多的領袖"},{"english":"naturally dominant personality","chinese":"天生強勢的性格"},{"english":"in this sense","chinese":"從這個意義上說"},{"english":"less like a gift and more like","chinese":"與其說像……，不如說像……"},{"english":"trained, tested and corrected","chinese":"經過訓練、考驗和修正"},{"english":"apart from leadership","chinese":"除了領導力之外"},{"english":"understand people","chinese":"理解人"},{"english":"make balanced decisions","chinese":"作出平衡的決定"},{"english":"is essential because","chinese":"……是必要的，因為"},{"english":"read the mood of","chinese":"察覺……的氣氛"},{"english":"create unnecessary tension","chinese":"製造不必要的緊張氣氛"},{"english":"technical knowledge","chinese":"專業知識"},{"english":"know when to","chinese":"知道何時應該……"},{"english":"step back","chinese":"退一步；放手"},{"english":"in addition","chinese":"此外"},{"english":"look for integrity and accountability","chinese":"尋找誠信和問責精神"},{"english":"control budgets","chinese":"管理預算"},{"english":"evaluate staff","chinese":"評核職員"},{"english":"communicate sensitive information","chinese":"傳達敏感資料"},{"english":"be trusted to act fairly","chinese":"被信任會公平行事"},{"english":"protect their own interests","chinese":"保護自己的利益"},{"english":"efficient on paper","chinese":"表面上有效率"},{"english":"harmful in practice","chinese":"實際上有害"},{"english":"an inborn talent","chinese":"天生才能"},{"english":"shaped by experience","chinese":"由經驗塑造"},{"english":"deliberate improvement","chinese":"有意識的改進"},{"english":"rightly assess","chinese":"正確地評估"},{"english":"personality as well as knowledge","chinese":"性格以及知識"},{"english":"qualities such as","chinese":"例如……的素質"},{"english":"empathy","chinese":"同理心"},{"english":"judgement, integrity and responsibility","chinese":"判斷力、誠信和責任感"}]},"model-essay-8-ielts-discuss-both-views":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-8-ielts-discuss-both-views","essayKey":"discuss-both-views:8","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-8-ielts-discuss-both-views","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/discuss-both-views-your-opinion/EdmundBd9ExpBth-Q8","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"Happiness at different stages of life is often debated. Some people believe that teenagers enjoy a happier life than adults, while others argue that adulthood offers a deeper and more stable form of happiness. In my view, adults are generally happier because they have greater independence and a clearer sense of direction.","chinese":"人生不同階段的幸福感經常受到討論。有些人認為青少年的生活比成年人更快樂，而另一些人則認為成年生活能帶來更深層、更穩定的幸福感。 在我看來，成年人通常更快樂，因為他們擁有更大的獨立性和更清晰的人生方向。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"On the one hand, teenagers may appear happier because their lives are usually less burdened by serious responsibilities. Many of them do not have to pay bills, support a family, or make major financial decisions, so they can spend more time on friendships, hobbies, entertainment, and personal interests. For example, a secondary school student may finish classes and then play sports, chat with friends, or watch films without worrying about rent or job security. This freedom can make teenage life feel light and enjoyable. In this sense, adolescence can seem like a carefree period, especially when compared with the pressure-filled world of work and family duties.","chinese":"一方面，青少年可能看起來更快樂，因為他們的生活通常較少受到重大責任的負擔 他們當中許多人不需要支付帳單、養家，或作出重大的財務決定，因此可以把更多時間花在友誼、興趣、娛樂和個人喜好上。 例如，一名中學生放學後可以去做運動、和朋友聊天，或看電影，而不必擔心租金或工作穩定性。 這種自由能使青少年生活感覺輕鬆而愉快。 從這個意義上說，青春期可能看起來像是一段無憂無慮的時期，尤其是與充滿工作和家庭責任壓力的成人世界相比。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"On the other hand, I believe adults are happier overall because their happiness is often built on independence, achievement, and emotional maturity. Adults can choose where to live, what career to pursue, how to spend their money, and who to build relationships with. These choices give them control over their lives, which is a powerful source of satisfaction. Moreover, adults are usually better at understanding themselves and dealing with problems. For instance, an adult who has worked hard to develop a career or support a family may feel a strong sense of purpose that teenagers rarely experience. Although adult life can be stressful, that stress is often balanced by meaningful rewards.","chinese":"另一方面，我認為成年人整體上更快樂，因為他們的幸福感往往建立在獨立、成就和情感成熟之上。 成年人可以選擇住在哪裡、追求甚麼職業、如何使用金錢，以及與誰建立關係。 這些選擇讓他們能掌控自己的生活，而這是一種強大的滿足感來源。 此外，成年人通常更擅長了解自己和處理問題。 例如，一名努力發展事業或支撐家庭的成年人，可能會感受到一種青少年很少經歷到的強烈人生目標感。 雖然成年生活可能充滿壓力，但這種壓力往往會被有意義的回報所平衡。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, teenagers may have more free time and fewer responsibilities, which can make them seem happier on the surface. However, I believe adults are generally happier because their lives contain more independence, purpose, and lasting fulfillment. Happiness is not just the absence of pressure; it is also the feeling that one’s life has direction and meaning.","chinese":"總結來說，青少年可能有更多自由時間和較少責任，這使他們表面上看起來更快樂。 然而，我認為成年人通常更快樂，因為他們的生活包含更多獨立性、目標感和持久的滿足。 幸福不只是沒有壓力；它也是一種感覺，即一個人的人生具有方向和意義。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"different stages of life","chinese":"人生不同階段"},{"english":"is often debated","chinese":"經常受到討論"},{"english":"teenagers enjoy a happier life","chinese":"青少年享有更快樂的生活"},{"english":"adulthood offers","chinese":"成年階段提供"},{"english":"a deeper and more stable form of","chinese":"更深層、更穩定的……形式"},{"english":"In my view","chinese":"在我看來"},{"english":"generally happier","chinese":"整體上更快樂"},{"english":"greater independence","chinese":"更大的獨立性"},{"english":"a clearer sense of direction","chinese":"更清晰的方向感"},{"english":"On the one hand","chinese":"一方面"},{"english":"may appear happier","chinese":"可能看起來更快樂"},{"english":"less burdened by","chinese":"較少受……負擔"},{"english":"serious responsibilities","chinese":"重大責任"},{"english":"pay bills","chinese":"交帳單"},{"english":"support a family","chinese":"養家"},{"english":"make major financial decisions","chinese":"作出重大財務決定"},{"english":"spend more time on","chinese":"花更多時間在……上"},{"english":"personal interests","chinese":"個人興趣"},{"english":"a secondary school student","chinese":"中學生"},{"english":"finish classes","chinese":"完成課堂"},{"english":"chat with friends","chinese":"和朋友聊天"},{"english":"without worrying about","chinese":"不用擔心"},{"english":"rent","chinese":"租金"},{"english":"job security","chinese":"工作保障"},{"english":"feel light and enjoyable","chinese":"感覺輕鬆愉快"},{"english":"In this sense","chinese":"從這個意義上說"},{"english":"adolescence","chinese":"青春期；青少年階段"},{"english":"a carefree period","chinese":"無憂無慮的時期"},{"english":"especially when compared with","chinese":"特別是與……相比時"},{"english":"pressure-filled","chinese":"充滿壓力的"},{"english":"the world of work","chinese":"職場世界"},{"english":"family duties","chinese":"家庭責任"},{"english":"On the other hand","chinese":"另一方面"},{"english":"happier overall","chinese":"整體上更快樂"},{"english":"built on independence","chinese":"建基於獨立"},{"english":"achievement","chinese":"成就"},{"english":"emotional maturity","chinese":"情緒成熟"},{"english":"choose where to live","chinese":"選擇住在哪裏"},{"english":"what career to pursue","chinese":"追求甚麼事業"},{"english":"how to spend their money","chinese":"如何花錢"},{"english":"build relationships with","chinese":"與……建立關係"},{"english":"give them control over","chinese":"讓他們掌控"},{"english":"control over their lives","chinese":"對自己生活的掌控"},{"english":"a powerful source of satisfaction","chinese":"強大的滿足感來源"},{"english":"Moreover","chinese":"此外"},{"english":"better at understanding themselves","chinese":"更擅長了解自己"},{"english":"dealing with problems","chinese":"處理問題"},{"english":"For instance","chinese":"例如"},{"english":"worked hard to","chinese":"努力去"},{"english":"develop a career","chinese":"發展事業"},{"english":"support a family","chinese":"養家"},{"english":"a strong sense of purpose","chinese":"強烈的目標感"},{"english":"rarely experience","chinese":"很少經歷"},{"english":"adult life","chinese":"成年生活"},{"english":"be stressful","chinese":"有壓力"},{"english":"balanced by","chinese":"由……平衡"},{"english":"meaningful rewards","chinese":"有意義的回報"},{"english":"free time","chinese":"空閒時間"},{"english":"fewer responsibilities","chinese":"較少責任"},{"english":"on the surface","chinese":"表面上"},{"english":"However","chinese":"然而"},{"english":"contain more independence","chinese":"包含更多獨立性"},{"english":"lasting fulfilment","chinese":"持久的滿足感"},{"english":"the absence of pressure","chinese":"沒有壓力"},{"english":"one's life has direction and meaning","chinese":"自己的人生有方向和意義"}]},"model-essay-8-ielts-opinion":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-8-ielts-opinion","essayKey":"opinion:8","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-8-ielts-opinion","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/opinions/EdmundBd9OP-Q8","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"In competitive markets, even products that genuinely solve consumers’ problems do not automatically sell themselves. Some people therefore argue that advertising is unnecessary if a product is already high-quality and useful. This essay completely disagrees, because advertising is still essential both for informing consumers and for helping good products gain credibility in crowded markets.","chinese":"在競爭激烈的市場中，即使產品確實能解決消費者的問題，也不會自然而然地自行暢銷 因此，有些人認為，如果一項產品本身已經品質優良而且實用，廣告便沒有必要。 本文完全不同意這種看法，因為廣告在向消費者提供資訊，以及幫助優質產品在選擇繁多、競爭激烈的市場中建立可信度這兩方面，仍然至關重要。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"The first reason advertising remains necessary is that consumers cannot choose a product they have never encountered. In most industries, buyers face countless similar options and do not have time to research each one independently. Advertising therefore performs an informative function: it tells people what a product does, who it is for, how it differs from rival goods and where it can be bought. Without this information, even an excellent product may remain invisible, meaning consumer needs are not met in practice. For example, a small company may produce an energy-efficient washing machine that cuts electricity bills and lasts longer than competing models, yet many households will still buy familiar brands if they never hear about this better alternative.","chinese":"廣告之所以仍然有其必要，第一個原因在於：消費者不可能選擇一項自己從未接觸過的產品。 在大多數行業中，買家面對的是無數相似的選擇，並沒有時間逐一獨立研究每一項產品。 因此，廣告發揮了資訊傳遞的功能：它告訴人們產品有甚麼用途、適合哪些人、與競爭商品有何不同，以及可以在哪裡購買。 若缺乏這些資訊，即使是一項優秀的產品，也可能一直不被看見，這意味着消費者的需要在實際上無法得到滿足。 例如，一家小公司也許生產出一款節能洗衣機，不但能降低電費開支，而且比競爭對手的型號更耐用；然而，如果許多家庭從未聽說過這個更好的替代選項，他們仍然會購買自己熟悉的品牌。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"Advertising is also necessary because quality alone does not remove perceived risk. When a brand is unfamiliar, consumers may still worry about reliability, safety or after-sales service, even if the product itself is highly effective. Advertising reduces this hesitation by showing demonstrations, guarantees, certifications and consistent brand messages, all of which make a company appear more credible. For instance, a start-up producing safer baby bottles may be overlooked until its advertising explains the materials used, the testing standards met and the refund policy offered.","chinese":"廣告之所以同樣必要，是因為單憑品質本身，並不能消除消費者主觀感受到的風險。 當一個品牌並不為人熟悉時，即使產品本身十分有效，消費者仍可能擔心它的可靠性、安全性或售後服務。 廣告透過展示產品示範、保證、認證，以及一致的品牌訊息，來減少這種猶豫；而這一切都能使一家公司顯得更具可信性。 例如，一家生產更安全奶瓶的新創公司，可能一直被人忽視，直到它的廣告清楚說明所採用的材料、符合的測試標準，以及所提供的退款政策為止。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, I completely disagree that advertising becomes unnecessary when a product is good. However useful a product may be, consumers still need information and reassurance, and without advertising many excellent goods would remain unnoticed and untrusted.","chinese":"總而言之，我完全不同意「只要產品優良，廣告便變得沒有必要」這種說法。 無論一項產品多麼實用，消費者仍然需要資訊與安心感；若沒有廣告，許多優秀的商品都會繼續無人注意，也難以獲得信任。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"in competitive markets","chinese":"在競爭激烈的市場中"},{"english":"genuinely solve consumers' problems","chinese":"真正解決消費者的問題"},{"english":"automatically sell themselves","chinese":"自動賣出；自然有人買"},{"english":"some people therefore argue that","chinese":"因此有些人認為"},{"english":"advertising is unnecessary","chinese":"廣告是不必要的"},{"english":"high-quality and useful","chinese":"高質素而實用"},{"english":"completely disagrees","chinese":"完全不同意"},{"english":"be still essential","chinese":"仍然必要"},{"english":"informing consumers","chinese":"向消費者提供資料"},{"english":"helping good products gain credibility","chinese":"幫助好產品建立可信度"},{"english":"gain credibility","chinese":"建立可信度"},{"english":"crowded markets","chinese":"擁擠的市場；競爭激烈的市場"},{"english":"the first reason","chinese":"第一個原因"},{"english":"remains necessary","chinese":"仍然必要"},{"english":"choose a product","chinese":"選擇產品"},{"english":"have never encountered","chinese":"從未接觸過"},{"english":"in most industries","chinese":"在大多數行業中"},{"english":"face countless similar options","chinese":"面對無數相似選擇"},{"english":"research each one independently","chinese":"獨立研究每一個"},{"english":"perform an informative function","chinese":"發揮提供資訊的功能"},{"english":"what a product does","chinese":"產品的用途"},{"english":"who it is for","chinese":"適合哪些人"},{"english":"differs from rival goods","chinese":"與競爭產品不同"},{"english":"rival goods","chinese":"競爭產品"},{"english":"where it can be bought","chinese":"可以在哪裏購買"},{"english":"without this information","chinese":"沒有這些資料"},{"english":"remain invisible","chinese":"仍然不被看見"},{"english":"consumer needs are not met","chinese":"消費者需要未被滿足"},{"english":"in practice","chinese":"在實際情況中"},{"english":"a small company","chinese":"小型公司"},{"english":"energy-efficient","chinese":"節能的"},{"english":"washing machine","chinese":"洗衣機"},{"english":"cut electricity bills","chinese":"減少電費"},{"english":"last longer than","chinese":"比……更耐用"},{"english":"competing models","chinese":"競爭型號"},{"english":"familiar brands","chinese":"熟悉的品牌"},{"english":"hear about","chinese":"聽說；得知"},{"english":"a better alternative","chinese":"更好的替代選擇"},{"english":"quality alone","chinese":"單靠質素"},{"english":"remove perceived risk","chinese":"消除感知風險"},{"english":"perceived risk","chinese":"感知風險"},{"english":"an unfamiliar brand","chinese":"不熟悉的品牌"},{"english":"worry about reliability","chinese":"擔心可靠性"},{"english":"after-sales service","chinese":"售後服務"},{"english":"the product itself","chinese":"產品本身"},{"english":"highly effective","chinese":"非常有效"},{"english":"reduce this hesitation","chinese":"減少這種猶豫"},{"english":"showing demonstrations","chinese":"展示示範"},{"english":"guarantees","chinese":"保證"},{"english":"certifications","chinese":"認證"},{"english":"consistent brand messages","chinese":"一致的品牌訊息"},{"english":"appear more credible","chinese":"顯得更可信"},{"english":"a start-up","chinese":"初創公司"},{"english":"safer baby bottles","chinese":"更安全的奶瓶"},{"english":"be overlooked","chinese":"被忽視"},{"english":"the materials used","chinese":"所使用的材料"},{"english":"the testing standards met","chinese":"符合的測試標準"},{"english":"the refund policy offered","chinese":"所提供的退款政策"},{"english":"become unnecessary","chinese":"變得不必要"},{"english":"however useful a product may be","chinese":"無論產品多有用"},{"english":"need information and reassurance","chinese":"需要資料和安心感"},{"english":"remain unnoticed and untrusted","chinese":"仍然無人注意和不被信任"}]},"model-essay-8-ielts-task1-bar-charts":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-8-ielts-task1-bar-charts","essayKey":"bar-charts:8","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-8-ielts-task1-bar-charts","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-1/bar-charts/bar-chart-8","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"The bar chart compares the total duration of telephone calls made in the UK, measured in billions of minutes, across three categories between 1995 and 2002.","chinese":"這張柱狀圖比較了 1995 年至 2002 年間英國三類電話通話的總時長，單位為十億分鐘。"},{"label":"Overview","english":"Overall, local fixed-line calls remained the largest category throughout, despite rising to a peak in the late 1990s and then returning to their initial level. By contrast, national and international fixed-line calls increased steadily, while mobile calls, though starting from a very low base, recorded by far the sharpest growth.","chinese":"整體而言，本地固定電話通話在整段期間一直是最大類別，雖然其通話時長在 1990 年代末升至高點，之後又回到起初水平。 相比之下，國內及國際固定電話通話穩定上升；而流動電話通話雖然起點非常低，卻錄得遠遠最顯著的增長。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"In 1995, local fixed-line calls accounted for about 72 billion minutes, almost twice the figure for national and international calls, at roughly 37 billion. The local category then climbed each year to around 90 billion minutes in 1998 and 1999, before falling back gradually to about 72 billion by 2002.","chinese":"在 1995 年，本地固定電話通話約佔 720 億分鐘，幾乎是國內及國際固定電話通話的兩倍，後者約為 370 億分鐘。 之後，本地通話類別逐年上升，在 1998 年和 1999 年達到約 900 億分鐘，然後逐步回落，到 2002 年降至約 720 億分鐘。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"The other two categories both followed upward trends. National and international fixed-line calls rose consistently from approximately 37 billion minutes in 1995 to just over 60 billion in 2002. Mobile calls showed a much more dramatic pattern: after increasing only modestly from about 3 to 12 billion minutes between 1995 and 1999, they surged to roughly 25 billion in 2000 and reached around 45 billion by the final year.","chinese":"其餘兩個類別都呈現上升趨勢。 國內及國際固定電話通話由 1995 年的約 370 億分鐘穩定上升至 2002 年的略高於 600 億分鐘。 流動電話通話則呈現更加顯著的變化：在 1995 年至 1999 年間，它只由約 30 億分鐘溫和上升至 120 億分鐘，但在 2000 年急升至約 250 億分鐘，並在最後一年達到約 450 億分鐘。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"the total duration of telephone calls","chinese":"電話通話總時長"},{"english":"telephone calls made in the UK","chinese":"在英國撥打的電話"},{"english":"measured in billions of minutes","chinese":"以十億分鐘計"},{"english":"across three categories","chinese":"涵蓋三個類別"},{"english":"between 1995 and 2002","chinese":"在1995年至2002年間"},{"english":"local fixed-line calls","chinese":"本地固網電話"},{"english":"remained the largest category throughout","chinese":"全期一直是最大類別"},{"english":"despite rising to a peak","chinese":"儘管升至高峰"},{"english":"rising to a peak","chinese":"上升至高峰"},{"english":"in the late 1990s","chinese":"在1990年代後期"},{"english":"returning to their initial level","chinese":"回到最初水平"},{"english":"their initial level","chinese":"最初水平"},{"english":"By contrast","chinese":"相比之下"},{"english":"national and international fixed-line calls","chinese":"國內及國際固網電話"},{"english":"increased steadily","chinese":"穩步上升"},{"english":"mobile calls","chinese":"流動電話通話"},{"english":"starting from a very low base","chinese":"從很低的基數開始"},{"english":"a very low base","chinese":"很低的基數"},{"english":"recorded by far the sharpest growth","chinese":"錄得遠遠最急劇的增長"},{"english":"by far the sharpest growth","chinese":"遠遠最急劇的增長"},{"english":"accounted for about 72 billion minutes","chinese":"佔約720億分鐘"},{"english":"almost twice the figure for","chinese":"幾乎是……數字的兩倍"},{"english":"the figure for national and international calls","chinese":"國內及國際電話的數字"},{"english":"at roughly 37 billion","chinese":"約為370億"},{"english":"the local category","chinese":"本地類別"},{"english":"climbed each year","chinese":"每年上升"},{"english":"around 90 billion minutes","chinese":"約900億分鐘"},{"english":"before falling back gradually","chinese":"隨後逐步回落"},{"english":"falling back gradually","chinese":"逐步回落"},{"english":"to about 72 billion by 2002","chinese":"到2002年回落至約720億"},{"english":"the other two categories","chinese":"其餘兩個類別"},{"english":"followed upward trends","chinese":"呈上升趨勢"},{"english":"rose consistently from","chinese":"由……持續上升"},{"english":"approximately 37 billion minutes","chinese":"約370億分鐘"},{"english":"to just over 60 billion","chinese":"至略高於600億"},{"english":"just over 60 billion","chinese":"略高於600億"},{"english":"showed a much more dramatic pattern","chinese":"呈現更急劇的走勢"},{"english":"a much more dramatic pattern","chinese":"急劇得多的走勢"},{"english":"after increasing only modestly","chinese":"在起初只輕微上升後"},{"english":"increasing only modestly","chinese":"只輕微上升"},{"english":"from about 3 to 12 billion minutes","chinese":"由約30億增至120億分鐘"},{"english":"between 1995 and 1999","chinese":"在1995年至1999年間"},{"english":"surged to roughly 25 billion","chinese":"急升至約250億"},{"english":"reached around 45 billion","chinese":"達到約450億"},{"english":"by the final year","chinese":"到最後一年"}]},"model-essay-8-ielts-task1-line-graph":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-8-ielts-task1-line-graph","essayKey":"line-graph:8","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-8-ielts-task1-line-graph","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-1/line-graphs/line-graph-8","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"The line graph illustrates the amount of energy consumed in the United States from six fuel sources between 1980 and 2030, measured in quadrillion units, with later figures projected.","chinese":"該折線圖說明了 1980 年至 2030 年間美國六種燃料來源的能源消耗量，單位為千萬億單位，後期數據為預測值。"},{"label":"Overview","english":"Overall, petrol and oil remained, and are expected to remain, the dominant fuel source. Coal and natural gas formed a second tier, though coal is projected to overtake gas after about 2015, while nuclear, solar/wind and hydropower accounted for only small amounts throughout.","chinese":"整體而言，汽油和石油一直是、並預計仍將是最主要的燃料來源。 煤和天然氣構成第二梯隊，不過煤預計在約 2015 年後超越天然氣；相反，核能、太陽能／風能和水電在整段期間的消耗量都很小。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"In 1980, petrol and oil consumption stood at around 35 quadrillion units, compared with about 20 for natural gas and 16 for coal. After dipping to just over 30 in the mid-1980s, petrol and oil rose steadily, reaching roughly 40 by 2005 and a projected 49 by 2030. Coal followed a gentler upward path, increasing to about 22 in the mid-1990s, remaining close to that level for several years, and then rising to approximately 32 by the end. Natural gas fluctuated around the low twenties before leveling off at about 25 from 2015 onwards.","chinese":"1980 年，汽油和石油的消耗量約為 35 千萬億單位，相比之下，天然氣約為 20 ，煤約為 16 。 在 1980 年代中期下降至略高於 30 後，汽油和石油的消耗量穩步上升，到 2005年達到約 40 ，並預計到 2030 年達到 49 。 煤的上升趨勢較為溫和，在 1990 年代中期增至約 22 ，之後數年保持在接近該水平，最後升至約 32 。 天然氣在二十出頭的水平附近波動，之後從 2015 年起穩定在約 25 。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"The remaining fuels were much less significant. Nuclear power climbed gradually from around 4 to about 8–9 units. Solar/wind also rose modestly to around 6, whereas hydropower fluctuated slightly and finished at roughly 4.","chinese":"其餘燃料的消耗量明顯小得多。 核能由約 4 逐漸上升至約 8 至 9 個單位。 太陽能／風能也溫和上升至約 6 ；相反，水電只是輕微波動，最後約為 4 。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"line graph","chinese":"折線圖"},{"english":"illustrates the amount of","chinese":"顯示……的數量"},{"english":"energy consumed","chinese":"所消耗的能源"},{"english":"fuel sources","chinese":"燃料來源"},{"english":"between 1980 and 2030","chinese":"在1980年至2030年間"},{"english":"measured in quadrillion units","chinese":"以千萬億單位計算"},{"english":"quadrillion units","chinese":"千萬億單位"},{"english":"with later figures projected","chinese":"後期數字為預測"},{"english":"projected","chinese":"預測的"},{"english":"petrol and oil","chinese":"汽油及石油"},{"english":"remained, and are expected to remain","chinese":"一直是，並預料仍會是"},{"english":"the dominant fuel source","chinese":"主要燃料來源"},{"english":"coal","chinese":"煤"},{"english":"natural gas","chinese":"天然氣"},{"english":"formed a second tier","chinese":"構成第二梯隊"},{"english":"second tier","chinese":"第二梯隊"},{"english":"is projected to overtake","chinese":"預計會超越"},{"english":"overtake gas","chinese":"超越天然氣"},{"english":"after about 2015","chinese":"約2015年後"},{"english":"nuclear","chinese":"核能"},{"english":"solar/wind","chinese":"太陽能／風能"},{"english":"hydropower","chinese":"水力發電"},{"english":"accounted for only small amounts","chinese":"只佔少量"},{"english":"small amounts","chinese":"少量"},{"english":"throughout","chinese":"在整段期間"},{"english":"consumption stood at around","chinese":"消耗量約為"},{"english":"stood at around","chinese":"約為"},{"english":"compared with about","chinese":"與約……相比"},{"english":"after dipping to","chinese":"在跌至……後"},{"english":"dipping to","chinese":"下跌至"},{"english":"just over 30","chinese":"略高於30"},{"english":"in the mid-1980s","chinese":"在1980年代中期"},{"english":"rose steadily","chinese":"穩步上升"},{"english":"reaching roughly 40","chinese":"達到約40"},{"english":"by 2005","chinese":"到2005年時"},{"english":"a projected 49","chinese":"預測為49"},{"english":"by 2030","chinese":"到2030年時"},{"english":"followed a gentler upward path","chinese":"呈現較溫和的上升走勢"},{"english":"gentler upward path","chinese":"較溫和的上升走勢"},{"english":"increasing to about","chinese":"增至約"},{"english":"in the mid-1990s","chinese":"在1990年代中期"},{"english":"remaining close to that level","chinese":"維持接近該水平"},{"english":"that level","chinese":"該水平"},{"english":"for several years","chinese":"數年間"},{"english":"rising to approximately","chinese":"上升至約"},{"english":"by the end","chinese":"到期末時"},{"english":"fluctuated around","chinese":"在……附近波動"},{"english":"the low twenties","chinese":"二十出頭"},{"english":"before leveling off at","chinese":"之後在……趨於平穩"},{"english":"leveling off","chinese":"趨於平穩"},{"english":"from 2015 onwards","chinese":"從2015年起"},{"english":"the remaining fuels","chinese":"其餘燃料"},{"english":"much less significant","chinese":"重要性低得多"},{"english":"nuclear power","chinese":"核能"},{"english":"climbed gradually","chinese":"逐步上升"},{"english":"from around 4 to about 8–9 units","chinese":"由約4升至約8至9單位"},{"english":"rose modestly","chinese":"溫和上升"},{"english":"to around 6","chinese":"至約6"},{"english":"whereas","chinese":"而；相比之下"},{"english":"fluctuated slightly","chinese":"輕微波動"},{"english":"finished at roughly","chinese":"最後約為"},{"english":"roughly 4","chinese":"約4"},{"english":"energy consumption","chinese":"能源消耗"},{"english":"long-term projection","chinese":"長期預測"},{"english":"upward trend","chinese":"上升趨勢"},{"english":"steady increase","chinese":"穩定增長"}]},"model-essay-8-ielts-task1-maps":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-8-ielts-task1-maps","essayKey":"maps:8","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-8-ielts-task1-maps","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-1/maps/maps-8","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"The two plans illustrate the current layout of a university sports centre and its proposed redevelopment.","chinese":"這兩張平面圖說明一所大學體育中心目前的布局，以及其擬議重建後的樣。"},{"label":"Overview","english":"Overall, the centre is expected to expand westwards and eastwards, replacing both outdoor court areas with indoor facilities. The existing central core, including the 25-metre pool, reception, original changing room and seating area, will remain largely unchanged, while the gym will be enlarged and new leisure and commercial amenities will be added.","chinese":"整體而言，該中心預計會向西和向東擴展，並用室內設施取代兩側的戶外球場區。 現有的中央核心區，包括 25 米泳池、接待處、原有更衣室和座位區，將大致保持不變；同時，健身房會擴大，並會增設新的休閒和商業設施。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"At present, the sports centre consists of a compact rectangular building. A 25-metre pool occupies the middle, with a gym directly to its north. On the western side of the pool there is a changing room, whereas seating is located to the east. The reception area stands at the southern entrance, and the building is flanked by outdoor courts on both sides.","chinese":"目前，該體育中心由一座緊湊的矩形建築組成。 一個 25 米泳池位於中間，其正北方是健身房。 泳池西側設有更衣室，而座位區位於東側。 接待處位於南面的入口處，而建築兩側各有一片戶外球場。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"After redevelopment, the western courts will be replaced by a large leisure pool, with an additional changing room and a sports shop to its south. On the eastern side, the courts will give way to a sports hall, two dance studios, a café and another changing room. The gym will also be extended across the northern part of the complex.","chinese":"重建後，西側球場將被一個大型休閒泳池取代，其南面會新增一間更衣室和一間體育用品商店。 在東側，球場將讓位給一個體育館、兩間舞蹈室、一間咖啡廳和另一間更衣室。 健身房也將沿著建築群北部擴建。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"illustrate the current layout of","chinese":"展示……的現時佈局"},{"english":"the current layout","chinese":"現時佈局"},{"english":"a university sports centre","chinese":"大學體育中心"},{"english":"its proposed redevelopment","chinese":"其擬議重建"},{"english":"proposed redevelopment","chinese":"擬議重建"},{"english":"is expected to","chinese":"預計會"},{"english":"expand westwards and eastwards","chinese":"向西及向東擴展"},{"english":"replacing X with Y","chinese":"以Y取代X"},{"english":"outdoor court areas","chinese":"戶外球場區"},{"english":"indoor facilities","chinese":"室內設施"},{"english":"the existing central core","chinese":"現有中央核心區"},{"english":"including","chinese":"包括"},{"english":"25-metre pool","chinese":"25米泳池"},{"english":"reception","chinese":"接待處"},{"english":"original changing room","chinese":"原有更衣室"},{"english":"seating area","chinese":"座位區"},{"english":"remain largely unchanged","chinese":"大致保持不變"},{"english":"while","chinese":"而；同時"},{"english":"the gym will be enlarged","chinese":"健身室將會擴大"},{"english":"leisure and commercial amenities","chinese":"休閒及商業設施"},{"english":"will be added","chinese":"將會增設"},{"english":"at present","chinese":"目前"},{"english":"consists of","chinese":"由……組成"},{"english":"a compact rectangular building","chinese":"緊湊的長方形建築"},{"english":"occupies the middle","chinese":"佔據中央位置"},{"english":"directly to its north","chinese":"就在其北面"},{"english":"on the western side of","chinese":"在……西面"},{"english":"whereas","chinese":"而；相反"},{"english":"be located to the east","chinese":"位於東面"},{"english":"the reception area","chinese":"接待區"},{"english":"stands at the southern entrance","chinese":"位於南面入口"},{"english":"the southern entrance","chinese":"南面入口"},{"english":"be flanked by","chinese":"兩側有……"},{"english":"on both sides","chinese":"在兩邊"},{"english":"after redevelopment","chinese":"重建後"},{"english":"the western courts","chinese":"西面的球場"},{"english":"will be replaced by","chinese":"將會被……取代"},{"english":"a large leisure pool","chinese":"大型休閒泳池"},{"english":"an additional changing room","chinese":"額外更衣室"},{"english":"a sports shop","chinese":"體育用品店"},{"english":"to its south","chinese":"在其南面"},{"english":"on the eastern side","chinese":"在東面"},{"english":"give way to","chinese":"讓位予……；被……取代"},{"english":"a sports hall","chinese":"體育館"},{"english":"dance studios","chinese":"舞蹈室"},{"english":"a café","chinese":"咖啡店"},{"english":"another changing room","chinese":"另一個更衣室"},{"english":"will also be extended","chinese":"亦會擴建"},{"english":"across the northern part","chinese":"橫跨北部"},{"english":"the northern part of the complex","chinese":"綜合建築的北部"},{"english":"the complex","chinese":"綜合建築；綜合設施"},{"english":"both outdoor courts","chinese":"兩邊戶外球場"},{"english":"be converted into indoor space","chinese":"被改造成室內空間"},{"english":"new facilities will be introduced","chinese":"將會引入新設施"},{"english":"the central section","chinese":"中央部分"},{"english":"the western extension","chinese":"西面擴建部分"},{"english":"the eastern extension","chinese":"東面擴建部分"},{"english":"the redeveloped centre","chinese":"重建後的體育中心"}]},"model-essay-8-ielts-task1-process-diagram":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-8-ielts-task1-process-diagram","essayKey":"process-diagram:8","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-8-ielts-task1-process-diagram","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-1/process-diagrams/process-diagram-8","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"The diagrams illustrate the life cycle of the salmon, showing the habitats, durations and sizes associated with its main developmental stages.","chinese":"這些圖表說明鮭魚的生命週期，展示其主要發育階段所對應的棲息地、所需時間和體型大小。"},{"label":"Overview","english":"Overall, salmon pass through three named growth stages—fry, smolt and adult salmon—and move from freshwater rivers to the open sea before returning upstream to reproduce. The cycle lasts roughly nine and a half years, with the longest period spent in the sea and most growth occurring during the marine phase.","chinese":"整體而言，鮭魚會經歷三個有名稱的成長階段 —— 幼魚、銀鮭幼魚和成年鮭魚，並從淡水河流移往開闊海域，之後再逆流返回繁殖。 整個週期大約持續九年半，其中最長的階段是在海中度過，而大部分體型增長也發生在海洋階段。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"At the beginning, salmon eggs are laid in the upper river, where slow-moving water, reeds and small stones provide the spawning environment. After approximately five to six months, they hatch into fry, measuring only 3–8 cm. These young fish then move downstream to the lower river, a faster-flowing area. They remain there for about four years, growing into smolt of around 12–15 cm.","chinese":"一開始，鮭魚卵被產在上游河段；那裡水流緩慢，並有蘆葦和小石頭，為產卵提供合適環境。 大約五至六個月後，魚卵孵化成幼魚，體長只有三至八厘米。 這些幼魚接著向下游移動，到達水流較快的下游河段。 牠們會在那裡停留大約四年，並成長為體長約十二至十五厘米的銀鮭幼魚。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"Following this freshwater stage, the smolt migrate to the open sea. This is the longest single phase, lasting about five years, during which they develop into adult salmon. By this point, their length has increased markedly to 70–76 cm. Finally, the mature fish swim back to the upper river, where they lay eggs and restart the cycle.","chinese":"在完成這個淡水階段後，銀鮭幼魚會遷徙到開闊海域。 這是最長的單一階段，持續約五年；在此期間，牠們發育成成年鮭魚。 到這個階段，牠們的體長已明顯增加到七十至七十六厘米。 最後，成熟的鮭魚會游回上游河段，在那裡產卵並重新開始整個週期。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"diagrams illustrate","chinese":"圖示說明"},{"english":"life cycle","chinese":"生命週期"},{"english":"the salmon","chinese":"三文魚；鮭魚"},{"english":"habitats","chinese":"棲息地"},{"english":"durations","chinese":"持續時間"},{"english":"sizes associated with","chinese":"與……相關的大小"},{"english":"main developmental stages","chinese":"主要發育階段"},{"english":"pass through","chinese":"經歷"},{"english":"named growth stages","chinese":"具名成長階段"},{"english":"fry","chinese":"幼魚"},{"english":"smolt","chinese":"銀化幼魚"},{"english":"adult salmon","chinese":"成年三文魚；成年鮭魚"},{"english":"freshwater rivers","chinese":"淡水河流"},{"english":"the open sea","chinese":"外海"},{"english":"returning upstream","chinese":"逆流而上返回"},{"english":"reproduce","chinese":"繁殖"},{"english":"lasts roughly","chinese":"大約持續"},{"english":"nine and a half years","chinese":"九年半"},{"english":"the longest period","chinese":"最長時期"},{"english":"spent in the sea","chinese":"在海中度過"},{"english":"most growth occurring during","chinese":"大部分成長發生於……期間"},{"english":"marine phase","chinese":"海洋階段"},{"english":"at the beginning","chinese":"在開始時"},{"english":"salmon eggs","chinese":"三文魚卵；鮭魚卵"},{"english":"are laid in","chinese":"被產於"},{"english":"upper river","chinese":"河流上游"},{"english":"slow-moving water","chinese":"流速緩慢的水"},{"english":"reeds","chinese":"蘆葦"},{"english":"small stones","chinese":"小石"},{"english":"provide the spawning environment","chinese":"提供產卵環境"},{"english":"spawning environment","chinese":"產卵環境"},{"english":"after approximately","chinese":"約……之後"},{"english":"five to six months","chinese":"五至六個月"},{"english":"hatch into fry","chinese":"孵化成幼魚"},{"english":"measuring only","chinese":"只有……長"},{"english":"3–8 cm","chinese":"3至8厘米"},{"english":"young fish","chinese":"幼魚"},{"english":"move downstream","chinese":"順流而下"},{"english":"lower river","chinese":"河流下游"},{"english":"faster-flowing area","chinese":"水流較快的區域"},{"english":"remain there for","chinese":"在那裏停留……"},{"english":"about four years","chinese":"約四年"},{"english":"growing into smolt","chinese":"成長為銀化幼魚"},{"english":"around 12–15 cm","chinese":"約12至15厘米"},{"english":"following this freshwater stage","chinese":"在這個淡水階段之後"},{"english":"freshwater stage","chinese":"淡水階段"},{"english":"migrate to","chinese":"遷移至"},{"english":"longest single phase","chinese":"最長的單一階段"},{"english":"lasting about five years","chinese":"持續約五年"},{"english":"during which","chinese":"在此期間"},{"english":"develop into","chinese":"發育成"},{"english":"by this point","chinese":"到這時"},{"english":"length has increased markedly","chinese":"長度大幅增加"},{"english":"markedly","chinese":"大幅地；明顯地"},{"english":"70–76 cm","chinese":"70至76厘米"},{"english":"mature fish","chinese":"成熟魚類"},{"english":"swim back to","chinese":"游回"},{"english":"lay eggs","chinese":"產卵"},{"english":"restart the cycle","chinese":"重新開始循環"},{"english":"developmental process","chinese":"發育過程"},{"english":"growth phase","chinese":"成長階段"},{"english":"river habitat","chinese":"河流棲息地"},{"english":"sea stage","chinese":"海洋階段"}]},"model-essay-8-ielts-task1-tables":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-8-ielts-task1-tables","essayKey":"tables:8","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-8-ielts-task1-tables","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-1/tables/table-8","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"The table compares the percentage of management posts occupied by women in finance, manufacturing, IT and hospitality in a European country in 2006.","chinese":"該表格比較了 2006 年某歐洲國家中，女性在金融、製造業、資訊科技和酒店款待業所佔管理職位的百分比。"},{"label":"Overview","english":"Overall, women were most strongly represented in hospitality and least represented in manufacturing across the three levels. In addition, their share generally decreased as seniority rose, although hospitality was an exception at the top level, where the proportion of female CEOs slightly exceeded that of female executives.","chinese":"整體而言，在三個職級中，女性在酒店款待業的代表性最高，而在製造業的代表性最低。 此外，女性所佔比例通常隨職級上升而下降；不過，酒店款待業在最高層級是一個例外，女性行政總裁的比例略高於女性行政人員。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"Among managers, hospitality had by far the highest figure, at 33.14%, roughly twice the shares recorded in finance and IT, which were almost identical at 16.39% and 16.04% respectively. Manufacturing was noticeably lower, with women making up only 9% of managers.","chinese":"在經理職位中，酒店款待業的數字遠高於其他行業，達 33.14% ，大約是金融和資訊科技業的兩倍；後兩者的比例幾乎相同，分別為 16.39% 和 16.04% 。 製造業則明顯較低，女性只佔經理職位的 9% 。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"A similar ranking can be seen among executives and CEOs, though the percentages were smaller. In hospitality, women accounted for 19.9% of executives and 20.6% of CEOs, far ahead of IT, where the equivalent figures were 12.82% and 6.58%. Female representation was much weaker in finance, at 4.58% for executives and just 1.98% for CEOs. Manufacturing had the lowest levels overall, with only 1.98% of executives and 1.21% of CEOs being women.","chinese":"在行政人員和行政總裁層面，也可以看到相似的排名，不過比例整體較低。 在酒店款待業中，女性佔行政人員的 19.9% ，並佔行政總裁的 20.6% ，遠高於資訊科技業；後者相應數字為 12.82% 和 6.58% 。 金融業的女性代表性則弱得多，女性行政人員佔 4.58% ，而女性行政總裁僅佔。 製造業整體水平最低，女性只佔行政人員的 1.98% ，並只佔行政總裁的 1.21%。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"the table compares","chinese":"表格比較"},{"english":"the percentage of","chinese":"……的百分比"},{"english":"management posts","chinese":"管理職位"},{"english":"occupied by women","chinese":"由女性擔任"},{"english":"held by women","chinese":"由女性擔任"},{"english":"in finance","chinese":"在金融業"},{"english":"manufacturing","chinese":"製造業"},{"english":"IT","chinese":"資訊科技業"},{"english":"hospitality","chinese":"酒店及款待業"},{"english":"in a European country","chinese":"在一個歐洲國家"},{"english":"in 2006","chinese":"在2006年"},{"english":"Overall","chinese":"整體而言"},{"english":"women were most strongly represented","chinese":"女性代表性最高"},{"english":"strongly represented","chinese":"代表性高"},{"english":"least represented","chinese":"代表性最低"},{"english":"across the three levels","chinese":"在三個級別中"},{"english":"their share","chinese":"她們所佔比例"},{"english":"generally decreased","chinese":"整體下降"},{"english":"as seniority rose","chinese":"隨着職級上升"},{"english":"seniority","chinese":"職級高低；資歷級別"},{"english":"although","chinese":"雖然"},{"english":"an exception at the top level","chinese":"高層級別的例外"},{"english":"at the top level","chinese":"在最高級別"},{"english":"the proportion of female CEOs","chinese":"女性行政總裁比例"},{"english":"female CEOs","chinese":"女性行政總裁"},{"english":"slightly exceeded","chinese":"略高於"},{"english":"that of female executives","chinese":"女性行政人員的比例"},{"english":"female executives","chinese":"女性行政人員"},{"english":"Among managers","chinese":"在經理級別中"},{"english":"by far the highest figure","chinese":"遠遠最高的數字"},{"english":"at 33.14%","chinese":"為33.14%"},{"english":"roughly twice","chinese":"大約兩倍"},{"english":"the shares recorded in","chinese":"在……錄得的比例"},{"english":"finance and IT","chinese":"金融業及資訊科技業"},{"english":"almost identical","chinese":"幾乎相同"},{"english":"respectively","chinese":"分別"},{"english":"noticeably lower","chinese":"明顯較低"},{"english":"with women making up","chinese":"其中女性佔"},{"english":"making up only 9%","chinese":"只佔9%"},{"english":"a similar ranking","chinese":"相似的排名"},{"english":"can be seen among","chinese":"可見於……之中"},{"english":"executives and CEOs","chinese":"行政人員及行政總裁"},{"english":"though","chinese":"不過；雖然"},{"english":"the percentages were smaller","chinese":"百分比較低"},{"english":"accounted for 19.9% of","chinese":"佔……的19.9%"},{"english":"far ahead of","chinese":"遠高於"},{"english":"the equivalent figures","chinese":"對應數字"},{"english":"12.82% and 6.58%","chinese":"12.82%及6.58%"},{"english":"female representation","chinese":"女性代表性"},{"english":"much weaker","chinese":"弱得多；低得多"},{"english":"at 4.58% for executives","chinese":"行政人員為4.58%"},{"english":"just 1.98% for CEOs","chinese":"行政總裁只有1.98%"},{"english":"had the lowest levels overall","chinese":"整體水平最低"},{"english":"the lowest levels overall","chinese":"整體最低水平"},{"english":"with only","chinese":"只有"},{"english":"1.98% of executives","chinese":"1.98%的行政人員"},{"english":"1.21% of CEOs","chinese":"1.21%的行政總裁"},{"english":"being women","chinese":"是女性"}]},"model-essay-9-ielts-advantage-disadvantage":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-9-ielts-advantage-disadvantage","essayKey":"advantage-disadvantage:9","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-9-ielts-advantage-disadvantage","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/advantage-and-disadvantage/EdmundBd9AdDisAd-Q9","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"In many schools, uniforms are treated as a basic part of discipline, while others allow children to dress with far more freedom. Requiring pupils to wear a uniform has several clear benefits, especially in relation to equality and school identity, but it can also create problems for self-expression and family finances.","chinese":"在許多學校中，校服被視為紀律的基本部分，而另一些學校則容許學生在衣著上有更多自由。 要求學生穿校服有幾個明顯好處，尤其是在平等和學校身份認同方面；但它也可能在自我表達和家庭財政方面帶來問題。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"One major advantage is that a uniform reduces visible social differences among children. If everyone wears similar clothes, pupils from poorer families are less likely to feel embarrassed by cheap or unfashionable outfits, and wealthier pupils have fewer chances to display expensive brands. This can make the classroom feel like a more equal place, where children are judged more by their behaviour and effort than by what they wear. Uniforms can also strengthen a sense of belonging. A child who puts on the same colours and badge as their classmates may feel that they are part of a shared community, much like a sports team whose kit quietly reminds its members that they represent something larger than themselves.","chinese":"其中一個主要優點是，校服可以減少孩子之間外在可見的社會差異。 如果每個人都穿著相似的衣服，來自較貧困家庭的學生便較不容易因為衣服便宜或不時尚而感到尷尬，而較富裕的學生也較少機會展示昂貴品牌。 這可以令課室感覺上更平等，孩子受到評價時，更多是基於他們的行為和努力，而不是他們穿甚麼。 校服也可以加強學生的歸屬感。 一個孩子穿上與同學相同顏色和校徽的校服時，可能會感到自己是共同群體的一部分，就像一支運動隊伍的隊服，會默默提醒隊員他們代表著比個人更大的整體。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"However, school uniforms also have disadvantages. The most obvious one is that they limit individuality. Children, especially teenagers, often use clothing to explore their personality, confidence, and taste. If every detail is tightly controlled, school may start to feel unnecessarily rigid, and minor choices such as hairstyles, shoes, or accessories can become sources of conflict rather than learning. Another drawback is cost. Although uniforms are meant to simplify clothing, they can be surprisingly expensive when schools require specific jackets, shoes, sportswear, or seasonal items from selected suppliers. For families with several children, these costs can place a real strain on the household budget.","chinese":"然而，校服也有缺點。 最明顯的一點是，校服限制了個人特色。 孩子，尤其是青少年，往往會透過衣著探索自己的個性、自信和品味。 如果每一個細節都受到嚴格控制，學校便可能開始令人覺得不必要地僵化，而髮型、鞋子或飾物這些小選擇，也可能變成衝突來源，而不是學習的一部分。 另一個缺點是成本。 雖然校服本意是簡化學生的衣著安排，但當學校要求學生購買特定外套、鞋子、運動服或指定供應商提供的季節性服裝時，校服的費用可能會出乎意料地高。 對於有幾個孩子的家庭來說，這些開支可能會對家庭預算造成實際壓力。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, school uniforms can promote equality, discipline, and a stronger school identity, but they may also restrict personal expression and create financial pressure. Overall, they bring clear social benefits, while also creating practical and personal drawbacks.","chinese":"總結來說，校服可以促進平等、紀律和更強的學校身份認同，但它們也可能限制個人表達，並造成財政壓力。 整體而言，校服帶來明顯的社會好處，但同時也會造成實際和個人層面的缺點。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"school uniforms","chinese":"校服"},{"english":"be treated as","chinese":"被視為……"},{"english":"a basic part of discipline","chinese":"紀律的基本部分"},{"english":"allow children to dress with far more freedom","chinese":"讓孩子穿着上有大得多的自由"},{"english":"dress with far more freedom","chinese":"穿着上有大得多的自由"},{"english":"requiring pupils to wear a uniform","chinese":"要求學生穿校服"},{"english":"several clear benefits","chinese":"幾個明顯好處"},{"english":"in relation to","chinese":"在……方面"},{"english":"equality and school identity","chinese":"平等和學校身份認同"},{"english":"create problems for","chinese":"為……帶來問題"},{"english":"self-expression","chinese":"自我表達"},{"english":"family finances","chinese":"家庭財政"},{"english":"one major advantage","chinese":"一個主要優點"},{"english":"reduces visible social differences","chinese":"減少可見的社會差異"},{"english":"visible social differences","chinese":"可見的社會差異"},{"english":"among children","chinese":"在孩子之間"},{"english":"pupils from poorer families","chinese":"來自較貧困家庭的學生"},{"english":"less likely to feel embarrassed by","chinese":"較不容易因……而感到尷尬"},{"english":"cheap or unfashionable outfits","chinese":"便宜或不時髦的衣着"},{"english":"wealthier pupils","chinese":"較富裕的學生"},{"english":"have fewer chances to","chinese":"較少機會去……"},{"english":"display expensive brands","chinese":"展示昂貴品牌"},{"english":"make the classroom feel like","chinese":"令課室感覺像……"},{"english":"a more equal place","chinese":"更平等的地方"},{"english":"be judged more by","chinese":"更多按……被評價"},{"english":"behaviour and effort","chinese":"行為和努力"},{"english":"than by what they wear","chinese":"而不是按他們的穿着"},{"english":"strengthen a sense of belonging","chinese":"加強歸屬感"},{"english":"a sense of belonging","chinese":"歸屬感"},{"english":"puts on the same colours and badge","chinese":"穿上相同顏色和校徽"},{"english":"classmates","chinese":"同班同學"},{"english":"part of a shared community","chinese":"共同群體的一分子"},{"english":"much like","chinese":"很像……"},{"english":"a sports team","chinese":"運動隊伍"},{"english":"quietly reminds its members that","chinese":"默默提醒其成員……"},{"english":"represent something larger than themselves","chinese":"代表比自己更大的整體"},{"english":"the most obvious one","chinese":"最明顯的一點"},{"english":"limit individuality","chinese":"限制個性"},{"english":"especially teenagers","chinese":"尤其是青少年"},{"english":"use clothing to explore","chinese":"用衣着去探索……"},{"english":"personality, confidence, and taste","chinese":"個性、自信和品味"},{"english":"every detail is tightly controlled","chinese":"每個細節都被嚴格控制"},{"english":"start to feel unnecessarily rigid","chinese":"開始令人覺得不必要地僵化"},{"english":"minor choices","chinese":"細微選擇"},{"english":"hairstyles, shoes, or accessories","chinese":"髮型、鞋履或配飾"},{"english":"sources of conflict","chinese":"衝突來源"},{"english":"rather than learning","chinese":"而不是學習"},{"english":"another drawback is cost","chinese":"另一個缺點是成本"},{"english":"are meant to simplify","chinese":"原意是簡化……"},{"english":"surprisingly expensive","chinese":"貴得令人意外"},{"english":"specific jackets","chinese":"指定外套"},{"english":"sportswear","chinese":"運動服"},{"english":"seasonal items","chinese":"季節性用品"},{"english":"selected suppliers","chinese":"指定供應商"},{"english":"families with several children","chinese":"有幾個孩子的家庭"},{"english":"place a real strain on","chinese":"對……造成實際壓力"},{"english":"household budget","chinese":"家庭預算"},{"english":"promote equality","chinese":"促進平等"},{"english":"a stronger school identity","chinese":"更強的學校身份認同"},{"english":"restrict personal expression","chinese":"限制個人表達"},{"english":"create financial pressure","chinese":"造成財政壓力"},{"english":"overall","chinese":"總括而言"},{"english":"clear social benefits","chinese":"明顯的社會好處"},{"english":"practical and personal drawbacks","chinese":"實際及個人方面的缺點"}]},"model-essay-9-ielts-cause-solution":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-9-ielts-cause-solution","essayKey":"cause-solution:9","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-9-ielts-cause-solution","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/problem-and-cause/EdmundBd9CnS-Q9","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"An increasing number of people now face serious health risks because they are overweight. This problem is best understood not as a simple failure of personal discipline, but as the result of a modern environment that quietly encourages inactivity and unhealthy eating. The most effective solution, therefore, is to make healthier routines easier to follow in ordinary life.","chinese":"越來越多人如今因為超重而面臨嚴重的健康風險。 這個問題最應被理解為現代環境所造成的結果，而不是單純的個人自律失敗；這種環境正悄悄鼓勵人們缺乏活動並養成不健康的飲食習慣。 因此，最有效的解決方法是讓較健康的日常習慣在普通生活中更容易實行。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"The main reason for the growth in overweight people is that many daily routines now involve too little movement and too much convenient, calorie-dense food. In many cities, people sit for long hours at school, at work and during travel, so their bodies use far less energy than before. At the same time, fast food, sugary drinks and processed snacks are cheap, widely available and heavily promoted. When these two forces work together, weight gain can become almost automatic. For example, a student who spends the day in class, travels home by car and then relaxes with online games may gradually build a lifestyle in which eating is easy but physical activity is rare.","chinese":"超重人數增加的主要原因是，現今許多日常生活模式都包含太少活動，以及太多方便而高熱量密度的食物。 在許多城市中，人們在學校、工作和通勤期間都長時間坐著，因此身體消耗的能量比以前少得多。 與此同時，快餐、含糖飲品和加工零食價格便宜、隨處可得，而且被大量推廣。 當這兩種力量同時發揮作用時，體重增加幾乎會變成一種自然而然的結果。 例如，一名學生整天在課室上課，放學後坐車回家，然後用網上遊戲放鬆，便可能逐漸形成一種飲食很容易、但體能活動很少的生活方式。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"To solve this problem, governments, schools and employers need to change the conditions that shape everyday behaviour. Governments could limit junk-food advertising aimed at children, require clearer nutrition labels and make fresh food more affordable. Schools should provide regular physical education and healthier meals, while workplaces could encourage active breaks, flexible lunch hours and safe facilities for walking or cycling. These measures are useful because they do not depend only on willpower. If healthy food is reasonably priced and exercise is built into the day, people are more likely to maintain a healthy weight without feeling that they are fighting their own routine.","chinese":"為了解決這個問題，政府、學校和僱主需要改變那些塑造日常行為的條件。 政府可以限制針對兒童的垃圾食品廣告，要求更清晰的營養標籤，並令新鮮食物更容易負擔。 學校應該提供定期的體育教育和更健康的膳食，而工作場所則可以鼓勵活動休息、彈性午餐時間，以及安全的步行或單車設施。 這些措施是有用的，因為它們並不只是依賴個人意志力。 如果健康食物價格合理，而運動又被融入日常生活之中，人們便更有可能維持健康體重，而不會覺得自己正在對抗自己的生活規律。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, the rise in overweight people is mainly caused by sedentary lifestyles combined with easy access to unhealthy food. It can be reduced by creating environments in which eating well and moving regularly become normal, practical and affordable choices.","chinese":"總結來說，超重人數上升主要是由久坐的生活方式，加上不健康食物容易取得所造成的。 這個問題可以透過創造一種環境來減少；在這種環境中，健康飲食和定期活動會成為正常、實際而且負擔得起的選擇。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"an increasing number of","chinese":"越來越多"},{"english":"face serious health risks","chinese":"面對嚴重健康風險"},{"english":"overweight","chinese":"超重"},{"english":"be best understood as","chinese":"最好理解為"},{"english":"a simple failure of personal discipline","chinese":"個人自律失敗這麼簡單"},{"english":"personal discipline","chinese":"個人自律"},{"english":"the result of","chinese":"……的結果"},{"english":"a modern environment","chinese":"現代環境"},{"english":"quietly encourages inactivity","chinese":"悄悄鼓勵缺乏活動"},{"english":"unhealthy eating","chinese":"不健康飲食"},{"english":"the most effective solution","chinese":"最有效的解決方法"},{"english":"healthier routines","chinese":"更健康的日常習慣"},{"english":"easier to follow","chinese":"更容易跟從"},{"english":"ordinary life","chinese":"日常生活"},{"english":"the growth in overweight people","chinese":"超重人口增加"},{"english":"daily routines","chinese":"日常習慣"},{"english":"involve too little movement","chinese":"涉及太少活動"},{"english":"convenient, calorie-dense food","chinese":"方便而高熱量的食物"},{"english":"calorie-dense food","chinese":"高熱量食物"},{"english":"sit for long hours","chinese":"長時間坐着"},{"english":"during travel","chinese":"在通勤途中"},{"english":"use far less energy","chinese":"消耗少得多能量"},{"english":"than before","chinese":"比以前"},{"english":"at the same time","chinese":"同時"},{"english":"fast food","chinese":"快餐"},{"english":"sugary drinks","chinese":"含糖飲品"},{"english":"processed snacks","chinese":"加工零食"},{"english":"widely available","chinese":"隨處可得"},{"english":"heavily promoted","chinese":"被大力宣傳"},{"english":"work together","chinese":"共同作用"},{"english":"weight gain","chinese":"體重增加"},{"english":"almost automatic","chinese":"幾乎自然而然"},{"english":"spend the day in class","chinese":"整天上課"},{"english":"travel home by car","chinese":"坐車回家"},{"english":"relax with online games","chinese":"玩網上遊戲放鬆"},{"english":"gradually build a lifestyle","chinese":"逐漸建立一種生活方式"},{"english":"physical activity","chinese":"體能活動"},{"english":"be rare","chinese":"很少見"},{"english":"solve this problem","chinese":"解決這個問題"},{"english":"change the conditions","chinese":"改變條件"},{"english":"shape everyday behaviour","chinese":"塑造日常行為"},{"english":"limit junk-food advertising","chinese":"限制垃圾食物廣告"},{"english":"aimed at children","chinese":"針對兒童"},{"english":"nutrition labels","chinese":"營養標籤"},{"english":"make fresh food more affordable","chinese":"令新鮮食物更可負擔"},{"english":"regular physical education","chinese":"定期體育課"},{"english":"healthier meals","chinese":"更健康的膳食"},{"english":"active breaks","chinese":"活動小休"},{"english":"flexible lunch hours","chinese":"彈性午膳時間"},{"english":"safe facilities for walking or cycling","chinese":"安全的步行或踩單車設施"},{"english":"do not depend only on","chinese":"不只依賴"},{"english":"willpower","chinese":"意志力"},{"english":"reasonably priced","chinese":"價格合理"},{"english":"be built into the day","chinese":"融入日常"},{"english":"maintain a healthy weight","chinese":"維持健康體重"},{"english":"fight their own routine","chinese":"與自己的日常習慣對抗"},{"english":"the rise in overweight people","chinese":"超重人口上升"},{"english":"sedentary lifestyles","chinese":"久坐少動的生活方式"},{"english":"be combined with","chinese":"與……結合"},{"english":"easy access to","chinese":"容易接觸到"},{"english":"unhealthy food","chinese":"不健康食物"},{"english":"be reduced by","chinese":"可以透過……減少"},{"english":"creating environments in which","chinese":"創造一種……的環境"},{"english":"eating well","chinese":"飲食健康"},{"english":"moving regularly","chinese":"定期活動"},{"english":"normal, practical and affordable choices","chinese":"正常、實際而可負擔的選擇"}]},"model-essay-9-ielts-direct-question":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-9-ielts-direct-question","essayKey":"direct-question:9","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-9-ielts-direct-question","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/direct-question/EdmundBd9Dir-Q9","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"Juvenile crime is often blamed on violent films, video games and online content, because these influences are visible and easy to criticise. However, I do not agree that media violence is the main cause. In my view, young people are far more likely to offend when they lack stable guidance, meaningful supervision and constructive outlets for their energy. The best response is therefore early intervention through families, schools and local communities.","chinese":"青少年犯罪常常被歸咎於暴力電影、電子遊戲和網上內容，因為這些影響因素十分顯眼，也很容易被批評。 然而，我不同意媒體暴力是主要原因。 在我看來，當年輕人缺乏穩定的引導、有意義的監督，以及能夠正面釋放精力的途徑時，他們犯罪的可能性要大得多。 因此，最好的應對方法是透過家庭、學校和本地社區進行早期介入。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"The central cause of youth crime is not what teenagers watch, but the environment in which they learn how to behave. If parents are absent, overwhelmed or unable to set boundaries, children may never develop a clear sense of consequence. A violent scene on a screen may shock them briefly, but daily neglect can quietly teach them that aggression, theft or defiance bring no serious cost. This problem becomes even worse in areas where teenagers have few positive role models and little to do after school. For instance, a boy who spends every evening with older peers involved in petty crime is not merely copying television; he is being pulled into a real social script.","chinese":"青少年犯罪的核心原因並不是他們觀看了甚麼，而是他們學習如何行為處事的環境。 如果父母缺席、不堪重負，或者無法設立界線，孩子可能永遠無法建立清晰的後果意識。 螢幕上的一個暴力場面可能會短暫地震撼他們，但日常的忽視卻可能悄悄地教會他們：攻擊、偷竊或反抗並不會帶來嚴重代價。 在一些青少年缺乏正面榜樣、放學後也沒有甚麼事情可做的地區，這個問題會變得更加嚴重。 例如，一個每天晚上都和參與輕微犯罪的年長同伴混在一起的男孩，並不只是單純地模仿電視；他其實是被拉進了一套真實的社會劇本之中。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"To deal with this situation, governments and communities should focus on support before punishment. Schools should identify pupils who show repeated aggression, truancy or isolation and connect them with counsellors, mentors and family-support services before their behaviour hardens into a pattern. At the same time, local authorities should fund affordable sports, arts and vocational programmes, especially in deprived neighbourhoods. These activities give teenagers structure, belonging and a legitimate sense of achievement. A young person who has a coach, a team and a reason to be proud is less likely to seek status through crime.","chinese":"為了處理這種情況，政府和社區應該先著重支援，而不是先著重懲罰。 學校應該識別那些反覆表現出攻擊行為、逃學或孤立情況的學生，並在他們的行為固化成一種模式之前，把他們與輔導員、導師和家庭支援服務連接起來。 同時，地方政府應該資助價格可負擔的體育、藝術和職業培訓項目，尤其是在資源匱乏的社區。 這些活動能給予青少年規律、歸屬感，以及一種正當的成就感。 一個擁有教練、團隊，以及值得自豪理由的年輕人，較不容易透過犯罪來尋求地位。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, media violence may seem like a convenient explanation, but it is not the main cause of juvenile crime. The deeper roots are weak supervision, poor support and under-resourced communities, and the best solutions are early intervention, stronger family support and purposeful activities for young people.","chinese":"總結來說，媒體暴力看似是一個方便的解釋，但它並不是青少年犯罪的主要原因。 更深層的根源在於薄弱的監督、不足的支援，以及資源不足的社區，而最好的解決方法是早期介入、更強的家庭支援，以及為年輕人提供有目的的活動。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"juvenile crime","chinese":"青少年犯罪"},{"english":"be blamed on","chinese":"被歸咎於"},{"english":"violent films","chinese":"暴力電影"},{"english":"online content","chinese":"網上內容"},{"english":"these influences","chinese":"這些影響因素"},{"english":"visible and easy to criticise","chinese":"明顯而容易批評"},{"english":"media violence","chinese":"媒體暴力"},{"english":"the main cause","chinese":"主要原因"},{"english":"far more likely to","chinese":"更有可能"},{"english":"offend","chinese":"犯法；犯罪"},{"english":"lack stable guidance","chinese":"缺乏穩定指導"},{"english":"meaningful supervision","chinese":"有實質意義的監督"},{"english":"constructive outlets for","chinese":"……的建設性出口"},{"english":"early intervention","chinese":"早期介入"},{"english":"local communities","chinese":"本地社區"},{"english":"the central cause of","chinese":"……的核心原因"},{"english":"youth crime","chinese":"青少年犯罪"},{"english":"learn how to behave","chinese":"學習如何行事"},{"english":"parents are absent","chinese":"父母缺席"},{"english":"overwhelmed","chinese":"不勝負荷的"},{"english":"set boundaries","chinese":"設立界線"},{"english":"develop a clear sense of consequence","chinese":"建立清晰的後果意識"},{"english":"a violent scene on a screen","chinese":"螢幕上的暴力場面"},{"english":"shock them briefly","chinese":"短暫震撼他們"},{"english":"daily neglect","chinese":"日常忽視"},{"english":"quietly teach them that","chinese":"悄悄教會他們"},{"english":"aggression, theft or defiance","chinese":"攻擊行為、偷竊或反抗"},{"english":"bring no serious cost","chinese":"不會帶來嚴重代價"},{"english":"positive role models","chinese":"正面的榜樣"},{"english":"little to do after school","chinese":"放學後無所事事"},{"english":"spends every evening with","chinese":"每晚都與……一起"},{"english":"older peers","chinese":"年紀較大的朋輩"},{"english":"involved in petty crime","chinese":"參與輕微犯罪"},{"english":"not merely copying","chinese":"不只是模仿"},{"english":"be pulled into","chinese":"被拉入；被捲入"},{"english":"a real social script","chinese":"真實的社會劇本"},{"english":"deal with this situation","chinese":"處理這種情況"},{"english":"focus on support before punishment","chinese":"先支援，後懲罰"},{"english":"repeated aggression","chinese":"反覆攻擊行為"},{"english":"truancy","chinese":"逃學"},{"english":"isolation","chinese":"孤立；孤僻"},{"english":"connect them with","chinese":"將他們與……連繫起來"},{"english":"counsellors","chinese":"輔導員"},{"english":"mentors","chinese":"導師；良師"},{"english":"family-support services","chinese":"家庭支援服務"},{"english":"hardens into a pattern","chinese":"固化成一種模式"},{"english":"local authorities","chinese":"地方政府；地方當局"},{"english":"affordable sports, arts and vocational programmes","chinese":"負擔得起的體育、藝術及職業培訓課程"},{"english":"vocational programmes","chinese":"職業培訓課程"},{"english":"deprived neighbourhoods","chinese":"貧困社區"},{"english":"give teenagers structure","chinese":"給青少年規律"},{"english":"belonging","chinese":"歸屬感"},{"english":"a legitimate sense of achievement","chinese":"正當的成就感"},{"english":"a reason to be proud","chinese":"值得自豪的理由"},{"english":"seek status through crime","chinese":"透過犯罪尋求地位"},{"english":"a convenient explanation","chinese":"方便的解釋"},{"english":"the deeper roots","chinese":"更深層的根源"},{"english":"weak supervision","chinese":"監督不足"},{"english":"poor support","chinese":"支援不足"},{"english":"under-resourced communities","chinese":"資源不足的社區"},{"english":"stronger family support","chinese":"更強的家庭支援"},{"english":"purposeful activities","chinese":"有目標的活動"},{"english":"young people","chinese":"年輕人"}]},"model-essay-9-ielts-discuss-both-views":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-9-ielts-discuss-both-views","essayKey":"discuss-both-views:9","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-9-ielts-discuss-both-views","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/discuss-both-views-your-opinion/EdmundBd9ExpBth-Q9","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"Human intelligence has long been debated, partly because some people appear naturally quick-minded while others develop their abilities gradually. Although innate ability can give individuals an early advantage, I believe intelligence is far more strongly shaped by education, practice and sustained learning.","chinese":"人類智力長久以來一直備受爭議，部分原因是有些人似乎天生反應敏捷，而另一些人則逐漸發展自己的能力。 儘管天生能力可以給予個人早期優勢，但我認為智力在更大程度上是由教育、練習和持續學習塑造的。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"Those who see intelligence as inborn often argue that people differ naturally in memory, reasoning and problem-solving speed. This view is understandable because children in the same classroom may receive the same instruction yet perform very differently. For instance, one student may grasp mathematical patterns almost instantly, while another needs repeated explanation before the idea becomes clear. Such differences suggest that certain mental capacities, like musical talent or athletic potential, may be partly inherited. If a person is born with a sharper ability to process information, learning may feel easier and faster from the beginning. In this sense, natural intelligence can act as a head start.","chinese":"那些認為智力是天生的人，往往主張人們在記憶力、推理能力和解決問題的速度方面天生就存在差異。 這種觀點是可以理解的，因為同一個課室裡的孩子可能接受相同的教學，但表現卻非常不同。 例如，一個學生可能幾乎立即掌握數學規律，而另一個學生則需要反覆解釋，才會明白這個概念。 這些差異顯示，某些心智能力，例如音樂天賦或運動潛能，可能有部分是遺傳而來的。 如果一個人天生具備較敏銳的資訊處理能力，那麼學習從一開始就可能感覺更容易、更快速。 從這個意義上說，天生智力可以起到領先起步的作用。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"However, I firmly believe that intelligence is not fixed, because learning can change how people think, analyse and solve problems. When students read widely, practise difficult skills and receive proper feedback, they gradually build stronger habits of reasoning. A child who struggles with science, for example, may become highly capable after years of guided practice, experiments and patient correction. This does not mean that everyone will reach exactly the same level, but it shows that intellectual ability can be stretched far beyond its starting point. More importantly, many forms of intelligence, such as judgement, creativity and emotional understanding, depend heavily on experience rather than birth. A naturally clever person who never studies may hit a ceiling, whereas a disciplined learner can continue to grow.","chinese":"然而，我堅定地認為智力並不是固定不變的，因為學習能夠改變人們思考、分析和解決問題的方式。 當學生廣泛閱讀、練習困難技能並獲得適當回饋時，他們會逐漸建立更強的推理習慣。 例如，一個在科學方面感到吃力的孩子，在多年有指導的練習、實驗和耐心糾正之後，可能會變得非常有能力。 這並不意味著每個人都會達到完全相同的水平，但它說明智力能力可以被延展到遠遠超出其起點的位置。 更重要的是，許多形式的智力，例如判斷力、創造力和情感理解，都高度依賴經驗，而不是出生時已經決定。 一個天生聰明但從不學習的人，可能會碰到上限；相反，一個自律的學習者則可以持續成長。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, innate ability may influence how quickly people learn at first, and it would be unrealistic to deny that some individuals have natural advantages. Nevertheless, intelligence is best understood as something that can be developed through learning, because education, effort and experience determine how far a person’s mind can truly go.","chinese":"總結來說，天生能力可能會影響人們最初學習的速度，而否認某些人具有天生優勢是不現實的。 然而，智力最好被理解為一種可以透過學習發展的東西，因為教育、努力和經驗決定了一個人的思維真正能走多遠。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"human intelligence","chinese":"人類智力"},{"english":"has long been debated","chinese":"長久以來備受爭議"},{"english":"partly because","chinese":"部分原因是"},{"english":"appear naturally quick-minded","chinese":"看起來天生反應快"},{"english":"develop their abilities gradually","chinese":"逐漸發展能力"},{"english":"innate ability","chinese":"天生能力"},{"english":"give individuals an early advantage","chinese":"給予個人早期優勢"},{"english":"far more strongly shaped by","chinese":"更大程度上受……塑造"},{"english":"sustained learning","chinese":"持續學習"},{"english":"see intelligence as inborn","chinese":"視智力為天生"},{"english":"differ naturally in","chinese":"在……方面天生有差異"},{"english":"reasoning","chinese":"推理能力"},{"english":"problem-solving speed","chinese":"解難速度"},{"english":"This view is understandable","chinese":"這種看法可以理解"},{"english":"receive the same instruction","chinese":"接受相同教學"},{"english":"perform very differently","chinese":"表現很不同"},{"english":"For instance","chinese":"例如"},{"english":"grasp mathematical patterns","chinese":"掌握數學規律"},{"english":"almost instantly","chinese":"幾乎立即"},{"english":"needs repeated explanation","chinese":"需要反覆解釋"},{"english":"the idea becomes clear","chinese":"概念變得清晰"},{"english":"Such differences suggest that","chinese":"這些差異顯示"},{"english":"mental capacities","chinese":"心智能力"},{"english":"musical talent","chinese":"音樂天賦"},{"english":"athletic potential","chinese":"運動潛能"},{"english":"partly inherited","chinese":"部分遺傳"},{"english":"be born with","chinese":"天生具有"},{"english":"a sharper ability to","chinese":"更敏銳的……能力"},{"english":"process information","chinese":"處理資料"},{"english":"feel easier and faster","chinese":"感覺更容易、更快"},{"english":"from the beginning","chinese":"從一開始"},{"english":"In this sense","chinese":"從這個意義上說"},{"english":"act as a head start","chinese":"成為起步優勢"},{"english":"firmly believe","chinese":"堅信"},{"english":"is not fixed","chinese":"並非固定不變"},{"english":"change how people think","chinese":"改變人們的思考方式"},{"english":"analyse and solve problems","chinese":"分析和解決問題"},{"english":"read widely","chinese":"廣泛閱讀"},{"english":"practise difficult skills","chinese":"練習困難技能"},{"english":"receive proper feedback","chinese":"獲得適當回饋"},{"english":"gradually build stronger habits of","chinese":"逐漸建立更強的……習慣"},{"english":"habits of reasoning","chinese":"推理習慣"},{"english":"struggles with science","chinese":"在科學方面感到吃力"},{"english":"highly capable","chinese":"能力很強"},{"english":"guided practice","chinese":"有指導的練習"},{"english":"patient correction","chinese":"耐心糾正"},{"english":"reach exactly the same level","chinese":"達到完全相同的水平"},{"english":"intellectual ability","chinese":"智力能力"},{"english":"be stretched far beyond","chinese":"被大大延伸至超越"},{"english":"its starting point","chinese":"它的起點"},{"english":"More importantly","chinese":"更重要的是"},{"english":"forms of intelligence","chinese":"智力形式"},{"english":"judgement","chinese":"判斷力"},{"english":"creativity","chinese":"創意"},{"english":"emotional understanding","chinese":"情感理解能力"},{"english":"depend heavily on","chinese":"很大程度上取決於"},{"english":"rather than birth","chinese":"而不是出生條件"},{"english":"naturally clever","chinese":"天生聰明"},{"english":"hit a ceiling","chinese":"遇到上限"},{"english":"a disciplined learner","chinese":"自律的學習者"},{"english":"continue to grow","chinese":"繼續成長"},{"english":"influence how quickly","chinese":"影響……有多快"},{"english":"at first","chinese":"起初"},{"english":"it would be unrealistic to deny that","chinese":"否認……並不現實"},{"english":"natural advantages","chinese":"天然優勢"},{"english":"Nevertheless","chinese":"然而"},{"english":"best understood as","chinese":"最好理解為"},{"english":"developed through learning","chinese":"透過學習發展"},{"english":"education, effort and experience","chinese":"教育、努力和經驗"},{"english":"determine how far","chinese":"決定……能走多遠"},{"english":"a person's mind","chinese":"一個人的頭腦；心智能力"}]},"model-essay-9-ielts-opinion":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-9-ielts-opinion","essayKey":"opinion:9","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-9-ielts-opinion","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/opinions/EdmundBd9OP-Q9","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"Because public policy shapes the long-term direction of a national economy, governments must decide where their support will produce the greatest benefit. Although many countries try to attract overseas corporations, I completely agree that governments should focus primarily on encouraging local businesses because domestic firms keep economic value within the country and provide a more stable basis for future growth.","chinese":"由於公共政策會塑造一國經濟的長期發展方向，政府必須決定應把支持投向何處，才能產生最大的效益。 雖然許多國家都試圖吸引海外企業，但我完全同意政府應優先把重點放在扶持本地企業，因為本國企業能把經濟價值留在國內，並為未來成長提供更穩定的基礎。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"The first reason local enterprises deserve greater support is that they circulate wealth through the domestic economy far more effectively. When a home-grown company expands, its profits are more likely to be reinvested locally, its taxes are paid to the same government that assisted it, and its operations usually depend on other national firms. This creates a powerful multiplier effect. A growing local business buys materials from domestic suppliers, pays wages to local employees, and purchases services such as transport, marketing and accounting from nearby companies. As a result, income spreads across several sectors rather than being transferred abroad, which strengthens employment and increases tax revenue. For example, if a locally owned food manufacturer receives government assistance, its growth may also benefit farmers, delivery companies and packaging providers within the same country.","chinese":"本地企業之所以更值得獲得支持，第一個原因在於它們能更有效地讓財富在國內經濟中流動。 當一家本土企業擴張時，它的利潤更有可能重新投資於本地；它所繳納的稅款也會回到曾經扶持它的同一個政府；而且它的營運通常也依賴其他本國企業。 這就會產生強大的乘數效應。 一家正在成長的本地企業會向國內供應商購買原料，支付薪資給本地員工，並向附近公司購買運輸、行銷及會計等服務。 因此，收入會擴散到多個產業，而不是被轉移到國外，這不但能強化就業，也能增加稅收。 例如，若一家由本地人擁有的食品製造商獲得政府援助，它的成長也可能同時讓同一國家的農民、配送公司及包裝供應商受惠。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"Governments should also prioritise local firms because excessive reliance on foreign companies can weaken national competitiveness over time. Large multinational corporations often enter new markets with vast financial resources, established global brands and the ability to undercut smaller rivals. If they are also offered tax breaks or special incentives, domestic businesses can struggle to survive, even when they have long-term potential. Once local competitors disappear, key industries may become dependent on foreign-owned firms whose decisions are made overseas. This creates a serious risk: if labour costs rise or profits fall, those companies can relocate, leaving job losses and economic disruption behind. A clear example can be seen when foreign retail chains dominate a market, forcing smaller local shops to close before later reducing investment when conditions become less favourable.","chinese":"政府也應該優先扶持本地企業，因為過度依賴外國公司，長遠而言可能削弱國家的競爭力。 大型跨國企業進入新市場時，往往挾帶雄厚的財力、成熟的全球品牌，以及以低價壓過較小競爭對手的能力。 如果這些企業還獲得減稅或特殊優惠，那麼本國企業即使具有長期發展潛力，也可能難以生存。 一旦本地競爭者消失，關鍵產業就可能轉而依賴外資擁有的企業，而這些企業的決策卻是在海外作出的。 這會造成嚴重風險：一旦勞工成本上升或利潤下跌，這些公司便可能遷走，留下失業問題與經濟動盪。 一個明顯的例子是，當外國零售連鎖企業主導市場時，它們會迫使規模較小的本地商店倒閉；而當市場條件變得不再那麼有利時，它們之後又可能減少投資。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, I wholly agree that governments should prioritise local businesses over foreign ones. Supporting domestic enterprise keeps wealth at home, strengthens related industries and builds a more self-reliant economy, whereas overdependence on overseas corporations can undermine long-term national resilience.","chinese":"總而言之，我完全同意政府應該優先支持本地企業，而不是外國企業。 支持本國企業能把財富留在國內、強化相關產業，並建立更具自立性的經濟體；相反地，過度依賴海外企業則可能削弱國家長期的韌性。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"public policy","chinese":"公共政策"},{"english":"shape the long-term direction of","chinese":"塑造……的長遠方向"},{"english":"a national economy","chinese":"國家經濟"},{"english":"decide where","chinese":"決定在哪裏"},{"english":"produce the greatest benefit","chinese":"產生最大效益"},{"english":"attract overseas corporations","chinese":"吸引海外企業"},{"english":"focus primarily on","chinese":"主要集中於"},{"english":"encouraging local businesses","chinese":"鼓勵本地企業"},{"english":"domestic firms","chinese":"本地企業"},{"english":"keep economic value within the country","chinese":"將經濟價值留在國內"},{"english":"provide a more stable basis for","chinese":"為……提供更穩定的基礎"},{"english":"future growth","chinese":"未來增長"},{"english":"local enterprises","chinese":"本地企業"},{"english":"deserve greater support","chinese":"值得得到更多支持"},{"english":"circulate wealth through","chinese":"令財富在……內流動"},{"english":"the domestic economy","chinese":"本地經濟"},{"english":"far more effectively","chinese":"有效得多"},{"english":"a home-grown company","chinese":"本土公司"},{"english":"profits are more likely to","chinese":"利潤更有可能"},{"english":"be reinvested locally","chinese":"在本地再投資"},{"english":"taxes are paid to","chinese":"稅款繳交給"},{"english":"assist","chinese":"協助"},{"english":"depend on","chinese":"依賴"},{"english":"national firms","chinese":"國內企業"},{"english":"a powerful multiplier effect","chinese":"強大的乘數效應"},{"english":"a growing local business","chinese":"正在增長的本地企業"},{"english":"domestic suppliers","chinese":"本地供應商"},{"english":"pay wages to","chinese":"向……支付工資"},{"english":"local employees","chinese":"本地僱員"},{"english":"purchase services such as","chinese":"購買例如……的服務"},{"english":"nearby companies","chinese":"附近公司"},{"english":"as a result","chinese":"因此"},{"english":"income spreads across","chinese":"收入擴散至"},{"english":"several sectors","chinese":"多個行業"},{"english":"rather than being transferred abroad","chinese":"而不是被轉移到海外"},{"english":"strengthen employment","chinese":"加強就業"},{"english":"increase tax revenue","chinese":"增加稅收"},{"english":"a locally owned food manufacturer","chinese":"本地擁有的食品製造商"},{"english":"receive government assistance","chinese":"獲得政府援助"},{"english":"benefit farmers","chinese":"令農民受惠"},{"english":"delivery companies","chinese":"送貨公司"},{"english":"packaging providers","chinese":"包裝供應商"},{"english":"within the same country","chinese":"在同一國家內"},{"english":"prioritise local firms","chinese":"優先支持本地企業"},{"english":"excessive reliance on","chinese":"過度依賴"},{"english":"foreign companies","chinese":"外國公司"},{"english":"weaken national competitiveness","chinese":"削弱國家競爭力"},{"english":"over time","chinese":"隨時間"},{"english":"large multinational corporations","chinese":"大型跨國企業"},{"english":"enter new markets","chinese":"進入新市場"},{"english":"vast financial resources","chinese":"龐大財政資源"},{"english":"established global brands","chinese":"已建立的全球品牌"},{"english":"undercut smaller rivals","chinese":"以低價擊敗較小競爭對手"},{"english":"tax breaks","chinese":"稅務寬減"},{"english":"special incentives","chinese":"特別優惠措施"},{"english":"struggle to survive","chinese":"難以生存"},{"english":"long-term potential","chinese":"長遠潛力"},{"english":"local competitors","chinese":"本地競爭者"},{"english":"key industries","chinese":"關鍵行業"},{"english":"become dependent on","chinese":"變得依賴"},{"english":"foreign-owned firms","chinese":"外資企業"},{"english":"be made overseas","chinese":"在海外作出"},{"english":"a serious risk","chinese":"嚴重風險"},{"english":"labour costs rise","chinese":"勞工成本上升"},{"english":"profits fall","chinese":"利潤下降"},{"english":"relocate","chinese":"遷走；遷移業務"},{"english":"leaving job losses behind","chinese":"留下失業問題"},{"english":"economic disruption","chinese":"經濟混亂"},{"english":"a clear example can be seen when","chinese":"一個明顯例子是"},{"english":"foreign retail chains","chinese":"外國零售連鎖店"},{"english":"dominate a market","chinese":"主導市場"},{"english":"force smaller local shops to close","chinese":"迫使較小本地店舖結業"},{"english":"reducing investment","chinese":"減少投資"},{"english":"conditions become less favourable","chinese":"情況變得較不利"},{"english":"wholly agree","chinese":"完全同意"},{"english":"prioritise local businesses over foreign ones","chinese":"優先支持本地企業而非外國企業"},{"english":"supporting domestic enterprise","chinese":"支持本地企業"},{"english":"keep wealth at home","chinese":"將財富留在本地"},{"english":"strengthen related industries","chinese":"加強相關行業"},{"english":"build a more self-reliant economy","chinese":"建立更自力更生的經濟"},{"english":"overdependence on","chinese":"過度依賴"},{"english":"overseas corporations","chinese":"海外企業"},{"english":"undermine long-term national resilience","chinese":"削弱國家的長遠韌性"}]},"model-essay-9-ielts-task1-line-graph":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-9-ielts-task1-line-graph","essayKey":"line-graph:9","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-9-ielts-task1-line-graph","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-1/line-graphs/line-graph-9","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"The line graph illustrates the volume of goods transported in the UK by road, water, rail and pipeline between 1974 and 2002.","chinese":"該折線圖說明了 1974 年至 2002 年間，英國透過公路、水路、鐵路和管道運輸的貨物量。"},{"label":"Overview","english":"Overall, road was consistently the dominant mode and recorded the largest increase. Water transport also rose considerably, whereas rail fluctuated and finished only slightly above its initial level. Pipeline remained the least-used method, despite steady growth.","chinese":"整體而言，公路運輸一直是最主要的運輸方式，並錄得最大的絕對增幅。 水路運輸也有明顯上升；相反，鐵路運輸有所波動，最後只略高於最初水平。 儘管管道運輸穩定增長，但它始終是使用量最低的運輸方式。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"In 1974, road haulage stood at about 70 million tonnes, compared with roughly 38 million by water and 40 million by rail. After a slight rise in 1978 and a dip in 1982, the road figure climbed to just over 80 million tonnes in 1990. It then fell marginally in 1994 before rising sharply to almost 100 million tonnes by 2002.","chinese":"在 1974 年，公路貨運量約為 7,000 萬噸，相比之下，水路約為 3,800 萬噸，鐵路約為 4,000 萬噸。 在 1978 年小幅上升、 1982 年回落之後，公路運輸量在 1990 年升至略高於 8,000萬噸。 隨後，它在 1994 年略微下降，之後大幅上升，到 2002 年接近 1 億噸。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"Water followed a gentler upward trend. Its volume increased from just under 40 million tonnes to around 55 million in 1982, stayed near this level until 1994, dipped in 1998, and then recovered to approximately 65 million tonnes. By contrast, rail dropped to around 30 million tonnes in 1986 and, despite another dip in 1994, recovered to just over 40 by the end. Pipeline transport rose steadily from about 5 to slightly above 20 million tonnes.","chinese":"水路運輸呈現較溫和的上升趨勢。 其運輸量從略低於 4,000 萬噸上升至 1982 年的約 5,500 萬噸，並一直維持在接近這一水平直到 1994 年，之後在 1998 年下降，最後回升至約 6,500 萬噸。 相比之下，鐵路運輸量在 1986 年下降至約 3,000 萬噸；儘管它在 1994 年再次下跌，但到最後回升至略高於 4,000 萬噸。 管道運輸量則從約 500 萬噸穩定上升至略高於 2,000 萬噸。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"line graph","chinese":"折線圖"},{"english":"illustrates the volume of","chinese":"顯示……的數量"},{"english":"the volume of goods transported","chinese":"貨物運輸量"},{"english":"goods transported by","chinese":"以……運送的貨物"},{"english":"by road, water, rail and pipeline","chinese":"以公路、水路、鐵路及管道方式"},{"english":"between 1974 and 2002","chinese":"在1974年至2002年間"},{"english":"Overall","chinese":"整體而言"},{"english":"consistently the dominant mode","chinese":"一直是佔主導地位的方式"},{"english":"the dominant mode of transport","chinese":"主要運輸方式"},{"english":"recorded the largest increase","chinese":"錄得最大升幅"},{"english":"the largest increase","chinese":"最大升幅"},{"english":"water transport","chinese":"水路運輸"},{"english":"rose considerably","chinese":"大幅上升"},{"english":"whereas","chinese":"而；相比之下"},{"english":"rail transport","chinese":"鐵路運輸"},{"english":"fluctuated","chinese":"波動"},{"english":"finished only slightly above its initial level","chinese":"最終只略高於起初水平"},{"english":"its initial level","chinese":"起初水平"},{"english":"pipeline transport","chinese":"管道運輸"},{"english":"remained the least-used method","chinese":"仍然是使用量最低的方式"},{"english":"the least-used method","chinese":"使用量最低的方式"},{"english":"despite steady growth","chinese":"儘管穩定增長"},{"english":"steady growth","chinese":"穩定增長"},{"english":"road haulage","chinese":"公路貨運"},{"english":"stood at about","chinese":"約為"},{"english":"about 70 million tonnes","chinese":"約7,000萬噸"},{"english":"million tonnes","chinese":"百萬噸"},{"english":"compared with roughly","chinese":"相比之下，約為"},{"english":"roughly 38 million","chinese":"約3,800萬"},{"english":"by water","chinese":"以水路方式"},{"english":"by rail","chinese":"以鐵路方式"},{"english":"a slight rise","chinese":"輕微上升"},{"english":"a dip in","chinese":"在……出現下跌"},{"english":"the figure for road transport","chinese":"公路運輸的數字"},{"english":"climbed to just over","chinese":"升至剛高於"},{"english":"just over 80 million tonnes","chinese":"剛高於8,000萬噸"},{"english":"fell marginally","chinese":"輕微下跌"},{"english":"before rising sharply","chinese":"之後急升"},{"english":"rose sharply to","chinese":"急升至"},{"english":"almost 100 million tonnes","chinese":"接近1億噸"},{"english":"followed a gentler upward trend","chinese":"呈現較溫和的上升趨勢"},{"english":"a gentler upward trend","chinese":"較溫和的上升趨勢"},{"english":"increased from","chinese":"由……增加"},{"english":"increased from … to …","chinese":"由……增加至……"},{"english":"just under 40 million tonnes","chinese":"剛低於4,000萬噸"},{"english":"around 55 million tonnes","chinese":"約5,500萬噸"},{"english":"stayed near this level","chinese":"保持接近這水平"},{"english":"near this level","chinese":"接近這水平"},{"english":"dipped in","chinese":"在……下跌"},{"english":"recovered to approximately","chinese":"回升至大約"},{"english":"approximately 65 million tonnes","chinese":"約6,500萬噸"},{"english":"By contrast","chinese":"相比之下；相反"},{"english":"dropped to around","chinese":"跌至約"},{"english":"around 30 million tonnes","chinese":"約3,000萬噸"},{"english":"despite another dip","chinese":"儘管再度下跌"},{"english":"another dip in","chinese":"在……再度下跌"},{"english":"recovered to just over","chinese":"回升至剛高於"},{"english":"just over 40 million tonnes","chinese":"剛高於4,000萬噸"},{"english":"by the end of the period","chinese":"到該時期結束時"},{"english":"rose steadily from","chinese":"由……穩步上升"},{"english":"from about … to slightly above …","chinese":"由約……升至略高於……"},{"english":"slightly above 20 million tonnes","chinese":"略高於2,000萬噸"}]},"model-essay-9-ielts-task1-maps":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-9-ielts-task1-maps","essayKey":"maps:9","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-9-ielts-task1-maps","flashDeckId":"","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"The two plans illustrate the layout of Grange Park when it opened in 1920 and its arrangement today.","chinese":"這兩張平面圖展示了格蘭奇公園在 1920 年首次開放時的布局，以及它今天的安排。"},{"label":"Overview","english":"Overall, the park has been substantially modernised, with recreational facilities such as an amphitheatre, café, children’s play area and underground parking added. However, the two main entrances on Arnold Avenue and Eldon Street have been retained, and rose gardens remain important, although they have been reduced and reorganised.","chinese":"整體而言，該公園已大幅現代化，新增了露天劇場、咖啡館、兒童遊樂區和地下停車場等休閒設施。 然而，位於阿諾德大道和埃爾登街的兩個主要入口被保留下來，而玫瑰園仍然是重要元素，儘管它們的數量已減少並被重新安排。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"In 1920, the park had a formal layout. A fountain stood at its centre, while a stage for musicians occupied the western side. Three rose gardens were located in the northwest, northeast and southwest corners, and seating was distributed around the edges. The eastern half contained a pond for water plants in the northeast and a glasshouse in the southeast.","chinese":"在 1920 年，該公園具有較正式的布局。 一座噴泉位於公園中央，而音樂家表演台則佔據西側位置。 三個玫瑰園分別位於西北角、東北角和西南角，座位則分布在公園邊緣一帶。 公園東半部包含位於東北方的水生植物池，以及位於東南方的玻璃溫室。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"Today, the central fountain has been replaced by a square rose garden, surrounded by seats on all four sides. The former musicians’ stage has given way to a larger amphitheatre for concerts. On the eastern side, the old pond and glasshouse have disappeared; in their place are a café, a children’s play area and a water feature. A new entrance to an underground car park has also been introduced from the southeast.","chinese":"如今，中央噴泉已被一個方形玫瑰園取代，而其四周均設有座位。 原本的音樂家表演台已被一個更大的露天音樂會劇場取代。 在東側，舊有的池塘和玻璃溫室已經消失；取而代之的是咖啡館、兒童遊樂區和水景設施。 此外，東南方也新增了一個通往地下停車場的入口。"}],"vocabulary":[]},"model-essay-9-ielts-task1-process-diagram":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-9-ielts-task1-process-diagram","essayKey":"process-diagram:9","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-9-ielts-task1-process-diagram","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-1/process-diagrams/process-diagram-9","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"The diagrams illustrate the stages and equipment used to make cement, and how this cement is then used to produce concrete for construction.","chinese":"這些圖表說明了製造水泥所使用的階段和設備，以及這種水泥如何進一步用於生產建築用混凝土。"},{"label":"Overview","english":"Overall, cement manufacture is a multi-stage linear process involving crushing, mixing, heating and grinding, whereas concrete production is much simpler, requiring only the blending of four measured ingredients. Gravel accounts for by far the largest share of concrete, while water is the smallest component.","chinese":"整體而言，水泥製造是一個多階段的線性流程，涉及壓碎、混合、加熱和研磨；相比之下，混凝土生產簡單得多，只需要把四種按比例計量的原料混合起來。 碎石在混凝土中佔遠遠最大的比例，而水則是最小的組成部分。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"At the beginning of the cement-making process, limestone and clay are fed into a crusher, where they are reduced to powder. This powder is transferred to a mixer and then passes into a rotating heater. As the mixture moves through this cylinder, heat is applied from one end, after which the heated material is processed in a grinder. The resulting cement is finally packed into bags.","chinese":"在水泥製造過程的開始，石灰石和黏土被送入破碎機，在那裡被壓碎成粉末。 這些粉末接著被轉移到混合器，然後進入旋轉加熱器。 當混合物通過這個圓筒時，熱量從一端施加；之後，加熱後的材料會在研磨機中進一步處理。 最後，製成的水泥被裝入袋中。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"Concrete production involves fewer stages. Cement, sand, gravel and water are all poured into a concrete mixer, which rotates to combine them. Gravel, labelled as small stones, makes up half of the mixture, while sand accounts for a further quarter. Cement and water constitute 15% and 10%, respectively, before the finished concrete is ready for building work.","chinese":"混凝土生產涉及的階段較少。 水泥、沙、碎石和水全部被倒入混凝土攪拌機中，該機器會旋轉將它們混合。 碎石，也就是圖中標註的小石子，佔整個混合物的一半，而沙則佔另外四分之一。 水泥和水分別佔 15% 和 10% ，然後製成的混凝土便可用於建築工程。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"diagrams illustrate","chinese":"圖示說明"},{"english":"stages and equipment","chinese":"階段及設備"},{"english":"used to make cement","chinese":"用於製造水泥"},{"english":"cement","chinese":"水泥"},{"english":"used to produce concrete","chinese":"用於生產混凝土"},{"english":"concrete","chinese":"混凝土"},{"english":"for construction","chinese":"用於建築"},{"english":"cement manufacture","chinese":"水泥製造"},{"english":"multi-stage linear process","chinese":"多階段線性流程"},{"english":"involving crushing, mixing, heating and grinding","chinese":"涉及壓碎、混合、加熱及研磨"},{"english":"crushing","chinese":"壓碎"},{"english":"mixing","chinese":"混合"},{"english":"heating","chinese":"加熱"},{"english":"grinding","chinese":"研磨"},{"english":"whereas","chinese":"而；相比之下"},{"english":"concrete production","chinese":"混凝土生產"},{"english":"much simpler","chinese":"簡單得多"},{"english":"requiring only","chinese":"只需要"},{"english":"blending of four measured ingredients","chinese":"混合四種已量度的材料"},{"english":"measured ingredients","chinese":"已量度的材料"},{"english":"gravel","chinese":"碎石"},{"english":"accounts for by far the largest share","chinese":"明顯佔最大比例"},{"english":"largest share of concrete","chinese":"混凝土中最大比例"},{"english":"smallest component","chinese":"最小成分"},{"english":"at the beginning of","chinese":"在……開始時"},{"english":"cement-making process","chinese":"水泥製造過程"},{"english":"limestone and clay","chinese":"石灰石及黏土"},{"english":"fed into a crusher","chinese":"被送入壓碎機"},{"english":"crusher","chinese":"壓碎機"},{"english":"reduced to powder","chinese":"被壓碎成粉末"},{"english":"powder","chinese":"粉末"},{"english":"transferred to a mixer","chinese":"被轉移到攪拌機"},{"english":"mixer","chinese":"攪拌機"},{"english":"passes into","chinese":"進入；通過進入"},{"english":"rotating heater","chinese":"旋轉加熱器"},{"english":"as the mixture moves through","chinese":"當混合物通過……時"},{"english":"cylinder","chinese":"圓筒"},{"english":"heat is applied from one end","chinese":"從一端加熱"},{"english":"heated material","chinese":"經加熱的物料"},{"english":"processed in a grinder","chinese":"在研磨機中處理"},{"english":"grinder","chinese":"研磨機"},{"english":"resulting cement","chinese":"形成的水泥"},{"english":"finally packed into bags","chinese":"最後被裝入袋中"},{"english":"concrete production involves fewer stages","chinese":"混凝土生產涉及較少階段"},{"english":"fewer stages","chinese":"較少階段"},{"english":"poured into a concrete mixer","chinese":"被倒入混凝土攪拌機"},{"english":"concrete mixer","chinese":"混凝土攪拌機"},{"english":"rotates to combine them","chinese":"旋轉以混合它們"},{"english":"labelled as small stones","chinese":"標示為小石"},{"english":"small stones","chinese":"小石"},{"english":"makes up half of the mixture","chinese":"佔混合物的一半"},{"english":"half of the mixture","chinese":"混合物的一半"},{"english":"accounts for a further quarter","chinese":"另佔四分之一"},{"english":"a further quarter","chinese":"另外四分之一"},{"english":"constitute 15% and 10%","chinese":"分別構成15%及10%"},{"english":"respectively","chinese":"分別"},{"english":"finished concrete","chinese":"製成的混凝土"},{"english":"ready for building work","chinese":"可用於建築工程"},{"english":"building work","chinese":"建築工程"},{"english":"production process","chinese":"生產過程"},{"english":"raw materials","chinese":"原材料"},{"english":"final product","chinese":"最終產品"},{"english":"construction material","chinese":"建築材料"}]},"model-essay-9-ielts-task1-tables":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-9-ielts-task1-tables","essayKey":"tables:9","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-9-ielts-task1-tables","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-1/tables/table-9","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"The table compares the daily per-person calorie intake from rice, wheat and maize in Cambodia, Poland, Egypt and Mexico.","chinese":"該表比較了柬埔寨、波蘭、埃及和墨西哥四國人民每日每人從米、小麥和玉米中攝取的卡路里。"},{"label":"Overview","english":"Overall, each country shows a clear dependence on a different staple: rice in Cambodia, wheat in Poland and Egypt, and maize in Mexico. Egypt records the broadest consumption across all three foods, while Poland has the narrowest pattern, with no calories from maize.","chinese":"整體而言，每個國家都明顯依賴不同的主食：柬埔寨主要依賴米，波蘭和埃及主要依賴小麥，而墨西哥則主要依賴玉米。 埃及在三種食物中都有較廣泛的攝取，而波蘭的飲食模式最狹窄，完全沒有來自玉米的卡路里。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"Rice is overwhelmingly dominant in Cambodia, at 1,445 calories per person per day, which is nearly three times Egypt's figure of 501. The two remaining countries consume little rice: Mexico stands at 57 calories, while Poland records only 19. Wheat, by contrast, is barely eaten in Cambodia, at just 18 calories. It is the main source in Egypt and Poland, at 1,095 and 865 calories respectively, whereas Mexico's figure is much lower, at 275.","chinese":"米在柬埔寨佔絕對主導地位，達到每日每人 1,445 卡路里，幾乎是埃及 501 卡路里的三倍。 其餘兩國的米攝取量很低：墨西哥為 57 卡路里，而波蘭只有 19 卡路里。 相比之下，小麥在柬埔寨幾乎不被食用，只有 18 卡路里。 小麥是埃及和波蘭的主要來源，分別為 1,095 和 865 卡路里，而墨西哥的數字則低得多，為 275 卡路里。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"Maize consumption follows a different pattern. Mexico records the highest intake, at 1,083 calories, far ahead of Egypt's 578 and over ten times Cambodia's 103. Poland, however, reports no maize consumption at all.","chinese":"玉米的攝取情況則呈現不同模式。 墨西哥的玉米攝取量最高，達 1,083 卡路里，遠高於埃及的 578 卡路里，也超過柬埔寨 103 卡路里的十倍。 然而，波蘭完全沒有玉米攝取量。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"the table compares","chinese":"表格比較"},{"english":"daily per-person calorie intake","chinese":"每人每日卡路里攝取量"},{"english":"calorie intake","chinese":"卡路里攝取量"},{"english":"from rice, wheat and maize","chinese":"來自米飯、小麥和粟米"},{"english":"Cambodia, Poland, Egypt and Mexico","chinese":"柬埔寨、波蘭、埃及和墨西哥"},{"english":"each country shows","chinese":"每個國家都顯示"},{"english":"a clear dependence on","chinese":"明顯依賴……"},{"english":"a different staple","chinese":"不同主糧"},{"english":"staple","chinese":"主糧"},{"english":"rice in Cambodia","chinese":"柬埔寨的米飯"},{"english":"wheat in Poland and Egypt","chinese":"波蘭和埃及的小麥"},{"english":"maize in Mexico","chinese":"墨西哥的粟米"},{"english":"shows the broadest pattern of consumption","chinese":"顯示最廣泛的消費模式"},{"english":"across all three foods","chinese":"在三種食物之中"},{"english":"the narrowest pattern","chinese":"最狹窄的模式"},{"english":"with no calories from","chinese":"沒有來自……的卡路里"},{"english":"overwhelmingly dominant","chinese":"佔絕對主導地位"},{"english":"dominant in","chinese":"在……佔主導地位"},{"english":"at 1,445 calories","chinese":"為1,445卡路里"},{"english":"calories per person per day","chinese":"每人每日卡路里"},{"english":"nearly three times","chinese":"接近……的三倍"},{"english":"Egypt's figure","chinese":"埃及的數字"},{"english":"the two remaining countries","chinese":"其餘兩個國家"},{"english":"consume little rice","chinese":"米飯攝取量很少"},{"english":"stands at","chinese":"為；達到"},{"english":"records only","chinese":"只錄得"},{"english":"by contrast","chinese":"相比之下"},{"english":"barely eaten","chinese":"幾乎不被食用"},{"english":"at just 18 calories","chinese":"只有18卡路里"},{"english":"the main source","chinese":"主要來源"},{"english":"in Egypt and Poland","chinese":"在埃及和波蘭"},{"english":"at 1,095 and 865 calories respectively","chinese":"分別為1,095和865卡路里"},{"english":"respectively","chinese":"分別"},{"english":"whereas","chinese":"而；相反"},{"english":"much lower","chinese":"低得多"},{"english":"maize consumption","chinese":"粟米消費量"},{"english":"follows a different pattern","chinese":"呈現不同模式"},{"english":"records the highest intake","chinese":"錄得最高攝取量"},{"english":"the highest intake","chinese":"最高攝取量"},{"english":"far ahead of","chinese":"遠高於；大幅領先"},{"english":"over ten times","chinese":"超過……的十倍"},{"english":"reports no maize consumption","chinese":"沒有粟米攝取量"},{"english":"no maize consumption at all","chinese":"完全沒有粟米攝取"},{"english":"different pattern of consumption","chinese":"不同消費模式"},{"english":"main calorie source","chinese":"主要卡路里來源"},{"english":"dietary pattern","chinese":"飲食模式"},{"english":"staple-food consumption","chinese":"主糧消費"},{"english":"food intake","chinese":"食物攝取量"},{"english":"vary greatly","chinese":"差異很大"},{"english":"the highest figure","chinese":"最高數字"},{"english":"the lowest figure","chinese":"最低數字"},{"english":"a non-zero figure","chinese":"非零數字"},{"english":"remain heavily dependent on","chinese":"仍然高度依賴……"},{"english":"rely mainly on","chinese":"主要依靠……"},{"english":"account for most calories","chinese":"佔大部分卡路里"},{"english":"contribute no calories","chinese":"沒有提供卡路里"},{"english":"a sharp contrast","chinese":"明顯對比"},{"english":"an uneven distribution","chinese":"分佈不平均"},{"english":"a balanced intake","chinese":"較平均的攝取量"},{"english":"the broadest spread","chinese":"最廣泛的分佈"},{"english":"the narrowest spread","chinese":"最狹窄的分佈"},{"english":"compared with","chinese":"與……相比"},{"english":"contrast strongly with","chinese":"與……形成強烈對比"},{"english":"be concentrated in","chinese":"集中於……"},{"english":"spread across","chinese":"分佈於……"},{"english":"substantial intake","chinese":"大量攝取"},{"english":"minimal intake","chinese":"極少攝取"},{"english":"no intake from","chinese":"沒有來自……的攝取量"},{"english":"the overall pattern","chinese":"整體模式"},{"english":"the dominant food","chinese":"主要食物"},{"english":"the least consumed food","chinese":"消耗最少的食物"},{"english":"the most heavily consumed food","chinese":"消耗最多的食物"},{"english":"the figure for X","chinese":"X 的數字"},{"english":"X's figure is much lower","chinese":"X 的數字低得多"},{"english":"in relative terms","chinese":"以相對數字而言"},{"english":"in absolute terms","chinese":"以實際數字而言"},{"english":"a clear reliance on","chinese":"明顯依賴……"},{"english":"the calorie contribution from","chinese":"來自……的卡路里貢獻"},{"english":"a country-specific pattern","chinese":"因國家而異的模式"},{"english":"unlike","chinese":"不像……"},{"english":"while","chinese":"而"},{"english":"however","chinese":"然而"},{"english":"overall dependence","chinese":"整體依賴"},{"english":"consumption profile","chinese":"消費概況"},{"english":"calorie source","chinese":"卡路里來源"}]},"model-essay-10-ielts-advantage-disadvantage":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-10-ielts-advantage-disadvantage","essayKey":"advantage-disadvantage:10","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-10-ielts-advantage-disadvantage","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/advantage-and-disadvantage/EdmundBd9AdDisAd-Q10","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"In some education systems, girls and boys are educated separately rather than together. Although this arrangement can produce a few short-term academic benefits, I believe its chief disadvantage is more significant: it leaves young people less prepared for the mixed world beyond school.","chinese":"在某些教育制度中，男女生並不是一起接受教育，而是分別在不同的學校就讀。 儘管這種安排可能帶來一些短期的學業好處，但我認為它更大的缺點更為嚴重：它會令年輕人較難為學校以外那個男女共處的真實世界作好準備。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"One advantage of single-sex schooling is that it can reduce distraction during adolescence. In mixed schools, some teenagers become overly concerned with appearance, popularity, or attracting the opposite sex. For example, part of a lesson can be lost to students trying to impress one another or becoming excessively self-conscious. When that pressure is removed, classrooms often become calmer and more focused. A second benefit is that students may participate more confidently in subjects that are often shaped by gender stereotypes. For instance, girls in an all-girls environment may speak up more readily in physics, while boys in a boys’ school may feel less embarrassed about contributing in literature or languages.","chinese":"單一性別學校的一個優點，是它能在青少年時期減少分心的情況。 在男女混合學校中，一些青少年可能會過分在意自己的外表、受歡迎程度，或是否能吸引異性。 例如，課堂上的一部分時間可能會被學生彼此取悅、刻意表現，或過度在意自己形象所浪費掉。 當這種壓力被移除後，課堂氣氛往往會變得更平靜，學生也更能集中注意力。 第二個好處是，學生在一些經常受性別刻板印象影響的科目中，可能會更有自信地參與。 例如，在全女校環境中，女生在物理課上可能會更願意發言；而在男校中，男生在文學或語言課堂上發表意見時，也可能較少感到尷尬。 因此，單一性別教育有時確實能營造出一個更專注、也更能建立自信的學習環境。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"Even so, the main disadvantage is that such schools can create an artificial social bubble. If students spend most of their formative years apart, they may enter adulthood with unnecessary awkwardness or shallow assumptions about the opposite sex. This is a serious problem because real life is not divided in that way: universities, workplaces, and public institutions all require men and women to communicate and cooperate naturally. A student who performs well in a sheltered setting may therefore struggle in mixed-group presentations at university or in workplace teams, where maturity, ease of interaction, and mutual respect matter just as much as academic knowledge.","chinese":"即便如此，這類學校最主要的缺點在於，它們可能會形成一種不自然的社交溫室。 如果學生在成長中最關鍵的那些年大多與異性分隔開來，他們長大後便可能帶著不必要的尷尬感，或對異性抱有流於表面的假設與誤解。 這是一個嚴重的問題，因為現實生活並不是這樣被劃分開來的：大學、職場以及各種公共機構，都要求男女能自然地溝通與合作。 因此，一個在受保護環境中表現優秀的學生，到了大學需要進行男女混合的小組報告時，或進入職場團隊合作時，便可能顯得不知所措；因為在那些情境中，成熟度、互動的自然程度，以及彼此尊重，和學術能力同樣重要。 因此，單一性別教育或許能在短期內保護學生，但同時也可能令他們較難應對成年後真實世界的要求。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"Overall, separate schooling may improve concentration and classroom confidence for some students, but those gains are outweighed by its larger social cost. Schools should not merely help children achieve good grades; they should also prepare them for life as it is actually lived.","chinese":"總結來說，單一性別教育或許能提升某些學生的專注力與課堂自信，但這些好處仍然被它更大的社會代價所蓋過。 學校不應只幫助孩子取得好成績；它們也應該讓學生為現實生活中真正的社會互動作好準備。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"education systems","chinese":"教育制度"},{"english":"be educated separately","chinese":"分開接受教育"},{"english":"rather than together","chinese":"而不是一起"},{"english":"this arrangement","chinese":"這種安排"},{"english":"short-term academic benefits","chinese":"短期學業好處"},{"english":"chief disadvantage","chinese":"主要缺點"},{"english":"more significant","chinese":"更重要"},{"english":"leave young people less prepared for","chinese":"令年輕人較沒有準備面對"},{"english":"the mixed world beyond school","chinese":"學校以外男女混合的世界"},{"english":"single-sex schooling","chinese":"單性別教育"},{"english":"reduce distraction","chinese":"減少分心"},{"english":"during adolescence","chinese":"青春期期間"},{"english":"mixed schools","chinese":"男女混合學校"},{"english":"overly concerned with","chinese":"過分關注"},{"english":"appearance and popularity","chinese":"外表和受歡迎程度"},{"english":"the opposite sex","chinese":"異性"},{"english":"part of a lesson can be lost to","chinese":"一堂課部分時間可能耗於"},{"english":"impress one another","chinese":"令彼此留下深刻印象"},{"english":"excessively self-conscious","chinese":"過分在意自己形象"},{"english":"when that pressure is removed","chinese":"當這種壓力被移除時"},{"english":"calmer and more focused","chinese":"更平靜和更專注"},{"english":"a second benefit","chinese":"第二個好處"},{"english":"participate more confidently","chinese":"更有信心地參與"},{"english":"be shaped by","chinese":"受……影響"},{"english":"gender stereotypes","chinese":"性別定型觀念"},{"english":"an all-girls environment","chinese":"全女校環境"},{"english":"speak up more readily","chinese":"更願意發言"},{"english":"physics","chinese":"物理"},{"english":"a boys' school","chinese":"男校"},{"english":"feel less embarrassed about","chinese":"對……較不感到尷尬"},{"english":"contributing in","chinese":"在……中發表意見"},{"english":"literature or languages","chinese":"文學或語言科"},{"english":"even so","chinese":"即使如此"},{"english":"the main disadvantage","chinese":"主要缺點"},{"english":"an artificial social bubble","chinese":"人為的社交泡沫"},{"english":"formative years","chinese":"成長形成期"},{"english":"enter adulthood with","chinese":"帶着……進入成年"},{"english":"unnecessary awkwardness","chinese":"不必要的尷尬"},{"english":"shallow assumptions about","chinese":"對……的膚淺假設"},{"english":"a serious problem","chinese":"嚴重問題"},{"english":"real life","chinese":"現實生活"},{"english":"be divided in that way","chinese":"以那種方式被分隔"},{"english":"public institutions","chinese":"公共機構"},{"english":"communicate and cooperate naturally","chinese":"自然地溝通和合作"},{"english":"performs well in","chinese":"在……表現良好"},{"english":"a sheltered setting","chinese":"受保護的環境"},{"english":"struggle in","chinese":"在……中感到困難"},{"english":"mixed-group presentations","chinese":"男女混合小組匯報"},{"english":"workplace teams","chinese":"職場團隊"},{"english":"maturity","chinese":"成熟程度"},{"english":"ease of interaction","chinese":"互動時的自然程度"},{"english":"mutual respect","chinese":"互相尊重"},{"english":"just as much as","chinese":"與……同樣重要"},{"english":"academic knowledge","chinese":"學術知識"},{"english":"overall","chinese":"整體而言"},{"english":"separate schooling","chinese":"分開教育"},{"english":"improve concentration","chinese":"提高專注力"},{"english":"classroom confidence","chinese":"課堂信心"},{"english":"those gains","chinese":"那些得益"},{"english":"be outweighed by","chinese":"被……蓋過"},{"english":"larger social cost","chinese":"更大的社會代價"},{"english":"not merely help children achieve good grades","chinese":"不只是幫助孩子取得好成績"},{"english":"achieve good grades","chinese":"取得好成績"},{"english":"prepare them for life","chinese":"讓他們為生活作好準備"},{"english":"as it is actually lived","chinese":"真實生活的樣子"}]},"model-essay-10-ielts-cause-solution":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-10-ielts-cause-solution","essayKey":"cause-solution:10","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-10-ielts-cause-solution","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/problem-and-cause/EdmundBd9CnS-Q10","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"Although walking is one of the simplest and cheapest ways to stay healthy, it has quietly disappeared from many people’s daily routines. This decline stems mainly from car-centred urban design and increasingly sedentary lifestyles. It can be addressed by improving public spaces and making walking a normal part of work, school and transport habits.","chinese":"儘管步行是保持健康最簡單、最便宜的方法之一，它卻已悄然從許多人的日常生活中消失。 這種下降主要源於以汽車為中心的城市設計，以及越來越久坐不動的生活方式。 這個問題可以透過改善公共空間，以及使步行成為工作、學校和交通習慣中的正常部分來解決。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"One major reason is that many modern cities are built around speed rather than movement. When homes, offices, shops and schools are far apart, walking becomes inconvenient or unsafe, especially in areas with wide roads, poor pavements and little shade. As a result, people choose cars, buses or ride-hailing services, not because walking has no value, but because the environment pushes them away from it. Another reason is the rise of desk-based routines. Many people spend long hours in front of screens, and after a tiring day they often choose the easiest option: lifts instead of stairs, online shopping instead of local errands, and entertainment at home instead of a short walk outside. Over time, these small choices harden into a sedentary lifestyle.","chinese":"其中一個主要原因是，許多現代城市是圍繞速度而非身體活動來建造的。 當住宅、辦公室、商店和學校相距甚遠時，步行就會變得不方便或不安全，尤其是在道路寬闊、行人路質素差、遮蔭不足的地區。 結果，人們選擇私家車、巴士或叫車服務，並不是因為步行沒有價值，而是因為環境把他們推離了步行。 另一個原因是以辦公桌為中心的日常模式越來越普遍。 許多人長時間坐在螢幕前，而在疲憊的一天過後，他們往往會選擇最輕鬆的選項：乘搭升降機而不是走樓梯、網上購物而不是到附近辦事、在家娛樂而不是到戶外短暫散步。 久而久之，這些小選擇便會固化成一種久坐不動的生活方式。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"To tackle this problem, governments should make walking safer, easier and more attractive. Wider pavements, shaded streets, better lighting, pedestrian zones and crossings can turn walking from a chore into a daily option. For example, if a neighbourhood has pleasant routes to schools, parks and shops, families are more likely to walk without feeling that they are sacrificing time or safety. At the same time, employers and schools should build movement into ordinary routines. Workplaces can encourage walking meetings and active commuting, while schools can promote walking buses or step-based challenges. These measures matter because they make walking feel like part of daily life, not an extra task squeezed into a crowded schedule.","chinese":"為了解決這個問題，政府應該使步行變得更安全、更容易，也更具吸引力。 更寬闊的行人路、有遮蔭的街道、更好的照明、行人專區和過路設施，可以把步行由一件麻煩事變成一個日常選項。 例如，如果一個社區有舒適的路線通往學校、公園和商店，家庭便更有可能步行，而不會覺得自己正在犧牲時間或安全。 同時，僱主和學校應該把身體活動融入日常安排之中。 工作場所可以鼓勵步行會議和主動通勤，而學校則可以推廣步行巴士或以步數為基礎的挑戰活動。 這些措施之所以重要，是因為它們能讓步行感覺像日常生活的一部分，而不是一項被硬塞進繁忙日程中的額外任務。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, fewer people are walking because their surroundings and routines often make inactivity easier than movement. The most effective response is to design walkable communities and create daily habits that make walking convenient, safe and normal again.","chinese":"總結來說，越來越少人步行，是因為他們所處的環境和日常習慣，往往令不活動比活動更容易。 最有效的應對方法，是設計適合步行的社區，並建立日常習慣，使步行重新變得方便、安全和正常。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"one of the simplest and cheapest ways to","chinese":"……最簡單又最便宜的方法之一"},{"english":"stay healthy","chinese":"保持健康"},{"english":"quietly disappeared from","chinese":"悄悄從……中消失"},{"english":"daily routines","chinese":"日常習慣"},{"english":"this decline stems mainly from","chinese":"這種下降主要源於"},{"english":"car-centred urban design","chinese":"以汽車為中心的城市設計"},{"english":"increasingly sedentary lifestyles","chinese":"越來越久坐的生活方式"},{"english":"be addressed by","chinese":"透過……處理"},{"english":"improving public spaces","chinese":"改善公共空間"},{"english":"a normal part of","chinese":"……的正常一部分"},{"english":"transport habits","chinese":"交通習慣"},{"english":"built around speed rather than movement","chinese":"圍繞速度而非活動來建設"},{"english":"far apart","chinese":"相距很遠"},{"english":"walking becomes inconvenient or unsafe","chinese":"步行變得不方便或不安全"},{"english":"wide roads","chinese":"寬闊馬路"},{"english":"poor pavements","chinese":"欠佳的行人路"},{"english":"little shade","chinese":"缺少遮蔭"},{"english":"as a result","chinese":"因此"},{"english":"ride-hailing services","chinese":"網約車服務"},{"english":"pushes them away from","chinese":"令……遠離"},{"english":"the rise of","chinese":"……的興起"},{"english":"desk-based routines","chinese":"以坐着辦公為主的日常模式"},{"english":"spend long hours in front of screens","chinese":"長時間坐在螢幕前"},{"english":"after a tiring day","chinese":"在疲累的一天後"},{"english":"the easiest option","chinese":"最容易的選擇"},{"english":"lifts instead of stairs","chinese":"升降機而不是樓梯"},{"english":"online shopping instead of local errands","chinese":"網上購物而不是到附近辦事"},{"english":"entertainment at home","chinese":"家中娛樂"},{"english":"harden into","chinese":"逐漸固定成"},{"english":"a sedentary lifestyle","chinese":"久坐的生活方式"},{"english":"tackle this problem","chinese":"處理這個問題"},{"english":"safer, easier and more attractive","chinese":"更安全、更方便、更吸引"},{"english":"wider pavements","chinese":"更寬闊的行人路"},{"english":"shaded streets","chinese":"有遮蔭的街道"},{"english":"better lighting","chinese":"更好的照明"},{"english":"pedestrian zones","chinese":"行人專區"},{"english":"crossings","chinese":"行人過路處"},{"english":"turn walking from a chore into","chinese":"將步行由苦差變成……"},{"english":"a daily option","chinese":"日常選擇"},{"english":"pleasant routes to","chinese":"通往……的舒適路線"},{"english":"are more likely to","chinese":"更有可能"},{"english":"sacrificing time or safety","chinese":"犧牲時間或安全"},{"english":"build movement into","chinese":"將活動融入……"},{"english":"ordinary routines","chinese":"日常安排"},{"english":"walking meetings","chinese":"步行會議"},{"english":"active commuting","chinese":"主動通勤；以步行或踩單車通勤"},{"english":"promote walking buses","chinese":"推廣步行校巴"},{"english":"step-based challenges","chinese":"以步數為目標的挑戰"},{"english":"these measures matter because","chinese":"這些措施重要，因為"},{"english":"part of daily life","chinese":"日常生活的一部分"},{"english":"an extra task","chinese":"額外任務"},{"english":"squeezed into","chinese":"被勉強擠進"},{"english":"a crowded schedule","chinese":"排得很滿的日程"},{"english":"surroundings and routines","chinese":"周邊環境和日常習慣"},{"english":"make inactivity easier than movement","chinese":"令不活動比活動更容易"},{"english":"the most effective response","chinese":"最有效的回應"},{"english":"walkable communities","chinese":"適合步行的社區"},{"english":"create daily habits","chinese":"建立日常習慣"},{"english":"convenient, safe and normal again","chinese":"再次變得方便、安全和正常"}]},"model-essay-10-ielts-direct-question":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-10-ielts-direct-question","essayKey":"direct-question:10","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-10-ielts-direct-question","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/direct-question/EdmundBd9Dir-Q10","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"Alcohol-related crime is a serious social problem because alcohol can weaken self-control, intensify aggression and turn minor disputes into violence. However, I do not think a total ban on alcohol would be an effective way to reduce crime. It would attack the surface of the problem rather than the behaviour that leads to crime.","chinese":"與酒精相關的犯罪是一個嚴重的社會問題，因為酒精會削弱自制力、加劇攻擊性，並把小爭執變成暴力事件。 然而，我不認為全面禁止酒精會是一種有效減少犯罪的方法。 這只會處理問題的表面，而不是處理導致犯罪的行為本身。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"The main weakness of prohibition is that it would be difficult to enforce and could create new criminal activity. If demand for alcohol remains high, people are likely to look for illegal suppliers, and a black market can quickly develop. Criminal groups could then sell unsafe products, exploit vulnerable customers and avoid regulation altogether. In this situation, the police would waste time chasing ordinary drinkers and underground sellers instead of focusing on violent offenders. Therefore, banning alcohol may simply move the problem into the shadows rather than remove it.","chinese":"禁酒的主要弱點在於它難以執行，而且可能製造新的犯罪活動。 如果人們對酒精的需求仍然很高，他們很可能會尋找非法供應者，而黑市也可能迅速形成。 犯罪集團便可能出售不安全的產品、剝削脆弱的顧客，並完全逃避監管。 在這種情況下，警方會把時間浪費在追查普通飲酒者和地下賣家身上，而不是集中處理暴力罪犯。 因此，禁止酒精可能只是把問題推入陰影之中，而不是把問題真正消除。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"A more effective solution is targeted control. Governments should restrict late-night alcohol sales, impose heavy penalties for drunk driving and alcohol-related violence, and require bars to refuse service to clearly intoxicated customers. These measures focus on the moments when drinking is most likely to trigger crime. For example, if a nightclub knows it may lose its licence for serving drunk customers, staff will have a strong reason to intervene before an argument turns into a fight. Prevention at this stage is far more practical than a blanket ban.","chinese":"一個更有效的解決方法是針對性的管制。 政府應該限制深夜售酒、對醉酒駕駛和與酒精相關的暴力行為施加嚴厲懲罰，並要求酒吧拒絕服務明顯醉酒的顧客。 這些措施集中處理飲酒最有可能引發犯罪的時刻。 例如，如果一間夜店知道自己可能因為服務醉酒顧客而失去牌照，員工便會有很強的理由在爭執變成打鬥之前介入。 在這個階段進行預防，遠比一刀切的禁令實際得多。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 3","english":"Another useful measure is treatment and education for people who repeatedly misuse alcohol. Some offenders do not simply need punishment; they need counselling, addiction support and a clearer understanding of the harm they cause. If schools and communities teach young people how alcohol affects judgment and self-control, future crime can be reduced at its roots.","chinese":"另一個有用的措施，是為反覆濫用酒精的人提供治療和教育。 有些犯罪者並不只是需要懲罰；他們需要輔導、戒癮支援，以及更清楚地理解自己所造成的傷害。 如果學校和社區能教導年輕人酒精如何影響判斷力和自制力，未來的犯罪便可以從根源上減少。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, banning alcohol is not an effective anti-crime policy. Stricter regulation, stronger enforcement and proper support for alcohol misuse would reduce alcohol-related crime more realistically and sustainably.","chinese":"總結來說，禁止酒精並不是一項有效的反犯罪政策。 更嚴格的規管、更有力的執法，以及對酒精濫用提供適當支援，才能以更現實和更可持續的方式減少與酒精相關的犯罪。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"alcohol-related crime","chinese":"與酒精有關的罪案"},{"english":"a serious social problem","chinese":"嚴重的社會問題"},{"english":"weaken self-control","chinese":"削弱自制能力"},{"english":"intensify aggression","chinese":"加劇攻擊性"},{"english":"minor disputes","chinese":"小爭執"},{"english":"turn minor disputes into violence","chinese":"將小爭執演變成暴力"},{"english":"a total ban on alcohol","chinese":"全面禁酒"},{"english":"an effective way to reduce crime","chinese":"減少罪案的有效方法"},{"english":"attack the surface of the problem","chinese":"只處理問題表面"},{"english":"rather than the behaviour that leads to crime","chinese":"而不是處理導致罪案的行為"},{"english":"the main weakness of","chinese":"……的主要弱點"},{"english":"prohibition","chinese":"禁令；禁酒令"},{"english":"difficult to enforce","chinese":"難以執行"},{"english":"create new criminal activity","chinese":"製造新的犯罪活動"},{"english":"demand for alcohol remains high","chinese":"對酒精的需求仍然高"},{"english":"look for illegal suppliers","chinese":"尋找非法供應者"},{"english":"a black market","chinese":"黑市"},{"english":"quickly develop","chinese":"迅速形成；迅速發展"},{"english":"criminal groups","chinese":"犯罪集團"},{"english":"unsafe products","chinese":"不安全產品"},{"english":"exploit vulnerable customers","chinese":"剝削弱勢顧客"},{"english":"avoid regulation altogether","chinese":"完全避開規管"},{"english":"waste time chasing","chinese":"浪費時間追查"},{"english":"ordinary drinkers","chinese":"普通飲酒人士"},{"english":"underground sellers","chinese":"地下賣家"},{"english":"violent offenders","chinese":"暴力罪犯"},{"english":"move the problem into the shadows","chinese":"將問題推入暗處"},{"english":"rather than remove it","chinese":"而不是將其消除"},{"english":"targeted control","chinese":"針對性管制"},{"english":"restrict late-night alcohol sales","chinese":"限制深夜酒精銷售"},{"english":"impose heavy penalties for","chinese":"對……施加重罰"},{"english":"drunk driving","chinese":"酒後駕駛"},{"english":"alcohol-related violence","chinese":"與酒精有關的暴力"},{"english":"refuse service to","chinese":"拒絕向……提供服務"},{"english":"clearly intoxicated customers","chinese":"明顯醉酒的顧客"},{"english":"focus on the moments when","chinese":"集中處理……的時刻"},{"english":"trigger crime","chinese":"引發罪案"},{"english":"lose its licence","chinese":"失去牌照"},{"english":"serve drunk customers","chinese":"向醉酒顧客提供服務"},{"english":"have a strong reason to intervene","chinese":"有充分理由介入"},{"english":"before an argument turns into a fight","chinese":"在爭執演變成打鬥之前"},{"english":"prevention at this stage","chinese":"在這個階段作出預防"},{"english":"far more practical than","chinese":"比……實際得多"},{"english":"a blanket ban","chinese":"一刀切禁令"},{"english":"treatment and education","chinese":"治療和教育"},{"english":"repeatedly misuse alcohol","chinese":"反覆濫用酒精"},{"english":"not simply need punishment","chinese":"不只是需要懲罰"},{"english":"counselling","chinese":"輔導"},{"english":"addiction support","chinese":"戒癮支援"},{"english":"a clearer understanding of","chinese":"對……有更清楚的理解"},{"english":"the harm they cause","chinese":"他們造成的傷害"},{"english":"affects judgment and self-control","chinese":"影響判斷力和自制力"},{"english":"be reduced at its roots","chinese":"從根源減少"},{"english":"anti-crime policy","chinese":"打擊罪案政策"},{"english":"stricter regulation","chinese":"更嚴格的規管"},{"english":"stronger enforcement","chinese":"更強力的執法"},{"english":"proper support for alcohol misuse","chinese":"對酒精濫用的適當支援"},{"english":"realistically and sustainably","chinese":"更實際和可持續地"}]},"model-essay-10-ielts-discuss-both-views":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-10-ielts-discuss-both-views","essayKey":"discuss-both-views:10","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-10-ielts-discuss-both-views","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/discuss-both-views-your-opinion/EdmundBd9ExpBth-Q10","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"People often make quick judgments when they meet someone for the first time. While some argue that these early impressions are important because they help us respond quickly in social and professional situations, I believe that it is much wiser not to judge people too soon.","chinese":"人們第一次見到某個人時，往往會很快作出判斷。 雖然有些人認為這些早期印象很重要，因為它們能幫助我們在社交和專業場合中迅速作出反應，但我認為，不要太快評斷別人會明智得多。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"On the one hand, first impressions can be useful because they give us immediate clues about a person’s attitude and behaviour. In many situations, people do not have the luxury of spending a long time getting to know one another. For example, during a job interview, an employer may notice whether a candidate arrives on time, speaks politely and listens carefully. These small details can suggest reliability, confidence and respect. In this sense, a first impression acts like a doorway: it does not show the whole house, but it tells us whether we may want to step inside.","chinese":"一方面，第一印象可能是有用的，因為它們能讓我們即時看出一個人的態度和行為。 在很多情況下，人們並沒有充裕的時間去慢慢了解彼此。 例如，在求職面試中，僱主可能會留意一位應徵者是否準時到達、說話是否有禮貌，以及是否用心聆聽。 這些細節可以反映出可靠、自信和尊重。 從這個角度來看，第一印象就像一道門口：它不能展示整間屋子的全貌，但它能告訴我們是否想走進去看看。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"On the other hand, judging someone too quickly can be deeply unfair, because a first meeting often captures only a temporary version of a person. Someone may seem quiet because they are nervous, distant because they are under pressure, or awkward because they are in an unfamiliar environment. If others label them immediately, that label may stick even when it is inaccurate. For instance, a new student who says very little on the first day may later become kind, loyal and helpful once they feel comfortable. Real character is shown through repeated actions, not through one brief encounter.","chinese":"另一方面，太快評斷一個人可能非常不公平，因為第一次見面往往只捕捉到一個人暫時的狀態。 一個人可能看起來安靜，是因為他們緊張；看起來疏離，是因為他們承受壓力；看起來笨拙，是因為他們身處陌生環境。 如果別人立刻給他們貼上標籤，即使那個標籤並不準確，也可能會一直留在他們身上。 例如，一位新學生第一天可能很少說話，但當他感到自在之後，日後可能會變得善良、忠誠，而且樂於助人。 真正的性格是透過反覆的行動展現出來的，而不是透過一次短暫的相遇。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In my opinion, although first impressions can provide useful signals, they should never become the final basis for judging another person. People are complex, and their true qualities usually appear only over time. Therefore, it is better to treat first impressions as a starting point, not a verdict.","chinese":"在我看來，雖然第一印象能提供有用的訊號，但它們絕不應該成為評斷另一個人的最終依據。 人是複雜的，而他們真正的品質通常只有經過時間才會顯現。 因此，我們最好把第一印象視為一個起點，而不是一項判決。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"crime prevention","chinese":"預防罪案"},{"english":"a central part of","chinese":"……的核心部分"},{"english":"safe and civilised society","chinese":"安全而文明的社會"},{"english":"take responsibility for","chinese":"為……承擔責任"},{"english":"their own safety","chinese":"自身安全"},{"english":"preventing crime","chinese":"預防犯罪"},{"english":"the duty of the state","chinese":"國家的責任"},{"english":"in my opinion","chinese":"在我看來"},{"english":"act sensibly","chinese":"行事謹慎；明智行事"},{"english":"carry the primary responsibility","chinese":"承擔首要責任"},{"english":"authority and resources","chinese":"權力和資源"},{"english":"reduce crime on a large scale","chinese":"大規模減少罪案"},{"english":"individual responsibility","chinese":"個人責任"},{"english":"lower their own risk","chinese":"降低自身風險"},{"english":"making careful choices","chinese":"作出謹慎選擇"},{"english":"install security cameras","chinese":"安裝保安攝錄機"},{"english":"avoid leaving valuables in visible places","chinese":"避免將貴重物品放在顯眼地方"},{"english":"valuables","chinese":"貴重物品"},{"english":"be cautious when","chinese":"在……時保持謹慎"},{"english":"sharing personal information online","chinese":"在網上分享個人資料"},{"english":"many crimes are opportunistic","chinese":"很多罪案是伺機而作的"},{"english":"make themselves an easy target","chinese":"令自己成為容易下手的目標"},{"english":"be more likely to","chinese":"更有可能"},{"english":"take advantage of","chinese":"利用；乘機傷害"},{"english":"from this perspective","chinese":"從這個角度來看"},{"english":"personal awareness","chinese":"個人警覺性"},{"english":"act as the first line of defence","chinese":"作為第一道防線"},{"english":"daily situations","chinese":"日常情況"},{"english":"physically present","chinese":"親身在場"},{"english":"cannot depend mainly on","chinese":"不能主要依賴"},{"english":"be responsible for creating and maintaining","chinese":"負責建立和維持"},{"english":"make society safe","chinese":"令社會安全"},{"english":"effective policing","chinese":"有效警務"},{"english":"fair laws","chinese":"公平法律"},{"english":"street lighting","chinese":"街燈照明"},{"english":"public education","chinese":"公眾教育"},{"english":"social support","chinese":"社會支援"},{"english":"a neighbourhood","chinese":"社區；街區"},{"english":"poor law enforcement","chinese":"執法不力"},{"english":"weak surveillance","chinese":"監察薄弱"},{"english":"few opportunities for young people","chinese":"年輕人機會不足"},{"english":"to a limited extent","chinese":"在有限程度上"},{"english":"lock its doors","chinese":"鎖門"},{"english":"organised crime","chinese":"有組織犯罪"},{"english":"unsafe public spaces","chinese":"不安全的公共空間"},{"english":"wider social problems","chinese":"更廣泛的社會問題"},{"english":"push people towards illegal behaviour","chinese":"推使人走向非法行為"},{"english":"illegal behaviour","chinese":"非法行為"},{"english":"coordinated public action","chinese":"協調一致的公共行動"},{"english":"private caution","chinese":"個人謹慎"},{"english":"take reasonable steps to","chinese":"採取合理措施去"},{"english":"protect themselves","chinese":"保護自己"},{"english":"replace the role of government","chinese":"取代政府的角色"},{"english":"a social problem rather than","chinese":"是社會問題，而不是"},{"english":"merely a personal inconvenience","chinese":"只屬個人不便"},{"english":"the state","chinese":"國家；政府"},{"english":"chiefly responsible for","chinese":"對……負主要責任"}]},"model-essay-10-ielts-opinion":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-10-ielts-opinion","essayKey":"opinion:10","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-10-ielts-opinion","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/opinions/EdmundBd9OP-Q10","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"In modern markets, businesses are under constant pressure to attract attention, so advertising is often treated as the decisive ingredient of commercial success. It is therefore unsurprising that some people believe marketing and promotion are the key to a successful business. This essay completely disagrees, because firms prosper above all when they offer genuine value and operate efficiently.","chinese":"在現代市場中，企業不斷承受吸引注意力的壓力，因此廣告常常被視為商業成功的決定性因素。 因此，有些人認為市場推廣和宣傳是企業成功的關鍵，這其實並不令人意外。 本文完全不同意這個看法， 因為企業真正能夠繁榮發展，最重要的是它們能提供真實價值並且有效率地運作。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"The primary reason promotion is not the key is that customers remain loyal only when a business delivers something worthwhile. A persuasive campaign may generate initial sales, but continued success comes from satisfaction: when goods are dependable or services are consistently professional, buyers return, spend more over time and recommend the company to others. This creates repeat custom and organic growth, both of which are far more stable than attention purchased through advertising. For example, a new restaurant may fill its tables through online discounts and social-media campaigns, yet those customers will not return if the food is mediocre or the staff are inattentive. In addition, strong products develop reputations of their own. Once trust is established, word of mouth becomes a powerful source of demand, showing that quality, rather than promotion, is the real engine of long-term success.","chinese":"宣傳之所以不是關鍵，最主要的原因是：只有當企業真正提供有價值的東西時，顧客才會保持忠誠。 一場有說服力的宣傳活動也許能帶來最初的銷售，但持續的成功來自滿意度：當產品可靠、服務穩定而專業時，顧客才會再度光顧、長期花費更多，並向他人推薦這家公司。 這樣便能帶來回頭客和自然成長，而這兩者都比透過廣告買來的關注穩定得多。 例如，一間新餐廳也許能透過網上折扣和社交媒體宣傳坐滿顧客，但如果食物品質普通，或員工服務不夠周到，那些顧客就不會再回來。 此外，優秀的產品本身也會建立起自己的聲譽。 一旦信任建立起來，口碑就會成為強大的需求來源，這說明真正推動長期成功的引擎是品質，而不是宣傳。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"Equally important is the way a business is managed. Even the most visible brand will struggle if it cannot control costs, train employees properly or deliver what it has promised. In such cases, marketing may actually accelerate failure: the more customers a weak company attracts, the more delayed orders, complaints and refund requests it creates, and these quickly damage public confidence. This pattern is common in e-commerce, where an aggressively advertised firm can still lose market share if deliveries are unreliable or customer support is ineffective. Sound management also enables a company to adapt, whether by improving products, responding to competition or investing wisely. These decisions determine whether a business survives beyond the short term, whereas promotion merely amplifies whatever underlying strengths or weaknesses already exist.","chinese":"同樣重要的，還有企業本身的管理方式。 即使是一個曝光率再高的品牌，如果無法控制成本、妥善培訓員工，或履行自己作出的承諾，最終也會陷入困境。 在這種情況下，市場推廣甚至可能加速失敗：一家本來就薄弱的公司吸引越多顧客，就會製造出越多延誤訂單、投訴和退款要求，而這些問題很快就會損害公眾信心。 這種情況在電子商務中十分常見：一家大力宣傳的公司，如果送貨不可靠或客服支援無效，仍然可能失去市場佔有率。 良好的管理也能讓企業具備適應能力，不論是改良產品、回應競爭，還是作出明智投資。 這些決定才真正左右一家企業能否超越短期生存，而宣傳本身不過只是放大原本已存在的優勢或弱點而已。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, I completely disagree that marketing and promotion are the key to a successful business. They may attract initial attention, but durable success is built on genuine value, customer trust and competent management.","chinese":"總而言之，我完全不同意市場推廣和宣傳是企業成功的關鍵。 它們也許能帶來最初的注意力，但持久的成功是建立在真實價值、顧客信任以及有能力的管理之上的。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"in modern markets","chinese":"在現代市場中"},{"english":"be under constant pressure to","chinese":"持續面對……的壓力"},{"english":"attract attention","chinese":"吸引注意"},{"english":"be treated as","chinese":"被視為"},{"english":"the decisive ingredient of","chinese":"……的決定性因素"},{"english":"commercial success","chinese":"商業成功"},{"english":"it is therefore unsurprising that","chinese":"因此難怪"},{"english":"marketing and promotion","chinese":"市場推廣和宣傳"},{"english":"the key to","chinese":"……的關鍵"},{"english":"firms prosper","chinese":"企業興旺發展"},{"english":"above all","chinese":"最重要的是"},{"english":"offer genuine value","chinese":"提供真正價值"},{"english":"operate efficiently","chinese":"高效營運"},{"english":"the primary reason","chinese":"主要原因"},{"english":"remain loyal","chinese":"保持忠誠"},{"english":"deliver something worthwhile","chinese":"提供有價值的東西"},{"english":"a persuasive campaign","chinese":"有說服力的宣傳活動"},{"english":"generate initial sales","chinese":"帶來初期銷售"},{"english":"continued success","chinese":"持續成功"},{"english":"come from satisfaction","chinese":"來自滿意度"},{"english":"goods are dependable","chinese":"商品可靠"},{"english":"services are consistently professional","chinese":"服務一貫專業"},{"english":"spend more over time","chinese":"隨時間花費更多"},{"english":"recommend the company to others","chinese":"向其他人推薦公司"},{"english":"repeat custom","chinese":"回頭客生意"},{"english":"organic growth","chinese":"自然增長"},{"english":"far more stable than","chinese":"比……穩定得多"},{"english":"attention purchased through advertising","chinese":"透過廣告買回來的關注"},{"english":"fill its tables","chinese":"坐滿餐桌；客滿"},{"english":"online discounts","chinese":"網上折扣"},{"english":"social-media campaigns","chinese":"社交媒體宣傳活動"},{"english":"mediocre","chinese":"平平無奇；質素一般"},{"english":"inattentive","chinese":"不夠細心；服務不周"},{"english":"in addition","chinese":"此外"},{"english":"develop reputations of their own","chinese":"建立本身的名聲"},{"english":"trust is established","chinese":"信任建立後"},{"english":"word of mouth","chinese":"口碑"},{"english":"a powerful source of demand","chinese":"強大的需求來源"},{"english":"rather than promotion","chinese":"而不是宣傳"},{"english":"the real engine of","chinese":"……的真正推動力"},{"english":"long-term success","chinese":"長遠成功"},{"english":"equally important","chinese":"同樣重要的是"},{"english":"the way a business is managed","chinese":"企業的管理方式"},{"english":"the most visible brand","chinese":"最受注目的品牌"},{"english":"will struggle if","chinese":"如果……便會陷入困難"},{"english":"control costs","chinese":"控制成本"},{"english":"train employees properly","chinese":"適當培訓員工"},{"english":"deliver what it has promised","chinese":"履行承諾"},{"english":"in such cases","chinese":"在這些情況下"},{"english":"accelerate failure","chinese":"加速失敗"},{"english":"the more customers a company attracts","chinese":"公司吸引越多顧客"},{"english":"delayed orders","chinese":"延誤訂單"},{"english":"complaints","chinese":"投訴"},{"english":"refund requests","chinese":"退款要求"},{"english":"damage public confidence","chinese":"損害公眾信心"},{"english":"this pattern is common in","chinese":"這種情況在……很常見"},{"english":"e-commerce","chinese":"電子商務"},{"english":"an aggressively advertised firm","chinese":"大力賣廣告的公司"},{"english":"lose market share","chinese":"失去市場佔有率"},{"english":"deliveries are unreliable","chinese":"送貨不可靠"},{"english":"customer support is ineffective","chinese":"客戶支援成效不彰"},{"english":"sound management","chinese":"穩健管理"},{"english":"enable a company to adapt","chinese":"使公司能夠適應"},{"english":"whether by","chinese":"不論是透過"},{"english":"improving products","chinese":"改善產品"},{"english":"responding to competition","chinese":"回應競爭"},{"english":"investing wisely","chinese":"明智地投資"},{"english":"determine whether","chinese":"決定是否"},{"english":"survive beyond the short term","chinese":"短期過後仍能生存"},{"english":"whereas","chinese":"然而"},{"english":"merely amplifies","chinese":"只是放大"},{"english":"underlying strengths or weaknesses","chinese":"潛在優勢或弱點"},{"english":"attract initial attention","chinese":"吸引初期注意"},{"english":"durable success","chinese":"持久成功"},{"english":"be built on","chinese":"建基於"},{"english":"customer trust","chinese":"顧客信任"},{"english":"competent management","chinese":"有能力的管理"}]},"model-essay-10-ielts-task1-maps":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-10-ielts-task1-maps","essayKey":"maps:10","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-10-ielts-task1-maps","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-1/maps/maps-10","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"The two maps compare an island before and after the construction of tourist facilities.","chinese":"這兩張地圖比較了一個島嶼在旅遊設施建設前後的情況。"},{"label":"Overview","english":"Overall, the island has been transformed from a largely undeveloped natural area into a compact resort, with accommodation, catering facilities and transport links added mainly in the western and central sections. However, the beach and most palm-tree areas have been retained, while the eastern end remains largely untouched.","chinese":"整體而言，這座島已經由一個基本未開發的自然區域轉變成一個小型度假區，住宿、餐飲設施和交通連接主要集中在西部和中部地區。 然而，海灘和大部分棕櫚樹區域被保留下來，而島的東端基本上仍未受到改動。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"Before development, the island contained only natural features. A beach lay on the western shore, and groups of palm trees were scattered across the middle and, more densely, towards the east. There were no buildings, roads, paths or landing facilities, so access to and movement around the island were not formally provided.","chinese":"在開發前，這座島只包含自然特徵。 一片海灘位於西岸，而棕櫚樹群分布在島的中部，並且在東部一帶更加密集。 圖中沒有建築物、道路、小徑或登岸設施，因此島上的進出和內部移動並沒有正式的安排。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"Following construction, two clusters of accommodation huts have been built: one close to the beach in the west and another around an open central area. These are linked by footpaths, one of which also runs to the beach, now marked for swimming. A reception building stands near the centre, with a restaurant just to its north. To the south, a pier has been added for boats, and vehicle tracks now connect it with both main service buildings.","chinese":"建設完成後，兩組住宿小屋被建成：一組靠近西部的海灘，另一組則圍繞中部的一片開放區域。 這些住宿小屋由步行小徑連接，其中一條小徑也通向海灘，而海灘現在被標示為游泳區。 一座接待處位於島的中部附近，其北面緊鄰一間餐廳。 在南部，一座供船隻使用的碼頭已被增設，而車道現在把碼頭與兩座主要服務建築連接起來。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"the two maps below","chinese":"以下兩幅地圖"},{"english":"before and after","chinese":"……之前和之後"},{"english":"the construction of","chinese":"……的興建"},{"english":"tourist facilities","chinese":"旅遊設施"},{"english":"summarise the information","chinese":"概述資料"},{"english":"by selecting and reporting","chinese":"透過選取並報告……"},{"english":"the main features","chinese":"主要特徵"},{"english":"make comparisons where relevant","chinese":"在相關之處作出比較"},{"english":"compare X before and after Y","chinese":"比較 X 在 Y 前後的情況"},{"english":"has been transformed from","chinese":"已由……轉變"},{"english":"a largely undeveloped natural area","chinese":"大致未發展的自然地區"},{"english":"a compact resort","chinese":"小型集中式度假區"},{"english":"accommodation","chinese":"住宿設施"},{"english":"catering facilities","chinese":"餐飲設施"},{"english":"transport links","chinese":"交通連接"},{"english":"have been added mainly in","chinese":"主要增設於……"},{"english":"the western and central sections","chinese":"西部及中央部分"},{"english":"have been retained","chinese":"得以保留"},{"english":"palm-tree areas","chinese":"棕櫚樹區"},{"english":"the eastern end","chinese":"東端"},{"english":"remains largely untouched","chinese":"大致未受影響；大致保持原貌"},{"english":"before development","chinese":"發展前"},{"english":"natural features","chinese":"自然特徵"},{"english":"lay on the western shore","chinese":"位於西岸"},{"english":"the western shore","chinese":"西岸"},{"english":"groups of palm trees","chinese":"一簇簇棕櫚樹"},{"english":"were scattered across","chinese":"散佈於……各處"},{"english":"across the middle","chinese":"橫跨中部"},{"english":"more densely","chinese":"更密集地"},{"english":"towards the east","chinese":"朝東面；在東面一帶"},{"english":"no buildings, roads or paths","chinese":"沒有建築物、道路或小徑"},{"english":"landing facilities","chinese":"登岸設施"},{"english":"access to","chinese":"前往……的通道"},{"english":"movement around","chinese":"在……內四處移動"},{"english":"access to and movement around","chinese":"前往及在……內移動"},{"english":"were not formally provided","chinese":"並無正式提供"},{"english":"following construction","chinese":"建成後"},{"english":"two clusters of","chinese":"兩組；兩簇"},{"english":"accommodation huts","chinese":"住宿小屋"},{"english":"have been built","chinese":"已建成"},{"english":"close to the beach","chinese":"靠近海灘"},{"english":"around an open central area","chinese":"圍繞中央空地"},{"english":"an open central area","chinese":"中央空地"},{"english":"are linked by","chinese":"由……連接"},{"english":"footpaths","chinese":"行人小徑"},{"english":"one of which","chinese":"其中一條"},{"english":"runs to the beach","chinese":"通往海灘"},{"english":"marked for swimming","chinese":"標示為游泳區"},{"english":"a reception building","chinese":"接待處大樓"},{"english":"stands near the centre","chinese":"位於中心附近"},{"english":"a restaurant","chinese":"餐廳"},{"english":"just to its north","chinese":"就在其北面"},{"english":"to the south","chinese":"在南面"},{"english":"a pier","chinese":"碼頭"},{"english":"has been added for","chinese":"已增設作……用途"},{"english":"for boats","chinese":"供船隻使用"},{"english":"vehicle tracks","chinese":"車道；車輛通道"},{"english":"now connect X with Y","chinese":"現時連接 X 和 Y"},{"english":"both main service buildings","chinese":"兩座主要服務建築"},{"english":"service buildings","chinese":"服務建築"},{"english":"the developed area","chinese":"已發展區域"},{"english":"be concentrated in","chinese":"集中於……"},{"english":"remain natural","chinese":"保持自然狀態"},{"english":"new tourist infrastructure","chinese":"新旅遊基建"},{"english":"a small-scale development","chinese":"小規模發展"},{"english":"retain its natural character","chinese":"保留其自然特色"}]},"model-essay-10-ielts-task1-tables":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-10-ielts-task1-tables","essayKey":"tables:10","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-10-ielts-task1-tables","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-1/tables/table-10","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"The table compares the proportions of pupils enrolled in four types of secondary school in 2000, 2005 and 2009.","chinese":"該表格比較了 2000 年、 2005 年和 2009 年四類中學的學生就讀比例。"},{"label":"Overview","english":"Overall, attendance shifted markedly away from voluntary-controlled and grammar schools towards community schools. While voluntary-controlled schools had by far the largest share at the beginning, community schools became the dominant type by 2009, and specialist schools remained the smallest or joint-smallest category throughout.","chinese":"整體而言，學生就讀比例明顯由志願控制學校和文法學校轉向社區學校。 雖然志願控制學校在最初佔比遠遠最高，但到 2009 年，社區學校已成為最主要的類別，而專科學校在整段期間一直是最小或並列最小的類別。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"In 2000, just over half of pupils attended voluntary-controlled schools, at 52%, making this sector more than twice as large as grammar schools, which accounted for 24%. Specialist and community schools each had 12%, so their combined share was equal to that of grammar schools alone. By 2005, however, voluntary-controlled schools had fallen to 38%, while community schools had climbed sharply to 32%, narrowing the gap between the two leading categories to only six percentage points.","chinese":"在 2000 年，剛過半數學生就讀於志願控制學校，比例為 52% ，使這一類別的佔比超過文法學校的兩倍；文法學校則佔 24% 。 專科學校和社區學校各佔 12% ，因此兩者合計比例正好等同於文法學校單獨的比例。 然而，到 2005 年，志願控制學校已下降至 38% ，而社區學校則大幅上升至 32%，使兩個主要類別之間的差距收窄至僅 6 個百分點。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"The change became more pronounced by 2009. Community schools rose further to 58%, almost five times their initial proportion. By contrast, voluntary-controlled schools dropped to 20%, less than half their 2000 figure. Grammar schools also declined steadily, from 24% to 12%, while specialist schools slipped only slightly, from 12% to 10%.","chinese":"到 2009 年，這一變化變得更加明顯。 社區學校進一步上升至 58% ，幾乎是其最初比例的五倍。 相比之下，志願控制學校下降至 20% ，不到其 2000 年數字的一半。 文法學校也持續下降，從 24% 跌至 12% ；而專科學校則只輕微下滑，從 12% 降至。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"the table shows","chinese":"表格顯示"},{"english":"the proportions of pupils","chinese":"學生比例"},{"english":"attending four secondary school types","chinese":"就讀四類中學"},{"english":"secondary school types","chinese":"中學類型"},{"english":"between 2000 and 2009","chinese":"在2000年至2009年間"},{"english":"summarise the information","chinese":"概述資料"},{"english":"selecting and reporting","chinese":"選取並報告"},{"english":"the main features","chinese":"主要特徵"},{"english":"make comparisons where relevant","chinese":"在相關之處作出比較"},{"english":"the table compares","chinese":"表格比較"},{"english":"enrolled in","chinese":"就讀於"},{"english":"four types of secondary school","chinese":"四類中學"},{"english":"in 2000, 2005 and 2009","chinese":"在2000年、2005年及2009年"},{"english":"Overall","chinese":"整體而言"},{"english":"attendance shifted markedly","chinese":"就讀比例明顯轉移"},{"english":"shifted markedly away from","chinese":"明顯從……轉移"},{"english":"towards community schools","chinese":"轉向社區學校"},{"english":"voluntary-controlled schools","chinese":"自願受控學校"},{"english":"grammar schools","chinese":"文法學校"},{"english":"community schools","chinese":"社區學校"},{"english":"specialist schools","chinese":"專科學校"},{"english":"had by far the largest share","chinese":"遠遠佔最大比例"},{"english":"the largest share","chinese":"最大比例"},{"english":"at the beginning","chinese":"在初期"},{"english":"became the dominant type","chinese":"成為主導類型"},{"english":"the dominant type","chinese":"主導類型"},{"english":"by 2009","chinese":"到2009年"},{"english":"remained the smallest category","chinese":"仍然是最小類別"},{"english":"joint-smallest category","chinese":"並列最小類別"},{"english":"throughout","chinese":"在整個時期內"},{"english":"In 2000","chinese":"在2000年"},{"english":"just over half of pupils","chinese":"略多於一半學生"},{"english":"attended voluntary-controlled schools","chinese":"就讀自願受控學校"},{"english":"at 52%","chinese":"為52%"},{"english":"making this sector","chinese":"使這一類別"},{"english":"this sector","chinese":"這一類別"},{"english":"more than twice as large as","chinese":"是……的兩倍多"},{"english":"accounted for 24%","chinese":"佔24%"},{"english":"each had 12%","chinese":"各佔12%"},{"english":"their combined share","chinese":"它們的合計比例"},{"english":"was equal to","chinese":"等於"},{"english":"grammar schools alone","chinese":"單是文法學校"},{"english":"By 2005","chinese":"到2005年"},{"english":"had fallen to","chinese":"已下降至"},{"english":"while","chinese":"而"},{"english":"had climbed sharply to","chinese":"已急升至"},{"english":"climbed sharply","chinese":"急升"},{"english":"narrowing the gap between","chinese":"收窄……之間的差距"},{"english":"the gap between","chinese":"……之間的差距"},{"english":"the two leading categories","chinese":"兩個領先類別"},{"english":"only six percentage points","chinese":"只有六個百分點"},{"english":"percentage points","chinese":"百分點"},{"english":"became more pronounced","chinese":"變得更加明顯"},{"english":"more pronounced","chinese":"更加明顯"},{"english":"rose further to","chinese":"進一步上升至"},{"english":"almost five times","chinese":"幾乎是五倍"},{"english":"their initial proportion","chinese":"其最初比例"},{"english":"By contrast","chinese":"相比之下"},{"english":"dropped to 20%","chinese":"下降至20%"},{"english":"less than half","chinese":"不足一半"},{"english":"their 2000 figure","chinese":"它們2000年的數字"},{"english":"declined steadily","chinese":"穩步下降"},{"english":"from 24% to 12%","chinese":"由24%下降至12%"},{"english":"slipped only slightly","chinese":"只輕微下跌"},{"english":"from 12% to 10%","chinese":"由12%跌至10%"}]},"model-essay-11-ielts-advantage-disadvantage":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-11-ielts-advantage-disadvantage","essayKey":"advantage-disadvantage:11","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-11-ielts-advantage-disadvantage","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/advantage-and-disadvantage/EdmundBd9AdDisAd-Q11","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"As classrooms become more digital, a growing number of schools no longer insist that children spend significant time improving their handwriting. This shift may free up lessons for computer-based skills and reduce pressure on pupils whose script is untidy. Nevertheless, I believe the disadvantages far outweigh the advantages, because handwriting still plays a crucial role in both learning and everyday independence.","chinese":"無論在職場還是私人生活中，愈來愈多的溝通如今都是透過數碼科技進行，而非面對面交流。 儘管這種發展可能削弱人際關係的質素，並增加誤解的風險， 我認為整體而言，它的優點更為顯著，因為它大幅提升了溝通效率，並使人們即使相隔遙遠，仍能維持聯繫。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"The main drawback is education. Writing by hand is a slower and more deliberate process than typing, so children must select key ideas, process language carefully and form each word consciously. This extra mental effort improves concentration, reinforces spelling and helps information stay in long-term memory. For example, a pupil who writes a short summary of a science lesson in a notebook is more likely to remember the key concepts than one who copies full sentences onto a screen with little thought. A second problem is that regular handwriting practice develops fine motor control and written fluency. If schools neglect it, children may become less confident in situations where handwriting is still required, such as handwritten tests, annotating printed texts or completing forms.","chinese":"科技化溝通最主要的優勢在於速度與便利性。 在專業環境中，電子郵件、即時通訊平台及視像會議免除了人們出行的需要，並使決策幾乎可以即時作出。 這不但縮短了回應時間、降低了營運成本，亦令企業能夠相當輕鬆地協調分布於不同城市，甚至不同大洲的團隊。 例如，一位經理可以透過一次網上會議便與海外同事解決生產問題，而不必等待數天後才進行面對面討論。 同樣的原理也適用於社交層面：居於不同地方的父母、子女及朋友，仍可透過通話和訊息每天保持聯絡。 因此，人際關係更容易維繫，也較不容易隨時間而逐漸疏遠。 例如，即使一家人的成員分散在不同國家，他們仍可透過視像通話分享日常近況，並彼此提供情感支持。 因此，數碼溝通在工作與個人生活兩方面都大大提升了效率與可及性。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"Admittedly, there are some benefits to reducing the emphasis on handwriting. First, schools can devote more time to typing, online research and digital communication, which are undeniably useful in higher education and many modern jobs. For instance, teaching children how to use collaborative software may prepare them more directly for office-based work. Second, weaker writers may feel less frustrated if neat penmanship is no longer treated as a sign of intelligence. However, these advantages are relatively limited. Digital literacy can be taught alongside handwriting rather than instead of it, and pupils with poor handwriting can be supported through targeted help without lowering expectations for everyone.","chinese":"然而，數碼溝通亦存在重要缺點，其中最嚴重的一點，是它缺乏情感層次。 面對面交流能傳遞語氣、面部表情及肢體語言，而這些元素有助人們更準確地理解意思、表達同理心，並建立信任。 當這些線索消失後，訊息便更容易被誤解，從而引發困惑，甚至衝突。 例如，一封簡短的電郵或文字訊息，即使本無冒犯之意，也可能給人冷淡甚至帶有敵意的感覺。 這在職場中尤其成問題，因為信任與細膩的理解對領導、協商及團隊合作都至關重要。 長遠而言，過度依賴螢幕亦可能助長表面的社交習慣，令人在網上看似時刻保持聯繫，卻依然感到孤立。 例如，一個人即使經常透過社交媒體與他人交談，仍可能感到孤單，因為數碼接觸始終無法完全取代真實的關注與人的陪伴。 因此，儘管科技讓溝通變得更容易，它同時亦可能削弱清晰度、信任感與情感深度。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, although this trend may appear practical in a technological age, its disadvantages are clearly more significant. Schools should modernise their curricula without treating handwriting as an obsolete skill, since it remains essential for deeper learning, functional competence and children’s overall development.","chinese":"總括而言，透過科技進行溝通在效率與可及性方面具有明顯優勢，儘管它可能削弱人際互動的深度與清晰度。 整體而言，我認為其優點大於缺點，因為數碼工具使工作與個人生活中的溝通都能跨越時間與距離而有效運作。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"classrooms become more digital","chinese":"課室變得更加數碼化"},{"english":"a growing number of","chinese":"越來越多的"},{"english":"no longer insist that","chinese":"不再堅持"},{"english":"spend significant time","chinese":"花大量時間"},{"english":"improving their handwriting","chinese":"改善書寫"},{"english":"this shift","chinese":"這種轉變"},{"english":"free up lessons for","chinese":"騰出課堂時間給……"},{"english":"computer-based skills","chinese":"電腦相關技能"},{"english":"reduce pressure on","chinese":"減輕……的壓力"},{"english":"pupils whose script is untidy","chinese":"字跡潦草的學生"},{"english":"nevertheless","chinese":"然而"},{"english":"far outweigh the advantages","chinese":"遠遠超過好處"},{"english":"plays a crucial role in","chinese":"在……中發揮關鍵作用"},{"english":"everyday independence","chinese":"日常生活上的獨立能力"},{"english":"the main drawback","chinese":"主要缺點"},{"english":"writing by hand","chinese":"用手書寫"},{"english":"a slower and more deliberate process","chinese":"較慢而更需要思考的過程"},{"english":"select key ideas","chinese":"篩選重點概念"},{"english":"process language carefully","chinese":"仔細處理語言"},{"english":"form each word consciously","chinese":"有意識地寫出每個字"},{"english":"extra mental effort","chinese":"額外的腦力付出"},{"english":"improves concentration","chinese":"提升專注力"},{"english":"reinforces spelling","chinese":"鞏固串字能力"},{"english":"stay in long-term memory","chinese":"留在長期記憶中"},{"english":"a short summary of","chinese":"……的簡短摘要"},{"english":"key concepts","chinese":"核心概念"},{"english":"copies full sentences onto a screen","chinese":"將完整句子複製到螢幕上"},{"english":"with little thought","chinese":"幾乎沒有思考"},{"english":"regular handwriting practice","chinese":"定期手寫練習"},{"english":"develops fine motor control","chinese":"發展精細動作控制能力"},{"english":"written fluency","chinese":"書寫流暢度"},{"english":"neglect it","chinese":"忽視它"},{"english":"less confident in situations where","chinese":"在……情況下較缺乏信心"},{"english":"handwriting is still required","chinese":"仍然需要手寫"},{"english":"handwritten tests","chinese":"手寫測驗"},{"english":"annotating printed texts","chinese":"在印刷文本上作註解"},{"english":"completing forms","chinese":"填寫表格"},{"english":"admittedly","chinese":"誠然"},{"english":"reducing the emphasis on","chinese":"減少對……的重視"},{"english":"devote more time to","chinese":"投放更多時間於……"},{"english":"typing","chinese":"打字"},{"english":"online research","chinese":"網上資料搜集"},{"english":"digital communication","chinese":"數碼溝通"},{"english":"undeniably useful in","chinese":"在……中無可否認地有用"},{"english":"higher education","chinese":"高等教育"},{"english":"modern jobs","chinese":"現代工作"},{"english":"collaborative software","chinese":"協作軟件"},{"english":"prepare them more directly for","chinese":"令他們更直接為……作準備"},{"english":"office-based work","chinese":"辦公室工作"},{"english":"weaker writers","chinese":"書寫能力較弱的學生"},{"english":"feel less frustrated","chinese":"感到較少挫敗"},{"english":"neat penmanship","chinese":"工整字體"},{"english":"be treated as","chinese":"被視為"},{"english":"a sign of intelligence","chinese":"智力的標誌"},{"english":"relatively limited","chinese":"相對有限"},{"english":"digital literacy","chinese":"數碼素養"},{"english":"alongside handwriting rather than instead of it","chinese":"與手寫並行，而不是取代手寫"},{"english":"targeted help","chinese":"針對性幫助"},{"english":"without lowering expectations for everyone","chinese":"不降低對所有人的期望"},{"english":"appear practical in a technological age","chinese":"在科技時代看似實際"},{"english":"clearly more significant","chinese":"明顯更重要"},{"english":"modernise their curricula","chinese":"更新課程"},{"english":"obsolete skill","chinese":"過時技能"},{"english":"remains essential for","chinese":"對……仍然必要"},{"english":"deeper learning","chinese":"更深入的學習"},{"english":"functional competence","chinese":"實用能力"},{"english":"overall development","chinese":"全面發展"}]},"model-essay-11-ielts-cause-solution":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-11-ielts-cause-solution","essayKey":"cause-solution:11","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-11-ielts-cause-solution","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/problem-and-cause/EdmundBd9CnS-Q11","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"In many parts of the world, rural-to-urban migration has become increasingly common. This movement is mainly driven by the belief that cities offer better life chances than villages or small towns. However, it can place serious pressure on urban systems and leave rural communities increasingly fragile.","chinese":"在世界許多地方，從農村遷往城市的現象已變得越來越普遍。 這種流動主要是由一種信念所推動：城市比村莊或小城鎮能提供更好的人生機會。 然而，這可能會對城市系統造成嚴重壓力，並使農村社區變得越來越脆弱。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"One major reason for this trend is economic opportunity. In many rural areas, work is still closely connected to farming, local trade, or small family businesses, all of which may provide unstable income. By contrast, cities usually offer a wider range of jobs in factories, offices, retail, hospitality, and technology. A young person who moves to a city, for example, may start with an entry-level position but still see a path towards promotion, training, and higher earnings. This sense of upward mobility makes urban life extremely attractive.","chinese":"造成這一趨勢的一個主要原因是經濟機會。 在許多農村地區，工作仍然與農業、本地貿易或小型家庭生意密切相關，而這些工作都可能帶來不穩定的收入。 相比之下，城市通常在工廠、辦公室、零售、酒店服務業和科技行業中提供更廣泛的工作選擇。 例如，一個搬到城市的年輕人可能一開始只是從事入門級職位，但仍然能看到晉升、培訓和獲得更高收入的路徑。 這種向上流動的感覺使城市生活極具吸引力。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"Another important reason is access to essential services. Cities tend to have better schools, universities, hospitals, transport networks, and digital infrastructure. For families, this can be decisive because education and healthcare are not luxuries; they are the foundations of long-term security. If a rural parent believes that a city school will give their child stronger qualifications and wider social exposure, relocation may seem not only sensible but necessary.","chinese":"另一個重要原因是能夠獲得基本服務。 城市往往擁有更好的學校、大學、醫院、交通網絡和數位基礎設施。 對家庭而言，這可能是決定性的因素，因為教育和醫療並不是奢侈品；它們是長遠保障的基礎。 如果一位農村家長相信城市學校能給孩子更強的資歷和更廣闊的社會接觸，那麼搬遷可能看起來不只是明智的選擇，而是必要的選擇。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 3","english":"This movement, however, can cause several problems. The most immediate one is urban overcrowding. When population growth is faster than planning, housing becomes expensive, roads become congested, and public services are stretched thin. As a result, some migrants may end up living in poor-quality accommodation while competing for limited jobs. At the same time, rural areas may decline. As younger and more capable residents leave, villages can lose workers, customers, and future community leaders. Schools may close, local businesses may struggle, and elderly residents may become increasingly isolated.","chinese":"然而，這種人口流動可能造成幾個問題。 最直接的一個問題是城市過度擁擠。 當人口增長快於城市規劃時，住房會變得昂貴，道路會變得擁堵，而公共服務也會被拉得非常緊張。 結果是，一些移民最終可能住在質素較差的住所，同時還要競爭有限的工作機會。 與此同時，農村地區可能會衰落。 隨著較年輕和較有能力的居民離開，村莊可能會失去工人、顧客，以及未來的社區領袖。 學校可能會關閉，本地商業可能會陷入困境，而年長居民也可能變得越來越孤立。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, people move to cities mainly for better employment prospects and access to services. Nevertheless, this trend can overload urban areas and weaken the social and economic life of the countryside.","chinese":"總結來說，人們搬到城市主要是為了更好的就業前景和獲得服務的機會。 然而，這一趨勢可能會使城市地區負荷過重，並削弱農村的社會和經濟生活。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"rural-to-urban migration","chinese":"由農村遷往城市"},{"english":"become increasingly common","chinese":"變得越來越普遍"},{"english":"this movement","chinese":"這種人口流動"},{"english":"be mainly driven by","chinese":"主要由……推動"},{"english":"life chances","chinese":"人生機會"},{"english":"villages or small towns","chinese":"村落或小城鎮"},{"english":"place serious pressure on","chinese":"對……造成嚴重壓力"},{"english":"urban systems","chinese":"城市系統"},{"english":"rural communities","chinese":"農村社區"},{"english":"increasingly fragile","chinese":"越來越脆弱"},{"english":"one major reason for","chinese":"……的一個主要原因"},{"english":"this trend","chinese":"這個趨勢"},{"english":"economic opportunity","chinese":"經濟機會"},{"english":"closely connected to","chinese":"與……密切相關"},{"english":"farming","chinese":"農耕"},{"english":"local trade","chinese":"本地商貿"},{"english":"small family businesses","chinese":"小型家族生意"},{"english":"unstable income","chinese":"不穩定收入"},{"english":"by contrast","chinese":"相比之下"},{"english":"a wider range of","chinese":"更廣泛的"},{"english":"retail","chinese":"零售業"},{"english":"hospitality","chinese":"酒店及餐飲服務業"},{"english":"entry-level position","chinese":"入門級職位"},{"english":"a path towards","chinese":"通往……的路徑"},{"english":"promotion","chinese":"晉升"},{"english":"higher earnings","chinese":"更高收入"},{"english":"upward mobility","chinese":"向上流動"},{"english":"urban life","chinese":"城市生活"},{"english":"extremely attractive","chinese":"極具吸引力"},{"english":"access to essential services","chinese":"獲得基本服務的機會"},{"english":"tend to have","chinese":"往往有"},{"english":"transport networks","chinese":"交通網絡"},{"english":"digital infrastructure","chinese":"數碼基礎設施"},{"english":"this can be decisive","chinese":"這可以成為決定性因素"},{"english":"not luxuries","chinese":"不是奢侈品"},{"english":"the foundations of","chinese":"……的基礎"},{"english":"long-term security","chinese":"長遠保障"},{"english":"stronger qualifications","chinese":"更有競爭力的學歷"},{"english":"wider social exposure","chinese":"更廣闊的社會接觸"},{"english":"relocation","chinese":"遷居"},{"english":"not only sensible but necessary","chinese":"不但合理，而且必要"},{"english":"cause several problems","chinese":"造成幾個問題"},{"english":"the most immediate one","chinese":"最即時的一個"},{"english":"urban overcrowding","chinese":"城市過度擠迫"},{"english":"population growth","chinese":"人口增長"},{"english":"faster than planning","chinese":"比規劃更快"},{"english":"housing becomes expensive","chinese":"住房變得昂貴"},{"english":"roads become congested","chinese":"道路變得擠塞"},{"english":"public services are stretched thin","chinese":"公共服務不勝負荷"},{"english":"as a result","chinese":"因此"},{"english":"end up living in","chinese":"最終住在"},{"english":"poor-quality accommodation","chinese":"低質素住所"},{"english":"competing for limited jobs","chinese":"競爭有限的工作機會"},{"english":"at the same time","chinese":"與此同時"},{"english":"rural areas may decline","chinese":"農村地區可能衰落"},{"english":"younger and more capable residents","chinese":"較年輕和較有能力的居民"},{"english":"future community leaders","chinese":"未來的社區領袖"},{"english":"local businesses may struggle","chinese":"本地生意可能經營困難"},{"english":"elderly residents","chinese":"年長居民"},{"english":"increasingly isolated","chinese":"越來越孤立"},{"english":"employment prospects","chinese":"就業前景"},{"english":"access to services","chinese":"獲得服務的機會"},{"english":"nevertheless","chinese":"然而"},{"english":"overload urban areas","chinese":"令城市地區不勝負荷"},{"english":"weaken the social and economic life of","chinese":"削弱……的社會和經濟生活"},{"english":"the countryside","chinese":"農村地區"}]},"model-essay-11-ielts-direct-question":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-11-ielts-direct-question","essayKey":"direct-question:11","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-11-ielts-direct-question","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/direct-question/EdmundBd9Dir-Q11","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"In many families, academic achievement is treated not merely as a personal goal for children, but as a measure of future security. This is why some parents place excessive pressure on their children to perform well at school. In my view, parents should be supportive guides in education: they should create discipline and confidence without turning learning into a source of fear.","chinese":"在許多家庭中，學業成就不僅被視為孩子的個人目標，也被看作未來保障的一種衡量標準。這就是為甚麼一些父母會給孩子施加過度壓力，要求他們在學校表現優異。 在我看來，父母在教育中應該成為支持性的引導者：他們應該建立紀律和信心，而不是把學習變成恐懼的來源。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"One reason parents become over-demanding is that they see education as the safest route to social mobility. In competitive societies, a strong academic record is often linked to better universities, higher-status jobs, and a more stable life. As a result, some parents believe that every grade and ranking may affect their child’s future. This fear can easily become pressure, especially when parents compare their children with classmates or relatives. Another reason is that some adults project their own ambitions or regrets onto their children. If they once missed educational opportunities themselves, they may push their sons or daughters too hard, hoping to rewrite their own story through the next generation.","chinese":"父母變得要求過高的一個原因是，他們把教育視為實現社會流動最安全的途徑。 在競爭激烈的社會中，優秀的學業成績往往與更好的大學、更高地位的工作，以及更穩定的生活相連。 因此，一些父母相信，每一個分數和排名都可能影響孩子的未來。 這種恐懼很容易變成壓力，尤其當父母把自己的孩子與同學或親戚作比較時。 另一個原因是，一些成年人會把自己的抱負或遺憾投射到孩子身上。 如果他們自己曾經錯過教育機會，他們可能會過分催迫自己的子女，希望透過下一代改寫自己的人生故事。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"However, the proper role of a parent is not to act as a second examiner at home. Parents should provide a calm structure: regular study habits, a suitable learning environment, and reasonable expectations. They should also notice when a child is genuinely struggling and respond with patience rather than blame. For example, if a child performs poorly in mathematics, a helpful parent would try to understand whether the problem is weak foundations, anxiety, or poor study methods, instead of simply demanding higher marks. Most importantly, parents should protect their child’s long-term attitude towards learning. Encouragement, honest feedback, and emotional security can help children become resilient and self-motivated, whereas constant pressure may make them associate education with shame and exhaustion.","chinese":"然而，父母的恰當角色並不是在家中扮演第二個考官。 父母應該提供一種平穩的結構：規律的學習習慣、合適的學習環境，以及合理的期望。 他們也應該留意孩子真正感到吃力的時候，並以耐心而不是責備作出回應。 例如，如果一個孩子數學表現不佳，一位有幫助的父母會嘗試了解問題是否來自基礎薄弱、焦慮，或學習方法不當，而不是單純要求更高分數。 最重要的是，父母應該保護孩子對學習的長遠態度。 鼓勵、誠實的回饋和情感上的安全感，可以幫助孩子變得有韌性並具備自我動力；相反，持續的壓力可能令他們把教育與羞愧和疲憊聯繫起來。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, excessive parental pressure often comes from fear, competition, and personal ambition. A parent’s true responsibility is to support learning firmly but kindly, so that education becomes a path to growth rather than a burden to survive.","chinese":"總結來說，過度的父母壓力往往來自恐懼、競爭，以及個人抱負。 父母真正的責任，是堅定但溫和地支持學習，使教育成為一條通向成長的道路，而不是一個需要硬撐過去的負擔。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"academic achievement","chinese":"學業成就"},{"english":"be treated not merely as","chinese":"不只是被視為"},{"english":"a personal goal","chinese":"個人目標"},{"english":"a measure of future security","chinese":"未來保障的衡量標準"},{"english":"place excessive pressure on","chinese":"對……施加過大壓力"},{"english":"perform well at school","chinese":"在學校表現良好"},{"english":"supportive guides in education","chinese":"教育上的支持者和引導者"},{"english":"create discipline and confidence","chinese":"培養自律和信心"},{"english":"turn learning into","chinese":"將學習變成……"},{"english":"a source of fear","chinese":"恐懼的來源"},{"english":"become over-demanding","chinese":"變得要求過高"},{"english":"the safest route to","chinese":"通往……最安全的途徑"},{"english":"social mobility","chinese":"社會流動"},{"english":"competitive societies","chinese":"競爭激烈的社會"},{"english":"a strong academic record","chinese":"優秀的學業成績"},{"english":"be linked to","chinese":"與……有關"},{"english":"higher-status jobs","chinese":"社會地位較高的工作"},{"english":"a more stable life","chinese":"更穩定的生活"},{"english":"as a result","chinese":"因此"},{"english":"every grade and ranking","chinese":"每個分數和排名"},{"english":"affect their child's future","chinese":"影響孩子的將來"},{"english":"compare their children with","chinese":"將自己的孩子與……比較"},{"english":"classmates or relatives","chinese":"同學或親戚"},{"english":"project their own ambitions onto","chinese":"將自己的抱負投射到……身上"},{"english":"project their regrets onto","chinese":"將自己的遺憾投射到……身上"},{"english":"missed educational opportunities","chinese":"錯過教育機會"},{"english":"push their children too hard","chinese":"對孩子逼得太緊"},{"english":"rewrite their own story","chinese":"改寫自己的人生故事"},{"english":"the next generation","chinese":"下一代"},{"english":"the proper role of","chinese":"……的恰當角色"},{"english":"act as a second examiner","chinese":"扮演第二個考官"},{"english":"provide a calm structure","chinese":"提供平和而有條理的安排"},{"english":"regular study habits","chinese":"定期學習習慣"},{"english":"a suitable learning environment","chinese":"合適的學習環境"},{"english":"reasonable expectations","chinese":"合理期望"},{"english":"genuinely struggling","chinese":"真的遇到困難"},{"english":"respond with patience rather than blame","chinese":"以耐性而非責備回應"},{"english":"performs poorly in","chinese":"在……表現欠佳"},{"english":"weak foundations","chinese":"基礎薄弱"},{"english":"poor study methods","chinese":"不良學習方法"},{"english":"demanding higher marks","chinese":"要求更高分數"},{"english":"long-term attitude towards learning","chinese":"對學習的長遠態度"},{"english":"honest feedback","chinese":"坦誠回饋"},{"english":"emotional security","chinese":"情感安全感"},{"english":"become resilient and self-motivated","chinese":"變得有抗逆力和自我推動"},{"english":"constant pressure","chinese":"持續不斷的壓力"},{"english":"associate education with","chinese":"將教育與……聯繫起來"},{"english":"shame and exhaustion","chinese":"羞愧和疲憊"},{"english":"excessive parental pressure","chinese":"過度的父母壓力"},{"english":"personal ambition","chinese":"個人抱負"},{"english":"true responsibility","chinese":"真正責任"},{"english":"support learning firmly but kindly","chinese":"堅定而仁慈地支持學習"},{"english":"a path to growth","chinese":"成長之路"},{"english":"a burden to survive","chinese":"必須捱過的負擔"}]},"model-essay-11-ielts-discuss-both-views":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-11-ielts-discuss-both-views","essayKey":"discuss-both-views:11","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-11-ielts-discuss-both-views","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/discuss-both-views-your-opinion/EdmundBd9ExpBth-Q11","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"Crime prevention is a central part of any safe and civilised society. While some people argue that individuals should take responsibility for their own safety, others believe that preventing crime is mainly the duty of the state. In my opinion, although citizens should act sensibly, the government must carry the primary responsibility because only it has the authority and resources to reduce crime on a large scale.","chinese":"預防犯罪是任何安全而文明的社會中的核心部分。 雖然有人認為個人應該為自身安全負責，但另一些人則相信預防犯罪主要是國家的責任 我認為，儘管市民應該理智地行事，但政府必須承擔主要責任，因為只有政府才擁有大規模減少犯罪所需的權力和資源。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"Those who support individual responsibility argue that people can lower their own risk by making careful choices. For example, homeowners can install security cameras, avoid leaving valuables in visible places, and be cautious when sharing personal information online. These habits are useful because many crimes are opportunistic; if a person makes themselves an easy target, criminals may be more likely to take advantage of them. From this perspective, personal awareness acts as the first line of defence, especially in daily situations where the police cannot be physically present.","chinese":"支持個人責任的人認為，人們可以透過作出謹慎的選擇來降低自身風險。 例如，屋主可以安裝保安攝像頭，避免把貴重物品放在顯眼的位置，並在網上分享個人資料時保持謹慎。 這些習慣是有用的，因為許多犯罪都是機會主義式的；如果一個人使自己成為容易下手的目標，罪犯便可能更容易利用他們。 從這個角度來看，個人警覺性就是第一道防線，尤其是警察無法親身在場的日常情況中"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"However, I believe that crime prevention cannot depend mainly on individuals. The government is responsible for creating and maintaining the systems that make society safe, such as effective policing, fair laws, street lighting, public education, and social support. If a neighbourhood has poor law enforcement, weak surveillance, and few opportunities for young people, individuals can only protect themselves to a limited extent. A family may lock its doors every night, but it cannot control organised crime, unsafe public spaces, or wider social problems that push people towards illegal behaviour. These issues require coordinated public action, not just private caution.","chinese":"然而，我認為預防犯罪不能主要依賴個人。 政府有責任建立並維持使社會安全的系統，例如有效的警務、公平的法律、街道照明、公共教育和社會支援。 如果一個社區執法不足、監察薄弱，而且年輕人的機會很少，個人就只能在有限程度上保護自己。 一個家庭或許可以每晚鎖好門，但它無法控制有組織犯罪、不安全的公共空間，或那些把人推向違法行為的更廣泛社會問題。 這些問題需要有組織的公共行動，而不只是個人的小心謹慎。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, individuals should certainly take reasonable steps to protect themselves, but this cannot replace the role of government. Since crime is a social problem rather than merely a personal inconvenience, the state should be chiefly responsible for preventing it.","chinese":"總結來說，個人當然應該採取合理措施保護自己，但這不能取代政府的角色。 由於犯罪是一個社會問題，而不僅僅是個人的不便，因此國家應該主要負責預防犯罪。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"crime prevention","chinese":"預防罪案"},{"english":"a central part of","chinese":"……的核心部分"},{"english":"safe and civilised society","chinese":"安全而文明的社會"},{"english":"take responsibility for","chinese":"為……承擔責任"},{"english":"their own safety","chinese":"自身安全"},{"english":"preventing crime","chinese":"預防犯罪"},{"english":"the duty of the state","chinese":"國家的責任"},{"english":"in my opinion","chinese":"在我看來"},{"english":"act sensibly","chinese":"行事謹慎；明智行事"},{"english":"carry the primary responsibility","chinese":"承擔首要責任"},{"english":"authority and resources","chinese":"權力和資源"},{"english":"reduce crime on a large scale","chinese":"大規模減少罪案"},{"english":"individual responsibility","chinese":"個人責任"},{"english":"lower their own risk","chinese":"降低自身風險"},{"english":"making careful choices","chinese":"作出謹慎選擇"},{"english":"install security cameras","chinese":"安裝保安攝錄機"},{"english":"avoid leaving valuables in visible places","chinese":"避免將貴重物品放在顯眼地方"},{"english":"valuables","chinese":"貴重物品"},{"english":"be cautious when","chinese":"在……時保持謹慎"},{"english":"sharing personal information online","chinese":"在網上分享個人資料"},{"english":"many crimes are opportunistic","chinese":"很多罪案是伺機而作的"},{"english":"make themselves an easy target","chinese":"令自己成為容易下手的目標"},{"english":"be more likely to","chinese":"更有可能"},{"english":"take advantage of","chinese":"利用；乘機傷害"},{"english":"from this perspective","chinese":"從這個角度來看"},{"english":"personal awareness","chinese":"個人警覺性"},{"english":"act as the first line of defence","chinese":"作為第一道防線"},{"english":"daily situations","chinese":"日常情況"},{"english":"physically present","chinese":"親身在場"},{"english":"cannot depend mainly on","chinese":"不能主要依賴"},{"english":"be responsible for creating and maintaining","chinese":"負責建立和維持"},{"english":"make society safe","chinese":"令社會安全"},{"english":"effective policing","chinese":"有效警務"},{"english":"fair laws","chinese":"公平法律"},{"english":"street lighting","chinese":"街燈照明"},{"english":"public education","chinese":"公眾教育"},{"english":"social support","chinese":"社會支援"},{"english":"a neighbourhood","chinese":"社區；街區"},{"english":"poor law enforcement","chinese":"執法不力"},{"english":"weak surveillance","chinese":"監察薄弱"},{"english":"few opportunities for young people","chinese":"年輕人機會不足"},{"english":"to a limited extent","chinese":"在有限程度上"},{"english":"lock its doors","chinese":"鎖門"},{"english":"organised crime","chinese":"有組織犯罪"},{"english":"unsafe public spaces","chinese":"不安全的公共空間"},{"english":"wider social problems","chinese":"更廣泛的社會問題"},{"english":"push people towards illegal behaviour","chinese":"推使人走向非法行為"},{"english":"illegal behaviour","chinese":"非法行為"},{"english":"coordinated public action","chinese":"協調一致的公共行動"},{"english":"private caution","chinese":"個人謹慎"},{"english":"take reasonable steps to","chinese":"採取合理措施去"},{"english":"protect themselves","chinese":"保護自己"},{"english":"replace the role of government","chinese":"取代政府的角色"},{"english":"a social problem rather than","chinese":"是社會問題，而不是"},{"english":"merely a personal inconvenience","chinese":"只屬個人不便"},{"english":"the state","chinese":"國家；政府"},{"english":"chiefly responsible for","chinese":"對……負主要責任"}]},"model-essay-11-ielts-opinion":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-11-ielts-opinion","essayKey":"opinion:11","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-11-ielts-opinion","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/opinions/EdmundBd9OP-Q11","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"Employment decisions should be based on competence and business need rather than assumptions about an applicant’s private life. Some people nevertheless argue that small businesses should avoid hiring young women who have not yet started families so that maternity leave will not become a future expense. This essay will argue that this view is entirely wrong because it replaces merit with discrimination and because it is financially short-sighted.","chinese":"聘用決策應該根據能力與業務需要，而不是建立在對求職者私人生活的假設之上。 然而，有些人仍然主張，小企業應避免聘用尚未開始組織家庭的年輕女性，以免未來需要承擔產假的成本。 本文將論證，這種看法完全錯誤，因為它以歧視取代了能力與才幹的評估，而且在財務上也十分目光短淺。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"The first reason I completely disagree is that recruitment based on possible motherhood is unfair and prevents businesses from selecting the strongest candidates. Once an employer excludes qualified women for a factor unrelated to job performance, the talent pool immediately becomes smaller, which makes poor hiring decisions more likely. A small design firm, for example, might reject an excellent applicant and appoint a less capable worker instead, leading to weaker ideas, lower client satisfaction and reduced revenue. This policy can also damage the workplace more broadly. When employees realise that hiring is shaped by prejudice rather than ability, confidence in management declines and morale suffers. In a small business, where every member of staff has a visible impact, this loss of trust can quickly undermine teamwork and productivity.","chinese":"我第一個完全不同意的理由是：根據女性未來可能成為母親來作招聘判斷，不但不公平，也會妨礙企業選出最優秀的人才。 一旦僱主因為與工作表現無關的因素而排除合資格女性，可供挑選的人才庫便會立刻縮小，也使錯誤的聘用決定更容易出現。 例如，一家小型設計公司可能拒絕一位非常優秀的申請者，反而聘用能力較弱的人，結果導致創意較差、客戶滿意度下降，以及收入減少。 這種政策也會對整體工作環境造成更廣泛的損害。 當員工意識到聘用決定是由偏見而不是能力所主導時，他們對管理層的信心便會下降，士氣也會受到打擊。 在小型企業裡，每一位員工的影響都清晰可見，因此這種信任的流失很快便會削弱團隊合作與工作效率。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"The second reason is that the financial logic behind this argument is deeply flawed. Maternity leave is a temporary and predictable cost, whereas bad recruitment and repeated staff turnover create much more serious long-term expense. If a company hires from a restricted group, it is more likely to spend money retraining unsuitable employees, correcting mistakes and replacing people who do not perform well. By contrast, fair and supportive employment practices often improve retention. Workers who feel respected are more likely to remain with the company and repay that support with loyalty and conscientious work. For instance, a small retailer that arranges temporary cover during parental leave may face a short-term cost, but it is far more likely to keep an experienced employee for years.","chinese":"第二個理由是，這種主張背後的財務邏輯本身就有很大的缺陷。 產假是一種暫時而且可預見的成本；相反地，錯誤的招聘以及反覆的人員流動，卻會造成更嚴重的長期開支。 如果公司只從受限制的群體中招聘，就更有可能把金錢花在重新培訓不合適的員工、修正錯誤，以及替換表現不佳的人身上。 相比之下，公平而具支持性的聘用做法往往能提高員工留任率。 感到被尊重的員工更有可能留在公司，並以忠誠和盡責的工作回報這份支持。 例如，一家在育兒假期間安排臨時替補的小型零售商，也許要承擔短期成本，但卻更有可能把一名經驗豐富的員工留住多年。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, I completely disagree that small businesses should avoid hiring young women in order to avoid maternity leave. This approach is unjust, wastes talent and rests on a false understanding of cost, so recruitment should always be based on merit rather than anticipated family choices.","chinese":"總而言之，我完全不同意小企業為了避免產假成本而不聘用年輕女性。 這種做法既不公正，也浪費人才，並且建立在對成本的錯誤理解之上，因此招聘應永遠以能力為依據，而不是以對未來家庭選擇的預測作判斷。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"employment decisions","chinese":"招聘決定；僱傭決定"},{"english":"be based on","chinese":"建基於"},{"english":"competence and business need","chinese":"能力和業務需要"},{"english":"rather than assumptions about","chinese":"而不是基於對……的假設"},{"english":"an applicant's private life","chinese":"申請人的私人生活"},{"english":"nevertheless argue that","chinese":"然而仍然認為"},{"english":"small businesses","chinese":"小型企業"},{"english":"avoid hiring","chinese":"避免聘請"},{"english":"have not yet started families","chinese":"尚未成家的"},{"english":"maternity leave","chinese":"產假"},{"english":"become a future expense","chinese":"成為日後開支"},{"english":"this view is entirely wrong","chinese":"這個觀點完全錯誤"},{"english":"replace merit with discrimination","chinese":"以歧視取代才幹"},{"english":"financially short-sighted","chinese":"財政上短視"},{"english":"recruitment based on","chinese":"基於……的招聘"},{"english":"possible motherhood","chinese":"可能成為母親"},{"english":"prevent businesses from","chinese":"阻止企業去"},{"english":"selecting the strongest candidates","chinese":"選出最強的候選人"},{"english":"once an employer excludes","chinese":"一旦僱主排除"},{"english":"qualified women","chinese":"合資格女性"},{"english":"a factor unrelated to","chinese":"與……無關的因素"},{"english":"job performance","chinese":"工作表現"},{"english":"the talent pool","chinese":"人才庫"},{"english":"become smaller","chinese":"變得更小"},{"english":"poor hiring decisions","chinese":"差劣的招聘決定"},{"english":"be more likely","chinese":"更有可能"},{"english":"a small design firm","chinese":"小型設計公司"},{"english":"reject an excellent applicant","chinese":"拒絕一位出色的申請人"},{"english":"appoint a less capable worker instead","chinese":"轉而任命能力較低的員工"},{"english":"leading to","chinese":"導致"},{"english":"weaker ideas","chinese":"較弱的想法；較差的創意"},{"english":"lower client satisfaction","chinese":"較低的客戶滿意度"},{"english":"reduced revenue","chinese":"收入減少"},{"english":"damage the workplace more broadly","chinese":"更廣泛地損害工作環境"},{"english":"realise that","chinese":"意識到"},{"english":"be shaped by prejudice","chinese":"受偏見影響"},{"english":"rather than ability","chinese":"而不是能力"},{"english":"confidence in management declines","chinese":"對管理層的信心下降"},{"english":"morale suffers","chinese":"士氣受損"},{"english":"every member of staff","chinese":"每位員工"},{"english":"have a visible impact","chinese":"有明顯影響"},{"english":"loss of trust","chinese":"信任流失"},{"english":"quickly undermine","chinese":"迅速削弱"},{"english":"teamwork and productivity","chinese":"團隊合作和生產力"},{"english":"the financial logic behind","chinese":"……背後的財務邏輯"},{"english":"deeply flawed","chinese":"有嚴重缺陷"},{"english":"a temporary and predictable cost","chinese":"暫時而可預計的成本"},{"english":"whereas","chinese":"然而"},{"english":"bad recruitment","chinese":"差劣招聘"},{"english":"repeated staff turnover","chinese":"反覆的員工流失"},{"english":"create much more serious long-term expense","chinese":"造成嚴重得多的長期開支"},{"english":"hire from a restricted group","chinese":"從受限制的群體中招聘"},{"english":"retraining unsuitable employees","chinese":"重新培訓不合適員工"},{"english":"correcting mistakes","chinese":"糾正錯誤"},{"english":"replacing people who do not perform well","chinese":"替換表現不佳的人"},{"english":"by contrast","chinese":"相反"},{"english":"fair and supportive employment practices","chinese":"公平而有支援的僱傭做法"},{"english":"improve retention","chinese":"提高留任率"},{"english":"feel respected","chinese":"感到受尊重"},{"english":"remain with the company","chinese":"留在公司"},{"english":"repay that support with","chinese":"以……回報那份支持"},{"english":"loyalty and conscientious work","chinese":"忠誠和盡責工作"},{"english":"arrange temporary cover","chinese":"安排臨時人手"},{"english":"parental leave","chinese":"育兒假"},{"english":"face a short-term cost","chinese":"面對短期成本"},{"english":"keep an experienced employee","chinese":"留住有經驗員工"},{"english":"in order to avoid","chinese":"為了避免"},{"english":"this approach is unjust","chinese":"這種做法不公義"},{"english":"waste talent","chinese":"浪費人才"},{"english":"rest on","chinese":"建基於"},{"english":"a false understanding of cost","chinese":"對成本的錯誤理解"},{"english":"based on merit","chinese":"基於才幹"},{"english":"anticipated family choices","chinese":"預期的家庭選擇"}]},"model-essay-11-ielts-task1-tables":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-11-ielts-task1-tables","essayKey":"tables:11","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-11-ielts-task1-tables","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-1/tables/table-11","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"The table compares the cost of meeting the minimum daily water requirement per person in five countries, expressed both in US cents and as a share of the average daily wage.","chinese":"該表比較了五個國家中，每人每日達到最低用水需求所需的成本，並同時以美仙及平均日薪比例呈現。"},{"label":"Overview","english":"Overall, Tanzania records the highest cost and the greatest wage burden, while the US has the lowest figures on both measures. More broadly, Tanzania, Uganda and Pakistan spend far larger proportions of daily earnings on this basic requirement than the UK and the US, even though the cash differences are only a few cents.","chinese":"整體而言，坦桑尼亞的用水成本最高，對工資造成的負擔也最大；而美國在兩項指標上都是最低。 更廣泛而言，坦桑尼亞、烏干達和巴基斯坦在這項基本需求上所花費的日薪比例，遠高於英國和美國，即使它們在實際金額上的差距只有數美仙。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"In monetary terms, Tanzania leads the table, at 6.4 cents per person per day. Uganda is next, at 4.1 cents, while Pakistan’s figure is considerably lower, at 1.76 cents. The two remaining countries are cheaper still: the UK stands at 1.3 cents, and the US records the lowest daily cost, at 0.85 cents.","chinese":"以金額來看，坦桑尼亞位居首位，每人每日成本為 6.4 美仙。 烏干達緊隨其後，為 4.1 美仙；而巴基斯坦的數字則低得多，為 1.76 美仙。 其餘兩個國家的成本更低：英國為 1.3 美仙，而美國錄得最低的每日成本，只有 0.85 美仙。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"The percentage figures show a much sharper contrast. In Tanzania, the minimum requirement takes up 5.7% of the average daily wage, compared with 3.2% in Uganda and 1.1% in Pakistan. By contrast, the equivalent shares in the UK and the US are tiny, at only 0.013% and 0.006% respectively; indeed, Tanzania’s percentage is almost 1,000 times the US figure.","chinese":"百分比數據呈現出更鮮明的對比。 在坦桑尼亞，最低用水需求佔平均日薪的 5.7% ；相比之下，烏干達為 3.2% ，巴基斯坦則為 1.1% 。 相比之下，英國和美國的相應比例極小，分別只有 0.013% 和 0.006% ；事實上，坦桑尼亞的比例幾乎是美國的 1,000 倍。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"the table below","chinese":"以下表格"},{"english":"gives information about","chinese":"提供關於……的資料"},{"english":"the daily cost of water","chinese":"每日用水成本"},{"english":"per person","chinese":"每人"},{"english":"five different countries","chinese":"五個不同國家"},{"english":"summarise the information","chinese":"概述資料"},{"english":"by selecting and reporting","chinese":"透過選取並報告……"},{"english":"the main features","chinese":"主要特徵"},{"english":"make comparisons where relevant","chinese":"在相關之處作出比較"},{"english":"the table compares","chinese":"表格比較"},{"english":"the cost of meeting","chinese":"滿足……所需的成本"},{"english":"minimum daily water requirement","chinese":"每日最低用水需求"},{"english":"expressed both in","chinese":"同時以……表示"},{"english":"US cents","chinese":"美仙"},{"english":"as a share of","chinese":"佔……的比例"},{"english":"average daily wage","chinese":"平均每日工資"},{"english":"records the highest cost","chinese":"錄得最高成本"},{"english":"the greatest wage burden","chinese":"最大工資負擔"},{"english":"the lowest figures","chinese":"最低數字"},{"english":"on both measures","chinese":"在兩項指標上"},{"english":"more broadly","chinese":"更廣泛而言"},{"english":"spend far larger proportions of","chinese":"花費大得多的比例於……"},{"english":"daily earnings","chinese":"每日收入"},{"english":"this basic requirement","chinese":"這項基本需求"},{"english":"even though","chinese":"即使"},{"english":"cash differences","chinese":"現金差距"},{"english":"only a few cents","chinese":"只有幾美仙"},{"english":"in monetary terms","chinese":"以金額計"},{"english":"leads the table","chinese":"在表格中居首"},{"english":"at 6.4 cents","chinese":"為6.4美仙"},{"english":"cents per person per day","chinese":"每人每日美仙"},{"english":"is next","chinese":"其次是"},{"english":"considerably lower","chinese":"低得多"},{"english":"the two remaining countries","chinese":"其餘兩個國家"},{"english":"cheaper still","chinese":"更便宜"},{"english":"stands at","chinese":"為；達到"},{"english":"records the lowest daily cost","chinese":"錄得最低每日成本"},{"english":"daily cost","chinese":"每日成本"},{"english":"percentage figures","chinese":"百分比數字"},{"english":"a much sharper contrast","chinese":"更鮮明的對比"},{"english":"takes up","chinese":"佔用；佔去"},{"english":"compared with","chinese":"與……相比"},{"english":"by contrast","chinese":"相比之下"},{"english":"equivalent shares","chinese":"相應比例"},{"english":"are tiny","chinese":"非常小"},{"english":"at only","chinese":"只有"},{"english":"respectively","chinese":"分別"},{"english":"indeed","chinese":"事實上"},{"english":"almost 1,000 times","chinese":"接近1,000倍"},{"english":"the US figure","chinese":"美國的數字"},{"english":"wage burden","chinese":"工資負擔"},{"english":"water requirement","chinese":"用水需求"},{"english":"basic water needs","chinese":"基本用水需要"},{"english":"affordability of water","chinese":"用水負擔能力"},{"english":"water affordability","chinese":"用水負擔能力"},{"english":"varies greatly","chinese":"差異很大"},{"english":"from country to country","chinese":"因國家而異"},{"english":"in absolute terms","chinese":"以實際金額計"},{"english":"in percentage terms","chinese":"以百分比計"},{"english":"a share of income","chinese":"收入比例"},{"english":"relative to wages","chinese":"相對於工資"},{"english":"the highest cash cost","chinese":"最高現金成本"},{"english":"the lowest cash cost","chinese":"最低現金成本"},{"english":"a small cash gap","chinese":"小額現金差距"},{"english":"a large percentage gap","chinese":"大幅百分比差距"},{"english":"the largest gap","chinese":"最大差距"},{"english":"a striking difference","chinese":"顯著差異"},{"english":"a clear divide","chinese":"明顯分野"},{"english":"the richer countries","chinese":"較富裕國家"},{"english":"the poorer countries","chinese":"較貧窮國家"},{"english":"far larger than","chinese":"遠大於"},{"english":"much smaller than","chinese":"遠小於"},{"english":"only slightly higher than","chinese":"只略高於"},{"english":"considerably higher than","chinese":"明顯高於"},{"english":"rank first","chinese":"排名第一"},{"english":"rank last","chinese":"排名最後"},{"english":"the overall pattern","chinese":"整體模式"},{"english":"the main contrast","chinese":"主要對比"},{"english":"the most expensive country","chinese":"成本最高的國家"},{"english":"the least expensive country","chinese":"成本最低的國家"},{"english":"a heavier burden","chinese":"較沉重負擔"},{"english":"a negligible burden","chinese":"微不足道的負擔"},{"english":"account for a small share","chinese":"佔小比例"},{"english":"account for a large share","chinese":"佔大比例"},{"english":"the minimum requirement","chinese":"最低需求"},{"english":"meeting basic needs","chinese":"滿足基本需要"},{"english":"expressed as a percentage","chinese":"以百分比表示"},{"english":"monetary cost","chinese":"金錢成本"},{"english":"relative cost","chinese":"相對成本"},{"english":"purchasing power","chinese":"購買力"},{"english":"financial burden","chinese":"財政負擔"},{"english":"the burden is minimal","chinese":"負擔極低"},{"english":"despite small cash differences","chinese":"儘管現金差距很小"},{"english":"widen dramatically","chinese":"大幅擴大"},{"english":"when expressed as","chinese":"當以……表示時"}]},"model-essay-12-ielts-advantage-disadvantage":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-12-ielts-advantage-disadvantage","essayKey":"advantage-disadvantage:12","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-12-ielts-advantage-disadvantage","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/advantage-and-disadvantage/EdmundBd9AdDisAd-Q12","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"It is often argued that the place where a child grows up can shape nearly every aspect of his or her development. While cities are widely associated with opportunity and convenience, the countryside is often regarded as a healthier and more peaceful environment. This essay will examine the advantages and disadvantages of both settings.","chinese":"[無論在職場還是私人生活中，越來越多的溝通如今都是透過數位科技進行，而不是以面對面互動的方式完成。] [儘管這種發展可能削弱人際關係的質素，並增加誤解的風險，] [我認為整體而言，它的優點更大，因為它使溝通變得高效得多，並讓人們即使相隔遙遠也能保持聯繫。]"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"Growing up in a city offers several important benefits. To begin with, urban areas usually provide better access to high-quality schools, specialised healthcare and a wide range of extracurricular activities. This means that children are more likely to receive strong academic support and to discover talents in fields such as music, sport or technology. In addition, city life exposes them to cultural diversity, which can broaden their horizons and help them become more adaptable. However, these advantages often come with serious drawbacks. Cities are frequently crowded, noisy and polluted, and many children have limited access to safe outdoor space. Moreover, heavy traffic, higher crime rates and the fast pace of urban life can create stress for both children and their parents.","chinese":"[科技化溝通最主要的優點在於速度與便利。] [在專業環境中，電子郵件、即時通訊平台以及視像會議免除了人們出行的需要，並使決策幾乎能夠即時作出。] [這不但縮短了回應時間、降低了營運成本，還使公司能夠極為輕鬆地協調分布於不同城市甚至不同大洲的團隊。] [例如，一位經理可以透過一次線上會議便與海外同事解決生產問題，而不必等待數天後才進行一次面對面的討論。] [同樣的道理也適用於社交層面：住得很遠的父母、子女和朋友，仍然可以透過通話和訊息每天聯絡。] [結果是，人際關係更容易維持，也較不容易隨時間流逝而逐漸淡化。] [例如，一個家庭即使成員分散於不同國家，仍然可以透過視像通話分享日常近況，並彼此提供情感支持。] [因此，數位溝通大大提升了工作與個人生活中的效率與可及性。]"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"By contrast, the countryside can provide a calmer and more grounded childhood. Cleaner air, open spaces and closer contact with nature are all conducive to physical health and emotional well-being. Rural communities are also often more close-knit, so children may grow up with a stronger sense of belonging and security. Nevertheless, life in the countryside is not without disadvantages. Educational and medical facilities may be fewer in number and less advanced, which can restrict children’s development in the long run. Furthermore, rural areas may offer fewer social, cultural and recreational opportunities, and this relative isolation can sometimes limit a child’s exposure to different people and ideas.","chinese":"[然而，數位溝通也有重要的缺點，其中最嚴重的一點在於它缺乏情感上的豐富性。] [面對面的交談能傳達語氣、面部表情和肢體語言，而這些都有助於人們更準確地理解意思、表達同理心，並建立信任。] [當這些線索消失時，訊息便更容易被誤讀，從而導致困惑，甚至引發衝突。] [例如，一封簡短的電郵或文字訊息，即使本來並無冒犯之意，也可能顯得冷淡，甚至帶有敵意。] [這在職場中尤其成問題，因為信任與細膩的理解對領導、協商及團隊合作都至關重要。] [長遠而言，過度依賴螢幕也可能助長膚淺的社交習慣，因此人們即使在線上一直保持聯絡，仍然可能感到孤立。] [例如，一個人即使經常透過社交媒體聊天，仍可能感到孤單，因為數位接觸始終無法完全取代真正的關注與人的陪伴。] [因此，儘管科技使溝通成為可能，它同時也可能削弱清晰度、信任感與情感深度。]"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, both the city and the countryside offer distinct advantages and disadvantages for children. Urban life provides opportunity and variety, whereas rural life offers space, tranquillity and a stronger connection to nature.","chinese":"[總結來說，透過科技進行溝通在效率與可及性方面具有明顯優勢，儘管它可能削弱人際互動的深度與清晰度。] [整體而言，我認為其優點大於缺點，因為數位工具使工作與個人生活中的溝通都能跨越時間與距離而有效運作。]"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"the place where a child grows up","chinese":"孩子成長的地方"},{"english":"shape nearly every aspect of","chinese":"塑造……幾乎每一方面"},{"english":"development","chinese":"發展"},{"english":"be widely associated with","chinese":"被廣泛聯想到"},{"english":"opportunity and convenience","chinese":"機會和便利"},{"english":"be regarded as","chinese":"被視為"},{"english":"a healthier and more peaceful environment","chinese":"更健康、更平靜的環境"},{"english":"examine the advantages and disadvantages of","chinese":"探討……的優點和缺點"},{"english":"both settings","chinese":"兩種環境"},{"english":"growing up in","chinese":"在……成長"},{"english":"urban areas","chinese":"城市地區"},{"english":"provide better access to","chinese":"提供更好的……機會"},{"english":"high-quality schools","chinese":"優質學校"},{"english":"specialised healthcare","chinese":"專門醫療服務"},{"english":"a wide range of","chinese":"廣泛的"},{"english":"extracurricular activities","chinese":"課外活動"},{"english":"be more likely to","chinese":"更有可能"},{"english":"receive strong academic support","chinese":"獲得強大的學業支援"},{"english":"discover talents in","chinese":"發掘在……方面的才能"},{"english":"fields such as","chinese":"例如……的領域"},{"english":"exposes them to","chinese":"讓他們接觸到"},{"english":"cultural diversity","chinese":"文化多樣性"},{"english":"broaden their horizons","chinese":"擴闊他們的眼界"},{"english":"become more adaptable","chinese":"變得更有適應力"},{"english":"come with serious drawbacks","chinese":"伴隨嚴重缺點"},{"english":"crowded, noisy and polluted","chinese":"擠迫、嘈吵和受污染"},{"english":"limited access to","chinese":"有限地接觸；缺乏……機會"},{"english":"safe outdoor space","chinese":"安全的戶外空間"},{"english":"moreover","chinese":"此外"},{"english":"heavy traffic","chinese":"繁忙交通"},{"english":"higher crime rates","chinese":"較高罪案率"},{"english":"the fast pace of urban life","chinese":"城市生活的急速節奏"},{"english":"create stress for","chinese":"為……造成壓力"},{"english":"by contrast","chinese":"相比之下"},{"english":"a calmer and more grounded childhood","chinese":"更平靜、更踏實的童年"},{"english":"cleaner air","chinese":"更清新的空氣"},{"english":"open spaces","chinese":"開闊空間"},{"english":"closer contact with nature","chinese":"與大自然更親近"},{"english":"be conducive to","chinese":"有助於"},{"english":"physical health","chinese":"身體健康"},{"english":"emotional well-being","chinese":"情緒健康"},{"english":"rural communities","chinese":"鄉郊社區"},{"english":"close-knit","chinese":"關係緊密的"},{"english":"grow up with","chinese":"帶着……成長"},{"english":"a stronger sense of belonging and security","chinese":"更強的歸屬感和安全感"},{"english":"nevertheless","chinese":"然而"},{"english":"not without disadvantages","chinese":"並非沒有缺點"},{"english":"educational and medical facilities","chinese":"教育和醫療設施"},{"english":"fewer in number","chinese":"數量較少"},{"english":"less advanced","chinese":"較不先進"},{"english":"restrict children's development","chinese":"限制兒童發展"},{"english":"in the long run","chinese":"長遠而言"},{"english":"furthermore","chinese":"此外"},{"english":"recreational opportunities","chinese":"康樂機會"},{"english":"relative isolation","chinese":"相對孤立"},{"english":"limit a child's exposure to","chinese":"限制孩子接觸……"},{"english":"different people and ideas","chinese":"不同的人和想法"},{"english":"distinct advantages and disadvantages","chinese":"明顯不同的優點和缺點"},{"english":"provides opportunity and variety","chinese":"提供機會和多樣性"},{"english":"whereas","chinese":"而；相比之下"},{"english":"tranquillity","chinese":"寧靜"},{"english":"a stronger connection to nature","chinese":"與大自然更強的聯繫"}]},"model-essay-12-ielts-cause-solution":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-12-ielts-cause-solution","essayKey":"cause-solution:12","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-12-ielts-cause-solution","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/problem-and-cause/EdmundBd9CnS-Q12","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"As cities attract more people in search of employment and better prospects, urban overpopulation has become a serious challenge. This essay will discuss two major problems caused by this trend, namely pressure on housing and public services, and the decline of everyday living conditions, before suggesting practical ways to address them.","chinese":"隨著城市吸引越來越多人前來尋找工作和更好的發展前景，城市人口過多已成為一個嚴重的挑戰。 本文將討論這一趨勢所造成的兩個主要問題，即住房和公共服務所承受的壓力，以及日常生活條件的下降，然後提出實際的方法來解決這些問題。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"The first problem is that housing becomes increasingly unaffordable and inadequate. When too many people compete for a limited number of homes, rents rise sharply, and poorer residents may be forced into cramped apartments or informal settlements. This also places heavy pressure on schools, hospitals and sanitation systems, because public services have to serve more people than they were designed for. As a result, city life may promise opportunity, but for many residents it becomes expensive, stressful and unhealthy.","chinese":"第一個問題是，住房變得越來越負擔不起，而且越來越不足。 當太多人爭奪數量有限的住房時，租金會急劇上升，而較貧困的居民可能被迫住進狹小的公寓或非正式聚居區。 這也會對學校、醫院和衛生系統造成沉重壓力，因為公共服務需要服務的人數超出了原本設計時所能承受的範圍。 結果是，城市生活也許象徵著機會，但對許多居民而言，它卻變得昂貴、充滿壓力，而且不健康。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"Another serious problem is the deterioration of daily life in crowded urban areas. Large populations usually lead to traffic congestion, longer commuting times and higher levels of air pollution. For example, if thousands of workers travel into the same business districts every morning, roads and public transport systems quickly become overloaded. This wastes time, reduces productivity and gradually turns the city into a place where people spend more time surviving the routine than enjoying its opportunities.","chinese":"另一個嚴重問題是，擁擠城市地區的日常生活質素下降。 龐大的人口通常會導致交通擠塞、通勤時間延長，以及空氣污染水平上升。 例如，如果每天早上有數以千計的上班族前往相同的商業區，道路和公共交通系統很快便會不勝負荷。 這會浪費時間、降低生產力，並逐漸把城市變成一個讓人花更多時間應付日常壓力，而不是享受城市機會的地方。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 3","english":"These problems can be solved through a combination of regional development and better urban planning. Governments should create jobs, universities and reliable public services in smaller towns so that moving to a major city is not the only path to a better life. At the same time, cities need more affordable housing, stronger public transport networks and stricter planning rules to prevent overcrowded neighbourhoods from expanding without proper infrastructure.","chinese":"這些問題可以透過區域發展和更好的城市規劃相結合來解決。 政府應該在較小的城鎮創造就業機會、建立大學，並提供可靠的公共服務，使搬到大城市不再是通往更好生活的唯一途徑。 與此同時，城市需要更多可負擔的住房、更完善的公共交通網絡，以及更嚴格的規劃規則，以防止過度擁擠的社區在缺乏適當基礎設施的情況下繼續擴張。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, overpopulation in cities can cause housing shortages, pressure on public services, congestion and pollution. However, these problems can be reduced if governments make smaller regions more attractive and manage urban growth more carefully.","chinese":"總結來說，城市人口過多可能會造成住房短缺、公共服務壓力、交通擠塞和污染。 然而，如果政府能使較小地區更具吸引力，並更謹慎地管理城市增長，這些問題便可以得到減輕。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"attract more people","chinese":"吸引更多人"},{"english":"in search of employment","chinese":"為了尋找工作"},{"english":"better prospects","chinese":"更好的前景"},{"english":"urban overpopulation","chinese":"城市人口過多"},{"english":"a serious challenge","chinese":"嚴重挑戰"},{"english":"two major problems caused by this trend","chinese":"由這個趨勢造成的兩個主要問題"},{"english":"pressure on housing and public services","chinese":"對房屋及公共服務的壓力"},{"english":"the decline of everyday living conditions","chinese":"日常生活條件下降"},{"english":"practical ways to address them","chinese":"處理這些問題的實際方法"},{"english":"increasingly unaffordable and inadequate","chinese":"越來越負擔不起及不足"},{"english":"compete for a limited number of homes","chinese":"爭奪數量有限的住所"},{"english":"a limited number of homes","chinese":"數量有限的住所"},{"english":"rents rise sharply","chinese":"租金急升"},{"english":"poorer residents","chinese":"較貧困的居民"},{"english":"be forced into","chinese":"被迫進入；被迫入住"},{"english":"cramped apartments","chinese":"狹窄的單位"},{"english":"informal settlements","chinese":"非正式聚居區；臨時聚居區"},{"english":"place heavy pressure on","chinese":"對……造成沉重壓力"},{"english":"sanitation systems","chinese":"衛生系統；環境衞生設施"},{"english":"serve more people than they were designed for","chinese":"服務超出原本設計承載的人數"},{"english":"city life may promise opportunity","chinese":"城市生活可能承諾機會"},{"english":"expensive, stressful and unhealthy","chinese":"昂貴、壓力大及不健康"},{"english":"the deterioration of daily life","chinese":"日常生活質素惡化"},{"english":"crowded urban areas","chinese":"擠迫的市區"},{"english":"lead to traffic congestion","chinese":"導致交通擠塞"},{"english":"longer commuting times","chinese":"更長的通勤時間"},{"english":"higher levels of air pollution","chinese":"更高程度的空氣污染"},{"english":"travel into the same business districts","chinese":"前往同一批商業區"},{"english":"business districts","chinese":"商業區"},{"english":"quickly become overloaded","chinese":"很快變得超出負荷"},{"english":"public transport systems","chinese":"公共交通系統"},{"english":"wastes time","chinese":"浪費時間"},{"english":"reduces productivity","chinese":"降低生產力"},{"english":"gradually turns the city into","chinese":"逐漸把城市變成"},{"english":"surviving the routine","chinese":"勉強應付日常生活"},{"english":"enjoying its opportunities","chinese":"享受其機會"},{"english":"through a combination of","chinese":"透過結合……"},{"english":"regional development","chinese":"區域發展"},{"english":"better urban planning","chinese":"更好的城市規劃"},{"english":"reliable public services","chinese":"可靠的公共服務"},{"english":"smaller towns","chinese":"較小的城鎮"},{"english":"the only path to a better life","chinese":"通往更好生活的唯一途徑"},{"english":"at the same time","chinese":"同時"},{"english":"affordable housing","chinese":"可負擔房屋"},{"english":"stronger public transport networks","chinese":"更完善的公共交通網絡"},{"english":"stricter planning rules","chinese":"更嚴格的規劃規則"},{"english":"prevent overcrowded neighbourhoods from expanding","chinese":"防止過度擠迫的社區擴張"},{"english":"proper infrastructure","chinese":"適當的基礎設施"},{"english":"housing shortages","chinese":"房屋短缺"},{"english":"congestion and pollution","chinese":"交通擠塞及污染"},{"english":"make smaller regions more attractive","chinese":"令較小地區更具吸引力"},{"english":"manage urban growth more carefully","chinese":"更審慎地管理城市增長"}]},"model-essay-12-ielts-direct-question":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-12-ielts-direct-question","essayKey":"direct-question:12","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-12-ielts-direct-question","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/direct-question/EdmundBd9Dir-Q12","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"Discipline is one of the most difficult responsibilities teachers face, especially when one child repeatedly prevents others from learning. However, I do not think asking a disruptive child to leave the classroom is the best way to handle the problem. It may create immediate silence, but it rarely addresses the reasons behind the behaviour. A better approach is to combine firm classroom management with support from the school and parents.","chinese":"紀律管理是教師面對的其中一項最困難的責任，尤其是當一名孩子反覆阻礙其他人學習時。 然而，我不認為要求一名擾亂課堂的孩子離開課室，是處理這個問題的最佳方法。 這樣做可能會立即帶來安靜，但它很少能處理該行為背後的原因。 更好的做法是把堅定的課堂管理，與學校和家長的支援結合起來。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"The first solution is to establish clear rules and predictable consequences before serious disruption occurs. Many children behave badly not because they are deliberately malicious, but because they do not understand boundaries or have never been made to face consistent outcomes. If a teacher explains what behaviour is acceptable, gives a warning when rules are broken, and then applies a fair consequence, students are more likely to take responsibility for their actions. For example, a pupil who keeps interrupting others could be moved to another seat, asked to complete a reflection task after class, or given a short meeting with the teacher. This keeps the child within the learning environment while making it clear that poor behaviour has a cost.","chinese":"第一個解決方法是在嚴重擾亂發生之前，建立清晰的規則和可預期的後果。 許多孩子表現不佳，並不是因為他們故意懷有惡意，而是因為他們不明白界線，或者從未被要求面對一致的後果。 如果老師解釋甚麼行為是可以接受的，在規則被打破時給予警告，然後施加公平的後果，學生便更有可能為自己的行為負責。 例如，一名不斷打斷別人的學生，可以被安排坐到另一個座位、被要求在課後完成一項反思任務，或者與老師進行一次簡短會面。 這樣既能讓孩子留在學習環境之中，同時也清楚表明不良行為是有代價的。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"Another important solution is to involve parents, counsellors, or senior teachers when the problem becomes repeated. Disruption is often a symptom of deeper issues, such as stress at home, low academic confidence, attention difficulties, or a desire for peer approval. Simply sending the child out may turn the corridor into an escape route rather than a real consequence. By contrast, a coordinated plan can identify the cause and respond more effectively. A school might set behavioural targets, offer counselling, or arrange regular communication with parents so that the child receives the same message from every direction.","chinese":"另一個重要的解決方法是，當問題反覆出現時，讓家長、輔導員或資深教師介入。 擾亂行為往往是更深層問題的症狀，例如家庭壓力、學業信心不足、注意力困難，或者渴望得到同輩認可。 單純把孩子送出去，可能會把走廊變成一條逃避路線，而不是真正的後果。 相比之下，一個協調一致的計劃能夠找出原因，並作出更有效的回應。 學校可以設定行為目標、提供輔導，或者安排與家長定期溝通，從而讓孩子從各方面都收到一致的訊息。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, removing a disruptive child from class is not the best response because it solves the appearance of disorder rather than the source of it. Clear rules, consistent consequences, and cooperation between teachers, families, and school specialists are more effective solutions.","chinese":"總結來說，把一名擾亂課堂的孩子移離課室並不是最佳回應，因為它解決的是混亂的表象，而不是混亂的根源。 清晰的規則、一致的後果，以及教師、家庭和學校專業人員之間的合作，才是更有效的解決方法。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"one of the most difficult responsibilities","chinese":"最困難的責任之一"},{"english":"teachers face","chinese":"教師面對的"},{"english":"repeatedly prevents others from","chinese":"反覆阻礙其他人"},{"english":"a disruptive child","chinese":"擾亂課堂的孩子"},{"english":"leave the classroom","chinese":"離開課室"},{"english":"the best way to handle the problem","chinese":"處理問題的最佳方法"},{"english":"create immediate silence","chinese":"立即帶來安靜"},{"english":"addresses the reasons behind","chinese":"處理……背後的原因"},{"english":"the behaviour","chinese":"行為"},{"english":"a better approach","chinese":"更好的做法"},{"english":"combine...with...","chinese":"將……與……結合"},{"english":"firm classroom management","chinese":"堅定的課堂管理"},{"english":"support from the school and parents","chinese":"來自學校和家長的支援"},{"english":"establish clear rules","chinese":"建立清晰規則"},{"english":"predictable consequences","chinese":"可預期的後果"},{"english":"before serious disruption occurs","chinese":"在嚴重擾亂發生之前"},{"english":"behave badly","chinese":"表現差；行為不當"},{"english":"deliberately malicious","chinese":"故意惡意的"},{"english":"understand boundaries","chinese":"明白界線"},{"english":"be made to face","chinese":"被要求面對"},{"english":"consistent outcomes","chinese":"一致的後果"},{"english":"acceptable behaviour","chinese":"可接受的行為"},{"english":"gives a warning","chinese":"給予警告"},{"english":"rules are broken","chinese":"規則被違反"},{"english":"applies a fair consequence","chinese":"執行公平的後果"},{"english":"take responsibility for","chinese":"對……負責"},{"english":"their actions","chinese":"他們的行為"},{"english":"keeps interrupting others","chinese":"不斷打斷別人"},{"english":"be moved to another seat","chinese":"被調到另一個座位"},{"english":"complete a reflection task","chinese":"完成反思任務"},{"english":"after class","chinese":"下課後"},{"english":"a short meeting with the teacher","chinese":"與老師短暫面談"},{"english":"within the learning environment","chinese":"在學習環境之內"},{"english":"poor behaviour has a cost","chinese":"不良行為是有代價的"},{"english":"involve parents","chinese":"讓家長參與"},{"english":"counsellors","chinese":"輔導員"},{"english":"senior teachers","chinese":"資深教師"},{"english":"the problem becomes repeated","chinese":"問題變得反覆出現"},{"english":"a symptom of deeper issues","chinese":"更深層問題的徵兆"},{"english":"stress at home","chinese":"家庭壓力"},{"english":"low academic confidence","chinese":"學業信心低"},{"english":"attention difficulties","chinese":"專注困難"},{"english":"a desire for peer approval","chinese":"渴望得到朋輩認同"},{"english":"sending the child out","chinese":"將孩子趕出課室"},{"english":"turn the corridor into","chinese":"將走廊變成"},{"english":"an escape route","chinese":"逃避途徑"},{"english":"rather than a real consequence","chinese":"而不是真正的後果"},{"english":"by contrast","chinese":"相比之下"},{"english":"a coordinated plan","chinese":"協調一致的計劃"},{"english":"identify the cause","chinese":"找出原因"},{"english":"respond more effectively","chinese":"更有效地回應"},{"english":"set behavioural targets","chinese":"設定行為目標"},{"english":"offer counselling","chinese":"提供輔導"},{"english":"arrange regular communication with","chinese":"安排與……定期溝通"},{"english":"receives the same message from every direction","chinese":"從各方面收到一致訊息"},{"english":"removing a disruptive child from class","chinese":"將擾亂課堂的孩子帶離課室"},{"english":"solves the appearance of disorder","chinese":"解決表面的混亂"},{"english":"the source of it","chinese":"問題的根源"},{"english":"consistent consequences","chinese":"一致的後果"},{"english":"cooperation between","chinese":"……之間的合作"},{"english":"school specialists","chinese":"學校專業人員"},{"english":"more effective solutions","chinese":"更有效的解決方法"}]},"model-essay-12-ielts-discuss-both-views":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-12-ielts-discuss-both-views","essayKey":"discuss-both-views:12","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-12-ielts-discuss-both-views","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/discuss-both-views-your-opinion/EdmundBd9ExpBth-Q12","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"Discipline has become a growing concern in many schools, as teachers increasingly have to deal with disruptive behaviour alongside their academic duties. While some people argue that teachers should be mainly responsible for maintaining discipline, others believe that parents must take the lead. In my view, although teachers play an important role in enforcing rules at school, parents should bear the primary responsibility for shaping children’s behaviour.","chinese":"在許多學校中，紀律已成為一個日益令人關注的問題，因為教師除了履行教學職責之外，也越來越需要處理擾亂課堂的行為。 有些人認為教師應主要負責維持紀律，而另一些人則認為父母必須擔當主導角色。 在我看來，雖然教師在學校執行規則方面扮演重要角色，但父母應該承擔塑造孩子行為的主要責任。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"On the one hand, teachers are clearly responsible for creating an orderly learning environment. Since students spend many hours in classrooms, schools must have rules that prevent lessons from being constantly interrupted. For example, if a student repeatedly talks over others, refuses to follow instructions, or distracts classmates, the teacher has to respond immediately; otherwise, the whole class may suffer. In this sense, discipline is not separate from education. Without basic classroom control, even the most skilled teacher may struggle to teach effectively. Schools can also provide consistent consequences, such as detentions or behavioural reports, so that students understand that actions have limits.","chinese":"一方面，教師顯然有責任創造一個有秩序的學習環境。 由於學生每天在課室中度過許多時間，學校必須制定規則，以防止課堂不斷被打斷。 例如，如果一名學生反覆打斷別人說話、拒絕遵從指示，或者分散同學的注意力，教師就必須立即作出回應；否則，整個班級都可能受到影響。 從這個意義上說，紀律並不是與教育分開的事情。 如果沒有基本的課堂管理，即使是最有能力的教師也可能難以有效教學。 學校也可以提供一致的後果，例如留堂或行為報告，讓學生明白行為是有界線的。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"On the other hand, good discipline usually begins long before a child enters the classroom. Parents are the first people who teach children respect, self-control, and responsibility. If a child has never been taught at home to listen to adults, control anger, or accept consequences, teachers are forced to repair habits that have already become deeply rooted. For instance, a child who is allowed to shout, ignore rules, or blame others at home is likely to bring the same behaviour into school. Teachers can manage such behaviour temporarily, but parents shape the character behind it. This is why parental guidance is more fundamental than school punishment.","chinese":"另一方面，良好的紀律通常早在孩子進入課室之前就已經開始形成。 父母是最早教導孩子尊重、自制力和責任感的人。 如果一個孩子在家中從未被教導要聆聽成年人、控制憤怒或接受後果，教師就會被迫修正一些已經根深蒂固的習慣。 例如，一個在家中被允許大叫、無視規則或責怪他人的孩子，很可能會把同樣的行為帶到學校。 教師可以暫時管理這類行為，但父母才是在塑造其背後的品格。 這就是為甚麼父母的引導比學校的懲罰更根本。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, teachers must maintain discipline within school because learning cannot happen in chaos. However, I believe parents have the greater responsibility, as children’s attitudes towards authority, respect, and self-control are mainly formed at home. A school can enforce rules, but a family builds the habits that make those rules work.","chinese":"總結來說，教師必須在學校內維持紀律，因為學習不可能在混亂中發生。 然而，我認為父母負有更大的責任，因為孩子對權威、尊重和自制力的態度主要是在家中形成的。 學校可以執行規則，但家庭建立的習慣，才是讓這些規則真正發揮作用的關鍵。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"discipline","chinese":"紀律；管教"},{"english":"a growing concern","chinese":"日益受關注的問題"},{"english":"deal with disruptive behaviour","chinese":"處理擾亂秩序的行為"},{"english":"disruptive behaviour","chinese":"擾亂秩序的行為"},{"english":"alongside their academic duties","chinese":"在履行學業職責的同時"},{"english":"academic duties","chinese":"學業職責"},{"english":"be mainly responsible for","chinese":"主要負責"},{"english":"maintaining discipline","chinese":"維持紀律"},{"english":"take the lead","chinese":"帶頭；主導"},{"english":"enforcing rules at school","chinese":"在學校執行規則"},{"english":"bear the primary responsibility for","chinese":"承擔首要責任"},{"english":"shaping children's behaviour","chinese":"塑造兒童行為"},{"english":"on the one hand","chinese":"一方面"},{"english":"create an orderly learning environment","chinese":"建立有秩序的學習環境"},{"english":"since","chinese":"由於"},{"english":"spend many hours in classrooms","chinese":"在課室度過很多時間"},{"english":"prevent lessons from being constantly interrupted","chinese":"防止課堂不斷被打斷"},{"english":"be constantly interrupted","chinese":"不斷被打斷"},{"english":"repeatedly talks over others","chinese":"不斷打斷別人說話"},{"english":"refuse to follow instructions","chinese":"拒絕遵從指示"},{"english":"distract classmates","chinese":"分散同學注意力"},{"english":"respond immediately","chinese":"立即回應"},{"english":"otherwise","chinese":"否則"},{"english":"the whole class may suffer","chinese":"全班都可能受影響"},{"english":"in this sense","chinese":"從這個意義上說"},{"english":"not separate from","chinese":"與……並非分開"},{"english":"basic classroom control","chinese":"基本課堂管理"},{"english":"struggle to teach effectively","chinese":"難以有效教學"},{"english":"skilled teacher","chinese":"熟練的老師"},{"english":"provide consistent consequences","chinese":"提供一致的後果；作出一致處分"},{"english":"detentions","chinese":"留堂"},{"english":"behavioural reports","chinese":"行為報告"},{"english":"actions have limits","chinese":"行為有界限"},{"english":"on the other hand","chinese":"另一方面"},{"english":"begin long before","chinese":"早在……之前開始"},{"english":"enter the classroom","chinese":"進入課室"},{"english":"teach children respect","chinese":"教導孩子尊重"},{"english":"self-control","chinese":"自制能力"},{"english":"responsibility","chinese":"責任感"},{"english":"be taught at home to","chinese":"在家中被教導去"},{"english":"listen to adults","chinese":"聆聽成年人說話"},{"english":"control anger","chinese":"控制怒氣"},{"english":"accept consequences","chinese":"承擔後果"},{"english":"be forced to repair","chinese":"被迫修補；被迫糾正"},{"english":"deeply rooted","chinese":"根深蒂固"},{"english":"be allowed to","chinese":"被容許去"},{"english":"ignore rules","chinese":"無視規則"},{"english":"blame others","chinese":"責怪他人"},{"english":"be likely to","chinese":"很可能會"},{"english":"bring the same behaviour into school","chinese":"將同樣行為帶到學校"},{"english":"manage such behaviour temporarily","chinese":"暫時管理這類行為"},{"english":"shape the character behind it","chinese":"塑造行為背後的品格"},{"english":"parental guidance","chinese":"父母指導"},{"english":"more fundamental than","chinese":"比……更根本"},{"english":"school punishment","chinese":"學校懲罰"},{"english":"maintain discipline within school","chinese":"在校內維持紀律"},{"english":"learning cannot happen in chaos","chinese":"學習不能在混亂中發生"},{"english":"the greater responsibility","chinese":"更大的責任"},{"english":"attitudes towards authority","chinese":"對權威的態度"},{"english":"respect and self-control","chinese":"尊重和自制"},{"english":"be mainly formed at home","chinese":"主要在家中形成"},{"english":"enforce rules","chinese":"執行規則"},{"english":"build the habits that","chinese":"建立令……奏效的習慣"},{"english":"make those rules work","chinese":"令那些規則奏效"}]},"model-essay-12-ielts-opinion":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-12-ielts-opinion","essayKey":"opinion:12","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-12-ielts-opinion","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/opinions/EdmundBd9OP-Q12","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"In an age of increasingly frictionless spending, borrowing has become so easy that many people barely notice when ordinary purchases turn into long-term financial liabilities. It is often argued that this problem is mainly caused by the excessive and irresponsible use of credit cards, and that banks should not provide such cards unless an applicant can clearly afford to repay what is borrowed. This essay completely agrees, because credit cards encourage spending without immediate financial pain, while banks have a clear duty to prevent unaffordable lending.","chinese":"在一個消費愈來愈毫不費力的時代，借貸已變得如此容易，以致許多人幾乎察覺不到，日常購物何時已變成長期的債務負擔。 人們常主張，這個問題主要是由過度且不負責任地使用信用卡所造成，而銀行不應發出這類卡片，除非申請人明確有能力償還所借款項。 本文完全同意這個觀點，因為信用卡會鼓勵人們在沒有即時財務痛感的情況下消費，而銀行也有明確責任防止人們承擔無力償還的借貸。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"The strongest reason for agreeing with this view is that credit cards weaken the natural restraint that other forms of payment impose. Because no money visibly leaves a person’s account at the moment of purchase, unnecessary spending feels harmless, so small discretionary expenses are repeated until they become difficult to control. For example, an office worker who routinely uses a credit card for takeaway meals, taxis and online shopping may not realise how much has been spent until the monthly statement arrives. The problem is then intensified by the repayment structure itself. Minimum payments create the illusion that the debt is manageable, whereas interest charges quietly increase the total balance. Someone who pays only a small portion of a holiday bill, for instance, may still be repaying it many months later.","chinese":"我之所以最同意這個觀點，最有力的理由是：信用卡削弱了其他付款方式原本會帶來的自然節制作用。 因為在購買當下，金錢並不會明顯地從個人帳戶中流出，因此不必要的消費會讓人覺得無傷大雅，而小額的非必要支出也就一再重複，直到變得難以控制。 例如，一名經常用信用卡支付外賣餐點、計程車和網上購物費用的上班族，可能要等到每月帳單寄來時，才意識到自己究竟花了多少錢。 而且，還款機制本身又會進一步加劇這個問題。 最低還款額會製造一種債務仍然可控的假象，然而利息費用卻會在不知不覺間推高總欠款額。 例如，一個人若在假期消費後只償還帳單中的一小部分，那麼幾個月之後，他可能仍然還在償還這筆債務。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"Banks should therefore issue credit cards only after carrying out strict affordability checks. In the first place, financial institutions possess the income data, credit history and risk-assessment tools needed to judge whether borrowing is realistic. A bank can see, for example, if an applicant already has multiple loans, unstable earnings or a record of overdraft use. More importantly, irresponsible lending can trap households in a cycle in which interest payments begin to consume money needed for essentials. A family living on one income, for instance, may start struggling with rent or utility bills once a poorly screened credit-card balance begins to grow. Requiring convincing proof of repayment ability is therefore not excessive caution but responsible lending.","chinese":"因此，銀行只有在進行嚴格的負擔能力審查之後，才應發出信用卡。 首先，金融機構掌握了判斷借貸是否實際可行所需的收入資料、信用紀錄以及風險評估工具。 例如，銀行可以看出申請人是否已經背負多筆貸款、收入不穩定，或有使用透支的紀錄。 更重要的是，不負責任的放貸會使家庭陷入一種惡性循環：利息支出開始吞噬原本應該用於基本生活所需的金錢。 例如，一個只靠單一收入維生的家庭，一旦經審查不周而產生的信用卡欠款開始增加，就可能開始難以負擔房租或水電費。 因此，要求申請人提出具說服力的還款能力證明，並不是過度謹慎，而是負責任的放貸。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, I completely agree that irresponsible credit-card use is a major cause of personal debt and that banks should not issue credit cards unless repayment is clearly affordable. Because such borrowing encourages detached spending and because lenders are uniquely placed to prevent debt spirals, stricter controls are both justified and necessary.","chinese":"總而言之，我完全同意，不負責任地使用信用卡是造成個人債務的主要原因之一，而除非申請人明確有能力負擔還款，否則銀行不應發出信用卡。 因為這種借貸會助長與實際支出脫節的消費方式，而放貸者又處於獨特的位置，能夠防止債務惡性循環的形成，所以更嚴格的管制既合理，也有其必要。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"in an age of","chinese":"在……的時代"},{"english":"increasingly frictionless spending","chinese":"越來越方便、幾乎無阻力的消費"},{"english":"borrowing has become so easy that","chinese":"借貸變得如此容易，以致"},{"english":"barely notice","chinese":"幾乎沒有察覺"},{"english":"ordinary purchases","chinese":"日常購物"},{"english":"turn into","chinese":"變成"},{"english":"long-term financial liabilities","chinese":"長期財務負擔"},{"english":"it is often argued that","chinese":"人們經常認為"},{"english":"be mainly caused by","chinese":"主要由……造成"},{"english":"excessive and irresponsible use of","chinese":"過度及不負責任地使用"},{"english":"credit cards","chinese":"信用卡"},{"english":"provide such cards","chinese":"提供這類卡"},{"english":"unless an applicant can clearly afford to","chinese":"除非申請人明顯有能力"},{"english":"repay what is borrowed","chinese":"償還所借款項"},{"english":"encourage spending","chinese":"鼓勵消費"},{"english":"immediate financial pain","chinese":"即時的財務痛楚"},{"english":"have a clear duty to","chinese":"明確有責任去"},{"english":"prevent unaffordable lending","chinese":"防止負擔不起的借貸"},{"english":"the strongest reason for agreeing with","chinese":"同意……的最有力原因"},{"english":"weaken the natural restraint","chinese":"削弱自然的節制"},{"english":"forms of payment","chinese":"付款方式"},{"english":"impose restraint","chinese":"施加約束"},{"english":"no money visibly leaves","chinese":"沒有金錢明顯離開"},{"english":"at the moment of purchase","chinese":"在購買的一刻"},{"english":"unnecessary spending","chinese":"不必要的消費"},{"english":"feel harmless","chinese":"感覺無害"},{"english":"discretionary expenses","chinese":"非必要開支；可自由決定的開支"},{"english":"be repeated until","chinese":"不斷重複，直到"},{"english":"difficult to control","chinese":"難以控制"},{"english":"routinely uses","chinese":"經常使用"},{"english":"takeaway meals","chinese":"外賣餐"},{"english":"online shopping","chinese":"網上購物"},{"english":"realise how much has been spent","chinese":"意識到已花了多少錢"},{"english":"the monthly statement arrives","chinese":"月結單到達"},{"english":"be intensified by","chinese":"因……而加劇"},{"english":"repayment structure","chinese":"還款結構"},{"english":"minimum payments","chinese":"最低還款額"},{"english":"create the illusion that","chinese":"製造……的錯覺"},{"english":"the debt is manageable","chinese":"債務可應付"},{"english":"whereas","chinese":"然而"},{"english":"interest charges","chinese":"利息費用"},{"english":"quietly increase","chinese":"悄悄增加"},{"english":"the total balance","chinese":"總結欠"},{"english":"pay only a small portion of","chinese":"只支付……的一小部分"},{"english":"a holiday bill","chinese":"假期開支賬單"},{"english":"still be repaying it","chinese":"仍在償還"},{"english":"many months later","chinese":"多個月後"},{"english":"issue credit cards","chinese":"發出信用卡"},{"english":"only after carrying out","chinese":"只有在進行……之後"},{"english":"strict affordability checks","chinese":"嚴格的負擔能力審查"},{"english":"in the first place","chinese":"首先"},{"english":"financial institutions","chinese":"金融機構"},{"english":"possess","chinese":"擁有"},{"english":"income data","chinese":"收入資料"},{"english":"credit history","chinese":"信貸紀錄"},{"english":"risk-assessment tools","chinese":"風險評估工具"},{"english":"judge whether borrowing is realistic","chinese":"判斷借貸是否實際可行"},{"english":"multiple loans","chinese":"多筆貸款"},{"english":"unstable earnings","chinese":"不穩定收入"},{"english":"a record of overdraft use","chinese":"使用透支的紀錄"},{"english":"more importantly","chinese":"更重要的是"},{"english":"irresponsible lending","chinese":"不負責任的放貸"},{"english":"trap households in a cycle","chinese":"令家庭陷入循環"},{"english":"interest payments","chinese":"利息付款"},{"english":"begin to consume","chinese":"開始消耗"},{"english":"money needed for essentials","chinese":"生活必需開支所需的金錢"},{"english":"living on one income","chinese":"靠一份收入生活"},{"english":"struggle with rent or utility bills","chinese":"難以應付租金或水電煤費"},{"english":"poorly screened","chinese":"審批不嚴的"},{"english":"credit-card balance","chinese":"信用卡結欠"},{"english":"begin to grow","chinese":"開始增加"},{"english":"convincing proof of repayment ability","chinese":"具說服力的還款能力證明"},{"english":"not excessive caution but responsible lending","chinese":"不是過分謹慎，而是負責任放貸"},{"english":"personal debt","chinese":"個人債務"},{"english":"a major cause of","chinese":"……的主要原因"},{"english":"repayment is clearly affordable","chinese":"還款明顯負擔得起"},{"english":"detached spending","chinese":"與實際金錢感脫節的消費"},{"english":"lenders are uniquely placed to","chinese":"貸款人特別有條件去"},{"english":"prevent debt spirals","chinese":"防止債務惡性循環"},{"english":"stricter controls","chinese":"更嚴格的管制"},{"english":"both justified and necessary","chinese":"既合理亦有必要"}]},"model-essay-13-ielts-cause-solution":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-13-ielts-cause-solution","essayKey":"cause-solution:13","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-13-ielts-cause-solution","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/problem-and-cause/EdmundBd9CnS-Q13","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"Children are going online with less adult supervision and from early ages, which can expose them to risks they are not mature enough to recognise. Parents therefore face two main difficulties: keeping children safe from harmful digital material and helping them develop self-control online. This essay will discuss these problems and suggest solutions.","chinese":"兒童在較少成人監督的情況下上網，而且從較小的年齡便開始接觸網絡，這可能使他們面對一些他們尚未成熟到足以辨識的風險。 因此，父母面對兩個主要困難：保護孩子遠離有害的數位內容，以及幫助他們在網上培養自我控制能力。 本文將討論這些問題並提出解決方法。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"One major problem is that parents cannot easily monitor what children see or whom they communicate with. The internet is not a single controlled space: a child may start by watching cartoons, but one click can lead to violent videos, misleading information, or conversations with strangers. Since children often lack the judgement to separate entertainment from manipulation, they may reveal private information, copy unsuitable behaviour, or become frightened by disturbing content. Another difficulty is the battle over screen time. Digital devices are designed to hold attention, so children may resist limits, rush homework, sleep late, or prefer online stimulation to face-to-face play. Parents are therefore managing not only a device, but also a powerful habit.","chinese":"其中一個主要問題是，父母難以輕易監察孩子在網上看到甚麼，或與誰交流。 互聯網並不是一個單一而受控制的空間：一個孩子可能只是從觀看卡通開始，但一次點擊便可能通向暴力影片、誤導性資訊，或與陌生人的對話。 由於孩子往往缺乏判斷力，難以分辨娛樂與操控之間的界線，他們可能會透露私人資料、模仿不合適的行為，或因令人不安的內容而感到害怕。 另一個困難是圍繞螢幕時間的拉鋸。 數位設備本身就是為了吸引注意力而設計的，因此孩子可能會抗拒限制、匆忙完成作業、晚睡，或更偏好網上刺激而不是面對面的玩耍。 因此，父母所管理的不只是一部設備，更是一種強大的習慣。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"These problems can be reduced through clear rules, technical safeguards and education. First, parents should create consistent household routines: devices can be used in shared areas, screen time can be limited after homework, and phones should be kept out of bedrooms at night. Second, parents should use age-appropriate controls, privacy settings and safe-search tools, not as a substitute for parenting, but as a safety net. Finally, children need to be taught digital judgement. Schools and parents can explain why personal details should not be shared, why online strangers may be dangerous, and why upsetting content should be reported immediately. This turns internet safety from a hidden battle into an open conversation.","chinese":"這些問題可以透過清晰規則、技術保障和教育來減少。 首先，父母應建立一致的家庭規律：設備可以只在公共空間使用，螢幕時間可以限制在完成功課之後，而手機在晚上應該放在睡房之外。 其次，父母應使用適合孩子年齡的管控功能、私隱設定和安全搜尋工具；這些不是用來取代父母管教，而是作為一張安全網。 最後，孩子需要被教導數位判斷力。 學校和父母可以解釋為甚麼不應分享個人資料、為甚麼網上陌生人可能很危險，以及為甚麼令人不安的內容應立即舉報。 這能把網絡安全從一場隱藏的角力，轉化為一場公開的對話。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, unsupervised internet use creates problems because parents struggle to monitor online risks and control digital habits. The most effective response is not a total ban, but a steady combination of boundaries, protection and education, so that children can use the internet safely as they grow.","chinese":"總結來說，缺乏監督的互聯網使用會造成問題，因為父母難以監察網上風險，也難以控制孩子的數位習慣。 最有效的應對方法並不是全面禁止，而是穩定地結合界線、保護和教育，使孩子在成長過程中能夠安全地使用互聯網。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"go online","chinese":"上網"},{"english":"less adult supervision","chinese":"較少成人監管"},{"english":"from an early age","chinese":"從小；年紀很小時"},{"english":"expose them to risks","chinese":"使他們接觸風險"},{"english":"mature enough to recognise","chinese":"成熟到足以識別"},{"english":"face two main difficulties","chinese":"面對兩個主要困難"},{"english":"harmful digital material","chinese":"有害的數碼內容"},{"english":"develop self-control online","chinese":"培養網上自制能力"},{"english":"monitor what children see","chinese":"監察兒童看到的內容"},{"english":"communicate with","chinese":"與……溝通"},{"english":"a single controlled space","chinese":"單一受控制的空間"},{"english":"one click can lead to","chinese":"一按就可能導致"},{"english":"violent videos","chinese":"暴力影片"},{"english":"misleading information","chinese":"誤導性資料"},{"english":"conversations with strangers","chinese":"與陌生人交談"},{"english":"lack the judgement to","chinese":"缺乏判斷力去……"},{"english":"separate entertainment from manipulation","chinese":"分辨娛樂和操控"},{"english":"reveal private information","chinese":"透露私人資料"},{"english":"unsuitable behaviour","chinese":"不合適的行為"},{"english":"disturbing content","chinese":"令人不安的內容"},{"english":"the battle over screen time","chinese":"圍繞屏幕時間的爭拗"},{"english":"screen time","chinese":"屏幕時間"},{"english":"be designed to hold attention","chinese":"被設計成吸引注意力"},{"english":"resist limits","chinese":"抗拒限制"},{"english":"rush homework","chinese":"匆忙完成家課"},{"english":"sleep late","chinese":"晚睡"},{"english":"online stimulation","chinese":"網上刺激"},{"english":"face-to-face play","chinese":"面對面的玩樂"},{"english":"managing not only","chinese":"不只是管理"},{"english":"a powerful habit","chinese":"強大的習慣"},{"english":"be reduced through","chinese":"透過……減少"},{"english":"clear rules","chinese":"清晰規則"},{"english":"technical safeguards","chinese":"技術保障措施"},{"english":"consistent household routines","chinese":"一致的家庭常規"},{"english":"shared areas","chinese":"共用空間"},{"english":"be limited after homework","chinese":"在完成家課後受限制"},{"english":"kept out of bedrooms","chinese":"不應放在睡房內"},{"english":"age-appropriate controls","chinese":"適合年齡的管制設定"},{"english":"privacy settings","chinese":"私隱設定"},{"english":"safe-search tools","chinese":"安全搜尋工具"},{"english":"a substitute for parenting","chinese":"育兒的替代品"},{"english":"a safety net","chinese":"安全網"},{"english":"digital judgement","chinese":"數碼判斷力"},{"english":"personal details","chinese":"個人資料"},{"english":"online strangers","chinese":"網上陌生人"},{"english":"upsetting content","chinese":"令人不安的內容"},{"english":"be reported immediately","chinese":"應立即舉報"},{"english":"internet safety","chinese":"網絡安全"},{"english":"a hidden battle","chinese":"隱藏的鬥爭"},{"english":"an open conversation","chinese":"開放的對話"},{"english":"unsupervised internet use","chinese":"無人監管的互聯網使用"},{"english":"struggle to monitor","chinese":"難以監察"},{"english":"online risks","chinese":"網上風險"},{"english":"control digital habits","chinese":"控制數碼習慣"},{"english":"the most effective response","chinese":"最有效的回應"},{"english":"a total ban","chinese":"全面禁止"},{"english":"a steady combination of","chinese":"……的穩定結合"},{"english":"boundaries","chinese":"界線"},{"english":"protection and education","chinese":"保護和教育"},{"english":"as they grow","chinese":"隨着他們成長"}]},"model-essay-13-ielts-direct-question":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-13-ielts-direct-question","essayKey":"direct-question:13","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-13-ielts-direct-question","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/direct-question/EdmundBd9Dir-Q13","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"Formal education is often treated as the clearest route to social value, especially because doctors, engineers and researchers rely on advanced knowledge. However, I do not think educated people are the most valuable members of society. Society is best served when academic expertise is combined with practical competence, and many essential skills are learned by doing rather than by studying alone.","chinese":"正規教育常被視為創造社會價值最清晰的途徑，尤其是因為醫生、工程師和研究人員都依賴高深知識。 然而，我並不認為受過教育的人就是社會中最有價值的成員。 當學術專業知識與實際能力結合時，社會才能得到最好的服務，而許多重要技能是透過實踐學會的，而不是單靠學習得來。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"The main reason is that value should be measured by contribution, not by credentials. An educated person may understand theories, systems and principles, but this knowledge only becomes socially useful when it is applied with judgment. A qualified manager, for instance, may know how an organisation should operate, yet an experienced shop owner, builder or community volunteer may understand people, timing and risk far better because they have solved real problems repeatedly. In this sense, education is a powerful tool, but it is not a crown that automatically makes one person more valuable than another. A society that respects only degrees can become blind to the quiet competence that keeps daily life running.","chinese":"主要原因是，價值應該以貢獻來衡量，而不是以學歷或資歷來衡量。 一個受過教育的人也許明白理論、系統和原則，但這些知識只有在被有判斷力地應用時，才會對社會真正有用。 例如，一位合資格的經理也許知道一個機構應該如何運作，但一位有經驗的店主、建築工人或社區義工，可能更了解人、時機和風險，因為他們已經反覆解決過真實問題。 從這個意義上說，教育是一種強大的工具，但它不是一頂能自動使一個人比另一個人更有價值的皇冠。 一個只尊重學位的社會，可能會看不見那些默默維持日常生活運作的實際能力。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"People can also learn several socially valuable skills through experience. One is practical problem-solving: workers who repair machines, care for children or manage busy kitchens often learn to notice small warning signs before they become serious failures. This benefits society because it prevents waste, accidents and disorder. Another is human judgment. Through years of dealing with customers, patients, neighbours or colleagues, people learn patience, negotiation and empathy, which help reduce conflict and build trust. For example, an experienced nurse, mechanic or elderly caregiver may calm a tense situation not because they have memorised a rule, but because they can read the room and respond wisely.","chinese":"人們也可以透過經驗學會幾種對社會有價值的技能。 其中一種是實際解決問題的能力：修理機器、照顧兒童或管理繁忙廚房的工人，往往會學懂在小小的警號變成嚴重失誤之前就先注意到它們。 這對社會有益，因為它能防止浪費、意外和混亂。 另一種是人的判斷力。 透過多年與顧客、病人、鄰居或同事打交道，人們會學會耐性、協商和同理心，而這些都有助於減少衝突並建立信任。 例如，一位有經驗的護士、機械師或長者照顧者，可能能夠安撫一個緊張的局面，不是因為他們背熟了一條規則，而是因為他們能夠看懂現場氣氛，並作出明智回應。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, I do not believe that educated people are the most valuable for society. Education is important, but social value also comes from experience-based skills such as practical judgment, communication, emotional intelligence and hands-on problem-solving.","chinese":"總結來說，我不相信受過教育的人就是對社會最有價值的人。 教育很重要，但社會價值也來自以經驗為基礎的技能，例如實際判斷力、溝通能力、情緒智慧和親手解決問題的能力。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"formal education","chinese":"正規教育"},{"english":"be treated as","chinese":"被視為"},{"english":"the clearest route to","chinese":"通往……最明確的途徑"},{"english":"social value","chinese":"社會價值"},{"english":"rely on advanced knowledge","chinese":"依賴高深知識"},{"english":"advanced knowledge","chinese":"高深知識"},{"english":"valuable members of society","chinese":"社會中有價值的成員"},{"english":"be best served when","chinese":"當……時最能受惠"},{"english":"academic expertise","chinese":"學術專業知識"},{"english":"be combined with","chinese":"與……結合"},{"english":"practical competence","chinese":"實務能力"},{"english":"essential skills","chinese":"必要技能"},{"english":"learned by doing","chinese":"從實踐中學習"},{"english":"rather than by studying alone","chinese":"而不是單靠讀書"},{"english":"be measured by","chinese":"應以……衡量"},{"english":"contribution, not credentials","chinese":"貢獻，而不是資歷"},{"english":"understand theories, systems and principles","chinese":"理解理論、系統和原則"},{"english":"socially useful","chinese":"對社會有用"},{"english":"be applied with judgment","chinese":"以判斷力加以運用"},{"english":"a qualified manager","chinese":"合資格的管理者"},{"english":"how an organisation should operate","chinese":"一個組織應如何運作"},{"english":"an experienced shop owner","chinese":"有經驗的店主"},{"english":"community volunteer","chinese":"社區義工"},{"english":"understand people, timing and risk","chinese":"理解人情、時機和風險"},{"english":"solve real problems repeatedly","chinese":"反覆解決真實問題"},{"english":"in this sense","chinese":"從這個意義上說"},{"english":"a powerful tool","chinese":"強大的工具"},{"english":"not a crown","chinese":"不是一頂冠冕"},{"english":"automatically makes one person more valuable","chinese":"自動令一個人更有價值"},{"english":"respects only degrees","chinese":"只尊重學位"},{"english":"become blind to","chinese":"對……視而不見"},{"english":"quiet competence","chinese":"默默的能力"},{"english":"keep daily life running","chinese":"維持日常生活運作"},{"english":"socially valuable skills","chinese":"對社會有價值的技能"},{"english":"through experience","chinese":"透過經驗"},{"english":"practical problem-solving","chinese":"實際解難能力"},{"english":"repair machines","chinese":"維修機器"},{"english":"care for children","chinese":"照顧兒童"},{"english":"manage busy kitchens","chinese":"管理繁忙的廚房"},{"english":"notice small warning signs","chinese":"察覺細微警號"},{"english":"serious failures","chinese":"嚴重故障；嚴重失誤"},{"english":"prevent waste, accidents and disorder","chinese":"防止浪費、意外和混亂"},{"english":"human judgment","chinese":"人情判斷；人的判斷力"},{"english":"years of dealing with","chinese":"多年處理……的經驗"},{"english":"patience, negotiation and empathy","chinese":"耐性、協商和同理心"},{"english":"reduce conflict","chinese":"減少衝突"},{"english":"build trust","chinese":"建立信任"},{"english":"an elderly caregiver","chinese":"長者照顧者"},{"english":"calm a tense situation","chinese":"平息緊張局面"},{"english":"memorise a rule","chinese":"背熟一條規則"},{"english":"read the room","chinese":"觀察現場氣氛；看懂場合"},{"english":"respond wisely","chinese":"明智地回應"},{"english":"experience-based skills","chinese":"以經驗為基礎的技能"},{"english":"practical judgment","chinese":"實際判斷力"},{"english":"emotional intelligence","chinese":"情緒智商"},{"english":"hands-on problem-solving","chinese":"親身實踐的解難能力"}]},"model-essay-13-ielts-discuss-both-views":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-13-ielts-discuss-both-views","essayKey":"discuss-both-views:13","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-13-ielts-discuss-both-views","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/discuss-both-views-your-opinion/EdmundBd9ExpBth-Q13","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"Homework is a long-standing part of schooling, but there is disagreement about whether children should receive it every day. Some argue that daily homework is essential for academic success, whereas others believe that children need regular breaks from schoolwork. In my view, children should not be given homework every day, because learning is stronger when practice is purposeful rather than constant.","chinese":"功課一直是學校教育中存在已久的一部分，但人們對於孩子是否應該每天都有功課存在分歧。 有些人認為每天做功課對學業成功是必要的，而另一些人則認為孩子需要定期從課業中休息。 在我看來，孩子不應該每天都有功課，因為當練習是有目的的，而不是不斷重複時，學習效果會更好。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"Those who support daily homework usually believe that it builds discipline and reinforces classroom learning. When pupils review a topic shortly after a lesson, they are more likely to remember key ideas and identify gaps in their understanding. For example, a child who practises a few mathematics problems after studying fractions may notice mistakes before the next lesson, rather than allowing confusion to grow quietly. Daily assignments can also create a steady routine, which may help less organised students develop responsibility. From this perspective, homework is not merely extra work; it is a structure that keeps children engaged with their studies.","chinese":"支持每天有功課的人通常認為，功課能培養紀律，並鞏固課堂學習。 當學生在課後不久複習一個課題時，他們更有可能記住重點概念，並發現自己理解上的漏洞。 例如，一個孩子在學習分數後做幾道數學題，可能會在下一課之前發現錯誤，而不是讓困惑在不知不覺中加深。 每天的功課也能建立穩定的日常習慣，這可能有助於較缺乏組織能力的學生培養責任感 從這個角度來看，功課不只是額外的工作；它是一種讓孩子持續投入學習的結構。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"However, I believe that giving homework every day can be counterproductive, especially for younger students. Children need time to rest, play, exercise, read for pleasure and interact with their families. If every school day ends with more academic tasks, education can begin to feel like an endless conveyor belt, and this may weaken motivation rather than strengthen it. A tired child who completes a worksheet mechanically is not necessarily learning deeply. Moreover, excessive homework can crowd out activities that also support success at school, such as sleep, sport and social development. These are not luxuries; they help children return to class with better concentration and emotional balance.","chinese":"然而，我認為每天給功課可能會適得其反，尤其是對年紀較小的學生而言。 孩子需要時間休息、玩耍、運動、為興趣而閱讀，以及與家人互動。 如果每個上學日都以更多學業任務作結，教育便可能開始像一條無止境的輸送帶，而這可能會削弱學習動機，而不是增強它。 一個疲倦的孩子即使機械式地完成工作紙，也不一定是在深入學習。 此外，過量功課可能擠走一些同樣有助於學業成功的活動，例如睡眠、運動和社交發展 這些並不是奢侈的東西；它們能幫助孩子以更好的專注力和情緒平衡回到課堂。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, daily homework may help students revise lessons and build study habits, but it should not be treated as a requirement for success. Schools should assign homework when it genuinely consolidates learning, not simply because another day has passed. A balanced approach is more educationally sound than a rigid daily routine.","chinese":"總結來說，每天做功課或許能幫助學生複習課堂內容並建立學習習慣，但它不應被視為成功的必要條件。 學校應該在功課真正能鞏固學習時才佈置功課，而不是單純因為又過了一天就安排功課。 相比僵化的每日功課安排，一種平衡的做法在教育上更加合理。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"a long-standing part of","chinese":"長久以來是……的一部分"},{"english":"schooling","chinese":"學校教育"},{"english":"there is disagreement about whether","chinese":"對於是否……有分歧"},{"english":"receive it every day","chinese":"每日收到它"},{"english":"daily homework","chinese":"每日家課"},{"english":"be essential for academic success","chinese":"對學業成功不可或缺"},{"english":"regular breaks from","chinese":"定期從……中休息"},{"english":"schoolwork","chinese":"學校功課"},{"english":"in my view","chinese":"在我看來"},{"english":"should not be given","chinese":"不應被給予"},{"english":"learning is stronger when","chinese":"當……時學習更有效"},{"english":"purposeful rather than constant","chinese":"有目的，而不是不停重複"},{"english":"support daily homework","chinese":"支持每日家課"},{"english":"build discipline","chinese":"培養自律"},{"english":"reinforce classroom learning","chinese":"鞏固課堂學習"},{"english":"review a topic","chinese":"重溫一個課題"},{"english":"shortly after a lesson","chinese":"上課後不久"},{"english":"remember key ideas","chinese":"記住重點概念"},{"english":"identify gaps in their understanding","chinese":"找出理解上的空隙"},{"english":"practise a few mathematics problems","chinese":"練習幾條數學題"},{"english":"studying fractions","chinese":"學習分數"},{"english":"notice mistakes","chinese":"發現錯誤"},{"english":"before the next lesson","chinese":"下一課之前"},{"english":"rather than allowing","chinese":"而不是任由"},{"english":"confusion to grow quietly","chinese":"困惑悄悄加深"},{"english":"daily assignments","chinese":"每日作業"},{"english":"create a steady routine","chinese":"建立穩定常規"},{"english":"less organised students","chinese":"組織能力較弱的學生"},{"english":"develop responsibility","chinese":"培養責任感"},{"english":"from this perspective","chinese":"從這個角度來看"},{"english":"not merely extra work","chinese":"不只是額外工作"},{"english":"a structure that keeps children engaged with","chinese":"讓孩子持續投入……的結構"},{"english":"engaged with their studies","chinese":"投入學習"},{"english":"giving homework every day","chinese":"每日給家課"},{"english":"counterproductive","chinese":"適得其反"},{"english":"younger students","chinese":"年幼學生"},{"english":"read for pleasure","chinese":"為興趣而閱讀"},{"english":"interact with their families","chinese":"與家人互動"},{"english":"every school day ends with","chinese":"每個上學日都以……結束"},{"english":"academic tasks","chinese":"學業任務"},{"english":"begin to feel like","chinese":"開始感覺像"},{"english":"an endless conveyor belt","chinese":"永無止境的輸送帶"},{"english":"weaken motivation rather than strengthen it","chinese":"削弱而不是增強動力"},{"english":"a tired child","chinese":"疲累的孩子"},{"english":"complete a worksheet mechanically","chinese":"機械式完成工作紙"},{"english":"not necessarily learning deeply","chinese":"不一定在深入學習"},{"english":"excessive homework","chinese":"過量家課"},{"english":"crowd out","chinese":"擠走；排擠掉"},{"english":"support success at school","chinese":"支持學校成功"},{"english":"social development","chinese":"社交發展"},{"english":"these are not luxuries","chinese":"這些不是奢侈品"},{"english":"return to class with","chinese":"帶着……回到課堂"},{"english":"better concentration","chinese":"更佳專注力"},{"english":"emotional balance","chinese":"情緒平衡"},{"english":"revise lessons","chinese":"複習課堂內容"},{"english":"build study habits","chinese":"建立學習習慣"},{"english":"be treated as","chinese":"被視為"},{"english":"a requirement for success","chinese":"成功的必要條件"},{"english":"assign homework","chinese":"分配家課"},{"english":"genuinely consolidates learning","chinese":"真正鞏固學習"},{"english":"not simply because","chinese":"不只是因為"},{"english":"another day has passed","chinese":"又過了一天"},{"english":"a balanced approach","chinese":"平衡做法"},{"english":"educationally sound","chinese":"在教育上更合理"},{"english":"a rigid daily routine","chinese":"僵化的每日常規"}]},"model-essay-13-ielts-opinion":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-13-ielts-opinion","essayKey":"opinion:13","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-13-ielts-opinion","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/opinions/EdmundBd9OP-Q13","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"In most areas of life, meaningful success does not happen by accident. Many people therefore believe that ambition is indispensable to achievement. I completely agree, because ambition gives people both the endurance to continue through difficulty and the drive to improve until opportunities become tangible results.","chinese":"在生活的大多數範疇中，有意義的成功並不是偶然發生的。 因此，許多人相信，抱負對成就而言是不可或缺的。 我完全同意， 因為抱負既給予人們在困難中堅持下去的耐力，也給予人們不斷進步的動力，直到機會轉化為具體成果。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"The first reason ambition is essential is that it sustains effort over long periods of time. Real success normally demands discipline, and ambitious people are far more willing to tolerate inconvenience in order to reach a goal. A student aiming for a highly competitive scholarship, for example, may spend evenings revising, reduce social activities and practise under constant pressure for months. Just as importantly, ambition helps people recover from setbacks instead of abandoning their plans at the first disappointment. When such a student performs badly in an early mock exam, ambition encourages them to analyse weaknesses and try again rather than conclude that success is impossible. Because achievement usually comes after sacrifice and failure, this kind of persistence is not optional; it is fundamental.","chinese":"抱負之所以重要，第一個原因是它能讓人長時間維持努力。 真正的成功通常需要紀律，而有抱負的人為了達成目標，往往更願意忍受種種不便。 例如，一名以競爭激烈的獎學金為目標的學生，可能會在晚上持續溫習、減少社交活動，並在持續壓力下練習數月。 同樣重要的是，抱負能幫助人們在遭遇挫折後重新站起來，而不是在第一次失望時就放棄原本的計劃。 當這樣的學生在早期模擬考中表現欠佳時，抱負會促使他們分析自己的弱點，並再次嘗試，而不是直接認定成功是不可能的。 因為成就通常是在犧牲與失敗之後才出現，這種堅持並不是可有可無的，而是根本性的條件。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"Ambition is equally important because it pushes people beyond mere competence. Those who genuinely want to succeed do not simply repeat familiar routines; they actively seek better methods, higher standards and more demanding responsibilities. An ambitious employee, for instance, is more likely to learn new software, request feedback and strengthen communication skills in order to prepare for promotion. Ambition also makes people alert to opportunities that less driven individuals often ignore. The same worker may volunteer for a difficult project or propose an innovative idea to senior managers, thereby gaining both experience and visibility. As a result, ambition does not just improve a person’s ability; it places that ability in situations where it can be recognised and rewarded.","chinese":"抱負同樣重要，因為它能推動人們超越僅僅「勝任」的層次。 真正想成功的人不會只是重複熟悉的做法；他們會主動尋求更好的方法、更高的標準，以及更具挑戰性的責任。 例如，一位有抱負的員工更有可能主動學習新軟件、要求回饋，並加強溝通能力，為晉升作準備。 抱負也會讓人更敏銳地留意那些較缺乏動力的人往往忽略的機會。 同一位員工可能會主動請纓參與艱難的項目，或向高層管理人員提出創新構想，從而同時獲得經驗與曝光機會。 因此，抱負不僅能提升一個人的能力，還能把這種能力放進能夠被看見和獲得回報的情境之中。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, I completely agree that ambition is essential for success. It enables people to endure sacrifice, recover from failure, pursue improvement and seize opportunities, and these are precisely the conditions in which meaningful achievement becomes possible.","chinese":"總而言之，我完全同意抱負對成功而言是不可或缺的。 它使人能夠承受犧牲、從失敗中恢復、追求進步並把握機會，而這些正是有意義的成就得以實現的條件。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"in most areas of life","chinese":"在生活大部分範疇中"},{"english":"meaningful success","chinese":"有意義的成功"},{"english":"happen by accident","chinese":"偶然發生"},{"english":"many people therefore believe that","chinese":"因此很多人相信"},{"english":"ambition","chinese":"雄心；抱負"},{"english":"be indispensable to","chinese":"對……不可或缺"},{"english":"achievement","chinese":"成就"},{"english":"I completely agree","chinese":"我完全同意"},{"english":"give people both","chinese":"同時給予人……和……"},{"english":"the endurance to continue through difficulty","chinese":"面對困難時堅持下去的耐力"},{"english":"the drive to improve","chinese":"進步的動力"},{"english":"tangible results","chinese":"實質成果"},{"english":"the first reason","chinese":"第一個原因"},{"english":"be essential","chinese":"是必要的"},{"english":"sustain effort","chinese":"維持努力"},{"english":"over long periods of time","chinese":"長時間地"},{"english":"real success","chinese":"真正的成功"},{"english":"demand discipline","chinese":"需要自律"},{"english":"be far more willing to","chinese":"更加願意"},{"english":"tolerate inconvenience","chinese":"忍受不便"},{"english":"in order to reach a goal","chinese":"為了達成目標"},{"english":"aim for","chinese":"以……為目標"},{"english":"a highly competitive scholarship","chinese":"競爭非常激烈的獎學金"},{"english":"spend evenings revising","chinese":"晚上花時間溫習"},{"english":"reduce social activities","chinese":"減少社交活動"},{"english":"practise under constant pressure","chinese":"在持續壓力下練習"},{"english":"just as importantly","chinese":"同樣重要的是"},{"english":"recover from setbacks","chinese":"從挫折中恢復過來"},{"english":"instead of","chinese":"而不是"},{"english":"abandon their plans","chinese":"放棄計劃"},{"english":"at the first disappointment","chinese":"一遇到失望便"},{"english":"perform badly","chinese":"表現欠佳"},{"english":"an early mock exam","chinese":"早期的模擬考試"},{"english":"analyse weaknesses","chinese":"分析弱點"},{"english":"try again rather than conclude that","chinese":"再嘗試，而不是斷定"},{"english":"success is impossible","chinese":"成功是不可能的"},{"english":"come after sacrifice and failure","chinese":"在犧牲和失敗之後出現"},{"english":"this kind of persistence","chinese":"這種堅持"},{"english":"not optional","chinese":"並非可有可無"},{"english":"be fundamental","chinese":"是根本的"},{"english":"be equally important","chinese":"同樣重要"},{"english":"push people beyond","chinese":"推動人超越……"},{"english":"mere competence","chinese":"單純稱職；基本能力"},{"english":"genuinely want to succeed","chinese":"真心想成功"},{"english":"simply repeat familiar routines","chinese":"只是重複熟悉的例行工作"},{"english":"familiar routines","chinese":"熟悉的例行工作"},{"english":"actively seek","chinese":"積極尋求"},{"english":"better methods","chinese":"更好的方法"},{"english":"higher standards","chinese":"更高標準"},{"english":"more demanding responsibilities","chinese":"要求更高的責任"},{"english":"for instance","chinese":"例如"},{"english":"be more likely to","chinese":"更有可能"},{"english":"learn new software","chinese":"學習新軟件"},{"english":"request feedback","chinese":"要求回饋"},{"english":"strengthen communication skills","chinese":"加強溝通技巧"},{"english":"prepare for promotion","chinese":"為晉升作準備"},{"english":"make people alert to","chinese":"令某人對……保持敏銳"},{"english":"alert to opportunities","chinese":"對機會保持敏銳"},{"english":"less driven individuals","chinese":"動力較低的人"},{"english":"volunteer for","chinese":"自願參與"},{"english":"a difficult project","chinese":"困難的項目"},{"english":"propose an innovative idea","chinese":"提出創新想法"},{"english":"senior managers","chinese":"高層經理"},{"english":"thereby gaining","chinese":"從而獲得"},{"english":"experience and visibility","chinese":"經驗和曝光機會"},{"english":"as a result","chinese":"因此"},{"english":"does not just improve","chinese":"不只是改善"},{"english":"place that ability in situations where","chinese":"將這種能力放在……的情境中"},{"english":"be recognised and rewarded","chinese":"得到認可和獎勵"},{"english":"in conclusion","chinese":"總括而言"},{"english":"enable people to","chinese":"使人能夠"},{"english":"endure sacrifice","chinese":"承受犧牲"},{"english":"recover from failure","chinese":"從失敗中恢復過來"},{"english":"pursue improvement","chinese":"追求進步"},{"english":"seize opportunities","chinese":"把握機會"},{"english":"precisely the conditions in which","chinese":"正正是……的條件"},{"english":"become possible","chinese":"變得可能"}]},"model-essay-14-ielts-advantage-disadvantage":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-14-ielts-advantage-disadvantage","essayKey":"advantage-disadvantage:14","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-14-ielts-advantage-disadvantage","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/advantage-and-disadvantage/EdmundBd9AdDisAd-Q14","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"In many countries, renting has become a common housing choice, especially in large cities where property prices are extremely high. This arrangement offers several clear advantages, including financial flexibility and greater mobility, although it also brings notable disadvantages, such as insecurity and the absence of long-term ownership benefits.","chinese":"在許多國家，租屋已成為一種常見的居住選擇，尤其是在房價極高的大城市裡更是如此。 雖然這種安排在靈活性和較低的初期成本方面具有明顯優勢， 但它同時也存在一些重要缺點，例如居住上的不穩定性，以及缺乏長遠的財務回報。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"One major advantage of renting is that it requires far less money at the outset. Buying a property usually demands a substantial deposit, legal fees and long-term mortgage repayments, whereas renting is far more accessible for young adults, newly married couples and people with modest incomes. As a result, tenants can direct their savings towards other priorities, such as education, childcare or emergency funds. Renting also gives people the freedom to move more easily. If a worker receives a job offer in another city, for instance, it is usually much easier to move at the end of a lease than to sell a home. Moreover, tenants are often spared major repair costs, which would otherwise place a heavy burden on homeowners.","chinese":"租住房屋的一大優點，是它在經濟上比買房容易負擔得多。 購買房產通常需要支付一大筆首期、法律費用以及長期按揭；相比之下，租屋在一開始所需的資金要少得多。 這降低了居住的財務門檻，並使人們——特別是年輕成年人或低收入家庭——可以把儲蓄用於其他重要需要。 例如，一對年輕夫婦可能會選擇租住一個單位，並把金錢用於育兒或進修，而不是讓自己被沉重的按揭負擔綁住。 租屋的另一個好處是，它提供了更高的流動性。 當工作、經濟狀況或家庭情況出現變化時，租客通常能更容易搬遷，而這對業主來說往往困難得多。 例如，一個人在另一個城市獲得工作機會時，可以在租約結束後直接搬走，而不必經歷出售物業那漫長又繁瑣的過程。 因此，租屋之所以具有很大吸引力，是因為它既減少了前期支出，也在充滿不確定性的世界中提供了更大的靈活性。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"However, renting is not without drawbacks. Perhaps the most serious one is the lack of security it creates. Tenants may face rising rents, restrictive contracts or sudden eviction if the landlord decides to sell the property. This uncertainty can be especially difficult for families with children, whose schooling and social lives may be disrupted by frequent moves. Another disadvantage is that rent payments do not build equity. After years of paying monthly rent, a tenant may have little to show for it financially, while homeowners gradually acquire an asset that may increase in value over time. Renters also have limited control over their living space, since even minor alterations often require the landlord’s approval.","chinese":"然而，租屋也有顯著的缺點，其中最嚴重的便是它所帶來的不穩定感。 如果業主決定出售物業，租客便可能面對租金上升、租約限制，甚至被迫遷出。 這種不確定性會令人難以安頓下來、規劃未來，或建立穩定的家庭生活。 例如，一個有學齡兒童的家庭可能被迫一再搬遷，從而干擾孩子的教育和社交關係。 租屋的另一個缺點是，租金支出最終不會轉化為房產擁有權。 即使多年來持續支付租金，租客也無法累積資產；相反，業主則會逐步擁有一項可能隨時間升值的財產。 例如，一個人若租屋二十年，可能已花費一大筆金錢，但到了最後仍然一無所有。 因此，雖然租屋在短期內可能相當實際，但從長遠來看，它可能使人們在財務和心理上都處於較脆弱的狀態。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In summary, renting can be attractive because it lowers the initial financial barrier, offers flexibility and reduces responsibility for major maintenance. Nevertheless, these benefits are balanced by weaker residential security, limited personal control and the fact that tenants do not accumulate property wealth.","chinese":"總結來說，租住房屋有明顯的優點，尤其是較低的初期成本，以及更大的搬遷自由。 與此同時，它也涉及嚴重的缺點，包括較低的居住穩定性，以及缺乏長遠的財務收益。 正因如此，租屋對某些人來說可以是一種務實的解決方式，但對另一些人而言，則未必是理想的安排。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"renting","chinese":"租樓"},{"english":"a common housing choice","chinese":"常見住屋選擇"},{"english":"large cities","chinese":"大城市"},{"english":"property prices","chinese":"樓價；物業價格"},{"english":"extremely high","chinese":"極高"},{"english":"this arrangement","chinese":"這種安排"},{"english":"clear advantages","chinese":"明顯好處"},{"english":"financial flexibility","chinese":"財政彈性"},{"english":"greater mobility","chinese":"更大的流動性"},{"english":"notable disadvantages","chinese":"明顯缺點"},{"english":"insecurity","chinese":"缺乏保障；不穩定"},{"english":"the absence of","chinese":"缺乏"},{"english":"long-term ownership benefits","chinese":"長期擁有業權的好處"},{"english":"one major advantage of","chinese":"……的一個主要好處"},{"english":"require far less money","chinese":"需要少得多金錢"},{"english":"at the outset","chinese":"一開始"},{"english":"demands a substantial deposit","chinese":"需要大額首期"},{"english":"legal fees","chinese":"律師費；法律費用"},{"english":"long-term mortgage repayments","chinese":"長期按揭還款"},{"english":"whereas","chinese":"然而；相比之下"},{"english":"far more accessible for","chinese":"對……容易負擔得多"},{"english":"young adults","chinese":"年輕成年人"},{"english":"newly married couples","chinese":"新婚夫婦"},{"english":"modest incomes","chinese":"中低收入"},{"english":"as a result","chinese":"因此"},{"english":"tenants","chinese":"租客"},{"english":"direct their savings towards","chinese":"將積蓄用於"},{"english":"other priorities","chinese":"其他優先事項"},{"english":"childcare","chinese":"照顧子女"},{"english":"emergency funds","chinese":"應急儲備"},{"english":"the freedom to move","chinese":"搬遷的自由"},{"english":"receive a job offer","chinese":"收到工作機會"},{"english":"in another city","chinese":"在另一個城市"},{"english":"at the end of a lease","chinese":"在租約期滿時"},{"english":"sell a home","chinese":"出售住宅"},{"english":"be spared","chinese":"免於承擔"},{"english":"major repair costs","chinese":"大型維修費用"},{"english":"would otherwise place a heavy burden on","chinese":"否則會對……造成沉重負擔"},{"english":"a heavy burden","chinese":"沉重負擔"},{"english":"homeowners","chinese":"自置物業人士；業主"},{"english":"not without drawbacks","chinese":"並非沒有缺點"},{"english":"perhaps the most serious one","chinese":"也許最嚴重的一點"},{"english":"the lack of security","chinese":"缺乏保障"},{"english":"rising rents","chinese":"租金上升"},{"english":"restrictive contracts","chinese":"限制多的合約"},{"english":"sudden eviction","chinese":"突然被迫遷"},{"english":"the landlord","chinese":"業主"},{"english":"sell the property","chinese":"出售物業"},{"english":"this uncertainty","chinese":"這種不確定性"},{"english":"especially difficult for","chinese":"對……尤其困難"},{"english":"schooling and social lives","chinese":"學業和社交生活"},{"english":"be disrupted by","chinese":"受……打亂"},{"english":"frequent moves","chinese":"頻繁搬遷"},{"english":"rent payments","chinese":"租金付款"},{"english":"build equity","chinese":"累積物業權益"},{"english":"monthly rent","chinese":"每月租金"},{"english":"have little to show for it","chinese":"沒有多少實質成果"},{"english":"financially","chinese":"在財政上"},{"english":"acquire an asset","chinese":"獲得一項資產"},{"english":"increase in value over time","chinese":"隨時間升值"},{"english":"limited control over","chinese":"對……控制有限"},{"english":"living space","chinese":"居住空間"},{"english":"minor alterations","chinese":"小型改動"},{"english":"require the landlord's approval","chinese":"需要業主批准"},{"english":"in summary","chinese":"總括而言"},{"english":"be attractive because","chinese":"因為……而具吸引力"},{"english":"lower the initial financial barrier","chinese":"降低最初的財政門檻"},{"english":"initial financial barrier","chinese":"最初的財政門檻"},{"english":"reduce responsibility for","chinese":"減少對……的責任"},{"english":"major maintenance","chinese":"大型維修保養"},{"english":"nevertheless","chinese":"然而"},{"english":"be balanced by","chinese":"被……抵消"},{"english":"residential security","chinese":"居住保障"},{"english":"personal control","chinese":"個人控制權"},{"english":"accumulate property wealth","chinese":"累積物業財富"}]},"model-essay-14-ielts-cause-solution":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-14-ielts-cause-solution","essayKey":"cause-solution:14","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-14-ielts-cause-solution","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/problem-and-cause/EdmundBd9CnS-Q14","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"Tourism has made air travel a normal part of modern life, and the rising number of travellers has naturally created greater demand for flights. This essay will discuss the environmental problems caused by this trend, especially carbon emissions and damage around airports, before suggesting practical measures to reduce these effects.","chinese":"旅遊業已經使航空旅行成為現代生活中正常的一部分，而旅客人數的上升自然也創造了對更多航班的更大需求。 本文將討論這一趨勢所造成的環境問題，尤其是碳排放和機場周邊的破壞，然後提出可行的措施來減少這些影響。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"The most serious problem is that more flights lead to higher fuel consumption and, therefore, greater greenhouse gas emissions. Aircraft burn large amounts of aviation fuel, so when airlines operate extra routes or increase flight frequency, more carbon dioxide is released into the atmosphere. Over time, this contributes to global warming, which can intensify heatwaves, rising sea levels and extreme weather. A second problem is the environmental pressure created on the ground. Busier airports often require larger terminals, longer runways and heavier road traffic, all of which can disturb nearby habitats and worsen local air and noise pollution. For communities and wildlife living close to airports, the constant movement of planes can become a heavy environmental burden.","chinese":"最嚴重的問題是，更多航班會導致更高的燃料消耗，因此也會帶來更多的溫室氣體排放。 飛機會燃燒大量航空燃料，所以當航空公司營運額外航線或增加航班頻率時，更多二氧化碳便會被釋放到大氣中。 長遠而言，這會加劇全球暖化，而全球暖化可能使熱浪、海平面上升和極端天氣變得更加嚴重。 第二個問題是在地面上造成的環境壓力。 更繁忙的機場通常需要更大的客運大樓、更長的跑道和更密集的道路交通，而這些都可能干擾附近的棲息地，並惡化當地的空氣和噪音污染。 對於居住在機場附近的社區和野生動物而言，飛機不斷升降移動可能會成為沉重的環境負擔"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"There are several measures that could limit these problems. First, governments should encourage cleaner aviation by setting stricter emissions standards and supporting investment in more efficient aircraft, sustainable aviation fuels and better air-traffic management. If planes use less fuel and spend less time circling or waiting on runways, each journey will leave a smaller environmental footprint. Second, countries should reduce unnecessary demand for short flights. For example, high-speed rail, better coach networks and convenient domestic transport can give travellers a realistic alternative when the destination is not far away. Airlines could also be required to include environmental costs in ticket prices, so that extremely cheap flights no longer encourage people to travel casually without considering the impact.","chinese":"有幾項措施可以限制這些問題。 首先，政府應該透過制定更嚴格的排放標準，並支持對更高效飛機、可持續航空燃料和更完善空中交通管理的投資，來鼓勵更清潔的航空業。 如果飛機使用較少燃料，並減少在空中盤旋或在跑道上等待的時間，每一次旅程所留下的環境足跡便會更小。 第二，各國應該減少對短途航班的不必要需求。 例如，當目的地並不遙遠時，高速鐵路、更完善的長途巴士網絡和便利的本地交通可以為旅客提供一個現實可行的替代選擇。 航空公司也可以被要求把環境成本納入機票價格之中，這樣極其便宜的航班便不再鼓勵人們在不考慮影響的情況下隨意出行。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, the rising demand for flights damages the environment mainly through increased emissions and greater pressure around airports. Cleaner technology, stricter regulation and attractive alternatives to flying are therefore necessary to reduce these problems.","chinese":"總結來說，對航班需求的上升主要透過增加排放和加大機場周邊壓力來破壞環境。 因此，更清潔的技術、更嚴格的監管，以及具吸引力的飛行替代方案，都是減少這些問題所必需的。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"air travel","chinese":"航空旅遊；乘搭飛機出行"},{"english":"a normal part of modern life","chinese":"現代生活的正常一部分"},{"english":"the rising number of travellers","chinese":"旅客人數上升"},{"english":"greater demand for flights","chinese":"對航班更大的需求"},{"english":"environmental problems caused by","chinese":"由……造成的環境問題"},{"english":"this trend","chinese":"這個趨勢"},{"english":"carbon emissions","chinese":"碳排放"},{"english":"damage around airports","chinese":"機場周邊的破壞"},{"english":"practical measures","chinese":"實際可行的措施"},{"english":"reduce these effects","chinese":"減少這些影響"},{"english":"the most serious problem","chinese":"最嚴重的問題"},{"english":"lead to","chinese":"導致"},{"english":"higher fuel consumption","chinese":"更高燃料消耗"},{"english":"greenhouse gas emissions","chinese":"溫室氣體排放"},{"english":"burn large amounts of","chinese":"燃燒大量……"},{"english":"aviation fuel","chinese":"航空燃料"},{"english":"operate extra routes","chinese":"營運額外航線"},{"english":"increase flight frequency","chinese":"增加航班班次"},{"english":"be released into the atmosphere","chinese":"被釋放到大氣中"},{"english":"carbon dioxide","chinese":"二氧化碳"},{"english":"contributes to global warming","chinese":"導致；促成全球暖化"},{"english":"intensify heatwaves","chinese":"加劇熱浪"},{"english":"rising sea levels","chinese":"海平面上升"},{"english":"extreme weather","chinese":"極端天氣"},{"english":"environmental pressure","chinese":"環境壓力"},{"english":"created on the ground","chinese":"在地面造成的"},{"english":"busier airports","chinese":"更繁忙的機場"},{"english":"larger terminals","chinese":"更大型客運大樓"},{"english":"longer runways","chinese":"更長跑道"},{"english":"heavier road traffic","chinese":"更繁忙的道路交通"},{"english":"disturb nearby habitats","chinese":"干擾附近棲息地"},{"english":"worsen local air and noise pollution","chinese":"令本地空氣和噪音污染惡化"},{"english":"local air pollution","chinese":"本地空氣污染"},{"english":"noise pollution","chinese":"噪音污染"},{"english":"communities and wildlife","chinese":"社區和野生動物"},{"english":"living close to airports","chinese":"住在／生活在機場附近"},{"english":"the constant movement of planes","chinese":"飛機不停升降和移動"},{"english":"a heavy environmental burden","chinese":"沉重的環境負擔"},{"english":"several measures","chinese":"幾項措施"},{"english":"limit these problems","chinese":"限制；減少這些問題"},{"english":"encourage cleaner aviation","chinese":"推動更清潔的航空業"},{"english":"stricter emissions standards","chinese":"更嚴格的排放標準"},{"english":"supporting investment in","chinese":"支持對……的投資"},{"english":"more efficient aircraft","chinese":"更高效的飛機"},{"english":"sustainable aviation fuels","chinese":"可持續航空燃料"},{"english":"better air-traffic management","chinese":"更好的空中交通管理"},{"english":"use less fuel","chinese":"使用較少燃料"},{"english":"spend less time circling","chinese":"花較少時間盤旋"},{"english":"waiting on runways","chinese":"在跑道上等候"},{"english":"each journey","chinese":"每趟旅程"},{"english":"leave a smaller environmental footprint","chinese":"留下較小的環境足跡"},{"english":"unnecessary demand for","chinese":"對……的不必要需求"},{"english":"short flights","chinese":"短途航班"},{"english":"high-speed rail","chinese":"高速鐵路"},{"english":"better coach networks","chinese":"更完善的長途巴士網絡"},{"english":"convenient domestic transport","chinese":"便利的本地交通"},{"english":"a realistic alternative","chinese":"現實可行的替代選擇"},{"english":"the destination is not far away","chinese":"目的地不遠"},{"english":"be required to","chinese":"被要求去……"},{"english":"include environmental costs in","chinese":"將環境成本包括在……內"},{"english":"ticket prices","chinese":"機票價格"},{"english":"extremely cheap flights","chinese":"極低價航班"},{"english":"travel casually","chinese":"隨意出行"},{"english":"considering the impact","chinese":"考慮影響"},{"english":"rising demand for flights","chinese":"對航班日益上升的需求"},{"english":"increased emissions","chinese":"增加的排放"},{"english":"greater pressure around airports","chinese":"機場周邊更大的壓力"},{"english":"cleaner technology","chinese":"更清潔的技術"},{"english":"stricter regulation","chinese":"更嚴格的規管"},{"english":"attractive alternatives to flying","chinese":"具吸引力的飛行替代方案"}]},"model-essay-14-ielts-direct-question":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-14-ielts-direct-question","essayKey":"direct-question:14","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-14-ielts-direct-question","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/direct-question/EdmundBd9Dir-Q14","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"The widening gap between education in wealthy and poor nations is a serious problem because it limits social mobility and traps many young people in cycles of disadvantage. Several practical solutions can reduce this divide, especially if governments, international organisations, and private institutions work together rather than treating education as a local issue alone.","chinese":"富裕國家與貧困國家之間的教育差距不斷擴大，是一個嚴重問題，因為它限制了社會流動，並使許多年輕人陷入劣勢循環之中。 有幾個實際可行的解決方法可以縮小這種差距，尤其是當政府、國際組織和私人機構共同合作，而不是只把教育視為單一地區問題時。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"One important solution is to increase long-term investment in basic educational infrastructure. In many poorer countries, students are not failing because they lack ability; they are held back by overcrowded classrooms, poorly equipped schools, and a shortage of trained teachers. International aid should therefore be directed not only towards building schools, but also towards maintaining them, supplying learning materials, and paying teachers properly. For example, a rural school with reliable electricity, internet access, textbooks, and qualified staff would immediately give its students a fairer chance to compete with those in richer countries. Without these foundations, even the most ambitious education reforms will remain paper promises.","chinese":"其中一個重要的解決方法，是增加對基礎教育設施的長期投資。 在許多較貧困的國家，學生失敗並不是因為他們缺乏能力；他們是被過度擁擠的課室、設備不足的學校，以及受過訓練教師的短缺所拖累。 因此，國際援助不應只投向興建學校，也應投向維修保養學校、提供學習材料，以及合理支付教師薪酬。 例如，一所擁有穩定電力、網絡連接、課本和合資格教職員的鄉村學校，會立即給予學生更公平的機會，去與富裕國家的學生競爭。 沒有這些基礎，即使是最有抱負的教育改革，也只會停留在紙上承諾。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"Another effective approach is to expand teacher training and digital learning. Teachers in poorer regions often have limited access to modern teaching methods, so regular professional development could help them deliver lessons more effectively. At the same time, technology can narrow the educational gap if it is introduced carefully. Online courses, recorded lectures, and low-cost learning platforms can bring high-quality instruction to students who would otherwise have no access to specialist teachers. However, this should not mean simply handing out devices. Governments and charities must also provide affordable internet, technical support, and locally relevant content, so that technology becomes a bridge rather than another barrier.","chinese":"另一個有效方法，是擴大教師培訓和數位學習。 較貧困地區的教師往往較少接觸現代教學方法，因此定期的專業發展可以幫助他們更有效地授課。 同時，如果科技被謹慎地引入，它也可以縮小教育差距。 網上課程、錄影講座和低成本學習平台，可以把高質素教學帶給那些原本無法接觸專科教師的學生。 然而，這不應該只是簡單地派發電子設備。 政府和慈善機構也必須提供可負擔的網絡、技術支援，以及符合本地需要的內容，使科技成為橋樑，而不是另一道障礙。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, the education gap between rich and poor countries cannot be solved by one quick policy. It requires sustained investment in schools, better teacher training, and well-managed digital access. If these measures are combined, poorer countries can give their young people not just classrooms, but genuine opportunities.","chinese":"總結來說，富裕國家與貧困國家之間的教育差距，不能靠一項快速政策解決。 它需要對學校的持續投資、更好的教師培訓，以及管理得宜的數位使用途徑。 如果這些措施能夠結合起來，較貧困的國家便能給予年輕人不只是課室，而是真正的機會"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"the widening gap between","chinese":"……之間不斷擴大的差距"},{"english":"wealthy and poor nations","chinese":"富裕和貧窮國家"},{"english":"a serious problem","chinese":"嚴重問題"},{"english":"limits social mobility","chinese":"限制社會流動"},{"english":"traps many young people in","chinese":"令很多年輕人陷入……"},{"english":"cycles of disadvantage","chinese":"惡性劣勢循環"},{"english":"practical solutions","chinese":"實際可行的解決方法"},{"english":"reduce this divide","chinese":"縮小這種差距"},{"english":"international organisations","chinese":"國際組織"},{"english":"private institutions","chinese":"私營機構"},{"english":"work together","chinese":"合作"},{"english":"rather than treating","chinese":"而不是把……視為"},{"english":"a local issue alone","chinese":"單純的本地問題"},{"english":"long-term investment in","chinese":"對……的長期投資"},{"english":"basic educational infrastructure","chinese":"基本教育基礎設施"},{"english":"lack ability","chinese":"缺乏能力"},{"english":"held back by","chinese":"被……拖慢發展；受到……阻礙"},{"english":"overcrowded classrooms","chinese":"過度擠迫的課室"},{"english":"poorly equipped schools","chinese":"設備不足的學校"},{"english":"a shortage of trained teachers","chinese":"受訓教師短缺"},{"english":"international aid","chinese":"國際援助"},{"english":"be directed towards","chinese":"被投放於……"},{"english":"building schools","chinese":"興建學校"},{"english":"maintaining them","chinese":"維修和保養它們"},{"english":"supplying learning materials","chinese":"提供學習材料"},{"english":"paying teachers properly","chinese":"合理支付教師薪酬"},{"english":"a rural school","chinese":"鄉村學校"},{"english":"reliable electricity","chinese":"穩定供電"},{"english":"internet access","chinese":"互聯網接入"},{"english":"qualified staff","chinese":"合資格職員；合資格教師"},{"english":"give its students a fairer chance","chinese":"給學生更公平的機會"},{"english":"compete with","chinese":"與……競爭"},{"english":"those in richer countries","chinese":"較富裕國家的學生"},{"english":"without these foundations","chinese":"沒有這些基礎"},{"english":"ambitious education reforms","chinese":"具雄心的教育改革"},{"english":"remain paper promises","chinese":"只停留在空頭承諾"},{"english":"another effective approach","chinese":"另一個有效方法"},{"english":"expand teacher training","chinese":"擴大教師培訓"},{"english":"digital learning","chinese":"數碼學習"},{"english":"poorer regions","chinese":"較貧窮地區"},{"english":"limited access to","chinese":"有限機會接觸……"},{"english":"modern teaching methods","chinese":"現代教學方法"},{"english":"regular professional development","chinese":"定期專業發展"},{"english":"deliver lessons more effectively","chinese":"更有效地授課"},{"english":"narrow the educational gap","chinese":"縮小教育差距"},{"english":"introduced carefully","chinese":"被謹慎引入"},{"english":"online courses","chinese":"網上課程"},{"english":"recorded lectures","chinese":"錄製講課"},{"english":"low-cost learning platforms","chinese":"低成本學習平台"},{"english":"high-quality instruction","chinese":"高質素教學"},{"english":"would otherwise have no access to","chinese":"否則無法接觸到……"},{"english":"specialist teachers","chinese":"專科教師"},{"english":"handing out devices","chinese":"派發裝置"},{"english":"affordable internet","chinese":"負擔得起的互聯網"},{"english":"technical support","chinese":"技術支援"},{"english":"locally relevant content","chinese":"切合本地需要的內容"},{"english":"becomes a bridge rather than another barrier","chinese":"成為橋樑，而不是另一道障礙"},{"english":"cannot be solved by","chinese":"不能靠……解決"},{"english":"one quick policy","chinese":"一項速成政策"},{"english":"sustained investment in schools","chinese":"對學校的持續投資"},{"english":"better teacher training","chinese":"更好的教師培訓"},{"english":"well-managed digital access","chinese":"管理得宜的數碼接入"},{"english":"if these measures are combined","chinese":"如果這些措施結合起來"},{"english":"genuine opportunities","chinese":"真正的機會"}]},"model-essay-14-ielts-discuss-both-views":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-14-ielts-discuss-both-views","essayKey":"discuss-both-views:14","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-14-ielts-discuss-both-views","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/discuss-both-views-your-opinion/EdmundBd9ExpBth-Q14","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"It is sometimes argued that children should spend their spare time on educational pursuits, while others believe that this creates unnecessary pressure. I agree with the latter view, because childhood free time should mainly serve recovery, play, and social development rather than become an extension of the classroom.","chinese":"有人有時主張，孩子應該把空閒時間用於教育活動，而另一些人則認為，這樣做會造成不必要的壓力。 我同意後者的觀點，因為童年的空閒時間應該主要用於恢復精力、玩樂和社交發展，而不是成為課堂的延伸。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"Those who support educational activities make a reasonable point. Many parents worry that unstructured leisure will be wasted on screens, games, or passive entertainment. If children use part of their free time to read, practise a language, learn music, or solve puzzles, they may strengthen useful skills in a less formal setting. Such activities can also build discipline: a child who gets used to reading after school, for example, may develop concentration and curiosity that support later academic success. From this perspective, educational leisure is not a punishment but a way of planting seeds for the future.","chinese":"支持教育活動的人提出了一個合理的觀點。 許多父母擔心，沒有安排的休閒時間會被浪費在螢幕、遊戲或被動娛樂上。 如果孩子利用部分空閒時間閱讀、練習語言、學習音樂或解謎，他們便可能在較非正式的環境中強化有用的技能。 這些活動也能培養自律：例如，一個習慣放學後閱讀的孩子，可能會培養出有助於日後學業成功的專注力和好奇心。 從這個角度來看，教育性休閒並不是一種懲罰，而是一種為未來播種的方式。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"However, I believe that turning free time into another learning session places children under harmful pressure. After school, many children are already mentally tired from lessons, homework, tests, and constant evaluation. If their evenings and weekends are filled with extra academic tasks, rest disappears, and learning begins to feel like a cage rather than a source of growth. A child who moves from school to tuition to online exercises may appear productive, but in reality they may become anxious, resentful, and less motivated. This is especially damaging because play is not an empty time. Through games, sport, imagination, and casual conversation, children learn cooperation, emotional control, independence, and problem-solving in ways that worksheets cannot easily provide.","chinese":"然而，我認為，把空閒時間變成另一段學習時間，會使孩子承受有害的壓力。 放學後，許多孩子已經因為課堂、功課、測驗和持續評估而在精神上感到疲累。 如果他們的晚上和週末都被額外的學業任務填滿，休息便會消失，而學習也會開始像一個牢籠，而不是成長的來源。 一個從學校到補習、再到網上練習的孩子，表面上可能看起來很有成效，但實際上他們可能會變得焦慮、反感，並且更缺乏動力。 這尤其有害，因為玩樂並不是空白的時間。 透過遊戲、運動、想像和日常交談，孩子能以工作紙難以輕易提供的方式，學習合作、情緒控制、獨立性和解決問題的能力。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, although this parental approach may have good intentions, I firmly believe that children should not be expected to spend their free time studying. Childhood should not be scheduled so tightly that every spare hour has an academic purpose. Free time is not wasted time; it is where children breathe, grow, and become whole people.","chinese":"總結來說，儘管這種父母的做法可能出於好意，但我堅定地認為，孩子不應被期望把空閒時間用於學習。 童年不應被安排得如此緊密，以至於每一個空閒小時都有學業目的。 空閒時間並不是被浪費的時間；它是孩子得以喘息、成長，並成為完整的人的地方。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"it is sometimes argued that","chinese":"有時有人認為"},{"english":"spare time","chinese":"空餘時間"},{"english":"educational pursuits","chinese":"教育性活動；學習追求"},{"english":"unnecessary pressure","chinese":"不必要壓力"},{"english":"the latter view","chinese":"後者觀點"},{"english":"childhood free time","chinese":"童年空餘時間"},{"english":"serve recovery, play, and social development","chinese":"用於恢復、玩樂和社交發展"},{"english":"rather than become","chinese":"而不是變成"},{"english":"an extension of the classroom","chinese":"課室的延伸"},{"english":"support educational activities","chinese":"支持教育性活動"},{"english":"make a reasonable point","chinese":"提出合理觀點"},{"english":"unstructured leisure","chinese":"沒有安排的休閒時間"},{"english":"be wasted on","chinese":"被浪費在"},{"english":"screens, games, or passive entertainment","chinese":"螢幕、遊戲或被動娛樂"},{"english":"use part of their free time to","chinese":"用部分空餘時間去"},{"english":"practise a language","chinese":"練習一種語言"},{"english":"learn music","chinese":"學音樂"},{"english":"solve puzzles","chinese":"解謎題"},{"english":"strengthen useful skills","chinese":"加強有用技能"},{"english":"in a less formal setting","chinese":"在較非正式的環境中"},{"english":"build discipline","chinese":"培養自律"},{"english":"get used to","chinese":"習慣於"},{"english":"reading after school","chinese":"放學後閱讀"},{"english":"develop concentration and curiosity","chinese":"培養專注力和好奇心"},{"english":"later academic success","chinese":"日後學業成功"},{"english":"from this perspective","chinese":"從這個角度來看"},{"english":"educational leisure","chinese":"教育性休閒活動"},{"english":"not a punishment but","chinese":"不是懲罰，而是"},{"english":"plant seeds for the future","chinese":"為將來播下種子"},{"english":"turning free time into","chinese":"將空餘時間變成"},{"english":"another learning session","chinese":"另一節學習時間"},{"english":"place children under harmful pressure","chinese":"令兒童承受有害壓力"},{"english":"mentally tired from","chinese":"因……而精神疲累"},{"english":"constant evaluation","chinese":"持續評核"},{"english":"be filled with","chinese":"充滿"},{"english":"extra academic tasks","chinese":"額外學業任務"},{"english":"rest disappears","chinese":"休息消失"},{"english":"feel like a cage rather than","chinese":"感覺像牢籠，而不是"},{"english":"a source of growth","chinese":"成長的來源"},{"english":"move from school to tuition to","chinese":"從學校轉到補習再到"},{"english":"tuition","chinese":"補習"},{"english":"online exercises","chinese":"網上練習"},{"english":"appear productive","chinese":"看似有成效"},{"english":"in reality","chinese":"實際上"},{"english":"anxious, resentful, and less motivated","chinese":"焦慮、憤恨和較缺乏動力"},{"english":"especially damaging","chinese":"尤其有害"},{"english":"not an empty time","chinese":"不是空白無用的時間"},{"english":"through games, sport, imagination, and casual conversation","chinese":"透過遊戲、運動、想像和輕鬆交談"},{"english":"cooperation","chinese":"合作"},{"english":"emotional control","chinese":"情緒控制"},{"english":"independence and problem-solving","chinese":"獨立性和解難能力"},{"english":"worksheets","chinese":"工作紙"},{"english":"cannot easily provide","chinese":"不能輕易提供"},{"english":"parental approach","chinese":"家長做法"},{"english":"good intentions","chinese":"良好原意"},{"english":"be expected to","chinese":"被期望去"},{"english":"spend their free time studying","chinese":"用空餘時間學習"},{"english":"be scheduled so tightly","chinese":"被安排得如此緊密"},{"english":"every spare hour","chinese":"每一個空餘小時"},{"english":"an academic purpose","chinese":"學業目的"},{"english":"wasted time","chinese":"浪費了的時間"},{"english":"breathe, grow, and become whole people","chinese":"喘息、成長並成為完整的人"}]},"model-essay-14-ielts-opinion":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-14-ielts-opinion","essayKey":"opinion:14","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-14-ielts-opinion","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/opinions/EdmundBd9OP-Q14","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"In many societies, successful people are often imagined as confident, magnetic, and naturally charming. As a result, some argue that charisma is a necessary ingredient for achievement. I completely disagree with this view, because long-term success depends far more on competence, discipline, and trustworthiness than on personal charm.","chinese":"在許多社會中，成功人士常常被想像成自信、有吸引力，而且天生具有人格魅力的人。因此，有些人認為個人魅力是取得成就的必要條件。 我完全不同意這個觀點，因為長期的成功更多取決於能力、自律和可靠性，而不是個人魅力。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"The main reason charisma is not essential is that many forms of success are built on skill rather than social appeal. In most professions, people are ultimately judged by whether they can solve problems, make sound decisions, and deliver consistent results. A doctor, for example, does not become successful simply by speaking warmly to patients; he or she must diagnose illnesses accurately and provide effective treatment. Similarly, an engineer whose work prevents a bridge from collapsing may be quiet and socially reserved, but that does not make the achievement any less valuable. In these cases, charisma may make communication smoother, but it cannot replace expertise. Success is therefore more like a foundation than a spotlight: what matters most is not how brightly a person shines in public, but how solidly they perform when real responsibility is placed on them.","chinese":"個人魅力並非必不可少的主要原因是，許多形式的成功是建立在技能之上，而不是建立在社交吸引力之上。 在大多數職業中，人們最終會根據他們是否能解決問題、作出明智決定，並持續交出穩定成果來受到評價。 例如，一名醫生並不會單純因為能親切地和病人說話而成功；他或她必須準確診斷疾病，並提供有效的治療。 同樣地，一名工程師的工作如果能防止一座橋倒塌，即使他可能安靜且不擅社交，這也不會令他的成就變得較不重要。 在這些情況下，個人魅力也許能讓溝通更順暢，但它不能取代專業能力。 因此，成功更像是一個基礎，而不是一道聚光燈：最重要的並不是一個人在公眾面前閃耀得多麼耀眼，而是當真正的責任落在他身上時，他能表現得多麼穩健。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"Another reason is that charisma without substance can be fragile, and sometimes even dangerous. Charismatic people may attract attention quickly, but attention is not the same as achievement. If a leader is charming but unreliable, employees may initially feel inspired, yet they will soon lose confidence when promises are broken or decisions are poorly made. By contrast, a less charismatic person who is honest, prepared, and dependable can gradually earn deep respect. This kind of respect is quieter, but it lasts longer. In business, education, and public life, people eventually trust results more than attractive words.","chinese":"另一個原因是，沒有實質能力支撐的個人魅力可能很脆弱，有時甚至會很危險。 有魅力的人也許能很快吸引注意力，但注意力並不等同於成就。 如果一位領導者很有魅力但不可靠，員工起初可能會受到鼓舞，但當承諾被打破或決策做得很差時，他們很快就會失去信心。 相比之下，一個魅力較少但誠實、有準備且可靠的人，能夠逐漸贏得深厚的尊重。 這種尊重較為安靜，但卻更持久。 在商業、教育和公共生活中，人們最終會信任成果多於動聽的言辭。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, charisma can be useful, but it is not essential for success. Real success is built on ability, consistency, and integrity, not merely on the power to impress others.","chinese":"總結來說，個人魅力可以是有用的，但它並不是成功所必需的。 真正的成功是建立在能力、穩定性和誠信之上，而不僅僅是建立在打動他人的能力之上"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"in many societies","chinese":"在很多社會中"},{"english":"be imagined as","chinese":"被想像成"},{"english":"confident, magnetic, and naturally charming","chinese":"自信、有吸引力而且天生有魅力"},{"english":"as a result","chinese":"因此"},{"english":"argue that","chinese":"主張；認為"},{"english":"charisma","chinese":"個人魅力"},{"english":"a necessary ingredient for achievement","chinese":"成就的必要因素"},{"english":"completely disagree with this view","chinese":"完全不同意這個看法"},{"english":"long-term success","chinese":"長遠的成功"},{"english":"depend far more on","chinese":"更大程度上取決於"},{"english":"competence, discipline, and trustworthiness","chinese":"能力、自律和可靠"},{"english":"personal charm","chinese":"個人魅力"},{"english":"the main reason","chinese":"主要原因"},{"english":"not essential","chinese":"並非必要"},{"english":"many forms of success","chinese":"很多形式的成功"},{"english":"be built on","chinese":"建基於"},{"english":"rather than","chinese":"而不是"},{"english":"social appeal","chinese":"社交吸引力"},{"english":"in most professions","chinese":"在大多數職業中"},{"english":"be ultimately judged by","chinese":"最終根據……被評價"},{"english":"solve problems","chinese":"解決問題"},{"english":"make sound decisions","chinese":"作出明智決定"},{"english":"deliver consistent results","chinese":"持續取得穩定成果"},{"english":"become successful simply by","chinese":"單靠……而成功"},{"english":"speak warmly to","chinese":"溫和親切地對……說話"},{"english":"diagnose illnesses accurately","chinese":"準確診斷疾病"},{"english":"provide effective treatment","chinese":"提供有效治療"},{"english":"similarly","chinese":"同樣地"},{"english":"prevent a bridge from collapsing","chinese":"防止橋樑倒塌"},{"english":"socially reserved","chinese":"不太擅長社交；性格較內斂"},{"english":"make the achievement any less valuable","chinese":"令成就變得較不值錢"},{"english":"in these cases","chinese":"在這些情況下"},{"english":"make communication smoother","chinese":"令溝通更順暢"},{"english":"cannot replace expertise","chinese":"不能取代專業知識"},{"english":"be more like a foundation than a spotlight","chinese":"更像基礎，而不是聚光燈"},{"english":"what matters most is not","chinese":"最重要的不是"},{"english":"shine in public","chinese":"在公眾面前發光發亮"},{"english":"perform solidly","chinese":"表現穩健"},{"english":"real responsibility","chinese":"真正的責任"},{"english":"be placed on","chinese":"落在……身上"},{"english":"another reason is that","chinese":"另一個原因是"},{"english":"without substance","chinese":"缺乏實質內容"},{"english":"can be fragile","chinese":"可能很脆弱"},{"english":"attract attention quickly","chinese":"很快吸引注意"},{"english":"attention is not the same as achievement","chinese":"受關注不等於有成就"},{"english":"charming but unreliable","chinese":"有魅力但不可靠"},{"english":"initially feel inspired","chinese":"起初感到受鼓舞"},{"english":"lose confidence","chinese":"失去信心"},{"english":"promises are broken","chinese":"承諾被打破"},{"english":"decisions are poorly made","chinese":"決策做得差"},{"english":"by contrast","chinese":"相反"},{"english":"a less charismatic person","chinese":"魅力較少的人"},{"english":"honest, prepared, and dependable","chinese":"誠實、有準備而可靠"},{"english":"gradually earn deep respect","chinese":"逐漸贏得深厚尊重"},{"english":"this kind of respect","chinese":"這種尊重"},{"english":"last longer","chinese":"維持更久"},{"english":"in business, education, and public life","chinese":"在商業、教育和公共生活中"},{"english":"eventually trust results more than attractive words","chinese":"最終更相信成果，而不是動聽說話"},{"english":"in conclusion","chinese":"總括而言"},{"english":"can be useful, but not essential","chinese":"可以有用，但並非必要"},{"english":"real success is built on","chinese":"真正的成功建基於"},{"english":"ability, consistency, and integrity","chinese":"能力、穩定性和誠信"},{"english":"not merely on","chinese":"不只是建基於"},{"english":"the power to impress others","chinese":"令人留下深刻印象的能力"}]},"model-essay-15-ielts-advantage-disadvantage":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-15-ielts-advantage-disadvantage","essayKey":"advantage-disadvantage:15","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-15-ielts-advantage-disadvantage","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/advantage-and-disadvantage/EdmundBd9AdDisAd-Q15","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"In many education systems, children are encouraged to begin learning a foreign language in primary school rather than in their teenage years. While this policy can create practical problems, I believe it is beneficial because younger learners acquire languages more easily and early instruction gives all pupils opportunities later in life.","chinese":"在許多教育制度中，兒童被鼓勵在小學階段而非青少年時期才開始學習外語。 雖然這項政策可能帶來一些實際問題， 我認為這樣做是有益的，因為年紀較小的學習者更容易掌握語言，而及早接受外語教育也能為所有學生在日後提供更多機會。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"The chief advantage is that young children absorb pronunciation and sentence patterns with unusual ease. Because they are less self-conscious than adolescents, they are usually more willing to repeat unfamiliar sounds, make mistakes and try again. This creates a chain effect: frequent practice improves memory, stronger memory builds fluency, and growing fluency makes later study far less intimidating. For example, a six-year-old who learns songs, greetings and simple classroom expressions often becomes a more confident speaker in secondary school than a student who starts with grammar at thirteen. Early language education also promotes fairness. If schools provide it to all children, the benefits of speaking another language, such as cultural awareness and better study or work options, are not limited to those whose parents can afford private lessons.","chinese":"在年幼時學習外語的主要優點，在於孩子能夠更自然、更有自信地吸收這門語言。 年紀較小的學習者通常比年長學生更容易模仿發音和基本句型。 由於他們較少感到難為情，也較不害怕犯錯，因此往往更願意反覆練習；持續練習會加強記憶，更好的記憶會培養流暢度，而更高的流暢度則使日後的學習不那麼令人畏懼。 例如，一個六歲時便學習歌曲、問候語及簡單課堂用語的孩子，到了中學階段往往會比十三歲才開始正式學習文法的學生更有口語自信。 及早進行外語教育也能促進公平，因為它讓所有孩子都有機會接觸有價值的語言能力。 如果學校為所有學生提供外語教學，那麼更廣闊的文化視野以及更好的升學或就業機會，便不會只屬於那些負擔得起私人補習的家庭的孩子。 例如，來自低收入家庭的孩子即使無力負擔私人補習，仍然可以透過學校教育培養實用的語言能力。 因此，及早學習外語既能提升長遠的語言能力，也能促進機會平等。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"The disadvantages are real but less significant. One problem is that badly designed lessons can create pressure. If young pupils are forced to memorise long vocabulary lists and are corrected too harshly, enjoyment can turn into anxiety, which reduces participation and weakens motivation. Another drawback is that, in poorly resourced schools, adding a compulsory subject may take time away from essential literacy work. For instance, a school with too few trained staff may squeeze basic language drills into a crowded timetable while weaker readers still need support in their first language. However, these are problems of implementation rather than proof that early language learning is misguided.","chinese":"然而，及早推行外語教育確實也有缺點，尤其是在實施方式欠佳的情況下。 其中一個問題是，設計不良的課程可能帶來壓力，而不是激發好奇心。 如果年幼學生被迫背誦冗長的單字表，並且在犯錯時受到過於嚴厲的糾正，原本的樂趣便可能轉化為焦慮；一旦焦慮取代了好奇心，學生的參與度便會下降，自信心會減弱，持續學習的動機也會隨之降低。 例如，一個孩子若因發音錯誤而一再受到批評，最終可能會在課堂上完全不願開口。 另一個缺點是，在資源不足的學校中，加入一門必修外語課程可能會擠壓基礎讀寫教育的時間。 當課程表本已十分緊湊，而受過專業訓練的教師又不足時，學校可能會把過多時間投入外語基本操練，然而閱讀能力較弱的學生其實仍需要母語方面的支援。 例如，一所合資格教師不足的小學，可能會為了把外語課塞進本已擁擠的課程安排中，而減少閱讀支援課節。 然而，這些問題反映的其實是實施不當，而非及早學習外語本身有何缺陷。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, teaching a foreign language at an early age has some disadvantages, especially when schools lack time or expertise, but the advantages are clearly greater. It helps children develop stronger long-term language ability and ensures that these benefits are available to all, not just the most privileged.","chinese":"總結而言，幼年開始學習外語確實存在一些缺點，尤其是在學校缺乏時間或專業能力的情況下，但其優點顯然更大。 它不但有助於孩子培養更強的長遠語言能力，也確保這些好處能夠惠及所有學生，而不只是最有優勢的一群。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"education systems","chinese":"教育制度"},{"english":"be encouraged to","chinese":"被鼓勵去……"},{"english":"begin learning a foreign language","chinese":"開始學習外語"},{"english":"primary school","chinese":"小學"},{"english":"rather than in","chinese":"而不是在……"},{"english":"teenage years","chinese":"青少年時期"},{"english":"this policy","chinese":"這項政策"},{"english":"create practical problems","chinese":"造成實際問題"},{"english":"beneficial because","chinese":"有益，因為……"},{"english":"younger learners","chinese":"較年幼的學習者"},{"english":"acquire languages","chinese":"學會語言"},{"english":"early instruction","chinese":"早期教學"},{"english":"opportunities later in life","chinese":"人生較後階段的機會"},{"english":"the chief advantage","chinese":"主要好處"},{"english":"absorb pronunciation and sentence patterns","chinese":"吸收發音和句式"},{"english":"with unusual ease","chinese":"異常容易地"},{"english":"less self-conscious than","chinese":"比……較少自我拘束"},{"english":"adolescents","chinese":"青少年"},{"english":"willing to repeat","chinese":"願意重複"},{"english":"unfamiliar sounds","chinese":"陌生的聲音"},{"english":"make mistakes and try again","chinese":"犯錯並再試"},{"english":"creates a chain effect","chinese":"產生連鎖效應"},{"english":"frequent practice","chinese":"頻繁練習"},{"english":"improves memory","chinese":"改善記憶"},{"english":"builds fluency","chinese":"建立流暢度"},{"english":"growing fluency","chinese":"不斷提升的流暢度"},{"english":"far less intimidating","chinese":"沒那麼令人畏懼"},{"english":"a six-year-old","chinese":"六歲小朋友"},{"english":"simple classroom expressions","chinese":"簡單課堂用語"},{"english":"a more confident speaker","chinese":"更有信心的說話者"},{"english":"secondary school","chinese":"中學"},{"english":"starts with grammar","chinese":"從文法開始"},{"english":"early language education","chinese":"早期語言教育"},{"english":"promotes fairness","chinese":"促進公平"},{"english":"provide it to all children","chinese":"向所有兒童提供"},{"english":"the benefits of speaking another language","chinese":"學會另一種語言的好處"},{"english":"cultural awareness","chinese":"文化意識"},{"english":"better study or work options","chinese":"更好的升學或工作選擇"},{"english":"be limited to","chinese":"只限於……"},{"english":"afford private lessons","chinese":"負擔得起私人補習"},{"english":"less significant","chinese":"較不重要"},{"english":"badly designed lessons","chinese":"設計欠佳的課堂"},{"english":"create pressure","chinese":"造成壓力"},{"english":"young pupils","chinese":"年幼學生"},{"english":"be forced to memorise","chinese":"被迫死記"},{"english":"long vocabulary lists","chinese":"長長的生字表"},{"english":"corrected too harshly","chinese":"被過分嚴厲地糾正"},{"english":"turn into anxiety","chinese":"變成焦慮"},{"english":"reduces participation","chinese":"減少參與"},{"english":"weakens motivation","chinese":"削弱動力"},{"english":"another drawback","chinese":"另一個缺點"},{"english":"poorly resourced schools","chinese":"資源不足的學校"},{"english":"adding a compulsory subject","chinese":"增加一科必修科"},{"english":"take time away from","chinese":"佔用……的時間"},{"english":"essential literacy work","chinese":"基本讀寫訓練"},{"english":"too few trained staff","chinese":"受訓教師太少；受訓人手太少"},{"english":"squeeze basic language drills into","chinese":"將基本語言操練硬擠進……"},{"english":"basic language drills","chinese":"基本語言操練"},{"english":"a crowded timetable","chinese":"排得很滿的時間表"},{"english":"weaker readers","chinese":"閱讀能力較弱的學生"},{"english":"their first language","chinese":"他們的第一語言"},{"english":"problems of implementation","chinese":"執行上的問題"},{"english":"proof that","chinese":"……的證據"},{"english":"early language learning","chinese":"早期語言學習"},{"english":"misguided","chinese":"方向錯誤的"},{"english":"at an early age","chinese":"在年幼時"},{"english":"lack time or expertise","chinese":"缺乏時間或專業知識"},{"english":"clearly greater","chinese":"明顯更大"},{"english":"long-term language ability","chinese":"長遠語言能力"},{"english":"not just the most privileged","chinese":"不只是最有優勢的人"}]},"model-essay-15-ielts-cause-solution":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-15-ielts-cause-solution","essayKey":"cause-solution:15","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-15-ielts-cause-solution","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/problem-and-cause/EdmundBd9CnS-Q15","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"Eco-tourism is often promoted as a responsible way to travel, but when visitors enter remote areas, they can place serious pressure on local cultures and communities. This essay will discuss the cultural and social problems that may result from eco-tourism, before suggesting practical measures to protect local people and their traditions.","chinese":"生態旅遊通常被宣傳為一種負責任的旅行方式，但當遊客進入偏遠地區時，他們可能會對當地文化和社區造成嚴重壓力。 本文將討論生態旅遊可能帶來的文化和社會問題，然後提出保護當地居民及其傳統的實際措施。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"One major problem is that local culture may be commercialised. When tourists are willing to pay for “authentic” experiences, traditional ceremonies, clothing, music, and religious practices may gradually be turned into performances. As a result, customs that once had deep spiritual or social meaning can become little more than tourist attractions. This can weaken local identity, especially among younger people, who may start to see their own culture as something to sell rather than something to preserve. Another problem is that remote communities may be disrupted by sudden outside influence. Tourists can bring different values, spending habits, and expectations, which may change local behaviour and increase tension between residents and visitors. In some cases, prices for food, land, and services may rise, making everyday life harder for local families.","chinese":"其中一個主要問題是，當地文化可能會被商業化。 當遊客願意為「地道」體驗付費時，傳統儀式、服飾、音樂和宗教習俗可能會逐漸被變成表演。 結果是，原本具有深厚精神或社會意義的習俗，可能會變得只不過是旅遊景點而已。 這可能會削弱當地身份認同，尤其是在年輕人當中，因為他們可能會開始把自己的文化看成可以出售的東西，而不是應該保存的東西。 另一個問題是，偏遠社區可能會受到突然出現的外來影響所干擾。 遊客可能會帶來不同的價值觀、消費習慣和期望，而這些可能會改變當地人的行為，並增加居民與遊客之間的緊張關係。 在某些情況下，食物、土地和服務的價格可能會上升，使當地家庭的日常生活變得更加困難"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"Several measures can be taken to reduce these problems. First, eco-tourism should be controlled by local communities rather than outside companies. Local leaders should decide how many tourists may visit, which areas are open to outsiders, and which cultural practices should remain private. This would allow communities to benefit from tourism without losing control of their way of life. Second, governments and tourism operators should introduce clear rules for visitors. For example, tourists should be educated about local customs, dress codes, sacred sites, and acceptable behaviour before entering remote areas. Visitor numbers should also be limited, and part of the income from eco-tourism should be used to support local schools, cultural centres, healthcare, and environmental protection.","chinese":"可以採取幾項措施來減少這些問題。 首先，生態旅遊應該由當地社區控制，而不是由外來公司控制。 當地領袖應該決定可以接待多少遊客、哪些地區可以向外來者開放，以及哪些文化習俗應該保持私密。 這能讓社區從旅遊中受益，同時不會失去對自身生活方式的控制。 第二，政府和旅遊營運者應該為遊客制定清晰的規則。 例如，在進入偏遠地區之前，遊客應該接受有關當地習俗、服裝規範、神聖場所和可接受行為的教育。 遊客人數也應該受到限制，而生態旅遊收入的一部分應該用來支持當地學校、文化中心、醫療服務和環境保護。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, eco-tourism can damage remote communities by commercialising culture and disturbing local life. However, community control, visitor education, and careful regulation can help protect local traditions while still allowing tourism to bring economic benefits.","chinese":"總結來說，生態旅遊可能會透過將文化商業化和干擾當地生活，對偏遠社區造成傷害。 然而，社區控制、遊客教育和審慎規管可以幫助保護當地傳統，同時仍然讓旅遊帶來經濟利益。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"eco-tourism","chinese":"生態旅遊"},{"english":"be promoted as","chinese":"被宣傳為"},{"english":"a responsible way to travel","chinese":"負責任的旅遊方式"},{"english":"enter remote areas","chinese":"進入偏遠地區"},{"english":"place serious pressure on","chinese":"對……造成嚴重壓力"},{"english":"local cultures and communities","chinese":"本地文化和社區"},{"english":"cultural and social problems","chinese":"文化和社會問題"},{"english":"may result from","chinese":"可能由……引起"},{"english":"practical measures","chinese":"實際措施"},{"english":"local people and their traditions","chinese":"本地居民及其傳統"},{"english":"one major problem","chinese":"一個主要問題"},{"english":"local culture","chinese":"本地文化"},{"english":"be commercialised","chinese":"被商業化"},{"english":"be willing to pay for","chinese":"願意付錢購買"},{"english":"authentic experiences","chinese":"原汁原味的體驗"},{"english":"traditional ceremonies","chinese":"傳統儀式"},{"english":"religious practices","chinese":"宗教習俗"},{"english":"gradually be turned into","chinese":"逐漸被變成"},{"english":"performances","chinese":"表演"},{"english":"as a result","chinese":"因此"},{"english":"customs","chinese":"習俗"},{"english":"deep spiritual or social meaning","chinese":"深層的精神或社會意義"},{"english":"become little more than","chinese":"變得只不過是"},{"english":"tourist attractions","chinese":"旅遊景點；遊客賣點"},{"english":"weaken local identity","chinese":"削弱本地身份認同"},{"english":"especially among younger people","chinese":"尤其在年輕人之中"},{"english":"start to see","chinese":"開始視為"},{"english":"their own culture","chinese":"他們自己的文化"},{"english":"something to sell rather than something to preserve","chinese":"可出售的東西，而不是要保育的東西"},{"english":"remote communities","chinese":"偏遠社區"},{"english":"be disrupted by","chinese":"被……擾亂"},{"english":"sudden outside influence","chinese":"突然的外來影響"},{"english":"bring different values","chinese":"帶來不同價值觀"},{"english":"spending habits","chinese":"消費習慣"},{"english":"expectations","chinese":"期望"},{"english":"change local behaviour","chinese":"改變本地人的行為"},{"english":"increase tension between","chinese":"增加……之間的緊張關係"},{"english":"residents and visitors","chinese":"居民和遊客"},{"english":"in some cases","chinese":"在某些情況下"},{"english":"prices for food, land, and services","chinese":"食物、土地和服務的價格"},{"english":"making everyday life harder for","chinese":"令……的日常生活更困難"},{"english":"local families","chinese":"本地家庭"},{"english":"several measures can be taken","chinese":"可以採取幾項措施"},{"english":"reduce these problems","chinese":"減少這些問題"},{"english":"be controlled by","chinese":"由……控制"},{"english":"rather than outside companies","chinese":"而不是由外來公司"},{"english":"local leaders","chinese":"本地領袖"},{"english":"decide how many tourists may visit","chinese":"決定可以有多少遊客到訪"},{"english":"open to outsiders","chinese":"向外來人士開放"},{"english":"cultural practices","chinese":"文化習俗"},{"english":"remain private","chinese":"保持私人；不對外公開"},{"english":"allow communities to benefit from","chinese":"讓社區從……受惠"},{"english":"without losing control of","chinese":"而不會失去對……的控制"},{"english":"their way of life","chinese":"他們的生活方式"},{"english":"tourism operators","chinese":"旅遊營辦商"},{"english":"introduce clear rules for","chinese":"為……引入清晰規則"},{"english":"be educated about","chinese":"接受有關……的教育"},{"english":"local customs","chinese":"本地習俗"},{"english":"dress codes","chinese":"衣着規定"},{"english":"sacred sites","chinese":"神聖地點"},{"english":"acceptable behaviour","chinese":"可接受的行為"},{"english":"visitor numbers","chinese":"遊客人數"},{"english":"be limited","chinese":"被限制"},{"english":"part of the income from","chinese":"來自……的部分收入"},{"english":"support local schools","chinese":"支援本地學校"},{"english":"cultural centres","chinese":"文化中心"},{"english":"healthcare","chinese":"醫療服務"},{"english":"environmental protection","chinese":"環境保護"},{"english":"damage remote communities","chinese":"損害偏遠社區"},{"english":"commercialising culture","chinese":"將文化商業化"},{"english":"disturbing local life","chinese":"擾亂本地生活"},{"english":"community control","chinese":"社區主導"},{"english":"visitor education","chinese":"遊客教育"},{"english":"careful regulation","chinese":"審慎規管"},{"english":"while still allowing","chinese":"同時仍然容許"},{"english":"bring economic benefits","chinese":"帶來經濟利益"}]},"model-essay-15-ielts-direct-question":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-15-ielts-direct-question","essayKey":"direct-question:15","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-15-ielts-direct-question","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/direct-question/EdmundBd9Dir-Q15","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"In several secondary schools, students are expected to take part in community service, including supporting elderly people or those with disabilities. I believe this benefits young people by developing empathy and practical maturity, and it should definitely be included in the school curriculum.","chinese":"在一些中學裡，學生被要求參與社區服務，包括支援長者或殘疾人士。 我認為這能透過培養同理心和實際成熟度來令年輕人受益，而且它絕對應該被納入學校課程之中。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"The clearest benefit is that community work helps students become more compassionate and socially aware. Many teenagers spend most of their time with people of a similar age, so their understanding of hardship can remain quite limited. When they assist an elderly person with daily tasks or spend time with someone who has a disability, they begin to see that vulnerability is not an abstract idea but a real part of human life. This experience can teach patience, respect, and responsibility far more effectively than a lecture in a classroom. For example, a student who helps an elderly resident use a phone or carry groceries may realise how small acts of kindness can make another person’s day easier. In this way, community service can turn moral values from empty words into lived experience.","chinese":"最明顯的好處是，社區服務能幫助學生變得更有同情心，也更具社會意識。 許多青少年大部分時間都和年齡相近的人相處，因此他們對困難處境的理解可能仍然相當有限。 當他們協助長者處理日常事務，或與殘疾人士共度時間時，他們便開始明白，脆弱並不是一個抽象概念，而是人類生活中真實存在的一部分。 這種經歷比課堂上的講授更能有效地教會學生耐性、尊重和責任感。 例如，一名學生如果幫助一位年長居民使用電話或提購物袋，可能會意識到小小的善意行為如何能令另一個人的一天變得更容易。 透過這種方式，社區服務可以把道德價值從空洞的說話轉化為真實的生活經驗。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"I also think this should be a formal part of the curriculum because schools should educate character as well as academic ability. If community work is left entirely to personal choice, only students who are already motivated may participate, while others may miss an important opportunity to grow. Making it part of school life ensures that every student is exposed to people beyond their usual social circle. It can also make education more balanced, since young people learn not only how to pass exams but also how to contribute to society. As long as the work is age-appropriate and properly supervised, it can become a meaningful stepping stone towards responsible adulthood.","chinese":"我也認為這應該成為正式課程的一部分，因為學校不僅應該培養學術能力，也應該培養品格。 如果社區服務完全由個人選擇決定，可能只有本身已有動力的學生會參與，而其他學生則可能錯過一個重要的成長機會。 把它納入學校生活之中，能確保每一位學生都接觸到自己平常社交圈以外的人。 它也能使教育更加平衡，因為年輕人學到的不只是如何通過考試，也包括如何為社會作出貢獻。 只要這些工作適合學生年齡，並且受到適當監督，它便可以成為邁向負責任成年階段的一塊有意義的踏腳石。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, community work benefits students by building empathy, maturity, and social responsibility. For this reason, I strongly believe it should be a required part of the high school curriculum.","chinese":"總結來說，社區服務透過建立同理心、成熟度和社會責任感來令學生受益。 基於這個原因，我強烈認為它應該成為高中課程中的必修部分。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"secondary schools","chinese":"中學"},{"english":"be expected to","chinese":"被期望；應該"},{"english":"take part in","chinese":"參與"},{"english":"community service","chinese":"社區服務"},{"english":"supporting elderly people","chinese":"支援長者"},{"english":"those with disabilities","chinese":"殘疾人士"},{"english":"benefit young people by","chinese":"透過……令年輕人受惠"},{"english":"developing empathy","chinese":"培養同理心"},{"english":"practical maturity","chinese":"實際處事上的成熟"},{"english":"be included in","chinese":"被納入……"},{"english":"the school curriculum","chinese":"學校課程"},{"english":"the clearest benefit","chinese":"最明顯的好處"},{"english":"community work","chinese":"社區工作"},{"english":"helps students become","chinese":"幫助學生成為；幫助學生變得"},{"english":"compassionate","chinese":"有同情心的"},{"english":"socially aware","chinese":"有社會意識的"},{"english":"people of a similar age","chinese":"年齡相近的人"},{"english":"understanding of hardship","chinese":"對困難處境的理解"},{"english":"remain quite limited","chinese":"仍然相當有限"},{"english":"assist an elderly person with","chinese":"協助長者處理……"},{"english":"daily tasks","chinese":"日常事務"},{"english":"spend time with","chinese":"花時間陪伴"},{"english":"someone who has a disability","chinese":"有殘疾的人"},{"english":"begin to see that","chinese":"開始明白"},{"english":"vulnerability","chinese":"脆弱；弱勢處境"},{"english":"an abstract idea","chinese":"抽象概念"},{"english":"a real part of human life","chinese":"人類生活中真實的一部分"},{"english":"teach patience, respect, and responsibility","chinese":"教會耐性、尊重和責任感"},{"english":"far more effectively than","chinese":"比……有效得多"},{"english":"a lecture in a classroom","chinese":"課室裏的一堂講課"},{"english":"an elderly resident","chinese":"年長居民"},{"english":"carry groceries","chinese":"拿雜貨；拿日用品"},{"english":"small acts of kindness","chinese":"小小的善舉"},{"english":"make another person's day easier","chinese":"令別人的一天輕鬆一點"},{"english":"in this way","chinese":"這樣一來"},{"english":"turn moral values from empty words into lived experience","chinese":"將道德價值由空話變成親身體驗"},{"english":"empty words","chinese":"空話"},{"english":"lived experience","chinese":"親身經歷；生活體驗"},{"english":"a formal part of","chinese":"……的正式部分"},{"english":"educate character","chinese":"培養品格"},{"english":"as well as academic ability","chinese":"以及學業能力"},{"english":"be left entirely to","chinese":"完全交由……決定；完全交給……負責"},{"english":"personal choice","chinese":"個人選擇"},{"english":"already motivated","chinese":"本身已有動力的"},{"english":"miss an important opportunity to grow","chinese":"錯過重要的成長機會"},{"english":"making it part of school life","chinese":"將它變成學校生活的一部分"},{"english":"ensures that","chinese":"確保"},{"english":"be exposed to","chinese":"接觸到"},{"english":"beyond their usual social circle","chinese":"在平常社交圈子以外"},{"english":"make education more balanced","chinese":"令教育更均衡"},{"english":"pass exams","chinese":"通過考試"},{"english":"contribute to society","chinese":"貢獻社會"},{"english":"as long as","chinese":"只要"},{"english":"age-appropriate","chinese":"適合年齡的"},{"english":"properly supervised","chinese":"得到適當監督"},{"english":"a meaningful stepping stone towards","chinese":"邁向……的有意義踏腳石"},{"english":"responsible adulthood","chinese":"負責任的成年階段"},{"english":"social responsibility","chinese":"社會責任感"},{"english":"a required part of","chinese":"……的必修部分"},{"english":"the high school curriculum","chinese":"高中課程"}]},"model-essay-15-ielts-discuss-both-views":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-15-ielts-discuss-both-views","essayKey":"discuss-both-views:15","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-15-ielts-discuss-both-views","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/discuss-both-views-your-opinion/EdmundBd9ExpBth-Q15","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"In an increasingly connected world, the ability to speak a foreign language has become a valuable educational asset. While some people believe that pupils should first study another language in secondary school, I firmly believe that language learning should begin at primary school.","chinese":"在一個日益互聯的世界中，能夠說一門外語已成為一項有價值的教育資產。 雖然有些人認為學生應該在中學才開始學習另一種語言， 我堅定地認為，語言學習應該從小學開始。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"Those who support a later start often argue that secondary school students are more mature. At that age, learners can understand grammar rules, sentence patterns and abstract vocabulary more consciously, so teachers may be able to explain the language in a systematic way. Older students may also have clearer academic goals, such as preparing for examinations or future employment. For example, a teenager who knows that English, French or Mandarin could improve career prospects may study with stronger discipline. From this perspective, secondary school can seem like a more efficient stage for serious language instruction.","chinese":"支持較遲開始的人通常認為，中學生更加成熟。 在那個年齡，學習者能夠更有意識地理解文法規則、句子結構和抽象詞彙，因此老師也許能夠以更有系統的方式解釋語言。 年紀較大的學生也可能有更清晰的學業目標，例如準備考試或未來就業。 例如，一個知道英語、法語或普通話能改善職業前景的青少年，可能會以更強的自律性去學習。 從這個角度來看，中學似乎可以是一個更有效率地進行認真語言教學的階段。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"However, the stronger argument is that primary school children are usually in a better position to build natural language habits. Young learners tend to absorb pronunciation, rhythm and basic expressions more easily because they are less self-conscious and more willing to imitate sounds. If a child regularly sings songs, plays language games and hears simple classroom instructions in another language, that language gradually becomes familiar rather than frightening. This early confidence matters because language learning is not mastered overnight; it grows through repeated exposure, mistakes and correction. A student who has met a foreign language from the age of six is therefore far less likely to see it as a wall to climb when it becomes more demanding in secondary school.","chinese":"然而，更有力的論點是，小學生通常處於更有利的位置去建立自然的語言習慣。 年幼的學習者往往更容易吸收發音、節奏和基本表達，因為他們較少感到自我意識過強，也更願意模仿聲音。 如果一個孩子經常唱歌、玩語言遊戲，並聽到另一種語言的簡單課堂指示，那種語言便會逐漸變得熟悉，而不是令人害怕。 這種早期信心十分重要，因為語言學習並不是一夜之間就能掌握的；它是透過反覆接觸、犯錯和改正慢慢成長的。 因此，一個從六歲起便接觸外語的學生，在中學階段語言學習變得更具要求時，便遠較不可能把它視為一道難以攀越的高牆。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, although secondary school students may study languages more deliberately, primary school is the better starting point. Early exposure builds confidence, natural habits and steady progress, making foreign-language learning far more effective.","chinese":"總結來說，儘管中學生可能會更有意識地學習語言，小學仍然是更好的起點。 早期接觸能建立信心、自然習慣和穩定進步，從而使外語學習有效得多。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"in an increasingly connected world","chinese":"在一個聯繫日益緊密的世界"},{"english":"the ability to speak","chinese":"說……的能力"},{"english":"a foreign language","chinese":"外語"},{"english":"a valuable educational asset","chinese":"寶貴的教育資產"},{"english":"pupils","chinese":"小學生；學生"},{"english":"first study another language","chinese":"首先學習另一種語言"},{"english":"firmly believe that","chinese":"堅信"},{"english":"language learning","chinese":"語言學習"},{"english":"begin at primary school","chinese":"在小學開始"},{"english":"those who support","chinese":"支持……的人"},{"english":"a later start","chinese":"較遲開始"},{"english":"secondary school students","chinese":"中學生"},{"english":"more mature","chinese":"較成熟"},{"english":"at that age","chinese":"在那個年紀"},{"english":"grammar rules","chinese":"文法規則"},{"english":"sentence patterns","chinese":"句式"},{"english":"abstract vocabulary","chinese":"抽象詞彙"},{"english":"more consciously","chinese":"更有意識地"},{"english":"in a systematic way","chinese":"以有系統的方式"},{"english":"clearer academic goals","chinese":"更清晰的學業目標"},{"english":"preparing for examinations","chinese":"準備考試"},{"english":"future employment","chinese":"未來就業"},{"english":"improve career prospects","chinese":"改善事業前景"},{"english":"study with stronger discipline","chinese":"以更強自律學習"},{"english":"from this perspective","chinese":"從這個角度來看"},{"english":"a more efficient stage","chinese":"更有效率的階段"},{"english":"serious language instruction","chinese":"認真的語言教學"},{"english":"the stronger argument","chinese":"更有力的論點"},{"english":"be in a better position to","chinese":"更有條件去"},{"english":"build natural language habits","chinese":"建立自然的語言習慣"},{"english":"young learners","chinese":"年幼學習者"},{"english":"tend to","chinese":"往往會"},{"english":"absorb pronunciation","chinese":"吸收發音"},{"english":"rhythm and basic expressions","chinese":"節奏和基本表達"},{"english":"less self-conscious","chinese":"較少自我意識；較不怕尷尬"},{"english":"more willing to imitate","chinese":"更願意模仿"},{"english":"imitate sounds","chinese":"模仿聲音"},{"english":"regularly sings songs","chinese":"定期唱歌"},{"english":"language games","chinese":"語言遊戲"},{"english":"classroom instructions","chinese":"課堂指示"},{"english":"gradually becomes familiar","chinese":"逐漸變得熟悉"},{"english":"rather than frightening","chinese":"而不是令人害怕"},{"english":"early confidence","chinese":"早期信心"},{"english":"is not mastered overnight","chinese":"不是一夜之間掌握"},{"english":"repeated exposure","chinese":"反覆接觸"},{"english":"mistakes and correction","chinese":"錯誤和糾正"},{"english":"from the age of six","chinese":"從六歲起"},{"english":"far less likely to","chinese":"遠遠較不可能"},{"english":"see it as a wall to climb","chinese":"將它視為一道要攀過的牆"},{"english":"becomes more demanding","chinese":"變得要求更高"},{"english":"in secondary school","chinese":"在中學"},{"english":"study languages more deliberately","chinese":"更有意識地學習語言"},{"english":"the better starting point","chinese":"更好的起點"},{"english":"early exposure","chinese":"早期接觸"},{"english":"build confidence","chinese":"建立信心"},{"english":"natural habits","chinese":"自然習慣"},{"english":"steady progress","chinese":"穩定進步"},{"english":"making foreign-language learning far more effective","chinese":"令外語學習有效得多"}]},"model-essay-15-ielts-opinion":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-15-ielts-opinion","essayKey":"opinion:15","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-15-ielts-opinion","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/opinions/EdmundBd9OP-Q15","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"The ability to speak persuasively in public is often regarded as a key ingredient of success. I completely agree that oratory skills are essential, because success rarely depends only on what people know; it also depends on how convincingly they can express, defend, and share that knowledge.","chinese":"在公共場合具說服力地表達的能力，通常被視為成功的一個關鍵要素。 我完全同意演說能力是必不可少的，因為成功很少只取決於人們知道甚麼；它也取決於他們能多有說服力地表達、捍衛和分享那些知識。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"First, strong speaking skills allow people to make their ideas visible. In the workplace, many capable employees remain overlooked not because their work lacks value, but because they cannot explain it clearly to colleagues, clients, or managers. By contrast, a person who can present an argument in an organised and engaging way is more likely to win trust, secure promotion, and lead others. For example, an engineer may design an excellent product, but if she cannot explain its benefits to investors or customers, the idea may never leave the meeting room. In this sense, public speaking turns private ability into public influence, which is central to professional success.","chinese":"首先，強大的表達能力使人們能夠讓自己的想法被看見。 在職場中，許多有能力的員工仍然被忽視，並不是因為他們的工作缺乏價值，而是因為他們無法向同事、客戶或管理層清楚解釋自己的工作。 相比之下，一個能夠以有條理且吸引人的方式提出論點的人，更有可能贏得信任、獲得晉升，並領導他人。 例如，一位工程師可能設計出一件出色的產品，但如果她無法向投資者或客戶解釋其好處，這個想法可能永遠無法離開會議室。 從這個意義上說，公開演說把個人的能力轉化為公共影響力，而這正是職業成功的核心"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"Moreover, oratory skills are essential because success often requires cooperation. Leaders, teachers, entrepreneurs, and community organisers all need to encourage, negotiate, calm, and inspire others. When people speak with confidence and sensitivity, they can reduce misunderstandings and bring others onto the same page. A manager who gives clear instructions and motivates a team during a crisis will achieve more than one who has technical expertise but communicates poorly. Similarly, students who can ask questions, defend opinions, and participate in discussions develop a confidence that later opens doors in both study and work. Effective speech, therefore, does not merely decorate ability; it releases it.","chinese":"此外，演說能力之所以重要，是因為成功往往需要合作。 領袖、教師、企業家和社區組織者都需要鼓勵、協商、安撫和激勵他人。 當人們能夠自信而敏銳地說話時，他們便能減少誤解，並讓其他人達成共識。 一位在危機中能給出清晰指示並激勵團隊的管理者，會比一位擁有技術專長但溝通能力差的管理者取得更多成就。 同樣地，能夠提出問題、捍衛觀點並參與討論的學生，會培養出一種自信，而這種自信日後會在學習和工作中為他們打開機會之門。 因此，有效的表達並不只是為能力作裝飾；它能真正釋放能力。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, I completely agree that oratory skills are essential for success. They help people present their abilities clearly, persuade others effectively, and build the relationships through which achievement usually happens.","chinese":"總結來說，我完全同意演說能力對成功是必不可少的。 它們幫助人們清楚展示自己的能力、有效說服他人，並建立那些通常使成就得以發生的人際關係。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"the ability to","chinese":"……的能力"},{"english":"speak persuasively in public","chinese":"在公開場合有說服力地發言"},{"english":"be regarded as","chinese":"被視為"},{"english":"a key ingredient of success","chinese":"成功的關鍵因素"},{"english":"I completely agree that","chinese":"我完全同意"},{"english":"oratory skills","chinese":"演說技巧"},{"english":"depend only on","chinese":"只取決於"},{"english":"express, defend, and share","chinese":"表達、捍衛和分享"},{"english":"make their ideas visible","chinese":"令自己的想法被看見"},{"english":"in the workplace","chinese":"在職場上"},{"english":"capable employees","chinese":"有能力的員工"},{"english":"remain overlooked","chinese":"仍然被忽視"},{"english":"lack value","chinese":"缺乏價值"},{"english":"explain it clearly to","chinese":"向……清楚解釋"},{"english":"by contrast","chinese":"相反"},{"english":"present an argument","chinese":"提出論點"},{"english":"in an organised and engaging way","chinese":"以有條理而吸引人的方式"},{"english":"win trust","chinese":"贏得信任"},{"english":"secure promotion","chinese":"獲得晉升"},{"english":"lead others","chinese":"領導他人"},{"english":"design an excellent product","chinese":"設計一件出色產品"},{"english":"explain its benefits to","chinese":"向……解釋其好處"},{"english":"investors or customers","chinese":"投資者或顧客"},{"english":"leave the meeting room","chinese":"走出會議室；得到實行"},{"english":"in this sense","chinese":"從這個意義上說"},{"english":"turn private ability into public influence","chinese":"將個人能力轉化為公眾影響力"},{"english":"be central to","chinese":"對……至關重要"},{"english":"professional success","chinese":"事業上的成功"},{"english":"moreover","chinese":"此外"},{"english":"require cooperation","chinese":"需要合作"},{"english":"community organisers","chinese":"社區組織者"},{"english":"encourage, negotiate, calm, and inspire","chinese":"鼓勵、協商、安撫和激勵"},{"english":"speak with confidence and sensitivity","chinese":"自信而體貼地說話"},{"english":"reduce misunderstandings","chinese":"減少誤解"},{"english":"bring others onto the same page","chinese":"令其他人達成共識"},{"english":"give clear instructions","chinese":"給予清晰指示"},{"english":"motivate a team","chinese":"激勵團隊"},{"english":"during a crisis","chinese":"在危機期間"},{"english":"technical expertise","chinese":"專業技術知識"},{"english":"communicate poorly","chinese":"溝通不善"},{"english":"ask questions","chinese":"提問"},{"english":"defend opinions","chinese":"捍衛意見"},{"english":"participate in discussions","chinese":"參與討論"},{"english":"open doors","chinese":"帶來機會"},{"english":"in both study and work","chinese":"在學業和工作兩方面"},{"english":"effective speech","chinese":"有效表達"},{"english":"does not merely decorate ability","chinese":"不只是為能力加上裝飾"},{"english":"release ability","chinese":"釋放能力；發揮能力"},{"english":"in conclusion","chinese":"總括而言"},{"english":"present their abilities clearly","chinese":"清楚展示自己的能力"},{"english":"persuade others effectively","chinese":"有效說服他人"},{"english":"build the relationships through which","chinese":"建立令……得以實現的人際關係"},{"english":"achievement usually happens","chinese":"成就通常得以實現"}]},"model-essay-16-ielts-advantage-disadvantage":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-16-ielts-advantage-disadvantage","essayKey":"advantage-disadvantage:16","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-16-ielts-advantage-disadvantage","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/advantage-and-disadvantage/EdmundBd9AdDisAd-Q16","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"In contemporary society, people are exposed to commercial messages almost constantly, whether on their phones, in print, or across city streets. This advertising-driven culture of consumerism can stimulate economic activity and encourage product improvement; however, I believe its overall impact is negative because it promotes wasteful spending and accelerates environmental damage.","chinese":"在當代社會中，人們幾乎時刻都暴露在商業訊息之下，無論是在手機上、印刷媒體中，還是在城市街道上。 這種由廣告推動的消費主義文化，的確能刺激經濟活動，並促使產品改善；然而， 我認為它的整體影響是負面的，因為它助長浪費性的消費，並加速環境破壞。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"Admittedly, consumerism can produce genuine benefits for the economy. To begin with, strong demand for goods keeps companies profitable and allows them to employ people across manufacturing, retail, logistics, and marketing. When a heavily advertised product sells well, the resulting income supports an entire chain of jobs rather than a single business. In turn, governments may collect more tax revenue, which can be used to fund public services. In addition, the need to attract customers often forces companies to improve what they sell. Since businesses must persuade consumers that a new item is worth buying, they tend to enhance quality, convenience, and efficiency. The smartphone industry illustrates this clearly, as intense competition has led to better batteries, stronger security systems, and more reliable cameras.","chinese":"誠然，消費主義的確能為經濟帶來真實的好處。 首先，對商品的強勁需求能使企業維持盈利，並讓它們在製造、零售、物流和市場推廣等領域提供就業機會。 當一項被大力宣傳的產品銷售表現良好時，由此產生的收入所支撐的並不只是單一企業，而是整條就業鏈。進一步來說，政府亦可因此獲得更多稅收，並將這些資金用於公共服務。 例如，一項被廣泛宣傳的消費產品若大賣，不但能為店舖員工帶來工作，也能同時帶動工廠工人、運輸司機以及廣告公司的就業。 此外，為了吸引顧客，企業往往不得不改良自己所出售的產品。 由於企業必須說服消費者某項新產品值得購買，它們通常會提升產品的品質、便利性和效率。 智能手機產業便清楚說明了這一點，因為激烈的競爭已促使電池更耐用、保安系統更強，以及相機功能更可靠。 因此，消費主義確實能促進經濟增長，並推動產品創新。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"Even so, the negative effects are more serious. The first is financial harm at the individual level. By repeatedly presenting non-essential items as symbols of success or happiness, advertising can blur the distinction between wants and needs. As a result, many people buy impulsively, reduce their savings, or rely on credit to purchase goods that add little real value to their lives. A young worker who frequently upgrades perfectly functional devices simply to follow trends, for example, may create unnecessary financial pressure. The second drawback is environmental. Consumerism depends on continual production, packaging, transport, and replacement, all of which consume energy and raw materials. Moreover, many cheap clothes and electronic products are discarded long before the end of their useful life, increasing landfill waste and pollution. For this reason, a culture of constant purchasing places a heavy burden on the planet.","chinese":"即便如此，消費主義所帶來的負面影響更加嚴重。 第一個問題，是它會在個人層面造成財務上的損害。 廣告一再把非必要物品包裝成成功或幸福的象徵，便會模糊「想要」與「需要」之間的界線。結果，很多人會衝動購物、減少儲蓄，甚至依賴借貸去購買一些對生活其實沒有太大實際價值的商品。 例如，一名年輕上班族若只是為了追趕潮流，便頻繁更換仍然運作良好的電子產品，便可能為自己帶來不必要的財務壓力。 第二個缺點則與環境有關。 消費主義依賴持續不斷的生產、包裝、運輸和替換，而這些過程全都會消耗能源和原材料。此外，許多廉價衣物和電子產品在尚未真正用盡之前便被丟棄，從而增加堆填區廢物及污染。 因此，這種不斷購買的文化，對地球造成了沉重的負擔。 因此，消費主義不但鼓勵不必要的消費，亦加劇了環境惡化。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, although consumerism can create employment and drive innovation, its disadvantages are ultimately more significant. Because it encourages needless expenditure and deepens environmental degradation, it is, on balance, a harmful social trend.","chinese":"總括而言，雖然消費主義能創造就業並推動創新，但它的缺點始終更為重大。 因為它助長不必要的開支，並加深環境破壞，所以整體來說，它是一種有害的社會趨勢"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"contemporary society","chinese":"當代社會"},{"english":"be exposed to","chinese":"接觸到"},{"english":"commercial messages","chinese":"商業訊息"},{"english":"almost constantly","chinese":"幾乎不斷地"},{"english":"whether on their phones, in print, or across city streets","chinese":"無論在手機上、印刷品中，還是在城市街道各處"},{"english":"advertising-driven culture","chinese":"由廣告推動的文化"},{"english":"consumerism","chinese":"消費主義"},{"english":"stimulate economic activity","chinese":"刺激經濟活動"},{"english":"encourage product improvement","chinese":"鼓勵產品改良"},{"english":"overall impact","chinese":"整體影響"},{"english":"promote wasteful spending","chinese":"鼓吹浪費性消費"},{"english":"accelerate environmental damage","chinese":"加速環境破壞"},{"english":"admittedly","chinese":"誠然"},{"english":"genuine benefits","chinese":"真正的好處"},{"english":"to begin with","chinese":"首先"},{"english":"strong demand for goods","chinese":"對商品的強勁需求"},{"english":"keeps companies profitable","chinese":"令公司保持盈利"},{"english":"employ people across","chinese":"在……各範疇聘用人手"},{"english":"manufacturing","chinese":"製造業"},{"english":"retail","chinese":"零售業"},{"english":"logistics","chinese":"物流業"},{"english":"a heavily advertised product","chinese":"大量宣傳的產品"},{"english":"sells well","chinese":"銷量好"},{"english":"the resulting income","chinese":"隨之而來的收入"},{"english":"an entire chain of jobs","chinese":"整條就業鏈"},{"english":"rather than a single business","chinese":"而不是單一企業"},{"english":"in turn","chinese":"繼而"},{"english":"collect more tax revenue","chinese":"收取更多稅收"},{"english":"fund public services","chinese":"資助公共服務"},{"english":"in addition","chinese":"此外"},{"english":"attract customers","chinese":"吸引顧客"},{"english":"forces companies to","chinese":"迫使公司去"},{"english":"persuade consumers that","chinese":"說服消費者"},{"english":"worth buying","chinese":"值得購買"},{"english":"tend to enhance","chinese":"往往會提升"},{"english":"quality, convenience, and efficiency","chinese":"質素、便利性和效率"},{"english":"illustrates this clearly","chinese":"清楚說明這一點"},{"english":"intense competition","chinese":"激烈競爭"},{"english":"has led to","chinese":"導致；帶來"},{"english":"stronger security systems","chinese":"更強的保安系統"},{"english":"more reliable cameras","chinese":"更可靠的相機"},{"english":"even so","chinese":"即使如此"},{"english":"negative effects","chinese":"負面影響"},{"english":"financial harm","chinese":"財務損害"},{"english":"at the individual level","chinese":"在個人層面"},{"english":"repeatedly presenting","chinese":"反覆呈現"},{"english":"non-essential items","chinese":"非必需品"},{"english":"symbols of success or happiness","chinese":"成功或快樂的象徵"},{"english":"blur the distinction between","chinese":"模糊……之間的區別"},{"english":"wants and needs","chinese":"想要的東西和需要的東西"},{"english":"as a result","chinese":"因此"},{"english":"buy impulsively","chinese":"衝動購物"},{"english":"reduce their savings","chinese":"減少儲蓄"},{"english":"rely on credit","chinese":"依賴信用貸款"},{"english":"add little real value to","chinese":"對……幾乎沒有真正價值"},{"english":"frequently upgrades","chinese":"經常升級"},{"english":"perfectly functional devices","chinese":"完全能正常使用的裝置"},{"english":"follow trends","chinese":"跟隨潮流"},{"english":"create unnecessary financial pressure","chinese":"造成不必要的財務壓力"},{"english":"the second drawback","chinese":"第二個缺點"},{"english":"continual production","chinese":"持續生產"},{"english":"packaging","chinese":"包裝"},{"english":"replacement","chinese":"替換"},{"english":"consume energy and raw materials","chinese":"消耗能源和原材料"},{"english":"moreover","chinese":"此外"},{"english":"cheap clothes and electronic products","chinese":"廉價衣服和電子產品"},{"english":"be discarded","chinese":"被棄置"},{"english":"long before the end of their useful life","chinese":"遠在其使用壽命結束之前"},{"english":"increasing landfill waste","chinese":"增加堆填區廢物"},{"english":"pollution","chinese":"污染"},{"english":"a culture of constant purchasing","chinese":"不斷購買的文化"},{"english":"places a heavy burden on","chinese":"對……造成沉重負擔"},{"english":"the planet","chinese":"地球"},{"english":"create employment","chinese":"創造就業"},{"english":"drive innovation","chinese":"推動創新"},{"english":"ultimately more significant","chinese":"最終更重要"},{"english":"needless expenditure","chinese":"不必要開支"},{"english":"deepens environmental degradation","chinese":"加劇環境惡化"},{"english":"on balance","chinese":"總體而言"},{"english":"a harmful social trend","chinese":"有害的社會趨勢"}]},"model-essay-16-ielts-cause-solution":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-16-ielts-cause-solution","essayKey":"cause-solution:16","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-16-ielts-cause-solution","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/problem-and-cause/EdmundBd9CnS-Q16","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"In many cities and towns, roads are carrying more vehicles than they can reasonably absorb. This problem is mainly caused by car-centred planning and weak alternatives to private transport. It can be addressed by improving public transport, managing road use more carefully and making short local journeys easier without a car.","chinese":"在許多城市和城鎮中，道路正承載著超出其合理容納範圍的車輛數量。 這個問題主要是由以汽車為中心的城市規劃，以及私人交通工具以外的替代選擇不足所造成的。 這個問題可以透過改善公共交通、更審慎地管理道路使用，以及讓人們在不使用汽車的情況下更容易完成短途本地出行來解決。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"One important cause is that many urban areas have been built around driving. When homes, workplaces, schools and shops are spread across wide distances, ordinary routines almost force people onto the road. A parent, for example, may need to drive to a school, an office and a supermarket in one morning, turning one household into several car trips. A second cause is the poor quality of public transport. If buses are slow, trains are overcrowded, or services do not connect well with residential areas, people will naturally see driving as the only practical choice. In that situation, each driver tries to save time, but everyone ends up losing time in congestion.","chinese":"其中一個重要原因是，許多城市地區都是圍繞駕車而建設的。 當住宅、工作場所、學校和商店分散在很遠的距離之間時，日常生活的安排幾乎會迫使人們上路開車。 例如，一位家長可能需要在一個早上開車前往學校、辦公室和超級市場，結果一個家庭便產生了數次汽車出行。 第二個原因是公共交通的質素欠佳。 如果巴士速度緩慢、火車過度擁擠，或者交通服務與住宅區連接不佳，人們自然會把駕車視為唯一實際可行的選擇。 在這種情況下，每位司機都試圖節省時間，但最後所有人都在交通擠塞中浪費了時間。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"The first solution is to make public transport genuinely convenient. Governments should invest in frequent buses, reliable rail services and simple ticketing systems, so that using a bus or train feels less like a sacrifice and more like common sense. For instance, a worker who can cross a city quickly with one affordable ticket is far less likely to drive. In addition, local authorities should manage car use through congestion charges, limited parking and bus lanes. Cities should also build safe walking and cycling routes, especially for short trips. These measures reduce unnecessary traffic without banning cars completely, leaving road space for essential journeys, deliveries and emergency vehicles.","chinese":"第一個解決方法是讓公共交通真正變得方便。 政府應投資於班次頻密的巴士、可靠的鐵路服務和簡單的票務系統，使乘搭巴士或火車感覺上不再像是一種犧牲，而更像是理所當然的選擇。 例如，如果一名上班族能夠用一張價格合理的車票快速穿越城市，他開車的可能性便會大大降低。 此外，地方政府應透過擁堵收費、限制泊車位和設置巴士專線來管理汽車使用。 城市亦應建設安全的步行和單車路線，尤其是為短途出行而設。 這些措施能在不完全禁止汽車的情況下減少不必要的交通流量，從而為必要出行、送貨車輛和緊急車輛騰出道路空間。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, heavy traffic is largely the result of car-dependent planning and unattractive transport alternatives. It can be reduced if cities improve public transport while encouraging people to make shorter and less essential journeys in other ways.","chinese":"總結來說，交通繁忙很大程度上是依賴汽車的城市規劃，以及缺乏吸引力的交通替代方案所造成的。 如果城市改善公共交通，同時鼓勵人們以其他方式完成較短和較不必要的出行，交通擠塞便可以得到減少。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"roads are carrying more vehicles than they can reasonably absorb","chinese":"道路承載的車輛超出可合理容納的程度"},{"english":"car-centred planning","chinese":"以汽車為中心的規劃"},{"english":"weak alternatives to private transport","chinese":"私人交通工具以外選擇不足"},{"english":"be addressed by","chinese":"可透過……處理；解決"},{"english":"improving public transport","chinese":"改善公共交通"},{"english":"managing road use more carefully","chinese":"更審慎地管理道路使用"},{"english":"short local journeys","chinese":"區內短途出行"},{"english":"without a car","chinese":"不用汽車"},{"english":"urban areas","chinese":"市區"},{"english":"built around driving","chinese":"圍繞駕駛而規劃"},{"english":"be spread across wide distances","chinese":"分散在很大範圍內"},{"english":"ordinary routines","chinese":"日常例行活動"},{"english":"force people onto the road","chinese":"迫使人們駕車上路"},{"english":"in one morning","chinese":"在一個早上內"},{"english":"turning one household into several car trips","chinese":"令一個家庭產生多次駕車行程"},{"english":"car trips","chinese":"駕車行程；汽車出行次數"},{"english":"the poor quality of public transport","chinese":"公共交通質素差"},{"english":"trains are overcrowded","chinese":"鐵路過於擠迫"},{"english":"connect well with residential areas","chinese":"與住宅區銜接良好"},{"english":"residential areas","chinese":"住宅區"},{"english":"see driving as the only practical choice","chinese":"視駕車為唯一實際可行的選擇"},{"english":"the only practical choice","chinese":"唯一實際可行的選擇"},{"english":"save time","chinese":"節省時間"},{"english":"end up losing time","chinese":"最終浪費時間"},{"english":"in congestion","chinese":"在交通擠塞中"},{"english":"make public transport genuinely convenient","chinese":"令公共交通真正方便"},{"english":"invest in","chinese":"投資於"},{"english":"frequent buses","chinese":"班次頻密的巴士"},{"english":"reliable rail services","chinese":"可靠的鐵路服務"},{"english":"simple ticketing systems","chinese":"簡單的票務系統"},{"english":"less like a sacrifice and more like common sense","chinese":"不像犧牲，而更像明智自然的選擇"},{"english":"cross a city quickly","chinese":"快速橫越一個城市"},{"english":"one affordable ticket","chinese":"一張負擔得起的車票"},{"english":"far less likely to drive","chinese":"駕車的機會大大降低"},{"english":"local authorities","chinese":"地方當局"},{"english":"manage car use through","chinese":"透過……管理汽車使用"},{"english":"congestion charges","chinese":"交通擠塞收費"},{"english":"limited parking","chinese":"限制泊車；有限泊車位"},{"english":"bus lanes","chinese":"巴士專線"},{"english":"safe walking and cycling routes","chinese":"安全的步行及單車路線"},{"english":"especially for short trips","chinese":"特別是短途出行"},{"english":"reduce unnecessary traffic","chinese":"減少不必要的交通流量"},{"english":"without banning cars completely","chinese":"無須完全禁止汽車"},{"english":"leaving road space for","chinese":"為……騰出道路空間"},{"english":"essential journeys","chinese":"必要行程"},{"english":"deliveries","chinese":"送貨"},{"english":"emergency vehicles","chinese":"緊急車輛"},{"english":"heavy traffic","chinese":"交通繁忙；嚴重交通擠塞"},{"english":"largely the result of","chinese":"很大程度上是……的結果"},{"english":"car-dependent planning","chinese":"依賴汽車的規劃"},{"english":"unattractive transport alternatives","chinese":"缺乏吸引力的交通替代選擇"},{"english":"encouraging people to","chinese":"鼓勵人們去"},{"english":"shorter and less essential journeys","chinese":"較短及非必要的行程"},{"english":"in other ways","chinese":"以其他方式"}]},"model-essay-16-ielts-direct-question":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-16-ielts-direct-question","essayKey":"direct-question:16","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-16-ielts-direct-question","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/direct-question/EdmundBd9Dir-Q16","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"Some people see teaching as the simple transfer of facts from an expert to a learner. I strongly disagree with this limited view. In my opinion, a teacher’s central role is to motivate and inspire students, because knowledge only becomes valuable when students are willing to engage with it, question it and use it beyond the classroom.","chinese":"有些人認為，教學只是把知識從專家傳遞給學習者。 我強烈不同意這種狹隘的看法。 在我看來，教師的核心角色是激勵和啟發學生，因為知識只有在學生願意投入其中、質疑它，並在課堂以外運用它時，才會真正變得有價值。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"The first reason is that motivation turns information into real learning. A teacher can deliver a perfectly accurate lesson, but if students are bored, passive or afraid of making mistakes, most of that knowledge will evaporate after the examination. By contrast, an inspiring teacher creates curiosity. Such a teacher does not merely tell students what happened in history or how a formula works; they help students see why it matters. For instance, a history teacher who connects past conflicts with modern ideas of justice may lead students to debate, challenge assumptions and remember the lesson more deeply. In this sense, inspiration is not decorative; it is the engine that keeps learning alive.","chinese":"第一個原因是，動機能把資訊轉化為真正的學習。 一位教師可以講授一堂完全準確的課，但如果學生感到沉悶、被動，或者害怕犯錯，那麼大部分知識在考試後都會逐漸消散。 相比之下，一位能啟發學生的教師會激發好奇心。 這樣的教師不只是告訴學生歷史上發生了甚麼，或者一條公式如何運作；他們會幫助學生明白為甚麼這些知識重要。 例如，一位把過去的衝突與現代正義觀念連繫起來的歷史老師，可能會引導學生辯論、挑戰既有假設，並更深刻地記住那堂課。 從這個意義上說，啟發並不是裝飾性的東西；它是讓學習持續運轉的引擎。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"Another reason is that teachers shape attitudes, confidence and habits that students carry into adulthood. Facts can now be found in books, videos and digital platforms, but a young person still needs guidance to develop discipline, resilience and intellectual courage. A teacher who motivates students can change how they see themselves as learners. For example, when a science teacher encourages a weak student after a failed experiment, the student may stop seeing failure as humiliation and start seeing it as part of discovery. That lesson is far more durable than a single chapter in a textbook.","chinese":"另一個原因是，教師會塑造學生帶入成年階段的態度、自信和習慣。 事實性知識現在可以在書本、影片和數碼平台上找到，但年輕人仍然需要引導，才能培養自律、韌性和intellectualcourage。 一位能激勵學生的教師，可以改變學生如何看待自己作為學習者的身份。 例如，當一位科學老師在一次實驗失敗後鼓勵一名能力較弱的學生時，這名學生可能會停止把失敗視為羞辱，並開始把它看成探索的一部分。 這一課比教科書中的單一章節更加持久。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, although teachers must explain knowledge clearly, their deeper role is to inspire students to care about learning. Information can be handed over, but confidence, curiosity and purpose have to be awakened.","chinese":"總結來說，雖然教師必須清楚解釋知識，但他們更深層的角色是啟發學生去重視學習。 資訊可以被傳遞，但自信、好奇心和目標感必須被喚醒"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"see teaching as","chinese":"將教學視為……"},{"english":"the simple transfer of facts","chinese":"簡單傳授知識"},{"english":"from an expert to a learner","chinese":"從專家到學習者"},{"english":"strongly disagree with","chinese":"強烈不同意……"},{"english":"this limited view","chinese":"這種狹隘看法"},{"english":"in my opinion","chinese":"在我看來；依我之見"},{"english":"a teacher's central role","chinese":"教師的核心角色"},{"english":"motivate and inspire","chinese":"激勵和啟發"},{"english":"becomes valuable when","chinese":"當……時才變得有價值"},{"english":"be willing to","chinese":"願意……"},{"english":"engage with","chinese":"投入；接觸並思考"},{"english":"question it","chinese":"質疑它"},{"english":"beyond the classroom","chinese":"在課室以外"},{"english":"turns information into real learning","chinese":"將資訊轉化為真正學習"},{"english":"deliver a lesson","chinese":"講授一堂課"},{"english":"a perfectly accurate lesson","chinese":"完全準確的一堂課"},{"english":"passive","chinese":"被動的"},{"english":"afraid of making mistakes","chinese":"害怕犯錯"},{"english":"most of that knowledge","chinese":"大部分知識"},{"english":"evaporate after the examination","chinese":"考試後消失"},{"english":"by contrast","chinese":"相比之下"},{"english":"an inspiring teacher","chinese":"有啟發性的教師"},{"english":"creates curiosity","chinese":"引發好奇心"},{"english":"does not merely","chinese":"不只是……"},{"english":"how a formula works","chinese":"公式如何運作"},{"english":"see why it matters","chinese":"明白它為何重要"},{"english":"past conflicts","chinese":"過去的衝突"},{"english":"modern ideas of justice","chinese":"現代的公義觀念"},{"english":"lead students to","chinese":"引導學生去……"},{"english":"challenge assumptions","chinese":"挑戰假設"},{"english":"remember the lesson more deeply","chinese":"更深刻地記住課堂內容"},{"english":"in this sense","chinese":"從這個意義上說"},{"english":"decorative","chinese":"裝飾性的；可有可無的"},{"english":"the engine that keeps learning alive","chinese":"令學習保持活力的引擎"},{"english":"shape attitudes","chinese":"塑造態度"},{"english":"carry into adulthood","chinese":"帶到成年階段"},{"english":"can now be found in","chinese":"現在可以在……找到"},{"english":"digital platforms","chinese":"數碼平台"},{"english":"guidance","chinese":"指導"},{"english":"develop discipline","chinese":"培養自律"},{"english":"resilience","chinese":"抗逆力"},{"english":"intellectual courage","chinese":"思想上的勇氣"},{"english":"change how they see themselves","chinese":"改變他們如何看待自己"},{"english":"see themselves as learners","chinese":"視自己為學習者"},{"english":"a weak student","chinese":"成績較弱的學生"},{"english":"a failed experiment","chinese":"失敗的實驗"},{"english":"stop seeing failure as","chinese":"不再將失敗視為……"},{"english":"humiliation","chinese":"羞辱"},{"english":"start seeing it as","chinese":"開始將它視為……"},{"english":"part of discovery","chinese":"探索過程的一部分"},{"english":"far more durable than","chinese":"比……持久得多"},{"english":"a single chapter in a textbook","chinese":"教科書中的單一章節"},{"english":"explain knowledge clearly","chinese":"清楚解釋知識"},{"english":"their deeper role","chinese":"他們更深層的角色"},{"english":"care about learning","chinese":"重視學習"},{"english":"be handed over","chinese":"被交付；被傳遞"},{"english":"confidence, curiosity and purpose","chinese":"信心、好奇心和目標感"},{"english":"have to be awakened","chinese":"必須被喚醒"}]},"model-essay-16-ielts-discuss-both-views":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-16-ielts-discuss-both-views","essayKey":"discuss-both-views:16","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-16-ielts-discuss-both-views","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/discuss-both-views-your-opinion/EdmundBd9ExpBth-Q16","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"Education budgets are often debated because schools must decide whether limited funds should be directed towards modern equipment or human instruction. Some argue that greater investment in technology, such as computers and digital platforms, is essential, while others believe that teachers deserve more financial support. In my view, although technology is useful, schools should prioritise spending on teachers because they remain the central force behind effective learning.","chinese":"教育預算經常引起討論，因為學校必須決定有限的資金應該投放於現代設備，還是投放於人的教學。 有些人認為，增加對科技的投資，例如電腦和數碼平台，是必不可少的；而另一些人則認為，教師更值得得到更多財政支持。 在我看來，儘管科技是有用的，學校仍應優先把資金用於教師身上，因為教師仍然是有效學習背後的核心力量。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"Those who support greater investment in technology argue that digital tools can make education more efficient and accessible. Computers allow students to research information quickly, practise independently, and develop digital skills that are now required in most workplaces. For example, a student who has access to online learning software can review difficult topics at home and learn at a pace that suits them. In this sense, technology can widen learning opportunities and prepare students for a world in which digital literacy is no longer optional.","chinese":"支持增加科技投資的人認為，數碼工具可以令教育更有效率，也更容易獲得。 電腦讓學生能夠快速搜尋資料、獨立練習，並培養現今大多數職場都需要的數碼技能。 例如，一名能夠使用網上學習軟件的學生，可以在家中重溫困難的課題，並按照適合自己的速度學習。 從這個角度來看，科技能夠擴大學習機會，並幫助學生為一個數碼素養已不再是可有可無的世界做好準備。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"However, spending more money on teachers is far more important because even the best technology cannot replace professional guidance, emotional support, and classroom judgment. A skilled teacher does not merely deliver information; they explain difficult ideas, notice when students are confused, adjust lessons, and motivate learners who may otherwise give up. For instance, a computer programme can mark an answer as wrong, but a teacher can identify why the mistake was made and show the student how to improve. Without well-trained and well-paid teachers, expensive devices may become little more than shiny distractions.","chinese":"然而，把更多金錢投放於教師身上重要得多，因為即使是最好的科技，也無法取代專業指導、情感支持和課堂判斷。 一位有能力的教師不只是傳遞資訊；他們會解釋困難的概念、察覺學生何時感到困惑、調整課堂，並鼓勵那些否則可能會放棄的學習者。 例如，一個電腦程式可以把答案標示為錯誤，但教師能夠指出錯誤產生的原因，並向學生展示如何改進。 如果沒有受過良好訓練並獲得合理薪酬的教師，昂貴的設備可能只會變成華而不實的干擾物。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 3","english":"I therefore believe that schools should invest more heavily in teachers. Better salaries can attract talented graduates into the profession, while regular training can help existing teachers use both traditional and digital methods more effectively. If teachers are supported properly, they can also make technology more meaningful in the classroom.","chinese":"因此，我認為學校應該更大力投資於教師。 更好的薪酬可以吸引有才華的畢業生加入這個行業，而定期培訓則可以幫助現有教師更有效地使用傳統和數碼教學方法。 如果教師得到適當支持，他們也能夠讓科技在課堂中變得更有意義。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, technology has a valuable role in modern education, but teachers should receive the larger share of school funding. Computers can assist learning, but teachers shape understanding, confidence, and long-term academic growth.","chinese":"總結來說，科技在現代教育中具有重要作用，但教師應該獲得學校資金中較大的部分。 電腦可以輔助學習，但教師塑造的是理解力、信心，以及長遠的學術成長。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"education budgets","chinese":"教育預算"},{"english":"be often debated","chinese":"經常被討論"},{"english":"limited funds","chinese":"有限資金"},{"english":"be directed towards","chinese":"被投放於"},{"english":"modern equipment","chinese":"現代設備"},{"english":"human instruction","chinese":"人的教學；教師指導"},{"english":"greater investment in","chinese":"對……更多投資"},{"english":"digital platforms","chinese":"數碼平台"},{"english":"be essential","chinese":"是必要的"},{"english":"deserve more financial support","chinese":"值得更多財政支持"},{"english":"in my view","chinese":"在我看來"},{"english":"prioritise spending on","chinese":"優先將資金投放於"},{"english":"the central force behind","chinese":"……背後的核心力量"},{"english":"effective learning","chinese":"有效學習"},{"english":"those who support","chinese":"支持……的人"},{"english":"digital tools","chinese":"數碼工具"},{"english":"make education more efficient and accessible","chinese":"令教育更高效和更容易取得"},{"english":"research information quickly","chinese":"快速查找資料"},{"english":"practise independently","chinese":"獨立練習"},{"english":"develop digital skills","chinese":"培養數碼技能"},{"english":"be required in","chinese":"在……中被要求"},{"english":"most workplaces","chinese":"大多數工作場所"},{"english":"have access to","chinese":"可以使用；可以取得"},{"english":"online learning software","chinese":"網上學習軟件"},{"english":"review difficult topics","chinese":"重溫困難課題"},{"english":"learn at a pace that suits them","chinese":"按適合自己的進度學習"},{"english":"in this sense","chinese":"從這個意義上說"},{"english":"widen learning opportunities","chinese":"擴闊學習機會"},{"english":"prepare students for","chinese":"讓學生為……作準備"},{"english":"digital literacy","chinese":"數碼素養"},{"english":"no longer optional","chinese":"不再是可有可無"},{"english":"spending more money on","chinese":"在……上花更多錢"},{"english":"far more important","chinese":"重要得多"},{"english":"even the best technology","chinese":"即使是最好的科技"},{"english":"cannot replace","chinese":"不能取代"},{"english":"professional guidance","chinese":"專業指導"},{"english":"emotional support","chinese":"情感支援"},{"english":"classroom judgment","chinese":"課堂判斷力"},{"english":"a skilled teacher","chinese":"熟練的老師"},{"english":"not merely deliver information","chinese":"不只是傳遞資訊"},{"english":"explain difficult ideas","chinese":"解釋困難概念"},{"english":"notice when students are confused","chinese":"留意到學生何時感到困惑"},{"english":"adjust lessons","chinese":"調整課堂"},{"english":"motivate learners","chinese":"激勵學習者"},{"english":"may otherwise give up","chinese":"否則可能會放棄"},{"english":"a computer programme","chinese":"電腦程式"},{"english":"mark an answer as wrong","chinese":"將答案標示為錯誤"},{"english":"identify why","chinese":"找出為何"},{"english":"the mistake was made","chinese":"錯誤是怎樣造成的"},{"english":"show the student how to improve","chinese":"向學生展示如何改進"},{"english":"well-trained and well-paid teachers","chinese":"受良好培訓且薪酬合理的老師"},{"english":"expensive devices","chinese":"昂貴裝置"},{"english":"little more than","chinese":"只不過是"},{"english":"shiny distractions","chinese":"外表吸引但分散注意力的東西"},{"english":"invest more heavily in","chinese":"加大對……的投資"},{"english":"better salaries","chinese":"更好的薪酬"},{"english":"attract talented graduates","chinese":"吸引有才華的畢業生"},{"english":"into the profession","chinese":"進入這個行業"},{"english":"regular training","chinese":"定期培訓"},{"english":"existing teachers","chinese":"現職教師"},{"english":"traditional and digital methods","chinese":"傳統和數碼方法"},{"english":"more effectively","chinese":"更有效地"},{"english":"be supported properly","chinese":"得到適當支持"},{"english":"make technology more meaningful","chinese":"令科技更有意義"},{"english":"in the classroom","chinese":"在課堂中"},{"english":"a valuable role in","chinese":"在……中有寶貴作用"},{"english":"modern education","chinese":"現代教育"},{"english":"the larger share of","chinese":"較大份額的"},{"english":"school funding","chinese":"學校資金"},{"english":"assist learning","chinese":"輔助學習"},{"english":"shape understanding","chinese":"塑造理解"},{"english":"confidence","chinese":"信心"},{"english":"long-term academic growth","chinese":"長遠學業成長"}]},"model-essay-16-ielts-opinion":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-16-ielts-opinion","essayKey":"opinion:16","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-16-ielts-opinion","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/opinions/EdmundBd9OP-Q16","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"Success is rarely achieved in isolation. In almost every field, from education to business, people have to work with others, persuade them, and respond to their expectations. For this reason, I completely agree that people skills are essential for success, because they turn individual ability into useful social and professional outcomes.","chinese":"成功很少是獨自一人便能取得的。在幾乎每一個領域中，從教育到商業，人們都必須與他人合作、說服他人，並回應他人的期望。 因此，我完全同意人際交往能力對成功至關重要，因為它們能把個人的能力轉化為有用的社交和專業成果。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"First, interpersonal skills determine how effectively a person can cooperate in a group. A capable worker who communicates poorly may produce good ideas, but those ideas can be misunderstood, ignored, or resisted. By contrast, someone who listens carefully, explains clearly, and handles disagreement calmly can keep a team moving in the same direction. For example, in a workplace project, the employee who can divide responsibilities tactfully and discuss problems before they become personal conflicts is more likely to deliver results than a brilliant colleague who alienates everyone. In this sense, people skills act as the bridge between competence and performance.","chinese":"首先，人際交往能力決定了一個人能多有效地在群體中合作。 一位有能力但溝通欠佳的員工或許能提出好主意，但那些想法可能會被誤解、忽視，甚至遭到抗拒。 相比之下，一個能夠仔細聆聽、清楚解釋，並冷靜處理分歧的人，能夠讓團隊朝著同一方向前進。 例如，在一個職場項目中，能夠得體地分配責任，並在問題變成人際衝突之前加以討論的員工，比起一位才華出眾卻疏遠所有人的同事，更有可能取得成果。 從這個意義上說，人際交往能力就像能力與表現之間的橋樑。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"Second, success often depends on trust and long-term relationships. Employers, clients, teachers, and colleagues are more likely to support people who appear reliable, respectful, and emotionally mature. Opportunities are rarely offered to qualifications on paper alone; they are offered to people whose character others can read and trust. A small business owner, for instance, may sell an excellent product, but if he dismisses customers’ concerns or treats staff harshly, his reputation will quickly suffer. On the other hand, an owner who listens to complaints, encourages employees, and builds loyalty can turn ordinary transactions into lasting relationships. These relationships often become the foundation of future growth.","chinese":"第二，成功往往取決於信任和長遠關係。 僱主、客戶、老師和同事更有可能支持那些看起來可靠、尊重他人，並且情緒成熟的人。 機會很少只會因紙面上的資歷而被提供；它們會被提供給那些其品格能被他人理解並信任的人。 例如，一位小企業老闆可能售賣非常出色的產品，但如果他忽視顧客的憂慮，或嚴苛對待員工，他的聲譽很快便會受損。 另一方面，一位願意聆聽投訴、鼓勵員工並建立忠誠度的老闆，能夠把普通的交易轉化為長久的關係。 這些關係往往會成為未來發展的基礎。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, I fully agree that people skills are essential for success. Knowledge, talent, and hard work matter greatly, but without the ability to communicate, cooperate, and earn trust, those strengths are far less likely to produce meaningful achievement.","chinese":"總結來說，我完全同意人際交往能力對成功至關重要。 知識、天分和努力都非常重要，但如果缺乏溝通、合作和贏得信任的能力，這些優勢便遠不那麼可能產生有意義的成就。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"success","chinese":"成功"},{"english":"rarely achieved in isolation","chinese":"很少能孤立地取得"},{"english":"in almost every field","chinese":"在幾乎每個領域"},{"english":"from education to business","chinese":"從教育到商業"},{"english":"work with others","chinese":"與他人合作"},{"english":"persuade them","chinese":"說服他們"},{"english":"respond to their expectations","chinese":"回應他們的期望"},{"english":"for this reason","chinese":"因此"},{"english":"people skills","chinese":"人際技巧"},{"english":"essential for success","chinese":"對成功必不可少"},{"english":"turn individual ability into","chinese":"將個人能力轉化為……"},{"english":"useful social and professional outcomes","chinese":"有用的社交和專業成果"},{"english":"interpersonal skills","chinese":"人際交往技巧"},{"english":"determine how effectively","chinese":"決定……有多有效"},{"english":"cooperate in a group","chinese":"在小組中合作"},{"english":"capable worker","chinese":"有能力的員工"},{"english":"communicates poorly","chinese":"溝通欠佳"},{"english":"produce good ideas","chinese":"提出好想法"},{"english":"be misunderstood, ignored, or resisted","chinese":"被誤解、忽視或抗拒"},{"english":"by contrast","chinese":"相比之下"},{"english":"listens carefully","chinese":"細心聆聽"},{"english":"explains clearly","chinese":"清楚解釋"},{"english":"handles disagreement calmly","chinese":"冷靜處理分歧"},{"english":"keep a team moving in the same direction","chinese":"令團隊朝同一方向前進"},{"english":"workplace project","chinese":"工作項目"},{"english":"divide responsibilities tactfully","chinese":"圓滑地分配責任"},{"english":"discuss problems before","chinese":"在……之前討論問題"},{"english":"personal conflicts","chinese":"個人衝突"},{"english":"be more likely to deliver results","chinese":"更有可能取得成果"},{"english":"brilliant colleague","chinese":"才華出眾的同事"},{"english":"alienates everyone","chinese":"疏離所有人"},{"english":"in this sense","chinese":"從這個意義上說"},{"english":"act as the bridge between","chinese":"成為……之間的橋樑"},{"english":"competence and performance","chinese":"能力和表現"},{"english":"depends on trust","chinese":"取決於信任"},{"english":"long-term relationships","chinese":"長遠關係"},{"english":"employers, clients, teachers, and colleagues","chinese":"僱主、客戶、老師和同事"},{"english":"be more likely to support","chinese":"更有可能支持"},{"english":"appear reliable","chinese":"顯得可靠"},{"english":"respectful","chinese":"尊重他人的"},{"english":"emotionally mature","chinese":"情緒成熟"},{"english":"qualifications on paper alone","chinese":"單靠紙面資歷"},{"english":"whose character others can read and trust","chinese":"其品格能被他人理解和信任的人"},{"english":"small business owner","chinese":"小企業東主"},{"english":"sell an excellent product","chinese":"銷售出色產品"},{"english":"dismisses customers' concerns","chinese":"漠視顧客的憂慮"},{"english":"treats staff harshly","chinese":"嚴厲對待員工"},{"english":"reputation will suffer","chinese":"聲譽會受損"},{"english":"on the other hand","chinese":"另一方面"},{"english":"listens to complaints","chinese":"聆聽投訴"},{"english":"encourages employees","chinese":"鼓勵員工"},{"english":"builds loyalty","chinese":"建立忠誠"},{"english":"ordinary transactions","chinese":"普通交易"},{"english":"lasting relationships","chinese":"持久關係"},{"english":"foundation of future growth","chinese":"未來發展的基礎"},{"english":"knowledge, talent, and hard work","chinese":"知識、才能和努力"},{"english":"matter greatly","chinese":"非常重要"},{"english":"the ability to communicate","chinese":"溝通能力"},{"english":"cooperate","chinese":"合作"},{"english":"earn trust","chinese":"贏得信任"},{"english":"far less likely to","chinese":"可能性低得多"},{"english":"meaningful achievement","chinese":"有意義的成就"}]},"model-essay-17-ielts-advantage-disadvantage":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-17-ielts-advantage-disadvantage","essayKey":"advantage-disadvantage:17","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-17-ielts-advantage-disadvantage","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/advantage-and-disadvantage/EdmundBd9AdDisAd-Q17","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"Public libraries have long been physical spaces where people borrow books, study quietly, and seek reliable information. However, some believe that these institutions will soon exist only online, with all books and services becoming digitally accessible. This development would bring several clear benefits, although it would also create notable drawbacks.","chinese":"[長久以來，公共圖書館一直是人們借閱書籍、安靜學習，以及尋找可靠資訊的實體場所。] [然而，有些人認為，這些機構很快將只以線上形式存在，所有書籍和服務都會以數碼方式供大眾使用。] [這種發展會帶來幾個明顯的好處，但同時也會產生不容忽視的缺點。]"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"One major advantage of online-only libraries is accessibility. Digital platforms allow users to obtain books, journals, and reference materials instantly, regardless of location or opening hours. This is especially beneficial for people living in remote areas, those with mobility issues, and full-time workers who may find it difficult to visit a library building in person. Another benefit is efficiency. Online collections can be updated more quickly, and searching for a specific title or topic becomes far easier when readers can use keywords rather than walk through shelves. In addition, digital services may reduce certain operational costs, such as maintaining large buildings or printing multiple physical copies of the same text.","chinese":"[線上圖書館的一大優點是可及性。] [數碼平台讓使用者無論身在何處，也不受開放時間限制，都能即時取得書籍、期刊和參考資料。] [這對居住在偏遠地區的人、行動不便者，以及難以親身前往圖書館的全職工作者尤其有利。] [另一個優點是效率。] [線上館藏可以更快更新，而當讀者能以關鍵字搜尋，而不是在書架間來回尋找時，要找到特定書名或主題也會容易得多。] [此外，數碼服務還可能降低某些營運成本，例如維持大型館舍的開支，或印刷同一文本的多本實體副本。] [因此，線上圖書館能同時提升資訊取得的便利性，以及圖書館服務的效率。]"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"However, the disappearance of library buildings would also have serious disadvantages. The most obvious is digital inequality. Not everyone has a stable internet connection, suitable devices, or the technical skills needed to use online resources comfortably. For such individuals, a fully digital system would not broaden access but narrow it. Furthermore, public libraries are more than book-lending services; they are community spaces. Many people rely on them as quiet places to study, attend workshops, use computers, or ask librarians for face-to-face guidance. Once a library exists only on a screen, that human element may be lost. Knowledge may remain available, yet the sense of welcome, support, and public belonging could quietly disappear.","chinese":"[然而，圖書館建築的消失也會帶來嚴重的缺點。] [其中最明顯的一點就是數碼不平等。] [並不是每個人都擁有穩定的網絡連線、合適的設備，或足以熟練使用網上資源的技術能力。] [對這些人而言，全面數碼化的系統不但不會擴大使用機會，反而會收窄它。] [此外，公共圖書館不只是借書服務；它們同時也是社區空間。] [很多人依賴圖書館作為安靜的學習場所、參加工作坊的地點、使用電腦的空間，或向館員尋求面對面的指導。] [一旦圖書館只存在於螢幕之上，那種人性化的元素便可能消失。知識也許仍然可以被取得，但那份被歡迎、被支持，以及對公共空間的歸屬感，卻可能悄然消散。] [因此，純線上圖書館在理論上看似提升可及性，但在實際上卻可能排除弱勢群體，並削弱社區生活。]"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, turning public libraries into entirely online services would improve convenience, reach, and efficiency. At the same time, it could deepen social inequality and weaken the wider community role that physical libraries still play.","chinese":"[總結來說，把公共圖書館完全轉為線上服務，將會提升便利性、覆蓋範圍和整體效率。] [與此同時，這也可能加劇社會不平等，並削弱實體圖書館至今仍然承擔的更廣泛社區功能。]"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"public libraries","chinese":"公共圖書館"},{"english":"have long been","chinese":"長久以來一直是"},{"english":"physical spaces","chinese":"實體空間"},{"english":"borrow books","chinese":"借閱圖書"},{"english":"study quietly","chinese":"安靜地溫習；安靜地學習"},{"english":"seek reliable information","chinese":"尋求可靠資料"},{"english":"these institutions","chinese":"這些機構"},{"english":"exist only online","chinese":"只以網上形式存在"},{"english":"digitally accessible","chinese":"可透過數碼方式取得"},{"english":"several clear benefits","chinese":"幾個明顯好處"},{"english":"notable drawbacks","chinese":"顯著缺點"},{"english":"online-only libraries","chinese":"純網上圖書館"},{"english":"accessibility","chinese":"可取得性；便利程度"},{"english":"digital platforms","chinese":"數碼平台"},{"english":"obtain books, journals, and reference materials","chinese":"取得圖書、期刊及參考資料"},{"english":"reference materials","chinese":"參考資料"},{"english":"regardless of location or opening hours","chinese":"不受地點或開放時間限制"},{"english":"opening hours","chinese":"開放時間"},{"english":"especially beneficial for","chinese":"對……尤其有益"},{"english":"remote areas","chinese":"偏遠地區"},{"english":"mobility issues","chinese":"行動不便"},{"english":"full-time workers","chinese":"全職工作人士"},{"english":"visit a library building in person","chinese":"親身到訪圖書館大樓"},{"english":"another benefit is efficiency","chinese":"另一個好處是效率"},{"english":"online collections","chinese":"網上館藏"},{"english":"be updated more quickly","chinese":"更快更新"},{"english":"searching for a specific title or topic","chinese":"搜尋特定書名或主題"},{"english":"far easier","chinese":"容易得多"},{"english":"use keywords","chinese":"使用關鍵字"},{"english":"walk through shelves","chinese":"在書架之間逐一尋找"},{"english":"digital services","chinese":"數碼服務"},{"english":"operational costs","chinese":"營運成本"},{"english":"maintaining large buildings","chinese":"維護大型建築物"},{"english":"printing multiple physical copies","chinese":"印製多本實體副本"},{"english":"physical copies","chinese":"實體副本"},{"english":"the disappearance of library buildings","chinese":"圖書館大樓的消失"},{"english":"serious disadvantages","chinese":"嚴重缺點"},{"english":"digital inequality","chinese":"數碼不平等"},{"english":"a stable internet connection","chinese":"穩定的互聯網連接"},{"english":"suitable devices","chinese":"合適的裝置"},{"english":"technical skills","chinese":"技術技能"},{"english":"online resources","chinese":"網上資源"},{"english":"broaden access","chinese":"擴大使用機會"},{"english":"narrow it","chinese":"收窄使用機會"},{"english":"book-lending services","chinese":"借書服務"},{"english":"community spaces","chinese":"社區空間"},{"english":"rely on them as","chinese":"依賴它們作為……"},{"english":"attend workshops","chinese":"參加工作坊"},{"english":"face-to-face guidance","chinese":"面對面指導"},{"english":"exists only on a screen","chinese":"只存在於屏幕上"},{"english":"the human element","chinese":"人情味；人與人之間的元素"},{"english":"may be lost","chinese":"可能會失去"},{"english":"knowledge may remain available","chinese":"知識可能仍然可取得"},{"english":"the sense of welcome","chinese":"受歡迎和被接納的感覺"},{"english":"public belonging","chinese":"公共歸屬感"},{"english":"quietly disappear","chinese":"悄然消失"},{"english":"turning public libraries into","chinese":"將公共圖書館變成……"},{"english":"entirely online services","chinese":"完全網上化的服務"},{"english":"improve convenience, reach, and efficiency","chinese":"提升便利性、覆蓋範圍和效率"},{"english":"at the same time","chinese":"同時"},{"english":"deepen social inequality","chinese":"加深社會不平等"},{"english":"weaken the wider community role","chinese":"削弱更廣泛的社區角色"},{"english":"physical libraries","chinese":"實體圖書館"},{"english":"still play","chinese":"仍然發揮"}]},"model-essay-17-ielts-cause-solution":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-17-ielts-cause-solution","essayKey":"cause-solution:17","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-17-ielts-cause-solution","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/problem-and-cause/EdmundBd9CnS-Q17","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"In many countries, a growing number of people from farming communities are leaving the countryside and moving to cities in search of paid employment. This trend can create serious pressure both in urban centres and in rural areas, but it can be addressed through stronger rural investment and better-managed urban planning.","chinese":"在許多國家，越來越多來自農業社群的人正離開鄉村，搬到城市尋找有薪工作。 這種趨勢可能同時為城市中心和農村地區帶來嚴重壓力，但它可以透過更強的農村投資和更妥善管理的城市規劃來應對。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"One major consequence is that cities may become overcrowded before they are ready to absorb the new population. When large numbers of rural workers arrive within a short period, housing, transport and public services can be stretched beyond their normal capacity. As a result, many newcomers may end up living in poor-quality accommodation, working in unstable jobs, or competing intensely for low-paid work. For example, a young farmer who moves to a major city without recognised qualifications may find that the city offers more opportunities in theory than in practice. At the same time, this movement can weaken rural communities. If too many working-age people leave agriculture, farms may lose labour, villages may become dominated by the elderly, and local food production may gradually decline.","chinese":"一個主要後果是，城市可能在尚未準備好吸收新增人口之前便變得過度擁擠。 當大量農村勞工在短時間內湧入城市時，住房、交通和公共服務可能會被拉扯到超出其正常承載能力的程度。 結果是，許多新來者最終可能住在質素低劣的住所中，從事不穩定的工作，或為低薪工作進行激烈競爭。 例如，一位沒有受認可資歷的年輕農民搬到大城市後，可能會發現這座城市在理論上提供更多機會，但在實際上並非如此。 與此同時，這種人口流動也可能削弱農村社群。 如果太多處於工作年齡的人離開農業，農場可能會失去勞動力，村莊可能會變成以長者為主，而本地糧食生產也可能逐漸下降。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"One practical response is to make rural life economically viable rather than treating cities as the only path to progress. Governments could invest in irrigation, storage facilities, rural roads and digital access so that farmers can sell their products more efficiently and earn a steadier income. They should also support modern agricultural training, small businesses and food-processing industries, which would create employment near people’s homes. In cities, authorities need to plan for migration instead of simply reacting to it. Affordable housing, vocational training and reliable public transport would help new arrivals enter the formal economy and avoid being pushed to the margins.","chinese":"一個實際的應對方法，是令農村生活在經濟上變得可行，而不是把城市視為唯一的進步道路。 政府可以投資灌溉系統、儲存設施、農村道路和數位連接，使農民能夠更有效率地出售產品，並賺取更穩定的收入。 他們也應該支持現代農業培訓、小型企業和食品加工產業，這些都能在人們居住地附近創造就業機會。 在城市中，當局需要為人口遷移作出規劃，而不是單純在問題出現後才作出反應。 可負擔住房、職業培訓和可靠的公共交通，將有助於新來者進入正規經濟體系，並避免被推向社會邊緣。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, rural-to-urban migration can lead to overcrowded cities, insecure employment and a decline in agricultural communities. However, if governments improve rural opportunities while managing urban growth carefully, this movement can become far less damaging and more sustainable.","chinese":"總結來說，農村到城市的人口遷移可能導致城市過度擁擠、就業不穩定，以及農業社群衰落。 然而，如果政府在謹慎管理城市增長的同時改善農村機會，這種人口流動便可以變得危害少得多，也更加可持續。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"a growing number of","chinese":"越來越多"},{"english":"farming communities","chinese":"農業社區"},{"english":"leave the countryside","chinese":"離開鄉郊"},{"english":"move to cities","chinese":"搬到城市"},{"english":"in search of paid employment","chinese":"尋找受薪工作"},{"english":"create serious pressure","chinese":"造成嚴重壓力"},{"english":"urban centres","chinese":"城市中心"},{"english":"rural areas","chinese":"鄉郊地區"},{"english":"be addressed through","chinese":"透過……處理"},{"english":"rural investment","chinese":"鄉郊投資"},{"english":"better-managed urban planning","chinese":"管理更完善的城市規劃"},{"english":"one major consequence","chinese":"一個主要後果"},{"english":"become overcrowded","chinese":"變得過度擠迫"},{"english":"be ready to absorb","chinese":"準備好吸收"},{"english":"the new population","chinese":"新增人口"},{"english":"rural workers","chinese":"鄉郊工人"},{"english":"within a short period","chinese":"在短時間內"},{"english":"public services","chinese":"公共服務"},{"english":"be stretched beyond","chinese":"超出……負荷"},{"english":"normal capacity","chinese":"正常承載能力"},{"english":"as a result","chinese":"因此"},{"english":"newcomers","chinese":"新來者"},{"english":"end up living in","chinese":"最終住在"},{"english":"poor-quality accommodation","chinese":"質素差的住所"},{"english":"unstable jobs","chinese":"不穩定的工作"},{"english":"compete intensely for","chinese":"激烈競爭"},{"english":"low-paid work","chinese":"低薪工作"},{"english":"recognised qualifications","chinese":"受承認的資歷"},{"english":"in theory than in practice","chinese":"理論上多於實際上"},{"english":"at the same time","chinese":"同時"},{"english":"weaken rural communities","chinese":"削弱鄉郊社區"},{"english":"working-age people","chinese":"適齡工作人口"},{"english":"leave agriculture","chinese":"離開農業"},{"english":"lose labour","chinese":"失去勞動力"},{"english":"be dominated by the elderly","chinese":"以長者為主"},{"english":"local food production","chinese":"本地糧食生產"},{"english":"gradually decline","chinese":"逐漸下降"},{"english":"one practical response","chinese":"一個實際對策"},{"english":"economically viable","chinese":"經濟上可行"},{"english":"the only path to progress","chinese":"進步的唯一途徑"},{"english":"invest in irrigation","chinese":"投資灌溉"},{"english":"storage facilities","chinese":"儲存設施"},{"english":"rural roads","chinese":"鄉郊道路"},{"english":"digital access","chinese":"數碼連接"},{"english":"sell their products more efficiently","chinese":"更有效率地銷售產品"},{"english":"earn a steadier income","chinese":"賺取較穩定的收入"},{"english":"modern agricultural training","chinese":"現代農業培訓"},{"english":"small businesses","chinese":"小型企業"},{"english":"food-processing industries","chinese":"食品加工業"},{"english":"create employment near","chinese":"在……附近創造就業"},{"english":"plan for migration","chinese":"為人口遷移作規劃"},{"english":"instead of simply reacting to it","chinese":"而不是只作被動回應"},{"english":"affordable housing","chinese":"可負擔住房"},{"english":"vocational training","chinese":"職業培訓"},{"english":"reliable public transport","chinese":"可靠的公共交通"},{"english":"new arrivals","chinese":"新到埗人士"},{"english":"enter the formal economy","chinese":"進入正規經濟"},{"english":"be pushed to the margins","chinese":"被推到邊緣"},{"english":"rural-to-urban migration","chinese":"鄉郊至城市的人口遷移"},{"english":"overcrowded cities","chinese":"過度擠迫的城市"},{"english":"insecure employment","chinese":"不穩定就業"},{"english":"a decline in agricultural communities","chinese":"農業社區的衰落"},{"english":"improve rural opportunities","chinese":"改善鄉郊機會"},{"english":"manage urban growth carefully","chinese":"謹慎管理城市增長"},{"english":"far less damaging","chinese":"破壞性大大降低"},{"english":"more sustainable","chinese":"更可持續"}]},"model-essay-17-ielts-direct-question":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-17-ielts-direct-question","essayKey":"direct-question:17","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-17-ielts-direct-question","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/direct-question/EdmundBd9Dir-Q17","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"Population growth and rapid urban expansion are placing intense pressure on forests, coastlines, rivers and other scenic areas. Protecting these places is not simply an environmental preference; it brings clear public, economic and cultural benefits. This essay will discuss those benefits and suggest how governments can prevent further loss.","chinese":"人口增長和快速城市擴張，正對森林、海岸線、河流以及其他風景優美的地區造成巨大壓力。 保護這些地方並不只是環境方面的偏好；它能帶來明顯的公共、經濟和文化利益。 本文將討論這些好處，並提出政府可以如何防止這些地方進一步流失。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"First, preserving natural beauty spots improves public health and quality of life. Parks, beaches and woodlands give people a place to breathe, walk and recover from the mental strain of city life. Without such spaces, urban living can become a concrete cage, especially for children and elderly residents who have few affordable ways to relax. These places also support tourism and local employment. A well-protected mountain trail or coastal reserve can attract visitors, create jobs for guides and small businesses, and give communities a reason to value their landscape rather than sell it off piece by piece. In addition, natural sites preserve a country’s identity, as many landscapes are tied to local history, traditions and collective memory.","chinese":"首先，保護自然美景地點能改善公共健康和生活質素。 公園、海灘和林地為人們提供了一個可以呼吸、散步，並從城市生活的精神壓力中恢復過來的地方。 如果沒有這些空間，城市生活可能會變成一個混凝土牢籠，尤其是對於兒童和長者而言，因為他們可負擔的放鬆方式並不多。 這些地方也能支持旅遊業和本地就業。 一條受到良好保護的山徑或海岸保護區，可以吸引遊客、為導遊和小型企業創造職位，並讓社區有理由珍惜自己的景觀，而不是把它一點一點地出售。 此外，自然地點也能保存一個國家的身份認同，因為許多景觀都與本地歷史、傳統和集體記憶緊密相連。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"This problem can be tackled through stronger planning laws and practical conservation funding. Governments should set legal boundaries around important natural sites, limit construction in sensitive zones, and require developers to restore or replace green space when building is unavoidable. This ensures that expansion does not spread like an unchecked tide across every open area. At the same time, protection must be made financially realistic. Entrance fees, eco-tourism revenue and public-private partnerships can fund maintenance, waste control and park staff, while schools and media campaigns can teach citizens why these places matter. When people see natural beauty as shared public wealth rather than empty land waiting to be developed, they are more likely to defend it.","chinese":"這個問題可以透過更強有力的規劃法律和實際的保育資金來處理。 政府應該在重要自然地點周圍設立法律邊界，限制在敏感地區進行建設，並在建築工程無法避免時，要求發展商修復或補回綠化空間。 這能確保城市擴張不會像失控的潮水一樣蔓延到每一片開放空間。 同時，保護工作必須在財政上變得切實可行。 入場費、生態旅遊收入和公私營合作，可以為維修保養、廢物管理和公園員工提供資金，而學校和媒體宣傳活動則可以教導市民為何這些地方重要。 當人們把自然美景視為共享的公共財富，而不是等待發展的空地時，他們更有可能保護它"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, protecting natural beauty spots benefits public health, local economies and cultural identity. The loss of these places can be reduced through firm urban planning, reliable funding and public education, so that development and environmental protection can move forward together.","chinese":"總結來說，保護自然美景地點有利於公共健康、本地經濟和文化身份。 這些地方的流失可以透過堅定的城市規劃、可靠的資金和公共教育來減少，從而讓發展與環境保護能夠共同向前推進。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"population growth","chinese":"人口增長"},{"english":"rapid urban expansion","chinese":"急速城市擴張"},{"english":"placing intense pressure on","chinese":"對……造成巨大壓力"},{"english":"forests, coastlines and rivers","chinese":"森林、海岸線和河流"},{"english":"scenic areas","chinese":"風景區"},{"english":"protecting these places","chinese":"保護這些地方"},{"english":"not simply an environmental preference","chinese":"不只是環保取向"},{"english":"clear public, economic and cultural benefits","chinese":"明顯的公眾、經濟和文化好處"},{"english":"prevent further loss","chinese":"防止進一步流失"},{"english":"preserving natural beauty spots","chinese":"保育自然景點"},{"english":"public health and quality of life","chinese":"公眾健康和生活質素"},{"english":"give people a place to","chinese":"給人們一個地方去……"},{"english":"recover from","chinese":"從……中恢復過來"},{"english":"the mental strain of","chinese":"……帶來的精神壓力"},{"english":"city life","chinese":"城市生活"},{"english":"urban living","chinese":"城市生活"},{"english":"a concrete cage","chinese":"混凝土牢籠"},{"english":"affordable ways to relax","chinese":"負擔得起的放鬆方式"},{"english":"elderly residents","chinese":"年長居民"},{"english":"support tourism and local employment","chinese":"支持旅遊業和本地就業"},{"english":"a well-protected mountain trail","chinese":"保護良好的山徑"},{"english":"coastal reserve","chinese":"海岸保護區"},{"english":"attract visitors","chinese":"吸引遊客"},{"english":"create jobs for","chinese":"為……創造職位"},{"english":"small businesses","chinese":"小型企業"},{"english":"give communities a reason to","chinese":"給社區理由去……"},{"english":"value their landscape","chinese":"珍惜自己的景觀"},{"english":"sell it off piece by piece","chinese":"逐步賣掉"},{"english":"preserve a country's identity","chinese":"保留一個國家的身份特色"},{"english":"be tied to","chinese":"與……有關連"},{"english":"local history and traditions","chinese":"本地歷史和傳統"},{"english":"collective memory","chinese":"集體記憶"},{"english":"be tackled through","chinese":"透過……處理"},{"english":"stronger planning laws","chinese":"更嚴格的規劃法例"},{"english":"practical conservation funding","chinese":"實際可行的保育資金"},{"english":"set legal boundaries around","chinese":"為……劃定法律界線"},{"english":"important natural sites","chinese":"重要自然地點"},{"english":"limit construction in","chinese":"限制在……興建"},{"english":"sensitive zones","chinese":"敏感地帶"},{"english":"require developers to","chinese":"要求發展商去……"},{"english":"restore or replace green space","chinese":"修復或替代綠化空間"},{"english":"when building is unavoidable","chinese":"當建設無可避免時"},{"english":"does not spread like","chinese":"不會像……般蔓延"},{"english":"an unchecked tide","chinese":"失控的潮水"},{"english":"every open area","chinese":"每一片開放空間"},{"english":"financially realistic","chinese":"財政上可行"},{"english":"entrance fees","chinese":"入場費"},{"english":"eco-tourism revenue","chinese":"生態旅遊收入"},{"english":"public-private partnerships","chinese":"公私營合作"},{"english":"fund maintenance","chinese":"資助維護工作"},{"english":"waste control","chinese":"廢物管理"},{"english":"park staff","chinese":"公園職員"},{"english":"media campaigns","chinese":"媒體宣傳活動"},{"english":"shared public wealth","chinese":"共享公共財富"},{"english":"empty land waiting to be developed","chinese":"等待開發的空地"},{"english":"more likely to defend","chinese":"更有可能捍衛"},{"english":"firm urban planning","chinese":"嚴格的城市規劃"},{"english":"reliable funding","chinese":"可靠資金"},{"english":"public education","chinese":"公眾教育"},{"english":"move forward together","chinese":"一起向前發展；並行發展"}]},"model-essay-17-ielts-discuss-both-views":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-17-ielts-discuss-both-views","essayKey":"discuss-both-views:17","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-17-ielts-discuss-both-views","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/discuss-both-views-your-opinion/EdmundBd9ExpBth-Q17","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"It is widely believed that a child’s academic progress is shaped either mainly by parents or mainly by teachers. While parents are undeniably important because they create the home environment in which learning habits begin, I believe teachers have the greater influence on academic development, as they directly control the quality, structure and direction of a child’s formal education.","chinese":"人們普遍認為，孩子的學業進步主要是由父母或老師所塑造的。 雖然父母無疑十分重要，因為他們創造了孩子學習習慣開始形成的家庭環境， 但我認為老師對學業發展有更大的影響，因為他們直接掌控孩子正規教育的質素、結構和方向。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"On the one hand, parents play a powerful role in shaping a child’s attitude towards study. Children who grow up in homes where reading, discipline and curiosity are encouraged are more likely to see education as a normal part of daily life rather than a burden. For example, a parent who sets regular study times, limits distractions and praises effort can help a child build persistence long before exam pressure appears. In this sense, parents are like the soil in which academic confidence first takes root: without their support, even a capable student may lose motivation.","chinese":"一方面，父母在塑造孩子對學習的態度方面扮演著重要角色。 在鼓勵閱讀、自律和好奇心的家庭中成長的孩子，更有可能把教育視為日常生活中正常的一部分，而不是一種負擔。 例如，一位會設定固定學習時間、限制干擾並讚賞努力的父母，能夠在考試壓力出現之前很早便幫助孩子建立堅持的能力。 從這個意義上說，父母就像學業信心最初扎根的土壤：如果沒有他們的支持，即使是有能力的學生也可能失去動力。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"On the other hand, teachers usually have a more direct and professional impact on a child’s academic growth. Their influence is not limited to encouragement; they design lessons, explain complex ideas, assess progress and correct misunderstandings before they become permanent weaknesses. A skilled mathematics teacher, for instance, can identify why a student keeps making the same algebra mistake and then adjust the explanation until the concept becomes clear. This kind of targeted academic guidance is difficult for most parents to provide, especially as subjects become more specialised. Moreover, teachers can compare a child’s performance with that of many peers, which allows them to judge strengths and weaknesses more accurately.","chinese":"另一方面，老師通常對孩子的學業成長有更直接且更專業的影響。 他們的影響並不局限於鼓勵；他們會設計課程、解釋複雜概念、評估進度，並在誤解變成長期弱點之前加以糾正。 例如，一位熟練的數學老師可以判斷為甚麼某個學生不斷犯同一個代數錯誤，然後調整解釋方式，直到概念變得清晰為止。 這種具針對性的學業指導，是大多數父母難以提供的，尤其當學科變得更加專門化時更是如此。 此外，老師可以將一個孩子的表現與許多同齡人作比較，這使他們能夠更準確地判斷孩子的優點和弱點。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, parents build the foundations of a child’s learning habits and emotional attitude towards education. However, because teachers possess subject expertise, teaching methods and regular access to academic performance, I believe they exert a greater influence on a child’s academic development.","chinese":"總結來說，父母建立了孩子學習習慣和對教育情感態度的基礎。 然而，由於老師擁有學科專業知識、教學方法，並能定期了解學生的學業表現，我認為他們對孩子的學業發展發揮更大的影響。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"it is widely believed that","chinese":"人們普遍相信"},{"english":"academic progress","chinese":"學業進展"},{"english":"be shaped by","chinese":"受……塑造"},{"english":"either mainly by ... or mainly by","chinese":"主要由……或主要由……"},{"english":"undeniably important","chinese":"無可否認地重要"},{"english":"create the home environment","chinese":"營造家庭環境"},{"english":"learning habits","chinese":"學習習慣"},{"english":"the greater influence on","chinese":"對……有更大影響"},{"english":"academic development","chinese":"學業發展"},{"english":"directly control","chinese":"直接控制"},{"english":"the quality, structure and direction of","chinese":"……的質素、結構和方向"},{"english":"formal education","chinese":"正規教育"},{"english":"on the one hand","chinese":"一方面"},{"english":"play a powerful role in","chinese":"在……中扮演重要角色"},{"english":"shape a child's attitude towards study","chinese":"塑造孩子對學習的態度"},{"english":"grow up in homes where","chinese":"在……的家庭中長大"},{"english":"reading, discipline and curiosity","chinese":"閱讀、自律和好奇心"},{"english":"be encouraged","chinese":"被鼓勵"},{"english":"be more likely to","chinese":"更有可能"},{"english":"see education as","chinese":"將教育視為"},{"english":"a normal part of daily life","chinese":"日常生活的正常一部分"},{"english":"rather than a burden","chinese":"而不是負擔"},{"english":"set regular study times","chinese":"設定固定溫習時間"},{"english":"limit distractions","chinese":"減少干擾"},{"english":"praise effort","chinese":"讚賞努力"},{"english":"build persistence","chinese":"建立毅力"},{"english":"long before","chinese":"早在……之前"},{"english":"exam pressure","chinese":"考試壓力"},{"english":"in this sense","chinese":"從這個意義上說"},{"english":"be like the soil in which","chinese":"像……扎根的土壤"},{"english":"academic confidence","chinese":"學業信心"},{"english":"take root","chinese":"扎根"},{"english":"without their support","chinese":"沒有他們的支持"},{"english":"a capable student","chinese":"有能力的學生"},{"english":"lose motivation","chinese":"失去動力"},{"english":"on the other hand","chinese":"另一方面"},{"english":"a more direct and professional impact on","chinese":"對……有更直接和專業的影響"},{"english":"academic growth","chinese":"學業成長"},{"english":"not limited to","chinese":"不限於"},{"english":"design lessons","chinese":"設計課堂"},{"english":"explain complex ideas","chinese":"解釋複雜概念"},{"english":"assess progress","chinese":"評估進展"},{"english":"correct misunderstandings","chinese":"糾正誤解"},{"english":"permanent weaknesses","chinese":"長期弱點"},{"english":"a skilled mathematics teacher","chinese":"熟練的數學老師"},{"english":"identify why","chinese":"找出為何"},{"english":"keep making the same mistake","chinese":"不斷犯同一個錯誤"},{"english":"algebra mistake","chinese":"代數錯誤"},{"english":"adjust the explanation","chinese":"調整解釋方式"},{"english":"the concept becomes clear","chinese":"概念變得清晰"},{"english":"targeted academic guidance","chinese":"針對性的學業指導"},{"english":"be difficult for most parents to provide","chinese":"對大多數家長來說難以提供"},{"english":"become more specialised","chinese":"變得更專門"},{"english":"compare a child's performance with","chinese":"將孩子的表現與……比較"},{"english":"peers","chinese":"同齡人；同學"},{"english":"judge strengths and weaknesses","chinese":"判斷強項和弱點"},{"english":"more accurately","chinese":"更準確地"},{"english":"build the foundations of","chinese":"建立……的基礎"},{"english":"emotional attitude towards","chinese":"對……的情感態度"},{"english":"possess subject expertise","chinese":"具備學科專業知識"},{"english":"teaching methods","chinese":"教學方法"},{"english":"regular access to","chinese":"定期接觸；定期掌握"},{"english":"academic performance","chinese":"學業表現"},{"english":"exert a greater influence on","chinese":"對……施加更大影響"}]},"model-essay-17-ielts-opinion":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-17-ielts-opinion","essayKey":"opinion:17","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-17-ielts-opinion","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/opinions/EdmundBd9OP-Q17","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"It is sometimes claimed that people in earlier generations were happier than people are today. I completely disagree with this view because modern life, despite its pressures, gives people better protection, wider choices, and more control over their lives.","chinese":"有時有人聲稱，以往世代的人比今天的人更加快樂。 我完全不同意這個觀點，因為現代生活雖然有壓力，但它給予人們更好的保障、更廣泛的選擇，以及對自己人生更大的掌控權。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"The first reason is that people today are less exposed to many of the basic fears that shaped life in the past. Earlier generations may be remembered through the warm light of nostalgia, but daily life was often physically harsher and more uncertain. Illness, unsafe work, limited public services, and financial insecurity could turn one setback into a family crisis. By contrast, modern healthcare, labour protection, sanitation, and social support reduce the amount of suffering that people have to accept as normal. For example, a worker who becomes seriously ill today is more likely to receive medical treatment, sick leave, or community support, whereas a similar problem in the past could easily destroy a household’s income. Happiness is not only about having a simple life; it also depends on being safe from preventable misery.","chinese":"第一個原因是，今天的人較少暴露於許多曾經塑造過去生活的基本恐懼之中。 以往世代也許會在懷舊的溫暖光影中被記起，但當時的日常生活往往在物質上更加艱苦，也更加不穩定。 疾病、不安全的工作、有限的公共服務，以及經濟上的不穩定，都可能把一次挫折變成一場家庭危機。 相比之下，現代醫療、勞工保障、衛生設施和社會支援，減少了人們必須視為正常的痛苦。 例如，今天一名嚴重患病的工人更有可能獲得醫療治療、病假或社區支援；然而，在過去，類似的問題很容易摧毀一個家庭的收入。 快樂不只是關於擁有簡單的生活；它也取決於人們是否能遠離可以避免的痛苦。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"Another important point is that modern society allows more personal freedom. In previous generations, many people were trapped by rigid expectations about gender, class, marriage, religion, and work. They might have appeared content, but appearance is not the same as inner happiness. Today, people are more able to choose their education, career, partner, lifestyle, and beliefs. This freedom can create pressure, but it also gives individuals room to build a life that actually fits them. For instance, a young woman who wants to study abroad, start a business, or delay marriage has far more freedom now than her grandmother probably had. That kind of choice is not a small luxury; it is one of the foundations of genuine fulfilment.","chinese":"另一個重要觀點是，現代社會容許更多個人自由。 在以往世代，許多人都被關於性別、階級、婚姻、宗教和工作的僵化期望所束縛。 他們或許看起來滿足，但外表上的滿足並不等同於內心真正的快樂。 今天，人們更能夠選擇自己的教育、職業、伴侶、生活方式和信念。 這種自由可能會帶來壓力，但它也給予個人空間去建立真正適合自己的生活。 例如，一位想出國讀書、創業或推遲婚姻的年輕女性，今天所擁有的自由很可能遠遠多於她祖母當年所擁有的自由。 這種選擇並不是一種微不足道的奢侈；它是真正滿足感的其中一個基礎。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, I completely reject the idea that earlier generations were happier. The past may look peaceful from a distance, but modern life offers greater security, freedom, and human dignity, which make true happiness more attainable today.","chinese":"總結來說，我完全否定以往世代的人更快樂這個想法。 從遠處看，過去也許顯得平靜，但現代生活提供了更大的安全感、自由和人的尊嚴，而這些都使真正的快樂在今天更加容易達到。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"it is sometimes claimed that","chinese":"有時有人聲稱……"},{"english":"earlier generations","chinese":"較早幾代人"},{"english":"completely disagree with","chinese":"完全不同意……"},{"english":"modern life","chinese":"現代生活"},{"english":"despite its pressures","chinese":"儘管有壓力"},{"english":"better protection","chinese":"更好的保障"},{"english":"wider choices","chinese":"更廣泛的選擇"},{"english":"more control over their lives","chinese":"對自己生活有更多掌控"},{"english":"be less exposed to","chinese":"較少面對……"},{"english":"basic fears","chinese":"基本恐懼"},{"english":"shaped life","chinese":"塑造生活"},{"english":"in the past","chinese":"在過去"},{"english":"be remembered through","chinese":"透過……被記住"},{"english":"warm light of nostalgia","chinese":"懷舊的溫暖光芒"},{"english":"daily life","chinese":"日常生活"},{"english":"physically harsher","chinese":"體力上更艱苦"},{"english":"more uncertain","chinese":"更不穩定；更難預測"},{"english":"unsafe work","chinese":"不安全的工作"},{"english":"limited public services","chinese":"有限的公共服務"},{"english":"financial insecurity","chinese":"經濟不穩"},{"english":"one setback","chinese":"一次挫折；一次打擊"},{"english":"family crisis","chinese":"家庭危機"},{"english":"by contrast","chinese":"相比之下"},{"english":"modern healthcare","chinese":"現代醫療"},{"english":"labour protection","chinese":"勞工保障"},{"english":"sanitation","chinese":"衞生設施；公共衞生"},{"english":"social support","chinese":"社會支援"},{"english":"reduce the amount of suffering","chinese":"減少痛苦的程度"},{"english":"accept as normal","chinese":"視為正常而接受"},{"english":"seriously ill","chinese":"病重"},{"english":"be more likely to","chinese":"更有可能"},{"english":"medical treatment","chinese":"醫療治療"},{"english":"sick leave","chinese":"病假"},{"english":"community support","chinese":"社區支援"},{"english":"whereas","chinese":"而；然而"},{"english":"destroy a household's income","chinese":"摧毀一個家庭的收入"},{"english":"household income","chinese":"家庭收入"},{"english":"simple life","chinese":"簡單生活"},{"english":"depends on","chinese":"取決於"},{"english":"preventable misery","chinese":"可避免的苦難"},{"english":"personal freedom","chinese":"個人自由"},{"english":"previous generations","chinese":"以往幾代人"},{"english":"be trapped by","chinese":"被……困住"},{"english":"rigid expectations","chinese":"僵化的期望"},{"english":"gender, class, marriage, religion, and work","chinese":"性別、階級、婚姻、宗教和工作"},{"english":"appeared content","chinese":"看似滿足"},{"english":"inner happiness","chinese":"內心幸福"},{"english":"be more able to","chinese":"更有能力去……"},{"english":"career, partner, lifestyle, and beliefs","chinese":"事業、伴侶、生活方式和信念"},{"english":"create pressure","chinese":"造成壓力"},{"english":"gives individuals room to","chinese":"給予個人空間去……"},{"english":"build a life","chinese":"建立一種生活"},{"english":"actually fits them","chinese":"真正適合他們"},{"english":"study abroad","chinese":"到外國留學"},{"english":"start a business","chinese":"創業"},{"english":"delay marriage","chinese":"延遲結婚"},{"english":"far more freedom","chinese":"多得多的自由"},{"english":"small luxury","chinese":"小小的奢侈品"},{"english":"one of the foundations of","chinese":"……的基礎之一"},{"english":"genuine fulfilment","chinese":"真正的滿足感"},{"english":"completely reject the idea that","chinese":"完全否定……的想法"},{"english":"look peaceful from a distance","chinese":"從遠處看似平靜"},{"english":"greater security","chinese":"更大的安全保障"},{"english":"human dignity","chinese":"人性尊嚴"},{"english":"true happiness","chinese":"真正幸福"},{"english":"more attainable","chinese":"更容易達到"}]},"model-essay-18-ielts-advantage-disadvantage":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-18-ielts-advantage-disadvantage","essayKey":"advantage-disadvantage:18","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-18-ielts-advantage-disadvantage","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/advantage-and-disadvantage/EdmundBd9AdDisAd-Q18","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"Economic development is widely seen as one of the most effective ways to raise living standards. Although rapid growth can weaken values such as community spirit and family cohesion, I firmly believe that its advantages clearly outweigh its disadvantages because it reduces material hardship and gives governments the means to improve essential public services.","chinese":"經濟發展普遍被視為提升生活水準最有效的方法之一。 儘管快速增長可能削弱社區精神和家庭凝聚力等價值， 我仍然堅信其優點明顯大於缺點，因為它不但能減輕物質匱乏，還能讓政府有能力改善關鍵的公共服務。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"The principal advantage of economic development is that it improves people’s lives in immediate, practical ways. As industries expand and businesses invest, more jobs are created, which allows families to earn stable incomes rather than merely get by. With higher earnings, people can afford better housing, more nutritious food and adequate medical care. At the same time, stronger economic activity generates more tax revenue, enabling governments to build schools, hospitals and transport systems. In many developing regions, for example, growth has brought clean water, reliable electricity and wider access to education, transforming daily life from the ground up.","chinese":"經濟發展最主要的優點，是它能以直接而實際的方式改善人們的生活。 當產業擴張、企業增加投資時，就會創造更多就業機會，讓家庭能夠獲得穩定收入，而不只是勉強維生。 有了更高的收入，人們便能負擔更好的住房、更有營養的食物，以及足夠的醫療照顧。 例如，當父母從收入不穩定的低薪工作轉為穩定就業時，他們的孩子通常更有可能享有更健康的飲食和更可靠的醫療照顧。 同時，更活躍的經濟活動也會帶來更多稅收，使政府能夠興建學校、醫院和交通系統。 這意味著，經濟增長不僅能在家庭層面提升生活水準，也能在整體社會層面帶來改善。 例如，在許多發展中地區，經濟增長帶來了潔淨的供水、穩定的電力，以及更廣泛的教育機會，從根本上改變了人們的日常生活。 因此，經濟發展以廣泛而明確的方式，為個人和整個社會帶來了實質的物質利益。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"Admittedly, economic progress can come at a social cost. In fast-paced, competitive societies, people often work longer hours, relocate for employment and become more preoccupied with personal success. As a result, values such as neighbourliness, family duty and collective responsibility may gradually fade into the background. For instance, in rapidly expanding cities, adult children may move away for work, leaving elderly parents with less day-to-day support. Consumerism can also encourage the belief that a person’s worth is measured mainly by income. Even so, these losses, serious as they are, do not outweigh the gains. Social values are not gone beyond repair; they can be strengthened through education, family upbringing and public policy, whereas poverty and poor public services cause deeper and more lasting harm.","chinese":"誠然，經濟進步也可能伴隨社會代價。 在節奏快速、競爭激烈的社會中，人們往往工時更長、因工作而搬遷，並且更加執著於個人成就。 結果，鄰里情誼、家庭責任和集體責任等價值，便可能逐漸退居次要位置。 例如，在快速擴張的城市中，成年子女可能因工作而搬離家鄉，令年長父母在日常生活中得到更少照顧與支持。 消費主義也可能助長一種觀念：一個人的價值主要是以收入來衡量的。 當金錢成就成為主要衡量標準時，善良、忠誠和公共精神等品質便可能不再受到同等重視。 這一點可見於某些人會自然而然地崇拜財富，即使那些財富是以犧牲家庭生活或社區責任為代價換來的。 即便如此，這些社會損失雖然嚴重，仍不足以超過經濟發展所帶來的好處，特別是因為這些價值仍可透過教育、家庭培養和公共政策重新加以強化。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, while economic development may erode some important social values, its overall impact is far more positive. By reducing poverty and funding better public services, it improves quality of life on a scale that the disadvantages do not surpass.","chinese":"總結來說，雖然經濟發展可能侵蝕一些重要的社會價值，但它的整體影響仍然遠較正面 透過減少貧窮並為更完善的公共服務提供資金，它在大規模上提升了生活品質，而這是其缺點所無法超越的。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"economic development","chinese":"經濟發展"},{"english":"be widely seen as","chinese":"被廣泛視為"},{"english":"one of the most effective ways to","chinese":"……最有效的方法之一"},{"english":"raise living standards","chinese":"提高生活水平"},{"english":"rapid growth","chinese":"快速增長"},{"english":"weaken values","chinese":"削弱價值觀"},{"english":"community spirit","chinese":"社區精神"},{"english":"family cohesion","chinese":"家庭凝聚力"},{"english":"clearly outweigh","chinese":"明顯大於"},{"english":"material hardship","chinese":"物質困難"},{"english":"gives governments the means to","chinese":"令政府有能力去"},{"english":"essential public services","chinese":"必要公共服務"},{"english":"the principal advantage of","chinese":"……的主要好處"},{"english":"immediate, practical ways","chinese":"即時而實際的方式"},{"english":"industries expand","chinese":"產業擴展"},{"english":"businesses invest","chinese":"企業投資"},{"english":"stable incomes","chinese":"穩定收入"},{"english":"rather than merely get by","chinese":"而不是僅僅勉強過活"},{"english":"get by","chinese":"勉強過活"},{"english":"higher earnings","chinese":"更高收入"},{"english":"afford better housing","chinese":"負擔得起更好的住屋"},{"english":"more nutritious food","chinese":"更有營養的食物"},{"english":"adequate medical care","chinese":"足夠的醫療護理"},{"english":"at the same time","chinese":"同時"},{"english":"stronger economic activity","chinese":"更強的經濟活動"},{"english":"tax revenue","chinese":"稅務收入"},{"english":"enabling governments to","chinese":"使政府能夠"},{"english":"transport systems","chinese":"交通系統"},{"english":"developing regions","chinese":"發展中地區"},{"english":"clean water","chinese":"清潔食水"},{"english":"reliable electricity","chinese":"可靠電力供應"},{"english":"wider access to education","chinese":"更廣泛的教育機會"},{"english":"transform daily life","chinese":"改變日常生活"},{"english":"from the ground up","chinese":"從根本上"},{"english":"admittedly","chinese":"無可否認"},{"english":"economic progress","chinese":"經濟進步"},{"english":"come at a social cost","chinese":"付出社會代價"},{"english":"fast-paced, competitive societies","chinese":"節奏急速、競爭激烈的社會"},{"english":"work longer hours","chinese":"工作時間更長"},{"english":"relocate for employment","chinese":"為工作而搬遷"},{"english":"become more preoccupied with","chinese":"變得更專注於"},{"english":"personal success","chinese":"個人成就"},{"english":"as a result","chinese":"因此"},{"english":"neighbourliness","chinese":"鄰里情誼"},{"english":"family duty","chinese":"家庭責任"},{"english":"collective responsibility","chinese":"集體責任"},{"english":"gradually fade into the background","chinese":"逐漸被淡化"},{"english":"rapidly expanding cities","chinese":"急速擴張的城市"},{"english":"move away for work","chinese":"因工作而搬離"},{"english":"elderly parents","chinese":"年老父母"},{"english":"day-to-day support","chinese":"日常支援"},{"english":"consumerism","chinese":"消費主義"},{"english":"encourage the belief that","chinese":"鼓勵一種……的信念"},{"english":"a person's worth","chinese":"一個人的價值"},{"english":"be measured mainly by","chinese":"主要以……衡量"},{"english":"even so","chinese":"即使如此"},{"english":"serious as they are","chinese":"儘管它們很嚴重"},{"english":"the gains","chinese":"得益；好處"},{"english":"beyond repair","chinese":"無法修復"},{"english":"be strengthened through","chinese":"透過……加強"},{"english":"family upbringing","chinese":"家庭教養"},{"english":"public policy","chinese":"公共政策"},{"english":"poverty","chinese":"貧窮"},{"english":"poor public services","chinese":"差劣的公共服務"},{"english":"deeper and more lasting harm","chinese":"更深遠和更持久的傷害"},{"english":"erode important social values","chinese":"侵蝕重要社會價值"},{"english":"overall impact","chinese":"整體影響"},{"english":"far more positive","chinese":"正面得多"},{"english":"reducing poverty","chinese":"減少貧窮"},{"english":"funding better public services","chinese":"資助更好的公共服務"},{"english":"quality of life","chinese":"生活質素"},{"english":"on a scale that","chinese":"以……的規模"},{"english":"do not surpass","chinese":"不會超過"}]},"model-essay-18-ielts-cause-solution":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-18-ielts-cause-solution","essayKey":"cause-solution:18","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-18-ielts-cause-solution","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/problem-and-cause/EdmundBd9CnS-Q18","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"In many modern societies, work has expanded beyond the office and begun to crowd out family, rest and personal growth. This problem is usually caused by unrealistic workplace expectations and weakened boundaries between professional and private life. It can be reduced if employers design healthier systems and individuals learn to protect their time deliberately.","chinese":"在許多現代社會中，工作已經延伸到辦公室之外，並開始擠壓家庭、休息和個人成長的空間。 這個問題通常是由不切實際的職場期望，以及工作生活與私人生活之間界線變得薄弱所造成的。 如果僱主能設計更健康的工作制度，而個人也學會有意識地保護自己的時間，這個問題便可以得到減輕。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"One major reason is that many employees are expected to be constantly available. Emails, messaging apps and online meetings allow work to follow people home, so the end of the working day no longer feels like a real end. As a result, a person may be physically with their family but mentally still at their desk. Another cause is financial pressure. When housing, childcare and daily expenses are high, people often accept overtime, second jobs or heavier workloads, even when these choices damage their health. Over time, this creates a cycle in which tired workers perform less efficiently, need more time to finish tasks, and lose even more of their personal lives.","chinese":"其中一個主要原因是，許多員工被期望隨時都能回應工作。 電子郵件、即時通訊應用程式和線上會議讓工作可以跟著人們回到家中，因此工作日的結束不再感覺像真正的結束。 結果是，一個人身體上可能和家人在一起，但精神上仍然停留在辦公桌前。 另一個原因是經濟壓力。 當住房、育兒和日常開支高昂時，人們即使知道這些選擇會損害健康，也往往會接受加班、第二份工作或更沉重的工作量。 長遠而言，這會形成一個循環：疲憊的員工工作效率下降，需要更多時間完成任務，並失去更多私人生活。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"The most effective solution is for employers to set clearer limits on work. For instance, companies can discourage non-urgent messages after office hours, monitor excessive overtime and give staff more control over when and where they work. These measures do not simply make employees happier; they also help them return to work with sharper concentration and better judgement. At the same time, individuals need to manage their own routines more firmly. This may mean setting fixed times for exercise, family meals or sleep, and treating these commitments as seriously as meetings with clients. Without such boundaries, personal life becomes the first thing to be sacrificed.","chinese":"最有效的解決方法是讓僱主為工作設立更清晰的界線。 例如，公司可以不鼓勵員工在辦公時間後發送非緊急訊息、監察過度加班的情況，並讓員工對自己的工作時間和工作地點有更多掌控權。 這些措施不只是讓員工更快樂；它們也能幫助員工以更敏銳的專注力和更好的判斷力重新投入工作。 同時，個人也需要更堅定地管理自己的日常安排。 這可能意味著為運動、家庭用餐或睡眠設定固定時間，並像對待與客戶的會議一樣認真看待這些承諾。 如果沒有這些界線，私人生活就會成為最先被犧牲的東西。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, poor work-life balance is mainly the result of constant connectivity, high workplace demands and financial pressure. However, it can be overcome when organisations create more humane working conditions and individuals draw a clearer line between their jobs and the rest of their lives.","chinese":"總結來說，糟糕的工作與生活平衡主要是由持續連線、高度職場要求和經濟壓力所造成的。 然而，當機構創造更人性化的工作條件，而個人也在工作和生活其他部分之間劃出更清晰的界線時，這個問題便可以被克服。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"modern societies","chinese":"現代社會"},{"english":"expanded beyond","chinese":"擴展至……之外"},{"english":"crowd out","chinese":"擠走；排擠掉"},{"english":"personal growth","chinese":"個人成長"},{"english":"unrealistic workplace expectations","chinese":"不切實際的職場期望"},{"english":"weakened boundaries between","chinese":"……之間變得薄弱的界線"},{"english":"professional and private life","chinese":"工作與私人生活"},{"english":"design healthier systems","chinese":"設計更健康的制度"},{"english":"protect their time deliberately","chinese":"有意識地保護自己的時間"},{"english":"one major reason","chinese":"一個主要原因"},{"english":"constantly available","chinese":"隨時候命"},{"english":"messaging apps","chinese":"通訊應用程式"},{"english":"online meetings","chinese":"網上會議"},{"english":"allow work to follow people home","chinese":"令工作跟着人回家"},{"english":"the working day","chinese":"工作日；工作時間"},{"english":"no longer feels like","chinese":"不再感覺像……"},{"english":"a real end","chinese":"真正的結束"},{"english":"as a result","chinese":"因此；結果"},{"english":"physically with their family","chinese":"身體上與家人在一起"},{"english":"mentally still at their desk","chinese":"精神上仍在工作"},{"english":"financial pressure","chinese":"經濟壓力"},{"english":"daily expenses","chinese":"日常開支"},{"english":"accept overtime","chinese":"接受加班"},{"english":"second jobs","chinese":"第二份工作"},{"english":"heavier workloads","chinese":"更沉重的工作量"},{"english":"damage their health","chinese":"損害健康"},{"english":"over time","chinese":"隨時間；久而久之"},{"english":"creates a cycle in which","chinese":"形成一個……的循環"},{"english":"tired workers","chinese":"疲累的員工"},{"english":"perform less efficiently","chinese":"工作效率較低"},{"english":"finish tasks","chinese":"完成任務"},{"english":"lose even more of","chinese":"失去更多……"},{"english":"the most effective solution","chinese":"最有效的解決方法"},{"english":"set clearer limits on","chinese":"為……設定更清晰的限制"},{"english":"discourage non-urgent messages","chinese":"不鼓勵非緊急訊息"},{"english":"after office hours","chinese":"辦公時間後"},{"english":"monitor excessive overtime","chinese":"監察過度加班"},{"english":"give staff more control over","chinese":"讓員工對……有更多控制權"},{"english":"when and where they work","chinese":"工作時間和地點"},{"english":"these measures","chinese":"這些措施"},{"english":"sharper concentration","chinese":"更敏銳的專注力"},{"english":"better judgement","chinese":"更好的判斷力"},{"english":"at the same time","chinese":"同時"},{"english":"manage their own routines","chinese":"管理自己的日常安排"},{"english":"more firmly","chinese":"更堅定地"},{"english":"setting fixed times for","chinese":"為……設定固定時間"},{"english":"family meals","chinese":"家庭用餐時間"},{"english":"treating these commitments as seriously as","chinese":"像對待……一樣認真對待這些承諾"},{"english":"meetings with clients","chinese":"與客戶的會議"},{"english":"such boundaries","chinese":"這樣的界線"},{"english":"personal life","chinese":"私人生活"},{"english":"the first thing to be sacrificed","chinese":"第一個被犧牲的東西"},{"english":"poor work-life balance","chinese":"差劣的工作與生活平衡"},{"english":"constant connectivity","chinese":"持續連線狀態"},{"english":"high workplace demands","chinese":"高職場要求"},{"english":"be overcome","chinese":"被克服"},{"english":"humane working conditions","chinese":"更人性化的工作條件"},{"english":"draw a clearer line between","chinese":"在……之間劃出更清晰的界線"},{"english":"the rest of their lives","chinese":"生活的其他部分"}]},"model-essay-18-ielts-direct-question":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-18-ielts-direct-question","essayKey":"direct-question:18","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-18-ielts-direct-question","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/direct-question/EdmundBd9Dir-Q18","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"As forests are cleared, cities expand, and wildlife is hunted for profit, many species are being pushed out of the ecosystems that once sustained them. I believe protecting animals is essential, not merely for sentimental reasons but because their survival is tied to ecological stability and, ultimately, human welfare.","chinese":"隨著森林被砍伐、城市不斷擴張，以及野生動物因牟利而被獵殺，許多物種正被迫離開曾經支撐它們生存的生態系統。 我認為保護動物是必要的，這並不只是出於情感上的原因，而是因為牠們的生存與生態穩定息息相關，並最終關乎人類福祉。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"The first reason animals must be protected is that they form part of a delicate natural balance. When one species disappears, the effect rarely stops there; it can ripple through the food chain and weaken an entire habitat. For instance, if predators are removed from a forest, smaller animals may multiply too quickly, damage vegetation, and reduce the food available for other species. In this sense, extinction is not just the loss of one creature; it is a crack in a much larger living system. Protecting animals therefore helps preserve the environmental conditions on which human beings also depend.","chinese":"動物必須受到保護的第一個原因是，牠們構成了脆弱自然平衡的一部分。 當一個物種消失時，其影響很少會就此停止；它可能會沿著食物鏈擴散，並削弱整個棲息地。 例如，如果捕食者從森林中消失，較小型的動物可能會繁殖得過快、破壞植被，並減少其他物種可獲得的食物。 從這個意義上說，滅絕並不只是失去一種生物；它是一個更龐大的生命系統中出現的一道裂縫。 因此，保護動物有助於維持人類同樣依賴的環境條件。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"Several practical measures can be taken to address this problem. Governments should first create and enforce stronger protected areas, where logging, construction, and hunting are strictly controlled. Such laws, however, must be more than words on paper: rangers need proper funding, illegal hunters must face serious penalties, and companies that destroy habitats should be held financially responsible. At the same time, conservation will be more effective if local communities are given a real stake in it. When people can earn income through eco-tourism, sustainable farming, or conservation-related jobs, they are less likely to see wildlife as an obstacle to survival.","chinese":"可以採取幾項實際措施來處理這個問題。 政府首先應該建立並執行更強力的保護區制度，在這些區域內，伐木、建設和狩獵都受到嚴格管制。 然而，這些法律不能只是紙上文字：護林員需要充足資金，非法獵人必須面對嚴厲懲罰，而破壞棲息地的公司亦應承擔財務責任。 同時，如果當地社區能夠在保育工作中擁有真正的利益，保育便會更加有效。 當人們能夠透過生態旅遊、可持續農業，或與保育相關的工作獲得收入時，他們便較不會把野生動物視為生存的障礙。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, animal protection is highly important because endangered species are part of the natural foundation that supports life itself. The most effective response is not a single dramatic solution, but a combination of strict legal protection, responsible land use, and community involvement.","chinese":"總結來說，動物保護非常重要，因為瀕危物種是支撐生命本身的自然基礎的一部分。 最有效的應對方法並不是某一個戲劇性的單一方案，而是結合嚴格的法律保護、負責任的土地使用，以及社區參與。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"As forests are cleared","chinese":"隨着森林被砍伐"},{"english":"cities expand","chinese":"城市擴張"},{"english":"wildlife is hunted for profit","chinese":"野生動物被獵殺牟利"},{"english":"many species","chinese":"許多物種"},{"english":"be pushed out of","chinese":"被迫離開……"},{"english":"ecosystems that once sustained them","chinese":"曾經維持牠們生存的生態系統"},{"english":"protecting animals","chinese":"保護動物"},{"english":"not merely for sentimental reasons","chinese":"不只是出於感情原因"},{"english":"be tied to","chinese":"與……息息相關"},{"english":"ecological stability","chinese":"生態穩定"},{"english":"ultimately","chinese":"最終"},{"english":"human welfare","chinese":"人類福祉"},{"english":"form part of","chinese":"是……的一部分"},{"english":"a delicate natural balance","chinese":"脆弱的自然平衡"},{"english":"one species disappears","chinese":"一個物種消失"},{"english":"the effect rarely stops there","chinese":"影響很少就此停止"},{"english":"ripple through","chinese":"波及；連鎖影響"},{"english":"the food chain","chinese":"食物鏈"},{"english":"weaken an entire habitat","chinese":"削弱整個棲息地"},{"english":"predators are removed from","chinese":"掠食者被從……移除"},{"english":"multiply too quickly","chinese":"繁殖得太快"},{"english":"damage vegetation","chinese":"破壞植被"},{"english":"reduce the food available for","chinese":"減少可供……的食物"},{"english":"in this sense","chinese":"從這個意義上說"},{"english":"extinction","chinese":"物種滅絕"},{"english":"the loss of one creature","chinese":"失去一種生物"},{"english":"a crack in","chinese":"……中的裂痕"},{"english":"a much larger living system","chinese":"更大的生命系統"},{"english":"helps preserve","chinese":"有助保護"},{"english":"environmental conditions","chinese":"環境條件"},{"english":"depend on","chinese":"依賴"},{"english":"practical measures","chinese":"實際措施"},{"english":"address this problem","chinese":"處理這個問題"},{"english":"create and enforce","chinese":"建立並執行"},{"english":"protected areas","chinese":"保護區"},{"english":"logging, construction, and hunting","chinese":"伐木、建築工程和狩獵"},{"english":"strictly controlled","chinese":"受到嚴格管制"},{"english":"laws must be more than words on paper","chinese":"法律不能只是紙上談兵"},{"english":"rangers","chinese":"護林員；巡護員"},{"english":"proper funding","chinese":"充足資金"},{"english":"illegal hunters","chinese":"非法獵人"},{"english":"face serious penalties","chinese":"面對嚴厲懲罰"},{"english":"destroy habitats","chinese":"破壞棲息地"},{"english":"be held financially responsible","chinese":"被追究經濟責任"},{"english":"conservation","chinese":"保育"},{"english":"local communities","chinese":"本地社區"},{"english":"be given a real stake in","chinese":"在……中有實質利益"},{"english":"earn income through","chinese":"透過……賺取收入"},{"english":"eco-tourism","chinese":"生態旅遊"},{"english":"sustainable farming","chinese":"可持續農業"},{"english":"conservation-related jobs","chinese":"與保育相關的工作"},{"english":"be less likely to","chinese":"較不可能"},{"english":"see wildlife as an obstacle to survival","chinese":"視野生動物為生存障礙"},{"english":"endangered species","chinese":"瀕危物種"},{"english":"the natural foundation that supports life","chinese":"支撐生命的自然基礎"},{"english":"the most effective response","chinese":"最有效的回應"},{"english":"a single dramatic solution","chinese":"單一而轟動的解決方法"},{"english":"a combination of","chinese":"……的結合"},{"english":"strict legal protection","chinese":"嚴格的法律保護"},{"english":"responsible land use","chinese":"負責任的土地使用"},{"english":"community involvement","chinese":"社區參與"}]},"model-essay-18-ielts-discuss-both-views":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-18-ielts-discuss-both-views","essayKey":"discuss-both-views:18","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-18-ielts-discuss-both-views","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/discuss-both-views-your-opinion/EdmundBd9ExpBth-Q18","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"Learning does not stop at any fixed age; it remains valuable even in later life. While some people argue that people over 65 are too old to acquire new knowledge or skills, I completely disagree. In my view, older people benefit greatly from learning because it keeps their minds active and allows them to live more independent, meaningful lives.","chinese":"學習不會在任何固定年齡停止；即使在人生後期，它仍然具有價值。 雖然有人認為65歲以上的人年紀太大，已經無法獲得新知識或新技能，但我完全不同意 在我看來，較年長的人能從學習中獲得很大益處，因為學習能使他們的思維保持活躍，並讓他們過上更獨立、更有意義的生活。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"The first reason is that learning something new gives elderly people a strong mental and emotional lift. Many retirees suddenly lose the daily structure that work once provided, so their days can become repetitive and empty. When they learn a language, musical instrument, digital skill or craft, they are not merely filling time; they are giving their minds a fresh challenge. This kind of challenge encourages concentration, patience and problem-solving, which can help them feel capable rather than forgotten. For example, an older person who joins a painting class may begin with shaky confidence, but over time the process of improving can become a quiet source of pride. In this sense, learning acts like a light being switched on in a room that had been growing dim.","chinese":"第一個原因是，學習新事物能給長者帶來強大的精神和情感提升。 許多退休人士會突然失去過去由工作所提供的日常結構，因此他們的日子可能變得重複而空洞。 當他們學習一種語言、一種樂器、一項數碼技能或一門手藝時，他們不只是填補時間；他們是在給自己的頭腦一個新的挑戰。這種挑戰能促進專注力、耐性和解難能力，從而幫助他們感到自己仍然有能力，而不是被遺忘。 例如，一位參加繪畫班的長者起初可能信心不足，但隨著時間過去，不斷進步的過程可以成為一種安靜而穩定的自豪感來源。 從這個意義上說，學習就像在一個逐漸變暗的房間裡打開了一盞燈。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"Another important benefit is that new skills help older people stay connected with modern society. The world changes quickly, especially through technology, and those who refuse to learn may become increasingly dependent on others. If senior citizens learn how to use smartphones, online banking or video calls, they can communicate with family, manage daily tasks and participate more fully in community life. This is not a small advantage; it protects their dignity. For instance, a grandmother who learns to use video chat can speak to her grandchildren abroad instead of feeling cut off from them. Such learning builds a bridge between generations.","chinese":"另一個重要好處是，新技能能幫助較年長的人與現代社會保持聯繫。 世界變化很快，尤其是在科技方面，而那些拒絕學習的人可能會越來越依賴他人。 如果長者學會使用智能手機、網上銀行或視像通話，他們便能與家人溝通、處理日常事務，並更充分地參與社區生活。 這並不是一個小小的優勢；它保護了他們的尊嚴。 例如，一位學會使用視像聊天的祖母，可以和身在海外的孫兒女說話，而不是感到與他們隔絕。 這樣的學習在不同世代之間建立了一座橋樑。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, it is never too late for older people to learn. After 65, learning is not a luxury; it is one of the best ways to preserve confidence, independence and a sense of purpose.","chinese":"總結來說，對較年長的人而言，學習永遠不會太遲。 65歲以後，學習並不是一種奢侈；它是維持自信、獨立和人生目標感的最佳方法之一。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"learning does not stop at","chinese":"學習不會在……停止"},{"english":"any fixed age","chinese":"任何固定年齡"},{"english":"remain valuable","chinese":"仍然有價值"},{"english":"in later life","chinese":"晚年；人生較後階段"},{"english":"people over 65","chinese":"65歲以上人士"},{"english":"too old to acquire","chinese":"年紀太大而不能學習"},{"english":"acquire new knowledge or skills","chinese":"學習新知識或技能"},{"english":"completely disagree","chinese":"完全不同意"},{"english":"in my view","chinese":"在我看來"},{"english":"benefit greatly from","chinese":"從……大大受惠"},{"english":"keep their minds active","chinese":"保持頭腦活躍"},{"english":"live more independent, meaningful lives","chinese":"過更獨立、更有意義的生活"},{"english":"the first reason","chinese":"第一個原因"},{"english":"elderly people","chinese":"長者"},{"english":"a strong mental and emotional lift","chinese":"精神和情緒上的強大提升"},{"english":"retirees","chinese":"退休人士"},{"english":"daily structure","chinese":"日常規律"},{"english":"work once provided","chinese":"工作曾經提供"},{"english":"repetitive and empty","chinese":"重複而空虛"},{"english":"learn a language","chinese":"學習一種語言"},{"english":"musical instrument","chinese":"樂器"},{"english":"digital skill","chinese":"數碼技能"},{"english":"craft","chinese":"手工藝"},{"english":"not merely filling time","chinese":"不只是消磨時間"},{"english":"a fresh challenge","chinese":"新鮮挑戰"},{"english":"this kind of challenge","chinese":"這種挑戰"},{"english":"encourage concentration","chinese":"促進專注"},{"english":"patience and problem-solving","chinese":"耐性和解難能力"},{"english":"feel capable rather than forgotten","chinese":"感到有能力，而不是被遺忘"},{"english":"joins a painting class","chinese":"參加繪畫班"},{"english":"begin with shaky confidence","chinese":"起初信心不足"},{"english":"over time","chinese":"隨時間"},{"english":"the process of improving","chinese":"進步的過程"},{"english":"a quiet source of pride","chinese":"默默的自豪感來源"},{"english":"in this sense","chinese":"從這個意義上說"},{"english":"acts like","chinese":"像……一樣發揮作用"},{"english":"a light being switched on","chinese":"一盞被打開的燈"},{"english":"growing dim","chinese":"逐漸變暗"},{"english":"another important benefit","chinese":"另一個重要好處"},{"english":"stay connected with","chinese":"與……保持聯繫"},{"english":"modern society","chinese":"現代社會"},{"english":"the world changes quickly","chinese":"世界變化迅速"},{"english":"especially through technology","chinese":"尤其透過科技"},{"english":"refuse to learn","chinese":"拒絕學習"},{"english":"become increasingly dependent on","chinese":"變得越來越依賴"},{"english":"senior citizens","chinese":"長者"},{"english":"smartphones","chinese":"智能手機"},{"english":"online banking","chinese":"網上銀行"},{"english":"video calls","chinese":"視像通話"},{"english":"communicate with family","chinese":"與家人溝通"},{"english":"manage daily tasks","chinese":"處理日常事務"},{"english":"participate more fully in","chinese":"更全面地參與"},{"english":"community life","chinese":"社區生活"},{"english":"not a small advantage","chinese":"這不是小小的好處"},{"english":"protect their dignity","chinese":"保護他們的尊嚴"},{"english":"use video chat","chinese":"使用視像聊天"},{"english":"grandchildren abroad","chinese":"海外的孫兒女"},{"english":"instead of feeling cut off from","chinese":"而不是感到與……隔絕"},{"english":"such learning","chinese":"這種學習"},{"english":"build a bridge between generations","chinese":"在世代之間建立橋樑"},{"english":"it is never too late for","chinese":"對……來說永遠不會太遲"},{"english":"after 65","chinese":"65歲之後"},{"english":"not a luxury","chinese":"不是奢侈品"},{"english":"one of the best ways to","chinese":"……的最佳方法之一"},{"english":"preserve confidence","chinese":"保持信心"},{"english":"independence","chinese":"獨立性"},{"english":"a sense of purpose","chinese":"目標感"}]},"model-essay-18-ielts-opinion":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-18-ielts-opinion","essayKey":"opinion:18","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-18-ielts-opinion","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/opinions/EdmundBd9OP-Q18","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"Stress has always been part of human life, and each generation has carried its own burdens. However, I completely disagree that people in previous generations were more stressed than people are today. Modern life, in my view, creates a more constant form of pressure because work is harder to escape and personal success is now judged against endless social comparison.","chinese":"壓力一直都是人類生活的一部分，而每一代人也都承受著各自的負擔。 然而，我完全不同意過去幾代人比今天的人承受更大壓力這一說法。 在我看來，現代生活製造了一種更持續的壓力，因為工作變得更難擺脫，而個人成就如今也會被放在無止境的社會比較之中衡量。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"The first reason is that modern work follows people far beyond the workplace. In the past, many jobs were physically exhausting, but once the working day ended, responsibilities were more likely to stop at the factory gate, the shop door, or the family farm. By contrast, many employees today are expected to answer messages, check emails and remain reachable even at home. This turns rest into another extension of work. For example, an office worker may leave the office at six, yet still feel anxious whenever a phone notification appears at night. Over time, this constant alertness can damage sleep, weaken concentration and make people feel that they are never truly off duty.","chinese":"第一個原因是，現代工作會跟隨人們遠遠超出工作場所本身。 在過去，許多工作在體力上令人疲憊，但一旦工作日結束，責任往往更有可能停留在工廠大門、店鋪門口或家庭農場之內。 相比之下，今天許多員工即使在家中，也被期望回覆訊息、查看電郵，並保持隨時可聯絡的狀態。 這使休息變成了工作的另一種延伸。 例如，一位辦公室員工可能六點已經離開公司，但每當晚上手機通知出現時，仍然會感到焦慮。 長遠而言，這種持續的警覺狀態會損害睡眠、削弱專注力，並令人覺得自己從未真正下班。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"Another major cause of stress today is the pressure to compare one’s life with others. Previous generations usually judged success against people in their immediate community, whereas people today are exposed to carefully polished versions of other people’s achievements, relationships and lifestyles. Social media can make an ordinary person feel inadequate even when nothing is seriously wrong with their own life. For instance, a student may feel unsuccessful simply because classmates appear to be winning prizes, travelling abroad or building impressive careers online. This quiet psychological pressure is easy to dismiss, but it can weigh heavily on self-esteem and mental health.","chinese":"今天另一個主要的壓力來源，是人們將自己的生活與他人比較的壓力。 過去幾代人通常是與自己身邊社區的人比較成功，而今天的人卻會接觸到別人被精心美化過的成就、關係和生活方式。 社交媒體可以使一個普通人在自己的生活並沒有嚴重問題的情況下，仍然感到自己不夠好。 例如，一名學生可能只是因為同學在網上看起來正在獲獎、到海外旅行，或建立令人印象深刻的事業，便覺得自己不成功。 這種安靜的心理壓力很容易被忽視，但可能會沉重地壓在一個人的自尊和心理健康之上"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, I fully disagree with the view that earlier generations were more stressed. They faced real hardship, but modern people live under pressure that is more continuous, more visible and far harder to switch off.","chinese":"總結來說，我完全不同意較早幾代人壓力更大的觀點。 他們確實面對真實的艱難處境，但現代人生活在一種更持續、更明顯，而且更難關掉的壓力之下。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"stress","chinese":"壓力"},{"english":"part of human life","chinese":"人類生活的一部分"},{"english":"each generation","chinese":"每一代人"},{"english":"carried its own burdens","chinese":"承受自己的負擔"},{"english":"previous generations","chinese":"以往幾代人"},{"english":"more stressed than","chinese":"比……壓力更大"},{"english":"in my view","chinese":"在我看來"},{"english":"constant form of pressure","chinese":"更持續的壓力形式"},{"english":"harder to escape","chinese":"更難逃離"},{"english":"personal success","chinese":"個人成功"},{"english":"be judged against","chinese":"以……作標準評價"},{"english":"endless social comparison","chinese":"無休止的社會比較"},{"english":"modern work","chinese":"現代工作"},{"english":"follows people far beyond","chinese":"遠遠跟隨人們超出……"},{"english":"the workplace","chinese":"工作場所"},{"english":"in the past","chinese":"在過去"},{"english":"physically exhausting","chinese":"體力上令人筋疲力盡"},{"english":"working day ended","chinese":"工作日結束"},{"english":"be more likely to","chinese":"更有可能"},{"english":"factory gate","chinese":"工廠大門"},{"english":"shop door","chinese":"店舖門口"},{"english":"family farm","chinese":"家庭農場"},{"english":"by contrast","chinese":"相比之下"},{"english":"be expected to","chinese":"被期望去……"},{"english":"answer messages","chinese":"回覆訊息"},{"english":"check emails","chinese":"查看電郵"},{"english":"remain reachable","chinese":"隨時可聯絡"},{"english":"even at home","chinese":"即使在家中"},{"english":"turns rest into","chinese":"將休息變成……"},{"english":"extension of work","chinese":"工作的延伸"},{"english":"office worker","chinese":"辦公室員工"},{"english":"feel anxious","chinese":"感到焦慮"},{"english":"phone notification","chinese":"手機通知"},{"english":"appears at night","chinese":"在晚上出現"},{"english":"over time","chinese":"隨着時間過去"},{"english":"constant alertness","chinese":"持續警覺"},{"english":"damage sleep","chinese":"損害睡眠"},{"english":"weaken concentration","chinese":"削弱專注力"},{"english":"truly off duty","chinese":"真正下班；真正不用當值"},{"english":"major cause of stress","chinese":"壓力的主要成因"},{"english":"compare one's life with others","chinese":"將自己的生活與別人比較"},{"english":"judged success against","chinese":"以……衡量成功"},{"english":"immediate community","chinese":"身邊社群"},{"english":"whereas","chinese":"而；然而"},{"english":"be exposed to","chinese":"接觸到……"},{"english":"carefully polished versions of","chinese":"經精心修飾的……版本"},{"english":"achievements, relationships and lifestyles","chinese":"成就、關係和生活方式"},{"english":"social media","chinese":"社交媒體"},{"english":"ordinary person","chinese":"普通人"},{"english":"feel inadequate","chinese":"覺得自己不足"},{"english":"even when","chinese":"即使在……時"},{"english":"nothing is seriously wrong with","chinese":"……沒有甚麼嚴重問題"},{"english":"feel unsuccessful","chinese":"感到不成功"},{"english":"simply because","chinese":"只是因為"},{"english":"appear to be","chinese":"看似正在……"},{"english":"winning prizes","chinese":"得獎"},{"english":"travelling abroad","chinese":"到外國旅行"},{"english":"building impressive careers","chinese":"建立令人羨慕的事業"},{"english":"quiet psychological pressure","chinese":"無聲的心理壓力"},{"english":"easy to dismiss","chinese":"容易被輕視"},{"english":"weigh heavily on","chinese":"對……造成沉重負擔"},{"english":"self-esteem","chinese":"自尊感"},{"english":"mental health","chinese":"精神健康"},{"english":"earlier generations","chinese":"較早幾代人"},{"english":"real hardship","chinese":"真正困難"},{"english":"live under pressure","chinese":"生活在壓力之下"},{"english":"more continuous","chinese":"更持續"},{"english":"more visible","chinese":"更明顯"},{"english":"far harder to switch off","chinese":"難得多去關掉"}]},"model-essay-19-ielts-advantage-disadvantage":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-19-ielts-advantage-disadvantage","essayKey":"advantage-disadvantage:19","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-19-ielts-advantage-disadvantage","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/advantage-and-disadvantage/EdmundBd9AdDisAd-Q19","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"Globalisation has become a defining feature of modern life, influencing how people trade, work, travel and consume culture. Although it can place pressure on local businesses and traditions, I believe its advantages are greater overall because it creates wider opportunities and brings societies into closer cooperation.","chinese":"全球化已成為現代生活的一個重要特徵，影響著人們如何貿易、工作、旅行，以及消費文化。 儘管它可能對本地企業和傳統造成壓力， 我認為整體而言，它的優點更大，因為全球化能創造更廣闊的機會，並使不同社會之間有更緊密的合作。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"One major disadvantage is that globalisation can weaken local economies. When international companies enter a country, small businesses may struggle to survive because they cannot match the prices, advertising power or supply networks of global brands. For example, a family-owned clothes shop may lose customers when a large foreign retailer opens nearby and sells similar products at lower prices. This can reduce local employment and make communities dependent on outside corporations. Another drawback is cultural dilution. If young people everywhere watch the same films, eat the same fast food and follow the same fashion trends, local customs may slowly fade into the background. In this sense, globalisation can sometimes make the world feel less like a garden of different flowers and more like one repeated pattern.","chinese":"全球化其中一個主要缺點是，它可能削弱本地經濟。 當國際企業進入一個國家時，小型企業可能難以生存，因為它們無法與全球品牌的價格、廣告能力或供應網絡競爭。 例如，當一間大型外國零售商在附近開業，並以更低價格出售類似產品時，一間家庭經營的服裝店可能會流失顧客。 這可能會減少本地就業機會，並使社區依賴外來企業。 另一個缺點是文化被淡化。 如果世界各地的年輕人都觀看相同的電影、吃相同的快餐，並追隨相同的時尚潮流，本地習俗便可能慢慢退到背景之中。 從這個意義上說，全球化有時會使世界不再像一個開滿不同花朵的花園，而更像是一個不斷重複的單一圖案。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"However, the benefits are more significant. Globalisation allows goods, knowledge and services to move across borders, which can improve people’s living standards. For instance, a hospital in a developing country may gain access to imported medical equipment, while students in poorer regions can use online courses created by overseas universities. These exchanges are not merely commercial; they can open doors that would otherwise remain closed. Globalisation also creates opportunities for workers and businesses. A small software company, for example, can sell its services to clients abroad instead of depending only on its local market. At the same time, contact between cultures can make people more open-minded, especially when they work, study or communicate with those from different backgrounds.","chinese":"然而，全球化的好處更加重要。 全球化使商品、知識和服務能夠跨越國界流動，這可以提升人們的生活水平。 例如，一間發展中國家的醫院可能可以獲得進口醫療設備，而較貧困地區的學生也可以使用海外大學製作的網上課程。 這些交流並不只是商業活動；它們能打開一些原本可能一直關上的大門。 全球化也為工人和企業創造機會。 例如，一間小型軟件公司可以把服務賣給海外客戶，而不是只依賴本地市場。 同時，文化之間的接觸也能使人變得更開明，尤其當他們與來自不同背景的人一起工作、學習或交流時。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, globalisation does have disadvantages, particularly for local businesses and cultural traditions. Nevertheless, I firmly believe it is positive overall because it spreads opportunity, knowledge and cooperation far more widely than a closed world ever could.","chinese":"總結來說，全球化確實有缺點，尤其是對本地企業和文化傳統而言。 然而，我堅定地認為，整體而言全球化是正面的，因為它比一個封閉的世界更能廣泛地傳播機會、知識和合作。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"globalisation","chinese":"全球化"},{"english":"a defining feature of","chinese":"……的標誌性特徵"},{"english":"modern life","chinese":"現代生活"},{"english":"influencing how people","chinese":"影響人們如何……"},{"english":"consume culture","chinese":"消費文化"},{"english":"place pressure on","chinese":"對……造成壓力"},{"english":"local businesses and traditions","chinese":"本地企業和傳統"},{"english":"greater overall","chinese":"整體而言更大"},{"english":"creates wider opportunities","chinese":"創造更廣泛的機會"},{"english":"brings societies into closer cooperation","chinese":"令社會之間更緊密合作"},{"english":"one major disadvantage","chinese":"一個主要缺點"},{"english":"weaken local economies","chinese":"削弱本地經濟"},{"english":"international companies","chinese":"跨國公司"},{"english":"enter a country","chinese":"進入一個國家"},{"english":"struggle to survive","chinese":"掙扎求存"},{"english":"match the prices","chinese":"與……的價格競爭"},{"english":"advertising power","chinese":"廣告力量"},{"english":"supply networks","chinese":"供應網絡"},{"english":"global brands","chinese":"全球品牌"},{"english":"a family-owned clothes shop","chinese":"家庭經營的服裝店"},{"english":"lose customers","chinese":"失去顧客"},{"english":"a large foreign retailer","chinese":"大型外國零售商"},{"english":"opens nearby","chinese":"在附近開業"},{"english":"similar products","chinese":"類似產品"},{"english":"at lower prices","chinese":"以較低價格"},{"english":"reduce local employment","chinese":"減少本地就業"},{"english":"make communities dependent on","chinese":"令社區依賴……"},{"english":"outside corporations","chinese":"外來企業"},{"english":"another drawback","chinese":"另一個缺點"},{"english":"cultural dilution","chinese":"文化淡化"},{"english":"follow the same fashion trends","chinese":"追隨相同的時尚潮流"},{"english":"local customs","chinese":"本地習俗"},{"english":"fade into the background","chinese":"逐漸退到背景；逐漸被淡忘"},{"english":"in this sense","chinese":"從這個意義上說"},{"english":"less like...and more like...","chinese":"與其說像……，不如說像……"},{"english":"a garden of different flowers","chinese":"百花齊放的花園"},{"english":"one repeated pattern","chinese":"單一重複的模式"},{"english":"the benefits are more significant","chinese":"好處更為重要"},{"english":"goods, knowledge and services","chinese":"商品、知識和服務"},{"english":"move across borders","chinese":"跨越國界流動"},{"english":"improve people's living standards","chinese":"改善人們的生活水平"},{"english":"a developing country","chinese":"發展中國家"},{"english":"gain access to","chinese":"獲得使用／接觸……的機會"},{"english":"imported medical equipment","chinese":"進口醫療設備"},{"english":"poorer regions","chinese":"較貧窮地區"},{"english":"online courses","chinese":"網上課程"},{"english":"overseas universities","chinese":"海外大學"},{"english":"these exchanges","chinese":"這些交流"},{"english":"not merely commercial","chinese":"不只是商業上的"},{"english":"open doors","chinese":"打開機會之門"},{"english":"would otherwise remain closed","chinese":"否則仍會關閉"},{"english":"creates opportunities for","chinese":"為……創造機會"},{"english":"a small software company","chinese":"小型軟件公司"},{"english":"sell its services to","chinese":"向……出售服務"},{"english":"clients abroad","chinese":"海外客戶"},{"english":"instead of depending only on","chinese":"而不是只依賴……"},{"english":"local market","chinese":"本地市場"},{"english":"at the same time","chinese":"同時"},{"english":"contact between cultures","chinese":"文化之間的接觸"},{"english":"open-minded","chinese":"思想開明的"},{"english":"different backgrounds","chinese":"不同背景"},{"english":"particularly for","chinese":"尤其對於……"},{"english":"cultural traditions","chinese":"文化傳統"},{"english":"nevertheless","chinese":"然而"},{"english":"firmly believe","chinese":"堅信"},{"english":"positive overall","chinese":"整體而言是正面的"},{"english":"spreads opportunity, knowledge and cooperation","chinese":"傳播機會、知識和合作"},{"english":"far more widely than","chinese":"遠比……更廣泛"},{"english":"a closed world","chinese":"封閉的世界"}]},"model-essay-19-ielts-cause-solution":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-19-ielts-cause-solution","essayKey":"cause-solution:19","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-19-ielts-cause-solution","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/problem-and-cause/EdmundBd9CnS-Q19","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"In many developing countries, children in rural communities are held back not by a lack of ability, but by a shortage of high-quality teachers. This problem is largely caused by poor working conditions and limited career prospects, and it can be addressed through targeted incentives and stronger professional support.","chinese":"在許多發展中國家，農村社區的兒童受到限制，並不是因為能力不足，而是因為缺乏高質素的教師。 這個問題主要是由惡劣的工作條件和有限的職業前景造成的，而它可以透過有針對性的激勵措施和更強的專業支援來解決。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"One major reason skilled teachers avoid rural areas is that these posts often come with serious personal and professional disadvantages. Many rural schools lack basic facilities, reliable transport, proper accommodation, and teaching materials, so even committed teachers may feel that they are being asked to do an important job with one hand tied behind their back. For example, a science teacher who has no laboratory, no stable internet connection, and overcrowded classes may struggle to deliver lessons effectively, which can quickly lead to frustration and burnout. Another reason is that rural appointments may appear to damage a teacher’s long-term career. In cities, teachers usually have better access to training, senior colleagues, promotion opportunities, and professional networks. By contrast, a rural teacher may feel invisible, no matter how hard he or she works.","chinese":"優秀教師避免到農村地區工作的其中一個主要原因，是這些職位往往伴隨嚴重的個人和職業劣勢。 許多農村學校缺乏基本設施、可靠交通、合適住宿和教學材料，因此即使是有熱誠的教師，也可能會覺得自己像是被綁住一隻手去完成一份重要工作。 例如，一位沒有實驗室、沒有穩定網絡連接，還要面對過度擠迫班級的科學老師，可能很難有效地授課，而這很快便會導致挫敗感和職業倦怠。 另一個原因是，農村任職安排可能看起來會損害教師的長遠職業發展。 在城市，教師通常更容易獲得培訓機會、接觸資深同事、得到晉升機會，並建立專業人脈網絡。 相比之下，一位農村教師無論多努力工作，都可能會覺得自己被忽視。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"To solve this problem, governments should first make rural teaching financially and practically attractive. This could include higher salaries, free housing, transport allowances, and priority access to future promotions. Such measures would not merely reward teachers; they would also signal that rural education is a national priority rather than a professional dead end. In addition, rural teachers need regular support, not just a contract and a classroom. Governments and schools could provide online mentoring, mobile training teams, and partnerships between urban and rural schools, so that teachers in remote areas can continue to improve their skills. Over time, developing local teacher-training programmes would also help, because teachers who come from rural communities are more likely to understand local needs and remain there.","chinese":"為了解決這個問題，政府首先應該使農村教學在經濟和實際層面上都更具吸引力。 這可以包括更高薪酬、免費住房、交通津貼，以及未來晉升的優先機會。 這些措施不只是獎勵教師；它們也會傳達一個訊息：農村教育是國家優先事項，而不是一條職業死路。 此外，農村教師需要定期支援，而不只是一份合約和一間課室。 政府和學校可以提供網上指導、流動培訓團隊，以及城鄉學校之間的合作關係，讓偏遠地區的教師能夠持續提升自己的技能。 長遠而言，發展本地教師培訓課程也會有幫助，因為來自農村社區的教師更有可能理解當地需要，並留在那裡工作。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, good teachers often avoid rural schools because the conditions are difficult and the career rewards are limited. Better incentives, stronger training, and clearer career pathways would make rural teaching more sustainable and improve children’s access to quality education.","chinese":"總結來說，優秀教師往往避免到農村學校工作，因為那裡的條件艱難，而且職業回報有限。 更好的激勵措施、更強的培訓，以及更清晰的職業發展路徑，將會使農村教學更可持續，並改善兒童接受優質教育的機會。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"developing countries","chinese":"發展中國家"},{"english":"rural communities","chinese":"農村社區"},{"english":"be held back not by..., but by...","chinese":"不是因為……而受阻，而是因為……"},{"english":"a lack of ability","chinese":"能力不足"},{"english":"a shortage of","chinese":"……短缺"},{"english":"high-quality teachers","chinese":"優質教師"},{"english":"largely caused by","chinese":"主要由……造成"},{"english":"poor working conditions","chinese":"惡劣工作條件"},{"english":"limited career prospects","chinese":"有限的事業前景"},{"english":"be addressed through","chinese":"透過……處理"},{"english":"targeted incentives","chinese":"針對性誘因"},{"english":"stronger professional support","chinese":"更強的專業支援"},{"english":"one major reason","chinese":"一個主要原因"},{"english":"skilled teachers","chinese":"有能力的教師"},{"english":"avoid rural areas","chinese":"避開農村地區"},{"english":"posts often come with","chinese":"職位往往伴隨"},{"english":"serious personal and professional disadvantages","chinese":"嚴重的個人及專業劣勢"},{"english":"lack basic facilities","chinese":"缺乏基本設施"},{"english":"reliable transport","chinese":"可靠交通"},{"english":"proper accommodation","chinese":"合適住宿"},{"english":"teaching materials","chinese":"教學材料"},{"english":"committed teachers","chinese":"敬業的教師"},{"english":"be asked to do","chinese":"被要求去做"},{"english":"with one hand tied behind their back","chinese":"束手束腳；在條件受限下做事"},{"english":"stable internet connection","chinese":"穩定的互聯網連接"},{"english":"overcrowded classes","chinese":"過度擠迫的班級"},{"english":"struggle to","chinese":"努力但困難地"},{"english":"deliver lessons effectively","chinese":"有效授課"},{"english":"lead to frustration and burnout","chinese":"導致挫敗感和倦怠"},{"english":"frustration and burnout","chinese":"挫敗感和倦怠"},{"english":"rural appointments","chinese":"農村任教崗位"},{"english":"appear to damage","chinese":"看似會損害"},{"english":"long-term career","chinese":"長遠事業發展"},{"english":"have better access to","chinese":"較容易獲得"},{"english":"senior colleagues","chinese":"資深同事"},{"english":"promotion opportunities","chinese":"晉升機會"},{"english":"professional networks","chinese":"專業人脈網絡"},{"english":"by contrast","chinese":"相比之下"},{"english":"feel invisible","chinese":"感到被忽視"},{"english":"no matter how hard","chinese":"無論多努力"},{"english":"to solve this problem","chinese":"為了解決這個問題"},{"english":"financially and practically attractive","chinese":"在經濟和實際層面具吸引力"},{"english":"higher salaries","chinese":"更高薪酬"},{"english":"free housing","chinese":"免費住房"},{"english":"transport allowances","chinese":"交通津貼"},{"english":"priority access to future promotions","chinese":"優先獲得日後晉升機會"},{"english":"such measures","chinese":"這些措施"},{"english":"not merely reward","chinese":"不只是獎勵"},{"english":"signal that","chinese":"顯示"},{"english":"a national priority","chinese":"國家優先事項"},{"english":"rather than","chinese":"而不是"},{"english":"a professional dead end","chinese":"事業上的死胡同"},{"english":"regular support","chinese":"定期支援"},{"english":"not just a contract and a classroom","chinese":"不只是一份合約和一間課室"},{"english":"online mentoring","chinese":"網上指導"},{"english":"mobile training teams","chinese":"流動培訓團隊"},{"english":"partnerships between urban and rural schools","chinese":"城市與農村學校之間的合作"},{"english":"remote areas","chinese":"偏遠地區"},{"english":"continue to improve their skills","chinese":"持續提升技能"},{"english":"over time","chinese":"隨着時間"},{"english":"developing local teacher-training programmes","chinese":"發展本地教師培訓課程"},{"english":"come from rural communities","chinese":"來自農村社區"},{"english":"understand local needs","chinese":"了解本地需要"},{"english":"remain there","chinese":"留在當地"},{"english":"career rewards","chinese":"事業回報"},{"english":"clearer career pathways","chinese":"更清晰的事業發展路徑"},{"english":"more sustainable","chinese":"更可持續"},{"english":"children's access to quality education","chinese":"兒童接受優質教育的機會"}]},"model-essay-19-ielts-discuss-both-views":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-19-ielts-discuss-both-views","essayKey":"discuss-both-views:19","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-19-ielts-discuss-both-views","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/discuss-both-views-your-opinion/EdmundBd9ExpBth-Q19","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"Human beings have altered the natural world on an unprecedented scale. Because forests have been cleared, oceans polluted and many species pushed towards extinction, some people argue that the damage done to plants and animals is now beyond repair. While I understand this pessimistic view, I believe that practical action can still reduce environmental harm and allow nature to recover.","chinese":"人類以前所未有的規模改變了自然世界。 由於森林被砍伐、海洋受到污染，許多物種也被推向滅絕邊緣，有些人認為人類對動植物造成的傷害如今已經無法修復。 雖然我理解這種悲觀觀點， 但我相信實際行動仍然可以減少環境傷害，並讓自然恢復。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"Those who think change is impossible usually point to the permanent nature of some environmental damage. Once a species disappears, for instance, no law or campaign can bring it back. In addition, modern life depends heavily on activities that harm ecosystems, such as mass farming, road building, air travel and industrial production. These activities are not small habits that can be removed overnight; they are woven into the way economies operate. As a result, even when governments promise greener policies, businesses and consumers often continue to prioritise convenience, profit and short-term growth. From this perspective, human impact seems like a tide that is too powerful to turn back.","chinese":"那些認為改變是不可能的人，通常會指出某些環境破壞具有永久性。 例如，一旦一個物種消失，就沒有任何法律或運動能夠把它帶回來。 此外，現代生活高度依賴會破壞生態系統的活動，例如大規模農業、道路建設、航空旅行和工業生產。 這些活動並不是可以一夜之間改掉的小習慣；它們已經編織進經濟運作的方式之中。 結果是，即使政府承諾推行更環保的政策，企業和消費者仍然經常優先考慮便利、利潤和短期增長。 從這個角度來看，人類的影響就像一股過於強大的潮水，似乎已經無法逆轉。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"However, I would argue that this view is too defeatist. Although some losses are irreversible, many forms of environmental damage can be limited, slowed or even partly reversed. Governments can protect forests, restrict illegal hunting, restore wetlands and punish companies that pollute rivers or destroy habitats. At the same time, individuals can change demand by eating less wastefully, choosing sustainable products and supporting conservation projects. For example, when a city creates protected green spaces and controls development, birds, insects and native plants can return over time. Nature is often remarkably resilient if people stop putting constant pressure on it.","chinese":"然而，我會認為這種觀點過於失敗主義。 雖然有些損失是不可逆轉的，但許多形式的環境破壞仍然可以被限制、減緩，甚至部分逆轉。 政府可以保護森林、限制非法狩獵、修復濕地，並懲罰污染河流或破壞棲息地的公司。 同時，個人也可以透過減少飲食浪費、選擇可持續產品，以及支持保育項目來改變需求 例如，當一座城市建立受保護的綠化空間並控制發展時，鳥類、昆蟲和本地植物可以隨著時間逐漸回歸。 如果人們停止不斷向自然施加壓力，自然往往具有驚人的復原力。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, human activity has undoubtedly caused deep damage to the natural world, and some of that damage cannot be undone. Nevertheless, I strongly believe that change is still possible. With firm laws, responsible businesses and more thoughtful daily choices, humans can stop making the problem worse and give plants and animals a real chance to survive.","chinese":"總結來說，人類活動無疑已對自然世界造成了深重傷害，而且其中一些傷害無法被復原 然而，我強烈相信改變仍然是可能的。 透過堅定的法律、負責任的企業，以及更審慎的日常選擇，人類可以停止讓問題惡化，並給予動植物真正的生存機會。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"alter the natural world","chinese":"改變自然世界"},{"english":"on an unprecedented scale","chinese":"以前所未有的規模"},{"english":"forests have been cleared","chinese":"森林被清除"},{"english":"oceans polluted","chinese":"海洋受到污染"},{"english":"be pushed towards extinction","chinese":"被推向滅絕"},{"english":"the damage done to","chinese":"對……造成的破壞"},{"english":"plants and animals","chinese":"動植物"},{"english":"beyond repair","chinese":"無法修復"},{"english":"this pessimistic view","chinese":"這種悲觀看法"},{"english":"practical action","chinese":"實際行動"},{"english":"reduce environmental harm","chinese":"減少環境傷害"},{"english":"allow nature to recover","chinese":"讓大自然恢復"},{"english":"point to","chinese":"指出；以……作為理由"},{"english":"the permanent nature of","chinese":"……的永久性"},{"english":"environmental damage","chinese":"環境破壞"},{"english":"once a species disappears","chinese":"一旦一個物種消失"},{"english":"bring it back","chinese":"使其回復；帶回來"},{"english":"in addition","chinese":"此外"},{"english":"depend heavily on","chinese":"非常依賴"},{"english":"harm ecosystems","chinese":"破壞生態系統"},{"english":"mass farming","chinese":"大規模農業"},{"english":"road building","chinese":"道路建設"},{"english":"air travel","chinese":"航空旅行"},{"english":"industrial production","chinese":"工業生產"},{"english":"be removed overnight","chinese":"一夜之間被移除"},{"english":"be woven into","chinese":"融入……之中"},{"english":"the way economies operate","chinese":"經濟運作方式"},{"english":"as a result","chinese":"因此"},{"english":"greener policies","chinese":"更環保的政策"},{"english":"continue to prioritise","chinese":"繼續優先考慮"},{"english":"convenience, profit and short-term growth","chinese":"方便、利潤和短期增長"},{"english":"from this perspective","chinese":"從這個角度來看"},{"english":"human impact","chinese":"人類影響"},{"english":"too powerful to turn back","chinese":"強大到無法扭轉"},{"english":"this view is too defeatist","chinese":"這個看法過於消極"},{"english":"irreversible","chinese":"不可逆轉的"},{"english":"many forms of","chinese":"很多形式的"},{"english":"be limited, slowed or even partly reversed","chinese":"被限制、減慢，甚至局部逆轉"},{"english":"protect forests","chinese":"保護森林"},{"english":"restrict illegal hunting","chinese":"限制非法狩獵"},{"english":"restore wetlands","chinese":"修復濕地"},{"english":"punish companies that","chinese":"懲罰……的公司"},{"english":"pollute rivers","chinese":"污染河流"},{"english":"destroy habitats","chinese":"破壞棲息地"},{"english":"at the same time","chinese":"同時"},{"english":"change demand","chinese":"改變需求"},{"english":"eating less wastefully","chinese":"減少飲食浪費"},{"english":"sustainable products","chinese":"可持續產品"},{"english":"supporting conservation projects","chinese":"支持保育項目"},{"english":"protected green spaces","chinese":"受保護綠化空間"},{"english":"control development","chinese":"控制發展"},{"english":"native plants","chinese":"本土植物"},{"english":"return over time","chinese":"隨時間回歸"},{"english":"remarkably resilient","chinese":"具有驚人的復原力"},{"english":"put constant pressure on","chinese":"對……施加持續壓力"},{"english":"undoubtedly caused deep damage to","chinese":"毫無疑問對……造成深遠破壞"},{"english":"the natural world","chinese":"自然世界"},{"english":"cannot be undone","chinese":"不能被逆轉"},{"english":"nevertheless","chinese":"然而"},{"english":"firm laws","chinese":"強硬法律"},{"english":"responsible businesses","chinese":"負責任的企業"},{"english":"thoughtful daily choices","chinese":"經深思熟慮的日常選擇"},{"english":"stop making the problem worse","chinese":"停止令問題惡化"},{"english":"give plants and animals a real chance to survive","chinese":"給動植物真正的生存機會"}]},"model-essay-19-ielts-opinion":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-19-ielts-opinion","essayKey":"opinion:19","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-19-ielts-opinion","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/opinions/EdmundBd9OP-Q19","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"In the modern media landscape, many celebrities are admired less for what they have done than for how luxurious their lives appear. I completely agree that this shift is harmful, because it teaches young people to value image, consumption and instant attention more than genuine achievement.","chinese":"在現代媒體環境中，許多名人受到仰慕，並不是因為他們做過甚麼，而是因為他們的生活看起來多麼奢華。 我完全同意這種轉變是有害的，因為它教導年輕人重視形象、消費和即時關注，而不是重視真正的成就。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"The first problem is that celebrity culture often presents success as something visual rather than earned. When young people constantly see famous figures praised for designer clothes, expensive cars and perfectly staged photos, they may begin to believe that public admiration matters more than effort, discipline or contribution. This is dangerous because achievement usually grows slowly, through practice, failure and patience, whereas glamour offers the illusion of overnight success. For example, a teenager who spends hours following influencers may become more interested in looking wealthy than in building real skills. Over time, this can weaken ambition in a quiet but serious way: the goal becomes to be seen, not to be useful.","chinese":"第一個問題是，名人文化常常把成功呈現為一種視覺上的東西，而不是靠努力得來的成果。 當年輕人不斷看到名人因名牌服裝、昂貴汽車和精心擺拍的照片而受到讚賞時，他們可能會開始相信，公眾的仰慕比努力、自律或貢獻更重要。 這是危險的，因為成就通常是透過練習、失敗和耐心慢慢累積而來的，而魅力和奢華卻製造了一種一夜成功的幻象。 例如，一個花數小時追蹤網紅的青少年，可能會對看起來富有更感興趣，而不是對建立真正技能感興趣。 長遠而言，這會以一種安靜但嚴重的方式削弱抱負：目標變成被看見，而不是變得有用。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"Another reason I agree is that this kind of fame can create unhealthy social pressure. Many celebrities display a lifestyle that is polished, selective and often unrealistic, yet young audiences may treat it as normal life. As a result, they may compare their own ordinary homes, bodies and possessions with a carefully manufactured image. This can lead to insecurity, wasteful spending and a belief that personal worth depends on appearance. A student, for instance, might feel embarrassed about using an old phone or wearing simple clothes, not because these things matter, but because the celebrity world has turned luxury into a symbol of status.","chinese":"我同意的另一個原因是，這種名氣可能製造不健康的社會壓力。 許多名人展示的是一種經過修飾、經過篩選，而且往往不現實的生活方式，然而年輕觀眾卻可能把它視為正常生活。 結果是，他們可能會把自己普通的家庭、身體和物品，與一種被精心製造出來的形象作比較。 這可能導致不安全感、浪費性消費，以及一種認為個人價值取決於外表的信念。 例如，一名學生可能會因為使用舊手機或穿著簡單衣服而感到尷尬，並不是因為這些事情本身重要，而是因為名人的世界已經把奢侈變成了地位的象徵。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, I fully agree that celebrities who are celebrated mainly for wealth and glamour set a poor example for young people. Fame should not become a glittering shortcut that replaces character, skill and meaningful achievement.","chinese":"總結來說，我完全同意，那些主要因財富和魅力而受到推崇的名人，為年輕人樹立了不良榜樣。 名氣不應變成一條閃閃發亮的捷徑，取代品格、技能和有意義的成就。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"modern media landscape","chinese":"現代媒體環境"},{"english":"be admired less for","chinese":"較少因……而受欣賞"},{"english":"what they have done","chinese":"他們所做過的事"},{"english":"luxurious their lives appear","chinese":"他們的生活看起來多奢華"},{"english":"this shift","chinese":"這種轉變"},{"english":"harmful","chinese":"有害的"},{"english":"teaches young people to","chinese":"教導年輕人去……"},{"english":"value image","chinese":"重視形象"},{"english":"consumption","chinese":"消費"},{"english":"instant attention","chinese":"即時關注"},{"english":"genuine achievement","chinese":"真正成就"},{"english":"celebrity culture","chinese":"名人文化"},{"english":"presents success as","chinese":"將成功呈現為……"},{"english":"visual rather than earned","chinese":"視覺上的，而不是努力得來的"},{"english":"famous figures","chinese":"著名人物"},{"english":"be praised for","chinese":"因……而受讚賞"},{"english":"designer clothes","chinese":"名牌衣服"},{"english":"expensive cars","chinese":"昂貴汽車"},{"english":"perfectly staged photos","chinese":"精心擺拍的照片"},{"english":"public admiration","chinese":"公眾仰慕"},{"english":"matters more than","chinese":"比……更重要"},{"english":"effort, discipline or contribution","chinese":"努力、紀律和貢獻"},{"english":"achievement usually grows slowly","chinese":"成就通常慢慢累積"},{"english":"through practice, failure and patience","chinese":"透過練習、失敗和耐性"},{"english":"whereas","chinese":"而；然而"},{"english":"glamour","chinese":"光鮮亮麗"},{"english":"the illusion of","chinese":"……的假象"},{"english":"overnight success","chinese":"一夜成名"},{"english":"following influencers","chinese":"追蹤網紅"},{"english":"looking wealthy","chinese":"看起來富有"},{"english":"building real skills","chinese":"建立真正技能"},{"english":"over time","chinese":"隨着時間過去"},{"english":"weaken ambition","chinese":"削弱抱負"},{"english":"in a quiet but serious way","chinese":"以不明顯但嚴重的方式"},{"english":"the goal becomes to","chinese":"目標變成……"},{"english":"be seen","chinese":"被看見"},{"english":"be useful","chinese":"有用；有價值"},{"english":"create unhealthy social pressure","chinese":"造成不健康的社會壓力"},{"english":"display a lifestyle","chinese":"展示一種生活方式"},{"english":"polished","chinese":"經修飾的"},{"english":"selective","chinese":"經篩選的"},{"english":"unrealistic","chinese":"不切實際的"},{"english":"young audiences","chinese":"年輕觀眾"},{"english":"treat it as normal life","chinese":"將它視為正常生活"},{"english":"compare their own","chinese":"將自己的……作比較"},{"english":"ordinary homes","chinese":"普通住家"},{"english":"bodies and possessions","chinese":"身體和財物"},{"english":"carefully manufactured image","chinese":"精心製造的形象"},{"english":"lead to insecurity","chinese":"導致不安全感"},{"english":"wasteful spending","chinese":"浪費性的消費"},{"english":"personal worth","chinese":"個人價值"},{"english":"depends on appearance","chinese":"取決於外表"},{"english":"feel embarrassed about","chinese":"因……而感到尷尬"},{"english":"old phone","chinese":"舊電話"},{"english":"wearing simple clothes","chinese":"穿着簡單衣服"},{"english":"these things matter","chinese":"這些東西重要"},{"english":"celebrity world","chinese":"名人世界"},{"english":"turn luxury into","chinese":"將奢華變成……"},{"english":"symbol of status","chinese":"地位象徵"},{"english":"be celebrated mainly for","chinese":"主要因……而受到追捧"},{"english":"wealth and glamour","chinese":"財富和光鮮"},{"english":"set a poor example for","chinese":"為……樹立壞榜樣"},{"english":"glittering shortcut","chinese":"閃亮的捷徑"},{"english":"replaces character","chinese":"取代品格"},{"english":"skill and meaningful achievement","chinese":"技能和有意義的成就"}]},"model-essay-20-ielts-advantage-disadvantage":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-20-ielts-advantage-disadvantage","essayKey":"advantage-disadvantage:20","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-20-ielts-advantage-disadvantage","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/advantage-and-disadvantage/EdmundBd9AdDisAd-Q20","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"In many land-scarce cities, ageing buildings are torn down to make way for modern development. While replacement can deliver safer and more efficient premises, I believe its drawbacks are greater because it erases heritage and causes avoidable environmental harm; therefore, the advantages do not outweigh the disadvantages.","chinese":"在許多土地短缺的城市中，老舊建築物為了騰出空間進行現代化發展而被拆除。 雖然以新建築取代它們可以提供更安全、更高效的空間， 我認為整體而言，拆除舊建築的弊端更大，因為這樣做會摧毀文化遺產，並造成不必要的環境破壞；因此，其優點並不大於缺點。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"The most serious disadvantage is the irreversible loss of historical character and cultural identity. Old buildings are not merely functional structures; they embody a city’s memory and give neighbourhoods a distinct sense of place. When a traditional market, theatre or row of shophouses is replaced by yet another glass tower, a city loses part of the story written into its streets. Over time, urban centres begin to look interchangeable, which can weaken residents’ attachment to their community and even reduce their appeal to visitors. Demolition also carries a heavy environmental cost. It produces vast quantities of rubble, while new construction consumes fresh steel, cement and energy. In short, what is presented as progress often comes with a sizeable ecological bill.","chinese":"拆除舊建築最嚴重的缺點，是歷史風貌與文化身分的不可逆轉流失。 舊建築不只是實體結構；它們承載著一座城市的記憶，並賦予社區鮮明的地方感。 當傳統市場、劇院或成排店屋消失時，城市空間便會逐漸變得千篇一律，這不但會削弱居民對社區的歸屬感，也可能降低城市對遊客的吸引力。 例如，如果一個歷史街區被另一幢玻璃辦公大樓取代，城市或許會增加可用樓面面積，卻同時失去自身故事中一個清晰可見的部分。 此外，拆除工程也會帶來重大的環境代價。 它會產生大量建築廢料，而新建築則需要全新的鋼材、水泥與能源，從而進一步增加資源消耗和碳排放。 例如，一個重建項目在任何一個新住宅單位或辦公空間落成之前，便可能已把大量瓦礫送往堆填區。 因此，拆除舊建築既會損害城市的文化認同，也會破壞其環境可持續性。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"The advantages of replacement are clear but ultimately less compelling. New buildings are usually safer, more energy-efficient and better suited to contemporary needs. In densely populated cities, high-rise redevelopment can also create more homes, offices and public facilities on scarce land. Nevertheless, these benefits do not outweigh the disadvantages because most of them are functional gains that can often be achieved through renovation or adaptive reuse. Cities can strengthen an old structure, upgrade its systems and redesign its interior without wiping the slate clean. Heritage, by contrast, is non-renewable: once it is destroyed, it cannot genuinely be recreated.","chinese":"以新建築取代舊建築的確有其好處，但這些優勢最終並不那麼有說服力。 新建築通常更安全、更節能，也更能符合當代需要。 在人口稠密的城市中，重建亦能在有限土地上提供更多住宅、辦公空間及公共設施，從而提升城市運作效率。 例如，以一幢現代高樓取代結構不安全的低層建築，可能既能提升安全標準，也能為更多居民提供空間。 然而，這些功能性的好處很多時候其實可以透過翻新或活化再利用來達成，而不必全面拆卸。 如果城市選擇加固舊建築、升級內部系統並重新設計室內空間，便能在不全部推倒重來的情況下滿足現代需求；相反，文化遺產一旦被破壞，便無法再生。 例如，一座舊倉庫可以改建成辦公室、藝廊或社區設施，同時保留其歷史立面與原有特色。 因此，雖然重建可以帶來實際利益，但這些收益仍不足以抵銷拆除所造成的永久損失。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, demolishing old buildings may produce modern space and more convenient facilities, but it also destroys urban identity and imposes avoidable environmental costs. For this reason, the advantages do not outweigh the disadvantages.","chinese":"總結來說，拆除舊建築或許能創造更安全、更便利的城市空間，但同時也會摧毀文化遺產，並造成本可避免的環境破壞。 整體而言，我認為其缺點更大，因為重建所帶來的實際好處很多時候都可以用較不具破壞性的方式達成；反之，歷史身分一旦失去，便無法真正復原。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"land-scarce cities","chinese":"土地短缺的城市"},{"english":"ageing buildings","chinese":"老化建築物"},{"english":"be torn down","chinese":"被拆卸"},{"english":"make way for","chinese":"為……讓路"},{"english":"modern development","chinese":"現代發展"},{"english":"replacement","chinese":"替換；重建"},{"english":"deliver safer and more efficient premises","chinese":"提供更安全、更高效的場所"},{"english":"drawbacks are greater","chinese":"缺點更大"},{"english":"erase heritage","chinese":"抹去文化遺產"},{"english":"avoidable environmental harm","chinese":"可避免的環境傷害"},{"english":"outweigh the disadvantages","chinese":"好處不大於壞處"},{"english":"the most serious disadvantage","chinese":"最嚴重的缺點"},{"english":"irreversible loss of","chinese":"……的不可逆轉損失"},{"english":"historical character","chinese":"歷史特色"},{"english":"cultural identity","chinese":"文化身份"},{"english":"not merely functional structures","chinese":"不只是實用建築物"},{"english":"embody a city's memory","chinese":"承載一座城市的記憶"},{"english":"give neighbourhoods a distinct sense of place","chinese":"賦予社區獨特的地方感"},{"english":"a traditional market","chinese":"傳統街市"},{"english":"a row of shophouses","chinese":"一排唐樓式商舖"},{"english":"be replaced by","chinese":"被……取代"},{"english":"yet another glass tower","chinese":"又一座玻璃大廈"},{"english":"loses part of the story","chinese":"失去故事的一部分"},{"english":"written into its streets","chinese":"寫進街道之中的"},{"english":"over time","chinese":"隨着時間"},{"english":"urban centres","chinese":"城市中心"},{"english":"look interchangeable","chinese":"看起來千篇一律"},{"english":"weaken residents' attachment to","chinese":"削弱居民對……的歸屬感"},{"english":"their community","chinese":"他們的社區"},{"english":"reduce their appeal to visitors","chinese":"降低對遊客的吸引力"},{"english":"demolition","chinese":"拆卸"},{"english":"carries a heavy environmental cost","chinese":"帶來沉重的環境代價"},{"english":"vast quantities of rubble","chinese":"大量瓦礫"},{"english":"new construction","chinese":"新建工程"},{"english":"consumes fresh steel, cement and energy","chinese":"消耗新的鋼材、水泥和能源"},{"english":"in short","chinese":"簡而言之"},{"english":"be presented as progress","chinese":"被包裝成進步"},{"english":"comes with","chinese":"伴隨"},{"english":"a sizeable ecological bill","chinese":"相當大的生態代價"},{"english":"ultimately less compelling","chinese":"最終較缺乏說服力"},{"english":"energy-efficient","chinese":"節能的"},{"english":"better suited to","chinese":"更適合"},{"english":"contemporary needs","chinese":"當代需要"},{"english":"densely populated cities","chinese":"人口稠密的城市"},{"english":"high-rise redevelopment","chinese":"高層重建"},{"english":"public facilities","chinese":"公共設施"},{"english":"scarce land","chinese":"稀缺土地"},{"english":"nevertheless","chinese":"然而"},{"english":"functional gains","chinese":"功能上的好處"},{"english":"be achieved through","chinese":"透過……達到"},{"english":"renovation","chinese":"翻新"},{"english":"adaptive reuse","chinese":"活化再利用"},{"english":"strengthen an old structure","chinese":"加固舊建築結構"},{"english":"upgrade its systems","chinese":"升級其系統"},{"english":"redesign its interior","chinese":"重新設計其內部"},{"english":"without wiping the slate clean","chinese":"而不是一切推倒重來"},{"english":"by contrast","chinese":"相比之下"},{"english":"non-renewable","chinese":"不可再生的"},{"english":"genuinely be recreated","chinese":"真正被重建出來"},{"english":"demolishing old buildings","chinese":"拆卸舊建築"},{"english":"modern space","chinese":"現代化空間"},{"english":"convenient facilities","chinese":"便利設施"},{"english":"destroys urban identity","chinese":"破壞城市身份"},{"english":"imposes avoidable environmental costs","chinese":"施加可避免的環境成本"}]},"model-essay-20-ielts-cause-solution":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-20-ielts-cause-solution","essayKey":"cause-solution:20","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-20-ielts-cause-solution","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/problem-and-cause/EdmundBd9CnS-Q20","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"Highly educated professionals often choose to pursue employment overseas after gaining expertise in their own fields. This is usually driven by stronger career incentives and better professional conditions, and it can create serious difficulties both for their home countries and for the individuals involved.","chinese":"受過良好教育的專業人士在自己的領域累積專門知識後，往往會選擇到海外工作。 這通常是由更強的職業誘因和更好的專業工作條件所推動，而這也可能為他們的原居國以及相關個人帶來嚴重困難。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"The main reason is that working abroad often offers a level of reward that is difficult to obtain at home. In many countries, even well-qualified workers may face low salaries, limited promotion prospects, or institutions that do not fully recognise their ability. By contrast, foreign employers may provide higher pay, clearer career paths, and more stable working conditions. A doctor, engineer, or researcher, for example, may move not simply for money, but because another country offers modern equipment, stronger professional networks, and a workplace where their skills can genuinely grow. In this sense, migration becomes less an act of escape than a search for room to breathe professionally.","chinese":"主要原因是，在海外工作往往能提供一種在本國難以獲得的回報水平。 在許多國家，即使是資歷優秀的工作者，也可能面對低薪、有限的晉升前景，或未能充分認可他們能力的機構。 相比之下，外國僱主可能提供更高薪酬、更清晰的職業發展道路，以及更穩定的工作條件 例如，一位醫生、工程師或研究人員移居海外，可能不單純是為了金錢，而是因為另一個國家能提供現代化設備、更強大的專業人脈，以及一個能讓他們的技能真正成長的工作環境。 從這個意義上說，移民與其說是一種逃離，不如說是在尋找專業上得以伸展和發展的空間"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"However, this movement can cause several problems. For the country of origin, the most serious consequence is a loss of human capital. When experienced teachers, medical specialists, scientists, or technical experts leave, the public systems that trained them may be left thinner and weaker. Hospitals may have longer waiting times, universities may lose capable lecturers, and local industries may struggle to innovate. Over time, this “brain drain” can widen the gap between richer and poorer countries, because the places that most need skilled workers are sometimes the least able to keep them. There may also be personal costs: migrants can face loneliness, cultural barriers, and the pressure of starting again in an unfamiliar professional environment.","chinese":"然而，這種流動也可能造成若干問題。 對原居國而言，最嚴重的後果是人力資本的流失。 當有經驗的教師、醫療專家、科學家或技術專家離開時，曾經培訓他們的公共系統可能會變得更薄弱、更缺乏力量。 醫院的輪候時間可能會變得更長，大學可能會失去有能力的講師，而本地產業也可能難以創新。 長遠而言，這種「人才外流」可能擴大富裕國家與較貧窮國家之間的差距，因為最需要技術人才的地方，有時反而最沒有能力留住他們。 此外，也可能存在個人層面的代價：移民者可能面對孤獨、文化障礙，以及在陌生的專業環境中重新開始的壓力。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, educated and experienced people usually move abroad because overseas work can offer better pay, recognition, resources, and long-term career development. Nevertheless, this trend can weaken essential services in their home countries and place emotional and social pressure on the workers themselves.","chinese":"總結來說，受過教育並具備經驗的人通常會移居海外，因為海外工作能提供更好的薪酬、認可、資源，以及長遠的職業發展。 然而，這一趨勢可能削弱他們原居國的重要服務，並為工作者本人帶來情感和社交上的壓力。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"highly educated professionals","chinese":"受過高等教育的專業人士"},{"english":"pursue employment overseas","chinese":"到海外尋求就業"},{"english":"gaining expertise in","chinese":"在……方面累積專業知識"},{"english":"in their own fields","chinese":"在自己的領域"},{"english":"be driven by","chinese":"由……推動"},{"english":"stronger career incentives","chinese":"更強的事業誘因"},{"english":"better professional conditions","chinese":"更好的專業工作條件"},{"english":"create serious difficulties","chinese":"造成嚴重困難"},{"english":"the individuals involved","chinese":"涉及其中的個人"},{"english":"working abroad","chinese":"到海外工作"},{"english":"a level of reward","chinese":"某種程度的回報"},{"english":"difficult to obtain at home","chinese":"在本國難以獲得"},{"english":"well-qualified workers","chinese":"資歷良好的工作者"},{"english":"low salaries","chinese":"低薪"},{"english":"limited promotion prospects","chinese":"有限的晉升前景"},{"english":"recognise their ability","chinese":"承認他們的能力"},{"english":"by contrast","chinese":"相比之下"},{"english":"foreign employers","chinese":"外國僱主"},{"english":"higher pay","chinese":"更高薪酬"},{"english":"clearer career paths","chinese":"更清晰的事業發展路徑"},{"english":"stable working conditions","chinese":"穩定的工作條件"},{"english":"modern equipment","chinese":"現代化設備"},{"english":"professional networks","chinese":"專業人脈網絡"},{"english":"genuinely grow","chinese":"真正成長"},{"english":"in this sense","chinese":"從這個意義上說"},{"english":"an act of escape","chinese":"逃離的行為"},{"english":"a search for","chinese":"對……的尋求"},{"english":"room to breathe professionally","chinese":"專業上有發展空間"},{"english":"this movement","chinese":"這種流動"},{"english":"the country of origin","chinese":"原籍國"},{"english":"the most serious consequence","chinese":"最嚴重的後果"},{"english":"human capital","chinese":"人力資本"},{"english":"medical specialists","chinese":"醫學專科人員"},{"english":"technical experts","chinese":"技術專家"},{"english":"public systems","chinese":"公共系統"},{"english":"be left thinner and weaker","chinese":"變得人手更薄弱、力量更弱"},{"english":"longer waiting times","chinese":"更長的輪候時間"},{"english":"capable lecturers","chinese":"有能力的講師"},{"english":"local industries","chinese":"本地產業"},{"english":"struggle to innovate","chinese":"難以創新"},{"english":"over time","chinese":"隨時間"},{"english":"brain drain","chinese":"人才流失"},{"english":"widen the gap between","chinese":"擴大……之間的差距"},{"english":"richer and poorer countries","chinese":"較富裕和較貧窮的國家"},{"english":"skilled workers","chinese":"技術熟練的工作者"},{"english":"the least able to keep them","chinese":"最無能力留住他們"},{"english":"personal costs","chinese":"個人成本；個人代價"},{"english":"cultural barriers","chinese":"文化障礙"},{"english":"the pressure of starting again","chinese":"重新開始的壓力"},{"english":"an unfamiliar professional environment","chinese":"陌生的專業工作環境"},{"english":"educated and experienced people","chinese":"受過教育而有經驗的人"},{"english":"long-term career development","chinese":"長遠事業發展"},{"english":"nevertheless","chinese":"然而"},{"english":"weaken essential services","chinese":"削弱必要服務"},{"english":"emotional and social pressure","chinese":"情緒和社交壓力"},{"english":"place pressure on","chinese":"對……施加壓力"},{"english":"the workers themselves","chinese":"工作者本人"}]},"model-essay-20-ielts-discuss-both-views":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-20-ielts-discuss-both-views","essayKey":"discuss-both-views:20","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-20-ielts-discuss-both-views","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/discuss-both-views-your-opinion/EdmundBd9ExpBth-Q20","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"Air pollution in major cities is often linked to the heavy use of private vehicles. While some people believe that an international car-free day would be a useful way to reduce this problem, others argue that broader measures would be more effective. In my view, although a car-free day can raise public awareness, lasting improvements require stronger and more permanent transport policies.","chinese":"大城市的空氣污染通常與私家車的大量使用有關。 雖然有些人認為，國際無車日會是減少這個問題的有效方法，但另一些人則認為，更廣泛的措施會更加有效。 在我看來，雖然無車日可以提高公眾意識，但持久的改善需要更強而有力、也更具永久性的交通政策。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"Supporters of an international car-free day argue that it can produce an immediate, visible reduction in traffic and emissions. If millions of drivers around the world left their cars at home for one day, city streets would become quieter, cleaner, and less congested. This could also encourage people to reflect on their daily travel habits. For example, an office worker who normally drives a short distance to work might realise that public transport, cycling, or walking is not as inconvenient as they had assumed. In this sense, a car-free day can act as a useful wake-up call, showing the public that cleaner urban life is possible.","chinese":"支持國際無車日的人認為，它能夠立即並明顯地減少交通流量和排放。 如果全球數以百萬計的司機有一天把車留在家中，城市街道便會變得更安靜、更清潔，也較不擁擠。 這也可以鼓勵人們反思自己的日常出行習慣。 例如，一位平時開車短途上班的辦公室職員，可能會意識到公共交通、騎單車或步行並不像他們原本以為的那麼不方便。 從這個意義上說，無車日可以成為一個有用的警醒，向公眾展示更清潔的城市生活是可能實現的。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"However, I believe other solutions are far more effective because air pollution is a daily problem, not a one-day problem. A symbolic event may briefly reduce emissions, but traffic usually returns to normal the next morning. Governments should instead invest in reliable public transport, create safe cycling lanes, and introduce stricter emission standards for vehicles. These policies change people’s behaviour over time because they make cleaner choices practical, affordable, and attractive. For instance, if buses and trains are cheap, punctual, and comfortable, many commuters will naturally choose them instead of driving. Unlike a car-free day, these measures attack the root of the problem.","chinese":"然而，我認為其他解決方法有效得多，因為空氣污染是一個每日存在的問題，而不是一個只存在一天的問題。 一個象徵性的活動也許能短暫地減少排放，但交通通常會在第二天早上恢復正常。 政府反而應該投資於可靠的公共交通、建設安全的單車徑，並為車輛引入更嚴格的排放標準。 這些政策會隨著時間改變人們的行為，因為它們使更清潔的選擇變得實際、負擔得起，並且有吸引力。 例如，如果巴士和火車便宜、準時又舒適，許多通勤者自然會選擇它們，而不是開車。 與無車日不同，這些措施能夠處理問題的根源。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, an international car-free day has some value because it can raise awareness and temporarily reduce pollution. Nevertheless, I firmly believe that long-term transport reform is a much more effective way to improve air quality, as it changes how people travel every day rather than only once a year.","chinese":"總結來說，國際無車日具有一定價值，因為它可以提高意識並暫時減少污染。 然而，我堅定地認為，長遠的交通改革是改善空氣質素更有效的方法，因為它改變的是人們每天的出行方式，而不是一年只有一次的行為。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"air pollution in major cities","chinese":"大城市的空氣污染"},{"english":"be linked to","chinese":"與……有關"},{"english":"the heavy use of","chinese":"大量使用"},{"english":"private vehicles","chinese":"私家車；私人車輛"},{"english":"an international car-free day","chinese":"國際無車日"},{"english":"a useful way to","chinese":"……的有用方法"},{"english":"reduce this problem","chinese":"減少這個問題"},{"english":"broader measures","chinese":"更廣泛的措施"},{"english":"more effective","chinese":"更有效"},{"english":"in my view","chinese":"在我看來"},{"english":"raise public awareness","chinese":"提高公眾意識"},{"english":"lasting improvements","chinese":"持久改善"},{"english":"stronger and more permanent transport policies","chinese":"更強而更永久的交通政策"},{"english":"supporters of","chinese":"……的支持者"},{"english":"produce an immediate, visible reduction in","chinese":"立即而明顯地減少"},{"english":"traffic and emissions","chinese":"交通流量和排放"},{"english":"around the world","chinese":"世界各地"},{"english":"leave their cars at home","chinese":"不駕車出門"},{"english":"for one day","chinese":"一日"},{"english":"city streets","chinese":"城市街道"},{"english":"quieter, cleaner, and less congested","chinese":"更寧靜、更清潔和較不擠塞"},{"english":"encourage people to reflect on","chinese":"鼓勵人反思"},{"english":"daily travel habits","chinese":"日常出行習慣"},{"english":"normally drives a short distance","chinese":"平日駕車走短距離"},{"english":"public transport, cycling, or walking","chinese":"公共交通、踩單車或步行"},{"english":"not as inconvenient as","chinese":"不像……那麼不方便"},{"english":"as they had assumed","chinese":"如他們原本以為般"},{"english":"in this sense","chinese":"從這個意義上說"},{"english":"act as a useful wake-up call","chinese":"發揮有用的警醒作用"},{"english":"cleaner urban life","chinese":"更清潔的城市生活"},{"english":"is possible","chinese":"是可能的"},{"english":"other solutions","chinese":"其他解決方法"},{"english":"far more effective","chinese":"有效得多"},{"english":"a daily problem","chinese":"每日都存在的問題"},{"english":"a one-day problem","chinese":"一日的問題"},{"english":"a symbolic event","chinese":"象徵性活動"},{"english":"briefly reduce emissions","chinese":"短暫減少排放"},{"english":"return to normal","chinese":"恢復正常"},{"english":"the next morning","chinese":"第二朝"},{"english":"should instead invest in","chinese":"反而應該投資於"},{"english":"reliable public transport","chinese":"可靠的公共交通"},{"english":"create safe cycling lanes","chinese":"設立安全單車徑"},{"english":"stricter emission standards","chinese":"更嚴格的排放標準"},{"english":"change people's behaviour over time","chinese":"隨時間改變人們的行為"},{"english":"cleaner choices","chinese":"較環保的選擇"},{"english":"practical, affordable, and attractive","chinese":"實際、負擔得起和吸引"},{"english":"cheap, punctual, and comfortable","chinese":"便宜、準時和舒適"},{"english":"commuters","chinese":"通勤人士"},{"english":"naturally choose","chinese":"自然會選擇"},{"english":"instead of driving","chinese":"而不是駕車"},{"english":"unlike","chinese":"不像"},{"english":"attack the root of the problem","chinese":"針對問題根源"},{"english":"have some value","chinese":"有一定價值"},{"english":"temporarily reduce pollution","chinese":"暫時減少污染"},{"english":"nevertheless","chinese":"然而"},{"english":"long-term transport reform","chinese":"長期交通改革"},{"english":"a much more effective way to","chinese":"……有效得多的方法"},{"english":"improve air quality","chinese":"改善空氣質素"},{"english":"changes how people travel every day","chinese":"改變人們每日的出行方式"},{"english":"rather than only once a year","chinese":"而不是一年只有一次"}]},"model-essay-20-ielts-opinion":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-20-ielts-opinion","essayKey":"opinion:20","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-20-ielts-opinion","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/opinions/EdmundBd9OP-Q20","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"In the modern entertainment industry, fame often comes with constant attention from newspapers, television programmes, and online platforms. Some people therefore argue that public exposure is simply the price celebrities pay for success. I strongly disagree. In my view, the media should not publish the private lives of famous people unless there is a clear public interest.","chinese":"在現代娛樂產業中，名氣往往伴隨著來自報紙、電視節目和網上平台的持續關注。 因此，有些人認為，公開曝光只是名人為成功所付出的代價。 我強烈不同意這種看法。在我看來，除非涉及明確的公共利益，否則媒體不應公開名人的私人生活。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"The main reason is that being well known does not remove a person’s basic right to privacy. Celebrities may choose to appear on screen, perform on stage, or promote their work online, but this does not mean they have agreed to have every corner of their personal lives examined. Their family problems, romantic relationships, health issues, and home addresses are usually irrelevant to their professional achievements. If journalists follow them to private places or publish photographs of their children, this is not entertainment; it is intrusion dressed up as news. Over time, such pressure can damage mental health and make normal family life almost impossible.","chinese":"主要原因是，知名並不會剝奪一個人基本的私隱權。 名人也許選擇出現在螢幕上、在舞台上表演，或在網上宣傳自己的作品，但這並不代表他們同意自己私人生活的每一個角落都被審視。 他們的家庭問題、感情關係、健康狀況和住址，通常都與他們的專業成就無關。 如果記者跟蹤他們到私人場所，或公開他們子女的照片，這並不是娛樂；這只是披著新聞外衣的侵犯。 長遠而言，這種壓力可能損害心理健康，並令正常的家庭生活幾乎變得不可能。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"Another reason is that unrestricted media attention encourages a harmful culture of gossip. When audiences are constantly fed stories about scandals and private conflicts, they may start to see celebrities less as human beings and more as public property. This is unfair, especially because many of these stories are exaggerated, misleading, or based on moments taken out of context. For example, a tired actor leaving a hospital or a singer arguing with a family member may be turned into a dramatic headline, even though the situation has nothing to do with the public. Responsible journalism should inform society, not feed curiosity at any cost.","chinese":"另一個原因是，不受限制的媒體關注會助長一種有害的八卦文化。 當觀眾不斷被餵養有關醜聞和私人衝突的故事時，他們可能會開始較少把名人看作人，而更多把他們看成公共財產。 這是不公平的，尤其是因為許多這類故事都被誇大、具有誤導性，或建基於被抽離語境的片刻。 例如，一位疲憊的演員離開醫院，或一位歌手與家人爭執，即使情況與公眾毫無關係，也可能被寫成戲劇性的標題。 負責任的新聞工作應該是告知社會，而不是不惜一切代價滿足人們的好奇心。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, although famous people should expect public discussion of their work and professional behaviour, their private lives should remain protected. Fame may open the door to attention, but it should not give the media a licence to walk through every room.","chinese":"總結來說，儘管名人應該預期自己的工作和專業行為會受到公眾討論，但他們的私人生活仍然應該受到保護。 名氣也許會打開通往關注的大門，但它不應該給予媒體一張可以走進每個房間的通行證"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"modern entertainment industry","chinese":"現代娛樂業"},{"english":"fame","chinese":"名氣；成名"},{"english":"come with","chinese":"伴隨着"},{"english":"constant attention","chinese":"持續關注"},{"english":"online platforms","chinese":"網上平台"},{"english":"public exposure","chinese":"公開曝光"},{"english":"the price celebrities pay for success","chinese":"名人為成功付出的代價"},{"english":"in my view","chinese":"在我看來"},{"english":"the media","chinese":"傳媒"},{"english":"publish the private lives of","chinese":"公開……的私生活"},{"english":"famous people","chinese":"名人"},{"english":"unless there is","chinese":"除非有……"},{"english":"clear public interest","chinese":"明確公眾利益"},{"english":"being well known","chinese":"眾所周知；有名氣"},{"english":"remove a person's basic right to","chinese":"取消一個人的基本……權利"},{"english":"basic right to privacy","chinese":"基本私隱權"},{"english":"choose to appear on screen","chinese":"選擇在螢幕上露面"},{"english":"perform on stage","chinese":"在舞台上表演"},{"english":"promote their work online","chinese":"在網上宣傳作品"},{"english":"agreed to have","chinese":"同意讓……"},{"english":"every corner of their personal lives","chinese":"他們私人生活的每個角落"},{"english":"be examined","chinese":"被檢視；被審視"},{"english":"family problems","chinese":"家庭問題"},{"english":"romantic relationships","chinese":"戀愛關係"},{"english":"health issues","chinese":"健康問題"},{"english":"home addresses","chinese":"住址"},{"english":"be irrelevant to","chinese":"與……無關"},{"english":"professional achievements","chinese":"專業成就"},{"english":"journalists","chinese":"記者"},{"english":"follow them to private places","chinese":"跟蹤他們到私人地方"},{"english":"publish photographs of","chinese":"刊登……的照片"},{"english":"intrusion dressed up as news","chinese":"包裝成新聞的侵擾"},{"english":"over time","chinese":"隨着時間過去"},{"english":"such pressure","chinese":"這種壓力"},{"english":"damage mental health","chinese":"損害精神健康"},{"english":"normal family life","chinese":"正常家庭生活"},{"english":"almost impossible","chinese":"幾乎不可能"},{"english":"unrestricted media attention","chinese":"不受限制的傳媒關注"},{"english":"harmful culture of gossip","chinese":"有害的八卦文化"},{"english":"audiences are constantly fed","chinese":"觀眾不斷被灌輸"},{"english":"scandals","chinese":"醜聞"},{"english":"private conflicts","chinese":"私人衝突"},{"english":"see celebrities less as","chinese":"較少將名人視為……"},{"english":"human beings","chinese":"有血有肉的人"},{"english":"public property","chinese":"公共財產"},{"english":"exaggerated","chinese":"被誇大的"},{"english":"misleading","chinese":"具誤導性的"},{"english":"based on moments taken out of context","chinese":"基於被抽離脈絡的片刻"},{"english":"taken out of context","chinese":"被抽離脈絡"},{"english":"tired actor","chinese":"疲倦的演員"},{"english":"arguing with a family member","chinese":"與家人爭吵"},{"english":"be turned into","chinese":"被變成"},{"english":"dramatic headline","chinese":"戲劇化標題"},{"english":"have nothing to do with","chinese":"與……無關"},{"english":"responsible journalism","chinese":"負責任的新聞工作"},{"english":"inform society","chinese":"向社會提供資訊"},{"english":"feed curiosity","chinese":"滿足好奇心"},{"english":"at any cost","chinese":"不惜任何代價"},{"english":"expect public discussion of","chinese":"預期會有關於……的公開討論"},{"english":"professional behaviour","chinese":"專業行為"},{"english":"remain protected","chinese":"繼續受到保護"},{"english":"open the door to","chinese":"打開通往……的大門"},{"english":"give the media a licence to","chinese":"給予傳媒……的許可"},{"english":"walk through every room","chinese":"走進人生的每個房間"}]},"model-essay-21-ielts-advantage-disadvantage":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-21-ielts-advantage-disadvantage","essayKey":"advantage-disadvantage:21","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-21-ielts-advantage-disadvantage","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/advantage-and-disadvantage/EdmundBd9AdDisAd-Q21","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"Household life has been transformed by technology over the past few decades. Tasks that were once done by hand, from washing clothes to cleaning floors, are now routinely handled by machines. Although this trend has created some new problems, I believe it brings far more advantages than disadvantages because it saves time and reduces the physical burden of domestic work.","chinese":"在過去幾十年間，家庭生活已被科技大大改變。 那些過去需要人手完成的工作，從洗衣服到清潔地板，如今都經常由機器處理。 雖然這種趨勢帶來了一些新的問題，但我認為它整體上是利多於弊，因為它能節省時間，並減輕家務勞動所帶來的體力負擔。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"The clearest benefit is efficiency. Machines can perform repetitive chores far more quickly than people can, which allows household members to devote their time to work, childcare or rest instead of routine housework. A washing machine, for example, can clean an entire load of laundry while its user is doing something else. Equally important is the fact that automation has made home life much less physically demanding. Before such appliances became common, many domestic duties involved prolonged standing, scrubbing and lifting, all of which were especially tiring for parents, older people and those in poor health. By taking over much of this domestic drudgery, machines improve comfort as well as overall quality of life.","chinese":"最明顯的好處就是效率提升。 機器執行重複性家務的速度，遠比人手更快。 這使家庭成員能把時間投入工作、照顧孩子或休息，而不是被例行家務佔據。 例如，洗衣機可以在使用者做其他事情的同時，把整桶衣物洗好。 同樣重要的是，自動化也使家庭生活在體力上不再那麼吃力。 在這類家電普及之前，許多家務都涉及長時間站立、刷洗和搬抬，這些工作對父母、長者以及健康欠佳的人尤其辛苦。 透過接手大量繁重而乏味的家務，機器不但提升了生活舒適度，也改善了整體生活質素"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"That said, this development is not entirely harmless. One drawback is overdependence: once people become accustomed to machines, even a simple task may feel difficult when a device breaks down or there is a power cut. Another concern is that some practical household skills may gradually disappear, particularly among younger generations who have never needed to do these jobs manually. However, these disadvantages are relatively limited. Losing the habit of hand-washing clothes is far less serious than spending hours on physically exhausting work every week.","chinese":"話雖如此，這種發展並非完全沒有代價。 其中一個缺點是過度依賴：一旦人們習慣了機器，當電器故障或停電時，即使是簡單的工作也可能變得難以處理。 另一個問題是，一些實用的家務技能可能會逐漸消失，尤其是在從未需要親手做這些工作的年輕一代之中。 不過，這些缺點其實相對有限。 比起每星期花上數小時去做耗費體力的家務，失去手洗衣物的習慣顯然沒有那麼嚴重。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, the mechanisation of household tasks is largely beneficial. Although it can encourage dependence and weaken certain manual skills, its overall effect is to make daily life more efficient, less tiring and more manageable for most families.","chinese":"總結來說，家務機械化整體上是利大於弊的。 雖然它可能助長依賴，並削弱某些手動技能，但它整體上的影響，是讓大多數家庭的日常生活更有效率、更不疲累，也更容易應付。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"household life","chinese":"家庭生活"},{"english":"be transformed by","chinese":"被……改變"},{"english":"over the past few decades","chinese":"在過去幾十年間"},{"english":"done by hand","chinese":"用人手完成"},{"english":"from washing clothes to cleaning floors","chinese":"從洗衣服到清潔地板"},{"english":"routinely handled by machines","chinese":"通常由機器處理"},{"english":"this trend","chinese":"這個趨勢"},{"english":"far more advantages than disadvantages","chinese":"利多於弊"},{"english":"saves time","chinese":"節省時間"},{"english":"reduces the physical burden of","chinese":"減輕……的體力負擔"},{"english":"domestic work","chinese":"家務工作"},{"english":"the clearest benefit","chinese":"最明顯的好處"},{"english":"perform repetitive chores","chinese":"做重複性的家務"},{"english":"far more quickly than","chinese":"比……快得多"},{"english":"household members","chinese":"家庭成員"},{"english":"devote their time to","chinese":"將時間投放於"},{"english":"childcare","chinese":"照顧孩子"},{"english":"routine housework","chinese":"日常家務"},{"english":"an entire load of laundry","chinese":"一整機衣物"},{"english":"while its user is doing something else","chinese":"在使用者做其他事情時"},{"english":"equally important","chinese":"同樣重要的是"},{"english":"automation","chinese":"自動化"},{"english":"made home life much less physically demanding","chinese":"令家居生活體力負擔大大減少"},{"english":"physically demanding","chinese":"體力要求高的"},{"english":"appliances became common","chinese":"電器變得普及"},{"english":"domestic duties","chinese":"家務職責"},{"english":"prolonged standing","chinese":"長時間站立"},{"english":"scrubbing and lifting","chinese":"擦洗和搬抬"},{"english":"especially tiring for","chinese":"對……尤其令人疲累"},{"english":"those in poor health","chinese":"身體狀況欠佳的人"},{"english":"taking over much of","chinese":"接手大部分……"},{"english":"domestic drudgery","chinese":"繁重沉悶的家務"},{"english":"improve comfort","chinese":"提升舒適度"},{"english":"overall quality of life","chinese":"整體生活質素"},{"english":"that said","chinese":"話雖如此"},{"english":"not entirely harmless","chinese":"並非完全無害"},{"english":"one drawback is","chinese":"一個缺點是"},{"english":"overdependence","chinese":"過度依賴"},{"english":"become accustomed to","chinese":"習慣於"},{"english":"a device breaks down","chinese":"裝置壞掉"},{"english":"a power cut","chinese":"停電"},{"english":"another concern is that","chinese":"另一個令人關注的問題是"},{"english":"practical household skills","chinese":"實用家務技能"},{"english":"gradually disappear","chinese":"逐漸消失"},{"english":"younger generations","chinese":"年輕一代"},{"english":"do these jobs manually","chinese":"人手做這些工作"},{"english":"relatively limited","chinese":"相對有限"},{"english":"losing the habit of","chinese":"失去……的習慣"},{"english":"hand-washing clothes","chinese":"人手洗衣服"},{"english":"far less serious than","chinese":"遠沒有……嚴重"},{"english":"physically exhausting work","chinese":"極耗體力的工作"},{"english":"mechanisation of household tasks","chinese":"家務機械化"},{"english":"largely beneficial","chinese":"大致上有益"},{"english":"encourage dependence","chinese":"鼓勵依賴；造成依賴"},{"english":"weaken certain manual skills","chinese":"削弱某些人手技能"},{"english":"its overall effect","chinese":"其整體影響"},{"english":"daily life","chinese":"日常生活"},{"english":"more efficient, less tiring and more manageable","chinese":"更有效率、較不疲累和更易處理"},{"english":"for most families","chinese":"對大多數家庭而言"}]},"model-essay-21-ielts-discuss-both-views":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-21-ielts-discuss-both-views","essayKey":"discuss-both-views:21","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-21-ielts-discuss-both-views","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/discuss-both-views-your-opinion/EdmundBd9ExpBth-Q21","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"Environmental problems are now among the most serious challenges facing humanity. Some argue that global warming should be treated as the greatest threat, while others believe that the destruction of forests does more immediate damage. Although deforestation clearly harms ecosystems and local communities, I believe global warming is the more urgent and far-reaching problem.","chinese":"環境問題如今已成為人類所面對的最嚴重挑戰之一。 有些人認為全球暖化應被視為最大的威脅，而另一些人則認為森林破壞會造成更即時的損害。 儘管砍伐森林明顯會傷害生態系統和本地社群，但我認為全球暖化是更緊迫且影響更深遠的問題。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"Those who regard global warming as the main environmental crisis have a strong argument because it affects almost every part of the planet. Rising temperatures can intensify droughts, floods and heatwaves, making ordinary life more difficult for both rich and poor countries. For example, farmers may lose crops after long dry seasons, while coastal cities may face repeated flooding as sea levels rise. This means that global warming is not only an environmental issue, but also a threat to food security, public health and economic stability. Since its effects spread across borders, it is extremely difficult for any single country to escape them.","chinese":"那些把全球暖化視為主要環境危機的人有很有力的理由，因為它幾乎影響地球的每一個部分。 氣溫上升會加劇乾旱、洪水和熱浪，使富裕國家和貧困國家的日常生活都變得更加困難。 例如，農民可能會在漫長的乾旱季節後失去收成，而沿海城市則可能因海平面上升而反覆面對洪水。 這意味著全球暖化不僅是一個環境問題，也對糧食安全、公共健康和經濟穩定構成威脅 由於它的影響會跨越國界，因此任何單一國家都極難逃避這些後果。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"On the other hand, many people see deforestation as even more destructive because forests are the lungs and living shelters of the earth. When large areas of woodland are cleared for farming, housing or commercial profit, countless animals lose their habitats, soil becomes weaker, and indigenous communities may be pushed off land that has supported them for generations. In addition, trees absorb carbon dioxide, so cutting them down can make climate change worse. In this sense, deforestation is not a small local problem; it can tear apart entire ecosystems and accelerate wider environmental damage.","chinese":"另一方面，許多人認為砍伐森林甚至更具破壞性，因為森林是地球的肺，也是生物賴以生存的庇護所。 當大片林地被清除，用於農業、住房或商業利益時，無數動物會失去棲息地，土壤會變得更脆弱，而原住民社群也可能被迫離開世代依靠的土地。 此外，樹木會吸收二氧化碳，因此砍伐樹木會使氣候變化更加嚴重。 從這個意義上說，砍伐森林並不是一個小型的地方問題；它可以摧毀整個生態系統，並加速更廣泛的環境破壞。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In my view, however, global warming remains the greater threat because it magnifies many other environmental problems, including deforestation itself. A destroyed forest is devastating, but an overheating planet can damage forests, oceans, cities and agriculture at the same time. Therefore, while governments must protect forests, tackling global warming should be the top environmental priority.","chinese":"然而，在我看來，全球暖化仍然是更大的威脅，因為它會放大許多其他環境問題，包括砍伐森林本身。 一片被摧毀的森林固然是災難性的，但一個過熱的地球卻可以同時破壞森林、海洋、城市和農業。 因此，儘管政府必須保護森林，應對全球暖化仍應是最優先的環境任務。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"environmental problems","chinese":"環境問題"},{"english":"among the most serious challenges","chinese":"最嚴重的挑戰之一"},{"english":"facing humanity","chinese":"人類面對的"},{"english":"global warming","chinese":"全球暖化"},{"english":"be treated as","chinese":"被視為"},{"english":"the greatest threat","chinese":"最大威脅"},{"english":"the destruction of forests","chinese":"森林破壞"},{"english":"do more immediate damage","chinese":"造成更即時的破壞"},{"english":"although","chinese":"雖然"},{"english":"deforestation","chinese":"砍伐森林"},{"english":"harm ecosystems","chinese":"破壞生態系統"},{"english":"local communities","chinese":"本地社區"},{"english":"the more urgent and far-reaching problem","chinese":"更迫切且影響深遠的問題"},{"english":"regard ... as","chinese":"將……視為"},{"english":"the main environmental crisis","chinese":"主要環境危機"},{"english":"have a strong argument","chinese":"有有力的論點"},{"english":"affect almost every part of","chinese":"影響……幾乎每個部分"},{"english":"the planet","chinese":"地球"},{"english":"rising temperatures","chinese":"氣溫上升"},{"english":"intensify droughts, floods and heatwaves","chinese":"加劇乾旱、水災和熱浪"},{"english":"ordinary life","chinese":"日常生活"},{"english":"both rich and poor countries","chinese":"富裕國家和貧窮國家"},{"english":"lose crops","chinese":"失去農作物收成"},{"english":"long dry seasons","chinese":"長時間旱季"},{"english":"coastal cities","chinese":"沿海城市"},{"english":"face repeated flooding","chinese":"面對反覆水浸"},{"english":"as sea levels rise","chinese":"隨着海平面上升"},{"english":"sea levels","chinese":"海平面"},{"english":"not only ... but also","chinese":"不但……而且"},{"english":"environmental issue","chinese":"環境問題"},{"english":"a threat to","chinese":"對……的威脅"},{"english":"food security","chinese":"糧食安全"},{"english":"public health","chinese":"公共衞生"},{"english":"economic stability","chinese":"經濟穩定"},{"english":"since","chinese":"由於"},{"english":"spread across borders","chinese":"跨越國界擴散"},{"english":"any single country","chinese":"任何單一國家"},{"english":"escape them","chinese":"逃避它們；避開它們"},{"english":"on the other hand","chinese":"另一方面"},{"english":"even more destructive","chinese":"更具破壞性"},{"english":"the lungs and living shelters of the earth","chinese":"地球的肺和生命庇護所"},{"english":"large areas of woodland","chinese":"大片林地"},{"english":"be cleared for","chinese":"被清除以作"},{"english":"farming, housing or commercial profit","chinese":"農業、房屋或商業利益"},{"english":"countless animals","chinese":"無數動物"},{"english":"lose their habitats","chinese":"失去棲息地"},{"english":"soil becomes weaker","chinese":"土壤變得較脆弱"},{"english":"indigenous communities","chinese":"原住民社群"},{"english":"be pushed off land","chinese":"被迫離開土地"},{"english":"for generations","chinese":"世世代代"},{"english":"in addition","chinese":"此外"},{"english":"absorb carbon dioxide","chinese":"吸收二氧化碳"},{"english":"cutting them down","chinese":"砍伐樹木"},{"english":"make climate change worse","chinese":"令氣候變化惡化"},{"english":"in this sense","chinese":"從這個意義上說"},{"english":"not a small local problem","chinese":"不是小型本地問題"},{"english":"tear apart entire ecosystems","chinese":"破壞整個生態系統"},{"english":"accelerate wider environmental damage","chinese":"加速更廣泛的環境破壞"},{"english":"in my view","chinese":"在我看來"},{"english":"remains the greater threat","chinese":"仍然是更大威脅"},{"english":"magnify many other environmental problems","chinese":"放大許多其他環境問題"},{"english":"including deforestation itself","chinese":"包括砍伐森林本身"},{"english":"a destroyed forest","chinese":"被摧毀的森林"},{"english":"devastating","chinese":"破壞性極大；令人震驚"},{"english":"an overheating planet","chinese":"過熱的地球"},{"english":"at the same time","chinese":"同時"},{"english":"protect forests","chinese":"保護森林"},{"english":"tackling global warming","chinese":"應對全球暖化"},{"english":"the top environmental priority","chinese":"最優先的環境事項"}]},"model-essay-21-ielts-opinion":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-21-ielts-opinion","essayKey":"opinion:21","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-21-ielts-opinion","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/opinions/EdmundBd9OP-Q21","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"It is common for people to form quick impressions from clothing, especially because appearance is often the first thing visible in social interaction. However, I strongly disagree with the view that a person’s dress reveals a great deal about their personality. In my opinion, clothing is more often shaped by circumstance and social expectation than by someone’s inner character.","chinese":"人們常常會從衣著快速形成印象，尤其是因為外表通常是社交互動中最先被看見的東西。 然而，我強烈不同意一個人的衣著能夠大量反映其性格這種看法。 在我看來，衣著更多時候是由處境和社會期望塑造，而不是由一個人的內在性格所決定"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"First, the clothes people wear are frequently determined by external factors. In many workplaces, for instance, employees must follow a dress code, whether they are naturally creative, reserved, confident or unconventional. A lawyer in a dark suit may simply be obeying professional norms, not showing that he is serious in every part of life. Similarly, a student wearing plain or inexpensive clothes may be limited by family income rather than lacking imagination or self-respect. Since clothing is influenced by weather, culture, money, occupation and occasion, it is unsafe to treat it as a clear window into personality. At best, it shows the situation a person is in; it does not reliably reveal who that person is.","chinese":"首先，人們所穿的衣服經常是由外在因素決定的。 例如，在許多工作場所中，員工都必須遵守服裝規定，無論他們本身是有創意、內斂、自信，還是不依常規的人。 一位穿著深色西裝的律師，可能只是遵守專業規範，而不是顯示他在人生每一方面都很嚴肅。 同樣地，一名穿著樸素或廉價衣服的學生，可能只是受家庭收入所限制，而不是缺乏想像力或自尊。 由於衣著會受到天氣、文化、金錢、職業和場合影響，因此把它視為了解性格的清晰窗口並不可靠。 充其量，它只能顯示一個人所處的情境；它並不能可靠地揭示那個人真正是誰。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"Second, people often dress to manage impressions rather than to express their true selves. Someone may wear formal clothes to an interview because they want to appear responsible, while a naturally shy person may choose fashionable outfits to seem more confident in public. In these cases, clothing functions almost like a mask: it helps people play a role, but it does not necessarily expose their deeper values, habits or temperament. If society relies too heavily on appearance, thoughtful people may be underestimated and superficial people may be admired too quickly. This can lead to unfair judgement, where the cover is mistaken for the book.","chinese":"第二，人們穿衣往往是為了管理他人印象，而不是表達真正的自我。 有人可能會在面試時穿正式服裝，因為他們希望看起來負責任；而一個天生害羞的人，也可能選擇時尚的服裝，讓自己在公眾場合顯得更有自信。 在這些情況下，衣著幾乎像一個面具：它幫助人們扮演某種角色，但不一定揭示他們更深層的價值觀、習慣或氣質。 如果社會過度依賴外表作判斷，有思想的人可能會被低估，而膚淺的人則可能太快受到欣賞。 這可能導致不公平的判斷，也就是把封面誤認為整本書本身。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, I strongly disagree that dress speaks volumes about personality. Although clothes can create first impressions, they are too dependent on context, money and social performance to be a reliable measure of character.","chinese":"總結來說，我強烈不同意衣著能充分反映性格這種說法。 雖然衣服可以製造第一印象，但它們太依賴背景、金錢和社交表現，因此不能成為衡量品格的可靠標準。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"form quick impressions","chinese":"形成快速印象"},{"english":"appearance","chinese":"外表"},{"english":"the first thing visible","chinese":"第一樣看得見的東西"},{"english":"social interaction","chinese":"社交互動"},{"english":"strongly disagree with","chinese":"強烈不同意……"},{"english":"reveals a great deal about","chinese":"透露很多有關……的事情"},{"english":"personality","chinese":"性格"},{"english":"in my opinion","chinese":"在我看來"},{"english":"be shaped by","chinese":"受……塑造"},{"english":"circumstance","chinese":"處境；情況"},{"english":"social expectation","chinese":"社會期望"},{"english":"inner character","chinese":"內在性格"},{"english":"be determined by","chinese":"由……決定"},{"english":"external factors","chinese":"外在因素"},{"english":"workplaces","chinese":"工作場所"},{"english":"follow a dress code","chinese":"遵守衣着規定"},{"english":"dress code","chinese":"衣着規定"},{"english":"naturally creative","chinese":"天生有創意"},{"english":"reserved","chinese":"內斂的"},{"english":"unconventional","chinese":"不落俗套的"},{"english":"dark suit","chinese":"深色西裝"},{"english":"professional norms","chinese":"專業規範"},{"english":"not showing that","chinese":"並不是顯示……"},{"english":"in every part of life","chinese":"在生活每個方面"},{"english":"similarly","chinese":"同樣地"},{"english":"plain or inexpensive clothes","chinese":"樸素或便宜的衣服"},{"english":"be limited by","chinese":"受……限制"},{"english":"family income","chinese":"家庭收入"},{"english":"lacking imagination","chinese":"缺乏想像力"},{"english":"self-respect","chinese":"自尊"},{"english":"be influenced by","chinese":"受……影響"},{"english":"occupation","chinese":"職業"},{"english":"occasion","chinese":"場合"},{"english":"unsafe to treat it as","chinese":"將它視為……是不可靠的"},{"english":"clear window into","chinese":"清楚看見……的窗口"},{"english":"at best","chinese":"充其量"},{"english":"the situation a person is in","chinese":"一個人所處的情況"},{"english":"reliably reveal","chinese":"可靠地揭示"},{"english":"who that person is","chinese":"那個人真正是怎樣的人"},{"english":"manage impressions","chinese":"管理別人對自己的印象"},{"english":"express their true selves","chinese":"表達真實自我"},{"english":"formal clothes","chinese":"正式衣服"},{"english":"appear responsible","chinese":"顯得負責任"},{"english":"naturally shy person","chinese":"天生害羞的人"},{"english":"fashionable outfits","chinese":"時尚服裝"},{"english":"seem more confident in public","chinese":"在公眾場合顯得更有自信"},{"english":"in these cases","chinese":"在這些情況下"},{"english":"functions almost like","chinese":"幾乎像……一樣發揮作用"},{"english":"a mask","chinese":"面具"},{"english":"play a role","chinese":"扮演角色"},{"english":"not necessarily expose","chinese":"不一定揭示"},{"english":"deeper values","chinese":"更深層的價值觀"},{"english":"habits or temperament","chinese":"習慣或性情"},{"english":"temperament","chinese":"性情；氣質"},{"english":"relies too heavily on","chinese":"過度依賴"},{"english":"thoughtful people","chinese":"有思想的人"},{"english":"be underestimated","chinese":"被低估"},{"english":"superficial people","chinese":"膚淺的人"},{"english":"be admired too quickly","chinese":"太快受到欣賞"},{"english":"lead to","chinese":"導致"},{"english":"unfair judgement","chinese":"不公平判斷"},{"english":"the cover is mistaken for the book","chinese":"將封面誤當成整本書"},{"english":"dress speaks volumes about","chinese":"衣着充分反映……"},{"english":"first impressions","chinese":"第一印象"},{"english":"dependent on","chinese":"取決於"},{"english":"context","chinese":"語境；情境"},{"english":"social performance","chinese":"社交表現"},{"english":"reliable measure of character","chinese":"衡量性格的可靠標準"}]},"model-essay-22-ielts-advantage-disadvantage":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-22-ielts-advantage-disadvantage","essayKey":"advantage-disadvantage:22","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-22-ielts-advantage-disadvantage","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/advantage-and-disadvantage/EdmundBd9AdDisAd-Q22","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"Labour-saving household appliances have made it increasingly possible for mothers to take paid employment while still raising dependent children. Although some people argue that this can place extra strain on family life, I believe the disadvantages are clearly outweighed by the advantages, chiefly because a working mother can improve a family’s financial security and create a more balanced home environment.","chinese":"省時省力的家用電器，使母親在照顧仍需依賴父母的子女的同時，也越來越有可能從事有薪工作。 儘管有些人認為這種情況會為家庭生活帶來額外壓力， 我認為其缺點明顯小於優點，主要原因在於，母親工作不但能提升家庭的經濟保障，亦能建立一個更平衡的家庭環境。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"The first major advantage is economic stability. When both parents earn an income, the household is less vulnerable to inflation, unexpected medical bills, or the loss of one job. This greater financial resilience allows parents to provide better food, safer housing, and stronger educational support, which directly benefits children. For example, a dual-income family may be able to afford reliable childcare, private tutoring, or a home in a better school district, opportunities that might otherwise be out of reach. Just as importantly, reduced financial pressure often leads to fewer arguments over money, so the home becomes calmer and more secure for everyone.","chinese":"第一個主要優點是經濟穩定。 當父母雙方都有收入時，家庭便較不容易受到通貨膨脹、突如其來的醫療開支或其中一方失業的影響。 更強的經濟抗壓能力，能讓父母為孩子提供更好的飲食、更安全的居住環境，以及更充足的教育支援，而這些都會直接令孩子受益。 例如，雙收入家庭可能有能力負擔可靠的托兒服務、私人補習，或搬到校網更佳的地區居住，而這些機會本來可能是他們無法取得的。 同樣重要的是，經濟壓力減輕通常也會減少因金錢而起的爭執，因此整個家庭對每一位成員而言都會變得更平靜、更有安全感。 當父母不再時刻為帳單和開支憂心時，他們更有可能保持耐性、願意合作，並在情感上更能照顧孩子的需要。 例如，一個收入較穩定的家庭，家中衝突往往會較少，這使父母能把時間用來支持孩子，而不是爭論金錢問題。 因此，母親就業所帶來的更大經濟保障，不但能在物質上加強家庭，也能在情感層面令家庭更穩固。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"A second benefit is that maternal employment can improve the overall culture of the family. Children who see their mother contributing professionally are more likely to grow up with a healthier understanding of responsibility, independence, and gender equality. A daughter may learn that motherhood does not require economic dependence, while a son may be less likely to assume that childcare and housework are solely female duties. Admittedly, there are drawbacks, most notably reduced time at home and the risk of fatigue. However, these problems are usually manageable through modern appliances, childcare arrangements, and a fairer division of labour between parents. In other words, a small loss of time is far less damaging than long-term financial insecurity or an unequal family structure.","chinese":"第二個優點是，母親工作可以改善整個家庭的文化與價值觀。 當孩子看見母親在職場上作出貢獻時，他們更有可能在成長過程中建立對責任感、獨立性以及性別平等的更健康理解。 這有助他們明白，男性與女性都可以支撐家庭、作出決策，並對社會作出有意義的貢獻。 例如，女兒可能會明白，成為母親並不代表必須在經濟上依附他人；而兒子則較不會認為照顧孩子和做家務只是女性的責任。 誠然，這樣的安排亦有缺點，其中最明顯的是母親留在家中的時間減少，以及更容易感到疲累。 然而，這些問題通常可以透過現代家電、適當的托兒安排，以及父母之間更公平的家務分工來加以處理。 例如，若父母雙方共同分擔家務，並善用節省時間的家用電器，母親的負擔便可大幅減輕，令這些缺點變得沒有那麼嚴重。 換言之，與長遠的經濟不穩定或不平等的家庭結構相比，少量相處時間的減少所造成的影響其實小得多。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, when a mother works, the family usually gains not only a stronger financial foundation but also a more modern and balanced set of values. While this arrangement can create some practical pressure, the disadvantages are limited and do not outweigh the substantial long-term benefits.","chinese":"總結而言，當母親工作時，家庭通常不但能獲得更穩固的經濟基礎，亦能建立一套更現代、更平衡的價值觀。 雖然這種安排可能帶來一些實際壓力，但其缺點是有限的，並不足以超過那些重大的長遠利益。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"labour-saving household appliances","chinese":"節省勞力的家用電器"},{"english":"increasingly possible for","chinese":"令……越來越有可能"},{"english":"take paid employment","chinese":"從事受薪工作"},{"english":"raise dependent children","chinese":"撫養需要照顧的子女"},{"english":"dependent children","chinese":"需要供養的子女"},{"english":"place extra strain on","chinese":"對……造成額外壓力"},{"english":"family life","chinese":"家庭生活"},{"english":"be clearly outweighed by","chinese":"明顯被……蓋過"},{"english":"chiefly because","chinese":"主要因為"},{"english":"a working mother","chinese":"在職母親"},{"english":"financial security","chinese":"經濟保障"},{"english":"a more balanced home environment","chinese":"更平衡的家庭環境"},{"english":"economic stability","chinese":"經濟穩定"},{"english":"earn an income","chinese":"賺取收入"},{"english":"less vulnerable to","chinese":"較不易受……影響"},{"english":"inflation","chinese":"通脹"},{"english":"unexpected medical bills","chinese":"意料之外的醫療費用"},{"english":"the loss of one job","chinese":"失去其中一份工作"},{"english":"financial resilience","chinese":"財務抗壓能力"},{"english":"educational support","chinese":"教育支援"},{"english":"directly benefits children","chinese":"直接令孩子受惠"},{"english":"a dual-income family","chinese":"雙收入家庭"},{"english":"reliable childcare","chinese":"可靠的托兒服務"},{"english":"private tutoring","chinese":"私人補習"},{"english":"a better school district","chinese":"較好的校區"},{"english":"otherwise be out of reach","chinese":"否則難以負擔；難以得到"},{"english":"just as importantly","chinese":"同樣重要的是"},{"english":"reduced financial pressure","chinese":"減少了的經濟壓力"},{"english":"arguments over money","chinese":"關於金錢的爭拗"},{"english":"calmer and more secure","chinese":"更平靜和更有安全感"},{"english":"maternal employment","chinese":"母親就業"},{"english":"the overall culture of the family","chinese":"家庭的整體文化"},{"english":"contributing professionally","chinese":"在專業上作出貢獻"},{"english":"be more likely to grow up with","chinese":"更有可能在成長中形成"},{"english":"a healthier understanding of","chinese":"對……更健康的理解"},{"english":"responsibility, independence and gender equality","chinese":"責任感、獨立和性別平等"},{"english":"economic dependence","chinese":"經濟依賴"},{"english":"be less likely to assume that","chinese":"較不會假設"},{"english":"childcare and housework","chinese":"照顧子女和家務"},{"english":"solely female duties","chinese":"純粹女性的責任"},{"english":"admittedly","chinese":"無可否認"},{"english":"reduced time at home","chinese":"在家的時間減少"},{"english":"the risk of fatigue","chinese":"疲勞的風險"},{"english":"manageable through","chinese":"可透過……處理"},{"english":"childcare arrangements","chinese":"托兒安排"},{"english":"a fairer division of labour","chinese":"更公平的分工"},{"english":"between parents","chinese":"父母之間"},{"english":"in other words","chinese":"換言之"},{"english":"a small loss of time","chinese":"少量時間上的損失"},{"english":"far less damaging than","chinese":"遠比……破壞性小"},{"english":"long-term financial insecurity","chinese":"長期經濟不穩"},{"english":"an unequal family structure","chinese":"不平等的家庭結構"},{"english":"gains not only","chinese":"不但得到"},{"english":"a stronger financial foundation","chinese":"更穩固的經濟基礎"},{"english":"a more modern and balanced set of values","chinese":"更現代和更平衡的價值觀"},{"english":"this arrangement","chinese":"這種安排"},{"english":"practical pressure","chinese":"實際壓力"},{"english":"do not outweigh","chinese":"不會大於"},{"english":"substantial long-term benefits","chinese":"重大的長遠好處"}]},"model-essay-22-ielts-discuss-both-views":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-22-ielts-discuss-both-views","essayKey":"discuss-both-views:22","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-22-ielts-discuss-both-views","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/discuss-both-views-your-opinion/EdmundBd9ExpBth-Q22","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"Environmental damage has become one of the defining concerns of modern life, affecting air, water, food systems and public health. Some argue that these problems are international in nature and therefore require government intervention, while others believe they can only be solved through individual responsibility. I firmly believe that governments must take the lead, because only they have the authority and resources to create changes on the scale required.","chinese":"環境破壞已成為現代生活中其中一個最具代表性的重大問題，影響著空氣、水資源、食物系統以及公共健康。 有些人認為這些問題本質上是國際性的，因此需要政府介入；而另一些人則相信，這些問題只能透過個人責任來解決。 我堅定地認為，政府必須發揮主導作用，因為只有政府才擁有足夠的權力和資源，去推動所需規模的改變。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"Those who support government action point out that many environmental problems are too large for private citizens to control. Climate change, industrial pollution and deforestation are not caused merely by careless household habits, but by national energy systems, transport networks and corporate activity. If a factory releases toxic waste into a river, for instance, ordinary residents may complain or boycott its products, but they cannot legally force it to change its production methods. Governments, by contrast, can impose strict regulations, fine polluters, invest in renewable energy and cooperate with other countries. Without this level of authority, environmental protection becomes a matter of goodwill rather than enforceable responsibility.","chinese":"支持政府行動的人指出，許多環境問題規模太大，並非普通市民能夠控制。 氣候變化、工業污染和森林砍伐，並不只是由粗心大意的家庭習慣造成，而是由國家能源系統、交通網絡和企業活動所造成。 例如，如果一間工廠把有毒廢料排入河流，普通居民可以投訴或抵制它的產品，但他們不能在法律上強制它改變生產方式。 相比之下，政府可以實施嚴格規管、懲罰污染者、投資可再生能源，並與其他國家合作 如果沒有這種層次的權力，環境保護就會變成一種善意行為，而不是可以被強制執行的責任。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"On the other hand, supporters of individual action argue that laws alone will not work if people continue to live wastefully. Everyday choices such as driving less, recycling properly, reducing plastic use and avoiding excessive consumption can collectively reduce pressure on the planet. For example, if millions of households waste less food and electricity, demand for energy and resources will fall. This view is reasonable because environmental damage is not only created in boardrooms and factories; it is also fed by ordinary routines. However, individual effort is like carrying water in a cup when the main pipe is still leaking: useful, but far from sufficient.","chinese":"另一方面，支持個人行動的人認為，如果人們繼續以浪費的方式生活，單靠法律並不能奏效。 日常選擇，例如減少駕車、正確回收、減少使用塑膠以及避免過度消費，都可以共同減輕地球的壓力。 例如，如果數百萬個家庭減少浪費食物和電力，對能源和資源的需求便會下降。 這種觀點是合理的，因為環境破壞不只是在董事會會議室和工廠中產生；它也受到日常生活習慣的推動。 然而，個人努力就像主水管仍在漏水時用杯子盛水一樣：有用，但遠遠不足夠。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, individuals should certainly behave more responsibly, but environmental issues cannot be left mainly to personal choice. Governments are best placed to regulate industries, shape infrastructure and coordinate international action, so they should bear the central responsibility for tackling today’s environmental crisis.","chinese":"總結來說，個人當然應該表現得更負責任，但環境問題不能主要交由個人選擇來處理。 政府最適合去規管產業、塑造基礎建設，並協調國際行動，因此它們應該承擔處理當今環境危機的核心責任。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"environmental damage","chinese":"環境破壞"},{"english":"one of the defining concerns of","chinese":"……中最具代表性的關注之一"},{"english":"modern life","chinese":"現代生活"},{"english":"affecting air, water, food systems and public health","chinese":"影響空氣、水、食物系統和公共衞生"},{"english":"international in nature","chinese":"本質上屬國際性"},{"english":"require government intervention","chinese":"需要政府干預"},{"english":"individual responsibility","chinese":"個人責任"},{"english":"firmly believe that","chinese":"堅信"},{"english":"take the lead","chinese":"帶頭；主導"},{"english":"authority and resources","chinese":"權力和資源"},{"english":"on the scale required","chinese":"達到所需規模"},{"english":"government action","chinese":"政府行動"},{"english":"point out that","chinese":"指出"},{"english":"too large for","chinese":"對……來說太大"},{"english":"private citizens","chinese":"普通公民"},{"english":"climate change","chinese":"氣候變化"},{"english":"industrial pollution","chinese":"工業污染"},{"english":"deforestation","chinese":"砍伐森林"},{"english":"not caused merely by","chinese":"並不只是由……造成"},{"english":"careless household habits","chinese":"不謹慎的家庭習慣"},{"english":"national energy systems","chinese":"國家能源系統"},{"english":"transport networks","chinese":"交通網絡"},{"english":"corporate activity","chinese":"企業活動"},{"english":"releases toxic waste into","chinese":"將有毒廢物排入"},{"english":"toxic waste","chinese":"有毒廢物"},{"english":"ordinary residents","chinese":"普通居民"},{"english":"boycott its products","chinese":"抵制其產品"},{"english":"legally force it to","chinese":"從法律上強制其"},{"english":"change its production methods","chinese":"改變其生產方式"},{"english":"by contrast","chinese":"相反"},{"english":"impose strict regulations","chinese":"實施嚴格規管"},{"english":"fine polluters","chinese":"向污染者罰款"},{"english":"invest in renewable energy","chinese":"投資可再生能源"},{"english":"cooperate with other countries","chinese":"與其他國家合作"},{"english":"without this level of authority","chinese":"沒有這種程度的權力"},{"english":"environmental protection","chinese":"環境保護"},{"english":"a matter of goodwill","chinese":"善意的事情"},{"english":"rather than enforceable responsibility","chinese":"而不是可執行的責任"},{"english":"supporters of individual action","chinese":"個人行動的支持者"},{"english":"laws alone","chinese":"單靠法律"},{"english":"continue to live wastefully","chinese":"繼續浪費地生活"},{"english":"everyday choices","chinese":"日常選擇"},{"english":"driving less","chinese":"少些駕車"},{"english":"recycling properly","chinese":"正確回收"},{"english":"reducing plastic use","chinese":"減少塑膠使用"},{"english":"avoiding excessive consumption","chinese":"避免過度消費"},{"english":"collectively reduce pressure on","chinese":"共同減輕對……的壓力"},{"english":"the planet","chinese":"地球"},{"english":"millions of households","chinese":"數以百萬計的家庭"},{"english":"waste less food and electricity","chinese":"少浪費食物和電力"},{"english":"demand for energy and resources","chinese":"對能源和資源的需求"},{"english":"this view is reasonable","chinese":"這個看法是合理的"},{"english":"boardrooms and factories","chinese":"會議室和工廠"},{"english":"be fed by","chinese":"由……助長"},{"english":"ordinary routines","chinese":"日常習慣"},{"english":"individual effort","chinese":"個人努力"},{"english":"carrying water in a cup","chinese":"用杯裝水"},{"english":"the main pipe is still leaking","chinese":"主水管仍在漏水"},{"english":"far from sufficient","chinese":"遠遠不足夠"},{"english":"behave more responsibly","chinese":"表現得更負責任"},{"english":"cannot be left mainly to","chinese":"不能主要交由……處理"},{"english":"personal choice","chinese":"個人選擇"},{"english":"be best placed to","chinese":"最有條件去"},{"english":"regulate industries","chinese":"規管行業"},{"english":"shape infrastructure","chinese":"塑造基建"},{"english":"coordinate international action","chinese":"協調國際行動"},{"english":"bear the central responsibility for","chinese":"承擔……的核心責任"},{"english":"tackling today's environmental crisis","chinese":"應對當今環境危機"}]},"model-essay-22-ielts-opinion":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-22-ielts-opinion","essayKey":"opinion:22","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-22-ielts-opinion","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/opinions/EdmundBd9OP-Q22","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"With digital technology now embedded in everyday life, many people predict that direct human interaction will eventually disappear. I completely disagree with this view. Although the internet and text messaging have changed the speed and convenience of communication, they cannot replace the emotional depth, trust, and practical value of meeting people in person.","chinese":"隨著數位科技如今已融入日常生活，許多人預測直接的人際互動最終將會消失。 我完全不同意這種觀點。 儘管互聯網和文字訊息改變了溝通的速度與便利性，它們無法取代面對面見面所帶來的情感深度、信任，以及實際價值。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"The strongest reason is that face-to-face communication carries human signals that written messages often flatten or distort. Tone of voice, eye contact, facial expression and body language all help people understand not only what is being said, but also how it is meant. Without these cues, even a simple sentence can be misunderstood, especially in sensitive situations. For example, a manager who needs to comfort an anxious employee, or a doctor who must explain bad news to a patient, cannot rely only on short written messages. In such moments, physical presence acts as a bridge between information and empathy. This is why direct interaction will remain essential wherever trust, reassurance and emotional intelligence are required.","chinese":"最有力的原因是，面對面溝通承載人性的訊號，而文字訊息往往會削弱或扭曲這些訊號 語氣、眼神接觸、面部表情和肢體語言，都能幫助人們理解的不只是說話的內容，還包括說話背後真正的意思。 如果沒有這些線索，即使是一句簡單的話也可能被誤解，尤其是在敏感情況之中。 例如，一位需要安慰焦慮員工的經理，或者一位必須向病人解釋壞消息的醫生，都不能只依賴簡短的文字訊息。 在這些時刻，實際在場就像資訊與同理心之間的一座橋樑。 這就是為甚麼凡是需要信任、安撫和情緒智慧的地方，直接互動都仍然會是不可或缺的"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"Another reason is that many parts of social and professional life still depend on shared physical experience. Families build closeness around meals, friends strengthen relationships through shared activities, and workplaces often solve complex problems more effectively when people are in the same room. Online tools may help people stay in contact, but they do not fully recreate the rhythm of real conversation, where ideas can be exchanged, challenged and refined instantly. A group of colleagues brainstorming around a table, for instance, can read one another’s reactions and adjust their thinking in real time. This makes face-to-face interaction not an outdated habit, but a living part of how societies cooperate.","chinese":"另一個原因是，社交和職業生活中的許多部分仍然依賴共同的實體經驗。 家庭會在一起用餐時建立親近感，朋友會透過共同活動加強關係，而當人們身處同一個房間時，職場也往往能更有效地解決複雜問題。 線上工具或許能幫助人們保持聯繫，但它們無法完全重現真實對話的節奏；在真實對話中，想法可以即時被交換、挑戰和完善。 例如，一群同事圍著桌子腦力激盪時，可以讀懂彼此的反應，並即時調整自己的思路 這使得面對面互動並不是一種過時的習慣，而是社會合作方式中仍然鮮活的一部分。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, I completely reject the idea that face-to-face communication will become obsolete. Digital communication will continue to grow, but direct human contact will remain irreplaceable because it provides emotional clarity, builds trust and supports real social connection.","chinese":"總結來說，我完全反對面對面溝通將會變得過時這一想法。 數位溝通將會繼續發展，但直接的人際接觸仍然無可取代，因為它能提供情感上的清晰度、建立信任，並支持真正的社會連結。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"digital technology","chinese":"數碼科技"},{"english":"be embedded in","chinese":"融入……之中"},{"english":"everyday life","chinese":"日常生活"},{"english":"direct human interaction","chinese":"直接人際互動"},{"english":"eventually disappear","chinese":"最終消失"},{"english":"the internet and text messaging","chinese":"互聯網和文字訊息溝通"},{"english":"changed the speed and convenience of","chinese":"改變了……的速度和便利"},{"english":"communication","chinese":"溝通"},{"english":"cannot replace","chinese":"不能取代"},{"english":"emotional depth","chinese":"情感深度"},{"english":"practical value","chinese":"實際價值"},{"english":"meeting people in person","chinese":"親身見面"},{"english":"the strongest reason","chinese":"最有力的原因"},{"english":"face-to-face communication","chinese":"面對面溝通"},{"english":"human signals","chinese":"人際信號"},{"english":"written messages","chinese":"書面訊息"},{"english":"flatten or distort","chinese":"淡化或扭曲"},{"english":"tone of voice","chinese":"語氣"},{"english":"eye contact","chinese":"眼神接觸"},{"english":"facial expression","chinese":"面部表情"},{"english":"body language","chinese":"肢體語言"},{"english":"not only what is being said","chinese":"不只是所說的內容"},{"english":"how it is meant","chinese":"說話背後的意思"},{"english":"without these cues","chinese":"沒有這些線索"},{"english":"be misunderstood","chinese":"被誤解"},{"english":"sensitive situations","chinese":"敏感情況"},{"english":"comfort an anxious employee","chinese":"安撫焦慮的員工"},{"english":"anxious employee","chinese":"焦慮的員工"},{"english":"explain bad news to","chinese":"向……解釋壞消息"},{"english":"rely only on","chinese":"只依賴"},{"english":"short written messages","chinese":"簡短書面訊息"},{"english":"in such moments","chinese":"在這些時刻"},{"english":"physical presence","chinese":"親身在場"},{"english":"acts as a bridge between","chinese":"成為……之間的橋樑"},{"english":"information and empathy","chinese":"資料和同理心"},{"english":"direct interaction","chinese":"直接互動"},{"english":"remain essential","chinese":"仍然必不可少"},{"english":"wherever","chinese":"在任何……的地方"},{"english":"trust and reassurance","chinese":"信任和安心感"},{"english":"emotional intelligence","chinese":"情緒智能"},{"english":"be required","chinese":"被需要"},{"english":"social and professional life","chinese":"社交和職業生活"},{"english":"depend on","chinese":"依賴"},{"english":"shared physical experience","chinese":"共同的實體經歷"},{"english":"build closeness around meals","chinese":"透過一起吃飯建立親密感"},{"english":"strengthen relationships","chinese":"加強關係"},{"english":"shared activities","chinese":"共同活動"},{"english":"solve complex problems","chinese":"解決複雜問題"},{"english":"more effectively","chinese":"更有效地"},{"english":"in the same room","chinese":"在同一房間"},{"english":"online tools","chinese":"網上工具"},{"english":"stay in contact","chinese":"保持聯絡"},{"english":"fully recreate","chinese":"完全重現"},{"english":"rhythm of real conversation","chinese":"真實對話的節奏"},{"english":"be exchanged, challenged and refined","chinese":"被交流、質疑和完善"},{"english":"instantly","chinese":"即時"},{"english":"group of colleagues","chinese":"一群同事"},{"english":"brainstorming around a table","chinese":"圍坐桌旁腦力激盪"},{"english":"read one another's reactions","chinese":"讀懂彼此的反應"},{"english":"adjust their thinking","chinese":"調整想法"},{"english":"in real time","chinese":"即時"},{"english":"outdated habit","chinese":"過時習慣"},{"english":"living part of","chinese":"……中活生生的一部分"},{"english":"societies cooperate","chinese":"社會如何合作"},{"english":"completely reject the idea that","chinese":"完全否定……的想法"},{"english":"become obsolete","chinese":"變得過時；被淘汰"},{"english":"digital communication","chinese":"數碼溝通"},{"english":"continue to grow","chinese":"繼續發展"},{"english":"direct human contact","chinese":"直接人際接觸"},{"english":"remain irreplaceable","chinese":"仍然無可取代"},{"english":"emotional clarity","chinese":"情感上的清晰度"},{"english":"builds trust","chinese":"建立信任"},{"english":"real social connection","chinese":"真實社交連繫"}]},"model-essay-23-ielts-advantage-disadvantage":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-23-ielts-advantage-disadvantage","essayKey":"advantage-disadvantage:23","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-23-ielts-advantage-disadvantage","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/advantage-and-disadvantage/EdmundBd9AdDisAd-Q23","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"In recent decades, the expansion of tourism and other forms of international contact has helped English become the most widely used language in the world. As a result, some people believe that humanity may one day share a single common tongue. Such a development would offer notable practical benefits, but it would also carry profound cultural and social costs.","chinese":"近幾十年來，旅遊業的發展以及其他形式的國際交流，促使英語成為世界上最廣泛使用的語言。 因此，有些人相信，人類有一天可能會共用一種共同語言。 這樣的發展會帶來顯著的實際好處，但同時也會付出深遠的文化與社會代價。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"The most obvious advantage of one global language is ease of communication. If people from different countries could speak to one another without interpreters or translation software, travel, trade, diplomacy and academic collaboration would all become more efficient. Misunderstandings could be reduced, and ideas could cross borders far more quickly. A common language could also widen access to education and employment. Students would be able to study abroad more easily, while workers could compete in a broader international labour market. In this sense, a shared language could act as a bridge, bringing people into closer contact with one another.","chinese":"全球只使用一種語言最明顯的優點，就是溝通會變得更容易。 如果來自不同國家的人能夠在沒有口譯員或翻譯軟體的情況下彼此交流，那麼旅遊、貿易、外交以及學術合作都會變得更有效率。 這樣一來，誤解可以減少，而各種想法也能更快速地跨越國界傳播。 例如，如果研究同一項醫療問題的國際研究人員都使用同一種語言，他們便能直接交換研究成果，並更快找到解決方法。 一種共同語言也可以擴大人們接受教育和獲得工作的機會。 學生將更容易到海外升學，而勞工也能在更廣闊的國際就業市場中競爭。 從這個角度來看，共通語言就像一座橋樑，使人與人之間的聯繫更加緊密。 因此，全球共用一種語言可以大大提升效率、流動性以及國際合作。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"However, serious disadvantages would also arise. Language is not merely a tool for exchanging information; it is also a carrier of memory, identity and tradition. If smaller languages were pushed aside by a global one, communities could lose folk stories, historical knowledge and cultural values that have been passed down for generations. In addition, a one-language world might not be as fair as it appears. Those born into the dominant language would enjoy an immediate advantage in business, media and higher education, whereas others might feel compelled to abandon their mother tongue in order to succeed. What is gained in convenience, therefore, could be paid for in cultural erosion and social imbalance.","chinese":"然而，這樣的情況也會帶來嚴重的缺點，其中最重要的就是語言與文化多樣性可能流失。 語言不僅僅是交換資訊的工具，它同時也是記憶、身份認同與傳統的載體。 如果較小的語言被全球通用語所取代，社群便可能失去那些代代相傳的民間故事、歷史知識以及文化價值。 例如，當一種少數語言消失時，那種獨特的世界觀與表達方式也可能隨之消失。 此外，只有一種語言的世界，未必像表面看起來那麼公平。 以主導語言為母語的人，會在商業、媒體和高等教育方面立刻擁有優勢；相反，其他人則可能被迫放棄母語，以換取成功的機會。 因此，便利所帶來的收穫，可能要以文化侵蝕與社會失衡作為代價。 因此，雖然一種共同語言可能使生活變得更簡單，但它也可能削弱文化認同，並加深不平等。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, having one language worldwide could simplify communication and create wider educational and economic opportunities. Nevertheless, it could also accelerate the loss of linguistic heritage and reinforce inequality between native and non-native speakers.","chinese":"總結來說，全球只使用一種語言可以簡化溝通，並創造更廣泛的教育與經濟機會。 然而，它同時也可能加速語言文化遺產的流失，並強化母語者與非母語者之間的不平等。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"in recent decades","chinese":"近幾十年來"},{"english":"the expansion of tourism","chinese":"旅遊業的擴張"},{"english":"other forms of international contact","chinese":"其他形式的國際接觸"},{"english":"the most widely used language","chinese":"最廣泛使用的語言"},{"english":"as a result","chinese":"因此；結果"},{"english":"humanity","chinese":"人類"},{"english":"one day","chinese":"有一天"},{"english":"share a single common tongue","chinese":"共享一種共同語言"},{"english":"such a development","chinese":"這樣的發展"},{"english":"notable practical benefits","chinese":"顯著的實際好處"},{"english":"carry profound cultural and social costs","chinese":"帶來深遠的文化和社會代價"},{"english":"the most obvious advantage of","chinese":"……最明顯的好處"},{"english":"one global language","chinese":"一種全球語言"},{"english":"ease of communication","chinese":"溝通便利"},{"english":"speak to one another","chinese":"彼此交談"},{"english":"without interpreters or translation software","chinese":"無需傳譯員或翻譯軟件"},{"english":"translation software","chinese":"翻譯軟件"},{"english":"travel, trade, diplomacy and academic collaboration","chinese":"旅遊、貿易、外交和學術合作"},{"english":"academic collaboration","chinese":"學術合作"},{"english":"become more efficient","chinese":"變得更有效率"},{"english":"misunderstandings could be reduced","chinese":"誤解可以減少"},{"english":"cross borders","chinese":"跨越國界"},{"english":"far more quickly","chinese":"快得多"},{"english":"widen access to","chinese":"擴大接觸……的機會"},{"english":"education and employment","chinese":"教育和就業"},{"english":"study abroad","chinese":"到海外升學"},{"english":"compete in","chinese":"在……中競爭"},{"english":"a broader international labour market","chinese":"更廣闊的國際勞動市場"},{"english":"in this sense","chinese":"從這個意義上說"},{"english":"a shared language","chinese":"共同語言"},{"english":"act as a bridge","chinese":"發揮橋樑作用"},{"english":"bring people into closer contact with","chinese":"令……更緊密接觸"},{"english":"serious disadvantages would also arise","chinese":"嚴重缺點也會出現"},{"english":"not merely a tool for","chinese":"不只是用來……的工具"},{"english":"exchanging information","chinese":"交換資料"},{"english":"a carrier of memory, identity and tradition","chinese":"記憶、身份和傳統的載體"},{"english":"smaller languages","chinese":"較小語言"},{"english":"pushed aside by","chinese":"被……排擠"},{"english":"communities","chinese":"社群"},{"english":"folk stories","chinese":"民間故事"},{"english":"historical knowledge","chinese":"歷史知識"},{"english":"cultural values","chinese":"文化價值"},{"english":"passed down for generations","chinese":"世代相傳"},{"english":"in addition","chinese":"此外"},{"english":"a one-language world","chinese":"單一語言的世界"},{"english":"as fair as it appears","chinese":"像表面看來那樣公平"},{"english":"born into","chinese":"生於……之中"},{"english":"the dominant language","chinese":"主導語言"},{"english":"enjoy an immediate advantage","chinese":"享有即時優勢"},{"english":"higher education","chinese":"高等教育"},{"english":"whereas","chinese":"然而；而"},{"english":"feel compelled to","chinese":"感到被迫去……"},{"english":"abandon their mother tongue","chinese":"放棄母語"},{"english":"in order to succeed","chinese":"為了成功"},{"english":"what is gained in convenience","chinese":"在便利上得到的東西"},{"english":"be paid for in","chinese":"以……為代價"},{"english":"cultural erosion","chinese":"文化侵蝕"},{"english":"social imbalance","chinese":"社會失衡"},{"english":"having one language worldwide","chinese":"全球使用一種語言"},{"english":"simplify communication","chinese":"簡化溝通"},{"english":"create wider educational and economic opportunities","chinese":"創造更廣泛的教育和經濟機會"},{"english":"nevertheless","chinese":"然而；儘管如此"},{"english":"accelerate the loss of","chinese":"加速……的流失"},{"english":"linguistic heritage","chinese":"語言遺產"},{"english":"reinforce inequality between","chinese":"加深……之間的不平等"},{"english":"native and non-native speakers","chinese":"母語和非母語使用者"}]},"model-essay-23-ielts-discuss-both-views":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-23-ielts-discuss-both-views","essayKey":"discuss-both-views:23","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-23-ielts-discuss-both-views","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/discuss-both-views-your-opinion/EdmundBd9ExpBth-Q23","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"Parents play a decisive role in shaping both the behaviour and the emotional development of their children. While some people believe that parents should mainly correct misbehaviour and teach moral values, others argue that their most important duty is to offer care, security and a stable home. In my view, although discipline is necessary, nurturing children in a safe environment is the more fundamental responsibility.","chinese":"父母在塑造孩子的行為和情感發展方面扮演著決定性的角色。 有些人認為父母主要應該糾正不當行為並教導道德價值，而另一些人則認為父母最重要的責任是提供關愛、安全感和穩定的家庭。 在我看來，雖然紀律是必要的，但在安全的環境中培育孩子才是更根本的責任。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"On the one hand, discipline is clearly an essential part of parenting because children are not born with a complete understanding of acceptable behaviour. Without guidance, they may struggle to respect rules, control their impulses or consider the feelings of others. For example, a child who is never corrected for lying, shouting or behaving selfishly may carry these habits into school and later into adult relationships. In this sense, parents act as a child’s first moral compass: they help children distinguish right from wrong before society has to impose harsher consequences. Good discipline, therefore, does not simply punish children; it teaches them self-control, responsibility and respect for others.","chinese":"一方面，紀律顯然是育兒中不可或缺的一部分，因為孩子並不是天生就完全明白甚麼行為是可以接受的。 如果沒有引導，他們可能會難以尊重規則、控制衝動，或顧及他人的感受。 例如，一個從未因說謊、大叫或自私行為而被糾正的孩子，可能會把這些習慣帶到學校，甚至日後帶進成年後的人際關係之中。 從這個意義上說，父母就像孩子最早的道德指南針：他們在社會不得不施加更嚴厲後果之前，先幫助孩子分辨是非對錯。 因此，良好的紀律並不只是懲罰孩子；它教會孩子自制力、責任感和對他人的尊重。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"On the other hand, I believe that emotional care and safety form the foundation on which all other lessons depend. A child who feels loved, protected and listened to is far more likely to accept guidance from parents, whereas a child raised mainly through fear may obey rules only temporarily. For instance, if parents respond to mistakes with calm explanations rather than constant anger, children can learn from failure without feeling worthless. A secure home also supports mental health, confidence and curiosity, all of which are vital for long-term development. Discipline without nurture is like building walls without a roof: it may create boundaries, but it does not provide true shelter.","chinese":"另一方面，我認為情感上的照顧和安全感構成了所有其他教育所依賴的基礎。 一個感到被愛、被保護和被聆聽的孩子，更有可能接受父母的引導；相反，一個主要在恐懼中長大的孩子，可能只會暫時服從規則。 例如，如果父母在孩子犯錯時以冷靜的解釋回應，而不是持續憤怒，孩子便能從失敗中學習，而不會覺得自己毫無價值。 一個安全的家庭也能支持心理健康、自信心和好奇心，而這些都對長遠發展至關重要。 沒有關愛的紀律就像建造沒有屋頂的牆壁：它或許能建立界線，卻不能提供真正的庇護"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, parents should certainly teach their children right from wrong, as discipline helps them become responsible members of society. However, their primary duty is to nurture them and provide a safe environment, because children can only grow into balanced and moral adults when they first feel secure, valued and emotionally supported.","chinese":"總結來說，父母當然應該教孩子分辨是非，因為紀律能幫助他們成為負責任的社會成員 然而，父母的首要責任是培育孩子並提供安全的環境，因為孩子只有先感到安全、被重視和在情感上受到支持，才能成長為平衡而有道德感的成年人。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"play a decisive role in","chinese":"在……中扮演決定性角色"},{"english":"shape both","chinese":"同時塑造"},{"english":"emotional development","chinese":"情緒發展"},{"english":"mainly correct misbehaviour","chinese":"主要糾正不當行為"},{"english":"teach moral values","chinese":"教導品德價值"},{"english":"their most important duty","chinese":"他們最重要的責任"},{"english":"offer care, security and a stable home","chinese":"提供照顧、安全感和穩定家庭"},{"english":"in my view","chinese":"在我看來"},{"english":"discipline is necessary","chinese":"管教是必要的"},{"english":"nurturing children","chinese":"培育孩子"},{"english":"a safe environment","chinese":"安全環境"},{"english":"the more fundamental responsibility","chinese":"更基本的責任"},{"english":"on the one hand","chinese":"一方面"},{"english":"an essential part of parenting","chinese":"育兒的重要部分"},{"english":"be born with","chinese":"天生具備"},{"english":"a complete understanding of","chinese":"對……的完整理解"},{"english":"acceptable behaviour","chinese":"可接受的行為"},{"english":"without guidance","chinese":"沒有指導"},{"english":"struggle to respect rules","chinese":"難以尊重規則"},{"english":"control their impulses","chinese":"控制衝動"},{"english":"consider the feelings of others","chinese":"顧及他人感受"},{"english":"be corrected for","chinese":"因……而被糾正"},{"english":"lying, shouting or behaving selfishly","chinese":"說謊、大叫或行為自私"},{"english":"carry these habits into","chinese":"將這些習慣帶入"},{"english":"adult relationships","chinese":"成年後的人際關係"},{"english":"in this sense","chinese":"從這個意義上說"},{"english":"act as","chinese":"充當；發揮……作用"},{"english":"a child's first moral compass","chinese":"孩子的第一個道德指南針"},{"english":"distinguish right from wrong","chinese":"分辨是非"},{"english":"impose harsher consequences","chinese":"施加更嚴厲後果"},{"english":"good discipline","chinese":"良好管教"},{"english":"does not simply punish","chinese":"不只是懲罰"},{"english":"teach them self-control","chinese":"教導他們自制"},{"english":"responsibility and respect for others","chinese":"責任感和尊重他人"},{"english":"on the other hand","chinese":"另一方面"},{"english":"emotional care and safety","chinese":"情感關懷和安全感"},{"english":"form the foundation","chinese":"構成基礎"},{"english":"all other lessons depend","chinese":"所有其他教導都依賴"},{"english":"feel loved, protected and listened to","chinese":"感到被愛、受保護和被聆聽"},{"english":"be far more likely to","chinese":"更有可能"},{"english":"accept guidance from","chinese":"接受……的引導"},{"english":"be raised mainly through fear","chinese":"主要在恐懼中被養育"},{"english":"obey rules only temporarily","chinese":"只會暫時服從規則"},{"english":"respond to mistakes with","chinese":"以……回應錯誤"},{"english":"calm explanations","chinese":"平靜解釋"},{"english":"rather than constant anger","chinese":"而不是持續憤怒"},{"english":"learn from failure","chinese":"從失敗中學習"},{"english":"without feeling worthless","chinese":"而不會覺得自己毫無價值"},{"english":"a secure home","chinese":"安全穩定的家庭"},{"english":"support mental health","chinese":"支持精神健康"},{"english":"confidence and curiosity","chinese":"信心和好奇心"},{"english":"vital for long-term development","chinese":"對長遠發展至關重要"},{"english":"discipline without nurture","chinese":"沒有關愛的管教"},{"english":"building walls without a roof","chinese":"建牆卻沒有屋頂"},{"english":"create boundaries","chinese":"建立界限"},{"english":"provide true shelter","chinese":"提供真正庇護"},{"english":"teach their children right from wrong","chinese":"教導孩子分辨是非"},{"english":"responsible members of society","chinese":"負責任的社會成員"},{"english":"primary duty","chinese":"首要責任"},{"english":"provide a safe environment","chinese":"提供安全環境"},{"english":"grow into balanced and moral adults","chinese":"成長為平衡而有道德的成年人"},{"english":"feel secure, valued and emotionally supported","chinese":"感到安全、被重視和得到情感支持"}]},"model-essay-23-ielts-opinion":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-23-ielts-opinion","essayKey":"opinion:23","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-23-ielts-opinion","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/opinions/EdmundBd9OP-Q23","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"Online communication has become woven into everyday life, allowing people to exchange messages, join communities and maintain relationships across distance. However, I completely disagree that this development means people will never be alone or will always be able to make new friends. Digital contact can widen access to others, but it cannot guarantee genuine companionship.","chinese":"網上溝通已經融入日常生活，使人們能夠交換訊息、加入群體，並跨越距離維持人際關係。 然而，我完全不同意這種發展意味著人們將永遠不會孤單，或永遠能夠結交新朋友。 數位接觸可以擴大人們接觸他人的機會，但它不能保證真正的陪伴。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"The first problem with the statement is that loneliness is not simply the absence of people around us. It is often caused by a lack of meaningful connection. A person may have hundreds of online contacts and still feel isolated if those exchanges are brief, performative or shallow. Social media, for instance, can encourage users to post polished versions of their lives rather than speak honestly about fear, disappointment or insecurity. When communication becomes a stream of likes, comments and short replies, it may create the impression of a company without providing emotional support. In this sense, online platforms can be a crowded room in which no one truly listens.","chinese":"這個說法的第一個問題是，孤單並不只是身邊沒有人。 它往往是由缺乏有意義的連結所造成的。 一個人即使擁有數百個網上聯絡人，如果那些交流只是短暫、表面化或膚淺的，他仍然可能感到孤立。 例如，社交媒體可能鼓勵用戶發布經過美化的人生版本，而不是誠實地談論恐懼、失望或不安全感。 當溝通變成一連串的讚好、留言和簡短回覆時，它可能營造出有人陪伴的感覺，卻沒有提供真正的情感支持。 從這個意義上說，網上平台可以像一個擠滿人的房間，但其中沒有任何人真正聆聽。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"Another reason is that making friends online still depends on social confidence, trust and shared effort. The internet may open the door, but people must still walk through it. Shy teenagers, elderly users or people who have previously experienced online bullying may find digital interaction stressful rather than liberating. Moreover, online spaces are not always safe or sincere; fake identities, hostile comments and scams can make users cautious about forming new relationships. Even in positive environments, friendships require time, honesty and mutual care, which cannot be produced automatically by technology.","chinese":"另一個原因是，在網上交朋友仍然取決於社交自信、信任和共同努力。 互聯網也許能打開一扇門，但人們仍然必須自己走進去。 害羞的青少年、年長用戶，或曾經遭受網絡欺凌的人，可能會覺得數位互動帶來壓力，而不是帶來解放感。 此外，網上空間並不總是安全或真誠的；虛假身份、敵意留言和騙局都可能令用戶在建立新關係時變得謹慎。 即使在正面環境中，友誼也需要時間、誠實和彼此關心，而這些都不能由科技自動產"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, online communication has made it easier to reach others, but it has not removed loneliness and it cannot promise friendship for everyone. Human connection is built through depth, trust and consistency, not merely through constant access to a screen.","chinese":"總結來說，網上溝通使人們更容易接觸他人，但它並沒有消除孤單，也不能向每個人承諾友誼。 人與人之間的連結是透過深度、信任和持續相處建立的，而不只是透過持續接觸螢幕而形成的。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"online communication","chinese":"網上溝通"},{"english":"become woven into","chinese":"融入……之中"},{"english":"everyday life","chinese":"日常生活"},{"english":"exchange messages","chinese":"交換訊息"},{"english":"join communities","chinese":"加入社群"},{"english":"maintain relationships across distance","chinese":"跨越距離維繫關係"},{"english":"this development means","chinese":"這種發展意味着"},{"english":"never be alone","chinese":"永遠不會孤單"},{"english":"make new friends","chinese":"結交新朋友"},{"english":"digital contact","chinese":"數碼接觸"},{"english":"widen access to","chinese":"擴大接觸……的機會"},{"english":"guarantee genuine companionship","chinese":"保證真正的陪伴"},{"english":"genuine companionship","chinese":"真正的陪伴"},{"english":"the first problem with","chinese":"……的第一個問題"},{"english":"loneliness","chinese":"孤獨；孤獨感"},{"english":"absence of","chinese":"缺乏……"},{"english":"people around us","chinese":"身邊的人"},{"english":"be caused by","chinese":"由……造成"},{"english":"meaningful connection","chinese":"有意義的連繫"},{"english":"online contacts","chinese":"網上聯絡人"},{"english":"feel isolated","chinese":"感到孤立"},{"english":"brief, performative or shallow","chinese":"簡短、表演式或膚淺"},{"english":"social media","chinese":"社交媒體"},{"english":"encourage users to","chinese":"鼓勵用戶去……"},{"english":"polished versions of their lives","chinese":"經修飾的生活版本"},{"english":"rather than speak honestly about","chinese":"而不是坦誠談論……"},{"english":"disappointment","chinese":"失望"},{"english":"insecurity","chinese":"不安全感"},{"english":"a stream of","chinese":"一連串……"},{"english":"likes, comments and short replies","chinese":"讚好、留言和簡短回覆"},{"english":"create the impression of","chinese":"造成……的印象"},{"english":"company","chinese":"陪伴"},{"english":"emotional support","chinese":"情感支援"},{"english":"online platforms","chinese":"網上平台"},{"english":"crowded room","chinese":"擠滿人的房間"},{"english":"truly listens","chinese":"真正聆聽"},{"english":"making friends online","chinese":"在網上交朋友"},{"english":"depends on","chinese":"取決於"},{"english":"social confidence","chinese":"社交自信"},{"english":"shared effort","chinese":"共同努力"},{"english":"open the door","chinese":"打開大門；創造機會"},{"english":"walk through it","chinese":"走進去；把握機會"},{"english":"shy teenagers","chinese":"害羞的青少年"},{"english":"elderly users","chinese":"年長用戶"},{"english":"previously experienced","chinese":"之前經歷過"},{"english":"online bullying","chinese":"網上欺凌"},{"english":"digital interaction","chinese":"數碼互動"},{"english":"stressful rather than liberating","chinese":"有壓力而不是令人解放"},{"english":"online spaces","chinese":"網上空間"},{"english":"safe or sincere","chinese":"安全或真誠"},{"english":"fake identities","chinese":"虛假身份"},{"english":"hostile comments","chinese":"敵意留言"},{"english":"scams","chinese":"騙案"},{"english":"cautious about","chinese":"對……保持謹慎"},{"english":"forming new relationships","chinese":"建立新關係"},{"english":"positive environments","chinese":"正面的環境"},{"english":"mutual care","chinese":"互相關心"},{"english":"be produced automatically by","chinese":"由……自動產生"},{"english":"removed loneliness","chinese":"消除孤獨感"},{"english":"promise friendship for everyone","chinese":"保證每個人都能得到友誼"},{"english":"human connection","chinese":"人與人之間的連繫"},{"english":"be built through","chinese":"透過……建立"},{"english":"depth, trust and consistency","chinese":"深度、信任和持續性"},{"english":"not merely through","chinese":"不只是透過……"},{"english":"constant access to a screen","chinese":"隨時接觸螢幕"}]},"model-essay-24-ielts-advantage-disadvantage":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-24-ielts-advantage-disadvantage","essayKey":"advantage-disadvantage:24","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-24-ielts-advantage-disadvantage","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/advantage-and-disadvantage/EdmundBd9AdDisAd-Q24","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"International air travel, once a luxury enjoyed by a small minority, has become a routine feature of modern life. While this trend has brought undeniable social and economic benefits, I take the firm view that these gains are outweighed by the damage it causes to the natural environment. The advantages are real, but the ecological costs are wider in scale and far more difficult to reverse.","chinese":"國際航空旅行曾經只是少數人才能享受的奢侈活動，如今卻已成為現代生活中的日常現象。 雖然這一趨勢帶來了無可否認的社會與經濟利益， 我堅定認為，這些好處仍然被它對自然環境所造成的破壞所超越。 這些優勢確實存在，但其生態代價影響範圍更廣，而且更難以逆轉。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"On the one hand, the rise in regular international flights has created several important benefits. First, it has stimulated tourism and cross-border business. When people are able to travel quickly and relatively cheaply, more visitors spend money on accommodation, food and local transport, which then supports employment and generates tax revenue. In many island nations and coastal cities, for example, large numbers of jobs depend directly on overseas travellers. Second, frequent flights have made global mobility far easier for students and professionals. This means that people can study abroad, attend international conferences and develop commercial partnerships, all of which promote the exchange of skills, knowledge and investment. A student who trains overseas and later returns home, for instance, may contribute valuable expertise to local industries.","chinese":"一方面，定期國際航班的增加確實帶來了幾項重要的好處。 首先，它促進了旅遊業以及跨境商業活動的發展。 當人們能夠以較快且相對便宜的方式出行時，便會有更多旅客在住宿、餐飲和本地交通方面消費，進而支持就業並帶來稅收收入。 例如，在許多島國和沿海城市，大量職位都直接依賴海外旅客。 其次，頻繁的航班使學生和專業人士的全球流動變得容易得多。 這意味著人們能夠到海外留學、參加國際會議以及建立商業合作關係，而這些都能促進技能、知識與投資的交流。 例如，一名在海外接受培訓後回國的學生，可能會為本地產業帶來寶貴的專業知識。 因此，國際航班的擴張顯然能促進經濟活動、人員流動以及全球交流。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"Even so, the environmental disadvantages are more serious. The clearest problem is that air travel is highly carbon-intensive. Every flight burns substantial quantities of aviation fuel, releasing carbon dioxide and other pollutants into the atmosphere; when this is repeated across millions of journeys, it accelerates climate change and worsens environmental instability. A single holiday flight may seem insignificant, but the cumulative effect of countless such trips is enormous. Furthermore, the expansion of air travel creates additional environmental pressure on the ground. More passengers require larger airports, more roads and more tourist infrastructure, which consume land, produce waste and place strain on fragile ecosystems. In popular coastal destinations, for example, rising visitor numbers often lead to habitat loss, litter and resource depletion.","chinese":"即便如此，環境方面的缺點更加嚴重。 最明顯的問題是，航空旅行屬於高度碳密集型活動。 每一趟航班都會燃燒大量航空燃料，向大氣中排放二氧化碳及其他污染物；當這種情況在數以百萬計的旅程中反覆出現時，便會加速氣候變化並惡化環境的不穩定性。 單一次度假航班看似微不足道，但無數類似旅程累積起來的影響卻極其巨大。 此外，航空旅行的擴張還會在地面層面造成額外的環境壓力。 更多旅客意味著需要更大的機場、更多道路以及更多旅遊基礎設施，而這些都會消耗土地、製造廢物，並對脆弱的生態系統造成壓力。 例如，在受歡迎的海岸旅遊地區，遊客數量上升往往會導致棲息地流失、垃圾增加以及資源耗竭。 因此，頻繁飛行所造成的環境危害並不僅限於排放問題，而是進一步擴展至更廣泛的生態破壞。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, regular international flights clearly promote prosperity, mobility and global connection. Nevertheless, because they significantly increase emissions and intensify wider ecological damage, their disadvantages to the environment outweigh their advantages. For this reason, the growth of international air travel should be regarded as a negative development overall.","chinese":"總結而言，定期國際航班的確促進了繁榮、人員流動以及全球連結。 然而，由於它們大幅增加排放，並加劇更廣泛的生態破壞，因此其對環境造成的缺點大於其帶來的好處。 基於這一原因，國際航空旅行的增長整體上應被視為一種負面發展。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"international air travel","chinese":"國際航空旅遊"},{"english":"once a luxury enjoyed by a small minority","chinese":"曾經是少數人享有的奢侈品"},{"english":"a routine feature of","chinese":"……的日常特徵"},{"english":"modern life","chinese":"現代生活"},{"english":"this trend","chinese":"這個趨勢"},{"english":"undeniable social and economic benefits","chinese":"不可否認的社會和經濟好處"},{"english":"take the firm view that","chinese":"堅定認為"},{"english":"these gains are outweighed by","chinese":"這些好處不及……；被……抵消"},{"english":"the natural environment","chinese":"自然環境"},{"english":"ecological costs","chinese":"生態代價"},{"english":"wider in scale","chinese":"規模更廣"},{"english":"difficult to reverse","chinese":"難以逆轉"},{"english":"on the one hand","chinese":"一方面"},{"english":"the rise in","chinese":"……的增加"},{"english":"regular international flights","chinese":"定期國際航班"},{"english":"stimulated tourism","chinese":"刺激旅遊業"},{"english":"cross-border business","chinese":"跨境商業"},{"english":"relatively cheaply","chinese":"相對便宜地"},{"english":"spend money on","chinese":"花錢在……上"},{"english":"accommodation","chinese":"住宿"},{"english":"local transport","chinese":"本地交通"},{"english":"supports employment","chinese":"支持就業"},{"english":"generates tax revenue","chinese":"產生稅收"},{"english":"island nations","chinese":"島國"},{"english":"coastal cities","chinese":"沿海城市"},{"english":"large numbers of jobs","chinese":"大量工作職位"},{"english":"depend directly on","chinese":"直接依賴"},{"english":"overseas travellers","chinese":"海外旅客"},{"english":"frequent flights","chinese":"頻繁航班"},{"english":"global mobility","chinese":"全球流動性"},{"english":"study abroad","chinese":"出國留學"},{"english":"attend international conferences","chinese":"參加國際會議"},{"english":"commercial partnerships","chinese":"商業合作關係"},{"english":"promote the exchange of","chinese":"促進……的交流"},{"english":"skills, knowledge and investment","chinese":"技能、知識和投資"},{"english":"trains overseas","chinese":"在海外接受培訓"},{"english":"returns home","chinese":"回到本地；回國"},{"english":"contribute valuable expertise to","chinese":"為……貢獻寶貴專業知識"},{"english":"local industries","chinese":"本地產業"},{"english":"even so","chinese":"即使如此"},{"english":"environmental disadvantages","chinese":"環境方面的缺點"},{"english":"the clearest problem","chinese":"最明顯的問題"},{"english":"highly carbon-intensive","chinese":"碳排放密集的"},{"english":"burns substantial quantities of","chinese":"消耗大量"},{"english":"aviation fuel","chinese":"航空燃油"},{"english":"releasing carbon dioxide","chinese":"釋放二氧化碳"},{"english":"other pollutants","chinese":"其他污染物"},{"english":"into the atmosphere","chinese":"進入大氣層"},{"english":"repeated across millions of journeys","chinese":"在數以百萬計的旅程中重複出現"},{"english":"accelerates climate change","chinese":"加速氣候變化"},{"english":"worsens environmental instability","chinese":"加劇環境不穩定"},{"english":"a single holiday flight","chinese":"一次假期航班"},{"english":"may seem insignificant","chinese":"可能看似微不足道"},{"english":"the cumulative effect of","chinese":"……的累積影響"},{"english":"countless such trips","chinese":"無數這類旅程"},{"english":"furthermore","chinese":"此外"},{"english":"the expansion of air travel","chinese":"航空旅遊的擴張"},{"english":"additional environmental pressure","chinese":"額外環境壓力"},{"english":"on the ground","chinese":"在地面上"},{"english":"larger airports","chinese":"更大型機場"},{"english":"tourist infrastructure","chinese":"旅遊基礎設施"},{"english":"consume land","chinese":"消耗土地"},{"english":"produce waste","chinese":"製造廢物"},{"english":"place strain on","chinese":"對……造成壓力"},{"english":"fragile ecosystems","chinese":"脆弱的生態系統"},{"english":"popular coastal destinations","chinese":"受歡迎的沿海目的地"},{"english":"rising visitor numbers","chinese":"不斷上升的遊客人數"},{"english":"lead to habitat loss","chinese":"導致棲息地喪失"},{"english":"litter","chinese":"垃圾"},{"english":"resource depletion","chinese":"資源耗盡"},{"english":"promote prosperity","chinese":"促進繁榮"},{"english":"global connection","chinese":"全球聯繫"},{"english":"significantly increase emissions","chinese":"大幅增加排放"},{"english":"intensify wider ecological damage","chinese":"加劇更廣泛的生態破壞"},{"english":"disadvantages to the environment","chinese":"對環境的缺點"},{"english":"outweigh their advantages","chinese":"超過其好處"},{"english":"should be regarded as","chinese":"應被視為"},{"english":"a negative development overall","chinese":"整體而言是負面發展"}]},"model-essay-24-ielts-discuss-both-views":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-24-ielts-discuss-both-views","essayKey":"discuss-both-views:24","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-24-ielts-discuss-both-views","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/discuss-both-views-your-opinion/EdmundBd9ExpBth-Q24","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"Childhood obesity has become a serious public health concern in many countries. While some argue that governments should be blamed for this trend, others believe that parents are mainly responsible. In my view, although parents play an important role in shaping children’s daily habits, the government bears greater responsibility because it controls the wider food and social environment in which families make their choices.","chinese":"兒童肥胖在許多國家已經成為一個嚴重的公共健康問題。 雖然有些人認為政府應該為這種趨勢受到指責，但另一些人則相信父母才是主要責任方 在我看來，儘管父母在塑造兒童日常習慣方面扮演重要角色，但政府承擔更大的責任，因為它掌控著家庭作出選擇時所處的更廣泛飲食和社會環境。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"Those who blame parents have a reasonable argument. Children rarely buy groceries, cook meals, or decide their daily routines entirely on their own, so parents strongly influence what they eat and how active they are. If mothers and fathers regularly serve fast food, allow excessive screen time, and fail to encourage exercise, children are likely to develop unhealthy habits from an early age. For example, a child who spends every evening watching videos while eating sugary snacks may gradually see this lifestyle as normal. In this sense, parents are the first line of defence against obesity because they control the home environment.","chinese":"那些責怪父母的人有一個合理的論點。 兒童很少會完全自己購買食材、烹調食物，或決定自己的日常作息，因此父母會強烈影響他們吃甚麼以及有多活躍。 如果父母經常提供快餐、容許過多螢幕時間，並且未能鼓勵運動，兒童很可能從小便養成不健康的習慣。 例如，一個每天晚上邊看影片邊吃含糖零食的孩子，可能會逐漸把這生活方式視為正常 從這個意義上說，父母是對抗肥胖的第一道防線，因為他們掌控著家庭環境。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"However, I believe governments are more responsible because they shape the conditions that make unhealthy choices so common. Many children are surrounded by aggressive advertising for junk food, cheap processed meals, and neighbourhoods where safe outdoor play is limited. These are not problems that individual parents can easily solve. Governments can restrict unhealthy food marketing, improve school meals, require clearer nutrition labels, and build parks or sports facilities. If public policy makes unhealthy food cheap, visible, and convenient, while healthy options remain expensive or inaccessible, parents are fighting an uphill battle.","chinese":"然而，我認為政府更有責任，因為它們塑造了使不健康選擇變得如此普遍的條件。 許多兒童被垃圾食品的強勢廣告、廉價加工食品，以及安全戶外玩樂空間有限的社區所包圍。 這些並不是個別父母能夠輕易解決的問題。 政府可以限制不健康食品的市場推廣、改善學校膳食、要求更清晰的營養標籤，並興建公園或體育設施。 如果公共政策使不健康食品變得廉價、顯眼和方便，而健康選擇仍然昂貴或難以取得，那麼父母就是在打一場艱難的仗。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, parents certainly influence children’s eating and exercise habits, but the stronger responsibility lies with the government. Families can guide children at home, yet only governments can regulate food companies, improve public spaces, and create a healthier environment for all children. Therefore, childhood obesity should be seen primarily as a failure of public policy rather than simply poor parenting.","chinese":"總結來說，父母固然會影響兒童的飲食和運動習慣，但更大的責任在於政府。 家庭可以在家中引導兒童，但只有政府能夠規管食品公司、改善公共空間，並為所有兒童創造一個更健康的環境。 因此，兒童肥胖應主要被視為公共政策的失敗，而不僅僅是父母教養不善的結果。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"childhood obesity","chinese":"兒童肥胖"},{"english":"a serious public health concern","chinese":"嚴重公共衞生問題"},{"english":"be blamed for","chinese":"因……被責怪"},{"english":"this trend","chinese":"這個趨勢"},{"english":"mainly responsible","chinese":"負主要責任"},{"english":"play an important role in","chinese":"在……中扮演重要角色"},{"english":"shape children's daily habits","chinese":"塑造兒童的日常習慣"},{"english":"bear greater responsibility","chinese":"承擔更大責任"},{"english":"the wider food and social environment","chinese":"更廣泛的食物及社會環境"},{"english":"make their choices","chinese":"作出選擇"},{"english":"blame parents","chinese":"責怪父母"},{"english":"a reasonable argument","chinese":"合理論點"},{"english":"buy groceries","chinese":"買日常食材"},{"english":"cook meals","chinese":"煮飯"},{"english":"decide their daily routines","chinese":"決定自己的日常作息"},{"english":"entirely on their own","chinese":"完全靠自己"},{"english":"strongly influence","chinese":"強烈影響"},{"english":"how active they are","chinese":"他們有多活躍"},{"english":"regularly serve fast food","chinese":"經常提供快餐"},{"english":"excessive screen time","chinese":"過量螢幕時間"},{"english":"fail to encourage exercise","chinese":"未能鼓勵運動"},{"english":"develop unhealthy habits","chinese":"養成不健康習慣"},{"english":"from an early age","chinese":"從小"},{"english":"spend every evening watching videos","chinese":"每晚花時間看影片"},{"english":"sugary snacks","chinese":"高糖零食"},{"english":"gradually see this lifestyle as normal","chinese":"逐漸視這種生活方式為正常"},{"english":"in this sense","chinese":"從這個意義上說"},{"english":"the first line of defence against","chinese":"對抗……的第一道防線"},{"english":"control the home environment","chinese":"控制家庭環境"},{"english":"more responsible","chinese":"責任更大"},{"english":"shape the conditions that","chinese":"塑造令……的條件"},{"english":"unhealthy choices","chinese":"不健康選擇"},{"english":"so common","chinese":"如此普遍"},{"english":"be surrounded by","chinese":"被……包圍"},{"english":"aggressive advertising","chinese":"進取的廣告宣傳"},{"english":"junk food","chinese":"垃圾食物"},{"english":"cheap processed meals","chinese":"廉價加工餐食"},{"english":"safe outdoor play","chinese":"安全的戶外玩耍"},{"english":"be limited","chinese":"受到限制"},{"english":"individual parents","chinese":"個別父母"},{"english":"easily solve","chinese":"輕易解決"},{"english":"restrict unhealthy food marketing","chinese":"限制不健康食品推廣"},{"english":"improve school meals","chinese":"改善學校膳食"},{"english":"require clearer nutrition labels","chinese":"要求更清晰的營養標籤"},{"english":"nutrition labels","chinese":"營養標籤"},{"english":"build parks or sports facilities","chinese":"興建公園或運動設施"},{"english":"public policy","chinese":"公共政策"},{"english":"cheap, visible, and convenient","chinese":"便宜、顯眼和方便"},{"english":"healthy options","chinese":"健康選擇"},{"english":"remain expensive or inaccessible","chinese":"仍然昂貴或難以取得"},{"english":"fight an uphill battle","chinese":"打一場艱難仗"},{"english":"eating and exercise habits","chinese":"飲食和運動習慣"},{"english":"the stronger responsibility lies with","chinese":"更大的責任在於"},{"english":"guide children at home","chinese":"在家中引導兒童"},{"english":"regulate food companies","chinese":"規管食品公司"},{"english":"improve public spaces","chinese":"改善公共空間"},{"english":"create a healthier environment for","chinese":"為……創造更健康的環境"},{"english":"be seen primarily as","chinese":"應主要被視為"},{"english":"a failure of public policy","chinese":"公共政策的失敗"},{"english":"rather than simply poor parenting","chinese":"而不只是管教不善"}]},"model-essay-24-ielts-opinion":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-24-ielts-opinion","essayKey":"opinion:24","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-24-ielts-opinion","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/opinions/EdmundBd9OP-Q24","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"It is often argued that the brief and simplified style of text messages and instant online conversations will eventually destroy people’s ability to use grammar and spelling correctly. I disagree with this view because informal digital language is mainly a matter of context, and modern communication can actually strengthen people’s awareness of written language.","chinese":"人們經常認為，文字訊息和即時網上對話那種簡短而簡化的風格，最終會破壞人們正確使用文法和拼字的能力。 我不同意這個觀點，因為非正式的數碼語言主要是語境問題，而現代溝通實際上可以加強人們對書面語言的意識。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"The first reason is that short online messages are not meant to follow the same conventions as academic essays, business letters, or official documents. When people type “u” instead of “you” or leave out punctuation in a quick message to a friend, they are usually choosing speed and convenience, not showing that they have forgotten standard English. This is similar to the way people speak differently at home and in a job interview. A student may write casually in a group chat, but the same student can still use full sentences, correct spelling, and formal vocabulary in an examination. In this sense, texting is not the death of grammar; it is simply another register of communication.","chinese":"第一個原因是，簡短的網上訊息本來就不是為了遵循學術文章、商業信件或正式文件的相同規範。 當人們在給朋友的快速訊息中輸入“u”而不是“you”，或者省略標點符號時，他們通常只是選擇速度和便利，而不是顯示他們已經忘記了標準英語。 這就類似於人們在家中和在工作面試中會用不同方式說話。 一名學生可能會在群組聊天中隨意書寫，但同一名學生仍然可以在考試中使用完整句子、正確拼字和正式詞彙。 從這個意義上說，發短訊並不是文法的死亡；它只不過是另一種溝通語域。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"Another important point is that digital communication has made writing a more regular part of daily life. Many people now compose emails, online comments, captions, messages, and work updates every day, so they are exposed to written language far more often than previous generations were. Admittedly, some online writing is careless, but poor habits are corrected by school, professional expectations, grammar-checking tools, and the need to be taken seriously in public or workplace settings. For example, an employee may use abbreviations with friends, yet still check spelling carefully before sending a proposal to a client. The pressure to communicate clearly has not disappeared; if anything, it has become more visible.","chinese":"另一個重要觀點是，數碼溝通已經使寫作成為日常生活中更常見的一部分。 現在許多人每天都會撰寫電郵、網上評論、圖片說明、訊息和工作更新，因此他們接觸書面語言的頻率遠高於以往世代。 誠然，有些網上寫作是粗心的，但不良習慣會被學校教育、專業期望、文法檢查工具，以及在公共或職場場合中被認真看待的需要所糾正。 例如，一名員工可能會和朋友使用縮寫，但在向客戶發送建議書之前，仍然會仔細檢查拼字。 清楚溝通的壓力並沒有消失；相反，它變得更加明顯。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, I do not believe that instant online communication will destroy grammar and spelling. Although texting encourages a shorter and simpler style, people can still adjust their language according to purpose and audience. Grammar is not dying; it is being used more flexibly.","chinese":"總結來說，我不認為即時網上溝通會破壞文法和拼字。 儘管發短訊會鼓勵一種較短和較簡單的風格，人們仍然可以根據目的和受眾調整自己的語言。 文法並沒有死亡；它只是被更靈活地使用。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"it is often argued that","chinese":"人們經常認為……"},{"english":"brief and simplified style","chinese":"簡短和簡化的風格"},{"english":"text messages","chinese":"文字訊息"},{"english":"instant online conversations","chinese":"即時網上對話"},{"english":"eventually destroy","chinese":"最終破壞"},{"english":"ability to use","chinese":"使用……的能力"},{"english":"grammar and spelling","chinese":"文法和串字"},{"english":"correctly","chinese":"正確地"},{"english":"informal digital language","chinese":"非正式數碼語言"},{"english":"a matter of context","chinese":"視乎語境的問題"},{"english":"modern communication","chinese":"現代溝通"},{"english":"strengthen people's awareness of","chinese":"加強人們對……的意識"},{"english":"written language","chinese":"書面語言"},{"english":"short online messages","chinese":"簡短網上訊息"},{"english":"be meant to","chinese":"旨在；本來要"},{"english":"follow the same conventions as","chinese":"遵循與……相同的慣例"},{"english":"academic essays","chinese":"學術文章"},{"english":"business letters","chinese":"商業信件"},{"english":"official documents","chinese":"官方文件"},{"english":"leave out punctuation","chinese":"省略標點符號"},{"english":"choosing speed and convenience","chinese":"選擇速度和方便"},{"english":"standard English","chinese":"標準英語"},{"english":"similar to","chinese":"與……相似"},{"english":"speak differently","chinese":"以不同方式說話"},{"english":"job interview","chinese":"求職面試"},{"english":"write casually","chinese":"隨意地寫"},{"english":"group chat","chinese":"群組聊天"},{"english":"full sentences","chinese":"完整句子"},{"english":"correct spelling","chinese":"正確串字"},{"english":"formal vocabulary","chinese":"正式詞彙"},{"english":"in this sense","chinese":"從這個意義上說"},{"english":"the death of grammar","chinese":"文法的死亡"},{"english":"another register of communication","chinese":"另一種溝通語域"},{"english":"digital communication","chinese":"數碼溝通"},{"english":"a more regular part of daily life","chinese":"日常生活中更恆常的一部分"},{"english":"compose emails","chinese":"撰寫電郵"},{"english":"online comments","chinese":"網上留言"},{"english":"captions","chinese":"圖片或影片說明文字"},{"english":"work updates","chinese":"工作進度更新"},{"english":"be exposed to","chinese":"接觸到……"},{"english":"far more often than","chinese":"比……頻密得多"},{"english":"previous generations","chinese":"以往幾代人"},{"english":"admittedly","chinese":"誠然"},{"english":"careless","chinese":"粗心；不嚴謹"},{"english":"poor habits","chinese":"不良習慣"},{"english":"be corrected by","chinese":"被……糾正"},{"english":"professional expectations","chinese":"專業期望"},{"english":"grammar-checking tools","chinese":"文法檢查工具"},{"english":"taken seriously","chinese":"被認真看待"},{"english":"workplace settings","chinese":"職場環境"},{"english":"abbreviations","chinese":"縮寫"},{"english":"proposal","chinese":"建議書"},{"english":"client","chinese":"客戶"},{"english":"pressure to communicate clearly","chinese":"清晰溝通的壓力"},{"english":"has not disappeared","chinese":"並沒有消失"},{"english":"if anything","chinese":"甚至可以說"},{"english":"become more visible","chinese":"變得更明顯"},{"english":"instant online communication","chinese":"即時網上溝通"},{"english":"encourages a shorter and simpler style","chinese":"鼓勵更短和更簡單的風格"},{"english":"adjust their language","chinese":"調整自己的語言"},{"english":"according to","chinese":"根據"},{"english":"purpose and audience","chinese":"目的和受眾"},{"english":"grammar is not dying","chinese":"文法並沒有死亡"},{"english":"being used more flexibly","chinese":"被更靈活地使用"}]},"model-essay-25-ielts-advantage-disadvantage":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-25-ielts-advantage-disadvantage","essayKey":"advantage-disadvantage:25","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-25-ielts-advantage-disadvantage","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/advantage-and-disadvantage/EdmundBd9AdDisAd-Q25","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"In many countries, once people obtain a driving licence, they can continue driving for years without being formally reassessed. Some therefore argue that motorists should be required to retake their driving test every five years. This policy would bring certain clear benefits, although it would also create practical difficulties.","chinese":"在許多國家，一旦人們取得駕駛執照，他們之後多年都可以繼續駕駛，而無須再接受正式評估。 因此，有些人認為，駕駛者應該被規定每五年重新參加一次駕駛考試。 這項政策會帶來一些明顯的好處，但同時也會造成實際上的困難。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"One obvious advantage is that repeated testing could improve road safety by ensuring that drivers still meet an acceptable standard. Over time, people often develop bad habits such as failing to check mirrors properly, signalling too late, or becoming careless at junctions. A compulsory retest would force them to correct these habits before they caused accidents. In addition, such a system would help authorities ensure that drivers remain familiar with current traffic laws. Road rules do not stand still, and many motorists who passed their test decades ago may be unaware of newer regulations on speed limits, mobile phone use, or cyclist protection. A periodic assessment could therefore act as both a safety net and a refresher.","chinese":"一個明顯的優點是，重複測試可以確保駕駛者仍然達到可接受的標準，從而提升道路安全 隨著時間過去，人們往往會養成壞習慣，例如沒有正確查看倒後鏡、打方向燈太遲，或者在路口變得粗心。 強制性的重考會迫使他們在這些習慣引發交通意外之前作出糾正。 此外，這樣的制度也能幫助當局確保駕駛者仍然熟悉現行交通法規。 交通規則並不是一成不變的，而許多在數十年前通過考試的駕駛者，可能並不知道有關車速限制、使用手機或保護單車使用者的新規定。 因此，定期評估既可以成為一道安全保障，也可以起到重新溫習和更新知識的作用。 總體而言，定期重考可以令道路更安全，並讓駕駛者跟上現代法規的更新。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"However, the drawbacks are equally significant. First, making every driver retake the test every five years would place a heavy burden on testing centres and examiners. In densely populated areas, the number of licence holders is so large that waiting times could become unmanageable, which would frustrate the public and stretch government resources. Second, this policy could unfairly affect competent drivers with long records of safe driving. Someone who has driven responsibly for twenty years may still fail because of nerves on the day rather than genuine incompetence. In that case, the system would punish anxiety instead of improving safety.","chinese":"然而，這項做法的缺點同樣相當明顯。 首先，要求每位駕駛者每五年重考一次，會對考試中心和考官造成沉重負擔。 在人口稠密的地區，持牌駕駛者的人數十分龐大，等候時間可能會變得難以控制，這不但會令公眾感到不滿，也會令政府資源承受壓力。 第二，這項政策可能會對那些長期安全駕駛、實際上很有能力的駕駛者造成不公平影響。 一個已經負責任地駕駛了二十年的人，仍然有可能只是因為當天緊張而未能通過考試，而不是因為真正缺乏駕駛能力。 在那種情況下，這個制度懲罰的其實是緊張情緒，而不是真正提升道路安全。 基於這些原因，強制重考可能會造成嚴重的行政問題，並為某些駕駛者帶來不公平的結果。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In summary, requiring people to retake their driving test every five years could raise driving standards and update drivers’ knowledge, but it could also create serious administrative pressure and unfair outcomes for some motorists.","chinese":"總結來說，要求人們每五年重新參加一次駕駛考試，可以提升駕駛水平，並更新駕駛者的知識。 與此同時，它也可能帶來嚴重的行政壓力，並對某些駕駛者造成不公平的結果。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"obtain a driving licence","chinese":"取得駕駛執照"},{"english":"continue driving for years","chinese":"繼續駕駛多年"},{"english":"without being formally reassessed","chinese":"沒有被正式重新評估"},{"english":"motorists","chinese":"駕駛者"},{"english":"be required to","chinese":"被要求去……"},{"english":"retake their driving test","chinese":"重考駕駛考試"},{"english":"every five years","chinese":"每五年"},{"english":"clear benefits","chinese":"明顯好處"},{"english":"practical difficulties","chinese":"實際困難"},{"english":"one obvious advantage","chinese":"一個明顯優點"},{"english":"repeated testing","chinese":"重複考核"},{"english":"improve road safety","chinese":"改善道路安全"},{"english":"ensuring that","chinese":"確保……"},{"english":"meet an acceptable standard","chinese":"達到可接受水平"},{"english":"over time","chinese":"隨時間"},{"english":"develop bad habits","chinese":"養成壞習慣"},{"english":"failing to check mirrors properly","chinese":"未有正確查看倒後鏡"},{"english":"signalling too late","chinese":"太遲打燈"},{"english":"becoming careless at junctions","chinese":"在路口變得粗心"},{"english":"compulsory retest","chinese":"強制重考"},{"english":"force them to correct these habits","chinese":"迫使他們改正這些習慣"},{"english":"before they caused accidents","chinese":"在它們造成意外之前"},{"english":"such a system","chinese":"這樣的制度"},{"english":"authorities","chinese":"當局"},{"english":"remain familiar with","chinese":"仍然熟悉……"},{"english":"current traffic laws","chinese":"現行交通法例"},{"english":"do not stand still","chinese":"不會停滯不變"},{"english":"passed their test decades ago","chinese":"數十年前考獲駕駛資格"},{"english":"be unaware of newer regulations","chinese":"不知道較新的規例"},{"english":"newer regulations on","chinese":"關於……的較新規例"},{"english":"speed limits","chinese":"速度限制"},{"english":"mobile phone use","chinese":"使用手機"},{"english":"cyclist protection","chinese":"單車使用者保護"},{"english":"periodic assessment","chinese":"定期評估"},{"english":"act as both","chinese":"同時起……作用"},{"english":"a safety net","chinese":"安全保障"},{"english":"a refresher","chinese":"溫故知新的複習"},{"english":"the drawbacks are equally significant","chinese":"缺點同樣重大"},{"english":"place a heavy burden on","chinese":"對……造成沉重負擔"},{"english":"testing centres","chinese":"考試中心"},{"english":"examiners","chinese":"考牌主任；考官"},{"english":"densely populated areas","chinese":"人口稠密地區"},{"english":"licence holders","chinese":"持牌人"},{"english":"waiting times","chinese":"等候時間"},{"english":"become unmanageable","chinese":"變得難以管理；難以處理"},{"english":"frustrate the public","chinese":"令公眾感到不滿"},{"english":"stretch government resources","chinese":"令政府資源緊張"},{"english":"unfairly affect competent drivers","chinese":"不公平地影響合格稱職的駕駛者"},{"english":"competent drivers","chinese":"合格稱職的駕駛者"},{"english":"long records of safe driving","chinese":"長期安全駕駛紀錄"},{"english":"driven responsibly","chinese":"負責任地駕駛"},{"english":"because of nerves on the day","chinese":"因考試當日緊張"},{"english":"genuine incompetence","chinese":"真正能力不足"},{"english":"punish anxiety instead of","chinese":"懲罰焦慮而不是……"},{"english":"improving safety","chinese":"改善安全"},{"english":"in summary","chinese":"總括而言"},{"english":"requiring people to retake","chinese":"要求人們重考"},{"english":"raise driving standards","chinese":"提高駕駛水平"},{"english":"update drivers' knowledge","chinese":"更新駕駛者的知識"},{"english":"serious administrative pressure","chinese":"嚴重行政壓力"},{"english":"unfair outcomes","chinese":"不公平結果"}]},"model-essay-25-ielts-direct-question":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-25-ielts-direct-question","essayKey":"direct-question:25","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-25-ielts-direct-question","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/direct-question/EdmundBd9Dir-Q25","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"Across many modern societies, both mothers and fathers now work full time, so children receive fewer hours of direct parental attention than earlier generations did. The main reason is economic pressure, and this can weaken family bonds and reduce the guidance children receive while they are growing up.","chinese":"在許多現代社會中，母親和父親現在都全職工作，因此與早期世代相比，孩子獲得父母直接關注的時間更少。 主要原因是經濟壓力，而這可能削弱家庭關係，並減少孩子在成長過程中所獲得的引導"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"The clearest reason is that one salary is often no longer enough to support a family comfortably. Housing, transport, food, childcare and education are expensive, so many parents feel they must remain in paid employment just to keep the household stable. In this sense, work is not simply a personal ambition; it is a financial lifeline. Because of this, parents often leave home early, return late, and depend on grandparents, nurseries or electronic devices to occupy their children.","chinese":"最明顯的原因是，一份薪金通常已不再足以讓一個家庭舒適地生活。 住房、交通、食物、childcare和教育都十分昂貴，因此許多父母覺得自己必須繼續受薪工作，才能維持家庭穩定。 從這個意義上說，工作不僅僅是個人抱負；它是一條經濟上的生命線。 正因如此，父母往往很早離家、很晚回家，並依靠祖父母、幼兒園或電子設備來讓孩子有事可做。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"One serious problem is emotional distance. Children need more than material comfort: they need small, regular moments of attention, such as family meals, bedtime conversations and help with homework. These routines may look ordinary, but they are the glue that holds relationships together. If they disappear, children may feel less valued or less secure, even when their parents love them deeply. Over time, this can reduce their confidence and make them less willing to discuss fears, mistakes or personal difficulties.","chinese":"其中一個嚴重問題是情感距離。 孩子需要的不只是物質上的舒適：他們需要細小而固定的關注時刻，例如家庭用餐、睡前對話，以及功課上的幫助。 這些日常習慣看起來或許很普通，但它們正是維繫關係的黏合劑。 如果這些習慣消失，即使父母深愛孩子，孩子也可能感到自己較不被重視，或較沒有安全感。 長遠而言，這可能削弱他們的自信，並使他們較不願意討論恐懼、錯誤或個人困難。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 3","english":"Another problem is weaker supervision. When parents are rarely available, children may turn to classmates, social media or online entertainment for advice and approval. For example, a teenager who spends hours online without adult guidance may copy unhealthy habits or absorb harmful values before anyone notices. Even responsible children can struggle to build discipline and self-control if no adult is consistently present to model those qualities.","chinese":"另一個問題是監管較弱。 當父母很少能陪伴在旁時，孩子可能會轉向同學、社交媒體或網上娛樂，以尋求建議和認同。 例如，一個在沒有成年人引導下花數小時上網的青少年，可能會在任何人察覺之前模仿不健康的習慣，或吸收有害的價值觀。 即使是負責任的孩子，如果沒有成年人持續在場示範這些品質，也可能難以建立紀律和自制力。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, children spend less time with their parents mainly because many families now need two incomes to survive. This can create emotional separation and leave children with less support, structure and moral guidance.","chinese":"總結來說，孩子與父母相處的時間減少，主要是因為許多家庭現在需要兩份收入才能維持生活。 這可能造成情感上的疏離，並使孩子得到較少的支持、規律和道德引導。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"across many modern societies","chinese":"在許多現代社會中"},{"english":"work full time","chinese":"全職工作"},{"english":"receive fewer hours of","chinese":"獲得較少時間的……"},{"english":"direct parental attention","chinese":"父母直接關注"},{"english":"earlier generations","chinese":"較早幾代人"},{"english":"the main reason is","chinese":"主要原因是"},{"english":"economic pressure","chinese":"經濟壓力"},{"english":"weaken family bonds","chinese":"削弱家庭聯繫"},{"english":"reduce the guidance children receive","chinese":"減少孩子得到的引導"},{"english":"while they are growing up","chinese":"在他們成長期間"},{"english":"the clearest reason","chinese":"最明顯的原因"},{"english":"one salary","chinese":"一份薪金"},{"english":"no longer enough to","chinese":"不再足以"},{"english":"support a family comfortably","chinese":"讓一家人生活得舒適"},{"english":"housing, transport, food, childcare and education","chinese":"住屋、交通、食物、育兒服務和教育"},{"english":"remain in paid employment","chinese":"繼續受薪工作"},{"english":"keep the household stable","chinese":"維持家庭穩定"},{"english":"In this sense","chinese":"從這個意義上說"},{"english":"personal ambition","chinese":"個人抱負"},{"english":"a financial lifeline","chinese":"財務生命線"},{"english":"because of this","chinese":"因此"},{"english":"leave home early","chinese":"很早離家"},{"english":"return late","chinese":"很晚回家"},{"english":"depend on","chinese":"依賴"},{"english":"grandparents","chinese":"祖父母；外祖父母"},{"english":"nurseries","chinese":"托兒所"},{"english":"electronic devices","chinese":"電子裝置"},{"english":"occupy their children","chinese":"讓孩子有事做；打發孩子"},{"english":"one serious problem","chinese":"一個嚴重問題"},{"english":"emotional distance","chinese":"情感距離"},{"english":"material comfort","chinese":"物質上的安穩"},{"english":"small, regular moments of attention","chinese":"細小而定期的關注時刻"},{"english":"family meals","chinese":"家庭用餐"},{"english":"bedtime conversations","chinese":"睡前談話"},{"english":"help with homework","chinese":"功課上的幫助"},{"english":"these routines","chinese":"這些日常習慣"},{"english":"look ordinary","chinese":"看起來普通"},{"english":"the glue that holds relationships together","chinese":"維繫關係的黏合劑"},{"english":"feel less valued","chinese":"感到較不受重視"},{"english":"less secure","chinese":"較沒有安全感"},{"english":"even when","chinese":"即使"},{"english":"love them deeply","chinese":"深深愛着他們"},{"english":"over time","chinese":"隨時間"},{"english":"reduce their confidence","chinese":"降低他們的信心"},{"english":"less willing to discuss","chinese":"較不願意討論"},{"english":"fears, mistakes or personal difficulties","chinese":"恐懼、錯誤或個人困難"},{"english":"another problem","chinese":"另一個問題"},{"english":"weaker supervision","chinese":"較弱的監督"},{"english":"rarely available","chinese":"很少有空"},{"english":"turn to","chinese":"轉向……尋求"},{"english":"classmates","chinese":"同學"},{"english":"social media","chinese":"社交媒體"},{"english":"online entertainment","chinese":"網上娛樂"},{"english":"advice and approval","chinese":"建議和認同"},{"english":"spends hours online","chinese":"花數小時上網"},{"english":"without adult guidance","chinese":"沒有成人引導"},{"english":"copy unhealthy habits","chinese":"模仿不健康習慣"},{"english":"absorb harmful values","chinese":"吸收有害價值觀"},{"english":"before anyone notices","chinese":"在任何人察覺之前"},{"english":"responsible children","chinese":"負責任的孩子"},{"english":"struggle to build","chinese":"難以建立"},{"english":"discipline and self-control","chinese":"紀律和自制力"},{"english":"consistently present","chinese":"持續在場"},{"english":"model those qualities","chinese":"示範那些特質"},{"english":"two incomes","chinese":"兩份收入"},{"english":"to survive","chinese":"為了生存"},{"english":"emotional separation","chinese":"情感分離"},{"english":"leave children with","chinese":"令孩子只有；使孩子缺乏"},{"english":"less support, structure and moral guidance","chinese":"較少支援、規律和道德引導"}]},"model-essay-25-ielts-discuss-both-views":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-25-ielts-discuss-both-views","essayKey":"discuss-both-views:25","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-25-ielts-discuss-both-views","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/discuss-both-views-your-opinion/EdmundBd9ExpBth-Q25","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"Public health has become one of the most important concerns in modern society. Some believe governments should manage it, while others argue individuals must take charge of their own well-being. Although personal habits clearly affect a person’s physical condition, I strongly believe that the government should carry the main responsibility because it controls the systems and rules that shape those habits.","chinese":"公共健康已成為現代社會中最重要的關注之一。 有些人認為政府應該管理公共健康，而另一些人則主張個人必須為自己的健康負責。 儘管個人習慣明顯會影響一個人的身體狀況，我強烈認為政府應該承擔主要責任，因為它掌控著塑造這些習慣的制度和規則。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"On one side, there is a persuasive argument that protecting public health is a duty of the state. Governments are the only bodies with the authority and resources to provide clean water, safe hospitals, vaccination programmes, food-safety inspections, and reliable health education. If these foundations are weak, even disciplined citizens are left exposed to risks they cannot personally control. For example, a family may eat well and exercise regularly, but they cannot inspect every restaurant kitchen, regulate air pollution, or make medical care affordable by themselves. In this sense, public health is not merely a private lifestyle issue; it is part of the social infrastructure that allows whole communities to live safely.","chinese":"一方面，有一個很有說服力的觀點認為，保護公共健康是國家的責任。 政府是唯一擁有權力和資源去提供清潔食水、安全醫院、疫苗接種計劃、食品安全檢查，以及可靠健康教育的機構。 如果這些基礎薄弱，即使是自律的市民，也會暴露在他們個人無法控制的風險之中。 例如，一個家庭可能飲食健康並定期運動，但他們無法親自檢查每一間餐廳的廚房、規管空氣污染，或靠自己令醫療服務變得負擔得起。 從這個意義上說，公共健康並不僅僅是一個私人生活方式問題；它是社會基礎設施的一部分，使整個社區能夠安全地生活。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"By contrast, supporters of individual responsibility argue that no government can force people to make healthy choices every day. A person who smokes heavily, eats mostly fast food, refuses exercise, and ignores medical advice will probably suffer health problems even in a well-funded system. This view is reasonable because daily routines are like the small hinges on which long-term health swings. However, it is less convincing as the main position. People’s choices are often shaped by price, advertising, working hours, local facilities, and education, all of which are strongly influenced by public policy. Therefore, while individuals should cooperate by making sensible decisions, they cannot replace the protective role of the state.","chinese":"相比之下，支持個人責任的人認為，沒有任何政府能夠強迫人們每天作出健康的選擇。 一個大量吸煙、主要吃快餐、拒絕運動，並忽視醫療建議的人，即使身處資金充足的醫療制度中，也很可能會出現健康問題。 這個觀點是合理的，因為日常習慣就像細小的鉸鏈，而長遠健康正是在這些鉸鏈上轉動 然而，把它作為主要立場則較缺乏說服力。 人們的選擇往往受到價格、廣告、工作時間、本地設施和教育所塑造，而這些全部都深受公共政策影響。 因此，雖然個人應該透過作出明智決定來配合，但他們不能取代國家的保護角色。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, people should certainly take care of their own bodies, but public health should remain mainly the responsibility of the government. Individual discipline matters, yet strong public systems are the safety net without which personal effort can easily fall short.","chinese":"總結來說，人們當然應該照顧自己的身體，但公共健康仍應主要由政府負責。 個人自律固然重要，然而強大的公共制度是一張安全網；沒有它，個人的努力很容易不足以應對問題。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"public health","chinese":"公共衞生"},{"english":"one of the most important concerns","chinese":"最重要的關注之一"},{"english":"modern society","chinese":"現代社會"},{"english":"manage it","chinese":"管理它"},{"english":"take charge of","chinese":"掌管；負責"},{"english":"well-being","chinese":"福祉；健康"},{"english":"personal habits","chinese":"個人習慣"},{"english":"physical condition","chinese":"身體狀況"},{"english":"carry the main responsibility","chinese":"承擔主要責任"},{"english":"systems and rules","chinese":"制度和規則"},{"english":"shape those habits","chinese":"塑造那些習慣"},{"english":"on one side","chinese":"一方面"},{"english":"a persuasive argument","chinese":"有說服力的論點"},{"english":"protecting public health","chinese":"保護公共衞生"},{"english":"a duty of the state","chinese":"國家的責任"},{"english":"the only bodies with","chinese":"唯一擁有……的機構"},{"english":"authority and resources","chinese":"權力和資源"},{"english":"provide clean water","chinese":"提供清潔食水"},{"english":"safe hospitals","chinese":"安全醫院"},{"english":"vaccination programmes","chinese":"疫苗接種計劃"},{"english":"food-safety inspections","chinese":"食物安全檢查"},{"english":"reliable health education","chinese":"可靠的健康教育"},{"english":"these foundations","chinese":"這些基礎"},{"english":"be left exposed to","chinese":"被置於……風險之中"},{"english":"disciplined citizens","chinese":"自律的市民"},{"english":"risks they cannot personally control","chinese":"他們個人無法控制的風險"},{"english":"eat well","chinese":"飲食健康"},{"english":"exercise regularly","chinese":"定期運動"},{"english":"inspect every restaurant kitchen","chinese":"檢查每間餐廳廚房"},{"english":"regulate air pollution","chinese":"規管空氣污染"},{"english":"make medical care affordable","chinese":"令醫療服務變得可負擔"},{"english":"by themselves","chinese":"靠自己"},{"english":"in this sense","chinese":"從這個意義上說"},{"english":"not merely a private lifestyle issue","chinese":"不只是私人生活方式問題"},{"english":"social infrastructure","chinese":"社會基礎建設"},{"english":"allow whole communities to","chinese":"讓整個社區能夠"},{"english":"live safely","chinese":"安全地生活"},{"english":"by contrast","chinese":"相反"},{"english":"supporters of individual responsibility","chinese":"個人責任的支持者"},{"english":"force people to","chinese":"強迫人們去"},{"english":"make healthy choices","chinese":"作出健康選擇"},{"english":"smokes heavily","chinese":"大量吸煙"},{"english":"eats mostly fast food","chinese":"主要吃快餐"},{"english":"refuses exercise","chinese":"拒絕運動"},{"english":"ignores medical advice","chinese":"忽視醫療建議"},{"english":"suffer health problems","chinese":"出現健康問題"},{"english":"a well-funded system","chinese":"資金充足的制度"},{"english":"this view is reasonable","chinese":"這個看法是合理的"},{"english":"daily routines","chinese":"日常習慣"},{"english":"small hinges on which","chinese":"……所依靠的小鉸鏈"},{"english":"long-term health","chinese":"長遠健康"},{"english":"less convincing as","chinese":"作為……較欠說服力"},{"english":"the main position","chinese":"主要立場"},{"english":"be shaped by","chinese":"受……塑造"},{"english":"price, advertising, working hours, local facilities, and education","chinese":"價格、廣告、工作時間、本地設施和教育"},{"english":"strongly influenced by","chinese":"受到……強烈影響"},{"english":"public policy","chinese":"公共政策"},{"english":"cooperate by","chinese":"透過……合作"},{"english":"making sensible decisions","chinese":"作出明智決定"},{"english":"replace the protective role of","chinese":"取代……的保護作用"},{"english":"the protective role of the state","chinese":"國家的保護作用"},{"english":"take care of their own bodies","chinese":"照顧自己的身體"},{"english":"remain mainly the responsibility of","chinese":"仍應主要由……負責"},{"english":"individual discipline","chinese":"個人自律"},{"english":"matters","chinese":"很重要"},{"english":"strong public systems","chinese":"強大的公共制度"},{"english":"the safety net","chinese":"安全網"},{"english":"without which","chinese":"沒有它便"},{"english":"personal effort","chinese":"個人努力"},{"english":"fall short","chinese":"未能達標；不足以成功"}]},"model-essay-25-ielts-opinion":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-25-ielts-opinion","essayKey":"opinion:25","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-25-ielts-opinion","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/opinions/EdmundBd9OP-Q25","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"Personality is often discussed as if it were written into a person before birth, like an invisible script that cannot be revised. I completely disagree with this view. Although genes may create certain tendencies, character is not fixed at birth; it is continually shaped by upbringing, experience and deliberate effort.","chinese":"性格經常被討論得好像人在出生之前就已經被寫好一樣，如同一份無形而無法修改的劇本。 我完全不同意這種看法。 雖然基因可能會造成某些傾向，但人的性格並不是在出生時就固定不變；它會不斷受到成長環境、人生經歷和有意識的努力所塑造。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"The first reason is that a person's environment strongly influences how their traits develop. A child may be naturally quiet, but this does not mean he must remain passive or anxious for life. If he grows up in a supportive family and attends a school where teachers encourage discussion, teamwork and public speaking, he is likely to become more confident over time. By contrast, a harsh environment can make even a cheerful child defensive or withdrawn. This suggests that genes may provide the raw material, but surroundings help mold the final shape of a person's character.","chinese":"第一個原因是，一個人的環境會強烈影響其性格特質如何發展。 一個孩子可能天生安靜，但這並不代表他一生都必然會保持被動或焦慮。 如果他在一個支持性的家庭中成長，並就讀於一所老師鼓勵討論、團隊合作和公開發言的學校，他很可能會隨著時間變得更加自信。 相比之下，一個嚴苛的環境甚至可以令原本開朗的孩子變得防備心重或退縮。 這說明基因或許提供了原材料，但周圍環境會幫助塑造一個人性格的最終形態。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"A second reason is that people can change their behaviour through practice, reflection and repeated experience. Traits such as patience, resilience and self-control are not simply inherited gifts; they can be strengthened like muscles. For example, someone who is easily angered may learn to pause before reacting, listen to feedback and practise calmer ways of handling conflict. Over time, these habits can become part of that person's normal character. Similarly, young adults who enter demanding workplaces often become more disciplined and emotionally mature because daily pressure forces them to adapt. If personality were entirely predetermined, such growth would be impossible, yet ordinary life shows the opposite.","chinese":"第二個原因是，人們可以透過練習、反思和反覆經驗來改變自己的行為。 耐性、韌性和自制力等特質並不只是遺傳而來的天賦；它們可以像肌肉一樣被強化。 例如，一個容易生氣的人可以學會在作出反應之前先停一停、聆聽別人的回饋，並練習以更冷靜的方式處理衝突。 隨著時間過去，這些習慣可以成為那個人正常性格的一部分。 同樣地，進入高要求職場的年輕成年人，往往會變得更有紀律，也在情緒上更加成熟，因為日常壓力會迫使他們適應。 如果性格完全是預先決定的，那麼這種成長便不可能出現；然而，日常生活所顯示的正正相反。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, I completely reject the idea that personality is locked in place before birth. Genes may influence people's starting points, but family, education, relationships and conscious effort can reshape character throughout life. Human personality is not a stone statue; it is more like a living tree, shaped by both its roots and the conditions in which it grows.","chinese":"總結來說，我完全否定性格在出生之前就已經被鎖定不變這種想法。 基因可能會影響人的起點，但家庭、教育、人際關係和有意識的努力，都可以在人生過程中重塑性格。 人的性格並不是一座石像；它更像一棵活著的樹，既受其根部影響，也受它生長環境的條件所塑造。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"personality","chinese":"性格"},{"english":"be discussed as if","chinese":"被討論得好像……"},{"english":"written into","chinese":"寫進……之中"},{"english":"before birth","chinese":"出生之前"},{"english":"invisible script","chinese":"隱形劇本"},{"english":"cannot be revised","chinese":"不能被修改"},{"english":"completely disagree with","chinese":"完全不同意……"},{"english":"genes","chinese":"基因"},{"english":"create certain tendencies","chinese":"形成某些傾向"},{"english":"character","chinese":"品格；性格"},{"english":"fixed at birth","chinese":"出生時已固定"},{"english":"continually shaped by","chinese":"不斷受……塑造"},{"english":"upbringing","chinese":"成長教養"},{"english":"deliberate effort","chinese":"有意識的努力"},{"english":"a person's environment","chinese":"一個人的環境"},{"english":"strongly influences","chinese":"強烈影響"},{"english":"traits","chinese":"特質"},{"english":"naturally quiet","chinese":"天生安靜"},{"english":"remain passive or anxious for life","chinese":"一生都被動或焦慮"},{"english":"supportive family","chinese":"支持性的家庭"},{"english":"attend a school where","chinese":"就讀一間……的學校"},{"english":"encourage discussion","chinese":"鼓勵討論"},{"english":"teamwork and public speaking","chinese":"團隊合作和公開演說"},{"english":"become more confident over time","chinese":"隨着時間變得更自信"},{"english":"by contrast","chinese":"相比之下"},{"english":"harsh environment","chinese":"嚴苛環境"},{"english":"cheerful child","chinese":"開朗的孩子"},{"english":"defensive or withdrawn","chinese":"有戒心或退縮"},{"english":"suggests that","chinese":"這顯示……"},{"english":"raw material","chinese":"原材料"},{"english":"surroundings","chinese":"周遭環境"},{"english":"mold the final shape of","chinese":"塑造……的最終形態"},{"english":"change their behaviour","chinese":"改變自己的行為"},{"english":"practice, reflection and repeated experience","chinese":"練習、反思和重複經驗"},{"english":"patience, resilience and self-control","chinese":"耐性、韌性和自制力"},{"english":"inherited gifts","chinese":"遺傳得來的天賦"},{"english":"be strengthened like muscles","chinese":"像肌肉一樣被鍛鍊"},{"english":"easily angered","chinese":"容易發怒"},{"english":"pause before reacting","chinese":"在反應前先停一停"},{"english":"listen to feedback","chinese":"聆聽回饋"},{"english":"handling conflict","chinese":"處理衝突"},{"english":"become part of","chinese":"成為……的一部分"},{"english":"normal character","chinese":"平常性格"},{"english":"young adults","chinese":"年輕成年人"},{"english":"demanding workplaces","chinese":"要求高的工作場所"},{"english":"emotionally mature","chinese":"情緒成熟"},{"english":"daily pressure","chinese":"日常壓力"},{"english":"forces them to adapt","chinese":"迫使他們適應"},{"english":"entirely predetermined","chinese":"完全預先決定"},{"english":"ordinary life","chinese":"日常生活"},{"english":"shows the opposite","chinese":"顯示相反情況"},{"english":"completely reject the idea that","chinese":"完全否定……的想法"},{"english":"locked in place","chinese":"被固定不變"},{"english":"starting points","chinese":"起點"},{"english":"conscious effort","chinese":"有意識的努力"},{"english":"reshape character","chinese":"重塑性格"},{"english":"throughout life","chinese":"終其一生"},{"english":"stone statue","chinese":"石像"},{"english":"living tree","chinese":"活生生的樹"},{"english":"shaped by both","chinese":"同時受兩者塑造"},{"english":"roots","chinese":"根"},{"english":"conditions in which it grows","chinese":"它生長的環境"}]},"model-essay-26-ielts-advantage-disadvantage":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-26-ielts-advantage-disadvantage","essayKey":"advantage-disadvantage:26","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-26-ielts-advantage-disadvantage","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/advantage-and-disadvantage/EdmundBd9AdDisAd-Q26","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"Traffic congestion has become a defining problem in many large cities, wasting commuters’ time, harming productivity, and putting pressure on existing transport systems. One proposed solution is to build sky trains, which run on elevated tracks rather than on roads or beneath the ground. This essay will examine the advantages and disadvantages of using this approach to reduce urban congestion.","chinese":"交通擠塞已成為許多大城市的典型問題，不但浪費通勤者的時間、損害生產力，亦對現有交通系統造成壓力。 其中一種被提出的解決方法，是興建空中列車，也就是在高架軌道上運行，而不是在地面道路或地下行駛。 本文將探討利用這種方法來紓緩城市交通擠塞的優點與缺點。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"One major advantage of sky trains is that they can transport large numbers of passengers without competing with cars, buses, or delivery vehicles for limited road space. Because the system operates above street level, it is largely unaffected by traffic lights, accidents, and rush-hour bottlenecks, which makes journeys faster and more reliable. For example, a worker travelling from an outer residential district to the city centre could still arrive on time even if the roads below were at a standstill. Another benefit is that elevated lines can, in some cases, be simpler to construct than underground railways, since they do not require extensive tunnelling beneath densely built-up areas. For instance, a city could install pillars and tracks above a wide central avenue more quickly than digging beneath historic buildings and buried utility lines.","chinese":"空中列車其中一個主要優點，是它能夠在不與私家車、巴士或送貨車爭奪有限路面空間的情況下運載大量乘客。 由於這套系統在街道上方運行，它大致不受交通燈、交通意外及繁忙時段樽頸情況影響，因而令行程更快捷，也更可靠。 這意味著通勤人士可以避開路面交通的不確定性，更準時到達目的地，並減輕本已擠塞道路的壓力。 例如，一名由外圍住宅區前往市中心上班的員工，即使下方道路完全陷入停滯，仍然可以準時到達。 另一個好處是，在某些情況下，高架鐵路比地下鐵路更容易興建，因為它不需要在建築密集地區下方進行大規模隧道工程。 結果是，城市可能可以更快擴展公共交通、避免部分工程上的複雜問題，並更早增加運載能力。 例如，一個城市可以在寬闊的中央大道上方興建支柱和軌道，而這往往比在歷史建築及地下公用設施下方開挖地鐵更快完成。 因此，空中列車能透過提供不受路面交通影響的出行方式，以及一種可能更快擴展交通基建的方法，來改善城市流動性。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"However, this solution also has clear disadvantages. The first is financial cost: although sky trains may be less expensive than subways, they still require substantial investment in land acquisition, engineering, stations, and long-term maintenance. For example, if a city spends most of its transport budget on one elevated line, it may have to postpone improvements to buses or suburban roads that are also badly needed. A second drawback is their impact on the urban environment. Large overhead structures can block sunlight, create noise, and reduce privacy for nearby residents. For instance, people living in apartment blocks beside an elevated track may have trains passing their windows from early morning until late at night, making the area less pleasant to live in.","chinese":"然而，這種解決方案亦有明顯缺點。 第一個缺點是財政成本：雖然空中列車可能比地下鐵路便宜，但它仍然需要在土地取得、工程建設、車站設施及長期維修方面投入大量資金。 當大量公共資金被投放到單一大型項目時，其他交通需求便可能被忽視或延後處理。 例如，如果一個城市把大部分交通預算投放在一條高架鐵路線上，它便可能需要延後改善同樣急需提升的巴士服務或郊區道路。 第二個缺點，是它對城市環境所造成的影響。 大型高架結構可能遮擋陽光、製造噪音，並削弱附近居民的私隱，從而令周邊社區變得較不宜居。 例如，居住在高架軌道旁邊公寓的居民，可能由清晨到深夜都會有列車從窗邊駛過，令日常生活明顯變得較不舒適。 因此，雖然空中列車或許能夠紓緩交通擠塞，但它同時也可能為城市帶來嚴重的財政及環境代價。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In summary, sky trains offer clear benefits because they can bypass road congestion and expand public transport capacity efficiently. At the same time, their high cost and their potential impact on surrounding neighbourhoods mean that they are not a perfect solution to urban traffic problems.","chinese":"總結來說，空中列車具有明顯優點，因為它能避開路面交通擠塞，並更有效地提升運輸能力。 與此同時，其高昂成本以及對周邊社區造成的負面影響，也意味著它並不是解決城市交通問題的完美方案。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"traffic congestion","chinese":"交通擠塞"},{"english":"a defining problem","chinese":"標誌性問題；主要問題"},{"english":"large cities","chinese":"大城市"},{"english":"waste commuters' time","chinese":"浪費通勤人士的時間"},{"english":"commuters","chinese":"通勤人士"},{"english":"harm productivity","chinese":"損害生產力"},{"english":"put pressure on","chinese":"對……造成壓力"},{"english":"existing transport systems","chinese":"現有交通系統"},{"english":"one proposed solution","chinese":"一個被提出的解決方案"},{"english":"sky trains","chinese":"高架列車"},{"english":"elevated tracks","chinese":"高架路軌"},{"english":"rather than on roads","chinese":"而不是在道路上"},{"english":"beneath the ground","chinese":"在地底下"},{"english":"examine the advantages and disadvantages of","chinese":"探討……的優點和缺點"},{"english":"this approach","chinese":"這種方法"},{"english":"reduce urban congestion","chinese":"減少城市交通擠塞"},{"english":"one major advantage","chinese":"一個主要優點"},{"english":"transport large numbers of passengers","chinese":"運載大量乘客"},{"english":"compete with","chinese":"與……競爭"},{"english":"delivery vehicles","chinese":"送貨車輛"},{"english":"limited road space","chinese":"有限道路空間"},{"english":"operate above street level","chinese":"在街道上方運行"},{"english":"largely unaffected by","chinese":"基本不受……影響"},{"english":"traffic lights","chinese":"交通燈"},{"english":"rush-hour bottlenecks","chinese":"繁忙時間的交通瓶頸"},{"english":"faster and more reliable","chinese":"更快和更可靠"},{"english":"an outer residential district","chinese":"外圍住宅區"},{"english":"the city centre","chinese":"市中心"},{"english":"arrive on time","chinese":"準時到達"},{"english":"at a standstill","chinese":"完全停頓"},{"english":"elevated lines","chinese":"高架鐵路線"},{"english":"simpler to construct","chinese":"較易興建"},{"english":"underground railways","chinese":"地下鐵路"},{"english":"extensive tunnelling","chinese":"大規模挖掘隧道"},{"english":"densely built-up areas","chinese":"建築密集地區"},{"english":"install pillars and tracks","chinese":"安裝支柱和路軌"},{"english":"a wide central avenue","chinese":"寬闊的市中心大道"},{"english":"digging beneath","chinese":"在……下面挖掘"},{"english":"historic buildings","chinese":"歷史建築"},{"english":"buried utility lines","chinese":"地底公用設施管線"},{"english":"clear disadvantages","chinese":"明顯缺點"},{"english":"financial cost","chinese":"財政成本"},{"english":"less expensive than","chinese":"比……便宜"},{"english":"subways","chinese":"地下鐵路"},{"english":"require substantial investment in","chinese":"需要在……方面作大量投資"},{"english":"substantial investment","chinese":"大量投資"},{"english":"land acquisition","chinese":"收地"},{"english":"engineering","chinese":"工程"},{"english":"long-term maintenance","chinese":"長期維修保養"},{"english":"transport budget","chinese":"交通預算"},{"english":"postpone improvements to","chinese":"推遲對……的改善"},{"english":"suburban roads","chinese":"市郊道路"},{"english":"badly needed","chinese":"非常需要"},{"english":"a second drawback","chinese":"第二個缺點"},{"english":"impact on","chinese":"對……的影響"},{"english":"the urban environment","chinese":"城市環境"},{"english":"overhead structures","chinese":"架空結構"},{"english":"block sunlight","chinese":"阻擋陽光"},{"english":"reduce privacy","chinese":"降低私隱"},{"english":"nearby residents","chinese":"附近居民"},{"english":"apartment blocks","chinese":"住宅大廈"},{"english":"beside an elevated track","chinese":"在高架路軌旁邊"},{"english":"passing their windows","chinese":"經過窗外"},{"english":"from early morning until late at night","chinese":"從清晨到深夜"},{"english":"less pleasant to live in","chinese":"居住起來較不舒適"},{"english":"in summary","chinese":"總括而言"},{"english":"offer clear benefits","chinese":"帶來明顯好處"},{"english":"bypass road congestion","chinese":"繞過道路交通擠塞"},{"english":"expand public transport capacity","chinese":"擴大公共交通運載能力"},{"english":"public transport capacity","chinese":"公共交通運載能力"},{"english":"efficiently","chinese":"有效率地"},{"english":"at the same time","chinese":"同時"},{"english":"potential impact on","chinese":"對……的潛在影響"},{"english":"surrounding neighbourhoods","chinese":"周邊社區"},{"english":"a perfect solution to","chinese":"……的完美解決方案"},{"english":"urban traffic problems","chinese":"城市交通問題"}]},"model-essay-26-ielts-direct-question":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-26-ielts-direct-question","essayKey":"direct-question:26","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-26-ielts-direct-question","flashDeckId":"","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"Because nuclear families have fewer members than extended households, they can relocate with less practical difficulty. In my view, children do benefit from moving, and the advantages clearly outweigh the disadvantages because relocation builds adaptability and may open the door to better opportunities.","chinese":"因為核心家庭的成員比大家庭少，所以它們在搬遷時面對的實際困難較少。 在我看來，孩子確實能從搬遷中受益，而且優點明顯大於缺點，因為搬遷能培養適應能力，並可能為他們打開通往更好機會的大門。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"The main benefit is that moving teaches children how to adjust to unfamiliar environments. When a child enters a new school or city, they must learn new routines, make friends, and read unfamiliar social expectations. This may be uncomfortable at first, but it trains them to observe, communicate, and cope with change rather than fear it. For example, a child who moves from a quiet town to a large city may initially feel lost; after joining classes and sports teams, however, they often become more confident around strangers. In this sense, relocation is not just a change of address; it is a practical lesson in resilience.","chinese":"主要好處是，搬遷能教會孩子如何適應陌生環境。 當一個孩子進入一所新學校或一個新城市時，他們必須學習新的日常規律、結交朋友，並理解陌生的社交期待。 這一開始可能會令人不舒服，但它訓練孩子去觀察、溝通，並應對變化，而不是害怕變化 例如，一個從安靜小鎮搬到大城市的孩子，起初可能會感到迷失；然而，在參加課堂和運動隊之後，他們往往會在陌生人面前變得更加自信。 從這個意義上說，搬遷不只是地址的改變；它是一堂關於韌性的實際課程。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"Moving can also improve a child’s long-term prospects. Parents often relocate for better jobs, safer neighbourhoods, stronger schools, or more reliable services. If a family moves to an area where education is stable and extracurricular activities are accessible, the child receives richer academic and social support. These conditions can shape future confidence, ambition, and career options.","chinese":"搬遷也能改善孩子的長遠前景。 父母往往會為了更好的工作、更安全的社區、更優質的學校，或更可靠的服務而搬遷。 如果一個家庭搬到教育穩定、課外活動容易接觸到的地區，孩子便能獲得更豐富的學業和社交支持。 這些條件能夠塑造孩子未來的自信、抱負和職業選擇。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 3","english":"Admittedly, moving can create emotional difficulties. Children may feel uprooted when they leave close friends, familiar teachers, and a place that feels like home. In some cases, this disruption may affect their mood or school performance for a while. However, these disadvantages are usually temporary if parents provide steady support, maintain routines, and help children stay connected with old friends while building new relationships. The discomfort of transition is real, but it is not greater than the lasting gains.","chinese":"誠然，搬遷可能會造成情感上的困難。 當孩子離開親密的朋友、熟悉的老師，以及一個讓他們感覺像家的地方時，他們可能會感到自己被連根拔起。 在某些情況下，這種干擾可能會在一段時間內影響他們的情緒或學校表現。 然而，如果父母能提供穩定的支持、維持日常規律，並幫助孩子在建立新關係的同時與舊朋友保持聯繫，這些缺點通常只是暫時的。 過渡期的不適是真實存在的，但它並不大於那些長遠的收穫。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, children can benefit significantly from moving. Although relocation may cause short-term stress, its advantages outweigh its disadvantages because it strengthens adaptability and may give children access to a better future.","chinese":"總結來說，孩子能夠從搬遷中獲得顯著好處。 儘管搬遷可能造成短期壓力，但它的優點大於缺點，因為它能加強適應能力，並可能讓孩子接觸到更好的未來。"}],"vocabulary":[]},"model-essay-26-ielts-discuss-both-views":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-26-ielts-discuss-both-views","essayKey":"discuss-both-views:26","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-26-ielts-discuss-both-views","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/discuss-both-views-your-opinion/EdmundBd9ExpBth-Q26","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"In many cities, the future of historic architecture has become a matter of debate. While some argue that old buildings should be preserved, others believe that demolishing them and constructing modern replacements is more practical. In my view, old buildings should be protected because they carry cultural value that cannot be rebuilt once it is lost.","chinese":"在許多城市，歷史建築的未來已成為一個備受爭議的問題。 雖然有些人認為舊建築應該被保留，但另一些人則相信，拆除它們並建造現代化的新建築會更加實際。 在我看來，舊建築應該受到保護，因為它們承載著一旦失去便無法重建的文化價值。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"Those who support replacing old buildings often have reasonable practical concern. Many ageing structures are expensive to maintain, especially when their foundations, wiring, or drainage systems no longer meet modern safety standards. If a city is short of housing or commercial space, keeping a large, outdated building may seem like a poor use of valuable land. For example, replacing a damaged warehouse with a modern apartment block could provide homes for hundreds of residents and reduce pressure on crowded neighbourhoods. From this perspective, newer buildings can make cities safer, more efficient, and better suited to present-day needs.","chinese":"支持取代舊建築的人，通常有一個合理的實際考量。 許多老化的建築維護成本高昂，尤其是當它們的地基、電線或排水系統已不再符合現代安全標準時。 如果一座城市缺乏住宅或商業空間，保留一座大型而過時的建築，可能看起來像是在不善用寶貴土地。 例如，用一座現代公寓大樓取代一個受損倉庫，可以為數百名居民提供住所，並減輕擁擠社區的壓力。 從這個角度來看，較新的建築可以使城市更安全、更有效率，也更能符合現代需求。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"However, I believe preservation is ultimately more important because old buildings give a city its identity. They are not merely piles of bricks; they are visible records of how previous generations lived, worked, and understood beauty. When such buildings are destroyed, a city may gain floor space, but it loses part of its memory. Historic streets, traditional shop houses, and old public buildings can also attract tourism and support local businesses, which means preservation can bring economic value as well as cultural value. More importantly, protected buildings can often be adapted rather than abandoned. An old theatre, for instance, can become a community arts centre, allowing the past to remain useful in the present.","chinese":"然而，我認為保育最終更重要，因為舊建築賦予一座城市身份。 它們不只是磚塊堆砌而成的東西；它們是前人如何生活、工作和理解美感的可見記錄。 當這些建築被摧毀時，一座城市也許會獲得更多樓面空間，但它會失去部分記憶。 歷史街道、傳統店屋和舊公共建築也可以吸引旅遊業並支持本地商業，這意味著保育不僅能帶來文化價值，也能帶來經濟價值。 更重要的是，受保護的建築往往可以被改造使用，而不是被廢棄。 例如，一座舊劇院可以變成社區藝術中心，讓過去在現在仍然保持有用。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, although replacing old buildings can sometimes solve practical problems, I strongly believe that they should be protected instead of being replaced. Cities need development, but development should not come at the cost of erasing their history.","chinese":"總結來說，雖然取代舊建築有時能解決實際問題，但我堅定地認為，它們應該被保護，而不是被取代。 城市需要發展，但發展不應以抹去其歷史為代價。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"historic architecture","chinese":"歷史建築"},{"english":"a matter of debate","chinese":"具爭議的問題"},{"english":"old buildings","chinese":"舊建築"},{"english":"be preserved","chinese":"被保育；被保留"},{"english":"demolishing them","chinese":"拆卸它們"},{"english":"constructing modern replacements","chinese":"興建現代化替代建築"},{"english":"more practical","chinese":"更實際"},{"english":"in my view","chinese":"在我看來"},{"english":"be protected","chinese":"被保護"},{"english":"carry cultural value","chinese":"承載文化價值"},{"english":"cannot be rebuilt","chinese":"不能被重建"},{"english":"once it is lost","chinese":"一旦失去"},{"english":"support replacing","chinese":"支持取代"},{"english":"reasonable practical concern","chinese":"合理的實際考慮"},{"english":"ageing structures","chinese":"老化建築"},{"english":"expensive to maintain","chinese":"維修成本高"},{"english":"foundations, wiring, or drainage systems","chinese":"地基、電線或排水系統"},{"english":"no longer meet","chinese":"不再符合"},{"english":"modern safety standards","chinese":"現代安全標準"},{"english":"be short of","chinese":"缺乏"},{"english":"housing or commercial space","chinese":"住房或商業空間"},{"english":"outdated building","chinese":"過時建築"},{"english":"a poor use of","chinese":"對……的低效使用"},{"english":"valuable land","chinese":"寶貴土地"},{"english":"a damaged warehouse","chinese":"受損倉庫"},{"english":"a modern apartment block","chinese":"現代化住宅大廈"},{"english":"provide homes for","chinese":"為……提供住所"},{"english":"hundreds of residents","chinese":"數百名居民"},{"english":"reduce pressure on","chinese":"減輕……的壓力"},{"english":"crowded neighbourhoods","chinese":"擠迫社區"},{"english":"from this perspective","chinese":"從這個角度來看"},{"english":"newer buildings","chinese":"較新的建築物"},{"english":"better suited to","chinese":"更適合"},{"english":"present-day needs","chinese":"現今需要"},{"english":"preservation","chinese":"保育"},{"english":"ultimately more important","chinese":"最終更重要"},{"english":"give a city its identity","chinese":"賦予城市身份"},{"english":"not merely piles of bricks","chinese":"不只是一堆磚頭"},{"english":"visible records of","chinese":"……的可見記錄"},{"english":"previous generations","chinese":"前幾代人"},{"english":"understood beauty","chinese":"理解美"},{"english":"be destroyed","chinese":"被摧毀"},{"english":"gain floor space","chinese":"增加樓面空間"},{"english":"lose part of its memory","chinese":"失去部分記憶"},{"english":"historic streets","chinese":"歷史街道"},{"english":"traditional shop houses","chinese":"傳統店屋"},{"english":"old public buildings","chinese":"舊公共建築"},{"english":"attract tourism","chinese":"吸引旅遊"},{"english":"support local businesses","chinese":"支持本地商戶"},{"english":"economic value as well as cultural value","chinese":"經濟價值以及文化價值"},{"english":"more importantly","chinese":"更重要的是"},{"english":"protected buildings","chinese":"受保護建築"},{"english":"be adapted rather than abandoned","chinese":"被改造再用，而不是被棄置"},{"english":"an old theatre","chinese":"舊劇院"},{"english":"a community arts centre","chinese":"社區藝術中心"},{"english":"allow the past to remain useful","chinese":"讓過去在當下繼續有用"},{"english":"in the present","chinese":"在當下"},{"english":"solve practical problems","chinese":"解決實際問題"},{"english":"instead of being replaced","chinese":"而不是被取代"},{"english":"cities need development","chinese":"城市需要發展"},{"english":"come at the cost of","chinese":"以犧牲……為代價"},{"english":"erasing their history","chinese":"抹去其歷史"}]},"model-essay-26-ielts-opinion":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-26-ielts-opinion","essayKey":"opinion:26","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-26-ielts-opinion","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/opinions/EdmundBd9OP-Q26","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"Discussions about gender and violence often rest on long-standing assumptions about personality. While women are sometimes described as more caring and less confrontational than men, I completely disagree that they are naturally more peaceful. In my view, peacefulness is shaped far more by upbringing, social expectations and power than by biological sex.","chinese":"關於性別與暴力的討論，往往建立在一些長久以來對性格的假設之上。 雖然女性有時被描述為比男性更關懷他人，也較少具對抗性， 但我完全不同意女性天生更加和平的說法。在我看來，和平的性格遠比生理性別更大程度上受到成長環境、社會期望和權力關係所塑造。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"First, the idea that women are born more peace-loving oversimplifies how character is formed. From childhood, boys and girls are often taught to behave in different ways: girls may be encouraged to be patient, polite and emotionally aware, whereas boys may be praised for toughness, competitiveness and dominance. Over time, these expectations can become a mask that people mistake for nature. For example, a girl who is repeatedly told to avoid conflict may learn to express disagreement quietly, while a boy who is rewarded for winning arguments may become more forceful. This does not prove that one sex is naturally peaceful and the other naturally aggressive; it shows that society trains people to perform different versions of acceptable behaviour.","chinese":"首先，女性天生更愛好和平這種想法，過度簡化了性格形成的過程。 從童年開始，男孩和女孩常常被教導以不同方式行事：女孩可能被鼓勵要有耐性、有禮貌並具備情緒覺察能力，而男孩則可能因堅強、好勝和具支配性而受到稱讚。 久而久之，這些期望可能變成一副面具，而人們卻誤以為那是天性。 例如，一個反覆被教導要避免衝突的女孩，可能會學會以安靜的方式表達不同意見；而一個因在爭論中取勝而受到獎勵的男孩，則可能變得更加強勢。 這並不能證明某一性別天生和平，而另一性別天生具攻擊性；它只是顯示社會訓練人們表現出不同版本的可接受行為。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"Moreover, describing women as naturally nurturing can be harmful because it places unfair moral expectations on them and excuses aggression in men. If women are assumed to be gentle by nature, those who are ambitious, angry or politically assertive may be judged as abnormal. At the same time, men who show violence may be treated as if they are simply following their instincts, which lowers the standard of responsibility expected of them. In reality, both men and women can be compassionate, cruel, diplomatic or confrontational depending on their values, circumstances and choices. A female leader can make ruthless decisions, just as a male teacher or father can create a calm and caring environment.","chinese":"此外，把女性描述為天生具養育特質可能是有害的，因為這會把不公平的道德期望加在女性身上，同時為男性的攻擊性開脫。 如果女性被假定為天性溫柔，那些有野心、會憤怒或在政治上立場堅定的女性，便可能被視為不正常。 與此同時，表現出暴力的男性可能會被看待成只是順從本能，這便降低了社會對他們責任感的要求標準。 事實上，男性和女性都可以是富有同情心的、殘酷的、圓融的或具對抗性的，這取決於他們的價值觀、處境和選擇。 一位女性領袖可以作出冷酷的決定，正如一位男性教師或父親也可以創造一個平靜而充滿關懷的環境。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, I entirely reject the claim that women are generally more peaceful because they are naturally more nurturing. Peace is not written into one gender like a birthmark; it is cultivated through education, culture and personal responsibility.","chinese":"總結來說，我完全反對女性通常更和平是因為她們天生更具養育特質這一說法。 和平並不像胎記一樣寫在某一個性別身上；它是透過教育、文化和個人責任培養出來的"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"gender and violence","chinese":"性別與暴力"},{"english":"rest on","chinese":"建基於；依賴"},{"english":"long-standing assumptions","chinese":"長久以來的假設"},{"english":"personality","chinese":"性格"},{"english":"be described as","chinese":"被描述為"},{"english":"caring","chinese":"關懷他人的"},{"english":"less confrontational","chinese":"較少對抗性的"},{"english":"naturally more peaceful","chinese":"天生較和平；天生較平和"},{"english":"in my view","chinese":"在我看來"},{"english":"peacefulness","chinese":"平和性格；和平傾向"},{"english":"be shaped by","chinese":"受……塑造"},{"english":"upbringing","chinese":"成長教養"},{"english":"social expectations","chinese":"社會期望"},{"english":"biological sex","chinese":"生理性別"},{"english":"be born more peace-loving","chinese":"天生較愛好和平"},{"english":"oversimplifies","chinese":"過分簡化"},{"english":"how character is formed","chinese":"性格如何形成"},{"english":"from childhood","chinese":"從童年開始"},{"english":"behave in different ways","chinese":"以不同方式行為"},{"english":"be encouraged to","chinese":"被鼓勵去……"},{"english":"emotionally aware","chinese":"對情緒有覺察力"},{"english":"whereas","chinese":"而；然而"},{"english":"be praised for","chinese":"因……而受到讚賞"},{"english":"toughness","chinese":"強硬；堅韌"},{"english":"competitiveness","chinese":"競爭性"},{"english":"dominance","chinese":"支配性"},{"english":"over time","chinese":"隨着時間過去"},{"english":"become a mask","chinese":"變成一個面具"},{"english":"mistake for nature","chinese":"誤以為是天性"},{"english":"avoid conflict","chinese":"避免衝突"},{"english":"express disagreement quietly","chinese":"安靜地表達不同意"},{"english":"be rewarded for","chinese":"因……而得到獎勵"},{"english":"winning arguments","chinese":"贏得爭論"},{"english":"forceful","chinese":"強勢的；有壓迫感的"},{"english":"naturally aggressive","chinese":"天生具攻擊性"},{"english":"trains people to","chinese":"訓練人們去……"},{"english":"perform different versions of","chinese":"表現出不同版本的……"},{"english":"acceptable behaviour","chinese":"可接受行為"},{"english":"describing women as","chinese":"將女性描述為……"},{"english":"naturally nurturing","chinese":"天生具照顧特質"},{"english":"places unfair moral expectations on","chinese":"對……施加不公平的道德期望"},{"english":"moral expectations","chinese":"道德期望"},{"english":"excuses aggression in","chinese":"為……的攻擊性開脫"},{"english":"assumed to be","chinese":"被假定為"},{"english":"gentle by nature","chinese":"天性溫和"},{"english":"politically assertive","chinese":"政治上敢於表達立場的"},{"english":"be judged as abnormal","chinese":"被評為不正常"},{"english":"at the same time","chinese":"同時"},{"english":"show violence","chinese":"表現出暴力"},{"english":"following their instincts","chinese":"遵循自己的本能"},{"english":"lowers the standard of responsibility","chinese":"降低對責任的要求"},{"english":"in reality","chinese":"實際上"},{"english":"compassionate","chinese":"有同情心的"},{"english":"cruel","chinese":"殘酷的"},{"english":"diplomatic","chinese":"善於協調的；圓融的"},{"english":"depending on","chinese":"取決於"},{"english":"values, circumstances and choices","chinese":"價值觀、處境和選擇"},{"english":"female leader","chinese":"女性領袖"},{"english":"ruthless decisions","chinese":"無情的決定"},{"english":"just as","chinese":"正如"},{"english":"calm and caring environment","chinese":"平靜而關愛的環境"},{"english":"entirely reject the claim","chinese":"完全否定這種說法"},{"english":"generally more peaceful","chinese":"一般較和平"},{"english":"written into one gender","chinese":"寫進某一性別之中"},{"english":"birthmark","chinese":"胎記"},{"english":"be cultivated through","chinese":"透過……培養"},{"english":"personal responsibility","chinese":"個人責任"}]},"model-essay-27-ielts-advantage-disadvantage":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-27-ielts-advantage-disadvantage","essayKey":"advantage-disadvantage:27","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-27-ielts-advantage-disadvantage","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/advantage-and-disadvantage/EdmundBd9AdDisAd-Q27","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"In many workplaces, especially those that rely heavily on digital communication, employers now expect staff to remain reachable even during annual leave. Although this arrangement may seem commercially sensible, I do not believe it has more advantages than disadvantages. Any gain in responsiveness is outweighed by the harm it causes to employees’ recovery, morale and long-term effectiveness.","chinese":"在許多職場中，尤其是那些高度依賴數碼溝通的工作環境裡，僱主如今要求員工即使在年假期間也要保持聯絡。 儘管這種安排在商業上看似合理， 我並不認為這種發展的優點大於缺點，因為它在回應速度上的任何好處，都被其對員工休息恢復、士氣以及長遠工作效率所造成的損害所超過。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"Admittedly, there is one clear benefit to this practice. If a serious problem arises unexpectedly, immediate contact with the relevant employee can prevent a minor disruption from developing into a major one. A delayed shipment, a software failure or an urgent client request can often be resolved quickly when a staff member is available to clarify information or make a decision. For example, if a hotel manager can reach the technician who understands the booking system during a holiday, dozens of reservations may be saved and customer complaints reduced. In genuinely urgent situations, therefore, constant availability can protect a company’s operations.","chinese":"誠然，這種做法的一項優點是它能讓緊急問題更快得到處理。 如果突發嚴重問題，立即聯絡相關員工可以防止小型干擾演變成重大事故。 由於該員工本身已具備所需知識或決策權，問題往往可以立即釐清，決策也能更快作出，而正常運作亦可在最少延誤下恢復。 例如，如果一位酒店經理能在假期期間聯絡到熟悉訂房系統的技術人員，便可能挽救數十個預約，並減少顧客投訴。 這種持續可聯絡的狀態，也可能令僱主和客戶更放心，認為機構能夠隨時應對突發情況。 這種印象可以增強商業信心，維護公司的聲譽，並在突發事件發生時減低財務損失的風險。 例如，一位在公眾假期期間仍能獲得緊急回覆的客戶，往往更有可能信任該公司，並維持雙方的合作關係。 因此，在真正緊急的情況下，假期期間仍可聯絡員工，的確能帶來某些運作上的好處。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"Nevertheless, the disadvantages are far more significant. First, employees who know they may be contacted at any moment are unable to disconnect mentally from work, even when they are officially resting. Because their attention remains partly fixed on possible messages or calls, holidays no longer serve their essential purpose of restoring energy and relieving stress. As a result, workers often return feeling drained rather than refreshed. Second, this culture gradually damages commitment to the employer. When private time is repeatedly interrupted, people feel that their personal boundaries are not respected, which breeds resentment and reduces loyalty. A nurse, teacher or office worker who is contacted during family trips or public holidays may cooperate at first, but repeated intrusion can eventually lead to burnout or resignation. Businesses then face higher recruitment costs, weaker team stability and lower productivity.","chinese":"然而，這種發展的缺點明顯更為嚴重，因為它不但妨礙員工得到真正休息，還會逐漸削弱他們對工作的投入感。 首先，當員工知道自己隨時可能被聯絡時，即使名義上正在休假，也無法在心理上真正脫離工作。 結果是，他們始終對來電或訊息保持某種警覺，壓力水平持續偏高，而假期亦無法如其應有的功能般幫助他們恢復精力。 例如，一名在家庭旅行期間不斷查看電郵的上班族，回到工作崗位時往往會感到精神疲憊，而非重新充電。 第二，私人時間一再被工作侵入，會使員工感到自己的個人界線沒有受到尊重。 這會滋生怨氣，削弱士氣，長遠而言更可能導致職業倦怠、忠誠度下降，甚至離職，而最終受害的其實也是機構本身。 一名護士、教師或文職員工如果年復一年在假期中被打擾，起初或許仍會配合，但最終很可能選擇辭職，轉到一份界線更健康的工作。 基於以上原因，長遠來看，假期期間持續聯絡員工帶來的傷害多於好處。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, while the ability to contact staff on holidays may occasionally help employers deal with emergencies, it is a negative development overall. The limited operational advantage is decisively outweighed by the damage done to workers’ wellbeing and to the sustainable performance of the organisation itself.","chinese":"總結而言，雖然在假期期間仍能聯絡員工有時的確能幫助僱主處理緊急情況，但整體來說，這是一種負面的發展。 在回應速度方面那種有限的優勢，顯然被它對員工福祉以及機構本身可持續表現所造成的損害所超過。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"rely heavily on","chinese":"非常依賴"},{"english":"digital communication","chinese":"數碼通訊"},{"english":"expect staff to remain reachable","chinese":"期望員工保持可聯絡"},{"english":"remain reachable","chinese":"保持可聯絡"},{"english":"annual leave","chinese":"年假"},{"english":"this arrangement","chinese":"這種安排"},{"english":"commercially sensible","chinese":"在商業上合理"},{"english":"has more advantages than disadvantages","chinese":"利多於弊"},{"english":"gain in responsiveness","chinese":"反應速度上的收益"},{"english":"be outweighed by","chinese":"被……超過；不及……重要"},{"english":"employees' recovery","chinese":"員工恢復狀態"},{"english":"morale","chinese":"士氣"},{"english":"long-term effectiveness","chinese":"長遠成效"},{"english":"admittedly","chinese":"誠然"},{"english":"one clear benefit to","chinese":"……的一個明顯好處"},{"english":"a serious problem arises unexpectedly","chinese":"嚴重問題突然出現"},{"english":"immediate contact with","chinese":"與……即時聯絡"},{"english":"the relevant employee","chinese":"相關員工"},{"english":"prevent a minor disruption from","chinese":"防止小阻礙……"},{"english":"developing into a major one","chinese":"發展成重大問題"},{"english":"a delayed shipment","chinese":"延誤的貨運"},{"english":"a software failure","chinese":"軟件故障"},{"english":"an urgent client request","chinese":"緊急客戶要求"},{"english":"be resolved quickly","chinese":"被迅速解決"},{"english":"clarify information","chinese":"澄清資料"},{"english":"make a decision","chinese":"作出決定"},{"english":"reach the technician","chinese":"聯絡到技術員"},{"english":"booking system","chinese":"預訂系統"},{"english":"during a holiday","chinese":"在假期期間"},{"english":"dozens of reservations","chinese":"幾十個預訂"},{"english":"customer complaints","chinese":"顧客投訴"},{"english":"genuinely urgent situations","chinese":"真正緊急的情況"},{"english":"constant availability","chinese":"長期可聯絡狀態"},{"english":"protect a company's operations","chinese":"保障公司營運"},{"english":"far more significant","chinese":"重要得多"},{"english":"at any moment","chinese":"在任何時候"},{"english":"disconnect mentally from work","chinese":"在心理上脫離工作"},{"english":"officially resting","chinese":"正式休息中"},{"english":"attention remains partly fixed on","chinese":"注意力仍部分集中在……"},{"english":"possible messages or calls","chinese":"可能出現的訊息或電話"},{"english":"serve their essential purpose","chinese":"發揮其基本作用"},{"english":"restoring energy","chinese":"恢復精力"},{"english":"relieving stress","chinese":"紓緩壓力"},{"english":"return feeling drained rather than refreshed","chinese":"回來時感到疲憊而不是精神恢復"},{"english":"this culture","chinese":"這種文化"},{"english":"damages commitment to","chinese":"損害對……的投入感"},{"english":"private time","chinese":"私人時間"},{"english":"repeatedly interrupted","chinese":"被反覆打斷"},{"english":"personal boundaries","chinese":"個人界線"},{"english":"not respected","chinese":"不被尊重"},{"english":"breeds resentment","chinese":"滋生怨氣"},{"english":"reduces loyalty","chinese":"降低忠誠度"},{"english":"cooperate at first","chinese":"起初配合"},{"english":"repeated intrusion","chinese":"反覆侵擾"},{"english":"eventually lead to","chinese":"最終導致"},{"english":"burnout","chinese":"職業倦怠"},{"english":"resignation","chinese":"辭職"},{"english":"higher recruitment costs","chinese":"更高招聘成本"},{"english":"weaker team stability","chinese":"較弱的團隊穩定性"},{"english":"lower productivity","chinese":"較低生產力"},{"english":"deal with emergencies","chinese":"處理緊急情況"},{"english":"a negative development overall","chinese":"整體而言是負面發展"},{"english":"limited operational advantage","chinese":"有限的營運好處"},{"english":"decisively outweighed by","chinese":"明顯被……超過"},{"english":"damage done to","chinese":"對……造成的傷害"},{"english":"workers' wellbeing","chinese":"員工身心健康"},{"english":"sustainable performance","chinese":"可持續表現"},{"english":"the organisation itself","chinese":"機構本身"}]},"model-essay-27-ielts-direct-question":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-27-ielts-direct-question","essayKey":"direct-question:27","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-27-ielts-direct-question","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/direct-question/EdmundBd9Dir-Q27","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"As life expectancy rises, care for people in their nineties is becoming a pressing social issue. Although family affection is valuable, I believe the responsibility for elderly care should rest with the government rather than with individual families, because old age now requires organised medical, financial, and social support that private households often cannot provide.","chinese":"隨著預期壽命上升，照顧九十多歲的人正成為一個迫切的社會問題。 儘管家庭親情很有價值，我認為照顧長者的責任應該落在政府身上，而不是個別家庭身上，因為如今的老年階段需要有組織的醫療、財政和社會支援，而私人家庭往往無法提供這些支援。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"The first reason is that modern elderly care is far too complex to be left to relatives. A person in their nineties may need daily nursing, medicine management, home modifications, physiotherapy, and transport to hospitals. Most adult children are already juggling jobs, mortgages, and their own children, so expecting them to deliver professional care can damage both the older person’s health and the carer’s livelihood. For instance, if an elderly woman develops dementia, goodwill from her family cannot replace trained carers, safe facilities, and regular medical supervision. Government-funded services, by contrast, can provide a reliable safety net through hospitals, community nurses, subsidised residential homes, and pensions.","chinese":"第一個原因是，現代長者照護太複雜，不能只交給親屬負責。 一位九十多歲的長者可能需要日常護理、藥物管理、家居改裝、物理治療，以及往返醫院的交通安排。 大多數成年子女已經要同時應付工作、按揭和自己的孩子，因此期望他們提供專業照護，可能同時損害長者的健康和照顧者的生計。 例如，如果一位年長女性患上認知障礙症，家人的善意並不能取代受過訓練的照顧者、安全的設施和定期的醫療監督。 相比之下，由政府資助的服務可以透過醫院、社區護士、受資助的安老院舍和退休金，提供一張可靠的安全網。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"Another reason is fairness. If care depends mainly on family, elderly people with no children, distant relatives, or poor households are punished for circumstances beyond their control, while those from wealthier families are more likely to age with dignity. A government system can set minimum standards, inspect care homes, offer home-care subsidies, and protect older people from neglect or financial exploitation. For example, a widower whose children live overseas should still be able to receive basic support, safe accommodation, and medical attention. In this sense, elderly care is not merely a private family matter; it is part of the social contract. People who have contributed to society throughout their working lives should not be abandoned when frailty arrives.","chinese":"另一個原因是公平。 如果照護主要依賴家庭，那麼沒有子女、親屬疏遠或家境貧困的長者，便會因一些他們無法控制的情況而受到懲罰；相反，來自較富裕家庭的人則更有可能有尊嚴地老去。 政府制度可以設立最低標準、巡查安老院舍、提供家居照護津貼，並保護長者免受忽視或財務剝削。 例如，一位子女住在海外的鰥夫，仍然應該能夠獲得基本支援、安全住所和醫療照顧。 從這個意義上說，長者照護不僅僅是私人家庭事務；它是社會契約的一部分。 那些在整個工作生涯中為社會作出貢獻的人，不應該在身體變得虛弱時被遺棄。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, families should remain emotionally involved, but the responsibility for caring for elderly citizens should belong to the government. Family love can provide warmth, but only public systems can provide consistent, regulated, and equitable care.","chinese":"總結來說，家庭應該繼續在情感上參與其中，但照顧年長公民的責任應該屬於政府。 家庭的愛可以提供溫暖，但只有公共制度才能提供持續、受監管且公平的照護。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"life expectancy rises","chinese":"預期壽命上升"},{"english":"people in their nineties","chinese":"九十多歲人士"},{"english":"a pressing social issue","chinese":"迫切的社會議題"},{"english":"family affection","chinese":"家庭感情"},{"english":"the responsibility for elderly care","chinese":"照顧長者的責任"},{"english":"should rest with","chinese":"應由……承擔"},{"english":"rather than with","chinese":"而不是由……"},{"english":"individual families","chinese":"個別家庭"},{"english":"old age","chinese":"老年階段"},{"english":"organised medical, financial, and social support","chinese":"有組織的醫療、財務和社會支援"},{"english":"private households","chinese":"私人家庭"},{"english":"the first reason","chinese":"第一個原因"},{"english":"modern elderly care","chinese":"現代長者照顧"},{"english":"far too complex to","chinese":"太複雜以致不能"},{"english":"be left to relatives","chinese":"留給親屬負責"},{"english":"daily nursing","chinese":"日常護理"},{"english":"medicine management","chinese":"藥物管理"},{"english":"home modifications","chinese":"家居改裝"},{"english":"physiotherapy","chinese":"物理治療"},{"english":"transport to hospitals","chinese":"前往醫院的交通安排"},{"english":"adult children","chinese":"成年子女"},{"english":"juggling jobs, mortgages, and their own children","chinese":"同時兼顧工作、按揭和自己的子女"},{"english":"expecting them to","chinese":"期望他們去"},{"english":"deliver professional care","chinese":"提供專業照顧"},{"english":"damage both...and...","chinese":"同時損害……和……"},{"english":"the older person's health","chinese":"長者的健康"},{"english":"the carer's livelihood","chinese":"照顧者的生計"},{"english":"develops dementia","chinese":"患上認知障礙症"},{"english":"goodwill from her family","chinese":"家人的善意"},{"english":"cannot replace","chinese":"不能取代"},{"english":"trained carers","chinese":"受過訓練的照顧者"},{"english":"safe facilities","chinese":"安全設施"},{"english":"regular medical supervision","chinese":"定期醫療監察"},{"english":"government-funded services","chinese":"政府資助服務"},{"english":"by contrast","chinese":"相比之下"},{"english":"a reliable safety net","chinese":"可靠的安全網"},{"english":"community nurses","chinese":"社區護士"},{"english":"subsidised residential homes","chinese":"資助安老院舍"},{"english":"pensions","chinese":"退休金；養老金"},{"english":"another reason is fairness","chinese":"另一個原因是公平"},{"english":"depends mainly on","chinese":"主要取決於"},{"english":"distant relatives","chinese":"關係疏遠的親屬"},{"english":"poor households","chinese":"貧困家庭"},{"english":"be punished for","chinese":"因……而受懲罰"},{"english":"circumstances beyond their control","chinese":"他們無法控制的情況"},{"english":"wealthier families","chinese":"較富裕的家庭"},{"english":"more likely to","chinese":"更有可能"},{"english":"age with dignity","chinese":"有尊嚴地老去"},{"english":"government system","chinese":"政府制度"},{"english":"set minimum standards","chinese":"訂立最低標準"},{"english":"inspect care homes","chinese":"巡查護老院"},{"english":"home-care subsidies","chinese":"家居照顧津貼"},{"english":"protect older people from","chinese":"保護長者免受……影響"},{"english":"neglect","chinese":"忽視；疏忽照顧"},{"english":"financial exploitation","chinese":"財務剝削"},{"english":"a widower","chinese":"鰥夫"},{"english":"live overseas","chinese":"居於海外"},{"english":"basic support","chinese":"基本支援"},{"english":"safe accommodation","chinese":"安全住所"},{"english":"medical attention","chinese":"醫療照顧"},{"english":"In this sense","chinese":"從這個意義上說"},{"english":"not merely a private family matter","chinese":"不只是私人家庭事務"},{"english":"the social contract","chinese":"社會契約"},{"english":"contributed to society","chinese":"為社會作出貢獻"},{"english":"throughout their working lives","chinese":"在整個工作生涯中"},{"english":"should not be abandoned","chinese":"不應被遺棄"},{"english":"frailty arrives","chinese":"身體衰弱來臨"},{"english":"remain emotionally involved","chinese":"保持情感上的參與"},{"english":"caring for elderly citizens","chinese":"照顧長者市民"},{"english":"should belong to","chinese":"應屬於"},{"english":"family love","chinese":"家庭關愛"},{"english":"provide warmth","chinese":"提供溫暖"},{"english":"public systems","chinese":"公共制度"},{"english":"consistent, regulated, and equitable care","chinese":"持續、受規管而公平的照顧"}]},"model-essay-27-ielts-discuss-both-views":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-27-ielts-discuss-both-views","essayKey":"discuss-both-views:27","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-27-ielts-discuss-both-views","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/discuss-both-views-your-opinion/EdmundBd9ExpBth-Q27","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"Corporate sponsorship has become a familiar part of modern sport, from logos on team shirts to branded stadiums and televised tournaments. While some people worry that this turns sport into a marketing tool, I firmly believe that company sponsorship is a positive development because it gives athletes and sporting organisations the financial support they need.","chinese":"企業贊助已成為現代體育中常見的一部分，從球隊球衣上的標誌，到冠名體育場和電視轉播賽事皆是如此。 雖然有些人擔心這會把體育變成一種行銷工具， 我堅定認為，公司贊助是一種正面的發展，因為它為運動員和體育組織提供了他們所需要的財政支持。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"There are clear reasons why many people welcome this practice. Sport is expensive to run, especially when clubs have to pay for coaching, equipment, travel, medical support and safe facilities. Without commercial backing, many smaller teams and young athletes would struggle to train properly, let alone compete at a high level. For example, a local basketball club that receives money from a company may be able to buy better equipment, reduce membership fees and send its players to regional competitions. In this way, sponsorship does not merely advertise a brand; it can open the door to wider participation and better performance.","chinese":"人們歡迎這種做法有明顯的原因。 體育運作成本高昂，尤其是當俱樂部需要支付教練、設備、交通、醫療支援和安全設施的費用時。 如果沒有商業支持，許多較小型的隊伍和年輕運動員將難以進行適當訓練，更不用說在高水平比賽中競爭。 例如，一間獲得公司資助的本地籃球俱樂部，可能便能購買更好的設備、降低會員費，並派球員參加地區比賽。 這樣一來，贊助並不只是為品牌做廣告；它還能為更廣泛的參與和更好的表現打開大門"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"However, the disadvantages should not be ignored. When sponsorship becomes too dominant, sport can lose some of its original spirit. A team’s identity may be buried under logos, and young fans may start to associate athletic success with products that are not always healthy or appropriate. This is particularly concerning when fast food, sugary drinks or gambling companies use popular athletes as a shortcut into the minds of children. In addition, clubs may feel pressure to please sponsors instead of making decisions based purely on sporting values. Even so, these problems are best solved through sensible rules rather than by rejecting sponsorship altogether.","chinese":"然而，這種做法的缺點也不應被忽視。 當贊助變得過於主導時，體育可能會失去一部分原本的精神。 一支隊伍的身份可能會被各種標誌掩蓋，而年輕球迷也可能開始把運動成就與一些並不總是健康或合適的產品聯繫起來。 當快餐、含糖飲品或博彩公司利用受歡迎的運動員作為進入兒童心智的捷徑時，這一點尤其令人擔憂。 此外，俱樂部可能會感到壓力，要取悅贊助商，而不是純粹根據體育價值作出決定。 即便如此，這些問題最好透過合理規則來解決，而不是完全拒絕贊助。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, although corporate sponsorship can commercialise sport and create ethical concerns, I believe its advantages are far greater. If advertising is regulated carefully, sponsorship can act as vital fuel for sport, helping athletes, clubs and communities grow.","chinese":"總結來說，儘管企業贊助可能使體育商業化，並帶來道德方面的疑慮，我認為它的優點遠遠更大。 如果廣告受到仔細規管，贊助便可以成為體育的重要燃料，幫助運動員、俱樂部和社區成長。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"corporate sponsorship","chinese":"企業贊助"},{"english":"a familiar part of","chinese":"……中常見的一部分"},{"english":"modern sport","chinese":"現代體育"},{"english":"logos on team shirts","chinese":"球衣上的標誌"},{"english":"branded stadiums","chinese":"品牌冠名球場"},{"english":"televised tournaments","chinese":"電視轉播賽事"},{"english":"turn sport into","chinese":"將體育變成"},{"english":"a marketing tool","chinese":"市場推廣工具"},{"english":"firmly believe that","chinese":"堅信"},{"english":"company sponsorship","chinese":"公司贊助"},{"english":"a positive development","chinese":"正面發展"},{"english":"sporting organisations","chinese":"體育組織"},{"english":"financial support","chinese":"財政支持"},{"english":"there are clear reasons why","chinese":"有明確原因解釋為何"},{"english":"welcome this practice","chinese":"歡迎這種做法"},{"english":"expensive to run","chinese":"營運成本高"},{"english":"have to pay for","chinese":"需要支付"},{"english":"medical support","chinese":"醫療支援"},{"english":"safe facilities","chinese":"安全設施"},{"english":"commercial backing","chinese":"商業支持"},{"english":"smaller teams","chinese":"較小型的隊伍"},{"english":"young athletes","chinese":"年輕運動員"},{"english":"struggle to train properly","chinese":"難以接受適當訓練"},{"english":"let alone","chinese":"更不用說"},{"english":"compete at a high level","chinese":"參與高水平比賽"},{"english":"a local basketball club","chinese":"本地籃球會"},{"english":"receive money from","chinese":"從……獲得資金"},{"english":"buy better equipment","chinese":"購買更好的裝備"},{"english":"reduce membership fees","chinese":"降低會員費"},{"english":"send its players to","chinese":"派其球員參加"},{"english":"regional competitions","chinese":"區域賽事"},{"english":"in this way","chinese":"這樣一來"},{"english":"does not merely advertise","chinese":"不只是宣傳"},{"english":"advertise a brand","chinese":"宣傳品牌"},{"english":"open the door to","chinese":"為……打開大門"},{"english":"wider participation","chinese":"更廣泛參與"},{"english":"better performance","chinese":"更佳表現"},{"english":"the disadvantages should not be ignored","chinese":"不應忽視缺點"},{"english":"become too dominant","chinese":"變得過於主導"},{"english":"lose some of its original spirit","chinese":"失去部分原本精神"},{"english":"a team's identity","chinese":"隊伍身份"},{"english":"be buried under","chinese":"被……掩蓋"},{"english":"young fans","chinese":"年輕粉絲"},{"english":"associate athletic success with","chinese":"將運動成功與……聯繫起來"},{"english":"athletic success","chinese":"運動成就"},{"english":"not always healthy or appropriate","chinese":"不一定健康或合適"},{"english":"particularly concerning","chinese":"尤其令人擔心"},{"english":"fast food","chinese":"快餐"},{"english":"sugary drinks","chinese":"高糖飲品"},{"english":"gambling companies","chinese":"博彩公司"},{"english":"popular athletes","chinese":"受歡迎的運動員"},{"english":"as a shortcut into","chinese":"作為進入……的捷徑"},{"english":"the minds of children","chinese":"兒童的思想"},{"english":"in addition","chinese":"此外"},{"english":"feel pressure to","chinese":"感到有壓力去"},{"english":"please sponsors","chinese":"取悅贊助商"},{"english":"instead of making decisions based purely on","chinese":"而不是純粹基於……作決定"},{"english":"sporting values","chinese":"體育價值"},{"english":"even so","chinese":"即使如此"},{"english":"be best solved through","chinese":"最好透過……解決"},{"english":"sensible rules","chinese":"合理規則"},{"english":"rather than by rejecting","chinese":"而不是透過拒絕"},{"english":"rejecting sponsorship altogether","chinese":"完全拒絕贊助"},{"english":"commercialise sport","chinese":"令體育商業化"},{"english":"create ethical concerns","chinese":"引起道德憂慮"},{"english":"advantages are far greater","chinese":"優點大得多"},{"english":"be regulated carefully","chinese":"被審慎監管"},{"english":"act as vital fuel for","chinese":"作為……的重要燃料"},{"english":"helping athletes, clubs and communities grow","chinese":"幫助運動員、球會和社區成長"}]},"model-essay-27-ielts-opinion":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-27-ielts-opinion","essayKey":"opinion:27","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-27-ielts-opinion","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/opinions/EdmundBd9OP-Q27","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"Crime prevention and criminal investigation have been transformed by modern technology. I strongly agree that crime rates are generally lower than in the past because today’s digital tools make offences harder to commit and much easier to solve.","chinese":"犯罪預防和刑事調查已被現代科技徹底改變。 我強烈同意，犯罪率整體上比過去更低，因為現今的數位工具令犯罪更難實施，也令破案容易得多。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"The first reason is that technology can stop many crimes before they happen. In the past, criminals often acted with little fear of being identified, especially in quiet streets, shops, car parks, or residential areas. Today, however, surveillance cameras, alarm systems, biometric locks, and mobile security apps have changed that completely. A thief who sees cameras outside a building or knows that an alarm will immediately alert the owner is far less likely to take the risk. For example, many modern shops now use CCTV and electronic tags, so stealing goods is no longer as simple as walking out unnoticed. This constant possibility of being recorded creates a powerful deterrent, which reduces everyday crimes such as theft, vandalism, and burglary.","chinese":"第一個原因是，科技可以在許多罪案發生之前便加以阻止。 在過去，罪犯行事時往往不太害怕被識別出來，尤其是在安靜的街道、商店、停車場或住宅區。 然而，今天監控攝影機、警報系統、生物識別門鎖和手機保安應用程式已完全改變了這種情況。 一個小偷如果看到建築物外有攝影機，或者知道警報會立即通知業主，就遠不太可能冒這個風險。 例如，許多現代商店現在都使用閉路電視和電子標籤，因此偷取貨物已不再像在無人察覺下走出去那麼簡單。 這種隨時可能被錄下來的可能性形成了強大的阻嚇作用，從而減少盜竊、破壞公物和入屋爆竊等日常罪案。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"Technology also helps the police solve crimes more quickly and accurately. Modern investigations no longer depend only on eyewitnesses, who may forget details or give unreliable accounts. Instead, officers can use DNA testing, fingerprint databases, phone records, GPS tracking, and digital footprints to identify suspects. For instance, if someone steals a car, the vehicle may be tracked through a GPS system, while nearby cameras can show where the thief went. Similarly, online fraudsters often leave behind bank records, IP addresses, or message histories. When criminals know that their actions can leave a trail, they are less willing to offend in the first place. This means technology not only catches offenders after a crime, but also discourages others from copying them.","chinese":"科技也幫助警方更快速、更準確地偵破罪案。 現代調查不再只依賴目擊者，因為他們可能會忘記細節，或者提供不可靠的陳述。 相反，執法人員可以使用DNA測試、指紋資料庫、電話紀錄、GPS追蹤和數位足跡來識別疑犯。 例如，如果有人偷車，該車輛可能可以透過GPS系統被追蹤，而附近的攝影機也可以顯示小偷去了哪裡。 同樣地，網上騙徒往往會留下銀行紀錄、IP地址或訊息紀錄。 當罪犯知道自己的行為可能會留下痕跡時，他們一開始便會較不願意犯罪。 這意味著科技不但能在罪案發生後捉拿犯罪者，也能阻止其他人模仿他們。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, I fully agree that advanced technology has helped reduce crime. By preventing offences and giving the police stronger evidence, it has made crime a much riskier and less attractive choice.","chinese":"總結來說，我完全同意先進科技已經幫助減少犯罪 透過預防罪案並為警方提供更有力的證據，科技已使犯罪成為一個風險更高、吸引力更低的選擇"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"crime prevention","chinese":"犯罪預防"},{"english":"criminal investigation","chinese":"刑事調查"},{"english":"be transformed by","chinese":"被……徹底改變"},{"english":"modern technology","chinese":"現代科技"},{"english":"crime rates","chinese":"罪案率"},{"english":"generally lower than","chinese":"一般比……低"},{"english":"in the past","chinese":"在過去"},{"english":"digital tools","chinese":"數碼工具"},{"english":"offences","chinese":"罪行"},{"english":"harder to commit","chinese":"更難犯下"},{"english":"easier to solve","chinese":"更容易偵破"},{"english":"stop many crimes before they happen","chinese":"在罪案發生前阻止它們"},{"english":"acted with little fear of","chinese":"幾乎不害怕……地行事"},{"english":"being identified","chinese":"被識別身份"},{"english":"quiet streets","chinese":"僻靜街道"},{"english":"car parks","chinese":"停車場"},{"english":"residential areas","chinese":"住宅區"},{"english":"surveillance cameras","chinese":"監控攝影機"},{"english":"alarm systems","chinese":"警報系統"},{"english":"biometric locks","chinese":"生物識別鎖"},{"english":"mobile security apps","chinese":"手機保安應用程式"},{"english":"alert the owner","chinese":"通知物主"},{"english":"far less likely to","chinese":"可能性低得多"},{"english":"take the risk","chinese":"冒險"},{"english":"CCTV","chinese":"閉路電視"},{"english":"electronic tags","chinese":"電子防盜標籤"},{"english":"stealing goods","chinese":"偷取貨物"},{"english":"walking out unnoticed","chinese":"未被察覺地走出去"},{"english":"constant possibility of","chinese":"……的持續可能性"},{"english":"being recorded","chinese":"被錄影"},{"english":"powerful deterrent","chinese":"強大的阻嚇因素"},{"english":"everyday crimes","chinese":"日常罪案"},{"english":"theft","chinese":"盜竊"},{"english":"vandalism","chinese":"破壞公物"},{"english":"burglary","chinese":"入屋爆竊"},{"english":"solve crimes more quickly and accurately","chinese":"更快速和準確地偵破罪案"},{"english":"modern investigations","chinese":"現代調查"},{"english":"no longer depend only on","chinese":"不再只依賴……"},{"english":"eyewitnesses","chinese":"目擊者"},{"english":"forget details","chinese":"忘記細節"},{"english":"unreliable accounts","chinese":"不可靠的說法"},{"english":"DNA testing","chinese":"DNA 測試"},{"english":"fingerprint databases","chinese":"指紋數據庫"},{"english":"phone records","chinese":"電話紀錄"},{"english":"GPS tracking","chinese":"GPS 追蹤"},{"english":"digital footprints","chinese":"數碼足跡"},{"english":"identify suspects","chinese":"識別疑犯"},{"english":"steals a car","chinese":"偷車"},{"english":"be tracked through","chinese":"透過……被追蹤"},{"english":"GPS system","chinese":"GPS 系統"},{"english":"nearby cameras","chinese":"附近的攝影機"},{"english":"where the thief went","chinese":"小偷去了哪裏"},{"english":"online fraudsters","chinese":"網上騙徒"},{"english":"leave behind","chinese":"留下"},{"english":"bank records","chinese":"銀行紀錄"},{"english":"IP addresses","chinese":"IP 地址"},{"english":"message histories","chinese":"訊息紀錄"},{"english":"leave a trail","chinese":"留下痕跡"},{"english":"less willing to offend","chinese":"較不願意犯罪"},{"english":"in the first place","chinese":"一開始；首先"},{"english":"catches offenders","chinese":"捉拿犯事者"},{"english":"discourages others from","chinese":"阻止其他人去……"},{"english":"copying them","chinese":"模仿他們"},{"english":"advanced technology","chinese":"先進科技"},{"english":"helped reduce crime","chinese":"幫助減少犯罪"},{"english":"preventing offences","chinese":"預防罪行"},{"english":"stronger evidence","chinese":"更有力證據"},{"english":"riskier and less attractive choice","chinese":"風險更高且吸引力較低的選擇"}]},"model-essay-28-ielts-advantage-disadvantage":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-28-ielts-advantage-disadvantage","essayKey":"advantage-disadvantage:28","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-28-ielts-advantage-disadvantage","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/advantage-and-disadvantage/EdmundBd9AdDisAd-Q28","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"As populations age and working lives lengthen, many firms are rethinking the composition of their workforce. Recruiting more older employees can certainly create challenges for a business, particularly in relation to labour costs and retraining. Nevertheless, the advantages are clearly greater, because older workers often enhance both the quality of decisions and the stability of the organisation.","chinese":"隨著人口老化，以及人們的工作年期不斷延長，許多公司都開始重新思考其勞動力的組成。 聘用更多年長員工，的確可能為企業帶來一些挑戰，尤其是在勞工成本和再培訓方面。 然而，這樣做的優點顯然更大，因為年長員工往往能提升決策的質素，以及整個組織的穩定性。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"The first major benefit is the depth of judgement that experienced staff can bring to a company. Having dealt with clients, deadlines and workplace problems for many years, older employees are often better at recognising risks before they become costly mistakes. A seasoned purchasing manager, for example, may detect signs that a supplier is unreliable and change vendors early, thereby preventing delays in production. Older recruits can also raise the performance of others, because their professional discipline and communication skills make them effective mentors. A veteran sales executive who coaches new hires in negotiation and client handling can shorten the adjustment period for an entire team. Consequently, the firm gains not only one capable employee, but also a more competent and resilient workforce.","chinese":"第一個主要優點，是有經驗的員工能為公司帶來更成熟、更有深度的判斷力。 由於多年來一直處理客戶、期限以及各種職場問題，年長員工往往更善於在風險演變成代價高昂的錯誤之前，及早察覺問題。 這代表他們能更早發現警號、及時採取預防措施，從而避免公司承受不必要的損失或運作上的混亂。 例如，一位資深採購經理可能會及早察覺某供應商不可靠的跡象，並提早更換供應商，從而防止生產延誤。 年長的新聘員工也能提升其他同事的表現，因為他們的專業紀律與溝通能力，使他們成為有效的指導者。 當較年輕的員工得到資深同事的指導時，他們通常能更快適應工作、避免常見錯誤，並在更短時間內達到工作成效。 例如，一位資深銷售主管若指導新員工如何談判及處理客戶關係，便能縮短整個團隊的適應期。 因此，公司得到的不只是單一一位能幹的員工，而是一支更有能力、也更有韌性的團隊。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"There are, however, some disadvantages. One is that older recruits may command higher salaries and better benefits, which can place pressure on payroll budgets, especially in smaller firms. If a start-up hires several highly experienced managers at once, its wage bill may rise faster than its revenue. Another drawback is that, in companies undergoing rapid digital change, some older employees may initially require more support when adapting to newly introduced platforms. For instance, a business that replaces paper-based systems with cloud software may need to provide extra training before output returns to normal. Even so, these are managerial challenges rather than compelling reasons to avoid older applicants.","chinese":"然而，這樣做也確實存在一些缺點。 其中一個缺點是，年長員工往往要求較高薪酬和較佳福利，這可能會對薪酬預算造成壓力，尤其是對小型企業而言。 如果人力成本上升得太快，公司便可能較難把資金投放於擴張、科技或其他營運需要之上。 例如，一間初創公司若一下子聘請多位高經驗的經理，其薪資開支的增長速度便可能快於收入增長。 另一個缺點是，在正經歷快速數碼轉型的公司中，一些年長員工在適應新引入的平台時，初期可能需要更多支援。 這可能會暫時拖慢工作流程、增加培訓需求，並使管理層需要投入更多時間，之後生產力才可恢復至原有水平。 例如，一間把紙本系統改為雲端軟件的公司，可能需要提供額外培訓，之後工作產出才會回復正常。 即使如此，這些仍只是管理上的挑戰，而不是足以令公司避免聘請年長求職者的有力理由。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, employing more older people can increase expenditure and create short-term training demands, but the benefits for companies are clearly greater. Their experience, reliability and positive influence on younger staff usually generate greater long-term value, particularly in roles that depend on judgement, trust and continuity. For this reason, more companies should be willing to recruit them.","chinese":"總括而言，聘用更多年長人士的確可能增加開支，並帶來短期培訓需求，但對公司來說，其優點顯然更大。 他們的經驗、可靠性，以及對年輕員工的正面影響，通常能帶來更高的長遠價值，尤其是在那些依賴判斷力、信任和持續性的職位中。 基於這一點，更多公司都應該更願意聘用年長員工。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"populations age","chinese":"人口老化"},{"english":"working lives lengthen","chinese":"工作年期延長"},{"english":"many firms","chinese":"許多公司"},{"english":"rethinking the composition of","chinese":"重新思考……的組成"},{"english":"workforce","chinese":"勞動力；員工隊伍"},{"english":"recruiting more older employees","chinese":"招聘更多年長員工"},{"english":"create challenges for","chinese":"為……帶來挑戰"},{"english":"particularly in relation to","chinese":"尤其與……有關"},{"english":"labour costs","chinese":"勞工成本"},{"english":"retraining","chinese":"再培訓"},{"english":"nevertheless","chinese":"然而"},{"english":"clearly greater","chinese":"明顯更大"},{"english":"enhance both...and...","chinese":"同時提升……和……"},{"english":"the quality of decisions","chinese":"決策質素"},{"english":"the stability of the organisation","chinese":"組織的穩定性"},{"english":"the first major benefit","chinese":"第一個主要好處"},{"english":"the depth of judgement","chinese":"深厚的判斷力"},{"english":"experienced staff","chinese":"經驗豐富的員工"},{"english":"bring to a company","chinese":"為公司帶來"},{"english":"having dealt with","chinese":"曾經處理過"},{"english":"deadlines","chinese":"截止期限"},{"english":"workplace problems","chinese":"工作場所問題"},{"english":"be better at recognising risks","chinese":"更善於識別風險"},{"english":"costly mistakes","chinese":"代價高昂的錯誤"},{"english":"a seasoned purchasing manager","chinese":"經驗老到的採購經理"},{"english":"detect signs that","chinese":"察覺……的跡象"},{"english":"a supplier is unreliable","chinese":"供應商不可靠"},{"english":"change vendors early","chinese":"及早更換供應商"},{"english":"thereby preventing","chinese":"從而防止"},{"english":"delays in production","chinese":"生產延誤"},{"english":"older recruits","chinese":"年長新聘員工"},{"english":"raise the performance of","chinese":"提升……的表現"},{"english":"professional discipline","chinese":"專業紀律"},{"english":"communication skills","chinese":"溝通技巧"},{"english":"effective mentors","chinese":"有效的導師"},{"english":"a veteran sales executive","chinese":"資深銷售主管"},{"english":"coaches new hires in","chinese":"指導新員工……"},{"english":"new hires","chinese":"新入職員工"},{"english":"negotiation","chinese":"談判"},{"english":"client handling","chinese":"客戶處理"},{"english":"shorten the adjustment period","chinese":"縮短適應期"},{"english":"an entire team","chinese":"整個團隊"},{"english":"consequently","chinese":"因此"},{"english":"capable employee","chinese":"有能力的員工"},{"english":"a more competent and resilient workforce","chinese":"更有能力和抗逆力的員工隊伍"},{"english":"there are, however, some disadvantages","chinese":"然而，也有一些缺點"},{"english":"command higher salaries","chinese":"要求較高薪酬"},{"english":"better benefits","chinese":"更好的福利"},{"english":"place pressure on","chinese":"對……造成壓力"},{"english":"payroll budgets","chinese":"薪酬預算"},{"english":"smaller firms","chinese":"較小型公司"},{"english":"at once","chinese":"一次過；同時；立即"},{"english":"wage bill","chinese":"工資開支"},{"english":"rise faster than","chinese":"增長得比……快"},{"english":"undergoing rapid digital change","chinese":"正經歷快速數碼轉型"},{"english":"initially require more support","chinese":"起初需要更多支援"},{"english":"adapting to","chinese":"適應"},{"english":"newly introduced platforms","chinese":"新引入的平台"},{"english":"paper-based systems","chinese":"紙本系統"},{"english":"cloud software","chinese":"雲端軟件"},{"english":"provide extra training","chinese":"提供額外培訓"},{"english":"output returns to normal","chinese":"產出回復正常"},{"english":"even so","chinese":"即使如此"},{"english":"managerial challenges","chinese":"管理上的挑戰"},{"english":"compelling reasons to avoid","chinese":"避免……的有力理由"},{"english":"older applicants","chinese":"年長申請者"},{"english":"employing more older people","chinese":"聘用更多年長人士"},{"english":"increase expenditure","chinese":"增加開支"},{"english":"short-term training demands","chinese":"短期培訓需求"},{"english":"reliability","chinese":"可靠性"},{"english":"positive influence on","chinese":"對……的正面影響"},{"english":"generate greater long-term value","chinese":"創造更大的長遠價值"},{"english":"roles that depend on","chinese":"依賴……的職位"},{"english":"judgement, trust and continuity","chinese":"判斷力、信任和延續性"},{"english":"be willing to recruit","chinese":"願意招聘"}]},"model-essay-28-ielts-direct-question":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-28-ielts-direct-question","essayKey":"direct-question:28","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-28-ielts-direct-question","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/direct-question/EdmundBd9Dir-Q28","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"In modern societies, governments often try to influence how citizens eat, travel, work and spend their leisure time. While public authorities have a legitimate duty to provide information and protect citizens from direct harm, lifestyle choices should ultimately be made by individuals themselves. This essay will argue that personal autonomy and practical effectiveness make individual decision-making the better approach.","chinese":"在現代社會中，政府經常試圖影響公民如何飲食、出行、工作，以及度過休閒時間。 雖然公共當局有正當責任提供資訊，並保護公民免受直接傷害，但生活方式的選擇最終應由個人自己作出。 本文將論證，個人自主和實際有效性使個人自行決策成為更好的做法。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"The strongest reason is that lifestyle is closely tied to personal freedom, identity and dignity. People differ widely in their values, health conditions, incomes, family duties and cultural habits, so a single government standard is unlikely to suit everyone. If the state decides how citizens should live, ordinary preferences can quickly be treated as social problems, and adults may be reduced to passive subjects rather than responsible human beings. For example, a diet that is sensible for a young athlete may be unsuitable for an elderly diabetic, while a work routine that suits one family may damage another. When lifestyle decisions are made by individuals, people can adapt general advice to their own circumstances instead of being trapped in a one-size-fits-all system.","chinese":"最有力的原因是，生活方式與個人自由、身份認同和尊嚴密切相關。 人們在價值觀、健康狀況、收入、家庭責任和文化習慣方面差異很大，因此單一的政府標準不太可能適合所有人。 如果國家決定公民應該如何生活，普通的個人偏好很快就可能被視為社會問題，而成年人也可能被降低為被動服從的對象，而不是有責任感的人。 例如，對年輕運動員來說合理的飲食，可能並不適合一位年長的糖尿病患者；而適合某個家庭的工作安排，也可能傷害另一個家庭。 當生活方式的決定由個人作出時，人們便能根據自己的情況調整一般性的建議，而不是被困在一套一體適用的制度之中。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"Another important point is that personal choice is usually more effective than official control. Healthy behaviour rarely lasts when it is imposed from above; it becomes sustainable when people understand the reason for it and choose it for themselves. A government may ban certain habits or dictate certain routines, but such pressure can create resentment, superficial compliance and even resistance. By contrast, policies such as clear food labels, public health education, safe parks and affordable sports facilities help people make wiser choices without taking ownership away from them. In this sense, the state should light the path, not drag citizens along it.","chinese":"另一個重要觀點是，個人選擇通常比官方控制更有效。 當健康行為是由上而下強加時，它很少能夠持久；當人們理解其原因並自行選擇時，它才會變得可持續。 政府也許可以禁止某些習慣，或規定某些日常安排，但這種壓力可能會引起怨氣、表面服從，甚至反抗。 相比之下，清晰的食品標籤、公共健康教育、安全的公園和價格合理的運動設施等政策，能幫助人們作出更明智的選擇，而不會剝奪他們對自己生活的主導權。 從這個意義上說，國家應該照亮道路，而不是拖著公民沿路前行。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, people should make their own lifestyle decisions. Governments should inform, warn and support, but the final choice about how to live must remain with the individual.","chinese":"總結來說，人們應該自行作出自己的生活方式決定。 政府應該提供資訊、作出提醒並給予支援，但關於如何生活的最終選擇，必須留在個人手中。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"modern societies","chinese":"現代社會"},{"english":"try to influence","chinese":"嘗試影響"},{"english":"how citizens eat, travel, work and spend their leisure time","chinese":"市民如何飲食、出行、工作和消閒"},{"english":"public authorities","chinese":"公共機關"},{"english":"a legitimate duty to","chinese":"合法而正當的責任去"},{"english":"provide information","chinese":"提供資料"},{"english":"protect citizens from","chinese":"保護市民免受……影響"},{"english":"direct harm","chinese":"直接傷害"},{"english":"lifestyle choices","chinese":"生活方式選擇"},{"english":"ultimately","chinese":"最終"},{"english":"be made by individuals themselves","chinese":"由個人自己作出"},{"english":"personal autonomy","chinese":"個人自主"},{"english":"practical effectiveness","chinese":"實際成效"},{"english":"individual decision-making","chinese":"個人決策"},{"english":"the better approach","chinese":"更好的方法"},{"english":"the strongest reason","chinese":"最有力的原因"},{"english":"closely tied to","chinese":"與……密切相關"},{"english":"personal freedom","chinese":"個人自由"},{"english":"identity and dignity","chinese":"身份認同和尊嚴"},{"english":"differ widely in","chinese":"在……方面有很大差異"},{"english":"values","chinese":"價值觀"},{"english":"health conditions","chinese":"健康狀況"},{"english":"family duties","chinese":"家庭責任"},{"english":"cultural habits","chinese":"文化習慣"},{"english":"a single government standard","chinese":"單一政府標準"},{"english":"unlikely to suit everyone","chinese":"不太可能適合所有人"},{"english":"the state decides","chinese":"國家決定"},{"english":"ordinary preferences","chinese":"普通個人偏好"},{"english":"be treated as social problems","chinese":"被視為社會問題"},{"english":"be reduced to","chinese":"被貶低為"},{"english":"passive subjects","chinese":"被動的受管對象"},{"english":"responsible human beings","chinese":"負責任的人"},{"english":"a diet that is sensible for","chinese":"對……合理的飲食"},{"english":"young athlete","chinese":"年輕運動員"},{"english":"unsuitable for","chinese":"不適合"},{"english":"elderly diabetic","chinese":"患糖尿病的長者"},{"english":"work routine","chinese":"工作規律"},{"english":"suits one family","chinese":"適合一個家庭"},{"english":"damage another","chinese":"損害另一個"},{"english":"adapt general advice to","chinese":"按照……調整一般建議"},{"english":"own circumstances","chinese":"自身情況"},{"english":"instead of being trapped in","chinese":"而不是被困在"},{"english":"a one-size-fits-all system","chinese":"一刀切制度"},{"english":"personal choice","chinese":"個人選擇"},{"english":"more effective than","chinese":"比……更有效"},{"english":"official control","chinese":"官方控制"},{"english":"healthy behaviour","chinese":"健康行為"},{"english":"rarely lasts","chinese":"很少能持久"},{"english":"be imposed from above","chinese":"由上而下強加"},{"english":"becomes sustainable","chinese":"變得可持續"},{"english":"understand the reason for","chinese":"明白……的原因"},{"english":"choose it for themselves","chinese":"自己選擇它"},{"english":"ban certain habits","chinese":"禁止某些習慣"},{"english":"dictate certain routines","chinese":"規定某些日常安排"},{"english":"such pressure","chinese":"這種壓力"},{"english":"create resentment","chinese":"造成怨氣"},{"english":"superficial compliance","chinese":"表面服從"},{"english":"resistance","chinese":"抗拒"},{"english":"By contrast","chinese":"相比之下"},{"english":"clear food labels","chinese":"清晰食物標籤"},{"english":"public health education","chinese":"公共健康教育"},{"english":"safe parks","chinese":"安全公園"},{"english":"affordable sports facilities","chinese":"負擔得起的運動設施"},{"english":"make wiser choices","chinese":"作出更明智的選擇"},{"english":"without taking ownership away from","chinese":"不奪走……的自主權"},{"english":"taking ownership","chinese":"承擔自主責任"},{"english":"light the path","chinese":"照亮道路"},{"english":"drag citizens along it","chinese":"拖着市民沿路走"},{"english":"make their own lifestyle decisions","chinese":"作出自己的生活方式決定"},{"english":"inform, warn and support","chinese":"提供資訊、警告和支援"},{"english":"the final choice about","chinese":"關於……的最終選擇"},{"english":"remain with the individual","chinese":"留給個人"}]},"model-essay-28-ielts-discuss-both-views":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-28-ielts-discuss-both-views","essayKey":"discuss-both-views:28","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-28-ielts-discuss-both-views","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/discuss-both-views-your-opinion/EdmundBd9ExpBth-Q28","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"Photographs have become a powerful part of modern journalism, with newspapers and television channels using images to make stories more immediate and persuasive. While some people believe that photographs cannot always be trusted, others argue that they provide undeniable evidence of what has happened. I will discuss both views, but I firmly believe that photographs should be treated as supporting evidence rather than irrefutable proof.","chinese":"照片已經成為現代新聞業中一個強而有力的部分，報紙和電視頻道都會使用圖像，使新聞故事更即時、更具說服力。 雖然有些人認為照片並不總是值得信任，但另一些人則認為照片提供了事情已經發生的不可否認的證據。 我將討論雙方觀點，但我堅定地認為，照片應被視為輔助證據，而不是無可反駁的證明"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"Those who distrust photographs have strong reasons for doing so. A picture may appear objective, but it can easily mislead the public if it is edited, cropped, staged, or presented without context. For example, a photograph of an angry protester might suggest violence, even if the wider scene was mostly peaceful. In this way, the camera does not always tell the whole story; it only captures one frozen moment. Moreover, with modern digital tools, images can be altered so convincingly that ordinary readers may struggle to separate fact from manipulation. As a result, relying on photographs alone can cause people to form quick but inaccurate judgments.","chinese":"那些不信任照片的人有充分理由這樣做。 一張照片可能看起來客觀，但如果它被編輯、裁剪、擺拍，或在沒有背景資料的情況下呈現，它便很容易誤導公眾。 例如，一張憤怒示威者的照片可能暗示暴力，即使更廣闊的現場其實大部分是和平的。 如此一來，相機並不總是講述完整的故事；它只是捕捉了一個凝固的瞬間。 此外，隨著現代數位工具的發展，圖像可以被修改得非常逼真，以至於普通讀者可能難以分辨事實與操控。 結果是，單靠照片可能會使人們迅速形成判斷，但這些判斷卻可能並不準確。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"On the other hand, many people regard photographs as extremely convincing because they show events in a direct and visible way. Unlike a written report, which depends heavily on the journalist’s wording and interpretation, an image can bring readers face to face with reality. Pictures of natural disasters, wars, or humanitarian crises can reveal suffering more powerfully than paragraphs of description. For instance, a photograph of destroyed homes after an earthquake may immediately communicate the scale of the damage. This is why photographs often act as a wake-up call, making distant events feel real and urgent.","chinese":"另一方面，許多人認為照片極具說服力，因為它們以直接而可見的方式呈現事件。 與書面報道不同，書面報道在很大程度上依賴記者的用詞和詮釋，而圖像則可以讓讀者直接面對現實。 自然災害、戰爭或人道危機的照片，比一段段文字描述更有力地揭示痛苦。 例如，一張地震後房屋被摧毀的照片，可以立即傳達破壞的規模。 這就是為什麼照片經常像一記警鐘，使遙遠的事件變得真實而迫切。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In my view, however, this emotional power is exactly why photographs must be handled carefully. They are valuable, but they are not self-explanatory. Without background information, verification, and responsible reporting, even a genuine image can create a false impression. Therefore, photographs are an important tool in journalism, but they should never be regarded as unquestionable evidence.","chinese":"然而，在我看來，這種情感力量正正是照片必須被謹慎處理的原因。 它們是有價值的，但它們本身並不能自動說明一切。 如果沒有背景資料、核實和負責任的報道，即使是真實的圖像也可能造成錯誤印象。 因此，照片是新聞業中的重要工具，但它們絕不應被視為不容質疑的證據。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"a powerful part of","chinese":"……的重要部分"},{"english":"modern journalism","chinese":"現代新聞業"},{"english":"newspapers and television channels","chinese":"報章和電視頻道"},{"english":"use images to","chinese":"使用圖片去"},{"english":"make stories more immediate and persuasive","chinese":"令新聞故事更即時、更有說服力"},{"english":"cannot always be trusted","chinese":"不一定可信"},{"english":"provide undeniable evidence of","chinese":"提供……的無可否認證據"},{"english":"what has happened","chinese":"發生過的事"},{"english":"discuss both views","chinese":"討論雙方觀點"},{"english":"be treated as","chinese":"被視為；被當作"},{"english":"supporting evidence","chinese":"輔助證據"},{"english":"rather than irrefutable proof","chinese":"而不是無可推翻的證明"},{"english":"irrefutable proof","chinese":"無可推翻的證明"},{"english":"distrust photographs","chinese":"不信任相片"},{"english":"have strong reasons for doing so","chinese":"這樣做有充分理由"},{"english":"appear objective","chinese":"看似客觀"},{"english":"mislead the public","chinese":"誤導公眾"},{"english":"be edited, cropped, staged, or presented without context","chinese":"被修改、裁剪、擺拍或脫離背景呈現"},{"english":"without context","chinese":"沒有背景脈絡"},{"english":"an angry protester","chinese":"憤怒的示威者"},{"english":"suggest violence","chinese":"暗示有暴力"},{"english":"the wider scene","chinese":"更廣闊的場面"},{"english":"mostly peaceful","chinese":"大致和平"},{"english":"in this way","chinese":"以這種方式"},{"english":"tell the whole story","chinese":"說出完整真相"},{"english":"capture one frozen moment","chinese":"捕捉一個凝固的瞬間"},{"english":"modern digital tools","chinese":"現代數碼工具"},{"english":"be altered so convincingly","chinese":"被改動得如此逼真"},{"english":"ordinary readers","chinese":"普通讀者"},{"english":"struggle to separate","chinese":"難以分辨"},{"english":"fact from manipulation","chinese":"事實和操控"},{"english":"as a result","chinese":"因此"},{"english":"relying on photographs alone","chinese":"單靠相片"},{"english":"form quick but inaccurate judgments","chinese":"形成快速但不準確的判斷"},{"english":"on the other hand","chinese":"另一方面"},{"english":"regard photographs as","chinese":"將相片視為"},{"english":"extremely convincing","chinese":"極具說服力"},{"english":"in a direct and visible way","chinese":"以直接而可見的方式"},{"english":"unlike a written report","chinese":"不像文字報道"},{"english":"depend heavily on","chinese":"非常依賴"},{"english":"the journalist's wording and interpretation","chinese":"記者的用字和詮釋"},{"english":"bring readers face to face with reality","chinese":"令讀者直接面對現實"},{"english":"natural disasters","chinese":"自然災害"},{"english":"humanitarian crises","chinese":"人道危機"},{"english":"reveal suffering","chinese":"揭示苦難"},{"english":"more powerfully than","chinese":"比……更有力"},{"english":"paragraphs of description","chinese":"大段文字描述"},{"english":"destroyed homes","chinese":"被摧毀的家園"},{"english":"after an earthquake","chinese":"地震之後"},{"english":"immediately communicate","chinese":"立即傳達"},{"english":"the scale of the damage","chinese":"損害的規模"},{"english":"act as a wake-up call","chinese":"發揮警醒作用"},{"english":"distant events","chinese":"遙遠事件"},{"english":"feel real and urgent","chinese":"感覺真實而迫切"},{"english":"in my view","chinese":"在我看來"},{"english":"emotional power","chinese":"情感力量"},{"english":"be handled carefully","chinese":"被謹慎處理"},{"english":"valuable, but not self-explanatory","chinese":"有價值，但不能自行說明一切"},{"english":"background information","chinese":"背景資料"},{"english":"verification","chinese":"核實"},{"english":"responsible reporting","chinese":"負責任的報道"},{"english":"a genuine image","chinese":"真實圖片"},{"english":"create a false impression","chinese":"製造錯誤印象"},{"english":"an important tool in journalism","chinese":"新聞業中的重要工具"},{"english":"never be regarded as","chinese":"絕不應被視為"},{"english":"unquestionable evidence","chinese":"不容置疑的證據"}]},"model-essay-28-ielts-opinion":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-28-ielts-opinion","essayKey":"opinion:28","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-28-ielts-opinion","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/opinions/EdmundBd9OP-Q28","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"Crime committed by young people is a serious concern in many communities, especially when the offences are violent or deeply harmful. However, I completely disagree that teenagers who commit major crimes should automatically receive the same punishment as adults, regardless of their age. A just legal system should punish serious wrongdoing firmly, but it should not ignore the offender’s stage of development.","chinese":"年輕人犯罪在許多社區中都是一個嚴重問題，尤其是當這些罪行涉及暴力或造成深遠傷害時。 然而，我完全不同意犯下重大罪行的青少年應該自動接受與成年人相同的懲罰，而不考慮他們的年齡。 公正的法律制度應該堅定地懲罰嚴重的不當行為，但不應忽視犯罪者所處的發展階段"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"The strongest reason is that teenagers are not fully mature in the way adults are. They are generally more impulsive, more vulnerable to peer pressure, and less able to judge long-term consequences. If the law treats a fourteen-year-old and a forty-year-old as identical simply because the offence is serious, punishment becomes a blunt weapon rather than a fair response. For example, a teenager who joins a violent attack because of gang influence may still deserve secure detention, strict supervision, and compensation to the victim. Yet placing that teenager in the adult system ignores the fact that his character is still being formed. Justice should hold him accountable, but it should also leave room for reform.","chinese":"最有力的理由是，青少年並不像成年人那樣完全成熟。 他們通常更衝動、更容易受到朋輩壓力影響，也較不擅長判斷長遠後果。 如果法律僅僅因為罪行嚴重，就把一名十四歲少年和一名四十歲成年人視為完全相同，那麼懲罰就會變成一件鈍器，而不是一種公平的回應。 例如，一名因受幫派影響而參與暴力襲擊的青少年，仍然可能應該接受安全拘留、嚴格監管，並向受害者作出賠償。 然而，把那名青少年放入成人司法系統，便忽視了他的性格仍在形成之中的事實。 司法應該要求他承擔責任，但也應該為改過自新留下空間。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"Adult punishment may also make society less safe in the long run. Teenagers sent to adult prisons are likely to lose access to education, family support, and positive role models, while being surrounded by experienced criminals. Instead of correcting their behaviour, the prison environment may teach them how to become more dangerous. When they are released, they may carry a criminal label, have few job prospects, and feel that ordinary society has closed its doors to them. By contrast, a strong youth justice system can combine secure custody with counselling, education, vocational training, and long-term monitoring. That approach protects the public while giving young offenders a realistic path back.","chinese":"從長遠來看，成人懲罰也可能令社會變得更不安全。 被送入成人監獄的青少年，很可能會失去接受教育、獲得家庭支持和接觸正面榜樣的機會，同時被有經驗的罪犯包圍。 監獄環境不但未必能糾正他們的行為，反而可能教會他們如何變得更加危險。 當他們獲釋後，他們可能背負罪犯標籤、缺乏就業前景，並感到正常社會已經向他們關上大門。 相比之下，一個完善的青少年司法制度可以把安全拘留與輔導、教育、職業培訓和長期監察結合起來。 這種做法既能保護公眾，也能給予年輕罪犯一條實際可行的回歸道路。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, I completely disagree with giving teenagers adult punishment regardless of age. Major crimes require serious consequences, but teenage offenders should be dealt with through a separate youth justice system that balances accountability, rehabilitation, and public safety.","chinese":"總結來說，我完全不同意不論年齡都給予青少年成人懲罰。 重大罪行需要嚴重後果，但青少年罪犯應該透過一個獨立的青少年司法制度處理，而這個制度應在問責、改造和公共安全之間取得平衡。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"crime committed by","chinese":"由……犯下的罪行"},{"english":"young people","chinese":"年輕人"},{"english":"serious concern","chinese":"嚴重憂慮"},{"english":"many communities","chinese":"許多社區"},{"english":"offences","chinese":"罪行"},{"english":"violent or deeply harmful","chinese":"暴力或造成深遠傷害"},{"english":"teenagers","chinese":"青少年"},{"english":"commit major crimes","chinese":"犯下嚴重罪行"},{"english":"automatically receive","chinese":"自動受到"},{"english":"same punishment as adults","chinese":"與成年人相同的刑罰"},{"english":"regardless of their age","chinese":"不論他們的年齡"},{"english":"just legal system","chinese":"公正的法律制度"},{"english":"punish serious wrongdoing firmly","chinese":"堅定地懲罰嚴重錯誤行為"},{"english":"serious wrongdoing","chinese":"嚴重錯誤行為"},{"english":"ignore the offender's stage of development","chinese":"忽視犯事者的發展階段"},{"english":"stage of development","chinese":"發展階段"},{"english":"fully mature","chinese":"完全成熟"},{"english":"impulsive","chinese":"衝動"},{"english":"vulnerable to peer pressure","chinese":"容易受同輩壓力影響"},{"english":"peer pressure","chinese":"同輩壓力"},{"english":"less able to judge","chinese":"較不能判斷"},{"english":"long-term consequences","chinese":"長遠後果"},{"english":"treats a fourteen-year-old and a forty-year-old as identical","chinese":"將十四歲和四十歲的人視為一樣"},{"english":"simply because","chinese":"只是因為"},{"english":"blunt weapon","chinese":"粗糙的武器"},{"english":"fair response","chinese":"公平回應"},{"english":"violent attack","chinese":"暴力襲擊"},{"english":"gang influence","chinese":"幫派影響"},{"english":"deserve secure detention","chinese":"應受到安全拘留"},{"english":"secure detention","chinese":"安全拘留"},{"english":"strict supervision","chinese":"嚴格監管"},{"english":"compensation to the victim","chinese":"向受害者作出賠償"},{"english":"adult system","chinese":"成人司法制度"},{"english":"his character is still being formed","chinese":"他的性格仍在形成中"},{"english":"hold him accountable","chinese":"追究他的責任"},{"english":"leave room for reform","chinese":"留有改過空間"},{"english":"make society less safe","chinese":"令社會長遠而言更不安全"},{"english":"in the long run","chinese":"長遠而言"},{"english":"adult prisons","chinese":"成人監獄"},{"english":"be likely to","chinese":"很可能"},{"english":"lose access to","chinese":"失去取得……的機會"},{"english":"positive role models","chinese":"正面榜樣"},{"english":"be surrounded by","chinese":"被……包圍"},{"english":"experienced criminals","chinese":"老練罪犯"},{"english":"correcting their behaviour","chinese":"糾正他們的行為"},{"english":"prison environment","chinese":"監獄環境"},{"english":"criminal label","chinese":"犯罪標籤"},{"english":"job prospects","chinese":"就業前景"},{"english":"ordinary society","chinese":"正常社會"},{"english":"closed its doors to them","chinese":"對他們關上大門"},{"english":"by contrast","chinese":"相比之下"},{"english":"youth justice system","chinese":"青少年司法制度"},{"english":"combine secure custody with","chinese":"將安全羈押與……結合"},{"english":"secure custody","chinese":"安全羈押"},{"english":"counselling","chinese":"輔導"},{"english":"vocational training","chinese":"職業培訓"},{"english":"long-term monitoring","chinese":"長期監察"},{"english":"protects the public while","chinese":"在……的同時保護公眾"},{"english":"young offenders","chinese":"青少年犯事者"},{"english":"realistic path back","chinese":"現實可行的回歸途徑"},{"english":"adult punishment","chinese":"成人刑罰"},{"english":"major crimes require serious consequences","chinese":"嚴重罪行需要嚴重後果"},{"english":"serious consequences","chinese":"嚴重後果"},{"english":"teenage offenders","chinese":"青少年犯事者"},{"english":"be dealt with through","chinese":"透過……處理"},{"english":"separate youth justice system","chinese":"獨立的青少年司法制度"},{"english":"balances accountability, rehabilitation, and public safety","chinese":"平衡問責、更生和公共安全"},{"english":"accountability","chinese":"問責"},{"english":"rehabilitation","chinese":"更生"},{"english":"public safety","chinese":"公共安全"}]},"model-essay-29-ielts-advantage-disadvantage":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-29-ielts-advantage-disadvantage","essayKey":"advantage-disadvantage:29","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-29-ielts-advantage-disadvantage","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/advantage-and-disadvantage/EdmundBd9AdDisAd-Q29","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"Many families encourage school-age children to take part-time jobs during weekends or school holidays. Such work can offer valuable lessons beyond the classroom. At the same time, it may expose young people to pressures that they are not yet mature enough to manage well.","chinese":"很多家庭會鼓勵學齡兒童在週末或學校假期做兼職工作。 這類工作可以帶來課堂以外的寶貴經驗，但同時也可能讓年輕人面對一些他們尚未成熟到足以妥善處理的壓力。 本文將探討孩子在空閒時間從事兼職工作的優點與缺點。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"One important advantage is that paid work can foster responsibility and financial awareness. When children are expected to arrive on time, follow instructions and earn their own wages, they begin to understand that money is linked to effort rather than simply provided on demand. For example, a teenager who spends a few hours each week working in a café may become far more careful about unnecessary spending. Another benefit is that part-time employment can build practical skills that schools do not always teach directly. By serving customers, cooperating with co-workers and solving small problems under pressure, young people can develop confidence, communication skills and better time management, all of which are likely to be useful in adult life.","chinese":"兼職工作的一個重要優點是，它能培養責任感和金錢觀念。 當孩子被要求準時上班、遵從指示並靠自己賺取薪水時，他們便會開始明白，金錢是與付出和努力連在一起的，而不是理所當然地隨時可得。 這有助於他們變得更有紀律、更理性地看待花費，也更懂得珍惜工作的價值。 例如，一名每週在咖啡店工作幾小時的青少年，一旦親自辛苦賺過那些錢，便可能會對購買不必要的東西變得謹慎得多。 另一個優點是，兼職工作能培養一些學校未必會直接教授的實用技能。 透過服務顧客、與同事合作，以及在壓力下處理小問題，年輕人可以培養自信、溝通能力和更好的時間管理能力。 例如，一個在小店幫忙的孩子，可能會學會如何有禮貌地與陌生人交談、在繁忙時段保持冷靜，以及在工作與學業責任之間取得平衡。 因此，兼職工作可以幫助孩子成長為更有責任感、更有能力、也更獨立的人。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"However, there are also clear disadvantages. The most obvious is that work can eat into time that should be reserved for study, sleep or family life. A child who works several evening shifts in a supermarket, for instance, may return home too tired to complete homework properly, and this can gradually weaken academic performance. In addition, early exposure to workplace stress may be harmful if the environment is demanding or poorly supervised. Some young workers may have to deal with rude customers, long hours or unrealistic expectations before they are emotionally ready, which can turn a potentially valuable experience into a heavy burden.","chinese":"然而，兼職工作也有明顯的缺點，尤其當它開始干擾孩子的學業或身心健康時。 最明顯的缺點是，工作可能會佔去本應留給學習、休息或家庭生活的時間。 如果孩子花太多時間工作，他們可能會變得疲累、難以好好完成作業，並且逐漸在學校表現變差。 例如，一個在超市上好幾個晚班的孩子，回到家後可能已經累得無法專心溫習，而這會慢慢損害其學業表現。 另一個缺點是，如果工作環境要求過高或缺乏妥善監管，過早接觸職場壓力可能會對孩子造成傷害。 年輕打工者可能在情感上尚未準備好之前，就要面對無禮的顧客、過長的工時或不切實際的期望，這會使原本有價值的經驗變成沉重的負擔。 例如，一名在繁忙餐廳工作的青少年，可能會因持續不斷的壓力與批評而感到不堪負荷，而不是從這段經驗中建立自信。 因此，雖然兼職工作可以帶來好處，但它也可能為孩子帶來學業和情緒上的壓力。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"Overall, part-time work can help children become more mature, capable and independent, yet it can also create academic and emotional strain. Its impact therefore depends largely on the amount of work involved and whether clear limits are kept in place.","chinese":"整體而言，兼職工作可以幫助孩子變得更成熟、更有能力和更獨立，但同時也可能帶來學業與情緒上的壓力。 它所帶來的影響，很大程度上取決於工作量是否適中，以及是否有合理的限制被清楚地設立。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"encourage school-age children to","chinese":"鼓勵學齡兒童去"},{"english":"school-age children","chinese":"學齡兒童"},{"english":"take part-time jobs","chinese":"做兼職工作"},{"english":"during weekends or school holidays","chinese":"在週末或學校假期期間"},{"english":"offer valuable lessons beyond the classroom","chinese":"提供課堂以外的寶貴經驗"},{"english":"beyond the classroom","chinese":"課堂以外"},{"english":"at the same time","chinese":"同時"},{"english":"expose young people to pressures","chinese":"令年輕人面對壓力"},{"english":"not yet mature enough to manage well","chinese":"尚未成熟到能妥善處理"},{"english":"paid work","chinese":"有薪工作"},{"english":"foster responsibility","chinese":"培養責任感"},{"english":"financial awareness","chinese":"理財意識"},{"english":"be expected to","chinese":"被期望要"},{"english":"arrive on time","chinese":"準時到達"},{"english":"follow instructions","chinese":"遵從指示"},{"english":"earn their own wages","chinese":"賺取自己的工資"},{"english":"be linked to effort","chinese":"與努力掛鈎"},{"english":"simply provided on demand","chinese":"不是有求必應地提供"},{"english":"spends a few hours each week working in","chinese":"每星期花數小時在……工作"},{"english":"become far more careful about","chinese":"對……變得謹慎得多"},{"english":"unnecessary spending","chinese":"不必要的開支"},{"english":"part-time employment","chinese":"兼職工作"},{"english":"practical skills","chinese":"實用技能"},{"english":"teach directly","chinese":"直接教授"},{"english":"serving customers","chinese":"服務顧客"},{"english":"cooperating with co-workers","chinese":"與同事合作"},{"english":"solving small problems under pressure","chinese":"在壓力下解決小問題"},{"english":"develop confidence","chinese":"建立自信"},{"english":"communication skills","chinese":"溝通技巧"},{"english":"better time management","chinese":"更好的時間管理"},{"english":"be useful in adult life","chinese":"在成年生活中有用"},{"english":"clear disadvantages","chinese":"明顯缺點"},{"english":"eat into time","chinese":"侵佔時間"},{"english":"be reserved for","chinese":"留作……之用"},{"english":"family life","chinese":"家庭生活"},{"english":"evening shifts","chinese":"晚班"},{"english":"return home too tired to","chinese":"回家時太疲倦而不能"},{"english":"complete homework properly","chinese":"妥善完成家課"},{"english":"gradually weaken academic performance","chinese":"逐漸削弱學業表現"},{"english":"academic performance","chinese":"學業表現"},{"english":"early exposure to workplace stress","chinese":"過早接觸職場壓力"},{"english":"workplace stress","chinese":"職場壓力"},{"english":"be harmful if","chinese":"如果……便可能有害"},{"english":"demanding","chinese":"要求高的"},{"english":"poorly supervised","chinese":"監督不足的"},{"english":"deal with rude customers","chinese":"應付粗魯顧客"},{"english":"long hours","chinese":"長時間工作"},{"english":"unrealistic expectations","chinese":"不切實際的期望"},{"english":"emotionally ready","chinese":"情緒上準備好"},{"english":"turn a potentially valuable experience into","chinese":"將本來可能有價值的經驗變成"},{"english":"a heavy burden","chinese":"沉重負擔"},{"english":"overall","chinese":"總括而言"},{"english":"mature, capable and independent","chinese":"成熟、有能力和獨立"},{"english":"academic and emotional strain","chinese":"學業及情緒壓力"},{"english":"its impact depends largely on","chinese":"其影響很大程度上取決於"},{"english":"the amount of work involved","chinese":"涉及的工作量"},{"english":"clear limits are kept in place","chinese":"清晰限制是否得以維持"}]},"model-essay-29-ielts-direct-question":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-29-ielts-direct-question","essayKey":"direct-question:29","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-29-ielts-direct-question","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/direct-question/EdmundBd9Dir-Q29","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"Childhood obesity has become a serious concern in many education systems, and some people argue that schools should devote more time to sport and exercise to address it. Although physical activity is certainly valuable, I do not believe that increasing PE lessons is the best way to solve this problem. A more effective approach is to improve children’s diets and reshape their daily habits both inside and outside school.","chinese":"兒童肥胖已成為許多教育制度中的嚴重問題，而一些人認為學校應該投放更多時間在體育和運動上，以處理這個問題。 儘管體能活動當然有價值，但我並不認為增加體育課是解決這個問題的最佳方法。 更有效的方法是改善兒童的飲食，並重塑他們在校內和校外的日常習慣。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"Extra exercise at school can help overweight children, but its impact is limited. Sport allows pupils to burn energy, build strength and develop a healthier attitude towards their bodies. It can also reduce the time they spend sitting in classrooms or staring at screens. However, a few additional hours of exercise each week can easily be cancelled out if children continue to eat sugary snacks, drink soft drinks and consume oversized portions every day. In other words, exercise may strengthen the engine, but poor diet keeps pouring the wrong fuel into it. For this reason, schools should not treat more sports as the main cure for childhood obesity.","chinese":"在學校增加運動確實可以幫助超重兒童，但其影響是有限的。 運動能讓學生消耗能量、增強體力，並對自己的身體建立更健康的態度。 它也可以減少他們坐在課室裡，或盯著螢幕的時間。 然而，如果兒童每天仍然吃含糖零食、喝汽水，並攝取過大的食物份量，那麼每週額外幾小時的運動很容易被抵消。 換句話說，運動或許能強化引擎，但不良飲食卻一直把錯誤的燃料倒進去。 因此，學校不應把增加運動視為治療兒童肥胖的主要方法。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"The most important solution is to change what children eat. Schools should provide healthier meals, restrict the sale of junk food on campus and teach pupils how everyday choices affect their weight. For example, a child who learns to replace sweet drinks with water and processed snacks with fruit is likely to make progress even without dramatic changes to their timetable. Parents must also be involved, because children’s eating patterns are usually formed at home. If families regularly cook balanced meals, limit screen time and encourage walking or outdoor play, healthy behaviour becomes a normal part of life rather than a punishment.","chinese":"最重要的解決方法是改變兒童的飲食內容。 學校應該提供更健康的膳食、限制校園內垃圾食品的銷售，並教導學生日常選擇如何影響他們的體重。 例如，一個學會用水取代甜飲、用水果取代加工零食的孩子，即使時間表沒有巨大改變，也很可能會有所進步。 父母也必須參與其中，因為兒童的飲食模式通常是在家中形成的。 如果家庭經常烹調均衡膳食、限制螢幕時間，並鼓勵步行或戶外玩耍，健康行為就會成為生活中的正常部分，而不是一種懲罰。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, increasing time for sport and exercise is a useful measure, but it is not the best solution to the problem of overweight children. The stronger answer is a combination of healthier school food, practical nutrition education and consistent support from families.","chinese":"總結來說，增加體育和運動時間是一項有用的措施，但它並不是解決兒童超重問題的最佳方法。 更有力的答案，是結合更健康的學校食物、實用的營養教育，以及來自家庭的持續支持"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"childhood obesity","chinese":"兒童肥胖"},{"english":"a serious concern","chinese":"嚴重關注的問題"},{"english":"education systems","chinese":"教育制度"},{"english":"devote more time to","chinese":"投放更多時間於"},{"english":"sport and exercise","chinese":"運動和鍛煉"},{"english":"address it","chinese":"處理它；應對它"},{"english":"physical activity","chinese":"體能活動"},{"english":"increasing PE lessons","chinese":"增加體育課"},{"english":"the best way to solve","chinese":"解決……的最佳方法"},{"english":"a more effective approach","chinese":"更有效的方法"},{"english":"improve children's diets","chinese":"改善孩子的飲食"},{"english":"reshape their daily habits","chinese":"重塑他們的日常習慣"},{"english":"inside and outside school","chinese":"校內和校外"},{"english":"extra exercise","chinese":"額外運動"},{"english":"overweight children","chinese":"超重兒童"},{"english":"its impact is limited","chinese":"它的影響有限"},{"english":"burn energy","chinese":"消耗能量"},{"english":"build strength","chinese":"增強體力"},{"english":"develop a healthier attitude towards","chinese":"對……培養更健康的態度"},{"english":"their bodies","chinese":"他們的身體"},{"english":"reduce the time they spend","chinese":"減少他們花在……上的時間"},{"english":"sitting in classrooms","chinese":"坐在課室裏"},{"english":"staring at screens","chinese":"盯着屏幕"},{"english":"a few additional hours of","chinese":"額外幾小時的……"},{"english":"each week","chinese":"每星期"},{"english":"be cancelled out","chinese":"被抵消"},{"english":"continue to eat","chinese":"繼續吃"},{"english":"sugary snacks","chinese":"高糖零食"},{"english":"soft drinks","chinese":"汽水；含糖飲品"},{"english":"oversized portions","chinese":"過大的食物分量"},{"english":"In other words","chinese":"換句話說"},{"english":"strengthen the engine","chinese":"強化引擎"},{"english":"poor diet","chinese":"不良飲食"},{"english":"keeps pouring","chinese":"不斷倒入"},{"english":"the wrong fuel","chinese":"錯誤燃料"},{"english":"For this reason","chinese":"因此"},{"english":"treat more sports as","chinese":"把更多運動視為"},{"english":"the main cure for","chinese":"……的主要解決方法"},{"english":"the most important solution","chinese":"最重要的解決方法"},{"english":"change what children eat","chinese":"改變孩子吃甚麼"},{"english":"provide healthier meals","chinese":"提供更健康的膳食"},{"english":"restrict the sale of","chinese":"限制……的售賣"},{"english":"junk food","chinese":"垃圾食物"},{"english":"on campus","chinese":"在校園內"},{"english":"everyday choices","chinese":"日常選擇"},{"english":"affect their weight","chinese":"影響他們的體重"},{"english":"learns to replace","chinese":"學會用……取代"},{"english":"sweet drinks","chinese":"甜飲品"},{"english":"processed snacks","chinese":"加工零食"},{"english":"be likely to","chinese":"有可能"},{"english":"make progress","chinese":"取得進步"},{"english":"even without","chinese":"即使沒有"},{"english":"dramatic changes to","chinese":"對……作出重大改變"},{"english":"timetable","chinese":"時間表"},{"english":"parents must also be involved","chinese":"父母也必須參與"},{"english":"eating patterns","chinese":"飲食模式"},{"english":"be formed at home","chinese":"在家中形成"},{"english":"regularly cook balanced meals","chinese":"定期煮均衡膳食"},{"english":"balanced meals","chinese":"均衡膳食"},{"english":"limit screen time","chinese":"限制使用屏幕的時間"},{"english":"encourage walking","chinese":"鼓勵步行"},{"english":"outdoor play","chinese":"戶外玩耍"},{"english":"healthy behaviour","chinese":"健康行為"},{"english":"a normal part of life","chinese":"生活中的正常一部分"},{"english":"rather than a punishment","chinese":"而不是懲罰"},{"english":"a useful measure","chinese":"有用措施"},{"english":"the stronger answer","chinese":"更有力的答案"},{"english":"a combination of","chinese":"……的結合"},{"english":"healthier school food","chinese":"更健康的學校食物"},{"english":"practical nutrition education","chinese":"實用營養教育"},{"english":"consistent support from families","chinese":"來自家庭的持續支持"}]},"model-essay-29-ielts-discuss-both-views":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-29-ielts-discuss-both-views","essayKey":"discuss-both-views:29","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-29-ielts-discuss-both-views","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/discuss-both-views-your-opinion/EdmundBd9ExpBth-Q29","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"Television has long been seen as a powerful influence on children, but people disagree about whether this influence comes mainly from the type of programmes they watch or from the number of hours they spend in front of the screen. In my view, the content children are exposed to has a stronger effect on their behaviour than viewing time alone.","chinese":"電視長期以來都被視為對兒童具有強大影響力，但人們對於這種影響主要來自他們所觀看的節目類型，還是來自他們花在螢幕前的時間長短，存在不同看法。 在我看來，兒童所接觸的內容，比單純的觀看時間對他們的行為有更強的影響。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"Those who focus on screen time argue that excessive television watching can damage children’s habits and character. When young people spend several hours a day watching television, they may become passive, less physically active, and less willing to engage with family members or classmates. This can gradually affect their discipline, social confidence, and attention span. For example, a child who spends most evenings watching television may have less time for homework, outdoor play, or face-to-face conversation. Over time, this routine can make them more impatient and less able to concentrate. From this perspective, the problem is not one particular programme, but the way television fills up a child’s daily life.","chinese":"那些重視觀看時間的人認為，過度看電視會損害兒童的習慣和性格。 當年輕人每天花數小時看電視時，他們可能會變得被動、較少進行體能活動，也較不願意與家人或同學互動。 這可能會逐漸影響他們的自律能力、社交信心和專注力。 例如，一個大部分晚上都在看電視的孩子，可能會有較少時間做功課、到戶外玩耍，或進行面對面的交流。 長遠而言，這種日常習慣可能會令他們變得更急躁，也更難集中注意力。 從這個角度來看，問題並不在某一個特定節目，而在於電視佔據了孩子日常生活的方式"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"However, I believe that what children watch matters more because content directly shapes their ideas, emotions, and patterns of behaviour. Children often learn by imitation, especially when they repeatedly see certain actions being rewarded or normalised. If a programme presents violence, rudeness, or selfishness as entertaining, young viewers may slowly absorb the message that such behaviour is acceptable. By contrast, educational programmes or stories with positive role models can encourage curiosity, kindness, and responsible choices. In this sense, television is like a mirror and a teacher at the same time: it reflects certain values, but it can also quietly plant them in a child’s mind.","chinese":"然而，我認為兒童觀看的內容更加重要，因為內容會直接塑造他們的想法、情緒和行為模式。 兒童往往透過模仿來學習，尤其是當他們反覆看到某些行為受到獎勵或被視為正常時。 如果一個節目把暴力、無禮或自私呈現成有趣的事情，年幼觀眾可能會慢慢吸收一種訊息：這類行為是可以接受的。 相比之下，教育性節目或具正面榜樣的故事，則可以鼓勵好奇心、善良和負責任的選擇 從這個意義上說，電視就像一面鏡子，同時也是一位老師：它反映某些價值觀，但也能悄悄地把這些價值觀種在孩子心中。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, the amount of time children spend watching television can certainly affect their routines and self-control. Nevertheless, I firmly believe that programme content has the greater influence, because it directly teaches children what to admire, copy, and accept as normal.","chinese":"總結來說，兒童花在看電視上的時間，確實會影響他們的日常習慣和自我控制能力。 然而，我堅定地認為，節目內容具有更大的影響力，因為它會直接教導兒童應該欣賞甚麼、模仿甚麼，以及把甚麼視為正常。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"has long been seen as","chinese":"長久以來被視為"},{"english":"a powerful influence on","chinese":"對……有強大影響"},{"english":"disagree about whether","chinese":"對於是否……有分歧"},{"english":"comes mainly from","chinese":"主要來自"},{"english":"the type of programmes","chinese":"節目的類型"},{"english":"spend in front of the screen","chinese":"花在螢幕前"},{"english":"in my view","chinese":"在我看來"},{"english":"be exposed to","chinese":"接觸到"},{"english":"have a stronger effect on","chinese":"對……有更強影響"},{"english":"viewing time alone","chinese":"單是觀看時間"},{"english":"focus on screen time","chinese":"着眼於螢幕時間"},{"english":"screen time","chinese":"螢幕時間"},{"english":"excessive television watching","chinese":"過度看電視"},{"english":"damage children's habits and character","chinese":"損害兒童的習慣和品格"},{"english":"spend several hours a day","chinese":"每日花數小時"},{"english":"become passive","chinese":"變得被動"},{"english":"less physically active","chinese":"較少活動身體"},{"english":"less willing to engage with","chinese":"較不願意與……互動"},{"english":"family members or classmates","chinese":"家人或同學"},{"english":"gradually affect","chinese":"逐漸影響"},{"english":"discipline","chinese":"自律"},{"english":"social confidence","chinese":"社交信心"},{"english":"attention span","chinese":"專注力持續時間"},{"english":"spend most evenings","chinese":"大多數晚上都花時間"},{"english":"outdoor play","chinese":"戶外玩耍"},{"english":"face-to-face conversation","chinese":"面對面交談"},{"english":"over time","chinese":"隨時間"},{"english":"this routine","chinese":"這種日常習慣"},{"english":"more impatient","chinese":"更加沒有耐性"},{"english":"less able to concentrate","chinese":"較難集中精神"},{"english":"from this perspective","chinese":"從這個角度來看"},{"english":"one particular programme","chinese":"某一個特定節目"},{"english":"fill up a child's daily life","chinese":"佔據兒童的日常生活"},{"english":"what children watch matters more","chinese":"兒童看甚麼更加重要"},{"english":"directly shape","chinese":"直接塑造"},{"english":"ideas, emotions, and patterns of behaviour","chinese":"想法、情緒和行為模式"},{"english":"learn by imitation","chinese":"透過模仿學習"},{"english":"repeatedly see","chinese":"反覆看見"},{"english":"certain actions being rewarded","chinese":"某些行為得到獎勵"},{"english":"be normalised","chinese":"被正常化"},{"english":"presents violence, rudeness, or selfishness as entertaining","chinese":"將暴力、粗魯或自私呈現為娛樂"},{"english":"young viewers","chinese":"年幼觀眾"},{"english":"slowly absorb the message that","chinese":"慢慢吸收……的訊息"},{"english":"such behaviour is acceptable","chinese":"這種行為是可以接受的"},{"english":"by contrast","chinese":"相反"},{"english":"educational programmes","chinese":"教育節目"},{"english":"positive role models","chinese":"正面榜樣"},{"english":"encourage curiosity","chinese":"鼓勵好奇心"},{"english":"responsible choices","chinese":"負責任的選擇"},{"english":"at the same time","chinese":"同時"},{"english":"reflect certain values","chinese":"反映某些價值觀"},{"english":"quietly plant them in","chinese":"悄悄植入……之中"},{"english":"a child's mind","chinese":"兒童的思想"},{"english":"the amount of time","chinese":"……的時間長短"},{"english":"self-control","chinese":"自制能力"},{"english":"nevertheless","chinese":"然而"},{"english":"programme content","chinese":"節目內容"},{"english":"the greater influence","chinese":"更大的影響"},{"english":"teach children what to admire","chinese":"教導兒童欣賞甚麼"},{"english":"copy and accept as normal","chinese":"模仿並視為正常"}]},"model-essay-29-ielts-opinion":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-29-ielts-opinion","essayKey":"opinion:29","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-29-ielts-opinion","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/opinions/EdmundBd9OP-Q29","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"Crime is a serious social problem because it weakens public safety and people's trust in everyday life. In response to rising crime rates, some people argue that putting more police officers on the streets is the only effective solution. I completely disagree with this view, because crime can be reduced more permanently through prevention and rehabilitation.","chinese":"犯罪是一個嚴重的社會問題，因為它削弱公共安全以及人們對日常生活的信任。 面對犯罪率上升，一些人認為在街上部署更多警察是唯一有效的解決方法。 我完全不同意這個觀點，因為犯罪可以透過預防和改造更長久地減少。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"The first reason is that many offences are rooted in social conditions, not merely in a lack of police presence. When young people grow up in poor neighbourhoods, leave school with few useful skills, or see little hope of stable work, crime can appear to be the quickest escape from hardship. More patrols may stop some offences in public places, but they do not remove the pressure that pushes people towards illegal behaviour. By contrast, better education, youth centres, job training and mental-health support can tackle crime at its source. For example, a teenager who has after-school supervision and a realistic path into employment is far less likely to join a gang or steal to survive. Prevention is therefore not a soft option; it is a practical way to stop crime before it takes root.","chinese":"第一個原因是，許多犯罪都根源於社會條件，而不只是因為警力不足。 當年輕人在貧困社區長大、離開學校時缺乏實用技能，或者看不到穩定工作的希望時，犯罪可能看起來像是逃離困境最快的方法。 更多巡邏或許能阻止公共場所中的犯罪，但它們並不能消除把人推向違法行為的壓力 相比之下，更好的教育、青少年中心、職業培訓和心理健康支援，能夠從源頭處理犯罪問題。 例如，一個有課後監督，並且有實際就業途徑的青少年，加入幫派或為了生存而偷竊的可能性會低得多。 因此，預防並不是一種軟弱的選擇；它是在犯罪生根之前阻止犯罪的實際方法。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"A second reason is that many crimes are committed by people who have already passed through the justice system. If prisons only punish offenders and release them without skills, support or employment prospects, society may simply be locking people away temporarily while leaving the underlying problem untouched. Rehabilitation programmes, counselling and supervised work opportunities can break this cycle of reoffending. A former prisoner who learns a trade and receives guidance after release has a stronger reason to live responsibly than one who returns to poverty and isolation. This makes rehabilitation a necessary partner to law enforcement, not a luxury.","chinese":"第二個原因是，許多犯罪都是由已經經歷過司法系統的人所犯下的。 如果監獄只是懲罰罪犯，然後在他們沒有技能、支援或就業前景的情況下釋放他們，社會可能只是暫時把人關起來，卻沒有處理根本問題。 改造計劃、輔導和受監督的工作機會，能夠打破這種再次犯罪的循環。 一個學會一門技能並在釋放後得到指導的前囚犯，比一個重新回到貧困和孤立中的人，更有理由負責任地生活。 這使得改造罪犯成為執法不可或缺的夥伴，而不是一種奢侈的選項。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, I completely disagree that street policing is the only way to reduce crime. Visible officers may discourage some offences, but lasting public safety depends on prevention, education, employment and rehabilitation.","chinese":"總結來說，我完全不同意街頭警力是減少犯罪的唯一方法。 可見的警察或許能阻嚇一些犯罪，但長久的公共安全取決於預防、教育、就業和改造。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"crime","chinese":"犯罪"},{"english":"serious social problem","chinese":"嚴重社會問題"},{"english":"public safety","chinese":"公共安全"},{"english":"trust in everyday life","chinese":"對日常生活的信任"},{"english":"in response to","chinese":"為了回應……"},{"english":"rising crime rates","chinese":"上升的罪案率"},{"english":"putting more police officers on the streets","chinese":"在街上增派警員"},{"english":"the only effective solution","chinese":"唯一有效的解決方法"},{"english":"crime can be reduced","chinese":"犯罪可以被減少"},{"english":"more permanently","chinese":"更持久地"},{"english":"prevention and rehabilitation","chinese":"預防和更生"},{"english":"many offences","chinese":"許多罪行"},{"english":"be rooted in","chinese":"根源在於……"},{"english":"social conditions","chinese":"社會環境"},{"english":"not merely in","chinese":"不只是源於……"},{"english":"lack of police presence","chinese":"缺乏警力出現"},{"english":"grow up in","chinese":"在……中成長"},{"english":"poor neighbourhoods","chinese":"貧困社區"},{"english":"leave school with","chinese":"帶着……離開學校"},{"english":"useful skills","chinese":"有用技能"},{"english":"little hope of","chinese":"對……幾乎沒有希望"},{"english":"stable work","chinese":"穩定工作"},{"english":"the quickest escape from hardship","chinese":"逃離困境最快的方法"},{"english":"hardship","chinese":"困境；艱難生活"},{"english":"more patrols","chinese":"更多巡邏"},{"english":"public places","chinese":"公共地方"},{"english":"remove the pressure","chinese":"消除壓力"},{"english":"pushes people towards","chinese":"將人推向……"},{"english":"illegal behaviour","chinese":"違法行為"},{"english":"by contrast","chinese":"相比之下"},{"english":"youth centres","chinese":"青少年中心"},{"english":"job training","chinese":"職業培訓"},{"english":"mental-health support","chinese":"精神健康支援"},{"english":"tackle crime at its source","chinese":"從源頭處理犯罪"},{"english":"after-school supervision","chinese":"課後監督"},{"english":"realistic path into employment","chinese":"進入就業的現實途徑"},{"english":"far less likely to","chinese":"可能性低得多"},{"english":"join a gang","chinese":"加入幫派"},{"english":"steal to survive","chinese":"為了生存而偷竊"},{"english":"soft option","chinese":"軟弱的選擇；寬鬆做法"},{"english":"practical way to","chinese":"……的實際方法"},{"english":"before it takes root","chinese":"在它扎根之前"},{"english":"be committed by","chinese":"由……犯下"},{"english":"have already passed through","chinese":"已經經歷過……"},{"english":"justice system","chinese":"司法制度"},{"english":"punish offenders","chinese":"懲罰犯事者"},{"english":"release them without","chinese":"在沒有……的情況下釋放他們"},{"english":"employment prospects","chinese":"就業前景"},{"english":"lock people away temporarily","chinese":"暫時將人關起來"},{"english":"underlying problem","chinese":"根本問題"},{"english":"untouched","chinese":"未被處理"},{"english":"rehabilitation programmes","chinese":"更生計劃"},{"english":"counselling","chinese":"輔導"},{"english":"supervised work opportunities","chinese":"受監管的工作機會"},{"english":"break this cycle of reoffending","chinese":"打破重犯循環"},{"english":"former prisoner","chinese":"前囚犯"},{"english":"learns a trade","chinese":"學一門手藝"},{"english":"receives guidance after release","chinese":"獲釋後得到指導"},{"english":"stronger reason to","chinese":"更有理由去……"},{"english":"live responsibly","chinese":"負責任地生活"},{"english":"returns to poverty and isolation","chinese":"回到貧窮和孤立之中"},{"english":"necessary partner to","chinese":"……的必要配合"},{"english":"law enforcement","chinese":"執法"},{"english":"not a luxury","chinese":"不是奢侈品"},{"english":"street policing","chinese":"街頭警務；街上巡邏"},{"english":"visible officers","chinese":"可見的警員"},{"english":"discourage some offences","chinese":"阻止部分罪行"},{"english":"lasting public safety","chinese":"持久公共安全"},{"english":"employment and rehabilitation","chinese":"就業和更生"}]},"model-essay-30-ielts-advantage-disadvantage":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-30-ielts-advantage-disadvantage","essayKey":"advantage-disadvantage:30","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-30-ielts-advantage-disadvantage","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/advantage-and-disadvantage/EdmundBd9AdDisAd-Q30","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"In many countries, online home-based work has become a normal form of employment. Although this shift can weaken workplace relationships and blur personal boundaries, I believe it is overall beneficial because it improves employees’ daily lives and makes the labour market more inclusive.","chinese":"在許多國家，在家線上工作已逐漸成為一種愈來愈普遍的就業模式。 儘管這種趨勢可能削弱職場人際關係，並模糊工作與私人生活之間的界線， 我認為整體而言這是一項正面的發展，因為它改善了員工的生活質素，並讓更廣泛的人群更容易獲得工作機會。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"One clear advantage is better work-life balance. Without long commutes, workers recover time for sleep, exercise, childcare, and a calmer start to the day. Less time pressure usually means less stress and better concentration, so productivity may also rise. For example, someone who no longer spends two hours commuting can prepare meals at home and begin work in a far better frame of mind. Another benefit is broader access to jobs. Because location matters less, firms can hire talent from rural areas, while parents and people with limited mobility can apply for roles once beyond their reach. For instance, a city-based company can employ a skilled programmer who lives hundreds of kilometres away.","chinese":"在家線上工作的主要優點是，它讓人們對自己的時間和日常安排有更大的掌控。 由於不需要每天通勤，員工可以節省原本要花在交通上的時間和精力。 這些額外時間可以用於睡眠、運動、照顧孩子，或只是以更從容的狀態開始一天，從而減輕壓力、提升專注力，並且往往帶來更好的工作表現。 例如，一名不再每天花兩小時通勤的員工，可能可以在家準備餐食，並以好得多的精神狀態開始工作。 另一個重要好處是，遙距工作擴大了就業機會的可及性。 由於地點不再那麼重要，公司可以聘用來自偏遠地區的人才，而家長及行動不便的人也能申請以往難以從事的工作。 例如，一間位於城市的公司，仍然可以聘用住在數百公里外的優秀軟件工程師。 因此，在家線上工作既能提升個人生活質素，也能增加人們獲得就業機會的可能。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"However, this trend also has disadvantages. The first is social and professional isolation. When communication happens mainly through screens, spontaneous conversations, informal mentoring, and team cohesion all decline. This is particularly damaging for younger staff, who often learn by observing experienced colleagues solve problems in real time. For example, a new employee may receive formal instructions online yet still miss the quick advice that would naturally be available in a shared office. A second drawback is that home working can erase the boundary between work and private life. Because the laptop is always nearby, some people keep checking messages late into the evening. A manager who replies to emails after dinner every night, for example, may gradually slip into fatigue and burnout instead of enjoying genuine flexibility.","chinese":"然而，這種趨勢也有明顯缺點，尤其是在社交連結和個人界線方面。 第一個問題是職場中的孤立感。 當大部分互動都透過螢幕進行時，自發性的交流、非正式指導以及團隊凝聚力往往都會下降，這會使員工對同事產生疏離感，並在工作中感到較少支援。 例如，一名新員工雖然可以在線上收到正式指示，但仍然會錯過在共享辦公室中本來能自然獲得的即時建議與支持。 第二個缺點是，在家工作會模糊工作與私人生活之間的界線。 由於電腦和手機總在身邊，有些員工會感到壓力，深夜仍要回覆訊息，結果彈性工作逐漸演變成隨時待命，最終導致疲勞甚至職業倦怠。 例如，一位每天晚飯後仍持續回覆電郵的經理，可能會發現自己根本無法真正放鬆。 因此，儘管遙距工作帶來了自由，它同時也可能削弱職場歸屬感，並助長過度工作。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, working online from home brings real drawbacks, but it remains a positive development overall. While it can reduce face-to-face interaction and encourage overwork, its benefits for well-being and access to employment are more significant.","chinese":"總括而言，在家線上工作的增加確實帶來一些缺點，但整體上仍屬正面發展。 雖然它可能削弱職場中的面對面互動，並模糊私人生活的界線，但它對日常生活質素及就業機會可及性的好處更為重要。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"online home-based work","chinese":"網上在家工作"},{"english":"a normal form of employment","chinese":"一種正常的就業形式"},{"english":"this shift","chinese":"這種轉變"},{"english":"weaken workplace relationships","chinese":"削弱職場關係"},{"english":"workplace relationships","chinese":"職場關係"},{"english":"blur personal boundaries","chinese":"模糊個人界線"},{"english":"personal boundaries","chinese":"個人界線"},{"english":"overall beneficial","chinese":"整體上有益"},{"english":"daily lives","chinese":"日常生活"},{"english":"the labour market","chinese":"勞動市場"},{"english":"more inclusive","chinese":"更具包容性"},{"english":"one clear advantage","chinese":"一個明顯好處"},{"english":"work-life balance","chinese":"工作與生活平衡"},{"english":"long commutes","chinese":"長時間通勤"},{"english":"recover time for","chinese":"騰回時間給"},{"english":"childcare","chinese":"照顧子女"},{"english":"a calmer start to the day","chinese":"一天較平靜的開始"},{"english":"time pressure","chinese":"時間壓力"},{"english":"better concentration","chinese":"更佳專注力"},{"english":"productivity may also rise","chinese":"生產力也可能上升"},{"english":"spend two hours commuting","chinese":"花兩小時通勤"},{"english":"prepare meals at home","chinese":"在家準備膳食"},{"english":"in a far better frame of mind","chinese":"以好得多的心情"},{"english":"broader access to jobs","chinese":"更廣泛的就業機會"},{"english":"location matters less","chinese":"地點變得不那麼重要"},{"english":"hire talent from rural areas","chinese":"聘請來自鄉郊地區的人才"},{"english":"limited mobility","chinese":"行動能力有限"},{"english":"apply for roles","chinese":"申請職位"},{"english":"beyond their reach","chinese":"以往難以接觸到"},{"english":"a city-based company","chinese":"以城市為基地的公司"},{"english":"employ a skilled programmer","chinese":"聘用熟練的程式員"},{"english":"hundreds of kilometres away","chinese":"數百公里之外"},{"english":"this trend","chinese":"這個趨勢"},{"english":"social and professional isolation","chinese":"社交和專業上的孤立"},{"english":"communication happens mainly through screens","chinese":"溝通主要透過屏幕進行"},{"english":"spontaneous conversations","chinese":"自然發生的交談"},{"english":"informal mentoring","chinese":"非正式指導"},{"english":"team cohesion","chinese":"團隊凝聚力"},{"english":"particularly damaging for","chinese":"對……尤其有害"},{"english":"younger staff","chinese":"年輕職員"},{"english":"learn by observing","chinese":"透過觀察學習"},{"english":"experienced colleagues","chinese":"有經驗的同事"},{"english":"solve problems in real time","chinese":"即時解決問題"},{"english":"formal instructions","chinese":"正式指示"},{"english":"quick advice","chinese":"即時的小建議"},{"english":"naturally be available","chinese":"自然會有"},{"english":"a shared office","chinese":"共用辦公室"},{"english":"a second drawback","chinese":"第二個缺點"},{"english":"erase the boundary between","chinese":"抹走……之間的界線"},{"english":"private life","chinese":"私人生活"},{"english":"always nearby","chinese":"總是在身邊"},{"english":"keep checking messages","chinese":"不停查看訊息"},{"english":"late into the evening","chinese":"直到深夜"},{"english":"reply to emails after dinner","chinese":"晚飯後回覆電郵"},{"english":"gradually slip into","chinese":"逐漸陷入"},{"english":"fatigue and burnout","chinese":"疲勞和職業倦怠"},{"english":"genuine flexibility","chinese":"真正的彈性"},{"english":"working online from home","chinese":"網上在家工作"},{"english":"real drawbacks","chinese":"真正的缺點"},{"english":"a positive development overall","chinese":"整體而言是正面的發展"},{"english":"face-to-face interaction","chinese":"面對面互動"},{"english":"encourage overwork","chinese":"鼓勵過度工作"},{"english":"well-being","chinese":"身心健康"},{"english":"access to employment","chinese":"就業機會"},{"english":"more significant","chinese":"更重要"}]},"model-essay-30-ielts-direct-question":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-30-ielts-direct-question","essayKey":"direct-question:30","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-30-ielts-direct-question","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/direct-question/EdmundBd9Dir-Q30","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"With populations rising, governments must decide whether to expand current urban areas or create entirely new settlements in rural regions. In my view, new housing should be concentrated in existing cities, because this uses public infrastructure more efficiently and protects the countryside from unnecessary damage.","chinese":"隨著人口上升，各國政府必須決定是擴展現有城市地區，還是在鄉郊地區建立全新的聚居地。 在我看來，新住房應該集中建於現有城市之中，因為這能更有效地使用公共基礎設施，並保護鄉郊免受不必要的破壞。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"The strongest argument for building in cities is that the basic framework for daily life is already there. Roads, railways, hospitals, schools, water systems and emergency services have usually been established over many decades, so additional homes can be connected to them more quickly and cheaply than homes in a new town. If a government builds a rural settlement from scratch, it must first lay down a whole skeleton of services before families can live there properly. That money could instead be spent on higher-density apartments, upgraded transport links and better public facilities in places where people already work and study. For example, replacing low-rise, underused urban land with well-designed apartment blocks can house thousands of residents without forcing them to commute from distant areas.","chinese":"支持在城市建房最有力的理由是，日常生活所需的基本框架已經存在。 道路、鐵路、醫院、學校、供水系統和緊急服務通常已經經過數十年建立起來，因此新增房屋能比新城鎮中的房屋更快速、更低成本地接駁到這些設施。 如果政府從零開始建設一個鄉郊聚居地，在家庭能夠真正適當地生活之前，它必須先建立一整套服務骨架。 這筆資金反而可以用於在人們已經工作和學習的地方興建更高密度的公寓、改善交通連接，以及提供更好的公共設施。 例如，以設計良好的公寓大樓取代低層且未被充分利用的城市土地，可以容納數以千計的居民，而不必迫使他們從遙遠地區通勤。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"Another reason is that expanding into the countryside often creates long-term social and environmental costs. Rural land is not simply empty space; it may be farmland, woodland, wildlife habitat or part of a local community’s identity. Once it is covered with concrete, it is extremely difficult to restore. New countryside towns can also produce car-dependent lifestyles, because jobs and major services normally remain in the city centre. As a result, residents may spend more time on the road, traffic may increase, and the supposed solution to the housing shortage may create another burden: a larger, more scattered urban footprint.","chinese":"另一個原因是，向鄉郊擴張往往會造成長遠的社會和環境成本。 鄉郊土地並不只是空地；它可能是農田、林地、野生動物棲息地，或者是本地社區身份的一部分。 一旦它被混凝土覆蓋，就極難恢復原狀。 新的鄉郊城鎮也可能造成依賴汽車的生活方式，因為工作機會和主要服務通常仍然留在市中心。 結果，居民可能會花更多時間在路上，交通流量可能會增加，而這個本應解決住房短缺的方案，可能會製造另一種負擔：更大、更分散的城市足跡。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, new homes should be constructed in existing cities rather than in newly built countryside towns. City-based housing makes better use of infrastructure, keeps people close to work and services, and prevents the countryside from being swallowed by poorly planned development.","chinese":"總結來說，新住房應該建於現有城市之中，而不是建於新建的鄉郊城鎮。 以城市為基礎的住房能更好地利用基礎設施，使人們靠近工作和服務，並防止鄉郊被規劃不善的發展所吞噬。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"populations rising","chinese":"人口上升"},{"english":"expand current urban areas","chinese":"擴展現有城市地區"},{"english":"create entirely new settlements","chinese":"建立全新的聚居地"},{"english":"rural regions","chinese":"農村地區；鄉郊地區"},{"english":"new housing","chinese":"新住房"},{"english":"be concentrated in","chinese":"集中於"},{"english":"existing cities","chinese":"現有城市"},{"english":"public infrastructure","chinese":"公共基礎設施"},{"english":"more efficiently","chinese":"更有效率地"},{"english":"protects the countryside from","chinese":"保護郊區免受……影響"},{"english":"unnecessary damage","chinese":"不必要的破壞"},{"english":"the strongest argument for","chinese":"支持……的最有力論點"},{"english":"building in cities","chinese":"在城市興建"},{"english":"the basic framework for","chinese":"……的基本框架"},{"english":"daily life","chinese":"日常生活"},{"english":"emergency services","chinese":"緊急服務"},{"english":"have been established over","chinese":"已經過……建立"},{"english":"over many decades","chinese":"經過數十年"},{"english":"additional homes","chinese":"額外住房"},{"english":"be connected to","chinese":"連接到"},{"english":"more quickly and cheaply","chinese":"更快、更便宜地"},{"english":"a rural settlement","chinese":"農村聚居地"},{"english":"from scratch","chinese":"從零開始"},{"english":"lay down","chinese":"鋪設；建立"},{"english":"a whole skeleton of services","chinese":"一整套基本服務框架"},{"english":"live there properly","chinese":"正常地生活在那裏"},{"english":"instead be spent on","chinese":"反而用於"},{"english":"higher-density apartments","chinese":"高密度住宅"},{"english":"upgraded transport links","chinese":"升級了的交通連接"},{"english":"public facilities","chinese":"公共設施"},{"english":"where people already work and study","chinese":"在人們已經工作和學習的地方"},{"english":"low-rise urban land","chinese":"低矮城市用地"},{"english":"underused urban land","chinese":"使用率低的城市土地"},{"english":"well-designed apartment blocks","chinese":"設計良好的住宅大廈"},{"english":"house thousands of residents","chinese":"容納數千名居民"},{"english":"without forcing them to","chinese":"不用迫使他們"},{"english":"commute from distant areas","chinese":"從遙遠地區通勤"},{"english":"another reason","chinese":"另一個原因"},{"english":"expanding into the countryside","chinese":"向郊區擴展"},{"english":"long-term social and environmental costs","chinese":"長遠社會和環境成本"},{"english":"not simply empty space","chinese":"不只是空地"},{"english":"farmland","chinese":"農地"},{"english":"woodland","chinese":"林地"},{"english":"wildlife habitat","chinese":"野生動物棲息地"},{"english":"local community's identity","chinese":"本地社區身份認同"},{"english":"covered with concrete","chinese":"被混凝土覆蓋"},{"english":"extremely difficult to restore","chinese":"極難恢復"},{"english":"countryside towns","chinese":"郊區新市鎮"},{"english":"car-dependent lifestyles","chinese":"依賴汽車的生活方式"},{"english":"major services","chinese":"主要服務"},{"english":"remain in the city centre","chinese":"留在市中心"},{"english":"as a result","chinese":"結果"},{"english":"spend more time on the road","chinese":"花更多時間在路上"},{"english":"traffic may increase","chinese":"交通流量可能增加"},{"english":"the supposed solution to","chinese":"對……所謂的解決方法"},{"english":"housing shortage","chinese":"住房短缺"},{"english":"create another burden","chinese":"造成另一個負擔"},{"english":"a larger, more scattered urban footprint","chinese":"更大、更分散的城市足跡"},{"english":"be constructed in","chinese":"在……興建"},{"english":"newly built countryside towns","chinese":"新建的郊區城鎮"},{"english":"city-based housing","chinese":"以城市為本的住房"},{"english":"makes better use of","chinese":"更善用"},{"english":"keeps people close to","chinese":"讓人們靠近"},{"english":"work and services","chinese":"工作地點和服務"},{"english":"prevents the countryside from being swallowed by","chinese":"防止郊區被……吞噬"},{"english":"poorly planned development","chinese":"規劃不善的發展"}]},"model-essay-30-ielts-discuss-both-views":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-30-ielts-discuss-both-views","essayKey":"discuss-both-views:30","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-30-ielts-discuss-both-views","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/discuss-both-views-your-opinion/EdmundBd9ExpBth-Q30","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"The rapid growth of digital reading has led some people to argue that e-books will eventually replace printed books, while others believe that traditional books will remain part of human life. This essay will discuss both views, but I strongly believe that paper books will not disappear.","chinese":"數位閱讀的迅速發展，使一些人認為電子書最終會取代印刷書籍，而另一些人則相信傳統書籍仍會是人類生活的一部分。 本文將討論雙方觀點，但我強烈認為紙本書不會消失。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"Those who predict the end of printed books usually focus on convenience. E-books allow readers to store hundreds of titles on one device, download new material instantly, and read almost anywhere without carrying heavy volumes. This is especially useful for students, commuters, and frequent travellers, who may need quick access to several texts at once. Digital books can also be cheaper to produce and distribute because publishers do not need paper, printing machines, warehouses, or physical delivery networks. In this sense, e-books seem like a more efficient tool for a fast-moving society, and it is understandable why some people see them as the natural successor to paper books.","chinese":"那些預測印刷書籍將會終結的人，通常著眼於便利性。 電子書讓讀者能夠在一部裝置中儲存數百本書、即時下載新材料，並且幾乎可以在任何地方閱讀，而不需要攜帶沉重的書本。 這對學生、通勤人士和常旅行的人尤其有用，因為他們可能需要同時快速查閱多份文本 數位書籍在製作和分發方面也可以更便宜，因為出版商不需要紙張、印刷機器、倉庫或實體配送網絡。 從這個角度來看，電子書似乎是一種更適合快速運轉社會的高效工具，因此有些人把它們視為紙本書的自然繼承者，也是可以理解的。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"However, I believe paper books will survive because they offer qualities that digital formats cannot fully replace. A printed book is not merely a container for words; it is also a physical object that many readers value for its texture, weight, appearance, and sense of permanence. Reading from paper can feel calmer and more focused than reading from a screen, particularly for people who already spend long hours using phones and computers. For example, many parents still prefer physical storybooks for children because turning pages together creates a warmer and more memorable experience. Libraries, collectors, bookshops, and schools also help keep printed books alive, as they give books cultural and emotional value beyond simple information.","chinese":"然而，我認為紙本書會繼續存在，因為它們具有數位形式無法完全取代的特質。 一本印刷書不僅僅是文字的載體；它同時也是一件實體物品，許多讀者重視它的質感、重量、外觀和持久感。 與螢幕閱讀相比，紙本閱讀可以讓人感覺更平靜、更專注，尤其是對那些已經長時間使用手機和電腦的人來說。 例如，許多父母仍然更喜歡為孩子選擇實體故事書，因為一起翻頁能創造更溫暖、更難忘的體驗。 圖書館、收藏者、書店和學校也有助於讓印刷書籍繼續存在，因為它們賦予書本超越單純資訊的文化和情感價值。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, e-books will continue to grow because they are practical, affordable, and highly accessible. Nevertheless, paper books will not vanish. Their physical presence, reading comfort, and cultural meaning will continue to protect their place in society.","chinese":"總結來說，電子書會繼續發展，因為它們實用、價格較低，而且非常容易取得。 然而，紙本書不會消失。 它們的實體存在、閱讀舒適感和文化意義，將會繼續保護它們在社會中的位置。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"rapid growth","chinese":"快速增長"},{"english":"digital reading","chinese":"數碼閱讀"},{"english":"has led some people to argue that","chinese":"令一些人認為……"},{"english":"e-books","chinese":"電子書"},{"english":"eventually replace","chinese":"最終取代"},{"english":"printed books","chinese":"紙本書"},{"english":"traditional books","chinese":"傳統書籍"},{"english":"remain part of human life","chinese":"仍然是人類生活的一部分"},{"english":"discuss both views","chinese":"討論雙方觀點"},{"english":"strongly believe that","chinese":"強烈相信……"},{"english":"paper books will not disappear","chinese":"紙本書不會消失"},{"english":"predict the end of","chinese":"預測……的終結"},{"english":"focus on convenience","chinese":"集中於方便性"},{"english":"allow readers to","chinese":"讓讀者可以……"},{"english":"store hundreds of titles","chinese":"儲存數百本書"},{"english":"on one device","chinese":"在一部裝置上"},{"english":"download new material instantly","chinese":"即時下載新內容"},{"english":"read almost anywhere","chinese":"幾乎在任何地方閱讀"},{"english":"carrying heavy volumes","chinese":"攜帶厚重書冊"},{"english":"especially useful for","chinese":"對……尤其有用"},{"english":"quick access to","chinese":"快速取得……"},{"english":"several texts at once","chinese":"同時幾份文本"},{"english":"cheaper to produce and distribute","chinese":"製作和分發成本較低"},{"english":"physical delivery networks","chinese":"實體配送網絡"},{"english":"in this sense","chinese":"從這個意義上說"},{"english":"a more efficient tool","chinese":"更有效率的工具"},{"english":"fast-moving society","chinese":"快速變動的社會"},{"english":"understandable why","chinese":"可以理解為甚麼"},{"english":"natural successor to","chinese":"自然繼承者；自然取代者"},{"english":"fully replace","chinese":"完全取代"},{"english":"not merely a container for words","chinese":"不只是文字容器"},{"english":"physical object","chinese":"實體物件"},{"english":"sense of permanence","chinese":"持久感；長存感"},{"english":"feel calmer and more focused","chinese":"感覺更平靜和更專注"},{"english":"spend long hours using","chinese":"長時間使用……"},{"english":"physical storybooks","chinese":"實體故事書"},{"english":"turning pages together","chinese":"一起翻頁"},{"english":"warmer and more memorable experience","chinese":"更溫暖和更難忘的經驗"},{"english":"keep printed books alive","chinese":"令紙本書繼續存在；保持紙本書生命力"},{"english":"cultural and emotional value","chinese":"文化和情感價值"},{"english":"beyond simple information","chinese":"超越簡單資訊"},{"english":"continue to grow","chinese":"繼續增長"},{"english":"practical, affordable, and highly accessible","chinese":"實用、可負擔且高度容易取得"},{"english":"will not vanish","chinese":"不會消失"},{"english":"physical presence","chinese":"實體存在"},{"english":"reading comfort","chinese":"閱讀舒適感"},{"english":"cultural meaning","chinese":"文化意義"},{"english":"protect their place in society","chinese":"保護它們在社會中的位置"}]},"model-essay-30-ielts-opinion":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-30-ielts-opinion","essayKey":"opinion:30","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-30-ielts-opinion","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/opinions/EdmundBd9OP-Q30","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"Public safety depends heavily on the quality of a country’s police force. Some people argue that women should be excluded from this profession, perhaps because policing is often seen as physically demanding. I strongly disagree with this view, as police work should be based on ability rather than gender, and female officers can make law enforcement more effective.","chinese":"公共安全在很大程度上取決於一個國家警隊的質素。 有些人認為女性應該被排除在這個職業之外，或許是因為警務工作經常被視為對體能要求很高。 我強烈不同意這種看法，因為警務工作應該以能力而不是性別為基礎，而且女性警員可以使執法工作更加有效。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"The first reason is that policing requires far more than physical strength. Although officers may sometimes need to arrest suspects or respond to dangerous situations, much of their daily work involves communication, judgment, patience, and emotional control. These qualities are not limited to men. If a woman can pass the same physical, psychological, and professional training as a man, there is no fair reason to prevent her from wearing the uniform. For example, many police duties involve interviewing witnesses, calming angry members of the public, investigating crimes, or writing accurate reports. In these situations, a clear mind and a steady voice may matter more than brute force. Excluding women simply because of their gender would therefore waste valuable talent and weaken the police force.","chinese":"第一個原因是，警務工作所需要的遠遠不只是體力。 儘管警員有時可能需要拘捕疑犯或應對危險情況，但他們大部分日常工作都涉及溝通、判斷、耐性和情緒控制。 這些特質並不限於男性。 如果一名女性能夠通過與男性相同的體能、心理和專業訓練，那麼便沒有公平的理由阻止她穿上制服。 例如，許多警務職責包括訪問證人、安撫憤怒的市民、調查罪案，或撰寫準確的報告。 在這些情況下，清晰的頭腦和沉穩的聲音可能比蠻力更加重要。 因此，單純因為性別而排除女性，會浪費寶貴的人才，並削弱警隊的力量。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"Another important point is that female officers can improve public trust, especially when dealing with vulnerable people. Victims of domestic violence, sexual assault, or child abuse may feel safer speaking to a female officer, particularly if they are frightened, embarrassed, or traumatised. In such cases, the presence of women in the police force is not symbolic; it can directly affect whether victims are willing to report crimes and cooperate with investigations. A police force that includes both men and women is also more likely to reflect the community it serves, which makes it appear fairer, more approachable, and more human.","chinese":"另一個重要觀點是，女性警員能夠提升公眾信任，尤其是在處理弱勢人士的案件時。 家庭暴力、性侵犯或虐待兒童的受害者，在與女性警員交談時可能會感到更安全，尤其是當他們感到害怕、尷尬或受到創傷時。 在這些情況下，女性在警隊中的存在並不只是象徵性的；它可以直接影響受害者是否願意報案並配合調查。 一支同時包含男性和女性的警隊，也更有可能反映它所服務的社區，這會令它看起來更公平、更容易接近，也更有人性。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, I completely disagree that women should be barred from police work. The badge should belong to those who are trained, capable, and committed, not only to those who fit an outdated stereotype. A stronger police force is one that welcomes ability wherever it is found.","chinese":"總結來說，我完全不同意女性應該被禁止從事警務工作。 警徽應該屬於那些受過訓練、有能力並且有承擔的人，而不應只屬於那些符合過時刻板印象的人。 一支更強大的警隊，是一支無論能力來自何處都願意接納的警隊。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"public safety","chinese":"公共安全"},{"english":"depends heavily on","chinese":"很大程度上取決於"},{"english":"police force","chinese":"警隊"},{"english":"be excluded from","chinese":"被排除於……之外"},{"english":"this profession","chinese":"這個職業"},{"english":"policing","chinese":"警務工作"},{"english":"be seen as","chinese":"被視為"},{"english":"physically demanding","chinese":"體力要求高的"},{"english":"strongly disagree with","chinese":"強烈不同意……"},{"english":"police work","chinese":"警務工作"},{"english":"be based on","chinese":"建基於"},{"english":"ability rather than gender","chinese":"能力而不是性別"},{"english":"female officers","chinese":"女性警務人員"},{"english":"law enforcement","chinese":"執法"},{"english":"more effective","chinese":"更有效"},{"english":"far more than","chinese":"遠不止"},{"english":"physical strength","chinese":"體力"},{"english":"arrest suspects","chinese":"拘捕疑犯"},{"english":"respond to dangerous situations","chinese":"應對危險情況"},{"english":"daily work","chinese":"日常工作"},{"english":"involves communication","chinese":"涉及溝通"},{"english":"judgment","chinese":"判斷力"},{"english":"emotional control","chinese":"情緒控制"},{"english":"be limited to","chinese":"局限於"},{"english":"pass the same training","chinese":"通過相同訓練"},{"english":"physical, psychological, and professional training","chinese":"體能、心理和專業訓練"},{"english":"fair reason to","chinese":"合理理由去……"},{"english":"prevent her from","chinese":"阻止她……"},{"english":"wearing the uniform","chinese":"穿上制服"},{"english":"police duties","chinese":"警務職責"},{"english":"interviewing witnesses","chinese":"訪問證人"},{"english":"calming angry members of the public","chinese":"安撫憤怒的公眾人士"},{"english":"investigating crimes","chinese":"調查罪案"},{"english":"accurate reports","chinese":"準確報告"},{"english":"in these situations","chinese":"在這些情況下"},{"english":"clear mind","chinese":"清晰頭腦"},{"english":"steady voice","chinese":"沉穩的聲音"},{"english":"matter more than","chinese":"比……更重要"},{"english":"brute force","chinese":"蠻力"},{"english":"simply because of","chinese":"只是因為"},{"english":"gender","chinese":"性別"},{"english":"waste valuable talent","chinese":"浪費寶貴人才"},{"english":"weaken the police force","chinese":"削弱警隊"},{"english":"public trust","chinese":"公眾信任"},{"english":"especially when dealing with","chinese":"尤其在處理……時"},{"english":"vulnerable people","chinese":"弱勢人士"},{"english":"victims of domestic violence","chinese":"家庭暴力受害者"},{"english":"sexual assault","chinese":"性侵犯"},{"english":"child abuse","chinese":"虐兒"},{"english":"feel safer speaking to","chinese":"與……交談時感到更安全"},{"english":"particularly if","chinese":"特別是如果"},{"english":"frightened, embarrassed, or traumatised","chinese":"受驚、尷尬或受創"},{"english":"in such cases","chinese":"在這些情況下"},{"english":"presence of women","chinese":"女性的存在"},{"english":"not symbolic","chinese":"不是象徵性的"},{"english":"directly affect whether","chinese":"直接影響是否……"},{"english":"be willing to","chinese":"願意去……"},{"english":"report crimes","chinese":"報案"},{"english":"cooperate with investigations","chinese":"配合調查"},{"english":"includes both men and women","chinese":"包括男性和女性"},{"english":"reflect the community it serves","chinese":"反映它所服務的社區"},{"english":"appear fairer","chinese":"顯得更公平"},{"english":"more approachable","chinese":"更親民；更容易接近"},{"english":"more human","chinese":"更有人情味"},{"english":"be barred from","chinese":"被禁止從事……"},{"english":"the badge","chinese":"警徽"},{"english":"trained, capable, and committed","chinese":"受過訓練、有能力和有承擔"},{"english":"fit an outdated stereotype","chinese":"符合過時的刻板印象"},{"english":"outdated stereotype","chinese":"過時的刻板印象"},{"english":"welcomes ability","chinese":"歡迎有能力的人才"},{"english":"wherever it is found","chinese":"無論能力出現在哪裏"}]},"model-essay-31-ielts-direct-question":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-31-ielts-direct-question","essayKey":"direct-question:31","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-31-ielts-direct-question","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/direct-question/EdmundBd9Dir-Q31","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"It is increasingly common for workplaces and educational buildings to be designed around large shared areas rather than separate rooms. This trend is mainly driven by the need for greater flexibility and closer interaction. I regard it as a positive development because, when planned properly, open spaces can make institutions more cooperative, adaptable and efficient.","chinese":"工作場所和教育建築越來越常以大型共享空間為核心來設計，而不是採用一間間獨立房間的形式。 這種趨勢主要是由於人們需要更高的靈活性和更緊密的互動。 我認為這是一種正面的發展，因為如果規劃得當，開放式空間可以使機構更具合作性、適應性和效率。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"The first reason behind this design choice is practical. Modern offices and schools rarely use rooms for one fixed purpose throughout the day. An open area can be rearranged quickly for group projects, staff meetings, presentations or independent work, whereas a building divided into many small rooms is much harder to adapt. In a school, for example, one large learning space can allow several classes to work on a science project together, with teachers moving freely between groups. In an office, the same logic applies: teams can form, separate and reform as projects change. This saves space and prevents buildings from becoming a maze of underused rooms.","chinese":"這種設計選擇背後的第一個原因是實用性。 現代辦公室和學校很少會整天只把房間用於一個固定用途。 開放式區域可以迅速重新安排，用於小組項目、員工會議、簡報或獨立工作；相反，一座被分割成許多小房間的建築則更難適應不同需要。 例如，在學校裡，一個大型學習空間可以讓幾個班級一起進行科學項目，而老師也能在不同小組之間自由走動。 在辦公室裡，同樣的道理也適用：團隊可以隨著項目變化而組成、分開，再重新組合。 這樣可以節省空間，並防止建築變成一個由大量使用不足房間組成的迷宮。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"I also see this as positive because open-plan buildings encourage communication. In many traditional offices, employees can become isolated behind closed doors, which slows down problem-solving and weakens team spirit. Similarly, in schools, students who learn only in sealed classrooms may have fewer chances to collaborate with classmates from other groups. Open spaces create more natural contact: people can ask quick questions, observe how others work and share ideas without turning every conversation into a formal meeting. This does not simply make a building look modern; it changes the rhythm of daily work and study.","chinese":"我也認為這是正面的，因為開放式建築能促進溝通。 在許多傳統辦公室裡，員工可能會被封閉的門隔離起來，這會減慢解決問題的速度，並削弱團隊精神。 同樣地，在學校裡，如果學生只在封閉課室中學習，他們與其他小組同學合作的機會可能會更少。 開放式空間能創造更自然的接觸：人們可以快速提問、觀察別人的工作方式，並分享想法，而不必把每一次交流都變成正式會議。 這不只是讓建築看起來現代化；它改變了日常工作和學習的節奏。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"Some noise and distraction are possible, but these can be reduced through quiet zones, movable partitions and sensible rules. The core idea remains sound. Overall, open-plan design is popular because it makes buildings more flexible, and I believe it is a positive development because it encourages collaboration and makes better use of space.","chinese":"一些噪音和干擾確實可能出現，但這些問題可以透過安靜區域、可移動隔板和合理規則來減少。 其核心理念仍然是合理的。 整體而言，開放式設計之所以受歡迎，是因為它使建築更具靈活性；而我認為這是一種正面的發展，因為它鼓勵合作，並能更有效地利用空間。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"increasingly common","chinese":"越來越普遍"},{"english":"workplaces and educational buildings","chinese":"工作場所和教育建築物"},{"english":"be designed around","chinese":"圍繞……設計"},{"english":"large shared areas","chinese":"大型共用空間"},{"english":"rather than separate rooms","chinese":"而不是獨立房間"},{"english":"mainly driven by","chinese":"主要由……推動"},{"english":"greater flexibility","chinese":"更大的靈活性"},{"english":"closer interaction","chinese":"更緊密的互動"},{"english":"regard it as","chinese":"把它視為"},{"english":"a positive development","chinese":"正面發展"},{"english":"when planned properly","chinese":"在妥善規劃下"},{"english":"more cooperative, adaptable and efficient","chinese":"更合作、更靈活、更高效"},{"english":"the first reason behind","chinese":"……背後的第一個原因"},{"english":"design choice","chinese":"設計選擇"},{"english":"for one fixed purpose","chinese":"作單一固定用途"},{"english":"throughout the day","chinese":"一整天"},{"english":"be rearranged quickly","chinese":"可快速重新安排"},{"english":"group projects","chinese":"小組項目"},{"english":"staff meetings","chinese":"員工會議"},{"english":"presentations","chinese":"匯報；簡報"},{"english":"independent work","chinese":"獨立工作"},{"english":"divided into","chinese":"被分成"},{"english":"much harder to adapt","chinese":"更難適應改變"},{"english":"learning space","chinese":"學習空間"},{"english":"allow several classes to","chinese":"讓幾個班級可以"},{"english":"work on a science project","chinese":"進行科學項目"},{"english":"moving freely between","chinese":"在……之間自由走動"},{"english":"the same logic applies","chinese":"同樣道理適用"},{"english":"teams can form, separate and reform","chinese":"團隊可以組成、分開再重組"},{"english":"as projects change","chinese":"隨着項目改變"},{"english":"saves space","chinese":"節省空間"},{"english":"prevents buildings from becoming","chinese":"防止建築物變成"},{"english":"a maze of","chinese":"一個由……組成的迷宮"},{"english":"underused rooms","chinese":"使用率低的房間"},{"english":"open-plan buildings","chinese":"開放式建築"},{"english":"encourage communication","chinese":"促進溝通"},{"english":"traditional offices","chinese":"傳統辦公室"},{"english":"become isolated behind closed doors","chinese":"在關上的門後變得孤立"},{"english":"slows down problem-solving","chinese":"拖慢解難"},{"english":"weakens team spirit","chinese":"削弱團隊精神"},{"english":"similarly","chinese":"同樣地"},{"english":"sealed classrooms","chinese":"封閉課室"},{"english":"have fewer chances to","chinese":"有較少機會去"},{"english":"collaborate with","chinese":"與……合作"},{"english":"classmates from other groups","chinese":"其他組別的同學"},{"english":"create more natural contact","chinese":"創造更自然的接觸"},{"english":"ask quick questions","chinese":"快速提問"},{"english":"observe how others work","chinese":"觀察其他人如何工作"},{"english":"share ideas","chinese":"分享想法"},{"english":"without turning every conversation into","chinese":"不用把每次對話都變成"},{"english":"a formal meeting","chinese":"正式會議"},{"english":"does not simply make","chinese":"不只是令……"},{"english":"look modern","chinese":"看起來現代化"},{"english":"changes the rhythm of","chinese":"改變……的節奏"},{"english":"daily work and study","chinese":"日常工作和學習"},{"english":"noise and distraction","chinese":"噪音和分心"},{"english":"be reduced through","chinese":"可透過……減少"},{"english":"quiet zones","chinese":"安靜區"},{"english":"movable partitions","chinese":"可移動間隔板"},{"english":"sensible rules","chinese":"合理規則"},{"english":"the core idea remains sound","chinese":"核心理念仍然合理"},{"english":"overall","chinese":"整體而言"},{"english":"makes buildings more flexible","chinese":"令建築物更靈活"},{"english":"encourages collaboration","chinese":"鼓勵協作"},{"english":"makes better use of space","chinese":"更善用空間"}]},"model-essay-31-ielts-discuss-both-views":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-31-ielts-discuss-both-views","essayKey":"discuss-both-views:31","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-31-ielts-discuss-both-views","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/discuss-both-views-your-opinion/EdmundBd9ExpBth-Q31","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"International organisations often support poorer nations as they try to improve infrastructure, education and public services. While some believe that money is the most useful form of assistance, others argue that practical support and expert guidance matter more. This essay will discuss both views and argue that practical aid and advice are more valuable because they help countries use resources effectively and become less dependent on donors.","chinese":"國際組織經常在較貧困國家嘗試改善基礎建設、教育和公共服務時提供支持。 雖然有些人認為金錢是最有用的援助形式，但另一些人則主張實際支援和專家指導更為重要。 本文將討論雙方觀點，並主張實際援助和建議更有價值，因為它們能幫助國家有效使用資源，並減少對捐助者的依賴。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"On the one hand, financial aid can be essential, especially when a country lacks the basic capital needed to start development projects. Without immediate funding, governments may be unable to build roads, supply clean water, buy medical equipment or keep schools open. For example, after a natural disaster or during a food shortage, direct financial assistance can help authorities respond quickly and prevent a temporary crisis from becoming a national catastrophe. Money also gives local leaders some flexibility because they can allocate it according to urgent domestic needs. Therefore, it is understandable why many people see financial aid as the foundation of development.","chinese":"一方面，財政援助可能是必不可少的，尤其當一個國家缺乏啟動發展項目所需的基本資金時。 如果沒有即時資金，政府可能無法修建道路、供應清潔食水、購買醫療設備，或維持學校運作。 例如，在自然災害之後，或糧食短缺期間，直接的財政援助可以幫助當局迅速應對，並防止一場暫時性的危機演變成全國性的災難。 金錢也能給予本地領導者一定的靈活性，因為他們可以根據國內的緊急需要分配資金。 因此，很多人把財政援助視為發展的基礎，是可以理解的。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"On the other hand, practical aid and professional advice are often more important in the long term. The main problem with money alone is that it can be wasted, mismanaged or spent on short-term solutions if a country does not have the skills and systems to use it well. By contrast, training doctors, advising farmers, improving public administration and helping engineers design reliable infrastructure can create capacity that remains after foreign donors leave. For instance, teaching local agricultural workers how to improve irrigation may raise food production year after year, whereas a cash donation may disappear within months. In this sense, practical support acts like a bridge towards self-reliance rather than a lifeline that must be constantly replaced.","chinese":"另一方面，從長遠來看，實際援助和專業建議往往更加重要。 單靠金錢的主要問題在於，如果一個國家沒有善用資金所需的技能和制度，金錢可能會被浪費、管理不善，或被花在短期解決方案上。 相比之下，培訓醫生、指導農民、改善公共行政，以及幫助工程師設計可靠的基礎建設，都能建立一種即使外國捐助者離開後仍然存在的能力。 例如，教導本地農業工作者如何改善灌溉，可能會年復一年地提高糧食產量，而一筆現金捐款則可能在數月內便消耗殆盡。 從這個意義上說，實際支援就像一座通往自力更生的橋，而不是一條必須不斷更換的救生索。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, financial aid is certainly useful for urgent needs and basic investment. However, I believe practical aid and advice are more important because they build knowledge, strengthen institutions and help developing countries stand on their own feet.","chinese":"總結來說，財政援助對於緊急需要和基本投資當然是有用的。 然而，我認為實際援助和建議更加重要，因為它們能建立知識、強化制度，並幫助發展中國家靠自己的力量站穩腳步。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"international organisations","chinese":"國際組織"},{"english":"support poorer nations","chinese":"支援較貧窮國家"},{"english":"improve infrastructure","chinese":"改善基建"},{"english":"public services","chinese":"公共服務"},{"english":"the most useful form of assistance","chinese":"最有用的援助形式"},{"english":"practical support","chinese":"實際支援"},{"english":"expert guidance","chinese":"專家指導"},{"english":"matter more","chinese":"更重要"},{"english":"discuss both views","chinese":"討論雙方觀點"},{"english":"practical aid and advice","chinese":"實際援助和建議"},{"english":"use resources effectively","chinese":"有效運用資源"},{"english":"become less dependent on","chinese":"減少對……的依賴"},{"english":"donors","chinese":"捐助者"},{"english":"on the one hand","chinese":"一方面"},{"english":"financial aid","chinese":"財政援助"},{"english":"be essential","chinese":"是必要的"},{"english":"especially when","chinese":"尤其當"},{"english":"lack the basic capital needed to","chinese":"缺乏……所需的基本資金"},{"english":"start development projects","chinese":"開展發展項目"},{"english":"immediate funding","chinese":"即時資金"},{"english":"be unable to","chinese":"無法"},{"english":"supply clean water","chinese":"供應清潔食水"},{"english":"buy medical equipment","chinese":"購買醫療設備"},{"english":"keep schools open","chinese":"維持學校運作"},{"english":"a natural disaster","chinese":"自然災害"},{"english":"food shortage","chinese":"糧食短缺"},{"english":"direct financial assistance","chinese":"直接財政援助"},{"english":"authorities","chinese":"當局"},{"english":"respond quickly","chinese":"快速應對"},{"english":"prevent a temporary crisis from becoming","chinese":"防止暫時危機變成"},{"english":"a national catastrophe","chinese":"全國性災難"},{"english":"local leaders","chinese":"本地領袖"},{"english":"give ... some flexibility","chinese":"給予……一定靈活性"},{"english":"allocate it according to","chinese":"按照……分配"},{"english":"urgent domestic needs","chinese":"迫切的國內需要"},{"english":"financial aid as the foundation of development","chinese":"將財政援助視為發展基礎"},{"english":"the foundation of development","chinese":"發展的基礎"},{"english":"on the other hand","chinese":"另一方面"},{"english":"professional advice","chinese":"專業建議"},{"english":"in the long term","chinese":"長遠而言"},{"english":"the main problem with","chinese":"……的主要問題"},{"english":"money alone","chinese":"單靠金錢"},{"english":"be wasted","chinese":"被浪費"},{"english":"mismanaged","chinese":"管理不善"},{"english":"be spent on short-term solutions","chinese":"被花在短期解決方法上"},{"english":"short-term solutions","chinese":"短期解決方法"},{"english":"skills and systems","chinese":"技能和制度"},{"english":"use it well","chinese":"妥善運用它"},{"english":"by contrast","chinese":"相反"},{"english":"training doctors","chinese":"培訓醫生"},{"english":"advising farmers","chinese":"指導農民"},{"english":"improving public administration","chinese":"改善公共行政"},{"english":"public administration","chinese":"公共行政"},{"english":"design reliable infrastructure","chinese":"設計可靠基建"},{"english":"create capacity","chinese":"建立能力"},{"english":"remains after foreign donors leave","chinese":"在外國捐助者離開後仍然保留"},{"english":"foreign donors","chinese":"外國捐助者"},{"english":"local agricultural workers","chinese":"本地農業工人"},{"english":"improve irrigation","chinese":"改善灌溉"},{"english":"raise food production","chinese":"提高糧食產量"},{"english":"year after year","chinese":"年復一年"},{"english":"a cash donation","chinese":"現金捐款"},{"english":"disappear within months","chinese":"在數月內用完"},{"english":"in this sense","chinese":"從這個意義上說"},{"english":"act like a bridge towards","chinese":"像通往……的橋樑"},{"english":"self-reliance","chinese":"自力更生"},{"english":"rather than a lifeline","chinese":"而不是救命索"},{"english":"be constantly replaced","chinese":"需要不斷被取代"},{"english":"urgent needs","chinese":"迫切需要"},{"english":"basic investment","chinese":"基本投資"},{"english":"build knowledge","chinese":"建立知識"},{"english":"strengthen institutions","chinese":"加強制度；強化機構"},{"english":"developing countries","chinese":"發展中國家"},{"english":"stand on their own feet","chinese":"自立；靠自己站穩"}]},"model-essay-31-ielts-opinion":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-31-ielts-opinion","essayKey":"opinion:31","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-31-ielts-opinion","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/opinions/EdmundBd9OP-Q31","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"The criminal justice system should protect society, but it should also punish offenders in a way that is proportionate and useful. I completely agree that some convicted offenders, particularly those who have committed non-violent or low-level crimes, should be required to do unpaid community work rather than be sent to prison.","chinese":"刑事司法制度應該保護社會，但它也應該以合乎比例並且有實際作用的方式懲罰違法者。 我完全同意，有些被定罪的罪犯，尤其是那些犯下非暴力或低層次罪行的人，應該被要求從事無薪社區工作，而不是被送進監獄。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"The strongest argument for this approach is that community service turns punishment into direct repayment. When an offender cleans public parks, repairs community facilities, or supports local charities, the penalty is not merely symbolic; it visibly gives something back to the society that was harmed. This can be more meaningful than locking a minor offender in a cell, where the public receives little benefit and the offender may simply become isolated and resentful. Community work also forces offenders to confront the practical consequences of wrongdoing. Instead of disappearing behind prison walls, they are made to spend time and effort repairing, at least in a modest way, the damage caused by antisocial behaviour. This makes the punishment both corrective and constructive.","chinese":"支持這種做法最有力的論點是，社區服務能把懲罰轉化為直接的補償。 當一名罪犯清潔公共公園、維修社區設施，或支援本地慈善機構時，這種懲罰就不只是象徵性的；它明顯地把一些東西回饋給受害的社會。 這可能比把一名輕微罪犯關進牢房更有意義，因為在監獄中，公眾幾乎得不到實際好處，而罪犯也可能只是變得孤立和怨恨。 社區工作也迫使罪犯面對違法行為所帶來的實際後果。 他們不是消失在監獄高牆之後，而是被要求花時間和精力，以至少較有限但實際的方式，修補反社會行為造成的損害。 這使懲罰既具有糾正作用，也具有建設性。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"Another reason is that prison can be a blunt tool for people who are not genuinely dangerous. Minor offenders who enter prison may lose their jobs, damage family relationships, and mix with more serious criminals. As a result, a short sentence can become a trapdoor rather than a turning point. By contrast, unpaid work allows suitable offenders to remain under supervision while still keeping some connection with normal life. For example, someone convicted of minor theft could be ordered to complete months of supervised work in public spaces. That sentence would still be unpleasant and demanding, but it would be less likely to destroy the person’s chance of rehabilitation.","chinese":"另一個原因是，對於那些並非真正危險的人而言，監獄可能是一種過於粗糙的工具。 進入監獄的輕微罪犯可能會失去工作、破壞家庭關係，並與更嚴重的罪犯混在一起。 結果是，一段短期刑期可能會變成一個陷阱，而不是人生的轉捩點。 相比之下，無薪工作讓合適的罪犯仍然受到監管，同時保持與正常生活的一定連繫。 例如，一名因輕微盜竊而被定罪的人，可以被命令在公共空間完成數個月受監督的工作 這種刑罰仍然會令人不快，而且要求甚高，但它較不可能摧毀這個人改過自新的機會。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, I fully agree that certain prisoners should do unpaid community work instead of being put behind bars. For non-dangerous offenders, it is a fairer, more useful, and more socially productive form of punishment.","chinese":"總結來說，我完全同意，某些囚犯應該從事無薪社區工作，而不是被關進監獄。 對於非危險罪犯而言，這是一種更公平、更有用，也更能為社會帶來成效的懲罰方式。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"criminal justice system","chinese":"刑事司法制度"},{"english":"protect society","chinese":"保護社會"},{"english":"punish offenders","chinese":"懲罰犯事者"},{"english":"proportionate and useful","chinese":"合乎比例而有用"},{"english":"convicted offenders","chinese":"被定罪的犯事者"},{"english":"non-violent crimes","chinese":"非暴力罪行"},{"english":"low-level crimes","chinese":"輕微罪行"},{"english":"be required to","chinese":"被要求去……"},{"english":"unpaid community work","chinese":"無薪社區工作"},{"english":"rather than be sent to prison","chinese":"而不是被送入監獄"},{"english":"the strongest argument for","chinese":"支持……的最有力論點"},{"english":"community service","chinese":"社區服務"},{"english":"turn punishment into","chinese":"將懲罰變成……"},{"english":"direct repayment","chinese":"直接補償"},{"english":"cleans public parks","chinese":"清潔公共公園"},{"english":"repairs community facilities","chinese":"維修社區設施"},{"english":"supports local charities","chinese":"支援本地慈善機構"},{"english":"the penalty","chinese":"懲罰；刑罰"},{"english":"merely symbolic","chinese":"只是象徵性的"},{"english":"visibly gives something back to","chinese":"明顯地回饋……"},{"english":"the society that was harmed","chinese":"受到傷害的社會"},{"english":"meaningful","chinese":"有意義的"},{"english":"locking a minor offender in a cell","chinese":"將輕微犯事者關進囚室"},{"english":"minor offender","chinese":"輕微犯事者"},{"english":"little benefit","chinese":"很少好處"},{"english":"isolated and resentful","chinese":"孤立和怨恨"},{"english":"confront the practical consequences of","chinese":"面對……的實際後果"},{"english":"wrongdoing","chinese":"不當行為"},{"english":"disappearing behind prison walls","chinese":"消失在監獄高牆後"},{"english":"be made to spend","chinese":"被安排花時間去……"},{"english":"time and effort","chinese":"時間和精力"},{"english":"at least in a modest way","chinese":"至少以有限但實際的方式"},{"english":"damage caused by","chinese":"由……造成的傷害"},{"english":"antisocial behaviour","chinese":"反社會行為"},{"english":"corrective and constructive","chinese":"具糾正作用和建設性"},{"english":"blunt tool","chinese":"粗糙的工具"},{"english":"genuinely dangerous","chinese":"真正危險"},{"english":"enter prison","chinese":"入獄"},{"english":"lose their jobs","chinese":"失去工作"},{"english":"damage family relationships","chinese":"損害家庭關係"},{"english":"mix with","chinese":"與……混在一起"},{"english":"more serious criminals","chinese":"更嚴重的罪犯"},{"english":"short sentence","chinese":"短期刑期"},{"english":"trapdoor rather than a turning point","chinese":"陷阱，而不是轉折點"},{"english":"suitable offenders","chinese":"合適的犯事者"},{"english":"remain under supervision","chinese":"繼續受到監管"},{"english":"keeping some connection with","chinese":"保持與……的一些聯繫"},{"english":"normal life","chinese":"正常生活"},{"english":"convicted of minor theft","chinese":"因輕微盜竊被定罪"},{"english":"be ordered to complete","chinese":"被命令完成"},{"english":"supervised work","chinese":"受監管工作"},{"english":"public spaces","chinese":"公共空間"},{"english":"unpleasant and demanding","chinese":"令人不快而要求高"},{"english":"be less likely to","chinese":"較不可能"},{"english":"destroy the person's chance of","chinese":"破壞某人……的機會"},{"english":"rehabilitation","chinese":"更生"},{"english":"certain prisoners","chinese":"某些囚犯"},{"english":"put behind bars","chinese":"被關進監獄"},{"english":"non-dangerous offenders","chinese":"非危險犯事者"},{"english":"fairer and more useful","chinese":"更公平和更有用"},{"english":"socially productive","chinese":"對社會更有建設性"},{"english":"form of punishment","chinese":"懲罰形式"}]},"model-essay-32-ielts-direct-question":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-32-ielts-direct-question","essayKey":"direct-question:32","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-32-ielts-direct-question","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/direct-question/EdmundBd9Dir-Q32","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"In a world where people receive information from newspapers, websites and social media, objectivity in news reporting is often regarded as essential. I do not think all news is true, even when it is produced by established media organisations. In my view, the main function of a newspaper is to give citizens reliable information and help them understand matters of public importance.","chinese":"在一個人們從報紙、網站和社交媒體接收資訊的世界裡，新聞報導中的客觀性通常被視為至關重要。 我並不認為所有新聞都是真實的，即使它們是由成熟的媒體機構製作的。 在我看來，報紙的主要功能是向公民提供可靠資訊，並幫助他們理解具有公共重要性的議題。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"Not all news can be considered true because journalism is produced by human beings, and human judgment is never completely neutral. A report may be based on real events, but the choice of headline, sources and images can still shape readers’ interpretation. For example, two newspapers may cover the same protest: one may describe it as a public demand for justice, while another may portray it as a threat to social order. Neither report may be entirely fabricated, but both can guide the reader towards a particular emotional response. In addition, commercial pressure can tempt newspapers to exaggerate stories, simplify complex issues or publish unverified claims in order to attract attention.","chinese":"並非所有新聞都可以被視為真實，因為新聞是由人製作的，而人的判斷從來不可能完全中立。 一篇報導可能以真實事件為基礎，但標題、資料來源和圖片的選擇仍然可以塑造讀者的解讀。 例如，兩份報紙可能報導同一場抗議：其中一份可能把它描述為公眾對公義的訴求，而另一份則可能把它描繪成對社會秩序的威脅。 兩篇報導可能都不是完全捏造的，但它們都可以引導讀者產生某種特定的情緒反應。 此外，商業壓力可能會誘使報紙為了吸引注意力而誇大故事、簡化複雜議題，或刊登未經核實的說法。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"The function of a newspaper, therefore, should be more serious than merely entertaining readers or filling pages. Its first responsibility is to inform the public about events that affect their lives, such as government decisions, economic problems, health warnings and social conflicts. More importantly, a newspaper should act as a public watchdog. By investigating corruption, questioning powerful institutions and presenting evidence clearly, it allows ordinary people to judge whether leaders and organisations are acting responsibly. This is especially important because most citizens cannot personally attend court cases, inspect public spending or interview officials. A responsible newspaper becomes their eyes and ears.","chinese":"因此，報紙的功能應該比單純娛樂讀者或填滿版面更加嚴肅。 它的首要責任是讓公眾了解會影響他們生活的事件，例如政府決策、經濟問題、健康警告和社會衝突。 更重要的是，報紙應該扮演公共監察者的角色。 透過調查貪污、質疑有權勢的機構，以及清楚呈現證據，報紙使普通人能夠判斷領袖和組織是否負責任地行事。 這一點尤其重要，因為大多數公民無法親自出席法庭案件、檢查公共開支或訪問官員。 一份負責任的報紙便成為他們的眼睛和耳朵。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, I do not believe all news is true, since facts can be selected, framed or distorted. However, this is exactly why newspapers matter. Their proper role is to verify information, explain important issues and protect the public from ignorance, manipulation and blind trust.","chinese":"總結來說，我不相信所有新聞都是真實的，因為事實可以被選擇、被框定，甚至被扭曲。 然而，這正正是報紙重要的原因。 它們真正的角色是核實資訊、解釋重要議題，並保護公眾免於無知、操控和盲目信任。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"receive information from","chinese":"從……接收資訊"},{"english":"newspapers, websites and social media","chinese":"報章、網站和社交媒體"},{"english":"objectivity in news reporting","chinese":"新聞報道中的客觀性"},{"english":"be regarded as essential","chinese":"被視為必不可少"},{"english":"all news is true","chinese":"所有新聞都是真實的"},{"english":"established media organisations","chinese":"具規模的媒體機構"},{"english":"in my view","chinese":"在我看來"},{"english":"the main function of","chinese":"……的主要功能"},{"english":"give citizens reliable information","chinese":"向市民提供可靠資訊"},{"english":"matters of public importance","chinese":"具有公共重要性的事情"},{"english":"can be considered true","chinese":"可被視為真實"},{"english":"produced by human beings","chinese":"由人類製作"},{"english":"human judgment","chinese":"人的判斷"},{"english":"completely neutral","chinese":"完全中立"},{"english":"be based on real events","chinese":"建基於真實事件"},{"english":"the choice of headline","chinese":"標題的選擇"},{"english":"sources and images","chinese":"消息來源和圖片"},{"english":"shape readers' interpretation","chinese":"影響讀者的解讀"},{"english":"cover the same protest","chinese":"報道同一場抗議"},{"english":"a public demand for justice","chinese":"公眾對公義的訴求"},{"english":"portray it as","chinese":"將它描繪成"},{"english":"a threat to social order","chinese":"對社會秩序的威脅"},{"english":"entirely fabricated","chinese":"完全捏造"},{"english":"guide the reader towards","chinese":"引導讀者走向"},{"english":"a particular emotional response","chinese":"某種特定情緒反應"},{"english":"in addition","chinese":"此外"},{"english":"commercial pressure","chinese":"商業壓力"},{"english":"tempt newspapers to","chinese":"誘使報章去"},{"english":"exaggerate stories","chinese":"誇大新聞故事"},{"english":"simplify complex issues","chinese":"簡化複雜議題"},{"english":"publish unverified claims","chinese":"發布未經核實的說法"},{"english":"in order to attract attention","chinese":"為了吸引注意"},{"english":"the function of","chinese":"……的功能"},{"english":"more serious than merely","chinese":"比單純……更嚴肅"},{"english":"entertaining readers","chinese":"娛樂讀者"},{"english":"filling pages","chinese":"填滿版面"},{"english":"first responsibility","chinese":"首要責任"},{"english":"inform the public about","chinese":"向公眾告知有關……"},{"english":"affect their lives","chinese":"影響他們的生活"},{"english":"government decisions","chinese":"政府決定"},{"english":"economic problems","chinese":"經濟問題"},{"english":"health warnings","chinese":"健康警告"},{"english":"social conflicts","chinese":"社會衝突"},{"english":"more importantly","chinese":"更重要的是"},{"english":"act as a public watchdog","chinese":"擔當公共監察者"},{"english":"investigating corruption","chinese":"調查貪污"},{"english":"questioning powerful institutions","chinese":"質疑有權勢的機構"},{"english":"presenting evidence clearly","chinese":"清楚呈現證據"},{"english":"ordinary people","chinese":"普通人"},{"english":"judge whether","chinese":"判斷是否"},{"english":"leaders and organisations","chinese":"領袖和機構"},{"english":"acting responsibly","chinese":"負責任地行事"},{"english":"especially important","chinese":"特別重要"},{"english":"attend court cases","chinese":"出席法庭案件"},{"english":"inspect public spending","chinese":"審查公共開支"},{"english":"interview officials","chinese":"訪問官員"},{"english":"becomes their eyes and ears","chinese":"成為他們的眼睛和耳朵"},{"english":"since facts can be selected","chinese":"因為事實可以被選取"},{"english":"framed or distorted","chinese":"被框定或扭曲"},{"english":"this is exactly why","chinese":"這正正是為甚麼"},{"english":"newspapers matter","chinese":"報章很重要"},{"english":"proper role","chinese":"應有角色"},{"english":"verify information","chinese":"核實資料"},{"english":"explain important issues","chinese":"解釋重要議題"},{"english":"protect the public from","chinese":"保護公眾免受……影響"},{"english":"ignorance","chinese":"無知"},{"english":"manipulation","chinese":"操控"},{"english":"blind trust","chinese":"盲目信任"}]},"model-essay-32-ielts-discuss-both-views":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-32-ielts-discuss-both-views","essayKey":"discuss-both-views:32","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-32-ielts-discuss-both-views","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/discuss-both-views-your-opinion/EdmundBd9ExpBth-Q32","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"Modern life is increasingly shaped by change, whether in work, technology, relationships, or personal goals. Some people regard this as a positive force because it keeps life dynamic and meaningful, while others argue that constant adjustment can place too much pressure on individuals. In my view, change is ultimately beneficial because it pushes people to grow, even though it can be uncomfortable in the short term.","chinese":"現代生活越來越受到變化塑造，無論是在工作、科技、人際關係，還是個人目標方面。 有些人把這視為一種積極力量，因為它令生活保持動感和意義，而另一些人則認為，持續調整會給個人帶來太大壓力。 在我看來，變化最終是有益的，因為它推動人們成長，即使它在短期內可能令人不舒服"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"Those who support change often argue that it prevents people from becoming mentally stagnant. When individuals remain in the same routine for too long, they may become overly comfortable and lose the motivation to develop new skills or explore better opportunities. By contrast, change forces people to adapt, think differently, and become more resilient. For example, a worker who moves into a new industry may initially feel uncertain, but the process can broaden their knowledge, improve their confidence, and open doors that would otherwise remain closed. In this sense, change is not merely a disruption; it is a powerful engine of personal growth.","chinese":"支持變化的人常常認為，它能防止人們在思想上停滯不前。 當個人長時間停留在同一種日常模式中時，他們可能會變得過於安逸，並失去發展新技能或探索更好機會的動力。 相比之下，變化迫使人們適應、以不同方式思考，並變得更有韌性。 例如，一名轉到新行業的員工一開始可能會感到不確定，但這個過程能擴闊他的知識、提升他的信心，並打開原本可能一直關閉的機會之門。 從這個意義上說，變化不僅僅是一種干擾；它是個人成長的強大引擎。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"On the other hand, it is understandable why some people see constant change as demanding. Frequent changes in jobs, living conditions, or social expectations can make people feel unstable and emotionally exhausted. A person who has to keep learning new systems at work, moving to new places, or adjusting to new rules may struggle to build a sense of security. However, this argument mainly shows that change needs to be managed carefully, not that it should be avoided. A life with no change may feel safe, but it can also become narrow, repetitive, and limiting.","chinese":"另一方面，有些人認為持續變化令人吃力，這是可以理解的。 工作、生活條件或社會期望的頻繁變化，會使人感到不穩定，並在情緒上筋疲力盡。 一個必須不斷在工作中學習新系統、搬到新地方，或適應新規則的人，可能會難以建立安全感。 然而，這個論點主要說明的是變化需要被謹慎管理，而不是它應該被避免。 沒有變化的生活可能感覺安全，但它也可能變得狹窄、重複和受限制。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, while constant change can certainly be tiring, I believe that change is generally good for people because it encourages adaptability, courage, and long-term development. Comfort may protect people from stress, but change helps them become stronger.","chinese":"總結來說，雖然持續變化確實可能令人疲倦，但我相信變化對人們整體而言是好的，因為它鼓勵適應力、勇氣和長遠發展。 安逸或許能保護人們免受壓力，但變化能幫助他們變得更強大。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"modern life","chinese":"現代生活"},{"english":"be increasingly shaped by","chinese":"越來越受……塑造"},{"english":"whether in","chinese":"不論是在"},{"english":"personal goals","chinese":"個人目標"},{"english":"regard this as","chinese":"將這視為"},{"english":"a positive force","chinese":"正面的力量"},{"english":"keep life dynamic and meaningful","chinese":"令生活保持有活力和有意義"},{"english":"while others argue that","chinese":"而其他人則認為"},{"english":"constant adjustment","chinese":"持續適應"},{"english":"place too much pressure on","chinese":"對……造成太大壓力"},{"english":"individuals","chinese":"個人"},{"english":"in my view","chinese":"在我看來"},{"english":"ultimately beneficial","chinese":"最終是有益的"},{"english":"push people to grow","chinese":"推動人成長"},{"english":"uncomfortable in the short term","chinese":"短期內令人不適"},{"english":"those who support","chinese":"支持……的人"},{"english":"becoming mentally stagnant","chinese":"思想變得停滯"},{"english":"remain in the same routine","chinese":"留在同一套例行生活中"},{"english":"for too long","chinese":"太久"},{"english":"become overly comfortable","chinese":"變得過於安逸"},{"english":"lose the motivation to","chinese":"失去……的動力"},{"english":"develop new skills","chinese":"培養新技能"},{"english":"explore better opportunities","chinese":"探索更好的機會"},{"english":"by contrast","chinese":"相反"},{"english":"force people to adapt","chinese":"迫使人適應"},{"english":"think differently","chinese":"以不同方式思考"},{"english":"become more resilient","chinese":"變得更有抗逆力"},{"english":"move into a new industry","chinese":"轉到新行業"},{"english":"initially feel uncertain","chinese":"起初感到不確定"},{"english":"the process","chinese":"這個過程"},{"english":"broaden their knowledge","chinese":"擴闊知識"},{"english":"improve their confidence","chinese":"提升信心"},{"english":"open doors","chinese":"帶來機會"},{"english":"would otherwise remain closed","chinese":"否則仍會關閉"},{"english":"in this sense","chinese":"從這個意義上說"},{"english":"not merely a disruption","chinese":"不只是干擾"},{"english":"a powerful engine of","chinese":"……的強大推動力"},{"english":"personal growth","chinese":"個人成長"},{"english":"on the other hand","chinese":"另一方面"},{"english":"it is understandable why","chinese":"可以理解為何"},{"english":"see constant change as demanding","chinese":"認為持續改變很吃力"},{"english":"frequent changes","chinese":"頻繁變化"},{"english":"living conditions","chinese":"生活條件"},{"english":"social expectations","chinese":"社會期望"},{"english":"make people feel unstable","chinese":"令人感到不穩定"},{"english":"emotionally exhausted","chinese":"情緒上筋疲力盡"},{"english":"keep learning new systems","chinese":"不斷學習新系統"},{"english":"move to new places","chinese":"搬到新地方"},{"english":"adjust to new rules","chinese":"適應新規則"},{"english":"struggle to build","chinese":"難以建立"},{"english":"a sense of security","chinese":"安全感"},{"english":"mainly shows that","chinese":"主要顯示"},{"english":"be managed carefully","chinese":"被審慎管理"},{"english":"should be avoided","chinese":"應被避免"},{"english":"a life with no change","chinese":"沒有改變的生活"},{"english":"become narrow, repetitive, and limiting","chinese":"變得狹窄、重複而受限制"},{"english":"can certainly be tiring","chinese":"確實可以令人疲累"},{"english":"generally good for","chinese":"一般對……有益"},{"english":"encourage adaptability","chinese":"培養適應能力"},{"english":"courage","chinese":"勇氣"},{"english":"long-term development","chinese":"長遠發展"},{"english":"protect people from stress","chinese":"保護人們免受壓力"},{"english":"become stronger","chinese":"變得更強大"}]},"model-essay-32-ielts-opinion":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-32-ielts-opinion","essayKey":"opinion:32","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-32-ielts-opinion","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/opinions/EdmundBd9OP-Q32","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"Crime control is one of the central responsibilities of a justice system, especially when violent offences are involved. Some argue that capital punishment is the most effective response to serious crime. I completely disagree with this view, because the death penalty is a weak deterrent in practice and can distract governments from measures that prevent crime more reliably.","chinese":"控制犯罪是司法制度其中一項核心責任，尤其是在涉及暴力罪行時更是如此。 有些人認為，死刑是應對嚴重犯罪最有效的方式。 我完全不同意這種觀點，因為死刑在實際上嚇阻力薄弱，而且可能使政府忽略那些更可靠地預防犯罪的措施。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"The first problem is that the death penalty assumes criminals make calm, rational calculations before offending. Many serious crimes, however, are committed in moments of rage, under the influence of drugs, or by people who believe they will not be caught. In such situations, the severity of the possible sentence matters less than the likelihood of detection. A robber who thinks the police will never identify him is unlikely to be stopped by the thought of execution, just as he might ignore a life sentence. What reduces crime more effectively is visible policing, quick investigation, and a court system that makes punishment certain rather than merely extreme.","chinese":"第一個問題是，死刑假設犯罪者在犯罪前會作出冷靜而理性的盤算。 然而，許多嚴重犯罪都是在憤怒失控、受毒品影響，或者由那些相信自己不會被抓到的人所犯下的。 在這種情況下，潛在刑罰的嚴重程度，並不如被偵破的可能性重要。 一名認為警方永遠不會認出他的劫匪，不太可能因為想到會被處決而停止犯罪，就正如他也可能會無視終身監禁一樣。 更有效減少犯罪的，是可見度高的警務、迅速的調查，以及一套能令懲罰變得確定，而不只是極端嚴厲的法庭制度。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"The death penalty also creates a serious moral and practical risk. If a person is wrongly convicted, an execution cannot be undone; a justice system that makes even rare mistakes should not use a punishment that leaves no room for correction. Moreover, capital punishment does little to address why serious crime occurs in the first place. Governments would protect the public better by investing in rehabilitation for offenders, support for vulnerable young people, and strong intelligence-led policing against organised crime. Life imprisonment can remove dangerous criminals from society without closing the door on appeals, review, or rehabilitation. This approach is less dramatic, but it is far more defensible and more useful for long-term public safety.","chinese":"死刑也會造成嚴重的道德和實務風險。 如果一個人被錯誤定罪，處決便無法挽回；即使一個司法制度只是偶爾犯錯，它也不應使用一種完全沒有修正空間的刑罰。 此外，死刑幾乎無法處理嚴重犯罪最初發生的原因。 政府若投資於罪犯更生、支援弱勢年輕人，以及針對有組織犯罪的強力情報主導警務，會更能保護公眾。 終身監禁可以把危險罪犯與社會隔離，同時不會關上上訴、覆核或更生的大門。 這種做法沒有那麼戲劇化，但它更站得住腳，也更有助於長遠的公共安全。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, the death penalty is not the best way to reduce serious crime. A safer society is built not by the harshest punishment, but by reliable policing, fair trials, prevention, and penalties that protect the public without risking irreversible injustice.","chinese":"總結來說，死刑並不是減少嚴重犯罪的最佳方法。 一個更安全的社會不是由最嚴厲的刑罰建立起來的，而是由可靠的警務、公平的審訊、犯罪預防，以及能保護公眾而不會冒上不可逆轉不公義風險的刑罰建立起來的。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"Crime control","chinese":"犯罪管控"},{"english":"central responsibilities","chinese":"核心責任"},{"english":"justice system","chinese":"司法制度"},{"english":"violent offences","chinese":"暴力罪行"},{"english":"be involved","chinese":"涉及其中"},{"english":"capital punishment","chinese":"死刑"},{"english":"the most effective response to","chinese":"對……最有效的回應"},{"english":"serious crime","chinese":"嚴重罪行"},{"english":"the death penalty","chinese":"死刑"},{"english":"weak deterrent","chinese":"阻嚇力弱的措施"},{"english":"in practice","chinese":"實際上"},{"english":"distract governments from","chinese":"令政府分心，忽略……"},{"english":"prevent crime more reliably","chinese":"更可靠地預防犯罪"},{"english":"assumes criminals make","chinese":"假設罪犯會作出……"},{"english":"calm, rational calculations","chinese":"冷靜而理性的計算"},{"english":"before offending","chinese":"犯案之前"},{"english":"be committed in moments of rage","chinese":"在憤怒一刻犯下"},{"english":"under the influence of drugs","chinese":"受毒品影響"},{"english":"believe they will not be caught","chinese":"相信自己不會被捕"},{"english":"in such situations","chinese":"在這些情況下"},{"english":"severity of the possible sentence","chinese":"可能刑罰的嚴重程度"},{"english":"matters less than","chinese":"不及……重要"},{"english":"likelihood of detection","chinese":"被偵破的可能性"},{"english":"robber","chinese":"劫匪"},{"english":"identify him","chinese":"辨認出他"},{"english":"be unlikely to be stopped by","chinese":"不大可能因……而被阻止"},{"english":"the thought of execution","chinese":"被處決的想法"},{"english":"life sentence","chinese":"終身監禁"},{"english":"visible policing","chinese":"可見的警力巡邏"},{"english":"quick investigation","chinese":"迅速調查"},{"english":"court system","chinese":"法庭制度"},{"english":"punishment certain","chinese":"刑罰確定"},{"english":"rather than merely extreme","chinese":"而不是只是極端嚴厲"},{"english":"moral and practical risk","chinese":"道德和實際風險"},{"english":"wrongly convicted","chinese":"被錯誤定罪"},{"english":"cannot be undone","chinese":"無法撤銷"},{"english":"rare mistakes","chinese":"罕見錯誤"},{"english":"leaves no room for correction","chinese":"沒有改正空間"},{"english":"address why","chinese":"處理為甚麼……"},{"english":"in the first place","chinese":"最初；根本上"},{"english":"protect the public","chinese":"保護公眾"},{"english":"investing in","chinese":"投資於……"},{"english":"rehabilitation for offenders","chinese":"犯事者更生"},{"english":"vulnerable young people","chinese":"弱勢年輕人"},{"english":"intelligence-led policing","chinese":"情報主導的警務工作"},{"english":"organised crime","chinese":"有組織犯罪"},{"english":"life imprisonment","chinese":"終身監禁"},{"english":"remove dangerous criminals from society","chinese":"將危險罪犯與社會隔離"},{"english":"without closing the door on","chinese":"而不關上……的大門"},{"english":"appeals","chinese":"上訴"},{"english":"review","chinese":"覆核"},{"english":"less dramatic","chinese":"較不戲劇化"},{"english":"far more defensible","chinese":"合理得多；更站得住腳"},{"english":"long-term public safety","chinese":"長遠公共安全"},{"english":"reduce serious crime","chinese":"減少嚴重罪行"},{"english":"safer society","chinese":"更安全的社會"},{"english":"harshest punishment","chinese":"最嚴厲的懲罰"},{"english":"reliable policing","chinese":"可靠的警務工作"},{"english":"fair trials","chinese":"公平審訊"},{"english":"prevention","chinese":"預防"},{"english":"penalties","chinese":"刑罰"},{"english":"irreversible injustice","chinese":"無法逆轉的不公義"}]},"model-essay-33-ielts-direct-question":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-33-ielts-direct-question","essayKey":"direct-question:33","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-33-ielts-direct-question","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/direct-question/EdmundBd9Dir-Q33","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"Modern news coverage often gives the impression that the world is dominated by conflict, disaster and crime. This is not because positive events are rare, but because negative events are usually more urgent, dramatic and commercially powerful. In my view, news organisations should present a healthier balance of both good and bad news.","chinese":"現代新聞報道往往給人一種印象，彷彿這個世界是由衝突、災難和犯罪所主導的。 這並不是因為正面的事情很少發生，而是因為負面事件通常更緊急、更具戲劇性，也更具商業吸引力。 在我看來，新聞機構應該呈現一種更健康的平衡，同時報道好消息和壞消息。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"There are two main reasons why bad news receives so much attention. Firstly, serious events such as wars, famines and accidents have immediate consequences for public safety, so journalists naturally treat them as priorities. If a disease spreads, a violent crime occurs, or a natural disaster destroys homes, people need to know quickly. Secondly, negative stories tend to attract stronger emotional reactions. Fear, shock and anger make people click, watch and share, which means media companies can gain larger audiences by focusing on crises rather than ordinary progress. In this sense, bad news often works like a loud alarm bell: it is hard to ignore, even when people are tired of hearing it.","chinese":"壞消息受到如此多關注，主要有兩個原因。 首先，戰爭、饑荒和意外事故等嚴重事件會對公共安全造成即時影響，因此記者自然會把它們視為優先報道的內容。 如果一種疾病正在傳播、一宗暴力犯罪發生，或一場自然災害摧毀了家園，人們就需要盡快知道。 其次，負面新聞往往更容易引發強烈的情緒反應。 恐懼、震驚和憤怒會促使人們點擊、觀看和分享，這意味著媒體公司透過聚焦危機，而不是普通的進步，可以獲得更大的受眾。 從這個角度來看，壞消息往往像一個響亮的警鐘：即使人們已經厭倦聽到它，也很難忽視它。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"However, I believe the news should include more positive stories as well. A constant stream of tragedy can make people feel helpless and cynical, as if society is only moving backwards. This is a distorted picture of reality. For example, stories about medical breakthroughs, successful community projects or declining crime in some areas can remind the public that problems are not always permanent. Good news does not mean shallow entertainment; it can show solutions, inspire responsible behaviour and give people a more complete understanding of the world. If journalism only shows the wound and never the healing, it fails to tell the whole story.","chinese":"然而，我認為新聞也應該包含更多正面的故事。 源源不絕的悲劇新聞可能會令人感到無助和憤世嫉俗，彷彿社會只是在不斷倒退。 這是一幅被扭曲的現實圖像。 例如，關於醫學突破、成功的社區項目，或某些地區犯罪率下降的新聞，可以提醒公眾：問題並不總是永久存在的。 好消息並不等於膚淺的娛樂；它可以展示解決方案、激發負責任的行為，並讓人們對世界有更完整的理解。 如果新聞只展示傷口，卻從不展示癒合的過程，它就沒有把整個故事說完整。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, bad news dominates because it is urgent, emotionally powerful and commercially attractive. Nevertheless, news outlets should report both negative and positive developments, since a balanced news diet would keep people informed without making them unnecessarily pessimistic.","chinese":"總結來說，壞消息佔主導地位，是因為它緊急、情緒力量強，也具有商業吸引力。 然而，新聞機構應該同時報道負面和正面的發展，因為平衡的新聞內容能讓人們保持知情，而不會使他們不必要地變得悲觀。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"modern news coverage","chinese":"現代新聞報道"},{"english":"gives the impression that","chinese":"給人……的印象"},{"english":"be dominated by","chinese":"被……主導"},{"english":"conflict, disaster and crime","chinese":"衝突、災難和罪案"},{"english":"positive events","chinese":"正面事件"},{"english":"not because...but because...","chinese":"不是因為……而是因為……"},{"english":"negative events","chinese":"負面事件"},{"english":"more urgent, dramatic and commercially powerful","chinese":"更緊急、更戲劇化、更具商業力量"},{"english":"news organisations","chinese":"新聞機構"},{"english":"present a healthier balance of","chinese":"呈現更健康的平衡"},{"english":"good and bad news","chinese":"好消息和壞消息"},{"english":"two main reasons why","chinese":"兩個主要原因解釋為何"},{"english":"receives so much attention","chinese":"受到如此多關注"},{"english":"serious events","chinese":"嚴重事件"},{"english":"wars, famines and accidents","chinese":"戰爭、饑荒和意外"},{"english":"immediate consequences for","chinese":"對……有即時後果"},{"english":"public safety","chinese":"公眾安全"},{"english":"treat them as priorities","chinese":"把它們視為優先事項"},{"english":"a disease spreads","chinese":"疾病傳播"},{"english":"a violent crime occurs","chinese":"暴力罪案發生"},{"english":"a natural disaster destroys homes","chinese":"天災摧毀家園"},{"english":"need to know quickly","chinese":"需要迅速知道"},{"english":"negative stories","chinese":"負面新聞故事"},{"english":"tend to attract","chinese":"往往吸引"},{"english":"stronger emotional reactions","chinese":"更強烈的情緒反應"},{"english":"fear, shock and anger","chinese":"恐懼、震驚和憤怒"},{"english":"click, watch and share","chinese":"點擊、觀看和分享"},{"english":"media companies","chinese":"媒體公司"},{"english":"gain larger audiences","chinese":"獲得更大觀眾群"},{"english":"focusing on crises","chinese":"聚焦危機"},{"english":"ordinary progress","chinese":"平常的進步"},{"english":"In this sense","chinese":"從這個意義上說"},{"english":"works like a loud alarm bell","chinese":"像響亮的警鐘一樣發揮作用"},{"english":"hard to ignore","chinese":"難以忽視"},{"english":"tired of hearing it","chinese":"厭倦聽到它"},{"english":"include more positive stories","chinese":"包含更多正面故事"},{"english":"a constant stream of","chinese":"源源不絕的……"},{"english":"tragedy","chinese":"悲劇"},{"english":"feel helpless and cynical","chinese":"感到無助和憤世嫉俗"},{"english":"as if","chinese":"彷彿"},{"english":"moving backwards","chinese":"倒退"},{"english":"a distorted picture of reality","chinese":"扭曲的現實圖像"},{"english":"medical breakthroughs","chinese":"醫學突破"},{"english":"successful community projects","chinese":"成功的社區項目"},{"english":"declining crime","chinese":"罪案下降"},{"english":"remind the public that","chinese":"提醒公眾"},{"english":"not always permanent","chinese":"並不總是永久的"},{"english":"shallow entertainment","chinese":"膚淺娛樂"},{"english":"show solutions","chinese":"展示解決方法"},{"english":"inspire responsible behaviour","chinese":"鼓勵負責任的行為"},{"english":"a more complete understanding of","chinese":"對……更完整的理解"},{"english":"journalism","chinese":"新聞工作；新聞業"},{"english":"shows the wound and never the healing","chinese":"只展示傷口而從不展示痊癒"},{"english":"fails to tell","chinese":"未能講述"},{"english":"the whole story","chinese":"完整故事"},{"english":"bad news dominates","chinese":"壞消息佔主導"},{"english":"emotionally powerful","chinese":"情緒感染力強"},{"english":"commercially attractive","chinese":"具有商業吸引力"},{"english":"news outlets","chinese":"新聞媒體"},{"english":"negative and positive developments","chinese":"負面和正面發展"},{"english":"a balanced news diet","chinese":"均衡的新聞資訊"},{"english":"keep people informed","chinese":"讓人們掌握資訊"},{"english":"without making them unnecessarily pessimistic","chinese":"不會令他們不必要地悲觀"}]},"model-essay-33-ielts-discuss-both-views":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-33-ielts-discuss-both-views","essayKey":"discuss-both-views:33","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-33-ielts-discuss-both-views","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/discuss-both-views-your-opinion/EdmundBd9ExpBth-Q33","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"Some people regard the search for extraterrestrial intelligence as one of humanity’s most exciting scientific ambitions. While a number of scientists believe that we should actively send messages to possible life forms beyond Earth, others argue that such contact could expose humanity to unnecessary danger. I strongly agree with the latter view, because the possible risks are far greater than the likely benefits.","chinese":"有些人認為，尋找外星智慧生命是人類最令人振奮的科學抱負之一。 雖然一些科學家認為我們應該主動向地球以外可能存在的生命形式發送訊息，但另一些人則認為，這種接觸可能會使人類暴露於不必要的危險之中。 我強烈同意後一種觀點，因為潛在風險遠遠大於可能帶來的好處。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"Those who support sending signals argue that contact with intelligent aliens could transform human knowledge. If another civilisation were advanced enough to receive and understand our messages, it might also possess scientific insights far beyond our own. Communication with such beings could, in theory, help humans understand space, technology and even the origins of life more deeply. Moreover, the attempt itself may encourage international cooperation, since sending a message into space would require scientists, governments and institutions to work towards a shared goal rather than compete with one another.","chinese":"支持發送訊號的人認為，與有智慧的外星生命接觸可能會徹底改變人類的知識。 如果另一個文明先進到能夠接收並理解我們的訊息，它也可能擁有遠遠超越我們的科學見解。 從理論上說，與這些生命溝通可以幫助人類更深入地理解太空、科技，甚至生命的起源。 此外，這種嘗試本身也可能促進國際合作，因為向太空發送訊息需要科學家、政府和機構朝著共同目標努力，而不是彼此競爭。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"However, I believe this optimism rests on a dangerous assumption: that any intelligent life we contact would be peaceful or helpful. Once a message is sent, it cannot be recalled, and humanity would have no control over who receives it or how they respond. A civilisation capable of travelling across vast distances might be far more technologically powerful than we are, and revealing our location could be like opening a door without knowing who is standing outside. Even if the chance of harm is small, the scale of the possible damage is so great that caution is the only responsible position.","chinese":"然而，我認為這種樂觀建立在一個危險的假設之上：那就是我們接觸到的任何智慧生命都會是和平或有幫助的。 一旦訊息被發出，它就無法被收回，而人類也無法控制誰接收到它，或對方如何回應 一個能夠跨越遙遠距離旅行的文明，可能在科技上遠比我們強大，而暴露我們的位置就像在不知道門外站著誰的情況下打開大門。 即使造成傷害的機會很小，潛在破壞的規模也如此巨大，以至於謹慎才是唯一負責任的立場。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, although sending messages to other planets could satisfy human curiosity and may lead to extraordinary discoveries, it is an unacceptable risk. Humanity should continue studying space and listening for signals, but deliberately announcing our presence to unknown civilisations is a gamble we should not take.","chinese":"總結來說，雖然向其他星球發送訊息可以滿足人類的好奇心，並可能帶來非凡的發現，但這是一個不可接受的風險。 人類應該繼續研究太空並聆聽訊號，但刻意向未知文明宣告我們的存在，是一場我們不應承擔的賭博。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"regard ... as","chinese":"將……視為"},{"english":"the search for extraterrestrial intelligence","chinese":"尋找外星智慧生命"},{"english":"one of humanity's most exciting scientific ambitions","chinese":"人類最令人興奮的科學抱負之一"},{"english":"a number of scientists","chinese":"一些科學家"},{"english":"actively send messages to","chinese":"主動向……發送訊息"},{"english":"possible life forms beyond Earth","chinese":"地球以外可能存在的生命體"},{"english":"such contact","chinese":"這種接觸"},{"english":"expose humanity to unnecessary danger","chinese":"使人類暴露於不必要的危險"},{"english":"the latter view","chinese":"後者觀點"},{"english":"possible risks","chinese":"可能風險"},{"english":"far greater than","chinese":"遠大於"},{"english":"the likely benefits","chinese":"可能帶來的好處"},{"english":"support sending signals","chinese":"支持發送信號"},{"english":"contact with intelligent aliens","chinese":"與智慧外星生命接觸"},{"english":"transform human knowledge","chinese":"改變人類知識"},{"english":"advanced enough to","chinese":"先進到足以"},{"english":"receive and understand our messages","chinese":"接收並理解我們的訊息"},{"english":"possess scientific insights","chinese":"擁有科學見解"},{"english":"far beyond our own","chinese":"遠超我們自己的"},{"english":"communication with","chinese":"與……溝通"},{"english":"such beings","chinese":"這類生命體"},{"english":"in theory","chinese":"理論上"},{"english":"the origins of life","chinese":"生命的起源"},{"english":"more deeply","chinese":"更深入地"},{"english":"the attempt itself","chinese":"嘗試本身"},{"english":"encourage international cooperation","chinese":"促進國際合作"},{"english":"sending a message into space","chinese":"向太空發送訊息"},{"english":"require scientists, governments and institutions to","chinese":"需要科學家、政府和機構去"},{"english":"work towards a shared goal","chinese":"為共同目標努力"},{"english":"rather than compete with one another","chinese":"而不是互相競爭"},{"english":"this optimism","chinese":"這種樂觀想法"},{"english":"rest on","chinese":"建基於"},{"english":"a dangerous assumption","chinese":"危險假設"},{"english":"intelligent life","chinese":"智慧生命"},{"english":"peaceful or helpful","chinese":"和平或有幫助"},{"english":"once a message is sent","chinese":"訊息一旦發出"},{"english":"cannot be recalled","chinese":"不能被收回"},{"english":"have no control over","chinese":"無法控制"},{"english":"how they respond","chinese":"他們如何回應"},{"english":"capable of travelling across vast distances","chinese":"有能力跨越遙遠距離"},{"english":"technologically powerful","chinese":"科技強大"},{"english":"revealing our location","chinese":"暴露我們的位置"},{"english":"be like opening a door","chinese":"就像打開一扇門"},{"english":"without knowing who is standing outside","chinese":"不知道門外站着誰"},{"english":"even if the chance of harm is small","chinese":"即使造成傷害的機會很小"},{"english":"the scale of the possible damage","chinese":"可能損害的規模"},{"english":"caution","chinese":"謹慎"},{"english":"the only responsible position","chinese":"唯一負責任的立場"},{"english":"sending messages to other planets","chinese":"向其他星球發送訊息"},{"english":"satisfy human curiosity","chinese":"滿足人類好奇心"},{"english":"lead to extraordinary discoveries","chinese":"帶來非凡發現"},{"english":"an unacceptable risk","chinese":"不能接受的風險"},{"english":"continue studying space","chinese":"繼續研究太空"},{"english":"listening for signals","chinese":"聆聽信號"},{"english":"deliberately announcing our presence","chinese":"故意宣告我們的存在"},{"english":"unknown civilisations","chinese":"未知文明"},{"english":"a gamble we should not take","chinese":"我們不應冒的賭注"}]},"model-essay-33-ielts-opinion":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-33-ielts-opinion","essayKey":"opinion:33","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-33-ielts-opinion","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/opinions/EdmundBd9OP-Q33","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"Crime is a serious social problem, and many people believe that offenders should simply be sent to prison. While imprisonment may appear to be the most direct response to criminal behaviour, I firmly believe that it is not the best general solution. In most cases, rehabilitation and carefully supervised community-based punishments are more effective because they address the causes of crime rather than merely hiding criminals from society.","chinese":"犯罪是一個嚴重的社會問題，而許多人認為罪犯應該直接被送入監獄。 雖然監禁看起來可能是對犯罪行為最直接的回應， 我堅定地認為，這並不是一般情況下最好的解決方法。在大多數情況下，改造和受到仔細監管的社區式懲罰更加有效，因為它們處理的是犯罪的根源，而不是僅僅把罪犯從社會中隱藏起來。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"Supporters of prison often argue that it protects the public and sends a clear warning to potential offenders. This view is understandable because dangerous criminals can cause real harm if they remain free. However, prison often treats the symptom rather than the disease. Many offenders commit crimes because of addiction, poor education, unemployment, or unstable family backgrounds. If these problems are ignored, prison can become a revolving door: criminals enter, serve their sentence, and return to society with the same weaknesses, or sometimes even worse ones. For example, a young person who commits a minor theft may leave prison with fewer job prospects and stronger links to hardened criminals. In this sense, prison can punish crime without actually reducing it.","chinese":"支持監禁的人經常認為，監獄能保護公眾，並向潛在犯罪者發出清晰警告。 這種看法是可以理解的，因為危險的罪犯如果仍然自由，確實可能造成真正的傷害。 然而，監獄往往處理的是症狀，而不是疾病本身。 許多犯罪者犯罪，是因為成癮、教育不足、失業，或不穩定的家庭背景。 如果這些問題被忽視，監獄就可能變成一扇旋轉門：罪犯進去、服刑，然後帶著同樣的弱點，甚至有時帶著更嚴重的問題回到社會。 例如，一個犯下輕微盜竊的年輕人，出獄後可能會有更少的就業機會，並與慣犯建立更深的聯繫。 從這個意義上說，監獄可以懲罰犯罪，卻未必真正減少犯罪。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"A better approach is to combine punishment with rehabilitation. Offenders should still face consequences, but those consequences should help them rebuild their lives and repay society. Drug treatment, psychological counselling, vocational training, community service, and victim compensation can all make punishment more constructive. For instance, someone who has committed a non-violent offence could be required to work in the community while attending training courses and meeting strict supervision conditions. This approach does not excuse the crime; rather, it turns punishment into a ladder instead of a cage. It gives offenders a realistic path back into society, which ultimately makes communities safer.","chinese":"更好的方法是把懲罰與改造結合起來。 犯罪者仍然應該承擔後果，但這些後果應該幫助他們重建生活，並回饋社會。 戒毒治療、心理輔導、職業培訓、社區服務，以及對受害者的賠償，都可以讓懲罰變得更具建設性。 例如，一個犯下非暴力罪行的人，可以被要求在社區工作，同時參加培訓課程，並遵守嚴格的監管條件。 這種方法並不是在為犯罪開脫；相反，它把懲罰變成一把梯子，而不是一個牢籠。 它給犯罪者一條實際可行的回歸社會之路，而這最終會令社區更加安全。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, prison may look like a strong solution, but it is often a blunt instrument. I believe that rehabilitation and structured alternatives are better ways to deal with most criminals because they reduce reoffending, repair damage, and help society break the cycle of crime.","chinese":"總結來說，監獄可能看起來是一種有力的解決方法，但它往往是一種粗糙不精準的工具 我認為，改造和有結構的替代方案是處理大多數罪犯更好的方法，因為它們能減少再犯、修補傷害，並幫助社會打破犯罪循環。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"crime","chinese":"犯罪"},{"english":"serious social problem","chinese":"嚴重社會問題"},{"english":"offenders","chinese":"犯事者"},{"english":"be sent to prison","chinese":"被送入監獄"},{"english":"imprisonment","chinese":"監禁"},{"english":"appear to be","chinese":"看似是"},{"english":"direct response to","chinese":"對……的直接回應"},{"english":"criminal behaviour","chinese":"犯罪行為"},{"english":"general solution","chinese":"一般解決方法"},{"english":"rehabilitation","chinese":"更生；改造"},{"english":"carefully supervised","chinese":"受到小心監管"},{"english":"community-based punishments","chinese":"社區為本的懲罰"},{"english":"more effective","chinese":"更有效"},{"english":"address the causes of crime","chinese":"處理犯罪成因"},{"english":"rather than merely","chinese":"而不是只是"},{"english":"hiding criminals from society","chinese":"將罪犯從社會中藏起來"},{"english":"supporters of prison","chinese":"支持監禁的人"},{"english":"protect the public","chinese":"保護公眾"},{"english":"send a clear warning to","chinese":"向……發出清晰警告"},{"english":"potential offenders","chinese":"潛在犯事者"},{"english":"understandable","chinese":"可以理解的"},{"english":"dangerous criminals","chinese":"危險罪犯"},{"english":"cause real harm","chinese":"造成真正傷害"},{"english":"remain free","chinese":"仍然自由"},{"english":"treat the symptom rather than the disease","chinese":"治標不治本"},{"english":"commit crimes","chinese":"犯罪"},{"english":"addiction","chinese":"成癮"},{"english":"poor education","chinese":"教育不足"},{"english":"unemployment","chinese":"失業"},{"english":"unstable family backgrounds","chinese":"不穩定的家庭背景"},{"english":"be ignored","chinese":"被忽視"},{"english":"revolving door","chinese":"循環不息的情況"},{"english":"serve their sentence","chinese":"服刑"},{"english":"return to society","chinese":"重返社會"},{"english":"with the same weaknesses","chinese":"帶着同樣弱點"},{"english":"minor theft","chinese":"輕微盜竊"},{"english":"job prospects","chinese":"就業前景"},{"english":"stronger links to","chinese":"與……有更強聯繫"},{"english":"hardened criminals","chinese":"老練罪犯；慣犯"},{"english":"in this sense","chinese":"從這個意義上說"},{"english":"punish crime","chinese":"懲罰犯罪"},{"english":"actually reducing it","chinese":"真正減少它"},{"english":"a better approach","chinese":"更好的方法"},{"english":"combine punishment with rehabilitation","chinese":"將懲罰與更生結合"},{"english":"face consequences","chinese":"承擔後果"},{"english":"rebuild their lives","chinese":"重建生活"},{"english":"repay society","chinese":"回報社會；彌補社會"},{"english":"drug treatment","chinese":"戒毒治療"},{"english":"psychological counselling","chinese":"心理輔導"},{"english":"vocational training","chinese":"職業培訓"},{"english":"community service","chinese":"社區服務"},{"english":"victim compensation","chinese":"對受害者的賠償"},{"english":"constructive","chinese":"有建設性的"},{"english":"non-violent offence","chinese":"非暴力罪行"},{"english":"be required to","chinese":"被要求去……"},{"english":"work in the community","chinese":"在社區工作"},{"english":"training courses","chinese":"培訓課程"},{"english":"strict supervision conditions","chinese":"嚴格監管條件"},{"english":"excuse the crime","chinese":"為罪行開脫"},{"english":"turn punishment into","chinese":"將懲罰變成……"},{"english":"a ladder instead of a cage","chinese":"階梯而不是牢籠"},{"english":"realistic path back into society","chinese":"重返社會的現實途徑"},{"english":"ultimately","chinese":"最終"},{"english":"makes communities safer","chinese":"令社區更安全"},{"english":"strong solution","chinese":"強硬的解決方法"},{"english":"blunt instrument","chinese":"粗糙的工具"},{"english":"structured alternatives","chinese":"有系統的替代方案"},{"english":"deal with","chinese":"處理"},{"english":"reduce reoffending","chinese":"減少重犯"},{"english":"repair damage","chinese":"修補傷害"},{"english":"break the cycle of crime","chinese":"打破犯罪循環"}]},"model-essay-34-ielts-direct-question":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-34-ielts-direct-question","essayKey":"direct-question:34","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-34-ielts-direct-question","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/direct-question/EdmundBd9Dir-Q34","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"Films are now consumed in a highly globalised media environment, where audiences can access productions from almost anywhere. Many viewers therefore choose international films over domestic ones because they often seem more polished, more varied, and better advertised. In my view, governments should increase support for the local film industry because it protects cultural identity and develops creative talent.","chinese":"如今，電影是在高度全球化的媒體環境中被觀看的，觀眾幾乎可以接觸到來自世界任何地方的作品。 因此，許多觀眾會選擇國際電影而不是本地電影，因為這些電影往往看起來製作更精良、種類更多元，而且宣傳也更到位。 在我看來，政府應該增加對本地電影業的支持，因為這能保護文化身份，並培養創意人才。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"The main reason foreign films attract large audiences is that they usually benefit from stronger commercial backing. Major studios can spend heavily on famous actors, visual effects, sound design, and worldwide promotion, so their films often feel exciting before the audience has even entered the cinema. They also tend to offer a wide range of genres, from superhero stories to historical dramas, which allows viewers to find something that matches their taste. By contrast, local films, especially in smaller markets, may have weaker marketing and fewer technical resources. Even when the storytelling is strong, the film can struggle to reach the public. In this sense, foreign cinema sometimes wins not because it is always better, but because it arrives with a louder voice and a brighter spotlight.","chinese":"外國電影吸引大量觀眾的主要原因，是它們通常受惠於更強大的商業支持。 大型電影公司可以在知名演員、視覺特效、音效設計和全球宣傳上投入大量資金，因此它們的電影往往在觀眾真正走進戲院之前，已經讓人覺得令人期待。 它們也往往提供種類廣泛的電影類型，從超級英雄故事到歷史劇都有，這讓觀眾能找到符合自己口味的作品。 相比之下，本地電影，尤其是在較小市場中的本地電影，可能行銷能力較弱，技術資源也較少。 即使故事本身很出色，這部電影也可能難以接觸到大眾。 從這個角度來看，外國電影有時勝出，並不是因為它總是更好，而是因為它帶著更響亮的聲音和更明亮的聚光燈登場。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"For this reason, I believe public funding for local cinema is necessary. Films are not only commercial products; they are also a way for a society to remember its language, values, humour, landscapes, and everyday problems. Without support, many local directors and writers may be forced to copy foreign formulas or leave the industry altogether. Government grants, training schemes, and subsidies for cinemas that show domestic films can give new talent room to breathe. For example, a young filmmaker who receives funding may tell a story about local families, workplaces, or traditions that international studios would never produce. This strengthens a whole creative ecosystem.","chinese":"基於這個原因，我認為公共資金支持本地電影是必要的。 電影不只是商業產品；它們也是一個社會記住自身語言、價值觀、幽默、風景和日常問題的一種方式。 如果沒有支持，許多本地導演和編劇可能會被迫模仿外國公式，或者乾脆完全離開這個行業。 政府補助、培訓計劃，以及對放映本地電影的戲院提供資助，都可以給新人才喘息和發展的空間。 例如，一位獲得資助的年輕電影製作人，可能會講述關於本地家庭、工作場所或傳統的故事，而這些故事是國際電影公司永遠不會製作的。 這能強化整個創意生態系統。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, people often prefer foreign films because they are better funded, promoted, and distributed. Nevertheless, governments should spend more money on local film industries, since national cinema preserves culture and gives local talent a genuine chance to grow.","chinese":"總結來說，人們經常較喜歡外國電影，是因為它們有更充足的資金、更強的宣傳，以及更完善的發行渠道。 然而，政府應該在本地電影業上投入更多資金，因為國家電影能保存文化，並給予本地人才真正成長的機會。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"be consumed in","chinese":"在……中被觀看；被消費"},{"english":"a highly globalised media environment","chinese":"高度全球化的媒體環境"},{"english":"audiences can access","chinese":"觀眾可以接觸到"},{"english":"productions from almost anywhere","chinese":"來自幾乎任何地方的作品"},{"english":"choose international films over","chinese":"選擇國際電影而不是"},{"english":"domestic ones","chinese":"本地電影"},{"english":"more polished","chinese":"更精緻"},{"english":"more varied","chinese":"更多元化"},{"english":"better advertised","chinese":"宣傳得更好"},{"english":"increase support for","chinese":"加強對……的支持"},{"english":"the local film industry","chinese":"本地電影業"},{"english":"protects cultural identity","chinese":"保護文化身份認同"},{"english":"develops creative talent","chinese":"培養創作人才"},{"english":"the main reason","chinese":"主要原因"},{"english":"attract large audiences","chinese":"吸引大量觀眾"},{"english":"benefit from","chinese":"受惠於"},{"english":"stronger commercial backing","chinese":"更強的商業支持"},{"english":"major studios","chinese":"大型電影公司"},{"english":"spend heavily on","chinese":"大量花費於"},{"english":"famous actors","chinese":"著名演員"},{"english":"visual effects","chinese":"視覺特效"},{"english":"sound design","chinese":"音效設計"},{"english":"worldwide promotion","chinese":"全球宣傳"},{"english":"feel exciting before","chinese":"在……之前已令人期待"},{"english":"entered the cinema","chinese":"進入戲院"},{"english":"tend to offer","chinese":"往往提供"},{"english":"a wide range of genres","chinese":"廣泛的電影類型"},{"english":"superhero stories","chinese":"超級英雄故事"},{"english":"historical dramas","chinese":"歷史劇"},{"english":"allows viewers to","chinese":"讓觀眾可以"},{"english":"matches their taste","chinese":"符合他們的口味"},{"english":"By contrast","chinese":"相比之下"},{"english":"local films","chinese":"本地電影"},{"english":"smaller markets","chinese":"較小的市場"},{"english":"weaker marketing","chinese":"較弱的市場推廣"},{"english":"fewer technical resources","chinese":"較少技術資源"},{"english":"the storytelling is strong","chinese":"故事性強"},{"english":"struggle to reach the public","chinese":"難以接觸大眾"},{"english":"In this sense","chinese":"從這個意義上說"},{"english":"foreign cinema","chinese":"外國電影"},{"english":"not because it is always better","chinese":"並不是因為它總是更好"},{"english":"arrives with a louder voice","chinese":"以更響亮的聲音登場"},{"english":"a brighter spotlight","chinese":"更耀眼的聚光燈"},{"english":"public funding","chinese":"公共資金；政府資助"},{"english":"local cinema","chinese":"本地電影"},{"english":"commercial products","chinese":"商業產品"},{"english":"a way for a society to","chinese":"社會用來……的一種方式"},{"english":"remember its language","chinese":"記住自身語言"},{"english":"everyday problems","chinese":"日常問題"},{"english":"without support","chinese":"沒有支持"},{"english":"local directors and writers","chinese":"本地導演和編劇"},{"english":"be forced to","chinese":"被迫"},{"english":"copy foreign formulas","chinese":"模仿外國公式"},{"english":"leave the industry altogether","chinese":"完全離開這個行業"},{"english":"government grants","chinese":"政府撥款"},{"english":"training schemes","chinese":"培訓計劃"},{"english":"subsidies for cinemas","chinese":"給戲院的津貼"},{"english":"domestic films","chinese":"本地電影"},{"english":"give new talent room to breathe","chinese":"給新人才發展空間"},{"english":"receives funding","chinese":"獲得資助"},{"english":"local families","chinese":"本地家庭"},{"english":"workplaces","chinese":"工作場所"},{"english":"traditions","chinese":"傳統"},{"english":"international studios","chinese":"國際電影公司"},{"english":"strengthens a whole creative ecosystem","chinese":"加強整個創意生態系統"},{"english":"better funded","chinese":"資金更充足"},{"english":"promoted and distributed","chinese":"宣傳和發行得更好"},{"english":"spend more money on","chinese":"在……上花更多錢"},{"english":"local film industries","chinese":"本地電影業"},{"english":"national cinema","chinese":"國家電影；本土電影"},{"english":"preserves culture","chinese":"保存文化"},{"english":"a genuine chance to","chinese":"真正的機會去"},{"english":"grow","chinese":"成長；發展"}]},"model-essay-34-ielts-discuss-both-views":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-34-ielts-discuss-both-views","essayKey":"discuss-both-views:34","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-34-ielts-discuss-both-views","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/discuss-both-views-your-opinion/EdmundBd9ExpBth-Q34","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"Human curiosity has always pushed society beyond familiar borders, and space is now the greatest frontier left to explore. While some argue that missions beyond Earth consume money and talent that could be used more practically, I firmly believe that space exploration is essential because it produces long-term scientific, technological, and survival benefits for humanity.","chinese":"人類的好奇心一直推動社會越過熟悉的邊界，而太空如今是仍有待探索的最大前沿。 雖然有些人認為，地球以外的探索任務會消耗本可更實際地使用的金錢和人才， 我堅定地認為，太空探索是不可或缺的，因為它能為人類帶來長遠的科學、科技和生存利益。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"On the one hand, the argument against space exploration is understandable. Launching rockets, maintaining space stations, and training astronauts require enormous financial and human resources. When hospitals are overcrowded, schools are underfunded, and many communities still lack clean water or basic infrastructure, spending billions on distant planets can appear morally questionable. For example, a taxpayer may reasonably wonder why public money is being used to examine rocks on Mars when children in poor areas cannot receive proper education. From this perspective, space exploration looks like an expensive luxury, especially because its benefits are not always immediate or visible.","chinese":"一方面，反對太空探索的論點是可以理解的。 發射火箭、維持太空站運作，以及訓練太空人都需要龐大的財政和人力資源。 當醫院人滿為患、學校資金不足，而許多社區仍然缺乏清潔食水或基本基礎設施時，把數十億資金花在遙遠星球上，便可能顯得在道德上值得質疑。 例如，一位納稅人可能會合理地質疑，為甚麼公共資金會被用來研究火星上的岩石，而貧困地區的兒童卻無法接受適當教育。 從這個角度來看，太空探索看起來像是一種昂貴的奢侈品，尤其是因為它的好處並不總是即時或明顯可見的。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"On the other hand, dismissing space exploration as a waste of resources is too narrow a view. Research beyond Earth often creates practical technologies and scientific knowledge that improve life on Earth. Satellites, for instance, support weather forecasting, global communication, navigation systems, and disaster monitoring, all of which are now woven into ordinary life. More importantly, exploring space prepares humanity for threats that cannot be solved by local policies alone, such as asteroid impacts, severe resource shortages, or the long-term possibility that Earth may become less habitable. If mankind never looks beyond its own planet, it risks becoming a species with no backup plan.","chinese":"另一方面，把太空探索視為資源浪費，是一種過於狹窄的看法。 地球以外的研究往往能創造實用科技和科學知識，從而改善地球上的生活。 例如，衛星支援天氣預報、全球通訊、導航系統和災害監測，而這些如今都已融入日常生活之中。 更重要的是，探索太空能讓人類為一些無法單靠本地政策解決的威脅作準備，例如小行星撞擊、嚴重資源短缺，或地球長遠而言可能變得較不宜居的可能性。 如果人類從不把目光投向自身星球之外，就有可能成為一個沒有後備計劃的物種。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, although critics are right to say that human needs on Earth must not be ignored, I do not believe space exploration is a wasteful activity. It is a long-term investment in knowledge, safety, and human survival. Governments and private companies should therefore continue exploring the universe, while ensuring that urgent problems on Earth are also responsibly addressed.","chinese":"總結來說，儘管批評者認為地球上的人類需求不應被忽視是正確的，但我並不認為太空探索是一項浪費資源的活動。 它是對知識、安全和人類生存的一項長遠投資。 因此，政府和私人企業應該繼續探索宇宙，同時確保地球上的緊急問題也得到負責任的處理。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"human curiosity","chinese":"人類好奇心"},{"english":"push society beyond","chinese":"推動社會超越"},{"english":"familiar borders","chinese":"熟悉的界限"},{"english":"the greatest frontier left to explore","chinese":"尚待探索的最大前沿"},{"english":"missions beyond Earth","chinese":"地球以外的任務"},{"english":"consume money and talent","chinese":"消耗金錢和人才"},{"english":"be used more practically","chinese":"被更實際地運用"},{"english":"firmly believe that","chinese":"堅信"},{"english":"space exploration","chinese":"太空探索"},{"english":"be essential","chinese":"是必要的"},{"english":"produce long-term benefits","chinese":"產生長遠好處"},{"english":"scientific, technological, and survival benefits","chinese":"科學、科技和生存方面的好處"},{"english":"for humanity","chinese":"對人類而言"},{"english":"the argument against","chinese":"反對……的論點"},{"english":"be understandable","chinese":"可以理解"},{"english":"launching rockets","chinese":"發射火箭"},{"english":"maintaining space stations","chinese":"維持太空站運作"},{"english":"training astronauts","chinese":"訓練太空人"},{"english":"require enormous financial and human resources","chinese":"需要龐大的財政和人力資源"},{"english":"overcrowded","chinese":"過度擠迫"},{"english":"underfunded","chinese":"資金不足"},{"english":"lack clean water","chinese":"缺乏清潔食水"},{"english":"basic infrastructure","chinese":"基本基建"},{"english":"spending billions on","chinese":"花費數十億於"},{"english":"distant planets","chinese":"遙遠星球"},{"english":"appear morally questionable","chinese":"看似在道德上有問題"},{"english":"a taxpayer","chinese":"納稅人"},{"english":"public money","chinese":"公帑"},{"english":"be used to","chinese":"被用來"},{"english":"examine rocks on Mars","chinese":"研究火星上的岩石"},{"english":"in poor areas","chinese":"在貧困地區"},{"english":"receive proper education","chinese":"接受適當教育"},{"english":"from this perspective","chinese":"從這個角度來看"},{"english":"look like an expensive luxury","chinese":"看似昂貴奢侈品"},{"english":"immediate or visible","chinese":"即時或明顯"},{"english":"dismiss space exploration as","chinese":"將太空探索視為"},{"english":"a waste of resources","chinese":"資源浪費"},{"english":"too narrow a view","chinese":"過於狹隘的看法"},{"english":"research beyond Earth","chinese":"地球以外的研究"},{"english":"practical technologies","chinese":"實用科技"},{"english":"scientific knowledge","chinese":"科學知識"},{"english":"improve life on Earth","chinese":"改善地球上的生活"},{"english":"weather forecasting","chinese":"天氣預報"},{"english":"global communication","chinese":"全球通訊"},{"english":"navigation systems","chinese":"導航系統"},{"english":"disaster monitoring","chinese":"災害監測"},{"english":"be woven into ordinary life","chinese":"融入日常生活"},{"english":"prepare humanity for","chinese":"令人類為……作準備"},{"english":"threats that cannot be solved by","chinese":"不能單靠……解決的威脅"},{"english":"local policies alone","chinese":"單靠本地政策"},{"english":"asteroid impacts","chinese":"小行星撞擊"},{"english":"severe resource shortages","chinese":"嚴重資源短缺"},{"english":"the long-term possibility that","chinese":"……的長遠可能性"},{"english":"become less habitable","chinese":"變得較不適合居住"},{"english":"look beyond its own planet","chinese":"放眼自身星球以外"},{"english":"risk becoming","chinese":"冒着變成……的風險"},{"english":"a species with no backup plan","chinese":"沒有後備方案的物種"},{"english":"critics are right to say that","chinese":"批評者說……是對的"},{"english":"human needs on Earth","chinese":"地球上的人類需要"},{"english":"must not be ignored","chinese":"不應被忽視"},{"english":"a wasteful activity","chinese":"浪費的活動"},{"english":"a long-term investment in","chinese":"對……的長遠投資"},{"english":"knowledge, safety, and human survival","chinese":"知識、安全和人類生存"},{"english":"private companies","chinese":"私營公司"},{"english":"continue exploring the universe","chinese":"繼續探索宇宙"},{"english":"while ensuring that","chinese":"同時確保"},{"english":"urgent problems on Earth","chinese":"地球上的迫切問題"},{"english":"be responsibly addressed","chinese":"得到負責任地處理"}]},"model-essay-34-ielts-opinion":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-34-ielts-opinion","essayKey":"opinion:34","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-34-ielts-opinion","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/opinions/EdmundBd9OP-Q34","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"Some people argue that poverty is the main cause of most criminal behaviour. I disagree with this view because crime is usually produced by a wider mixture of motives, choices and social conditions, rather than by financial hardship alone.","chinese":"有些人認為，貧窮是大多數犯罪行為的主要原因。 我不同意這個觀點，因為犯罪通常是由更廣泛的動機、個人選擇和社會條件共同造成的，而不是單單由經濟困難所導致。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"Poverty may place people under pressure, but it does not automatically push them into crime. Many people who live with limited income still obey the law, support their families honestly and take pride in doing the right thing. If poverty were the central explanation for most crimes, almost every poor community would be dominated by criminals, which is clearly not the case. In reality, crime often begins when individuals lack self-control, moral guidance or respect for the law. For example, a young person from a poor background may face real hardship, but whether he steals from a shop depends not only on his empty pocket, but also on his values, his family influence and his fear of consequences. Poverty may be the stage, but it is not always the actor.","chinese":"貧窮可能會使人承受壓力，但它並不會自動把人推向犯罪。 許多收入有限的人仍然遵守法律、誠實地養活家人，並為自己做正確的事而感到自豪。 如果貧窮真的是大多數犯罪的核心解釋，那麼幾乎每一個貧困社區都會被罪犯主導，而這顯然並非事實。 事實上，犯罪往往始於個人缺乏自制力、道德指引或對法律的尊重。 例如，一個出身貧困的年輕人可能確實面對困苦，但他是否會從商店偷竊，不只取決於他口袋空空，也取決於他的價值觀、家庭影響，以及他是否害怕後果。 貧窮或許是犯罪發生的舞台，但它並不總是那個真正行動的主角。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"Moreover, many serious crimes are committed by people who are not poor at all. Fraud, corruption, tax evasion and cybercrime are often driven by greed, ambition or a desire for power. A wealthy businessperson who cheats investors is not acting out of hunger; he is choosing profit over honesty. Similarly, some violent crimes are linked to anger, revenge, addiction or social breakdown rather than simple economic need. This shows that crime is not merely a question of income, but a question of character, opportunity and the strength of social institutions.","chinese":"此外，許多嚴重罪行其實是由根本不貧窮的人所犯下的。 詐騙、貪污、逃稅和網絡犯罪往往是由貪婪、野心或對權力的渴望所驅動。 一個欺騙投資者的富裕商人並不是因為飢餓而行事；他是在誠實與利益之間選擇了利益。 同樣地，一些暴力犯罪與憤怒、報復、成癮或社會關係崩壞有關，不是單純的經濟需要 這說明犯罪並不只是收入問題，而是涉及品格、機會，以及社會制度強弱的問題。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, I disagree that poverty is the reason behind most crimes. Although financial hardship can increase pressure on individuals, crime has deeper roots, including greed, weak moral education, poor law enforcement and personal choice. Poverty may open the door to temptation, but it does not hold the key to most criminal behaviour.","chinese":"總結來說，我不同意貧窮是大多數犯罪背後原因的說法。 雖然經濟困難可以增加個人的壓力，但犯罪有更深層的根源，包括貪婪、薄弱的道德教育、執法不足以及個人選擇。 貧窮或許會為誘惑打開一扇門，但它並不掌握大多數犯罪行為的關鍵。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"poverty","chinese":"貧窮"},{"english":"main cause of","chinese":"……的主要原因"},{"english":"criminal behaviour","chinese":"犯罪行為"},{"english":"disagree with","chinese":"不同意……"},{"english":"be produced by","chinese":"由……產生"},{"english":"wider mixture of","chinese":"更廣泛的混合因素"},{"english":"motives, choices and social conditions","chinese":"動機、選擇和社會環境"},{"english":"rather than by","chinese":"而不是由……"},{"english":"financial hardship alone","chinese":"單靠經濟困難"},{"english":"place people under pressure","chinese":"令人民承受壓力"},{"english":"automatically push them into","chinese":"自動將他們推向……"},{"english":"limited income","chinese":"有限收入"},{"english":"obey the law","chinese":"遵守法律"},{"english":"support their families honestly","chinese":"誠實地養活家人"},{"english":"take pride in","chinese":"以……為榮"},{"english":"doing the right thing","chinese":"做正確的事"},{"english":"central explanation for","chinese":"……的核心解釋"},{"english":"poor community","chinese":"貧困社區"},{"english":"be dominated by","chinese":"被……主導"},{"english":"which is clearly not the case","chinese":"但事實明顯並非如此"},{"english":"in reality","chinese":"實際上"},{"english":"lack self-control","chinese":"缺乏自制力"},{"english":"moral guidance","chinese":"道德指引"},{"english":"respect for the law","chinese":"對法律的尊重"},{"english":"poor background","chinese":"貧困背景"},{"english":"face real hardship","chinese":"面對真正困難"},{"english":"steal from a shop","chinese":"從商店偷東西"},{"english":"depends not only on","chinese":"不只取決於……"},{"english":"empty pocket","chinese":"空空的口袋；缺錢"},{"english":"family influence","chinese":"家庭影響"},{"english":"fear of consequences","chinese":"對後果的恐懼"},{"english":"poverty may be the stage","chinese":"貧窮可能是舞台"},{"english":"not always the actor","chinese":"不一定是主角"},{"english":"serious crimes","chinese":"嚴重罪行"},{"english":"be committed by","chinese":"由……犯下"},{"english":"not poor at all","chinese":"一點也不貧窮"},{"english":"fraud","chinese":"欺詐"},{"english":"corruption","chinese":"貪污；腐敗"},{"english":"tax evasion","chinese":"逃稅"},{"english":"cybercrime","chinese":"網絡犯罪"},{"english":"be driven by","chinese":"由……驅使"},{"english":"greed, ambition or a desire for power","chinese":"貪婪、野心或對權力的渴望"},{"english":"wealthy businessperson","chinese":"富有商人"},{"english":"cheats investors","chinese":"欺騙投資者"},{"english":"act out of hunger","chinese":"出於飢餓而行事"},{"english":"choosing profit over honesty","chinese":"選擇利潤而非誠實"},{"english":"violent crimes","chinese":"暴力罪行"},{"english":"be linked to","chinese":"與……有關"},{"english":"anger, revenge, addiction or social breakdown","chinese":"憤怒、報復、成癮或社會崩壞"},{"english":"simple economic need","chinese":"單純經濟需要"},{"english":"not merely a question of","chinese":"不只是……的問題"},{"english":"a question of character","chinese":"品格問題"},{"english":"opportunity","chinese":"機會"},{"english":"strength of social institutions","chinese":"社會制度的強度"},{"english":"the reason behind","chinese":"……背後的原因"},{"english":"increase pressure on","chinese":"增加對……的壓力"},{"english":"deeper roots","chinese":"更深層根源"},{"english":"weak moral education","chinese":"薄弱的道德教育"},{"english":"poor law enforcement","chinese":"執法不力"},{"english":"personal choice","chinese":"個人選擇"},{"english":"open the door to temptation","chinese":"打開誘惑之門"},{"english":"hold the key to","chinese":"掌握……的關鍵"}]},"model-essay-35-ielts-direct-question":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-35-ielts-direct-question","essayKey":"direct-question:35","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-35-ielts-direct-question","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/direct-question/EdmundBd9Dir-Q35","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"In modern consumer societies, shopping is no longer limited to meeting basic needs. Many people now purchase items they could easily live without and replace perfectly functional products long before necessary. This essay will argue that this behaviour is mainly driven by advertising and social pressure, and that it is clearly a negative development.","chinese":"在現代消費型社會中，購物已不再只是為了滿足基本需要。如今，許多人會購買一些即使沒有也完全可以生活的物品，並且在完全沒有必要之前，就更換仍然功能正常的產品。 本文將主張，這種行為主要是由廣告和社會壓力所推動，而且它明顯是一種負面的發展"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"One major reason people buy unnecessary goods is that companies have become highly skilled at creating desire. Advertisements rarely present products as ordinary objects; instead, they connect them with beauty, success, confidence, or social belonging. As a result, consumers may start to feel that owning the newest phone, outfit, or household device will improve their identity rather than simply serve a practical function. This pressure is even stronger on social media, where people are constantly exposed to influencers and friends displaying new purchases. When consumption becomes a way to gain approval, people are more likely to buy things they do not genuinely need.","chinese":"人們購買不必要商品的一個主要原因是，企業已經非常擅長製造欲望。 廣告很少把產品呈現為普通物品；相反，它們會把產品與美貌、成功、自信或社會歸屬感聯繫起來。 結果，消費者可能會開始覺得，擁有最新的手機、服裝或家用設備能提升他們的身份形象，而不只是滿足實際功能。 這種壓力在社交媒體上更加強烈，因為人們不斷看到網紅和朋友展示新的購買品。 當消費變成一種獲得認同的方式時，人們便更有可能購買自己並不真正需要的東西。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"Another reason is that many products are designed to feel outdated very quickly. Technology companies, for instance, release new models every year, even when the improvements are relatively minor. A person whose phone still works well may still feel tempted to replace it because the newer version looks more fashionable or slightly faster. In this way, shopping becomes less about solving real problems and more about chasing novelty. This habit can easily turn into a cycle: people buy something, enjoy it briefly, and then soon begin looking for the next upgrade.","chinese":"另一個原因是，許多產品被設計成很快就讓人覺得過時。 例如，科技公司每年都會推出新型號，即使改進其實相對有限。 一個人的手機即使仍然運作良好，也可能因為新版本看起來更時尚或速度稍快，而想要更換它。 這樣一來，購物便不再主要是為了解決真正的問題，而更像是在追逐新鮮感。 這種習慣很容易變成一個循環：人們買下某樣東西，短暫享受它，然後很快又開始尋找下一次升級。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 3","english":"I do not think this is a good thing. On a personal level, unnecessary consumption can lead to wasted money and poor financial habits, especially among people who buy on credit. More seriously, it creates environmental damage because discarded goods often end up as electronic waste, plastic waste, or landfill. Producing constant replacements also consumes energy and natural resources that could be used more responsibly.","chinese":"我不認為這是一件好事。 在個人層面上，不必要的消費可能導致金錢浪費和不良的理財習慣，尤其是在那些使用信貸購物的人身上。 更嚴重的是，它會造成環境破壞，因為被丟棄的商品往往最終變成電子垃圾、塑膠垃圾或堆填區廢物。 持續生產替代品也會消耗能源和自然資源，而這些資源本可以被更負責任地使用。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, people often buy needless products because advertising, social comparison, and rapid product cycles make unnecessary purchases seem attractive. However, this behaviour is harmful because it encourages financial waste and places avoidable pressure on the environment.","chinese":"總結來說，人們經常購買不必要的產品，是因為廣告、社會比較和快速的產品週期，令不必要的購買看起來具有吸引力。 然而，這種行為是有害的，因為它鼓勵金錢浪費，並對環境造成本可避免的壓力。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"modern consumer societies","chinese":"現代消費社會"},{"english":"be no longer limited to","chinese":"不再局限於"},{"english":"meeting basic needs","chinese":"滿足基本需要"},{"english":"purchase items","chinese":"購買物品"},{"english":"could easily live without","chinese":"沒有也可以輕易生活"},{"english":"perfectly functional products","chinese":"功能完全正常的產品"},{"english":"long before necessary","chinese":"遠早於有需要之前"},{"english":"this behaviour","chinese":"這種行為"},{"english":"mainly driven by","chinese":"主要由……推動"},{"english":"advertising and social pressure","chinese":"廣告和社會壓力"},{"english":"a negative development","chinese":"負面發展"},{"english":"one major reason","chinese":"一個主要原因"},{"english":"unnecessary goods","chinese":"不必要的商品"},{"english":"highly skilled at","chinese":"非常擅長"},{"english":"creating desire","chinese":"製造慾望"},{"english":"ordinary objects","chinese":"普通物件"},{"english":"instead","chinese":"相反；而是"},{"english":"connect them with","chinese":"將它們與……連繫起來"},{"english":"social belonging","chinese":"社會歸屬感"},{"english":"As a result","chinese":"結果"},{"english":"start to feel that","chinese":"開始覺得"},{"english":"owning the newest phone","chinese":"擁有最新手機"},{"english":"household device","chinese":"家用裝置"},{"english":"improve their identity","chinese":"提升自己的身份形象"},{"english":"rather than simply serve","chinese":"而不只是發揮"},{"english":"a practical function","chinese":"實際功能"},{"english":"even stronger on social media","chinese":"在社交媒體上更強"},{"english":"constantly exposed to","chinese":"不斷接觸到"},{"english":"influencers","chinese":"網紅"},{"english":"displaying new purchases","chinese":"展示新購買的物品"},{"english":"consumption becomes a way to","chinese":"消費成為一種……的方式"},{"english":"gain approval","chinese":"獲得認同"},{"english":"more likely to","chinese":"更有可能"},{"english":"genuinely need","chinese":"真正需要"},{"english":"another reason","chinese":"另一個原因"},{"english":"be designed to","chinese":"被設計成"},{"english":"feel outdated","chinese":"感覺過時"},{"english":"very quickly","chinese":"很快"},{"english":"technology companies","chinese":"科技公司"},{"english":"release new models","chinese":"推出新型號"},{"english":"every year","chinese":"每年"},{"english":"relatively minor","chinese":"相對輕微"},{"english":"still works well","chinese":"仍然運作良好"},{"english":"feel tempted to","chinese":"忍不住想"},{"english":"replace it","chinese":"替換它"},{"english":"the newer version","chinese":"較新的版本"},{"english":"more fashionable","chinese":"更時尚"},{"english":"slightly faster","chinese":"稍快一點"},{"english":"In this way","chinese":"以這種方式"},{"english":"becomes less about...and more about...","chinese":"較少是關於……而更多是關於……"},{"english":"solving real problems","chinese":"解決實際問題"},{"english":"chasing novelty","chinese":"追求新鮮感"},{"english":"turn into a cycle","chinese":"變成一個循環"},{"english":"enjoy it briefly","chinese":"短暫享受它"},{"english":"begin looking for","chinese":"開始尋找"},{"english":"the next upgrade","chinese":"下一次升級"},{"english":"on a personal level","chinese":"在個人層面上"},{"english":"unnecessary consumption","chinese":"不必要消費"},{"english":"lead to","chinese":"導致"},{"english":"wasted money","chinese":"浪費金錢"},{"english":"poor financial habits","chinese":"不良財務習慣"},{"english":"buy on credit","chinese":"賒購；用信貸購買"},{"english":"more seriously","chinese":"更嚴重的是"},{"english":"environmental damage","chinese":"環境破壞"},{"english":"discarded goods","chinese":"被丟棄的商品"},{"english":"end up as","chinese":"最終成為"},{"english":"electronic waste","chinese":"電子廢物"},{"english":"plastic waste","chinese":"塑膠廢物"},{"english":"landfill","chinese":"堆填區"},{"english":"constant replacements","chinese":"不斷替換的產品"},{"english":"consumes energy","chinese":"消耗能源"},{"english":"natural resources","chinese":"天然資源"},{"english":"used more responsibly","chinese":"更負責任地使用"},{"english":"needless products","chinese":"不必要產品"},{"english":"social comparison","chinese":"社會比較"},{"english":"rapid product cycles","chinese":"快速產品週期"},{"english":"unnecessary purchases","chinese":"不必要購買"},{"english":"harmful","chinese":"有害的"},{"english":"encourages financial waste","chinese":"鼓勵金錢浪費"},{"english":"places avoidable pressure on","chinese":"對……造成可避免的壓力"},{"english":"the environment","chinese":"環境"}]},"model-essay-35-ielts-discuss-both-views":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-35-ielts-discuss-both-views","essayKey":"discuss-both-views:35","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-35-ielts-discuss-both-views","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/discuss-both-views-your-opinion/EdmundBd9ExpBth-Q35","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"Risk has always been part of sport, yet the question is whether the state should remove that risk by banning dangerous activities altogether. While supporters of prohibition believe this would protect people from serious harm, I firmly believe that adults should remain free to choose such sports, provided that proper safety rules are enforced.","chinese":"風險一直都是運動的一部分，然而問題在於，政府是否應該透過全面禁止危險活動來消除這種風險。 雖然支持禁止的人認為這樣可以保護人們免受嚴重傷害， 我堅定地認為，只要適當的安全規則得到執行，成年人仍然應該有自由選擇這類運動"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"Those who favour banning dangerous sports have a reasonable concern: some activities can lead to severe injury or death even when participants are experienced. Sports such as rock climbing, boxing, motor racing, and skydiving do not merely involve mild discomfort; one mistake can cause permanent damage. If an amateur climber ignores bad weather, for instance, rescue teams may have to risk their own lives to save him. In this sense, dangerous sports can create costs not only for the individual but also for families, medical services, and the wider community. From this perspective, a ban may seem like a simple way to prevent avoidable tragedy.","chinese":"支持禁止危險運動的人有一個合理的擔憂：有些活動即使參與者經驗豐富，也可能導致嚴重受傷或死亡。 攀岩、拳擊、賽車和跳傘等運動並不只是帶來輕微不適；一個錯誤便可造成永久性傷害 例如，如果一名業餘攀岩者忽視惡劣天氣，救援隊可能不得不冒著自己的生命危險去拯救他。 從這個意義上說，危險運動不但可能令個人付出代價，也可能令家庭、醫療服務和更廣泛的社區承受負擔。 從這個角度來看，禁令似乎是一種防止可避免悲劇的簡單方法。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"However, I believe this argument goes too far because personal freedom should not be sacrificed simply because an activity contains risk. Many meaningful human experiences, from travelling alone to starting a business, involve danger or uncertainty, but society does not ban them for that reason. A better response is strict regulation. For example, skydiving centres can require professional instructors, medical checks, age limits, high-quality equipment, and emergency procedures. These measures reduce unnecessary danger while still allowing people to test their courage, discipline, and physical limits. If a sport is driven underground by a ban, it may become even less safe because participants will no longer operate under official supervision.","chinese":"然而，我認為這種論點走得太遠，因為個人自由不應該僅僅因為某項活動包含風險就被犧牲。 許多有意義的人類經歷，從獨自旅行到創業，都包含危險或不確定性，但社會並不會因此禁止它們。 更好的應對方法是嚴格監管。 例如，跳傘中心可以要求專業教練、身體檢查、年齡限制、高質素裝備和緊急程序。 這些措施可以減少不必要的危險，同時仍然允許人們考驗自己的勇氣、紀律和身體極限 如果一項運動因禁令而轉入地下，它可能會變得更加不安全，因為參與者將不再受到官方監管。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, although dangerous sports can produce serious consequences, banning them is not the right solution. People should be allowed to take part in these activities because freedom, responsibility, and well-designed safety standards are a stronger answer than outright prohibition.","chinese":"總結來說，雖然危險運動可能帶來嚴重後果，但禁止它們並不是正確的解決方法。 人們應該被允許參與這些活動，因為自由、責任和設計良好的安全標準，比全面禁止更能有效回應這個問題。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"be part of","chinese":"是……的一部分"},{"english":"the question is whether","chinese":"問題在於是否"},{"english":"the state","chinese":"國家；政府"},{"english":"remove that risk","chinese":"消除那種風險"},{"english":"banning dangerous activities altogether","chinese":"完全禁止危險活動"},{"english":"supporters of prohibition","chinese":"禁令支持者"},{"english":"protect people from serious harm","chinese":"保護人們免受嚴重傷害"},{"english":"firmly believe that","chinese":"堅信"},{"english":"remain free to choose","chinese":"仍然有自由選擇"},{"english":"provided that","chinese":"只要；前提是"},{"english":"proper safety rules","chinese":"適當安全規則"},{"english":"be enforced","chinese":"被執行"},{"english":"favour banning","chinese":"支持禁止"},{"english":"dangerous sports","chinese":"危險運動"},{"english":"a reasonable concern","chinese":"合理擔憂"},{"english":"lead to severe injury or death","chinese":"導致嚴重受傷或死亡"},{"english":"even when","chinese":"即使在……時"},{"english":"participants are experienced","chinese":"參加者有經驗"},{"english":"sports such as","chinese":"例如……的運動"},{"english":"rock climbing","chinese":"攀石"},{"english":"motor racing","chinese":"賽車"},{"english":"skydiving","chinese":"跳傘"},{"english":"do not merely involve","chinese":"不只是涉及"},{"english":"mild discomfort","chinese":"輕微不適"},{"english":"one mistake can cause","chinese":"一個錯誤可以造成"},{"english":"permanent damage","chinese":"永久傷害"},{"english":"an amateur climber","chinese":"業餘攀山者"},{"english":"ignore bad weather","chinese":"忽視惡劣天氣"},{"english":"rescue teams","chinese":"救援隊"},{"english":"risk their own lives","chinese":"冒生命危險"},{"english":"in this sense","chinese":"從這個意義上說"},{"english":"create costs not only for","chinese":"不只為……帶來代價"},{"english":"the individual","chinese":"個人"},{"english":"medical services","chinese":"醫療服務"},{"english":"the wider community","chinese":"更廣泛的社群"},{"english":"from this perspective","chinese":"從這個角度來看"},{"english":"seem like a simple way to","chinese":"看似是……的簡單方法"},{"english":"prevent avoidable tragedy","chinese":"防止可避免的悲劇"},{"english":"this argument goes too far","chinese":"這個論點走得太遠"},{"english":"personal freedom","chinese":"個人自由"},{"english":"should not be sacrificed","chinese":"不應被犧牲"},{"english":"simply because","chinese":"只因為"},{"english":"contain risk","chinese":"帶有風險"},{"english":"meaningful human experiences","chinese":"有意義的人生經歷"},{"english":"travelling alone","chinese":"獨自旅行"},{"english":"starting a business","chinese":"創業"},{"english":"involve danger or uncertainty","chinese":"涉及危險或不確定性"},{"english":"for that reason","chinese":"因為那個原因"},{"english":"a better response","chinese":"更好的回應"},{"english":"strict regulation","chinese":"嚴格監管"},{"english":"professional instructors","chinese":"專業教練"},{"english":"medical checks","chinese":"醫療檢查"},{"english":"age limits","chinese":"年齡限制"},{"english":"high-quality equipment","chinese":"高質素裝備"},{"english":"emergency procedures","chinese":"緊急程序"},{"english":"reduce unnecessary danger","chinese":"減少不必要危險"},{"english":"while still allowing","chinese":"同時仍然容許"},{"english":"test their courage","chinese":"考驗自己的勇氣"},{"english":"physical limits","chinese":"身體極限"},{"english":"be driven underground by","chinese":"因禁令而轉入地下"},{"english":"become even less safe","chinese":"變得更加不安全"},{"english":"operate under official supervision","chinese":"在官方監督下進行"},{"english":"produce serious consequences","chinese":"造成嚴重後果"},{"english":"the right solution","chinese":"正確的解決方法"},{"english":"be allowed to take part in","chinese":"被容許參與"},{"english":"freedom, responsibility, and well-designed safety standards","chinese":"自由、責任和設計完善的安全標準"},{"english":"a stronger answer than","chinese":"比……更有力的答案"},{"english":"outright prohibition","chinese":"全面禁止"}]},"model-essay-35-ielts-opinion":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-35-ielts-opinion","essayKey":"opinion:35","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-35-ielts-opinion","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/opinions/EdmundBd9OP-Q35","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"In my view, parents should not be punished when their children commit crimes. Although family upbringing undeniably shapes a young person’s character, criminal punishment must be based on personal responsibility, not guilt by association.","chinese":"我認為，當孩子犯罪時，父母不應該受到懲罰。 儘管家庭教育無疑會塑造一個年輕人的性格，但刑事懲罰必須建立在個人責任之上，而不是基於連坐式的罪責。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"The first reason is that blaming parents for a child’s offence would make the justice system deeply unfair. Children, especially teenagers, are influenced by many forces beyond the home, including friends, online content, school pressure, and the neighbourhood in which they grow up. A mother and father may set clear rules, teach right from wrong, and still be unable to control every decision their child makes outside the house. If a teenager steals from a shop after being encouraged by a peer group, punishing the parents would not address the actual choice made by the offender. It would simply turn the family into a convenient scapegoat, which is a dangerous way to administer justice.","chinese":"第一個原因是，把孩子的罪行歸咎於父母，會使司法制度變得極不公平。 孩子，尤其是青少年，會受到家庭以外許多力量的影響，包括朋友、網上內容、學校壓力，以及他們成長的社區環境。 父母可能已經訂立清晰規矩、教導孩子分辨是非，但仍然無法控制孩子在家以外作出的每一個決定。 如果一名青少年在同輩群體的鼓動下從商店偷竊，懲罰父母並不能處理犯罪者本身作出的實際選擇。 這只會把家庭變成一個方便的代罪羔羊，而這是一種危險的司法執行方式。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"Another important point is that punishing parents may make youth crime harder to solve. When parents fear fines, prosecution, or public disgrace, they may become defensive and less willing to work with teachers, police officers, or social workers. This would damage the very cooperation that young offenders often need in order to change. By contrast, if parents are treated as partners in rehabilitation, they can help rebuild routines, monitor behaviour, and guide their child away from harmful influences. For example, a young offender who is required to attend counselling is far more likely to improve if the family supports the process rather than feels attacked by it. In this sense, parental punishment may satisfy public anger, but it is unlikely to produce safer communities.","chinese":"另一個重要觀點是，懲罰父母可能會使青少年犯罪更難解決。 當父母害怕罰款、檢控或公開羞辱時，他們可能會變得防衛，並且較不願意與教師、警察或社工合作。 這會破壞青少年犯人改變時往往最需要的那種合作。 相比之下，如果父母被視為改過自新過程中的合作夥伴，他們便可以幫助孩子重建生活規律、監察行為，並引導孩子遠離有害影響。 例如，一名被要求接受輔導的青少年犯人，如果家庭支持這個過程，而不是覺得自己受到攻擊，他便更有可能改善。 從這個角度來看，懲罰父母或許能滿足公眾怒氣，但它不太可能創造出更安全的社區。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, I disagree that parents should be punished for crimes committed by their children. Responsibility should fall on the offender, while parents should be encouraged to assist with rehabilitation rather than be treated as criminals themselves.","chinese":"總結來說，我不同意父母應該因孩子所犯的罪行而受到懲罰。 責任應該落在犯罪者身上，而父母應該被鼓勵協助改過自新，而不是被當作罪犯看待。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"in my view","chinese":"在我看來"},{"english":"be punished when","chinese":"在……時受到懲罰"},{"english":"commit crimes","chinese":"犯罪"},{"english":"family upbringing","chinese":"家庭教養"},{"english":"undeniably shapes","chinese":"無可否認地塑造"},{"english":"young person's character","chinese":"年輕人的性格"},{"english":"criminal punishment","chinese":"刑事懲罰"},{"english":"be based on","chinese":"建基於"},{"english":"personal responsibility","chinese":"個人責任"},{"english":"guilt by association","chinese":"連坐式歸罪"},{"english":"blaming parents for","chinese":"因……而責怪父母"},{"english":"child's offence","chinese":"孩子的違法行為"},{"english":"justice system","chinese":"司法制度"},{"english":"deeply unfair","chinese":"極不公平"},{"english":"be influenced by","chinese":"受……影響"},{"english":"forces beyond the home","chinese":"家庭以外的力量"},{"english":"online content","chinese":"網上內容"},{"english":"school pressure","chinese":"學校壓力"},{"english":"neighbourhood","chinese":"社區；居住環境"},{"english":"grow up","chinese":"成長"},{"english":"set clear rules","chinese":"訂立清晰規則"},{"english":"teach right from wrong","chinese":"教導分辨是非"},{"english":"be unable to control","chinese":"無法控制"},{"english":"outside the house","chinese":"在家以外"},{"english":"steals from a shop","chinese":"從商店偷東西"},{"english":"be encouraged by","chinese":"受到……鼓動"},{"english":"peer group","chinese":"同輩群體"},{"english":"address the actual choice","chinese":"處理實際選擇"},{"english":"offender","chinese":"犯事者"},{"english":"convenient scapegoat","chinese":"方便的代罪羔羊"},{"english":"administer justice","chinese":"執行司法公義"},{"english":"youth crime","chinese":"青少年犯罪"},{"english":"harder to solve","chinese":"更難解決"},{"english":"fear fines","chinese":"害怕罰款"},{"english":"prosecution","chinese":"檢控"},{"english":"public disgrace","chinese":"公開蒙羞"},{"english":"become defensive","chinese":"變得有戒心"},{"english":"less willing to work with","chinese":"較不願意與……合作"},{"english":"police officers","chinese":"警務人員"},{"english":"social workers","chinese":"社工"},{"english":"damage the very cooperation","chinese":"損害正正需要的合作"},{"english":"young offenders","chinese":"青少年犯事者"},{"english":"in order to change","chinese":"為了改變"},{"english":"partners in rehabilitation","chinese":"更生過程中的合作伙伴"},{"english":"rebuild routines","chinese":"重建日常規律"},{"english":"monitor behaviour","chinese":"監察行為"},{"english":"guide their child away from","chinese":"引導孩子遠離……"},{"english":"harmful influences","chinese":"有害影響"},{"english":"be required to attend counselling","chinese":"被要求接受輔導"},{"english":"far more likely to improve","chinese":"更加有可能改善"},{"english":"supports the process","chinese":"支持這個過程"},{"english":"rather than feels attacked by it","chinese":"而不是覺得受到攻擊"},{"english":"satisfy public anger","chinese":"滿足公眾怒氣"},{"english":"unlikely to produce","chinese":"不大可能帶來"},{"english":"safer communities","chinese":"更安全的社區"},{"english":"crimes committed by","chinese":"由……犯下的罪行"},{"english":"responsibility should fall on","chinese":"責任應落在……身上"},{"english":"be encouraged to assist with","chinese":"被鼓勵協助……"},{"english":"rather than be treated as","chinese":"而不是被視為"},{"english":"criminals themselves","chinese":"他們本人也是罪犯"}]},"model-essay-36-ielts-direct-question":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-36-ielts-direct-question","essayKey":"direct-question:36","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-36-ielts-direct-question","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/direct-question/EdmundBd9Dir-Q36","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"A child’s first years at school are often shaped by what has already happened before formal education begins. Early reading is especially important because it gives children access to language, instructions and ideas, all of which are central to academic learning. However, reading alone does not determine success; preschool children are also strongly influenced by their home environment, social development and emotional readiness.","chinese":"孩子在學校最初幾年的表現，往往受到正式教育開始之前已經發生的事情所影響。 早期閱讀尤其重要，因為它讓孩子接觸語言、指示和思想，而這些全都是學術學習的核心。 然而，單靠閱讀並不能決定成功；學前兒童也會受到家庭環境、社交發展和情緒準備程度的強烈影響。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"Early reading skills play a crucial role in academic performance because they form the gateway to almost every subject. A child who can recognise words, follow a sentence and understand a simple story is not merely learning English; they are learning how to learn. For example, even a basic mathematics worksheet requires pupils to read questions accurately, while science depends heavily on understanding explanations. Early readers are therefore less likely to feel lost in class and more likely to build confidence as schoolwork becomes harder. This confidence can become a quiet engine of progress, pushing them to ask questions, complete tasks independently and develop stronger study habits.","chinese":"早期閱讀能力在學業表現中扮演關鍵角色，因為它們幾乎是通往每一個學科的入口。 一個能夠認字、理解句子並明白簡單故事的孩子，並不只是正在學習英文；他們是在學習如何學習。 例如，即使是一份基本的數學工作紙，也要求學生準確閱讀題目，而科學則高度依賴對解釋內容的理解。 因此，早期具備閱讀能力的孩子在課堂上較不容易感到迷失，也更有可能在課業變得更困難時建立自信。 這份自信可以成為一個安靜卻有力的進步引擎，推動他們提出問題、獨立完成任務，並培養更強的學習習慣。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"That said, several other preschool factors also shape later achievement. One of the most important is parental involvement, especially when parents talk to children regularly, answer their questions and create a calm routine at home. Such children often arrive at school with better vocabulary, stronger concentration and a clearer sense that learning matters. Social and emotional development is another key factor. Children who can share toys, wait for their turn and cope with small frustrations are usually better prepared for classroom life. In this sense, preschool success is not only built with books; it is also built through conversation, play and stable relationships.","chinese":"話雖如此，其他幾個學前因素也會塑造孩子日後的成就。 其中最重要的因素之一是父母的參與，尤其是當父母經常與孩子交談、回答他們的問題，並在家中建立平穩的日常規律時。 這樣的孩子入學時通常已經具備更好的詞彙量、更強的專注力，以及更清楚明白學習是重要的。 社交和情緒發展是另一個關鍵因素。 能夠分享玩具、等待輪到自己，以及處理小挫折的孩子，通常更能為課堂生活作好準備。 從這個意義上說，學前成功並不只是由書本建立起來的；它也透過對話、遊戲和穩定的關係建立起來。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, early reading skills are extremely important because they support understanding, confidence and independent learning across the curriculum. Nevertheless, a child’s academic future is also shaped by family support, emotional maturity and social habits developed before school.","chinese":"總結來說，早期閱讀能力極為重要，因為它們支撐孩子在整個課程中的理解力、自信心和獨立學習能力。 然而，一個孩子的學業未來也會受到入學前已經建立的家庭支持、情緒成熟度和社交習慣所塑造。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"a child's first years at school","chinese":"孩子最初幾年的學校生活"},{"english":"be shaped by","chinese":"受……塑造"},{"english":"formal education","chinese":"正規教育"},{"english":"early reading","chinese":"早期閱讀"},{"english":"gives children access to","chinese":"讓孩子接觸到"},{"english":"language, instructions and ideas","chinese":"語言、指示和概念"},{"english":"be central to","chinese":"對……至關重要"},{"english":"academic learning","chinese":"學業學習"},{"english":"reading alone","chinese":"單靠閱讀"},{"english":"determine success","chinese":"決定成功"},{"english":"preschool children","chinese":"學前兒童"},{"english":"strongly influenced by","chinese":"深受……影響"},{"english":"home environment","chinese":"家庭環境"},{"english":"social development","chinese":"社交發展"},{"english":"emotional readiness","chinese":"情緒準備程度"},{"english":"play a crucial role in","chinese":"在……中扮演關鍵角色"},{"english":"academic performance","chinese":"學業表現"},{"english":"form the gateway to","chinese":"成為通往……的門戶"},{"english":"almost every subject","chinese":"幾乎每一個科目"},{"english":"recognise words","chinese":"認字"},{"english":"follow a sentence","chinese":"理解一句句子"},{"english":"understand a simple story","chinese":"理解簡單故事"},{"english":"not merely learning","chinese":"不只是學習"},{"english":"learning how to learn","chinese":"學會如何學習"},{"english":"a basic mathematics worksheet","chinese":"基本數學工作紙"},{"english":"requires pupils to","chinese":"要求學生去"},{"english":"read questions accurately","chinese":"準確閱讀題目"},{"english":"depends heavily on","chinese":"很大程度上取決於"},{"english":"understanding explanations","chinese":"理解解釋"},{"english":"less likely to","chinese":"較不可能"},{"english":"feel lost in class","chinese":"在課堂上感到迷失"},{"english":"more likely to","chinese":"更有可能"},{"english":"build confidence","chinese":"建立信心"},{"english":"schoolwork becomes harder","chinese":"學校功課變得更難"},{"english":"a quiet engine of progress","chinese":"默默推動進步的力量"},{"english":"push them to","chinese":"推動他們去"},{"english":"ask questions","chinese":"提問"},{"english":"complete tasks independently","chinese":"獨立完成任務"},{"english":"develop stronger study habits","chinese":"建立更強的學習習慣"},{"english":"That said","chinese":"話雖如此"},{"english":"preschool factors","chinese":"學前因素"},{"english":"shape later achievement","chinese":"塑造日後成就"},{"english":"parental involvement","chinese":"父母參與"},{"english":"talk to children regularly","chinese":"定期與孩子交談"},{"english":"answer their questions","chinese":"回答他們的問題"},{"english":"create a calm routine at home","chinese":"在家中建立平靜規律"},{"english":"arrive at school with","chinese":"帶着……入學"},{"english":"better vocabulary","chinese":"更好的詞彙量"},{"english":"stronger concentration","chinese":"更強的專注力"},{"english":"a clearer sense that","chinese":"更清楚意識到"},{"english":"learning matters","chinese":"學習很重要"},{"english":"another key factor","chinese":"另一個關鍵因素"},{"english":"share toys","chinese":"分享玩具"},{"english":"wait for their turn","chinese":"等候輪到自己"},{"english":"cope with small frustrations","chinese":"應付小挫折"},{"english":"better prepared for","chinese":"為……作好更充分準備"},{"english":"classroom life","chinese":"課堂生活"},{"english":"In this sense","chinese":"從這個意義上說"},{"english":"built with books","chinese":"由書本建立"},{"english":"through conversation, play and stable relationships","chinese":"透過交談、遊戲和穩定關係"},{"english":"stable relationships","chinese":"穩定關係"},{"english":"support understanding","chinese":"支持理解"},{"english":"independent learning","chinese":"獨立學習"},{"english":"across the curriculum","chinese":"橫跨整個課程"},{"english":"academic future","chinese":"學業前途"},{"english":"family support","chinese":"家庭支援"},{"english":"emotional maturity","chinese":"情緒成熟"},{"english":"social habits","chinese":"社交習慣"},{"english":"developed before school","chinese":"在入學前培養"}]},"model-essay-36-ielts-discuss-both-views":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-36-ielts-discuss-both-views","essayKey":"discuss-both-views:36","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-36-ielts-discuss-both-views","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/discuss-both-views-your-opinion/EdmundBd9ExpBth-Q36","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"Sport plays an important role in childhood because it teaches lessons that are difficult to learn only from books. Some people argue that its main value is that it trains children to compete, whereas others believe that it primarily develops teamwork. I will discuss both views, but I strongly believe that teamwork is the more valuable lesson.","chinese":"運動在童年中扮演重要角色，因為它能教會孩子一些單靠書本難以學到的道理。 有些人認為，運動最主要的價值在於訓練孩子競爭；然而，另一些人則相信，運動主要培養的是團隊合作能力。 我將討論雙方觀點，但我強烈認為，團隊合作是更有價值的一課。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"On the one hand, sport clearly helps children understand healthy competition. When young people take part in races, matches, or tournaments, they learn that success usually comes from effort, discipline, and preparation rather than luck. This matters because children who never face competition may struggle when they later meet academic pressure, job interviews, or professional rivalry. For example, a child who loses a football match can learn to accept disappointment, analyse mistakes, and try again instead of giving up. In this sense, competition can build resilience and teach children how to win modestly and lose gracefully.","chinese":"一方面，運動顯然能幫助孩子理解健康的競爭。 當年輕人參加賽跑、比賽或錦標賽時，他們會明白成功通常來自努力、自律和準備，而不是運氣。 這一點很重要，因為從未面對過競爭的孩子，日後遇到學業壓力、工作面試或職場競爭時，可能會難以應對。 例如，一個輸掉足球比賽的孩子，可以學會接受失望、分析錯誤，並再次嘗試，而不是選擇放棄。 從這個意義上說，競爭能建立孩子的抗逆力，並教會他們如何謙遜地勝利，以及有風度地面對失敗。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"On the other hand, team sports are even more powerful because they show children that achievement often depends on cooperation. In games such as basketball or football, no player can succeed simply by showing individual talent; children must pass, communicate, trust their teammates, and sometimes put the group’s interest before personal glory. This creates a practical lesson that reaches far beyond the sports field. For instance, a child who learns to listen to teammates during a match is also more likely to contribute well in classroom projects or future workplaces. Since most real-life success depends on working with other people, teamwork is a deeper and more transferable skill than competition alone.","chinese":"另一方面，團隊運動更具影響力，因為它們讓孩子明白，成就往往取決於合作。 在籃球或足球這類運動中，沒有任何球員能單靠個人天分取得成功；孩子必須傳球、溝通、信任隊友，有時還要把團隊利益置於個人榮耀之上。 這帶來了一種實用的教育意義，而且其影響遠遠超出運動場本身。 例如，一個在比賽中學會聆聽隊友的孩子，也更有可能在課堂小組項目或未來職場中作出良好貢獻。 由於現實生活中的大多數成功都取決於與他人合作，因此團隊合作比單純的競爭更深層，也更具可轉移性。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, sport does teach children how to compete, especially by helping them deal with pressure, failure, and self-improvement. However, I believe its greatest benefit is that it teaches teamwork, because cooperation, trust, and shared responsibility are essential in school, work, and society.","chinese":"總結來說，運動確實能教會孩子如何競爭，尤其是幫助他們應對壓力、失敗和自我提升 然而，我認為運動最大的好處是它能教會孩子團隊合作，因為合作、信任和共同責任在學校、工作和社會中都是不可或缺的。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"play an important role in","chinese":"在……中扮演重要角色"},{"english":"childhood","chinese":"童年"},{"english":"teach lessons that are difficult to learn","chinese":"教授難以學會的道理"},{"english":"only from books","chinese":"只從書本中"},{"english":"its main value","chinese":"其主要價值"},{"english":"train children to compete","chinese":"訓練兒童競爭"},{"english":"whereas","chinese":"然而"},{"english":"primarily develops teamwork","chinese":"主要培養團隊合作"},{"english":"discuss both views","chinese":"討論雙方觀點"},{"english":"strongly believe that","chinese":"強烈相信"},{"english":"the more valuable lesson","chinese":"更有價值的一課"},{"english":"on the one hand","chinese":"一方面"},{"english":"healthy competition","chinese":"健康競爭"},{"english":"take part in","chinese":"參加"},{"english":"races, matches, or tournaments","chinese":"賽跑、比賽或錦標賽"},{"english":"success usually comes from","chinese":"成功通常來自"},{"english":"effort, discipline, and preparation","chinese":"努力、自律和準備"},{"english":"rather than luck","chinese":"而不是運氣"},{"english":"this matters because","chinese":"這一點很重要，因為"},{"english":"face competition","chinese":"面對競爭"},{"english":"may struggle when","chinese":"在……時可能會感到吃力"},{"english":"academic pressure","chinese":"學業壓力"},{"english":"job interviews","chinese":"求職面試"},{"english":"professional rivalry","chinese":"職場競爭"},{"english":"lose a football match","chinese":"輸掉一場足球比賽"},{"english":"accept disappointment","chinese":"接受失望"},{"english":"analyse mistakes","chinese":"分析錯誤"},{"english":"try again instead of giving up","chinese":"再嘗試而不是放棄"},{"english":"in this sense","chinese":"從這個意義上說"},{"english":"build resilience","chinese":"建立抗逆力"},{"english":"win modestly","chinese":"謙虛地勝出"},{"english":"lose gracefully","chinese":"有風度地落敗"},{"english":"on the other hand","chinese":"另一方面"},{"english":"team sports","chinese":"團隊運動"},{"english":"even more powerful","chinese":"更有力量；影響更大"},{"english":"achievement often depends on","chinese":"成就往往取決於"},{"english":"cooperation","chinese":"合作"},{"english":"in games such as","chinese":"在例如……的比賽中"},{"english":"no player can succeed simply by","chinese":"沒有球員可以單靠……成功"},{"english":"individual talent","chinese":"個人才華"},{"english":"trust their teammates","chinese":"信任隊友"},{"english":"put the group's interest before","chinese":"將團隊利益放在……之前"},{"english":"personal glory","chinese":"個人榮耀"},{"english":"create a practical lesson","chinese":"帶來實用的一課"},{"english":"reach far beyond","chinese":"遠遠超出"},{"english":"the sports field","chinese":"運動場"},{"english":"for instance","chinese":"例如"},{"english":"listen to teammates","chinese":"聆聽隊友"},{"english":"during a match","chinese":"在比賽期間"},{"english":"be more likely to","chinese":"更有可能"},{"english":"contribute well in","chinese":"在……中作出良好貢獻"},{"english":"classroom projects","chinese":"課堂項目"},{"english":"future workplaces","chinese":"未來職場"},{"english":"since most real-life success depends on","chinese":"由於大多數現實成功取決於"},{"english":"real-life success","chinese":"現實生活中的成功"},{"english":"working with other people","chinese":"與他人合作"},{"english":"a deeper and more transferable skill","chinese":"更深入且更能轉移應用的技能"},{"english":"competition alone","chinese":"單靠競爭"},{"english":"deal with pressure","chinese":"應對壓力"},{"english":"failure and self-improvement","chinese":"失敗和自我提升"},{"english":"its greatest benefit","chinese":"其最大好處"},{"english":"cooperation, trust, and shared responsibility","chinese":"合作、信任和共同責任"},{"english":"shared responsibility","chinese":"共同責任"},{"english":"be essential in","chinese":"在……中不可或缺"},{"english":"school, work, and society","chinese":"學校、工作和社會"}]},"model-essay-36-ielts-opinion":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-36-ielts-opinion","essayKey":"opinion:36","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-36-ielts-opinion","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/opinions/EdmundBd9OP-Q36","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"For centuries, literacy and numeracy have formed the core of schooling because they allow people to read information, express ideas and solve practical problems. In the digital age, however, I completely agree that computer skills should be treated as a fourth fundamental skill, since they are now essential for learning, employment and responsible participation in society.","chinese":"幾個世紀以來，讀寫能力和計算能力一直構成學校教育的核心，因為它們使人能夠閱讀資訊、表達想法並解決實際問題。 然而，在數碼時代，我完全同意電腦技能應被視為第四項基本技能，因為它們如今對學習、就業以及負責任地參與社會都至關重要。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"The strongest reason is that computers have become one of the main gateways to knowledge. A student who cannot use basic software, search engines or online learning platforms is no longer simply missing a technical ability; he or she is cut off from a large part of modern education. For example, research assignments often require students to find credible sources, organize files, produce presentations and submit work through digital systems. If these skills are left to chance, students from less technologically confident families may fall behind, even when they are intelligent and hardworking. Teaching computer literacy systematically would therefore make education fairer and more complete.","chinese":"最有力的原因是，電腦已經成為通往知識的主要門戶之一。 一個不會使用基本軟件、搜尋引擎或網上學習平台的學生，不再只是缺少一項技術能力；他或她其實是被切斷了與現代教育很大一部分的連接。 例如，研究作業經常要求學生尋找可信資料來源、整理檔案、製作簡報，並透過數碼系統提交功課。 如果這些技能被任由學生自行摸索，來自較缺乏科技信心家庭的學生便可能落後，即使他們本身聰明又勤奮。 因此，系統地教授電腦素養會使教育更加公平，也更加完整。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"Computer skills are also indispensable beyond the classroom. In many workplaces, even ordinary jobs now involve emails, spreadsheets, databases, video meetings or digital payment systems. A person who reads well and calculates accurately may still struggle if they cannot handle these tools efficiently. More importantly, computer education can teach pupils how to use technology safely and responsibly. They need to understand privacy, online scams, passwords and the difference between reliable information and digital noise. Without this guidance, computers may become a source of confusion rather than empowerment.","chinese":"電腦技能在課室之外同樣不可或缺。 在許多工作場所中，即使是普通工作，如今也涉及電子郵件、試算表、資料庫、視像會議或數碼支付系統。 一個閱讀能力強、計算準確的人，如果不能有效地操作這些工具，仍然可能在工作上遇到困難。 更重要的是，電腦教育能教導學生如何安全並負責任地使用科技。 他們需要理解私隱、網上騙局、密碼安全，以及可靠資訊與數碼雜音之間的分別。 如果沒有這種指導，電腦可能會成為混亂的來源，而不是賦能的工具。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, reading, writing and mathematics remain irreplaceable, but they are no longer sufficient by themselves. Computer literacy should be added as a fourth core skill because it gives students access to knowledge, improves their future employability and helps them navigate the digital world with judgment rather than fear.","chinese":"總結來說，閱讀、寫作和數學仍然無可取代，但單靠它們已經不再足夠。 電腦素養應被加入為第四項核心技能，因為它讓學生能夠接觸知識、提升他們未來的就業能力，並幫助他們以判斷力而非恐懼去面對數碼世界。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"for centuries","chinese":"多個世紀以來"},{"english":"literacy and numeracy","chinese":"讀寫能力和計算能力"},{"english":"formed the core of","chinese":"構成……的核心"},{"english":"schooling","chinese":"學校教育"},{"english":"read information","chinese":"閱讀資料"},{"english":"express ideas","chinese":"表達想法"},{"english":"solve practical problems","chinese":"解決實際問題"},{"english":"in the digital age","chinese":"在數碼時代"},{"english":"computer skills","chinese":"電腦技能"},{"english":"be treated as","chinese":"被視為"},{"english":"fourth fundamental skill","chinese":"第四項基本技能"},{"english":"essential for","chinese":"對……必不可少"},{"english":"responsible participation in society","chinese":"負責任地參與社會"},{"english":"main gateways to knowledge","chinese":"通往知識的主要途徑"},{"english":"basic software","chinese":"基本軟件"},{"english":"search engines","chinese":"搜尋器"},{"english":"online learning platforms","chinese":"網上學習平台"},{"english":"no longer simply","chinese":"不再只是"},{"english":"missing a technical ability","chinese":"缺少一項技術能力"},{"english":"be cut off from","chinese":"與……隔絕"},{"english":"a large part of modern education","chinese":"現代教育的一大部分"},{"english":"research assignments","chinese":"研究功課"},{"english":"credible sources","chinese":"可信來源"},{"english":"organise files","chinese":"整理檔案"},{"english":"produce presentations","chinese":"製作簡報"},{"english":"submit work through","chinese":"透過……提交功課"},{"english":"digital systems","chinese":"數碼系統"},{"english":"be left to chance","chinese":"任由機會決定"},{"english":"technologically confident families","chinese":"對科技較有信心的家庭"},{"english":"fall behind","chinese":"落後"},{"english":"intelligent and hardworking","chinese":"聰明而勤奮"},{"english":"computer literacy","chinese":"電腦素養"},{"english":"systematically","chinese":"有系統地"},{"english":"make education fairer","chinese":"令教育更公平"},{"english":"more complete","chinese":"更完整"},{"english":"indispensable beyond the classroom","chinese":"在課室以外不可或缺"},{"english":"workplaces","chinese":"工作場所"},{"english":"ordinary jobs","chinese":"普通工作"},{"english":"involve emails","chinese":"涉及電郵"},{"english":"spreadsheets","chinese":"試算表"},{"english":"databases","chinese":"數據庫"},{"english":"video meetings","chinese":"視像會議"},{"english":"digital payment systems","chinese":"數碼支付系統"},{"english":"reads well","chinese":"閱讀能力好"},{"english":"calculates accurately","chinese":"計算準確"},{"english":"handle these tools efficiently","chinese":"高效地使用這些工具"},{"english":"more importantly","chinese":"更重要的是"},{"english":"use technology safely and responsibly","chinese":"安全而負責任地使用科技"},{"english":"understand privacy","chinese":"明白私隱"},{"english":"online scams","chinese":"網上騙案"},{"english":"passwords","chinese":"密碼"},{"english":"reliable information","chinese":"可靠資料"},{"english":"digital noise","chinese":"數碼雜音；網上雜亂資訊"},{"english":"without this guidance","chinese":"沒有這種指引"},{"english":"a source of confusion","chinese":"混亂的來源"},{"english":"rather than empowerment","chinese":"而不是賦權"},{"english":"remain irreplaceable","chinese":"仍然無可取代"},{"english":"sufficient by themselves","chinese":"單靠它們已不足夠"},{"english":"be added as","chinese":"被加入作為……"},{"english":"fourth core skill","chinese":"第四項核心技能"},{"english":"access to knowledge","chinese":"接觸知識的機會"},{"english":"future employability","chinese":"未來就業能力"},{"english":"navigate the digital world","chinese":"在數碼世界中應對自如"},{"english":"with judgment rather than fear","chinese":"憑判斷力而不是恐懼"}]},"model-essay-37-ielts-direct-question":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-37-ielts-direct-question","essayKey":"direct-question:37","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-37-ielts-direct-question","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/direct-question/EdmundBd9Dir-Q37","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"Modernisation has brought clear benefits, but it has also pushed many traditional ways of life to the margins. In my view, preserving these traditions is important because they give people cultural identity and social continuity. This can be achieved by making traditions part of education and community life, rather than treating them as museum pieces.","chinese":"現代化帶來了明顯的好處，但它也把許多傳統生活方式推向了邊緣。 在我看來，保留這些傳統是重要的，因為它們給予人們文化身份和社會延續性。 這可以透過把傳統融入教育和社區生活來實現，而不是把它們當成博物館裡的展品。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"The main reason traditional lifestyles should be protected is that they connect people with their history and with one another. Customs such as local festivals, family rituals, traditional crafts and regional food are not merely old habits; they carry shared values, memories and forms of knowledge that cannot be replaced by technology or consumer culture. When these practices disappear, younger generations may still live in modern cities, but they can lose a sense of belonging to a wider story. For example, a child who learns only global popular culture may know how to use the latest devices, yet know little about the language, manners or celebrations that shaped their grandparents’ lives. In this sense, tradition acts as a bridge between generations and helps societies remain rooted while they move forward.","chinese":"傳統生活方式應該受到保護的主要原因，是它們把人們與自己的歷史以及彼此連結起來。 本地節日、家庭儀式、傳統工藝和地區食物等習俗，並不只是舊習慣；它們承載著共同的價值觀、記憶和知識形式，而這些是科技或消費文化無法取代的。 當這些做法消失時，年輕一代也許仍然生活在現代城市中，但他們可能會失去一種屬於更大歷史故事的歸屬感。 例如，一個只接觸全球流行文化的孩子，可能知道如何使用最新的電子設備，卻對塑造祖父母生活的語言、禮儀或慶祝方式所知甚少。 從這個意義上說，傳統就像世代之間的一座橋樑，幫助社會在向前發展的同時仍然保持根基。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"However, traditions survive only if they are kept alive in practical ways. Schools should teach local history, traditional arts and community customs through activities rather than dry memorisation, so students can experience culture instead of simply reading about it. At the same time, governments and local communities should support festivals, craft markets, oral-history projects and public spaces where older people can pass on skills to the young. Technology can also help: short videos, digital archives and online lessons can make traditional knowledge accessible to people living far from their original communities.","chinese":"然而，傳統只有在以實際方式被延續時，才能真正存活下來。 學校應該透過活動教授本地歷史、傳統藝術和社區習俗，而不是依靠枯燥的背誦，這樣學生才能親身體驗文化，而不只是閱讀有關文化的內容。 同時，政府和本地社區應該支持節日活動、手工藝市集、口述歷史項目，以及讓長者能夠把技能傳授給年輕人的公共空間。 科技也可以提供幫助：短片、數碼檔案和網上課程，可以讓那些遠離原本社區生活的人也能接觸到傳統知識。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, it is important to preserve traditional ways of life because they protect cultural identity and strengthen social bonds. The best approach is not to resist modern life, but to weave tradition into education, community activities and digital platforms, so it remains a living part of society.","chinese":"總結來說，保留傳統生活方式是重要的，因為它們保護文化身份，並加強社會連繫。 最好的方法不是抗拒現代生活，而是把傳統編織進教育、社區活動和數碼平台之中，使它仍然成為社會中一個鮮活的部分。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"modernisation","chinese":"現代化"},{"english":"brought clear benefits","chinese":"帶來明顯好處"},{"english":"traditional ways of life","chinese":"傳統生活方式"},{"english":"push...to the margins","chinese":"把……推到邊緣"},{"english":"In my view","chinese":"在我看來"},{"english":"preserving these traditions","chinese":"保留這些傳統"},{"english":"cultural identity","chinese":"文化身份認同"},{"english":"social continuity","chinese":"社會延續性"},{"english":"be achieved by","chinese":"可以透過……達成"},{"english":"part of education and community life","chinese":"教育和社區生活的一部分"},{"english":"rather than treating them as","chinese":"而不是把它們視為"},{"english":"museum pieces","chinese":"博物館展品"},{"english":"the main reason","chinese":"主要原因"},{"english":"traditional lifestyles","chinese":"傳統生活方式"},{"english":"connect people with","chinese":"將人們與……連繫起來"},{"english":"with one another","chinese":"彼此之間"},{"english":"customs such as","chinese":"例如……的習俗"},{"english":"local festivals","chinese":"本地節慶"},{"english":"family rituals","chinese":"家庭儀式"},{"english":"traditional crafts","chinese":"傳統手工藝"},{"english":"regional food","chinese":"地區特色食物"},{"english":"not merely old habits","chinese":"不只是舊習慣"},{"english":"carry shared values","chinese":"承載共同價值觀"},{"english":"forms of knowledge","chinese":"知識形式"},{"english":"be replaced by","chinese":"被……取代"},{"english":"consumer culture","chinese":"消費文化"},{"english":"these practices disappear","chinese":"這些做法消失"},{"english":"younger generations","chinese":"年輕一代"},{"english":"lose a sense of belonging","chinese":"失去歸屬感"},{"english":"a wider story","chinese":"更宏大的故事"},{"english":"global popular culture","chinese":"全球流行文化"},{"english":"the latest devices","chinese":"最新裝置"},{"english":"know little about","chinese":"對……所知甚少"},{"english":"shaped their grandparents' lives","chinese":"塑造了祖父母輩的生活"},{"english":"In this sense","chinese":"從這個意義上說"},{"english":"acts as a bridge between generations","chinese":"成為世代之間的橋樑"},{"english":"remain rooted","chinese":"保持根基"},{"english":"move forward","chinese":"向前發展"},{"english":"kept alive in practical ways","chinese":"以實際方式保持活力"},{"english":"local history","chinese":"本地歷史"},{"english":"traditional arts","chinese":"傳統藝術"},{"english":"community customs","chinese":"社區習俗"},{"english":"through activities","chinese":"透過活動"},{"english":"dry memorisation","chinese":"枯燥的死記硬背"},{"english":"experience culture","chinese":"體驗文化"},{"english":"simply reading about it","chinese":"只是閱讀相關內容"},{"english":"at the same time","chinese":"同時"},{"english":"local communities","chinese":"本地社區"},{"english":"craft markets","chinese":"手工藝市集"},{"english":"oral-history projects","chinese":"口述歷史項目"},{"english":"public spaces","chinese":"公共空間"},{"english":"pass on skills to","chinese":"把技能傳給"},{"english":"the young","chinese":"年輕人"},{"english":"digital archives","chinese":"數碼檔案"},{"english":"online lessons","chinese":"網上課堂"},{"english":"make traditional knowledge accessible","chinese":"令傳統知識更容易接觸"},{"english":"original communities","chinese":"原來的社區"},{"english":"protect cultural identity","chinese":"保護文化身份認同"},{"english":"strengthen social bonds","chinese":"加強社會聯繫"},{"english":"the best approach","chinese":"最佳做法"},{"english":"resist modern life","chinese":"抗拒現代生活"},{"english":"weave tradition into","chinese":"把傳統融入"},{"english":"community activities","chinese":"社區活動"},{"english":"digital platforms","chinese":"數碼平台"},{"english":"a living part of society","chinese":"社會中有生命力的一部分"}]},"model-essay-37-ielts-discuss-both-views":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-37-ielts-discuss-both-views","essayKey":"discuss-both-views:37","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-37-ielts-discuss-both-views","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/discuss-both-views-your-opinion/EdmundBd9ExpBth-Q37","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"International sporting events are now seen by many governments as powerful opportunities to raise their country’s profile. While some people argue that hosting these competitions creates serious financial and social problems, I believe that the long-term benefits outweigh these drawbacks.","chinese":"國際體育賽事如今被許多政府視為提升國家形象的強大機會。 雖然有些人認為，舉辦這些比賽會造成嚴重的財政和社會問題， 但我認為，其長遠利益大於這些缺點。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"On the one hand, many countries are eager to host major sports events because they can bring economic and reputational rewards. When a nation welcomes athletes, journalists, and spectators, local businesses such as hotels, restaurants, airlines, and shops often receive a significant boost. More importantly, these events can put a country on the world map. A successful Olympic Games or World Cup allows the host nation to present itself as modern, organised, and culturally attractive. This can strengthen tourism even after the final whistle has blown. In addition, large sporting events can unite citizens behind a shared national moment, creating a sense of pride that ordinary government projects rarely generate.","chinese":"一方面，許多國家渴望舉辦大型體育賽事，因為它們可以帶來經濟和聲譽上的回報。 當一個國家迎接運動員、記者和觀眾時，酒店、餐廳、航空公司和商店等本地企業通常會得到顯著的帶動。 更重要的是，這些賽事可以讓一個國家登上世界舞台。 一屆成功的奧運會或世界盃能讓主辦國展示自己現代化、有組織，並且具有文化吸引力的一面。 即使在賽事結束之後，這仍然可以加強旅遊業。 此外，大型體育賽事能讓國民因一個共同的國家時刻而團結起來，創造出普通政府項目很少能產生的自豪感。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"On the other hand, critics argue that the costs of hosting such events can be dangerously high. Governments may spend enormous sums on stadiums, transport systems, security, and temporary facilities, even when schools, hospitals, and housing need urgent investment. If the venues are rarely used afterwards, they can become expensive “white elephants” rather than valuable public assets. There may also be disruption for local residents, especially when construction projects cause traffic, noise, or even the relocation of communities. For poorer countries in particular, these risks can make hosting an international tournament look more like a burden than a blessing.","chinese":"另一方面，批評者認為，舉辦這類賽事的成本可能高得危險。 政府可能會在體育場、交通系統、保安和臨時設施上花費巨額資金，即使學校、醫院和住房都急需投資。 如果這些場館之後很少被使用，它們便可能成為昂貴的「白象工程」，而不是有價值的公共資產。 本地居民也可能受到干擾，尤其是當建設工程造成交通問題、噪音，甚至導致社區搬遷時。 尤其對較貧窮的國家而言，這些風險可能會使舉辦國際賽事看起來更像是一種負擔，而不是一種福氣。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 3","english":"In my view, however, these problems do not outweigh the advantages. The real issue is not the event itself, but poor planning. If governments build facilities that serve the public after the tournament and control spending carefully, international sports events can generate tourism, improve infrastructure, and strengthen national identity.","chinese":"然而，在我看來，這些問題並不會超過其優點。 真正的問題並不是賽事本身，而是規劃不善。 如果政府建設的設施能在賽事後繼續服務公眾，並且謹慎控制開支，國際體育賽事便能促進旅遊業、改善基礎建設，並加強國家身份認同。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, although hosting major sports events can create financial pressure and local disruption, I believe countries should still welcome them because their economic, cultural, and social benefits are greater.","chinese":"總結來說，雖然舉辦大型體育賽事可能造成財政壓力和本地干擾， 但我認為各國仍然應該歡迎這些賽事，因為它們在經濟、文化和社會方面的利益更大。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"international sporting events","chinese":"國際體育盛事"},{"english":"be seen by many governments as","chinese":"被很多政府視為"},{"english":"powerful opportunities to","chinese":"……的強大機會"},{"english":"raise their country's profile","chinese":"提升國家形象；提高國際知名度"},{"english":"hosting these competitions","chinese":"主辦這些賽事"},{"english":"financial and social problems","chinese":"財政和社會問題"},{"english":"long-term benefits","chinese":"長遠好處"},{"english":"outweigh these drawbacks","chinese":"大於這些缺點"},{"english":"on the one hand","chinese":"一方面"},{"english":"be eager to","chinese":"渴望；熱衷於"},{"english":"host major sports events","chinese":"主辦大型體育賽事"},{"english":"economic and reputational rewards","chinese":"經濟和聲譽上的回報"},{"english":"welcome athletes, journalists, and spectators","chinese":"迎接運動員、記者和觀眾"},{"english":"local businesses","chinese":"本地商戶"},{"english":"receive a significant boost","chinese":"得到顯著推動"},{"english":"more importantly","chinese":"更重要的是"},{"english":"put a country on the world map","chinese":"令一個國家受到國際關注"},{"english":"a successful Olympic Games or World Cup","chinese":"成功的奧運會或世界盃"},{"english":"the host nation","chinese":"主辦國"},{"english":"present itself as","chinese":"將自己展示為"},{"english":"modern, organised, and culturally attractive","chinese":"現代化、有組織和具文化吸引力"},{"english":"strengthen tourism","chinese":"促進旅遊業"},{"english":"after the final whistle has blown","chinese":"賽事結束後"},{"english":"in addition","chinese":"此外"},{"english":"unite citizens behind","chinese":"令國民團結在……之下"},{"english":"a shared national moment","chinese":"共同的國家時刻"},{"english":"a sense of pride","chinese":"自豪感"},{"english":"ordinary government projects","chinese":"一般政府項目"},{"english":"rarely generate","chinese":"很少產生"},{"english":"on the other hand","chinese":"另一方面"},{"english":"critics argue that","chinese":"批評者認為"},{"english":"the costs of hosting","chinese":"主辦成本"},{"english":"dangerously high","chinese":"高得危險；過高"},{"english":"spend enormous sums on","chinese":"花費巨額金錢於"},{"english":"transport systems","chinese":"交通系統"},{"english":"temporary facilities","chinese":"臨時設施"},{"english":"need urgent investment","chinese":"急需投資"},{"english":"venues","chinese":"場館"},{"english":"rarely used afterwards","chinese":"之後很少被使用"},{"english":"expensive white elephants","chinese":"昂貴的大白象工程"},{"english":"valuable public assets","chinese":"有價值的公共資產"},{"english":"disruption for local residents","chinese":"對本地居民的滋擾"},{"english":"construction projects","chinese":"建築工程"},{"english":"the relocation of communities","chinese":"社區搬遷"},{"english":"for poorer countries in particular","chinese":"對較貧窮國家尤其如此"},{"english":"these risks","chinese":"這些風險"},{"english":"an international tournament","chinese":"國際錦標賽"},{"english":"more like a burden than a blessing","chinese":"更像負擔而不是好事"},{"english":"in my view","chinese":"在我看來"},{"english":"do not outweigh the advantages","chinese":"不會大於優點"},{"english":"the real issue","chinese":"真正問題"},{"english":"the event itself","chinese":"事件本身"},{"english":"poor planning","chinese":"規劃不善"},{"english":"serve the public","chinese":"服務公眾"},{"english":"after the tournament","chinese":"錦標賽之後"},{"english":"control spending carefully","chinese":"審慎控制開支"},{"english":"generate tourism","chinese":"帶動旅遊業"},{"english":"improve infrastructure","chinese":"改善基建"},{"english":"strengthen national identity","chinese":"加強國民身份認同"},{"english":"financial pressure","chinese":"財政壓力"},{"english":"local disruption","chinese":"對本地造成滋擾"},{"english":"should still welcome them","chinese":"仍然應該歡迎它們"},{"english":"economic, cultural, and social benefits","chinese":"經濟、文化和社會好處"}]},"model-essay-37-ielts-opinion":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-37-ielts-opinion","essayKey":"opinion:37","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-37-ielts-opinion","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/opinions/EdmundBd9OP-Q37","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"Scientific education is often seen as the engine of national development, especially in an age shaped by medicine, engineering and technology. However, I completely disagree that governments should prioritise funding for science teaching over all other subjects. A country does not progress through scientific knowledge alone; it develops through a broad, balanced education system that produces skilled, thoughtful and socially responsible citizens.","chinese":"科學教育常被視為國家發展的引擎，尤其是在一個由醫學、工程和科技所塑造的時代。 然而，我完全不同意政府應該把科學教學的資金優先置於所有其他學科之上。 一個國家並不是單靠科學知識就能進步；它是透過一個廣泛而均衡的教育制度來發展，而這個制度能培養有技能、有思想，並且具有社會責任感的公民。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"The first reason is that non-science subjects are essential to the practical functioning of a modern society. Languages, history, economics and the arts are not decorative extras; they shape how people communicate, govern, trade and understand one another. For example, a nation may train excellent engineers, but if it lacks capable teachers, lawyers, journalists and public administrators, its scientific achievements may never translate into stable institutions or public trust. Development is not only about building laboratories or inventing machines. It is also about building judgment, culture and cooperation, which are largely strengthened through the humanities and social sciences.","chinese":"第一個原因是，非科學學科對現代社會的實際運作是不可或缺的。 語言、歷史、經濟學和藝術並不是裝飾性的附加項目；它們塑造了人們如何溝通、治理、交易，以及互相理解。 例如，一個國家也許能培養出優秀的工程師，但如果它缺乏有能力的教師、律師、記者和公共行政人員，它的科學成就可能永遠無法轉化為穩定的制度或公眾信任。 發展不只是關於建造實驗室或發明機器。 它同時也是關於建立判斷力、文化和合作精神，而這些能力在很大程度上是透過人文學科和社會科學來強化的。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"Another problem with giving science a privileged share of public funding is that it may narrow students’ opportunities and weaken the wider economy. Not every young person is suited to physics, chemistry or biology, and forcing the education system to revolve around these areas could waste human potential. Some students may become outstanding designers, entrepreneurs, translators or artists if they are properly supported. These fields also contribute directly to national progress by creating jobs, attracting investment and strengthening a country’s cultural identity. In this sense, a science-heavy curriculum may look efficient on paper, but it can become a narrow road when a country actually needs many roads to move forward.","chinese":"給予科學在公共資金中更優先的份額，另一個問題是它可能會收窄學生的機會，並削弱整體經濟。 並不是每一個年輕人都適合物理、化學或生物，而強迫教育制度圍繞這些領域運作，可能會浪費人的潛能。 如果得到適當支持，有些學生可能會成為出色的設計師、企業家、翻譯員或藝術家。 這些領域也能透過創造就業、吸引投資，以及強化一個國家的文化身份，直接為國家進步作出貢獻。 從這個意義上說，一個過度偏重科學的課程表面上看起來可能很有效率，但當一個國家其實需要多條道路向前發展時，它就可能變成一條狹窄的道路。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, while science education deserves strong public investment, it should not receive greater funding at the expense of other subjects. True national progress depends on a balanced education system, because countries need not only scientists, but also communicators, leaders, thinkers and creators.","chinese":"總結來說，雖然科學教育值得得到強而有力的公共投資，但它不應該以犧牲其他學科為代價，獲得更多資金。 真正的國家進步取決於一個均衡的教育制度，因為國家不只需要科學家，也需要溝通者、領導者、思想者和創造者。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"scientific education","chinese":"科學教育"},{"english":"be seen as","chinese":"被視為"},{"english":"engine of national development","chinese":"國家發展的引擎"},{"english":"national development","chinese":"國家發展"},{"english":"especially in an age shaped by","chinese":"尤其在一個由……塑造的時代"},{"english":"medicine, engineering and technology","chinese":"醫學、工程和科技"},{"english":"prioritise funding for","chinese":"優先撥款給……"},{"english":"science teaching","chinese":"科學教學"},{"english":"over all other subjects","chinese":"優先於所有其他科目"},{"english":"progress through","chinese":"透過……進步"},{"english":"scientific knowledge alone","chinese":"單靠科學知識"},{"english":"broad, balanced education system","chinese":"廣泛而均衡的教育制度"},{"english":"skilled, thoughtful and socially responsible citizens","chinese":"有技能、有思想和有社會責任感的公民"},{"english":"non-science subjects","chinese":"非科學科目"},{"english":"essential to","chinese":"對……必不可少"},{"english":"practical functioning of","chinese":"……的實際運作"},{"english":"modern society","chinese":"現代社會"},{"english":"languages, history, economics and the arts","chinese":"語言、歷史、經濟和藝術"},{"english":"decorative extras","chinese":"裝飾性的附加物"},{"english":"shape how people communicate","chinese":"塑造人們如何溝通"},{"english":"govern, trade and understand one another","chinese":"管治、貿易和互相理解"},{"english":"train excellent engineers","chinese":"培訓出色工程師"},{"english":"capable teachers","chinese":"有能力的教師"},{"english":"lawyers, journalists and public administrators","chinese":"律師、記者和公共行政人員"},{"english":"scientific achievements","chinese":"科學成就"},{"english":"translate into","chinese":"轉化為"},{"english":"stable institutions","chinese":"穩定制度"},{"english":"public trust","chinese":"公眾信任"},{"english":"not only about","chinese":"不只是關於……"},{"english":"building laboratories","chinese":"建設實驗室"},{"english":"inventing machines","chinese":"發明機器"},{"english":"building judgment, culture and cooperation","chinese":"建立判斷力、文化和合作"},{"english":"largely strengthened through","chinese":"很大程度上透過……加強"},{"english":"the humanities and social sciences","chinese":"人文學科和社會科學"},{"english":"privileged share of","chinese":"優先佔有較大份額的……"},{"english":"public funding","chinese":"公共撥款"},{"english":"narrow students' opportunities","chinese":"收窄學生的機會"},{"english":"weaken the wider economy","chinese":"削弱更廣泛的經濟"},{"english":"be suited to","chinese":"適合"},{"english":"forcing the education system to","chinese":"強迫教育制度去……"},{"english":"revolve around","chinese":"圍繞……運作"},{"english":"waste human potential","chinese":"浪費人的潛能"},{"english":"outstanding designers","chinese":"出色設計師"},{"english":"entrepreneurs, translators or artists","chinese":"企業家、翻譯員或藝術家"},{"english":"properly supported","chinese":"得到適當支持"},{"english":"contribute directly to","chinese":"直接促進"},{"english":"national progress","chinese":"國家進步"},{"english":"creating jobs","chinese":"創造就業機會"},{"english":"attracting investment","chinese":"吸引投資"},{"english":"strengthening a country's cultural identity","chinese":"加強一個國家的文化身份"},{"english":"cultural identity","chinese":"文化身份"},{"english":"science-heavy curriculum","chinese":"偏重科學的課程"},{"english":"look efficient on paper","chinese":"在紙面上看似高效"},{"english":"narrow road","chinese":"狹窄的道路"},{"english":"move forward","chinese":"向前發展"},{"english":"deserves strong public investment","chinese":"值得大量公共投資"},{"english":"at the expense of","chinese":"以犧牲……為代價"},{"english":"true national progress","chinese":"真正的國家進步"},{"english":"communicators, leaders, thinkers and creators","chinese":"溝通者、領袖、思想者和創作者"}]},"model-essay-38-ielts-direct-question":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-38-ielts-direct-question","essayKey":"direct-question:38","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-38-ielts-direct-question","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/direct-question/EdmundBd9Dir-Q38","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"History has always been one of the main ways through which societies understand themselves. Although different cultures preserve the past in different forms, history can be passed on through education, storytelling, public memory, and cultural traditions. It remains important because it gives people identity, wisdom, and a shared sense of direction.","chinese":"歷史一直是社會理解自身的主要方式之一。 儘管不同文化以不同形式保存過去，歷史可以透過教育、故事傳承、公共記憶和文化傳統傳給下一代。 歷史之所以仍然重要，是因為它給予人們身份認同、智慧，以及共同的方向感。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"There are several ways in which history can be handed down to younger generations. The most obvious method is formal education, as schools can teach students about major events, influential figures, and the development of their own country. However, history is not only found in textbooks. It is also preserved through oral traditions, family stories, monuments, museums, documentaries, and national ceremonies. For example, grandparents may tell children about wartime hardship or migration, allowing them to feel that the past is not just a distant chapter in a book, but part of their family’s living memory. In this way, history is like a bridge between generations: it allows people who never met to remain connected.","chinese":"歷史可以透過幾種方式傳承給年輕一代。 最明顯的方法是正規教育，因為學校可以教導學生了解重大事件、重要人物，以及自己國家的發展。 然而，歷史並不只存在於課本之中。 歷史也可以透過口述傳統、家庭故事、紀念碑、博物館、紀錄片和國家儀式被保存下來。 例如，祖父母可能會向孩子講述戰爭時期的艱難或移民經歷，讓他們感受到過去並不只是書本中遙遠的一章，而是家庭鮮活記憶的一部分。 這樣一來，歷史就像世代之間的一座橋：它讓從未見過面的人仍然保持連結。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"History is also vital to society because it shapes collective identity and helps people make wiser decisions. A community that understands its past is more likely to appreciate its language, customs, values, and struggles. Without this knowledge, people may feel rootless, as if they are living in a house whose foundations they cannot see. More importantly, history teaches societies the consequences of human choices. Wars, social movements, scientific discoveries, and political mistakes all provide lessons about power, justice, conflict, and progress. If these lessons are ignored, societies may repeat old errors under new names.","chinese":"歷史對社會也至關重要，因為它塑造集體身份，並幫助人們作出更明智的決定。 一個理解自身過去的社群，更有可能珍惜自己的語言、習俗、價值觀和曾經經歷的奮鬥。 如果沒有這種知識，人們可能會感到失去根基，彷彿住在一間看不見地基的房子裡。 更重要的是，歷史教導社會明白人類選擇所帶來的後果。 戰爭、社會運動、科學發現和政治錯誤，都提供了關於權力、正義、衝突和進步的教訓。 如果這些教訓被忽視，社會便可能以新的形式重複舊有的錯誤。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, history can be passed on through schools, families, cultural institutions, media, and public traditions. Its importance lies not only in preserving old facts, but also in helping society understand where it came from, who it is, and how it should move forward.","chinese":"總結來說，歷史可以透過學校、家庭、文化機構、媒體和公共傳統傳承下去。 它的重要性不僅在於保存過去的事實，也在於幫助社會理解自己從何而來、自己是誰，以及未來應該如何前進。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"one of the main ways through which","chinese":"……的主要方式之一"},{"english":"understand themselves","chinese":"了解自身"},{"english":"preserve the past","chinese":"保存過去"},{"english":"in different forms","chinese":"以不同形式"},{"english":"be passed on through","chinese":"透過……傳承"},{"english":"storytelling","chinese":"講故事；口述故事"},{"english":"public memory","chinese":"公共記憶"},{"english":"cultural traditions","chinese":"文化傳統"},{"english":"remains important","chinese":"仍然重要"},{"english":"gives people identity","chinese":"給予人身份認同"},{"english":"a shared sense of direction","chinese":"共同方向感"},{"english":"several ways in which","chinese":"幾種……的方式"},{"english":"be handed down to","chinese":"傳給"},{"english":"younger generations","chinese":"年輕一代"},{"english":"the most obvious method","chinese":"最明顯的方法"},{"english":"formal education","chinese":"正規教育"},{"english":"major events","chinese":"重大事件"},{"english":"influential figures","chinese":"有影響力的人物"},{"english":"the development of","chinese":"……的發展"},{"english":"their own country","chinese":"自己的國家"},{"english":"not only found in textbooks","chinese":"不只存在於教科書中"},{"english":"oral traditions","chinese":"口述傳統"},{"english":"family stories","chinese":"家族故事"},{"english":"monuments","chinese":"紀念碑；歷史建築"},{"english":"museums","chinese":"博物館"},{"english":"documentaries","chinese":"紀錄片"},{"english":"national ceremonies","chinese":"國家儀式"},{"english":"wartime hardship","chinese":"戰時艱苦"},{"english":"migration","chinese":"遷移；移民經歷"},{"english":"allowing them to","chinese":"讓他們能夠"},{"english":"a distant chapter in a book","chinese":"書中遙遠的一章"},{"english":"living memory","chinese":"鮮活記憶"},{"english":"In this way","chinese":"以這種方式"},{"english":"a bridge between generations","chinese":"世代之間的橋樑"},{"english":"remain connected","chinese":"保持連繫"},{"english":"vital to society","chinese":"對社會至關重要"},{"english":"shapes collective identity","chinese":"塑造集體身份認同"},{"english":"make wiser decisions","chinese":"作出更明智的決定"},{"english":"understands its past","chinese":"了解自身過去"},{"english":"more likely to","chinese":"更有可能"},{"english":"appreciate its language","chinese":"珍惜自身語言"},{"english":"customs","chinese":"風俗習慣"},{"english":"values","chinese":"價值觀"},{"english":"struggles","chinese":"奮鬥歷程；艱難經歷"},{"english":"without this knowledge","chinese":"沒有這些知識"},{"english":"feel rootless","chinese":"感到沒有根"},{"english":"as if","chinese":"彷彿"},{"english":"foundations","chinese":"根基"},{"english":"cannot see","chinese":"看不見"},{"english":"More importantly","chinese":"更重要的是"},{"english":"the consequences of","chinese":"……的後果"},{"english":"human choices","chinese":"人類選擇"},{"english":"wars","chinese":"戰爭"},{"english":"social movements","chinese":"社會運動"},{"english":"scientific discoveries","chinese":"科學發現"},{"english":"political mistakes","chinese":"政治失誤"},{"english":"provide lessons about","chinese":"提供關於……的教訓"},{"english":"power and justice","chinese":"權力和公義"},{"english":"conflict and progress","chinese":"衝突和進步"},{"english":"be ignored","chinese":"被忽視"},{"english":"repeat old errors","chinese":"重複舊錯誤"},{"english":"under new names","chinese":"以新的名義"},{"english":"cultural institutions","chinese":"文化機構"},{"english":"media","chinese":"媒體"},{"english":"public traditions","chinese":"公共傳統"},{"english":"its importance lies not only in","chinese":"它的重要性不只在於"},{"english":"preserving old facts","chinese":"保存舊事實"},{"english":"where it came from","chinese":"它從何而來"},{"english":"who it is","chinese":"它是誰；自身身份"},{"english":"move forward","chinese":"向前發展"}]},"model-essay-38-ielts-opinion":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-38-ielts-opinion","essayKey":"opinion:38","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-38-ielts-opinion","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/opinions/EdmundBd9OP-Q38","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"Modern education is often expected to equip young people for a fast-changing, technology-driven world. Because of this, some argue that schools should remove art and music from the curriculum and give more time to practical subjects such as information technology. I completely disagree with this view, as creative subjects are not decorative extras but an essential part of a balanced education.","chinese":"現代教育通常被期望裝備年輕人去面對一個快速變化、由科技推動的世界。 正因如此，有些人主張學校應該把美術和音樂從課程中刪除，並把更多時間分配給資訊科技等實用科目。 我完全不同意這個觀點，因為創意科目並不是可有可無的裝飾，而是均衡教育中不可或缺的一部分。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"First, art and music develop forms of thinking that technical subjects alone cannot easily provide. In IT lessons, students may learn how to use software, write code or analyse digital systems. However, when they paint, compose or perform, they learn how to interpret ideas, experiment with possibilities and solve open-ended problems. These habits are highly relevant to the modern workplace, where many tasks require originality rather than mechanical obedience. For example, a student designing a website needs not only programming knowledge but also a sense of layout, colour, rhythm and audience. Without creative training, technology can become a tool in the hands of someone who knows how to press buttons but not how to create meaning.","chinese":"首先，美術和音樂能培養一些單靠技術科目難以提供的思維方式。 在資訊科技課堂中，學生可能會學習如何使用軟件、編寫程式或分析數碼系統。 然而，當他們繪畫、作曲或表演時，他們會學習如何詮釋想法、嘗試不同可能性，並解決沒有固定答案的問題。 這些習慣與現代職場高度相關，因許多工作任務需要的是原創性，而不是機械式的服從 例如，一名設計網站的學生不只需要程式知識，也需要對版面、色彩、節奏和受眾有敏感度。 如果沒有創意訓練，科技可能只會變成一件工具，落在一個懂得按按鈕、卻不懂得創造意義的人手中。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"Second, schools should prepare children for life, not merely for employment. Art and music give students a language for emotion, culture and identity, which is especially important in an age dominated by screens and rapid information. A child who learns music may become more patient and disciplined through regular practice, while a child who studies art may become more observant and sensitive to different perspectives. These qualities are not soft luxuries; they help young people communicate, collaborate and remain human in a highly digital world. Removing such subjects would make education narrower, colder and less complete.","chinese":"第二，學校應該讓孩子為人生作準備，而不只是為就業作準備。 美術和音樂給予學生一種表達情感、文化和身份認同的語言，而這在一個由螢幕和快速資訊主導的時代尤其重要。 一個學習音樂的孩子，可能會透過規律練習變得更有耐性和紀律；而一個學習美術的孩子，可能會變得更善於觀察，也更能敏銳地理解不同角度。 這些特質並不是柔弱而奢侈的附加品；它們能幫助年輕人在高度數碼化的世界中溝通、合作，並保持人的本質。 刪除這些科目會令教育變得更狹窄、更冰冷，也更不完整。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, IT is undeniably useful, but it should not replace art and music. A curriculum that combines technological competence with creativity is far better suited to the modern world than one that treats children as future machines.","chinese":"總結來說，資訊科技無疑是有用的，但它不應取代美術和音樂。 一個把科技能力與創造力結合起來的課程，比一個把孩子視為未來機器的課程，更適合現代世界。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"be expected to","chinese":"被期望去……"},{"english":"equip young people for","chinese":"讓年輕人為……作好準備"},{"english":"fast-changing","chinese":"快速變化的"},{"english":"technology-driven world","chinese":"由科技主導的世界"},{"english":"because of this","chinese":"因此"},{"english":"remove art and music from","chinese":"將藝術和音樂從……移除"},{"english":"curriculum","chinese":"課程"},{"english":"give more time to","chinese":"給予更多時間"},{"english":"practical subjects","chinese":"實用科目"},{"english":"information technology","chinese":"資訊科技"},{"english":"creative subjects","chinese":"創意科目"},{"english":"decorative extras","chinese":"裝飾性的附加物"},{"english":"essential part of","chinese":"……的重要部分"},{"english":"balanced education","chinese":"均衡教育"},{"english":"develop forms of thinking","chinese":"培養思維方式"},{"english":"technical subjects alone","chinese":"單靠技術科目"},{"english":"use software","chinese":"使用軟件"},{"english":"write code","chinese":"編寫程式碼"},{"english":"analyse digital systems","chinese":"分析數碼系統"},{"english":"paint, compose or perform","chinese":"繪畫、作曲或表演"},{"english":"interpret ideas","chinese":"詮釋想法"},{"english":"experiment with possibilities","chinese":"嘗試不同可能性"},{"english":"solve open-ended problems","chinese":"解決開放式問題"},{"english":"highly relevant to","chinese":"與……高度相關"},{"english":"modern workplace","chinese":"現代職場"},{"english":"tasks require originality","chinese":"任務需要原創性"},{"english":"rather than mechanical obedience","chinese":"而不是機械式服從"},{"english":"programming knowledge","chinese":"編程知識"},{"english":"a sense of layout","chinese":"對版面佈局的觸覺"},{"english":"colour, rhythm and audience","chinese":"色彩、節奏和受眾"},{"english":"creative training","chinese":"創意訓練"},{"english":"a tool in the hands of","chinese":"在……手中的工具"},{"english":"press buttons","chinese":"按按鈕"},{"english":"create meaning","chinese":"創造意義"},{"english":"prepare children for life","chinese":"讓孩子為生活作好準備"},{"english":"not merely for employment","chinese":"不只是為了就業"},{"english":"a language for emotion, culture and identity","chinese":"表達情感、文化和身份的語言"},{"english":"especially important in","chinese":"在……中特別重要"},{"english":"an age dominated by","chinese":"一個由……主導的時代"},{"english":"screens and rapid information","chinese":"螢幕和快速資訊"},{"english":"patient and disciplined","chinese":"有耐性和有紀律"},{"english":"regular practice","chinese":"定期練習"},{"english":"become more observant","chinese":"變得更善於觀察"},{"english":"sensitive to different perspectives","chinese":"對不同角度更敏感"},{"english":"soft luxuries","chinese":"可有可無的軟性奢侈品"},{"english":"communicate, collaborate and remain human","chinese":"溝通、協作並保持人性"},{"english":"highly digital world","chinese":"高度數碼化的世界"},{"english":"removing such subjects","chinese":"移除這類科目"},{"english":"narrower, colder and less complete","chinese":"更狹窄、更冷冰冰和更不完整"},{"english":"undeniably useful","chinese":"無可否認地有用"},{"english":"replace art and music","chinese":"取代藝術和音樂"},{"english":"combines technological competence with creativity","chinese":"結合科技能力和創意"},{"english":"technological competence","chinese":"科技能力"},{"english":"far better suited to","chinese":"更適合……得多"},{"english":"treats children as future machines","chinese":"將孩子視為未來的機器"}]},"model-essay-39-ielts-direct-question":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-39-ielts-direct-question","essayKey":"direct-question:39","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-39-ielts-direct-question","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/direct-question/EdmundBd9Dir-Q39","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"Every culture expresses itself through music and art, whether through songs, paintings, dance, sculpture, or public performances. These creative forms are not merely sources of entertainment; they carry social meaning and personal value. This essay will explain how music and art strengthen social identity and enrich individual emotional life.","chinese":"每一種文化都會透過音樂和藝術表達自己，無論是透過歌曲、繪畫、舞蹈、雕塑，還是公共表演。 這些創作形式並不只是娛樂來源；它們承載著社會意義和個人價值。 本文將解釋音樂和藝術如何強化社會身份認同，並豐富個人的情感生活。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"At the societal level, music and art are important because they preserve culture and create a shared sense of belonging. A society is not defined only by its laws, economy, or political system, but also by the stories, emotions, and values that people pass from one generation to the next. Traditional songs, murals, festivals, and performances often keep historical memory alive in a way that textbooks alone cannot. For example, national songs or folk dances can remind people of their common roots, especially during public celebrations or difficult periods. In this sense, the arts act as a cultural bridge: they connect the past with the present and help people feel that they are part of something larger than themselves.","chinese":"在社會層面，音樂和藝術之所以重要，是因為它們能保存文化，並創造共同的歸屬感。 一個社會並不只由它的法律、經濟或政治制度所定義，也由人們代代相傳的故事、情感和價值觀所定義。 傳統歌曲、壁畫、節慶和表演，往往能以教科書單獨無法做到的方式，使歷史記憶保持鮮活。 例如，國歌或民間舞蹈可以提醒人們他們共同的根源，尤其是在公共慶典或艱難時期。 從這個意義上說，藝術就像一座文化橋樑：它們連接過去與現在，並幫助人們感到自己是某個比自身更大的整體的一部分。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"For individuals, music and art are equally valuable because they provide a powerful outlet for emotion, imagination, and self-understanding. Many feelings are difficult to explain directly, but a song, a painting, or a poem can express them with surprising clarity. Someone who feels stressed after work, for instance, may listen to music to calm down, while another person may draw or write in order to process sadness or confusion. These activities do not simply fill empty time; they help people make sense of their inner lives. Without such forms of expression, life would be more practical perhaps, but also colder and less human.","chinese":"對個人而言，音樂和藝術同樣有價值，因為它們為情感、想像力和自我理解提供了一個強大的出口。 許多感受很難直接解釋，但一首歌、一幅畫或一首詩，卻能以令人驚訝的清晰度把它們表達出來。 例如，一個下班後感到壓力的人，可能會聽音樂讓自己平靜下來，而另一個人則可能會透過繪畫或寫作來處理悲傷或困惑。 這些活動並不只是填補空閒時間；它們幫助人們理解自己的內心生活。 如果沒有這些表達形式，生活也許會更加實用，但也會更加冰冷、更加缺乏人性。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, music and art are important because they give societies cultural depth and give individuals emotional space. They preserve identity, build connection, and allow people to express what ordinary language often cannot.","chinese":"總結來說，音樂和藝術之所以重要，是因為它們賦予社會文化深度，也給予個人情感空間。 它們保存身份認同、建立連結，並使人們能夠表達普通語言往往無法表達的東西。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"expresses itself through","chinese":"透過……表達自身"},{"english":"music and art","chinese":"音樂和藝術"},{"english":"public performances","chinese":"公開表演"},{"english":"creative forms","chinese":"創作形式"},{"english":"not merely sources of","chinese":"不只是……的來源"},{"english":"sources of entertainment","chinese":"娛樂來源"},{"english":"carry social meaning","chinese":"承載社會意義"},{"english":"personal value","chinese":"個人價值"},{"english":"strengthen social identity","chinese":"加強社會身份認同"},{"english":"enrich individual emotional life","chinese":"豐富個人的情感生活"},{"english":"at the societal level","chinese":"在社會層面上"},{"english":"preserve culture","chinese":"保存文化"},{"english":"create a shared sense of belonging","chinese":"建立共同歸屬感"},{"english":"a shared sense of belonging","chinese":"共同歸屬感"},{"english":"be defined only by","chinese":"只由……定義"},{"english":"political system","chinese":"政治制度"},{"english":"pass from one generation to the next","chinese":"代代相傳"},{"english":"traditional songs","chinese":"傳統歌曲"},{"english":"murals","chinese":"壁畫"},{"english":"historical memory","chinese":"歷史記憶"},{"english":"keep historical memory alive","chinese":"保持歷史記憶鮮活"},{"english":"in a way that","chinese":"以一種……的方式"},{"english":"textbooks alone","chinese":"單靠教科書"},{"english":"national songs","chinese":"國歌；民族歌曲"},{"english":"folk dances","chinese":"民間舞蹈"},{"english":"remind people of","chinese":"令人民想起"},{"english":"common roots","chinese":"共同根源"},{"english":"public celebrations","chinese":"公眾慶祝活動"},{"english":"difficult periods","chinese":"困難時期"},{"english":"In this sense","chinese":"從這個意義上說"},{"english":"the arts","chinese":"藝術"},{"english":"act as a cultural bridge","chinese":"成為文化橋樑"},{"english":"connect the past with the present","chinese":"連繫過去與現在"},{"english":"part of something larger than themselves","chinese":"比自己更大的整體的一部分"},{"english":"equally valuable","chinese":"同樣有價值"},{"english":"provide a powerful outlet for","chinese":"為……提供強大的出口"},{"english":"emotion, imagination, and self-understanding","chinese":"情感、想像力和自我理解"},{"english":"difficult to explain directly","chinese":"難以直接解釋"},{"english":"express them with surprising clarity","chinese":"以令人意外的清晰度表達它們"},{"english":"surprising clarity","chinese":"令人意外的清晰"},{"english":"feels stressed after work","chinese":"下班後感到有壓力"},{"english":"calm down","chinese":"冷靜下來；放鬆下來"},{"english":"process sadness or confusion","chinese":"處理悲傷或困惑"},{"english":"do not simply fill empty time","chinese":"不只是填補空閒時間"},{"english":"empty time","chinese":"空閒時間"},{"english":"make sense of","chinese":"理解"},{"english":"inner lives","chinese":"內心世界"},{"english":"forms of expression","chinese":"表達形式"},{"english":"more practical perhaps","chinese":"也許更實際"},{"english":"colder and less human","chinese":"更冷漠、更少人情味"},{"english":"cultural depth","chinese":"文化深度"},{"english":"emotional space","chinese":"情感空間"},{"english":"preserve identity","chinese":"保留身份認同"},{"english":"build connection","chinese":"建立連繫"},{"english":"ordinary language","chinese":"普通語言"}]},"model-essay-39-ielts-discuss-both-views":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-39-ielts-discuss-both-views","essayKey":"discuss-both-views:39","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-39-ielts-discuss-both-views","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/discuss-both-views-your-opinion/EdmundBd9ExpBth-Q39","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"In recent years, online communication has become one of the most common ways for people to meet others and maintain social contact. While some argue that this has made human relationships stronger by removing barriers of distance, I believe that it has, on balance, made many people more socially isolated.","chinese":"近年來，網上溝通已成為人們認識他人和維持社交聯繫最常見的方式之一。 雖然有些人認為，這透過消除距離上的障礙，使人際關係變得更牢固， 但我認為，整體而言，這反而使許多人在社交上變得更加孤立。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"On the one hand, the internet can certainly bring people closer together. Social media platforms, messaging apps and online communities allow individuals to stay in touch even when they live in different cities or countries. This is especially valuable for families separated by work, study or migration, as they can share daily experiences almost instantly rather than waiting for occasional visits. The internet also helps people who feel excluded in their local environment to find others with similar interests. For example, a shy student who struggles to make friends at school may feel more confident joining an online group about music, gaming or art. In this sense, digital communication can act as a bridge between people who might otherwise never meet.","chinese":"一方面，互聯網確實可以拉近人與人之間的距離。 社交媒體平台、即時通訊應用程式和網上社群，使人們即使住在不同城市或國家，也能保持聯絡。 這對因工作、學習或移民而分隔兩地的家庭尤其有價值，因為他們可以幾乎即時分享日常經歷，而不必等待偶爾的探訪。 互聯網也幫助那些在本地環境中感到被排斥的人，找到與自己有相似興趣的人。 例如，一個在學校難以交朋友的害羞學生，可能會在加入關於音樂、遊戲或藝術的網上群組時感到更有信心。 從這個意義上說，數位溝通可以在人們之間搭建橋樑，讓一些原本可能永遠不會相遇的人產生聯繫。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"However, I think the stronger argument is that online socialising often creates a thinner and less satisfying form of connection. Many people now spend hours scrolling through posts, sending short messages or reacting to photos, but these interactions rarely provide the emotional depth of face-to-face conversation. When people become used to communicating through screens, they may gradually lose the habit of meeting friends in person, reading body language, or dealing with awkward but necessary real-life conversations. For instance, a group of friends may sit together in a café while each person is absorbed in their own phone. Although they are physically close, they are socially distant. Over time, this can make relationships feel more convenient but less meaningful.","chinese":"然而，我認為更有力的觀點是，網上社交往往創造出一種較薄弱、也較不令人滿足的聯繫形式。 如今，許多人花數小時瀏覽帖文、發送簡短訊息或回應照片，但這些互動很少能提供面對面交談所具有的情感深度。 當人們習慣透過螢幕溝通時，他們可能會逐漸失去親身見朋友、理解肢體語言，以及處理尷尬但必要的現實對話的習慣。 例如，一群朋友可能一起坐在咖啡店裡，但每個人都沉浸在自己的手機之中。 雖然他們在身體距離上很接近，但在社交上卻彼此疏離。 長遠而言，這可能會使人際關係感覺更方便，卻更缺乏意義。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, the internet has undoubtedly made it easier for people to contact one another and form new connections. Nevertheless, I believe it has made society more isolated overall because online interaction too often replaces, rather than strengthens, genuine human contact","chinese":"總結來說，互聯網無疑使人們更容易彼此聯絡，並建立新的關係。 然而，我認為它整體上使社會變得更加孤立，因為網上互動太常取代真正的人際接觸，而不是加強它。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"in recent years","chinese":"近年來"},{"english":"online communication","chinese":"網上溝通"},{"english":"one of the most common ways","chinese":"最常見的方法之一"},{"english":"meet others","chinese":"認識他人"},{"english":"maintain social contact","chinese":"維持社交聯繫"},{"english":"human relationships","chinese":"人際關係"},{"english":"by removing barriers of distance","chinese":"透過消除距離障礙"},{"english":"barriers of distance","chinese":"距離障礙"},{"english":"on balance","chinese":"總體而言"},{"english":"socially isolated","chinese":"社交上更加孤立"},{"english":"on the one hand","chinese":"一方面"},{"english":"bring people closer together","chinese":"拉近人與人之間的距離"},{"english":"social media platforms","chinese":"社交媒體平台"},{"english":"messaging apps","chinese":"即時通訊應用程式"},{"english":"online communities","chinese":"網上社群"},{"english":"allow individuals to","chinese":"讓個人能夠"},{"english":"stay in touch","chinese":"保持聯絡"},{"english":"live in different cities or countries","chinese":"住在不同城市或國家"},{"english":"especially valuable for","chinese":"對……尤其有價值"},{"english":"separated by work, study or migration","chinese":"因工作、學業或移民而分隔"},{"english":"share daily experiences","chinese":"分享日常經歷"},{"english":"almost instantly","chinese":"幾乎即時地"},{"english":"rather than waiting for","chinese":"而不是等待"},{"english":"occasional visits","chinese":"偶爾探訪"},{"english":"feel excluded","chinese":"感到被排斥"},{"english":"local environment","chinese":"本地環境"},{"english":"find others with similar interests","chinese":"找到有相似興趣的人"},{"english":"a shy student","chinese":"害羞的學生"},{"english":"struggle to make friends","chinese":"難以交朋友"},{"english":"feel more confident","chinese":"感到更有信心"},{"english":"joining an online group","chinese":"加入網上群組"},{"english":"in this sense","chinese":"從這個意義上說"},{"english":"digital communication","chinese":"數碼溝通"},{"english":"act as a bridge between","chinese":"作為……之間的橋樑"},{"english":"might otherwise never meet","chinese":"否則可能永遠不會見面"},{"english":"the stronger argument","chinese":"更有力的論點"},{"english":"online socialising","chinese":"網上社交"},{"english":"a thinner and less satisfying form of connection","chinese":"較薄弱而較不滿足的聯繫形式"},{"english":"spend hours scrolling through posts","chinese":"花數小時瀏覽帖文"},{"english":"sending short messages","chinese":"發送簡短訊息"},{"english":"reacting to photos","chinese":"對相片作出反應"},{"english":"rarely provide","chinese":"很少提供"},{"english":"emotional depth","chinese":"情感深度"},{"english":"face-to-face conversation","chinese":"面對面交談"},{"english":"become used to","chinese":"習慣於"},{"english":"communicating through screens","chinese":"透過螢幕溝通"},{"english":"gradually lose the habit of","chinese":"逐漸失去……的習慣"},{"english":"meeting friends in person","chinese":"親身與朋友見面"},{"english":"reading body language","chinese":"解讀身體語言"},{"english":"dealing with","chinese":"處理；應對"},{"english":"awkward but necessary real-life conversations","chinese":"尷尬但必要的現實對話"},{"english":"a group of friends","chinese":"一班朋友"},{"english":"sit together in a café","chinese":"一起坐在咖啡店裏"},{"english":"be absorbed in","chinese":"專注於；沉迷於"},{"english":"their own phone","chinese":"自己的手機"},{"english":"physically close","chinese":"身體上接近"},{"english":"socially distant","chinese":"社交上疏離"},{"english":"over time","chinese":"隨時間"},{"english":"feel more convenient but less meaningful","chinese":"感覺更方便但較沒有意義"},{"english":"undoubtedly","chinese":"毫無疑問"},{"english":"make it easier for people to","chinese":"令人們更容易"},{"english":"contact one another","chinese":"互相聯絡"},{"english":"form new connections","chinese":"建立新聯繫"},{"english":"nevertheless","chinese":"然而"},{"english":"more isolated overall","chinese":"整體上更加孤立"},{"english":"online interaction","chinese":"網上互動"},{"english":"too often replaces","chinese":"太經常取代"},{"english":"rather than strengthens","chinese":"而不是加強"},{"english":"genuine human contact","chinese":"真正的人與人接觸"}]},"model-essay-39-ielts-opinion":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-39-ielts-opinion","essayKey":"opinion:39","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-39-ielts-opinion","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/opinions/EdmundBd9OP-Q39","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"At a time when schools are under pressure to prepare teenagers for a competitive job market, some argue that high school students should abandon literature and focus on more practical subjects. I completely disagree. Studying poems and novels is not a decorative extra; it is a vital part of education because it strengthens students’ language, judgment and humanity.","chinese":"在學校承受壓力、需要為青少年準備競爭激烈的就業市場之際，有些人認為高中學生應該放棄文學，專注於更實用的科目。 我完全不同意。 學習詩歌和小說並不是一種裝飾性的附加內容；它是教育中至關重要的一部分，因為它能強化學生的語言能力、判斷力和人性素養。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"First, literature trains students to read and think with precision. A poem is often compact but dense; a novel follows characters, motives and conflicts over time. To understand these texts, students must infer, compare, question and support interpretations with evidence. These are not soft skills in the trivial sense. They help students write persuasively, evaluate information online and communicate clearly in adult life. For example, a student who learns to explain why a character behaves in a certain way is also learning how to build an argument rather than merely give an opinion. Literature therefore sharpens the mind instead of wasting it.","chinese":"首先，文學訓練學生精準地閱讀和思考。 詩歌通常篇幅短小但含義密集；小說則隨著時間推進人物、動機和衝突。 為了理解這些文本，學生必須推論、比較、提問，並用證據支持自己的詮釋。 這些並不是瑣碎意義上的「軟技能」。 它們幫助學生有說服力地寫作、評估網上資訊，並在成年生活中清楚溝通。 例如，一名學會解釋某個角色為何以某種方式行動的學生，同時也在學習如何建立論證，而不只是提出意見。 因此，文學是在磨練思維，而不是浪費時間。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"Second, literature gives teenagers emotional and moral insight that purely technical subjects often cannot provide. High school students are still forming their identities, and novels and poems allow them to step into lives unlike their own. When they read about loss, ambition, injustice or courage, abstract values become human and memorable. This matters because education should not produce efficient workers alone; it should also produce thoughtful citizens. A class discussion about a tragic hero, for instance, can make students reflect on responsibility, prejudice and compassion far more deeply than a list of rules ever could. In this sense, literature is like a quiet rehearsal for real life: students meet difficult situations on the page before they meet them in the world.","chinese":"其次，文學給予青少年情感和道德上的洞察，而這些往往是純技術科目無法提供的。 高中學生仍在形成自己的身份，而小說和詩歌讓他們走進與自己不同的人生。 當他們讀到失去、抱負、不公或勇氣時，抽象的價值便變得有人性，也更令人難忘。 這一點很重要，因為教育不應只培養高效率的工作者；它也應培養有思想的公民。 例如，一場關於悲劇英雄的課堂討論，能讓學生比閱讀一串規則更深入地反思責任、偏見和同情心。 從這個意義上說，文學就像真實人生的一場安靜預演：學生會先在書頁上遇見困難處境，然後才在現實世界中真正面對它們。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, I completely reject the view that literature is a waste of time for high school students. Poems and novels cultivate precise thinking, expressive language and emotional maturity. Removing them from the curriculum would make education narrower, poorer and less human.","chinese":"總結來說，我完全反對文學對高中學生來說是浪費時間的看法。 詩歌和小說培養精準思維、具表達力的語言，以及情感成熟度。 把它們從課程中移除，會使教育變得更狹窄、更貧乏，也更缺乏人性。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"at a time when","chinese":"在……的時候"},{"english":"be under pressure to","chinese":"承受壓力去……"},{"english":"prepare teenagers for","chinese":"讓青少年為……作好準備"},{"english":"competitive job market","chinese":"競爭激烈的就業市場"},{"english":"abandon literature","chinese":"放棄文學"},{"english":"focus on","chinese":"專注於"},{"english":"practical subjects","chinese":"實用科目"},{"english":"decorative extra","chinese":"裝飾性的附加物"},{"english":"vital part of","chinese":"……的重要部分"},{"english":"strengthens students' language","chinese":"加強學生的語言能力"},{"english":"judgment and humanity","chinese":"判斷力和人性"},{"english":"trains students to","chinese":"訓練學生去……"},{"english":"with precision","chinese":"精準地"},{"english":"compact but dense","chinese":"簡短但含意豐富"},{"english":"follows characters, motives and conflicts","chinese":"跟隨人物、動機和衝突"},{"english":"over time","chinese":"隨着時間推移"},{"english":"infer","chinese":"推斷"},{"english":"support interpretations with evidence","chinese":"用證據支持詮釋"},{"english":"soft skills","chinese":"軟技能"},{"english":"in the trivial sense","chinese":"在瑣碎的意義上"},{"english":"write persuasively","chinese":"有說服力地寫作"},{"english":"evaluate information online","chinese":"評估網上資料"},{"english":"communicate clearly","chinese":"清晰溝通"},{"english":"adult life","chinese":"成年生活"},{"english":"behaves in a certain way","chinese":"以某種方式行為"},{"english":"build an argument","chinese":"建立論點"},{"english":"rather than merely","chinese":"而不是只是"},{"english":"give an opinion","chinese":"發表意見"},{"english":"sharpens the mind","chinese":"磨練思維"},{"english":"wasting it","chinese":"浪費它"},{"english":"emotional and moral insight","chinese":"情感和道德洞察"},{"english":"purely technical subjects","chinese":"純技術科目"},{"english":"forming their identities","chinese":"形成自己的身份認同"},{"english":"step into lives unlike their own","chinese":"走進與自己不同的人生"},{"english":"loss, ambition, injustice or courage","chinese":"失去、抱負、不公或勇氣"},{"english":"abstract values","chinese":"抽象價值"},{"english":"become human and memorable","chinese":"變得有人性而令人難忘"},{"english":"produce efficient workers alone","chinese":"只培養高效率工人"},{"english":"thoughtful citizens","chinese":"有思想的公民"},{"english":"class discussion","chinese":"課堂討論"},{"english":"tragic hero","chinese":"悲劇英雄"},{"english":"reflect on","chinese":"反思"},{"english":"responsibility, prejudice and compassion","chinese":"責任、偏見和同情心"},{"english":"far more deeply than","chinese":"比……深入得多"},{"english":"a list of rules","chinese":"一張規則清單"},{"english":"in this sense","chinese":"從這個意義上說"},{"english":"quiet rehearsal for real life","chinese":"現實生活的安靜排練"},{"english":"difficult situations","chinese":"困難情況"},{"english":"on the page","chinese":"在書頁中"},{"english":"completely reject the view that","chinese":"完全否定……的看法"},{"english":"a waste of time","chinese":"浪費時間"},{"english":"cultivate precise thinking","chinese":"培養精準思維"},{"english":"expressive language","chinese":"有表達力的語言"},{"english":"emotional maturity","chinese":"情緒成熟"},{"english":"removing them from","chinese":"將它們從……移除"},{"english":"curriculum","chinese":"課程"},{"english":"narrower, poorer and less human","chinese":"更狹窄、更貧乏、更少人情味"}]},"model-essay-40-ielts-direct-question":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-40-ielts-direct-question","essayKey":"direct-question:40","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-40-ielts-direct-question","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/direct-question/EdmundBd9Dir-Q40","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"Modern technology has become embedded in professional life. I believe it has transformed work mainly by making it faster, more flexible and less tied to physical location. However, excessive reliance on digital systems can weaken human judgement and create serious disruption when those systems fail.","chinese":"現代科技已經深深融入職業生活之中。 我認為，它主要透過令工作變得更快捷、更靈活，以及較少受實際地點限制，從而改變了我們的工作方式。 然而，過度依賴數碼系統可能會削弱人的判斷力，並在這些系統失靈時造成嚴重干擾。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"One major change is that employees can now communicate, produce and manage work with far greater efficiency. Emails, cloud platforms, video meetings and automated software allow tasks that once required paper files, travel or long meetings to be completed almost instantly. For example, a marketing team can now edit the same document, speak to overseas clients and monitor campaign results without being in the same office. This does not merely save time; it changes workplace expectations. Workers are now expected to respond quickly, learn new tools and collaborate across departments and time zones. In this sense, technology has turned many jobs from slow, location-based routines into faster and more connected forms of work.","chinese":"其中一個主要變化是，員工現在能夠以高得多的效率進行溝通、生產和管理工作。 電子郵件、雲端平台、視像會議和自動化軟件，讓過去需要紙本文件、出差或長時間會議才能完成的任務，幾乎可以即時完成。 例如，一個市場推廣團隊現在可以在不身處同一間辦公室的情況下，共同編輯同一份文件、與海外客戶交談，並監察宣傳活動的成效。 這不只是節省時間；它也改變了職場期望。 如今，員工被期望能夠快速回應、學習新工具，並跨部門、跨時區合作。 從這個意義上說，科技已經把許多工作從緩慢、依賴固定地點的日常流程，轉變成更快捷、更互相連繫的工作形式。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"Nevertheless, relying too heavily on technology has clear disadvantages. The most serious problem is that people may lose important practical skills when machines make too many decisions for them. If employees always depend on software to calculate, organise or communicate, they may become less confident when they need to solve problems independently. A further risk is vulnerability: when a company’s internet, database or automated system breaks down, work can grind to a halt. For instance, a hospital, bank or logistics company that cannot access its digital records may struggle to serve customers safely and efficiently. Technology is useful, but when it becomes the only road available, one broken bridge can stop the whole journey.","chinese":"然而，過度依賴科技也有明顯的缺點。 最嚴重的問題是，當機器替人作出過多決定時，人們可能會失去重要的實用技能。 如果員工總是依賴軟件去計算、組織或溝通，當他們需要獨立解決問題時，便可能變得較缺乏信心。 另一個風險是脆弱性：當一間公司的網絡、資料庫或自動化系統故障時，工作可能會陷入停頓。 例如，一間醫院、銀行或物流公司如果無法存取其數碼記錄，便可能難以安全而有效地為客戶服務。 科技是有用的，但當它變成唯一可走的道路時，一座斷橋便可能令整段旅程停下來。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, modern technology has changed work by making it quicker, more flexible and more globally connected. Even so, I believe excessive dependence on it is dangerous because it can reduce human competence and leave organisations exposed to technical failure. The best workplaces therefore use technology as a powerful tool, not as a substitute for human judgement.","chinese":"總結來說，現代科技透過令工作變得更快捷、更靈活，以及更具全球連繫性，改變了我們的工作方式。 即使如此，我認為過度依賴科技是危險的，因為它可能削弱人的能力，並令機構容易受到技術故障的影響。 因此，最理想的工作場所會把科技視為強大的工具，而不是人的判斷力的替代品。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"modern technology","chinese":"現代科技"},{"english":"become embedded in","chinese":"深入融入……"},{"english":"professional life","chinese":"職業生活"},{"english":"transformed work","chinese":"改變工作模式"},{"english":"mainly by making it","chinese":"主要透過令它……"},{"english":"more flexible","chinese":"更靈活"},{"english":"less tied to","chinese":"較少受……限制"},{"english":"physical location","chinese":"實體地點"},{"english":"excessive reliance on","chinese":"過度依賴"},{"english":"digital systems","chinese":"數碼系統"},{"english":"weaken human judgement","chinese":"削弱人的判斷力"},{"english":"create serious disruption","chinese":"造成嚴重干擾"},{"english":"when those systems fail","chinese":"當那些系統失靈時"},{"english":"one major change","chinese":"一個主要變化"},{"english":"communicate, produce and manage work","chinese":"溝通、生產和管理工作"},{"english":"far greater efficiency","chinese":"高得多的效率"},{"english":"cloud platforms","chinese":"雲端平台"},{"english":"video meetings","chinese":"視像會議"},{"english":"automated software","chinese":"自動化軟件"},{"english":"once required","chinese":"曾經需要"},{"english":"paper files","chinese":"紙本文件"},{"english":"be completed almost instantly","chinese":"幾乎即時完成"},{"english":"a marketing team","chinese":"市場推廣團隊"},{"english":"edit the same document","chinese":"編輯同一份文件"},{"english":"overseas clients","chinese":"海外客戶"},{"english":"monitor campaign results","chinese":"監察宣傳活動成效"},{"english":"without being in","chinese":"不用身處於"},{"english":"does not merely save time","chinese":"不只是節省時間"},{"english":"workplace expectations","chinese":"職場期望"},{"english":"be expected to","chinese":"被期望"},{"english":"respond quickly","chinese":"快速回應"},{"english":"learn new tools","chinese":"學習新工具"},{"english":"collaborate across","chinese":"跨……協作"},{"english":"departments and time zones","chinese":"部門和時區"},{"english":"In this sense","chinese":"從這個意義上說"},{"english":"turned many jobs from...into...","chinese":"將許多工作由……變成……"},{"english":"slow, location-based routines","chinese":"緩慢、受地點限制的常規工作"},{"english":"more connected forms of work","chinese":"更互相連繫的工作形式"},{"english":"Nevertheless","chinese":"然而"},{"english":"relying too heavily on","chinese":"過度依賴"},{"english":"clear disadvantages","chinese":"明顯缺點"},{"english":"the most serious problem","chinese":"最嚴重的問題"},{"english":"practical skills","chinese":"實用技能"},{"english":"make too many decisions for","chinese":"為……作出太多決定"},{"english":"depend on software to","chinese":"依賴軟件去"},{"english":"calculate, organise or communicate","chinese":"計算、整理或溝通"},{"english":"become less confident","chinese":"變得較缺乏信心"},{"english":"solve problems independently","chinese":"獨立解決問題"},{"english":"a further risk","chinese":"另一個風險"},{"english":"vulnerability","chinese":"脆弱性；容易受影響"},{"english":"automated system breaks down","chinese":"自動化系統故障"},{"english":"grind to a halt","chinese":"逐漸停頓；陷入停擺"},{"english":"digital records","chinese":"數碼紀錄"},{"english":"struggle to serve customers","chinese":"難以服務顧客"},{"english":"safely and efficiently","chinese":"安全而高效地"},{"english":"the only road available","chinese":"唯一可用的道路"},{"english":"one broken bridge","chinese":"一條斷橋"},{"english":"stop the whole journey","chinese":"令整段旅程停下來"},{"english":"globally connected","chinese":"更具全球連繫"},{"english":"excessive dependence on","chinese":"對……過度依賴"},{"english":"reduce human competence","chinese":"降低人的能力"},{"english":"leave organisations exposed to","chinese":"使機構容易受到……影響"},{"english":"technical failure","chinese":"技術故障"},{"english":"the best workplaces","chinese":"最好的工作場所"},{"english":"a powerful tool","chinese":"強大的工具"},{"english":"a substitute for","chinese":"……的替代品"},{"english":"human judgement","chinese":"人的判斷力"}]},"model-essay-40-ielts-discuss-both-views":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-40-ielts-discuss-both-views","essayKey":"discuss-both-views:40","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-40-ielts-discuss-both-views","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/discuss-both-views-your-opinion/EdmundBd9ExpBth-Q40","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"Tourism has become one of the most visible forces shaping local communities, especially in places with distinctive traditions, architecture, and ways of life. Some argue that certain areas should be closed to tourists in order to preserve their cultural identity. However, I believe that banning tourism is not a useful solution, because culture is better protected through careful management than complete isolation.","chinese":"旅遊已成為塑造本地社區最明顯的力量之一，尤其是在擁有獨特傳統、建築和生活方式的地方。 有些人認為，某些地區應該禁止遊客進入，以保護其文化身份。 然而，我認為禁止旅遊並不是一個有用的解決方法，因為文化透過細心管理比透過完全隔離更能得到保護。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"Those who support bans usually argue that local culture can be damaged when too many outsiders enter a place. Tourists may treat sacred sites, traditional festivals, or historic neighbourhoods as entertainment rather than living parts of a community. As a result, residents may feel that their customs are being turned into products, and businesses may start changing local food, music, or crafts simply to satisfy visitors. For example, a quiet fishing village could gradually become filled with souvenir shops and staged performances, making its original lifestyle harder to recognise. From this perspective, limiting or even banning tourism seems like a direct way to stop culture from being diluted.","chinese":"支持禁令的人通常認為，當太多外來者進入一個地方時，本地文化可能會受到破壞。 遊客可能會把神聖場所、傳統節日或歷史街區當作娛樂，而不是視為社區中仍然存在並運作的生活部分。 結果，居民可能會覺得自己的習俗正在被變成商品，而商家也可能開始改變本地食物、音樂或手工藝，只是為了迎合遊客。 例如，一條寧靜的漁村可能會逐漸充滿紀念品商店和刻意安排的表演，使它原本的生活方式變得更難辨認。 從這個角度來看，限制甚至禁止旅遊似乎是一種直接阻止文化被稀釋的方法。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"Nevertheless, I strongly believe that banning tourism would bring few real benefits. Culture has never been frozen in time; it naturally changes as people move, communicate, trade, and adapt. If tourism is banned completely, local people may lose income, young residents may leave for better opportunities, and the community may become weaker rather than more authentic. More importantly, a ban does not teach visitors to behave respectfully. A better approach would be to control visitor numbers, protect sensitive sites, involve local residents in tourism planning, and ensure that profits support cultural preservation. That way, tourism becomes a tool for protecting heritage rather than a force that washes it away.","chinese":"然而，我強烈認為禁止旅遊幾乎不會帶來真正的好處。 文化從來都不是凝固在時間之中的；隨著人們遷移、溝通、貿易和適應，它自然會發生變化。 如果旅遊被完全禁止，本地人可能會失去收入，年輕居民可能會為了更好的機會而離開，而社區也可能變得更弱，而不是更真實。 更重要的是，禁令並不會教導遊客如何以尊重的方式行事。 更好的做法是控制遊客數量、保護敏感地點、讓本地居民參與旅遊規劃，並確保收益能夠支持文化保育。 這樣一來，旅遊便會成為保護文化遺產的工具，而不是沖走它的力量。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, while banning tourism may appear to protect local culture, it is too extreme and often ineffective. In my view, well-managed tourism is the wiser solution, as it allows culture to survive, adapt, and remain meaningful to both residents and visitors.","chinese":"總結來說，雖然禁止旅遊看似可以保護本地文化，但這種做法過於極端，而且往往無效 在我看來，管理得宜的旅遊才是更明智的解決方法，因為它能讓文化得以延續、適應變化，並且對居民和遊客都保持意義。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"some researchers believe that","chinese":"一些研究人員認為……"},{"english":"in the future","chinese":"在未來"},{"english":"humanity","chinese":"人類"},{"english":"voluntarily settle on","chinese":"自願選定"},{"english":"one shared global language","chinese":"一種共同全球語言"},{"english":"a negative development","chinese":"負面發展"},{"english":"not merely a tool for communication","chinese":"不只是溝通工具"},{"english":"carries culture, identity and social memory","chinese":"承載文化、身份和社會記憶"},{"english":"cultural loss","chinese":"文化流失"},{"english":"a particular way of seeing the world","chinese":"一種看世界的特定方式"},{"english":"family relationships","chinese":"家庭關係"},{"english":"local traditions","chinese":"本地傳統"},{"english":"moral values","chinese":"道德價值觀"},{"english":"abandon their mother tongues","chinese":"放棄母語"},{"english":"mother tongues","chinese":"母語"},{"english":"in favour of","chinese":"轉而支持；取而用"},{"english":"a single global language","chinese":"單一全球語言"},{"english":"linguistic container","chinese":"語言容器"},{"english":"disappear in translation","chinese":"在翻譯中消失"},{"english":"traditional songs","chinese":"傳統歌曲"},{"english":"proverbs and stories","chinese":"諺語和故事"},{"english":"depend on","chinese":"取決於；依賴"},{"english":"wordplay","chinese":"文字遊戲；雙關語"},{"english":"historical references","chinese":"歷史典故"},{"english":"be fully recreated","chinese":"被完全重現"},{"english":"in another language","chinese":"用另一種語言"},{"english":"once a language stops being used","chinese":"一旦一種語言停止被使用"},{"english":"public life","chinese":"公共生活"},{"english":"with the doors locked","chinese":"大門上鎖的"},{"english":"may still exist","chinese":"可能仍然存在"},{"english":"ordinary people","chinese":"普通人"},{"english":"live inside them","chinese":"活在其中"},{"english":"another serious concern","chinese":"另一個嚴重憂慮"},{"english":"deepen inequality","chinese":"加深不平等"},{"english":"rather than remove it","chinese":"而不是消除它"},{"english":"the global standard","chinese":"全球標準"},{"english":"almost certainly","chinese":"幾乎肯定"},{"english":"belong to","chinese":"屬於"},{"english":"be controlled by","chinese":"被……控制"},{"english":"existing political, economic or technological power","chinese":"現有政治、經濟或科技力量"},{"english":"enjoy an immediate advantage","chinese":"享有即時優勢"},{"english":"international institutions","chinese":"國際機構"},{"english":"spend years catching up","chinese":"花多年時間追趕"},{"english":"turn communication into","chinese":"將溝通變成……"},{"english":"gatekeeping system","chinese":"把關制度；門檻制度"},{"english":"depend less on","chinese":"較少取決於……"},{"english":"early access to","chinese":"早期接觸……的機會"},{"english":"dominant language","chinese":"主導語言"},{"english":"linguistic uniformity","chinese":"語言一致化"},{"english":"on the surface","chinese":"表面上"},{"english":"quietly reward","chinese":"悄悄獎勵"},{"english":"the already privileged","chinese":"已經享有特權的人"},{"english":"would not become richer","chinese":"不會變得更豐富"},{"english":"flatter, poorer and less human","chinese":"更平面、更貧乏、更少人情味"},{"english":"for this reason","chinese":"因此"},{"english":"predicted change","chinese":"預測中的轉變"}]},"model-essay-40-ielts-opinion":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-40-ielts-opinion","essayKey":"opinion:40","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-40-ielts-opinion","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/opinions/EdmundBd9OP-Q40","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"Education is one of the few public goods that can change a person’s life before poverty becomes permanent. I completely agree that schooling and university education should be free for everyone, regardless of family income, because education is both a basic social right and a long-term investment in society.","chinese":"教育是少數能在貧窮變成永久困境之前，改變一個人一生的公共資源之一。 我完全同意學校教育和大學教育都應該對每個人免費，無論其家庭收入如何，因為教育既是一項基本社會權利，也是社會的長期投資。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"The first reason is that fees turn education into a privilege rather than a genuine opportunity. Children do not choose the household into which they are born, so it is deeply unfair if their future is decided by their parents’ bank balance. When families have to pay for school places, books, examinations or tuition, low-income parents may be forced to choose between education and daily necessities. As a result, bright students can be pushed out of the classroom before their abilities have had a chance to grow. Free education changes this picture: it gives every child a seat at the table and allows talent, effort and character to matter more than wealth. For a poor but capable student, school can become a ladder, not a locked gate.","chinese":"第一個原因是，學費會把教育變成一種特權，而不是一個真正的機會。 孩子並不能選擇自己出生於哪一個家庭，因此如果他們的未來由父母的銀行存款決定，這是極不公平的。 當家庭必須支付學位、書本、考試或學費時，低收入父母可能會被迫在教育和日常生活必需品之間作出選擇。 結果是，聰明的學生可能在自己的能力有機會成長之前，便被迫離開課室。 免費教育能改變這個局面：它讓每個孩子都有參與的機會，並使天分、努力和品格比財富更加重要。 對於一個貧窮但有能力的學生而言，學校可以成為一把梯子，而不是一道上鎖的大門。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"This principle should also apply to tertiary education, because modern societies need highly trained citizens. Doctors, teachers, engineers and researchers are not produced by primary education alone; they require years of advanced study. If university fees are extremely high, many young people either abandon their ambitions or begin adult life under a mountain of debt. That is not only harmful to individuals, but also wasteful for society, since national talent is left unused. Some may argue that free higher education would place pressure on public budgets. However, governments already fund roads, hospitals and police services because they benefit the whole community. Education deserves the same treatment: it creates skilled workers, informed voters and more stable communities.","chinese":"這個原則也應該適用於高等教育，因為現代社會需要受過高度訓練的公民。 醫生、教師、工程師和研究人員並不是單靠小學教育就能培養出來的；他們需要多年高階學習。 如果大學學費極高，許多年輕人不是放棄自己的抱負，就是在沉重債務下開始成年生活 這不但對個人有害，也會浪費社會資源，因為國家的才華被閒置不用。 有些人可能會認為，免費高等教育會對公共財政造成壓力。 然而，政府本來就會資助道路、醫院和警察服務，因為它們有利於整個社區。 教育也值得同樣的對待：它能培養技術熟練的勞動者、有判斷力的選民，以及更穩定的社區。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, I fully agree that education at every level should be free. A fair society should not allow money to decide who learns, who progresses, and who is left behind.","chinese":"總結來說，我完全同意每一個階段的教育都應該免費。 一個公平的社會不應該讓金錢決定誰能學習、誰能進步，以及誰會被拋在後面。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"one of the few public goods","chinese":"少數公共利益之一"},{"english":"public goods","chinese":"公共利益；公共產品"},{"english":"change a person's life","chinese":"改變一個人的人生"},{"english":"before poverty becomes permanent","chinese":"在貧窮變成永久之前"},{"english":"schooling and university education","chinese":"學校教育和大學教育"},{"english":"free for everyone","chinese":"對所有人免費"},{"english":"regardless of family income","chinese":"不論家庭收入"},{"english":"basic social right","chinese":"基本社會權利"},{"english":"long-term investment in society","chinese":"對社會的長期投資"},{"english":"turn education into","chinese":"將教育變成……"},{"english":"a privilege rather than","chinese":"特權而不是……"},{"english":"genuine opportunity","chinese":"真正機會"},{"english":"do not choose","chinese":"不能選擇"},{"english":"the household into which they are born","chinese":"他們出生的家庭"},{"english":"deeply unfair","chinese":"極不公平"},{"english":"be decided by","chinese":"由……決定"},{"english":"parents' bank balance","chinese":"父母的銀行存款"},{"english":"school places","chinese":"學位"},{"english":"examinations or tuition","chinese":"考試或學費"},{"english":"low-income parents","chinese":"低收入父母"},{"english":"be forced to choose between","chinese":"被迫在……之間作選擇"},{"english":"daily necessities","chinese":"生活必需品"},{"english":"as a result","chinese":"因此"},{"english":"bright students","chinese":"聰明學生"},{"english":"be pushed out of","chinese":"被迫離開……"},{"english":"before their abilities have had a chance to grow","chinese":"在能力有機會發展之前"},{"english":"changes this picture","chinese":"改變這種情況"},{"english":"gives every child a seat at the table","chinese":"讓每個孩子都有參與機會"},{"english":"talent, effort and character","chinese":"才能、努力和品格"},{"english":"matter more than wealth","chinese":"比財富更重要"},{"english":"poor but capable student","chinese":"貧窮但有能力的學生"},{"english":"become a ladder","chinese":"成為階梯"},{"english":"locked gate","chinese":"上鎖的大門"},{"english":"this principle should also apply to","chinese":"這個原則也應適用於……"},{"english":"tertiary education","chinese":"高等教育"},{"english":"modern societies","chinese":"現代社會"},{"english":"highly trained citizens","chinese":"受過高度訓練的公民"},{"english":"are not produced by","chinese":"並不是由……培養出來"},{"english":"primary education alone","chinese":"單靠小學教育"},{"english":"years of advanced study","chinese":"多年的高階學習"},{"english":"university fees","chinese":"大學學費"},{"english":"extremely high","chinese":"極高"},{"english":"abandon their ambitions","chinese":"放棄抱負"},{"english":"begin adult life","chinese":"開始成年生活"},{"english":"under a mountain of debt","chinese":"背負沉重債務"},{"english":"harmful to individuals","chinese":"對個人有害"},{"english":"wasteful for society","chinese":"對社會來說浪費"},{"english":"national talent","chinese":"國家人才"},{"english":"be left unused","chinese":"被閒置；未被善用"},{"english":"place pressure on","chinese":"對……造成壓力"},{"english":"public budgets","chinese":"公共預算"},{"english":"roads, hospitals and police services","chinese":"道路、醫院和警察服務"},{"english":"benefit the whole community","chinese":"令整個社區受惠"},{"english":"deserves the same treatment","chinese":"值得得到同樣待遇"},{"english":"skilled workers","chinese":"熟練工人"},{"english":"informed voters","chinese":"有知識的選民"},{"english":"stable communities","chinese":"穩定社區"},{"english":"at every level","chinese":"在每個階段"},{"english":"fair society","chinese":"公平社會"},{"english":"allow money to decide","chinese":"讓金錢決定"},{"english":"who is left behind","chinese":"誰被拋在後面"}]},"model-essay-41-ielts-direct-question":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-41-ielts-direct-question","essayKey":"direct-question:41","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-41-ielts-direct-question","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/direct-question/EdmundBd9Dir-Q41","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"Over the last half-century, technology has changed childhood from a mostly local experience into one shaped by screens, algorithms and instant communication. While this gives children convenience and access to information, it also creates problems for both society and family life.","chinese":"在過去半個世紀裡，科技已經把童年從一種主要以本地生活為中心的經驗，轉變成一種由螢幕、演算法和即時通訊所塑造的經驗。 雖然這給孩子帶來了便利和獲取資訊的途徑，但它也為社會和家庭生活帶來了問題。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"At the social level, the main problem is that children may develop weaker interpersonal and emotional skills. In the past, many children learned patience, cooperation and compromise through outdoor games and neighbourhood activities. By contrast, a child who spends most free time on a phone may avoid the difficulties of real interaction, such as reading facial expressions or resolving disagreements. Over time, this can produce young people who are less confident in conversation and less comfortable with conflict. Technology also exposes children to adult pressures too early. Social media and online entertainment often present edited bodies, luxurious lifestyles and popularity contests as if they were normal life. A child who constantly compares himself with influencers may begin to measure his own worth through appearance, attention and likes. This can feed anxiety and low self-esteem, creating a generation that is connected to thousands online but still feels insecure and alone.","chinese":"在社會層面上，主要問題是孩子可能會形成較弱的人際交往能力和情緒能力。 在過去，許多孩子透過戶外遊戲和社區活動學會耐性、合作和妥協。 相比之下，一個把大部分空閒時間都花在手機上的孩子，可能會避開真實互動中的困難，例如理解面部表情或解決分歧。 長遠而言，這可能會造成一批在交談中較缺乏自信、也較不適應衝突的年輕人。 科技也使孩子過早接觸成人世界的壓力。 社交媒體和網上娛樂經常把修飾過的身體、奢華的生活方式和人氣競爭呈現得彷彿它們就是正常生活。 一個不斷把自己與網紅比較的孩子，可能會開始透過外貌、關注度和讚好數來衡量自己的價值。 這可能會助長焦慮和低自尊，形成一代在線上與成千上萬的人連繫，卻仍然感到不安和孤單的人。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"Within the family, the clearest problem is the loss of meaningful communication. Even when parents and children are sitting in the same room, separate screens can pull them into separate worlds. Meals become quieter, conversations become shorter and parents may fail to notice changes in their children’s mood. In addition, technology makes parental authority more difficult because parents must now control screen time, online friendships and unsuitable content. These rules can easily lead to arguments and mistrust, especially when children feel that parents are invading their private digital space. As a result, the home may become less like a place of guidance and more like a battlefield of control.","chinese":"在家庭內部，最明顯的問題是有意義溝通的流失。 即使父母和孩子坐在同一個房間裡，不同的螢幕也可以把他們拉進不同的世界。 用餐變得更安靜，對話變得更短，而父母也可能無法察覺孩子情緒上的變化。 此外，科技使父母權威更難維持，因為父母現在必須管理螢幕時間、網上朋友關係和不適合的內容。 這些規則很容易導致爭吵和不信任，尤其是當孩子覺得父母正在侵犯他們的私人數位空間時。 結果，家庭可能變得不太像一個提供引導的地方，而更像一個控制權爭奪的戰場。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, modern technology can weaken society by damaging children’s social skills and emotional health. It can also harm family life by reducing real conversation and making parental guidance harder.","chinese":"總結來說，現代科技可能會透過損害孩子的社交能力和情緒健康來削弱社會。 它也可能透過減少真實對話，並使父母引導變得更困難，從而損害家庭生活。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"over the last half-century","chinese":"在過去半個世紀"},{"english":"a mostly local experience","chinese":"主要屬於本地生活圈的經驗"},{"english":"shaped by","chinese":"受……塑造"},{"english":"screens, algorithms and instant communication","chinese":"屏幕、演算法和即時通訊"},{"english":"access to information","chinese":"獲取資料"},{"english":"creates problems for","chinese":"為……造成問題"},{"english":"society and family life","chinese":"社會和家庭生活"},{"english":"at the social level","chinese":"在社會層面上"},{"english":"the main problem is that","chinese":"主要問題是"},{"english":"develop weaker interpersonal skills","chinese":"培養出較弱的人際交往能力"},{"english":"emotional skills","chinese":"情緒能力"},{"english":"in the past","chinese":"過去"},{"english":"cooperation and compromise","chinese":"合作和妥協"},{"english":"outdoor games","chinese":"戶外遊戲"},{"english":"neighbourhood activities","chinese":"社區活動"},{"english":"By contrast","chinese":"相比之下"},{"english":"spends most free time on","chinese":"把大部分空閒時間花在……上"},{"english":"avoid the difficulties of","chinese":"避開……的困難"},{"english":"real interaction","chinese":"真實互動"},{"english":"reading facial expressions","chinese":"解讀面部表情"},{"english":"resolving disagreements","chinese":"解決分歧"},{"english":"over time","chinese":"隨時間"},{"english":"less confident in conversation","chinese":"在交談中較缺乏信心"},{"english":"less comfortable with conflict","chinese":"對衝突較不自在"},{"english":"exposes children to","chinese":"使孩子接觸到"},{"english":"adult pressures","chinese":"成人壓力"},{"english":"too early","chinese":"太早"},{"english":"social media","chinese":"社交媒體"},{"english":"online entertainment","chinese":"網上娛樂"},{"english":"edited bodies","chinese":"經修飾的身體形象"},{"english":"luxurious lifestyles","chinese":"奢華生活方式"},{"english":"popularity contests","chinese":"人氣競賽"},{"english":"as if they were normal life","chinese":"彷彿它們是正常生活"},{"english":"constantly compares himself with","chinese":"不斷把自己與……比較"},{"english":"influencers","chinese":"網紅"},{"english":"measure his own worth through","chinese":"透過……衡量自己的價值"},{"english":"appearance, attention and likes","chinese":"外貌、關注和讚好"},{"english":"feed anxiety","chinese":"加劇焦慮"},{"english":"low self-esteem","chinese":"低自尊"},{"english":"connected to thousands online","chinese":"在網上與成千上萬人連繫"},{"english":"feels insecure and alone","chinese":"感到不安和孤單"},{"english":"within the family","chinese":"在家庭內"},{"english":"the clearest problem","chinese":"最明顯的問題"},{"english":"the loss of meaningful communication","chinese":"有意義溝通的流失"},{"english":"sitting in the same room","chinese":"坐在同一個房間"},{"english":"separate screens","chinese":"各自的屏幕"},{"english":"pull them into separate worlds","chinese":"把他們拉進不同世界"},{"english":"meals become quieter","chinese":"用餐變得更安靜"},{"english":"conversations become shorter","chinese":"對話變得更短"},{"english":"fail to notice changes in","chinese":"未能察覺……的變化"},{"english":"children's mood","chinese":"孩子的情緒"},{"english":"in addition","chinese":"此外"},{"english":"parental authority","chinese":"父母權威"},{"english":"control screen time","chinese":"控制使用屏幕的時間"},{"english":"online friendships","chinese":"網上友誼"},{"english":"unsuitable content","chinese":"不合適內容"},{"english":"lead to arguments and mistrust","chinese":"導致爭執和不信任"},{"english":"invading their private digital space","chinese":"侵犯他們的私人數碼空間"},{"english":"as a result","chinese":"結果"},{"english":"a place of guidance","chinese":"提供引導的地方"},{"english":"a battlefield of control","chinese":"控制權的戰場"},{"english":"weaken society","chinese":"削弱社會"},{"english":"damaging children's social skills","chinese":"損害孩子的社交能力"},{"english":"emotional health","chinese":"情緒健康"},{"english":"harm family life","chinese":"損害家庭生活"},{"english":"reducing real conversation","chinese":"減少真實對話"},{"english":"making parental guidance harder","chinese":"令父母引導更困難"}]},"model-essay-41-ielts-discuss-both-views":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-41-ielts-discuss-both-views","essayKey":"discuss-both-views:41","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-41-ielts-discuss-both-views","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/discuss-both-views-your-opinion/EdmundBd9ExpBth-Q41","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"Air pollution has become one of the most pressing environmental problems in many urban areas, and road transport is often seen as a major cause. While an international car-free day can raise public awareness and temporarily improve air quality, I believe that stricter, permanent transport policies are far more effective.","chinese":"空氣污染已成為許多城市地區最迫切的環境問題之一，而道路交通往往被視為主要原因 雖然國際無車日可以提高公眾意識，並暫時改善空氣質素， 我認為更嚴格、永久性的交通政策有效得多。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"On the one hand, supporters of a global car-free day argue that it can produce an immediate, visible reduction in pollution. If private vehicles are kept off the road for even a single day, fewer exhaust fumes are released, and city centres may become cleaner, quieter and more pleasant. More importantly, such an event can act as a public reminder that everyday travel choices have environmental consequences. For example, when commuters are encouraged to walk, cycle or use buses for a day, some may realise that driving is not always necessary. In this sense, a car-free day is not merely a symbolic gesture; it can plant the seed of cleaner habits.","chinese":"一方面，全球無車日的支持者認為，它能夠立即帶來可見的污染減少。 如果私人車輛即使只是一天不上路，排放的廢氣也會減少，而市中心可能會變得更清潔、更安靜，也更令人舒適。 更重要的是，這類活動可以提醒公眾，日常出行選擇會帶來環境後果。 例如，當通勤者被鼓勵在一天之內步行、騎單車或乘搭巴士時，有些人可能會意識到開車並非總是必要的。 從這個意義上說，無車日不僅僅是一種象徵性姿態；它可以種下更清潔生活習慣的種子"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"However, I believe this approach is too limited to deal with a problem that occurs every day. Air pollution is not caused by one day of traffic but by millions of repeated journeys, so the solution must also be continuous. Governments should improve public transport, expand cycling lanes, and make high-emission vehicles more expensive to use. These measures directly change people’s long-term behaviour because they make cleaner options easier and dirtier choices less attractive. For instance, if buses and trains are affordable, reliable and widely available, many workers will naturally leave their cars at home, not once a year but throughout the week. This is where real environmental progress is made.","chinese":"然而，我認為這種方法太有限，無法應對一個每天都在發生的問題。 空氣污染並不是由一天的交通造成的，而是由數以百萬計反覆發生的旅程造成的，因此解決方法也必須是持續性的。 政府應該改善公共交通、擴展單車徑，並提高高排放車輛的使用成本。 這些措施會直接改變人們的長期行為，因為它們令更清潔的選擇變得更容易，也令污染較大的選擇變得較不吸引。 例如，如果巴士和火車價格合理、可靠，而且覆蓋廣泛，許多上班族自然會把車留在家中，而不是一年一次，而是整個星期都這樣做。 這才是真正環境進步發生的地方。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, an international car-free day may be useful as a wake-up call, since it shows people what a cleaner city could feel like. Nevertheless, I strongly believe that lasting reductions in air pollution depend on permanent policies that reshape daily transport habits.","chinese":"總結來說，國際無車日或許可以作為一個警醒，因為它讓人們看見一個更清潔的城市可以是甚麼感覺。 【原始 PDF 未提供中文翻譯】"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"air pollution","chinese":"空氣污染"},{"english":"one of the most pressing environmental problems","chinese":"最迫切的環境問題之一"},{"english":"urban areas","chinese":"市區"},{"english":"road transport","chinese":"道路交通"},{"english":"be seen as","chinese":"被視為"},{"english":"a major cause","chinese":"主要原因"},{"english":"an international car-free day","chinese":"國際無車日"},{"english":"raise public awareness","chinese":"提高公眾意識"},{"english":"temporarily improve air quality","chinese":"暫時改善空氣質素"},{"english":"stricter, permanent transport policies","chinese":"更嚴格而永久的交通政策"},{"english":"far more effective","chinese":"有效得多"},{"english":"on the one hand","chinese":"一方面"},{"english":"supporters of","chinese":"……的支持者"},{"english":"a global car-free day","chinese":"全球無車日"},{"english":"produce an immediate, visible reduction in","chinese":"立即而明顯地減少"},{"english":"be kept off the road","chinese":"不准上路"},{"english":"for even a single day","chinese":"即使只是一日"},{"english":"exhaust fumes","chinese":"廢氣"},{"english":"be released","chinese":"被排放"},{"english":"city centres","chinese":"市中心"},{"english":"cleaner, quieter and more pleasant","chinese":"更清潔、更寧靜和更舒適"},{"english":"more importantly","chinese":"更重要的是"},{"english":"such an event","chinese":"這類活動"},{"english":"act as a public reminder","chinese":"發揮公共提醒的作用"},{"english":"everyday travel choices","chinese":"日常出行選擇"},{"english":"have environmental consequences","chinese":"帶來環境後果"},{"english":"commuters","chinese":"通勤人士"},{"english":"be encouraged to","chinese":"被鼓勵去"},{"english":"use buses","chinese":"乘搭巴士"},{"english":"realise that","chinese":"意識到"},{"english":"not always necessary","chinese":"並非總是必要"},{"english":"in this sense","chinese":"從這個意義上說"},{"english":"not merely a symbolic gesture","chinese":"不只是象徵性姿態"},{"english":"plant the seed of","chinese":"播下……的種子"},{"english":"cleaner habits","chinese":"更環保的習慣"},{"english":"this approach","chinese":"這種做法"},{"english":"too limited to deal with","chinese":"太有限，無法處理"},{"english":"occur every day","chinese":"每日都發生"},{"english":"be caused by","chinese":"由……造成"},{"english":"one day of traffic","chinese":"一日的交通"},{"english":"millions of repeated journeys","chinese":"數以百萬計重複的旅程"},{"english":"the solution must be continuous","chinese":"解決方法必須是持續的"},{"english":"improve public transport","chinese":"改善公共交通"},{"english":"expand cycling lanes","chinese":"擴展單車徑"},{"english":"high-emission vehicles","chinese":"高排放車輛"},{"english":"more expensive to use","chinese":"使用成本更高"},{"english":"directly change people's long-term behaviour","chinese":"直接改變人們的長期行為"},{"english":"long-term behaviour","chinese":"長期行為"},{"english":"cleaner options","chinese":"較環保的選擇"},{"english":"dirtier choices","chinese":"較污染的選擇"},{"english":"less attractive","chinese":"較不吸引"},{"english":"affordable, reliable and widely available","chinese":"負擔得起、可靠和覆蓋廣泛"},{"english":"leave their cars at home","chinese":"不駕車出門"},{"english":"not once a year but throughout the week","chinese":"不是一年一次，而是整個星期"},{"english":"throughout the week","chinese":"整個星期"},{"english":"real environmental progress","chinese":"真正的環境進步"},{"english":"be useful as a wake-up call","chinese":"作為警醒訊號是有用的"},{"english":"a wake-up call","chinese":"警醒訊號"},{"english":"what a cleaner city could feel like","chinese":"一個更清潔城市的感覺"},{"english":"nevertheless","chinese":"然而"},{"english":"lasting reductions in","chinese":"……的持久減少"},{"english":"depend on permanent policies","chinese":"取決於永久政策"},{"english":"reshape daily transport habits","chinese":"重塑日常交通習慣"}]},"model-essay-41-ielts-opinion":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-41-ielts-opinion","essayKey":"opinion:41","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-41-ielts-opinion","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/opinions/EdmundBd9OP-Q41","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"Schools are often under pressure to raise the performance of pupils who fall behind academically. Some people argue that the most effective solution is to make after-school activities compulsory, on the grounds that this will increase pupils’ involvement in school and improve their grades. I completely disagree with this view because compulsory activities do not address the real causes of underachievement and may even weaken students’ motivation.","chinese":"學校經常面對壓力，需要提升學業落後學生的表現。 有些人認為，最有效的解決方法是把課後活動變成強制性，理由是這樣能增加學生對學校的參與感，並改善他們的成績。 我完全不同意這種看法，因為強制性活動並沒有處理學業表現不佳的真正原因，甚至可能削弱學生的學習動機。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"The main problem with this proposal is that it mistakes attendance for learning. Underachieving pupils are not necessarily failing because they spend too little time on school premises; they may be struggling because they have weak foundations, poor study habits, low confidence, or difficulties at home. For example, a student who cannot understand basic algebra will not suddenly improve simply because he is required to stay after school for a general activity. What he needs is targeted academic support, patient explanation, and regular feedback. If schools force such pupils to attend extra sessions that do not directly solve their learning gaps, the policy may become a burden rather than a bridge to progress.","chinese":"這項建議的主要問題在於，它把出席誤以為是學習。 學業表現不佳的學生未必是因為他們在學校逗留的時間太少而失敗；他們可能是因為基礎薄弱、學習習慣差、信心不足，或家中存在困難而掙扎。 例如，一個無法理解基礎代數的學生，不會僅僅因為被要求放學後留下來參加一般活動，就突然有所進步。 他真正需要的是有針對性的學業支援、耐心的講解，以及定期的回饋。 如果學校強迫這些學生參加一些不能直接解決學習差距的額外課程，這項政策便可能成為負擔，而不是通往進步的橋樑。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"Compulsory after-school activities can also damage the very engagement they are supposed to create. Many weaker pupils already associate school with stress, failure, or embarrassment. Extending the school day by force may make them feel punished for underperforming, which can lead to resentment and even poorer attitudes towards learning. A better approach would be to offer personalised tutoring, mentoring, smaller study groups, and meaningful choices in extracurricular programmes. When pupils feel that support is designed for them rather than imposed on them, they are more likely to take ownership of their progress.","chinese":"強制性課後活動也可能破壞它們原本想要建立的參與感。 許多較弱的學生本來已經把學校和壓力、失敗或尷尬聯繫在一起。 強行延長上學時間可能會令他們覺得自己因表現欠佳而受到懲罰，這可能導致怨氣，甚至令他們對學習產生更差的態度。 更好的做法是提供個人化補習、導師輔導、較小型的學習小組，以及在課外活動中提供有意義的選擇。 當學生感到支援是為他們而設，而不是強加在他們身上時，他們更有可能主動為自己的進步負責。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, I strongly disagree that compulsory after-school activities are the best way to help underachieving pupils. Real improvement comes from diagnosing students’ specific problems and giving them focused, respectful support, not from forcing them to spend more time at school.","chinese":"總結來說，我強烈不同意強制性課後活動是幫助學業表現不佳學生的最佳方法。 真正的進步來自診斷學生的具體問題，並給予他們有重點且尊重他們的支援，而不是強迫他們花更多時間留在學校。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"be under pressure to","chinese":"承受壓力去……"},{"english":"raise the performance of","chinese":"提高……的表現"},{"english":"fall behind academically","chinese":"學業上落後"},{"english":"the most effective solution","chinese":"最有效的解決方法"},{"english":"after-school activities","chinese":"課後活動"},{"english":"compulsory","chinese":"強制性的；必須參加的"},{"english":"on the grounds that","chinese":"基於……理由"},{"english":"increase pupils' involvement in","chinese":"增加學生對……的參與"},{"english":"improve their grades","chinese":"提高他們的成績"},{"english":"completely disagree with","chinese":"完全不同意……"},{"english":"address the real causes of","chinese":"處理……的真正成因"},{"english":"underachievement","chinese":"學業表現不理想"},{"english":"weaken students' motivation","chinese":"削弱學生的動力"},{"english":"the main problem with","chinese":"……的主要問題"},{"english":"this proposal","chinese":"這項建議"},{"english":"mistakes attendance for learning","chinese":"將出席誤當作學習"},{"english":"underachieving pupils","chinese":"成績落後的學生"},{"english":"are not necessarily failing because","chinese":"不一定是因為……而失敗"},{"english":"school premises","chinese":"校園範圍"},{"english":"be struggling because","chinese":"因為……而感到困難"},{"english":"weak foundations","chinese":"基礎薄弱"},{"english":"poor study habits","chinese":"不良學習習慣"},{"english":"low confidence","chinese":"信心不足"},{"english":"difficulties at home","chinese":"家庭困難"},{"english":"basic algebra","chinese":"基礎代數"},{"english":"suddenly improve","chinese":"突然進步"},{"english":"be required to","chinese":"被要求去……"},{"english":"general activity","chinese":"一般活動"},{"english":"targeted academic support","chinese":"有針對性的學業支援"},{"english":"patient explanation","chinese":"耐心講解"},{"english":"regular feedback","chinese":"定期回饋"},{"english":"force such pupils to","chinese":"強迫這些學生去……"},{"english":"extra sessions","chinese":"額外課節"},{"english":"directly solve","chinese":"直接解決"},{"english":"learning gaps","chinese":"學習缺口"},{"english":"a burden rather than a bridge to progress","chinese":"成為負擔，而不是通往進步的橋樑"},{"english":"damage the very engagement","chinese":"損害正正想建立的投入感"},{"english":"be supposed to","chinese":"本應該"},{"english":"associate school with","chinese":"將學校與……聯繫起來"},{"english":"stress, failure, or embarrassment","chinese":"壓力、失敗或尷尬"},{"english":"extending the school day","chinese":"延長上課日"},{"english":"by force","chinese":"強行地"},{"english":"feel punished for","chinese":"因……而感到受罰"},{"english":"underperforming","chinese":"表現未如理想"},{"english":"lead to resentment","chinese":"導致怨氣"},{"english":"poorer attitudes towards learning","chinese":"對學習更差的態度"},{"english":"a better approach","chinese":"更好的方法"},{"english":"personalised tutoring","chinese":"個人化補習"},{"english":"mentoring","chinese":"導師指導"},{"english":"smaller study groups","chinese":"較小型學習小組"},{"english":"meaningful choices","chinese":"有意義的選擇"},{"english":"extracurricular programmes","chinese":"課外活動計劃"},{"english":"be designed for","chinese":"為……而設計"},{"english":"imposed on","chinese":"強加於……"},{"english":"be more likely to","chinese":"更有可能"},{"english":"take ownership of","chinese":"主動掌握；承擔"},{"english":"their progress","chinese":"他們的進步"},{"english":"the best way to","chinese":"……的最佳方法"},{"english":"real improvement","chinese":"真正進步"},{"english":"diagnosing students' specific problems","chinese":"找出學生的具體問題"},{"english":"focused, respectful support","chinese":"有針對性而尊重學生的支援"},{"english":"forcing them to spend more time at school","chinese":"強迫他們花更多時間留在學校"}]},"model-essay-42-ielts-direct-question":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-42-ielts-direct-question","essayKey":"direct-question:42","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-42-ielts-direct-question","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/direct-question/EdmundBd9Dir-Q42","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"Tourism has become one of the most visible parts of the modern global economy, with millions of people travelling for leisure, work and cultural experience. In my view, its greatest benefits are that it broadens individuals’ understanding of the world and strengthens society by creating jobs, funding public services and protecting local culture.","chinese":"旅遊業已成為現代全球經濟中最顯眼的部分之一，數以百萬計的人為了休閒、工作和文化體驗而旅行。 在我看來，旅遊業最大的好處是它能拓寬個人對世界的理解，並透過創造就業、資助公共服務和保護本地文化來強化社會。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"On an individual level, tourism allows people to step outside the narrow routine of daily life and see how others live. When travellers encounter different languages, customs and ways of thinking, they often become more open-minded and less quick to judge unfamiliar lifestyles. A student who visits Kyoto, for example, may learn more from observing local manners, temples and food traditions than from reading a chapter in a textbook. This kind of first-hand experience is powerful because it turns culture from an abstract idea into something people can see, hear and remember. Tourism can therefore make individuals more curious, adaptable and culturally sensitive.","chinese":"在個人層面上，旅遊讓人們走出日常生活中狹窄的固定模式，並看見其他人如何生活。 當旅客接觸到不同的語言、習俗和思維方式時，他們往往會變得更加開明，也較不會急於批判陌生的生活方式。 例如，一名到訪京都的學生，可能會透過觀察當地禮儀、寺廟和飲食傳統，學到比閱讀教科書一章更多的東西。 這種第一手經驗很有力量，因為它把文化從一個抽象概念，轉化成人們能夠看見、聽見並記住的東西。 因此，旅遊能使個人變得更有好奇心、更能適應不同環境，也更具文化敏感度。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"Tourism also brings clear social benefits, especially in countries whose towns and cities rely on visitors. Hotels, restaurants, transport companies, museums and small shops all need workers, so tourism can provide income for families and reduce unemployment. The money spent by tourists can also support wider public life: governments may collect more tax revenue, improve transport links and maintain historic sites that might otherwise be neglected. For instance, when an old district becomes popular with visitors, local authorities have a stronger reason to restore buildings, train guides and keep the area clean. In this way, tourism does not merely bring money into a country; it can also give communities a practical reason to preserve their identity.","chinese":"旅遊業也帶來明顯的社會好處，尤其是在那些城鎮和城市依賴旅客的國家。 酒店、餐廳、交通公司、博物館和小商店都需要員工，因此旅遊業能為家庭提供收入，並減少失業。 旅客所花費的金錢也能支持更廣泛的公共生活：政府可以徵收更多稅收、改善交通連接，並維護那些否則可能被忽視的歷史遺址。 例如，當一個舊區變得受旅客歡迎時，地方政府便有更強的理由去修復建築、培訓導遊，並保持該區清潔。 透過這種方式，旅遊業不只是為一個國家帶來金錢；它也能給予社區一個實際理由去保留自身身份。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, tourism benefits individuals by widening their horizons and benefits society by creating employment, improving local facilities and encouraging cultural preservation. Managed responsibly, it can be both an economic engine and a bridge between cultures.","chinese":"總結來說，旅遊業透過拓寬個人視野來使個人受益，也透過創造就業、改善本地設施和鼓勵文化保育來使社會受益。 如果管理得當，旅遊業既可以成為經濟引擎，也可以成為文化之間的橋樑。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"one of the most visible parts of","chinese":"……最明顯的部分之一"},{"english":"the modern global economy","chinese":"現代環球經濟"},{"english":"travel for leisure","chinese":"為消閒而旅行"},{"english":"cultural experience","chinese":"文化體驗"},{"english":"In my view","chinese":"在我看來"},{"english":"greatest benefits","chinese":"最大好處"},{"english":"broadens individuals' understanding of","chinese":"擴闊個人對……的理解"},{"english":"strengthens society","chinese":"加強社會"},{"english":"creating jobs","chinese":"創造就業"},{"english":"funding public services","chinese":"資助公共服務"},{"english":"protecting local culture","chinese":"保護本地文化"},{"english":"on an individual level","chinese":"在個人層面上"},{"english":"step outside","chinese":"走出"},{"english":"the narrow routine of daily life","chinese":"狹窄的日常生活模式"},{"english":"see how others live","chinese":"了解其他人的生活方式"},{"english":"encounter different languages","chinese":"接觸不同語言"},{"english":"customs","chinese":"風俗習慣"},{"english":"ways of thinking","chinese":"思維方式"},{"english":"become more open-minded","chinese":"變得更開明"},{"english":"less quick to judge","chinese":"不那麼快作出批判"},{"english":"unfamiliar lifestyles","chinese":"陌生的生活方式"},{"english":"observing local manners","chinese":"觀察本地禮儀"},{"english":"temples","chinese":"寺廟"},{"english":"food traditions","chinese":"飲食傳統"},{"english":"a chapter in a textbook","chinese":"教科書中的一章"},{"english":"first-hand experience","chinese":"第一手經驗"},{"english":"turns culture from...into...","chinese":"將文化由……變成……"},{"english":"an abstract idea","chinese":"抽象概念"},{"english":"something people can see, hear and remember","chinese":"人們可以看見、聽見和記住的東西"},{"english":"make individuals more curious","chinese":"令個人更加好奇"},{"english":"adaptable","chinese":"適應力強的"},{"english":"culturally sensitive","chinese":"對文化更敏感；更懂得尊重不同文化"},{"english":"brings clear social benefits","chinese":"帶來明顯社會好處"},{"english":"rely on visitors","chinese":"依賴遊客"},{"english":"need workers","chinese":"需要員工"},{"english":"provide income for","chinese":"為……提供收入"},{"english":"reduce unemployment","chinese":"減低失業率"},{"english":"money spent by tourists","chinese":"遊客花費的金錢"},{"english":"wider public life","chinese":"更廣泛的公共生活"},{"english":"collect more tax revenue","chinese":"收取更多稅收"},{"english":"improve transport links","chinese":"改善交通連接"},{"english":"maintain historic sites","chinese":"維護歷史遺址"},{"english":"otherwise be neglected","chinese":"否則可能被忽視"},{"english":"old district","chinese":"舊區"},{"english":"becomes popular with","chinese":"受到……歡迎"},{"english":"local authorities","chinese":"地方當局"},{"english":"have a stronger reason to","chinese":"有更強理由去"},{"english":"restore buildings","chinese":"修復建築物"},{"english":"train guides","chinese":"培訓導遊"},{"english":"keep the area clean","chinese":"保持該區清潔"},{"english":"In this way","chinese":"以這種方式"},{"english":"does not merely bring money into","chinese":"不只是為……帶來金錢"},{"english":"practical reason to","chinese":"實際理由去"},{"english":"preserve their identity","chinese":"保留自身身份特色"},{"english":"widening their horizons","chinese":"擴闊眼界"},{"english":"creating employment","chinese":"創造就業"},{"english":"improving local facilities","chinese":"改善本地設施"},{"english":"encouraging cultural preservation","chinese":"鼓勵文化保育"},{"english":"managed responsibly","chinese":"在負責任管理下"},{"english":"an economic engine","chinese":"經濟引擎；經濟推動力"},{"english":"a bridge between cultures","chinese":"文化之間的橋樑"}]},"model-essay-42-ielts-discuss-both-views":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-42-ielts-discuss-both-views","essayKey":"discuss-both-views:42","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-42-ielts-discuss-both-views","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/discuss-both-views-your-opinion/EdmundBd9ExpBth-Q42","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"Traffic congestion has become one of the most persistent problems in modern cities. While some people argue that privately owned vehicles should be prohibited from city centres, others believe that such a policy would be impractical. In my view, although banning private cars may appear attractive in theory, it is an unrealistic solution in practice.","chinese":"交通擠塞已成為現代城市中最持久的問題之一。 有些人認為私人擁有的車輛應該被禁止進入市中心，而另一些人則認為這樣的政策並不切實際。 在我看來，雖然禁止私家車在理論上可能看似吸引，但在實際操作上卻是一個不現實的解決方法。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"On the one hand, supporters of this policy argue that a ban on private vehicles would make city centres cleaner, safer, and less crowded. Private cars often carry only one or two passengers, yet they occupy a large amount of road space. If they were removed from central areas, buses, trams, cyclists, and pedestrians could move far more efficiently. This would not only reduce traffic jams but also lower air pollution, since fewer cars would mean fewer emissions. For example, a busy shopping district with fewer private vehicles would likely become more pleasant for residents, workers, and visitors alike. From this perspective, restricting car access seems to be a direct way to improve urban life.","chinese":"一方面，支持這項政策的人認為，禁止私人車輛進入市中心會令市中心更清潔、更安全，也更不擁擠。 私家車通常只載一兩名乘客，卻佔用了大量道路空間。 如果它們被移出市中心地區，巴士、電車、單車使用者和行人便能更有效率地移動。 這不但能減少交通堵塞，也能降低空氣污染，因為車輛減少就意味著排放減少。 例如，一個繁忙的購物區如果私家車較少，對居民、上班族和遊客而言都很可能會變得更加舒適。 從這個角度來看，限制汽車進入似乎是一種直接改善城市生活的方法。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"On the other hand, opponents argue that a complete ban would create serious practical problems. Many people depend on private vehicles because public transport is either unreliable, overcrowded, or unavailable in certain areas. Elderly people, disabled passengers, families with young children, and workers who carry equipment may find it especially difficult to enter city centres without their own cars. In addition, businesses could suffer if customers, suppliers, or employees were suddenly unable to travel conveniently. A policy that sounds simple on paper could therefore disrupt daily life and place an unfair burden on people whose needs cannot be met by public transport alone.","chinese":"另一方面，反對者認為，全面禁止私家車會造成嚴重的實際問題。 許多人依賴私人車輛，因為公共交通在某些地區可能不可靠、過於擁擠，或者根本無法使用。 長者、殘疾乘客、有年幼子女的家庭，以及需要攜帶工具或設備的工人，如果沒有自己的車，可能會特別難以進入市中心。 此外，如果顧客、供應商或員工突然無法方便地出行，商業活動也可能受到損害。 因此，一項在紙面上聽起來簡單的政策，實際上可能會擾亂日常生活，並對那些單靠公共交通無法滿足需要的人造成不公平的負擔。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 3","english":"I strongly believe that banning privately owned vehicles from city centres is unrealistic. A better approach would be to reduce car use through congestion charges, improved public transport, limited parking, and better cycling infrastructure. These measures would ease congestion without punishing people who genuinely need to drive.","chinese":"我強烈認為，禁止私人擁有的車輛進入市中心是不現實的。 更好的方法是透過徵收擠塞費、改善公共交通、限制泊車，以及建設更完善的單車基礎設施來減少汽車使用。 這些措施能夠紓緩交通擠塞，同時不會懲罰那些真正需要駕車的人。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, although banning private vehicles could reduce traffic and pollution, it is too rigid to work fairly in real cities. Governments should manage car use more intelligently rather than impose a complete ban.","chinese":"總結來說，雖然禁止私人車輛能夠減少交通和污染，但它過於僵硬，難以在真實城市中公平地運作。 政府應該更明智地管理汽車使用，而不是實施全面禁令。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"traffic congestion","chinese":"交通擠塞"},{"english":"one of the most persistent problems","chinese":"最持續存在的問題之一"},{"english":"modern cities","chinese":"現代城市"},{"english":"privately owned vehicles","chinese":"私家車；私人擁有的車輛"},{"english":"be prohibited from","chinese":"被禁止進入"},{"english":"city centres","chinese":"市中心"},{"english":"such a policy","chinese":"這樣的政策"},{"english":"be impractical","chinese":"不切實際"},{"english":"in my view","chinese":"在我看來"},{"english":"appear attractive in theory","chinese":"理論上看似吸引"},{"english":"an unrealistic solution in practice","chinese":"實際上不切實際的解決方法"},{"english":"on the one hand","chinese":"一方面"},{"english":"supporters of this policy","chinese":"這項政策的支持者"},{"english":"a ban on private vehicles","chinese":"對私家車的禁令"},{"english":"cleaner, safer, and less crowded","chinese":"更清潔、更安全和較不擠迫"},{"english":"carry only one or two passengers","chinese":"只載一兩名乘客"},{"english":"occupy a large amount of road space","chinese":"佔用大量道路空間"},{"english":"central areas","chinese":"中心地區"},{"english":"buses, trams, cyclists, and pedestrians","chinese":"巴士、電車、單車人士和行人"},{"english":"move far more efficiently","chinese":"流動效率高得多"},{"english":"not only reduce traffic jams but also","chinese":"不但減少塞車，而且"},{"english":"traffic jams","chinese":"塞車"},{"english":"lower air pollution","chinese":"降低空氣污染"},{"english":"fewer emissions","chinese":"較少廢氣排放"},{"english":"a busy shopping district","chinese":"繁忙購物區"},{"english":"would likely become","chinese":"很可能會變得"},{"english":"residents, workers, and visitors alike","chinese":"居民、上班族和遊客都一樣"},{"english":"from this perspective","chinese":"從這個角度來看"},{"english":"restricting car access","chinese":"限制汽車進入"},{"english":"a direct way to","chinese":"……的直接方法"},{"english":"improve urban life","chinese":"改善城市生活"},{"english":"on the other hand","chinese":"另一方面"},{"english":"opponents argue that","chinese":"反對者認為"},{"english":"a complete ban","chinese":"全面禁令"},{"english":"create serious practical problems","chinese":"造成嚴重實際問題"},{"english":"depend on private vehicles","chinese":"依賴私家車"},{"english":"public transport","chinese":"公共交通工具"},{"english":"unreliable","chinese":"不可靠"},{"english":"overcrowded","chinese":"過度擠迫"},{"english":"unavailable in certain areas","chinese":"在某些地區沒有提供"},{"english":"elderly people","chinese":"長者"},{"english":"disabled passengers","chinese":"殘疾乘客；行動不便乘客"},{"english":"families with young children","chinese":"有年幼子女的家庭"},{"english":"workers who carry equipment","chinese":"需要攜帶工具的工人"},{"english":"find it especially difficult to","chinese":"覺得特別困難去"},{"english":"enter city centres","chinese":"進入市中心"},{"english":"without their own cars","chinese":"沒有自己的車"},{"english":"in addition","chinese":"此外"},{"english":"businesses could suffer","chinese":"企業可能受影響"},{"english":"customers, suppliers, or employees","chinese":"顧客、供應商或僱員"},{"english":"be suddenly unable to","chinese":"突然無法"},{"english":"travel conveniently","chinese":"方便出行"},{"english":"sound simple on paper","chinese":"紙面上聽起來簡單"},{"english":"disrupt daily life","chinese":"擾亂日常生活"},{"english":"place an unfair burden on","chinese":"對……造成不公平負擔"},{"english":"whose needs cannot be met by","chinese":"其需要不能由……滿足"},{"english":"public transport alone","chinese":"單靠公共交通工具"},{"english":"a better approach","chinese":"更好的做法"},{"english":"reduce car use","chinese":"減少汽車使用"},{"english":"congestion charges","chinese":"擠塞收費"},{"english":"improved public transport","chinese":"改善公共交通"},{"english":"limited parking","chinese":"限制泊車"},{"english":"cycling infrastructure","chinese":"單車基建"},{"english":"these measures","chinese":"這些措施"},{"english":"ease congestion","chinese":"紓緩交通擠塞"},{"english":"without punishing","chinese":"而不會懲罰"},{"english":"genuinely need to drive","chinese":"真正需要駕車"},{"english":"reduce traffic and pollution","chinese":"減少交通和污染"},{"english":"too rigid to work fairly","chinese":"過於僵化，難以公平實行"},{"english":"in real cities","chinese":"在真實城市中"},{"english":"manage car use more intelligently","chinese":"更明智地管理汽車使用"},{"english":"rather than impose","chinese":"而不是實施"},{"english":"impose a complete ban","chinese":"實施全面禁令"}]},"model-essay-42-ielts-opinion":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-42-ielts-opinion","essayKey":"opinion:42","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-42-ielts-opinion","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/opinions/EdmundBd9OP-Q42","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"It is sometimes argued that governments waste excessive public money on wildlife conservation when more urgent social problems exist. I strongly disagree with this view because protecting wildlife is not a luxury; it is a necessary part of protecting human life, environmental stability, and long-term economic security.","chinese":"有人認為，當社會上存在更迫切的問題時，政府把過多公共資金浪費在野生動物保育上。 我強烈不同意這種看法，因為保護野生動物並不是一種奢侈行為；它是保障人類生活、環境穩定和長遠經濟安全的必要部分。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"The first reason is that wildlife protection is closely connected to the health of the natural systems on which people depend. Animals and plants are not decorative extras in the background of human life; they form part of complex ecosystems that regulate climate, maintain soil quality, support food production, and keep natural habitats balanced. If governments allow forests, oceans, and animal populations to collapse, the damage will eventually return to human society in the form of food shortages, floods, disease, and higher living costs. For example, if bee populations decline because their habitats are destroyed, crop production can suffer, which may make basic food more expensive for ordinary families. In this sense, spending money on wildlife is not money thrown into the wilderness. It is an investment in the invisible machinery that keeps human life running.","chinese":"第一個原因是，野生動物保護與人類所依賴的自然系統健康密切相關。 動物和植物並不是人類生活背景中的裝飾性附屬品；它們是複雜生態系統的一部分，而這些系統能調節氣候、維持土壤質素、支持糧食生產，並保持自然棲息地的平衡。 如果政府任由森林、海洋和動物種群崩潰，這種破壞最終會以糧食短缺、洪水、疾病和更高生活成本的形式回到人類社會。 例如，如果蜜蜂種群因棲息地被破壞而減少，農作物產量便可能受影響，這可能使普通家庭的基本食物變得更昂貴。 從這個意義上說，花錢保護野生動物並不是把錢丟進荒野之中。這是對維持人類生活運作的無形機器作出投資。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"Another important point is that conservation and social welfare should not be treated as enemies competing for the same piece of bread. Responsible governments must fund hospitals, schools, housing, and public safety, but this does not mean that wildlife protection should be pushed aside. In fact, many conservation projects also benefit local communities directly. National parks, marine reserves, and forest-protection schemes can create jobs, attract tourism, preserve clean water, and protect rural livelihoods. When these projects are managed well, they do not drain public resources; they create long-term value. Ignoring wildlife may seem cheaper in the short term, but it can become far more expensive when environmental damage has to be repaired later.","chinese":"另一個重要觀點是，保育和社會福利不應被視為爭奪同一塊麵包的敵人。 負責任的政府必須資助醫院、學校、住房和公共安全，但這並不代表野生動物保護應該被擱置一旁。 事實上，許多保育項目也能直接惠及本地社區。 國家公園、海洋保護區和森林保護計劃可以創造就業、吸引旅遊、保護潔淨水源，並保障農村生計。 當這些項目管理得宜時，它們不會耗盡公共資源；相反，它們會創造長遠價值。 忽視野生動物在短期內可能看似較便宜，但當日後必須修復環境破壞時，代價可能會高得多。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, I do not agree that governments spend too much on protecting wildlife. Although many social problems deserve serious attention, wildlife conservation is one of the foundations of a safe, healthy, and sustainable society.","chinese":"總結來說，我不同意政府在保護野生動物方面花費過多這一說法。 雖然許多社會問題都值得認真關注，但野生動物保育是建立安全、健康和可持續社會的基礎之一。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"waste excessive public money on","chinese":"在……上浪費過多公帑"},{"english":"wildlife conservation","chinese":"野生動物保育"},{"english":"urgent social problems","chinese":"迫切社會問題"},{"english":"strongly disagree with","chinese":"強烈不同意……"},{"english":"not a luxury","chinese":"不是奢侈品"},{"english":"a necessary part of","chinese":"……的必要部分"},{"english":"environmental stability","chinese":"環境穩定"},{"english":"long-term economic security","chinese":"長遠經濟保障"},{"english":"be closely connected to","chinese":"與……密切相關"},{"english":"natural systems","chinese":"自然系統"},{"english":"depend on","chinese":"依賴"},{"english":"decorative extras","chinese":"裝飾性的附加物"},{"english":"in the background of","chinese":"在……的背景中"},{"english":"complex ecosystems","chinese":"複雜生態系統"},{"english":"regulate climate","chinese":"調節氣候"},{"english":"maintain soil quality","chinese":"維持土壤質素"},{"english":"support food production","chinese":"支持糧食生產"},{"english":"keep natural habitats balanced","chinese":"維持自然棲息地平衡"},{"english":"allow forests, oceans, and animal populations to collapse","chinese":"讓森林、海洋和動物種群崩潰"},{"english":"animal populations","chinese":"動物種群"},{"english":"eventually return to","chinese":"最終回到；反過來影響"},{"english":"in the form of","chinese":"以……的形式"},{"english":"food shortages","chinese":"糧食短缺"},{"english":"higher living costs","chinese":"更高生活成本"},{"english":"bee populations","chinese":"蜜蜂種群"},{"english":"decline","chinese":"下降；減少"},{"english":"habitats are destroyed","chinese":"棲息地被破壞"},{"english":"crop production","chinese":"農作物生產"},{"english":"can suffer","chinese":"可能受損"},{"english":"basic food","chinese":"基本食物"},{"english":"ordinary families","chinese":"普通家庭"},{"english":"in this sense","chinese":"從這個意義上說"},{"english":"money thrown into the wilderness","chinese":"投進荒野而白白浪費的錢"},{"english":"investment in","chinese":"對……的投資"},{"english":"invisible machinery","chinese":"隱形機器"},{"english":"keeps human life running","chinese":"令人的生活得以運作"},{"english":"conservation","chinese":"保育"},{"english":"social welfare","chinese":"社會福利"},{"english":"be treated as enemies","chinese":"被視為敵對"},{"english":"competing for","chinese":"爭奪……"},{"english":"the same piece of bread","chinese":"同一塊麵包；同一份資源"},{"english":"responsible governments","chinese":"負責任的政府"},{"english":"public safety","chinese":"公共安全"},{"english":"be pushed aside","chinese":"被擱置一旁"},{"english":"conservation projects","chinese":"保育項目"},{"english":"local communities","chinese":"本地社區"},{"english":"national parks","chinese":"國家公園"},{"english":"marine reserves","chinese":"海洋保護區"},{"english":"forest-protection schemes","chinese":"森林保護計劃"},{"english":"create jobs","chinese":"創造就業機會"},{"english":"attract tourism","chinese":"吸引旅遊業"},{"english":"preserve clean water","chinese":"保存潔淨水源"},{"english":"protect rural livelihoods","chinese":"保護鄉郊生計"},{"english":"managed well","chinese":"管理得宜"},{"english":"drain public resources","chinese":"耗盡公共資源"},{"english":"create long-term value","chinese":"創造長遠價值"},{"english":"ignoring wildlife","chinese":"忽視野生動物"},{"english":"in the short term","chinese":"短期內"},{"english":"become far more expensive","chinese":"變得昂貴得多"},{"english":"be repaired later","chinese":"日後被修復"},{"english":"spend too much on","chinese":"在……上花費太多"},{"english":"deserve serious attention","chinese":"值得認真關注"},{"english":"one of the foundations of","chinese":"……的基礎之一"},{"english":"safe, healthy, and sustainable society","chinese":"安全、健康和可持續的社會"}]},"model-essay-43-ielts-direct-question":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-43-ielts-direct-question","essayKey":"direct-question:43","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-43-ielts-direct-question","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/direct-question/EdmundBd9Dir-Q43","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"Tourism has made many historic places more accessible than ever, but it has also placed some of the world’s most fragile buildings and sites under severe pressure. Once ancient walls, temples, or monuments are permanently damaged, they cannot simply be rebuilt with the same cultural value. To prevent this, governments and heritage authorities should focus on both controlling visitor behaviour and creating a stable system for conservation.","chinese":"旅遊業使許多歷史場所比以往任何時候都更容易被人接觸，但它也令世界上一些最脆弱的建築和遺址承受沉重壓力。 一旦古老的城牆、寺廟或紀念建築受到永久性破壞，它們便不能簡單地以相同的文化價值被重建。 為了防止這種情況，政府和文物保育機構應同時著重控制遊客行為，以及建立一個穩定的保育制度。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"The first and most immediate measure is to limit the physical pressure placed on vulnerable sites. Many historic attractions are damaged not by one careless visitor, but by thousands of people walking, touching, climbing, and crowding the same spaces every day. For this reason, authorities should introduce timed tickets, daily visitor limits, protected walking routes, and restricted zones around especially delicate structures. For example, if tourists are allowed to view an ancient temple from a controlled path instead of walking freely through it, the risk of erosion, accidental damage, and overcrowding is greatly reduced. This would not stop people from enjoying cultural heritage; rather, it would allow them to experience it without slowly destroying it.","chinese":"第一個也是最直接的措施，是限制脆弱遺址所承受的實際壓力。 許多歷史景點並不是被某一個粗心的遊客破壞，而是被每天成千上萬的人在同一空間中行走、觸摸、攀爬和擁擠所損害。 正因如此，當局應引入限時門票、每日遊客人數上限、受保護的步行路線，以及在特別脆弱的建築周圍設立限制區域。 例如，如果遊客只能從受管制的路徑觀賞一座古老寺廟，而不是在其中自由行走，侵蝕、意外損壞和過度擁擠的風險便會大大降低。 這並不會阻止人們欣賞文化遺產；相反，這能讓他們在不慢慢破壞它的情況下體驗它。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"Another important solution is to make tourism directly fund preservation. Entrance fees, tourism taxes, or conservation charges should be used specifically to repair buildings, employ trained staff, install protective equipment, and monitor damage over time. At the same time, tour operators should be required to educate visitors before they enter sensitive sites, while strict fines should be imposed on those who ignore rules, remove objects, or vandalise property. Clear signs alone are often not enough; rules need both explanation and enforcement. When tourists understand that they are entering a piece of shared history rather than just another photo opportunity, they are more likely to behave responsibly.","chinese":"另一個重要的解決方法，是讓旅遊業直接資助保育工作。 入場費、旅遊稅或保育費應專門用於修復建築、聘請受過訓練的員工、安裝保護設備，以及長期監察損壞情況。 與此同時，旅行社和導遊機構應被要求在遊客進入敏感遺址前教育他們，而對於無視規則、取走物件或破壞財物的人，則應施加嚴厲罰款。 單靠清晰的標示往往並不足夠；規則既需要解釋，也需要執行。 當遊客明白自己進入的是一段共同歷史，而不只是另一個拍照機會時，他們便更有可能負責任地行事。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, historic sites can be protected by reducing excessive visitor pressure and by using tourism revenue to support long-term conservation. Tourism should open a window onto the past, not close it forever.","chinese":"總結來說，歷史遺址可以透過減少過度的遊客壓力，以及利用旅遊收入支持長期保育來得到保護。 旅遊業應該為人們打開一扇通往過去的窗，而不是永遠把它關上。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"historic places","chinese":"歷史名勝；歷史地方"},{"english":"more accessible than ever","chinese":"比以往更容易到達"},{"english":"fragile buildings and sites","chinese":"脆弱的建築物和遺址"},{"english":"under severe pressure","chinese":"承受嚴重壓力"},{"english":"ancient walls","chinese":"古老城牆"},{"english":"temples","chinese":"寺廟"},{"english":"monuments","chinese":"紀念碑；古蹟"},{"english":"permanently damaged","chinese":"永久受損"},{"english":"cannot simply be rebuilt","chinese":"不能簡單地重建"},{"english":"the same cultural value","chinese":"相同的文化價值"},{"english":"prevent this","chinese":"防止這種情況"},{"english":"heritage authorities","chinese":"文物保育機構"},{"english":"focus on","chinese":"專注於"},{"english":"controlling visitor behaviour","chinese":"管控遊客行為"},{"english":"a stable system for conservation","chinese":"穩定的保育制度"},{"english":"the first and most immediate measure","chinese":"第一項也是最即時的措施"},{"english":"physical pressure","chinese":"實際壓力"},{"english":"vulnerable sites","chinese":"脆弱的遺址"},{"english":"historic attractions","chinese":"歷史景點"},{"english":"careless visitor","chinese":"粗心大意的遊客"},{"english":"walking, touching, climbing, and crowding","chinese":"行走、觸摸、攀爬和擠滿"},{"english":"the same spaces","chinese":"同一片空間"},{"english":"for this reason","chinese":"因此"},{"english":"introduce timed tickets","chinese":"推出分時段門票"},{"english":"daily visitor limits","chinese":"每日遊客人數限制"},{"english":"protected walking routes","chinese":"受保護的步行路線"},{"english":"restricted zones","chinese":"限制進入區域"},{"english":"especially delicate structures","chinese":"特別脆弱的結構"},{"english":"be allowed to","chinese":"被允許"},{"english":"view an ancient temple","chinese":"參觀古老寺廟"},{"english":"a controlled path","chinese":"受管制的路徑"},{"english":"instead of walking freely through","chinese":"而不是自由穿行於"},{"english":"the risk of erosion","chinese":"侵蝕風險"},{"english":"accidental damage","chinese":"意外損壞"},{"english":"overcrowding","chinese":"過度擠迫"},{"english":"greatly reduced","chinese":"大大減少"},{"english":"cultural heritage","chinese":"文化遺產"},{"english":"rather","chinese":"反而；而是"},{"english":"experience it without","chinese":"在不……的情況下體驗"},{"english":"slowly destroying it","chinese":"慢慢破壞它"},{"english":"directly fund preservation","chinese":"直接資助保育"},{"english":"entrance fees","chinese":"入場費"},{"english":"tourism taxes","chinese":"旅遊稅"},{"english":"conservation charges","chinese":"保育費"},{"english":"be used specifically to","chinese":"專門用於"},{"english":"repair buildings","chinese":"修復建築物"},{"english":"employ trained staff","chinese":"聘請受過訓練的職員"},{"english":"install protective equipment","chinese":"安裝保護設備"},{"english":"monitor damage over time","chinese":"長期監察損壞情況"},{"english":"at the same time","chinese":"同時"},{"english":"tour operators","chinese":"旅行社；旅遊營辦商"},{"english":"be required to","chinese":"被要求"},{"english":"educate visitors","chinese":"教育遊客"},{"english":"sensitive sites","chinese":"敏感遺址；需特別保護的地方"},{"english":"strict fines","chinese":"嚴厲罰款"},{"english":"be imposed on","chinese":"施加於"},{"english":"ignore rules","chinese":"無視規則"},{"english":"remove objects","chinese":"拿走物件"},{"english":"vandalise property","chinese":"破壞財物"},{"english":"clear signs alone","chinese":"單靠清晰標誌"},{"english":"explanation and enforcement","chinese":"解釋和執法"},{"english":"shared history","chinese":"共同歷史"},{"english":"photo opportunity","chinese":"拍照機會"},{"english":"behave responsibly","chinese":"負責任地行事"},{"english":"excessive visitor pressure","chinese":"過度遊客壓力"},{"english":"tourism revenue","chinese":"旅遊收入"},{"english":"long-term conservation","chinese":"長遠保育"},{"english":"open a window onto the past","chinese":"打開通往過去的一扇窗"},{"english":"close it forever","chinese":"永遠關上它"}]},"model-essay-43-ielts-discuss-both-views":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-43-ielts-discuss-both-views","essayKey":"discuss-both-views:43","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-43-ielts-discuss-both-views","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/discuss-both-views-your-opinion/EdmundBd9ExpBth-Q43","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"Completing a university degree is often seen as a direct route to secure and well-paid employment. Others, however, argue that practical experience and soft skills are more valuable in the modern workplace. Although university education can provide an important foundation, I strongly believe that experience and interpersonal abilities are more important for long-term career success.","chinese":"完成大學學位常被視為獲得穩定且高薪工作的直接途徑。 然而，其他人則認為，在現代職場中，實際經驗和軟技能更有價值。 儘管大學教育能提供重要基礎，但我堅信，經驗和人際能力對長遠職業成功更加重要。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"On the one hand, a university qualification can be essential because it gives people specialised knowledge and formal credibility. In fields such as medicine, engineering, law, and finance, employers cannot simply rely on a candidate’s personality or enthusiasm; they need evidence that the person has mastered complex theories, technical procedures, and professional standards. A degree also signals discipline, commitment, and the ability to complete demanding tasks over several years. For example, a hospital would naturally prefer a doctor who has completed medical school, because patients’ lives depend on accurate knowledge and careful training. In this sense, university education acts as a gatekeeper for many respected professions.","chinese":"一方面，大學學歷可能是必要的，因為它能給予人們專門知識和正式可信度。 在醫學、工程、法律和金融等領域，僱主不能單純依靠求職者的性格或熱情；他們需要證據證明這個人已經掌握複雜理論、技術程序和專業標準。 學位也代表著自律、承諾，以及在數年時間內完成高要求任務的能力。 例如，醫院自然會更傾向聘請一位完成醫學院訓練的醫生，因為病人的生命取決於準確的知識和嚴謹的訓練。 從這個意義上說，大學教育對許多受人尊重的專業而言，起著把關人的作用。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"On the other hand, experience and soft skills are often what allow people to perform well after they are hired. Many graduates understand theory but struggle to communicate clearly, solve real problems, manage pressure, or work with difficult colleagues. By contrast, someone who has spent years in a workplace may know how to handle customers, adapt to sudden changes, and make practical decisions under pressure. These abilities are not easily taught in lecture halls; they are developed through real situations, mistakes, feedback, and responsibility. For instance, a manager with strong communication skills can motivate a team and resolve conflict, whereas a highly educated but inflexible employee may damage morale and slow down progress.","chinese":"另一方面，經驗和軟技能往往才是讓人們在受聘後表現出色的因素。 許多畢業生懂得理論，卻難以清晰溝通、解決實際問題、應對壓力，或與難相處的同事合作。 相比之下，一個在職場工作多年的人，可能知道如何應對客戶、適應突發變化，並在壓力下作出實際決定。 這些能力並不容易在演講廳中教授；它們是透過真實情境、錯誤、反饋和責任逐步培養出來的。 例如，一位具備強大溝通能力的經理可以激勵團隊並解決衝突，而一位受過高等教育但缺乏彈性的員工，則可能損害士氣並拖慢進度。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, university education is valuable, especially in professions that require technical expertise. However, I believe experience and soft skills are more important overall, because they determine whether a person can actually succeed in the complex, human reality of the workplace.","chinese":"總結來說，大學教育是有價值的，尤其是在需要專業技術知識的職業中。 然而，我認為整體而言，經驗和軟技能更加重要，因為它們決定了一個人能否真正地在複雜而充滿人際因素的職場現實中取得成功。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"completing a university degree","chinese":"完成大學學位"},{"english":"be seen as","chinese":"被視為"},{"english":"a direct route to","chinese":"通往……的直接途徑"},{"english":"secure and well-paid employment","chinese":"穩定而高薪的工作"},{"english":"practical experience","chinese":"實際經驗"},{"english":"soft skills","chinese":"軟技能"},{"english":"more valuable in","chinese":"在……中更有價值"},{"english":"the modern workplace","chinese":"現代職場"},{"english":"university education","chinese":"大學教育"},{"english":"provide an important foundation","chinese":"提供重要基礎"},{"english":"strongly believe that","chinese":"強烈相信"},{"english":"interpersonal abilities","chinese":"人際能力"},{"english":"long-term career success","chinese":"長遠事業成功"},{"english":"on the one hand","chinese":"一方面"},{"english":"university qualification","chinese":"大學資歷"},{"english":"be essential","chinese":"是必要的"},{"english":"specialised knowledge","chinese":"專門知識"},{"english":"formal credibility","chinese":"正式可信度；正式認可"},{"english":"in fields such as","chinese":"在例如……的領域"},{"english":"cannot simply rely on","chinese":"不能單純依賴"},{"english":"a candidate's personality or enthusiasm","chinese":"求職者的性格或熱情"},{"english":"need evidence that","chinese":"需要證據證明"},{"english":"master complex theories","chinese":"掌握複雜理論"},{"english":"technical procedures","chinese":"技術程序"},{"english":"professional standards","chinese":"專業標準"},{"english":"signal discipline and commitment","chinese":"顯示自律和投入"},{"english":"complete demanding tasks","chinese":"完成要求高的任務"},{"english":"over several years","chinese":"長達數年"},{"english":"naturally prefer","chinese":"自然會較喜歡"},{"english":"complete medical school","chinese":"完成醫學院課程"},{"english":"patients' lives depend on","chinese":"病人的生命取決於"},{"english":"accurate knowledge","chinese":"準確知識"},{"english":"careful training","chinese":"嚴謹訓練"},{"english":"in this sense","chinese":"從這個意義上說"},{"english":"act as a gatekeeper for","chinese":"作為……的入門門檻"},{"english":"respected professions","chinese":"受尊重的專業"},{"english":"on the other hand","chinese":"另一方面"},{"english":"perform well after they are hired","chinese":"受聘後表現良好"},{"english":"understand theory","chinese":"理解理論"},{"english":"struggle to communicate clearly","chinese":"難以清楚溝通"},{"english":"solve real problems","chinese":"解決實際問題"},{"english":"manage pressure","chinese":"應對壓力"},{"english":"work with difficult colleagues","chinese":"與難相處的同事合作"},{"english":"by contrast","chinese":"相反"},{"english":"spend years in a workplace","chinese":"在職場工作多年"},{"english":"handle customers","chinese":"應對顧客"},{"english":"adapt to sudden changes","chinese":"適應突如其來的變化"},{"english":"make practical decisions under pressure","chinese":"在壓力下作出實際決定"},{"english":"be not easily taught","chinese":"不容易被教授"},{"english":"lecture halls","chinese":"演講廳；大學課堂"},{"english":"be developed through","chinese":"透過……培養"},{"english":"real situations","chinese":"真實情境"},{"english":"mistakes, feedback, and responsibility","chinese":"錯誤、回饋和責任"},{"english":"for instance","chinese":"例如"},{"english":"strong communication skills","chinese":"強大的溝通技巧"},{"english":"motivate a team","chinese":"激勵團隊"},{"english":"resolve conflict","chinese":"解決衝突"},{"english":"highly educated but inflexible","chinese":"學歷高但不懂變通的"},{"english":"damage morale","chinese":"損害士氣"},{"english":"slow down progress","chinese":"拖慢進度"},{"english":"technical expertise","chinese":"專業技術知識"},{"english":"more important overall","chinese":"整體而言更重要"},{"english":"determine whether","chinese":"決定是否"},{"english":"actually succeed","chinese":"真正成功"},{"english":"the complex, human reality of","chinese":"……中複雜而涉及人際的現實"},{"english":"the workplace","chinese":"職場"}]},"model-essay-43-ielts-opinion":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-43-ielts-opinion","essayKey":"opinion:43","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-43-ielts-opinion","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/opinions/EdmundBd9OP-Q43","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"Environmental damage is one of the most serious challenges facing the modern world, and fuel consumption is often seen as an obvious target. However, I completely disagree that making fuel more expensive is the best way to deal with global environmental problems. This approach is too blunt, too unfair, and far less effective than long-term investment and regulation.","chinese":"環境破壞是現代世界面臨的最嚴重挑戰之一，而燃料消耗通常被視為一個明顯針對目標 然而，我完全不同意提高燃料價格是處理全球環境問題的最佳方法。 這種做法過於粗暴、過於不公平，而且遠不如長期投資和監管有效。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"The first problem is that higher fuel prices would punish many ordinary people without giving them a realistic way to change their behaviour. In many towns and rural areas, workers, parents, and small business owners depend on cars or vans because public transport is limited, unreliable, or simply unavailable. If petrol or diesel becomes much more expensive, these people may not drive less; they may just have less money for food, rent, healthcare, or education. For example, a delivery driver whose income depends on daily travel cannot suddenly stop using fuel because prices rise. In this case, the policy becomes a financial burden rather than a genuine environmental solution.","chinese":"第一個問題是，更高的燃料價格會懲罰許多普通人，卻沒有給予他們一種現實可行的方法去改變自己的行為。 在許多城鎮和鄉郊地區，工人、父母和小企業主都依賴汽車或貨車，因為公共交通有限、不可靠，或者根本不存在。 如果汽油或柴油變得昂貴得多，這些人未必會減少駕駛；他們可能只是會有更少金錢用於食物、租金、醫療或教育。 例如，一名收入依賴每日出行的送貨司機，不可能因為價格上升就突然停止使用燃料。 在這種情況下，這項政策會變成一種經濟負擔，而不是真正的環境解決方案。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"A better answer is to make cleaner choices that are practical and attractive. Governments should invest heavily in public transport, renewable energy, charging networks, and greener urban design so that people can reduce fuel use without sacrificing their basic needs. When buses are frequent, trains are affordable, and clean energy is widely available, lower-emission behaviour becomes a natural part of daily life rather than a forced sacrifice. At the same time, strict rules should be placed on industries that produce large amounts of pollution, because global environmental damage is not caused only by private drivers. Factories, airlines, shipping companies, and energy producers must also be required to modernise their systems and reduce emissions at source.","chinese":"更好的答案是讓更清潔的選擇變得實際而有吸引力。 政府應該大量投資於公共交通、可再生能源、充電網絡和更環保的城市設計，使人們能夠在不犧牲基本需要的情況下減少燃料使用。 當巴士班次頻密、火車價格可負擔，而清潔能源也廣泛可得時，低排放行為便會成為日常生活中自然的一部分，而不是一種被迫作出的犧牲。 與此同時，應該對製造大量污染的行業實施嚴格規則，因為全球環境破壞並不只是由私人駕駛者造成的。 工廠、航空公司、航運公司和能源生產商也必須被要求將其系統現代化，並從源頭減少排放。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, increasing the cost of fuel is not the best solution to global environmental problems. Real progress depends on building cleaner alternatives and holding major polluters responsible, not simply making everyday life more expensive for ordinary people.","chinese":"總結來說，提高燃料成本並不是解決全球環境問題的最佳方法。 真正的進展取決於建立更清潔的替代方案，並讓主要污染者承擔責任，而不是單純讓普通人的日常生活變得更加昂貴。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"environmental damage","chinese":"環境破壞"},{"english":"one of the most serious challenges","chinese":"最嚴重挑戰之一"},{"english":"facing the modern world","chinese":"現代世界所面對的"},{"english":"fuel consumption","chinese":"燃料消耗"},{"english":"be seen as","chinese":"被視為"},{"english":"obvious target","chinese":"明顯目標"},{"english":"making fuel more expensive","chinese":"令燃料更昂貴"},{"english":"deal with","chinese":"處理"},{"english":"global environmental problems","chinese":"全球環境問題"},{"english":"this approach","chinese":"這種做法"},{"english":"too blunt","chinese":"過於粗糙"},{"english":"too unfair","chinese":"過於不公平"},{"english":"far less effective than","chinese":"遠不及……有效"},{"english":"long-term investment","chinese":"長期投資"},{"english":"regulation","chinese":"規管"},{"english":"higher fuel prices","chinese":"較高燃料價格"},{"english":"punish ordinary people","chinese":"懲罰普通人"},{"english":"realistic way to","chinese":"現實可行的方法去……"},{"english":"change their behaviour","chinese":"改變他們的行為"},{"english":"rural areas","chinese":"鄉郊地區"},{"english":"small business owners","chinese":"小企業東主"},{"english":"depend on cars or vans","chinese":"依賴私家車或客貨車"},{"english":"public transport","chinese":"公共交通"},{"english":"limited, unreliable, or simply unavailable","chinese":"有限、不可靠或根本沒有"},{"english":"petrol or diesel","chinese":"汽油或柴油"},{"english":"drive less","chinese":"減少駕駛"},{"english":"have less money for","chinese":"用於……的錢較少"},{"english":"healthcare","chinese":"醫療護理"},{"english":"delivery driver","chinese":"送貨司機"},{"english":"income depends on","chinese":"收入取決於……"},{"english":"daily travel","chinese":"日常出行"},{"english":"suddenly stop using fuel","chinese":"突然停止使用燃料"},{"english":"prices rise","chinese":"價格上升"},{"english":"financial burden","chinese":"財政負擔"},{"english":"rather than a genuine environmental solution","chinese":"而不是真正的環保解決方案"},{"english":"genuine environmental solution","chinese":"真正的環保解決方案"},{"english":"a better answer","chinese":"更好的答案；更好的做法"},{"english":"cleaner choices","chinese":"較清潔的選擇"},{"english":"practical and attractive","chinese":"實際可行而具吸引力"},{"english":"invest heavily in","chinese":"大量投資於……"},{"english":"renewable energy","chinese":"可再生能源"},{"english":"charging networks","chinese":"充電網絡"},{"english":"greener urban design","chinese":"更環保的城市設計"},{"english":"reduce fuel use","chinese":"減少燃料使用"},{"english":"without sacrificing","chinese":"而不犧牲……"},{"english":"basic needs","chinese":"基本需要"},{"english":"buses are frequent","chinese":"巴士班次頻密"},{"english":"trains are affordable","chinese":"火車價格可負擔"},{"english":"clean energy is widely available","chinese":"清潔能源廣泛可用"},{"english":"lower-emission behaviour","chinese":"較低排放的行為"},{"english":"natural part of daily life","chinese":"日常生活中自然的一部分"},{"english":"forced sacrifice","chinese":"被迫作出的犧牲"},{"english":"at the same time","chinese":"同時"},{"english":"strict rules","chinese":"嚴格規則"},{"english":"be placed on","chinese":"施加於……"},{"english":"produce large amounts of pollution","chinese":"產生大量污染"},{"english":"private drivers","chinese":"私家車司機"},{"english":"factories, airlines, shipping companies, and energy producers","chinese":"工廠、航空公司、航運公司和能源生產商"},{"english":"be required to","chinese":"被要求去……"},{"english":"modernise their systems","chinese":"現代化其系統"},{"english":"reduce emissions at source","chinese":"從源頭減少排放"},{"english":"increasing the cost of fuel","chinese":"增加燃料成本"},{"english":"real progress","chinese":"真正進步"},{"english":"cleaner alternatives","chinese":"較清潔的替代選擇"},{"english":"hold major polluters responsible","chinese":"追究主要污染者的責任"},{"english":"everyday life","chinese":"日常生活"},{"english":"more expensive for ordinary people","chinese":"對普通人而言更昂貴"}]},"model-essay-44-ielts-direct-question":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-44-ielts-direct-question","essayKey":"direct-question:44","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-44-ielts-direct-question","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/direct-question/EdmundBd9Dir-Q44","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"Congestion has become one of the most stubborn problems in modern cities. One proposed response is to raise taxes on private vehicles. This would ease pressure on roads by changing commuters’ behaviour, but cities also need dependable alternatives to driving. This essay will explain the effect of such taxation and outline two further measures.","chinese":"交通擠塞已成為現代城市中最頑固的問題之一。 其中一個被提出的應對方法，是提高私家車的稅項。 這可以透過改變通勤者的行為來減輕道路壓力，但城市也需要提供可靠的駕車替代選擇。 本文將解釋這種稅收政策的作用，並概述另外兩項措施。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"A higher tax could reduce congestion because it makes private car ownership and use less attractive. If registration fees, annual licences or ownership charges become more expensive, many people will begin to question whether every journey needs to be made by car. For example, a worker who drives a short distance to the office mainly out of habit may switch to a train or bus once the cost of keeping a car becomes harder to justify. When thousands of similar decisions are made across a city, the number of vehicles on the road falls. In addition, the money collected from these taxes could be used to improve public transport, so the policy would not simply punish drivers; it would create a cleaner and more efficient transport system.","chinese":"較高的稅項可以減少交通擠塞，因為它會降低擁有和使用私家車的吸引力。 如果登記費、年度牌照費或車輛擁有成本變得更昂貴，許多人便會開始思考是否每一次出行都必須駕車。 例如，一位主要出於習慣而短途駕車上班的員工，一旦覺得養車成本越來越難以合理化，便可能改乘火車或巴士。 當一座城市中有成千上萬人作出類似決定時，道路上的車輛數量便會下降。 此外，從這些稅項中收取的資金可以用來改善公共交通，因此這項政策並不只是懲罰駕駛者；它會創造一個更清潔、更高效的交通系統。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"Other measures are also necessary because taxation alone cannot solve urban congestion. The first is to make public transport fast, affordable and reliable. People will not leave their cars at home if buses are infrequent, trains are overcrowded or routes are poorly connected. Cities should therefore expand rail services, add dedicated bus lanes and connect residential districts more directly with workplaces and schools. A second measure is to manage road use more carefully through congestion charges, higher parking fees in crowded districts, and safer walking and cycling routes. These policies reduce unnecessary car trips while giving residents realistic alternatives.","chinese":"其他措施同樣必要，因為單靠稅收無法解決城市交通擠塞。 第一項措施是讓公共交通變得快捷、價格合理並且可靠。 如果巴士班次疏落、火車過度擠迫，或者路線銜接不佳，人們便不會把車留在家中。 因此，城市應該擴展鐵路服務、增設巴士專用線，並讓住宅區與工作地點和學校有更直接的連接。 第二項措施是透過擠塞收費、在人流密集地區提高泊車費，以及建立更安全的步行和單車路線，來更謹慎地管理道路使用。 這些政策可以減少不必要的私家車出行，同時為居民提供切實可行的替代選擇。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, increasing the tax on private vehicles can alleviate congestion by discouraging car dependency and funding better transport. However, cities will only see lasting improvement if this is combined with stronger public transport, road pricing policies and safe alternatives to driving.","chinese":"總結來說，提高私家車稅項可以透過減少人們對汽車的依賴，並為更好的交通系統提供資金，從而紓緩交通擠塞。 然而，只有當這項措施與更完善的公共交通、道路收費政策，以及安全的駕車替代選擇結合起來時，城市才會看到持久的改善。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"congestion","chinese":"交通擠塞"},{"english":"one of the most stubborn problems","chinese":"最棘手的問題之一"},{"english":"modern cities","chinese":"現代城市"},{"english":"one proposed response","chinese":"一個建議的應對方法"},{"english":"raise taxes on","chinese":"提高……的稅項"},{"english":"private vehicles","chinese":"私家車"},{"english":"ease pressure on roads","chinese":"紓緩道路壓力"},{"english":"commuters' behaviour","chinese":"通勤者的行為"},{"english":"dependable alternatives to","chinese":"可靠的……替代選擇"},{"english":"driving","chinese":"駕駛"},{"english":"such taxation","chinese":"這種徵稅"},{"english":"outline two further measures","chinese":"概述另外兩項措施"},{"english":"a higher tax","chinese":"較高稅項"},{"english":"private car ownership and use","chinese":"擁有及使用私家車"},{"english":"less attractive","chinese":"吸引力較低"},{"english":"registration fees","chinese":"登記費"},{"english":"annual licences","chinese":"年度牌照費"},{"english":"ownership charges","chinese":"車輛擁有收費"},{"english":"begin to question","chinese":"開始質疑"},{"english":"every journey","chinese":"每一程"},{"english":"be made by car","chinese":"以駕車方式完成"},{"english":"drives a short distance","chinese":"短途駕車"},{"english":"mainly out of habit","chinese":"主要出於習慣"},{"english":"switch to","chinese":"轉用"},{"english":"keeping a car","chinese":"養車"},{"english":"harder to justify","chinese":"更難說得過去"},{"english":"similar decisions","chinese":"類似決定"},{"english":"across a city","chinese":"遍及整個城市"},{"english":"the number of vehicles on the road","chinese":"路面車輛數量"},{"english":"falls","chinese":"下降"},{"english":"money collected from","chinese":"從……收取的款項"},{"english":"public transport","chinese":"公共交通"},{"english":"not simply punish drivers","chinese":"不只是懲罰司機"},{"english":"a cleaner and more efficient transport system","chinese":"更潔淨、更高效的交通系統"},{"english":"other measures","chinese":"其他措施"},{"english":"taxation alone","chinese":"單靠徵稅"},{"english":"solve urban congestion","chinese":"解決城市交通擠塞"},{"english":"fast, affordable and reliable","chinese":"快捷、負擔得起而可靠"},{"english":"leave their cars at home","chinese":"把車留在家中"},{"english":"infrequent","chinese":"班次不頻密的"},{"english":"overcrowded","chinese":"過度擠迫的"},{"english":"poorly connected","chinese":"連接不佳的"},{"english":"expand rail services","chinese":"擴展鐵路服務"},{"english":"dedicated bus lanes","chinese":"巴士專用線"},{"english":"residential districts","chinese":"住宅區"},{"english":"more directly with","chinese":"更直接地與……連接"},{"english":"workplaces and schools","chinese":"工作地點和學校"},{"english":"manage road use","chinese":"管理道路使用"},{"english":"congestion charges","chinese":"擠塞徵費"},{"english":"higher parking fees","chinese":"較高泊車費"},{"english":"crowded districts","chinese":"擠迫地區"},{"english":"safer walking and cycling routes","chinese":"更安全的步行和單車路線"},{"english":"reduce unnecessary car trips","chinese":"減少不必要的汽車旅程"},{"english":"realistic alternatives","chinese":"切實可行的替代選擇"},{"english":"increasing the tax on","chinese":"提高……的稅項"},{"english":"alleviate congestion","chinese":"紓緩交通擠塞"},{"english":"discouraging car dependency","chinese":"減少對汽車的依賴"},{"english":"funding better transport","chinese":"資助更好的交通"},{"english":"lasting improvement","chinese":"持久改善"},{"english":"be combined with","chinese":"與……結合"},{"english":"road pricing policies","chinese":"道路收費政策"},{"english":"safe alternatives to driving","chinese":"安全的駕駛替代選擇"}]},"model-essay-44-ielts-opinion":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-44-ielts-opinion","essayKey":"opinion:44","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-44-ielts-opinion","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/opinions/EdmundBd9OP-Q44","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"Environmental damage is no longer a distant concern, and governments must decide carefully where limited public money should go. Some argue that local environmental issues should receive less funding so that more can be spent on global warming. I completely disagree with this view, because local problems are often immediate threats to public health and are also part of the wider climate crisis.","chinese":"環境破壞已不再是一個遙遠的問題，而政府必須謹慎決定有限的公共資金應該投放到哪裡。 有些人認為，本地環境問題應該獲得較少資金，這樣便可以把更多資源投放到全球暖化上。 我完全不同意這個觀點，因為本地問題往往是對公共健康的即時威脅，同時也是更廣泛氣候危機的一部分。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"First, local environmental problems are not minor just because they happen close to home. Polluted rivers, poor air quality, illegal dumping and unsafe drinking water can damage people’s daily lives far more directly than distant climate projections. If councils and national authorities cut spending in these areas, ordinary citizens may pay the price through respiratory illness, contaminated neighbourhoods and declining living standards. For example, a city that neglects waste collection and drainage may soon face blocked waterways, flooding and disease after heavy rain. In this sense, local environmental funding is not a luxury; it is a basic form of public protection.","chinese":"首先，本地環境問題並不會因為發生在我們身邊而變得微不足道。 受污染的河流、惡劣的空氣質素、非法傾倒垃圾以及不安全的飲用水，對人們日常生活的傷害，遠比遙遠的氣候預測更加直接。 如果地方議會和國家政府削減這些方面的開支，普通市民便可能要以呼吸系統疾病、受污染的社區和下降的生活水平作為代價。 例如，一個忽視垃圾收集和排水系統的城市，在大雨過後可能很快便會面對水道堵塞、水浸和疾病問題。 從這個意義上說，本地環境資金並不是一種奢侈，而是一種基本的公共保護。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"Second, tackling global warming actually depends on strong local action. Carbon emissions are produced in real streets, homes, factories and transport systems, not in some abstract global arena. When governments invest in cleaner buses, better recycling systems, energy-efficient buildings and urban green spaces, they are addressing local problems and climate change at the same time. Reducing this funding would therefore be like removing the bricks from a house while trying to strengthen its roof. A serious climate strategy needs both a national vision and practical local delivery.","chinese":"第二，應對全球暖化其實有賴於強而有力的本地行動。 碳排放是在真實的街道、家庭、工廠和交通系統中產生的，而不是在某個抽象的全球場域中產生的。 當政府投資於更清潔的巴士、更完善的回收系統、更節能的建築和城市綠化空間時，它們其實是在同時處理本地問題和氣候變化。 因此，削減這些資金就像一邊試圖加固屋頂，一邊卻把房子的磚塊拆走。 一個認真的氣候策略既需要國家層面的願景，也需要本地層面的實際執行。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, I strongly disagree that governments should divert money away from local environmental problems. Global warming is undeniably urgent, but it cannot be solved by neglecting the smaller environmental battles that protect communities and reduce emissions. The wiser approach is to strengthen local environmental programmes, because they are the foundation on which broader climate action is built.","chinese":"總結來說，我強烈不同意政府應該把資金從本地環境問題上轉移走。 全球暖化無疑是緊急問題，但它不能透過忽視那些保護社區和減少排放的較小型環境戰役來解決。 更明智的做法是加強本地環境計劃，因為它們正是更廣泛氣候行動得以建立的"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"environmental damage","chinese":"環境破壞"},{"english":"distant concern","chinese":"遙遠的憂慮"},{"english":"limited public money","chinese":"有限公帑"},{"english":"should go","chinese":"應該投放到哪裏"},{"english":"local environmental issues","chinese":"本地環境問題"},{"english":"receive less funding","chinese":"獲得較少撥款"},{"english":"be spent on","chinese":"被用於……"},{"english":"global warming","chinese":"全球暖化"},{"english":"immediate threats to","chinese":"對……的即時威脅"},{"english":"public health","chinese":"公共健康"},{"english":"part of the wider climate crisis","chinese":"更廣泛氣候危機的一部分"},{"english":"not minor just because","chinese":"不會只是因為……而變得輕微"},{"english":"happen close to home","chinese":"發生在身邊"},{"english":"polluted rivers","chinese":"受污染的河流"},{"english":"poor air quality","chinese":"惡劣空氣質素"},{"english":"illegal dumping","chinese":"非法傾倒廢物"},{"english":"unsafe drinking water","chinese":"不安全的飲用水"},{"english":"damage people's daily lives","chinese":"損害人們的日常生活"},{"english":"far more directly than","chinese":"比……直接得多"},{"english":"distant climate projections","chinese":"遙遠的氣候預測"},{"english":"councils and national authorities","chinese":"地方議會和國家機關"},{"english":"cut spending in","chinese":"削減在……上的開支"},{"english":"ordinary citizens","chinese":"普通市民"},{"english":"pay the price through","chinese":"透過……付出代價"},{"english":"respiratory illness","chinese":"呼吸系統疾病"},{"english":"contaminated neighbourhoods","chinese":"受污染的社區"},{"english":"declining living standards","chinese":"生活水平下降"},{"english":"neglects waste collection","chinese":"忽視垃圾收集"},{"english":"waste collection","chinese":"垃圾收集"},{"english":"drainage","chinese":"排水系統"},{"english":"blocked waterways","chinese":"水道堵塞"},{"english":"flooding and disease","chinese":"水浸和疾病"},{"english":"heavy rain","chinese":"大雨"},{"english":"in this sense","chinese":"從這個意義上說"},{"english":"local environmental funding","chinese":"本地環境撥款"},{"english":"not a luxury","chinese":"不是奢侈品"},{"english":"basic form of public protection","chinese":"基本公共保護形式"},{"english":"tackling global warming","chinese":"應對全球暖化"},{"english":"depends on","chinese":"取決於"},{"english":"strong local action","chinese":"強而有力的本地行動"},{"english":"carbon emissions","chinese":"碳排放"},{"english":"real streets, homes, factories and transport systems","chinese":"真實街道、住宅、工廠和交通系統"},{"english":"abstract global arena","chinese":"抽象的全球場域"},{"english":"invest in","chinese":"投資於……"},{"english":"cleaner buses","chinese":"較清潔的巴士"},{"english":"recycling systems","chinese":"回收系統"},{"english":"energy-efficient buildings","chinese":"節能建築"},{"english":"urban green spaces","chinese":"城市綠化空間"},{"english":"at the same time","chinese":"同時"},{"english":"reducing this funding","chinese":"削減這筆撥款"},{"english":"be like removing the bricks from","chinese":"就像從……拆走磚塊"},{"english":"trying to strengthen its roof","chinese":"試圖加固屋頂"},{"english":"serious climate strategy","chinese":"認真的氣候策略"},{"english":"national vision","chinese":"國家願景"},{"english":"practical local delivery","chinese":"實際的本地執行"},{"english":"divert money away from","chinese":"將資金從……轉走"},{"english":"undeniably urgent","chinese":"無可否認地迫切"},{"english":"be solved by neglecting","chinese":"透過忽視……來解決"},{"english":"smaller environmental battles","chinese":"較小規模的環境戰役"},{"english":"protect communities","chinese":"保護社區"},{"english":"reduce emissions","chinese":"減少排放"},{"english":"wiser approach","chinese":"更明智的方法"},{"english":"strengthen local environmental programmes","chinese":"加強本地環境計劃"},{"english":"the foundation on which","chinese":"……的基礎"},{"english":"broader climate action","chinese":"更廣泛的氣候行動"}]},"model-essay-45-ielts-direct-question":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-45-ielts-direct-question","essayKey":"direct-question:45","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-45-ielts-direct-question","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/direct-question/EdmundBd9Dir-Q45","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"In many parts of the developing world, work is judged less by personal fulfilment than by the basic security it provides. This is why job satisfaction is often seen as a privilege rather than an ordinary expectation. I believe, however, that it is extremely important, because a society which ignores workers’ well-being eventually pays a price in productivity, health and human dignity.","chinese":"在許多發展中地區，人們評價工作的標準較少在於個人滿足感，而更多在於它所提供的基本保障。 這就是為甚麼工作滿足感經常被視為一種特權，而不是一種普通的期待。 然而，我認為它極其重要，因為一個忽視員工福祉的社會，最終會在生產力、健康和人的尊嚴方面付出代價。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"The main reason job satisfaction appears luxurious is economic pressure. In countries where wages are low, social protection is weak and unemployment is high, people often have little room to choose work that matches their interests or values. Their first concern is not whether a job is inspiring, but whether it can pay for food, rent and their children’s education. For example, a factory worker or delivery rider may accept long hours, unsafe conditions or repetitive tasks because losing the job would threaten the whole family. When survival is at stake, fulfilment naturally takes a back seat.","chinese":"工作滿足感之所以顯得像一種奢侈，主要原因是經濟壓力。 在工資低、社會保障薄弱、失業率高的國家，人們往往幾乎沒有空間去選擇符合自己興趣或價值觀的工作。 他們最先關心的並不是一份工作是否令人受到啟發，而是它是否能夠支付食物、租金和子女教育的開支。 例如，一名工廠工人或外賣配送員可能會接受長工時、不安全的工作環境或重複性的任務，因為失去這份工作會威脅到整個家庭。 當生存受到威脅時，滿足感自然會退居次位。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"Another reason is that many labour markets in poorer countries offer limited bargaining power. Workers may not have strong unions, clear contracts or realistic chances of promotion, so they cannot easily demand better treatment. In such circumstances, job satisfaction can feel like a luxury reserved for people with education, savings or professional skills. Those without these advantages may feel that they must take whatever work is available, even if it leaves them exhausted or undervalued.","chinese":"另一個原因是，許多較貧困國家的勞動市場給予工人的議價能力有限。 工人可能沒有強大的工會、清晰的合約，或實際可行的晉升機會，因此他們不容易要求更好的待遇。 在這種情況下，工作滿足感可能會讓人感覺像是一種只留給受過教育、有積蓄或具備專業技能人士的奢侈品。 沒有這些優勢的人可能會覺得，他們必須接受任何能找到的工作，即使那份工作令他們筋疲力盡或感到不被重視。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 3","english":"Despite this, job satisfaction should not be dismissed as unimportant. People spend much of their lives at work, so a job that causes constant stress can damage both mental and physical health. By contrast, employees who feel respected and purposeful are more likely to stay motivated, improve their skills and contribute positively to their workplace.","chinese":"儘管如此，工作滿足感不應被視為不重要而被忽略。 人們一生中有大量時間都花在工作上，因此一份會造成持續壓力的工作，可能會損害心理和身體健康。 相比之下，感到受尊重並且有目標感的員工，更有可能保持動力、提升技能，並對工作場所作出正面貢獻。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, job satisfaction is considered a luxury in many developing countries because economic insecurity limits people’s choices. Nevertheless, it is essential, not decorative, because decent work is one of the foundations of a healthier and more productive society.","chinese":"總結來說，在許多發展中國家，工作滿足感被視為一種奢侈，是因為經濟上的不安全限制了人們的選擇。 然而，它是必要的，而不是裝飾性的，因為體面的工作是建立一個更健康、更具生產力社會的基礎之一。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"in many parts of","chinese":"在……很多地區"},{"english":"the developing world","chinese":"發展中地區"},{"english":"be judged less by...than by...","chinese":"較少以……而更多以……評價"},{"english":"personal fulfilment","chinese":"個人成就感；個人滿足感"},{"english":"basic security","chinese":"基本保障"},{"english":"This is why","chinese":"這就是為甚麼"},{"english":"job satisfaction","chinese":"工作滿足感"},{"english":"be seen as","chinese":"被視為"},{"english":"a privilege rather than","chinese":"是一種特權而不是"},{"english":"an ordinary expectation","chinese":"普通期望"},{"english":"workers' well-being","chinese":"工人的福祉；身心健康"},{"english":"eventually pays a price in","chinese":"最終在……方面付出代價"},{"english":"productivity","chinese":"生產力"},{"english":"human dignity","chinese":"人的尊嚴"},{"english":"the main reason","chinese":"主要原因"},{"english":"appears luxurious","chinese":"顯得奢侈"},{"english":"economic pressure","chinese":"經濟壓力"},{"english":"wages are low","chinese":"工資低"},{"english":"social protection is weak","chinese":"社會保障薄弱"},{"english":"unemployment is high","chinese":"失業率高"},{"english":"have little room to","chinese":"幾乎沒有空間去"},{"english":"choose work that matches","chinese":"選擇符合……的工作"},{"english":"interests or values","chinese":"興趣或價值觀"},{"english":"first concern","chinese":"首要考慮"},{"english":"whether a job is inspiring","chinese":"一份工作是否有啟發性"},{"english":"pay for food and rent","chinese":"支付食物和租金"},{"english":"children's education","chinese":"子女教育"},{"english":"factory worker","chinese":"工廠工人"},{"english":"delivery rider","chinese":"外賣速遞員"},{"english":"accept long hours","chinese":"接受長工時"},{"english":"unsafe conditions","chinese":"不安全的工作環境"},{"english":"repetitive tasks","chinese":"重複性工作"},{"english":"threaten the whole family","chinese":"威脅整個家庭"},{"english":"survival is at stake","chinese":"生存受到威脅"},{"english":"take a back seat","chinese":"退居次位"},{"english":"labour markets","chinese":"勞動市場"},{"english":"poorer countries","chinese":"較貧窮的國家"},{"english":"limited bargaining power","chinese":"有限的議價能力"},{"english":"strong unions","chinese":"強大的工會"},{"english":"clear contracts","chinese":"清晰合約"},{"english":"realistic chances of promotion","chinese":"實際的晉升機會"},{"english":"demand better treatment","chinese":"要求更好待遇"},{"english":"in such circumstances","chinese":"在這種情況下"},{"english":"feel like a luxury","chinese":"感覺像奢侈品"},{"english":"reserved for","chinese":"留給；專屬於"},{"english":"professional skills","chinese":"專業技能"},{"english":"without these advantages","chinese":"沒有這些優勢"},{"english":"whatever work is available","chinese":"任何可得到的工作"},{"english":"leaves them exhausted","chinese":"令他們精疲力竭"},{"english":"undervalued","chinese":"不受重視"},{"english":"Despite this","chinese":"儘管如此"},{"english":"be dismissed as unimportant","chinese":"被視為不重要而不理會"},{"english":"spend much of their lives at work","chinese":"把人生很多時間花在工作上"},{"english":"constant stress","chinese":"持續壓力"},{"english":"mental and physical health","chinese":"身心健康"},{"english":"By contrast","chinese":"相比之下"},{"english":"feel respected and purposeful","chinese":"感到受尊重和有目標"},{"english":"more likely to","chinese":"更有可能"},{"english":"stay motivated","chinese":"保持動力"},{"english":"improve their skills","chinese":"提升技能"},{"english":"contribute positively to","chinese":"對……作出正面貢獻"},{"english":"be considered a luxury","chinese":"被視為奢侈品"},{"english":"economic insecurity","chinese":"經濟不穩定"},{"english":"limits people's choices","chinese":"限制人們的選擇"},{"english":"Nevertheless","chinese":"然而"},{"english":"essential, not decorative","chinese":"是必要的，不是裝飾性的"},{"english":"decent work","chinese":"體面的工作"},{"english":"one of the foundations of","chinese":"……的基礎之一"},{"english":"a healthier and more productive society","chinese":"更健康、更有生產力的社會"}]},"model-essay-45-ielts-opinion":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-45-ielts-opinion","essayKey":"opinion:45","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-45-ielts-opinion","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/opinions/EdmundBd9OP-Q45","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"Public parks are often seen as pleasant but non-essential spaces, especially in cities facing pressure from population growth and economic competition. Some argue that this land would be more useful if it were converted into housing or commercial districts. I completely disagree with this view, because parks are essential to public health, social life, and the long-term sustainability of cities.","chinese":"公共公園常被視為令人愉快但並非必要的空間，尤其是在面對人口增長和經濟競爭壓力的城市中。 有些人認為，如果這些土地被改建成住宅區或商業區，會更有用途。 我完全不同意這個觀點，因為公園對公共健康、社交生活，以及城市的長遠可持續發展都是不可或缺的。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"The strongest reason for protecting public parks is that they provide a form of health support that buildings cannot replace. In crowded urban areas, many residents live in small apartments, work long hours, and have limited access to open space. Parks give people somewhere to walk, exercise, breathe fresh air, and recover from the pressure of city life. For example, a family living in a dense neighbourhood may not be able to afford private sports facilities, but a nearby park allows children to play safely and adults to stay active without spending money. If these spaces are replaced by apartments or offices, cities may become more crowded, more stressful, and less humane.","chinese":"保護公共公園最有力的理由是，它們提供了一種建築物無法取代的健康支持。 在擁擠的城市地區，許多居民住在狹小的公寓裡，工作時間很長，而且接觸開放空間的機會有限。 公園給人們一個可以散步、運動、呼吸新鮮空氣，並從城市生活壓力中恢復過來的地方 例如，一個住在人口密集社區的家庭，未必負擔得起私人運動設施，但附近的公園可以讓孩子安全玩耍，也讓成年人不用花錢便能保持活躍。 如果這些空間被公寓或辦公室取代，城市可能會變得更加擁擠、更令人感到壓力，也更缺乏人情味。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"Public parks also strengthen communities and improve the quality of urban development. They are shared spaces where people from different ages and backgrounds can meet naturally, rather than remaining isolated in private homes or workplaces. This matters because a successful city is not simply a collection of houses and businesses; it is a living environment where people feel connected and safe. Moreover, parks can support the economy indirectly by making cities more attractive to residents, workers, and visitors. A city with only concrete, traffic, and commercial buildings may generate short-term profit, but it risks becoming a place people want to escape from rather than invest in.","chinese":"公共公園也能加強社區聯繫，並提升城市發展的質素。 它們是共享空間，讓不同年齡和背景的人可以自然地相遇，而不是一直被隔離在私人住宅或工作場所之中。 這一點很重要，因為一個成功的城市並不只是房屋和商業機構的集合；它是一個讓人們感到有聯繫和安全感的生活環境。 此外，公園也可以透過讓城市對居民、工作者和遊客更具吸引力，間接支持經濟。 一個只有混凝土、交通和商業建築的城市，或許能創造短期利潤，但它也有可能變成一個人們想逃離，而不是願意投資其中的地方。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, I strongly disagree that public parks should be replaced by housing or business developments. While population growth and economic development are important, sacrificing green public spaces would damage health, weaken communities, and reduce the overall liveability of cities.","chinese":"總結來說，我強烈不同意公共公園應被住宅或商業發展取代。 雖然人口增長和經濟發展都很重要，但犧牲綠色公共空間將會損害健康、削弱社區，並降低城市整體的宜居程度。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"public parks","chinese":"公共公園"},{"english":"be seen as","chinese":"被視為"},{"english":"pleasant but non-essential spaces","chinese":"宜人但非必要的空間"},{"english":"especially in cities facing","chinese":"尤其在面對……的城市中"},{"english":"pressure from population growth","chinese":"來自人口增長的壓力"},{"english":"economic competition","chinese":"經濟競爭"},{"english":"be converted into","chinese":"被改建成"},{"english":"housing or commercial districts","chinese":"住宅或商業區"},{"english":"completely disagree with","chinese":"完全不同意……"},{"english":"essential to","chinese":"對……必不可少"},{"english":"public health","chinese":"公共健康"},{"english":"social life","chinese":"社交生活"},{"english":"long-term sustainability","chinese":"長遠可持續性"},{"english":"the strongest reason for","chinese":"……的最有力原因"},{"english":"protecting public parks","chinese":"保護公共公園"},{"english":"a form of health support","chinese":"一種健康支援"},{"english":"cannot replace","chinese":"不能取代"},{"english":"crowded urban areas","chinese":"擠迫的城市地區"},{"english":"small apartments","chinese":"小型住宅單位"},{"english":"work long hours","chinese":"長時間工作"},{"english":"limited access to","chinese":"接觸……的機會有限"},{"english":"open space","chinese":"開放空間"},{"english":"somewhere to","chinese":"可以……的地方"},{"english":"breathe fresh air","chinese":"呼吸新鮮空氣"},{"english":"recover from","chinese":"從……中恢復"},{"english":"pressure of city life","chinese":"城市生活的壓力"},{"english":"dense neighbourhood","chinese":"人口密集的社區"},{"english":"afford private sports facilities","chinese":"負擔私人運動設施"},{"english":"nearby park","chinese":"附近的公園"},{"english":"play safely","chinese":"安全地玩耍"},{"english":"stay active","chinese":"保持活動量"},{"english":"without spending money","chinese":"不用花錢"},{"english":"be replaced by","chinese":"被……取代"},{"english":"apartments or offices","chinese":"住宅單位或辦公室"},{"english":"more stressful","chinese":"更令人有壓力"},{"english":"less humane","chinese":"較不人性化"},{"english":"strengthen communities","chinese":"加強社區聯繫"},{"english":"improve the quality of","chinese":"改善……的質素"},{"english":"urban development","chinese":"城市發展"},{"english":"shared spaces","chinese":"共享空間"},{"english":"different ages and backgrounds","chinese":"不同年齡和背景"},{"english":"meet naturally","chinese":"自然地相遇"},{"english":"rather than remaining isolated","chinese":"而不是繼續孤立"},{"english":"private homes or workplaces","chinese":"私人住宅或工作場所"},{"english":"this matters because","chinese":"這很重要，因為……"},{"english":"successful city","chinese":"成功的城市"},{"english":"a collection of houses and businesses","chinese":"一堆住宅和商業機構"},{"english":"living environment","chinese":"生活環境"},{"english":"feel connected and safe","chinese":"感到有連繫和安全"},{"english":"support the economy indirectly","chinese":"間接支持經濟"},{"english":"make cities more attractive to","chinese":"令城市對……更有吸引力"},{"english":"residents, workers, and visitors","chinese":"居民、工人和遊客"},{"english":"commercial buildings","chinese":"商業大廈"},{"english":"generate short-term profit","chinese":"產生短期利潤"},{"english":"risk becoming","chinese":"有可能變成"},{"english":"escape from","chinese":"逃離"},{"english":"rather than invest in","chinese":"而不是投資於……"},{"english":"business developments","chinese":"商業發展項目"},{"english":"population growth","chinese":"人口增長"},{"english":"economic development","chinese":"經濟發展"},{"english":"sacrificing green public spaces","chinese":"犧牲綠色公共空間"},{"english":"damage health","chinese":"損害健康"},{"english":"weaken communities","chinese":"削弱社區"},{"english":"overall liveability","chinese":"整體宜居程度"}]},"model-essay-46-ielts-direct-question":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-46-ielts-direct-question","essayKey":"direct-question:46","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-46-ielts-direct-question","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/direct-question/EdmundBd9Dir-Q46","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"In many less economically developed nations, the movement of workers from villages to urban centres has become increasingly common. This trend is largely driven by the search for better employment and improved living standards, but it can also create serious pressure on both cities and rural communities.","chinese":"在許多經濟發展程度較低的國家，工人從鄉村遷移到城市中心的現象已變得越來越普遍。 這種趨勢主要是由尋找更好的就業機會和改善生活水平所推動，但它也可能對城市和農村社區造成嚴重壓力。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"The main reason people leave rural areas is that cities appear to offer a wider range of economic opportunities. In many villages, work is often limited to farming or small-scale manual labour, which may be seasonal, poorly paid, and vulnerable to weather or market changes. By contrast, cities usually have factories, service industries, construction projects, and informal businesses that seem to promise more stable incomes. For example, a young worker from a farming family may move to a capital city because even a low-paid job in a shop or factory can provide more regular cash than agricultural work. In this sense, migration is not simply a matter of ambition; for many people, it is a practical attempt to escape poverty.","chinese":"人們離開農村地區的主要原因是，城市看起來能提供更廣泛的經濟機會。 在許多村莊，工作往往局限於農業或小規模體力勞動，而這些工作可能具有季節性、薪酬低，並且容易受到天氣或市場變化的影響。 相比之下，城市通常有工廠、服務業、建築項目和非正式商業活動，而這些似乎能提供更穩定的收入。 例如，一位來自農民家庭的年輕工人可能會搬到首都城市，因為即使是在商店或工廠中一份低薪工作，也能比農業工作提供更穩定的現金收入。 從這個意義上說，遷移並不單純是野心的問題；對許多人而言，這是一種逃離貧窮的實際嘗試。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"Another reason is that urban areas are often associated with better public services. Cities tend to have more schools, hospitals, transport links, and training centres, so workers may believe that moving there will improve not only their own lives but also their children’s future prospects. This hope can be especially powerful when rural communities lack basic infrastructure.","chinese":"另一個原因是，城市地區通常與更好的公共服務聯繫在一起。 城市往往有更多學校、醫院、交通網絡和培訓中心，因此工人可能相信，搬到城市不但能改善自己的生活，也能改善子女未來的前景。 當農村社區缺乏基本基礎設施時，這種希望可能尤其強烈。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 3","english":"However, large-scale rural-to-urban migration can cause several problems. The most immediate one is overcrowding. When too many people arrive faster than housing, roads, and public services can expand, cities may develop slums, traffic congestion, poor sanitation, and higher living costs. At the same time, rural areas may suffer from a shortage of young and productive workers. If mostly young adults leave, villages are left with an ageing population and weaker local economies.","chinese":"然而，大規模的農村到城市遷移可能造成幾個問題。 最直接的一個問題是過度擁擠。 當太多人湧入的速度快過住房、道路和公共服務的擴展速度時，城市可能會出現貧民窟、交通擠塞、衛生條件差和生活成本上升等問題。 與此同時，農村地區可能會面臨年輕且有生產力的勞動人口短缺。 如果離開的主要是年輕成年人，村莊便會剩下老齡化人口，並且本地經濟會變得更薄弱"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, workers in developing countries often move to cities because they want better jobs and services. Nevertheless, this movement can lead to overcrowded cities and declining rural communities if it is not managed carefully.","chinese":"總結來說，發展中國家的工人經常遷移到城市，是因為他們想要更好的工作和服務。 然而，如果這種人口流動沒有得到妥善管理，它可能會導致城市過度擁擠，以及農村社區衰落。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"less economically developed nations","chinese":"經濟較不發達的國家"},{"english":"the movement of workers","chinese":"工人的流動"},{"english":"from villages to urban centres","chinese":"從鄉村到城市中心"},{"english":"has become increasingly common","chinese":"變得越來越普遍"},{"english":"this trend","chinese":"這個趨勢"},{"english":"largely driven by","chinese":"很大程度上由……推動"},{"english":"the search for","chinese":"尋找"},{"english":"better employment","chinese":"更好的就業機會"},{"english":"improved living standards","chinese":"改善了的生活水平"},{"english":"create serious pressure on","chinese":"對……造成嚴重壓力"},{"english":"rural communities","chinese":"農村社區"},{"english":"the main reason","chinese":"主要原因"},{"english":"leave rural areas","chinese":"離開農村地區"},{"english":"appear to offer","chinese":"似乎提供"},{"english":"a wider range of","chinese":"更廣泛的……"},{"english":"economic opportunities","chinese":"經濟機會"},{"english":"be limited to","chinese":"局限於"},{"english":"farming","chinese":"農業"},{"english":"small-scale manual labour","chinese":"小規模體力勞動"},{"english":"seasonal","chinese":"季節性的"},{"english":"poorly paid","chinese":"薪酬低的"},{"english":"vulnerable to","chinese":"容易受……影響"},{"english":"weather or market changes","chinese":"天氣或市場變化"},{"english":"By contrast","chinese":"相比之下"},{"english":"service industries","chinese":"服務行業"},{"english":"construction projects","chinese":"建築項目"},{"english":"informal businesses","chinese":"非正式企業；非正規生意"},{"english":"seem to promise","chinese":"似乎承諾；似乎帶來"},{"english":"more stable incomes","chinese":"更穩定的收入"},{"english":"a young worker from","chinese":"來自……的年輕工人"},{"english":"farming family","chinese":"農民家庭"},{"english":"capital city","chinese":"首都城市"},{"english":"low-paid job","chinese":"低薪工作"},{"english":"provide more regular cash","chinese":"提供更穩定的現金收入"},{"english":"agricultural work","chinese":"農業工作"},{"english":"In this sense","chinese":"從這個意義上說"},{"english":"migration","chinese":"遷移；移居"},{"english":"not simply a matter of","chinese":"不只是……的問題"},{"english":"a practical attempt to","chinese":"實際嘗試去"},{"english":"escape poverty","chinese":"擺脫貧窮"},{"english":"Another reason is that","chinese":"另一個原因是"},{"english":"urban areas","chinese":"城市地區"},{"english":"be associated with","chinese":"與……有關"},{"english":"public services","chinese":"公共服務"},{"english":"tend to have","chinese":"往往有"},{"english":"transport links","chinese":"交通連接"},{"english":"training centres","chinese":"培訓中心"},{"english":"improve not only...but also...","chinese":"不但改善……，也改善……"},{"english":"future prospects","chinese":"未來前景"},{"english":"especially powerful","chinese":"特別強烈"},{"english":"lack basic infrastructure","chinese":"缺乏基本基礎設施"},{"english":"large-scale rural-to-urban migration","chinese":"大規模由農村到城市的遷移"},{"english":"cause several problems","chinese":"造成幾個問題"},{"english":"the most immediate one","chinese":"最即時的一個"},{"english":"overcrowding","chinese":"過度擠迫"},{"english":"arrive faster than","chinese":"到達速度快過"},{"english":"public services can expand","chinese":"公共服務能夠擴展"},{"english":"develop slums","chinese":"形成貧民窟"},{"english":"traffic congestion","chinese":"交通擠塞"},{"english":"poor sanitation","chinese":"惡劣衛生環境"},{"english":"higher living costs","chinese":"更高生活成本"},{"english":"At the same time","chinese":"與此同時"},{"english":"suffer from a shortage of","chinese":"面對……短缺"},{"english":"productive workers","chinese":"有生產力的工人"},{"english":"mostly young adults","chinese":"主要是年輕成年人"},{"english":"are left with","chinese":"只剩下；留下"},{"english":"an ageing population","chinese":"人口老化"},{"english":"weaker local economies","chinese":"較弱的本地經濟"},{"english":"developing countries","chinese":"發展中國家"},{"english":"move to cities","chinese":"搬到城市"},{"english":"better jobs and services","chinese":"更好的工作和服務"},{"english":"Nevertheless","chinese":"然而"},{"english":"lead to","chinese":"導致"},{"english":"overcrowded cities","chinese":"過度擠迫的城市"},{"english":"declining rural communities","chinese":"衰落中的農村社區"},{"english":"if it is not managed carefully","chinese":"如果沒有妥善管理"}]},"model-essay-46-ielts-opinion":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-46-ielts-opinion","essayKey":"opinion:46","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-46-ielts-opinion","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/opinions/EdmundBd9OP-Q46","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"Environmental damage is no longer a local inconvenience but a global crisis, affecting climate, biodiversity and public health. Some argue that wealthy countries should shoulder this burden because they have created much of the problem and have the resources to fix it. I understand this view, but I disagree that poorer nations should bear no responsibility at all.","chinese":"環境破壞已不再只是局部不便，而是一場影響氣候、生物多樣性和公共健康的全球危機 有人認為富裕國家應該承擔這項責任，因為它們造成了問題中的很大一部分，也擁有解決問題的資源 我理解這種觀點，但我不同意較貧困國家完全不需要承擔任何責任。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"There is a strong case for placing heavier responsibility on rich countries. Many of them built their prosperity through decades of industrial expansion, during which coal, oil and heavy manufacturing were treated as engines of growth. As a result, they enjoyed the benefits of development while leaving a large environmental footprint. Moreover, richer governments usually have the money, technology and expertise needed to invest in renewable energy, cleaner transport and climate-resilient infrastructure. For example, a wealthy country can subsidise electric buses or build flood defences without sacrificing basic services. In this sense, asking rich nations to lead is not charity; it is a fair return for the advantages they have already gained.","chinese":"把更重的責任放在富裕國家身上，是有很強道理的。 它們當中許多國家的繁榮，都是透過數十年的工業擴張建立起來的；在這段期間，煤炭、石油和重工業都被視為經濟增長的引擎。 結果是，它們享受了發展帶來的好處，同時也留下了巨大的環境足跡。 此外，較富裕的政府通常擁有投資可再生能源、更清潔交通和具氣候韌性基礎建設所需的資金、科技和專業知識。 例如，一個富裕國家可以資助電動巴士，或興建防洪設施，而不需要犧牲基本公共服務。 從這個意義上說，要求富裕國家帶頭行動並不是慈善，而是它們對已經獲得的利益作出合理回報。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"However, it does not follow that poorer countries can step aside. Environmental protection is not a spectator sport. If developing nations ignore pollution controls, destroy forests for short-term profit or allow cities to grow without proper waste systems, the damage will still be real and often irreversible. A poorer country may not be able to fund advanced technology, but it can still enforce basic rules, protect natural resources and choose development plans that do not poison its own land and water. To say that responsibility belongs only to rich nations also sends a dangerous message: that poverty gives governments permission to repeat the same mistakes that wealthier nations once made.","chinese":"然而，這並不代表較貧困國家就可以置身事外。 環境保護不是一項旁觀者運動。 如果發展中國家忽視污染管制、為短期利益而破壞森林，或容許城市在沒有完善廢物處理系統的情況下擴張，造成的破壞仍然是真實的，而且往往是不可逆轉的。 一個較貧困的國家未必有能力資助先進科技，但它仍然可以執行基本規則、保護自然資源，並選擇不會毒害自身土地和水源的發展計劃。 說責任只屬於富裕國家，也會傳遞一個危險訊息：貧窮似乎讓政府有權重複富裕國家曾經犯下的同樣錯誤。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, rich countries should lead because they have greater historical responsibility and stronger capacity. Nevertheless, I do not agree that poorer nations are free from duty. Global environmental problems require unequal contributions but shared responsibility; otherwise, the world is trying to clean one river while muddying another.","chinese":"總結來說，富裕國家應該帶頭，因為它們承擔更大的歷史責任，也擁有更強的能力。 然而，我不同意較貧困國家可以完全免除責任。 全球環境問題需要不平等的貢獻，但也需要共同承擔責任；否則，世界就像一邊清理一條河流，另一邊卻把另一條河弄髒。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"environmental damage","chinese":"環境破壞"},{"english":"no longer a local inconvenience","chinese":"不再是地方性不便"},{"english":"global crisis","chinese":"全球危機"},{"english":"affecting climate, biodiversity and public health","chinese":"影響氣候、生物多樣性和公共健康"},{"english":"wealthy countries","chinese":"富裕國家"},{"english":"shoulder this burden","chinese":"承擔這個重擔"},{"english":"created much of the problem","chinese":"造成了問題的大部分"},{"english":"have the resources to","chinese":"有資源去……"},{"english":"poorer nations","chinese":"較貧窮國家"},{"english":"bear no responsibility at all","chinese":"完全不用承擔責任"},{"english":"a strong case for","chinese":"有充分理由支持……"},{"english":"placing heavier responsibility on","chinese":"將更大責任放在……身上"},{"english":"built their prosperity through","chinese":"透過……建立繁榮"},{"english":"decades of industrial expansion","chinese":"數十年的工業擴張"},{"english":"heavy manufacturing","chinese":"重工業製造"},{"english":"engines of growth","chinese":"增長引擎"},{"english":"enjoyed the benefits of development","chinese":"享受發展帶來的好處"},{"english":"environmental footprint","chinese":"環境足跡；環境影響"},{"english":"technology and expertise","chinese":"技術和專業知識"},{"english":"renewable energy","chinese":"可再生能源"},{"english":"cleaner transport","chinese":"較清潔的交通"},{"english":"climate-resilient infrastructure","chinese":"具氣候韌性的基礎設施"},{"english":"subsidise electric buses","chinese":"資助電動巴士"},{"english":"build flood defences","chinese":"建設防洪設施"},{"english":"without sacrificing","chinese":"而不犧牲……"},{"english":"basic services","chinese":"基本服務"},{"english":"asking rich nations to lead","chinese":"要求富裕國家帶頭"},{"english":"a fair return for","chinese":"對……的公平回報"},{"english":"advantages they have already gained","chinese":"它們已經獲得的優勢"},{"english":"it does not follow that","chinese":"這並不代表……"},{"english":"step aside","chinese":"置身事外"},{"english":"environmental protection","chinese":"環境保護"},{"english":"spectator sport","chinese":"旁觀者遊戲"},{"english":"developing nations","chinese":"發展中國家"},{"english":"ignore pollution controls","chinese":"忽視污染管制"},{"english":"destroy forests for short-term profit","chinese":"為短期利益破壞森林"},{"english":"proper waste systems","chinese":"妥善的廢物處理系統"},{"english":"often irreversible","chinese":"往往不可逆轉"},{"english":"advanced technology","chinese":"先進技術"},{"english":"enforce basic rules","chinese":"執行基本規則"},{"english":"protect natural resources","chinese":"保護自然資源"},{"english":"development plans","chinese":"發展計劃"},{"english":"poison its own land and water","chinese":"污染自己的土地和水源"},{"english":"belongs only to","chinese":"只屬於……"},{"english":"sends a dangerous message","chinese":"傳達危險的信息"},{"english":"gives governments permission to","chinese":"給予政府許可去……"},{"english":"repeat the same mistakes","chinese":"重複同樣錯誤"},{"english":"historical responsibility","chinese":"歷史責任"},{"english":"stronger capacity","chinese":"更強的能力"},{"english":"free from duty","chinese":"免於責任"},{"english":"unequal contributions","chinese":"不均等的貢獻"},{"english":"shared responsibility","chinese":"共同責任"},{"english":"muddying another","chinese":"弄濁另一條河"}]},"model-essay-47-ielts-direct-question":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-47-ielts-direct-question","essayKey":"direct-question:47","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-47-ielts-direct-question","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/direct-question/EdmundBd9Dir-Q47","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"In contemporary workplaces, promotion is often treated as a visible sign that an employee’s effort has been recognised. People are strongly motivated by it because it usually brings better pay, higher status and greater control over their professional future. However, hard work is also shaped by less tangible factors, such as purpose, security and workplace culture.","chinese":"在當代職場中，晉升通常被視為員工努力得到認可的一個明顯標誌。 人們會受到晉升的強烈激勵，因為它通常帶來更高的薪酬、更高的地位，以及對自己職業未來更大的掌控權。 然而，努力工作也受到一些較不具體的因素影響，例如目標感、安全感和職場文化。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"The first reason promotion is so powerful is that it connects effort with material and social reward. A more senior position often means a higher salary, better benefits and a stronger sense of financial stability, so employees see it as a practical route to improving their quality of life. Beyond money, promotion also carries psychological value. Being promoted suggests that a person’s judgement, discipline and competence have been noticed by managers and colleagues. This public recognition can be deeply motivating because many workers want to feel that their sacrifices have led somewhere. For example, an employee who regularly works late to complete projects may view promotion not simply as a new title, but as proof that their commitment has not disappeared into the background.","chinese":"晉升之所以如此有力量，第一個原因是它把努力與物質和社會回報連結起來。 一個更高級的職位通常意味著更高的薪金、更好的福利，以及更強的經濟穩定感，因此員工會把它視為改善生活質素的一條實際途徑。 除了金錢之外，晉升也具有心理上的價值。 獲得晉升意味著一個人的判斷力、自律能力和工作能力已經被管理層和同事看見。 這種公開的認可能夠帶來很深的激勵作用，因為許多員工都希望感覺到自己的付出並沒有白費，而是走向了某個成果。 例如，一位經常加班完成項目的員工，可能不會單純把晉升看成一個新的職銜，而會把它看作自己投入和付出沒有被埋沒的證明。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"Nevertheless, promotion is not the only force that pushes people to work hard. One major factor is meaningful work. When employees believe their tasks benefit customers, students, patients or society in general, they are more likely to stay committed even without an immediate reward. Another important influence is the working environment. Supportive managers, fair rules and respectful colleagues can make people willing to raise their standards, whereas a toxic workplace can drain motivation even when promotion is possible. Personal ambition also plays a role: some people work hard because they want to master a skill, build confidence or prove to themselves that they can meet demanding goals.","chinese":"然而，晉升並不是推動人們努力工作的唯一力量。 其中一個重要因素是有意義的工作。 當員工相信自己的工作能夠令顧客、學生、病人或整個社會受益時，即使沒有即時回報，他們也更有可能保持投入。 另一個重要影響因素是工作環境。 支持員工的管理者、公平的規則和互相尊重的同事，能夠使人願意提高自己的標準；相反，即使存在晉升機會，有毒的職場環境也會耗盡人的動力。 個人抱負同樣扮演著一定角色：有些人努力工作，是因為他們想掌握一項技能、建立自信，或者向自己證明他們能夠達成具挑戰性的目標。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, promotion motivates people because it offers money, recognition and a clearer career path. Still, lasting effort also depends on purpose, fairness, personal growth and the emotional atmosphere of the workplace.","chinese":"總結來說，晉升能夠激勵人們，是因為它提供金錢、認可以及更清晰的職業道路。 不過，持久的努力也取決於目標感、公平、個人成長，以及職場中的情緒氛圍。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"contemporary workplaces","chinese":"現代職場"},{"english":"be treated as","chinese":"被視為"},{"english":"a visible sign that","chinese":"……的明顯標誌"},{"english":"effort has been recognised","chinese":"努力得到認可"},{"english":"strongly motivated by","chinese":"受到……強烈激勵"},{"english":"brings better pay","chinese":"帶來更高薪酬"},{"english":"higher status","chinese":"更高地位"},{"english":"greater control over","chinese":"對……有更大掌控"},{"english":"professional future","chinese":"職業前途"},{"english":"be shaped by","chinese":"受……塑造"},{"english":"less tangible factors","chinese":"較不具體的因素"},{"english":"workplace culture","chinese":"職場文化"},{"english":"the first reason","chinese":"第一個原因"},{"english":"connects effort with","chinese":"將努力與……連繫起來"},{"english":"material and social reward","chinese":"物質和社會回報"},{"english":"a more senior position","chinese":"更高級的職位"},{"english":"better benefits","chinese":"更好的福利"},{"english":"a stronger sense of","chinese":"更強的……感覺"},{"english":"financial stability","chinese":"財務穩定"},{"english":"a practical route to","chinese":"通往……的實際途徑"},{"english":"improving their quality of life","chinese":"改善生活質素"},{"english":"beyond money","chinese":"除了金錢之外"},{"english":"carries psychological value","chinese":"具有心理價值"},{"english":"being promoted","chinese":"獲得晉升"},{"english":"judgement, discipline and competence","chinese":"判斷力、紀律和能力"},{"english":"have been noticed by","chinese":"被……注意到"},{"english":"managers and colleagues","chinese":"經理和同事"},{"english":"public recognition","chinese":"公開認可"},{"english":"deeply motivating","chinese":"非常有激勵作用"},{"english":"feel that","chinese":"感覺到"},{"english":"their sacrifices have led somewhere","chinese":"他們的犧牲帶來了成果"},{"english":"regularly works late","chinese":"經常工作至很晚"},{"english":"complete projects","chinese":"完成項目"},{"english":"may view promotion as","chinese":"可能把晉升視為"},{"english":"not simply as","chinese":"不只是作為"},{"english":"a new title","chinese":"新職銜"},{"english":"proof that","chinese":"……的證明"},{"english":"commitment","chinese":"投入；承擔"},{"english":"disappear into the background","chinese":"被埋沒；消失在背景中"},{"english":"Nevertheless","chinese":"然而"},{"english":"the only force that","chinese":"唯一推動……的力量"},{"english":"pushes people to","chinese":"推動人們去"},{"english":"meaningful work","chinese":"有意義的工作"},{"english":"benefit customers","chinese":"令顧客受惠"},{"english":"society in general","chinese":"整個社會"},{"english":"more likely to","chinese":"更有可能"},{"english":"stay committed","chinese":"保持投入"},{"english":"without an immediate reward","chinese":"即使沒有即時回報"},{"english":"another important influence","chinese":"另一個重要影響因素"},{"english":"working environment","chinese":"工作環境"},{"english":"supportive managers","chinese":"支持員工的經理"},{"english":"fair rules","chinese":"公平規則"},{"english":"respectful colleagues","chinese":"尊重別人的同事"},{"english":"raise their standards","chinese":"提高自己的標準"},{"english":"a toxic workplace","chinese":"有毒的職場；惡劣職場"},{"english":"drain motivation","chinese":"消耗動力"},{"english":"even when promotion is possible","chinese":"即使有晉升機會"},{"english":"personal ambition","chinese":"個人抱負"},{"english":"plays a role","chinese":"發揮作用"},{"english":"master a skill","chinese":"掌握一項技能"},{"english":"build confidence","chinese":"建立信心"},{"english":"prove to themselves that","chinese":"向自己證明"},{"english":"meet demanding goals","chinese":"達成高要求目標"},{"english":"a clearer career path","chinese":"更清晰的事業發展路徑"},{"english":"lasting effort","chinese":"持久努力"},{"english":"depends on","chinese":"取決於"},{"english":"personal growth","chinese":"個人成長"},{"english":"emotional atmosphere","chinese":"情緒氛圍"}]},"model-essay-47-ielts-opinion":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-47-ielts-opinion","essayKey":"opinion:47","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-47-ielts-opinion","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/opinions/EdmundBd9OP-Q47","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"Environmental issues have become one of the defining challenges of the modern world. While local governments clearly have a role in protecting rivers, forests and public health, I completely agree that the most serious environmental problems must be addressed internationally because their causes and consequences do not stop at national borders.","chinese":"環境問題已成為現代世界其中一項最具代表性的挑戰。 雖然地方政府在保護河流、森林和公共健康方面明顯有其角色， 但我完全同意，最嚴重的環境問題必須在國際層面處理，因為它們的成因和後果都不會止於國界。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"The first reason is that many forms of environmental damage are borderless by nature. Climate change, air pollution, ocean waste and the loss of biodiversity are not problems that one country can solve behind its own walls. For example, a nation may spend heavily on clean energy, but its efforts will have limited impact if neighbouring countries continue to burn large amounts of fossil fuels. Similarly, plastic dumped into one part of the ocean can be carried by currents and damage marine life thousands of miles away. In this sense, treating global environmental problems as purely domestic matters is like trying to clean one room while smoke is still entering from the rest of the house. International cooperation is therefore essential because it allows countries to set common targets and move in the same direction.","chinese":"第一個原因是，許多形式的環境破壞本質上都是沒有國界的。 氣候變化、空氣污染、海洋垃圾和生物多樣性喪失，都不是一個國家能夠在自己的國界內單獨解決的問題。 例如，一個國家可能在清潔能源方面投入大量資金，但如果鄰近國家繼續燃燒大量化石燃料，它的努力所產生的影響仍然會十分有限。 同樣地，被傾倒到海洋某一處的塑膠垃圾，可能會被洋流帶走，並傷害數千英里以外的海洋生物。 從這個意義上說，把全球環境問題視為純粹的國內事務，就像只清潔一個房間，卻仍然讓煙霧從屋子的其他地方不斷飄進來。 因此，國際合作是必不可少的，因為它能讓各國設定共同目標，並朝著同一方向前進。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"Another important reason is that global action can distribute responsibility more fairly. Poorer countries are often the most exposed to floods, droughts and food insecurity, even though richer industrialised nations have historically produced far more pollution. If each country is left to act alone, wealthier states may protect themselves while weaker ones are left carrying an unfair burden. International agreements, by contrast, can encourage financial support, technology sharing and joint monitoring. This makes environmental protection not only more effective, but also more just.","chinese":"另一個重要原因是，全球行動能夠更公平地分配責任。 較貧困的國家往往最容易受到洪水、乾旱和糧食不安全的影響，儘管歷史上較富裕的工業化國家製造了更多污染。 如果每個國家都被迫單獨行動，較富裕的國家可能能夠保護自己，而較弱小的國家則會被迫承擔不公平的負擔。 相比之下，國際協議能夠促進資金支援、技術分享和共同監察。 這使環境保護不但更有效，也更公平。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, I fully agree that global environmental problems should be dealt with internationally rather than domestically. National policies are useful, but without coordinated international action, they are only small patches on a much larger wound. The planet is shared, and its protection must be shared as well.","chinese":"總結來說，我完全同意全球環境問題應該在國際層面處理，而不是只在國內層面處理。 國家政策是有用的，但如果沒有協調一致的國際行動，它們只是在一個更大傷口上的小小補丁。 地球是共同擁有的，因此保護地球的責任也必須共同承擔。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"environmental issues","chinese":"環境問題"},{"english":"defining challenges","chinese":"具代表性的重大挑戰"},{"english":"modern world","chinese":"現代世界"},{"english":"local governments","chinese":"地方政府"},{"english":"have a role in","chinese":"在……中有角色"},{"english":"protecting rivers, forests and public health","chinese":"保護河流、森林和公共健康"},{"english":"the most serious environmental problems","chinese":"最嚴重的環境問題"},{"english":"be addressed internationally","chinese":"在國際層面處理"},{"english":"causes and consequences","chinese":"成因和後果"},{"english":"stop at national borders","chinese":"止於國界"},{"english":"environmental damage","chinese":"環境破壞"},{"english":"borderless by nature","chinese":"本質上不受國界限制"},{"english":"climate change","chinese":"氣候變化"},{"english":"air pollution","chinese":"空氣污染"},{"english":"ocean waste","chinese":"海洋廢物"},{"english":"the loss of biodiversity","chinese":"生物多樣性喪失"},{"english":"behind its own walls","chinese":"在自己的圍牆內"},{"english":"spend heavily on","chinese":"大量投放資金於……"},{"english":"clean energy","chinese":"清潔能源"},{"english":"have limited impact","chinese":"影響有限"},{"english":"neighbouring countries","chinese":"鄰近國家"},{"english":"burn large amounts of fossil fuels","chinese":"燃燒大量化石燃料"},{"english":"similarly","chinese":"同樣地"},{"english":"be carried by currents","chinese":"被水流帶走"},{"english":"marine life","chinese":"海洋生物"},{"english":"thousands of miles away","chinese":"數千英里之外"},{"english":"in this sense","chinese":"從這個意義上說"},{"english":"purely domestic matters","chinese":"純粹國內事務"},{"english":"trying to clean one room","chinese":"嘗試只清潔一個房間"},{"english":"smoke is still entering","chinese":"煙仍然進入"},{"english":"the rest of the house","chinese":"屋內其餘部分"},{"english":"international cooperation","chinese":"國際合作"},{"english":"set common targets","chinese":"訂立共同目標"},{"english":"move in the same direction","chinese":"朝同一方向前進"},{"english":"global action","chinese":"全球行動"},{"english":"distribute responsibility more fairly","chinese":"更公平地分配責任"},{"english":"be exposed to","chinese":"面對……的風險最大；暴露於……"},{"english":"floods","chinese":"水災"},{"english":"droughts","chinese":"旱災"},{"english":"food insecurity","chinese":"糧食不安全"},{"english":"richer industrialised nations","chinese":"較富裕的工業化國家"},{"english":"historically produced","chinese":"在歷史上產生"},{"english":"far more pollution","chinese":"多得多的污染"},{"english":"be left to act alone","chinese":"被迫各自單獨行動"},{"english":"wealthier states","chinese":"較富裕國家"},{"english":"protect themselves","chinese":"保護自己"},{"english":"weaker ones","chinese":"較弱勢的國家；較弱勢者"},{"english":"be left carrying","chinese":"被留下承擔"},{"english":"unfair burden","chinese":"不公平負擔"},{"english":"international agreements","chinese":"國際協議"},{"english":"by contrast","chinese":"相比之下"},{"english":"financial support","chinese":"財政支援"},{"english":"technology sharing","chinese":"技術共享"},{"english":"joint monitoring","chinese":"共同監察"},{"english":"not only more effective","chinese":"不但更有效"},{"english":"more just","chinese":"更公正"},{"english":"be dealt with internationally","chinese":"在國際層面處理"},{"english":"rather than domestically","chinese":"而不是在國內層面"},{"english":"national policies","chinese":"國家政策"},{"english":"coordinated international action","chinese":"協調一致的國際行動"},{"english":"small patches on","chinese":"……上的小補丁"},{"english":"larger wound","chinese":"更大的傷口"},{"english":"the planet is shared","chinese":"地球是共享的"},{"english":"its protection must be shared","chinese":"對它的保護也必須共同承擔"}]},"model-essay-48-ielts-direct-question":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-48-ielts-direct-question","essayKey":"direct-question:48","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-48-ielts-direct-question","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/direct-question/EdmundBd9Dir-Q48","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"Choosing a career is no longer simply a matter of personal ambition; for many adults, it is directly connected to the welfare of the people who depend on them. I believe that money is undoubtedly an important factor when selecting a job, because a stable income gives a family protection and dignity. However, other considerations, especially health, suitability and long-term development, must also be taken seriously.","chinese":"選擇職業已不再只是個人抱負的問題；對許多成年人來說，這與依賴他們的人的福祉直接相關。 我認為，選擇工作時金錢無疑是一個重要因素，因為穩定的收入能給家庭帶來保障和尊嚴。 然而，其他考慮因素，尤其是健康、適合程度和長遠發展，也必須被認真看待。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"Income matters because family security usually begins with basic financial stability. A person who earns enough to pay for housing, food, education and medical care is less likely to expose their household to constant anxiety. This is particularly true for parents, whose career choices can affect not only their own comfort but also their children’s opportunities. For example, a father or mother may prefer a creative but poorly paid job, but if that income cannot cover rent or school expenses, the whole family may be forced to live under unnecessary pressure. In this sense, money is not greed; it is a safety net.","chinese":"收入很重要，因為家庭安全通常始於基本的財務穩定。 一個能賺取足夠收入去支付住房、食物、教育和醫療費用的人，較不容易讓家庭長期處於焦慮之中。 這對父母來說尤其如此，因為他們的職業選擇不但會影響自己的生活舒適度，也會影響子女的機會。 例如，一位父親或母親可能較喜歡一份有創意但薪酬低的工作，但如果那份收入無法支付租金或學費，整個家庭便可能被迫承受不必要的壓力。 從這個角度來看，金錢並不是貪婪；它是一張安全網。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"Nevertheless, a job should not be chosen by salary alone. One major factor is work-life balance, because a high-paying occupation can damage family life if it demands excessive hours or creates severe stress. A well-paid employee who is always exhausted, absent or emotionally unavailable may fail to provide the very security that money was supposed to create. Another important factor is whether the job suits the person’s abilities and offers room for growth. When people work in a field where they can improve their skills, gain experience and build a sustainable career, they are more likely to remain employable and confident in the long run.","chinese":"然而，一份工作不應該單憑薪金來選擇。 其中一個主要因素是工作與生活平衡，因為一份高薪工作如果要求過長工時或造成嚴重壓力，便可能損害家庭生活。 一位收入很高但總是疲憊、缺席或情感上無法投入的員工，可能反而無法提供金錢本應帶來的那種安全感。 另一個重要因素是，這份工作是否適合個人的能力，並能否提供成長空間。 當人們在一個能提升技能、累積經驗並建立可持續職業生涯的領域工作時，他們長遠而言更有可能保持就業能力和自信。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, I believe money is a vital factor when choosing a job, especially for those with family responsibilities. However, the best career choice is one that provides financial stability without sacrificing health, family relationships or future development.","chinese":"總結來說，我認為金錢是選擇工作時一個至關重要的因素，尤其對有家庭責任的人而言更是如此。 然而，最好的職業選擇，是既能提供財務穩定，又不犧牲健康、家庭關係或未來發展的選擇。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"choosing a career","chinese":"選擇事業"},{"english":"no longer simply a matter of","chinese":"不再只是……的問題"},{"english":"personal ambition","chinese":"個人抱負"},{"english":"directly connected to","chinese":"與……直接相關"},{"english":"the welfare of","chinese":"……的福祉"},{"english":"depend on them","chinese":"依靠他們"},{"english":"undoubtedly","chinese":"毫無疑問"},{"english":"an important factor","chinese":"重要因素"},{"english":"selecting a job","chinese":"選擇工作"},{"english":"a stable income","chinese":"穩定收入"},{"english":"protection and dignity","chinese":"保障和尊嚴"},{"english":"other considerations","chinese":"其他考慮因素"},{"english":"long-term development","chinese":"長遠發展"},{"english":"be taken seriously","chinese":"被認真看待"},{"english":"income matters","chinese":"收入很重要"},{"english":"family security","chinese":"家庭保障"},{"english":"begins with","chinese":"始於"},{"english":"basic financial stability","chinese":"基本財務穩定"},{"english":"earns enough to","chinese":"賺取足夠金錢去"},{"english":"pay for housing","chinese":"支付住屋開支"},{"english":"medical care","chinese":"醫療護理"},{"english":"less likely to","chinese":"較不可能"},{"english":"expose their household to","chinese":"使家庭面對"},{"english":"constant anxiety","chinese":"持續焦慮"},{"english":"particularly true for","chinese":"對……尤其如此"},{"english":"career choices","chinese":"事業選擇"},{"english":"affect not only...but also...","chinese":"不但影響……，也影響……"},{"english":"own comfort","chinese":"自己的安穩"},{"english":"children's opportunities","chinese":"子女的機會"},{"english":"may prefer","chinese":"可能較喜歡"},{"english":"a creative but poorly paid job","chinese":"有創意但薪酬低的工作"},{"english":"cover rent","chinese":"支付租金"},{"english":"school expenses","chinese":"學校開支"},{"english":"be forced to","chinese":"被迫"},{"english":"live under unnecessary pressure","chinese":"在不必要的壓力下生活"},{"english":"In this sense","chinese":"從這個意義上說"},{"english":"greed","chinese":"貪婪"},{"english":"a safety net","chinese":"安全網"},{"english":"Nevertheless","chinese":"然而"},{"english":"be chosen by salary alone","chinese":"只按薪酬選擇"},{"english":"one major factor","chinese":"一個主要因素"},{"english":"work-life balance","chinese":"工作與生活平衡"},{"english":"high-paying occupation","chinese":"高薪職業"},{"english":"damage family life","chinese":"損害家庭生活"},{"english":"demands excessive hours","chinese":"要求過長工時"},{"english":"creates severe stress","chinese":"造成嚴重壓力"},{"english":"well-paid employee","chinese":"高薪員工"},{"english":"always exhausted","chinese":"經常精疲力竭"},{"english":"emotionally unavailable","chinese":"情感上無法投入的"},{"english":"fail to provide","chinese":"未能提供"},{"english":"the very security that","chinese":"正正是……的保障"},{"english":"be supposed to","chinese":"本應"},{"english":"suits the person's abilities","chinese":"適合那個人的能力"},{"english":"offers room for growth","chinese":"提供成長空間"},{"english":"work in a field where","chinese":"在一個……的領域工作"},{"english":"improve their skills","chinese":"提升技能"},{"english":"gain experience","chinese":"累積經驗"},{"english":"build a sustainable career","chinese":"建立可持續的事業"},{"english":"more likely to remain employable","chinese":"更有可能保持就業能力"},{"english":"confident in the long run","chinese":"長遠而言更有信心"},{"english":"a vital factor","chinese":"關鍵因素"},{"english":"family responsibilities","chinese":"家庭責任"},{"english":"the best career choice","chinese":"最佳事業選擇"},{"english":"provides financial stability","chinese":"提供財務穩定"},{"english":"without sacrificing","chinese":"不犧牲"},{"english":"family relationships","chinese":"家庭關係"},{"english":"future development","chinese":"未來發展"}]},"model-essay-48-ielts-opinion":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-48-ielts-opinion","essayKey":"opinion:48","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-48-ielts-opinion","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/opinions/EdmundBd9OP-Q48","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"Air pollution has become a serious concern in many parts of the world, and aviation is often criticised because aircraft burn large amounts of fuel. However, I completely disagree with the view that restricting air travel is the only way to prevent this problem. Such a policy focuses too narrowly on one source of pollution, while more effective and balanced solutions are available.","chinese":"空氣污染已成為世界許多地方的嚴重問題，而航空業經常受到批評，因為飛機會燃燒大量燃料。 然而，我完全不同意限制航空旅行是防止這個問題的唯一方法這一觀點。 這樣的政策過於狹窄地集中在其中一個污染來源上，而其實還有更有效和更平衡的解決方案。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"The first reason is that air pollution is produced by many everyday activities, not by aviation alone. Cars, lorries, factories, power stations and construction sites can all release harmful gases or particles into the air. If governments simply limit flights while allowing old vehicles to run, industrial plants to operate with weak standards and cities to depend on dirty energy, the air will remain polluted. For example, a city with fewer international flights may still suffer from thick smog if millions of commuters drive petrol cars every day. Blaming air travel alone is like cleaning one window while leaving the rest of the house covered in dust.","chinese":"第一個原因是，空氣污染是由許多日常活動造成的，而不只是由航空業造成。 汽車、貨車、工廠、發電站和建築工地都可能向空氣中釋放有害氣體或微粒。 如果政府只是限制航班，卻容許舊車繼續行駛、工業廠房以寬鬆標準運作，以及城市繼續依賴污染性能源，空氣仍然會受到污染。 例如，一個國際航班較少的城市，如果每天仍有數百萬通勤者駕駛汽油車，仍然可能受到濃厚煙霧的困擾。 只責怪航空旅行，就像只清潔一扇窗，卻讓房子的其他部分仍然滿是灰塵。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"A better approach is to reduce pollution across the whole transport and energy system. Governments can invest in reliable public transport, encourage electric vehicles, tighten emissions standards for factories and shift electricity production towards cleaner sources. These measures would affect people’s daily habits and industrial behaviour, so their impact would be far broader than simply discouraging people from flying. At the same time, the aviation industry itself can be pushed to improve fuel efficiency and adopt cleaner technology, instead of being treated as a problem that can only be solved by restriction. This is more practical because air travel also supports business, tourism and family connections across long distances.","chinese":"更好的做法是在整個交通和能源系統中減少污染。 政府可以投資可靠的公共交通、鼓勵使用電動車、收緊工廠的排放標準，並將發電轉向更清潔的來源。 這些措施會影響人們的日常習慣和工業行為，因此它們的影響會比單純勸阻人們乘飛機更加廣泛。 同時，航空業本身也可以被推動去提高燃油效率並採用更清潔的技術，而不是被視為一個只能透過限制來解決的問題。 這樣做更實際，因為航空旅行也支撐著商業、旅遊，以及跨越長距離的家庭聯繫。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, restricting air travel may play a small role in reducing emissions, but it is certainly not the only way to tackle air pollution. I strongly believe that cleaner cities require wider reforms in transport, industry and energy, rather than a narrow focus on flights alone.","chinese":"總結來說，限制航空旅行或許在減少排放方面能發揮一小部分作用，但它絕對不是處理空氣污染的唯一方法。 我強烈認為，更清潔的城市需要在交通、工業和能源方面進行更廣泛的改革，而不是只狹隘地集中於航班本身。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"air pollution","chinese":"空氣污染"},{"english":"serious concern","chinese":"嚴重憂慮"},{"english":"in many parts of the world","chinese":"在世界很多地方"},{"english":"aviation","chinese":"航空業"},{"english":"be often criticised","chinese":"經常受到批評"},{"english":"burn large amounts of fuel","chinese":"燃燒大量燃料"},{"english":"restrict air travel","chinese":"限制航空旅遊"},{"english":"the only way to","chinese":"……的唯一方法"},{"english":"prevent this problem","chinese":"防止這個問題"},{"english":"such a policy","chinese":"這樣的政策"},{"english":"focus too narrowly on","chinese":"過於狹窄地集中於……"},{"english":"source of pollution","chinese":"污染來源"},{"english":"balanced solutions","chinese":"平衡的解決方法"},{"english":"be available","chinese":"可供使用；存在"},{"english":"be produced by","chinese":"由……產生"},{"english":"everyday activities","chinese":"日常活動"},{"english":"aviation alone","chinese":"單靠航空業"},{"english":"cars, lorries, factories, power stations and construction sites","chinese":"汽車、貨車、工廠、發電廠和建築地盤"},{"english":"release harmful gases","chinese":"釋放有害氣體"},{"english":"particles","chinese":"微粒"},{"english":"into the air","chinese":"進入空氣中"},{"english":"simply limit flights","chinese":"只是限制航班"},{"english":"allowing old vehicles to run","chinese":"允許舊車繼續行駛"},{"english":"industrial plants","chinese":"工業廠房"},{"english":"operate with weak standards","chinese":"在低標準下運作"},{"english":"depend on dirty energy","chinese":"依賴污染能源"},{"english":"remain polluted","chinese":"仍然受污染"},{"english":"fewer international flights","chinese":"較少國際航班"},{"english":"suffer from","chinese":"受……困擾"},{"english":"thick smog","chinese":"濃厚煙霧"},{"english":"millions of commuters","chinese":"數以百萬計的通勤人士"},{"english":"petrol cars","chinese":"汽油車"},{"english":"blaming air travel alone","chinese":"單單責怪航空旅遊"},{"english":"cleaning one window","chinese":"清潔一扇窗"},{"english":"the rest of the house","chinese":"屋內其餘部分"},{"english":"covered in dust","chinese":"滿佈灰塵"},{"english":"a better approach","chinese":"更好的方法"},{"english":"reduce pollution across","chinese":"在整個……中減少污染"},{"english":"whole transport and energy system","chinese":"整個交通和能源系統"},{"english":"reliable public transport","chinese":"可靠的公共交通"},{"english":"encourage electric vehicles","chinese":"鼓勵使用電動車"},{"english":"tighten emissions standards","chinese":"收緊排放標準"},{"english":"emissions standards","chinese":"排放標準"},{"english":"shift electricity production towards","chinese":"將發電轉向……"},{"english":"cleaner sources","chinese":"較清潔的來源"},{"english":"affect people's daily habits","chinese":"影響人們的日常習慣"},{"english":"industrial behaviour","chinese":"工業行為"},{"english":"their impact","chinese":"它們的影響"},{"english":"far broader than","chinese":"比……廣泛得多"},{"english":"simply discouraging people from","chinese":"只是阻止人們……"},{"english":"at the same time","chinese":"同時"},{"english":"aviation industry","chinese":"航空業"},{"english":"be pushed to","chinese":"被推動去……"},{"english":"improve fuel efficiency","chinese":"提高燃油效率"},{"english":"adopt cleaner technology","chinese":"採用較清潔的技術"},{"english":"instead of being treated as","chinese":"而不是被視為……"},{"english":"be solved by restriction","chinese":"透過限制來解決"},{"english":"more practical","chinese":"更實際"},{"english":"supports business","chinese":"支持商業"},{"english":"tourism","chinese":"旅遊業"},{"english":"family connections","chinese":"家庭聯繫"},{"english":"across long distances","chinese":"跨越長距離"},{"english":"play a small role in","chinese":"在……中發揮小作用"},{"english":"reducing emissions","chinese":"減少排放"},{"english":"certainly not","chinese":"肯定不是"},{"english":"tackle air pollution","chinese":"處理空氣污染"},{"english":"cleaner cities","chinese":"更清潔的城市"},{"english":"wider reforms","chinese":"更廣泛的改革"},{"english":"transport, industry and energy","chinese":"交通、工業和能源"},{"english":"narrow focus on","chinese":"對……的狹窄關注"},{"english":"flights alone","chinese":"單單航班"}]},"model-essay-49-ielts-opinion":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-49-ielts-opinion","essayKey":"opinion:49","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-49-ielts-opinion","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/opinions/EdmundBd9OP-Q49","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"Television has become a familiar part of many children's daily lives, and it is sometimes seen as an easy way to support learning. However, I completely disagree that children should be encouraged to watch it regularly either at home or at school. Even when a programme is well made, regular viewing is a poor substitute for active, guided education.","chinese":"電視已經成為許多孩子日常生活中熟悉的一部分，而且有時被視為一種支持學習的簡單方式。 然而，我完全不同意孩子應該被鼓勵在家中或學校定期觀看電視。 即使一個節目製作精良，定期觀看電視也不能很好地取代主動、有引導性的教育。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"The main problem is that television usually turns children into passive receivers rather than active learners. When a child reads, discusses, writes, experiments, or asks questions, the mind has to work: ideas are tested, mistakes are corrected, and understanding becomes deeper. Television, by contrast, often delivers information in a polished stream, leaving little room for reflection or interaction. For example, a child watching a science programme about plants may remember a few colourful images, but a child who grows a plant, records its changes, and explains the process to a teacher is far more likely to understand the concept properly. Regular television viewing therefore risks creating the illusion of learning, while real intellectual habits remain underdeveloped.","chinese":"主要問題是，電視通常會把孩子變成被動接收者，而不是主動學習者。 當孩子閱讀、討論、寫作、實驗或提問時，大腦必須運作：想法會被檢驗，錯誤會被糾正，理解也會變得更深入。 相比下，電視往往以一種經過包裝的連續形式傳遞資訊，幾乎沒有留下反思或互動空間 例如，一個觀看植物科學節目的孩子可能會記住幾個色彩鮮明的畫面，但一個親自種植植物、記錄其變化，並向老師解釋過程的孩子，更有可能真正理解這個概念。 因此，定期觀看電視有可能製造出一種正在學習的錯覺，而真正的思考習慣卻仍然未能充分發展。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"Another reason is that encouraging television at both home and school would weaken children’s concentration and social development. Young learners need routines that train patience, attention, and communication. If screens become a normal learning tool too often, children may find slower but more demanding tasks, such as reading a chapter, solving a problem, or listening to classmates, less appealing. At home, this could also reduce time for family conversation, outdoor play, and independent study. At school, it may turn valuable classroom time into a one-way broadcast, where students watch rather than participate. Education should not be a theatre seat; it should be a workshop.","chinese":"另一個原因是，在家庭和學校都鼓勵孩子看電視，會削弱他們的專注力和社交發展。 年幼的學習者需要一些能訓練耐性、專注力和溝通能力的日常安排。 如果螢幕過於頻繁地成為常規學習工具，孩子可能會覺得一些較慢但要求更高的任務，例如閱讀一個章節、解決一道問題，或聆聽同學發言，變得不那麼吸引。 在家中，這也可能減少孩子用於家庭對話、戶外玩耍和自主學習的時間。 在學校，它可能會把寶貴的課堂時間變成單向播放，讓學生只是觀看，而不是參與。 教育不應該是一個劇院座位；它應該是一個工作坊。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, I completely disagree with the idea that children should be encouraged to watch television regularly. As a regular habit at home and in school, it encourages passivity, weakens attention, and takes children away from richer forms of learning.","chinese":"總結來說，我完全不同意孩子應該被鼓勵定期觀看電視這個觀點。 作為家庭和學校中的一種常規習慣，它會鼓勵被動、削弱專注力，並使孩子遠離更豐富的學習形式。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"familiar part of","chinese":"……中常見的一部分"},{"english":"children's daily lives","chinese":"兒童日常生活"},{"english":"be seen as","chinese":"被視為"},{"english":"support learning","chinese":"支持學習"},{"english":"be encouraged to","chinese":"被鼓勵去……"},{"english":"watch it regularly","chinese":"定期觀看它"},{"english":"either at home or at school","chinese":"無論在家中還是在學校"},{"english":"well made","chinese":"製作精良"},{"english":"regular viewing","chinese":"定期觀看"},{"english":"a poor substitute for","chinese":"……的差劣替代品"},{"english":"active, guided education","chinese":"主動而有引導的教育"},{"english":"the main problem","chinese":"主要問題"},{"english":"turn children into","chinese":"將孩子變成……"},{"english":"passive receivers","chinese":"被動接收者"},{"english":"active learners","chinese":"主動學習者"},{"english":"asks questions","chinese":"提問"},{"english":"the mind has to work","chinese":"大腦需要運作"},{"english":"ideas are tested","chinese":"想法受到檢驗"},{"english":"mistakes are corrected","chinese":"錯誤得到糾正"},{"english":"understanding becomes deeper","chinese":"理解變得更深入"},{"english":"by contrast","chinese":"相比之下"},{"english":"delivers information","chinese":"傳遞資料"},{"english":"polished stream","chinese":"經修飾而流暢的資訊流"},{"english":"leave little room for","chinese":"幾乎沒有空間給……"},{"english":"reflection or interaction","chinese":"反思或互動"},{"english":"science programme","chinese":"科學節目"},{"english":"colourful images","chinese":"色彩鮮明的畫面"},{"english":"grows a plant","chinese":"種植植物"},{"english":"records its changes","chinese":"記錄它的變化"},{"english":"explains the process to","chinese":"向……解釋過程"},{"english":"far more likely to","chinese":"更加有可能"},{"english":"understand the concept properly","chinese":"正確理解概念"},{"english":"regular television viewing","chinese":"定期看電視"},{"english":"risks creating","chinese":"有可能造成"},{"english":"the illusion of learning","chinese":"學習的假象"},{"english":"intellectual habits","chinese":"思維習慣"},{"english":"remain underdeveloped","chinese":"仍未充分發展"},{"english":"another reason","chinese":"另一個原因"},{"english":"weaken children's concentration","chinese":"削弱兒童的專注力"},{"english":"social development","chinese":"社交發展"},{"english":"young learners","chinese":"年幼學習者"},{"english":"train patience","chinese":"訓練耐性"},{"english":"attention, and communication","chinese":"專注力和溝通能力"},{"english":"become a normal learning tool","chinese":"成為常規學習工具"},{"english":"too often","chinese":"過於頻密"},{"english":"slower but more demanding tasks","chinese":"較慢但要求更高的任務"},{"english":"reading a chapter","chinese":"閱讀一章"},{"english":"solving a problem","chinese":"解決問題"},{"english":"listening to classmates","chinese":"聆聽同學"},{"english":"less appealing","chinese":"較不吸引"},{"english":"reduce time for","chinese":"減少……的時間"},{"english":"family conversation","chinese":"家庭對話"},{"english":"outdoor play","chinese":"戶外玩耍"},{"english":"independent study","chinese":"自主學習"},{"english":"valuable classroom time","chinese":"寶貴課堂時間"},{"english":"one-way broadcast","chinese":"單向廣播"},{"english":"watch rather than participate","chinese":"觀看而不是參與"},{"english":"theatre seat","chinese":"劇院座位"},{"english":"workshop","chinese":"工作坊"},{"english":"regular habit","chinese":"恆常習慣"},{"english":"encourages passivity","chinese":"助長被動"},{"english":"weakens attention","chinese":"削弱注意力"},{"english":"takes children away from","chinese":"使孩子遠離……"},{"english":"richer forms of learning","chinese":"更豐富的學習形式"}]},"model-essay-50-ielts-opinion":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-50-ielts-opinion","essayKey":"opinion:50","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-50-ielts-opinion","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/opinions/EdmundBd9OP-Q50","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"Children today are often given far more independence than young people in the past, whether in choosing their hobbies, expressing their opinions, or making personal decisions. I believe this is a positive development because greater freedom helps children become more confident and better prepared for adult life.","chinese":"如今的孩子往往比過去的年輕人獲得更多獨立性，無論是在選擇興趣、表達意見，還是作出個人決定方面。 我認為這是一種正面的發展，因為更大的自由能幫助孩子變得更有自信，並為成年生活作好更充分的準備。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"The main benefit is that freedom allows children to develop independence from an earlier age. In previous generations, many children were expected to obey adults without question, which could make them disciplined but not necessarily thoughtful. By contrast, when children are allowed to make age-appropriate choices, they learn to think, compare options, and accept the consequences of their decisions. For example, a child who is trusted to manage his own study schedule may sometimes make mistakes, but those mistakes can teach him responsibility more effectively than constant parental control. In this sense, freedom acts as a training ground for real life, where people must make decisions without always being told what to do.","chinese":"主要好處是，自由能讓孩子從較早的年齡開始培養獨立性。 在過去幾代人中，許多孩子被期望毫無疑問地服從成年人，這可能使他們變得守紀律，但未必能使他們變得有思考能力。 相比之下，當孩子被允許作出符合年齡的選擇時，他們會學會思考、比較不同選項，並承擔自己決定所帶來的後果。 例如，一個被信任能夠管理自己學習時間表的孩子，有時可能會犯錯，但這些錯誤能比父母持續控制更有效地教會他責任感。 從這個意義上說，自由就像現實生活的訓練場，因為人在現實生活中必須作出決定，而不能總是由別人告訴他們該怎麼做。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"Another reason this trend is positive is that it encourages stronger self-expression and emotional growth. Children who are allowed to speak openly are more likely to understand their own feelings, communicate their needs, and build healthier relationships with others. If young people are always silenced or overprotected, they may grow up afraid of disagreement or unable to defend themselves. For instance, when parents listen to a child’s views about school, friendships, or future goals, the child feels respected rather than controlled. This does not mean children should be allowed to do whatever they want, but reasonable freedom can help them develop confidence, judgment, and a stronger sense of identity.","chinese":"這種趨勢之所以正面，另一個原因是它能鼓勵更強的自我表達和情感成長。 被允許坦誠表達的孩子，更有可能理解自己的感受、表達自己的需要，並與他人建立更健康的關係。 如果年輕人總是被壓制或過度保護，他們長大後可能會害怕分歧，或者無法為自己辯護 例如，當父母聆聽孩子對學校、友誼或未來目標的看法時，孩子會感到自己受到尊重，而不是被控制。 這並不意味著孩子應該被允許做任何他們想做的事，但合理的自由可以幫助他們培養自信、判斷力，以及更強的身份認同感。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, giving children more freedom is a positive change. Although guidance is still necessary, independence and self-expression are essential for helping young people become responsible, confident, and emotionally mature adults.","chinese":"總結來說，給予孩子更多自由是一種正面的改變。 雖然引導仍然是必要的，但獨立性和自我表達對幫助年輕人成為負責任、有自信並且情感成熟的成年人至關重要。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"far more independence","chinese":"多得多的獨立性"},{"english":"in the past","chinese":"在過去"},{"english":"choosing their hobbies","chinese":"選擇自己的興趣"},{"english":"expressing their opinions","chinese":"表達意見"},{"english":"making personal decisions","chinese":"作出個人決定"},{"english":"a positive development","chinese":"正面發展"},{"english":"greater freedom","chinese":"更大的自由"},{"english":"become more confident","chinese":"變得更有自信"},{"english":"better prepared for","chinese":"為……作好更充分準備"},{"english":"adult life","chinese":"成年生活"},{"english":"the main benefit","chinese":"主要好處"},{"english":"develop independence","chinese":"培養獨立性"},{"english":"from an earlier age","chinese":"從較早年紀開始"},{"english":"previous generations","chinese":"以往幾代人"},{"english":"be expected to","chinese":"被期望去……"},{"english":"obey adults without question","chinese":"毫不質疑地服從成年人"},{"english":"disciplined but not necessarily thoughtful","chinese":"有紀律但不一定有思考能力"},{"english":"by contrast","chinese":"相比之下"},{"english":"be allowed to","chinese":"被允許去……"},{"english":"age-appropriate choices","chinese":"適合年齡的選擇"},{"english":"compare options","chinese":"比較選項"},{"english":"accept the consequences of","chinese":"承擔……的後果"},{"english":"manage his own study schedule","chinese":"管理自己的學習時間表"},{"english":"make mistakes","chinese":"犯錯"},{"english":"teach him responsibility","chinese":"教會他責任感"},{"english":"more effectively than","chinese":"比……更有效地"},{"english":"constant parental control","chinese":"持續父母管束"},{"english":"in this sense","chinese":"從這個意義上說"},{"english":"acts as","chinese":"充當；起……作用"},{"english":"training ground","chinese":"訓練場"},{"english":"real life","chinese":"現實生活"},{"english":"make decisions","chinese":"作出決定"},{"english":"without always being told what to do","chinese":"不用總是被告知要做甚麼"},{"english":"another reason","chinese":"另一個原因"},{"english":"encourages stronger self-expression","chinese":"鼓勵更強的自我表達"},{"english":"emotional growth","chinese":"情感成長"},{"english":"speak openly","chinese":"坦誠表達"},{"english":"be more likely to","chinese":"更有可能"},{"english":"understand their own feelings","chinese":"理解自己的感受"},{"english":"communicate their needs","chinese":"表達自己的需要"},{"english":"build healthier relationships with","chinese":"與……建立更健康的關係"},{"english":"be always silenced","chinese":"總是被要求沉默"},{"english":"overprotected","chinese":"被過度保護"},{"english":"grow up afraid of","chinese":"長大後害怕……"},{"english":"disagreement","chinese":"意見分歧"},{"english":"unable to defend themselves","chinese":"無法為自己辯護；無法保護自己"},{"english":"listen to a child's views","chinese":"聆聽孩子的看法"},{"english":"future goals","chinese":"未來目標"},{"english":"feel respected rather than controlled","chinese":"感到被尊重，而不是被控制"},{"english":"do whatever they want","chinese":"做任何想做的事"},{"english":"reasonable freedom","chinese":"合理自由"},{"english":"develop confidence","chinese":"培養自信"},{"english":"judgment","chinese":"判斷力"},{"english":"a stronger sense of identity","chinese":"更強的身份認同"},{"english":"giving children more freedom","chinese":"給予孩子更多自由"},{"english":"positive change","chinese":"正面轉變"},{"english":"guidance is still necessary","chinese":"引導仍然必要"},{"english":"independence and self-expression","chinese":"獨立性和自我表達"},{"english":"responsible, confident, and emotionally mature adults","chinese":"負責任、有自信和情緒成熟的成年人"}]},"model-essay-51-ielts-opinion":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-51-ielts-opinion","essayKey":"opinion:51","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-51-ielts-opinion","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/opinions/EdmundBd9OP-Q51","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"Family and school both shape a person’s future, but I completely agree that the values learned from parents and family have a greater influence on long-term success than academic skills or classroom knowledge. This is because family values form the inner habits that determine how people use whatever they later learn.","chinese":"家庭和學校都會塑造一個人的未來，但我完全同意，從父母和家庭中學到的價值觀，比在學校學到的任何技能或知識，對長遠成功有更大的影響。 這是因為家庭價值觀會形成一個人內在的習慣，而這些習慣會決定他們日後如何運用所學到的一切。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"First, values such as discipline, responsibility, honesty, and perseverance are the foundation on which achievement is built. Schools can teach mathematics, science, or writing, but these abilities are useful only when a person has the character to apply them consistently. A student who grows up in a family where effort is valued is more likely to revise regularly, accept corrections, and keep going after poor results. By contrast, someone who has knowledge but lacks self-control may waste opportunities, give up too quickly, or look for shortcuts. In this sense, family values are like the roots of a tree: invisible at first, but essential when the weather turns rough.","chinese":"首先，紀律、責任感、誠實和毅力等價值觀，是成就得以建立的基礎。 學校可以教授數學、科學或寫作，但只有當一個人具備能夠持續運用這些能力的品格時，這些能力才真正有用。 一個在重視努力的家庭中長大的學生，更有可能定期溫習、接受改正，並在成績不理想後繼續堅持下去。 相比之下，一個有知識但缺乏自制力的人，可能會浪費機會、太快放棄，或者尋找捷徑 從這個角度來看，家庭價值觀就像一棵樹的根：起初看不見，但風雨來臨時卻至關重要"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"Another reason is that success in adult life depends heavily on the way people deal with others. Qualities such as respect, empathy, patience, and reliability are often first learned at home through daily interactions with parents, siblings, and relatives. These qualities later affect friendships, teamwork, leadership, and professional trust. For example, two graduates may leave university with similar qualifications, but the one who listens carefully, treats colleagues fairly, and keeps promises is far more likely to earn respect and responsibility at work. Technical knowledge may open the door, but character often decides whether a person can stay in the room.","chinese":"另一個原因是，成年後的成功在很大程度上取決於人們如何與他人相處。 尊重、同理心、耐性和可靠性等品質，往往最初都是透過在家中與父母、兄弟姊妹和親戚的日常互動中學會的。 這些品質日後會影響友誼、團隊合作、領導能力和職場信任。 例如，兩名畢業生離開大學時可能擁有相似的資歷，但那個懂得仔細聆聽、公平對待同事並信守承諾的人，更有可能在工作中贏得尊重和責任。 專業知識也許能打開機會之門，但品格往往決定一個人能否真正留在其中。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, I fully agree that family values have a stronger influence on future success than school-based skills or knowledge. Education is undeniably useful, but without the right values, it becomes a tool without direction. The habits and principles formed at home guide people through study, work, and relationships, making them the deeper source of lasting achievement.","chinese":"總結來說，我完全同意，家庭價值觀比學校所教授的技能或知識，對未來成功有更強的影響。 教育無疑是有用的，但如果沒有正確的價值觀，它就會變成一件沒有方向的工具。 在家中形成的習慣和原則，會引導人們面對學習、工作和人際關係，使它們成為持久成就更深層的來源。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"shape a person's future","chinese":"塑造一個人的未來"},{"english":"values learned from","chinese":"從……學到的價值觀"},{"english":"have a greater influence on","chinese":"對……有更大影響"},{"english":"long-term success","chinese":"長遠成功"},{"english":"academic skills","chinese":"學術技能"},{"english":"classroom knowledge","chinese":"課堂知識"},{"english":"form the inner habits","chinese":"形成內在習慣"},{"english":"determine how","chinese":"決定如何……"},{"english":"whatever they later learn","chinese":"他們日後學到的一切"},{"english":"discipline, responsibility, honesty, and perseverance","chinese":"紀律、責任感、誠實和毅力"},{"english":"the foundation on which","chinese":"……的基礎"},{"english":"achievement is built","chinese":"成就得以建立"},{"english":"useful only when","chinese":"只有在……時才有用"},{"english":"apply them consistently","chinese":"持續運用它們"},{"english":"grows up in","chinese":"在……中成長"},{"english":"effort is valued","chinese":"努力受到重視"},{"english":"be more likely to","chinese":"更有可能"},{"english":"revise regularly","chinese":"定期溫習"},{"english":"accept corrections","chinese":"接受糾正"},{"english":"keep going after","chinese":"在……之後繼續努力"},{"english":"poor results","chinese":"差的成績"},{"english":"by contrast","chinese":"相比之下"},{"english":"lacks self-control","chinese":"缺乏自制力"},{"english":"waste opportunities","chinese":"浪費機會"},{"english":"give up too quickly","chinese":"太快放棄"},{"english":"look for shortcuts","chinese":"尋找捷徑"},{"english":"in this sense","chinese":"從這個意義上說"},{"english":"roots of a tree","chinese":"樹根"},{"english":"invisible at first","chinese":"起初看不見"},{"english":"when the weather turns rough","chinese":"當環境變得艱難時"},{"english":"adult life","chinese":"成年生活"},{"english":"depends heavily on","chinese":"很大程度上取決於"},{"english":"deal with others","chinese":"與他人相處"},{"english":"respect, empathy, patience, and reliability","chinese":"尊重、同理心、耐性和可靠"},{"english":"first learned at home","chinese":"首先在家中學到"},{"english":"daily interactions","chinese":"日常互動"},{"english":"siblings and relatives","chinese":"兄弟姊妹和親戚"},{"english":"later affect","chinese":"日後影響"},{"english":"friendships, teamwork, leadership, and professional trust","chinese":"友誼、團隊合作、領導力和專業信任"},{"english":"similar qualifications","chinese":"相似資歷"},{"english":"listens carefully","chinese":"細心聆聽"},{"english":"treats colleagues fairly","chinese":"公平對待同事"},{"english":"keeps promises","chinese":"遵守承諾"},{"english":"far more likely to","chinese":"更加有可能"},{"english":"earn respect and responsibility","chinese":"贏得尊重和責任"},{"english":"technical knowledge","chinese":"技術知識"},{"english":"open the door","chinese":"打開機會之門"},{"english":"character often decides whether","chinese":"品格往往決定是否……"},{"english":"stay in the room","chinese":"留在那個位置；持續站穩"},{"english":"stronger influence on","chinese":"對……有更強影響"},{"english":"school-based skills","chinese":"學校所教的技能"},{"english":"undeniably useful","chinese":"無可否認地有用"},{"english":"a tool without direction","chinese":"沒有方向的工具"},{"english":"habits and principles","chinese":"習慣和原則"},{"english":"formed at home","chinese":"在家中形成"},{"english":"guide people through","chinese":"引導人們經歷……"},{"english":"study, work, and relationships","chinese":"學習、工作和人際關係"},{"english":"deeper source of","chinese":"……更深層的來源"},{"english":"lasting achievement","chinese":"持久成就"}]},"model-essay-52-ielts-opinion":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-52-ielts-opinion","essayKey":"opinion:52","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-52-ielts-opinion","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/opinions/EdmundBd9OP-Q52","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"In every country, protecting citizens is one of the state’s core duties. Some argue that this duty requires higher defence budgets and lower spending on welfare programmes. I completely disagree with this view, because safety is not created by weapons alone; it also depends on the health, stability and dignity of ordinary people.","chinese":"在每一個國家，保護公民都是國家的核心職責之一。 有些人認為，這項責任需要政府增加國防預算，並減少在社會福利計劃上的開支。 我完全不同意這個觀點，因為安全並不是單靠武器創造出來的；它也取決於普通人的健康、穩定和尊嚴。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"First, reducing social benefits can make society less safe, not more. Welfare spending funds healthcare, unemployment support, pensions and housing assistance. These are not luxuries; they keep vulnerable citizens from falling into desperation. When families cannot afford medicine, rent or basic food, problems that begin as private hardship can spill over into public disorder, crime and social division. For example, a worker who loses his job but receives temporary support has time to retrain and find employment. Without that safety net, the same person may face debt, eviction and deep resentment. In this sense, social benefits are not soft spending, but a form of domestic security.","chinese":"首先，削減社會福利可能會令社會變得更不安全，而不是更安全。 福利開支資助醫療、失業援助、退休金和住房援助。 這些並不是奢侈品；它們能防止弱勢公民陷入絕望。 當家庭無法負擔藥物、租金或基本食物時，原本屬於私人困境的問題，可能會蔓延成公共秩序混亂、犯罪和社會分裂。 例如，一名失業工人如果能獲得臨時支援，就有時間重新接受培訓並尋找工作。 如果沒有這張安全網，同一個人可能會面對債務、被迫搬離住所，以及深層的怨恨。 從這個意義上說，社會福利並不是軟性開支，而是一種國內安全保障。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"Second, excessive military spending can become a poor use of limited public money when it crowds out services that citizens rely on every day. A larger army or newer equipment may protect borders, but it cannot educate children, treat chronic illnesses or support elderly citizens living alone. These services strengthen a country from within by producing healthier workers, more capable young people and communities that trust the state. A government that neglects these foundations risks building a strong shield around a weak society. For instance, if hospitals are underfunded while defence projects expand, citizens may feel abandoned by their own leaders even in peacetime.","chinese":"其次，當過度的軍事開支擠壓了公民日常依賴的服務時，它就可能變成對有限公共資金的不良使用。 更龐大的軍隊或更新式的裝備或許能保護邊境，但它不能教育兒童、治療慢性疾病，或支援獨居長者。 這些服務能從內部強化一個國家，因為它們能培養更健康的勞動人口、更有能力的年輕人，以及更信任政府的社區。 一個忽視這些基礎的政府，可能會冒著在一個脆弱社會外圍建立強大盾牌的風險。 例如，如果醫院資金不足，而國防項目卻不斷擴張，公民即使在和平時期也可能會覺得被自己的領袖拋棄。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, I do not agree that governments should finance higher defence spending by cutting social benefits. True public safety is broader than military protection. It comes not only from secure borders, but also from citizens who are healthy, educated and protected from extreme hardship.","chinese":"總結來說，我不同意政府應該透過削減社會福利來資助更高的國防開支。 真正的公共安全比軍事保護更加廣泛。 它不僅來自安全的邊境，也來自健康、受教育，並受到保護而免於極端困境的公民。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"protecting citizens","chinese":"保護公民"},{"english":"core duties","chinese":"核心職責"},{"english":"the state","chinese":"國家；政府"},{"english":"higher defence budgets","chinese":"更高國防預算"},{"english":"lower spending on","chinese":"減少在……上的開支"},{"english":"welfare programmes","chinese":"福利計劃"},{"english":"completely disagree with","chinese":"完全不同意……"},{"english":"weapons alone","chinese":"單靠武器"},{"english":"depends on","chinese":"取決於"},{"english":"health, stability and dignity","chinese":"健康、穩定和尊嚴"},{"english":"ordinary people","chinese":"普通人"},{"english":"reducing social benefits","chinese":"削減社會福利"},{"english":"social benefits","chinese":"社會福利"},{"english":"make society less safe","chinese":"令社會更不安全"},{"english":"welfare spending","chinese":"福利開支"},{"english":"unemployment support","chinese":"失業支援"},{"english":"pensions","chinese":"退休金"},{"english":"housing assistance","chinese":"住屋援助"},{"english":"not luxuries","chinese":"不是奢侈品"},{"english":"vulnerable citizens","chinese":"弱勢公民"},{"english":"falling into desperation","chinese":"陷入絕望"},{"english":"afford medicine","chinese":"負擔藥物"},{"english":"basic food","chinese":"基本食物"},{"english":"private hardship","chinese":"個人困境"},{"english":"spill over into","chinese":"擴散成……"},{"english":"public disorder","chinese":"公共秩序混亂"},{"english":"social division","chinese":"社會分化"},{"english":"loses his job","chinese":"失去工作"},{"english":"temporary support","chinese":"臨時支援"},{"english":"retrain","chinese":"再培訓"},{"english":"find employment","chinese":"找到工作"},{"english":"safety net","chinese":"安全網"},{"english":"face debt","chinese":"面對債務"},{"english":"eviction","chinese":"被迫遷"},{"english":"deep resentment","chinese":"深層怨氣"},{"english":"in this sense","chinese":"從這個意義上說"},{"english":"soft spending","chinese":"軟性開支；非必要開支"},{"english":"domestic security","chinese":"國內安全"},{"english":"excessive military spending","chinese":"過度軍事開支"},{"english":"poor use of","chinese":"對……的不善使用"},{"english":"limited public money","chinese":"有限公帑"},{"english":"crowds out","chinese":"排擠"},{"english":"rely on every day","chinese":"每天依賴"},{"english":"larger army","chinese":"更龐大的軍隊"},{"english":"newer equipment","chinese":"較新的裝備"},{"english":"protect borders","chinese":"保護邊境"},{"english":"treat chronic illnesses","chinese":"治療慢性疾病"},{"english":"chronic illnesses","chinese":"慢性疾病"},{"english":"elderly citizens living alone","chinese":"獨居長者"},{"english":"strengthen a country from within","chinese":"從內部強化一個國家"},{"english":"healthier workers","chinese":"更健康的工人"},{"english":"more capable young people","chinese":"更有能力的年輕人"},{"english":"trust the state","chinese":"信任國家；信任政府"},{"english":"neglects these foundations","chinese":"忽視這些基礎"},{"english":"risks building","chinese":"有可能建立……"},{"english":"strong shield","chinese":"強大的盾牌"},{"english":"weak society","chinese":"脆弱的社會"},{"english":"underfunded","chinese":"資金不足"},{"english":"defence projects","chinese":"國防項目"},{"english":"feel abandoned by","chinese":"感到被……拋棄"},{"english":"own leaders","chinese":"自己的領袖"},{"english":"in peacetime","chinese":"在和平時期"},{"english":"finance higher defence spending","chinese":"資助更高國防開支"},{"english":"cutting social benefits","chinese":"削減社會福利"},{"english":"true public safety","chinese":"真正的公共安全"},{"english":"broader than","chinese":"比……更廣泛"},{"english":"military protection","chinese":"軍事保護"},{"english":"secure borders","chinese":"安全邊境"},{"english":"protected from extreme hardship","chinese":"受到保護免於極端困苦"},{"english":"extreme hardship","chinese":"極端困苦"}]},"model-essay-53-ielts-opinion":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-53-ielts-opinion","essayKey":"opinion:53","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-53-ielts-opinion","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/opinions/EdmundBd9OP-Q53","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"Creative work is often treated as a private passion, yet it also shapes how a society remembers, feels and understands itself. I completely agree that governments should provide financial support to artists, musicians and other creative people, because their work creates public value that the market alone rarely protects.","chinese":"創意工作經常被視為一種個人的熱情，但也塑造了一個社會如何記憶、感受和理解自身 我完全同意政府應該向藝術家、音樂家和其他創意人士提供財政支持，因為他們的作品創造了公共價值，而單靠市場往往難以保護這種價值。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"The first reason is that the arts preserve and enrich a nation’s culture. Paintings, songs, films and performances are not merely forms of entertainment; they are part of a country’s collective memory. If talented people are forced to abandon their work simply because they cannot earn a stable income, valuable stories, traditions and local voices may quietly disappear. Public grants can give them the time, materials and venues they need to produce work that later becomes part of a community’s identity. For example, a composer who receives funding to write music based on local folk traditions may create performances that schools, festivals and museums can use for many years. In this sense, supporting creative people is not charity; it is cultural investment.","chinese":"第一個原因是，藝術能夠保存並豐富一個國家的文化。 繪畫、歌曲、電影和表演並不只是娛樂形式；它們是一個國家集體記憶的一部分。 如果有才華的人只是因為無法獲得穩定收入而被迫放棄創作，那麼珍貴的故事、傳統和本土聲音可能會悄然消失。 公共資助可以給予他們所需的時間、材料和場地，讓他們創作出日後成為社區身份一部分的作品。 例如，一位作曲家如果獲得資助，根據本地民間傳統創作音樂，便可能創造出學校、節日活動和博物館多年都能使用的表演作品。 從這個角度來看，支持創意人士並不是慈善；這是一種文化投資。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"Another important reason is that creative work can benefit the wider public, even when it is not immediately profitable. Commercial markets tend to reward what sells quickly, not necessarily what is meaningful, experimental or socially useful. With government support, artists and musicians can offer free concerts in public spaces, run workshops for children, decorate neglected neighbourhoods or create work that helps people think about social issues. These projects may not make anyone rich, but they can make a city feel more alive, humane and connected. Without such funding, creativity risks becoming a luxury available only to those who can already afford to pursue it.","chinese":"另一個重要原因是，創意作品即使不能立即帶來盈利，也能惠及更廣泛的公眾。 商業市場往往獎勵那些能快速售出的東西，而不一定獎勵有意義、具實驗性或對社會有用的作品。 在政府支持下，藝術家和音樂家可以在公共空間舉辦免費音樂會、為兒童舉辦工作坊、裝飾被忽視的社區，或創作能幫助人們思考社會議題的作品。 這些項目未必會令任何人致富，但它們能讓一座城市感覺更有活力、更有人情味，也更有連結感。 如果沒有這類資助，創意便有可能變成一種奢侈品，只屬於那些本來就有能力追求它的人。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, I fully agree that governments should give money to creative people. Art and music strengthen culture, widen public access to beauty and imagination, and give society something deeper than material comfort. A country that supports its artists is not wasting money; it is keeping its cultural heartbeat alive.","chinese":"總結來說，我完全同意政府應該給予創意人士金錢支持。 藝術和音樂能強化文化，擴大公眾接觸美感與想像力的機會，並給予社會一些比物質舒適更深層的東西。 一個支持藝術家的國家並不是在浪費金錢；它是在讓自己的文化心跳繼續跳動。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"creative work","chinese":"創作工作"},{"english":"be treated as","chinese":"被視為"},{"english":"private passion","chinese":"個人熱情"},{"english":"shapes how a society remembers","chinese":"塑造社會如何記憶"},{"english":"understands itself","chinese":"理解自身"},{"english":"provide financial support to","chinese":"向……提供財政支援"},{"english":"artists, musicians and other creative people","chinese":"藝術家、音樂家和其他創意工作者"},{"english":"creates public value","chinese":"創造公共價值"},{"english":"the market alone","chinese":"單靠市場"},{"english":"rarely protects","chinese":"很少保護"},{"english":"preserve and enrich","chinese":"保存並豐富"},{"english":"a nation's culture","chinese":"一個國家的文化"},{"english":"paintings, songs, films and performances","chinese":"繪畫、歌曲、電影和表演"},{"english":"not merely forms of entertainment","chinese":"不只是娛樂形式"},{"english":"collective memory","chinese":"集體記憶"},{"english":"be forced to abandon","chinese":"被迫放棄"},{"english":"abandon their work","chinese":"放棄他們的工作"},{"english":"stable income","chinese":"穩定收入"},{"english":"valuable stories","chinese":"有價值的故事"},{"english":"traditions and local voices","chinese":"傳統和本地聲音"},{"english":"quietly disappear","chinese":"悄悄消失"},{"english":"public grants","chinese":"公共資助；政府撥款"},{"english":"the time, materials and venues","chinese":"時間、材料和場地"},{"english":"produce work","chinese":"創作作品"},{"english":"community's identity","chinese":"社區身份認同"},{"english":"composer","chinese":"作曲家"},{"english":"receives funding to","chinese":"獲得資助去……"},{"english":"local folk traditions","chinese":"本地民間傳統"},{"english":"schools, festivals and museums","chinese":"學校、節日活動和博物館"},{"english":"supporting creative people","chinese":"支持創意工作者"},{"english":"not charity","chinese":"不是慈善"},{"english":"cultural investment","chinese":"文化投資"},{"english":"wider public","chinese":"更廣泛的公眾"},{"english":"immediately profitable","chinese":"即時有利可圖"},{"english":"commercial markets","chinese":"商業市場"},{"english":"tend to reward","chinese":"往往獎勵"},{"english":"what sells quickly","chinese":"快速賣得出的東西"},{"english":"not necessarily","chinese":"不一定"},{"english":"meaningful, experimental or socially useful","chinese":"有意義、具實驗性或對社會有用"},{"english":"with government support","chinese":"在政府支持下"},{"english":"public spaces","chinese":"公共空間"},{"english":"run workshops for children","chinese":"為兒童舉辦工作坊"},{"english":"decorate neglected neighbourhoods","chinese":"裝飾被忽略的社區"},{"english":"neglected neighbourhoods","chinese":"被忽略的社區"},{"english":"think about social issues","chinese":"思考社會議題"},{"english":"make anyone rich","chinese":"令任何人致富"},{"english":"feel more alive","chinese":"感覺更有活力"},{"english":"humane and connected","chinese":"人性化和有連繫"},{"english":"without such funding","chinese":"沒有這類資助"},{"english":"risks becoming","chinese":"有可能變成"},{"english":"a luxury available only to","chinese":"只有……才可享有的奢侈品"},{"english":"afford to pursue it","chinese":"負擔得起去追求它"},{"english":"give money to creative people","chinese":"向創意工作者提供資金"},{"english":"strengthen culture","chinese":"加強文化"},{"english":"widen public access to","chinese":"擴大公眾接觸……的機會"},{"english":"beauty and imagination","chinese":"美感和想像力"},{"english":"material comfort","chinese":"物質舒適"},{"english":"a country that supports its artists","chinese":"支持藝術家的國家"},{"english":"wasting money","chinese":"浪費金錢"},{"english":"cultural heartbeat","chinese":"文化心跳"},{"english":"keeping its cultural heartbeat alive","chinese":"令文化生命力延續"}]},"model-essay-54-ielts-opinion":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-54-ielts-opinion","essayKey":"opinion:54","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-54-ielts-opinion","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/opinions/EdmundBd9OP-Q54","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"Public money is always limited, so governments must decide carefully which areas deserve priority. Some people argue that funding for the arts should be reduced so that more money can be spent on education. I completely disagree with this view because the arts are an essential part of education and also bring wider cultural and economic benefits.","chinese":"公共資金始終是有限的，因此政府必須謹慎決定哪些範疇應該獲得優先考慮。 有些人認為，藝術方面的資助應該被削減，從而使更多金錢可以用於教育。 我完全不同意這種看法，因為藝術是教育不可或缺的一部分，而且也能帶來更廣泛的文化和經濟利益。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"The first reason is that cutting arts funding would actually weaken education rather than improve it. Education is not only about textbooks, examinations, and academic subjects; it should also develop creativity, confidence, emotional intelligence, and critical thinking. Subjects such as music, drama, design, and visual arts allow students to express ideas, solve problems in original ways, and understand human experience more deeply. For example, a student who takes part in school theatre may become more confident in public speaking, while a student who studies painting may learn patience, observation, and interpretation. If the government reduces support for the arts, schools may treat these subjects as luxuries, and students will receive a narrower and poorer form of education.","chinese":"第一個原因是，削減藝術資助實際上會削弱教育，而不是改善教育。 教育不僅僅關乎課本、考試和學術科目；它也應該培養創造力、自信、情緒智力和批判性思維。 音樂、戲劇、設計和視覺藝術等科目，能讓學生表達想法、以原創方式解決問題，並更深入地理解人的經驗。 例如，一個參與學校戲劇的學生，可能會在公開演說方面變得更有自信；而一個學習繪畫的學生，則可能學會耐性、觀察力和詮釋能力。 如果政府減少對藝術的支持，學校可能會把這些科目視為奢侈品，而學生將會接受一種更狹窄、也更貧乏的教育。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"Another important point is that the arts create value beyond the classroom. Museums, galleries, concerts, public performances, and cultural festivals help preserve national identity and bring communities together. They also support jobs in tourism, media, entertainment, design, and the creative industries. In many cities, cultural attractions are not decorative extras; they are part of the local economy and public life. If arts organisations lose funding, talented people may leave the sector, cultural venues may close, and society may become richer in test scores but poorer in imagination. Education needs more investment, but that money should come from wasteful spending or inefficient policies, not from a field that gives society both memory and meaning.","chinese":"另一個重要觀點是，藝術能在課室之外創造價值。 博物館、畫廊、音樂會、公眾表演和文化節，有助保存國家身份，並把社區凝聚在一起 它們也支撐著旅遊、媒體、娛樂、設計和創意產業中的工作機會。 在許多城市，文化景點並不是裝飾性的附加品；它們是本地經濟和公共生活的一部分。 如果藝術機構失去資助，有才華的人可能會離開這個行業，文化場地可能會關閉，而社會也可能在考試分數上變得更富有，卻在想像力上變得更貧乏。 教育需要更多投資，但這些金錢應該來自浪費性的開支或低效率的政策，而不是來自一個同時給予社會記憶與意義的範疇。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, I strongly disagree that governments should lower the arts budget to fund education. A wiser policy is to invest in both, because strong education needs creativity, and a healthy society needs culture.","chinese":"總結來說，我強烈不同意政府應該削減藝術預算來資助教育。 更明智的政策是同時投資於兩者，因為強大的教育需要創造力，而健康的社會需要文化"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"public money","chinese":"公帑；公共資金"},{"english":"deserve priority","chinese":"值得優先處理"},{"english":"funding for the arts","chinese":"藝術撥款"},{"english":"be reduced","chinese":"被削減"},{"english":"be spent on education","chinese":"被用於教育"},{"english":"completely disagree with","chinese":"完全不同意……"},{"english":"an essential part of","chinese":"……的重要部分"},{"english":"wider cultural and economic benefits","chinese":"更廣泛的文化和經濟好處"},{"english":"cutting arts funding","chinese":"削減藝術撥款"},{"english":"weaken education","chinese":"削弱教育"},{"english":"rather than improve it","chinese":"而不是改善它"},{"english":"not only about","chinese":"不只是關於……"},{"english":"textbooks, examinations, and academic subjects","chinese":"教科書、考試和學術科目"},{"english":"develop creativity","chinese":"培養創意"},{"english":"emotional intelligence","chinese":"情緒智能"},{"english":"critical thinking","chinese":"批判思維"},{"english":"subjects such as","chinese":"例如……的科目"},{"english":"visual arts","chinese":"視覺藝術"},{"english":"allow students to","chinese":"讓學生可以……"},{"english":"express ideas","chinese":"表達想法"},{"english":"solve problems in original ways","chinese":"以創新的方式解決問題"},{"english":"understand human experience","chinese":"理解人類經驗"},{"english":"more deeply","chinese":"更深入地"},{"english":"take part in","chinese":"參與"},{"english":"school theatre","chinese":"學校戲劇"},{"english":"public speaking","chinese":"公開演說"},{"english":"studies painting","chinese":"學習繪畫"},{"english":"patience, observation, and interpretation","chinese":"耐性、觀察力和詮釋能力"},{"english":"reduce support for","chinese":"減少對……的支持"},{"english":"treat these subjects as luxuries","chinese":"將這些科目視為奢侈品"},{"english":"narrower and poorer form of education","chinese":"更狹窄和更貧乏的教育形式"},{"english":"create value beyond","chinese":"在……以外創造價值"},{"english":"beyond the classroom","chinese":"課室以外"},{"english":"museums, galleries, concerts, public performances, and cultural festivals","chinese":"博物館、畫廊、音樂會、公開表演和文化節"},{"english":"preserve national identity","chinese":"保存國家身份認同"},{"english":"bring communities together","chinese":"凝聚社區"},{"english":"support jobs in","chinese":"支持……中的就業"},{"english":"creative industries","chinese":"創意產業"},{"english":"cultural attractions","chinese":"文化景點"},{"english":"decorative extras","chinese":"裝飾性的附加物"},{"english":"local economy","chinese":"本地經濟"},{"english":"public life","chinese":"公共生活"},{"english":"arts organisations","chinese":"藝術機構"},{"english":"lose funding","chinese":"失去撥款"},{"english":"talented people","chinese":"有才能的人"},{"english":"leave the sector","chinese":"離開該行業"},{"english":"cultural venues","chinese":"文化場地"},{"english":"richer in test scores but poorer in imagination","chinese":"考試分數更高，但想像力更貧乏"},{"english":"more investment","chinese":"更多投資"},{"english":"wasteful spending","chinese":"浪費性的開支"},{"english":"inefficient policies","chinese":"低效政策"},{"english":"a field that gives society both memory and meaning","chinese":"給予社會記憶和意義的領域"},{"english":"lower the arts budget","chinese":"削減藝術預算"},{"english":"fund education","chinese":"資助教育"},{"english":"wiser policy","chinese":"更明智的政策"},{"english":"invest in both","chinese":"同時投資於兩者"},{"english":"healthy society","chinese":"健康的社會"},{"english":"needs culture","chinese":"需要文化"}]},"model-essay-55-ielts-opinion":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-55-ielts-opinion","essayKey":"opinion:55","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-55-ielts-opinion","flashDeckId":"","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"Societies are shaped by many forces, but public debate often focuses on where real power lies. Some argue that meaningful social change can only come from the government because it controls laws, budgets and public institutions. I strongly disagree with this view. In my opinion, individuals can have a major influence on society because their everyday choices shape social norms and their collective voices can push institutions to change.","chinese":"社會是由許多力量塑造的，但公共討論往往集中於真正的力量究竟在哪裡。 有些人認為，有意義的社會變革只能來自政府，因為政府掌握法律、預算和公共機構。 我強烈不同意這種觀點。 在我看來，個人能夠對社會產生重大影響，因為他們的日常選擇會塑造社會規範，而他們集體的聲音也能推動機構作出改變。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"The first reason is that social change often begins with ordinary behaviour, not official instructions. When individuals alter the way they live, speak or spend money, they gradually change what society accepts as normal. For example, if many people choose to reduce waste, avoid unnecessary plastic and support environmentally responsible businesses, companies are pressured to improve their practices. Over time, these small actions can spread through families, workplaces and communities until they become part of public expectation. A law may draw a line on paper, but people’s habits decide whether that line matters in real life.","chinese":"第一個原因是，社會變革往往始於普通人的行為，而不是官方指示。 當個人改變自己的生活方式、說話方式或消費方式時，他們會逐漸改變社會所接受的「正常」標準。 例如，如果許多人選擇減少浪費、避免不必要的塑膠，並支持對環境負責的企業，公司便會受到壓力去改善自身的做法。 隨著時間推移，這些小行動可以在家庭、工作場所和社區之間擴散，直到它們成為公眾期望的一部分。 法律或能在紙面上劃出界線，但人們的習慣才決定那條界線在現實生活中是否真正重要"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"Another reason is that individuals can influence society by challenging unfair systems and giving others the courage to do the same. A single person who speaks out against discrimination, corruption or poor working conditions may seem powerless at first, but their voice can become the first spark in a much larger movement. For instance, a student who reports bullying, a worker who exposes unsafe practices, or a parent who campaigns for better school support may inspire others to act. Once enough people join that pressure, governments and organisations often have no choice but to respond.","chinese":"另一個原因是，個人可以透過挑戰不公平的制度，並給予他人同樣行動的勇氣，從而影響社會。 一個人站出來反對歧視、貪污或惡劣的工作條件，起初可能看似無力，但他的聲音可以成為更大運動中的第一點火花。 例如，一名舉報欺凌的學生、一位揭露不安全工作做法的工人，或一位爭取更好學校支援的家長，都可能激勵其他人採取行動。 一旦有足夠多的人加入這股壓力，政府和組織往往別無選擇，只能作出回應。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, although governments have formal authority, they are not the only force capable of changing society. Real progress often starts with individuals, whose choices, voices and courage can move public opinion and eventually reshape institutions.","chinese":"總結來說，儘管政府擁有正式權力，但它們並不是唯一能夠改變社會的力量。 真正的進步往往始於個人，因為他們的選擇、聲音和勇氣能夠推動公眾意見，並最終重塑制度。"}],"vocabulary":[]},"model-essay-56-ielts-opinion":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-56-ielts-opinion","essayKey":"opinion:56","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-56-ielts-opinion","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/opinions/EdmundBd9OP-Q56","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"Good health policy should not begin at the hospital door. I completely agree that preventing illness is more important than treating it after it has already developed, and public funding should therefore give prevention the strongest priority.","chinese":"好的健康政策不應該從醫院門口才開始。 我完全同意，預防疾病比在疾病已經形成後才進行治療更加重要，因此公共資金應該把預防放在最優先的位置。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"The first reason is that prevention saves both money and human suffering. When governments invest in health education, vaccination programmes, early screening, safe parks, and better nutrition in schools, many serious conditions can be stopped before they become expensive medical crises. A health system that only responds after people are already sick is always fighting fires: hospitals become crowded, doctors are overstretched, and taxpayers must pay for long-term treatment that might have been avoided. For example, if children are taught healthy eating habits and are given places to exercise, they are less likely to develop obesity-related illnesses later in life. This means fewer patients needing complex surgery, lifelong medication, or repeated hospital visits. Prevention, therefore, does not merely reduce costs; it protects people from pain that no medicine can fully erase.","chinese":"第一個原因是，預防既能節省金錢，也能減少人類痛苦。 當政府投資於健康教育、疫苗接種計劃、早期篩查、安全的公園，以及學校中更好的營養安排時，許多嚴重疾病都可以在變成昂貴的醫療危機之前被阻止。 一個只在人們已經生病後才作出回應的醫療系統，永遠都像是在到處救火：醫院變得擁擠，醫生負擔過重，而納稅人也必須為原本可能避免的長期治療付費。 例如，如果孩子從小被教導健康飲食習慣，並且有地方可以運動，他們日後患上與肥胖相關疾病的可能性便會較低。 這意味著，需要複雜手術、終身服藥或反覆到醫院求診的病人會減少。 因此，預防不只是降低成本；它也保護人們免受那些任何藥物都無法完全抹去的痛苦。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"Another reason is that preventive spending creates a fairer society. Treatment often reaches people only after damage has been done, whereas prevention can protect whole communities before illness takes root. This is especially important for poorer families, who may lack access to nutritious food, safe housing, mental-health support, or regular medical checks. If public money is used to improve air quality, provide free health screenings, support school meals, and promote active lifestyles, the benefits are shared widely rather than reserved for those who can afford private care. In this sense, prevention is not just a medical strategy; it is a social investment that helps citizens remain healthy, productive, and independent.","chinese":"另一個原因是，預防性開支能創造一個更公平的社會。 治療往往只是在傷害已經造成後才接觸到人們，然而預防卻能在疾病扎根之前保護整個社區。 這對較貧困的家庭尤其重要，因為他們可能缺乏獲得營養食物、安全住所、心理健康支援或定期身體檢查的渠道。 如果公共資金被用來改善空氣質素、提供免費健康篩查、支援學校膳食，並推廣積極健康的生活方式，這些好處便能被廣泛分享，而不是只留給那些負擔得起私人醫療的人。 從這個意義上說，預防不只是一種醫療策略；它是一項社會投資，能幫助市民保持健康、有生產力，並維持獨立。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, governments should clearly prioritise the prevention of disease because it reduces avoidable suffering, lowers pressure on healthcare systems, and protects society more equally. Treating illness matters, but preventing it is the wiser use of public money.","chinese":"總結來說，政府應該明確優先考慮疾病預防，因為它能減少可避免的痛苦、降低醫療系統的壓力，並以更公平的方式保護社會。 治療疾病固然重要，但預防疾病才是更明智地使用公共資金的方式。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"health policy","chinese":"健康政策"},{"english":"begin at the hospital door","chinese":"從醫院門口才開始"},{"english":"preventing illness","chinese":"預防疾病"},{"english":"treating it after it has already developed","chinese":"在疾病已經形成後才治療"},{"english":"public funding","chinese":"公共資金；公帑"},{"english":"give prevention the strongest priority","chinese":"將預防放在最優先位置"},{"english":"saves both money and human suffering","chinese":"同時節省金錢和減少人類痛苦"},{"english":"invest in","chinese":"投資於……"},{"english":"health education","chinese":"健康教育"},{"english":"vaccination programmes","chinese":"疫苗接種計劃"},{"english":"early screening","chinese":"早期篩查"},{"english":"safe parks","chinese":"安全的公園"},{"english":"better nutrition","chinese":"更好的營養"},{"english":"serious conditions","chinese":"嚴重病症"},{"english":"be stopped before","chinese":"在……之前被阻止"},{"english":"expensive medical crises","chinese":"昂貴的醫療危機"},{"english":"respond after","chinese":"在……之後才回應"},{"english":"fighting fires","chinese":"疲於救火"},{"english":"hospitals become crowded","chinese":"醫院變得擠迫"},{"english":"doctors are overstretched","chinese":"醫生不勝負荷"},{"english":"taxpayers","chinese":"納稅人"},{"english":"long-term treatment","chinese":"長期治療"},{"english":"might have been avoided","chinese":"本來可以避免"},{"english":"healthy eating habits","chinese":"健康飲食習慣"},{"english":"places to exercise","chinese":"運動的地方"},{"english":"be less likely to develop","chinese":"較不可能患上……"},{"english":"obesity-related illnesses","chinese":"與肥胖有關的疾病"},{"english":"later in life","chinese":"日後；人生較後階段"},{"english":"complex surgery","chinese":"複雜手術"},{"english":"lifelong medication","chinese":"終身服藥"},{"english":"repeated hospital visits","chinese":"反覆到醫院求診"},{"english":"does not merely reduce costs","chinese":"不只是降低成本"},{"english":"protect people from pain","chinese":"保護人們免受痛苦"},{"english":"no medicine can fully erase","chinese":"沒有藥物能完全消除"},{"english":"preventive spending","chinese":"預防性開支"},{"english":"creates a fairer society","chinese":"建立更公平的社會"},{"english":"damage has been done","chinese":"傷害已經造成"},{"english":"whereas","chinese":"而；然而"},{"english":"protect whole communities","chinese":"保護整個社區"},{"english":"takes root","chinese":"扎根；形成"},{"english":"poorer families","chinese":"較貧困家庭"},{"english":"lack access to","chinese":"缺乏取得……的機會"},{"english":"nutritious food","chinese":"有營養的食物"},{"english":"safe housing","chinese":"安全住所"},{"english":"mental-health support","chinese":"精神健康支援"},{"english":"regular medical checks","chinese":"定期身體檢查"},{"english":"improve air quality","chinese":"改善空氣質素"},{"english":"provide free health screenings","chinese":"提供免費健康篩查"},{"english":"support school meals","chinese":"支持學校膳食"},{"english":"promote active lifestyles","chinese":"推廣活躍生活方式"},{"english":"be shared widely","chinese":"被廣泛共享"},{"english":"rather than reserved for","chinese":"而不是只留給……"},{"english":"private care","chinese":"私營醫療服務"},{"english":"in this sense","chinese":"從這個意義上說"},{"english":"medical strategy","chinese":"醫療策略"},{"english":"social investment","chinese":"社會投資"},{"english":"remain healthy, productive, and independent","chinese":"保持健康、有生產力和獨立"},{"english":"prioritise the prevention of disease","chinese":"優先考慮疾病預防"},{"english":"avoidable suffering","chinese":"可避免的痛苦"},{"english":"lowers pressure on","chinese":"降低……的壓力"},{"english":"healthcare systems","chinese":"醫療系統"},{"english":"protects society more equally","chinese":"更公平地保護社會"},{"english":"treating illness matters","chinese":"治療疾病很重要"},{"english":"wiser use of public money","chinese":"更明智地使用公帑"}]},"model-essay-57-ielts-opinion":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-57-ielts-opinion","essayKey":"opinion:57","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-57-ielts-opinion","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/opinions/EdmundBd9OP-Q57","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"In many developed societies, ill health is increasingly linked not to infections, but to the way people live: long working hours, poor diets, chronic stress and physical inactivity. I completely disagree that this should lead us back towards traditional medicine. The more sensible response is to prevent these conditions through healthier routines and to keep treatment firmly based on modern evidence.","chinese":"在許多發達社會中，健康問題越來越不是與感染有關，而是與人們的生活方式有關：長時間工作、不良飲食、長期壓力以及缺乏運動。 我完全不同意這應該使我們重新回到傳統醫學。 更合理的回應，是透過更健康的日常習慣來預防這些問題，並讓治療牢牢建立在現代證據之上。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"Most modern lifestyle illnesses are rooted in habits and environments rather than in the absence of ancient remedies. A person who spends ten hours at a desk, eats takeaway meals and sleeps badly is not ill because society has forgotten herbal treatments; he is ill because his body is being pushed beyond healthy limits. In such a case, pills may reduce blood pressure or sugar levels, but no medicine, traditional or modern, can substitute for exercise, rest and better food. Therefore, governments, schools and employers should focus on prevention by promoting active transport, balanced diets, reasonable working hours and better mental-health support.","chinese":"大多數現代生活方式疾病的根源，在於習慣和環境，而不是因為缺乏古老療法。 一個每天在辦公桌前坐十小時、吃外賣、睡眠質素差的人，並不是因為社會忘記了草藥療法而生病；他生病是因為他的身體被推到了健康極限之外。 在這種情況下，藥物也許可以降低血壓或血糖水平，但無論是傳統醫學還是現代醫學，都不能取代運動、休息和更好的飲食。 因此，政府、學校和僱主應該把重點放在預防上，例如推廣主動出行、均衡飲食、合理工作時間，以及更好的心理健康支援。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"Encouraging a return to traditional medicine could also give people a false sense of security. Traditional practices are often based on cultural memory rather than rigorous testing, so their effects, side effects and safe doses may be unclear. If patients rely on them for serious conditions linked to stress, obesity or heart disease, they may delay proper diagnosis until the problem becomes harder to treat. Modern healthcare is not perfect, but it offers check-ups, counselling, nutritional advice and medicines that can be tested, monitored and improved. Replacing this evidence-based system with traditional remedies would be like exchanging a map for a comforting story.","chinese":"鼓勵人們回歸傳統醫學，也可能給人一種錯誤的安全感。 傳統療法往往是基於文化記憶，而不是嚴謹測試，因此它們的效果、副作用和安全劑量可能並不清楚。 如果病人依賴它們來處理與壓力、肥胖或心臟病有關的嚴重問題，他們可能會延誤正確診斷，直到問題變得更難治療。 現代醫療並不完美，但它提供身體檢查、輔導、營養建議，以及可以被測試、監察和改良的藥物。 用傳統療法取代這種以證據為基礎的系統，就像用一張地圖換取一個令人安心的故事。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, I completely disagree that society should encourage a return to traditional medicine. Lifestyle-related illnesses should be tackled through prevention and evidence-based healthcare, not through treatments whose reliability is often uncertain.","chinese":"總結來說，我完全不同意社會應該鼓勵人們回歸傳統醫學。 與生活方式有關的疾病，應該透過預防和以證據為基礎的醫療來處理，而不是依靠可靠性往往不確定的療法。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"developed societies","chinese":"發達社會"},{"english":"ill health","chinese":"健康欠佳"},{"english":"be increasingly linked to","chinese":"越來越與……有關"},{"english":"infections","chinese":"感染"},{"english":"the way people live","chinese":"人們的生活方式"},{"english":"long working hours","chinese":"長時間工作"},{"english":"poor diets","chinese":"不良飲食"},{"english":"chronic stress","chinese":"長期壓力"},{"english":"physical inactivity","chinese":"缺乏體能活動"},{"english":"lead us back towards","chinese":"帶領我們回到……"},{"english":"traditional medicine","chinese":"傳統醫學"},{"english":"sensible response","chinese":"明智得多的回應"},{"english":"prevent these conditions","chinese":"預防這些病症"},{"english":"healthier routines","chinese":"更健康的日常習慣"},{"english":"firmly based on","chinese":"牢牢建基於……"},{"english":"modern evidence","chinese":"現代證據"},{"english":"lifestyle illnesses","chinese":"生活方式疾病"},{"english":"be rooted in","chinese":"根源在於……"},{"english":"habits and environments","chinese":"習慣和環境"},{"english":"rather than in","chinese":"而不是在於……"},{"english":"the absence of","chinese":"缺乏……"},{"english":"ancient remedies","chinese":"古老療法"},{"english":"spend ten hours at a desk","chinese":"在書桌前坐十小時"},{"english":"takeaway meals","chinese":"外賣餐"},{"english":"sleep badly","chinese":"睡得不好"},{"english":"herbal treatments","chinese":"草藥療法"},{"english":"be pushed beyond healthy limits","chinese":"被推到超出健康界限"},{"english":"in such a case","chinese":"在這種情況下"},{"english":"blood pressure","chinese":"血壓"},{"english":"sugar levels","chinese":"血糖水平"},{"english":"substitute for","chinese":"取代"},{"english":"exercise, rest and better food","chinese":"運動、休息和更好的飲食"},{"english":"focus on prevention","chinese":"專注於預防"},{"english":"active transport","chinese":"主動出行"},{"english":"balanced diets","chinese":"均衡飲食"},{"english":"reasonable working hours","chinese":"合理工作時間"},{"english":"mental-health support","chinese":"精神健康支援"},{"english":"encouraging a return to","chinese":"鼓勵回歸……"},{"english":"false sense of security","chinese":"錯誤的安全感"},{"english":"traditional practices","chinese":"傳統做法"},{"english":"be based on","chinese":"建基於……"},{"english":"cultural memory","chinese":"文化記憶"},{"english":"rigorous testing","chinese":"嚴謹測試"},{"english":"effects, side effects and safe doses","chinese":"效果、副作用和安全劑量"},{"english":"be unclear","chinese":"不清楚"},{"english":"rely on","chinese":"依賴"},{"english":"serious conditions linked to","chinese":"與……有關的嚴重病症"},{"english":"obesity","chinese":"肥胖"},{"english":"heart disease","chinese":"心臟病"},{"english":"delay proper diagnosis","chinese":"延誤正確診斷"},{"english":"harder to treat","chinese":"較難治療"},{"english":"modern healthcare","chinese":"現代醫療"},{"english":"check-ups","chinese":"身體檢查"},{"english":"counselling","chinese":"輔導"},{"english":"nutritional advice","chinese":"營養建議"},{"english":"be tested, monitored and improved","chinese":"被測試、監察和改良"},{"english":"evidence-based system","chinese":"以證據為本的制度"},{"english":"traditional remedies","chinese":"傳統療法"},{"english":"exchanging a map for","chinese":"以……換取……"},{"english":"comforting story","chinese":"令人安心的故事"},{"english":"society should encourage","chinese":"社會應該鼓勵"},{"english":"lifestyle-related illnesses","chinese":"與生活方式有關的疾病"},{"english":"be tackled through","chinese":"透過……處理"},{"english":"prevention","chinese":"預防"},{"english":"evidence-based healthcare","chinese":"以證據為本的醫療"},{"english":"reliability is often uncertain","chinese":"可靠性往往不確定"}]},"model-essay-58-ielts-opinion":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-58-ielts-opinion","essayKey":"opinion:58","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-58-ielts-opinion","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/opinions/EdmundBd9OP-Q58","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"Healthcare is one of the most essential public services in any society, and debates about who should pay for it are understandably sensitive. Some people argue that medical treatment should never be free because individuals are responsible for their own health. I completely disagree with this view, as illness is not always caused by personal choices, and free healthcare protects both individuals and society as a whole.","chinese":"醫療保健是任何社會中最基本的公共服務之一，而關於應由誰支付醫療費用的討論，自然是相當敏感的。 有些人認為，醫療服務不應該是免費的，因為個人應該對自己的健康負責。 我完全不同意這個觀點，因為疾病並不總是由個人選擇造成，而免費醫療能夠保護個人，也能保護整個社會。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"The first reason is that many health problems are beyond a person’s control. Although lifestyle choices such as diet, exercise, and smoking can affect health, it is far too simplistic to suggest that every patient is personally to blame for their condition. Children may be born with genetic disorders, workers may develop illnesses because of unsafe environments, and elderly people often require treatment simply because their bodies become weaker with age. For example, a low-income worker who develops cancer should not be denied medical care merely because they cannot afford expensive treatment. If healthcare depends entirely on personal wealth, disease becomes not only a medical problem but also a financial punishment for the vulnerable.","chinese":"第一個原因是，許多健康問題並不是個人能夠控制的。 雖然飲食、運動和吸煙等生活方式選擇會影響健康，但認為每位病人都應為自己的病情負上個人責任，這種說法實在過於簡化。 孩子可能天生患有遺傳疾病，工人可能因不安全的工作環境而患病，而長者往往只是因為身體隨年齡變弱而需要治療。 例如，一位低收入工人若患上癌症，不應該僅因為負擔不起昂貴治療而被剝奪醫療照顧 如果醫療完全取決於個人財富，疾病就不再只是醫學問題，也會變成對弱勢人士的一種經濟懲罰"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"Another important point is that free healthcare benefits society, not just individual patients. When people can access treatment early, illnesses are more likely to be diagnosed before they become severe. This reduces pressure on hospitals in the long term and prevents contagious diseases from spreading widely. For instance, if poor families avoid seeing a doctor because of high fees, minor infections may worsen or spread to others in schools, workplaces, and communities. In this sense, free healthcare is not simply an act of kindness; it is a practical investment in public safety and social stability.","chinese":"另一個重要觀點是，免費醫療受益的不只是個別病人，而是整個社會。 當人們能夠及早接受治療時，疾病便更有可能在惡化之前被診斷出來。 從長遠來看，這能減輕醫院的壓力，並防止傳染病大範圍擴散。 例如，如果貧困家庭因為高昂費用而避免看醫生，輕微感染可能會惡化，或在學校、工作場所和社區中傳染給其他人。 從這個意義上說，免費醫療並不只是善意的表現；它更是對公共安全和社會穩定的一項實際投資。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, I strongly disagree that healthcare should never be free. While individuals should certainly be encouraged to make healthy choices, society should not abandon people when they fall ill. A fair healthcare system recognises that health is partly personal, but never entirely personal.","chinese":"總結來說，我強烈不同意醫療永遠不應免費這個觀點。 雖然社會當然應該鼓勵個人作出健康的選擇，但當人們生病時，社會不應該拋棄他們。 一個公平的醫療制度會承認健康在某程度上屬於個人責任，但它絕不全只是個人的責任"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"healthcare","chinese":"醫療服務"},{"english":"essential public services","chinese":"必要公共服務"},{"english":"in any society","chinese":"在任何社會中"},{"english":"debates about","chinese":"關於……的爭論"},{"english":"understandably sensitive","chinese":"可以理解地敏感"},{"english":"medical treatment","chinese":"醫療治療"},{"english":"should never be free","chinese":"絕不應該免費"},{"english":"be responsible for","chinese":"對……負責"},{"english":"personal choices","chinese":"個人選擇"},{"english":"free healthcare","chinese":"免費醫療服務"},{"english":"society as a whole","chinese":"整個社會"},{"english":"health problems","chinese":"健康問題"},{"english":"beyond a person's control","chinese":"超出個人控制範圍"},{"english":"lifestyle choices","chinese":"生活方式選擇"},{"english":"affect health","chinese":"影響健康"},{"english":"far too simplistic to suggest","chinese":"認為……實在過於簡化"},{"english":"personally to blame for","chinese":"對……負有個人責任"},{"english":"their condition","chinese":"他們的病情"},{"english":"be born with","chinese":"天生患有"},{"english":"genetic disorders","chinese":"遺傳疾病"},{"english":"develop illnesses","chinese":"患上疾病"},{"english":"unsafe environments","chinese":"不安全的環境"},{"english":"elderly people","chinese":"長者"},{"english":"require treatment","chinese":"需要治療"},{"english":"become weaker with age","chinese":"隨着年齡增長而變弱"},{"english":"low-income worker","chinese":"低收入工人"},{"english":"develop cancer","chinese":"患上癌症"},{"english":"be denied medical care","chinese":"被拒絕醫療護理"},{"english":"merely because","chinese":"只是因為"},{"english":"afford expensive treatment","chinese":"負擔昂貴治療"},{"english":"depends entirely on","chinese":"完全取決於……"},{"english":"personal wealth","chinese":"個人財富"},{"english":"financial punishment","chinese":"經濟懲罰"}]},"model-essay-59-ielts-opinion":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-59-ielts-opinion","essayKey":"opinion:59","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-59-ielts-opinion","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/opinions/EdmundBd9OP-Q59","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"Health has become a major concern in modern society, especially as many people now spend long hours sitting, working under pressure, and eating poorly. Some argue that exercising every day is the most effective way to become healthier. I completely agree with this view because daily exercise improves both physical condition and mental well-being in a way that few other habits can match.","chinese":"健康已成為現代社會中的一個主要關注，尤其是因為許多人如今長時間坐著、在壓力下工作，並且飲食不良。 有些人認為，每天運動是變得更健康的最有效方法。 我完全同意這個觀點，因為每天運動能改善身體狀況和心理健康，而很少有其他習慣能達到同樣的效果。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"The strongest reason is that regular physical activity directly strengthens the body. When people move every day, their heart, lungs, muscles, and joints are all forced to work, adapt, and become more resilient. This makes the body better able to control weight, maintain energy, and reduce the risk of common lifestyle problems. For example, an office worker who walks briskly for thirty minutes after work each day is likely to feel less tired, sleep more easily, and gradually become fitter. By contrast, a person who remains inactive may find that small physical tasks, such as climbing stairs or carrying shopping bags, become unnecessarily difficult. Therefore, daily exercise is not just a hobby; it is a practical foundation for better physical health.","chinese":"最有力的原因是，規律的身體活動能直接強化身體。 當人們每天活動時，他們的心臟、肺部、肌肉和關節都會被迫運作、適應，並變得更有韌性。 這使身體更能控制體重、維持精力，並降低常見生活方式問題的風險。 例如，一位上班族如果每天放工後快步走三十分鐘，很可能會感到較不疲倦、更容易入睡，並逐漸變得更健康。 相比之下，一個長期缺乏活動的人可能會發現，一些細小的體力任務，例如爬樓梯或提購物袋，都變得不必要地困難。 因此，每天運動不只是一種興趣；它是改善身體健康的實際基礎。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"Another important point is that exercise also improves mental health, which is an essential part of overall well-being. Many people today suffer from stress because of study, work, and financial pressure. Daily exercise gives them a healthy outlet, allowing the mind to release tension rather than store it. For instance, a student who feels overwhelmed by examinations may feel calmer and more focused after jogging, swimming, or playing basketball. This kind of routine can also build discipline, confidence, and a stronger sense of control over life. As a result, exercise improves health not only from the outside, but also from the inside.","chinese":"另一個重要觀點是，運動也能改善心理健康，而是整體福祉中不可或缺的一部分 如今許多人因為學習、工作和經濟壓力而承受壓力。 每天運動能給他們一個健康的出口，讓心靈釋放壓力，而不是把壓力積存在內心。 例如，一個因考試而感到不堪重負的學生，在跑步、游泳或打籃球之後，可能會感到更平靜，也更能集中精神。 這種習慣也能培養自律、自信，以及對生活更強的掌控感。 結果是，運動不但從外在改善健康，也從內在改善健康。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, I fully agree that exercising daily is the best way to improve health. It strengthens the body, clears the mind, and creates a stable routine that supports long-term well-being.","chinese":"總結來說，我完全同意每天運動是改善健康的最佳方法。 它能強化身體、清理思緒，並建立一種支持長遠福祉的穩定習慣。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"a major concern","chinese":"主要關注"},{"english":"modern society","chinese":"現代社會"},{"english":"especially as","chinese":"尤其因為"},{"english":"spend long hours sitting","chinese":"長時間坐着"},{"english":"work under pressure","chinese":"在壓力下工作"},{"english":"eat poorly","chinese":"飲食不良"},{"english":"some argue that","chinese":"有些人認為"},{"english":"exercising every day","chinese":"每日做運動"},{"english":"the most effective way to","chinese":"……的最有效方法"},{"english":"become healthier","chinese":"變得更健康"},{"english":"completely agree with this view","chinese":"完全同意這個看法"},{"english":"daily exercise","chinese":"每日運動"},{"english":"improve both","chinese":"同時改善"},{"english":"physical condition","chinese":"身體狀況"},{"english":"mental well-being","chinese":"精神健康；心理健康"},{"english":"few other habits can match","chinese":"很少其他習慣能媲美"},{"english":"the strongest reason","chinese":"最有力的原因"},{"english":"regular physical activity","chinese":"規律體能活動"},{"english":"directly strengthens the body","chinese":"直接強化身體"},{"english":"move every day","chinese":"每日活動身體"},{"english":"heart, lungs, muscles, and joints","chinese":"心臟、肺部、肌肉和關節"},{"english":"be forced to","chinese":"被迫去"},{"english":"work, adapt, and become more resilient","chinese":"運作、適應並變得更有韌性"},{"english":"become more resilient","chinese":"變得更有韌性"},{"english":"better able to","chinese":"更能夠"},{"english":"control weight","chinese":"控制體重"},{"english":"maintain energy","chinese":"保持精力"},{"english":"reduce the risk of","chinese":"減低……的風險"},{"english":"common lifestyle problems","chinese":"常見生活方式問題"},{"english":"an office worker","chinese":"辦公室職員"},{"english":"walk briskly","chinese":"快步行走"},{"english":"for thirty minutes","chinese":"三十分鐘"},{"english":"after work","chinese":"下班後"},{"english":"be likely to","chinese":"很可能會"},{"english":"feel less tired","chinese":"感到較不疲倦"},{"english":"sleep more easily","chinese":"更容易入睡"},{"english":"gradually become fitter","chinese":"逐漸變得更健壯"},{"english":"by contrast","chinese":"相反"},{"english":"remain inactive","chinese":"保持不活動；缺乏活動"},{"english":"small physical tasks","chinese":"細小體力任務"},{"english":"climbing stairs","chinese":"行樓梯"},{"english":"carrying shopping bags","chinese":"提購物袋"},{"english":"become unnecessarily difficult","chinese":"變得不必要地困難"}]},"model-essay-60-ielts-opinion":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-60-ielts-opinion","essayKey":"opinion:60","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-60-ielts-opinion","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/opinions/EdmundBd9OP-Q60","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"It is often argued that doctors ought to take responsibility for teaching patients how to protect and improve their health. I completely agree with this view, because medical advice is most effective when it is practical, personal, and given by someone whom patients already trust.","chinese":"人們經常主張，醫生應該承擔責任，教導病人如何保護並改善自己的健康。 我完全同意這個觀點，因為當醫療建議具備實用性、個人化，並由病人本已信任的人提出時，它最能發揮效果。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"The first reason is that doctors are in the best position to turn general health knowledge into specific guidance. Many people already know that they should eat well, exercise regularly, and avoid harmful habits, but such advice can feel vague and easy to ignore. A doctor, however, can connect these habits directly to a patient’s condition. For example, a patient with high blood pressure may not understand the danger of a salty diet until a doctor explains how it affects the heart and blood vessels. In that moment, education is not just information; it becomes a wake-up call. When advice is linked to a real medical risk, patients are more likely to take it seriously and change their behaviour.","chinese":"第一個原因是，醫生最有能力把一般性的健康知識轉化為具體指導。 很多人其實已經知道自己應該健康飲食、定期運動，並避免有害習慣，但這類建議可能會顯得模糊，也很容易被忽視。 然而，醫生可以把這些習慣直接與病人的身體狀況聯繫起來。 例如，一名患有高血壓的病人，可能直到醫生解釋高鹽飲食如何影響心臟和血管時，才真正明白其危險性。 在那一刻，教育不只是資訊；它變成了一次警醒。 當建議與真實的健康風險聯繫起來時，病人便更可能認真對待，並改變自己的行為。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"Another important reason is that patient education can prevent future illness and reduce pressure on the healthcare system. If doctors only treat diseases after they appear, medicine becomes a cycle of repair rather than prevention. By explaining early warning signs, healthy routines, and the consequences of neglecting minor symptoms, doctors can help patients avoid serious problems later. For instance, a person who is taught how to manage weight, sleep, and stress may be less likely to develop long-term conditions such as diabetes or heart disease. This not only improves individual well-being, but also allows hospitals and clinics to focus more resources on patients who urgently need treatment.","chinese":"另一個重要原因是，病人教育能夠預防未來疾病，並減輕醫療系統的壓力。 如果醫生只是在疾病出現後才加以治療，醫療就會變成一個修補的循環，而不是預防。 透過解釋早期警號、健康日常習慣，以及忽視輕微症狀的後果，醫生能夠幫助病人避免日後出現嚴重問題。 例如，一個學會如何管理體重、睡眠和壓力的人，日後患上糖尿病或心臟病等長期疾病的可能性可能會較低。 這不但能改善個人的健康福祉，也能讓醫院和診所有更多資源集中照顧迫切需要治療的病人"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, I fully agree that doctors should educate patients about improving their health. Their guidance is trusted, personalised, and potentially life-changing, so health education should be seen as a core part of medical care rather than an optional extra.","chinese":"總結來說，我完全同意醫生應該教育病人如何改善健康。 他們的指導值得信任、具個人化，而且可能改變人生，因此健康教育應被視為醫療照護的核心部分，而不是可有可無的附加項目。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"it is often argued that","chinese":"人們經常認為……"},{"english":"ought to take responsibility for","chinese":"應該承擔……的責任"},{"english":"teaching patients how to","chinese":"教導病人如何……"},{"english":"protect and improve their health","chinese":"保護和改善健康"},{"english":"completely agree with","chinese":"完全同意……"},{"english":"medical advice","chinese":"醫療建議"},{"english":"most effective when","chinese":"在……時最有效"},{"english":"practical, personal, and given by","chinese":"實用、個人化，並由……給出"},{"english":"already trust","chinese":"已經信任"},{"english":"in the best position to","chinese":"最適合去……"},{"english":"general health knowledge","chinese":"一般健康知識"},{"english":"specific guidance","chinese":"具體指引"},{"english":"eat well","chinese":"飲食健康"},{"english":"exercise regularly","chinese":"定期運動"},{"english":"avoid harmful habits","chinese":"避免有害習慣"},{"english":"feel vague","chinese":"感覺含糊"},{"english":"easy to ignore","chinese":"容易忽視"},{"english":"connect these habits directly to","chinese":"將這些習慣直接聯繫到……"},{"english":"patient's condition","chinese":"病人的病情"},{"english":"high blood pressure","chinese":"高血壓"},{"english":"the danger of","chinese":"……的危險"},{"english":"salty diet","chinese":"高鹽飲食"},{"english":"affects the heart and blood vessels","chinese":"影響心臟和血管"},{"english":"in that moment","chinese":"在那一刻"},{"english":"not just information","chinese":"不只是資料"},{"english":"wake-up call","chinese":"警醒；警號"},{"english":"be linked to","chinese":"與……聯繫起來"},{"english":"real medical risk","chinese":"真正的醫療風險"},{"english":"be more likely to","chinese":"更有可能"},{"english":"take it seriously","chinese":"認真看待它"},{"english":"change their behaviour","chinese":"改變行為"},{"english":"patient education","chinese":"病人教育"},{"english":"prevent future illness","chinese":"預防日後疾病"},{"english":"reduce pressure on","chinese":"減輕……的壓力"},{"english":"healthcare system","chinese":"醫療系統"},{"english":"treat diseases","chinese":"治療疾病"},{"english":"after they appear","chinese":"在它們出現之後"},{"english":"a cycle of repair","chinese":"修補循環"},{"english":"rather than prevention","chinese":"而不是預防"},{"english":"early warning signs","chinese":"早期警號"},{"english":"healthy routines","chinese":"健康生活習慣"},{"english":"the consequences of","chinese":"……的後果"},{"english":"neglecting minor symptoms","chinese":"忽視輕微症狀"},{"english":"avoid serious problems later","chinese":"避免日後出現嚴重問題"},{"english":"manage weight, sleep, and stress","chinese":"管理體重、睡眠和壓力"},{"english":"be less likely to develop","chinese":"較不可能患上……"},{"english":"long-term conditions","chinese":"長期病患"},{"english":"diabetes","chinese":"糖尿病"},{"english":"heart disease","chinese":"心臟病"},{"english":"individual well-being","chinese":"個人身心健康"},{"english":"allows hospitals and clinics to","chinese":"讓醫院和診所可以……"},{"english":"focus more resources on","chinese":"將更多資源集中於……"},{"english":"urgently need treatment","chinese":"急需治療"},{"english":"educate patients about","chinese":"教育病人有關……"},{"english":"trusted, personalised, and potentially life-changing","chinese":"可信、個人化，而且有可能改變人生"},{"english":"potentially life-changing","chinese":"有可能改變人生"},{"english":"health education","chinese":"健康教育"},{"english":"core part of","chinese":"……的核心部分"},{"english":"medical care","chinese":"醫療護理"},{"english":"optional extra","chinese":"可有可無的附加項目"}]},"model-essay-61-ielts-opinion":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-61-ielts-opinion","essayKey":"opinion:61","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-61-ielts-opinion","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/opinions/EdmundBd9OP-Q61","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"Urban land is becoming scarce, so decisions about empty plots in cities and towns require careful judgement. Although many people believe these spaces should be used for residential buildings, I completely agree that they should be reserved for trees and green areas, because this would make urban life healthier and more sustainable.","chinese":"城市土地正變得越來越稀缺，因此關於城市和城鎮中空置土地的決定需要審慎判斷。 儘管許多人認為這些空間應該用來興建住宅樓宇， 我完全同意它們應該被保留作種植樹木和綠化空間之用，因為這會令城市生活更健康、更可持續。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"The most immediate reason is that trees make densely populated areas far more liveable. In many towns, residents already spend their daily lives surrounded by roads, concrete walls, and traffic, so the few remaining open spaces should not simply be swallowed by more construction. Trees provide shade, reduce dust, soften noise, and give people somewhere calm to walk or rest. A city without greenery can feel like a concrete oven, especially during hot seasons. For example, a small tree-filled space near apartment blocks can become a place where children play safely, elderly people exercise, and office workers clear their minds after work. This does not merely improve the appearance of a neighbourhood; it supports public health and everyday well-being.","chinese":"最直接的原因是，樹木能使人口密集的地區更加宜居。 在許多城鎮中，居民的日常生活已經被道路、混凝土牆和交通包圍，因此僅餘的少數空地不應該只是被更多建築吞噬。 樹木能提供陰涼、減少塵埃、緩和噪音，並給人們一個安靜散步或休息的地方。 一個沒有綠化的城市可能會感覺像一個混凝土焗爐，尤其是在炎熱季節。 例如，公寓大樓附近一片種滿樹木的小空間，可以成為孩子安全玩耍、長者運動，以及上班族下班後放鬆頭腦的地方。 這並不只是改善社區的外觀；它也支持公共健康和日常福祉。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"Another reason is that building housing on every vacant plot is a short-sighted solution to urban problems. Housing shortages are serious, but they should be addressed through better planning, redevelopment of abandoned buildings, and more efficient use of existing residential land. If every empty area is turned into apartments, cities may gain a few more homes but lose the natural spaces that help them breathe. More buildings can also increase traffic, put pressure on drainage systems, and make crowded districts even more stressful. By contrast, trees act as quiet public infrastructure: they cool the air, absorb pollution, and reduce the impact of heavy rain. Once these green spaces are destroyed, they are extremely difficult to restore.","chinese":"另一個原因是，在每一塊空置土地上興建住房，是一種短視的城市問題解決方法。 住房短缺確實嚴重，但它們應該透過更好的規劃、重建廢棄建築，以及更有效地利用現有住宅用地來處理。 如果每一片空地都被改建成公寓，城市或許會多獲得一些住房，但卻會失去幫助它們呼吸的自然空間。 更多建築也可能增加交通流量、加重排水系統的壓力，並令擁擠地區變得更加壓抑。 相比之下，樹木就像安靜的公共基礎設施：它們能降低氣溫、吸收污染，並減輕暴雨帶來的影響。 一旦這些綠色空間被破壞，它們就極難恢復。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, I strongly agree that vacant urban areas should be used for planting trees rather than constructing more housing. Homes are necessary, but cities also need green lungs if they are to remain healthy, humane, and sustainable.","chinese":"總結來說，我強烈同意城市中的空置地區應該用來種植樹木，而不是建造更多住房。 住房是必要的，但如果城市要保持健康、人性化和可持續，它們也需要綠色的肺。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"urban land","chinese":"城市土地"},{"english":"becoming scarce","chinese":"變得短缺"},{"english":"empty plots","chinese":"空置地皮"},{"english":"cities and towns","chinese":"城市和市鎮"},{"english":"require careful judgement","chinese":"需要謹慎判斷"},{"english":"residential buildings","chinese":"住宅樓宇"},{"english":"be reserved for","chinese":"被保留作……用途"},{"english":"trees and green areas","chinese":"樹木和綠化地區"},{"english":"urban life","chinese":"城市生活"},{"english":"more sustainable","chinese":"更可持續"},{"english":"the most immediate reason","chinese":"最直接的原因"},{"english":"densely populated areas","chinese":"人口稠密地區"},{"english":"far more liveable","chinese":"宜居得多"},{"english":"daily lives","chinese":"日常生活"},{"english":"be surrounded by","chinese":"被……包圍"},{"english":"concrete walls","chinese":"石屎牆"},{"english":"traffic","chinese":"交通；車流"},{"english":"remaining open spaces","chinese":"剩餘的開放空間"},{"english":"be swallowed by","chinese":"被……吞噬"},{"english":"construction","chinese":"建築工程"},{"english":"provide shade","chinese":"提供遮蔭"},{"english":"reduce dust","chinese":"減少塵埃"},{"english":"soften noise","chinese":"減低噪音"},{"english":"somewhere calm to","chinese":"可以安靜地……的地方"},{"english":"walk or rest","chinese":"散步或休息"},{"english":"without greenery","chinese":"沒有綠化"},{"english":"concrete oven","chinese":"石屎焗爐"},{"english":"especially during","chinese":"尤其是在……期間"},{"english":"hot seasons","chinese":"炎熱季節"},{"english":"tree-filled space","chinese":"種滿樹木的空間"},{"english":"apartment blocks","chinese":"住宅大廈"},{"english":"play safely","chinese":"安全地玩耍"},{"english":"elderly people","chinese":"長者"},{"english":"office workers","chinese":"辦公室員工"},{"english":"clear their minds","chinese":"清理思緒"},{"english":"after work","chinese":"下班後"},{"english":"does not merely improve","chinese":"不只是改善"},{"english":"appearance of a neighbourhood","chinese":"社區外觀"},{"english":"supports public health","chinese":"支持公共健康"},{"english":"everyday well-being","chinese":"日常身心健康"},{"english":"vacant plot","chinese":"空置地皮"},{"english":"short-sighted solution","chinese":"短視的解決方法"},{"english":"urban problems","chinese":"城市問題"},{"english":"housing shortages","chinese":"房屋短缺"},{"english":"be addressed through","chinese":"透過……處理"},{"english":"better planning","chinese":"更好的規劃"},{"english":"redevelopment of abandoned buildings","chinese":"重建廢棄建築物"},{"english":"more efficient use of","chinese":"更有效使用……"},{"english":"existing residential land","chinese":"現有住宅土地"},{"english":"be turned into apartments","chinese":"被改建成住宅單位"},{"english":"gain a few more homes","chinese":"增加少量住宅"},{"english":"natural spaces","chinese":"自然空間"},{"english":"help them breathe","chinese":"幫助城市呼吸"},{"english":"increase traffic","chinese":"增加交通流量"},{"english":"put pressure on","chinese":"對……造成壓力"},{"english":"drainage systems","chinese":"排水系統"},{"english":"crowded districts","chinese":"擠迫地區"},{"english":"by contrast","chinese":"相比之下"},{"english":"quiet public infrastructure","chinese":"安靜的公共基礎設施"},{"english":"cool the air","chinese":"令空氣降溫"},{"english":"absorb pollution","chinese":"吸收污染"},{"english":"reduce the impact of","chinese":"減低……的影響"},{"english":"heavy rain","chinese":"大雨"},{"english":"be destroyed","chinese":"被破壞"},{"english":"extremely difficult to restore","chinese":"極難恢復"},{"english":"vacant urban areas","chinese":"城市空置地"},{"english":"planting trees","chinese":"種樹"},{"english":"rather than constructing","chinese":"而不是建造……"},{"english":"green lungs","chinese":"綠肺"},{"english":"remain healthy, humane, and sustainable","chinese":"保持健康、人性化和可持續"}]},"model-essay-62-ielts-opinion":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-62-ielts-opinion","essayKey":"opinion:62","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-62-ielts-opinion","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/opinions/EdmundBd9OP-Q62","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"In my view, cities should definitely be designed to appeal to both residents and international visitors. A successful city is not merely a place where people live or pass through; it is a public home whose streets, buildings, and open spaces should make daily life richer while also presenting the city confidently to the wider world.","chinese":"在我看來，城市確實應該被設計得能夠吸引本地居民和國際旅客。 一個成功的城市不僅僅是一個讓人居住或經過的地方；它是一個公共的家園，而它的街道、建築和開放空間應該讓日常生活更加豐富，同時也自信地向更廣闊的世界展現這座城市。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"The strongest reason is that attractive urban design improves the lives of local people. When a city contains green parks, safe pavements, efficient public transport, and welcoming community spaces, residents are more likely to walk, meet, relax, and feel attached to their surroundings. This matters because people do not experience a city only through major landmarks; they experience it through their daily routines, from commuting to work to taking their children to playgrounds. For example, a well-designed square with shade, seating, trees, and nearby shops can become a small social heart of a neighbourhood. It gives people somewhere to pause, talk, and breathe. In this sense, beauty is not a luxury; it is part of public well-being.","chinese":"最有力的原因是，具吸引力的城市設計能改善本地人的生活。 當一座城市擁有綠色公園、安全的人行道、高效的公共交通，以及令人感到親切的社區空間時，居民便更有可能步行、見面、放鬆，並對周圍環境產生歸屬感。 這一點很重要，因為人們並不是只透過主要地標去體驗一座城市；他們是透過日常生活去體驗城市，從上班通勤到帶孩子去遊樂場都是如此。 例如，一個設計良好的廣場，如果有遮蔭、座位、樹木和附近的商店，就可以成為一個社區小小的社交核心。 它給人們一個可以停下來、交談和喘息的地方。 從這個意義上說，美感並不是一種奢侈品；它是公共福祉的一部分。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"At the same time, designing cities to attract foreign tourists is equally important because tourism can strengthen both the economy and cultural identity of a place. Visitors are drawn to cities that are clean, accessible, distinctive, and easy to explore. If historic streets, museums, waterfronts, and public markets are carefully maintained, tourists will spend money in local businesses while also learning about the character of the city. More importantly, this kind of design does not have to serve outsiders at the expense of residents. A preserved old district, a lively pedestrian street, or a clear transport system benefits everyone. Good urban design can therefore turn local culture into something shared rather than something hidden.","chinese":"同時，把城市設計得能吸引外國遊客也同樣重要，因為旅遊業可以同時加強一個地方的經濟和文化身份。 遊客會被那些乾淨、交通便利、具獨特性，而且容易探索的城市所吸引。 如果歷史街道、博物館、海濱和公共市場得到細心維護，遊客便會在本地商店消費，同時也會了解這座城市的特色。 更重要的是，這種設計不必以犧牲居民利益為代價去服務外來者。 一個被保留下來的舊區、一條充滿活力的行人街，或者一個清晰易用的交通系統，都能惠及所有人。 因此，良好的城市設計可以把本地文化變成一種被共同分享的東西，而不是被隱藏起來的東西。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, I fully agree that cities should be made attractive for both local people and foreign tourists. When this is done well, a city becomes liveable for its residents and memorable for its visitors.","chinese":"總結來說，我完全同意城市應該被打造得對本地人和外國遊客都具有吸引力。 當這一點做得好時，一座城市便會成為居民宜居的地方，也會成為遊客難忘的地方。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"in my view","chinese":"在我看來"},{"english":"be designed to","chinese":"被設計成……"},{"english":"appeal to","chinese":"吸引；迎合"},{"english":"residents and international visitors","chinese":"居民和國際遊客"},{"english":"successful city","chinese":"成功的城市"},{"english":"not merely","chinese":"不只是"},{"english":"pass through","chinese":"經過"},{"english":"public home","chinese":"公共家園"},{"english":"open spaces","chinese":"開放空間"},{"english":"make daily life richer","chinese":"令日常生活更豐富"},{"english":"present the city confidently to","chinese":"自信地向……展示城市"},{"english":"the wider world","chinese":"更廣闊的世界"},{"english":"attractive urban design","chinese":"吸引人的城市設計"},{"english":"improve the lives of","chinese":"改善……的生活"},{"english":"local people","chinese":"本地人"},{"english":"green parks","chinese":"綠化公園"},{"english":"safe pavements","chinese":"安全的行人路"},{"english":"efficient public transport","chinese":"高效公共交通"},{"english":"welcoming community spaces","chinese":"友善宜人的社區空間"},{"english":"be more likely to","chinese":"更有可能"},{"english":"feel attached to","chinese":"對……有歸屬感"},{"english":"their surroundings","chinese":"他們周圍的環境"},{"english":"this matters because","chinese":"這很重要，因為……"},{"english":"experience a city through","chinese":"透過……體驗一座城市"},{"english":"major landmarks","chinese":"主要地標"},{"english":"daily routines","chinese":"日常習慣"},{"english":"commuting to work","chinese":"上班通勤"},{"english":"taking their children to playgrounds","chinese":"帶孩子去遊樂場"},{"english":"well-designed square","chinese":"設計良好的廣場"},{"english":"shade","chinese":"遮蔭"},{"english":"seating","chinese":"座位"},{"english":"nearby shops","chinese":"附近商店"},{"english":"social heart of","chinese":"……的社交核心"},{"english":"neighbourhood","chinese":"社區"},{"english":"somewhere to pause","chinese":"可以停下來的地方"},{"english":"talk, and breathe","chinese":"交談和放鬆"},{"english":"in this sense","chinese":"從這個意義上說"},{"english":"not a luxury","chinese":"不是奢侈品"},{"english":"public well-being","chinese":"公共福祉"},{"english":"at the same time","chinese":"同時"},{"english":"attract foreign tourists","chinese":"吸引外國遊客"},{"english":"equally important","chinese":"同樣重要"},{"english":"tourism","chinese":"旅遊業"},{"english":"strengthen both","chinese":"同時加強兩者"},{"english":"cultural identity","chinese":"文化身份"},{"english":"be drawn to","chinese":"被……吸引"},{"english":"clean, accessible, distinctive, and easy to explore","chinese":"清潔、容易到達、有特色和易於探索"},{"english":"easy to explore","chinese":"易於探索"},{"english":"historic streets","chinese":"歷史街道"},{"english":"museums","chinese":"博物館"},{"english":"waterfronts","chinese":"海濱地區"},{"english":"public markets","chinese":"公共市場"},{"english":"carefully maintained","chinese":"細心保養"},{"english":"spend money in","chinese":"在……消費"},{"english":"local businesses","chinese":"本地商戶"},{"english":"learn about","chinese":"了解"},{"english":"the character of the city","chinese":"城市特色"},{"english":"more importantly","chinese":"更重要的是"},{"english":"serve outsiders","chinese":"服務外來人士"},{"english":"at the expense of","chinese":"以犧牲……為代價"},{"english":"preserved old district","chinese":"保留下來的舊區"},{"english":"lively pedestrian street","chinese":"熱鬧的行人專用街道"},{"english":"clear transport system","chinese":"清晰的交通系統"},{"english":"benefits everyone","chinese":"令所有人受惠"},{"english":"good urban design","chinese":"良好的城市設計"},{"english":"turn local culture into","chinese":"將本地文化變成……"},{"english":"something shared rather than something hidden","chinese":"共享的東西，而不是隱藏的東西"},{"english":"be made attractive for","chinese":"被打造得對……有吸引力"},{"english":"local people and foreign tourists","chinese":"本地人和外國遊客"},{"english":"when this is done well","chinese":"當這件事做得好時"},{"english":"liveable for","chinese":"對……宜居"},{"english":"memorable for","chinese":"對……來說難忘"}]},"model-essay-63-ielts-opinion":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-63-ielts-opinion","essayKey":"opinion:63","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-63-ielts-opinion","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/opinions/EdmundBd9OP-Q63","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"Some people argue that key services, including shops, schools and commercial centres, should be moved away from central urban areas. I completely disagree, because this would reduce access to essential facilities and weaken the social and economic life of cities.","chinese":"有些人認為，主要服務設施，包括商店、學校和商業中心，應該搬離城市中心地區。 我完全不同意，因為這樣做會降低人們使用基本設施的便利性，並削弱城市的社會與經濟活力。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"The strongest reason for keeping these services in city centres is accessibility. Central districts are usually where transport networks meet, so people from different neighbourhoods can reach schools, shops and workplaces without travelling far. If these services were pushed to the outskirts, many residents would have to rely on cars or longer public-transport journeys. This would be especially harmful for families with young children, elderly people and low-income workers, who may not have the money or flexibility to travel long distances every day. For example, a parent who can now take a child to a nearby school and then walk to work might be forced into a costly commute. Relocation, therefore, would not make cities better organised; it would simply make daily life less convenient and less fair.","chinese":"把這些服務保留在市中心的最有力理由，是可及性。 中心地區通常是交通網絡匯聚的地方，因此來自不同社區的人可以不必長途跋涉，便到達學校、商店和工作場所。 如果這些服務被推到城市外圍，許多居民就不得不依賴汽車，或者花更長時間乘坐公共交通。 這對有年幼子女的家庭、長者和低收入工人尤其不利，因為他們未必有金錢或時間彈性每天長距離通勤。 例如，一位家長現在可以把孩子帶到附近的學校，然後步行上班；但如果服務搬離市中心，他可能會被迫承擔昂貴的通勤。 因此，搬遷這些服務並不會令城市規劃得更好；它只會讓日常生活變得更不方便，也更不公平。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"Another important point is that these services keep city centres alive. Shops, schools and commercial centres create foot traffic, employment and regular human interaction. Without them, central areas could become empty spaces that people pass through rather than places where communities actually function. Moving businesses to the edge of the city could also encourage car-dependent development, increasing congestion and pollution instead of reducing them. A healthy city centre should not be a silent monument of offices and roads; it should be a mixed, active environment where people can learn, work, buy goods and meet others in the same area.","chinese":"另一個重要觀點是，這些服務能讓市中心保持活力。 商店、學校和商業中心能帶來人流、就業機會，以及持續的人際互動。 如果沒有這些服務，中心地區可能會變成人們只是經過的空洞空間，而不再是真正有社區功能的地方。 把商業設施搬到城市邊緣，也可能鼓勵依賴汽車的發展模式，從而增加交通擠塞和污染，而不是減少它們。 一個健康的市中心不應該只是由辦公室和道路組成的沉默紀念碑；它應該是一個混合而活躍的環境，讓人們可以在同一區域學習、工作、購物和與他人相遇。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, I completely disagree that major services should be relocated out of city centres. Keeping them there protects accessibility, supports urban life and makes cities more practical for the people who use them every day.","chinese":"總結來說，我完全不同意主要服務應該搬離市中心。 把它們保留在市中心能保障可及性、支持城市生活，並讓城市對每天使用它的人來說更加實用。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"key services","chinese":"主要服務"},{"english":"including shops, schools and commercial centres","chinese":"包括商店、學校和商業中心"},{"english":"be moved away from","chinese":"從……遷走"},{"english":"central urban areas","chinese":"城市中心地區"},{"english":"reduce access to","chinese":"減少接觸……的機會"},{"english":"essential facilities","chinese":"必要設施"},{"english":"weaken the social and economic life of","chinese":"削弱……的社會和經濟生活"},{"english":"city centres","chinese":"市中心"},{"english":"the strongest reason for","chinese":"……的最有力原因"},{"english":"keeping these services","chinese":"保留這些服務"},{"english":"accessibility","chinese":"可達性；方便到達"},{"english":"central districts","chinese":"中心區"},{"english":"transport networks meet","chinese":"交通網絡交匯"},{"english":"different neighbourhoods","chinese":"不同社區"},{"english":"reach schools, shops and workplaces","chinese":"到達學校、商店和工作地點"},{"english":"without travelling far","chinese":"不用走很遠"},{"english":"be pushed to the outskirts","chinese":"被推到市郊"},{"english":"the outskirts","chinese":"市郊；外圍地區"},{"english":"rely on cars","chinese":"依賴汽車"},{"english":"public-transport journeys","chinese":"公共交通旅程"},{"english":"especially harmful for","chinese":"對……特別有害"},{"english":"families with young children","chinese":"有年幼子女的家庭"},{"english":"elderly people","chinese":"長者"},{"english":"low-income workers","chinese":"低收入工人"},{"english":"the money or flexibility to","chinese":"金錢或靈活性去……"},{"english":"travel long distances","chinese":"長途出行"},{"english":"nearby school","chinese":"附近的學校"},{"english":"walk to work","chinese":"步行上班"},{"english":"be forced into","chinese":"被迫陷入……"},{"english":"costly commute","chinese":"昂貴的通勤"},{"english":"relocation","chinese":"遷移；搬遷"},{"english":"better organised","chinese":"組織得更好"},{"english":"less convenient and less fair","chinese":"較不方便和較不公平"},{"english":"another important point","chinese":"另一個重要觀點"},{"english":"keep city centres alive","chinese":"令市中心保持活力"},{"english":"create foot traffic","chinese":"帶來人流"},{"english":"employment","chinese":"就業機會"},{"english":"regular human interaction","chinese":"恆常的人際互動"},{"english":"empty spaces","chinese":"空蕩的地方"},{"english":"pass through rather than","chinese":"只是經過而不是……"},{"english":"places where communities actually function","chinese":"社區真正運作的地方"},{"english":"move businesses to","chinese":"將商業遷到……"},{"english":"the edge of the city","chinese":"城市邊緣"},{"english":"car-dependent development","chinese":"依賴汽車的發展"},{"english":"increasing congestion and pollution","chinese":"增加交通擠塞和污染"},{"english":"instead of reducing them","chinese":"而不是減少它們"},{"english":"healthy city centre","chinese":"健康的市中心"},{"english":"silent monument","chinese":"沉默的紀念碑"},{"english":"offices and roads","chinese":"辦公室和道路"},{"english":"mixed, active environment","chinese":"多元而活躍的環境"},{"english":"buy goods","chinese":"購買商品"},{"english":"in the same area","chinese":"在同一區域"},{"english":"major services","chinese":"主要服務"},{"english":"be relocated out of","chinese":"從……遷出"},{"english":"protect accessibility","chinese":"保障可達性"},{"english":"support urban life","chinese":"支持城市生活"},{"english":"make cities more practical for","chinese":"令城市對……更實用"},{"english":"use them every day","chinese":"每天使用它們"}]},"model-essay-64-ielts-opinion":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-64-ielts-opinion","essayKey":"opinion:64","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-64-ielts-opinion","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/opinions/EdmundBd9OP-Q64","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"Urban planners often face difficult choices over how limited land should be used. Some people argue that public green spaces should take priority over new residential projects. I strongly disagree with this view, because affordable housing is a more basic urban need, and parks can still be protected through intelligent design.","chinese":"城市規劃者經常面對艱難的選擇，要決定有限的土地應該如何被使用。 有些人認為，公共綠化空間應該比新的住宅發展項目獲得更高優先次序。 我強烈不同意這個觀點，因為可負擔住房是更基本的城市需要，而公園仍然可以透過明智的設計得到保護。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"The main reason is that housing directly affects people's security, health and dignity. When cities fail to build enough homes, rents rise, families are forced into overcrowded flats, and young adults may be unable to live independently. These problems do not stay private; they spill into society through homelessness, long commutes and weaker community ties. For example, a teacher who cannot afford to live near school may spend hours travelling every day, arriving tired before the working day even begins. A pleasant park may improve that person's weekend, but a stable home shapes every day of their life. Therefore, where land is limited, residential development should come first.","chinese":"主要原因是，住房直接影響人們的安全感、健康和尊嚴。 當城市未能興建足夠住房時，租金會上升，家庭會被迫住進過度擠迫的單位，而年輕成年人也可能無法獨立生活。 這些問題不會只停留在私人層面；它們會透過無家可歸、漫長通勤和較弱的社區聯繫擴散到整個社會。 例如，一位負擔不起住在學校附近的教師，可能每天要花數小時通勤，甚至在工作日正式開始前已經感到疲憊。 一個舒適的公園也許能改善那個人的週末，但一個穩定的住所卻會塑造他們生活中的每一天。 因此，在土地有限的地方，住宅發展應該優先。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"Another reason is that prioritising housing does not mean sacrificing nature. The real issue is not whether cities should have homes or green spaces, but whether they can combine the two wisely. Modern housing projects can include small gardens, tree-lined streets, rooftop greenery and shared courtyards, giving residents access to nature without leaving badly needed homes unbuilt. By contrast, placing large parks above housing developments may create attractive scenery while ordinary workers are priced out of the city. A city that looks green but cannot house its people is like a beautifully painted door that no one can enter. Parks should therefore support housing policy, not outrank it.","chinese":"另一個原因是，優先考慮住房並不代表要犧牲自然。 真正的問題並不是城市應該擁有住房還是綠化空間，是它們能否明智地把兩者結合起來 現代住宅項目可以包括小花園、綠樹成蔭的街道、天台綠化和共享庭院，讓居民能夠接觸自然，同時又不會讓急需的住房無法興建。 相比之下，把大型公園置於住宅發展之上，可能會創造吸引人的景觀，卻同時令普通工人被高昂成本排擠出城市。 一座看起來綠意盎然卻無法安置居民的城市，就像一扇畫得很漂亮、但沒有人能夠進入的門 因此，公園應該配合住房政策，而不是凌駕於住房政策之上。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, I strongly disagree that cities should prioritise parks rather than housing developments. Green spaces are valuable, but housing is the foundation of a liveable city.","chinese":"總結來說，我強烈不同意城市應該優先考慮公園而不是住宅發展。 綠化空間固然有價值，但住房才是一座宜居城市的基礎。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"urban planners","chinese":"城市規劃師"},{"english":"face difficult choices over","chinese":"面對關於……的艱難選擇"},{"english":"limited land","chinese":"有限土地"},{"english":"be used","chinese":"被使用"},{"english":"public green spaces","chinese":"公共綠化空間"},{"english":"take priority over","chinese":"優先於……"},{"english":"residential projects","chinese":"住宅項目"},{"english":"strongly disagree with","chinese":"強烈不同意……"},{"english":"affordable housing","chinese":"可負擔住屋"},{"english":"basic urban need","chinese":"基本城市需要"},{"english":"be protected through","chinese":"透過……得到保護"},{"english":"intelligent design","chinese":"智慧設計"},{"english":"the main reason","chinese":"主要原因"},{"english":"directly affects","chinese":"直接影響"},{"english":"security, health and dignity","chinese":"安全感、健康和尊嚴"},{"english":"fail to build enough homes","chinese":"未能興建足夠住宅"},{"english":"rents rise","chinese":"租金上升"},{"english":"be forced into","chinese":"被迫住進；被迫進入"},{"english":"overcrowded flats","chinese":"擠迫單位"},{"english":"young adults","chinese":"年輕成年人"},{"english":"live independently","chinese":"獨立生活"},{"english":"spill into society","chinese":"擴散到社會層面"},{"english":"homelessness","chinese":"無家者問題；露宿問題"},{"english":"long commutes","chinese":"漫長通勤"},{"english":"weaker community ties","chinese":"較薄弱的社區聯繫"},{"english":"cannot afford to","chinese":"負擔不起去……"},{"english":"live near school","chinese":"住在學校附近"},{"english":"spend hours travelling","chinese":"花數小時通勤；花數小時出行"},{"english":"arriving tired","chinese":"疲倦地到達"},{"english":"working day","chinese":"工作日"},{"english":"pleasant park","chinese":"宜人的公園"},{"english":"shape every day of","chinese":"塑造……的每一天"},{"english":"stable home","chinese":"穩定住所"},{"english":"residential development","chinese":"住宅發展"},{"english":"come first","chinese":"放在首位"},{"english":"prioritising housing","chinese":"優先考慮住屋"},{"english":"sacrificing nature","chinese":"犧牲自然環境"},{"english":"the real issue","chinese":"真正問題"},{"english":"combine the two wisely","chinese":"明智地結合兩者"},{"english":"modern housing projects","chinese":"現代住宅項目"},{"english":"include small gardens","chinese":"包括小花園"},{"english":"tree-lined streets","chinese":"綠樹成蔭的街道"},{"english":"rooftop greenery","chinese":"天台綠化"},{"english":"shared courtyards","chinese":"共享庭院"},{"english":"give residents access to","chinese":"讓居民接觸到……"},{"english":"access to nature","chinese":"接觸自然的機會"},{"english":"badly needed homes","chinese":"急需的住宅"},{"english":"leaving homes unbuilt","chinese":"讓住宅沒有被興建"},{"english":"by contrast","chinese":"相比之下"},{"english":"place large parks above","chinese":"將大型公園置於……之上"},{"english":"housing developments","chinese":"住宅發展項目"},{"english":"attractive scenery","chinese":"吸引人的景色"},{"english":"ordinary workers","chinese":"普通工人"},{"english":"be priced out of the city","chinese":"因負擔不起而被迫離開城市"},{"english":"a beautifully painted door","chinese":"漆得漂亮的門"},{"english":"no one can enter","chinese":"沒有人能進入"},{"english":"support housing policy","chinese":"支持住屋政策"},{"english":"outrank it","chinese":"凌駕於其上"},{"english":"prioritise parks rather than","chinese":"優先考慮公園而不是……"},{"english":"green spaces are valuable","chinese":"綠化空間有價值"},{"english":"the foundation of","chinese":"……的基礎"},{"english":"liveable city","chinese":"宜居城市"}]},"model-essay-65-ielts-opinion":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-65-ielts-opinion","essayKey":"opinion:65","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-65-ielts-opinion","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/opinions/EdmundBd9OP-Q65","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"Translation software has become an ordinary part of daily life, and it can now convert many texts within seconds. However, I completely disagree that this makes foreign-language learning pointless, because a language is not only a tool for decoding words; it is also a way of thinking, building relationships and participating in another culture.","chinese":"翻譯軟件已經成為日常生活中普通的一部分，而且它現在能夠在數秒之內轉換許多文本 然而，我完全不同意這使外語學習變得毫無意義， 因為語言不只是解讀文字的工具；它也是一種思考方式、一種建立關係的方式，以及一種參與另一種文化的方式。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"The first reason is that computer translation, however convenient, cannot replace genuine human understanding. Many expressions carry tone, humour, politeness and cultural assumptions that are hidden behind the literal meaning of words. A device may translate a sentence accurately on the surface, but it may still miss whether the speaker is being warm, sarcastic, formal or rude. For example, a tourist who relies entirely on a translation app may understand a restaurant menu, but they may still fail to notice local etiquette or the emotional weight of certain phrases. In this sense, translation is like a map: useful for direction, but unable to recreate the full landscape. Learning the language allows people to engage with others more naturally and respectfully.","chinese":"第一個原因是，電腦翻譯無論多麼方便，都無法取代真正的人類理解。 許多表達都帶有語氣、幽默、禮貌和文化假設，而這些往往隱藏在文字的字面意思背後。 一部裝置也許能在表面上準確翻譯一句話，但它仍然可能錯過說話者究竟是親切、諷刺、正式還是無禮。 例如，一位完全依賴翻譯應用程式的遊客，也許能看懂餐廳菜單，但他們仍然可能無法察覺當地禮儀，或者某些短語背後的情感分量。 從這個意義上說，翻譯就像一張地圖：它對指引方向很有用，但無法重現完整的風景。 學習一種語言能讓人們更自然、更有尊重地與他人交流。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"Another reason is that studying a foreign language brings lasting educational and professional benefits. It trains people to think more flexibly, listen more carefully and express ideas with greater precision. These skills are valuable far beyond the language classroom. In the workplace, for instance, an employee who can speak directly to overseas clients is often more trusted than someone who must pause after every sentence to use a machine. Direct communication creates confidence, speed and a stronger human connection, especially in negotiations, interviews or teamwork. Even if technology improves, people who know another language will still have an advantage because they can communicate without a digital wall standing between them and others.","chinese":"另一個原因是，學習外語能帶來長遠的教育和職業好處。 它訓練人們更靈活地思考、更仔細地聆聽，並更精準地表達想法。 這些能力的價值遠遠超出了語言課堂本身。 例如，在職場中，一位能夠直接與海外客戶交談的員工，往往比一個每說完一句話都必須停下來使用機器的人更容易獲得信任。 直接溝通能建立信心、提升速度，並形成更強的人際連結，尤其是在談判、面試或團隊合作之中。 即使科技進步，懂得另一種語言的人仍然會有優勢，因為他們能夠溝通，而不需要一道數碼牆隔在自己和他人之間。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, I completely disagree that learning foreign languages is a waste of time. Computers can support communication, but they cannot replace the cultural understanding, personal confidence and human connection that language learning provides.","chinese":"總結來說，我完全不同意學習外語是浪費時間。 電腦可以支援溝通，但它們無法取代語言學習所帶來的文化理解、個人信心和人際連結"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"translation software","chinese":"翻譯軟件"},{"english":"an ordinary part of daily life","chinese":"日常生活中普通的一部分"},{"english":"convert many texts within seconds","chinese":"在數秒內轉換大量文字"},{"english":"completely disagree that","chinese":"完全不同意……"},{"english":"makes foreign-language learning pointless","chinese":"令外語學習變得毫無意義"},{"english":"not only a tool for","chinese":"不只是用來……的工具"},{"english":"decoding words","chinese":"解讀文字"},{"english":"a way of thinking","chinese":"思維方式"},{"english":"building relationships","chinese":"建立關係"},{"english":"participating in another culture","chinese":"參與另一種文化"},{"english":"computer translation","chinese":"電腦翻譯"},{"english":"however convenient","chinese":"無論多方便"},{"english":"genuine human understanding","chinese":"真正的人類理解"},{"english":"carry tone, humour, politeness and cultural assumptions","chinese":"承載語氣、幽默、禮貌和文化假設"},{"english":"cultural assumptions","chinese":"文化假設"},{"english":"hidden behind","chinese":"隱藏在……背後"},{"english":"literal meaning","chinese":"字面意思"},{"english":"translate a sentence accurately","chinese":"準確翻譯一句句子"},{"english":"on the surface","chinese":"表面上"},{"english":"miss whether","chinese":"錯過判斷是否……"},{"english":"warm, sarcastic, formal or rude","chinese":"親切、諷刺、正式或無禮"},{"english":"relies entirely on","chinese":"完全依賴"},{"english":"translation app","chinese":"翻譯應用程式"},{"english":"restaurant menu","chinese":"餐廳餐牌"},{"english":"fail to notice","chinese":"未能察覺"},{"english":"local etiquette","chinese":"當地禮儀"},{"english":"emotional weight","chinese":"情感分量"},{"english":"certain phrases","chinese":"某些短語"},{"english":"in this sense","chinese":"從這個意義上說"},{"english":"useful for direction","chinese":"對指引方向有用"},{"english":"unable to recreate","chinese":"無法重現"},{"english":"the full landscape","chinese":"完整景象"},{"english":"engage with others","chinese":"與他人交流互動"},{"english":"more naturally and respectfully","chinese":"更自然和更有禮地"},{"english":"studying a foreign language","chinese":"學習外語"},{"english":"lasting educational and professional benefits","chinese":"長遠的教育和專業好處"},{"english":"trains people to","chinese":"訓練人們去……"},{"english":"think more flexibly","chinese":"更靈活地思考"},{"english":"listen more carefully","chinese":"更細心聆聽"},{"english":"express ideas with greater precision","chinese":"更精準地表達想法"},{"english":"valuable far beyond","chinese":"價值遠超……"},{"english":"language classroom","chinese":"語言課堂"},{"english":"in the workplace","chinese":"在職場中"},{"english":"speak directly to","chinese":"直接與……交談"},{"english":"overseas clients","chinese":"海外客戶"},{"english":"more trusted than","chinese":"比……更受信任"},{"english":"pause after every sentence","chinese":"每句之後停頓"},{"english":"direct communication","chinese":"直接溝通"},{"english":"stronger human connection","chinese":"更強的人際連繫"},{"english":"especially in","chinese":"尤其在……"},{"english":"negotiations","chinese":"談判"},{"english":"even if technology improves","chinese":"即使科技進步"},{"english":"know another language","chinese":"懂另一種語言"},{"english":"have an advantage","chinese":"有優勢"},{"english":"without a digital wall","chinese":"沒有一道數碼牆"},{"english":"standing between them and others","chinese":"站在他們和別人之間"},{"english":"a waste of time","chinese":"浪費時間"},{"english":"support communication","chinese":"支援溝通"},{"english":"cultural understanding","chinese":"文化理解"},{"english":"personal confidence","chinese":"個人信心"},{"english":"human connection","chinese":"人際連繫"}]},"model-essay-66-ielts-opinion":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-66-ielts-opinion","essayKey":"opinion:66","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-66-ielts-opinion","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/opinions/EdmundBd9OP-Q66","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"Some researchers believe that, in the future, humanity may voluntarily settle on one shared global language. I believe this would be a negative development because language is not merely a tool for communication; it also carries culture, identity and social memory.","chinese":"一些研究人員認為，在未來，人類可能會自願地選擇使用一種共同的全球語言。 我認為這會是一種負面的發展，因為語言不僅僅是溝通工具；它也承載著文化、身份認同和社會記憶。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"The first problem is cultural loss. Every language contains a particular way of seeing the world, from family relationships and humour to local traditions and moral values. If people gradually abandon their mother tongues in favour of a single global language, these meanings would not simply move into a new linguistic container; many would disappear in translation. For example, traditional songs, proverbs and stories often depend on sounds, wordplay and historical references that cannot be fully recreated in another language. Once a language stops being used in homes, schools and public life, it becomes like an old library with the doors locked: the books may still exist, but ordinary people can no longer enter and live inside them.","chinese":"第一個問題是文化流失。 每一種語言都包含一種獨特的世界觀，從家庭關係和幽默感，到本地傳統和道德價值，皆包含其中。 如果人們逐漸放棄自己的母語，轉而使用一種單一的全球語言，這些意義並不會只是被轉移到一個新的語言容器中；許多意義會在翻譯中消失。 例如，傳統歌曲、諺語和故事往往依賴聲音、文字遊戲和歷史典故，而這些都無法在另一種語言中被完整重現。 一旦一種語言停止在家庭、學校和公共生活中被使用，它就會變得像一座門被鎖上的舊圖書館：書本也許仍然存在，但普通人已經無法再進入其中，並活在那些文字所承載的世界裡。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"Another serious concern is that a single global language would deepen inequality rather than remove it. The language chosen as the global standard would almost certainly belong to, or be controlled by, a group with existing political, economic or technological power. Those who already speak it would enjoy an immediate advantage in education, business and international institutions, while others would have to spend years catching up. This would turn communication into a gatekeeping system, where opportunities depend less on talent and more on early access to the dominant language. In this sense, linguistic uniformity would look fair on the surface but would quietly reward the already privileged.","chinese":"另一個嚴重的問題是，單一的全球語言會加深不平等，而不是消除不平等。 被選為全球標準的語言，幾乎肯定會屬於某個已經擁有政治、經濟或科技權力的群體，或者受到這個群體控制。 那些本來已經會說這種語言的人，會立即在教育、商業和國際機構中享有優勢，而其他人則需要花多年時間追趕。 這會把溝通變成一種把關制度，在這種制度下，機會較少取決於才能，而更多取決於一個人是否早早接觸到主導語言。 從這個角度來看，語言上的一致性表面上看似公平，但實際上會悄悄地獎賞那些本來已經處於優勢地位的人。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, the world would not become richer if everyone spoke only one global language. It would become flatter, poorer and less human. For this reason, I see this predicted change as a negative development.","chinese":"總結來說，如果每個人只說一種全球語言，世界並不會變得更豐富。 它會變得更單薄、更貧乏，也更缺少人性的厚度。 基於這個原因，我認為這種被預測的改變是一種負面的發展。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"some researchers believe that","chinese":"一些研究人員認為……"},{"english":"in the future","chinese":"在未來"},{"english":"humanity","chinese":"人類"},{"english":"voluntarily settle on","chinese":"自願選定"},{"english":"one shared global language","chinese":"一種共同全球語言"},{"english":"a negative development","chinese":"負面發展"},{"english":"not merely a tool for communication","chinese":"不只是溝通工具"},{"english":"carries culture, identity and social memory","chinese":"承載文化、身份和社會記憶"},{"english":"cultural loss","chinese":"文化流失"},{"english":"a particular way of seeing the world","chinese":"一種看世界的特定方式"},{"english":"family relationships","chinese":"家庭關係"},{"english":"local traditions","chinese":"本地傳統"},{"english":"moral values","chinese":"道德價值觀"},{"english":"abandon their mother tongues","chinese":"放棄母語"},{"english":"mother tongues","chinese":"母語"},{"english":"in favour of","chinese":"轉而支持；取而用"},{"english":"a single global language","chinese":"單一全球語言"},{"english":"linguistic container","chinese":"語言容器"},{"english":"disappear in translation","chinese":"在翻譯中消失"},{"english":"traditional songs","chinese":"傳統歌曲"},{"english":"proverbs and stories","chinese":"諺語和故事"},{"english":"depend on","chinese":"取決於；依賴"},{"english":"wordplay","chinese":"文字遊戲；雙關語"},{"english":"historical references","chinese":"歷史典故"},{"english":"be fully recreated","chinese":"被完全重現"},{"english":"in another language","chinese":"用另一種語言"},{"english":"once a language stops being used","chinese":"一旦一種語言停止被使用"},{"english":"public life","chinese":"公共生活"},{"english":"with the doors locked","chinese":"大門上鎖的"},{"english":"may still exist","chinese":"可能仍然存在"},{"english":"ordinary people","chinese":"普通人"},{"english":"live inside them","chinese":"活在其中"},{"english":"another serious concern","chinese":"另一個嚴重憂慮"},{"english":"deepen inequality","chinese":"加深不平等"},{"english":"rather than remove it","chinese":"而不是消除它"},{"english":"the global standard","chinese":"全球標準"},{"english":"almost certainly","chinese":"幾乎肯定"},{"english":"belong to","chinese":"屬於"},{"english":"be controlled by","chinese":"被……控制"},{"english":"existing political, economic or technological power","chinese":"現有政治、經濟或科技力量"},{"english":"enjoy an immediate advantage","chinese":"享有即時優勢"},{"english":"international institutions","chinese":"國際機構"},{"english":"spend years catching up","chinese":"花多年時間追趕"},{"english":"turn communication into","chinese":"將溝通變成……"},{"english":"gatekeeping system","chinese":"把關制度；門檻制度"},{"english":"depend less on","chinese":"較少取決於……"},{"english":"early access to","chinese":"早期接觸……的機會"},{"english":"dominant language","chinese":"主導語言"},{"english":"linguistic uniformity","chinese":"語言一致化"},{"english":"on the surface","chinese":"表面上"},{"english":"quietly reward","chinese":"悄悄獎勵"},{"english":"the already privileged","chinese":"已經享有特權的人"},{"english":"would not become richer","chinese":"不會變得更豐富"},{"english":"flatter, poorer and less human","chinese":"更平面、更貧乏、更少人情味"},{"english":"for this reason","chinese":"因此"},{"english":"predicted change","chinese":"預測中的轉變"}]},"model-essay-67-ielts-opinion":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-67-ielts-opinion","essayKey":"opinion:67","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-67-ielts-opinion","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/opinions/EdmundBd9OP-Q67","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"As digital devices become an established part of school life, some schools have begun to reduce, or even remove, handwriting lessons. I strongly believe that children should still be taught how to write with a pen, because handwriting supports early learning and remains a basic practical skill.","chinese":"隨著數位裝置成為學校生活中既定的一部分，一些學校已開始減少，甚至取消手寫課程 我堅信兒童仍然應該被教導如何用筆書寫，因為手寫能支持早期學習，並且仍然是一項基本的實用技能。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"The first reason is that handwriting helps children build a stronger foundation for literacy. When young learners form letters by hand, they do not simply copy shapes; they connect sound, movement, spelling and meaning at the same time. This slower physical process can make words feel more memorable than pressing keys on a screen. For example, a child who repeatedly writes difficult words such as “beautiful” or “necessary” is more likely to notice their letter patterns than a child who only types them and relies on autocorrect. In this sense, handwriting acts like a small workshop for the mind: it trains attention, patience and accuracy while children are still developing basic language skills.","chinese":"第一個原因是，手寫能幫助兒童為讀寫能力建立更堅實的基礎。 當年幼的學習者用手寫出字母時，他們不只是複製形狀；他們同時把聲音、動作、拼寫和意思連結起來。 這種較慢的身體動作過程，能使單字比在螢幕上按鍵更容易被記住。 例如，一個反覆書寫“beautiful”或“necessary”這類困難單字的孩子，比起只打字並依賴自動更正的孩子，更有可能注意到這些單字的字母模式。 從這個意義上說，手寫就像一個給大腦使用的小工作坊：當孩子仍在發展基本語言能力時，它訓練了專注力、耐心和準確性。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"Another important reason is that handwriting gives children independence in situations where technology is unavailable or inappropriate. Schools should prepare pupils not only for ideal digital environments, but also for ordinary real-life moments. A student may need to complete a paper exam, write a quick note, label a diagram, fill in a form or communicate when a device has run out of battery. If handwriting is abandoned completely, children may become unnecessarily dependent on screens for even the simplest written tasks. This would be a narrow form of progress, because a useful old skill would be lost without a good reason.","chinese":"另一個重要原因是，在科技不可用或不適合使用的情況下，手寫能給予兒童獨立能力。 學校不應只讓學生為理想的數位環境作準備，也應讓他們為普通的真實生活場景作準備 一名學生可能需要完成紙本考試、快速寫一張便條、為圖表加上標籤、填寫表格，或在裝置沒電時進行溝通。 如果手寫被完全放棄，兒童甚至在最簡單的書寫任務上，也可能變得不必要地依賴螢幕 這將會是一種狹隘的進步，因為一項有用的舊技能會在沒有充分理由的情況下被失去。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, children should definitely learn handwriting skills. Typing is essential in the modern world, but it should add to children’s abilities rather than replace handwriting altogether. A pen may look old-fashioned beside a tablet, but it still teaches control, concentration and self-reliance.","chinese":"總結來說，兒童絕對應該學習手寫技能。 打字在現代世界中是必要的，但它應該增加兒童的能力，而不是完全取代手寫。 一支筆在平板電腦旁邊也許看起來很老派，但它仍能教會人控制力、專注力和自立能力"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"digital devices","chinese":"數碼裝置"},{"english":"an established part of","chinese":"……中固定的一部分"},{"english":"school life","chinese":"學校生活"},{"english":"have begun to","chinese":"已開始去……"},{"english":"reduce, or even remove","chinese":"減少，甚至取消"},{"english":"handwriting lessons","chinese":"手寫課"},{"english":"strongly believe that","chinese":"強烈相信……"},{"english":"be taught how to","chinese":"被教導如何……"},{"english":"write with a pen","chinese":"用筆書寫"},{"english":"supports early learning","chinese":"支持早期學習"},{"english":"basic practical skill","chinese":"基本實用技能"},{"english":"build a stronger foundation for","chinese":"為……建立更穩固的基礎"},{"english":"literacy","chinese":"讀寫能力"},{"english":"young learners","chinese":"年幼學習者"},{"english":"form letters by hand","chinese":"用手寫出字母"},{"english":"do not simply","chinese":"不只是"},{"english":"copy shapes","chinese":"複製形狀"},{"english":"connect sound, movement, spelling and meaning","chinese":"連繫聲音、動作、串法和意思"},{"english":"at the same time","chinese":"同時"},{"english":"slower physical process","chinese":"較慢的身體動作過程"},{"english":"make words feel more memorable","chinese":"令文字感覺更容易記住"},{"english":"pressing keys on a screen","chinese":"在螢幕上按鍵"},{"english":"repeatedly writes","chinese":"反覆書寫"},{"english":"difficult words","chinese":"困難的字詞"},{"english":"be more likely to notice","chinese":"更有可能留意到"},{"english":"letter patterns","chinese":"字母組合規律"},{"english":"relies on autocorrect","chinese":"依賴自動更正"},{"english":"in this sense","chinese":"從這個意義上說"},{"english":"acts like","chinese":"像……一樣發揮作用"},{"english":"a small workshop for the mind","chinese":"大腦的小型工作室"},{"english":"trains attention, patience and accuracy","chinese":"訓練專注、耐性和準確度"},{"english":"basic language skills","chinese":"基本語言技能"},{"english":"gives children independence","chinese":"給予孩子獨立能力"},{"english":"unavailable or inappropriate","chinese":"無法使用或不適合使用"},{"english":"prepare pupils not only for","chinese":"讓學生不只是為……作好準備"},{"english":"ideal digital environments","chinese":"理想的數碼環境"},{"english":"ordinary real-life moments","chinese":"普通的現實生活時刻"},{"english":"complete a paper exam","chinese":"完成紙本考試"},{"english":"write a quick note","chinese":"寫一張簡短便條"},{"english":"label a diagram","chinese":"標註圖表"},{"english":"fill in a form","chinese":"填寫表格"},{"english":"run out of battery","chinese":"電量耗盡"},{"english":"be abandoned completely","chinese":"被完全放棄"},{"english":"become unnecessarily dependent on","chinese":"變得不必要地依賴……"},{"english":"the simplest written tasks","chinese":"最簡單的書寫任務"},{"english":"a narrow form of progress","chinese":"狹隘形式的進步"},{"english":"useful old skill","chinese":"有用的舊技能"},{"english":"be lost without a good reason","chinese":"無充分理由地失去"},{"english":"definitely learn","chinese":"絕對應該學習"},{"english":"handwriting skills","chinese":"手寫技能"},{"english":"essential in the modern world","chinese":"在現代世界中必不可少"},{"english":"add to children's abilities","chinese":"增加孩子的能力"},{"english":"rather than replace handwriting altogether","chinese":"而不是完全取代手寫"},{"english":"old-fashioned beside","chinese":"在……旁邊顯得過時"},{"english":"teaches control, concentration and self-reliance","chinese":"教導控制力、專注力和自立能力"}]},"model-essay-68-ielts-opinion":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-68-ielts-opinion","essayKey":"opinion:68","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-68-ielts-opinion","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/opinions/EdmundBd9OP-Q68","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"Culture is not simply a collection of food, festivals, and traditional clothing; it is also a way of thinking that is stored in language. I completely agree that a person cannot truly understand a country’s culture unless they speak its language, because language carries shared values and allows meaningful contact with local people.","chinese":"文化並不只是一系列食物、節日和傳統服飾；它也是一種儲存在語言之中的思維方式。 我完全同意，一個人若不會說一個國家的語言，就不能真正理解該國文化，因為語言承載著共同價值，也讓人能夠與當地人建立有意義的接觸。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"The first reason is that language contains meanings which are often invisible to outsiders. Words do not only describe objects; they express politeness, humour, hierarchy, emotion, and social expectations. If a visitor relies only on translation, these deeper meanings can easily disappear. For example, in many Asian cultures, indirect expressions are often used to show respect or avoid embarrassment. A foreigner may understand the literal meaning of a sentence, but without knowing the language, they may miss why something is said gently, indirectly, or even left unsaid. In this sense, language is like a cultural map: without it, people may see the landscape, but they cannot read the signs.","chinese":"第一個原因是，語言包含一些對外來者而言往往看不見的意義。 詞語不只是描述事物；它們也表達禮貌、幽默、階級、情感和社會期望。 如果一位訪客只依賴翻譯，這些更深層的意義便很容易消失。 例如，在許多亞洲文化中，間接的表達方式常被用來表示尊重或避免尷尬。 外國人或許能理解一句話的字面意思，但如果不懂該語言，他們便可能錯過為甚麼某些話要說得委婉、間接，甚至選擇不說出口。 從這個意義上說，語言就像一張文化地圖：沒有它，人們或許能看見風景，卻讀不懂其中的指示牌。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"Another reason is that real cultural understanding comes from interaction, not passive observation. A person can watch local ceremonies, eat local food, and visit famous buildings, but these experiences remain fairly shallow if they cannot communicate with residents in their own language. Speaking the language allows people to ask questions, understand jokes, join ordinary conversations, and notice how people behave in daily life. For instance, someone who speaks Spanish while living in Mexico is far more likely to understand family values, humour, and social warmth than someone who only observes these things from a distance. Language opens doors that sightseeing alone cannot open.","chinese":"另一個原因是，真正的文化理解來自互動，而不是被動觀察。 一個人可以觀看當地儀式、品嚐當地食物、參觀著名建築，但如果不能用當地人的語言與居民溝通，這些經歷仍然相當表面。 會說該語言讓人能夠提出問題、理解笑話、參與日常對話，並留意人們在日常生活中的行為方式 例如，一個住在墨西哥並會說西班牙語的人，比一個只是從遠處觀察這些事情的人，更有可能理解當地的家庭價值、幽默感和社交上的溫暖。 語言能打開一些單靠觀光無法打開的門。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, I fully agree that language is essential for understanding culture. Without it, people may gain impressions of a country, but those impressions remain incomplete. To understand a culture deeply, one must understand the language through which that culture breathes.","chinese":"總結來說，我完全同意語言對理解文化是不可或缺的。 沒有語言，人們也許能對一個國家形成一些印象，但這些印象仍然是不完整的。 要深入理解一種文化，一個人必須理解那種文化賴以呼吸的語言。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"not simply","chinese":"不只是"},{"english":"a collection of","chinese":"一系列；一組"},{"english":"traditional clothing","chinese":"傳統服飾"},{"english":"a way of thinking","chinese":"思維方式"},{"english":"be stored in","chinese":"儲存在……中"},{"english":"truly understand","chinese":"真正理解"},{"english":"a country's culture","chinese":"一個國家的文化"},{"english":"unless they speak","chinese":"除非他們會說……"},{"english":"carries shared values","chinese":"承載共同價值觀"},{"english":"meaningful contact with","chinese":"與……有意義的接觸"},{"english":"local people","chinese":"當地人"},{"english":"contains meanings","chinese":"包含意思"},{"english":"invisible to outsiders","chinese":"外人看不見的；外人難以察覺的"},{"english":"describe objects","chinese":"描述物件"},{"english":"express politeness","chinese":"表達禮貌"},{"english":"hierarchy","chinese":"等級關係"},{"english":"social expectations","chinese":"社會期望"},{"english":"rely only on","chinese":"只依賴……"},{"english":"translation","chinese":"翻譯"},{"english":"deeper meanings","chinese":"更深層的意思"},{"english":"can easily disappear","chinese":"很容易消失"},{"english":"Asian cultures","chinese":"亞洲文化"},{"english":"indirect expressions","chinese":"間接表達"},{"english":"be used to","chinese":"被用來……"},{"english":"show respect","chinese":"表示尊重"},{"english":"avoid embarrassment","chinese":"避免尷尬"},{"english":"literal meaning","chinese":"字面意思"},{"english":"miss why","chinese":"錯過理解為甚麼"},{"english":"be said gently","chinese":"被溫和地說出"},{"english":"left unsaid","chinese":"沒有說出口"},{"english":"in this sense","chinese":"從這個意義上說"},{"english":"cultural map","chinese":"文化地圖"},{"english":"see the landscape","chinese":"看見風景"},{"english":"read the signs","chinese":"看懂標記；理解暗示"},{"english":"real cultural understanding","chinese":"真正的文化理解"},{"english":"passive observation","chinese":"被動觀察"},{"english":"watch local ceremonies","chinese":"觀看當地儀式"},{"english":"visit famous buildings","chinese":"參觀著名建築"},{"english":"remain fairly shallow","chinese":"仍然相當膚淺"},{"english":"communicate with residents","chinese":"與居民溝通"},{"english":"in their own language","chinese":"用他們自己的語言"},{"english":"allows people to","chinese":"讓人們可以……"},{"english":"ask questions","chinese":"提問"},{"english":"understand jokes","chinese":"明白笑話"},{"english":"join ordinary conversations","chinese":"參與日常對話"},{"english":"notice how people behave","chinese":"留意人們如何行為"},{"english":"daily life","chinese":"日常生活"},{"english":"far more likely to","chinese":"更有可能"},{"english":"family values","chinese":"家庭價值觀"},{"english":"social warmth","chinese":"社交上的親切感"},{"english":"from a distance","chinese":"從遠處"},{"english":"opens doors","chinese":"打開機會之門"},{"english":"sightseeing alone","chinese":"單靠觀光"},{"english":"essential for","chinese":"對……必不可少"},{"english":"gain impressions of","chinese":"對……獲得印象"},{"english":"remain incomplete","chinese":"仍然不完整"},{"english":"understand a culture deeply","chinese":"深入理解一種文化"},{"english":"through which","chinese":"透過……"},{"english":"culture breathes","chinese":"文化得以呼吸；文化活起來"}]},"model-essay-69-ielts-opinion":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-69-ielts-opinion","essayKey":"opinion:69","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-69-ielts-opinion","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/opinions/EdmundBd9OP-Q69","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"Language learning has changed greatly in recent years, especially because learners can now communicate, study, and practise across borders. Some argue that true fluency is impossible unless a person has lived or worked in the country where that language is spoken. I completely disagree, because fluency depends far more on purposeful practice than on physical location.","chinese":"近年來，語言學習已經發生了很大變化，尤其是因為學習者如今可以跨越地域進行溝通、學習和練習。 有些人認為，除非一個人曾經在使用該語言的國家生活或工作，否則真正的流利是不可能達到的。 我完全不同意，因為流利程度更多取決於有目的的練習，而不是身處哪個地方。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"The strongest reason is that modern learners can build real communicative ability without moving abroad. Fluency is not produced by scenery; it is produced by repeated use, correction, and confidence under pressure. A learner who speaks the language every day, receives feedback from teachers, and engages with native-level materials can gradually train the mind to respond naturally rather than translate word by word. For example, a student in Hong Kong who joins an English debate club, takes online lessons with native speakers, reads English news, and watches interviews without subtitles is constantly exposed to natural rhythm, vocabulary, and pronunciation. Over time, this kind of deliberate routine can turn the language from a school subject into a living tool. Therefore, a well-designed learning environment at home can still lead to genuine fluency.","chinese":"最有力的原因是，現代學習者即使不移居海外，也能建立真正的溝通能力。 流利並不是由周圍環境本身產生的；它是由反覆使用、糾正，以及在壓力下建立起來的信心所產生的。 一個每天說該語言、從老師那裡獲得反饋，並接觸母語水平材料的學習者，可以逐漸訓練大腦自然回應，而不是逐字翻譯。 例如，一名香港學生如果參加英語辯論社、與母語人士上網課、閱讀英文新聞，並觀看沒有字幕的訪談，就會不斷接觸自然的語言節奏、詞彙和發音。 久而久之，這種有意識的日常練習可以把一門語言從學校科目轉化成一種真正生活中的工具。 因此，一個設計良好的本地學習環境，仍然可以帶來真正的流利程度。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"Another reason is that living in a country does not automatically create fluency. A person may spend years abroad but remain linguistically isolated if they mainly socialise with people from their own background, rely on translation apps, or avoid difficult conversations. In that case, the language is around them, but it never truly enters their daily thinking. By contrast, someone who has never left home but actively speaks, writes, listens, and reflects every day may progress much faster. Fluency grows when learners step into the language and use it actively; passive exposure alone is only background noise.","chinese":"另一個原因是，生活在某個國家並不會自動帶來語言流利。 一個人可能在海外生活多年，但如果他們主要與相同背景的人社交、依賴翻譯應用程式，或者避免有難度的對話，他們在語言上仍然可能是孤立的。 在這種情況下，語言雖然存在於他們周圍，卻從未真正進入他們的日常思維之中。 相比之下，一個從未離開本地、但每天主動說、寫、聽和反思的人，可能進步得更快。 當學習者真正走進語言並主動使用它時，流利程度才會增長；單靠被動接觸只不過是背景噪音。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, I completely disagree that living or working in a country is necessary for language fluency. The decisive factor is not where learners are, but how consistently and meaningfully they use the language.","chinese":"總結來說，我完全不同意在一個國家生活或工作是達到語言流利的必要條件。 決定性因素不是學習者身處哪裡，而是他們能否持續並有意義地使用該語言。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"language learning","chinese":"語言學習"},{"english":"changed greatly","chinese":"有很大改變"},{"english":"in recent years","chinese":"近年來"},{"english":"especially because","chinese":"尤其是因為"},{"english":"communicate, study, and practise","chinese":"溝通、學習和練習"},{"english":"across borders","chinese":"跨越國界"},{"english":"true fluency","chinese":"真正流利"},{"english":"is impossible unless","chinese":"除非……否則不可能"},{"english":"where that language is spoken","chinese":"使用該語言的地方"},{"english":"completely disagree","chinese":"完全不同意"},{"english":"depend far more on","chinese":"更大程度上取決於……"},{"english":"purposeful practice","chinese":"有目的的練習"},{"english":"physical location","chinese":"實際身處的地方"},{"english":"the strongest reason","chinese":"最有力的原因"},{"english":"build real communicative ability","chinese":"建立真正的溝通能力"},{"english":"without moving abroad","chinese":"不用移居外國"},{"english":"be produced by","chinese":"由……產生"},{"english":"repeated use","chinese":"重複使用"},{"english":"correction","chinese":"糾正"},{"english":"confidence under pressure","chinese":"在壓力下的信心"},{"english":"receive feedback from","chinese":"從……獲得回饋"},{"english":"engage with","chinese":"接觸並投入使用……"},{"english":"native-level materials","chinese":"母語者水平的材料"},{"english":"gradually train the mind to","chinese":"逐漸訓練大腦去……"},{"english":"respond naturally","chinese":"自然回應"},{"english":"rather than translate word by word","chinese":"而不是逐字翻譯"},{"english":"debate club","chinese":"辯論學會"},{"english":"online lessons","chinese":"網上課堂"},{"english":"native speakers","chinese":"母語者"},{"english":"without subtitles","chinese":"不看字幕"},{"english":"be constantly exposed to","chinese":"不斷接觸到……"},{"english":"natural rhythm","chinese":"自然節奏"},{"english":"vocabulary and pronunciation","chinese":"詞彙和發音"},{"english":"over time","chinese":"隨着時間過去"},{"english":"deliberate routine","chinese":"有意識安排的習慣"},{"english":"turn the language from","chinese":"將語言由……轉化為……"},{"english":"school subject","chinese":"學科"},{"english":"living tool","chinese":"活生生的工具"},{"english":"well-designed learning environment","chinese":"設計良好的學習環境"},{"english":"lead to","chinese":"帶來；通往"},{"english":"genuine fluency","chinese":"真正流利"},{"english":"living in a country","chinese":"住在一個國家"},{"english":"does not automatically create","chinese":"不會自動帶來"},{"english":"remain linguistically isolated","chinese":"在語言上仍然孤立"},{"english":"socialise with","chinese":"與……交往"},{"english":"people from their own background","chinese":"與自己背景相同的人"},{"english":"rely on translation apps","chinese":"依賴翻譯應用程式"},{"english":"avoid difficult conversations","chinese":"避免艱難的對話"},{"english":"in that case","chinese":"在那種情況下"},{"english":"around them","chinese":"在他們身邊"},{"english":"truly enters their daily thinking","chinese":"真正進入他們的日常思維"},{"english":"by contrast","chinese":"相比之下"},{"english":"actively speaks, writes, listens, and reflects","chinese":"主動說、寫、聽和反思"},{"english":"progress much faster","chinese":"進步快得多"},{"english":"step into the language","chinese":"走進那種語言"},{"english":"use it actively","chinese":"主動使用它"},{"english":"passive exposure alone","chinese":"單靠被動接觸"},{"english":"background noise","chinese":"背景噪音"},{"english":"living or working in","chinese":"在……生活或工作"},{"english":"necessary for","chinese":"對……必要"},{"english":"language fluency","chinese":"語言流利程度"},{"english":"decisive factor","chinese":"決定性因素"},{"english":"not where learners are, but how","chinese":"不是學習者身處何地，而是如何……"},{"english":"consistently and meaningfully","chinese":"持續而有意義地"}]},"model-essay-70-ielts-opinion":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-70-ielts-opinion","essayKey":"opinion:70","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-70-ielts-opinion","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/opinions/EdmundBd9OP-Q70","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"Violence has become a familiar feature of modern entertainment, from films and online videos to games and social media clips. I completely agree that such content encourages violence in society because it can normalise aggressive behaviour and give vulnerable audiences models to copy.","chinese":"暴力已成現代娛樂中常見的一部分，從電影、網上影片到遊戲和社交媒體短片皆是如此 我完全同意這類內容會助長社會中的暴力，因為它可能使攻擊性行為變得正常化，並為容易受影響的觀眾提供可模仿的模式。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"The first reason is that repeated exposure to violent scenes can make aggression seem ordinary rather than shocking. When viewers constantly see characters solving problems through threats, revenge, or physical force, violence may gradually lose its moral weight. This is especially harmful for young people, whose judgement and self-control are still developing. For example, a child who repeatedly watches heroes being rewarded for brutal behaviour may begin to see intimidation as a sign of strength rather than a serious social harm. Over time, this does not create violence in every individual, but it can lower society’s emotional resistance to it, like slowly turning down the volume on a warning alarm.","chinese":"第一個原因是，反覆接觸暴力場面會使攻擊行為看起來普通，而不再令人震驚。 當觀眾不斷看到角色透過威脅、報復或武力解決問題時，暴力可能會逐漸失去其道德上的嚴重性。 這對年輕人尤其有害，因為他們的判斷力和自我控制能力仍在發展之中。 例如，一個反覆觀看英雄因殘暴行為而受到獎賞的孩子，可能會開始把恐嚇視為力量的象徵，而不是嚴重的社會傷害。 長遠而言，這並不會使每個人都變得暴力，但它可能降低社會對暴力的情感抵抗力，就像慢慢把警報器的音量調低一樣。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"Another problem is that media violence often provides a script for real-life behaviour. Some people who already feel angry, isolated, or powerless may imitate what they have seen because the media offers them ready-made images of how to act. Online platforms make this risk even greater, as violent clips can spread quickly and be watched again and again without much context or adult guidance. For instance, teenagers involved in conflicts may copy aggressive language, fighting styles, or even the desire to record violent acts for attention. In this way, the media does not merely reflect violence; it can amplify it and make it more visible, dramatic, and tempting.","chinese":"另一個問題是，媒體暴力往往為現實生活中的行為提供了一套劇本。 一些本來已經感到憤怒、孤立或無力的人，可能會模仿他們所看到的內容，因為媒體為他們提供了現成的行為畫面。 網上平台使這種風險變得更大，因為暴力短片可以迅速傳播，並在缺乏充分背景或成人指導的情況下被反覆觀看。 例如，捲入衝突的青少年可能會模仿攻擊性的語言、打鬥方式，甚至模仿為了吸引注意而錄下暴力行為的想法。 這樣一來，媒體並不只是反映暴力；它還可能放大暴力，使其變得更加顯眼、更具戲劇性，也更具誘惑力。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, I fully agree that violence in the media promotes violence in society. While not every viewer becomes aggressive, repeated exposure can normalise harmful conduct and provide clear patterns for imitation, particularly among those who are young or emotionally unstable.","chinese":"總結來說，我完全同意媒體中的暴力會助長社會中的暴力。 雖然不是每一位觀眾都會變得具攻擊性，但反覆接觸這類內容可能會使有害行為正常化，並提供清晰的模仿模式，尤其是在年輕或情緒不穩定的人群之中。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"a familiar feature of","chinese":"……的常見特徵"},{"english":"modern entertainment","chinese":"現代娛樂"},{"english":"online videos","chinese":"網上影片"},{"english":"social media clips","chinese":"社交媒體短片"},{"english":"such content","chinese":"這類內容"},{"english":"encourage violence in society","chinese":"鼓勵社會中的暴力"},{"english":"normalise aggressive behaviour","chinese":"令攻擊性行為變得正常化"},{"english":"vulnerable audiences","chinese":"脆弱觀眾；易受影響的觀眾"},{"english":"models to copy","chinese":"可模仿的模式"},{"english":"repeated exposure to","chinese":"反覆接觸……"},{"english":"violent scenes","chinese":"暴力場面"},{"english":"make aggression seem ordinary","chinese":"令攻擊性看起來平常"},{"english":"rather than shocking","chinese":"而不是令人震驚"},{"english":"constantly see","chinese":"不斷看見"},{"english":"solving problems through","chinese":"透過……解決問題"},{"english":"threats, revenge, or physical force","chinese":"威脅、報復或武力"},{"english":"gradually lose its moral weight","chinese":"逐漸失去其道德重量"},{"english":"especially harmful for","chinese":"對……特別有害"},{"english":"judgement and self-control","chinese":"判斷力和自制力"},{"english":"still developing","chinese":"仍在發展中"},{"english":"be rewarded for","chinese":"因……而得到獎賞"},{"english":"brutal behaviour","chinese":"殘暴行為"},{"english":"begin to see","chinese":"開始視……為"},{"english":"intimidation","chinese":"恐嚇"},{"english":"a sign of strength","chinese":"強大的表現"},{"english":"serious social harm","chinese":"嚴重社會傷害"},{"english":"over time","chinese":"隨着時間過去"},{"english":"in every individual","chinese":"在每個人身上"},{"english":"lower society's emotional resistance to","chinese":"降低社會對……的情感抵抗"},{"english":"turn down the volume on","chinese":"調低……的音量"},{"english":"warning alarm","chinese":"警報"},{"english":"media violence","chinese":"媒體暴力"},{"english":"provide a script for","chinese":"為……提供劇本"},{"english":"real-life behaviour","chinese":"現實生活中的行為"},{"english":"feel angry, isolated, or powerless","chinese":"感到憤怒、孤立或無力"},{"english":"imitate what they have seen","chinese":"模仿他們所見過的事"},{"english":"ready-made images","chinese":"現成的畫面"},{"english":"how to act","chinese":"如何行動"},{"english":"online platforms","chinese":"網上平台"},{"english":"make this risk even greater","chinese":"令這種風險更大"},{"english":"spread quickly","chinese":"快速傳播"},{"english":"again and again","chinese":"一次又一次"},{"english":"without much context","chinese":"缺乏足夠背景脈絡"},{"english":"adult guidance","chinese":"成人指導"},{"english":"teenagers involved in conflicts","chinese":"捲入衝突的青少年"},{"english":"copy aggressive language","chinese":"模仿攻擊性語言"},{"english":"fighting styles","chinese":"打鬥方式"},{"english":"violent acts","chinese":"暴力行為"},{"english":"for attention","chinese":"為了博取注意"},{"english":"in this way","chinese":"以這種方式"},{"english":"merely reflect","chinese":"只是反映"},{"english":"amplify it","chinese":"將它放大"},{"english":"make it more visible","chinese":"令它更顯眼"},{"english":"dramatic and tempting","chinese":"戲劇化而具誘惑力"},{"english":"promotes violence in society","chinese":"助長社會中的暴力"},{"english":"not every viewer becomes aggressive","chinese":"不是每個觀眾都會變得具攻擊性"},{"english":"harmful conduct","chinese":"有害行為"},{"english":"clear patterns for imitation","chinese":"清晰的模仿模式"},{"english":"particularly among","chinese":"尤其是在……之中"},{"english":"emotionally unstable","chinese":"情緒不穩定的"}]},"model-essay-71-ielts-opinion":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-71-ielts-opinion","essayKey":"opinion:71","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-71-ielts-opinion","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/opinions/EdmundBd9OP-Q71","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"The private lives of famous people have become an increasingly profitable target for newspapers, television programmes, and online platforms. Some argue that celebrities and media personalities should accept this as the price of fame and lose any claim to privacy. I completely disagree with this view, because public recognition does not remove a person’s basic human rights, and intrusive reporting often creates harm without serving any genuine public interest.","chinese":"名人的私人生活已經成為報紙、電視節目和網上平台越來越有利可圖的目標。 有些人認為，名人和媒體人物應該把這視為成名的代價，並失去任何主張私隱的權利。 我完全不同意這種觀點，因為公眾知名度並不會剝奪一個人的基本人權，而侵擾性的報道往往會造成傷害，卻沒有服務任何真正的公共利益。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"The strongest reason is that famous people are still human beings, not public property. Although they may choose careers that place them in the spotlight, this does not mean every part of their life should be exposed. Constant surveillance can damage their mental health, relationships, and sense of safety. For example, a singer may be willing to discuss a new album in an interview, but that does not justify photographers following their children to school or publishing private medical details. When the press crosses that line, journalism stops being information and becomes harassment. A society that allows this is not protecting free speech; it is feeding public curiosity at another person’s expense.","chinese":"最有力的理由是，名人仍然是人，而不是公共財產。 儘管他們可能選擇了使自己處於聚光燈下的職業，但這並不意味著他們生活中的每一部分都應該被公開。 持續的監視可能會損害他們的心理健康、人際關係和安全感。 例如，一位歌手可能願意在訪問中談論新專輯，但這並不能合理化攝影師跟蹤他們的孩子上學，或公開他們的私人醫療資料。 當新聞媒體越過這條界線時，新聞便不再是資訊，而變成騷擾。 一個容許這種情況的社會，並不是在保護言論自由；它只是在以犧牲他人為代價來滿足公眾的好奇心。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"Moreover, removing privacy from famous people can encourage a shallow and irresponsible media culture. Instead of reporting on work, talent, public behaviour, or serious wrongdoing, media outlets may focus on rumours, private arguments, or embarrassing photographs simply because they attract attention. This lowers the quality of public discussion and teaches audiences to confuse gossip with news. Of course, the press should be allowed to investigate celebrities when their actions affect the public, such as criminal behaviour, fraud, or hypocrisy in public campaigns. However, that is very different from claiming that famous people deserve no privacy at all.","chinese":"此外，剝奪名人的私隱可能會助長一種膚淺而不負責任的媒體文化。 媒體機構可能不再報道工作、才華、公眾行為或嚴重不當行為，而是只因為謠言、私人爭執或尷尬照片能吸引注意，便把焦點放在這些內容上。 這會降低公共討論的質素，並使觀眾把八卦和新聞混為一談。 當然，當名人的行為影響公眾時，例如涉及犯罪行為、欺詐，或在公共宣傳中表裡不一，新聞媒體應該被允許調查他們。 然而，這與聲稱名人完全不應享有私隱是非常不同的。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, I completely disagree that famous people in the media should have no right to privacy. Fame may bring public attention, but it should never turn a person’s private life into an open hunting ground for the press. A fair society must protect both responsible journalism and basic human dignity.","chinese":"總結來說，我完全不同意媒體中的名人不應享有私隱權這種說法。 名氣可能會帶來公眾關注，但它絕不應該把一個人的私人生活變成新聞媒體可以公開狩獵的場地。 一個公平的社會必須同時保護負責任的新聞工作和基本的人性尊嚴。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"private lives of famous people","chinese":"名人私生活"},{"english":"increasingly profitable target","chinese":"越來越有利可圖的目標"},{"english":"newspapers, television programmes, and online platforms","chinese":"報章、電視節目和網上平台"},{"english":"media personalities","chinese":"媒體名人"},{"english":"the price of fame","chinese":"成名的代價"},{"english":"lose any claim to privacy","chinese":"失去任何私隱權主張"},{"english":"completely disagree with","chinese":"完全不同意……"},{"english":"public recognition","chinese":"公眾知名度"},{"english":"remove a person's basic human rights","chinese":"取消一個人的基本人權"},{"english":"intrusive reporting","chinese":"侵擾式報道"},{"english":"creates harm","chinese":"造成傷害"},{"english":"genuine public interest","chinese":"真正的公眾利益"},{"english":"the strongest reason","chinese":"最有力的原因"},{"english":"human beings","chinese":"人；有血有肉的人"},{"english":"public property","chinese":"公共財產"},{"english":"choose careers that","chinese":"選擇……的職業"},{"english":"place them in the spotlight","chinese":"令他們成為焦點"},{"english":"every part of their life","chinese":"他們生活的每一部分"},{"english":"be exposed","chinese":"被公開"},{"english":"constant surveillance","chinese":"持續監視"},{"english":"mental health","chinese":"精神健康"},{"english":"sense of safety","chinese":"安全感"},{"english":"be willing to","chinese":"願意去……"},{"english":"discuss a new album","chinese":"談論新專輯"},{"english":"in an interview","chinese":"在訪問中"},{"english":"justify photographers following","chinese":"使攝影師跟蹤……變得合理"},{"english":"publishing private medical details","chinese":"公開私人醫療資料"},{"english":"private medical details","chinese":"私人醫療資料"},{"english":"cross that line","chinese":"越過那條界線"},{"english":"journalism","chinese":"新聞工作"},{"english":"stops being information","chinese":"不再是提供資訊"},{"english":"becomes harassment","chinese":"變成騷擾"},{"english":"free speech","chinese":"言論自由"},{"english":"feed public curiosity","chinese":"滿足公眾好奇心"},{"english":"at another person's expense","chinese":"以犧牲別人為代價"},{"english":"removing privacy from","chinese":"剝奪……的私隱"},{"english":"shallow and irresponsible media culture","chinese":"膚淺而不負責任的媒體文化"},{"english":"instead of reporting on","chinese":"而不是報道……"},{"english":"media outlets","chinese":"傳媒機構"},{"english":"public behaviour","chinese":"公開行為"},{"english":"serious wrongdoing","chinese":"嚴重不當行為"},{"english":"focus on rumours","chinese":"專注於謠言"},{"english":"private arguments","chinese":"私人爭吵"},{"english":"embarrassing photographs","chinese":"令人尷尬的相片"},{"english":"simply because","chinese":"只是因為"},{"english":"attract attention","chinese":"吸引注意"},{"english":"lower the quality of","chinese":"降低……的質素"},{"english":"public discussion","chinese":"公共討論"},{"english":"confuse gossip with news","chinese":"將八卦與新聞混淆"},{"english":"of course","chinese":"當然"},{"english":"be allowed to investigate","chinese":"被允許調查"},{"english":"actions affect the public","chinese":"行為影響公眾"},{"english":"criminal behaviour","chinese":"犯罪行為"},{"english":"fraud","chinese":"欺詐"},{"english":"hypocrisy in public campaigns","chinese":"公開宣傳活動中的虛偽"},{"english":"very different from","chinese":"與……很不同"},{"english":"deserve no privacy at all","chinese":"完全不應有私隱"},{"english":"have no right to privacy","chinese":"沒有私隱權"},{"english":"bring public attention","chinese":"帶來公眾關注"},{"english":"should never turn","chinese":"絕不應將……變成"},{"english":"private life","chinese":"私生活"},{"english":"open hunting ground for the press","chinese":"供傳媒任意追逐的場所"},{"english":"responsible journalism","chinese":"負責任的新聞工作"},{"english":"basic human dignity","chinese":"基本人性尊嚴"}]},"model-essay-72-ielts-opinion":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-72-ielts-opinion","essayKey":"opinion:72","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-72-ielts-opinion","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/opinions/EdmundBd9OP-Q72","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"The rapid growth of digital platforms has changed how people follow news, music, and entertainment. Some therefore argue that radio is approaching the end of its life. I completely disagree with this view, because radio still serves practical needs that online media cannot fully replace and it can adapt successfully to the digital age.","chinese":"數位平台的快速發展已經改變了人們獲取新聞、音樂和娛樂內容的方式。 因此，有些人認為收音機正逐漸走向生命的盡頭。 我完全不同意這個觀點，因為收音機仍然滿足一些網上媒體無法完全取代的實際需要，而且它能夠成功適應數位時代。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"First, radio remains valuable because it allows people to receive information without giving their full visual attention. Online media is powerful, but much of it depends on screens, scrolling, and constant interaction. Radio, by contrast, can be used while people are driving, cooking, exercising, or working. A driver travelling through heavy traffic, for instance, can listen to a traffic bulletin immediately, whereas checking a website or watching a news clip would be unsafe and impractical. This everyday convenience gives radio a lasting role. It is not merely an old device from the past, but a simple and reliable companion in situations where screens become a burden.","chinese":"首先，收音機仍然有價值，因為它讓人們能夠在不需要全神貫注觀看螢幕的情況下接收資訊。 網上媒體固然強大，但其中很多內容都依賴螢幕、滑動操作和持續互動。 相比之下，人們在駕車、煮食、運動或工作時仍然可以使用收音機。 例如，一位正在繁忙交通中駕駛的人可以即時收聽交通消息；相反，查看網站或觀看新聞短片則既不安全，也不實際。 這種日常便利性賦予了收音機一個持久的角色。 它不僅僅是一件來自過去的舊設備，而是在螢幕變成負擔的情況下，一個簡單而可靠的陪伴"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"Second, the development of online media can actually strengthen radio rather than destroy it. Modern radio is no longer confined to a physical receiver in the corner of a room. Stations can stream live programmes, upload interviews, share short audio clips, and reach listeners through mobile phones. More importantly, radio often provides a local and human voice that large online platforms struggle to offer. During community events, bad weather, or public emergencies, people may still value a familiar presenter who speaks directly to their area and explains what is happening in plain language. This sense of immediacy and trust is difficult to replace.","chinese":"第二，網上媒體的發展其實可以強化收音機，而不是摧毀它。 現代收音機不再局限於房間角落裡的一部實體接收器。 電台可以直播節目、上載訪問、分享短音訊片段，並透過手機接觸聽眾。 更重要的是，收音機往往能提供一種本地而具有人情味的聲音，而這正是大型網上平台難以提供的。 在社區活動、惡劣天氣或公共緊急情況期間，人們仍然可能重視一位熟悉的主持人，因為他能直接向他們所在的地區說話，並用簡明的語言解釋正在發生的事情。 這種即時感和信任感是很難被取代的。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, I completely disagree that radio has no future. Although online media has changed people’s habits, radio remains useful because it is convenient, accessible, adaptable, and locally relevant. Its form may continue to evolve, but its core purpose will survive.","chinese":"總結來說，我完全不同意收音機沒有未來這種說法。 儘管網上媒體已經改變了人們的習慣，收音機仍然有用，因為它方便、容易接觸、具適應力，並且與本地生活息息相關。 它的形式可能會繼續演變，但它的核心功能將會繼續存在。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"rapid growth of","chinese":"……的快速增長"},{"english":"digital platforms","chinese":"數碼平台"},{"english":"changed how people","chinese":"改變了人們如何……"},{"english":"follow news","chinese":"追蹤新聞"},{"english":"entertainment","chinese":"娛樂"},{"english":"therefore argue that","chinese":"因此認為……"},{"english":"approaching the end of its life","chinese":"快將走到盡頭"},{"english":"completely disagree with","chinese":"完全不同意……"},{"english":"serves practical needs","chinese":"滿足實際需要"},{"english":"online media","chinese":"網上媒體"},{"english":"fully replace","chinese":"完全取代"},{"english":"adapt successfully to","chinese":"成功適應……"},{"english":"the digital age","chinese":"數碼時代"},{"english":"remains valuable","chinese":"仍然有價值"},{"english":"receive information","chinese":"接收資料"},{"english":"without giving their full visual attention","chinese":"不用完全投入視覺注意力"},{"english":"visual attention","chinese":"視覺注意力"},{"english":"powerful","chinese":"強大；有影響力"},{"english":"depends on","chinese":"依賴"},{"english":"screens, scrolling, and constant interaction","chinese":"螢幕、滑動瀏覽和持續互動"},{"english":"by contrast","chinese":"相比之下"},{"english":"while people are driving","chinese":"當人們駕車時"},{"english":"exercising","chinese":"做運動"},{"english":"heavy traffic","chinese":"交通非常擠塞"},{"english":"traffic bulletin","chinese":"交通消息"},{"english":"immediately","chinese":"即時"},{"english":"whereas","chinese":"而；然而"},{"english":"checking a website","chinese":"查看網站"},{"english":"news clip","chinese":"新聞短片"},{"english":"unsafe and impractical","chinese":"不安全且不實際"},{"english":"everyday convenience","chinese":"日常便利"},{"english":"lasting role","chinese":"持久的角色"},{"english":"merely an old device","chinese":"只是舊時代的裝置"},{"english":"from the past","chinese":"來自過去"},{"english":"simple and reliable companion","chinese":"簡單而可靠的陪伴"},{"english":"in situations where","chinese":"在……的情況下"},{"english":"become a burden","chinese":"成為負擔"},{"english":"the development of","chinese":"……的發展"},{"english":"actually strengthen","chinese":"其實加強"},{"english":"rather than destroy it","chinese":"而不是摧毀它"},{"english":"modern radio","chinese":"現代電台廣播"},{"english":"no longer confined to","chinese":"不再局限於……"},{"english":"physical receiver","chinese":"實體收音機"},{"english":"in the corner of a room","chinese":"在房間角落"},{"english":"stream live programmes","chinese":"串流直播節目"},{"english":"upload interviews","chinese":"上載訪問"},{"english":"share short audio clips","chinese":"分享音頻短片"},{"english":"reach listeners through","chinese":"透過……接觸聽眾"},{"english":"mobile phones","chinese":"手提電話"},{"english":"more importantly","chinese":"更重要的是"},{"english":"local and human voice","chinese":"本地而有人情味的聲音"},{"english":"large online platforms","chinese":"大型網上平台"},{"english":"struggle to offer","chinese":"難以提供"},{"english":"community events","chinese":"社區活動"},{"english":"bad weather","chinese":"惡劣天氣"},{"english":"public emergencies","chinese":"公共緊急情況"},{"english":"familiar presenter","chinese":"熟悉的主持人"},{"english":"speaks directly to","chinese":"直接向……說話"},{"english":"their area","chinese":"他們所屬地區"},{"english":"in plain language","chinese":"用淺白語言"},{"english":"sense of immediacy","chinese":"即時感"},{"english":"trust","chinese":"信任"},{"english":"difficult to replace","chinese":"難以取代"},{"english":"has no future","chinese":"沒有未來"},{"english":"changed people's habits","chinese":"改變了人們的習慣"},{"english":"convenient, accessible, adaptable, and locally relevant","chinese":"方便、容易接觸、適應力強，並切合本地需要"},{"english":"locally relevant","chinese":"切合本地需要"},{"english":"continue to evolve","chinese":"繼續演變"},{"english":"core purpose","chinese":"核心目的"},{"english":"will survive","chinese":"會繼續存在"}]},"model-essay-73-ielts-opinion":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-73-ielts-opinion","essayKey":"opinion:73","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-73-ielts-opinion","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/opinions/EdmundBd9OP-Q73","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"In recent years, online streaming platforms have changed the way people watch films and series. Because viewers can now enjoy a huge range of content at home, some argue that cinemas will eventually disappear. I completely disagree with this view because cinemas offer a social and sensory experience that streaming cannot fully replace, and they remain commercially important for the film industry.","chinese":"近年來，網上串流平台改變了人們觀看電影和劇集的方式。 由於觀眾現在可以在家中欣賞大量不同類型的內容，有些人認為電影院最終會消失。 我完全不同意這個觀點，因為電影院提供的是一種社交和感官體驗，而串流平台無法完全取代，而且電影院對電影產業來說在商業上仍然十分重要。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"The strongest reason cinemas will survive is that watching a film on a large screen is fundamentally different from watching it on a phone, laptop or television. A cinema is not just a place where people consume a story; it is a place where sound, scale and atmosphere work together. When the lights go down and the audience becomes silent, even an ordinary film can feel more memorable. By contrast, home viewing is often interrupted by messages, household noise or the temptation to pause. For example, action films, fantasy films and horror films are usually far more powerful in a theatre, where the visual effects and sound design can be experienced as intended. This unique atmosphere gives cinemas a role that online platforms cannot simply copy.","chinese":"電影院會繼續存在的最有力原因是，在大銀幕上看電影，和在手機、手提電腦或電視上看電影，本質上是完全不同的體驗。 電影院不只是一個讓人觀看故事的地方；它是一個讓聲音、畫面規模和氣氛共同發揮作用的空間。 當燈光暗下來，而觀眾安靜下來時，即使是一部普通的電影也可以變得更加令人難忘。 相比之下，在家中觀影經常會被訊息、家中的噪音，或想要暫停影片的誘惑所打斷。 例如，動作片、奇幻片和恐怖片通常在戲院中更具震撼力，因為觀眾能按照創作者原本設計的方式體驗視覺效果和聲音設計。 這種獨特的氣氛賦予了電影院一種網上平台無法輕易複製的角色。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"Another reason is that cinemas remain valuable to both filmmakers and audiences as public cultural spaces. Major studios still use theatrical releases to create excitement, media attention and a sense of occasion. A film that becomes successful in cinemas often gains prestige before it moves to streaming services. Moreover, many people treat going to the cinema as a shared activity, not merely a way to pass time. Families, couples and friends often go there to mark birthdays, weekends or special releases. If cinemas disappeared, society would lose one of the few entertainment spaces where strangers can enjoy the same story together.","chinese":"另一個原因是，作為公共文化空間，電影院對電影製作人和觀眾來說仍然具有價值。 大型電影公司仍然利用院線上映來製造期待感、媒體關注和一種盛事感。 一部在電影院取得成功的電影，往往會在轉到串流平台之前先獲得聲望。 此外，許多人把去電影院看電影視為一種共同參與的活動，而不僅僅是消磨時間的方法。 家庭、情侶和朋友經常會去電影院慶祝生日、度過週末，或觀看特別上映的電影。 如果電影院消失，社會將會失去少數能讓陌生人一起欣賞同一個故事的娛樂空間之一。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, although streaming services have made home entertainment more convenient, they will not cause cinemas to close completely. Cinemas will continue to exist because they provide immersion, community and cultural value that private screens cannot match.","chinese":"總結來說，雖然串流服務讓家庭娛樂變得更加方便，但它們不會導致電影院完全關閉。 電影院將會繼續存在，因為它們提供了私人螢幕無法相比的沉浸感、群體感和文化價值"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"in recent years","chinese":"近年來"},{"english":"online streaming platforms","chinese":"網上串流平台"},{"english":"changed the way","chinese":"改變了……的方式"},{"english":"films and series","chinese":"電影和劇集"},{"english":"huge range of content","chinese":"大量不同類型的內容"},{"english":"at home","chinese":"在家中"},{"english":"eventually disappear","chinese":"最終消失"},{"english":"completely disagree with","chinese":"完全不同意……"},{"english":"social and sensory experience","chinese":"社交和感官體驗"},{"english":"fully replace","chinese":"完全取代"},{"english":"remain commercially important","chinese":"在商業上仍然重要"},{"english":"film industry","chinese":"電影業"},{"english":"the strongest reason","chinese":"最有力的原因"},{"english":"will survive","chinese":"會繼續存在"},{"english":"large screen","chinese":"大銀幕"},{"english":"fundamentally different from","chinese":"與……有根本不同"},{"english":"consume a story","chinese":"消費一個故事"},{"english":"sound, scale and atmosphere","chinese":"聲音、規模感和氣氛"},{"english":"work together","chinese":"共同發揮作用"},{"english":"the lights go down","chinese":"燈光暗下來"},{"english":"the audience becomes silent","chinese":"觀眾安靜下來"},{"english":"ordinary film","chinese":"普通電影"},{"english":"feel more memorable","chinese":"感覺更難忘"},{"english":"by contrast","chinese":"相比之下"},{"english":"home viewing","chinese":"在家觀看"},{"english":"be interrupted by","chinese":"被……打斷"},{"english":"household noise","chinese":"家中噪音"},{"english":"the temptation to pause","chinese":"想暫停的誘惑"},{"english":"action films","chinese":"動作片"},{"english":"fantasy films","chinese":"奇幻電影"},{"english":"horror films","chinese":"恐怖片"},{"english":"far more powerful","chinese":"有震撼力得多"},{"english":"in a theatre","chinese":"在戲院裏"},{"english":"visual effects","chinese":"視覺效果"},{"english":"sound design","chinese":"聲音設計"},{"english":"be experienced as intended","chinese":"按原意被體驗"},{"english":"unique atmosphere","chinese":"獨特氣氛"},{"english":"cannot simply copy","chinese":"不能簡單複製"},{"english":"remain valuable to","chinese":"對……仍然有價值"},{"english":"filmmakers and audiences","chinese":"電影製作人和觀眾"},{"english":"public cultural spaces","chinese":"公共文化空間"},{"english":"major studios","chinese":"大型電影公司"},{"english":"theatrical releases","chinese":"戲院上映"},{"english":"create excitement","chinese":"製造興奮感"},{"english":"media attention","chinese":"媒體關注"},{"english":"a sense of occasion","chinese":"一種特別時刻的感覺"},{"english":"become successful in cinemas","chinese":"在戲院取得成功"},{"english":"gain prestige","chinese":"獲得聲望"},{"english":"move to streaming services","chinese":"轉到串流服務"},{"english":"moreover","chinese":"此外"},{"english":"going to the cinema","chinese":"去戲院看電影"},{"english":"shared activity","chinese":"共同活動"},{"english":"merely a way to pass time","chinese":"只是打發時間的方式"},{"english":"mark birthdays","chinese":"慶祝生日"},{"english":"special releases","chinese":"特別上映的電影"},{"english":"society would lose","chinese":"社會會失去"},{"english":"one of the few","chinese":"少數……之一"},{"english":"entertainment spaces","chinese":"娛樂空間"},{"english":"strangers","chinese":"陌生人"},{"english":"enjoy the same story together","chinese":"一起欣賞同一個故事"},{"english":"home entertainment","chinese":"家庭娛樂"},{"english":"more convenient","chinese":"更方便"},{"english":"close completely","chinese":"完全結業"},{"english":"continue to exist","chinese":"繼續存在"},{"english":"provide immersion","chinese":"提供沉浸感"},{"english":"community and cultural value","chinese":"社群和文化價值"},{"english":"private screens","chinese":"私人螢幕"},{"english":"cannot match","chinese":"不能媲美"}]},"model-essay-74-ielts-opinion":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-74-ielts-opinion","essayKey":"opinion:74","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-74-ielts-opinion","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/opinions/EdmundBd9OP-Q74","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"Television remains a powerful commercial medium, especially in the hours after school, when many children are tired, hungry, and looking for entertainment. I firmly believe that advertisements deliberately aimed at young viewers should be prohibited, because children are not mature enough to recognise persuasive techniques and because such marketing places unnecessary pressure on families.","chinese":"電視仍然是一種強大的商業媒介，尤其是在放學後的時段，當許多孩子感到疲倦、飢餓，並正在尋找娛樂時。 我堅定地認為，刻意針對年輕觀眾的廣告應該被禁止，因為兒童尚未成熟到足以識別說服技巧，而且這類行銷會給家庭帶來不必要的壓力。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"The strongest reason for banning these advertisements is that children are especially easy to influence. Unlike adults, they often cannot separate information from persuasion, so a colourful commercial can feel less like a sales pitch and more like a promise of happiness. Advertisers know this, and they frequently use cartoon characters, catchy songs, exaggerated excitement, and bright images to turn ordinary products into objects of desire. For example, a child who sees an advert for a sugary cereal or a new toy may not think about nutrition, cost, or whether the product is necessary; they simply feel that they must have it. This is not fair competition. It is the deliberate use of adult marketing skills against people whose judgement is still developing.","chinese":"禁止這些廣告最有力的理由是，兒童特別容易受到影響。 與成年人不同，他們往往無法區分資訊與說服，因此一個色彩繽紛的廣告可能不像是在推銷商品，而更像是在承諾幸福。 廣告商深知這一點，因此他們經常使用卡通人物、朗朗上口的歌曲、誇張的興奮感和鮮明的畫面，把普通產品變成令人渴望的物品。 例如，一個看到含糖早餐穀物或新玩具廣告的孩子，可能不會思考營養、成本，或這件產品是否必要；他們只是覺得自己一定要擁有它。 這並不是公平競爭。這是刻意把成年人的行銷技巧用在判斷力仍在發展中的人身上。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"Another important concern is the pressure these advertisements create inside the home. When children are repeatedly encouraged to want particular snacks, toys, or fast-food meals, parents are often forced into an unnecessary battle. They either give in and spend money on things the family may not need, or they refuse and face arguments, disappointment, and guilt. This problem is even sharper for low-income families, where every small purchase matters. In addition, many child-focused advertisements promote short-term pleasure rather than healthy habits, which can quietly normalise overconsumption. Childhood should not become a marketplace in which family routines are constantly interrupted by commercial demands.","chinese":"另一個重要的擔憂，是這些廣告在家庭內部製造的壓力。 當兒童被反覆鼓勵去想要某些零食、玩具或快餐時，父母往往會被迫陷入一場不必要的爭戰。 他們要麼讓步，花錢購買家庭可能並不需要的東西；要麼拒絕，然後面對爭吵、失望和內疚。 對低收入家庭來說，這個問題更加尖銳，因為每一筆小額開支都很重要。 此外，許多以兒童為對象的廣告推廣的是短暫的快樂，而不是健康的習慣，這可能會悄悄地使過度消費變得正常化。 童年不應該變成一個市場，讓家庭日常不斷被商業需求打斷。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, advertisements aimed at children should not be allowed. Young viewers deserve protection from manipulation, and parents should not have to compete with carefully designed marketing campaigns in their own living rooms.","chinese":"總結來說，針對兒童的廣告不應該被允許。 年輕觀眾應該受到保護，免受操控，而父母也不應該在自己的客廳裡與精心設計的行銷活動競爭。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"remains a powerful commercial medium","chinese":"仍然是強大的商業媒介"},{"english":"commercial medium","chinese":"商業媒介"},{"english":"especially in the hours after school","chinese":"尤其是在放學後的時段"},{"english":"looking for entertainment","chinese":"尋找娛樂"},{"english":"firmly believe that","chinese":"堅信……"},{"english":"advertisements deliberately aimed at","chinese":"蓄意針對……的廣告"},{"english":"young viewers","chinese":"年輕觀眾"},{"english":"should be prohibited","chinese":"應被禁止"},{"english":"mature enough to","chinese":"成熟到足以……"},{"english":"recognise persuasive techniques","chinese":"識別說服技巧"},{"english":"persuasive techniques","chinese":"說服技巧"},{"english":"such marketing","chinese":"這類營銷"},{"english":"place unnecessary pressure on","chinese":"對……造成不必要壓力"},{"english":"the strongest reason for","chinese":"……的最有力原因"},{"english":"banning these advertisements","chinese":"禁止這些廣告"},{"english":"especially easy to influence","chinese":"特別容易受影響"},{"english":"unlike adults","chinese":"不像成年人"},{"english":"separate information from persuasion","chinese":"分辨資料和說服"},{"english":"colourful commercial","chinese":"色彩鮮艷的廣告"},{"english":"sales pitch","chinese":"推銷說辭"},{"english":"a promise of happiness","chinese":"幸福的承諾"},{"english":"advertisers","chinese":"廣告商"},{"english":"frequently use","chinese":"經常使用"},{"english":"cartoon characters","chinese":"卡通人物"},{"english":"catchy songs","chinese":"易記的歌曲"},{"english":"exaggerated excitement","chinese":"誇張的興奮感"},{"english":"bright images","chinese":"鮮明圖像"},{"english":"turn ordinary products into","chinese":"將普通產品變成……"},{"english":"objects of desire","chinese":"渴望得到的東西"},{"english":"sugary cereal","chinese":"高糖早餐穀物"},{"english":"a new toy","chinese":"新玩具"},{"english":"think about nutrition","chinese":"考慮營養"},{"english":"whether the product is necessary","chinese":"產品是否必要"},{"english":"must have it","chinese":"必須擁有它"},{"english":"fair competition","chinese":"公平競爭"},{"english":"deliberate use of","chinese":"蓄意使用……"},{"english":"adult marketing skills","chinese":"成人營銷技巧"},{"english":"against people whose judgement is still developing","chinese":"對判斷力仍在發展的人"},{"english":"judgement is still developing","chinese":"判斷力仍在發展"},{"english":"another important concern","chinese":"另一個重要憂慮"},{"english":"inside the home","chinese":"在家庭內"},{"english":"be repeatedly encouraged to","chinese":"反覆被鼓勵去……"},{"english":"particular snacks","chinese":"特定零食"},{"english":"fast-food meals","chinese":"快餐餐點"},{"english":"be forced into","chinese":"被迫陷入……"},{"english":"unnecessary battle","chinese":"不必要的爭執"},{"english":"give in","chinese":"讓步"},{"english":"spend money on","chinese":"花錢在……上"},{"english":"refuse","chinese":"拒絕"},{"english":"face arguments, disappointment, and guilt","chinese":"面對爭吵、失望和內疚"},{"english":"low-income families","chinese":"低收入家庭"},{"english":"every small purchase matters","chinese":"每一筆小開支都重要"},{"english":"in addition","chinese":"此外"},{"english":"child-focused advertisements","chinese":"針對兒童的廣告"},{"english":"short-term pleasure","chinese":"短暫快樂"},{"english":"rather than healthy habits","chinese":"而不是健康習慣"},{"english":"normalise overconsumption","chinese":"令過度消費變得正常化"},{"english":"overconsumption","chinese":"過度消費"},{"english":"childhood","chinese":"童年"},{"english":"become a marketplace","chinese":"變成市場"},{"english":"family routines","chinese":"家庭日常"},{"english":"be constantly interrupted by","chinese":"不斷被……打斷"},{"english":"commercial demands","chinese":"商業要求"},{"english":"be allowed","chinese":"被允許"},{"english":"deserve protection from","chinese":"值得受到保護，免受……"},{"english":"manipulation","chinese":"操控"},{"english":"compete with","chinese":"與……競爭"},{"english":"carefully designed marketing campaigns","chinese":"精心設計的營銷活動"},{"english":"in their own living rooms","chinese":"在自己的客廳裏"}]},"model-essay-75-ielts-opinion":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-75-ielts-opinion","essayKey":"opinion:75","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-75-ielts-opinion","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/opinions/EdmundBd9OP-Q75","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"Foreign films are now watched widely in many parts of the world, and some people fear that they weaken local traditions. I completely disagree with this view. Rather than damaging local culture, foreign films can broaden people’s understanding of the world and even encourage local artists to value their own cultural identity more deeply.","chinese":"外國電影如今在世界許多地方被廣泛觀看，而有些人擔心它們會削弱本地傳統。 我完全不同意這個觀點。 外國電影並不會破壞本地文化，反而能拓闊人們對世界的理解，甚至鼓勵本地藝術工作者更深入地重視自身的文化身份。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"The first reason is that exposure to foreign films does not automatically make people abandon their own customs. Culture is not a fragile glass ornament that breaks the moment it touches something new; it is a living system that can absorb outside influences while still keeping its own character. When people watch films from other countries, they may learn about different languages, family values, social problems, and ways of life. This comparison can actually make them more aware of what is special about their own society. For example, a young person who watches Japanese or Korean films may notice differences in manners, humour, or family relationships, but this does not mean they will stop valuing local festivals, food, or traditions. In many cases, contrast makes cultural identity clearer, not weaker.","chinese":"第一個原因是，接觸外國電影並不會自動使人們放棄自己的習俗。 文化並不是一件脆弱的玻璃裝飾品，一接觸新事物就會破碎；它是一個有生命力的系統，能夠吸收外來影響，同時仍然保留自身特色。 當人們觀看來自其他國家的電影時，他們可能會了解不同的語言、家庭價值觀、社會問題和生活方式。 這種比較其實可以使他們更加意識到自己社會的獨特之處。 例如，一個觀看日本或韓國電影的年輕人，可能會注意到禮儀、幽默感或家庭關係方面的差異，但這並不意味著他們會停止重視本地節日、食物或傳統。 在許多情況下，對比會使文化身份更加清晰，而不是更加薄弱。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"Another important point is that foreign films can push local film industries to improve. If audiences are exposed only to domestic productions, local filmmakers may become comfortable and repetitive. However, when they compete with international films, they are often forced to tell better stories, improve production quality, and present local culture in a more attractive way. For instance, a director may choose to use local dialects, historical settings, or traditional music more carefully in order to give the film a distinct voice. In this sense, foreign films can act as a spark rather than a threat.","chinese":"另一個重要觀點是，外國電影可以推動本地電影業進步。 如果觀眾只接觸本地作品，本地電影製作人可能會變得安於現狀並不斷重複。 然而，當他們與國際電影競爭時，他們往往會被迫講述更好的故事、提升製作品質，並以更具吸引力的方式呈現本地文化。 例如，一位導演可能會選擇更仔細地使用本地方言、歷史背景或傳統音樂，以賦予電影一種鮮明的聲音。 從這個意義上說，外國電影可以是一種火花，而不是一種威脅。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, I completely disagree that foreign films have a negative impact on local culture. They widen people’s perspectives and can motivate local creators to protect and present their culture more powerfully.","chinese":"總結來說，我完全不同意外國電影會對本地文化產生負面影響這一說法。 它們能拓闊人們的視野，並能激勵本地創作者更有力地保護和呈現自己的文化。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"foreign films","chinese":"外國電影"},{"english":"be watched widely","chinese":"被廣泛觀看"},{"english":"local traditions","chinese":"本地傳統"},{"english":"weaken local traditions","chinese":"削弱本地傳統"},{"english":"completely disagree with","chinese":"完全不同意……"},{"english":"rather than damaging","chinese":"而不是損害……"},{"english":"local culture","chinese":"本地文化"},{"english":"broaden people's understanding of","chinese":"擴闊人們對……的理解"},{"english":"encourage local artists to","chinese":"鼓勵本地藝術家去……"},{"english":"cultural identity","chinese":"文化身份"},{"english":"more deeply","chinese":"更深入地"},{"english":"exposure to","chinese":"接觸……"},{"english":"does not automatically","chinese":"不會自動；不一定會"},{"english":"abandon their own customs","chinese":"放棄自己的習俗"},{"english":"fragile glass ornament","chinese":"脆弱的玻璃擺設"},{"english":"the moment","chinese":"一……就……"},{"english":"something new","chinese":"新事物"},{"english":"living system","chinese":"活的系統"},{"english":"absorb outside influences","chinese":"吸收外來影響"},{"english":"keep its own character","chinese":"保持自身特色"},{"english":"films from other countries","chinese":"來自其他國家的電影"},{"english":"family values","chinese":"家庭價值觀"},{"english":"social problems","chinese":"社會問題"},{"english":"ways of life","chinese":"生活方式"},{"english":"this comparison","chinese":"這種比較"},{"english":"make them more aware of","chinese":"令他們更意識到……"},{"english":"what is special about","chinese":"……有何特別之處"},{"english":"own society","chinese":"自己的社會"},{"english":"Japanese or Korean films","chinese":"日本或韓國電影"},{"english":"notice differences in","chinese":"注意到……上的差異"},{"english":"manners","chinese":"禮貌；行為禮儀"},{"english":"humour","chinese":"幽默"},{"english":"family relationships","chinese":"家庭關係"},{"english":"stop valuing","chinese":"停止重視"},{"english":"local festivals","chinese":"本地節日"},{"english":"in many cases","chinese":"在很多情況下"},{"english":"contrast","chinese":"對比"},{"english":"clearer, not weaker","chinese":"更清晰，而不是更薄弱"},{"english":"push local film industries to improve","chinese":"推動本地電影業進步"},{"english":"local film industries","chinese":"本地電影業"},{"english":"be exposed only to","chinese":"只接觸到……"},{"english":"domestic productions","chinese":"本地製作"},{"english":"local filmmakers","chinese":"本地電影製作人"},{"english":"become comfortable and repetitive","chinese":"變得安於現狀和重複"},{"english":"compete with","chinese":"與……競爭"},{"english":"international films","chinese":"國際電影"},{"english":"be forced to","chinese":"被迫去……"},{"english":"tell better stories","chinese":"講出更好的故事"},{"english":"improve production quality","chinese":"提高製作質素"},{"english":"present local culture","chinese":"呈現本地文化"},{"english":"in a more attractive way","chinese":"以更吸引人的方式"},{"english":"local dialects","chinese":"本地方言"},{"english":"historical settings","chinese":"歷史背景"},{"english":"traditional music","chinese":"傳統音樂"},{"english":"give the film a distinct voice","chinese":"令電影有獨特聲音"},{"english":"act as a spark","chinese":"起激發作用"},{"english":"rather than a threat","chinese":"而不是威脅"},{"english":"have a negative impact on","chinese":"對……有負面影響"},{"english":"widen people's perspectives","chinese":"擴闊人們的視野"},{"english":"motivate local creators to","chinese":"推動本地創作者去……"},{"english":"protect and present their culture","chinese":"保護並呈現他們的文化"},{"english":"more powerfully","chinese":"更有力地"}]},"model-essay-76-ielts-opinion":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-76-ielts-opinion","essayKey":"opinion:76","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-76-ielts-opinion","flashDeckId":"","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"Historical dramas occupy an interesting place between education and entertainment. Some people argue that any film drawn from real events must reproduce the past with total precision. I disagree with this view because absolute accuracy is unrealistic in cinema and would often weaken the historical understanding that such films can create.","chinese":"歷史劇情片處於教育與娛樂之間一個相當有趣的位置。 有些人認為，任何取材自真實事件的電影，都必須以完全精確的方式重現過去。 我不同意這種看法，因為在電影中做到絕對準確並不現實，而且往往會削弱這類電影所能創造的歷史理解。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"First, complete accuracy is almost impossible once history is turned into a two-hour narrative. Historical events usually involve missing records, conflicting accounts, and countless minor details that no screenwriter can verify or include. If a director had to show every conversation, journey and background figure exactly as it happened, the film would become painfully slow and almost impossible to follow. For example, a film about a revolution may need to combine several minor politicians into one character or compress months of negotiation into a few scenes. These changes do not betray history when they help viewers grasp its main forces without getting lost in its dust.","chinese":"首先，一旦歷史被轉化成一個兩小時的敘事，完全準確便幾乎是不可能的。 歷史事件通常涉及缺失的記錄、互相矛盾的說法，以及無數編劇既無法核實也無法全部包含的細微細節。 如果導演必須把每一段對話、每一段旅程和每一位背景人物都完全按照真實情況呈現出來，電影就會變得極其沉悶，並且幾乎難以理解。 例如，一部關於革命的電影，可能需要把幾位次要政治人物合併成一個角色，或者把數月的談判濃縮成幾個場景。 當這些改動能幫助觀眾掌握歷史的主要力量，而不是迷失在瑣碎細節之中時，它們並不算是背叛歷史。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"Second, films are valuable because they make the past emotionally accessible. Many people first become interested in history through a gripping story, not through an archive or a textbook. Dramatic dialogue, selective scenes and carefully shaped characters can make distant events feel human, especially for younger audiences who might otherwise see history as a dry list of dates. A film that captures fear, courage and moral conflict may leave a stronger educational impression than one that merely records every factual detail. Therefore, the standard should be historical responsibility rather than perfect reproduction: filmmakers should not reverse causes, whitewash crimes or invent outcomes, but they should be free to simplify the path by which the story is told.","chinese":"第二，電影之所以有價值，是因為它們能讓過去在情感上變得更容易接近。 許多人最初對歷史產生興趣，是透過一個扣人心弦的故事，而不是透過檔案或教科書。 富有戲劇性的對話、經過選取的場景，以及被精心塑造的人物，可以讓遙遠的事件顯得更有人情味，尤其是對年輕觀眾而言；否則，他們可能只會把歷史看成一串枯燥的日期。 一部能捕捉恐懼、勇氣和道德衝突的電影，可能比一部只是記錄每一個事實細節的電影留下更深刻的教育印象。 因此，標準應該是歷史責任，而不是完美重現：電影製作者不應顛倒因果、美化罪行或虛構結果，但他們應該有自由去簡化故事被講述的方式。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, I do not agree that historical films ought to be completely accurate. Total accuracy is neither achievable nor desirable in a cinematic form. What matters more is that such films preserve the essential truth of events while using the language of cinema to make history vivid and meaningful.","chinese":"總結來說，我不同意歷史電影應該完全準確。 在電影形式中，完全準確既無法實現，也未必值得追求。 更重要的是，這類電影應該保留事件的核心真實，同時運用電影語言使歷史變得生動而有意義。"}],"vocabulary":[]},"model-essay-77-ielts-opinion":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-77-ielts-opinion","essayKey":"opinion:77","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-77-ielts-opinion","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/opinions/EdmundBd9OP-Q77","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"Advertising is one of the most powerful tools in modern business, and fast food brands use it especially well. While some people argue that every company should be free to promote its products, I believe that fast food companies should not be allowed to advertise because their products can damage public health and their marketing often targets vulnerable consumers.","chinese":"廣告是現代商業中最強大的工具之一，而快餐品牌尤其善於運用它。 雖然有些人認為每間公司都應該有自由推廣自己的產品， 但我認為快餐公司不應該被允許賣廣告，因為它們的產品可能損害公共健康，而且它們的營銷往往針對容易受影響的消費者。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"The strongest reason for banning fast food advertising is that it encourages unhealthy eating habits on a large scale. Fast food is usually high in salt, sugar, and fat, so repeated exposure to attractive advertisements can make people see it as a normal part of daily life rather than an occasional choice. This is particularly harmful because advertising does not simply provide information; it creates desire. For example, a busy worker who constantly sees posters and online promotions for fried food is more likely to buy a quick meal instead of preparing something healthier. Over time, this can contribute to obesity, heart disease, and other diet-related problems. Therefore, restricting these advertisements would be a reasonable way to protect public health.","chinese":"禁止快餐廣告最有力的原因是，它會大規模地鼓勵不健康的飲食習慣。 快餐通常含有高鹽、高糖和高脂肪，因此反覆接觸吸引人的廣告，可能會使人們把它視為日常生活中的正常部分，而不是偶爾的選擇。 這尤其有害，因為廣告並不只是提供資訊；它會製造慾望。 例如，一位忙碌的上班族如果經常看到炸物的海報和網上促銷，就更有可能買一份快捷餐，而不是準備一些更健康的食物。 長遠而言，這可能導致肥胖、心臟病以及其他與飲食相關的健康問題。 因此，限制這些廣告會是保護公共健康的一種合理方式。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"Another important point is that fast food marketing often influences children and teenagers, who may not have the maturity to judge advertising critically. Bright colours, cartoon characters, celebrity endorsements, and catchy slogans can make unhealthy food seem exciting and harmless. Although companies may claim that they are only exercising their commercial freedom, this freedom should not come at the expense of young people’s well-being. Society already limits the advertising of some harmful products, such as cigarettes, because profit should not be placed above health. Fast food may not be as dangerous as tobacco, but the same basic principle applies: when a product creates serious social costs, advertising it should be controlled.","chinese":"另一個重要觀點是，快餐營銷經常影響兒童和青少年，而他們未必有足夠成熟度去批判性地判斷廣告。 鮮艷的顏色、卡通人物、名人代言和朗朗上口的標語，可能會令不健康的食物看起來令人興奮而且無害。 儘管公司可能聲稱自己只是在行使商業自由，但這種自由不應以年輕人的福祉作為代價 社會已經限制一些有害產品的廣告，例如香煙，因為利潤不應被置於健康之上。 快餐或許不像煙草那樣危險，但同樣的基本原則仍然適用：當一種產品造成嚴重的社會成本時，它的廣告就應該受到控制。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, I strongly believe that fast food companies should not have the right to advertise freely. Business freedom is important, but public health is more important, especially when children and long-term eating habits are involved.","chinese":"總結來說，我強烈認為快餐公司不應該擁有自由賣廣告的權利。 商業自由很重要，但公共健康更為重要，尤其是當涉及兒童和長期飲食習慣時。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"advertising","chinese":"廣告"},{"english":"one of the most powerful tools","chinese":"最強大的工具之一"},{"english":"modern business","chinese":"現代商業"},{"english":"fast food brands","chinese":"快餐品牌"},{"english":"be free to","chinese":"可自由去……"},{"english":"promote its products","chinese":"推廣其產品"},{"english":"not be allowed to","chinese":"不應被允許去……"},{"english":"damage public health","chinese":"損害公共健康"},{"english":"vulnerable consumers","chinese":"弱勢消費者"},{"english":"the strongest reason for","chinese":"……的最有力原因"},{"english":"banning fast food advertising","chinese":"禁止快餐廣告"},{"english":"unhealthy eating habits","chinese":"不健康的飲食習慣"},{"english":"on a large scale","chinese":"大規模地"},{"english":"high in salt, sugar, and fat","chinese":"鹽、糖和脂肪含量高"},{"english":"repeated exposure to","chinese":"反覆接觸……"},{"english":"attractive advertisements","chinese":"吸引人的廣告"},{"english":"a normal part of daily life","chinese":"日常生活中正常的一部分"},{"english":"rather than an occasional choice","chinese":"而不是偶爾的選擇"},{"english":"particularly harmful","chinese":"特別有害"},{"english":"provide information","chinese":"提供資料"},{"english":"create desire","chinese":"製造慾望"},{"english":"busy worker","chinese":"忙碌的上班族"},{"english":"constantly sees","chinese":"不斷看見"},{"english":"online promotions","chinese":"網上推廣"},{"english":"fried food","chinese":"油炸食物"},{"english":"be more likely to","chinese":"更有可能"},{"english":"buy a quick meal","chinese":"買一頓快捷餐"},{"english":"instead of preparing","chinese":"而不是準備……"},{"english":"something healthier","chinese":"較健康的東西"},{"english":"over time","chinese":"隨着時間過去"},{"english":"contribute to","chinese":"導致；促成"},{"english":"obesity","chinese":"肥胖"},{"english":"heart disease","chinese":"心臟病"},{"english":"diet-related problems","chinese":"與飲食有關的問題"},{"english":"restricting these advertisements","chinese":"限制這些廣告"},{"english":"a reasonable way to","chinese":"……的合理方法"},{"english":"protect public health","chinese":"保障公共健康"},{"english":"another important point","chinese":"另一個重要觀點"},{"english":"fast food marketing","chinese":"快餐推廣"},{"english":"influence children and teenagers","chinese":"影響兒童和青少年"},{"english":"have the maturity to","chinese":"有成熟程度去……"},{"english":"judge advertising critically","chinese":"批判地判斷廣告"},{"english":"bright colours","chinese":"鮮艷顏色"},{"english":"cartoon characters","chinese":"卡通人物"},{"english":"celebrity endorsements","chinese":"名人代言"},{"english":"catchy slogans","chinese":"易記的口號"},{"english":"make unhealthy food seem","chinese":"令不健康食物看起來……"},{"english":"exciting and harmless","chinese":"令人興奮而無害"},{"english":"claim that","chinese":"聲稱"},{"english":"exercising their commercial freedom","chinese":"行使其商業自由"},{"english":"commercial freedom","chinese":"商業自由"},{"english":"come at the expense of","chinese":"以犧牲……為代價"},{"english":"young people's well-being","chinese":"年輕人的身心健康"},{"english":"society already limits","chinese":"社會已經限制"},{"english":"harmful products","chinese":"有害產品"},{"english":"such as cigarettes","chinese":"例如香煙"},{"english":"profit","chinese":"利潤"},{"english":"be placed above","chinese":"被置於……之上"},{"english":"as dangerous as tobacco","chinese":"像煙草一樣危險"},{"english":"the same basic principle applies","chinese":"同一基本原則適用"},{"english":"create serious social costs","chinese":"造成嚴重社會成本"},{"english":"be controlled","chinese":"受到管制"},{"english":"strongly believe that","chinese":"強烈相信……"},{"english":"the right to advertise freely","chinese":"自由賣廣告的權利"},{"english":"business freedom","chinese":"商業自由"},{"english":"long-term eating habits","chinese":"長遠飲食習慣"},{"english":"be involved","chinese":"涉及其中"}]},"model-essay-78-ielts-opinion":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-78-ielts-opinion","essayKey":"opinion:78","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-78-ielts-opinion","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/opinions/EdmundBd9OP-Q78","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"With the rise of smartphones, streaming platforms and short online articles, some argue that books are becoming less central to how people learn and relax. I completely disagree with this view. Although the form of reading has changed, books, whether printed or digital, remain one of the most valuable sources of both reliable knowledge and meaningful enjoyment.","chinese":"隨著智能手機、串流平台和短篇網上文章的興起，有些人認為書本在人們學習和放鬆的方式中正變得不那麼重要。 我完全不同意這種看法。 儘管閱讀的形式已經改變，但無論是紙本書還是電子書，書本仍然是可靠知識和有意義娛樂中最有價值的來源之一。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"First, books still play an essential role in providing deep and structured information. Unlike many online posts, which are often brief, fragmented and written for speed, books usually develop an argument carefully and place facts in context. This matters because real understanding rarely comes from isolated pieces of information; it grows when readers can follow a subject from its foundations to its wider implications. For example, a person who wants to understand personal finance, history or health may find short videos useful for quick tips, but a well-written book can explain the principles behind those tips. In this sense, books do not merely give answers; they build judgement.","chinese":"首先，書本在提供深入而有系統的資訊方面，仍然扮演著不可或缺的角色。 不同於許多網上帖文通常簡短、零散，並且為了快速閱讀而寫，書本通常會仔細地發展一個論點，並把事實放在適當的背景之中。 這一點很重要，因為真正的理解很少來自零散孤立的資訊；當讀者能夠從一個主題的基礎一路理解到它更廣泛的影響時，理解才會逐漸形成。 例如，一個想了解個人理財、歷史或健康的人，可能會覺得短片對獲取快速提示很有用，但一本寫得好的書能夠解釋這些提示背後的原則。 從這個意義上說，書本不只是給出答案；它們還能培養判斷力"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"Books are also far from obsolete as a form of entertainment. In fact, their slower pace is precisely what makes them valuable. A novel allows readers to enter a world gradually, imagine characters in their own way and experience emotions without the constant noise of advertisements, notifications and algorithms. This kind of entertainment is quieter than a film or a game, but it can be just as powerful. For instance, many commuters still read crime stories, romances or autobiographies on trains, not because they lack digital alternatives, but because reading gives them a private mental space. Books therefore offer an experience that modern media often struggles to replace.","chinese":"作為一種娛樂形式，書本也遠遠未被淘汰。 事實上，書本較慢的節奏正正是它們有價值的地方。 一本小說能讓讀者慢慢進入一個世界，以自己的方式想像人物，並在沒有廣告、通知和演算法不斷干擾的情況下體驗情感。 這種娛樂比電影或遊戲更安靜，但它同樣可以很有力量。 例如，許多通勤者仍然會在火車上閱讀犯罪故事、愛情小說或自傳，並不是因為他們缺乏數碼娛樂選擇，而是因為閱讀能給他們一個私人的精神空間。 因此，書本提供了一種現代媒體往往難以取代的體驗。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, I do not agree that books are losing importance. Technology has changed the way people access information and entertainment, but it has not reduced the fundamental value of books. They remain important because they encourage depth, concentration and imagination, qualities that are becoming more necessary, not less.","chinese":"總結來說，我不同意書本正在失去重要性這一看法。 科技已經改變了人們獲取資訊和娛樂的方式，但它並沒有削弱書本的根本價值。 書本仍然重要，因為它們鼓勵深度、專注力和想像力，而這些素質正變得更加必要，而不是更不必要。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"with the rise of","chinese":"隨着……的興起"},{"english":"streaming platforms","chinese":"串流平台"},{"english":"short online articles","chinese":"網上短文"},{"english":"become less central to","chinese":"對……變得較不核心"},{"english":"learn and relax","chinese":"學習和放鬆"},{"english":"although the form of reading has changed","chinese":"雖然閱讀形式已經改變"},{"english":"whether printed or digital","chinese":"不論是印刷版還是數碼版"},{"english":"one of the most valuable sources of","chinese":"……最有價值的來源之一"},{"english":"reliable knowledge","chinese":"可靠知識"},{"english":"meaningful enjoyment","chinese":"有意義的享受"},{"english":"play an essential role in","chinese":"在……中發揮重要作用"},{"english":"deep and structured information","chinese":"深入而有系統的資料"},{"english":"unlike many online posts","chinese":"不像許多網上帖文"},{"english":"brief, fragmented and written for speed","chinese":"簡短、零碎，並為速度而寫"},{"english":"develop an argument carefully","chinese":"仔細展開論點"},{"english":"place facts in context","chinese":"將事實放在背景脈絡中"},{"english":"real understanding","chinese":"真正理解"},{"english":"isolated pieces of information","chinese":"零散資料"},{"english":"follow a subject from","chinese":"從……追溯一個主題"},{"english":"its foundations","chinese":"它的基礎"},{"english":"wider implications","chinese":"更廣泛的影響"},{"english":"personal finance","chinese":"個人理財"},{"english":"quick tips","chinese":"快速貼士"},{"english":"well-written book","chinese":"寫得好的書"},{"english":"the principles behind","chinese":"……背後的原則"},{"english":"in this sense","chinese":"從這個意義上說"},{"english":"not merely give answers","chinese":"不只是提供答案"},{"english":"build judgement","chinese":"培養判斷力"},{"english":"far from obsolete","chinese":"遠未過時"},{"english":"form of entertainment","chinese":"娛樂形式"},{"english":"slower pace","chinese":"較慢的節奏"},{"english":"precisely what makes them valuable","chinese":"正正是令它們有價值的地方"},{"english":"enter a world gradually","chinese":"逐漸進入一個世界"},{"english":"imagine characters in their own way","chinese":"以自己的方式想像角色"},{"english":"constant noise of","chinese":"持續的……滋擾"},{"english":"advertisements, notifications and algorithms","chinese":"廣告、通知和演算法"},{"english":"just as powerful","chinese":"同樣有力量"},{"english":"commuters","chinese":"通勤人士"},{"english":"crime stories","chinese":"犯罪小說"},{"english":"romances","chinese":"愛情小說"},{"english":"autobiographies","chinese":"自傳"},{"english":"lack digital alternatives","chinese":"缺乏數碼替代選擇"},{"english":"private mental space","chinese":"私人的精神空間"},{"english":"offer an experience","chinese":"提供一種體驗"},{"english":"modern media","chinese":"現代媒體"},{"english":"struggle to replace","chinese":"難以取代"},{"english":"losing importance","chinese":"重要性下降"},{"english":"access information and entertainment","chinese":"接觸資料和娛樂"},{"english":"fundamental value","chinese":"根本價值"},{"english":"encourage depth","chinese":"鼓勵深入思考"},{"english":"concentration and imagination","chinese":"專注力和想像力"},{"english":"becoming more necessary, not less","chinese":"變得更加必要，而不是更不必要"}]},"model-essay-79-ielts-opinion":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-79-ielts-opinion","essayKey":"opinion:79","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-79-ielts-opinion","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/opinions/EdmundBd9OP-Q79","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"In many families, activities are often judged by how quickly they produce visible results. For that reason, some people believe that children who spend many hours reading story books are wasting time that could be used for more practical pursuits. I completely disagree with this view, because story reading develops language, thinking, and emotional intelligence in ways that few childhood activities can match.","chinese":"在許多家庭中，活動往往會根據它們能多快產生可見成果來被評價。 因此，有些人認為，花很多時間閱讀故事書的兒童是在浪費時間，而這些時間本可以用於更實用的活動。 我完全不同意這種觀點，因為閱讀故事能培養語言、思考能力和情緒智力，而這些是很少其他兒童活動能夠相比的。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"The first reason is that story books build the foundation for almost every form of learning. When children read, they are not merely passing time; they are absorbing vocabulary, sentence patterns, ideas, and ways of organising events. A child who follows a plot must remember earlier details, predict what may happen next, and understand why characters make certain choices. This is mental training, not idleness. For example, a child who regularly reads adventure stories may gradually become better at explaining causes, describing situations, and writing coherent paragraphs at school. Other activities may teach useful habits, but story books give children a language-rich environment, and language is the bridge to almost every academic subject.","chinese":"第一個原因是，故事書為幾乎所有形式的學習建立基礎。 當兒童閱讀時，他們並不只是在消磨時間；他們是在吸收詞彙、句式、想法，以及組織事件的方式。 一個跟隨情節發展的孩子，必須記住之前的細節、預測接下來可能發生的事情，並理解角色為何作出某些選擇。 這是思維訓練，而不是無所事事。 例如，一個經常閱讀冒險故事的孩子，可能會逐漸更擅長在學校解釋原因、描述情境，以及寫出連貫的段落。 其他活動也許能教導有用的習慣，但故事書能給孩子一個語言豐富的環境，而語言正是通往幾乎所有學科的橋樑。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"Reading story books is also valuable because it develops imagination and empathy. Unlike many forms of entertainment, a book does not hand every image to the child ready-made; it asks the child to picture places, voices, dangers, and emotions internally. This quiet act of imagination strengthens concentration and gives children space to think deeply. More importantly, stories allow them to step into other people’s shoes. A child who reads about a lonely character, a frightened animal, or a brave friend can begin to understand feelings beyond his or her own small world. That kind of emotional growth is not a decorative extra; it helps children become kinder classmates, better listeners, and more thoughtful adults.","chinese":"閱讀故事書同樣有價值，因為它能培養想像力和同理心。 不同於許多娛樂形式，書本不會把每一個畫面都現成地交給孩子；它要求孩子在內心想像地方、聲音、危險和情感。 這種安靜的想像行為能加強專注力，並給孩子深入思考的空間。 更重要的是，故事讓他們能夠代入他人的處境。 一個讀到孤單角色、受驚動物或勇敢朋友的孩子，能開始理解超出自己小小世界之外的情感。 那種情感上的成長並不是可有可無的裝飾；它能幫助孩子成為更友善的同學、更好的聆聽者，以及更體貼的成年人。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, I completely reject the idea that reading children’s story books is a waste of time. Far from being useless, it is one of the richest ways for children to build language, imagination, and character.","chinese":"總結來說，我完全反對「閱讀兒童故事書是浪費時間」這個想法。 它絕非毫無用處，反而是兒童建立語言能力、想像力和品格最豐富的方式之一。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"Visiible results","chinese":"可見成果"},{"english":"practical pursuits","chinese":"實用活動"},{"english":"spend many hours reading","chinese":"花很多時間閱讀"},{"english":"wasting time","chinese":"浪費時間"},{"english":"completely disagree with","chinese":"完全不同意……"},{"english":"develop language, thinking, and emotional intelligence","chinese":"培養語言、思維和情緒智能"},{"english":"few childhood activities can match","chinese":"很少童年活動能媲美"},{"english":"build the foundation for","chinese":"為……打好基礎"},{"english":"almost every form of learning","chinese":"幾乎每一種學習形式"},{"english":"not merely passing time","chinese":"不只是打發時間"},{"english":"absorb vocabulary","chinese":"吸收詞彙"},{"english":"sentence patterns","chinese":"句式"},{"english":"ways of organising events","chinese":"組織事件的方式"},{"english":"follow a plot","chinese":"跟隨情節發展"},{"english":"remember earlier details","chinese":"記住較早前的細節"},{"english":"predict what may happen next","chinese":"預測接下來可能發生甚麼"},{"english":"make certain choices","chinese":"作出某些選擇"},{"english":"mental training","chinese":"思維訓練"},{"english":"idleness","chinese":"無所事事"},{"english":"adventure stories","chinese":"冒險故事"},{"english":"gradually become better at","chinese":"逐漸更擅長……"},{"english":"explaining causes","chinese":"解釋原因"},{"english":"describing situations","chinese":"描述情況"},{"english":"coherent paragraphs","chinese":"連貫的段落"},{"english":"useful habits","chinese":"有用的習慣"},{"english":"language-rich environment","chinese":"語言豐富的環境"},{"english":"the bridge to","chinese":"通往……的橋樑"},{"english":"academic subject","chinese":"學科"},{"english":"imagination and empathy","chinese":"想像力和同理心"},{"english":"unlike many forms of entertainment","chinese":"不像許多娛樂形式"},{"english":"hand every image to","chinese":"將每個畫面直接交給……"},{"english":"ready-made","chinese":"現成的"},{"english":"picture places, voices, dangers, and emotions","chinese":"想像地方、聲音、危險和情緒"},{"english":"internally","chinese":"在內心；在腦海中"},{"english":"quiet act of imagination","chinese":"安靜的想像行為"},{"english":"strengthen concentration","chinese":"加強專注力"},{"english":"give children space to","chinese":"給孩子空間去……"},{"english":"think deeply","chinese":"深入思考"},{"english":"more importantly","chinese":"更重要的是"},{"english":"step into other people's shoes","chinese":"代入別人的處境"},{"english":"lonely character","chinese":"孤獨的角色"},{"english":"frightened animal","chinese":"受驚的動物"},{"english":"brave friend","chinese":"勇敢的朋友"},{"english":"feelings beyond","chinese":"超出……以外的感受"},{"english":"own small world","chinese":"自己狹小的世界"},{"english":"emotional growth","chinese":"情感成長"},{"english":"decorative extra","chinese":"可有可無的附加物"},{"english":"kinder classmates","chinese":"更友善的同學"},{"english":"better listeners","chinese":"更好的聆聽者"},{"english":"thoughtful adults","chinese":"更有思想的成年人"},{"english":"completely reject the idea that","chinese":"完全否定……的想法"},{"english":"a waste of time","chinese":"浪費時間"},{"english":"far from being useless","chinese":"絕非無用"},{"english":"one of the richest ways to","chinese":"……最豐富的方式之一"},{"english":"build language, imagination, and character","chinese":"培養語言、想像力和品格"}]},"model-essay-80-ielts-opinion":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-80-ielts-opinion","essayKey":"opinion:80","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-80-ielts-opinion","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/opinions/EdmundBd9OP-Q80","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"Libraries have traditionally been associated with long shelves of printed books, but their purpose has changed in an age where information is increasingly digital. I fully agree that libraries should prioritise technological resources rather than simply expanding their paper-book collections, because technology makes knowledge more accessible and helps users develop skills that are essential in modern life.","chinese":"圖書館傳統上一直與一排排擺滿紙本書籍的書架聯繫在一起，但在資訊日益數碼化的時代，它們的功能已經發生變化。 我完全同意圖書館應該優先發展科技資源，而不是單純擴大紙本書籍館藏，因為科技能讓知識更容易取得，並幫助使用者培養現代生活中不可或缺的技能。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"The strongest reason is that digital resources allow libraries to serve far more people than printed books can. A physical book can usually be borrowed by only one reader at a time, and it must be collected, returned and stored. By contrast, e-books, online journals, academic databases and digital archives can often be accessed by many users at the same time, even from home. This is especially useful for students, shift workers and elderly people who may not be able to visit a library regularly. For example, a student preparing for an assignment can search electronic journals within minutes, whereas relying only on printed volumes may involve several visits and a great deal of wasted time. In this sense, technology allows libraries to reach beyond their own walls.","chinese":"最有力的原因是，數碼資源能讓圖書館服務的人數遠遠多於紙本書籍所能服務的人數。 一本實體書通常一次只能由一位讀者借閱，而且它必須被領取、歸還和存放。 相比之下，電子書、網上期刊、學術資料庫和數碼檔案往往可以由許多使用者同時存取，甚至可以在家中使用。 這對學生、輪班工作者和長者尤其有用，因為他們未必能夠定期親身前往圖書館。 例如，一位正在準備作業的學生可以在幾分鐘內搜尋電子期刊，而如果只依賴紙本書籍，可能需要多次到訪圖書館，並浪費大量時間。 從這個意義上說，科技使圖書館能夠突破自身建築空間的限制，接觸到更廣泛的人群。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"Another important point is that modern libraries should help people build practical digital skills. Education, employment and public services increasingly depend on the ability to search for, evaluate and use online information responsibly. If libraries invest in computers, media rooms, online catalogues and trained staff, they become active learning centres rather than quiet storage spaces. Children can learn how to research safely, job seekers can prepare applications, and adults can access government services that have moved online. A larger paper collection alone cannot meet these needs. It may look impressive, but it is like adding more candles in an age that requires electric light.","chinese":"另一個重要觀點是，現代圖書館應該幫助人們建立實用的數碼技能。 教育、就業和公共服務越來越依賴人們負責任地搜尋、評估和使用網上資訊的能力。 如果圖書館投資於電腦、媒體室、網上目錄和受過培訓的職員，它們就會成為活躍的學習中心，而不只是安靜的儲存空間。 兒童可以學習如何安全地進行資料搜集，求職者可以準備求職申請，而成年人則可以使用已轉移到網上的政府服務。 單靠更大的紙本館藏無法滿足這些需求。 它也許看起來令人印象深刻，但這就像在一個需要電燈的時代裡增加更多蠟燭一樣。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, I completely agree that libraries should focus on improving their technological resources instead of building ever-larger collections of paper books. This approach gives libraries wider reach, greater efficiency and a more relevant role in contemporary society.","chinese":"總結來說，我完全同意圖書館應該專注於改善科技資源，而不是建立越來越龐大的紙本書籍館藏。 這種做法能讓圖書館擁有更廣泛的覆蓋範圍、更高的效率，以及在當代社會中更貼切的角色。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"have traditionally been associated with","chinese":"傳統上與……有關"},{"english":"long shelves of printed books","chinese":"一排排印刷書籍"},{"english":"their purpose has changed","chinese":"它們的用途已經改變"},{"english":"in an age where","chinese":"在一個……的時代"},{"english":"increasingly digital","chinese":"越來越數碼化"},{"english":"fully agree that","chinese":"完全同意……"},{"english":"prioritise technological resources","chinese":"優先發展科技資源"},{"english":"rather than simply","chinese":"而不是單純……"},{"english":"expanding their paper-book collections","chinese":"擴充紙本藏書"},{"english":"make knowledge more accessible","chinese":"令知識更容易取得"},{"english":"develop skills","chinese":"培養技能"},{"english":"be essential in modern life","chinese":"在現代生活中必不可少"},{"english":"digital resources","chinese":"數碼資源"},{"english":"serve far more people than","chinese":"服務比……多得多的人"},{"english":"printed books","chinese":"印刷書籍"},{"english":"physical book","chinese":"實體書"},{"english":"be borrowed by","chinese":"被……借閱"},{"english":"one reader at a time","chinese":"每次一位讀者"},{"english":"be collected, returned and stored","chinese":"被取走、歸還和存放"},{"english":"by contrast","chinese":"相比之下"},{"english":"e-books","chinese":"電子書"},{"english":"online journals","chinese":"網上期刊"},{"english":"academic databases","chinese":"學術數據庫"},{"english":"digital archives","chinese":"數碼檔案庫"},{"english":"be accessed by","chinese":"被……取用"},{"english":"at the same time","chinese":"同時"},{"english":"even from home","chinese":"甚至在家中"},{"english":"especially useful for","chinese":"對……特別有用"},{"english":"shift workers","chinese":"輪班工作者"},{"english":"elderly people","chinese":"長者"},{"english":"visit a library regularly","chinese":"定期到訪圖書館"},{"english":"preparing for an assignment","chinese":"準備功課"},{"english":"search electronic journals","chinese":"搜尋電子期刊"},{"english":"within minutes","chinese":"幾分鐘內"},{"english":"whereas","chinese":"而；然而"},{"english":"relying only on","chinese":"只依賴……"},{"english":"printed volumes","chinese":"紙本書冊"},{"english":"involve several visits","chinese":"涉及多次到訪"},{"english":"a great deal of wasted time","chinese":"大量浪費的時間"},{"english":"in this sense","chinese":"從這個意義上說"},{"english":"reach beyond their own walls","chinese":"超越自身建築範圍"},{"english":"practical digital skills","chinese":"實用數碼技能"},{"english":"public services","chinese":"公共服務"},{"english":"increasingly depend on","chinese":"越來越依賴"},{"english":"the ability to search for","chinese":"搜尋……的能力"},{"english":"evaluate and use online information responsibly","chinese":"負責任地評估和使用網上資料"},{"english":"invest in","chinese":"投資於……"},{"english":"media rooms","chinese":"媒體室"},{"english":"online catalogues","chinese":"網上目錄"},{"english":"trained staff","chinese":"受過訓練的職員"},{"english":"active learning centres","chinese":"主動學習中心"},{"english":"rather than quiet storage spaces","chinese":"而不是安靜的儲物空間"},{"english":"research safely","chinese":"安全地做資料搜集"},{"english":"job seekers","chinese":"求職者"},{"english":"prepare applications","chinese":"準備申請"},{"english":"access government services","chinese":"使用政府服務"},{"english":"have moved online","chinese":"已轉到網上"},{"english":"paper collection alone","chinese":"單靠紙本藏書"},{"english":"meet these needs","chinese":"滿足這些需要"},{"english":"look impressive","chinese":"看起來令人印象深刻"},{"english":"adding more candles","chinese":"增加更多蠟燭"},{"english":"requires electric light","chinese":"需要電燈"},{"english":"focus on improving","chinese":"專注於改善……"},{"english":"instead of building","chinese":"而不是建立……"},{"english":"ever-larger collections of","chinese":"越來越龐大的……藏量"},{"english":"this approach","chinese":"這種做法"},{"english":"wider reach","chinese":"更廣的覆蓋範圍"},{"english":"greater efficiency","chinese":"更高效率"},{"english":"a more relevant role","chinese":"更切合需要的角色"},{"english":"contemporary society","chinese":"當代社會"}]},"model-essay-81-ielts-opinion":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-81-ielts-opinion","essayKey":"opinion:81","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-81-ielts-opinion","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/opinions/EdmundBd9OP-Q81","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"Marriage has long been associated not only with love and family life, but also with economic protection. In many societies, however, women now have far greater access to education and paid work. I completely agree that this financial independence is the main reason why many women no longer regard marriage as a necessity.","chinese":"婚姻長久以來不只與愛情和家庭生活有關，也與經濟保障聯繫在一起。 然而，在許多社會中，女性如今有更多機會接受教育和從事有薪工作。 我完全同意，這種經濟獨立是許多女性不再把婚姻視為必要選擇的主要原因。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"The strongest reason is that earning an income allows women to meet their basic needs without depending on a husband. In the past, a woman who could not easily own property, enter well-paid employment or support children alone often had little choice but to see marriage as a safety net. By contrast, a woman with a stable salary can rent a home, pay bills, save for the future and make major life decisions on her own terms. For example, a professional woman in a large city may postpone or reject marriage because her career already gives her the security that marriage once promised. In this sense, money does not simply buy comfort; it buys freedom.","chinese":"最有力的原因是，賺取收入使女性能夠滿足自己的基本需要，而不必依賴丈夫。 在過去，一個不容易擁有財產、進入高薪工作或獨自撫養孩子的女性，往往別無選擇，只能把婚姻視為一張安全網。 相比之下，一個擁有穩定薪水的女性可以租住房屋、支付賬單、為將來儲蓄，並按照自己的條件作出重大人生決定。 例如，一位在大城市工作的專業女性可能會推遲甚至拒絕婚姻，因為她的事業已經給予她婚姻過去所承諾的安全感。 從這個意義上說，金錢買到的不只是舒適；它買到的是自由。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"Financial independence also changes how women judge relationships. When marriage is no longer required for survival, it has to offer emotional respect, equality and genuine companionship. A woman who can support herself is less likely to tolerate a controlling or unhappy marriage merely because leaving would be financially impossible. This shift raises the standard of marriage itself: it becomes a choice rather than a cage. For instance, many working women would rather remain single than enter a relationship where domestic responsibilities, career sacrifice and emotional labour fall mainly on them.","chinese":"經濟獨立也改變了女性判斷關係的方式。 當婚姻不再是生存所必需的條件時，它就必須提供情感上的尊重、平等和真正的陪伴。 一個能夠養活自己的女性，較不可能僅僅因為離開在經濟上不可行，就忍受一段控制慾強或不快樂的婚姻。 這種轉變提高了婚姻本身的標準：它變成了一種選擇，而不是一個牢籠。 例如，許多職業女性寧願保持單身，也不願進入一段家務責任、事業犧牲和情感勞動主要都落在自己身上的關係。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, I fully agree that women’s ability to earn their own income is the key reason why marriage feels less necessary in many countries. As financial dependence fades, marriage loses its old function as economic protection and must stand on the firmer ground of love, respect and equality.","chinese":"總結來說，我完全同意，女性能夠賺取自己的收入，是婚姻在許多國家變得較不必要的關鍵原因。 隨著經濟依賴逐漸消退，婚姻失去了其作為經濟保障的舊有功能，並必須建立在愛、尊重和平等這些更穩固的基礎之上。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"has long been associated with","chinese":"長久以來與……有關"},{"english":"not only with","chinese":"不只是與……"},{"english":"but also with","chinese":"而且與……"},{"english":"economic protection","chinese":"經濟保障"},{"english":"far greater access to","chinese":"更大得多的機會接觸……"},{"english":"paid work","chinese":"受薪工作"},{"english":"financial independence","chinese":"經濟獨立"},{"english":"the main reason why","chinese":"……的主要原因"},{"english":"no longer regard","chinese":"不再視為"},{"english":"as a necessity","chinese":"作為必需品"},{"english":"earning an income","chinese":"賺取收入"},{"english":"meet their basic needs","chinese":"滿足基本需要"},{"english":"depend on","chinese":"依賴"},{"english":"in the past","chinese":"在過去"},{"english":"own property","chinese":"擁有物業"},{"english":"well-paid employment","chinese":"高薪工作"},{"english":"support children alone","chinese":"獨自撫養孩子"},{"english":"have little choice but to","chinese":"別無選擇，只能……"},{"english":"a safety net","chinese":"安全網"},{"english":"by contrast","chinese":"相比之下"},{"english":"stable salary","chinese":"穩定薪金"},{"english":"rent a home","chinese":"租屋"},{"english":"pay bills","chinese":"支付帳單"},{"english":"save for the future","chinese":"為將來儲蓄"},{"english":"make major life decisions","chinese":"作出重大人生決定"},{"english":"on her own terms","chinese":"按自己的條件"},{"english":"professional woman","chinese":"職業女性"},{"english":"postpone marriage","chinese":"延遲結婚"},{"english":"reject marriage","chinese":"拒絕結婚"},{"english":"gives her the security","chinese":"給予她安全感"},{"english":"once promised","chinese":"曾經承諾"},{"english":"in this sense","chinese":"從這個意義上說"},{"english":"buy comfort","chinese":"買來舒適"},{"english":"buy freedom","chinese":"買來自由"},{"english":"judge relationships","chinese":"評價關係"},{"english":"be no longer required for","chinese":"不再是……所必需"},{"english":"offer emotional respect","chinese":"提供情感上的尊重"},{"english":"genuine companionship","chinese":"真正的陪伴"},{"english":"support herself","chinese":"養活自己"},{"english":"be less likely to","chinese":"較不可能"},{"english":"tolerate","chinese":"容忍"},{"english":"controlling marriage","chinese":"控制慾強的婚姻"},{"english":"unhappy marriage","chinese":"不快樂的婚姻"},{"english":"merely because","chinese":"只是因為"},{"english":"financially impossible","chinese":"經濟上不可行"},{"english":"this shift","chinese":"這種轉變"},{"english":"raises the standard of","chinese":"提高……的標準"},{"english":"a choice rather than a cage","chinese":"一個選擇，而不是牢籠"},{"english":"remain single","chinese":"保持單身"},{"english":"enter a relationship","chinese":"進入一段關係"},{"english":"domestic responsibilities","chinese":"家務責任"},{"english":"career sacrifice","chinese":"事業上的犧牲"},{"english":"emotional labour","chinese":"情緒勞動"},{"english":"fall mainly on","chinese":"主要落在……身上"},{"english":"ability to earn","chinese":"賺取……的能力"},{"english":"own income","chinese":"自己的收入"},{"english":"the key reason why","chinese":"……的關鍵原因"},{"english":"feels less necessary","chinese":"感覺較不必要"},{"english":"financial dependence fades","chinese":"經濟依賴逐漸消退"},{"english":"loses its old function as","chinese":"失去其作為……的舊功能"},{"english":"stand on the firmer ground of","chinese":"建基於更穩固的……基礎上"},{"english":"love, respect and equality","chinese":"愛、尊重和平等"}]},"model-essay-82-ielts-opinion":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-82-ielts-opinion","essayKey":"opinion:82","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-82-ielts-opinion","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/opinions/EdmundBd9OP-Q82","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"Homelessness is one of the clearest signs that a society is failing some of its most vulnerable members, and it is natural to feel that handing over money is a kind response. However, I completely disagree that this is the best way to help homeless people. Direct cash can ease immediate discomfort, but lasting help must address the causes of homelessness.","chinese":"無家可歸是最清楚顯示一個社會未能照顧部分最弱勢成員的跡象之一，而人們自然會覺得直接給錢是一種善意的回應。 然而，我完全不同意這是幫助無家可歸者的最佳方法。 直接給予金錢可以緩解眼前的不適，但長遠的幫助必須處理無家可歸的根本原因。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"The first reason is that money treats the problem as if it were only financial. A person living on the street may need a meal, but they may also lack a stable address, official documents, medical care, family support or the confidence to return to work. In such cases, a donation can be swallowed by daily survival without changing the person’s life. For example, someone might use the money to buy food and stay safe for one more night, yet wake up the next morning facing the same barriers. This is a kind action, but it is not a real solution.","chinese":"第一個原因是，金錢把這個問題處理得好像它只是經濟問題。 一個露宿街頭的人可能需要一餐飯，但他們也可能缺乏穩定地址、官方文件、醫療照顧、家庭支持，或者重新工作的信心。 在這些情況下，一筆捐款可能只會被日常求生所消耗，而不能真正改變這個人的生活。 例如，有人可能會用這筆錢買食物，並安全地度過多一個晚上，但第二天早上醒來時仍然要面對同樣的障礙。 這是一種善意的行動，但它並不是真正的解決方法。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"A more effective response is to provide organised support that helps people rebuild their lives step by step. Shelters, counselling, addiction treatment, affordable housing and job-training schemes deal with the roots of homelessness rather than merely softening its surface. Trained workers can also guide homeless individuals through systems that are difficult to manage alone. For instance, helping someone get an identity card, attend medical appointments and move into temporary accommodation can become a bridge back into ordinary life. In this sense, money is useful only when it is turned into structure, safety and direction.","chinese":"一個更有效的回應，是提供有組織的支援，幫助人們一步一步重建生活。 庇護所、輔導、戒癮治療、可負擔房屋和職業培訓計劃，處理的是無家可歸的根源，而不只是減輕其表面問題。 受過訓練的工作人員也可以引導無家可歸者處理一些獨自難以應付的制度。 例如，幫助一個人取得身份證、出席醫療預約，並搬進臨時住所，可以成為他回到正常生活的一座橋樑。 從這個意義上說，金錢只有在被轉化為制度、保障和方向時，才真正有用。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, I strongly disagree that giving money is the best response to homelessness. Although the impulse is compassionate, it is too limited for such a deep social problem. The best help is sustained support that gives people a genuine route off the street.","chinese":"總結來說，我強烈不同意給錢是應對無家可歸問題的最佳方法。 雖然這種衝動是出於同情，但對於這樣一個深層的社會問題而言，它太有限了。 最好的幫助，是持續性的支援，為人們提供一條真正離開街頭的道路。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"homelessness","chinese":"無家者問題；露宿問題"},{"english":"official documents","chinese":"官方文件"},{"english":"medical care","chinese":"醫療照顧"},{"english":"family support","chinese":"家庭支援"},{"english":"the confidence to return to work","chinese":"重返工作的信心"},{"english":"in such cases","chinese":"在這些情況下"},{"english":"be swallowed by","chinese":"被……耗盡"},{"english":"daily survival","chinese":"每日求生"},{"english":"without changing","chinese":"而沒有改變……"},{"english":"stay safe","chinese":"保持安全"},{"english":"one more night","chinese":"多一晚"},{"english":"wake up the next morning","chinese":"第二天早上醒來"},{"english":"face the same barriers","chinese":"面對同樣障礙"},{"english":"a real solution","chinese":"真正的解決方法"},{"english":"a more effective response","chinese":"更有效的回應"},{"english":"organised support","chinese":"有組織的支援"},{"english":"rebuild their lives","chinese":"重建生活"},{"english":"step by step","chinese":"一步一步地"},{"english":"shelters","chinese":"收容所；臨時宿舍"},{"english":"counselling","chinese":"輔導"},{"english":"addiction treatment","chinese":"戒癮治療"},{"english":"affordable housing","chinese":"可負擔房屋"},{"english":"job-training schemes","chinese":"職業培訓計劃"},{"english":"deal with the roots of","chinese":"處理……的根源"},{"english":"rather than merely","chinese":"而不是只是……"},{"english":"soften its surface","chinese":"只紓緩表面問題"},{"english":"trained workers","chinese":"受過訓練的工作人員"},{"english":"guide homeless individuals through","chinese":"引導無家者通過……"},{"english":"difficult to manage alone","chinese":"難以獨自處理"},{"english":"identity card","chinese":"身份證"},{"english":"attend medical appointments","chinese":"出席醫療預約"},{"english":"temporary accommodation","chinese":"臨時住宿"},{"english":"a bridge back into","chinese":"回到……的橋樑"},{"english":"ordinary life","chinese":"正常生活"},{"english":"in this sense","chinese":"從這個意義上說"},{"english":"be turned into","chinese":"被轉化為"},{"english":"structure, safety and direction","chinese":"結構、安全和方向"},{"english":"strongly disagree that","chinese":"強烈不同意……"},{"english":"the impulse is compassionate","chinese":"這種衝動是出於同情心"},{"english":"too limited for","chinese":"對……來說太有限"},{"english":"deep social problem","chinese":"深層社會問題"},{"english":"sustained support","chinese":"持續支援"},{"english":"genuine route off the street","chinese":"真正脫離街頭生活的途徑"}]},"model-essay-83-ielts-opinion":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-83-ielts-opinion","essayKey":"opinion:83","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-83-ielts-opinion","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/opinions/EdmundBd9OP-Q83","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"It is often argued that international travel makes people more tolerant and more capable of understanding those who live differently. I completely agree with this view because travelling replaces distant assumptions with real human contact, and it also teaches people the humility that comes from being a stranger in another society.","chinese":"人們常常認為，國際旅行會使人更加寬容，也更有能力理解那些生活方式與自己不同的人。 我完全同意這個觀點，因為旅行會用真實的人際接觸取代遙遠的假設，而且它也教會人們一種謙卑：那就是身處另一個社會、成為陌生人時所產生的謙卑。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"The first reason is that travelling weakens stereotypes. When people judge foreign cultures from a distance, their opinions are often shaped by headlines, films, or second-hand stories, which can reduce whole communities to a few simple labels. However, once travellers eat local food, use public transport, speak to residents, and observe daily routines, unfamiliar customs begin to make sense. For example, a visitor who initially sees quiet public behaviour in another country as cold or unfriendly may later realise that it reflects respect for shared spaces. In this way, travel turns differences from something suspicious into something understandable.","chinese":"第一個原因是，旅行會削弱刻板印象。 當人們從遠處評價外國文化時，他們的看法往往受到新聞標題、電影或二手故事所影響，而這可能會把整個群體簡化成幾個簡單的標籤。 然而，一旦旅客品嚐當地食物、使用公共交通、與居民交談，並觀察日常生活習慣，那些原本陌生的風俗便開始變得可以理解。 例如，一位旅客起初可能會把另一個國家安靜的公共行為視為冷淡或不友善，但後來可能會意識到，這其實反映了對公共空間的尊重。 透過這種方式，旅行把差異從一種令人懷疑的東西，轉化成一種可以理解的東西。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"Another important reason is that travel forces people to experience vulnerability. In a foreign country, even simple tasks such as ordering a meal, asking for directions, or reading a sign can become unexpectedly difficult. This experience can be uncomfortable, but it is also valuable because it reminds travellers how it feels to be confused, dependent, or misunderstood. A person who has once struggled with a foreign language is less likely to look down on immigrants or tourists who face the same problem at home. Travel therefore acts like a mirror: it shows people not only how others live, but also how easily their own confidence depends on familiar surroundings.","chinese":"另一個重要原因是，旅行會迫使人們體驗脆弱感。 在外國，即使是點餐、問路或閱讀標示這些簡單任務，也可能變得出乎意料地困難。 這種經歷可能令人不舒服，但它同時也很有價值，因為它提醒旅客，被困惑、依賴他人或被誤解是一種怎樣的感覺。 一個曾經因外語而掙扎的人，較容易看不起那些在自己國家面對同樣問題的移民或遊客 因此，旅行就像一面鏡子：它不但讓人看見別人如何生活，也讓人看見自己的自信其實多麼容易依賴熟悉的環境。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, I fully agree that travelling abroad can make people more tolerant and understanding. By challenging stereotypes and placing individuals in unfamiliar situations, it broadens their judgement and softens their attitude towards others.","chinese":"總結來說，我完全同意，到海外旅行能使人更加寬容，也更能理解他人。 透過挑戰刻板印象，並把個人置於陌生情境之中，旅行能拓寬人的判斷力，也能使他們對他人的態度變得更柔和。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"it is often argued that","chinese":"人們經常認為……"},{"english":"international travel","chinese":"國際旅遊"},{"english":"more tolerant","chinese":"更包容"},{"english":"be capable of","chinese":"有能力去……"},{"english":"live differently","chinese":"以不同方式生活"},{"english":"completely agree with","chinese":"完全同意……"},{"english":"replace distant assumptions with","chinese":"以……取代遠距離的假設"},{"english":"distant assumptions","chinese":"遠距離的假設"},{"english":"real human contact","chinese":"真實的人與人接觸"},{"english":"teach people the humility","chinese":"教會人謙卑"},{"english":"comes from","chinese":"來自……"},{"english":"being a stranger","chinese":"成為陌生人"},{"english":"another society","chinese":"另一個社會"},{"english":"weaken stereotypes","chinese":"削弱刻板印象"},{"english":"judge foreign cultures from a distance","chinese":"從遠處評價外國文化"},{"english":"be shaped by","chinese":"受……塑造"},{"english":"headlines","chinese":"新聞標題"},{"english":"second-hand stories","chinese":"二手故事；間接聽來的故事"},{"english":"reduce whole communities to","chinese":"將整個群體簡化為……"},{"english":"whole communities","chinese":"整個群體"},{"english":"a few simple labels","chinese":"幾個簡單標籤"},{"english":"however","chinese":"然而"},{"english":"once travellers","chinese":"一旦旅客……"},{"english":"eat local food","chinese":"吃當地食物"},{"english":"use public transport","chinese":"使用公共交通"},{"english":"speak to residents","chinese":"與居民交談"},{"english":"observe daily routines","chinese":"觀察日常習慣"},{"english":"unfamiliar customs","chinese":"陌生習俗"},{"english":"begin to make sense","chinese":"開始變得合理；開始明白"},{"english":"initially sees","chinese":"起初視為"},{"english":"quiet public behaviour","chinese":"公共場合安靜的行為"},{"english":"cold or unfriendly","chinese":"冷漠或不友善"},{"english":"may later realise that","chinese":"後來可能意識到……"},{"english":"reflect respect for","chinese":"反映對……的尊重"},{"english":"shared spaces","chinese":"共享空間"},{"english":"in this way","chinese":"以這種方式"},{"english":"turn differences from","chinese":"將差異由……轉化為……"},{"english":"something suspicious","chinese":"可疑的東西"},{"english":"something understandable","chinese":"可以理解的東西"},{"english":"force people to","chinese":"迫使人們去……"},{"english":"experience vulnerability","chinese":"經歷脆弱感"},{"english":"even simple tasks","chinese":"即使是簡單任務"},{"english":"ordering a meal","chinese":"點餐"},{"english":"asking for directions","chinese":"問路"},{"english":"reading a sign","chinese":"閱讀告示"},{"english":"unexpectedly difficult","chinese":"出乎意料地困難"},{"english":"uncomfortable","chinese":"令人不自在"},{"english":"reminds travellers how it feels to","chinese":"提醒旅客……是甚麼感受"},{"english":"be confused, dependent, or misunderstood","chinese":"感到困惑、依賴他人或被誤解"},{"english":"struggle with","chinese":"為……而感到困難"},{"english":"foreign language","chinese":"外語"},{"english":"be less likely to","chinese":"較不可能"},{"english":"look down on","chinese":"看不起"},{"english":"immigrants","chinese":"移民"},{"english":"face the same problem","chinese":"面對同樣問題"},{"english":"at home","chinese":"在本地；在自己國家"},{"english":"acts like a mirror","chinese":"像一面鏡子"},{"english":"not only how","chinese":"不只是如何……"},{"english":"how others live","chinese":"別人如何生活"},{"english":"how easily","chinese":"多麼容易"},{"english":"confidence depends on","chinese":"自信取決於……"},{"english":"familiar surroundings","chinese":"熟悉的環境"},{"english":"travelling abroad","chinese":"到外國旅遊"},{"english":"tolerant and understanding","chinese":"包容和體諒"},{"english":"challenging stereotypes","chinese":"挑戰刻板印象"},{"english":"placing individuals in","chinese":"將個人置於……"},{"english":"unfamiliar situations","chinese":"陌生情況"},{"english":"broaden their judgement","chinese":"擴闊判斷"},{"english":"soften their attitude towards","chinese":"軟化對……的態度"},{"english":"towards others","chinese":"對他人"}]},"model-essay-84-ielts-opinion":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-84-ielts-opinion","essayKey":"opinion:84","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-84-ielts-opinion","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/opinions/EdmundBd9OP-Q84","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"Many governments devote substantial public funds to programmes that search for life beyond Earth. I completely agree that this is an unjustifiable use of taxpayers’ money, because governments have an immediate duty to solve human problems and because this research can be pursued by private organisations rather than the state.","chinese":"許多政府把大量公共資金投放於尋找地球以外生命的計劃。 我完全同意，這是對納稅人金錢的不合理使用，因為政府有即時責任去解決人類面對的問題，而且這類研究可以由私人機構而不是國家來進行。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"The strongest reason is that public money is limited, so it should first protect citizens whose basic needs are still unmet. In many countries, hospitals are overcrowded, schools lack resources, and low-income families struggle with housing and food. When a government spends huge sums trying to detect alien life, it is choosing a distant possibility over visible suffering. This choice is hard to defend because public services are not luxuries; they are the foundation of a stable society. For example, money directed towards medical equipment, mental-health support, or rural schools can improve lives within years, whereas the search for extraterrestrial life may produce no practical benefit for generations. Government budgets should not chase stars while ordinary citizens are left in the dark.","chinese":"最有力的理由是，公共資金是有限的，因此它應該首先保障那些基本需求仍未被滿足的市民。 在許多國家，醫院過度擠迫，學校缺乏資源，而低收入家庭則在住房和食物方面苦苦掙扎。 當政府花費巨額資金試圖探測外星生命時，它就是在把一個遙遠的可能性置於眼前可見的痛苦之上。 這種選擇很難被合理辯護，因為公共服務並不是奢侈品；它們是一個穩定社會的基礎。 例如，投放在醫療設備、心理健康支援或鄉村學校上的金錢，可以在數年內改善人們的生活；然而，尋找地球以外生命的工作，可能幾代人都不會產生實際利益。 政府預算不應該在普通市民仍被留在黑暗中時，卻去追逐星辰。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"Another reason is that discovering life on other planets is a scientific curiosity rather than a core governmental responsibility. Granted, space science can inspire innovation, but the specific goal of finding alien life does not deserve priority over poverty, disease, and unemployment. If wealthy technology companies, universities, or international research bodies wish to explore this question, they are better placed to do so because they can accept long-term uncertainty without neglecting public duties. Governments, by contrast, are elected to provide security, opportunity, and basic welfare. Every dollar spent on speculative missions is a dollar not spent on making healthcare more accessible, education more equal, or cities safer.","chinese":"另一個理由是，發現其他星球上的生命是一種科學上的好奇心，而不是政府的核心責任 誠然，太空科學可以激發創新；然而，尋找外星生命這一具體目標，並不應比貧窮、疾病和失業更優先。 如果富有的科技公司、大學或國際研究機構希望探索這個問題，它們更適合去做，因為它們可以承受長期的不確定性，而不會忽略公共責任。 相比之下，政府是被選出來提供安全、機會和基本福利的。 每一元花在投機性的任務上，就等於少了一元用來讓醫療更容易取得、教育更平等，或城市更安全。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, I fully agree that governments should reduce spending on the search for life on other planets and redirect those funds to public problems. Curiosity is valuable, but public responsibility must come first; a government should repair the ground beneath its people’s feet before looking for life in the sky.","chinese":"總結來說，我完全同意政府應該減少在尋找其他星球生命方面的開支，並把這些資金重新投放到公共問題上。 好奇心是有價值的，但公共責任必須優先；政府應該先修補人民腳下的土地，才去仰望天空尋找生命。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"devote substantial public funds to","chinese":"投入大量公帑於……"},{"english":"search for life beyond Earth","chinese":"尋找地球以外的生命"},{"english":"unjustifiable use of","chinese":"對……不合理的使用"},{"english":"taxpayers' money","chinese":"納稅人的錢"},{"english":"immediate duty to","chinese":"有即時責任去……"},{"english":"human problems","chinese":"人類問題"},{"english":"be pursued by","chinese":"由……進行"},{"english":"private organisations","chinese":"私營機構"},{"english":"rather than the state","chinese":"而不是由國家"},{"english":"public money is limited","chinese":"公帑有限"},{"english":"protect citizens","chinese":"保護公民"},{"english":"basic needs are still unmet","chinese":"基本需要仍未得到滿足"},{"english":"hospitals are overcrowded","chinese":"醫院過度擠迫"},{"english":"schools lack resources","chinese":"學校缺乏資源"},{"english":"low-income families","chinese":"低收入家庭"},{"english":"struggle with","chinese":"為……而掙扎"},{"english":"housing and food","chinese":"住屋和食物"},{"english":"spend huge sums","chinese":"花費巨額金錢"},{"english":"detect alien life","chinese":"探測外星生命"},{"english":"a distant possibility","chinese":"遙遠的可能性"},{"english":"visible suffering","chinese":"眼前可見的苦難"},{"english":"hard to defend","chinese":"難以辯護"},{"english":"public services","chinese":"公共服務"},{"english":"not luxuries","chinese":"不是奢侈品"},{"english":"the foundation of","chinese":"……的基礎"},{"english":"stable society","chinese":"穩定社會"},{"english":"money directed towards","chinese":"投放於……的金錢"},{"english":"medical equipment","chinese":"醫療設備"},{"english":"mental-health support","chinese":"精神健康支援"},{"english":"rural schools","chinese":"鄉郊學校"},{"english":"improve lives within years","chinese":"在數年內改善生活"},{"english":"whereas","chinese":"而；然而"},{"english":"extraterrestrial life","chinese":"地球以外的生命"},{"english":"practical benefit","chinese":"實際好處"},{"english":"for generations","chinese":"好幾代人"},{"english":"government budgets","chinese":"政府預算"},{"english":"chase stars","chinese":"追逐星辰；追求遙遠目標"},{"english":"ordinary citizens","chinese":"普通公民"},{"english":"be left in the dark","chinese":"被留在黑暗中；得不到幫助"},{"english":"scientific curiosity","chinese":"科學上的好奇"},{"english":"core governmental responsibility","chinese":"政府核心責任"},{"english":"granted","chinese":"誠然"},{"english":"inspire innovation","chinese":"啟發創新"},{"english":"the specific goal of","chinese":"……這個具體目標"},{"english":"deserve priority over","chinese":"比……更值得優先處理"},{"english":"poverty, disease, and unemployment","chinese":"貧窮、疾病和失業"},{"english":"wealthy technology companies","chinese":"富有的科技公司"},{"english":"universities","chinese":"大學"},{"english":"international research bodies","chinese":"國際研究機構"},{"english":"explore this question","chinese":"探索這個問題"},{"english":"be better placed to","chinese":"更適合去……"},{"english":"accept long-term uncertainty","chinese":"接受長期不確定性"},{"english":"without neglecting","chinese":"而不忽視……"},{"english":"public duties","chinese":"公共責任"},{"english":"by contrast","chinese":"相比之下"},{"english":"be elected to","chinese":"被選出去……"},{"english":"provide security","chinese":"提供安全保障"},{"english":"opportunity","chinese":"機會"},{"english":"basic welfare","chinese":"基本福利"},{"english":"speculative missions","chinese":"投機性任務；不確定性高的任務"},{"english":"make healthcare more accessible","chinese":"令醫療更容易取得"},{"english":"education more equal","chinese":"令教育更平等"},{"english":"cities safer","chinese":"令城市更安全"},{"english":"reduce spending on","chinese":"減少在……上的開支"},{"english":"redirect those funds to","chinese":"將那些資金重新投放到……"},{"english":"public problems","chinese":"公共問題"},{"english":"public responsibility","chinese":"公共責任"},{"english":"come first","chinese":"放在首位"},{"english":"repair the ground beneath","chinese":"修補人民腳下的土地"},{"english":"before looking for life in the sky","chinese":"在尋找天上生命之前"}]},"model-essay-85-ielts-opinion":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-85-ielts-opinion","essayKey":"opinion:85","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-85-ielts-opinion","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/opinions/EdmundBd9OP-Q85","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"Teamwork is an essential social skill, and many parents believe that children can learn it best through team sports. However, I completely disagree with the view that introducing children to sports such as football, basketball, or volleyball is the best way to teach this quality. A more reliable method is to involve children in structured group tasks where cooperation is directly taught, monitored, and reflected upon.","chinese":"團隊合作是一項重要的社交技能，而許多父母相信，孩子最能透過團隊運動學會這能力 然而，我完全不同意讓孩子接觸足球、籃球或排球等運動是教授這種品質的最佳方式這一觀點。 一種更可靠的方法，是讓孩子參與有結構的團體任務，在這些任務中，合作會被直接教授、監察並反思。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"The main weakness of team sports is that they often reward performance more than cooperation. In a competitive game, children may become focused on winning, scoring, or avoiding blame, rather than listening carefully to others or sharing responsibility fairly. Stronger players can easily dominate the activity, while less confident children may be pushed to the side and learn silence rather than teamwork. For example, in a school football match, the fastest child may receive most of the passes because classmates believe this gives them the best chance of winning. In that situation, the group may appear united, but the weaker players are not genuinely learning how to contribute, negotiate, or solve problems together.","chinese":"團隊運動的主要弱點在於，它們往往更重視表現，而不是合作。 在競爭性的比賽中，孩子可能會專注於取勝、得分或避免被責怪，而不是仔細聆聽他人，或公平地分擔責任。 能力較強的孩子很容易主導整個活動，而較缺乏自信的孩子則可能被推到一旁，學到的不是團隊合作，而是沉默。 例如，在一場校內足球比賽中，跑得最快的孩子可能會接到大多數傳球，因為同學們相信這樣最有機會獲勝。 在這種情況下，整個團體看起來可能很團結，但較弱的孩子並沒有真正學會如何貢獻、協商或共同解決問題。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"By contrast, carefully designed group activities teach teamwork more directly and inclusively. When children complete a class project, prepare a group presentation, or organise a small charity event, they must divide responsibilities, exchange ideas, manage disagreements, and depend on one another’s effort. These activities also allow adults to guide the process explicitly. A teacher can ask children why one member was ignored, how tasks should be shared more fairly, and what the group should do when someone falls behind. This kind of reflection turns cooperation from a vague experience into a conscious skill. It also prepares children for real-life teamwork, where success usually depends less on physical ability and more on communication, patience, and shared accountability.","chinese":"相比之下，經過精心設計的團體活動能夠更直接、更具包容性地教授團隊合作。 當孩子完成班級專題、準備小組匯報，或組織一場小型慈善活動時，他們必須分配責任、交換想法、處理分歧，並依靠彼此的努力。 這些活動也讓成人能夠明確地引導整個合作過程。 老師可以問孩子，為甚麼某位成員被忽略、任務應如何更公平地分配，以及當有人落後時，小組應該怎樣處理。 這種反思能把合作從一種模糊的經驗，轉化為一項有意識的技能。 它也能讓孩子為現實生活中的團隊合作做好準備，因為在真實世界中，成功通常較少取決於體能，而更多取決於溝通、耐性和共同責任感。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, I completely disagree that team sports are the best way to teach children teamwork. Structured collaborative tasks are more effective because they give every child a meaningful role and teach the actual habits that teamwork requires.","chinese":"總結來說，我完全不同意團隊運動是教導孩子團隊合作的最佳方式。 有結構的合作任務更有效，因為它們能讓每個孩子都擁有有意義的角色，並教會他們團隊合作真正需要的習慣。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"teamwork","chinese":"團隊合作"},{"english":"essential social skill","chinese":"重要社交技能"},{"english":"learn it best through","chinese":"最能透過……學到"},{"english":"team sports","chinese":"團隊運動"},{"english":"introducing children to","chinese":"讓孩子接觸……"},{"english":"football, basketball, or volleyball","chinese":"足球、籃球或排球"},{"english":"the best way to teach","chinese":"教授……的最佳方法"},{"english":"this quality","chinese":"這種品質"},{"english":"a more reliable method","chinese":"更可靠的方法"},{"english":"involve children in","chinese":"讓孩子參與……"},{"english":"structured group tasks","chinese":"結構化小組任務"},{"english":"directly taught","chinese":"被直接教授"},{"english":"monitored","chinese":"被監察"},{"english":"reflected upon","chinese":"被反思"},{"english":"the main weakness of","chinese":"……的主要弱點"},{"english":"reward performance more than cooperation","chinese":"獎勵表現多於合作"},{"english":"competitive game","chinese":"競爭性比賽"},{"english":"become focused on","chinese":"變得專注於……"},{"english":"avoiding blame","chinese":"避免受責備"},{"english":"rather than listening carefully to","chinese":"而不是細心聆聽……"},{"english":"sharing responsibility fairly","chinese":"公平分擔責任"},{"english":"stronger players","chinese":"較強的隊員"},{"english":"dominate the activity","chinese":"主導活動"},{"english":"less confident children","chinese":"較缺乏自信的孩子"},{"english":"be pushed to the side","chinese":"被推到一旁"},{"english":"learn silence rather than teamwork","chinese":"學會沉默而不是團隊合作"},{"english":"school football match","chinese":"學校足球比賽"},{"english":"receive most of the passes","chinese":"接到大部分傳球"},{"english":"the best chance of winning","chinese":"最大勝算"},{"english":"appear united","chinese":"看似團結"},{"english":"genuinely learning how to","chinese":"真正學會如何……"},{"english":"contribute","chinese":"作出貢獻"},{"english":"negotiate","chinese":"協商"},{"english":"solve problems together","chinese":"一起解決問題"},{"english":"by contrast","chinese":"相比之下"},{"english":"carefully designed group activities","chinese":"精心設計的小組活動"},{"english":"more directly and inclusively","chinese":"更直接和更具包容性地"},{"english":"complete a class project","chinese":"完成課堂專題"},{"english":"prepare a group presentation","chinese":"準備小組匯報"},{"english":"organise a small charity event","chinese":"組織小型慈善活動"},{"english":"divide responsibilities","chinese":"分配責任"},{"english":"exchange ideas","chinese":"交流想法"},{"english":"manage disagreements","chinese":"處理分歧"},{"english":"depend on one another's effort","chinese":"依靠彼此的努力"},{"english":"allow adults to","chinese":"讓成年人可以……"},{"english":"guide the process explicitly","chinese":"明確地引導過程"},{"english":"one member was ignored","chinese":"某個成員被忽視"},{"english":"be shared more fairly","chinese":"被更公平地分配"},{"english":"falls behind","chinese":"落後；跟不上"},{"english":"this kind of reflection","chinese":"這種反思"},{"english":"vague experience","chinese":"模糊的經驗"},{"english":"conscious skill","chinese":"有意識的技能"},{"english":"real-life teamwork","chinese":"現實生活中的團隊合作"},{"english":"depend less on","chinese":"較少取決於……"},{"english":"physical ability","chinese":"體能"},{"english":"communication, patience, and shared accountability","chinese":"溝通、耐性和共同問責"},{"english":"structured collaborative tasks","chinese":"結構化協作任務"},{"english":"meaningful role","chinese":"有意義的角色"},{"english":"actual habits","chinese":"實際習慣"},{"english":"teamwork requires","chinese":"團隊合作所需要的"}]},"model-essay-86-ielts-opinion":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-86-ielts-opinion","essayKey":"opinion:86","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-86-ielts-opinion","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/opinions/EdmundBd9OP-Q86","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"Regular physical activity is essential to children’s health, yet I completely disagree that it should be treated only as a parental duty or removed from the school timetable. Schools should continue to provide sports lessons because they ensure equal access to exercise and support children’s wider development.","chinese":"定期進行體能活動對兒童健康至關重要，然而我完全不同意它應該只被視為父母的責任，或應該從學校時間表中移除。 學校應該繼續提供體育課，因為它們能確保所有孩子都有平等的運動機會，並支持兒童更全面的發展。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"The first reason is that leaving physical exercise entirely to parents would create serious inequalities. Some parents have the time, money and knowledge to take their children to parks, sports clubs or swimming lessons, but many do not. Others may work long hours, live in unsafe neighbourhoods or simply underestimate how much movement children need. If schools abandon physical education, the children who already have fewer opportunities outside school will be the first to lose out. By contrast, compulsory sports lessons give every child a regular chance to move, regardless of family background. For example, a child from a low-income household may never join a private football academy, but school PE can still introduce that child to running, teamwork and basic fitness. In this sense, schools act as a safety net, not a substitute for parents.","chinese":"第一個原因是，將體能活動完全交由父母負責，會造成嚴重的不平等。 有些父母有時間、金錢和知識，可以帶孩子去公園、體育俱樂部或游泳課，但許多父母並沒有這些條件。 另一些父母可能長時間工作、住在不安全的社區，或者只是低估了孩子需要多少活動量 如果學校放棄體育教育，那些在校外本來已經較少機會運動的孩子，將會是最先受損的一群 相比之下，必修體育課能給每一個孩子定期活動的機會，不論他們的家庭背景如何。 例如，一個來自低收入家庭的孩子可能永遠不會參加私人足球學院，但學校體育課仍然可以讓這個孩子接觸跑步、團隊合作和基本體能訓練。 從這個意義上說，學校扮演的是安全網的角色，而不是父母的替代品。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"Moreover, sports lessons are not a waste of valuable school time; they make academic time more effective. Children are not machines that can sit at desks all day and absorb information without rest. Physical activity improves concentration, reduces stress and teaches discipline, cooperation and resilience. These qualities matter just as much as exam results because education should prepare young people for life, not only for tests. For instance, a basketball lesson can teach pupils how to follow rules, handle defeat and work with others towards a shared goal. These are practical lessons that cannot be learned as easily from textbooks.","chinese":"此外，體育課並不是浪費寶貴的學校時間；它們反而令學術學習時間更有效。 孩子並不是機器，不能整天坐在書桌前，毫無休息地吸收資訊。 體能活動能提升專注力、減輕壓力，並教會孩子紀律、合作和抗逆力。 這些素質和考試成績一樣重要，因為教育應該讓年輕人為人生作好準備，而不只是為考試作準備。 例如，一堂籃球課可以教學生如何遵守規則、面對失敗，並與他人一起朝著共同目標努力。 這些都是實用的人生課，而它們並不能輕易地從課本中學到。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, I completely disagree with the view that schools should remove sports from the curriculum. Parents certainly influence children’s habits, but schools have a vital responsibility to guarantee regular exercise for all pupils and to educate the whole child.","chinese":"總結來說，我完全不同意學校應該將體育從課程中移除這一觀點。 父母固然會影響孩子的習慣，但學校也有重要責任，去確保所有學生都能定期運動，並讓孩子獲得全面教育。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"regular physical activity","chinese":"定期體能活動"},{"english":"be essential to","chinese":"對……必不可少"},{"english":"children's health","chinese":"兒童健康"},{"english":"be treated only as","chinese":"只被視為……"},{"english":"parental duty","chinese":"父母責任"},{"english":"be removed from","chinese":"從……移除"},{"english":"school timetable","chinese":"學校時間表"},{"english":"continue to provide","chinese":"繼續提供"},{"english":"sports lessons","chinese":"體育課"},{"english":"ensure equal access to","chinese":"確保平等接觸……的機會"},{"english":"exercise","chinese":"運動"},{"english":"wider development","chinese":"更全面的發展"},{"english":"leaving physical exercise entirely to","chinese":"將體能活動完全交給……"},{"english":"create serious inequalities","chinese":"造成嚴重不平等"},{"english":"have the time, money and knowledge to","chinese":"有時間、金錢和知識去……"},{"english":"sports clubs","chinese":"體育會；運動俱樂部"},{"english":"swimming lessons","chinese":"游泳課"},{"english":"work long hours","chinese":"長時間工作"},{"english":"unsafe neighbourhoods","chinese":"不安全的社區"},{"english":"underestimate how much","chinese":"低估……有多少"},{"english":"movement","chinese":"活動量"},{"english":"abandon physical education","chinese":"放棄體育教育"},{"english":"physical education","chinese":"體育教育；體育課"},{"english":"fewer opportunities","chinese":"較少機會"},{"english":"outside school","chinese":"在校外"},{"english":"be the first to lose out","chinese":"最先吃虧"},{"english":"by contrast","chinese":"相比之下"},{"english":"compulsory sports lessons","chinese":"必修體育課"},{"english":"a regular chance to move","chinese":"定期活動身體的機會"},{"english":"regardless of family background","chinese":"不論家庭背景"},{"english":"low-income household","chinese":"低收入家庭"},{"english":"private football academy","chinese":"私人足球學院"},{"english":"school PE","chinese":"學校體育課"},{"english":"introduce that child to","chinese":"讓那個孩子接觸到……"},{"english":"teamwork","chinese":"團隊合作"},{"english":"basic fitness","chinese":"基本體能"},{"english":"act as a safety net","chinese":"充當安全網"},{"english":"substitute for","chinese":"……的替代品"},{"english":"moreover","chinese":"此外"},{"english":"a waste of valuable school time","chinese":"浪費寶貴上課時間"},{"english":"academic time","chinese":"學習時間"},{"english":"more effective","chinese":"更有效"},{"english":"sit at desks all day","chinese":"整天坐在書桌前"},{"english":"absorb information","chinese":"吸收資料"},{"english":"without rest","chinese":"沒有休息"},{"english":"improve concentration","chinese":"提高專注力"},{"english":"reduce stress","chinese":"減輕壓力"},{"english":"teach discipline","chinese":"教導紀律"},{"english":"cooperation and resilience","chinese":"合作和韌性"},{"english":"matter just as much as","chinese":"與……同樣重要"},{"english":"exam results","chinese":"考試成績"},{"english":"prepare young people for life","chinese":"讓年輕人為生活作好準備"},{"english":"not only for tests","chinese":"不只是為考試"},{"english":"basketball lesson","chinese":"籃球課"},{"english":"follow rules","chinese":"遵守規則"},{"english":"handle defeat","chinese":"面對失敗"},{"english":"work with others towards","chinese":"與他人一起為……努力"},{"english":"shared goal","chinese":"共同目標"},{"english":"practical lessons","chinese":"實用課堂；實際教訓"},{"english":"cannot be learned as easily from","chinese":"不能那麼容易從……學到"},{"english":"remove sports from the curriculum","chinese":"將體育從課程中移除"},{"english":"curriculum","chinese":"課程"},{"english":"influence children's habits","chinese":"影響孩子的習慣"},{"english":"a vital responsibility","chinese":"重要責任"},{"english":"guarantee regular exercise","chinese":"保障定期運動"},{"english":"educate the whole child","chinese":"培育孩子的全面發展"}]},"model-essay-87-ielts-opinion":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-87-ielts-opinion","essayKey":"opinion:87","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-87-ielts-opinion","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/opinions/EdmundBd9OP-Q87","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"In modern workplaces, employees are often expected to remain seated for long hours while meeting demanding deadlines. I strongly believe that companies should set aside time for physical exercise during the working day, because this would improve both employee health and workplace performance.","chinese":"在現代職場中，員工經常被期望長時間坐著，同時應付要求很高的截止期限。 我堅定認為，公司應該在工作日中預留時間讓員工進行體育鍛煉，因為這既能改善員工健康，也能提升工作表現。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"The most important reason is that regular movement helps protect workers from the physical and mental damage caused by sedentary jobs. Many office employees spend most of the day in front of a screen, which can lead to back pain, tiredness and stress. If companies allow staff to take a short period for exercise, such as stretching, walking or using a gym, workers are more likely to return to their desks feeling refreshed rather than drained. For example, an accountant who takes a twenty-minute walk after several hours of concentrated work may be able to clear his mind and avoid the sense of exhaustion that often builds up in the afternoon. In this sense, exercise time is not a luxury; it is a practical way to prevent the workplace from slowly damaging people’s well-being.","chinese":"最重要的原因是，定期活動有助於保護員工免受久坐工作所造成的身體和心理損害。 許多辦公室員工一天大部分時間都在螢幕前度過，這可能導致背痛、疲倦和壓力。 如果公司允許員工用一小段時間做運動，例如伸展、步行或使用健身室，員工回到辦公桌時便更可能感到精神恢復，而不是筋疲力盡。 例如，一位會計師在數小時專注工作後散步二十分鐘，可能能夠清理思緒，並避免下午經常累積起來的疲憊感。 從這個意義上說，運動時間並不是奢侈品；它是一種實際的方法，可以防止職場慢慢損害人們的身心健康。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"It is also likely to benefit employers themselves. A healthy workforce tends to be more energetic, focused and loyal, so the time spent on exercise can be recovered through better productivity. Some managers may worry that exercise breaks reduce working hours, but this view is rather short-sighted. Employees who are tired, inactive and under pressure rarely produce their best work simply because they sit at their desks for longer. By contrast, when a company encourages exercise, it sends a clear message that staff are valued as human beings, not just as machines for producing output. This can strengthen morale and reduce unnecessary absence.","chinese":"這也很可能會讓僱主本身受益。 健康的員工隊伍往往更有活力、更專注，也更忠誠，因此花在運動上的時間可以透過更高的生產力補回來。 有些管理者可能會擔心運動休息會減少工作時間，但這種看法相當短視。 疲倦、缺乏活動並承受壓力的員工，很少會僅僅因為坐在辦公桌前更久，就能交出最佳工作表現。 相比之下，當一家公司鼓勵運動時，它傳達出一個清晰的訊息：員工是作為人被重視，而不只是被視為產出工作的機器。 這可以增強士氣，並減少不必要的缺勤。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, I firmly support the idea that companies should provide exercise time during the day. Done sensibly, it protects employees’ health and helps businesses build a more productive, humane workplace.","chinese":"總結來說，我堅定支持公司應該在一天中提供運動時間這個想法。 如果做得合理，它能保護員工健康，並幫助企業建立一個更具生產力、也更有人性的工作場所。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"modern workplaces","chinese":"現代工作場所"},{"english":"be expected to","chinese":"被期望去……"},{"english":"remain seated","chinese":"保持坐着"},{"english":"for long hours","chinese":"長時間"},{"english":"demanding deadlines","chinese":"要求高的限期"},{"english":"strongly believe that","chinese":"強烈相信……"},{"english":"set aside time for","chinese":"預留時間給……"},{"english":"physical exercise","chinese":"體能運動"},{"english":"during the working day","chinese":"在工作日內"},{"english":"employee health","chinese":"員工健康"},{"english":"workplace performance","chinese":"工作場所表現"},{"english":"the most important reason","chinese":"最重要的原因"},{"english":"regular movement","chinese":"定期活動身體"},{"english":"protect workers from","chinese":"保護員工免受……"},{"english":"physical and mental damage","chinese":"身體和精神上的損害"},{"english":"caused by","chinese":"由……造成"},{"english":"sedentary jobs","chinese":"久坐的工作"},{"english":"office employees","chinese":"辦公室員工"},{"english":"spend most of the day","chinese":"花大半天"},{"english":"in front of a screen","chinese":"在螢幕前"},{"english":"lead to","chinese":"導致"},{"english":"back pain","chinese":"背痛"},{"english":"tiredness and stress","chinese":"疲倦和壓力"},{"english":"allow staff to","chinese":"允許員工去……"},{"english":"take a short period for","chinese":"抽一小段時間去……"},{"english":"stretching","chinese":"伸展運動"},{"english":"using a gym","chinese":"使用健身室"},{"english":"be more likely to","chinese":"更有可能"},{"english":"return to their desks","chinese":"回到辦公桌"},{"english":"feeling refreshed","chinese":"感到精神恢復"},{"english":"rather than drained","chinese":"而不是筋疲力盡"},{"english":"accountant","chinese":"會計師"},{"english":"twenty-minute walk","chinese":"二十分鐘步行"},{"english":"concentrated work","chinese":"高度集中的工作"},{"english":"clear his mind","chinese":"清理思緒"},{"english":"avoid the sense of exhaustion","chinese":"避免疲憊感"},{"english":"build up","chinese":"逐漸累積"},{"english":"in the afternoon","chinese":"在下午"},{"english":"in this sense","chinese":"從這個意義上說"},{"english":"not a luxury","chinese":"不是奢侈品"},{"english":"practical way to","chinese":"……的實際方法"},{"english":"prevent the workplace from","chinese":"防止工作場所……"},{"english":"slowly damaging","chinese":"慢慢損害"},{"english":"well-being","chinese":"身心健康"},{"english":"be likely to benefit","chinese":"很可能令……受惠"},{"english":"employers themselves","chinese":"僱主本身"},{"english":"healthy workforce","chinese":"健康的員工隊伍"},{"english":"tend to be","chinese":"往往會"},{"english":"energetic, focused and loyal","chinese":"精力充沛、專注和忠誠"},{"english":"time spent on","chinese":"花在……上的時間"},{"english":"be recovered through","chinese":"透過……補回"},{"english":"better productivity","chinese":"更高生產力"},{"english":"exercise breaks","chinese":"運動休息時間"},{"english":"reduce working hours","chinese":"減少工作時間"},{"english":"short-sighted","chinese":"短視的"},{"english":"inactive","chinese":"缺乏活動的"},{"english":"under pressure","chinese":"承受壓力"},{"english":"produce their best work","chinese":"發揮最佳工作表現"},{"english":"sit at their desks for longer","chinese":"在辦公桌前坐更久"},{"english":"by contrast","chinese":"相比之下"},{"english":"encourages exercise","chinese":"鼓勵運動"},{"english":"send a clear message","chinese":"傳達清晰信息"},{"english":"be valued as human beings","chinese":"作為人而受到重視"},{"english":"producing output","chinese":"製造產出"},{"english":"strengthen morale","chinese":"提升士氣"},{"english":"reduce unnecessary absence","chinese":"減少不必要的缺勤"},{"english":"firmly support","chinese":"堅定支持"},{"english":"provide exercise time","chinese":"提供運動時間"},{"english":"done sensibly","chinese":"如果安排得宜"},{"english":"productive, humane workplace","chinese":"高效而人性化的工作場所"}]},"model-essay-88-ielts-opinion":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-88-ielts-opinion","essayKey":"opinion:88","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-88-ielts-opinion","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/opinions/EdmundBd9OP-Q88","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"An unhealthy rise in body weight has led some people to argue that every university student should be required to study sport, regardless of their degree. I completely disagree with this proposal. Making sport compulsory across all courses would distort the purpose of higher education and offer a blunt response to a complex health problem.","chinese":"體重不健康地上升，使一些人認為每一位大學生都應該被要求修讀體育，不論他們攻讀的是甚麼學位。 我完全不同意這項建議。 把體育變成所有課程的必修科，會扭曲高等教育的目的，並且以一種粗糙的方式回應一個複雜的健康問題。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"The first reason is that university programmes should be built around academic and professional priorities, not a one-size-fits-all activity requirement. A medical student, an engineering student and a literature student already face demanding lectures, projects, placements and deadlines. Adding an assessed sport module would take time away from the specialist training that their degrees are meant to provide. Universities are not health camps; their central role is to cultivate knowledge, judgement and employable expertise. If every course is forced to carry the same sports requirement, curricula become less flexible, and students may see exercise not as a healthy habit but as another box to tick.","chinese":"第一個原因是，大學課程應該圍繞學術和專業優先事項來設計，而不是圍繞一項一刀切的活動要求。 醫科,工程學生和文學學生本身已經要面對要求很高的講座、項目、實習和截止日期 加入一個需要評核的體育單元，會佔用他們本應用於專業訓練的時間，而這正是他們的學位應該提供的核心內容。 大學不是健康訓練營；它們的核心角色是培養知識、判斷力和具就業價值的專業能力。 如果每個課程都被迫加入相同的體育要求，課程設計就會變得較不靈活，而學生也可能不再把運動視為一種健康習慣，而只是另一項需要完成的任務。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"A second problem is that compulsory sport is unlikely to tackle the real causes of weight gain. Many students become overweight because of poor diet, stress, lack of sleep, long screen time and habits formed long before they enter university. Forcing them to play sport for a few hours a week may change their timetable, but it will not necessarily change their lifestyle. In fact, compulsion can backfire: students who dislike sport may participate reluctantly, do the bare minimum, or associate exercise with embarrassment and punishment. Universities would be wiser to provide accessible gyms, affordable healthy food, counselling, active travel schemes and optional fitness classes. These measures encourage students to build routines they can sustain.","chinese":"第二個問題是，強制體育不太可能處理體重增加的真正原因。 許多學生變得超重，是因為飲食不良、壓力、睡眠不足、長時間使用螢幕，以及早在進入大學之前已經形成的習慣。 強迫他們每週做幾小時運動，或許能改變他們的時間表，但未必能真正改變他們的生活方式。 事實上，強制措施可能適得其反：不喜歡運動的學生可能只是勉強參與、做最低限度的要求，甚至把運動和尷尬、懲罰聯繫起來。 大學更明智的做法，是提供容易使用的健身設施、價格可負擔的健康食物、輔導服務、鼓勵步行或騎車的出行計劃，以及自願參加的健身課程。 這些措施能鼓勵學生建立他們可以長期維持的日常習慣"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, I do not agree that sport should be made a compulsory module on every degree course. Universities should support healthier living, but they should not sacrifice academic purpose or pretend that obesity can be solved by forcing all students into the same sporting mold.","chinese":"總結來說，我不同意體育應該被列為每一個學位課程的必修單元。 大學應該支持更健康的生活方式，但它們不應犧牲學術目的，也不應假裝只要把所有學生強行套入同一種運動模式，就可以解決肥胖問題。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"unhealthy rise in body weight","chinese":"體重不健康地上升"},{"english":"has led some people to argue that","chinese":"令一些人主張……"},{"english":"be required to","chinese":"被要求去……"},{"english":"regardless of","chinese":"不論；不管"},{"english":"this proposal","chinese":"這項建議"},{"english":"making sport compulsory","chinese":"將體育列為必修"},{"english":"across all courses","chinese":"在所有課程中"},{"english":"distort the purpose of","chinese":"扭曲……的目的"},{"english":"higher education","chinese":"高等教育"},{"english":"a blunt response to","chinese":"對……的粗糙回應"},{"english":"complex health problem","chinese":"複雜的健康問題"},{"english":"university programmes","chinese":"大學課程"},{"english":"be built around","chinese":"圍繞……而設計"},{"english":"academic and professional priorities","chinese":"學術和專業上的優先事項"},{"english":"one-size-fits-all activity requirement","chinese":"一刀切的活動要求"},{"english":"medical student","chinese":"醫科學生"},{"english":"engineering student","chinese":"工程學生"},{"english":"literature student","chinese":"文學學生"},{"english":"demanding lectures","chinese":"要求高的講課"},{"english":"placements and deadlines","chinese":"實習安排和限期"},{"english":"assessed sport module","chinese":"受評核的體育單元"},{"english":"take time away from","chinese":"佔用……的時間"},{"english":"specialist training","chinese":"專門訓練"},{"english":"be meant to provide","chinese":"旨在提供"},{"english":"health camps","chinese":"健康訓練營"},{"english":"central role","chinese":"核心角色"},{"english":"cultivate knowledge","chinese":"培養知識"},{"english":"judgement","chinese":"判斷力"},{"english":"employable expertise","chinese":"有助就業的專業知識"},{"english":"be forced to carry","chinese":"被迫加入"},{"english":"sports requirement","chinese":"體育要求"},{"english":"curricula become less flexible","chinese":"課程變得較不靈活"},{"english":"healthy habit","chinese":"健康習慣"},{"english":"another box to tick","chinese":"另一項要完成的指定任務"},{"english":"compulsory sport","chinese":"強制體育"},{"english":"be unlikely to","chinese":"不大可能"},{"english":"tackle the real causes of","chinese":"處理……的真正成因"},{"english":"weight gain","chinese":"體重增加"},{"english":"become overweight","chinese":"變得超重"},{"english":"poor diet","chinese":"不良飲食"},{"english":"lack of sleep","chinese":"睡眠不足"},{"english":"long screen time","chinese":"長時間使用螢幕"},{"english":"habits formed long before","chinese":"早已形成的習慣"},{"english":"enter university","chinese":"入讀大學"},{"english":"forcing them to","chinese":"強迫他們去……"},{"english":"for a few hours a week","chinese":"每星期幾小時"},{"english":"change their timetable","chinese":"改變他們的時間表"},{"english":"not necessarily","chinese":"不一定"},{"english":"in fact","chinese":"事實上"},{"english":"compulsion","chinese":"強制"},{"english":"backfire","chinese":"產生反效果"},{"english":"participate reluctantly","chinese":"勉強參與"},{"english":"do the bare minimum","chinese":"只做最低限度"},{"english":"associate exercise with","chinese":"將運動與……聯繫起來"},{"english":"embarrassment and punishment","chinese":"尷尬和懲罰"},{"english":"be wiser to provide","chinese":"更明智的是提供……"},{"english":"accessible gyms","chinese":"容易使用的健身室"},{"english":"affordable healthy food","chinese":"可負擔的健康食物"},{"english":"counselling","chinese":"輔導服務"},{"english":"active travel schemes","chinese":"主動出行計劃"},{"english":"optional fitness classes","chinese":"自選健身課程"},{"english":"encourage students to","chinese":"鼓勵學生去……"},{"english":"build routines","chinese":"建立日常習慣"},{"english":"sustain","chinese":"維持"},{"english":"be made a compulsory module","chinese":"被列為必修單元"},{"english":"degree course","chinese":"學位課程"},{"english":"support healthier living","chinese":"支持更健康的生活"},{"english":"sacrifice academic purpose","chinese":"犧牲學術目的"},{"english":"pretend that","chinese":"假裝……"},{"english":"obesity","chinese":"肥胖問題"},{"english":"be solved by","chinese":"透過……解決"},{"english":"force all students into","chinese":"強迫所有學生進入……"},{"english":"the same sporting mold","chinese":"同一套體育模式"}]},"model-essay-89-ielts-opinion":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-89-ielts-opinion","essayKey":"opinion:89","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-89-ielts-opinion","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/opinions/EdmundBd9OP-Q89","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"Professional athletes occupy a powerful place in modern society. Because many children admire them not only for their skill but also for their image, I completely agree that they have a responsibility to behave as good role models at all times.","chinese":"職業運動員在現代社會中佔有非常有影響力的位置。 由於許多孩子崇拜他們，不只是因為他們的技術，也因為他們的形象，所以我完全同意他們有責任在任何時候都表現得像良好的榜樣。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"The first reason is that children often copy what famous sports figures do before they fully understand why they are doing it. A young fan may watch a footballer arguing with a referee, insulting an opponent, or boasting online, and see that behaviour as a sign of confidence rather than immaturity. Over time, this can normalise arrogance, aggression, and poor discipline. By contrast, when athletes show respect after defeat, train consistently, and accept responsibility for mistakes, they turn success into something children can actually learn from. Their behaviour becomes a silent lesson, and for impressionable minds that lesson can be louder than any classroom speech.","chinese":"第一個原因是，孩子往往會模仿著名體育人物的行為，甚至在他們還未完全明白為甚麼那樣做之前便已經開始模仿。 一位年輕球迷可能會看到一名足球員與裁判爭吵、侮辱對手，或在網上自誇，並把這些行為視為自信的表現，而不是不成熟。 長遠而言，這可能會使傲慢、攻擊性和缺乏紀律的行為變得正常化。 相比之下，當運動員在失敗後表現出尊重、持續訓練，並為錯誤承擔責任時，他們便能把成功轉化成孩子真正可以學習的東西。 他們的行為會成為一堂無聲的課，而對容易受影響的孩子來說，這堂課可能比任何課堂演講都更有力量。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"Another important point is that professional sportspeople benefit directly from public admiration. Their fame, sponsorships, and high salaries are built partly on the loyalty of ordinary fans, including young supporters who buy shirts, watch matches, and follow them online. Since they enjoy these privileges, they should also accept the social duty that comes with them. This does not mean they must live like saints or pretend to be perfect. It simply means that, whether they are on the field, in interviews, online, or away from competition, they should show basic decency, restraint, and integrity. For example, an athlete who avoids drugs, treats teammates respectfully, and apologises sincerely after a mistake sends a far healthier message than one who hides behind talent as an excuse for bad conduct.","chinese":"另一個重要觀點是，職業運動員直接受益於公眾的仰慕。 他們的名氣、贊助和高薪，在一定程度上建立於普通球迷的忠誠之上，包括那些購買球衣、觀看比賽，並在網上追蹤他們的年輕支持者。 既然他們享有這些特權，他們也應該接受隨之而來的社會責任。 這並不代表他們必須像聖人一樣生活，或者假裝自己完美無缺。 這只是意味著，無論他們是在球場上、接受訪問時、在網上，還是離開比賽場合，他們都應該表現出基本的得體、克制和誠信。 例如，一位遠離毒品、尊重隊友，並在犯錯後真誠道歉的運動員，所傳達的信息遠比一位用天賦作為不良行為藉口的運動員健康得多。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, I strongly agree that professional sportspeople should be good role models at all times. Their influence on children is too great to be treated casually, and their privileged position makes responsible behaviour not a burden, but part of the job.","chinese":"總結來說，我強烈同意職業運動員應該在任何時候都成為良好的榜樣。 他們對孩子的影響太大，不能被隨便看待，而他們所處的優越位置，也使負責任的行為不是一種負擔，而是這份工作的一部分。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"professional athletes","chinese":"職業運動員"},{"english":"occupy a powerful place","chinese":"佔有重要而有影響力的位置"},{"english":"modern society","chinese":"現代社會"},{"english":"admire them not only for","chinese":"欣賞他們不只是因為……"},{"english":"their skill","chinese":"他們的技術"},{"english":"their image","chinese":"他們的形象"},{"english":"have a responsibility to","chinese":"有責任去……"},{"english":"behave as","chinese":"表現得像……"},{"english":"good role models","chinese":"好榜樣"},{"english":"at all times","chinese":"在任何時候"},{"english":"famous sports figures","chinese":"著名體育人物"},{"english":"fully understand why","chinese":"完全明白為甚麼"},{"english":"a young fan","chinese":"年輕粉絲"},{"english":"arguing with a referee","chinese":"與裁判爭論"},{"english":"insulting an opponent","chinese":"侮辱對手"},{"english":"boasting online","chinese":"在網上吹噓"},{"english":"see that behaviour as","chinese":"將那種行為視為……"},{"english":"a sign of confidence","chinese":"自信的表現"},{"english":"rather than immaturity","chinese":"而不是不成熟"},{"english":"over time","chinese":"隨着時間過去"},{"english":"normalise arrogance","chinese":"令傲慢變得正常化"},{"english":"aggression","chinese":"攻擊性"},{"english":"poor discipline","chinese":"缺乏紀律"},{"english":"by contrast","chinese":"相比之下"},{"english":"show respect after defeat","chinese":"失敗後表現尊重"},{"english":"train consistently","chinese":"持續訓練"},{"english":"accept responsibility for","chinese":"為……承擔責任"},{"english":"turn success into","chinese":"將成功轉化成……"},{"english":"learn from","chinese":"從……中學習"},{"english":"a silent lesson","chinese":"無聲的教訓"},{"english":"impressionable minds","chinese":"容易受影響的心智"},{"english":"louder than any classroom speech","chinese":"比任何課堂演講更有力"},{"english":"professional sportspeople","chinese":"職業運動員"},{"english":"benefit directly from","chinese":"直接受惠於……"},{"english":"public admiration","chinese":"公眾仰慕"},{"english":"fame","chinese":"名氣"},{"english":"sponsorships","chinese":"贊助"},{"english":"high salaries","chinese":"高薪"},{"english":"be built partly on","chinese":"部分建基於……"},{"english":"the loyalty of ordinary fans","chinese":"普通球迷的支持和忠誠"},{"english":"young supporters","chinese":"年輕支持者"},{"english":"watch matches","chinese":"觀看比賽"},{"english":"follow them online","chinese":"在網上追蹤他們"},{"english":"enjoy these privileges","chinese":"享有這些特權"},{"english":"accept the social duty","chinese":"承擔社會責任"},{"english":"comes with them","chinese":"隨之而來"},{"english":"live like saints","chinese":"像聖人般生活"},{"english":"pretend to be perfect","chinese":"假裝完美"},{"english":"on the field","chinese":"在球場上"},{"english":"in interviews","chinese":"在訪問中"},{"english":"away from competition","chinese":"離開比賽場合時"},{"english":"basic decency","chinese":"基本得體和正派"},{"english":"restraint","chinese":"克制"},{"english":"integrity","chinese":"誠信；正直"},{"english":"avoid drugs","chinese":"避免毒品"},{"english":"treat teammates respectfully","chinese":"尊重地對待隊友"},{"english":"apologise sincerely after","chinese":"在……之後真誠道歉"},{"english":"send a far healthier message","chinese":"傳達健康得多的信息"},{"english":"hide behind talent","chinese":"躲在天賦背後"},{"english":"as an excuse for","chinese":"作為……的藉口"},{"english":"bad conduct","chinese":"不良行為"},{"english":"strongly agree that","chinese":"強烈同意……"},{"english":"influence on children","chinese":"對兒童的影響"},{"english":"too great to be treated casually","chinese":"太大而不能隨便看待"},{"english":"privileged position","chinese":"優越地位"},{"english":"responsible behaviour","chinese":"負責任的行為"},{"english":"not a burden, but part of the job","chinese":"不是負擔，而是工作的一部分"}]},"model-essay-90-ielts-opinion":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-90-ielts-opinion","essayKey":"opinion:90","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-90-ielts-opinion","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/opinions/EdmundBd9OP-Q90","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"Some people believe that combat sports such as boxing and martial arts should be removed from television and international sporting events because they involve physical aggression. I completely disagree with this view. Although these sports must be regulated carefully, banning them would be an excessive response that misunderstands both their nature and social value.","chinese":"有些人認為，拳擊和武術等搏擊運動應該從電視和國際體育賽事中移除，因為它們涉及身體上的攻擊性。 我完全不同意這個觀點。 雖然這些運動必須受到謹慎規管，但禁止它們會是一種過度反應，而且誤解了它們的本質和社會價值。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"The first reason is that organised combat sports are not the same as uncontrolled violence. In a street fight, there are no rules, medical checks, or clear limits. By contrast, professional boxing, judo, karate, and taekwondo are built around agreed rules, trained referees, protective procedures, and fair contests. This structure turns physical force into disciplined competition. When audiences watch a properly supervised match, they are not simply seeing people hurt one another; they are seeing athletes control fear, respect boundaries, and accept victory or defeat with restraint. For example, a young viewer who sees a referee stop a fight when one competitor is at risk can learn that strength must be governed by rules. Removing these sports from television would not remove aggression from society; it may simply push interest towards less regulated entertainment.","chinese":"第一個原因是，有組織的搏擊運動並不等同於失控的暴力。 在街頭打鬥中，沒有規則、醫療檢查，也沒有清晰的限制。 相比之下，職業拳擊、柔道、空手道和跆拳道都是建立在共同認可的規則、受訓裁判、保護程序和公平競賽之上的。 這種結構把身體力量轉化為有紀律的競技。 當觀眾觀看一場受到妥善監督的比賽時，他們看到的並不只是人們互相傷害；他們看到的是運動員控制恐懼、尊重界線，並以克制的態度接受勝利或失敗。 例如，一位年輕觀眾看到裁判在其中一名選手有危險時中止比賽，便可以學到力量必須受到規則約束。 把這些運動從電視上移除並不會消除社會中的攻擊性；這可能只是把人們的興趣推向較少受到規管的娛樂形式。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"A ban on international competition would also be unfair to athletes and damaging to sport as a whole. Many combat sports require years of sacrifice, technical training, and mental discipline. For competitors from less privileged backgrounds, these events can provide income, national pride, and personal dignity. Moreover, martial arts are often tied to cultural traditions in which respect, patience, and self-control are central values. If they were excluded from global tournaments, society would be treating committed athletes as if they were criminals rather than skilled professionals. A better solution is to improve safety standards, age guidance, and responsible broadcasting, not to erase the sports altogether.","chinese":"禁止它們出現在國際比賽中，也會對運動員不公平，並對整個體育界造成損害。 許多搏擊運動都需要多年犧牲、技術訓練和心理紀律。 對於來自較不優越背景的參賽者而言，這些賽事可以帶來收入、民族自豪感和個人尊嚴 此外，武術往往與文化傳統相連，而在這些傳統中，尊重、耐性和自我控制都是核心價值。 如果它們被排除在全球性賽事之外，社會便會把投入訓練的運動員視為罪犯，而不是技術純熟的專業人士。 更好的解決方法是改善安全標準、年齡指引和負責任的播放安排，而不是完全抹去這些運動。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, I strongly disagree that combat sports should be banned from television or international competitions. With proper regulation, they can promote discipline, opportunity, and cultural respect far more effectively than a blanket ban ever could.","chinese":"總結來說，我強烈不同意搏擊運動應該被禁止出現在電視或國際比賽中。 在適當規管之下，它們能夠促進紀律、機會和文化尊重，而這遠比一刀切的禁令更有效"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"combat sports","chinese":"格鬥運動"},{"english":"boxing and martial arts","chinese":"拳擊和武術"},{"english":"be removed from","chinese":"從……移除"},{"english":"international sporting events","chinese":"國際體育賽事"},{"english":"involve physical aggression","chinese":"涉及肢體攻擊性"},{"english":"completely disagree with","chinese":"完全不同意……"},{"english":"be regulated carefully","chinese":"受到小心規管"},{"english":"banning them","chinese":"禁止它們"},{"english":"an excessive response","chinese":"過度反應"},{"english":"misunderstand both their nature and social value","chinese":"誤解它們的本質和社會價值"},{"english":"organised combat sports","chinese":"有組織的格鬥運動"},{"english":"uncontrolled violence","chinese":"不受控制的暴力"},{"english":"street fight","chinese":"街頭打鬥"},{"english":"medical checks","chinese":"醫療檢查"},{"english":"clear limits","chinese":"清晰界限"},{"english":"by contrast","chinese":"相比之下"},{"english":"agreed rules","chinese":"約定好的規則"},{"english":"trained referees","chinese":"受過訓練的裁判"},{"english":"protective procedures","chinese":"保護程序"},{"english":"fair contests","chinese":"公平競賽"},{"english":"physical force","chinese":"身體力量"},{"english":"disciplined competition","chinese":"有紀律的競賽"},{"english":"properly supervised match","chinese":"受到適當監督的比賽"},{"english":"hurt one another","chinese":"互相傷害"},{"english":"control fear","chinese":"控制恐懼"},{"english":"respect boundaries","chinese":"尊重界限"},{"english":"accept victory or defeat with restraint","chinese":"克制地接受勝利或失敗"},{"english":"young viewer","chinese":"年輕觀眾"},{"english":"referee stop a fight","chinese":"裁判叫停比賽"},{"english":"at risk","chinese":"處於危險中"},{"english":"be governed by rules","chinese":"受規則約束"},{"english":"remove aggression from society","chinese":"消除社會中的攻擊性"},{"english":"push interest towards","chinese":"將興趣推向……"},{"english":"less regulated entertainment","chinese":"較少受規管的娛樂"},{"english":"a ban on international competition","chinese":"禁止國際比賽"},{"english":"damaging to sport as a whole","chinese":"對整個體育界有害"},{"english":"years of sacrifice","chinese":"多年的犧牲"},{"english":"technical training","chinese":"技術訓練"},{"english":"mental discipline","chinese":"心理紀律"},{"english":"competitors from less privileged backgrounds","chinese":"來自較弱勢背景的參賽者"},{"english":"provide income","chinese":"提供收入"},{"english":"national pride","chinese":"國家自豪感"},{"english":"personal dignity","chinese":"個人尊嚴"},{"english":"be tied to","chinese":"與……有關聯"},{"english":"cultural traditions","chinese":"文化傳統"},{"english":"central values","chinese":"核心價值"},{"english":"be excluded from","chinese":"被排除於……之外"},{"english":"global tournaments","chinese":"全球錦標賽"},{"english":"committed athletes","chinese":"投入的運動員"},{"english":"as if they were criminals","chinese":"好像他們是罪犯一樣"},{"english":"rather than skilled professionals","chinese":"而不是熟練的專業人士"},{"english":"improve safety standards","chinese":"改善安全標準"},{"english":"age guidance","chinese":"年齡指引"},{"english":"responsible broadcasting","chinese":"負責任的播放安排"},{"english":"erase the sports altogether","chinese":"完全抹走這些運動"},{"english":"proper regulation","chinese":"適當規管"},{"english":"promote discipline","chinese":"促進紀律"},{"english":"cultural respect","chinese":"文化尊重"},{"english":"blanket ban","chinese":"一刀切禁令"}]},"model-essay-91-ielts-opinion":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-91-ielts-opinion","essayKey":"opinion:91","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-91-ielts-opinion","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/opinions/EdmundBd9OP-Q91","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"Technology has changed not only how people communicate, but also how much effort they put into real social contact. I agree that inventions such as mobile phones are making people less socially interactive, because they often weaken face-to-face communication and replace meaningful conversations with quick, shallow exchanges.","chinese":"科技不但改變了人們溝通的方式，也改變了人們願意投入多少努力進行真正的社交接觸 我同意手機等發明正在使人們變得較少進行社交互動，因為它們往往削弱面對面溝通，並以快速而膚淺的交流取代有意義的對話。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"The first reason is that mobile phones constantly compete for people's attention in social settings. A person may be physically present at a dinner table, in a classroom or at a workplace, but mentally pulled away by messages, notifications and online content. When this happens, conversation becomes fragmented: people listen with half an ear, respond mechanically, and miss the small expressions that make communication warm and personal. For example, it is now common to see friends sitting together in a café while each person silently scrolls through their phone. They are sharing the same space, but not really sharing the same moment. Over time, this habit can make direct interaction feel less natural and less valued.","chinese":"第一個原因是，手機在社交場合中不斷爭奪人們的注意力。 一個人可能身體上在飯桌旁、課室裡或工作場所中，但精神上卻被訊息、通知和網上內容拉走。 當這種情況發生時，對話便會變得零碎：人們只用半邊耳朵聆聽、機械式地回應，並錯過那些使溝通變得溫暖而個人的細微表情。 例如，現在很常見到朋友們一起坐在咖啡店裡，但每個人卻都靜靜地滑著自己的手機。 他們共享著同一個空間，但其實並沒有真正共享同一個時刻。 長遠而言，這種習慣會使直接互動變得較不自然，也較不被重視。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"Another important issue is that mobile phones encourage people to choose convenience over genuine engagement. Sending a short message or reacting with an emoji is easier than meeting someone, having a difficult discussion, or building a relationship through regular conversation. This is especially harmful for younger people, who need practice in reading body language, handling disagreement and speaking confidently with others. If most of their communication takes place behind a screen, they may become less comfortable with spontaneous face-to-face contact. In other words, the phone can become a social shortcut, but one that slowly removes the skills needed for deeper human connection.","chinese":"另一個重要問題是，手機鼓勵人們選擇方便，而不是真正投入地交流。 傳送一則短訊或用一個表情符號作出反應，比起與某人見面、進行困難的討論，或透過定期交談建立關係，都要容易得多。 這對年輕人尤其有害，因為他們需要練習理解肢體語言、處理分歧，以及自信地與他人交談。 如果他們大部分溝通都是在螢幕背後進行，他們便可能變得較不習慣自然即興的面對面接觸。 換言之，手機可以變成一種社交捷徑，但這種捷徑會慢慢削弱建立更深層人際連結所需要的能力。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, I agree that modern technologies, particularly mobile phones, are reducing social interaction. They distract people from those around them and make low-effort digital contact feel like a substitute for real conversation. While they connect us quickly, they can also quietly make us less present, less attentive and less socially confident.","chinese":"總結來說，我同意現代科技，尤其是手機，正在減少人們的社交互動。 它們使人們分心，不再專注於身邊的人，並令低成本的數位接觸感覺像是真實對話的替代品。 雖然它們能讓我們快速連繫彼此，但它們也可能悄悄地使我們變得較不投入、較不專注，也較缺乏社交自信。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"not only how","chinese":"不只是如何……"},{"english":"how much effort","chinese":"多少努力"},{"english":"put into","chinese":"投入於……"},{"english":"real social contact","chinese":"真實社交接觸"},{"english":"inventions such as","chinese":"例如……的發明"},{"english":"mobile phones","chinese":"手提電話"},{"english":"less socially interactive","chinese":"較少社交互動"},{"english":"weaken face-to-face communication","chinese":"削弱面對面溝通"},{"english":"replace meaningful conversations with","chinese":"以……取代有意義的對話"},{"english":"meaningful conversations","chinese":"有意義的對話"},{"english":"quick, shallow exchanges","chinese":"快速而膚淺的交流"},{"english":"constantly compete for","chinese":"不斷爭奪……"},{"english":"people's attention","chinese":"人們的注意力"},{"english":"social settings","chinese":"社交場合"},{"english":"physically present","chinese":"身體在場"},{"english":"mentally pulled away","chinese":"心思被拉走"},{"english":"messages, notifications and online content","chinese":"訊息、通知和網上內容"},{"english":"conversation becomes fragmented","chinese":"對話變得零碎"},{"english":"listen with half an ear","chinese":"心不在焉地聽"},{"english":"respond mechanically","chinese":"機械式地回應"},{"english":"small expressions","chinese":"細微表情"},{"english":"warm and personal","chinese":"溫暖而有人情味"},{"english":"it is now common to","chinese":"現在很常見"},{"english":"sitting together","chinese":"坐在一起"},{"english":"silently scrolls through","chinese":"默默地滑動瀏覽"},{"english":"share the same space","chinese":"共享同一空間"},{"english":"share the same moment","chinese":"共享同一時刻"},{"english":"over time","chinese":"隨着時間過去"},{"english":"direct interaction","chinese":"直接互動"},{"english":"less natural and less valued","chinese":"較不自然，也較不被重視"},{"english":"another important issue","chinese":"另一個重要問題"},{"english":"choose convenience over","chinese":"選擇方便而非……"},{"english":"genuine engagement","chinese":"真誠投入；真正互動"},{"english":"sending a short message","chinese":"發一個短訊"},{"english":"reacting with an emoji","chinese":"用表情符號回應"},{"english":"having a difficult discussion","chinese":"進行艱難的討論"},{"english":"building a relationship through","chinese":"透過……建立關係"},{"english":"regular conversation","chinese":"恆常對話"},{"english":"especially harmful for","chinese":"對……特別有害"},{"english":"need practice in","chinese":"需要練習……"},{"english":"reading body language","chinese":"解讀肢體語言"},{"english":"handling disagreement","chinese":"處理分歧"},{"english":"speaking confidently with","chinese":"自信地與……交談"},{"english":"take place behind a screen","chinese":"在螢幕背後進行"},{"english":"less comfortable with","chinese":"對……較不自在"},{"english":"spontaneous face-to-face contact","chinese":"自然即興的面對面接觸"},{"english":"in other words","chinese":"換句話說"},{"english":"social shortcut","chinese":"社交捷徑"},{"english":"slowly removes","chinese":"慢慢奪走"},{"english":"skills needed for","chinese":"……所需的技能"},{"english":"deeper human connection","chinese":"更深入的人際連繫"},{"english":"modern technologies","chinese":"現代科技"},{"english":"particularly mobile phones","chinese":"尤其是手提電話"},{"english":"reduce social interaction","chinese":"減少社交互動"},{"english":"distract people from","chinese":"令某人分心，忽略……"},{"english":"those around them","chinese":"身邊的人"},{"english":"low-effort digital contact","chinese":"低投入的數碼接觸"},{"english":"feel like a substitute for","chinese":"感覺像是……的替代品"},{"english":"real conversation","chinese":"真實對話"},{"english":"connect us quickly","chinese":"令我們快速連繫"},{"english":"quietly make us less present","chinese":"悄悄令我們較不投入當下"},{"english":"less attentive","chinese":"較不專注"},{"english":"less socially confident","chinese":"社交上較不自信"}]},"model-essay-92-ielts-opinion":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-92-ielts-opinion","essayKey":"opinion:92","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-92-ielts-opinion","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/opinions/EdmundBd9OP-Q92","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"Television and video games have become a normal part of childhood, and many children now spend hours each day in front of a screen. I completely agree that this pattern is harmful to their mental health because it weakens emotional control and replaces healthier forms of social and imaginative play.","chinese":"電視和電子遊戲已經成為童年的正常一部分，而許多孩子現在每天都會花數小時坐在螢幕前。 我完全同意這種模式對他們的心理健康有害，因為它會削弱情緒控制能力，並取代更健康的社交和想像性遊戲形式。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"The first major problem is that excessive screen entertainment can overstimulate the developing mind. Many programmes and games are built around fast movement, instant rewards, loud sounds, and constant visual change. When children are exposed to this for long periods, their minds become used to a high level of stimulation. As a result, ordinary activities such as reading, homework, or conversation may start to feel slow and unrewarding. For example, a child who spends every evening playing action games may become angry when asked to stop, not because he has a bad character, but because his brain has grown used to a quick cycle of challenge, reward, and excitement. Over time, this can erode patience, concentration, and emotional stability.","chinese":"第一個主要問題是，過度的螢幕娛樂可能會過度刺激正在發展中的大腦。 許多節目和遊戲都是圍繞快速動作、即時獎勵、響亮聲音和不斷變化的畫面而設計的。 當孩子長時間接觸這些內容時，他們的大腦便會習慣高強度的刺激。 結果是，閱讀、做功課或交談等普通活動可能開始顯得緩慢而缺乏回報感。 例如，一個每晚都玩動作遊戲的孩子，在被要求停止時可能會變得憤怒，這並不是因為他性格不好，而是因為他的大腦已經習慣了挑戰、獎勵和興奮快速循環的模式。 久而久之，這可能會侵蝕耐性、專注力和情緒穩定性。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"Another reason is that heavy screen use pushes aside the experiences that protect children’s mental health. Children need exercise, sleep, face-to-face friendships, and unstructured play in order to process feelings and build confidence. If television and gaming fill most of their free time, these protective routines are squeezed out. Instead of learning how to negotiate, share, lose gracefully, and solve conflict in the real world, children become spectators or players in an artificial one. A lonely child who goes straight home to video games every day may feel entertained, but not genuinely connected. This can deepen isolation and make social situations feel more difficult later.","chinese":"另一個原因是，大量使用螢幕會擠走那些能保護兒童心理健康的經歷。 兒童需要運動、睡眠、面對面的友誼，以及非結構化的遊戲，才能處理情緒並建立自信。 如果電視和遊戲佔據了大部分的空閒時間，這些具有保護作用的日常活動便會被擠走 孩子不是在真實世界中學習如何協商、分享、體面地面對失敗和解決衝突，而是變成了一個人工世界中的旁觀者或玩家。 一個孤獨的孩子如果每天放學後直接回家打電子遊戲，他可能會感到被娛樂了，但並沒有真正與他人建立聯繫。 這可能會加深孤立感，並使日後的社交場合變得更加困難。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, I completely agree that excessive television viewing and video gaming are damaging to children’s mental health. They may look like harmless entertainment, but when they dominate a child’s daily life, they can weaken emotional control, reduce real-world interaction, and turn childhood into a much narrower experience.","chinese":"總結來說，我完全同意過度觀看電視和玩電子遊戲會損害兒童的心理健康。 它們看起來可能像是無害的娛樂，但當它們主導孩子的日常生活時，便可能削弱情緒控制能力、減少真實世界中的互動，並把童年變成一種狹窄得多的經歷"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"television and video games","chinese":"電視和電子遊戲"},{"english":"a normal part of childhood","chinese":"童年生活中正常的一部分"},{"english":"spend hours each day","chinese":"每天花數小時"},{"english":"in front of a screen","chinese":"在螢幕前"},{"english":"completely agree that","chinese":"完全同意……"},{"english":"this pattern","chinese":"這種模式"},{"english":"be harmful to","chinese":"對……有害"},{"english":"mental health","chinese":"精神健康"},{"english":"weaken emotional control","chinese":"削弱情緒控制"},{"english":"replace healthier forms of","chinese":"取代較健康形式的……"},{"english":"social and imaginative play","chinese":"社交和想像遊戲"},{"english":"the first major problem","chinese":"第一個主要問題"},{"english":"excessive screen entertainment","chinese":"過度的螢幕娛樂"},{"english":"overstimulate","chinese":"過度刺激"},{"english":"the developing mind","chinese":"發展中的心智"},{"english":"be built around","chinese":"圍繞……而設計"},{"english":"fast movement","chinese":"快速動作"},{"english":"instant rewards","chinese":"即時獎勵"},{"english":"loud sounds","chinese":"嘈雜聲音"},{"english":"constant visual change","chinese":"持續的視覺變化"},{"english":"be exposed to","chinese":"接觸到……"},{"english":"for long periods","chinese":"長時間"},{"english":"become used to","chinese":"習慣於……"},{"english":"a high level of stimulation","chinese":"高度刺激"},{"english":"as a result","chinese":"因此"},{"english":"ordinary activities","chinese":"日常活動"},{"english":"start to feel","chinese":"開始覺得"},{"english":"slow and unrewarding","chinese":"緩慢而沒有回報感"},{"english":"playing action games","chinese":"玩動作遊戲"},{"english":"be asked to stop","chinese":"被要求停止"},{"english":"not because","chinese":"並不是因為"},{"english":"bad character","chinese":"性格差"},{"english":"grow used to","chinese":"逐漸習慣"},{"english":"a quick cycle of","chinese":"……的快速循環"},{"english":"challenge, reward, and excitement","chinese":"挑戰、獎勵和興奮感"},{"english":"over time","chinese":"隨着時間過去"},{"english":"erode patience","chinese":"侵蝕耐性"},{"english":"concentration","chinese":"專注力"},{"english":"emotional stability","chinese":"情緒穩定"},{"english":"heavy screen use","chinese":"大量使用螢幕"},{"english":"push aside","chinese":"排擠；擠走"},{"english":"protect children's mental health","chinese":"保護兒童精神健康"},{"english":"face-to-face friendships","chinese":"面對面的友誼"},{"english":"unstructured play","chinese":"非結構化遊戲"},{"english":"in order to","chinese":"為了"},{"english":"process feelings","chinese":"處理情緒"},{"english":"build confidence","chinese":"建立自信"},{"english":"fill most of their free time","chinese":"佔據大部分空餘時間"},{"english":"protective routines","chinese":"具保護作用的日常習慣"},{"english":"be squeezed out","chinese":"被擠走"},{"english":"instead of learning how to","chinese":"而不是學習如何……"},{"english":"negotiate","chinese":"協商"},{"english":"lose gracefully","chinese":"有風度地接受失敗"},{"english":"solve conflict","chinese":"解決衝突"},{"english":"in the real world","chinese":"在現實世界中"},{"english":"spectators or players","chinese":"旁觀者或玩家"},{"english":"an artificial one","chinese":"人造的世界"},{"english":"go straight home to","chinese":"直接回家做……"},{"english":"feel entertained","chinese":"感到被娛樂"},{"english":"genuinely connected","chinese":"真正與人連繫"},{"english":"deepen isolation","chinese":"加深孤立感"},{"english":"social situations","chinese":"社交場合"},{"english":"excessive television viewing","chinese":"過度看電視"},{"english":"video gaming","chinese":"打機；玩電子遊戲"},{"english":"damaging to","chinese":"對……有損害"},{"english":"harmless entertainment","chinese":"無害的娛樂"},{"english":"dominate a child's daily life","chinese":"主導孩子的日常生活"},{"english":"real-world interaction","chinese":"現實世界中的互動"},{"english":"turn childhood into","chinese":"將童年變成……"},{"english":"a much narrower experience","chinese":"狹窄得多的經歷"}]},"model-essay-93-ielts-opinion":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-93-ielts-opinion","essayKey":"opinion:93","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-93-ielts-opinion","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/opinions/EdmundBd9OP-Q93","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"Modern households are increasingly filled with smartphones, tablets and laptops, and it is no longer unusual for parents and children to retreat into separate digital worlds. I fully agree that this trend damages family relationships and weakens communication, because it reduces shared time and changes the way relatives respond to one another.","chinese":"現代家庭中越來越充滿智能手機、平板電腦和手提電腦，而父母和子女各自退回自己的數碼世界，已經不再罕見。 我完全同意這種趨勢會損害家庭關係並削弱溝通，因為它減少了家人共同相處的時間，也改變了親人之間回應彼此的方式。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"The first reason is that personal technology quietly replaces the ordinary moments through which family bonds are built. Family relationships do not usually grow through dramatic conversations; they are strengthened by repeated small interactions, such as eating together, chatting after school, or helping one another with daily tasks. When every family member has a screen in front of them, these simple moments are easily lost. For example, a child may watch videos during dinner while the parents answer work messages, so the meal becomes a silent routine rather than a chance to reconnect. Over time, this habit creates emotional distance, because people may live under the same roof but no longer share the same space in any meaningful sense.","chinese":"第一個原因是，個人科技會悄悄取代那些建立家庭關係的日常時刻。 家庭關係通常不是透過戲劇性的對話而成長；它們是透過反覆出現的小互動而被加強，例如一起吃飯、放學後聊天，或在日常事情上互相幫助。 當每個家庭成員面前都有一個螢幕時，這些簡單的時刻便很容易消失。 例如，一個孩子可能在晚餐時觀看影片，而父母則回覆工作訊息，因此這頓飯便變成一個沉默的例行程序，而不是重新建立聯繫的機會。 久而久之，這種習慣會造成情感距離，因為人們可能住在同一屋簷下，卻不再以任何真正有意義的方式共享同一個空間。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"Another serious problem is that modern devices encourage shallow and fragmented communication. Face-to-face conversation requires attention, eye contact and patience, whereas digital entertainment trains people to expect constant stimulation and quick replies. If a teenager is always wearing headphones or checking social media, parents may find it harder to understand their child’s worries, friendships or behaviour. Similarly, children may begin to see their parents as distant figures who are physically present but mentally elsewhere. This weakens trust, and without trust, small misunderstandings can easily grow into family tension.","chinese":"另一個嚴重問題是，現代設備會助長膚淺而零碎的溝通。 面對面的交談需要專注、眼神接觸和耐性，而數碼娛樂則訓練人們期待持續刺激和快速回覆。 如果一個青少年總是戴著耳機或查看社交媒體，父母可能會更難理解孩子的煩惱、友誼或行為。 同樣地，孩子也可能開始把父母看成是遙遠的人物：身體上在場，但精神上卻在別處。 這會削弱信任，而沒有信任，小小的誤解也很容易發展成家庭緊張。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, I completely agree that individual ownership of modern technology can lead to a breakdown in family relationships and communication. By stealing everyday interaction and replacing deep conversation with distraction, personal devices can turn the family home from a shared living space into a collection of isolated private worlds.","chinese":"總結來說，我完全同意個人擁有現代科技產品可能導致家庭關係和溝通破裂。 透過偷走日常互動，並以分心取代深入交談，個人設備可以把家庭住所從一個共享的生活空間，變成一個個孤立私人世界的集合。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"modern households","chinese":"現代家庭"},{"english":"be increasingly filled with","chinese":"越來越充滿……"},{"english":"smartphones, tablets and laptops","chinese":"智能電話、平板電腦和手提電腦"},{"english":"it is no longer unusual for","chinese":"……已不再罕見"},{"english":"retreat into","chinese":"退到；躲進"},{"english":"separate digital worlds","chinese":"各自分離的數碼世界"},{"english":"fully agree that","chinese":"完全同意……"},{"english":"damage family relationships","chinese":"損害家庭關係"},{"english":"weaken communication","chinese":"削弱溝通"},{"english":"shared time","chinese":"共同相處的時間"},{"english":"respond to one another","chinese":"互相回應"},{"english":"personal technology","chinese":"個人科技"},{"english":"quietly replaces","chinese":"悄悄取代"},{"english":"ordinary moments","chinese":"平凡時刻"},{"english":"family bonds","chinese":"家庭感情；家庭聯繫"},{"english":"be built through","chinese":"透過……建立"},{"english":"dramatic conversations","chinese":"戲劇性的對話"},{"english":"be strengthened by","chinese":"透過……加強"},{"english":"repeated small interactions","chinese":"重複的小互動"},{"english":"eating together","chinese":"一起吃飯"},{"english":"chatting after school","chinese":"放學後聊天"},{"english":"daily tasks","chinese":"日常事務"},{"english":"a screen in front of them","chinese":"面前有一個螢幕"},{"english":"simple moments","chinese":"簡單時刻"},{"english":"be easily lost","chinese":"很容易失去"},{"english":"watch videos during dinner","chinese":"晚飯時看影片"},{"english":"answer work messages","chinese":"回覆工作訊息"},{"english":"silent routine","chinese":"沉默的例行公事"},{"english":"rather than a chance to reconnect","chinese":"而不是重新聯繫的機會"},{"english":"reconnect","chinese":"重新聯繫"},{"english":"over time","chinese":"隨着時間過去"},{"english":"emotional distance","chinese":"情感距離"},{"english":"live under the same roof","chinese":"住在同一屋簷下"},{"english":"share the same space","chinese":"共享同一空間"},{"english":"in any meaningful sense","chinese":"在任何有意義的層面上"},{"english":"another serious problem","chinese":"另一個嚴重問題"},{"english":"modern devices","chinese":"現代電子裝置"},{"english":"shallow and fragmented communication","chinese":"膚淺而零碎的溝通"},{"english":"face-to-face conversation","chinese":"面對面交談"},{"english":"eye contact","chinese":"眼神接觸"},{"english":"whereas","chinese":"而；然而"},{"english":"digital entertainment","chinese":"數碼娛樂"},{"english":"constant stimulation","chinese":"持續刺激"},{"english":"quick replies","chinese":"快速回覆"},{"english":"check social media","chinese":"查看社交媒體"},{"english":"find it harder to","chinese":"發覺更難去……"},{"english":"friendships or behaviour","chinese":"友誼或行為"},{"english":"distant figures","chinese":"疏離的人物"},{"english":"physically present","chinese":"身體在場"},{"english":"mentally elsewhere","chinese":"心不在焉"},{"english":"weaken trust","chinese":"削弱信任"},{"english":"small misunderstandings","chinese":"小誤會"},{"english":"family tension","chinese":"家庭緊張關係"},{"english":"individual ownership of","chinese":"個人擁有……"},{"english":"lead to","chinese":"導致"},{"english":"a breakdown in","chinese":"……的破裂"},{"english":"stealing everyday interaction","chinese":"奪走日常互動"},{"english":"deep conversation","chinese":"深入交談"},{"english":"replace deep conversation with distraction","chinese":"以分心取代深入交談"},{"english":"personal devices","chinese":"個人電子裝置"},{"english":"shared living space","chinese":"共享生活空間"},{"english":"a collection of isolated private worlds","chinese":"一堆孤立的私人世界"}]},"model-essay-94-ielts-opinion":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-94-ielts-opinion","essayKey":"opinion:94","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-94-ielts-opinion","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/opinions/EdmundBd9OP-Q94","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"Travel content has become an established part of modern entertainment, from television documentaries to short videos posted by influencers. Some argue that because people can now see foreign cities, landscapes and cultures on a screen, they will be less prepared to spend money on overseas trips. I completely disagree with this view, as digital travel content usually stimulates curiosity rather than replacing real travel, and the experience of being abroad cannot be reproduced through media.","chinese":"旅遊內容已成為現代娛樂中既定的一部分，從電視紀錄片到網紅發布的短影片皆是如此 有些人認為，由於人們現在可以透過螢幕看到外國城市、風景和文化，他們便會較不願意花錢到海外旅行。 我完全不同意這個觀點，因為數位旅遊內容通常會激發好奇心，而不是取代真正的旅行；而身處外國的體驗也無法透過媒體被複製。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"The first reason is that travel programmes and online videos often act as a gateway to tourism. When viewers see clear blue water in Greece, street food in Thailand or ancient streets in Italy, they are not simply ticking these places off a list; they are being invited to imagine themselves there. Social media, in particular, turns destinations into living postcards, making people feel that a place is reachable, desirable and worth saving for. For example, a person who watches several videos about Japan may become more interested in visiting temples, trying local food and experiencing the atmosphere in person. In this sense, online travel content is more likely to spark curiosity than extinguish it.","chinese":"第一個原因是，旅遊節目和網上影片往往會成為人們走向旅遊的入口。 當觀眾看到希臘清澈湛藍的海水、泰國的街頭美食，或意大利古老的街道時，他們並不只是把這些地方從清單上劃掉；他們其實是在被邀請去想像自己身處其中。 尤其是社交媒體，會把旅遊目的地變成生動的明信片，讓人們覺得一個地方是可到達的、令人嚮往的，也是值得為其儲錢的。 例如，一個看過幾段關於日本影片的人，可能會變得更想親身參觀寺廟、品嘗當地食物，並感受那裡的氣氛。 從這個角度來看，網上旅遊內容更有可能點燃好奇心，而不是熄滅它。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"More importantly, watching a destination is fundamentally different from living it. A screen can show the colour of a market or the shape of a mountain, but it cannot reproduce the smell of local food, the pressure of a crowded train, or the small conversations that make travel memorable. People do not pay for foreign trips merely to collect information; they pay for freedom, discovery and a break from their normal routines. Even a beautifully filmed documentary remains second-hand experience, whereas travelling abroad gives people direct contact with places and people that may change how they see the world.","chinese":"更重要的是，觀看一個目的地和親身經歷它，在本質上是完全不同的。 螢幕可以呈現市場的色彩或山脈的形狀，但它無法重現當地食物的氣味、擁擠列車中的壓迫感，或那些令旅行變得難忘的小小對話。 人們花錢到外國旅行，並不只是為了收集資訊；他們付錢是為了自由、探索，以及暫時脫離日常生活的規律。 即使是一部拍攝精美的紀錄片，也始終只是二手經驗；相比之下，出國旅行能讓人們直接接觸地方和人，而這些接觸可能會改變他們看待世界的方式。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, I disagree that travel media will reduce people’s willingness to pay for international travel. It may entertain audiences at home, but it more often fuels their desire to go abroad and experience the world first-hand.","chinese":"總結來說，我不同意旅遊媒體會降低人們願意為國際旅行付費的意願。 它或許能娛樂留在家中的觀眾，但更多時候，它會激發他們出國並親身體驗世界的渴望"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"travel content","chinese":"旅遊內容"},{"english":"an established part of","chinese":"……中固定的一部分"},{"english":"modern entertainment","chinese":"現代娛樂"},{"english":"television documentaries","chinese":"電視紀錄片"},{"english":"short videos posted by influencers","chinese":"由網紅發布的短片"},{"english":"foreign cities, landscapes and cultures","chinese":"外國城市、風景和文化"},{"english":"on a screen","chinese":"在螢幕上"},{"english":"be less prepared to","chinese":"較不願意去……"},{"english":"spend money on","chinese":"花錢在……上"},{"english":"overseas trips","chinese":"海外旅行"},{"english":"completely disagree with","chinese":"完全不同意……"},{"english":"digital travel content","chinese":"數碼旅遊內容"},{"english":"stimulate curiosity","chinese":"激發好奇心"},{"english":"rather than replacing","chinese":"而不是取代……"},{"english":"real travel","chinese":"真實旅遊"},{"english":"the experience of being abroad","chinese":"身處外地的體驗"},{"english":"cannot be reproduced through","chinese":"無法透過……重現"},{"english":"through media","chinese":"透過媒體"},{"english":"travel programmes","chinese":"旅遊節目"},{"english":"online videos","chinese":"網上影片"},{"english":"act as a gateway to","chinese":"成為通往……的入口"},{"english":"tourism","chinese":"旅遊業；旅遊活動"},{"english":"clear blue water","chinese":"清澈蔚藍的海水"},{"english":"street food","chinese":"街頭小食"},{"english":"ancient streets","chinese":"古老街道"},{"english":"tick these places off a list","chinese":"將這些地方從清單上剔走"},{"english":"be invited to imagine","chinese":"被引導去想像"},{"english":"imagine themselves there","chinese":"想像自己身處當地"},{"english":"social media","chinese":"社交媒體"},{"english":"in particular","chinese":"尤其是"},{"english":"turn destinations into","chinese":"將目的地變成……"},{"english":"living postcards","chinese":"活生生的明信片"},{"english":"reachable, desirable and worth saving for","chinese":"可到達、令人嚮往，而且值得儲錢去"},{"english":"worth saving for","chinese":"值得為……儲錢"},{"english":"become more interested in","chinese":"對……變得更感興趣"},{"english":"visit temples","chinese":"參觀寺廟"},{"english":"try local food","chinese":"嘗試當地食物"},{"english":"experience the atmosphere in person","chinese":"親身感受氣氛"},{"english":"more likely to","chinese":"更有可能"},{"english":"spark curiosity","chinese":"激發好奇心"},{"english":"extinguish it","chinese":"將它熄滅；消除它"},{"english":"more importantly","chinese":"更重要的是"},{"english":"fundamentally different from","chinese":"與……有根本不同"},{"english":"living it","chinese":"親身體驗它"},{"english":"reproduce the smell of","chinese":"重現……的氣味"},{"english":"local food","chinese":"當地食物"},{"english":"the pressure of a crowded train","chinese":"擠迫火車帶來的壓迫感"},{"english":"small conversations","chinese":"小小的交談"},{"english":"make travel memorable","chinese":"令旅遊難忘"},{"english":"merely to collect information","chinese":"只是為了收集資料"},{"english":"a break from","chinese":"從……中暫時抽離"},{"english":"normal routines","chinese":"日常慣例"},{"english":"beautifully filmed documentary","chinese":"拍攝精美的紀錄片"},{"english":"second-hand experience","chinese":"間接體驗"},{"english":"whereas","chinese":"而；然而"},{"english":"travelling abroad","chinese":"到外國旅行"},{"english":"direct contact with","chinese":"與……直接接觸"},{"english":"change how they see the world","chinese":"改變他們看世界的方式"},{"english":"travel media","chinese":"旅遊媒體"},{"english":"reduce people's willingness to","chinese":"降低人們去……的意願"},{"english":"pay for international travel","chinese":"為國際旅遊付費"},{"english":"entertain audiences at home","chinese":"娛樂在家中的觀眾"},{"english":"fuel their desire to","chinese":"加強他們想……的慾望"},{"english":"experience the world first-hand","chinese":"親身體驗世界"}]},"model-essay-95-ielts-opinion":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-95-ielts-opinion","essayKey":"opinion:95","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-95-ielts-opinion","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/opinions/EdmundBd9OP-Q95","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"International travel brings people into contact with customs that may be unfamiliar, uncomfortable, or even puzzling at first. Some people therefore argue that visitors should adjust to the local way of life rather than expect the host culture to accommodate them. I completely agree with this view, because adaptation is both a basic form of respect and the best route to genuine cultural understanding.","chinese":"國際旅行使人們接觸到一些起初可能陌生、令人不自在，甚至令人困惑的風俗習慣。 因此，有些人認為，旅客應該適應當地的生活方式，而不是期望東道主文化去遷就他們 我完全同意這觀點，因為適應既是一種基本的尊重，也是通往真正文化理解的最佳途徑。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"The first reason is that local customs often act as unwritten rules for peaceful social life. They are not merely decorative traditions; they show what a community regards as polite, modest, sacred, or offensive. If a tourist speaks loudly in a temple, ignores dress expectations at a religious site, or walks into a home with shoes on, the action may be innocent in intention but insulting in effect. By contrast, when visitors observe local etiquette, they show that residents are not just part of the scenery but people whose values deserve recognition. This reduces unnecessary tension and allows both sides to meet on more respectful ground.","chinese":"第一個原因是，當地習俗往往充當著和平社會生活中的不成文規則。 它們不只是裝飾性的傳統；它們顯示了一個社群認為甚麼是禮貌、謙遜、神聖，或冒犯的行為。 如果一名遊客在寺廟裡大聲說話、忽視宗教場所的衣著要求，或穿著鞋走進別人家中，這個行為在意圖上可能是無心的，但實際效果卻可能帶有冒犯性。 相比之下，當旅客遵守當地禮儀時，他們便表明當地居民並不只是風景的一部分，而是其價值觀值得被承認的人。 這能減少不必要的緊張，並讓雙方在更尊重彼此的基礎上交流。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"Adapting to local practices also makes travel more meaningful. A person who carries their own habits everywhere may see another culture only through a glass wall: close enough to photograph, but not close enough to understand. Simple acts, such as learning local greetings, following dining customs, or joining community routines, can open doors to real conversation. Residents are more likely to explain traditions, share stories, and treat visitors as sincere guests rather than passing consumers. In this sense, adaptation does not narrow a traveller’s freedom; it expands the experience by turning observation into participation.","chinese":"適應當地習俗也會使旅行變得更有意義。 一個無論到哪裡都帶著自己習慣的人，可能只會隔著一道玻璃牆去看另一種文化：距離近得足以拍照，卻不足以真正理解。 一些簡單的行為，例如學習當地問候語、遵守用餐習俗，或參與社區日常活動，都能為真正的交流打開大門。 當地居民便更有可能解釋傳統、分享故事，並把旅客視為真誠的客人，而不是匆匆而過的消費者。 從這個意義上說，適應並不會限制旅客的自由；它反而透過把旁觀轉化為參與，擴展了旅行體驗。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, I fully agree that people should adapt to local practices and customs when travelling in a different culture. Such adaptation protects social harmony and transforms travel from shallow sightseeing into respectful cultural exchange.","chinese":"總結來說，我完全同意人們在前往不同文化旅行時，應該適應當地的習俗和做法。 這種適應能維護社會和諧，並把旅行從表面的觀光轉化為尊重彼此的文化交流。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"international travel","chinese":"國際旅遊"},{"english":"bring people into contact with","chinese":"令人民接觸到……"},{"english":"customs","chinese":"習俗"},{"english":"unfamiliar, uncomfortable, or even puzzling","chinese":"陌生、不自在，甚至令人困惑"},{"english":"at first","chinese":"起初"},{"english":"adjust to","chinese":"適應……"},{"english":"the local way of life","chinese":"當地生活方式"},{"english":"rather than expect","chinese":"而不是期望……"},{"english":"host culture","chinese":"東道主文化；當地文化"},{"english":"accommodate them","chinese":"遷就他們"},{"english":"completely agree with","chinese":"完全同意……"},{"english":"adaptation","chinese":"適應"},{"english":"a basic form of respect","chinese":"基本的尊重形式"},{"english":"the best route to","chinese":"通往……的最佳途徑"},{"english":"genuine cultural understanding","chinese":"真正的文化理解"},{"english":"local customs","chinese":"當地習俗"},{"english":"act as","chinese":"充當；起……作用"},{"english":"unwritten rules","chinese":"不成文規則"},{"english":"peaceful social life","chinese":"和諧的社會生活"},{"english":"merely decorative traditions","chinese":"只是裝飾性的傳統"},{"english":"regard as","chinese":"視為……"},{"english":"polite, modest, sacred, or offensive","chinese":"有禮、端莊、神聖或冒犯"},{"english":"religious site","chinese":"宗教場所"},{"english":"innocent in intention","chinese":"動機上無惡意"},{"english":"insulting in effect","chinese":"效果上令人感到冒犯"},{"english":"by contrast","chinese":"相比之下"},{"english":"observe local etiquette","chinese":"遵守當地禮儀"},{"english":"part of the scenery","chinese":"景色的一部分"},{"english":"deserve recognition","chinese":"值得被認可"},{"english":"reduce unnecessary tension","chinese":"減少不必要的緊張"},{"english":"both sides","chinese":"雙方"},{"english":"on more respectful ground","chinese":"在更互相尊重的基礎上"},{"english":"local practices","chinese":"當地做法；當地習慣"},{"english":"meaningful","chinese":"有意義的"},{"english":"carry their own habits everywhere","chinese":"到處都帶着自己的習慣"},{"english":"through a glass wall","chinese":"隔着玻璃牆"},{"english":"close enough to","chinese":"足夠接近去……"},{"english":"local greetings","chinese":"當地問候語"},{"english":"dining customs","chinese":"用餐習俗"},{"english":"community routines","chinese":"社區日常習慣"},{"english":"open doors to","chinese":"為……打開機會"},{"english":"real conversation","chinese":"真正的交流"},{"english":"be more likely to","chinese":"更有可能"},{"english":"explain traditions","chinese":"解釋傳統"},{"english":"share stories","chinese":"分享故事"},{"english":"sincere guests","chinese":"真誠的客人"},{"english":"rather than passing consumers","chinese":"而不是短暫停留的消費者"},{"english":"in this sense","chinese":"從這個意義上說"},{"english":"narrow a traveller's freedom","chinese":"限制旅客的自由"},{"english":"expand the experience","chinese":"擴闊體驗"},{"english":"turn observation into participation","chinese":"將旁觀變成參與"},{"english":"adapt to local practices and customs","chinese":"適應當地做法和習俗"},{"english":"travelling in a different culture","chinese":"在不同文化中旅遊"},{"english":"protect social harmony","chinese":"維護社會和諧"},{"english":"transform travel from","chinese":"將旅遊由……轉化為……"},{"english":"shallow sightseeing","chinese":"膚淺的觀光"},{"english":"respectful cultural exchange","chinese":"互相尊重的文化交流"}]},"model-essay-96-ielts-opinion":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-96-ielts-opinion","essayKey":"opinion:96","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-96-ielts-opinion","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/opinions/EdmundBd9OP-Q96","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"Air pollution caused by aviation is a serious environmental concern, and some people believe that international flights should simply be made more expensive. I completely disagree. Raising ticket prices is a blunt and unfair measure, whereas reducing pollution at its source would be far more effective.","chinese":"航空所造成的空氣污染是一個嚴重的環境問題，而有些人認為國際航班應該直接變得更昂貴。 我完全不同意。 提高機票價格是一種粗暴而不公平的措施，而從源頭減少污染會有效得多。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"The first problem is that higher airfares would mainly restrict ordinary passengers rather than solve the environmental problem itself. Families visiting relatives abroad, students studying overseas, and migrant workers returning home would be hit hard, while wealthy travellers and large companies could still afford to fly as often as before. In other words, the policy would place the heaviest burden on those with thinner wallets, but it would not necessarily change the behaviour of the biggest users of air travel. A business executive might still take regular long-haul flights, while a family might have to give up one important trip after years of saving. This reduces access, not pollution, in a fair or reliable way.","chinese":"第一個問題是，更高的機票價格主要會限制普通乘客，而不是解決環境問題本身。 探望海外親人的家庭、在外國讀書的學生，以及回鄉的外籍勞工會受到嚴重打擊，而富裕旅客和大型公司仍然能夠像以前一樣經常乘搭飛機。 換句話說，這項政策會把最沉重的負擔加在經濟能力較弱的人身上，但它未必能改變最大航空使用者的行為。 一位企業高層可能仍然會定期乘搭長途航班，而一個家庭則可能在多年儲蓄後，仍不得不放棄一次重要的旅程。 這只是限制了人們的出行機會，而不是以公平或可靠的方式減少污染。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"A better approach is to make each flight cleaner and to replace unnecessary flights with practical alternatives. Governments should require airlines to use cleaner fuels, newer aircraft, stricter emission standards, and more efficient routes. If planes burn less fuel, avoid wasteful delays, and operate with modern technology, pollution falls on every journey, not only on the journeys that poorer people can no longer afford. At the same time, rail links where practical and wider acceptance of online business meetings can reduce avoidable flights without treating travel as a luxury for the rich. This kind of policy attacks the engine of the problem rather than merely raising the gate price.","chinese":"更好的方法是讓每一班航班變得更清潔，並用實際可行的替代方式取代不必要的飛行。 政府應該要求航空公司使用更清潔的燃料、更新型的飛機、更嚴格的排放標準，以及更高效率的航線。 如果飛機燃燒更少燃料、避免浪費性的延誤，並使用現代科技運作，那麼每一次旅程的污染都會下降，而不只是減少那些較貧窮人士再也負擔不起的旅程。 同時，在可行的地方發展鐵路連接，以及更廣泛地接受線上商務會議，都可以減少可避免的航班，而不會把旅行變成富人的奢侈品。 這類政策針對的是問題的核心，而不是僅僅提高進門的價格。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, I do not agree that increasing the cost of international flights is the best way to reduce air pollution. It may discourage some travel, but it is socially unfair and environmentally incomplete. Cleaner aviation and better alternatives would produce a deeper and more balanced solution.","chinese":"總結來說，我不同意提高國際航班成本是減少空氣污染的最佳方法。 它也許會阻止部分出行，但在社會層面上並不公平，在環境層面上也並不完整。 更清潔的航空技術和更好的替代方案，才會帶來更深入、更平衡的解決方法。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"air pollution caused by","chinese":"由……造成的空氣污染"},{"english":"aviation","chinese":"航空業"},{"english":"environmental concern","chinese":"環境憂慮"},{"english":"international flights","chinese":"國際航班"},{"english":"be made more expensive","chinese":"被變得更昂貴"},{"english":"raising ticket prices","chinese":"提高票價"},{"english":"a blunt and unfair measure","chinese":"粗糙而不公平的措施"},{"english":"whereas","chinese":"而；然而"},{"english":"reduce pollution at its source","chinese":"從源頭減少污染"},{"english":"far more effective","chinese":"有效得多"},{"english":"higher airfares","chinese":"較高機票價格"},{"english":"restrict ordinary passengers","chinese":"限制普通乘客"},{"english":"rather than solve","chinese":"而不是解決"},{"english":"the environmental problem itself","chinese":"環境問題本身"},{"english":"visiting relatives abroad","chinese":"探望海外親人"},{"english":"studying overseas","chinese":"海外升學"},{"english":"migrant workers returning home","chinese":"回鄉的外來工人"},{"english":"be hit hard","chinese":"受到沉重打擊"},{"english":"wealthy travellers","chinese":"富裕旅客"},{"english":"large companies","chinese":"大公司"},{"english":"afford to fly","chinese":"負擔得起乘飛機"},{"english":"as often as before","chinese":"像以前一樣頻密"},{"english":"in other words","chinese":"換句話說"},{"english":"place the heaviest burden on","chinese":"將最沉重負擔加於……"},{"english":"those with thinner wallets","chinese":"經濟能力較弱的人"},{"english":"not necessarily","chinese":"不一定"},{"english":"change the behaviour of","chinese":"改變……的行為"},{"english":"the biggest users of ……","chinese":"的最大使用者"},{"english":"business executive","chinese":"商業行政人員"},{"english":"regular long-haul flights","chinese":"定期長途航班"},{"english":"give up","chinese":"放棄"},{"english":"years of saving","chinese":"多年儲蓄"},{"english":"reduce access","chinese":"減少使用機會"},{"english":"in a fair or reliable way","chinese":"以公平或可靠的方式"},{"english":"a better approach","chinese":"更好的方法"},{"english":"replace unnecessary flights with","chinese":"以……取代不必要的航班"},{"english":"practical alternatives","chinese":"實際可行的替代選擇"},{"english":"require airlines to","chinese":"要求航空公司去……"},{"english":"cleaner fuels","chinese":"較清潔的燃料"},{"english":"newer aircraft","chinese":"較新的飛機"},{"english":"stricter emission standards","chinese":"更嚴格的排放標準"},{"english":"more efficient routes","chinese":"更高效的航線"},{"english":"burn less fuel","chinese":"燃燒較少燃料"},{"english":"avoid wasteful delays","chinese":"避免浪費性的延誤"},{"english":"operate with modern technology","chinese":"以現代技術運作"},{"english":"pollution falls","chinese":"污染下降"},{"english":"on every journey","chinese":"在每次旅程中"},{"english":"can no longer afford","chinese":"不再負擔得起"},{"english":"at the same time","chinese":"同時"},{"english":"rail links","chinese":"鐵路連接"},{"english":"where practical","chinese":"在可行的地方"},{"english":"wider acceptance of","chinese":"對……更廣泛接受"},{"english":"online business meetings","chinese":"網上商務會議"},{"english":"avoidable flights","chinese":"可避免的航班"},{"english":"treat travel as a luxury for the rich","chinese":"將旅遊視為富人的奢侈品"},{"english":"attack the engine of the problem","chinese":"針對問題的核心"},{"english":"merely raising","chinese":"只是提高……"},{"english":"the gate price","chinese":"入場門檻價格"},{"english":"increasing the cost of","chinese":"增加……的成本"},{"english":"discourage some travel","chinese":"阻止部分出行"},{"english":"socially unfair","chinese":"社會上不公平"},{"english":"environmentally incomplete","chinese":"環保上不完整"},{"english":"cleaner aviation","chinese":"更清潔的航空業"},{"english":"better alternatives","chinese":"更好的替代選擇"},{"english":"a deeper and more balanced solution","chinese":"更深入而更平衡的解決方案"}]},"model-essay-97-ielts-opinion":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-97-ielts-opinion","essayKey":"opinion:97","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-97-ielts-opinion","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/opinions/EdmundBd9OP-Q97","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"Traffic congestion is a serious problem in modern life. Some argue that people should be encouraged to live in cities rather than in suburbs or rural areas to solve transport problems. I completely agree, because compact urban living makes public transport more efficient and reduces long daily journeys.","chinese":"交通擠塞是現代生活中的一個嚴重問題。 有人認為，為了解決交通問題，應該鼓勵人們居住在城市，而不是住在郊區或鄉村地區 我完全同意，因為緊湊的城市生活能使公共交通更有效率，並減少漫長的日常出行。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"The strongest reason is that cities can support public transport in a way that low-density areas usually cannot. When many people live close together, governments can justify investing in underground railways, buses, tram lines, and cycle lanes, since these services will be used by large numbers of passengers each day. By contrast, when homes are spread across distant suburbs or villages, public transport becomes expensive to run and inconvenient to use. Residents then often have no realistic choice but to drive. For example, an office worker who lives near a metro station can travel to work without adding another car to the road, whereas someone in a remote suburb may need to drive even for basic errands. Urban concentration therefore turns transport from a private burden into a shared public service.","chinese":"最有力的原因是，城市能夠支撐公共交通，而低密度地區通常做不到這一點。 當很多人住得很接近時，政府便有理由投資地下鐵路、巴士、電車路線和單車徑，因為這些服務每天都會被大量乘客使用。 相比之下，當住宅分散在遙遠的郊區或村莊時，公共交通的營運成本會變得很高，而且使用起來也不方便。 居民於是往往沒有實際選擇，只能開車。 例如，一位住在地鐵站附近的上班族可以不增加路面車輛便前往工作地點；然而，住在偏遠郊區的人即使只是處理基本雜務，也可能需要開車。 因此，城市集中化能把交通從個人的負擔，轉化為共享的公共服務。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"Another reason is that city life shortens the distance between people and the places they need to reach. In well-planned cities, workplaces, schools, hospitals, shops, and entertainment venues are often within walking, cycling, or short-transit distance. This matters because traffic problems are not caused simply by vehicles; they are caused by unnecessary vehicle journeys. If people can walk to a supermarket, cycle to a park, or take a short bus ride to a clinic, fewer cars will be needed. Over time, this reduces congestion, fuel use, parking pressure, and pollution. Rural living may offer space and quiet, but it often turns every small task into a car trip.","chinese":"另一個原因是，城市生活縮短了人們與他們需要前往的地方之間的距離。 在規劃良好的城市中，工作場所、學校、醫院、商店和娛樂場所通常都在步行、騎單車或短途公共交通可達的範圍內。 這一點很重要，因為交通問題並不只是由車輛造成的；它們是由不必要的車程造成的。 如果人們可以步行去超市、騎單車去公園，或乘搭短途巴士去診所，需要使用的汽車便會減少。 長遠而言，這會減少交通擠塞、燃料使用、泊車壓力和污染。 鄉村生活或許能提供空間與寧靜，但它往往會把每一件小事都變成一次汽車出行。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, I fully agree that people should be encouraged to live in cities in order to ease transport problems. Dense urban living makes public transport viable and daily travel shorter, which directly tackles the roots of congestion.","chinese":"總結來說，我完全同意人們應該被鼓勵居住在城市，以緩解交通問題。 高密度的城市生活使公共交通變得可行，並縮短日常出行，而這正正直接處理了交通擠塞的根源。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"traffic congestion","chinese":"交通擠塞"},{"english":"a serious problem","chinese":"嚴重問題"},{"english":"modern life","chinese":"現代生活"},{"english":"be encouraged to","chinese":"被鼓勵去……"},{"english":"rather than in","chinese":"而不是在……"},{"english":"suburbs or rural areas","chinese":"郊區或鄉郊地區"},{"english":"solve transport problems","chinese":"解決交通問題"},{"english":"compact urban living","chinese":"緊湊的城市生活"},{"english":"public transport","chinese":"公共交通"},{"english":"reduce long daily journeys","chinese":"減少漫長的日常通勤"},{"english":"the strongest reason","chinese":"最有力的原因"},{"english":"support public transport","chinese":"支持公共交通發展"},{"english":"in a way that","chinese":"以……的方式"},{"english":"low-density areas","chinese":"低密度地區"},{"english":"live close together","chinese":"住得很近"},{"english":"justify investing in","chinese":"有理由投資於……"},{"english":"underground railways","chinese":"地下鐵路"},{"english":"tram lines","chinese":"電車路線"},{"english":"cycle lanes","chinese":"單車徑"},{"english":"large numbers of passengers","chinese":"大量乘客"},{"english":"by contrast","chinese":"相比之下"},{"english":"be spread across","chinese":"分散在……"},{"english":"distant suburbs","chinese":"遙遠的郊區"},{"english":"expensive to run","chinese":"營運成本高"},{"english":"inconvenient to use","chinese":"使用不方便"},{"english":"have no realistic choice but to","chinese":"除了……之外沒有現實選擇"},{"english":"office worker","chinese":"上班族"},{"english":"metro station","chinese":"地鐵站"},{"english":"travel to work","chinese":"上班；通勤"},{"english":"add another car to the road","chinese":"增加路面車輛"},{"english":"remote suburb","chinese":"偏遠郊區"},{"english":"basic errands","chinese":"基本日常雜務"},{"english":"urban concentration","chinese":"城市集中發展"},{"english":"turn transport from","chinese":"將交通由……轉變為……"},{"english":"private burden","chinese":"個人負擔"},{"english":"shared public service","chinese":"共享公共服務"},{"english":"city life","chinese":"城市生活"},{"english":"shorten the distance between","chinese":"縮短……之間的距離"},{"english":"well-planned cities","chinese":"規劃良好的城市"},{"english":"entertainment venues","chinese":"娛樂場所"},{"english":"within walking distance","chinese":"在步行距離內"},{"english":"cycling distance","chinese":"在踩單車可到的距離內"},{"english":"short-transit distance","chinese":"短途公共交通可到的距離內"},{"english":"matters because","chinese":"這很重要，因為……"},{"english":"unnecessary vehicle journeys","chinese":"不必要的車程"},{"english":"take a short bus ride to","chinese":"乘短途巴士去……"},{"english":"fewer cars will be needed","chinese":"所需車輛會較少"},{"english":"over time","chinese":"隨着時間過去"},{"english":"fuel use","chinese":"燃油使用"},{"english":"parking pressure","chinese":"泊車壓力"},{"english":"rural living","chinese":"鄉郊生活"},{"english":"offer space and quiet","chinese":"提供空間和寧靜"},{"english":"turn every small task into","chinese":"將每件小事變成……"},{"english":"car trip","chinese":"駕車出行"},{"english":"in order to ease","chinese":"為了紓緩"},{"english":"dense urban living","chinese":"高密度城市生活"},{"english":"public transport viable","chinese":"令公共交通具可行性"},{"english":"daily travel","chinese":"日常出行"},{"english":"directly tackles","chinese":"直接處理"},{"english":"the roots of congestion","chinese":"交通擠塞的根源"}]},"model-essay-98-ielts-opinion":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-98-ielts-opinion","essayKey":"opinion:98","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-98-ielts-opinion","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/opinions/EdmundBd9OP-Q98","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"Air travel has become one of the most visible symbols of modern convenience, but its environmental cost is increasingly difficult to ignore. Some argue that governments should raise taxes on flights in order to reduce the number of passengers. I disagree that this would solve the problem, because it would affect travellers unevenly while doing too little to change the aviation system itself.","chinese":"航空旅行已成為現代便利生活中最明顯的象徵之一，但它所帶來的環境代價也越來越難以被忽視。 有些人認為，政府應該提高航班稅，以減少乘客數量。 我不同意這能解決問題，因為它會不公平地影響不同旅客，同時對航空系統本身的改變太少。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"To begin with, a higher flight tax would be a blunt and unfair tool. Many people do not fly for pleasure; they travel for work, education, medical treatment or family responsibilities. If tickets became more expensive, these passengers would simply pay more rather than stop flying, especially when there is no realistic alternative. At the same time, wealthier tourists would barely feel the increase, so the policy would punish ordinary travellers more than frequent luxury passengers. A measure that mainly changes who can afford to fly, rather than how aviation operates, cannot be considered a genuine environmental solution.","chinese":"首先，更高的航班稅會是一種粗糙而不公平的工具。 許多人乘搭飛機並不是為了享樂；他們是為了工作、教育、醫療治療或家庭責任而出行 如果機票變得更昂貴，這些乘客只會支付更多費用，而不是停止飛行，尤其是在沒有現實可行替代方案的情況下。 與此同時，較富裕的遊客幾乎不會感受到加價，因此這項政策對普通旅客的懲罰會比對經常乘搭豪華航班的乘客更大。 一項主要改變誰負擔得起飛行，而不是改變航空業如何運作的措施，不能被視為真正的環境解決方案。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"The deeper problem is that aircraft still rely heavily on polluting fuel, and taxation alone does not automatically fix that. Airlines may pass the cost to customers without improving their fleets, while governments may spend the extra revenue on unrelated areas. A more effective approach would be to invest directly in cleaner aircraft technology, sustainable fuels and high-speed rail routes for shorter journeys. For example, if people could take an affordable train between major cities, many would choose it without feeling that they had been forced off planes. This would reduce emissions in a practical and lasting way.","chinese":"更深層的問題是，飛機仍然嚴重依賴污染性燃料，而單靠徵稅並不會自動解決這一點。 航空公司可能會把成本轉嫁給顧客，而不改善機隊；同時，政府也可能把額外收入花在不相關的領域。 更有效的方法會是直接投資於更清潔的飛機技術、可持續燃料，以及適合短途旅程的高速鐵路路線。 例如，如果人們可以在主要城市之間乘搭價格合理的火車，許多人會選擇這種方式，而不會覺得自己是被迫放棄飛機。 這將以實際而持久的方式減少排放。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, increasing tax on flights would not solve the environmental damage caused by aviation. Instead of using price as a gatekeeper, governments should focus on cleaner transport systems and realistic alternatives that reduce the need to fly.","chinese":"總結來說，提高航班稅並不能解決航空業所造成的環境破壞。 政府不應把價格作為限制人們出行的門檻，而應該專注於更清潔的交通系統，以及能減少飛行需求的現實替代方案。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"air travel","chinese":"航空旅遊；乘搭飛機"},{"english":"one of the most visible symbols of ……","chinese":"最明顯的象徵之一"},{"english":"modern convenience","chinese":"現代便利"},{"english":"environmental cost","chinese":"環境代價"},{"english":"increasingly difficult to ignore","chinese":"越來越難以忽視"},{"english":"raise taxes on flights","chinese":"提高航班稅"},{"english":"in order to reduce","chinese":"為了減少"},{"english":"the number of passengers","chinese":"乘客數量"},{"english":"solve the problem","chinese":"解決問題"},{"english":"affect travellers unevenly","chinese":"對旅客造成不均等影響"},{"english":"do too little to","chinese":"對……作用太小"},{"english":"the aviation system itself","chinese":"航空系統本身"},{"english":"to begin with","chinese":"首先"},{"english":"flight tax","chinese":"航班稅"},{"english":"a blunt and unfair tool","chinese":"粗糙而不公平的工具"},{"english":"fly for pleasure","chinese":"為了娛樂而乘飛機"},{"english":"medical treatment","chinese":"醫療治療"},{"english":"family responsibilities","chinese":"家庭責任"},{"english":"simply pay more rather than","chinese":"只是支付更多，而不是……"},{"english":"no realistic alternative","chinese":"沒有現實可行的替代選擇"},{"english":"at the same time","chinese":"同時"},{"english":"wealthier tourists","chinese":"較富裕的遊客"},{"english":"barely feel the increase","chinese":"幾乎感受不到加幅"},{"english":"punish ordinary travellers","chinese":"懲罰普通旅客"},{"english":"frequent luxury passengers","chinese":"經常奢華旅遊的乘客"},{"english":"a measure that","chinese":"一項……的措施"},{"english":"afford to fly","chinese":"負擔得起乘飛機"},{"english":"rather than how","chinese":"而不是如何……"},{"english":"aviation operates","chinese":"航空業運作"},{"english":"be considered","chinese":"被視為"},{"english":"genuine environmental solution","chinese":"真正的環保解決方案"},{"english":"the deeper problem","chinese":"更深層的問題"},{"english":"rely heavily on","chinese":"嚴重依賴"},{"english":"polluting fuel","chinese":"造成污染的燃料"},{"english":"taxation alone","chinese":"單靠徵稅"},{"english":"automatically fix","chinese":"自動解決"},{"english":"pass the cost to customers","chinese":"將成本轉嫁給顧客"},{"english":"improve their fleets","chinese":"改善機隊"},{"english":"extra revenue","chinese":"額外收入"},{"english":"unrelated areas","chinese":"無關範疇"},{"english":"a more effective approach","chinese":"更有效的方法"},{"english":"invest directly in","chinese":"直接投資於……"},{"english":"cleaner aircraft technology","chinese":"更清潔的飛機技術"},{"english":"sustainable fuels","chinese":"可持續燃料"},{"english":"high-speed rail routes","chinese":"高速鐵路路線"},{"english":"shorter journeys","chinese":"較短途旅程"},{"english":"take an affordable train","chinese":"乘搭可負擔的火車"},{"english":"major cities","chinese":"主要城市"},{"english":"without feeling that","chinese":"而不覺得……"},{"english":"be forced off planes","chinese":"被迫不乘飛機"},{"english":"reduce emissions","chinese":"減少排放"},{"english":"in a practical and lasting way","chinese":"以實際而持久的方式"},{"english":"increasing tax on flights","chinese":"增加航班稅"},{"english":"environmental damage caused by","chinese":"由……造成的環境破壞"},{"english":"instead of using","chinese":"而不是使用……"},{"english":"price as a gatekeeper","chinese":"以價格作為門檻"},{"english":"cleaner transport systems","chinese":"更清潔的交通系統"},{"english":"realistic alternatives","chinese":"現實可行的替代選擇"},{"english":"reduce the need to fly","chinese":"減少乘飛機的需要"}]},"model-essay-99-ielts-opinion":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-99-ielts-opinion","essayKey":"opinion:99","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-99-ielts-opinion","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/opinions/EdmundBd9OP-Q99","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"Poor infrastructure is often one of the clearest signs that a country is struggling to develop. Some argue that foreign aid should therefore deal with this issue before anything else. I completely agree, because strong infrastructure is the foundation on which education, healthcare, trade, and government services can properly function.","chinese":"貧乏的基礎建設往往是一個國家正努力發展時最明顯的跡象之一。 因此，有些人認為外國援助應該先處理這個問題，再處理其他事情。 我完全同意，因為完善的基礎建設是教育、醫療、貿易和政府服務能夠正常運作的根基。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"The first reason is that infrastructure directly affects almost every part of national development. Without reliable roads, electricity, clean water, and communication networks, even well-intentioned aid projects may fail to reach the people who need them most. For example, a rural school may receive books and trained teachers, but if there are no safe roads or stable electricity, students may be unable to attend regularly and lessons may remain extremely limited. Similarly, hospitals cannot operate effectively if medicines cannot be transported, equipment cannot be powered, and patients cannot reach treatment in time. In this sense, infrastructure is not merely one development problem among many; it is the bridge that allows other forms of aid to work.","chinese":"第一個原因是，基礎建設會直接影響國家發展的幾乎每一個部分。 如果沒有可靠的道路、電力、清潔食水和通訊網絡，即使是出於善意的援助項目，也可能無法到達最需要幫助的人手中。 例如，一所鄉村學校可能收到書本，也可能有受過訓練的教師，但如果沒有安全的道路或穩定的電力，學生可能無法定期上學，課堂也可能仍然受到極大限制。 同樣地，如果藥物無法運送、設備無法供電，而病人又不能及時獲得治療，醫院便無法有效運作。 從這個意義上說，基礎建設並不只是眾多發展問題中的其中一個；它是一座橋樑，讓其他形式的援助能夠發揮作用。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"Another reason is that better infrastructure helps under-developed countries become less dependent on foreign support in the long run. When roads, ports, power systems, and digital networks improve, local businesses can grow, farmers can bring goods to wider markets, and workers can access more employment opportunities. This creates a stronger domestic economy, which is far more sustainable than repeated short-term donations. For instance, building a dependable transport system may allow small producers to sell their products nationally rather than only within isolated villages. As income rises, the government can collect more tax revenue and reinvest it in public services. Foreign aid, therefore, should first strengthen the physical backbone of the country so that future progress can stand on its own feet.","chinese":"另一個原因是，從長遠來看，更好的基礎建設能幫助欠發達國家減少對外國支援的依賴。 當道路、港口、電力系統和數碼網絡得到改善時，本地企業便能成長，農民能把商品帶到更廣闊的市場，工人也能獲得更多就業機會。 這會創造一個更強大的國內經濟，而這比反覆接受短期捐助要可持續得多。 例如，建立一個可靠的交通系統，可能讓小型生產者把產品銷售到全國，而不是只能在偏遠村落內出售。 隨著收入上升，政府可以徵收更多稅收，並將其重新投資於公共服務。 因此，外國援助應該首先強化一個國家的實體骨幹，使未來的進步能夠靠自身力量站穩腳步。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, I fully agree that poor infrastructure should be the first issue addressed by foreign aid. Without it, other development efforts are likely to be slow, fragile, and inefficient; with it, a country gains the basic platform it needs to modernise independently.","chinese":"總結來說，我完全同意，貧乏的基礎建設應該是外國援助首先處理的問題。 沒有它，其他發展努力很可能會緩慢、脆弱而低效；有了它，一個國家便能獲得獨立現代化所需要的基本平台。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"poor infrastructure","chinese":"落後的基礎設施"},{"english":"one of the clearest signs","chinese":"最明顯跡象之一"},{"english":"struggle to develop","chinese":"難以發展"},{"english":"foreign aid","chinese":"外國援助"},{"english":"deal with this issue","chinese":"處理這個問題"},{"english":"before anything else","chinese":"優先於其他事情"},{"english":"the foundation on which ……","chinese":"的基礎"},{"english":"properly function","chinese":"正常運作"},{"english":"national development","chinese":"國家發展"},{"english":"reliable roads","chinese":"可靠的道路"},{"english":"clean water","chinese":"潔淨食水"},{"english":"communication networks","chinese":"通訊網絡"},{"english":"well-intentioned aid projects","chinese":"出於好意的援助項目"},{"english":"fail to reach","chinese":"未能到達；未能幫助"},{"english":"need them most","chinese":"最需要它們"},{"english":"rural school","chinese":"鄉村學校"},{"english":"trained teachers","chinese":"受過培訓的教師"},{"english":"safe roads","chinese":"安全道路"},{"english":"stable electricity","chinese":"穩定電力"},{"english":"attend regularly","chinese":"定期上課；經常出席"},{"english":"remain extremely limited","chinese":"仍然極為有限"},{"english":"operate effectively","chinese":"有效運作"},{"english":"be transported","chinese":"被運送"},{"english":"be powered","chinese":"獲得供電"},{"english":"reach treatment in time","chinese":"及時接受治療"},{"english":"in this sense","chinese":"從這個意義上說"},{"english":"merely one development problem among many","chinese":"眾多發展問題中的其中一個"},{"english":"other forms of aid","chinese":"其他形式的援助"},{"english":"under-developed countries","chinese":"欠發達國家"},{"english":"become less dependent on","chinese":"變得較少依賴……"},{"english":"foreign support","chinese":"外國支援"},{"english":"in the long run","chinese":"長遠而言"},{"english":"power systems","chinese":"電力系統"},{"english":"digital networks","chinese":"數碼網絡"},{"english":"local businesses","chinese":"本地企業"},{"english":"bring goods to wider markets","chinese":"將貨物帶到更廣闊的市場"},{"english":"employment opportunities","chinese":"就業機會"},{"english":"domestic economy","chinese":"本地經濟"},{"english":"far more sustainable than","chinese":"比……可持續得多"},{"english":"short-term donations","chinese":"短期捐助"},{"english":"dependable transport system","chinese":"可靠的運輸系統"},{"english":"small producers","chinese":"小型生產者"},{"english":"sell their products nationally","chinese":"在全國銷售產品"},{"english":"rather than only within","chinese":"而不只是局限於……"},{"english":"isolated villages","chinese":"偏遠村落"},{"english":"as income rises","chinese":"隨着收入上升"},{"english":"collect more tax revenue","chinese":"收取更多稅收"},{"english":"reinvest it in","chinese":"將其重新投資於……"},{"english":"public services","chinese":"公共服務"},{"english":"strengthen the physical backbone","chinese":"加強國家的實體支柱"},{"english":"future progress","chinese":"未來進步"},{"english":"stand on its own feet","chinese":"自力更生"},{"english":"fully agree that","chinese":"完全同意……"},{"english":"be the first issue addressed by","chinese":"成為……首先處理的問題"},{"english":"development efforts","chinese":"發展工作"},{"english":"be likely to","chinese":"很可能會"},{"english":"slow, fragile, and inefficient","chinese":"緩慢、脆弱而低效"},{"english":"basic platform","chinese":"基本平台"},{"english":"modernise independently","chinese":"獨立地現代化"}]},"model-essay-100-ielts-opinion":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-100-ielts-opinion","essayKey":"opinion:100","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-100-ielts-opinion","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/opinions/EdmundBd9OP-Q100","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"In today’s competitive labour market, many applicants possess similar degrees, training, and technical skills, so employers often rely on interviews to decide who is truly suitable. I completely agree that performing well in an interview is the key to securing a good job because it allows candidates to create trust and demonstrate qualities that a written application cannot fully show.","chinese":"在當今競爭激烈的勞動市場中，許多求職者都擁有相似的學位、培訓和技術能力，因此僱主往往依靠面試來判斷誰才是真正合適的人選。 我完全同意，在面試中表現出色是獲得一份好工作的關鍵，因為它能讓求職者建立信任，並展現書面申請無法完全呈現的特質。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"The most important reason is that interviews turn a candidate from a set of documents into a real person. A strong first impression can make employers feel that an applicant is confident, prepared, and reliable, which is crucial when they are choosing someone to represent their company. If a candidate answers clearly, listens carefully, and speaks with genuine interest, the interviewer is more likely to imagine that person working well with colleagues and clients. For example, two graduates may have almost identical academic results, but the one who explains ideas calmly and shows enthusiasm will usually appear more employable. In this sense, the interview is not a minor formality; it is the moment when paper qualifications become professional credibility.","chinese":"最重要的原因是，面試能把一位求職者從一堆文件轉化成一個真實的人。 良好的第一印象能讓僱主覺得申請者自信、有準備，而且可靠；當他們要選擇一個能代表公司的人時，這一點至關重要。 如果求職者回答清晰、細心聆聽，並且帶著真誠的興趣說話，面試官就更有可能想像這個人能與同事和客戶良好合作。 例如，兩位畢業生的學業成績可能幾乎完全相同，但能夠冷靜解釋想法並展現熱誠的那一位，通常會顯得更具就業能力。 從這個意義上說，面試並不是一個次要的形式程序；它是紙面資歷轉化為專業可信度的時刻。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"Another reason is that many valuable workplace qualities can only be tested through direct interaction. A good job rarely depends on technical knowledge alone. Employers also need people who can communicate under pressure, solve problems sensibly, and adapt to unexpected questions. Interviews reveal these abilities because candidates must think on their feet rather than hide behind polished documents. For instance, when an applicant is asked how they would handle a difficult customer or a tight deadline, their response can show maturity, judgement, and emotional control. These qualities are difficult to measure through a résumé, yet they strongly influence whether someone will succeed in a demanding role.","chinese":"另一個原因是，許多寶貴的職場特質只能透過直接互動來測試。 一份好工作很少只取決於技術知識本身。 僱主也需要能夠在壓力下溝通、理性解決問題，並適應意想不到問題的人。 面試能揭示這些能力，因為求職者必須即場思考，而不是躲在精心修飾的文件背後。 例如，當一位申請者被問到他們會如何處理一位難應付的客戶或一個緊迫的截止期限時，他們的回答可以展現成熟度、判斷力和情緒控制能力。 這些特質很難透過履歷來衡量，但它們會強烈影響一個人能否在要求高的職位中取得成功"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, I completely agree that doing well in interviews is central to getting a good job. Qualifications may help a candidate enter the race, but the interview is usually where the race is won.","chinese":"總結來說，我完全同意，在面試中表現出色是獲得一份好工作的核心。 資歷也許能幫助求職者進入這場競賽，但面試通常才是這場競賽勝出的地方。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"competitive labour market","chinese":"競爭激烈的勞動市場"},{"english":"possess similar degrees","chinese":"擁有相似學位"},{"english":"technical skills","chinese":"技術技能"},{"english":"rely on interviews to","chinese":"依靠面試去……"},{"english":"truly suitable","chinese":"真正適合"},{"english":"performing well in an interview","chinese":"在面試中表現良好"},{"english":"the key to securing","chinese":"獲得……的關鍵"},{"english":"create trust","chinese":"建立信任"},{"english":"demonstrate qualities","chinese":"展示特質"},{"english":"written application","chinese":"書面申請"},{"english":"fully show","chinese":"充分展示"},{"english":"a set of documents","chinese":"一組文件"},{"english":"a real person","chinese":"真實的人"},{"english":"strong first impression","chinese":"良好的第一印象"},{"english":"make employers feel that","chinese":"令僱主覺得……"},{"english":"confident, prepared, and reliable","chinese":"自信、有準備和可靠"},{"english":"be crucial when","chinese":"在……時十分關鍵"},{"english":"represent their company","chinese":"代表公司"},{"english":"answer clearly","chinese":"清楚回答"},{"english":"listens carefully","chinese":"細心聆聽"},{"english":"speaks with genuine interest","chinese":"帶着真誠興趣說話"},{"english":"be more likely to imagine","chinese":"更有可能想像"},{"english":"working well with","chinese":"與……合作良好"},{"english":"colleagues and clients","chinese":"同事和客戶"},{"english":"almost identical academic results","chinese":"幾乎相同的學業成績"},{"english":"explains ideas calmly","chinese":"冷靜地解釋想法"},{"english":"shows enthusiasm","chinese":"表現出熱誠"},{"english":"appear more employable","chinese":"顯得更適合受聘"},{"english":"in this sense","chinese":"從這個意義上說"},{"english":"a minor formality","chinese":"小小的形式程序"},{"english":"paper qualifications","chinese":"紙面資歷"},{"english":"professional credibility","chinese":"專業可信度"},{"english":"valuable workplace qualities","chinese":"有價值的職場特質"},{"english":"direct interaction","chinese":"直接互動"},{"english":"technical knowledge alone","chinese":"單靠技術知識"},{"english":"communicate under pressure","chinese":"在壓力下溝通"},{"english":"solve problems sensibly","chinese":"理智地解決問題"},{"english":"adapt to unexpected questions","chinese":"適應突如其來的問題"},{"english":"reveal these abilities","chinese":"顯示這些能力"},{"english":"think on their feet","chinese":"即場反應；臨場思考"},{"english":"hide behind","chinese":"躲在……背後"},{"english":"polished documents","chinese":"經修飾的文件"},{"english":"handle a difficult customer","chinese":"處理難纏顧客"},{"english":"a tight deadline","chinese":"緊迫的限期"},{"english":"maturity, judgement, and emotional control","chinese":"成熟、判斷力和情緒控制"},{"english":"be difficult to measure through","chinese":"難以透過……衡量"},{"english":"a résumé","chinese":"履歷；履歷表"},{"english":"strongly influence whether","chinese":"強烈影響是否……"},{"english":"succeed in","chinese":"在……中成功"},{"english":"demanding role","chinese":"要求高的職位"},{"english":"doing well in interviews","chinese":"在面試中表現好"},{"english":"be central to","chinese":"對……十分重要"},{"english":"enter the race","chinese":"進入競爭"},{"english":"where the race is won","chinese":"決勝之處"}]},"model-essay-101-ielts-opinion":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-101-ielts-opinion","essayKey":"opinion:101","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-101-ielts-opinion","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/opinions/EdmundBd9OP-Q101","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"In many countries, the largest salaries are often earned by actors, singers and professional athletes rather than by those who protect public health or educate the next generation. I completely agree that doctors, nurses and teachers should be paid more than entertainment and sports celebrities, because their work is both more socially essential and more deserving of public investment.","chinese":"在許多國家，最高的薪酬往往由演員、歌手和職業運動員賺取，而不是由那些保護公共健康或教育下一代的人獲得。 我完全同意醫生、護士和教師應該比娛樂和體育明星獲得更高薪酬，因為他們的工作在社會上更為重要，也更值得公共投資。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"The strongest reason is that these professionals form the backbone of a functioning society. Doctors and nurses do not merely perform a job; they preserve life, relieve suffering and keep families from falling apart when illness strikes. Their decisions can mean the difference between recovery and tragedy. Teachers play a similarly fundamental role, although their contribution is less dramatic on the surface. A good teacher can turn a confused child into a confident learner, and that learner may later become a skilled worker, responsible parent or thoughtful citizen. Celebrities may entertain millions, but entertainment is a luxury; healthcare and education are the oxygen of social progress. For this reason, it is morally difficult to justify paying a footballer more than a nurse who saves lives every week.","chinese":"最有力的理由是，這些專業人士構成了一個正常運作社會的支柱。 醫生和護士不只是執行一份工作；他們守護生命、減輕痛苦，並在疾病來襲時防止家庭崩潰。 他們的決定可能意味著康復與悲劇之間的差別。 教師也扮演著同樣根本的角色，儘管他們的貢獻在表面上沒有那麼戲劇性。 一位好老師可以把一個迷惘的孩子變成一個有自信的學習者，而這位學習者日後可能成為一名有技能的工人、負責任的父母，或有思想的公民。 名人或許能娛樂數以百萬計的人，但娛樂是一種奢侈；醫療和教育才是社會進步的氧氣 因此，從道德角度看，很難合理化一名足球員比一位每週拯救生命的護士獲得更高薪酬"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"Higher pay for these professions is also necessary because it would attract and retain capable people in demanding public-service roles. Becoming a doctor, nurse or teacher requires years of training, emotional resilience and daily responsibility, yet many of these workers face stress, long hours and limited recognition. If their salaries remain modest, talented young people may avoid these careers or leave them early, which weakens hospitals and schools. By contrast, celebrity income is often inflated by advertising, ticket sales and global media attention, not by deeper social importance. A society that rewards fame more than service sends the wrong message about what it values.","chinese":"提高這些職業的薪酬也是必要的，因為這能吸引並留住有能力的人才，讓他們繼續從事要求很高的公共服務崗位。 成為醫生、護士或教師需要多年的訓練、情緒韌性和日常責任感，然而這些工作者中的許多人卻面對壓力、長工時和有限的認可。 如果他們的薪酬仍然偏低，有才華的年輕人可能會避開這些職業，或很早便離開，這會削弱醫院和學校的力量。 相比之下，名人的收入往往是由廣告、門票銷售和全球媒體關注所推高，而不是由更深層的社會重要性所決定。 一個獎勵名氣多於服務的社會，會向人們傳遞錯誤的價值訊息。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, I firmly agree that doctors, nurses and teachers should be paid more than entertainment and sports celebrities. While celebrities can enrich people’s leisure time, essential workers protect lives, shape minds and hold society together.","chinese":"總結來說，我堅定同意醫生、護士和教師應該比娛樂和體育明星獲得更高薪酬。 雖然名人可豐富人們的休閒時間，但必要工作者保護生命、塑造思想，並維繫整個社會"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"the largest salaries","chinese":"最高薪酬"},{"english":"be earned by","chinese":"由……賺取"},{"english":"professional athletes","chinese":"職業運動員"},{"english":"rather than by","chinese":"而不是由……"},{"english":"protect public health","chinese":"保障公共健康"},{"english":"educate the next generation","chinese":"教育下一代"},{"english":"completely agree that","chinese":"完全同意……"},{"english":"be paid more than","chinese":"薪酬高於……"},{"english":"entertainment and sports celebrities","chinese":"娛樂和體育名人"},{"english":"socially essential","chinese":"對社會更必要"},{"english":"deserving of public investment","chinese":"更值得公共投資"},{"english":"the strongest reason","chinese":"最有力的原因"},{"english":"form the backbone of","chinese":"構成……的支柱"},{"english":"functioning society","chinese":"正常運作的社會"},{"english":"merely perform a job","chinese":"只是做一份工作"},{"english":"preserve life","chinese":"維持生命；保護生命"},{"english":"relieve suffering","chinese":"減輕痛苦"},{"english":"keep families from falling apart","chinese":"防止家庭崩潰"},{"english":"when illness strikes","chinese":"當疾病來襲時"},{"english":"mean the difference between","chinese":"可能決定是……還是……"},{"english":"recovery and tragedy","chinese":"康復和悲劇"},{"english":"play a similarly fundamental role","chinese":"發揮同樣根本的作用"},{"english":"contribution","chinese":"貢獻"},{"english":"less dramatic on the surface","chinese":"表面上較不戲劇化"},{"english":"on the surface","chinese":"表面上"},{"english":"turn a confused child into","chinese":"將一個困惑的孩子變成……"},{"english":"confident learner","chinese":"有自信的學習者"},{"english":"skilled worker","chinese":"熟練工人"},{"english":"responsible parent","chinese":"負責任的父母"},{"english":"thoughtful citizen","chinese":"有思想的公民"},{"english":"entertain millions","chinese":"娛樂數以百萬計的人"},{"english":"a luxury","chinese":"奢侈品；非必需品"},{"english":"the oxygen of social progress","chinese":"社會進步的氧氣"},{"english":"morally difficult to justify","chinese":"道德上難以合理化"},{"english":"saves lives","chinese":"拯救生命"},{"english":"higher pay","chinese":"較高薪酬"},{"english":"attract and retain","chinese":"吸引並留住"},{"english":"capable people","chinese":"有能力的人才"},{"english":"demanding public-service roles","chinese":"要求高的公共服務職位"},{"english":"require years of training","chinese":"需要多年培訓"},{"english":"emotional resilience","chinese":"情緒韌性"},{"english":"daily responsibility","chinese":"日常責任"},{"english":"face stress","chinese":"面對壓力"},{"english":"long hours","chinese":"長時間工作"},{"english":"limited recognition","chinese":"有限認可"},{"english":"salaries remain modest","chinese":"薪酬維持不高"},{"english":"talented young people","chinese":"有才能的年輕人"},{"english":"avoid these careers","chinese":"避免選擇這些職業"},{"english":"leave them early","chinese":"早早離開這些職業"},{"english":"weakens hospitals and schools","chinese":"削弱醫院和學校"},{"english":"by contrast","chinese":"相比之下"},{"english":"celebrity income","chinese":"名人收入"},{"english":"be inflated by","chinese":"因……而被推高"},{"english":"advertising","chinese":"廣告"},{"english":"ticket sales","chinese":"門票銷售"},{"english":"global media attention","chinese":"全球媒體關注"},{"english":"deeper social importance","chinese":"更深層的社會重要性"},{"english":"reward fame more than service","chinese":"獎勵名氣多於服務"},{"english":"send the wrong message","chinese":"傳達錯誤信息"},{"english":"what it values","chinese":"它重視甚麼"},{"english":"firmly agree that","chinese":"堅定同意……"},{"english":"enrich people's leisure time","chinese":"豐富人們的閒暇時間"},{"english":"essential workers","chinese":"必要工作者"},{"english":"shape minds","chinese":"塑造思想"},{"english":"hold society together","chinese":"維繫社會"}]},"model-essay-103-ielts-opinion":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-103-ielts-opinion","essayKey":"opinion:103","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-103-ielts-opinion","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/opinions/EdmundBd9OP-Q103","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"In any organisation, pay is more than a monthly transfer; it is a signal of responsibility, contribution, and trust. For this reason, I completely disagree that giving all workers the same salary would create genuine harmony or mutual respect. Although the idea may sound fair at first glance, it would quickly become unfair in practice.","chinese":"在任何機構中，薪酬不僅僅是每月的一筆轉帳；它也是責任、貢獻和信任的象徵。 因此，我完全不同意給所有員工相同薪金會創造真正的和諧或相互尊重。 儘管這個想法乍看之下可能很公平，但在實際操作中，它很快便會變得不公平。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"The main problem is that equal pay ignores real differences in workload, skill, and responsibility. A senior engineer who designs complex systems, a manager who is accountable for a whole department, and a junior employee who is still being trained do not carry the same burden. If they all receive identical salaries, the company is not treating them equally; it is refusing to recognise meaningful differences. This can easily breed resentment rather than unity, because employees whose roles are more demanding may feel that their effort has been quietly erased. For example, a team leader who works late to solve client problems is unlikely to feel respected if a colleague with far fewer duties receives exactly the same reward.","chinese":"主要問題是，劃一薪酬忽視了工作量、技能和責任上的真實差異。 一位設計複雜系統的資深工程師、一位需要對整個部門負責的經理，以及一位仍在接受培訓的初級員工，並不承擔相同的負擔。 如果他們都獲得完全相同的薪金，公司並不是在平等對待他們；而是在拒絕承認有意義的差異。 這很容易滋生怨氣，而不是團結，因為那些職責更繁重的員工可能會覺得自己的努力被悄悄抹去。 例如，一位為了解決客戶問題而工作至很晚的團隊主管，如果看到一位職責少得多的同事獲得完全相同的報酬，便很難感到自己受到尊重。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"Another reason is that a flat salary system would weaken motivation and damage performance. In a healthy workplace, pay should not be the only incentive, but it is still one important way to reward progress, reliability, and excellence. If extra effort brings no extra recognition, ambitious workers may eventually slow down or leave for companies that value their contribution more accurately. At the same time, weaker employees may have little reason to improve, since the system protects them from the consequences of poor performance. Over time, this would not create a peaceful workplace; it would create a quiet frustration under the surface.","chinese":"另一個原因是，劃一薪酬制度會削弱動力並損害工作表現。 在一個健康的工作場所中，薪酬不應該是唯一的激勵因素，但它仍然是獎勵進步、可靠性和卓越表現的重要方式之一。 如果額外努力得不到額外認可，有抱負的員工最終可能會放慢步伐，或者離開並加入那些能更準確重視他們貢獻的公司。 與此同時，表現較弱的員工可能沒有太多改善的理由，因為這個制度會保護他們免受低效表現所帶來的後果。 長遠而言，這並不會創造一個平和的工作場所；它只在表面之下製造一種沉默的挫敗感"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, paying everyone the same may appear to remove jealousy, but it would actually undermine fairness, motivation, and respect. True workplace harmony comes from fair treatment, not identical treatment.","chinese":"總結來說，給每個人相同薪金看似可以消除嫉妒，但實際上卻會削弱公平、動力和尊重 真正的職場和諧來自公平對待，而不是完全相同的對待。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"in any organisation","chinese":"在任何機構中"},{"english":"pay is more than","chinese":"薪酬不只是……"},{"english":"a monthly transfer","chinese":"每月轉賬"},{"english":"a signal of ……","chinese":"的信號；……的象徵"},{"english":"responsibility, contribution, and trust","chinese":"責任、貢獻和信任"},{"english":"for this reason","chinese":"因此"},{"english":"completely disagree that","chinese":"完全不同意……"},{"english":"giving all workers the same salary","chinese":"給所有員工相同薪金"},{"english":"genuine harmony","chinese":"真正的和諧"},{"english":"mutual respect","chinese":"互相尊重"},{"english":"sound fair at first glance","chinese":"乍看之下似乎公平"},{"english":"unfair in practice","chinese":"實際上變得不公平"},{"english":"equal pay","chinese":"相同薪酬"},{"english":"ignore real differences in","chinese":"忽視……的實際差異"},{"english":"workload, skill, and responsibility","chinese":"工作量、技能和責任"},{"english":"senior engineer","chinese":"高級工程師"},{"english":"design complex systems","chinese":"設計複雜系統"},{"english":"be accountable for","chinese":"對……負責"},{"english":"a whole department","chinese":"整個部門"},{"english":"junior employee","chinese":"初級員工"},{"english":"be still being trained","chinese":"仍在接受培訓"},{"english":"carry the same burden","chinese":"承擔相同負擔"},{"english":"receive identical salaries","chinese":"收取完全相同的薪金"},{"english":"treat them equally","chinese":"平等對待他們"},{"english":"refuse to recognise","chinese":"拒絕承認"},{"english":"meaningful differences","chinese":"有意義的差異"},{"english":"breed resentment rather than unity","chinese":"滋生怨氣而不是團結"},{"english":"roles are more demanding","chinese":"職位要求更高"},{"english":"effort has been quietly erased","chinese":"努力被默默抹去"},{"english":"team leader","chinese":"團隊主管"},{"english":"work late","chinese":"工作至很晚"},{"english":"solve client problems","chinese":"解決客戶問題"},{"english":"far fewer duties","chinese":"少得多的職責"},{"english":"exactly the same reward","chinese":"完全相同的回報"},{"english":"flat salary system","chinese":"劃一薪酬制度"},{"english":"weaken motivation","chinese":"削弱動力"},{"english":"damage performance","chinese":"損害表現"},{"english":"healthy workplace","chinese":"健康的工作場所"},{"english":"the only incentive","chinese":"唯一誘因"},{"english":"one important way to ……","chinese":"的一個重要方式"},{"english":"reward progress","chinese":"獎勵進步"},{"english":"reliability and excellence","chinese":"可靠性和卓越表現"},{"english":"extra effort","chinese":"額外努力"},{"english":"extra recognition","chinese":"額外認可"},{"english":"ambitious workers","chinese":"有抱負的員工"},{"english":"eventually slow down","chinese":"最終放慢步伐"},{"english":"value their contribution","chinese":"重視他們的貢獻"},{"english":"more accurately","chinese":"更準確地"},{"english":"weaker employees","chinese":"表現較弱的員工"},{"english":"have little reason to","chinese":"沒有太大理由去……"},{"english":"protect them from","chinese":"保護他們免受……"},{"english":"the consequences of ……","chinese":"的後果"},{"english":"poor performance","chinese":"表現欠佳"},{"english":"over time","chinese":"隨着時間過去"},{"english":"peaceful workplace","chinese":"和諧安穩的工作場所"},{"english":"quiet frustration under the surface","chinese":"表面下暗藏的不滿"},{"english":"appear to remove jealousy","chinese":"看似消除妒忌"},{"english":"undermine fairness","chinese":"損害公平"},{"english":"true workplace harmony","chinese":"真正的職場和諧"},{"english":"fair treatment","chinese":"公平對待"},{"english":"identical treatment","chinese":"一模一樣的待遇"}]},"model-essay-104-ielts-opinion":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-104-ielts-opinion","essayKey":"opinion:104","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-104-ielts-opinion","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/opinions/EdmundBd9OP-Q104","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"The movement of workers across national borders has become an important part of many modern economies. Some argue that foreign workers should no longer be recruited for jobs that local people refuse to do because their presence may create pressure within the community. I completely disagree with this view, as stopping this practice would damage essential services and ignore the real causes of local tension.","chinese":"勞工跨越國界流動，已經成為許多現代經濟體的重要一部分。 有些人認為，不應再招聘外籍工人去從事本地人拒絕做的工作，因為他們的存在可能會為本地社區帶來壓力。 我完全不同意這個觀點，因為停止這種做法會損害基本服務，並忽視本地緊張關係的真正原因。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"The first reason is that many communities rely heavily on migrant workers to keep basic sectors functioning. Jobs in agriculture, elderly care, cleaning, construction, and food production are often physically demanding, low-status, or poorly paid, which explains why many local workers avoid them. If employers were suddenly prevented from hiring foreign staff, these roles would not magically become attractive to domestic workers. Instead, farms could lose crops, care homes could become understaffed, and building projects could slow down. For example, a city that depends on migrant carers for its ageing population would face a serious welfare problem if those workers were removed. In this sense, banning foreign labour would not protect the community; it would weaken the very services that residents depend on.","chinese":"第一個原因是，許多社區都高度依賴外來勞工來維持基本行業的運作。 農業、長者照顧、清潔、建築和食品生產方面的工作，往往體力要求高、社會地位較低，或者薪酬欠佳，這解釋了為甚麼許多本地工人會避開這些工作。 如果僱主突然被禁止聘請外籍員工，這些職位並不會神奇地變得吸引本地工人。 相反，農場可能會失去收成，護老院可能會人手不足，而建築項目也可能會放慢。 例如，一個依賴外來護理員照顧老齡人口的城市，如果這些工人被移走，便會面對嚴重的福利問題。 從這個角度來看，禁止外籍勞工並不會保護社區；它反而會削弱居民所依賴的基本服務。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"Another reason is that the problems linked to foreign workers are usually caused by poor management rather than immigration itself. Local resentment may arise when wages are unfair, housing is overcrowded, or newcomers are left socially isolated. However, these issues can be addressed through stronger labour laws, fair recruitment, language support, and proper housing standards. Blaming foreign workers is therefore a convenient but shallow solution. It treats them as the problem, when in reality they are often filling gaps that the local labour market has failed to solve. A well-regulated system can protect domestic workers, prevent exploitation, and help migrants integrate into the community more smoothly.","chinese":"另一個原因是，與外籍工人有關的問題通常是由管理不善造成，而不是由移民本身造成 當工資不公平、住房過度擁擠，或者新來者在社交上被孤立時，本地人的不滿情緒便可能出現 然而，這些問題可以透過更強而有力的勞工法例、公平招聘、語言支援和適當的住房標準來處理。 因此，責怪外籍工人是一個方便但膚淺的解決方法。 這種做法把他們視為問題，但事實上，他們往往是在填補本地勞動市場未能解決的空缺 一個受到良好規管的制度可以保障本地工人、防止剝削，並幫助移民更順利地融入社區。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, I completely disagree that foreign workers should be stopped from taking jobs local workers are unwilling to do. Such a ban would create labour shortages, harm public services, and fail to address the underlying causes of social conflict. The better solution is not exclusion, but fair regulation and thoughtful integration.","chinese":"總結來說，我完全不同意應該阻止外籍工人從事本地工人不願意做的工作。 這樣的禁令會造成勞工短缺、損害公共服務，並且無法處理社會衝突背後的根本原因。 更好的解決方法不是排斥，而是公平規管和周全融合。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"the movement of workers","chinese":"工人的流動"},{"english":"across national borders","chinese":"跨越國界"},{"english":"modern economies","chinese":"現代經濟體"},{"english":"foreign workers","chinese":"外勞；外籍工人"},{"english":"no longer be recruited","chinese":"不再被招聘"},{"english":"local people refuse to do","chinese":"本地人拒絕做的"},{"english":"their presence","chinese":"他們的存在"},{"english":"create pressure within","chinese":"在……內造成壓力"},{"english":"completely disagree with","chinese":"完全不同意"},{"english":"stopping this practice","chinese":"停止這種做法"},{"english":"essential services","chinese":"基本服務"},{"english":"local tension","chinese":"本地緊張關係"},{"english":"rely heavily on","chinese":"非常依賴"},{"english":"migrant workers","chinese":"外來工人；移民工人"},{"english":"keep basic sectors functioning","chinese":"維持基本行業運作"},{"english":"agriculture","chinese":"農業"},{"english":"elderly care","chinese":"長者照顧"},{"english":"food production","chinese":"食品生產"},{"english":"physically demanding","chinese":"體力要求高的"},{"english":"low-status","chinese":"社會地位較低的"},{"english":"poorly paid","chinese":"薪酬低的"},{"english":"explains why","chinese":"解釋了為甚麼"},{"english":"local workers","chinese":"本地工人"},{"english":"be prevented from","chinese":"被阻止去……"},{"english":"hiring foreign staff","chinese":"聘請外籍員工"},{"english":"magically become attractive to","chinese":"神奇地變得對……有吸引力"},{"english":"domestic workers","chinese":"本地工人"},{"english":"lose crops","chinese":"失去農作物收成"},{"english":"care homes","chinese":"護老院"},{"english":"become understaffed","chinese":"人手不足"},{"english":"building projects","chinese":"建築項目"},{"english":"slow down","chinese":"放慢；拖慢"},{"english":"depend on migrant carers","chinese":"依賴外來護理員"},{"english":"ageing population","chinese":"老齡化人口"},{"english":"face a serious welfare problem","chinese":"面對嚴重的福利問題"},{"english":"be removed","chinese":"被移走；被撤走"},{"english":"banning foreign labour","chinese":"禁止外勞"},{"english":"protect the community","chinese":"保護社區"},{"english":"weaken the very services","chinese":"削弱正正是……的服務"},{"english":"residents depend on","chinese":"居民依賴"},{"english":"problems linked to","chinese":"與……有關的問題"},{"english":"poor management","chinese":"管理不善"},{"english":"rather than immigration itself","chinese":"而不是移民本身"},{"english":"local resentment","chinese":"本地人的不滿"},{"english":"may arise when","chinese":"可能在……時出現"},{"english":"wages are unfair","chinese":"工資不公平"},{"english":"housing is overcrowded","chinese":"住屋過度擠迫"},{"english":"newcomers","chinese":"新來者"},{"english":"be left socially isolated","chinese":"被社會孤立"},{"english":"be addressed through","chinese":"透過……處理"},{"english":"stronger labour laws","chinese":"更強而有力的勞工法例"},{"english":"fair recruitment","chinese":"公平招聘"},{"english":"language support","chinese":"語言支援"},{"english":"proper housing standards","chinese":"適當的住屋標準"},{"english":"blaming foreign workers","chinese":"責怪外勞"},{"english":"a convenient but shallow solution","chinese":"方便但膚淺的解決方法"},{"english":"in reality","chinese":"實際上"},{"english":"filling gaps","chinese":"填補缺口"},{"english":"local labour market","chinese":"本地勞動市場"},{"english":"well-regulated system","chinese":"監管良好的制度"},{"english":"prevent exploitation","chinese":"防止剝削"},{"english":"integrate into the community","chinese":"融入社區"},{"english":"more smoothly","chinese":"更順利地"},{"english":"be stopped from","chinese":"被阻止做……"},{"english":"unwilling to do","chinese":"不願意做"},{"english":"such a ban","chinese":"這樣的禁令"},{"english":"labour shortages","chinese":"勞工短缺"},{"english":"harm public services","chinese":"損害公共服務"},{"english":"underlying causes","chinese":"根本原因"},{"english":"social conflict","chinese":"社會衝突"},{"english":"exclusion","chinese":"排斥"},{"english":"fair regulation","chinese":"公平監管"},{"english":"thoughtful integration","chinese":"周全的融合措施"}]},"model-essay-105-ielts-opinion":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-105-ielts-opinion","essayKey":"opinion:105","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-105-ielts-opinion","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/opinions/EdmundBd9OP-Q105","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"In any organisation, employers have to decide whether their main duty is to improve the human atmosphere of the workplace or to invest in better physical resources. In my view, creating a respectful and supportive environment should be the clear priority, because people cannot perform well for long if they feel ignored, unsafe, or unfairly treated.","chinese":"在任何機構中，僱主都必須決定，他們的主要責任是改善工作場所中的人際氛圍，還是投資於更好的實體資源。 在我看來，創造一個尊重和支持員工的環境應該是明確的優先事項，因為如果人們感到被忽視、不安全或受到不公平對待，他們便無法長期有良好表現。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"The strongest reason is that a healthy workplace culture directly affects motivation and loyalty. When employees are respected equally, they are more willing to share ideas, admit mistakes, and cooperate with colleagues. This kind of trust is not a soft luxury; it is the foundation on which serious work is built. For example, a junior employee who is listened to during meetings is more likely to point out a problem early, whereas someone who is constantly dismissed may stay silent until the problem becomes costly. In this sense, respect can prevent small issues from growing into major failures.","chinese":"最有力的原因是，健康的職場文化會直接影響員工的動力和忠誠度。 當員工受到平等尊重時，他們會更願意分享想法、承認錯誤，並與同事合作。 這種信任並不是一種可有可無的溫和奢侈品；它是嚴肅工作得以建立的基礎。 例如，一位在會議中受到聆聽的初級員工，更有可能及早指出問題；相反，一個經常被否定的人，可能會保持沉默，直到問題變得代價高昂。 從這個角度來看，尊重可以防止小問題演變成重大失誤。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"Better facilities and equipment are certainly useful, but they cannot compensate for a toxic or unequal environment. A modern computer, a comfortable office, or an attractive staff room may make daily tasks easier, yet these things have limited value if workers feel humiliated by managers or excluded by their team. In fact, employees in such conditions may use the best tools with little enthusiasm, simply doing the minimum because they no longer feel emotionally invested in the organisation. By contrast, people in a fair and encouraging workplace often remain productive even when resources are not perfect, because they feel that their effort matters.","chinese":"更好的設施和設備當然有用，但它們無法彌補一個有毒或不平等的工作環境。 一部現代化的電腦、一間舒適的辦公室，或一個吸引人的員工休息室，可能會令日常工作更容易完成；然而，如果員工感到被管理層羞辱，或被團隊排斥，這些東西的價值便十分有限。 事實上，在這種情況下的員工，即使使用最好的工具，也可能缺乏熱情，只是完成最低限度的工作，因為他們在情感上已不再投入這個機構。 相比之下，在一個公平而鼓勵人的工作場所中，即使資源並不完美，人們往往仍能保持生產力，因為他們覺得自己的努力是有意義的。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, although equipment and facilities can improve efficiency, they should not be the employer’s central focus. A workplace where people are respected, valued, and supported is far more important, because it builds the trust and commitment that no machine or office design can replace.","chinese":"總結來說，儘管設備和設施可以提升效率，它們不應該成為僱主的核心關注點。 一個讓人受到尊重、重視和支持的工作場所遠為重要，因為它能建立信任和投入感，而這是任何機器或辦公室設計都無法取代的。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"in any organisation","chinese":"在任何機構中"},{"english":"main duty","chinese":"主要責任"},{"english":"improve the human atmosphere","chinese":"改善人際氣氛"},{"english":"the workplace","chinese":"工作場所"},{"english":"invest in","chinese":"投資於……"},{"english":"physical resources","chinese":"實體資源"},{"english":"in my view","chinese":"在我看來"},{"english":"respectful and supportive environment","chinese":"互相尊重和支持的環境"},{"english":"the clear priority","chinese":"明確的優先事項"},{"english":"perform well for long","chinese":"長期有良好表現"},{"english":"feel ignored","chinese":"感到被忽視"},{"english":"unfairly treated","chinese":"受到不公平對待"},{"english":"the strongest reason","chinese":"最有力的原因"},{"english":"healthy workplace culture","chinese":"健康的工作場所文化"},{"english":"directly affects","chinese":"直接影響"},{"english":"motivation and loyalty","chinese":"動力和忠誠度"},{"english":"be respected equally","chinese":"受到平等尊重"},{"english":"be more willing to","chinese":"更願意去……"},{"english":"share ideas","chinese":"分享想法"},{"english":"admit mistakes","chinese":"承認錯誤"},{"english":"cooperate with colleagues","chinese":"與同事合作"},{"english":"this kind of trust","chinese":"這種信任"},{"english":"a soft luxury","chinese":"可有可無的奢侈品"},{"english":"the foundation on which ……","chinese":"的基礎"},{"english":"serious work","chinese":"認真而重要的工作"},{"english":"a junior employee","chinese":"初級員工"},{"english":"be listened to","chinese":"被聆聽"},{"english":"during meetings","chinese":"在會議期間"},{"english":"be more likely to","chinese":"更有可能"},{"english":"point out a problem","chinese":"指出問題"},{"english":"constantly dismissed","chinese":"經常被否定"},{"english":"stay silent","chinese":"保持沉默"},{"english":"become costly","chinese":"變得代價高昂"},{"english":"in this sense","chinese":"從這個意義上說"},{"english":"prevent small issues from","chinese":"防止小問題……"},{"english":"major failures","chinese":"重大失誤"},{"english":"better facilities and equipment","chinese":"更好的設施和設備"},{"english":"compensate for","chinese":"彌補"},{"english":"toxic environment","chinese":"有害的工作環境"},{"english":"unequal environment","chinese":"不平等的環境"},{"english":"comfortable office","chinese":"舒適的辦公室"},{"english":"attractive staff room","chinese":"吸引人的員工休息室"},{"english":"daily tasks","chinese":"日常工作"},{"english":"have limited value","chinese":"價值有限"},{"english":"feel humiliated by","chinese":"因……而感到受辱"},{"english":"be excluded by","chinese":"被……排斥"},{"english":"in such conditions","chinese":"在這種情況下"},{"english":"use the best tools","chinese":"使用最好的工具"},{"english":"with little enthusiasm","chinese":"沒有甚麼熱誠"},{"english":"do the minimum","chinese":"只做最低限度的工作"},{"english":"emotionally invested in","chinese":"在情感上投入於……"},{"english":"by contrast","chinese":"相比之下"},{"english":"fair and encouraging workplace","chinese":"公平而鼓勵人的工作場所"},{"english":"remain productive","chinese":"保持生產力"},{"english":"resources are not perfect","chinese":"資源並不完善"},{"english":"their effort matters","chinese":"他們的努力有價值"},{"english":"improve efficiency","chinese":"提高效率"},{"english":"central focus","chinese":"核心焦點"},{"english":"be respected, valued, and supported","chinese":"受到尊重、重視和支持"},{"english":"far more important","chinese":"重要得多"},{"english":"build the trust and commitment","chinese":"建立信任和承諾"},{"english":"no machine or office design can replace","chinese":"沒有機器或辦公室設計可以取代"}]},"model-essay-106-ielts-opinion":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-106-ielts-opinion","essayKey":"opinion:106","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-106-ielts-opinion","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/opinions/EdmundBd9OP-Q106","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"In many parts of the world, family-run companies are a familiar part of commercial life, from small shops to large enterprises. Although such businesses may appear stable because relatives know one another well, I do not believe that family ownership is the best way to run a company. In my view, it often creates more serious problems than advantages because it can weaken professional decision-making and turn private tensions into business risks.","chinese":"在世界許多地方，家族企業都是商業生活中常見的一部分，從小型店舖到大型企業皆是如此。 儘管這類企業可能看起來很穩定，因為親屬之間彼此熟悉， 我並不認為家族擁有權是經營公司的最佳方式。 在我看來，它往往會帶來比好處更嚴重的問題，因為它可能削弱專業決策，並把私人緊張關係轉化為商業風險。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"The first problem is that family businesses can easily place loyalty above competence. When important positions are given mainly to relatives, promotion no longer depends on ability, experience, or performance. For example, a founder may appoint a son or daughter to manage sales even though an experienced employee is clearly better suited to the role. This does not only damage efficiency; it also sends a quiet but powerful message to other workers that hard work may never be rewarded fairly. Over time, talented staff may leave, standards may fall, and the company can become a closed room rather than a growing organisation.","chinese":"第一個問題是，家族企業很容易把忠誠放在能力之上。 當重要職位主要交給親屬時，晉升便不再取決於能力、經驗或表現。 例如，一位創辦人可能會任命自己的兒子或女兒管理銷售部門，即使一位有經驗的員工明顯更適合這個職位。 這不但會損害效率，也會向其他員工傳遞一個安靜卻有力的訊息：努力工作可能永遠不會得到公平回報。 長遠而言，有才能的員工可能會離開，標準可能會下降，而公司也可能變成一個封閉的房間，而不是一個正在成長的組織。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"A second issue is that family relationships can make business decisions emotionally complicated. In a professionally managed company, disagreements can be handled through clear rules, contracts, and performance targets. In a family firm, however, a dispute about money, succession, or control may carry years of personal history behind it. For instance, two siblings may argue over whether profits should be reinvested or shared among family members, and this private conflict can quickly slow down decisions that affect employees, customers, and suppliers. When the dining table and the boardroom start to overlap, the business becomes vulnerable to emotions that have little to do with commercial judgment.","chinese":"第二個問題是，家庭關係可能會使商業決策在情感上變得複雜。 在一間由專業方式管理的公司中，分歧可以透過清晰的規則、合約和績效目標來處理。 然而，在家族企業中，一場關於金錢、繼承或控制權的爭議，背後可能承載著多年的私人恩怨與家庭歷史。 例如，兩名兄弟姊妹可能會爭論利潤應該重新投資，還是分配給家庭成員，而這種私人衝突很快就可能拖慢影響員工、顧客和供應商的決策。 當飯桌和董事會議室開始重疊時，企業便會容易受到情緒影響，而這些情緒與商業判斷幾乎沒有關係。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, I firmly believe that family ownership is not the best way to run a business. While trust between relatives may seem useful, a company needs merit-based leadership, clear boundaries, and professional accountability more than family loyalty.","chinese":"總結來說，我堅定地認為，家族擁有權並不是經營企業的最佳方式。 雖然親屬之間的信任看似有用，但一間公司更需要以能力為本的領導、清晰的界線，以及專業的問責，而不是家族忠誠。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"family-run companies","chinese":"家族經營的公司"},{"english":"a familiar part of ……","chinese":"中常見的一部分"},{"english":"commercial life","chinese":"商業生活；商業活動"},{"english":"small shops to large enterprises","chinese":"從小店到大型企業"},{"english":"appear stable","chinese":"看似穩定"},{"english":"know one another well","chinese":"彼此十分熟悉"},{"english":"family ownership","chinese":"家族擁有權"},{"english":"run a company","chinese":"經營一間公司"},{"english":"in my view","chinese":"在我看來"},{"english":"create more serious problems than advantages","chinese":"帶來的嚴重問題多於好處"},{"english":"weaken professional decision-making","chinese":"削弱專業決策"},{"english":"private tensions","chinese":"私人矛盾"},{"english":"business risks","chinese":"商業風險"},{"english":"place loyalty above competence","chinese":"將忠誠置於能力之上"},{"english":"important positions","chinese":"重要職位"},{"english":"depend on","chinese":"取決於"},{"english":"ability, experience, or performance","chinese":"能力、經驗或表現"},{"english":"appoint a son or daughter to","chinese":"任命兒子或女兒去……"},{"english":"manage sales","chinese":"管理銷售"},{"english":"experienced employee","chinese":"有經驗的員工"},{"english":"be clearly better suited to","chinese":"明顯更適合……"},{"english":"damage efficiency","chinese":"損害效率"},{"english":"send a quiet but powerful message","chinese":"傳達一個不明顯但有力的信息"},{"english":"be rewarded fairly","chinese":"得到公平回報"},{"english":"over time","chinese":"隨着時間過去"},{"english":"talented staff","chinese":"有才能的員工"},{"english":"standards may fall","chinese":"水準可能下降"},{"english":"a growing organisation","chinese":"不斷發展的組織"},{"english":"family relationships","chinese":"家庭關係"},{"english":"emotionally complicated","chinese":"情緒上複雜"},{"english":"professionally managed company","chinese":"專業管理的公司"},{"english":"disagreements","chinese":"分歧；意見不合"},{"english":"be handled through","chinese":"透過……處理"},{"english":"clear rules","chinese":"清晰規則"},{"english":"performance targets","chinese":"表現目標"},{"english":"family firm","chinese":"家族企業"},{"english":"a dispute about","chinese":"關於……的爭議"},{"english":"succession","chinese":"繼承權；接班安排"},{"english":"carry years of personal history behind it","chinese":"背後帶有多年的私人恩怨"},{"english":"argue over whether","chinese":"就是否……而爭論"},{"english":"be reinvested","chinese":"被重新投資"},{"english":"be shared among","chinese":"在……之間分配"},{"english":"family members","chinese":"家庭成員"},{"english":"private conflict","chinese":"私人衝突"},{"english":"slow down decisions","chinese":"拖慢決策"},{"english":"affect employees, customers, and suppliers","chinese":"影響員工、顧客和供應商"},{"english":"the dining table and the boardroom","chinese":"飯桌和董事會會議室"},{"english":"start to overlap","chinese":"開始重疊"},{"english":"become vulnerable to","chinese":"容易受到……影響"},{"english":"have little to do with","chinese":"與……幾乎無關"},{"english":"commercial judgment","chinese":"商業判斷"},{"english":"firmly believe that","chinese":"堅信"},{"english":"not the best way to","chinese":"不是……的最佳方法"},{"english":"trust between relatives","chinese":"親屬之間的信任"},{"english":"merit-based leadership","chinese":"以能力為本的領導"},{"english":"clear boundaries","chinese":"清晰界線"},{"english":"professional accountability","chinese":"專業問責"},{"english":"more than family loyalty","chinese":"多於家族忠誠"}]}};
